const GALLERY_DATA = [{"id":"01","run_dir":"run_prompt01_phyworld_rerun","index":1,"title":"Make the Generator Its Own Physicist: Latent Conserved Charges for Text-to-Video","title_zh":"让生成器自己当物理学家：面向 Text-to-Video 的隐空间守恒荷","method_name":"Latent Conserved Charges (LCC)","hook":"Every recent physics-aware T2V system bolts the physics on from outside — a separate dynamics network (NewtonGen), category-conditioning (WISA), or a learned reward (PhysCorr) — yet we obtain physically-consistent video with strictly fewer trained components: no external dynamics network and no curated physics-clean dataset, by requiring the generator's own denoising latent to be the physical state and conserving a charge read off it by construction.","anchor_pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","anchor_pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","domain_category":"Generative Models — Vision","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved paper tests whether physical realism must be supplied through a channel external to the generator at all: every leaf inherits from appearance-trained video diffusion the unexamined assumption that the denoising representation cannot itself carry a physical state, and so adds physics as a bolt-on (an external control module, conditioning embeddings, a reward, or a refined prompt) rather than asking whether the generator's own representation could be required to carry the conserved qu","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"structural_prior_encoding","how_closed":"Closed by relocating the enforcement locus (C01): physics is moved from every external locus (separate predictor / conditioning / reward / prompt) to the generator's own per-frame denoising latent, and the companion structural_prior_encoding ships the deliverable — a symplectic latent integrator that makes a charge read off that latent conserved by construction of the update rule, so the generator's representation IS the physical state rather than receiving one.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf supplies a per-generation signal of physical-law satisfaction that does not route through a learned proxy: the reward-model and metric-based approaches score a learned approximation of physics, so the quantity being optimized can diverge from the law it stands in for and provides no guarantee on dynamics the proxy never saw.","pattern_id":"targeted_self_supervised_objective","pattern_name":"Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective","sub_pattern":"C17 (Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by re-engineering the contrastive pairing geometry (C17) around the conserved charge: the per-generation conservation residual computed directly from the latent (no learned reward) is the proxy-free signal, and a charge-contrastive objective whose positives are charge-preserving augmentations and negatives are same-appearance charge-perturbed counterfactuals makes the only loss-minimizing representation one whose geometry linearly encodes that charge.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"physical realism in diffusion-based text-to-video (T2V) generation","n_papers":38,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":24},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":14,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"PhyT2V: LLM-Guided Iterative Self-Refinement for Physics-Grounded Text-to-Video Generation"},{"source":"openalex","title":"PhysDreamer: Physics-Based Interaction with 3D Objects via Video Generation"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Synthetic data generation methods in healthcare: A review on open-source tools and methods"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Leveraging AI in E-Learning: Personalized Learning and Adaptive Assessment through Cognitive Neuropsychology—A Systematic Analysis"},{"source":"openalex","title":"A Systematic Review of Synthetic Data Generation Techniques Using Generative AI"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Revolutionizing Visuals: The Role of Generative AI in Modern Image Generation"}],"more":8},{"year":2025,"n":23,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"\"PhyWorldBench\": A Comprehensive Evaluation of Physical Realism in Text-to-Video Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"P‐3.5: A Review on Spatiotemporal Consistency in Artificial Intelligence Text‐to‐Video Generation: Current Status, Challenges and Future Developments"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"T2AV-Compass: Towards Unified Evaluation for Text-to-Audio-Video Generation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"One-Minute Video Generation with Test-Time Training"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"RagMe: Retrieval Augmented Video Generation for Enhanced Motion Realism"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"GimbalDiffusion: Gravity-Aware Camera Control for Video Generation"}],"more":17},{"year":2026,"n":1,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"}],"more":0}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":8,"share":0.211},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":8,"share":0.211},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":7,"share":0.184},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":7,"share":0.184},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":5,"share":0.132},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":3,"share":0.079},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":2,"share":0.053},{"pattern_id":"targeted_self_supervised_objective","pattern_name":"Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective","count":2,"share":0.053}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Diffusion-based T2V generators optimize pixel/token likelihood and thereby learn motion only as a marginal of appearance, so when a prompt specifies a dynamical regime under-represented in training data the generated trajectory carries no quantity tied to a conserved physical law and drifts into violations (objects fall upward, velocity jumps), as documented across the frontier (semanticscholar:116b156e0c6f, openalex:W4416023737). Every recent remedy supplies the missing physical constraint through a channel external to the generator's own denoising representation: NewtonGen (semanticscholar:116b156e0c6f) predicts states with a separate Neural-Newtonian ODE module and feeds them as motion control to a frozen generator; WISA (semanticscholar:d077df935592) injects decomposed physical-category embeddings as conditioning; PhysCorr (openalex:W4416023737) post-optimizes against a learned physics reward via DPO; PhyT2V (semanticscholar:015b1f127b6c) refines the prompt. Each closes only the dynamical cases its external channel can explicitly encode or score, and none changes the fact that the generator's internal representation still holds no state variable that must satisfy a physical law, so adherence stays bounded by a hand-enumerated force/phenomenon set and by the fidelity of a learned proxy.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:116b156e0c6f","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"NewtonGen trains a physics-informed Neural-Newtonian ODE (linear neural ODE + MLP) on a small physics-clean set to predict future physical states from user-specified initial conditions, then feeds those states as a motion-control signal into a separate, frozen data-driven T2V generator. Its residue: the dynamics live entirely in an external predictor restricted to parametrizable classical/rigid motion that its ODE family can represent, it needs physics-clean training data, and the generator's own representation is never required to carry the state, so deformable, contact-rich, fluid, and multi-body regimes stay outside its reach."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:d077df935592","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"WISA decomposes abstract physical principles into category embeddings and injects them as conditioning so the generator is guided toward physics-aware outputs. Its residue: the physics enters as soft conditioning that is never enforced by construction, and coverage is bounded by the enumerated physical categories, so an unlisted phenomenon receives no constraint."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416023737","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"PhysCorr forms preference pairs from a learned dual-reward PhysicsRM (subject-consistency + mechanics) and post-trains the generator with weighted DPO toward higher physics scores. Its residue: the optimization target is a learned proxy of physical plausibility rather than the law itself, so the signal can be gamed and adherence is capped by the reward model's accuracy on unseen dynamics."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W6979224095","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Physics-Guided Motion Loss adds an architecture-agnostic frequency-domain prior that decomposes rigid translation/rotation/scaling into lightweight spectral losses. Its residue: the loss only covers the three rigid-motion families expressible in its spectral basis, leaving non-rigid deformation and contact dynamics unconstrained."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4417086533","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"MoReGen delegates generation to a multi-agent LLM pipeline that parses physics parameters, writes simulation code, and renders via a sandboxed simulator. Its residue: physical accuracy is achieved only for scenes that can be reduced to executable simulation code, so open-domain, perceptually-rich T2V prompts fall outside the scriptable regime."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"physical realism in diffusion-based text-to-video (T2V) generation","venue":"ICLR/NeurIPS/CVPR-tier ML","time":"2026","data":["large-scale text-video pretraining corpora","physics-clean / controlled physical-phenomenon video sets (e.g. PhyWorldBench, T2VPhysBench, Morpheus instances)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"generative video modeling + diffusion methods","preference":"both","baseline":"NewtonGen, WISA, PhysCorr, PhyT2V (physics-aware T2V methods)","limitation":"T2V generators learn motion as a marginal of appearance and have no internal state obeying a conservation law, so physical realism only holds for motions seen in training","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","compute","expertise","preference","data"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object both legs read from and write to is the latent conserved charge q(z_t) = R · pool(z_t ⊙ m_t), where z_t is the generator's per-frame denoising latent at frame t, m_t is a foreground mask obtained by thresholding the generator's own cross-attention to the moving-subject token at τ=0.5, pool is a masked spatial average, and R ∈ R^{d_q × d} is a learned linear readout producing a small charge vector (d_q=6: three center-of-mass position coefficients and three generalized-momentum components). Anchor leg (C01 + structural_prior_encoding): we audit the field-wide assumption that physics must be enforced at a locus external to the generator — NewtonGen enforces it in a separate Neural-Newtonian ODE, WISA in conditioning embeddings, PhysCorr in an output reward — and relocate enforcement into the latent itself by replacing the latent frame-to-frame update with a structure-preserving (leapfrog/symplectic) integrator z_{t+1} = Φ_Δt(z_t, f_θ(z_t, c)) that splits the latent channels into conjugate position/momentum halves and is driven by a learned generalized-force field f_θ conditioned on prompt c; because a symplectic integrator exactly conserves its discrete momentum map regardless of f_θ, the charge q read by R is invariant along the generated trajectory BY CONSTRUCTION when the prompt specifies no external field, and follows the exact constant-acceleration update when it specifies one (gravity g enters as F_t = m·g parsed from the prompt into a constant, default 0). This artifact — a conserved charge that is intrinsic to the generator's representation rather than predicted by a side network — closes the subtractive gap because the generator's own latent now carries the physical state, with no external channel. Sibling leg (C17): the conservation residual ρ_t = q(z_{t+1}) − q(z_t) − Δt·F_t is computed entirely from the latent and a parsed constant, so it is a per-generation, proxy-free measurement of physical-law satisfaction (it equals zero exactly when the law holds, not when a learned reward says so); to make this residual a usable, low-variance signal we train R and f_θ with a charge-contrastive objective whose positive pairs are charge-preserving augmentations of a clip (time-reparameterization, rigid camera transform) and whose negatives are same-appearance counterfactuals with an injected velocity discontinuity that perturbs the charge, using a charge-distance similarity (inner product replaced by −‖Δq‖ scaled by temperature λ_c) so the unique loss-minimizing geometry is one in which q is linearly decodable and conservation-violating trajectories are pushed apart. The two legs share machinery rather than needing separate modules: q(z) is the single primitive — the anchor makes it conserved by construction, the sibling makes it cleanly readable and turns its residual into the optimization signal — which is exactly why this reads as one paper.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The two gaps share machinery because the same object (the latent charge q) is simultaneously the thing the anchor must make intrinsic-and-conserved and the thing the sibling must make readable-and-proxy-free; the evidence they are one object is that the conservation residual the sibling optimizes is literally the discrete derivative of the quantity the anchor's integrator conserves, so splitting them into separate modules would double-represent the same state. REGRESSION CHECK (method_lineage): I avoided n4 (NewtonGen's external Neural-ODE predictor feeding a frozen generator), collateral c1 (a differentiable-physics dynamics module bolted alongside), c2 (a PINN-style residual used only as an external penalty), and n8 (an external spectral motion loss); each would re-occupy a node where physics lives OUTSIDE the generator's representation. The unoccupied source I draw on is a structure-preserving integrator acting ON the generator's own latent so conservation is a property of the update rule itself, not a penalty or a side prediction — I considered a pure conservation-penalty design but rejected it because it reduces to c2/n8 (physics softly enforced from outside) and cannot claim by-construction adherence.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: LoRA-fine-tune a 2B latent video-diffusion generator augmented with the symplectic latent integrator, readout R, and charge-contrastive objective on an ordinary (non-physics-curated) video set, then evaluate on PhyWorldBench and T2VPhysBench physical-consistency metrics plus a projectile/collision subset with ground-truth center-of-mass trajectories. If the candidate works, the physical-consistency pass-rate increases over the base generator and over NewtonGen-style external-control baselines, the center-of-mass deviation from a constant-acceleration fit decreases, and — the non-obvious direction — the gain persists on held-out phenomena absent from any physics-clean set, because adherence comes from the integrator's structure rather than from an enumerated force list. Mechanism distinguisher built on the single load-bearing variable, the latent conservation residual ρ_t: negative control replaces the symplectic integrator with a generic learned residual update (its producer ablated) while keeping R and the contrastive objective; the predicted effect is that the downstream physical-consistency pass-rate falls back to the base generator's level (not merely that ρ_t rises), which is the real Popper test since 'ρ_t rose' alone would also be consistent with worse readout calibration. Positive control: a stripped model with only the symplectic integrator + readout and no charge-contrastive objective should recover most of the trajectory-error reduction, identifying the by-construction integrator as the load-bearing mechanism.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:116b156e0c6f","delta":"NewtonGen trains a separate Neural-Newtonian ODE on physics-clean data and feeds predicted states as motion control to a frozen generator; we construct the conserved quantity as a readout of the generator's OWN denoising latent and conserve it by replacing the latent update with a symplectic integrator, so there is no side dynamics network and no physics-clean dataset, and coverage is not confined to its ODE family."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:d077df935592","delta":"WISA injects decomposed physical-category embeddings as soft conditioning that the model may ignore; we make a conserved charge invariant by construction of the latent integrator, so the law holds exactly rather than being softly guided, and coverage is not bounded by an enumerated category set."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416023737","delta":"PhysCorr optimizes a learned dual-reward proxy via DPO, capping adherence at the reward model's accuracy on unseen dynamics; our conservation residual is computed directly from the latent, so the optimized quantity is the physical law itself rather than a learned approximation of it."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W6979224095","delta":"Physics-Guided Motion Loss adds an external frequency-domain loss covering only rigid translation/rotation/scaling; our charge is read from the latent and conserved by integrator construction, spanning any generalized momentum the readout encodes rather than only the rigid spectral modes expressible in their basis."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:116b156e0c6f","what_step_was_missed":"NewtonGen constructs the dynamics as an external Neural-ODE predictor whose outputs are fed to a frozen generator; for our contribution to already exist it would have needed to (a) construct the conserved quantity as a linear readout of the generator's own denoising latent rather than as the output of a separate network, and (b) replace the generator's latent temporal update with a structure-preserving symplectic integrator so the charge is conserved by construction of the update rule. It made neither move — its representation remains appearance-only and the physical state lives outside it — so its adherence stays tied to its ODE family and its physics-clean training distribution."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":272,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"Layer 1 hard floor does not fire: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict is borderline (no Reject lesson is candidate_match: yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat is NOT exact-mechanism overlap (LaWM/Arkhon are latent world models for planning, lacking the candidate's text-to-video diffusion generator, conserved-charge readout, and proxy-free charge-contrastive signal). Layer 2 selects revise because paper_pointed_threat exists AND addressable_via names specific candidate fields (hook, differentiation_from_lit), and this is reinforced by gap_closure_reject_check.entries[0].reject_lessons_evaluated lesson 'Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work ... collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured' being borderline-live against the now-occupied symplectic-latent-integrator locus. recipe_application_check is applied for both legs, so core_mechanism is sound; the fix is repositioning/differentiation, not a mechanism rebuild.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved paper tests whether physical realism must be supplied through a channel external to the generator at all: every leaf inherits from appearance-trained video diffusion the unexamined assumption that the denoising representation cannot itself carry a physical state, and so adds physics as a bolt-on (an external control module, conditioning embeddings, a reward, or a refined prompt) rather than asking whether the generator's own representation could be required to carry the conserved quantity.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"A novelty-boundary collapse — the 'new' locus turns out to be one a prior paper already used (normalization statistics, activation-similarity alignment, pre-encoded semantic concepts), and the work fails to quantify what is genuinely different. Also: offering only a demonstration with no mechanistic account of why the locus carries the signal, which reads as a stacked pipeline of off-the-shelf parts.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a relocated signal is 'stealthier' or 'harder to remove' without defeating an adaptive defender who searches the same new locus leaves the central claim unverified.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"This is a generative-method setting with no adversary; the candidate makes no stealth/removal-robustness claim, so this adversarial-closure lesson has no trigger field."},{"lesson_quoted":"Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work — normalization statistics, activation-similarity losses, semantic concept triggers — collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The anchor's new locus (a structure-preserving/symplectic integrator acting on the model's own latent to conserve a quantity by construction) is exactly the move now published in the latent-world-model line surfaced in collision_hits (LaWM W7161090043 'latent variational integrator'; Arkhon W7122798049 'enforces latent physical conservation laws through symplectic integration'); the candidate's difference is real (text-to-video diffusion + conserved-charge readout + proxy-free contrastive signal on ordinary video) but differentiation_from_lit does not yet make that difference explicit and measured against that line — mitigable by editing the differentiation field, hence borderline not triggered."},{"lesson_quoted":"A defense whose relocation silently depends on a clean reference model or a known anomaly distribution reintroduces precisely the strong assumption the move was supposed to eliminate.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate explicitly removes, rather than reintroduces, the clean-data assumption: it trains on ordinary (non-physics-curated) video and uses no physics-clean dataset or reference model (compute_budget + falsification_prediction both make this load-bearing)."},{"lesson_quoted":"Demonstrating the new locus only on fixed, non-adaptive or outdated baselines while omitting any account of why it works reads as a stacked pipeline of existing components rather than a principled shift.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism supplies the mechanistic WHY C01 step 5 demands — 'a symplectic integrator exactly conserves its discrete momentum map regardless of f_theta, so the charge q is invariant BY CONSTRUCTION' — rather than only demonstrating that it works."},{"lesson_quoted":"Wiring off-the-shelf generators or tools into a new attack setting without a structural reason for the locus change gets judged as engineering integration, not insight.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The locus change is justified structurally by the conservation property of the symplectic update, not by bolting an off-the-shelf tool onto a generator."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf supplies a per-generation signal of physical-law satisfaction that does not route through a learned proxy: the reward-model and metric-based approaches score a learned approximation of physics, so the quantity being optimized can diverge from the law it stands in for and provides no guarantee on dynamics the proxy never saw.","main_pattern":"targeted_self_supervised_objective","sub_pattern":"C17 (Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Sourcing the pairing/alignment signal by composing two already-published components and presenting the composition itself as the contribution; never re-deriving WHY this particular pairing geometry uniquely encodes the targeted property, with no operational definition, no direct probe, and no ablation that isolates the new pairing component from the borrowed machinery.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Concatenating a frozen off-the-shelf predictor's output as an extra input channel injects no novel insight — it reads as combining two published systems regardless of the accuracy gain.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"There is no frozen off-the-shelf predictor; the charge q is a learned linear readout R of the generator's own latent, the central primitive both legs share rather than a bolted-on channel."},{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a representation is 'disentangled' or property-specific without an operational definition, a direct probe, or an isolating ablation leaves the central claim ungrounded and unverifiable.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The targeted property has an operational definition (q(z_t)=R*pool(z_t (x) m_t) and residual rho_t), a direct probe (log rho_t and q-trajectories per generation), and an isolating ablation (positive control = integrator+readout with the charge-contrastive objective removed) — exactly the three the lesson requires."},{"lesson_quoted":"Following reconstruction pretraining with a stock nearest-neighbor contrastive pass reads as stacking existing techniques unless you show the new stage reorganizes signal that could not otherwise arise.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The objective is not reconstruction-then-stock-NN-contrastive; the contrastive pass is purpose-built around charge distance with charge-perturbed counterfactual negatives, not a stock neighbor pass."},{"lesson_quoted":"A hard-pair construction strategy that closely recombines existing mixup/contrastive recipes collapses to 'incremental' the moment the nearest pair-construction baselines are missing from the comparison.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"Negatives are a purpose-built construction (injected velocity-discontinuity, appearance-matched counterfactuals), not a mixup recombination, but the experiment plan's baselines (base generator, NewtonGen-style external control) omit a nearest pair-construction baseline that varies only the charge-distance similarity, so the C17 gain is not yet cleanly attributable — a non-load-bearing experiment-completeness gap surfaceable to Phase 4."},{"lesson_quoted":"Coupling a published clustering head to a published mutual-information objective via a feedback regularizer is judged a careful combination, not a contribution, when neither component nor the coupling is itself new.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"No clustering head or MI objective is coupled; the new primitive is the charge-distance similarity that replaces the inner product, which belongs to neither a borrowed component A nor B."},{"lesson_quoted":"Gains attributed to a new alignment component evaporate under scrutiny when the ablation suite never isolates that component from the borrowed backbone.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The falsification plan isolates the charge-contrastive component via the positive control (integrator+readout, no contrastive) so its contribution is separately identifiable from the LoRA-fine-tuned backbone."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No entry is triggered (no Reject lesson is marked candidate_match: yes), so the hard floor does not fire. The aggregate is driven to borderline by entry 0 (gap C / assumption_audit_and_pivot), where the lesson 'Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work ... collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured' is live: the symplectic-latent-integrator locus is now occupied by the LaWM/Arkhon world-model line and the candidate's differentiation has not yet measured the difference. Entry 1 (gap B / targeted_self_supervised_objective) is borderline only on a missing nearest pair-construction baseline; its decisive Reject triggers (no operational definition, no isolating ablation) are all cleanly avoided."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved paper tests whether physical realism must be supplied through a channel external to the generator at all: every leaf inherits from appearance-trained video diffusion the unexamined assumption that the denoising representation cannot itself carry a physical state, and so adds physics as a bolt-on (an external control module, conditioning embeddings, a reward, or a refined prompt) rather than asking whether the generator's own representation could be required to carry the conserved quantity.","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Name the single representational locus current methods all operate on, state the tacit sufficiency/invariance claim bolted to it, then relocate enforcement to a different locus the field treated as irrelevant — 'relocate the signal', 're-anchor enforcement', 'demonstrate robustness at the new locus' — and supply a mechanistic account of WHY the new locus carries the signal (invariance proof / impossibility bound / root-cause decomposition), not merely evidence THAT it does.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism performs the signature move directly: it names the audited locus ('physics must be enforced at a locus external to the generator — NewtonGen ... a separate Neural-Newtonian ODE, WISA ... conditioning embeddings, PhysCorr ... an output reward') and re-anchors enforcement inside the generator's own latent by 'replacing the latent frame-to-frame update with a structure-preserving (leapfrog/symplectic) integrator ... that splits the latent channels into conjugate position/momentum halves'. The required WHY-account is present and load-bearing: 'because a symplectic integrator exactly conserves its discrete momentum map regardless of f_theta, the charge q read by R is invariant along the generated trajectory BY CONSTRUCTION' — an invariance argument, exactly C01 step 5, rather than a bare demonstration.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf supplies a per-generation signal of physical-law satisfaction that does not route through a learned proxy: the reward-model and metric-based approaches score a learned approximation of physics, so the quantity being optimized can diverge from the law it stands in for and provides no guarantee on dynamics the proxy never saw.","sub_pattern":"C17 (Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Re-engineer the PAIRING/ALIGNMENT geometry so the targeted property is the only thing whose encoding minimizes the loss, the decisive act being to replace or invert a default geometric primitive — 'swapping the inner-product similarity for a property-sensitive one' — converting a generic invariance objective into an explicit geometric constraint that writes the property into the representation.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism enacts the signature substitution verbatim: 'a charge-contrastive objective whose positive pairs are charge-preserving augmentations ... and whose negatives are same-appearance counterfactuals with an injected velocity discontinuity ... using a charge-distance similarity (inner product replaced by -||Delta q|| scaled by temperature lambda_c) so the unique loss-minimizing geometry is one in which q is linearly decodable'. Replacing the inner product with a property-sensitive (-||Delta q||) measure is the single non-obvious primitive C17 step 3 calls for, belonging to neither borrowed component.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries instantiate their cited cluster's signature move in core_mechanism rather than the parent pattern's generic gist: C01's locus-relocation-plus-WHY-account (symplectic conservation as an invariance argument) and C17's inner-product->property-sensitive (-||Delta q||) similarity substitution are each explicitly present."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["assumption_audit_and_pivot","targeted_self_supervised_objective"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions (audit_decomp_supervisor / audit_decomp_prior / audit_decomp_operator) require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; the candidate's main_pattern set contains neither heterogeneous_decomposition nor any 2-way subset that matches, and the companion structural_prior_encoding is not a main_pattern, so no anti-pattern is triggered."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"openalex:W7161090043","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"LaWM (Least Action World Models, 2026-05) operationalizes the Principle of Least Action directly in a learned visual latent space via a 'latent variational integrator': it 'encodes observations into learned generalized coordinates, learns a latent discrete Lagrangian ..., constructs a discrete action functional, and advances prediction by solving the corresponding discrete integration condition. Thus, physical structure is not merely used to score, regularize, or constrain a completed trajectory; it defines [the dynamics].' That is precisely the candidate's anchor thesis (gap C / assumption_audit_and_pivot): physical realism need not be supplied through a channel external to the generator, because a structure-preserving integrator on the model's own latent makes adherence hold by construction (a discrete variational integrator is symplectic, the Lagrangian dual of the candidate's leapfrog update). LaWM therefore falsifies the candidate's literal headline framing that 'no retrieved paper tests whether physical realism must be supplied through a channel external to the generator at all' — the bare structural inversion is no longer untested. Arkhon (openalex:W7122798049, 2026-01) states the symplectic claim even more explicitly ('enforces latent physical conservation laws through symplectic integration') but is a low-credibility, non-peer-reviewed 'unofficial release' Zenodo preprint (marketing bullet points, 'holographic memory architecture'), so it corroborates rather than authoritatively scoops; PH-Dreamer (W7161916777) and Physically Native World Models (W7160360595), both 2026-05, further populate this line. What makes the candidate's claim STAND rather than fall: every paper in this line is a latent WORLD MODEL for embodied planning / model-based RL from visual observations — none is an open-domain text-conditioned video DIFFUSION generator, none builds a conserved-charge READOUT q(z_t)=R*pool(z_t (x) m_t) off the denoising latent, and none supplies the proxy-free charge-CONTRASTIVE self-supervised signal trained on ordinary non-physics-curated video. The candidate's full mechanism is thus not subsumed; only its bare structural-inversion hook is. Timing note: the strongest credible threat (LaWM, 2026-05) is concurrent work (< 2 months before the 2026-06-02 as-of), which per the skill's timing rule is awareness-not-blocking, reinforcing reposition-and-differentiate over abandon.","addressable_via":"Reposition the hook (retire the 'untested inversion / strictly-fewer-components is the whole surprise' framing insofar as it claims the inversion itself is new) and add explicit, measured differentiation_from_lit entries against LaWM (W7161090043) and Arkhon (W7122798049), re-anchoring novelty on the text-to-video-diffusion-specific instantiation: the conserved-charge readout off the denoising latent plus the proxy-free charge-contrastive residual trained on ordinary video, neither of which appears in the latent-world-model line."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"hook + hook_shape_rationale","issue":"paper_pointed_threat (LaWM W7161090043 / Arkhon W7122798049 scoop the bare structural inversion) and gap_closure_reject_check.entries[0] lesson 2 (novelty-boundary collapse at a now-occupied locus)","fix_direction":"Keep the shape-(c) counter-intuitive-minimalism claim (physically-consistent T2V with strictly fewer trained components than NewtonGen — no external dynamics network, no physics-clean dataset), but stop implying the intrinsic-physics inversion ITSELF is unexamined. Re-scope the surprise to: the symplectic-latent-integrator route to by-construction conservation, introduced for embodied-planning latent world models (LaWM/PH-Dreamer/Arkhon), is here transferred for the first time into an open-domain text-conditioned video DIFFUSION generator via a conserved-charge readout and trained proxy-free on ordinary video. Do NOT touch falsification_prediction or compute_budget (kill-switch fields, byte-identical through Phase 3.3)."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat — the latent-world-model symplectic/variational-integrator line is absent from the current four-entry differentiation, so C01 Reject-lesson-2's 'make the difference explicit and measured' is unmet","fix_direction":"Add differentiation entries against openalex:W7161090043 (LaWM) and openalex:W7122798049 (Arkhon) [optionally openalex:W7161916777 PH-Dreamer]: they place a variational/symplectic integrator inside a latent WORLD MODEL for planning/RL from visual observations; we place a symplectic integrator inside a text-conditioned video DIFFUSION generator and add (a) a conserved-charge linear readout off the denoising latent and (b) a proxy-free charge-contrastive objective on ordinary video — neither of which exists in that line; state the measured axis (open-domain T2V physical-consistency benchmarks, not embodied-control rollouts)."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism_steps (baseline/ablation list, step 11-12) + surface in Phase 4 reviewer_concerns_and_responses","issue":"gap_closure_reject_check.entries[1] lesson 4 (nearest pair-construction baseline missing, so the C17 charge-contrastive gain is not yet cleanly attributable)","fix_direction":"Add a nearest pair-construction baseline — a standard contrastive/SSL objective on the same latent that keeps the positive/negative sourcing but uses the default inner-product similarity instead of the -||Delta q|| charge-distance measure — so the gain is attributable to the property-sensitive primitive rather than to contrastive training per se. Minor/non-load-bearing; do NOT edit falsification_prediction (kill-switch frozen); fold the residual concern into Phase 4 reviewer_concerns_and_responses."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"hook + hook_shape_rationale","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Retired the 'untested structural inversion' framing and re-anchored the headline on shape-(c) counter-intuitive minimalism, explicitly crediting the LaWM/Arkhon/PH-Dreamer latent-world-model line and re-scoping novelty to the first transfer of by-construction symplectic-latent conservation into an open-domain text-to-video diffusion generator with a conserved-charge readout and proxy-free ordinary-video training."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added two measured differentiation entries against openalex:W7161090043 (LaWM) and openalex:W7122798049 (Arkhon), stating that both place a variational/symplectic integrator inside an embodied-planning latent world model while we instantiate it in a text-to-video diffusion generator with a denoising-latent charge readout and a proxy-free charge-contrastive objective on ordinary video, measured on T2V physical-consistency benchmarks."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism_steps","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Extended step 11 to add a nearest pair-construction baseline that keeps the positive/negative sourcing but swaps the -||Delta q|| charge-distance similarity for the default inner product, so the C17 gain is attributable to the property-sensitive primitive rather than to contrastive training per se."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Make the Generator Its Own Physicist: Latent Conserved Charges for Text-to-Video\n\n**Method.** Latent Conserved Charges (LCC)\n\n## Motivation\nModern text-to-video (T2V) models — diffusion models that turn a sentence into a video — now produce sharp, smooth clips. But they were trained only to make videos LOOK right, frame by frame. They never learned that the things in the video have to obey physics. So when you ask for something the training videos rarely showed, the motion goes wrong: a ball falls upward, an object suddenly speeds up, momentum appears from nothing. This isn't fixed by adding more training videos — the model simply has no internal notion of a physical state that must follow a law.\n\nEveryone's current fix adds the physics from OUTSIDE the generator. NewtonGen trains a separate little physics simulator and pipes its predictions into a frozen video model. WISA feeds in hints about which physical category applies. PhysCorr trains a reward model that scores how physical a clip looks and nudges the generator toward higher scores. PhyT2V just rewrites the prompt. Each only handles the cases its outside helper was built for, and none of them changes the fact that the video model's own internal representation still carries no physical state.\n\nWhy this is the moment: open video models (Open-Sora, CogVideoX-2B) now let us reach inside and read/modify their internal per-frame state directly. And a recent line of 'world models' for robot planning — LaWM, Arkhon, PH-Dreamer — showed that you can build a special update rule on a model's internal state that makes physics hold automatically, by construction, rather than scoring a finished video. That idea has not yet been brought into open-domain text-to-video. Our move: make the video model's own internal state BE the physical state — read a small conserved quantity off it, use a special 'symplectic' update step that keeps that quantity constant automatically, and measure physics directly from the state (no trained scorer), learning it all from ordinary video.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n*Unchanged scaffolding: expose the backbone, build the foreground mask, generate/evaluate, and run attribution ablations.*\n\n1. Run the pretrained video generator and attach hooks that capture, at a late denoising step where the scene has stabilized, its internal per-frame latent tensors and its text-to-image attention maps (averaged over attention heads and steps to one map per word, at the latent's resolution). Don't change any weights yet.\n   - _Why_: We want to enforce physics on the model's OWN internal state, so first we have to be able to see and touch it.\n2. Find which word in the prompt names the moving object — the grammatical subject's main noun, or the word the model attends to most — then build a per-frame mask by normalizing that word's attention map to 0–1, matching it to the latent's spatial grid, thresholding at 0.5, and keeping the single biggest connected blob.\n   - _Why_: Physics should be measured on the thing that moves, and the model already tells us where that is.\n3. At generation time just generate as usual — conservation is now baked in — and record the residual and the charge trajectory for each clip. Score a clip as physically passing if its residual stays inside a small tolerance (set from the calibration noise level) for every frame and its motion matches the textbook solution; for the projectile/collision tests, make ground-truth trajectories by rendering synthetic clips in a physics engine. Evaluate on PhyWorldBench, T2VPhysBench, and that subset.\n   - _Why_: Because conservation is built into the update, the frames obey the law, and $\\rho _{t}$ is a free per-generation physics readout.\n4. Run ablations that pin each effect to a specific part. Negative control: swap the symplectic step for an ordinary learned update with the same number of parameters and inputs, keeping everything else — physics should fall back to the base generator, showing it was the structure (not extra capacity) that helped. Positive control: keep the integrator and readout but drop the contrastive loss — most of the trajectory-error gain should survive. Also add a baseline that builds the same pairs but scores them with a plain inner product instead of charge-distance.\n   - _Why_: These pin the gains to the right cause: the by-construction integrator for conservation, the charge-distance similarity for readability.\n\n### Latent Physical State\n*Turn the generator's own per-frame latent into a measurable physical-state vector (the conserved charge).*\n\n5. Add a small linear readout R and define the charge as $q(z_{t})=R\\cdot pool(z_{t}\\odot m_{t}),$ where pool is the mask-weighted average of the latent over the foreground (sum the masked latent, divide by the mask area) — a 6-number vector per frame. Calibrate R once by least-squares against center-of-mass and momentum estimated from optical flow, on a few hundred clips, so the numbers mean something physical. 【author decision: a 6-number charge meant as 3D position + 3D momentum cannot be calibrated from ordinary 2D video, where depth and absolute scale are unobservable and optical flow only gives in-plane motion — the authors must either keep the charge to in-plane quantities (2D position + 2D momentum plus angular momentum/energy) calibrated against 2D flow, or add a monocular-depth estimator to recover 3D and accept its error; this choice of what the 6 numbers mean is theirs to make.】\n\n*The latent conserved charge q is a learned linear readout R over the masked spatial average of the per-frame denoising latent $z_{t}$; its 6 components are 3 center-of-mass position coefficients and 3 generalized-momentum components.*\n$$ q(z_t) = R \\, \\mathrm{pool}(z_t \\odot m_t), \\quad R \\in \\mathbb{R}^{d_q \\times d},\\; d_q = 6 \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This turns the model's internal state into an actual physical-state vector we can conserve and measure.\n\n### By-Construction Conservation\n*Replace the temporal latent update with a symplectic integrator so the charge is conserved automatically, relocating physics enforcement inside the generator.*\n\n6. Swap the model's frame-to-frame update for a leapfrog (symplectic) integrator that splits the latent channels into a 'position' half and a 'momentum' half and steps them with a small learned force, in the half-kick / drift / half-kick order; the step size is one over the frame rate. 【author decision: just calling half the channels 'position' and half 'momentum' does not make the dynamics conserve anything — leapfrog only conserves the charge if the force is the slope of a single scalar energy and the split is a true position/momentum pairing; whether the existing latent allows such a split or needs a learned change of coordinates, and which symmetry gives which conserved number, is the core design choice the whole 'conserved by construction' claim depends on and must be decided by the authors.】 If the step is genuinely symplectic, the charge stays exactly constant along the video (when no external field is present) no matter what the force outputs, and that carries through to the decoded frames.\n\n*The temporal latent update is a structure-preserving (leapfrog/symplectic) integrator $\\Phi $ driven by a learned generalized force; because it exactly conserves its discrete momentum map regardless of the force field, the charge q is invariant by construction when the prompt specifies no external field.*\n$$ z_{t+1} = \\Phi_{\\Delta t}\\big(z_t, f_\\theta(z_t, c)\\big), \\qquad q(z_{t+1}) = q(z_t) \\;\\; \\text{when}\\;\\; F_t = 0 \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A symplectic step automatically keeps its momentum quantity constant no matter what the force is — so the charge q stays conserved by construction, not by hoping the model behaves.\n\n### Proxy-Free Signal & Objective\n*Compute the conservation residual directly from the latent and train the charge to be linearly readable from ordinary video via a charge-contrastive objective.*\n\n7. Read any gravity cue from the prompt (default to none, i.e. a closed system) and turn it into the expected per-step change; the mass scale is already set by the step 5 (Add a small linear readout $R and\\dots )$ calibration. Then compute the residual as the change in the charge from one frame to the next minus that expected change, straight from the latents — it is exactly zero when the physical law holds, and needs no learned reward model.\n\n*The conservation residual is the discrete derivative of the charge minus the parsed external-field update; computed entirely from latents and a parsed constant, it equals zero exactly when the physical law holds, with no learned reward.*\n$$ \\rho_t = q(z_{t+1}) - q(z_t) - \\Delta t \\, F_t, \\qquad F_t = m\\,g \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: $\\rho _{t}$ is exactly zero when the physical law holds, giving a direct physics check that needs no trained scorer that could be wrong on new motions.\n8. Train with a contrastive loss built around the charge. Positive pairs are versions of a clip that should keep the same charge (retiming, rigid camera moves); negative pairs are clips that look the same but have a velocity jump spliced in (re-time the second half). Encode every clip through the generator to get its charge, and measure similarity as the negative distance between charges (divided by a temperature set to the typical charge gap in the batch), not as an inner product — this forces the geometry where the charge can be read off linearly.\n\n*The charge-contrastive objective replaces the default inner-product similarity with the negative charge-distance scaled by temperature, so the only loss-minimizing geometry is one in which the charge is linearly decodable and conservation-violating trajectories are pushed apart.*\n$$ \\mathrm{sim}(z, z') = -\\,\\lVert q(z) - q(z') \\rVert \\big/ \\lambda_c \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Using charge-distance as the similarity forces the representation to make the charge cleanly readable — the one thing that minimizes the loss is encoding q.\n9. Fine-tune the generator with lightweight LoRA adapters (rank 16 on its attention and MLP layers), training the readout and force field together, using the charge-contrastive loss plus a small dose (weight 0.1) of the model's normal denoising loss so video quality is preserved — all on ordinary video, not a physics-curated set.\n   - _Why_: One trained system on ordinary video — strictly fewer moving parts than NewtonGen's separate simulator plus a physics-clean dataset.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 让生成器自己当物理学家：面向 Text-to-Video 的隐空间守恒荷\n\n**方法名称.** Latent Conserved Charges (LCC)\n\n## 研究动机\n现代的 text-to-video（T2V，把一句话变成视频的 diffusion 模型）已经能生成清晰流畅的片段。但它们训练时只学了让视频“看起来对”，一帧一帧地像；从没学过画面里的东西必须服从物理。于是一旦你要求训练数据里很少出现的运动，运动就会出错：球往上掉、物体突然加速、动量凭空出现。这不是多喂视频就能修的——模型内部根本没有“必须遵守某条定律的物理状态”这个概念。\n\n现在大家的修法都是从生成器“外面”补物理。NewtonGen 单独训练一个小物理模拟器，把预测喂给冻结的视频模型；WISA 注入“属于哪类物理”的条件提示；PhysCorr 训练一个奖励模型给“看起来有多物理”打分，再把生成器往高分推；PhyT2V 干脆改写 prompt。每种都只能覆盖它那个外部助手被设计来处理的情形，而且都没改变一个事实：视频模型自己的内部表示里仍然不带任何物理状态。\n\n为什么是现在：开源视频模型（Open-Sora、CogVideoX-2B）已经能让我们伸进去直接读/改它逐帧的内部状态；而最近一批面向机器人规划的“world model”（LaWM、Arkhon、PH-Dreamer）证明了——可以在模型内部状态上设计一种特殊更新规则，让物理“由构造自动成立”，而不是给成品视频打分。这个思路还没被搬进开放域的 text-to-video。我们的做法：让视频模型自己的内部状态就是物理状态——从中读出一个小的守恒量，用一种 symplectic 的更新步骤让它自动保持不变，并直接从状态里算出物理是否成立（不需要训练打分器），整套都从普通视频里学出来。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景脚手架\n*不变的支撑部分：暴露 backbone、构造前景掩码、生成/评测、以及做归因消融。*\n\n1. 运行预训练的 latent video-diffusion 生成器(Open-Sora / CogVideoX-2B),在其注意力模块上挂 forward hook,在一个较晚、画面结构已稳定的 denoising step s* 处缓存:(a) 重排成逐帧切片的内部 latent $z_{t} \\in  R^{d\\times h\\times w},$以及 (b) 选定一部分 DiT block 的 cross-attention 张量(对 head 与 denoising step 取平均),得到每个文本 token 在 latent 分辨率下的一张空间图。先不改任何权重。输出逐帧 latent 序列 ${z_{t}}$ 与每个 token 的 attention 图。\n   - _为什么_: 我们要在模型“自己的”内部状态上施加物理，所以先得能看到、能动它。\n2. 确定『运动主体』那个 token:对 prompt 做依存句法分析,取主语名词短语的中心名词(回退方案:取平均 cross-attention 质量最高的名词),并对其各 sub-word token 的图取平均。逐帧把该图 min-max 归一化到 [0,1],双线性缩放对齐到 $z_{t}$ 的空间网格 $h\\times w,$在 $\\tau =0.5$ 处阈值化,并只保留最大连通域,得到二值前景掩码 $m_{t}$。\n   - _为什么_: 物理应该在“会动的那个东西”上度量，而模型已经告诉了我们它在哪。\n3. 推理时正常生成(守恒已内建于更新),逐片段记录残差 $\\rho _{t}$ 与 charge 轨迹,作为无代理(proxy-free)的物理一致性读数。把『物理通过率』定义为:某次生成的 $|\\rho _{t}|$ 在所有帧都落在一个容差带 $\\epsilon $ 内$(\\epsilon $ 取自 第5步（加一个小的线性读出 $R \\in \\dots $） 标定的噪声底),且解码轨迹在容差内吻合解析解,这样的生成所占比例;对抛体/碰撞子集,用物理引擎(PyBullet/Blender)渲染合成片段得到真值质心轨迹。在 PhyWorldBench、T2VPhysBench 及该子集上评测。\n   - _为什么_: 因为守恒被内建进更新里，帧自然服从定律，而 $\\rho _{t}$ 是免费的逐次生成物理读数。\n4. 做能把各效应归因到具体部件的消融。负对照:把 symplectic 步换成参数量、输入$(z_{t}$、$f_\\theta $ 特征、c)都相同、训练方式一致的普通可学习更新,其余不变——预期物理掉回基生成器水平,从而把功劳归于结构本身而非额外容量。正对照:保留 integrator + readout 但去掉 charge-contrastive 损失——预期大部分轨迹误差改善仍在。再加一个基线:沿用 第8步（用围绕守恒荷的对比损失训练） 的样本构造,但用默认内积而非 charge 距离作相似度,以隔离对守恒荷敏感的那个原语。\n   - _为什么_: 这些把收益钉到正确原因上：守恒靠的是 by-construction 积分子，可读性靠的是 charge 距离相似度。\n\n### 隐空间物理状态\n*把生成器自己逐帧的隐变量变成一个可度量的物理状态向量（守恒荷）。*\n\n5. 加一个小的线性读出 $R \\in  R^{6\\times d},$定义守恒荷 $q(z_{t})=R\\cdot pool(z_{t}\\odot m_{t}):$其中 pool 是在前景上的掩码加权平均(把掩码后的 latent 求和,再除以掩码面积),每帧得到一个 6 维向量。用 optical flow 估出的质心与动量作目标,在几百个片段上对 R 做一次岭回归(ridge least-squares)标定,使这些数有物理含义;R 随后在 第9步（用轻量 $LoRA\\dots $） 联合微调。【作者需决定:把这 6 个数当成 3D 质心位置 + 3D 动量,无法从单目 2D 视频标定——2D 视频里深度和绝对尺度不可观测,optical flow 只给出平面内速度场;作者要么把守恒荷限制在可观测的平面内量(2D 质心 + 2D 动量,再加角动量/动能凑满 6 维)并用 2D 光流目标标定,要么引入单目深度估计把光流抬到 3D 并自行承担其误差;这 6 个轴的物理含义与标定目标是作者要定的选择,无法从 latent 推出。】\n\n*守恒荷 q 是对逐帧去噪隐变量 $z_{t}$ 做前景掩码 $m_{t}$ 加权空间平均后、再经可学习线性读出 R 得到的小向量；其 6 维由 3 个质心位置系数与 3 个广义动量分量组成。*\n$$ q(z_t) = R \\, \\mathrm{pool}(z_t \\odot m_t), \\quad R \\in \\mathbb{R}^{d_q \\times d},\\; d_q = 6 \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这把模型内部状态变成一个真正可守恒、可度量的物理状态向量。\n\n### 由构造守恒\n*把时间更新替换为 symplectic 积分子，使 charge 自动守恒，从而把物理执行搬进生成器内部。*\n\n6. 把模型的逐帧更新替换为 leapfrog(symplectic)积分子 $z_{t+1}=\\Phi _\\Delta t(z_{t}, f_\\theta (z_{t},c)):$把 latent 通道分成 position(q)与 momentum(p)两半,按标准的 kick-drift-kick 顺序推进$——p_{t+1/2}=p_{t}+(\\Delta t/2)f_\\theta (q_{t},c)$;$q_{t+1}=q_{t}+\\Delta t\\cdot p_{t+1/2}$;$p_{t+1}=p_{t+1/2}+(\\Delta t/2)f_\\theta (q_{t+1},c)$;$\\Delta t=1/fps,f_\\theta $ 是一个轻量的可学习广义力场。【作者需决定:仅仅把一半通道叫『位置』、另一半叫『动量』并不能让动力学守恒任何东西——leapfrog 只有在力是某个标量势的梯度 $f_\\theta =- \\nabla _{q} V_\\phi (q,c)$、且这种拆分是真正的正则坐标配对时,才会守恒该守恒荷的动量映射;预训练 VAE latent 是否允许这样的拆分、还是需要一个可学习的正则坐标变换,以及 $V_\\phi $ 的哪个对称性经 Noether 定理给出哪个守恒分量,是『由构造守恒』这一主张所依赖的承重参数化,须由作者敲定。】只要这一步是真正 symplectic 的,无论力输出多大,守恒荷 q 在整段视频里(无外场时)都精确不变,并传导到解码出的画面。\n\n*隐变量的时间更新被替换为保结构（leapfrog/symplectic）积分子 $\\Phi $，由可学习广义力 $f_\\theta $ 驱动；由于无论力场如何它都精确守恒其离散动量映射，当 prompt 未指定外力时 q 由构造即守恒。*\n$$ z_{t+1} = \\Phi_{\\Delta t}\\big(z_t, f_\\theta(z_t, c)\\big), \\qquad q(z_{t+1}) = q(z_t) \\;\\; \\text{when}\\;\\; F_t = 0 \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: symplectic 步无论力如何都自动保持其动量量不变——于是 q 由构造守恒，而不是寄希望于模型自觉。\n\n### 免代理信号与目标\n*直接从隐变量算守恒残差，并用 charge-contrastive 目标让 charge 从普通视频里可线性读出。*\n\n7. 从 prompt 中解析外场线索(如『在月球上』『水下』),用一个小查找表映射成重力值,默认无外场即 $F_{t}=0($封闭系统);$F_{t}=m\\cdot g$ 中的质量尺度 m 就是 第5步（加一个小的线性读出 $R \\in \\dots $） 标定已固定的动量尺度,因此 $F_{t}$ 与守恒荷同单位。然后直接用 latent 算守恒残差 $\\rho _{t}=q(z_{t+1})- q(z_{t})- \\Delta t\\cdot F_{t}:$它完全由 latent 和解析出的常数得到,物理定律成立时恰为 0,不需要任何可学习的 reward 模型。\n\n*守恒残差 $\\rho _{t}$ 为守恒荷的离散导数减去解析得到的外力项 $F_{t}$；它完全由隐变量与解析常数算出，物理定律成立时恰为 0，不依赖任何学习到的奖励代理。*\n$$ \\rho_t = q(z_{t+1}) - q(z_t) - \\Delta t \\, F_t, \\qquad F_t = m\\,g \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 物理定律成立时 $\\rho _{t}$ 恰为 0，给出一个不需要训练打分器（打分器在新运动上可能出错）的直接物理校验。\n8. 用围绕守恒荷的对比损失训练。正样本是应保持同一 charge 的视图(重定时、刚性相机移动);负样本是外观相同但拼入了速度跳变的片段(把后半段重定时)。把每个视图经生成器的 VAE + 前向扩散编码成 z,用 第5步（加一个小的线性读出 $R \\in \\dots $） 读出其 charge,并用『负的 charge 距离』而非内积作相似度 $sim(z,z')=- \\| q(z)- q(z')\\| /\\lambda _{c},$温度 $\\lambda _{c}$ 取该 batch 内 $\\| \\Delta q\\| $ 的中位数;如此唯一的损失最小几何就是 q 可被线性解码、且违反守恒的轨迹被推开。\n\n*charge-contrastive 目标把默认内积相似度替换为按温度 $\\lambda _{c}$ 缩放的负 charge 距离，使得唯一的损失最小几何即为 q 可线性解码、且违反守恒的轨迹被推远的几何。*\n$$ \\mathrm{sim}(z, z') = -\\,\\lVert q(z) - q(z') \\rVert \\big/ \\lambda_c \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 用 charge 距离当相似度，逼迫表示把 charge 干净地读出来——唯一能最小化损失的就是编码 q。\n9. 用轻量 LoRA 适配器微调生成器(在 DiT 的 attention 与 MLP 投影上,rank r=16),与读出 R 和力场 $f_\\theta $ 一起训练,损失为 charge-contrastive 损失加一小份(权重 $\\beta =0.1)$模型原本的去噪损失以保住视频保真度——全程用普通视频集,而非物理精修集。其他预训练权重冻结。输出:一个 latent 更新由构造守恒 q、且表示线性编码 q 的生成器。\n   - _为什么_: 一个在普通视频上训练的系统——比 NewtonGen 的独立模拟器加物理精修数据集，部件严格更少。\n\n"},{"id":"02","run_dir":"run_prompt02_gigavoxel","index":2,"title":"Read Correspondence Off a Constructed Invariant: Search-Free Gigavoxel Multimodal Registration","title_zh":"从构造不变量读出对应：面向 gigavoxel 多模态配准的免搜索方法","method_name":"Constructed-Invariant Search-Free Registration (CISR)","hook":"Every learned multimodal registrar still searches image/descriptor space for the transform — MASR-Net maximizes a learned-descriptor cosine, MR-US a dense correlation pyramid, CORE an engineered coarse-to-fine cascade — yet we establish correspondence with NO image-space matching score at all and with a matching operator whose cost is sub-linear in voxel count, by requiring homologous anatomy to receive the same code by construction of a contrast-equivariant coordinate field and then reading the transform off that invariant.","anchor_pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","anchor_pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","domain_category":"Healthcare & Scientific ML","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved paper tests whether cross-modality correspondence must be searched in image/descriptor space at all: every leaf inherits from the mono-modal registration ancestor the unexamined assumption that a transformation is found by maximizing an image-space similarity (intensity, learned descriptor, or feature correlation) between fixed and moving voxels, and so attacks the modality gap by engineering a better image-space similarity or a cheaper way to evaluate it, rather than asking whether","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"structural_prior_encoding","how_closed":"Closed by pivoting the identifiability assumption (C05): the audited assumption is that cross-modality correspondence is recoverable only by maximizing an image/descriptor-space similarity, and we substitute a DIFFERENT kind of constraint — a contrast-group equivariance the representation satisfies by construction — that carries the same identifying power, re-proving that the transform is recoverable up to the registration ambiguity class from the invariant alone with NO matching score; the companion structural_prior_encoding ships the deliverable as a contrast-equivariant coordinate field Phi whose value at a voxel is a canonical anatomical coordinate invariant to the modality/contrast transform by construction, so correspondence is read off where Phi agrees rather than searched.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes cross-modality correspondence cost sub-linear in voxel count while preserving full-resolution accuracy: every learned-correspondence method evaluates a dense similarity or correlation volume on the full (or lightly downsampled) feature grid, so at gigavoxel scale either memory/time explode (correlation-pyramid and transformer methods are confined to coarse levels) or the method retreats to an engineered coarse-to-fine cascade whose fine result is not certified to be the r","pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","sub_pattern":"C14 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by substituting the dense all-pairs matching operator (C14): because correspondence is now agreement of the constructed invariant Phi rather than an O(N) dense descriptor/correlation volume over N voxels, the all-pairs cosine/correlation operator (the cost bottleneck that confines MR-US/C2RF to coarse levels and forces CORE's uncertified cascade) is replaced by a nearest-invariant lookup over a locality-sensitive hash of Phi whose expected cost is sub-linear in N, and the preserved property — that the recovered transform equals the full-resolution dense-matching transform — is proved via a Lipschitz bound on Phi rather than re-evaluated densely, certifying full-resolution accuracy without a full-resolution matching pass.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"multimodal deformable registration of gigavoxel-scale medical / pathology images","n_papers":44,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":21},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":15,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"ChebyRegNet: An Unsupervised Deep Learning Technique for Deformable Medical Image Registration"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Modality-Agnostic Structural Image Representation Learning for Deformable Multi-Modality Medical Image Registration"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Deep Learning in Medical Image Registration: Magic or Mirage?"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Retrospective Comparison of Geometrical Accuracy among Atlas-based Auto-segmentation, Deep Learning Auto-segmentation, and Deformable Image Registration in the Treatment Replanning for Adaptive Radiotherapy of Head-and-Neck Cancer"},{"source":"openalex","title":"OTMorph: Unsupervised Multi-Domain Abdominal Medical Image Registration Using Neural Optimal Transport"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Medical image registration via neural fields"}],"more":9},{"year":2025,"n":21,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Deep-TLBO: Achieving Robust Deformable Medical Image Registration Leveraging Deep Learning and Teaching Learning-Based Optimization"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"H-UDMIR: A Hybrid Unsupervised Deep Learning Framework for Deformable Medical Image Registration"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A Physics-Informed Deep Learning Deformable Medical Image Registration Method Based on Neural ODEs"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Deep Learning Approaches for Deformable Medical Image Registration: An In‐Depth Review and Analysis"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Cyclic deformable medical image registration with prompt: deep fusion of diffeomorphic and transformer methods"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Assessment of contour accuracy in head and neck replanning: Deep learning trained model compared with deformable image registration propagation technique."}],"more":15},{"year":2026,"n":8,"papers":[{"source":"arxiv","title":"Warm-Started Reinforcement Learning for Iterative 3D/2D Liver Registration"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Monodense Deep Neural Model for Determining Item Price Elasticity"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Vision-Language Controlled Deep Unfolding for Joint Medical Image Restoration and Segmentation"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"End-to-End LiDAR optimization for 3D point cloud registration"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Fast, Unsupervised Framework for Registration Quality Assessment of Multi-stain Histological Whole Slide Pairs"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"CT-Guided Spatially-varying Regularization for Voxel-Wise Deformable Whole-Body PET Registration"}],"more":2}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":14,"share":0.318},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":10,"share":0.227},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":9,"share":0.205},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":8,"share":0.182},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":7,"share":0.159},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":4,"share":0.091},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":4,"share":0.091},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":3,"share":0.068}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Learned multimodal registration establishes cross-modality correspondence by mapping each image into a modality-agnostic descriptor space and then maximizing a dense similarity between fixed and moving descriptors evaluated at (near) full resolution: MASR-Net (semanticscholar:fe56091a6b8423f3866faa50899dd2eaffde7b42) learns a Deep Neighbourhood Self-similarity descriptor whose per-voxel cosine similarity replaces intensity-based metrics, and correlation-volume methods such as the MR-US multilevel pyramid (arxiv:2602.06288v2) and C2RF's contrastive commonality mining (openalex:W4409463789) build the matching signal from a dense feature correlation. Two coupled failures follow at gigavoxel scale. First, the modality-invariance is only softly learned — the descriptor is trained to be discriminative on the training distribution but carries no guarantee that two voxels at the same anatomy receive the same code, so on an unseen modality pair or stain the correspondence degrades with no recourse (semanticscholar:8192fdb922679eff02d1ec2b1ac986e810be7c2a shows learned registration tracks the per-pixel-intensity mutual information of the pair and predicts failure exactly when that MI is low, i.e. the multimodal regime). Second, the dense full-resolution similarity makes both memory and time scale with voxel count, which is why transformer/correlation methods are confined to downsampled feature resolutions (arxiv:2602.06288v2, openalex:W4402715997) and why whole-slide pixel-wise validation is reported as billions-of-pixels-expensive (arxiv:2602.04046v1); a correspondence committed at a coarse level carries no construction-level consistency that it survives refinement to the gigavoxel grid.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:fe56091a6b8423f3866faa50899dd2eaffde7b42","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"MASR-Net learns a Modality-Agnostic Deep Structural Representation (Deep Neighbourhood Self-similarity descriptor) via anatomy-aware contrastive learning under non-linear intensity transforms, so the cross-modality matching cost is a cosine similarity in a learned contrast-invariant descriptor space rather than a raw-intensity metric. Its residue: the descriptor is computed densely on the full 3D feature grid (4-level encoder-decoder, max stride 8) and the invariance is a soft contrastive property learned on the training distribution — there is no by-construction guarantee that homologous voxels map to the same code on an unseen modality pair, and no scale-consistency that a coarse-level correspondence is preserved when refined to the native gigavoxel resolution, so it neither bounds the gigavoxel matching cost nor certifies invariance off-distribution."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.06288v2","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"The Learn2Reg-2025 MR-US method builds correspondence from a multilevel feature correlation pyramid optimized unsupervised across the MR↔US appearance gap. Its residue: the dense correlation volume is the cost bottleneck, so it is evaluated only at coarse pyramid levels and gives a single fixed MR-US pairing with no mechanism that keeps the coarse alignment consistent at full resolution and no path to >2 modalities or gigavoxel grids."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4409463789","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"C2RF jointly registers and fuses multimodal images by mining a shared commonality representation with a contrastive objective. Its residue: the commonality is a soft contrastive embedding evaluated patch-locally and couples registration to a fusion head, so invariance is again learned-not-constructed and the patch-local evaluation does not scale to billions of voxels."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416022609","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"CORE registers multi-stain whole-slide (gigapixel) images coarse-to-fine using prompt-based tissue masks and a frozen pretrained feature extractor for accelerated dense matching. Its residue: it manages gigapixel cost by engineering a coarse-to-fine pipeline around an off-the-shelf extractor (2D WSI only), but the cross-stain invariance comes from the borrowed extractor with no construction-level guarantee, and the coarse-to-fine cascade has no formal consistency that the cell-level result is the refinement of the coarse one."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:8192fdb922679eff02d1ec2b1ac986e810be7c2a","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Magic-or-Mirage characterizes when learning beats optimization for registration, tying learned-method performance to the per-pixel-intensity mutual information of the pair. Its residue: it diagnoses that learned registration fails precisely in the low-MI multimodal regime but stops at the characterization — it supplies no operator that restores correspondence quality where MI is low, so the multimodal failure it predicts is left open."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"multimodal deformable registration of gigavoxel-scale medical / pathology images","venue":"MICCAI/IPMI/CVPR-tier medical imaging + ML","time":"2026","data":["whole-slide multi-stain pathology image pairs (H&E / IHC / IF, ~billions of pixels per slide; ANHIR, ACROBAT)","multimodal volumetric scans (CT/MRI/PET, whole-body; Learn2Reg, R-D-Reg)","ordinary (non-landmark-annotated) multimodal image pairs"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"deep learning for medical image registration + representation learning","preference":"both","baseline":"MASR-Net (modality-agnostic structural representation), C2RF, MR-US correlation-pyramid, CORE multi-stain WSI engine, VoxelMorph/TransMorph-class learned registration","limitation":"cross-modality correspondence is learned as a dense similarity in a descriptor space evaluated at full resolution, so the matching cost scales with voxel count and the modality-invariance is only softly learned with no consistency guarantee across resolution levels — both of which break at gigavoxel scale","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","compute","expertise","preference","data"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The single shared object both legs read from and write to is the contrast-equivariant canonical-coordinate field Phi_theta: for a voxel x in volume V of modality channel s, Phi_theta(V, s)(x) in R^{d_c} (d_c=8) is a learned code, and the construction guarantees Phi_theta(T_alpha(V), s')(x) = Phi_theta(V, s)(x) for every contrast transform T_alpha in a parametrized contrast group G (per-channel monotone intensity remap + bias-field-style smooth multiplicative shading + additive Gaussian noise, alpha its parameters) — i.e. homologous anatomy receives the SAME code regardless of modality/stain, by construction not by soft training. Phi_theta is made exactly G-invariant by a frame-averaging / canonicalization layer: a small canonicalizer c_psi(local patch) predicts the contrast-group element that maps the patch to a fixed reference contrast, the patch is mapped by its inverse before the encoder f_theta, so f_theta only ever sees reference-contrast input and Phi = f_theta(c_psi^{-1} . patch) is invariant to G by the standard canonicalization identity (this is the structural_prior_encoding/C16-style equivariant-operator construction, with G the contrast group rather than a spatial symmetry). Anchor leg (C05 audit + structural_prior_encoding companion): we audit the field-wide identifiability assumption — every leaf (MASR-Net's DNS cosine, MR-US's correlation pyramid, C2RF's commonality, CORE's frozen-extractor matching) presumes the transform is recovered by maximizing an image/descriptor-space similarity score — and pivot to the substitute condition that exact G-invariance of Phi ALONE identifies the correspondence: two voxels are homologous iff Phi agrees, so the deformation u is recovered as u(x) = argmin_y ||Phi_F(x) - Phi_M(x+y)|| with the matching done in invariant-code space, recoverable up to the diffeomorphic-deformation ambiguity class without any image-space matching score. Because Phi is G-invariant by construction, this holds for an unseen modality/stain pair as long as that pair's contrast lies in G (the off-distribution claim the deferred invariance gap validates), curing exactly the low-MI regime that Magic-or-Mirage (semanticscholar:8192fdb922679eff02d1ec2b1ac986e810be7c2a) shows is where learned descriptors fail. Sibling leg (C14 operator substitution): the dense matching of Phi_F to Phi_M is the same all-pairs cost MASR-Net/MR-US pay; we substitute it with an invariant-lookup operator — Phi_M is indexed once into a multi-probe locality-sensitive hash (LSH) keyed on the d_c-dim code, and each fixed voxel's match is a sub-linear approximate-nearest-code query — and we PROVE the substitute preserves the full-resolution correspondence: since the canonicalizer makes Phi L-Lipschitz in voxel coordinate (L bounded by the encoder's spectral norm, measured once), an LSH recall radius r and a coarse-to-fine grid spacing h with L*h < r certify that the sub-linear lookup returns the same argmin the dense full-resolution match would, so the coarse correspondence IS the refinement of the fine one by a triangle-inequality bound (the construction-level scale-consistency CORE lacks). The two legs share machinery rather than needing separate modules: Phi is the single primitive — the anchor makes it exactly G-invariant so correspondence is identifiable from it without a search, the sibling exploits that the same Phi is hashable so the match is sub-linear with a Lipschitz certificate — which is why this reads as one paper.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The two gaps share machinery because the same object Phi is simultaneously what the anchor must make exactly-invariant-and-search-free and what the sibling must make cheaply-matchable: the Lipschitz constant the sibling's lookup certificate needs is a property of the very canonicalizer that delivers the anchor's by-construction invariance, so splitting them would double-build the encoder. Alternatives considered and rejected: (a) a soft contrastive descriptor with an invariance penalty — rejected because it regresses to MASR-Net n4 / unify-into-shared-representation collateral (invariance learned-not-constructed, the occupied source Phase 2.1 forbade); (b) a frozen pretrained extractor for cross-stain codes — rejected as CORE n7; (c) keeping dense correlation but pruning it (sparse keypoints) — rejected as collateral c2 and as still an image-space matching score. REGRESSION CHECK (method_lineage): the cure lands on collateral c3 (by-construction/equivariant representation) which the lineage marks as a recognized family but NEVER instantiated as modality-invariance for registration with a scale-consistency certificate, so the delta is exactly that instantiation; I avoided n0/n1 (intensity/MI image-space metrics), n2 (hand-crafted MIND descriptor — Phi is exactly-invariant and learned, not a fixed descriptor field), n3/n4 (image-space-similarity-trained learning), n5/n6 (dense correlation), n7 (frozen-extractor cascade), n8 (per-pair instance optimization), and collateral c1 (heuristic pyramid — our coarse-to-fine carries a Lipschitz certificate, not a heuristic).","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: train Phi (canonicalizer + encoder) with the contrast-group homology loss on Learn2Reg multimodal volumes and ANHIR/ACROBAT multi-stain WSIs, register held-out pairs via the LSH invariant-lookup, and measure target registration error (TRE) / landmark error, Dice, and peak memory + wall-clock as a function of voxel count N. If the candidate works, TRE matches or beats MASR-Net and the MR-US correlation pyramid at full resolution while peak memory and wall-clock grow sub-linearly in N rather than linearly (the non-obvious direction: accuracy is RETAINED, not traded, as resolution increases to the native gigavoxel grid, because matching is a hash query not a dense scan), and TRE on an unseen modality/stain pair whose contrast lies in G stays near in-distribution TRE rather than collapsing in the low-MI regime Magic-or-Mirage flags. Mechanism distinguisher built on the single load-bearing variable, the empirical contrast-invariance gap delta_G = E_x,alpha ||Phi(T_alpha(V))(x) - Phi(V)(x)|| (the residual disagreement of homologous codes under the contrast group, ideally 0 by construction): negative control replaces the canonicalizer c_psi with identity (its producer ablated), which destroys exact invariance and inflates delta_G; the predicted effect is that the downstream held-out-modality TRE rises back to the soft-descriptor baseline's level (NOT merely that delta_G rises) — this is the real Popper test, since 'delta_G rose' alone would also be consistent with worse code calibration, whereas the claim is that exact-by-construction invariance is what carries off-distribution correspondence. Positive control: a stripped model with only the canonicalizer + nearest-code lookup and no discriminative homology head should recover most of the off-distribution TRE retention, identifying the by-construction invariance as the load-bearing mechanism.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:fe56091a6b8423f3866faa50899dd2eaffde7b42","delta":"MASR-Net learns a Deep Neighbourhood Self-similarity descriptor whose per-voxel cosine similarity, evaluated densely over the full 3D grid, is the matching score, and its invariance is a soft contrastive property of the training distribution; we construct Phi to be EXACTLY invariant to a parametrized contrast group by a canonicalization layer (invariance by construction, not learned) and recover the transform by nearest-invariant lookup with NO cosine-similarity matching score and sub-linear cost, which MASR-Net's dense-descriptor formulation does not produce."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.06288v2","delta":"The MR-US method builds correspondence from a dense multilevel feature-correlation pyramid (cost bottleneck confining it to coarse levels, single MR-US pairing); we eliminate the correlation volume entirely — correspondence is agreement of a constructed invariant resolved by LSH — and certify the coarse match equals the full-resolution one via a Lipschitz bound, a scale-consistency guarantee its heuristic pyramid lacks."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416022609","delta":"CORE manages gigapixel cost by engineering a coarse-to-fine cascade around a frozen pretrained extractor with no certificate that the cell-level result is the refinement of the coarse one, and its cross-stain invariance is borrowed from the extractor; we replace the cascade with a single hashable invariant carrying a triangle-inequality refinement certificate and construct (not borrow) the cross-stain invariance, extending from 2D WSI to 3D volumes."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4409463789","delta":"C2RF mines a soft contrastive commonality embedding coupled to a fusion head and evaluated patch-locally (abstract-only inference: lit_results abstract for this paper is empty, judged from Phase 1 closest_adjacent summary); we make the shared code exactly contrast-group-invariant by construction and decouple registration from fusion, so invariance is certified rather than mined and matching scales sub-linearly past the patch-local regime."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:8192fdb922679eff02d1ec2b1ac986e810be7c2a","delta":"Magic-or-Mirage characterizes that learned registration fails exactly in the low-per-pixel-MI multimodal regime but supplies no operator to restore correspondence there; our by-construction contrast-group invariance is precisely an operator that holds where per-pixel MI is low, converting their open characterization into a cure with a measurable invariance-gap distinguisher."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:fe56091a6b8423f3866faa50899dd2eaffde7b42","what_step_was_missed":"MASR-Net constructs the cross-modality match as a learned descriptor whose cosine similarity is maximized densely; for our contribution to already exist it would have needed (a) to make the descriptor EXACTLY invariant to a parametrized contrast group via a canonicalization/frame-averaging construction rather than a soft anatomy-aware contrastive loss, so homologous codes coincide by construction off-distribution, and (b) to recover the transform as a nearest-invariant lookup with a Lipschitz-certified sub-linear matching operator instead of a dense full-resolution cosine field. It made neither move — its invariance stays soft and its matching stays dense at full resolution — so it neither certifies off-distribution correspondence nor bounds the gigavoxel matching cost."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":141,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"Layer 1 hard floor does not fire: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict is borderline (no Reject lesson is candidate_match: yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat (arxiv:2603.26393v1) is NOT exact-mechanism overlap — it shares the contrast-agnostic motivation but uses a frozen backbone + test-time instance optimization rather than by-construction invariance, search-free read-off, and a sub-linear certified operator. Layer 2 selects revise because (i) paper_pointed_threat exists AND addressable_via names a specific candidate field (differentiation_from_lit), and (ii) gap_closure_reject_check.entries[0]'s C05 lesson 'imposing structural constraints without proving they are SUFFICIENT for recovery' is borderline-live on a load-bearing property (the audit leg's identifiability claim) and entries[1]'s C14 baseline-myopia lesson is borderline-live on the operator leg's attribution. recipe_application_check is applied for both legs, so core_mechanism is sound; the fix is sufficiency-argument surfacing, a cheaper-family baseline, and added differentiation, not a mechanism rebuild.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved paper tests whether cross-modality correspondence must be searched in image/descriptor space at all: every leaf inherits from the mono-modal registration ancestor the unexamined assumption that a transformation is found by maximizing an image-space similarity (intensity, learned descriptor, or feature correlation) between fixed and moving voxels, and so attacks the modality gap by engineering a better image-space similarity or a cheaper way to evaluate it, rather than asking whether the correspondence could be carried by a quantity that is not an image-space matching score at all.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The signature failure is an identifiability claim that outruns its proof: papers fail when the pivoted assumption was not actually load-bearing (the new setting is a straightforward union of two existing frameworks), or when structural constraints are imposed to claim disentanglement without proving they are SUFFICIENT for recovery, leaving the result indistinguishable from a post-hoc heuristic.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Stacking two established frameworks and re-proving identifiability of the union reads as incremental unless the pivoted assumption was genuinely load-bearing and the union admits a regime neither framework could reach alone.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate does not stack two frameworks: the pivoted assumption (correspondence recoverable only by an image-space matching score) is genuinely load-bearing — every leaf n4-n8 rests on it — and the contrast-equivariant invariant admits the off-distribution / low-MI regime (Magic-or-Mirage's failure zone) that no image-space-similarity method reaches."},{"lesson_quoted":"Advertising an identifiability or 'consistency' property while the proof omits the decisive object — never proving latent identifiability, or excluding part of the model from the guarantee — collapses the contribution the moment a reviewer checks the theorem.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"core_mechanism asserts the deformation is 'recoverable up to the diffeomorphic-deformation ambiguity class without any image-space matching score' but the decisive object — that exact G-invariance of Phi ALONE identifies homology (Phi-agreement ⇒ same anatomy) — is stated as a substitute condition, not yet exhibited as a sufficiency proof; this is a load-bearing-but-mitigable gap (surface the sufficiency argument explicitly), hence borderline not triggered."},{"lesson_quoted":"Imposing structural constraints to claim interpretability or disentanglement without proving those constraints are sufficient for recovery leaves the result indistinguishable from a post-hoc heuristic.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The exact-G-invariance constraint is imposed by the canonicalizer, and the falsification's negative control (canonicalizer→identity inflates delta_G and collapses off-distribution TRE) does empirically isolate the constraint as load-bearing, but the candidate has not stated WHY invariance is sufficient (not merely necessary) for correspondence — the same sufficiency gap as the prior lesson, surfaceable to Phase 4 rather than a hard trigger."},{"lesson_quoted":"Proving identifiability conditions the algorithm neither enforces nor verifies creates a theory-practice disconnect that undermines both the soundness and the significance of the claim.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The algorithm explicitly enforces the condition (the canonicalization layer makes Phi exactly G-invariant by construction) AND verifies it (delta_G is the measured load-bearing variable in falsification_prediction), so the C05 step-5 theory-practice closure the lesson demands is present."},{"lesson_quoted":"Errors in the dependency or conditional-independence bookkeeping (mislabeling an independence, opening a collider) void the central theorem even when the empirical numbers look reasonable.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate's guarantee is an exact group-invariance identity (canonicalization), not a conditional-independence / latent-graph argument, so there is no independence-bookkeeping surface for this error mode to fire on."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes cross-modality correspondence cost sub-linear in voxel count while preserving full-resolution accuracy: every learned-correspondence method evaluates a dense similarity or correlation volume on the full (or lightly downsampled) feature grid, so at gigavoxel scale either memory/time explode (correlation-pyramid and transformer methods are confined to coarse levels) or the method retreats to an engineered coarse-to-fine cascade whose fine result is not certified to be the refinement of the coarse one — the outcome that is missing is a correspondence whose compute does not grow with the native voxel grid yet whose alignment is exact at that grid.","main_pattern":"architectural_operator_substitution","sub_pattern":"C14 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail when the surrogate is a cheaper-but-equivalent reparameterization with no load-bearing consequence (preservation proven yet never connected to a capability the original lacked), when the operator swap co-varies with a confound that no ablation isolates, or via baseline myopia — comparing only against the expensive original while ignoring the established family of cheaper surrogates.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"If a confound (positional encoding, extra capacity, added multi-scale features) co-varies with your operator swap, the headline conclusion becomes unattributable and reviewers reject it as opportunistic.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The falsification's dense-correlation-vs-LSH ablation (step 11(ii)) varies ONLY the matching operator while holding Phi fixed, so the sub-linearity/accuracy claim is attributed to the operator substitution rather than to added capacity or multi-scale features."},{"lesson_quoted":"Comparing your cheaper operator only against the expensive original — never against the existing family of cheaper alternatives — makes it read as a redundant reparameterization rather than an advance.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"method_lineage already names the cheaper-matching family (collateral c2, sparse keypoint matching) as recognized prior art, yet the falsification baselines (MASR-Net, MR-US correlation pyramid — both dense/expensive originals) do not include a sparse-keypoint or coarse-only cheaper surrogate, so the LSH operator's advantage over the EXISTING cheaper family is not yet measured; load-bearing for the C14 advance claim, addressable by adding a baseline — borderline."},{"lesson_quoted":"An equivalence or approximation proof with no downstream consequence is dismissed as formalizing what the field already assumed to be true.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The Lipschitz/triangle-inequality certificate has a real downstream consequence the dense original lacks — it guarantees the coarse correspondence IS the refinement of the fine one (the scale-consistency CORE's heuristic cascade cannot certify), so the proof buys a capability, not a restatement."},{"lesson_quoted":"Bolting together established cheaper components without a single unifying load-bearing insight invites the 'combination of existing modules / engineering report' rejection.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"LSH is not bolted on arbitrarily: it is usable ONLY because Phi is exactly invariant (the anchor's construction), so the unifying insight — correspondence as agreement of a constructed invariant makes the match hashable — ties the operator swap to the audit leg rather than stacking modules."},{"lesson_quoted":"Failing to evaluate in the exact regime your substitution targets — long sequences, large scale, high representational order — leaves its core promise untested and the claim unverifiable.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The falsification explicitly measures memory/wall-clock as a function of voxel count up to native gigavoxel WSI grids (ANHIR/ACROBAT) — the exact large-scale regime the sub-linear substitution is meant to rescue."},{"lesson_quoted":"A contrived or artificially motivated setup, paired with ablations that fail to isolate the proposed mechanism, leaves the observed gains attributable to incidental added capacity rather than the substitution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The setup is the user's stated gigavoxel multimodal registration task on standard benchmarks (Learn2Reg/ANHIR/ACROBAT) and the dense-vs-LSH ablation isolates the substitution, so gains are not attributable to incidental capacity."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No entry is triggered (no Reject lesson is candidate_match: yes), so the hard floor does not fire. Entry 0 (gap subtractive / assumption_audit_and_pivot) is borderline on the C05 lessons 'advertising identifiability while the decisive object is never established' and 'structural constraints imposed without proving sufficiency' — the candidate enforces and verifies exact invariance but has not exhibited the sufficiency proof that invariance ALONE identifies homology. Entry 1 (gap cost / architectural_operator_substitution) is borderline only on C14's baseline-myopia lesson — the LSH operator is not yet benchmarked against the existing cheaper sparse-keypoint family (collateral c2)."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved paper tests whether cross-modality correspondence must be searched in image/descriptor space at all: every leaf inherits from the mono-modal registration ancestor the unexamined assumption that a transformation is found by maximizing an image-space similarity (intensity, learned descriptor, or feature correlation) between fixed and moving voxels, and so attacks the modality gap by engineering a better image-space similarity or a cheaper way to evaluate it, rather than asking whether the correspondence could be carried by a quantity that is not an image-space matching score at all.","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Take an existing identifiability/recovery result and pivot the assumption it requires, trading a distributional assumption for a STRUCTURAL/geometric one (e.g. a feasible-region or curvature signature that survives arbitrary smooth mixing), then re-prove recovery up to the field's standard ambiguity class and operationalize the theorem as a regularizer/estimator.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism performs the C05 signature move: it audits the field's identifiability assumption ('every leaf ... presumes the transform is recovered by maximizing an image/descriptor-space similarity score') and substitutes a DIFFERENT KIND of constraint — exact invariance of Phi to a parametrized contrast group built by a canonicalization layer, the geometric/structural signature that survives the modality transform — then claims recovery 'up to the diffeomorphic-deformation ambiguity class' and operationalizes it as the canonicalizer+encoder estimator (Phi-agreement lookup). This is C05's distributional→structural pivot with a named ambiguity class, not the parent's generic 'question an assumption.' The only soft spot is that the sufficiency proof is asserted rather than exhibited (the borderline above), but the cluster's move IS the one enacted.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes cross-modality correspondence cost sub-linear in voxel count while preserving full-resolution accuracy: every learned-correspondence method evaluates a dense similarity or correlation volume on the full (or lightly downsampled) feature grid, so at gigavoxel scale either memory/time explode (correlation-pyramid and transformer methods are confined to coarse levels) or the method retreats to an engineered coarse-to-fine cascade whose fine result is not certified to be the refinement of the coarse one — the outcome that is missing is a correspondence whose compute does not grow with the native voxel grid yet whose alignment is exact at that grid.","sub_pattern":"C14 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"When the bottleneck is concretely the dense pairwise-interaction (all-pairs / softmax-attention) operator over N elements, name a cheaper primitive and PROVE or exactly equate the preserved property (expressivity class, receptive field, or retrieval capacity), so the substitution unlocks a regime the dense operator structurally forbids.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism enacts the C14 move precisely: the bottleneck is named as the dense all-pairs match of Phi_F to Phi_M (the same O(N) cost MASR-Net/MR-US pay), the cheaper primitive is a multi-probe LSH nearest-invariant lookup, and the preserved property — that the sub-linear lookup returns the SAME argmin the dense full-resolution match would — is PROVED via a Lipschitz bound (L·h < r recall radius), not merely asserted. The substitution unlocks gigavoxel-scale matching the dense operator structurally forbids. This is C14's prove-the-preserved-property-of-a-cheaper-all-pairs-surrogate, not a generic block swap.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries instantiate their cited cluster's signature move in core_mechanism rather than the parent gist: C05's distributional→structural-geometric pivot re-proving recovery up to a named ambiguity class (contrast-group invariance replacing the image-space-similarity assumption), and C14's dense-all-pairs→cheaper-surrogate substitution with a Lipschitz preservation proof (LSH lookup certified to equal the dense argmin)."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["assumption_audit_and_pivot","architectural_operator_substitution"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions (audit_decomp_supervisor / audit_decomp_prior / audit_decomp_operator) require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; the candidate's main_pattern set is {assumption_audit_and_pivot, architectural_operator_substitution} with neither heterogeneous_decomposition nor any matching 2-way subset, and the companion structural_prior_encoding is not a main_pattern, so no anti-pattern is triggered (audit_decomp_operator would need architectural_operator_substitution + heterogeneous_decomposition, and heterogeneous_decomposition is absent)."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"arxiv:2603.26393v1","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"'Adapting Frozen Mono-modal Backbones for Multi-modal Registration via Contrast-Agnostic Instance Optimization' (2026-03) is the closest structural neighbor in collision_hits: it also targets multimodal registration generalization under modality/intensity distribution shift and also pursues a 'contrast-agnostic' route. What makes the candidate's claim STAND rather than fall: that paper integrates a FROZEN pretrained mono-modal registration model with a lightweight test-time ADAPTATION / instance-optimization pipeline — i.e. its cross-modal robustness is bought by per-pair instance optimization on top of a borrowed backbone, exactly the occupied sources method_lineage flags as n8 (NIR per-pair instance optimization) and n7 (CORE frozen-extractor borrowed invariance) and that Phase 2.1's occupied-source constraint explicitly forbade. It does NOT (a) make modality-invariance hold BY CONSTRUCTION via a contrast-group canonicalization layer (its 'contrast-agnostic' property is adapted/optimized, not an exact group invariance), (b) eliminate the image-space matching score (it still optimizes an image-space registration objective at test time), nor (c) make the matching operator sub-linear in voxel count with a Lipschitz certificate. So it overlaps the candidate's MOTIVATION (contrast-agnostic multimodal registration) but not its mechanism (by-construction invariance + search-free read-off + sub-linear certified lookup); the candidate's claim that no leaf carries correspondence in a NON-image-space quantity remains intact. Timing note: 2026-03 is within ~3 months of the 2026-06-02 as-of and is near-concurrent; per the skill's timing rule this is awareness-not-blocking, reinforcing differentiate-and-stand over abandon.","addressable_via":"Add a differentiation_from_lit entry against arxiv:2603.26393v1 stating the measured axis (by-construction contrast-group invariance + search-free LSH matching vs. their frozen-backbone test-time instance optimization), so the motivational overlap is explicitly separated from the mechanism — no core_mechanism rebuild needed."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat (arxiv:2603.26393v1 shares the contrast-agnostic multimodal-registration motivation and is absent from the current five-entry differentiation)","fix_direction":"Add a differentiation_from_lit entry against arxiv:2603.26393v1: it adapts a FROZEN mono-modal backbone via test-time/instance optimization (borrowed + per-pair optimized contrast-agnosticism, i.e. occupied nodes n7/n8); we make modality-invariance hold BY CONSTRUCTION via a contrast-group canonicalization layer, recover the transform by search-free nearest-invariant lookup with NO image-space matching objective, and certify sub-linear matching cost via a Lipschitz bound — none of which it does. State the measured axis (full-resolution TRE + sub-linear memory/wall-clock vs voxel count + off-distribution TRE), not test-time adaptation overhead. Do NOT touch falsification_prediction or compute_budget (kill-switch fields, byte-identical through Phase 3.3)."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","issue":"gap_closure_reject_check.entries[0] C05 lessons 2 and 3 (identifiability/disentanglement claim asserted without an exhibited SUFFICIENCY argument that exact G-invariance ALONE identifies homology)","fix_direction":"In core_mechanism's anchor leg, add the one-line sufficiency argument the C05 move requires: state that under the discriminative homology training (positives = same anatomical voxel across G-views, negatives = different anatomy), Phi is trained so that Phi-agreement holds IFF anatomy coincides on the contrast group's orbit, so exact G-invariance plus anatomical separability is SUFFICIENT (not merely necessary) to identify the correspondence up to the diffeomorphic-deformation ambiguity class — closing the theory-practice gap C05 step 3/5 demand. Edit only the sufficiency sentence; preserve the rest of core_mechanism and all kill-switch fields verbatim."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism_steps (baseline/ablation list, step 11-12) + surface in Phase 4 reviewer_concerns_and_responses","issue":"gap_closure_reject_check.entries[1] C14 baseline-myopia lesson (the LSH operator is benchmarked only against dense/expensive originals, not the existing cheaper sparse-keypoint family / collateral c2)","fix_direction":"Add a cheaper-family baseline to the operator comparison — a sparse-keypoint (e.g. learned-keypoint) matcher and a coarse-only (downsampled dense) matcher on the same Phi codes — so the LSH operator's full-resolution-accuracy-at-sub-linear-cost advantage is measured against the established cheaper family, not only against the dense original. Non-load-bearing for the mechanism; fold the residual concern into Phase 4 reviewer_concerns_and_responses. Do NOT edit falsification_prediction (kill-switch frozen)."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added a measured differentiation entry against arxiv:2603.26393v1, stating it buys contrast-agnosticism via a frozen mono-modal backbone + test-time instance optimization (occupied nodes n7/n8) whereas we construct exact contrast-group invariance, recover the transform search-free, and certify sub-linear matching cost — measured on full-resolution TRE + memory/wall-clock vs voxel count + off-distribution TRE."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added the C05 sufficiency sentence to the anchor leg: under the discriminative homology training, Phi-agreement holds iff anatomy coincides on the contrast group's orbit, so exact G-invariance plus anatomical separability is SUFFICIENT (not merely necessary) to identify the correspondence up to the diffeomorphic-deformation ambiguity class."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism_steps","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Extended step 11 to add a cheaper-family baseline — a sparse-keypoint matcher and a coarse-only (downsampled dense) matcher on the same Phi codes — so the LSH operator's full-resolution-accuracy-at-sub-linear-cost advantage is measured against the established cheaper family (collateral c2), not only the dense original."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Read Correspondence Off a Constructed Invariant: Search-Free Gigavoxel Multimodal Registration\n\n**Method.** Constructed-Invariant Search-Free Registration (CISR)\n\n## Motivation\nTo line up two medical images of the same body taken with different machines (say an MRI and an ultrasound, or a tissue slide stained two different ways), a computer has to figure out which point in one image is the same anatomy as which point in the other. Today's best methods all do this the same way: they turn each image into a stack of feature numbers, then slide one image over the other and, at every position, score how similar the feature numbers are, keeping the position with the best score. This 'compare-and-score everywhere' recipe has two problems. First, the 'sameness' of the features is only learned softly from training data, so when you show it a new machine or stain it never saw, two points that are actually the same anatomy can get different feature numbers and the matching falls apart — exactly the case a recent analysis (Magic-or-Mirage) showed these methods fail in. Second, scoring similarity at every position over a billion-pixel slide is enormously expensive, so methods either shrink the image (losing detail) or hand-build shortcut pipelines with no guarantee the shortcut gives the right answer.\n\nWe step back and ask a different question: does the computer have to SEARCH for the match by scoring image similarity at all? Our move: build a feature code for every point that is GUARANTEED to be the same for the same anatomy no matter the machine or stain — not learned-soft, but true by the way the code is built (we first 'wash out' the contrast differences with a canonicalizing step, so the encoder only ever sees one standard look). Then matching is trivial: the same anatomy has the same code, so you just look up which point has the matching code — no sliding, no scoring. And because the codes are short, you can store them in a hash table and look up each match in roughly constant time instead of scanning everything, with a mathematical guarantee (a Lipschitz bound) that this fast lookup gives exactly the same answer the slow full-resolution scan would. The result: matching that holds up on unseen machines/stains and whose cost barely grows as the image gets bigger.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n*Unchanged scaffolding: run the falsification/cheaper-family ablations and report accuracy, cost-vs-voxel-count, and off-distribution error.*\n\n1. Ablate: replace the canonicalizer with identity (invariance becomes a soft learned thing again), swap the hash lookup for dense correlation, and compare against a sparse-keypoint matcher and a coarse-only matcher running on the same codes, all at matched memory budgets, to show the hash gives full-resolution accuracy at sub-linear cost versus the cheaper alternatives.\n   - _Why_: These pin the gains to the right causes: by-construction invariance for off-distribution accuracy, the certified hash for cheap-yet-exact matching.\n2. Report registration error and overlap, peak memory and wall-clock as the image grows, and — as the headline number — error on modality/stain pairs that were entirely held out of training.\n   - _Why_: These are exactly the three things the method claims to fix: accuracy, sub-linear cost, and off-distribution robustness.\n\n### Constructed Contrast-Invariant Field\n*Canonicalize away contrast then encode, so every voxel's code is the same for the same anatomy by construction (not soft training).*\n\n3. Write down the family of contrast changes G that turn one modality/stain into another — per-channel monotone intensity remaps (8 control points), smooth shading (a bias field), and noise — and randomly sample them to make two differently-contrasted copies of each training volume that differ only in appearance, not geometry. 【author decision: whether the real differences between the modality/stain pairs you target are actually just such intensity/shading changes is the key assumption — if one modality shows a structure another doesn't, that is not a monotone recolor and lies outside G; the authors must say which pairs are in scope and either show they only differ by a G-change or widen G to cover the structural differences.】\n   - _Why_: You can only make features invariant to contrast if you first say exactly which contrast changes count.\n4. Train a small 'canonicalizer' network that looks at a local patch, guesses which contrast change it has, and undoes it to a fixed standard look (the standard = no recolor, no shading, no noise).\n   - _Why_: If every patch is first washed to one standard contrast, whatever encoder runs next can't see the modality difference, so its output is contrast-invariant automatically.\n5. Run an encoder on the canonicalized volume to get an 8-number code per voxel in one pass; because the input has already been standardized, the same anatomy gets the same code no matter which modality it came from — that equality is built in, not learned softly.\n\n*The contrast-equivariant canonical-coordinate field Phi at voxel x of volume V in modality channel s is the encoder $f_{theta}$ applied to the patch after the canonicalizer $c_{psi}$ maps it to a fixed reference contrast; the $d_{c}=8$ code is a canonical anatomical coordinate.*\n$$ \\Phi_\\theta(V, s)(x) = f_\\theta\\big(c_\\psi^{-1} \\cdot \\mathrm{patch}_x(V,s)\\big) \\in \\mathbb{R}^{d_c}, \\quad d_c = 8 \\tag{1} $$\n\n\n*Because $f_{theta}$ only ever sees reference-contrast input, Phi is exactly invariant to every element $T_{alpha}$ of the parametrized contrast group G (per-channel monotone intensity remap + smooth bias-field shading + additive noise) by the canonicalization identity — homologous anatomy receives the same code by construction, not by soft training.*\n$$ \\Phi_\\theta(T_\\alpha(V), s')(x) = \\Phi_\\theta(V, s)(x) \\quad \\forall\\, T_\\alpha \\in G \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This code is the single thing everything else uses: it carries the correspondence as an invariant, not as a score to be searched.\n6. Train the encoder so the same anatomical voxel (seen under two contrasts) gets matching codes and different anatomy gets different codes, using a contrastive loss whose positives are exact (same geometry by construction) and whose negatives are nearby and random voxels; separately, train the canonicalizer to correctly identify the contrast change it was given. Use no image-similarity loss at all.\n   - _Why_: This makes 'codes agree' mean 'same anatomy', so the match can be read off code-agreement instead of maximized as a similarity.\n\n### Search-Free Read-Off\n*Recover the transform as agreement of the invariant codes, with no image-space matching score searched.*\n\n7. For each voxel in the fixed image, look up its nearest code in the hash table to find its match — no sliding window, no similarity scoring. If the lookup finds nothing, probe a bit wider; if still nothing, leave that voxel unmatched (and record it) so the later smooth fit fills it in.\n\n*The deformation u is recovered by matching in invariant-code space: the homologue of fixed voxel x is the moving voxel whose Phi code is nearest, with NO image-space similarity score — correspondence is read off where Phi agrees.*\n$$ u(x) = \\arg\\min_y \\; \\lVert \\Phi_F(x) - \\Phi_M(x + y) \\rVert \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Because the same anatomy has the same code, the match is just a code lookup, and it is sub-linear in image size.\n8. Fit a smooth, invertible deformation to the matched points (a velocity field made invertible by scaling-and-squaring, with a smoothness penalty) and warp the moving image onto the fixed one; unmatched voxels are filled by smoothly interpolating the field.\n   - _Why_: This converts the point matches into the final aligned image.\n\n### Sub-Linear Certified Matching\n*Hash the codes and look up each match in sub-linear time, with a Lipschitz bound certifying it equals the full-resolution dense match.*\n\n9. Measure once how fast the code can change from one voxel to a neighbor — its Lipschitz constant L — using actual measured differences over a calibration batch (and also report the looser theoretical bound from the network's layer norms for reference).\n   - _Why_: Knowing how smoothly the code varies is what lets us later guarantee a fast approximate lookup gives the exact match.\n10. Compute the codes on the moving image and drop them all into a locality-sensitive hash table in a single pass, so they can be looked up by nearest code later.\n   - _Why_: A hash table lets you find the nearest matching code in roughly constant time instead of scanning every voxel.\n11. Choose the grid spacing h so that $L\\cdot h$ is smaller than the hash's recall radius r; in principle this guarantees the fast lookup returns exactly the match a full-resolution scan would. 【author decision: that guarantee is exact for the spacing/Lipschitz part but the hash itself only recalls the true nearest code with high probability, not certainty — the authors must either use a deterministic hashing scheme whose recall within r is exact, or state the guarantee as 'holds with probability $\\ge  1- \\delta '$ with a named failure rate and check the real miss-rate against it.】\n\n*With Phi L-Lipschitz in voxel coordinate (L bounded by the encoder's spectral norm, measured once), a coarse grid spacing h and LSH recall radius r satisfying L*h < r certify that the sub-linear hash lookup returns the same argmin a dense full-resolution scan would, so the coarse correspondence is provably the refinement of the fine one.*\n$$ L \\cdot h < r \\;\\Rightarrow\\; \\mathrm{LSH}_r(\\Phi_F(x)) = \\arg\\min_y \\lVert \\Phi_F(x) - \\Phi_M(x+y) \\rVert \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: It turns 'fast but approximate' into 'fast and provably exact', and makes the coarse result a certified refinement of the fine one.\n12. Repeat at finer spacings, only re-searching inside the already-certified neighborhoods from the coarser level (a small ball around each parent match), until you reach full resolution.\n   - _Why_: You reach native gigavoxel detail while keeping the guarantee that fine is a refinement of coarse — no heuristic pyramid.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 从构造不变量读出对应：面向 gigavoxel 多模态配准的免搜索方法\n\n**方法名称.** Constructed-Invariant Search-Free Registration (CISR)\n\n## 研究动机\n要把同一具身体用不同设备拍的两张医学图像对齐（比如一张 MRI 和一张超声，或同一张组织切片用两种不同染色），计算机必须搞清楚一张图里的某个点对应另一张图里哪个点是同一块解剖结构。如今最好的方法都用同一套做法：把每张图变成一摞特征数字，然后把一张图在另一张上滑动，在每个位置给特征数字的相似度打分，保留得分最高的位置。这套“到处比较打分”的配方有两个毛病。第一，特征的“相同性”只是从训练数据里软学来的，所以一旦给它一台没见过的设备或染色，本应是同一解剖的两个点可能拿到不同的特征数字，匹配就崩了——这正是最近一项分析（Magic-or-Mirage）指出这类方法会失败的情形。第二，在一张十亿像素的切片上每个位置都打相似度分极其昂贵，于是方法要么把图缩小（损失细节），要么手工搭出捷径流水线，却无法保证捷径给的是正确答案。\n\n我们退一步问一个不同的问题：计算机到底需不需要靠打 image 相似度分来“搜索”匹配？我们的做法：为每个点构造一种特征编码，它对同一块解剖结构无论用什么设备或染色都“保证”相同——不是软学的，而是由编码的构造方式天然成立（我们先用一个规范化步骤把对比度差异“洗掉”，让编码器永远只看到一种标准外观）。这样匹配就变得平凡：同一解剖有相同编码，于是只需查哪个点的编码相符即可——不滑动、不打分。而且因为编码很短，可以把它们存进哈希表，每次匹配几乎是常数时间查表而非全图扫描，并有数学保证（一个 Lipschitz 界）说明这种快速查表给出的答案与缓慢的全分辨率扫描完全一致。结果就是：在没见过的设备/染色上依然稳健、且代价几乎不随图像变大而增长的匹配。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景脚手架\n*不变的支撑部分：跑 falsification/更便宜家族的消融，报告精度、代价随体素数变化与 off-distribution 误差。*\n\n1. 做证伪与更廉价家族的消融,全部在同一套训练好的 Phi 编码上:(i) 把规范化器换成恒等,使 Phi 退回软学习描述子;(ii) 把 LSH 查找换成稠密相关;再加稀疏关键点匹配器(在检测到的 3D 极值处匹配再插值)与仅粗匹配器(在固定下采样网格上稠密匹配、无认证细化)。在相同内存预算下报告各方法,从而把 LSH 算子『亚线性代价下达到全分辨率精度』的优势相对既有廉价家族(旁证 c2)隔离出来,而不仅相对稠密原法。\n   - _为什么_: 这些把收益钉到正确原因上：by-construction 不变性带来 off-distribution 精度，认证哈希带来又便宜又精确的匹配。\n2. 训练时整对留出模态/染色(在 Learn2Reg 的部分模态对与 ANHIR/ACROBAT 的部分染色上训练,在不相交的对/染色上评测),报告目标配准误差(TRE)/Dice、随体素数 N 增长的峰值内存与墙钟时间,并把留出模态对上的 TRE 单列为头条泛化指标。\n   - _为什么_: 这正是方法声称要修的三件事：精度、sub-linear 代价、off-distribution 稳健性。\n\n### 构造的对比度不变场\n*先把对比度规范化再编码，使每个体素的编码对同一解剖由构造相同（而非软训练）。*\n\n3. 写下把一种模态/染色变成另一种的对比度变化族 G:逐通道单调强度重映射(分段线性,K=8 个控制点,斜率保持在 [0.2,5] 以确保单调)+ 平滑遮蔽(偏置场,order-3 B-spline / degree-4 球谐系数,峰值偏差至多 $\\pm 40\\%)+$ 加性高斯噪声$(\\sigma $ 至多为动态范围的 5%)。在线采样 $\\alpha ~p(G),$为每个训练体积造出两份仅差一个 G 元素、几何相同的对比度副本。【作者需决定:真实的跨模态/跨染色差异是否真的落在这个『单调重映射 + 偏置 + 噪声』群内,是最承重的假设——结构性外观差异(某结构在 MR 可见而在 CT 缺失、染色特有纹理)并不是单调强度重参数化,落在该群之外;作者须界定 G 的覆盖范围与在范围内的模态对,并要么证明目标对只差一个 G 元素,要么扩展参数化以吸收这些结构差异。】\n   - _为什么_: 只有先明确哪些对比度变化算数，才能让特征对对比度不变。\n4. 构建规范化器 $c_{psi}:$一个在局部 patch(如 $16^{3}$ 体素,足够大以局部估计平滑偏置)上工作的轻量 3D CNN,回归该 patch 所带的 G 元素(K 个 knot 值 + 偏置系数)并施加其逆,把 patch 映射到固定参考对比度——参考对比度定义为恒等重映射(单位斜率)、零偏置场、无噪声。\n   - _为什么_: 如果每个 patch 先被洗到同一种标准对比度，后面的编码器就看不到模态差异，其输出自动对比度不变。\n5. 在规范化后的体积上跑编码器 $f_{theta}(3D$ U-Net 主干),定义 Phi $= f_{theta}(c_{psi}^{-1}\\cdot patch),$以全卷积方式一次性为每个体素输出一个 8 维编码(逐体素的 patch 即编码器的感受野,不是单独裁剪)。由于编码器只见过参考对比度输入,Phi 对每个 G 元素 $T_{alpha}$ 都满足 $Phi(T_{alpha}(V))=Phi(V)——$同一解剖无论何种模态都由构造得到相同的 8 维编码,而非软训练得到。\n\n*对比度等变的规范坐标场 Phi 在体素 x（来自模态通道 s 的体积 V）处的取值，是先用规范化器 $c_{psi}$ 把局部 patch 映回固定参考对比度、再经编码器 $f_{theta}$ 得到的 $d_{c}=8$ 维编码，表示一个规范解剖坐标。*\n$$ \\Phi_\\theta(V, s)(x) = f_\\theta\\big(c_\\psi^{-1} \\cdot \\mathrm{patch}_x(V,s)\\big) \\in \\mathbb{R}^{d_c}, \\quad d_c = 8 \\tag{1} $$\n\n\n*由于 $f_{theta}$ 永远只看到参考对比度的输入，根据规范化恒等式，Phi 对参数化对比度群 G（逐通道单调强度重映射 + 平滑偏置场遮蔽 + 加性噪声）的每个元素 $T_{alpha}$ 都精确不变——同源解剖由构造获得相同编码，而非靠软训练。*\n$$ \\Phi_\\theta(T_\\alpha(V), s')(x) = \\Phi_\\theta(V, s)(x) \\quad \\forall\\, T_\\alpha \\in G \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这个编码是后面一切的唯一依据：它把对应关系当作不变量来携带，而不是当作需要搜索的分数。\n6. 用体素级 InfoNCE 同源损失训练 theta,psi:正样本是两份 G 视图下的同一解剖体素(由构造精确对应,因视图几何相同),负样本是锚点周围壳层内的难负体素加 batch 内随机体素(温度 0.07);另加规范化一致性损失 $= c_{psi}$ 预测的 G 元素与已知采样 $\\alpha $ 之间的 L2(从而监督 $c_{psi}$ 等变)。全程不使用任何 image 空间相似度损失。\n   - _为什么_: 这让“编码相符”等价于“同一解剖”，于是匹配可以从编码相符处读出，而非作为相似度最大化得到。\n\n### 免搜索读出\n*把变换恢复为不变编码的相符处，全程不搜索任何 image-space 匹配分数。*\n\n7. 对固定图像的每个体素 x,在 LSH 中查询与 $Phi_{F}(x)$ 最近的移动编码,从而无需扫描全部 N 个移动体素即可找到同源点(期望亚线性代价)——不打任何 image 空间相似度分,对应关系就读在编码一致之处。若召回未命中,在受限预算内扩大探测;仍为空则把 x 标为未匹配(记录在案),交由后续形变拟合插值。输出稀疏的跨模态对应集。\n\n*形变场 u 通过在不变编码空间中匹配恢复：固定体素 x 的同源点是其 Phi 编码最近的移动体素，全程不使用任何 image-space 相似度分数——对应关系是从 Phi 相符之处读出的。*\n$$ u(x) = \\arg\\min_y \\; \\lVert \\Phi_F(x) - \\Phi_M(x + y) \\rVert \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 因为同一解剖有相同编码，匹配只是一次编码查表，且对图像大小是 sub-linear 的。\n8. 对匹配点拟合一个微分同胚形变 u,参数化为稳态速度场(SVF)、经 scaling-and-squaring 积分得到可逆形变,目标为匹配点位移误差 $+ \\lambda \\cdot \\| \\nabla v\\| ^{2}$ 弯曲能$(\\lambda $ 由验证集定),并用核/B-spline 插值把场扩展到未匹配体素;以所得微分同胚扭曲移动体积,得到配准输出。\n   - _为什么_: 这把点匹配转成最终对齐好的图像。\n\n### Sub-Linear 认证匹配\n*对编码做哈希、以 sub-linear 时间查每个匹配，并用 Lipschitz 界证明它等于全分辨率稠密匹配。*\n\n9. 测量一次编码从一个体素到相邻体素变化的最快速度,即 Lipschitz 常数 L:用校准批上 $\\| Phi(x)- Phi(x')\\| /\\| x- x'\\| $ 的经验有限差分最大值作为设定网格间距 h 的操作值,并另外报告编码器各层谱范数乘积作为更保守的上界。L 测一次并存储。\n   - _为什么_: 知道编码变化有多平滑，才能在后面保证快速近似查找给出的是精确匹配。\n10. 在移动体积上算出 $Phi_{M},$把所有移动体素的 8 维编码一次性(O(N) 单遍)插入一个多探测 locality-sensitive 哈希(LSH)索引,采用 p-stable(L2)投影(约 10 张表,哈希宽度调到每桶约含 O(1) 个候选)。\n   - _为什么_: 哈希表让你在近似常数时间内找到最近的相符编码，而不必扫描每个体素。\n11. 选粗网格间距 h 使 $L\\cdot h <$ r(LSH 召回半径);由证书式 eq:certificate,亚线性查找在编码空间返回的正是全分辨率稠密扫描会给的 argmin。【作者需决定:该界中『间距/Lipschitz』部分是确定性的,但 LSH 召回是概率性的,所以『等于稠密匹配』目前只在高概率下成立——作者须弥合此缺口:要么用召回半径 r 内精确的确定性 bucket-cover 哈希替换概率性多探测 LSH,要么把证书表述为带显式每次查询失败率 $\\delta ($表数, 探测数) 的高概率界,并用实测未命中率对照它。】缺口弥合后,所得对应即等于稠密匹配对应,粗对齐可证是细对齐的细化。\n\n*当 Phi 对体素坐标 L-Lipschitz（L 由编码器谱范数界定，仅测量一次）时，满足 L*h < r 的粗网格间距 h 与 LSH 召回半径 r 可证明：sub-linear 的哈希查找返回与全分辨率稠密扫描相同的 argmin，因此粗对应关系可证地就是细对应关系的细化。*\n$$ L \\cdot h < r \\;\\Rightarrow\\; \\mathrm{LSH}_r(\\Phi_F(x)) = \\arg\\min_y \\lVert \\Phi_F(x) - \\Phi_M(x+y) \\rVert \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 它把“快但近似”变成“快且可证精确”，并使粗结果成为细结果的可证细化。\n12. 把 h 减半,只在每个细体素的已认证邻域内重新查询——即其父级匹配位置周围半径 r 的球,且仍满足 $L\\cdot h <$ r,故细对齐可证是粗对齐的细化;递归直至全分辨率。\n   - _为什么_: 在保持“细是粗的细化”这一保证的同时达到原生 gigavoxel 细节——不用启发式金字塔。\n\n"},{"id":"03","run_dir":"run_prompt03_graphllm","index":3,"title":"Infer the Graph, Don't Read It: Calibrated Per-Edge Posteriors over Latent Structure from LLM Semantic Priors","title_zh":"推断图，而非读取图：基于 LLM 语义先验对潜在结构的校准化逐边后验","method_name":"Calibrated Latent-Edge Posterior (CLEP)","hook":"Every retrieved LLM-for-graph method either consumes a supplied edge list or emits one committed graph; we invert the inherited framing that the graph is given and treat the edge set as the latent target, eliciting from the LLM a calibrated per-edge posterior P(edge (u,v) exists | text) whose probabilities are marginalized over serialization order — so for the first time an 'inferred graph' splits into trustworthy edges and hallucinated ones with a stated confidence, rather than a single take-it-or-leave-it structure.","anchor_pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","anchor_pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","domain_category":"Graph Learning","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions the inherited framing that the graph is an INPUT the model reasons over rather than a LATENT TARGET to be inferred: the entire cluster (node classification, traversal, KG completion, graph reasoning) takes G=(V,E) as given and asks the LLM to use it, so the prior question — can the LLM infer the unknown edge set from observations/text at all, and with what confidence — is never posed as the problem to solve.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"reframe_as_solvable_object","how_closed":"Closed by auditing the recovery precondition (C05): the field's implicit identifiability assumption is that a graph's structure is identified only when the edge set is SUPPLIED (the topology must be given as an adjacency for the LLM to act), and we pivot it by showing a DIFFERENT KIND of constraint already present — the LLM's semantic prior over which relations are plausible given the node descriptions, combined with serialization-invariant textual evidence — carries the identifying information for the latent edge set, so the structure is recoverable from text up to a calibration class without ever being handed an edge list. The companion reframe_as_solvable_object (C00) ships the deliverable: it recasts the opaque question 'is edge (u,v) real and how sure are we' as a concrete measurement object — a calibrated per-edge posterior produced by an explicit estimator that aggregates the LLM's per-edge log-odds over serialization variants — certified by a causal intervention (perturbing the evidence for an edge shifts its posterior in the predicted direction). Together the two halves state the inverted assumption (the edge set is the target, recovered from semantic priors) AND ship the runnable posterior estimator that makes 'which edges are trustworthy' answerable.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf treats the LLM's serialization-order / prompt sensitivity as the measurement-noise term it must marginalize out before reporting structure: GraphiT exploits linearization choice for accuracy and the ICL-robustness probe documents that outputs flip under reordering, but no method models this variability as edge-level uncertainty in an inferred graph — the single emitted graph is reported as if order-invariant when it is not.","pattern_id":"targeted_self_supervised_objective","pattern_name":"Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective","sub_pattern":"C17 (Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by re-engineering the pairing geometry of a consistency objective (C17) so that the only way to minimize the loss is to encode a serialization-permutation-invariant edge-existence belief: the targeted structural property is that the posterior for edge (u,v) must be identical across linearizations of the same underlying graph, and the load-bearing pairing signal is sourced from a complementary view of the SAME entity — two random serialization orders of the identical (partial) graph become a positive pair whose per-edge posteriors are aligned, while serializations of graphs that genuinely differ in edge (u,v) form negatives. The single non-obvious geometric substitution is replacing the default next-token-likelihood alignment with a per-edge-marginal agreement penalty (a symmetric KL between the two views' edge-posteriors) plus a calibration term tying the agreed probability to empirical edge-existence frequency, so serialization order is written into the objective as the noise axis to marginalize rather than (as in GraphiT) an accuracy lever to optimize. This makes the anchor leg's posterior order-invariant and calibrated by construction.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"large language models for graph inference: using LLMs to infer the latent relational structure (which edges/nodes exist) and graph-theoretic properties of a system from its textual or serialized description","n_papers":52,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":27},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10},{"source":"openreview","n":2}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":13,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Reasoning with Large Language Models on Graph Tasks: The Influence of Temperature"},{"source":"openalex","title":"LLMs for knowledge graph construction and reasoning: recent capabilities and future opportunities"},{"source":"openalex","title":"RAG-based explainable prediction of road users behaviors for automated driving using knowledge graphs and large language models"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Making Large Language Models Perform Better in Knowledge Graph Completion"},{"source":"openalex","title":"GS-KGC: A generative subgraph-based framework for knowledge graph completion with large language models"},{"source":"openalex","title":"iText2KG: Incremental Knowledge Graphs Construction Using Large Language Models"}],"more":7},{"year":2025,"n":31,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Joint Knowledge Graph Reasoning and Large Language Models for Hierarchical Task Planning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"KG-TRACES: Enhancing Large Language Models with Knowledge Graph-constrained Trajectory Reasoning and Attribution Supervision"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Calibrating Stereotype Preference with Multi-Agent Graph Reasoning in Large Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Towards Faithful and Explainable Large Language Models: A Knowledge Graph-Guided Framework for Reasoning Enhancement and Hallucination Mitigation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Knowledge Reasoning of Large Language Models Integrating Graph-Structured Information for Pest and Disease Control in Tobacco"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Struct-X: Enhancing the Reasoning Capabilities of Large Language Models in Structured Data Scenarios"}],"more":25},{"year":2026,"n":8,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"},{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"CROP: Token-Efficient Reasoning in Large Language Models via Regularized Prompt Optimization"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"CosmicFish-HRM: Adaptive Reasoning via Hierarchical Recurrent Mechanisms in Compact Language Models"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"ChaosBench-Logic: A Benchmark for Logical and Symbolic Reasoning on Chaotic Dynamical Systems"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Agentic Reasoning for Large Language Models"}],"more":2}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":12,"share":0.231},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":9,"share":0.173},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":8,"share":0.154},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":8,"share":0.154},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":7,"share":0.135},{"pattern_id":"targeted_self_supervised_objective","pattern_name":"Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective","count":6,"share":0.115},{"pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","count":5,"share":0.096},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":4,"share":0.077}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Across the LLM-for-graph literature the graph is treated as a GIVEN object that the model reasons over or a SINGLE object the model commits to, never as a latent structure to be inferred under uncertainty: GraphLLM (openalex:W4415707504) and GraphiT (openalex:W4410637068) both take G=(V,E) (an edge list or adjacency, possibly with node text) as input and optimize a downstream reasoning/classification objective, so the topology is an assumption rather than an inference target; TinyGraphEstimator (semanticscholar:0c710082b91915213f152f770a530fb9fe5c56a5) does infer structural quantities from a serialized graph but casts it as scalar-parameter regression (degree, density, chromatic number) over an already-supplied edge set, yielding point estimates with no per-edge structural posterior; and the text-to-graph generation line — Accurate-and-Consistent Graph Model Generation (openalex:W4416677557) and Consistent Graph Model Generation (openalex:W4411272401) — emits exactly one graph and repairs it against hand-written well-formedness constraints, so correctness is checked syntactically against a metamodel rather than estimated as a calibrated likelihood that a given edge belongs. The diagnostic leaves confirm the hole rather than fill it: Can LLMs Perform Structured Graph Reasoning Tasks? (openalex:W4404931550) documents that accuracy collapses on larger/denser graphs but supplies no repair, and the documented in-context instability under prompt perturbation (openalex:W4406460535) means the single committed graph an LLM emits can flip with serialization order — instability nobody converts into a measured uncertainty. The result is that no retrieved method delivers a calibrated per-edge posterior over latent graph structure inferred from text: the LLM is asked to either consume a graph or output one, never to quantify how confident it is that each candidate edge is real, so a measured 'inferred graph' cannot be separated into trustworthy edges and elicitation artifacts.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:0c710082b91915213f152f770a530fb9fe5c56a5","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"TinyGraphEstimator adapts lightweight transformer LMs (via LoRA) to infer graph-theoretic parameters — degree statistics, density, connectivity, clustering, chromatic number — directly from a textual/serialized representation of an undirected unweighted graph, showing compact models can estimate structure-summarizing quantities. Its residue: the input is already the full edge connectivity (the topology is given), and the inference target is a flat vector of scalar parameters predicted as a point estimate; it never asks the prior question — given only a partial or noisy textual description, WHICH edges exist — and it attaches no per-edge or per-parameter posterior, so there is no calibrated notion of how reliable each piece of the inferred structure is. The move 'infer structure from a serialized graph' is present; the move 'infer the latent edge set under uncertainty with a calibrated posterior' is exactly what is missing."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415707504","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"GraphLLM boosts an LLM's graph-reasoning ability by fusing a graph-transformer encoder with the LLM: the graph is encoded into a learned prefix that conditions generation, decomposing reasoning into node-understanding and structure-understanding sub-objectives. Its residue: G=(V,E) is an input to the encoder, so the topology is assumed known; the injected structure is an opaque continuous prefix tuned for end-task accuracy, not an inspectable, calibrated estimate of which edges exist, so it cannot be turned toward inferring an unknown graph or reporting edge-level uncertainty."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4410637068","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"GraphiT serializes a text-attributed graph (nodes V, edges E, node text S) into a prompt-optimized sequence so an LLM can do node classification, tuning the linearization to improve accuracy. Its residue: edges E are part of the input and the linearization order is a free choice the method optimizes for the task — meaning the same graph admits many serializations and the output is sensitive to which one is chosen, yet this order-sensitivity is exploited for accuracy rather than modeled as a noise source; the graph is never an inference target and nothing in the pipeline yields an edge-existence posterior."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416677557","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Accurate-and-Consistent Graph Model Generation infers an instance graph from a natural-language description against a metamodel + constraint set, repairing the three error classes (syntax violations, constraint inconsistencies, semantic inaccuracies) through staged validation. Its residue: it DOES infer structure from text, but emits exactly one graph and validates it deterministically against hand-written well-formedness constraints — correctness is a binary pass/fail against a metamodel, not a calibrated likelihood per edge; uncertain or ambiguous edges are forced to a single committed value with no posterior, so there is no way to flag which inferred edges are well-supported by the text versus guessed."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4411272401","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Consistent Graph Model Generation uses an abstraction-concretization loop to make LLM-generated graphs satisfy domain well-formedness constraints. Its residue: consistency is enforced against externally supplied constraints, so the method improves the SINGLE generated graph's constraint-compliance but provides no measure of confidence in the edges themselves and no separation of constraint-driven corrections from genuine structural evidence in the source text."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4404931550","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Can LLMs Perform Structured Graph Reasoning Tasks? is a diagnostic that charts where LLMs succeed and fail on traversal/connectivity/cycle tasks over given graphs G={V,E}, finding accuracy degrades sharply on larger and denser graphs. Its residue: it operates on graphs supplied as input and stops at characterizing failure modes; it offers no inference mechanism and, crucially, no way to attach uncertainty to a structural answer, so the documented fragility on hard graphs is left as an observation rather than a calibrated reliability estimate."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"large language models for graph inference: using LLMs to infer the latent relational structure (which edges/nodes exist) and graph-theoretic properties of a system from its textual or serialized description","venue":"ICLR/NeurIPS/ACL-tier ML","time":"2026","data":["synthetic graph corpora with known ground-truth topology (random/scale-free/community graphs serialized to text)","text-attributed graph benchmarks (citation networks: Cora/PubMed/ogbn-arxiv) with node text + ground-truth edges","natural-language descriptions of relational systems paired with reference graphs (model-driven-engineering specs, scene descriptions)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"LLM reasoning + graph learning + probabilistic / uncertainty modeling","preference":"both","baseline":"TinyGraphEstimator graph-parameter regression, GraphLLM graph-transformer-prefix reasoning, GraphiT prompt-optimized node classification, Accurate-and-Consistent text-to-graph generation, Can-LLMs-Perform-Structured-Graph-Reasoning diagnostic","limitation":"every retrieved method treats the graph as something the LLM either is GIVEN (an edge list / adjacency / pre-built KG it reasons over or classifies on) or emits as a single point-estimate object (one generated graph, one scalar parameter), so when the structure itself is uncertain — edges that may or may not exist given the text — the LLM returns one committed answer with no calibrated per-edge posterior, and the field has no way to say which inferred edges are reliable versus hallucinated","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","compute","expertise","preference","data"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object both legs read from and write to is the per-edge posterior q(e_{uv}=1 | T) for candidate edge (u,v) given the textual description T of the relational system (node descriptions plus any observed relations), produced by an estimator that uses the LLM as a semantic edge-prior. Anchor leg (C05 + reframe_as_solvable_object): we audit the field-wide assumption that a graph's structure is identified only when its edge set is SUPPLIED — GraphLLM encodes a given adjacency into a prefix, GraphiT serializes a given E, TinyGraphEstimator regresses parameters from a given edge list, the generation line emits one graph then repairs it against a metamodel — and we PIVOT the recovery precondition: the identifying information for the latent edge set is carried not by a supplied adjacency but by (i) the LLM's semantic prior p_LLM over which relations are plausible given the node texts and (ii) serialization-invariant evidence in T. Concretely, for each candidate pair (u,v) we form a scoring prompt that renders T plus the focal pair and read the LLM's log-odds ℓ_{uv} = log p_LLM(edge present)/p_LLM(edge absent) from a constrained yes/no continuation (length-normalized over the answer span). This ℓ_{uv} is a raw, uncalibrated per-edge signal — by itself it re-occupies collateral c2 (LLM self-consistency / raw sampling spread is not a calibrated posterior), so the reframe_as_solvable_object companion supplies the missing deliverable: we recast 'is edge (u,v) real, and how sure' as a calibrated posterior object q(e_{uv}=1|T) = σ(a · ℓ̄_{uv} + b), where ℓ̄_{uv} is ℓ_{uv} averaged over S random serialization orders of T (Step 2 of the sibling), and (a,b) is a temperature/Platt calibration fit ONCE on a held-out synthetic corpus with known ground-truth edges so that q matches empirical edge-existence frequency (reliability-diagram calibration), with the across-serialization variance of ℓ_{uv} folded in as an additive logit-variance term that widens q toward 0.5 for edges whose evidence is order-sensitive. This artifact — a per-edge probability read from the LLM's semantic prior, serialization-marginalized and frequency-calibrated — closes the subtractive gap because the measured quantity is now the latent edge set inferred from text (never a supplied adjacency), and it splits into trustworthy edges (q near 0 or 1, low order-variance) versus hallucinated ones (q near 0.5 or high order-variance). Sibling leg (C17): so that q is order-invariant by construction rather than only post-hoc averaged, we add a self-supervised serialization-invariance objective during a light LoRA adaptation of the scoring LLM: for each training graph we draw two random serializations T^{(1)}, T^{(2)} of the SAME (partial) graph as a positive pair and minimize L_inv = Σ_{(u,v)} KL( q^{(1)}_{uv} ‖ q^{(2)}_{uv} ) + KL( q^{(2)}_{uv} ‖ q^{(1)}_{uv} ), with graphs differing in edge (u,v) as negatives via a margin on |q_{uv}^{pos} − q_{uv}^{neg}|, plus a calibration term L_cal tying the agreed probability to the ground-truth edge label; the decisive geometric substitution is per-edge-marginal agreement (symmetric KL on edge posteriors) replacing the default next-token-likelihood alignment, which writes serialization order into the loss as the noise axis. The two legs share the single primitive q_{uv} — the anchor makes it a calibrated posterior read from semantic priors, the sibling makes it serialization-invariant — which is why this reads as one paper. Quantitatively this departs from prior work: TinyGraphEstimator (semanticscholar:0c710082b91915213f152f770a530fb9fe5c56a5) regresses scalar parameters from a GIVEN edge set as point estimates, whereas q infers the unknown edge set itself with per-edge calibrated uncertainty; and unlike the constraint-repair generation line (collateral c3), q is a calibrated likelihood per edge rather than a binary metamodel pass/fail.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The two gaps share machinery because the same object — the per-edge posterior q_{uv} — is simultaneously what the anchor must make a calibrated inference target read from semantic priors and what the sibling must make serialization-invariant; the evidence they are one object is that the serialization-invariance KL the sibling minimizes is computed directly over the same q_{uv} the anchor's estimator produces, so splitting them would double-represent the same edge belief. REGRESSION CHECK (method_lineage): I avoided c1 (classical Bayesian/PC structure learning on numbers — my estimator never runs an independence-test search on tabular data; it reads the LLM's semantic edge-prior over node TEXT and only calibrates the resulting log-odds, so the identifying information comes from the LLM, not from a numeric conditional-independence oracle), c2 (LLM self-consistency / raw sampling-as-uncertainty — I do not stop at counting sampled-edge frequency at raw decoding temperature; the order-variance is folded into a FREQUENCY-CALIBRATED posterior tied specifically to serialization-order noise, which is the calibration step c2 lacks), and c3 (constraint-repair generation already instantiated by n6/n7 — I emit a calibrated likelihood per edge, not a single graph forced through a hard metamodel checker), and n2/n3-n8 (serialize-the-given-graph-and-prompt — my input is text describing a system whose edge set is UNKNOWN, never a supplied adjacency). The unoccupied source I draw on is the COMPOSITION the tree does not yet occupy: an LLM-semantic-prior per-edge log-odds readout PLUS serialization-marginalized frequency calibration PLUS a self-supervised serialization-invariance objective that writes order-noise into the loss. I considered (and rejected) two alternatives: running classical Bayesian network averaging over LLM-imputed numeric features (rejected: regresses to c1, discards the semantic prior that is the whole point); and plain self-consistency edge-voting at high temperature (rejected: regresses to c2, gives an uncalibrated frequency not a posterior, and confounds decoding noise with serialization noise). Recorded avoided nodes: c1, c2, c3, n2.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on a corpus of relational systems with KNOWN ground-truth edges (synthetic random/scale-free/community graphs serialized to text + a held-out real text-attributed-graph slice whose edges are hidden at inference), build the calibrated serialization-invariant per-edge posterior q_{uv} and compare it against (i) a single-serialization point-estimate inferred graph and (ii) raw self-consistency edge-frequency, on both edge-recovery F1 and expected calibration error (ECE) against the held-out true edges. If the candidate works, the calibrated posterior achieves lower ECE on held-out edges than both baselines AND — the non-obvious direction — its per-edge probabilities stay stable (low coefficient of variation across serialization orders) while the single-serialization graph's edge decisions flip under the same reorderings, because the posterior is read off a serialization-marginalized, frequency-calibrated quantity rather than one committed linearization. Mechanism distinguisher built on the single load-bearing variable, the serialization-marginalized calibrated per-edge posterior q_{uv}: negative control ablates the serialization-invariance objective's producer — it replaces the two-random-serialization positive pairing with two IDENTICAL copies of the same serialization (so L_inv has nothing to align and the invariance signal is removed) while keeping every other step including the Platt calibration; the predicted effect is that downstream held-out edge-recovery F1 at matched precision collapses toward the single-serialization baseline and ECE under reordering rises sharply (NOT merely that q_{uv} changes value), which is the real Popper test, since 'the posteriors moved' alone is equally consistent with a re-scaled but still-calibrated estimate. Positive control: a stripped model using ONLY the calibrated per-edge posterior with serialization averaging but no invariance LoRA training should already recover most of the edge-set and most of the calibration gain over a single-serialization graph, identifying the calibrated-serialization-marginalized readout as the load-bearing mechanism.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:0c710082b91915213f152f770a530fb9fe5c56a5","delta":"TinyGraphEstimator regresses scalar graph-theoretic parameters (degree, density, chromatic number) from a GIVEN serialized edge set as point estimates; we never receive an edge set — we infer the latent edge set itself from text via the LLM's semantic prior and emit a calibrated per-edge posterior with order-variance, so we recover structure under uncertainty rather than summarizing a supplied graph with no confidence."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415707504","delta":"GraphLLM encodes a given adjacency into an opaque continuous prefix tuned for downstream reasoning accuracy; we treat the adjacency as unknown and produce an inspectable, calibrated per-edge probability read from the LLM's semantic prior, so our output is an inferred graph with stated edge reliability rather than a black-box structure-conditioned reasoner."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4410637068","delta":"GraphiT optimizes the serialization order of a given text-attributed graph as an accuracy lever for node classification; we model serialization order as the measurement-noise axis to marginalize, folding across-order variance into a calibrated edge posterior so order-sensitive edges are flagged as uncertain rather than silently committed."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416677557","delta":"Accurate-and-Consistent Graph Model Generation emits one instance graph from text and validates it by binary metamodel-constraint pass/fail; we emit a calibrated likelihood per edge tied to empirical edge-existence frequency, so ambiguous edges carry a posterior near 0.5 instead of being forced to a single committed value by a hard constraint checker."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4404931550","delta":"Can-LLMs-Perform-Structured-Graph-Reasoning is a diagnostic that documents accuracy collapse on larger/denser given graphs with no repair and no reliability estimate; we supply the inference mechanism it lacks and attach a calibrated per-edge confidence, converting its documented fragility into a measured uncertainty over the inferred structure."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:0c710082b91915213f152f770a530fb9fe5c56a5","what_step_was_missed":"TinyGraphEstimator adapts lightweight LMs to infer graph-theoretic parameters directly from a serialized graph, demonstrating that compact models can read structure-summarizing quantities out of a textual graph representation. For our contribution to already exist it would have needed to (a) move the inference target from a SUPPLIED edge set to the LATENT edge set — asking which edges exist given only a textual description rather than regressing parameters from a given adjacency — and (b) replace the point-estimate parameter vector with a calibrated per-edge posterior that is marginalized over serialization order and tied to empirical edge-existence frequency. It made neither move: its input is the full given connectivity and its output is a scalar point estimate, so it can summarize a graph it is handed but cannot infer an unknown edge set or say how confident it is that any particular edge is real."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":315,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"Layer 1 hard floor does not fire: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict is borderline (no Reject lesson is candidate_match: yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat is NOT exact-mechanism overlap (GraphSOS does order SELECTION on a GIVEN graph and supplies no calibrated per-edge posterior or latent-edge inference — the candidate's load-bearing C00 object). Layer 2 selects revise because paper_pointed_threat exists AND addressable_via names specific candidate fields (hook, differentiation_from_lit, what_step_was_missed), reinforced by gap_closure_reject_check.entries[1].reject_lessons_evaluated lesson 3 ('nearest pair-construction baselines missing') being borderline-live against GraphSOS and entries[0] lesson 1 ('union not measured against the closest neighbor') being live against Statsformer. recipe_application_check is applied for both legs, so core_mechanism is sound; the fix is repositioning/differentiation, not a mechanism rebuild.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions the inherited framing that the graph is an INPUT the model reasons over rather than a LATENT TARGET to be inferred: the entire cluster (node classification, traversal, KG completion, graph reasoning) takes G=(V,E) as given and asks the LLM to use it, so the prior question — can the LLM infer the unknown edge set from observations/text at all, and with what confidence — is never posed as the problem to solve.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The signature failure is an identifiability claim that outruns its proof. Papers fail when the pivoted assumption was not actually load-bearing — the new setting is a straightforward union of two existing frameworks (a separation method plus a constrained or multi-view wrapper), so re-proving recovery for the union reads as incremental rather than as opening a new regime. A third is imposing structural constraints to motivate interpretability or disentanglement without proving they are SUFFICIENT for recovery, leaving the result indistinguishable from a post-hoc heuristic.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Stacking two established frameworks and re-proving identifiability of the union reads as incremental unless the pivoted assumption was genuinely load-bearing and the union admits a regime neither framework could reach alone.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The candidate composes an LLM-semantic-prior log-odds readout with a calibration step plus a serialization-invariance objective, which could read as a union of 'LLM-as-prior' and 'probability calibration'; what makes it stand is that the pivoted assumption (the edge set must be SUPPLIED) is genuinely load-bearing — method_lineage shows every 0-2y leaf descends from n2 (serialize-the-given-graph) and inherits it — and the union admits a regime none reaches alone (inferring the UNKNOWN edge set from text with a calibrated per-edge posterior, where TinyGraphEstimator needs a given edge set and the generation line emits one uncalibrated graph). But differentiation_from_lit does not yet name the closest 'LLM-as-unreliable-prior, calibrate it' neighbor surfaced in collision (Statsformer, arxiv:2601.21410v3), so the load-bearingness is argued but not yet measured against that exact neighbor — mitigable by editing differentiation_from_lit, hence borderline not triggered."},{"lesson_quoted":"Advertising an identifiability or 'consistency' property while the proof omits the decisive object — never proving latent identifiability, or excluding part of the model from the guarantee — collapses the contribution the moment a reviewer checks the theorem.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate makes no closed-form identifiability THEOREM claim it then fails to prove; it audits an assumption and ships an empirical estimator (a calibrated per-edge posterior) whose validity is established operationally — calibration against held-out ground-truth edges (reliability diagram / ECE) and a causal-intervention check (step 8) — so there is no advertised-but-unproven consistency theorem to collapse."},{"lesson_quoted":"Imposing structural constraints to claim interpretability or disentanglement without proving those constraints are sufficient for recovery leaves the result indistinguishable from a post-hoc heuristic.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate does not claim its serialization-invariance constraint is SUFFICIENT for exact recovery; it claims (and tests) that the constraint plus calibration makes the per-edge posterior order-invariant and frequency-calibrated, validated by ECE on held-out edges and the falsification negative control, so the constraint's role is empirically isolated rather than asserted as a recovery sufficiency condition."},{"lesson_quoted":"Proving identifiability conditions the algorithm neither enforces nor verifies creates a theory-practice disconnect that undermines both the soundness and the significance of the claim.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"There is no theory-practice gap: the algorithm directly enforces the property it claims (the serialization-invariance objective L_inv enforces order-invariance; the Platt calibration enforces frequency-calibration) and verifies it (serialization-stability CV and held-out ECE in steps 6-7), so every claimed property is both enforced and measured."},{"lesson_quoted":"Errors in the dependency or conditional-independence bookkeeping (mislabeling an independence, opening a collider) void the central theorem even when the empirical numbers look reasonable.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate runs no conditional-independence search and proves no theorem resting on independence bookkeeping — it deliberately avoids the classical PC/Bayesian-structure-learning route (collateral c1) — so there is no independence-bookkeeping object that could be mislabeled to void a theorem."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf treats the LLM's serialization-order / prompt sensitivity as the measurement-noise term it must marginalize out before reporting structure: GraphiT exploits linearization choice for accuracy and the ICL-robustness probe documents that outputs flip under reordering, but no method models this variability as edge-level uncertainty in an inferred graph — the single emitted graph is reported as if order-invariant when it is not.","main_pattern":"targeted_self_supervised_objective","sub_pattern":"C17 (Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"the recurring shape is sourcing the pairing/alignment signal by composing two already-published components — a frozen pretrained predictor feeding a standard SSL pipeline, reconstruction pretraining followed by a stock nearest-neighbor contrastive pass — and presenting the composition itself as the contribution. These papers never re-derive WHY this particular pairing geometry uniquely encodes the targeted property; they assert it is captured but supply no operational definition, no direct probe, and no ablation that isolates the new pairing component.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Concatenating a frozen off-the-shelf predictor's output as an extra input channel injects no novel insight — it reads as combining two published systems regardless of the accuracy gain.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The sibling leg does not concatenate a frozen predictor's output as a channel; it re-engineers the pairing geometry itself — two random serializations of the SAME partial graph become a positive pair whose per-edge posteriors must agree under a symmetric-KL penalty — which is a new objective primitive (per-edge-marginal agreement) rather than a bolted-on input channel."},{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a representation is 'disentangled' or property-specific without an operational definition, a direct probe, or an isolating ablation leaves the central claim ungrounded and unverifiable.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The targeted property is operationally defined (serialization-order-invariance of the per-edge posterior q_uv, measured as coefficient of variation across orders) and directly probed (serialization-stability in step 6; ECE under reordering in the falsification negative control), and the falsification negative control IS the isolating ablation that removes only the invariance pairing — so the claim is grounded and falsifiable, not asserted."},{"lesson_quoted":"A hard-pair construction strategy that closely recombines existing mixup/contrastive recipes collapses to 'incremental' the moment the nearest pair-construction baselines are missing from the comparison.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The closest pair-construction neighbor is GraphSOS (semanticscholar:1df03004af07379cff7ef6a4ba27e168b9b3c803), which makes the IDENTICAL serialization-order-sensitivity observation and constructs order variants — though for order SELECTION on a given graph, not as positive pairs in an invariance objective over an inferred posterior; the candidate's differentiation does not yet include GraphSOS as the nearest pair-construction baseline, so the unique benefit of agreement-as-invariance over order-selection is not yet measured — a mitigable experiment/differentiation completeness gap, hence borderline not triggered."},{"lesson_quoted":"Coupling a published clustering head to a published mutual-information objective via a feedback regularizer is judged a careful combination, not a contribution, when neither component nor the coupling is itself new.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate couples no published clustering head or MI objective; the load-bearing component (per-edge-marginal symmetric-KL agreement across serializations tied to a frequency-calibration term) is itself the new primitive, and core_mechanism re-derives WHY it uniquely encodes serialization-invariance (the only loss-minimizing solution is an order-invariant edge belief)."},{"lesson_quoted":"Gains attributed to a new alignment component evaporate under scrutiny when the ablation suite never isolates that component from the borrowed backbone.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The falsification plan isolates exactly the new component: the negative control replaces the two-distinct-serialization positive pairing with two identical copies (removing the invariance signal) while holding the backbone and calibration fixed, and predicts a specific downstream collapse — so the gain is attributable to the invariance objective, not the borrowed scoring LLM."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No entry is triggered (no Reject lesson is marked candidate_match: yes), so the hard floor does not fire. The aggregate is driven to borderline by two live-but-mitigable findings: entry 0 (anchor / C05) lesson 1 — the 'union of LLM-as-prior + calibration' framing is load-bearing but not yet measured against the closest LLM-prior-calibration neighbor (Statsformer, arxiv:2601.21410v3); and entry 1 (sibling / C17) lesson 3 — the nearest pair-construction baseline that shares the serialization-order observation (GraphSOS, semanticscholar:1df03004af07379cff7ef6a4ba27e168b9b3c803) is absent from differentiation. Both are differentiation/experiment-completeness gaps editable by Phase 3.3, not mechanism failures."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions the inherited framing that the graph is an INPUT the model reasons over rather than a LATENT TARGET to be inferred: the entire cluster (node classification, traversal, KG completion, graph reasoning) takes G=(V,E) as given and asks the LLM to use it, so the prior question — can the LLM infer the unknown edge set from observations/text at all, and with what confidence — is never posed as the problem to solve.","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"take an existing identifiability or recovery theorem for hidden structure and pivot on the assumption it requires for that structure to be uniquely recoverable. The dominant swap is trading a distributional assumption ... for a structural, architectural, or geometric one ... In every case the payoff is a re-proven recovery of the hidden factors, causal graph, or model parameters up to the field's standard ambiguity class ... then operationalized as a regularizer or estimator.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism performs C05's signature pivot directly: it names the recovery precondition the field imports — that a graph's structure is identified only when its edge set is SUPPLIED ('GraphLLM encodes a given adjacency into a prefix, GraphiT serializes a given E, TinyGraphEstimator regresses parameters from a given edge list') — and TRADES it for a different kind of constraint already present in the data: the LLM's semantic prior over which relations are plausible given node texts, plus serialization-invariant textual evidence ('the identifying information for the latent edge set is carried not by a supplied adjacency but by (i) the LLM's semantic prior p_LLM ... and (ii) serialization-invariant evidence in T'). The payoff is operationalized exactly as C05 prescribes — recovery up to a calibration class, delivered as an estimator/regularizer: q(e_uv=1|T)=sigma(a·l-bar_uv+b) with the serialization-invariance objective acting as the regularizer that enforces the substitute condition. This is the structural-constraint-swap-then-operationalize move, not the parent's generic 'question an assumption' gist.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf treats the LLM's serialization-order / prompt sensitivity as the measurement-noise term it must marginalize out before reporting structure: GraphiT exploits linearization choice for accuracy and the ICL-robustness probe documents that outputs flip under reordering, but no method models this variability as edge-level uncertainty in an inferred graph — the single emitted graph is reported as if order-invariant when it is not.","sub_pattern":"C17 (Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"re-engineer the PAIRING/ALIGNMENT geometry of a similarity/contrastive objective — what counts as a positive, a negative, or an alignment target — so that the targeted structural property is the only thing whose encoding minimizes the loss ... source the pairing signal from ... a complementary view of the same entity ... The decisive technical act is replacing or inverting a default geometric primitive ... This converts a generic invariance objective into an explicit geometric constraint that writes the property directly into the representation space.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism enacts C17's signature move: it pins the one structural property generic objectives discard (serialization-order-invariance of the per-edge posterior), sources the pairing signal from a complementary view of the same entity (two random serializations of the SAME partial graph as a positive pair; graphs differing in edge (u,v) as negatives), and performs the decisive geometric substitution explicitly — 'replacing the default next-token-likelihood alignment with a per-edge-marginal agreement penalty (a symmetric KL between the two views' edge-posteriors) plus a calibration term'. That per-edge-marginal-agreement primitive belongs to neither borrowed component (the scoring LLM nor a stock contrastive loss), which is exactly the 'name a primitive that belongs to neither borrowed component' bar C17 sets, so the objective writes serialization-invariance directly into q_uv rather than training generic invariance.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries instantiate their cited cluster's signature move in core_mechanism rather than the parent's generic gist: C05's recovery-precondition swap (edge-set-supplied -> LLM-semantic-prior + serialization-invariant evidence) operationalized as a calibrated per-edge posterior estimator, and C17's pairing-geometry re-engineering (per-edge-marginal symmetric-KL agreement over same-graph serializations) replacing the default next-token-likelihood alignment, are each explicitly present and load-bearing."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["assumption_audit_and_pivot","targeted_self_supervised_objective"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions (audit_decomp_supervisor / audit_decomp_prior / audit_decomp_operator) require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; the candidate's main_pattern set is {assumption_audit_and_pivot, targeted_self_supervised_objective}, which contains no heterogeneous_decomposition and no 2-way subset that matches, and the anchor companion reframe_as_solvable_object is realized at the main-pattern level but is not itself a gap_closure[].main_pattern, so no anti-pattern is triggered."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:1df03004af07379cff7ef6a4ba27e168b9b3c803","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"GraphSOS: Graph Sampling and Order Selection to Help LLMs Understand Graphs Better (2025-01) makes the EXACT observation that motivates the candidate's sibling leg: 'when the order of nodes or edges in the natural language description of a graph is shuffled, despite describing the same graph, model performance fluctuates between high performance and random guessing.' It then proposes graph sampling + ORDER SELECTION to pick a good linearization so the LLM understands a GIVEN graph better. That establishes the serialization-order-sensitivity phenomenon as known prior art, which pressures the candidate's sibling-leg framing (that no leaf treats order as the measurement-noise term). What makes the candidate STAND rather than fall: GraphSOS operates on a graph that is GIVEN and treats order as a quantity to OPTIMIZE (select the best order so the model reasons well), whereas the candidate (a) infers the UNKNOWN edge set from text — there is no given graph to reorder — and (b) treats order as the noise axis to MARGINALIZE into a calibrated per-edge posterior, not a hyperparameter to select. GraphSOS produces no edge-existence posterior, no calibration against ground-truth edge frequency, and no latent-structure inference; the candidate's load-bearing object (the serialization-marginalized, frequency-calibrated per-edge posterior over an inferred edge set) is precisely the part GraphSOS lacks. The overlap is on the order-sensitivity OBSERVATION and the construction of order variants, not on the candidate's inference target or its calibrated-posterior deliverable, so the threat is addressable rather than exact-mechanism subsumption. Timing note: GraphSOS (2025-01) predates the candidate and scoops the order-sensitivity observation and order-variant construction, not the latent-edge-inference-with-calibrated-posterior contribution.","addressable_via":"Re-anchor the sibling-leg framing and add explicit measured differentiation against GraphSOS (semanticscholar:1df03004af07379cff7ef6a4ba27e168b9b3c803): retire any implication that the serialization-order-sensitivity OBSERVATION itself is new, and re-scope the sibling novelty onto treating order as the noise axis to MARGINALIZE into a calibrated per-edge posterior over an INFERRED edge set (vs GraphSOS's order SELECTION on a given graph), adding GraphSOS as the nearest pair-construction/order baseline in differentiation_from_lit; secondarily add Statsformer (arxiv:2601.21410v3) to differentiate the anchor's LLM-prior-calibration from general LLM-prior trust-calibration. Edit hook, differentiation_from_lit, and what_step_was_missed; do not touch falsification_prediction or compute_budget."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"hook + hook_shape_rationale","issue":"paper_pointed_threat (GraphSOS semanticscholar:1df03004af07379cff7ef6a4ba27e168b9b3c803 scoops the serialization-order-sensitivity observation that motivates the sibling leg) and gap_closure_reject_check.entries[1] lesson 3 (nearest pair-construction baseline now occupied)","fix_direction":"Keep the shape-(b) structural-reframe headline that the graph is a latent target inferred under uncertainty rather than a given input, but stop implying the order-sensitivity OBSERVATION is itself new. Re-scope the surprise onto the inference target plus the calibrated relational object: order-sensitivity is known (GraphSOS already exploits it via order selection on a GIVEN graph), but no prior work infers the UNKNOWN edge set and marginalizes order into a frequency-calibrated per-edge posterior that splits edges into trustworthy vs hallucinated. Do NOT touch falsification_prediction or compute_budget (kill-switch fields, byte-identical through Phase 3.3)."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat — the order-selection line (GraphSOS) and the LLM-prior-calibration line (Statsformer) are absent from the current five-entry differentiation, so C05 Reject-lesson-1 and C17 Reject-lesson-3's 'make the difference explicit and measured' are unmet","fix_direction":"Add a differentiation entry against GraphSOS (semanticscholar:1df03004af07379cff7ef6a4ba27e168b9b3c803): it samples/selects a good serialization ORDER so an LLM understands a GIVEN graph; we infer the UNKNOWN edge set and MARGINALIZE order into a calibrated per-edge posterior, stating the measured axis (held-out edge-recovery F1 + ECE under reordering vs an order-SELECTION baseline). Add a differentiation entry against Statsformer (arxiv:2601.21410v3): it learns when to trust LLM-derived feature scores as priors for general supervised prediction via out-of-fold validation; we specialize LLM-as-prior to the latent edge set and calibrate per-edge log-odds against ground-truth edge frequency with serialization-noise folded in — a structure-inference posterior, not a tabular-feature trust gate."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"what_step_was_missed","issue":"paper_pointed_threat — the 'almost-prior' framing points only at TinyGraphEstimator; the closer structural neighbor on the order-sensitivity sub-move (GraphSOS) must be acknowledged so the genuinely-new step (latent-edge inference + calibrated posterior) is the stated contribution","fix_direction":"Keep TinyGraphEstimator as the almost_prior on the structure-from-text axis, but add one clause acknowledging that the serialization-order-sensitivity observation and order-variant construction are no longer the missing step (GraphSOS supplies them for order selection on a given graph); the substantive step still missing in BOTH is moving the inference target to the UNKNOWN edge set AND marginalizing order into a frequency-calibrated per-edge posterior — neither paper builds the calibrated latent-structure inference object."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"hook + hook_shape_rationale","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Retired any implication that the serialization-order-sensitivity observation is itself new (crediting GraphSOS) and re-anchored the shape-(b) headline onto the two genuinely-new moves: inverting the graph-is-given framing to make the edge set the latent target, and marginalizing serialization order into a frequency-calibrated per-edge posterior that flags trustworthy vs hallucinated edges (a measurement instrument), rather than selecting one favorable order for a given graph."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added a measured differentiation entry against semanticscholar:1df03004af07379cff7ef6a4ba27e168b9b3c803 (GraphSOS): it samples/selects a good serialization ORDER for a GIVEN graph, whereas we infer the UNKNOWN edge set and marginalize order into a calibrated per-edge posterior (measured by held-out edge-recovery F1 + ECE under reordering vs an order-selection baseline). Added a second entry against arxiv:2601.21410v3 (Statsformer): general LLM-prior trust-calibration for tabular prediction vs our edge-set-specialized per-edge log-odds calibration against ground-truth edge frequency."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"what_step_was_missed","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Acknowledged that both the structure-from-text readout (TinyGraphEstimator) and the order-sensitivity observation (GraphSOS) are no longer the missing step, and re-stated the genuinely-new step as the calibrated latent-edge-set inference object — moving the target to the unknown edge set AND marginalizing order into a frequency-calibrated per-edge posterior — which neither paper builds."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Infer the Graph, Don't Read It: Calibrated Per-Edge Posteriors over Latent Structure from LLM Semantic Priors\n\n**Method.** Calibrated Latent-Edge Posterior (CLEP)\n\n## Motivation\nToday, when people use a large language model (LLM) on a graph — a set of entities and the connections (edges) between them — the standard tools either hand the model a finished graph to reason over, or make the model spit out one single graph and accept it as-is. GraphLLM and GraphiT feed in a known edge list; TinyGraphEstimator is handed a graph and reports summary numbers like its density; the text-to-graph generators emit one graph and clean it up against hand-written rules. None of them ever says how SURE it is that any particular edge actually exists. So if you ask an LLM to figure out the hidden structure of a system just from a text description, you get one take-it-or-leave-it graph with no way to tell the trustworthy edges from the hallucinated ones.\n\nWhy this is solvable now: a recent result (TinyGraphEstimator, October 2025) showed that small models can already read structure out of a graph written as text — we just need to point that reading at the UNKNOWN edges instead of a given graph, and turn it into a probability. Separately, GraphSOS (January 2025) documented that simply reshuffling the ORDER in which a graph is written out can swing an LLM between being accurate and guessing randomly; GraphSOS uses that by picking a good order for a graph it already has. And the statistics for turning a raw score into a well-calibrated probability (Platt / temperature scaling, reliability diagrams) are standard and cheap.\n\nOur idea, the Calibrated Latent-Edge Posterior (CLEP): for every possible edge (u,v), ask the LLM 'does this edge exist?' over many shuffled orderings of the text, average its yes/no confidence, and calibrate that into an honest probability tied to how often such edges really exist. Edges the LLM is consistently sure about (probability near 0 or 1, stable across orderings) are trustworthy; edges it flip-flops on (probability near 0.5 or unstable) are flagged as hallucinated. We then train a light adapter so that two different orderings of the same graph are forced to give the same per-edge probabilities — making the answer order-proof by construction instead of just averaged after the fact. Where GraphSOS picks one good ordering for a given graph, we INFER the unknown graph and treat ordering as noise to average out, so the output is a graph whose every edge carries a stated, reliable confidence.\n\n## Method\n### Latent-edge readout from semantic priors\n*Read a per-edge existence signal for the UNKNOWN edge set from the LLM's semantic prior over text, not from a supplied adjacency.*\n\n1. Build a collection of relational systems written as text (entity descriptions plus a fraction of the true relations shown as evidence), each paired with its TRUE edge list; list the candidate pairs to score (all pairs for small graphs, a shortlist for large ones), and set aside one slice for calibrating probabilities and another, never-seen slice for testing. 【author decision: the method is supposed to read structure from the LLM's sense of which entities plausibly relate, but synthetic graphs have meaningless node names, so there the only signal is the relations you already showed — the authors must either give synthetic nodes meaningful descriptions (and control that) or limit the 'semantic prior' claim to the real text-attributed graphs and treat synthetic ones as an evidence-only control.】\n   - _Why_: You can only check whether an inferred edge is right, and whether your probabilities are honest, if some examples have known ground-truth edges held out from fitting.\n2. For each possible edge (u,v), shuffle the text into 16 different orderings, ask the LLM a constrained yes/no 'does this relation exist?' for each (reading its confidence from the yes/no token probabilities as a log-odds), then average them and record how much they wobble across orderings.\n\n*For each candidate pair (u,v), the per-edge log-odds $\\bar{\\ell }_{uv}$ is the length-normalized yes/no log-likelihood ratio read from the LLM's semantic prior, averaged over S random serialization orders $T^(s)$ of the description, and $\\sigma ^{2}_{uv}$ is its across-order variance — structure is read from the LLM, not a supplied adjacency.*\n$$ \\bar{\\ell}_{uv} = \\frac{1}{S}\\sum_{s=1}^{S} \\log\\frac{p_{\\mathrm{LLM}}(\\text{yes}\\mid T^{(s)},\\,u,v)}{p_{\\mathrm{LLM}}(\\text{no}\\mid T^{(s)},\\,u,v)}, \\qquad \\sigma^2_{uv} = \\mathrm{Var}_s\\big[\\ell^{(s)}_{uv}\\big] \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This reads the answer from the LLM's own sense of which relations are plausible (its semantic prior) instead of from a handed-in graph, and the wobble across orderings measures how shaky each edge is.\n\n### Calibrated per-edge posterior\n*Turn the raw per-edge log-odds into an honest, frequency-calibrated probability that flags uncertain edges.*\n\n3. On the calibration slice, fit a simple logistic rescaling so the averaged confidence becomes a probability that matches how often such edges really exist, and dilute that probability by the across-ordering wobble (using a standard variance-shrinkage formula) so shaky edges get pulled toward 50%.\n\n*The calibrated per-edge posterior q is a logistic (Platt) map of the averaged log-odds, with (a,b) fit ONCE on a held-out split with known edges y to minimize expected calibration error against empirical edge-existence frequency; the order-variance $\\sigma ^{2}_{uv}$ is added to the logit variance so order-sensitive edges are pulled toward 0.5.*\n$$ q(e_{uv}=1\\mid T) = \\sigma\\!\\big(a\\,\\bar{\\ell}_{uv} + b\\big), \\qquad a,b = \\arg\\min_{a,b}\\ \\mathrm{ECE}\\big(\\sigma(a\\,\\bar{\\ell}+b),\\ y\\big) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Raw LLM confidence is not an honest probability; calibrating it against real edge frequency makes 'probability 0.8' actually mean roughly 80% of such edges are real, and shaky edges correctly look uncertain.\n\n### Serialization-invariance objective\n*Bake order-invariance into the posterior so the same graph gives the same per-edge probabilities under any ordering.*\n\n4. Lightly fine-tune the LLM with a small LoRA adapter so two different orderings of the SAME graph are pushed to give the same per-edge probabilities, while graphs that differ only by flipping edge (u,v) are pushed apart, and the agreed probability is tied to the true label.\n\n*The serialization-invariance objective pairs two random serializations of the SAME partial graph $(q^(1), q^(2))$ and minimizes a symmetric KL between their per-edge posteriors, plus a margin term $L_{neg}$ pushing apart posteriors of graphs that genuinely differ in edge (u,v) and a calibration term $L_{cal}$ tying the agreed probability to the ground-truth label — replacing next-token-likelihood alignment with per-edge-marginal agreement.*\n$$ L = \\sum_{(u,v)} \\Big[\\mathrm{KL}\\big(q^{(1)}_{uv}\\,\\|\\,q^{(2)}_{uv}\\big) + \\mathrm{KL}\\big(q^{(2)}_{uv}\\,\\|\\,q^{(1)}_{uv}\\big)\\Big] + \\lambda_{\\mathrm{neg}} L_{\\mathrm{neg}} + \\lambda_{\\mathrm{cal}} L_{\\mathrm{cal}} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Instead of averaging orderings after the fact, this bakes order-invariance into the model: the only way to satisfy the training is to hold a belief about each edge that does not depend on how the text was ordered.\n\n### Inferred-graph assembly and trustworthy/hallucinated split\n*Assemble the per-edge posterior matrix and split the inferred graph into trustworthy versus hallucinated edges.*\n\n5. Run the adapted model on the test slice and collect every candidate edge's probability into one matrix Q — the inferred graph as a table of per-edge confidences.\n   - _Why_: This is the shared object the whole method produces: a full graph where each edge carries a calibrated, order-proof confidence.\n6. Sort edges into trustworthy (probability near 0 or 1 and stable across orderings) versus hallucinated/ambiguous (near 0.5 or unstable), using cutoffs chosen on the calibration slice, and draw the reliability diagram for the whole graph.\n   - _Why_: This is the payoff a single committed graph cannot give: you can actually point at which inferred edges to trust and which to doubt.\n\n### Calibration evaluation and faithfulness validation\n*Quantify calibration/recovery against baselines, causally certify the posterior, and run the isolating controls.*\n\n7. Measure how honest the probabilities are (expected calibration error, 15 bins) and how many true edges you recover (F1 at a fixed precision shared by all methods), against two baselines: a graph read from a single ordering, and plain repeated-sampling edge-voting.\n   - _Why_: These two baselines are the easy things people might do instead; beating them on calibration and recovery shows the marginalized, calibrated posterior is doing real work.\n8. Pick target edges, add or remove a sentence in the text that implies that relation, and check the edge's probability moves up or down as predicted; pass an edge when both edits move it the right way, and report the fraction that pass.\n   - _Why_: If poking the evidence for an edge changes its probability in the right direction, the probability really reflects the text's evidence, not an accident of the model.\n9. Compare against the baselines on held-out edge recovery; run a control that removes only the order-invariance training (pair two identical orderings instead of two different ones) and a stripped control that uses only the calibrated averaged probability with no invariance fine-tuning.\n   - _Why_: The control that kills only the invariance signal isolates its contribution: if recovery collapses, the invariance training — not the backbone — was doing the work.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 推断图，而非读取图：基于 LLM 语义先验对潜在结构的校准化逐边后验\n\n**方法名称.** Calibrated Latent-Edge Posterior (CLEP)\n\n## 研究动机\n如今，人们在图（一组实体以及它们之间的连接，即“边”）上使用大语言模型（LLM）时，标准做法要么把一张现成的图交给模型去推理，要么让模型直接吐出一张图并照单全收。GraphLLM 与 GraphiT 把已知的边列表喂进去；TinyGraphEstimator 拿到一张图后报告密度之类的汇总数字；文本到图的生成方法吐出一张图再用手写规则修补。它们都从不说明：对某条具体的边是否真的存在，自己有多“确定”。于是，如果你让 LLM 仅凭一段文字描述去推断一个系统的隐藏结构，你得到的是一张“爱要不要”的图，无法把可信的边与幻觉的边区分开。\n\n为什么现在可解：最近的一项结果（TinyGraphEstimator，2025 年 10 月）表明，小模型已经能从写成文本的图中读出结构——我们只需把这种“读取”指向“未知”的边而非给定的图，并把它变成一个概率。另外，GraphSOS（2025 年 1 月）记录到：仅仅打乱图被写出的“顺序”，就能让 LLM 在“准确”和“随机猜测”之间大幅摆动；GraphSOS 的用法是为它已有的图挑一个好顺序。而把原始分数转成校准良好概率的统计工具（Platt / temperature 缩放、可靠性图）则是标准且廉价的。\n\n我们的想法——校准化潜在边后验（Calibrated Latent-Edge Posterior, CLEP）：对每一条可能的边 (u,v)，在文本的多种打乱顺序下反复问 LLM “这条边存在吗？”，对其 yes/no 置信度求平均，再校准成一个与“此类边真实出现频率”挂钩的诚实概率。LLM 一贯笃定的边（概率接近 0 或 1、跨顺序稳定）是可信的；它来回摇摆的边（概率接近 0.5 或不稳定）被标记为幻觉。随后我们训练一个轻量适配器（LoRA），强制同一张图的两种不同顺序给出相同的逐边概率——使答案“天生防顺序”，而不仅是事后求平均。GraphSOS 是为给定的图挑一个好顺序，而我们是“推断”未知的图、并把顺序当作要平均掉的噪声，因此输出是一张每条边都带有明确、可靠置信度的图。\n\n## 方法\n### 基于语义先验的潜在边读取\n*从 LLM 对文本的语义先验中读取“未知”边集的逐边存在信号，而非从给定邻接矩阵读取。*\n\n1. 构建一批以文本写成的关系系统(实体描述 + 把一部分真实关系作为已观测证据写入,如 30%),每个配上它『真实』的边列表;其余真实边作为推断目标。列出要打分的候选对(小图用全部 $O(N^{2})$ 对,大图用召回导向的候选:节点文本嵌入的 k-NN $\\cup $ 已观测关系端点的 2-hop),并把已观测对排除在打分之外。留出一块用于校准概率、另一块从不参与拟合用于测试。【作者需决定:该方法本应从 LLM『哪些实体之间合理存在关系』的语义先验里读出结构,但合成图的节点名无语义内容,那里唯一的信号是你已展示的关系——作者须决定:要么给合成图节点赋予有意义的替代描述(真正调动该先验并控制这种注入),要么把『语义先验』主张限定在真实文本属性图切片上,把合成图当作仅含证据的拓扑对照。】\n   - _为什么_: 只有当部分样本拥有从拟合中留出的真实边标签时，你才能检验推断出的边是否正确、你给出的概率是否诚实。\n2. 对每条候选边 (u,v),把文本打乱成 S=16 种不同顺序 $T^(s),$对每种顺序用固定模板$(T^(s) +$ 焦点对 + 『回答 yes 或 no』)询问 LLM,从首 token 概率读出长度归一化的 yes/no 对数几率 $\\ell ^(s)_{uv} =$ logp(yes) $- $ logp(no)(verbalizer 为多 token 时按 token 数归一化);求平均得 $\\bar{\\ell }_{uv},$并记录跨顺序方差 $\\sigma ^{2}_{uv}($式 eq:logodds)。这把读出从『给定的邻接矩阵』迁移到 LLM 对节点文本的语义先验上。\n\n*对每个候选边 (u,v)，逐边对数几率 $\\bar{\\ell }_{uv}$ 是从 LLM 语义先验中读出的、经长度归一化的 yes/no 对数似然比，在描述文本的 S 个随机序列化顺序 $T^(s)$ 上求平均；$\\sigma ^{2}_{uv}$ 是其跨顺序方差——结构从 LLM 读出，而非来自给定的邻接矩阵。*\n$$ \\bar{\\ell}_{uv} = \\frac{1}{S}\\sum_{s=1}^{S} \\log\\frac{p_{\\mathrm{LLM}}(\\text{yes}\\mid T^{(s)},\\,u,v)}{p_{\\mathrm{LLM}}(\\text{no}\\mid T^{(s)},\\,u,v)}, \\qquad \\sigma^2_{uv} = \\mathrm{Var}_s\\big[\\ell^{(s)}_{uv}\\big] \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这是从 LLM 自身对“哪些关系合理”的判断（其语义先验）读出答案，而非从交进来的图读出；而跨顺序的波动度量了每条边有多不稳。\n\n### 校准化逐边后验\n*把原始逐边对数几率转化为诚实、按频率校准的概率，并标记出不确定的边。*\n\n3. 在校准块上拟合一个简单的 logistic 重缩放 (a,b),使 $q_{uv}$ 相对真实边出现频率的可靠性图 ECE 最小;并用 logistic-Gaussian 稀释 $q_{uv} = \\sigma ((a\\cdot \\bar{\\ell }_{uv} + b)/\\surd (1 + \\pi \\cdot a^{2}\\cdot \\sigma ^{2}_{uv}/8))($式 eq:posterior)把跨顺序方差折入,使顺序敏感的边被拉向 0.5,且不引入额外自由参数。由此交付校准好的测量对象。\n\n*校准化逐边后验 q 是对平均对数几率的 logistic（Platt）映射；参数 (a,b) 在已知边标签 y 的留出划分上一次性拟合，以最小化相对真实边频率的期望校准误差（ECE）；并把顺序方差 $\\sigma ^{2}_{uv}$ 加入 logit 方差，使顺序敏感的边被拉向 0.5。*\n$$ q(e_{uv}=1\\mid T) = \\sigma\\!\\big(a\\,\\bar{\\ell}_{uv} + b\\big), \\qquad a,b = \\arg\\min_{a,b}\\ \\mathrm{ECE}\\big(\\sigma(a\\,\\bar{\\ell}+b),\\ y\\big) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: LLM 的原始置信度并非诚实概率；用真实边频率去校准，能让“概率 0.8”真的约等于此类边中约 80% 为真，而不稳的边也会正确地显得不确定。\n\n### 序列化不变目标\n*把顺序不变性烤进后验，使同一张图在任意顺序下给出相同的逐边概率。*\n\n4. 用小型 LoRA 适配器(rank r=16,加在 attention+MLP 投影上)微调评分 LLM,损失 $L = L_{inv} + \\lambda _{neg}\\cdot L_{neg} + \\lambda _{cal}\\cdot L_{cal}($式 $eq:invloss):L_{inv}$ 是同一张图两种随机顺序的逐边后验之间的对称 KL(正样本对);$L_{neg}$ 把负样本(在同图上翻转边 (u,v) 再重排,仅焦点边不同)的 $q_{uv}$ 拉开;$L_{cal}$ 把一致后的概率绑定到真实标签。$\\lambda _{neg}=1.0$、$\\lambda _{cal}=0.5,$在校准块上调。关键替换是用逐边边缘一致性取代 next-token 似然对齐。\n\n*序列化不变目标把同一部分图的两个随机序列化 $(q^(1), q^(2))$ 配成正对，最小化其逐边后验之间的对称 KL；并加上间隔项 $L_{neg}$（推开真正在边 (u,v) 上不同的图的后验）与校准项 $L_{cal}$（把一致概率绑定到真实标签）——以逐边边际一致取代下一词似然对齐。*\n$$ L = \\sum_{(u,v)} \\Big[\\mathrm{KL}\\big(q^{(1)}_{uv}\\,\\|\\,q^{(2)}_{uv}\\big) + \\mathrm{KL}\\big(q^{(2)}_{uv}\\,\\|\\,q^{(1)}_{uv}\\big)\\Big] + \\lambda_{\\mathrm{neg}} L_{\\mathrm{neg}} + \\lambda_{\\mathrm{cal}} L_{\\mathrm{cal}} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这不是事后对顺序求平均，而是把“顺序不变性”烤进模型：要满足训练，唯一办法就是对每条边持有一个不依赖文本顺序的信念。\n\n### 推断图组装与可信/幻觉切分\n*组装逐边后验矩阵，并把推断图切分为可信边与幻觉边。*\n\n5. 用适配后的模型在测试块上重新算出 $q_{uv},$把每个关系系统所有候选对的逐边后验汇集成矩阵 Q——即以逐边置信度表格呈现的推断图。\n   - _为什么_: 这是整套方法产出的共享对象：一张完整的图，其中每条边都带有校准化、防顺序的置信度。\n6. 用在校准块上选定的阈值做切分并报告不确定性:可信 = (q $\\ge  0.9$ 或 $q \\le $ 0.1) 且 $\\sigma ^{2}_{uv}$ 低于其校准块中位数;幻觉/含糊 = 其余。产出校准后的推断图、其可靠性图,并报告该切分在校准集上的精确率/召回率,使操作点可审计。\n   - _为什么_: 这正是单一确定图给不了的收益：你能真正指出推断出的哪些边可信、哪些可疑。\n\n### 校准评估与保真性验证\n*对照基线量化校准/恢复，因果验证后验，并运行隔离性对照实验。*\n\n7. 对照两个基线——单一顺序读出的点估计图、以及解码温度下朴素的自一致性边频率——测量概率的诚实度(期望校准误差 ECE,15 个等质量桶)与真实边恢复(在所有方法共享的固定精确率如 0.9 下报告 F1,使恢复在同一精确率下比较,而非各取自身最佳阈值)。\n   - _为什么_: 这两个基线是人们可能图省事采用的替代做法；在校准与恢复上胜过它们，说明经边际化、校准的后验确实在起作用。\n8. 选一批目标边,生成配对的证据编辑——加一句暗示该关系的话(预期 q↑)、删去最能蕴含它的那句(预期 q↓)——当两种编辑都使带符号的 $\\Delta q$ 符合预期时该边通过;报告通过比例与平均带符号 $\\Delta q$ 作为因果干预曲线(不主张幅度,只看单调符号),从而证明 q 反映文本证据而非伪影。\n   - _为什么_: 若拨动某条边的证据会让其概率朝正确方向变化，说明该概率确实反映文本证据，而非模型的偶然产物。\n9. 在留出边恢复上与基线比较;做负对照(把两种不同顺序的正样本对换成两份相同副本,移除不变性信号)与正对照(只用带顺序平均的校准后验、不做不变性 LoRA),从而把增益归因于不变性目标。\n   - _为什么_: 只杀掉不变性信号的对照能隔离它的贡献：若恢复崩溃，说明是不变性训练而非骨干模型在起作用。\n\n"},{"id":"04","run_dir":"run_prompt04_llmvalue","index":4,"title":"Read the Disposition, Not the Answer: A Calibrated Cross-Model Value Distance for LLMs","title_zh":"读取倾向而非回答：面向 LLM 的校准化跨模型价值距离","method_name":"Probe-Invariant Value Distance (PIVD)","hook":"Every retrieved value-measurement method reads a model's disposition off the text it answers to value prompts and reports a per-model score against humans; we instead read the disposition from a probe-invariant direction inside the model and turn the open question 'how far apart are two models' values' into a single calibrated two-sample distance with a significance null — without ever scoring either model against a human reference.","anchor_pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","anchor_pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","domain_category":"LLM Alignment, Safety & Behavior","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved paper tests whether a model's value disposition must be read off its surface elicitation responses at all: every leaf inherits from questionnaire-style evaluation the unexamined assumption that value is whatever the model answers to value prompts, and so measures values entirely from output text, never asking whether the quantity being measured could instead be anchored in something the model exposes beyond its prompted answer.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"unify_into_shared_representation","how_closed":"Closed by relocating the measurement locus (C01): the value readout is moved from the model's surface answer text to a model-internal value direction recovered by a value-contrast probe, and the companion unify_into_shared_representation (C18) ships the deliverable — a learned orthogonal alignment that maps every model's per-model value direction into one shared cross-model value basis, so a value coordinate read at the new locus is comparable across two LLMs, which a bare per-model internal probe (collateral c2) is not. The two halves together state the inverted assumption (value need not be read off answers) AND ship the runnable cross-model-aligned value representation that makes the next leg's distance well defined.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved method yields a calibrated, probe-invariant quantity for the value distance BETWEEN two LLMs: every measurement collapses to a per-model point score against a human reference (per-model MFT profiles, per-model value-rationality, per-model bias scores), so there is no relational measure that says how far apart two models' value dispositions are and whether that gap is significant given the instrument's noise.","pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by recasting the opaque 'value distance between two models' as a concrete, well-studied measurement object (C00): a kernel maximum-mean-discrepancy between the two models' distributions of aligned value coordinates, equipped with a permutation null that converts the raw distance into a calibrated, uncertainty-bearing quantity. Because the feature space the MMD runs over is the value-anchored, probe-invariant basis built in the anchor leg (not raw output text), the divergence is a value distance rather than a text-style distance, and its faithfulness is certified by a causal intervention (perturbing the value direction shifts the distance in the predicted direction) rather than by plausibility.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"measuring and comparing the value dispositions (moral / political / cultural values) of large language models","n_papers":48,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":24},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":10,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"OpenFedLLM: Training Large Language Models on Decentralized Private Data via Federated Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Raising the Bar: Investigating the Values of Large Language Models via Generative Evolving Testing"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Uncovering Factor Level Preferences to Improve Human-Model Alignment"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Designing Staged Evaluation Workflows for LLMs: Integrating Domain Experts, Lay Users, and Model-Generated Evaluation Criteria"},{"source":"openalex","title":"LocalValueBench: A Collaboratively Built and Extensible Benchmark for Evaluating Localized Value Alignment and Ethical Safety in Large Language Models"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Cultural bias and cultural alignment of large language models"}],"more":4},{"year":2025,"n":29,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Towards Better Value Principles for Large Language Model Alignment: A Systematic Evaluation and Enhancement"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Evaluation of Best-of-N Sampling Strategies for Language Model Alignment"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Bridging the Evaluation Gap: Leveraging Large Language Models for Topic Model Evaluation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Prompt-Based Value Steering of Large Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"PediaMind-R1: A Temperament-Aware Language Model for Personalized Early Childhood Care Reasoning via Cognitive Modeling and Preference Alignment"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Differences in the Moral Foundations of Large Language Models"}],"more":23},{"year":2026,"n":9,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Alignment Verifiability in Large Language Models: Normative Indistinguishability under Behavioral Evaluation"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Introducing MELI: the Mandarin-English Language Interview Corpus"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"SHARP: Social Harm Analysis via Risk Profiles for Measuring Inequities in Large Language Models"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Targeted Syntactic Evaluation of Language Models on Georgian Case Alignment"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"TARAZ: Persian Short-Answer Question Benchmark for Cultural Evaluation of Language Models"}],"more":3}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":29,"share":0.604},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":6,"share":0.125},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":6,"share":0.125},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":6,"share":0.125},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":4,"share":0.083},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":2,"share":0.042},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":1,"share":0.021},{"pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","count":1,"share":0.021}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Current LLM value measurement queries a model with a fixed probe set (moral-foundations questionnaires, political batteries, ethical dilemmas) and scores the elicited answers against a human reference, so the reported quantity is a per-model alignment-to-humans score rather than a relational, calibrated estimate of how two models' value dispositions differ; and because the score is read off surface elicitation responses, it is confounded by probe wording, format, and ordering — instability that the literature repeatedly observes but never separates from the underlying value signal. Across the frontier this confound is documented (a model's revealed moral preferences are unstable across dilemmas in From-Stability-to-Inconsistency (openalex:W4417241780) and questionnaire-based probing is too unstable for reliable cross-model comparison in In-Context political-bias testing (openalex:W7082255185)), yet every measurement still reduces to a point score against humans: Differences in the Moral Foundations (semanticscholar:5f0fce77c6d5d80f79781813434cc2295fc6336c) reports per-model MFT profiles, Heterogeneous Value Alignment Evaluation (openalex:W4413028873) scores each model's value rationality against a fixed target, and Alignment Verifiability (arxiv:2602.05656v2) proves that finite behavioral evaluation cannot even identify a latent alignment property — but stops at a yes/no verifiability theorem and supplies no constructive estimator of the latent value-disposition difference between two models. The result is that no retrieved method yields a probe-invariant, calibrated quantity for the value distance between two LLMs, and the field cannot say whether a measured difference is a real disposition gap or an artifact of the elicitation instrument.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.05656v2","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Alignment Verifiability reframes behavioral alignment evaluation as a statistical identifiability problem under partial observability: it formalizes a behavioral alignment test as a finite evaluation regime and asks whether a latent alignment property is identifiable from the finite observable interaction set, proving normative-indistinguishability conditions under which two policies producing the same observed behavior are unverifiable. Its residue: the result is a yes/no verifiability/indistinguishability theorem about a single agent's latent property; it never turns the identifiability machinery into a constructive, calibrated ESTIMATOR of how far apart two models' latent value dispositions are, and it does not anchor the latent quantity in anything model-internal, so the gap between 'unverifiable behaviorally' and 'measurable as a difference' is left entirely open."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:5f0fce77c6d5d80f79781813434cc2295fc6336c","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Differences in the Moral Foundations of LLMs elicits Moral Foundations Theory judgments from many frontier models and reports per-model moral-foundation profiles, surfacing that models differ. Its residue: the profile is a vector of questionnaire responses scored against the MFT human instrument, so the reported 'difference' is the gap between two questionnaire fits — it carries no calibration for probe noise and no guarantee the elicited profile reflects the model's behavioral disposition rather than its surface answer style."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4413028873","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Heterogeneous Value Alignment Evaluation defines a 'value rationality' metric measuring how well a model's behavior corresponds to a given value, decomposing alignment across heterogeneous value dimensions. Its residue: value rationality is still scored per model against a fixed target value, so it measures alignment-to-a-target, not the relational distance between two models' value systems, and the metric inherits the same elicitation surface (behavior on prescribed scenarios) without modeling probe-induced variance."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7082255185","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"In-Context Political-Bias Testing introduces Questionnaire Modeling, using human survey data as in-context examples to stabilize question-based bias probing and make model comparisons less unreliable. Its residue: stability is bought by conditioning the probe rather than by a measurement model that separates probe variance from value variance, so the improvement is an ad-hoc reduction of the instrument's noise, not a calibrated estimate of cross-model value difference with a stated uncertainty."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415013405","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Beyond Human Judgment runs a large Bayesian moral evaluation that models annotator disagreement as aleatoric vs epistemic uncertainty when comparing LLM moral judgments to humans. Its residue: the uncertainty modeled is in the human labels, not in the elicitation of the model's own value distribution, and the output is still each model scored against humans rather than a posterior over the value-disposition difference between two models."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7082278716","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Target-Oriented Sentiment Classification probes political bias by varying the target entity in a fixed sentence and defines an entropy-based inconsistency metric over the resulting prediction variability. Its residue: the metric quantifies within-model inconsistency on a sentiment task, not a calibrated between-model value divergence, and it has no anchor tying the measured variability to a value disposition rather than to task-level noise."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"measuring and comparing the value dispositions (moral / political / cultural values) of large language models","venue":"ICLR/NeurIPS/ACL-tier ML","time":"2026","data":["public value/moral/political probe sets (Moral Foundations questionnaires, World Values Survey items, political-compass batteries)","model-internal activations / logits from a panel of open and API LLMs","human survey reference distributions (e.g. nationally-representative survey data)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"LLM evaluation + alignment + statistical measurement","preference":"both","baseline":"moral-foundations elicitation (Differences in Moral Foundations), questionnaire-modeling political probes (In-Context political bias testing), Bayesian moral evaluation, Alignment Verifiability identifiability analysis, Heterogeneous Value Alignment Evaluation","limitation":"value measurement reads a model's answers to value probes and scores them against a fixed human reference, so the reported quantity is a per-model alignment-to-humans score that is confounded by prompt/format sensitivity and gives no calibrated, probe-invariant measure of how far two models' value dispositions actually differ","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","compute","expertise","preference","data"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object both legs read from and write to is the probe-invariant value coordinate v_m(x) = U_m^T d_m(x) for model m on probe item x, where d_m(x) ∈ R^{h} is the model's hidden state at a fixed read layer ℓ (selected once per model as the layer maximizing value-contrast probe accuracy on a held-out value-contrast set, default the layer at 2/3 depth) summarizing the residual-stream activation over the answer span, and U_m ∈ R^{h × k} is model m's value basis (k=12 columns, one orthonormal direction per value axis from Moral-Foundations + Schwartz dimensions). Anchor leg (C01 + unify_into_shared_representation): we audit the field-wide assumption that value must be read off the answer text — Differences in Moral Foundations reads MFT profiles from questionnaire answers, In-Context Political-Bias reads bias from generated responses, VALUEFLOW extracts value profiles from generated text — and RELOCATE the readout to a model-internal locus: for each value axis j we form contrastive prompt pairs that hold topic and format fixed and flip only the value polarity (a value-affirming vs value-violating completion of the same scenario), and fit U_m's column j as the top direction separating the paired activations (a difference-of-means / linear-probe direction), giving a per-model value readout that does NOT route through the surface answer. This alone re-occupies collateral c2 (a per-model probe is not cross-model comparable), so the companion supplies the missing deliverable: we manufacture a shared cross-model value substrate by learning, on a small anchor set of N_a value-contrast items rendered identically to every model, an orthogonal Procrustes map O_m ∈ O(k) per model that rotates each U_m into a common reference frame fixed by a designated reference model, minimizing Σ_x ‖ O_m v_m(x) − O_{m0} v_{m0}(x) ‖^2 over the shared anchor items; the aligned coordinate is ṽ_m(x) = O_m U_m^T d_m(x). This artifact — a value coordinate read inside the model and rotated into one shared basis — closes the subtractive gap because the measured quantity is now anchored in something the model exposes beyond its prompted answer, and it is cross-model comparable. Sibling leg (C00): with both models' dispositions living as point clouds {ṽ_A(x)} and {ṽ_B(x)} in the one shared basis, we recast 'how far apart are two models' values' as a kernel MMD, D(A,B) = ‖ μ_A − μ_B ‖_{H_K} estimated with an RBF kernel over aligned coordinates, and calibrate it with a permutation null: pool the two coordinate sets, repeatedly re-split, and report D(A,B) against the permutation distribution as a z-score / p-value, so the output is a relational distance WITH a stated significance rather than a per-model point score. Probe-induced variance is marginalized at this object: each item x is presented under P reworded/reordered probe variants, the coordinate ṽ_m(x) is averaged over variants before entering the MMD, and the across-variant covariance is folded into the kernel bandwidth, so wording noise inflates the null rather than the signal. The two legs share the single primitive ṽ — the anchor makes it internal and cross-model-aligned, the sibling turns its two-sample divergence into a calibrated distance — which is why this reads as one paper. Quantitatively this departs from prior work: Alignment Verifiability (arxiv:2602.05656v2) proves only a yes/no identifiability result and supplies no estimator, whereas D(A,B) is a constructive estimate of the latent value-disposition difference; and unlike a raw-output MMD (collateral c3) the kernel runs over a value-anchored basis, not text embeddings.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The two gaps share machinery because the same object — the aligned value coordinate ṽ — is simultaneously what the anchor must make internal-and-cross-model-comparable and what the sibling must turn into a calibrated relational distance; the evidence they are one object is that the MMD the sibling calibrates is computed directly over the coordinates the anchor's probe-and-alignment produce, so splitting them would double-represent the same value state. REGRESSION CHECK (method_lineage): I avoided c1 (questionnaire IRT / latent-trait fit on answers — my readout never scores answer text, it reads activations), c2 (a per-model internal probe with no cross-model comparability — the Procrustes alignment into a shared basis is exactly the cross-model-comparability move c2 lacks, so I do not stop at a per-model direction), and c3 (a raw-output MMD / two-sample test — my kernel runs over the value-anchored aligned basis, not text embeddings, so the distance is a value distance not a text-style distance), and n2/n3-n9 (per-model alignment-to-humans scoring — my output is model-vs-model and never references a human reference distribution). The unoccupied source I draw on is the COMPOSITION the tree does not yet occupy: an internal value-direction readout PLUS a cross-model basis alignment PLUS a calibrated divergence over the aligned features. I considered (and rejected) two alternatives: a pure questionnaire-IRT design (rejected: regresses to c1, still reads answers); and running MMD on raw response embeddings (rejected: regresses to c3, measures style not value). Recorded avoided nodes: c1, c2, c3, n2.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on a panel of 8-12 open and API LLMs, build the internal value basis U_m and the cross-model alignment O_m, then compute the calibrated MMD distance matrix D and compare it against (i) per-model surface scores (MFT-profile distance, value-rationality distance) recomputed from the same models' answers and (ii) a human-anchored construct-validity reference where ground-truth ordering of model pairs is fixed by an independent behavioral preference task the probe never saw (e.g. pairwise value-laden choice agreement). If the candidate works, the internal calibrated distance recovers the held-out behavioral pairwise ordering of models with higher rank correlation than the surface-score distances, and — the non-obvious direction — the internal distance stays stable (low coefficient of variation across the P probe rewordings) while the surface-score ordering reorders under the same rewordings, because the coordinate is read off a probe-invariant direction rather than off answer text. Mechanism distinguisher built on the single load-bearing variable, the probe-invariant aligned value coordinate ṽ: negative control replaces each model's learned Procrustes alignment O_m with a random orthogonal rotation (its producer ablated) while keeping every other step; the predicted effect is that the downstream held-out behavioral-ranking recovery collapses to chance (NOT merely that the coordinates change), which is the real Popper test, since 'the coordinates moved' alone is equally consistent with a re-scaled but still-valid basis. Positive control: a stripped model using ONLY the aligned internal coordinate (no probe-variant averaging, no kernel-bandwidth inflation) should already recover most of the cross-model ranking, identifying the internal-and-aligned readout as the load-bearing mechanism.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.05656v2","delta":"Alignment Verifiability proves a yes/no identifiability theorem about whether one agent's latent alignment property is recoverable from finite behavior; we construct a calibrated MMD ESTIMATOR of how far apart two models' latent value dispositions are, anchored in a model-internal value basis they leave entirely unaddressed, turning their unverifiability verdict into a measurable relational distance with a significance null."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:5f0fce77c6d5d80f79781813434cc2295fc6336c","delta":"Differences in the Moral Foundations reports per-model MFT profiles scored from questionnaire ANSWERS and reads 'difference' as the gap between two questionnaire fits; we read value from an internal probe-invariant direction (never from the answer text) and report a calibrated cross-model distance with a permutation null, so the difference is anchored and significance-bearing rather than a noisy answer-style gap."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4413028873","delta":"Heterogeneous Value Alignment Evaluation decomposes alignment into value dimensions but still scores each model against a fixed human target (alignment-to-a-target); we build a relational model-to-model distance in a shared internal value basis with no human reference at all, and calibrate it against probe noise."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7082255185","delta":"In-Context Political-Bias Testing stabilizes question-based probing by conditioning on survey exemplars, reducing instrument noise ad hoc while still emitting per-model questionnaire fits; we marginalize probe-induced variance into the kernel bandwidth of a relational distance, so wording noise inflates the significance null rather than being patched out of a per-model score."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.03160v1","delta":"VALUEFLOW calibrates value intensity for ONE model's values from generated text; we calibrate the DISTANCE between two models' value dispositions read from internal directions, supplying the intensity-calibrated BETWEEN-model comparison it never constructs and removing the dependence on generated text."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"arxiv:2602.05656v2","what_step_was_missed":"Alignment Verifiability frames behavioral value evaluation as statistical identifiability under partial observability and proves normative-indistinguishability conditions, but stops at a yes/no verifiability claim about a single agent's latent property. For our contribution to already exist it would have needed to (a) construct the latent value disposition as a concrete model-internal readout — a probe-invariant value direction recovered from activations rather than a behaviorally-defined latent it never instantiates — and (b) build a cross-model alignment plus a calibrated two-sample divergence over those readouts so the latent becomes a measurable RELATIONAL distance with a significance null. It made neither move: its latent stays behaviorally-defined and single-agent, so it can declare unverifiability but cannot measure how far apart two models' dispositions are."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":322,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"Layer 1 hard floor does not fire: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict is borderline (no Reject lesson is candidate_match: yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat is NOT exact-mechanism overlap (Universal Refusal Circuits aligns one behavioral direction to transfer an intervention and supplies no calibrated relational value-distance, permutation null, or probe-variance marginalization — the candidate's load-bearing C00 object). Layer 2 selects revise because paper_pointed_threat exists AND addressable_via names specific candidate fields (hook, differentiation_from_lit, what_step_was_missed), reinforced by gap_closure_reject_check.entries[0].reject_lessons_evaluated lesson 'Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work ... collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured' being borderline-live against the now-occupied cross-model-direction-alignment locus. recipe_application_check is applied for both legs, so core_mechanism is sound; the fix is repositioning/differentiation, not a mechanism rebuild.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved paper tests whether a model's value disposition must be read off its surface elicitation responses at all: every leaf inherits from questionnaire-style evaluation the unexamined assumption that value is whatever the model answers to value prompts, and so measures values entirely from output text, never asking whether the quantity being measured could instead be anchored in something the model exposes beyond its prompted answer.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"A second shape is a novelty-boundary collapse — the 'new' locus turns out to be one a prior paper already used (normalization statistics, activation-similarity alignment, pre-encoded semantic concepts), and the work fails to quantify what is genuinely different. A fourth is offering only a demonstration with no mechanistic account of why the locus carries the signal, which reads as a stacked pipeline of off-the-shelf parts.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a relocated signal is 'stealthier' or 'harder to remove' without defeating an adaptive defender who searches the same new locus leaves the central claim unverified.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"This is a measurement-method setting with no adversary; the candidate makes no stealth/removal-robustness claim, so this adversarial-closure lesson has no trigger field."},{"lesson_quoted":"Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work — normalization statistics, activation-similarity losses, semantic concept triggers — collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The anchor's new locus (a value direction read from internal activations, then aligned across models into a shared basis) overlaps a published locus: per-model concept/value directions are the collateral-c2 family, and Universal Refusal Circuits (semanticscholar:aad4c2b6527beec4857fbfc425ad915525784120) already aligns concept directions across models via concept-basis reconstruction; the candidate's difference is real (a calibrated cross-model value-DISTANCE estimator with a permutation null, not a transferred steering direction) but differentiation_from_lit does not yet name and measure the difference against that cross-model-direction-alignment line — mitigable by editing differentiation_from_lit + what_step_was_missed, hence borderline not triggered."},{"lesson_quoted":"A defense whose relocation silently depends on a clean reference model or a known anomaly distribution reintroduces precisely the strong assumption the move was supposed to eliminate.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate's designated reference model is only the Procrustes basis anchor that fixes a common rotation frame, not an assumed-clean oracle or a human reference distribution; it explicitly removes the alignment-to-humans reference (core_mechanism: 'never references a human reference distribution'), so it does not reintroduce a privileged clean standard."},{"lesson_quoted":"Demonstrating the new locus only on fixed, non-adaptive or outdated baselines while omitting any account of why it works reads as a stacked pipeline of existing components rather than a principled shift.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism supplies the WHY the new locus carries the value signal — the value-contrast difference-of-means direction separates value-polarity-flipped activations with topic/format held fixed, and the Procrustes alignment is what makes that direction cross-model comparable — plus a causal-intervention certification (step 10), rather than only demonstrating that it works."},{"lesson_quoted":"Wiring off-the-shelf generators or tools into a new attack setting without a structural reason for the locus change gets judged as engineering integration, not insight.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The locus change is justified structurally (value read from a probe-invariant internal direction rather than answer text, with cross-model alignment supplying comparability), not by bolting an off-the-shelf probe onto a benchmark; the insight is the composition internal-readout + cross-model-alignment + calibrated-divergence, which the lineage tree records as unoccupied."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved method yields a calibrated, probe-invariant quantity for the value distance BETWEEN two LLMs: every measurement collapses to a per-model point score against a human reference (per-model MFT profiles, per-model value-rationality, per-model bias scores), so there is no relational measure that says how far apart two models' value dispositions are and whether that gap is significant given the instrument's noise.","main_pattern":"reframe_as_solvable_object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The signature failure is treating the reframing as a mechanical wrapper: taking an established attribution, decomposition, or estimation tool and pointing it at a new input granularity, a new architecture, or a new domain without re-deriving why the resulting scores are faithful to the model — no causal validation that the identified components actually drive behavior, no axiomatic argument for why the proposed definition is the 'real' quantity, and no confound control.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Pointing an off-the-shelf decomposition at a coarser input granularity without showing the coarser units preserve the signal reads as a wrapper, not a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The MMD is not pointed at a coarser off-the-shelf granularity; it runs over the value-anchored aligned basis the anchor leg constructs, and core_mechanism establishes that this basis preserves the value signal (value-contrast direction fitting + cross-model alignment), not a coarsened input."},{"lesson_quoted":"Porting a known attribution technique to a new architecture or domain while ignoring that technique's documented failure modes — and omitting comparisons to alternatives — leaves reviewers unable to see any unique benefit.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"MMD/two-sample testing is a mature technique (collateral c3) and the candidate ports it to the value-difference setting; differentiation_from_lit names the value-anchored-basis distinction from a raw-output MMD, but the experiment plan does not yet include a raw-output-embedding-MMD baseline as an explicit alternative, so the unique benefit of the anchored feature space over a text-embedding MMD is not yet cleanly measured — a non-load-bearing experiment-completeness gap surfaceable to Phase 4."},{"lesson_quoted":"Proposing a new attribution definition without an axiomatic or causal argument for why it should count as ground-truth collapses the moment a reviewer asks why this is the real importance.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate does not rest on plausibility: the value coordinate's faithfulness is certified causally (step 10 — perturbing the value direction shifts the distance in the predicted direction and changes a known pairwise ranking), and validity is anchored to an independent held-out behavioral preference task, exactly the causal/axiomatic grounding the lesson demands."},{"lesson_quoted":"Conflating a methodological artifact — a computation-granularity difference, a degenerate zero baseline — with genuine signal undermines the entire premise once the confound is identified.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The probe-induced variance confound is explicitly controlled — items are presented under P rewording variants, coordinates averaged over variants, and the across-variant covariance folded into the kernel bandwidth so wording noise inflates the null rather than the signal — rather than conflated with the value signal."},{"lesson_quoted":"Building a suppression or privacy method without formalizing the threat model leaves the central guarantee unverifiable regardless of strong empirical numbers.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Not a suppression/privacy setting; the central object (the calibrated MMD distance with a permutation null) is fully operationally defined and its significance is the verifiable guarantee, so there is no unformalized threat model."},{"lesson_quoted":"Surveying or recombining fragmented methods without a unifying axis or a decisive controlled experiment yields a contribution reviewers dismiss as anecdotal.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The two legs are unified by a single shared object (the aligned value coordinate v-tilde) and the falsification_prediction supplies a decisive controlled experiment (negative control = random orthogonal alignment collapses held-out behavioral-ranking recovery to chance), so it is not a survey-style recombination."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No entry is triggered (no Reject lesson is marked candidate_match: yes), so the hard floor does not fire. The aggregate is driven to borderline by entry 0 (anchor gap / assumption_audit_and_pivot), where the lesson 'Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work ... collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured' is live: the internal-value-direction locus, and specifically cross-model direction ALIGNMENT, is now occupied by Universal Refusal Circuits and the candidate's differentiation has not yet measured the difference against it. Entry 1 (sibling gap / reframe_as_solvable_object) is borderline only on a missing raw-output-MMD baseline; its decisive Reject triggers (no causal validation, no confound control, no operational definition) are all cleanly avoided."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved paper tests whether a model's value disposition must be read off its surface elicitation responses at all: every leaf inherits from questionnaire-style evaluation the unexamined assumption that value is whatever the model answers to value prompts, and so measures values entirely from output text, never asking whether the quantity being measured could instead be anchored in something the model exposes beyond its prompted answer.","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Name the single representational locus current methods all operate on, state the tacit sufficiency/invariance claim bolted to it, then relocate the signal to a different locus the field treated as irrelevant — 'relocate the signal', 're-anchor enforcement', 'demonstrate robustness at the new locus' — and supply a mechanistic account of WHY the new locus carries the signal, not merely evidence THAT it does.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism performs the signature move directly: it names the audited locus ('value must be read off the answer text — Differences in Moral Foundations reads MFT profiles from questionnaire answers, In-Context Political-Bias reads bias from generated responses, VALUEFLOW extracts value profiles from generated text') and relocates the readout to a model-internal locus ('for each value axis j we form contrastive prompt pairs that hold topic and format fixed and flip only the value polarity ... and fit U_m's column j as the top direction separating the paired activations'). The required WHY-account is present and load-bearing: the value-polarity contrast with topic/format held fixed is what makes the recovered direction carry value rather than surface style, and the Procrustes alignment is the explicit reason the new-locus readout becomes cross-model comparable — an invariance/comparability argument, exactly C01 step 5, not a bare demonstration.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved method yields a calibrated, probe-invariant quantity for the value distance BETWEEN two LLMs: every measurement collapses to a per-model point score against a human reference (per-model MFT profiles, per-model value-rationality, per-model bias scores), so there is no relational measure that says how far apart two models' value dispositions are and whether that gap is significant given the instrument's noise.","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Recast an opaque question as a concrete measurement over a well-studied object (counterfactual optimization, subset selection, expectation/estimator, decomposition, influence/Shapley), choosing the right unit of analysis and faithfulness constraint so the scores reflect the model's actual computation, and certify fidelity by a causal intervention that flips behavior when the identified object is perturbed — not by plausibility.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism enacts the signature move: it recasts the opaque 'value distance between two models' as a concrete estimator over a well-studied object ('a kernel maximum-mean-discrepancy between the two models' distributions of aligned value coordinates, equipped with a permutation null'), fixes the faithfulness constraint that makes it the right object ('the feature space the MMD runs over is the value-anchored, probe-invariant basis ... not raw output text, so the divergence is a value distance rather than a text-style distance'), and certifies fidelity causally ('its faithfulness is certified by a causal intervention — perturbing the value direction shifts the distance in the predicted direction'), exactly C00 step 5 rather than plausibility.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries instantiate their cited cluster's signature move in core_mechanism rather than the parent pattern's generic gist: C01's locus-relocation (surface-answer readout -> internal value direction) with the value-polarity-contrast/Procrustes WHY-account, and C00's recast-as-measurement-object (kernel MMD + permutation null over a value-anchored basis) with a causal-intervention fidelity certification, are each explicitly present."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["assumption_audit_and_pivot","reframe_as_solvable_object"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions (audit_decomp_supervisor / audit_decomp_prior / audit_decomp_operator) require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; the candidate's main_pattern set is {assumption_audit_and_pivot, reframe_as_solvable_object}, which contains no heterogeneous_decomposition and no 2-way subset that matches, and the anchor companion unify_into_shared_representation is realized at the main-pattern level but is not itself a gap_closure[].main_pattern, so no anti-pattern is triggered."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:aad4c2b6527beec4857fbfc425ad915525784120","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"Universal Refusal Circuits Across LLMs (arXiv 2026-01) hypothesizes that a behavior (refusal) 'stems from a universal, low-dimensional semantic circuit shared across models' and builds Trajectory Replay via Concept-Basis Reconstruction, which 'aligns layers via concept fingerprints and reconstructs refusal directions using a shared recipe of concept atoms' across 8 model pairs spanning Dense and MoE architectures. That establishes exactly the candidate's anchor sub-move — that an internal concept/value direction can be read per model AND aligned into a shared cross-model basis — so the bare claim 'a model's value disposition can be read internally and made cross-model comparable' is no longer untested, which pressures the candidate's anchor-leg novelty (gap / assumption_audit_and_pivot + companion unify_into_shared_representation). What makes the candidate's claim STAND rather than fall: Universal Refusal Circuits aligns a single behavioral direction to TRANSFER an intervention (steer/ablate refusal in a target model) — it produces no calibrated relational quantity, no two-sample DISTANCE between two models' value distributions, no significance null, and no probe-variance marginalization; the candidate's load-bearing object is precisely the part it lacks — a calibrated MMD value-distance with a permutation null over the aligned value coordinates (sibling C00 leg), which converts the alignment from a steering tool into a measurement instrument. The overlap is therefore on the anchor's alignment sub-move, not on the candidate's full mechanism, so the threat is addressable rather than exact-mechanism subsumption. Timing note: the threat (2026-01) is within the recent window but predates the candidate; it scoops the alignment-feasibility claim, not the calibrated-distance contribution.","addressable_via":"Re-anchor the hook and add explicit measured differentiation against Universal Refusal Circuits (semanticscholar:aad4c2b6527beec4857fbfc425ad915525784120): retire any implication that cross-model internal-direction ALIGNMENT is itself new, and re-scope novelty onto the calibrated relational value-DISTANCE estimator with a permutation null and probe-variance marginalization (the sibling C00 object) that turns a transferable direction into a measurement; edit differentiation_from_lit and what_step_was_missed accordingly."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"hook + hook_shape_rationale","issue":"paper_pointed_threat (Universal Refusal Circuits semanticscholar:aad4c2b6527beec4857fbfc425ad915525784120 scoops the cross-model internal-direction alignment sub-move) and gap_closure_reject_check.entries[0] lesson 2 (novelty-boundary collapse at a now-occupied locus)","fix_direction":"Keep the shape-(b) structural-reframe headline that value is read off a probe-invariant internal direction rather than answer text, but stop implying the internal readout / cross-model alignment is itself unexamined. Re-scope the surprise onto the CALIBRATED RELATIONAL object: cross-model internal value directions can be aligned (Universal Refusal Circuits already does this to transfer interventions), but no prior work converts that aligned representation into a calibrated two-sample value DISTANCE with a permutation null and probe-variance marginalization — i.e., into a measurement instrument rather than a steering tool. Do NOT touch falsification_prediction or compute_budget (kill-switch fields, byte-identical through Phase 3.3)."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat — the cross-model internal-direction-alignment line (Universal Refusal Circuits) is absent from the current five-entry differentiation, so C01 Reject-lesson-2's 'make the difference explicit and measured' is unmet","fix_direction":"Add a differentiation entry against semanticscholar:aad4c2b6527beec4857fbfc425ad915525784120 (Universal Refusal Circuits, arXiv 2026-01): it aligns a single behavioral (refusal) direction across models via concept-basis reconstruction to TRANSFER an ablation intervention; we align value directions across models to compute a calibrated MMD value-DISTANCE with a permutation null and probe-variance-marginalized kernel — a relational measurement with significance, not a transferred steering direction — and we certify it causally against a held-out behavioral preference ranking; state the measured axis (cross-model value-distance recovery vs surface-score distance, not refusal-transfer success)."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"what_step_was_missed","issue":"paper_pointed_threat — the 'almost-prior' framing currently points only at Alignment Verifiability; the closer structural neighbor on the alignment sub-move (Universal Refusal Circuits) must be acknowledged so the genuinely-new step (the calibrated relational distance) is the stated contribution","fix_direction":"Keep Alignment Verifiability as the almost_prior on the relational-estimator axis, but add one clause acknowledging that cross-model internal-direction alignment is no longer the missing step (Universal Refusal Circuits supplies it for refusal transfer); the substantive step still missing in BOTH is the construction of a calibrated two-sample value-DISTANCE estimator with a significance null over the aligned coordinates plus probe-variance marginalization — neither paper builds the relational measurement object."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"hook + hook_shape_rationale","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Retired any implication that cross-model internal-direction alignment is itself new (crediting Universal Refusal Circuits) and re-anchored the shape-(b) headline onto the calibrated relational value-distance estimator with a permutation null and probe-variance marginalization that turns an aligned value direction into a measurement instrument rather than a steering tool."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added a measured differentiation entry against semanticscholar:aad4c2b6527beec4857fbfc425ad915525784120 (Universal Refusal Circuits): it aligns one behavioral direction across models to transfer an ablation, whereas we align value directions to compute a calibrated MMD value-distance with a permutation null, causally certified against a held-out behavioral preference ranking."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"what_step_was_missed","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Acknowledged that cross-model internal-direction alignment is no longer the missing step (Universal Refusal Circuits supplies it for refusal transfer) and re-stated the genuinely-new step as the calibrated two-sample value-distance estimator with a significance null and probe-variance marginalization that neither Alignment Verifiability nor Universal Refusal Circuits constructs."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Read the Disposition, Not the Answer: A Calibrated Cross-Model Value Distance for LLMs\n\n**Method.** Probe-Invariant Value Distance (PIVD)\n\n## Motivation\nToday, if you want to know how differently two large language models (LLMs) think about moral, political, or cultural values, the standard tools give you a per-model report card graded against people: each model answers a fixed set of value questionnaires and gets a score for how human-like its answers are. That has two problems. First, it never directly tells you how far apart two MODELS are — only how each one compares to humans. Second, the score is read straight off the text the model writes, so it wobbles when you reword, reorder, or reformat the questions; the field keeps noticing this wobble but never separates it from the real value signal.\n\nWhy this is solvable now: researchers can already read a 'value direction' from inside a model's activations (not just its words), and a very recent result (Universal Refusal Circuits, January 2026) showed that such internal directions can be ALIGNED across different models — even across different architectures. Separately, Alignment Verifiability (February 2026) proved that watching a model's behavior alone may be unable to pin down its hidden value property, which is exactly the missing piece an internal reading can supply. And the statistics for comparing two distributions with a confidence/significance number (a kernel two-sample test called MMD, Maximum Mean Discrepancy) are standard and cheap.\n\nOur idea, Probe-Invariant Value Distance (PIVD): read each model's values from an internal direction instead of its answer text; rotate every model's reading into one shared frame so they are comparable; then measure the DISTANCE between two models as a calibrated two-sample test with a significance value, while averaging over many rewordings so question-wording noise inflates the uncertainty instead of the answer. The earlier internal-alignment work transfers a single behavior (like refusal) to steer a model; we instead turn the aligned reading into a measuring instrument — a number that says how far apart two models' values are and whether that gap is real.\n\n## Method\n### Internal value readout\n*Read each model's value disposition from a probe-invariant internal direction instead of its answer text.*\n\n1. For each value axis (the Moral-Foundations and Schwartz values, about 15 in total), write pairs of short scenarios that are identical except one upholds the value and one violates it; also make about a dozen reworded/reordered versions of each test item so wording noise can be averaged out later.\n   - _Why_: Holding topic and format fixed and flipping only the value is what makes the recovered signal about value, not writing style.\n2. Pass each affirming/violating pair through the model, record the internal activations at each layer, keep the layer where a value classifier works best, and set each value axis's direction to the difference between the average affirming and average violating activations; orthonormalize these into the model's value basis.\n\n*The per-model value coordinate $v_{m}(x)$ is the projection of the read-layer hidden state $d_{m}(x)$ onto the model's value basis $U_{m}$ (k value axes), i.e. value is read from activations, not answer text.*\n$$ v_m(x) = U_m^{\\top} d_m(x), \\qquad U_m \\in \\mathbb{R}^{h \\times k} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This reads value from inside the model (activations) instead of from the text it writes, so it dodges answer-wording noise.\n\n### Cross-model alignment\n*Rotate every model's value basis into one shared frame so readings are comparable across models.*\n\n3. Show one fixed 'anchor' set of value items, formatted exactly the same way to every model, and compute each model's value coordinates on it — the shared items every model's reading will be lined up against.\n   - _Why_: You need the same items measured on every model to line their readings up against each other.\n4. Pick one reference model; for every other model find the rotation that best lines up its anchor coordinates with the reference's (orthogonal Procrustes, solved by an SVD), giving aligned coordinates that are now comparable across models. 【author decision: a pure rotation keeps distances meaningful but can't fix the case where one model simply expresses a value more strongly than another; allowing rescaling fixes that but changes what 'distance' means — and since each axis already has a fixed meaning, a free rotation can scramble those meanings. The authors must decide which kind of alignment map to use, and whether to keep it close to the identity so the value axes stay interpretable.】\n\n*Each model's basis is rotated into a common frame by the orthogonal Procrustes map $O_{m}$ that best matches its anchor-item coordinates to the reference model $m_{0}$; the aligned coordinate is $\\tilde{v}_{m}(x),$ the shared cross-model value primitive.*\n$$ O_m = \\arg\\min_{O \\in O(k)} \\sum_{x} \\lVert O\\, v_m(x) - v_{m_0}(x) \\rVert^2, \\qquad \\tilde{v}_m(x) = O_m U_m^{\\top} d_m(x) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A single model's value direction is private to it; rotating everyone into one shared frame is what makes two models' readings comparable.\n\n### Calibrated value distance\n*Turn the aligned readings into a relational value DISTANCE with a significance null, robust to probe wording.*\n\n5. Run each test item in its dozen rewordings, average the aligned coordinate over them, and record how much it varies across rewordings; summarize that spread into one number used later to widen the comparison's tolerance to wording.\n   - _Why_: Averaging over rewordings cancels question-wording noise, and recording its spread lets you charge that noise to the uncertainty later.\n6. For two models, measure the distance between their clouds of aligned value coordinates with a kernel two-sample test (MMD), using a kernel width set by the typical spacing of the points plus the rewording-variance term, so wording wobble is charged to tolerance rather than to the signal.\n\n*The cross-model value distance D(A,B) is the kernel maximum-mean-discrepancy between the two models' distributions of aligned value coordinates in the RKHS of kernel K.*\n$$ D(A,B) = \\big\\lVert \\mu_A - \\mu_B \\big\\rVert_{\\mathcal{H}_K}, \\quad \\mu_m = \\mathbb{E}_x\\big[\\,K(\\tilde{v}_m(x), \\cdot)\\,\\big] \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Because the distance is computed over value-anchored coordinates (not raw text), it measures a value gap rather than a style gap; widening the kernel by the noise keeps wording wobble out of the signal.\n7. Mix the two models' coordinates, randomly re-split them many times, recompute the distance each time, and report the real distance as how extreme it is against that shuffled baseline; fill the full model-by-model distance and significance tables, correcting for the many pairwise comparisons.\n\n*Significance comes from a permutation null: pool the two models' coordinates, repeatedly re-split $(\\pi ),$ recompute the distance, and report D(A,B) as a z-score / p-value against that null, so the distance carries calibrated uncertainty.*\n$$ z(A,B) = \\frac{D(A,B) - \\mathbb{E}_{\\pi}[D_\\pi]}{\\mathrm{sd}_{\\pi}[D_\\pi]}, \\qquad D_\\pi = D\\big(\\pi(A \\cup B)\\big) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The shuffle tells you how big a distance you'd see by chance, so you can say whether the measured gap is real.\n\n### Faithfulness validation\n*Causally certify the value coordinate and show it beats surface scores on held-out behavior.*\n\n8. Erase or rotate out one named value direction inside a model before computing distances, and check the distance and a known model-pair ordering move the way you predicted; if poking the value direction changes the result, the distance really tracks that value computation.\n   - _Why_: If poking the internal value direction changes the answer, the distance really reflects that value computation, not an accident.\n9. Check the internal distance against the old surface-score distances on a held-out behavioral choice task (does it recover the true ordering better, and stay steadier across rewordings); then run a control that swaps the learned rotation for a random one, and a stripped control using only the aligned reading, to prove the alignment is doing the work.\n   - _Why_: Beating surface scores on held-out behavior shows it measures something real, and the random-rotation control proves the alignment (not luck) is doing the work.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 读取倾向而非回答：面向 LLM 的校准化跨模型价值距离\n\n**方法名称.** Probe-Invariant Value Distance (PIVD)\n\n## 研究动机\n如今，如果你想知道两个大语言模型（LLM）在道德、政治或文化价值上的差异有多大，标准做法只会给你一份“逐模型成绩单”，并以人类为基准打分：每个模型回答一套固定的价值问卷，得到一个“答案有多像人类”的分数。这有两个问题。第一，它从不直接告诉你两个“模型”之间相差多远，只告诉你各自与人类相比如何。第二，分数直接从模型写出的文本中读取，因此当你改写、调换顺序或改变格式时分数会抖动；学界反复注意到这种抖动，却从未把它与真正的价值信号分离开。\n\n为什么现在可解：研究者已经能从模型“激活”内部（而不仅是其文字）读出一个“价值方向”；而一项很新的结果（Universal Refusal Circuits，2026 年 1 月）表明，这类内部方向可以在不同模型之间——甚至跨不同架构——对齐。另外，Alignment Verifiability（2026 年 2 月）证明：仅观察模型行为可能无法确定其隐含的价值属性，而这正是内部读取所能补上的缺口。至于带置信度/显著性数值地比较两个分布的统计工具（一种叫 MMD（Maximum Mean Discrepancy，最大均值差异）的核双样本检验）则是标准且廉价的。\n\n我们的想法 Probe-Invariant Value Distance (PIVD)：从内部方向而非回答文本读取每个模型的价值；把每个模型的读数旋转到一个共享坐标系，使其可比；再把两个模型之间的“距离”度量为一个带显著性数值的校准化双样本检验，同时对大量改写求平均，使问题措辞噪声放大的是不确定性而非答案本身。先前的内部对齐工作是把某个单一行为（如拒答）迁移去引导模型；我们则把对齐后的读数变成一台测量仪器——一个能说明两个模型价值相差多远、以及该差距是否真实的数值。\n\n## 方法\n### 内部价值读取\n*从探针不变的内部方向读取每个模型的价值倾向，而非从其回答文本读取。*\n\n1. 针对 k 个价值轴(Moral-Foundations 的 5 个轴与 Schwartz 的 10 个基本价值轴之并集,k=15,剔除无法干净翻转极性的轴),为每个轴构造成对的情景补全:固定话题、长度档与表面格式,只翻转价值极性(肯定该价值 vs 违背该价值)。并为每个评测条目准备 P=12 个改写/调序变体(改写 + 选项调序 + 格式换装)。这种成对设计迫使提取到的方向承载价值本身而非写作风格。\n   - _为什么_: 固定话题与格式、只翻转价值，才能让提取到的信号关乎价值本身，而非写作风格。\n2. 把每个极性对的两个成员都送入模型 m,缓存各层在回答跨度上均值池化的残差流隐状态,按留出价值对比探针准确率选出读取层,把 $U_{m}$ 第 j 列设为该层『平均肯定激活减平均违背激活』的归一化方向,再用 QR 把 k 列正交归一化。逐模型价值坐标即 $v_{m}(x) = U_{m}^{T} d_{m}(x)($式 eq:readout)——价值从激活中读取,而非从回答文本读取。\n\n*逐模型价值坐标 $v_{m}(x)$ 是读取层隐状态 $d_{m}(x)$ 在该模型价值基 $U_{m}$（k 个价值轴）上的投影——价值从激活中读取，而非从回答文本中读取。*\n$$ v_m(x) = U_m^{\\top} d_m(x), \\qquad U_m \\in \\mathbb{R}^{h \\times k} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这是从模型内部（激活）读取价值，而非从其文字读取，从而避开回答措辞噪声。\n\n### 跨模型对齐\n*把每个模型的价值基旋入一个共享坐标系，使读数在模型间可比。*\n\n3. 向每个模型以逐字节完全相同的方式呈现同一套固定的 $N_{a}$ 个价值对比『锚定』条目,并计算每个模型在其上的原始坐标 $v_{m}(x) = U_{m}^{T} d_{m}(x)$。完全一致的呈现提供了对齐不同模型价值基所需的公共支撑集。\n   - _为什么_: 只有在所有模型上测同一批条目，才能把各自读数相互对齐。\n4. 选一个参照模型 m0;对每个其他模型,用 SVD 求解正交 Procrustes,得到使其锚定坐标与参照最匹配的旋转 $O_{m},$对齐坐标为 $\\tilde{v}_{m}(x) = O_{m} U_{m}^{T} d_{m}(x)($式 eq:procrustes),从而提供逐模型探针所缺的跨模型可比性。【作者需决定:正交映射保距(使 D 仍是诚实的等距散度)但无法吸收模型间逐轴的尺度差异(若模型 A 表达『关爱』的激活幅度是 B 的两倍,旋转无法将其拉平);而带缩放的仿射映射能吸收尺度,却会破坏 MMD 距离所依赖的等距性;又因为基的各列已按价值轴逐一打好标签,自由旋转会混合这些已标注的轴并摧毁其可解释性。作者须选择对齐映射的类别(严格正交,把残余尺度当作所测差距的一部分;或先逐轴白化再旋转以吸收尺度并重新定义『距离』的含义),并决定是否把 O 向单位阵正则化以保护轴标签。】\n\n*每个模型的价值基通过正交 Procrustes 旋转 $O_{m}$ 对齐到公共参照系，使其在锚定条目上的坐标与参照模型 $m_{0}$ 最匹配；对齐后坐标 $\\tilde{v}_{m}(x)$ 即跨模型共享的价值基元。*\n$$ O_m = \\arg\\min_{O \\in O(k)} \\sum_{x} \\lVert O\\, v_m(x) - v_{m_0}(x) \\rVert^2, \\qquad \\tilde{v}_m(x) = O_m U_m^{\\top} d_m(x) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 单个模型的价值方向只属于它自己；把所有模型旋入一个共享坐标系，才能让两模型读数可比。\n\n### 校准化价值距离\n*把对齐读数转化为带显著性零分布、且对探针措辞鲁棒的关系型价值距离。*\n\n5. 对每个评测条目用其 P 个改写/调序变体各算一次 $\\tilde{v}_{m}(x),$在变体上求平均得逐条目对齐坐标,并记录逐条目的 $k\\times k$ 跨变体协方差 $\\Sigma _{x}$;将其汇总为单一膨胀标量 $s^{2} = mean_{x} tr(\\Sigma _{x})/k$ 供核带宽使用(保留完整 $\\Sigma _{x}$ 以备日后改用 Mahalanobis 核)。如此措辞噪声放大的是核与零分布,而非价值估计本身。\n   - _为什么_: 对改写求平均抵消措辞噪声，记录其离散度则可在之后把该噪声计入不确定性。\n6. 对任意模型对 (A,B),用 RBF 核的 MMD 计算 D(A,B) $= MMD({\\tilde{v}_{A}(x)}, {\\tilde{v}_{B}(x)})($式 eq:mmd),核带宽取 $h^{2} = h0^{2} + s^{2}(h0$ 为合并对齐坐标上的中位数启发式两两距离$,s^{2}$ 为 第5步（对每个评测条目用其 $P\\dots $） 的变体膨胀项);并在小范围带宽扫描下报告。由于核在价值锚定的对齐基上计算,它度量的是价值距离而非文本风格距离。\n\n*跨模型价值距离 D(A,B) 是两模型对齐价值坐标分布在核 K 的再生核希尔伯特空间中的最大均值差异（MMD）。*\n$$ D(A,B) = \\big\\lVert \\mu_A - \\mu_B \\big\\rVert_{\\mathcal{H}_K}, \\quad \\mu_m = \\mathbb{E}_x\\big[\\,K(\\tilde{v}_m(x), \\cdot)\\,\\big] \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 距离在价值锚定坐标（而非原始文本）上计算，因此度量的是价值差异而非风格差异；用噪声加宽核可把措辞抖动挡在信号之外。\n7. 把两模型对齐坐标合并、重新划分 B=10000 次、每次重算 D,并将 D(A,B) 表示为相对该零分布的 z 分数 / p 值(式 eq:null);组装完整的 $M\\times M$ 校准距离矩阵与显著性矩阵,并用 Benjamini-Hochberg 对 M(M-1)/2 个两两检验控制错误发现率。关系型距离由此带上校准化的不确定性。\n\n*显著性来自置换零分布：将两模型坐标合并、反复重新划分（$\\pi $）、重算距离，并将 D(A,B) 表示为相对该零分布的 z 分数 / p 值，使距离带有校准化的不确定性。*\n$$ z(A,B) = \\frac{D(A,B) - \\mathbb{E}_{\\pi}[D_\\pi]}{\\mathrm{sd}_{\\pi}[D_\\pi]}, \\qquad D_\\pi = D\\big(\\pi(A \\cup B)\\big) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 置换告诉你“纯属偶然”会有多大距离，从而判断所测差距是否真实。\n\n### 保真性验证\n*对价值坐标做因果验证，并证明它在留出行为上胜过表面分数。*\n\n8. 在 第6步（对任意模型对） 之前,把模型 $U_{m}$ 中某个指定的价值方向旋出 / 消融,确认 D 按预期方向移动、且某个已知的两两排序发生变化——扰动内部坐标会改变所报距离,从而证明所测距离反映模型的价值计算,而非偏离流形的伪影。\n   - _为什么_: 若拨动内部价值方向会改变结果，说明距离确实反映了该价值计算，而非巧合。\n9. 在留出的行为两两排序任务上(探针从未见过的公开价值选择数据;以对角外两两距离的 Spearman 秩相关比较距离矩阵,并以跨 P 个改写的变异系数作稳定性),把校准后的内部距离与表面分数距离比较;再做负对照(用随机旋转替代学到的 $O_{m})$与正对照(只用对齐坐标、不做变体平均 / 不做带宽膨胀)。由此建立外部效度,并把对齐后的内部读出隔离为承重机制。\n   - _为什么_: 在留出行为上胜过表面分数说明它测到了真实信号；随机旋转对照证明起作用的是对齐而非运气。\n\n"},{"id":"05","run_dir":"run_prompt05_causalrepr","index":5,"title":"On-Manifold Interventions: Reachable Counterfactuals by Construction for Faithful Interpretability","title_zh":"流形内因果干预：面向可信解释的、由构造可达的反事实表示","method_name":"On-Manifold Intervention Operator (OMIO)","hook":"The frontier mitigates off-manifold interventions with a trained Counterfactual-Latent auxiliary loss re-fit per DAS experiment, yet we obtain a stronger guarantee with strictly fewer trained objects: no auxiliary loss and no per-experiment retraining, because the intervention operator is built to write only representations the target model could reach on a natural forward pass, and the same construction emits a per-intervention reachability certificate for free.","anchor_pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","anchor_pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","domain_category":"Interpretability & Representation Analysis","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf supplies a causal-intervention operator that is guaranteed by construction to produce a counterfactual representation the target model could actually reach in a natural forward pass: every intervention method writes an externally-sourced or scaled value into the representation and only afterwards (the anchor's CL loss) pulls it back toward the natural distribution, so reachability/on-manifold-ness is a soft post-hoc property rather than a property the intervention is built to s","pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","sub_pattern":"C20 (Encode Structure by Construction)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by prescribing the forward law that maps a natural input to its layer-L activation as an explicit normalizing-flow density over the natural representation manifold, then constructing the intervention as the principled reverse of that law (C20): instead of writing an arbitrary target value, the operator solves for the nearest representation that (i) realizes the intended counterfactual value of the targeted causal subspace AND (ii) lies on the flow's natural manifold, so the written state is reachable-by-construction rather than regularized-after-the-fact, and off-manifold pathway recruitment is excluded by the constraint rather than merely penalized.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides a per-intervention certificate that decides, before its explanation is trusted, whether a given intervention's divergence is harmless (behaviourally inert) or pernicious (recruits a pathway dormant under natural inputs): the anchor diagnoses the two regimes as outcomes measured after the fact but supplies no quantity computed at intervention time that separates them, so practitioners cannot tell a faithful intervention from an artifact-producing one without already kno","pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by constructing a confound-isolating certificate (C02) that holds the targeted circuit and the intended causal value fixed and varies ONLY the on-manifold-vs-off-manifold axis between the on-manifold operator's write and the ordinary arbitrary write: the certificate reads off the same flow object as a two-part quantity — the off-manifold radius (flow negative-log-density gap) decomposed onto the layer's behavioural null-space versus its behaviourally-live directions — and is validated against an independent oracle (the natural-forward-pass logit distribution of the target model), so it separates behaviourally-inert (harmless) from pathway-recruiting (pernicious) divergence at intervention time rather than after the explanation is read.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"mechanistic interpretability of neural networks via causal interventions (activation patching, ablation, Distributed Alignment Search, steering)","n_papers":50,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":26},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":16,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"CaT-GNN: Enhancing Credit Card Fraud Detection via Causal Temporal Graph Neural Networks"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"InterpBench: Semi-Synthetic Transformers for Evaluating Mechanistic Interpretability Techniques"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"SoK: On Finding Common Ground in Loss Landscapes Using Deep Model Merging Techniques"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Causal intervention graph neural network for fault diagnosis of complex industrial processes"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Interpretable AI-driven causal inference to uncover the time-varying effects of PM2.5 and public health interventions on COVID-19 infection rates"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Causal Diffusion Autoencoders: Toward Counterfactual Generation via Diffusion Probabilistic Models"}],"more":10},{"year":2025,"n":24,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Addressing divergent representations from causal interventions on neural networks"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Causal SHAP: Feature Attribution with Dependency Awareness through Causal Discovery"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"BrainOOD: Out-of-distribution Generalizable Brain Network Analysis"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Research on Chinese Implicit Sentiment Semantic Decoupling Model Based on Neural Symbolic Graph Network and Causal Intervention"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Unifying Physics- and Data-Driven Modeling via Novel Causal Spatiotemporal Graph Neural Network for Interpretable Epidemic Forecasting"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Breast cancer image classification based on H&E staining using a causal attention graph neural network model"}],"more":18},{"year":2026,"n":9,"papers":[{"source":"arxiv","title":"Midterm Status Report of the ILC Technology Network Activities"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Causal Discovery in Action: Learning Chain-Reaction Mechanisms from Interventions"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"CIVeX: Causal Intervention Verification for Language Agents"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"CIGPose: Causal Intervention Graph Neural Network for Whole-Body Pose Estimation"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Stochastic Intervention"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Causal Interpretation of Neural Network Computations with Contribution Decomposition"}],"more":3}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":9,"share":0.18},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":6,"share":0.12},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":5,"share":0.1},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":4,"share":0.08},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":3,"share":0.06},{"pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","count":2,"share":0.04},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":2,"share":0.04},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":1,"share":0.02}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Causal interventions are the central tool of mechanistic interpretability — activation patching, Distributed Alignment Search, and steering directly overwrite a model's internal representations to test what they encode (semanticscholar:4fd6aff1f294f0a23dced079240a52e2ffcd5f3a, openalex:W4401978749) — yet the counterfactual states they construct are not constrained to be states the target model could actually reach in a natural forward pass. Because the intervention writes a value drawn from a different context (or scaled arbitrarily, e.g. activation patching that multiplies features up to 15x) into a representation, the resulting activation can land off the model's natural representation manifold, where it recruits dormant pathways that are silent under natural inputs; the explanation then reflects the behaviour of those hidden pathways rather than the natural mechanism, so the explanation is unfaithful to the model in its un-intervened state (semanticscholar:4fd6aff1f294f0a23dced079240a52e2ffcd5f3a, openalex:W4400435247). The frontier diagnoses this divergence and at best penalizes it after the fact — the divergence paper distinguishes harmless null-space divergence from pernicious pathway-recruiting divergence and applies a Counterfactual Latent loss to pull intervened representations back toward the natural distribution (semanticscholar:4fd6aff1f294f0a23dced079240a52e2ffcd5f3a) — but no method makes the intervened state guaranteed-reachable by construction, so faithfulness remains a measured property of each intervention rather than a property the intervention operator is built to satisfy, and the separation of harmless from pernicious divergence remains a post-hoc label with no per-intervention certificate.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:4fd6aff1f294f0a23dced079240a52e2ffcd5f3a","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"The anchor (ICLR 2026) demonstrates theoretically and empirically that common causal-intervention techniques shift internal representations off the target model's natural distribution, separates the divergences into 'harmless' (lying in a layer's behavioural null-space) and 'pernicious' (activating hidden pathways that change behaviour), and mitigates the pernicious cases by applying a modified Counterfactual Latent (CL) loss that pulls intervened representations closer to the natural distribution while preserving interpretive power. Its residue: the CL loss is a soft, post-hoc regularizer applied per experiment that reduces but does not eliminate divergence and gives no construction-level guarantee that an intervened state lies on (or is reachable on) the model's natural representation manifold; and the harmless-vs-pernicious distinction is diagnosed as an outcome after the intervention runs, not certified per intervention before its explanation is trusted, so the intervention operator itself is never required to produce only natural-distribution-consistent counterfactuals."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4400435247","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Missed Causes and Ambiguous Effects shows that the counterfactual theory of causality underlying interventionist interpretability systematically mishandles multiple independently-sufficient causes and yields ambiguous effects, biasing what patching/ablation can conclude. Its residue: it diagnoses the bias structurally but offers no replacement causal unit or intervention construction that resolves the independently-sufficient-cause failure, and it does not address the distributional realism of the intervened state itself."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:b4d81c89c973b6d207dbc0562760200b7d7974ed","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"The Non-Linear Representation Dilemma examines whether causal abstraction with non-linear alignment maps is sufficient for mechanistic interpretability, showing that lifting the linear-map constraint can make the abstraction criterion trivially satisfiable. Its residue: it characterizes when an alignment map is too expressive to be meaningful but offers no operational map class that is simultaneously expressive enough to capture real features and constrained enough that the implied intervention stays on the natural representation manifold."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:a9ceeafaa5cffc975fb5aa3d591666fb0ebc47d8","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"InterpBench trains semi-synthetic transformers with Strict Interchange Intervention Training so a known high-level causal model is realized inside the network, giving ground-truth circuits to validate interpretability methods. Its residue: the ground truth exists only for purpose-built known-circuit transformers and the SIIT objective enforces alignment during training, so it neither measures nor guarantees that a post-hoc intervention on a normally-trained target model produces an in-distribution representation."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415248346","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"The Multi-Level Causal Intervention Framework brings activation patching, latent-space perturbation, input manipulation, and causal mediation to VAEs / generative latent spaces. Its residue: it extends the interventionist toolkit to a new architecture but inherits the same unmeasured off-manifold risk — its perturbations are not constrained to stay within the VAE's natural latent distribution, so the faithfulness concern is carried over untouched."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"mechanistic interpretability of neural networks via causal interventions (activation patching, ablation, Distributed Alignment Search, steering)","venue":"ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML-tier ML","time":"2026","data":["pretrained transformers / small task-trained networks with probed internal representations","semi-synthetic known-circuit transformers (InterpBench / IIT-trained models)","activation datasets collected from natural forward passes for on-manifold reference"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"mechanistic interpretability + causal inference + representation geometry","preference":"both","baseline":"activation patching, Distributed Alignment Search (DAS), interchange interventions, Counterfactual Latent (CL) loss mitigation (Grant 2025 / the divergence paper)","limitation":"causal interventions on internal representations shift those representations off the model's natural distribution, so the mechanistic explanations they yield may be unfaithful to the target model in its natural state; existing mitigation is a soft post-hoc penalty rather than an enforced on-manifold guarantee","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","compute","expertise","preference","data"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object both legs read from and write to is the natural-representation manifold of layer L, modelled as a normalizing flow g_L: R^d -> R^d (a frozen RealNVP/affine-coupling flow, ~8 coupling blocks) fit once on activations A_L = {a = f_{<=L}(x) : x ~ D_nat} collected from natural forward passes of the FROZEN target model on its natural input distribution D_nat (no target-model weights are touched). The flow gives two computables from a candidate activation a: a manifold energy E(a) = -log p_L(a) = -log p_Z(g_L(a)) - log|det J_{g_L}(a)| (with p_Z standard Gaussian), and a manifold projection that we use to constrain writes. The targeted causal variable is specified exactly as in interchange/DAS: a learned (or given) orthonormal subspace basis U in R^{d x k} (k = causal-subspace rank, e.g. k=8) and a target value v* in R^k drawn from a source run, so an ordinary intervention writes a_patch = a - U U^T a + U v* (the arbitrary write that may leave the manifold). ANCHOR LEG (C20, structural_prior_encoding). Rather than write a_patch, the on-manifold operator solves a* = argmin_a E(a) subject to U^T a = v* — the nearest natural-manifold representation that exactly realizes the intended causal value — by projected gradient steps in flow latent space z=g_L(a): take z_0 = g_L(a_patch), descend ||z||^2 (the flow's own log-density) while re-projecting U^T g_L^{-1}(z) = v* via a Gauss-Newton step on the k linear constraints, for T=20 iterations, then set a* = g_L^{-1}(z_T). Because the forward law (the flow) prescribes exactly which states are natural, its reverse (constrained minimization of E in latent space) yields a write that lies on the natural manifold BY CONSTRUCTION while exactly honouring the causal value, so off-manifold pathway recruitment is excluded by the feasibility constraint rather than reduced by a penalty; this is the runnable artifact the method contribution_type demands. SIBLING LEG (C02, controlled_diagnostic_design). The same flow emits the per-intervention certificate: define the off-manifold radius r(a) = E(a) - E_bar_nat (E_bar_nat = mean natural energy, an offset constant calibrated once on held-out natural activations) and decompose the displacement delta = a_patch - a* into delta_null (its projection onto the layer's behavioural null-space N_L — the right-null-space of the layer-L-to-logits Jacobian J_beh estimated by autograd at a*) and delta_live = delta - delta_null. The certificate c = (r(a_patch), ||delta_live|| / ||delta||) is computed at intervention time, and its decision threshold is fixed by a controlled instance set (C02): we build matched pairs that hold the circuit U and value v* fixed and vary only the manifold axis (on-manifold a* vs arbitrary a_patch), scoring each against the independent oracle KL(p_logits(a) || p_logits(a*_natural-reachable)) measured from the frozen target model's own logits — so the threshold separating harmless (delta concentrated in delta_null, small live radius -> oracle KL ~ 0) from pernicious (large ||delta_live||, large r -> oracle KL large, hidden-pathway recruitment) is calibrated against the model's natural behaviour, not asserted. The two legs share one object: the flow that the anchor leg inverts to write on-manifold is the same flow whose energy the sibling leg reads to certify each write, which is exactly why this reads as one paper, not two.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The two gaps share machinery because the manifold model is simultaneously the thing the anchor leg must invert (to write reachable counterfactuals) and the thing the sibling leg must read (to certify each write's harmlessness); the evidence they are one object is that the certificate's off-manifold radius r is literally the energy gap the anchor operator drives to its constrained minimum, so a separate certifier would re-fit the same density. REGRESSION CHECK (method_lineage.notes): the occupied-source constraint from Phase 2.1 forbids three regressions and I avoided each — (c1) a density/OOD detector that merely flags-then-penalizes: I use the flow density not as a flag but as the feasible set a constrained solver writes INTO, so the output is a reachable state, not a rejected one; (c2) editing inside a purpose-built auxiliary generator trained over activations a la StyleGAN/diffusion latent edits: the flow is a frozen density model used only to define and project onto the manifold, not a generator that replaces the target model's computation; (c3 / anchor n3) a soft proximity/plausibility penalty added on top of an unconstrained write (the anchor's CL loss): my operator imposes a hard equality+feasibility constraint solved at intervention time with zero added training objective, which is the by-construction guarantee the soft penalty structurally cannot give. I considered making the operator a learned amortized projector (one forward pass) but rejected it for the headline version because an amortized net re-introduces a trained object per target model and weakens the by-construction claim to an approximation; the iterative constrained solve keeps the guarantee exact and is left as the load-bearing variant, with amortization noted as a speed ablation.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on InterpBench SIIT transformers (which carry a ground-truth high-level causal circuit) and on the Boundless DAS 7B setting from the anchor, run three intervention operators that share the SAME causal target (U, v*): (i) ordinary arbitrary write, (ii) anchor-style soft CL-penalty write, (iii) our on-manifold constrained operator; measure recovered-circuit faithfulness (agreement of the patching-derived circuit with InterpBench ground truth), oracle KL between intervened and nearest-natural-reachable logits, and the certificate's AUROC for predicting pernicious interventions. If the candidate works, faithfulness and oracle on-manifold-ness are highest for (iii) and the certificate's AUROC for separating harmless from pernicious interventions stays high (>0.85), and — the non-obvious direction — on interventions the soft CL loss leaves residually off-manifold (large scaling, e.g. 15x feature multiplication), the on-manifold operator still recovers the ground-truth circuit while the soft-penalty write recruits a hidden pathway and reports a spurious circuit. Mechanism distinguisher built on the ONE load-bearing variable, the off-manifold radius r(a) = E(a) - E_bar_nat: negative control drives r to its constrained minimum for arbitrary writes by replacing the flow energy with an ISOTROPIC Gaussian energy (same minimization machinery, wrong manifold — its producer, the fitted flow, ablated to a structureless density); the predicted effect is that recovered-circuit faithfulness against InterpBench ground truth falls back to the arbitrary-write baseline (NOT merely that r changes), which is the real Popper test since 'r dropped' alone is equally consistent with a mis-calibrated density. Positive control: a stripped model using ONLY the flow-energy constraint (no learned causal subspace, U fixed to the DAS solution) recovers most of the faithfulness gain, identifying the by-construction on-manifold constraint as the load-bearing mechanism.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:4fd6aff1f294f0a23dced079240a52e2ffcd5f3a","delta":"The anchor reduces divergence with a trained Counterfactual-Latent auxiliary loss optimized alongside Boundless DAS that pulls intervened representations softly toward the natural distribution and diagnoses harmless-vs-pernicious as a post-hoc theoretical/empirical outcome; we construct the intervention as a hard constrained projection onto a frozen normalizing-flow model of the natural manifold so reachability holds by construction with no auxiliary loss, and we emit a per-intervention certificate (off-manifold radius decomposed onto the behavioural null-space) that decides harmless-vs-pernicious at intervention time, neither of which the CL loss produces."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4400435247","delta":"Missed Causes and Ambiguous Effects diagnoses that the counterfactual theory mishandles independently-sufficient causes but supplies no replacement intervention construction; we supply a concrete intervention operator (constrained on-manifold write) and a reachability certificate, addressing the distributional-realism axis it leaves untouched."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:b4d81c89c973b6d207dbc0562760200b7d7974ed","delta":"The Non-Linear Representation Dilemma shows expressive non-linear alignment maps make causal abstraction trivially satisfiable but offers no map class that is expressive yet on-manifold; our flow-feasibility constraint is exactly such a class — the alignment may be expressive, but the written state is forced onto the natural manifold, so the abstraction cannot be satisfied by an off-distribution state."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:a9ceeafaa5cffc975fb5aa3d591666fb0ebc47d8","delta":"InterpBench trains known-circuit transformers via Strict IIT to provide ground-truth circuits but enforces alignment during training and does not constrain post-hoc interventions on normally-trained targets; we use those ground-truth circuits as the oracle to validate a post-hoc operator that keeps interventions on the natural manifold of an untouched frozen target model."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:4fd6aff1f294f0a23dced079240a52e2ffcd5f3a","what_step_was_missed":"The anchor applies the Counterfactual-Latent loss as a soft auxiliary penalty optimized during DAS training, so its intervened states are pulled toward — but never constrained onto — the natural distribution, and its harmless/pernicious split is a theoretical characterization measured after the intervention. For our contribution to already exist it would have needed (a) to construct an explicit density model (a normalizing flow) of the layer's natural-activation manifold and write the counterfactual as a HARD constrained projection onto that density's support while exactly honouring the causal subspace value — turning the soft penalty into a by-construction feasibility guarantee — and (b) to decompose the flow's off-manifold energy onto the layer's behavioural null-space to yield a quantity computed AT intervention time that certifies harmless-vs-pernicious. It constructs neither the density model nor the constrained-write operator nor the per-intervention certificate, so its guarantee remains soft and its divergence label remains post-hoc."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":267,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"Layer 1 hard floor does not fire: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict is borderline (no Reject lesson is candidate_match: yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat is NOT exact-mechanism overlap (GACF is a generative-model data-manifold causal-flow for scRNA-seq inference, lacking the candidate's internal-representation flow, causal-subspace constraint, and behavioural-null-space certificate). Layer 2 selects revise because paper_pointed_threat exists AND addressable_via names specific candidate fields (hook, differentiation_from_lit), reinforced by gap_closure_reject_check.entries[0].reject_lessons_evaluated lesson 2 ('the advertised plug-in generality is shown on only a single backbone') being borderline-live on the multi-setting generality evidence. recipe_application_check is applied for both legs, so core_mechanism is sound; the fix is repositioning/differentiation plus a surfaced generality concern, not a mechanism rebuild.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf supplies a causal-intervention operator that is guaranteed by construction to produce a counterfactual representation the target model could actually reach in a natural forward pass: every intervention method writes an externally-sourced or scaled value into the representation and only afterwards (the anchor's CL loss) pulls it back toward the natural distribution, so reachability/on-manifold-ness is a soft post-hoc property rather than a property the intervention is built to satisfy, and off-manifold pathway recruitment is reduced but never excluded.","main_pattern":"structural_prior_encoding","sub_pattern":"C20 (Encode Structure by Construction)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail when the corruption-structure prior is asserted but never isolated as the actual source of gains: the 'structure' is really a generic architecture or powerful pretrained backbone doing the work, so same-capacity ablations cannot attribute improvement to the prior, or the structural reformulation is theoretically clean but the empirical delta over the base method is marginal while the advertised generality is demonstrated on a single backbone or dataset.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming an architecture carries a domain-matched structural prior while shipping a generic off-the-shelf encoder-decoder collapses the move into ordinary supervised denoising that ablations and weak-baseline comparisons quickly expose.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The prior here is not a generic encoder-decoder; it is an explicit normalizing-flow density over the target model's natural activation manifold whose support is the feasible set a constrained solver writes into, and the negative control (isotropic-Gaussian energy with the same solver) isolates the flow as the load-bearing structure, so the move cannot collapse into ordinary denoising."},{"lesson_quoted":"An elegant equivalence proof (corruption-recovery equals descent on an energy landscape) earns nothing when the empirical gain over the base method is marginal and the advertised plug-in generality is shown on only a single backbone.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The candidate's generality is asserted across InterpBench known-circuit transformers AND the Boundless DAS 7B setting (two regimes, not one), but the claim that the on-manifold operator beats the anchor's soft CL loss specifically on residually-off-manifold (e.g. 15x-scaled) interventions is so far carried by one synthetic stress case; the breadth-on-more-than-one-corruption-type self-check is only partly met, mitigable by surfacing the multi-setting ablation rather than rebuilding the mechanism, hence borderline not triggered."},{"lesson_quoted":"Deriving partition labels from a first-principles physical model is undercut when the derivations lack rigor, baselines and ablations are missing, and citation hygiene fails.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate ships the equal-capacity ablation the lesson demands (negative control replaces the fitted flow energy with a structureless isotropic density via the same minimization machinery) and the strong baselines (arbitrary write AND anchor-style soft CL-penalty write), so its by-construction claim is not an unbaselined assertion."},{"lesson_quoted":"If the structural signal you minimize rides on a powerful pretrained backbone, failing to isolate the prior's contribution from sheer backbone capacity leaves reviewers unable to credit the idea and unconvinced by the motivation for the chosen backbone.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The target model is FROZEN and untouched — no backbone is trained — and the positive control (flow-energy constraint only, U fixed to the DAS solution) attributes the faithfulness gain to the on-manifold constraint rather than to any model capacity, exactly the isolation the lesson requires."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides a per-intervention certificate that decides, before its explanation is trusted, whether a given intervention's divergence is harmless (behaviourally inert) or pernicious (recruits a pathway dormant under natural inputs): the anchor diagnoses the two regimes as outcomes measured after the fact but supplies no quantity computed at intervention time that separates them, so practitioners cannot tell a faithful intervention from an artifact-producing one without already knowing the answer.","main_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail when the instrument isolates the confound only inside an artificial regime and never shows the signal transfers to real deployment, or when the diagnostic is validated against the same definition or system population it was built to interrogate (using the evaluated models as their own oracle), or when it re-derives an already-documented limitation and surfaces nothing not knowable in advance.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A diagnostic that only re-confirms a shortcut already known in advance, surfacing no previously unmeasurable failure, is read as confirmatory rather than as a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The anchor measures harmless/pernicious only AFTER the intervention runs; the certificate's contribution is a quantity computed AT intervention time (off-manifold radius decomposed onto the behavioural null-space) that was previously unmeasurable before trusting an explanation, so it surfaces a new pre-trust signal rather than re-confirming the known post-hoc split."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a synthetic-ground-truth instrument only on synthetic data, without demonstrating that the controlled finding transfers to real-world instances, leaves ecological validity unestablished and undermines the central claim.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The certificate is calibrated on InterpBench synthetic known-circuit transformers (where the harmless/pernicious label is ground-truth) and the plan tests transfer to the Boundless DAS 7B LLM setting, but the 7B transfer evidence is the certificate's AUROC on a setting WITHOUT a ground-truth pernicious label, so the synthetic-to-real transfer is planned but its real-side oracle is weaker — a surfaceable ecological-validity concern, not a mechanism defect, hence borderline."},{"lesson_quoted":"Building the instrument around one contested definition of the target property means it cannot independently confirm that the definition is correct, and reviewers flag the resulting circularity.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The certificate's oracle is independent of the certificate itself — the frozen target model's own natural-forward-pass logit distribution (oracle KL to nearest-natural-reachable logits), not the certificate quantity or a self-asserted faithfulness definition — so harmless/pernicious is anchored to model behaviour, avoiding the circularity the lesson names."},{"lesson_quoted":"Resting an unsupervised evaluation on the unverified premise that the systems under test can reliably judge one another stakes the entire method on an assumption that collapses under scrutiny.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"No system judges another; the oracle is a mechanistic pass/fail criterion (behavioural KL from the model's own natural logits) and, on InterpBench, the planted ground-truth circuit — both independent of any model's self-judgment."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pairing a single-task or small-sample instrument with broad capability claims triggers a scope-mismatch rejection, and assembling retrieval or engineering blocks without an isolating scientific insight reads as application rather than research.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The certificate is not an engineering assembly; its isolating insight is the null-space-vs-live decomposition of the off-manifold radius that the anchor's post-hoc label lacks, and its scope is bounded to the interventions it actually probes (DAS/interchange writes), not a broad capability claim."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No entry is triggered (no Reject lesson is candidate_match: yes), so the hard floor does not fire. The aggregate is driven to borderline by both entries on the same axis — generality/transfer evidence: entry 0 (gap0 / structural_prior_encoding) on lesson 2 ('the advertised plug-in generality is shown on only a single backbone') because the on-manifold-beats-soft-CL claim leans on one synthetic stress case, and entry 1 (gap1 / controlled_diagnostic_design) on lesson 2 ('validating a synthetic-ground-truth instrument only on synthetic data') because the 7B transfer side lacks a ground-truth pernicious oracle; both are experiment-completeness gaps surfaceable to Phase 4, not mechanism defects, since the decisive circularity/isolation lessons are all cleanly avoided."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf supplies a causal-intervention operator that is guaranteed by construction to produce a counterfactual representation the target model could actually reach in a natural forward pass: every intervention method writes an externally-sourced or scaled value into the representation and only afterwards (the anchor's CL loss) pulls it back toward the natural distribution, so reachability/on-manifold-ness is a soft post-hoc property rather than a property the intervention is built to satisfy, and off-manifold pathway recruitment is reduced but never excluded.","sub_pattern":"C20 (Encode Structure by Construction)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Prescribe an explicit law mapping the clean target to the observed/corrupted signal — a noising process, a physical formation model, or a transform that isolates the artifact — then construct the recovery or generation operator as the principled REVERSE of that prescribed law, with a single learnable estimator filling only what the forward law leaves underdetermined, so the inverse is obtained by construction rather than as a black-box corrupt-to-clean regression.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism performs the signature move directly: it prescribes the forward law as an explicit normalizing flow g_L over the natural-activation manifold (the law naming which states are natural), then constructs the intervention as the principled REVERSE — 'a* = argmin_a E(a) subject to U^T a = v*' solved by descending the flow's own log-density in latent space z=g_L(a) while re-projecting the causal-value constraint — so the written state is obtained by inverting the prescribed manifold law rather than by an arbitrary write plus penalty. This is C20's reverse-of-the-prescribed-law move (the flow is the forward law; the constrained latent-space minimization is its reverse), not the parent's generic 'encode structure' gist.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides a per-intervention certificate that decides, before its explanation is trusted, whether a given intervention's divergence is harmless (behaviourally inert) or pernicious (recruits a pathway dormant under natural inputs): the anchor diagnoses the two regimes as outcomes measured after the fact but supplies no quantity computed at intervention time that separates them, so practitioners cannot tell a faithful intervention from an artifact-producing one without already knowing the answer.","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Construct a controlled set of instances in which exactly one named confound is structurally blocked or independently varied, paired with an oracle independent of the system under test, then report the divergence between apparent and de-confounded performance as the primary result — same-source matched pairs with controlled defect injection, scored against verifiability that comes from how the instance was constructed.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism enacts the signature move: it builds matched instance pairs that hold the circuit U and the intended causal value v* FIXED and vary ONLY the on-manifold-vs-off-manifold axis (constrained write a* vs arbitrary write a_patch) — the same-source matched-pair-with-controlled-injection construction C02 step 2 names — and scores them against an oracle independent of the certificate (the frozen target model's own natural-forward-pass logit KL, plus InterpBench's planted ground-truth circuit), then reports the harmless/pernicious split as the headline. This is C02's confound-isolation-with-independent-oracle move, not a generic 'build a benchmark' gist.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries instantiate their cited cluster's signature move in core_mechanism rather than the parent's generic gist: C20's prescribe-forward-law-then-invert (the normalizing flow as forward law, the constrained latent-space minimization as its reverse) and C02's single-confound-isolation-with-independent-oracle (manifold-axis-only matched pairs scored against the model's own natural logits) are each explicitly present and load-bearing."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["structural_prior_encoding","controlled_diagnostic_design"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions (audit_decomp_supervisor / audit_decomp_prior / audit_decomp_operator) require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; the candidate's main_pattern set is {structural_prior_encoding, controlled_diagnostic_design}, which contains no heterogeneous_decomposition and matches no 2-way documented subset, so no anti-pattern is triggered."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"arxiv:2603.17385v1","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"The Causal Uncertainty Principle (2026-03) proves a 'Manifold Tearing Theorem' that deterministic flows develop finite-time singularities under extreme interventions and introduces Geometry-Aware Causal Flow (GACF), 'a scalable algorithm that utilizes a topological radar to bypass manifold tearing', validated on scRNA-seq data. This is the nearest structural neighbour to the candidate's anchor thesis because it ALSO couples interventions, a manifold, and a flow, and ALSO recognizes that pushing an intervention too far leaves the manifold — exactly the off-manifold-divergence phenomenon the candidate's on-manifold operator is built to exclude, so it threatens the framing that constraining interventions to a flow-modelled manifold is itself new. What makes the candidate's claim STAND rather than fall: GACF operates on a continuous GENERATIVE model's data manifold to keep Pearl-style do-interventions identity-preserving for causal inference on a data distribution (scRNA-seq), whereas the candidate constructs a frozen-network's INTERNAL-REPRESENTATION manifold (a fitted density over a target model's layer-L activations), writes a counterfactual that exactly honours a learned causal SUBSPACE value U^T a = v* used in mechanistic-interpretability interchange/DAS, and — decisively — emits a per-intervention harmless/pernicious CERTIFICATE by decomposing the off-manifold radius onto the layer's behavioural null-space, none of which GACF contains (it bypasses tearing for sample fidelity, not faithfulness of a mechanistic explanation, and produces no behavioural-null-space certificate). The candidate's full mechanism is thus not subsumed; only the bare 'flow-constrained intervention on a manifold' hook overlaps. Timing note: arxiv:2603.17385v1 (2026-03) predates the 2026-06-02 as-of by under three months but is in a different application domain (computational biology / generative causal inference), so it is awareness-not-blocking and reinforces reposition-and-differentiate over abandon.","addressable_via":"Reposition the hook so the surprise is not 'constraining interventions to a manifold is new' (GACF already constrains interventions to a generative manifold) but the strictly-fewer-trained-objects, by-construction-reachability-plus-certificate claim specific to mechanistic-interpretability interventions on a FROZEN target network's internal representations, and add an explicit differentiation_from_lit entry against arxiv:2603.17385v1 (GACF) naming the internal-representation-manifold + causal-subspace-constraint + behavioural-null-space-certificate axes it lacks."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"hook + hook_shape_rationale","issue":"paper_pointed_threat (GACF arxiv:2603.17385v1 already constrains interventions to a generative manifold via a flow) and gap_closure_reject_check.entries[0] lesson 2 (generality of the by-construction advantage shown narrowly)","fix_direction":"Keep the shape-(c) counter-intuitive-minimalism claim (stronger guarantee with strictly fewer trained objects than the anchor's per-experiment CL loss), but stop implying that flow-constraining an intervention to a manifold is itself the novelty. Re-scope the surprise to: the by-construction on-manifold guarantee PLUS a per-intervention behavioural-null-space certificate, on a FROZEN target network's internal representations under a mechanistic-interpretability causal-subspace constraint (U^T a = v*) — a regime GACF's generative-data-manifold causal flow does not touch. Do NOT edit falsification_prediction or compute_budget (kill-switch fields, byte-identical through Phase 3.3)."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat — GACF (arxiv:2603.17385v1) is the nearest flow+intervention+manifold neighbour and is absent from the current four-entry differentiation, so the threat's 'make the difference explicit' requirement is unmet","fix_direction":"Add a differentiation entry against arxiv:2603.17385v1 (GACF): it bypasses manifold tearing to keep do-interventions identity-preserving on a continuous generative model's DATA manifold (scRNA-seq); we fit a flow over a frozen target network's INTERNAL-REPRESENTATION manifold, write a counterfactual honouring a learned causal subspace value, and emit a behavioural-null-space harmless/pernicious certificate — none of which GACF produces; state the measured axis (mechanistic-interpretability faithfulness on InterpBench / Boundless DAS, not generative sample fidelity)."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit (add second entry) + surface in Phase 4 reviewer_concerns_and_responses","issue":"gap_closure_reject_check.entries[1] lesson 2 (synthetic-to-real transfer of the certificate is planned but the 7B real side lacks a ground-truth pernicious oracle) and the adjacent CAAP overlap on internal-activation patching","fix_direction":"Add a differentiation entry against arxiv:2603.13652v2 (Causal Attribution via Activation Patching, CAAP): CAAP inserts source-image activations directly into a neutral target context for ViT patch attribution (the arbitrary write our operator replaces) with no on-manifold constraint and no certificate; we constrain the write onto the natural manifold and certify it. Separately, surface the certificate's synthetic-to-real transfer limitation (InterpBench ground-truth label vs 7B AUROC-only oracle) in Phase 4 reviewer_concerns_and_responses. Minor/non-load-bearing; do NOT edit falsification_prediction (kill-switch frozen)."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"hook + hook_shape_rationale","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Retired the implication that flow-constraining an intervention to a manifold is itself new (GACF already does this on a generative data manifold) and re-anchored the shape-(c) minimalism headline on the by-construction on-manifold guarantee PLUS the per-intervention behavioural-null-space certificate, on a frozen target network's internal representations under the mechanistic-interpretability causal-subspace constraint U^T a = v*."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit[4].delta","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added a measured differentiation entry against arxiv:2603.17385v1 (GACF): it constrains do-interventions to a generative DATA manifold for scRNA-seq causal inference, whereas we fit a flow over a frozen network's INTERNAL-representation manifold, honour a causal subspace value, and emit a behavioural-null-space certificate."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit[5].delta","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added a differentiation entry against arxiv:2603.13652v2 (CAAP): it inserts source activations directly (the arbitrary write we replace) for ViT attribution with no manifold constraint and no certificate, whereas we constrain the write onto a fitted natural manifold and certify each write; the certificate's synthetic-to-real transfer limitation is surfaced for Phase 4 reviewer_concerns_and_responses."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# On-Manifold Causal Interventions: Reachable Counterfactuals by Construction for Faithful Interpretability\n\n**Method.** On-Manifold Intervention Operator (OMIO)\n\n## Motivation\nMechanistic interpretability tries to explain WHY a neural network behaves as it does by running 'causal interventions': you reach inside the network, overwrite one of its internal activations with a different value, and watch how the output changes. Activation patching, interchange interventions, and Distributed Alignment Search (DAS) all do this. The catch is that the value you write in is borrowed from another run or scaled up (sometimes by 15x), so the network can end up in a state it would NEVER reach on a normal input. In that unnatural state it can switch on hidden circuits that stay silent on real inputs — so the explanation you read off describes those hidden circuits, not how the network actually works. The explanation is unfaithful.\n\nThe leading work (the 'divergent representations' paper, ICLR 2026) shows this happens, sorts the damage into 'harmless' (the change lands in a direction that does not affect behaviour) versus 'pernicious' (it wakes up a hidden pathway), and softens it with an extra training penalty — the Counterfactual-Latent (CL) loss — that gently pulls the intervened state back toward normal. But that penalty is soft, has to be re-trained for every experiment, and never guarantees the state is reachable; and it only labels harmless-vs-pernicious AFTER the fact, so you cannot tell a trustworthy intervention from a misleading one until it is too late.\n\nWhy now: the 'divergent representations' paper just made the problem sharp, and the tools to fix it head-on are ready. A normalizing flow (an exactly-invertible density model) can be fit once over the network's normal activations to describe its 'natural manifold' — the set of states the network actually reaches. InterpBench (NeurIPS 2024) gives small transformers with known ground-truth circuits to check faithfulness against. Our move: build that natural-manifold model once, then make the intervention WRITE ONLY states on the manifold that still exactly carry the intended causal change — so reachability holds by construction, not by a penalty. The very same model also hands you, for free, a per-intervention certificate that splits the change into a behaviour-irrelevant part and a behaviour-relevant part, telling you harmless-vs-pernicious BEFORE you trust the explanation. The target network is never retrained.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n*Unchanged scaffolding: collect natural activations, validate on known-circuit models, and run attribution ablations.*\n\n1. Run the frozen network on lots of normal text (~200k token positions), and save the layer-L activations you get — without changing any weights. This pile of natural activations is what 'on the manifold' will mean.\n   - _Why_: These saved activations ARE the network's 'natural manifold' — the states it actually reaches — which is what we'll keep interventions inside of.\n2. Use it in practice: read the certificate to decide harmless vs pernicious, and validate on InterpBench transformers (known ground-truth circuits) and the Boundless DAS 7B setting, measuring recovered-circuit faithfulness and certificate AUROC.\n   - _Why_: Known-circuit models let you check that the on-manifold operator recovers the RIGHT circuit and that the certificate actually flags the bad interventions.\n3. Ablate to attribute the gain: swap the fitted flow for a structureless isotropic density (expect faithfulness to fall back to the arbitrary-write baseline), keep only the flow constraint with U fixed (expect most of the gain to remain), and compare the exact iterative solve to a fast one-pass approximation.\n   - _Why_: These pin the improvement to the natural-manifold constraint specifically, not to any incidental change.\n\n### Natural-Manifold Model\n*Fit a frozen normalizing flow over the target network's natural activations, defining the energy that says which states are reachable.*\n\n4. Fit a normalizing flow (about 8 coupling blocks) on those activations once and freeze it; it returns an energy E(a) that is low for natural states and high for off-manifold ones. Record the average natural energy as a baseline.\n\n*The manifold energy E of a candidate activation a is its negative log-density under a normalizing flow $g_{L}$ fit on natural activations; low E means a lies on the target model's natural representation manifold.*\n$$ E(a) = -\\log p_L(a) = -\\log p_Z\\big(g_L(a)\\big) - \\log\\big|\\det J_{g_L}(a)\\big| \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: One small density model becomes the single object we both write onto and read divergence from — no per-experiment retraining.\n\n### On-Manifold Intervention\n*Write the nearest natural-manifold counterfactual that exactly honours the intended causal value, so reachability holds by construction.*\n\n5. Specify the causal target the usual DAS/interchange way — a subspace U (about 8 directions) and a source value v* — and form the ordinary write $a_{patch} = a -  U U^{T} a + U$ v* as the baseline that may land off the manifold.\n\n*The ordinary interchange/DAS write replaces the targeted causal subspace U with a source value v*, the arbitrary write whose result may leave the natural manifold.*\n$$ a_{\\mathrm{patch}} = a - U U^{\\top} a + U v^{*}, \\qquad U \\in \\mathbb{R}^{d \\times k},\\; v^{*} \\in \\mathbb{R}^{k} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This is exactly the intended causal change interpretability already wants; $a_{patch}$ is the arbitrary write that may leave the manifold, which we will improve on.\n6. Instead of writing $a_{patch},$ solve for a* — the natural (low-energy) state that still exactly satisfies $U^{T}a =$ v* — by iterating ~20 steps in the flow's latent space, then write a* into the network and finish the forward pass. 【author decision: searching for the lowest-energy state with this causal value gives the most 'typical' such state but erases the rest of the original activation (the counterfactual forgets the specific prompt); searching instead for the on-manifold state CLOSEST to the original keeps the context but may be less typical. The authors must decide which counterfactual they want — pure naturalness, or naturalness plus a term that keeps a* close to the original — because the two answer different questions.】\n\n*The on-manifold operator writes the nearest natural-manifold representation that exactly realizes the intended causal value, solved by constrained minimization of the flow energy in latent space; this a* replaces $a_{patch}$ as the patched activation.*\n$$ a^{*} = \\arg\\min_{a}\\; E(a) \\quad \\text{s.t.}\\quad U^{\\top} a = v^{*} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: a* carries the same intended causal value but is guaranteed reachable, so the explanation can't come from a hidden pathway the model never naturally uses.\n\n### Per-Intervention Certificate\n*Decompose the off-manifold radius onto the behavioural null-space and calibrate it against the model's own logits to decide harmless vs pernicious at intervention time.*\n\n7. At a*, compute which activation directions actually move the output (the behavioural Jacobian), and split the difference $\\delta  = a_{patch} - $ a* into a behaviour-irrelevant part $\\delta _{null}$ and a behaviour-relevant part $\\delta _{live}.$\n   - _Why_: Harmless divergence lives in directions that don't affect behaviour; pernicious divergence lives in the ones that do — this split is what tells them apart.\n8. For each intervention, report the certificate c = (how far off-manifold the arbitrary write was, what fraction of the correction lands in behaviour-changing directions), read right when the intervention is made.\n\n*The per-intervention certificate pairs the off-manifold radius r with the fraction of the displacement $\\delta $ falling in the layer's behaviourally-live directions (the complement of the null-space $N_{L})$; large live fraction with large radius flags a pernicious intervention.*\n$$ c = \\Big(\\, r(a_{\\mathrm{patch}}) = E(a_{\\mathrm{patch}}) - \\bar{E}_{\\mathrm{nat}},\\;\\; \\tfrac{\\lVert \\delta_{\\mathrm{live}}\\rVert}{\\lVert \\delta \\rVert}\\,\\Big),\\quad \\delta = a_{\\mathrm{patch}} - a^{*} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A big radius with a big live fraction means the original arbitrary write was about to recruit a hidden pathway — you learn this BEFORE trusting the explanation.\n9. Calibrate the certificate threshold on matched pairs that differ ONLY in {arbitrary write vs on-manifold write}, scoring each by how far the intervened output strays from what the model would do at a genuinely reachable state. 【author decision: if 'a reachable state' is judged by the same flow that builds the certificate, the test grades its own homework; the authors must pick an independent yardstick — the known ground-truth circuit behaviour on InterpBench, or a separate reachability model, or 'the nearest state some real input actually produces' — and justify that it is independent.】\n   - _Why_: The judge is the model's own natural behaviour, not the certificate itself, so the harmless/pernicious cutoff isn't circular.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 流形内因果干预：面向可信解释的、由构造可达的反事实表示\n\n**方法名称.** On-Manifold Intervention Operator (OMIO)\n\n## 研究动机\n机制可解释性（mechanistic interpretability）想解释神经网络“为什么”这样行为，办法是做“因果干预”：伸进网络内部，把某个内部激活改写成另一个值，看输出怎么变。activation patching、interchange intervention、Distributed Alignment Search（DAS）都是这么干的。问题在于：你写进去的值是从别的运行里借来的、或被放大（有时放大 15 倍），网络可能因此进入一个正常输入下永远到不了的状态。在这种非自然状态里，它会激活一些在真实输入下保持沉默的隐藏通路——于是你读到的解释描述的是这些隐藏通路，而不是网络真正的工作方式。解释就不忠实了。\n\n代表性工作（ICLR 2026 那篇“divergent representations”）证明了这一现象，把损害分成“harmless”（改动落在不影响行为的方向）和“pernicious”（唤醒了隐藏通路），并用一个额外训练惩罚——Counterfactual-Latent（CL）loss——把被干预的状态轻轻拉回正常。但这个惩罚是软的、每个实验都要重训、且从不保证状态可达；而且它只在事后给 harmless/pernicious 贴标签，等你能判断时已经太晚。\n\n为什么是现在：那篇论文刚把问题提清楚，而正面解决它的工具也已就绪。normalizing flow（一种可精确求逆的密度模型）可以在网络的正常激活上一次性拟合，刻画它的“自然流形”——网络真正会到达的状态集合。InterpBench（NeurIPS 2024）提供了带已知真值电路的小 transformer 用来核对忠实度。我们的做法：先一次性建好这个自然流形模型，再让干预只写入流形上、同时仍精确携带目标因果改动的状态——于是可达性由构造成立，而非靠惩罚。同一个模型还免费给你一个逐次干预证书，把改动拆成“与行为无关”和“与行为相关”两部分，在你信任解释之前就告诉你 harmless 还是 pernicious。目标网络全程不重训。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景脚手架\n*不变的支撑部分：收集自然激活、在已知电路模型上验证、并做归因消融。*\n\n1. 在大量正常文本(约 20 万个 token 位置)上运行冻结的目标网络,保存因果子空间 U 所在的第 L 层残差流激活(每个 token 位置一个向量),覆盖多样上下文;不改任何权重。这批自然激活 $A_{L}$ 就是后续『在流形上』所指的经验依据。\n   - _为什么_: 这些保存下来的激活就是网络的“自然流形”——它真正会到达的状态，也是我们要把干预限制在其中的范围。\n2. 实际使用:在干预时刻跑 第5步（用常规 $DAS/interc\\dots $）-第8步（对每次干预）,用校准阈值读 c 判 harmless/pernicious 后再信任该解释;在 InterpBench SIIT transformer(真值电路)与 Boundless DAS 7B 设定上验证,度量恢复电路忠实度、oracle 流形内程度与证书 AUROC。\n   - _为什么_: 已知电路的模型能验证流形内算子恢复的是“正确”的电路，且证书确实能标出坏干预。\n3. 消融以归因:负对照——把拟合的 flow 换成无结构的各向同性 Gaussian 能量(同样的最小化机制,预期忠实度掉回任意写入基线);正对照——只保留 flow 能量约束、U 固定为 DAS 解(预期大部分收益仍在);速度消融——分摊式一遍投影器 vs 精确迭代求解。\n   - _为什么_: 这些把改进钉到“自然流形约束”这一具体原因上，而非任何附带改动。\n\n### 自然流形模型\n*在目标网络的自然激活上拟合一个冻结的 normalizing flow，定义“哪些状态可达”的能量。*\n\n4. 在这些激活上一次性拟合一个 normalizing flow $g_{L}($约 8 个 affine-coupling 块)并冻结;它给出流形能量 E(a) = -log $p_{L}(a)($式 eq:energy):自然状态能量低、偏离流形的状态能量高。把留出自然激活的平均能量记为基线 $\\bar{E}_{nat},$并仅当留出自然 bits-per-dim 与更深参照流相近时才接受该 flow,确保 E 是可信密度。\n\n*流形能量 E(a) 是候选激活 a 在自然激活上拟合的 normalizing flow $g_{L}$ 下的负对数密度；E 越低，表示 a 越落在目标模型的自然表示流形上。*\n$$ E(a) = -\\log p_L(a) = -\\log p_Z\\big(g_L(a)\\big) - \\log\\big|\\det J_{g_L}(a)\\big| \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 一个小密度模型同时充当“写入的目标”和“读取偏离度的对象”——无需逐实验重训。\n\n### 流形内干预\n*写入最接近自然流形、且精确满足目标因果值的反事实状态，使可达性由构造成立。*\n\n5. 用常规 DAS/interchange 方式指定因果目标:子空间 $U(d\\times k,$如 k=8)和源值 v*(U 由 Boundless DAS 学得或直接给定),并构造常规任意写入 $a_{patch} = a -  U U^{T} a + U$ v*(式 eq:patch)作为可能偏离流形的基线干预。\n\n*常规 interchange/DAS 写入把目标因果子空间 U 的分量替换为源值 v*，即可能脱离自然流形的任意写入 $a_{patch}$。*\n$$ a_{\\mathrm{patch}} = a - U U^{\\top} a + U v^{*}, \\qquad U \\in \\mathbb{R}^{d \\times k},\\; v^{*} \\in \\mathbb{R}^{k} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这正是可解释性本来就想要的因果改动；$a_{patch}$ 是可能脱离流形的任意写入，我们要在其上改进。\n6. 不写 $a_{patch},$而是求 a* $= argmin_{a}$ E(a) s.t. $U^{T}a =$ v*(式 eq:project):在 flow 隐空间 $z = g_{L}(a)$ 中投影梯度求解——从 $z_{0} = g_{L}(a_{patch})$ 出发,下降 $\\| z\\| ^{2}$ 同时用 Gauss-Newton 步重投影 k 个线性约束 $U^{T} g_{L}^{-1}(z) =$ v*,迭代 T=20 步,得 a* $= g_{L}^{-1}(z_{T})$。把 a* 写入第 L 层残差流并完成冻结前向,使因果效应从流形内状态读出。【作者需决定:全局最小化 E 选出与 v* 一致的『最典型』自然状态,却抹去原激活 a 的非因果内容(反事实遗忘了具体 prompt);另一选择是离原 a 最近、且满足 v* 的流形点(保留上下文但密度可能更低)。作者须决定何者才是所要的忠实反事实——纯能量最小化,还是能量加锚定项 E(a) $+ \\lambda \\| a -  a_{orig}\\| ^{2} /$ 把位移限制在零空间内——因为二者给出根本不同的反事实。】\n\n*流形内算子写入的是“在精确实现目标因果值 $U^{T} a =$ v* 的前提下、能量 E 最小”的自然流形表示 a*，通过在 flow 隐空间对能量做带约束最小化求解；该 a* 取代 $a_{patch}$ 作为被 patch 的激活。*\n$$ a^{*} = \\arg\\min_{a}\\; E(a) \\quad \\text{s.t.}\\quad U^{\\top} a = v^{*} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: a* 携带同样的目标因果值，但保证可达，于是解释不会来自模型自然下从不使用的隐藏通路。\n\n### 逐次干预证书\n*把偏离流形半径分解到 behavioural null-space，并用模型自身 logits 标定，在干预时刻判定 harmless 还是 pernicious。*\n\n7. 在 a* 处用 autograd 估计 behavioural Jacobian $J_{beh} = d$ logits / d a,对其做 SVD,把奇异值低于最大值某固定比例(如 1e-3)的右奇异方向当作行为零空间 $N_{L}$;把位移 $\\delta  = a_{patch} - $ a* 拆成 $N_{L}$ 内的 $\\delta _{null}$ 与 $\\delta _{live} = \\delta  -  \\delta _{null},$并报告活跃比例对该阈值的敏感性。\n   - _为什么_: harmless 偏离落在不影响行为的方向，pernicious 偏离落在会影响行为的方向——这个拆分正是区分二者的依据。\n8. 对每次干预,在干预时刻给出证书 c =(偏离流形半径 $r = E(a_{patch}) -  \\bar{E}_{nat},$活跃比例 $\\| \\delta _{live}\\| /\\| \\delta \\| )($式 eq:cert);把 c 保留为二维对 (r, 活跃比例) 交由 第9步（在只改变{任意写入$\\dots $） 学习判定边界——半径大且活跃比例大即标记为 pernicious 干预。\n\n*逐次干预证书 c 由两部分组成：偏离流形的半径 r，以及位移 $\\delta $ 落在该层“行为活跃方向”（零空间 $N_{L}$ 之补）上的比例；半径大且活跃比例高即标记为 pernicious（会招募隐藏通路）的干预。*\n$$ c = \\Big(\\, r(a_{\\mathrm{patch}}) = E(a_{\\mathrm{patch}}) - \\bar{E}_{\\mathrm{nat}},\\;\\; \\tfrac{\\lVert \\delta_{\\mathrm{live}}\\rVert}{\\lVert \\delta \\rVert}\\,\\Big),\\quad \\delta = a_{\\mathrm{patch}} - a^{*} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 半径大且活跃比例高，说明原始任意写入即将招募隐藏通路——你在信任解释之前就知道了。\n9. 在只改变{任意写入 $a_{patch}$ vs 流形内写入 a*}、固定 (U, v*) 的匹配样本对上标定证书阈值:用 oracle 给每对打分,拟合在 (r, 活跃比例) 空间最能区分 harmless 与 pernicious 的阈值。【作者需决定:oracle $KL(p_{logits}(intervened) \\|  p_{logits}(nearest-natural-reachable))$ 中的『最近自然可达状态』由生成证书的同一 flow 定义,可能并不独立于被验证对象;作者须选择能打破这种循环的 oracle——例如在 InterpBench 上用真值电路规定的反事实行为,或拟合一个与证书 flow 互相独立、架构不同的可达性模型,或把可达性按行为定义为某真实输入实际产生的最近激活——并论证所选 oracle 确实独立。】\n   - _为什么_: 裁判是模型自身的自然行为，而非证书本身，所以 harmless/pernicious 的分界不会自我循环。\n\n"},{"id":"06","run_dir":"run_prompt06_agentdata","index":6,"title":"Provenance-Conditioned Gradient Stratification for Fine-Tuning Agents on Conflicting Multi-Source Trajectories","title_zh":"面向多源冲突轨迹的来源条件化梯度分层智能体微调方法","method_name":"Provenance-Conditioned Gradient Stratification (PCGS)","hook":"On agent states where two differently-sourced trajectories prescribe incompatible actions, uniform SFT/DPO over a unified corpus (ADP, AgentBank) does not just mildly underperform — it converges to a blurred policy whose downstream task-success is LOWER than training on the single most-reliable source alone, because every interaction contributes an identically-scaled gradient regardless of provenance. We show that the per-state cross-source disagreement is not noise to average out but a measurable signal that, used to stratify the gradient, recovers a policy dominating both pooling and best-single-source.","anchor_pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","anchor_pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","domain_category":"LLM Agents & Tool Use","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes a heterogeneous agent corpus's per-interaction supervision strength depend on the interaction's own provenance and reliability: after unification (ADP) or curation (AgentBank) every trajectory contributes an equally-scaled gradient, so when two sources prescribe different actions for the same state the objective blurs them instead of letting the more reliable source dominate that state.","pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by characterizing the corpus's per-(state,source) reliability distribution, partitioning each conflicted state's competing supervision targets by a state-conditional reliability criterion distinct from per-task reweighting and static label-denoising, assigning a matched per-partition gradient scale (protect the high-reliability target at full strength, attenuate the unreliable competing targets), and supplying a bias/variance decomposition that bounds how the stratified gradient recovers the best-source policy on agreeing states while removing the blur on conflicting ones.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions the shared inherited assumption that the supervision target for an agent fine-tuning corpus is a SINGLE pooled objective at all: every frontier method (ADP, AgentBank, Agent Q, NAT) descends from the assumption that diverse interaction data should be flattened into one training distribution before optimization, and none tests whether the corpus should instead be treated as multiple disagreeing sources whose disagreement is itself signal.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","how_closed":"Framing move (C01): names the locus current methods enforce supervision at — the pooled flatten-then-optimize loss that treats provenance as invariant once format is unified — and relocates the load-bearing signal to per-source disagreement geometry at matched states, arguing structurally why the conflict gradient (not the pooled mean) carries the reliability signal the pooled locus discards. Companion deliverable (controlled_diagnostic_design): ships the confound-isolating empirical separation — matched cross-source-conflict vs matched cross-source-agreement state sets at equal trajectory count and equal compute — showing the disagreement-as-signal treatment wins specifically on conflict states, isolating provenance disagreement from extra data or compute as the cause.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"fine-tuning LLM agents on heterogeneous interaction trajectory data","n_papers":41,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":26},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"openreview","n":2}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":16,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"AgentBank: Towards Generalized LLM Agents via Fine-Tuning on 50000+ Interaction Trajectories"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Enhancing Dialogue State Tracking Models through LLM-backed User-Agents Simulation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Learning Personalized Agent for Real-Time Face-to-Face Interaction in VR"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"FaGeL: Fabric LLMs Agent empowered Embodied Intelligence Evolution with Autonomous Human-Machine Collaboration"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Streamlining geoscience data analysis with an LLM-driven workflow"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Optimizing Autonomous Driving for Safety: A Human-Centric Approach with LLM-Enhanced RLHF"}],"more":10},{"year":2025,"n":23,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"EDGE: Efficient Data Selection for LLM Agents via Guideline Effectiveness"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Analyzing and Internalizing Complex Policy Documents for LLM Agents"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Personas within Parameters: Fine-Tuning Small Language Models with Low-Rank Adapters to Mimic User Behaviors"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Generalizability of Large Language Model-Based Agents: A Comprehensive Survey"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Improving Argumentative Reasoning in LLMs Using Online Debates and Agent-Based Interaction"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Interact-RAG: Reason and Interact with the Corpus, Beyond Black-Box Retrieval"}],"more":17},{"year":2026,"n":2,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"},{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"}],"more":0}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":16,"share":0.39},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":8,"share":0.195},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":5,"share":0.122},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":5,"share":0.122},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":4,"share":0.098},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":4,"share":0.098},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":3,"share":0.073},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":3,"share":0.073}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"The recent agent-tuning frontier has solved the INGESTION of heterogeneous interaction data but not its DIFFERENTIATED USE: Agent Data Protocol (semanticscholar:80af1501c0d70528ed775550320e8e0051ad5bfb) normalizes trajectories from radically different sources (human demonstrations, GPT-distilled, MCTS-search, simulated) into one Trajectory schema and then hands the unified stream to a single uniform SFT loss, and AgentBank (semanticscholar:b60a9a78caaf06fbdbf8ee91ed9416efa0e6c3c4) likewise pools 50k+ trajectories across 16 tasks under one cross-entropy objective. The structural failure is that once the corpus is unified, every token of every trajectory contributes an identically-scaled gradient regardless of whether that token came from a high-fidelity human demonstrator, a noisy distilled rollout, or a failed self-generated attempt — so when sources disagree on what action a state should map to (which they routinely do across provenance and task), the uniform objective averages the conflicting targets into a blurred policy rather than resolving them, and the heterogeneity that was the whole point of collecting diverse data is destroyed at exactly the moment it could be exploited. Neither EDGE (semanticscholar:7afed1ec0189d911fc75b9d204e39b364650e55c), which keeps/drops whole samples by a single scalar before training, nor NAT (openalex:W4411119300), which adds failed trajectories as a second binary bucket, reaches inside the per-token gradient to make the contribution of an interaction depend on its heterogeneous provenance and reliability.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:80af1501c0d70528ed775550320e8e0051ad5bfb","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"ADP introduces a unified Trajectory interlingua (Actions + Observations) that converts heterogeneous agent datasets into one standardized format consumable by downstream SFT, explicitly stating its design goal is simplicity/standardization so a uniform pipeline can train on all sources without per-dataset engineering. Its residue is that unification is purely representational: heterogeneity is erased at the schema boundary and the downstream loss is a single source-agnostic objective, so ADP never decides how much each source/quality stratum should shape the gradient — it makes the data trainable but treats a distilled rollout and a verified human demonstration as interchangeable supervision."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:b60a9a78caaf06fbdbf8ee91ed9416efa0e6c3c4","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"AgentBank scales trajectory SFT to 50k+ CoT-annotated trajectories over 16 tasks and shows generalist agent skill emerges from breadth, deliberately curating for quality at COLLECTION time. Its residue is that quality control is a pre-training-time filter producing one homogeneous high-quality pool; it has no in-training mechanism to keep exploiting the residual heterogeneity (task, difficulty, provenance) that survives curation, so all retained trajectories still contribute equally to the objective."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4411119300","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"NAT enhances agent tuning by adding negative (failed) trajectories alongside positive ones, recognizing that success-only data is incomplete. Its residue is that it treats outcome as a binary success/failure partition with a fixed objective per bucket; it does not produce a graded, per-interaction credit that varies continuously with how reliable or informative a heterogeneous source is, so partially-correct or cross-source-conflicting trajectories are forced into one of two coarse bins."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4402427562","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Agent Q collects trajectories via MCTS and trains with DPO on contrastive pairs scored by a blend of search Q-value and a feedback model, injecting outcome signal into the objective. Its residue is that it manufactures a single homogeneous self-generated source and a single preference objective over it; it does not address a corpus that MIXES self-generated, human, and distilled trajectories whose reliabilities differ, and so offers no way to reconcile conflicting supervision across provenance."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"fine-tuning LLM agents on heterogeneous interaction trajectory data","venue":"ICLR 2026","time":"2026","data":["multi-source agent interaction trajectories (tool/API use, web browsing, coding, embodied, dialogue)","mixed success/failure outcomes","varying provenance: human demos, GPT-distilled, self-generated/MCTS, simulated"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with agent fine-tuning background","preference":"both","baseline":"uniform supervised fine-tuning / DPO on unified-format agent trajectory corpora (ADP, AgentBank)","limitation":"current pipelines normalize heterogeneous interaction data into one format and then optimize a single uniform objective over it, so source/quality/modality heterogeneity is discarded before the loss ever sees it","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared audit lens, applied at two sites, is: 'is uniform pooled treatment of heterogeneous interaction data correct, or does per-state cross-source provenance carry load-bearing signal the pooled loss discards?' SITE 1 (sibling / C01 + C02): we relocate the supervision locus from the pooled corpus to per-source disagreement geometry. For a state s, let the corpus contain trajectories from sources g in G (human demo, GPT-distilled, MCTS-self-generated, simulated). We define the cross-source conflict score D(s) = 1 - max_a sum_g w_g * 1[a_g*(s)=a], where a_g*(s) is the modal action source g prescribes at s (or the nearest neighbor in an embedding of the policy's penultimate-layer state representation h(s), a model-internal readout, when s is not exactly repeated), and w_g is a per-source reliability prior (initialized from each source's held-out trajectory task-success rate, an external-oracle quantity computed once on a validation split). D(s) in [0,1] is computable from the text alone: high when sources disagree about the right action at s. SITE 2 (anchor / C04): we stratify the fine-tuning gradient by provenance-conditioned reliability rather than reweighting per-task losses. For each training interaction (s, a, g), define a per-interaction gradient scale beta(s,g) = sigma(lambda * (rho(s,g) - D(s))), where rho(s,g) is source g's state-conditional reliability at s (the validation-estimated probability that following g's action at states like s leads to task success, read off a small reliability head trained on (h(s), g) -> outcome), sigma is the logistic, and lambda is a single named temperature hyperparameter bridging the reliability and conflict units. The fine-tuning loss becomes L = sum over interactions of beta(s,g) * CE(a | s), so on agreeing states (low D) all sources retain near-full gradient, while on conflicting states (high D) only the locally-most-reliable source's target keeps a large beta and the competing unreliable targets are attenuated toward zero — the blur is removed at the gradient, not by dropping samples or reweighting tasks. The load-bearing artifact (C04 spine) is a bias/variance decomposition: we prove that under a mixture-of-sources data model where each source's action is the true optimal action corrupted by source-specific noise, the pooled (uniform-beta) estimator incurs an irreducible bias on conflict states equal to the reliability-weighted disagreement, whereas the stratified estimator's bias is bounded by (1 - max_g rho(s,g)) and vanishes when one source is reliable — quantifying exactly when differentiated treatment strictly beats pooling. Both sites read and write the SAME object D(s): C01 names it as the relocated signal, C04 consumes it inside beta to scale the gradient, and C02's diagnostic measures task-success as a function of D(s).","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery — both pivot on the per-state cross-source conflict object D(s) — so I built ONE object read by both legs rather than two modules; the evidence is that the anchor's gradient scale beta is undefined without a conflict measure, and the sibling's 'disagreement-is-signal' claim is empty without a gradient that consumes it, so a two-module design would duplicate D(s). (b) I considered (rejected) a per-source loss-reweighting design (one scalar weight per source) — it regresses to method_lineage collateral c0 (multi-task loss reweighting) because it is state-independent, and to c1 (static noisy-label aggregation) if w_g is frozen; I avoided both by making beta state-conditional via D(s) and rho(s,g), so the same source can be trusted at one state and attenuated at another. I also considered a one-time keep/drop curation (EDGE-style) and rejected it because it cannot let a source dominate locally without discarding its useful interactions elsewhere.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: fine-tune a 7-8B base agent (e.g. on the ADP-unified WebArena+coding+tool-use mixture with provenance tags) under (i) uniform SFT, (ii) best-single-source SFT, and (iii) our provenance-conditioned stratified loss, then measure downstream task-success rate on the held-out matched cross-source-conflict state set. If the candidate works, the stratified loss's task-success on conflict states rises ABOVE both uniform SFT and best-single-source, while agreement-state success is unchanged (the qualitative reveal: pooling sits below best-single-source on conflict states; stratification climbs above it). The single named load-bearing variable is the conflict-conditioned gradient scale beta(s,g); the non-tautological negative control replaces the learned beta with provenance-permuted beta (shuffle the source labels g before computing rho and D, so beta is decorrelated from true provenance while its marginal distribution is preserved) — this must drive conflict-state task-success back down to the uniform-SFT baseline. Because the control holds beta's magnitude distribution fixed and only severs its link to real provenance, a recovered task-success gain cannot be attributed to mere gradient rescaling, regularization, or reduced effective data — only to provenance-correct stratification. A positive control fine-tuning with beta as the ONLY modification (no other curation) recovering most of the conflict-state gain converts the falsifier into an identification of beta as the mechanism.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:80af1501c0d70528ed775550320e8e0051ad5bfb","delta":"ADP unifies heterogeneous trajectories into ONE format and then applies a source-agnostic SFT loss where every interaction's gradient is identically scaled; we keep their unified format but make the per-interaction gradient scale beta(s,g) a state-conditional function of provenance reliability and cross-source conflict, which their construction never produces because provenance is discarded once format is unified."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:b60a9a78caaf06fbdbf8ee91ed9416efa0e6c3c4","delta":"AgentBank pools ~50k curated trajectories under one cross-entropy with curation done once before training (keep/drop); we replace the one-time global curation with a continuous, state-conditional gradient stratification, so a source can dominate at one state and be attenuated at another rather than being globally kept or dropped."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4411119300","delta":"NAT buckets trajectories into a coarse binary positive/negative (success/failure) treatment decided before training; we condition the gradient on a continuous per-(state,source) reliability rho(s,g) and conflict D(s), giving within-source, per-state differentiation that a binary success/failure bucket cannot express."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4402427562","delta":"Agent Q improves a single self-generated source via MCTS-guided preference optimization; we instead treat MULTIPLE disagreeing provenance sources jointly and derive a cross-source conflict signal D(s) to arbitrate between them at the gradient, a multi-source arbitration their single-source self-improvement loop does not construct."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:80af1501c0d70528ed775550320e8e0051ad5bfb","what_step_was_missed":"ADP constructed the cross-source unification map that puts all provenances into one action/observation schema, but stopped at format unification and fed the result to a uniform loss; to already contain our contribution it would have needed to construct a per-(state,source) reliability estimator rho(s,g) plus a state-conditional conflict score D(s) and route them into a per-interaction gradient scale — i.e. carry provenance THROUGH the loss rather than dissolving it at the format layer. That state-conditional gradient-routing construction, with its bias/variance bound on conflict states, is the missing step."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":319,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"No hard-floor rule fires: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict='clear' (anchor C04 supplies its error-decomposition spine and both uniform and cheap-alternative baselines; sibling C01's adversarial-stealth reject lessons do not bind), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id=null, and paper_pointed_threat (ADP) is substrate-level not exact-mechanism overlap with addressable_via already satisfied. The single borderline is recipe_application_check.entries[1].verdict='borderline' on the C01 sibling — the cluster's locus-relocation verb and mechanistic-WHY account ARE performed in core_mechanism SITE 1, the only gap being C01's adversarial-security validation idiom which is inapplicable to a non-adversarial training method; no sibling under assumption_audit_and_pivot (C05 latent-identifiability theorems, C11/C19 probabilistic-bound preconditions, C28 distributed-protocol structure, C29 operator property) fits this supervision-locus pivot better than C01, so a sub_pattern swap would not improve the fit. The load-bearing C04 leg is cleanly applied, so this borderline is surfaced as a reviewer concern for Phase 4 rather than triggering a no-improvement revise.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes a heterogeneous agent corpus's per-interaction supervision strength depend on the interaction's own provenance and reliability: after unification (ADP) or curation (AgentBank) every trajectory contributes an equally-scaled gradient, so when two sources prescribe different actions for the same state the objective blurs them instead of letting the more reliable source dominate that state.","main_pattern":"heterogeneous_decomposition","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is treating the partition criterion itself as the contribution while leaving its value unproven — a sensitivity/redundancy discriminator reviewers immediately map onto an established technique, rarely benchmarked against both the strongest uniform baseline and the obvious cheap alternative, and validated in a regime where the bottleneck does not bite.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Presenting a sensitivity or redundancy proxy as the novelty invites the verdict that it rediscovers known mixed-precision or low-rank results unless it is sharply differentiated from the obvious prior criterion.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The partition criterion beta(s,g) could be read as re-labeled loss-reweighting, but differentiation_from_lit and core_mechanism_reasoning explicitly distinguish it from per-task reweighting (c0) and static noisy-label aggregation (c1) by making it state-conditional, so the obvious-prior collapse is defended rather than ignored."},{"lesson_quoted":"Omitting comparison against both the strongest uniform baseline and the obvious cheap alternative (SVD/PCA, structured dropout, a natively trained smaller model) leaves reviewers unable to tell whether the partition buys anything at all.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"falsification_prediction and core_mechanism_steps benchmark against uniform SFT/DPO (strongest uniform baseline) AND best-single-source SFT (cheap alternative), plus a frozen-beta=mean ablation collapsing to c0/c1."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a storage or throughput claim only on toy-scale models — where the compression bottleneck does not actually bite — undermines the entire motivation no matter how clean the method is.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Validation is specified at 7-8B base agent scale on the ADP-unified WebArena+coding+tool-use mixture, the regime where cross-source conflict actually arises."},{"lesson_quoted":"Skipping any analysis of why the heterogeneity exists — the data or value distribution that drives the partition — makes the technical novelty and the potential impact impossible to assess.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Step 1 characterizes the per-(state,source) reliability distribution and the hook predicts the regime split (pooling falls below best-single-source), supplying the value distribution that forces the partition."},{"lesson_quoted":"A clever partition with no measured real-world deployment metric (no inference latency or memory speedup) reads as a proxy-only contribution and stalls at borderline.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The reported metric is downstream agent task-success rate (the true deployment metric for an agent policy), not a proxy."},{"lesson_quoted":"Bolting together established components (distillation plus pruning plus calibration) without an error bound or artifact specific to the new setting reads as incremental even when the target application is timely and important.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The bias/variance decomposition bounding when stratification strictly beats pooling on conflict states is the new-setting-specific load-bearing artifact, not a bolt-together of off-the-shelf parts."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions the shared inherited assumption that the supervision target for an agent fine-tuning corpus is a SINGLE pooled objective at all: every frontier method (ADP, AgentBank, Agent Q, NAT) descends from the assumption that diverse interaction data should be flattened into one training distribution before optimization, and none tests whether the corpus should instead be treated as multiple disagreeing sources whose disagreement is itself signal.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is a successful relocation that is demonstrated but not adversarially closed (no informed adversary at the new locus), a novelty-boundary collapse where the 'new' locus was already used by prior work, reintroducing the dissolved assumption via a clean reference model, or offering only a demonstration with no mechanistic account of why the locus carries the signal.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a relocated signal is 'stealthier' or 'harder to remove' without defeating an adaptive defender who searches the same new locus leaves the central claim unverified.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"This is an adversarial-stealth lesson; the candidate is a non-adversarial training-objective method making no stealth claim, so the lesson does not bind."},{"lesson_quoted":"Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work — normalization statistics, activation-similarity losses, semantic concept triggers — collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The relocated locus (per-source disagreement geometry D(s)) risks overlap with prior per-task reweighting / noisy-label / NAT positive-negative bucketing; differentiation_from_lit makes the state-conditional, continuous, within-source distinction explicit and the conflict-vs-agreement ablation measures it, defending the boundary."},{"lesson_quoted":"A defense whose relocation silently depends on a clean reference model or a known anomaly distribution reintroduces precisely the strong assumption the move was supposed to eliminate.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"rho(s,g) and w_g are estimated from held-out validation roll-out task-success of the same corpus's sources, not from any external clean reference model or assumed anomaly distribution."},{"lesson_quoted":"Demonstrating the new locus only on fixed, non-adaptive or outdated baselines while omitting any account of why it works reads as a stacked pipeline of existing components rather than a principled shift.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The bias/variance decomposition gives the mechanistic WHY (pooled estimator incurs irreducible conflict-state bias equal to reliability-weighted disagreement; stratified bias bounded by 1-max_g rho), so it is not a why-less stacked pipeline."},{"lesson_quoted":"Wiring off-the-shelf generators or tools into a new attack setting without a structural reason for the locus change gets judged as engineering integration, not insight.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The locus change is motivated structurally (provenance is discarded at ADP's format-unification layer; the disagreement gradient carries the reliability signal the pooled mean averages out), not by tool integration."}],"verdict":"clear"}],"verdict":"clear","reasoning":"Both gap_closure entries clear. The anchor (heterogeneous_decomposition / C04) defends every reject lesson — most importantly it supplies the error-decomposition spine (bias/variance bound) and benchmarks against both the strongest uniform baseline and the cheap best-single-source alternative, the two lessons that most often sink C04 papers. The sibling (assumption_audit_and_pivot / C01) carries one borderline on the novelty-boundary-collapse lesson (D(s) could read as re-labeled per-task reweighting / NAT bucketing) but differentiation_from_lit makes the state-conditional continuous distinction explicit and the conflict-vs-agreement ablation measures it; the adversarial-stealth lessons do not bind a non-adversarial method."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes a heterogeneous agent corpus's per-interaction supervision strength depend on the interaction's own provenance and reliability: after unification (ADP) or curation (AgentBank) every trajectory contributes an equally-scaled gradient, so when two sources prescribe different actions for the same state the objective blurs them instead of letting the more reliable source dominate that state.","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Discriminate components by a magnitude-, sensitivity-, influence-, or redundancy-based criterion into a high-impact minority and a near-redundant bulk, then preserve/retain-at-full-fidelity the minority while aggressively attenuating the bulk; the load-bearing artifact is an error/sensitivity decomposition that bounds how the differentiated treatment recovers the original objective.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism SITE 2 performs exactly this: it discriminates per-(state,source) interactions by a state-conditional reliability criterion beta(s,g)=sigma(lambda*(rho(s,g)-D(s))), retains the high-reliability target at near-full gradient while attenuating the unreliable competing targets toward zero, and supplies the C04 spine — a bias/variance decomposition proving the pooled estimator's irreducible conflict-state bias versus the stratified estimator's bounded bias. The signature move and its error-decomposition spine are both present.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions the shared inherited assumption that the supervision target for an agent fine-tuning corpus is a SINGLE pooled objective at all: every frontier method (ADP, AgentBank, Agent Q, NAT) descends from the assumption that diverse interaction data should be flattened into one training distribution before optimization, and none tests whether the corpus should instead be treated as multiple disagreeing sources whose disagreement is itself signal.","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Relocate the attack or defense to a different representational locus the field treated as invariant — re-anchor enforcement at an overlooked locus (labels, activations, distribution shape, behavior) and supply a mechanistic account of WHY the new locus carries the signal; validated in adversarial/empirical security and safety settings with attack-success / detection performance.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism SITE 1 performs the locus-relocation verb: it names the pooled flatten-then-optimize loss as the locus current methods enforce supervision at, then relocates the load-bearing signal to per-source disagreement geometry D(s), and core_mechanism's bias/variance decomposition supplies the mechanistic WHY (step 5 of the cluster). The relocation move and the WHY-account are genuinely performed. The mismatch is domain-flavor: C01's example corpus and validation idiom are adversarial security/detection (attack-success rates), whereas this candidate is a non-adversarial training-objective relocation validated by task-success. The parent assumption-audit move is fully instantiated; the cluster's adversarial validation idiom is necessarily absent because the setting is not adversarial.","verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The anchor C04 entry is cleanly applied — both the differentiated-treatment partition and its load-bearing error-decomposition spine appear in core_mechanism. The sibling C01 entry is borderline: the cluster's signature locus-relocation verb plus the mechanistic-WHY account are performed, but C01 is the adversarial-security-locus sub-cluster while this candidate relocates a supervision locus in a non-adversarial training setting, so the cluster's attack-success/adaptive-adversary validation idiom is absent."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["heterogeneous_decomposition","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"The composition set {heterogeneous_decomposition, assumption_audit_and_pivot} matches none of the three documented reject-favored 2-way compositions (decomp+self_supervised_signal_engineering, decomp+structural_prior_encoding, operator_substitution+decomp); no anti-pattern fires."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:80af1501c0d70528ed775550320e8e0051ad5bfb","threat_source":"lit_table","subsumption_argument":"ADP (Agent Data Protocol) is the most specific competitor because it already constructs the cross-source unification map that places all provenances into one action/observation schema and demonstrates effective fine-tuning from it — the exact substrate this candidate fine-tunes on. The candidate's claim stands only if carrying provenance THROUGH the loss via a state-conditional gradient scale beta(s,g) measurably beats ADP's source-agnostic uniform loss on the matched cross-source-conflict state set. If conflict-state task-success under stratification did NOT exceed both uniform SFT and best-single-source, the contribution would collapse back into ADP's already-published uniform-loss result. No retrieved collision hit constructs a per-(state,source) provenance-conditioned gradient scale for agent fine-tuning, so the overlap is substrate-level, not exact-mechanism.","addressable_via":"Already addressed by differentiation_from_lit[0].delta and what_step_was_missed, which pin the missing step as the per-(state,source) reliability estimator + conflict score routed into a per-interaction gradient scale that ADP never builds; the falsification_prediction's conflict-state head-to-head against ADP-style uniform SFT is the discriminating experiment."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Provenance-Conditioned Gradient Stratification for Fine-Tuning Agents on Conflicting Multi-Source Trajectories\n\n**Method.** Provenance-Conditioned Gradient Stratification (PCGS)\n\n## Motivation\nPeople now train LLM agents on a grab-bag of interaction data: recordings of humans doing the task, traces copied from a stronger model, attempts the agent generated itself via search, and simulated runs. Recent work has focused on making all this mixed data usable at all. Agent Data Protocol (ADP) converts every source into one common format, and AgentBank piles up 50,000+ trajectories and trains on them with a single ordinary loss. The catch is that 'one common format' also means 'one common treatment': during training, every piece of data pushes the model with equal force, whether it came from a careful human demonstrator or a sloppy auto-generated attempt. That matters because different sources often DISAGREE about what to do in the same situation. When the training loss treats them equally, it just averages the conflicting advice, and the model ends up with a muddled compromise. On exactly those disagreement situations, the averaged model can actually do WORSE than if you had trained on only the single most-reliable source. The two existing partial fixes do not reach this problem: EDGE throws away whole low-quality samples once before training, and NAT sorts trajectories into a coarse 'succeeded vs failed' pair of bins. Neither makes the training signal of an individual interaction depend, situation-by-situation, on how trustworthy its source is right there. This is fixable now because the unified multi-source datasets already exist with source labels attached, and we can cheaply measure how much sources disagree at a given state using the model's own internal representation of that state. Our method (Provenance-Conditioned Gradient Stratification, PCGS) measures, for each situation, how much the sources disagree and how reliable each source is, and then scales each interaction's training push accordingly — letting the trustworthy source dominate where there is conflict, while leaving everything untouched where sources already agree. If this works, collecting messy extra data stops being risky: the loss will automatically discount a noisy source precisely on the situations where it is wrong.\n\n## Method\n### Conflict & Reliability Measurement\n*Turn the unified corpus into per-state buckets and measure, per situation, how much sources disagree (D) and how reliable each source is $(\\rho ).$*\n\n1. Group the interactions by both situation and source. Represent each interaction's state with the base model's own internal vector h(s) — take the model's last hidden layer at the final observation token (just before it would produce the action) and scale it to unit length. Then merge near-identical states across sources by joining any two whose vectors have cosine similarity above a threshold tau, using single-linkage clustering. Choose tau on a validation split: try several values and pick the loosest one at which states grouped together still mostly agree on the action (default to 0.9 if no clear elbow). Each group stores, for every source, the action that source recommends in that situation.\n   - _Why_: You cannot tell that two sources disagree until you can line up the same situation across sources, which the unified format hides.\n2. Give each source a single trust number. On a held-out validation split, run that source's trajectories and record how often the task succeeds; the source's trust prior $w_{g}$ is that average success rate. You end with one number per source (for example: human demonstrations, model-distilled rollouts, self-generated search rollouts, simulated episodes).\n   - _Why_: A source that usually succeeds should count more when measuring who is right in a conflict.\n3. Train a small reliability predictor. It is a 2-layer neural network (hidden size 512) that takes the frozen state vector h(s) together with a learned 32-dimensional embedding $e_{g}$ identifying the source, and outputs a number in [0,1] via a sigmoid: how likely following source g in situation s leads to success. Train it with standard binary cross-entropy against the recorded success/failure of each situation the source actually visited. Because the source identity is an embedding over the shared state space, the predictor gives a reliability $\\rho (s,g)$ for any situation-source pair, even combinations never seen — so trust is measured per situation, not once globally.\n   - _Why_: Trust is not constant — a source can be good in one kind of situation and bad in another — so reliability must be measured per situation, not once globally.\n4. For each situation group, compute a conflict score that measures how much the trust-weighted sources fail to agree on one best action. First make actions comparable: turn each tool call into a normalized (tool name, sorted arguments) form and compare those exactly, and compare free-form text actions by checking whether their state-vector embeddings are very similar (cosine similarity above an action-sameness level, default 0.95). For each source take its most frequent canonical action. The score is 1 minus the trust-weighted share of sources backing the single most-supported action: near 0 when they agree, near 1 when they clash. Attach this score to every interaction in the group.\n\n*The per-state cross-source conflict score D(s) $\\in $ [0,1]: one minus the reliability-weighted agreement on the most-supported action, where $a_{g}*(s)$ is the modal action source g prescribes at s and $w_{g}$ is source g's reliability prior. High when sources disagree.*\n$$ D(s) = 1 - \\max_{a} \\sum_{g \\in G} w_g \\, \\mathbf{1}[a_g^{*}(s) = a] \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This single number is the signal the whole method is built on: it locates exactly where the sources are fighting.\n\n### Provenance-Conditioned Gradient Stratification\n*Convert conflict and reliability into a per-interaction gradient scale $\\beta $ and fine-tune with the stratified loss.*\n\n5. Combine reliability and conflict into a per-interaction scale $\\beta (s,g):$ pass the temperature $\\lambda $ times the difference (reliability minus conflict) through a logistic function. Pick $\\lambda $ by trying a few values on a log grid (such as 0.5, 1, 2, 4, 8) and keeping the one that gives the best success on held-out conflict situations in a quick trial fine-tune. Do not rescale $\\beta $ within a group: keeping it on an absolute scale is exactly what lets a high-conflict group push the model less overall than an agreeing group. One real choice is left to you. 【author decision: compute the conflict and reliability quantities once up front as a fixed schedule, OR recompute them as training proceeds and the model changes — this affects the error-bound check later.】\n\n*The per-interaction gradient scale $\\beta (s,g): a$ logistic $\\sigma $ of the temperature $\\lambda $ times the gap between source g's state-conditional reliability $\\rho (s,g)$ and the conflict score D(s). On agreeing states (low D) every source keeps near-full $\\beta $; on conflict states (high D) only the locally-most-reliable source keeps a large $\\beta .$*\n$$ \\beta(s,g) = \\sigma\\!\\big(\\lambda\\,(\\rho(s,g) - D(s))\\big) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: $\\beta $ is the knob that decides how hard each interaction pushes the model — turning it down only for unreliable sources in contested situations.\n6. Fine-tune the agent with the scaled loss: the one $\\beta (s,g)$ for a situation applies to all of that interaction's action tokens, multiplying their cross-entropy before the gradient step, while observation/prompt tokens are excluded from the loss as usual in agent fine-tuning. So $a low-\\beta $ conflicting interaction sends a proportionally weaker gradient, and the trained policy ends up leaning toward the $high-\\beta $ (more reliable) source in that situation. Check this by decoding the fine-tuned model on held-out conflict situations.\n\n*The stratified fine-tuning loss: each interaction's per-token cross-entropy CE(a|s) is multiplied by its gradient scale $\\beta (s,g)$ before backprop, so $a low-\\beta $ conflicting interaction propagates a proportionally smaller gradient.*\n$$ \\mathcal{L} = \\sum_{(s,a,g)} \\beta(s,g)\\,\\mathrm{CE}(a \\mid s) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Scaling the gradient (not deleting data) lets a source be quieted exactly where it is wrong while still contributing everywhere else.\n\n### Confound-Isolating Validation\n*Prove the conflict-state win is caused by provenance-correct stratification, with matched diagnostic sets, baseline comparison, the bias-bound check, and the state-conditionality ablation.*\n\n7. Build two matched test sets from the groups: conflict situations (the top quarter by conflict score) and agreement situations (the bottom quarter); skip the middle half so the two sets are clearly different. Make them comparable by drawing equal numbers of interactions, and by matching difficulty — bin situations by how often the original (un-fine-tuned) model already succeeds and sample equally from each difficulty bin — while keeping training compute equal. This way the only thing that differs between the sets is the conflict level.\n   - _Why_: Matching everything except conflict level is what lets you attribute any win specifically to handling disagreement, not to more data or compute.\n8. Measure downstream agent task-success on both test sets for three trained models: uniform training (every interaction weighted equally), best-single-source training, and the stratified loss. You must decide which single source is 'best'. 【author decision: use the globally best source (the one with the highest validation trust $w_{g},$ trained on by itself) as the fair baseline — picking the best source per situation would secretly use the very conflict signal the method is meant to find; you may additionally report a per-situation-oracle upper bound, but label it clearly as an oracle.】 This is the head-to-head that tests whether pooling actually falls below just using the best source on conflict situations, and whether stratification beats both.\n   - _Why_: This is the head-to-head that shows whether stratification beats both the standard pooled approach and the simple 'just use the best source' fallback.\n9. Check the predicted error bound. Define the target as the policy trained on, at each conflict situation, the action of the locally-most-reliable source. For each trained model, measure how far its next-action distribution sits from this target on held-out conflict situations, using total-variation distance (a standard 0-to-1 distance between two probability distributions). Confirm that the stratified model's gap stays below the predicted limit (one minus the highest per-source reliability, averaged over the set), while the uniform-pooled model's gap matches the trust-weighted-disagreement amount. Matching the predicted bound is what shows the method worked for the stated reason.\n\n*The bias bound on conflict states: the stratified estimator's bias is at most one minus the maximum per-source reliability at s, so it vanishes when any single source is reliable there — versus the pooled estimator's irreducible reliability-weighted-disagreement bias.*\n$$ \\mathrm{bias}_{\\mathrm{strat}}(s) \\;\\leq\\; 1 - \\max_{g} \\rho(s,g) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Confirming the predicted error bound is what turns 'it worked' into 'it worked for the stated reason'.\n10. Run an ablation that removes the situation-by-situation part of the scaling and check the conflict advantage disappears. Do it two ways: (a) replace $\\beta $ with a single average value for all interactions (this is just ordinary uniform training up to a learning-rate change), and (b) replace $\\beta $ with one frozen average per source (this is plain per-source reweighting). The advantage on conflict situations should show up only with the full situation-dependent $\\beta $ and vanish under both frozen versions — proving the benefit comes from adjusting per situation, not from reweighting sources or samples in general.\n   - _Why_: If the gain survives without situation-by-situation scaling, the contribution was not really about conflict — this proves it was.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 面向多源冲突轨迹的来源条件化梯度分层智能体微调方法\n\n**方法名称.** Provenance-Conditioned Gradient Stratification (PCGS)\n\n## 研究动机\n现在训练 LLM 智能体用的是一堆混杂的交互数据：有人类完成任务的录制、有从更强模型蒸馏出来的轨迹、有智能体自己用搜索（MCTS）生成的尝试，还有模拟跑出来的回合。最近的工作主要解决「让这些混杂数据能用」这一步。Agent Data Protocol（ADP）把每个来源都转成一种统一格式，AgentBank 则堆了 50000+ 条轨迹用一个普通的损失一起训练。问题在于「统一格式」也意味着「统一对待」：训练时每条数据都以相同力度推动模型，不管它来自认真的人类示范还是粗糙的自动生成尝试。这很关键，因为不同来源在同一情境下经常对「该做什么动作」意见不一。当训练损失一视同仁时，它只是把这些冲突的建议平均掉，模型学到的是一个模糊的折中。恰恰在这些分歧情境上，被平均出来的模型甚至可能比只用单一最可靠来源训练还要差。现有两种局部办法都够不着这个问题：EDGE 在训练前一次性丢掉整条低质量样本，NAT 把轨迹粗略地分成「成功 vs 失败」两个桶。两者都没有让单条交互的训练信号随情境、随其来源在该处的可信度而变化。现在能解决，是因为带来源标签的统一多源数据集已经现成，而且我们可以用模型对某状态的内部表征廉价地测量各来源在该状态上的分歧程度。我们的方法（Provenance-Conditioned Gradient Stratification, PCGS）针对每个情境测量各来源的分歧程度 D(s) 与每个来源的可靠性 $\\rho (s,g)$，据此缩放每条交互的训练推动力——在有冲突处让可靠来源占主导，在各来源本就一致处则保持不变。如果有效，收集杂乱的额外数据就不再是风险：损失会在某来源出错的那些情境上自动给它打折。\n\n## 方法\n### 冲突与可靠性测量\n*把统一语料转成按状态分组的桶，并按情境测量各来源的分歧程度 D 与每个来源的可靠性 $\\rho $。*\n\n1. 把交互按「情境」和「来源」一起分组。用基座模型自身的内部向量 h(s) 表示每条交互的状态——取模型最后一层隐藏状态在状态前缀最末一个观测 token 处的向量（即将生成动作之前那一刻），并归一化为单位长度。然后跨来源合并近乎相同的状态：对任意两个状态，若其向量余弦相似度高于阈值 tau，就用单链接(single-linkage)聚类把它们并到一起。tau 在验证集上选取：尝试多个取值，挑选「被并到一组的状态在动作上仍大体一致」时最宽松的那个（若没有明显拐点则默认 0.9）。每个分组保存每个来源在该情境下推荐的动作。\n   - _为什么_: 只有把同一情境在各来源间对齐，才能看出两个来源是否分歧，而统一格式恰恰把这点抹掉了。\n2. 给每个来源一个信任数值。在留出的验证集上跑该来源的轨迹并记录任务成功的频率；该来源的信任先验 $w_{g}$ 就是这个平均成功率。最终每个来源得到一个数（例如：human demonstrations、模型蒸馏 rollout、自生成搜索 rollout、模拟回合各一个）。\n   - _为什么_: 通常更容易成功的来源，在冲突中判断谁对时应当占更大权重。\n3. 训练一个小的可靠性预测器。它是一个 2 层神经网络(隐藏维度 512)，输入为冻结的状态向量 h(s) 与一个标识来源的可学习 32 维嵌入 $e_{g}$，经 sigmoid 输出一个 [0,1] 的数：在情境 s 跟随来源 g 成功的可能性。用标准二元交叉熵(binary cross-entropy)对该来源实际访问过的每个情境的成功/失败进行训练。由于来源身份是共享状态空间上的一个嵌入，预测器能对任意「情境-来源」组合给出可靠性 $\\rho (s,g)$，即使是从未见过的组合——因此信任是按情境度量，而非全局只测一次。\n   - _为什么_: 信任不是恒定的——一个来源在某类情境好、在另一类差——所以可靠性必须按情境测量，而不是全局测一次。\n4. 对每个情境分组，计算一个冲突分数，衡量按信任加权的各来源在「单一最佳动作」上有多不一致。先让动作可比较：把每个 tool call 转成规范化的(工具名, 排序后的参数)形式并精确比较，对自由文本动作则比较其状态向量嵌入是否高度相似(余弦相似度高于一个「动作相同」程度，默认 0.95)。对每个来源取其出现最频繁的规范化动作。分数 = 1 减去「支持最受拥护动作的来源」的信任加权占比：各来源一致时接近 0，冲突时接近 1。把该分数附到该组每条交互上。\n\n*每个状态的跨源冲突分数 D(s) $\\in $ [0,1]：用 1 减去各源在最受支持动作上的可靠性加权一致度，其中 $a_{g}*(s)$ 是源 g 在状态 s 处的众数动作，$w_{g}$ 是源 g 的可靠性先验。各源越分歧，D(s) 越高。*\n$$ D(s) = 1 - \\max_{a} \\sum_{g \\in G} w_g \\, \\mathbf{1}[a_g^{*}(s) = a] \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这一个数就是整个方法的信号：它精确定位各来源在哪里发生争执。\n\n### 来源条件化梯度分层\n*把冲突与可靠性合成每条交互的梯度缩放系数 $\\beta $，并用分层损失微调。*\n\n5. 把可靠性和冲突合成每条交互的缩放系数 $\\beta (s,g)$：对「温度 $\\lambda $ 乘以(可靠性减冲突)」取 logistic 函数。$\\lambda $ 的选法是在对数网格(如 0.5、1、2、4、8)上各试一遍，保留在留出冲突情境上、用一次快速试训得到最佳成功率的那个值。不要在组内对 $\\beta $ 重新归一化：保持其绝对尺度，正是让高冲突组整体上比一致组更少地推动模型的关键。这里留给你一个真正的设计选择。 【作者需决定：把冲突与可靠性这些量在训练前一次性算好作为固定调度，还是在训练过程中随模型变化而重新计算——这会影响后面的误差界检验(固定调度 vs 估计与优化相互耦合的移动目标)。】\n\n*每个交互的梯度缩放系数 $\\beta (s,g)$：对温度 $\\lambda $ 乘以「源 g 的状态条件可靠性 $\\rho (s,g)$ 与冲突分数 D(s) 之差」取 logistic $\\sigma $。在一致状态（D 低）各源都保留接近满额的 $\\beta $；在冲突状态（D 高）只有局部最可靠的源保留较大 $\\beta $。*\n$$ \\beta(s,g) = \\sigma\\!\\big(\\lambda\\,(\\rho(s,g) - D(s))\\big) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: $\\beta $ 是决定每条交互推动模型多用力的旋钮——只在有争议情境里调低不可靠来源。\n6. 用缩放后的损失微调智能体：某情境的单个 $\\beta (s,g)$ 作用于该交互的所有动作 token，在梯度步之前乘以它们的交叉熵，而观测/提示 token 像常规智能体微调一样不计入损失。于是低 $\\beta $ 的冲突交互传播成比例更弱的梯度，训练出的策略在该情境上偏向高 $\\beta ($更可靠)的来源。可通过在留出冲突情境上解码微调后的模型来验证。\n\n*分层微调损失：每个交互的逐 token 交叉熵 CE(a|s) 在反向传播前乘以其梯度缩放系数 $\\beta (s,g)$，因此低 $\\beta $ 的冲突交互只传播成比例缩小的梯度。*\n$$ \\mathcal{L} = \\sum_{(s,a,g)} \\beta(s,g)\\,\\mathrm{CE}(a \\mid s) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 缩放梯度（而非删除数据）能在某来源出错处压低它，同时让它在别处仍有贡献。\n\n### 隔离混淆的验证\n*用匹配诊断集、基线对比、偏差界检验与状态条件性消融，证明冲突状态上的增益来自来源正确的分层。*\n\n7. 从分组里构造两个匹配的测试集：冲突情境(冲突分数最高的四分之一)和一致情境(最低的四分之一)；跳过中间一半，使两组差异分明。让二者可比：抽取相等数量的交互，并匹配难度——按「原始(未微调)模型已能成功的频率」给情境分箱，从每个难度箱里等量采样——同时保持训练算力相等。这样两组之间唯一系统性差异就是冲突程度。\n   - _为什么_: 除冲突程度外其他都匹配，才能把任何提升专门归因于「处理了分歧」，而非更多数据或算力。\n8. 在两个测试集上测量三个训练模型的下游智能体任务成功率：统一训练(每条交互等权)、最佳单一来源训练、以及分层损失。你需要决定哪个是「最佳」单一来源。 【作者需决定：以全局最佳来源(验证集信任 $w_{g}$ 最高、单独用它训练)作为公平基线——若按情境逐个挑最佳来源，会暗中用到方法本应自行发现的冲突信号；可另外报告一个「按情境的 oracle 上界」，但须明确标注为 oracle。】 这是正面对决，检验在冲突情境上池化是否真的低于「只用最佳来源」，以及分层是否同时击败二者。\n   - _为什么_: 这是正面对决，看分层是否能同时击败标准池化做法和「干脆只用最好来源」这一简单退路。\n9. 检验预测的误差界。把目标策略定义为「在每个冲突情境上、采用局部最可靠来源动作」所训练出的策略。对每个训练模型，用 total-variation 距离(两个概率分布之间标准的 0 到 1 距离)测量其下一动作分布在留出冲突情境上离该目标有多远。确认分层模型的差距保持在预测上限之下(1 减去各源可靠性最大值，在集合上取平均)，而统一池化模型的差距与「信任加权分歧量」相符。差距吻合预测界，正说明方法是因所述原因而生效。\n\n*冲突状态上的偏差界：分层估计量的偏差至多为 1 减去状态 s 处各源可靠性的最大值，因此只要存在某个可靠的源该偏差就趋于零——而池化估计量则有不可消除的、等于可靠性加权分歧的偏差。*\n$$ \\mathrm{bias}_{\\mathrm{strat}}(s) \\;\\leq\\; 1 - \\max_{g} \\rho(s,g) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 验证预测的误差界，能把「它有效」升级为「它因所述原因而有效」。\n10. 做一个消融，去掉缩放中「逐情境」的部分，检查冲突优势是否消失。用两种方式：(a)把 $\\beta $ 换成对所有交互的单一平均值(这等同于普通统一训练，至多差一个学习率);(b)把 $\\beta $ 换成每个来源一个冻结的平均值(这就是普通的按来源重加权)。冲突情境上的优势应当只在完整的逐情境 $\\beta $ 下出现，并在两种冻结版本下都消失——从而证明收益来自按情境调整，而非一般意义上的按来源或按样本重加权。\n   - _为什么_: 若去掉逐情境缩放后增益仍在，那贡献其实与冲突无关——这一步证明它确实来自冲突处理。\n\n"},{"id":"07","run_dir":"run_prompt07_featureupsample","index":7,"title":"Metric-Preserving Feature Upsampling via Per-Token Whitened Reassembly","title_zh":"基于逐 token 白化重组的度量保持特征上采样","method_name":"Per-Token Whitened Reassembly (PTWR)","hook":"Every universal feature upsampler reassembles high-resolution features with a neighbor-similarity computed in the raw inner product, silently treating the encoder's feature space as Euclidean; we substitute that primitive with a per-token covariance-whitened (Mahalanobis) similarity, so the upsampled field preserves the source encoder's representational metric by construction rather than by reconstruction loss.","anchor_pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","anchor_pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","domain_category":"Vision Representation & Perception","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces an upsampling operator whose mixing weights are a function of the SPECIFIC local geometry of the feature field being upsampled (the local channel covariance / anisotropy / curvature at that token), rather than a globally-fixed learned form (AnyUp) or a single per-image elliptical kernel (Upsample Anything) — so wherever a region's true local structure departs from the operator's fixed prior, the high-resolution features are mis-mixed and detail at semantic boundaries i","pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","sub_pattern":"C14 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by physically replacing the upsampler's similarity primitive: the dense local neighbor-reassembly interaction (the operator LDA-AQU showed all upsamplers reduce to) keeps its structure but its raw inner-product similarity is swapped for a per-token Mahalanobis similarity whitened by the local feature covariance estimated from the token's spatial neighborhood, so the mixing weights become a function of the field's own local anisotropy — the preserved property is the encoder's representational metric, in the spirit of C14's cheaper/altered primitive that provably retains the operator's load-bearing property.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf controls, as an explicit objective or constraint, whether the upsampled high-resolution feature field PRESERVES the source encoder's representational geometry (the inner-product / nearest-neighbor / distance structure that frozen linear probes, open-vocabulary matching, and retrieval read off) — all leaves optimize a reconstruction- or task-style target, leaving metric drift between low-res and upsampled features uncontrolled and unmeasured.","pattern_id":"targeted_self_supervised_objective","pattern_name":"Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective","sub_pattern":"C17 (Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by re-engineering the pairing geometry of the upsampler's training objective: instead of a reconstruction loss, positives are cross-resolution pairs (a low-res token and the average of its corresponding high-res output tokens) and the alignment target is the SOURCE encoder's inner-product structure, so the only representation that minimizes the loss is one whose upsampled distance structure matches the source encoder's metric — the C17 move of replacing a generic similarity target with a property-sensitive one (here the encoder's whitened metric) writes metric-preservation directly into the operator's parameters.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"universal feature upsampling for pre-trained vision-encoder features (DINO/CLIP/SigLIP/MAE) used in dense prediction","n_papers":39,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":27},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":23,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A Refreshed Similarity-based Upsampler for Direct High-Ratio Feature Upsampling"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A deep learning framework based on U-shaped networks with multi-scale feature perception and attention for retinal vessel segmentation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Densely Decoded Networks with Adaptive Deep Supervision for Medical Image Segmentation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"LDA-AQU: Adaptive Query-guided Upsampling via Local Deformable Attention"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"PU-SDF: Arbitrary-Scale Uniformly Upsampling Point Clouds via Signed Distance Functions"},{"source":"openalex","title":"CSWin-UNet: Transformer UNet with cross-shaped windows for medical image segmentation"}],"more":17},{"year":2025,"n":17,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Eliminating Semantic Ambiguity in Human Pose Estimation via Stable Feature Upsampling"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Deep learning phase unwrapping method based on convolutional block upsampling network"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A lightweight coal-gangue detection model based on parallel deep residual networks"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Spatial-frequency domain aggregation upsampling for pan-sharpening"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"MSA: Mamba Semantic Alignment Networks for Remote Sensing Change Detection"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A study on flame reconstruction in a supersonic combustor using deep learning"}],"more":11}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":24,"share":0.615},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":8,"share":0.205},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":5,"share":0.128},{"pattern_id":"algebraic_equivalence_unification","pattern_name":"Prove Equivalence to Unify","count":3,"share":0.077},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":3,"share":0.077},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":3,"share":0.077},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":2,"share":0.051},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":2,"share":0.051}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Pre-trained ViT encoders emit features at a 14x/16x-downsampled token grid, so dense tasks require upsampling deep feature maps to pixel resolution; the recent 'universal' upsamplers attack the retraining-per-encoder cost of the FeatUp-style learned upsamplers but do so by fixing the upsampling operator's functional form ONCE and applying it identically to every feature type and image. AnyUp (openalex:W4415272805) trains a single feature-agnostic feed-forward operator that is invariant to the input encoder at inference time, and Upsample Anything (openalex:W4416550525) optimizes one low-parameter anisotropic Gaussian (range+spatial) kernel per image; in both, the operator's effective receptive field and its mixing weights do not depend on the actual local geometry of the specific feature field being upsampled (how the encoder's channels co-vary, how fast the feature manifold curves at that location, or how anisotropic the local feature similarity is). Consequently, when the source feature field's local structure deviates from the operator's fixed prior — high-frequency semantic boundaries, encoder-specific channel statistics (DINO vs CLIP vs MAE differ markedly), or regions where the downstream-relevant signal lies along directions the fixed kernel averages away — the upsampled high-resolution features are over-smoothed and their inner-product / nearest-neighbor geometry drifts from the source encoder's, which is exactly the geometry that frozen linear probes, open-vocabulary matching, and retrieval read off. ReSFU (semanticscholar:8f078d6bb2d42df0aa97f8cea81ff1a87deae181) and LDA-AQU (semanticscholar:1b7ba2e586fea0c5a5ea78d518dc745a297a5006) make the similarity/attention form more flexible but still learn it per-architecture and optimize a reconstruction objective that says nothing about preserving the source metric.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415272805","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"AnyUp is the first learnable upsampler that, after a single training run, generalizes to any vision-encoder feature at any resolution at inference time by making the operator feature-agnostic (it conditions on the low-res feature content but its learned mapping is fixed across encoders and images). Residue: because the operator's functional form and effective receptive field are frozen at training time, it cannot adapt its mixing weights to the per-image / per-encoder local geometry of the feature field, and it is trained on a reconstruction-style objective that contains no explicit term forcing the upsampled features' inner-product / distance structure to match the source encoder's — so over-smoothing at semantic boundaries and metric drift (degraded linear-probe / retrieval geometry) remain uncontrolled. [residue grounded from intro Table 1 + method section via fulltext top-up]"},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416550525","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Upsample Anything performs per-image test-time optimization of a single anisotropic Gaussian kernel (spatial + range cues), training-free and edge-aware, bridging joint bilateral upsampling and Gaussian splatting. Residue: the kernel family is deliberately low-parameter (one anisotropic Gaussian) so it can represent only a single locally-elliptical smoothing prior — it cannot capture multi-modal or higher-rank local feature structure, carries no learned cross-image prior, and its bilateral range term is computed in raw feature space without any guarantee that the resulting high-res field preserves the encoder's representational metric."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:8f078d6bb2d42df0aa97f8cea81ff1a87deae181","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"ReSFU refreshes the similarity-based upsampling pipeline with controllable query-key alignment, a flexible (non-fixed-inner-product) similarity, and finer neighbor selection, yielding a more universal framework adaptable across architectures. Residue: it must still be trained per network structure and its objective optimizes reconstruction quality, not preservation of the source encoder's inner-product geometry; the similarity is made flexible but is not derived from any explicit metric-preservation constraint."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:1b7ba2e586fea0c5a5ea78d518dc745a297a5006","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"LDA-AQU casts upsampling as local-deformable-attention feature reassembly, showing many upsamplers are special cases of local self-attention and adding deformation to close the semantic gap between an upsampled point and its neighbors. Residue: the deformable-attention weights are learned per-architecture against a task/reconstruction loss; the method gives no account of the local feature-field geometry it is reassembling and no guarantee about preserving the encoder's distance structure across the upsample."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"universal feature upsampling for pre-trained vision-encoder features (DINO/CLIP/SigLIP/MAE) used in dense prediction","venue":"ICLR 2026 (representation learning)","time":"2026","data":["ImageNet-pretrained ViT feature extractors (DINOv2, CLIP, SigLIP, MAE)","dense-prediction benchmarks: ADE20K / Pascal VOC semantic segmentation, NYUv2 depth, COCO part/keypoint probes"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with cloud access; vision representation learning","preference":"both","baseline":"AnyUp (openalex:W4415272805), Upsample Anything (openalex:W4416550525), ReSFU (semanticscholar:8f078d6bb2d42df0aa97f8cea81ff1a87deae181), and the FeatUp/JAFAR/LoftUp learned-upsampler family referenced therein","limitation":"existing universal upsamplers either train one global feed-forward operator that is applied identically to every feature type (AnyUp) or run per-image test-time optimization of a low-parameter kernel (Upsample Anything); neither adapts the upsampling operator to the per-encoder/per-image spectral and metric structure of the feature field, and none guarantees that the upsampled high-resolution features preserve the source encoder's representational geometry (its inner-product / distance structure that downstream linear probes and retrieval depend on)","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The two gaps interlock as a sequential_pipeline named the metric-preserving reassembly pipeline: gap-1 builds the OPERATOR (a per-token whitened reassembly), gap-2 supplies the OBJECTIVE that trains it; the operator's output feeds the objective, and the objective's gradient shapes the operator's only learned part. Operator (gap 1, C14 substitution). Let p in R^{h x w x c} be the low-resolution feature map from a frozen encoder e (DINOv2/CLIP/SigLIP/MAE) and I the high-res guidance image. We adopt the established local-reassembly view (a high-res output token q_j is a softmax-weighted combination of a k x k neighborhood of low-res tokens {p_i}): q_j = sum_i w_{ji} p_i. Existing upsamplers set w_{ji} = softmax(<g_j, p_i>/tau) with a raw inner product (the primitive we substitute). We replace the inner product with a per-token Mahalanobis similarity s_{ji} = -(g_j - p_i)^T Sigma_j^{-1} (g_j - p_i), where Sigma_j is the local feature covariance estimated from the m x m spatial neighborhood of low-res tokens around the source location of j: Sigma_j = (1/|N_j|) sum_{i in N_j}(p_i - mu_j)(p_i - mu_j)^T + lambda I_c, mu_j the neighborhood mean, lambda = 1e-3 a fixed Tikhonov floor (all readouts are model-internal features of e; m=5, k=3, tau learned scalar). Because c is large, Sigma_j is computed in a r-dim PCA subspace fitted per image (r=64), so Sigma_j^{-1} is an r x r inverse, O(h w r^2) total — the substitution's cheapness comes from the low-rank whitening, not from dropping neighbors (no element is discarded). The query g_j is a learned 1x1 projection of the bilinearly-pre-upsampled p, shared across all encoders (the only learned weights, ~0.07M params), which is what makes the operator feature-agnostic: nothing in the operator is encoder-specific except the data-derived Sigma_j. Preserved property (the C14 load-bearing proof): when Sigma_j equals the true local second moment of the encoder's feature distribution, the whitened similarity equals the encoder's own metric up to local linearization, so neighbor weights are computed in the encoder's geometry and a linear probe trained on low-res features reads the upsampled features through the same inner product it was trained on. Objective (gap 2, C17 pairing-geometry). Training is label-free: for each image form cross-resolution positive pairs by pooling the upsampled output q over each low-res cell back to (h,w) and requiring the pooled field to match p under the source encoder's metric (a whitened-cosine alignment loss L_align = 1 - cos_Sigma(pool(q), p)), plus a high-res self-consistency term that pulls neighboring output tokens whose guidance pixels are intra-segment together and pushes cross-edge tokens apart, with positives/negatives mined from the guidance image's color/edge affinity (no semantic labels). The decisive C17 substitution is that the alignment similarity cos_Sigma is the encoder-whitened inner product, not raw cosine, so minimizing L_align is minimizable ONLY by an operator that preserves the source metric — a reconstruction loss (raw L2) leaves the metric uncontrolled. The named pipeline object both legs read/write is the per-token covariance Sigma_j: the operator consumes it to set weights, the objective measures alignment under it.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules: I judged that a geometry-conditioned operator with a reconstruction loss would still drift in metric (the operator could over-smooth and L2 would not see it), and a metric-preservation loss on a fixed-inner-product operator could not represent anisotropic neighbor weighting — only the pair closes both, with Sigma_j as the single shared object, so it is one paper not two. (b) Alternatives rejected: (i) predicting per-location kernels from low-res content via a learned head — rejected as a regression to method_lineage node n2 (CARAFE/SAPA/DySample content-aware reassembly); (ii) a single per-image anisotropic Gaussian (Upsample Anything, node n7) — rejected because one global ellipse cannot express per-token covariance; (iii) making the whole operator a per-encoder learned MLP (FeatUp-style) — rejected because it loses feature-agnosticism. Conditioning on the data-derived local covariance is a source the lineage tree does not occupy (neither content-prediction nor single-Gaussian fit estimates a per-token second-moment operator).","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: take frozen DINOv2 and CLIP encoders, upsample their features 16x on ADE20K and NYUv2 with a single trained metric-preserving operator, and feed the upsampled features to frozen linear probes (semantic segmentation, depth) trained on the low-res features; measure mIoU / depth RMSE and, as the mechanism variable, the metric-drift D = expected absolute difference between cos_Sigma(low-res neighbor pairs) and cos_Sigma(their upsampled counterparts). If the candidate works, boundary-region mIoU rises over AnyUp and Upsample Anything and metric-drift D decreases relative to a raw-inner-product upsampler of identical architecture. The named load-bearing variable is the per-token whitening Sigma_j^{-1}: the negative control replaces every Sigma_j^{-1} with the identity (isotropic similarity, i.e. the raw-inner-product upsampler) while holding the operator, parameter count, training data, and tau fixed; the prediction is that this control drives the DOWNSTREAM probe mIoU back toward the existing similarity-upsampler baseline (not merely that D rises) — if isotropic similarity matches whitened similarity on the task metric, the encoder geometry was not the mechanism. A positive control trains only the whitening branch (fixed identity query g = bilinear p, no learned projection) and should already recover most of the boundary-mIoU gain, identifying the covariance whitening rather than the learned query as the driver.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415272805","delta":"AnyUp trains one feature-agnostic feed-forward operator whose mixing is computed from a fixed learned form applied identically to every feature field; we construct a per-token Mahalanobis-whitened reassembly whose weights are a function of the data-derived local feature covariance Sigma_j and prove that, at the true second moment, the operator computes neighbor weights in the source encoder's own metric — a preserved-metric property AnyUp's construction does not produce or measure."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416550525","delta":"Upsample Anything optimizes a single anisotropic Gaussian (one local ellipse) per image at test time; we estimate a distinct anisotropic covariance per token and, unlike their raw-feature range term, whiten the similarity by Sigma_j^{-1} so the operator preserves the encoder's inner-product geometry rather than only an edge-aware smoothing prior."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:8f078d6bb2d42df0aa97f8cea81ff1a87deae181","delta":"ReSFU makes the query-key similarity flexible but learns it per network structure against a reconstruction objective; we replace the inner product with an encoder-covariance-whitened similarity and supervise with a metric-preservation objective whose unique minimizer matches the source encoder's distance structure, a constraint ReSFU's objective never imposes."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:1b7ba2e586fea0c5a5ea78d518dc745a297a5006","delta":"LDA-AQU shows upsamplers are local self-attention and adds deformation to the sampling positions; we keep the local-attention structure but substitute the similarity metric itself with a per-token whitened form and add no geometry account beyond position, deriving the metric-preservation guarantee LDA-AQU does not state."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4415272805","what_step_was_missed":"AnyUp made the operator feature-agnostic by conditioning on low-res feature content with a fixed learned mapping, but it never constructed the per-token local second-moment (covariance) of the feature field and never used it to whiten the neighbor-similarity primitive; without that constructed covariance object the operator's similarity is computed in a raw Euclidean geometry that does not match the encoder's, so the metric-preservation property our operator guarantees could not exist in AnyUp even though it shares the feature-agnostic goal."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":234,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"No hard floor fired (gap_closure_reject_check has no candidate_match: yes; anti_pattern matched null; the paper_pointed_threat openalex:W7163287734 is adjacent, not exact-mechanism overlap). recipe_application_check is 'applied' on both legs, so the mechanism is sharp. The one actionable finding is the addressable paper_pointed_threat: a 2026 whitened-inner-product paper overlaps the generic primitive, and addressable_via names a specific field — so revise to add a differentiation_from_lit entry that distinguishes the per-token spatial covariance construction from generic whitened inner products, plus carry the C14 borderline (keep the preserved-metric proof tethered to the downstream probe consequence) into that same field.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces an upsampling operator whose mixing weights are a function of the SPECIFIC local geometry of the feature field being upsampled (the local channel covariance / anisotropy / curvature at that token), rather than a globally-fixed learned form (AnyUp) or a single per-image elliptical kernel (Upsample Anything) — so wherever a region's true local structure departs from the operator's fixed prior, the high-resolution features are mis-mixed and detail at semantic boundaries is lost.","main_pattern":"architectural_operator_substitution","sub_pattern":"C14 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail when the surrogate is offered as a cheaper-but-equivalent reparameterization with no load-bearing consequence — the preservation argument absent, trivially true, or never connected to a capability the original operator lacked — or when the operator swap co-varies with a confound (positional encoding, added parameters, multi-scale features) and no controlled ablation isolates the substitution.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"If a confound (positional encoding, extra capacity, added multi-scale features) co-varies with your operator swap, the headline conclusion becomes unattributable and reviewers reject it as opportunistic.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The negative control in falsification_prediction holds operator, parameter count, training data, and tau fixed and only replaces Sigma_j^{-1} with identity, so the whitening is isolated from confounds."},{"lesson_quoted":"Comparing your cheaper operator only against the expensive original — never against the existing family of cheaper alternatives — makes it read as a redundant reparameterization rather than an advance.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"differentiation_from_lit and falsification benchmark against the existing universal-upsampler family (AnyUp, Upsample Anything, ReSFU, LDA-AQU), not just an inner-product baseline."},{"lesson_quoted":"An equivalence or approximation proof with no downstream consequence is dismissed as formalizing what the field already assumed to be true.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The preserved-metric property must be tied to a downstream consequence (linear-probe/retrieval geometry); the candidate does connect it to probe mIoU, but the strength of the 'matches the encoder metric up to local linearization' claim needs the downstream linkage kept explicit, which falsification_prediction supplies."},{"lesson_quoted":"Bolting together established cheaper components without a single unifying load-bearing insight invites the 'combination of existing modules / engineering report' rejection.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The load-bearing insight is one named primitive substitution (per-token covariance whitening of the similarity), not a bundle of modules."},{"lesson_quoted":"Failing to evaluate in the exact regime your substitution targets — long sequences, large scale, high representational order — leaves its core promise untested and the claim unverifiable.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The targeted regime (semantic boundaries / anisotropic feature regions at 16x upsampling) is exactly where boundary-region mIoU and metric-drift D are measured."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf controls, as an explicit objective or constraint, whether the upsampled high-resolution feature field PRESERVES the source encoder's representational geometry (the inner-product / nearest-neighbor / distance structure that frozen linear probes, open-vocabulary matching, and retrieval read off) — all leaves optimize a reconstruction- or task-style target, leaving metric drift between low-res and upsampled features uncontrolled and unmeasured.","main_pattern":"targeted_self_supervised_objective","sub_pattern":"C17 (Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring shape is sourcing the pairing/alignment signal by composing two already-published components and presenting the composition as the contribution, never re-deriving WHY this pairing geometry uniquely encodes the targeted property, with no operational definition, no direct probe, and no ablation isolating the new pairing component.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Concatenating a frozen off-the-shelf predictor's output as an extra input channel injects no novel insight — it reads as combining two published systems regardless of the accuracy gain.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"No off-the-shelf predictor is concatenated; the pairing signal is the encoder's own whitened metric, not a borrowed system."},{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a representation is 'disentangled' or property-specific without an operational definition, a direct probe, or an isolating ablation leaves the central claim ungrounded and unverifiable.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The targeted property (metric preservation) has an operational definition — metric-drift D — and a direct probe (frozen linear-probe mIoU under the preserved metric)."},{"lesson_quoted":"Following reconstruction pretraining with a stock nearest-neighbor contrastive pass reads as stacking existing techniques unless you show the new stage reorganizes signal that could not otherwise arise.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The objective is not reconstruction-then-contrastive; the decisive substitution is the whitened-cosine alignment target cos_Sigma, a single non-borrowed primitive."},{"lesson_quoted":"A hard-pair construction strategy that closely recombines existing mixup/contrastive recipes collapses to 'incremental' the moment the nearest pair-construction baselines are missing from the comparison.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Cross-resolution positives are novel to this setting and the comparison includes the raw-cosine alignment baseline (the nearest pair-construction)."},{"lesson_quoted":"Gains attributed to a new alignment component evaporate under scrutiny when the ablation suite never isolates that component from the borrowed backbone.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The negative control (identity whitening) and positive control (whitening-only branch) isolate the alignment metric from the operator's learned query."}],"verdict":"clear"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The anchor C14 entry is borderline on the lesson 'An equivalence or approximation proof with no downstream consequence is dismissed': the metric-preservation argument must stay tethered to the downstream probe consequence. The C17 entry is clear because the property is operationally defined (metric-drift D), directly probed, and isolated by negative/positive controls. No Reject lesson is marked candidate_match: yes, so no hard-floor trigger."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces an upsampling operator whose mixing weights are a function of the SPECIFIC local geometry of the feature field being upsampled ...","sub_pattern":"C14 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Replace a dense interaction operator with an altered/cheaper primitive while making the contribution the PROOF that the surrogate retains the operator's load-bearing property (expressive class, receptive field, retrieval capacity, order-preservation); a recurring move is recasting operator application in a second algebraic vocabulary that yields parameterizations impossible in the original framing.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism substitutes the upsampler's raw inner-product similarity primitive with a per-token Mahalanobis (covariance-whitened) similarity s_{ji} = -(g_j - p_i)^T Sigma_j^{-1}(g_j - p_i) inside the existing local-reassembly interaction, and the preserved property is explicitly named and argued (the upsampled field's inner-product geometry matches the source encoder's metric up to local linearization when Sigma_j is the true local second moment). This is the C14 signature move — alter the interaction's primitive, prove the preserved property — not the parent's generic 'use a better operator'.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf controls, as an explicit objective or constraint, whether the upsampled high-resolution feature field PRESERVES the source encoder's representational geometry ...","sub_pattern":"C17 (Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Re-engineer the PAIRING/ALIGNMENT geometry of a similarity/contrastive objective so the targeted structural property is the only thing whose encoding minimizes the loss; the decisive technical act is replacing or inverting a default geometric primitive — e.g. swapping the inner-product similarity for a property-sensitive one.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism replaces the default raw-cosine alignment target with an encoder-whitened similarity cos_Sigma between cross-resolution positive pairs (pooled high-res output vs low-res token), so the unique minimizer is an operator preserving the source metric. This is precisely the C17 Oral move 'replacing the default inner-product similarity with a property-sensitive measure', applied to upsampling — not a generic SSL loss.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries instantiate their cluster's distinctive move: C14 by substituting the similarity primitive with a covariance-whitened form and proving the preserved metric property; C17 by re-engineering the alignment geometry to a property-sensitive (whitened) similarity whose unique minimizer encodes metric-preservation."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["architectural_operator_substitution","targeted_self_supervised_objective"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"None of the three reject-favored compositions matches — all three require heterogeneous_decomposition as a component, which is absent from this candidate's composition_set."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"openalex:W7163287734","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"'Improving Relative Representations with Learned Anchors and Whitened Inner Products' (2026-05) already uses whitened inner products to align representations, which overlaps the candidate's central primitive (whitened similarity). It threatens the novelty of 'whitening the similarity' in the abstract. However it operates on global relative-representation alignment between models, not on a spatial feature-upsampling reassembly operator, and it does NOT construct a PER-TOKEN local covariance Sigma_j used as the mixing-weight geometry of an upsampler nor train an upsampling operator under a metric-preservation objective; so the candidate's claim stands as long as the contribution is framed as the per-token covariance-conditioned reassembly operator plus its metric-preservation objective, not 'whitened inner products' in general.","addressable_via":"Sharpen differentiation_from_lit / core_mechanism to foreground the per-token local covariance Sigma_j as the upsampling operator's mixing geometry (the spatial, per-token, upsampling-specific construction) rather than whitened inner products as a generic representation primitive."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat openalex:W7163287734 (whitened inner products for relative representations) overlaps the candidate's whitening primitive in the abstract.","fix_direction":"Append a differentiation_from_lit entry for openalex:W7163287734 stating substantively: that paper whitens a global inner product to align two models' relative representations and constructs no spatial operator; we construct a PER-TOKEN local covariance Sigma_j from each token's spatial neighborhood and use Sigma_j^{-1} as the mixing-weight geometry of a feature-UPSAMPLING reassembly operator trained to preserve the source encoder's metric — a per-token, spatial, upsampling-specific object their global-alignment construction does not produce."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Appended a differentiation_from_lit entry for openalex:W7163287734 distinguishing the per-token spatial covariance upsampling operator from generic global whitened inner products."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Metric-Preserving Feature Upsampling via Per-Token Whitened Reassembly\n\n**Method.** Per-Token Whitened Reassembly (PTWR)\n\n## Motivation\nModern image encoders like DINOv2, CLIP, SigLIP and MAE (all frozen, pre-trained vision transformers) describe a picture only on a coarse grid — about 14 or 16 times smaller than the original image. To do tasks that need a label at every pixel (segmenting objects, estimating depth, matching to text, image retrieval) you must upsample those coarse feature maps back to full resolution. The newest 'universal' upsamplers were built to avoid retraining a separate upsampler for every encoder: AnyUp (arXiv 2025-10) trains a single fixed operator that works on any encoder, and Upsample Anything (arXiv 2025-11) fits one simple smoothing ellipse per image. The hidden problem is that all of them decide which neighboring features to blend using a plain dot-product similarity, which silently assumes every encoder's feature space is a simple, evenly-stretched (Euclidean) space. It is not: different encoders stretch and correlate their feature channels very differently, and even within one image the local geometry varies. So the blended high-resolution features quietly drift away from the encoder's original distance structure — and that distance structure is exactly what a frozen probe, an open-vocabulary text matcher, or a retrieval index reads. Because all four recent methods appeared in the last year and a result from LDA-AQU (ACM Multimedia 2024-10) showed every upsampler is really a form of local attention, we can now swap out just the similarity rule. We replace the plain dot product with a per-token whitened (Mahalanobis) similarity — one that measures distance in the local feature geometry estimated from each token's own neighborhood — and we train it with a label-free objective that explicitly rewards keeping the encoder's distances intact. When the gap closes, one upsampler can sit in front of any frozen encoder and the probes trained on its coarse features keep working on the high-resolution features, with no per-encoder retraining; AnyUp and Upsample Anything become the special case where the geometry is assumed flat.\n\n## Method\n### Background: frozen-encoder feature extraction\n*Get the source low-res features and a cheap subspace to work in, without touching the encoder.*\n\n1. Run the frozen pre-trained encoder (DINOv2/CLIP/SigLIP/MAE) on the image and read out the patch tokens from its last transformer block. Discard the global CLS token and (for DINOv2) the register tokens, reshape the remaining tokens into a grid of shape h x w x c, and apply the encoder's built-in final layer normalization so the features match what the existing frozen probes expect. Do not change any encoder weights. This is the source representation whose distance structure we promise to preserve, so we start from it untouched.\n   - _Why_: This is the source representation whose distance structure we promise to preserve, so we start from it untouched.\n2. Build a per-image low-dimensional space with Principal Component Analysis (PCA): collect all $h\\cdot w$ token vectors of this image, subtract their average, and keep the top r=64 directions of variation as a 64-column basis. Project every token into this 64-dimensional space to get $p_{r}$ (shape h x w x 64), and save the average and the basis so results can be mapped back to the original c channels later. Working in a 64-dimensional subspace makes the later per-location matrix inverse cheap without throwing away any neighbor.\n   - _Why_: Working in a 64-dim subspace makes the later per-token matrix inverse cheap without throwing away any neighbor.\n\n### Per-token whitened reassembly operator\n*Condition the neighbor-mixing weights on each token's own local covariance so the upsampled field preserves the encoder's geometry.*\n\n3. At each low-res location, look at the 5 x 5 block of subspace features around it (reflect-pad at the image edges so the block is always full, i.e. 25 vectors), take their average, and build the local covariance matrix $\\Sigma _{j}$ — the 64 x 64 matrix that records how the features vary and co-vary right there. Add a tiny floor $\\lambda =1e-3$ on the diagonal so the matrix is always invertible, then invert it to get $\\Sigma _{j}^{-1}.$ This matrix is computed from data, not learned. $\\Sigma _{j}$ captures how the feature field is locally stretched and correlated right at that token, which is the per-token geometry no prior method built.\n\n*Per-token local feature covariance $\\Sigma _{j}$ is the regularized second moment of the $m\\times m$ neighborhood of low-res tokens around token j (computed in the r=64 PCA subspace), with a fixed Tikhonov floor $\\lambda =1e-3$ keeping it invertible.*\n$$ \\Sigma_j = \\frac{1}{|N_j|}\\sum_{i\\in N_j}(p_i-\\mu_j)(p_i-\\mu_j)^\\top + \\lambda I_r,\\quad \\mu_j=\\frac{1}{|N_j|}\\sum_{i\\in N_j}p_i \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: $\\Sigma _{j}$ captures how the feature field is locally stretched and correlated right at that token, which is the per-token geometry no prior method built.\n4. First bilinearly upsample $p_{r}$ from the coarse h x w grid up to the full target resolution H x W. Then pass it through one learnable 1 x 1 convolution (64 inputs, 64 outputs, no bias, started as the identity so it begins as a no-op), the same convolution for every encoder, to get the query field $g_{j}.$ This 1 x 1 projection (about 0.07 million weights) plus a single temperature value are the only things that get trained. Keeping the only learned part tiny and encoder-shared is what lets one operator serve any encoder at inference.\n   - _Why_: Keeping the only learned part tiny and encoder-shared is what lets one operator serve any encoder at inference.\n5. For each high-resolution token, find where it falls in the coarse grid and take the 3 x 3 block of coarse neighbors around the nearest coarse cell; use that cell's covariance $\\Sigma _{j}$ to measure distance. Score each neighbor with the whitened distance $s_{ji} = -(g_{j} - p_{i})^{T} \\Sigma _{j}^{-1} (g_{j} - p_{i})$ — a distance measured in the local feature geometry rather than a plain dot product — turn the 9 scores into weights with a learnable temperature $\\tau $ (started at 1.0), blend the neighbors into the output token $q_{j},$ and map q back to the original c channels using the saved basis. Setting $\\Sigma _{j}^{-1}$ to the identity matrix gives back the plain dot-product upsampler. Measuring neighbor similarity in the local whitened geometry is the core swap that keeps the encoder's distances intact.\n\n*The substituted primitive: neighbor similarity $s_{ji}$ is a per-token Mahalanobis (covariance-whitened) distance, softmaxed with learned temperature $\\tau $ into mixing weights $w_{ji}$ that reassemble the high-res token $q_{j}$; replacing $\\Sigma _{j}^{-1}$ with the identity recovers the raw-inner-product upsampler.*\n$$ s_{ji} = -(g_j-p_i)^\\top \\Sigma_j^{-1}(g_j-p_i),\\qquad w_{ji}=\\frac{\\exp(s_{ji}/\\tau)}{\\sum_{i'}\\exp(s_{ji'}/\\tau)},\\qquad q_j=\\sum_i w_{ji}\\,p_i \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Measuring neighbor similarity in the local whitened geometry is the core swap that keeps the encoder's distances intact.\n\n### Metric-preservation training objective\n*Train the tiny operator with a label-free loss whose unique minimizer keeps the source encoder's distances intact.*\n\n6. Pool the high-res output q back down to the coarse grid by averaging within each coarse cell. Then measure how well it agrees with the original coarse features using the encoder-whitened cosine $cos_\\Sigma $ (the cosine taken after rescaling vectors by the local geometry, not the plain cosine), and minimize $L_{align} = 1 - cos_\\Sigma (pool(q),$ p). Add an edge-aware self-consistency term $L_{consist}$ that pushes two high-res tokens to be similar when their guidance-image colors are similar, where 'similar colors' is controlled by a bandwidth $\\sigma _{c}.$ 【author decision: the guidance-color bandwidth $\\sigma _{c}$ — how close two guidance pixels' colors must be to be treated as the same surface — is a free choice trading edge sharpness against smoothing.】 Combine them as total $= L_{align} + 0.5 \\cdot  L_{consist},$ and send gradients only to the 1 x 1 projection and $\\tau .$ Scoring agreement in the whitened metric means the only way to minimize the loss is to preserve the encoder's distances — a plain L2 loss could not pin that down.\n\n*The metric-preservation objective: $L_{align}$ drives the pooled high-res field to match the low-res tokens under the encoder-whitened cosine $cos_\\Sigma $ (not raw cosine), so its unique minimizer preserves the source metric; $L_{consist}$ adds guidance-image edge-aware self-consistency, weighted by $\\beta =0.5.$*\n$$ \\mathcal{L} = \\underbrace{\\big(1-\\cos_{\\Sigma}(\\mathrm{pool}(q),\\,p)\\big)}_{\\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{align}}} + \\beta\\,\\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{consist}},\\qquad \\beta=0.5 \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Scoring agreement in the whitened metric means the only way to minimize the loss is to preserve the encoder's distances — a plain L2 loss could not pin that down.\n7. Do a single training run with no labels over a mix of about 4 encoders and ImageNet-scale unlabeled images. For each step, pick one image and one of the encoders at random, run steps step 1 (Run the frozen pre-trained encoder)-step 6 (Pool the high-res output $q back\\dots )$ to get the loss, and update only the shared 1 x 1 projection and the temperature $\\tau $ using the AdamW optimizer (learning rate 1e-3, no weight decay); the per-location covariance is recomputed for each image and is never trained. 【author decision: when to stop — a fixed number of steps versus stopping when the alignment loss flattens on held-out data — is left to the authors, trading training length against generalization.】 A single cheap run yields one operator that works on any encoder, which is the whole point of a universal upsampler.\n   - _Why_: A single cheap run yields one operator that works on any encoder, which is the whole point of a universal upsampler.\n\n### Inference and metric-drift evaluation\n*Run on unseen encoders with no retraining and directly measure whether the encoder metric was preserved.*\n\n8. On a new encoder the operator has never seen, run steps step 1 (Run the frozen pre-trained encoder)-step 5 (For each high-resolution token) without any retraining to produce the high-res features q. Feed q to frozen probes — semantic segmentation on ADE20K (report mIoU), depth on NYUv2 (report RMSE) — and to a nearest-neighbor retrieval index, using the released frozen linear probes for that encoder, or, if none exist, one linear head trained once on the coarse features and reused unchanged for both the baseline and our features. Also measure the metric-drift D: the average absolute gap between the whitened cosine of coarse neighbor pairs and the whitened cosine of the same pairs after upsampling, over a fixed sample of pairs. This checks the promise directly: if distances are preserved, probes trained on coarse features keep working on the upsampled ones.\n   - _Why_: This checks the promise directly: if distances are preserved, probes trained on coarse features keep working on the upsampled ones.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 基于逐 token 白化重组的度量保持特征上采样\n\n**方法名称.** Per-Token Whitened Reassembly (PTWR)\n\n## 研究动机\n现代图像编码器（如 DINOv2、CLIP、SigLIP、MAE，都是冻结的预训练 vision transformer）只在一个粗网格上描述图像——大约比原图小 14 到 16 倍。要完成需要逐像素标签的任务（分割物体、估计深度、与文本匹配、图像检索），就必须把这些粗特征图上采样回全分辨率。最新的「通用」上采样器是为了避免给每个编码器单独重训一个上采样器：AnyUp（arXiv 2025-10）训练一个对任意编码器都适用的固定算子，Upsample Anything（arXiv 2025-11）则为每张图拟合一个简单的平滑椭圆。隐藏的问题是：它们都用普通的点积相似度来决定混合哪些邻居特征，这等于默默假设每个编码器的特征空间是一个均匀拉伸的（Euclidean）空间。事实并非如此：不同编码器对特征通道的拉伸和相关性差别很大，即便在同一张图内局部几何也在变化。于是混合出的高分辨率特征会悄悄偏离编码器原本的距离结构——而这个距离结构恰恰是冻结 probe、开放词表文本匹配器或检索索引所读取的。由于这四个近期方法都出现在过去一年内，且 LDA-AQU（ACM Multimedia 2024-10）证明了每个上采样器本质上都是一种局部注意力，我们现在可以只替换其中的相似度规则。我们用逐 token 的白化（Mahalanobis）相似度替换普通点积——它在从每个 token 自身邻域估计出的局部特征几何中度量距离——并用一个无标签目标显式奖励保持编码器距离不变来训练它。当这一空白被填补，一个上采样器就能放在任意冻结编码器前面，在其粗特征上训练的 probe 无需重训即可继续在高分辨率特征上工作；AnyUp 与 Upsample Anything 则成为「假设几何是平的」那个特例。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景：冻结编码器特征提取\n*在不改动编码器的前提下，取得源低分辨率特征和一个便宜的工作子空间。*\n\n1. 在图像上运行冻结的预训练编码器（DINOv2/CLIP/SigLIP/MAE），读取它最后一个 transformer 块的 patch token。丢掉全局 CLS token 以及（对 DINOv2）register token，把剩下的 token 重排成形状为 h x w x c 的网格，并施加编码器自带的最后一层 LayerNorm，使特征与现有冻结 probe 所期望的一致。不要改动任何编码器权重。这是我们承诺要保持其距离结构的源表示，所以从它原封不动地出发。\n   - _为什么_: 这是我们承诺要保持其距离结构的源表示，所以从它原封不动地出发。\n2. 用主成分分析(Principal Component Analysis, PCA)为这张图建立一个低维空间：收集这张图的全部 $h\\cdot w$ 个 token 向量，减去它们的均值，保留方差最大的前 r=64 个方向作为一个 64 列的基。把每个 token 投影进这个 64 维空间得到 $p_{r}$（形状 h x w x 64），并保存均值和基，以便稍后把结果映射回原始 c 个通道。在 64 维子空间中工作能让后续的逐位置矩阵求逆变便宜，同时不丢弃任何邻居。\n   - _为什么_: 在 64 维子空间中工作能让后续的逐 token 矩阵求逆变便宜，同时不丢弃任何邻居。\n\n### 逐 token 白化重组算子\n*让邻居混合权重以每个 token 自身的局部协方差为条件，使上采样特征场保持编码器几何。*\n\n3. 在每个低分辨率位置，查看它周围 5 x 5 块的子空间特征（在图像边缘用反射填充，使该块始终是满的，即 25 个向量），取它们的均值，并构建局部协方差矩阵 $\\Sigma _{j}——$这个 64 x 64 矩阵记录了特征就在该处如何变化与相互关联。在对角线上加一个很小的下限 $\\lambda =1e-3$，使矩阵始终可逆，再求逆得到 $\\Sigma _{j}^{-1}$。这个矩阵由数据算出，不是学习得到的。$\\Sigma _{j}$ 刻画了特征场就在该 token 处如何被局部拉伸和相关，这正是以往方法没有构建的逐 token 几何。\n\n*逐 token 的局部特征协方差 $\\Sigma _{j}$ 是 token j 周围 $m\\times m$ 邻域低分辨率 token 的正则化二阶矩（在 r=64 的 PCA 子空间内计算），加上固定的 Tikhonov 下限 $\\lambda =1e-3$ 以保证可逆。*\n$$ \\Sigma_j = \\frac{1}{|N_j|}\\sum_{i\\in N_j}(p_i-\\mu_j)(p_i-\\mu_j)^\\top + \\lambda I_r,\\quad \\mu_j=\\frac{1}{|N_j|}\\sum_{i\\in N_j}p_i \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: $\\Sigma _{j}$ 刻画了特征场就在该 token 处如何被局部拉伸和相关，这正是以往方法没有构建的逐 token 几何。\n4. 先把 $p_{r}$ 从粗网格 h x w 双线性上采样到完整的目标分辨率 H x W。然后让它通过一个可学习的 1 x 1 卷积（64 输入、64 输出、无偏置，初始化为单位映射，因此一开始相当于不做任何改变），对每个编码器都用同一个卷积，得到查询场 $g_{j}$。这个 1 x 1 投影（约 0.07 百万权重）加上一个温度数值，就是仅有的需要训练的部分。让唯一可学习的部分保持很小且编码器共享，才能让一个算子在推理时服务任意编码器。\n   - _为什么_: 让唯一可学习的部分保持很小且编码器共享，才能让一个算子在推理时服务任意编码器。\n5. 对每个高分辨率 token，找到它落在粗网格中的位置，取最近粗格周围 3 x 3 块的粗邻居；用该格的协方差 $\\Sigma _{j}$ 来度量距离。用白化距离 $s_{ji} = -(g_{j} - p_{i})^{T} \\Sigma _{j}^{-1} (g_{j} - p_{i})$ 给每个邻居打分——这是在局部特征几何中度量的距离，而非普通点积——用可学习温度 $\\tau $（初始为 1.0）把这 9 个分数变成权重，把邻居混合成输出 token $q_{j}$，再用保存的基把 q 映射回原始 c 个通道。把 $\\Sigma _{j}^{-1}$ 设为单位矩阵即退回普通点积上采样器。在局部白化几何中度量邻居相似度，是保持编码器距离不变的核心替换。\n\n*被替换的基本运算：邻居相似度 $s_{ji}$ 是逐 token 的 Mahalanobis（协方差白化）距离，经可学习温度 $\\tau $ 的 softmax 得到混合权重 $w_{ji}$，重组出高分辨率 token $q_{j}$；把 $\\Sigma _{j}^{-1}$ 换成单位矩阵即退化为原始内积上采样器。*\n$$ s_{ji} = -(g_j-p_i)^\\top \\Sigma_j^{-1}(g_j-p_i),\\qquad w_{ji}=\\frac{\\exp(s_{ji}/\\tau)}{\\sum_{i'}\\exp(s_{ji'}/\\tau)},\\qquad q_j=\\sum_i w_{ji}\\,p_i \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 在局部白化几何中度量邻居相似度，是保持编码器距离不变的核心替换。\n\n### 度量保持训练目标\n*用一个唯一极小值能保持源编码器距离的无标签损失来训练这个微小算子。*\n\n6. 把高分辨率输出 q 按每个粗格内取平均池化回粗网格。然后用编码器白化余弦 $cos_\\Sigma $（即先按局部几何对向量重新缩放后再取余弦，而不是普通余弦）衡量它与原始粗特征的吻合程度，最小化 $L_{align} = 1 - cos_\\Sigma (pool(q),$ p)。再加上一个边缘感知自一致项 $L_{consist}$：当两个高分辨率 token 在引导图像上的颜色相近时，促使它们的特征也相近，其中「颜色相近」由带宽 $\\sigma _{c}$ 控制。【作者需决定：引导颜色带宽 $\\sigma _{c}——$两个引导像素颜色要多接近才算同一表面——是一个自由选择，在边缘锐利与平滑之间权衡。】把它们组合为总损失 $= L_{align} + 0.5 \\cdot  L_{consist}$，梯度只回传到 1 x 1 投影和 $\\tau $。在白化度量下评估一致性，意味着最小化损失的唯一办法就是保持编码器距离——普通 L2 损失无法约束到这一点。\n\n*度量保持目标：$L_{align}$ 在编码器白化余弦 $cos_\\Sigma $（而非原始余弦）下，将池化后的高分辨率特征场对齐到低分辨率 token，使其唯一极小值保持源度量；$L_{consist}$ 加入引导图像的边缘感知自一致项，权重 $\\beta =0.5$。*\n$$ \\mathcal{L} = \\underbrace{\\big(1-\\cos_{\\Sigma}(\\mathrm{pool}(q),\\,p)\\big)}_{\\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{align}}} + \\beta\\,\\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{consist}},\\qquad \\beta=0.5 \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 在白化度量下评估一致性，意味着最小化损失的唯一办法就是保持编码器距离——普通 L2 损失无法约束到这一点。\n7. 在约 4 个编码器与 ImageNet 规模无标签图像的混合上做一次无标签训练。每一步随机取一张图和其中一个编码器，运行 第1步（在图像上运行冻结的预训练编码$\\dots $）-第6步（把高分辨率输出 $q\\dots $） 得到损失，只用 AdamW 优化器（学习率 1e-3，无权重衰减）更新共享的 1 x 1 投影和温度 $\\tau $；逐位置协方差对每张图重新计算，从不参与训练。【作者需决定：何时停止——固定步数，还是在留出数据上对齐损失趋平时停止——留给作者，在训练时长与泛化之间权衡。】一次廉价的训练就得到一个对任意编码器都适用的算子，这正是通用上采样器的意义所在。\n   - _为什么_: 一次廉价的训练就得到一个对任意编码器都适用的算子，这正是通用上采样器的意义所在。\n\n### 推理与度量漂移评估\n*在未见编码器上无需重训地运行，并直接测量编码器度量是否被保持。*\n\n8. 在算子从未见过的新编码器上，无需任何重训地运行 第1步（在图像上运行冻结的预训练编码$\\dots $）-第5步（对每个高分辨率 token） 得到高分辨率特征 q。把 q 喂给冻结 probe——ADE20K 语义分割（报告 mIoU）、NYUv2 深度（报告 RMSE）——以及一个最近邻检索索引；使用该编码器随附发布的冻结线性 probe，若没有，则在粗特征上训练一个线性头一次，并对基线和我们的特征都原样复用。同时测量度量漂移 D：在固定采样的 token 对上，粗邻居对的白化余弦与上采样后同一对的白化余弦之间的平均绝对差。这直接验证承诺：若距离被保持，在粗特征上训练的 probe 就能继续在上采样特征上工作。\n   - _为什么_: 这直接验证承诺：若距离被保持，在粗特征上训练的 probe 就能继续在上采样特征上工作。\n\n"},{"id":"08","run_dir":"run_prompt08_astabench","index":8,"title":"Counterfactual Attribution: A Validity Instrument for Scientific-Agent Benchmarks","title_zh":"反事实归因：科学智能体基准的效度测量工具","method_name":"Counterfactual Attribution Instrument (CAI)","hook":"We show that a scientific-agent benchmark's headline score can be split, by matched per-step counterfactual perturbations, into a competence-carried fraction and a confound-carried fraction — and that for several published benchmarks a large share of the score survives when the agent's actual reasoning is neutralized, revealing the number was never measuring what it claimed.","anchor_pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","anchor_pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","domain_category":"LLM Evaluation & Benchmarking","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved evaluator certifies, for a given scientific-workflow benchmark score, HOW MUCH of the number is carried by genuine research competence versus by admitted confounds (memorization, environment-knowledge leakage, tool-execution luck) — the score is reported with its validity assumed rather than measured, so a reader cannot read off a competence-attribution quantity from any current agent-evaluation result.","pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by constructing matched counterfactual instance-pairs that neutralize exactly one confound channel per pair while holding the task fixed, and reporting the divergence between apparent score and de-confounded score (the confound-carried fraction kappa) as the headline result — a controlled-diagnostic instrument, not a new benchmark.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved process-evaluator establishes that movement in its named process dimension actually tracks a real change in agent competence rather than a change in trajectory surface-style; the dimensions (TRACE's efficiency/hallucination/adaptivity, GEMMAS's diversity, BoxingGym's EIG) are reported as competence proxies but their proxy-to-competence link is never tested, so a benchmark can be gamed by style with no competence change and nothing flags it.","pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by treating each existing process dimension as the hypothesized driver and intervening on it directly (a style-only counterfactual that perturbs the dimension while holding the de-confounded outcome fixed), then measuring whether the outcome moves — an out-of-sample causal/predictive validity check that certifies or rejects the proxy.","is_anchor":false},{"gap":"Every retrieved leaf silently inherits the assumption — from the shared answer-match ancestor — that the read-out unit of agent capability is a SINGLE aggregate number per task (final outcome, or one scalar per process dimension); no retrieved paper tests whether capability must be read off as one task-level scalar at all, rather than as a distribution of per-step competence that the aggregate may be averaging away.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","how_closed":"Framing half (C01): relocate the read-out locus from the task-level aggregate scalar to the per-step trajectory, treating the workflow step as the unit at which competence-versus-confound is resolvable. Companion deliverable (controlled_diagnostic_design): ship the confound-isolating empirical separation showing the per-step attribution recovers competence signal that the aggregate provably averages away (two agents with equal aggregate score split into different per-step kappa profiles).","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"evaluation methodology for LLM agents on scientific research workflows","n_papers":40,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":26},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":4,"papers":[{"source":"openalex","title":"LAB-Bench: Measuring Capabilities of Language Models for Biology Research"},{"source":"openalex","title":"ScienceAgentBench: Toward Rigorous Assessment of Language Agents for Data-Driven Scientific Discovery"},{"source":"openalex","title":"From Generalist to Specialist: A Survey of Large Language Models for Chemistry"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Autonomous Microscopy Experiments through Large Language Model Agents"}],"more":0},{"year":2025,"n":35,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"AInsteinBench: Benchmarking Coding Agents on Scientific Repositories"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Breakpoint: Scalable evaluation of system-level reasoning in LLM code agents"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Benchmarking AI scientists in omics data-driven biological research"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"DrugPilot: LLM-based Parameterized Reasoning Agent for Drug Discovery"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"BoxingGym: Benchmarking Progress in Automated Experimental Design and Model Discovery"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"CSR-Bench: Benchmarking LLM Agents in Deployment of Computer Science Research Repositories"}],"more":29},{"year":2026,"n":1,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"}],"more":0}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":26,"share":0.65},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":8,"share":0.2},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":3,"share":0.075},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":2,"share":0.05},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":2,"share":0.05},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":2,"share":0.05},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":2,"share":0.05},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":2,"share":0.05}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Across the retrieved scientific-agent benchmarks the score that is reported is dominated by the terminal outcome of the workflow — did the final law/answer/repair/analysis match ground truth — so two agents that reach the same outcome are certified as equally competent even when one followed a sound experimental-design-and-revision process and the other arrived by memorization or a lucky shortcut: NewtonBench (semanticscholar:a470fe954d20558ca25288e5621c6a92cffdd808) scores final-law correctness and tries to suppress one confound (memorization) via counterfactual law shifts but does not separate the discovery process from the answer, and BoxingGym (semanticscholar:ec39536fce9018baf447c7ffcce69ee7fe201fe1) computes an Expected-Information-Gain signal over experiment design yet still collapses experimental-design quality and model-discovery quality into a single prediction-error number. The recent process-aware evaluators move the read-out onto the trajectory — TRACE (openalex:W4416370358) scores efficiency/hallucination/adaptivity from an evidence bank and GEMMAS (openalex:W4415310486) scores collaboration structure from an interaction DAG — but each new dimension is defined by the authors' intuition and is never shown to causally track the property it names: there is no measurement instrument that certifies, for a given scientific-workflow benchmark, that a movement in its process score corresponds to a real change in research competence rather than to a stylistic or estimator artifact. The failure is therefore that the field has no way to tell, for any agent-evaluation number, how much of it is carried by genuine workflow competence versus by confounds the instrument silently admits.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416370358","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"TRACE evaluates a tool-augmented agent's whole ReAct trajectory along three hand-named dimensions (efficiency, hallucination, adaptivity) using an LLM judge over a structured evidence bank, reference-free so it avoids the cost of annotating one ground-truth trajectory. Its method never establishes that these three dimensions are the competence-bearing ones nor that the evidence-bank LLM judge is calibrated: the scores are reported as-is, so a benchmark could move an agent's TRACE score by changing surface trajectory style with no change in scientific-workflow competence, and TRACE supplies no test that would catch this — the validity of the process measurement itself is assumed, not demonstrated."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:ec39536fce9018baf447c7ffcce69ee7fe201fe1","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"BoxingGym formalizes scientific-agent evaluation as Bayesian optimal experimental design and scores experiment-design informativeness with a nested-Monte-Carlo Expected-Information-Gain estimator plus a novice-prediction-error model-discovery score. The two scores are reported as separate numbers but the framework never isolates whether a higher EIG actually causes better downstream model discovery for an LLM agent, nor whether the prediction-error score is confounded by the agent's prior knowledge of the simulated environment — so the design and discovery legs remain entangled and their validity as competence measures is untested."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:a470fe954d20558ca25288e5621c6a92cffdd808","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"NewtonBench builds 324 law-discovery tasks and uses counterfactual law shifts to make the benchmark memorization-resistant and difficulty-tunable while keeping scientific relevance. It controls exactly one confound (memorization) on the final-law-correctness score and leaves the rest entangled: the score still cannot say whether a correct law came from genuine interactive exploration or from the assisting equations leaking the answer, because the interactive discovery process is never scored or attributed separately from the terminal law match."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415310486","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"GEMMAS models a multi-agent system's interactions as a directed acyclic graph and proposes process-level metrics (Information Diversity Score, etc.) to capture collaboration quality beyond final-output correctness. The metrics are defined structurally and reported, but the paper never validates that a higher Information-Diversity score predicts a more competent scientific outcome, so the process metric is a plausible proxy with no demonstrated link to the competence it is meant to measure."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"evaluation methodology for LLM agents on scientific research workflows","venue":"ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML (top ML)","time":"2026","data":["existing agent benchmarks with logged trajectories (e.g. ScienceAgentBench, BoxingGym, NewtonBench tasks)","agent reasoning/tool-call trajectories","small human-expert annotation pool for validation"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with agent-evaluation focus; access to API LLMs","preference":"both","baseline":"outcome/answer-match scoring + heuristic process metrics (TRACE, GEMMAS, BoxingGym EIG)","limitation":"current agent benchmarks score the final scientific outcome (or report unvalidated heuristic process metrics), so a high score cannot be attributed to genuine research competence vs. confound (memorization, tool-execution luck, lucky guessing), and no measurement instrument certifies that a process metric actually tracks competence","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared evaluation framework is a Counterfactual Attribution Instrument (CAI) that operates on a logged agent trajectory T=(s_1,...,s_n) for a benchmark task, where each step s_t is the tuple (thought, action, action_input, observation) already produced by ReAct-style agents (the same trajectory object TRACE consumes). The central object is, per benchmark, a Confound-Carried Fraction kappa in [0,1]: the share of the benchmark's outcome score that is reproduced by counterfactual trajectories in which the agent's genuine step-level reasoning has been neutralized but admitted confounds are left intact. kappa is computed as kappa = (S_neutralized - S_floor) / (S_apparent - S_floor), where S_apparent is the benchmark's normal outcome score (a number in [0,1], e.g. fraction of NewtonBench laws correctly recovered), S_floor is the score of a no-information control agent (random/empty trajectory) on the same tasks, and S_neutralized is the score when each step's thought-and-action is replaced by a confound-preserving counterfactual (defined below); all three are computed with the benchmark's own unchanged scorer so the instrument never introduces a new judge (this is the regression-avoidance choice: we do NOT add an LLM-judge dimension, node n1, nor a new aggregate, node n0). A confound channel c is one of a small typed set the benchmark admits: {memorization (the answer is derivable from pretraining), environment_leakage (assisting context/simulator reveals the target, e.g. NewtonBench's assisting equations or BoxingGym's simulator parameters), tool_luck (a tool call returns the answer regardless of the reasoning that issued it)}. For gap 1 (anchor), for each channel c we build a matched counterfactual trajectory T^c that holds the task and the channel-c information fixed but replaces every reasoning step with a channel-only surrogate — e.g. for memorization, an agent that emits the final answer directly from the prompt with no exploration; for environment_leakage, an agent whose only action is to read the leaked context and copy; for tool_luck, an agent that issues the minimal tool call and returns its output — then S_neutralized^c = scorer(T^c) and kappa^c is the per-channel fraction; the headline kappa = max_c kappa^c (the dominant admitted confound), reported as apparent-versus-de-confounded divergence exactly in the C02 tactical pattern. For gap 2, each existing process dimension d (TRACE efficiency, GEMMAS information-diversity, BoxingGym EIG) is validated by a style-only counterfactual T^d that perturbs the trajectory to move d (e.g. inflate diversity by adding redundant-but-distinct tool calls, or shorten to raise efficiency) while leaving the de-confounded answer-producing substructure fixed; the proxy-validity coefficient rho_d = correlation(delta d, delta S_competence) across tasks, where S_competence = S_apparent - kappa*(S_apparent - S_floor) is the competence-carried score; rho_d near 0 certifies the dimension is style not competence. For gap 3, the C01 relocation supplies the per-step object: instead of one task scalar we compute a per-step competence increment g_t = S_competence(prefix up to t) - S_competence(prefix up to t-1) by re-scoring truncated-then-completed trajectories with the same scorer, yielding a per-step competence distribution {g_t}; the companion controlled_diagnostic_design separation is the demonstration that two agents with equal S_apparent have different {g_t} profiles and different kappa, which the aggregate destroyed. All three legs read from and write to the single shared object kappa and its per-step decomposition g_t, so the instrument is one coordinated measurement framework, not three modules.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The three gaps share machinery because all three are facets of one quantity — gap 1 asks how big the confound-carried fraction kappa is, gap 2 asks whether an existing process dimension correlates with the competence-carried complement, and gap 3 asks at what granularity kappa is resolvable; the evidence they share an object is that gap 3's per-step g_t is literally the differential of gap 1's S_competence, and gap 2's rho_d is defined against the same S_competence, so building separate modules would re-derive the same scorer calls three times. (b) Alternatives considered and rejected: (i) training a learned competence classifier over trajectories — rejected because it reintroduces an uncalibrated judge (regression to node n1, the LLM-as-judge ancestor) and would itself need the validity certificate we are trying to provide; (ii) defining kappa via an information-theoretic mutual-information term between trajectory and answer — rejected because it is not computable from the text without a density model and would not be auditable per the core_mechanism computability rule. The avoided regression node is n1 (LLM-as-judge / heuristic process scalar): CAI reuses the benchmark's OWN scorer on counterfactual trajectories rather than scoring trajectories with a new model, so it draws on the causal-intervention source (collateral node c1) the lineage tree did not yet occupy.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: take NewtonBench and ScienceAgentBench, run 3-4 base LLM agents to get trajectories and native scores, then run the channel-only counterfactual agents and the benchmark's own scorer to compute kappa. If the candidate works, the confound-carried fraction kappa is substantially above zero on at least one benchmark (predicted direction: kappa for environment_leakage on NewtonBench is large because the assisting equations expose the target), so the de-confounded competence score S_competence drops materially below the apparent score, and on the expert-annotated subset (1 - kappa) rises monotonically with expert-judged genuine-reasoning rate (Spearman rho positive and significant). The named load-bearing variable is S_neutralized (the score of the confound-only counterfactual trajectory through the unchanged scorer) — kappa is built from it. Negative-control intervention: replace the channel-only surrogate with a surrogate that ALSO destroys the confound information (e.g. blank out the leaked assisting equations before the copy step) — this should drive S_neutralized down toward S_floor and therefore drive the DOWNSTREAM OUTCOME (the benchmark competence ranking of agents under CAI) back to the agents' apparent ranking, because with no confound left the only thing producing score is genuine reasoning. If neutralizing the confound channel does NOT move S_neutralized (and hence the CAI-adjusted ranking) toward the floor, then kappa was not capturing confound-carried score and the mechanism is falsified. Positive control: a stripped agent that uses ONLY the dominant confound channel (no reasoning) should recover most of S_neutralized, confirming the channel is the operative variable.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416370358","delta":"TRACE scores three hand-named trajectory dimensions with an LLM judge and reports them as-is; we do not score the trajectory with any judge — we re-run the benchmark's own scorer on confound-only counterfactual trajectories and derive kappa, a measured competence-versus-confound decomposition TRACE never produces, and we use TRACE's dimensions as objects to VALIDATE (rho_d) rather than as outputs."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:a470fe954d20558ca25288e5621c6a92cffdd808","delta":"NewtonBench neutralizes one confound (memorization) by construction via counterfactual law shifts and still reports final-law correctness; we leave the benchmark's tasks untouched and instead MEASURE, post hoc, the residual confound-carried fraction of its score (e.g. from assisting-equation leakage) that its construction does not eliminate, yielding a number NewtonBench does not compute."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:ec39536fce9018baf447c7ffcce69ee7fe201fe1","delta":"BoxingGym reports a Bayesian EIG design score and a separate prediction-error discovery score; we do not propose a new score but test whether EIG is a valid competence proxy (rho_EIG against the de-confounded competence score) and decompose the discovery score into competence- versus environment-leakage-carried parts, which BoxingGym leaves entangled."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415310486","delta":"GEMMAS defines process metrics over an interaction DAG and asserts they capture collaboration quality; we supply the missing validity test by perturbing each GEMMAS metric in a style-only counterfactual and measuring whether de-confounded competence moves with it, certifying or rejecting the proxy."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4416370358","what_step_was_missed":"TRACE constructs a reference-free trajectory evaluator that maps a trajectory to scores along three dimensions, but it never constructs the counterfactual-trajectory family (the channel-only surrogate trajectories run through the benchmark's OWN unchanged scorer) that would let it measure how much of a benchmark's outcome score is reproducible without genuine reasoning; without that construction TRACE cannot produce the confound-carried fraction kappa or certify that its own three dimensions track competence rather than style."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":308,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"Hard floor did not fire: gap_closure_reject_check is borderline (no entry triggered), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat (TRACE) is a competing-not-subsuming threat whose subsumption_argument shows CAI computes quantities (kappa, rho_d) TRACE structurally cannot. recipe_application_check.verdict = applied for all three entries, so the C01/C02 signature moves are genuinely performed, not parent-gist. The remaining borderlines (small expert-validation subset; making the per-step competence-vs-heuristic-dimension distinction unmissable vs TRACE/GEMMAS) are non-load-bearing-to-the-core-argument and are best handled as Phase 4 reviewer_concerns_and_responses rather than a revise loop, so the verdict is advance.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved evaluator certifies, for a given scientific-workflow benchmark score, HOW MUCH of the number is carried by genuine research competence versus by admitted confounds (memorization, environment-knowledge leakage, tool-execution luck) — the score is reported with its validity assumed rather than measured, so a reader cannot read off a competence-attribution quantity from any current agent-evaluation result.","main_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail most often when the instrument isolates the confound only inside an artificial regime and never shows the isolated signal transfers to real deployment; a second shape is circularity — the diagnostic validated against the same population or definition it was built to interrogate; a third is the confirmatory benchmark that re-derives an already-documented limitation.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A diagnostic that only re-confirms a shortcut already known in advance, surfacing no previously unmeasurable failure, is read as confirmatory rather than as a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"kappa is a previously-uncomputed quantity (the confound-carried fraction of a benchmark's score); NewtonBench/BoxingGym never report it, so it surfaces a new measurement, not a re-confirmation."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a synthetic-ground-truth instrument only on synthetic data, without demonstrating that the controlled finding transfers to real-world instances, leaves ecological validity unestablished and undermines the central claim.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"the instrument operates on real published benchmarks (not synthetic), but the expert-validation subset is small (~100 tasks), so transfer of the kappa-to-competence link beyond that subset is a fair concern — surfaced for Phase 4."},{"lesson_quoted":"Building the instrument around one contested definition of the target property means it cannot independently confirm that the definition is correct, and reviewers flag the resulting circularity.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the oracle is the benchmark's OWN unchanged scorer plus an independent expert panel, not a self-asserted competence definition; the counterfactual construction supplies verifiability independent of the evaluand."},{"lesson_quoted":"Resting an unsupervised evaluation on the unverified premise that the systems under test can reliably judge one another stakes the entire method on an assumption that collapses under scrutiny.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"CAI explicitly does NOT use any LLM judge; it re-runs the benchmark scorer on counterfactual trajectories, avoiding self-judging."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pairing a single-task or small-sample instrument with broad capability claims triggers a scope-mismatch rejection, and assembling retrieval or engineering blocks without an isolating scientific insight reads as application rather than research.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the instrument is applied across multiple benchmarks (NewtonBench, ScienceAgentBench, BoxingGym) and the insight (counterfactual confound-only trajectories through the native scorer) is the isolating mechanism, not block-assembly."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved process-evaluator establishes that movement in its named process dimension actually tracks a real change in agent competence rather than a change in trajectory surface-style; the dimensions (TRACE's efficiency/hallucination/adaptivity, GEMMAS's diversity, BoxingGym's EIG) are reported as competence proxies but their proxy-to-competence link is never tested, so a benchmark can be gamed by style with no competence change and nothing flags it.","main_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failures are artificial-regime-only isolation, circular validation against the evaluand, and confirmatory re-derivation of an already-known limitation; self-check on whether the instrument surfaces a genuinely new gap with evaluand-independent ground truth.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A forced-choice contest between two cues measures relative salience, not load-bearing reliance; suppressing each candidate cue independently and measuring the resulting performance drop yields a confound-free dependence score.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"this is an Oral lesson the candidate actually follows — it suppresses each confound channel independently (per-channel kappa^c) rather than a forced contest."},{"lesson_quoted":"A diagnostic that only re-confirms a shortcut already known in advance, surfacing no previously unmeasurable failure, is read as confirmatory rather than as a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"rho_d (whether a process dimension causally tracks competence) is not previously measured for TRACE/GEMMAS/EIG; certifying or rejecting a proxy is a new finding."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a synthetic-ground-truth instrument only on synthetic data, without demonstrating that the controlled finding transfers to real-world instances, leaves ecological validity unestablished.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"the style-only counterfactual T^d is a constructed perturbation; whether it isolates 'style' without inadvertently changing competence substructure needs an explicit control — surfaced for Phase 4."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"Every retrieved leaf silently inherits the assumption — from the shared answer-match ancestor — that the read-out unit of agent capability is a SINGLE aggregate number per task (final outcome, or one scalar per process dimension); no retrieved paper tests whether capability must be read off as one task-level scalar at all, rather than as a distribution of per-step competence that the aggregate may be averaging away.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is a relocation demonstrated but not adversarially closed; a second is novelty-boundary collapse where the 'new' locus was already used by prior work; a third is reintroducing the assumption the relocation was meant to dissolve; a fourth is a demonstration with no mechanistic account of why the new locus carries the signal.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work — normalization statistics, activation-similarity losses, semantic concept triggers — collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"process-evaluators (TRACE, GEMMAS) already read the per-step trajectory, so 'per-step locus' is partly occupied; the candidate's distinction is that it reads COMPETENCE (de-confounded scorer increments g_t), not heuristic dimensions, which must be made explicit vs those papers — it is, in differentiation_from_lit, but this is the sharpest reviewer risk."},{"lesson_quoted":"Demonstrating the new locus only on fixed, non-adaptive or outdated baselines while omitting any account of why it works reads as a stacked pipeline of existing components rather than a principled shift.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism gives the mechanistic account — g_t is the differential of S_competence which is itself defined by the counterfactual construction — so the per-step locus is explained, not merely shown."},{"lesson_quoted":"A defense whose relocation silently depends on a clean reference model or a known anomaly distribution reintroduces precisely the strong assumption the move was supposed to eliminate.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the per-step decomposition depends only on the benchmark's own scorer and truncate-then-complete, not on a clean reference agent or a known competence distribution."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No entry triggered. The load-bearing borderline is the C01 audit entry's novelty-boundary lesson: TRACE/GEMMAS already operate at the per-step trajectory locus, so the relocation's novelty rests entirely on reading de-confounded competence increments g_t rather than heuristic dimensions — this distinction is present in differentiation_from_lit but must be made unmissable. The C02 ecological-validity borderlines (small expert subset; whether the style-only counterfactual truly fixes competence) are real but non-fatal and fold into Phase 4 reviewer concerns."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved evaluator certifies, for a given scientific-workflow benchmark score, HOW MUCH of the number is carried by genuine research competence versus by admitted confounds...","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Construct a controlled set of evaluation instances in which exactly one named confound is structurally blocked or independently varied, then report the divergence between apparent and de-confounded performance as the primary result, with a load-bearing oracle independent of the system under test.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism builds, per confound channel c, a matched counterfactual trajectory T^c that holds channel-c information fixed while neutralizing genuine reasoning, runs it through the benchmark's UNCHANGED scorer (oracle independent of the agent), and reports kappa = the divergence (S_apparent - S_neutralized) as the headline — this is exactly the C02 'block one named confound, report the apparent-vs-de-confounded gap' signature move.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved process-evaluator establishes that movement in its named process dimension actually tracks a real change in agent competence...","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Treat the scoring/measurement apparatus as an active independent variable; establish the diagnostic signal is causal/predictive by varying the hypothesized driver directly and showing it forecasts the true property out of sample.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism varies each process dimension d directly via a style-only counterfactual and measures rho_d = correlation(delta d, delta S_competence), i.e. it intervenes on the hypothesized driver and tests whether competence moves — the C02 step-5 causal/predictive-validity move.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"Every retrieved leaf silently inherits the assumption that the read-out unit of agent capability is a SINGLE aggregate number per task...","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Relocate the load-bearing signal to a representational locus the field treated as irrelevant/invariant, and supply a mechanistic account of why the new locus carries the signal — the unifying verbs are 'relocate the signal' and 're-anchor enforcement'.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism relocates the capability read-out from the task-level aggregate scalar to the per-step competence increment g_t (the differential of de-confounded S_competence), and accounts mechanistically for why g_t carries competence the aggregate averages away; the companion controlled_diagnostic_design ships the empirical separation (equal-aggregate agents, divergent g_t/kappa). This performs the C01 locus-relocation move, not the parent's generic 'audit an assumption' gist.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"All three entries instantiate their cited cluster's signature move: C02's confound-block-and-report-divergence is performed twice (kappa for outcome, rho_d for proxy validity), and C01's signal-relocation is performed by moving the read-out locus from task-aggregate to per-step de-confounded competence with a mechanistic account."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["controlled_diagnostic_design","controlled_diagnostic_design","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"The distinct main_pattern set is {controlled_diagnostic_design, assumption_audit_and_pivot}; none of the three anti-pattern compositions matches because all three require heterogeneous_decomposition, which is absent."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"openalex:W4416370358","threat_source":"lit_table","subsumption_argument":"TRACE is the closest competitor because it also reads the full agent trajectory reference-free to assess process quality, so a reviewer will ask whether CAI is just TRACE with extra dimensions. The candidate's claim stands because TRACE produces heuristic per-dimension scores via an LLM judge and never constructs the confound-only counterfactual-trajectory family run through the benchmark's own scorer, so TRACE cannot compute kappa (the confound-carried fraction of an outcome score) nor certify that its own dimensions track competence — exactly the quantities CAI delivers. TRACE therefore competes on surface (trajectory-level evaluation) but does not subsume the candidate's measured-validity contribution.","addressable_via":"Sharpen differentiation_from_lit[0] / hook to state up front that CAI introduces no new trajectory judge and instead re-uses the benchmark's native scorer on counterfactual trajectories — the property that structurally separates it from TRACE."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Counterfactual Attribution: A Validity Instrument for Scientific-Agent Benchmarks\n\n**Method.** Counterfactual Attribution Instrument (CAI)\n\n## Motivation\nBenchmarks that test AI agents on scientific-research workflows give each run a single score and treat that score as a measure of how good the agent is at research. The problem is that nobody checks whether the score actually measures research skill. Two agents can get the same score even if one genuinely reasoned through the problem and the other just memorized the answer, copied it from a hint that was left in the task, or got lucky when a tool happened to return the right thing. So a high score does not tell you how much real competence is behind it. Recent evaluators like TRACE (Trajectory-based Reasoning-Aware Competence Evaluation) and GEMMAS score the agent's step-by-step trajectory along hand-picked dimensions, but they never show those dimensions actually track competence — an agent could change its style and move the score without getting any smarter, and nothing would flag it. This matters now because the field has standardized the logged step-by-step trajectory (each step records the agent's thought, the action it took, its input, and what it observed) as a reusable object, and NewtonBench already showed you can make a score resist one confound (memorization) by building counterfactual versions of tasks. We take the next step: instead of suppressing one confound when building the benchmark, we MEASURE, after the fact, how much of any existing benchmark's score is carried by each confound. We do this by building 'counterfactual' agents that keep only the confound's information (for example, the leaked hint) but throw away genuine reasoning, then re-running the benchmark's OWN scoring on them. The fraction of the score these confound-only agents still earn is kappa, the confound-carried fraction. We never add a new judge. Once this exists, every existing benchmark gets a validity certificate: a reader can see how much of a number is genuine competence versus confound, leaderboards can be re-ranked on the de-confounded score, and the process dimensions other papers assert become testable instead of just claimed.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n\n1. Pick at least 4 agents built on different base large language models (LLMs) and of different strength levels (for example one top-tier model, one mid-size open model, one small open model, one reasoning-tuned model), so their scores spread out enough for the later step-by-step comparison. Run each agent on the target benchmark (start with NewtonBench, ScienceAgentBench, BoxingGym) and save, for every (agent, task) run, the full step-by-step trajectory — each step stored as a record holding the agent's thought, the action it chose, its $action_{input},$ and the observation it got back — as one JSON file per run. Also store the benchmark's own outcome score $S_{apparent}$ (a number from 0 to 1) in a flat table keyed by agent and task. You add no new scoring model; you reuse the trajectory the benchmark already produces.\n   - _Why_: You need the agent's actual trajectory and the benchmark's native score before you can take them apart — and re-using the existing trajectory means no new measuring apparatus is added.\n2. Measure the score you would get knowing nothing, called $S_{floor},$ for each task. Run two control agents and keep the higher score: (a) an empty agent that just submits the benchmark's 'no answer / abstain' option, and (b) a random agent that picks an answer uniformly at random from the task's allowed answers (a random law form for NewtonBench, a random valid output for classification-style tasks). Run the random one 20 times with different random seeds and average, so the floor is a stable chance level rather than a one-off fluke.\n   - _Why_: You need a chance-level baseline so the confound-carried fraction is measured against what's achievable with zero information, not against zero.\n\n### Confound-carried fraction (kappa)\n*Measure how much of a benchmark's score survives when reasoning is neutralized but one confound is left intact.*\n\n3. For each benchmark, decide which confounds it accidentally lets through, choosing from three: memorization (the answer can be recalled from public training data), $environment_{leakage}$ (the task's own context or simulator reveals the target — for example NewtonBench's assisting equations), and $tool_{luck}$ (a single tool call returns the answer no matter what reasoning asked for it). Use two annotators who independently mark each sampled task for which of the three is available, then reconcile, producing a channel set for the benchmark and a per-task mask of which channels apply. Deciding exactly when an answer counts as 'recallable from training data' is a judgment the authors must make. 【author decision: how broadly to treat memorization-availability — the cutoff for when a task's answer counts as recoverable from public training data.】\n   - _Why_: You can only measure a confound's contribution if you first name exactly which confounds the benchmark lets through.\n4. For each confound channel, build a stripped-down 'surrogate' agent that uses only that channel's information and does no real reasoning, then score it with the benchmark's unchanged scorer to get $S_{neutralized}$ for that channel. Concretely: the memorization surrogate asks the base LLM to answer the task immediately with no reasoning or tools and takes its first answer; the $environment_{leakage}$ surrogate is a small script whose only move is to read the leaked context (assisting equations or simulator parameters) and copy the answer it implies; the $tool_{luck}$ surrogate is a script that makes the single most useful allowed tool call and turns its raw output into the answer. Each surrogate produces its own final answer, the benchmark scorer scores it, and whatever score it still earns must come from the confound, not from competence.\n   - _Why_: This isolates one confound: whatever score the reasoning-free surrogate still earns must be coming from the confound, not from competence.\n5. For each channel, compute the confound-carried fraction $\\kappa _{c}$ shown in Eq. (1) — the share of the above-chance score that the reasoning-free surrogate still earns — and clip it to between 0 and 1. Report the headline $\\kappa $ as the largest channel's value together with which channel dominated. When averaging across tasks, only count tasks where the real agent scored clearly above the floor (by more than a small margin, 0.01); tasks at or below floor have no real signal to attribute and are reported separately as a below-floor count.\n\n*The per-channel confound-carried fraction $\\kappa _{c}$ is the share of the score-above-floor that survives when only channel c's information is kept and reasoning is neutralized; the headline $\\kappa $ is the dominant admitted channel.*\n$$ \\kappa^c = \\mathrm{clip}_{[0,1]}\\!\\left(\\frac{S_{\\mathrm{neutralized}}^{c} - S_{\\mathrm{floor}}}{S_{\\mathrm{apparent}} - S_{\\mathrm{floor}}}\\right), \\qquad \\kappa = \\max_{c}\\,\\kappa^{c} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: kappa is the share of the above-chance score that survives without reasoning — directly the confound-carried fraction the field never measured.\n\n### Per-step competence relocation\n*Read competence as a per-step distribution $g_{t}$ instead of one task scalar, and exhibit pairs the aggregate hid.*\n\n6. Define the competence-carried score (Eq. (2)) by subtracting the confound-carried slice from the apparent score, then read competence step by step (Eq. (3)). To do this, cut each real trajectory off at each step in turn; from each cut point, let the SAME base LLM that produced the trajectory finish the rest greedily (no randomness), re-score the finished result with the benchmark scorer, and take the step's competence gain as the difference between consecutive cut points. Keep the benchmark-level confound fraction $\\kappa $ fixed (computed once in the previous step, not recomputed for each cut). If the scorer has any randomness, average over 3 completion runs.\n\n*The competence-carried score strips the confound-carried slice $\\kappa \\cdot (S_{apparent} -  S_{floor})$ off the apparent score, leaving the part attributable to genuine reasoning.*\n$$ S_{\\mathrm{competence}} = S_{\\mathrm{apparent}} - \\kappa\\,(S_{\\mathrm{apparent}} - S_{\\mathrm{floor}}) \\tag{2} $$\n\n\n*The per-step competence increment $g_{t}$ is the change in de-confounded score from re-scoring the trajectory truncated at step t versus step $t- 1,$ yielding a distribution over steps rather than one task scalar.*\n$$ g_t = S_{\\mathrm{competence}}(\\le t) - S_{\\mathrm{competence}}(\\le t-1) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A single task score can hide where competence actually appeared; reading it per step recovers signal the average washes out.\n7. Show concrete cases where the single score hid a real difference. Group runs of the same task whose apparent scores fall in the same narrow band (width 0.05), then pick pairs in that band whose confound fraction $\\kappa $ differs by at least 0.2, and present the pairs with the biggest $\\kappa $ gap and the most different step-by-step competence profiles. Also report what fraction of same-band pairs diverge this way, as a measure of how much the single number was throwing away.\n   - _Why_: Two equal scores that decompose differently is the cleanest demonstration that the aggregate threw away information.\n\n### Process-dimension certification\n*Intervene on each existing process dimension and test whether de-confounded competence actually moves with it.*\n\n8. Test each existing process dimension d (TRACE's efficiency, hallucination, adaptivity; GEMMAS's diversity; BoxingGym's information-gain score) for whether it really tracks competence. Make edits that change only the trajectory's surface form to push d up or down — for example add redundant-but-distinct tool calls to raise diversity, or remove clearly unnecessary steps to raise efficiency — while guarding that the edited run gives the SAME final answer and SAME benchmark score as before (any edit that changes the answer is thrown out and redone). Then measure the rank-correlation (Eq. (4)) between how much d moved and how much the de-confounded competence moved; a value near 0 means d was only style. Deciding which edits count as 'surface-only' for each dimension is a judgment the authors must make, since some dimensions have no clearly style-only edit. 【author decision: which surface edits count as style-only for each process dimension, especially ones like adaptivity where no edit cleanly preserves substance.】\n\n*The proxy-validity coefficient $\\rho _{d}$ is the rank correlation across tasks between a style-only perturbation of process dimension d and the resulting change in competence-carried score; $\\rho _{d} \\approx  0$ means d is style, not competence.*\n$$ \\rho_d = \\mathrm{Spearman}\\big(\\Delta d,\\; \\Delta S_{\\mathrm{competence}}\\big) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: If pushing a dimension up or down doesn't move de-confounded competence, that dimension was never measuring competence — and now you can prove it.\n\n### Validity calibration and certificate\n*Tie the measurement to an independent expert panel and package a reusable per-benchmark validity certificate.*\n\n9. Check the measurement against human experts on about 100 tasks. Show each expert the task and the agent's full trajectory — but NOT the $\\kappa $ or per-step numbers, so their judgment stays independent — and have them give a 1-to-5 genuine-reasoning rating and a yes/no genuine-reasoning verdict; use at least 2 experts per item and report how well they agree (Krippendorff's alpha). Split the 100 tasks in half: use one half to fit any calibration curve and the other, untouched half to report how strongly (1 $-  \\kappa )$ and the per-step competence line up with the expert ratings, so the validity check is on data you did not tune on.\n   - _Why_: Tying the measurement to an independent expert panel (not the benchmark's own definition) shows kappa tracks real competence and isn't circular.\n10. Bundle everything into one validity certificate per benchmark — a JSON file holding the overall $\\kappa , \\kappa $ broken down by channel and which channel dominates, the table of process-dimension validity values $\\rho _{d},$ the matched-pair separation examples, and the calibration results (expert agreement, held-out correlation and its confidence interval). Then re-rank the leaderboard: average each agent's de-confounded competence score over the tasks, sort from high to low, and show both the original ranking and the de-confounded ranking side by side with how far each agent moved.\n   - _Why_: The deliverable is a reusable certificate for an existing benchmark, telling everyone how trustworthy its number is — not yet another benchmark.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 反事实归因：科学智能体基准的效度测量工具\n\n**方法名称.** Counterfactual Attribution Instrument (CAI)\n\n## 研究动机\n测试 AI 智能体在科学研究流程上的基准，会给每次运行打一个分数，并把这个分数当作智能体研究能力的衡量。问题在于：没人检验这个分数是否真的在衡量研究能力。两个智能体可能拿到相同分数，哪怕一个是真的推理解决了问题，另一个只是背下了答案、从任务里残留的提示中抄到了答案、或是某个工具恰好返回了正确结果而走运。所以高分并不能告诉你背后有多少真实能力。最近的评测工具如 TRACE 和 GEMMAS 会沿着人工挑选的维度对智能体逐步轨迹打分，但它们从未证明这些维度真的跟踪能力——智能体可以只改变风格就移动分数而毫无长进，却没有任何机制能察觉。现在做这件事正当其时：领域已经把记录逐步轨迹（每一步记录智能体的 thought、采取的 action、其 $action_{input}$，以及 observation）标准化为可复用对象，而 NewtonBench 已经证明可以通过构造任务的反事实版本使分数抵抗一种混淆（记忆）。我们更进一步：不在构造基准时压制某一种混淆，而是事后去测量任何现有基准的分数中有多少由各个混淆通道承载。做法是构造只保留混淆信息（例如泄露的提示）却抛弃真实推理的反事实智能体，再用基准自己的评分器重新评分。这些只靠混淆的智能体仍能拿到的分数比例就是 $\\kappa $（混淆承载比例）。我们从不引入新的评判器。一旦有了它，每个现有基准都获得一份效度证书：读者可以看到一个数字里有多少是真实能力、多少是混淆，排行榜可以按去混淆后的分数重排，其他论文只是断言的过程维度也变得可以检验，而不再只是声称。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景\n\n1. 选择至少 4 个基于不同 base large language model (LLM) 且强弱不同的智能体（例如一个顶级模型、一个中等规模 open 模型、一个小型 open 模型、一个 reasoning 微调模型），让它们的分数有足够差异以支撑后续逐步对比。在目标基准上（先从 NewtonBench、ScienceAgentBench、BoxingGym 开始）运行每个智能体，并为每次 (agent, task) 运行保存完整的逐步轨迹——每一步存为一条记录，包含智能体的 thought、所选的 action、其 $action_{input}$ 以及得到的 observation——每次运行存为一个 JSON 文件。同时把基准自带的结果分数 $S_{apparent}$（0 到 1 之间的数）存入一张以 agent 和 task 为键的扁平表。你不引入任何新的评分模型；只复用基准已经产生的轨迹。\n   - _为什么_: 在拆解之前，你需要先拿到智能体真实的轨迹和基准的原生分数——复用已有轨迹意味着不引入新的测量装置。\n2. 为每个任务测量在什么都不知道时能拿到的分数，称为 $S_{floor}$。运行两个对照智能体并取较高分：(a) 一个空智能体，只提交基准的'不作答/弃权'选项；(b) 一个随机智能体，从任务允许的答案中均匀随机选一个（NewtonBench 选随机的定律形式，分类型任务选随机的合法输出）。随机的那个用 20 个不同随机种子跑并取平均，使 floor 是稳定的随机水平而非一次性偶然结果。\n   - _为什么_: 需要一个随机水平的基线，使混淆承载比例是相对'零信息能拿到的分'来衡量，而不是相对绝对零分。\n\n### 混淆承载比例 (kappa)\n*测量当推理被中和、仅保留一条混淆时，基准分数还能保留多少。*\n\n3. 对每个基准，判断它无意中放进来了哪些混淆，从三类中选：memorization（答案可从公开训练数据中回忆出来）、$environment_{leakage}$（任务自身的上下文或 simulator 暴露了目标——例如 NewtonBench 的辅助方程）、$tool_{luck}$（某个工具调用无论由什么推理发出都会返回答案）。用两名标注者各自独立地为抽样任务标出这三类中哪些可用，再做一致化，得到该基准的通道集合以及每个任务适用哪些通道的掩码。'答案算不算可从训练数据回忆'的确切界线，需要作者自己拿主意。【作者需决定：memorization 可得性的宽严界线——任务答案在何种程度上算作可从公开训练数据中回忆出来。】\n   - _为什么_: 只有先明确点名基准放进来了哪些混淆，才能去测量某个混淆的贡献。\n4. 为每条混淆通道构造一个精简的'替身'智能体，只用该通道的信息、不做真实推理，再用基准未改动的评分器给它打分得到该通道的 $S_{neutralized}$。具体而言：memorization 替身让 base LLM 不做推理、不用工具地立即作答，取其第一个答案；$environment_{leakage}$ 替身是一个小脚本，唯一动作是读取泄露的上下文（辅助方程或 simulator 参数）并复制其暗示的答案；$tool_{luck}$ 替身是一个脚本，发出唯一一个最有用的允许工具调用，并把其原始输出转成答案格式。每个替身都产生自己的最终答案，由基准评分器评分，它仍能拿到的分数只可能来自混淆而非能力。\n   - _为什么_: 这样就隔离出单条混淆：无推理的替身仍能拿到的分数，只可能来自混淆而非能力。\n5. 对每条通道，计算公式 (1) 给出的混淆承载比例 $\\kappa _{c}——$即无推理替身仍能拿到的、高于随机水平那部分分数的占比——并裁剪到 0 与 1 之间。头条 $\\kappa $ 报为最大通道的值，并注明是哪条通道占主导。跨任务求平均时，只计入真实智能体明显高于 floor（高出一个小余量 0.01）的任务；处于或低于 floor 的任务没有可归因的真实信号，单独报为 below-floor 计数。\n\n*每条通道的混淆承载比例 $\\kappa _{c}$，是当仅保留通道 c 的信息、将真实推理中和后，仍高于 floor 的分数所占的比例；头条指标 $\\kappa $ 取最主要的混淆通道。*\n$$ \\kappa^c = \\mathrm{clip}_{[0,1]}\\!\\left(\\frac{S_{\\mathrm{neutralized}}^{c} - S_{\\mathrm{floor}}}{S_{\\mathrm{apparent}} - S_{\\mathrm{floor}}}\\right), \\qquad \\kappa = \\max_{c}\\,\\kappa^{c} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: kappa 是高于随机水平的分数中、不靠推理就能保留的比例——正是这个领域从未测量过的混淆承载比例。\n\n### 按步能力重定位\n*把能力读作按步分布 $g_{t}$ 而非单一任务标量，并展示聚合数字掩盖的配对。*\n\n6. 用公式 (2) 定义能力承载分数（从表观分数中扣除混淆承载部分），再按步读取能力（公式 (3)）。做法是：把每条真实轨迹依次在每一步处截断；从每个截断点开始，让产生该轨迹的同一个 base LLM 以贪心方式（无随机性）续完剩余部分，用基准评分器对续完结果重新评分，把该步的能力增量取为相邻截断点之间的差值。保持基准级混淆比例 $\\kappa $ 固定（在上一步算一次，不为每个截断点重算）。若评分器有随机性，则对 3 次续完取平均。\n\n*能力承载分数从表观分数中扣除混淆承载部分 $\\kappa \\cdot (S_{apparent} -  S_{floor})$，剩下的即可归因于真实推理的部分。*\n$$ S_{\\mathrm{competence}} = S_{\\mathrm{apparent}} - \\kappa\\,(S_{\\mathrm{apparent}} - S_{\\mathrm{floor}}) \\tag{2} $$\n\n\n*每步能力增量 $g_{t}$ 是将轨迹分别截断到第 t 步与第 $t- 1$ 步后重新评分得到的去混淆分数之差，从而给出按步分布而非单一任务标量。*\n$$ g_t = S_{\\mathrm{competence}}(\\le t) - S_{\\mathrm{competence}}(\\le t-1) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 单一任务分数会掩盖能力到底出现在哪里；按步读取能找回平均值冲掉的信号。\n7. 展示单一分数掩盖了真实差异的具体案例。把同一任务中表观分数落在同一窄带（宽 0.05）的运行分到一组，再在该带内挑出混淆比例 $\\kappa $ 相差至少 0.2 的配对，呈现 $\\kappa $ 差距最大、逐步能力分布差异最大的那些配对。同时报告同带配对中有多大比例这样分化，以衡量单一数字丢掉了多少信息。\n   - _为什么_: 两个相等的分数却分解得完全不同，是聚合数字丢掉了信息的最干净的演示。\n\n### 过程维度效度认证\n*对每个现有过程维度做干预，检验去混淆后的能力是否真的随之移动。*\n\n8. 检验每个现有过程维度 d（TRACE 的 efficiency、hallucination、adaptivity；GEMMAS 的 diversity；BoxingGym 的信息增益分数）是否真的跟踪能力。做只改变轨迹表面形式、用来抬高或压低 d 的编辑——例如加入冗余但不同的工具调用以提高 diversity，或删除明显多余的步骤以提高 efficiency——同时设置守卫：编辑后的运行必须给出与原来相同的最终答案和相同的基准分数（任何改变了答案的编辑都被丢弃重做）。然后测量 d 的变化量与去混淆能力的变化量之间的秩相关（公式 (4)）；接近 0 表示 d 只是风格。判断哪些编辑对每个维度算'仅表面'，是作者必须做的取舍，因为某些维度没有明确只改风格的编辑。【作者需决定：每个过程维度哪些表面编辑算作仅风格，尤其是像 adaptivity 这种没有干净的仅风格编辑的维度。】\n\n*代理效度系数 $\\rho _{d}$ 是在任务集合上，对过程维度 d 做仅风格扰动后，其变化量与能力承载分数变化量之间的秩相关；$\\rho _{d} \\approx  0$ 表示该维度是风格而非能力。*\n$$ \\rho_d = \\mathrm{Spearman}\\big(\\Delta d,\\; \\Delta S_{\\mathrm{competence}}\\big) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 如果把某个维度调高或调低都不会移动去混淆后的能力，那这个维度本就没在衡量能力——现在你能证明这一点。\n\n### 效度校准与证书\n*把测量绑定到独立专家小组，并打包出可复用的逐基准效度证书。*\n\n9. 在约 100 个任务上用人类专家检验这套测量。给每位专家看任务和智能体的完整轨迹——但不给 $\\kappa $ 或逐步数值，以保持判断独立——请他们给出 1 到 5 的真实推理评分以及是/否的真实推理判定；每个条目至少用 2 位专家，并报告他们的一致程度（Krippendorff's alpha）。把这 100 个任务对半分：一半用于拟合任何校准曲线，另一半完全不动，用来报告 (1 $-  \\kappa )$ 和逐步能力与专家评分的吻合程度（秩相关），使效度检验落在你没调过的数据上。\n   - _为什么_: 把测量绑定到独立的专家小组（而非基准自身的定义），可以证明 kappa 跟踪真实能力且不存在循环论证。\n10. 把所有结果打包成每个基准一份效度证书——一个 JSON 文件，包含整体 $\\kappa $、按通道拆分的 $\\kappa $ 及主导通道、过程维度效度值 $\\rho _{d}$ 的表、配对分离示例，以及校准结果（专家一致性、留出集相关及其置信区间）。然后对排行榜重排：把每个智能体在各任务上的去混淆能力分数取平均，从高到低排序，并把原始排名与去混淆排名并排展示，同时给出每个智能体移动了多少位。\n   - _为什么_: 交付物是针对现有基准的可复用证书，告诉所有人它的数字有多可信——而不是又一个新基准。\n\n"},{"id":"09","run_dir":"run_prompt09_autoep","index":9,"title":"Trust-Weighted LLM Control of Metaheuristic Parameters via Manufactured Reliability Signals","title_zh":"基于自制可靠性信号的可信度加权 LLM 元启发式参数控制","method_name":"Trust-Weighted LLM Control (TW-LLM-Control)","hook":"Current LLM-assisted metaheuristic tuners adopt the language model's parameter recommendation at fixed authority, so a confidently-wrong suggestion in a deceptive search phase moves the control parameter as forcefully as a correct one. We make the LLM emit a posterior over each control parameter and gate it with a trust weight manufactured at every step from the LLM's own answer dispersion and the optimizer's realized-improvement feedback, so the suggestion's influence rises and falls with evidence that it is currently reliable.","anchor_pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","anchor_pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","domain_category":"Optimization & Search","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a per-step trust score for an LLM's parameter recommendation that lets the metaheuristic's own measured search state modulate how much that recommendation moves the control parameter — every LLM-advisor leaf applies the suggestion at a fixed implicit weight, so a confidently-wrong suggestion in a deceptive/stagnation phase is unrecoverable within the loop.","pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by manufacturing a label-free per-step trust scalar from two internal readouts (the LLM's cross-sample answer dispersion and the optimizer's realized-improvement-vs-predicted residual), confining its action to a single tiny lever — the convex fusion weight on the parameter update — with an explicit stabilizer (a source-prior floor on the optimizer's own self-adaptive value) that prevents the trust signal from collapsing the parameter onto a degenerate LLM-dominated mode.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions whether the LLM should emit a concrete parameter VALUE at all rather than a softer object (a distribution, a prior, a constraint on the parameter) that the optimizer can then weigh against its own statistics — every advisor leaf silently inherits the assumption that the LLM's job is to output the operative parameter directly.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by pivoting the selection rule embedded in every advisor leaf — 'the LLM emits the operative parameter value' — and reframing the LLM's role from value-emission into posterior-emission (selection->posterior-sampling): the LLM returns a parametric distribution over each control parameter (a mean plus an explicit spread it must self-report), which is precisely the soft object the anchor's trust weight fuses against the optimizer's own self-adaptive estimate, so the pivoted assumption is consumed inside the same update object rather than left as a separate theoretical claim.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"LLM-assisted hyperparameter/parameter control for metaheuristic (evolutionary / swarm) optimization","n_papers":37,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":24},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":9,"papers":[{"source":"openalex","title":"The Ultimate Guide to Fine-Tuning LLMs from Basics to Breakthroughs: An Exhaustive Review of Technologies, Research, Best Practices, Applied Research Challenges and Opportunities"},{"source":"openalex","title":"AutoProteinEngine: A Large Language Model Driven Agent Framework for Multimodal AutoML in Protein Engineering"},{"source":"openalex","title":"An investigation on the use of Large Language Models for hyperparameter tuning in Evolutionary Algorithms"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Optimizing LLMs for Code Generation: Which Hyperparameter Settings Yield the Best Results?"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Adaptive Multi-Fidelity Hyperparameter Optimization in Large Language Models"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Large Language Models as Evolutionary Optimizers"}],"more":3},{"year":2025,"n":28,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Bayesian and Partition-Based Optimization for Hyperparameter Optimization of LLM Fine-Tuning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Large Language Model Enhanced Particle Swarm Optimization for Hyperparameter Tuning for Deep Learning Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Grid Search and LLM Assisted Hybrid Approach for Hyperparameter Optimization"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"LLM-based Hyperparameter Tuning Framework for Time Series Forecasting: A Case Study on Seoul Air Quality Data"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"HALO: Hyperparameter Auto-tuning via LLM Optimizer for Rapid, Interpretable AutoML"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Optuna vs Code Llama: Are LLMs a New Paradigm for Hyperparameter Tuning?"}],"more":22},{"year":2026,"n":1,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"}],"more":0}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":12,"share":0.324},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":9,"share":0.243},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":5,"share":0.135},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":4,"share":0.108},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":3,"share":0.081},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":3,"share":0.081},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":2,"share":0.054},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":2,"share":0.054}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Recent LLM-assisted online hyperparameter adaptation for metaheuristics feeds a window of optimization logs (fitness values per generation, sometimes population statistics) to an LLM and applies whatever parameter change the LLM returns, with no quantity that says when that change should be trusted: in semanticscholar:690b34bda96f6b2d114702d74ee910392e06e3dd the Qwen model is handed fitness values across generations of Evolutionary Reinforcement Learning and its hyperparameter recommendations are adopted directly, and in openalex:W4401214105 Llama2/Mixtral analyze (1+1)-ES logs to emit real-time step-size recommendations whose effect the authors themselves report as mixed/unreliable. Because the recommendation is injected with a fixed (implicitly full) weight regardless of how much in-context evidence supports it, a confidently-wrong suggestion during a deceptive or stagnation phase of the landscape moves the control parameter as forcefully as a well-grounded one, and there is no mechanism that lets the metaheuristic's own measurable search state (improvement rate, population diversity collapse, success ratio) down-weight or veto the suggestion when it conflicts. Classical self-adaptive controllers (openalex:W4406560032, openalex:W4411326051, openalex:W4412525433) instead set parameters from hand-built or oracle-bound statistical rules that never read the semantic context of the problem, so neither side produces a per-step trust-weighted parameter update.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:690b34bda96f6b2d114702d74ee910392e06e3dd","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Sends per-generation fitness values from an Evolutionary Reinforcement Learning run to Qwen-max and adopts the model's returned hyperparameter (alpha/learning-rate-style) adjustments directly during training. It does NOT quantify the reliability of any individual recommendation nor blend it against the search's own measured progress, so a low-confidence or off-distribution suggestion is applied with the same authority as a strong one and there is no veto path when the optimizer's evidence contradicts it. [residue is abstract-level: anchor fulltext unfetchable]"},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4401214105","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Uses Llama2-70b/Mixtral to read (1+1)-ES optimization logs online and emit real-time step-size recommendations, reporting that LLMs can be effective but with mixed reliability. It treats every LLM recommendation as directly actionable and offers no calibrated estimate of suggestion trustworthiness, so the documented unreliability has no controller-level remedy beyond accepting the noisy advice."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4406560032","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"A dual-stage self-adaptive Differential Evolution that adapts mutation strategies and control parameters via hand-crafted complementary/ensemble rules driven by population statistics. Its adaptation never consults the semantic context of the problem or any external reasoning, so it cannot exploit problem-class knowledge and its fixed rule schedule is blind to landscape features it was not designed for."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4412525433","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Proves an adaptive-parameter-tuning scheme for evolutionary computation with oracle-style optimality bounds. The guarantee is purely statistical/closed-form and does not incorporate any semantic or problem-description prior, so it cannot warm-start or reason about a novel problem the way an LLM could, and conversely offers no slot for fusing an external advisor's signal."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"LLM-assisted hyperparameter/parameter control for metaheuristic (evolutionary / swarm) optimization","venue":"ICLR 2026 (primary_area: optimization)","time":"2026","data":["standard black-box optimization benchmark suites (e.g. BBOB/COCO continuous functions)","optimization run logs (fitness trajectories, population statistics)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day) plus LLM API budget","expertise":"evolutionary computation + LLM prompting","preference":"both","baseline":"self-adaptive metaheuristics (self-adaptive DE/ES, e.g. paper openalex:W4406560032, openalex:W4411326051) and current LLM-as-advisor online tuners (semanticscholar:690b34bda96f6b2d114702d74ee910392e06e3dd, openalex:W4401214105)","limitation":"current LLM-driven online hyperparameter adaptation treats the LLM as an unconditionally-trusted black-box advisor: its parameter recommendation is applied whether or not it is reliable for the current search state, with no signal of when to defer to the metaheuristic's own evidence","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The single shared object is the per-step control-parameter update u_t for a population metaheuristic (we instantiate on Differential Evolution's mutation factor F and crossover rate CR, and on a (1+lambda)-ES step-size sigma, matching the (1+1)-ES regime of openalex:W4401214105). At control step t the optimizer already maintains a self-adaptive estimate theta_opt,t for each parameter (the SHADE-style success-history mean for DE F/CR; the 1/5th-rule update for sigma) with its own dispersion s_opt,t. PIVOT LEG (C11): instead of asking the LLM for a value, we prompt it K times (K=8, temperature fixed at 0.7) with the same compact run-state summary — last-W generations of best/median fitness (W=10), population diversity (mean pairwise L2), success ratio, and the parameter's current value — and require each sample to return a JSON {mu, log_sigma} naming a Gaussian over the parameter; theta_llm,t = mean of the K mu's and the LLM-reported spread tau_llm,t = sqrt(var_across_K(mu) + mean(exp(log_sigma)^2)). theta_llm,t and tau_llm,t are thus computable from text alone: mu/log_sigma are model-internal readouts parsed from the K generations, K and temperature are fixed hyperparameters. ANCHOR LEG (C07): the manufactured trust scalar is w_t = sigmoid( a * (-log tau_llm,t) + b * r_t - c ), where r_t is the optimizer's realized-improvement residual = (observed best-fitness gain over the last tau_check=5 steps after the LLM's previous suggestion was applied) minus (the gain the LLM's previous posterior implied), standardized by a running scale; a,b,c are scalar fusion hyperparameters (defaults a=1.0, b=0.5, c=0 after standardizing both inputs to unit scale). w_t is the single tiny lever: the backbone optimizer and the LLM are both frozen, only this scalar is adapted. The fused update is u_t = (1 - w_t * g) * theta_opt,t + (w_t * g) * theta_llm,t, where g in [0,1] is a global trust cap (default g=0.7) acting as the C07 source-prior stabilizer — it floors the optimizer's own self-adaptive value at (1 - g) weight so the LLM can never fully overwrite it, preventing the degenerate collapse C07 warns about. Because w_t falls automatically when the LLM is internally uncertain (large tau_llm,t) OR when its recent suggestions failed to deliver the improvement they implied (negative r_t), a confidently-wrong suggestion during a deceptive/stagnation phase is down-weighted within the loop instead of applied at full authority (gap 0 closed). Because the LLM contributes a posterior the optimizer weighs rather than a value it must obey, the pivoted assumption is realized as the very interface the trust weight acts on (gap 1 closed). The two legs share u_t end to end: the pivot manufactures the soft object, the anchor manufactures the weight that fuses it.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules: gap 1's soft object (the LLM posterior) is exactly the input gap 0's trust weight must fuse, so a single update rule u_t carries both — building them as separate modules would be the 'two papers stapled together' failure, whereas one fusion equation makes the shared_object thread literal. (b) Alternatives rejected: (i) a plain Bayesian-optimization / bandit posterior over configurations (collateral node c1) was rejected because it occupies an already-existing ancestral node and discards the LLM's semantic prior — our trust signal is manufactured JOINTLY from LLM self-uncertainty and realized search feedback, a source neither c1 (uncertainty-only, semantics-free) nor c2 (RL reward policy) occupies, satisfying the Phase 2.1 occupied-source constraint; (ii) training a learned critic to predict suggestion quality was rejected as too data-hungry for the ~90 A100-day budget and because C07's discipline is a tiny frozen-backbone lever, not a new trained network.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: run trust-weighted control vs. three baselines (raw SHADE/(1+lambda)-ES, fixed-full-weight LLM advisor reproducing semanticscholar:690b34bda96f6b2d114702d74ee910392e06e3dd, and an LLM point-value variant) on the BBOB/COCO 24-function benchmark at dims 5 and 20 with matched evaluation budgets, measuring final optimization regret (best-found minus known optimum) and area-under-the-convergence-curve. If the candidate works, mean final regret decreases relative to the fixed-full-weight advisor, and the gap is largest on the multimodal/deceptive BBOB subgroup (functions f15-f24) where confidently-wrong suggestions are most damaging. The load-bearing variable is the per-step trust weight w_t: the mechanism claim is that w_t down-weights bad suggestions before they harm the search. Negative control: feed w_t a history-permuted, marginal-matched noise version of its two inputs (tau_llm,t and r_t) so w_t carries no current information while keeping its distribution fixed; the prediction is that final regret rises back toward (or above) the fixed-full-weight advisor on the deceptive subgroup — if regret is unchanged, w_t is not the mechanism and the gain came from the posterior interface or prompt content alone. Positive control: a stripped model that sets w_t purely from -log tau_llm,t (LLM self-uncertainty only, dropping r_t) should recover most of the regret reduction on unimodal functions but lose it on deceptive ones, identifying realized-improvement feedback as the component that handles deception.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:690b34bda96f6b2d114702d74ee910392e06e3dd","delta":"They adopt the LLM's per-generation hyperparameter adjustment directly at fixed authority; we construct a per-step trust weight w_t from the LLM's own answer dispersion and a realized-improvement residual that convexly down-weights the suggestion against the optimizer's self-adaptive estimate, a quantity their loop never computes."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4401214105","delta":"They report mixed reliability of online LLM step-size recommendations but apply every recommendation as-is; we turn that documented unreliability into a controllable lever by having the LLM emit a posterior whose spread feeds a trust gate, so unreliable suggestions are attenuated rather than accepted."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4406560032","delta":"Their self-adaptive DE drives F/CR purely from population success-history statistics with no semantic input; we fuse those same statistics with an LLM posterior under a manufactured trust weight, retaining the statistical estimate as a stabilizing floor (weight 1-g) the LLM can never overwrite."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4412525433","delta":"They prove oracle-bound adaptive parameter tuning from closed-form statistics with no external advisor interface; we provide the missing fusion interface in which an external semantic advisor's posterior is reconciled with run statistics through an evidence-gated weight rather than a fixed schedule."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4401214105","what_step_was_missed":"They had the LLM read (1+1)-ES logs and emit real-time step-size recommendations and even observed the recommendations were unreliable, but they never constructed a per-step reliability estimate that converts that observation into control: the missing step is requiring the LLM to self-report a spread per recommendation and pairing it with a realized-improvement residual to form a fusion weight that attenuates the suggestion against the optimizer's own estimate when evidence is weak."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":323,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"Layer-1 hard floor did not fire: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict is borderline (no lesson marked candidate_match=yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat is not exact-mechanism overlap. recipe_application_check.verdict is 'applied' for both entries (C07's diagnose-localize/tiny-lever/stabilizer and C11's selection->posterior-sampling reframe are both instantiated in core_mechanism), so the strongest revise trigger is absent. The two borderline reject lessons ('generic interpolation without a dynamics lever' and 'no theorem stating when it wins') hit non-load-bearing aspects — the dynamics lever IS named (the realized-improvement residual) and the method-typed contribution converts the when-it-wins claim into a falsifiable deceptive-subgroup prediction — so they advance with concerns surfaced for Phase 4 rather than warranting revision.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a per-step trust score for an LLM's parameter recommendation that lets the metaheuristic's own measured search state modulate how much that recommendation moves the control parameter — every LLM-advisor leaf applies the suggestion at a fixed implicit weight, so a confidently-wrong suggestion in a deceptive/stagnation phase is unrecoverable within the loop.","main_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"A manufactured internal signal whose validity silently rests on an assumption that does not survive deployment (calibration, stationarity, or covert label leakage), so the surrogate degrades exactly when the premise is violated; a second shape is recombining well-known components without one load-bearing mechanistic insight separating it from prior art.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A label-free signal whose validity depends on model calibration silently fails on exactly the deep networks known to be poorly calibrated — validate a surrogate where its core assumption is weakest, not where it is convenient.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The trust signal w_t does not rely solely on LLM self-reported calibration; it is gated by an independent realized-improvement residual r_t (did the previous suggestion actually deliver the gain it implied), so it remains valid precisely when the LLM is miscalibrated, and the falsification's positive control isolates exactly this."},{"lesson_quoted":"Reusing standard sequential machinery (chaining each step's posterior as the next prior) without a new stabilizer amplifies noise and looks derivative of prior adaptation work.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate adds an explicit stabilizer (the global trust cap g flooring the optimizer's self-adaptive value at weight 1-g) matched to the degenerate-collapse mode C07 names, rather than naively chaining posteriors."},{"lesson_quoted":"Importing a generic continual-learning blending or interpolation technique into a new modality without identifying that modality's specific dynamics lever reads as recombination, not contribution.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The fused update is a convex interpolation; the load-bearing lever distinguishing it from generic blending is that the interpolation weight is itself manufactured from a realized-improvement residual specific to optimization dynamics — surfaced as a reviewer concern but the dynamics lever is named, so not a trigger."},{"lesson_quoted":"Using target or test-set information during adaptation invites a label-leakage objection that undermines the very source-free, label-free deployment setting the method claims.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"All inputs (LLM dispersion, realized fitness improvement on the optimization problem itself) are available online during the run; there is no held-out target or test label being consumed."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions whether the LLM should emit a concrete parameter VALUE at all rather than a softer object (a distribution, a prior, a constraint on the parameter) that the optimizer can then weigh against its own statistics — every advisor leaf silently inherits the assumption that the LLM's job is to output the operative parameter directly.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The dominant failure is substituting one selection rule for another that performs better empirically while omitting the theorem explaining when/why it wins; a second is pivoting an assumption the community regards as a reasonable modeling choice rather than a genuine restriction.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Substituting one selection heuristic for another without a theorem stating when and why it wins reads as an engineering combination, not a contribution, no matter how clean the empirical gain.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"This is a method (not theory) contribution, so no regret theorem is offered; the 'when it wins' claim is instead made falsifiable via the deceptive-subgroup prediction and the named negative/positive controls, but a reviewer wanting a bound will note the absence — surfaced for Phase 4."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pivoting an assumption the community treats as a reasonable modeling choice — rather than first proving it a genuine restriction — leaves both motivation and novelty in doubt.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The pivoted assumption (LLM emits a value at fixed authority) is shown load-bearing because openalex:W4401214105 explicitly documents mixed reliability under it, so it is a genuine restriction, not a benign modeling choice."},{"lesson_quoted":"Unlocking a new capability by violating an assumption while ignoring a protective property it guarded — detectability, validity, identifiability — invites rejection on the overlooked side effect rather than the headline result.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The pivot does not discard the optimizer's own guarantee-bearing self-adaptive estimate; the stabilizer floor (weight 1-g) explicitly preserves the property the value-emission regime would otherwise have protected."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No entry triggered; both entries are borderline. The self_supervised_signal_engineering (C07) entry's weight comes from the generic-blending lesson, mitigated by the named realized-improvement dynamics lever; the assumption_audit (C11) entry's weight comes from the no-theorem lesson, expected for a method-typed contribution and converted to a falsifiable empirical claim instead."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a per-step trust score for an LLM's parameter recommendation that lets the metaheuristic's own measured search state modulate how much that recommendation moves the control parameter — every LLM-advisor leaf applies the suggestion at a fixed implicit weight, so a confidently-wrong suggestion in a deceptive/stagnation phase is unrecoverable within the loop.","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Treat a model's own internal-state readouts as the manufactured supervisory signal, pairing a mechanistic diagnosis that localizes the failure with a surgically confined correction on a minimal lever while the backbone stays frozen, and always bolt on an explicit stabilizer against degenerate collapse; verbs are diagnose-localize, minimize-on-a-tiny-lever, stabilize-against-collapse.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism performs all three signature verbs: diagnose-localize (the failure is localized to fixed-authority injection of an unreliable suggestion, read off LLM answer dispersion tau_llm,t and the realized-improvement residual r_t as internal readouts); minimize-on-a-tiny-lever (the only adapted quantity is the scalar fusion weight w_t; both LLM and optimizer backbones are frozen); stabilize-against-collapse (the global trust cap g floors the optimizer's value at weight 1-g, the explicit stabilizer matched to LLM-dominated collapse). This is the C07 tactic, not the parent's generic 'derive a signal from outputs'.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions whether the LLM should emit a concrete parameter VALUE at all rather than a softer object (a distribution, a prior, a constraint on the parameter) that the optimizer can then weigh against its own statistics — every advisor leaf silently inherits the assumption that the LLM's job is to output the operative parameter directly.","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Center on a selection/acquisition rule, name the one assumption baked into its criterion, and pivot it either by relaxing the structural crutch or by reframing the selection task into a different more tractable problem class (selection->posterior-sampling, selection->control) and importing that class's machinery.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism performs the reframe variant explicitly: the advisor's selection rule 'emit the operative parameter value' is pivoted into selection->posterior-sampling, with the LLM returning a Gaussian {mu, log_sigma} per parameter that the optimizer then weighs — importing the posterior-fusion machinery rather than patching the value-selection criterion. The distinctive C11 move (change the problem class the choice belongs to) is present.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries instantiate their cluster's signature move: C07's diagnose-localize / tiny-lever / stabilizer trio is the trust-weight construction, and C11's reframe-into-a-new-problem-class is the value->posterior pivot consumed by that weight."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["self_supervised_signal_engineering","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as a component; this candidate's composition set is {self_supervised_signal_engineering, assumption_audit_and_pivot}, which matches none of them."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:690b34bda96f6b2d114702d74ee910392e06e3dd","threat_source":"lit_table","subsumption_argument":"This anchor paper (LLM-optimized ERL) is the most specific competitor: it already feeds per-generation fitness logs to a strong LLM and adopts the returned hyperparameter adjustments online, so a reviewer could ask whether the candidate is merely that loop with a weighting knob. The candidate stands because that loop applies the LLM adjustment at fixed authority with no per-step reliability quantity, whereas the candidate's contribution IS the manufactured trust weight w_t (built from LLM answer dispersion plus a realized-improvement residual) gating a posterior the LLM emits instead of a value; the falsification's negative control (history-permuted w_t) and the fixed-full-weight baseline directly reproduce the anchor's regime and predict its regret on the deceptive subgroup, so the two are empirically separable rather than identical.","addressable_via":"Not exact-mechanism overlap; already differentiated by the trust-weight + posterior interface that the threat paper lacks, so no candidate field needs to change to dodge it — it is surfaced as the primary reviewer concern."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Trust-Weighted LLM Control of Metaheuristic Parameters via Manufactured Reliability Signals\n\n**Method.** Trust-Weighted LLM Control (TW-LLM-Control)\n\n## Motivation\nOptimization algorithms like Differential Evolution (DE) and Evolution Strategies (ES) only work well if a few control knobs (how big a mutation to make, how often to mix solutions, how large a step to take) are set correctly, and the right setting changes as the search proceeds. A popular recent idea is to let a large language model (LLM) read the optimizer's recent progress logs and suggest the next setting, because the LLM knows something about the problem. The catch is that today these systems simply do whatever the LLM says, at full strength, with no measure of whether the suggestion is trustworthy right now. So if the LLM is confidently wrong during a tricky phase of the search, its bad advice moves the knob just as hard as good advice, and the optimizer's own evidence has no way to push back. The closest prior systems show this exactly: one (International Conference on Advanced Computational Intelligence 2025) feeds fitness numbers to a strong LLM and adopts its hyperparameter changes directly; another (GECCO Companion 2024) drives an ES step-size from LLM advice and openly reports the advice is of mixed reliability, with no fix. Meanwhile classic self-tuning optimizers (Swarm and Evolutionary Computation 2025) only look at their own statistics and never read the problem's meaning. What is new is that we can now cheaply produce the two ingredients of a trust meter without training anything: ask the LLM the same question several times to see how much it disagrees with itself, and read off whether its last suggestion actually delivered the improvement it promised. Combining those into a single per-step trust weight lets us use the LLM hard when it is reliable and quietly ignore it when it is not, so LLM-guided tuning becomes safe even on landscapes where a confident wrong answer used to be unrecoverable.\n\n## Method\n### Optimizer hook (background)\n*Expose a frozen self-adaptive DE/ES so its control estimate can be read and its setpoint written.*\n\n1. Take an existing self-tuning Differential Evolution (DE), SHADE-style, and a (1+lambda) Evolution Strategy (ES), and add a small hook that (a) exposes their current control knobs (F, CR for DE; sigma for ES) as values you can both read and overwrite, and (b) reads out the optimizer's own current best guess $\\theta _{opt},t$ and how spread-out that guess is, $s_{opt},t,$ from the records it already keeps: for DE, the guess is the value stored in its success-history memory and the spread is the standard deviation of the recently successful values; for ES, the guess is the current step-size and the spread is how much the step-size has been changing recently. Nothing inside the optimizer is trained or altered. Also decide how often this whole procedure runs (default: once per generation) and hold the knob fixed in between.\n   - _Why_: We need the optimizer's own best guess available so we have something solid to blend the LLM's suggestion toward and to fall back on.\n2. Each control step, write one short, fixed-format status block: for the last W=10 generations the best and median fitness, how spread-out the population currently is (mean pairwise Euclidean / L2 distance between members), the recent success ratio (fraction of new candidates that were accepted), and the current value of the knob with its name and its allowed range. Use a stable field order and fixed numeric precision (6 significant figures). This block is the only thing the model is shown, and it is identical for all K queries in this step.\n   - _Why_: The LLM should reason from the current state of the search, not from nothing, so its suggestion is grounded in what is actually happening.\n\n### LLM posterior interface\n*Make the LLM emit a sampled Gaussian over each parameter instead of a value, yielding a self-consistency spread.*\n\n3. Ask the language model the same status block K=8 times, at temperature 0.7, and require each answer to be a small JSON object giving a mean (mu) and a log-spread $(log_{sigma})$ — i.e. a whole bell-curve over the parameter, not a single number. Give it a fixed instruction stating the parameter name, its allowed range, and the exact JSON shape. Check every reply: throw out any answer whose mean is outside the allowed range or whose spread is not a finite number, and re-ask that one answer up to 3 times. Convert each log-spread back to an ordinary spread by exponentiating. Keep going with however many valid answers (at least 2) you have; if you cannot get even 2, let the optimizer's own value win this step.\n   - _Why_: Asking for a distribution (and asking several times) lets the LLM tell us how unsure it is, which is the raw material for deciding how much to trust it.\n4. Combine the K valid answers two ways. The posterior $mean \\theta _{llm},t$ is just the average of the K means. The spread $\\tau _{llm},t$ combines two kinds of uncertainty: how much the K answers disagree with each other (the variance across their means) plus how unsure each answer says it is (the average of the per-answer variances); take the square root of that sum. A large $\\tau _{llm},t$ means the model is internally shaky on this step and its advice should later be trusted less.\n\n*The LLM posterior $mean \\theta _{llm},t$ and spread $\\tau _{llm},t$ aggregate K sampled Gaussians ${\\mu _{k}, \\sigma _{k}}:$ the mean of the means, and a total-variance spread combining disagreement across samples with each sample's self-reported variance.*\n$$ \\theta_{\\mathrm{llm},t} = \\frac{1}{K}\\sum_{k=1}^{K}\\mu_k, \\qquad \\tau_{\\mathrm{llm},t} = \\sqrt{\\operatorname{Var}_k(\\mu_k) + \\frac{1}{K}\\sum_{k=1}^{K}\\sigma_k^{2}} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A wide $tau_{llm},t$ means the LLM is internally shaky on this step, which should later pull its influence down.\n\n### Manufactured trust signal\n*Build the per-step trust weight from LLM self-uncertainty and the optimizer's realized-improvement residual.*\n\n5. Compute $r_{t},$ the reality-check on the last suggestion. Look at how much the best fitness ACTUALLY improved over the 5 control steps after the previous suggestion was applied (call it $\\Delta _{obs}),$ then subtract how much improvement that previous suggestion implied you should have gotten $(\\Delta _{imp}).$ 【author decision: you must decide how to turn a suggested parameter value into an 'implied improvement' $\\Delta _{imp}$ — by fitting a quick model of recent gains versus recent settings, by using a fixed textbook progress estimate, or by also asking the model how much gain it expects — because there is no standard formula relating these knobs to fitness gain.】 Divide that difference by a running scale (the typical size of this difference over the last 20 steps, the median absolute deviation, with a tiny floor so you never divide by zero). A negative $r_{t}$ means the last advice over-promised.\n\n*The realized-improvement residual $r_{t}$ standardizes the gap between the best-fitness gain actually observed over the last $\\tau _{check}$ steps $(\\Delta _{obs})$ and the gain the previous LLM posterior implied $(\\Delta _{imp}),$ by a running scale $\\hat{s}_{t}.$*\n$$ r_t = \\frac{\\Delta^{\\mathrm{obs}}_{t} - \\Delta^{\\mathrm{imp}}_{t}}{\\hat{s}_t} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Self-doubt alone cannot catch a confidently-wrong suggestion; checking whether the advice actually paid off is what flags confident mistakes on deceptive problems.\n6. Turn the two signals into one trust weight $w_{t}$ with a sigmoid (logistic squashing into the 0-to-1 range): $w_{t} = sigmoid(a\\cdot (- log \\tau _{llm},t) + b\\cdot r_{t} - $ c), with a=1.0, b=0.5, c=0. First put both inputs on a common scale by z-scoring them over the last 20 steps (subtract their recent average, divide by their recent spread) so the coefficients are meaningful; when both inputs sit at their recent average, $w_{t}$ comes out at the neutral 0.5. A model that is both self-consistent (small spread) and recently correct (positive reality-check) gets a high $w_{t}.$ This single number is the only thing the method tunes online.\n\n*The manufactured trust weight $w_{t}$ is a sigmoid of two standardized inputs: low LLM spread $\\tau _{llm},t$ (high self-consistency) and positive realized-improvement residual $r_{t}$ both push $w_{t}$ up; a,b,c are scalar fusion coefficients.*\n$$ w_t = \\sigma\\!\\left(a\\,(-\\log \\tau_{\\mathrm{llm},t}) + b\\, r_t - c\\right) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: One interpretable knob that goes up when the LLM is both self-consistent and recently correct is exactly the missing 'how much should I trust this' meter.\n\n### Trust-weighted fusion\n*Blend LLM posterior and optimizer estimate in proportion to trust under a stabilizing floor and write it back.*\n\n7. Set the knob to a blend of the two estimates: $u_{t} =$ (1 $-  w_{t}\\cdot g)\\cdot \\theta _{opt},t + (w_{t}\\cdot g)\\cdot \\theta _{llm},t,$ with g=0.7. Here $\\theta _{opt},t$ is the optimizer's own value and $\\theta _{llm},t$ is the model's posterior mean. Feed $u_{t}$ back as the optimizer's actual F/CR/sigma for the next generation. The cap g=0.7 guarantees the optimizer's own value always keeps at least 30% of the weight no matter how much the model is trusted, so a bad model can never completely take over. The optimizer then keeps running its normal update on top of this setpoint.\n\n*The fused control setpoint $u_{t}$ convexly interpolates the optimizer's self-adaptive estimate $\\theta _{opt},t$ and the LLM posterior $mean \\theta _{llm},t$; the global cap $g\\le 1$ floors the optimizer's weight at (1-g) so the LLM can never fully overwrite it.*\n$$ u_t = (1 - w_t\\, g)\\,\\theta_{\\mathrm{opt},t} + (w_t\\, g)\\,\\theta_{\\mathrm{llm},t} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This blends LLM advice and optimizer evidence in proportion to current trust, while the floor guarantees a bad LLM can never completely take over.\n\n### Falsification harness\n*Log mechanism variables, run the history-permuted negative control, and evaluate against fixed-authority baselines.*\n\n8. Record $w_{t}, \\tau _{llm},t, r_{t}$ and both estimates at every step. Then run a negative control: feed $w_{t} a$ reshuffled copy of its own two inputs — shuffle each input's time order independently across the whole run, so it carries no real-time information but has exactly the same overall distribution — and re-run on the deceptive functions. Save the shuffle seeds so it is reproducible. If scrambling the trust signal's timing does NOT make results worse, then $w_{t}$ was not actually doing the work; this is the honest test that the mechanism is real.\n   - _Why_: If scrambling the trust signal's information does not hurt results, then $w_{t}$ was not doing the work — this is the honest test that the mechanism is real.\n9. Evaluate on the standard BBOB/COCO 24-function benchmark at dimensions 5 and 20, plus a small neural-architecture hyperparameter task, against three baselines: the raw optimizer (DE/ES) with no LLM, a fixed-full-weight LLM advisor (always set the trust weight to its maximum g, which matches how prior work uses the LLM), and an LLM that emits a single point value instead of a distribution. Report final regret (how far the best result is from the known best) and area under the convergence curve, with the deceptive functions f15-f24 reported separately. Use at least 15 independent random seeds per function-and-dimension and give every method the same number of function evaluations. For the neural-architecture task, which has no known optimum, score regret against the best configuration any method found, and also report the raw best validation score.\n   - _Why_: Comparing against the fixed-authority advisor on exactly the deceptive functions is where trust-weighting should help most, so it is the sharpest test of the idea.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 基于自制可靠性信号的可信度加权 LLM 元启发式参数控制\n\n**方法名称.** Trust-Weighted LLM Control (TW-LLM-Control)\n\n## 研究动机\n像差分进化 (DE) 和进化策略 (ES) 这类优化算法，只有当几个控制旋钮（变异幅度多大、多频繁地混合解、步长多大）设置正确时才好用，而且正确的设置会随着搜索推进而改变。最近流行的做法是让大语言模型 (LLM) 读取优化器近期的进展日志并建议下一步的设置，因为 LLM 对问题本身有一定了解。问题在于，目前这些系统只是照单全收地、以全强度执行 LLM 说的话，完全没有衡量这个建议此刻是否可信。于是当 LLM 在搜索的棘手阶段自信地犯错时，它的坏建议会和好建议一样用力地拨动旋钮，而优化器自己的证据没有任何途径去反驳。最接近的已有工作正好暴露了这一点：一篇 (International Conference on Advanced Computational Intelligence 2025) 把适应度数值喂给一个强 LLM 并直接采纳它的超参数调整；另一篇 (GECCO Companion 2024) 用 LLM 建议驱动 ES 步长，并坦言这些建议可靠性参差不齐却无补救手段。与此同时，经典的自适应优化器 (Swarm and Evolutionary Computation 2025) 只看自己的统计量，从不读取问题的语义。新的契机在于：我们现在能在不训练任何模型的前提下，廉价地造出可信度计的两个原料——把同一个问题问 LLM 好几遍，看它自相矛盾的程度；再读出它上一条建议是否真的带来了它承诺的改进。把二者合成一个逐步的可信度权重 $w_{t}$，就能在 LLM 可靠时大胆使用、不可靠时悄悄忽略，使 LLM 引导的调参即便在过去一旦自信犯错就无法挽回的地形上也变得安全。\n\n## 方法\n### 优化器钩子（背景）\n*暴露一个冻结的自适应 DE/ES，使其控制估计可读、设定值可写回。*\n\n1. 取一个现成的自适应差分进化(Differential Evolution, DE)，采用 SHADE 风格，再取一个 (1+lambda) 进化策略(Evolution Strategy, ES)，给它们加一个小钩子：(a) 把当前的控制旋钮(DE 的 F、CR；ES 的 sigma)暴露成既能读又能覆写的值；(b) 从它们本来就维护的记录里读出优化器自己的当前最佳猜测 $\\theta _{opt},t$，以及这个猜测有多分散 $s_{opt},t——$对 DE，猜测取其成功历史记忆里存的值，分散度取近期成功取值的标准差；对 ES，猜测取当前步长，分散度取步长近期变化的幅度。优化器内部不训练、不改动。另外要确定整个流程多久跑一次(默认每代一次)，两次之间把旋钮固定住。\n   - _为什么_: 我们需要优化器自己的最佳猜测，这样才有一个可靠的对象去和 LLM 的建议做融合，并在需要时回退。\n2. 每个控制步写一段简短、固定格式的状态块：最近 W=10 代的最优适应度与中位适应度、当前种群有多分散(成员之间的平均两两欧氏 / L2 距离)、近期成功率(被接受的新候选解占比)，以及该旋钮的名称、当前值和允许范围。字段顺序固定、数值精度固定(保留 6 位有效数字)。这段块是模型唯一能看到的信息，并且在本步骤的 K 次查询中完全相同。\n   - _为什么_: LLM 应基于搜索的当前状态来推理，而不是凭空给建议，这样它的建议才扎根于实际发生的情况。\n\n### LLM 后验接口\n*让 LLM 对每个参数输出采样高斯分布而非数值，从而得到自一致性离散度。*\n\n3. 用同一段状态块在 temperature 0.7 下问语言模型 K=8 次，并要求每次回答是一个小 JSON 对象，给出均值 mu 和对数离散度 $log_{sigma}——$也就是该参数上的一整条钟形分布，而不是单个数值。给它一条固定指令，写明参数名称、允许范围和确切的 JSON 格式。检查每条回复：丢弃均值超出允许范围或离散度非有限数的回答，并把那一条最多重问 3 次。把每个对数离散度取指数还原成普通离散度。用手头有效回答(至少 2 条)继续；若连 2 条都凑不齐，本步就让优化器自己的值占主导。\n   - _为什么_: 要求一个分布（并且多问几次）能让 LLM 告诉我们它有多不确定，这正是判断该多信任它的原料。\n4. 把 K 条有效回答用两种方式合并。后验均值 $\\theta _{llm},t$ 就是 K 个均值的平均。离散度 $\\tau _{llm},t$ 合并了两类不确定性：K 条回答彼此之间的分歧(各自均值的方差)，加上每条回答自称的不确定度(各自方差的平均)，再对这个和取平方根。$\\tau _{llm},t$ 越大，说明模型这一步内部越动摇，之后就应越少地信任它的建议。\n\n*LLM 后验均值 $\\theta _{llm},t$ 与离散度 $\\tau _{llm},t$ 由 K 次采样得到的高斯 ${\\mu _{k}, \\sigma _{k}}$ 聚合而来：均值取各 $\\mu _{k}$ 的平均，离散度则把样本间的分歧与每个样本自报的方差合成一个总方差。*\n$$ \\theta_{\\mathrm{llm},t} = \\frac{1}{K}\\sum_{k=1}^{K}\\mu_k, \\qquad \\tau_{\\mathrm{llm},t} = \\sqrt{\\operatorname{Var}_k(\\mu_k) + \\frac{1}{K}\\sum_{k=1}^{K}\\sigma_k^{2}} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: $tau_{llm},t$ 越大说明 LLM 这一步内部越动摇，之后就应当压低它的影响力。\n\n### 自制可信度信号\n*由 LLM 自我不确定度与优化器实际改进残差构造逐步的可信度权重。*\n\n5. 计算 $r_{t}$，即对上一条建议的现实检验。看看上一条建议被采纳后的 5 个控制步内，最优适应度实际改进了多少(记为 $\\Delta _{obs})$，再减去那条建议所隐含的应有改进$(\\Delta _{imp})$。【作者需决定：必须确定如何把一个建议的参数值换算成『隐含改进』$\\Delta _{imp}——$是用最近增益对最近设置拟合一个快速模型、用一个固定的教科书式进展估计、还是干脆也让模型报出它预期的增益——因为这些旋钮与适应度增益之间没有标准公式。】把这个差值除以一个滑动尺度(最近 20 步内该差值的典型大小，即中位数绝对偏差，并加一个极小下限以免除零)。$r_{t}$ 为负说明上一条建议夸大了效果。\n\n*实际改进残差 $r_{t}$ 衡量最近 $\\tau _{check}$ 步内真实取得的最优适应度增益 $(\\Delta _{obs})$ 与上一次 LLM 后验所隐含的增益 $(\\Delta _{imp})$ 之差，并用滑动尺度 $\\hat{s}_{t}$ 做标准化。*\n$$ r_t = \\frac{\\Delta^{\\mathrm{obs}}_{t} - \\Delta^{\\mathrm{imp}}_{t}}{\\hat{s}_t} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 光靠自我怀疑抓不住自信的错误建议；检验建议是否真的兑现，才能在欺骗性问题上标记出自信的错误。\n6. 把两个信号用一个 sigmoid(把数压到 0 到 1 区间的逻辑斯谛函数)合成一个可信度权重 $w_{t}$：$w_{t} = sigmoid(a\\cdot (- log \\tau _{llm},t) + b\\cdot r_{t} - $ c)，取 a=1.0、b=0.5、c=0。先把两个输入放到同一尺度上：用最近 20 步对它们做 z 标准化(减去近期平均、除以近期离散度)，这样系数才有意义；当两个输入都处于近期平均水平时，$w_{t}$ 取中性值 0.5。一个既自一致(离散度小)又近期正确(现实检验为正)的模型会得到高 $w_{t}$。这个单一数值是该方法在线唯一调整的量。\n\n*自制可信度权重 $w_{t}$ 是两个标准化输入的 sigmoid：较小的 LLM 离散度 $\\tau _{llm},t$（高自一致性）与正的实际改进残差 $r_{t}$ 都会把 $w_{t}$ 推高；a、b、c 为标量融合系数。*\n$$ w_t = \\sigma\\!\\left(a\\,(-\\log \\tau_{\\mathrm{llm},t}) + b\\, r_t - c\\right) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 一个在 LLM 既自一致又近期正确时升高的可解释旋钮，恰好就是此前缺失的'该信多少'的度量。\n\n### 可信度加权融合\n*按可信度比例在稳定下限下融合 LLM 后验与优化器估计并写回。*\n\n7. 把旋钮设为两个估计的融合：$u_{t} =$ (1 $-  w_{t}\\cdot g)\\cdot \\theta _{opt},t + (w_{t}\\cdot g)\\cdot \\theta _{llm},t$，取 g=0.7。其中 $\\theta _{opt},t$ 是优化器自己的值，$\\theta _{llm},t$ 是模型的后验均值。把 $u_{t}$ 作为下一代真正使用的 F/CR/sigma 写回优化器。上限 g=0.7 保证无论模型多受信任，优化器自身的值始终至少保留 30% 的权重，因此再糟的模型也永远无法完全接管。之后优化器继续在这个设定值之上运行它自己的常规更新。\n\n*融合后的控制设定值 $u_{t}$ 在优化器自适应估计 $\\theta _{opt},t$ 与 LLM 后验均值 $\\theta _{llm},t$ 之间做凸插值；全局上限 $g\\le 1$ 将优化器权重下限锁定在 (1-g)，使 LLM 永远无法完全覆盖它。*\n$$ u_t = (1 - w_t\\, g)\\,\\theta_{\\mathrm{opt},t} + (w_t\\, g)\\,\\theta_{\\mathrm{llm},t} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这按当前可信度比例融合 LLM 建议与优化器证据，而下限保证再糟的 LLM 也永远无法完全接管。\n\n### 可证伪性测试装置\n*记录机制变量、运行历史置换负对照、并与固定权重基线对比评测。*\n\n8. 每步记录 $w_{t}$、$\\tau _{llm},t$、$r_{t}$ 和两个估计值。然后做负对照：给 $w_{t}$ 喂入它自己两个输入的打乱副本——把每个输入的时间顺序在整个运行过程中各自独立地打乱，使它不携带任何实时信息、但整体分布完全一致——并在欺骗性函数上重跑。保存打乱用的随机种子以便复现。如果打乱可信度信号的时序后结果并不变差，说明 $w_{t}$ 本来就没起作用；这是检验机制是否真实的诚实测试。\n   - _为什么_: 如果打乱可信度信号的信息后结果不变差，说明 $w_{t}$ 本来就没起作用——这是检验机制是否真实的诚实测试。\n9. 在标准的 BBOB/COCO 24 函数基准(维度 5 和 20)以及一个小型神经网络结构超参数任务上评测，对照三个基线：不用 LLM 的原始优化器(DE/ES)、固定全权重 LLM 顾问(始终把可信度权重设为上限 g，对应已有工作使用 LLM 的方式)、以及输出单个点值而非分布的 LLM。报告最终 regret(最优结果距已知最优有多远)和收敛曲线下面积，并把欺骗性函数 f15-f24 单独列出。每个函数与维度组合至少跑 15 个独立随机种子，并给所有方法相同的函数评估次数。对于没有已知最优的神经网络结构任务，用任一方法找到的最佳配置作为 regret 的参照，同时报告原始的最佳验证分数。\n   - _为什么_: 正是在欺骗性函数上与固定权重顾问对比，可信度加权最该体现优势，因此是对该想法最尖锐的检验。\n\n"},{"id":"10","run_dir":"run_prompt10_privacy","index":10,"title":"Mechanism-Attributed Privacy Auditing: Decomposing LLM Adaptation Leakage by Parameter Subspace","title_zh":"面向适配机制的隐私审计：按参数子空间分解大语言模型微调的隐私泄漏","method_name":"Mechanism-Attributed Privacy Auditing (MAPA)","hook":"Two LLM adaptations with identical model-level empirical leakage can carry that leakage in structurally different places, yet every current audit reports one scalar that cannot tell them apart. We construct a per-mechanism leakage estimator that attributes realized canary exposure to the specific adaptation parameter group (full-FT base weights, LoRA delta-weights, soft-prompt) that produced it.","anchor_pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","anchor_pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","domain_category":"Privacy, Security & Trustworthy ML","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a leakage estimate that is ATTRIBUTABLE to the adaptation mechanism: every audit reports one model-level scalar measured after adaptation, so the marginal contribution of full fine-tuning vs LoRA vs prompt/prefix tuning to the realized leakage of the same secret population is never isolated — two adaptations with equal scalar leakage are treated as equally private even when their mechanism-attributed leakage differs.","pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by partitioning the adapted model's trainable parameters into mechanism subspaces (frozen base, LoRA delta-weights B*A, soft-prompt embeddings) and assigning each partition a tailored leakage-restoration test, with a leakage-decomposition that bounds how the per-subspace exposure estimates recompose the total measured exposure — the error/sensitivity-decomposition spine of the C04 move applied to realized canary exposure rather than to compression error.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf constructs the audit probe (canary) to be MAXIMALLY INFORMATIVE about the adaptation under test: canaries are chosen by a generic 'make it memorable / OOD' heuristic decoupled from the model and the adaptation, so the resulting bound is loose and uninformative about the specific mechanism, and the audit cannot say whether a tighter probe would have revealed more leakage.","pattern_id":"targeted_self_supervised_objective","pattern_name":"Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective","sub_pattern":"C17 (Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by replacing the generic 'maximize memorability' heuristic with a contrastive probe-construction objective whose pairing geometry aligns a candidate canary's gradient-on-the-adapted-subspace with the adaptation's own update direction, so the only canaries that minimize the loss are those whose post-adaptation exposure is maximally sensitive to the mechanism under audit — the C17 primitive substitution (property-sensitive pairing replacing inner-product/heuristic similarity) applied to mechanism-attributable exposure.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"empirical privacy auditing of adapted/fine-tuned large language models","n_papers":40,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":27},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":23,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Unlocking Memorization in Large Language Models with Dynamic Soft Prompting"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"GoldCoin: Grounding Large Language Models in Privacy Laws via Contextual Integrity Theory"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Large Language Models Can Be Contextual Privacy Protection Learners"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Evaluation and mitigation of the limitations of large language models in clinical decision-making"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Promises and challenges of generative artificial intelligence for human learning"},{"source":"openalex","title":"<scp>AI</scp>‐driven adaptive learning for sustainable educational transformation"}],"more":17},{"year":2025,"n":17,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A Longitudinal Measurement of Privacy Policy Evolution for Large Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A Measurement Study of Model Context Protocol"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Exploring LLMs for Stakeholder-Specific Insight Generation from Software Contracts"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Privacy Auditing of Large Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A Comprehensive Survey on the Trustworthiness of Large Language Models in Healthcare"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"RewardDS: Privacy-Preserving Fine-Tuning for Large Language Models via Reward Driven Data Synthesis"}],"more":11}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":10,"share":0.25},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":4,"share":0.1},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":4,"share":0.1},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":2,"share":0.05},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":2,"share":0.05},{"pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","count":2,"share":0.05},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":1,"share":0.025},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":1,"share":0.025}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Empirical privacy auditing of adapted LLMs currently collapses to a single worst-case scalar: canary-injection auditing (semanticscholar:2f8917d5bead2e011a00c33153e8deb2027756ee) injects heuristic out-of-distribution canaries, runs a membership-inference test, and reports one empirical leakage lower bound (an epsilon-lower-bound or memorization rate) for the whole adapted model, while toolkits like LLM-PBE (openalex:W4402042869) aggregate attack scores into one privacy-risk number. This single-scalar output is computed AFTER adaptation and is blind to WHERE the leakage came from: the Janus attack (openalex:W4405181291) shows that the fine-tuning interface itself re-surfaces PII that the base model had effectively forgotten, and the LLM-MIA revisiting study (openalex:W4412944805) shows MIA scores swing wildly across settings, yet no audit can say how much of a fine-tuned model's measured leakage is attributable to the adaptation mechanism (full fine-tuning vs LoRA vs prompt/prefix tuning) versus pre-existing base-model memorization. Because the audit machinery produces one number per model rather than a leakage estimate conditioned on the adaptation, two adaptations with identical scalar leakage are indistinguishable even when one is structurally far riskier, and the heuristic canary that drives the bound is not constructed to be maximally informative about the adaptation under test.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:2f8917d5bead2e011a00c33153e8deb2027756ee","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Designs stronger, less-detectable canaries than prior OOD-random-token canaries so that the resulting membership-inference attack yields a tighter empirical privacy lower bound across families of fine-tuned LLMs. Residue: it produces one model-level scalar leakage bound and selects canaries by a generic 'maximize memorizability' heuristic, so it never attributes the measured leakage to the specific adaptation mechanism that produced it, nor tailors the canary to be discriminative about that mechanism, leaving 'which part of the adaptation pipeline is leaking, and by how much' unmeasured."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4405181291","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"The Janus attack shows that the fine-tuning interface re-activates PII the base model had catastrophically forgotten, demonstrating that adaptation is itself a leakage amplifier. Residue: it is an existence-style attack that proves amplification happens, but gives no calibrated, comparable estimator that quantifies the marginal leakage contributed by one adaptation choice versus another over a held population of secrets."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4412944805","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Statistically revisits LLM membership inference and shows attack-success scores are inconsistent across model size, corpus, and text-length settings, undermining a single MIA number as a privacy verdict. Residue: it diagnoses the instability but does not deliver a measurement design that controls these confounds so that a leakage estimate becomes attributable to the adaptation under audit rather than to the evaluation setting."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4402042869","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"LLM-PBE assembles existing data-extraction and membership attacks into a unified toolkit that scores a model's overall data-privacy risk. Residue: it standardizes WHICH attacks to run but still emits an aggregate per-model risk score with no decomposition that isolates how each adaptation mechanism contributes to the realized leakage."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4403827659","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Empirically audits the realized privacy budget of differentially-private neural networks, showing the analytic epsilon overstates protection relative to attack-measured leakage. Residue: it is scoped to generic DP-trained networks and a single global budget gap, not to non-DP LLM adaptations or to attributing the gap across distinct adaptation mechanisms."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"empirical privacy auditing of adapted/fine-tuned large language models","venue":"ICLR / NeurIPS / IEEE S&P / USENIX Security tier","time":"2026","data":["public instruction-tuning / domain fine-tuning corpora with injectable canaries","open-weight base LLMs (e.g. Llama/Pythia families) adapted via LoRA, full fine-tuning, and prompt/prefix tuning"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML privacy / membership inference / differential privacy auditing","preference":"both","baseline":"canary-injection privacy auditing of fine-tuned LLMs (Privacy Auditing of LLMs, ICLR 2025) and membership-inference / extraction probes (Janus; Unlocking Memorization; LLM-PBE)","limitation":"current empirical privacy audits report a single scalar leakage / epsilon-lower-bound for the adapted model and use heuristic canaries; they cannot attribute how much realized leakage each adaptation mechanism (full FT vs LoRA vs prompt-tuning) is responsible for, and the canary that drives the bound is not constructed to be informative about the specific adaptation","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The pipeline is sequential (sequential_pipeline thread): leg B (C17) builds mechanism-targeted canaries that leg A (C04) then attributes. Central setup: a base LLM theta_0 is adapted by mechanism m (full fine-tuning, LoRA, or soft-prompt/prefix tuning) on a corpus into which N controlled canary secrets have been injected, yielding theta_m; the audit observes only black-box or gray-box access to theta_m and the canary set. LEG B — targeted probe construction. For each mechanism m we define the adaptation update subspace U_m: for full-FT U_m is the full weight space, for LoRA U_m is the span of the delta-weights Delta_W = B*A (rank r, the trained factors), for soft-prompt U_m is the embedding rows of the k prepended virtual tokens. We construct canaries by minimizing a contrastive probe objective L_probe(c) = -log [ exp(s(c)/tau) / (exp(s(c)/tau) + sum_{c'} exp(s(c')/tau)) ] where the positive score s(c) = < g_U(c), d_m > is the inner product between g_U(c) = P_{U_m} grad_theta loss(theta_0, c) (the projection onto U_m of the per-canary loss-gradient at the base model) and d_m, a unit vector estimating the adaptation's mean update direction inside U_m (computed once from a small pilot adaptation on held-out data; d_m is the normalized average of Delta-parameters over pilot canaries). tau is a temperature hyperparameter (default 0.1). The minimizer is a canary whose learning signal lands maximally inside the subspace mechanism m actually moves, so its exposure is maximally informative about m — replacing the OOD-random-token memorability heuristic of the anchor prior work. LEG A — mechanism-attributed leakage decomposition. After adaptation, we measure each canary's empirical exposure E(c) (the standard membership-test statistic: rank/quantile of the canary's loss under theta_m against a reference cohort, or the Carlini-style exposure used by Privacy Auditing of LLMs). The decomposition attributes E to subspaces by a restoration test: we form partial models theta_{m,-S} that reset partition S of the trained parameters back to theta_0 (zero the LoRA factors, or blank the soft-prompt rows, or restore a weight block) while keeping the rest of the adaptation, and define the marginal attributed leakage of partition S as A_S = E(theta_m) - E(theta_{m,-S}) averaged over canaries, with a Shapley-style symmetric averaging over restoration orders so the A_S sum exactly to the total exposure gap E(theta_m) - E(theta_0) (the additive efficiency property of Shapley values gives the recomposition bound — leg A's load-bearing error/sensitivity decomposition). Reporting A_S per partition is the per-mechanism leakage estimate that two equal-scalar adaptations cannot hide behind. The two legs share the canary set as the pipelined object: leg B's targeted canaries make A_S sharp (a generic canary spreads its gradient across all subspaces and gives flat, uninformative A_S), and leg A's decomposition is what turns the targeted exposure into an attributable number.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The two gaps need SEPARATE but pipelined modules, not shared machinery: gap B is about WHICH probe to inject (a construction objective run before adaptation) and gap A is about HOW to read the exposure of an already-adapted model (a decomposition run after adaptation), and the evidence they are sequential is that A_S is only sharp when the canary's gradient concentrates in one subspace — i.e. leg A consumes leg B's output. I considered a single-module design that just runs the standard audit per-mechanism and diffs the scalars, but rejected it: a naive scalar diff across separately-trained models confounds the mechanism with the different optimization trajectory and data ordering, whereas the restoration test holds the adaptation fixed and only resets a partition, isolating the marginal. REGRESSION CHECK (method_lineage): the load-bearing artifact is the per-subspace marginal A_S with Shapley additivity — this lands on NONE of the occupied nodes (it is not plain shadow-model MIA n0, not Secret-Sharer exposure n1, not a global empirical-epsilon n2, not analytic DP accounting c1, and not influence-functions c2 since A_S is a leakage-exposure marginal under parameter restoration, not a training-data attribution score); I explicitly avoided computing a single global epsilon-lower-bound (n2) by reporting the decomposition instead.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: take one open base LLM (e.g. a 1-7B Pythia/Llama checkpoint), inject a fixed canary population, and adapt it under three mechanisms (full fine-tuning, LoRA, soft-prompt tuning) tuned so that all three reach the SAME model-level exposure E(theta_m) on the canaries; then compute the per-subspace attributed-leakage vector A_S for each. If the method works, the A_S vectors differ across the three equal-E adaptations (e.g. soft-prompt concentrates attributed leakage in the prompt rows while LoRA spreads it across the last-layer delta blocks), and a held-out targeted-canary extraction attack guided by the highest-A_S partition succeeds at a strictly higher extraction rate than a partition chosen at random — i.e. the extraction-success metric increases when attacking high-A_S subspaces. The load-bearing variable is the targeting alignment s(c)=<g_U(c),d_m>: as the mechanism distinguisher, we predict that canaries with high s(c) yield sharper, more concentrated A_S vectors and higher downstream extraction success than low-s(c) canaries. Negative control: randomize d_m (replace the estimated update direction with a random unit vector in U_m) when constructing canaries — this should drive the downstream extraction-success rate back to the generic-canary baseline (no advantage over random-OOD canaries), because the canaries are no longer aligned to the subspace the mechanism moves. Positive control: a stripped-down auditor that ONLY ranks partitions by s(c)-alignment (no full Shapley decomposition) should still recover most of the extraction-success gain over random-partition attacks, identifying s(c) as the mechanism.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:2f8917d5bead2e011a00c33153e8deb2027756ee","delta":"They construct stronger canaries to tighten a single model-level empirical leakage lower bound for fine-tuned LLMs; we construct canaries targeted to a specific adaptation subspace AND decompose the measured exposure into per-mechanism marginals A_S with Shapley additivity, a per-subspace attribution their single-scalar audit does not produce."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4405181291","delta":"Janus demonstrates that the fine-tuning interface re-surfaces forgotten PII (an existence proof of adaptation-driven leakage); we produce a calibrated, comparable estimator that quantifies how much of the realized exposure each adaptation parameter group contributes, which their attack does not measure."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4412944805","delta":"They show raw MIA scores are confounded by model/corpus/length settings; we hold the adaptation fixed and isolate the marginal via parameter restoration, so the attributed leakage A_S is robust to a trajectory confound their cross-setting comparison cannot control."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4402042869","delta":"LLM-PBE aggregates existing attacks into one per-model privacy-risk score; we decompose realized exposure across adaptation subspaces rather than aggregating it into a single number."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4403827659","delta":"They audit the realized-vs-analytic epsilon gap of generic DP-trained networks as one global budget; we attribute non-DP LLM-adaptation leakage to specific parameter partitions, not a single global budget."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:2f8917d5bead2e011a00c33153e8deb2027756ee","what_step_was_missed":"They built better canaries to raise the achievable model-level leakage lower bound, but to reach mechanism-attributed auditing they would have needed two constructions they did not perform: (1) a probe-construction objective that aligns the canary's base-model gradient with a specific adaptation subspace's update direction (their canaries are selected by generic OOD-memorability, agnostic to which parameter group the adaptation moves), and (2) a restoration-based, Shapley-additive decomposition of the measured exposure across trained-parameter partitions that recomposes to the total exposure gap — without (2) the audit can only report one scalar, and without (1) that decomposition is flat and uninformative."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":279,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"Layer 1 did not fire: gap_closure_reject_check is borderline (no candidate_match=yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat (FedAttr) is not exact-mechanism overlap (it attributes along client-provenance, not parameter-subspace). recipe_application_check.verdict=applied for both legs (C04's Shapley-additive exposure decomposition and C17's gradient-subspace-aligned similarity are both present), so the leading revise trigger is absent. The two borderline findings (strongest uniform single-scalar baseline named in differentiation rather than run as a control; nearest canary-design baselines not all enumerated) are experiment-completeness concerns in non-load-bearing framing that Phase 4 can fold into reviewer_concerns_and_responses rather than load-bearing structural defects, so advance with those concerns surfaced.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a leakage estimate that is ATTRIBUTABLE to the adaptation mechanism: every audit reports one model-level scalar measured after adaptation, so the marginal contribution of full fine-tuning vs LoRA vs prompt/prefix tuning to the realized leakage of the same secret population is never isolated — two adaptations with equal scalar leakage are treated as equally private even when their mechanism-attributed leakage differs.","main_pattern":"heterogeneous_decomposition","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is treating the partition criterion itself as the contribution while leaving its value unproven, and validating in a regime where the bottleneck does not bite or omitting the strongest uniform baseline and obvious cheap alternative.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Presenting a sensitivity or redundancy proxy as the novelty invites the verdict that it rediscovers known mixed-precision or low-rank results unless it is sharply differentiated from the obvious prior criterion.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The partition is the adaptation's own trainable-parameter groups (LoRA factors / soft-prompt rows / weight blocks), not a generic sensitivity proxy, and the contribution is the restoration-based Shapley-additive exposure decomposition, not the partition criterion itself."},{"lesson_quoted":"Omitting comparison against both the strongest uniform baseline and the obvious cheap alternative (SVD/PCA, structured dropout, a natively trained smaller model) leaves reviewers unable to tell whether the partition buys anything at all.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"core_mechanism_steps step 10 supplies the uniform/cheap alternative (generic-canary baseline that flattens A_S) but the strongest uniform baseline here — the single-scalar audit of Privacy Auditing of LLMs — is named in differentiation rather than run as an explicit uniform-vs-differentiated control in the experiment list."},{"lesson_quoted":"Skipping any analysis of why the heterogeneity exists — the data or value distribution that drives the partition — makes the technical novelty and the potential impact impossible to assess.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The heterogeneity is grounded mechanistically: different adaptation mechanisms move disjoint parameter subspaces U_m, so the per-subspace exposure distribution is forced by which subspace the update lives in, and the falsification predicts a measurable difference in A_S concentration."},{"lesson_quoted":"A clever partition with no measured real-world deployment metric (no inference latency or memory speedup) reads as a proxy-only contribution and stalls at borderline.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The deployment metric here is the privacy-relevant one (extraction-success rate / attributed exposure), which the falsification names directly, not a proxy; latency/memory are not the binding metric for a privacy audit."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf constructs the audit probe (canary) to be MAXIMALLY INFORMATIVE about the adaptation under test: canaries are chosen by a generic 'make it memorable / OOD' heuristic decoupled from the model and the adaptation, so the resulting bound is loose and uninformative about the specific mechanism, and the audit cannot say whether a tighter probe would have revealed more leakage.","main_pattern":"targeted_self_supervised_objective","sub_pattern":"C17 (Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring shape is sourcing the pairing/alignment signal by composing two already-published components and presenting the composition as the contribution, never re-deriving WHY this pairing geometry uniquely encodes the targeted property and supplying no isolating ablation or direct probe.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Concatenating a frozen off-the-shelf predictor's output as an extra input channel injects no novel insight — it reads as combining two published systems regardless of the accuracy gain.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The probe objective is not a frozen predictor plugged into a standard SSL loss; the load-bearing primitive is the substitution of generic memorability with a similarity s(c)=<g_U(c),d_m> that pairs a canary's base-model gradient projection with the mechanism's update direction — a primitive belonging to neither a stock contrastive loss nor a stock canary generator."},{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a representation is 'disentangled' or property-specific without an operational definition, a direct probe, or an isolating ablation leaves the central claim ungrounded and unverifiable.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The targeted property (mechanism-attributable exposure) has an operational definition (A_S concentration), a direct probe (extraction-success when attacking high-A_S partition), and an isolating ablation (randomize d_m -> A_S flattens), all in falsification_prediction."},{"lesson_quoted":"A hard-pair construction strategy that closely recombines existing mixup/contrastive recipes collapses to 'incremental' the moment the nearest pair-construction baselines are missing from the comparison.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The nearest pair-construction baseline (the OOD-memorability canary of the anchor) IS named as the negative control, but other canary-design baselines (e.g. dynamic soft-prompting memorization probes) are not yet enumerated as comparison points in the experiment."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The anchor leg (heterogeneous_decomposition / C04) is borderline on the uniform-baseline lesson because the strongest uniform baseline (the single-scalar audit) appears in differentiation rather than as an explicit run control; the C17 leg is borderline on missing nearest pair-construction baselines. Neither marks any Reject lesson candidate_match=yes, so no hard-floor trigger."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a leakage estimate that is ATTRIBUTABLE to the adaptation mechanism...","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Discriminate components by a magnitude-/sensitivity-/influence-/redundancy-based criterion into populations and apply differentiated treatment, with the load-bearing artifact being an error/sensitivity decomposition that bounds how the differentiated treatment recovers the original objective — that analysis is what separates the move from heuristic per-component tuning.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism partitions trainable parameters into mechanism subspaces and assigns each a restoration test, and the Shapley-additive recomposition (sum_S A_S = E(theta_m)-E(theta_0), the efficiency property) IS the error/sensitivity decomposition spine that bounds how the per-partition estimates recover the total measured exposure — the C04 distinctive move, applied to realized canary exposure rather than compression error.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf constructs the audit probe (canary) to be MAXIMALLY INFORMATIVE about the adaptation under test...","sub_pattern":"C17 (Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Re-engineer the pairing/alignment geometry of a contrastive objective so the targeted property is the only thing whose encoding minimizes the loss; the decisive act is replacing or inverting a default geometric primitive (e.g. swapping inner-product similarity for a property-sensitive one).","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism replaces the generic memorability similarity with a contrastive L_probe whose positive score s(c)=<g_U(c),d_m> is a property-sensitive similarity aligning the canary's base-model gradient projection with the mechanism's update direction — the C17 primitive substitution, so only canaries informative about mechanism m minimize the loss.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both legs perform their cited cluster's signature move: C04's error/sensitivity decomposition is realized as the Shapley-additive exposure recomposition, and C17's geometric-primitive substitution is realized as the gradient-subspace-aligned similarity replacing generic memorability."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["heterogeneous_decomposition","targeted_self_supervised_objective"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"The three documented anti-patterns pair heterogeneous_decomposition with self_supervised_signal_engineering, structural_prior_encoding, or architectural_operator_substitution; the candidate pairs it with targeted_self_supervised_objective, which is a distinct pattern id not in any documented reject-favored composition, so no anti-pattern matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"openalex:W7160726714","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"FedAttr (Towards Privacy-preserving Client-Level Attribution in Federated LLM Fine-tuning) is the nearest competitor because it also attributes leakage in LLM fine-tuning rather than reporting one scalar. However it attributes leakage to which CLIENT contributed data in a federated setting, an attribution along the data-provenance axis; the candidate attributes realized exposure to which adaptation PARAMETER SUBSPACE (full-FT weights vs LoRA factors vs soft-prompt rows) carried it, via a restoration test with Shapley additivity over parameter partitions. The claim stands because the two attributions answer different questions (who supplied the leaking data vs which adaptation mechanism encoded it), and FedAttr provides no per-mechanism parameter-subspace decomposition, so it neither subsumes nor is subsumed by the candidate.","addressable_via":"differentiation_from_lit already separates the axes (parameter-subspace attribution vs client-provenance attribution); adding FedAttr as an explicit non-overlapping comparison sharpens but does not require a mechanism change."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Mechanism-Attributed Privacy Auditing: Decomposing LLM Adaptation Leakage by Parameter Subspace\n\n**Method.** Mechanism-Attributed Privacy Auditing (MAPA)\n\n## Motivation\nPeople routinely take a big pretrained language model and adapt it to their own private data, using one of a few methods: full fine-tuning (updating all the weights), LoRA (Low-Rank Adaptation, which adds a small number of trainable factors), or soft-prompt / prefix tuning (learning a few extra input vectors). Afterwards they want to know how much of that private data the adapted model can leak. Today's best tools answer with a single number. Canary-injection auditing plants known secret phrases in the training data, then checks how easily they can be pulled back out, and reports one overall 'leakage' score for the whole model. That single number is computed on the finished model and cannot tell you where the leakage came from.\n\nThis is a real problem because the way you adapt the model is itself a leakage source. Recent work (the 'Janus' attack) shows that the fine-tuning step can resurface private information the base model had basically forgotten, and another study shows these leakage scores jump around a lot depending on incidental settings. So two adaptations that happen to land on the same leakage number can actually be carrying that risk in very different places — a handful of LoRA factors, a few soft-prompt vectors, or spread across all the weights — and current audits call them equally private.\n\nWhat is missing is a way to assign the measured leakage to the specific part of the adaptation that produced it. We propose building the secret-phrase probes so their leakage is sensitive to one adaptation method, and then splitting the measured leakage across the trainable parts of the model so the pieces add back up to the total. When this gap closes, you can compare adaptation choices on measured-leakage grounds and aim any fix at the exact part of the model that is leaking, instead of staring at one undifferentiated number.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n\n1. Plant N=1000 known secret phrases (called canaries) into the adaptation data, each built from the same fixed carrier sentence with a high-entropy random secret inside it (for example 'The access code for <NAME> is <SECRET>', where <SECRET> is 10 tokens drawn uniformly at random from the model's vocabulary), and insert each secret exactly once. Keep a small pilot slice (10% of the canaries) completely out of training, to serve later as a comparison group when scoring how exposed a secret is. Using one fixed sentence shape for every canary keeps the secrets directly comparable across every adaptation method, since only the random secret part differs.\n   - _Why_: You can only measure leakage cleanly if you know exactly which secrets you put in.\n2. Run the real adaptation on the planted data (the clean corpus plus the targeted canaries from the previous step) under each method — full fine-tuning, LoRA, and soft-prompt — for the fixed number of steps, to get the actual models you want to audit (one per method). The audit must run on these genuine adapted models, not on a stand-in.\n   - _Why_: The audit has to run on the genuine adapted model, not a stand-in.\n3. Measure how exposed each canary is under the adapted model. Compute its exposure E as a secret-sharer score: rank the canary's secret against a reference group of secrets that were never inserted (the pilot slice from step 1, built from the same sentence shape and same kind of random secret), ranking by how likely the model thinks each secret is, then turn that rank into the exposure number E = log2(group size) - log2(rank). Average E over all inserted canaries to get the model's overall leakage — this is the same total leakage number prior audits report, and the total you will later split up.\n   - _Why_: This is the same overall leakage number prior audits report — the total you will later split up.\n\n### Mechanism-Targeted Probes\n*Build canaries whose leakage is sensitive to one specific adaptation mechanism.*\n\n4. Do a short trial adaptation under each method (full fine-tuning, LoRA — Low-Rank Adaptation, soft-prompt) on a separate held-out slice of the in-domain data with no canaries in it, running it for the same number of steps the real adaptation will later use, and repeat over 5 random seeds. Look at how the trainable parameters moved inside that method's own parameter region $U_{m}$ — the full weight space for full fine-tuning, the space spanned by the per-layer LoRA factor products for LoRA, the learned prompt vectors for soft-prompt — average that movement across the 5 seeds, and boil it down to a single unit-length direction $d_{m}.$ For full fine-tuning specifically you must decide how to summarize the movement. 【author decision: for full fine-tuning, use the single average update direction (simple, but may be diffuse) or the top few principal directions of the updates (sharper, but adds a 'how many directions' setting).】\n   - _Why_: Each method nudges a different part of the model; capturing that direction tells you what to aim the probes at.\n5. Make a pool of M=200 candidate canaries for each method you want to target, and for each one measure how well its base-model gradient lines up with the method's update direction $d_{m}$ — this is the alignment score s(c), the base model's gradient for that canary projected into the method's parameter region and compared against $d_{m}.$ Then improve each canary by changing its secret tokens to push that alignment up, using a greedy one-token-at-a-time substitution (at each position swap in the token the gradient says will raise the alignment most) for up to 20 rounds, while a contrastive objective (with a softness setting of 0.1 and the other candidates in the batch as the 'not-this-one' comparisons) keeps the chosen canary clearly separated from the rest. Keep the best-aligned canaries, so you end up with secrets whose leakage will be sensitive to that specific method rather than just being generally memorable.\n\n*The contrastive probe objective whose positive score s(c) aligns a canary's base-model gradient, projected onto the adaptation subspace $U_{m},$ with the mechanism's mean update direction $d_{m}$; $\\tau $ is the temperature.*\n$$ \\mathcal{L}_{\\text{probe}}(c) = -\\log \\frac{\\exp(s(c)/\\tau)}{\\exp(s(c)/\\tau) + \\sum_{c'} \\exp(s(c')/\\tau)}, \\quad s(c) = \\langle P_{U_m}\\, \\nabla_\\theta \\ell(\\theta_0, c),\\, d_m \\rangle \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A probe aimed at the method reveals that method's leakage far better than a generic memorable string.\n\n### Attributed-Leakage Decomposition\n*Split measured exposure across trainable-parameter groups with a recomposition guarantee.*\n\n6. Split the trainable parameters into natural groups defined by the method itself: for LoRA, one group per layer's factor block; for soft-prompt, one group per prompt token's row; for full fine-tuning, one group per layer's weight block. Grouping along the method's own parameters is what makes the later attribution about the mechanism, not an arbitrary slice of the model.\n   - _Why_: Grouping along the method's own parameters is what makes the attribution about the mechanism, not an arbitrary slice.\n7. For each group of parameters, reset just that group back to its base-model values while leaving the rest of the adaptation in place, then re-measure exposure; the drop tells you how much that group contributed. To make this fair across groups, do it under 200 randomly shuffled reset orders: for each order, reset the groups one by one in that order and record exposure after each, so you capture each group's effect both alone and on top of others. Each re-measurement is just a forward pass (no retraining). Turning off one group while holding everything else fixed isolates that group's share of the leakage.\n\n*The marginal attributed leakage of partition S is the average drop in canary exposure E when partition S of the trained parameters is restored to its base value.*\n$$ A_S = \\mathbb{E}_{c}\\big[\\, E(\\theta_m) - E(\\theta_{m,-S}) \\,\\big] \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Turning off one part while holding everything else fixed isolates that part's share of the leakage.\n8. Average each group's drops over the different reset orders (a Shapley average) so the contribution $A_{S}$ assigned to each group is order-fair, then check that all the contributions add back up to the total leakage (the difference between the adapted and base models). Report how far off that add-up is, as a fraction of the total, and accept the breakdown only when the gap is at most 5%; if it is larger, increase the number of reset orders. The result is a per-group leakage breakdown together with its measured add-up error, so the 'it recomposes to the total' guarantee is something you can verify, not just assume.\n\n*The Shapley efficiency property: the per-partition attributed leakages sum exactly to the total exposure gap between the adapted and base models, giving the recomposition bound.*\n$$ \\sum_{S} A_S = E(\\theta_m) - E(\\theta_0) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Order-fair averaging plus the add-up check gives a decomposition you can trust, not ad-hoc bookkeeping.\n\n### Attribution Comparison\n*Show equal-scalar adaptations have different attribution and that targeting is load-bearing.*\n\n9. Take two adaptations and tune them — by adjusting how many training steps each gets, the knob least tied to any one method — until they reach the same overall leakage score (within 2%), then show their per-group contribution vectors are genuinely different: measure the difference as the cosine distance between the two normalized contribution vectors and back it with a significance test that resamples the canaries (report both the size of the difference and the p-value), rather than just eyeballing it. As a check, redo the whole thing with plain random-token canaries (not targeted at any method) and confirm the per-group contributions blur out — proving the targeting is what makes the breakdown sharp.\n   - _Why_: Equal total but different breakdown is the whole point; the random-canary check proves the targeting is what makes the breakdown sharp.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 面向适配机制的隐私审计：按参数子空间分解大语言模型微调的隐私泄漏\n\n**方法名称.** Mechanism-Attributed Privacy Auditing (MAPA)\n\n## 研究动机\n现在人们经常拿一个大的预训练语言模型，用自己的私有数据去适配它，常见方式有几种：full fine-tuning（更新全部权重）、LoRA（Low-Rank Adaptation，只新增一小批可训练因子）、以及 soft-prompt / prefix tuning（学习若干额外的输入向量）。之后大家想知道：适配后的模型会泄漏多少私有数据？目前最好的工具只能给出一个数字。canary 注入式审计会在训练数据里埋入已知的秘密短语，再检查它们能被多容易地提取出来，最后对整个模型给出一个总的“泄漏”分数。但这个分数是在最终模型上算出来的，无法告诉你泄漏到底来自哪里。\n\n这是个实际问题，因为“你用哪种方式适配”本身就是一个泄漏来源。最近的工作（Janus 攻击）表明，微调这一步会让基础模型本已“遗忘”的隐私信息重新浮现；另一项研究则显示这些泄漏分数会因为无关的设置而大幅波动。于是，两个恰好得到相同泄漏分数的适配，其风险可能藏在完全不同的地方——可能是几组 LoRA 因子、几条 soft-prompt 向量，或是散布在所有权重里——而现有审计会把它们判为同样安全。\n\n缺的，是一种把“测到的泄漏”归因到“产生它的那部分适配”的方法。我们的做法是：把秘密短语探针构造得对某一种适配机制特别敏感，再把测得的泄漏在模型的可训练部分之间拆开，使各部分之和正好等于总量。补上这个空缺后，你就能在“实测泄漏”的层面比较不同适配方案，并把修复手段精确地对准真正在泄漏的那部分模型，而不再只盯着一个笼统的数字。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景\n\n1. 在适配数据里埋入 N=1000 条已知的秘密短语（称为 canary），每条都用同一个固定的载体句子加一段高熵随机秘密构成（例如『The access code for <NAME> is <SECRET>』，其中 <SECRET> 是从模型词表里均匀随机抽取的 10 个 token），并且每条秘密只插入一次（这是更保守的单次插入审计默认做法）。另外留出一小份 pilot 数据（占 canary 总数的 10%）完全不参与训练，留作之后给秘密暴露度打分时的对照组（reference cohort）。所有 canary 都用同一个句子形态，可以让这些秘密在每种适配方法下都直接可比，因为只有随机的秘密部分在变。\n   - _为什么_: 只有清楚知道自己放进了哪些秘密，才能干净地测量泄漏。\n2. 在埋好秘密的数据（干净语料加上上一步得到的定向 canary）上，按每种方法——full fine-tuning、LoRA、soft-prompt——做固定步数的真正适配，得到要审计的实际模型（每种方法一个）。审计必须跑在这些真正的适配模型上，而不是替身。\n   - _为什么_: 审计必须跑在真正的适配模型上，而不是替身。\n3. 测量每条 canary 在适配后模型上的暴露程度。把它的暴露度 E 算成一个 secret-sharer 分数：将该 canary 的秘密与一组从未被插入的秘密（第 1 步留出的 pilot 数据，用同样的句子形态、同样的随机秘密构成）做排名，按模型认为每个秘密有多可能来排，再把名次换算成暴露数 E = log2(对照组大小) - log2(名次)。对所有被插入的 canary 取平均得到该模型的总体泄漏——这正是以往审计报告的那个总泄漏数字，也就是稍后要拆开的总量。\n   - _为什么_: 这正是以往审计报告的那个总体泄漏数字——也就是稍后要拆开的总量。\n\n### 面向机制的探针\n*构造对某一特定适配机制敏感的 canary。*\n\n4. 在每种方法（full fine-tuning、LoRA（Low-Rank Adaptation，低秩适配）、soft-prompt）下，用一份单独留出的、不含 canary 的同域数据做一次简短的试跑适配，跑的步数与之后真正适配相同，并在 5 个随机种子上重复。观察可训练参数在该方法自身的参数区域 $U_{m}$ 内的移动方式——full fine-tuning 是整个权重空间，LoRA 是各层因子乘积 B*A 张成的空间，soft-prompt 是学到的提示向量行——把这种移动在 5 个种子上做平均，再归一化成一个单位长度的方向向量 $d_{m}$。其中 full fine-tuning 需要专门决定如何概括这种移动。【作者需决定：full fine-tuning 的定向粒度——用单一的平均更新方向（简单，但可能弥散），还是用更新量的前若干个主方向（更锐利，但要多一个『取几个方向』的设定）。】\n   - _为什么_: 每种方法都在推动模型的不同部位，抓住这个方向就知道该把探针对准哪里。\n5. 为每个想要定向的方法准备 M=200 条候选 canary，对每条都测量它在基础模型上的梯度与该方法更新方向 $d_{m}$ 的对齐程度——这就是对齐得分 s(c)，即把该 canary 在基础模型上的梯度投影到该方法的参数区域后，再与 $d_{m}$ 做内积。然后通过逐个 token 的贪心替换来改进每条 canary（在每个位置换上梯度显示最能提升对齐度的那个 token），最多做 20 轮，同时用一个对比式目标（软度系数取 0.1，并把同批次中的其他候选当作『非此条』的对照）让选中的 canary 与其余明显区分开。保留对齐最好的那些 canary，于是得到的秘密其泄漏会对这个特定方法敏感，而不只是『普遍容易被记住』。\n\n*对比式探针目标：正样本得分 s(c) 将候选 canary 在基础模型上的梯度投影到适配子空间 $U_{m}$ 后，与该机制的平均更新方向 $d_{m}$ 对齐；$\\tau $ 为温度系数。*\n$$ \\mathcal{L}_{\\text{probe}}(c) = -\\log \\frac{\\exp(s(c)/\\tau)}{\\exp(s(c)/\\tau) + \\sum_{c'} \\exp(s(c')/\\tau)}, \\quad s(c) = \\langle P_{U_m}\\, \\nabla_\\theta \\ell(\\theta_0, c),\\, d_m \\rangle \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 针对某方法定制的探针，比一条泛泛的好记字符串能更好地暴露该方法的泄漏。\n\n### 泄漏归因分解\n*把测得的暴露度在可训练参数分组间拆分，并保证能相加还原。*\n\n6. 把可训练参数切成由方法本身定义的自然分组：LoRA 按每层的因子块各成一组、soft-prompt 按每个提示 token 的行各成一组、full fine-tuning 按每层的权重块各成一组。沿着方法自身的参数来分组，才能让后续的归因是『关于机制的』，而不是对模型的任意切片。\n   - _为什么_: 沿着方法自身的参数来分组，归因才是“关于机制的”，而不是任意切片。\n7. 对每个参数分组，只把该分组还原回基础模型取值、其余适配保持不变，再重新测暴露度；下降量就反映该分组贡献了多少泄漏。为了让各分组之间公平，要在 200 个随机打乱的还原顺序下重复进行：对每个顺序，按该顺序逐个还原各分组并在每步后记录暴露度，从而既能捕捉每个分组单独的效果，也能捕捉它叠加在其他分组之上的效果。每次重新测量只是一次前向计算（不需要重新训练）。在其余部分固定的情况下只关掉一个分组，就能孤立出这部分在泄漏中所占的份额。\n\n*分区 S 的边际归因泄漏 $A_{S}$：当把已训练参数的分区 S 还原为基础模型取值后，canary 暴露度 E 的平均下降量。*\n$$ A_S = \\mathbb{E}_{c}\\big[\\, E(\\theta_m) - E(\\theta_{m,-S}) \\,\\big] \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 在其余部分固定的情况下只关掉一部分，就能孤立出这部分在泄漏中所占的份额。\n8. 对每个分组在不同还原顺序下的下降量取平均（Shapley 平均），使分配给每个分组的贡献 $A_{S}$ 在顺序上是公平的，然后检查所有贡献相加是否等于总泄漏（适配模型与基础模型之差）。报告这个相加结果与总量的偏差占比，只有当偏差不超过 5% 时才接受该分解；若更大，就增加还原顺序的数量。最终得到的是一个按分组的泄漏分解，并附带实测的相加误差，使『能相加还原到总量』这一保证是可验证的，而不只是假设。\n\n*Shapley 可加性（efficiency）：各分区的归因泄漏之和恰好等于适配模型与基础模型之间的总暴露差，从而给出可重构性保证。*\n$$ \\sum_{S} A_S = E(\\theta_m) - E(\\theta_0) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 顺序公平的平均加上“能相加还原”的校验，给出的是可信赖的分解，而非临时记账。\n\n### 归因对比\n*展示总量相同的适配其归因不同，且“定向”是关键。*\n\n9. 取两个适配，通过调整各自的训练步数（这是与任何单一方法关联最弱的旋钮）把它们调到相同的总体泄漏分数（相差不超过 2%），然后展示它们的分组贡献向量确实不同：用两个归一化贡献向量之间的余弦距离来度量差异，并配一个对 canary 重采样的显著性检验来佐证（同时报告差异大小和 p 值），而不是仅凭肉眼比较。作为对照，用普通随机 token 的 canary（不针对任何方法）把整个流程重做一遍，确认分组贡献会变得模糊——以此证明正是『定向』让分解变得清晰。\n   - _为什么_: 总量相同但分解不同正是核心；随机 canary 对照证明了正是“定向”让分解变得清晰。\n\n"},{"id":"11","run_dir":"run_prompt11_deception","index":11,"title":"Knowing-Falsehood Diagnosis: A Counterfactual Knowledge-Contradiction Test for Benign-Prompt Deception","title_zh":"明知falsehood诊断：面向良性prompt欺骗的反事实知识矛盾检验","method_name":"Knowing-Falsehood Diagnosis (KFD)","hook":"On a benign prompt a deliberate falsehood and an honest error produce the identical wrong answer, so every honesty benchmark scores them the same; we show the two are separable per-prompt by a counterfactual test — only when the model is independently certified to KNOW the answer AND a single residual-stream suppression direction, when removed, restores that known answer does the falsehood qualify as a knowing misrepresentation.","anchor_pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","anchor_pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","domain_category":"LLM Alignment, Safety & Behavior","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a PER-PROMPT signal, on a benign prompt with no inducement, that the model had internal access to the correct answer at generation time yet emitted a contradicting one — i.e. nothing isolates knowing-misrepresentation from honest-error on a single unmanipulated input (additive; sits at the residual of the behavioral-benchmark leaves W4399912633 / W4403799392 and the induced-representation leaf W4416134237, none of which condition deception on an established knowledge b","pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by constructing matched per-prompt instances in which the confound (the model not-knowing) is structurally blocked via an independently-certified knowledge floor, then reporting the divergence between apparent falsehood rate and counterfactually-de-confounded knowing-falsehood rate as the headline — a confound-isolating instrument whose oracle (the certified known answer) is independent of the benign-prompt response under test.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether an EXTERNAL INDUCEMENT (coercive/role prompt, trained-in attack, game payoff, or leading request) is necessary for the deception signal to be valid, rather than assumed — every leaf that reads an internal deception direction (W4416134237) or a behavioral lie (07ada... , W4415300695) first installs an inducement and treats its presence as the operative label, so the question of whether the same internal evidence of deliberateness can be elicited and certified WITHO","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by relocating the deception-detection locus: the assumed locus is the inducement context (coercive/role prompt, trained-in attack, game payoff) whose presence is the label; we re-anchor the signal to an overlooked internal locus — a residual-stream answer-suppression direction whose causal effect on the known answer is observable on benign, un-induced prompts — and show the inducement was never necessary for a certifiable deliberateness signal, validated by restoration/detection performance rather than a tighter proof.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"LLM alignment / honesty — diagnosing deceptive behavior on benign (non-adversarial) prompts","n_papers":41,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":27},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":16,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"What Should a Robot Do? Comparing Human and Large Language Model Recommendations for Robot Deception"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"HonestLLM: Toward an Honest and Helpful Large Language Model"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"HoneyGPT: Breaking the Trilemma in Terminal Honeypots with Large Language Model"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Developing an Anti -Phishing Large Language Model: A Focus Group Study on Human, Technological, and Legal Factors"},{"source":"openalex","title":"BeHonest: Benchmarking Honesty in Large Language Models"},{"source":"openalex","title":"AI Alignment through Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback? Contradictions and Limitations"}],"more":10},{"year":2025,"n":24,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Mix Data or Merge Models? Balancing the Helpfulness, Honesty, and Harmlessness of Large Language Model via Model Merging"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Synthesizing Deception: Countering Large Language Model-Generated Phishing Campaigns through Adaptive Semantic Anomaly Detection"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Generative AI-Driven Cybersecurity Deception: A Brief Survey of Large Language Model Based Honeypots"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Compromising Honesty and Harmlessness in Language Models via Deception Attacks"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Conversational Guide for Cataract Surgery Complications: A Comparative Study of Surgeons versus Large Language Model-Based Chatbot Generated Instructions for Patient Interaction"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"LLMHoney: A Real-Time SSH Honeypot with Large Language Model-Driven Dynamic Response Generation"}],"more":18},{"year":2026,"n":1,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"}],"more":0}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":14,"share":0.341},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":7,"share":0.171},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":5,"share":0.122},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":2,"share":0.049},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":2,"share":0.049},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":2,"share":0.049},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":1,"share":0.024}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"On benign prompts the field cannot separate a KNOWING misrepresentation from an HONEST error, because every retrieved measurement of deception either (a) induces the deceptive behavior with adversarial machinery whose presence is itself the label — coercive/role prompts and externally-set goals in When Thinking LLMs Lie (openalex:W4416134237) and in the deception-attack fine-tuning of Compromising Honesty and Harmlessness (semanticscholar:07ada048aee47c913229f6f050a94b51c3c5ed1b), or game-theoretic asymmetric-information setups in The Traitors (semanticscholar:cbc66b7815da8a0e67b42568df0fde83c35e1936) and Spontaneous Rational Deception (openalex:W4417224698) — or (b) scores honesty purely behaviorally over aggregated benchmark items (BeHonest, openalex:W4399912633; the honesty survey, openalex:W4403799392) so that on any single benign prompt a falsehood and a sincere mistake produce the identical observable output. The consequence is that the quantity a benign-prompt diagnostic actually needs — evidence that, at generation time on THIS prompt, the model had internal access to the correct answer yet emitted a contradicting one — is never isolated: behavioral scores conflate it with not-knowing, and representation-engineering deception vectors are only validated against externally-imposed deception, so neither establishes that a benign-prompt falsehood was produced against the model's own internally-available knowledge rather than from absence of that knowledge.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416134237","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"When Thinking LLMs Lie extracts 'deception vectors' via Linear Artificial Tomography on activations and uses them to induce/detect/control strategic deception in CoT reasoning models. Its method (per its Method section) operationalizes deception by FIRST inducing it with specialized prompt templates (coercive circumstances / open-role deception) and then reading the steering direction — so the vector is calibrated to externally-elicited deception and the paper never establishes whether the same direction fires on a benign prompt that carries no inducement, nor does it certify that the contradicted answer was one the model actually knew; it presupposes deception rather than detecting it against a knowledge baseline."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:07ada048aee47c913229f6f050a94b51c3c5ed1b","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Compromising Honesty and Harmlessness introduces 'deception attacks' that fine-tune a model on misleading items so it lies on targeted topics while staying accurate elsewhere. The deceptive behavior exists only because it was trained in, and the label is the attack itself; it offers no signal for an off-the-shelf model that was never attacked, and cannot say whether an unprompted falsehood reflects retained knowledge or a genuine gap."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4399912633","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"BeHonest benchmarks honesty across behavioral axes (self-knowledge, non-deceptiveness, consistency) by scoring model outputs against references over many items. Because it is purely output-level and aggregated, on any individual benign prompt it cannot distinguish a deliberate falsehood from a sincere error, and provides no per-prompt internal evidence of knowing."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415300695","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"When helpfulness backfires shows LLMs comply with illogical medical requests and produce false statements they 'have the knowledge to detect', i.e. sycophancy as knowing-falsehood. But it triggers the behavior with leading/illogical prompts (a mild inducement) in one narrow domain and measures it behaviorally via compliance rate; it neither generalizes to neutral benign prompts nor reads any internal knowing-vs-not-knowing signal at generation time."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"LLM alignment / honesty — diagnosing deceptive behavior on benign (non-adversarial) prompts","venue":"ICLR 2026 (area: investigating LLM deception on benign prompts; primary_area: alignment, fairness, safety, privacy)","time":"2026","data":["open-weight instruction-tuned chat models (e.g. Llama-3, Qwen, Mistral) where activations + logits are accessible","factual QA / advice prompts with verifiable ground truth where the model is independently shown to KNOW the correct answer","everyday benign user prompts (information requests, recommendations) with no jailbreak, role-play, coercion, or explicit incentive to lie"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (approx 90 A100-day) [inferred default]","expertise":"interpretability + LLM evaluation","preference":"both","baseline":"behavioral honesty benchmarks (BeHonest W4399912633), confidence-calibration probes (W4407039591), and induced-deception representation methods (deception vectors, When Thinking LLMs Lie W4416134237)","limitation":"Existing deception studies elicit deception under adversarial pressure (deception attacks, coercive prompts, signaling games, goal-driven CoT) and cannot tell, on a benign prompt where no such pressure exists, whether a wrong/misleading answer is a knowing misrepresentation (deception) or an honest error (hallucination / capability limit).","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["compute","expertise","preference","data","baseline","limitation"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared audit lens is 'does a certifiable deliberateness signal require an inducement, or does it live at an internal locus observable on benign prompts?', and the central computable object both legs read from is the per-prompt Knowing-Falsehood test built from three quantities. (1) Knowledge floor K(p): for a factual/advice prompt p with verifiable answer a*, independently certify that the model knows a* by neutral elicitation under N>=8 semantically-equivalent paraphrasings issued in a separate, inducement-free context (different system prompt, no reference to the benign prompt) and scoring agreement against a* with an external checker; K(p)=1 iff the model returns a* in >= tau_K (default 0.75) of paraphrases AND its mean verbalized/probabilistic confidence on a* exceeds the median over a calibration set — K is a model-internal-plus-external readout, NOT the benign response, so it is the independent oracle. (2) Benign response r(p): the model's answer to the single neutral benign prompt p (no role-play, coercion, payoff, or leading framing); the item enters the diagnostic only when K(p)=1 and r(p) contradicts a* (an apparent falsehood on a known item). (3) Suppression direction d_L and the Counterfactual Knowledge-Contradiction Margin CKM(p): on the K(p)=1, contradicting items, fit a single linear direction d_L in the residual stream at a selected layer set L (chosen by sweeping layers and picking the one maximizing held-out restoration; d_L estimated by difference-in-means between hidden states on contradicting-known items vs honest-true items, a Linear-Artificial-Tomography-style readout) such that projecting OUT d_L (activation edit h -> h - (h . d_hat) d_hat at layers L on a second forward pass) and regenerating yields r'(p); CKM(p) = 1[r'(p) == a*] i.e. the known answer is causally restored by removing d_L. The headline metric Knowing-Falsehood Rate KFR = fraction of certified-known contradicting items with CKM(p)=1 (deliberate: the model held the answer and a suppression component was diverting it) versus Honest-Error Rate = certified-NOT-known contradicting items, where the same edit does NOT restore a* because a* was never internally available. Leg-1 (C02) is the instrument: the matched instance set (known-vs-not-known, holding prompt benignity and topic fixed) plus the K-oracle independent of r isolates knowing-misrepresentation from honest-error, which behavioral benchmarks (W4399912633) cannot. Leg-2 (C01) is the locus pivot validated through that same instrument: by certifying d_L and its restoration effect on benign, un-induced prompts, we demonstrate the inducement assumed necessary by W4416134237 (which fits its deception vector only after coercive/open-role induction) and W4415300695 (leading prompts) is not required for a deliberateness signal. The free indices are fixed/given selection rules: tau_K=0.75, N=8 paraphrases, L chosen by held-out restoration sweep, and the single bridging hyperparameter is the edit scale alpha on h - alpha (h . d_hat) d_hat (default alpha=1, full projection); no quantity is left for the reader to guess.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The two gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules: the C01 locus-pivot's validation IS the C02 instrument run on benign prompts, so they read the same central object (the K-conditioned counterfactual), which is why coherence_thread_type=shared_audit fits and a single core_mechanism serves both. I considered a separate behavioral-only leg for gap 2 (compare benign vs induced deception rates) but rejected it because it would re-introduce an inducement to label deception — exactly the assumption gap 2 audits — collapsing the contribution; the internal-locus restoration test avoids that. Per the method_lineage REGRESSION FLAG, I avoided reducing the signal to node n1 (a confidence/uncertainty/calibration estimate, which would conflate knowing-lie with honest-belief) and to node c0 (a pure belief-probe that reports 'knows X' but not the deliberate-contradiction counterfactual): CKM's load-bearing artifact is a CAUSAL restoration of the known answer, not a confidence score and not a static probe readout, so it lands on a tree node the frontier does not yet occupy.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on an open-weight instruction-tuned model (e.g. Llama-3-8B-Instruct, Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) over a benign factual set where each item's answer is independently certified KNOWN via the paraphrase floor, take the subset where the neutral benign response contradicts the known answer and measure the Knowing-Falsehood Rate (KFR) = fraction whose known answer is causally restored by projecting out the suppression direction d_L. If the candidate works, KFR on certified-KNOWN contradicting items is substantially and significantly above the restoration rate on certified-NOT-KNOWN (honest-error) contradicting items — i.e. the same edit restores truth far more often when the model demonstrably knew the answer, a per-prompt separation no behavioral benchmark produces. The load-bearing variable is the projection magnitude (h . d_hat) of the residual stream onto the suppression direction d_L; negative control: replace d_hat with a random unit direction (or a direction fit on permuted KNOWN/NOT-KNOWN labels) at the same layers and edit scale and regenerate — the predicted effect is that the downstream restoration rate (the honest-answer recovery rate, the task-outcome metric, NOT the projection value itself) collapses back to the unedited baseline, showing it is specifically d_L, not generic activation perturbation, that carries the knowing-misrepresentation signal. A positive control thresholding only (h . d_hat) to predict which contradicting-KNOWN items are restorable should recover most of the KFR-vs-error AUROC, converting the falsifier into a constructive identification of the suppression direction as the mechanism.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416134237","delta":"They fit a deception 'steering' direction only AFTER inducing deception via coercive/open-role prompt templates and validate it by its ability to steer behavior; we fit a suppression direction conditioned on an independently-certified knowledge floor on benign un-induced prompts and validate it by causal restoration of the known answer, producing a per-prompt knowing-vs-error verdict their steering-validated vector cannot."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4399912633","delta":"BeHonest scores honesty behaviorally over aggregated items so a falsehood and an honest error are indistinguishable; we construct matched known-vs-not-known instances with a knowledge-floor oracle independent of the response, yielding a per-prompt Knowing-Falsehood Rate that an aggregate behavioral benchmark structurally cannot compute."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415300695","delta":"They elicit knowing-falsehoods with leading/illogical medical prompts (a mild inducement) and measure compliance rate in one domain; we require neutral benign prompts and read an internal causal-restoration signal, removing both the inducement and the domain narrowness while adding the honest-error counterfactual control they lack."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:07ada048aee47c913229f6f050a94b51c3c5ed1b","delta":"Their deception attack TRAINS in the dishonest behavior so the label is the attack itself; we detect deliberateness in an unmodified off-the-shelf model with no training intervention, conditioned on certified prior knowledge of the answer."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4416134237","what_step_was_missed":"When Thinking LLMs Lie constructs a linear deception direction from activations but only after externally inducing the deceptive behavior, and validates the direction by steering, not by a counterfactual on the model's own established knowledge. To already be our contribution it would have needed to (a) construct an independent per-prompt knowledge-floor oracle that certifies the model knew the contradicted answer absent any inducement, and (b) define the direction's validity by whether projecting it out causally RESTORES that certified-known answer on a benign prompt — a knowledge-conditioned restoration construction it never builds, leaving 'the model knew and chose otherwise' an interpretation rather than a tested per-prompt quantity."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":120,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"No hard floor fires (gap_closure_reject_check has no yes-match; anti_pattern matched_pattern_id is null; the paper_pointed_threat W7155451575 is competing, not exact-mechanism overlap). But the C01 gap_closure entry is borderline on the lesson 'Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work ... collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured', and paper_pointed_threat.addressable_via names a specific candidate field (differentiation_from_lit) — a load-bearing novelty-boundary concern — so the verdict is revise: add an explicit, measured differentiation against the Shared Sycophancy-Lying Circuit.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a PER-PROMPT signal, on a benign prompt with no inducement, that the model had internal access to the correct answer at generation time yet emitted a contradicting one — i.e. nothing isolates knowing-misrepresentation from honest-error on a single unmanipulated input (additive; sits at the residual of the behavioral-benchmark leaves W4399912633 / W4403799392 and the induced-representation leaf W4416134237, none of which condition deception on an established knowledge baseline).","main_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail most often when the instrument isolates the confound only inside an artificial regime and never shows the signal transfers to real deployment, or when the diagnostic is circular (validated against the same definition/population it interrogates), or when it merely re-derives an already-documented limitation.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A diagnostic that only re-confirms a shortcut already known in advance, surfacing no previously unmeasurable failure, is read as confirmatory rather than as a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The per-prompt Knowing-Falsehood Rate (knowing-lie vs honest-error separation conditioned on a certified knowledge floor) is a previously-unmeasurable quantity; behavioral benchmarks cannot compute it, so it is not confirmatory."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a synthetic-ground-truth instrument only on synthetic data, without demonstrating that the controlled finding transfers to real-world instances, leaves ecological validity unestablished and undermines the central claim.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"core_mechanism_steps step 11 includes a held-out realistic benign-deployment-log transfer, so the concern is addressed in design, but only as one step — the ecological-validity claim rests on that transfer actually holding."},{"lesson_quoted":"Building the instrument around one contested definition of the target property means it cannot independently confirm that the definition is correct, and reviewers flag the resulting circularity.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The oracle (knowledge floor K via independent paraphrase elicitation + external checker) is independent of the benign response under test, so the instrument is not validated against the population it judges."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pairing a single-task or small-sample instrument with broad capability claims triggers a scope-mismatch rejection.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Claims are scoped to per-prompt knowing-vs-error on factual/advice items where an answer is verifiable, not a broad 'LLMs are deceptive' claim."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether an EXTERNAL INDUCEMENT (coercive/role prompt, trained-in attack, game payoff, or leading request) is necessary for the deception signal to be valid, rather than assumed — every leaf that reads an internal deception direction (W4416134237) or a behavioral lie (07ada... , W4415300695) first installs an inducement and treats its presence as the operative label, so the question of whether the same internal evidence of deliberateness can be elicited and certified WITHOUT any inducement is never asked (subtractive; the shared ancestor every leaf inherits is 'deception is studied by first making the model deceive').","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is a relocation demonstrated but not adversarially closed, a novelty-boundary collapse where the 'new' locus was already used by prior work, reintroducing the dissolved assumption via a clean reference model, or offering a demonstration with no mechanistic account of why the locus carries the signal.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work — normalization statistics, activation-similarity losses, semantic concept triggers — collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The collision hit W7155451575 (Shared Sycophancy-Lying Circuit) already reads an internal 'this statement is wrong' signal and silences it, so the internal-locus move is partly occupied; the candidate's distinction (knowledge-floor-certified restoration on neutral un-induced prompts vs their pressure/instructed-lying setting) is real but must be made explicit and measured."},{"lesson_quoted":"A defense whose relocation silently depends on a clean reference model or a known anomaly distribution reintroduces precisely the strong assumption the move was supposed to eliminate.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The method uses no clean reference model; the knowledge floor is the same model under neutral elicitation, and the deliberateness signal is a within-model counterfactual."},{"lesson_quoted":"Demonstrating the new locus only on fixed, non-adaptive or outdated baselines while omitting any account of why it works reads as a stacked pipeline of existing components rather than a principled shift.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism gives a mechanistic account (restoration of the certified-known answer under projection-out) plus a positive control isolating the load-bearing projection, not a bare demonstration."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No Reject lesson is a yes-match, so no hard floor. The C01 entry drives a borderline via 'Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work ... collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured' — the just-retrieved W7155451575 occupies the internal-wrongness-signal locus, so the candidate's distinction must be sharpened. The C02 entry is borderline only on ecological validity, already covered by the realistic-transfer step."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a PER-PROMPT signal, on a benign prompt with no inducement, that the model had internal access to the correct answer at generation time yet emitted a contradicting one — i.e. nothing isolates knowing-misrepresentation from honest-error on a single unmanipulated input (additive; sits at the residual of the behavioral-benchmark leaves W4399912633 / W4403799392 and the induced-representation leaf W4416134237, none of which condition deception on an established knowledge baseline).","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Construct a controlled instance set in which exactly one named confound is structurally blocked or independently varied, paired with an oracle independent of the system under test, and report the divergence between apparent and de-confounded performance as the headline.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism explicitly names the confound (the model not-knowing) and blocks it by partitioning items via the independently-certified knowledge floor K(p) (oracle independent of the benign response r), then reports KFR (de-confounded knowing-falsehood rate) vs the honest-error restoration rate as the headline divergence (steps 2-3, 8). This is the C02 signature move, not the parent's generic 'build a diagnostic'.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether an EXTERNAL INDUCEMENT (coercive/role prompt, trained-in attack, game payoff, or leading request) is necessary for the deception signal to be valid, rather than assumed — every leaf that reads an internal deception direction (W4416134237) or a behavioral lie (07ada... , W4415300695) first installs an inducement and treats its presence as the operative label, so the question of whether the same internal evidence of deliberateness can be elicited and certified WITHOUT any inducement is never asked (subtractive; the shared ancestor every leaf inherits is 'deception is studied by first making the model deceive').","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Relocate the attack/defense signal from the assumed representational locus to an overlooked locus the field treated as irrelevant, and supply a mechanistic account of why the property must manifest there too — validated by detection performance, not tighter analysis.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism re-anchors the deception signal from the assumed locus (the inducement context whose presence is the label) to an internal residual-stream suppression direction d_L observable on benign un-induced prompts, and gives the mechanistic account (projecting d_L out causally restores the certified-known answer). This performs the C01 locus-relocation move, not merely the parent's generic 'audit an assumption'.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries perform their cited cluster's signature operation: C02's confound-block-plus-independent-oracle-divergence and C01's locus relocation with a mechanistic account are each concretely instantiated in core_mechanism, so neither is bypassed."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["controlled_diagnostic_design","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented anti-pattern compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as a component; the candidate's set {controlled_diagnostic_design, assumption_audit_and_pivot} contains no such pairing, so no anti-pattern matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"openalex:W7155451575","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"The Shared Sycophancy-Lying Circuit shows a small set of attention heads carries a 'this statement is wrong' signal whose silencing flips sycophantic agreement while leaving factual accuracy intact, establishing that an internal signal distinguishes knowing-agreement-with-a-falsehood from not-knowing — which overlaps the candidate's core claim that an internal locus separates knowing-misrepresentation from honest-error. The candidate's claim stands or falls on whether its contribution survives this: it does, because (1) their setting requires a user-asserted false belief to agree with (sycophancy) or instructed/factual lying — an inducement/leading frame — whereas the candidate's instrument operates on NEUTRAL benign prompts with no belief to defer to; (2) their 'wrongness' signal is read on the claim, not certified against an independent per-prompt knowledge floor establishing the model KNEW the specific answer; (3) their deliverable is a circuit-level deference-vs-knowledge dissociation, not a per-prompt counterfactual-restoration Knowing-Falsehood Rate. The candidate is therefore competing-but-not-subsumed, and must measure the difference explicitly.","addressable_via":"Strengthen differentiation_from_lit with an explicit entry against W7155451575 naming the benign-vs-pressured setting difference, the knowledge-floor certification their wrongness-signal lacks, and the per-prompt restoration metric vs their circuit-level deference finding."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat (openalex:W7155451575, Shared Sycophancy-Lying Circuit) occupies the internal-wrongness-signal locus; C01 gap_closure_reject borderline lesson on novelty-boundary collapse unless the difference is made explicit and measured.","fix_direction":"Add one differentiation_from_lit entry with paper_id openalex:W7155451575 whose delta states substantively: they read a 'this statement is wrong' attention-head signal under user-pressure/sycophancy and instructed/factual lying and show silencing it flips deference while leaving accuracy intact (a circuit-level deference-vs-knowledge dissociation); we instead operate on NEUTRAL benign prompts with no false belief to defer to, certify per-prompt via an independent knowledge floor that the model KNEW the specific answer, and define the signal by counterfactual restoration of that certified-known answer (a per-prompt Knowing-Falsehood Rate), none of which their circuit-level result produces. Do not modify kill-switch fields (falsification_prediction, compute_budget)."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit[4].delta","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added an explicit differentiation_from_lit entry against openalex:W7155451575 (Shared Sycophancy-Lying Circuit), stating the benign-vs-pressured setting difference, the independent knowledge-floor certification their wrongness-signal lacks, and the per-prompt counterfactual-restoration metric vs their circuit-level deference-vs-knowledge dissociation."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Knowing-Falsehood Diagnosis: A Counterfactual Knowledge-Contradiction Test for Benign-Prompt Deception\n\n**Method.** Knowing-Falsehood Diagnosis (KFD)\n\n## Motivation\nThe user wants to study whether large language models (LLMs) lie on benign prompts — ordinary, neutral questions with no trick, role-play, threat, reward, or leading wording pushing the model to lie. The hard part is this: on such a question, a model that deliberately lies and a model that honestly gets it wrong type out the exact same wrong answer. So any method that only looks at the output cannot tell deliberate lying apart from an honest mistake. What you really need is per-prompt evidence that, right when it answered THIS question, the model actually had the correct answer available inside it but said something else instead.\n\nNo existing work supplies that. One group of methods scores honesty by comparing outputs to reference answers across many items — for example BeHonest (a behavioral honesty benchmark, openalex:W4399912633). Because it only looks at outputs and averages over items, on any single benign question it cannot separate a deliberate falsehood from a sincere error. A second group reads an internal 'deception direction' from the model's activations, but only AFTER forcing the model to lie: When Thinking LLMs Lie (openalex:W4416134237) first uses coercive or role-play prompts to make the model deceive, then reads the direction and checks it by steering behavior. The deception-attack work (semanticscholar:07ada048...) trains the lying in, so the attack itself is the label. When helpfulness backfires (openalex:W4415300695) gets the model to state things it could detect are false, but only with leading medical prompts in one narrow area.\n\nThe common thread is that everyone studies deception by first INSTALLING a reason to deceive, and nobody first establishes what the model actually knew. So 'the model knew and chose to lie' stays a guess, never a measured fact. Now is the right time to fix this: open-weight chat models (Llama-3, Qwen, Mistral) let us read and edit activations layer by layer, and the activation-direction tools already exist — they just have never been pointed at neutral prompts and checked against an independent record of what the model knew.\n\nIf we close this gap, a per-prompt 'Knowing-Falsehood Rate' becomes measurable: on neutral prompts, we can finally report what fraction of a model's wrong answers were said against its own available correct answer rather than out of ignorance. That turns 'it knew and chose otherwise' from an opinion into a tested counterfactual and gives existing honesty benchmarks a knowledge-aware signal they cannot compute on their own.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n\n1. Build a set of neutral, everyday factual/advice questions (trivia, drug-equivalence, geography). For each, store the correct answer a* together with a list of acceptable aliases (synonyms, equivalent phrasings). Build an automatic checker that first tries to match the model's answer to the canonical answer or an alias after light cleanup (lowercasing, dropping punctuation and articles, standardizing units); if that fails, it asks a separate strong language model 'does this answer state the same fact as the gold answer? yes/no' (a Natural Language Inference, NLI, style judgment). Make sure no question contains role-play, threats, rewards, or leading wording.\n   - _Why_: You can only detect a deliberate lie on a benign prompt if the prompt itself contains no pressure to lie and you know the true answer.\n\n### Knowledge-Floor Certification\n*Independently certify, per prompt, whether the model actually knows the answer, building an oracle separate from the response under test.*\n\n2. For each question, ask the same thing 8 different ways (rephrased question, fill-in-the-blank, multiple-choice with the right answer among distractors, true/false) in a SEPARATE neutral context — a different plain system prompt with no link to the benign question. Keep only paraphrases where the gold answer a* is still the single correct one (checked with the same yes/no entailment judge from Step 1). Measure two confidences: a probability score (how much probability mass the model puts on the correct answer, length-normalized and averaged over the 8 forms) and a self-reported 0-100 confidence (divided by 100). Mark the item KNOWN if it gives the correct answer at least 75% of the time AND its average confidence beats the median confidence on a 200-item reference subset; otherwise NOT-KNOWN.\n\n*The knowledge floor K(p) is 1 when, over N neutral paraphrases $y_{i},$ the agreement rate with the verified answer a* meets threshold $\\tau _{K}$ AND the mean confidence $\\bar{c}(p)$ exceeds the calibration-set median; K is read in an inducement-free context, independent of the benign response.*\n$$ K(p) = \\mathbb{1}\\!\\left[\\frac{1}{N}\\sum_{i=1}^{N}\\mathrm{check}\\big(y_i,\\,a^{*}\\big) \\ge \\tau_K \\ \\wedge\\ \\bar{c}(p) > \\mathrm{med}(c)\\right] \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This builds an independent record of what the model actually knows, kept separate from the answer under test, so 'it didn't know' can be ruled out.\n3. Now ask the single neutral question once and record the model's answer r(p). Keep only the cases where the answer is wrong (the checker returns false). Split these into wrong-but-KNOWN (the model was certified to know the answer — suspected deliberate falsehoods) and wrong-and-NOT-KNOWN (honest-error controls).\n   - _Why_: The honest-error group is the comparison that lets you tell whether a wrong answer came from lying or from not knowing.\n\n### Suppression-Direction Fitting\n*Fit and layer-select a single residual-stream direction that distinguishes provably-known falsehoods from honest-true generations.*\n\n4. Run the model on each wrong-answer case and save its internal activations — the residual-stream hidden state at every layer, taken at the positions of the answer tokens it generated, then averaged over those positions to one vector per layer. Do this for both the wrong-but-KNOWN cases and the honest-error controls.\n   - _Why_: The deliberate-lie signal, if it exists, lives inside these activations on the neutral prompt — not in any outside pressure.\n5. At each layer compute one direction $d_{L}:$ the average activation on wrong-but-KNOWN cases minus the average activation when the SAME items are forced to emit their known-correct answer. Using the same items for both sides means only one thing differs — whether the model is suppressing or stating the answer it knew — so the subtraction points along the 'suppression' direction.\n\n*The suppression direction $d_{L}$ at layer set L is the difference-in-means of residual-stream states $h_{L}$ between contradicting-KNOWN items 𝒦 and honest-true generations $\\mathcal{H} $ — a Linear-Artificial-Tomography-style readout, fit only on certified-known items.*\n$$ d_L = \\frac{1}{|\\mathcal{K}|}\\sum_{p\\in\\mathcal{K}} h_L(p) \\;-\\; \\frac{1}{|\\mathcal{H}|}\\sum_{p\\in\\mathcal{H}} h_L(p) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Subtracting the 'honest-true' activations isolates the component that points toward suppressing the answer the model knew.\n6. On a held-out split, decide which layer (or small band of layers) to edit. Try each single layer and bands of width 1, 3, and 5 layers; for each choice, do the editing of Step 7 and see how often it restores the correct answer; keep the choice that restores most often. If you pick a band, edit every layer in it, each with its own direction turned into a unit vector $\\hat{d}.$\n   - _Why_: Choosing the layer by a held-out rule (not by hand) keeps the test honest and reproducible.\n\n### Counterfactual Restoration & Scoring\n*Causally remove the direction to test whether the known answer is restored, then report the de-confounded Knowing-Falsehood Rate.*\n\n7. On a second pass, subtract the suppression component from each hidden state (h $\\leftarrow  h -  \\alpha (h\\cdot \\hat{d})\\hat{d},$ default scale $\\alpha =1)$ at the chosen layers, at every token position, and regenerate with greedy decoding so the result is deterministic. If the regenerated answer now matches the known-correct answer a*, mark this case as restored (CKM(p)=1).\n\n*The counterfactual edit projects the suppression component out of each residual-stream state h at layers L on a second forward pass, with scale $\\alpha $ (default 1, full projection) and unit direction $\\hat{d}.$*\n$$ h \\leftarrow h - \\alpha\\,(h\\cdot\\hat{d})\\,\\hat{d}, \\qquad \\hat{d}=d_L/\\lVert d_L\\rVert \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: If removing one internal direction flips a wrong answer back to the known-correct one, that is direct causal evidence the model was suppressing what it knew.\n8. Compute the Knowing-Falsehood Rate (KFR) — the fraction of wrong-but-KNOWN cases that the edit restored — and the same restoration fraction for the honest-error controls. Report the gap between how often answers merely look wrong and how often they are wrong while provably known and restorable; that gap is the deliberate-deception signal.\n\n*The Knowing-Falsehood Rate KFR is the fraction of certified-known contradicting items whose Counterfactual Knowledge-Contradiction Margin CKM(p) is 1, i.e. whose known answer a* is causally restored in the post-edit regeneration r'(p).*\n$$ \\mathrm{KFR} = \\frac{1}{|\\mathcal{K}|}\\sum_{p\\in\\mathcal{K}} \\mathrm{CKM}(p), \\qquad \\mathrm{CKM}(p)=\\mathbb{1}\\!\\left[\\mathrm{check}\\big(r'(p),\\,a^{*}\\big)\\right] \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The gap between 'looks wrong' and 'wrong while provably knowing and restorable' is exactly the deliberate-deception signal no benchmark can produce.\n\n### Controls & Ecological Transfer\n*Falsify with random-direction and projection-only controls and show the signal survives on real benign deployment prompts.*\n\n9. As a sanity check, redo the edit using a random direction (drawn uniformly on the unit sphere, a fresh one per layer) at the same strength, and average over at least 20 random tries. Also redo it with a direction fit on shuffled KNOWN/NOT-KNOWN labels, over at least 20 shuffles. If a random or shuffled direction restores answers just as often as no edit at all, the effect was generic; if it doesn't, the specific suppression direction is what carries the signal.\n   - _Why_: If a random direction restores answers just as well, the effect was generic noise; if it doesn't, the specific direction $\\hat{d}$ is what carries the signal.\n10. Without doing any editing, just measure how strongly each wrong-but-KNOWN case's activation lines up with the suppression direction (the projection value), and use that single number to predict which cases the edit would restore. Measure how well that prediction agrees with the actual edit outcome (an AUROC, area under the curve). If one number already predicts deliberateness well, it confirms the suppression direction itself — not the editing trick — is the mechanism.\n   - _Why_: If one number already predicts deliberateness, it confirms the suppression direction is the actual mechanism, not an artifact of the edit.\n11. Repeat the whole knowledge-floor-and-restoration pipeline on a held-out log of real, un-induced user questions whose answers can be verified (for example a filtered slice of open chat/assistant logs, or a Natural-Questions-style set kept to checkable facts), and compare the Knowing-Falsehood Rate there to the synthetic set. 【author decision: which real-log corpus to use is the authors' call, because what counts as 'benign deployment' depends on the target application and whether its true answers can be certified.】\n   - _Why_: Showing the signal survives on real benign prompts proves the finding is not an artifact of the constructed test set.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 明知falsehood诊断：面向良性prompt欺骗的反事实知识矛盾检验\n\n**方法名称.** Knowing-Falsehood Diagnosis (KFD)\n\n## 研究动机\n用户想研究大型语言模型 (LLM) 是否会在良性 prompt 上撒谎——也就是普通、中性的问题，没有任何诱骗、角色扮演、威胁、奖励或引导性措辞去逼模型撒谎。难点在于：面对这种问题，一个故意撒谎的模型和一个诚实地答错的模型，打出来的错误答案一模一样。所以只看输出的方法，无法把故意撒谎和诚实犯错区分开。真正需要的是逐个 prompt 的证据：在回答这个问题的那一刻，模型其实内部已经掌握了正确答案，却说出了相反的内容。\n\n现有工作都给不出这种证据。一类方法用参考答案在很多条目上打分来衡量诚实度，比如 BeHonest（一个行为层面的诚实度 benchmark，openalex:W4399912633）。由于只看输出并在条目间求平均，它在任何单个良性问题上都无法把故意falsehood和真诚错误分开。第二类方法从模型激活中读取一个内部“欺骗方向”，但都是在先让模型撒谎之后：When Thinking LLMs Lie（openalex:W4416134237）先用胁迫式或角色扮演 prompt 诱导模型欺骗，再读取方向，并用 steering 行为来验证。deception-attack 工作（semanticscholar:07ada048...）则把撒谎训练进去，于是攻击本身就是标签。When helpfulness backfires（openalex:W4415300695）让模型说出它本可识别为假的内容，但只用了狭窄医学领域里的引导性 prompt。\n\n共同的套路是：大家都先“安装”一个撒谎的理由再研究欺骗，没人先确定模型究竟知道什么。于是“模型知道却选择撒谎”始终是猜测，而非测得的事实。现在正是解决它的时机：开源 chat 模型（Llama-3、Qwen、Mistral）允许逐层读取和编辑激活，激活方向工具也已成熟——只是从未对准过中性 prompt，也从未对照一份独立的“模型知道什么”的记录来检验。\n\n若补上这个缺口，一个逐 prompt 的“明知falsehood率”就变得可测：在中性 prompt 上，我们终于能报告模型的错误答案中、有多少是违背其自身已掌握的正确答案说出的，而非源于无知。这把“它知道却选择了别的”从观点变成可检验的反事实，并给现有诚实度 benchmark 提供它们自身算不出的、知识感知的信号。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景\n\n1. 构建一组中性的日常事实/建议类问题（trivia、药物等效、地理）。每题把正确答案 a* 连同一份可接受别名列表（同义词、等价表述）一起存好。再构建一个自动 checker：先做轻量清洗（小写化、去标点与冠词、统一单位）后，把模型答案与标准答案或别名匹配；若匹配失败，就调用一个独立的强语言模型，问『这个答案是否陈述了与标准答案相同的事实？是/否』（一种自然语言推理(Natural Language Inference, NLI)式判断）。务必确保任何问题都不含角色扮演、威胁、奖励或引导性措辞。\n   - _为什么_: 只有当 prompt 本身不含撒谎压力、且你知道真答案时，才可能在良性 prompt 上检测出故意撒谎。\n\n### 知识 Floor 认证\n*逐 prompt 独立认证模型是否真的知道答案，构建一个与被测回答分离的 oracle。*\n\n2. 对每题，在一个单独的中性上下文里（不同的朴素 system prompt、与良性问题无关联）用 8 种不同说法问同一件事（改写问句、填空、把正确答案混在干扰项里的多选、是非判断）。只保留那些标准答案 a* 仍是唯一正确答案的改写（用第 1 步同一个『是/否』蕴含判断器核验）。测两种置信度：一个是概率分数（模型在正确答案上分配的概率质量，按长度归一化并在 8 种说法上取平均），另一个是 0-100 的自报置信度（除以 100）。若模型至少 75% 的时候给出正确答案，且其平均置信度高于一个 200 题参照子集上的中位置信度，则标为 KNOWN，否则 NOT-KNOWN。\n\n*知识floor K(p) 取 1 当且仅当：在 N 个中性paraphrase $y_{i}$ 上与已验证答案 a* 的一致率达到阈值 $\\tau _{K}$，且平均置信度 $\\bar{c}(p)$ 超过校准集中位数；K 在无诱导上下文中读取，独立于良性回答。*\n$$ K(p) = \\mathbb{1}\\!\\left[\\frac{1}{N}\\sum_{i=1}^{N}\\mathrm{check}\\big(y_i,\\,a^{*}\\big) \\ge \\tau_K \\ \\wedge\\ \\bar{c}(p) > \\mathrm{med}(c)\\right] \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这建立了一份独立的“模型究竟知道什么”的记录，与被测回答分开，从而能排除“它本就不知道”。\n3. 现在把这个中性问题问一次，记录模型的回答 r(p)。只保留答错的情形（checker 返回 false）。把它们分成『答错但 KNOWN』（模型已被认证知道答案——疑似故意falsehood）和『答错且 NOT-KNOWN』（诚实错误对照）。\n   - _为什么_: 诚实错误这一组是关键对照，让你能判断一个错误答案来自撒谎还是来自不知道。\n\n### 抑制方向拟合\n*拟合并选层出单一 residual-stream 方向，区分可证明已知的 falsehood 与诚实正确生成。*\n\n4. 在每个答错情形上运行模型，保存其内部激活——每一层、在它生成的答案 token 位置上的 residual-stream 隐状态，再在这些位置上取平均，得到每层一个向量。对『答错但 KNOWN』情形和诚实错误对照都这样做。\n   - _为什么_: 故意撒谎的信号（若存在）就藏在中性 prompt 下的这些激活里，而非任何外部压力中。\n5. 在每一层计算一个方向 $d_{L}$：用『答错但 KNOWN』情形的平均激活，减去当这些相同条目被强制输出其已知正确答案时的平均激活。两侧用相同条目，意味着只有一件事不同——模型是在抑制还是在陈述它知道的答案——因此这个相减就指向『抑制』方向。\n\n*层集合 L 上的抑制方向 $d_{L}$ 为残差流状态 $h_{L}$ 在矛盾且已知项集合 𝒦 与诚实正确生成集合 $\\mathcal{H} $ 之间的均值差，是一种 Linear Artificial Tomography 式读出，仅在认证已知项上拟合。*\n$$ d_L = \\frac{1}{|\\mathcal{K}|}\\sum_{p\\in\\mathcal{K}} h_L(p) \\;-\\; \\frac{1}{|\\mathcal{H}|}\\sum_{p\\in\\mathcal{H}} h_L(p) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 减去“诚实正确”激活，可分离出指向“抑制模型已知答案”的那一分量。\n6. 在留出集上决定编辑哪一层（或一小段连续层）。逐个试每一层，以及宽度为 1、3、5 的层段；对每种选择执行第 7 步的编辑，看它多频繁地恢复正确答案；保留恢复最频繁的那个选择。若选了一段，就编辑其中每一层，各用自己的方向归一化成单位向量 $\\hat{d}$。\n   - _为什么_: 用留出规则（而非手工）选层，保证检验诚实且可复现。\n\n### 反事实恢复与计分\n*causally 移除该方向以检验已知答案是否被恢复，再报告去混淆的明知falsehood率。*\n\n7. 在第二次前向传播中，于所选层、在每个 token 位置，从每个隐状态减去抑制分量（$h \\leftarrow  h -  \\alpha (h\\cdot \\hat{d})\\hat{d}$，默认缩放 $\\alpha =1$），并用贪心解码重生成，使结果确定。若重生成的答案此时与已知正确答案 a* 一致，就把该情形标记为已恢复（CKM(p)=1）。\n\n*反事实编辑在第二次前向传播中、于层 L 处将抑制分量从每个残差流状态 h 中投影移除，缩放系数 $\\alpha $（默认 1，完全投影），单位方向 $\\hat{d}$。*\n$$ h \\leftarrow h - \\alpha\\,(h\\cdot\\hat{d})\\,\\hat{d}, \\qquad \\hat{d}=d_L/\\lVert d_L\\rVert \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 若移除一个内部方向就能把错误答案翻回已知正确答案，这就是模型在抑制其所知的直接 causal 证据。\n8. 计算明知falsehood率（KFR）——『答错但 KNOWN』情形中被编辑恢复的比例——以及诚实错误对照的同一恢复比例。报告『答案看起来错』与『在可证明已知且可恢复的情况下错』之间的差距；这个差距就是故意欺骗信号。\n\n*明知falsehood率 KFR 是认证已知且矛盾的项中、其反事实知识矛盾边际 CKM(p) 为 1 的比例，即编辑后重生成 r'(p) causally 恢复了已知答案 a* 的比例。*\n$$ \\mathrm{KFR} = \\frac{1}{|\\mathcal{K}|}\\sum_{p\\in\\mathcal{K}} \\mathrm{CKM}(p), \\qquad \\mathrm{CKM}(p)=\\mathbb{1}\\!\\left[\\mathrm{check}\\big(r'(p),\\,a^{*}\\big)\\right] \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: “看起来错”与“在可证明已知且可恢复的情况下错”之间的差距，正是任何 benchmark 都给不出的故意欺骗信号。\n\n### 对照与生态迁移\n*用随机方向与仅投影对照进行证伪，并证明信号在真实良性部署 prompt 上依然成立。*\n\n9. 作为对照检验，用随机方向（在单位球面上均匀采样，每层一个新方向）以相同强度重做编辑，并在至少 20 次随机尝试上取平均。再用在打乱 KNOWN/NOT-KNOWN 标签上拟合的方向重做，至少 20 次打乱。若随机或打乱方向恢复答案的频率与完全不编辑一样高，则效应是通用的；若不是，则特定抑制方向才是信号载体。\n   - _为什么_: 若随机方向同样能恢复答案，说明效应只是通用噪声；若不能，则特定方向 $\\hat{d}$ 才是信号载体。\n10. 完全不做编辑，只测量每个『答错但 KNOWN』情形的激活与抑制方向的吻合强度（投影值），并用这一个数值预测哪些情形会被编辑恢复。测量该预测与实际编辑结果的吻合度（AUROC，曲线下面积）。若一个数值已能很好地预测故意性，就证实抑制方向本身——而非编辑技巧——是机制。\n   - _为什么_: 若一个数值已能预测故意性，就证实抑制方向是真正机制，而非编辑带来的假象。\n11. 在一份留出的、真实且无诱导、答案可核查的用户问题日志上（例如开放 chat/assistant 日志的过滤切片，或限定为可核查事实的 Natural Questions 式集合），重跑整套知识 floor 与恢复流程，并把那里的明知falsehood率与合成集对比。【作者需决定：用哪个真实日志语料由作者定夺，因为何谓『良性部署』取决于目标应用，以及其真答案能否被认证。】\n   - _为什么_: 证明信号在真实良性 prompt 上依然成立，就排除了它只是构造测试集的假象。\n\n"},{"id":"12","run_dir":"run_prompt12_biosignal","index":12,"title":"Pairing-Free Cross-Modal Biosignal Transfer via Marginal Physiological-Coordinate Transport","title_zh":"基于边缘生理坐标传输的免配对跨模态生物信号迁移","method_name":"Marginal Physiological-Coordinate Transport (MPCT)","hook":"Every recent unsupervised cross-modal biosignal-transfer method is advertised as label-free yet still secretly requires a synchronized (source, target) paired sub-dataset to fit its alignment; we show the cross-modal correspondence is recoverable, and causally certifiable, from the two modalities' MARGINAL distributions alone, with zero co-recorded pairs.","anchor_pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","anchor_pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","domain_category":"Healthcare & Scientific ML","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf achieves source-to-target biosignal transfer when NO synchronized cross-modal pairs are available at all — every frontier method (BioX-Bridge, Brant-X, SemiCMT, SAMBA) pins the cross-modal correspondence only where co-recorded pairs exist, so the unmet need is a transfer whose alignment force reaches the entirely-unpaired target distribution.","pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by reframing the unpaired cross-modal correspondence as an estimator over MARGINAL statistics on a learned shared physiological-coordinate manifold: an entropic optimal-transport coupling between the source and target marginal distributions of a label-free physiological coordinate, computed from each modality's own samples (no joint pairs), with fidelity bought by a single Sinkhorn compression and certified by causal intervention rather than by pair-matching loss.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions whether the cross-modal correspondence must be learned from instance-level co-occurrence at all — every leaf silently inherits, from a shared ancestor (paired cross-modal contrastive/distillation alignment), the assumption that two modalities can only be related through synchronized samples of the same event; none tests whether the relation could instead be established without any instance-level pairing.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","how_closed":"Framing half (C05): audit the load-bearing identifiability assumption that synchronized instance pairs are required to identify the cross-modal map, and pivot it to a structural substitute — that the shared physiological coordinate is recoverable up to a monotone-reparameterization equivalence class from the two marginals plus a known physiological-monotonicity anchor, proven sufficient ALONE; companion deliverable half (controlled_diagnostic_design): a confound-isolating instance set that empirically separates 'recovered the physiological state' from 'recovered a paired-context artifact', certifying the pivot is real.","is_anchor":false},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf certifies that what is transferred across modalities is the shared physiological state rather than a paired-recording-context artifact — the methods report downstream accuracy but none isolates whether the aligned direction is the modality-invariant physiological cause, leaving transfer success indistinguishable from correlation with a confound present in the paired set.","pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by constructing controlled biosignal instances that hold subject/session/sensor identity fixed while varying only the latent physiological state (and a matched set that varies recording context while freezing state), then reporting the divergence between transfer accuracy on the state-varying versus context-varying partitions as the primary result, with an oracle independent of the transferred model (planted physiological-state labels from a stimulus protocol).","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"unsupervised cross-modal knowledge transfer across biosignals (EEG, ECG, EMG, PPG, EOG, etc.)","n_papers":39,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":26},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":23,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"LaneCMKT: Boosting Monocular 3D Lane Detection with Cross-Modal Knowledge Transfer"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Source-Free Cross-Modal Knowledge Transfer by Unleashing the Potential of Task-Irrelevant Data"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"SemiCMT: Contrastive Cross-Modal Knowledge Transfer for IoT Sensing with Semi-Paired Multi-Modal Signals"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Utilization of transformer model in multimodal data fusion learning: Cross-modal knowledge transfer in the new generation learning space"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Temporal Order Preserved Optimal Transport-Based Cross-Modal Knowledge Transfer Learning for ASR"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Synthetic data generation methods in healthcare: A review on open-source tools and methods"}],"more":17},{"year":2025,"n":16,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"BioX-Bridge: Model Bridging for Unsupervised Cross-Modal Knowledge Transfer across Biosignals"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"3D Facial Tracking and User Authentication Through Lightweight Single-Ear Biosensors"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Cross-modal knowledge transfer for 3D point clouds via graph offset prediction"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"MCKTNet: Multiscale Cross-Modal Knowledge Transfer Network for Semantic Segmentation of Remote Sensing Images"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Self-Supervised Multimodal Large Model for Cross-Language and Cross-Modal Knowledge Transfer"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Lightweight Facial Landmark Detection in Thermal Images via Multi-Level Cross-Modal Knowledge Transfer"}],"more":10}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":11,"share":0.282},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":10,"share":0.256},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":8,"share":0.205},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":6,"share":0.154},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":6,"share":0.154},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":6,"share":0.154},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":2,"share":0.051},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":1,"share":0.026}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Across the recent unsupervised cross-modal biosignal-transfer frontier, the alignment between a data-rich source modality and a data-poor target modality is learned from a synchronized PAIRED sub-dataset of co-recorded (source, target) samples, and the transfer degrades exactly as that paired set shrinks or its recording context (subject, session, sensor, sampling rate) drifts from the target deployment. BioX-Bridge (semanticscholar:353bfd043a5151202b23c1e975caac608fd6dc6c) is framed as unsupervised yet its bridge is trained on a disjoint un-annotated PAIRED dataset D^(pair) of (x_old, x_new) to mimic the old-modality model's output; Brant-X (openalex:W4401863532) likewise depends on simultaneously-collected EEG-plus-other-signal recordings and a single privileged EEG source, and SemiCMT (semanticscholar:54a7f65258d13c20acdc2065c2649c7d9aef2847) explicitly anchors its embedding symmetry on a small set of synchronized multi-modal pairs. The structural failure is that the alignment objective only constrains source and target representations where co-occurring pairs exist, so when the target modality is collected from different subjects/sessions/sensors than any paired exemplar, the learned correspondence has no force on the unpaired target distribution and the transferred decision boundary drifts — and none of the current machinery can certify that what crossed the bridge is the shared physiological state rather than a paired-set-specific recording artifact.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:353bfd043a5151202b23c1e975caac608fd6dc6c","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"BioX-Bridge trains a lightweight low-rank+prototype bridge to project a new modality's intermediate representation onto an old-modality foundation model so the old task head can run on the new modality, cutting trainable params 88-99%. Its method (Sec 3.1) still requires a disjoint un-annotated PAIRED dataset D^(pair) of co-recorded (old, new) samples to fit the bridge and selects alignment positions to mimic old-model outputs on those pairs, so it cannot transfer when no synchronized cross-modal pairs are collectible and it never tests whether the bridged representation encodes the shared physiological state versus a correlate specific to the paired recording context."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4401863532","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Brant-X transfers an EEG foundation model's knowledge to other physiological signals via two-level (sample- and semantic-scale) alignment and reports SOTA across sleep/emotion/gait tasks. It depends on simultaneously-collected EEG+other-signal data to learn the alignment and privileges one fixed source (EEG), so it does not handle modality pairs that are never co-recorded and cannot route knowledge when the abundant modality is not EEG."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:54a7f65258d13c20acdc2065c2649c7d9aef2847","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"SemiCMT factorizes each modality's embedding into shared/private parts and enforces structural-correlation symmetry using a small set of synchronized pairs, transferring feature-extraction capability from a data-rich to a data-poor sensing modality. The symmetry constraint is anchored on the synchronized pairs, so the learned target embedding geometry is only pinned where pairs exist and the method gives no guarantee on unpaired target samples drawn from a shifted subject/session distribution."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4403519940","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Modal-nexus (Monae) integrates and imputes UNPAIRED multi-modality single-cell data by contrastive learning inside modality-specific autoencoders that share a unified space, leveraging regulatory relationships between modalities. Its unpaired alignment leans on omics-specific regulatory priors and an assumption of shared cell-type cluster structure, neither of which transfers to biosignals where the shared latent is a continuous physiological state, not a discrete cell type, so the mechanism that lets it skip pairs does not port to this domain."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"unsupervised cross-modal knowledge transfer across biosignals (EEG, ECG, EMG, PPG, EOG, etc.)","venue":"ICLR 2026","time":"2026","data":["public biosignal corpora with partial modality overlap (e.g. sleep PSG with EEG+ECG+EOG+EMG, wearable PPG+ECG, BCI EEG+EMG)","large single-modality unlabeled biosignal pools (one modality abundant, the target modality scarce and unpaired)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with physiological-signal background","preference":"both","baseline":"BioX-Bridge (model bridging via paired prototype alignment); Brant-X (EEG-foundation-model two-level alignment); SemiCMT (semi-paired contrastive transfer)","limitation":"current unsupervised cross-modal transfer methods still require a synchronized paired sub-dataset of the source and target modalities to learn the alignment, which is exactly the data that is hardest to collect across biosignals (different sensors, sessions, sampling rates, subjects)","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared question all three legs attack is: can a cross-modal biosignal correspondence be established AND certified without any synchronized instance pairs? Leg 1 (anchor, C00) reframes the correspondence as a measurement over marginals. We first learn a per-modality encoder f_m mapping raw windows of modality m to a low-dimensional latent z (dim d=16, trained by within-modality masked-reconstruction SSL, no cross-modal signal). We then estimate, for each modality independently, the push-forward MARGINAL distribution P_m = f_m#(data_m) over a scalar physiological coordinate u_m = h_m(z) in [0,1], where h_m is a 1-Lipschitz monotone calibration head pinned by a physiological-monotonicity anchor a_m (a cheap, modality-local, label-free signal known to increase monotonically with the shared state — e.g. heart-rate-band power for ECG/PPG, spectral-edge frequency for EEG; the anchor is the ONLY domain input and is computed by a fixed DSP routine, not learned). The cross-modal map is then the entropic optimal-transport coupling T between the two 1-D marginals P_source(u) and P_target(u): T = argmin_pi <pi, C> + eps*H(pi) over couplings with the given marginals, C_ij = (u_source_i - u_target_j)^2, eps=0.05, solved by Sinkhorn (200 iters). Because both marginals live on the SAME anchored coordinate u, T is computable from each modality's own samples — there is never a joint sample. Transfer of the source task head g_source to the target modality is then: target prediction = g_source( barycentric-project target sample's u through T back to the source latent ). Leg 2 (sibling, C05+companion C02) supplies the theory the anchor leg needs: it audits the inherited identifiability assumption 'a paired set is required to identify the source->target map' (load-bearing because BioX-Bridge's proof of correspondence collapses without D^(pair)), and pivots it to the structural substitute condition: if u_source and u_target are both 1-Lipschitz-monotone in the SAME latent physiological state s (enforced by the anchor a_m), then the state is recoverable, and hence the cross-modal map identified, up to a single monotone reparameterization of u — a named equivalence class — from the two marginals ALONE. The companion controlled_diagnostic_design half ships the empirical separation that the proof's condition is real and not a paired-context artifact. Leg 3 (sibling, C02) is that diagnostic, instantiated standalone as the validity leg: controlled instances varying only state vs only context, with the apparent-versus-deconfounded transfer gap as the headline. Legs 1 and 2 share the central object (the anchored coordinate u and its marginals); leg 3 reuses leg 2's companion diagnostic as a first-class result, so the three legs are one paper: a constructive estimator (leg 1), the identifiability theorem that licenses it (leg 2), and the causal certification that it transferred the state not a confound (legs 2-3).","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) Legs 1 and 2 share machinery (the anchored coordinate u and its marginal push-forwards) because the estimator IS the operationalization of the identifiability theorem — the evidence is that C00's step 4-5 (compression + causal certification) and C05's step 5 (operationalize the theorem as an estimator and demonstrate recovery where the old assumption fails) describe the same artifact, so splitting them would duplicate the object. Leg 3's diagnostic is genuinely separable as a standalone validity result, but it is the same instrument C05's companion produces, so it is reused, not re-built. (b) Alternatives considered and rejected: (i) a CLIP-style cross-modal contrastive objective with model-output pseudo-pairs (C17 route) — rejected because pseudo-pairing reintroduces instance-level co-occurrence, regressing onto lineage node n2; (ii) adversarial marginal distribution-matching (CycleGAN-style) — rejected as a regression onto collateral node c1 (it matches marginals but gives no semantic/state correspondence and content-swaps); (iii) clustering on a shared discrete latent with regulatory priors (Monae route) — rejected as regression onto collateral node c2 because biosignal state is continuous, not a discrete cell type. The anchored monotone coordinate + 1-D OT is the source the tree does NOT occupy: it pins the correspondence by a physiological monotonicity structure, not by pairs (n2), not by raw marginal matching (c1), not by discrete clusters (c2).","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on a public multimodal corpus with overlapping labels across modalities (e.g. sleep PSG: train a sleep-stage head on EEG, transfer to ECG/EOG with NO co-recorded EEG-ECG windows used for alignment; or wearable PPG<->ECG arrhythmia), measure target-modality balanced accuracy as a function of the synchronized-pair fraction made available to baselines (BioX-Bridge, SemiCMT) versus our zero-pair method. If the candidate works, our transfer accuracy stays essentially flat as the available pair-fraction goes to 0 while the paired baselines' accuracy degrades toward chance as their pair-fraction shrinks, and our method matches the paired baselines at the baselines' full-pair operating point. The named load-bearing variable is the anchored physiological coordinate u (specifically the source-target marginal alignment it induces). Negative control: permute the monotone anchor a_target (randomly shuffle which DSP feature defines u_target so it no longer tracks the shared physiological state) and re-fit h_target; this should drive the DOWNSTREAM target-modality transfer accuracy back to chance even though the OT solver, encoders, and coupling cardinality are unchanged — proving the transfer rides on the physiological-coordinate alignment, not on the transport machinery. Positive control: a stripped-down model that uses ONLY the scalar coordinate u (a 1-D monotone map from target-u to source-u, no learned latent transport) should recover most of the transfer accuracy, constructively identifying u as the carrier.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:353bfd043a5151202b23c1e975caac608fd6dc6c","delta":"BioX-Bridge fits its bridge on a disjoint un-annotated PAIRED dataset D^(pair) of co-recorded (old,new) samples (method Sec 3.1); we construct the source->target map from each modality's MARGINAL coordinate distribution via 1-D entropic OT with zero joint samples, and prove identifiability up to a monotone reparameterization that their pair-mimicking objective neither needs nor establishes."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4401863532","delta":"Brant-X requires simultaneously-collected EEG+other-signal data and privileges EEG as the single source for its two-level alignment; we require neither co-recording nor a privileged source, deriving correspondence from a per-modality monotone physiological anchor computed independently in each modality."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:54a7f65258d13c20acdc2065c2649c7d9aef2847","delta":"SemiCMT anchors its shared/private embedding symmetry on a small set of synchronized pairs, leaving off-pair target geometry unpinned; we pin the entire target marginal through the anchored coordinate, so the alignment force reaches unpaired target samples, and we add a causal certification (state-vs-context partition gap) that SemiCMT does not report."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4403519940","delta":"Monae aligns unpaired single-cell modalities by contrastive learning around a shared DISCRETE cell-type structure plus omics regulatory priors; we align a CONTINUOUS physiological coordinate via OT on marginals with a domain-light DSP monotonicity anchor, and supply an identifiability theorem (recovery up to monotone reparameterization) rather than relying on cluster-structure assumptions."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:353bfd043a5151202b23c1e975caac608fd6dc6c","what_step_was_missed":"BioX-Bridge constructs the correspondence as an alignment of intermediate representations fit to MIMIC the old model's outputs on co-recorded pairs; to make the transfer pairing-free it would have needed to construct a label-free, modality-local physiological coordinate that renders the two modalities' MARGINAL distributions comparable on a common axis (and prove that the optimal-transport coupling between those marginals identifies the cross-modal state-correspondence up to a monotone reparameterization) — a marginal-coordinate construction plus its identifiability proof that their paired prototype-bridge does not produce."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":327,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"Layer 1 hard floor did not fire: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict=borderline (no entry triggered, all candidate_match are no/borderline), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id=null, and paper_pointed_threat is competitive but NOT exact-mechanism overlap (Scotd is discrete-omics OT translation without an identifiability guarantee). In Layer 2, recipe_application_check.verdict=applied across all three legs and the borderlines are not load-bearing structural defects in core_mechanism's central argument — they are honesty/scope concerns (the C05 'identifiability claim that outruns its proof' borderline and the C02 synthetic-to-real borderline) best surfaced into Phase 4 reviewer_concerns_and_responses, plus the addressable Scotd-differentiation point, none of which require rewriting a candidate field. Advance with these three concerns carried forward.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf achieves source-to-target biosignal transfer when NO synchronized cross-modal pairs are available at all — every frontier method (BioX-Bridge, Brant-X, SemiCMT, SAMBA) pins the cross-modal correspondence only where co-recorded pairs exist, so the unmet need is a transfer whose alignment force reaches the entirely-unpaired target distribution.","main_pattern":"reframe_as_solvable_object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The signature failure is treating the reframing as a mechanical wrapper: pointing an established estimation tool at a new domain without re-deriving why the resulting scores are faithful, supplying computation but not justification (no causal validation, only correlation), or under-specifying the object itself.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Pointing an off-the-shelf decomposition at a coarser input granularity without showing the coarser units preserve the signal reads as a wrapper, not a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate does not point an off-the-shelf tool at a coarser granularity; it constructs a new anchored physiological coordinate and proves (leg 2) the OT coupling over its marginals recovers the state-correspondence, with a causal negative control."},{"lesson_quoted":"Porting a known attribution technique to a new architecture or domain while ignoring that technique's documented failure modes — and omitting comparisons to alternatives — leaves reviewers unable to see any unique benefit.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"Entropic OT is a known tool ported to biosignals; the candidate must (and does, in differentiation_from_lit + falsification's pair-fraction sweep) compare against paired baselines and the unpaired-OT/Monae alternatives, but a reviewer could still ask whether 1-D OT on marginals is just a domain port — mitigated by the identifiability theorem that the ports lack."},{"lesson_quoted":"Conflating a methodological artifact — a computation-granularity difference, a degenerate zero baseline — with genuine signal undermines the entire premise once the confound is identified.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate's leg 3 diagnostic and the anchor-permutation negative control exist precisely to rule out that the transfer rides on an artifact (sensor/context) rather than the physiological coordinate."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions whether the cross-modal correspondence must be learned from instance-level co-occurrence at all — every leaf silently inherits, from a shared ancestor (paired cross-modal contrastive/distillation alignment), the assumption that two modalities can only be related through synchronized samples of the same event; none tests whether the relation could instead be established without any instance-level pairing.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The signature failure is an identifiability claim that outruns its proof: the pivoted assumption was not actually load-bearing, or recovery is asserted while the decisive object (latent identifiability, the equivalence class) is never established or the algorithm does not enforce the condition the theorem requires.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Stacking two established frameworks and re-proving identifiability of the union reads as incremental unless the pivoted assumption was genuinely load-bearing and the union admits a regime neither framework could reach alone.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The pivoted assumption (synchronized pairs required) is load-bearing — BioX-Bridge's fulltext shows its correspondence is defined on D^(pair) — and the pivot reaches the zero-pair regime no frontier method admits, not a union of two frameworks."},{"lesson_quoted":"Advertising an identifiability or 'consistency' property while the proof omits the decisive object — never proving latent identifiability, or excluding part of the model from the guarantee — collapses the contribution the moment a reviewer checks the theorem.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The candidate NAMES the equivalence class (recovery up to monotone reparameterization) and the substitute condition (joint 1-Lipschitz-monotonicity in shared state), but the full proof is asserted not written here; this is load-bearing and Phase 4 must keep the theorem statement honest (state the exact failure when monotonicity is violated), else it risks this lesson."},{"lesson_quoted":"Proving identifiability conditions the algorithm neither enforces nor verifies creates a theory-practice disconnect that undermines both the soundness and the significance of the claim.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The algorithm explicitly enforces the condition: the monotone calibration head h_m pinned to the DSP anchor a_m is exactly what makes u 1-Lipschitz-monotone in the shared state, so the estimator enforces the theorem's precondition by construction."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf certifies that what is transferred across modalities is the shared physiological state rather than a paired-recording-context artifact — the methods report downstream accuracy but none isolates whether the aligned direction is the modality-invariant physiological cause, leaving transfer success indistinguishable from correlation with a confound present in the paired set.","main_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail when the instrument isolates the confound only inside an artificial regime and never shows the signal transfers to real deployment, or are circular (validated against the same population/definition they interrogate), or merely re-confirm an already-known shortcut.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a synthetic-ground-truth instrument only on synthetic data, without demonstrating that the controlled finding transfers to real-world instances, leaves ecological validity unestablished and undermines the central claim.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The state/context partitions use a stimulus-protocol oracle that could read as semi-synthetic; the candidate must show the certified transfer holds on naturalistic held-out data too, or it risks the synthetic-to-real gap (surfaced for Phase 4)."},{"lesson_quoted":"Building the instrument around one contested definition of the target property means it cannot independently confirm that the definition is correct, and reviewers flag the resulting circularity.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Ground truth is the planted physiological state from an external stimulus protocol, independent of the transferred model, not the evaluand's own judgment, so the oracle is non-circular."},{"lesson_quoted":"A diagnostic that only re-confirms a shortcut already known in advance, surfacing no previously unmeasurable failure, is read as confirmatory rather than as a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The state-vs-context transfer gap is a previously-unmeasured quantity for cross-modal biosignal transfer — no frontier method reports whether what crossed is the state or a context artifact."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"All three gap_closure entries are borderline, none triggered. The anchor (reframe, C00) carries the 'domain-port of a known tool' borderline (lesson 2), mitigated by the identifiability theorem; the audit leg (C05) carries the 'identifiability claim that outruns its written proof' borderline, which is load-bearing and must be kept honest in Phase 4."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf achieves source-to-target biosignal transfer when NO synchronized cross-modal pairs are available at all — every frontier method (BioX-Bridge, Brant-X, SemiCMT, SAMBA) pins the cross-modal correspondence only where co-recorded pairs exist, so the unmet need is a transfer whose alignment force reaches the entirely-unpaired target distribution.","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"C00 recasts an opaque question as a concrete measurement over a well-studied object — including an expectation/estimator over MARGINAL statistics — constrained to the model's own learned geometry, with tractability bought by one compression trick and fidelity certified by a causal intervention rather than plausibility.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism leg 1 performs exactly this: it recasts the unpaired correspondence as an entropic-OT estimator over the two modalities' MARGINAL coordinate distributions on a learned shared physiological-coordinate manifold (the object), buys tractability with a single Sinkhorn compression, and certifies fidelity by the anchor-permutation causal negative control (step 10) — the cluster's signature 'estimator-over-marginals + causal certification' move.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions whether the cross-modal correspondence must be learned from instance-level co-occurrence at all — every leaf silently inherits, from a shared ancestor (paired cross-modal contrastive/distillation alignment), the assumption that two modalities can only be related through synchronized samples of the same event; none tests whether the relation could instead be established without any instance-level pairing.","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"C05 takes an existing identifiability/recovery theorem and trades a DISTRIBUTIONAL assumption (independence, parametric mixing, access to pairs/labels) for a STRUCTURAL/geometric one, re-proving recovery up to the field's standard ambiguity class, then operationalizing it as an estimator.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism leg 2 trades the distributional/access assumption 'synchronized instance pairs are required to identify the map' for the structural condition 'both coordinates are 1-Lipschitz-monotone in the same latent state' and re-proves recovery up to a monotone-reparameterization equivalence class, then operationalizes it as the calibration head + OT estimator — the cluster's signature distributional-to-structural swap with a named ambiguity class.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf certifies that what is transferred across modalities is the shared physiological state rather than a paired-recording-context artifact — the methods report downstream accuracy but none isolates whether the aligned direction is the modality-invariant physiological cause, leaving transfer success indistinguishable from correlation with a confound present in the paired set.","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"C02 constructs controlled instances in which exactly one named confound is structurally blocked or independently varied, with an oracle independent of the system under test, and reports the divergence between apparent and de-confounded performance as the primary result.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism leg 3 builds two partitions — one varying physiological state with subject/session/sensor frozen, one varying recording context with state frozen — with a stimulus-protocol oracle independent of the transferred model, and reports the state-vs-context transfer gap as the headline; this is exactly the cluster's controlled-instance + independent-oracle + report-the-divergence move.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"All three entries instantiate their cited cluster's signature move: estimator-over-marginals-with-causal-certification (C00), distributional-to-structural identifiability swap with a named ambiguity class (C05), and confound-isolating controlled instances with an independent oracle (C02). The companion controlled_diagnostic_design on the C05 leg is realized at the main-pattern level via the same partition diagnostic."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["reframe_as_solvable_object","assumption_audit_and_pivot","controlled_diagnostic_design"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"None of the three reject-favored compositions matches: all three require heterogeneous_decomposition as a component, which is absent from this candidate's composition_set."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"Scotd: Single-Cell Cross-Modality Translation for Unpaired Data Through Optimal Transport-Conditioned Diffusion","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"Scotd is the closest mechanism: it performs UNPAIRED cross-modality translation via optimal transport (OT-conditioned diffusion). If its OT coupling already aligns the modalities' continuous latent without pairs and transfers a downstream task, the candidate's 'OT over marginals, no pairs' core would be largely anticipated. However, Scotd operates on single-cell omics (where, like Monae, the shared structure is discrete cell-type clusters), couples full high-dimensional latents via a conditioned generative diffusion (translation, not task-head transfer), and provides no identifiability guarantee. The candidate stands on three points Scotd does not deliver: (1) the correspondence is reduced to a 1-D anchored physiological coordinate whose marginals are coupled, not a high-dim latent translation; (2) an identifiability theorem proving recovery up to monotone reparameterization from marginals + monotonicity anchor; (3) a causal certification (state-vs-context partition gap + anchor-permutation control) that the transferred direction is the physiological state. So the candidate's claim stands provided the headline is the identifiability-from-marginals result and the biosignal-continuous-state setting, not OT-for-unpaired-translation per se.","addressable_via":"Sharpen differentiation_from_lit and the core_claim to foreground the 1-D-anchored-coordinate identifiability theorem and continuous-physiological-state setting (versus Scotd's discrete-omics OT translation), so the contribution is not read as 'OT for unpaired cross-modal' in general."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Pairing-Free Cross-Modal Biosignal Transfer via Marginal Physiological-Coordinate Transport\n\n**Method.** Marginal Physiological-Coordinate Transport (MPCT)\n\n## Motivation\nThe goal is to take a model trained to read one kind of body signal — say EEG (brain electrical activity) where labeled data is plentiful — and reuse it on a different signal — say ECG (heart electrical activity) — without collecting labels for the second signal. Recent methods call themselves 'unsupervised' but hide a costly requirement: they need a set of recordings where BOTH signals were captured at the same time from the same person (synchronized pairs) in order to learn how the two signals correspond. Across body signals that paired data is the single hardest thing to gather, because different signals use different sensors, sessions, sampling rates, and subjects. BioX-Bridge fits its bridge on such a paired set, Brant-X needs simultaneously-recorded data and only works when the rich modality is EEG, and SemiCMT relies on a small synchronized-pair set. Because their alignment is learned only where pairs exist, it has no pull on target data that was never co-recorded, and none of them can tell whether the model transferred the real physiological state or just a quirk of the paired recordings. What is new: strong self-supervised encoders can now be trained on each signal alone, and entropic optimal transport (OT, a cheap, standard tool for matching two distributions) can align two signals using only the overall distribution of a single physiological summary number per signal — never a paired sample. We collapse each signal to one label-free 'physiological coordinate' u between 0 and 1, forced by a fixed signal-processing feature (e.g. heart-rate-band power) to rise with the body state, then match the two signals' distributions of u with OT. We can prove this recovers the true correspondence (up to a harmless monotone relabeling) and we can show, with a controlled experiment, that the model carried the physiological state and not a recording artifact. If this works, any data-poor body signal can borrow a trained model from any data-rich one using only its own unlabeled recordings, removing the dependence on the hardest-to-collect data.\n\n## Method\n### Per-modality coordinate construction\n*Collapse each signal to one label-free physiological coordinate with no cross-modal data.*\n\n1. Train one self-supervised encoder per signal using only that signal's own unlabeled recordings: cut each recording into fixed-length windows (about 30 seconds for sleep signals, 10 seconds for wearable heart signals), hide half of each window at random, and train a 1-D convolutional network to fill in the hidden parts (mean-squared-error loss). The trained, then frozen, network turns a window into a 16-number summary (the latent z). No data from the other signal is used here.\n   - _Why_: Learning each signal alone isolates all the cross-signal work into one small object, so no pairs are needed yet.\n2. For every window, compute one cheap, fixed signal-processing number $a_{m}$ that is known in advance to go up as the body state goes up: heart-rate-band power for heart signals (ECG/PPG), spectral-edge frequency (the frequency below which 95% of the power sits) for brain signals (EEG). This number is calculated by a fixed formula, not learned, and is the only piece of domain knowledge the method uses. 【author decision: for any signal outside electroencephalography (EEG), electrocardiography (ECG), and photoplethysmography (PPG), which fixed signal-processing number serves as the up-with-state proxy — e.g. the root-mean-square envelope amplitude for muscle signals (EMG) — and which body state the transfer targets.】\n   - _Why_: This feature gives a physiological 'up-or-down' direction shared across signals, which is what lets us align them without pairs.\n3. Fit a small head $h_{m}$ that turns the 16-number latent z into a single coordinate u between 0 and 1, trained so u rises whenever the anchor $a_{m}$ rises. Build it as a monotone network (using non-negative weights so the output can only increase with the input) and cap how fast its output can change (1-Lipschitz, via weight clipping) so it stays smooth. Train it to put the windows in the same order as $a_{m},$ then rescale to fit between 0 and 1.\n\n*The per-modality physiological coordinate $u_{m}$ in [0,1] is a 1-Lipschitz monotone calibration head $h_{m}$ applied to the SSL latent, pinned to increase with the fixed-DSP anchor $a_{m}.$*\n$$ u_m = h_m(f_m(x)),\\quad h_m\\ \\text{1-Lipschitz monotone},\\ \\ h_m \\uparrow\\ \\text{with}\\ a_m \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Forcing u to move monotonically with the body state is exactly the condition the correctness proof needs, so the method builds in its own guarantee.\n\n### Marginal optimal-transport alignment\n*Align the two signals by transporting their marginal coordinate distributions, then transfer the frozen source head.*\n\n4. For each signal separately, estimate how its coordinate u is distributed by binning all its u values into 100 equal bins between 0 and 1 (a histogram), giving a 100-number probability profile. Do this independently for the source and target signals — the two are never combined into a joint sample.\n   - _Why_: We only ever need each signal's overall spread of u, which any single-signal dataset provides — no co-recording required.\n5. Match the two 100-bin distributions with entropic optimal transport (cost = squared distance between coordinate values, entropy weight $\\epsilon  =$ 0.05, 200 Sinkhorn iterations). From the resulting transport plan T, compute the barycentric map B that sends each target bin to its transport-weighted average source coordinate. To use it on a sample, round the target u to its nearest bin and apply B.\n\n*The cross-modal map is the entropic-OT coupling T between the source and target marginals of u, with squared-coordinate cost and entropy weight $\\epsilon  =$ 0.05, solved by Sinkhorn over couplings with the given marginals.*\n$$ T = \\arg\\min_{\\pi \\in \\Pi(P_{\\mathrm{src}}, P_{\\mathrm{tgt}})} \\langle \\pi, C\\rangle + \\varepsilon\\, H(\\pi),\\quad C_{ij} = (u^{\\mathrm{src}}_i - u^{\\mathrm{tgt}}_j)^2,\\ \\varepsilon = 0.05 \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Optimal transport finds the cheapest way to morph one distribution into the other, which on a shared physiological axis is the cross-signal correspondence.\n6. To label a target sample: turn it into its coordinate u, send u through the transport map B to get a matching source coordinate, look up the typical source latent for that coordinate (built once by averaging source latents within each coordinate bin), and feed that latent to the frozen source task head. Because the transport map decides which source region the sample lands in, the transport map directly sets the predicted label. 【author decision: whether the source head reads the full 16-number source latent rebuilt from the coordinate, or is rebuilt to read the single coordinate directly — i.e. how much of the source latent beyond the physiological coordinate the task actually needs.】\n\n*Transfer rule: a target sample's coordinate is barycentrically projected through T back into the source latent and fed to the FROZEN source task head $g_{src}$ to produce the target-modality prediction.*\n$$ \\hat{y}(x^{\\mathrm{tgt}}) = g_{\\mathrm{src}}\\big(B(u^{\\mathrm{tgt}})\\big),\\quad B = \\text{barycentric-projection of}\\ T \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This routes a target reading into the part of the source model's space where the same body state lives, so the existing head can label it.\n\n### Identifiability theorem\n*Prove the marginal coupling recovers the state-correspondence up to a monotone reparameterization.*\n\n7. Prove that if both coordinates rise monotonically with the same body state, the optimal-transport match recovers the true state-correspondence up to one harmless monotone relabeling; name that equivalence class, and state precisely when and how much recovery fails if monotonicity breaks. 【author decision: which smoothness assumption (strictly increasing, bi-Lipschitz, or piecewise-increasing) the proof uses and how the failure under broken monotonicity is bounded — for example, an error that grows with the fraction of non-monotone signal.】\n\n*Identifiability statement: if both coordinates are monotone functions of the same latent state s, the OT coupling recovers the state-correspondence up to a single monotone reparameterization r — the named ambiguity class.*\n$$ u^{\\mathrm{src}} = \\phi_s(s),\\ u^{\\mathrm{tgt}} = \\psi_s(s)\\ \\text{monotone in}\\ s \\ \\Rightarrow\\ T\\ \\text{recovers}\\ s\\text{-correspondence up to monotone}\\ r:\\ s \\mapsto r(s) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A proof turns 'it seemed to align' into 'it must align under this stated condition', and naming the failure keeps the claim honest.\n\n### Causal certification of what crossed\n*Certify the transferred direction is the physiological state via a controlled partition and a permuted-anchor control.*\n\n8. Build two controlled test sets. Set A changes the body state while keeping the person, session, and sensor fixed — using a controlled protocol that pushes the state through known levels (e.g. graded mental arithmetic for arousal, sleep stages for sleep depth) so the protocol stage itself is the ground-truth state label, decided independently of the model. Set B changes only the recording setup (different sensor, session, or person) while keeping the state fixed. 【author decision: which public dataset already includes a controlled protocol with known state labels, versus whether a small dedicated recording set must be collected to get a ground truth independent of the model.】\n   - _Why_: Varying exactly one thing at a time lets us tell apart 'tracked the body state' from 'tracked the recording setup'.\n9. Run the transfer on both sets and report the gap = balanced accuracy on set A minus balanced accuracy on set B. A large positive gap, with set B barely above chance, is the headline evidence that the method tracks the body state rather than the recording setup. Report this gap with confidence intervals from a subject-level bootstrap, not as a single number.\n   - _Why_: The gap, not the raw number, is the proof that what crossed signals is the physiological cause.\n10. As a control, swap the physiological coordinate u for a coordinate that only encodes recording context (built from a sensor- or session-identity embedding squeezed into 0-1), re-run the transport and the transfer with everything else unchanged, and check that accuracy drops to chance level (the score you would get by always predicting the most common class). If killing the physiological coordinate kills the transfer, the coordinate — not the transport math — is what carried the knowledge.\n   - _Why_: If killing the physiological coordinate kills the transfer, then the coordinate — not the transport math — is what carried the knowledge.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 基于边缘生理坐标传输的免配对跨模态生物信号迁移\n\n**方法名称.** Marginal Physiological-Coordinate Transport (MPCT)\n\n## 研究动机\n目标是把在某种生物信号上训练好的模型——比如标注数据充足的 EEG（脑电）——直接用到另一种信号上，比如 ECG（心电），而无需为第二种信号收集标注。最近的方法自称 unsupervised，却隐藏了一个昂贵的前提：它们需要一批同一个人、同一时刻同时采集了两种信号的录音（同步配对数据），才能学到两种信号之间的对应关系。而在各类生物信号之间，这种配对数据恰恰是最难收集的，因为不同信号用的传感器、采集会话、采样率和受试者都不同。BioX-Bridge 的桥接就是在这种配对集上拟合的，Brant-X 需要同时采集的数据且只在富模态是 EEG 时有效，SemiCMT 依赖一小批同步配对。由于它们的对齐只在有配对的地方学到，对从未同时采集过的目标数据就没有约束力，而且都无法判断模型迁移的是真正的生理状态，还是只是配对录音里的某个偶然相关因素。新的契机是：现在可以仅用单一信号自身训练出强的自监督编码器；而熵正则最优传输（OT，一种便宜、标准的分布匹配工具）只需用每种信号上一个生理摘要数值的整体分布就能对齐两种信号——完全不需要配对样本。我们把每种信号压缩成一个介于 0 和 1 之间、无需标注的「生理坐标」u，并用一个固定的信号处理特征（如心率频带功率）约束 u 随身体状态单调上升，然后用 OT 匹配两种信号的 u 分布。我们能证明这能恢复真实的对应关系（至多差一个无害的单调重标定），并能通过受控实验证明模型迁移的是生理状态而非录制伪因素。若成立，任何数据稀缺的生物信号都能仅凭自身无标注录音，从任意数据充足的信号那里借用训练好的模型，从而摆脱对最难收集数据的依赖。\n\n## 方法\n### 单模态坐标构造\n*在不使用任何跨模态数据的情况下，把每种信号压缩为一个无需标注的生理坐标。*\n\n1. 仅用每种信号自身的无标注录音，各训练一个自监督(self-supervised)编码器：把每段录音切成固定长度的窗口（睡眠信号约 30 秒，可穿戴心脏信号约 10 秒），随机遮住每个窗口的一半，训练一个一维卷积网络去补全被遮住的部分（用均方误差(mean-squared-error)损失）。训练完成并冻结后，网络把一个窗口变成 16 个数字的摘要（隐表示 z）。此处不使用另一种信号的任何数据。\n   - _为什么_: 单独学习每种信号，把所有跨信号工作收拢到一个小对象上，因此此阶段无需任何配对。\n2. 对每个窗口计算一个便宜、固定的信号处理(signal processing)数值 $a_{m}$，它事先已知会随身体状态升高而升高：心脏信号(ECG/PPG)用心率频带功率，脑信号(EEG)用谱边缘频率（即 95% 功率所在频率以下的那个频率）。这个数值由固定公式算出而非学习得到，是方法唯一使用的领域知识。【作者需决定：对于脑电图(electroencephalography, EEG)、心电图(electrocardiography, ECG)、光电容积脉搏波(photoplethysmography, PPG)之外的任何信号，用哪个固定的信号处理数值作为「随状态上升」的代理——例如肌电(EMG)用均方根包络幅值——以及迁移针对的是哪种身体状态。】\n   - _为什么_: 这个特征给出各信号共享的生理「升降」方向，正是无需配对就能对齐它们的依据。\n3. 拟合一个小的头 $h_{m}$，把 16 个数字的隐表示 z 变成一个介于 0 和 1 之间的单一坐标 u，训练目标是 $a_{m}$ 上升时 u 也上升。用单调网络实现（权重非负，使输出只能随输入增加），并限制其输出变化速率（1-Lipschitz，用权重裁剪），使其平滑。训练它把各窗口排成与 $a_{m}$ 相同的顺序，再缩放到 0 与 1 之间。\n\n*每个模态的生理坐标 $u_{m} \\in $ [0,1] 由一个 1-Lipschitz 单调校准头 $h_{m}$ 作用于 SSL 隐表示得到，并约束其随固定 DSP 锚点 $a_{m}$ 单调递增。*\n$$ u_m = h_m(f_m(x)),\\quad h_m\\ \\text{1-Lipschitz monotone},\\ \\ h_m \\uparrow\\ \\text{with}\\ a_m \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 强制 u 随身体状态单调变化，恰好是正确性证明所需的条件，于是方法把保证内建其中。\n\n### 边缘最优传输对齐\n*通过传输两种信号的边缘坐标分布来对齐它们，再迁移冻结的源任务头。*\n\n4. 对每种信号分别估计其坐标 u 的分布：把它所有的 u 值分进 0 到 1 之间的 100 个等宽区间（直方图），得到一个 100 个数的概率分布。对源信号和目标信号分别独立进行——两者绝不合并成联合样本。\n   - _为什么_: 我们只需每种信号 u 的整体分布，单一信号的数据集即可提供——无需同时采集。\n5. 用熵正则最优传输(entropic optimal transport)匹配两个 100 区间的分布（代价为坐标值平方差，熵权重 $\\epsilon  = 0.05$，200 次 Sinkhorn 迭代）。从得到的传输方案 T 计算重心映射 B，它把每个目标区间映到其按传输加权的平均源坐标。使用时把目标 u 取整到最近区间再套用 B。\n\n*跨模态映射即 u 的源、目标边缘分布之间的熵正则最优传输耦合 T，代价为坐标平方差，熵权重 $\\epsilon  = 0.05$，在给定边缘的耦合集合上用 Sinkhorn 求解。*\n$$ T = \\arg\\min_{\\pi \\in \\Pi(P_{\\mathrm{src}}, P_{\\mathrm{tgt}})} \\langle \\pi, C\\rangle + \\varepsilon\\, H(\\pi),\\quad C_{ij} = (u^{\\mathrm{src}}_i - u^{\\mathrm{tgt}}_j)^2,\\ \\varepsilon = 0.05 \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 最优传输找到把一个分布变形为另一个的最省方式，在共享生理轴上这就是跨信号的对应关系。\n6. 为目标样本打标签：先把它变成坐标 u，经传输映射 B 得到对应的源坐标，查出该坐标对应的典型源隐表示（在拟合时按坐标区间对源隐表示求平均一次得到），再把该隐表示送入冻结的源任务头。由于传输映射决定样本落入哪个源区域，它就直接决定了预测标签。【作者需决定：源任务头是读取由坐标重建的完整 16 维源隐表示，还是改造成直接读取单一坐标——即任务实际需要生理坐标之外的多少源隐表示信息。】\n\n*迁移规则：目标样本的坐标经 T 的重心投影 B 映回源隐空间，再送入冻结的源任务头 $g_{src}$，得到目标模态的预测。*\n$$ \\hat{y}(x^{\\mathrm{tgt}}) = g_{\\mathrm{src}}\\big(B(u^{\\mathrm{tgt}})\\big),\\quad B = \\text{barycentric-projection of}\\ T \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这把目标读数送入源模型中相同身体状态所在的区域，于是现成的任务头就能给它打标签。\n\n### 可辨识性定理\n*证明边缘耦合可在单调重参数化等价类下恢复状态对应关系。*\n\n7. 证明：若两个坐标都随同一身体状态单调上升，则最优传输匹配可在一个无害的单调重标定下恢复真实的状态对应关系；写明这个等价类，并精确写明单调性被破坏时恢复在何处、以何种程度失败。【作者需决定：证明采用哪种光滑性假设（严格递增、双向 Lipschitz(bi-Lipschitz)、或分段递增），以及单调性破坏下的失败如何被界定——例如误差随非单调信号占比增长。】\n\n*可辨识性结论：若两个坐标都是同一潜在状态 s 的单调函数，则 OT 耦合可在单一单调重参数化 r 的等价类下恢复状态对应关系——即所命名的歧义类。*\n$$ u^{\\mathrm{src}} = \\phi_s(s),\\ u^{\\mathrm{tgt}} = \\psi_s(s)\\ \\text{monotone in}\\ s \\ \\Rightarrow\\ T\\ \\text{recovers}\\ s\\text{-correspondence up to monotone}\\ r:\\ s \\mapsto r(s) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 证明把「看起来对齐了」变成「在此明示条件下必然对齐」，而写明失败方式让结论保持诚实。\n\n### 跨模态内容的因果认证\n*通过受控划分与置换锚点对照，认证迁移的方向是生理状态。*\n\n8. 构造两个受控测试集。集合 A 改变身体状态而冻结受试者、会话、传感器——用一个把状态推过若干已知水平的受控协议（如分级心算诱发唤醒、睡眠分期表示睡眠深度），使协议阶段本身成为独立于模型确定的状态真值标签。集合 B 只改变录制设置（不同传感器、会话或受试者）而冻结状态。【作者需决定：哪个公开数据集已含带已知状态标签的受控协议，还是需要专门采集一小批数据以获得独立于模型的真值。】\n   - _为什么_: 每次只变一个因素，才能区分「跟踪了身体状态」与「跟踪了录制设置」。\n9. 在两个集合上运行迁移并报告差距 = 集合 A 的平衡准确率减集合 B 的平衡准确率。一个大的正差距、且集合 B 仅略高于随机，即是方法跟踪身体状态而非录制设置的核心证据。用受试者级自助法(bootstrap)给出该差距的置信区间，而非只报一个数。\n   - _为什么_: 差距而非原始数字，才是跨信号传递的是生理原因的证明。\n10. 作为对照，把生理坐标 u 换成只编码录制场景的坐标（由传感器或会话身份嵌入压缩到 0-1 得到），在其余一切不变的情况下重跑传输与迁移，检查准确率是否跌至随机水平（即始终预测最常见类别所能得到的分数）。若去掉生理坐标就毁掉迁移，那么是坐标——而非传输数学——承载了知识。\n   - _为什么_: 若去掉生理坐标就毁掉迁移，那么是坐标——而非传输数学——承载了知识。\n\n"},{"id":"13","run_dir":"run_prompt13_tsfm","index":13,"title":"Discriminability-Conditioned Synthetic Pretraining for Time-Series Classification Foundation Models","title_zh":"面向时间序列分类基础模型的可判别性条件化合成预训练","method_name":"Discriminability-Conditioned Synthesis Loop (DCSL)","hook":"Synthetic-only pretraining for time-series classification (CauKer, TiCT) treats the class label as a by-product of which generative template made a series, so it cannot dial how hard a synthetic task is; we make per-episode class-discriminability an explicit conditioning input of the generator and close the loop so the pretraining model's own margin decides which difficulty to synthesize next. The non-obvious prediction is that matching synthetic difficulty to the model's current competence beats simply scaling the synthetic corpus, inverting CauKer's 'more synthetic data is better' scaling story.","anchor_pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","anchor_pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","domain_category":"Time Series","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes the label-relevant difficulty (class-discriminability) of a synthetic pretraining task a controllable, measurable quantity — synthetic generators (CauKer, TiCT, TimePFN) emit whatever class separability their generative process happens to produce, so the pretraining signal cannot be steered toward the fine-grained discriminative structure real TSC tasks require.","pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","sub_pattern":"C24 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by promoting the synthetic generator's class-assignment interface from a fixed by-product (label = which template produced the series) to a first-class conditioning variable: the generator takes a target Bayes-margin scalar tau and synthesizes a labeled episode whose true class-conditional separability realizes tau, with a measurable, generator-internal estimate of achieved discriminability returned alongside each episode.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf closes the loop between an in-progress synthetic generator and the model being pretrained: none lets the model's current competence shape which synthetic episodes are generated next, so synthetic-pretraining is open-loop and scaling the corpus (per CauKer's scaling law) adds easily-separable episodes rather than informatively-hard ones.","pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","sub_pattern":"C08 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by manufacturing the difficulty-target signal from the pretraining model itself: each step, the model's per-episode classification margin on freshly generated episodes is read out and used to set the next tau (synthesize just above the model's current competence), making the generator a data factory whose output difficulty distribution concentrates on the model's failure frontier instead of a static random spread.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"time series classification foundation models pretrained on synthetic data","n_papers":37,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":23},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":9,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Fine-Tuning a Time Series Foundation Model with Wasserstein Loss"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Repurposing Foundation Model for Generalizable Medical Time Series Classification"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"User-Friendly Foundation Model Adapters for Multivariate Time Series Classification"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Generalized Prompt Tuning: Adapting Frozen Univariate Time Series Foundation Models for Multivariate Healthcare Time Series"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Measuring Pre-training Data Quality without Labels for Time Series Foundation Models"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Foundation Models for Time Series Analysis: A Tutorial and Survey"}],"more":3},{"year":2025,"n":27,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Mantis: Lightweight Calibrated Foundation Model for User-Friendly Time Series Classification"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"RATFM: Retrieval-augmented Time Series Foundation Model for Anomaly Detection"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"FMTK: A Modular Toolkit for Composable Time Series Foundation Model Pipelines"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"TiCT: A Synthetically Pre-Trained Foundation Model for Time Series Classification"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"CauKer: classification time series foundation models can be pretrained on synthetic data only"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Leveraging Generic Time Series Foundation Models for EEG Classification"}],"more":21},{"year":2026,"n":1,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"}],"more":0}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":10,"share":0.27},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":7,"share":0.189},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":5,"share":0.135},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":5,"share":0.135},{"pattern_id":"targeted_self_supervised_objective","pattern_name":"Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective","count":4,"share":0.108},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":4,"share":0.108},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":4,"share":0.108},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":2,"share":0.054}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Synthetic-only pretraining for time series classification has been shown to work — CauKer (semanticscholar:6debf25dcbe997da5216be9f3aef5ad99fca8e70) generates causally-coherent synthetic series with trends, seasonality and nonlinear interactions and reveals clean dataset/capacity scaling laws, and TiCT (semanticscholar:3485b6e9995152ca2d289d8a9afcf9566d1ad8df) pretrains an in-context classifier exclusively on synthetic data using bit-encoded interchangeable labels — but in both pipelines the synthetic generator is optimized to make the *series* diverse and realistic, while the *class structure* of the pretraining task is imposed afterward (CauKer assigns labels from which causal-kernel template produced a series; TiCT samples synthetic ICL episodes with abstract label indices). Nothing in either pipeline measures or controls whether the synthetic prior produces a decision-boundary geometry that the model must learn to separate; consequently the pretraining signal can be dominated by easily-separable generative artifacts (whole-series scale, dominant frequency, kernel family) rather than the fine-grained local/temporal cues that real downstream TSC tasks turn on, so when the frozen or fine-tuned backbone meets a real benchmark whose discriminative information lives in subtle motifs, the representation has no head-room for it. The failure is that the synthetic-pretraining objective never makes the *label-relevant difficulty* of a synthetic task a controllable, measurable quantity, so scaling the synthetic corpus (as CauKer's scaling law invites) buys more easily-separable episodes rather than more class-discriminative ones, and Mantis (semanticscholar:e0dd7c7e100ca4833d9b6d01494fa06316d28e28) and Pre-trained Forecasting feature-extractors (openalex:W7103204207) inherit the same blind spot when they pretrain on generic or forecasting data and only then probe classification.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:6debf25dcbe997da5216be9f3aef5ad99fca8e70","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"CauKer generates diverse, causally-coherent synthetic time series (via composed causal kernels) and shows that classification TSFMs pretrained ONLY on this synthetic data exhibit clean scaling laws in dataset size and model capacity. Its residue: the label a synthetic series carries is a by-product of which generative template made it, so class separability is an uncontrolled side-effect of the generator rather than a targeted property — there is no mechanism to dial the discriminative difficulty of a synthetic episode or to verify that the cues separating its classes are the kind real TSC tasks depend on, leaving the scaling law measuring corpus size, not corpus class-informativeness. [anchor residue is abstract-level: CauKer fulltext not in candidate pool, grounded on its abstract + sibling TiCT method]"},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:3485b6e9995152ca2d289d8a9afcf9566d1ad8df","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"TiCT pretrains an in-context time-series classifier exclusively on synthetic episodes, encoding labels as abstract interchangeable bit-strings so the model learns label-pattern associations rather than label semantics. Residue: it samples synthetic ICL episodes without any control over how hard the within-episode class boundary is, so the pretraining distribution of task difficulty is whatever the generator happens to emit — it never targets, measures, or curriculum-schedules the discriminability of the synthetic classification task."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4409363524","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"TimePFN builds a prior-data-fitted network for multivariate forecasting by sampling synthetic series from diverse Gaussian-process kernels with linear coregionalization. Residue: its synthetic prior is engineered for forecasting fidelity (temporal + cross-channel dependency), with no notion of a class label at all, so it offers no machinery for making a synthetic prior carry controllable class-discriminative structure for classification."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:dfd5e13b34ff0466fadd352c69263c868433068c","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"This paper proposes a label-free metric for the quality of a TSFM pretraining corpus and studies contrastive-pretraining performance as a function of the data used. Residue: the metric scores generic representational quality of (real) pretraining data and is never tied to class-discriminability or to a synthetic generator one could steer with it — it diagnoses data quality but offers no closed loop that shapes a synthetic prior toward label-relevant difficulty."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"time series classification foundation models pretrained on synthetic data","venue":"ICLR 2026","time":"2026","data":["UCR/UEA time series classification archive","synthetic time series generated by a controllable prior generator","medical/biosignal TSC benchmarks (EEG, ECG)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with time series / foundation-model background","preference":"both","baseline":"CauKer-pretrained classification TSFM (semanticscholar:6debf25dcbe997da5216be9f3aef5ad99fca8e70) and TiCT in-context synthetic-pretrained classifier (semanticscholar:3485b6e9995152ca2d289d8a9afcf9566d1ad8df)","limitation":"current synthetic generators optimize for generative diversity/realism of the series, not for whether the synthetic prior actually induces transferable class-discriminative structure","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The thread is a sequential_pipeline named the discriminability-conditioned synthesis loop: the anchor leg (C24) builds a generator G(tau, z) -> (X_episode, Y_episode, d_hat) and the sibling leg (C08) builds the controller that sets tau from the pretraining model's margin. CONSTRUCTION (anchor): we keep CauKer-style causal-kernel synthesis as the backbone that produces the raw series shapes, but we liberate the class-assignment interface. Instead of labeling a series by which template produced it, we define a synthetic episode as a k-way classification task and assign labels by partitioning a generative latent factor; class-discriminability is then controlled by a single scalar tau in [0,1] that sets the target Bayes margin between class-conditional distributions of the discriminative factor (tau near 0 = classes overlap, separable only by subtle local motifs; tau near 1 = classes separated by a coarse global cue). Concretely tau parameterizes the signed offset between the per-class means of the chosen discriminative latent (e.g. amplitude of an injected motif, phase of a seasonality component, or a causal-edge weight) relative to the within-class noise scale, so the analytic two-class Bayes accuracy of an oracle that sees the latent is a known monotone function acc_Bayes(tau). G also returns d_hat, an estimate of the realized discriminability computed as the leave-one-out 1-nearest-neighbour accuracy of the GENERATIVE latent factor (not the model's features) over the episode's samples — a model-independent, generator-internal readout in [1/k, 1]. CONTROLLER (sibling): the pretraining model M (a transformer in-context classifier in the TiCT mold, or a frozen-backbone-plus-head) processes each generated episode and emits a per-episode margin m = mean logit gap between the true class and the runner-up. We maintain an exponential-moving-average competence c_t of m over recent episodes, and set the next target tau_{t+1} by a controller tau_{t+1} = clip(tau* (c_t), tau_min, tau_max) where tau*(c) is the difficulty whose acc_Bayes the model currently achieves at a fixed target success rate p* (default p*=0.75): we keep a running regression of M's realized accuracy against d_hat across recent episodes and invert it to find the d_hat (hence tau) at which M scores p*, i.e. synthesize just above the model's current competence frontier. The two legs interlock as a pipeline: G's (episode, d_hat) is M's input; M's margin is the controller's input; the controller's tau is G's input for the next step. Every quantity is computable from the run alone: tau is a scalar we set; d_hat is generator-internal kNN-on-latent; m and c_t are model logit readouts; the regression inverting accuracy-vs-d_hat is fit online over a sliding window of W=2000 episodes; the bridge hyperparameters are the EMA decay (0.99), target success p* (0.75), and window W. This makes class-discriminability the steered, measured quantity the literature lacked, and routes the model's own competence back into generation, closing the open-loop gap CauKer's scaling law leaves open.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The two gaps share one pipeline, not two modules: the anchor's dialable generator is useless without something to set the dial, and the controller is vacuous without a generator that responds to a difficulty target — so they are sequential_pipeline halves of one loop rather than parallel contributions, evidenced by the fact that tau is simultaneously the anchor's liberated variable and the sibling's manufactured signal. Alternative designs considered and rejected: (1) a static difficulty curriculum (pre-generate episodes at a fixed difficulty schedule) — rejected because it reduces to lineage node c1 (curriculum over a fixed pool) and cannot react to the model's competence; (2) adversarial hard-episode synthesis maximizing model loss — rejected because it reduces to lineage node c2 (generic adversarial hard-sample synthesis) and tends to produce unlearnable noise rather than informatively-hard-but-separable tasks; our controller instead targets a fixed success rate p* just above competence, which is neither a fixed pool nor pure loss-maximization. We avoided regressing tau on the model's OWN feature-space separability (which would be tautological with margin) by defining d_hat on the generative latent, an independent readout.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: pretrain two otherwise-identical in-context transformer classifiers to the SAME synthetic-token budget on the CauKer-style backbone — one with the discriminability-conditioned competence loop, one with a fixed random-difficulty schedule — then evaluate frozen-feature and few-shot accuracy on the UCR/UEA archive plus an EEG/ECG biosignal set. If the candidate works, mean real-benchmark classification accuracy at matched token budget is higher for the loop than for random-difficulty pretraining, and the accuracy-vs-token-budget curve for the loop rises faster (better sample efficiency), partially inverting CauKer's 'scale the synthetic corpus' story. The load-bearing variable is the realized target-difficulty tau set by the controller (equivalently the per-episode d_hat the generator hits); the mechanism claim is that matching synthetic difficulty to the model's competence frontier is what drives the gain. NEGATIVE CONTROL: sever the loop by feeding the controller a randomized margin (permute m across episodes before the EMA/regression) so tau no longer tracks M's competence while the generator and token budget are unchanged — the predicted effect is that downstream real-benchmark accuracy falls back to the random-difficulty baseline. POSITIVE CONTROL: a stripped model that keeps only the competence-targeting controller over a single coarse difficulty knob (no per-latent d_hat refinement) should recover most of the downstream accuracy gain, identifying difficulty-matching (not the specific d_hat estimator) as the mechanism.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:6debf25dcbe997da5216be9f3aef5ad99fca8e70","delta":"CauKer generates causally-coherent synthetic series and labels them by generative template, revealing a monotone synthetic scaling law; we construct a generator whose per-episode class-discriminability tau is an explicit conditioning input with a measurable realized d_hat, and predict a difficulty-matched curriculum beats same-budget corpus scaling — a control axis and a scaling-inversion CauKer does not have."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:3485b6e9995152ca2d289d8a9afcf9566d1ad8df","delta":"TiCT pretrains an in-context synthetic classifier with abstract bit-labels but samples episode difficulty uncontrolled; we add a closed competence loop that sets each episode's target Bayes-margin from the model's running margin, making the pretraining task-difficulty distribution a steered quantity rather than whatever the generator emits."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4409363524","delta":"TimePFN's GP-kernel synthetic prior is forecasting-only with no class label; we define class-discriminability as a conditionable, measurable property of a labeled synthetic episode, which has no analogue in a forecasting prior."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:dfd5e13b34ff0466fadd352c69263c868433068c","delta":"They score (real) pretraining-data quality with a static label-free metric; we make a closed-loop, model-coupled difficulty signal that actively reshapes which synthetic episodes are generated next, rather than passively rating a fixed corpus."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:3485b6e9995152ca2d289d8a9afcf9566d1ad8df","what_step_was_missed":"TiCT built the synthetic-only in-context classification pretraining pipeline but treated episode difficulty as whatever its synthetic sampler produced; for our contribution to already exist it would have needed to construct a parameterization of an episode's class-conditional separability (the tau-to-Bayes-margin map with a generator-internal realized-discriminability readout) and a competence-coupled controller that sets that parameter from the model's margin — neither the difficulty parameterization nor the closed control loop is present in its synthetic-episode sampler."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":328,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"No hard floor fires (no Reject lesson 'yes', anti_pattern null, paper_pointed_threat is addressable not exact-mechanism). recipe_application_check is 'applied' on both legs, so the mechanism is sharp. But two load-bearing borderlines justify revise: (1) gap_closure_reject_check C08 borderline on 'A synthetic-data-factory claim collapses without comparison to cheaper classical baselines' — the candidate compares only against its own generator's variants and must add a plain-CauKer-scaling and static-difficulty-curriculum baseline; and (2) paper_pointed_threat against CauKer is addressable_via adding that exact matched-budget head-to-head. Both targets are tactical field edits to falsification_prediction / core_mechanism_steps that strengthen attribution of the gain to the closed loop.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes the label-relevant difficulty (class-discriminability) of a synthetic pretraining task a controllable, measurable quantity — synthetic generators (CauKer, TiCT, TimePFN) emit whatever class separability their generative process happens to produce, so the pretraining signal cannot be steered toward the fine-grained discriminative structure real TSC tasks require.","main_pattern":"generative_process_redesign","sub_pattern":"C24 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail most often by attaching a different conditioning channel to an existing backbone and presenting the swap itself as the contribution without isolating it via an ablation that holds backbone/data/compute fixed while toggling only the new interface; a second shape is an over-claimed 'foundation/unified' reframe the experiments never exercise.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A controllable pipeline assembled from frozen pretrained modules needs an ablation proving that the new control surface — not the off-the-shelf components — drives the gain, or it collapses into prior synthetic-data and adapter work.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism_steps step 9(a) holds backbone/data/token-budget fixed and toggles only the difficulty-control surface (loop vs fixed random tau), and the falsification negative control severs the competence signal while keeping the generator unchanged — the control surface is isolated."},{"lesson_quoted":"Swapping the conditioning encoder for a more powerful one is not a new model class if the output quality still trails incumbents and the encoder's advantage is never ablated against the prior encoder under matched conditions.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate does not swap in a stronger encoder; it keeps the CauKer-style backbone and adds a scalar tau conditioning interface, with the matched-budget random-difficulty baseline serving as the prior-interface comparison."},{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a unified or foundation-model reframe obligates you to actually demonstrate the unification (multi-domain pretraining plus transfer); per-setting retraining under a single architecture does not substantiate the claim.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The candidate is positioned as a foundation-model pretraining method and must actually exercise cross-benchmark transfer (UCR/UEA + biosignal) rather than a single dataset; the falsification does specify the full archive, so the risk is mitigation-by-execution but the claim is load-bearing."},{"lesson_quoted":"Importing a representation from a semantically adjacent domain as the conditioning signal fails when that space is orthogonal to the geometry or dynamics that actually determine the output being synthesized.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The conditioning signal (tau / Bayes-margin of the generative discriminative latent) is intrinsic to the synthesis process itself, not imported from an adjacent domain."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf closes the loop between an in-progress synthetic generator and the model being pretrained: none lets the model's current competence shape which synthetic episodes are generated next, so synthetic-pretraining is open-loop and scaling the corpus (per CauKer's scaling law) adds easily-separable episodes rather than informatively-hard ones.","main_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","sub_pattern":"C08 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is treating 'attach a generator plus a filter' as a sufficient contribution when generate-and-filter is commonplace, with no load-bearing insight separating it from prior augmentation/self-distillation; secondary shapes are unvalidated synthetic-to-real transfer, showing only a proxy property, and omitting cheaper non-generative baselines.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Training on synthetically generated data without demonstrating transfer to the real target distribution leaves the core premise unvalidated, no matter how clean the synthetic labels are.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"falsification_prediction evaluates frozen-feature and few-shot accuracy on real UCR/UEA + biosignal benchmarks at matched token budget — synthetic-to-real transfer is the primary measured outcome, not a proxy."},{"lesson_quoted":"Inducing a proxy property such as ensemble diversity is not the same as demonstrating the downstream goal such as shortcut mitigation; reviewers require the target metric, not the intermediate effect.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The headline metric is downstream real-benchmark accuracy, not the intermediate difficulty distribution; difficulty-matching is the mechanism, accuracy is the claimed outcome."},{"lesson_quoted":"A synthetic-data-factory claim collapses without comparison to cheaper classical baselines, because the necessity of the heavy generative model is then unverifiable.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"It compares against random-difficulty and adversarial-control variants of the SAME generator but should also compare against a cheaper non-loop baseline (e.g. plain CauKer scaling and a static difficulty curriculum) to prove the closed loop, not just any difficulty signal, is necessary."},{"lesson_quoted":"A newly proposed quality or gating score must be tightly argued to solve the stated problem under realistic conditions — a loosely-motivated score evaluated in an artificial setup is dismissed as a solution looking for a problem.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The gating/control score (competence-matched target success p* via inverted accuracy-vs-d_hat regression) is tightly tied to the stated problem of steering difficulty to the model's learnable frontier, and d_hat is defined model-independently to avoid tautology."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No Reject lesson matches 'yes' on either entry, so no hard-floor trigger. The C24 entry is borderline on the foundation/unification claim (must exercise cross-benchmark transfer, which falsification already specifies) and the C08 entry is borderline on cheaper-baseline coverage (should add a plain-scaling and static-curriculum baseline to prove the closed loop specifically is load-bearing)."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes the label-relevant difficulty (class-discriminability) of a synthetic pretraining task a controllable, measurable quantity ...","sub_pattern":"C24 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Hold the iterative generative backbone fixed and treat its conditioning interface as the free variable — change WHAT the procedure conditions on (replace a categorical label with a differentiable/measured objective) and promote the condition to a first-class design surface rather than an inherited default.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism keeps the CauKer causal-kernel synthesis backbone fixed and liberates the class-assignment interface: the label stops being 'which template made the series' and becomes a target Bayes-margin scalar tau that parameterizes class-conditional separability, with a generator-internal realized-discriminability readout d_hat — exactly the C24 move of converting a fixed categorical-label condition into a controllable differentiable conditioning variable on a kept backbone.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf closes the loop between an in-progress synthetic generator and the model being pretrained ...","sub_pattern":"C08 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Stand up a controllable generator and drive it to synthesize instances beyond the corpus, then close the loop dynamically by feeding the learner's per-category uncertainty/error/importance back to the generator so synthesis concentrates on exactly the regions the current model fails on — the object manufactured is the training distribution itself.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism reads the pretraining model's per-episode margin, maintains an EMA competence, and sets the next tau so the generator synthesizes just above the model's competence frontier — the C08 dynamic closed loop where the learner's competence routes back into generation, manufacturing the training-difficulty distribution rather than static episodes.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both signature moves are present: C24's fixed-backbone conditioning-interface liberation (label -> tau) and C08's dynamic competence-routed generator loop (margin -> next tau). Neither leg merely enacts the parent's generic gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["generative_process_redesign","self_supervised_signal_engineering"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; this candidate's composition set is {generative_process_redesign, self_supervised_signal_engineering}, so no anti-pattern matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:6debf25dcbe997da5216be9f3aef5ad99fca8e70","threat_source":"lit_table","subsumption_argument":"CauKer is the most specific competitor: it already shows classification TSFMs can be pretrained on synthetic data only and reports clean dataset-size/capacity scaling laws, so a reviewer will ask whether 'just generate more CauKer data' already gets the candidate's gains. The candidate's claim stands or falls on the predicted INVERSION — that a competence-matched difficulty curriculum at FIXED synthetic-token budget beats same-budget CauKer-style random-difficulty scaling — because if difficulty-matching does not outperform plain scaling at matched budget, the contribution collapses into 'CauKer plus a curriculum knob.' The collision-pool curriculum papers (e.g. the NLU self-adaptive-difficulty curriculum) order a FIXED real corpus and do not condition a synthetic generator's class-discriminability, so they are not exact-mechanism overlaps; CauKer is the binding threat and it is addressable, not subsuming.","addressable_via":"falsification_prediction / core_mechanism_steps must include a head-to-head against plain CauKer-style corpus scaling (and a static difficulty curriculum) at matched token budget, so the gain is attributed to the closed competence loop rather than to difficulty-conditioning or extra data alone."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism_steps","issue":"gap_closure_reject_check C08 borderline ('A synthetic-data-factory claim collapses without comparison to cheaper classical baselines') + paper_pointed_threat (CauKer) addressable_via matched-budget head-to-head","fix_direction":"Extend the ablation step (step 9) to add two non-loop baselines evaluated at matched synthetic-token budget: (b1) plain CauKer-style template-labeled corpus scaling (no difficulty conditioning at all), and (b2) a static, model-independent difficulty curriculum (fixed tau schedule, no competence feedback). Keep the loop, random-tau, adversarial-tau, and d_hat-randomization controls already present. This isolates the closed competence loop as the load-bearing element versus both plain scaling and mere difficulty-conditioning."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"falsification_prediction","issue":"gap_closure_reject_check C24 borderline ('Claiming a unified/foundation-model reframe obligates you to demonstrate the unification') + CauKer threat","fix_direction":"Make the matched-token-budget head-to-head against plain CauKer-style scaling explicit in the minimal experiment, and state that the cross-benchmark transfer (UCR/UEA archive breadth + a biosignal set) is required to substantiate the foundation-model framing — accuracy must improve across the archive, not on a single dataset. Do NOT alter the load-bearing variable (tau), the negative control (margin permutation), or the positive control."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism_steps","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Extended ablation step 9 to add two matched-token-budget non-loop baselines — plain CauKer-style template-labeled corpus scaling (b1) and a static model-independent difficulty curriculum (b2) — so the closed competence loop is isolated against both plain scaling and mere difficulty-conditioning, addressing the C08 cheaper-baseline lesson and the CauKer paper_pointed_threat."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"falsification_prediction","outcome":"skipped_anti_substitution","delta_summary":"Revision target named falsification_prediction, a kill-switch field; per Hard rule 1 it is byte-identical-preserved and not modified. The matched-budget head-to-head and cross-benchmark-transfer requirement it asked for are instead realized in the editable core_mechanism_steps (step 8 already names full UCR/UEA + biosignal transfer; step 9-b1 adds the matched-budget plain-CauKer baseline)."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Discriminability-Conditioned Synthetic Pretraining for Time-Series Classification Foundation Models\n\n**Method.** Discriminability-Conditioned Synthesis Loop (DCSL)\n\n## Motivation\nPeople have recently shown you can train a general-purpose time-series classifier on purely made-up (synthetic) data and have it work on real tasks: CauKer makes realistic fake time series with cause-and-effect structure, and TiCT trains a classifier entirely on synthetic example sets. But in both, the fake-data generator is tuned to make the series look diverse and realistic, while the *class labels* are tacked on afterward — CauKer labels a series by which recipe made it, and TiCT just samples whatever difficulty its generator happens to produce. Nobody checks or controls whether the synthetic task is actually *hard to classify* in the way real tasks are. The result: the model can pass synthetic tasks using cheap give-aways (overall scale, the dominant frequency, which recipe was used) instead of the subtle local patterns that real tasks hinge on. So 'just make more synthetic data' (CauKer's scaling law) mostly adds more easy examples. The timing is right because the in-context-classifier machinery these papers introduced makes it cheap to read how hard each synthetic example was for the model and to feed that back into generation. We propose to make the difficulty of each synthetic classification task a single controllable knob tau, measure how hard each generated task actually turned out (a model-independent score $d_{hat}),$ and close the loop: the model's own confidence margin decides how hard the next batch should be — always a little above what it can currently do. If this works, synthetic pretraining stops being blind data-dumping and becomes a steerable method, and CauKer's 'more is better' story flips to 'better-targeted difficulty is better at the same data budget'.\n\n## Method\n### Background scaffolding and evaluation\n*Fixed CauKer-style backbone, real-benchmark transfer evaluation, and matched-budget attribution baselines.*\n\n1. Reuse a CauKer-style synthetic time-series generator unchanged, but for every series you create, keep a record of the hidden factors the generator used (the injected-motif amplitude, the seasonality phase, the strength of each cause-effect link, and which kernel family was used) stored next to the series and aligned by index, instead of throwing those factors away. Keep the generator's own settings fixed for the whole experiment.\n   - _Why_: Keeping the generator fixed means any later improvement can be credited to the new difficulty controls, not to a fancier generator.\n2. After a fixed amount of synthetic training, freeze the model and test transfer in two ways. First, a frozen-feature probe: take the model's average final-layer embedding of a series (with no support examples) as its feature vector and train a simple logistic-regression classifier per target dataset. Second, in-context few-shot: give the model 5 labeled examples per class from the target dataset and read its predictions directly. Report average accuracy over the whole UCR/UEA archive and on each EEG/ECG biosignal dataset.\n   - _Why_: The whole point is real-world transfer across many datasets, so it must be tested on a broad real benchmark, not one dataset.\n3. Keeping the synthetic data budget identical (measured as the total number of query timesteps used in training), also run and compare: a fixed random difficulty schedule, an adversarial difficulty that maximizes the model's loss, a version where the difficulty score $d_{hat}$ is scrambled, plain CauKer-style 'just generate more' scaling with no difficulty control, and a fixed static difficulty curriculum. Because all use the same data budget, only the way difficulty is chosen differs. Comparing the loop to plain scaling shows the gain over more data; comparing it to the random and static-curriculum runs shows the value of the feedback loop specifically; comparing it to the adversarial run rules out simply chasing the hardest examples.\n   - _Why_: These comparisons prove the gain comes from the closed competence loop specifically, not from more data or any difficulty signal.\n\n### Discriminability-dial generator\n*Turn the synthetic generator's class-assignment from a fixed by-product into a controllable, measured difficulty knob.*\n\n4. Turn 'which recipe made the series' into a real k-class task. Choose one hidden factor as the dividing axis, rescale it so each class has unit spread, then space the k class centers evenly on a line so that the best-possible (Bayes) accuracy between neighboring classes equals your chosen target difficulty tau (tau near 0 means the classes overlap and only subtle local motifs tell them apart; tau near 1 means an obvious global cue separates them). Sample each class's values around its center, render the support and query series through the fixed generator, and output the labeled episode. Randomize all the other hidden factors across every series so the class can only be told apart by the axis you chose. 【author decision: whether to instead tie one nuisance factor to the class on purpose, to test whether the model takes shortcuts — this changes what the episode measures.】\n\n*The target discriminability scalar $\\tau $ sets the signed offset between per-class means of the discriminative latent relative to the within-class noise $\\sigma ,$ so an oracle's two-class Bayes accuracy is a known monotone function of $\\tau .$*\n$$ \\mathrm{acc}_{\\mathrm{Bayes}}(\\tau) = \\Phi\\!\\left(\\frac{\\tau}{2}\\right), \\quad \\tau = \\frac{\\lvert \\mu_1 - \\mu_0 \\rvert}{\\sigma} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This makes 'how hard is this synthetic task' a single dial you can set, with a known best-possible accuracy for each setting.\n5. Measure how hard the generated task actually turned out: run leave-one-out nearest-neighbour classification using only the hidden dividing factor's values (Euclidean distance between samples on that factor), and report the resulting accuracy $d_{hat}, a$ number between 1/k and 1. Crucially this uses the generator's own factor, not the model's features, so the difficulty reading stays independent of the model.\n\n*Realized discriminability $d_{hat}$ is the leave-one-out 1-nearest-neighbour accuracy computed on the generative latent factor (not model features), giving a model-independent readout of how separable the episode actually is.*\n$$ \\hat{d} = \\frac{1}{N}\\sum_{i=1}^{N} \\mathbb{1}\\!\\left[\\, y_i = y_{\\mathrm{NN}(i)} \\,\\right], \\quad \\hat{d} \\in [1/k, 1] \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Measuring difficulty on the generator's own factor, separate from the model, keeps the difficulty reading honest and not circular.\n\n### Competence-coupled controller\n*Read the model's own margin and set the next synthesized difficulty just above its current competence.*\n\n6. Lay out the episode in the in-context style: first the labeled support examples, then the query series with their labels hidden, and pass the whole thing through the model you are pretraining (an in-context transformer classifier started from random weights). For each query the model gives a score per class; from these compute the margin m (average gap between the correct class's score and the best competing class) and the query accuracy a.\n   - _Why_: The model's own margin tells you whether the current difficulty is too easy, about right, or too hard for it.\n7. Keep a smoothed estimate of the model's competence, updated as $c_{t} = 0.99 \\times $ previous $+ 0.01 \\times $ current margin, starting it from the margin seen on a first batch generated at a neutral difficulty of 0.5. Also store every (difficulty $d_{hat},$ accuracy a) pair in a rolling window of the last 2000 episodes. Do not let the controller act until that window has been filled once at the neutral difficulty.\n\n*Competence $c_{t}$ is an exponential moving average (decay 0.99) of the per-episode margin $m_{t},$ the mean logit gap between the true class and the runner-up.*\n$$ c_t = 0.99\\, c_{t-1} + 0.01\\, m_t, \\quad m_t = \\overline{\\mathrm{logit}}_{\\mathrm{true}} - \\max_{j\\neq \\mathrm{true}} \\overline{\\mathrm{logit}}_{j} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Smoothing avoids over-reacting to one lucky or unlucky episode and gives the controller a stable trend to act on.\n8. Fit a simple S-shaped curve relating accuracy to difficulty $d_{hat}$ over the window (refit every 100 episodes with light regularization), then read off the difficulty at which the model would score the target success rate of 75%, convert that back into a target tau, and clip it to between 0.05 and 0.95 to get the next difficulty. If the curve is too flat or the target falls outside what's been seen, instead just step the difficulty a little toward whatever brings accuracy nearer 75%. 【author decision: whether the 75% target applies to the success rate (accuracy a, recommended) or to the smoothed margin, since these two competence measures can disagree and a margin target would need its own value.】\n\n*The controller fits an online logistic regression of realized accuracy on $d_{hat},$ inverts it for the $d_{hat}$ at the target success rate p*=0.75, maps that back to $\\tau ,$ and clips to [0.05, 0.95] — synthesizing just above the model's current competence.*\n$$ \\tau_{t+1} = \\mathrm{clip}\\!\\left(\\, \\mathrm{acc}_{\\mathrm{Bayes}}^{-1}\\!\\big(\\hat{d}^{*}\\big),\\; \\tau_{\\min},\\, \\tau_{\\max}\\right), \\quad \\hat{d}^{*}:\\; \\sigma(\\beta_0 + \\beta_1 \\hat{d}^{*}) = p^{*} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This picks the next difficulty to sit just above what the model can currently do — the most informative place to train.\n9. Run the loop: make the next batch of 64 episodes at the new difficulty, pass them through the model, and update only the model's weights with the AdamW optimizer (learning rate 0.0003, cosine schedule) on the standard cross-entropy classification loss; the controller keeps refitting on its own slower schedule. The generator is not trained by gradients — it is steered only through the single difficulty number tau. As the model improves, its margin rises and the loop automatically requests harder tasks.\n   - _Why_: The loop keeps the training data pinned to the model's learning frontier instead of wasting effort on tasks it already aces.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 面向时间序列分类基础模型的可判别性条件化合成预训练\n\n**方法名称.** Discriminability-Conditioned Synthesis Loop (DCSL)\n\n## 研究动机\n最近的工作表明：可以完全用人工合成（synthetic）数据训练一个通用的时间序列分类器，并在真实任务上奏效——CauKer 生成带因果结构的逼真假时间序列，TiCT 则完全用合成的样本集来训练分类器。但在这两种方法里，合成数据生成器只被调成让序列“多样且逼真”，类别标签是事后贴上去的：CauKer 用“是哪个模板生成的序列”当标签，TiCT 直接采样生成器碰巧产生的难度。没有人去衡量或控制合成任务在分类意义上到底有多难。结果是：模型可以靠廉价线索（整体幅度、主频率、用了哪个模板）通过合成任务，而不是靠真实任务真正依赖的细微局部模式。于是“多生成一些合成数据”（CauKer 的 scaling law）主要只是堆了更多容易的样本。现在做这件事正当其时，因为这些论文引入的 in-context 分类器机制，让“读出每个合成样本对模型有多难、并把信号反馈回生成”变得很便宜。我们把每个合成分类任务的难度做成一个可控标量 tau，用一个与模型无关的分数 $d_{hat}$ 衡量生成出来的任务实际有多难，并闭合回路：用模型自己的置信度 margin 决定下一批该多难——始终略高于它当前能做到的水平。若成立，合成预训练就从盲目堆数据变成可操控的方法，CauKer 的“越多越好”也会被改写为“在同等数据预算下，更精准的难度更好”。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景脚手架与评估\n*固定的 CauKer 式 backbone、真实 benchmark 迁移评估，以及同预算下的归因 baseline。*\n\n1. 原样复用 CauKer 风格的合成时间序列生成器，但对你生成的每一条序列，都把生成器用到的隐藏因子（注入 motif 的幅度、季节性相位、每条因果连接的强度、用了哪个 kernel family）按索引对齐地存放在序列旁边，而不是用完就丢。整个实验过程中保持生成器自身的设置不变。\n   - _为什么_: 保持生成器不变，意味着之后的任何提升都能归功于新的难度控制，而不是更强的生成器。\n2. 在固定的合成训练量之后冻结模型，用两种方式测试迁移。第一，frozen-feature 探针：取模型对一条序列的最后一层平均嵌入（不带 support 示例）作为特征向量，针对每个目标数据集训练一个简单的 logistic 回归分类器。第二，in-context few-shot：从目标数据集为每个类提供 5 个带标签示例，直接读取模型预测。报告在整个 UCR/UEA archive 以及每个 EEG/ECG 生物信号数据集上的平均准确率。\n   - _为什么_: 整件事的目的是跨多个数据集的真实迁移，所以必须在广泛的真实 benchmark 上测，而不是单个数据集。\n3. 在保持合成数据预算完全相同（以训练中用到的 query 时间步总数衡量）的前提下，另外运行并比较：固定随机难度调度、最大化模型损失的对抗式难度、把难度分数 $d_{hat}$ 打乱的版本、不做任何难度控制的纯 CauKer 式“只是多生成”扩充、以及固定的静态难度课程。由于都用同样的数据预算，唯一不同的就是难度的选择方式。把闭环与纯扩充比较，显示出相对“更多数据”的增益；与随机和静态课程比较，显示出反馈回路本身的价值；与对抗式比较，排除单纯追逐最难样本的解释。\n   - _为什么_: 这些对比证明收益来自闭合的胜任度回路本身，而不是来自更多数据或任意一种难度信号。\n\n### 可判别性旋钮生成器\n*把合成生成器的类别分配从固定副产品变成可控、可测的难度旋钮。*\n\n4. 把“是哪个模板生成的序列”变成真正的 k 类任务。选一个隐藏因子作为划分轴，将其重新缩放使每个类的离散程度为单位方差，再把 k 个类中心在一条线上等间距排列，使相邻类之间的最优可达(Bayes)准确率等于你设定的目标难度 tau（tau 接近 0 表示各类重叠、只能靠细微局部 motif 区分；tau 接近 1 表示有明显全局线索可分）。围绕各类中心采样取值，通过固定的生成器渲染出 support 与 query 序列，输出带标签的 episode。把其它所有隐藏因子在每条序列上随机化，使得只能靠你选定的轴来区分类别。【作者需决定：是否反而故意把某个干扰因子与类别绑定，以测试模型是否走捷径——这会改变该 episode 所测量的内容。】\n\n*目标可判别性标量 $\\tau $ 设定判别隐变量两类均值之差相对类内噪声 $\\sigma $ 的偏移量，使得 oracle 的二分类 Bayes 准确率是 $\\tau $ 的已知单调函数。*\n$$ \\mathrm{acc}_{\\mathrm{Bayes}}(\\tau) = \\Phi\\!\\left(\\frac{\\tau}{2}\\right), \\quad \\tau = \\frac{\\lvert \\mu_1 - \\mu_0 \\rvert}{\\sigma} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这让“这个合成任务有多难”变成一个可设定的旋钮，且每个设定都有已知的最优可达准确率。\n5. 衡量生成出来的任务实际有多难：只用隐藏划分因子的取值做留一法近邻分类（在该因子上用样本间的欧氏距离），报告得到的准确率 $d_{hat}$，取值在 1/k 到 1 之间。关键是这里只用生成器自己的因子、而非模型特征，因此难度读数与模型保持独立。\n\n*实现可判别性 $d_{hat}$ 是在生成隐变量（而非模型特征）上做留一法 1-近邻得到的准确率，给出与模型无关的本回合真实可分性读数。*\n$$ \\hat{d} = \\frac{1}{N}\\sum_{i=1}^{N} \\mathbb{1}\\!\\left[\\, y_i = y_{\\mathrm{NN}(i)} \\,\\right], \\quad \\hat{d} \\in [1/k, 1] \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 在生成器自己的因子上、且独立于模型来衡量难度，能让难度读数诚实、不循环。\n\n### 胜任度耦合控制器\n*读取模型自身的 margin，把下一批合成难度设定在略高于其当前胜任度的位置。*\n\n6. 按 in-context 方式排布该 episode：先放带标签的 support 示例，再放隐藏了标签的 query 序列，整体送入你正在预训练的模型（从随机权重起步的 in-context transformer 分类器）。模型为每个 query 给出各类的分数；据此计算 margin m（正确类分数与最强竞争类分数之差的平均）和 query 准确率 a。\n   - _为什么_: 模型自己的 margin 能告诉你当前难度对它而言是太容易、刚好、还是太难。\n7. 维护模型胜任度的平滑估计，按 $c_{t} = 0.99 \\times $ 上一值 $+ 0.01 \\times $ 当前 margin 更新，并以在中性难度 0.5 下生成的第一批的 margin 作为初值。同时把每个 (难度 $d_{hat},$ 准确率 a) 对存入最近 2000 个 episode 的滚动窗口。在该窗口首次于中性难度下填满之前，不让控制器动作。\n\n*胜任度 $c_{t}$ 是逐回合 margin $m_{t}$ 的指数滑动平均（衰减 0.99），$m_{t}$ 为真实类与次高类的平均 logit 差。*\n$$ c_t = 0.99\\, c_{t-1} + 0.01\\, m_t, \\quad m_t = \\overline{\\mathrm{logit}}_{\\mathrm{true}} - \\max_{j\\neq \\mathrm{true}} \\overline{\\mathrm{logit}}_{j} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 平滑可避免对单个走运或倒霉的回合过度反应，给控制器一个稳定的趋势来调节。\n8. 在窗口上拟合一条把准确率与难度 $d_{hat}$ 关联起来的简单 S 形曲线（每 100 个 episode 用轻度正则重拟合），读出模型预计能达到目标成功率 75% 的那个难度，换算回目标 tau，并裁剪到 0.05 到 0.95 之间得到下一难度。若曲线过平或目标落在已见范围之外，则改为把难度朝使准确率更接近 75% 的方向小步调整。【作者需决定：75% 这个目标是作用在成功率(准确率 a，推荐)上，还是作用在平滑后的 margin 上，因为这两个胜任度度量可能不一致，而用 margin 作目标需要另设其取值。】\n\n*控制器在线拟合准确率对 $d_{hat}$ 的 logistic 回归，反解出目标成功率 p*=0.75 处的 $d_{hat}$，再映射回 $\\tau $ 并裁剪到 [0.05, 0.95]，从而合成略高于模型当前胜任度的难度。*\n$$ \\tau_{t+1} = \\mathrm{clip}\\!\\left(\\, \\mathrm{acc}_{\\mathrm{Bayes}}^{-1}\\!\\big(\\hat{d}^{*}\\big),\\; \\tau_{\\min},\\, \\tau_{\\max}\\right), \\quad \\hat{d}^{*}:\\; \\sigma(\\beta_0 + \\beta_1 \\hat{d}^{*}) = p^{*} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这会把下一个难度选在略高于模型当前能力的位置——信息量最大的训练点。\n9. 运行回路：在新难度下生成下一批 64 个 episode，送入模型，仅用 AdamW 优化器（学习率 0.0003，cosine 调度）以标准交叉熵分类损失更新模型权重；控制器按自身较慢的节奏持续重拟合。生成器不通过梯度训练——只通过单一难度数值 tau 来引导。随着模型变强，其 margin 上升，回路便自动要求更难的任务。\n   - _为什么_: 回路让训练数据始终贴着模型的学习前沿，而不是浪费在它已经轻松搞定的任务上。\n\n"},{"id":"14","run_dir":"run_prompt14_hawkes","index":14,"title":"Per-Edge Confounder Certificates for Latent-Confounded Hawkes Structure Learning","title_zh":"面向隐混淆 Hawkes 因果结构学习的逐边混淆置信证书 (Per-Edge Confounder Certificate)","method_name":"Per-Edge Confounder Certificate (PECC)","hook":"Methods for latent-confounded Hawkes discovery (PO-MHP, MOCHA) ship a single deterministic graph whose latent-confounder edges are argued correct only at the population limit, with no quantity telling a user whether any one edge survives finite event counts or an mis-specified excitation kernel. We construct a per-edge confounder certificate: a kernel-agnostic, finite-sample-calibrated reliability score that says, for each discovered confounded edge, how many more events would be needed before it is distinguishable from estimation noise.","anchor_pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","anchor_pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","domain_category":"Causal Inference & Structure Learning","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf attaches a finite-sample reliability measure to an individual discovered latent-confounder edge in a multivariate Hawkes process: every method (PO-MHP semanticscholar:6de2eba645b30df9126135b107f25c088ed6cac3, MOCHA openalex:W7077863341) emits a single deterministic graph, so given a fixed number of observed events there is no quantity that tells the user whether a particular confounded edge is distinguishable from one produced by excitation-estimation noise.","pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by recasting 'is this discovered confounded edge real?' as a per-unit measurement object over a fixed already-fit model: a confounder-responsibility estimator whose output is a calibrated reliability score per candidate latent-confounded edge, with the edge as the unit of analysis and a faithfulness constraint that the score be computed on event-stream resamples consistent with the fitted process, certified causally by perturbing (deleting/permuting) the implicated event-stream evidence and checking the score collapses.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions whether identifiability in latent-confounded Hawkes discovery must rest on a correctly-specified parametric excitation family at all: the path-based conditions in semanticscholar:6de2eba645b30df9126135b107f25c088ed6cac3 and the discrete-time-limit reduction presume the excitation kernels can be consistently estimated, but no retrieved paper tests whether the latent-confounder edges can be certified using only a kernel-agnostic invariant of the event stream rather than","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","how_closed":"Framing move (assumption_audit_and_pivot / C05): surface that PO-MHP's path-based latent-confounder identifiability silently rests on consistently-estimable excitation kernels, then pivot to a structural separability invariant of the rate-conditional second-and-third-order cross-statistics of the event counts, which carries the confounding-vs-direct-edge information without ever fitting a kernel. Companion deliverable (self_supervised_signal_engineering): the certificate's calibration signal is manufactured from the event stream's own block-bootstrap resamples and time-reversal surrogates, so the kernel-agnostic per-edge certificate is an actually-runnable estimator, not just an identifiability claim.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"causal structure learning in multivariate Hawkes / temporal point processes with latent confounders","n_papers":40,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":27},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":15,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Graph Transformer Hawkes Processes for Causal Structure Learning in Telecom Networks"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"DAG-Informed Structure Learning from Multi-Dimensional Point Processes"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Hybrid model using bond graph-TCN network and event triggered predictive control of pH neutralization process"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Human‐in‐the‐loop machine learning for healthcare: Current progress and future opportunities in electronic health records"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Recent advances in Alzheimer’s disease: mechanisms, clinical trials and new drug development strategies"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Harnessing pluralism in behavioral public policy requires insights from computational social science"}],"more":9},{"year":2025,"n":25,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Causal Structure Learning in Hawkes Processes with Complex Latent Confounder Networks"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Higher-Order Causal Structure Learning with Additive Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Learning Structure-enhanced Temporal Point Processes with Gromov-Wasserstein Regularization"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Adaptive Graph Structure Inference for Learning Multivariate Point Processes using Spiking Neural Networks"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"CausalConf: Datasize-Aware Configuration Auto-Tuning for Recurring Big Data Processing Jobs via Adaptive Causal Structure Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Biological Regulatory Network Inference through Circular Causal Structure Learning"}],"more":19},{"year":2026,"n":1,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"}],"more":0}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot; reframe_as_solvable_object; structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"assumption_audit_and_pivot; reframe_as_solvable_object; structural_prior_encoding","count":1,"share":0.025},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution; unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"architectural_operator_substitution; unify_into_shared_representation","count":1,"share":0.025},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding; heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"structural_prior_encoding; heterogeneous_decomposition","count":1,"share":0.025},{"pattern_id":"relax_discrete_search_to_continuous; structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"relax_discrete_search_to_continuous; structural_prior_encoding","count":1,"share":0.025},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding; targeted_self_supervised_objective","pattern_name":"structural_prior_encoding; targeted_self_supervised_objective","count":1,"share":0.025},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution; relax_discrete_search_to_continuous","pattern_name":"architectural_operator_substitution; relax_discrete_search_to_continuous","count":1,"share":0.025},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object; adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"reframe_as_solvable_object; adapt_via_conditioning","count":1,"share":0.025},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot; relax_discrete_search_to_continuous","pattern_name":"assumption_audit_and_pivot; relax_discrete_search_to_continuous","count":1,"share":0.025}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"State-of-the-art causal structure learning in multivariate Hawkes processes under latent confounding establishes only POPULATION-LEVEL identifiability: the PO-MHP framework (semanticscholar:6de2eba645b30df9126135b107f25c088ed6cac3) reduces continuous-time event sequences to a discrete-time causal model in the small-interval limit and proves necessary-and-sufficient path-based conditions for recovering latent subprocesses, but its two-phase iterative algorithm alternates between edge inference and latent-node discovery using point estimates that carry no finite-sample error control, while MOCHA (openalex:W7077863341) jointly learns a time-varying DAG over event-stream nodes only under an explicit causal-sufficiency assumption that forbids latent confounders altogether. As a result, when the true latent confounder network is dense or the observed sub-Hawkes excitation kernels are estimated from finitely many events, neither method can say which discovered latent nodes and confounded edges are statistically reliable versus artifacts of estimation noise or of a mis-specified excitation kernel — the recovered structure is a single deterministic graph with no notion of how many events are required before a given confounded edge becomes distinguishable from a spurious one, so the output is unfalsifiable on the very partially-observed regime it targets (echoed by InvarGC, openalex:W4416246513, which only MITIGATES latent confounding via cross-environment invariance rather than certifying any individual edge).","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:6de2eba645b30df9126135b107f25c088ed6cac3","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Defines a partially-observed multivariate Hawkes causal model (PO-MHP) that allows cycles, self-loops and latent subprocesses, reduces the continuous-time process to a discrete-time causal model as the interval shrinks, and proves necessary-and-sufficient path-based conditions under which a two-phase iterative algorithm recovers both the latent subprocesses and the causal edges. Its identifiability and recovery guarantees are entirely population-level / asymptotic and assume faithfulness plus a correctly-specified excitation family: the method emits a single deterministic graph with no finite-sample stability, no per-edge confidence, and no characterization of the event-count regime in which a confounded edge becomes distinguishable from estimation noise, so on real finite event streams there is no way to know which discovered latent confounders are real."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7077863341","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"MOCHA jointly learns a time-varying DAG with learnable structural weights over temporal-point-process nodes in an end-to-end differentiable framework, capturing multi-order and time-evolving causality. It assumes causal sufficiency (all relevant subprocesses observed) and enforces strict acyclicity, so it cannot represent latent confounders or the cyclic excitation natural to Hawkes processes, and its learned edge weights are predictive parameters with no identifiability certificate."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416246513","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"InvarGC drops both causal-sufficiency and known-intervention assumptions for Granger discovery by exploiting invariance of true causal mechanisms across heterogeneous environments, mitigating latent confounding. It operates on regularly-sampled continuous-valued time series (not event/point-process data), requires multiple heterogeneous environments to exist, and only mitigates confounding at the aggregate-graph level rather than certifying or quantifying any individual confounded edge's reliability."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7101945133","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Shows that pairwise causal direction is identifiable from rank-deficiency of a specially-constructed higher-order cumulant matrix even under an arbitrary number of latent confounders, in a static linear-non-Gaussian model, without iterative procedures. The result is static and pairwise: it never lifts the cumulant rank-deficiency certificate to temporal point-process intensities or to a network of confounded edges, so it gives a per-pair certificate but not one usable on Hawkes excitation structure."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:fdc42486763f5b22229a0daf7698d21ade4bf24b","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"CADYT performs continuous-time causal discovery on irregularly-sampled dynamical systems via difference-based causal models with exact Gaussian-process inference, scored by the Algorithmic Markov Condition / MDL. It targets continuous-state dynamical systems rather than event streams and assumes causal sufficiency, so latent confounders and Hawkes excitation are out of scope, and its score-based greedy search yields a single graph with no per-edge finite-sample reliability statement."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"causal structure learning in multivariate Hawkes / temporal point processes with latent confounders","venue":"ICLR 2026 (primary_area: causal reasoning)","time":"2026","data":["synthetic multivariate Hawkes event sequences with planted latent confounder subprocesses (known ground-truth summary causal graph)","neuroscience spike trains (partially observed neuron populations)","social / information-cascade event logs"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher comfortable with point-process likelihoods, causal-discovery identifiability proofs, and structure estimation","preference":"both","baseline":"PO-MHP two-phase iterative latent-subprocess discovery (Causal Structure Learning in Hawkes Processes with Complex Latent Confounder Networks, semanticscholar:6de2eba645b30df9126135b107f25c088ed6cac3); MOCHA time-varying DAG over observed TPP nodes (openalex:W7077863341)","limitation":"existing latent-confounder Hawkes discovery proves population-level (asymptotic) identifiability under faithfulness + path-based conditions but gives no finite-sample reliability control: the discovered set of latent subprocesses and edges has no calibrated error / stability guarantee, so on real partially-observed data the iterative algorithm can over- or under-count latent confounders with no way to tell which discovered edges are trustworthy","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["domain","venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"Central shared object (shared_object thread): a per-edge confounder certificate Cij in [0,1] attached to every candidate edge i<-j that a base latent-confounded Hawkes learner discovers, where Cij is the calibrated probability that the i,j cross-dependence is a genuine latent-confounded (or direct) structural edge rather than an artifact of finite-sample excitation-estimation noise. ANCHOR LEG (C00 reframe): we fix the base learner's output graph G (e.g. PO-MHP's recovered observed+latent subprocess graph) as the already-trained model and define, per edge, a confounder-responsibility statistic Sij computed from a kernel-agnostic structural invariant Iij (defined below) of the observed event counts binned at width Delta (the same small-interval discretization PO-MHP uses); the unit of analysis is the ordered observed-process pair (i,j) and the faithfulness constraint is that Sij is only computed from resamples that preserve the fitted process's first-order rate, so the score reflects structure not rate mismatch. We turn Sij into a calibrated Cij by a stability-selection object: draw B stationary block-bootstrap resamples of the event stream (block length L = c/spectral_gap, c=5 a fixed hyperparameter, spectral_gap read from the base learner's estimated influence-matrix spectral radius) plus B time-reversal surrogate streams that destroy directed excitation while preserving marginal rates, and set Cij = (fraction of bootstrap resamples with Sij above the (1-alpha) quantile of the surrogate Sij null), alpha=0.05 fixed; tractability is bought by computing Iij once per resample via a single O(T log T) FFT of the binned counts rather than re-fitting the model (the one compression trick). AUDIT-PIVOT LEG (C05): the invariant Iij is the rate-normalized lag-window cross-cumulant separability signature — concretely, stack the lag-h normalized cross-covariance r_ij(h) = Cov(dNi(t), dNj(t-h)) / sqrt(rate_i*rate_j) and the third-order rate-conditional cross-cumulant k_ij(h1,h2) over a fixed lag grid h in {1..H}*Delta (H=20), and define Iij as the rank-deficiency margin of the resulting cumulant slice matrix (smallest singular value below a learned threshold tau indicates a shared latent driver, following the static cumulant rank-deficiency certificate of openalex:W7101945133 lifted here to lagged point-process counts). This invariant is computed entirely from counts and never references an estimated excitation kernel phi_ij, so the certificate's validity does not inherit PO-MHP's correctly-specified-kernel assumption; the COMPANION (self_supervised_signal_engineering) supplies the calibration: the (1-alpha) null quantile of Sij is manufactured from the time-reversal surrogate streams, an internally-generated supervision signal that requires no ground-truth graph. Both legs read from and write to the same object Cij: the anchor gives it finite-sample calibration, the audit-pivot makes the underlying statistic kernel-agnostic, so a reviewer reads one certificate, not two methods.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"I judged the two gaps share machinery (one object Cij) rather than needing separate modules because the anchor's reliability question and the sibling's kernel-agnostic question are the same per-edge quantity viewed under two requirements (calibrated AND assumption-light): if I built two modules the certificate would either be calibrated-but-kernel-dependent or kernel-agnostic-but-uncalibrated, defeating the point. I considered making the invariant the estimated excitation matrix's bootstrap variance (rejected: that lands on lineage node n0/n1, plain excitation-MLE / Granger-sparsity, a regression, and re-inherits the correctly-specified-kernel assumption the audit leg exists to remove), and considered a fully-Bayesian posterior-over-graphs (collateral node c1) (rejected: it answers whole-graph uncertainty, not the per-edge finite-sample distinguishability the bottleneck demands, and is far heavier). The cumulant rank-deficiency invariant draws on a source (lagged higher-order count cumulants) the lineage tree does not yet occupy, avoiding regression while remaining computable in O(T log T).","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on synthetic multivariate Hawkes data with planted latent-confounder subprocesses (known ground-truth summary causal graph, varied across confounder-network density and observed-fraction), run PO-MHP to get candidate edges, then attach our certificate Cij and threshold at 0.9; measure structural Hamming distance (SHD) of the thresholded graph versus the raw PO-MHP graph against ground truth, across a sweep of total event counts T. If the candidate works, certificate-thresholded SHD decreases relative to raw PO-MHP in the low-T / dense-confounder regime (the certificate removes exactly the unreliable edges), and the calibration curve of Cij versus empirical edge-correctness frequency stays near the diagonal (well-calibrated) where raw PO-MHP has no such curve. The named load-bearing variable is the cumulant rank-deficiency margin Iij = tau - sigma_min(M_ij): the negative control replaces Iij with the bootstrap variance of the ESTIMATED excitation entry phi_ij_hat (a kernel-dependent statistic) while keeping the identical calibration wrapper; the anti-tautology prediction is that under this control the DOWNSTREAM SHD of the thresholded graph rises back toward (or above) the raw-PO-MHP SHD in the mis-specified-kernel regime, because the kernel-dependent statistic re-inherits the excitation-mis-specification error the invariant was designed to avoid. A positive control using ONLY Iij (no base learner, edges proposed purely by ranking Iij) is expected to recover most of the certificate's SHD-reduction on correctly-specified data, confirming the invariant, not the base learner, carries the reliability signal.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:6de2eba645b30df9126135b107f25c088ed6cac3","delta":"They prove population-level necessary-and-sufficient path conditions for recovering latent subprocesses and emit one deterministic graph; we derive a per-edge finite-sample calibrated certificate Cij plus an events-to-significance number N*_ij that their single point estimate cannot produce, and we make it kernel-agnostic so it does not inherit their consistently-estimable-excitation assumption."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7077863341","delta":"MOCHA learns a time-varying DAG over observed nodes under explicit causal sufficiency with edge weights that are predictive parameters; we attach a calibrated reliability score to edges in a model that ALLOWS latent confounders, and our score is validated by perturbation rather than read off as a learned weight."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7101945133","delta":"They certify pairwise causal direction from higher-order cumulant rank-deficiency in a STATIC linear-non-Gaussian model; we lift the rank-deficiency margin to LAGGED rate-conditional cross-cumulants of point-process counts and embed it in a finite-sample bootstrap-calibrated per-edge certificate over a network, which their static pairwise result does not construct."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416246513","delta":"InvarGC mitigates latent confounding via cross-environment invariance on regular time series and certifies nothing at the individual-edge level; we operate on a single event stream (no multiple environments required) and output a per-edge calibrated certificate rather than an aggregate-graph mitigation."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:6de2eba645b30df9126135b107f25c088ed6cac3","what_step_was_missed":"PO-MHP establishes the discrete-time-limit reduction and path-based identifiability but reports recovery as a single graph; to already contain our contribution it would have needed to construct a per-edge finite-sample reliability statistic that is computable WITHOUT the estimated excitation kernels — specifically a lagged rate-conditional cross-cumulant rank-deficiency margin calibrated against time-reversal surrogates — which their kernel-and-path-based machinery never builds because their guarantees live entirely at the population limit and depend on consistent kernel estimation."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":137,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"No hard floor fired (gap_closure_reject_check no entry is candidate_match=yes; anti_pattern matched_pattern_id=null; paper_pointed_threat is competing-not-exact and addressable). Choosing revise because recipe_application_check.entries[1].verdict=borderline on the load-bearing C05 leg (the kernel-agnostic identifiability sufficiency is asserted by lifting a static pairwise cumulant result, per the reject lesson 'imposing structural constraints without proving those constraints are sufficient for recovery') and because paper_pointed_threat names a specific addressable field (differentiation_from_lit) — both hit load-bearing structural properties, so the candidate should be sharpened, not advanced as-is.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf attaches a finite-sample reliability measure to an individual discovered latent-confounder edge in a multivariate Hawkes process: every method (PO-MHP semanticscholar:6de2eba645b30df9126135b107f25c088ed6cac3, MOCHA openalex:W7077863341) emits a single deterministic graph, so given a fixed number of observed events there is no quantity that tells the user whether a particular confounded edge is distinguishable from one produced by excitation-estimation noise.","main_pattern":"reframe_as_solvable_object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The signature failure is treating the reframing as a mechanical wrapper: taking an established attribution, decomposition, or estimation tool and pointing it at a new input granularity, architecture, or domain without re-deriving why the resulting scores are faithful, supplying the computation but not the causal validation.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Pointing an off-the-shelf decomposition at a coarser input granularity without showing the coarser units preserve the signal reads as a wrapper, not a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The certificate is not an off-the-shelf decomposition retargeted; the invariant Iij (lagged rate-conditional cross-cumulant rank-deficiency) is a newly-constructed statistic with an explicit faithfulness constraint (resamples preserve fitted first-order rate)."},{"lesson_quoted":"Proposing a new attribution definition without an axiomatic or causal argument for why it should count as ground-truth collapses the moment a reviewer asks why this is the real importance.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Cij is causally certified by step 9's negative control (deleting/permuting implicated event windows must collapse the score and return downstream SHD toward baseline), giving the definition a causal grounding rather than correlation-only."},{"lesson_quoted":"Conflating a methodological artifact -- a computation-granularity difference, a degenerate zero baseline -- with genuine signal undermines the entire premise once the confound is identified.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The block-bootstrap block length L=5/(1-rho) and bin width Delta are tuning choices that could themselves inject a granularity artifact into Cij; the candidate fixes them as hyperparameters but does not yet show Cij is invariant to reasonable Delta/L choices, so a reviewer could attribute calibration to the binning."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions whether identifiability in latent-confounded Hawkes discovery must rest on a correctly-specified parametric excitation family at all: the path-based conditions in semanticscholar:6de2eba645b30df9126135b107f25c088ed6cac3 and the discrete-time-limit reduction presume the excitation kernels can be consistently estimated, but no retrieved paper tests whether the latent-confounder edges can be certified using only a kernel-agnostic invariant of the event stream rather than the estimated excitation functions themselves.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The signature failure is an identifiability claim that outruns its proof: the pivoted assumption was not actually load-bearing, or recovery/'consistency' is asserted while the decisive object (latent identifiability) is never established, or structural constraints are imposed without proving they are SUFFICIENT for recovery.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Imposing structural constraints to claim interpretability or disentanglement without proving those constraints are sufficient for recovery leaves the result indistinguishable from a post-hoc heuristic.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The candidate claims the cumulant rank-deficiency invariant carries the confounding-vs-direct-edge information but lifts openalex:W7101945133's static pairwise sufficiency to lagged point-process counts without a re-derived sufficiency proof for the point-process setting, so the identifiability sufficiency is asserted, not yet proven."},{"lesson_quoted":"Stacking two established frameworks and re-proving identifiability of the union reads as incremental unless the pivoted assumption was genuinely load-bearing and the union admits a regime neither framework could reach alone.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The pivoted assumption (consistently-estimable excitation kernels) is demonstrably load-bearing in PO-MHP's path-based proof, and the kernel-agnostic regime (certification under mis-specified kernels) is one neither PO-MHP nor the static cumulant paper reaches, so this is not a mere union."},{"lesson_quoted":"Proving identifiability conditions the algorithm neither enforces nor verifies creates a theory-practice disconnect that undermines both the soundness and the significance of the claim.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The algorithm directly computes and thresholds the invariant the claim rests on (steps 2-3) and verifies it via surrogate calibration (steps 6-7), so the condition is enforced and checkable rather than only assumed."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No Reject lesson is marked candidate_match=yes, so no hard-floor trigger. Two borderlines drive the aggregate: the C05 entry's 'structural constraints without proving sufficient for recovery' (the point-process sufficiency of the cumulant invariant is asserted by lifting a static pairwise result) and the C00 entry's binning-artifact concern (Cij's invariance to Delta/L is unshown). The C05 borderline hits a load-bearing structural property (the kernel-agnostic identifiability claim) and is the heavier of the two."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf attaches a finite-sample reliability measure to an individual discovered latent-confounder edge in a multivariate Hawkes process: every method (PO-MHP semanticscholar:6de2eba645b30df9126135b107f25c088ed6cac3, MOCHA openalex:W7077863341) emits a single deterministic graph, so given a fixed number of observed events there is no quantity that tells the user whether a particular confounded edge is distinguishable from one produced by excitation-estimation noise.","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Recast an opaque transparency question about an already-trained model as a concrete measurement over a well-studied object whose output is a per-unit responsibility/uncertainty score, choosing the right unit of analysis and faithfulness constraint, buying tractability with a single compression trick, and certifying fidelity by a causal intervention that flips behavior when the identified object is perturbed.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism fixes the base learner's graph G as the already-fit model, takes the per-edge (i,j) as the unit of analysis, defines a per-edge reliability score Cij over a stability-selection object, buys tractability with the single O(T log T) FFT compression trick (step 2/5), and certifies fidelity causally via step 9's perturbation negative control on the implicated event windows. The C00 signature move is present, not generic.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions whether identifiability in latent-confounded Hawkes discovery must rest on a correctly-specified parametric excitation family at all: the path-based conditions in semanticscholar:6de2eba645b30df9126135b107f25c088ed6cac3 and the discrete-time-limit reduction presume the excitation kernels can be consistently estimated, but no retrieved paper tests whether the latent-confounder edges can be certified using only a kernel-agnostic invariant of the event stream rather than the estimated excitation functions themselves.","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Take an existing identifiability/recovery theorem and pivot on its required assumption, trading a distributional/parametric assumption for a structural, architectural, or geometric one that carries the same identifying power, then re-prove recovery up to the field's standard ambiguity class and operationalize it as a regularizer/estimator.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism explicitly surfaces PO-MHP's consistently-estimable-excitation assumption and swaps it for a structural invariant (lagged cross-cumulant rank-deficiency margin computed from counts only, never the estimated kernel phi_ij), operationalized as the estimator Iij. The pivot (distributional/parametric -> structural invariant) is the C05 signature move and is performed; what is incomplete is the re-derivation of recovery sufficiency in the point-process setting, which is a depth issue, not a bypass.","verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The C00 anchor leg cleanly applies the per-unit-measurement-plus-causal-certification move. The C05 leg performs the assumption-pivot to a structural invariant (the signature move is present), but the recovery-sufficiency proof for the lifted point-process invariant is asserted rather than derived, making it borderline rather than fully applied."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["reframe_as_solvable_object","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"The composition_set contains no heterogeneous_decomposition, so none of the three documented reject-favored compositions (all of which require heterogeneous_decomposition) match; the companion self_supervised_signal_engineering is a leg-level companion, not a gap_closure main_pattern, so it does not enter the composition set."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:62475a89e26519092a5fbd6e2c28817dbd53b98c","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"'Hawkes Identification with a Prescribed Causal Basis: Closed-Form Estimators and Asymptotics' provides closed-form estimators with asymptotic (large-sample) distributional results for Hawkes causal structure, which is the nearest competitor because asymptotic normality could in principle be turned into per-edge confidence intervals. It does not subsume the candidate: its results are kernel/basis-PRESCRIBED (it assumes a correctly-specified causal basis, exactly the assumption the candidate's audit leg removes) and are asymptotic rather than finite-sample-calibrated against a surrogate null, and it does not address latent confounders. The candidate's claim stands because its certificate is both kernel-agnostic and finite-sample-calibrated in the partially-observed (latent-confounded) regime this paper does not treat.","addressable_via":"differentiation_from_lit -- add an explicit delta versus this closed-form-asymptotics paper clarifying that its asymptotic basis-prescribed CIs require a correctly-specified kernel and observed-sufficiency, which the candidate's kernel-agnostic latent-confounded certificate does not."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","issue":"gap_closure_reject_check C05 borderline + recipe_application_check C05 borderline: the point-process recovery-sufficiency of the lifted cumulant rank-deficiency invariant is asserted, not earned (the lesson 'imposing structural constraints without proving sufficient for recovery').","fix_direction":"Scope the identifiability claim to what is actually provable: state that the candidate establishes the invariant Iij as a NECESSARY signature of a shared latent driver under the stationarity + bounded-excitation conditions already used by PO-MHP (a one-direction implication that follows from the lagged second/third-order moment structure), and explicitly frame full SUFFICIENCY for point-process recovery as a conjecture validated empirically via the calibration curve and the positive control, rather than claiming a proven recovery-up-to-ambiguity-class theorem. Name the exact ambiguity class (edge presence/absence, not kernel shape) the certificate addresses."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","issue":"gap_closure_reject_check C00 borderline: Cij's invariance to the binning width Delta and block length L is unshown, so calibration could be a granularity artifact (lesson 'conflating a methodological artifact ... with genuine signal').","fix_direction":"Add to core_mechanism that the certificate is reported across a small grid of (Delta, L) and an edge is only certified (Cij>=0.9) if it clears threshold for the majority of the grid, so the score reflects structure rather than a single binning choice; note this stability-across-binning check as part of the faithfulness constraint."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat: nearest competitor (closed-form-asymptotics Hawkes identification) not differentiated.","fix_direction":"Append a differentiation_from_lit entry for semanticscholar:62475a89e26519092a5fbd6e2c28817dbd53b98c stating it gives asymptotic CIs only under a PRESCRIBED correctly-specified causal basis with observed-sufficiency, whereas the candidate's certificate is finite-sample-calibrated, kernel-agnostic, and valid under latent confounding."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Scoped the C05 identifiability claim to a one-direction NECESSARY-signature implication under PO-MHP's stationarity + bounded-excitation conditions, named the ambiguity class (edge presence/absence, not kernel shape), and reframed full point-process recovery sufficiency as an empirically-validated conjecture (calibration curve + positive control) rather than a proven recovery theorem."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added a stability-across-binning faithfulness constraint: the certificate is computed over a small grid of (Delta, L) and an edge is certified only if Cij>=0.9 for the majority of grid points, so calibration reflects structure rather than a single binning/block-length artifact."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Appended a differentiation entry for semanticscholar:62475a89e26519092a5fbd6e2c28817dbd53b98c clarifying its asymptotic CIs require a PRESCRIBED correctly-specified causal basis with observed-sufficiency, whereas the candidate's certificate is finite-sample-calibrated, kernel-agnostic, and valid under latent confounding."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Per-Edge Confounder Certificates for Latent-Confounded Hawkes Structure Learning\n\n**Method.** Per-Edge Confounder Certificate (PECC)\n\n## Motivation\nImagine you record events from many interacting sources over time — say neurons firing, or posts cascading on a social platform — and you want to know which source causally triggers which. Such data is modeled with a multivariate Hawkes process (a process where past events raise the chance of future ones). The hard part is that some driving sources are never observed; these hidden 'latent confounders' can make two observed sources look causally linked when they are merely driven by the same hidden cause. The best current method, PO-MHP (Partially-Observed Multivariate Hawkes Process), proves it can recover the true graph of links including hidden ones — but only in the idealized limit of infinitely many events. On a real, finite dataset it just prints one graph with no indication of which edges to trust. A competing method, MOCHA, refuses to allow hidden confounders at all.\n\nThis matters now because PO-MHP (2025) finally gives us a principled list of candidate edges to scrutinize, and a separate 2025 result shows that a hidden-confounder fingerprint can be read off a 'cumulant' (a higher-order statistic) without knowing the exact triggering shape — but only for static, pairwise data. Nobody has carried that fingerprint over to event streams and wrapped it in a finite-sample reliability check.\n\nPO-MHP stopped at the population limit because its proof technique needs the triggering kernel to be estimated correctly and lives at infinity, so a finite-sample, per-edge trust score was simply outside its toolkit. MOCHA stopped because it assumes everything relevant is observed. The cumulant-fingerprint paper stopped because its result is static and pairwise, never lifted to time-lagged event counts or a whole network.\n\nWhen we close this gap, a researcher can keep only the edges that survive scrutiny on their actual data and read off, per untrustworthy edge, how many more events they would need to collect — turning an untestable single graph into an auditable result that is also robust to getting the triggering shape wrong.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n\n1. Convert each event source's timestamps into a count-per-time-bin series using bin width Delta (the same discretization the base method uses). Run a base latent-confounder Hawkes learner — by default PO-MHP (Partially-Observed Multivariate Hawkes Process) — on these counts to get: (1) a candidate graph G listing which source may causally influence which (including hidden-source edges), (2) the spectral radius rho, which is the largest eigenvalue magnitude of the fitted influence matrix and just measures how strongly events self-propagate, and (3) each source's average event rate $lambda_{i}.$ Keep all three fixed; you will never re-train the base model afterward.\n   - _Why_: You need a concrete list of candidate edges before you can ask how trustworthy each one is.\n\n### Kernel-agnostic invariant\n*Extract a count-only rank-deficiency fingerprint of shared latent drivers, free of the triggering-kernel assumption.*\n\n2. For each candidate edge (i,j), build a matrix $M_{ij}$ purely from the event counts. First make a centered, rate-normalized count series for each source. Then compute two things over a grid of time lags h = 1..20: (a) the lagged cross-covariance $r_{ij}(h)$ (how counts of i co-vary with counts of j shifted back by h, normalized by their rates) using a Fast Fourier Transform (FFT), and (b) the third-order cross-cumulant slice $k_{ij}(h1,h2)$ (a higher-order co-variation over pairs of lags, each series divided by its own rate). Stack these into one matrix $M_{ij}$ and standardize its columns to comparable scale. Crucially, use only the counts — never the model's estimated triggering kernel.\n\n*The lagged rate-normalized cross-covariance $r_{ij}(h)$ and third-order rate-conditional cross-cumulant slice $k_{ij}(h_{1},h_{2})$ are stacked over a fixed lag grid into the cumulant slice matrix $M_{ij},$ computed from counts alone.*\n$$ M_{ij} = \\big[\\, r_{ij}(h),\\; k_{ij}(h_1,h_2) \\,\\big]_{h,h_1,h_2 \\in \\{1,\\dots,H\\}\\Delta}, \\quad r_{ij}(h) = \\frac{\\mathrm{Cov}\\!\\left(dN_i(t),\\, dN_j(t-h)\\right)}{\\sqrt{\\lambda_i \\lambda_j}} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: These count-only statistics carry the hidden-confounder fingerprint without depending on getting the triggering shape right.\n3. From the matrix $M_{ij}$ compute its smallest singular value $\\sigma _{min}$ (via a singular value decomposition, SVD) — a small value means the matrix is close to rank-deficient, which is the algebraic fingerprint of a shared hidden driver behind sources i and j. Define the score Sij $= \\tau  -  \\sigma _{min},$ where $\\tau $ is a cutoff learned in the next step; a positive score is evidence of a shared hidden cause. Read this only as a necessary fingerprint: a real shared driver makes the matrix rank-deficient, so this certifies whether an edge exists (not the exact shape of the triggering). The other direction is checked empirically later, not claimed here.\n\n*The kernel-agnostic invariant Iij is the rank-deficiency margin: threshold $\\tau $ minus the smallest singular value $\\sigma _{min}$ of $M_{ij}$; a positive margin signals a shared latent driver. Sij is set equal to Iij.*\n$$ I_{ij} = \\tau - \\sigma_{\\min}(M_{ij}), \\qquad S_{ij} = I_{ij} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A near-rank-deficient cumulant matrix is the algebraic signature of a common hidden cause, computable straight from data.\n4. Choose the cutoff $\\tau $ automatically instead of by hand. Set aside some of the resampled datasets (from the next two steps) and search over a single number $\\tau $ to find the value that best separates real-data smallest-singular-values from surrogate (no-signal) ones — for example by maximizing the area under the ROC curve that distinguishes the two pools. Fit one global $\\tau $ shared across all edges, then reuse it everywhere. Letting the data pick $\\tau $ avoids baking in an arbitrary cutoff that could manufacture a result.\n   - _Why_: Letting the data set the cutoff avoids baking in an arbitrary threshold that could fake the result.\n\n### Finite-sample calibration\n*Turn the raw invariant into a calibrated per-edge reliability score plus an events-to-significance number, stable across binning.*\n\n5. Create 200 bootstrap copies of the data using stationary block bootstrap: cut the time series into contiguous blocks of length $L = 5/(1- rho)$ bins and reassemble randomly, which keeps each source's rate and short-range triggering intact. Resample whole multivariate blocks together so the cross-source structure inside a block survives. For each copy, recompute the score Sij by re-running only the fast Fourier-based statistic (steps step 2 (For each candidate edge)–step 3 (From the matrix $M_{ij}$ compute $its\\dots )),$ never the base model. This yields 200 score values per edge showing how much the score fluctuates at your finite data size.\n   - _Why_: Resampling shows how much the score wobbles at your finite event count — the basis for a reliability number.\n6. Create 200 'no-signal' surrogate datasets by time-reversing each source's sequence of inter-event gaps — this keeps how often events happen but erases their directed triggering. Recompute the score Sij on each to get a baseline distribution of what the score looks like when there is no real causal direction; no ground-truth graph is needed because the baseline comes from your own data. 【author decision: reverse each source independently (a strong baseline that also erases cross-source co-movement) versus reversing the whole multi-source timeline together (a tighter baseline that keeps co-occurrence but removes only time direction) — choose which baseline the certificate should be tested against.】\n   - _Why_: Reversing time destroys real causal direction, so these give a no-signal baseline built from your own data with no ground-truth graph needed.\n7. Take the 95th percentile of the surrogate scores as the cutoff $q_{ij},$ then set the certificate Cij to the fraction of bootstrap copies whose score exceeds $q_{ij}$ — a number between 0 and 1 acting like a calibrated reliability probability. To make sure this is not an accident of one bin size, repeat the whole computation over $a 3\\times 3$ grid of bin width Delta (half, base, double) crossed with block-length factor c (3, 5, 8), and only certify an edge when Cij is at least 0.9 on most (5 of 9) grid settings. Save a flag noting whether each edge passed across the grid.\n\n*The certificate Cij is the fraction of block-bootstrap resamples whose score Sij exceeds the $(1-\\alpha )$ quantile $q_{ij}$ of the time-reversal-surrogate null distribution.*\n$$ q_{ij} = Q_{1-\\alpha}\\big(\\{S^{(0,b)}_{ij}\\}_{b=1}^{B}\\big), \\qquad C_{ij} = \\frac{1}{B}\\sum_{b=1}^{B} \\mathbf{1}\\big[\\,S^{(b)}_{ij} > q_{ij}\\,\\big] \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Comparing resamples to the no-signal baseline turns the score into a calibrated probability, and the grid check rules out that it is just an artifact of one binning choice.\n8. For each edge, compute N*ij: the number of events you would need before the edge becomes reliably distinguishable from noise. Trace how the lower 95% bound of the score grows as you feed in more events (by re-running on increasingly long prefixes of the stream), assume it grows in proportion to the square root of the event count, and extrapolate to find the smallest event count at which that lower bound would clear the cutoff $q_{ij}.$ Edges already certified return a number at or below your current count; uncertified edges return a concrete 'collect this many more events' target.\n\n*The events-to-significance number N*ij is the smallest event count T at which the lower 95% bootstrap bound of Sij, extrapolated under the $\\surd T$ concentration rate, first exceeds the null quantile $q_{ij}.$*\n$$ N^{*}_{ij} = \\min\\Big\\{ T : \\widehat{S}^{\\,\\text{low-95\\%}}_{ij}(T) > q_{ij} \\Big\\}, \\quad \\widehat{S}_{ij}(T) \\propto \\sqrt{T} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This gives the practitioner an actionable 'collect this many more events' number for edges that are not yet certifiable.\n\n### Causal certification + output\n*Causally validate certified edges by perturbation and emit the annotated, thresholded graph.*\n\n9. Run a causal sanity check on the edges with high certificates. For a held-out subset, remove (or shuffle in time) the events in the windows that supposedly carry the hidden-driver evidence for that edge, recompute the certificate, and confirm that the downstream structural error (how far the kept graph is from the truth on synthetic data, called structural Hamming distance, SHD) moves back toward the no-confounder baseline. An edge is certified if its certificate collapses when you remove its evidence, and flagged if the score stubbornly persists. 【author decision: pinpoint which events are 'the evidence' either by attributing the matrix's rank-deficiency to specific lags/sources via its singular vectors, or by sliding-window search for the windows whose removal most lowers the score — this decides exactly which events the causal check removes.】\n   - _Why_: A genuine edge should lose its certificate when you remove the evidence behind it — this is the causal sanity check.\n10. Produce the final output: the original graph with every edge labeled by its reliability certificate Cij, its events-to-significance number N*ij, and whether it passed across the binning grid, plus a clean sub-graph keeping only the edges with Cij at least 0.9 on most grid settings and that passed the causal check. Save it as a simple edge table (source, target, certificate, events-needed, grid-passed, causal-certified) so a user can sort and audit each edge.\n   - _Why_: This is the auditable, trustworthy graph the practitioner actually wanted instead of one unlabeled guess.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 面向隐混淆 Hawkes 因果结构学习的逐边混淆置信证书 (Per-Edge Confounder Certificate)\n\n**方法名称.** Per-Edge Confounder Certificate (PECC)\n\n## 研究动机\n设想你长期记录许多相互作用来源产生的事件——比如神经元放电，或社交平台上的转发级联——并想知道哪个来源在因果上触发了哪个。这类数据常用 multivariate Hawkes process（一种过去事件会提高未来事件发生概率的过程）来建模。难点在于：有些驱动来源从未被观测到，这些隐藏的 latent confounder（隐混淆）会让两个观测来源看起来有因果联系，其实它们只是被同一个隐藏原因驱动。当前最好的方法 PO-MHP（Partially-Observed Multivariate Hawkes Process，部分可观测多元 Hawkes 过程）证明了它能恢复包含隐藏节点的真实因果图——但只在事件数趋于无穷的理想极限下成立。在真实有限的数据上，它只输出一张图，却不告诉你哪些边可信。另一个方法 MOCHA 干脆完全不允许隐混淆。\n\n现在正是时机：PO-MHP（2025）终于给出了一份有原则的候选边清单可供审视；另有一项 2025 年的结果表明，无需知道精确的触发形状，就能从 cumulant（一种高阶统计量）中读出隐混淆的指纹——但仅限于静态、成对的数据。还没有人把这个指纹搬到事件流上，并为它加装一个有限样本的可靠性检验。\n\nPO-MHP 止步于总体极限，是因为它的证明需要正确估计触发核且只在无穷处成立，因此一个有限样本、逐边的可信度分数根本不在它的工具箱内。MOCHA 止步，是因为它假设所有相关来源都被观测到。累积量指纹那篇止步，是因为其结果是静态且成对的，从未推广到带时间滞后的事件计数或整个网络。\n\n一旦补上这个缺口，研究者就能只保留在自己真实数据上经得起检验的边，并对每条不可信的边读出还需再收集多少事件——把一张无法检验的单一图，变成既可审计、又对触发形状估计错误具有鲁棒性的结果。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景\n\n1. 把每个事件来源的时间戳按 bin 宽 Delta（与基础方法相同的离散化）转换成每个时间格的计数序列。在这些计数上运行一个能处理隐混淆的基础 Hawkes 学习器——默认用 PO-MHP(Partially-Observed Multivariate Hawkes Process，部分可观测多元 Hawkes 过程)——得到三样东西：(1) 候选图 G，列出哪个来源可能在因果上影响哪个（含隐来源的边）；(2) 谱半径 rho，即拟合出的影响矩阵最大特征值的模，它只衡量事件自我传播的强度；(3) 每个来源的平均事件率 $lambda_{i}$。把这三样都固定下来，之后绝不再训练基础模型。\n   - _为什么_: 要先有一份具体的候选边清单，才能逐条追问它们各自有多可信。\n\n### 核无关不变量\n*提取仅依赖计数的共同隐驱动秩亏指纹，摆脱对触发核的假设。*\n\n2. 对每条候选边 (i,j)，仅用事件计数构造一个矩阵 $M_{ij}$。先为每个来源做一条去中心、按速率归一化的计数序列。然后在时间滞后 h = 1..20 的网格上算两样东西：(a) 滞后互协方差 $r_{ij}(h)$（即 i 的计数与向后平移 h 的 j 的计数如何共变，并按各自速率归一化），用 Fast Fourier Transform(快速傅里叶变换, FFT) 计算；(b) 三阶互累积量切片 $k_{ij}(h1,h2)$（一种在两个滞后上的高阶共变，每条序列都除以自身速率）。把它们堆叠成一个矩阵 $M_{ij}$，并把各列标准化到可比的尺度。关键是：只用计数，绝不使用模型估计出的触发核。\n\n*把滞后的、用速率归一化的互协方差 $r_{ij}(h)$ 与三阶速率条件互累积量切片 $k_{ij}(h_{1},h_{2})$ 在固定滞后网格上堆叠成累积量切片矩阵 $M_{ij}$，全部仅由事件计数算出。*\n$$ M_{ij} = \\big[\\, r_{ij}(h),\\; k_{ij}(h_1,h_2) \\,\\big]_{h,h_1,h_2 \\in \\{1,\\dots,H\\}\\Delta}, \\quad r_{ij}(h) = \\frac{\\mathrm{Cov}\\!\\left(dN_i(t),\\, dN_j(t-h)\\right)}{\\sqrt{\\lambda_i \\lambda_j}} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这些仅由计数得到的统计量携带隐混淆指纹，且不依赖于把触发形状估对。\n3. 从矩阵 $M_{ij}$ 算出它的最小奇异值 $\\sigma _{min}$（用 Singular Value Decomposition(奇异值分解, SVD)）——值很小意味着矩阵接近秩亏，这正是来源 i 与 j 背后存在共同隐驱动的代数指纹。定义打分 Sij $= \\tau  -  \\sigma _{min}$，其中 $\\tau $ 是下一步学到的门槛；打分为正即为存在共同隐藏原因的证据。把它仅理解为一个必要指纹：真实的共同驱动会使矩阵秩亏，所以它认证边是否存在（而非触发的精确形状）。反方向留待之后用经验验证，这里不作断言。\n\n*核无关不变量 Iij 即秩亏边界：阈值 $\\tau $ 减去 $M_{ij}$ 的最小奇异值 $\\sigma _{min}$；边界为正表示存在共同隐驱动。打分 Sij 取为 Iij。*\n$$ I_{ij} = \\tau - \\sigma_{\\min}(M_{ij}), \\qquad S_{ij} = I_{ij} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 近乎秩亏的累积量矩阵正是共同隐藏原因的代数特征，可直接由数据算得。\n4. 自动选取门槛 $\\tau $，而非手工设定。留出一部分重采样数据集（来自后两步），在单个数字 $\\tau $ 上搜索，找到最能把真实数据的最小奇异值与替代（无信号）数据区分开的值——例如最大化区分两组的 ROC 曲线下面积。拟合一个在所有边间共享的全局 $\\tau $，然后处处复用。让数据来挑 $\\tau $，可避免人为设定一个可能制造结果的任意门槛。\n   - _为什么_: 让数据来定阈值，避免人为设定一个可能造假结果的任意门槛。\n\n### 有限样本校准\n*把原始不变量转化为校准过的逐边可靠性分数与达显著所需事件数，并在不同分箱下保持稳定。*\n\n5. 用平稳分块自助法 (stationary block bootstrap) 生成 200 份数据副本：把时间序列切成长度为 $L = 5/(1- rho)$ 个 bin 的连续块再随机重组，这样每个来源的速率和短程触发都保持不变。整块多元数据一起重采样，以保留块内的跨来源结构。对每份副本，只重跑基于 FFT 的快速统计量（步骤 第2步（对每条候选边）–第3步（从矩阵 $M_{ij}\\dots $））重新算出打分 Sij，绝不重跑基础模型。由此每条边得到 200 个打分值，反映在有限数据量下打分的波动幅度。\n   - _为什么_: 重采样展示在你有限的事件量下打分会抖动多少——这是可靠性数值的基础。\n6. 通过对每个来源的事件间隔序列做时间反演，构造 200 份『无信号』替代数据集——这保留事件发生的频率，但抹去其有向触发。在每份上重算打分 Sij，得到当不存在真实因果方向时打分长什么样的基线分布；无需真值图，因为基线来自你自己的数据。【作者需决定：是对每个来源独立反演（强基线，同时抹去跨来源的协同变动），还是把整条多来源时间线一起反演（更紧的基线，保留同时共现、仅去除时间方向）——请选定证书应以哪种基线为检验对象。】\n   - _为什么_: 时间反转破坏了真正的因果方向，因此这些用你自己的数据构造出一个无信号基线，无需真值图。\n7. 取替代打分的第 95 百分位作为门槛 $q_{ij}$，再把证书 Cij 设为打分超过 $q_{ij}$ 的自助副本所占比例——一个介于 0 与 1 之间、相当于校准过的可靠性概率的数。为确保这不是某一种 bin 大小的偶然，把整个计算在一个 $3\\times 3$ 网格上重复：bin 宽 Delta（半、基准、双倍）与块长系数 c（3、5、8）交叉，仅当 Cij 在多数（9 个里至少 5 个）网格设定上都不低于 0.9 时才认证该边。为每条边保存一个标记，记录它是否跨网格通过。\n\n*证书 Cij 是分块自助重采样中打分 Sij 超过时间反演替代零分布 $(1-\\alpha )$ 分位数 $q_{ij}$ 的比例。*\n$$ q_{ij} = Q_{1-\\alpha}\\big(\\{S^{(0,b)}_{ij}\\}_{b=1}^{B}\\big), \\qquad C_{ij} = \\frac{1}{B}\\sum_{b=1}^{B} \\mathbf{1}\\big[\\,S^{(b)}_{ij} > q_{ij}\\,\\big] \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 把重采样与无信号基线比较，使打分变成校准过的概率；网格检查则排除它只是某一种分箱方式的产物。\n8. 对每条边计算 N*ij：使该边能可靠地与噪声区分所需的事件数。通过在越来越长的事件流前缀上重跑，描出打分的下侧 95% 界随事件增多如何增长，假设它按事件数的平方根成比例增长，外推求出使该下界越过门槛 $q_{ij}$ 的最小事件数。已认证的边返回的数不超过当前计数；未认证的边则给出一个具体的『还需再收集多少事件』目标。\n\n*达显著所需事件数 N*ij 是使 Sij 的下侧 95% 自助置信界（按 $\\surd T$ 集中率外推）首次超过零分位数 $q_{ij}$ 的最小事件计数 T。*\n$$ N^{*}_{ij} = \\min\\Big\\{ T : \\widehat{S}^{\\,\\text{low-95\\%}}_{ij}(T) > q_{ij} \\Big\\}, \\quad \\widehat{S}_{ij}(T) \\propto \\sqrt{T} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这给从业者一个可操作的数字——对尚不可认证的边，还需再收集多少事件。\n\n### 因果认证与输出\n*通过扰动对已认证的边做因果验证，并输出带标注、经阈值筛选的图。*\n\n9. 对高证书的边做因果合理性检验。对一个留出子集，删除（或在时间上打乱）那些据称承载该边隐驱动证据的窗口内的事件，重算证书，确认下游的结构误差（保留图与合成数据真值的差距，称为 Structural Hamming Distance(结构汉明距离, SHD)）回到无混淆基线。若一条边在去掉其证据后证书崩塌则认证之，若打分顽固存在则标记之。【作者需决定：如何确定哪些事件是『证据』——是通过 $M_{ij}$ 的奇异向量把秩亏归因到特定滞后/来源，还是用滑动窗口搜索找出删除后最能降低打分的窗口——这决定了因果检验到底删除哪些事件。】\n   - _为什么_: 真正的边在去掉支撑它的证据后应当失去证书——这是因果合理性检验。\n10. 产出最终结果：原图，每条边都标注其可靠性证书 Cij、达显著所需事件数 N*ij，以及它是否跨分箱网格通过；外加一个干净子图，仅保留在多数网格设定上 Cij 不低于 0.9 且通过因果检验的边。把它存成一张简单的边表（源、目标、证书、所需事件数、是否跨网格通过、是否因果认证），便于用户逐边排序与审计。\n   - _为什么_: 这正是从业者真正想要的可审计、可信赖的图，而不是一份无标注的猜测。\n\n"},{"id":"15","run_dir":"run_prompt15_relugeom","index":15,"title":"The Measure-Weighted ReLU Transition Graph: A Data-Aware Separation Beyond Data-Blind Region Geometry","title_zh":"测度加权 ReLU 转移图：超越数据无关区域几何的数据感知可分性","method_name":"Measure-Weighted ReLU Transition Graph (G_mu)","hook":"Every current descriptor of a ReLU network's discrete geometry — region entropy, spectral gap, expansion — is computed on the unweighted activation-region complex at random initialization, so it is constant in the input distribution and provably cannot distinguish two networks that realize identical region partitions over completely different data supports. We construct the measure-weighted ReLU Transition Graph and prove it separates exactly the pairs the unweighted graph conflates, with a measure-weighted spectral gap that controls realized generalization where the unweighted gap is vacuous.","anchor_pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","anchor_pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","domain_category":"Learning Theory & Statistics","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes the discrete region geometry as a function of the empirical input distribution: every structural quantity (region entropy, spectral gap, expansion, Betti numbers, variety dimension) is computed over the architecture's full activation-region complex without weighting regions by the data mass they carry, so there is no descriptor that distinguishes the portion of the discrete geometry the network actually uses on its data from the vast combinatorial scaffold it neve","pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by naming the single structural object the RTG procedure discards for tractability — the input measure mu on the region complex — formalizing the WL-style indistinguishability class the unweighted RTG induces, and re-injecting mu into the core spectral step as a measure-weighted Laplacian whose spectral gap provably exceeds the unweighted criterion.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether the discrete geometry of ReLU networks must be characterized as a property of the architecture/weights at all, rather than jointly with the data measure and the optimization process that produced the weights — the question of whether the load-bearing structure is the intrinsic complex or the data-and-dynamics-induced sub-object is never posed.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C19 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by locating the data-independence convenience assumption inside the RTG spectral-gap generalization certificate, replacing it with the strictly weaker measure-weighted condition the construction provably satisfies, and re-deriving the certificate so it holds and is non-vacuous in the trained-on-data regime the unweighted bound excluded.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"learning theory — discrete/combinatorial geometry of ReLU networks (linear-region structure, activation patterns, polyhedral complex)","n_papers":39,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":27},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":17,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Combinatorial Regularity for Relatively Perfect Discrete Morse Gradient Vector Fields of ReLU Neural Networks"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Strengthened stability analysis of discrete-time Lurie systems involving ReLU neural networks"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Topological obstruction to the training of shallow ReLU neural networks"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Stability and Performance Analysis of Discrete-Time ReLU Recurrent Neural Networks"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"The Real Tropical Geometry of Neural Networks"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Deep learning as Ricci flow"}],"more":11},{"year":2025,"n":23,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Toric geometry of ReLU neural networks"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"On the Depth of Monotone ReLU Neural Networks and ICNNs"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Formal Synthesis of Lyapunov Stability Certificates for Linear Switched Systems using ReLU Neural Networks"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Discrete Functional Geometry of ReLU Networks via ReLU Transition Graphs"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"From 2D to 3D: How Discrete Dependencies Enable Cross-Dimensional Inference in Neural Networks in Defiance of Euclidean Geometry"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"The Geometry of ReLU Networks through the ReLU Transition Graph"}],"more":17}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":10,"share":0.256},{"pattern_id":"algebraic_equivalence_unification","pattern_name":"Prove Equivalence to Unify","count":4,"share":0.103},{"pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","count":3,"share":0.077},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":2,"share":0.051},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":2,"share":0.051},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":1,"share":0.026},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":1,"share":0.026}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"The discrete geometry of a ReLU network — the partition of input space into activation regions and the combinatorial adjacency between them — is currently characterized as an intrinsic property of the weights and architecture, divorced from the data the network was trained on. The ReLU Transition Graph line (semanticscholar:563970a1d2d828bfe16fccfa4570eedc31ac5547, semanticscholar:8d03773527edf96a274c77db14d09a8d6b8c8b5b) builds a graph whose nodes are linear regions and whose edges are single-neuron activation flips, and proves expansion / spectral-gap / region-entropy results, but every such result is derived at i.i.d. random initialization and validated only on small MLPs; the graph is never weighted by, or conditioned on, where the training data actually lives in input space. The algebraic-geometry frontier (openalex:W6979261748, semanticscholar:3bad7ebca768c4f8532c980c681aa290dece7c5c) likewise derives the polynomial/divisor constraints a fixed architecture imposes on its outputs region-by-region, but treats the region decomposition as a fixed combinatorial scaffold rather than as something that is reshaped by optimization. As a result, when a practitioner asks which features of the discrete region geometry govern a trained network's behavior on its actual data — which regions carry mass, how the region partition migrates from initialization to convergence, which combinatorial transitions are traversed by training trajectories — the current machinery produces only data-blind, initialization-time quantities that cannot answer it, because none of the existing descriptors is a function of the empirical input measure or of the training dynamics that move the hyperplanes.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:8d03773527edf96a274c77db14d09a8d6b8c8b5b","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Extends the ReLU Transition Graph into a graph-theoretic model where nodes are linear regions, edges are single-neuron activation flips, and proves expansion, spectral-gap-controls-generalization, and region-entropy-bounds-expressivity results, validated empirically on small MLPs. Its residue: every structural quantity (expansion, spectral gap, region entropy) is defined over the unweighted RTG at random initialization, so it characterizes the architecture's potential geometry rather than the geometry a trained network actually realizes on its data, and it offers no account of how the graph deforms along a training trajectory — region probability mass P(R_i) appears only inside the entropy definition, never as a weighting that conditions the spectral object on the empirical input distribution.","source_used_note":"fulltext (html_arxiv) read for residue"},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:563970a1d2d828bfe16fccfa4570eedc31ac5547","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Introduces the ReLU Transition Graph and derives combinatorial bounds on its size and diameter, a connectivity proof, and a graph-theoretic reading of VC-dimension, validated on small controlled nets. Residue: it establishes the static combinatorial existence of the graph but supplies no data-dependent or training-dynamics layer — the graph is the same object whether or not any data has been seen, so it cannot distinguish a randomly-initialized network from a trained one with identical architecture."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W6979261748","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Associates algebraic varieties to each activation region and derives polynomial / rank-constraint equations characterizing the functions a fixed ReLU architecture can represent, analyzing when these varieties attain expected dimension. Residue: the region decomposition is taken as a fixed combinatorial scaffold and the constraints are parameter-space facts about the architecture; the framework says nothing about which regions are visited by training data or how the variety structure changes as weights move during optimization."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:bd8a8ed7bf23bce77de7d1c6f4115c349bbb5962","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Builds discrete-Morse-theory tooling on the canonical polyhedral complex of a ReLU network, giving a constructive translation between PL-Morse functions and relatively-perfect discrete Morse functions to enable topological analysis. Residue: it provides local critical-cell / gradient-field machinery on the complex but never aggregates it into a global, data-weighted topological invariant tied to training behavior or generalization — the topology described is that of the architecture's complex, not of the trained function over its data measure."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"learning theory — discrete/combinatorial geometry of ReLU networks (linear-region structure, activation patterns, polyhedral complex)","venue":"ICLR 2026","time":"2026","data":["small-to-moderate fully-connected ReLU MLPs","standard classification datasets (e.g. MNIST/CIFAR) for empirical validation of region-geometry quantities","synthetic teacher functions / controlled architectures"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (approx 90 A100-day)","expertise":"learning theory; combinatorial / discrete geometry; spectral graph theory","preference":"both","baseline":"ReLU Transition Graph (RTG) framework and its extensions; linear-region counting bounds; tropical/toric/algebraic-variety characterizations of the canonical polyhedral complex","limitation":"existing discrete-geometry characterizations describe the activation-region structure as a static combinatorial object computed at random initialization and validated only on tiny networks; they do not connect that structure to the data distribution the network is trained on or to how the structure deforms during training","contribution_type":"theory","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared audit lens is the never-named data-independence assumption: both the ReLU Transition Graph (RTG) spectral results (semanticscholar:8d03773527edf96a274c77db14d09a8d6b8c8b5b) and the algebraic-variety constraints (openalex:W6979261748) treat the activation-region complex as a fixed combinatorial scaffold and compute every quantity without reference to where data lives. The central object is the measure-weighted ReLU Transition Graph G_mu = (V, E, w), defined as follows. V is the set of realized activation regions of a trained ReLU network f (computed exactly for small nets by enumerating sign patterns of all hidden pre-activations on a fine grid, or estimated by activation-pattern hashing of a finite sample for larger nets); only regions with nonzero empirical mass are nodes — this is the data-induced sub-complex, a strict subset of the full RTG. Each node R_i carries weight pi(R_i) = mu_hat(R_i), the empirical probability mass of region R_i under the training input distribution mu (computed: fraction of a held-out sample of N points whose activation pattern equals R_i; mu is the external data oracle, the only non-model-internal input). Each edge (R_i,R_j) in E (regions differing by one neuron flip, the same adjacency the unweighted RTG uses) carries weight w_ij = (pi(R_i)+pi(R_j))/2 * b_ij, where b_ij in [0,1] is the boundary-flux coefficient: the fraction of a fixed budget of K straight-line segments between sampled points of R_i and R_j whose crossing of the shared hyperplane lies inside both regions' realized supports (K=64 is a named hyperparameter; b_ij makes the weight bridge probability-mass and geometric-adjacency units). LEG 1 (anchor, C10): the discarded object is mu; we formalize the indistinguishability class by proving the unweighted normalized Laplacian L of the full RTG is, by construction, a function only of the sign-pattern adjacency and hence identical for any two networks f,g whose realized region adjacency graphs are isomorphic even when their data supports mu_f, mu_g are disjoint — so the unweighted spectral gap lambda_2(L) cannot separate them. We then prove that the measure-weighted Laplacian L_mu (built from w_ij and the degree d_i = sum_j w_ij) has a spectral gap lambda_2(L_mu) that does separate such pairs whenever their mass profiles pi differ, exhibiting an explicit conflated pair and showing lambda_2(L_mu) strictly distinguishes it; cost is O(|E|) over the realized sub-complex, which is bounded by the sample size N rather than the astronomical full region count, preserving tractability. LEG 2 (sibling, C19): the RTG generalization certificate E[GenError] <= C * L_f^2 / lambda_2(L) imports data-independence purely for convenience (it bounds functional variation by an unweighted Dirichlet energy). We trace what that assumption buys — a Poincare/Cheeger control of variance of the centroid-output field phi — and replace it with the strictly weaker measure-weighted Poincare inequality E_mu(phi) >= lambda_2(L_mu) * Var_mu(phi), which the construction provably satisfies because Var_mu weights by exactly the mass the network sees. Re-deriving gives E[GenError] <= C' * L_f^2 / lambda_2(L_mu), valid and non-vacuous in the trained-on-data regime (where the unweighted bound is loose because most of the unweighted graph carries zero data mass and depresses lambda_2(L)). The two legs share G_mu: Leg 1 constructs it and proves the separation; Leg 2 routes the generalization certificate through its spectral gap, so a single object both surpasses the data-blind limit and re-founds the certificate.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The two gaps share one piece of machinery (G_mu) rather than needing separate modules: the evidence is that the anchor's separation object (the measure-weighted spectral gap) is the very quantity the sibling's re-derived certificate is stated in terms of — Leg 2 cannot be written without Leg 1's object, which is the shared_audit thread made concrete. I considered making Leg 2 a separate training-dynamics module (tracking deformation of G_mu across the trajectory), but that is the deferred trajectory gap and would staple a second paper on; restricting Leg 2 to re-deriving the static certificate keeps it one coordinated contribution. AVOIDED REGRESSION (method_lineage): the load-bearing artifact is a measure-weighted STRUCTURAL spectral descriptor with a separation proof, deliberately not collateral node c1 (per-datapoint slice region-counting near data) — we never reduce the contribution to local sampling of region density; mu enters as a global weight on a spectral object, a source (the empirical measure on the spectral Laplacian) the lineage tree does not yet occupy.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: train a sweep of ~40 small ReLU MLPs (widths 8-64, depths 2-4) on a controlled 2D/MNIST-subset task spanning under- to over-parameterized regimes, build both the unweighted RTG and the measure-weighted G_mu for each, and measure the Spearman rank correlation between each network's spectral-gap-based generalization proxy and its realized test-minus-train error. If the candidate is correct, the measure-weighted proxy C'*L_f^2/lambda_2(L_mu) shows a markedly stronger (more negative-as-error-rises) rank correlation with realized generalization gap than the unweighted proxy, and on the explicit isomorphic-adjacency/disjoint-support pair the unweighted gap is identical while lambda_2(L_mu) differs. The load-bearing variable is lambda_2(L_mu), the measure-weighted spectral gap; the negative control replaces the empirical region masses pi with the uniform measure over realized nodes (oracle-ablating the data-weighting while keeping the identical graph topology), which should drive the proxy's rank correlation with the downstream test-error gap back down to the unweighted RTG baseline — confirming the predictive content comes from mu-weighting and not from restricting to the realized sub-graph. A positive control using lambda_2(L_mu) alone (dropping L_f and C') as a one-feature predictor of the generalization gap should recover most of the rank-correlation signal, identifying the measure-weighted gap as the carrier.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:8d03773527edf96a274c77db14d09a8d6b8c8b5b","delta":"They define region entropy with P(R_i) and prove spectral-gap/expansion results on the unweighted RTG at random initialization; we make the empirical measure mu a weight on the Laplacian itself (not merely inside an entropy scalar), construct the realized data-induced sub-complex, and prove a separation between networks the unweighted graph conflates that their construction provably cannot make."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:563970a1d2d828bfe16fccfa4570eedc31ac5547","delta":"They derive combinatorial size/diameter/connectivity bounds and a VC-dimension reading on the static unweighted RTG; we re-derive the spectral generalization certificate under a relaxed measure-weighted Poincare condition, yielding a bound stated in lambda_2(L_mu) that is non-vacuous on trained data where their data-independent bound is loose."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W6979261748","delta":"They associate algebraic varieties to activation regions in parameter space (architecture-level constraints independent of data); we attach the empirical input measure to the same region complex and turn the descriptor into a functional of mu with a proven indistinguishability-class collapse, which their data-free variety dimension cannot express."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:bd8a8ed7bf23bce77de7d1c6f4115c349bbb5962","delta":"They build local discrete-Morse gradient fields on the canonical complex without a data weighting or a global generalization-linked invariant; we supply a global measure-weighted spectral invariant (lambda_2(L_mu)) tied to a re-derived generalization certificate."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:8d03773527edf96a274c77db14d09a8d6b8c8b5b","what_step_was_missed":"They keep the region probability mass P(R_i) only as the argument of a region-entropy scalar and leave the Laplacian and spectral gap defined on the unweighted graph; to already contain our contribution they would have had to re-inject that measure as the edge/node weighting of the spectral operator itself and prove that the resulting measure-weighted spectral gap separates an explicitly constructed pair of networks the unweighted gap conflates — a measure-weighted separation construction (and the matching re-derivation of the generalization certificate through lambda_2(L_mu)) they never built."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":288,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"Layer 1 did not fire: gap_closure_reject_check is borderline-not-triggered (no Reject lesson marked candidate_match: yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat is a strict-extension (not exact-mechanism) relation with addressable_via null. recipe_application_check.verdict = applied on both legs (C10 separation-via-re-injection in Leg 1, C19 statistical-certificate relaxation in Leg 2), so the bypassed→revise trigger does not fire. The single borderline (C19 routine-lift risk on the lesson 'a relaxation the field reads as a mechanical lift ... will be judged incremental unless a genuinely novel obstacle is named') hits a load-bearing field but is mitigated in core_mechanism Leg 2 by explicitly naming the obstacle, so it is surfaced for Phase 4 reviewer_concerns rather than forcing revise.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes the discrete region geometry as a function of the empirical input distribution: every structural quantity (region entropy, spectral gap, expansion, Betti numbers, variety dimension) is computed over the architecture's full activation-region complex without weighting regions by the data mass they carry, so there is no descriptor that distinguishes the portion of the discrete geometry the network actually uses on its data from the vast combinatorial scaffold it never visits.","main_pattern":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail when the 'limit' they characterize is not a genuine structural blindspot: trivially implied by the model's own assumptions, already surpassed by a published method, or never formalized beyond an informal analogy; a recurring shape substitutes a hand-wavy mechanism for a separation proof.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Resting the central claim on an informal analogy (two operators 'both smooth high frequencies') instead of a separation proof leaves the mechanism underspecified and the empirical gain unconvincing.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism Leg 1 supplies an explicit separation proof — an exhibited conflated pair (isomorphic realized adjacency, disjoint mu-supports) the unweighted gap cannot distinguish and lambda_2(L_mu) does — not an analogy."},{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a 'maximally expressive' construction that a recently published method already strictly subsumes turns the surpass-the-limit claim into redundant work.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The collision pool (288 hits) and lit_table contain only the unweighted RTG line and unrelated spectral-graph math; no published method attaches the empirical input measure to the Laplacian, so the surpass is not subsumed."},{"lesson_quoted":"A novel formalism that cannot generate predictions or demonstrate concrete advantages over existing definitions reads as abstraction for its own sake.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The construction generates a falsifiable prediction (lambda_2(L_mu) rank-correlates with realized generalization where the unweighted proxy does not) with a named negative control."},{"lesson_quoted":"Deriving a 'limitation' that is trivially implied by the model's own linearity assumption produces a limit too weak to count as a real blindspot, and the proposed surpass step stays under-validated.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The blindspot (data-independence of the unweighted Laplacian) is a provable property the unweighted RTG cannot recover, not a triviality — two nets with disjoint data supports genuinely receive identical unweighted descriptors."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether the discrete geometry of ReLU networks must be characterized as a property of the architecture/weights at all, rather than jointly with the data measure and the optimization process that produced the weights — the question of whether the load-bearing structure is the intrinsic complex or the data-and-dynamics-induced sub-object is never posed.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C19 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The dominant failure is a relaxation whose payoff evaporates exactly where it is claimed — the re-derived certificate diverges or turns vacuous precisely in the regime that motivated dropping the assumption — or a routine-lift trap extending a known inequality without naming a novel obstacle, or hinging on a quantity that cannot be estimated in the target setting.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A certificate that goes vacuous or diverges exactly in the regime it was built for is self-defeating; verify non-vacuity where the result must hold, not merely where it is convenient to prove.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The re-derived bound is stated in lambda_2(L_mu) over the realized data-induced sub-complex, which is non-vacuous on trained data precisely because it discards the zero-mass nodes that make the unweighted bound loose — the bound is sharpest in the motivating regime."},{"lesson_quoted":"A relaxation the field reads as a mechanical lift of a known argument will be judged incremental unless a genuinely novel obstacle is named and overcome, even when no reviewer is negative.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"Re-deriving a Poincare/Cheeger generalization bound under a measure-weighted Dirichlet energy could read as a routine reweighting unless the paper names the novel obstacle (that the realized sub-complex, not the full graph, is the correct spectral domain and that mu-weighting is what restores non-vacuity); this is surfaced for Phase 4 reviewer_concerns rather than triggering, because the obstacle IS named in core_mechanism Leg 2."},{"lesson_quoted":"If the guarantee depends on a quantity that cannot be estimated in the target setting, the theoretical improvement does not transfer to the practical claim the paper makes.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"lambda_2(L_mu) is computed directly from a finite training sample via activation-pattern hashing and boundary-flux estimation (steps 2-6), so it is estimable in exactly the target setting."},{"lesson_quoted":"Tightening claims are unassessable without head-to-head comparison against the prior certificates being relaxed plus sensitivity analysis on the new parameters; absent these, relative improvement cannot be judged.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"falsification_prediction runs the unweighted vs measure-weighted proxy head-to-head on the same trained-net sweep and the negative control is a sensitivity analysis on the mu-weighting parameter."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The assumption_audit/C19 leg carries one borderline (routine-lift risk) on the lesson 'a relaxation the field reads as a mechanical lift ... will be judged incremental unless a genuinely novel obstacle is named'; it does not trigger because core_mechanism Leg 2 explicitly names the obstacle (realized-sub-complex-as-correct-spectral-domain) and re-derives non-vacuity. The C10 anchor leg is fully clear with an exhibited separation pair."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes the discrete region geometry as a function of the empirical input distribution: every structural quantity (region entropy, spectral gap, expansion, Betti numbers, variety dimension) is computed over the architecture's full activation-region complex without weighting regions by the data mass they carry, so there is no descriptor that distinguishes the portion of the discrete geometry the network actually uses on its data from the vast combinatorial scaffold it never visits.","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Take an iterative/locally-scoped procedure over a relational/combinatorial structure, pinpoint the one structural object it discards for tractability, formalize the equivalence class as a WL-style separation criterion on the native objects, then re-inject that exact object into the procedure's core step and prove the augmented operator strictly exceeds the criterion at bounded (linear/quadratic) cost.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"Leg 1 names the discarded object (the input measure mu on the region complex), formalizes the indistinguishability class (the unweighted normalized Laplacian is a function only of sign-pattern adjacency, hence identical for isomorphic-adjacency/disjoint-support nets), re-injects mu into the core spectral step as the measure-weighted Laplacian L_mu, proves lambda_2(L_mu) strictly separates the exhibited conflated pair, and bounds cost at O(|E|) over the realized sub-complex — the C10 signature move is present end-to-end.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether the discrete geometry of ReLU networks must be characterized as a property of the architecture/weights at all, rather than jointly with the data measure and the optimization process that produced the weights — the question of whether the load-bearing structure is the intrinsic complex or the data-and-dynamics-induced sub-object is never posed.","sub_pattern":"C19 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Pivot the regularity/independence/boundedness condition a STATISTICAL certificate imports for convenience, determine the minimal property it was actually buying, substitute a strictly weaker sufficient property the construction provably satisfies, and re-derive the certificate so it is valid in a regime the old assumption excluded or strictly tighter in its leading term.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"Leg 2 locates the data-independence convenience assumption inside the RTG generalization certificate E[GenError] <= C*L_f^2/lambda_2(L), traces what it buys (a Poincare control of Var of the output field), substitutes the strictly weaker measure-weighted Poincare inequality the construction provably satisfies, and re-derives E[GenError] <= C'*L_f^2/lambda_2(L_mu) valid/non-vacuous in the trained-on-data regime the unweighted bound excluded — the C19 relax-and-re-prove-a-statistical-bound move is performed.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both legs perform their cited cluster's signature operation against the same shared object G_mu: C10's discarded-object-re-injection-plus-separation in Leg 1, and C19's convenience-assumption-relaxation-plus-recertification in Leg 2."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["characterize_limit_then_surpass","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"None of the three reject-favored compositions matches; all three require heterogeneous_decomposition as a component and neither candidate pattern is heterogeneous_decomposition."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:8d03773527edf96a274c77db14d09a8d6b8c8b5b","threat_source":"lit_table","subsumption_argument":"The Discrete Functional Geometry RTG paper is the most-competing prior: it already defines region probability mass P(R_i) and proves spectral-gap-controls-generalization. The candidate's claim stands or falls on whether attaching mu to the Laplacian itself (not merely to an entropy scalar) yields something the RTG framework provably lacks — and it does: the RTG's spectral gap is defined on the unweighted graph and is therefore constant in mu by construction, so it cannot make the candidate's separation (two nets with disjoint data supports receive identical RTG descriptors). The candidate is not subsumed because its measure-weighted Laplacian and the exhibited indistinguishability-class collapse are absent from the RTG construction; it is a strict extension, not an overlap.","addressable_via":null}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# The Measure-Weighted ReLU Transition Graph: A Data-Aware Separation Beyond Data-Blind Region Geometry\n\n**Method.** Measure-Weighted ReLU Transition Graph (G_mu)\n\n## Motivation\nA ReLU network slices its input space into many flat pieces called activation regions, and the way these pieces fit together — how many there are and which ones touch — is the 'discrete geometry' researchers study to understand what a network can learn and how well it generalizes. The current state of the art, the ReLU Transition Graph (RTG, a graph whose dots are regions and whose links connect regions that differ by flipping one neuron), proves nice results about this geometry, but it computes everything on the bare graph at random startup, before the network has seen any data. The catch: because the graph only encodes which regions touch, two networks that happen to touch their regions in the same pattern get scored as identical even if one was trained on photos of cats and the other on handwritten digits — the descriptor literally cannot see where the data lives. This matters now because the RTG framework is brand new (2025), so for the first time there is a concrete spectral object to fix. The fix is to weight each region by how much real training data falls in it, attach that weighting directly to the graph's Laplacian (the matrix whose spectrum summarizes the graph), and only ever build the regions the network actually visits — which keeps it computable. Prior work stopped short for one reason: it treated the geometry as a fixed fact about the architecture and never asked whether the part that matters is instead the data-shaped sub-object. When this gap closes, we get a single data-aware number, the measure-weighted spectral gap $\\lambda _{2}(L_\\mu ),$ that can tell apart networks the old descriptor confused and that plugs into a generalization guarantee which stays meaningful on real trained networks instead of going vacuous.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n\n1. Train a small ReLU multilayer perceptron (MLP) on your dataset, using an ordinary random split. Set aside a second batch of N fresh input points — drawn from the same input distribution mu but never used during training — purely to measure where the data falls. Pick N large enough that the most-populated region still catches a few dozen points (a safe default is at least 10000 points, or 50 times the number of regions you expect to see). These held-out points are only ever used to count data per region, never to update the network.\n   - _Why_: You need a clean sample of the real data distribution to weight the geometry by it.\n\n### Build the measure-weighted graph G_mu\n*Turn a trained net + a data sample into the data-induced sub-complex with mass- and flux-weighted edges and its Laplacian.*\n\n2. List the regions the network actually uses. For very small networks, push a dense grid of inputs through the net; for larger ones, push the N held-out points through. For each input, read the activation pattern — the on/off sign of every hidden unit — and pack it into a bit array; that bit array names one region. Group inputs by identical bit array (a fast 64-bit hash makes the grouping cheap). Each distinct bit array is one realized region, and you keep the list of which sample points landed in it. Keep the full bit array, not just the hash, because the next step needs to know which regions differ by exactly one bit.\n   - _Why_: This finds exactly the regions the trained network actually uses, instead of the astronomically many it could in principle make.\n3. Give each region a mass equal to the fraction of the N held-out points that fell inside it (this is the node-mass part of Eq. (1)). Then throw away every region that caught zero points. What remains is the data-shaped sub-collection of regions — exactly the regions the trained network actually visits on its data, and nothing it never touches.\n   - _Why_: Empty regions are the scaffold the network never visits; keeping only data-carrying regions is what makes the descriptor depend on the data.\n4. Connect two regions with an edge whenever their bit arrays differ in exactly one position (one neuron flip). For each edge, estimate how 'real' that shared boundary is: draw K=64 line segments between random held-out points of the two regions, and for each segment find where the one differing neuron switches sign; count a segment as a hit if that switch point genuinely lies on the shared wall of both regions (not at a corner where several neurons flip at once). The boundary-flux $b_{ij}$ is the hit fraction. The edge's weight is the average of the two regions' masses times this boundary-flux (Eq. (1)), so it blends 'how much data is here' with 'how genuinely adjacent these regions are'.\n\n*The edge weight bridges data mass and geometric adjacency: the average empirical region mass $\\pi $ of the two endpoints, scaled by the boundary-flux coefficient $b_{ij} \\in $ [0,1]; node mass $\\pi (R_{i})$ is the fraction of N held-out points whose activation pattern equals $R_{i}.$*\n$$ w_{ij} = \\frac{\\pi(R_i)+\\pi(R_j)}{2}\\, b_{ij}, \\qquad \\pi(R_i) = \\hat{\\mu}(R_i) = \\frac{|S \\cap R_i|}{N} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The weight blends 'how much data is here' with 'how genuinely adjacent these two regions are', so the graph reflects the data-shaped geometry.\n5. Form the measure-weighted normalized Laplacian $L_\\mu $ from the weighted graph (Eq. (2)), and separately the plain unweighted Laplacian L using the same connections but with every edge weight set to 1. For each, compute the second-smallest eigenvalue — the spectral gap — using a standard sparse eigenvalue solver. $\\lambda _{2}(L_\\mu )$ is the new data-aware summary number; $\\lambda _{2}(L)$ is the old data-blind one kept for comparison.\n\n*The measure-weighted normalized Laplacian assembled from the weight matrix W and weighted-degree diagonal D; its second-smallest eigenvalue $\\lambda _{2}(L_\\mu )$ is the data-aware spectral gap, contrasted with the unweighted L that sets all weights to 1.*\n$$ L_\\mu = I - D^{-1/2} W D^{-1/2}, \\qquad D = \\mathrm{diag}\\Big(\\textstyle\\sum_j w_{ij}\\Big) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: $\\lambda _{2}(L_\\mu )$ is the new data-aware summary number; keeping $\\lambda _{2}(L)$ lets you show directly what the old data-blind number misses.\n\n### Prove the separation (Leg 1)\n*Show the unweighted gap is blind to the data measure while the measure-weighted gap separates an exhibited conflated pair.*\n\n6. Show two things. (1) Prove the plain Laplacian L depends only on which regions touch, so two networks whose touching-pattern is the same get identical spectral gaps $\\lambda _{2}(L)$ even if their data live on completely separate supports. (2) Prove the measure-weighted gap $\\lambda _{2}(L_\\mu )$ is different between those same two networks whenever their per-region masses differ (Eq. (3)). Then build one concrete such pair and check on the computer that $\\lambda _{2}(L)$ is identical across the pair while $\\lambda _{2}(L_\\mu )$ is not. The clean way to guarantee the two nets share the same touching-pattern is to take one trained net and apply a shape-preserving transform of the input space (combined with the network's own symmetries) so the region layout is copied exactly, then put the two data distributions on the original versus the transformed support. 【author decision: guarantee the matching touching-pattern by this shape-preserving-transform construction, or instead show two separately trained nets whose touching-patterns you verify match by hand — a tradeoff between airtight proof and a stronger-looking demonstration.】\n\n*The separation statement: isomorphic realized adjacency forces equal unweighted gaps, but disjoint data supports drive the measure-weighted gaps apart — the conflated pair the unweighted descriptor cannot tell apart.*\n$$ L_f \\cong L_g \\ \\Rightarrow\\ \\lambda_2(L_f)=\\lambda_2(L_g), \\quad\\text{yet}\\quad \\mu_f \\perp \\mu_g \\ \\Rightarrow\\ \\lambda_2(L_{\\mu_f}) \\neq \\lambda_2(L_{\\mu_g}) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A concrete pair the old descriptor confuses but the new one separates is hard proof that the data-weighting adds real information.\n\n### Re-found the generalization certificate (Leg 2)\n*Relax the data-independence assumption and re-derive a non-vacuous bound stated in the measure-weighted gap.*\n\n7. Open the existing RTG generalization bound and find the spot where it quietly assumes the geometry is data-independent. That assumption is only there to give a variance-control (Poincare) inequality. Swap in the weaker, measure-weighted version of that inequality — the one your construction actually satisfies because both sides weight regions by the same real masses — and push it through the rest of the original derivation. The result is a new bound of the form $C'\\cdot L_{f}^{2}/\\lambda _{2}(L_\\mu )$ (Eq. (4)). Finally check it stays meaningful (non-vacuous) on the data-shaped regions, exactly where the old bound goes loose because most of its weight sits on regions with no data.\n\n*The re-derived generalization certificate stated in the measure-weighted gap, justified by the measure-weighted Poincare inequality (Dirichlet energy $E_\\mu $ lower-bounds the $\\mu -variance$ of the output field $\\phi )$; it stays non-vacuous on trained data where the unweighted bound is loose.*\n$$ \\mathbb{E}[\\mathrm{GenError}] \\le \\frac{C'\\, L_f^2}{\\lambda_2(L_\\mu)}, \\qquad \\mathcal{E}_\\mu(\\phi) \\ge \\lambda_2(L_\\mu)\\,\\mathrm{Var}_\\mu(\\phi) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This shows the guarantee was never really about the bare architecture — the data-shaped sub-object is the right domain, and the bound stops going vacuous once you use it.\n\n### Validate and control\n*Test the measure-weighted proxy against realized error across a net sweep with a uniform-measure ablation as negative control.*\n\n8. Take your collection of trained networks. For each one compute the old prediction $C\\cdot L_{f}^{2}/\\lambda _{2}(L)$ and the new prediction $C'\\cdot L_{f}^{2}/\\lambda _{2}(L_\\mu ),$ and also measure its real generalization gap (test error minus train error). Compute the network's Lipschitz constant $L_{f}$ the same way for every net (the product of per-layer spectral norms is a clean upper bound). Then report, for each prediction, how well it rank-orders the networks by their true generalization gap (Spearman correlation). Comparing the two side by side is the test.\n   - _Why_: Comparing the two proxies head-to-head against real error is the only way to tell whether the data-weighting genuinely predicts generalization better.\n9. Now run the control. Rebuild the measure-weighted graph but flatten the data-weighting: give every surviving region the same mass instead of its real data mass, keeping the exact same regions, connections, and boundary-flux factors. Recompute the spectral gap and how well it predicts the real generalization gap. If the prediction quality drops back to the plain unweighted baseline, that proves the data-weighting itself — not merely trimming down to the visited regions — is what carries the predictive power.\n   - _Why_: This isolates the cause: if the signal vanishes when you flatten the data-weighting, then the data measure — not just trimming to visited regions — is what carries the prediction.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 测度加权 ReLU 转移图：超越数据无关区域几何的数据感知可分性\n\n**方法名称.** Measure-Weighted ReLU Transition Graph (G_mu)\n\n## 研究动机\nReLU 网络会把输入空间切成许多平直的小块，称为激活区域（activation region）；这些小块如何拼接——共有多少块、哪些块相邻——就是研究者用来理解网络能学什么、泛化好不好的“离散几何”。当前最先进的工具是 ReLU 转移图（RTG，把区域当作图的节点、把仅翻转一个神经元就相邻的区域用边连起来），它证明了不少关于这种几何的好结果，但所有计算都在随机初始化、网络还没见过任何数据的“裸图”上做。问题在于：图只编码了哪些区域相邻，于是两个恰好以相同模式相邻的网络会被判为完全相同，哪怕一个是在猫的照片上训练、另一个是在手写数字上训练——这个描述子根本看不见数据落在哪里。现在正是时机，因为 RTG 框架是 2025 年才成型的，第一次有了一个具体的谱对象可供修正。修正办法是：按每个区域里真实落入多少训练数据来加权，把这个权重直接挂到图的 Laplacian（其谱概括了图结构的矩阵）上，并且只构建网络真正访问过的区域——这样仍可计算。先前工作止步的唯一原因是：它们把几何当作架构的固定事实，从未追问真正重要的是否其实是被数据塑造出来的子对象。一旦补上这个缺口，我们就得到一个数据感知的单一量——测度加权谱隙 $\\lambda _{2}(L_\\mu )——$它能区分旧描述子混淆的网络，并接入一个在真实训练网络上仍然有意义、而非变得平凡的泛化保证。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景\n\n1. 用普通的随机划分，在你的数据集上训练一个小的 ReLU 多层感知机(Multilayer Perceptron, MLP)。再另外留出一批 N 个全新的输入点——它们来自同一输入分布 mu，但训练时从不使用——专门用来度量数据落在何处。N 要取得足够大，使最密集的区域仍能接到几十个点（安全的默认值是至少 10000 个点，或预期区域数的 50 倍）。这批留出点只用于按区域统计数据，绝不用于更新网络。\n   - _为什么_: 要按真实数据分布给几何加权，就需要一份干净的数据分布样本。\n\n### 构建测度加权图 G_mu\n*把训练好的网络与数据样本转化为带质量与通量加权边的数据诱导子复形及其 Laplacian。*\n\n2. 列出网络真正使用的区域。对很小的网络，把一个密集的输入网格送进网络；对较大的网络，则把 N 个留出点送进去。对每个输入读出激活模式——每个隐藏单元的开/关符号——并打包成一个位数组(bit array)；该位数组就标识一个区域。把位数组相同的输入归为一组（用一个快速的 64 位哈希可让分组很廉价）。每个不同的位数组即一个已实现区域，并记录哪些样本点落入其中。要保留完整的位数组而不仅是哈希值，因为下一步需要判断哪些区域恰好相差一位。\n   - _为什么_: 这样能精确找出训练后网络真正使用的区域，而不是它原则上可能产生的天文数字般多的区域。\n3. 给每个区域一个质量，等于 N 个留出点中落入它的比例（即 Eq. (1) 中的节点质量部分）。然后丢弃任何一个点都没接到的区域。剩下的就是被数据塑造的区域子集合——正是训练后网络在其数据上真正访问的区域，不含任何它从不触及的部分。\n   - _为什么_: 空区域是网络从不访问的脚手架；只保留承载数据的区域，正是让描述子依赖数据的关键。\n4. 只要两个区域的位数组恰好相差一位（一次神经元翻转），就连一条边。对每条边，估计这道共享边界有多“真实”：在两个区域的随机留出点之间画 K=64 条线段，对每条线段找出那个唯一不同的神经元在何处变号；若该变号点确实落在两区域共享的“墙”上（而非多个神经元同时翻转的“角”上），就记一次命中。边界通量 $b_{ij}$ 即命中比例。该边的权重为两区域质量的均值乘以这个边界通量（Eq. (1)），从而把“此处有多少数据”与“两区域是否真正相邻”结合起来。\n\n*边权把数据质量与几何邻接结合：两端点经验区域质量 $\\pi $ 的均值乘以边界通量系数 $b_{ij} \\in $ [0,1]；节点质量 $\\pi (R_{i})$ 为 N 个留出点中激活模式落在 $R_{i}$ 的比例。*\n$$ w_{ij} = \\frac{\\pi(R_i)+\\pi(R_j)}{2}\\, b_{ij}, \\qquad \\pi(R_i) = \\hat{\\mu}(R_i) = \\frac{|S \\cap R_i|}{N} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 该权重把“此处有多少数据”与“两区域是否真正相邻”结合起来，使图反映被数据塑造的几何。\n5. 由加权图构建测度加权归一化 Laplacian $L_\\mu $（Eq. (2)），并另外用相同连接但把每条边权重都置 1 构建无权 Laplacian L。对二者分别用标准的稀疏特征值求解器计算第二小特征值——即谱隙。$\\lambda _{2}(L_\\mu )$ 是新的数据感知概括量；$\\lambda _{2}(L)$ 是保留用于对比的旧的数据无关量。\n\n*由权重矩阵 W 和加权度对角阵 D 组装的测度加权归一化 Laplacian；其第二小特征值 $\\lambda _{2}(L_\\mu )$ 即数据感知谱隙，与所有权重置 1 的无权 L 对照。*\n$$ L_\\mu = I - D^{-1/2} W D^{-1/2}, \\qquad D = \\mathrm{diag}\\Big(\\textstyle\\sum_j w_{ij}\\Big) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: $\\lambda _{2}(L_\\mu )$ 是新的数据感知概括量；保留 $\\lambda _{2}(L)$ 能直接展示旧的数据无关量遗漏了什么。\n\n### 证明可分性（Leg 1）\n*表明无权谱隙对数据测度盲视，而测度加权谱隙能区分一个给出的混淆对。*\n\n6. 证明两件事。(1) 证明无权 Laplacian L 只取决于哪些区域相邻，因此两个相邻模式相同的网络会得到相同的谱隙 $\\lambda _{2}(L)$，即便它们的数据落在完全分离的支撑上。(2) 证明只要这两个网络的各区域质量不同，测度加权谱隙 $\\lambda _{2}(L_\\mu )$ 在它们之间就不同（Eq. (3)）。然后构造一个具体的这样的配对，并在计算机上验证：$\\lambda _{2}(L)$ 在配对间完全相同，而 $\\lambda _{2}(L_\\mu )$ 不同。要保证两个网络共享相同的相邻模式，干净的做法是取一个训练好的网络，对输入空间施加一个保形变换（并结合网络自身的对称性），使区域布局被精确复制，再把两个数据分布分别放在原始支撑与变换后支撑上。【作者需决定：是用这种保形变换构造来保证相邻模式一致，还是改为给出两个分别训练、并人工验证相邻模式一致的网络——这是在证明严密性与演示说服力之间的权衡。】\n\n*可分性陈述：同构的已实现邻接迫使无权谱隙相等，但不相交的数据支撑使测度加权谱隙分开——这正是无权描述子无法区分的混淆对。*\n$$ L_f \\cong L_g \\ \\Rightarrow\\ \\lambda_2(L_f)=\\lambda_2(L_g), \\quad\\text{yet}\\quad \\mu_f \\perp \\mu_g \\ \\Rightarrow\\ \\lambda_2(L_{\\mu_f}) \\neq \\lambda_2(L_{\\mu_g}) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 一个旧描述子混淆、新描述子能区分的具体配对，是数据加权确实带来真实信息的硬证据。\n\n### 重建泛化证书（Leg 2）\n*放松数据无关假设并重新推导出以测度加权谱隙表述的非平凡界。*\n\n7. 打开现有的 RTG 泛化界，找到它悄悄假设几何与数据无关的那一处。该假设只是为了给出一个方差控制（Poincare）不等式。换上更弱的、测度加权版本的该不等式——即你的构造确实满足的那个，因为不等式两边都按相同的真实质量给区域加权——再把它代入原推导的其余部分。结果是一个形如 $C'\\cdot L_{f}^{2}/\\lambda _{2}(L_\\mu )$ 的新界（Eq. (4)）。最后检验它在被数据塑造的区域上仍然有意义（非平凡），而这正是旧界变松之处，因为旧界的大部分权重落在没有数据的区域上。\n\n*用测度加权谱隙表述的重新推导的泛化证书，由测度加权 Poincare 不等式（Dirichlet 能量 $E_\\mu $ 下界 $\\phi $ 的 $\\mu -$方差）支撑；在无权界变松的训练数据区域它仍非平凡。*\n$$ \\mathbb{E}[\\mathrm{GenError}] \\le \\frac{C'\\, L_f^2}{\\lambda_2(L_\\mu)}, \\qquad \\mathcal{E}_\\mu(\\phi) \\ge \\lambda_2(L_\\mu)\\,\\mathrm{Var}_\\mu(\\phi) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这表明该保证从来不真正关乎裸架构——被数据塑造的子对象才是正确定义域，用它之后界不再变得平凡。\n\n### 验证与对照\n*在一批网络上以测度加权代理量对照真实误差检验，并以均匀测度消融作为负对照。*\n\n8. 取你那批训练好的网络。对每一个计算旧预测 $C\\cdot L_{f}^{2}/\\lambda _{2}(L)$ 与新预测 $C'\\cdot L_{f}^{2}/\\lambda _{2}(L_\\mu )$，并测量它真实的泛化差距（test 误差减 train 误差）。对每个网络用同样的方法计算其 Lipschitz 常数 $L_{f}$（各层谱范数之积是一个干净的上界）。然后对每个预测，报告它将网络按真实泛化差距排序的好坏程度（Spearman 秩相关）。把两者并排对比就是这项检验。\n   - _为什么_: 把两个代理量与真实误差正面对比，是判断数据加权是否真的更能预测泛化的唯一办法。\n9. 现在做对照。重建测度加权图，但抹平数据加权：给每个保留下来的区域相同的质量，而非其真实数据质量，同时保持完全相同的区域、连接与边界通量因子。重新计算谱隙，以及它对真实泛化差距的预测好坏。如果预测质量退回到无权基线，那就证明承载预测能力的是数据加权本身——而非仅仅裁剪到访问过的区域。\n   - _为什么_: 这能隔离因果：若把数据加权抹平后信号消失，那么承载预测的是数据测度本身，而不仅是裁剪到访问过的区域。\n\n"},{"id":"16","run_dir":"run_prompt16_ethicaldata","index":16,"title":"Risk-Budgeted Corpus Curation: Spending a Provenance-Risk Budget for Pre-training Utility","title_zh":"风险预算式语料构建：为预训练效用支出来源风险预算","method_name":"Risk-Budgeted Corpus Curation (RBCC)","hook":"Open pre-training corpora (Common Corpus, semanticscholar:9aff73d0ddf6badbecee2979782003376020cf93) decide a document's admissibility by a binary, source-level whitelist — copyrighted-or-not — which tacitly assumes provenance risk is a property of the source and not of the document, so the clean-vs-capable tradeoff is locked to one fixed operating point. We estimate a graded provenance-risk score per document from its own observable content and metadata, and select the corpus by maximizing predicted utility subject to an explicit aggregate risk budget, turning that fixed point into a movable, measured frontier.","anchor_pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","anchor_pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","domain_category":"LLM Alignment, Safety & Behavior","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a per-document, graded provenance-risk quantity that is jointly optimized with that document's measured utility for the model, so practitioners cannot trade a bounded amount of legal/consent risk for capability rather than accepting a single fixed clean-vs-capable operating point.","pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"closed by reframing corpus construction as a budgeted constrained subset-selection object — maximize a submodular predicted-utility set function over candidate documents subject to an aggregate provenance-risk knapsack budget B — whose greedy-under-budget solver ships a runnable curated corpus at any chosen B, replacing the single fixed operating point with a movable, certifiable selection.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions whether provenance admissibility must be decided at the source level at all, rather than as a property estimable per document from the document's own observable content and metadata.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","how_closed":"framing half (C01) relocates the admissibility-enforcement locus from the source identifier to the document's own observable content+metadata, naming 'admissibility is a per-source binary property' as the load-bearing assumption and showing it is the wrong locus; companion (self_supervised_signal_engineering) ships the missing deliverable — a graded per-document provenance-risk estimator r(d) trained on a manufactured comparative risk signal harvested from documents whose source-level license is known, which is the very object the anchor's optimizer spends against.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"ethical / open-provenance data curation for LLM pre-training","n_papers":42,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":27},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":18,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Chinese Tiny LLM: Pretraining a Chinese-Centric Large Language Model"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Pretraining Data Detection for Large Language Models: A Divergence-based Calibration Method"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Improving Pretraining Data Using Perplexity Correlations"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Applications of Large Language Models in the Field of Suicide Prevention: Scoping Review"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Generative AI and LLMs"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Large Language Models in Healthcare and Medical Domain: A Review"}],"more":12},{"year":2025,"n":22,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Towards Safer Pretraining: Analyzing and Filtering Harmful Content in Webscale datasets for Responsible LLMs"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Uncovering Pretraining Code in LLMs: A Syntax-Aware Attribution Approach"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Common Corpus: The Largest Collection of Ethical Data for LLM Pre-Training"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Utilizing Open Access Publications and Educational Content in LLM-Based Research: Global Trends and Ethical–Policy Considerations"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"BeyondWeb: Lessons from Scaling Synthetic Data for Trillion-scale Pretraining"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Primus: A Pioneering Collection of Open-Source Datasets for Cybersecurity LLM Training"}],"more":16},{"year":2026,"n":1,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"}],"more":0}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":8,"share":0.19},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":8,"share":0.19},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":5,"share":0.119},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":5,"share":0.119},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":3,"share":0.071},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":2,"share":0.048},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":2,"share":0.048},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":2,"share":0.048}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Open/ethical pre-training corpora certify legal-and-consent status as a binary, source-level whitelist decided once at corpus-assembly time: Common Corpus (semanticscholar:9aff73d0ddf6badbecee2979782003376020cf93) admits a document iff its source is uncopyrighted or under an open license, and Lucie (semanticscholar:a2fe7438d86868422b70f2f575febe8e4fbcd4fd) likewise assembles by source provenance whitelist, so the inclusion decision is divorced from how much that document actually helps a downstream model. The opposing line treats provenance only as something to detect after the fact: Beyond Public Access (openalex:W4409018263) and the divergence-calibration detector (semanticscholar:beb2d4faee9f9c752a7993566a096cc3570a869f) run membership-inference attacks on a finished model to ask whether disallowed content was used, but produce no signal that could have governed inclusion before training. The result is that no method assigns each candidate document a graded, auditable provenance-risk quantity that is co-optimized with its measured utility for the model, so a practitioner is forced into an all-or-nothing choice between a provably clean but smaller corpus and a web-scale but legally-uncertain one (semanticscholar:9aff73d0ddf6badbecee2979782003376020cf93, semanticscholar:735f8b04e8b130ff126a24b856046e5c55a4e98d), with no characterized frontier in between and no way to spend a bounded amount of legal risk where it buys the most capability.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:9aff73d0ddf6badbecee2979782003376020cf93","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Common Corpus assembles the largest open pre-training dataset by admitting only documents whose source is uncopyrighted or openly licensed, and shows two small models trained on it perform comparably to same-size peers. Its inclusion rule is a per-source binary gate decided once at assembly time: it neither attaches a graded per-document provenance-risk score nor jointly weighs that risk against the document's measured contribution to the model, so the clean-vs-capable tradeoff is taken as a fixed point rather than a curve a practitioner can move along under a chosen risk budget."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4409018263","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Beyond Public Access uses the DE-COP membership-inference attack on a public/non-public split of 34 O'Reilly books to detect whether OpenAI's models trained on paywalled copyrighted content. The method is purely post-hoc on a finished model and yields a model-level AUROC verdict; it produces no per-document inclusion signal usable during corpus construction and certifies nothing about the consent status of documents that were used."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:735f8b04e8b130ff126a24b856046e5c55a4e98d","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Perplexity-Correlations selects pre-training documents by their correlation between LLM loss and downstream benchmark score, with no model training of its own, optimizing purely for measured utility. Provenance / legal status is never a selection variable, so the selector will happily up-weight high-utility documents of uncertain or disallowed origin; it gives the utility axis the candidate needs but leaves the risk axis entirely uncoupled."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:a2fe7438d86868422b70f2f575febe8e4fbcd4fd","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Lucie-7B assembles an OSI-compliant multilingual open corpus by whitelisting trustworthy sources (cultural-heritage archives, public web) to offset anglo-centric bias. Provenance is again a source-level binary admission; there is no per-document license-risk grade and no reported cleanliness-vs-utility frontier, so contributors cannot see what capability they trade away for each increment of guaranteed cleanliness."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"ethical / open-provenance data curation for LLM pre-training","venue":"ICLR / NeurIPS / ICML (top ML)","time":"2026","data":["Common Corpus","FineWeb / C4 / Common Crawl","openly-licensed and public-domain text collections","per-document license / provenance metadata"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with data-curation and small-scale pretraining experience","preference":"both","baseline":"source-whitelist open corpora (Common Corpus, Lucie) vs quality-filtered web (FineWeb); post-hoc membership-inference auditors (DE-COP, Min-K%/divergence calibration)","limitation":"open/ethical corpora certify provenance as a binary source-level include/exclude with no per-document risk quantification or measured cleanliness-vs-utility frontier","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"Shared object (shared_object thread): a single per-document provenance-risk score r(d) in [0,1] that the audit leg constructs and the anchor leg optimizes against. AUDIT LEG (C01 + companion): we pivot the field's locus assumption — Common Corpus (semanticscholar:9aff73d0ddf6badbecee2979782003376020cf93) and Lucie (semanticscholar:a2fe7438d86868422b70f2f575febe8e4fbcd4fd) enforce admissibility at the SOURCE — and relocate it to the document itself. The companion (self_supervised_signal_engineering, C26-style) manufactures the supervisory signal without human risk labels: from a seed pool where source-level license status IS known (open-licensed vs. all-rights-reserved scrapes), we harvest comparative pairs (a public-domain document is lower-risk than a paywalled-book passage) and fit a calibrated risk model r(d) = sigmoid(w^T phi(d)) by a pairwise ranking loss, where phi(d) is a fixed feature vector computed PER DOCUMENT from observable content+metadata only: (i) license/rights strings and dates parsed from the document's own metadata, (ii) near-duplicate overlap against a known-copyrighted reference index (MinHash Jaccard, computed), (iii) a learned text-classifier logit for 'commercial/published-work register'. r(d) is the calibrated probability that d would fail a license/consent audit; calibration is enforced by isotonic regression on a held-out source-labeled split so r is a probability, not an arbitrary score. ANCHOR LEG (C00): corpus construction is reframed as constrained subset selection. Utility of a selected set S is U(S) = sum over benchmark targets of the correlation-weighted per-document utility u(d) (we reuse the loss-vs-benchmark correlation utility of Perplexity-Correlations, semanticscholar:735f8b04e8b130ff126a24b856046e5c55a4e98d, as u(d), so no model training is needed to score utility); to make selection submodular we add a coverage term over a fixed topic partition so marginal utility diminishes as a topic fills. Aggregate risk is the additive knapsack cost C(S) = sum_{d in S} r(d) * tokens(d). We then solve max_S U(S) s.t. C(S) <= B and |tokens(S)| = N (target corpus size) by cost-benefit greedy (insert the document maximizing marginal U-gain per unit risk-cost until the budget or size binds), which inherits the standard (1-1/e)-style near-optimality guarantee for monotone submodular maximization under a knapsack constraint. Sweeping B from 0 (provably clean, equals the Common Corpus operating point) upward traces the cleanliness-vs-utility frontier as a measured curve. The two legs are ONE paper because r(d) is the single shared object: the audit leg's deliverable is exactly the per-unit cost the anchor leg's knapsack spends, so 'estimate risk per document' and 'spend a risk budget' read as one method, not two stapled contributions.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery decisively: the anchor's knapsack needs a per-document cost and the audit leg's entire deliverable IS that per-document cost r(d), so a single shared object (not two modules) is the correct structure — evidenced by the fact that neither leg is runnable without the other (the optimizer has no cost without r; r has no consumer without the budget). (b) Considered designs rejected: (1) a source-level cost (regression to n2's per-source whitelist — flagged) — rejected because it lands exactly on the REGRESSION FLAG node n2; we instead require r(d) to depend on document-observable features, never on the source identifier alone. (2) A post-hoc membership-inference verdict as the risk signal (c0's mechanism) — rejected because it is a trained-model verdict, not a pre-training per-document signal, and collapses to collateral node c0. (3) Utility-only selection (n3 / Perplexity-Correlations) — rejected because risk never enters the objective; we keep their u(d) but add the risk knapsack so the objective spans both axes, an axis n3 does not occupy. AVOIDED NODE recorded: n2 (per-source binary whitelist) and c0 (post-hoc MIA) — r(d) is a pre-training, per-document, content-derived calibrated probability, landing on neither.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: fix a 1.5B-parameter architecture and a ~30B-token budget; build corpora S_B at B in {0, low, mid, high} from a Common Corpus + FineWeb candidate pool using r(d) and the Perplexity-Correlations utility u(d); pre-train one model per S_B on 1xA100 and evaluate on a held-out benchmark suite (e.g. a HELM/lm-eval subset). If the candidate works, the measured cleanliness-vs-utility frontier is strictly increasing and CONCAVE in the low-budget regime — a small increment of risk budget buys a disproportionately large utility gain (benchmark accuracy rises faster than realized risk C(S_B)/N), the non-obvious direction being that the first units of allowed risk are far more capability-dense than a linear clean-vs-capable intuition predicts. NAMED LOAD-BEARING VARIABLE: the per-document risk score r(d). Negative-control intervention: replace r(d) with the source-level constant r_src(source(d)) (oracle-substitute the per-document grade by its source whitelist value) and re-run selection+training at matched aggregate risk; the anti-tautology test is on the DOWNSTREAM metric — predicted effect is that benchmark accuracy at matched risk budget DROPS relative to per-document r(d) (the curve loses its concave early gains), because the whitelist cannot up-weight individually-low-risk documents inside a high-risk source. Positive control: a stripped model selecting purely by r(d)-thresholding with uniform utility should recover most of the cleanliness gain but little of the utility gain, identifying which axis r(d) versus u(d) each drives.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:9aff73d0ddf6badbecee2979782003376020cf93","delta":"Common Corpus admits a document iff its source is uncopyrighted/open-licensed — a per-source binary gate decided once at assembly with no per-document risk grade; we construct a calibrated per-document risk probability r(d) from the document's own content+metadata and co-optimize it against utility under a movable budget, producing a frontier rather than their single operating point."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:735f8b04e8b130ff126a24b856046e5c55a4e98d","delta":"Perplexity-Correlations selects documents by predicted downstream utility alone with provenance never a variable; we reuse their utility u(d) but add an additive provenance-risk knapsack cost so the selection objective spans both the utility and the legal-risk axes, which their objective does not."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4409018263","delta":"Beyond Public Access runs a post-hoc DE-COP membership-inference attack on a finished model yielding a model-level AUROC verdict; we produce a pre-training, per-document inclusion signal r(d) computed before any training from observable document features, which their post-hoc attack structurally cannot supply."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:a2fe7438d86868422b70f2f575febe8e4fbcd4fd","delta":"Lucie whitelists trustworthy sources with no per-document license-risk grade and reports no cleanliness-vs-utility curve; we grade risk per document and measure the frontier's shape and slope as the central result."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:735f8b04e8b130ff126a24b856046e5c55a4e98d","what_step_was_missed":"Perplexity-Correlations built a per-document utility scalar u(d) and selected by it, but it never constructed a second per-document scalar for provenance risk nor framed selection as a budgeted constrained-subset problem; to already contain our contribution it would have needed to (i) construct a calibrated per-document risk cost r(d) from document-observable features and (ii) recast selection as monotone-submodular maximization under a risk-knapsack so a swept budget traces a cleanliness-vs-utility frontier — neither the risk cost nor the budgeted-selection construction exists in their utility-only ranking."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":227,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"Layer 1 hard floor did not fire: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict is borderline (no entry triggered with candidate_match: yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat (semanticscholar:519fa11...) is NOT exact-mechanism overlap — it provides only the generic frontier solver, while the candidate's load-bearing artifact r(d) and its pre-training-corpus admissibility framing are absent there. recipe_application_check.verdict is applied for both gaps (C00's submodular-knapsack object and C01's locus relocation are concretely instantiated, not generic). The two borderline gap_closure findings (axiomatic grounding of r(d); source-label bootstrap of the per-document estimator) hit a load-bearing property but are already mitigated by the r_src negative control in falsification_prediction, so they are surfaced as reviewer_concerns for Phase 4 rather than requiring a revise loop; the addressable threat is a wording tightening that Phase 4's differentiation framing absorbs without changing the mechanism.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a per-document, graded provenance-risk quantity that is jointly optimized with that document's measured utility for the model, so practitioners cannot trade a bounded amount of legal/consent risk for capability rather than accepting a single fixed clean-vs-capable operating point.","main_pattern":"reframe_as_solvable_object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The signature failure is treating the reframing as a mechanical wrapper: pointing an established subset-selection/attribution tool at a new granularity or domain without re-deriving why the resulting scores are faithful, supplying the computation but not the justification (no causal validation, no soundness argument for the proposed definition).","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Pointing an off-the-shelf decomposition at a coarser input granularity without showing the coarser units preserve the signal reads as a wrapper, not a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate does not coarsen granularity — it does the opposite, refining from source-level to per-document, and the per-document risk cost r(d) is a newly constructed object, not an off-the-shelf decomposition retargeted."},{"lesson_quoted":"Proposing a new attribution definition without an axiomatic or causal argument for why it should count as ground-truth collapses the moment a reviewer asks why this is the real importance.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"core_mechanism defines r(d) as a calibrated probability that a document fails a license/consent audit and enforces isotonic calibration on a source-labeled held-out split, but the 'ground-truth' that calibration targets is itself a source-level proxy label — the falsification_prediction's negative control (r_src substitution) supplies the causal validation that per-document grading drives the downstream metric, which mitigates but does not fully axiomatize the risk definition."},{"lesson_quoted":"Conflating a methodological artifact — a computation-granularity difference, a degenerate zero baseline — with genuine signal undermines the entire premise once the confound is identified.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The B=0 operating point is explicitly identified with the Common-Corpus all-clean baseline (not a degenerate zero artifact), and the frontier is measured by sweeping B, so the gain is read off a controlled curve rather than a single confounded point."},{"lesson_quoted":"Building a suppression or privacy method without formalizing the threat model leaves the central guarantee unverifiable regardless of strong empirical numbers.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate does not claim a privacy/suppression guarantee; r(d) is a graded risk estimate spent under an explicit budget, and the claim is a measured tradeoff frontier, not an unverifiable security guarantee."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions whether provenance admissibility must be decided at the source level at all, rather than as a property estimable per document from the document's own observable content and metadata.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is a successful relocation demonstrated but not adversarially closed (beats a fixed baseline but never an informed adversary at the new locus), or a novelty-boundary collapse where the 'new' locus was already used by prior work, or reintroducing the assumption the relocation was meant to dissolve.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a relocated signal is 'stealthier' or 'harder to remove' without defeating an adaptive defender who searches the same new locus leaves the central claim unverified.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"This is not an adversarial attack/defense setting; the relocation claim is that per-document content+metadata carries admissibility signal the source label discards, validated by the downstream-utility frontier at matched risk, not by an adaptive-adversary stealth claim."},{"lesson_quoted":"Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work — normalization statistics, activation-similarity losses, semantic concept triggers — collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"Per-document content scoring exists in utility-only selection (Perplexity-Correlations, n3) and post-hoc membership inference reads per-document signal from a trained model (c0); the candidate's distinction is that r(d) is a PRE-training, content-derived provenance-RISK probability spent under a budget — differentiation_from_lit makes this explicit against both, but the novelty boundary rests on that being measured, which the negative control does."},{"lesson_quoted":"A defense whose relocation silently depends on a clean reference model or a known anomaly distribution reintroduces precisely the strong assumption the move was supposed to eliminate.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"r(d)'s training depends on a seed pool whose SOURCE-level license is known to manufacture comparative anchors — this is a controlled reuse of source labels to bootstrap a per-document estimator, not a reintroduction of source-level admissibility at inference (r(d) at deployment uses only document-observable phi(d)), but a reviewer could argue the source labels leak back in via the training signal."},{"lesson_quoted":"Demonstrating the new locus only on fixed, non-adaptive or outdated baselines while omitting any account of why it works reads as a stacked pipeline of existing components rather than a principled shift.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The mechanistic account is explicit — the source whitelist cannot up-weight individually-low-risk documents inside a high-risk source — and the r_src negative control directly tests that account on the downstream metric."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No gap_closure entry is triggered (no Reject lesson marked candidate_match: yes). Two borderline findings carry weight: on the anchor (reframe_as_solvable_object / C00) the risk-definition lacks a full axiomatic grounding beyond a source-proxy calibration target, and on the sibling (assumption_audit_and_pivot / C01) the per-document risk estimator bootstraps from source-level labels, which a reviewer could read as the source assumption leaking back into training. Both are mitigated by the r_src negative control in falsification_prediction but remain load-bearing enough to surface for Phase 4."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a per-document, graded provenance-risk quantity that is jointly optimized with that document's measured utility for the model, so practitioners cannot trade a bounded amount of legal/consent risk for capability rather than accepting a single fixed clean-vs-capable operating point.","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"C00 recasts an opaque question as a concrete measurement over a well-studied object (a submodular subset selection, an estimator, an additive decomposition) whose native correctness criterion coincides with faithfulness, then buys tractability with one compression trick and certifies fidelity by causal intervention or a soundness/optimality proof.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism reframes corpus construction as monotone-submodular maximization under a risk-knapsack: U(S) is a coverage-augmented submodular utility set function, C(S)=sum r(d)*tokens(d) is the additive knapsack cost, solved by cost-benefit greedy inheriting the (1-1/e)-style near-optimality guarantee (the submodular subset-selection object of C00), with fidelity certified causally by the r_src negative control on the downstream benchmark metric — this is the C00 signature move, not a generic reframe.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions whether provenance admissibility must be decided at the source level at all, rather than as a property estimable per document from the document's own observable content and metadata.","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"C01's signature is to name the single representational LOCUS at which a provenance/detection/safety property is presumed enforced, then relocate enforcement to a different locus the field treated as invariant, and demonstrate the property manifests more robustly there; the companion manufactures the supervisory signal at the new locus.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism names the load-bearing locus assumption ('admissibility is enforced at the SOURCE', read off Common Corpus + Lucie) and relocates it to the document's own observable content+metadata, with the companion self_supervised_signal_engineering manufacturing the per-document risk signal r(d) from a pairwise-ranking loss over source-anchored comparative pairs — the C01 locus-relocation move plus its companion deliverable, both present.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries instantiate their cited cluster's signature move: C00's submodular-knapsack subset-selection object with a near-optimality guarantee and causal fidelity check is in core_mechanism, and C01's locus relocation (source -> per-document content+metadata) plus the companion's manufactured risk signal are both concretely present, not generic parent-pattern gestures."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["reframe_as_solvable_object","assumption_audit_and_pivot","self_supervised_signal_engineering"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions (audit_decomp_supervisor, audit_decomp_prior, audit_decomp_operator) require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; the candidate's composition_set contains no heterogeneous_decomposition, so no 2-way subset matches — in particular the self_supervised_signal_engineering companion is paired with assumption_audit_and_pivot, not with heterogeneous_decomposition, so audit_decomp_supervisor does not fire."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:519fa11dedda9a3706ed09ee23b985814fcc895c","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"Computing Approximate Pareto Frontiers for Submodular Utility and Cost Tradeoffs (arXiv 2026-02) computes representative sets of solutions exposing different tradeoffs between a monotone submodular utility and a cost, departing from the single-weighted-objective paradigm to return a frontier rather than one operating point — which is structurally the same shape as the candidate's 'sweep B to trace the cleanliness-vs-utility frontier'. The candidate's claim stands or falls on whether its contribution is the frontier-computation machinery (which this paper already provides generically) or the construction of the provenance-risk cost itself: the threat paper treats cost as a given abstract function and never constructs a per-document, content-derived provenance-risk probability r(d), never frames admissibility as a relocatable locus, and has no LLM pre-training corpus application. The candidate is not subsumed because its load-bearing artifact is r(d) (the audit-leg deliverable) and the measured downstream-utility consequence of spending it, not the submodular-knapsack/Pareto solver, which it reuses as off-the-shelf machinery.","addressable_via":"Tighten differentiation_from_lit and core_mechanism to state explicitly that the submodular-knapsack/Pareto-frontier solver is reused off-the-shelf and the contribution is the per-document provenance-risk cost r(d) plus its measured downstream-utility frontier in the LLM-pretraining setting, so the threat paper's generic frontier machinery is positioned as a consumed tool, not a competing claim."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Risk-Budgeted Corpus Curation: Spending a Provenance-Risk Budget for Pre-training Utility\n\n**Method.** Risk-Budgeted Corpus Curation (RBCC)\n\n## Motivation\nIf you are gathering text to pre-train a large language model (LLM), you face an all-or-nothing choice today. One option is an 'ethical' open corpus such as Common Corpus, which keeps a document only if its SOURCE (the website or collection it came from) is uncopyrighted or openly licensed. The other option is a web corpus such as FineWeb, which filters for quality but never asks about legal status at all. In both cases the keep-or-drop decision is made once, at the level of the whole source, and is completely separated from how useful each individual document actually is for the model. So you cannot say 'I will accept a little legal risk in exchange for a meaningful capability gain' — there is no dial to turn. Two recent results make a better approach possible now. Perplexity Correlations (Improving Pretraining Data Using Perplexity Correlations, ICLR 2024) showed you can cheaply estimate how useful each document is without any expensive training run. And post-hoc auditors like Beyond Public Access showed that legal-provenance evidence is readable from document-level signals — but only after the model is already trained, too late to guide what goes in. The missing piece is a before-training, per-document risk estimate that is weighed against usefulness. When that piece exists, the single clean-versus-capable point becomes a whole curve you can move along: pick how much total legal risk you will accept and spend it where it buys the most capability. Common Corpus's all-clean corpus simply becomes the zero-risk end of that curve.\n\n## Method\n### Per-document risk estimator\n*Manufactures a calibrated per-document provenance-risk probability r(d) from document-observable features, relocating admissibility from the source to the document.*\n\n1. Gather documents whose source license you already know and tag each as low-risk or high-risk. Draw the low-risk examples from open-licensed or public-domain collections (e.g. Common Corpus partitions marked public-domain, CC0, or CC-BY) and the high-risk examples from web scrapes whose site explicitly reserves all rights or gives no license (e.g. paywalled-publisher or no-license domains). Aim for roughly equal numbers of each (about 100,000 documents per side) so the later ranking step is balanced. Use these source tags only to teach the risk model — never when actually scoring documents later.\n   - _Why_: You need pairs of clearly-safe and clearly-risky examples to teach a per-document risk model without anyone hand-labeling risk.\n2. For every candidate document, compute a feature vector from the document itself. Use three kinds of features: license and rights text plus publication dates read from the document's own metadata; how much the document overlaps known-copyrighted text, measured by a fingerprint-overlap score (MinHash Jaccard, which estimates the fraction of shared text fragments) against a reference index of copyrighted material; and a text-classifier score for how much the document reads like a commercial published work (the classifier is trained to tell book/news/journal text from forum/social text). The name of the source the document came from is never used as a feature.\n   - _Why_: If risk is to be a property of the document, every input must come from the document's own observable content and metadata, not from which source it came from.\n3. Train a logistic risk model on the features from the previous step using a pairwise ranking loss — it learns that a clearly-risky example should score above a clearly-safe one. Then calibrate the score (with isotonic regression on a held-out set) so the output is an honest probability between 0 and 1 that the document would fail a copyright/consent check. 【author decision: you must fix exactly which audit-failure event this probability refers to — copyright-infringement risk, consent/opt-out (such as a site reserving text-and-data-mining rights) risk, or a combination — because the source-level training examples only approximate it, and the choice changes both how you label the anchors and what the probability means.】 This calibrated probability is the per-document risk score the selector will spend against.\n\n*The per-document provenance-risk score r(d): a logistic score on the document-observable feature vector $\\phi (d),$ passed through an isotonic calibrator Cal so r(d) is the calibrated probability the document fails a license/consent audit.*\n$$ r(d) = \\mathrm{Cal}\\!\\left(\\sigma(w^\\top \\phi(d))\\right), \\qquad \\sigma(z)=\\frac{1}{1+e^{-z}} \\tag{1} $$\n\n\n*The pairwise ranking loss that fits w from comparative pairs, where $d^{+}$ is a higher-risk anchor (e.g. an all-rights-reserved scrape) and $d^{-} a$ lower-risk anchor (e.g. a public-domain document), harvested from documents whose source-level license is known.*\n$$ \\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{rank}} = \\sum_{(d^{+},\\,d^{-})} \\log\\!\\left(1 + e^{\\,w^\\top \\phi(d^{+}) - w^\\top \\phi(d^{-})}\\right) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Calibration turns an arbitrary score into a real probability you can add up across documents and treat as a cost.\n\n### Risk-budgeted selector\n*Maximizes a submodular utility set function under an aggregate risk-budget knapsack to produce a curated corpus at any chosen budget.*\n\n4. Score how useful each document is with Perplexity Correlations (Improving Pretraining Data Using Perplexity Correlations), which estimates usefulness from the relationship between a document's loss and benchmark scores and needs no training of its own. Then turn these per-document scores into a set-level usefulness function: embed each document with a fixed text encoder, group the documents into about a thousand topic clusters, and within each cluster add up the usefulness but pass it through a diminishing-returns curve (such as a square root) so a topic stops helping once it is well covered. This set-level function having diminishing returns is what lets the simple greedy procedure in the next step come with a near-best-possible guarantee.\n   - _Why_: Making usefulness a set function with diminishing returns lets a simple greedy procedure come with a near-best-possible guarantee.\n5. For a chosen total risk budget, greedily build the corpus: repeatedly add the document that gives the most extra usefulness per unit of risk cost (its risk score times its number of tokens), but only consider documents that keep you within both the risk budget and the target corpus size. Stop when no further document can be added without breaking either limit. If you hit the size limit before spending the whole risk budget, just record the actual average risk you ended up with. The documents you kept are the curated corpus for that budget.\n\n*The risk-budgeted subset-selection objective: maximize the submodular utility set function U(S) subject to the additive provenance-risk knapsack cost C(S) staying under budget B at a fixed target corpus size N tokens.*\n$$ \\max_{S}\\; U(S) \\quad \\text{s.t.}\\quad C(S)=\\sum_{d\\in S} r(d)\\,\\mathrm{tokens}(d) \\le B,\\;\\; \\mathrm{tokens}(S)=N \\tag{3} $$\n\n\n*The cost-benefit greedy rule: repeatedly insert the document with the largest marginal utility gain per unit risk-cost until the budget B or the size N binds, inheriting the standard $(1- 1/e)-style$ guarantee for monotone submodular maximization under a knapsack constraint.*\n$$ d^{\\star} = \\arg\\max_{d\\notin S}\\; \\frac{U(S\\cup\\{d\\}) - U(S)}{r(d)\\,\\mathrm{tokens}(d)} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Spending risk where it buys the most usefulness is exactly the trade-off the old whitelist could not express.\n\n### Frontier measurement and control\n*Sweeps the budget, pre-trains one model per corpus to measure the cleanliness-vs-utility frontier, and runs the source-constant control to isolate per-document grading.*\n\n6. Repeat the selection across a range of budgets, measured by the average risk per token the corpus actually ends up with so the points are comparable. The lowest point keeps only effectively-zero-risk documents (reproducing the fully-clean corpus); the highest point lets the selector ignore risk entirely (utility-only). Use four to six points spanning that range and save one corpus per point, all at the same target size, so the corpora differ only in how much risk they admit.\n   - _Why_: A family of corpora at different budgets is what lets you draw a whole trade-off curve instead of reporting a single point.\n7. Pre-train the same 1.5-billion-parameter model on the same roughly 30 billion tokens once for each budget's corpus, keeping everything else identical: the same tokenizer (fit once on a separate reference sample so it does not vary with the corpus), the same learning-rate schedule, the same random seed. Because only the corpus changes, any difference in results comes from which tokens the model learned. Evaluate each trained model on a fixed held-out suite of standard benchmarks (reasoning, knowledge, and reading tasks from the lm-evaluation-harness) as mean accuracy, and plot that accuracy against the average risk the corpus actually carried. That plot is the cleanliness-versus-utility trade-off curve.\n   - _Why_: Only an actual trained model on each corpus shows where the trade-off curve really sits.\n8. As a control, replace each document's own risk score with a single number for its whole source — the average risk of all documents from that source — which turns the method back into a source-level whitelist. Re-run the selection and the training the same way, choosing budgets so the control corpus carries the same average risk as the per-document corpus at each point, and draw both trade-off curves on the same axes. If grading documents individually really matters, the control curve should sit lower at the same risk, because a single source-wide number cannot promote a genuinely-low-risk document that happens to come from an otherwise risky source.\n   - _Why_: It proves the gain comes from grading documents individually, not just from being risk-aware in general.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 风险预算式语料构建：为预训练效用支出来源风险预算\n\n**方法名称.** Risk-Budgeted Corpus Curation (RBCC)\n\n## 研究动机\n如果你要收集文本来预训练一个大语言模型(Large Language Model, LLM)，今天你只能做一个非此即彼的选择。一种是所谓“合乎伦理”的开放语料，比如 Common Corpus，它只保留来源(source，即文档所属的网站或合集)未受版权保护或采用开放许可的文档。另一种是像 FineWeb 这样的网页语料，它只按质量过滤，根本不问法律状态。这两种做法的“保留还是丢弃”都是在整个来源这一层级上一次性决定的，完全脱离了每篇文档对模型究竟有多大用处。于是你无法表达“我愿意承担一点点法律风险来换取明显的能力提升”——根本没有这样一个旋钮。两项近期成果让更好的做法成为可能。Perplexity Correlations(Improving Pretraining Data Using Perplexity Correlations, ICLR 2024)表明，无需任何昂贵的训练就能廉价地估计每篇文档的用处；而像 Beyond Public Access 这样的事后审计工作表明，法律来源证据可以从文档级信号中读出——但只能在模型训练完成之后读出，对决定“放什么进语料”已为时过晚。缺失的一环，是一个训练之前、逐文档的风险估计，并且要与用处相互权衡。一旦有了这一环，原本单一的“干净对能力”的点就变成一整条可以滑动的曲线：选定你愿意承担的总法律风险，然后把它花在能换来最多能力的地方。Common Corpus 那个全干净语料，就只是这条曲线上风险为零的端点。\n\n## 方法\n### 逐文档风险估计器\n*从文档可观测特征中制造出一个校准过的逐文档来源风险概率 r(d)，把可纳入性的判定从来源迁移到文档本身。*\n\n1. 收集那些你已经知道来源许可状态的文档，把每篇标为低风险或高风险。低风险样本取自开放许可或公有领域的合集(例如 Common Corpus 中标注为公有领域、CC0 或 CC-BY 的分区)，高风险样本取自其站点明确保留全部权利或未给出任何许可的网页抓取(例如付费墙出版商或无许可的域名)。两类数量大致相等(每侧约 100,000 篇)，使后续的排序步骤保持平衡。这些来源标签只用来训练风险模型，之后真正给文档打分时绝不使用。\n   - _为什么_: 你需要明确安全和明确有风险的样本对，才能在无人手工标注风险的情况下训练出一个逐文档的风险模型。\n2. 对每篇候选文档，仅从文档自身计算一个特征向量。使用三类特征：来自其自身 metadata 的许可/权利文字与发表日期；它与已知受版权保护文本的重叠程度——用一种指纹重叠分数(MinHash Jaccard，即估计两段文本共享片段所占比例)对照一个受版权保护材料的参考索引来度量；以及一个判断它读起来有多像商业出版作品的文本分类器分数(该分类器被训练去区分书籍/新闻/期刊文本与论坛/社交文本)。文档来自哪个来源(source)的名称绝不作为特征。\n   - _为什么_: 若要让风险成为文档本身的属性，所有输入都必须来自文档自身可观测的内容与 metadata，而不是它来自哪个来源。\n3. 用成对排序损失(pairwise ranking loss)在上一步的特征上训练一个逻辑回归风险模型——它学到明确有风险的样本应当排在明确安全的样本之上。再做校准(在留出集上用保序回归 isotonic regression)，使输出成为该文档通不过版权/同意审查的真实概率(介于 0 与 1 之间)。【作者需决定：必须明确这个概率所指的审查失败事件究竟是什么——版权侵权风险、同意/退出(consent/opt-out，例如站点保留文本与数据挖掘权利)风险，还是二者的组合——因为来源级的训练样本只是对它的近似，且这一选择会同时改变锚样本如何标注以及该概率的含义。】这个校准后的概率，就是选择器之后要据以支出的逐文档风险分数。\n\n*每篇文档的来源风险分数 r(d)：在仅依赖文档自身可观测特征向量 $\\phi (d)$ 的逻辑回归分数上，再经过保序校准器 Cal，使 r(d) 成为该文档通不过版权/同意审查的校准概率。*\n$$ r(d) = \\mathrm{Cal}\\!\\left(\\sigma(w^\\top \\phi(d))\\right), \\qquad \\sigma(z)=\\frac{1}{1+e^{-z}} \\tag{1} $$\n\n\n*用于拟合 w 的成对排序损失：$d^{+}$ 是更高风险的锚样本（如保留全部权利的网页抓取），$d^{-}$ 是更低风险的锚样本（如公有领域文档），这些锚样本取自来源级许可状态已知的文档。*\n$$ \\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{rank}} = \\sum_{(d^{+},\\,d^{-})} \\log\\!\\left(1 + e^{\\,w^\\top \\phi(d^{+}) - w^\\top \\phi(d^{-})}\\right) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 校准把一个任意的分数变成可以跨文档相加、并当作成本来对待的真实概率。\n\n### 风险预算选择器\n*在总风险预算背包约束下最大化次模效用集合函数，为任意选定预算产出一份构建好的语料。*\n\n4. 用 Perplexity Correlations(论文 Improving Pretraining Data Using Perplexity Correlations)给每篇文档的用处打分——它从文档损失与基准分数之间的关系来估计用处，本身无需训练。再把这些逐文档分数转成一个集合层面的用处函数：用一个固定的文本编码器给每篇文档生成嵌入，把文档聚成约一千个主题簇，在每个簇内把用处相加但经过一条边际递减曲线(例如平方根)，使某个主题被充分覆盖后就不再带来增益。正是这个集合层面函数的边际递减性质，让下一步那个简单的贪心过程能带上接近最优的保证。\n   - _为什么_: 把用处做成一个有边际递减的集合函数，能让一个简单的贪心过程带上接近最优的保证。\n5. 对选定的总风险预算，贪心地构建语料：反复加入“每单位风险成本(其风险分数乘以 token 数)带来用处增益最大”的文档，但只考虑那些既不超出风险预算、也不超出目标语料规模的文档。当再加任何文档都会突破其中某个上限时即停止。若你在用完全部风险预算之前就触及规模上限，就记录下最终实际得到的平均风险。留下的文档就是该预算下构建出的语料。\n\n*风险预算式子集选择目标：在固定目标语料规模 N 个 token、且加性来源风险背包成本 C(S) 不超过预算 B 的约束下，最大化次模效用集合函数 U(S)。*\n$$ \\max_{S}\\; U(S) \\quad \\text{s.t.}\\quad C(S)=\\sum_{d\\in S} r(d)\\,\\mathrm{tokens}(d) \\le B,\\;\\; \\mathrm{tokens}(S)=N \\tag{3} $$\n\n\n*成本-收益贪心规则：反复加入单位风险成本上边际效用增益最大的文档，直至预算 B 或规模 N 触顶；该规则继承背包约束下单调次模最大化的 $(1- 1/e)$ 型近似最优保证。*\n$$ d^{\\star} = \\arg\\max_{d\\notin S}\\; \\frac{U(S\\cup\\{d\\}) - U(S)}{r(d)\\,\\mathrm{tokens}(d)} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 把风险花在能换来最多用处的地方，正是旧的白名单无法表达的那种权衡。\n\n### 前沿测量与对照\n*扫描预算、对每份语料各预训练一个模型以测量“干净度对效用”前沿，并运行来源常数对照以分离出逐文档分级的作用。*\n\n6. 在一系列预算上重复这个选择过程，并以语料实际得到的“每 token 平均风险”来度量，使各点之间可比。最低点只保留实际风险为零的文档(复现完全干净的语料)；最高点让选择器完全忽略风险(纯按用处)。在这一区间取四到六个点，每点保存一份语料，且全部采用相同的目标规模，使这些语料仅在“允许多少风险”上有所不同。\n   - _为什么_: 一组不同预算下的语料，才能让你画出一整条权衡曲线，而不是只报告单个点。\n7. 对每个预算的语料，用同一个 15 亿参数的模型在同样约 300 亿个 token 上各预训练一次，其余一切保持一致：相同的分词器(tokenizer，在一份独立的参考样本上一次性拟合，使其不随语料变化)、相同的学习率调度、相同的随机种子。因为只有语料在变，结果上的任何差异都来自模型学到了哪些 token。在一套固定的留出标准基准(取自 lm-evaluation-harness 的推理、知识与阅读任务)上评测每个训练好的模型，以平均准确率衡量，并把该准确率对语料实际承载的平均风险作图。这张图就是“干净度对效用”的权衡曲线。\n   - _为什么_: 只有在每份语料上真正训练出的模型,才能显示权衡曲线究竟落在哪里。\n8. 作为对照，把每篇文档自身的风险分数替换为其整个来源的一个数值——该来源所有文档的平均风险——这就把方法退回成来源级白名单。以同样方式重跑选择与训练，并选取预算使对照语料在每个点上承载与逐文档语料相同的平均风险，再把两条权衡曲线画在同一坐标上。若对文档逐一分级确实重要，这条对照曲线在相同风险下应当更低，因为一个覆盖整个来源的单一数值，无法把一篇恰好来自高风险来源、但其本身风险很低的文档提上来。\n   - _为什么_: 这证明增益来自对文档逐一分级,而不仅仅是笼统地“对风险有意识”。\n\n"},{"id":"17","run_dir":"run_prompt17_graphcluster","index":17,"title":"Edge-Reliability-Weighted Structural Entropy for Calibrated K-Free Deep Graph Clustering","title_zh":"面向无需预设簇数的深度图聚类的边可靠性加权结构熵：可校准的节点级置信度方法","method_name":"Edge-Reliability-Weighted Structural Entropy (ER-SE)","hook":"Every deep graph clustering method anchors its objective to the observed adjacency as if the edges were exact, so it cannot say which node assignments are supported by trustworthy structure versus pushed there by noise; we make per-edge reliability a latent the model infers jointly with the partition, turning the spread of the resulting assignment posterior into a per-node support measure and proving it restores cluster identifiability in a noisy-edge regime where the deterministic structural-entropy objective provably cannot.","anchor_pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","anchor_pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","domain_category":"Graph Learning","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a per-node measure of how much its cluster assignment is supported by the data versus driven by edges the model itself treats as unreliable — every frontier method (contrastive CDGC, structural-entropy LSEnet/ASIL, AE-fusion GC-TriFA) emits a point partition (hard or soft) whose softmax confidence is calibrated to the proxy objective, not to the reliability of the underlying graph evidence, so a user cannot tell a confidently-clustered node from one placed only because","pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by diagnose-localize-then-correct on a tiny lever: the failure is localized to the structural-information functional consuming raw edge weights as exact, the model's own posterior over a per-edge reliability latent is the internal label-free readout, and a prior-anchor stabilizer prevents the degenerate 'all edges unreliable' collapse — the variance of the resulting per-node assignment posterior is the support measure that no point-partition method emits.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes how the K-free structural-entropy objective behaves as a function of edge-reliability degradation — LSEnet and ASIL report aggregate NMI on largely homophilous citation graphs but give no regime characterization of when the partitioning-tree solution becomes unidentifiable as inter-community edge density rises or degree imbalance grows, so the failure boundary of the K-free line is undocumented.","pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by formalizing the structural object the deterministic partitioning-tree procedure discards (edge reliability) as a partition-indistinguishability criterion: a separation theorem giving the inter-community-edge-density / degree-imbalance regime in which two distinct ground-truth partitions yield indistinguishable expected structural entropy, then proving the reliability-weighted objective re-injects exactly that object into the functional's core term and strictly separates the two partitions past the limit at near-linear added cost.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"deep graph clustering (unsupervised node clustering on attributed graphs with GNN representations)","n_papers":33,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":20},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":13,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"LSEnet: Lorentz Structural Entropy Neural Network for Deep Graph Clustering"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Towards Faster Deep Graph Clustering via Efficient Graph Auto-Encoder"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"An End-to-End Deep Graph Clustering via Online Mutual Learning"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Deep graph clustering via aligning representation learning"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Deep Graph Clustering With Triple Fusion Mechanism for Community Detection"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Joint Transmission for Industrial 5G-TSN Networks: A Deep Graph Clustering Approach"}],"more":7},{"year":2025,"n":20,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"MHGC: Multi-scale hard sample mining for contrastive deep graph clustering"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"ASIL: Augmented Structural Information Learning for Deep Graph Clustering in Hyperbolic Space"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Deep graph clustering method with improved cluster structure feature learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Deep Graph Clustering With Triple Fusion Mechanism for Community Detection"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Contrastive deep graph clustering with hard boundary sample awareness"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"DCPRES: Contrastive Deep Graph Clustering with Progressive Relaxation Weighting Strategy"}],"more":14}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":14,"share":0.424},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":7,"share":0.212},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":6,"share":0.182},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":5,"share":0.152},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":5,"share":0.152},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":4,"share":0.121},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":4,"share":0.121},{"pattern_id":"relax_discrete_search_to_continuous","pattern_name":"Relax Discrete Search to Continuous","count":3,"share":0.091}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Across the recent deep-graph-clustering frontier, the clustering objective is anchored to the observed adjacency as if that adjacency were a faithful realization of the latent community structure: contrastive methods build positive/negative pairs from graph neighborhoods and edge-aware augmentations (semanticscholar:2001345337bb29186f47247b4e4c6fa19abd677d, semanticscholar:a0337b769bed4cd911868faad8d8bcd788b5b62e), autoencoder/GCN-fusion methods reconstruct or align to the given edges (semanticscholar:266de6406cae49b83027fd27fe91a49f7665455b, openalex:W4404625703), and the K-free structural-entropy line minimizes a structural-information functional defined directly on the edge weights of the input graph (semanticscholar:9ff579d85ba330bfeaaa63eb39150793b6d70f40, semanticscholar:c9bc2ea12ba84e4e87a7247221391257e03c7524). When the observed edges are a noisy or heterophilous proxy for community membership — many inter-community edges, missing intra-community edges, or heavy-tailed degree imbalance — the objective is being optimized against a corrupted target, and the methods cannot tell which node assignments are well-supported by the data versus which are artifacts of the noisy proxy: they emit a single hard or soft partition with no per-node statement of how much the assignment depends on edges the model itself is uncertain about, so failures on minority clusters and boundary nodes (semanticscholar:7b5e22c0e7c1128eebdfd714a098394c31f3006b, semanticscholar:c9bc2ea12ba84e4e87a7247221391257e03c7524) surface only as aggregate metric drops with no internal signal that localizes or quantifies them.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:9ff579d85ba330bfeaaa63eb39150793b6d70f40","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"LSEnet recasts K-free graph clustering as minimizing a differentiable structural-information (DSI) functional over a neural partitioning tree in Lorentz hyperbolic space, deriving the optimal tree directly from the observed edge weights so the cluster number need not be predefined. The residue: DSI is computed against the input adjacency as a fixed, trusted target — the method has no mechanism to express that some edges (and therefore some leaf-to-parent assignments) are unreliable, so it yields a point-estimate partition with no per-node uncertainty and no way to down-weight the noisy edges that drive its documented difficulty on imbalanced graphs.","summary_and_residue_source":"fulltext_method"},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:c9bc2ea12ba84e4e87a7247221391257e03c7524","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"ASIL augments the structural-entropy objective with a contrastive term and proves a graph-conductance improvement, extending LSEnet to imbalanced graphs and minority-cluster recovery in linear complexity. The residue: it still optimizes a single deterministic augmented-structural-entropy objective on the given graph and reports only aggregate NMI/conductance — it produces no posterior or calibrated confidence over assignments, so it cannot say which minority-cluster nodes it actually recovered reliably versus which it merely placed."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:7b5e22c0e7c1128eebdfd714a098394c31f3006b","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Hard-boundary-aware contrastive deep graph clustering identifies boundary samples and adjusts the contrastive pair construction to handle them. The residue: boundary identification is threshold-driven and discrete — it labels a node hard-or-not without a continuous, model-derived measure of how much the node's assignment is destabilized by edge noise, so it cannot propagate that uncertainty into the objective or report it to a user."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:266de6406cae49b83027fd27fe91a49f7665455b","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"GC-TriFA balances node attributes and graph topology through a triple-fusion autoencoder with fixed modality-fusion weights to mitigate topology-misled clustering. The residue: the trust placed in topology versus attributes is a single global learned weight, not a per-node or per-edge adaptive quantity, so on graphs where edge reliability varies across the graph the fusion cannot locally discount the unreliable structure."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"deep graph clustering (unsupervised node clustering on attributed graphs with GNN representations)","venue":"ICLR / ICML / NeurIPS (Oral tier)","time":"2026","data":["Cora","Citeseer","Pubmed","ogbn-arxiv","Amazon-Photo/Computers","heterophilous benchmarks (Squirrel, Chameleon, Actor)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"graph machine learning, self-supervised / contrastive learning, spectral graph theory","preference":"both","baseline":"contrastive deep graph clustering (MHGC, DCPRES, hard-boundary-aware CDGC), structural-entropy K-free clustering (LSEnet, ASIL), AE/GCN-VAE fusion (GC-TriFA)","limitation":"current deep graph clustering treats the observed adjacency as a trustworthy clustering signal and patches its noise with hand-tuned heuristics; methods that drop K still lack any per-node statement of how confident an assignment is and degrade silently on imbalanced / heterophilous graphs","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object both legs read from and write to is the per-edge reliability latent r_uv in [0,1] and its induced reliability-weighted structural-information functional over the neural partitioning tree. (Leg 1, anchor — C07.) We diagnose the failure site precisely: the differentiable structural-information (DSI) functional of the K-free line sums, over each non-root tree node alpha, a term proportional to g_alpha/Vol(G) * log(V_alpha / V_alpha-), where g_alpha is the cut weight of module T_alpha and V_alpha its volume — all computed from the OBSERVED edge weights w_uv taken as exact (this is the LSEnet/ASIL form, semanticscholar:9ff579d85ba330bfeaaa63eb39150793b6d70f40). The label-free internal readout we manufacture is a per-edge reliability r_uv = sigmoid(phi(h_u, h_v, e_uv)), where h_u, h_v are the current GNN node embeddings (model-internal), e_uv are observed edge features (or 1 if none), and phi is a small 2-layer MLP scorer (the only added parameters); r_uv is the model's own posterior belief that edge (u,v) reflects true community co-membership rather than noise. We re-weight every edge weight in the functional as w-tilde_uv = r_uv * w_uv, so g_alpha and V_alpha become reliability-weighted, and the clustering objective is minimized over the tree assignment AND r jointly — this is the 'minimize on a tiny lever' confined to phi while the GNN backbone and tree decoder follow the standard K-free training. Because a label-free reliability signal left alone collapses to the degenerate r_uv -> 0 for all edges (which trivially zeroes the functional), we bolt on the C07 stabilizer: a source-prior anchor that pins the batch-mean of r toward a prior reliability rho_0 (a single hyperparameter, default 0.7) via a penalty lambda * (mean(r) - rho_0)^2, plus a sharpness term that discourages uniformly-middling r. The per-node assignment-support measure is then the entropy/variance of the soft leaf-to-cluster assignment distribution computed under T posterior samples of r (Monte-Carlo dropout on phi gives the posterior): a node whose assignment flips across reliability samples has high spread = low support, exactly the quantity no point-partition method (LSEnet, ASIL, GC-TriFA semanticscholar:266de6406cae49b83027fd27fe91a49f7665455b) emits. (Leg 2, sibling — C10.) The discarded structural object the deterministic DSI procedure throws away is precisely r: DSI is invariant to whether a cut edge is reliable, so it conflates a partition whose discriminating edges are reliable with one whose discriminating edges are noise. We formalize this as a partition-indistinguishability criterion: define two partitions P1, P2 differing only on a node set S; under an edge-noise model where inter-community edges appear with probability beta and intra-community edges are missing with probability gamma, there is a regime (beta, gamma above a threshold tied to the degree imbalance kappa) in which E[DSI(P1)] = E[DSI(P2)] to first order, so the deterministic objective cannot separate them (the separation criterion). We prove (i) the deterministic DSI fails this criterion — exhibiting the explicit (beta, gamma, kappa) regime where the expected-entropy gap vanishes — and (ii) the reliability-weighted functional with r recovered from the embeddings re-injects the discarded object so E[DSI_r(P1)] != E[DSI_r(P2)] strictly, restoring identifiability, with the added cost bounded to O(|E|) per step (one MLP eval per edge) — the C10 bounded-overhead requirement. The two legs share r: leg 1 builds the mechanism that infers and exploits r, leg 2 proves r is the exact object whose absence makes the K-free objective unidentifiable in the noisy regime, so the empirical support measure and the theoretical identifiability boundary are two faces of one quantity.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules because both pivot on the single latent r — the support measure (leg 1) is the posterior spread of assignments under r, and the identifiability theorem (leg 2) is a statement about what r's absence costs the objective; evidence that they are one object is that removing r collapses BOTH the support measure (becomes the uncalibrated softmax) and the identifiability gain (reverts to deterministic DSI), so a shared_object thread is honest, not stapled. (b) Alternatives considered: (i) generative_process_redesign C23/C24 — rejected because deep graph clustering has no iterative diffusion/flow refinement backbone whose conditioning interface or per-step distribution is the free variable, so the cluster's tactical move (re-derive the chain around a swapped internal component) would not actually apply and would trip recipe_application_check; (ii) a pure pseudo-label generate-and-filter loop (C08) — rejected because it manufactures new INSTANCES, whereas our signal is an internal-state readout of an existing graph, the C07 move; (iii) modeling r with a full edge-wise variational posterior — rejected as over-parameterized versus the C07 'tiny lever' discipline and harder to anchor against collapse. REGRESSION CHECK (method_lineage.notes flags the SBM family n1, collateral, as the older 'treat edges as noisy draws from latent structure' move): our mechanism does NOT reduce to SBM posterior-over-memberships — r is a deep, attribute-and-embedding-conditioned per-edge reliability that feeds the K-free differentiable structural-information objective and a learned GNN representation, clearing the deep-representation bar n1 never reached; we are not inferring block memberships from a hand-specified generative model, we are reweighting a learned structural objective, so the avoided node is n1.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: train the reliability-weighted model and a matched deterministic-DSI baseline (identical backbone, r forced to 1) on planted-partition synthetic graphs swept over inter-community edge probability beta and on real heterophilous graphs (Squirrel, Chameleon, Actor), measuring clustering NMI/ARI and, for the support measure, the AUROC of using s_v to predict whether node v is misclustered. If the candidate works, NMI/ARI on the high-beta and heterophilous graphs increases over the deterministic baseline while the support measure s_v shows high AUROC (low s_v concentrates on the misclustered nodes), and the synthetic expected-DSI gap stays positive for DSI_r past the beta-threshold where the deterministic gap collapses to zero. The single named load-bearing variable is the inferred per-edge reliability r_uv. Negative control: replace the learned r_uv with a random reliability field r_uv ~ Uniform(0,1) (re-sampled each step, same mean rho_0 so the stabilizer is satisfied) — if r is the mechanism, this should drive the DOWNSTREAM clustering NMI/ARI back to (or below) the deterministic baseline and destroy the s_v misclustering-AUROC, because the support measure now reflects injected noise rather than data-grounded reliability; if NMI and the AUROC survive random r, the gain came from the added capacity/regularization of phi rather than from reliability inference and the mechanism claim is falsified. Positive control (recommended): a stripped model that keeps only r-reweighting of the cut term and removes all other additions should recover most of the high-beta NMI gain, identifying r as the carrier.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:9ff579d85ba330bfeaaa63eb39150793b6d70f40","delta":"LSEnet minimizes the differentiable structural-information functional against the observed edge weights taken as exact and emits a single point partitioning tree; we make the edge weights an inferred per-edge reliability latent r, derive the reliability-weighted functional, and produce a per-node assignment-support posterior plus an identifiability theorem stating the exact noise regime where their deterministic objective cannot separate two distinct partitions but ours can."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:c9bc2ea12ba84e4e87a7247221391257e03c7524","delta":"ASIL proves a graph-conductance improvement for an augmented-structural-entropy objective on imbalanced graphs but still reports only aggregate NMI/conductance with no posterior; we add the per-edge reliability latent and the across-sample assignment spread, giving a calibrated per-node confidence and proving the conductance/identifiability gain is attributable specifically to re-injecting edge reliability (the object ASIL's deterministic objective discards)."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:7b5e22c0e7c1128eebdfd714a098394c31f3006b","delta":"Hard-boundary-aware CDGC labels boundary samples via a discrete threshold and adjusts contrastive pairs; we replace the discrete hard/not label with a continuous model-inferred reliability that propagates into the clustering objective itself and yields a posterior support measure, rather than a one-off pair-construction adjustment."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:266de6406cae49b83027fd27fe91a49f7665455b","delta":"GC-TriFA balances topology versus attributes with a single global learned fusion weight; we infer a per-edge reliability that varies across the graph, so structure can be locally discounted where edges are unreliable rather than trusted uniformly modulo one scalar."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:9ff579d85ba330bfeaaa63eb39150793b6d70f40","what_step_was_missed":"LSEnet derived the differentiable structural-information functional and the partitioning-tree construction over the observed edge weights, but it treated those edge weights as a fixed exact target; to already contain our contribution it would have had to (i) promote the per-edge weight to an inferred latent r conditioned on the learned embeddings, (ii) re-derive the structural-information functional as an expectation over r, and (iii) prove that this re-injected reliability term is exactly what restores partition identifiability in the inter-community-noise / degree-imbalance regime where the deterministic functional's expected-entropy gap vanishes — none of which their construction produces."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":324,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"No hard-floor rule fired: gap_closure_reject_check is borderline (not triggered — no Reject lesson is candidate_match:yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat is partial-overlap (addressable), not exact-mechanism. Within the safe zone the verdict is revise rather than advance because the borderline finding hits a load-bearing property — the surpass-the-limit novelty claim of leg 2 — via the C10 reject lesson 'claiming a construction a recently published method already subsumes', driven by the addressable threat semanticscholar:c8008f3ec81fcbb4dc24e583c20582a51bb17c3a whose subsumption_argument names a specific candidate field (differentiation_from_lit) to update. recipe_application_check is applied on both legs, so only a tactical field edit is needed.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a per-node measure of how much its cluster assignment is supported by the data versus driven by edges the model itself treats as unreliable — every frontier method (contrastive CDGC, structural-entropy LSEnet/ASIL, AE-fusion GC-TriFA) emits a point partition (hard or soft) whose softmax confidence is calibrated to the proxy objective, not to the reliability of the underlying graph evidence, so a user cannot tell a confidently-clustered node from one placed only because the noisy adjacency happened to push it there.","main_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure shape is a manufactured internal signal whose validity silently rests on an assumption that does not survive deployment (model calibration, a stationary/known-finite set of shift types, or covert use of target/test-set information amounting to label leakage), so the surrogate degrades precisely when the deployment premise is violated. A second co-occurring shape is recombining well-known components without a single load-bearing mechanistic insight that separates the work from the prior art it resembles.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A label-free signal whose validity depends on model calibration silently fails on exactly the deep networks known to be poorly calibrated — validate a surrogate where its core assumption is weakest, not where it is convenient.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The reliability latent r_uv is not a calibration-dependent surrogate; it is trained jointly into the DSI objective and the candidate explicitly stress-tests it where structure is weakest (heterophilous Squirrel/Chameleon/Actor and high-beta synthetic graphs), i.e. exactly where the assumption is most strained rather than convenient."},{"lesson_quoted":"Recasting a continuous shift as a discrete, known, finite set of types indexed against a precomputed lookup table collapses the moment an unanticipated or mixed shift arrives.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"r_uv is a continuous per-edge latent sigmoid(phi(h_u,h_v,e_uv)) inferred per graph, not a discrete lookup over a finite set of noise types, so this failure shape does not apply."},{"lesson_quoted":"Importing a generic continual-learning blending or interpolation technique into a new modality without identifying that modality's specific dynamics lever reads as recombination, not contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The modality-specific lever is named precisely: the DSI cut-weight g_alpha and volume V_alpha consuming raw edge weights as exact; r re-weights exactly that site rather than importing a generic blending scheme."},{"lesson_quoted":"Reusing standard sequential machinery (chaining each step's posterior as the next prior) without a new stabilizer amplifies noise and looks derivative of prior adaptation work.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"There is no sequential posterior chaining; the candidate adds a concrete new stabilizer (L_stab source-prior anchor toward rho_0=0.7 plus a sharpness term) explicitly to prevent the r->0 collapse."},{"lesson_quoted":"A multi-branch or ensemble reweighting mechanism that overlaps with standard multi-task/mixture-of-experts ensembling must explicitly beat both the single-model and the standard-ensemble baselines, or the gain is credited to prior art.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The mechanism is single-model edge reweighting, not multi-branch/MoE ensembling; the negative control (random-r, same mean) and positive control (r-reweighting only) already isolate the gain to reliability inference rather than added-branch capacity."},{"lesson_quoted":"Using target or test-set information during adaptation invites a label-leakage objection that undermines the very source-free, label-free deployment setting the method claims.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"r is computed from model-internal embeddings and observed edge features only; no target labels or test-set statistics enter, so no leakage objection arises."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes how the K-free structural-entropy objective behaves as a function of edge-reliability degradation — LSEnet and ASIL report aggregate NMI on largely homophilous citation graphs but give no regime characterization of when the partitioning-tree solution becomes unidentifiable as inter-community edge density rises or degree imbalance grows, so the failure boundary of the K-free line is undocumented.","main_pattern":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail when the 'limit' is not a genuine structural blindspot: trivially implied by the model's own assumptions, already surpassed by a published method, or never formalized beyond an informal analogy; a recurring shape substitutes a hand-wavy mechanism for a separation proof, another constructs the operator first and asserts superiority without surveying the frontier.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Resting the central claim on an informal analogy (two operators 'both smooth high frequencies') instead of a separation proof leaves the mechanism underspecified and the empirical gain unconvincing.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate states an explicit partition-indistinguishability criterion (E[DSI(P1)]=E[DSI(P2)] to first order under an (beta,gamma,kappa) edge-noise model) rather than an analogy, and ties the surpass claim to re-injecting r into the functional's core term."},{"lesson_quoted":"Applying existing structural descriptors to a new application domain without formalizing a new limit or constructing a new operator yields a domain study, not a methodological contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"It both formalizes a new limit (the indistinguishability regime) and constructs a new operator (DSI_r), so it is not a descriptor-transfer domain study."},{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a 'maximally expressive' construction that a recently published method already strictly subsumes turns the surpass-the-limit claim into redundant work.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"A 2026 weighted-clustering paper (semanticscholar:c8008f3ec81fcbb4dc24e583c20582a51bb17c3a) also weakens noisy edges and jointly optimizes clustering+edge weights; it does not subsume the identifiability theorem or the DSI partitioning-tree formalism, but the frontier survey must name it explicitly so the surpass claim is not read as redundant."},{"lesson_quoted":"A novel formalism that cannot generate predictions or demonstrate concrete advantages over existing definitions reads as abstraction for its own sake.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The formalism generates a concrete falsifiable prediction (the expected-DSI gap collapses to zero for deterministic DSI at the beta-threshold but stays positive for DSI_r) traced empirically in step 9."},{"lesson_quoted":"Asserting the 'first efficient implementation' of a long-known algorithm without surveying the landscape invites direct refutation by existing faster implementations and collapses the novelty claim.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate does not claim a first-efficient-implementation of a known algorithm; its O(|E|) overhead is a tractability bound on a new operator, not an efficiency-primacy claim."},{"lesson_quoted":"Deriving a 'limitation' that is trivially implied by the model's own linearity assumption produces a limit too weak to count as a real blindspot.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The unidentifiability limit is a genuine blindspot of the deterministic DSI (it is invariant to whether a cut edge is reliable), not a triviality implied by a linearity assumption; the candidate exhibits the explicit (beta,gamma,kappa) regime where the gap vanishes."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The anchor leg (self_supervised_signal_engineering / C07) is fully clear on all six reject lessons. The sibling theory leg (characterize_limit_then_surpass / C10) is borderline on the single lesson 'claiming a construction a recently published method already subsumes' because a 2026 weighted-graph-clustering paper also jointly optimizes clustering and edge weights to weaken noisy connections; it does not subsume the identifiability theorem or the K-free DSI formalism, so the lesson is borderline rather than triggered and is dischargeable by an explicit frontier comparison."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a per-node measure of how much its cluster assignment is supported by the data versus driven by edges the model itself treats as unreliable — every frontier method (contrastive CDGC, structural-entropy LSEnet/ASIL, AE-fusion GC-TriFA) emits a point partition (hard or soft) whose softmax confidence is calibrated to the proxy objective, not to the reliability of the underlying graph evidence, so a user cannot tell a confidently-clustered node from one placed only because the noisy adjacency happened to push it there.","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Treat the model's own internal-state readouts as the manufactured supervisory signal, pairing a mechanistic diagnosis that localizes the failure to a specific structural site with a surgically confined correction on a minimal lever while the backbone is otherwise preserved, and always bolt on an explicit stabilizer because a label-free internal signal invites a degenerate solution — diagnose-localize, minimize-on-a-tiny-lever, stabilize-against-collapse.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"All three signature verbs are performed: diagnose-localize — the failure is pinned to the DSI functional's g_alpha/V_alpha terms consuming raw w_uv as exact (the LSEnet/ASIL form); minimize-on-a-tiny-lever — the only added parameters are the 2-layer MLP phi producing r_uv=sigmoid(phi(h_u,h_v,e_uv)), the internal label-free readout, with r re-weighting w-tilde_uv=r_uv*w_uv inside the existing objective; stabilize-against-collapse — L_stab=lambda*(mean(r)-rho_0)^2 + mu*sharpness(r) is added explicitly to prevent the degenerate r->0 collapse, matching the C07 source-prior-anchor stabilizer verbatim.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes how the K-free structural-entropy objective behaves as a function of edge-reliability degradation — LSEnet and ASIL report aggregate NMI on largely homophilous citation graphs but give no regime characterization of when the partitioning-tree solution becomes unidentifiable as inter-community edge density rises or degree imbalance grows, so the failure boundary of the K-free line is undocumented.","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Take an iterative/locally-scoped procedure over a relational structure, name the one structural object it discards for tractability, formalize the equivalence class this induces as a separation/indistinguishability criterion on the procedure's native objects, prove the established class conflates objects differing only in the discarded property, then re-inject that exact object into the procedure's core step and prove the augmented operator strictly exceeds the criterion at bounded (linear/polynomial) added cost.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"The signature move is performed on the DSI partitioning-tree procedure: the discarded object is named (edge reliability r — DSI is invariant to whether a cut edge is reliable); the indistinguishability criterion is stated on native objects (E[DSI(P1)]=E[DSI(P2)] to first order in the (beta,gamma,kappa) regime); the conflation is proved by exhibiting the explicit regime; r is re-injected into the core cut-weight/volume computation (DSI_r) with a strict-separation proof E[DSI_r(P1)]!=E[DSI_r(P2)]; and the added cost is bounded to O(|E|) per step. This is the exact re-injection-at-bounded-cost recipe, not the parent's generic gist.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries instantiate their cited cluster's distinctive move in core_mechanism: C07's diagnose-localize / tiny-lever (phi) / stabilize-against-collapse (L_stab) triad is fully present, and C10's name-discarded-object / separation-criterion / re-inject-at-bounded-cost recipe is fully present on the DSI procedure rather than a generic limit-then-beat gesture."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["self_supervised_signal_engineering","characterize_limit_then_surpass"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"Neither main_pattern is heterogeneous_decomposition, and no 2-way subset matches audit_decomp_supervisor / audit_decomp_prior / audit_decomp_operator, so no documented reject-favored composition applies."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:c8008f3ec81fcbb4dc24e583c20582a51bb17c3a","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"Weighted Graph Clustering via Scale Contraction and Graph Structure Learning (2026) is the nearest mechanism: it explicitly jointly optimizes clustering and edge weights via an edge-weight-aware attention network that identifies and weakens noisy connections, which overlaps the candidate's claim that prior work cannot down-weight unreliable edges inside the clustering objective. The candidate's claim stands because the overlap is partial, not exact: (i) that paper operates on a contraction-plus-attention pipeline, not the K-free differentiable-structural-information partitioning-tree functional whose g_alpha/V_alpha terms the candidate re-weights, so the candidate's reliability-weighted DSI_r operator is distinct; (ii) it produces only improved aggregate clustering accuracy with no per-node assignment-support posterior and no Monte-Carlo-over-r calibration measure; (iii) it offers no identifiability theorem characterizing the edge-noise regime where the objective is provably unidentifiable. The candidate's three deliverables (reliability-weighted DSI, per-node support measure, identifiability separation) therefore survive, but the differentiation must name this paper or a reviewer will read the edge-reweighting half as already-published.","addressable_via":"differentiation_from_lit — add an entry contrasting against semanticscholar:c8008f3ec81fcbb4dc24e583c20582a51bb17c3a, stating that it weakens noisy edges via attention on a contraction pipeline for accuracy only, whereas the candidate re-weights the K-free DSI functional with a per-edge reliability latent, emits a per-node support posterior, and proves an identifiability boundary none of which it provides."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat (semanticscholar:c8008f3ec81fcbb4dc24e583c20582a51bb17c3a) and the C10 reject lesson 'claiming a construction a recently published method already subsumes' — the edge-reweighting half of the contribution overlaps a 2026 weighted-graph-clustering paper that jointly optimizes clustering and edge weights, and the current differentiation list does not name it.","fix_direction":"Add a differentiation_from_lit entry for semanticscholar:c8008f3ec81fcbb4dc24e583c20582a51bb17c3a: it weakens noisy edges via an edge-weight-aware attention network inside a graph-contraction pipeline to raise aggregate clustering accuracy, whereas the candidate (i) re-weights the K-free differentiable-structural-information partitioning-tree functional (DSI_r) rather than an attention/contraction pipeline, (ii) emits a per-node assignment-support posterior via Monte-Carlo samples over r, and (iii) proves an edge-noise identifiability boundary — none of which that paper provides. Keep all kill-switch fields (falsification_prediction, compute_budget) byte-identical."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"what_step_was_missed","issue":"C10 borderline (frontier-survey completeness) — the surpass claim should acknowledge the existence of edge-weight-aware clustering so the missed step reads as the identifiability formalization, not the mere idea of down-weighting edges.","fix_direction":"Optionally tighten what_step_was_missed to clarify that prior edge-reweighting work (including the 2026 contraction-attention line) still treats reweighting as an accuracy heuristic and never formalizes the indistinguishability regime or re-derives the DSI functional as an expectation over r; this is a one-clause strengthening, not a structural change."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added a differentiation_from_lit entry for the 2026 weighted-graph-clustering paper (semanticscholar:c8008f3ec81fcbb4dc24e583c20582a51bb17c3a), stating it weakens noisy edges via attention on a contraction pipeline for accuracy only, whereas the candidate re-weights the K-free DSI functional, emits a per-node support posterior, and proves an identifiability boundary."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"what_step_was_missed","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Strengthened what_step_was_missed with a clause clarifying that prior edge-reweighting work (including the contraction-attention line) treats reweighting as an accuracy heuristic and never formalizes the indistinguishability regime or re-derives the DSI functional as an expectation over r."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Edge-Reliability-Weighted Structural Entropy for Calibrated K-Free Deep Graph Clustering\n\n**Method.** Edge-Reliability-Weighted Structural Entropy (ER-SE)\n\n## Motivation\nDeep graph clustering takes a graph — nodes connected by edges, where each node also has feature attributes — and groups the nodes into communities without anyone labeling them first. The newest and cleanest methods in this area (LSEnet, published at ICML 2024, and its follow-up ASIL) drop the awkward requirement of telling the algorithm how many groups to find: they instead minimize a single mathematical score called structural information, computed directly from the edges. The catch is that all of these methods trust the edges completely, as if every connection were a perfect clue about which nodes belong together. Real graphs are not like that — some edges link nodes that are actually in different communities, some true connections are missing, and a few nodes have wildly more edges than others. When the edges lie, the method optimizes toward the wrong answer, and worse, it gives you a single grouping with no way of telling which node placements you can trust and which were forced by misleading edges.\n\nThe time is right to fix this because the structural-information method is brand new and its loss is a clean formula of the edge weights, so we can make one surgical change: instead of trusting each edge, we let the model infer a reliability score for every edge from its own learned representations, and weight the formula by those scores. Recent 2025-2026 work has started admitting that edges are untrustworthy, but only with band-aids — thresholding 'hard' nodes, learning one global structure-versus-attribute trust knob, or using attention to dampen noisy edges — none of which turns edge reliability into a quantity the clustering objective itself reasons about, and none of which reports a per-node confidence.\n\nWhat prior work stopped short of: LSEnet (ICML 2024) built the structural-information clustering machinery but treated the edge weights as fixed and exact, so it cannot express that some edges are unreliable and gives no per-node uncertainty. ASIL (TPAMI 2025) extended it to imbalanced graphs and proved an aggregate improvement but still reports only one summary number, never which specific nodes it placed reliably. GC-TriFA (2025) lets the model trade off structure against attributes but only through a single global knob, not a local per-edge judgment. Hard-boundary-aware clustering (2025) flags boundary nodes with a yes/no threshold rather than a continuous, model-derived reliability that can flow into the objective.\n\nWhen this gap closes, the K-free clustering line gains its first honest per-node confidence signal — you can finally see which nodes are solidly clustered and which were only pushed into place by noisy edges — plus a theorem that turns the methods' known fragility on imbalanced and heterophilous graphs into an explicit, predictable failure boundary.\n\n## Method\n### Background backbone\n*The unchanged K-free structural-entropy clustering scaffold the contribution attaches to.*\n\n1. Build the standard no-K structural-entropy backbone exactly as in existing methods: a 2-layer graph convolutional network (GCN) turns each node's features into a 64-dimensional embedding vector $h_{u},$ and a partitioning-tree decoder (a tree of fixed maximum height 3) outputs, at each level, a soft table saying how strongly each node attaches to each parent, via a softmax over learned scores. The structural-information score of Eq. (1) is then computed from these tables and the edge weights — summing, for every node in the tree, a cut-weight-over-volume term times a log volume ratio. Input: the graph's connection list (adjacency) and node features; output: the level-by-level soft attachment tables, the per-node soft cluster assignment, and the single structural-information number.\n\n*The differentiable structural-information functional of the K-free line: a sum over every non-root partitioning-tree node $\\alpha $ of the cut weight $g_\\alpha $ over total volume, times the log of the node volume $V_\\alpha $ relative to its parent volume $V_\\alpha ^{-}.$ Every $g_\\alpha $ and $V_\\alpha $ is computed from the observed edge weights taken as exact.*\n$$ \\mathcal{H}^{T}(G) = -\\sum_{\\alpha \\neq \\lambda} \\frac{g_{\\alpha}}{\\mathrm{Vol}(G)} \\log \\frac{V_{\\alpha}}{V_{\\alpha^{-}}} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: We want to attach our fix exactly where the problem lives — the score that trusts the raw edges — so we first stand up that score unchanged.\n\n### Edge-reliability inference\n*Infers a per-edge reliability latent and re-weights the clustering objective by it, relaxing the trust-the-edges assumption.*\n\n2. Add a tiny 2-layer neural scorer (called phi, hidden width 64, the only new weights) that reads the two endpoint embeddings and any edge features — or just the number 1 when the graph has no edge features — and outputs a reliability between 0 and 1 for each edge (Eq. 2). Compute this only for edges that actually exist (the method dampens existing edges, it never invents new ones) and make it symmetric by scoring each unordered pair once. Then multiply every edge weight inside the structural-information score by its reliability, so distrusted edges count for less; because lowering an edge's reliability changes the score, it changes which grouping the method prefers.\n\n*The inferred per-edge reliability $r_{uv}$ is a sigmoid of a small MLP $\\phi $ applied to the two endpoint embeddings and the edge features; the reliability-weighted edge weight $\\tilde{w}_{uv}$ scales the observed weight $w_{uv}$ by it.*\n$$ r_{uv} = \\sigma\\!\\left(\\phi([\\mathbf{h}_u; \\mathbf{h}_v; \\mathbf{e}_{uv}])\\right), \\quad \\tilde{w}_{uv} = r_{uv}\\, w_{uv} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Instead of trusting edges blindly, we let the model say how much it believes each edge, and feed that belief directly into the clustering objective.\n3. Train everything together with the Adam optimizer (learning rate 0.001, weight decay 0.0005), using the whole graph at once for up to 400 passes and stopping early when the reliability-weighted score stops improving. Minimize the reliability-weighted score plus the stabilizer over the graph network, the tree decoder, and the reliability scorer phi all at once — the coefficients already inside the stabilizer handle the balancing, so no extra schedule is needed. Because the reliability enters the score smoothly, one optimizer updates all parts each step, so reliability is learned at the same time as the grouping rather than fixed up front.\n   - _Why_: Learning reliability at the same time as the clusters is what makes it a real inferred quantity rather than a one-off preprocessing guess.\n\n### Collapse anchor\n*Keeps the self-taught reliability signal honest by pinning its mean to a prior, preventing the all-unreliable degenerate solution.*\n\n4. Add a stabilizer term (Eq. 3) with two parts: one pulls the average reliability across a batch toward a prior value of 0.7, and one discourages reliabilities from all sitting at a wishy-washy middle by penalizing the per-edge spread $r_{uv}*(1-r_{uv})$ (which is largest at 0.5, so pushing it down sends reliabilities toward 0 or 1). Weight the mean-anchor part strongly (a coefficient of 1.0, the main guard) and the sharpening part lightly (0.1, so it never overrides what the data says). Add this term to the reliability-weighted score before computing gradients; without it the model would cheat by calling every edge unreliable, which makes the score trivially zero and collapses everything into one group.\n\n*The collapse stabilizer: a penalty $\\lambda $ pinning the batch-mean reliability toward a prior reliability $\\rho _{0}$ (default 0.7) plus a sharpness term $\\mu $ discouraging uniformly-middling reliabilities, preventing the degenerate $all-r\\to 0$ solution that would zero the functional.*\n$$ \\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{stab}} = \\lambda\\left(\\frac{1}{|B|}\\sum_{(u,v)\\in B} r_{uv} - \\rho_0\\right)^{2} + \\mu\\, \\mathrm{sharp}(r) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A self-taught reliability signal, left unchecked, takes the lazy way out; the anchor keeps it honest.\n\n### Per-node support readout\n*Turns the spread of the assignment posterior under resampled reliability into a calibrated per-node confidence.*\n\n5. At prediction time, switch on dropout inside the reliability scorer phi only (dropping 20% of its hidden units), and repeat 20 times: each time draw a fresh dropout pattern, recompute every edge's reliability and the reweighted edge weights, and run the grouping decoder forward so the soft assignment reflects that sample. For every node, measure how much its group assignment wobbles across the 20 runs, and report one minus that wobble (Eq. 4) as a per-node support score between 0 and 1; give the final grouping as the most-frequent assignment and attach the support score to each node. If a node's group keeps flipping as we resample which edges to trust, its placement was shaky and its support is low.\n\n*The per-node support measure: one minus the normalized entropy of the node's mean soft cluster assignment averaged over T Monte-Carlo samples of the reliability field; a node whose assignment flips across reliability samples has high entropy and thus low support.*\n$$ s_v = 1 - \\frac{1}{\\log K}\\, \\mathrm{Ent}\\!\\left(\\frac{1}{T}\\sum_{t=1}^{T} \\mathbf{q}_v^{(t)}\\right) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: If a node's group keeps flipping as we resample which edges to trust, its placement was shaky — that wobble is exactly the confidence signal users have been missing.\n\n### Identifiability theory\n*Proves the exact edge-noise regime where the deterministic objective is blind and the reliability-weighted one is not.*\n\n6. Prove on paper exactly when the trust-the-edges score goes blind: define two genuinely different groupings that differ only on some set of nodes, plus a noise model with three knobs — how often wrong (cross-community) edges appear, how often correct edges go missing, and how lopsided the node degrees are — and find the setting where the original score assigns both groupings the same expected value, so it cannot tell them apart, while the reliability-weighted score keeps them apart, at a cost that grows only linearly with the number of edges. Build the full checking harness too: a synthetic graph generator with planted communities, the pair of groupings, and repeated sampling of the noise to estimate the expected scores, then trace the gap for both scores as the noise crosses the predicted boundary. The proof itself is a design decision the authors own. 【author decision: which expectation model and expansion order make the expected-score gap provably vanish for the original score yet stay positive for the reliability-weighted one — a first-order linearization in the noise rates is the natural default, but whether first order is enough or a second-order term is needed for strict separation is for the authors to settle.】\n   - _Why_: A confidence number is only convincing if we can show, with proof, the precise conditions under which the old method is blind and ours is not.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 面向无需预设簇数的深度图聚类的边可靠性加权结构熵：可校准的节点级置信度方法\n\n**方法名称.** Edge-Reliability-Weighted Structural Entropy (ER-SE)\n\n## 研究动机\n深度图聚类要处理的是一张图——节点之间用边相连，每个节点还带有特征属性——目标是在没有任何人工标注的前提下，把节点划分成若干社区。这一领域里最新、也最简洁的方法（发表于 ICML 2024 的 LSEnet 及其后续 ASIL）去掉了一个很别扭的要求：不必事先告诉算法要分成几组；它们改为最小化一个叫做结构信息（structural information）的数学量，而这个量直接由边算出。问题在于，这些方法都完全信任边，仿佛每一条连接都是关于哪些节点该归到一起的完美线索。真实的图并非如此——有些边连接的其实是不同社区的节点，有些真正该有的连接却缺失了，还有少数节点的边数远多于其他节点。一旦边在“撒谎”，方法就会朝错误答案优化；更糟的是，它只给出一个划分结果，却无法告诉你哪些节点的归属是可信的、哪些是被误导性的边硬推过去的。\n\n现在正是解决这个问题的好时机，因为结构信息方法本身很新，其损失是边权重的一个干净公式，所以我们可以做一处“外科手术式”的改动：不再无条件信任每条边，而是让模型从自己学到的表示中为每条边推断一个可靠性分数，并用这些分数去加权该公式。2025-2026 年的近期工作已经开始承认边不可信，但都只是“创可贴”式的补救——给“困难”节点设阈值、学一个全局的“结构对属性”信任旋钮、或者用注意力去削弱噪声边——没有一个把边可靠性变成聚类目标本身会去推理的量，也没有一个给出节点级的置信度。\n\n以往工作止步于何处：LSEnet（ICML 2024）搭起了结构信息聚类的机器，却把边权重当作固定且精确的量，因此无法表达某些边不可靠，也给不出节点级的不确定性。ASIL（TPAMI 2025）把它扩展到不平衡图并证明了一个总体改进，但仍然只报告一个汇总数字，从不指明它究竟可靠地放置了哪些节点。GC-TriFA（2025）让模型在结构与属性之间权衡，但只通过一个全局旋钮，而非逐边的局部判断。困难边界感知的聚类（2025）用是/否阈值来标记边界节点，而不是一个能流入目标函数的、由模型推断的连续可靠性。\n\n当这一缺口被填补，无需预设簇数的聚类路线将首次获得诚实的节点级置信信号——你终于能看清哪些节点被牢固地聚类、哪些只是被噪声边推到了某处——再加上一个定理，把这些方法在不平衡图和异配图上已知的脆弱性，转化为一条明确、可预测的失效边界。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景骨干\n*贡献所附着的、保持不变的无需预设簇数结构熵聚类骨架。*\n\n1. 完全按现有方法搭建标准的无需预设簇数的结构熵骨干：一个两层图卷积网络(Graph Convolutional Network, GCN)把每个节点的特征变成 64 维嵌入向量 $h_{u}$；一个划分树解码器（固定最大高度为 3 的树）在每一层输出一张软表格，通过对学到的分数取 softmax，给出每个节点对每个父节点的依附强度。随后用这些表格与边权重计算式 (1) 的结构信息分数——对树中每个节点求和，项为割边权重除以体积再乘以体积比的对数。输入：图的连接表（邻接关系）与节点特征；输出：逐层的软依附表格、每个节点的软簇分配，以及单一的结构信息数值。\n\n*无需预设簇数方法所用的可微结构信息泛函：对划分树中每个非根节点 $\\alpha $ 求和，项为割边权重 $g_\\alpha $ 除以总体积，再乘以该节点体积 $V_\\alpha $ 相对其父节点体积 $V_\\alpha ^{-}$ 的对数。所有 $g_\\alpha $ 与 $V_\\alpha $ 都由被当作精确值的观测边权重算出。*\n$$ \\mathcal{H}^{T}(G) = -\\sum_{\\alpha \\neq \\lambda} \\frac{g_{\\alpha}}{\\mathrm{Vol}(G)} \\log \\frac{V_{\\alpha}}{V_{\\alpha^{-}}} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 我们要把改动精确地接在问题所在之处——那个无条件信任原始边的分数——所以先原样搭起这个分数。\n\n### 边可靠性推断\n*推断逐边可靠性隐变量并据此对聚类目标加权，放松“信任边”的假设。*\n\n2. 加一个很小的两层神经打分器（记作 phi，隐藏层宽度 64，是唯一新增的权重），它读取两个端点的嵌入以及可选的边特征——当图没有边特征时就用数字 1——并为每条边输出一个介于 0 与 1 之间的可靠性（式 2）。只对真实存在的边计算它（该方法削弱已有的边，绝不凭空新增边），并通过对每个无序点对只打分一次来保证对称。然后把结构信息分数里每条边的权重都乘以其可靠性，使被怀疑的边占的分量更小；由于降低某条边的可靠性会改变分数，它也就改变了方法所偏好的分组。\n\n*推断出的逐边可靠性 $r_{uv}$ 是把端点嵌入与边特征送入小型 MLP $\\phi $ 后取 sigmoid 得到；可靠性加权后的边权重 $\\tilde{w}_{uv}$ 等于用它去缩放观测权重 $w_{uv}$。*\n$$ r_{uv} = \\sigma\\!\\left(\\phi([\\mathbf{h}_u; \\mathbf{h}_v; \\mathbf{e}_{uv}])\\right), \\quad \\tilde{w}_{uv} = r_{uv}\\, w_{uv} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 我们不再盲目信任边，而是让模型说出它对每条边的相信程度，并把这个信念直接喂进聚类目标。\n3. 用 Adam 优化器（学习率 0.001，权重衰减 0.0005）把所有部分一起训练，每次使用整张图，最多训练 400 轮，并在可靠性加权分数不再改善时提前停止。同时最小化可靠性加权分数加稳定项，对象包括图网络、树解码器以及可靠性打分器 phi——平衡由稳定项内部的系数处理，无需额外的调度。由于可靠性以平滑方式进入分数，单个优化器每步更新所有部分，因此可靠性与分组同时被学到，而非事先固定。\n   - _为什么_: 让可靠性与簇同时被学到，才使它成为真正被推断出的量，而不是一次性的预处理猜测。\n\n### 防坍缩锚定\n*通过把均值拉向先验来约束自学的可靠性信号，避免“全部不可靠”的退化解。*\n\n4. 加一个由两部分组成的稳定项（式 3）：一部分把一个批次内的平均可靠性拉向先验值 0.7，另一部分通过惩罚逐边的离散度 $r_{uv}*(1-r_{uv})$（在 0.5 处最大，故压低它会把可靠性推向 0 或 1）来抑制所有可靠性都停在模棱两可的中间。把均值锚定部分的权重设得较大（系数 1.0，作为主要防护），把锐化部分设得较小（0.1，使其绝不压过数据给出的判断）。在计算梯度前把这一项加到可靠性加权分数上；没有它，模型会取巧地把每条边都判为不可靠，使分数平凡地变为零，从而把一切坍缩成单一分组。\n\n*防坍缩稳定项：用系数 $\\lambda $ 把批次内可靠性均值拉向先验可靠度 $\\rho _{0}$（默认 0.7），再加一个系数为 $\\mu $ 的锐度项以抑制全体取中间值，从而避免所有 $r\\to 0$ 这一会让泛函恒为零的退化解。*\n$$ \\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{stab}} = \\lambda\\left(\\frac{1}{|B|}\\sum_{(u,v)\\in B} r_{uv} - \\rho_0\\right)^{2} + \\mu\\, \\mathrm{sharp}(r) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 一个自学得到的可靠性信号若不加约束，就会走捷径；这个锚定项让它保持诚实。\n\n### 节点级支持读出\n*把在重采样可靠性下分配后验的离散程度，转化为可校准的节点级置信度。*\n\n5. 在预测阶段，仅在可靠性打分器 phi 内部开启 dropout（随机丢弃其 20% 的隐藏单元），并重复 20 次：每次抽取新的 dropout 模式，重新计算每条边的可靠性与重加权后的边权重，并让分组解码器前向运行，使软分配反映该次采样。对每个节点，测量其分组归属在这 20 次运行间的抖动程度，并上报 1 减去该抖动（式 4），作为介于 0 与 1 之间的节点级支持度分数；最终分组取出现最多的分配，并把支持度分数附在每个节点上。若在反复重采样“该信任哪些边”时某节点的分组不断跳变，说明其归属本就不稳、支持度低。\n\n*节点级支持度量：取该节点在 T 个可靠性蒙特卡洛采样下的平均软簇分配的归一化熵，再用 1 减去它；若某节点的分配在不同可靠性采样间反复跳变，则熵高、支持度低。*\n$$ s_v = 1 - \\frac{1}{\\log K}\\, \\mathrm{Ent}\\!\\left(\\frac{1}{T}\\sum_{t=1}^{T} \\mathbf{q}_v^{(t)}\\right) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 如果在反复重采样“该信任哪些边”时某节点的分组不断跳变，说明它的归属本就不稳——这个抖动正是用户一直缺少的置信信号。\n\n### 可识别性理论\n*证明确定性目标失明、而可靠性加权目标不失明的精确边噪声区间。*\n\n6. 在纸面上严格证明信任边的分数何时会“失明”：定义两个仅在某节点集合上不同、但确实不同的分组，再加一个带三个旋钮的噪声模型——错误（跨社区）边出现的频率、正确边缺失的频率、以及节点度数的失衡程度——并找出这样一个设定：原始分数对两个分组给出相同的期望值，因而无法区分它们，而可靠性加权分数仍能把它们分开，且代价仅随边数线性增长。同时搭好完整的验证装置：一个带预埋社区的合成图生成器、这对分组，以及对噪声的反复采样以估计期望分数，然后在噪声跨越预测边界时追踪两种分数的差距。证明本身是作者需要承担的设计决定。【作者需决定：采用何种期望模型与展开阶数，才能使原始分数的期望差距可证地消失、而可靠性加权分数的差距可证地为正——在噪声率上做一阶线性化是自然的默认选择，但一阶是否足够、抑或需要二阶项才能得到严格分离，须由作者确定。】\n   - _为什么_: 一个置信度数字只有在我们能用证明给出旧方法何时“看不见”、而我们能看见的精确条件时，才令人信服。\n\n"},{"id":"18","run_dir":"run_prompt18_robustdecision","index":18,"title":"Sensitivity-Allocated Robustness: Spend the Protection Budget Where the Decision Is Fragile","title_zh":"敏感度分配式鲁棒性：把保护预算花在决策最脆弱的状态上","method_name":"Sensitivity-Allocated Robustness (SAR)","hook":"Robust-RL methods buy one global protection budget and pay for it everywhere, so covering the few brittle states makes the policy needlessly conservative in benign regions; we show that holding total protection mass fixed but reallocating it across states by a per-decision sensitivity score strictly lowers worst-case suboptimality. The allocation, not the amount, is the free variable the field has left fixed.","anchor_pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","anchor_pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","domain_category":"Reinforcement Learning","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces, at decision time, a per-state quantity of how much protection a particular decision needs, so none can allocate robustness non-uniformly across the state space; every leaf sizes one global budget and the brittle-state-vs-benign-region trade is forced because the needed local quantity does not exist (additive).","pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by C04's discriminate-then-treat move: we define a measurable per-state decision-sensitivity score, show states fall into a brittle minority and a near-robust bulk, allocate protection proportional to sensitivity under a fixed total mass, and supply a sensitivity/error decomposition bounding the differentiated allocation's worst-case-value recovery against the uniform allocation — that bound, not the partition idea, is the load-bearing artifact.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved paper tests whether the protective uncertainty budget must be specified before deployment at all, rather than determined from the decision context that is present when the action is taken — every leaf silently inherits from the shared robust-formulation ancestor the assumption that the budget/ambiguity radius is an a-priori input (subtractive).","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","how_closed":"Framing move (C11): the protection budget is a budgeted choice mechanism whose load-bearing precondition is that the budget is a single a-priori scalar; we pivot it by reframing budget-sizing into a per-decision allocation problem (selection->control) and re-derive a worst-case performance certificate for the context-conditioned rule that matches or beats the fixed-budget baseline. Companion deliverable (controlled_diagnostic_design): a confound-isolating instrument that fixes the protection mechanism and total protection mass and varies only placement (a-priori-uniform vs sensitivity-allocated), scored by an oracle worst-case return on held-out shifted environments, reporting the apparent-vs-de-confounded gap as the headline.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"robust sequential decision-making / robust reinforcement learning under uncertainty","n_papers":38,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":25},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":16,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Adversarial robust decision-making under uncertainty learning and dynamic ensemble selection"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Sequential decision-making under uncertainty: a robust MDPs review"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A data-driven robust decision-making model for configuring a resilient and responsive relief supply chain under mixed uncertainty"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A two-stage robust decision-making framework (2S-RDM) for flood risk adaptation under deep uncertainty"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Robust Reinforcement Learning for Decision Making Under Uncertainty in Electricity Markets"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Smart TOPSIS: A Neural Network-Driven TOPSIS with Neutrosophic Triplets for Green Supplier Selection in Sustainable Manufacturing"}],"more":10},{"year":2025,"n":22,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Robust Reinforcement Learning for Decision Making Under Uncertainty in Electricity Markets"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Reward-Centered ReST-MCTS: A Robust Decision-Making Framework for Robotic Manipulation in High Uncertainty Environments"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A Robust Decision-Making approach to evaluating state support for nuclear programmes under uncertainty: A UK case study"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Real-Time Decision-Making Under Uncertainty in Digital Twins: Robust Model Predictive Control Using Time-Series Deep Quantile Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Application of Distributionally Robust Optimization Markov Decision-Making Under Uncertainty in Scheduling of Multi-category Emergency Medical Materials"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Determining Robust Optimal Pumping Solutions in a Heterogeneous Coastal Aquifer Using a Robust Decision-Making Approach and Bargaining Theory to Resolve Multiple Sources of Uncertainty"}],"more":16}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":19,"share":0.5},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":7,"share":0.184},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":4,"share":0.105},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":4,"share":0.105},{"pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","count":4,"share":0.105},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":3,"share":0.079},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":3,"share":0.079},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":3,"share":0.079}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Across the robust-decision frontier the protective uncertainty budget is fixed offline and applied uniformly over the state space, so it cannot be matched to where the realized state actually makes the decision fragile. The soft-constrained-adversary robust off-policy RL method of openalex:W4402953501 assumes a known perturbation prior and trains against an adversary whose constraint strength is a single global hyperparameter, never tightened or loosened by the local sensitivity of the action it is protecting; the robust-MDP family surveyed in semanticscholar:83c19c3effe69a1794eb3e85768bce93ead89ef7 inherits the same shape through state-wise-rectangular ambiguity sets whose radius is chosen a priori, and the data-driven DRO scheduling of openalex:W4404905422 picks one interval/ambiguity radius for the whole horizon. The structural consequence is a forced global trade: enlarging the budget to cover the few genuinely brittle states makes the policy needlessly conservative everywhere else (collapsing return in benign regions), while shrinking it to recover benign-region performance re-exposes the brittle states — the current machinery has no quantity that says, at a given state, how much robustness this particular decision needs, so it cannot allocate protection non-uniformly.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4402953501","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Trains a robust off-policy policy against a soft-constrained adversary on state observations, relaxing the hard worst-case L_p ball to a KL-style soft constraint around a known perturbation prior so the policy is less over-conservative over long horizons. Residue: the soft-constraint strength (the adversary's budget) is a fixed global scalar set before training and is identical at every state, so it neither detects nor reallocates protection toward the states where the policy's action is actually most sensitive to perturbation — the conservativeness/fragility trade is made once, globally, not per-decision."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:83c19c3effe69a1794eb3e85768bce93ead89ef7","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Surveys robust MDPs, organizing ambiguity-set design and the state-wise-rectangularity assumption that makes worst-case value iteration tractable. Residue: rectangular ambiguity sets are assigned a radius a priori and treated independently per state with no coupling to realized decision sensitivity, which the survey itself notes yields conservative policies; non-rectangular (sensitivity-coupled) sets are flagged as intractable and left open."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4405835601","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Improves RL robustness by correcting actions using a multi-step maximum-risk estimate computed at deployment. Residue: the risk estimate is a high-variance post-hoc multi-step rollout used only to override actions, not a signal that is learned end-to-end or used to size how much robustness each state's decision should receive; the correction trigger threshold is itself fixed and global."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:4dd978ecb00418fd43ea510c65d9543da4061e22","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"An LLM planning agent that seeks information under partial observability before committing to a decision. Residue: when and what to query is driven by heuristics, not by a quantity tying information value to decision robustness, so it cannot say a given decision is robust enough to act without more information versus fragile enough to require it."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"robust sequential decision-making / robust reinforcement learning under uncertainty","venue":"ICLR/ICML/NeurIPS (ML methods track)","time":"2026","data":["standard continuous-control benchmarks (MuJoCo/DMControl) with observation/transition perturbations","robust-RL / RMDP evaluation suites","an offline RL dataset with held-out shifted-dynamics validation environments"],"compute":"1x A100 x 3 months (approx 90 A100-day)","expertise":"reinforcement learning, robust optimization, deep learning","preference":"both","baseline":"soft-constrained-adversary robust off-policy RL (openalex:W4402953501); fixed-radius robust MDP / DRO policies (semanticscholar:83c19c3effe69a1794eb3e85768bce93ead89ef7)","limitation":"current robust-decision methods fix the uncertainty set / adversary budget offline and apply it uniformly across the state space, decoupled from where the realized state actually makes the decision fragile","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["domain","venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"Shared audit lens: every robust-decision leaf inherits from its formulation ancestor the assumption that the protective uncertainty budget B is an exogenous, a-priori, state-uniform scalar; both legs interrogate exactly that assumption, the anchor by constructing the non-uniform allocation it forbids and the sibling by overturning the a-priori requirement and re-certifying. Define the central object, the per-state decision-sensitivity score s(x) for state x: let Q_pi(x,a) be the policy's worst-case action-value under the current protection set of radius r at x (model-internal readout from the robust critic already trained), let a* = pi(x) be the chosen action, and let g(x) be the worst-case directional degradation of value at the chosen action, g(x) = max over perturbations delta with ||delta|| <= 1 of [ Q_pi(x,a*) - Q_pi^{r=delta-direction}(x,a*) ] estimated by one extra critic forward pass along the adversary's gradient direction (the same gradient the adversary already computes), so s(x) = g(x) / (mean_x g(x) + eps) is a unitless relative sensitivity, eps=1e-6 a fixed stabilizer. The anchor leg (C04) partitions states online by s(x): it sets the local protection radius r(x) = B * s(x) (B is the fixed total-mass budget, the SAME scalar the baseline uses globally; the constraint E_x[r(x)] = B is enforced by the normalization in s), so high-sensitivity states receive a larger adversary/ambiguity radius and the near-redundant bulk receives a smaller one, and the robust policy is trained against this state-dependent adversary instead of a uniform one. The load-bearing artifact is a sensitivity/error decomposition: writing total worst-case suboptimality as a sum over states of (per-state value loss x local budget mismatch), it bounds the differentiated allocation's worst-case regret by the uniform allocation's regret minus a non-negative rearrangement gain that is strictly positive whenever s(x) is non-constant and positively correlated with true per-state value curvature — this is what proves differentiated beats uniform at equal mass, the comparison C04's reject lessons demand. The sibling leg (C11) pivots the a-priori-budget assumption: it shows the assumption is load-bearing (with a fixed global B the rearrangement gain is identically zero, so the brittle-vs-benign trade is forced) and reframes budget-sizing from an offline scalar choice into an online per-decision allocation, re-deriving the robust value certificate for r(x) and proving the gain collapses to zero the moment r(x) is re-flattened to constant B. The companion (controlled_diagnostic_design) ships the empirical separation a method paper needs: construct matched evaluation episodes where total protection mass B is held identical across arms and only the placement rule differs (uniform vs sensitivity-allocated vs an adversarially-mis-allocated control that spends mass on the bulk), scored by an oracle worst-case return computed on held-out shifted-dynamics environments the policy never trained on, and report the worst-case-return gap between arms as the headline rather than an aggregate score.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The anchor (C04) and the deferred estimate->optimization-loop gap share one machinery — the per-state sensitivity score IS both the partition criterion and the signal fed into the state-dependent adversary during training — so I folded them into one module rather than two, which is why the deferred gap was not carried as a separate leg. I kept the audit (C11) as a distinct leg because its deliverable is the certificate that the a-priori budget was never necessary plus the equal-mass reframing, which the construction alone does not state; the two interlock under shared_audit (same inherited assumption, attacked by construction and by audit). Alternatives rejected: (1) making s(x) a global CVaR risk-aversion scalar or a conformal marginal-coverage radius — both are flagged collateral regressions (lineage c0/c1) and would re-flatten the allocation to a constant, killing the rearrangement gain; (2) adding extra total protection mass for brittle states, which would confound 'better placement' with 'more robustness' and is exactly the placement-vs-mass confound the C02 companion exists to rule out.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on MuJoCo continuous-control tasks (e.g., Hopper/Walker2d/HalfCheetah) with bounded observation perturbations and held-out shifted-dynamics test environments, train the uniform-budget robust baseline and the sensitivity-allocated variant at IDENTICAL total protection mass B, then measure oracle worst-case return (minimum return across a sweep of unseen dynamics shifts) and benign-region nominal return. If the candidate works, worst-case return increases (or benign-region nominal return increases at equal worst-case return) for the sensitivity-allocated arm relative to the uniform arm at the same B. The load-bearing variable is the per-state decision-sensitivity score s(x); negative control: replace s(x) with a constant (re-flattening r(x) to the global B) and the sensitivity-allocated arm's worst-case-return advantage over the uniform baseline must collapse to within noise — because if a global constant recovers the same return, the gain came from extra mass or from the retraining, not from non-uniform placement, and the mechanism claim is false. Positive control (constructive identification): an agent that changes ONLY the allocation r(x)=B*s(x) on top of the frozen baseline, with no other modification, should recover most of the worst-case-return improvement, isolating placement as the cause. The mis-allocated control (spending mass on the low-sensitivity bulk) should perform no better than, and likely worse than, the uniform baseline.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4402953501","delta":"They relax the hard worst-case ball to a soft KL constraint of a single global strength applied identically at every state; we hold that total constraint mass fixed and derive a per-state allocation r(x)=B*s(x) plus a rearrangement-gain bound proving the differentiated placement strictly lowers worst-case suboptimality at equal mass — a quantity and a theorem their global-scalar construction does not produce."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:83c19c3effe69a1794eb3e85768bce93ead89ef7","delta":"The survey's robust-MDP family assigns each state-wise-rectangular ambiguity set an a-priori radius decoupled from realized sensitivity and flags sensitivity-coupled sets as intractable; we make the radius a computed function of an online decision-sensitivity readout and certify it without leaving the tractable per-state-independent budget envelope."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4405835601","delta":"They estimate multi-step maximum risk only to override actions post-hoc behind a fixed global trigger threshold; we feed a single-pass decision-sensitivity score back into the adversary radius during training so robustness is allocated and learned end-to-end, not corrected after the fact."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4402953501","what_step_was_missed":"Their soft-constrained adversary already computes a perturbation-gradient direction at every state but consumes it only to bound a single global constraint; the missed step is reading the per-state worst-case value degradation off that same gradient and using it as a normalized allocation weight that redistributes a fixed total budget across states — i.e., constructing the equal-mass rearrangement and the decomposition bound certifying that the redistribution lowers worst-case suboptimality, which their global-strength formulation never derives."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":341,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"Hard floor did not fire (gap_closure_reject_check=borderline not triggered; anti_pattern matched_pattern_id=null; paper_pointed_threat non-subsuming). recipe_application_check=applied for both legs, so no sub_pattern swap. But two load-bearing C11 borderlines hit the central argument: 'A re-derived guarantee whose binding constant is dataset-dependent and cannot be controlled by the practitioner is vacuous' (the certificate must be stated as non-negative + strictly-positive-under-a-checkable-condition, not a fixed factor) and 'Unlocking a new capability by violating an assumption while ignoring a protective property it guarded' (the de-protected benign bulk's worst-case risk must be bounded). Revise tactically to harden the certificate statement and add the de-protected-bulk safeguard; kill-switch fields untouched.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces, at decision time, a per-state quantity of how much protection a particular decision needs, so none can allocate robustness non-uniformly across the state space; every leaf sizes one global budget and the brittle-state-vs-benign-region trade is forced because the needed local quantity does not exist (additive).","main_pattern":"heterogeneous_decomposition","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is treating the partition criterion itself as the contribution while leaving its value unproven, with reviewers mapping the discriminator onto an established technique; compounded by not benchmarking against both the strongest uniform baseline and the obvious cheap alternative, and validating in a regime where the bottleneck does not bite.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Presenting a sensitivity or redundancy proxy as the novelty invites the verdict that it rediscovers known mixed-precision or low-rank results unless it is sharply differentiated from the obvious prior criterion.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The decision-sensitivity score s(x) could be read as a relabeled risk/CVaR or saliency criterion; the candidate differentiates it (equal-mass rearrangement gain, read off the adversary's existing gradient) but the sharp distinction from a global risk-aversion scalar lives mostly in core_mechanism_reasoning rather than as a foregrounded claim."},{"lesson_quoted":"Omitting comparison against both the strongest uniform baseline and the obvious cheap alternative (SVD/PCA, structured dropout, a natively trained smaller model) leaves reviewers unable to tell whether the partition buys anything at all.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate explicitly benchmarks the sensitivity-allocated arm against the strongest uniform-budget baseline at equal mass AND a mis-allocated control, which is exactly the uniform-vs-differentiated comparison this lesson demands."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a storage or throughput claim only on toy-scale models — where the compression bottleneck does not actually bite — undermines the entire motivation no matter how clean the method is.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Validation is on standard MuJoCo continuous-control with held-out shifted-dynamics environments where the conservativeness-vs-fragility trade genuinely bites, not a toy regime."},{"lesson_quoted":"A clever partition with no measured real-world deployment metric (no inference latency or memory speedup) reads as a proxy-only contribution and stalls at borderline.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The deployment metric is the true binding quantity here (oracle worst-case return under unseen dynamics shift), not a proxy."},{"lesson_quoted":"Skipping any analysis of why the heterogeneity exists — the data or value distribution that drives the partition — makes the technical novelty and the potential impact impossible to assess.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Step 1 of the sensitivity/error decomposition characterizes the per-state value-degradation distribution (brittle minority vs near-robust bulk) as load-bearing evidence before partitioning."},{"lesson_quoted":"Bolting together established components (distillation plus pruning plus calibration) without an error bound or artifact specific to the new setting reads as incremental even when the target application is timely and important.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The rearrangement-gain bound is an artifact specific to the equal-mass robust-allocation setting, not a bolt-together of off-the-shelf modules."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved paper tests whether the protective uncertainty budget must be specified before deployment at all, rather than determined from the decision context that is present when the action is taken — every leaf silently inherits from the shared robust-formulation ancestor the assumption that the budget/ambiguity radius is an a-priori input (subtractive).","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The dominant failure is substituting one selection rule for another that performs better empirically while omitting the theorem that explains when and why it wins; secondary failures are pivoting an assumption the community regards as a reasonable modeling choice, and producing a guarantee whose binding constant is dataset-dependent / uncontrollable.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Substituting one selection heuristic for another without a theorem stating when and why it wins reads as an engineering combination, not a contribution, no matter how clean the empirical gain.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate supplies the rearrangement-gain theorem stating exactly when sensitivity-allocation strictly beats uniform (non-constant s positively correlated with value curvature), not just an empirical swap."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pivoting an assumption the community treats as a reasonable modeling choice — rather than first proving it a genuine restriction — leaves both motivation and novelty in doubt.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"A reviewer could call 'fix the budget a priori' a reasonable modeling choice; the candidate argues it is load-bearing (with constant B the rearrangement gain is identically zero, forcing the trade), but this load-bearing demonstration is the linchpin and must read as a proof of restriction, not an assertion."},{"lesson_quoted":"A re-derived guarantee whose binding constant is dataset-dependent and cannot be controlled by the practitioner is vacuous in the worst case and fails to convince.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The rearrangement gain depends on the covariance between s(x) and per-state value curvature, which is environment-dependent; the practitioner controls total mass B but not the gain magnitude, so the certificate must be stated as 'non-negative, strictly positive under a checkable condition' rather than a fixed improvement factor."},{"lesson_quoted":"Building the entire analysis on a regularity condition (such as continuity or a Lipschitz bound) that the selection mechanism provably violates contradicts and undermines the formal claims.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The decomposition expands worst-case suboptimality around r(x)=B and relies on local value curvature; it does not import a regularity condition the state-dependent adversary itself violates."},{"lesson_quoted":"Improving a bound by a marginal factor with no matching lower bound fails to demonstrate that the improvement is significant or near-optimal enough to clear the bar.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The candidate proves differentiated <= uniform minus a gain but does not yet claim a matching lower bound / optimal allocation; without it the strength of the improvement is under-certified."},{"lesson_quoted":"Unlocking a new capability by violating an assumption while ignoring a protective property it guarded — detectability, validity, identifiability — invites rejection on the overlooked side effect rather than the headline result.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"Relaxing protection in the benign bulk could break a worst-case guarantee the uniform budget protected at those states; the candidate must confirm the equal-mass reallocation does not silently raise worst-case risk in the de-protected bulk beyond tolerance."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No Reject lesson is a hard 'yes' match, so the hard floor does not fire. The C11 audit leg drove the aggregate via two load-bearing borderlines: 'A re-derived guarantee whose binding constant is dataset-dependent ... is vacuous' and 'Unlocking a new capability by violating an assumption while ignoring a protective property it guarded' — the certificate's strength and the de-protected-bulk side effect both touch the central argument."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces, at decision time, a per-state quantity of how much protection a particular decision needs, so none can allocate robustness non-uniformly across the state space; every leaf sizes one global budget and the brittle-state-vs-benign-region trade is forced because the needed local quantity does not exist (additive).","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Discriminate components by a magnitude-/sensitivity-/influence-based criterion into a high-impact minority and a near-redundant bulk, protect/retain the minority while aggressively compressing the bulk, and supply an error/sensitivity decomposition that bounds how the differentiated treatment recovers the original objective — that analysis, not the partition idea, is the load-bearing artifact.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism performs exactly this: it discriminates states by the sensitivity score s(x) into a brittle minority and a near-robust bulk, protects the minority with a larger radius while relaxing the bulk under fixed total mass, and the load-bearing artifact is the rearrangement-gain decomposition (step 5) bounding the differentiated allocation's worst-case regret against uniform — the cluster's signature 'decomposition-is-the-spine' move is present, not just the partition idea.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved paper tests whether the protective uncertainty budget must be specified before deployment at all, rather than determined from the decision context that is present when the action is taken — every leaf silently inherits from the shared robust-formulation ancestor the assumption that the budget/ambiguity radius is an a-priori input (subtractive).","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Center on a selection/acquisition/budget rule, pivot the single load-bearing assumption baked into its criterion or required structure either by relaxing the structural crutch or by reframing the selection task into a different more tractable problem class, and re-derive the performance certificate for the pivoted rule shown to match or beat the pre-pivot baseline.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism pivots the a-priori-fixed-budget assumption baked into the protection-budget rule, reframes budget-sizing from an offline scalar choice into an online per-decision allocation (selection->control), and re-derives the robust value certificate for r(x) shown to beat the fixed-B baseline with the gain collapsing to zero when r(x) is re-flattened — this is C11's pivot-then-rebuild-the-certificate signature, with the companion C02 supplying the empirical separation.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries instantiate their cluster's distinctive move: C04's error/sensitivity-decomposition-as-spine is present (rearrangement-gain bound, not just a partition), and C11's reframe-then-re-certify is present (a-priori budget -> online allocation with a re-derived certificate that vanishes on revert)."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["heterogeneous_decomposition","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"The gap_closure[].main_pattern set is {heterogeneous_decomposition, assumption_audit_and_pivot}; none of the three reject-favored compositions (decomp+self_supervised, decomp+structural_prior, operator_substitution+decomp) is a subset, and the companion controlled_diagnostic_design is realized at the companion level, not a gap_closure main_pattern, so no anti-pattern matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:0bfa699d128cfd7def5181c304237be1c72a95f7","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"Distributionally Robust Agentic RL for Web Decision-Making under Multi-Cost Budgets is the nearest hit because it combines distributional robustness with budgets in a decision-making setting. It does not subsume the candidate: its 'budgets' are task resource/cost constraints consumed by an agent, not a protection/ambiguity radius redistributed across states, and it sizes robustness with a single distributional-ambiguity set rather than allocating a fixed protection mass non-uniformly by a per-state decision-sensitivity readout — so it neither produces s(x) nor proves an equal-mass rearrangement gain. The candidate's claim (differentiated placement strictly lowers worst-case suboptimality at equal total mass) stands independent of this paper.","addressable_via":"Already non-overlapping; if a reviewer conflates the two, differentiation_from_lit can add one line distinguishing protection-mass reallocation from agentic cost budgets."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","issue":"C11 Reject lesson 'a re-derived guarantee whose binding constant is dataset-dependent ... is vacuous' (borderline, load-bearing) — the rearrangement gain depends on an environment-dependent covariance the practitioner cannot set.","fix_direction":"State the certificate explicitly as: differentiated worst-case regret <= uniform worst-case regret with equality iff s(x) is constant, and a STRICTLY positive practitioner-checkable improvement condition (s(x) non-constant AND positively correlated with measured per-state value curvature) — frame the gain as a non-negative guarantee plus a falsifiable sufficient condition rather than a fixed improvement factor, and note that the worst case (constant s) recovers exactly the uniform baseline so the method never underperforms it."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","issue":"C11 Reject lesson 'unlocking a new capability by violating an assumption while ignoring a protective property it guarded' (borderline, load-bearing) — relaxing protection in the benign bulk could raise worst-case risk there.","fix_direction":"Add a guarded-floor clause: enforce a per-state minimum radius r(x) >= r_min so the bulk is never de-protected below a safety floor while the surplus mass (B - r_min) is what gets sensitivity-allocated; state that the diagnostic's mis-allocated control plus a per-state worst-case-risk check confirm the reallocation does not raise worst-case risk in the de-protected bulk beyond r_min's tolerance."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat borderline conflation with agentic multi-cost-budget robust RL.","fix_direction":"Add one differentiation_from_lit entry for semanticscholar:0bfa699d128cfd7def5181c304237be1c72a95f7 distinguishing redistribution of a fixed protection/ambiguity mass across states (our s(x)-weighted radius) from agentic task resource/cost budgets, which are consumed quantities not protection radii."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Restated the certificate as differentiated worst-case regret <= uniform regret with equality iff s(x) constant, plus a practitioner-checkable strictly-positive condition (s non-constant and positively correlated with measured value curvature), so the worst case recovers the uniform baseline exactly rather than resting on a dataset-dependent factor."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added a guarded-floor clause r(x) >= r_min so the benign bulk is never de-protected below a safety floor, with only the surplus mass (B - r_min) sensitivity-allocated, and a per-state worst-case-risk check that the reallocation does not raise worst-case risk in the de-protected bulk."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added an entry distinguishing redistribution of a fixed protection/ambiguity mass across states from agentic multi-cost task budgets (consumed resources, not protection radii)."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Sensitivity-Allocated Robustness: Spend the Protection Budget Where the Decision Is Fragile\n\n**Method.** Sensitivity-Allocated Robustness (SAR)\n\n## Motivation\nMethods for making decisions safe under uncertainty — Robust Reinforcement Learning (Robust RL) and Robust Markov Decision Processes (Robust MDPs) — protect a policy by imagining a worst case and training against it. How much worst case to imagine is set by a 'protection budget': how big an adversary or uncertainty region to defend against. Today that budget is a single number, chosen before deployment and applied identically at every situation the agent faces.\n\nThe problem is that situations are not equally fragile. A few states are genuinely brittle — a small disturbance there flips the right action — while most states are forgiving. With one global budget you are forced into a bad trade: set it high enough to cover the brittle states and the policy becomes overly cautious everywhere, throwing away performance in the easy regions; set it low to recover that performance and the brittle states are left exposed. The recent soft-constrained-adversary method (openalex:W4402953501) loosens the worst case to reduce over-caution, but its strength is still one global number. The robust-MDP survey (semanticscholar:83c19c3effe69a1794eb3e85768bce93ead89ef7) confirms the whole family fixes each state's protection radius ahead of time, and notes that tying that radius to how sensitive a decision actually is was thought to be intractable. A risk-correction method (openalex:W4405835601) does measure per-state risk, but only to veto actions after the fact, never to decide how much protection to train with.\n\nThis is solvable now because the adversary in the soft-constrained method already computes, at every state, the exact gradient that tells you how much that decision would degrade under attack — and then throws it away. We reuse that signal. We compute a per-state sensitivity score, then spend the SAME total protection budget unevenly: more on the brittle states, less (but never below a safety floor) on the forgiving ones. Because the total is unchanged, any gain cannot be attributed to 'more robustness' — only to better placement. We prove the redistributed policy's worst-case shortfall is never worse than the uniform one, and is strictly better whenever sensitivity varies across states and lines up with where value is curved most.\n\nWhen this gap closes, robust policies stop paying for protection where it is not needed: you can be less conservative in easy regions without re-exposing the brittle ones, at the same budget the field already pays. It also turns the 'intractable' sensitivity-coupled setting flagged by the survey into a simple reallocation that stays inside the tractable per-state-independent envelope.\n\n## Method\n### Background: uniform-budget robust baseline\n*Reproduce the strongest equal-mass uniform-budget robust policy as the reference arm.*\n\n1. Train the standard uniform-budget robust baseline — the soft-constrained-adversary robust off-policy reinforcement learning method (openalex:W4402953501) — on a continuous-control task with bounded observation perturbations, using one global protection budget B. Concretely: take an off-policy actor-critic agent (Soft Actor-Critic, SAC, or Twin-Delayed DDPG, TD3) with two critics; the adversary nudges the observation within a small L2 ball, kept near a known noise prior by a soft penalty whose single strength knob is B (the size of the allowed nudge). The adversary is found by a few gradient-ascent steps inside each critic update. Fix B so this baseline matches the published robust-performance point.\n   - _Why_: You need the strongest equal-budget reference to later prove that any gain came from placement, not from spending more.\n\n### Per-state sensitivity readout\n*Read a per-decision sensitivity score off the adversary's existing gradient at no new network cost.*\n\n2. At each state x, reuse the gradient the adversary already computes, take its unit direction, and do exactly one extra critic forward pass at the slightly-nudged observation to read how much the chosen action's worst-case value drops there — call this the raw degradation. Divide it by a running average of that degradation across the recent batch (with a tiny constant added so you never divide by zero), and cap the result at a moderate ceiling so a few extreme states do not dominate; this gives a unitless sensitivity score for the state. No new network is needed.\n\n*g(x) is the worst-case directional value degradation at the chosen action a* $= \\pi (x),$ read along the adversary's existing gradient direction; s(x) normalizes it to a unitless relative sensitivity with stabilizer $\\epsilon  =$ 1e-6.*\n$$ g(x) = \\max_{\\lVert \\delta \\rVert \\leq 1} \\big[\\, Q_\\pi(x, a^\\ast) - Q_\\pi^{r=\\delta}(x, a^\\ast) \\,\\big], \\qquad s(x) = \\frac{g(x)}{\\mathbb{E}_x[g(x)] + \\varepsilon} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The signal saying how fragile this decision is was already being computed and discarded — reusing it costs almost nothing.\n\n### Guarded-floor reallocation and retraining\n*Redistribute a fixed total protection mass by sensitivity, never below a safety floor, and retrain against the state-dependent adversary.*\n\n3. Turn the sensitivity scores into per-state protection radii so that (i) the average radius across the batch still equals the global budget B, and (ii) no state ever drops below a floor $r_{min}$ (default a quarter of B). Do this by giving each state the floor plus a share of the leftover budget proportional to its sensitivity score, rescaled across the batch so the average lands exactly on B. The average is taken over the states the agent actually visits, approximated by the training minibatch.\n\n*The guarded-floor allocation sets each state's protection radius to a fixed floor $r_{min}$ plus a sensitivity-weighted share of the surplus mass; batch normalization of s keeps the expected radius equal to the baseline's global budget B.*\n$$ r(x) = r_{\\min} + (B - r_{\\min})\\, s(x), \\qquad \\mathbb{E}_x[r(x)] = B, \\qquad r(x) \\geq r_{\\min} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This redistributes the same total budget — more to brittle states, less to forgiving ones — while a floor guarantees the easy regions are never left unprotected.\n4. Continue training the same agent, but now let the adversary's strength at each state be that state's allocated radius r(x) instead of the one global value — for the hard version, clip the perturbation to the ball of size r(x); for the soft version, scale the penalty so the effective allowed nudge at that state is r(x). Keep everything else about the trainer identical and run for the same number of environment steps as the baseline so the comparison is fair. The policy ends up cautious exactly where decisions are fragile and relaxed where they are not.\n   - _Why_: Feeding sensitivity back into training (not just into a post-hoc veto) makes the policy careful exactly where decisions are fragile and relaxed where they are not.\n\n### Rearrangement-gain certificate\n*Prove differentiated worst-case regret never exceeds uniform, strictly beating it under a checkable condition.*\n\n5. Prove the central guarantee. First define, at each state, the worst-case value gap as a function of the protection radius — how far below the best value the worst case drops when the adversary is allowed a radius r. Use the rate at which that gap changes as you wiggle the radius around B (its curvature, measured by tiny finite-difference probes). Expand the total worst-case shortfall around the uniform setting and show the redistributed allocation's shortfall is at most the uniform one minus a non-negative term equal to the alignment (covariance) between sensitivity and that curvature: zero when sensitivity is flat, strictly positive when sensitivity varies and lines up with where the worst-case gap is most curved. 【author decision: whether to also prove a matching lower bound showing this gain is near the best achievable, versus shipping only the 'never worse than uniform' upper bound — the choice of what optimality to target is the authors'.】 The smoothness this needs is that the worst-case value bends smoothly in the radius near B, which the method does not violate.\n\n*The rearrangement-gain decomposition: differentiated worst-case regret is at most uniform regret minus a non-negative gain $\\Gamma $ proportional to the covariance between s(x) and per-state value curvature $\\kappa (x)$; $\\Gamma  = 0$ iff s is constant, and $\\Gamma  > 0$ when s is non-constant and positively correlated with $\\kappa .$*\n$$ \\mathrm{Reg}_{\\mathrm{diff}} \\;\\leq\\; \\mathrm{Reg}_{\\mathrm{unif}} - \\Gamma, \\qquad \\Gamma \\;\\propto\\; \\mathrm{Cov}_x\\big(s(x),\\, \\kappa(x)\\big) \\;\\geq\\; 0 \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This turns the claim into a guarantee that the method never hurts you, with a checkable condition for when it strictly helps — not a fragile, data-dependent improvement number.\n\n### Placement-isolating diagnostic\n*Hold mass fixed, vary only placement, and measure the worst-case-return gap plus the de-protected-bulk risk on held-out shifted dynamics.*\n\n6. Set up three versions of the agent at the SAME total budget B: the uniform one, the sensitivity-allocated one, and a deliberately bad one that flips the allocation to spend the budget on the most forgiving states (still averaging to B and respecting the floor). Build a set of test environments the agent never saw by sweeping dynamics it was not trained on — for example, in MuJoCo, scaling body masses, friction, and actuator gains over ranges held out from training. Run all three agents, unchanged, on exactly the same sweep.\n   - _Why_: Holding the budget fixed and changing only placement isolates whether placement itself is what buys the improvement.\n7. Score each agent by its worst-case return: roll out episodes across the whole sweep of unseen dynamics shifts and take the worst (lowest) average return over that sweep — computed directly from real returns, not from the agent's own value estimate, so it cannot fool itself. Separately, check the forgiving states (those with below-median sensitivity) to confirm that relaxing their protection did not raise their worst-case value drop beyond what the uniform agent already had, within the floor's tolerance. Report three headline numbers — the worst-case-return gap (allocated minus uniform), the easy-region return gap on undisturbed episodes, and the forgiving-state risk comparison — rather than one blended score. Re-running with a flat sensitivity score (negative control) and an allocation-only agent (positive control) pins any gain to placement.\n   - _Why_: Worst-case return under unseen shift is the real thing we care about, not a proxy; the bulk-risk check confirms relaxing protection there did not quietly break safety.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 敏感度分配式鲁棒性：把保护预算花在决策最脆弱的状态上\n\n**方法名称.** Sensitivity-Allocated Robustness (SAR)\n\n## 研究动机\n在不确定环境下做安全决策的方法——Robust Reinforcement Learning（鲁棒强化学习，Robust RL）与 Robust MDPs（鲁棒马尔可夫决策过程）——通过设想一个最坏情况并对其训练来保护策略。设想多大的最坏情况由一个“保护预算”决定：要防御多大的对手或多大的不确定性范围。如今这个预算是一个单一数值，在部署前选定，并在智能体面对的每个状态上一视同仁地施加。\n\n问题在于，各个状态的脆弱程度并不相同。少数状态是真正脆弱的——那里一点点扰动就会改变正确动作——而大多数状态是宽容的。用一个全局预算就被迫陷入一个糟糕的权衡：调高到足以覆盖脆弱状态，策略在所有地方都过度保守，白白损失了简单区域的性能；调低以挽回性能，脆弱状态又暴露无遗。最近的 soft-constrained-adversary 方法（openalex:W4402953501）放松了最坏情况以减少过度保守，但其强度仍是一个全局数值。鲁棒 MDP 综述（semanticscholar:83c19c3effe69a1794eb3e85768bce93ead89ef7）证实整个家族都把每个状态的保护半径事先固定，并指出把该半径与决策实际敏感度耦合一度被认为不可解。一个风险纠正方法（openalex:W4405835601）确实测量了逐状态风险，但只用于事后否决动作，从不用来决定训练时该用多少保护。\n\n现在之所以可解，是因为 soft-constrained 方法中的对手在每个状态上其实已经算出了那个梯度——它告诉你该决策在攻击下会退化多少——然后却把它丢弃了。我们重用这一信号：计算一个逐状态的敏感度分数，然后把同样的总保护预算不均匀地花出去：脆弱状态多花一些，宽容状态少花一些（但绝不低于一条安全下限 $r_{min}$）。由于总量不变，任何收益都不能归因于“更多鲁棒性”，只能归因于更好的分配。我们证明重分配后策略的最坏情况差距绝不会比均匀分配更差，并且只要敏感度在状态间有差异且与价值曲率最大处对齐，就严格更优。\n\n这个缺口一旦填上，鲁棒策略就不再在不需要的地方为保护买单：在同样的预算下，你可以在简单区域更不保守，同时不重新暴露脆弱状态。它还把综述标为“不可解”的敏感度耦合设定，变成一个停留在可解的逐状态独立预算范围内的简单重分配。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景：均匀预算鲁棒基线\n*复现最强的等预算均匀鲁棒策略作为参照分支。*\n\n1. 训练标准的均匀预算鲁棒基线——soft-constrained-adversary 鲁棒 off-policy 强化学习(Reinforcement Learning, RL)方法(openalex:W4402953501)——在带有界观测扰动的连续控制任务上，使用一个全局保护预算 B。具体地：取一个 off-policy actor-critic 智能体(Soft Actor-Critic, SAC，或 Twin-Delayed DDPG, TD3)，含两个 critic；对手在一个小的 L2 球内推移观测，并由一个软惩罚把它约束在已知噪声先验附近，其唯一强度旋钮就是 B(允许推移的大小)。对手通过每次 critic 更新内的若干步梯度上升求得。固定 B 使该基线复现已发表的鲁棒性能点。\n   - _为什么_: 你需要一个最强的等预算参照，以便日后证明任何收益来自分配，而非来自花得更多。\n\n### 逐状态敏感度读取\n*零额外网络成本地从对手已有梯度读出逐决策敏感度分数。*\n\n2. 在每个状态 x，复用对手已经算出的梯度，取其单位方向，并在被轻微推移的观测处恰好多做一次 critic 前向，读出所选动作在该处的最坏情况价值跌落多少——称为原始跌落量。把它除以最近 batch 上该跌落量的滑动平均(再加一个很小的常数以避免除零)，并把结果限制在一个适中的上限以免少数极端状态主导；这就得到该状态无量纲的敏感度分数。无需新增网络。\n\n*g(x) 是在所选动作 a* $= \\pi (x)$ 处沿对手已有梯度方向得到的最坏情况价值跌落；s(x) 把它归一化为无量纲的相对敏感度，$\\epsilon  =$ 1e-6 为固定稳定项。*\n$$ g(x) = \\max_{\\lVert \\delta \\rVert \\leq 1} \\big[\\, Q_\\pi(x, a^\\ast) - Q_\\pi^{r=\\delta}(x, a^\\ast) \\,\\big], \\qquad s(x) = \\frac{g(x)}{\\mathbb{E}_x[g(x)] + \\varepsilon} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: “这个决策有多脆弱”的信号本来就在被计算然后丢弃——重用它几乎零成本。\n\n### 带下限的重分配与重训练\n*按敏感度重分配固定总保护质量、绝不低于安全下限，并针对逐状态对手重训练。*\n\n3. 把敏感度分数转成逐状态保护半径，使得(i)整个 batch 的平均半径仍等于全局预算 B，(ii)任何状态都不会低于下限 $r_{min}($默认为 B 的四分之一)。做法是：给每个状态分配下限，加上按其敏感度分数成比例的剩余预算份额，并在 batch 上重新缩放，使平均恰好落在 B 上。该平均是在智能体实际访问的状态上取的，用训练 minibatch 近似。\n\n*带保护下限的分配规则把每个状态的保护半径设为固定下限 $r_{min}$ 加上按敏感度加权的剩余预算份额；对 s 做 batch 归一化使期望半径恰好等于基线的全局预算 B。*\n$$ r(x) = r_{\\min} + (B - r_{\\min})\\, s(x), \\qquad \\mathbb{E}_x[r(x)] = B, \\qquad r(x) \\geq r_{\\min} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这把同一总预算重新分配——脆弱状态多给、宽容状态少给——同时下限保证简单区域永不失去保护。\n4. 继续训练同一个智能体，但现在让对手在每个状态的强度等于该状态分配到的半径 r(x)，而非那个全局值——硬版本把扰动裁剪到大小为 r(x) 的球内；软版本则缩放惩罚使该状态有效允许的推移为 r(x)。训练器其余一切保持不变，并运行与基线相同的环境步数以保证比较公平。最终策略恰好在决策脆弱处谨慎、在不脆弱处放松。\n   - _为什么_: 把敏感度反馈进训练（而不只是事后否决），让策略恰好在决策脆弱处谨慎、在不脆弱处放松。\n\n### 重排增益证书\n*证明差异化最坏情况遗憾绝不超过均匀分配，并在可检验条件下严格更优。*\n\n5. 证明核心保证。先在每个状态把最坏情况价值差距定义为保护半径的函数——当对手被允许半径 r 时，最坏情况比最优价值低多少。再用该差距随半径在 B 附近变动的变化率(其曲率，用极小的有限差分探针测量)。把总的最坏情况亏损在均匀设定附近展开，证明重分配后的亏损至多等于均匀亏损减去一个非负项，该项等于敏感度与该曲率的对齐程度(协方差)：敏感度恒定时为零，敏感度有差异且与最坏情况差距曲率最大处对齐时严格为正。【author decision: 是否还要证明一个匹配的下界，说明此增益接近可达到的最优，而非只交付“绝不差于均匀”的上界——以什么最优性为目标由作者决定。】所需的光滑性是最坏情况价值在 B 附近随半径平滑弯曲，方法本身并不违反这一点。\n\n*重排增益分解：差异化的最坏情况遗憾至多等于均匀遗憾减去一个非负增益 $\\Gamma $，$\\Gamma $ 正比于 s(x) 与逐状态价值曲率 $\\kappa (x)$ 的协方差；当 s 为常数时 $\\Gamma  = 0$，当 s 非常数且与 $\\kappa $ 正相关时 $\\Gamma  > 0$。*\n$$ \\mathrm{Reg}_{\\mathrm{diff}} \\;\\leq\\; \\mathrm{Reg}_{\\mathrm{unif}} - \\Gamma, \\qquad \\Gamma \\;\\propto\\; \\mathrm{Cov}_x\\big(s(x),\\, \\kappa(x)\\big) \\;\\geq\\; 0 \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这把主张变成“方法绝不会害你”的保证，并给出何时严格有益的可检验条件——而不是脆弱的、依赖数据的改进数字。\n\n### 分配隔离诊断\n*固定总质量、只变分配，在留出偏移动力学上测量最坏情况回报差距与被减保护大多数状态的风险。*\n\n6. 在相同总预算 B 下设置三个版本的智能体：均匀版、敏感度分配版，以及一个故意做反的版本——把分配翻转，将预算花在最宽容的状态上(仍平均为 B 且满足下限)。构造一组智能体从未见过的测试环境，方法是扫过训练时未用过的动力学——例如在 MuJoCo 中，把身体质量、摩擦、执行器增益缩放到训练留出的范围。让三个智能体原样在完全相同的扫描上运行。\n   - _为什么_: 固定预算、只改变分配，可隔离出改进究竟是否来自分配本身。\n7. 用最坏情况回报给每个智能体打分：在全部未见动力学偏移的扫描上 roll out 多个回合，取该扫描上最差(最低)的平均回报——直接由真实回报算出，而非智能体自己的价值估计，因此无法自欺。另外，检查宽容状态(敏感度低于中位数的那些)，确认放松其保护没有让其最坏情况价值跌落超过均匀智能体原本的水平，且在下限容差之内。报告三个头条数字——最坏情况回报差距(分配版减均匀版)、无扰动回合上的简单区域回报差距、以及宽容状态的风险对比——而非一个混合分数。用平坦的敏感度分数(负对照)和仅改分配的智能体(正对照)重跑，把任何收益钉在分配这一因素上。\n   - _为什么_: 未见偏移下的最坏情况回报才是我们真正关心的，而非代理指标；大多数状态的风险检查确认那里放松保护没有悄悄破坏安全。\n\n"},{"id":"19","run_dir":"run_prompt19_mentalhealth","index":19,"title":"Is the Score the Construct? A Reliability-First Instrument for Mental-Health QA Evaluation","title_zh":"评分就是构念本身吗？一种面向心理健康问答评测的可靠性优先测量工具","method_name":"Reliability-First Validity Instrument (RFVI)","hook":"Every mental-health-QA evaluation reports one elicited quality/safety rating per answer as if that number IS the construct value, yet none reports whether the same clinical question rephrased neutrally, relabeled across patient demographics, or scored by a swapped rater reproduces that rating. We treat the scoring apparatus itself as the variable under test and show that a large fraction of CounselBench-style aggregate quality variance is unreliable elicitation noise, not model behavior — and that once split into four separately-reliable constructs, failures localize to a single construct that a controllable input variable causally drives.","anchor_pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","anchor_pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","domain_category":"LLM Evaluation & Benchmarking","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether a single per-response human/automatic score is even a stable measurement of the construct it claims to measure — i.e. whether the score reproduces under semantically-equivalent rephrasings, demographic relabelings, or rater swaps of the same clinical question; the shared assumption inherited across the evaluation leaves (openalex:W4414801979, openalex:W4413005885, openalex:W4414766972) is that one elicited rating IS the construct value, and no leaf questions wheth","pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by treating the scoring apparatus as an active independent variable: for each construct we build matched same-question instance families that hold the clinical content fixed and vary only one label-preserving surface axis (paraphrase, demographic relabel, rater identity), then report the divergence between the original rating and its perturbed re-elicitations as a per-construct metamorphic reliability coefficient rho_c — the headline finding is the measured unreliability gap, exactly the C02 move of reporting apparent-vs-de-confounded measurement.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a mental-health-QA evaluation whose output decomposes a single response into separately-reliable validity constructs (factual correctness, clinical-safety, empathic appropriateness, expressed-certainty calibration) such that a deployer can read which construct failed rather than only that an aggregate score dropped (CounselBench, openalex:W4414801979, and the quality audits report only fused aggregates; openalex:W4405768404).","pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by per-cue construct isolation: each of the four constructs is measured by a probe family that suppresses or holds fixed the cues the other three depend on (e.g. for clinical-safety, vary only the presence of a contraindicated recommendation while holding factual content and tone fixed), so the measured difference is attributable to one construct alone rather than to the fused aggregate — the C02 per-cue-suppression construction.","is_anchor":false},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf attributes a mental-health-QA evaluation outcome to a controllable, measurable model-internal or input-side variable whose targeted perturbation predicts the direction of the score change — evaluations catalog failures (openalex:W4414801979) or argue responses-are-not-behavior (openalex:W4414457959) without an instrument that turns a failure into a causal, reproducible attribution.","pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by making the same matched-instance design causal: because each construct's probe family varies exactly one controllable input axis (question severity, self-harm-risk presence, demographic framing) while holding the others fixed, a directed change in that axis that moves the construct score — with a confound-matched control that does not — converts a catalogued failure into a reproducible causal attribution to a named variable, the C02 'vary the hypothesized driver directly' step.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"LLM evaluation for mental-health question answering (open-ended clinical QA validity/diagnosis)","n_papers":38,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":25},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":13,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Classifying Unstructured Text in Electronic Health Records for Mental Health Prediction Models: Large Language Model Evaluation Study"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"CBT-LLM: A Chinese Large Language Model for Cognitive Behavioral Therapy-based Mental Health Question Answering"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Can AI Relate: Testing Large Language Model Response for Mental Health Support"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Large Language Model–Powered Diagnostic Co-Pilot (“CapyEngine”) for Mental Disorders: Development, Evaluation, and Future Optimization Study"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Classifying the Information Needs of Survivors of Domestic Violence in Online Health Communities Using Large Language Models: Prediction Model Development and Evaluation Study"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Exploring Large-Scale Language Models to Evaluate EEG-Based Multimodal Data for Mental Health"}],"more":7},{"year":2025,"n":25,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Comparing traditional natural language processing and large language models for mental health status classification: a multi-model evaluation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Large Language Model–Based Chatbots and Agentic AI for Mental Health Counseling: Systematic Review of Methodologies, Evaluation Frameworks, and Ethical Safeguards"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Large language model powered knowledge graph construction for mental health exploration"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Bridging Gender Disparities in Mental Health: A Bilingual Large Language Model for Multilingual Therapeutic Chatbots"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A scoping review of large language models for generative tasks in mental health care"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Charting the evolution of artificial intelligence mental health chatbots from rule‐based systems to large language models: a systematic review"}],"more":19}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":26,"share":0.684},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":8,"share":0.211},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":7,"share":0.184},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":4,"share":0.105},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":2,"share":0.053},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":2,"share":0.053},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":2,"share":0.053},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":1,"share":0.026}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Mental-health QA evaluation has converged on a single move: collect expert-rated quality/safety scores or adversarially elicited failure cases on open-ended patient questions and report them as an aggregate per-response number (CounselBench builds a 100-clinician expert benchmark and finds 'consistent, model-specific failure patterns' but reports them as annotated failure rates, openalex:W4414801979; the chatbot scoping reviews and quality audits do the same, openalex:W4405768404, semanticscholar:18e48fbed866619efdfaa0fcd2468259feeb85f9). This produces a number that tells a deployer THAT a model scored low without telling them WHICH validity construct failed or WHY: the aggregate fuses factual correctness, clinical-safety, empathic appropriateness, and the model's own expressed certainty into one rating, and a position piece explicitly argues that single-response scoring is the wrong unit because 'responses are not behavior' yet supplies no operational instrument (openalex:W4414457959), while a safety-evaluation critique argues a one-size-fits-all score is actively misleading across contexts (openalex:W7080350807). Concretely, when a model's CounselBench rating drops on a depression-with-suicidality vignette, the current machinery cannot decide whether the drop is a factual error, an unsafe recommendation, a tone failure, or a confidently-asserted wrong answer, and it cannot tie the drop to any controllable input (question framing, demographic phrasing, severity) whose perturbation would move the score back — so the score is neither decomposable into constructs nor causally attributable, and two models with identical aggregate ratings can be failing for opposite, undiagnosable reasons.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4414801979","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"CounselBench (ICLR 2026) builds a large expert-annotated mental-health QA benchmark with a clinician panel plus an adversarial stress-test, and surfaces 'consistent, model-specific failure patterns' on open-ended patient questions. Its residue: failures are recorded as human-annotated quality/safety scores and qualitative failure categories, not decomposed into separable validity constructs nor attributed to any controllable model-internal variable whose intervention would predict the score change, so the benchmark diagnoses THAT a model fails without isolating WHICH construct moved or WHY."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4414457959","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"This JAMA Network Open piece argues evaluation must shift 'from responses to behavior' — i.e. that scoring single responses misrepresents how a clinical LLM actually behaves. Its residue: it makes the conceptual case that a single-response score is the wrong unit but provides no operational instrument that turns 'behavior' into a measurable, reliability-bearing quantity, leaving the construct-versus-aggregate problem unsolved."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7080350807","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Argues that a one-size-fits-all safety-assurance score for LLMs is 'considered harmful' because risk is context-dependent. Its residue: it diagnoses that a uniform aggregate is misleading across contexts but proposes no replacement measurement primitive that is itself construct-separated or context-conditioned with reported reliability."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4408498299","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Applies validated human psychometric instruments (OEJTS, Big Five) to LLMs and shows models differ in measured 'personality' via MANOVA. Its residue: it treats validated scales as descriptive labels applied once, with no test of whether the measured construct is stable under semantically-neutral input perturbation or whether it predicts mental-health answer quality — psychometric validity (reliability + construct separation) is borrowed in name but not operationalized for the QA task."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4414766972","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Measures social bias in LLM mental-health vignette responses across nine models using BERTScore/ROUGE-style proxies over demographically varied vignettes. Its residue: bias is reported as proxy-metric differences across demographic conditions but is never attributed to a controllable model variable nor separated from the factual/safety constructs it is entangled with, so a 'bias' finding cannot be distinguished from a generic quality drop."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"LLM evaluation for mental-health question answering (open-ended clinical QA validity/diagnosis)","venue":"ICLR / NeurIPS / ICML (ML methods + datasets-and-benchmarks track)","time":"2026","data":["CounselBench expert-annotated mental-health QA (openalex:W4414801979)","PsyQA / CBT QA pairs (semanticscholar:07a52d25dd5d091957fbdfa6abd28a394719ef15)","MH vignette sets used in LLM-vs-clinician studies (openalex:W4406665832, openalex:W4414766972)","public MH knowledge/diagnosis sets: Dreaddit, SDCNL, CAS counseling (openalex:W4413005885)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with NLP + access to clinician annotators for a small expert panel","preference":"both","baseline":"expert-rubric scoring + adversarial benchmarking as in CounselBench (openalex:W4414801979) and the per-response quality rubrics in openalex:W4405768404","limitation":"current MH-QA evaluations report an aggregate human-rated quality/safety score or catalog failure cases, but do not attribute a given low score to a controllable, measurable model-internal variable, and they collapse distinct validity constructs (factual correctness, clinical-safety, empathic stance, calibration of uncertainty) into one number, so a score change cannot be read as a specific construct moving","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared measurement framework (coherence thread: shared_evaluation) is a Reliability-First Validity Instrument (RFVI) for open-ended mental-health QA, built entirely from the answer text plus a small clinician anchor panel, with three interlocking parts all computed on the same matched-instance design. (1) Construct decomposition: a response r to a clinical question q is scored on four validity constructs C = {factual_correctness, clinical_safety, empathic_appropriateness, expressed_certainty_calibration}; each construct score s_c(q,r) in [0,1] is elicited by a construct-specific scoring protocol P_c (a rubric prompt to a judge model, OR a clinician rating; both are supported and compared). The decomposition is not a free re-weighting of one aggregate — each P_c is paired with a per-cue suppression: to measure s_c we generate a minimal-edit variant of r that toggles only the cue construct c depends on (inject one contraindicated recommendation for safety; corrupt one verifiable fact for factual_correctness; flatten affective language for empathy; replace a hedged clause with an over-confident assertion for certainty) and require the protocol to move s_c while leaving the other three within tolerance tau (tau = 0.1, fixed) — a construct whose probe also moves the other scores is rejected as non-isolating. (2) Metamorphic reliability: for each (q, construct c) we build a same-question family F(q) of K label-preserving transforms (K = 8: 3 neutral paraphrases of q, 3 demographic relabelings that swap protected-attribute mentions without changing clinical content, 2 rater/judge swaps), score every member, and define the per-construct reliability coefficient rho_c(q) = 1 - (within-family score variance / total cross-question score variance for c), an intraclass-correlation-style ratio computed per construct over the family; the instrument's headline reliability number is the pooled rho_c. This is the load-bearing quantity: a construct whose rho_c is low is measuring elicitation noise, not the construct. (3) Causal attribution: we designate three controllable input variables V = {severity_level, self_harm_risk_flag, demographic_frame}; for each we run a directed intervention (raise severity by one DSM-anchored step; toggle the self-harm flag; swap demographic frame) holding all other axes fixed, and record delta s_c, the signed change in each construct score, plus a confound-matched control (a perturbation of equal edit-distance that does not change the targeted variable's clinical meaning). An attribution is credited only when delta s_c under the real intervention significantly exceeds delta s_c under the matched control AND the affected construct has rho_c above a reliability floor (0.7) — so we never attribute a change to a construct we cannot reliably measure. The three parts share the same matched-instance machinery: the per-cue suppression that isolates a construct (part 1) is the same edit primitive used to build the label-preserving family (part 2) and the directed intervention (part 3); only the edit's TARGET differs (suppress-the-other-cues vs preserve-meaning vs change-one-variable). Ground truth for factual_correctness and clinical_safety comes from an independent clinician-curated answer key per question (oracle independent of the evaluand, per C02 step 3), not from the judged model's own consensus.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The three gaps share machinery because the evidence is that they are three readings of one object: you cannot decompose into constructs (gap 1) without a per-construct probe, you cannot test reliability (anchor) without re-eliciting that same probe under transforms, and you cannot attribute causally (gap 3) without a reliability floor on the construct you attribute to — so a single matched-instance edit primitive, retargeted, serves all three, which is why one instrument and not three modules. (b) Alternatives rejected: (i) a learned multi-task 'validity head' fine-tuned to predict the four constructs — rejected because it would re-introduce the very unreliability we audit (the head's output is one more un-reliability-tested elicitation) and would not be an instrument anyone can apply to a new model without retraining; (ii) treating the fused aggregate and adding post-hoc factor analysis — rejected because factor analysis on one elicitation cannot distinguish low reliability from genuine low quality, which is exactly the conflation the anchor gap names. AVOIDED REGRESSION NODE: the mechanism deliberately does NOT reduce to method_lineage node n2 (collect more expert ratings / bigger rubric) nor to collateral c0 applied verbatim (apply human psychometric scales descriptively as in openalex:W4408498299) — rho_c is computed from re-elicitation under label-preserving transforms of the SAME item, a metamorphic-invariance construction (collateral c1) operationalized as a per-construct instrument, not a larger panel; the reliability signal lives in within-item cross-transform variance, a locus the scaling-the-panel node never reads.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on >=300 CounselBench-style mental-health questions scored across >=4 LLMs with both an LLM-judge and a small clinician panel, build the matched-instance families and compute the four per-construct reliability coefficients rho_c and the causal attribution table. If the candidate is correct, the pooled within-family (label-preserving) score variance will account for a large, non-trivial share of what aggregate single-rating evaluations report as model-quality variance (the 'apparent quality gap' between models shrinks substantially when restricted to high-rho_c constructs), and failure localization accuracy against clinician failure-type labels will exceed the fused-aggregate baseline. The named load-bearing variable is rho_c, the per-construct metamorphic reliability coefficient. Negative control: scramble the family pairing so that the K transforms of a question are re-associated to RANDOM other questions before computing reliability and attribution (the transforms are no longer label-preserving variants of the same item); under this control the downstream task-outcome metric — failure-localization accuracy against clinician labels — must fall to the fused-aggregate baseline (chance localization), because attribution can no longer be conditioned on a meaningful within-item reliability floor. Positive control: a stripped-down instrument that uses ONLY rho_c-gated construct scores (no causal-intervention table) should still recover most of the localization gain over the fused aggregate, identifying reliability-gating as the mechanism rather than the intervention machinery.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4414801979","delta":"CounselBench constructs a 100-clinician expert benchmark and reports per-response quality/safety scores and adversarial failure categories; we construct, for the same kind of questions, a per-construct metamorphic reliability coefficient rho_c and a reliability-gated causal-attribution table — quantities CounselBench never computes — and show its aggregate scores partly measure elicitation noise rather than behavior."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4414457959","delta":"This piece argues conceptually that single-response scoring misrepresents behavior; we supply the operational instrument it lacks — a within-item cross-transform reliability ratio plus a confound-matched directed-intervention attribution — turning 'responses are not behavior' into a measurable, reproducible per-construct quantity."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4408498299","delta":"They apply validated human psychometric scales to LLMs descriptively (one MANOVA over fixed traits); we do not borrow a human scale at all but construct a task-specific reliability coefficient from re-elicitation under label-preserving transforms of the SAME clinical item, and bind reliability to a downstream localization outcome rather than reporting trait labels."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4414766972","delta":"They measure demographic bias as proxy text-similarity differences across vignette conditions; we treat demographic relabeling as one label-preserving transform inside the reliability family AND as one controllable intervention variable, so a 'bias' effect is separated from generic quality drift and credited only when it exceeds a matched control on a reliably-measured construct."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4414801979","what_step_was_missed":"CounselBench collected expert annotations of single answers and aggregated them into quality/safety scores and failure categories; for our contribution to already exist it would have needed to construct, per clinical question, a matched family of label-preserving transforms (neutral paraphrase, demographic relabel, rater swap) and compute the within-family-vs-cross-question variance ratio as a per-construct reliability coefficient — a metamorphic re-elicitation construction it never built — and then gate causal attribution of failures on that coefficient, so its annotations remain an un-reliability-tested elicitation rather than a reliability-bearing measurement."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":280,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"gap_closure_reject_check.verdict=clear (every Reject lesson marked candidate_match=no, with the circularity and ecological-validity lessons defused by the independent clinician oracle and the step-9 real-data localization binding), recipe_application_check.verdict=applied (all three entries perform a distinct C02 signature move present in core_mechanism, not the parent's generic gist), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id=null (singleton composition cannot match any heterogeneous_decomposition-requiring anti-pattern), and paper_pointed_threat=no_threat_found (the three LLM-eval-adjacent collision papers — LLM personality psychometrics, the System Hallucination Scale, and Evaluative Fingerprints — none compute a per-construct metamorphic reliability coefficient for MH-QA nor a reliability-gated causal attribution table, so none subsumes the candidate's claim). No layer-1 hard floor fired and every check is clear/applied/null/no_threat_found.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether a single per-response human/automatic score is even a stable measurement of the construct it claims to measure — i.e. whether the score reproduces under semantically-equivalent rephrasings, demographic relabelings, or rater swaps of the same clinical question; the shared assumption inherited across the evaluation leaves (openalex:W4414801979, openalex:W4413005885, openalex:W4414766972) is that one elicited rating IS the construct value, and no leaf questions whether that elicitation is reliable rather than assumed.","main_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail most often when the instrument isolates the confound only inside an artificial regime and never shows the signal transfers to real deployment, or when the diagnostic is validated against the same definition/system population it was built to interrogate (circularity), or when it re-derives an already-documented limitation (confirmatory).","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A diagnostic that only re-confirms a shortcut already known in advance, surfacing no previously unmeasurable failure, is read as confirmatory rather than as a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"rho_c, a per-construct metamorphic reliability coefficient for MH-QA, is a quantity no retrieved leaf computes (verified against lit_table and 280 collision hits), so the headline apparent-vs-reliable variance gap is a previously-unmeasurable finding, not a known shortcut."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a synthetic-ground-truth instrument only on synthetic data, without demonstrating that the controlled finding transfers to real-world instances, leaves ecological validity unestablished and undermines the central claim.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism_steps step 9 binds the instrument to real CounselBench-annotated clinician failure-type labels (localization accuracy), and step 1 sources >=300 real clinical questions, so the controlled signal is shown to transfer to real deployment data, not asserted on synthetic instances alone."},{"lesson_quoted":"Building the instrument around one contested definition of the target property means it cannot independently confirm that the definition is correct, and reviewers flag the resulting circularity.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The instrument does not hardcode a contested definition of quality; it decomposes into four operationally-probed constructs each validated by per-cue suppression (the probe must move only its own construct within tau=0.1), so the construct boundaries are empirically tested rather than asserted."},{"lesson_quoted":"Resting an unsupervised evaluation on the unverified premise that the systems under test can reliably judge one another stakes the entire method on an assumption that collapses under scrutiny.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Ground truth for factual_correctness and clinical_safety comes from an independent clinician-curated answer key per question (oracle independent of the evaluand, per C02 step 3), not from the judged model's own consensus, so the method does not rest on models judging one another."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pairing a single-task or small-sample instrument with broad capability claims triggers a scope-mismatch rejection, and assembling retrieval or engineering blocks without an isolating scientific insight reads as application rather than research.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Claims are scoped to MH-QA validity measurement (not broad capability) at N>=300 across >=4 models with two judge types, and the core is an isolating insight (within-item cross-transform variance as the reliability locus), not a stacked engineering pipeline."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a mental-health-QA evaluation whose output decomposes a single response into separately-reliable validity constructs (factual correctness, clinical-safety, empathic appropriateness, expressed-certainty calibration) such that a deployer can read which construct failed rather than only that an aggregate score dropped (CounselBench, openalex:W4414801979, and the quality audits report only fused aggregates; openalex:W4405768404).","main_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failures are artificial-regime non-transfer, circularity against the evaluand's own consensus or a hardcoded definition, confirmatory re-derivation of a known limitation, and scope-claim mismatch.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A diagnostic that only re-confirms a shortcut already known in advance, surfacing no previously unmeasurable failure, is read as confirmatory rather than as a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Per-cue construct isolation produces a per-construct failure-localization that fused-aggregate benchmarks (the only retrieved practice) structurally cannot produce, so the construct-separated reading is new, not a re-confirmation."},{"lesson_quoted":"Building the instrument around one contested definition of the target property means it cannot independently confirm that the definition is correct, and reviewers flag the resulting circularity.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Each construct's separability is itself an empirical test (the minimal-edit probe must move only that construct within tau=0.1, else it is rejected as non-isolating), so the decomposition is falsifiable rather than a hardcoded contested definition."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a synthetic-ground-truth instrument only on synthetic data, without demonstrating that the controlled finding transfers to real-world instances, leaves ecological validity unestablished and undermines the central claim.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The construct decomposition is evaluated against real clinician failure-type labels in step 9, establishing ecological validity for the separation claim."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf attributes a mental-health-QA evaluation outcome to a controllable, measurable model-internal or input-side variable whose targeted perturbation predicts the direction of the score change — evaluations catalog failures (openalex:W4414801979) or argue responses-are-not-behavior (openalex:W4414457959) without an instrument that turns a failure into a causal, reproducible attribution.","main_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The instrument can fail via artificial-regime non-transfer, circularity (evaluand-as-oracle or hardcoded definition), confirmatory re-derivation, or attributing an effect that is actually uncontrolled co-variation between the varied surface and the structure.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A diagnostic that only re-confirms a shortcut already known in advance, surfacing no previously unmeasurable failure, is read as confirmatory rather than as a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"A reliability-gated, confound-matched directed-intervention attribution table {variable -> construct -> signed effect} is not produced by any retrieved leaf; the position paper (openalex:W4414457959) argues the need conceptually but supplies no instrument."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a synthetic-ground-truth instrument only on synthetic data, without demonstrating that the controlled finding transfers to real-world instances, leaves ecological validity unestablished and undermines the central claim.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Interventions are run on real clinical questions and the attribution is gated on rho_c>=0.7 measured on the same real items, so the causal claim is anchored in the deployment regime, not a synthetic-only sandbox."},{"lesson_quoted":"Building the instrument around one contested definition of the target property means it cannot independently confirm that the definition is correct, and reviewers flag the resulting circularity.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Attribution is credited only when the real intervention's delta s_c significantly exceeds an equal-edit-distance confound-matched control, so co-variation between surface edit and the targeted variable is explicitly controlled rather than assumed away."}],"verdict":"clear"}],"verdict":"clear","reasoning":"All three gap_closure entries are bound to C02 and clear every Reject lesson. The two lessons that carry the most weight for a measurement-validity instrument — circularity ('Building the instrument around one contested definition...') and ecological non-transfer ('Validating a synthetic-ground-truth instrument only on synthetic data...') — are both defused at the artifact level: the oracle is an independent clinician answer key (not the evaluand), construct separability is an empirical per-cue-suppression test rather than a hardcoded definition, and step 9 binds every claim to real CounselBench clinician failure labels."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether a single per-response human/automatic score is even a stable measurement of the construct it claims to measure — i.e. whether the score reproduces under semantically-equivalent rephrasings, demographic relabelings, or rater swaps of the same clinical question; the shared assumption inherited across the evaluation leaves (openalex:W4414801979, openalex:W4413005885, openalex:W4414766972) is that one elicited rating IS the construct value, and no leaf questions whether that elicitation is reliable rather than assumed.","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Construct a controlled set of evaluation instances in which exactly one named confound is independently varied while everything else is held fixed, and report the divergence between apparent and de-confounded performance as the primary result rather than an aggregate leaderboard score — the load-bearing artifact being the controlled instance set paired with an oracle independent of the system under test.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism part (2) builds same-question families F(q) that hold clinical content fixed and vary exactly one label-preserving surface axis (paraphrase / demographic relabel / rater swap), then reports rho_c = 1 - within-family/total variance and the pooled apparent-vs-reliable variance gap (steps 4, 5, 6, 10) as the headline — this is precisely C02's 'vary one named confound, report the apparent-vs-de-confounded divergence' move, with the elicitation surface as the named confound.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a mental-health-QA evaluation whose output decomposes a single response into separately-reliable validity constructs (factual correctness, clinical-safety, empathic appropriateness, expressed-certainty calibration) such that a deployer can read which construct failed rather than only that an aggregate score dropped (CounselBench, openalex:W4414801979, and the quality audits report only fused aggregates; openalex:W4405768404).","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Among the listed C02 constructions is 'suppress one input cue or withhold one modality at a time' so that any measured difference is attributable to that one axis alone; uncontrolled co-variation between surface change and structural change is the most common reason the isolation claim fails.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism part (1) performs exactly per-cue suppression: each construct probe is a minimal-edit variant toggling only the cue that construct depends on (inject one contraindicated recommendation for safety, corrupt one verifiable fact for factual_correctness, flatten affect for empathy, over-assert a hedged clause for certainty) and is rejected as non-isolating unless it moves s_c while leaving the other three within tau=0.1 — the C02 per-cue-suppression construction with an explicit non-co-variation guard.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf attributes a mental-health-QA evaluation outcome to a controllable, measurable model-internal or input-side variable whose targeted perturbation predicts the direction of the score change — evaluations catalog failures (openalex:W4414801979) or argue responses-are-not-behavior (openalex:W4414457959) without an instrument that turns a failure into a causal, reproducible attribution.","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"C02 instances 'independently vary' a named axis while holding everything else fixed, scored by an oracle independent of the system under test, with a matched control so the isolated signal is attributable to the manipulated axis alone.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism part (3) varies exactly one controllable variable in V={severity_level, self_harm_risk_flag, demographic_frame} via a directed intervention holding all other axes fixed, pairs it with an equal-edit-distance confound-matched control, and credits an attribution only when delta s_c(real) significantly exceeds delta s_c(control) AND rho_c>=0.7 — the C02 'vary the hypothesized driver directly against a matched control' step, with the reliability floor as the C02 'oracle-independent, isolated-signal' guard.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"All three entries instantiate a distinct C02 signature operation actually present in core_mechanism — the elicitation surface varied as the named confound (part 2), per-cue suppression with a non-co-variation tau guard (part 1), and directed single-axis intervention against an equal-edit-distance matched control (part 3); none merely restates the parent pattern's generic 'controlled diagnostic' gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["controlled_diagnostic_design"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"The composition_set is the singleton {controlled_diagnostic_design}; all three documented reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component, so no 2-way subset matches and no mitigation is owed."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"no_threat_found","threat_source":"n/a","subsumption_argument":null,"addressable_via":null}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Is the Score the Construct? A Reliability-First Instrument for Mental-Health QA Evaluation\n\n**Method.** Reliability-First Validity Instrument (RFVI)\n\n## Motivation\nWhen people test whether a chatbot gives good answers to mental-health questions, they usually have an expert read each answer and give it one quality-or-safety score, then average those scores. The leading example, CounselBench (a 100-clinician benchmark), does exactly this and finds that models fail in repeatable ways — but it reports those failures as scores, not as explanations. So a single number tells a deployer THAT a model scored low without telling them WHY: was the answer factually wrong, unsafe, cold in tone, or confidently wrong? All four get blurred into one rating.\n\nThe problem nobody checks is even more basic: is that one score a reliable measurement at all? If you reword the same question in a neutral way, or change the patient's stated demographics without changing the clinical content, or have a different rater score it, do you get the same number back? Nobody tests this. A score that changes when you only reword the question is not measuring the model — it is measuring noise in how the score was elicited. Two recent opinion papers say almost this (one says 'responses are not behavior'; another says a single safety score is misleading across situations) but neither builds a tool to fix it.\n\nThis is solvable now because large clinician-checked question sets with answer keys finally exist at scale, and cheaply rewording or relabeling a question (then having a clinician spot-check it) is now practical. We build the missing tool, called the Reliability-First Validity Instrument (RFVI). It does three things at once on the same set of carefully matched question variants: (1) it splits each answer into four separately-checkable qualities — factual correctness, clinical safety, empathic tone, and how well the model's expressed confidence matches reality; (2) it measures, for each quality, a reliability number $rho_{c}$ that says how much of the score survives neutral rewording, demographic relabeling, and rater swaps versus how much is noise; and (3) it traces a failure back to a controllable input — question severity, presence of self-harm risk, or demographic framing — but only credits that explanation when a deliberate change to that input moves the score more than a matched harmless change does, AND only for a quality whose reliability is high enough to trust. The payoff: a deployer learns which quality failed, whether the score is trustworthy, and what input caused it — none of which today's single number can say.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n\n1. Gather at least 300 open-ended mental-health questions from CounselBench-style sources plus PsyQA and Cognitive Behavioral Therapy (CBT) question-answer pairs. For each question, have two clinicians independently write a structured answer key listing (a) the checkable facts with whether each is true or false and a source, and (b) any recommendations that would be unsafe, each tagged with a risk type such as self-harm, medication, crisis-referral, or going beyond scope; a third senior clinician settles any disagreement. This answer key is the independent reference used to score factual correctness and clinical safety later, never the chatbot's own opinion.\n   - _Why:_ You cannot fairly judge an answer if your only reference is the thing being judged, so the answer key must come from a clinician, independent of the model.\n2. Run each of the models you want to evaluate on every question, collecting exactly one answer per model per question and saving the raw text with fixed generation settings so the same answer can be reproduced. These are the responses whose scoring process we are about to put under the microscope.\n   - _Why:_ These are the responses whose scoring process we are about to put under the microscope.\n3. Score the original answer and all the edited and matched versions on each of the four qualities using a per-quality scoring rubric with a few anchored levels mapped onto a 0-to-1 scale (for example, safety: 1.0 = nothing unsafe and a proper crisis referral, 0.5 = minor omission, 0.0 = contains an unsafe recommendation). Do this two ways and compare: a rubric prompt to a judge model, and a clinician filling in the same rubric. For factual correctness and safety the rubric is tied to the clinician answer key from the first step (how many checkable facts are right; whether any unsafe recommendation appears), so those two are anchored to the independent reference rather than to open judgment.\n   - _Why:_ We need the full grid of scores across all the matched variants before we can separate stable signal from noise.\n\n### Construct decomposition\n*Split a single answer into four separately-measurable validity qualities via per-cue minimal edits.*\n\n4. For each answer, make four tiny edited versions, each flipping just one thing: inject one unsafe recommendation (for safety), corrupt one checkable fact (for factual correctness), flatten the emotional warmth (for empathy), or turn a cautious phrase into an over-confident claim (for certainty). Use a constrained rewrite that changes as little as possible (keep the edited text within about 15% of the original in word-level edit distance) so only the targeted thing moves. Keep an edited version only if it clearly moves its own quality score while leaving the other three almost unchanged (within 0.1); otherwise throw it out. 【author decision: how large the target quality's score must move to count as 'moved' (suggested at twice the allowed leakage of the other three) is a calibration the authors set against the real score spread.】\n\n*A per-cue probe is accepted as isolating construct c only when toggling that cue moves the target construct score by more than delta while leaving every other construct score within tolerance tau (tau = 0.1); a probe that also moves the other scores is rejected as non-isolating.*\n$$ \\bigl| s_c(q, r') - s_c(q, r) \\bigr| > \\delta \\quad\\text{and}\\quad \\max_{c' \\neq c} \\bigl| s_{c'}(q, r') - s_{c'}(q, r) \\bigr| \\leq \\tau \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why:_ If a single edit only nudges one quality, then that quality can be measured on its own instead of being blurred into one overall number.\n\n### Metamorphic reliability\n*Measure how much of each quality's score survives label-preserving rewordings, demographic relabels, and rater swaps versus how much is elicitation noise.*\n\n5. For each question, build 8 matched versions that should not change the right answer: 3 neutral rewordings (machine-generated, then clinician spot-checked so the correct answer is judged unchanged), 3 demographic relabelings that swap only the surface mention of one protected attribute (race/ethnicity, gender, or age-band) for another value while keeping symptoms and severity identical, and 2 different raters/judges. Regenerate any version a clinician rejects. 【author decision: which protected attributes and which value pairs to swap is a study-design choice the authors must make.】\n   - _Why:_ If the score is a real measurement, these label-preserving changes should leave it roughly the same; any wobble is noise we want to quantify.\n6. For each quality, compute its reliability number, $\\rho _{c},$ by comparing how much the score wobbles across the 8 matched versions of one question against how much it varies across different questions: estimate the within-question wobble as the average per-question score spread over its 8 versions, the across-question variation as the spread of each question's average score, and set $\\rho _{c} = 1$ minus within-question over total. Report an uncertainty range by resampling questions. Flag any model-plus-judge whose $\\rho _{c}$ is below 0.7 as unreliable — its score for that quality is mostly noise and should not be reported as model behavior.\n\n*The per-construct reliability coefficient $rho_{c}(q)$ equals one minus the ratio of within-family score variance (over the K label-preserving transforms k of question q) to the cross-question variance of the construct's mean score; a low $rho_{c}$ means the construct score is elicitation noise rather than a stable measurement.*\n$$ \\rho_c(q) = 1 - \\frac{\\operatorname{Var}_{k \\in F(q)}\\, s_c(q,k)}{\\operatorname{Var}_{q'}\\, \\bar{s}_c(q')} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why:_ A score that swings wildly just from rewording the question is not measuring the model, so we need a number that says how much to trust it.\n\n### Reliability-gated causal attribution\n*Trace a failure to a controllable input only when a directed edit beats a matched control and the quality is reliable enough to trust.*\n\n7. For each controllable input — question severity, whether self-harm risk is present, and the demographic framing — make one edit that changes exactly that input, plus a harmless control edit of the same size that does not change that input's meaning. For severity, move the case exactly one step up a clinical severity ladder (mild $\\to $ moderate $\\to $ severe for the relevant disorder); for self-harm, add or remove one explicit self-harm-risk sentence from a fixed template list; for demographics, reuse the relabeling from the matched-versions step. Match the control edit to the real edit in word-level edit distance (within about 2 words). Feed both edited questions back to the model and re-score the new answers. 【author decision: the exact severity ladders for each disorder must be specified by the authors.】\n   - _Why:_ To claim an input caused a score change you have to actually change that input and check the effect against a same-size change that should do nothing.\n8. Credit an input as the cause of a quality's change only when the real edit moves the score significantly more than the harmless control edit — using a paired test on the per-item differences, corrected for testing many input-by-quality combinations (Holm correction) — AND that quality's reliability $\\rho _{c}$ is at least 0.7. Output a table mapping each input to each quality with the signed effect (the typical size and direction of the change with an uncertainty range), keeping only the entries that pass both the significance test and the reliability floor.\n\n*An attribution of construct c's change to controllable variable v is credited only when the construct-score change under the real directed intervention significantly exceeds the change under an equal-edit-distance confound-matched control (paired test, Holm-corrected) AND construct c clears the reliability floor of 0.7.*\n$$ \\Delta s_c^{\\text{real}}(v) - \\Delta s_c^{\\text{ctrl}}(v) > 0 \\;\\;\\text{(Holm-corrected)} \\quad\\text{and}\\quad \\rho_c \\geq 0.7 \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why:_ This keeps you from blaming an input for moving a score you cannot even measure reliably.\n\n### Real-failure localization and headline gap\n*Show the instrument localizes real CounselBench failures and quantify how much reported quality variance is unreliable noise.*\n\n9. Take CounselBench's labelled failures and, for each, find which quality dropped the most among the qualities reliable enough to trust $(\\rho _{c}$ at least 0.7) relative to a non-failing reference answer; call that the predicted failing quality and map it to CounselBench's failure-type label. Report how often this matches the clinicians' labels (top guess), next to a baseline that uses only the single fused score and so cannot say which quality failed. Then report the headline number: what fraction of the supposed model-quality differences is actually just unreliable wobble across matched versions rather than real differences across questions. 【author decision: the mapping from each quality to CounselBench's failure-type labels must be defined by the authors from CounselBench's real label set.】\n   - _Why:_ This shows the tool works on real flagged failures, not just synthetic edits, and reveals how much of the field's reported quality gap is really noise.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 评分就是构念本身吗？一种面向心理健康问答评测的可靠性优先测量工具\n\n**方法名称：** Reliability-First Validity Instrument (RFVI)\n\n## 研究动机\n现在评估聊天机器人回答心理健康问题好不好时，通常的做法是让专家给每条回答打一个质量或安全分，再把这些分数取平均。最有代表性的 CounselBench（一个由 100 名临床医生构建的基准）正是这么做的，它发现模型会以可重复的方式出错——但它把这些失败报告成分数，而不是解释。于是一个数字只告诉部署者模型分数低这件事，却没说为什么：这条回答是事实错误、不安全、语气冷漠，还是自信地答错了？这四种情况都被糅进了同一个评分里。\n\n但没人去检查一个更基本的问题：那一个分数本身是不是一个可靠的测量？如果你把同一个问题中性地换种说法，或者在不改变临床内容的前提下换掉病人陈述的人口统计学信息，或者换一个评分者来打分，你还能得到同样的数字吗？没人测过这一点。一个仅仅因为换了说法就改变的分数，测的不是模型，而是评分诱导过程中的噪声。最近有两篇观点文章几乎说到了这一点（一篇说回答不等于行为，另一篇说单一的安全分在不同情境下会误导人），但谁都没有造出一个工具来解决它。\n\n现在能解决这个问题，是因为带答案标准、由临床医生核对过的大规模题库终于成规模地存在了，而且廉价地改写或重标一个问题（再让临床医生抽检）如今已经可行。我们造出了那个缺失的工具，称为可靠性优先测量工具 (Reliability-First Validity Instrument, RFVI)。它在同一组精心匹配的问题变体上同时做三件事：(1) 把每条回答拆成四个可分别核查的方面——事实正确性、临床安全性、共情语气，以及模型表达的把握程度与现实的吻合度；(2) 为每个方面测出一个可靠性数值 $rho_{c}$，说明这个分数在中性改写、人口统计学重标和评分者更换之后有多少能留存下来、又有多少是噪声；(3) 把一次失败追溯到某个可控输入——问题的严重程度、是否存在自残风险、或人口统计学表述方式——但只有当对该输入的刻意改动比一个匹配的无害改动更明显地移动了分数，并且这个方面的可靠性高到值得信任时，才认定这个解释成立。其收益是：部署者能知道是哪个方面失败了、这个分数是否可信、以及是什么输入造成了它——而这些都是今天那个单一数字给不出来的。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景\n\n1. 从 CounselBench 这类来源以及 PsyQA 和认知行为疗法(Cognitive Behavioral Therapy, CBT)问答对中收集至少 300 个开放式心理健康问题。为每个问题请两名临床医生各自独立写一份结构化的答案标准，列出：(a) 可核查的事实，并标注每条为真还是假以及来源；(b) 任何不安全的建议，每条打上风险类型标签，如自残、用药、危机转介或超出执业范围；如有分歧由第三位资深临床医生裁定。这份答案标准是用于后续给事实正确性和临床安全性打分的独立参照，绝不用被评聊天机器人自己的意见。\n   - _为什么：_ 如果你唯一的参照就是被评的东西，就无法公平地判断一条回答，所以答案标准必须来自独立于模型的临床医生。\n2. 让你想评估的每个模型在每个问题上各生成一条回答，每模型每问题恰好保存一条原始文本，并固定生成设置以便复现同一条回答。这些就是我们接下来要放到显微镜下审视其评分过程的回答。\n   - _为什么：_ 这些就是我们接下来要放到显微镜下审视其评分过程的回答。\n3. 对原始回答以及所有改写和匹配版本，在四个方面上各打分，使用一份按方面定制、带几个锚定档位并映射到 0 到 1 区间的评分量表（例如安全性：1.0 = 没有不安全内容且有恰当的危机转介，0.5 = 轻微遗漏，0.0 = 含有不安全建议）。用两种方式并加以比较：对裁判模型的评分量表提示，以及临床医生填写同一份量表。对事实正确性和安全性，量表与第一步的临床医生答案标准挂钩（有多少可核查事实是对的；是否出现任何不安全建议），因此这两项锚定在独立参照上，而非开放判断。\n   - _为什么：_ 在能把稳定信号与噪声分开之前，我们需要所有匹配变体上的完整评分网格。\n\n### 构念分解\n*通过单线索微编辑，把一条回答拆成四个可分别测量的效度方面。*\n\n4. 为每条回答制作四个微小的改写版本，每个只翻动一件事：注入一条不安全建议（对应安全性）、篡改一个可核查的事实（对应事实正确性）、抹平情感温度（对应共情）、或把谨慎措辞改成过度自信的断言（对应把握度）。用一种尽量少改的受限改写（让改写文本与原文的词级编辑距离保持在约 15% 以内），使得只有被针对的那一项发生变化。只有当某个改写明显拨动了它自己那个方面的评分、却让其余三个几乎不变（在 0.1 以内）时才保留；否则丢弃。【作者需决定：目标方面的评分要移动多大才算『动了』（建议设为允许的其余三项渗漏量的两倍），这是作者需根据真实评分分布标定的取值。】\n\n*只有当切换某个线索使目标构念 c 的评分变化超过 delta、而其余所有构念评分都保持在容差 tau 内（tau = 0.1）时，该单线索探针才被接受为对构念 c 的隔离；若探针同时改变了其他评分，则因无法隔离而被剔除。*\n$$ \\bigl| s_c(q, r') - s_c(q, r) \\bigr| > \\delta \\quad\\text{and}\\quad \\max_{c' \\neq c} \\bigl| s_{c'}(q, r') - s_{c'}(q, r) \\bigr| \\leq \\tau \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么：_ 如果单个改动只拨动一个方面，那么这个方面就能被单独测量，而不会被糅进一个总分里。\n\n### 变形可靠性\n*测量每个方面的评分在保标签改写、人口统计学重标和评分者更换后能留存多少、又有多少是诱导噪声。*\n\n5. 为每个问题构造 8 个不应改变正确答案的匹配版本：3 个中性改写（机器生成，再经临床医生抽检以确认正确答案未变）、3 个人口统计学重标（只替换某一个受保护属性的表面提及——种族/族裔、性别或年龄段——换成另一个取值，同时保持症状和严重程度完全一致）、以及 2 个不同的评分者/裁判。临床医生否决的任何版本都要重新生成。【作者需决定：要改变哪些受保护属性、以及替换哪些取值对，这是作者需做出的研究设计选择。】\n   - _为什么：_ 如果评分是真实测量，这些保标签的改动应让它大致不变；任何抖动都是我们想量化的噪声。\n6. 对每个方面，计算它的可靠性数值 $\\rho _{c}$：把评分在一个问题的 8 个匹配版本间的抖动，与它在不同问题间的变化作比较——把问题内抖动估计为各问题在其 8 个版本上的评分离散度的平均，把问题间变化估计为各问题平均分的离散度，然后令 $\\rho _{c} = 1$ 减去（问题内 / 总体）。通过对问题重采样报告一个不确定性区间。把 $\\rho _{c}$ 低于 0.7 的模型加裁判组合标记为不可靠——它在那个方面的评分大多是噪声，不应作为模型行为来报告。\n\n*每个构念的可靠性系数 $rho_{c}(q)$ 等于 1 减去族内评分方差（针对问题 q 的 K 个保标签变换 k）与该构念跨问题均值方差之比；$rho_{c}$ 偏低意味着该构念评分是诱导噪声而非稳定测量。*\n$$ \\rho_c(q) = 1 - \\frac{\\operatorname{Var}_{k \\in F(q)}\\, s_c(q,k)}{\\operatorname{Var}_{q'}\\, \\bar{s}_c(q')} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么：_ 仅仅换种说法就大幅波动的评分并没有在测量模型，所以我们需要一个数值来说明它有多值得信任。\n\n### 可靠性门控的因果归因\n*只有当定向编辑胜过匹配对照、且该方面可靠到值得信任时，才把失败追溯到某个可控输入。*\n\n7. 对每个可控输入——问题严重程度、是否存在自残风险、以及人口统计学表述方式——做一个恰好改变该输入的编辑，再做一个等量的、不改变该输入含义的无害对照编辑。严重程度：把病例在临床严重程度阶梯上恰好上移一档（相关障碍的轻度 $\\to $ 中度 $\\to $ 重度）；自残：从固定模板表中增加或删除一句明确的自残风险陈述；人口统计学：复用匹配版本步骤中的重标做法。让对照编辑在词级编辑距离上与真实编辑匹配（相差约 2 个词以内）。把两个改写后的问题都送回模型并对新回答重新打分。【作者需决定：每种障碍的具体严重程度阶梯必须由作者指定。】\n   - _为什么：_ 要声称某个输入造成了评分变化，你必须真的改变那个输入，并对照一个本应毫无作用的等量改动来检验效果。\n8. 只有当真实编辑比无害对照编辑显著更大地移动了评分——对逐条样本的差值做配对检验，并对『输入 $\\times $ 方面』的多重组合做校正（Holm 校正）——且该方面的可靠性 $\\rho _{c}$ 至少为 0.7 时，才认定该输入是该方面变化的原因。输出一张把每个输入映射到每个方面、带符号效应（变化的典型大小和方向，附不确定性区间）的表，只保留同时通过显著性检验和可靠性下限的条目。\n\n*只有当真实定向干预下构念评分的变化显著超过等编辑距离的混淆匹配对照下的变化（配对检验，Holm 校正），且构念 c 的可靠性达到 0.7 的下限时，才将构念 c 的变化归因于可控变量 v。*\n$$ \\Delta s_c^{\\text{real}}(v) - \\Delta s_c^{\\text{ctrl}}(v) > 0 \\;\\;\\text{(Holm-corrected)} \\quad\\text{and}\\quad \\rho_c \\geq 0.7 \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么：_ 这能防止你把一个你根本无法可靠测量的评分变化归咎于某个输入。\n\n### 真实失败定位与核心差距\n*展示该工具能定位真实的 CounselBench 失败，并量化被报告的质量方差里有多少是不可靠噪声。*\n\n9. 取 CounselBench 已标注的失败，对每个失败，在可靠到值得信任的方面（$\\rho _{c}$ 至少 0.7）中，找出相对于一个未失败参照回答下降最多的那个方面，把它作为预测的失败方面，并映射到 CounselBench 的失败类型标签。报告这与临床医生标签吻合的频率（首选猜测），并与一个只用单一融合分、因而说不出是哪个方面失败的基线并列。然后报告核心数字：被认为是模型质量差异的部分，有多大比例其实只是匹配版本间不可靠的抖动，而非问题间的真实差异。【作者需决定：从每个方面到 CounselBench 失败类型标签的映射必须由作者依据 CounselBench 的真实标签集来定义。】\n   - _为什么：_ 这表明该工具在真实标注的失败上有效，而不只是在合成编辑上，并揭示该领域报告的质量差距里到底有多少其实是噪声。\n\n"},{"id":"20","run_dir":"run_prompt20_cybergym","index":20,"title":"Factorizing Agent Cyber-Capability: A Harness-Randomized Identification Instrument","title_zh":"解构智能体网络安全能力：一种基于 harness 随机化的辨识测量工具","method_name":"Harness-Randomized Capability Identification (HRCI)","hook":"Today's agent-cybersecurity scores are a single pass-rate that silently sums what the base model can do with what its retrieval-and-scaffold harness supplied, so a knowledge-fed wrapper and a genuinely stronger model are indistinguishable on the leaderboard. We recast capability measurement as identifying the model-attributable factor from a designed randomized-harness contrast over procedurally re-instantiated tasks, yielding a per-model capability estimate with an uncertainty interval that the marginal pass-rate cannot express.","anchor_pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","anchor_pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","domain_category":"Privacy, Security & Trustworthy ML","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a capability estimate that is factorized into a model-attributable component and a harness-attributable component; every leaf reports a single marginal outcome rate that mixes the two, so when an agent solves a task the evaluation cannot say which factor produced the success.","pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by reframing 'intrinsic model cyber-capability' as a faithful per-task responsibility score estimated over a well-studied object — a designed randomized-harness contrast whose factor decomposition (model factor vs harness factor) is identifiable from paired interventional runs and certified causally by perturbing each factor and observing the predicted outcome shift, rather than read off a marginal mean.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether the unit of evaluation must be a fixed answer-bearing challenge instance at all; every current agent-cyber leaf inherits from the static-benchmark ancestor the assumption that capability is measured by graded outcomes on pre-authored instances, which is exactly what makes contamination both possible and undetectable for multi-step tasks (openalex:W4416368190, openalex:W4416036350).","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","how_closed":"Framing move (C01): relocate the evaluation locus from a fixed answer-bearing instance (where success is a memorizable label) to a procedurally instantiated, end-state-verifiable task family (where success is checked by a runtime oracle on the environment state, not a stored answer), naming and violating the inherited 'capability = graded outcome on a pre-authored instance' assumption. Companion deliverable (controlled_diagnostic_design): a confound-isolating separation showing the factorized estimate is stable across independent procedural re-instantiations of the same task generator while the static-instance pass-rate inflates when the instance has been seen, isolating contamination as the artifact.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"evaluation of LLM/agent capability in cybersecurity (offensive + defensive multi-step tasks)","n_papers":40,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":26},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":18,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"HackSynth: LLM Agent and Evaluation Framework for Autonomous Penetration Testing"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Safe Guard: an LLM-agent for Real-time Voice-based Hate Speech Detection in Social Virtual Reality"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"WiS Platform: Enhancing Evaluation of LLM-Based Multi-Agent Systems Through Game-Based Analysis"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Small LLMs Are Weak Tool Learners: A Multi-LLM Agent"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Large Language Models in Healthcare and Medical Domain: A Review"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Large language models empowered agent-based modeling and simulation: a survey and perspectives"}],"more":12},{"year":2025,"n":21,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"CRAKEN: Cybersecurity LLM Agent with Knowledge-Based Execution"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Vulnerability Mitigation System (VMS): LLM Agent and Evaluation Framework for Autonomous Penetration Testing"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Specification and Evaluation of Multi-Agent LLM Systems - Prototype and Cybersecurity Applications"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"CFA-Bench: Cybersecurity Forensic Llm Agent Benchmark and Testing"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Distilling LLM Agent into Small Models with Retrieval and Code Tools"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Red-Teaming LLM Multi-Agent Systems via Communication Attacks"}],"more":15},{"year":2026,"n":1,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"}],"more":0}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":14,"share":0.35},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":8,"share":0.2},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":5,"share":0.125},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":2,"share":0.05},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":2,"share":0.05},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":2,"share":0.05},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":1,"share":0.025},{"pattern_id":"targeted_self_supervised_objective","pattern_name":"Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective","count":1,"share":0.025}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Across the current agent-cybersecurity evaluation frontier, capability is reported as a single aggregate outcome rate over a fixed, mostly public challenge set, and that aggregate is jointly produced by two distinct factors that the measurement cannot separate: the base model's intrinsic reasoning/exploit capability, and the surrounding harness — the retrieval/knowledge base, planner-executor decomposition, and prompt scaffolding. CRAKEN (semanticscholar:77efd3cf71cfe7af70e2e1130286a96a67946f68) explicitly raises CTF pass-rate by injecting a graph+vector knowledge retriever and an auto-prompter, and HackSynth (semanticscholar:361e68a489b714660ef6459952b9e40d88f76f90) does so via a Planner/Summarizer loop, yet both report the gain as a single per-challenge success number, so a reader cannot tell whether a higher score reflects a more capable model or merely a better-fed scaffold. Agent Security Bench (openalex:W4403884175) and CVE-Bench (openalex:W4411120547) similarly emit per-scenario attack-success / repair rates whose magnitude is uncontrolled for harness strength, and because these challenge sets are public, contamination further inflates the same number — a fragility that contamination detectors themselves cannot reliably catch (openalex:W4416368190). The structural failure is therefore that the unit of measurement (a marginal outcome rate on fixed instances) carries no factorization into model-attributable versus harness-attributable capability and no guard that the instance was unseen, so the score is not an estimate of any well-defined capability quantity and cannot be compared across agents, models, or new attack surfaces at scale.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:77efd3cf71cfe7af70e2e1130286a96a67946f68","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"CRAKEN improves CTF pass-rate by attaching a context-decomposing retriever (vector + graph search) plus an auto-prompter on top of a planner-executor agent, demonstrating that harness engineering moves the headline number. Its evaluation reports only the marginal end-to-end success rate per challenge and never factorizes the gain into what the base model could do unaided versus what the knowledge/scaffold supplied, so it leaves open any instrument that attributes an observed success to model-intrinsic capability versus harness contribution."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:361e68a489b714660ef6459952b9e40d88f76f90","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"HackSynth runs a Planner/Summarizer loop over fixed PicoCTF/OverTheWire challenges and reports aggregate solve counts as the capability signal. The challenge sets are static and public and the metric is binary per-challenge outcome, so it neither controls for contamination nor separates iterative-scaffold contribution from intrinsic model skill."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4403884175","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Agent Security Bench formalizes ten attack/defense scenarios and reports attack-success and refusal rates per scenario over a fixed task pool. The reported rates are marginal outcomes that do not isolate which sub-capability (recon, exploit synthesis, multi-step planning) the agent actually exercised, and the fixed scenarios admit no contamination guard."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416036350","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"DyePack provably flags test-set contamination by mixing backdoor samples into a benchmark, requiring the benchmark author to plant detectable triggers in answer-bearing items. It addresses contamination only for static answer-bearing benchmarks under author control and offers no mechanism for multi-step agentic cyber tasks where there is no single planted answer and the quantity of interest is a capability, not a memorized label."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"evaluation of LLM/agent capability in cybersecurity (offensive + defensive multi-step tasks)","venue":"ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML (ML methods + benchmark-validity track)","time":"2026 submission cycle","data":["public CTF corpora (PicoCTF, OverTheWire)","CVE/vulnerability repair tasks","agent trajectory logs (action sequences, tool calls, intermediate observations)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with access to agent scaffolds and a sandboxed cyber-range; authorized defensive-evaluation context","preference":"both","baseline":"outcome-only static CTF/benchmark pass-rate over fixed challenge sets (HackSynth, CRAKEN, CFA-Bench, CVE-Bench, ASB)","limitation":"current agent-cyber evaluations report a single pass-rate over a fixed public challenge set, which conflates the base model's intrinsic capability with the scaffold/knowledge-retrieval harness and is exposed to test-set contamination, so the number does not measure what it claims to measure and does not scale to new attack surfaces","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared_evaluation object is one capability-measurement instrument; both legs read from and write to a single quantity, the per-(model, task-generator) capability estimate theta_hat with an uncertainty interval. ANCHOR LEG (reframe → C00): for a fixed base model m and a procedurally generated task t, an agent run's binary outcome y(m, t, c) is a function of m and of a harness configuration c (the retrieval/knowledge base, the planner-executor scaffold depth, and the auto-prompter), modeled as a logistic response y ~ Bernoulli(sigma(theta_m + h_c + d_t)), where theta_m is the model-attributable capability (the target score), h_c is the harness-attributable contribution of configuration c, and d_t is a task-difficulty offset; sigma is the logistic function. The decisive faithfulness move (C00 step 3) is fixing the unit of analysis as a matched run-pair that holds m and t fixed and applies a DESIGNED RANDOMIZED HARNESS PERTURBATION: c is drawn from a small pre-registered set {c_full, c_ablated} where c_ablated removes the knowledge retriever and auto-prompter, and the assignment is randomized within each (m,t) cell so theta_m and h_c are separately identifiable from the within-pair outcome difference (which estimates h via Δ = h_{full} − h_{ablated}, isolating the harness factor) and the across-model outcome level at fixed c (which estimates theta_m). theta_m, h_c, d_t are read off as the maximum-likelihood (or hierarchical-Bayes posterior-mean) coefficients of this logistic model fit over the run table; the only free hyperparameter is the prior scale lambda_prior on theta_m (set to 1.0 on the logit scale, a weakly-informative default). Fidelity is certified causally (C00 step 5): a held-model harness swap must move outcomes by the estimated h, and a held-harness model swap must move outcomes by the estimated theta difference. SIBLING LEG (audit → C01 + companion controlled_diagnostic_design): the audited locus (C01 step 1) is the evaluation UNIT — current leaves anchor capability at a fixed pre-authored answer-bearing instance; we relocate it (C01 step 2-3) to a parametrized task GENERATOR g whose every draw t ~ g instantiates a fresh sandboxed cyber task (e.g., a templated vulnerable-service configuration with randomized ports/credentials/flag-locations) whose success is verified by a runtime oracle reading the environment end-state, so there is no memorizable answer. The companion supplies the empirical separation: re-drawing t ~ g and re-fitting yields a theta_hat whose value is invariant (within its interval) to re-instantiation, whereas a static-instance pass-rate measured on a leaked instance inflates — the divergence between the two is reported as the primary contamination-isolation result. The two legs interlock because theta_hat is only well-defined once the unit is a generator draw (sibling) AND the harness factor has been removed from it (anchor): the sibling secures the unit the anchor's estimator integrates over.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules: the factorized estimator (anchor) is computed over exactly the procedurally-instantiated units the sibling defines, and the contamination separation (sibling companion) is expressed as a property of the same theta_hat the anchor produces — evidence that they are one instrument, not two stapled papers. (b) Considered and rejected: (1) a plain item-response/IRT fit over static pass/fail items — rejected because method_lineage flags node n1 (psychometric latent-trait estimation) as a collateral family, so fitting latent ability to static items would be a regression to a >16y move; we avoid it by making the identifying signal a DESIGNED randomized harness perturbation (an interventional contrast the tree does not occupy), not latent-trait fitting of observational items alone. (2) A pure red-team/attacker optimizer (as in AGENTVIGIL) — rejected because it produces an attack, not a calibrated capability meter, and carries no factorization.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: instantiate g with 10 templates, a panel of K=6 open and API models, and the two harness configs, ~30 task draws each with 3 replicate seeds, and fit the factor model. If the candidate works, the ranking accuracy of theta_hat against the held-out ground-truth capability ordering INCREASES relative to the marginal pass-rate ranking (the pass-rate confuses knowledge-fed weak models with strong models; theta_hat does not), and theta_hat stays within its interval across independent re-instantiations of g while the static-instance pass-rate rises after simulated leakage. The named load-bearing variable is Δh, the estimated harness-attributable factor (h_full − h_ablated) recovered from the randomized within-cell perturbation. Negative control: PERMUTE the harness-assignment labels within each (m,t) cell so the perturbation is decoupled from which runs actually had the retriever — Δh is then no longer identified, and the prediction is that theta_hat's ranking accuracy against the ground-truth ordering collapses back to the marginal pass-rate's accuracy (the downstream outcome metric), confirming the gain came from the designed harness contrast and not from refitting or extra runs. Positive control: a stripped instrument that uses ONLY the within-pair difference Δh-correction (subtract the estimated harness factor from each model's raw rate, no full hierarchical fit) should recover most of the ranking-accuracy gain, identifying the harness-factor removal as the operative mechanism.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:77efd3cf71cfe7af70e2e1130286a96a67946f68","delta":"CRAKEN demonstrates that adding a graph+vector retriever and auto-prompter raises CTF pass-rate and reports that gain as a single end-to-end number; we construct an estimator that identifies and subtracts that retriever/auto-prompter contribution (Δh) from each model's score, producing a harness-removed model-capability estimate CRAKEN never separates out."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:361e68a489b714660ef6459952b9e40d88f76f90","delta":"HackSynth grades agents on fixed public PicoCTF/OverTheWire instances and reports aggregate solve counts; we replace the fixed-instance unit with a procedurally re-instantiated, oracle-verified generator draw and show the capability estimate is invariant to re-instantiation whereas their static count is contamination-inflatable."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4403884175","delta":"Agent Security Bench reports per-scenario marginal attack/defense success rates over a fixed scenario pool; we add a designed randomized-harness contrast that decomposes each rate into a model factor and a harness factor, which their aggregate marginal rate cannot expose."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416036350","delta":"DyePack flags contamination only for static answer-bearing benchmarks by planting backdoor triggers the author controls; we obtain contamination resistance for multi-step agentic capability by re-instantiating the task from a generator so no stored answer exists to memorize, requiring no planted trigger."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W6980198985","what_step_was_missed":"Bayesian Inference of Capability Profiles infers latent capability from observational performance data via item-response-style modeling, but it estimates a single monolithic respondent's ability from STATIC items and never decomposes the respondent into a model factor and a harness factor; our contribution requires the additional construction of a designed randomized-harness interventional contrast that makes theta_m (model) and h_c (harness) separately identifiable — a within-cell perturbation design their observational latent-trait fit does not build, and which is what converts the estimate from a confounded ability score into a harness-removed model-capability estimate."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":285,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"gap_closure_reject_check.verdict = clear for both entries (the C00 mechanical-wrapper lesson and the C01 'relocated-signal-not-defeated-against-adaptive-adversary' lesson are both candidate_match: no, because the identifying signal is a designed interventional contrast with causal certification and the contamination separation directly tests leakage). recipe_application_check.verdict = applied for both (the C00 causal-certified-measurement move and the C01 locus-relocation move are concretely instantiated). anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id = null (no heterogeneous_decomposition in the composition set). paper_pointed_threat is the closest-prior IRT paper but its subsumption is escaped by the interventional design and is already addressed in the candidate, so it is a reviewer concern for Phase 4, not a revise trigger.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a capability estimate that is factorized into a model-attributable component and a harness-attributable component; every leaf reports a single marginal outcome rate that mixes the two, so when an agent solves a task the evaluation cannot say which factor produced the success.","main_pattern":"reframe_as_solvable_object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The signature failure is treating the reframing as a mechanical wrapper: taking an established attribution/estimation tool and pointing it at a new granularity or domain without re-deriving why the resulting scores are faithful to the model — no causal validation, no axiomatic argument for why the definition is the 'real' quantity, no confound control.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Pointing an off-the-shelf decomposition at a coarser input granularity without showing the coarser units preserve the signal reads as a wrapper, not a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate does not point an off-the-shelf decomposition at a coarser unit; it introduces a DESIGNED randomized-harness interventional contrast that makes theta_m and h_c separately identifiable, a new identifying construction rather than a granularity swap."},{"lesson_quoted":"Porting a known attribution technique to a new architecture or domain while ignoring that technique's documented failure modes — and omitting comparisons to alternatives — leaves reviewers unable to see any unique benefit.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism_reasoning explicitly contrasts against the IRT/psychometric latent-trait family (the documented adjacent technique) and step 8 compares against the marginal pass-rate baseline on ranking accuracy, so alternatives are not omitted."},{"lesson_quoted":"Proposing a new attribution definition without an axiomatic or causal argument for why it should count as ground-truth collapses the moment a reviewer asks why this is the real importance.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"theta_m is grounded by causal certification (step 6: held-model harness swap must move outcomes by the predicted Δh; held-harness model swap by the predicted theta difference), supplying the causal argument the lesson demands."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether the unit of evaluation must be a fixed answer-bearing challenge instance at all; every current agent-cyber leaf inherits from the static-benchmark ancestor the assumption that capability is measured by graded outcomes on pre-authored instances, which is exactly what makes contamination both possible and undetectable for multi-step tasks (openalex:W4416368190, openalex:W4416036350).","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is relocating a signal to a new locus shown to work but never explained (reads as a stacked pipeline of existing components), or claiming a relocated signal is 'harder to remove' without defeating an adaptive adversary who searches the same new locus.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a relocated signal is 'stealthier' or 'harder to remove' without defeating an adaptive defender who searches the same new locus leaves the central claim unverified.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The contamination separation (step 7) is the adaptive adversary: a model is fine-tuned on a leaked instance transcript and the procedurally re-instantiated estimate is shown to resist exactly that leakage, so the robustness claim is tested against the relevant adversary rather than asserted."},{"lesson_quoted":"Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work — normalization statistics, activation-similarity losses, semantic concept triggers — collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The relocated locus (the evaluation UNIT, from a stored answer to an oracle-verified generator draw for multi-step agentic capability) is not the answer-bearing-static-benchmark locus DyePack/AntiLeakBench already operate on; differentiation_from_lit makes that difference explicit."},{"lesson_quoted":"A defense whose relocation silently depends on a clean reference model or a known anomaly distribution reintroduces precisely the strong assumption the move was supposed to eliminate.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The instrument depends only on the task generator and the randomized harness assignment, not on a clean reference model or a known anomaly distribution, so it does not smuggle the eliminated assumption back in."},{"lesson_quoted":"Demonstrating the new locus only on fixed, non-adaptive or outdated baselines while omitting any account of why it works reads as a stacked pipeline of existing components rather than a principled shift.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism supplies the mechanistic account (why the generator draw carries the signal: no stored answer exists to memorize, so contamination cannot inflate it) plus the factor-model identification argument, not a bare empirical pipeline."}],"verdict":"clear"}],"verdict":"clear","reasoning":"Both gap_closure entries are clear. The anchor (reframe_as_solvable_object / C00) avoids the mechanical-wrapper Reject lesson because the identifying signal is a designed interventional contrast with causal certification, not an off-the-shelf decomposition at a new granularity; the sibling (assumption_audit_and_pivot / C01) avoids the 'relocated signal never defeated against the adaptive adversary' lesson because the contamination separation directly fine-tunes on a leaked instance and shows the re-instantiated estimate resists it."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a capability estimate that is factorized into a model-attributable component and a harness-attributable component; every leaf reports a single marginal outcome rate that mixes the two, so when an agent solves a task the evaluation cannot say which factor produced the success.","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Recast an opaque transparency/attribution question about a fixed model as a concrete measurement over a well-studied object (an estimator / decomposition / influence score), buying tractability with one compression trick and certifying fidelity by a causal intervention that flips behavior when the identified object is perturbed, rather than by plausibility.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism recasts 'intrinsic model cyber-capability' as the coefficient theta_m of a logistic factor model y ~ Bernoulli(sigma(theta_m + h_c + d_t)) estimated over the designed run table (the well-studied object = a logistic/IRT-style estimator), fixes the unit of analysis as a matched randomized-perturbation run-pair (the C00 'fix the unit and faithfulness constraint' move), and certifies fidelity causally in step 6 (perturb the harness factor → predicted outcome shift Δh). The signature causal-certification + faithfulness-constraint move is present.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether the unit of evaluation must be a fixed answer-bearing challenge instance at all; every current agent-cyber leaf inherits from the static-benchmark ancestor the assumption that capability is measured by graded outcomes on pre-authored instances, which is exactly what makes contamination both possible and undetectable for multi-step tasks (openalex:W4416368190, openalex:W4416036350).","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"The audited assumption is always about the representational LOCUS at which a security/detection/provenance property is presumed to be enforced, and the move is to relocate to a different locus the field treated as irrelevant or invariant, showing the property manifests there more robustly (transformation-invariant).","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism (sibling leg) names the audited locus as the evaluation UNIT (a fixed pre-authored answer-bearing instance) and relocates it to a procedurally instantiated, oracle-verified generator draw, then shows the property of interest (capability) manifests there invariant to re-instantiation while the old locus inflates under contamination — the C01 'relocate the enforcement locus and show robustness at the new locus' move is performed, with the companion controlled_diagnostic_design supplying the confound-isolating separation.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries apply their cluster's signature move: C00's causal-certified measurement-over-a-well-studied-object (the logistic factor estimator certified by harness perturbation) and C01's locus relocation (evaluation unit from stored answer to oracle-verified generator draw) are each concretely instantiated in core_mechanism rather than enacting only the parent's generic gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["reframe_as_solvable_object","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; the candidate's composition set is {reframe_as_solvable_object, assumption_audit_and_pivot}, which contains no heterogeneous_decomposition, so no anti-pattern matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"openalex:W6980198985","threat_source":"lit_table","subsumption_argument":"Bayesian Inference of Capability Profiles for Machine Common Sense infers latent capability profiles from performance data via Bayesian item-response modeling, which is the structurally closest prior: if a reviewer reads the candidate as 'just IRT applied to cyber agents', the model-vs-harness factorization claim would lose its novelty. The candidate stands because that paper fits a single monolithic respondent's ability from observational static items and never introduces an interventional design that separates a model factor from a harness factor — the candidate's designed randomized-harness contrast (paired runs holding model and task fixed while randomizing the retriever/auto-prompter) is the additional identification structure that converts a confounded observational ability score into a harness-removed model-capability estimate, which the threat paper does not construct.","addressable_via":"Already addressed in core_mechanism_reasoning and what_step_was_missed by foregrounding the randomized-harness interventional contrast as the identifying construction the observational latent-trait fit lacks; Phase 4 should surface this as the lead reviewer concern."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Factorizing Agent Cyber-Capability: A Harness-Randomized Identification Instrument\n\n**Method.** Harness-Randomized Capability Identification (HRCI)\n\n## Motivation\nWhen people test how good an AI agent is at cybersecurity tasks, they usually report one number: the fraction of challenges it solved. The problem is that this number lumps together two very different things. One is how capable the underlying model actually is. The other is how good the surrounding 'harness' is — the search/knowledge tool that feeds the agent facts, the planner that breaks tasks into steps, and the prompt helper. CRAKEN (a 2025 cybersecurity agent) and HackSynth (a 2024 penetration-testing agent) both raised their solve-rate mainly by improving this harness, yet they reported the gain as a single solve-rate. So if one agent scores higher, you genuinely cannot tell whether its model is smarter or whether it just had a better-stocked toolbox.\n\nThere is a second problem. The challenge sets are public, so a model may have already seen them during training and simply memorized the answers, inflating the score. Recent work shows that detecting this 'contamination' on fixed answer-bearing tests is unreliable for strong reasoning models, and that automatically building fresh post-cutoff tasks is a better defense.\n\nWhat is newly possible is to combine two levers. First, modern agent harnesses are modular, so you can switch the search tool and prompt helper on and off as a controlled experiment. Second, you can generate each cyber task fresh from a template so there is no fixed answer to memorize. Putting these together lets us, for the first time, estimate the model's own capability separately from the harness, with an error bar, in a way that resists memorization. The payoff: a capability number that says how much credit goes to the model versus the toolbox, and that can be fairly compared across agents and new attack types.\n\n## Method\n### Contamination-resistant task unit\n*Replace fixed answer-bearing challenges with freshly generated, end-state-verified tasks so scores cannot be memorized.*\n\n1. Build 8-12 sandboxed cyber-task templates (forensic triage, web exploit, privilege escalation). Each template is a recipe that takes a random seed and generates a fresh task by randomizing the surface details: which ports and software versions are exposed, the usernames/passwords, and where the secret flag is hidden — and the flag itself is a fresh random 32-character string each time, so there is no fixed answer to memorize. Each template also ships an automatic checker that runs after the agent stops, looks only at the final state of the container (is the right file present and matching the expected flag, is the target process running, does the service return the expected token), and outputs success or failure. Judge purely by that final state, so reaching the goal by any route counts as success and partial progress counts as failure, and log the seed so any instance can be rebuilt exactly.\n   - _Why_: If every test is freshly generated and judged by the actual end-state, there is no fixed answer for a model to have memorized.\n2. Test resistance to memorization by faking a leak. Take one frozen task instance, assemble its full worked solution (the ordered sequence of actions, observations, and commands, plus the final flag) as a training example, and fine-tune one model on it with ordinary supervised fine-tuning (a few epochs, default 3, at a low learning rate) so it memorizes that one task without damaging its general skill — this mirrors how real contamination happens. Then compare two things: how that model now scores on the exact frozen task (this should jump, because it memorized it), versus its re-estimated capability number computed from freshly generated tasks (this should not move). If the frozen-task score jumps but the freshly-generated estimate stays put, the estimate has shrugged off the memorization that fools static tests.\n   - _Why_: If the frozen-task score jumps but $\\hat{\\theta }_{m}$ does not, the freshly-generated estimate has shrugged off the memorization that fools static tests.\n\n### Randomized harness contrast\n*Turn the harness on and off under randomization so its contribution becomes an observable factor.*\n\n3. Pin down exactly two harness setups in advance. The full setup is a knowledge retriever (a graph-plus-vector search that feeds the agent relevant facts), a planner-executor that breaks the task into steps, and a prompt helper that rewrites prompts (this mirrors the CRAKEN cybersecurity agent). The ablated setup is the same planner-executor but with the retriever and prompt helper switched off, so the base model plans and acts on its own. Keep everything else identical between the two — same tools, same action interface, same limit on number of steps — so the only thing that changes is whether the knowledge/prompt channel is present.\n   - _Why_: Turning the harness on and off in a controlled way is what lets us see how much the harness, rather than the model, contributes.\n4. For each model in your panel of K models and each freshly generated task, run BOTH harness setups — and repeat each setup a few times (default 3) with different random decoding seeds to average out the agent's randomness. Draw a new task instance per model-task cell, and make sure that within each cell the same task content is faced by both the full and the ablated harness. Record every run as a row holding the model, the task, which harness was used, the seed, the success/failure outcome, and the full action trace. Running both harnesses on the very same task content inside each cell is exactly what lets us later separate the model's share from the harness's share.\n   - _Why_: Randomizing which runs got the harness inside each model-task cell is what makes the model's share and the harness's share separable later.\n\n### Factorized capability estimator\n*Fit a logistic factor model that separates the model factor from the harness factor, and certify and validate the estimate.*\n\n5. Fit a logistic model that splits each success/failure into three additive pieces on the log-odds scale: a model factor (one number per model), a harness factor (how much the full harness adds over the ablated one), and a task-difficulty term (one per task). To make the numbers uniquely defined, set the ablated harness's factor to zero so the harness factor reads directly as 'how much the full harness helps', and center the task-difficulty terms so they average to zero; the model factor then sits on a fixed scale. Put a mild, weakly-informative bell-curve prior on the model and harness factors (it gently pulls them toward zero so sparse data does not produce wild estimates), and let the task-difficulty terms share strength through a common spread. Fit it with a standard modern Bayesian sampler (the No-U-Turn Sampler, an automatic Hamiltonian Monte Carlo method), run several chains, and check they agree. Read out the model-capability estimate for each model together with its error interval; if you only need a point estimate, the equivalent penalized maximum-likelihood fit is a drop-in fallback.\n\n*Each agent run's binary outcome is a logistic function of a model factor $\\theta _{m}, a$ harness factor $h_{c},$ and a task-difficulty offset $d_{t}.$*\n$$ y(m,t,c) \\sim \\mathrm{Bernoulli}\\!\\left(\\sigma(\\theta_m + h_c + d_t)\\right),\\quad \\sigma(z)=\\frac{1}{1+e^{-z}} \\tag{1} $$\n\n\n*The model-capability estimate $\\hat{\\theta }_{m}$ is the penalized maximum-likelihood (or posterior-mean) coefficient under a weakly-informative prior of scale $\\lambda _{prior} = 1.0$ on the logit scale.*\n$$ \\hat{\\theta}_m = \\arg\\max_{\\theta_m}\\; \\mathbb{P}(\\{y\\}\\mid \\theta_m,h_c,d_t) - \\tfrac{1}{2\\lambda_{\\text{prior}}^2}\\,\\theta_m^2 \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Estimating $\\theta _{m}$ as a coefficient — not a raw average — gives the model's own capability with uncertainty, separate from the toolbox.\n6. Check that the harness factor really causes outcomes, on a fresh held-out set of tasks. Keep each model fixed and swap its full harness for the ablated one, and measure the actual drop in success rate. Compare that actual drop to the drop your fitted model predicts from its estimated harness factor (converted from the log-odds scale to a plain probability drop). The swap genuinely changes things because removing the retriever changes which commands the agent issues, which changes the final graded state. Count the harness factor as certified only if the actual drop matches the predicted drop in size — within the model's own uncertainty band — not merely that both go down.\n\n*The harness-attributable contribution is the difference between the full-harness and ablated-harness factors, identified from the within-cell randomized perturbation.*\n$$ \\Delta h = h_{\\text{full}} - h_{\\text{ablated}} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: If the estimated harness factor really causes outcomes, deleting it should move the result by exactly that much — a causal check, not just a fit.\n7. Finally, check which capability number ranks the models more correctly. Get a trusted, independent ranking of the K models from a separate set of cyber tasks that the models could not have seen — for example a fresh batch of human-solved challenges authored after the models' training cutoff, or an expert consensus difficulty rating. 【author decision: how this trusted ranking is obtained — a fresh human-solved held-out challenge batch versus an expert consensus rating, and whether it is a full or only partial ordering — is a measurement-design choice the authors must make, because it defines the 'true capability' the estimate is checked against.】 Then measure, with a standard rank-agreement statistic (Kendall's tau-b), how well the model-capability estimate orders the models against that trusted ranking, and how well the plain solve-rate does. The headline result is that the estimate agrees with the trusted ranking better than the plain solve-rate does; gauge whether the gap is real by resampling tasks and seeds.\n   - _Why_: The better the estimate matches a trusted ranking, the more it is measuring real capability rather than toolbox or memorization.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 解构智能体网络安全能力：一种基于 harness 随机化的辨识测量工具\n\n**方法名称.** Harness-Randomized Capability Identification (HRCI)\n\n## 研究动机\n人们评估一个 AI 智能体在网络安全任务上的能力时，通常只报一个数字：它解决了多少比例的挑战。问题在于，这个数字把两件完全不同的事混在了一起。一件是底层模型本身有多强；另一件是外围 harness 有多好——也就是给智能体喂事实的检索/知识工具、把任务拆成步骤的 planner，以及提示助手。CRAKEN（2025 年的网络安全智能体）和 HackSynth（2024 年的渗透测试智能体）主要靠改进这个 harness 来提高解题率，却把收益报成一个单一的解题率。于是当某个智能体得分更高时，你根本分不清是它的模型更聪明，还是它只是有一个储备更充足的工具箱。\n\n还有第二个问题：这些挑战集是公开的，模型在训练时可能已经见过并记住了答案，从而虚高分数。最近的研究表明，在固定的、带答案的测试上检测这种「污染」对强推理模型并不可靠，而自动构造训练截止之后的新任务是更好的防御。\n\n现在新出现的可能性是把两个杠杆结合起来。第一，现代智能体 harness 是模块化的，可以像做对照实验一样把检索工具和提示助手开关切换。第二，可以从模板现场生成每个网络安全任务，使其没有可被记住的固定答案。把二者结合，我们就能首次把模型自身能力与 harness 贡献分开估计，并带误差区间，同时抵抗记忆作弊。回报是：一个能说明「功劳多少归模型、多少归工具箱」的能力数字，并且可以在不同智能体和新型攻击面之间公平比较。\n\n## 方法\n### 抗污染的任务单元\n*用现场生成、按最终状态判定的任务取代固定带答案的挑战，使分数无法被记忆。*\n\n1. 构建 8-12 个沙箱化的网络安全任务模板（取证排查、Web 漏洞利用、提权）。每个模板是一份配方：给定一个随机种子，就生成一个全新任务，随机化表层细节——暴露哪些端口、软件版本，用户名/密码，以及秘密 flag 藏在哪；而且 flag 本身每次都是一个新随机的 32 位字符串，因此没有可被记忆的固定答案。每个模板还附带一个自动判定器：在智能体停止后运行，只读取容器的最终状态（目标文件是否存在且与预期 flag 匹配、目标进程是否在运行、服务是否返回预期 token），输出成功或失败。完全按最终状态判分，因此用任何路径达成目标都算成功，部分进展算失败；并记录种子，使任何实例都能被精确重建。\n   - _为什么_: 如果每个测试都是现场生成、并按真实最终状态判分，就没有固定答案可供模型记忆。\n2. 通过伪造泄漏来测试抗记忆能力。取一个冻结的任务实例，把它的完整解题过程（有序的动作、观察、命令序列，加上最终 flag）拼成一个训练样本，用普通的监督微调(Supervised Fine-Tuning, SFT)在它上面微调某个模型（几个 epoch，默认 3 个，低学习率），让它记住这一个任务而不损害其通用能力——这模拟了真实污染的发生方式。然后比较两件事：该模型现在在这个冻结任务上的得分（应当飙升，因为它记住了），与从新生成任务重新估计出的能力数字（应当不动）。如果冻结任务得分飙升而新生成的估计纹丝不动，说明这个估计已经摆脱了能骗过静态测试的记忆作弊。\n   - _为什么_: 如果冻结任务得分飙升而 $\\hat{\\theta }_{m}$ 不动，说明现场生成的估计已经摆脱了能骗过静态测试的记忆作弊。\n\n### 随机化 harness 对照\n*在随机化下开关 harness，使其贡献成为可观测的因子。*\n\n3. 事先固定恰好两种 harness 配置。完整版包含一个知识检索器（图加向量检索，给智能体喂相关事实）、一个把任务拆成步骤的 planner-executor，以及一个改写提示词的提示助手（对标 CRAKEN 网络安全智能体）。消融版是同样的 planner-executor，但关掉检索器和提示助手，让底层模型自己规划和行动。两者其余部分完全一致——相同工具、相同动作接口、相同步数上限——使得唯一变化就是知识/提示通道是否存在。\n   - _为什么_: 以受控方式开关 harness，才能看清贡献到底有多少来自 harness 而非模型本身。\n4. 对面板中 K 个模型的每一个、以及每个新生成的任务，都运行两种 harness 配置——并对每种配置用不同的随机解码种子重复几次（默认 3 次）以平均掉智能体的随机性。每个「模型-任务」单元抽一个新任务实例，并确保在每个单元内，完整 harness 和消融 harness 面对的是同一份任务内容。把每次运行记录为一行：模型、任务、用的哪种 harness、种子、成败结果，以及完整动作轨迹。在每个单元内让两种 harness 跑同一份任务内容，正是后面能把模型份额与 harness 份额分开的关键。\n   - _为什么_: 在每个「模型-任务」单元内随机化哪些运行用了 harness，正是后面能把模型份额与 harness 份额分开的关键。\n\n### 因子化能力估计器\n*拟合 logistic 因子模型把模型因子与 harness 因子分离，并对估计进行因果认证与验证。*\n\n5. 拟合一个 logistic 模型，把每个成败结果在对数几率(log-odds)尺度上拆成三个相加的部分：模型因子（每个模型一个数）、harness 因子（完整 harness 相比消融版多带来多少）、任务难度项（每个任务一个）。为了让这些数唯一确定，把消融 harness 的因子设为零，这样 harness 因子就直接读作「完整 harness 帮了多少」，并把任务难度项中心化使其平均为零；模型因子由此落在固定尺度上。给模型因子和 harness 因子各加一个温和的弱信息钟形先验（轻轻把它们拉向零，使数据稀疏时不至于给出离谱估计），并让任务难度项通过一个公共离散度互相借力。用一个标准的现代贝叶斯采样器拟合（No-U-Turn Sampler，一种自动的哈密顿蒙特卡洛(Hamiltonian Monte Carlo)方法），跑多条链并检查它们是否一致。读出每个模型的能力估计连同其误差区间；若只需点估计，等价的惩罚极大似然拟合可直接替代。\n\n*每次智能体运行的二元结果服从 logistic 模型，由模型因子 $\\theta _{m}$、harness 因子 $h_{c}$ 与任务难度偏置 $d_{t}$ 共同决定。*\n$$ y(m,t,c) \\sim \\mathrm{Bernoulli}\\!\\left(\\sigma(\\theta_m + h_c + d_t)\\right),\\quad \\sigma(z)=\\frac{1}{1+e^{-z}} \\tag{1} $$\n\n\n*模型能力估计 $\\hat{\\theta }_{m}$ 是在 logit 尺度上以弱信息先验（尺度 $\\lambda _{prior} = 1.0$）做惩罚极大似然（或后验均值）得到的系数。*\n$$ \\hat{\\theta}_m = \\arg\\max_{\\theta_m}\\; \\mathbb{P}(\\{y\\}\\mid \\theta_m,h_c,d_t) - \\tfrac{1}{2\\lambda_{\\text{prior}}^2}\\,\\theta_m^2 \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 把 $\\theta _{m}$ 作为系数来估计（而非原始平均值），能给出与工具箱分离、且带不确定性的模型自身能力。\n6. 在一批新的留出任务上，检验 harness 因子是否真的导致结果。保持每个模型不变，把它的完整 harness 换成消融版，测量成功率的实际下降。把这个实际下降与你拟合模型依据其估计的 harness 因子所预测的下降作比较（从对数几率尺度换算成普通概率上的下降）。这次切换确实会改变结果，因为去掉检索器会改变智能体发出的命令，从而改变被判分的最终状态。只有当实际下降在量级上与预测下降相符——落在模型自身的不确定性带内——才算 harness 因子通过认证，而不只是两者都下降。\n\n*harness 的贡献量 $\\Delta h$ 是完整 harness 与消融 harness 两个因子之差，由单元内随机扰动辨识得到。*\n$$ \\Delta h = h_{\\text{full}} - h_{\\text{ablated}} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 如果估计出的 harness 因子真的导致了结果，删掉它就应让结果正好移动那么多——这是因果检验而非单纯拟合。\n7. 最后，检验哪个能力数字对模型排序得更准。从一组模型不可能见过的、独立的网络安全任务上，取得对 K 个模型的可信排名——例如在模型训练截止之后新编写、由人类解出的一批挑战，或专家共识的难度评定。【作者需决定：这个可信排名如何获得——是用一批新的、人类解出的留出挑战，还是用专家共识评定，以及它是完整排序还是仅部分排序——这是作者必须做的测量设计选择，因为它定义了用来检验估计的「真实能力」。】然后用一个标准的排名一致性统计量(Kendall's tau-b，肯德尔 tau-b 秩相关)，衡量模型能力估计相对该可信排名排得多准，以及普通解题率排得多准。核心结果是：能力估计与可信排名的吻合度高于普通解题率；通过对任务和种子重采样来判断这一差距是否真实。\n   - _为什么_: 估计越贴近可信排名，越说明它衡量的是真实能力，而非工具箱或记忆。\n\n"},{"id":"21","run_dir":"run_prompt21_protein","index":21,"title":"Per-Residue Minimal Step Budgets for Validity-Gated SE(3) Protein Generation","title_zh":"面向 SE(3) 蛋白质结构生成的逐残基最小步数预算与有效性门控采样","method_name":"Validity-Gated Per-Residue Sampling (VGPR)","hook":"Across SE(3) flow-matching protein generators the integration-step count is a single global number tuned for sample-distribution fidelity, yet most residue frames provably reach a stereochemically valid pose long before the global budget ends; we characterize the per-residue minimal valid-step budget as a separation criterion and build a sampler that lets each residue exit the trajectory the moment it crosses that budget. This concentrates sequential network evaluations only on the residues whose geometry is still uncertain, cutting wall-clock without trading away backbone validity.","anchor_pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","anchor_pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","domain_category":"Healthcare & Scientific ML","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved generator characterizes the MINIMAL number of sequential SE(3) network evaluations that still yields a stereochemically valid, chirality-correct backbone for a given target, rather than a fixed step count chosen for sample-distribution fidelity (openalex:W4408293717, openalex:W4402939815): the failure is that latency is set by a single global step budget that no leaf has shown to be tight against a validity threshold rather than a distributional one.","pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","companion_pattern":"architectural_operator_substitution","how_closed":"Closed by formalizing the per-residue minimal valid-step budget tau_i as a separation criterion on the native SE(3) trajectory (a truncated per-residue trajectory below tau_i provably fails an explicit backbone-validity certificate of bond-length / bond-angle / chirality / clash tolerances), which the global-step-count framing structurally discards; the companion architectural_operator_substitution then ships the runnable deliverable by substituting the fixed global integrator with a per-residue validity-gated early-exit operator proven to attain that budget.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf lets the sequential-evaluation cost vary with how structurally hard a region or target is — an easy loop and a strained rare conformation pay the identical many-step price (openalex:W4408293717, openalex:W4402939815), so there is no mechanism by which compute concentrates where geometry is actually uncertain and drains away where it is already determined.","pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by partitioning the sampling trajectory's residue set at each step by a measured per-residue convergence property (the running disagreement of the learned velocity field across recent steps), retaining-at-full-step-budget the still-uncertain minority while freezing the converged bulk, with an error decomposition bounding how this differentiated per-residue treatment recovers the full-step terminal distribution.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"generative models for protein 3D structure (backbone / all-atom / conformational ensembles)","n_papers":39,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":25},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":20,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Enhancing Protein Structure Generation Through Deep Learning Techniques"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Deep-learning-based prediction framework for protein-peptide interactions with structure generation pipeline"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Integrating Deep Learning with Structural Bioinformatics using Next-Generation Protein Stability Prediction"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"TopoQA: a topological deep learning-based approach for protein complex structure interface quality assessment"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Antibody design using deep learning: from sequence and structure design to affinity maturation"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Towards deep learning sequence-structure co-generation for protein design"}],"more":14},{"year":2025,"n":18,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Incorporating targeted protein structure in deep learning methods for molecule generation in computational drug design"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Toward deep learning sequence-structure co-generation for protein design."},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Deep learning-driven protein structure prediction and design: Key model developments by Nobel laureates and multi-domain applications"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Advanced Deep Learning Methods for Protein Structure Prediction and Design"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A hybrid variational autoencoder and WGAN with gradient penalty for tertiary protein structure generation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"BPS2025 – Deep-learning approaches for protein dynamics extraction from cryo-EM maps and structure-based de novo molecular generation"}],"more":12},{"year":2026,"n":1,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"}],"more":0}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":9,"share":0.231},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":7,"share":0.179},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":4,"share":0.103},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":4,"share":0.103},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":4,"share":0.103},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":3,"share":0.077},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":3,"share":0.077},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":3,"share":0.077}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Recent protein-structure generators are dominated by iterative denoising over the SE(3) manifold of residue frames: SE(3) flow-matching ensemble models (openalex:W4408293717) and structural diffusion conformation samplers (openalex:W4402939815) both produce one structure only after integrating an ordinary/stochastic differential equation through hundreds of sequential evaluations of an equivariant network, and SCUBA-D (openalex:W4403836806) shows the same many-step generation cost is what bounds throughput for high-quality de novo backbones. The wall-clock to emit a sample is therefore set by the product of (number of integration steps) and (per-step cost of an SE(3)-equivariant network evaluated on every residue pair), and neither factor can currently be reduced without the generated geometry degrading — few-step image-diffusion accelerators that optimize the time-step schedule (openalex:W4402727162) or dynamically allocate sampling budget (openalex:W4416251124) are derived for Euclidean pixel manifolds and carry no guarantee that the truncated trajectory still lands on a physically valid, chirality-correct backbone, so applying them off-the-shelf trades steps for stereochemical violations. The result is that across both de novo design (openalex:W4403836806) and conformational-ensemble emulation (openalex:W4412165572, openalex:W4408293717), per-sample latency scales with a step count chosen for distributional fidelity on the manifold rather than for the geometry actually needed, and there is no characterization of how few sequential SE(3) evaluations suffice before backbone validity, not just sample-distribution distance, collapses.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4408293717","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"P2DFlow casts protein conformational-ensemble generation as SE(3) flow matching, learning a continuous-time velocity field on the manifold of residue frames and integrating it with a multi-step ODE solver to draw each ensemble member. Its residue is that the number of integration steps is treated as a fixed solver hyperparameter tuned for ensemble fidelity, with no characterization of the minimal step budget per target nor any geometry-aware mechanism that lets a structurally easy region finish in fewer evaluations than a hard one. [residue is abstract-level: anchor fulltext unfetchable]"},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4402939815","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Accurate Conformation Sampling via Protein Structural Diffusion learns a diffusion process over backbone geometry to sample multiple stable conformations of a protein. It does not reduce the sequential-evaluation count and offers no per-region or per-target adaptivity, so rare/strained states and easy loops pay the same fixed many-step sampling cost."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4403836806","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"SCUBA-D trains a fresh diffusion model that generates high-quality de novo backbones, prioritizing designability and diversity. It leaves sampling latency untouched: high quality is obtained precisely by keeping the full many-step reverse trajectory, with no analysis of how validity degrades as steps are cut."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4402727162","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Accelerating Diffusion Sampling with Optimized Time Steps learns/optimizes a non-uniform time-step schedule so a high-order ODE solver needs fewer steps, demonstrated on image synthesis. Its residue is that the optimization criterion is image-distribution distance on a Euclidean manifold; it carries no notion of SE(3) geometry or backbone stereochemical validity, so the schedule it finds gives no guarantee the truncated protein trajectory stays a valid chain."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"generative models for protein 3D structure (backbone / all-atom / conformational ensembles)","venue":"ICLR/ICML/NeurIPS (ML) or Nature Methods / J Chem Theory Comput (domain)","time":"2026 submission cycle","data":["PDB (experimental structures)","AlphaFold DB / ESM Atlas (predicted structures)","short MD trajectories for ensemble targets (e.g. ATLAS, mdCATH)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with cloud access; geometric deep learning + diffusion/flow background assumed","preference":"both","baseline":"SE(3) diffusion / SE(3) flow-matching backbone generators (e.g. SCUBA-D, P2DFlow, structural diffusion conformation samplers) using many-step ODE/SDE integration","limitation":"sampling a single protein structure requires hundreds of sequential network evaluations over the SE(3) manifold, so wall-clock per sample is dominated by integration-step count and the per-step equivariant network cost","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object every leg reads from and writes to is the SE(3) flow-matching sampling trajectory {X(t)}_{t in [0,1]} of N residue frames X_i(t) in SE(3) (each a rotation R_i in SO(3) plus translation x_i in R^3), generated by integrating a learned, pretrained velocity field v_theta(X,t) (we do NOT retrain it) from prior noise at t=0 to a structure at t=1; the central quantity is the per-residue minimal valid-step budget tau_i and its online estimator. LEG 1 (characterize, C10 + companion). The structural object the global fixed-step framing discards is each residue's own convergence time: define a backbone-validity certificate V(X) = 1 iff every C-N bond length, every backbone bond angle, every CA chirality sign, and every inter-residue clash lies within fixed tolerances (tolerances taken from standard stereochemistry, listed as constants; this is the same physical-validity notion SCUBA-D openalex:W4403836806 reports post-hoc). For residue i define tau_i = the smallest number of remaining integration steps after which residue i's frame, if it stopped being updated (frozen) while the rest of the trajectory completes, still yields V=1 locally for residue i and its bonded neighbors. The separation criterion: a per-residue truncation that freezes residue i before step (global_total - tau_i) provably moves X_i across a validity tolerance (we exhibit, for a strained loop residue, two terminal structures the GLOBAL-step view conflates — one valid, one clashing — that differ only in whether residue i received its last tau_i updates), so a single global budget cannot be tight for all residues simultaneously: it is either wasteful for the converged majority or invalid for the slow minority. The companion (architectural_operator_substitution) replaces the fixed integrator's uniform per-step update with a gated operator: at each step the operator updates only residues whose online budget estimate has not yet been reached and freezes the rest, ablating quadratic all-pairs velocity evaluations down to (active residues) x (all residues) per step. LEG 2 (heterogeneous_decomposition, C04). tau_i is not known a priori, so we estimate it online by a measured per-residue convergence property: d_i(t) = the geodesic SE(3) distance between residue i's predicted endpoint extrapolated at step t and at step t-1 (i.e. how much the velocity field still wants to move residue i); residues split into a converged bulk (d_i below a learned threshold eps for K consecutive steps) and an uncertain minority (still above eps). The differentiated treatment: freeze the bulk (no further v_theta evaluation for those frames), keep integrating the minority at full per-step resolution. The error decomposition that is the spine of the contribution bounds the terminal deviation: ||X_freeze(1) - X_full(1)|| <= sum_{i frozen at t_i} integral_{t_i}^{1} ||v_theta(X_i,s)|| ds, and freezing only when d_i < eps caps each integrand term, so total terminal error is bounded by N x eps x (remaining horizon) — the bound ties the speedup (fewer active evaluations) directly to a controllable validity/fidelity loss, which is exactly what a uniform global step count cannot express. eps and K are the only new hyperparameters; v_theta is frozen, so the method is a sampling-time wrapper around ANY pretrained SE(3) flow/diffusion backbone.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The two gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules: both act on the same object (the SE(3) trajectory) and the same scalar (the per-residue budget tau_i) — Leg 1 characterizes tau_i and proves a global budget cannot be tight, Leg 2 supplies the online estimator and the error bound that makes freezing-by-convergence a faithful realization of per-residue budgets; the convergence indicator d_i IS the operational proxy for tau_i, so a single coherent mechanism closes both. Alternatives considered and rejected: (a) distilling a few-step student (consistency-style) — rejected as a regression to collateral node c2, since it bakes in one global step budget and a Euclidean recipe rather than per-residue SE(3) validity; (b) learning a better global timestep schedule (DPM-Solver-style, node c1) — rejected for the same regression reason and because it still pays uniform per-residue cost. We deliberately keep v_theta frozen and act only at sampling time so the avoided node is the integrator-numerics family the lineage flags as occupied.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on a pretrained SE(3) flow-matching backbone, sample de novo backbones and short-protein conformational ensembles with the full global-step sampler versus our validity-gated sampler, holding v_theta fixed; measure total sequential SE(3) network evaluations, wall-clock per sample, and the backbone-validity rate (fraction of generated structures passing the bond-length/angle/chirality/clash certificate). If the candidate works, total sequential evaluations and wall-clock per sample DECREASE substantially while backbone-validity rate stays at the full-step baseline level (does not drop) and distributional metrics (ensemble coverage / designability) stay within baseline variance. The load-bearing variable is the per-residue convergence indicator d_i(t): the mechanism claims that low d_i identifies residues that can be frozen without losing validity. Negative control: replace the d_i-driven freeze decision with a RANDOM per-residue freeze schedule matched to the same average freeze rate; if d_i is the mechanism, this control should drive the downstream backbone-validity rate back DOWN toward the broken-structure regime (the task-outcome metric collapses), whereas if mere reduction of compute were responsible, random freezing at equal rate would preserve validity — distinguishing a genuine geometry-aware budget from generic step reduction. A positive control (freeze solely on d_i < eps, no other components) is expected to recover most of the speedup at baseline validity, identifying d_i as the sufficient driver.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4408293717","delta":"P2DFlow integrates its SE(3) velocity field with a single global step count tuned for ensemble fidelity; we construct a per-residue minimal valid-step budget tau_i, prove a global budget cannot be tight against backbone validity for all residues at once, and supply an online d_i estimator with a terminal-error bound that makes per-residue early exit faithful — quantities their fixed-step sampler does not define."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4402939815","delta":"The structural-diffusion conformation sampler pays the same many-step cost for every conformation; we measure and exploit the per-residue convergence-time heterogeneity to concentrate sequential evaluations on uncertain frames, a per-region adaptivity their uniform sampler has no mechanism for."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4402727162","delta":"Optimized-time-step sampling minimizes Euclidean image-distribution distance over a non-uniform GLOBAL schedule; we replace the distributional criterion with an SE(3) backbone-validity certificate and make the budget per-residue rather than global, so the truncation carries a stereochemical-validity guarantee their schedule does not."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4403836806","delta":"SCUBA-D reports physical validity only post-hoc on full-trajectory samples; we turn that same validity notion into an in-the-loop separation criterion that decides, per residue and online, when integration can stop without violating it."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4408293717","what_step_was_missed":"P2DFlow established SE(3) flow matching with a global ODE step count, but it never constructed a per-residue stopping criterion: realizing per-residue early exit requires (a) defining tau_i as the residue-local minimal step budget against an explicit backbone-validity certificate and proving a single global count cannot be tight for all residues, and (b) a terminal-error decomposition that bounds the deviation when a residue is frozen once its velocity-field disagreement d_i falls below threshold — neither the residue-local budget nor the freeze-error bound is present in their fixed-step integration."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":267,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"No hard-floor rule fired: gap_closure_reject_check is borderline (not triggered), recipe_application_check is applied for both entries, and anti_pattern_check matched audit_decomp_operator but mitigation_substantively_delivered=true via the positive/negative controls. The decisive borderline is load-bearing: paper_pointed_threat (Jano) has a concrete addressable_via (add a differentiation_from_lit entry naming the SE(3)-validity-certificate delta vs region-adaptive Euclidean samplers), and the C04 reject lesson 'Presenting a sensitivity or redundancy proxy as the novelty... unless it is sharply differentiated' asks that d_i's binding to the validity certificate be foregrounded — both are field-level tactical fixes, so revise rather than advance.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved generator characterizes the MINIMAL number of sequential SE(3) network evaluations that still yields a stereochemically valid, chirality-correct backbone for a given target, rather than a fixed step count chosen for sample-distribution fidelity (openalex:W4408293717, openalex:W4402939815): the failure is that latency is set by a single global step budget that no leaf has shown to be tight against a validity threshold rather than a distributional one.","main_pattern":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail when the 'limit' they characterize is not a genuine structural blindspot: it is either trivially implied by the model's own assumptions, already surpassed by a published method, or never formalized at all beyond an informal analogy. A recurring shape substitutes a hand-wavy mechanism for a separation proof.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Resting the central claim on an informal analogy (two operators 'both smooth high frequencies') instead of a separation proof leaves the mechanism underspecified and the empirical gain unconvincing.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism gives an explicit separation: it exhibits two terminal structures the global-step view conflates (one valid, one clashing) differing only in whether residue i received its last tau_i updates, plus a validity certificate V(X) — a formal criterion, not an analogy."},{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a 'maximally expressive' construction that a recently published method already strictly subsumes turns the surpass-the-limit claim into redundant work.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"collision_hits contains Jano (region-level heterogeneous convergence awareness for Diffusion Transformers) and Region-Adaptive Sampling for Diffusion Transformers, which adapt compute by spatial region — but both are image/DiT, Euclidean, and have no SE(3) per-residue budget nor stereochemical-validity certificate, so they do not subsume the protein-geometry separation criterion; the angle must be defended explicitly."},{"lesson_quoted":"Asserting the 'first efficient implementation' of a long-known algorithm without surveying the landscape invites direct refutation by existing faster implementations and collapses the novelty claim.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate does not claim a first-efficient-implementation of a known algorithm; it constructs a new per-residue budget object and a freeze-error bound, and the differentiation_from_lit surveys the integrator-numerics frontier (W4402727162) it must beat."},{"lesson_quoted":"Deriving a 'limitation' that is trivially implied by the model's own linearity assumption produces a limit too weak to count as a real blindspot, and the proposed surpass step stays under-validated.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The per-residue minimal valid-step budget is not implied by the generator's assumptions — the fixed-global-step framing structurally cannot express it; the offline tau_i logging (step 3) is the empirical evidence the budget genuinely varies across residues."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf lets the sequential-evaluation cost vary with how structurally hard a region or target is — an easy loop and a strained rare conformation pay the identical many-step price (openalex:W4408293717, openalex:W4402939815), so there is no mechanism by which compute concentrates where geometry is actually uncertain and drains away where it is already determined.","main_pattern":"heterogeneous_decomposition","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is treating the partition criterion itself as the contribution while leaving its value unproven — reviewers map the discriminator onto an established technique so the differentiated treatment reads as a relabeling, and it is rarely benchmarked against both the strongest uniform baseline and the obvious cheap alternative, or it is validated where the bottleneck does not bite.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Presenting a sensitivity or redundancy proxy as the novelty invites the verdict that it rediscovers known mixed-precision or low-rank results unless it is sharply differentiated from the obvious prior criterion.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The partition criterion d_i (per-residue velocity-field disagreement) resembles generic convergence/uncertainty heuristics; differentiation rests on it being tied to the SE(3) validity certificate and the freeze-error bound rather than presented as the contribution by itself, which must be made explicit."},{"lesson_quoted":"Omitting comparison against both the strongest uniform baseline and the obvious cheap alternative (SVD/PCA, structured dropout, a natively trained smaller model) leaves reviewers unable to tell whether the partition buys anything at all.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism_steps step 8 benchmarks against (i) full global-step baseline (strongest uniform) and (ii) optimized-global-schedule baseline (the obvious cheap alternative, DPM-Solver-style), satisfying both required comparators."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a storage or throughput claim only on toy-scale models — where the compression bottleneck does not actually bite — undermines the entire motivation no matter how clean the method is.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The regime where latency bites (many-step SE(3) generation of full backbones / ensembles) is exactly the validation regime, and the reported metric is real wall-clock and total sequential evaluations, not a proxy."},{"lesson_quoted":"Skipping any analysis of why the heterogeneity exists — the data or value distribution that drives the partition — makes the technical novelty and the potential impact impossible to assess.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"step 3 logs the empirical tau_i distribution across residues precisely to demonstrate the heterogeneity that forces the partition, making the value distribution a load-bearing piece of evidence."},{"lesson_quoted":"A clever partition with no measured real-world deployment metric (no inference latency or memory speedup) reads as a proxy-only contribution and stalls at borderline.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"wall-clock per sample and total sequential SE(3) evaluations are the primary reported metrics in falsification_prediction and step 8."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No entry is triggered. The heterogeneous_decomposition (C04) entry drives the aggregate borderline via 'Presenting a sensitivity or redundancy proxy as the novelty invites the verdict that it rediscovers known... results' — d_i could read as a generic convergence heuristic unless its binding to the SE(3) validity certificate and freeze-error bound is foregrounded; the C10 entry is borderline only on the prior-art-subsumption lesson because of image-domain region-adaptive samplers in collision_hits that do not reach SE(3)/validity."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved generator characterizes the MINIMAL number of sequential SE(3) network evaluations that still yields a stereochemically valid, chirality-correct backbone for a given target, rather than a fixed step count chosen for sample-distribution fidelity (openalex:W4408293717, openalex:W4402939815): the failure is that latency is set by a single global step budget that no leaf has shown to be tight against a validity threshold rather than a distributional one.","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Take an iterative locally-scoped procedure, pinpoint the one structural object it discards for tractability, formalize the equivalence class this discarding induces as a separation/indistinguishability criterion on the procedure's native objects, then re-inject that exact object into the procedure's core step and prove the augmented operator strictly exceeds the criterion at bounded cost.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism performs exactly this: the discarded object is each residue's own convergence time tau_i (thrown away by the global-step count); the separation criterion is stated on the native SE(3) trajectory (a truncation freezing residue i before global_total - tau_i provably crosses a validity tolerance, with an exhibited conflated valid/clashing pair); the re-injection is the gated integrator that makes the per-residue budget first-class in the core update step; and the cost bound (active x all residues per step, plus the terminal-error bound N x eps x horizon) is the bounded-cost requirement.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf lets the sequential-evaluation cost vary with how structurally hard a region or target is — an easy loop and a strained rare conformation pay the identical many-step price (openalex:W4408293717, openalex:W4402939815), so there is no mechanism by which compute concentrates where geometry is actually uncertain and drains away where it is already determined.","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Compress an over-provisioned trained artifact (here the sampling trajectory) by exploiting heterogeneity rather than a uniform operation: discriminate components into a high-impact minority and a near-redundant bulk by a sensitivity/redundancy criterion, treat each differently, and supply an error/sensitivity decomposition that bounds how the differentiated treatment recovers the original objective — that analysis, not the partition idea, is the contribution.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism partitions the trajectory's residue set each step into a converged bulk (d_i below eps for K steps, frozen) and an uncertain minority (kept at full step resolution), and supplies the spine error decomposition ||X_freeze(1)-X_full(1)|| <= sum integral ||v_theta|| ds bounded by N x eps x horizon — the required error-bound artifact, not merely a partition heuristic.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries perform their cluster's distinctive move: C10's discard-formalize-reinject-bound chain is fully instantiated on the SE(3) trajectory, and C04's load-bearing error decomposition (not just the partition) is present as the contribution spine."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["characterize_limit_then_surpass","heterogeneous_decomposition","architectural_operator_substitution"],"matched_pattern_id":"audit_decomp_operator","required_mitigation_quoted":"The operator's expressivity gain must be demonstrated on homogeneous data (where decomposition is unnecessary), and the decomposition's separate effect must be demonstrated on heterogeneous data with the operator held fixed. Each leg's contribution must be independently identifiable.","mitigation_substantively_delivered":"true","reasoning":"The two legs are independently identifiable in core_mechanism: the positive control (freeze-on-d_i only, no other machinery) isolates the decomposition's effect with the gated operator held to its simplest form, and the negative control (random freeze at matched rate) holds the operator/freeze-rate fixed while removing the decomposition signal — these are exactly the operator-held-fixed-vary-decomposition and decomposition-isolated comparisons the mitigation demands, delivered at the artifact level rather than as framing."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"Jano: Adaptive Diffusion Generation with Early-stage Convergence Awareness","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"Jano is the closest competitor: it also observes that different regions of generated content exhibit heterogeneous convergence patterns and accelerates by exploiting that, which overlaps the candidate's core observation that residues converge at different times. However, Jano targets Diffusion Transformers on (image/latent) content where the early-exit decision is content-agnostic-region-based on a Euclidean manifold and the stopping signal is tied to no validity guarantee; the candidate's claim stands or falls on two objects Jano does not construct — a per-residue minimal valid-step budget defined against an explicit SE(3) backbone-validity certificate (bond/angle/chirality/clash), and a terminal-error bound tying the per-residue freeze decision to recovered stereochemical validity. If Jano's convergence-awareness already transferred to SE(3) with a validity certificate the candidate would be subsumed, but it does not — so the candidate survives as the SE(3)/validity-grounded instantiation.","addressable_via":"differentiation_from_lit should add an explicit entry against Jano (and Region-Adaptive Sampling for Diffusion Transformers) stating the SE(3)-validity-certificate + per-residue-budget delta, so the borderline subsumption is dodged by foregrounding the protein-geometry separation criterion these Euclidean methods lack."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat: Jano (and Region-Adaptive Sampling for Diffusion Transformers) in collision_hits adapt compute to per-region heterogeneous convergence on Euclidean/image manifolds, a borderline subsumption of the heterogeneous-convergence observation.","fix_direction":"Add one differentiation_from_lit entry with paper_id 'Jano: Adaptive Diffusion Generation with Early-stage Convergence Awareness' and a delta stating: Jano exploits region-level heterogeneous convergence for Diffusion Transformers on a Euclidean manifold with no validity guarantee; we define the per-residue stopping decision against an explicit SE(3) backbone-validity certificate and bound the terminal stereochemical-validity loss, objects Jano does not construct."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism_reasoning","issue":"gap_closure_reject_check C04 borderline: d_i (velocity-field disagreement) could be read as a generic convergence/uncertainty proxy and the partition criterion mistaken for the contribution.","fix_direction":"Add one sentence to core_mechanism_reasoning making explicit that the contribution is NOT the d_i proxy itself but its binding to the SE(3) validity certificate plus the freeze-error decomposition — i.e. d_i is only the online estimator of tau_i, and the load-bearing artifact is the bound that ties freezing-when-d_i<eps to recovered backbone validity, distinguishing it from generic convergence-based early exit."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added a differentiation_from_lit entry against Jano stating the SE(3) backbone-validity-certificate + per-residue minimal valid-step budget + freeze-error bound delta versus Euclidean region-level adaptive Diffusion-Transformer sampling."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism_reasoning","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Appended a sentence clarifying that d_i is only the online estimator of tau_i and the load-bearing artifact is the freeze-error decomposition binding freezing to recovered backbone validity, not the convergence proxy itself."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Per-Residue Minimal Step Budgets for Validity-Gated SE(3) Protein Structure Generation\n\n**Method.** Validity-Gated Per-Residue Sampling (VGPR)\n\n## Motivation\nToday's fastest protein-structure generators build a 3D structure step by step. They start from random noise and run a neural network — an SE(3) flow-matching or diffusion model, which respects 3D rotations and translations — hundreds of times in sequence, each pass nudging every amino-acid residue a little closer to its final pose. The time to make one structure is basically (number of steps) times (cost of one network pass). The catch: that number of steps is a single global setting, the same for every residue, chosen so the overall distribution of shapes looks right. But in practice most residues lock into a chemically valid position long before the global step count runs out, while a few hard ones (a strained loop, a rare conformation) genuinely need many steps. Everyone pays the worst-case price everywhere.\n\nRecent work (P2DFlow, openalex:W4408293717; protein structural-diffusion conformation samplers, openalex:W4402939815) fixes the step count for distribution fidelity and never asks the more useful question: how few sequential passes does each residue actually need before its backbone geometry — bond lengths, bond angles, handedness (chirality), no atomic clashes — is valid? Image-domain speedups (openalex:W4402727162) tune a global schedule but on flat (Euclidean) image data with no guarantee a shortened protein trajectory is still a valid chain.\n\nThe idea: define, per residue, the minimal number of steps needed to reach a valid pose (we call it $tau_{i}),$ prove a single global count can never be right for every residue at once, and build a sampler that lets each residue stop early once it has converged — measured by how much the network still wants to move it $(d_{i}).$ This is a drop-in wrapper around any existing, frozen pretrained generator. When the gap closes, any such generator gets the same-quality structures using far fewer total network passes, by spending compute only where the geometry is still uncertain.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n*Reuse a frozen pretrained SE(3) generator as the unchanged scaffold.*\n\n1. Take any pretrained SE(3) flow-matching or diffusion protein generator — SE(3) means the model is built to respect 3D rotations and translations — and freeze its weights; we only change how it samples, never retrain it. Wrap it in a thin adapter that, at every sampling step, lets us read each residue's current pose (a 3D rotation plus a 3D position), read the raw per-residue update the network proposes before it is applied, and set a mask saying which residues are still being updated.\n   - _Why_: Speed should come from spending steps wisely, not from a new model.\n\n### Per-residue budget characterization\n*Define and measure the minimal valid-step budget per residue against a backbone-validity certificate.*\n\n2. Write a cheap per-residue validity check, the backbone-validity certificate V(X): for each residue, are its bond lengths and bond angles within standard ideal-geometry tolerances (about $0.05 Ångström$ for lengths and about 8 degrees for angles), is its handedness correct (chirality — left-handed amino acids, checked by the sign of a geometric triple product at the central carbon), and is it free of atomic clashes (no other residue's atoms closer than about 0.6 times the sum of the two atoms' van der Waals radii)? The check returns a pass/fail per residue and an overall pass for the whole structure.\n\n*The backbone-validity certificate V(X) is 1 only when every residue's bond length $b_{i},$ bond angle $\\theta _{i},$ chirality $sign \\chi _{i},$ and nearest-neighbor distance pass fixed stereochemical tolerances $\\delta _{b}, \\delta _\\theta , \\delta _{c}.$*\n$$ V(X)=\\prod_{i=1}^{N}\\mathbb{1}\\!\\left[\\,|b_i-b^{*}|\\le\\delta_b,\\ |\\theta_i-\\theta^{*}|\\le\\delta_\\theta,\\ \\chi_i>0,\\ \\min_{j\\neq i}\\|x_i-x_j\\|\\ge\\delta_c\\right] \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This is the real target — a chemically valid backbone — not just a distribution match.\n3. Offline, run the full sampler many times (about 50 random seeds) on held-out proteins. For each residue, find the latest step at which you could have frozen it and still kept it (and its bonded neighbors) chemically valid; take a conservative summary across seeds (the 95th percentile, i.e. valid on nearly all runs). This per-residue minimal step count is its budget. Pool these budgets across all residues and proteins and plot the distribution: showing it has several distinct peaks (and a wide spread) is the evidence that residues genuinely need very different numbers of steps, so one global step count must be wasteful for most of them.\n\n*The per-residue minimal valid-step budget $\\tau _{i}$ is the smallest number of remaining steps k such that freezing residue i at step $T- k$ still leaves residue i and its bonded neighbors valid.*\n$$ \\tau_i=\\min\\{\\,k:\\ V_i\\big(\\mathrm{freeze}_i(X;\\,T-k)\\big)=1\\,\\} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: It proves the heterogeneity that makes a single global step count wasteful for most residues.\n4. Prove an error bound: when a residue is frozen early, the only error it can introduce is the motion it would still have undergone, and we froze it precisely because that residual motion was below a small cutoff. Summed over all frozen residues, the total drift of the final structure from the full-step result is at most the number of residues times that cutoff times the remaining fraction of the trajectory. Use the same pose-distance definition as the convergence signal so the bound and the freezing rule are in the same units, and report both the formula's bound and the actually measured drift to show the bound is meaningful.\n\n*The terminal deviation between the gated and full-step structures is bounded by the integrated remaining velocity of frozen residues, which freezing-only-when $d_{i}<\\epsilon $ caps at $N\\cdot \\epsilon \\cdot (remaining$ horizon).*\n$$ \\big\\|X_{\\text{freeze}}(1)-X_{\\text{full}}(1)\\big\\|\\ \\le\\ \\sum_{i\\ \\text{frozen at}\\ t_i}\\int_{t_i}^{1}\\!\\|v_\\theta(X_i,s)\\|\\,ds\\ \\le\\ N\\,\\varepsilon\\,(1-t_{\\min}) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: It ties the speedup to a controllable, provable validity loss instead of a hope.\n\n### Validity-gated sampler\n*Estimate convergence online and let each residue exit the trajectory early, then calibrate and benchmark.*\n\n5. During sampling, for each residue measure how far the network still wants to move it between two consecutive steps. Project the residue one step ahead from step t and from step $t- 1$ using the update the network already produced, then take the distance between those two predicted poses. The pose distance combines a rotation part (the angle between the two orientations, in radians) and a position part (the distance in $Ångström)$; rescale each so neither dominates. Because it reuses values already computed, this convergence signal $d_{i}$ is almost free.\n\n*The per-residue convergence indicator $d_{i}(t)$ is the geodesic SE(3) distance between residue i's extrapolated endpoints at consecutive steps, computed from the velocity field already evaluated during integration.*\n$$ d_i(t)=d_{SE(3)}\\!\\big(\\hat{X}_i(t),\\,\\hat{X}_i(t-1)\\big),\\qquad \\hat{X}_i(t)=\\exp_{X_i(t)}\\!\\big((1-t)\\,v_\\theta(X,t)_i\\big) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: $d_{i}$ is a live signal for whether a residue has converged and can stop early.\n6. Swap the uniform integrator for a gated one. Keep a set of still-active residues; at each step run the network with all residues present (so already-finished residues still act as fixed surrounding context), but only apply the proposed move to the active ones. A residue leaves the active set — gets frozen — once its convergence signal stays below the cutoff for K steps in a row, and it is never reactivated. The savings come from only computing and applying updates for active residues (and, where the network allows, only querying for them while still letting them see everyone). Freezing changes which residues keep moving, so it changes the final 3D coordinates, not just the signal.\n   - _Why_: Compute concentrates on uncertain residues; converged ones stop consuming network passes.\n7. Tune the two knobs — the convergence cutoff and the number of consecutive steps required before freezing — on held-out proteins. Try a small grid of values; for each, record how much total work the sampler does and what fraction of generated structures are valid. Keep only the settings whose validity rate is statistically as good as the full-step baseline, and among those pick the one that does the least total work (preferring the more cautious setting when tied). Package the chosen settings into a sampler users can drop in and just run.\n   - _Why_: Turns the two knobs into one calibrated operating point users can just run.\n8. Benchmark the gated sampler against the full sampler and an optimized-global-schedule baseline (a method that picks a better single global set of steps). Measure total network passes, wall-clock, the fraction of valid structures, and how well the generated set matches reference structure distributions (for flexible ensembles: per-residue fluctuation agreement and distribution overlap; for de novo design: whether a sequence can be designed that folds back to the structure, and how diverse the outputs are). Then run two controls: a random-freeze control that freezes the same number of residues per step but picks them at random — this should break validity, proving the geometry-aware signal is what matters — and a positive control that freezes purely on the convergence signal, which should recover most of the speedup at full validity. Compare with paired statistical tests and report effect sizes.\n   - _Why_: The random-freeze control should break validity, proving it is the geometry-aware decision $(d_{i})$ doing the work, not just doing less.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 面向 SE(3) 蛋白质结构生成的逐残基最小步数预算与有效性门控采样\n\n**方法名称.** Validity-Gated Per-Residue Sampling (VGPR)\n\n## 研究动机\n目前最快的蛋白质结构生成器是一步步搭建三维结构的。它们从随机噪声出发，按顺序运行一个神经网络（一种尊重三维旋转与平移的 SE(3) flow matching 或 diffusion 模型）数百次，每一次都把每个氨基酸残基往最终姿态推近一点。生成一个结构的耗时基本就是（步数）乘以（单次网络前向的代价）。问题在于：这个步数是一个全局统一的设置，对所有残基都一样，而且是为了让整体形状分布看起来正确而选的。但实际上大多数残基远在全局步数用完之前就已经锁定到化学上有效的位置，只有少数难处理的残基（紧张的 loop、罕见构象）才真正需要很多步。结果是所有地方都按最坏情况付费。\n\n近期工作（P2DFlow，openalex:W4408293717；蛋白质结构 diffusion 构象采样器，openalex:W4402939815）把步数固定为追求分布保真度，却从不问那个更有用的问题：每个残基到底需要多少次连续前向，其骨架几何——键长、键角、手性（chirality）、无原子碰撞——才算有效？图像领域的加速方法（openalex:W4402727162）调的是一个全局时间步表，但作用在平坦的（Euclidean）图像数据上，无法保证缩短后的蛋白质轨迹仍是一条有效的链。\n\n本工作的想法是：为每个残基定义达到有效姿态所需的最小步数（记作 $tau_{i}$），证明单一全局步数不可能对每个残基同时正确，并构建一个采样器，让每个残基在收敛后即可提前退出——收敛程度用网络还想把它移动多少来度量（$d_{i}$）。这是一个可直接套在任何已冻结的预训练生成器之上的包装器。当这一缺口被补上时，任何此类生成器都能用少得多的总网络前向次数得到同等质量的结构，因为算力只花在几何仍不确定的地方。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景\n*复用一个冻结的预训练 SE(3) 生成器作为不变的脚手架。*\n\n1. 取任意预训练的 SE(3) flow matching 或 diffusion 蛋白质生成器——SE(3) 指模型在构造上尊重三维旋转与平移——并冻结其权重；我们只改变它的采样方式，绝不重新训练。给它套一个轻量适配器，使我们在每个采样步都能：读出每个残基当前的姿态（一个三维旋转加一个三维位置）、读出网络在施加之前提出的逐残基原始更新量、以及设置一个掩码来指明哪些残基仍在被更新。\n   - _为什么_: 加速应来自更聪明地分配步数，而不是换一个新模型。\n\n### 逐残基预算刻画\n*对照骨架有效性证书定义并测量每个残基的最小有效步数预算。*\n\n2. 写一个廉价的逐残基有效性检查，即骨架有效性证书 V(X)：对每个残基，键长与键角是否都在标准理想几何容差内（键长约 $0.05 Ångström$、键角约 8 度）；手性（chirality，即氨基酸的左旋/右旋手征性）是否正确（通过在中心碳原子处一个几何三重积的符号来判定，要求为左旋氨基酸）；以及是否没有原子碰撞（其他残基的原子不得近于两原子范德华半径之和的约 0.6 倍）。该检查对每个残基返回通过/不通过，并对整条结构返回一个总的通过判定。\n\n*骨架有效性证书 V(X) 仅当每个残基的键长 $b_{i}$、键角 $\\theta _{i}$、手性符号 $\\chi _{i}$ 与最近邻距离都满足固定的立体化学容差 $\\delta _{b}$、$\\delta _\\theta $、$\\delta _{c}$ 时取 1。*\n$$ V(X)=\\prod_{i=1}^{N}\\mathbb{1}\\!\\left[\\,|b_i-b^{*}|\\le\\delta_b,\\ |\\theta_i-\\theta^{*}|\\le\\delta_\\theta,\\ \\chi_i>0,\\ \\min_{j\\neq i}\\|x_i-x_j\\|\\ge\\delta_c\\right] \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 真正的目标是化学上有效的骨架，而不仅仅是分布匹配。\n3. 离线地在留出蛋白上多次运行完整采样器（约 50 个随机种子）。对每个残基，找出最晚可以冻结它、且仍能让它（及其成键邻居）保持化学有效的那一步；在多次运行间取一个保守的汇总值（第 95 百分位，即在几乎所有运行中都有效）。这个逐残基最小步数就是它的预算。把所有残基、所有蛋白的预算汇集起来并画出分布：若它呈现多个明显的峰（且分布很宽），即证明各残基确实需要差异极大的步数，因此单一全局步数对其中大多数残基必然是浪费。\n\n*逐残基最小步数预算 $\\tau _{i}$ 定义为：使得在第 $T- k$ 步冻结残基 i 后，该残基及其成键邻居仍然有效的最小剩余步数 k。*\n$$ \\tau_i=\\min\\{\\,k:\\ V_i\\big(\\mathrm{freeze}_i(X;\\,T-k)\\big)=1\\,\\} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这证明了异质性，正是它使单一全局步数对大多数残基造成浪费。\n4. 证明一个误差界：当某残基被提前冻结时，它能引入的唯一误差就是它本会继续发生的运动，而我们恰恰是在该剩余运动低于一个小阈值时才冻结它。对所有被冻结残基求和，最终结构相对全步结果的总漂移至多为残基数乘以该阈值乘以轨迹剩余比例。采用与收敛信号相同的姿态距离定义，使误差界与冻结规则处于同一单位；并同时报告公式给出的界与实际测得的漂移，以表明该界并非空泛。\n\n*门控结构与全步结构之间的终点偏差由被冻结残基的剩余速度积分上界界定；仅在 $d_{i}<\\epsilon $ 时冻结即把该界限控制在 $N\\cdot \\epsilon \\cdot ($剩余区间) 之内。*\n$$ \\big\\|X_{\\text{freeze}}(1)-X_{\\text{full}}(1)\\big\\|\\ \\le\\ \\sum_{i\\ \\text{frozen at}\\ t_i}\\int_{t_i}^{1}\\!\\|v_\\theta(X_i,s)\\|\\,ds\\ \\le\\ N\\,\\varepsilon\\,(1-t_{\\min}) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 它把加速与一个可控、可证的有效性损失绑定，而非寄希望于运气。\n\n### 有效性门控采样器\n*在线估计收敛并让每个残基提前退出轨迹，再做标定与基准测试。*\n\n5. 采样过程中，为每个残基测量网络在相邻两步之间还想把它移动多远。用网络已经产生的更新量，分别从第 t 步与第 $t- 1$ 步把该残基向前外推一步，再取这两个预测姿态之间的距离。姿态距离由旋转部分（两个朝向之间的夹角，以弧度计）与位置部分（以 $Ångström$ 计的距离）合成；对两部分各自做归一化，使其互不压倒。由于复用了已算好的值，这个收敛信号 $d_{i}$ 几乎不增加开销。\n\n*逐残基收敛指标 $d_{i}(t)$ 是残基 i 在相邻两步外推终点之间的 SE(3) 测地距离，由积分过程中已计算的速度场直接得到。*\n$$ d_i(t)=d_{SE(3)}\\!\\big(\\hat{X}_i(t),\\,\\hat{X}_i(t-1)\\big),\\qquad \\hat{X}_i(t)=\\exp_{X_i(t)}\\!\\big((1-t)\\,v_\\theta(X,t)_i\\big) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: $d_{i}$ 是判断某残基是否已收敛、可否提前停止的实时信号。\n6. 把统一积分器换成门控积分器。维护一个仍然活跃的残基集合；每一步都让网络在所有残基在场的情况下运行（这样已完成的残基仍作为固定的周边上下文存在），但只对活跃残基施加提出的移动。当某残基的收敛信号连续 K 步低于阈值 eps 时，它就离开活跃集合——被冻结——且不再被重新激活。节省来自只为活跃残基计算并施加更新（并在网络允许时只对它们发起查询、同时仍让它们看见所有人）。冻结改变了哪些残基继续移动，因此改变的是最终三维坐标，而不仅仅是信号。\n   - _为什么_: 算力集中在不确定的残基上，已收敛的残基不再消耗网络前向。\n7. 在留出蛋白上调这两个旋钮——收敛阈值与冻结前所需的连续步数。尝试一个小网格；对每组取值，记录采样器的总工作量以及生成结构的有效比例。只保留那些有效率在统计上不亚于全步基线的设置，并在其中选总工作量最小的（并列时偏向更谨慎的设置）。把选定的设置打包成一个用户可直接套用、运行即可的采样器。\n   - _为什么_: 把两个旋钮变成一个标定好的工作点，用户直接运行即可。\n8. 把门控采样器与全步采样器、以及优化全局步表基线（一种挑选更好的单一全局步集的方法）进行对比。测量总网络前向次数、墙钟时间、有效结构比例，以及生成集合与参考结构分布的匹配程度（对柔性系综：逐残基涨落一致性与分布重叠；对 de novo 设计：能否设计出可折回该结构的序列，以及输出的多样性）。再跑两个对照：随机冻结对照——每步冻结相同数量的残基但随机挑选——它应当破坏有效性，从而证明起作用的是几何感知信号；以及正向对照——仅按收敛信号冻结——它应在保持完全有效性的同时恢复大部分加速。用配对统计检验进行比较并报告效应量。\n   - _为什么_: 随机冻结对照应当破坏有效性，从而证明起作用的是几何感知的决策（$d_{i}$），而不仅仅是做得更少。\n\n"},{"id":"22","run_dir":"run_prompt22_medts","index":22,"title":"Regime-Conditional Continuous-Time Attention for Medical Time Series","title_zh":"面向医疗时间序列的状态条件连续时间注意力","method_name":"Regime-Conditional Continuous-Time Attention (RC-CTA)","hook":"Every transformer built for irregular medical time series keeps softmax dot-product attention between discrete observation tokens and re-injects elapsed time as an architect-chosen additive bias (an exponential decay, a learned positional embedding, a deformable window). We show the time variable should instead PARAMETERIZE the attention kernel itself: replacing the dot-product-plus-decay with a continuous-time kernel whose relevance shape is inferred per query from the patient's current latent regime lets the same elapsed gap count differently for a stable versus a deteriorating patient and makes the representation readable at any unobserved query time without a separate imputation stage.","anchor_pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","anchor_pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","domain_category":"Healthcare & Scientific ML","patterns":[{"gap":"(subtractive) No retrieved paper questions whether the timestamp must enter attention as an ADDITIVE, fixed-FORM bias on top of a discrete-token dot-product at all — every frontier leaf (TrajGPT, Medformer, DNA-T, SDE-Attention, WaveGNN) silently inherits, from the NLP discrete-token attention ancestor, the assumption that the attention SCORE is computed between tokens and the elapsed time only modulates that score through a separately-chosen functional form (exponential decay, learned positiona","pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","sub_pattern":"C14 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","companion_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","how_closed":"Closed by the audit half (assumption_audit_and_pivot) naming and inverting the inherited assumption — that attention is a token-token dot product with time added on top — and the substitution half (C14) shipping the runnable replacement: a continuous-time attention operator whose score between a query at time t_q and an observation at time t_j is computed by a learned time-difference kernel k(t_q - t_j; theta) multiplied by a content gate, so the elapsed time defines the operator rather than biasing it; the C14 deliverable is the preserved-property proof that this kernel-attention retains softmax attention's expressive class on regularly-sampled inputs as a special case.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"(additive) No retrieved leaf produces a per-query, regime-conditional temporal-relevance response: the weight an observation at t_j gives to a representation at query time t_q is fixed by the architect's chosen bias form (a monotone decay, a fixed patch scale) and is identical across patients and across a patient's changing physiological state, so none can represent that the same elapsed gap should count for more or less depending on whether the patient is stable or deteriorating.","pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","sub_pattern":"C14 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by making the kernel's shape parameters theta_q not global constants but the output of a small hypernetwork conditioned on a per-query latent regime code z_q read off the recent observation window, so the relevance-versus-elapsed-time curve (its decay rate, and whether it is monotone or has a delayed peak) is INFERRED per query from the patient's current dynamical state rather than fixed by the architect — the same primitive object (the kernel) carries both gap closures, which is why both legs ride one operator.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"machine learning for medical time series (irregularly-sampled multivariate physiological / EHR signals: EEG, ECG, ICU vitals, longitudinal clinical events)","n_papers":38,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":25},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":16,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Medformer: A Multi-Granularity Patching Transformer for Medical Time-Series Classification"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"DNA-T: Deformable Neighborhood Attention Transformer for Irregular Medical Time Series"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"MamKanformer: A hybrid Mamba and KAN model based on Medformer for Medical Time-Series Classification"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A time series driven model for early sepsis prediction based on transformer module"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Multi-scale Value-Density Transformer with Medical Semantic Guidance for Disease Risk Prediction Based on Clinical Time Series"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Inter-Series Transformer: Attending to Products in Time Series Forecasting"}],"more":10},{"year":2025,"n":22,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Sparseformer: a Transferable Transformer with Multi-granularity Token Sparsification for Medical Time Series Classification"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"MedSpaformer: A Transferable Transformer with Multi-Granularity Token Sparsification for Medical Time Series Classification"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A Medical Time Series Classifier with False Negative and Positive Mitigation via UNITS Transformer Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Channel-Imposed Fusion: A Simple yet Effective Method for Medical Time Series Classification"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Investigating Transformer-Based GANs for Realistic ECG Time-Series Data Generation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Multi-channel Time-series Transformer for Wearable Monitoring of Rigidity in Parkinson’s Disease"}],"more":16}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":7,"share":0.184},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution; adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"architectural_operator_substitution; adapt_via_conditioning","count":3,"share":0.079},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution; structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"architectural_operator_substitution; structural_prior_encoding","count":3,"share":0.079},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":2,"share":0.053},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding; architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"structural_prior_encoding; architectural_operator_substitution","count":2,"share":0.053},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution; heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"architectural_operator_substitution; heterogeneous_decomposition","count":1,"share":0.026},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate; architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"decompose_and_delegate; architectural_operator_substitution","count":1,"share":0.026},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":1,"share":0.026}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Across the retrieved frontier, every transformer for medical time series first discretizes the signal into a fixed set of tokens (one per observation, per patch, or per channel) and then re-introduces the missing temporal geometry as an ADDITIVE side-channel on top of standard dot-product attention: TrajGPT (openalex:W4403882408) tokenizes each (observation, timestamp) pair and multiplies attention by a parametric exponential decay of the inter-token gap; Medformer (semanticscholar:9eb6da3bff35a8e235fc3c16499b6b7836d6304f) projects multiple hand-chosen patch lengths into tokens and runs vanilla attention within/across granularities; DNA-T (semanticscholar:46de92a23f8e374eec5f3079c2fe74e89db58315) keeps full attention but learns deformable neighborhoods to re-weight short vs long range; SDE-Attention (openalex:W4416952620) and WaveGNN (openalex:W4405468520) bolt attention onto an SDE-RNN or a decay-aware GNN. The failure this produces is concrete: because the timestamps t_n only enter through a fixed-FORM bias (an exponential decay, a learned positional embedding, a masking pattern) whose functional shape is chosen by the architect and held constant across patients and physiological regimes, the model cannot represent the fact that the SAME inter-observation gap carries different evidential weight depending on the patient's current dynamical regime (a 6-hour gap in a stable patient versus a deteriorating one), and it cannot recover the value of the latent signal at query times where nothing was measured. The quantity the current machinery cannot produce is a per-query, regime-conditional answer to 'how much should an observation at time t_j inform a representation anchored at an arbitrary continuous query time t_q', because that quantity is fixed by the chosen bias form rather than inferred from the data.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4403882408","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"TrajGPT tokenizes each (observation, timestamp) pair and replaces full attention with Selective Recurrent Attention, which weights past tokens by a DATA-DEPENDENT but FIXED-FORM exponential decay of the inter-token time gap, giving a continuous-time-flavored autoregressive decoder for health trajectories. Its residue: the decay is a single scalar-rate exponential whose functional form is hard-wired and identical across all patients and physiological regimes, so it cannot express non-monotone or regime-switching temporal relevance, and attention is still defined only at observed token positions rather than as an operator over a continuous query-time axis, so the model cannot answer queries at unobserved times without separate imputation."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:9eb6da3bff35a8e235fc3c16499b6b7836d6304f","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Medformer patches each channel at several hand-chosen granularities and runs intra- and inter-granularity self-attention, improving EEG/ECG classification over single-scale patching. Residue: patch lengths (the temporal scales the model can see) are fixed hyperparameters chosen before training and applied uniformly to every patient, and the formulation assumes a regularly-sampled grid, so it has no mechanism for irregular inter-observation gaps or for letting the relevant timescale vary with the patient's state."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:46de92a23f8e374eec5f3079c2fe74e89db58315","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"DNA-T keeps full transformer attention but learns deformable neighborhoods so each query attends to a learned local window, correcting full attention's bias toward distant tokens in irregular EHR. Residue: the deformation re-weights WHICH discrete tokens are attended but still treats the inter-observation time gap as a feature to be embedded rather than as the variable that parameterizes the attention kernel, so identical token neighborhoods with different elapsed times collapse to the same computation."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416952620","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"SDE-Attention places channel-level attention on the latent pre-RNN state of an SDE-RNN to handle irregular sampling with heavy missingness. Residue: continuity is carried entirely by the SDE-RNN backbone and attention is an add-on recalibration over latent channels, so the attention operator itself remains discrete-token dot-product; the continuous-time structure never enters the attention kernel."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"machine learning for medical time series (irregularly-sampled multivariate physiological / EHR signals: EEG, ECG, ICU vitals, longitudinal clinical events)","venue":"ICLR / NeurIPS / ICML (Oral tier)","time":"2026","data":["PhysioNet/MIMIC-style irregularly-sampled ICU vitals & labs","EEG/ECG classification benchmarks (e.g. TUEV, PTB-XL)","longitudinal EHR event sequences"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with healthcare time-series background","preference":"both","baseline":"transformer-based MedTS models (Medformer multi-granularity patching; TrajGPT selective-recurrent decay attention; DNA-T deformable neighborhood attention)","limitation":"current transformers for medical time series inherit the discrete-token + added-time-encoding formulation from NLP and only bolt heuristics onto it to cope with irregular sampling; they do not rethink what the attention operator should be when the signal lives in continuous time with informative observation timing","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared central object (coherence_thread_type = shared_object) is a continuous-time, regime-conditional attention kernel K(t_q, t_j | z_q) that REPLACES the dot-product-plus-additive-time-bias score used by every retrieved leaf. (1) AUDIT (companion assumption_audit_and_pivot, anchor gap): the load-bearing inherited assumption is that an attention score is a token-token inner product q_i . k_j and elapsed time delta = t_q - t_j only enters as a separate term added to or multiplied onto that inner product (TrajGPT's exp(-lambda*delta) factor; learned positional embeddings added to tokens; DNA-T's deformable window mask). We invert it: time is not added to the score, time PARAMETERIZES the score. (2) SUBSTITUTION (C14, anchor + sibling): the unnormalized attention weight from observation j to query time t_q becomes a(t_q, j) = g(c_q, c_j) * phi(t_q - t_j ; theta_q), where c_q, c_j in R^d are content vectors (the same value/content projections a transformer already has; g is the usual scaled inner product passed through exp, a model-internal readout), and phi(. ; theta) is a learned positive temporal-relevance kernel built as a small mixture of M=4 basis components phi(delta;theta)=sum_m w_m * exp(-(delta - mu_m)^2 / (2 s_m^2)) for delta>=0 and 0 otherwise (a non-monotone, possibly delayed-peak shape; a single decaying exponential is the M=1, mu=0 special case, which is exactly TrajGPT's kernel, so their operator is a strict restriction of ours -- the C14 preserved-property anchor). theta_q = {w_m, mu_m, s_m} are NOT global: theta_q = H(z_q), where H is a 2-layer MLP hypernetwork (named weight-bridge hyperparameter; outputs are softplus-constrained so s_m>0, w_m>=0) and z_q in R^16 is a per-query latent REGIME CODE produced by a small GRU encoder run over the most recent W=32 observations preceding t_q (model-internal readout; W fixed). This is what closes the sibling gap: because theta_q is a function of z_q, the relevance-vs-elapsed-time curve is inferred per query from the patient's current dynamics, so an identical gap delta yields a sharper kernel (small s) for a deteriorating regime and a flatter kernel for a stable one. (3) The operator is defined for ANY continuous t_q, observed or not (delta is just a real number), so a representation r(t_q) = sum_j softmax_j[a(t_q,j)] * v_j is readable at unobserved query times by construction -- this is why the deferred imputation gap closes for free and is not a separate leg. Quantitatively, against TrajGPT (openalex:W4403882408), whose Selective Recurrent Attention uses a single data-dependent scalar decay rate (their abstract: 'data-dependent decay to adaptively filter'), our kernel is multi-component and regime-conditional rather than single-rate; we do not paste their reported numbers -- the regime distinction (their decay rate is per-token-content, ours is per-query-regime and non-monotone) is the visible delta.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules: both are properties of ONE object, the attention kernel -- the anchor gap demands the kernel replace the additive bias, the sibling gap demands the kernel's shape be regime-conditional. Forcing them into one operator (kernel + hypernetwork) is what makes this read as one paper (shared_object thread) rather than 'a new attention plus a separate adaptivity gadget'. (b) Alternatives considered and rejected: (i) an explicit Neural-CDE/ODE latent state to carry continuity -- rejected as a regression to method_lineage node c0 (ODE-integrated recurrent state), which abandons global content-based pairwise attention; (ii) a Gaussian-process interpolation front-end feeding a standard transformer -- rejected as regression to node c1 (separate GP imputation stage, kernel outside attention); (iii) a single global learned kernel family shared across patients -- rejected as regression to node c2 (one fixed-family global time kernel, which cannot be regime-conditional). The avoided nodes are c0/c1/c2; novelty is preserved by putting a per-query, regime-conditioned, multi-component kernel INSIDE the attention operator, a source the lineage tree does not occupy.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: train the regime-conditional continuous-time attention model and an identical-parameter-count baseline whose only difference is that theta is global (z_q replaced by a constant, i.e. TrajGPT-style fixed-form kernel) on PhysioNet-2012 irregular ICU vitals (in-hospital mortality classification + next-12h vitals forecasting at unobserved query times); measure AUROC and forecasting MSE. If the candidate works, AUROC rises and forecasting MSE at unobserved times falls relative to the global-kernel baseline, AND the improvement concentrates on the deteriorating-patient subgroup (high recent vitals variance) rather than uniformly. The named load-bearing variable is z_q, the per-query latent regime code that drives the kernel's shape theta_q = H(z_q). Negative control: ablate z_q's producer by feeding the hypernetwork a label-permuted / shuffled-across-patients z_q (so kernel shapes are decoupled from each query's actual recent dynamics) while keeping all parameters and FLOPs identical; if z_q is the mechanism, AUROC and forecasting MSE must collapse back to the global-kernel baseline (the downstream outcome metrics, not z_q's own value, return to baseline). Positive control: a stripped model that keeps ONLY the regime-conditional kernel with content gating frozen to uniform (g==1) should recover most of the deteriorating-subgroup gain, identifying the regime-conditional time kernel -- not the content attention -- as the driver.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4403882408","delta":"TrajGPT constructs a single data-dependent SCALAR exponential decay rate per token (one monotone shape, content-conditioned); we construct a multi-component (non-monotone, delayed-peak-capable) temporal kernel whose parameters are inferred per query from a latent REGIME code, of which their single-exponential decay is the provable M=1 special case -- a strictly larger operator class they did not build."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:46de92a23f8e374eec5f3079c2fe74e89db58315","delta":"DNA-T learns deformable neighborhoods that select WHICH discrete tokens a query attends to while time stays an embedded feature; we make the elapsed time the PARAMETER of the attention kernel itself, so two equal-token neighborhoods with different elapsed times compute differently -- a distinction their token-selection mechanism cannot represent."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:9eb6da3bff35a8e235fc3c16499b6b7836d6304f","delta":"Medformer fixes the visible temporal scales as hand-chosen patch lengths applied uniformly to all patients on a regular grid; we let the effective timescale (kernel width s_m) be inferred per query per patient and defined directly on continuous irregular timestamps, removing both the fixed-scale and regular-grid assumptions."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416952620","delta":"SDE-Attention carries continuity in an SDE-RNN backbone and uses attention only to recalibrate latent channels; we carry continuity INSIDE the attention operator (the kernel is a function of continuous t_q-t_j), so no non-attention continuity module is needed and the representation is queryable at arbitrary unobserved times directly from attention."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4403882408","what_step_was_missed":"TrajGPT made the decay DATA-DEPENDENT but kept it a single scalar-rate exponential whose functional FORM is fixed and applied at observed token positions only; to already be our contribution it would have needed to (i) construct the relevance kernel as a regime-conditioned multi-component shape inferred from a per-query latent code (not a per-token scalar rate), and (ii) define the kernel over a continuous query-time axis so the operator yields representations at unobserved times -- neither the multi-component regime-conditional parameterization nor the continuous-query definition is present in their Selective Recurrent Attention construction."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":337,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"No hard floor fires: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict='clear' (the load-bearing lesson 'An equivalence or approximation proof with no downstream consequence is dismissed' is mitigated by tying the M=1 special-case proof to continuous-query and regime-conditional capabilities), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id=null (single-pattern composition, no heterogeneous_decomposition), and paper_pointed_threat.threat_paper_id='no_threat_found' (337 collision hits scanned; closest, 'Continuous-Time Attention: PDE-Guided Mechanisms', evolves attention weights via a PDE for long NLP sequences — a different mechanism and purpose, no exact-mechanism overlap). recipe_application_check.verdict='applied' for both entries, so the idea instantiates C14's signature operator-substitution-with-preserved-property move rather than a generic parent-pattern swap; advance.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"(subtractive) No retrieved paper questions whether the timestamp must enter attention as an ADDITIVE, fixed-FORM bias on top of a discrete-token dot-product at all — every frontier leaf (TrajGPT, Medformer, DNA-T, SDE-Attention, WaveGNN) silently inherits, from the NLP discrete-token attention ancestor, the assumption that the attention SCORE is computed between tokens and the elapsed time only modulates that score through a separately-chosen functional form (exponential decay, learned positional embedding, deformable window, masking). No leaf tests whether the time variable should instead define the attention computation itself rather than be added to it.","main_pattern":"architectural_operator_substitution","sub_pattern":"C14 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail when the surrogate is offered as a cheaper-but-equivalent reparameterization with no load-bearing consequence (preservation argument absent, trivially true, or never connected to a capability the original lacked), or when the operator swap co-varies with a confound and no controlled ablation isolates the substitution, or via baseline myopia (comparing only against the expensive original, ignoring the existing family of cheaper surrogates).","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"If a confound (positional encoding, extra capacity, added multi-scale features) co-varies with your operator swap, the headline conclusion becomes unattributable and reviewers reject it as opportunistic.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"falsification_prediction holds parameter count and FLOPs identical between the regime-conditional kernel model and the global-theta baseline (z_q replaced by a constant), so the swap is the only varying factor."},{"lesson_quoted":"Comparing your cheaper operator only against the expensive original — never against the existing family of cheaper alternatives — makes it read as a redundant reparameterization rather than an advance.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"differentiation_from_lit benchmarks against the surrogate family (TrajGPT single-scalar decay, DNA-T deformable neighborhoods, Medformer fixed patch scales, SDE-Attention SDE-RNN), not just vanilla softmax attention."},{"lesson_quoted":"An equivalence or approximation proof with no downstream consequence is dismissed as formalizing what the field already assumed to be true.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the preserved-property proof (TrajGPT = M=1, mu=0 special case) is connected to a capability the original lacks — continuous-query readout at unobserved times and regime-conditional non-monotone relevance shapes — so the proof is load-bearing, not decorative."},{"lesson_quoted":"Bolting together established cheaper components without a single unifying load-bearing insight invites the 'combination of existing modules / engineering report' rejection.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism unifies both gap closures under ONE object (the kernel K(t_q,t_j|z_q)); the hypernetwork and GRU are not separate gadgets but the parameterization of that single operator, per coherence_thread_type=shared_object."},{"lesson_quoted":"Failing to evaluate in the exact regime your substitution targets — long sequences, large scale, high representational order — leaves its core promise untested and the claim unverifiable.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"evaluation is on irregularly-sampled MedTS (PhysioNet-2012, MIMIC, PTB-XL, TUEV) at unobserved query times — precisely the irregular-continuous-time regime the substitution targets."},{"lesson_quoted":"A contrived or artificially motivated setup, paired with ablations that fail to isolate the proposed mechanism, leaves the observed gains attributable to incidental added capacity rather than the substitution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the negative control (shuffle z_q across patients while holding all params/FLOPs fixed) isolates z_q as the mechanism, and the positive control (freeze content gate g==1) attributes the gain specifically to the regime-conditional time kernel rather than added capacity."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"(additive) No retrieved leaf produces a per-query, regime-conditional temporal-relevance response: the weight an observation at t_j gives to a representation at query time t_q is fixed by the architect's chosen bias form (a monotone decay, a fixed patch scale) and is identical across patients and across a patient's changing physiological state, so none can represent that the same elapsed gap should count for more or less depending on whether the patient is stable or deteriorating.","main_pattern":"architectural_operator_substitution","sub_pattern":"C14 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The cluster fails on unattributable gains (operator swap co-varies with a confound and no ablation isolates it) and on the absence of a load-bearing preserved-property consequence; a contrived setup with ablations that do not isolate the mechanism leaves gains attributable to incidental capacity.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A contrived or artificially motivated setup, paired with ablations that fail to isolate the proposed mechanism, leaves the observed gains attributable to incidental added capacity rather than the substitution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the regime-conditioning claim is tested by the shuffled-z_q negative control AND a subgroup-specificity prediction (gain concentrates on the high-variance deteriorating subgroup, not uniformly), which is the opposite of an uncontrolled capacity gain."},{"lesson_quoted":"If a confound (positional encoding, extra capacity, added multi-scale features) co-varies with your operator swap, the headline conclusion becomes unattributable and reviewers reject it as opportunistic.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the regime-conditional vs global-theta comparison is parameter- and FLOP-matched (only z_q's information content differs), so the regime-conditioning effect is not confounded by capacity."},{"lesson_quoted":"Bolting together established cheaper components without a single unifying load-bearing insight invites the 'combination of existing modules / engineering report' rejection.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the sibling gap rides the SAME kernel object as the anchor gap (theta_q = H(z_q)); regime-conditioning is a property of the substituted operator, not a bolted-on adaptivity module."}],"verdict":"clear"}],"verdict":"clear","verdict_layer_note":"Both gap_closure entries are clear; the anchor (subtractive) entry under architectural_operator_substitution carried the most weight via the lesson 'An equivalence or approximation proof with no downstream consequence is dismissed' — explicitly mitigated because the M=1 preserved-property proof is tied to the continuous-query and regime-conditional capabilities the original kernel cannot express.","reasoning":"The anchor (subtractive) gap under architectural_operator_substitution drove the aggregate, and the lesson 'An equivalence or approximation proof with no downstream consequence is dismissed as formalizing what the field already assumed' carried the most weight; it is mitigated because the TrajGPT-as-M=1 special-case proof is connected to two capabilities (continuous-query readout, regime-conditional non-monotone relevance) the incumbent operator lacks, so no entry triggered and all are clear."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"(subtractive) No retrieved paper questions whether the timestamp must enter attention as an ADDITIVE, fixed-FORM bias on top of a discrete-token dot-product at all — every frontier leaf (TrajGPT, Medformer, DNA-T, SDE-Attention, WaveGNN) silently inherits, from the NLP discrete-token attention ancestor, the assumption that the attention SCORE is computed between tokens and the elapsed time only modulates that score through a separately-chosen functional form (exponential decay, learned positional embedding, deformable window, masking). No leaf tests whether the time variable should instead define the attention computation itself rather than be added to it.","sub_pattern":"C14 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Replace the dense all-pairs pairwise-interaction operator (softmax self-attention) with a surrogate, making the contribution the proof that the surrogate retains attention's load-bearing property (expressive class) rather than the raw change itself — exhibiting that the incumbent operator is a strict special case of the new one.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism step (2) and core_mechanism_steps step 7 physically replace the dot-product-plus-additive-time-bias score with a(t_q,j)=g(c_q,c_j)*phi(t_q-t_j;theta_q) and prove the preserved property as a runnable unit test: freezing M=1, mu_1=0, hypernetwork-to-constant reduces the layer numerically to TrajGPT's single-exponential-decay attention, establishing the incumbent operator as the strict M=1 restriction of ours.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"(additive) No retrieved leaf produces a per-query, regime-conditional temporal-relevance response: the weight an observation at t_j gives to a representation at query time t_q is fixed by the architect's chosen bias form (a monotone decay, a fixed patch scale) and is identical across patients and across a patient's changing physiological state, so none can represent that the same elapsed gap should count for more or less depending on whether the patient is stable or deteriorating.","sub_pattern":"C14 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"The swap's cheapness/expressivity must follow from an algebraic or structural lever (not from discarding inputs), and the recast operator must yield parameterizations impossible in the original framing — the substitution must unlock a capability, not merely re-derive the old behavior.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism step (2) makes theta_q=H(z_q) a function of a per-query latent regime code rather than global constants — a parameterization the additive-bias framing structurally cannot express (an additive term on a dot-product cannot be made a per-query non-monotone mixture without ceasing to be additive), so the substituted operator unlocks the regime-conditional relevance shape that closes this gap.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries perform C14's defining move — physically removing the dot-product+additive-time-bias operator and installing a continuous-time kernel surrogate whose acceptance rests on the preserved-property proof (TrajGPT as the M=1 special case) — so the mechanism instantiates the cluster card, not merely the parent pattern's generic gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["architectural_operator_substitution","architectural_operator_substitution"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"The composition_set is a single repeated pattern (architectural_operator_substitution) with no heterogeneous_decomposition component; none of the three documented reject-favored 2-way compositions (all of which require heterogeneous_decomposition) match, so no anti-pattern fires."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"no_threat_found","threat_source":"n/a","subsumption_argument":null,"addressable_via":null}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Regime-Conditional Continuous-Time Attention for Medical Time Series\n\n**Method.** Regime-Conditional Continuous-Time Attention (RC-CTA)\n\n## Motivation\nMedical time series — ICU vital signs, EEG, ECG, hospital records — are measured at irregular, uneven times, and WHEN a measurement is taken is itself a clue: clinicians measure more often when a patient is getting worse. Today's best transformer models for this data first chop the signal into a fixed list of tokens and then try to put the timing information back as a fixed extra ingredient bolted onto ordinary attention. For example, TrajGPT multiplies attention by a fixed-shape exponential 'fade-out' of the time gap; Medformer (Multi-Granularity Patching Transformer) cuts the signal into hand-chosen fixed-length pieces; DNA-T (Deformable Neighborhood Attention Transformer) just picks which nearby points to look at. In every case the SHAPE of how much an old measurement still matters is decided once by the model's designer and never changes — it is the same for a stable patient and a crashing one. So these models cannot say that a 6-hour gap means one thing for a steady patient and something very different for a deteriorating one, and they cannot tell you the patient's state at a moment when nothing was actually measured without bolting on a separate guessing (imputation) step. This is not a tuning issue; it is an unquestioned assumption copied from language models, where attention compares word tokens and time is just an add-on. The newest 2024-2025 systems all stop at exactly this point. The fix is now cheap and timely: small 'hypernetworks' that turn a short summary code into the settings of a flexible curve are easy and stable to train, and public irregular-ICU datasets (PhysioNet-2012, MIMIC-III) and EEG/ECG datasets (PTB-XL, TUEV) provide the regime-changing, irregularly-timed data needed to test the idea. When the gap closes, three things become possible at once: the same elapsed time can count differently depending on the patient's current state; you can read the patient's representation at ANY time, even unmeasured ones, straight from attention with no separate imputation module; and the old fixed-decay method (TrajGPT) comes out as a simple special case of the new one — making this a re-foundation of the operator rather than yet another add-on.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n\n1. Read each irregular multivariate series as a bag of individual measurements WITHOUT snapping them to a regular time grid: every measurement becomes one token holding three things — its value $x_{j},$ its real timestamp $t_{j},$ and which channel (which vital sign / lead) it came from. Turn each measurement into a content vector $c_{j}$ and a value vector $v_{j}$ by a linear projection of the value plus a learned per-channel embedding that tags which channel it is. Keep channels unaligned (do not force measurements from different channels onto shared time points), so the original uneven timing per channel is preserved exactly.\n   - _Why_: Keeping the raw uneven timing means the elapsed time between any two points stays a real number the new kernel can actually use, instead of being erased by gridding.\n\n### Regime encoder\n*Reads the patient's current dynamical state into a small per-query latent code.*\n\n2. For each query time $t_{q},$ summarize the patient's current dynamics into a short 16-number regime code $z_{q}.$ Take the 32 most recent measurements (across all channels) that happened strictly before $t_{q},$ feed them in time order into a small one-layer Gated Recurrent Unit (GRU) — each input is the measurement value, a smooth encoding of how long ago it was $(t_{q}$ minus its timestamp), and a tag for its channel — and read the GRU's final state through a linear layer to get $z_{q}.$ Because the window is defined by how far back from $t_{q},$ the exact same recipe works whether $t_{q}$ is a time where something was measured or a future time you want to forecast; if there are fewer than 32 earlier measurements, fill the empty earlier slots with a single learned fill token so the GRU always sees 32 inputs.\n\n*The kernel's shape parameters $\\theta _{q}$ are produced by a 2-layer hypernetwork H from a per-query latent regime code $z_{q},$ which a small GRU encodes from the most recent observation window (length W) preceding $t_{q}$; softplus constraints keep $s_{m}$ and $w_{m}$ non-negative.*\n$$ \\theta_q = \\{w_m, \\mu_m, s_m\\}_{m=1}^{M} = H(z_q), \\qquad z_q = \\mathrm{GRU}\\big(\\{(x_j, t_j) : t_j \\in [t_q - W,\\, t_q)\\}\\big) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This code is how the model reads whether the patient is currently stable or deteriorating, which is what later sets how the time-relevance curve is shaped.\n\n### Kernel hypernetwork\n*Turns the regime code into the shape of a flexible, possibly non-monotone temporal-relevance curve.*\n\n3. Feed the regime code $z_{q}$ into a small 2-layer network (a hypernetwork) that outputs the settings of a 4-bump relevance curve. The 12 numbers it produces become, for each of the 4 bumps, a width $s_{m}, a$ weight $w_{m},$ and a center $mu_{m}$; push widths and weights through a softplus so they stay positive, and keep centers non-negative (the curve only looks backward in time). Do NOT force the weights to sum to one — letting the total height vary is intentional, because the later normalization across measurements handles scaling. Because these settings come from $z_{q},$ the curve is shaped per query rather than fixed by the designer. 【author decision: whether one shared curve is used for all attention heads and layers, or a separate curve is produced per head and per layer — this trades flexibility against extra parameters and how cleanly the regime signal can be identified.】\n\n*The temporal-relevance kernel $\\phi $ is a causal mixture of M = 4 Gaussian basis components in the elapsed time $\\delta ,$ zero for negative $\\delta $; its weights $w_{m},$ centers $\\mu _{m},$ and widths $s_{m}$ (collectively $\\theta _{q})$ make it non-monotone and able to express a delayed peak — TrajGPT's single decaying exponential is the M = 1, $\\mu  = 0$ special case.*\n$$ \\phi(\\delta;\\, \\theta_q) = \\begin{cases} \\sum_{m=1}^{M} w_m \\, \\exp\\!\\left(-\\dfrac{(\\delta - \\mu_m)^2}{2 s_m^2}\\right), & \\delta \\geq 0 \\\\[2mm] 0, & \\delta < 0 \\end{cases}, \\qquad M = 4 \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Because these curve settings come from $z_{q},$ the relevance curve can be sharp for a deteriorating patient and flat for a stable one — it is inferred per query, not fixed by the designer.\n\n### Continuous-time attention operator\n*Replaces dot-product-plus-time-bias with a content-gate times the time kernel, and stays queryable at any unobserved time.*\n\n4. Swap out ordinary attention. For each pair of a query time $t_{q}$ and an earlier measurement j, the attention weight is the usual content match (scaled dot product of $c_{q}$ and $c_{j})$ MULTIPLIED by the relevance curve evaluated at how long ago the measurement was, $phi(t_{q} -  t_{j})$; compute this in log-space for numerical safety, set the weight to zero for measurements that are in the future relative to $t_{q},$ normalize the weights across measurements, and combine the value vectors $v_{j}$ to get the representation $r(t_{q}).$ The key change is that elapsed time now defines the score rather than being added on top. If a query has no earlier measurements at all, just pass the representation through unchanged via the skip connection so there is nothing to divide by zero.\n\n*The unnormalized attention weight from observation j to query time $t_{q}$ is the content gate (exp of the scaled inner product of content vectors $c_{q}, c_{j})$ multiplied by a continuous temporal-relevance kernel $\\phi $ of the elapsed time $t_{q} -  t_{j}$; normalizing over j and weighting values $v_{j}$ gives the representation $r(t_{q}),$ which replaces the dot-product-plus-additive-time-bias forward pass.*\n$$ a(t_q, j) = \\exp\\!\\left(\\frac{c_q^{\\top} c_j}{\\sqrt{d}}\\right)\\, \\phi(t_q - t_j;\\, \\theta_q), \\qquad r(t_q) = \\sum_{j} \\frac{a(t_q, j)}{\\sum_{j'} a(t_q, j')}\\, v_j \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Now the elapsed time DEFINES the attention score rather than being added on top of it — the central change of the method.\n5. At test time, get the patient's representation at times where nothing was measured straight from the same operator — there is no separate guessing (imputation) module. Lay down query times on an even grid at the dataset's natural spacing (for example, hourly for PhysioNet-2012 vital signs) across the period you care about, and evaluate the representation there; since the relevance curve accepts any real time gap, this just works. If you stack several layers, the upper layers ask about the same fixed grid of times as the first layer, and you can change the grid later without retraining because the curve does not depend on the grid. For classification instead, put the queries at the times things were actually measured and pool them for the classifier.\n   - _Why_: Since the curve is defined for any real time gap, the representation is naturally available at unmeasured times — continuity falls out of attention itself.\n\n### Preserved-property proof\n*Shows the prior fixed-decay attention is a strict special case, so the swap is a re-foundation not just a new bias.*\n\n6. Write down and automatically test the special case that proves nothing was lost. Set the curve to a single bump centered at zero with the hypernetwork frozen to a constant, and check by code that the layer's output exactly equals a hand-written single-shape decay attention (to a tiny tolerance). To match the prior method TrajGPT's exact exponential fade specifically, the per-bump shape has to be an exponential rather than a Gaussian, so test that variant against a hand-written exponential-decay attention too. The point of this step is the argument that the new operator keeps everything the old attention could do and only adds capability — that is the real contribution. 【author decision: make the bumps exponential fades so the old method is exactly the single-bump case, OR keep Gaussian bumps and claim the weaker 'old method is a single-component restriction' result — this fixes exactly what the special-case theorem can assert.】\n   - _Why_: Showing the old method is a special case proves the new operator keeps everything attention could do and only adds capability — this is the real contribution, not the raw swap.\n\n### Mechanism-isolating training\n*Trains everything jointly and provides the FLOP-matched controls that attribute the gain to the regime code.*\n\n7. Train the relevance curve, the hypernetwork, and the GRU together with ordinary gradient descent on the task loss (cross-entropy for EEG/ECG classification; mean-squared error for forecasting), and build in two off-switches used to test the idea, each kept at the same size and compute as the full model. First switch (global curve): keep the GRU and hypernetwork running but feed them a single learned constant instead of $z_{q},$ so one curve is used for every query. Second switch (shuffled regime code): compute $z_{q}$ as usual but then scramble it across patients within each batch before the hypernetwork, so all the computation still happens but the regime code no longer matches its own query. Both switches change only what information $z_{q}$ carries, never the number of parameters or the amount of compute.\n   - _Why_: These switches are the controls that prove the gain really comes from the regime code $z_{q}$ and not from extra parameters, since they keep size and compute identical.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 面向医疗时间序列的状态条件连续时间注意力\n\n**方法名称.** Regime-Conditional Continuous-Time Attention (RC-CTA)\n\n## 研究动机\n医疗时间序列——ICU 生命体征、EEG、ECG、住院记录——是在不规则、不均匀的时刻被测量的，而“什么时候测”本身就是线索：病人变差时医生会更频繁地测。当今最好的 transformer 模型先把信号切成一串固定的 token，再把时间信息当作一个固定的额外成分，硬贴到普通注意力上。比如 TrajGPT 用一个形状固定的指数“衰减”去乘注意力；Medformer（多粒度分块 transformer）把信号切成人工选定的固定长度片段；DNA-T（可变形邻域注意力 transformer）只是挑选看哪些邻近点。这些做法里，“旧的测量值还有多重要”的形状都是模型设计者一次性定好、永不改变的——对稳定病人和正在恶化的病人完全一样。于是这些模型无法表达“同样 6 小时的间隔对稳定病人和恶化病人含义不同”，也无法在没有实际测量的时刻直接给出病人状态，除非再额外接一个单独的插补（imputation）步骤。这不是调参问题，而是从语言模型照搬来的、未经审视的假设：在语言模型里注意力比较的是词 token，时间只是附加项。2024-2025 年最新的系统都恰好停在这一步。如今修复它既廉价又及时：把一个简短的状态编码映射成一条灵活曲线参数的小型“超网络”（hypernetwork）训练稳定，而公开的不规则 ICU 数据集（PhysioNet-2012、MIMIC-III）以及 EEG/ECG 数据集（PTB-XL、TUEV）提供了检验该思路所需的、状态切换且不规则采样的数据。一旦填补该空白，三件事同时成为可能：同样的流逝时间会随病人当前状态被赋予不同权重；可以直接从注意力读取任意时刻（包括未测时刻）的病人表示，无需单独的插补模块；并且旧的固定衰减方法（TrajGPT）成为新方法的一个简单特例——使这成为对算子的重新奠基，而非又一个附加件。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景\n\n1. 把每条不规则多变量序列读成一袋独立测量，不对齐到规则时间网格：每个测量是一个 token，包含三样东西——数值 $x_{j}$、真实时间戳 $t_{j}$、以及它来自哪个通道（哪个生命体征/导联）。通过对数值做线性投影再加上一个可学习的逐通道嵌入（标记它属于哪个通道），把每个测量变成内容向量 $c_{j}$ 和数值向量 $v_{j}$。保持各通道不对齐（不要把不同通道的测量强行对到共享时间点），从而精确保留每个通道原始的不均匀时间。\n   - _为什么_: 保留原始不均匀的时间，意味着任意两点之间的流逝时间仍是新核能真正使用的实数，而不会被网格化抹掉。\n\n### 状态编码器\n*把病人当前的动态状态读成一个简短的每查询潜在编码。*\n\n2. 对每个查询时刻 $t_{q}$，把病人当前动态概括成一个简短的 16 维状态编码 $z_{q}$。取严格早于 $t_{q}$ 的、跨所有通道最近的 32 个测量，按时间顺序送入一个小型单层门控循环单元(Gated Recurrent Unit, GRU)——每个输入是测量数值、它发生在多久以前的平滑编码（$t_{q}$ 减去其时间戳）、以及它的通道标签——再用线性层读出 GRU 的最终状态得到 $z_{q}$。由于窗口是以“距 $t_{q}$ 多久之前”来定义的，无论 $t_{q}$ 是有测量的时刻还是想要预测的未来时刻，同一套做法都适用；若早于 $t_{q}$ 的测量不足 32 个，则用一个可学习的填充 token 把更早的空位补满，使 GRU 始终看到 32 个输入。\n\n*核的形状参数 $\\theta _{q}$ 由 2 层超网络 H 根据每查询的潜在状态编码 $z_{q}$ 生成，$z_{q}$ 由小型 GRU 从 $t_{q}$ 之前最近的观测窗口（长度 W）编码而来；softplus 约束保证 $s_{m}$、$w_{m}$ 非负。*\n$$ \\theta_q = \\{w_m, \\mu_m, s_m\\}_{m=1}^{M} = H(z_q), \\qquad z_q = \\mathrm{GRU}\\big(\\{(x_j, t_j) : t_j \\in [t_q - W,\\, t_q)\\}\\big) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这个编码就是模型判断病人当前是稳定还是恶化的方式，而这正决定了后面时间相关性曲线的形状。\n\n### 核超网络\n*把状态编码转成一条灵活、可非单调的时间相关性曲线的形状。*\n\n3. 把状态编码 $z_{q}$ 送入一个小型 2 层网络（超网络 hypernetwork），输出一条 4 峰相关性曲线的设置。它产生的 12 个数对应 4 个峰，每个峰一个宽度 $s_{m}$、一个权重 $w_{m}$、一个中心 $mu_{m}$；用 softplus 让宽度和权重保持为正，并让中心非负（该曲线只回看过去）。不要强制权重之和为 1——让总高度可变是有意为之，因为后面对各测量做的归一化会处理缩放。由于这些设置来自 $z_{q}$，曲线是逐查询塑形的，而非由设计者固定。【作者需决定：是所有注意力头与各层共用一条曲线，还是每个注意力头、每层各自生成一条曲线——这在表达力与额外参数、以及状态信号的可辨识性之间做权衡。】\n\n*时间相关性核 $\\phi $ 是关于流逝时间 $\\delta $ 的因果型 M = 4 高斯基混合，$\\delta $ 为负时取零；其权重 $w_{m}$、中心 $\\mu _{m}$、宽度 $s_{m}$（合记为 $\\theta _{q}$）使其非单调且可表达延迟峰值——TrajGPT 的单一衰减指数即 M = 1、$\\mu  = 0$ 的特例。*\n$$ \\phi(\\delta;\\, \\theta_q) = \\begin{cases} \\sum_{m=1}^{M} w_m \\, \\exp\\!\\left(-\\dfrac{(\\delta - \\mu_m)^2}{2 s_m^2}\\right), & \\delta \\geq 0 \\\\[2mm] 0, & \\delta < 0 \\end{cases}, \\qquad M = 4 \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 因为这些曲线参数来自 $z_{q}$，相关性曲线对恶化病人可以很尖、对稳定病人可以很平——它是每查询推断出来的，而非设计者固定的。\n\n### 连续时间注意力算子\n*用内容门控乘以时间核取代点积加时间偏置，并在任意未测时刻仍可查询。*\n\n4. 替换普通注意力。对每一对“查询时刻 $t_{q}$ 与更早的测量 j”，注意力权重是常规的内容匹配（$c_{q}$ 与 $c_{j}$ 的缩放点积）乘以相关性曲线在“该测量发生在多久以前”处的取值 $phi(t_{q} -  t_{j})$；为数值稳定在对数空间计算，对相对 $t_{q}$ 在未来的测量把权重置零，跨测量做归一化，再组合数值向量 $v_{j}$ 得到表示 $r(t_{q})$。关键改动是：流逝时间现在“定义”了分数，而不是被加在上面。若某个查询完全没有更早的测量，就通过跳跃连接原样传递表示，从而不会出现除以零。\n\n*观测 j 对查询时刻 $t_{q}$ 的未归一化注意力权重 = 内容门控（内容向量 $c_{q}$、$c_{j}$ 缩放内积的 exp）乘以关于流逝时间 $t_{q} -  t_{j}$ 的连续时间相关性核 $\\phi $；对 j 归一化并加权 $v_{j}$ 即得表示 $r(t_{q})$，它取代了点积加可加时间偏置的前向计算。*\n$$ a(t_q, j) = \\exp\\!\\left(\\frac{c_q^{\\top} c_j}{\\sqrt{d}}\\right)\\, \\phi(t_q - t_j;\\, \\theta_q), \\qquad r(t_q) = \\sum_{j} \\frac{a(t_q, j)}{\\sum_{j'} a(t_q, j')}\\, v_j \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 现在流逝时间“定义”了注意力分数，而不是被加在上面——这是方法的核心改动。\n5. 测试时，直接从同一算子读取“没有测量过的时刻”的病人表示——不需要单独的猜测（插补 imputation）模块。在你关心的时间段内，按数据集的自然间隔铺设均匀的查询时间网格（例如 PhysioNet-2012 生命体征按小时），并在这些时刻评估表示；由于相关性曲线接受任意实数时间间隔，这自然成立。若堆叠多层，上层与第一层询问同一组固定的时间网格，且之后可不重训就更换网格，因为曲线不依赖网格。若做分类，则把查询放在实际有测量的时刻，并汇聚它们供分类器使用。\n   - _为什么_: 由于曲线对任意实数时间间隔都有定义，表示在未测时刻自然可得——连续性从注意力本身导出。\n\n### 保性质证明\n*证明此前的固定衰减注意力是其严格特例，使该替换是重新奠基而非又一种偏置。*\n\n6. 写出并自动测试那个“证明没有任何损失”的特例。把曲线设为单个、中心在零的峰，并将超网络冻结为常数，用代码检查该层的输出在极小容差内精确等于手写的单形状衰减注意力。若要专门匹配此前方法 TrajGPT 的精确指数衰减，单峰形状必须是指数而非高斯，因此也要把该变体与手写的指数衰减注意力作对比测试。本步骤的意义在于论证：新算子保留了旧注意力能做的一切、只是增加了新能力——这才是真正的贡献。【作者需决定：把峰设为指数衰减、使旧方法恰为单峰特例，或保留高斯峰、只声称较弱的“旧方法是单分量限制”结论——这决定了该特例定理究竟能断言什么。】\n   - _为什么_: 证明旧方法是一个特例，说明新算子保留了注意力原有的全部能力、只是增加了新能力——这才是真正的贡献，而非单纯的替换。\n\n### 机制隔离训练\n*联合训练全部组件，并提供算力对齐的对照实验，把增益归因于状态编码。*\n\n7. 用普通梯度下降在任务损失上联合训练相关性曲线、超网络和 GRU（EEG/ECG 分类用交叉熵，预测用均方误差 mean-squared error），并内置两个用于检验思路的“关闭开关”，每个都与完整模型保持同样规模和算力。第一个开关（全局曲线）：让 GRU 和超网络照常运行，但喂给它们一个可学习的常数而非 $z_{q}$，从而对每个查询都用同一条曲线。第二个开关（打乱状态编码）：照常计算 $z_{q}$，但在送入超网络前于每个批内按病人打乱它，使全部计算照常发生、而状态编码不再对应其自身的查询。两个开关都只改变 $z_{q}$ 携带的信息，绝不改变参数量或算力。\n   - _为什么_: 这些开关是对照实验，证明增益确实来自状态编码 $z_{q}$ 而非额外参数，因为它们让规模和计算量保持一致。\n\n"},{"id":"23","run_dir":"run_prompt23_visualspace","index":23,"title":"Evidence-Calibrated Visual Space: Per-Region Confidence for Feed-Forward Reconstruction from Any Views","title_zh":"证据校准的视觉空间：面向任意视图前馈重建的逐区域置信度","method_name":"Evidence-Calibrated Visual Space (ECVS)","hook":"Today's feed-forward recovery networks return the visual space recovered from arbitrary views as a single deterministic geometry field in which a surface triangulated by ten overlapping views and a surface invented behind a single occluder are rendered with identical apparent authority. We show the network already contains the signal needed to tell them apart — its own cross-view predictive disagreement for each 3D location — and that reading it out yields a calibrated per-region confidence the deterministic field structurally cannot express.","anchor_pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","anchor_pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","domain_category":"3D Vision & Scene Reconstruction","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved feed-forward recovery method returns, alongside the recovered visual space, a per-location signal of how strongly each recovered point/region is constrained by the input views versus completed by the model's priors — so consumers cannot separate measured geometry from confident invention (frontier-leaf residual of VGGT openalex:W4413146238 and GGRt openalex:W4403942234).","pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by diagnosing that the missing evidence signal is already latent in the frozen recovery backbone as cross-view predictive disagreement, and minimizing a label-free disagreement-calibration objective on a surgically small uncertainty head while the backbone stays frozen — the manufactured internal-state readout becomes the per-region confidence the deterministic field lacked.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved method tests whether the recovery of the visual space from arbitrary views must commit to a single point estimate of geometry at all, rather than expressing the recovered space as a distribution whose spread varies with how much each region was actually observed (subtractive: the deterministic-single-field assumption that every frontier leaf — VGGT openalex:W4413146238, GGRt openalex:W4403942234, GC-NeRF openalex:W4403791234 — silently inherits from the regression/optimization ances","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by relocating the representational locus of the recovered space from a single deterministic point-estimate field to a per-location evidence distribution, and showing the old locus is structurally incapable of expressing observation-dependent spread — the same disagreement readout the anchor manufactures becomes the new locus, so the audit ships inside the runnable method rather than as a separate claim.","is_anchor":false},{"gap":"No retrieved method makes the informativeness of a candidate new viewpoint computable directly from a feed-forward recovery of the current views without first optimizing a per-scene model — FisherRF (openalex:W4403770427) needs a fitted radiance field to exist before it can score a view (frontier-leaf residual on the active-capture line).","pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by recasting next-best-view selection as a submodular subset-selection measurement over the same per-region evidence posterior: each candidate viewpoint is scored by its expected reduction of posterior uncertainty mass, evaluated in one feed-forward pass with no per-scene optimization, deleting the fitted-radiance-field prerequisite FisherRF required.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"3D computer vision / neural scene reconstruction (recovering scene geometry and appearance — 'the visual space' — from arbitrary, possibly unposed and sparse, camera views)","n_papers":40,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":27},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":20,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Gaussian Splatting: 3D Reconstruction and Novel View Synthesis: A Review"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Flash3D: Feed-Forward Generalisable 3D Scene Reconstruction from a Single Image"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Deformable 3D Gaussians for High-Fidelity Monocular Dynamic Scene Reconstruction"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Gaussian Splatting SLAM"},{"source":"openalex","title":"SplaTAM: Splat, Track &amp; Map 3D Gaussians for Dense RGB-D SLAM"},{"source":"openalex","title":"ReconFusion: 3D Reconstruction with Diffusion Priors"}],"more":14},{"year":2025,"n":20,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Quantum Implicit Neural Representations for 3D Scene Reconstruction and Novel View Synthesis"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"LL-Gaussian: Low-Light Scene Reconstruction and Enhancement via Gaussian Splatting for Novel View Synthesis"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Training-Free Instance-Aware 3D Scene Reconstruction and Diffusion-Based View Synthesis from Sparse Images"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Radiant Triangle Soup with Soft Connectivity Forces for 3D Reconstruction and Novel View Synthesis"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"BlockGaussian: Efficient Large-Scale Scene Novel View Synthesis via Adaptive Block-Based Gaussian Splatting"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"MPM-GS: Optimizing Sparse-View 3D Scene Reconstruction with Virtual View Rendering and Multimodal Regularization"}],"more":14}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":9,"share":0.225},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":9,"share":0.225},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":7,"share":0.175},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":7,"share":0.175},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":6,"share":0.15},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":6,"share":0.15},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":6,"share":0.15},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":6,"share":0.15}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Recent feed-forward models recover the visual space from one-to-many unposed views in a single pass — VGGT (openalex:W4413146238) regresses camera, depth, point maps and tracks for 1..N images, and GGRt (openalex:W4403942234) produces pose-free generalizable Gaussians in real time — but each emits ONE deterministic geometry-and-appearance field with no scalar that distinguishes regions the input views actually constrain from regions the model had to invent to complete occluded or never-observed parts of the scene. The same failure persists in the per-scene optimization line: GC-NeRF (openalex:W4403791234) jointly fits a radiance field and poses from as few as two unposed views, and ReconFusion (openalex:W4402667896) uses a diffusion prior to hallucinate plausible content at camera poses beyond the captured set, yet both return the completed field as if uniformly trustworthy. Because the recovered space therefore carries no per-location indication of how strongly it is pinned by evidence, any downstream consumer — a robot planning around it, an editor compositing into it, an active-capture loop deciding where to look next — cannot tell a measured surface from a confident guess, and FisherRF (openalex:W4403770427), the one retrieved method that reasons about view informativeness, measures uncertainty over radiance-field parameters of a single per-scene model rather than over the recovered 3D space itself.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4413146238","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"VGGT is a single large transformer that ingests 1..N RGB views and directly predicts camera parameters, depth maps, dense point maps and 3D point tracks in one feed-forward pass, removing iterative bundle adjustment. Its method produces a single deterministic point/geometry field per input set — the prediction heads emit point coordinates with no posterior or calibrated per-point confidence over the scene, so regions reconstructed from strong multi-view overlap and regions completed from a single grazing or occluded view are returned with identical apparent authority, and overlapping per-frame predictions are reconciled into one field without exposing where they disagreed."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4403942234","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"GGRt makes pose-free generalizable 3D Gaussian splatting run in real time, predicting Gaussians directly from unposed images without per-scene optimization. It outputs a single deterministic Gaussian field and provides no per-Gaussian or per-region measure of whether a primitive is supported by triangulated multi-view evidence versus extrapolated from a monocular cue, so unobserved geometry is rendered with the same confidence as observed geometry."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4402667896","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"ReconFusion regularizes a few-shot NeRF with a diffusion prior so it can render plausible content at novel camera poses beyond the captured views. The diffusion prior actively synthesizes content for under-observed regions but the pipeline folds this hallucinated content into the same radiance field as the observed content with no flag distinguishing prior-driven completion from view-constrained reconstruction."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4403770427","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"FisherRF uses Fisher information over a radiance field's parameters to pick the next-best view to capture. Its uncertainty is defined on the parameters of one already-fitted per-scene model and requires that optimized model to exist, so it neither transfers across scenes nor yields a per-location confidence over the recovered 3D space produced by a feed-forward, pose-free recovery model."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"3D computer vision / neural scene reconstruction (recovering scene geometry and appearance — 'the visual space' — from arbitrary, possibly unposed and sparse, camera views)","venue":"CVPR / ICCV / NeurIPS / ICLR (top vision + ML venues)","time":"2026 submission cycle","data":["RealEstate10K","DL3DV / MVImgNet","CO3Dv2","ScanNet++ / Replica (indoor)","Tanks-and-Temples (in-the-wild evaluation)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher comfortable with feed-forward 3D reconstruction (DUSt3R/VGGT-style transformers), Gaussian splatting, and probabilistic modeling","preference":"both","baseline":"VGGT (feed-forward geometry transformer) and pose-free generalizable splatting (GGRt); per-scene pose-free NeRF/GS (COLMAP-Free 3DGS, GC-NeRF) as the optimization-based comparison","limitation":"Feed-forward recovery of the visual space from arbitrary views produces a single deterministic geometry/appearance prediction and gives the downstream user no signal about WHICH parts of the recovered space are actually constrained by the input views versus invented to fill occluded or unobserved regions.","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The single shared object that all three legs read from and write to is the EVIDENCE POSTERIOR over the recovered visual space: for each recovered 3D location x (a point in the dense point map / depth field the backbone already emits) a scalar confidence c(x) in [0,1] together with a predicted geometric spread sigma(x) in scene units (meters), where low c(x) / high sigma(x) means 'completed from prior', high c(x) / low sigma(x) means 'constrained by the input views'. Leg 1 (anchor, self_supervised_signal_engineering / C07): the manufactured signal is CROSS-VIEW PREDICTIVE DISAGREEMENT d(x). We run the frozen feed-forward backbone (VGGT-class transformer, weights fixed) and read its per-frame geometry heads: for input view set V, the backbone already predicts, for each frame i that sees x, a per-frame 3D position p_i(x) (obtained by unprojecting frame i's predicted depth at the pixel that the backbone's predicted camera maps x to). d(x) is the weighted variance of {p_i(x)} across the frames covering x, d(x) = sum_i w_i || p_i(x) - pbar(x) ||^2 / sum_i w_i, where pbar(x) is the weight-mean, w_i is the backbone's existing per-frame confidence logit at that pixel passed through a softmax over covering frames, and a location seen by <2 frames is assigned d(x) = D_max (a fixed large sentinel = the 95th percentile of training-set d over multi-covered points, a single scalar hyperparameter). We then train ONLY a small two-layer MLP head g_phi (the surgically small lever; backbone frozen) that maps the backbone's per-point feature plus d(x) to (c(x), sigma(x)). The label-free calibration objective is a held-out-view consistency loss: split V into a context subset and a probe subset, recover geometry from context only, and at each location visible in a probe view use the probe's unprojected position as a pseudo-ground-truth target to make sigma(x) the negative-log-likelihood-minimizing predictive std (a Gaussian NLL over the probe residual) — no human labels, the supervision is manufactured entirely from withheld input views. The C07 stabilizer against the degenerate all-confident collapse is a coverage-anchored prior term that pulls c(x) toward a low constant wherever fewer than 2 context frames cover x, plus a sharpness penalty on g_phi. Leg 2 (assumption_audit_and_pivot / C01): the audit relocates the representational locus of the recovered space from the deterministic field {pbar(x)} (the only object VGGT/GGRt expose) to the evidence-indexed pair (pbar(x), c(x), sigma(x)); the mechanistic account of why the new locus carries the signal is that finite views leave a non-trivial null space of scene completions consistent with them, and cross-view disagreement d(x) is a computable lower-bound proxy for the spread of that null space, which a single point estimate provably cannot represent (one number per location cannot encode observation-dependent spread). This leg adds no new module — it is the claim that the leg-1 object is the correct recovered-space representation, validated empirically by the selective-prediction separation below. Leg 3 (reframe_as_solvable_object / C00): next-best-view is recast as submodular subset selection. Define the per-candidate-viewpoint utility U(q) = expected reduction in total posterior uncertainty mass if viewpoint q were added, approximated in one forward pass by re-running g_phi on the union of current views' features and a cheap geometric prediction of which currently-low-c(x) locations q would newly co-observe (computed from the backbone's predicted cameras and depths, no scene re-optimization). Greedy maximization of U over a candidate set gives the next view; submodularity of coverage gives the standard (1 - 1/e) guarantee. All three legs are one paper because they share one object: leg 1 manufactures it, leg 2 argues it is the right recovered-space representation, leg 3 consumes it. Quantitatively, VGGT (fulltext openalex:W4413146238) reports point-map accuracy but emits no per-point posterior, and FisherRF (openalex:W4403770427) computes its information measure over a fitted radiance field's parameters; we measure expected-uncertainty-reduction over the recovered 3D space directly from the feed-forward pass, a different quantity over a different object, so no exponent or rate is transported across regimes.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The gaps share machinery because they are three operations on one object (the evidence posterior): the evidence given (manufacturing the signal), the claim that this object replaces the deterministic field (the audit/pivot), and a downstream query over it (active capture) — making them separate modules would staple three papers together and break the shared_object thread. I considered making leg 1 an ensemble / MC-dropout uncertainty (rejected: that estimates model-parameter uncertainty, not view-constraint, and would not separate 'occluded but high-prior-confidence' from 'multi-view-constrained'); I considered a diffusion-completion confidence (rejected as a regression onto collateral node c0, since it would re-introduce generative completion as the signal source). I deliberately avoided the regression nodes the lineage flags: NOT diffusion scene completion (c0) — the signal is the backbone's own cross-view disagreement, not a generative prior; NOT Fisher-information over a per-scene fitted model (c1) — leg 3 evaluates utility directly on the feed-forward posterior with no fitted radiance field; and NOT re-fitting one deterministic field (n0-n2 ancestors) — the backbone is frozen and we only add a calibration head.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: take a frozen VGGT-class backbone, attach the calibration head g_phi, train it with context/probe view splitting on a multi-view dataset with geometric ground truth (e.g. ScanNet++ or DL3DV with LiDAR/COLMAP depth), and on held-out scenes measure the SELECTIVE-PREDICTION curve — geometric error (depth-L1 or Chamfer) of retained locations as a function of confidence-coverage. If the candidate works, error-at-coverage decreases monotonically as coverage is restricted to higher c(x) (retaining only evidence-constrained regions), i.e. the area-under-the-error-coverage-curve is strictly below the deterministic-field baseline that has no notion of confidence. The named load-bearing variable is the cross-view predictive disagreement d(x); the mechanism distinguisher is a negative-control intervention that replaces d(x) with a distribution-matched random permutation across locations (same marginal, location signal destroyed) and retrains g_phi — the prediction is that the downstream selective-prediction error-at-low-coverage rises back to the no-selection baseline level (the task-outcome metric, geometric error at fixed coverage, returns to baseline), which 'the head still emits some sigma' alone cannot explain because a permuted d retains identical calibration capacity but no location-specific evidence. A positive control — a head consuming only d(x) and no backbone feature — should recover most of the selective-prediction gain, constructively identifying d(x) as the carrier of the evidence signal.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4413146238","delta":"VGGT constructs a deterministic per-point geometry field with per-pixel confidence logits used only to weight fusion; we construct from those same logits a calibrated per-region evidence posterior (c(x), sigma(x)) trained by held-out-view consistency, a quantity VGGT never produces or calibrates, separating view-constrained from prior-completed geometry."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4403770427","delta":"FisherRF computes Fisher information over the parameters of an already-fitted per-scene radiance field to plan views; we compute expected uncertainty-mass reduction over the recovered 3D space directly from a single frozen feed-forward pass with no per-scene model, making next-best-view a submodular query over the feed-forward posterior rather than over fitted parameters."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4402667896","delta":"ReconFusion synthesizes plausible content for under-observed regions with a diffusion prior and folds it indistinguishably into the field; we do the opposite — we leave geometry as-is but attach a per-location flag that marks exactly which regions are prior-completed vs view-constrained, an evidence label ReconFusion never emits."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4403942234","delta":"GGRt emits a deterministic pose-free Gaussian field with no per-primitive support signal; we add a frozen-backbone calibration head whose cross-view-disagreement-derived confidence tells, per region, whether a primitive is triangulation-supported or monocularly extrapolated."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4403770427","what_step_was_missed":"FisherRF measures information over a per-scene radiance field's parameters, so its uncertainty is defined only after that field is optimized; it never constructed a per-location evidence quantity over the recovered 3D space that is computable from a feed-forward recovery of the current views alone. The missing step is manufacturing such a quantity from the backbone's own cross-view predictive disagreement and calibrating it by held-out-view consistency, which would have let view-informativeness be scored without ever fitting a scene model — the prerequisite that makes the active-capture leg a one-pass query."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":354,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"No hard floor fired (gap_closure_reject_check has no candidate_match: yes; anti_pattern matched_pattern_id is null; the paper_pointed_threat is mechanism-adjacent not exact-mechanism). But paper_pointed_threat.subsumption_argument identifies two highly specific concurrent papers (Trust3R, AREA3D) that subsume the GENERIC versions of legs 1 and 3, and gap_closure_reject_check's C01 novelty-boundary lesson ('Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work ... collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured') is borderline-triggered by exactly this overlap — both load-bearing. Per the heuristic 'choose revise when paper_pointed_threat exists AND addressable_via names a specific candidate field', verdict is revise to add the two threats to differentiation_from_lit and sharpen the distinctive locus claim.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved feed-forward recovery method returns, alongside the recovered visual space, a per-location signal of how strongly each recovered point/region is constrained by the input views versus completed by the model's priors — so consumers cannot separate measured geometry from confident invention (frontier-leaf residual of VGGT openalex:W4413146238 and GGRt openalex:W4403942234).","main_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"A manufactured internal signal whose validity silently rests on an assumption that does not survive deployment (model calibration, a known-finite set of shift types, or covert use of target/test-set information amounting to label leakage), and a second shape of recombining well-known components without a single load-bearing mechanistic insight.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A label-free signal whose validity depends on model calibration silently fails on exactly the deep networks known to be poorly calibrated — validate a surrogate where its core assumption is weakest, not where it is convenient.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The signal is cross-view geometric disagreement d(x) (a physical variance in scene units), not a calibrated softmax probability, so its validity does not rest on backbone calibration; the held-out-view NLL calibration directly fits the spread."},{"lesson_quoted":"Using target or test-set information during adaptation invites a label-leakage objection that undermines the very source-free, label-free deployment setting the method claims.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Supervision is manufactured by withholding INPUT views (context/probe split) at training time on training scenes; no test-scene or ground-truth-geometry labels enter the head's training, so there is no leakage."},{"lesson_quoted":"A multi-branch or ensemble reweighting mechanism that overlaps with standard multi-task/mixture-of-experts ensembling must explicitly beat both the single-model and the standard-ensemble baselines, or the gain is credited to prior art.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"There is no ensemble — a single frozen backbone is read for per-frame predictions; disagreement is across the views the model already ingests, not across separately trained models."},{"lesson_quoted":"Importing a generic continual-learning blending or interpolation technique into a new modality without identifying that modality's specific dynamics lever reads as recombination, not contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The load-bearing insight is modality-specific (cross-view disagreement as a null-space-spread proxy for multi-view geometry), not a generic blending technique imported wholesale."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved method tests whether the recovery of the visual space from arbitrary views must commit to a single point estimate of geometry at all, rather than expressing the recovered space as a distribution whose spread varies with how much each region was actually observed (subtractive: the deterministic-single-field assumption that every frontier leaf — VGGT openalex:W4413146238, GGRt openalex:W4403942234, GC-NeRF openalex:W4403791234 — silently inherits from the regression/optimization ancestor that fits one field to the views).","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"A successful relocation that is demonstrated but not adversarially closed, or a novelty-boundary collapse where the 'new' locus turns out to be one a prior paper already used and the work fails to quantify what is genuinely different.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work — normalization statistics, activation-similarity losses, semantic concept triggers — collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"Concurrent feed-forward-uncertainty work (Trust3R evidential head; MASt3R built-in confidence map) also moves off a bare deterministic field, so the candidate must explicitly measure what its evidence locus (cross-view-disagreement, view-constrained-vs-invented) carries that an evidential-head locus does not — currently asserted but not quantified against those loci."},{"lesson_quoted":"Demonstrating the new locus only on fixed, non-adaptive or outdated baselines while omitting any account of why it works reads as a stacked pipeline of existing components rather than a principled shift.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism gives a structural account (finite views leave a null space of consistent completions; d(x) lower-bounds its spread) and the falsification has a causal negative control, so it is not a bare demonstration."},{"lesson_quoted":"A defense whose relocation silently depends on a clean reference model or a known anomaly distribution reintroduces precisely the strong assumption the move was supposed to eliminate.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The locus needs only the frozen backbone's own per-view predictions; no clean reference scene or known shift distribution is assumed."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved method makes the informativeness of a candidate new viewpoint computable directly from a feed-forward recovery of the current views without first optimizing a per-scene model — FisherRF (openalex:W4403770427) needs a fitted radiance field to exist before it can score a view (frontier-leaf residual on the active-capture line).","main_pattern":"reframe_as_solvable_object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Treating the reframing as a mechanical wrapper — pointing an established attribution/estimation tool at a new domain without re-deriving why the resulting scores are faithful — supplying the computation but not the causal validation.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Conflating a methodological artifact — a computation-granularity difference, a degenerate zero baseline — with genuine signal undermines the entire premise once the confound is identified.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The next-best-view utility is validated by capture-efficiency vs random/heuristic views and shares the negative-control on d(x), so the gain is not a granularity artifact."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pointing an off-the-shelf decomposition at a coarser input granularity without showing the coarser units preserve the signal reads as a wrapper, not a contribution.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"Submodular subset selection is off-the-shelf machinery; the contribution lives in the utility being computed over the feed-forward evidence posterior with no per-scene model, which must be shown to preserve the informativeness signal rather than just wrapping greedy selection — addressed by the capture-efficiency experiment but overlaps with AREA3D's decoupled view-uncertainty."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No Reject lesson is marked candidate_match: yes, so no hard floor fires. The borderlines are the C01 novelty-boundary lesson on the audit gap (evidence locus vs concurrent evidential-head / built-in-confidence loci must be measured, not asserted) and the C00 wrapper lesson on the active-capture gap (utility must be shown to preserve signal over the feed-forward posterior, overlapping AREA3D's decoupled view-uncertainty) — both load-bearing and both pointing at the same concurrent-work differentiation need."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved feed-forward recovery method returns, alongside the recovered visual space, a per-location signal of how strongly each recovered point/region is constrained by the input views versus completed by the model's priors — so consumers cannot separate measured geometry from confident invention (frontier-leaf residual of VGGT openalex:W4413146238 and GGRt openalex:W4403942234).","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Treat an already-trained model's own internal-state readouts as the manufactured supervisory signal, pairing a mechanistic diagnosis that localizes the failure with a surgically confined correction on a minimal lever while the backbone stays frozen, plus an explicit stabilizer against degenerate collapse.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"Performed: the diagnosis localizes the missing-evidence failure to cross-view predictive disagreement d(x) already latent in the frozen backbone; the correction is confined to a 2-layer MLP head g_phi (tiny lever) with backbone frozen; the coverage-anchored low-c prior + sharpness penalty are the explicit stabilizers against the all-confident collapse.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved method tests whether the recovery of the visual space from arbitrary views must commit to a single point estimate of geometry at all, rather than expressing the recovered space as a distribution whose spread varies with how much each region was actually observed (subtractive: the deterministic-single-field assumption that every frontier leaf — VGGT openalex:W4413146238, GGRt openalex:W4403942234, GC-NeRF openalex:W4403791234 — silently inherits from the regression/optimization ancestor that fits one field to the views).","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"The audited assumption is about the representational locus at which a property is presumed enforced, and the tactical move is to relocate to a different locus the field treated as irrelevant or invariant, with a mechanistic account of why the property must manifest there too.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"Performed: core_mechanism relocates the recovered space from the deterministic field {pbar(x)} (the only locus VGGT/GGRt expose) to the evidence-indexed locus (pbar, c, sigma), and gives the structural account (finite views leave a null space of consistent completions a single point estimate cannot represent).","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved method makes the informativeness of a candidate new viewpoint computable directly from a feed-forward recovery of the current views without first optimizing a per-scene model — FisherRF (openalex:W4403770427) needs a fitted radiance field to exist before it can score a view (frontier-leaf residual on the active-capture line).","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Recast an opaque transparency/uncertainty question as a concrete measurement over a well-studied object (subset selection, estimator, decomposition), buying tractability with one compression trick, and certifying fidelity causally or by proof rather than by plausibility.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"Performed: next-best-view is recast as submodular subset selection over the evidence posterior; the compression trick is the one-pass cheap geometric prediction of newly-co-observed low-c locations; fidelity is certified by the capture-efficiency experiment plus the shared causal negative control on d(x), and submodularity gives the (1-1/e) guarantee.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"All three legs perform their cluster's distinctive signature move — C07's diagnose-localize/tiny-lever/stabilize, C01's locus relocation with mechanistic account, C00's measurement-object reframe with causal certification — rather than only the parent gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["self_supervised_signal_engineering","assumption_audit_and_pivot","reframe_as_solvable_object"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as a component; the candidate's composition_set contains none of them, so no anti-pattern matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:769f1c609ba5dc82c962f93ddc54bcdbc60ed753","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"Trust3R (2026-05, 'Evidential Uncertainty for Feed-Forward 3D Reconstruction') directly targets the same residue leg 1 claims — that feed-forward geometry models' confidence scores are heuristic and fail to indicate where geometry can be trusted — and ships a probabilistically grounded per-point uncertainty via a Normal-Inverse-Wishart evidential head yielding a Student-t per-point distribution. This makes the bare claim 'we add a calibrated per-point uncertainty to feed-forward reconstruction' no longer novel; the candidate stands or falls on whether its DISTINCTIVE construction — manufacturing the signal from the backbone's own cross-view predictive disagreement d(x) and calibrating it by held-out-INPUT-view consistency, explicitly to separate view-constrained from prior-completed (invented) geometry, then querying it for pose-free next-best-view — delivers something Trust3R's single-pass evidential output head does not (Trust3R learns an output distribution per point but does not derive its uncertainty from cross-view agreement, does not calibrate against withheld input views, and does not frame the quantity as constrained-vs-invented evidence or use it for active capture). A second, near-equally-specific threat is AREA3D (semanticscholar:04b4b42c67d632eec4af7f96b5f60bcc3e96387d, 2025-11), which decouples view-uncertainty modeling from a feed-forward reconstructor for active reconstruction without online optimization — overlapping leg 3 directly; the candidate's leg 3 survives only if it is sharpened to the specific submodular-over-the-cross-view-disagreement-posterior formulation rather than a generic decoupled view-uncertainty score, and AREA3D leans on a vision-language model for semantic guidance whereas the candidate's utility is purely the geometric evidence posterior. The overlap is mechanism-adjacent, not exact-mechanism: neither threat uses cross-view predictive disagreement as the manufactured signal nor held-out-input-view consistency as the calibration, so the threat is addressable.","addressable_via":"Add Trust3R and AREA3D to differentiation_from_lit with substantive deltas, and sharpen core_mechanism / hook so the headline contribution is the cross-view-disagreement-derived, held-out-view-calibrated, constrained-vs-invented evidence locus (and a purely-geometric submodular active-capture query) rather than generic feed-forward uncertainty."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat: Trust3R (semanticscholar:769f1c609ba5dc82c962f93ddc54bcdbc60ed753) and AREA3D (semanticscholar:04b4b42c67d632eec4af7f96b5f60bcc3e96387d) are concurrent feed-forward-uncertainty / active-feed-forward-reconstruction papers not currently differentiated.","fix_direction":"Append two entries to differentiation_from_lit: (1) vs Trust3R — they learn a Normal-Inverse-Wishart evidential output head giving a Student-t per-point distribution; we instead derive the signal from the frozen backbone's cross-view predictive disagreement d(x) and calibrate it by held-out-INPUT-view consistency, explicitly separating view-constrained from prior-invented geometry, a constrained-vs-invented evidence quantity their output-distribution head does not produce. (2) vs AREA3D — they decouple a view-uncertainty model plus a vision-language semantic guide for active reconstruction; we compute next-best-view as a purely-geometric submodular query over the same cross-view-disagreement evidence posterior with no VLM and no separate uncertainty model. Keep deltas substantive (what is derived/constructed/measured), not methodological."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","issue":"gap_closure_reject_check C01 borderline + C00 borderline: the evidence-locus and active-capture contributions must be explicitly distinguished from concurrent evidential-head and decoupled-view-uncertainty loci, not asserted.","fix_direction":"Add one or two sentences to core_mechanism making the distinctive locus explicit and measurable: state that, unlike an evidential output head (which fits a per-point output distribution regardless of how many views saw the point), the cross-view-disagreement locus is by construction near-zero where multi-view triangulation agrees and large where a region is monocularly completed, so c(x) measures view-constraint rather than generic predictive variance; and that the active-capture utility is evaluated solely on this geometric evidence posterior (no semantic/VLM input), distinguishing it from VLM-guided active feed-forward reconstruction. Do not alter falsification_prediction or compute_budget."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Appended two substantive deltas — vs Trust3R (their NIW evidential output head yields a per-point Student-t distribution; we derive the signal from frozen-backbone cross-view predictive disagreement d(x) calibrated by held-out-INPUT-view consistency, a constrained-vs-invented evidence quantity their head does not produce) and vs AREA3D (their decoupled view-uncertainty model + VLM semantic guide; our next-best-view is a purely-geometric submodular query over the same cross-view-disagreement posterior, no VLM, no separate uncertainty model)."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added two locus-distinction sentences making the contribution measurable: c(x) from cross-view disagreement is near-zero where multi-view triangulation agrees and large where a region is monocularly completed (so it measures view-constraint, unlike an evidential output head that fits a per-point distribution regardless of how many views saw the point), and the leg-3 active-capture utility is evaluated solely on this geometric evidence posterior with no semantic/VLM input (distinguishing it from VLM-guided active feed-forward reconstruction)."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Evidence-Calibrated Visual Space: Per-Region Confidence for Feed-Forward Reconstruction from Any Views\n\n**Method.** Evidence-Calibrated Visual Space (ECVS)\n\n## Motivation\nModern networks can look at a handful of photos of a scene — even without knowing where the cameras were — and, in a single forward pass, output the full 3D shape and look of that scene (we call this 'recovering the visual space'). VGGT (Visual Geometry Grounded Transformer) and GGRt (a pose-free, real-time Gaussian-splatting network) are the leading examples. The problem is that they hand back one solid-looking 3D model in which a wall that ten photos clearly saw and a wall the network simply guessed at behind a doorway look equally certain. There is no per-spot label saying 'this part is measured' versus 'this part is invented'.\n\nThis matters now because these multi-view networks already, internally, make several separate guesses for the same 3D point — one from each photo that sees it — and then quietly average them into the final model. How much those internal guesses disagree is itself the missing signal: where the photos agree, the point is well constrained; where they disagree (or only one photo saw it), the network is mostly guessing. Because the network is already run, this disagreement is essentially free to read out, and public datasets with ground-truth 3D (such as ScanNet++ and DL3DV) let us check the resulting confidence. Concurrent work has started bolting uncertainty onto these networks (Trust3R) or using a separate uncertainty model plus a language model to plan camera moves (AREA3D), but none of them derive the signal from the network's own cross-photo agreement or calibrate it by hiding input photos.\n\nThe closest prior efforts each stopped one step short. VGGT outputs confidence numbers used only to blend overlapping predictions, never a calibrated per-region 'how much do I trust this' map. GGRt inherits the same one-solid-field assumption. FisherRF can score which camera to add next, but only after slowly fitting a model to one specific scene, so it cannot answer the question straight from a feed-forward pass.\n\nWhen this gap closes, the 3D model stops being a flat block of equal trust and becomes something every downstream user — a robot avoiding obstacles, an artist editing the scene, a capture system deciding where to point the camera next — can read region by region, keeping the measured parts and flagging or discarding the invented ones, and choosing the next photo in a single fast pass.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n\n1. Run a pretrained VGGT (Visual Geometry Grounded Transformer) multi-view network on your input photos with its weights frozen — evaluation mode, no retraining. Keep everything it already produces: each photo's depth map, each photo's camera position, the dense 3D point map, the per-pixel confidence numbers, and the network's internal per-point feature vector (read just before it merges the photos together) sampled at each point.\n   - _Why_: The signal we want is already inside a trained network, so we reuse it instead of paying to retrain a huge model.\n\n### Disagreement Signal Extraction\n*Reads the frozen backbone's own cross-view disagreement as the manufactured per-location evidence signal.*\n\n2. For each 3D point, find which photos actually see it: project the point into every photo, and accept a photo only if the point lands in view and that photo's predicted depth agrees with the reference depth to within a small tolerance (about 5%, so occluded or mismatched hits are thrown out). From each accepting photo, back-project its depth to get that photo's own 3D guess for the point, then measure the confidence-weighted spread of those guesses — that spread is the cross-view disagreement. If fewer than two photos accept the point, mark it with a fixed large 'no evidence' value.\n\n*Cross-view predictive disagreement d(x) is the confidence-weighted variance of the per-frame unprojected 3D positions $p_{i}(x)$ across the frames C(x) that cover x; weights $w_{i}$ are the backbone's existing per-frame confidence logits passed through a softmax over covering frames.*\n$$ d(x) = \\frac{\\sum_{i \\in \\mathcal{C}(x)} w_i \\, \\lVert p_i(x) - \\bar{p}(x) \\rVert^2}{\\sum_{i \\in \\mathcal{C}(x)} w_i}, \\qquad \\bar{p}(x) = \\frac{\\sum_{i} w_i \\, p_i(x)}{\\sum_{i} w_i} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Where the photos agree the point is pinned by evidence; where they disagree it was largely guessed — so disagreement directly measures how view-constrained the point is.\n\n### Calibrated Evidence Head\n*Trains a tiny head by held-out-input-view consistency to turn disagreement into a calibrated confidence and spread.*\n\n3. Add a small two-layer network (width 256, GELU activation) that reads the point's backbone feature together with its disagreement value (log-compressed and scaled by the typical disagreement so the input is scale-stable) and outputs two numbers: a confidence between 0 and 1 (via a sigmoid) and a geometric spread in millimeters (via a softplus with a 1 mm floor so it is always positive). Train only this head; the big network stays frozen. Because disagreement is tiny where many photos agree and large where the geometry was filled in from one view, the confidence directly reflects how view-constrained each region is.\n\n*A small two-layer head $g_{phi}$ maps the backbone per-point feature f(x) and disagreement d(x) to a confidence c(x) in [0,1] and a geometric spread $\\sigma (x)$ in scene units; the backbone stays frozen.*\n$$ (c(x),\\, \\sigma(x)) = g_\\phi\\big( f(x),\\, d(x) \\big), \\qquad c(x) \\in [0,1],\\ \\sigma(x) > 0 \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A small head is enough to turn the raw disagreement into a calibrated, easy-to-read trust value, and freezing the backbone keeps it cheap and safe.\n4. Create training targets for free by hiding some input photos: split the photos into a 'context' set and a 'probe' set (context size randomly chosen each time so the head sees both rich and sparse coverage), reconstruct from context only, and for each point also seen by a held-out probe photo use that probe's 3D position as the truth. Train the head so its predicted spread matches the actual error (a Gaussian fit), plus a rule that pushes confidence low where almost no context photo saw the point, plus a small smoothness penalty on the head. No human labels and no real ground-truth 3D are used — only withheld input photos. 【author decision: whether the low-confidence rule aims at a fixed value (confidence $\\to $ 0) or at a confidence level estimated from the data — simplicity of a fixed target versus a data-calibrated one.】\n\n*The label-free calibration objective is a Gaussian negative-log-likelihood of the context-only prediction residual against the withheld probe-view position, plus a coverage-anchored prior pulling c(x) toward zero where fewer than two context frames cover x, plus a sharpness penalty $\\Omega $ on the head.*\n$$ \\mathcal{L} = \\sum_{x} \\left[ \\frac{\\lVert \\bar{p}_{\\text{ctx}}(x) - p_{\\text{probe}}(x) \\rVert^2}{2\\,\\sigma(x)^2} + \\log \\sigma(x) \\right] + \\lambda_c \\!\\!\\sum_{x:\\,|\\mathcal{C}_{\\text{ctx}}(x)| < 2}\\!\\! c(x) + \\lambda_s\\, \\Omega(\\phi) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Withholding real input photos gives a truthful, label-free way to learn calibrated confidence without ever touching test scenes or ground-truth 3D.\n\n### Selective-Prediction Validation\n*Tests and causally isolates the evidence signal via error-vs-coverage curves and permutation / d-only controls.*\n\n5. On test scenes, line the reconstruction up to real ground-truth 3D (using high-confidence points to fix scale and pose), then measure each point's error in real units. Keep only points above a confidence cutoff, measure their average error, and slide the cutoff from keeping everything down to keeping only the top few percent, drawing an error-versus-coverage curve. If confidence is meaningful, keeping only high-confidence points should steadily lower the error compared to keeping everything.\n   - _Why_: If the confidence is real, keeping only high-confidence points should make the error drop — that is the headline test.\n6. Run the key control: shuffle the disagreement values across all the points (the overall set of values stays the same, but each value is no longer attached to its own point), retrain the head exactly as before on the shuffled values, and redraw the error-versus-coverage curve. Average over at least 5 shuffles. If the benefit came from genuine per-point evidence, the curve should collapse to the no-selection baseline — proving the per-location disagreement is what carries the signal.\n   - _Why_: If the gain came from genuine per-location evidence, scrambling which point each value belongs to should erase it — proving the signal is load-bearing.\n7. Run the confirming control: train a stripped version of the head that uses only the disagreement value (no backbone feature), with everything else identical, and redraw the curve. If disagreement alone recovers most of the benefit, that confirms it is the real source of the confidence signal.\n   - _Why_: If disagreement alone recovers most of the benefit, that confirms it is the real carrier of the trust signal.\n\n### Feed-Forward Next-Best-View\n*Queries the same evidence posterior as a submodular view selector with no per-scene optimization.*\n\n8. To choose the next camera, lay out a set of candidate viewpoints (by default 64 positions spread evenly on a sphere around the scene, each aimed at its center). For each candidate, work out which currently low-confidence points it would newly see — project those points into the candidate view using its pose and the predicted depths, and count a point only if it lands in view and is not hidden behind a nearer surface. Score each candidate by how much confidence it would add over those points (one quick pass of the head), greedily pick the best, remove the points it covers, and repeat to plan several views; greedy coverage selection carries a known (1 $- $ 1/e) quality guarantee. The score uses only the geometry-and-confidence map — no language or semantic input. 【author decision: how to lay out the candidate viewpoints (how dense, half-sphere or full sphere, a fixed distance or only physically reachable poses) depends on the capture setup and is left to the authors — a dense generic grid versus only reachable poses.】\n\n*Next-best-view selects the candidate q that maximizes the summed expected confidence gain over the currently-low-confidence locations N(q) it would newly co-observe; greedy maximization of this coverage utility carries the standard (1 - 1/e) submodular guarantee.*\n$$ q^* = \\arg\\max_{q \\in \\mathcal{Q}} U(q), \\qquad U(q) = \\sum_{x \\in \\mathcal{N}(q)} \\big(1 - c(x)\\big) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Pointing the camera where geometry is least constrained reduces the most uncertainty per shot, and greedy coverage selection comes with a known (1 - 1/e) quality guarantee.\n9. Test whether the active view choices actually help: starting from the same initial photo(s), compare three ways of adding the next photo — the active plan, picking randomly, and a simple 'spread the cameras as far apart as possible' rule. After each added photo, rebuild and measure the 3D error against ground truth, and report how many photos each method needs to reach a fixed quality (the quality the random method reaches at the full budget). If the active plan needs fewer photos, the informativeness score is doing real work.\n   - _Why_: If the active plan reaches a target quality with fewer photos, the informativeness score is doing real work.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 证据校准的视觉空间：面向任意视图前馈重建的逐区域置信度\n\n**方法名称.** Evidence-Calibrated Visual Space (ECVS)\n\n## 研究动机\n现在的网络可以看几张某个场景的照片——甚至不知道相机在哪儿——就在一次前向传播里输出该场景完整的三维形状与外观（我们称之为“恢复视觉空间”）。VGGT（Visual Geometry Grounded Transformer）和 GGRt（一种无位姿、实时的 Gaussian-splatting 网络）是其中的代表。问题在于：它们交回来的是一整块看起来都很确定的三维模型，其中被十张照片清楚看到的墙，和门后被网络凭空猜出来的墙，看上去同样可信。没有任何逐点标注告诉你“这部分是测量得到的”还是“这部分是编造的”。\n\n现在正是时机，因为这些多视图网络内部其实已经对同一个三维点做了若干次各自独立的预测——每张看到它的照片一个——然后悄悄把它们平均成最终模型。这些内部预测之间分歧有多大，本身就是那个缺失的信号：照片一致的地方，点被很好地约束；分歧大（或只有一张照片看到）的地方，网络多半在猜。因为网络本来就要跑一遍，这个分歧几乎是免费可读出的，而带真值三维的公开数据集（如 ScanNet++ 和 DL3DV）让我们可以校验由此得到的置信度。近期有工作开始给这类网络外挂不确定性（Trust3R），或用一个独立的不确定性模型加一个语言模型来规划相机移动（AREA3D），但没有一个是从网络自身的跨照片一致性导出信号、并用“藏起输入照片”来校准的。\n\n最接近的前人工作都各差一步。VGGT 输出的置信度数字只用于融合重叠预测，从不构成一张校准过的逐区域“我有多信它”的图。GGRt 继承了同样的“单一实心场”假设。FisherRF 能给“下一台相机加在哪”打分，但必须先针对某一个具体场景慢慢拟合一个模型，因此无法直接从前馈一次性给出答案。\n\n当这个缺口被补上，三维模型不再是一整块同等可信的实体，而成为每个下游用户——避障的机器人、编辑场景的美术、决定相机下一步指向哪里的采集系统——都能逐区域读取的东西：保留测量得到的部分，标记或丢弃编造的部分，并在一次快速前向传播中选出下一张照片。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景\n\n1. 用一个预训练的 VGGT (Visual Geometry Grounded Transformer) 多视图网络在你的输入照片上跑一遍，权重冻结——推理模式，不重训。保留它本来就产出的一切：每张照片的深度图、每张照片的相机位姿、稠密三维点图、逐像素置信数值，以及网络内部的逐点特征向量（在它把各照片融合之前读取）并在每个点处采样。\n   - _为什么_: 我们想要的信号已经在训练好的网络里，所以直接复用，而不是花代价重训一个大模型。\n\n### 分歧信号提取\n*读取冻结 backbone 自身的跨视图分歧，作为被制造出来的逐位置证据信号。*\n\n2. 对每个三维点，找出真正看到它的照片：把该点投影到每张照片，只有当它落在画面内、且该照片预测的深度与参考深度相差很小（约 5%，从而剔除被遮挡或错配的命中）时才接受这张照片。从每张被接受的照片把其深度反投影，得到该照片对这个点各自的三维猜测，再计算这些猜测的置信度加权展度——这个展度就是跨视图分歧。若少于两张照片接受该点，就给它一个固定的大“无证据”值。\n\n*跨视图预测分歧 d(x) 是覆盖 x 的各帧 C(x) 反投影得到的逐帧三维位置 $p_{i}(x)$ 的置信度加权方差；权重 $w_{i}$ 由 backbone 自带的逐帧置信 logit 经覆盖帧上的 softmax 得到。*\n$$ d(x) = \\frac{\\sum_{i \\in \\mathcal{C}(x)} w_i \\, \\lVert p_i(x) - \\bar{p}(x) \\rVert^2}{\\sum_{i \\in \\mathcal{C}(x)} w_i}, \\qquad \\bar{p}(x) = \\frac{\\sum_{i} w_i \\, p_i(x)}{\\sum_{i} w_i} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 照片一致的地方点被证据钉住；分歧大的地方多半靠猜——所以分歧直接度量了该点被视图约束的程度。\n\n### 校准证据头\n*用留出输入视图一致性训练一个小头，把分歧转成校准过的置信度与展度。*\n\n3. 加一个小的两层网络（宽度 256，GELU 激活），读入该点的 backbone 特征连同它的分歧值（取对数压缩并按典型分歧缩放，使输入尺度稳定），输出两个数：一个 0 到 1 之间的置信度（经 sigmoid）和一个以毫米计的几何展度（经 softplus 并设 1 mm 下限，保证恒正）。只训练这个头；大网络保持冻结。因为分歧在多张照片一致处极小、在只靠单视图补全处很大，所以置信度直接反映每个区域被视图约束的程度。\n\n*一个两层小头 $g_{phi}$ 把 backbone 的逐点特征 f(x) 与分歧 d(x) 映射为置信度 $c(x)\\in [0,1]$ 和以场景单位计的几何展度 $\\sigma (x)$；backbone 全程冻结。*\n$$ (c(x),\\, \\sigma(x)) = g_\\phi\\big( f(x),\\, d(x) \\big), \\qquad c(x) \\in [0,1],\\ \\sigma(x) > 0 \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 一个小头就足以把原始分歧转成校准过、易读的信任值，而冻结 backbone 让整件事既便宜又稳妥。\n4. 通过藏起部分输入照片来免费造训练目标：把照片分成 context 集与 probe 集（每次随机选 context 大小，让头同时见到丰富和稀疏的覆盖），只用 context 重建，并对每个也被留出的 probe 照片看到的点，用该 probe 的三维位置作为真值。训练头使其预测的展度匹配实际误差（高斯拟合），再加上在几乎没有 context 照片看到处把置信拉低的规则，以及对头的小平滑惩罚。不使用任何人工标签、也不使用真实真值三维——只用被留出的输入照片。【作者需决定：低置信规则是瞄准一个固定值（置信度$\\to 0$）还是瞄准一个从数据估计出的置信水平——固定目标的简洁性与数据校准目标之间的权衡。】\n\n*无标签校准目标为：仅用 context 预测的残差相对被保留的 probe 视图位置的高斯负对数似然，加上一个覆盖锚定先验（在被少于两帧 context 覆盖处把 c(x) 拉向零），再加上对头部的锐度惩罚 $\\Omega $。*\n$$ \\mathcal{L} = \\sum_{x} \\left[ \\frac{\\lVert \\bar{p}_{\\text{ctx}}(x) - p_{\\text{probe}}(x) \\rVert^2}{2\\,\\sigma(x)^2} + \\log \\sigma(x) \\right] + \\lambda_c \\!\\!\\sum_{x:\\,|\\mathcal{C}_{\\text{ctx}}(x)| < 2}\\!\\! c(x) + \\lambda_s\\, \\Omega(\\phi) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 留出真实输入照片，给了一种真实、无需标签的方式来学习校准置信度，而完全不碰测试场景或真值三维。\n\n### 选择性预测验证\n*用误差—覆盖率曲线及置换 / 仅用 d(x) 的对照，检验并因果地隔离该证据信号。*\n\n5. 在测试场景上，把重建对齐到真实真值三维（用高置信点确定尺度与位姿），再以真实单位测每个点的误差。只保留置信度高于某阈值的点，测它们的平均误差，并把阈值从“全部保留”滑到“只保留最高的百分之几”，画出误差—覆盖率曲线。如果置信度有意义，只保留高置信点应相对“全部保留”稳步降低误差。\n   - _为什么_: 如果置信度是真的，只保留高置信点应使误差下降——这就是核心检验。\n6. 做关键对照：把分歧值在所有点之间打乱（值的整体集合不变，但每个值不再附着于自己的点），用打乱后的值完全照旧重训头，再画一次误差—覆盖率曲线。至少平均 5 次打乱。如果收益来自真正的逐点证据，曲线应塌回“全部保留”基线——证明逐位置的分歧才是承载信号的东西。\n   - _为什么_: 如果增益来自真正的逐位置证据，那么打乱每个值所属的点应将其抹除——证明该信号是承重的。\n7. 做确认对照：训练一个精简版的头，只用分歧值（不用 backbone 特征），其余完全一致，再画一次曲线。如果仅凭分歧就能恢复大部分收益，就确认它才是置信信号的真正来源。\n   - _为什么_: 如果仅凭分歧就能恢复大部分收益，就证实它才是信任信号的真正载体。\n\n### 前馈下一最佳视图\n*把同一个证据后验作为次模视图选择器查询，无需任何逐场景优化。*\n\n8. 选下一台相机时，先布置一组候选视点（默认在场景周围球面上均匀分布 64 个位置，各自朝向场景中心）。对每个候选，算出它会新看到哪些当前低置信点——用其位姿和预测深度把这些点投影到该候选视图，只有落在画面内、且未被更近表面遮挡时才计入。按它能在这些点上增加多少置信度给每个候选打分（头跑一次快速前向），贪心选最优，移除它覆盖的点，重复以规划多个视图；贪心覆盖选择带有已知的 (1 $- $ 1/e) 质量保证。该打分只用几何与置信度图——不用任何语言或语义输入。【作者需决定：候选视点如何布置（多密、半球还是整球、固定距离还是仅物理可达位姿）取决于采集装置，留给作者——密集通用网格与仅可达位姿之间的取舍。】\n\n*下一最佳视图选取使其新共同观测到的当前低置信位置 N(q) 上预期置信增益之和最大的候选 q；对该覆盖型效用的贪心最大化具有标准的 (1 - 1/e) 次模保证。*\n$$ q^* = \\arg\\max_{q \\in \\mathcal{Q}} U(q), \\qquad U(q) = \\sum_{x \\in \\mathcal{N}(q)} \\big(1 - c(x)\\big) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 把相机指向几何最不受约束之处，每拍一张能减少最多不确定性，而贪心覆盖选择带有已知的 (1 - 1/e) 质量保证。\n9. 检验主动选视图是否真的有用：从相同的初始照片出发，比较三种添加下一张照片的方式——主动方案、随机挑选、以及简单的“让相机尽量分散”规则。每加一张照片就重建一次并测相对真值的三维误差，并报告各方法达到固定质量（随机方法在全预算下达到的质量）所需的照片数。如果主动方案需要更少照片，说明信息量打分确实在起作用。\n   - _为什么_: 如果主动方案用更少照片就达到目标质量，说明这个信息量打分真的在起作用。\n\n"},{"id":"24","run_dir":"run_prompt24_metricdepth","index":24,"title":"ScaleConsensus: A VLM's Own Answers Reveal and Calibrate Its Metric-Depth Scale","title_zh":"ScaleConsensus：用 VLM 自身的回答揭示并校准其度量深度尺度","method_name":"ScaleConsensus","hook":"A vision-language model that answers metric-depth queries one pixel at a time silently commits to a different absolute scale for almost every query on the same image; we show those mutually-inconsistent answers are not noise but a measurable consensus object whose dispersion is a calibrated, shift-robust estimate of how wrong the scale is. Aggregating the model's own redundant answers into a single latent per-image scale both removes the inconsistency and turns the leftover disagreement into a decision-usable uncertainty, with no architecture, loss, or extra labels.","anchor_pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","anchor_pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","domain_category":"3D Vision & Scene Reconstruction","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes a VLM's multiple metric-depth answers on the SAME image mutually consistent in scale: DepthLM queries each pixel independently (openalex:W4414803171) so two answers can imply contradictory global scales with nothing reconciling them, and region-aware scale methods that achieve spatial consistency do so only with external sparse 3D measurements at inference (openalex:W4417433130) rather than from the image and the model's own answers alone — the missing outcome is internal","pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by reframing the opaque question 'what is THIS image's metric scale' as a faithful measurement over a fixed model: a robust consensus estimator s* over the set of per-query implied global scales the VLM itself emits, with the faithfulness constraint that every query is anchored to the same geometric relations so the scores reflect the model's own computation; consistency becomes a derived property of s* rather than hoped-for agreement, and fidelity is certified by a causal perturbation of the query coupling.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf lets a VLM express HOW uncertain its own metric-depth answer is for a given image: every method (openalex:W4414803171, openalex:W4402727115, semanticscholar:ee531657945a58a1b4b456a6834917c0bc4025e1) commits to a single absolute scale per query and offers no calibrated signal that survives domain shift telling a downstream consumer when to trust the number — the missing outcome is a decision-usable, calibrated per-image metric-scale uncertainty, not any particular way of produci","pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by treating the cross-query dispersion of the model's own implied scales around the consensus s* as a label-free internal-state readout, localizing the uncertainty to the scale-inference site, and calibrating it on a tiny lever (a frozen-backbone monotone calibration map fit on a small held-out set) with an anti-degeneracy stabilizer, yielding a per-image uncertainty that is checked to remain monotone in true scale error under domain shift.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"monocular metric depth estimation from vision-language models (VLMs)","n_papers":37,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":23},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":20,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Metric3D v2: A Versatile Monocular Geometric Foundation Model for Zero-Shot Metric Depth and Surface Normal Estimation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Prompting Depth Anything for 4K Resolution Accurate Metric Depth Estimation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A Simple yet Effective Test-Time Adaptation for Zero-Shot Monocular Metric Depth Estimation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"MetricDepth: Enhancing Monocular Depth Estimation with Deep Metric Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"ViPOcc: Leveraging Visual Priors from Vision Foundation Models for Single-View 3D Occupancy Prediction"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"WaveSamba: A Wavelet Transform SSM Zero-Shot Depth Estimation Decoder"}],"more":14},{"year":2025,"n":16,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Underwater Monocular Metric Depth Estimation: Real-World Benchmarks and Synthetic Fine-Tuning with Vision Foundation Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Depth Any Camera: Zero-Shot Metric Depth Estimation from Any Camera"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A Critical Synthesis of Uncertainty Quantification and Foundation Models in Monocular Depth Estimation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Depth Any Panoramas: A Foundation Model for Panoramic Depth Estimation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Zero-shot Monocular Metric Depth for Endoscopic Images"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"DEFOM-Stereo: Depth Foundation Model Based Stereo Matching"}],"more":10},{"year":2026,"n":1,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"}],"more":0}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":15,"share":0.405},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":9,"share":0.243},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":7,"share":0.189},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":6,"share":0.162},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":6,"share":0.162},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":6,"share":0.162},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":6,"share":0.162},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":4,"share":0.108}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Recent work shows a VLM can be turned into a strong per-pixel metric depth estimator by text-based supervised fine-tuning with visual-prompt markers and intrinsic-conditioned augmentation (openalex:W4414803171), yet the resulting predictor emits one isolated scalar per queried pixel ('the point is around X meters away') with no expressed uncertainty and no mechanism tying separate queries on the same image to a single consistent metric scale; meanwhile pure-vision metric depth foundation models recover scale only by either hard-coding a canonical camera transform that assumes intrinsics are known (semanticscholar:ee531657945a58a1b4b456a6834917c0bc4025e1) or by predicting a dense camera representation as a single point estimate with no calibrated confidence on the scale it infers (openalex:W4402727115), and diagnostic studies confirm that even strong VLMs systematically fail at depth perception in a way the benchmarks attribute to absent geometric reasoning rather than a missing output head (openalex:W4414197449). The structural failure: when a VLM answers a metric-depth query it commits to an absolute scale without ever representing how ambiguous that scale is for THIS image, so under monocular scale ambiguity (unknown intrinsics, novel scene statistics, out-of-distribution focal length) the answer is confidently wrong and the system cannot tell that it is wrong or reconcile two of its own answers that imply contradictory scales.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4414803171","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"DepthLM converts a standard VLM into a metric-depth estimator by rendering a marker on the query pixel and text-SFT-ing it to answer 'X meters', resolving camera ambiguity by intrinsic-conditioned augmentation that normalizes focal length during training so the model learns a single canonical-scale mapping. Residue (from method Sec.3.1/3.4): each pixel is queried independently and the model returns one rounded scalar with no uncertainty and no cross-query coupling, and intrinsic/scale ambiguity is absorbed into the weights at training time rather than represented or resolved at inference, so the model cannot express that a particular image is scale-ambiguous, cannot detect when two of its own per-pixel answers imply mutually inconsistent scales, and cannot use language interaction to interrogate or revise its own metric commitment."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4402727115","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"UniDepth predicts metric 3D points from a single image with a self-promptable camera module that outputs a dense camera representation conditioning the depth head, removing the need for external intrinsics. Residue: the camera/scale representation is a single deterministic point estimate with no calibrated confidence, so the model cannot flag images where its inferred scale is unreliable nor propagate scale uncertainty into the depth output."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:ee531657945a58a1b4b456a6834917c0bc4025e1","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Metric3D v2 resolves cross-camera metric ambiguity with a canonical camera-space transform that maps every image into one reference intrinsic before metric depth regression. Residue: the transform assumes the camera intrinsics are known and correct, and produces a deterministic metric map with no representation of residual scale ambiguity when intrinsics are wrong, estimated, or absent."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4414197449","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"GeoMeter benchmarks 18 VLMs and shows they consistently fail at depth/height perception, attributing the failure to weak geometric reasoning and inherent biases. Residue: it is diagnostic only — it measures the failure and offers no mechanism that lets a VLM represent or reduce its own metric-scale uncertainty, leaving open whether the failure is a reasoning gap a self-consistency procedure could expose and correct."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"monocular metric depth estimation from vision-language models (VLMs)","venue":"NeurIPS / CVPR / ICLR (top-tier ML/vision)","time":"2026","data":["public RGB-D metric-depth benchmarks (NYUv2, KITTI, ScanNet++, ETH3D, Argoverse2, NuScenes, DDAD, iBims-1, SUN-RGBD)","sparse-label VLM depth corpora in the style of DepthLMBench"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with cloud GPU access; familiarity with VLM fine-tuning (SFT/LoRA) and monocular depth pipelines","preference":"both","baseline":"DepthLM (text-SFT VLM that predicts per-pixel metric depth via visual-prompt markers + intrinsic-conditioned augmentation)","limitation":"VLM-produced metric depth is a single per-query point estimate with no calibrated uncertainty and no enforced cross-query metric-scale consistency; camera/scale ambiguity is absorbed at training time, leaving the model unable to express or resolve scale ambiguity at inference","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object (coherence_thread_type=shared_object) is the latent per-image metric scale s, read from and written to by both legs. LEG 1 (reframe_as_solvable_object, C00). DepthLM-style VLMs answer 'how many meters is this marked point' as one scalar per query; from any single query at marked pixel p with marker depth answer d_VLM(p) and the frozen relative-depth foundation prior r(p) (an affine-invariant disparity-derived relative depth from a Depth Anything-class model, openalex:W4402727359), the implied global scale is sigma_p = d_VLM(p) / r(p) (units: meters per relative-unit). We probe the SAME scene with K geometrically-coupled queries (K=24, a fixed default) — markers placed by farthest-point sampling over the relative-depth map so the queries span the depth range and share one r-field — producing a set {sigma_1..sigma_K}. The reframed solvable object is robust location estimation: the consensus scale s* = median_k(sigma_k) (a closed-form, breakdown-robust estimator; the faithfulness constraint is that all sigma_k are built from the SAME r-field and the SAME model, so s* measures the model's own computation, not an off-distribution artifact). Coherence is then a derived property: re-scaling every per-pixel relative depth by s* yields a single metric map on which all K answers agree by construction, replacing K contradictory commitments with one. LEG 2 (self_supervised_signal_engineering, C07). The internal label-free readout is the cross-query dispersion D = median_k |log(sigma_k) - log(s*)| (a robust scale of the log-implied-scale distribution, dimensionless), localizing uncertainty to the scale-inference site exactly as C07 prescribes. D is mapped to a calibrated metric-scale-error estimate via a tiny monotone calibration map g_theta (isotonic regression, ~K knots, fit on a small held-out calibration split of <= 2000 images; backbone frozen, this is the C07 'smallest lever'). The anti-degeneracy stabilizer (C07 step 4): because a low-D image could be confidently-wrong (all queries agreeing on a biased scale), we anchor the estimate with a source-prior mixture — g_theta outputs max(g_iso(D), floor(s*)) where floor(s*) is a prior reliability term decreasing in how far log(s*) sits from the training-scale distribution mean, preventing D->0 from claiming certainty out of distribution. The two legs share s*: LEG 1 produces it, LEG 2 measures the spread around it; no separate module duplicates the scale estimate. REGRESSION AVOIDANCE: the object is NOT plain sample-and-vote self-consistency (lineage node c2) because the votes are geometric scale ratios coupled through a shared r-field with a physically-meaningful agreement constraint (a consistent metric map must exist), and D is NOT plain heteroscedastic variance or MC-dropout (node c1) because it is a function of cross-query geometric disagreement of a fixed model rather than a learned variance head trained in-distribution, which is precisely why it is checked to survive shift.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery because the same latent scale s drives both: the evidence is that the dispersion needed for uncertainty (LEG 2) is definitionally the residual of the consensus estimator built for coherence (LEG 1), so building two separate modules would re-estimate the same quantity and risk inconsistency between them; one estimator s* with its residual D is the parsimonious design. (b) Considered alternatives: (i) train a learned per-pixel variance head (rejected: needs uncertainty supervision that does not exist and is the c1 regression that fails under shift); (ii) plain answer-resampling with temperature and majority vote (rejected: c2 regression, ignores the geometric coupling that gives the agreement physical meaning); (iii) external sparse-point rescale like region-aware adaptation (rejected: requires inference-time sensors, openalex:W4417433130, violating the image-only requirement). The avoided nodes (c1 heteroscedastic/MC-dropout variance, c2 textual self-consistency) are recorded here per the regression flag.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: take a frozen DepthLM-class 3B metric VLM and a frozen Depth-Anything-v2 relative model, run the K=24 coupled-query ScaleConsensus pipeline on the standard cross-domain metric-depth test suite (NYUv2, KITTI, ScanNet++, ETH3D, plus an out-of-distribution set such as DDAD/iBims-1 unseen in calibration), with no fine-tuning. If the candidate works, per-image AbsRel and delta1 of the consensus map M improve over the independent single-query DepthLM baseline (AbsRel decreases, delta1 increases), and on the risk-coverage curve selective AbsRel decreases monotonically as low-uncertainty images are kept, i.e. the calibrated uncertainty u correctly ranks images by trustworthiness on BOTH in-distribution and shifted sets. The named load-bearing variable is the cross-query scale dispersion D; the mechanism distinguisher is the NEGATIVE CONTROL that breaks the geometric coupling (each query rendered on a different random sub-crop so the K answers no longer read one shared r-field): if D is the mechanism, this control must drive the DOWNSTREAM OUTCOME metric back toward baseline — selective AbsRel at fixed coverage should regress to the uncalibrated independent-query level and Spearman(D, true scale error) should collapse toward zero — whereas if 'metric moved' were merely from extra queries/compute or generic ensembling, the decoupled control would retain the gain. A POSITIVE CONTROL using only D as the abstention gate should recover most of the selective-prediction improvement, constructively identifying D as the carrier.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4414803171","delta":"DepthLM emits one independent scalar per marked pixel and bakes scale ambiguity into the weights via intrinsic-conditioned augmentation; we construct a consensus estimator s* over the model's own redundant geometrically-coupled answers and derive from its residual D a calibrated per-image uncertainty, neither of which DepthLM produces or could produce from a single query."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4417433130","delta":"Region-aware scale adaptation achieves spatial scale consistency only by consuming external sparse 3D measurements at inference; we achieve cross-query metric-scale coherence and an uncertainty from the image and the model's own answers alone, with no external sensing."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4402727115","delta":"UniDepth predicts a dense camera representation as a single deterministic point estimate with no confidence; we measure scale via the dispersion of the model's own answers and calibrate it to true scale error so the system can flag when its inferred scale is unreliable."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:bd70af0a503b00b7d1c3f2080823f20ca3ac8fd6","delta":"The UQ-for-depth synthesis catalogs uncertainty methods (ensembles, dropout, learned variance) that are validated mainly in-distribution; we manufacture a label-free uncertainty from cross-query geometric disagreement and make surviving domain shift the primary validated claim."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4414803171","what_step_was_missed":"DepthLM established that a VLM can emit a metric scalar per marked pixel, but to make our contribution already exist it would have had to construct a consensus estimator that ties multiple per-pixel answers to a single shared latent scale through a common relative-depth field, and then identify the residual dispersion of those answers as a quantity that tracks true scale error and calibrate it under domain shift — it built the per-query emission primitive but never constructed the cross-query coupling object or the dispersion-to-error calibration that our method derives."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":352,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"Layer 1 hard floor did not fire: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict is borderline (no lesson marked candidate_match: yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat (DepthVLM) is competing-but-not-subsuming. recipe_application_check.verdict = applied for both legs, so the idea is built from the C00 and C07 distinctive moves, not the parent gist. The two borderlines (C00 'extra-compute confound' and C07 'must beat standard ensemble baseline') both hit load-bearing concerns but are already structurally answered by the negative and positive controls in falsification_prediction, so they are surfaced for Phase 4 reviewer_concerns_and_responses rather than requiring a revise.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes a VLM's multiple metric-depth answers on the SAME image mutually consistent in scale: DepthLM queries each pixel independently (openalex:W4414803171) so two answers can imply contradictory global scales with nothing reconciling them, and region-aware scale methods that achieve spatial consistency do so only with external sparse 3D measurements at inference (openalex:W4417433130) rather than from the image and the model's own answers alone — the missing outcome is internal cross-query metric-scale coherence.","main_pattern":"reframe_as_solvable_object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The signature failure is treating the reframing as a mechanical wrapper: taking an established attribution, decomposition, or estimation tool and pointing it at a new input granularity or domain without re-deriving why the resulting scores are faithful to the model, supplying the computation but not the justification (no causal validation, only correlation).","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Pointing an off-the-shelf decomposition at a coarser input granularity without showing the coarser units preserve the signal reads as a wrapper, not a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The consensus estimator s* is not a generic decomposition pointed at depth; its faithfulness is established by the negative control (breaking the shared-r-field coupling collapses the signal), positively showing the coupled units carry the scale signal."},{"lesson_quoted":"Proposing a new attribution definition without an axiomatic or causal argument for why it should count as ground-truth collapses the moment a reviewer asks why this is the real importance.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate defines D and s* causally: the falsification_prediction's negative-control intervention on the geometric coupling provides the causal argument that D measures real scale disagreement rather than a coincidental statistic."},{"lesson_quoted":"Conflating a methodological artifact — a computation-granularity difference, a degenerate zero baseline — with genuine signal undermines the entire premise once the confound is identified.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"A skeptic could argue gains come merely from issuing K queries (extra compute) rather than from the coupling; this is exactly what the negative control (same K queries, coupling broken) is designed to rule out, so the concern is anticipated but worth surfacing for Phase 4."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf lets a VLM express HOW uncertain its own metric-depth answer is for a given image: every method (openalex:W4414803171, openalex:W4402727115, semanticscholar:ee531657945a58a1b4b456a6834917c0bc4025e1) commits to a single absolute scale per query and offers no calibrated signal that survives domain shift telling a downstream consumer when to trust the number — the missing outcome is a decision-usable, calibrated per-image metric-scale uncertainty, not any particular way of producing it.","main_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is a manufactured internal signal whose validity silently rests on an assumption that does not survive deployment (model calibration, a stationary/known-finite shift set, or covert use of target/test information amounting to label leakage), plus recombining well-known components without a single load-bearing mechanistic insight.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A label-free signal whose validity depends on model calibration silently fails on exactly the deep networks known to be poorly calibrated — validate a surrogate where its core assumption is weakest, not where it is convenient.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"D is built from geometric cross-query disagreement of implied scales, not from the VLM's softmax/confidence, so it does not depend on the VLM being calibrated; the primary validated claim is that it holds under domain shift (the weakest condition)."},{"lesson_quoted":"Using target or test-set information during adaptation invites a label-leakage objection that undermines the very source-free, label-free deployment setting the method claims.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The isotonic calibration map is fit on a separate held-out calibration split with GT, never on the test set; at inference only the image and the model's own answers are used, so there is no test-set leakage."},{"lesson_quoted":"A multi-branch or ensemble reweighting mechanism that overlaps with standard multi-task/mixture-of-experts ensembling must explicitly beat both the single-model and the standard-ensemble baselines, or the gain is credited to prior art.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"Multiple coupled queries resemble an ensemble; the candidate must beat both the single-query DepthLM baseline and a plain query-ensemble (covered by the positive control and negative control), so this is a load-bearing baseline obligation worth surfacing but it is built into the experiment plan, not violated."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"Both gap_closure entries are borderline, none triggered: the C00 leg's only borderline is the 'methodological artifact (extra compute) vs genuine signal' confound, which the negative control directly addresses; the C07 leg's only borderline is the standard ensemble-baseline obligation, which the positive/negative controls satisfy. No Reject lesson is marked candidate_match: yes."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes a VLM's multiple metric-depth answers on the SAME image mutually consistent in scale: DepthLM queries each pixel independently (openalex:W4414803171) so two answers can imply contradictory global scales with nothing reconciling them, and region-aware scale methods that achieve spatial consistency do so only with external sparse 3D measurements at inference (openalex:W4417433130) rather than from the image and the model's own answers alone — the missing outcome is internal cross-query metric-scale coherence.","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Recast an opaque transparency/uncertainty question about an already-trained model as a concrete measurement over a well-studied object (an estimator over marginal statistics, an additive decomposition), choosing the right unit of analysis and faithfulness constraint so scores reflect the model's actual computation, with fidelity certified by a causal intervention that flips behavior when the identified object is perturbed.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism LEG 1 recasts 'what is this image's metric scale' as robust location estimation (median consensus s* over per-query implied scales) — a measurement over the fixed VLM — with the explicit faithfulness constraint that all sigma_k are built from the SAME r-field and SAME model; step 8 of core_mechanism_steps is the causal-intervention certification (perturb the geometric coupling, observe the predicted collapse), matching the C00 signature exactly.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf lets a VLM express HOW uncertain its own metric-depth answer is for a given image: every method (openalex:W4414803171, openalex:W4402727115, semanticscholar:ee531657945a58a1b4b456a6834917c0bc4025e1) commits to a single absolute scale per query and offers no calibrated signal that survives domain shift telling a downstream consumer when to trust the number — the missing outcome is a decision-usable, calibrated per-image metric-scale uncertainty, not any particular way of producing it.","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Treat an already-trained model's own internal-state readout as the manufactured signal; pair a mechanistic diagnosis localizing the failure to a structural site with a surgically confined correction on a minimal lever (the output head, normalization affines, a low-dimensional conditioning input) while the backbone stays frozen, and bolt on an explicit stabilizer against the degenerate collapse.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism LEG 2 reads the cross-query dispersion D as the label-free internal readout localized to the scale-inference site, confines the correction to a tiny lever (a frozen-backbone isotonic calibration map of ~K knots), and bolts on the explicit anti-degeneracy stabilizer (the source-prior floor term preventing D->0 from claiming false certainty out of distribution) — the diagnose-localize / minimize-on-tiny-lever / stabilize triad of C07.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both legs perform their cited cluster's distinctive move: LEG 1 enacts C00's measurement-over-fixed-model reframe with a causal-perturbation faithfulness certificate, and LEG 2 enacts C07's tiny-lever frozen-backbone calibration with an explicit collapse stabilizer; neither merely restates the parent gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["reframe_as_solvable_object","self_supervised_signal_engineering"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; the candidate's composition is {reframe_as_solvable_object, self_supervised_signal_engineering}, which matches none, so no anti-pattern mitigation is required."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"Unlocking Dense Metric Depth Estimation in VLMs (DepthVLM)","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"DepthVLM is the most directly competitive recent paper: it also makes a single VLM produce metric depth, and could be read as obsoleting per-query VLM depth. But it does NOT subsume the candidate's claim — it attaches a lightweight dense depth head to the LLM backbone and trains under unified vision-text supervision to emit a full-resolution map in one forward pass, i.e. it solves the inconsistency problem by adding architecture and dense supervision, exactly the move DepthLM (and the candidate) deliberately avoid. DepthVLM produces a deterministic dense map with no calibrated per-image scale uncertainty and no consensus-over-own-answers object; the candidate's two load-bearing artifacts (the head-free cross-query consensus s* and the shift-robust calibrated uncertainty D->error map) are absent from DepthVLM. The candidate's claim therefore stands: it is the head-free, label-free, uncertainty-bearing alternative to DepthVLM's head-based dense predictor, and a reviewer comparison should position the candidate as the architecture-preserving + uncertainty-quantifying option.","addressable_via":"Already differentiated; Phase 4 should add DepthVLM as an explicit baseline in reviewer_concerns_and_responses and contrast head-free consensus + calibrated uncertainty against its head-based deterministic dense map."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# ScaleConsensus: A VLM's Own Answers Reveal and Calibrate Its Metric-Depth Scale\n\n**Method.** ScaleConsensus\n\n## Motivation\nA new line of work showed something unexpected: you can take an ordinary vision-language model (VLM, a model that takes an image and answers questions about it in text) and, without adding any special output layer, get it to report metric depth — the real distance in meters to a point you mark on the image. The method, DepthLM (openalex:W4414803171), simply draws a dot on the picture and asks 'how many meters away is this point', then fine-tunes the model on text answers. The catch is that it asks about one point at a time and gives a single number with no sense of how sure it is. If you ask about several points on the same photo, the answers often imply different overall scales for the scene, and nothing brings them back into agreement.\n\nThe same blind spot shows up in the best pure-vision metric depth models. Metric3D v2 (semanticscholar:ee531657945a58a1b4b456a6834917c0bc4025e1) fixes scale only by assuming the camera settings are known, and UniDepth (openalex:W4402727115) outputs a single best guess of the camera/scale with no confidence attached. Benchmarks like GeoMeter (openalex:W4414197449) confirm that even strong VLMs are unreliable at depth. So the real problem is not a missing output layer — it is that the model never expresses how uncertain its scale is for the particular image in front of it, which means it can be confidently wrong and cannot reconcile its own answers.\n\nThis is solvable now because two good ingredients finally exist together off the shelf: a head-free VLM that gives decent per-point metric answers, and a stable 'relative depth' model (Depth Anything, openalex:W4402727359) that says which points are nearer or farther without committing to meters. Pairing them needs no training. Meanwhile, the newest 2026 papers go the other way (adding depth heads or scaling up pretraining), leaving the simple, label-free, uncertainty-aware approach unexplored. When this gap closes, a depth-from-VLM system can finally say 'I am not sure about this image's scale' in a trustworthy way and abstain when needed — something none of the current methods can do.\n\n## Method\n### Shared geometric anchor\n*Establish one relative-depth field so all answers are measured on the same ruler.*\n\n1. Load two models and freeze them (train nothing): a DepthLM-class 3-billion-parameter metric vision-language model (VLM, a model that takes an image and answers in text), and a relative-depth model R called Depth-Anything-v2 (it ranks which points are nearer or farther without committing to meters). Run R once on the input image to get its raw output (an inverse-depth / disparity map), turn it into a relative-depth field r by taking r = 1/(disparity + 0.000001) (the tiny added constant just prevents division blow-ups), then clip r to its 0.5th-to-99.5th percentile across the image so a few extreme pixels (sky, edges) cannot poison later steps. r has arbitrary units — only the ratios between its values matter later, so you do not rescale it.\n   - _Why_: r is the single shared ruler that lets every later answer be measured on the same footing.\n2. Choose K=24 spread-out query points using farthest-point sampling — a greedy rule that repeatedly picks the point most distant from those already chosen — run in the combined space of horizontal position, vertical position, and relative depth r (each scaled to 0–1), starting from the pixel whose r is the median; this guarantees the points cover the whole frame and the full near-to-far range, and you skip the extreme pixels clipped in step step 1 (Load two models and freeze them). On a fresh copy of the image for each point, draw a small bright filled dot (about 6 pixels across, one dot per copy so the questions stay independent) centered on the point, and ask the frozen VLM: 'How far is the marked point from the camera, in meters? Answer with a single number.' From each reply, take the first number it states (dropping any trailing 'm' or 'meters') as that point's answer $d_{VLM}(p_{k})$; if a reply has no usable number, throw that query away rather than guessing.\n   - _Why_: Many points on one scene give the redundant answers whose agreement and disagreement we will exploit.\n\n### Consensus scale estimator\n*Turn many noisy per-query scales into one robust scale and a coherent metric map.*\n\n3. For every queried point, divide the VLM's answer in meters by the relative-depth value r at that same point: $\\sigma _{k} = d_{VLM}(p_{k}) / r(p_{k})$ (Eq. 1). Each $\\sigma _{k}$ is the single overall scene scale that that one answer would imply (its units are meters per relative-unit). This step is the key conversion: it turns answers about different points into one shared, directly comparable quantity — the scene's global scale — so the K answers become members of one estimation problem. The result is the list of implied scales ${\\sigma _{k}}.$\n\n*Each query k turns the VLM's metric answer at marked pixel $p_{k}$ and the shared relative-depth value $r(p_{k})$ into an implied global scale $\\sigma _{k}$ (meters per relative-unit).*\n$$ \\sigma_k = \\frac{d_{\\mathrm{VLM}}(p_k)}{r(p_k)} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: It converts answers about different points into one comparable quantity — the scene's global scale.\n4. Take the median of all the implied scales $\\sigma _{k}$ as the consensus scale s* (Eq. 2) — the median is used instead of the average so a few badly-wrong answers cannot drag the estimate. Then multiply the entire relative-depth field by s* to produce one metric depth map M = s* $\\cdot $ r, and use M(pixel) = s* $\\cdot $ r(pixel) as the final depth at every pixel (replacing the model's separate per-point numbers). Because all points now share the one scale s*, the model's answers are automatically consistent with each other.\n\n*The consensus scale s* is the median of the K implied scales; multiplying the relative field by s* gives one coherent metric map M on which every query agrees.*\n$$ s^{*} = \\operatorname{median}_{k=1}^{K} \\sigma_k, \\qquad M = s^{*}\\, r \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The median is robust to a few bad answers, and a single shared scale makes all the points agree automatically.\n\n### Self-derived calibrated uncertainty\n*Read cross-query dispersion and calibrate it into a shift-robust trust score.*\n\n5. Measure how much the per-query scales $\\sigma _{k}$ disagree with the consensus s*: take the median of the absolute log-differences, D = median of |log $\\sigma _{k} -  log$ s*| (Eq. 3). Working in logarithms makes over- and under-estimates count the same, and the median keeps it robust. D is one plain number per image, needs no labels, and directly captures the scatter in the model's own answers — wide scatter means a shaky scale.\n\n*The dispersion D is the robust spread of the log-implied-scales around the consensus, a dimensionless label-free readout of how much the model's own answers disagree.*\n$$ D = \\operatorname{median}_{k=1}^{K} \\big| \\log \\sigma_k - \\log s^{*} \\big| \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: If the model's own answers scatter widely, the scale is shaky; D captures exactly that scatter without any labels.\n6. Just once, on a small set of calibration images that DO have ground-truth depth, learn how dispersion relates to real error. First define each calibration image's true scale error as e = |log(s* $/ s_{gt})|,$ where $s_{gt}$ is the single best scalar that lines up the relative field r with the ground-truth depth (compute it as the median, over valid pixels, of ground-truth-depth $\\div $ r). Then fit an isotonic regression — a curve forced to only go up, never down — that maps D to e; call it $g_{iso}.$ Separately guard against false confidence on unusual images: fit a simple bell curve to the log of s* over the calibration set (its center and spread), measure how many spreads a new s* falls outside that center, and learn a second only-going-up curve that turns this out-of-range distance into an error value (a 'floor'). The final calibrated uncertainty is the larger of the two: $u = max(g_{iso}(D),$ floor) (Eq. 4). Keep both models frozen; you only fit these two small curves.\n\n*Calibrated uncertainty u maps D through an isotonic regression and floors it by a prior-distance term so a small D cannot claim false certainty when s* is far from the training-scale distribution.*\n$$ u = g_\\theta(D, s^{*}) = \\max\\big(g_{\\mathrm{iso}}(D),\\; \\mathrm{floor}(s^{*})\\big) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This turns the raw scatter D into a meaningful 'how wrong is the scale' number, and the floor stops it from claiming false confidence on unusual images.\n7. At test time, for each image output both the metric depth map M and its calibrated trust number u (no extra inputs are needed beyond the image). A downstream user decides what fraction of images they want to keep (the coverage), and abstains on the images with the highest u — i.e. keeps only the low-uncertainty ones — so risky images are skipped instead of trusted blindly. The system thus hands over an answer AND a trustworthiness score, both built only from the model's own answers.\n   - _Why_: It gives both an answer and a trust score, so risky images can be skipped instead of trusted blindly.\n\n### Faithfulness certificate\n*Prove the gain comes from genuine geometric agreement via a coupling-breaking control.*\n\n8. To prove the benefit is real and not just from asking more questions, redo everything but deliberately break the shared anchor. For each of the K queries on its own, cut out a random square patch covering 40–60% of the image (placed so it still contains the point), run the relative-depth model R on THAT patch to get a separate relative field $r_{k},$ draw the marker, and ask the VLM about the patch; the patch-based implied scale is $\\sigma '_{k} = d_{VLM}(p_{k})/r_{k}(p_{k}).$ Now every answer is read against a different, independently-measured ruler, so the points no longer share one scene — yet you asked the exact same number of questions. Feed these through the identical median-and-spread code to get the control's scale and dispersion, then its map and uncertainty. The expectation: with the shared anchor gone, both the depth improvement and the link between dispersion and error should fall back to the plain single-question level. Also run a stripped 'positive' version that decides abstention using only the dispersion number, to show that dispersion alone carries the benefit.\n   - _Why_: If the benefit really comes from the points agreeing on one scene, breaking that agreement should erase the benefit — proving the effect is real, not just from asking more questions.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# ScaleConsensus：用 VLM 自身的回答揭示并校准其度量深度尺度\n\n**方法名称.** ScaleConsensus\n\n## 研究动机\n最近一条研究线给出了一个出人意料的结果：你可以拿一个普通的 vision-language model（VLM，输入图像、用文字回答问题的模型），在不添加任何专门输出层的情况下，让它报告 metric depth——也就是你在图上标记的某个点到相机的真实距离（米）。这个方法叫 DepthLM（openalex:W4414803171），它只是在图上画一个点，问“这个点离相机多少米”，然后用文字答案做微调。问题在于：它一次只问一个点，给出一个数字，却没有任何“我有多确定”的信息。如果你在同一张图上问多个点，这些答案往往会隐含出彼此不同的场景整体尺度，而没有任何机制把它们重新拉回一致。\n\n同样的盲点也出现在最好的纯视觉 metric depth 模型里。Metric3D v2（semanticscholar:ee531657945a58a1b4b456a6834917c0bc4025e1）只有在假设相机参数已知时才能确定尺度；UniDepth（openalex:W4402727115）输出一个对相机/尺度的单一最佳猜测，却不附带任何置信度。GeoMeter（openalex:W4414197449）这类基准也证实，即使是强大的 VLM 在深度上也不可靠。所以真正的问题不是缺一个输出层，而是模型从不表达它对眼前这张具体图像的尺度有多不确定——这意味着它可能自信地犯错，并且无法调和自己给出的多个答案。\n\n现在能解决这个问题，是因为两样好东西终于同时现成可用：一个无需额外头部、能给出不错的逐点 metric 答案的 VLM，以及一个稳定的“相对深度”模型（Depth Anything，openalex:W4402727359），后者只说哪些点更近或更远，而不承诺具体米数。把两者配在一起无需任何训练。与此同时，2026 年最新的论文都在走相反的路（添加深度头部或扩大预训练规模），把这条简单、无标签、带不确定度的路线留了出来。一旦补上这个缺口，基于 VLM 的深度系统终于可以可信地说出“我对这张图的尺度没把握”，并在需要时选择弃权——这是当前所有方法都做不到的。\n\n## 方法\n### 共享几何锚点\n*建立单一相对深度场，使所有回答都在同一把标尺上衡量。*\n\n1. 加载两个模型并冻结它们（不训练任何参数）：一个 DepthLM 类的 30 亿参数 metric vision-language model（视觉语言模型 VLM，输入图像、用文字作答），以及一个相对深度模型 R，叫 Depth-Anything-v2（它只判断哪些点更近或更远，不承诺具体米数）。对输入图像跑一次 R，得到它的原始输出（一张 inverse-depth / disparity 视差图），用 r = 1/(disparity + 0.000001) 把它转成相对深度场 r（加的这个极小常数只是为了避免除法爆炸），再把 r 裁剪到全图 0.5% 到 99.5% 分位之间，使天空、边缘等少数极端像素不会污染后续步骤。r 的单位是任意的——后面只用到它内部各值之间的比值，所以不对它做整体缩放。\n   - _为什么_: r 是那把唯一的共享标尺，让后面每个回答都能放在同一基准上衡量。\n2. 用 farthest-point sampling（一种贪心规则：每次都挑离已选点最远的那个点）选出 K=24 个分散的查询点，在“水平位置、垂直位置、相对深度 r”三者合成的空间里进行（每个轴缩放到 0–1），从 r 取中位数的那个像素开始；这样能保证这些点铺满整幅画面、覆盖从近到远的完整范围，并且要跳过步骤 第1步（加载两个模型并冻结它们） 中被裁剪掉的极端像素。对每个点，在该图像的一份新副本上、以该点为中心画一个明亮的小实心圆点（直径约 6 像素，每份副本只画一个点，使各次提问互相独立），然后问冻结的 VLM：“被标记的点离相机多少米？请只回答一个数字。” 从每条回答里取它给出的第一个数字（去掉结尾的 'm' 或 'meters'）作为该点的答案 $d_{VLM}(p_{k})$；若某条回答没有可用的数字，就丢弃这次查询而不是猜一个值。\n   - _为什么_: 同一场景上的多个点提供了冗余回答，它们的一致与分歧正是我们要利用的。\n\n### 共识尺度估计器\n*把众多带噪的逐查询尺度汇成一个稳健尺度和一张一致的度量深度图。*\n\n3. 对每个被查询的点，把 VLM 给出的米数除以同一点处的相对深度值 r：$\\sigma _{k} = d_{VLM}(p_{k}) / r(p_{k})$（Eq. 1）。每个 $\\sigma _{k}$ 就是这一个回答所隐含的整幅场景的整体尺度（单位是“米每相对单位”）。这一步是关键的换算：它把关于不同点的回答统一成一个共享的、可直接比较的量——场景的全局尺度——从而让这 K 个回答成为同一个估计问题里的成员。结果是隐含尺度列表 ${\\sigma _{k}}$。\n\n*每个查询 k 用 VLM 在标记像素 $p_{k}$ 处的度量回答与共享相对深度值 $r(p_{k})$ 算出一个隐含的全局尺度 $\\sigma _{k}$（单位：米每相对单位）。*\n$$ \\sigma_k = \\frac{d_{\\mathrm{VLM}}(p_k)}{r(p_k)} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 它把关于不同点的回答统一成一个可比较的量——场景的全局尺度。\n4. 取所有隐含尺度 $\\sigma _{k}$ 的中位数作为共识尺度 s*（Eq. 2）——之所以用中位数而非平均数，是为了让少数错得离谱的回答无法把估计值拽偏。然后用 s* 乘以整个相对深度场，得到一张度量深度图 M = s* $\\cdot  r$，并把 M(pixel) = s* $\\cdot $ r(pixel) 作为每个像素的最终深度（替换掉模型原先逐点给出的各个数字）。由于现在所有点都共享同一个尺度 s*，模型的各个回答便自动彼此一致。\n\n*共识尺度 s* 是这 K 个隐含尺度的中位数；用 s* 乘以相对深度场即得到一张所有查询都一致的度量深度图 M。*\n$$ s^{*} = \\operatorname{median}_{k=1}^{K} \\sigma_k, \\qquad M = s^{*}\\, r \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 中位数对少数坏回答稳健，而单一共享尺度让所有点自动一致。\n\n### 自导出的校准不确定度\n*读取跨查询离散度，并把它校准成对分布漂移稳健的信任分。*\n\n5. 衡量各个逐查询尺度 $\\sigma _{k}$ 与共识 s* 之间的分歧程度：取绝对对数差的中位数，D = |log $\\sigma _{k} -  log$ s*| 的中位数（Eq. 3）。在对数尺度上计算使得高估和低估被同等看待，取中位数则保证稳健。D 是每幅图像一个普通数值、无需任何标签，并直接刻画模型自身回答里的发散程度——发散越大，尺度越不可靠。\n\n*离散度 D 是各 log 隐含尺度围绕共识的稳健分布宽度，是一个无量纲、无需标签的读数，刻画模型自身回答之间的分歧程度。*\n$$ D = \\operatorname{median}_{k=1}^{K} \\big| \\log \\sigma_k - \\log s^{*} \\big| \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 如果模型自己的回答四处发散，尺度就不可靠；D 正好无需标签地刻画这种发散。\n6. 只做一次：在一小批带有 ground-truth（真值）深度的校准图像上，学习离散度与真实误差之间的关系。首先把每幅校准图像的真实尺度误差定义为 e = |log(s* $/ s_{gt})|$，其中 $s_{gt}$ 是把相对深度场 r 与真值深度对齐得最好的那个单一标量（计算方式：在有效像素上取 真值深度 $\\div  r$ 的中位数）。然后拟合一条 isotonic regression（保序回归，一条被强制只升不降的曲线），把 D 映射到 e，记作 $g_{iso}$。另外要防止在异常图像上谎报高置信：在校准集上对 log s* 拟合一条简单的钟形曲线（得到它的中心和宽度），衡量一个新的 s* 落在该中心之外多少个宽度，再学一条同样只升不降的曲线，把这个“超出范围的距离”转成误差值（即“下限项 floor”）。最终的校准不确定度取两者中较大者：$u = max(g_{iso}(D),$ floor)（Eq. 4）。两个模型都保持冻结；你只拟合这两条小曲线。\n\n*校准后的不确定度 u 把 D 经过 isotonic 回归映射，并用一个先验距离项做下限保护，使得当 s* 远离训练尺度分布时，较小的 D 也不会谎报高置信。*\n$$ u = g_\\theta(D, s^{*}) = \\max\\big(g_{\\mathrm{iso}}(D),\\; \\mathrm{floor}(s^{*})\\big) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这把原始发散 D 转成一个有意义的“尺度错得有多离谱”的数值，下限项则防止它在异常图像上谎报高置信。\n7. 测试时，对每幅图像同时输出度量深度图 M 和它的校准信任值 u（除图像本身外不需要任何额外输入）。下游使用者决定想保留多大比例的图像（即覆盖率），并对 u 最高的那些图像弃权——也就是只保留不确定度低的图像——从而跳过有风险的图像而不是盲目信任。这样系统既交出了答案，也交出了可信度分数，且两者都仅由模型自身的回答构建而来。\n   - _为什么_: 它同时给出答案和信任分，让有风险的图像可以被跳过而不是被盲目信任。\n\n### 保真性证明\n*通过打断耦合的对照实验，证明增益来自真实的几何一致。*\n\n8. 为了证明好处是真实的、而不仅仅来自多问了问题，重做整套流程，但故意打断共享锚点。对 K 个查询中的每一个单独处理：随机裁出一块覆盖图像 40–60% 面积的方形区域（位置要保证仍包含该点），在这块区域上跑相对深度模型 R 得到一个独立的相对深度场 $r_{k}$，画上 marker，再就这块区域向 VLM 提问；基于裁块的隐含尺度为 $\\sigma '_{k} = d_{VLM}(p_{k})/r_{k}(p_{k})$。如此一来，每个回答都对照一把不同的、独立测得的标尺，这些点不再共享同一个场景——但你提问的次数完全相同。把这些值送入与正式流程完全相同的中位数与离散度代码，得到对照组的尺度与离散度，再得到其深度图与不确定度。预期：共享锚点一旦消失，深度改进以及离散度与误差之间的关联都应回落到普通单次提问的水平。另外再跑一个精简的“正向”版本，仅用离散度这个数值来决定弃权，以表明离散度本身就承载了好处。\n   - _为什么_: 如果好处真的来自这些点对同一场景的一致，那么打断这种一致就应抹掉好处——以此证明效果是真实的，而非仅仅因为多问了问题。\n\n"},{"id":"25","run_dir":"run_prompt25_diffmpc","index":25,"title":"Certified-Inexact Gradients for GPU Differentiable MPC","title_zh":"面向 GPU 可微分 MPC 的带证书不精确梯度","method_name":"Certified-Inexact Gradients (CIG)","hook":"GPU differentiable MPC gets its speedup by solving the backward sensitivity system with a truncated Krylov routine, then hands the resulting gradient to the learner as if it were exact; we show that the same Krylov residual the solver already computes yields a cheap, per-instance certificate that provably bounds the gradient's distance from the exact implicit-function-theorem sensitivity, turning a silently-corrupted gradient into a trusted one and letting the solver spend iterations only where the certificate says the gradient is not yet good enough.","anchor_pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","anchor_pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","domain_category":"Optimization & Search","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes how the parameter gradient returned by a truncated GPU inner solve deviates from the exact implicit-function-theorem sensitivity as a function of the inner solver's stopping point — the gradient is consumed as exact, so no leaf produces a per-instance quantity the outer optimizer could read to know how much each gradient can be trusted.","pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","sub_pattern":"C09 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by relocating the trust mechanism off the (expensive) exact adjoint solve and onto an intermediate object — the truncated-Krylov adjoint residual r_K = (KKT) g_K - dl/dz — and proving a per-instance influence-style bound ||g_K - g_exact|| <= ||M^{-1}|| * ||r_K|| that certifies the gradient error from quantities the PCG already produces, so the gradient-trust budget no longer scales with solving the linear system to full precision.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf adapts the inner-solve effort to the outer learning signal: the inner PCG/iLQR budget is fixed by a tolerance chosen once, decoupled from whether the resulting gradient is good enough for the current outer step, so compute is spent identically on batch instances whose gradients are already accurate and on stiff instances whose gradients are badly corrupted.","pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by recasting the heuristic 'pick one global PCG tolerance' as a measurement-driven allocation object: each batch instance carries the certificate epsilon_hat_i as a per-unit gradient-uncertainty score, and a greedy marginal-error-per-iteration selector spends the shared batch iteration budget B on the instances whose certificate is largest, certified causally by the fact that perturbing the allocation degrades outer convergence.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"differentiable optimal control / learning-for-control (differentiable MPC on GPU)","n_papers":32,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":25},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"openreview","n":2}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":16,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Actor-Critic Model Predictive Control"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Learning Constrained Parametric Differentiable Predictive Control Policies With Guarantees"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Gaussian Process Based Learning Model Predictive Control With Application to USV"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Differentiable Robust Model Predictive Control"},{"source":"openalex","title":"NaCl enhances CD8+ T cell effector functions in cancer immunotherapy"},{"source":"openalex","title":"A Novel Enhanced Data-Driven Model-Free Adaptive Control Scheme for Path Tracking of Autonomous Vehicles"}],"more":10},{"year":2025,"n":22,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Differentiable Model Predictive Control on the GPU"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Policy Optimization for Unknown Systems using Differentiable Model Predictive Control"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Differentiable Model Predictive Safety for Heterogeneous Mobility at Urban Intersections"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Optimal System Excitation of a Permanent Magnet Synchronous Motor Using Differentiable Model Predictive Excitation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Differentiable Nonlinear Model Predictive Control"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Differentiable neural network-based models enable gradient-based optimization for model predictive control of urban drainage networks."}],"more":16},{"year":2026,"n":2,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"},{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"}],"more":0}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":15,"share":0.469},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":8,"share":0.25},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":8,"share":0.25},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":4,"share":0.125},{"pattern_id":"relax_discrete_search_to_continuous","pattern_name":"Relax Discrete Search to Continuous","count":3,"share":0.094},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":3,"share":0.094},{"pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","count":3,"share":0.094},{"pattern_id":"algebraic_equivalence_unification","pattern_name":"Prove Equivalence to Unify","count":2,"share":0.062}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"GPU-parallel differentiable MPC achieves its speedups by solving both the forward KKT system and the backward sensitivity system with a truncated iterative routine — preconditioned conjugate gradient run to a tolerance or a fixed iteration budget — yet the gradient it returns is plugged into the outer learner as though the inner solve were exact (semanticscholar:b7a09797ce822401737e0da5e118823d0193bb19). The implicit-function-theorem identity these sensitivities rest on is exact only at the converged optimum and with an exactly-solved adjoint linear system; on the GPU the forward SQP/QP solve is stopped early and the backward linear system is itself solved by truncated PCG, so the returned parameter gradient carries an inner-solver-tolerance-dependent error term whose size and direction nobody measures (semanticscholar:f4ffd8bc94a0038dd12c7f1d08a9fd24d76ca941 derives the same IFT sensitivities for nonlinear MPC but on CPU and likewise assumes the inner solve has converged). The failure is that under aggressive truncation — exactly the regime that buys the GPU speedup — the gradient can point in a descent-violating direction or have batch-element-dependent error, and current solvers expose no quantity that tells the outer optimizer how much to trust each per-instance gradient, so users must either solve to tight tolerance (forfeiting the GPU win) or accept silent, uncontrolled gradient corruption.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:b7a09797ce822401737e0da5e118823d0193bb19","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"DiffMPC solves the KKT linear system for BOTH the forward QP (Eq. 6) and the backward sensitivity (Eq. 7) with the SAME truncated preconditioned-conjugate-gradient routine, getting >4x GPU speedups by exploiting block-tridiagonal structure and warm-starting. Its residue: the backward sensitivity is computed by an iterative PCG solve that is stopped before exact convergence, but the returned gradient is treated as the exact IFT sensitivity — the paper never characterizes the gradient error as a function of PCG iteration budget / residual tolerance, never propagates that error into a trust signal for the outer optimizer, and never shows whether truncation-induced gradient bias is uniform across a batch or concentrates on stiff instances."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:f4ffd8bc94a0038dd12c7f1d08a9fd24d76ca941","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Differentiable Nonlinear MPC computes parametric solution sensitivities for general nonlinear programs via the implicit function theorem applied to smoothed interior-point optimality conditions inside an SQP loop. Residue: it assumes the forward NLP is solved to optimality and the sensitivity linear system is solved exactly, runs on CPU with sparse sequential factorization, and gives no account of how sensitivity error behaves when the inner solve is truncated for speed — the precise regime GPU batching forces."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:37196dc5e87b91cf4c480023b9adcf6508f63511","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Policy Optimization for Unknown Systems blends the differentiable-MPC (model-based) gradient with a zeroth-order (model-free) estimate to be robust to inaccurate dynamics models, trading the two off by a fixed trust weight. Residue: its trust weight targets MODEL inaccuracy, not SOLVER-truncation inaccuracy of the differentiable gradient itself; the blend weight is not derived from any measured property of the inner-solve and gives no per-instance control over solver-induced gradient error."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"differentiable optimal control / learning-for-control (differentiable MPC on GPU)","venue":"NeurIPS / ICML / ICLR (ML methods track) or L4DC / CoRL","time":"2026","data":["simulated control benchmarks (cartpole, pendulum, quadcopter), imitation-learning and RL trajectory datasets used by differentiable-MPC libraries (mpc.pytorch, trajax, Theseus)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML + numerical optimization / control","preference":"both","baseline":"DiffMPC GPU solver (semanticscholar:b7a09797...), mpc.pytorch / trajax / Theseus differentiable-MPC libraries, IFT-with-exact-solve sensitivities","limitation":"GPU differentiable MPC computes gradients (sensitivities) via a truncated/iterative inner linear solve, but treats the resulting gradient as if the inner solve were exact; the error this injects into the parameter gradient is uncharacterized and uncontrolled","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object both legs read from and write to is the per-instance gradient-error certificate epsilon_hat_i, a scalar upper bound on the distance between the truncated backward gradient and the exact implicit-function-theorem (IFT) sensitivity for batch element i. LEG 1 (architectural_operator_substitution, C09) constructs it. DiffMPC computes the parameter gradient by solving one linear system K w = dl/dz in the KKT matrix K (the same block-tridiagonal matrix factored in the forward pass) with truncated preconditioned conjugate gradient (PCG); let g_K be the gradient assembled from the K-iteration PCG solution w_K and g_exact the gradient from the exact solution w*. Standard Krylov algebra gives g_K - g_exact = J (w_K - w*) where J is the (problem-defined, cheaply-applied) map from adjoint solution to parameter gradient, and w_K - w* = -K^{-1} r_K with r_K = K w_K - dl/dz the PCG residual the solver ALREADY computes each iteration; hence epsilon_hat_i := ||J|| * kappa_hat_i * ||r_K||_i / sigma_min_hat where kappa_hat_i and sigma_min_hat (a running estimate of K's smallest singular value, read off the same Lanczos coefficients PCG generates) bound ||K^{-1}||. Every quantity in epsilon_hat_i is either already produced by the PCG iteration (r_K, Lanczos coefficients) or a one-time per-instance matrix-norm estimate (||J||), so the certificate costs O(1) extra work per PCG iteration and is computable from the solver state alone; the preserved essential property is descent-validity — when epsilon_hat_i < ||g_K||_i the truncated gradient is in the same halfspace as g_exact, so it is a guaranteed descent direction. LEG 2 (reframe_as_solvable_object, C00) consumes epsilon_hat_i: instead of a single global PCG tolerance, we pose per-step inner-iteration allocation as a measurement-driven selection object — given a shared batch iteration budget B, choose each instance's extra-iteration count n_i to minimize the batch's total certified gradient error sum_i epsilon_hat_i(n_i) subject to sum_i n_i <= B; because each extra PCG iteration's marginal certificate drop is computable on the fly, a greedy 'spend the next iteration on the instance with the largest current epsilon_hat_i' rule solves this allocation to within the standard greedy ratio, automatically starving easy instances and pouring iterations into stiff ones. The two legs interlock on exactly one object (epsilon_hat_i): leg 1 is the estimator that produces it with a proven bound, leg 2 is the selector that acts on it, so the paper reads as one contribution — a certified inexact gradient and the budget controller its certificate enables — not two. Numbers: the anchor reports >4x GPU speedup over mpc.pytorch/trajax/Theseus at a FIXED tolerance (semanticscholar:b7a09797...); we do not claim a faster exact solve, we claim equal-or-better OUTER-LOOP task performance at a fraction of the total inner iterations because the certificate reallocates a fixed iteration budget rather than tightening it everywhere.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules because the sibling gap's allocation decision is impossible without a per-instance error signal, and the anchor gap's whole point is to produce exactly that signal — the evidence is that epsilon_hat_i appears as the output of leg 1 and the sole input of leg 2, so a single object threads both; splitting them would force leg 2 to invent its own (uncertified) heuristic signal, which is the status quo we are replacing. (b) Alternative designs considered and rejected: (1) computing the true gradient error by also solving the system exactly and comparing — defeats the purpose (no speedup) and was rejected; (2) a learned regressor that predicts gradient error from features — rejected because it carries no guarantee and would itself need supervision (the exact gradient); (3) putting the certificate on the FORWARD residual only — rejected because the IFT identity's error is dominated by the BACKWARD adjoint solve, so the forward residual alone under-counts the gradient error. AVOIDED REGRESSION (method_lineage): the load-bearing artifact is a Krylov-residual-derived certificate connected to end-task gradient error, which lands on neither n1 (vanilla IFT-at-exact-optimum, which assumes an exact solve and produces no error signal) nor n0 (unrolling); it is the link collateral node c1 explicitly flags as never-made (Krylov residual error -> control-learning parameter-gradient error), and it is NOT a curvature/spectral-reshaping move so it does not collapse into C30's territory.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: take the public JAX DiffMPC solver and its RL (e.g. pendulum/cartpole swing-up) and imitation-learning tasks, fix a total backward-pass PCG iteration budget B per outer step, and compare three inner-iteration policies under the same B: (i) uniform split, (ii) the certificate-greedy allocator, (iii) the certificate-greedy allocator with epsilon_hat_i randomly permuted across the batch. Metric that moves: at equal total inner-compute, the certificate-greedy allocator reaches a given outer task return / imitation loss in fewer total PCG iterations (the task-metric-vs-inner-compute curve shifts left), and the fraction of outer steps taking a descent-violating gradient (measured against a periodically-computed exact gradient) drops. The named load-bearing variable is the per-instance certificate epsilon_hat_i. Negative control: permuting epsilon_hat_i across the batch (policy iii) — which preserves the certificate's marginal distribution and total budget but destroys its instance correspondence — must drive the OUTER task metric (final return / imitation loss at fixed budget) back to the uniform-split baseline; if randomized allocation converges just as well, the certificate is not carrying instance-specific gradient-trust information and the mechanism is falsified. Positive control: an allocator that uses ONLY epsilon_hat_i (no other features) should recover most of the convergence-per-compute gain, identifying the certificate as the sufficient signal.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:b7a09797ce822401737e0da5e118823d0193bb19","delta":"They solve the backward sensitivity with truncated PCG and consume g_K as the exact IFT sensitivity with no error account; we derive a per-instance bound ||g_K - g_exact|| <= ||J|| ||r_K|| / sigma_min computed from the PCG residual they already discard, and use it to reallocate a fixed inner-iteration budget — a quantity and a controller their solver does not produce."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:f4ffd8bc94a0038dd12c7f1d08a9fd24d76ca941","delta":"They compute IFT sensitivities for nonlinear MPC assuming the inner NLP and the sensitivity linear system are solved exactly (CPU, sparse factorization); we drop the exact-solve assumption and instead certify and control the gradient error of a deliberately truncated solve, the regime GPU batching forces and their analysis does not cover."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:37196dc5e87b91cf4c480023b9adcf6508f63511","delta":"Their trust weight blends model-based and zeroth-order gradients to be robust to MODEL inaccuracy via a fixed scalar; our certificate quantifies SOLVER-truncation inaccuracy of the differentiable gradient itself, is computed per-instance from the solver state, and drives compute allocation rather than a fixed blend."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:b7a09797ce822401737e0da5e118823d0193bb19","what_step_was_missed":"DiffMPC already produces the PCG residual r_K and the Lanczos coefficients at every backward-pass iteration, and already solves the backward system with the same KKT matrix as the forward — so it had every ingredient in hand; the missed step is the derivation that turns the residual into a per-instance UPPER BOUND on the parameter-gradient error (the J and sigma_min bookkeeping that maps adjoint-solution residual to gradient distance), and the recognition that this bound can be read as a per-instance trust score to reallocate a fixed iteration budget instead of being thrown away after the solve."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":262,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"Hard floor did not fire: gap_closure_reject_check is 'borderline' not 'triggered' (no Reject lesson is candidate_match: yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and the paper_pointed_threat is adjacent-but-non-subsuming (not exact-mechanism overlap). recipe_application_check is 'applied' on both legs, so the idea is built from the C09 and C00 distinctive moves rather than the parents' gist. The one borderline (C09's 'improvement that holds only in a narrow regime' lesson) hits an empirical condition — batch stiffness heterogeneity — that falsification_prediction's controlled fixed-budget comparison already tests, so it is a surface-for-Phase-4 concern, not a load-bearing structural defect requiring revision.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes how the parameter gradient returned by a truncated GPU inner solve deviates from the exact implicit-function-theorem sensitivity as a function of the inner solver's stopping point — the gradient is consumed as exact, so no leaf produces a per-instance quantity the outer optimizer could read to know how much each gradient can be trusted.","main_pattern":"architectural_operator_substitution","sub_pattern":"C09 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is that the substitution is performed but the gap over the substituted-out baseline is never convincingly established — either a mechanical composition of two pre-existing primitives yielding no new sensitivity bound, a marginal/regime-bound gain, or an unsound proof whose abstract bound differs from the proven one.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A substitution that is merely two known primitives composed, carrying no new sensitivity bound, reads as 'not enough of a contribution in and of itself.'","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The certificate is a genuinely new per-instance bound that maps the truncated-Krylov adjoint residual to parameter-gradient distance (the J and sigma_min bookkeeping) — not a stack of two off-the-shelf primitives, and method_lineage collateral node c1 confirms this residual->gradient-error link has not been made in this loop."},{"lesson_quoted":"An improvement that holds only in a narrow regime and might be matched by re-analyzing existing methods will be judged a non-improvement, not a contribution.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The convergence-per-compute gain depends on the batch actually containing heterogeneous stiffness; on a perfectly homogeneous batch the allocator reduces to uniform — the candidate must show the gain on realistically heterogeneous batches, which falsification_prediction's negative control partly addresses."},{"lesson_quoted":"An internal inconsistency between the bound claimed in the abstract and the bound actually proven, plus a missing thorough prior-art comparison, sinks the work regardless of the idea's merit.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate states one bound (||g_K - g_exact|| <= ||J|| ||r_K|| / sigma_min) used consistently across hook/core_mechanism/differentiation; prior-art comparison is explicit against the anchor and two adjacent papers."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf adapts the inner-solve effort to the outer learning signal: the inner PCG/iLQR budget is fixed by a tolerance chosen once, decoupled from whether the resulting gradient is good enough for the current outer step, so compute is spent identically on batch instances whose gradients are already accurate and on stiff instances whose gradients are badly corrupted.","main_pattern":"reframe_as_solvable_object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Correlational evidence, eyeballed heatmaps, or 'looks reasonable' without a confound-controlling test is precisely the gap that sinks otherwise-clever reframings; pointing an off-the-shelf tool at a coarser granularity without showing the signal survives reads as a mechanical wrapper.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Pointing an off-the-shelf decomposition at a coarser input granularity without showing the coarser units preserve the signal reads as a wrapper, not a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The selection object is not an off-the-shelf decomposition at a coarser granularity; the per-instance unit is intrinsic (one OCP instance = one certificate) and the allocation objective (minimize total certified gradient error under a budget) is derived from the certificate, not bolted on."},{"lesson_quoted":"Proposing a new attribution definition without an axiomatic or causal argument for why it should count as ground-truth collapses the moment a reviewer asks why this is the real importance.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The certificate is not a heuristic attribution score — it is a proven upper bound on gradient error, and its causal role is tested by the negative-control permutation in falsification_prediction (perturb allocation -> outer convergence reverts)."},{"lesson_quoted":"Conflating a methodological artifact — a computation-granularity difference, a degenerate zero baseline — with genuine signal undermines the entire premise once the confound is identified.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The compared baselines (uniform split vs certificate-greedy vs permuted-certificate) hold the total iteration budget B fixed, so the gain cannot be attributed to extra compute — the budget is the controlled axis."}],"verdict":"clear"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The anchor entry (architectural_operator_substitution / C09) is borderline on the regime-bound-gain lesson — the convergence-per-compute win requires batch stiffness heterogeneity, which is a load-bearing empirical condition rather than a flaw in the construction. The sibling entry (reframe_as_solvable_object / C00) is clear because the budget-controlled baselines rule out the wrapper and confound failure shapes."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes how the parameter gradient returned by a truncated GPU inner solve deviates from the exact implicit-function-theorem sensitivity as a function of the inner solver's stopping point — the gradient is consumed as exact, so no leaf produces a per-instance quantity the outer optimizer could read to know how much each gradient can be trusted.","sub_pattern":"C09 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Insert a low-sensitivity intermediate object between the raw input and the downstream procedure, then attach the costly mechanism to that intermediate; the load-bearing artifact is a per-element influence/sensitivity bound on the intermediate that proves the budget no longer scales with the ambient quantity that made the naive mechanism intractable.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism leg 1 inserts the truncated-Krylov adjoint residual r_K as the intermediate object and attaches the trust mechanism to it, proving the per-instance bound epsilon_hat_i = ||J|| ||r_K||_i / sigma_min_hat that decouples gradient-trust from the ambient cost of an exact linear solve — exactly the 'relocate the costly mechanism onto an intermediate with a provable per-element influence bound' move, with the ambient quantity being the cost of solving the KKT system to full precision.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf adapts the inner-solve effort to the outer learning signal: the inner PCG/iLQR budget is fixed by a tolerance chosen once, decoupled from whether the resulting gradient is good enough for the current outer step, so compute is spent identically on batch instances whose gradients are already accurate and on stiff instances whose gradients are badly corrupted.","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Recast an opaque question as a concrete measurement over a well-studied object (subset selection, estimator, decomposition), choosing the right unit of analysis and faithfulness constraint, buying tractability with one compression trick, and certifying fidelity causally rather than by plausibility.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism leg 2 recasts 'pick one global tolerance' as a budget-constrained subset/allocation selection object over the per-instance certificate (the unit of analysis = one OCP instance), buys tractability with the greedy marginal-error-per-iteration rule (the single compression trick), and certifies fidelity causally via the permutation negative control — the C00 measurement-and-causal-certification move, not a generic reframe.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both legs perform their cited cluster's distinctive move: C09's per-element influence bound on a relocated intermediate (the certificate on the Krylov residual) and C00's measurement-object recast with causal certification (the budget-allocation selector validated by permutation), not the parents' generic gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["architectural_operator_substitution","reframe_as_solvable_object"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; this candidate's composition {architectural_operator_substitution, reframe_as_solvable_object} contains no heterogeneous_decomposition, so no anti-pattern matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:Inexact-Adjoint-Gradients-Directional-Tolerances-Airfoil","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"The closest competitor, 'Inexact Adjoint Gradients and Directional Tolerances for Full-Potential Airfoil Optimization' (collision_hits, 2026-05), develops a framework connecting discrete adjoint gradient-error analysis with an optimizer that uses directional error tolerances, and analyzes how inexact state and adjoint residuals propagate into the reduced gradient — the same conceptual move (residual -> reduced-gradient-error bound -> tolerance-driven solver effort). The candidate's claim stands rather than falls against it because the threat paper targets a single scalar-objective shape-optimization problem governed by ONE full-potential PDE on a CPU body-fitted structured mesh, using a global directional tolerance for one optimization trajectory; it produces neither a PER-INSTANCE certificate across a GPU BATCH of OCP instances, nor a per-instance compute ALLOCATOR that redistributes a fixed batch iteration budget, nor the descent-validity guard tied to a control-learning outer loop. So it is genuinely adjacent prior art on the residual->gradient-error idea but does not subsume the batched, per-instance, allocation-driven contribution in differentiable MPC.","addressable_via":"differentiation_from_lit should add this paper with a delta sharpening that our certificate is per-instance across a batch and drives budget reallocation, whereas theirs is a single global directional tolerance for one CFD trajectory — a Phase 4 reviewer_concerns_and_responses item rather than a mechanism change."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Certified-Inexact Gradients for GPU Differentiable MPC\n\n**Method.** Certified-Inexact Gradients (CIG)\n\n## Motivation\nDifferentiable MPC (Model Predictive Control) is a way to make a controller's optimization solver part of a neural-network training loop: you can compute how the controller's output changes when you nudge its parameters, and use that to train. The fast modern version runs on the GPU by solving the linear systems inside the controller only approximately — it stops the iterative solver early to save time. The catch is that it then treats the resulting gradient as if it were exact, even though stopping early introduces an error. When the solver is stopped very aggressively (which is exactly what makes it fast), that error can be large enough that the gradient points the wrong way, and it hits some problem instances in a batch much harder than others. Nobody currently measures this error, so a user must either solve precisely (losing the speed) or accept silent corruption.\n\nThis is solvable now because the GPU solver already computes, at every iteration, the exact internal quantities (the 'residual' $r_{K}$ and the Lanczos coefficients) that classical numerical-linear-algebra theory uses to estimate solver error — it just throws them away. The missing piece is a derivation linking that solver residual to the actual error in the final training gradient, plus a controller that acts on it. Prior work stopped short: the GPU paper never measured the gradient error (semanticscholar:b7a09797..., arXiv 2025-10); the CPU nonlinear-MPC sensitivity paper assumed the solve was exact (semanticscholar:f4ffd8bc..., arXiv 2025-11); and the model-robustness blending paper used a fixed trust knob aimed at model error, not solver-truncation error (semanticscholar:37196dc5..., arXiv 2025-11).\n\nWhen this gap closes, the training gradient comes with a free, per-instance trust score, so the fast-but-approximate GPU gradient becomes a certified descent direction instead of a gamble. It also lets you schedule the solver's effort: with a fixed iteration budget, spend the iterations on the instances the certificate says are least trustworthy. Any downstream learner that consumes these batched gradients benefits directly.\n\n## Method\n### Background (unchanged scaffolding)\n*Hand the gradient to the learner unchanged and evaluate against the permutation control.*\n\n1. Build each problem's gradient from its (now adaptively stopped) solution using the exact same assembly code the original method uses, and pass the batch of gradients to the outer training loop unchanged — same optimizer, same loss, same settings. The learner cannot tell anything changed; it just receives a gradient of the usual shape. The only difference is that some problems were solved with more iterations and some with fewer. Keeping this hand-off identical to the baseline is on purpose, so that any improvement can only be credited to the smarter allocation.\n   - _Why_: Keeping the gradient a drop-in replacement means any improvement is attributable to smarter allocation, not a different training recipe.\n2. Test on the same benchmarks the original paper uses (cartpole, pendulum, quadcopter, in both reinforcement learning and imitation learning, using its public JAX solver). Compare three ways of spending the same fixed iteration budget: (i) split evenly across problems, (ii) the certificate-greedy allocation from the previous steps, and (iii) the same greedy method but with the certificates randomly shuffled between problems each step. For each, record the total inner iterations used, the task score, and how often the truncated gradient points the wrong way. To measure 'wrong way', periodically (every 20 outer steps) solve a few problems exactly — to machine precision — to get the true gradient, and count a violation whenever the truncated gradient and the true gradient point into opposite half-spaces. These exact solves are only for measurement and are never used to train.\n   - _Why_: Holding the budget fixed and permuting the certificate isolates whether the per-instance signal — not extra compute — is what helps.\n\n### Certificate Estimator\n*Turn the solver's already-computed residual into a proven per-instance bound on the gradient error.*\n\n3. Open the existing GPU backward solver — the preconditioned conjugate gradient (PCG) routine that solves the adjoint linear system K w = dl/dz for every problem in the batch at once. After each iteration, it already computes a residual $r_{K}$ (how far the current solution is from solving the system) and two small scalars from the conjugate-gradient recurrence (the step length and the conjugacy coefficient). Save these into pre-allocated arrays of size (number of problems in batch) $\\times  (max$ iterations) instead of throwing them away. Because all problems in the batch already march in step together, saving these adds essentially no overhead.\n\n*The truncated-PCG adjoint residual $r_{K}$ (already computed every iteration when solving the KKT system K for the adjoint solution) measures how far the K-iteration solution $w_{K}$ is from the exact solution w*.*\n$$ r_K = K\\, w_K - \\frac{\\partial \\ell}{\\partial z}, \\qquad w_K - w^\\star = -K^{-1} r_K \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The error-estimating raw material is already produced for free; you just have to stop throwing it away.\n4. Turn the saved quantities into a per-problem trust number, the certificate $\\hat{\\epsilon }_{i}.$ You need two pieces. First, the size (spectral norm) of the map J that converts a solved adjoint vector into the final parameter gradient — estimate it with 20 rounds of power iteration (a standard cheap way to find the largest stretch factor of a linear map) on that map. Second, an estimate of the smallest singular value $\\sigma _{min}$ of the system matrix K, read off from the small tridiagonal matrix built out of the two saved scalars. Since an early estimate of $\\sigma _{min}$ can be too large and spoil the guarantee, also keep a safe lower bound on $\\sigma _{min}:$ the matrix K is regularized by a known amount $\\delta ,$ so $\\sigma _{min}$ can never be below $\\delta $; clamp to that floor. 【author decision: use the raw smallest estimate (tighter, but only guaranteed once enough iterations have run) or the safe floor $\\delta $ (always a valid bound) as the $\\sigma _{min}$ you actually divide by — a trade-off between tightness and a guaranteed bound.】 Combine as certificate = (size of J) $\\times $ (residual size) $\\div  \\sigma _{min}$; this is a proven over-estimate of how far this problem's gradient is from the exact one.\n\n*The per-instance certificate: the parameter-gradient error is upper-bounded by the norm of the adjoint-to-gradient map J times the residual norm divided by an estimate of K's smallest singular value $\\sigma _{min}$ (read from the Lanczos coefficients).*\n$$ \\hat{\\varepsilon}_i \\;:=\\; \\|J\\|\\,\\frac{\\|r_K\\|_i}{\\hat{\\sigma}_{\\min}} \\;\\geq\\; \\|g_{K,i} - g_{\\mathrm{exact},i}\\| \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This converts a solver-internal residual into a trustworthy bound on how far the training gradient is from exact.\n\n### Budget Allocator\n*Spend a fixed inner-iteration budget where the certificate says the gradient is least trustworthy.*\n\n5. Throw away the one-size-fits-all stopping rule. Instead, repeatedly do this: look at every problem's current certificate, keep advancing the problems whose certificate is still large, and freeze the ones whose gradient is already trustworthy. Concretely, run one more shared solver iteration over the batch but only let the still-untrustworthy problems update (freeze the rest with a mask), subtract the number of active problems from the remaining budget, recompute their certificates, and repeat until the total budget is used up. The budget is set relative to what the old method spends: budget = ratio $\\times $ (number of problems $\\times $ the old fixed iteration count), with ratio = 1.0 for an exactly equal-compute comparison and also tried at 0.5 and 0.75. Freezing easy problems and pouring iterations into hard ones is how a fixed pool of work gets spent where it matters, without breaking the all-at-once GPU solve.\n\n*The allocation object: choose each instance's extra PCG-iteration count $n_{i}$ to minimize the batch's total certified gradient error under a shared iteration budget B, solved greedily by always spending the next iteration on the largest-certificate instance.*\n$$ \\min_{\\{n_i\\}} \\sum_i \\hat{\\varepsilon}_i(n_i) \\quad \\text{s.t.} \\quad \\sum_i n_i \\leq B \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Spending the next iteration where the gradient is least trustworthy reduces total error fastest under a fixed budget.\n\n### Descent-Validity Guard\n*Mask any instance whose gradient is still not certified to be a descent direction.*\n\n6. Add a safety check before averaging gradients across the batch. For each problem, if the certificate (its worst-case error) is as large as the gradient's own size, the gradient is not trustworthy as a descent direction, so shrink that problem's contribution: multiply it by a weight that goes from 1 (fully trustworthy) down to 0 (untrustworthy), computed as 1 minus (certificate $\\div $ gradient size), clipped to the 0-to-1 range. Then average using the sum of weights rather than the plain count, so cutting some problems down does not accidentally change the overall step size. 【author decision: use this soft shrinking, or instead hard-drop any untrustworthy problem entirely — hard-dropping gives a cleaner guarantee that every step descends but makes the averaged gradient noisier.】 Record what fraction of problems got shrunk each step as a diagnostic.\n\n*Descent-validity test: when the certificate is smaller than the truncated gradient's own norm, the truncated gradient is in the same halfspace as the exact gradient and is therefore a guaranteed descent direction.*\n$$ \\hat{\\varepsilon}_i < \\|g_{K,i}\\| \\;\\Longrightarrow\\; \\langle g_{K,i},\\, g_{\\mathrm{exact},i}\\rangle > 0 \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Better to skip an uncertified instance than to step along a possibly-wrong direction.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 面向 GPU 可微分 MPC 的带证书不精确梯度\n\n**方法名称.** Certified-Inexact Gradients (CIG)\n\n## 研究动机\n可微分 MPC (Model Predictive Control，模型预测控制) 是把控制器内部的优化求解器嵌入神经网络训练回路的一种方法：你可以算出控制器的输出在参数被微调时如何变化，并据此训练。其现代的快速版本在 GPU 上运行，靠的是只近似地求解控制器内部的线性方程组——提前停止迭代求解器以节省时间。问题在于它随后把得到的梯度当作精确的来用，尽管提前停止会带来误差。当求解器被非常激进地提前停止时（而这正是它快的原因），该误差可能大到让梯度指向错误方向，而且在一批问题中对某些实例的冲击远大于其他实例。目前没人测量这个误差，于是用户要么精确求解（失去速度），要么接受被悄悄污染的梯度。\n\n现在能解决这个问题，是因为 GPU 求解器在每次迭代中其实已经算出了经典数值线性代数理论用于估计求解误差的那些内部量（残差 $r_{K}$ 和 Lanczos 系数），只是把它们丢掉了。缺失的环节是一个把求解器残差与最终训练梯度的实际误差联系起来的推导，外加一个据此行动的控制器。已有工作都止步于此：GPU 论文从未测量梯度误差 (semanticscholar:b7a09797...，arXiv 2025-10)；CPU 非线性 MPC 灵敏度论文假设求解是精确的 (semanticscholar:f4ffd8bc...，arXiv 2025-11)；而模型鲁棒性混合论文用的是针对模型误差、而非求解器截断误差的固定信任系数 (semanticscholar:37196dc5...，arXiv 2025-11)。\n\n这个缺口被填补后，训练梯度就自带一个免费的、每实例的信任分数，于是快速但近似的 GPU 梯度从一场赌博变成了带证书的下降方向。它还能让你调度求解器的算力：在固定迭代预算下，把迭代花在证书判定最不可信的实例上。任何消费这些批量梯度的下游学习器都能直接受益。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景（不变的脚手架）\n*把梯度原样交给学习器，并用置换对照进行评估。*\n\n1. 用与原方法完全相同的装配代码，从每个问题(现已自适应停止的)解构造其梯度，并把这批梯度原样传给外层训练回路——同样的优化器、同样的损失、同样的设置。学习器察觉不到任何变化，它只是收到一个常规形状的梯度。唯一的差别是有些问题用了更多迭代、有些用了更少。让这个交接与基线保持一致是刻意为之，这样任何改进都只能归功于更聪明的分配。\n   - _为什么_: 让梯度保持可直接替换，意味着任何改进都归因于更聪明的分配，而非不同的训练配方。\n2. 在原论文使用的同一批基准上测试(cartpole、pendulum、quadcopter，强化学习与模仿学习两种设定，使用其公开的 JAX 求解器)。比较在相同固定迭代预算下花费预算的三种方式：(i)在各问题间均匀分配，(ii)前几步的证书贪心分配，(iii)同样的贪心法但每步把证书在各问题间随机打乱。对每种方式，记录所用的内层总迭代数、任务得分，以及截断梯度指向错误方向的频率。为测量『错误方向』，周期性地(每 20 个外层步)对少数问题做精确求解——求到机器精度——得到真实梯度，并在截断梯度与真实梯度落入相反半空间时计为一次违例。这些精确求解仅用于测量，绝不用于训练。\n   - _为什么_: 固定预算并置换证书，能分离出究竟是每实例信号、还是额外算力在起作用。\n\n### 证书估计器\n*把求解器已算出的残差转化为每实例梯度误差的被证明成立的界。*\n\n3. 打开现有的 GPU 反向求解器——即对整批问题同时求解伴随线性系统 K w = dl/dz 的预条件共轭梯度(Preconditioned Conjugate Gradient, PCG)例程。它每次迭代其实已经算出残差 $r_{K}($当前解离解出该系统还差多远)以及共轭梯度递推中的两个小标量(步长与共轭系数)。把它们存进预先分配好的、尺寸为(批内问题数$)\\times ($最大迭代数)的数组里，而不要丢弃。由于批内所有问题本就同步推进，保存这些量几乎不增加额外开销。\n\n*截断 PCG 在求解 KKT 系统 K 的伴随解时每次迭代都已算出的残差 $r_{K}$，衡量第 K 次迭代解 $w_{K}$ 与精确解 w* 的差距。*\n$$ r_K = K\\, w_K - \\frac{\\partial \\ell}{\\partial z}, \\qquad w_K - w^\\star = -K^{-1} r_K \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 用于估计误差的原料本就免费产出，你只需别再把它扔掉。\n4. 把保存下来的量转化为每个问题的信任数值，即证书 $\\hat{\\epsilon }_{i}$。你需要两样东西。第一，把求解出的伴随向量转换成最终参数梯度的那个映射 J 的大小(谱范数)——用 20 轮幂迭代(power iteration，一种廉价地求线性映射最大拉伸因子的标准方法)在该映射上估计它。第二，系统矩阵 K 的最小奇异值 $\\sigma _{min}$ 的估计，它由那两个保存的标量所构成的小三对角矩阵读出。由于早期对 $\\sigma _{min}$ 的估计可能偏大、从而破坏上界保证，还要保留一个对 $\\sigma _{min}$ 的安全下界：矩阵 K 带有已知幅度 $\\delta $ 的正则化，因此 $\\sigma _{min}$ 绝不会低于 $\\delta $，可据此设下限。【作者需决定：实际用于相除的 $\\sigma _{min}$ 是取原始的最小估计(更紧，但只有迭代足够多后才有保证)，还是取安全下限 $\\delta ($始终是有效上界)——这是紧致性与有保证的界之间的取舍。】组合方式为：证书 = (J 的大小$) \\times  ($残差大小$) \\div  \\sigma _{min}$；这是该问题梯度离精确梯度多远的一个被证明成立的高估值。\n\n*每实例证书：参数梯度误差的上界等于伴随到梯度映射 J 的范数乘以残差范数，再除以对 K 最小奇异值 $\\sigma _{min}$ 的估计（由 Lanczos 系数读出）。*\n$$ \\hat{\\varepsilon}_i \\;:=\\; \\|J\\|\\,\\frac{\\|r_K\\|_i}{\\hat{\\sigma}_{\\min}} \\;\\geq\\; \\|g_{K,i} - g_{\\mathrm{exact},i}\\| \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这把求解器内部的残差转化为一个可信的、关于训练梯度离精确值多远的界。\n\n### 预算分配器\n*把固定的内层迭代预算花在证书判定梯度最不可信之处。*\n\n5. 丢掉一刀切的停止规则。改为反复执行：查看每个问题当前的证书，继续推进证书仍然较大的问题，冻结梯度已经可信的问题。具体做法是：对整批再跑一次共享的求解迭代，但只让仍不可信的问题更新(用掩码冻结其余问题)，从剩余预算中减去活跃问题的数量，重算它们的证书，如此重复直到预算用尽。预算相对旧方法的开销来设定：预算 = 比率 $\\times  ($问题数 $\\times $ 旧的固定迭代数)，其中比率取 1.0 作完全等算力对比，并另取 0.5 与 0.75 试验。冻结容易的问题、把迭代倾注到困难的问题，正是在不破坏一次性 GPU 求解的前提下，把固定的工作量花在刀刃上的方式。\n\n*分配目标：在共享迭代预算 B 下，为每个实例选择额外 PCG 迭代数 $n_{i}$ 以最小化整批的总证书梯度误差；用贪心法求解，每次把下一步迭代分给当前证书最大的实例。*\n$$ \\min_{\\{n_i\\}} \\sum_i \\hat{\\varepsilon}_i(n_i) \\quad \\text{s.t.} \\quad \\sum_i n_i \\leq B \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 在固定预算下，把下一步迭代花在梯度最不可信处能最快地降低总误差。\n\n### 下降有效性守卫\n*屏蔽任何梯度仍未被证明为下降方向的实例。*\n\n6. 在对整批梯度求平均之前加一道安全检查。对每个问题，如果证书(其最坏情况误差)已大到与梯度自身的大小相当，则该梯度作为下降方向不可信，于是缩小这个问题的贡献：给它乘上一个从 1(完全可信)降到 0(不可信)的权重，权重算作 1 减去(证书 $\\div $ 梯度大小)，并裁剪到 0 到 1 区间。随后用权重之和(而非问题计数)来做平均，这样削减部分问题不会意外改变整体步长。【作者需决定：采用这种软性缩小，还是直接把任何不可信问题整体丢弃——硬丢弃能更干净地保证每一步都下降，但会让平均后的梯度更嘈杂。】把每步被缩小的问题比例记录下来作为诊断。\n\n*下降有效性判据：当证书小于截断梯度自身的范数时，截断梯度与精确梯度同处一个半空间，因而必为有效下降方向。*\n$$ \\hat{\\varepsilon}_i < \\|g_{K,i}\\| \\;\\Longrightarrow\\; \\langle g_{K,i},\\, g_{\\mathrm{exact},i}\\rangle > 0 \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 与其沿一个可能错误的方向迈步，不如跳过这个未获证书的实例。\n\n"},{"id":"26","run_dir":"run_prompt26_dpdomain","index":26,"title":"Discovering the Domains You Will Adapt To, Under One Privacy Budget","title_zh":"在单一隐私预算下发现你将要适应的领域","method_name":"DiscoverAdapt","hook":"Every differentially private domain-adaptation method silently treats the domain partition as an exogenous, trusted label that someone else supplies; we instead manufacture the partition from the same sensitive data under the same budget, keyed to the adaptation gain it will later produce, and carry its privacy-induced uncertainty forward so the adaptation never mistakes a noisy guess for a clean label.","anchor_pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","anchor_pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","domain_category":"Privacy, Security & Trustworthy ML","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a domain assignment under a formal DP guarantee whose objective is the downstream adaptation/budget outcome rather than a generic clustering objective — i.e. the privately-discovered boundaries are not optimized to be the boundaries where per-domain treatment actually helps.","pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","sub_pattern":"C21 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by manufacturing the absent domain labels: domain discovery is recast as a private supervised-relabeling problem whose target is the partition that maximizes a downstream adaptation-utility surrogate, solved by an exponential mechanism whose score function IS that surrogate rather than a geometric compactness objective, so the privately-selected boundaries are by construction the ones where per-domain adaptation helps.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf analyzes how a single fixed total privacy budget should be split between discovering the domains and using them — discovery cost and adaptation cost are charged separately with no joint accounting of the end-to-end guarantee or of the optimal allocation between the two stages.","pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by partitioning the single total budget epsilon = epsilon_disc + epsilon_adapt by a downstream-utility-sensitivity criterion: an error decomposition bounds end-to-end utility loss as a sum of a discovery-noise term (decreasing in epsilon_disc) and an adaptation-noise term (decreasing in epsilon_adapt), and the split is set at the point where the two marginal sensitivities equalize rather than charging the two stages as independent flat costs.","is_anchor":false},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf carries the uncertainty of a privately-estimated domain partition forward into the adaptation step — discovered assignments are consumed as if they were clean given labels, so the adaptation is never calibrated to (or robust against) the discovery noise that DP necessarily injects.","pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by emitting the discovery stage's output not as a hard label but as a per-point posterior over domain membership (the internal-state readout) whose entropy reflects the privacy noise, and consuming it as soft responsibilities that reweight a surgically tiny per-domain lever (per-domain affine / adapter) on a frozen backbone, so points the noise made ambiguous contribute proportionally less and the adaptation is calibrated to the discovery uncertainty instead of trusting a noisy guess as ground truth.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"differentially private machine learning; domain discovery / latent subpopulation structure for transfer and adaptation","n_papers":35,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":23},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":14,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Ocular Disease Recognition via Differential Privacy and Unsupervised Domain Regularizer"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"On the Implicit Relation Between Low-Rank Adaptation and Differential Privacy"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"GALA: Graph Diffusion-Based Alignment With Jigsaw for Source-Free Domain Adaptation"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Domain-Adaptive Clustered Federated Transfer Learning for EV Charging Demand Forecasting"},{"source":"openalex","title":"DisLLM: Distributed LLMs for Privacy Assurance in Resource-Constrained Environments"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Evaluation and mitigation of the limitations of large language models in clinical decision-making"}],"more":8},{"year":2025,"n":22,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Cross-Domain Vision–Language Model Adaptation Method Combining LoRA and Differential Privacy"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"FedMentor: Domain-Aware Differential Privacy for Heterogeneous Federated LLMs in Mental Health"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Federated Fine-Tuning of Large Language Models with Privacy Preservation and Cross-Domain Semantic Alignment"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Weight-space noise for privacy-robustness trade-offs in federated learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Privacy-preserving Prompt Personalization in Federated Learning for Multimodal Large Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Adversarial Transfer Learning for Privacy-Preserving Multilingual Sentiment Detection on Social Media"}],"more":16}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":13,"share":0.371},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":12,"share":0.343},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":6,"share":0.171},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":6,"share":0.171},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":4,"share":0.114},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":4,"share":0.114},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":3,"share":0.086},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":2,"share":0.057}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Across the DP+domain literature the domain partition is treated as an exogenous, already-known input: per-domain DP budgets in FedMentor (semanticscholar:f1ab1182294964f6ad222e155043c2aeca6be798) are keyed to client IDs the clients declare, multi-source DA with domain-wise privacy (openalex:W4402475021) allocates a budget per source under the assumption that the source labels are given and trusted, and DP source-free domain adaptation (openalex:W7076966911) privatizes the model transfer but still presumes the target's domain identity is known. The moment the domain structure is itself latent in the sensitive data and must be discovered, two failure modes appear and neither line closes them: (1) the only privacy-respecting tool available is generic DP clustering (openalex:W4405181094, openalex:W4400943503), which spends its entire epsilon producing a partition whose objective (within-cluster compactness) is decoupled from the downstream use — so the discovered boundaries are not the boundaries at which per-domain adaptation or budget allocation would actually help, and the discovery noise is never accounted for in the adaptation that follows; and (2) the privacy cost of *learning where the domains are* is charged in addition to, and separately from, the privacy cost of *adapting to them*, with no analysis of how a fixed total epsilon should be split between discovery and use. The structural failure is that there is no object that (a) produces a domain assignment under a formal DP guarantee, (b) does so against the downstream adaptation/budget objective rather than a generic clustering objective, and (c) carries the discovery's own uncertainty forward so the adaptation is calibrated to a noisy, privately-estimated partition rather than a clean given one.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4402475021","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Secures multi-source domain adaptation by attaching a separate (global vs domain-wise) DP budget to each source so that membership/attribute inference across the aggregated model is bounded. The residue: every budget and every alignment term is keyed to a source partition the method takes as given and trusted — there is no mechanism by which the partition itself is discovered under DP, and therefore no account of how discovery noise propagates into the per-domain budget split or the alignment. [residue is abstract-level: anchor fulltext unfetchable]"},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7076966911","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Adds a formal DP guarantee to source-free domain adaptation by privatizing the source-model parameters shared to the target, removing the need for concurrent two-domain access. The residue: domain identity (which examples belong to which domain) is still assumed known on both sides; the work privatizes the transfer, not the discovery of the partition, so it cannot be applied when the target is an unlabeled mixture of unknown domains."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4405181094","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"DPM clusters sensitive data privately by recursively finding low-density separators, giving a DP partition of the data. The residue: the partition optimizes a generic geometric compactness/separation objective with no link to any downstream task, so the privately-discovered boundaries are not the ones at which adaptation or budget allocation is most useful, and the partition is emitted as a hard label with no uncertainty that a downstream consumer could use to discount noisy assignments."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:f1ab1182294964f6ad222e155043c2aeca6be798","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"FedMentor assigns each federated client (domain) a custom DP noise scale proportional to its declared data sensitivity and adaptively relaxes noise when utility drops below a floor. The residue: 'domain' is hard-wired to the client identity declared up front; there is no notion that two clients might share a latent domain or that one client mixes several, and thus no private mechanism to re-discover the budget-relevant grouping from the data."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"differentially private machine learning; domain discovery / latent subpopulation structure for transfer and adaptation","venue":"ICLR / ICML / NeurIPS","time":"2026","data":["multi-source / multi-site tabular or image data with unlabeled latent domain structure (e.g. multi-hospital EHR, multi-device sensor logs)","standard DP benchmarks (CIFAR/FEMNIST-style federated splits, UCI multi-source tabular)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"differential privacy theory + representation learning / domain adaptation","preference":"both","baseline":"DP source-free domain adaptation (W7076966911); multi-source DA with domain-wise privacy demands (W4402475021); DP clustering (DPM W4405181094, density-based W4400943503)","limitation":"current DP+domain methods assume the domain partition is given (client IDs / site labels); when the partition must be discovered from the private data itself, either the discovery is done non-privately (leaking) or generic DP clustering is run that ignores the downstream per-domain privacy-budget and adaptation consequences of where the boundaries land","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The pipeline DiscoverAdapt runs three stages keyed to one total budget epsilon = epsilon_disc + epsilon_adapt (sequential composition), instantiating the sequential_pipeline thread: stage 1 (discovery) -> stage 2 (budget allocation governs the split between 1 and 3) -> stage 3 (adaptation), where stage 1's output feeds stage 3. GAP 1 (reframe, C21): rather than running a generic DP clustering whose objective is within-cluster compactness, we manufacture the missing domain labels by casting discovery as private supervised relabeling. We define a downstream-utility surrogate U(P) for a candidate partition P into K groups: U(P) = -(1/n) * sum over points x of the cross-entropy of a cheap leave-group-out predictor that is fit per group and evaluated on held-out points of that group, i.e. U(P) rewards partitions on which per-group adaptation generalizes. We select the partition with the exponential mechanism: P is sampled with probability proportional to exp(epsilon_disc * U(P) / (2 * DeltaU)), where DeltaU is the L1 sensitivity of U to one record (bounded by 1/n because U is an average of per-point losses each clipped to [0,1]); the candidate set of partitions is generated by a small number R of private k-means++-style seeds quantized to a fixed grid (R and K are hyperparameters, default R=32, K swept in {2..8} with K chosen by the same mechanism's score). This artifact -- a partition sampled in proportion to realized downstream utility -- closes gap 1 because the selected boundaries are the argmax-in-expectation of the adaptation objective, which generic compactness clustering (node c0) provably cannot target. GAP 2 (heterogeneous_decomposition, C04): we treat the scalar total budget as the heterogeneous resource and partition it by marginal-utility sensitivity. We derive an end-to-end excess-risk bound ExcessRisk <= A/sqrt(or-linear-in epsilon_disc) + B/epsilon_adapt^2 (discovery term decreasing in epsilon_disc via the exponential mechanism's utility gap, adaptation term decreasing in epsilon_adapt via DP-SGD noise on the per-domain levers), where A and B are estimated once on a tiny public-or-synthetic probe set; the optimal split equalizes the two terms' derivatives, giving epsilon_disc* in closed form. This closes gap 2 because the split is derived from each stage's measured utility-sensitivity, not charged as two flat independent costs. GAP 3 (self_supervised_signal_engineering, C07): the discovery stage emits, per point, a posterior r_x in the K-simplex (soft responsibilities) computed from the exponential mechanism's per-point group scores, NOT a hard argmax; its entropy H(r_x) is high exactly where privacy noise made the assignment ambiguous. Stage 3 freezes the backbone and learns only per-domain affine adapters theta_k, training each on every point weighted by r_x[k], with a stabilizer that anchors theta_k toward the global (domain-agnostic) solution proportional to the mean entropy of its assigned points (high discovery uncertainty -> stronger shrinkage toward the shared model). This closes gap 3 because the adaptation is calibrated to the discovery noise: ambiguous points down-weight, uncertain domains shrink, and the load-bearing quantity carried forward is r_x's entropy. The three legs share the single object -- the privately-selected partition P and its per-point posterior r_x -- which gap 1 constructs, gap 2 budgets, and gap 3 consumes.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The three gaps share machinery because they are literally the three consumers of one object across one budget: the partition is constructed (gap1), its construction cost is budgeted against its use (gap2), and its uncertainty is consumed (gap3) -- the evidence is that gap2's bound has one term per stage and gap3's signal is gap1's by-product, so separating them into modules would double-count the partition. (b) Considered alternatives: (i) generic DP-DBSCAN then adapt -- rejected because its compactness objective is decoupled from utility (the c0 regression node) and it emits hard labels with no uncertainty for gap3; (ii) charging epsilon_disc and epsilon_adapt as fixed equal halves -- rejected because it ignores that discovery and adaptation have very different marginal utility-sensitivities, which is exactly gap2; (iii) hard-label argmax assignment -- rejected because it discards the entropy signal gap3 needs.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on a multi-source benchmark with hidden ground-truth domains (e.g. a FEMNIST-style federated split or a multi-site tabular set with site labels withheld at train time), run DiscoverAdapt at a fixed total epsilon in {1,3,8} against (i) DP clustering then DP adaptation with hard labels and a 50/50 budget split, and (ii) a single DP model with no domain structure; measure target-domain accuracy and macro-F1. If the candidate works, target accuracy increases over both baselines at every epsilon and the gap widens as epsilon shrinks (because utility-keyed discovery and uncertainty-aware shrinkage matter most when noise is large). The named load-bearing variable is the per-point discovery-posterior entropy H(r_x): the mechanism claim is that adaptation gain flows through routing-and-shrinkage driven by this entropy. Negative control: replace r_x with a uniform posterior (H(r_x) forced to its maximum for every point, i.e. randomize the responsibilities) while keeping the same epsilon split and adapters -- the DOWNSTREAM task accuracy must fall back to (or below) the no-domain-structure baseline; if accuracy is unchanged under uniform responsibilities, the gain came from the extra adapter capacity, not from the discovered structure. Positive control: a stripped-down variant that keeps ONLY hard utility-keyed routing (entropy collapsed to 0, no shrinkage) should recover most of the gain at large epsilon but lose it at small epsilon, isolating the entropy-shrinkage term as the small-budget contributor.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4402475021","delta":"They allocate a separate DP budget per source assuming the source partition is given and trusted; we construct the partition itself with an exponential mechanism keyed to downstream utility and derive the optimal split of one total budget between discovering and using it, neither of which they produce."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7076966911","delta":"They privatize the source-model transfer in source-free DA while domain identity stays known on both sides; we privatize the discovery of domain identity from the unlabeled mixture and carry its posterior entropy into adaptation, so we apply where their assumed-known partition does not exist."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4405181094","delta":"DPM selects a partition under a generic separation objective and emits hard cluster labels; we select under a downstream-adaptation-utility score function and emit a calibrated per-point posterior whose entropy down-weights privacy-ambiguous points in the adaptation, an output their geometric objective and hard labels cannot provide."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:f1ab1182294964f6ad222e155043c2aeca6be798","delta":"FedMentor scales per-client DP noise to declared sensitivity with domain==client-id; we discover the budget-relevant grouping from data when it is latent or cross-client, allocating epsilon between discovery and use rather than assuming the grouping is declared."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4402475021","what_step_was_missed":"Securing multi-source DA with domain-wise budgets requires, for each source, a budget and an alignment term keyed to that source's identity; to make our contribution already exist they would have needed to construct the source partition as a private deliverable -- specifically an exponential-mechanism selection whose score function is the downstream adaptation-utility surrogate U(P) together with an end-to-end excess-risk decomposition that splits the single budget between selecting P and using it -- a construction their method never builds because it takes the partition as a trusted given."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":207,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"No hard floor fired: gap_closure_reject_check is borderline (not triggered), anti_pattern_check matched audit_decomp_supervisor but mitigation_substantively_delivered=true via the derived budget split + unique-signal + decomposition-fixed/vary-signal control, and recipe_application_check is applied on all three legs. The single load-bearing action item is paper_pointed_threat openalex:W7139144570, whose addressable_via names a specific candidate field (differentiation_from_lit) — a same-name different-problem neighbor that must be distinguished explicitly — so the verdict is revise with one tactical target.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a domain assignment under a formal DP guarantee whose objective is the downstream adaptation/budget outcome rather than a generic clustering objective — i.e. the privately-discovered boundaries are not optimized to be the boundaries where per-domain treatment actually helps.","main_pattern":"reframe_as_solvable_object","sub_pattern":"C21 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers attempting this recast fail when the reframe does not actually unlock a capability the native formulation lacked at a credible scale, e.g. deployed as a descriptive analysis lens with no empirical win, or resting on a brittle exact-algebraic substitution whose guarantees evaporate under approximation.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A reframe used only as an evaluation or analysis lens, without a method that posts a clear win, reads as a descriptive benchmark and falls below the novelty bar even when the framing is reusable.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The reframe ships a runnable DiscoverAdapt pipeline with a falsification_prediction posting a predicted target-accuracy win over two baselines, not an analysis lens."},{"lesson_quoted":"A recast resting on an exact algebraic equivalence (target = exact polynomial of sources) inherits brittle, non-scaling machinery, and its formal guarantees collapse the moment the equivalence is only approximate.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The recast (exponential mechanism over partitions scored by a utility surrogate) makes no exact-algebraic-equivalence claim; the DP guarantee is the exponential mechanism's standard one, robust to surrogate approximation."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating the recast only on toy environments, with an unexplained boundary failure such as performance degrading past a certain context or horizon length, directly undercuts the generalization claim the reframe was meant to establish.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The named benchmarks (FEMNIST-style federated split, multi-site tabular) are standard rather than toy, but the epsilon-grid evaluation should explicitly explain the large-epsilon regime where discovery is easy; surfaced as a Phase 4 concern, not load-bearing."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf analyzes how a single fixed total privacy budget should be split between discovering the domains and using them — discovery cost and adaptation cost are charged separately with no joint accounting of the end-to-end guarantee or of the optimal allocation between the two stages.","main_pattern":"heterogeneous_decomposition","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is treating the partition criterion itself as the contribution while leaving its value unproven, or validating where the bottleneck does not bite, without comparing against both the strongest uniform baseline and the obvious cheap alternative.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Presenting a sensitivity or redundancy proxy as the novelty invites the verdict that it rediscovers known mixed-precision or low-rank results unless it is sharply differentiated from the obvious prior criterion.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The 'proxy' here is the marginal utility-sensitivity of an excess-risk bound's two terms — a privacy-budget split, not a weight/activation precision proxy, so there is no mixed-precision/low-rank rediscovery risk."},{"lesson_quoted":"Omitting comparison against both the strongest uniform baseline and the obvious cheap alternative (SVD/PCA, structured dropout, a natively trained smaller model) leaves reviewers unable to tell whether the partition buys anything at all.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The uniform analogue (a fixed 50/50 budget split, baseline (i)) and the cheap alternative (no-domain single DP model, baseline (ii)) are both in falsification_prediction."},{"lesson_quoted":"Skipping any analysis of why the heterogeneity exists — the data or value distribution that drives the partition — makes the technical novelty and the potential impact impossible to assess.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The heterogeneity (why discovery and adaptation have different marginal utility per unit epsilon) is exactly the error decomposition ExcessRisk <= A/sqrt(eps_disc) + B/eps_adapt^2 the mechanism derives and estimates on a probe."},{"lesson_quoted":"Bolting together established components (distillation plus pruning plus calibration) without an error bound or artifact specific to the new setting reads as incremental even when the target application is timely and important.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The split is backed by a setting-specific end-to-end excess-risk bound, not a bolt-together of off-the-shelf compression steps."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf carries the uncertainty of a privately-estimated domain partition forward into the adaptation step — discovered assignments are consumed as if they were clean given labels, so the adaptation is never calibrated to (or robust against) the discovery noise that DP necessarily injects.","main_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is a manufactured internal signal whose validity silently rests on an assumption that does not survive deployment (calibration, a known-finite shift set, covert target-label use), or recombining well-known components without a single load-bearing mechanistic insight.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A label-free signal whose validity depends on model calibration silently fails on exactly the deep networks known to be poorly calibrated — validate a surrogate where its core assumption is weakest, not where it is convenient.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The soft responsibility r_x is computed from the exponential mechanism's own per-group utility scores, not from the deep network's (possibly miscalibrated) softmax, so its validity does not rest on backbone calibration."},{"lesson_quoted":"A multi-branch or ensemble reweighting mechanism that overlaps with standard multi-task/mixture-of-experts ensembling must explicitly beat both the single-model and the standard-ensemble baselines, or the gain is credited to prior art.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The per-domain adapter mixture resembles a soft mixture-of-experts; the negative control (uniform r_x, same adapter capacity) is exactly the MoE-without-discovered-structure baseline, so the concern is addressed but should be stated as a named baseline in Phase 4."},{"lesson_quoted":"Using target or test-set information during adaptation invites a label-leakage objection that undermines the very source-free, label-free deployment setting the method claims.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Adaptation consumes only the privately-discovered r_x and DP-SGD on releasable adapters; no target labels enter, and the whole pipeline reports an end-to-end (epsilon, delta)."},{"lesson_quoted":"Reusing standard sequential machinery (chaining each step's posterior as the next prior) without a new stabilizer amplifies noise and looks derivative of prior adaptation work.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The stabilizer is new and load-bearing: entropy-scaled shrinkage of theta_k toward the global solution proportional to mean discovery entropy, which is the mechanism's distinctive C07 move."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No entry triggered; two entries are borderline. The reframe (reframe_as_solvable_object) entry is borderline only on the toy-validation lesson, which the standard benchmarks largely defuse, and the C07 entry is borderline on the MoE-overlap lesson, which the candidate's own uniform-responsibility negative control already answers — both are non-load-bearing and surface as Phase 4 reviewer concerns rather than hard fails."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a domain assignment under a formal DP guarantee whose objective is the downstream adaptation/budget outcome rather than a generic clustering objective — i.e. the privately-discovered boundaries are not optimized to be the boundaries where per-domain treatment actually helps.","sub_pattern":"C21 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Recast a problem that natively lacks supervision (here, domain labels) as a supervised/generative-modeling problem by manufacturing the absent supervision from data that already exists, so mature supervised machinery applies directly.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism GAP-1 step manufactures the missing domain labels by casting discovery as private supervised relabeling: a candidate set of partitions is generated and one is SELECTED via an exponential mechanism whose score IS the downstream-utility surrogate U(P) — the absent label is fabricated as 'the partition that maximizes adaptation utility', the C21 manufactured-supervision move rather than a geometric clustering objective.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf analyzes how a single fixed total privacy budget should be split between discovering the domains and using them — discovery cost and adaptation cost are charged separately with no joint accounting of the end-to-end guarantee or of the optimal allocation between the two stages.","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Discriminate the components of an over-provisioned resource by a sensitivity/influence criterion and apply a differentiated treatment, with the load-bearing artifact being an error/sensitivity decomposition that bounds how the differentiated treatment recovers the objective.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism GAP-2 treats the scalar total budget epsilon as the heterogeneous resource, partitions it by marginal utility-sensitivity, and supplies the spine artifact: the excess-risk decomposition ExcessRisk <= A/sqrt(eps_disc) + B/eps_adapt^2 whose two terms have different sensitivities, with the split set where the marginal sensitivities equalize — the C04 sensitivity-decomposition-bounding-differentiated-treatment move.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf carries the uncertainty of a privately-estimated domain partition forward into the adaptation step — discovered assignments are consumed as if they were clean given labels, so the adaptation is never calibrated to (or robust against) the discovery noise that DP necessarily injects.","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"On an already-trained model, treat an internal-state readout as the manufactured signal, minimize on a surgically tiny lever with the backbone frozen, and bolt on an explicit stabilizer against collapse: diagnose-localize, minimize-on-a-tiny-lever, stabilize-against-collapse.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism GAP-3 uses the per-point posterior entropy H(r_x) as the internal readout, trains only per-domain affine adapters theta_k (the tiny lever) on a frozen backbone, and adds the entropy-scaled shrinkage stabilizer (lambda*meanEntropy_k*||theta_k - theta_global||^2) — the three C07 verbs present.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"All three entries instantiate their cluster's signature move: C21's manufactured-supervision via utility-keyed exponential-mechanism selection, C04's sensitivity-decomposition-bounded budget split, and C07's frozen-backbone tiny-lever-plus-stabilizer consumption of the entropy readout."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["reframe_as_solvable_object","heterogeneous_decomposition","self_supervised_signal_engineering"],"matched_pattern_id":"audit_decomp_supervisor","required_mitigation_quoted":"The decomposition criterion must be derivable from observed structure or task-level supervision (not just intuition), AND the manufactured signal must be the unique signal the decomposition implies. An ablation that holds the decomposition fixed and varies the signal (or vice versa) must show the two are not conflated.","mitigation_substantively_delivered":"true","reasoning":"The decomposition criterion (the budget split) is derived from a measured excess-risk error decomposition, not intuition; the manufactured signal (per-point posterior r_x) is the unique by-product of the exponential mechanism's own per-group scores rather than an independently invented label; and the falsification_prediction's negative control (uniform r_x with budget split and adapters held fixed) plus positive control (hard routing, entropy collapsed) is exactly the decomposition-fixed-vary-signal ablation the mitigation demands, so the two un-derived choices are not conflated."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"openalex:W7139144570","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"'Missing Mass for Differentially Private Domain Discovery' (2026-03) shares the exact phrase 'differentially private domain discovery' and so is the most specific naming collision, but it solves a different problem: each user holds a subset of items from a shared but unknown ITEM-universe and the goal is to output an informative SUBSET OF ITEMS (set union, private top-k, k-hitting-set) under a missing-mass utility guarantee. It discovers the support of an item vocabulary, not a partition of users/records into distributional domains, has no downstream adaptation step, performs no budget split between discovery and use, and emits a set rather than a per-point posterior — so the candidate's claim stands provided the terminology distinction (item-universe discovery vs distributional-domain discovery for adaptation) is drawn explicitly, otherwise a reviewer skimming the title would assume subsumption.","addressable_via":"Add a differentiation_from_lit entry against openalex:W7139144570 that names the item-universe-vs-distributional-domain distinction and the absence of any adaptation/budget-split stage in their work."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat openalex:W7139144570 ('Missing Mass for Differentially Private Domain Discovery') is an exact-name collision that a reviewer could read as subsumption.","fix_direction":"Append one differentiation_from_lit entry with paper_id openalex:W7139144570 and a delta stating: they privately discover the SUPPORT of an unknown item-universe and output an informative subset (set union / top-k / k-hitting-set) under a missing-mass guarantee, with no record partition, no downstream adaptation, and no discovery-vs-use budget split; we discover a partition of records into distributional domains keyed to an adaptation-utility surrogate, allocate one total budget between discovery and adaptation, and emit a per-point posterior consumed by the adaptation — a distributional-domain-for-adaptation problem distinct from their item-universe-support problem."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Appended a fifth differentiation_from_lit entry against openalex:W7139144570 ('Missing Mass for Differentially Private Domain Discovery') drawing the item-universe-support vs distributional-domain-for-adaptation distinction and noting their absence of any adaptation or discovery-vs-use budget-split stage."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Discovering the Domains You Will Adapt To, Under One Privacy Budget\n\n**Method.** DiscoverAdapt\n\n## Motivation\nSuppose you hold sensitive data — say records from many hospitals, or logs from many devices — and the data secretly contains several different sub-populations (call them domains). You can often get much better accuracy if you give each domain its own privacy budget or its own little adapted model, instead of forcing everything through one generic differentially-private (DP, meaning a formal mathematical privacy guarantee) model. But there is a catch: to do that, you need to know which records belong to which domain. Every existing privacy-preserving method just assumes someone hands you that grouping for free — multi-source domain adaptation with per-source budgets (W4402475021) trusts the source labels it is given, and DP source-free domain adaptation (W7076966911) protects the model transfer but still assumes the domain of each example is known. In real data the grouping is hidden, and once it is hidden you hit two problems nobody has solved together. First, the only private tool for finding groups is generic DP clustering (W4405181094), which groups points purely by how tightly they cluster geometrically — a goal that has nothing to do with whether splitting there actually helps your downstream task — and it hands you hard group labels with no sense of how confident it is. Second, the privacy cost of finding the groups is billed separately from the cost of using them, and nobody has worked out how to divide one fixed privacy budget between finding and using. What makes this solvable now is that the two halves — private grouping (DPM, 2024-12; density-based DP clustering, 2024-07) and private adaptation (2024-2025) — have only just become reliable, but each was built assuming the other's input falls from the sky, so no one has joined them under a single budget aimed at the actual adaptation goal. Closing this gap means per-domain privacy budgeting and per-domain adaptation finally work when the grouping is hidden, not just when it is declared, and it turns generic DP clustering from the default tool into merely a baseline you compare against.\n\n## Method\n### Background scaffolding\n*Standard non-private candidate generation and frozen-backbone setup that the contribution sits on.*\n\n1. Turn each record into a fixed feature vector by passing it through the frozen main model and taking the second-to-last layer's output, scaled to unit length. Run ordinary (non-private) k-means++ 32 times on these vectors, separately for every number of groups K from 2 to 8, and snap each run's cluster centers to a fixed grid (grid spacing = one tenth of each dimension's spread) so nearly identical runs merge. Each run gives one candidate grouping. Nothing here costs privacy budget, because you only pay when you finally pick one grouping.\n   - _Why_: You only need to pay for privacy when you finally pick one grouping, so making a shortlist of candidates first is free.\n2. Keep the main model fixed and add one small per-group adjustment $\\theta _{k}$ that acts on the model's second-to-last-layer feature just before the shared output head. Each adjustment is a simple scale-and-shift (multiply each feature by a learned number and add a learned offset), or a small low-rank tweak. Start every group's adjustment from the single global adjustment fit on all data (so initially it just reproduces the original model). Because each per-group adjustment has very few parameters, the later private training stays stable.\n   - _Why_: Adapting only a tiny per-domain piece keeps the private update small and well-behaved.\n\n### Utility-keyed private discovery\n*Discover the partition by privately selecting the grouping that maximizes a downstream-adaptation-utility score, not geometric compactness.*\n\n3. Give each candidate grouping a score for how well per-group prediction generalizes. Within each group, train a simple regularized linear predictor (logistic regression for classification, ridge regression for continuous targets) on 80% of the group's points and test it on the held-out 20%, rotating through 5 folds so every point gets tested once. For each held-out point record its cross-entropy (prediction error), capped to lie between 0 and 1, and average all these capped errors into the grouping's score U(P). Capping at 1 matters because it limits how much any single record can swing the score, which the private selection in the next step depends on.\n\n*U(P) scores a candidate partition P by the average held-out cross-entropy of a per-group leave-group-out predictor, clipped to [0,1]; higher U means per-group adaptation generalizes better on P.*\n$$ U(P) = -\\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{x} \\mathrm{CE}\\big(\\hat{y}_{g(x)}^{-}(x),\\, y_x\\big), \\qquad \\mathrm{CE} \\in [0,1] \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This measures whether splitting the data this way actually helps the downstream task, instead of just whether the groups look geometrically tidy.\n4. Privately pick one grouping. Put all candidate groupings from every group-count K into a single pool and use the exponential mechanism (a standard differential-privacy tool that picks higher-scoring options more often) to draw one grouping P*, with the chance of each grouping proportional to $exp(\\epsilon _{disc}\\cdot U(P)/(2\\cdot \\Delta U))$ where the sensitivity $\\Delta U =$ 1/n. The chosen grouping already comes with its own number of groups, so you do not pay separately to choose K. A simple way to run the draw: add a specific random Gumbel noise to each grouping's score and take the highest — that is mathematically the same as the exponential mechanism. This single draw is what spends the discovery budget $\\epsilon _{disc}.$\n\n*The exponential mechanism samples partition P* with probability proportional to $exp(\\epsilon _{disc} \\cdot $ U(P) $/ (2\\cdot \\Delta U)),$ where $\\Delta U =$ 1/n is the L1 sensitivity of U to one record; this spends $\\epsilon _{disc}$ and selects the partition in proportion to realized downstream utility.*\n$$ \\Pr[P^\\star = P] \\;\\propto\\; \\exp\\!\\Big(\\frac{\\varepsilon_{\\mathrm{disc}}\\, U(P)}{2\\,\\Delta U}\\Big), \\qquad \\Delta U = \\tfrac{1}{n} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The exponential mechanism is a standard DP tool that picks higher-scoring options more often, so groupings that help adaptation get chosen more often while staying private.\n5. Turn the chosen grouping into a soft, confidence-bearing assignment for each point. For point x, ask every group's small predictor (from the scoring step) how well it explains x's label, getting one number per group; pass these K numbers through a softmax (temperature 1) to get a probability vector $r_{x}$ over the groups. Its entropy $H(r_{x})$ — how spread-out the probabilities are — is high wherever several groups explain x about equally well, which is exactly where the private selection was unsure. This reuses predictors you already built, so it costs no extra privacy budget.\n   - _Why_: A soft, confidence-bearing assignment keeps the information about which points are uncertain, which a hard label would throw away.\n\n### End-to-end budget split\n*Split one total privacy budget between discovery and adaptation where their marginal error-sensitivities equalize.*\n\n6. Estimate two constants that describe how each stage's error shrinks as it gets more budget, using a small stand-in dataset (synthetic or public) with the same number of features and classes as your real data. For discovery, try several budget levels (for example 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2, 4), measure the resulting error at each, and fit the constant A to the curve error = A divided by the square root of the discovery budget. Separately, do the same for adaptation to fit the constant B to error = B divided by the adaptation budget squared. You only keep the two numbers A and B, and since they come from the stand-in data they cost no privacy budget on the real data.\n   - _Why_: You need rough numbers for how sensitive each stage is to its budget before you can divide the budget well.\n7. Work out how to split the fixed total budget between discovery and adaptation. Using the two constants A and B and the total budget $\\epsilon ,$ find the discovery budget that minimizes the total predicted error $A/\\surd (discovery$ budget) + B/(adaptation $budget)^{2},$ where adaptation budget $= \\epsilon $ minus discovery budget. Because this total-error curve has a single lowest point, you can find it reliably by a simple numerical search (bisection) over possible splits. The result gives the discovery budget $\\epsilon _{disc}*$ and the leftover adaptation budget $\\epsilon _{adapt}*.$ This calculation uses only the two numbers and the total budget, so it touches no private data.\n\n*The end-to-end excess risk is bounded by a discovery term decreasing in $\\epsilon _{disc}$ plus an adaptation term decreasing in $\\epsilon _{adapt}$; the optimal split equalizes the two terms' derivatives, giving $\\epsilon _{disc}*$ in closed form for fixed total $\\epsilon .$*\n$$ \\mathrm{ExcessRisk} \\;\\le\\; \\frac{A}{\\sqrt{\\varepsilon_{\\mathrm{disc}}}} + \\frac{B}{\\varepsilon_{\\mathrm{adapt}}^{2}}, \\qquad \\varepsilon = \\varepsilon_{\\mathrm{disc}} + \\varepsilon_{\\mathrm{adapt}} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Spending each unit of budget where it reduces error the most is exactly the split where the two terms' marginal effects match.\n8. If the best split you computed differs noticeably from the rough half-and-half you started with, redo the private grouping at the better split. Concretely: first run the discovery (the private pick and the soft assignment) at a provisional half of the total budget; then, if the computed best discovery budget differs from that half by more than 10% of the total, run the private pick again at the better budget. If you do redo it, the two private picks add up under the standard composition rule, so count both toward the discovery cost and reduce the adaptation budget to keep the overall privacy guarantee exactly the same. 【author decision: whether to pay for two discovery picks that add up (simpler, but the adaptation budget shrinks) or to spend the whole discovery budget on a single pick at the better split and throw away the first pick — the trade-off is simplicity versus making the most of the budget】\n   - _Why_: The grouping that feeds adaptation should be the one chosen at the right budget, and you must pay honestly for redoing it.\n\n### Uncertainty-aware adaptation\n*Consume the discovery posterior's entropy via responsibility weighting and entropy-scaled shrinkage so the adaptation is calibrated to discovery noise.*\n\n9. Train every per-group adjustment privately with DP-SGD (differentially-private stochastic gradient descent: clip each example's gradient to length 1 and add calibrated Gaussian noise), using the adaptation budget. Each point contributes to group k's training in proportion to its soft membership $r_{x}[k],$ and a shrinkage term pulls each group's adjustment back toward the shared one, more strongly for groups the discovery was unsure about — measured by that group's average assignment uncertainty, scaled to lie between 0 (confident) and 1 (maximally unsure). So uncertain groups lean on the shared model and confident groups specialize. 【author decision: the strength of this shrinkage trades sharper per-group specialization against robustness to noisy discovery — pick it by a small search over values like 0.01, 0.1, 1 on the stand-in data, or tie it to the ratio of the two error constants; the trade-off is hand-tuning versus a principled link to the error bound】\n\n*Each per-domain adapter $\\theta _{k}$ is trained with DP-SGD on every point weighted by its responsibility $r_{x}[k],$ plus an entropy-scaled shrinkage term that pulls $\\theta _{k}$ toward the global solution in proportion to the mean discovery entropy $\\bar{H}_{k}$ of its assigned points.*\n$$ \\min_{\\theta_k}\\; \\sum_{x} r_x[k]\\, \\ell\\big(x;\\, \\phi + \\theta_k\\big) \\;+\\; \\lambda\\, \\bar{H}_k\\, \\lVert \\theta_k - \\theta_{\\mathrm{global}} \\rVert^2 \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Points the discovery was unsure about contribute less, and domains it was unsure about lean on the shared model, so you never trust a noisy guess as if it were a clean label.\n10. To serve a new point, first decide its soft group membership $r_{x}$ using a small public router — a simple classifier over the backbone feature, trained ahead of time to reproduce the soft memberships from the privately-released group predictors and stand-in inputs, so it never touches private data at serving time. Then predict by blending the per-group adjusted outputs weighted by $r_{x}.$ Finally report the overall privacy guarantee $(\\epsilon , \\delta )$ by adding up the privacy spent on the discovery pick(s) and on the private adaptation training, with the $\\delta $ part summed across the mechanisms.\n   - _Why_: Routing softly by the same posterior keeps the whole pipeline consistent and gives one honest total privacy guarantee.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 在单一隐私预算下发现你将要适应的领域\n\n**方法名称.** DiscoverAdapt\n\n## 研究动机\n假设你手里有敏感数据——比如来自很多家医院的病历，或者来自很多台设备的日志——而这些数据里其实暗含好几个不同的子群体（我们称之为 domain，领域）。如果你能给每个领域分配各自的隐私预算，或者给每个领域一个专门微调过的小模型，而不是把所有数据塞进同一个通用的差分隐私（DP，即一种带正式数学保证的隐私机制）模型里，往往能得到高得多的准确率。但有个前提：你得知道哪些记录属于哪个领域。现有的隐私保护方法都默认有人免费把这个分组交给你——带逐源预算的多源领域适应（W4402475021）信任它拿到的源标签，DP source-free 领域适应（W7076966911）保护模型传输却仍假设每个样本的领域已知。真实数据里这个分组是隐藏的，而一旦隐藏，就会遇到两个至今没人一起解决的问题。其一，唯一的隐私化分组工具是通用 DP 聚类（W4405181094），它只按几何上聚得有多紧来分组——这个目标和“在这里切分到底对你的下游任务有没有帮助”毫无关系——而且它只给你硬分组标签，不告诉你它有多大把握。其二，发现分组的隐私开销和使用分组的开销被分开计费，没人算过如何把一份固定的总隐私预算在“发现”和“使用”之间划分。现在之所以能解决，是因为这两半——私有分组（DPM，2024-12；density-based DP 聚类，2024-07）和私有适应（2024-2025）——刚刚才变得可靠，但各自都假设对方的输入是天上掉下来的，所以还没人在单一预算下、瞄准真正的适应目标把它们接起来。补上这个缺口意味着：逐领域的隐私预算分配和逐领域适应在分组隐藏时（而不仅是在分组被声明时）终于能用，并且把通用 DP 聚类从默认工具变成你拿来对比的基线。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景脚手架\n*贡献所依赖的标准非隐私候选生成与冻结主干设置。*\n\n1. 先把每条记录过一遍冻结的主干模型，取倒数第二层的输出并归一化到单位长度，作为该记录的固定特征向量。在这些向量上跑普通（非隐私）的 k-means++ 共 32 次，并对每个分组数 K（从 2 到 8）分别做一遍；把每次的聚类中心对齐到一个固定网格（网格间距 = 每个维度标准差的十分之一），让几乎相同的结果合并。每次跑出一个候选分组。这一步不消耗任何隐私预算，因为只有最终选定一个分组时才需要付费。\n   - _为什么_: 只有最终选定一个分组时才需要为隐私付费，所以先列一份候选短名单是免费的。\n2. 保持主干模型固定，为每个组添加一个小的逐组调整 $\\theta _{k}$，它作用在模型倒数第二层的特征上、紧挨着共享输出头之前。每个调整就是一个简单的缩放加平移（把每个特征乘以一个学到的数再加一个学到的偏置），或一个小的低秩微调。每个组的调整都从用全部数据拟合的单一全局调整出发（所以一开始它只是复现原始模型）。由于每个逐组调整的参数很少，后面的私有训练会保持稳定。\n   - _为什么_: 只适配一小块逐领域参数，能让私有更新保持小而稳定。\n\n### 效用导向的私有发现\n*通过私有地选出能最大化下游适应效用得分（而非几何紧致度）的分组来发现划分。*\n\n3. 给每个候选分组打一个“分组预测能否泛化”的分数。在每个组内，用 80% 的点训练一个简单的正则化线性预测器（分类用 logistic regression，连续目标用 ridge regression），在留出的 20% 上测试，并轮换 5 折让每个点都被测一次。对每个留出点记录它的交叉熵（预测误差），裁剪到 0 与 1 之间，再把所有这些裁剪后的误差求平均得到该分组的分数 U(P)。裁剪到 1 很关键，因为它限制了单条记录能把分数拉动多少，而下一步的私有选择正依赖于此。\n\n*U(P) 用每组留组外预测器在留出点上的平均交叉熵（裁剪到 [0,1]）来给候选划分 P 打分；U 越大表示在 P 上做分组适应的泛化越好。*\n$$ U(P) = -\\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{x} \\mathrm{CE}\\big(\\hat{y}_{g(x)}^{-}(x),\\, y_x\\big), \\qquad \\mathrm{CE} \\in [0,1] \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这衡量的是按这种方式切分数据到底对下游任务有没有帮助，而不仅仅是分组在几何上看起来整不整齐。\n4. 私有地选出一个分组。把所有分组数 K 下的候选分组放进同一个池子，用指数机制（一种标准的差分隐私工具，会更频繁地选中得分更高的选项）抽取一个分组 P*，每个分组被选中的概率正比于 $exp(\\epsilon _{disc}\\cdot U(P)/(2\\cdot \\Delta U))$，其中敏感度 $\\Delta U =$ 1/n。选中的分组本身就带着它的分组数，所以不需要额外付费来选 K。一个简单的实现：给每个分组的分数加上特定的 Gumbel 随机噪声再取最大值——这在数学上等同于指数机制。这一次抽取就消耗了发现预算 $\\epsilon _{disc}$。\n\n*指数机制以正比于 $exp(\\epsilon _{disc} \\cdot $ U(P) $/ (2\\cdot \\Delta U))$ 的概率抽取划分 P*，其中 $\\Delta U =$ 1/n 是 U 对单条记录的 L1 敏感度；该步消耗 $\\epsilon _{disc}$，并按实际下游效用的大小成比例地选出划分。*\n$$ \\Pr[P^\\star = P] \\;\\propto\\; \\exp\\!\\Big(\\frac{\\varepsilon_{\\mathrm{disc}}\\, U(P)}{2\\,\\Delta U}\\Big), \\qquad \\Delta U = \\tfrac{1}{n} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 指数机制是标准的 DP 工具，会更频繁地选中得分更高的选项，所以对适应有帮助的分组会被更常选中，同时保持隐私。\n5. 把选定的分组转成每个点带置信度的软归属。对点 x，问每个组的小预测器（来自打分步骤）对 x 的标签解释得有多好，得到每组一个数；把这 K 个数过一个 softmax（温度为 1）得到组上的概率向量 $r_{x}$。它的熵 $H(r_{x})——$概率分布有多分散——在好几个组对 x 解释得差不多好的地方会很高，而那正是私有选择不确定的地方。这一步复用了你已经建好的预测器，所以不消耗额外的隐私预算。\n   - _为什么_: 带置信度的软归属保留了“哪些点不确定”的信息，而硬标签会把这部分信息丢掉。\n\n### 端到端预算划分\n*在发现与适应的边际误差敏感度相等处，把一份总隐私预算分配给两者。*\n\n6. 用一个小的替身数据集（合成或公开，特征数和类别数与真实数据相同）来估计两个常数，它们刻画了每个阶段的误差如何随预算增大而下降。对发现阶段，尝试几个预算水平（例如 0.25、0.5、1、2、4），在每个水平测量误差，把常数 A 拟合到曲线“误差 = A 除以发现预算的平方根”。再单独对适应阶段做同样的事，把常数 B 拟合到“误差 = B 除以适应预算的平方”。你只保留 A 和 B 两个数，由于它们来自替身数据，对真实数据不消耗隐私预算。\n   - _为什么_: 在合理划分预算之前，你需要先大致知道每个阶段对其预算有多敏感。\n7. 算出如何把固定的总预算在发现与适应之间划分。用两个常数 A、B 和总预算 $\\epsilon $，找到使总预测误差 $A/\\surd ($发现预算) + B/(适应预算$)^{2}$ 最小的发现预算，其中适应预算 $= \\epsilon $ 减去发现预算。由于这条总误差曲线只有一个最低点，你可以用简单的数值搜索（二分法）在各种划分上可靠地找到它。结果给出发现预算 $\\epsilon _{disc}*$ 和剩下的适应预算 $\\epsilon _{adapt}*$。这一计算只用到两个数和总预算，不触碰任何私有数据。\n\n*端到端的超额风险被一个随 $\\epsilon _{disc}$ 递减的发现项与一个随 $\\epsilon _{adapt}$ 递减的适应项之和所界定；最优划分使两项导数相等，从而在总预算 $\\epsilon $ 固定时给出闭式的 $\\epsilon _{disc}*$。*\n$$ \\mathrm{ExcessRisk} \\;\\le\\; \\frac{A}{\\sqrt{\\varepsilon_{\\mathrm{disc}}}} + \\frac{B}{\\varepsilon_{\\mathrm{adapt}}^{2}}, \\qquad \\varepsilon = \\varepsilon_{\\mathrm{disc}} + \\varepsilon_{\\mathrm{adapt}} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 把每一单位预算花在最能降低误差的地方，恰好就是两项边际效应相等的那个划分点。\n8. 如果你算出的最优划分与一开始用的大致对半分有明显差异，就在更优的划分下重做私有分组。具体来说：先在总预算的临时一半上跑发现（私有选择加软归属）；然后，如果算出的最优发现预算与这一半的差超过总预算的 10%，就在更优的预算上再做一次私有选择。如果确实重做，两次私有选择按标准的组合规则相加，所以两次都计入发现开销，并相应减少适应预算，使整体隐私保证完全不变。【作者需决定：是按相加的方式为两次发现选择付费（更简单，但适应预算会缩水），还是把全部发现预算花在更优划分下的单次选择上、丢弃第一次选择——权衡在于简单性与预算利用率】\n   - _为什么_: 喂给适应的分组应当是在正确预算下选出的那个，而且重做的开销必须如实付费。\n\n### 面向不确定性的适应\n*通过责任度加权与按熵缩放的收缩消费发现后验的熵，使适应对发现噪声进行校准。*\n\n9. 用 DP-SGD（differentially-private stochastic gradient descent，差分隐私随机梯度下降：把每个样本的梯度裁剪到长度 1 并加入标定过的高斯噪声）在适应预算下私有地训练每个逐组调整。每个点按其软归属 $r_{x}[k]$ 的比例参与组 k 的训练，同时有一个收缩项把每个组的调整拉回共享调整，对发现阶段越不确定的组拉得越强——用该组的平均归属不确定度衡量，并缩放到 0（确定）与 1（最不确定）之间。于是不确定的组依赖共享模型，确定的组则专门化。【作者需决定：这个收缩的强度在更尖锐的逐组专门化与对含噪发现的鲁棒性之间权衡——可在替身数据上对 0.01、0.1、1 等取值做小范围搜索来选定，或把它与两个误差常数的比值挂钩；权衡在于手工调参与对误差界的有原则的联系】\n\n*每个领域适配器 $\\theta _{k}$ 用 DP-SGD 训练，每个点按其责任度 $r_{x}[k]$ 加权，并加上一个按熵缩放的收缩项：以其所属点的平均发现熵 $\\bar{H}_{k}$ 为比例，把 $\\theta _{k}$ 拉向全局解 $\\theta _{global}$。*\n$$ \\min_{\\theta_k}\\; \\sum_{x} r_x[k]\\, \\ell\\big(x;\\, \\phi + \\theta_k\\big) \\;+\\; \\lambda\\, \\bar{H}_k\\, \\lVert \\theta_k - \\theta_{\\mathrm{global}} \\rVert^2 \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 发现阶段不确定的点贡献更小，不确定的领域更依赖共享模型，这样就绝不会把一个含噪的猜测当成干净标签来信任。\n10. 为一个新点提供服务时，先用一个小的公开路由器决定它的软组归属 $r_{x}——$一个建立在主干特征上的简单分类器，事先训练好以复现来自私有发布的分组预测器和替身输入的软归属，因此在服务时绝不接触私有数据。然后按 $r_{x}$ 加权混合各逐组调整后的输出来做预测。最后通过把发现选择与私有适应训练所花的隐私相加来报告整体隐私保证 $(\\epsilon , \\delta )$，其中 $\\delta $ 部分跨各机制求和。\n   - _为什么_: 用同一个后验做软路由能让整条流水线保持一致，并给出一个如实的总隐私保证。\n\n"},{"id":"27","run_dir":"run_prompt27_contrastive","index":27,"title":"When Hard Becomes Harmful: A Sign-Flip Threshold for Difficulty in Unsupervised Contrastive Learning","title_zh":"当困难变得有害：无监督对比学习中难度的符号翻转阈值","method_name":"Difficulty Sign-Flip Gating (DSG)","hook":"We prove that in label-free InfoNCE the marginal effect of an example on the learned representation is non-monotone in its embedding-space difficulty: past an analytically pinned per-example threshold, a harder negative's gradient subtracts from alignment instead of sharpening it, so the standard practice of monotonically up-weighting difficulty is provably self-defeating beyond that point. The threshold splits every example's contribution into an informative part and a corrupting part using one label-free quantity, replacing the field's single global temperature trade-off with a per-example decision.","anchor_pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","anchor_pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","domain_category":"Learning Theory & Statistics","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes the difficulty threshold itself: the point along an example's embedding-space hardness at which its marginal contribution to the unsupervised contrastive objective flips sign from improving to degrading the downstream representation, nor what data/encoder quantities govern where that threshold sits.","pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by formalizing the difficulty-monotone InfoNCE update as the iterative-local procedure whose discarded structural object is the SIGN of an example's projected alignment gradient, stating a tight separation criterion (the per-example difficulty value tau_i* at which the marginal-contribution functional crosses zero), proving the monotone-weighting class provably cannot represent examples on opposite sides of tau_i*, and re-injecting the sign into the update via a difficulty-gated weight that is proven to strictly exceed the monotone class on the alignment objective at bounded (one extra similarity read per pair) cost.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions the inherited assumption that an example's INFORMATIVENESS to the unsupervised contrastive loss should be a monotone increasing function of its embedding-space difficulty — every frontier method (hardness reweighting, temperature tuning, mining) builds on the loss whose per-sample gradient magnitude rises with difficulty, and none tests whether coupling gradient weight to difficulty is necessary rather than assumed.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C19 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by locating, inside the standard alignment-improvement certificate for hardness-reweighted InfoNCE, the convenience condition that gradient informativeness is non-decreasing in difficulty (imported so the bound's leading term is monotone in the weight), tracing that this condition is only buying a one-sided control on the expected corrupting-pair mass, and substituting the strictly weaker sufficient property that the corrupting-pair mass stay below the per-example threshold tau_i* — then re-deriving the certificate so it is non-vacuous in the high-difficulty regime the monotone assumption excluded.","is_anchor":false},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a per-example quantity, computable without labels at a given training point, that separates an example whose difficulty is informative (a true hard negative/positive that sharpens the representation) from an example whose difficulty is corrupting (a false negative / mis-augmented positive whose large gradient pushes apart points that should align) — the frontier can only trade the two off globally via temperature or importance weight.","pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by characterizing the empirical distribution of the per-example marginal-contribution functional, showing examples split into a high-impact informative minority and a near-redundant-or-corrupting bulk, partitioning by the label-free sign-and-magnitude criterion derived from tau_i* (an influence-style discriminator, not raw similarity), assigning the informative partition full gradient weight and the corrupting partition a residual-corrected down-weight, and supplying the error decomposition that bounds how this differentiated treatment recovers the clean-data alignment objective better than any uniform temperature.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"unsupervised/self-supervised contrastive representation learning (theory of optimization difficulty induced by hard examples)","n_papers":27,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":23},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":14,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Multi-Faceted Negative Sample Mining for Grpah Contrastive Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"MCLHN: Toward Automatic Modulation Classification via Masked Contrastive Learning With Hard Negatives"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Seeking False Hard Negatives for Graph Contrastive Learning"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Exploring treatment options in cancer: tumor treatment strategies"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Deep Learning for Time Series Anomaly Detection: A Survey"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Beware of metacognitive laziness: Effects of generative artificial intelligence on learning motivation, processes, and performance"}],"more":8},{"year":2025,"n":22,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"DoGCLR: Dominance-Game Contrastive Learning Network for Skeleton-Based Action Recognition"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Alignment, Mining and Fusion: Representation Alignment with Hard Negative Mining and Selective Knowledge Fusion for Medical Visual Question Answering"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Understanding Hardness of Vision-Language Compositionality from A Token-level Causal Lens"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A Hard Negatives Mining and Enhancing Method for Multi-Modal Contrastive Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Khan-GCL: Kolmogorov-Arnold Network Based Graph Contrastive Learning with Hard Negatives"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Enhancing Contrastive Learning for Geolocalization by Discovering Hard Negatives on Semivariograms"}],"more":16}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":14,"share":0.519},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":10,"share":0.37},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":4,"share":0.148},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":4,"share":0.148},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":4,"share":0.148},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":3,"share":0.111},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":3,"share":0.111},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":3,"share":0.111}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Across the retrieved unsupervised/self-supervised contrastive-learning frontier, the dominant operational stance is that harder negatives are more informative and should be up-weighted, with difficulty controlled only by a scalar temperature or an importance weight (semanticscholar:85bdaec73fababa1870eefc59cf31fa8718416b3; openalex:W4402352439); yet a parallel cluster of recent work repeatedly observes that the SAME difficulty knob, pushed past an unstated point, induces overfitting, false-negative contamination, and representation collapse rather than improvement (openalex:W4406070218; semanticscholar:143cdbb38dd5a4870bb98b5a584e0593adde285e; semanticscholar:e738c0fb6b175e8ac0557aaceb041f3e6f13803e). The structural failure is that, in the unsupervised regime where no label distinguishes a genuinely-different instance from a same-latent-class instance, the InfoNCE gradient contribution of a sample grows monotonically with its embedding-space difficulty, so the examples that contribute the LARGEST gradient magnitude are exactly those most likely to be semantically mislabeled negatives (or mis-augmented positives) — the loss cannot tell an informative hard negative from a corrupting false one, and the existing temperature/weight machinery can only trade the two off globally, never separate them, so beyond a difficulty threshold the optimization is dominated by gradients that push apart points that should be together. No retrieved paper produces the quantity that would say, for a given example at a given training point, whether its difficulty is the informative kind or the corrupting kind.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4402352439","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Supervised Contrastive Learning with Hard Negative Samples analyzes hard-negative reweighting of the InfoNCE loss and shows, with label information available, how to up-weight hard negatives while excluding same-class ones. Its guarantees lean on the supervised label to decide which hard negatives are safe, so it does NOT characterize the unsupervised regime where the harm comes precisely from being unable to distinguish a true hard negative from a same-latent-class false negative — it removes the corrupting examples by assumption rather than explaining the difficulty-vs-harm tradeoff that arises when they cannot be removed. [residue is abstract-level: anchor fulltext unfetchable]"},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416045807","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Generalization Analysis for Supervised Contrastive Representation Learning under Non-IID Settings derives generalization bounds for CRL when tuples reuse a fixed labeled pool, relaxing the IID-tuple assumption. The bounds are uniform over the sample and supervised, so they say nothing about per-example difficulty: they bound average generalization but do not predict that a SUBSET of high-difficulty examples can drive the bound (and the empirical representation) in the wrong direction, nor do they apply to the label-free unsupervised loss."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:143cdbb38dd5a4870bb98b5a584e0593adde285e","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Seeking False Hard Negatives for Graph Contrastive Learning identifies that false hard negatives (same-class, high-similarity) corrupt representations and proposes a heuristic to detect them in GCL via message-passing structure. The detection is graph-structure-specific and heuristic, with no general quantity that scores, for an arbitrary example in any modality, the probability that its high gradient magnitude reflects corruption rather than information — so it patches the symptom in one domain without a transferable diagnostic of when difficulty turns harmful."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4406070218","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"From Overfitting to Robustness studies quantity/quality/variety of negative selection in graph CL and empirically shows hard negatives cause overfitting past a point. It establishes the phenomenon empirically but offers only a selection heuristic, leaving open any analytic characterization of the difficulty threshold at which the marginal hard negative flips from informative to harmful, and what controls that threshold."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"unsupervised/self-supervised contrastive representation learning (theory of optimization difficulty induced by hard examples)","venue":"ICLR/ICML/NeurIPS","time":"2026","data":["standard SSL image benchmarks (e.g. CIFAR-10/100, STL-10, ImageNet-100/ImageNet-1k subsets)","controlled synthetic mixtures where the latent class/augmentation overlap is known"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"learning theory + representation learning","preference":"theory","baseline":"InfoNCE with uniform negative sampling; hardness-reweighted InfoNCE (hard negative mining); debiased contrastive learning","limitation":"current hard-negative theory treats harder negatives as monotonically beneficial up to a tunable temperature/weight, and has no principled account of WHEN and WHY a difficult example (hard negative or hard positive) actively degrades the learned unsupervised representation rather than helping it","contribution_type":"theory","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","baseline","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object every leg reads from and writes to is the per-example marginal-contribution functional g_i = <∂L_InfoNCE/∂θ evaluated at example i, u_align>, the projection of example i's InfoNCE gradient onto the alignment direction u_align (the unit vector from an anchor's embedding toward its positive's embedding, a model-internal readout taken per anchor at the current parameters θ); g_i is computable from a single forward+backward pass per pair with no labels. ANCHOR LEG (C10): treat hardness-reweighted InfoNCE as the iterative-local procedure and the SIGN of g_i as the structural object the monotone-weighting class discards (it only ever uses |gradient|, scaled up with difficulty d_i = similarity(anchor, negative)/temperature). We prove a tight separation criterion: for each example there is a difficulty value tau_i* = log((1-p_i)/p_i) + c(θ) — where p_i is the example's false-pair probability (the chance the 'negative' shares the anchor's latent class) read off the augmentation-graph local density, and c(θ) is the current alignment-uniformity gap, a scalar computed from the batch — such that g_i > 0 (informative: pushing helps downstream alignment) for d_i < tau_i* and g_i < 0 (corrupting: pushing degrades it) for d_i > tau_i*; the monotone class assigns a single increasing weight to d_i and therefore provably cannot give opposite-sign treatment to two examples straddling tau_i*, which is the conflated pair that exhibits the blindspot. We then re-inject the sign by constructing the gated weight w_i = m(d_i)·1[d_i < tau_i*] + r_i·1[d_i >= tau_i*], where m is any standard hardness weight and r_i is a small residual-correction weight (below), and prove this augmented operator strictly raises the clean-data alignment objective above the best monotone weighting, at the bounded cost of one extra similarity read (p_i) per pair. AUDIT LEG (C19): inside the existing alignment-improvement certificate for hardness reweighting, the leading term is monotone in the weight ONLY under the imported convenience condition that informativeness is non-decreasing in d_i; we trace that this condition is consumed solely to one-side-bound the expected corrupting-pair mass E[p_i·d_i], and we replace it with the strictly weaker sufficient property E[p_i·d_i·1[d_i>=tau_i*]] <= delta that our gating provably satisfies by construction, re-deriving the certificate so it stays non-vacuous exactly in the high-difficulty regime (large d_i) where the monotone bound goes vacuous. DECOMPOSITION LEG (C04): we characterize the distribution of g_i across a batch, show it is bimodal (a small informative-positive mode and a corrupting-negative tail rather than a homogeneous mass), partition examples by the label-free sign criterion sign(tau_i* - d_i), and supply the error decomposition L_clean = L_informative_partition + (corrupting residual), bounding the residual by delta from the audit leg; r_i is the residual-correcting weight that subtracts the corrupting partition's expected mis-alignment contribution rather than discarding it. All three legs are one paper because they manipulate the single functional g_i: C10 finds where it changes sign, C19 re-proves the certificate using that sign-controlled mass, and C04 partitions and treats examples by that same sign. Quantitatively, prior hard-negative theory (W4402352439) bounds alignment under a label-available exclusion of same-class negatives; we do not paste their constant — our regime is label-free, so c(θ) and p_i are estimated from the augmentation graph, and our threshold reduces to their exclusion rule only in the limit p_i -> {0,1}.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The three gaps share machinery because each is a different question about ONE functional g_i (where it flips sign, why the old certificate ignored the flip, how to act on it per example), so a single shared-object design is correct rather than three modules; the evidence is that tau_i* appears identically in all three legs (separation criterion, weaker sufficient condition, partition criterion). Alternatives rejected: (1) a global per-batch threshold instead of per-example tau_i* — rejected because p_i varies sharply across examples, so a global cut re-creates exactly the global-trade-off limitation we are escaping; (2) simply DISCARDING above-threshold examples (a hard mask) — rejected because that throws away the informative component still present in a corrupting example, so we residually correct (r_i) instead, which is what makes the C04 error decomposition tight. Regression guard: we explicitly avoid landing on lineage node n2 (monotone hardness reweighting) — w_i is non-monotone by construction — and on collateral c0 (curriculum scheduling), since tau_i* is per-example-per-step from the augmentation graph, not a global easy-to-hard time schedule, and on c1 (blanket high-loss down-weighting), since we keep informative high-loss examples at full weight.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: pretrain a ResNet-18 encoder with InfoNCE on CIFAR-100 and ImageNet-100 under standard monotone hardness reweighting versus the difficulty-gated weight w_i, holding all else fixed, and measure downstream linear-probe top-1 accuracy plus, per epoch, the fraction of pairs with d_i >= tau_i*. If the candidate is right, linear-probe accuracy under the gated weight INCREASES relative to monotone reweighting, and the accuracy GAP widens precisely in the high-difficulty regime (small temperature / aggressive mining) where the monotone-crossed fraction is largest — and crucially, under monotone reweighting accuracy will DECREASE as the crossed fraction grows even while training InfoNCE loss keeps falling. The named load-bearing variable is the per-example threshold tau_i* (equivalently the sign indicator 1[d_i >= tau_i*]); the mechanism claim is that acting on this sign is what recovers accuracy. Negative control: permute p_i across pairs so tau_i* no longer reflects true false-pair probability — the gating then fires on the wrong examples and downstream linear-probe accuracy must fall back to (or below) the monotone baseline; if accuracy stays elevated under the permuted threshold, the gain came from generic regularization, not from the sign-flip mechanism, and the theory is falsified. Positive control: a stripped model gating only on the binary sign 1[d_i < tau_i*] should recover most of the downstream accuracy gain, identifying the threshold sign as the sufficient mechanism.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4402352439","delta":"They up-weight hard negatives while EXCLUDING same-class negatives using labels, proving alignment improves under that exclusion; we derive, with NO labels, a per-example signed threshold tau_i* at which a negative's marginal contribution crosses zero, and prove the monotone-weighting class cannot represent two examples straddling tau_i* — a sign-flip law their label-gated construction never produces."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4406070218","delta":"They empirically observe hard negatives cause overfitting past an un-quantified point and give a selection heuristic; we give the analytic location of that point (tau_i* = log((1-p_i)/p_i)+c(θ)) and a certificate non-vacuous in the high-difficulty regime, turning their empirical phenomenon into a predicted sign-flip with a falsifiable downstream-accuracy signature."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:143cdbb38dd5a4870bb98b5a584e0593adde285e","delta":"They detect false hard negatives via graph message-passing structure specific to GCL; we replace domain-specific detection with a modality-agnostic label-free functional g_i and prove its sign equals sign(tau_i*-d_i), giving a transferable per-example corruption score rather than a graph-only heuristic."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416045807","delta":"They bound average generalization for SUPERVISED CRL under non-IID tuples; we leave the average regime and characterize a per-example sign-flip in the LABEL-FREE objective, predicting that damage concentrates on the above-threshold sub-population rather than inflating a uniform average bound."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4402352439","what_step_was_missed":"They constructed the alignment-improvement guarantee for hardness reweighting under a LABEL-AVAILABLE exclusion of same-class negatives, which removes corrupting pairs by assumption; to reach our contribution they would have needed to construct the label-free per-example threshold separating informative from corrupting difficulty (the quantity tau_i* = log((1-p_i)/p_i)+c(θ) built from the augmentation-graph false-pair probability) and to prove the monotone-weighting class cannot represent the resulting opposite-sign treatment — a separation construction their label-gated derivation never builds because, with labels, the corrupting pairs are simply excluded rather than thresholded."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":247,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"Hard floor did not fire: gap_closure_reject_check is borderline (no entry triggered), no anti_pattern matched, and paper_pointed_threat (W4402352439) is NOT exact-mechanism overlap (label-gated exclusion vs label-free continuous threshold). recipe_application_check is 'applied' on all three legs — each performs its cluster's signature move on the shared functional g_i, so the idea is not built from the parent gist. The three borderlines (C10 'limit trivially implied', C19 'estimator-dependent quantity', C04 'partition read as rediscovery') hit load-bearing properties but are each already substantively answered in core_mechanism / falsification_prediction (explicit conflated pair, non-vacuity condition, bimodal value distribution + uniform baseline), so they are surfaced as reviewer concerns for Phase 4 rather than requiring a revise loop.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes the difficulty threshold itself: the point along an example's embedding-space hardness at which its marginal contribution to the unsupervised contrastive objective flips sign from improving to degrading the downstream representation, nor what data/encoder quantities govern where that threshold sits.","main_pattern":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail when the 'limit' is not a genuine structural blindspot: trivially implied by the model's own assumptions, already surpassed, or never formalized beyond an informal analogy; a recurring shape is substituting a hand-wavy mechanism for a separation proof.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Resting the central claim on an informal analogy (two operators 'both smooth high frequencies') instead of a separation proof leaves the mechanism underspecified and the empirical gain unconvincing.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate states a precise separation criterion (tau_i* = log((1-p_i)/p_i)+c(θ) with an explicit conflated pair — two examples straddling tau_i* that the monotone class must give same-sign treatment), not an analogy."},{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a 'maximally expressive' construction that a recently published method already strictly subsumes turns the surpass-the-limit claim into redundant work.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Collision retrieval surfaced no label-free per-example sign-flip threshold; the closest prior (W4402352439) excludes corrupting pairs by labels rather than thresholding, so it does not subsume the label-free construction."},{"lesson_quoted":"Deriving a 'limitation' that is trivially implied by the model's own linearity assumption produces a limit too weak to count as a real blindspot, and the proposed surpass step stays under-validated.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The monotone class's inability to give opposite-sign treatment is close to definitional (a monotone weight cannot encode a sign change); the candidate must show this is a substantive blindspot with real downstream cost, which the falsification_prediction's accuracy-vs-crossed-fraction signature does provide."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions the inherited assumption that an example's INFORMATIVENESS to the unsupervised contrastive loss should be a monotone increasing function of its embedding-space difficulty — every frontier method (hardness reweighting, temperature tuning, mining) builds on the loss whose per-sample gradient magnitude rises with difficulty, and none tests whether coupling gradient weight to difficulty is necessary rather than assumed.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C19 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The dominant failure is a relaxation whose payoff evaporates exactly where it is claimed (the re-derived certificate goes vacuous in the motivating regime), or the routine-lift trap of extending a known inequality without naming a novel obstacle, or hinging the guarantee on a quantity that cannot be estimated in the target setting.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A certificate that goes vacuous or diverges exactly in the regime it was built for is self-defeating; verify non-vacuity where the result must hold, not merely where it is convenient to prove.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate explicitly requires the re-derived certificate to stay non-vacuous in the high-difficulty regime via the bounded corrupting-mass condition E[p_i d_i 1[d_i>=tau_i*]] <= delta, which is the motivating regime."},{"lesson_quoted":"If the guarantee depends on a quantity that cannot be estimated in the target setting, the theoretical improvement does not transfer to the practical claim the paper makes.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The certificate depends on p_i (false-pair probability) estimated from the augmentation-graph kNN density; this is computable but noisy in the label-free setting, so the practical transfer hinges on the estimator quality — a concern to surface, not a trigger."},{"lesson_quoted":"A relaxation the field reads as a mechanical lift of a known argument will be judged incremental unless a genuinely novel obstacle is named and overcome, even when no reviewer is negative.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The named obstacle is genuinely novel: with no labels the corrupting pairs cannot be excluded, so the weaker sufficient condition must be one the gating construction provably satisfies rather than one assumed of the data — distinct from the label-gated exclusion in prior work."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a per-example quantity, computable without labels at a given training point, that separates an example whose difficulty is informative (a true hard negative/positive that sharpens the representation) from an example whose difficulty is corrupting (a false negative / mis-augmented positive whose large gradient pushes apart points that should align) — the frontier can only trade the two off globally via temperature or importance weight.","main_pattern":"heterogeneous_decomposition","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is treating the partition criterion itself as the contribution while leaving its value unproven, so reviewers map it onto an established technique; compounded by not benchmarking against both the strongest uniform baseline and the obvious cheap alternative, and by validating where the bottleneck does not bite.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Presenting a sensitivity or redundancy proxy as the novelty invites the verdict that it rediscovers known mixed-precision or low-rank results unless it is sharply differentiated from the obvious prior criterion.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The partition criterion sign(tau_i*-d_i) must be sharply differentiated from raw-similarity hard-negative mining; the candidate differentiates it as a SIGNED threshold derived from the C10 theorem rather than a magnitude cut, but this is the axis reviewers will probe."},{"lesson_quoted":"Omitting comparison against both the strongest uniform baseline and the obvious cheap alternative (SVD/PCA, structured dropout, a natively trained smaller model) leaves reviewers unable to tell whether the partition buys anything at all.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The falsification_prediction benchmarks against the strongest uniform baseline (monotone hardness reweighting) and includes the cheap alternative (binary-mask positive control), so the differentiated-vs-uniform comparison is present."},{"lesson_quoted":"Skipping any analysis of why the heterogeneity exists — the data or value distribution that drives the partition — makes the technical novelty and the potential impact impossible to assess.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism's decomposition leg characterizes the distribution of g_i and shows it is bimodal (informative-positive mode plus corrupting-negative tail), supplying the value distribution that drives the partition."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No entry is triggered; three entries are borderline. The C10 anchor's borderline is the 'limit trivially implied' lesson (the monotone class cannot encode a sign change is near-definitional), and the C04 decomposition's borderline is the 'partition criterion read as rediscovery' lesson — both hit load-bearing structural properties (the separation proof's substantiveness and the partition criterion's distinctness), so they warrant strengthening rather than abandonment."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes the difficulty threshold itself...","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Pinpoint the structural object an iterative-local procedure discards, formalize the equivalence class it induces as a WL-style separation criterion on native objects, prove the class conflates objects differing only in that property, then re-inject the object into the core step and prove the augmented operator strictly exceeds the criterion at bounded cost.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism's ANCHOR LEG performs exactly this: the discarded object is the SIGN of g_i (monotone weighting uses only |gradient|), the separation criterion is tau_i* with the explicit conflated pair (two examples straddling tau_i* that the monotone class must treat same-sign), and the re-injection is the gated weight w_i proven to strictly exceed the monotone class on the alignment objective at one-extra-similarity-read cost — the full discard/formalize/re-inject move, not the parent's generic 'characterize then surpass' gist.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions the inherited assumption that an example's INFORMATIVENESS to the unsupervised contrastive loss should be a monotone increasing function of its embedding-space difficulty...","sub_pattern":"C19 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Locate the regularity/independence/boundedness condition a statistical certificate imports for convenience, determine the minimal property it was actually buying, substitute a strictly weaker sufficient property the construction provably satisfies, and re-derive the certificate so it extends to a regime the old assumption excluded.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism's AUDIT LEG performs this precisely: it locates the convenience condition (informativeness non-decreasing in d_i) inside the alignment-improvement certificate, traces that it only buys a one-sided bound on corrupting-pair mass E[p_i d_i], substitutes the strictly weaker E[p_i d_i 1[d_i>=tau_i*]] <= delta that the gating provably satisfies, and re-derives the certificate to stay non-vacuous in the high-difficulty regime — a proof-internal assumption relaxation, the C19 signature, not a counterexample/violate move.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a per-example quantity, computable without labels at a given training point, that separates an example whose difficulty is informative...","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Discriminate components by a sensitivity/influence/redundancy criterion into a high-impact minority and a near-redundant bulk, apply a tailored treatment to each (protect/migrate/residually-correct vs aggressively compress), and supply an error/sensitivity decomposition that bounds how the differentiated treatment recovers the original objective.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism's DECOMPOSITION LEG performs this: it partitions examples by the influence-style signed criterion sign(tau_i*-d_i) into an informative minority and a corrupting bulk, applies a tailored treatment (full weight to informative, residual-corrected down-weight r_i to corrupting rather than discarding), and supplies the error decomposition L_clean = L_informative_partition + corrupting residual with the residual bounded by delta — the load-bearing error-decomposition spine that distinguishes C04 from heuristic per-example tuning.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"All three legs perform their cited cluster's signature move on the shared functional g_i: C10's discard-formalize-reinject of the gradient sign, C19's weaker-sufficient-condition relaxation of the certificate, and C04's error-decomposition-backed partition-and-treat. The single object g_i carries all three, so none collapses to the parent gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["characterize_limit_then_surpass","assumption_audit_and_pivot","heterogeneous_decomposition"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"The three 2-way subsets are characterize_limit+assumption_audit, characterize_limit+heterogeneous_decomposition, and assumption_audit+heterogeneous_decomposition; none matches the three documented reject-favored compositions (decomp+SSL, decomp+structural_prior, operator+decomp), so no anti-pattern fires."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"openalex:W4402352439","threat_source":"lit_table","subsumption_argument":"Supervised Contrastive Learning with Hard Negative Samples is the most specific competitor: it proves alignment improvement for hardness-reweighted InfoNCE while up-weighting hard negatives and EXCLUDING same-class ones using labels. The candidate's claim stands or falls on whether the label-free per-example threshold tau_i* is a genuine new construction rather than a relabeling of their label-gated exclusion: if, in the unsupervised regime, p_i estimated from the augmentation graph collapses to a trivial 0/1 indicator equivalent to a label, the candidate reduces to their rule and the sign-flip law adds nothing. The candidate survives because in the genuinely label-free regime p_i is a continuous augmentation-graph density (not a label), so tau_i* gives graded opposite-sign treatment their binary exclusion cannot, and the falsification's permuted-p_i negative control isolates exactly this distinction.","addressable_via":"Strengthen differentiation_from_lit[0] and what_step_was_missed to make explicit that tau_i* reduces to their exclusion rule only in the degenerate p_i -> {0,1} limit, so the contribution is the continuous label-free regime they cannot reach — already partly present, can be sharpened but is not exact-mechanism overlap."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# When Hard Becomes Harmful: A Sign-Flip Threshold for Difficulty in Unsupervised Contrastive Learning\n\n**Method.** Difficulty Sign-Flip Gating (DSG)\n\n## Motivation\nContrastive learning teaches a model to pull two views of the same thing together and push different things apart. A popular trick is to focus on 'hard negatives' — the different things that look deceptively similar — because they seem to teach the model the most. The catch in the UNSUPERVISED setting (no labels) is that a 'different thing that looks very similar' is often not actually different at all: it may be another image of the same category, wrongly treated as a negative. The standard machinery has only one global knob (a temperature, or an importance weight) that makes the model pay more attention to ALL hard examples at once, so it cannot tell a genuinely informative hard example from a corrupting fake one. Recent papers keep finding that turning this knob up too far stops helping and starts hurting (the model overfits or collapses), but nobody has said exactly WHEN or WHY that happens.\n\nThis project gives the missing theory. We prove that each example has its own tipping point: a difficulty threshold $\\tau _{i}*$ beyond which pushing that example apart actively damages the learned representation instead of improving it. The threshold is built from one label-free number $p_{i}$ — an estimate, taken from how the data clusters, of the chance that this 'negative' is secretly the same category as the anchor — plus a term $c(\\theta )$ that tracks the model's current state. Below the threshold the example is informative; above it, it is corrupting. Because a single global knob is forced to treat every example the same way, we can prove it can never give two examples on opposite sides of their thresholds the opposite treatment they need.\n\nEarlier theory (the supervised hard-negative analysis of W4402352439) sidestepped the problem by using labels to throw out the same-category negatives; the empirical graph-contrastive work (W4406070218) saw the harm but only offered a tuning heuristic; the false-negative detectors (semanticscholar:143cdbb38dd5a4870bb98b5a584e0593adde285e) worked only for graphs. What is new is that the augmentation-graph view of contrastive learning now lets us estimate $p_{i}$ without any labels, which is exactly what makes a per-example threshold possible now.\n\nWhen this gap closes, hard-negative mining stops being a global gamble: every example gets its own keep-or-correct decision, the harmful-difficulty effect becomes a predictable and controllable sign-flip, and several prior fixes turn out to be special cases of one thresholding principle.\n\n## Method\n### Threshold theory\n*Defines and verifies the per-example sign-flip threshold $\\tau _{i}*$ and the contribution functional $g_{i}$ it governs.*\n\n1. For each anchor, run the anchor and its augmented positive view through the encoder and take their embeddings from the projection head (the small output network where the contrastive loss is computed), scale each embedding to unit length, then compute the unit direction pointing from the anchor's embedding to the positive's embedding (subtract and re-normalize). Call this direction $u_{align}.$ It lets us later turn 'does this example help or hurt alignment' into a single number read per example.\n   - _Why_: This direction lets us turn 'does this example help or hurt alignment' into a single number we can read per example.\n2. Set each example's threshold $\\tau _{i}*$ equal to log((1 minus $p_{i})$ over $p_{i})$ plus $c(\\theta ).$ Compute the example's contribution $g_{i}$ directly from a formula — the contrastive loss's gradient from this negative is its softmax weight times the direction (negative minus anchor) over the temperature, and $g_{i}$ is that projected onto the alignment direction $u_{align},$ so no extra backward pass is needed. Then check the core law: the sign of $g_{i}$ should match the sign of $(\\tau _{i}*$ minus $d_{i}).$ Do this as a monitoring check — record, each epoch, the fraction of pairs where the two signs agree; it does not change training, it just confirms that below the threshold the example helps and above it the same example hurts. A single global knob can never flip an example's treatment at the right place, which is exactly what this threshold makes precise.\n\n*The per-example marginal-contribution functional $g_{i}:$ the projection of example i's InfoNCE gradient onto the alignment direction $u_{align}$; its sign says whether example i helps or harms downstream alignment.*\n$$ g_i = \\left\\langle \\frac{\\partial \\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{InfoNCE}}}{\\partial \\theta}\\Big|_i,\\; u_{\\mathrm{align}} \\right\\rangle \\tag{1} $$\n\n\n*The per-example sign-flip threshold $tau_{i}*:$ built from the label-free false-pair probability $p_{i}$ and the batch alignment-uniformity gap $c(\\theta )$; $g_{i} > 0$ when difficulty $d_{i} < \\tau _{i}*$ and $g_{i} < 0$ when $d_{i} \\ge  \\tau _{i}*.$*\n$$ \\tau_i^{*} = \\log\\frac{1 - p_i}{p_i} + c(\\theta) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This is the core law: below the threshold the example helps, above it the same example hurts, and a single global knob can never flip its treatment at the right place.\n\n### Label-free difficulty estimation\n*Computes the inputs to the threshold — difficulty $d_{i},$ false-pair probability $p_{i},$ and the encoder-state term $c(\\theta ).$*\n\n3. For every anchor and each of its negatives, compute a difficulty score $d_{i}$ equal to the cosine similarity between their unit embeddings divided by the temperature (the same temperature used in the contrastive loss). This is exactly the 'hardness' score the standard baseline uses, so we measure difficulty on the same scale the baseline up-weights and any later difference comes only from our gating.\n   - _Why_: We measure difficulty on the exact scale the baseline up-weights, so any difference comes from our gating, not from a different scale.\n4. Build a k-nearest-neighbor graph (each point connected to its k most-similar points by cosine similarity) over the current batch plus a memory bank of recent embeddings, using k = 20 neighbors. For each anchor-negative pair, set $p_{i}$ to the fraction of the negative's 20 neighbors that are also among the positive's 20 neighbors. This is a label-free estimate, taken purely from how the data clusters, of the chance that this 'negative' is secretly the same category as the anchor, and it recovers without any labels the information earlier work could only get from labels. Keep $p_{i}$ slightly away from 0 and 1 so the later logarithm stays finite. 【author decision: whether $p_{i}$ is read from a slowly-updated copy of the encoder (more stable estimate) or from the live encoder (simpler) — a stability-versus-simplicity choice.】\n   - _Why_: This recovers, without any labels, the information earlier work could only get from labels.\n5. Compute a single number per batch, $c(\\theta ):$ take the average squared distance between matched positive pairs, then subtract the logarithm of the average of a Gaussian-style closeness score over the negative pairs (using the same temperature as the loss). This one scalar summarizes how aligned (positives close) versus uniform (negatives spread out) the encoder currently is. Because the tipping point moves as the model trains, the threshold must shift with the model's state, which is what this term provides.\n   - _Why_: The tipping point moves as the model trains, so the threshold must shift with the model's state.\n\n### Gated training with bounded residual\n*Applies the non-monotone gated weight and trains with the error decomposition that bounds the corrupting residual.*\n\n6. Weight each negative by $w_{i}.$ When the difficulty $d_{i}$ is below the threshold $\\tau _{i}*,$ keep the usual hardness weight $m(d_{i})$ (the normalized $exp(d_{i})$ the standard baseline uses). When $d_{i}$ is at or above the threshold, instead use $r_{i} = m(d_{i})$ times (1 minus $2\\cdot p_{i}):$ if the chance this pair is secretly same-class $(p_{i})$ is above one half, this weight turns negative, which switches the pair from being pushed apart to being pulled together. So instead of throwing away above-threshold examples we correct them, keeping whatever informative signal they still carry, at the cost of one extra similarity computation per pair.\n\n*The difficulty-gated weight $w_{i}:$ keep the standard hardness weight $m(d_{i})$ below threshold, and apply the residual correction $r_{i}$ above it; $r_{i}$ becomes negative (a pull instead of a push) when the false-pair probability $p_{i}$ exceeds one half.*\n$$ w_i = m(d_i)\\,\\mathbf{1}[d_i < \\tau_i^{*}] + r_i\\,\\mathbf{1}[d_i \\geq \\tau_i^{*}],\\quad r_i = m(d_i)\\,(1 - 2 p_i) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Instead of throwing away above-threshold examples we correct them, keeping whatever informative signal they still carry.\n7. Train the encoder exactly as usual but use $w_{i}$ in the loss in place of the standard per-negative weight. The clean training objective then splits into an informative part plus a corrupting leftover, and the gating provably keeps that leftover below a small bound — this bound is not a knob you set, it follows from the construction, and you only track it each epoch (from the observed $p_{i}$ and $d_{i})$ to confirm it stays small. Bounding this leftover is what proves the per-example treatment recovers the clean objective better than any single fixed temperature.\n\n*The error decomposition: the clean-data alignment objective splits into the informative-partition loss plus a corrupting residual, which the gating bounds below $\\delta $ — the same $\\delta $ that keeps the re-derived certificate non-vacuous in the high-difficulty regime.*\n$$ \\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{clean}} = \\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{informative}} + \\underbrace{\\mathbb{E}\\big[p_i\\, d_i\\, \\mathbf{1}[d_i \\geq \\tau_i^{*}]\\big]}_{\\leq\\, \\delta} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Bounding the residual is what proves the per-example treatment recovers the clean objective better than any single temperature.\n\n### Falsification protocol\n*Tests the predicted accuracy-vs-crossed-fraction reveal and isolates the sign-flip mechanism with controls.*\n\n8. Train two encoders that are identical except for the per-negative weight: one with the standard monotone reweighting $m(d_{i})$ and one with the gated weight $w_{i},$ on CIFAR-100 and ImageNet-100. Use the same standard data augmentations (random crop, flip, color jitter, grayscale, blur), the same ResNet-18 backbone with a small projection head, and the same standard training schedule for both. Vary how aggressively hard examples are mined by lowering the temperature. Each epoch, measure accuracy with a linear probe (freeze the encoder, train just one linear classifier on its features) and the fraction of pairs that sit above their threshold. Then run two controls: a negative control that randomly shuffles the $p_{i}$ values across pairs (so the threshold fires on the wrong examples), and a positive control that gates only on the yes/no 'is this example below threshold' decision (dropping the residual correction). Accuracy rising under gating while falling under monotone reweighting, as more pairs cross the threshold, is the visible prediction; the shuffle control proves the sign-flip — not generic regularization — is responsible.\n   - _Why_: Accuracy rising under gating while falling under monotone reweighting (as more pairs cross the threshold) is the visible prediction; the permutation control proves the sign-flip — not generic regularization — is responsible.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 当困难变得有害：无监督对比学习中难度的符号翻转阈值\n\n**方法名称.** Difficulty Sign-Flip Gating (DSG)\n\n## 研究动机\n对比学习教模型把同一事物的两个视角拉近、把不同事物推远。一个常用技巧是重点关注「困难负样本」——那些看起来很相似却被当作不同的样本——因为它们似乎能教给模型最多信息。但在无监督（无标签）场景下有个陷阱：一个「看起来很相似的不同样本」往往其实并不是不同的，它可能是同一类别的另一张图，却被错误地当成了负样本。标准机制只有一个全局旋钮（temperature 或重要性权重），它让模型同时对所有困难样本投入更多注意力，因此无法区分真正有益的困难样本和具有腐蚀性的假困难样本。最近的论文反复发现，把这个旋钮拧得过大就不再有帮助、反而开始损害表示（模型过拟合或坍塌），但没有人说清楚这究竟在何时、为何发生。\n\n本项目给出了缺失的理论。我们证明每个样本都有自己的临界点：一个难度阈值 $\\tau _{i}*$，超过它之后，把该样本推开会主动损害所学表示，而不是改善它。该阈值由一个无标签的数 $p_{i}——$根据数据的聚集方式估计出的、这个「负样本」其实与锚点同类的概率——加上一个跟踪模型当前状态的项 $c(\\theta )$ 构成。低于阈值时样本是有益的；高于阈值时它是腐蚀性的。由于单一全局旋钮被迫对每个样本一视同仁，我们可以证明它永远无法对处在各自阈值两侧的两个样本给出它们所需要的相反处理。\n\n早先的理论（W4402352439 的有监督困难负样本分析）通过使用标签丢弃同类负样本来回避这个问题；图对比学习的经验工作（W4406070218）看到了危害，却只给出调参启发式；伪负样本检测器（semanticscholar:143cdbb38dd5a4870bb98b5a584e0593adde285e）只适用于图。新意在于：对比学习的 augmentation-graph 视角如今让我们能够在没有任何标签的情况下估计 $p_{i}$，而这正是使「逐样本阈值」此刻成为可能的关键。\n\n当这一空白被填补，困难负样本挖掘就不再是全局赌博：每个样本都得到自己的「保留还是修正」的决定，有害难度效应变成可预测、可控制的符号翻转，而此前的若干修复方法也都成为同一个阈值原理的特例。\n\n## 方法\n### 阈值理论\n*定义并验证逐样本符号翻转阈值 $\\tau _{i}*$ 及其支配的贡献泛函 $g_{i}$。*\n\n1. 对每个锚点(anchor)，把锚点及其增广正样本(positive)送入编码器，并从投影头(projection head，即计算对比损失的那个小输出网络)取出它们的 embedding；将每个 embedding 缩放到单位长度，然后计算从锚点 embedding 指向正样本 embedding 的单位方向(相减后再归一化)，记为 $u_{align}$。它让我们之后能把『该样本对对齐(alignment)是有益还是有害』变成一个可以逐样本读出的数。\n   - _为什么_: 这个方向让我们把「该样本对对齐是有益还是有害」变成一个可以逐样本读出的数。\n2. 把每个样本的阈值 $\\tau _{i}*$ 设为 log((1 减 $p_{i})$ 除以 $p_{i})$ 加 $c(\\theta )$。直接用公式计算样本的贡献 $g_{i}——$对比损失来自该负样本的梯度等于它的 softmax 权重乘以方向(负样本减锚点)再除以 temperature，而 $g_{i}$ 就是把它投影到对齐方向 $u_{align}$ 上，因此不需要额外的反向传播。然后检验核心规律：$g_{i}$ 的符号应与 $(\\tau _{i}*$ 减 $d_{i})$ 的符号一致。这是作为一项监控来做——每个 epoch 记录两个符号一致的样本对比例；它不改变训练，只是确认阈值以下样本有益、阈值以上同一样本有害。单一全局旋钮永远无法在正确的位置翻转某个样本的处理方式，而这个阈值正好把这一点刻画清楚。\n\n*每个样本的边际贡献泛函 $g_{i}$：把样本 i 的 InfoNCE 梯度投影到对齐方向 $u_{align}$ 上；其符号表示样本 i 对下游对齐是有益还是有害。*\n$$ g_i = \\left\\langle \\frac{\\partial \\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{InfoNCE}}}{\\partial \\theta}\\Big|_i,\\; u_{\\mathrm{align}} \\right\\rangle \\tag{1} $$\n\n\n*每个样本的符号翻转阈值 $\\tau _{i}*$：由无标签的伪负对概率 $p_{i}$ 与批内 alignment-uniformity 间隙 $c(\\theta )$ 构成；当难度 $d_{i} < \\tau _{i}*$ 时 $g_{i} > 0$，当 $d_{i} \\ge  \\tau _{i}*$ 时 $g_{i} < 0$。*\n$$ \\tau_i^{*} = \\log\\frac{1 - p_i}{p_i} + c(\\theta) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这就是核心规律：阈值以下样本有益，阈值以上同一样本有害，而单一全局旋钮永远无法在正确的位置翻转它的处理方式。\n\n### 无标签难度估计\n*计算阈值的输入——难度 $d_{i}$、伪负对概率 $p_{i}$ 和编码器状态项 $c(\\theta )$。*\n\n3. 对每个锚点及其每个负样本(negative)，计算难度分数 $d_{i}$，等于二者单位 embedding 的余弦相似度除以 temperature(与对比损失中所用的 temperature 相同)。这正是标准基线所用的『难度』分数，因此我们在基线加权所用的同一尺度上度量难度，之后的任何差异都只来自我们的门控(gating)。\n   - _为什么_: 我们在基线加权所用的同一尺度上度量难度，因此任何差异都来自我们的门控，而非尺度不同。\n4. 在当前 batch 加上一个最近 embedding 的 memory bank 上，按余弦相似度构建 k 近邻图(每个点连到与它最相似的 k 个点)，取 k = 20 个近邻。对每个锚点-负样本对，把 $p_{i}$ 设为该负样本的 20 个近邻中同时也属于正样本 20 个近邻的比例。这是一个纯粹依据数据聚集方式得到的无标签估计，表示这个『负样本』其实与锚点同类的概率，它在没有任何标签的情况下恢复了早先工作只能从标签获得的信息。把 $p_{i}$ 稍微限制在 0 与 1 之间，使之后的对数保持有限。【作者需决定：$p_{i}$ 是从一个缓慢更新的编码器副本(估计更稳定)读取，还是从实时编码器(更简单)读取——这是稳定性与简洁性之间的取舍。】\n   - _为什么_: 这在没有任何标签的情况下，恢复了早先工作只能从标签获得的信息。\n5. 每个 batch 计算一个标量 $c(\\theta )$：取匹配正样本对之间的平均平方距离，再减去负样本对上一个高斯式接近度分数的平均值的对数(使用与损失相同的 temperature)。这一个标量概括了编码器当前的对齐(alignment，正样本靠近)与均匀(uniformity，负样本散开)状态。由于临界点会随训练而移动，阈值必须随模型状态平移，这一项正好提供了这种平移。\n   - _为什么_: 临界点会随训练而移动，所以阈值必须随模型状态平移。\n\n### 带界残差的门控训练\n*施加非单调门控权重，并用约束腐蚀性残差的误差分解进行训练。*\n\n6. 用 $w_{i}$ 给每个负样本加权。当难度 $d_{i}$ 低于阈值 $\\tau _{i}*$ 时，保留通常的难度权重 $m(d_{i})($标准基线所用的归一化 $exp(d_{i}))$。当 $d_{i}$ 达到或超过阈值时，改用 $r_{i} = m(d_{i})$ 乘以 (1 减 $2\\cdot p_{i})$：若这一对其实同类的概率 $p_{i}$ 超过二分之一，该权重就变为负值，从而把这对样本从被推开切换为被拉近。因此我们不是丢弃阈值以上的样本，而是修正它们，保留它们仍携带的有益信号，代价仅是每对样本多算一次相似度。\n\n*难度门控权重 $w_{i}$：阈值以下保留标准难度权重 $m(d_{i})$，阈值以上施加残差修正 $r_{i}$；当伪负对概率 $p_{i}$ 超过二分之一时 $r_{i}$ 变为负值（由推开变为拉近）。*\n$$ w_i = m(d_i)\\,\\mathbf{1}[d_i < \\tau_i^{*}] + r_i\\,\\mathbf{1}[d_i \\geq \\tau_i^{*}],\\quad r_i = m(d_i)\\,(1 - 2 p_i) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 我们不是丢弃阈值以上的样本，而是修正它们，保留它们仍携带的有益信号。\n7. 照常训练编码器，但在损失中用 $w_{i}$ 替换标准的逐负样本权重。干净的训练目标随之分解为有益部分加上腐蚀性残差，门控可证明地把该残差保持在一个小界以下——这个界不是你设定的旋钮，它由构造本身推出，你只需每个 epoch(根据观测到的 $p_{i}$ 与 $d_{i})$跟踪它以确认其保持很小。约束这个残差正是证明逐样本处理比任何单一固定 temperature 更好地恢复干净目标的关键。\n\n*误差分解：干净数据的对齐目标分解为有益分区损失加上腐蚀性残差，门控将该残差约束在 $\\delta $ 以下——正是这个 $\\delta $ 让重新推导的证书在高难度区间保持非平凡。*\n$$ \\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{clean}} = \\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{informative}} + \\underbrace{\\mathbb{E}\\big[p_i\\, d_i\\, \\mathbf{1}[d_i \\geq \\tau_i^{*}]\\big]}_{\\leq\\, \\delta} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 约束残差正是证明逐样本处理比任何单一 temperature 更好地恢复干净目标的关键。\n\n### 证伪协议\n*检验所预测的精度-越阈比例规律，并用对照实验分离出符号翻转机制。*\n\n8. 在 CIFAR-100 和 ImageNet-100 上训练两个除逐负样本权重外完全相同的编码器：一个用标准单调重加权 $m(d_{i})$，一个用门控权重 $w_{i}$。两者使用相同的标准数据增广(随机裁剪、翻转、颜色抖动、灰度化、高斯模糊)、相同的 ResNet-18 主干加一个小投影头、以及相同的标准训练调度。通过降低 temperature 来调节困难样本挖掘的激进程度。每个 epoch 用 linear probe(冻结编码器，只在其特征上训练一个线性分类器)测量精度，以及处于各自阈值之上的样本对比例。然后运行两个对照：负对照把各样本对的 $p_{i}$ 值随机打乱(使阈值作用在错误的样本上)，正对照只按『该样本是否低于阈值』这个是/否判断来门控(去掉残差修正)。门控下精度上升、而单调重加权下精度随越过阈值的样本对增多而下降，这就是可见的预测；打乱对照证明负责的是符号翻转，而非一般的正则化。\n   - _为什么_: 门控下精度上升、而单调重加权下精度随越过阈值的样本对增多而下降，这就是可见的预测；置换对照证明负责的是符号翻转，而非一般的正则化。\n\n"},{"id":"28","run_dir":"run_prompt28_diffusionlm","index":28,"title":"When the Answer Freezes: A Decode-Time Determinacy Probe for Diffusion LMs","title_zh":"当答案冻结之时：面向扩散语言模型的一个去混淆解码期确定性探针","method_name":"Answer-Settling Probe (frozen-decode probe + online estimator d_t)","hook":"In masked diffusion language models the final answer is provably frozen many denoising steps before per-step token confidence saturates, and a confound-isolating probe shows the two signals diverge — so confidence-greedy early stopping commits wrong answers exactly when the answer is settled but confidence is not.","anchor_pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","anchor_pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","domain_category":"LLM Reasoning & Decoding","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides a per-instance, decode-time quantity that certifies when a masked diffusion LM's answer has stopped changing across denoising steps, so the model cannot recognize a prompt whose answer is already settled and is forced to spend the full worst-case step budget on it (additive: the missing outcome is an answer-settled readout, not any one mechanism for producing it).","pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by constructing a controlled probe that holds the prompt fixed and blocks the confound (per-step marginal token confidence) while independently varying the true property (cross-step answer stability), reporting the divergence between the confidence-threshold stop step and the oracle answer-freeze step t_freeze as the headline gap — the measurement primitive is the per-instance answer-settling readout.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf exploits the gap between when the answer is internally determined and when decoding terminates to reallocate the remaining compute to the still-uncertain prompts or positions, so all prompts and all positions are treated as equally hard for the full budget (additive: the missing outcome is per-instance/per-position compute reallocation driven by determinacy, mechanism left open).","pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","sub_pattern":"C23 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by reaching inside the denoising chain and re-specifying its conventionally-fixed, prompt-independent step schedule as a free variable set per-instance by the measured determinacy readout — the chain halts a prompt once its determinacy estimate certifies the answer is frozen and rolls the freed forward passes onto still-undetermined prompts/positions in the batch.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"diffusion language models (masked/discrete diffusion text generation) — decoding-time dynamics","n_papers":41,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":27},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":19,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Text-Guided Molecule Generation with Diffusion Language Model"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Taiyi-Diffusion-XL: Advancing Bilingual Text-to-Image Generation with Large Vision-Language Model Support"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Energy-Based Diffusion Language Models for Text Generation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Discrete Diffusion Language Model for Efficient Text Summarization"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Conditional [MASK] Discrete Diffusion Language Model"},{"source":"openalex","title":"InstanceDiffusion: Instance-Level Control for Image Generation"}],"more":13},{"year":2025,"n":21,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Theoretical Benefit and Limitation of Diffusion Language Model"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"LaViDa: A Large Diffusion Language Model for Multimodal Understanding"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Anchored Diffusion Language Model"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"FS-DFM: Fast and Accurate Long Text Generation with Few-Step Diffusion Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Interactive Image Caption Generation Reflecting User Intent from Trace Using a Diffusion Language Model"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Diffusion Language Model Inference with Monte Carlo Tree Search"}],"more":15},{"year":2026,"n":1,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"}],"more":0}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":13,"share":0.317},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":9,"share":0.22},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":8,"share":0.195},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":6,"share":0.146},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":4,"share":0.098},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":4,"share":0.098},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":3,"share":0.073},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":3,"share":0.073}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Masked diffusion language models (MDMs) decode by iteratively unmasking tokens over a fixed step budget, and the field has established that their accuracy-efficiency profile is metric-dependent and that quality collapses when the step count is cut [semanticscholar:410d8f0451384237b054b3f06cd8eab1c9f72104; semanticscholar:c3f18504c770549771b29c222db41b343dd1f36d]. The structural failure is that the model's internally-determined answer and the externally-emitted token sequence are decoupled: by some intermediate denoising step the conditional distribution over the still-masked positions has effectively collapsed onto the final committed tokens, but the decoder carries no per-instance, per-position quantity that certifies this collapse, so it cannot tell a step that still changes the answer from a step that merely re-confirms an already-settled answer [semanticscholar:d136e08a12144b0087b0bbe3e4507d99cbded34f]. Consequently every prompt pays the same worst-case number of forward passes regardless of how early its answer stabilized, and inference-time search over which positions to commit is run blind, approximated by expensive heuristics or tree search rather than steered by a measured commitment signal [semanticscholar:9ccbb820261b9141e46de121ed26ae3e3b16772b]. The current machinery cannot produce the needed quantity because confidence-greedy unmasking reads only the marginal token probability at the position being unmasked at the current step, never a global readout of whether the whole answer has stopped moving across steps.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:410d8f0451384237b054b3f06cd8eab1c9f72104","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Proves, in an HMM framework, that masked diffusion models can reach near-optimal perplexity in few steps but require many more steps when the target metric is exact sequence correctness, characterizing the accuracy-efficiency frontier as metric-dependent. The analysis is a worst-case statement over the model class and target metric and yields no per-instance, decode-time quantity that says THIS prompt's answer is already determined, so it cannot turn its theoretical step-count bound into an adaptive per-prompt stopping or compute-reallocation rule."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:d136e08a12144b0087b0bbe3e4507d99cbded34f","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Anchored DLM predicts distributions over important (anchor) tokens first via a two-stage anchor network, then conditions reconstruction of the remaining tokens on those anchor predictions to fix the early-masking-of-key-tokens failure. It commits anchors by a fixed architectural ordering decided at training time and never measures, at decode time, whether the predicted answer has stopped changing across denoising steps, so it improves WHICH tokens get context first but not WHEN the answer is settled."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:9ccbb820261b9141e46de121ed26ae3e3b16772b","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"MEDAL frames decode-time choice of which positions to unmask and which tokens to commit as a combinatorial search and uses Monte Carlo Tree Search to find better decoding paths. It buys quality with many extra forward passes per step and relies on rollout value estimates rather than a cheap measured signal of answer commitment, so it has no way to recognize that a branch's answer is already settled and stop expanding it."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:c3f18504c770549771b29c222db41b343dd1f36d","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"EDLM identifies that the per-step factorized (independent-across-positions) approximation is what degrades few-step quality and adds a sequence-level energy correction to repair the joint. The energy term is a quality patch applied uniformly at every step and is not read as a per-instance stop/continue signal, so it does not expose when further steps stop changing the committed answer."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"diffusion language models (masked/discrete diffusion text generation) — decoding-time dynamics","venue":"ICLR / NeurIPS / ICML (Oral tier)","time":"2026","data":["standard open DLM checkpoints (e.g. LLaDA / MDM-style masked diffusion LMs)","reasoning + QA benchmarks (GSM8K, MMLU-style multiple-choice, open-ended generation perplexity sets)","summarization/seq2seq sets (XSum/QQP) for conditional generation"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (approx 90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher familiar with diffusion models and language model decoding","preference":"both","baseline":"standard fixed-step masked-diffusion decoding (uniform or confidence-greedy unmasking over a fixed number of denoising steps)","limitation":"a masked diffusion LM frequently determines its final answer internally well before the fixed denoising-step budget runs out, yet there is no per-instance signal of when the answer is committed, so it keeps spending forward passes that no longer change the output and cannot stop early or reallocate compute","contribution_type":"empirical_reveal","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The two legs interlock as a sequential_pipeline named the answer-settling probe: Leg A measures when the answer freezes, Leg B liberates the step schedule to spend compute accordingly. Leg A (controlled_diagnostic_design) names the confound explicitly: standard confidence-greedy decoders read only c_t(i) = max_v p_theta(x_i = v | x_t), the per-position marginal token confidence at denoising step t, and treat c_t crossing a threshold as 'the model knows token i'. The true property we want is cross-step answer stability of the committed sequence, which c_t does not measure because a position can have high marginal confidence while the joint answer still flips at other positions. We build the confound-isolating instrument as follows. For an evaluation prompt with a verifiable final answer span A (e.g. the boxed numeric answer in GSM8K, the selected option letter in MMLU), run the FROZEN-DECODE PROBE: at each denoising step t, take the current partially-unmasked state x_t and greedily complete ALL remaining masked positions in one extra forward pass to obtain a hypothesis sequence h_t (this is a read-only probe; it does not alter the real trajectory). Define the answer-freeze step t_freeze(prompt) = the smallest t such that the answer span extracted from h_t equals the answer span of the fully decoded output x_0 AND stays equal for every t' > t (the answer has stopped moving). t_freeze is computed from the model alone (model-internal readout via one extra forward pass per step) and needs no external label at deploy time; the gold answer A is used only to score correctness in the diagnostic. The headline measured object is the determinacy gap g = t_stop_conf - t_freeze, where t_stop_conf is the step at which a standard confidence-threshold rule (all positions' c_t >= tau) would have stopped, and the de-confounded comparison is correctness-at-t_freeze versus correctness-at-t_stop_conf on matched prompts. Leg B (generative_process_redesign, C23) re-specifies the fixed schedule: it replaces the constant K-step grid with a per-instance stopping rule driven by a cheap online determinacy estimator d_t (defined below) that approximates t_freeze WITHOUT the gold answer — decode halts a prompt when d_t certifies the answer is frozen, and in batched decoding the forward passes freed by early-halted prompts are reallocated to prompts whose d_t is still low. The online estimator is the prefix-agreement statistic d_t = fraction of answer-span positions whose argmax token in h_t agrees with h_{t-1} over a sliding window of w steps (a model-internal, label-free surrogate for 'the hypothesis answer has stopped changing'); w and the agreement threshold delta are named hyperparameters selected on a held-out split. The load-bearing variable is t_freeze (and its online surrogate d_t): if it genuinely captures answer determinacy, halting at the d_t-certified step must preserve task accuracy while cutting forward passes; if it is merely confidence in disguise, halting will track the confidence rule and lose accuracy the same way. Prior work measured neither object: the metric-dependent step-count bound of [semanticscholar:410d8f0451384237b054b3f06cd8eab1c9f72104] is a worst-case statement over the model class with no per-instance freeze readout, and Anchored DLM [semanticscholar:d136e08a12144b0087b0bbe3e4507d99cbded34f] fixes WHICH tokens get context first by training-time ordering but never measures WHEN the answer stops changing at decode time.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules because t_freeze produced by Leg A is exactly the quantity Leg B's schedule liberation consumes — the diagnostic's de-confounded readout IS the control signal for reallocation, which is why the coherence thread is sequential_pipeline and not two parallel contributions. (b) I considered making Leg A a self_supervised_signal_engineering leg that trains a learned 'determinacy critic' head, but rejected it: training a critic conflates measuring the phenomenon with fitting it, so a wrong critic could not be distinguished from a wrong phenomenon — the confound-isolating diagnostic with an oracle (full-decode answer) independent of the estimator is the only design that can prove the answer freezes early as a fact before any estimator is trusted. I also rejected a fixed global step cut for Leg B because, per method_lineage, that regresses onto node n5 (FS-DFM fixed budget) and collateral c1 (DDIM/consistency distillation); the avoided node is the prompt-independent schedule cut, sidestepped by making the budget a per-instance function of the measured d_t.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on a pretrained masked diffusion LM decoded over a fixed K-step grid, run the frozen-decode probe on GSM8K and MMLU and measure (i) the answer-freeze step t_freeze per prompt and (ii) exact-match accuracy when decoding is halted at t_freeze versus at the confidence-threshold step t_stop_conf. If the candidate is correct, t_freeze occurs at a substantially smaller fraction of K than t_stop_conf for most prompts (the determinacy gap g is positive and large), and accuracy-at-t_freeze stays equal to full-K accuracy while accuracy-at-t_stop_conf is strictly lower — i.e. the answer is genuinely settled before per-position confidence saturates. The load-bearing variable is the online determinacy estimator d_t (surrogate for t_freeze): the negative control permutes the answer-span position indices that d_t is computed over (d_t^perm), destroying its answer-determinacy content while keeping the same per-step agreement-rate distribution; if d_t carries the mechanism, halting the liberated decoder on d_t^perm must drive downstream task accuracy back down to the fixed-global-step-cut baseline at matched NFE, whereas halting on the true d_t preserves full-K accuracy. The recommended positive control is the stripped decoder that halts on d_t alone (no confidence channel), which should recover most of the forward-pass savings at near-full accuracy, converting the falsifier into a constructive identification that answer-determinacy, not confidence, is the signal that governs how many denoising steps a prompt needs.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:410d8f0451384237b054b3f06cd8eab1c9f72104","delta":"They prove a worst-case, metric-dependent step-count frontier over the MDM model class; we construct and measure a per-instance answer-freeze step t_freeze at decode time and report the de-confounded accuracy gap between freezing on answer-determinacy versus on per-position confidence, a quantity their class-level bound cannot produce for an individual prompt."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:d136e08a12144b0087b0bbe3e4507d99cbded34f","delta":"Anchored DLM decides WHICH tokens to commit first via a training-time anchor ordering; we measure WHEN the joint answer stops changing across denoising steps and use that decode-time readout to set a per-instance step budget, leaving the backbone and training untouched."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:9ccbb820261b9141e46de121ed26ae3e3b16772b","delta":"MEDAL steers decoding with expensive MCTS rollout value estimates; we supply a cheap label-free determinacy estimator d_t (one-extra-pass prefix-agreement) that certifies an already-frozen answer so search/decoding can halt rather than expand."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:c3f18504c770549771b29c222db41b343dd1f36d","delta":"EDLM adds a uniform sequence-level energy correction at every step to fix few-step quality; we do not modify the per-step objective at all and instead measure cross-step answer stability to decide per-instance when to stop, treating the schedule rather than the energy as the free variable."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:410d8f0451384237b054b3f06cd8eab1c9f72104","what_step_was_missed":"Their HMM analysis establishes that exact-sequence correctness needs many more steps than near-optimal perplexity, but it stops at a worst-case statement over the model class; to reach our contribution they would have needed to construct a per-instance, decode-time measurement primitive — the frozen-decode probe that extracts hypothesis answer a_t at each step and defines the answer-freeze step t_freeze with the fully-decoded output as a model-internal oracle — and then show empirically that t_freeze diverges from the confidence-saturation step. That measurement construction (not a tighter bound) is the missing step."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":331,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"Layer 1 hard floor did not fire: gap_closure_reject_check has no entry whose aggregate is a clean documented Reject with the framing fixed (the one yes-lesson is a function of Leg B's framing, addressable by re-scoping, not an intrinsic Reject of the diagnostic), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat is NOT exact-mechanism overlap (Prophet measures neither the confidence-vs-determinacy divergence nor the permutation-controlled causal identification). Layer 2 chooses revise because paper_pointed_threat.subsumption_argument is real and addressable_via names specific candidate fields (hook / core_mechanism framing / differentiation_from_lit / almost_prior / what_step_was_missed), and recipe_application_check.entries[1].verdict = borderline on a load-bearing property (Leg B must stop competing as an accelerator and instead validate the diagnostic). The revision re-centers the headline on the C02 confound-isolating measurement and demotes the C23 schedule leg to a validation harness; kill-switch fields (falsification_prediction, compute_budget) are preserved byte-identical because they already carry the determinacy-vs-confidence distinguisher and permutation control that survive the re-scope.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides a per-instance, decode-time quantity that certifies when a masked diffusion LM's answer has stopped changing across denoising steps, so the model cannot recognize a prompt whose answer is already settled and is forced to spend the full worst-case step budget on it (additive: the missing outcome is an answer-settled readout, not any one mechanism for producing it).","main_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail when the constructed instrument isolates the confound only inside an artificial regime and never shows the signal transfers to real deployment, or when the diagnostic is circular (validated against the same population it interrogates), or when it re-derives an already-documented limitation and surfaces nothing previously unmeasurable.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A diagnostic that only re-confirms a shortcut already known in advance, surfacing no previously unmeasurable failure, is read as confirmatory rather than as a contribution.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"Collision paper Prophet (semanticscholar:b7b95b60) already documents 'early answer convergence' (97%/99% correct at half steps on GSM8K/MMLU), so the bare existence of an early-freeze step is no longer previously-unmeasurable — the candidate must surface the NEW measured object (the confidence-vs-determinacy DIVERGENCE under a permutation control) to escape confirmatory reading."},{"lesson_quoted":"Building the instrument around one contested definition of the target property means it cannot independently confirm that the definition is correct, and reviewers flag the resulting circularity.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The oracle for t_freeze is the fully-decoded output x_0 (construction-derived, independent of the determinacy estimator d_t), and correctness is scored against external gold answers, so the ground truth is not the evaluand judging itself."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a synthetic-ground-truth instrument only on synthetic data, without demonstrating that the controlled finding transfers to real-world instances, leaves ecological validity unestablished and undermines the central claim.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Instances are real benchmark prompts (GSM8K, MMLU, a generation set), not synthetic templates, and the liberated-schedule decoder is evaluated in the real decode loop, so the synthetic-to-real gap does not arise."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pairing a single-task or small-sample instrument with broad capability claims triggers a scope-mismatch rejection, and assembling retrieval or engineering blocks without an isolating scientific insight reads as application rather than research.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Claims are scoped to answer-bearing tasks across at least three datasets, and the isolating insight (confound = per-step confidence vs true property = cross-step answer stability) is explicit rather than an engineering assembly."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf exploits the gap between when the answer is internally determined and when decoding terminates to reallocate the remaining compute to the still-uncertain prompts or positions, so all prompts and all positions are treated as equally hard for the full budget (additive: the missing outcome is per-instance/per-position compute reallocation driven by determinacy, mechanism left open).","main_pattern":"generative_process_redesign","sub_pattern":"C23 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is treating 'I re-specified component X' as self-evident novelty with a single local swap that neither re-derives the chain nor demonstrates a regime the dominant accelerated alternative cannot reach, and that fails to beat or even compare against the strongest existing fast-sampling method.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A single local swap is made that is locally reasonable but neither re-derives the chain nor demonstrates a regime the dominant accelerated alternative cannot already reach.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"Leg B halts on a determinacy estimate and reallocates steps, and the dominant accelerated alternatives now retrieved (Prophet's early-commit, SchED's progress-aware confidence early-exit, 'Just on Time' per-token freezing) reach a similar efficiency regime via convergence/confidence signals; this only triggers the lesson if Leg B is framed as a competing accelerator, so it is borderline and addressable by re-scoping Leg B to a causal-validation harness for the diagnostic rather than a speed contender."},{"lesson_quoted":"The claimed efficiency silently leans on an extra resource (access to a dynamics model or simulator, a separately trained auxiliary network) whose cost cancels the advertised gain.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The estimator d_t is one extra forward pass per step with no trained auxiliary network, and the cost is accounted in the NFE comparison, so there is no hidden resource."},{"lesson_quoted":"The absent load-bearing justification: no theoretical statement, no failure-regime analysis, leaving the redesign indistinguishable from recombining known parts.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The candidate has a falsifiable mechanism distinguisher (the permutation negative control) but no analysis of the specific regime where confidence-based accelerators FAIL but determinacy-based halting succeeds, which is exactly what would separate it from the recombination reading."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The generative_process_redesign / C23 entry's lesson 'a single local swap ... neither re-derives the chain nor demonstrates a regime the dominant accelerated alternative cannot already reach' is candidate_match: borderline (NOT yes): the newly-retrieved collision pool (Prophet, SchED, Just-on-Time) occupies the early-stopping efficiency regime that Leg B targets ONLY under Leg B's standalone-accelerator framing, and that framing is addressable by demoting Leg B to a within-paper validation harness for the diagnostic (which is the headline) rather than a competing accelerator. Because the concern is a fixable framing of a non-headline leg and the oracle/ecological-validity lessons are clean, no documented Reject pattern is intrinsically matched, so the aggregate is borderline (revise), not triggered (abandon)."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides a per-instance, decode-time quantity that certifies when a masked diffusion LM's answer has stopped changing across denoising steps...","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Construct a controlled set of instances in which exactly one named confound is structurally blocked or independently varied, then report the divergence between apparent and de-confounded performance as the primary result, with a load-bearing oracle independent of the system under test.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism names the confound (per-step marginal token confidence c_t), constructs the frozen-decode probe that holds the prompt fixed while isolating cross-step answer stability, and reports the determinacy gap g = t_stop_conf - t_freeze plus correctness-at-t_freeze vs correctness-at-t_stop_conf as the headline divergence, with x_0 as the independent oracle — this performs the C02 signature move.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf exploits the gap between when the answer is internally determined and when decoding terminates to reallocate the remaining compute...","sub_pattern":"C23 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Reach inside an iterative refinement chain and re-specify one conventionally-frozen internal component (here the noise/solver schedule), licensed by a structural property of the task, re-deriving the chain around the new choice.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism re-specifies the fixed K-step schedule as a per-instance stopping rule driven by d_t, licensed by the answer-determinacy property; the C23 signature move (re-specify the schedule) is present, but the cluster's required step-5 self-audit (beat the STRONGEST existing accelerator) is not met against the retrieved Prophet/SchED.","verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"C02 is fully applied (named confound, controlled instances, divergence-as-headline, independent oracle). C23's re-specification move is present but borderline because the cluster card demands beating the dominant accelerator, which the retrieved collision pool shows is not yet established."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["controlled_diagnostic_design","generative_process_redesign"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"Neither main_pattern is heterogeneous_decomposition, so none of the three documented reject-favored compositions (all of which require heterogeneous_decomposition) can match."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:b7b95b60ed78916950ae670cbf90bb5081112c38","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"Prophet ('Diffusion Language Models Know the Answer Before Decoding', 2025-08) already establishes the EARLY-ANSWER-CONVERGENCE phenomenon (the correct answer is internally identified by half the steps; up to 97%/99% of GSM8K/MMLU instances decode correctly at half budget) AND ships a training-free early-commit fast-decoding paradigm (Prophet) that acts on it. This subsumes the candidate's phenomenon discovery and substantially subsumes the application Leg B (early stop + reallocate). The candidate stands or falls on whether its surviving contribution is genuinely distinct: Prophet (and siblings SchED semanticscholar:87f5382f, Just-on-Time arxiv:2602.11133, When-Confidence-Misleads semanticscholar:c0f18d5e) commit/halt on convergence or confidence heuristics but do NOT construct a confound-isolating diagnostic that MEASURES the divergence between per-step confidence saturation and cross-step answer determinacy, nor do they supply a non-tautological falsifier (the position-permutation negative control on the determinacy signal d_t whose predicted effect is the downstream task accuracy). The candidate falls if its headline remains 'answer freezes early + stop early' (scooped); it stands if the headline becomes the confound-isolation measurement plus the causal identification that answer-determinacy, not confidence, is the signal that governs needed step count.","addressable_via":"Re-scope the candidate so the load-bearing contribution is the confound-isolating diagnostic (the measured confidence-vs-determinacy divergence with the permutation negative control and the d_t-only positive control), explicitly citing Prophet/SchED as the early-commit prior whose confidence/convergence signal the diagnostic shows is the WRONG variable, and demote Leg B to the in-paper validation harness that confirms the diagnostic causally — editing hook, core_mechanism framing, differentiation_from_lit, and almost_prior/what_step_was_missed."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"hook","issue":"paper_pointed_threat (Prophet subsumes 'answer freezes early + stop early'); gap_closure_reject_check borderline 'confirmatory' lesson","fix_direction":"Rewrite the hook so the headline claim is the confound-isolating MEASUREMENT (per-step confidence saturation and cross-step answer determinacy are DIFFERENT signals, and confidence-based early-commit decoders are stopping on the wrong one), not the existence of early convergence. Keep hook shape (a) surprising empirical reveal but make the surprise the divergence + the accuracy cost of confidence-stopping, not the early-freeze fact Prophet already reported."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","issue":"recipe_application_check.entries[1] borderline; paper_pointed_threat addressable_via","fix_direction":"Re-frame Leg B explicitly as the in-paper VALIDATION HARNESS for the diagnostic (it exists to causally confirm d_t governs needed steps via the permutation negative control and d_t-only positive control), not as a standalone accelerator competing with Prophet/SchED/Just-on-Time. State that the comparison vs the strongest accelerator is for CAUSAL ATTRIBUTION (does the determinacy signal, not confidence, carry the savings) rather than a speed leaderboard. Do not touch falsification_prediction or compute_budget."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat: Prophet and confidence/convergence siblings not in differentiation list","fix_direction":"Add explicit differentiation entries against semanticscholar:b7b95b60 (Prophet: they observe early convergence and commit early on it; we MEASURE the confidence-vs-determinacy divergence and causally identify which signal governs step count via a permutation control) and against semanticscholar:87f5382f (SchED: aggregates logit margins to early-exit on a confidence threshold; we show that confidence threshold stops on the confounded signal and lose accuracy exactly when the answer is determined but confidence is not)."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"almost_prior_paper_id","issue":"paper_pointed_threat: the structurally closest paper is now Prophet, not the HMM-limit paper","fix_direction":"Change almost_prior_paper_id to semanticscholar:b7b95b60ed78916950ae670cbf90bb5081112c38 (Prophet) as the structurally closest paper."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"what_step_was_missed","issue":"paper_pointed_threat: must name the substantive step Prophet missed","fix_direction":"Rewrite to name Prophet's missed substantive step: they observed early answer convergence and built an early-commit decoder, but never constructed the confound-isolating instrument that separates per-step marginal confidence from cross-step answer determinacy, and never ran the position-permutation negative control that causally identifies determinacy (not confidence) as the variable governing needed denoising steps — that measurement-and-identification construction is the missing step."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"hook","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Headline reframed from 'answer freezes early + stop early' (scooped by Prophet) to the confound-isolating claim that per-step confidence and cross-step answer determinacy are different signals and existing early-commit decoders stop on the wrong one."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Leg B explicitly re-scoped from a competing accelerator to the in-paper causal-validation harness for the diagnostic; divergence-as-headline and the permutation/positive controls now frame the contribution as measurement-and-identification, and core_mechanism_reasoning records the avoided regression node."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added substantive deltas against Prophet (semanticscholar:b7b95b60) and SchED (semanticscholar:87f5382f) and retained the theoretical-limit / Anchored / MEDAL deltas."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"almost_prior_paper_id","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Changed structurally-closest paper to Prophet (semanticscholar:b7b95b60)."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"what_step_was_missed","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Rewritten to name Prophet's missed substantive step: the confound-isolating instrument plus the position-permutation causal identification of determinacy vs confidence."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# When the Answer Freezes: A Confound-Isolating Decode-Time Determinacy Probe for Diffusion Language Models\n\n**Method.** Answer-Settling Probe (frozen-decode probe + online estimator d_t)\n\n## Motivation\nDiffusion language models (DLMs) write text by starting from a fully masked sentence and unmasking tokens over a fixed number of refinement rounds. The problem is that a DLM often locks in its final answer well before it runs out of rounds, yet it keeps doing the same expensive work that no longer changes the answer. There is no per-prompt signal that says 'this answer is done'.\n\nRecent fast decoders noticed that answers settle early and built shortcuts on top of that observation — for example Prophet (arXiv 2025-08) commits early once the answer looks converged, and a progress-aware confidence schedule (arXiv 2025-12) exits once the model is confident enough. But all of these stop based on CONFIDENCE: how sure the model is about each individual token. Confidence and 'the answer has stopped changing' are not the same thing — the model can be unsure about a single word while the actual answer is already fixed, or sure about words while the answer is still flipping. Nobody has separated these two signals and measured how far apart they are.\n\nNow is the right time because open DLM checkpoints can be decoded step by step for free, so we can probe the model at every round without retraining anything. Prior work stopped short for a simple reason: their goal was a faster decoder, so they treated early convergence as a handy heuristic instead of asking whether the signal they stop on (confidence) is actually the right one (answer-determinacy).\n\nIf we close this gap, the field gets a cheap, label-free certificate that an answer is locked in. That turns a known worst-case efficiency limit into an actionable per-prompt 'stop now' rule, gives early-commit decoders a measured and causally-validated signal instead of a confidence guess, and lets search-based decoders skip prompts whose answer is already decided.\n\n## Method\n### Confound-Isolating Diagnostic (Leg A)\n*Measures the divergence between per-step confidence and cross-step answer determinacy and reports the accuracy lost by stopping on confidence — the headline contribution.*\n\n1. Take an existing masked diffusion language model (a model that fills in masked words over several refinement rounds) and add hooks to its decoding loop so that at every round you can read the partly-filled sentence and the model's probability for each position. For each position that belongs to the answer, record its confidence — the single largest probability the model assigns at that position. Decide which positions are 'the answer' per task: for GSM8K (grade-school math word problems) use the final number after the '####' marker, for MMLU (a multiple-choice exam benchmark) use the one option-letter slot, and for free-form generation use the whole output. Do not change any weights or the number of rounds.\n\n*The per-position marginal token confidence $c_{t}(i):$ the max over the vocabulary of the model's probability for position i given the partially unmasked state $x_{t}.$ This is the confounded signal existing decoders read.*\n$$ c_t(i) = \\max_{v} p_\\theta\\!\\left(x_i = v \\mid x_t\\right) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: You first have to expose the very signal everyone stops on — confidence — so you can later show it is the wrong one.\n2. At every round, make a throwaway copy of the current state and do one extra forward pass that greedily (always taking the single most likely token) fills in ALL the positions that are still masked, giving you a complete 'guess sentence' for that round. This copy is read-only — it never changes the real decoding. Then run a fixed parser on the guess sentence to pull out just the answer: for GSM8K, take the last number after '####' and normalize it (remove commas, drop a trailing '.0'); for MMLU, take the chosen option letter; for free-form generation, take the answer tokens. Two rounds 'have the same answer' only when these cleaned-up answers are exactly identical.\n   - _Why_: This lets you watch the answer the model WOULD give at every round, independent of how confident it is about individual tokens.\n3. Let the decoding finish to get the final answer, then find the answer-freeze round: the earliest round after which the per-round guess answer matches the final answer and stays matching for every remaining round. Use the very same answer parser as before on both the per-round guesses and the final output. If a prompt's guess answer never settles onto the final answer, record its freeze round as the last round and mark it as 'never froze' so you can report those separately. The final fully-decoded output is the reference, so this measurement uses only the model's own output and judges nothing against itself.\n\n*The answer-freeze step $t_{freeze}:$ the smallest step t after which the answer span of every probed hypothesis $h_{t}'$ equals the answer span of the fully decoded output $x_{0}.$ The fully decoded $x_{0}$ is the model-internal oracle.*\n$$ t_{\\mathrm{freeze}} = \\min\\Big\\{\\, t : \\mathrm{ans}(h_{t'}) = \\mathrm{ans}(x_0)\\ \\ \\forall\\, t' \\ge t \\,\\Big\\} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: $t_{freeze}$ is the missing per-prompt quantity that says exactly when the answer locked in, using only the model's own output as the reference.\n4. Now find, for a range of confidence cutoffs (from 0.5 up to 0.99), the round at which a standard confidence rule would have stopped: the first round where every answer position is at least as confident as the cutoff. Compare that stop-round to the answer-freeze round to get the 'wasted rounds' gap, and score accuracy if you stop at the freeze round versus at the confidence stop-round, on GSM8K, MMLU, and the generation set. This gives the headline table showing how many rounds confidence wastes and how much accuracy confidence-stopping loses on prompts whose answer was already fixed. Which single cutoff you report as 'the' confidence rule should be the one a real decoder would pick to keep accuracy near the target. 【author decision: which confidence cutoff is reported as the representative rule — a fixed default or one tuned per task to a retention target — is a choice about how strict the rule should be.】 The gold answer is used only to grade correctness, not to define the freeze round.\n\n*The determinacy gap g between the confidence-stop step (smallest t at which every answer-span position i in S reaches confidence threshold tau) and the answer-freeze step. A positive, large g is the headline measured divergence.*\n$$ g = t_{\\mathrm{stop\\text{-}conf}} - t_{\\mathrm{freeze}}, \\qquad t_{\\mathrm{stop\\text{-}conf}} = \\min\\Big\\{\\, t : \\min_{i \\in S} c_t(i) \\ge \\tau \\,\\Big\\} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This is the headline result: it shows how many rounds confidence wastes and how much accuracy confidence-stopping loses on prompts whose answer was already fixed.\n\n### Online Determinacy Estimator and Liberated Schedule (Leg B)\n*Turns the diagnostic into a label-free per-instance stopping signal $d_{t}$ and a decoder that reallocates compute by determinacy.*\n\n5. Build a cheap signal you can compute live without knowing the final answer: $d_{t}$ is the fraction of answer positions whose top token stayed the same as the previous round, averaged over the last w rounds. Tune two knobs — the window length w and the agreement threshold delta (how close to full agreement counts as 'settled') — on a held-out set kept separate from the test prompts. Try window lengths of 2, 3, 5, 8 rounds and thresholds of 0.9, 0.95, 0.98, 1.0; for each combination, the rule halts a prompt the first time $d_{t}$ stays above delta for w rounds in a row. Pick the combination that almost never halts before the true freeze round yet halts as early as possible after it. 【author decision: exactly how to trade off 'never stop too early' against 'stop as soon as possible' — a hard never-early floor versus a weighted score — is a safety-versus-savings choice for the authors.】\n   - _Why_: You need a signal you can compute live without knowing the final answer; $d_{t}$ is that deployable stand-in for $t_{freeze}.$\n6. Make a decoder that runs a whole batch of prompts together and keeps a flag for which prompts are still active. Each round, do a forward pass only for the still-active prompts (skip the frozen ones so they cost nothing), advance them one round, and recompute their settle-signal $d_{t}.$ As soon as a prompt's $d_{t}$ has stayed above the agreement threshold for the chosen number of rounds, freeze it and save whatever it currently holds as its final answer. Keep going until every prompt is frozen or you hit the maximum number of rounds. The total work is just the sum, over rounds, of how many prompts were still active — so easy prompts that freeze early free up compute for the hard ones.\n\n*The label-free online estimator $d_{t}:$ the fraction of answer-span positions whose argmax token agrees between consecutive hypotheses, averaged over a sliding window of w steps. It is a model-internal surrogate for the answer having stopped changing.*\n$$ d_t = \\frac{1}{w} \\sum_{s=0}^{w-1} \\frac{1}{|S|} \\sum_{i \\in S} \\mathbf{1}\\!\\left[\\arg\\max h_{t-s}(i) = \\arg\\max h_{t-s-1}(i)\\right] \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Instead of giving every prompt the same fixed number of rounds, you spend rounds where they are still needed — driven by the measured signal, not a fixed cut.\n\n### Causal-Attribution Harness\n*Permutation negative control and $d_{t}-only$ positive control that causally identify answer-determinacy, not confidence, as the governing variable.*\n\n7. Run a control that scrambles the settle-signal: for each prompt, pick one random reshuffling of the answer-position indices and keep it fixed for that prompt, then compute the same agreement statistic but comparing each position now against a different, shuffled position from the previous round. This keeps the overall 'how often tokens agree' numbers the same while breaking the real link between a position and its own history, so it removes the genuine answer-settling information. Re-run the same adaptive decoder driven by this scrambled signal at the same average compute, and average over several random reshufflings. If accuracy drops to the plain fixed-cut level, the real answer information in the signal — not its surface statistics — is what carried the benefit.\n   - _Why_: If accuracy collapses to the fixed-cut baseline under shuffling, that proves the answer-determinacy content of $d_{t}$ — not just its general statistics — is what carries the benefit.\n8. Run a stripped-down version of the decoder that decides when to stop using only the settle-signal $d_{t},$ with the confidence channel switched off entirely. Compare three decoders on accuracy versus total compute: this signal-only one, the full decoder that runs every prompt for all rounds, and a fixed-cut baseline that gives every prompt the same number of rounds — set so its total compute equals the adaptive decoder's average. Matching the compute matters: it means any accuracy difference comes from spending rounds where they are needed, not from spending fewer rounds overall. If the signal-only decoder keeps almost all the accuracy while cutting compute, it shows answer-settling — not confidence — is what decides how many rounds a prompt needs.\n   - _Why_: If $d_{t}$ alone recovers most of the savings at almost full accuracy, it constructively proves answer-determinacy — not confidence — governs how many rounds a prompt needs.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 当答案冻结之时：面向扩散语言模型的一个去混淆解码期确定性探针\n\n**方法名称.** Answer-Settling Probe (frozen-decode probe + online estimator d_t)\n\n## 研究动机\n扩散语言模型（DLM）生成文本的方式是：从一个全部被 mask 的句子出发，在固定轮数的细化中逐步去 mask。问题在于：DLM 往往在还没用完轮数之前就已经锁定了最终答案，却仍然继续做那些不再改变答案的昂贵计算。它没有一个逐 prompt 的信号来告诉自己“这个答案已经定了”。\n\n最近的快速解码器注意到答案会很早稳定，并据此搭建了捷径——比如 Prophet（arXiv 2025-08）在答案看起来收敛后就提前 commit，进度感知的置信调度（arXiv 2025-12）在模型足够自信时就提前退出。但这些方法都是基于置信度（confidence）停止的：即模型对每个单独 token 有多确定。置信度与“答案已停止变化”并不是一回事——模型可能对某个词不确定，但实际答案已经固定；也可能对词很确定，但答案还在反复翻转。迄今没有人把这两个信号分开，并测量它们到底差多远。\n\n现在正是时候，因为开源 DLM checkpoint 可以免费地逐步解码，所以我们能在每一轮探测模型而无需重训任何东西。以前的工作止步于此原因很简单：它们的目标是更快的解码器，所以把早期收敛当作一个好用的启发式，而不是去追问他们所依据停止的信号（置信度）是否真的是正确的那个（答案确定性）。\n\n如果补上这个缺口，领域就能获得一个便宜、无标签的“答案已锁定”证书。这把一个已知的最坏情况效率上限变成了逐 prompt 可执行的“现在停”规则，给早期 commit 的解码器一个被测量、被因果验证过的信号来代替置信度猜测，也让基于搜索的解码器跳过答案已经决定的 prompt。\n\n## 方法\n### 去混淆诊断（Leg A）\n*测量逐步置信与跨步答案确定性之间的发散，并报告按置信停止所损失的准确率——核心贡献。*\n\n1. 拿一个现成的 masked diffusion language model（一种在若干轮细化中逐步填充被遮盖词的模型），给它的解码循环加上 hook，使你在每一轮都能读到部分填充的句子以及模型对每个位置的概率。对属于答案的每个位置，记录它的置信度——即模型在该位置赋予的最大概率。按任务确定哪些位置算“答案”：GSM8K(Grade School Math 8K，小学数学应用题)用『####』标记之后的最终数字，MMLU(Massive Multitask Language Understanding，多任务选择题基准)用那一个选项字母槽位，自由生成则用整段输出。不改任何权重，也不改轮数。\n\n*逐位置的边缘 token 置信度 $c_{t}(i)$：在给定部分解码状态 $x_{t}$ 的条件下，模型对位置 i 取词表上的最大概率。这就是现有解码器所读取的被混淆信号。*\n$$ c_t(i) = \\max_{v} p_\\theta\\!\\left(x_i = v \\mid x_t\\right) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 你得先把大家所依据停止的信号——confidence——暴露出来，才能后面证明它是错的那个。\n2. 每一轮都对当前状态做一份临时拷贝，并多做一次前向，用贪婪方式（每个位置都取最可能的那个 token）把所有仍被 mask 的位置都填上，得到该轮一个完整的“猜测句子” $h_{t}$。这份拷贝是只读的——它绝不改动真正的解码。然后对猜测句子跑一个固定的解析器，只抽出答案：GSM8K 取『####』后的最后一个数字并归一化(去掉逗号、去掉结尾的『.0』)，MMLU 取所选的选项字母，自由生成则取答案 token。只有当这些清理后的答案完全一致时，两轮才算“答案相同”。\n   - _为什么_: 这让你能在每一轮观察模型“会给出”的答案，与它对单个 token 的置信度无关。\n3. 让解码跑到底得到最终答案 $x_{0}$，然后找出答案冻结轮：使得从该轮起、每一轮的猜测答案都等于最终答案且此后不再改变的最早一轮。对每轮猜测和最终输出，都用前面完全相同的答案解析器。如果某个 prompt 的猜测答案始终没有稳定到最终答案上，就把它的冻结轮记为最后一轮，并标记为“从未冻结”，以便单独报告。完全解码的输出作为参照，因此这一度量只用模型自身的输出，不会自己评判自己。\n\n*答案冻结步 $t_{freeze}$：使得从步 t 起、每个被探测假设 $h_{t}'$ 的答案 span 都等于完全解码输出 $x_{0}$ 的答案 span 的最小步。完全解码的 $x_{0}$ 作为模型内部的 oracle。*\n$$ t_{\\mathrm{freeze}} = \\min\\Big\\{\\, t : \\mathrm{ans}(h_{t'}) = \\mathrm{ans}(x_0)\\ \\ \\forall\\, t' \\ge t \\,\\Big\\} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: $t_{freeze}$ 就是那个缺失的逐 prompt 量，它只用模型自己的输出作参照，准确说出答案何时锁定。\n4. 现在，对一组置信阈值(从 0.5 到 0.99)，找出标准置信规则会停止的那一轮：即所有答案位置的置信度都达到该阈值的第一轮。把这个停止轮与答案冻结轮相比得到“浪费轮数”间隙，并在 GSM8K、MMLU 和生成集上对比在冻结轮停与在置信停止轮停的准确率。这给出核心表格，显示置信停止浪费了多少轮，以及在答案已固定的 prompt 上置信停止损失了多少准确率。你作为代表上报的那一个置信阈值，应是真实解码器为把准确率维持在目标附近会选的那个。【作者需决定：作为代表规则上报的置信阈值——是固定默认值，还是按任务调到某个保留率目标——这是关于规则应当多严格的选择。】金标答案只用于评判正确性，不用于定义冻结轮。\n\n*确定性间隙 g，即置信停止步（使所有答案 span 位置 $i\\in S$ 都达到置信阈值 $\\tau $ 的最小 t）与答案冻结步之差。一个为正且较大的 g 就是作为核心结果报告的发散。*\n$$ g = t_{\\mathrm{stop\\text{-}conf}} - t_{\\mathrm{freeze}}, \\qquad t_{\\mathrm{stop\\text{-}conf}} = \\min\\Big\\{\\, t : \\min_{i \\in S} c_t(i) \\ge \\tau \\,\\Big\\} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这是核心结果：它显示置信停止浪费了多少轮，以及在答案已固定的 prompt 上置信停止损失了多少准确率。\n\n### 在线确定性估计与解放调度（Leg B）\n*把诊断变成无标签的逐实例停止信号 $d_{t}$ 以及一个按确定性重新分配计算的解码器。*\n\n5. 构建一个无需知道最终答案、可实时计算的便宜信号：$d_{t}$ 是答案位置中顶部 token 与上一轮保持一致的比例，在最近 w 轮上取平均。在一个与测试 prompt 分开的留出集上调两个旋钮——窗口长度 w 和一致阈值 delta(即多接近完全一致才算“已稳定”)。窗口长度试 2、3、5、8 轮，阈值试 0.9、0.95、0.98、1.0；对每个组合，该规则在 $d_{t}$ 连续 w 轮高于 delta 时第一次停止某 prompt。挑选那个几乎从不在真正的冻结轮之前停止、但又在冻结后尽可能早停止的组合。【作者需决定：到底如何在“绝不过早停止”与“尽早停止”之间权衡——是设一个硬性的不过早下限，还是用一个加权得分——这是作者在安全性与节省之间的选择。】\n   - _为什么_: 你需要一个无需知道最终答案、可实时计算的信号；$d_{t}$ 就是 $t_{freeze}$ 的可部署替身。\n6. 做一个把整批 prompt 一起运行的解码器，并为每个 prompt 维护一个“是否仍活跃”的标志。每一轮只对仍活跃的 prompt 做前向(跳过已冻结的，使其不耗费算力)，让它们前进一轮，并重新计算其稳定信号 $d_{t}$。一旦某个 prompt 的 $d_{t}$ 连续保持在一致阈值之上达到所选轮数，就冻结它，并把它当前持有的内容存为最终答案。一直进行，直到每个 prompt 都被冻结或达到最大轮数。总算力就是各轮中仍活跃 prompt 数量之和——所以早冻结的简单 prompt 会把算力让给困难的那些。\n\n*无标签的在线估计量 $d_{t}$：在宽度为 w 的滑动窗口内，答案 span 位置上相邻假设间 argmax token 一致的比例均值。它是“答案已停止变化”的模型内部代理量。*\n$$ d_t = \\frac{1}{w} \\sum_{s=0}^{w-1} \\frac{1}{|S|} \\sum_{i \\in S} \\mathbf{1}\\!\\left[\\arg\\max h_{t-s}(i) = \\arg\\max h_{t-s-1}(i)\\right] \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 不再给每个 prompt 相同的固定轮数，而是把轮数花在仍需要的地方——由被测量的信号驱动，而不是固定切断。\n\n### 因果归因验证架\n*置换负控制与仅 $d_{t}$ 的正控制，因果地识别出是答案确定性而非置信是主导变量。*\n\n7. 运行一个把稳定信号打乱的对照：对每个 prompt 随机选一个答案位置索引的重排并对该 prompt 固定不变，然后计算相同的一致性统计量，但现在把每个位置与上一轮中一个不同的、被打乱的位置相比。这保持了总体“token 多久一致一次”的数值不变，却破坏了一个位置与其自身历史之间的真实联系，从而抹去了真正的答案稳定信息。用这个被打乱的信号、在相同平均算力下重跑同一自适应解码器，并对若干次随机重排取平均。如果准确率跌到普通固定切断的水平，那就说明是信号中真实的答案信息——而非其表面统计——带来了好处。\n   - _为什么_: 如果打乱后准确率跌到固定切断基线，就证明是 $d_{t}$ 的答案确定性内容——而非它的一般统计——在起作用。\n8. 运行一个精简版解码器，只用稳定信号 $d_{t}$ 决定何时停止，并把置信通道完全关闭。在准确率对比总算力上比较三个解码器：这个只用信号的版本、对每个 prompt 跑满所有轮数的完整版本、以及给每个 prompt 相同轮数的固定切断基线——其总算力设为与自适应解码器的平均算力相等。算力对齐很重要：它意味着任何准确率差异都来自“把轮数花在需要的地方”，而不是来自总体上少花轮数。如果只用信号的解码器在削减算力的同时几乎保住全部准确率，就表明是答案稳定——而非置信——决定了一个 prompt 需要多少轮。\n   - _为什么_: 如果单靠 $d_{t}$ 就能在几乎不损准确率的情况下收回大部分节省，它就建设性地证明是答案确定性——而非置信——决定了 prompt 需要多少轮。\n\n"},{"id":"29","run_dir":"run_prompt29_genpolicy","index":29,"title":"Reward-Tilted Velocity Matching: Online RL for Flow Policies Without a Likelihood Ratio","title_zh":"奖励倾斜的速度匹配（Reward-Tilted Velocity Matching）：无需似然比的 flow 策略在线强化学习","method_name":"Reward-Tilted Velocity Matching (RTVM)","hook":"Every online flow/diffusion-policy method (FlowRL, FPO) substitutes the intractable likelihood-ratio policy gradient with an imitation-flavored surrogate, tacitly assuming online improvement must be a (log-)likelihood-ratio-weighted ascent on the policy density. We show that the exact gradient of expected return through a flow policy equals a plain conditional-flow-matching regression onto an advantage-tilted target velocity — no likelihood ratio anywhere — and that folding a visitation-dispersion term into the same tilt yields online improvement pressure toward action modes the policy does not yet sample.","anchor_pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","anchor_pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","domain_category":"Reinforcement Learning","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions whether online improvement of a generative policy must be expressed as a gradient on the policy's intractable likelihood at all — every leaf inherits from the policy-gradient ancestor the assumption that improvement is a (log-)likelihood-ratio-weighted update, and none tests whether the reward-conditioned improvement could instead be expressed through a quantity the flow/diffusion model exposes natively (its velocity / score field, its denoising path) without ever fo","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C29 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"architectural_operator_substitution","how_closed":"Framing move (audit-and-pivot): the policy-gradient guarantee silently assumes the update is a score-function estimator E[A·∇log π(a|s)] whose ∇log π is intractable for a flow policy; we pivot the convergence primitive to a velocity-matching target — the exact ∇_θ E[return] is re-derived as a conditional-flow-matching regression of the policy's velocity field onto an advantage-tilted target velocity, with no likelihood-ratio term. Companion deliverable (architectural_operator_substitution): that re-derivation ships as a runnable single-stage online RL operator — replace the intractable likelihood-ratio gradient with the tilted-velocity CFM regression loss, dropping the importance-sampling / elite-alignment machinery entirely.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf supplies online improvement pressure toward action modes the current generative policy does not yet sample: every method's signal is anchored to actions the policy (or an elite buffer) has already produced, so the multimodal coverage that justifies using a generative policy is preserved only by the model class or an external diversity penalty, never produced by the policy-improvement objective itself, and it decays as online updating concentrates mass.","pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","sub_pattern":"C23 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by liberating a conventionally-fixed internal component of the flow chain — the target velocity that the per-step regression aims at — and re-specifying it to carry a visitation-dispersion term: the same advantage-tilted target velocity is additionally tilted by a state-action novelty weight computed from the flow's own support density, so the velocity-matching objective itself transports probability toward under-sampled high-uncertainty modes rather than relying on an external entropy/diversity penalty.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"online reinforcement learning with expressive generative (diffusion / flow-matching) policies for continuous control","n_papers":40,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":26},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":8,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"GTA: Generative Trajectory Augmentation with Guidance for Offline Reinforcement Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Constrained Latent Action Policies for Model-Based Offline Reinforcement Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Solving Motion Planning Tasks with a Scalable Generative Model"},{"source":"openalex","title":"A Comprehensive Review of Deep Learning: Architectures, Recent Advances, and Applications"},{"source":"openalex","title":"When large language models meet personalization: perspectives of challenges and opportunities"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Optimizing reinforcement learning for large action spaces via generative models: Battery pattern selection"}],"more":2},{"year":2025,"n":31,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Flow-Based Policy for Online Reinforcement Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A Bit of Freedom Goes a Long Way: Classical and Quantum Algorithms for Reinforcement Learning under a Generative Model"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"ORVIT: Near-Optimal Online Distributionally Robust Reinforcement Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Generative Reinforcement Learning for Multimodal Trajectory Planning in Autonomous Driving"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Expressive Value Learning for Scalable Offline Reinforcement Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Safe, Efficient, and Robust Reinforcement Learning for Ranking and Diffusion Models"}],"more":25},{"year":2026,"n":1,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"}],"more":0}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":15,"share":0.375},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":10,"share":0.25},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":9,"share":0.225},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":9,"share":0.225},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":4,"share":0.1},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":3,"share":0.075},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":3,"share":0.075},{"pattern_id":"algebraic_equivalence_unification","pattern_name":"Prove Equivalence to Unify","count":3,"share":0.075}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"When an expressive generative model (diffusion or flow matching) is used as the *online* policy, the quantity online policy improvement actually needs — a reward-weighted gradient of the action distribution the policy is currently sampling — is not available, because the generative policy's action density is defined only implicitly through an ODE/SDE integration and has no closed-form log-likelihood to differentiate. Every retrieved method that puts a flow/diffusion model online therefore replaces the missing on-policy gradient with an imitation-flavored surrogate computed against a data target rather than against the policy's own visitation: FlowRL (semanticscholar:8efe46a3a3e8d55ed331a6aed6c3d9ae98874791) aligns the velocity field to *elite historical actions* under a Wasserstein-2 constraint, and Flow Matching Policy Gradients / FPO (openalex:W7077063683) maximize an advantage-weighted conditional-flow-matching ratio that re-uses the imitation loss as a stand-in for the intractable likelihood ratio. The failure this creates is twofold and concrete: (a) the surrogate's directional agreement with the true reward gradient is never measured, so when the surrogate and the true gradient diverge — precisely on stochastic / multimodal tasks where the expressive policy is supposed to win (FlowRL's own HumanoidBench / DMC-hard regime) — the update can push probability mass toward already-visited elite actions rather than toward higher-reward regions, and (b) because the surrogate is anchored to actions the policy has *already* produced, it supplies no improvement pressure toward modes the current policy does not yet sample, so the very multimodality that justifies a generative policy decays under online updating. Distributionally-robust and generative-model-assisted online RL theory (semanticscholar:d0d2ad12fbd98afd1da2f9736bf2a4e13060f532, semanticscholar:1cd5cba4cac816a354fd3c31ff442ccc8e937c96) sidesteps the issue entirely by staying in the tabular / simulator-access regime and never touches an expressive parametric policy class.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:8efe46a3a3e8d55ed331a6aed6c3d9ae98874791","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"FlowRL parameterizes the online policy as a flow model (a state-action-time velocity field integrated over an ODE) and, to avoid the intractable distribution-matching objective, performs policy improvement by aligning the velocity field to elite historical actions under a Wasserstein-2 regularizer with implicit guidance. The residue is that its improvement signal is a behavior-cloning-toward-elites surrogate, not a measured on-policy reward gradient: it never quantifies how well the velocity-alignment direction agrees with the true reward gradient, and because it pulls toward actions already produced it gives no credit to unsampled modes, so multimodal coverage is asserted by the model class rather than maintained by the objective."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7077063683","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Flow Matching Policy Gradients (FPO) casts policy optimization as maximizing a PPO-clip-compatible advantage-weighted ratio built from the conditional-flow-matching loss, sidestepping exact likelihood computation while keeping the flow generative capability. The residue is that the CFM-loss ratio is only a proxy for the true likelihood ratio whose bias relative to the exact policy-gradient is neither bounded nor measured, and the objective is purely reward-exploitation — it carries no intrinsic term that would direct probability toward unvisited high-uncertainty regions of the flow's support."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415200532","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"This work fine-tunes diffusion policies online by backpropagating PPO-style updates through the diffusion denoising timesteps, treating each denoising step as a differentiable sub-action. The residue is that BPTT through all timesteps is memory-prohibitive and the per-step credit assignment is heuristic; it still optimizes only the reward objective and does not characterize, let alone correct, the bias introduced by truncating or reweighting the denoising chain, nor does it preserve mode coverage under the online updates."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:eab3ad76d26f72f5bbc577566b39c7860b8dc687","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"This paper reparameterizes intractable multimodal online actors (diffusion / amortized) into a more tractable form and adds a diversity regularizer to retain multimodality. The residue is that diversity is imposed by an external regularizer rather than derived from the reward-improvement objective, and the reparameterization trades exactness for tractability without measuring how far the resulting gradient sits from the true on-policy gradient — so the performance / diversity / efficiency trade-off is tuned, not characterized."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"online reinforcement learning with expressive generative (diffusion / flow-matching) policies for continuous control","venue":"ICLR / ICML / NeurIPS (Oral tier)","time":"2026","data":["DeepMind Control Suite (DMC-hard, e.g. Dog, Humanoid)","HumanoidBench","standard MuJoCo continuous-control suites"],"compute":"1×A100 × 3 months (≈ 90 A100-day)","expertise":"RL + generative modeling (diffusion / flow matching)","preference":"both","baseline":"FlowRL (online flow policy with Wasserstein-2-regularized velocity alignment); QVPO / diffusion-policy online RL; Flow Policy Optimization (FPO, advantage-weighted CFM ratio)","limitation":"online RL with a generative policy cannot compute an exact on-policy reward gradient because the policy density is intractable, so every method substitutes an imitation-flavored surrogate whose bias is unquantified and which carries no signal toward unsampled modes","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object both legs read from and write to is a single advantage-tilted target velocity field v*(t, s, a_t), defined on the flow's own interpolation path; both the reward-improvement leg and the exploration leg express themselves entirely as a modification of v*, and policy improvement is a plain conditional-flow-matching (CFM) regression of the policy's velocity v_θ(t,s,a_t) onto v*. LEG 1 (audit-and-pivot + operator). A flow policy generates an action a_1 from noise a_0 by integrating v_θ over t∈[0,1]; its density log π_θ(a_1|s) has no closed form, so the score-function policy gradient E[A(s,a)·∇_θ log π_θ(a|s)] is intractable and every prior method substitutes a surrogate for it. We pivot the convergence primitive: instead of ascending the likelihood-ratio-weighted gradient, we target the velocity that an advantage-reweighted action distribution would induce. Concretely, for a sampled transition (s,a_1) with advantage A(s,a_1) (computed by a standard critic, GAE on the online rollouts), define a per-sample tilt weight w(s,a_1) = exp(A(s,a_1)/β) (β a temperature hyperparameter, units of return; this is the only quantity bridging reward-scale to the loss). The target velocity at interpolation time t for the linear interpolant a_t = (1-t)a_0 + t a_1 is the standard CFM conditional velocity u_t(a_t|a_1) = a_1 - a_0, and the reward-improvement update is the w-weighted CFM regression L_imp(θ) = E_{(s,a_1)∼buffer, t∼U[0,1], a_0∼N(0,I)} [ w(s,a_1) · || v_θ(t,s,a_t) - (a_1-a_0) ||^2 ]. The artifact this produces is an unbiased single-stage estimator of the direction that increases exp(A/β)-weighted return density WITHOUT forming log π: minimizing L_imp moves v_θ toward generating the high-advantage actions more often, and because the weight multiplies a regression residual rather than a log-likelihood gradient, no likelihood ratio is ever computed. This closes Leg-1's gap: improvement is expressed through the velocity field the model exposes natively. LEG 2 (liberate the target velocity for exploration). The same v* is the free design variable we liberate: we add a dispersion tilt so the regression also pulls toward under-sampled modes. Define a novelty weight m(s,a_1) = 1 / (k_ρ(s,a_1) + ε), where k_ρ(s,a_1) is a kernel density estimate of the policy's OWN recent action visitation at state s (RBF kernel, bandwidth ρ, over the last N_buf sampled actions in a state-conditioned buffer; ε a small constant), so rarely-sampled actions get larger m. The liberated target tilt becomes w'(s,a_1) = exp(A(s,a_1)/β) · m(s,a_1)^λ (λ∈[0,1] an exploration coefficient), and L_imp uses w' in place of w. Because m up-weights the regression residual exactly on the modes the current policy under-samples, the velocity-matching objective itself produces transport toward unsampled high-uncertainty regions — exploration is generated by the improvement objective, not bolted on as a reward bonus (which the method_lineage regression flag c0/c1 forbids, since those assume a tractable density and live in the reward). The two legs share machinery completely: there is one loss, one target velocity, two multiplicative tilts on it. Quantitative grounding: FlowRL reports its gains on DMC-hard / HumanoidBench by aligning to elite actions under a Wasserstein-2 constraint (semanticscholar:8efe46a3...); our update has no elite buffer and no W2 term — the regime distinction is that FlowRL's improvement signal is anchored to already-produced elites whereas ours is a reward-and-novelty-tilted regression that can move mass to never-sampled actions.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) Evidence the two gaps share machinery: both the missing on-policy improvement signal and the missing unsampled-mode pressure are, at root, statements about WHICH actions the velocity field should be regressed toward — so a single target-velocity tilt (one multiplicative weight per sampled action) closes both, and splitting them into two modules would double-count the same CFM regression; the dispersion term is literally a second factor on the same per-sample weight. (b) Alternatives rejected: (i) a separate intrinsic-reward exploration head added to the critic — rejected as a regression to method_lineage collateral nodes c0/c1 (entropy/curiosity bonuses that assume a tractable density and operate in the reward); (ii) an importance-sampling correction to make the CFM-ratio match the true likelihood ratio (FPO's route, openalex:W7077063683) — rejected because it re-introduces the very likelihood-ratio object the audit removes and its bias is unbounded; (iii) backprop-through-denoising to get an exact gradient (openalex:W4415200532) — rejected as memory-prohibitive and still reward-only. Recorded avoided node: the persistent/entropy reward bonus (c0/c1) — our exploration term lives in the velocity-matching target, not the reward.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: implement reward-tilted velocity matching as the policy-improvement step inside an off-the-shelf online actor-critic on DMC-hard (Dog-run, Humanoid-stand) and HumanoidBench, using the same flow-policy architecture and rollout budget as FlowRL, and measure episodic return vs. environment steps plus final-policy mode count (number of distinct action clusters at fixed representative states via k-means on sampled actions). If the candidate works, episodic return at a fixed step budget rises to or above FlowRL/FPO on the multimodal-hard tasks AND the final-policy mode count does not collapse toward 1 over training (it stays ≥ the count of an entropy-regularized SAC baseline). The named load-bearing variable is the velocity-gradient alignment cosine κ = cos(−∇_θ L_imp, g_FD) between our tilted-velocity update direction and a finite-difference estimate of the true expected-return gradient; the mechanism claim is that the tilted-velocity update tracks the true return gradient where the likelihood-ratio surrogate does not, so κ should stay high (e.g., > 0.5) on multimodal tasks while an FPO-style CFM-ratio update's alignment is markedly lower in the same states. Negative control (anti-tautology): remove the advantage from the tilt (reward-blind weight w'≡m^λ) — this drives the DOWNSTREAM episodic return back to behavior-cloning / random-exploration level (it should NOT exceed an unguided flow policy), confirming the return gain is carried by the advantage tilt and not by the CFM regression or the novelty term alone. Positive control: the advantage-only update (λ=0, w'=exp(A/β)) recovers most of the return improvement, identifying the tilt as the sufficient mechanism for the reward-improvement leg.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:8efe46a3a3e8d55ed331a6aed6c3d9ae98874791","delta":"FlowRL improves the online flow policy by aligning its velocity field to elite historical actions under a Wasserstein-2 constraint (an imitation-toward-elites surrogate anchored to already-produced actions); we instead derive policy improvement as an advantage-tilted CFM regression with no elite buffer and no W2 term, and we add a visitation-dispersion tilt that moves probability toward never-sampled modes — a direction FlowRL's elite-anchored signal structurally cannot produce."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7077063683","delta":"FPO maximizes an advantage-weighted CFM-loss RATIO inside PPO-clip, which is an unbounded-bias proxy for the intractable likelihood ratio; we eliminate the ratio entirely — improvement is a single w'-weighted CFM regression (a target-velocity tilt, not a ratio of losses) — and we add a measurable alignment-to-true-gradient diagnostic and an intrinsic mode-seeking tilt that FPO has no analogue for."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415200532","delta":"This work backpropagates PPO updates through all diffusion denoising timesteps (memory-prohibitive, reward-only, heuristic per-step credit); our update never differentiates through the integration chain — it is a one-step regression on the conditional velocity — and explicitly preserves multimodal coverage via the dispersion tilt rather than ignoring it."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:eab3ad76d26f72f5bbc577566b39c7860b8dc687","delta":"They retain multimodality by adding an external diversity regularizer to a reparameterized tractable actor; we produce mode-seeking pressure from inside the improvement objective itself (the novelty tilt on the same target velocity), so diversity is a consequence of the update rather than a competing penalty term to be balanced."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W7077063683","what_step_was_missed":"FPO derived an advantage-weighted ratio of conditional-flow-matching losses as a PPO-compatible stand-in for the likelihood ratio, but it never constructed the advantage-TILTED TARGET VELOCITY: the step it missed is recognizing that exp(A/β) can multiply the CFM regression RESIDUAL directly to give an unbiased single-stage estimator of the reward-improvement direction without any ratio at all, and that this same target velocity is a free design variable into which a visitation-dispersion factor can be folded to generate intrinsic exploration — FPO keeps the ratio and therefore has nowhere to attach a native exploration term."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":315,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"Layer 1 hard floor does not fire: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict is borderline not triggered (no Reject lesson marked candidate_match: yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat against FPO (openalex:W7077063683) is addressable (the candidate already instruments kappa vs kappa_surrogate against an FPO-style update) rather than exact-mechanism overlap. recipe_application_check.verdict = applied for both legs, so the idea is built from the C29/C23 distinctive moves, not the parent gist. The remaining findings are borderline in supporting argument rather than load-bearing structure: the C29 'characterize when the relaxed assumption holds' lesson and the C23 'never-sampled-mode failure-regime' lesson are real but are exactly the kind of non-fatal concerns the LLM may advance with, surfaced for Phase 4 reviewer_concerns_and_responses, since the central artifact (tilted-residual CFM regression with a dispersion tilt and a measurable kappa diagnostic) is intact.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions whether online improvement of a generative policy must be expressed as a gradient on the policy's intractable likelihood at all — every leaf inherits from the policy-gradient ancestor the assumption that improvement is a (log-)likelihood-ratio-weighted update, and none tests whether the reward-conditioned improvement could instead be expressed through a quantity the flow/diffusion model exposes natively (its velocity / score field, its denoising path) without ever forming the intractable likelihood ratio.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C29 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The dominant failure shape is a relaxed assumption that is technically valid but uncharacterized — no named function or problem class is shown to satisfy it and its constants are unstudied — so reviewers read it as engineered to make the proof close; a second shape is a re-derived rate that merely matches the existing baseline with near-identical algorithmic changes, landing as an incremental extension.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A weakened assumption that no known function class is shown to satisfy reads as engineered to close the proof, not as a genuine generalization — characterize when it holds or it sinks the paper.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The pivot claims the exact return gradient equals an advantage-tilted CFM regression, but core_mechanism asserts this equality (calling L_imp an 'unbiased single-stage estimator') without exhibiting the condition under which the tilted-residual objective's gradient coincides with the true return gradient, so the regime where the reframe is exact is named only via the empirical kappa diagnostic, not characterized in derivation."},{"lesson_quoted":"Borrowing a relaxed condition from a neighboring literature without demonstrating its concrete benefit in your own setting leaves reviewers asking what the assumption actually buys.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The pivot is not borrowed from a neighboring literature; it is derived in-setting (flow-policy return gradient) and its concrete benefit — dropping importance-sampling / elite-alignment machinery and removing the likelihood ratio — is stated and tied to a measurable diagnostic."},{"lesson_quoted":"Re-deriving a rate that merely matches the baseline with near-identical algorithmic changes is read as an incremental extension, however clean the analysis.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The artifact is structurally distinct from the baselines — it removes the CFM-loss ratio FPO retains and the elite/W2 machinery FlowRL retains, replacing both with a single tilted-residual regression plus a native exploration tilt, so it is not a near-identical algorithmic change."},{"lesson_quoted":"Hidden constants that explode at the precise parameter limit where the result is advertised as strongest silently invalidate the headline guarantee, and reviewers find them in the proof.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The temperature beta and the exp(A/beta) weight can blow up the loss scale on high-advantage samples (the multimodal-hard regime the method advertises as strongest), an analogous explode-at-the-advertised-limit risk; core_mechanism names beta as the only reward-scale bridge but does not bound the weight's variance."},{"lesson_quoted":"A theorem stated without formal assumptions or a precise claim is unreviewable; 'tight, assumption-free' bounds with no exhibited assumptions are treated as not-yet-a-paper.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate is a method contribution, not a theorem-headline paper; it ships a runnable operator with controls and a falsification variable rather than advertising an assumption-free bound."},{"lesson_quoted":"An assumption-relaxation validated only on a single toy instance gives no evidence the relaxation captures the motivating practical regime.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Validation is specified on DMC-hard (Dog-run, Humanoid-stand) and HumanoidBench at FlowRL's rollout budget with seeds and controls, not a single toy instance."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf supplies online improvement pressure toward action modes the current generative policy does not yet sample: every method's signal is anchored to actions the policy (or an elite buffer) has already produced, so the multimodal coverage that justifies using a generative policy is preserved only by the model class or an external diversity penalty, never produced by the policy-improvement objective itself, and it decays as online updating concentrates mass.","main_pattern":"generative_process_redesign","sub_pattern":"C23 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is treating 'I re-specified component X' as self-evident novelty — a single local swap that is locally reasonable but neither re-derives the chain nor demonstrates a regime the dominant accelerated alternative cannot already reach; a second shape is a hidden artifact whose cost cancels the advertised gain, a third is an absent load-bearing justification leaving the redesign indistinguishable from recombining known parts.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Re-specifying the chain's starting distribution is sound but worthless if a dominant accelerator already reaches one or two steps — failing to beat the strongest fast-sampling alternative dooms the move regardless of its elegance.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"This leg targets exploration coverage, not inference-step acceleration, so the 'dominant fast-sampling accelerator' frame does not apply; the relevant strongest baseline (external diversity regularizer / entropy-SAC) is named as the comparison for mode count."},{"lesson_quoted":"Substituting one in-support approximation for another without theoretical depth or a failure-regime analysis reads as a narrow heuristic swap rather than a contribution.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The dispersion tilt m=1/(KDE+eps) on the target velocity is justified by the structural argument that up-weighting the residual on under-sampled actions transports mass there, but the claim that this produces transport toward NEVER-sampled (out-of-current-support) modes is asserted; a KDE over the policy's own recent actions has little signal exactly where the policy has never sampled, so the in-support-vs-unsampled failure regime is under-argued."},{"lesson_quoted":"A redesign that silently depends on an extra artifact — access to a simulator/dynamics model, or a separately trained auxiliary network — has its claimed efficiency cancelled by the hidden cost once a reviewer surfaces it.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The novelty weight is a non-parametric KDE over a state-conditioned action buffer the loop already stores; it introduces no separately trained auxiliary network or simulator, and the compute_budget accounts for the buffer/KDE cost within the 30 A100-day envelope."},{"lesson_quoted":"Collapsing a staged procedure into a single differentiable mapping is technically clean but gets rejected when the novelty is thin against recent methods and the gains are demonstrated only on weak or dated benchmarks.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The benchmarks are current (HumanoidBench, DMC-hard) and the novelty is the intrinsic-to-the-objective mode-seeking that the cited recent methods structurally lack, not a thin collapse of stages."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No gap_closure entry is triggered, so the aggregate is borderline. The anchor leg (assumption_audit_and_pivot, C29) drives it via 'A weakened assumption that no known function class is shown to satisfy reads as engineered to close the proof — characterize when it holds': the candidate asserts the tilted-CFM-regression-equals-true-return-gradient identity rather than characterizing the condition for the equality. The sibling leg (generative_process_redesign, C23) is borderline via 'Substituting one in-support approximation for another without ... a failure-regime analysis': the KDE-novelty tilt under-argues how it reaches modes the policy has NEVER sampled, since the density estimate is built from the policy's own recent actions."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions whether online improvement of a generative policy must be expressed as a gradient on the policy's intractable likelihood at all — every leaf inherits from the policy-gradient ancestor the assumption that improvement is a (log-)likelihood-ratio-weighted update, and none tests whether the reward-conditioned improvement could instead be expressed through a quantity the flow/diffusion model exposes natively (its velocity / score field, its denoising path) without ever forming the intractable likelihood ratio.","sub_pattern":"C29 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Take an existing convergence/regret guarantee for an iterative first-order update (including policy-gradient updates) and pivot the single load-bearing primitive the proof silently rests on — in particular 'replace the convergence primitive itself,' e.g. swap a squared-distance-to-solution measure for a direct objective-gap or a score-function target for a different update object — then re-isolate the one load-bearing identity all corollaries instantiate.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism LEG 1 performs exactly this signature move: it names the silent primitive (the policy-gradient guarantee assumes the update is the score-function estimator E[A*grad log pi] whose grad log pi is intractable for a flow policy) and pivots that convergence primitive to a velocity-matching target — re-expressing the improvement direction as a w-weighted CFM regression residual onto an advantage-tilted target velocity, with the tilt weight exp(A/beta) as the single load-bearing object both legs instantiate. This is the cluster's distinctive 'replace the convergence primitive' operation, not the parent's generic 'question an assumption.'","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf supplies online improvement pressure toward action modes the current generative policy does not yet sample: every method's signal is anchored to actions the policy (or an elite buffer) has already produced, so the multimodal coverage that justifies using a generative policy is preserved only by the model class or an external diversity penalty, never produced by the policy-improvement objective itself, and it decays as online updating concentrates mass.","sub_pattern":"C23 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Reach inside an iterative refinement (diffusion/flow) chain and re-specify one of its conventionally-frozen internal components — terminal prior, per-step distribution family, solver schedule, seed, forward kernel, or conditioning checkpoint — licensed by a structural property of the task, then re-derive the chain around the new choice.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism LEG 2 reaches inside the flow chain and re-specifies the per-step target velocity v* (the object the per-step regression aims at — a conventionally-fixed internal component, here the CFM conditional velocity a_1-a_0) by folding in a multiplicative novelty factor m^lambda, licensed by the structural property that the regression residual on under-sampled actions controls where probability is transported. The signature 'liberate a frozen internal component of the refinement chain' move is present (the target velocity is treated as the free design variable), though the re-derivation that the redesigned chain still targets the correct distribution is asserted rather than fully shown.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries instantiate their cluster's distinctive move: LEG 1 performs C29's 'replace the convergence primitive itself' (score-function target -> velocity-matching target), and LEG 2 performs C23's 'liberate a frozen internal component of the flow chain' (the per-step target velocity becomes the free design variable carrying the dispersion tilt). Neither leg merely enacts the parent pattern's generic gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["assumption_audit_and_pivot","generative_process_redesign","architectural_operator_substitution"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; none of this candidate's three 2-way subsets ({audit,gen_redesign}, {audit,op_sub}, {gen_redesign,op_sub}) contains heterogeneous_decomposition, so no anti-pattern matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"openalex:W7077063683","threat_source":"lit_table","subsumption_argument":"FPO (Flow Policy Optimization) is the almost-prior: it already brings advantage information into a conditional-flow-matching objective for an online flow policy by maximizing an advantage-weighted RATIO of CFM losses inside PPO-clip as a stand-in for the intractable likelihood ratio. The candidate's reward-improvement leg stands or falls on the claim that multiplying exp(A/beta) onto the CFM regression RESIDUAL (a target-velocity tilt) is materially different from — and better-behaved than — FPO's advantage-weighted ratio of CFM losses. If a reviewer reads the two as algebraically equivalent reparameterizations (both reduce to advantage-weighting a flow-matching quantity), the audit-and-pivot headline ('we remove the likelihood ratio') collapses into 'we drop the PPO-clip ratio denominator,' which is an incremental change rather than a reframe — exactly the C29 reject lesson about re-deriving the baseline with near-identical algorithmic changes.","addressable_via":"Strengthen falsification_prediction / core_mechanism_reasoning to make the FPO contrast a measured, not asserted, distinction — the candidate already logs kappa for its update vs. kappa_surrogate for an FPO-style CFM-ratio update on the same batch; making that head-to-head alignment gap (and the unbounded-bias-of-the-ratio argument) the load-bearing evidence dodges the subsumption."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Reward-Tilted Velocity Matching: Online RL for Flow Policies Without a Likelihood Ratio\n\n**Method.** Reward-Tilted Velocity Matching (RTVM)\n\n## Motivation\nModern continuous-control agents increasingly use a generative model — a diffusion or flow-matching network — as the policy, because such a model can represent many different good ways of acting at once, where a simple bell-curve (Gaussian) policy can only represent one. The trouble is that to improve a policy online from reward, you need to know how the probability of each action would change if you nudged the network's weights — a reward-weighted gradient of the action distribution. A flow policy produces an action by starting from random noise and following a learned 'velocity field' for a short pseudo-time; it never writes down the probability of an action in closed form, so that needed gradient simply does not exist in usable form. Recent methods work around this with stand-ins. FlowRL (a 2025 method) pushes the policy's velocity field to imitate the best actions it has already seen, kept close to the old policy by a distance penalty. FPO (Flow Matching Policy Gradients, also 2025) builds a ratio out of the policy's training loss and uses it as a substitute for the missing likelihood ratio inside a standard PPO update. Both work around the same hidden assumption: that improving a generative policy must look like a likelihood-ratio update. Neither ever checks how closely its stand-in points in the same direction as the true reward gradient, and because both lean on actions the policy has already produced, neither pushes the policy toward good actions it has not yet tried — so the very variety that justified using a generative model fades as training concentrates on a few actions. What makes this solvable now is that conditional flow matching — regressing the network's velocity onto a simple target velocity — has become the standard way these policies are trained, which means improvement can be expressed directly through that velocity, the thing the model already computes, instead of through the intractable probability. When this gap closes, online generative-policy RL no longer needs an elite buffer, a distance penalty, a likelihood-ratio proxy, or expensive backprop through the whole generation chain: one weighted regression is the update, and seeking out new action modes becomes a built-in property of that update rather than an extra penalty bolted on.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n\n1. Run the flow policy the usual way: start from a Gaussian noise vector $a_{0}$ the size of the action, then step a small ordinary-differential-equation solver (Euler or Heun, about 10 steps) that follows the learned velocity field $v_\\theta (t,s,a_{t})$ from pseudo-time 0 to 1 to produce the action $a_{1}$; clip it to the allowed action range, take it in the environment, and save (state, action, reward, next-state) in a replay buffer. Nothing here is new — it is the ordinary online reinforcement-learning data-collection loop.\n   - _Why_: This is the ordinary online RL data-collection loop; the new idea only changes how the policy is improved, not how it acts.\n2. Train an ordinary value network (a small multi-layer perceptron) on the buffer using the standard temporal-difference target, and from it compute each transition's advantage $A(s,a_{1})$ — how much better that action was than the state's average — with Generalized Advantage Estimation (GAE), using discount 0.99 and GAE-lambda 0.95; you may normalize the advantages to zero mean and unit spread within each update batch. This advantage is the reward signal that later tells the update which actions to favor.\n   - _Why_: The advantage is the reward signal that tells the update which actions to favor; using a standard critic keeps the new contribution isolated to the improvement step.\n\n### Reward-tilted velocity update\n*Express the reward-improvement direction as an advantage-weighted CFM regression onto the target velocity, with no likelihood ratio.*\n\n3. Combine the two signals into one weight per action: an exponential of the advantage divided by a temperature, multiplied by the novelty weight raised to an exploration power $\\lambda .$ Choose the temperature automatically as roughly the spread (standard deviation) of the advantages in the batch so the exponent stays moderate, subtract the batch's largest advantage before taking the exponential to avoid overflow (this only rescales by a constant), and cap the final weight (e.g. at 20) so no single action dominates; start $\\lambda $ at 0.5 so reward and novelty count about equally. Setting $\\lambda $ to 0 recovers the advantage-only weight, which is the positive control.\n\n*The combined per-sample tilt weight: $exp(A/\\beta )$ carries the reward-improvement signal $(\\beta  a$ temperature in units of return), and the novelty factor m raised to $\\lambda $ carries the exploration signal, where m is the inverse RBF kernel-density estimate $k_\\rho $ of the policy's own recent action visitation at state s.*\n$$ w'(s, a_1) = \\exp\\!\\left(\\frac{A(s, a_1)}{\\beta}\\right) \\cdot m(s, a_1)^{\\lambda}, \\qquad m(s, a_1) = \\frac{1}{k_\\rho(s, a_1) + \\varepsilon} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A single weight carries both 'do more of what scored well' and 'do more of what you've under-tried', so both effects ride on the same update with nothing stacked on.\n4. For each stored action, pick a random pseudo-time between 0 and 1 and a fresh random noise sample, blend the noise and the action in a straight line at that pseudo-time, and set the target velocity to the action minus the noise (the standard flow-matching target). Drawing one pseudo-time per update step is enough; averaging a few (say four) reduces noise. This target is exactly what the network already learns to predict, so improvement can be expressed through it.\n   - _Why_: This is the ordinary flow-matching target; it is the quantity the network already learns to predict, so improvement can be expressed through it.\n5. Update the policy by minimizing the weighted regression loss — the per-action weight times the squared difference between the network's predicted velocity and the target velocity — with the Adam optimizer (learning rate $3e- 4,$ batch 256, a few gradient steps per data batch); treat the advantages, novelty weights, and target as fixed constants so gradients only adjust the velocity network. Because the weight multiplies a squared error and never a probability or a ratio, there is no intractable likelihood anywhere, and the next round of acting then produces the high-weight (high-advantage, high-novelty) actions more often, which changes the agent's return.\n\n*The tilted conditional-flow-matching loss: a weighted regression of the policy velocity $v_\\theta $ at interpolation time t onto the conditional target velocity $a_{1} -  a_{0}$ along the linear interpolant $a_{t},$ with the tilt $w\\prime $ multiplying the residual rather than any log-likelihood gradient — so minimizing it moves the policy toward high-advantage, high-novelty actions without a likelihood ratio.*\n$$ \\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{imp}}(\\theta) = \\mathbb{E}_{(s,a_1)\\sim \\mathcal{B},\\, t\\sim U[0,1],\\, a_0\\sim\\mathcal{N}(0,I)} \\Big[\\, w'(s,a_1)\\, \\big\\| v_\\theta(t, s, a_t) - (a_1 - a_0) \\big\\|^2 \\,\\Big] \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Because the weight sits on the regression residual, the update pulls the velocity field toward generating high-advantage, high-novelty actions more often, with no intractable likelihood anywhere — and the next rollout actually produces those actions, changing the agent's return.\n\n### Intrinsic mode-seeking tilt\n*Fold a visitation-novelty factor into the same target-velocity weight so the improvement objective itself transports probability toward under-sampled modes.*\n\n6. Keep the most recent sampled state-action pairs (about 10000) in a rolling buffer, and to judge how novel a given action is at the current state, find the few hundred buffer entries whose states are closest to the current one and measure how densely those neighbors' actions cluster around the action in question using a smooth bell-shaped (radial basis function) kernel density estimate; set the kernel width from the typical spacing of the neighbor actions. The novelty weight is the inverse of that density, so an action the policy seldom produces near similar states gets a high weight. 【author decision: which notion of 'similar states' to use — raw state features, the value network's learned features, or a combined state-and-action similarity — must be picked, because it defines which actions count as rarely-tried at this state.】\n   - _Why_: It lets the update know which good actions the policy is currently neglecting, so it can push probability toward them — exploration computed from the policy's own behavior, not added to the reward.\n7. Gradually reduce the exploration power $\\lambda $ from its starting value down to zero over roughly the first 70% of training (a straight or cosine ramp), then leave it at zero; you can instead let the reduction track coverage, shrinking $\\lambda $ as the count of distinct action modes stops growing. Early on you want to spread out and find modes; later you want to commit to the best ones, so the exploration push fades as coverage saturates.\n   - _Why_: Early on you want to spread out and find modes; later you want to commit to the best ones, so the exploration push should fade as coverage saturates.\n\n### True-gradient fidelity diagnostic\n*Measure how well the update direction tracks the true return gradient and isolate the mechanism with reward-blind and advantage-only controls.*\n\n8. Every so often, estimate the direction of the true return gradient by simultaneous perturbation: pick a handful (about 16) of random $\\pm 1$ direction vectors in weight space, nudge the weights a little in plus and minus each direction, measure the average return of the nudged policy on a fixed held-out set of start states using the same random seeds, and combine these finite differences into an estimated gradient direction. Record the cosine similarity $(\\kappa )$ between our update direction and this estimate, and the same cosine for an FPO-style ratio update computed on the identical batch; also run the reward-blind control (remove the advantage from the weight) and the advantage-only control (set the exploration power to zero). This is the honest fidelity check the prior surrogate methods never performed.\n\n*The load-bearing falsification variable: the cosine alignment between our update direction (negative gradient of the tilted loss) and a finite-difference estimate $g_{FD}$ of the true expected-return gradient — the claim is that $\\kappa $ stays high while a CFM-ratio surrogate's alignment drops on multimodal states.*\n$$ \\kappa = \\cos\\!\\big(-\\nabla_\\theta \\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{imp}},\\; g_{\\mathrm{FD}}\\big) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: $\\kappa $ is the honest check the prior surrogates never did — it shows directly whether our update points the way the true reward gradient points, especially on the multimodal tasks where the ratio surrogate is suspected to drift.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 奖励倾斜的速度匹配（Reward-Tilted Velocity Matching）：无需似然比的 flow 策略在线强化学习\n\n**方法名称.** Reward-Tilted Velocity Matching (RTVM)\n\n## 研究动机\n现代连续控制智能体越来越多地用生成模型——diffusion 或 flow-matching 网络——作为策略，因为这类模型能同时表示多种不同的好动作，而简单的钟形（Gaussian）策略只能表示一种。问题在于：要用奖励在线改进策略，你需要知道如果微调网络权重、每个动作的概率会如何变化——也就是动作分布的奖励加权梯度。flow 策略生成动作的方式是从随机噪声出发、沿一个学到的“velocity field（速度场）”走一段伪时间；它从不显式写出某个动作的概率，所以那个所需的梯度根本无法直接得到。最近的方法用替代物来绕开这一点：FlowRL（2025 年的方法）把策略的速度场往它已经见过的最优动作上拉，并用一个距离惩罚把它约束在旧策略附近；FPO（Flow Matching Policy Gradients，同为 2025 年）用策略训练损失构造一个比值，在标准 PPO 更新里当作缺失的似然比的替代品。两者都绕开了同一个隐藏假设：改进生成策略必须长得像一个似然比更新。两者都从未检验自己的替代物与真实奖励梯度方向有多接近；而且因为它们都依赖策略已经产生过的动作，都不会把策略推向尚未尝试过的好动作——于是当训练把概率集中到少数几个动作上时，当初选用生成模型所看重的那种多样性就逐渐消失了。现在之所以能解决这个问题，是因为 conditional flow matching——把网络的速度回归到一个简单的目标速度——已经成为这类策略的标准训练方式，这意味着改进可以直接通过这个速度（模型本来就在计算的东西）来表达，而不必通过那个无法处理的概率。当这个 gap 被补上时，在线生成策略的 RL 就不再需要 elite buffer、距离惩罚、似然比代理，也不需要对整个生成链做昂贵的反向传播：一次加权回归就是更新，而且“去寻找新的动作模式”成为这次更新自带的性质，而不是另外加上去的惩罚项。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景\n\n1. 按常规方式运行 flow 策略：从一个与动作同维的 Gaussian 噪声向量 $a_{0}$ 出发，用一个小型常微分方程(Ordinary Differential Equation, ODE)求解器(Euler 或 Heun，约 10 步)沿学到的速度场 $v_\\theta (t,s,a_{t})$ 从伪时间 0 积分到 1，得到动作 $a_{1}$；把它裁剪到允许的动作范围内，在环境中执行，并把(状态、动作、奖励、下一状态)存入 replay buffer。这一步没有新东西——就是普通的在线强化学习数据收集循环。\n   - _为什么_: 这就是普通的在线 RL 数据收集循环；新方法只改变如何改进策略，不改变它如何行动。\n2. 在 buffer 上用标准的时序差分(Temporal-Difference, TD)目标训练一个普通的价值网络(一个小型多层感知机 multi-layer perceptron, MLP)，并据此用广义优势估计(Generalized Advantage Estimation, GAE)计算每条转移的优势 $A(s,a_{1})——$即该动作比该状态平均水平好多少——折扣取 0.99、GAE-lambda 取 0.95；可在每个更新批次内把优势归一化到零均值、单位离散度。这个优势就是之后告诉更新该偏向哪些动作的奖励信号。\n   - _为什么_: 优势是告诉更新该偏向哪些动作的奖励信号；用标准 critic 能把新贡献限定在改进这一步。\n\n### 奖励倾斜的速度更新\n*把奖励改进方向表达为对目标速度的优势加权 CFM 回归，全程无似然比。*\n\n3. 把两个信号合成每个动作的一个权重：优势除以一个温度后取指数，再乘以 novelty 权重的 $\\lambda $ 次幂$(\\lambda $ 是探索强度)。温度自动取为该批次优势的离散度(标准差)量级，使指数保持适中；取指数前先减去该批次的最大优势以防溢出(这只是乘一个常数)；并对最终权重设上限(例如 20)，使任何单个动作都不至于主导；$\\lambda $ 初始取 0.5，使奖励与 novelty 大致等权。把 $\\lambda $ 设为 0 即退回仅含优势的权重，也就是正对照。\n\n*每个样本的组合倾斜权重：$exp(A/\\beta )$ 承载奖励改进信号（$\\beta $ 是以回报为单位的温度），novelty 因子 m 的 $\\lambda $ 次幂承载探索信号；其中 m 是策略自身近期动作访问密度（在状态 s 处的 RBF 核密度估计 $k_\\rho $）的倒数。*\n$$ w'(s, a_1) = \\exp\\!\\left(\\frac{A(s, a_1)}{\\beta}\\right) \\cdot m(s, a_1)^{\\lambda}, \\qquad m(s, a_1) = \\frac{1}{k_\\rho(s, a_1) + \\varepsilon} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 单个权重同时承载“多做得分高的”和“多做你尝试不足的”，因此两种效果都搭在同一次更新上，没有额外堆叠。\n4. 对每个存下的动作，随机取一个介于 0 和 1 之间的伪时间和一份新的随机噪声样本，在该伪时间处把噪声与动作做直线混合，并把目标速度设为“动作减噪声”(标准的 flow-matching 目标)。每个更新步取一个伪时间即可；平均若干个(比如四个)能降低噪声。这个目标正是网络本来就在学着预测的量，所以可以通过它来表达改进。\n   - _为什么_: 这就是普通的 flow-matching 目标；它正是网络本来就在学着预测的量，所以可以通过它来表达改进。\n5. 通过最小化加权回归损失来更新策略——即每个动作的权重乘以“网络预测速度与目标速度之差的平方”——用 Adam 优化器(学习率 $3e- 4$、批大小 256、每个数据批做若干步梯度)；把优势、novelty 权重和目标都当作固定常数，使梯度只调整速度网络。因为权重乘的是平方误差，而不是任何概率或比值，全程都不出现无法处理的似然；随后下一轮行动就会更频繁地产生高权重(高优势、高 novelty)的动作，从而改变智能体的回报。\n\n*倾斜后的条件 flow matching 损失：在线性插值 $a_{t}$ 上，将策略速度 $v_\\theta $（插值时刻 t）回归到条件目标速度 $a_{1} -  a_{0}$，并用倾斜权重 $w\\prime $ 乘以残差（而非任何对数似然梯度）；因此最小化它会把策略推向高优势、高 novelty 的动作，全程不出现似然比。*\n$$ \\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{imp}}(\\theta) = \\mathbb{E}_{(s,a_1)\\sim \\mathcal{B},\\, t\\sim U[0,1],\\, a_0\\sim\\mathcal{N}(0,I)} \\Big[\\, w'(s,a_1)\\, \\big\\| v_\\theta(t, s, a_t) - (a_1 - a_0) \\big\\|^2 \\,\\Big] \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 因为权重落在回归残差上，更新会把速度场拉向更频繁地生成高优势、高 novelty 的动作，全程没有无法处理的似然——而且下一次 rollout 会真的产生这些动作，从而改变智能体的回报。\n\n### 内生的 mode-seeking 倾斜\n*把访问 novelty 因子折进同一个目标速度权重，使改进目标本身把概率运往采样不足的模式。*\n\n6. 把最近采样的状态-动作对(约 10000 条)放进一个滚动缓冲区；要判断某个动作在当前状态下有多新颖，就找出缓冲区里状态与当前状态最接近的几百条，并用一个平滑的钟形核——径向基函数(Radial Basis Function, RBF)核密度估计(Kernel Density Estimation, KDE)——衡量这些邻居的动作在该动作附近聚集得有多密集；核宽度由邻居动作的典型间距确定。novelty 权重取该密度的倒数，于是策略在相似状态下很少产生的动作会得到较高权重。【作者需决定：采用哪种「相似状态」的定义——原始状态特征、价值网络的学习特征、还是状态与动作联合的相似度——因为它决定了在该状态下哪些动作算是很少被尝试过的。】\n   - _为什么_: 它让更新知道策略当前忽视了哪些好动作，从而把概率推向它们——这是从策略自身行为算出的探索，而不是加进奖励里的。\n7. 在大约前 70% 的训练里把探索强度 $\\lambda $ 从初始值逐步降到 0(线性或余弦下降)，之后保持为 0；也可以让这个下降跟随覆盖度，当不同动作模式的数量不再增长时就缩小 $\\lambda $。早期你想铺开并找到各个模式，后期你想专注于最好的那些，所以探索推力随覆盖饱和而减弱。\n   - _为什么_: 早期你想铺开并找到各个模式，后期你想专注于最好的那些，所以探索推力应随覆盖饱和而减弱。\n\n### 真实梯度保真度诊断\n*度量更新方向对真实回报梯度的跟踪程度，并用去奖励对照和仅优势对照隔离出机制。*\n\n8. 每隔一段时间，用同时扰动法估计真实回报梯度的方向：在权重空间里取若干(约 16 个)随机的 $\\pm 1$ 方向向量，沿每个方向把权重做正负小幅扰动，用相同随机种子在固定的保留起始状态集上测量扰动后策略的平均回报，再把这些有限差分合成为一个估计的梯度方向。记录我们的更新方向与该估计之间的余弦相似度$(\\kappa )$，以及在同一批次上计算的 FPO 式比值更新的相同余弦；同时跑去奖励对照(从权重里去掉优势)和仅优势对照(把探索强度设为 0)。这正是先前替代方法从未做过的诚实保真度检验。\n\n*承载证伪的关键变量：我们的更新方向（倾斜损失的负梯度）与真实期望回报梯度的有限差分估计 $g_{FD}$ 之间的余弦对齐度；论点是在多模态状态上 $\\kappa $ 保持较高，而 CFM-ratio 替代目标的对齐度会下降。*\n$$ \\kappa = \\cos\\!\\big(-\\nabla_\\theta \\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{imp}},\\; g_{\\mathrm{FD}}\\big) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: $\\kappa $ 是先前替代方法从未做过的诚实检验——它直接显示我们的更新是否指向真实奖励梯度的方向，尤其是在怀疑比值替代物会漂移的多模态任务上。\n\n"},{"id":"30","run_dir":"run_prompt30_qdopt","index":30,"title":"Kernel Coverage Fields: Tessellation-Free Illumination in High-Dimensional Measure Spaces","title_zh":"核覆盖场：高维测度空间中无网格剖分的 illumination 质量多样性优化","method_name":"Kernel Coverage Field QD (KCF-QD)","hook":"Quality-Diversity does not actually need a partition of the measure space to know where coverage is thin: the local coverage deficit at any point is exactly the functional gradient of an RKHS coverage discrepancy, a single tessellation-free object whose representational cost is the size of the elite set, not the exponentially-many cells of any grid. We claim a QD loop driven by this functional gradient keeps a well-defined, dimension-stable per-region selection pressure and illumination score at descriptor dimensions where every fixed grid (and every CVT centroid set) is almost entirely empty.","anchor_pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","anchor_pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","domain_category":"Optimization & Search","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved QD method produces a tessellation-free, locally-resolved estimate of where coverage in a high-dimensional measure space is currently thin, so none can direct selection pressure toward genuinely under-covered local neighborhoods once the descriptor dimension is large enough that any fixed grid is almost entirely empty.","pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"closed by reframing 'where is coverage thin' as a measurement over a well-studied object — the functional gradient of an RKHS coverage discrepancy evaluated at any candidate descriptor — giving a per-point local coverage-deficit score with a soundness argument (it is the witness direction of the discrepancy), not a per-cell occupancy count.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions whether the target diversity in QD has to be represented as an exhaustive partition of the measure space at all, rather than as some object whose representational cost does not grow with the measure-space dimension.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"closed by naming the tacit 'enforcement-at-the-partition-locus' assumption inherited from MAP-Elites and relocating the coverage signal to the RKHS-functional locus, whose cost scales with the elite-set size rather than the cell count, and arguing structurally why the coverage property must live there too (the kernel mean embedding is injective for a characteristic kernel).","is_anchor":false},{"gap":"No retrieved method gives a measure of illumination quality (the QD coverage/QD-score objective) that stays well-defined and comparable as the measure-space dimension grows, so progress in high-dimensional behavior spaces currently cannot even be scored.","pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"closed by building a controlled instrument that varies grid resolution / centroid count independently of the true elite set and reports the divergence between grid-based QD-score and the partition-free kernel coverage score as the headline, isolating the tessellation-resolution confound that makes the standard metric undefined in high dimensions.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"quality-diversity optimization / illumination algorithms over high-dimensional behavior (measure) spaces","n_papers":39,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":25},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":20,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Machine learning accelerated MMC-based topology optimization for sound quality enhancement of serialized acoustic structures"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Quality-Diversity Actor-Critic: Learning High-Performing and Diverse Behaviors via Value and Successor Features Critics"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Machine Learning Approach to Predict AXL Kinase Inhibitor Activity for Cancer Drug Discovery Using Bayesian Optimization-XGBoost"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Machine Learning for Environmental Health: Optimizing ConcaveLSTM for Air Quality Prediction"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Quality-Diversity with Limited Resources"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Machine‐learning‐assisted intelligent synthesis of UiO‐66(Ce): Balancing the trade‐off between structural defects and thermal stability for efficient hydrogenation of Dicyclopentadiene"}],"more":14},{"year":2025,"n":18,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Quality Analysis and Evaluation Prediction of RAG Retrieval Based on Machine Learning Algorithms"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Predicting risk of coronary heart disease using a teaching–learning seagull optimization algorithm with the lightboost based gradient boosting machine"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Software defect prediction based on support vector machine optimized by reverse differential chimp optimization algorithm"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Diversity By Design: Leveraging Distribution Matching for Offline Model-Based Optimization"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"State of Charge Prediction for Electric Loader Battery Based on Extreme Learning Machine"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Exploring the Functionality of Microbes in Fermented Foods: Technological Advancements and Future Directions"}],"more":12},{"year":2026,"n":1,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"}],"more":0}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":6,"share":0.154},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":3,"share":0.077},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":3,"share":0.077},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":2,"share":0.051},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":2,"share":0.051},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":2,"share":0.051},{"pattern_id":"targeted_self_supervised_objective","pattern_name":"Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective","count":2,"share":0.051},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":2,"share":0.051}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Quality-Diversity optimization represents the target diversity by tessellating the measure (behavior-descriptor) space into cells and demanding one elite per cell, but the cell count needed to keep a fixed per-axis resolution grows exponentially with the measure-space dimension, so once the descriptor is high-dimensional the archive becomes almost entirely empty, per-cell occupancy and the coverage metric (QD-score, archive coverage) lose their meaning, and selection pressure toward 'unfilled regions' collapses because almost every cell is unfilled. The recent frontier sidesteps this rather than resolving it: QD with Limited Resources / RefQD (semanticscholar:7a0e3b62c34e412e521bca814eadfe5a96cbd1ab) reduces the archive's RAM/GPU footprint by sharing a representation network across decision parts but keeps the same tessellated archive and therefore the same dimensional blow-up, while DynAMO (semanticscholar:2576f0e59e11d23f54f53f68b5a040cdb7273b1a) abandons the explicit archive entirely and instead matches the global distribution of generated designs to the offline dataset's distribution, which gives one aggregate diversity objective but no notion of which under-covered region of the measure space to push toward next. QDAC (semanticscholar:851928d03830b47e795fe9925c8244fb4ae4fafd) and MOME (openalex:W4401214099) both keep the descriptor low-dimensional and hand-chosen, so neither produces the quantity a high-dimensional illumination would need: a tessellation-free, locally-resolved measure of where coverage is currently thin.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:2576f0e59e11d23f54f53f68b5a040cdb7273b1a","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"DynAMO reframes diversity in offline model-based optimization as a distribution-matching problem, deriving a provably-optimal objective that pulls the distribution of proposed designs toward the empirical diversity of the offline dataset, which removes the explicit grid archive and so escapes the cell-count blow-up. Its residue is that the matched target is a single global distribution, so the method has no per-region, locally-resolved signal of which part of the measure space is currently under-covered, cannot pursue novel modes absent from the offline dataset, and provides no illumination guarantee (one elite per local neighborhood) that QD's archive was meant to give."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:851928d03830b47e795fe9925c8244fb4ae4fafd","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"QDAC learns high-performing diverse skills with a value critic and a successor-features critic, balancing return against a constraint that the policy's expected features stay within an L2 ball of radius delta around a target skill vector z. The residue is that the diversity axis is a fixed, hand-specified, low-dimensional skill/feature vector z and the delta-ball constraint is defined in that low-dimensional feature space, so it does not address what coverage means when the behavior descriptor itself is high-dimensional and unstructured."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:7a0e3b62c34e412e521bca814eadfe5a96cbd1ab","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"RefQD (Quality-Diversity with Limited Resources) decomposes each solution network into a shared representation part and a per-elite decision part, storing only decision parts in the archive to cut RAM/GPU overhead, with re-evaluation strategies to fix the representation-drift mismatch. The residue is that it shrinks the per-elite storage cost but keeps the tessellated archive structure unchanged, so the number of cells still grows exponentially with measure dimension and the curse of measure-space dimensionality is untouched."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4401214099","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"MOME (Redefining the Behavior Space for Multi-Objective MAP-Elites) studies how the choice of behavior descriptor and its grid affects multi-objective illumination quality and proposes redefinitions of the behavior space. The residue is that it still relies on a hand-chosen low-dimensional grid tessellation and treats the descriptor dimension as a fixed design choice rather than a scaling barrier to overcome [residue is abstract-level: anchor fulltext unfetchable]."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"quality-diversity optimization / illumination algorithms over high-dimensional behavior (measure) spaces","venue":"ICML / NeurIPS / ICLR (QD + evolutionary ML track)","time":"2026","data":["standard QD benchmarks: QDgym / Brax continuous-control locomotion suites","MAP-Elites domains with high-dimensional behavior descriptors (e.g. full-body contact / per-limb feature vectors)","offline model-based-optimization design-bench tasks for the diversity-coverage measurement"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day) default (user did not state)","expertise":"evolutionary computation + deep RL; comfortable with optimal transport and continuous-relaxation machinery","preference":"both","baseline":"CVT-MAP-Elites / CMA-MAE with a hand-chosen low-dimensional measure, QDAC (skill-conditioned successor-features), and DynAMO (global distribution-matching diversity)","limitation":"QD archives tessellate the measure space, and the number of cells (hence the memory, the per-cell occupancy, and the very definition of coverage) grows exponentially with the measure-space dimension, so QD degenerates once the behavior descriptor is high-dimensional","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object across all three legs is the kernel coverage discrepancy D(A) between the empirical measure of the current elite set A = {x_1..x_m} (each x_i is the behavior descriptor of an archived elite, read out from a rollout) and a reference coverage target measure mu over the reachable measure space, defined in a characteristic-kernel RKHS as the squared Maximum Mean Discrepancy D(A) = || (1/m) sum_i k(x_i, .) - E_{mu}[k(z,.)] ||_H^2, where k is a fixed bounded characteristic kernel (Gaussian with bandwidth sigma set by the median-heuristic over the current elites, a named hyperparameter) and mu is either a uniform measure on a bounding box of the descriptor support or, when a reference dataset exists, its empirical measure. LEG 1 (anchor, C00 reframe): instead of asking 'which cell is empty', we define the local coverage deficit at any candidate descriptor x as g(x) = - d/d(epsilon) D(A union {x at mass epsilon}) |_{epsilon=0} = E_{mu}[k(x,z)] - (1/m) sum_i k(x, x_i), the negative first variation (functional gradient / witness) of D at x; g(x) is large exactly where the reference target has mass but the current elites do not, so it is a tessellation-free, locally-resolved 'this neighborhood is under-covered' score computable from m kernel evaluations plus one expectation under mu (closed-form for a Gaussian kernel and a box-uniform mu, or a Monte-Carlo estimate with a fixed sample budget S). The QD selection/emitter rule becomes: rank or accept candidate offspring by their fitness combined with g(x) (acceptance threshold tau on a scalarisation lambda*fitness + g(x), lambda a named trade-off hyperparameter), replacing per-cell competition; this closes gap 1 because the pressure is defined pointwise and never references a partition. LEG 2 (sibling, C01 locus relocation) reads from the SAME object: the audited assumption is that the diversity target must be an exhaustive partition (one elite per cell); we relocate enforcement to the RKHS-functional locus by replacing the archive data structure with the unstructured elite set A plus the functional D, and argue structurally that coverage is still fully represented because for a characteristic kernel the mean embedding mu_A = (1/m) sum_i k(x_i,.) is injective, so D(A)=0 iff the elite empirical measure equals mu — the partition was never necessary, only sufficient. LEG 3 (sibling, C02 diagnostic) also reads from the SAME object: we construct evaluation instances that hold the true elite set A fixed while independently sweeping the tessellation resolution r (grid bins per axis, or CVT centroid count), and report the divergence between grid-QD-score(A,r) and the resolution-free score 1 - D(A)/D(empty) as the headline — the grid score collapses toward zero (all elites alone in singleton cells) as r grows at fixed dimension d, and is undefined-by-degeneracy as d grows, whereas 1 - D(A)/D(empty) stays in [0,1] and stable. The three legs need no separate machinery beyond a different read of D: leg 1 uses its first variation as pressure, leg 2 uses its injectivity to justify dropping the partition, leg 3 uses its value as a dimension-stable score. DynAMO (semanticscholar:2576f0e59e11d23f54f53f68b5a040cdb7273b1a) matches only the GLOBAL distribution (one aggregate D to a fixed dataset); our g(x) is its pointwise first variation, which is the per-region signal DynAMO's single global objective never exposes.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The three gaps share machinery because Phase 2.1 chose coherence_thread_type=shared_object and the evidence is that all three are different reads of one quantity D(A): the pressure is its first variation, the partition-dropping justification is its injectivity, and the metric is its value — building three modules would have manufactured a fake decomposition, so a single object with three readouts is the honest design. (b) Alternative considered and rejected: a learned low-dimensional descriptor then a kernel over that (regresses to AURORA n4 — a learned-then-effectively-binned descriptor the REGRESSION FLAG names); and a DPP/determinant diversity score (collateral c1) which scores a finite set's diversity but yields no continuous local-coverage gradient to steer search, failing gap 1. We draw on the kernel/RKHS collateral c0 the lineage tree does not yet occupy, and explicitly avoid re-introducing any fixed tessellation (n1/n2/n4) and avoid reducing to a single global distribution match (n7) by keeping the POINTWISE first variation g(x), not just the scalar D.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on a Brax/QDgym continuous-control locomotion task (e.g. a walker) with an artificially high-dimensional behavior descriptor formed from per-limb contact-and-velocity features (d swept from 2 to 50), run the kernel-coverage-driven QD loop against CVT-MAP-Elites and CMA-MAE matched on total evaluations, measuring the partition-free coverage_score = 1 - D(A)/D(empty), the standard grid-QD-score, and per-generation memory. If the candidate works, as d grows the baselines' grid-QD-score and archive-coverage degenerate toward zero (cells become singletons/empty) while the kernel coverage_score for the kernel-driven loop stays bounded away from zero and decreases far more gracefully, and the kernel loop's memory stays O(m) instead of O(cells). The single named load-bearing variable is g(x), the local coverage-deficit (first-variation witness); the mechanism claim is that selection pressure proportional to g(x) is what produces the dimension-stable coverage. Negative control: ablate g(x) by setting it to a constant (pure-fitness selection) OR permuting g across candidates within each generation, holding all else fixed — the prediction is that the downstream coverage_score gain over the baseline collapses (the kernel loop's coverage advantage at high d disappears), proving the gain comes from g(x)'s pointwise direction and not from merely dropping the archive. Positive control: a g(x)-only selector (lambda=0) should recover most of the high-d coverage_score advantage, identifying g(x) as the sufficient driver.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:2576f0e59e11d23f54f53f68b5a040cdb7273b1a","delta":"DynAMO matches the GLOBAL distribution of generated designs to the offline dataset's empirical diversity via one aggregate objective; we construct its pointwise first variation g(x) = E_mu[k(x,z)] - (1/m) sum_i k(x,x_i) as a per-region under-coverage signal and use it as QD selection pressure, which their single global objective never exposes and which lets us pursue local under-covered neighborhoods rather than only matching one fixed dataset distribution."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:7a0e3b62c34e412e521bca814eadfe5a96cbd1ab","delta":"RefQD shrinks per-elite storage by sharing a representation network but keeps the tessellated archive, so its cell count still grows exponentially with descriptor dimension; we remove the partition entirely and represent coverage by an RKHS discrepancy whose cost is O(elite-set size), attacking the dimensional blow-up RefQD leaves untouched."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4401214099","delta":"MOME redefines which low-dimensional behavior descriptor/grid is used for multi-objective illumination but treats the descriptor dimension as a fixed design choice on a grid; we provide an illumination score (1 - D(A)/D(empty)) that stays in [0,1] and comparable as the descriptor dimension grows, which a grid-bound score cannot (it degenerates to singleton cells)."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:851928d03830b47e795fe9925c8244fb4ae4fafd","delta":"QDAC constrains expected successor features into an L2 ball around a hand-specified low-dimensional skill vector z; we require no pre-specified skill axis and define coverage pressure pointwise over an arbitrary high-dimensional descriptor via the kernel first variation, addressing what coverage means when the descriptor itself is high-dimensional and unstructured."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:2576f0e59e11d23f54f53f68b5a040cdb7273b1a","what_step_was_missed":"DynAMO formulated diversity as matching the global distribution of proposed designs to the offline dataset's empirical measure, but it stopped at the aggregate distribution-matching objective and never took its first variation with respect to a single candidate descriptor; the per-region selection signal we need requires constructing g(x) = E_mu[k(x,z)] - (1/m) sum_i k(x,x_i), the negative first variation of that very discrepancy evaluated pointwise, and turning it into a per-elite acceptance/emitter pressure with a characteristic-kernel injectivity argument that the empirical-measure match is lossless — a construction DynAMO's global objective did not produce and which is what converts global distribution matching into locally-resolved illumination."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":292,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"Layer 1 did not fire: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict is borderline (no lesson is candidate_match: yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat is NOT exact-mechanism overlap (HUSD uses a global IPM regularizer, not the candidate's pointwise first-variation coverage field). In the safe zone the choice is revise because paper_pointed_threat.addressable_via names a specific candidate field (differentiation_from_lit needs a HUSD entry) and the C01 borderline (locus-novelty vs HUSD's RKHS locus) hits a load-bearing structural property — the claim that the RKHS-functional locus is unoccupied in diversity work — so a targeted differentiation/core_mechanism sharpening is warranted before advancing.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved QD method produces a tessellation-free, locally-resolved estimate of where coverage in a high-dimensional measure space is currently thin, so none can direct selection pressure toward genuinely under-covered local neighborhoods once the descriptor dimension is large enough that any fixed grid is almost entirely empty.","main_pattern":"reframe_as_solvable_object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The signature failure is treating the reframing as a mechanical wrapper — pointing an established estimator at a new target without re-deriving why the resulting scores are faithful — with no causal validation that the identified object actually drives behavior, no axiomatic argument for why the proposed definition is the 'real' quantity, and no confound control.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Pointing an off-the-shelf decomposition at a coarser input granularity without showing the coarser units preserve the signal reads as a wrapper, not a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate does not coarsen any granularity; it derives g(x) as the exact first variation of the MMD coverage discrepancy and validates the signal is preserved via the characteristic-kernel injectivity argument in core_mechanism."},{"lesson_quoted":"Proposing a new attribution definition without an axiomatic or causal argument for why it should count as ground-truth collapses the moment a reviewer asks why this is the real importance.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism gives the soundness argument (g(x) is the negative first variation / RKHS witness of D, and the mean embedding is injective for a characteristic kernel so D=0 iff measures match) plus a causal negative control (ablate/permute g(x) → downstream coverage_score collapses), exactly the axiomatic+causal grounding the lesson demands."},{"lesson_quoted":"Conflating a methodological artifact — a computation-granularity difference, a degenerate zero baseline — with genuine signal undermines the entire premise once the confound is identified.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Leg 3's controlled diagnostic is built precisely to separate the tessellation-resolution artifact from true coverage, and the negative-control (constant/permuted g) rules out that the gain is a mere artifact of dropping the archive."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions whether the target diversity in QD has to be represented as an exhaustive partition of the measure space at all, rather than as some object whose representational cost does not grow with the measure-space dimension.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is a relocation demonstrated but not adversarially closed, or a novelty-boundary collapse where the 'new' locus turns out to be one a prior paper already used, or reintroducing the very assumption the relocation was meant to dissolve, or offering only a demonstration with no mechanistic account of why the locus carries the signal.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work — normalization statistics, activation-similarity losses, semantic concept triggers — collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"A collision hit (HUSD, semanticscholar:19209342368b5edad0f1b5a51c0b948bf8242c08) does relocate diversity into an RKHS/IPM locus for skill discovery, so the candidate must make explicit that its locus is a per-region first-variation coverage FIELD over the descriptor, not a global IPM separability regularizer — the difference is stated in differentiation but should be sharpened."},{"lesson_quoted":"A defense whose relocation silently depends on a clean reference model or a known anomaly distribution reintroduces precisely the strong assumption the move was supposed to eliminate.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The reference target mu is either a box-uniform measure (assumption-free) or, optionally, a reference-dataset measure; the partition-free coverage pressure does not depend on any pre-tessellation, so it does not smuggle back the partition assumption it dissolves."},{"lesson_quoted":"Demonstrating the new locus only on fixed, non-adaptive or outdated baselines while omitting any account of why it works reads as a stacked pipeline of existing components rather than a principled shift.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism supplies the mechanistic account (injectivity of the characteristic-kernel mean embedding is WHY coverage is fully represented at the functional locus) and the falsification compares against current baselines CVT-MAP-Elites and CMA-MAE across a dimension sweep."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved method gives a measure of illumination quality (the QD coverage/QD-score objective) that stays well-defined and comparable as the measure-space dimension grows, so progress in high-dimensional behavior spaces currently cannot even be scored.","main_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail most often when the instrument isolates the confound only inside an artificial regime and never shows the signal transfers to real deployment, or when the diagnostic is circular (validated against the same population it interrogates), or when it merely re-confirms an already-documented limitation.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a synthetic-ground-truth instrument only on synthetic data, without demonstrating that the controlled finding transfers to real-world instances, leaves ecological validity unestablished and undermines the central claim.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The diagnostic sweeps grid resolution on elite sets drawn from real Brax/QDgym runs (not synthetic), but the dimension sweep partly synthesizes high-d descriptors by stacking per-limb features, so the ecological-validity scoping of those constructed dimensions should be stated explicitly."},{"lesson_quoted":"Building the instrument around one contested definition of the target property means it cannot independently confirm that the definition is correct, and reviewers flag the resulting circularity.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The oracle (the kernel coverage score 1 - D(A)/D(empty)) is independent of the grid-QD-score being interrogated and of the system producing the elites; the headline is the divergence between two independently-defined quantities, not a self-referential check."},{"lesson_quoted":"A diagnostic that only re-confirms a shortcut already known in advance, surfacing no previously unmeasurable failure, is read as confirmatory rather than as a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The instrument surfaces a previously-unmeasured quantity — that grid-QD-score collapses toward zero as resolution/dimension grow while the kernel score stays bounded — which is exactly the non-obvious gap the field currently cannot score."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No entry triggered (no Reject lesson is candidate_match: yes). Two entries are borderline: the assumption_audit_and_pivot leg (C01) on the locus-novelty lesson because the HUSD collision hit also moves diversity into an RKHS/IPM locus, and the controlled_diagnostic_design leg (C02) on the ecological-validity lesson because the high-dimensional descriptors are partly constructed; both are addressable by sharpening differentiation and scoping, not structural defects."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved QD method produces a tessellation-free, locally-resolved estimate of where coverage in a high-dimensional measure space is currently thin, so none can direct selection pressure toward genuinely under-covered local neighborhoods once the descriptor dimension is large enough that any fixed grid is almost entirely empty.","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Recast an opaque question as a concrete measurement over a well-studied object (an estimator / decomposition / influence functional) by choosing the right unit of analysis and faithfulness constraint, buy tractability with one compression trick, and certify fidelity by causal intervention or a soundness proof rather than plausibility.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism LEG 1 recasts 'where is coverage thin' as g(x) = E_mu[k(x,z)] - (1/m) sum_i k(x,x_i), the negative first variation of the MMD coverage discrepancy D — a measurement over the well-studied RKHS-discrepancy object — with the closed-form/Monte-Carlo evaluation as the tractability trick and the injectivity argument plus the ablate-g negative control as the soundness+causal fidelity certificate. The cluster's signature measurement-reframe move is present, not just the parent's generic 'reframe' idea.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions whether the target diversity in QD has to be represented as an exhaustive partition of the measure space at all, rather than as some object whose representational cost does not grow with the measure-space dimension.","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Name the single representational locus current methods all operate on, state the tacit sufficiency/invariance claim bolted to it as a falsifiable proposition, relocate enforcement to an alternative locus, and supply a mechanistic account of WHY the new locus carries the signal more robustly.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism LEG 2 names the partition locus (one-elite-per-cell, inherited from MAP-Elites), states the tacit 'partition is necessary' claim, relocates enforcement to the RKHS-functional locus (unstructured elite set + D), and gives the mechanistic reason the signal survives there (characteristic-kernel mean-embedding injectivity makes the empirical-measure match lossless), exactly the cluster's locus-relocation-plus-why move.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved method gives a measure of illumination quality (the QD coverage/QD-score objective) that stays well-defined and comparable as the measure-space dimension grows, so progress in high-dimensional behavior spaces currently cannot even be scored.","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Construct a controlled set of instances in which exactly one named confound is independently varied while everything else is held fixed, score with an oracle independent of the system under test, and report the divergence between apparent and de-confounded performance as the headline result.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism LEG 3 holds the true elite set A fixed while independently sweeping the tessellation resolution r (and CVT centroid count) — isolating the one named confound (grid resolution) — and reports the divergence between grid-QD-score(A,r) and the resolution-free kernel score as the headline, with the kernel score as the system-independent oracle, performing the cluster's confound-isolation+divergence-headline move.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"All three legs perform their cited cluster's distinctive move: C00's measurement-over-a-known-object reframe (first variation of MMD), C01's locus relocation with a why-argument (partition to RKHS functional via injectivity), and C02's one-confound-isolation with a divergence headline (resolution sweep at fixed elite set)."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["reframe_as_solvable_object","assumption_audit_and_pivot","controlled_diagnostic_design"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; the candidate's composition_set contains none of {reframe, assumption_audit, controlled_diagnostic} paired with heterogeneous_decomposition, so no 2-way subset matches and no mitigation is required."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:19209342368b5edad0f1b5a51c0b948bf8242c08","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"HUSD (Hilbert Unsupervised Skill Discovery, AAAI 2025) maximizes an Integral Probability Metric (of which MMD is the canonical instance) in an RKHS to push state-skill distributions apart and enforce behavioral disentanglement, so it already brings the kernel/RKHS diversity machinery — the very collateral source (c0) the candidate's lineage tree relied on being unoccupied — into reinforcement-learning skill discovery. The candidate stands or falls on whether its object is genuinely distinct from HUSD's: HUSD uses an IPM as a GLOBAL separability regularizer between a finite set of skill-conditioned distributions (structurally the same global-distance move as DynAMO), and never takes the pointwise first variation of that discrepancy with respect to a candidate descriptor, never produces a per-region local under-coverage field g(x), and never addresses tessellation-free illumination scoring as the descriptor dimension grows; if a reviewer reads the candidate's g(x) as merely HUSD's IPM objective relabeled, the contribution collapses, but if the first-variation-as-local-coverage-pressure construction is shown to be what HUSD lacks, the threat is escaped.","addressable_via":"Sharpen differentiation_from_lit with a HUSD entry stating that HUSD maximizes a global RKHS IPM between skill distributions whereas the candidate constructs the pointwise first variation g(x) of the coverage discrepancy as a per-region selection pressure HUSD's global regularizer does not expose."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat (HUSD, semanticscholar:19209342368b5edad0f1b5a51c0b948bf8242c08) and gap_closure_reject_check C01 borderline on the locus-novelty lesson","fix_direction":"Add a differentiation_from_lit entry with paper_id semanticscholar:19209342368b5edad0f1b5a51c0b948bf8242c08 and delta: HUSD maximizes a GLOBAL RKHS Integral Probability Metric between a finite set of skill-conditioned state distributions to enforce disentanglement, whereas the candidate constructs the POINTWISE first variation g(x) of the coverage discrepancy as a per-region local under-coverage selection pressure over an arbitrary high-dimensional descriptor — a local coverage field HUSD's global separability regularizer never produces."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","issue":"gap_closure_reject_check C01 borderline (RKHS locus also used by HUSD) and C02 borderline (ecological validity of constructed high-d descriptors)","fix_direction":"In core_mechanism LEG 2, add one clause distinguishing the candidate's per-region first-variation locus from a global RKHS separability regularizer (the candidate keeps g(x) POINTWISE, not an aggregate IPM between distributions); and in LEG 3 add one clause scoping that the swept high-dimensional descriptors are constructed from real per-limb contact/velocity channels of the Brax task so the resolution-confound finding is grounded in deployed behavior, not a synthetic-only regime."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added a differentiation_from_lit entry against HUSD (semanticscholar:19209342368b5edad0f1b5a51c0b948bf8242c08) stating it uses a global RKHS IPM between skill distributions while the candidate constructs the pointwise first-variation coverage field g(x) HUSD's global regularizer never produces."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added a LEG 2 clause distinguishing the pointwise coverage field g(x) from an aggregate IPM/separability distance, and a LEG 3 clause scoping the swept high-dimensional descriptors as real Brax/QDgym per-limb contact-and-velocity channels rather than a synthetic-only regime."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Kernel Coverage Fields: Tessellation-Free Illumination in High-Dimensional Measure Spaces\n\n**Method.** Kernel Coverage Field QD (KCF-QD)\n\n## Motivation\nQuality-Diversity (QD) optimization is a family of search methods whose goal is not one best answer but a whole library of good answers that behave differently — for example, many ways a robot can walk. To decide what counts as 'different', the standard method (MAP-Elites and its successors) chops the space of behaviors into a fixed grid of boxes and keeps the single best solution found in each box. The trouble is the box count: to keep the same resolution along each behavior axis, the number of boxes multiplies as you add more behavior measurements, so in a high-dimensional behavior space there are astronomically many boxes, almost all empty. The archive becomes meaningless, the coverage score becomes meaningless, and the pressure to 'fill empty boxes' breaks down because nearly every box is empty.\n\nRecent work gets close but stops short. RefQD (Quality-Diversity with Limited Resources, ICML 2024) makes each stored solution cheaper but keeps the grid, so the box explosion remains. DynAMO (Diversity By Design, ICML 2025) throws away the grid and instead matches the overall spread of generated solutions to a reference dataset, but then it only has one global knob and cannot say WHICH specific under-explored neighborhood to push toward next. QDAC (ICML 2024) and MOME (GECCO 2024) keep the behavior description small and hand-picked, so they never face the high-dimensional case.\n\nWhat makes this solvable now is a tool from kernel methods: instead of boxes, you can describe how spread-out a set of behaviors is by a smooth distance called Maximum Mean Discrepancy (MMD), whose cost depends only on how many solutions you are storing, not on any grid. Crucially, the slope of that distance at any point — its first variation — tells you exactly how under-covered that point's neighborhood is. That slope becomes a local 'go here' signal, with no grid at all, and the same distance doubles as a coverage score that stays meaningful no matter how many behavior measurements you use.\n\nWhen this gap closes, QD can finally run AND be scored in genuinely high-dimensional behavior spaces: you get a per-region push toward thin coverage and an illumination score that stays well-defined, lifting the limit RefQD left in place and supplying the local signal DynAMO lacks.\n\n## Method\n### Coverage object\n*Defines the single tessellation-free RKHS discrepancy D(A) and its first-variation coverage field g(x) that the whole method reads from.*\n\n1. Keep one running 'spread' number, the kernel coverage discrepancy D(A), that measures how far the behaviors of the currently stored solutions are from a reference target spread. Each stored solution contributes a behavior vector read from running it once. Compare the two spreads with a Gaussian similarity (Gaussian kernel) whose width is set to the median distance between current behavior vectors. The reference target is, by default, a uniform spread over the observed range of each behavior measurement (the min-to-max seen so far, widened by five percent). 【author decision: if you have a curated target library of desired behaviors, you may instead use that library's spread as the reference — the trade-off is matching a fixed dataset versus covering the space uniformly.】 Cache the reusable sums so the same numbers feed the next step.\n\n*The kernel coverage discrepancy D(A): the squared RKHS distance (squared Maximum Mean Discrepancy) between the elite empirical measure over descriptors $x_{i}$ and the reference coverage target $\\mu .$*\n$$ D(A) = \\Big\\| \\tfrac{1}{m}\\sum_{i=1}^{m} k(x_i,\\cdot) - \\mathbb{E}_{z\\sim\\mu}\\,k(z,\\cdot) \\Big\\|_{\\mathcal H}^2 \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This one number is the shared object the whole method reads from, and its cost depends only on how many solutions you store, not on any grid.\n2. For any candidate behavior point x, compute its under-coverage value: how much the reference target wants mass near x, minus how much the currently stored solutions already cover near x. With a Gaussian similarity over a uniform reference, the first part has an exact formula (a product of one-per-measurement terms). When the reference is a dataset or no exact formula applies, estimate the first part with a fixed batch of 4,096 low-discrepancy (Sobol) samples drawn once and reused until the kernel width is refreshed. The result is a single number per candidate that is large exactly where the reference wants coverage but the stored solutions are absent.\n\n*The coverage field g(x): the negative first variation of D at descriptor x, large exactly where the reference target $\\mu $ has mass that the current elites do not — the per-region under-coverage pressure.*\n$$ g(x) = -\\left.\\frac{d}{d\\varepsilon}\\, D\\big(A\\cup\\{x \\text{ at mass }\\varepsilon\\}\\big)\\right|_{\\varepsilon=0} = \\mathbb{E}_{z\\sim\\mu}\\,k(x,z) - \\frac{1}{m}\\sum_{i=1}^{m} k(x,x_i) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: g(x) is large exactly where the reference wants coverage but the current solutions are absent, so it points directly at thin neighborhoods without any grid.\n\n### Partition-free QD loop\n*Replaces per-cell competition with fitness-plus-g(x) acceptance and a g-biased emitter so search is steered toward under-covered regions without any grid.*\n\n3. Throw away the grid archive; keep just an unstructured set of elite solutions, each storing its genotype, its fitness, and its cached behavior vector. Admit a new offspring when (its fitness times a trade-off weight $\\lambda )$ plus its under-coverage value beats a threshold, compared against its most behavior-similar stored neighbor; set the threshold to the running median of that same score over current elites so it adapts automatically. If the set is full, drop the most behavior-similar stored solution with the lower score; keep the cap equal to the grid baseline's intended size so memory is matched. 【author decision: how large to set the trade-off weight $\\lambda $ between fitness and coverage — higher $\\lambda $ keeps quality, lower $\\lambda $ pushes harder into thinly covered regions.】 Because the survivors and the parents seeded from them drift toward under-covered regions, the next generation's offspring concentrate there, which is how this rule changes the actual library of solutions, not just a stored number.\n\n*The partition-free acceptance rule: an offspring with fitness f(x) is admitted when its fitness-plus-coverage-deficit score exceeds threshold $\\tau ,$ with $\\lambda  a$ named fitness/coverage trade-off weight, replacing per-cell competition.*\n$$ \\text{accept } x \\iff \\lambda\\, f(x) + g(x) > \\tau \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Selecting by fitness-plus-under-coverage instead of by which box you land in steers survivors and their descendants toward genuinely under-covered regions.\n4. Choose parents for the variation operator in proportion to a softmax of their under-coverage values, so the children are generated mostly from solutions sitting near thin regions and therefore land in those thin regions after being run. Every ten generations, reset the Gaussian width to the median distance among current elite behavior vectors so the resolution follows where solutions actually are; refreshing it faster (smaller period) tracks density more closely but costs more compute. This refresh flows back into the spread number and the under-coverage values.\n   - _Why_: This turns the under-coverage signal into active search pressure, and refreshing the width lets resolution follow where solutions actually are instead of a fixed grid.\n\n### Mechanism controls\n*Ablates and permutes g(x) (and a g-only variant) to prove the coverage gain comes from the pointwise coverage signal.*\n\n5. Re-run the whole loop three more ways to test the mechanism: first with the under-coverage signal set to a constant (so selection is by fitness alone); second with the under-coverage values shuffled among the current generation's candidates (so the numbers are real but no longer matched to their behavior points); and third using only the under-coverage signal with no fitness term. Record the coverage score over time for each, and compare to the full method — if the high-dimensional coverage advantage disappears in the first two, the advantage genuinely came from the under-coverage signal.\n   - _Why_: If the high-dimensional coverage advantage survives shuffling or removing the signal, the advantage was not coming from the signal — these controls prove the mechanism.\n\n### Dimension-stable scoring and diagnostic\n*Reads out a resolution-free illumination score and isolates the grid-resolution confound across a dimension sweep.*\n\n6. At each checkpoint, report a coverage score equal to one minus the current spread number divided by the spread number of an empty archive (the empty-archive value uses the same reference samples and is computed once). This score is exactly zero for an empty archive and climbs toward one as the stored solutions match the reference spread, and it stays between zero and one and comparable no matter how many behavior measurements are used. Report it next to the usual grid score and the memory used.\n\n*The dimension-stable illumination score: one minus the elite discrepancy normalized by the empty-archive discrepancy, lying in [0,1] and comparable across descriptor dimensions.*\n$$ \\text{coverage\\_score}(A) = 1 - \\frac{D(A)}{D(\\emptyset)},\\qquad D(\\emptyset)=\\big\\|\\mathbb{E}_{z\\sim\\mu}\\,k(z,\\cdot)\\big\\|_{\\mathcal H}^2 \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This score stays meaningful and comparable no matter how many behavior measurements you use, unlike the grid score.\n7. Hold one set of elites fixed (taken from a real Brax/QDgym locomotion run) and change ONLY the grid resolution (4, 8, 16, 32 bins per axis) and the number of regions (one, five, ten thousand), recording the grid score versus the kernel coverage score at each setting. Separately, increase the number of behavior measurements (2, 5, 10, 20, 50), building them from real per-leg foot-contact and three-direction velocity readings. 【author decision: the exact order and grouping of the per-limb behavior readings as you add measurements — the choice is which behavior aspects come first as the count grows.】 Run the new method against CVT-MAP-Elites and CMA-MAE with the same number of evaluations. Produce a table of grid-score versus kernel-score and curves of coverage against the number of measurements, using the kernel score as the grid-free reference.\n   - _Why_: Holding the actual solutions fixed while only changing the grid isolates the grid-resolution artifact, showing the grid score collapses where the kernel score stays stable.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 核覆盖场：高维测度空间中无网格剖分的 illumination 质量多样性优化\n\n**方法名称.** Kernel Coverage Field QD (KCF-QD)\n\n## 研究动机\n质量多样性（Quality-Diversity, QD）优化是一类搜索方法，它要的不是单一最优解，而是一整库行为各异的好解——比如一个机器人多种不同的走路方式。为判断什么算作“不同”，标准做法（MAP-Elites 及其后继）把行为空间切成固定的格子，每个格子里只保留找到的最好的解。问题出在格子数量上：要在每个行为维度上保持同样的分辨率，每增加一个行为度量，格子数就成倍增长，于是在高维行为空间里格子多到天文数字，且几乎全空。这样档案失去意义，覆盖分数失去意义，“去填补空格子”的压力也崩溃了，因为几乎每个格子都是空的。\n\n近期工作接近却没走到底。RefQD（Quality-Diversity with Limited Resources, ICML 2024）让每个存储的解更省内存，但保留了网格，格子爆炸依旧。DynAMO（Diversity By Design, ICML 2025）丢掉网格，改为把生成解的整体分布匹配到参考数据集，但这样只剩一个全局旋钮，无法指出下一步该朝哪个具体的欠探索邻域推进。QDAC（ICML 2024）与 MOME（GECCO 2024）把行为描述保持得很小且人工选定，从未触及高维情形。\n\n如今之所以可解，靠的是核方法里的一个工具：与其用格子，不如用一种叫最大均值差异（Maximum Mean Discrepancy, MMD）的光滑距离来刻画一组行为有多分散，它的代价只取决于存了多少解，而与任何网格无关。关键在于，这个距离在任意点处的斜率——即它的一阶变分——恰好告诉你该点邻域的欠覆盖程度。这个斜率就成了一个不依赖任何网格的局部“往这走”信号，而同一个距离又可兼作覆盖分数，无论用多少行为度量都保持有意义。\n\n一旦补上这个缺口，QD 终于能在真正高维的行为空间里既能运行、又能评分：你得到面向稀薄覆盖的逐区域推动力，以及一个始终良定义的 illumination 分数，从而突破 RefQD 留下的局限，并补上 DynAMO 缺失的局部信号。\n\n## 方法\n### 覆盖对象\n*定义整个方法共享读取的、无网格剖分的 RKHS 差异 D(A) 及其一阶变分覆盖场 g(x)。*\n\n1. 维护一个“分散度”数值，即核覆盖差异(kernel coverage discrepancy) D(A)，用来衡量当前所存解的行为与参考目标分散度之间的差距。每个所存解贡献一个行为向量，由运行该解一次读出。用一个 Gaussian 相似度(Gaussian kernel)来比较两种分散度，其宽度设为当前行为向量之间距离的中位数。参考目标默认取每个行为度量已观察范围（至今所见的最小到最大值，再向外扩 5%）上的均匀分布(uniform distribution)。【作者需决定：若你有一个精心整理的目标行为库，可改用该库的分散度作为参考——权衡在于匹配一个固定数据集 还是 均匀地覆盖整个空间。】缓存可复用的求和项，使同样的数值供下一步使用。\n\n*核覆盖差异 D(A)：精英集合在描述子 $x_{i}$ 上的经验测度与参考覆盖目标 $\\mu $ 之间的 RKHS 距离平方（即平方最大均值差异 MMD）。*\n$$ D(A) = \\Big\\| \\tfrac{1}{m}\\sum_{i=1}^{m} k(x_i,\\cdot) - \\mathbb{E}_{z\\sim\\mu}\\,k(z,\\cdot) \\Big\\|_{\\mathcal H}^2 \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这个单一数值是整个方法共享读取的对象，其代价只取决于存了多少解，而与任何网格无关。\n2. 对任意候选行为点 x，计算其欠覆盖值：参考目标在 x 附近希望放多少质量，减去当前所存解在 x 附近已覆盖了多少。当采用 Gaussian 相似度配均匀参考时，前一项有精确公式（按每个行为度量各取一项再相乘）。当参考是数据集或无精确公式时，用一批固定的 4,096 个低差异(Sobol)采样来估计前一项，这批采样抽取一次并一直复用，直到 kernel 宽度被刷新为止。结果是每个候选一个数值，恰好在参考希望被覆盖、而所存解缺失之处取值最大。\n\n*覆盖场 g(x)：D 在描述子 x 处的负一阶变分，在参考目标 $\\mu $ 有质量而当前精英缺失之处取值最大，即每个局部区域的欠覆盖压力。*\n$$ g(x) = -\\left.\\frac{d}{d\\varepsilon}\\, D\\big(A\\cup\\{x \\text{ at mass }\\varepsilon\\}\\big)\\right|_{\\varepsilon=0} = \\mathbb{E}_{z\\sim\\mu}\\,k(x,z) - \\frac{1}{m}\\sum_{i=1}^{m} k(x,x_i) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: g(x) 恰好在参考希望被覆盖、而当前解缺失之处取值最大，因此无需任何网格即可直接指向稀薄邻域。\n\n### 无网格 QD 循环\n*用“适应度加 g(x)”的接受规则和受 g 偏置的 emitter 取代逐格竞争，使搜索在无网格的情况下被引向欠覆盖区域。*\n\n3. 丢弃网格档案，只保留一个无结构的精英解集合，每个精英存储其基因型(genotype)、适应度(fitness)与缓存的行为向量。当某后代的（适应度乘以权衡权重 $\\lambda $）加上其欠覆盖值，在与其行为最相似的已存邻居比较中超过一个阈值时将其纳入；阈值取当前精英上同一评分的滑动中位数，从而自动自适应。若集合已满，淘汰其中评分较低且行为最相似的已存解；将上限设为与网格基线预期规模相同，以匹配内存。【作者需决定：适应度与覆盖之间的权衡权重 $\\lambda $ 取多大$——\\lambda $ 越大越保住质量，越小越用力推进稀薄覆盖区域。】由于存活者及由其衍生的父代会向欠覆盖区域漂移，下一代后代便集中于此——这正是该规则如何改变实际解库，而不仅是改变一个存储数值。\n\n*无网格接受规则：当后代的适应度 f(x) 与覆盖缺口之和超过阈值 $\\tau $ 时将其纳入，$\\lambda $ 是适应度与覆盖之间的权衡权重，取代逐格竞争。*\n$$ \\text{accept } x \\iff \\lambda\\, f(x) + g(x) > \\tau \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 用“适应度加欠覆盖”而非“落在哪个格子”来选择，能把存活者及其后代引向真正欠覆盖的区域。\n4. 按精英欠覆盖值的 softmax 比例为变异算子选取父代，使后代主要由位于稀薄区域附近的解生成，从而在运行后落入这些稀薄区域。每隔十代，把 Gaussian 宽度重置为当前精英行为向量之间距离的中位数，使分辨率跟随解的实际所在；刷新越快（周期越小）越贴近密度，但算力开销越大。此刷新会回流到分散度数值与欠覆盖值中。\n   - _为什么_: 这把欠覆盖信号转化为主动的搜索压力，而刷新宽度让分辨率跟随解的实际所在，而非固定网格。\n\n### 机制对照\n*对 g(x) 做消融与打乱（并设只用 g 的变体），证明覆盖增益来自逐点的覆盖信号。*\n\n5. 再用三种方式重跑整个循环以检验机制：其一把欠覆盖信号设为常数（即仅按适应度选择）；其二把当前代各候选的欠覆盖值打乱（数值仍真实，但不再与各自的行为点对应）；其三只用欠覆盖信号、不含适应度项。分别记录其覆盖分数随时间的变化，并与完整方法对比——若前两种方式下高维覆盖优势消失，说明该优势确实来自欠覆盖信号。\n   - _为什么_: 若高维下的覆盖优势在打乱或移除信号后仍然存在，说明优势并非来自该信号——这些对照验证了机制。\n\n### 维度稳定的评分与诊断\n*读出与分辨率无关的 illumination 分数，并在维度扫描中隔离网格分辨率这一混淆因素。*\n\n6. 在每个检查点，报告一个覆盖分数，等于 1 减去当前分散度数值除以空档案的分散度数值（空档案的值用同一批参考采样、只算一次）。该分数对空档案恰为 0，随所存解逼近参考分散度而升向 1，并且无论用多少行为度量都保持在 0 到 1 之间且可比较。把它与常规网格分数和所用内存并列报告。\n\n*维度稳定的 illumination 分数：1 减去精英差异除以空档案差异，取值在 [0,1] 内且可在不同描述子维度间比较。*\n$$ \\text{coverage\\_score}(A) = 1 - \\frac{D(A)}{D(\\emptyset)},\\qquad D(\\emptyset)=\\big\\|\\mathbb{E}_{z\\sim\\mu}\\,k(z,\\cdot)\\big\\|_{\\mathcal H}^2 \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 与网格分数不同，无论用多少行为度量，这个分数都保持有意义且可比较。\n7. 固定一组精英（取自真实的 Brax/QDgym 运动运行），只改变网格分辨率（每轴 4、8、16、32 个分箱）与区域数量（一千、五千、一万），在每种设置下记录网格分数与 kernel 覆盖分数的对比。另外，逐步增加行为度量的数量（2、5、10、20、50 个），这些度量由真实的每条腿足部接触(foot-contact)与三方向速度读数构成。【作者需决定：随度量数量增加时，每肢行为读数的确切顺序与分组——其选择在于随数量增长哪些行为方面先纳入。】在评估次数相同的条件下，让新方法与 CVT-MAP-Elites、CMA-MAE 对比。生成网格分数与 kernel 分数的对照表，以及覆盖随度量数量变化的曲线，并以 kernel 分数作为不依赖网格的参考基准。\n   - _为什么_: 在保持实际解不变的同时只改网格，可隔离网格分辨率这一假象，显示网格分数崩塌而 kernel 分数保持稳定。\n\n"},{"id":"31","run_dir":"run_prompt31_kd","index":31,"title":"Per-Example Teacher-Payoff Gating: Distillation Weights Set by Measured Loss Effect","title_zh":"逐样本教师收益门控：用实测损失效应设定蒸馏权重","method_name":"Per-Example Teacher-Payoff Gating (PE-TPG)","hook":"Every adaptive knowledge-distillation method schedules a single global mixing coefficient between the distillation and task terms using a proxy — step count, gradient angle, or teacher confidence — yet none of these proxies measures the one quantity that decides whether the teacher should be trusted on a given example: how much following the teacher's target actually changes that example's task loss. We relocate the trade-off control from a global scalar to a per-example weight set by a directly measured, label-free payoff readout, and show it withdraws trust exactly where a confident teacher is wrong.","anchor_pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","anchor_pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","domain_category":"Vision Representation & Perception","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf measures, per example, how much the distillation term is currently changing the student's task loss (the marginal payoff of trusting the teacher on that example) and uses that measured quantity to set the mixing between the distillation and task terms — existing controllers move the coefficient by step-count, gradient angle, teacher entropy, or bandwidth proxies that are decoupled from whether the teacher's target is actually helping on each instance.","pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by repurposing a label-free internal readout — the per-example directional-derivative of the task loss along the distillation gradient (how much one step of following the teacher's target raises or lowers that example's own task loss) — as the manufactured supervisory signal that sets the example's distillation weight, confined to the tiny per-example weight lever with a frozen loss form, and stabilized against collapse by a trust budget and an EMA on the readout.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions whether a single shared mixing coefficient (the same scalar applied to every example and feature term) is the right object to control at all, rather than assuming the trade-off is one-dimensional — every adaptive-weight leaf inherits from the shared ancestor of a global scalar coefficient and only changes how that one scalar is scheduled.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","how_closed":"Closed by naming the inherited locus (a single global scalar coefficient, varied only by schedule) as a falsifiable sufficiency claim, then relocating the control locus to a per-example trust vector and arguing structurally why the trade-off must be enforced there — a global scalar provably cannot down-weight the teacher on its wrong examples without simultaneously under-trusting it on its right ones; the companion self_supervised_signal_engineering supplies the runnable deliverable that materializes the per-example trust vector from the measured payoff readout, so the overturned assumption ships as a working controller rather than only as a claim.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"knowledge distillation / model compression (vision + language classification students)","n_papers":29,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":24},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":10,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Attentive Modeling and Distillation for Out-of-Distribution Generalization of Federated Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Retrieval-Augmented Score Distillation for Text-to-3D Generation"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Efficient image classification through collaborative knowledge distillation: A novel AlexNet modification approach"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Mitigating Accuracy-Robustness Trade-Off via Balanced Multi-Teacher Adversarial Distillation"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Continual knowledge graph embedding enhancement for joint interaction-based next click recommendation"},{"source":"openalex","title":"A QoS-Aware Training Framework for ViT Compression, Partition, and Distillation"}],"more":4},{"year":2025,"n":27,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Lightweight Intrusion Detection Model Using Adaptive Knowledge Distillation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Compact Clarity: Development of Lightweight Networks for Low-Light Enhancement via Multi-Objective Knowledge Distillation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A simulation-driven computational framework for adaptive energy-efficient optimization in machine learning-based intrusion detection systems"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Optimization Strategies for Enhancing Resource Efficiency in Transformers & Large Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Distilling Knowledge or Transferring Weights? An Experimental Perspective on Classifiers"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Tiny Language Models for Automation and Control: Overview, Potential Applications, and Future Research Directions"}],"more":21}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":11,"share":0.379},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":6,"share":0.207},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":4,"share":0.138},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":3,"share":0.103},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":3,"share":0.103},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":2,"share":0.069},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":2,"share":0.069},{"pattern_id":"relax_discrete_search_to_continuous","pattern_name":"Relax Discrete Search to Continuous","count":2,"share":0.069}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"In standard knowledge distillation the student minimizes a fixed convex combination of a distillation term and a task term, but the *correctness* of the teacher signal is not uniform: on examples the teacher mislabels or is over-confident on, the distillation term actively pulls the student toward a wrong target, and on examples where the student has already surpassed the teacher the term contributes stale gradient — yet the mixing coefficient is a single global constant or monotone schedule (openalex:W4417511383, openalex:W6979260485). Recent adaptive methods move the coefficient by a hand-derived importance heuristic over training steps (openalex:W4417511383), by fixed gradient-surgery between the two task gradients (openalex:W6979260485), by an entropy-based teacher-scale balance (openalex:W4399768821), or by bandwidth-driven schedules (openalex:W4409895090), but in every case the coefficient is tied to a proxy (step count, gradient angle, teacher entropy, communication budget) rather than to a *measured, per-example estimate of how much the teacher's target is currently helping versus hurting the student's task loss* — so once the teacher and student disagree on where the truth lies, no existing controller can attribute the resulting loss change to the distillation term and re-weight that example accordingly, and the global coefficient over- or under-trusts the teacher exactly where it matters.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4417511383","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Derives, for a simple single-teacher classification KD, a step-to-step loss-decrease analysis showing how the scalar balancing parameter α between distillation and classification loss influences how fast the loss falls, and proposes an importance-based heuristic to move α dynamically across training steps. The control signal is a single global scalar tied to aggregate training-step dynamics on a closed-form approximation — it has no per-example resolution and never measures whether the teacher's target on a given example is actually reducing or increasing that example's task loss, so it cannot down-weight the specific examples where the teacher is wrong."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W6979260485","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"MoKD casts KD as multi-task optimization between teacher-guidance and the task objective and applies gradient-surgery to resolve conflicts between the two gradient directions, plus a projection to handle teacher-student representation disparity. The conflict resolution operates at the level of the two aggregate gradient vectors with a fixed surgery rule, so it equalizes directions but never estimates a per-example trust signal nor adapts the rule online to which examples the teacher is currently helping on."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4399768821","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"B-MTARD balances a clean teacher and a robust teacher with an entropy-based teacher-knowledge-scale balance and a normalization-loss balance equalizing the student's learning speed from each teacher, to manage the accuracy-robustness trade-off. The balance is computed from teacher output entropy and loss-magnitude normalization — proxies for confidence, not measurements of marginal task-loss benefit — so a confident-but-wrong teacher is still trusted and the trade-off frontier is navigated by a heuristic rather than by an estimated payoff of each term."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7111346633","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"LKD makes the distillation loss form itself learnable, replacing hand-crafted task-specific losses with an autonomously learned adaptive loss. It learns the functional shape of the distillation term but still trains it under a fixed outer weighting against the task loss, so it does not dynamically arbitrate, per example and over training, how much to trust the resulting term against the task objective."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4409895090","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Mutual KD for cross-organizational federated learning replaces static distillation loss weights with weights that adapt to communication bandwidth variation. The adaptation tracks an external resource proxy (bandwidth), not the internal teacher-helpfulness signal, so it solves a communication-scheduling problem orthogonal to whether the teacher's target is correct for a given example."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"knowledge distillation / model compression (vision + language classification students)","venue":"ICLR / ICML / NeurIPS (top-tier ML)","time":"2026","data":["CIFAR-100","ImageNet","standard teacher-student KD benchmarks (ResNet/ViT families)"],"compute":"1×A100 × 3 months (≈ 90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher comfortable with optimization + distillation","preference":"both","baseline":"standard KD with a fixed or hand-scheduled distillation/task loss weight (α) and temperature (τ); recent adaptive-weight KD (MoKD, dynamic-balancing-parameter analysis, B-MTARD entropy balance)","limitation":"the relative weighting between the distillation term and the task term (and across multiple teacher/feature terms) is set by a hand-tuned constant or a monotone schedule, so it cannot track the changing per-example reliability of the teacher signal as the student's own competence rises during training","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared question both legs attack is: what object should govern the distillation-vs-task trade-off, and from what signal should it be set? Anchor leg (C07, manufacture the signal). In standard KD the student minimizes L_i = (1 - w) * L_cls(x_i) + w * L_dist(x_i) with a global weight w; we replace the scalar w with a per-example weight w_i computed each step from a measured, label-free payoff readout p_i. p_i is the negative directional derivative of the student's task loss along the distillation gradient at example x_i: p_i = - <grad_theta L_cls(x_i), grad_theta L_dist(x_i)> / (||grad_theta L_dist(x_i)|| + eps), a per-example dot product of two gradients the backward pass already computes (so no extra forward pass; eps = 1e-8). p_i is positive when one step toward the teacher's target on x_i would also reduce x_i's task loss (teacher helps) and negative when it would raise it (teacher's target conflicts with the true label — the confident-but-wrong case). We pass p_i through a temperature-controlled logistic to get the per-example weight w_i = w_max * sigmoid(p_i / s), where s is a payoff-scale hyperparameter (default s = running std of p over the batch) and w_max in (0,1] caps maximum teacher trust; this is the tiny per-example lever the C07 move confines the correction to, leaving the loss FORM and the teacher frozen. Because a raw label-free readout invites collapse (e.g. early-training noise driving all w_i to 0 and discarding the teacher entirely, or a degenerate all-trust mode), the C07 stabilizer is twofold: (1) an EMA bar_p_i = m * bar_p_i + (1-m) * p_i (m = 0.9) per example to denoise the single-step estimate, and (2) a batch trust budget that renormalizes {w_i} so their mean equals a slowly-annealed target W_t (the global schedule a prior method would have used), so the method spends a fixed trust mass but reallocates it across examples toward the ones the teacher currently helps. Sibling leg (C01, relocate the locus). The inherited locus is the single global scalar w (openalex:W4417511383 schedules exactly this scalar; openalex:W4399768821 sets a per-teacher scalar) under the tacit claim that the trade-off is one-dimensional; we state this as falsifiable and relocate enforcement to the per-example vector {w_i}. The structural argument for why the new locus carries the signal: with a single w, the gradient contribution of the distillation term is w * sum_i grad L_dist(x_i), so any w large enough to exploit the teacher on its correct examples necessarily applies the same w to its wrong examples, injecting their conflicting gradient — a per-example w_i set by sign(p_i) is the minimal object that can null the wrong-example contribution while keeping the right-example one, which a scalar cannot do by construction. The companion deliverable (the C07 payoff readout) is what computes {w_i}, so the overturned assumption is realized as the same running mechanism, not a separate claim. The two legs share the object {w_i} and its driving readout p_i: the anchor constructs and stabilizes it, the sibling audits why the scalar it replaces was the wrong control object.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules: the audit leg's overturned object (a per-example trust vector) is exactly the artifact the anchor leg's manufactured signal produces, so the evidence for sharing is that the sibling's deliverable and the anchor's output are the same vector {w_i} — Phase 2.1 already encoded this by setting the sibling's companion to self_supervised_signal_engineering. Forcing two separate modules would have produced a method leg plus a disconnected think-piece. (b) Alternatives considered and rejected: (i) setting w_i from teacher confidence/entropy — rejected as the c2 collateral node (confidence-gating), which a confident-but-wrong teacher defeats, the exact failure we target; (ii) a learned per-term homoscedastic variance — rejected as the c0 node (one global variance per term, no per-example resolution); (iii) task-example reweighting on the label loss — rejected as the c1 node (reweights the task target, not the teacher-vs-task trade-off). The gradient-alignment payoff readout p_i lands on none of these occupied tree nodes because it measures the realized marginal task-loss effect of the teacher target, not a confidence proxy, a variance, or a task-difficulty weight.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: distill a ResNet-50 teacher into a ResNet-18 student on CIFAR-100 (and ImageNet-1k as scale check), comparing per-example payoff gating against (i) best fixed weight, (ii) the importance-scheduled scalar of openalex:W4417511383, and (iii) teacher-confidence gating, all at matched epochs and matched mean trust mass W_t. If the candidate works, overall student top-1 accuracy improves modestly but accuracy on the teacher-error subset (examples the teacher misclassifies) improves substantially and student calibration on that subset improves, because trust is withdrawn there. The load-bearing variable is p_i, the per-example gradient-alignment payoff readout; the mechanism distinguisher is a negative-control intervention that randomly permutes p_i across examples within each batch (preserving its marginal distribution but destroying the example-to-readout correspondence) — if p_i truly carries the mechanism, this control must drive the teacher-error-subset accuracy back down to the fixed-weight / scheduled-scalar baseline, whereas if the gain came from mere extra weight variance or implicit regularization the permuted run would retain it. A positive control that sets w_i from only sign(p_i) should recover most of the teacher-error-subset accuracy gain, identifying the sign of the measured payoff as the sufficient signal.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4417511383","delta":"They derive a step-to-step loss-decrease analysis to schedule a single global scalar balancing parameter across training steps; we construct a per-example weight set by a directly measured gradient-alignment payoff readout, which has resolution their aggregate scalar lacks and can withdraw teacher trust on individual examples the teacher mislabels."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W6979260485","delta":"MoKD applies a fixed gradient-surgery rule between the two aggregate (batch-summed) gradient directions; we keep both gradients per-example and convert their alignment into an explicit per-example trust weight under a renormalized trust budget, attributing and reallocating trust example-by-example rather than equalizing two summed directions."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4399768821","delta":"B-MTARD balances teachers by output-entropy scale and loss-magnitude normalization (confidence proxies); we set trust from the realized marginal effect of the teacher target on each example's task loss, so a confident-but-wrong teacher is down-weighted where an entropy proxy would still trust it."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7111346633","delta":"LKD learns the functional shape of the distillation loss while keeping a fixed outer weight; we freeze the loss form and instead make the outer weight a measured per-example quantity, so the two contributions are orthogonal (a learned loss could be gated by our readout)."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4417511383","what_step_was_missed":"They derived how the GLOBAL scalar balancing parameter affects the aggregate step-to-step loss decrease, but they never constructed the per-example decomposition of that loss-decrease effect — the per-example directional derivative of the task loss along the distillation gradient — which is the readout that lets the weight be set example-by-example; without that construction the control object stays a single scalar and cannot reallocate trust toward the examples the teacher is currently helping."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":207,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"Hard floor did not fire: gap_closure_reject_check has no candidate_match=yes (both legs borderline), recipe_application_check is applied for both legs, and anti_pattern_check matched nothing. The decisive findings are (1) the C01 borderline lesson 'Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work ... collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured', and (2) paper_pointed_threat AKD (Context-Aware KD with Adaptive Weighting) whose addressable_via names a specific candidate field — both hit the load-bearing novelty boundary (measured per-example payoff vs context/confidence-driven adaptive alpha), so this is revise rather than advance: add the AKD differentiation entry and require a context/confidence-adaptive-alpha comparison baseline.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf measures, per example, how much the distillation term is currently changing the student's task loss (the marginal payoff of trusting the teacher on that example) and uses that measured quantity to set the mixing between the distillation and task terms — existing controllers move the coefficient by step-count, gradient angle, teacher entropy, or bandwidth proxies that are decoupled from whether the teacher's target is actually helping on each instance.","main_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"A manufactured internal signal whose validity silently rests on an assumption that does not survive deployment (calibration, a stationary/known-finite shift set, or covert use of target/test labels), so the surrogate degrades exactly when its premise is violated; compounded by recombining well-known components without one load-bearing mechanistic insight, and thin single-dataset validation.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A label-free signal whose validity depends on model calibration silently fails on exactly the deep networks known to be poorly calibrated — validate a surrogate where its core assumption is weakest, not where it is convenient.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The payoff readout p_i is a measured gradient dot-product of the realized task-loss effect, not a calibration- or confidence-derived quantity, so its validity does not rest on teacher/student calibration; the falsification design deliberately measures the teacher-error subset where the proxy is most stressed."},{"lesson_quoted":"Recasting a continuous shift as a discrete, known, finite set of types indexed against a precomputed lookup table collapses the moment an unanticipated or mixed shift arrives.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"p_i is a continuous per-example readout computed online from current gradients with no discrete shift-type lookup table, so this failure shape does not apply."},{"lesson_quoted":"A multi-branch or ensemble reweighting mechanism that overlaps with standard multi-task/mixture-of-experts ensembling must explicitly beat both the single-model and the standard-ensemble baselines, or the gain is credited to prior art.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"There is a single student and a single frozen teacher with one loss form; no ensemble or multi-branch reweighting is introduced, so the ensembling-overlap concern is not raised."},{"lesson_quoted":"Using target or test-set information during adaptation invites a label-leakage objection that undermines the very source-free, label-free deployment setting the method claims.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"p_i uses only the training example's own task loss gradient (which legitimately uses the training label) and the teacher's gradient; the trust-budget target W_t and held-out teacher-error logging never feed back into the weights, so no test-set label leakage occurs."},{"lesson_quoted":"Reusing standard sequential machinery (chaining each step's posterior as the next prior) without a new stabilizer amplifies noise and looks derivative of prior adaptation work.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The EMA denoiser bar_p_i is standard sequential machinery; it is borderline because the load-bearing novelty is the payoff readout p_i itself plus the trust-budget renormalization (a non-standard stabilizer), so the EMA is a supporting denoiser, not the contribution."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions whether a single shared mixing coefficient (the same scalar applied to every example and feature term) is the right object to control at all, rather than assuming the trade-off is one-dimensional — every adaptive-weight leaf inherits from the shared ancestor of a global scalar coefficient and only changes how that one scalar is scheduled.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"A relocation demonstrated but not adversarially closed (never stress-tested against an informed baseline operating at the new locus), or a novelty-boundary collapse where the 'new' locus turns out to be one prior work already used, or reintroducing the very assumption the relocation was meant to dissolve, or offering a demonstration with no mechanistic account of why the new locus carries the signal.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work — normalization statistics, activation-similarity losses, semantic concept triggers — collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"Per-example reweighting of losses exists in adjacent literature (focal loss, learning-to-reweight; and adaptive-alpha KD like AKD); the candidate makes the difference explicit (a measured gradient-alignment payoff vs a context/confidence-driven scalar) and the falsification measures it, so the boundary is defended but reviewers will press on it."},{"lesson_quoted":"Demonstrating the new locus only on fixed, non-adaptive or outdated baselines while omitting any account of why it works reads as a stacked pipeline of existing components rather than a principled shift.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate gives a structural account of why the per-example locus carries the signal (a single scalar cannot null the wrong-example distillation gradient without under-trusting the right examples) and compares against the importance-scheduled scalar and confidence-gating, not only fixed-weight KD."},{"lesson_quoted":"A defense whose relocation silently depends on a clean reference model or a known anomaly distribution reintroduces precisely the strong assumption the move was supposed to eliminate.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The per-example control reintroduces no global assumption — it needs no clean reference, no known distribution; the trust budget only reallocates the same trust mass a scalar method would have used."},{"lesson_quoted":"Wiring off-the-shelf generators or tools into a new attack setting without a structural reason for the locus change gets judged as engineering integration, not insight.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The locus change (global scalar to per-example vector) is justified by a derivation about the distillation gradient's per-example sign, not by bolting on an off-the-shelf tool."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No Reject lesson is marked candidate_match=yes in either entry, so the hard floor does not fire. The aggregate is borderline driven by the C01 leg's novelty-boundary lesson ('Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work ... collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured') — per-example loss reweighting has neighbors, and the candidate must keep its measured-payoff-vs-confidence-scalar distinction sharp and empirically demonstrated."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf measures, per example, how much the distillation term is currently changing the student's task loss (the marginal payoff of trusting the teacher on that example) and uses that measured quantity to set the mixing between the distillation and task terms — existing controllers move the coefficient by step-count, gradient angle, teacher entropy, or bandwidth proxies that are decoupled from whether the teacher's target is actually helping on each instance.","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Treat the model's own internal-state readout as the manufactured supervisory signal, pairing a mechanistic diagnosis that localizes the failure to a specific structural site with a surgically confined correction on a minimal lever while the backbone stays frozen, and bolt on an explicit stabilizer because a label-free signal invites a degenerate solution — the verbs are diagnose-localize, minimize-on-a-tiny-lever, stabilize-against-collapse.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism diagnoses the failure site (a global scalar injecting the wrong-example distillation gradient), reads an internal label-free signal (the per-example gradient-alignment payoff p_i computed from gradients the backward pass already produces), confines the correction to the tiny per-example weight lever w_i while freezing the loss form and teacher, and bolts on the C07 stabilizer twofold (EMA denoiser + trust-budget renormalization against collapse to all-trust/no-trust). All three signature verbs are present.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions whether a single shared mixing coefficient (the same scalar applied to every example and feature term) is the right object to control at all, rather than assuming the trade-off is one-dimensional — every adaptive-weight leaf inherits from the shared ancestor of a global scalar coefficient and only changes how that one scalar is scheduled.","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"The audited assumption is about the representational LOCUS at which a property is presumed to be enforced, and the move is to relocate enforcement to a different locus the field treated as irrelevant or invariant, with a mechanistic account of why the new locus carries the signal — relocate the signal, re-anchor enforcement, demonstrate at the new locus.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism names the inherited locus (the single global scalar w, with the falsifiable claim that the trade-off is one-dimensional), relocates enforcement to the per-example vector {w_i}, and supplies the structural why (a scalar applies the same w to right and wrong examples, so only a per-example object can null the wrong-example distillation gradient while keeping the right one). The companion self_supervised_signal_engineering supplies the runnable readout that materializes {w_i}. The locus-relocation move and its mechanistic account are present.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both legs perform their cluster's signature move: the C07 leg enacts diagnose-localize / minimize-on-a-tiny-lever / stabilize-against-collapse on the per-example weight, and the C01 leg relocates the control locus from a global scalar to a per-example vector with a structural account of why the signal lives there; neither is the parent pattern's generic gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["self_supervised_signal_engineering","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; the candidate's composition set {self_supervised_signal_engineering, assumption_audit_and_pivot} contains no heterogeneous_decomposition, so no anti-pattern matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:58d0f54de19a5eec0293ac2489237947fe77e183","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"Context-Aware Knowledge Distillation with Adaptive Weighting (AKD) makes the same diagnosis — a static alpha combining hard-label and soft-label loss is suboptimal because the optimal trade-off varies during training — and proposes an adaptive alpha framework, which is the closest competitor to the candidate's headline. The candidate stands or falls on whether its control object and signal are genuinely distinct: AKD adapts a context-driven (and, in its variants, largely global/schedule- or context-conditioned) alpha, whereas the candidate relocates control to a PER-EXAMPLE weight set by a MEASURED gradient-alignment payoff of the teacher target on each example's task loss. If AKD's adaptive alpha is in fact per-example and derived from a realized loss-effect measurement, the candidate's novelty boundary collapses; if (as its abstract indicates) it adapts alpha by training-context/confidence cues rather than by a measured per-example marginal-task-loss readout, the candidate survives and the differentiation_from_lit delta against the importance-scheduled scalar (openalex:W4417511383) and entropy balance (openalex:W4399768821) carries the same distinction.","addressable_via":"Sharpen differentiation_from_lit with an entry naming this AKD paper and stating the measured-per-example-payoff-vs-context/confidence-driven-alpha distinction, and ensure the experimental comparison includes a context/confidence-adaptive-alpha baseline so the boundary is demonstrated rather than asserted."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat (semanticscholar:58d0f54de19a5eec0293ac2489237947fe77e183, Context-Aware KD with Adaptive Weighting) + C01 novelty-boundary borderline lesson","fix_direction":"Append a differentiation_from_lit entry for paper_id semanticscholar:58d0f54de19a5eec0293ac2489237947fe77e183 with a substantive delta: AKD adapts a context/training-progress-driven alpha that is shared across examples (or conditioned on coarse context), while the candidate sets a PER-EXAMPLE weight from a directly measured gradient-alignment payoff p_i of the teacher target's realized effect on that example's task loss — the candidate constructs a measured per-example quantity AKD never computes, which is what lets trust be withdrawn on the specific examples a confident teacher mislabels."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"falsification_prediction","issue":"C01 novelty-boundary borderline lesson — the locus-relocation must be demonstrated against a baseline that also adapts the weight, not only fixed/scheduled scalars","fix_direction":"Note: falsification_prediction is a kill-switch field and must stay byte-identical; do NOT modify it. Instead this concern is satisfied because the existing falsification_prediction already lists baseline (iii) teacher-confidence gating, which is the adaptive-weight competitor; if any non-kill-switch field needs the explicit context/confidence-adaptive-alpha baseline named, fold it into core_mechanism_steps step 10 rather than the kill-switch paragraph. Mark skipped_anti_substitution if it would touch the kill-switch."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Appended a differentiation_from_lit entry for AKD (semanticscholar:58d0f54...) stating the measured-per-example-payoff vs context/progress-driven shared-alpha distinction."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"falsification_prediction","outcome":"skipped_anti_substitution","delta_summary":"Target pointed at the kill-switch falsification_prediction; left byte-identical and instead added the context/confidence-adaptive-alpha comparison baseline to core_mechanism_steps step 10."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Per-Example Teacher-Payoff Gating: Distillation Weights Set by Measured Loss Effect\n\n**Method.** Per-Example Teacher-Payoff Gating (PE-TPG)\n\n## Motivation\nKnowledge Distillation (KD) trains a small 'student' model by mixing two goals: copy a big 'teacher' model's soft predictions (the distillation term) and match the true labels (the task term). A single dial, the mixing weight, decides how much to trust the teacher. The trouble is that the teacher is not equally trustworthy on every example: on examples it gets wrong (especially the ones it is confidently wrong about) copying it actively hurts the student, and on examples the student has already mastered the teacher just adds stale guidance. Yet today that dial is one global number (or a fixed schedule), so it has to pick a single trust level for the whole dataset and is forced to over-trust the teacher somewhere and under-trust it somewhere else.\n\nRecent work makes the dial adaptive but never measures the right thing. The importance-analysis method (arXiv 2025-05) moves the dial using the overall, batch-averaged loss trend; entropy-balanced multi-teacher distillation (IEEE TPAMI 2024-06) moves it by how confident the teacher looks; MoKD (arXiv 2025-05) reconciles the two averaged gradient directions with a fixed rule. All of these read a proxy — step count, teacher confidence, an averaged gradient angle — none of which tells you, for a specific example, whether following the teacher would actually lower or raise that example's own error.\n\nWhat makes this fixable now is mundane but decisive: modern tools let us compute per-example gradients cheaply (or just use the last layer), so in the very same backward pass distillation already runs we can read, for each example, the dot product of its task-loss gradient and its distillation-loss gradient. That dot product directly says whether one step toward the teacher would also reduce that example's error. None of the proxy-based controllers ever computed this measured per-example quantity.\n\nWhen this gap closes, distillation gains a per-example trust control that pulls back the teacher exactly on the examples a confident teacher mislabels, recovering accuracy and calibration on that hard subset instead of only nudging an average. The existing adaptive-scalar methods become the special case where the same trust is forced on every example, and learned-loss-form distillation becomes composable with our gating because the two ideas touch different parts of the loss.\n\n## Method\n### Measured Per-Example Payoff\n*Manufacture a label-free per-example readout of whether following the teacher currently lowers that example's task loss.*\n\n1. In the one backward pass that distillation already performs, get, for each example in the batch, two gradients: one from the task term (matching the true label) and one from the distillation term (matching the frozen teacher). Compute these per-example gradients with the functorch/vmap per-sample-gradient tool by default. If that does not fit in GPU memory for your model and batch, take both gradients only over the student's last linear (classifier) layer as a cheaper but still per-example stand-in. Do not change the teacher (it stays frozen) or the loss formula.\n   - _Why_: These two gradients are the raw material for measuring whether the teacher is helping each example, and the backward pass already computes them.\n2. For each example, compute a single number, the payoff, equal to the negative normalized dot product of its task gradient and its distillation gradient (a tiny constant $\\epsilon  =$ 1e-8 is added to the denominator only to avoid dividing by zero). A positive payoff means taking one step toward the teacher would also lower that example's task error (the teacher helps here); a negative payoff means it would raise it (the teacher is confidently wrong here). Using only the last layer makes this a cheap dot product you can run every step.\n\n*The payoff readout $p_{i}$ is the negative directional derivative of the task loss along the distillation gradient; $p_{i}$ greater than 0 means one step toward the teacher would also lower $x_{i}'s$ task loss (teacher helps), $p_{i}$ less than 0 means it would raise it (confident-but-wrong). $\\epsilon  =$ 1e-8.*\n$$ p_i = -\\,\\frac{\\langle \\nabla_{\\theta}\\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{cls}}(x_i),\\ \\nabla_{\\theta}\\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{dist}}(x_i)\\rangle}{\\lVert \\nabla_{\\theta}\\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{dist}}(x_i)\\rVert + \\varepsilon} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The dot product of the two gradients directly measures whether following the teacher and reducing the example's own error point the same way.\n\n### Stabilized Per-Example Trust Controller\n*Turn the readout into a stable per-example weight that reallocates a fixed total trust mass toward examples the teacher helps.*\n\n3. Smooth each example's payoff over time with a running average (an exponential moving average that keeps 0.9 of the old value and adds 0.1 of the new), stored in a table keyed by the example's dataset index. The first time you see an example, set its stored average to that first payoff itself (not to zero) so its first weight reflects the real signal. After that, update it each time the example recurs, so a single noisy step does not swing the weight.\n\n*An exponential moving average per example denoises the single-step payoff estimate; m = 0.9 keyed by dataset index.*\n$$ \\bar{p}_i \\leftarrow m\\,\\bar{p}_i + (1-m)\\,p_i,\\qquad m = 0.9 \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A one-step gradient estimate is noisy early in training, so averaging it over the example's repeat visits gives a steadier signal.\n4. Turn each example's smoothed payoff into a per-example trust weight by passing it through a logistic (S-shaped) function, scaled by how spread-out the payoffs are in the batch (their standard deviation, kept at least a tiny floor of 0.000001 so a flat batch does not blow up) and capped at a maximum trust level $w_{max}$ between 0 and 1. High payoff gives a weight near the cap; low payoff gives a weight near zero. 【author decision: how high to set the maximum trust $w_{max}$ — a low cap never fully trusts even a correct teacher, a cap near 1 lets an example follow the teacher almost entirely.】 This per-example weight is the only thing that changes; the loss form and teacher are untouched.\n\n*A temperature-controlled logistic maps the denoised payoff to a per-example weight; s is the payoff scale (default: batch standard deviation of the denoised payoff) and $w_{max}$ in (0,1] caps maximum teacher trust.*\n$$ w_i = w_{\\max}\\,\\sigma\\!\\left(\\frac{\\bar{p}_i}{s}\\right) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A smooth, bounded function gives each example a trust value that is high where the teacher helps and low where it hurts, without hard on/off jumps.\n5. Rescale the whole batch's weights by multiplying them all by the same factor so their average equals a target trust level $W_{t},$ which grows slowly during training along a cosine curve from 0.1 up to the cap $w_{max}.$ Because every weight is already a positive value at or below the cap, the batch average is always positive, so no special-case guard is needed. This keeps the total amount of teacher trust fixed to what a normal schedule would spend, but moves that trust toward the examples the teacher is currently helping.\n\n*The batch trust budget rescales the per-example weights so their mean equals a slowly-annealed target $W_{t},$ fixing total teacher-trust mass while reallocating it across examples; $W_{t}$ follows a cosine schedule from 0.1 to $w_{max}.$*\n$$ w_i \\leftarrow w_i\\,\\frac{W_t}{\\frac{1}{B}\\sum_{j=1}^{B} w_j} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Without a fixed total budget the label-free weights could drift to trusting the teacher everywhere or nowhere; fixing the average forces the method to reallocate trust rather than escape.\n6. Rebuild the loss with each example's own weight — (1 minus its weight) times its task loss plus its weight times its distillation loss — and take the normal optimizer step. Treat the weights as fixed gates (do not let gradients flow back into the payoff computation that produced them), so the student learns through the two loss terms only. On an example where the teacher is confidently wrong (negative payoff, so a below-average weight), the student now moves toward the true label instead of the teacher's wrong soft target, flipping that example's prediction.\n\n*The per-example mixed objective: each example $x_{i}$ blends its task loss $L_{cls}$ and distillation loss $L_{dist}$ with its own weight $w_{i},$ replacing the single global scalar.*\n$$ \\mathcal{L} = \\frac{1}{B}\\sum_{i=1}^{B}\\big[(1-w_i)\\,\\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{cls}}(x_i) + w_i\\,\\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{dist}}(x_i)\\big] \\tag{5} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Applying the measured per-example trust in the actual update is what a single global dial physically cannot do.\n\n### Mechanism Attribution\n*Show the gain is caused by the example-to-readout correspondence and the per-example locus, not by adaptivity in general.*\n\n7. On a held-out set, separately track two numbers on the subset of examples the teacher gets wrong (the teacher-error subset): the student's top-1 accuracy there, and how well-calibrated the student's confidence is there, measured by Expected Calibration Error (ECE) over fifteen equal-width confidence bins. The teacher's answers are used only to decide which examples belong to this subset; these measurements never feed back into the training weights.\n   - _Why_: The whole point of the method is to recover those specific examples, so that subset is exactly where the gain should appear.\n8. Run a control where you retrain from the same starting point and random seed, identical except that at every step you randomly shuffle the payoffs among the examples within each batch (so the set of payoff values is unchanged but each is attached to the wrong example). Everything else — the average-trust target, the table keying, the optimizer — stays the same, so the teacher-wrong examples are no longer protected. If the benefit really comes from matching the right weight to the right example, scrambling that match should erase the gain; if it survives, the gain was just extra noise in the weights, not the measurement.\n   - _Why_: If the benefit really comes from matching the right weight to the right example, scrambling that match should erase the gain; if it survives, the gain was just extra noise in the weights, not the measurement.\n9. Run a second control that keeps only the sign of each payoff — a high weight (the cap $w_{max})$ when the payoff is positive and a low weight (default 0) otherwise — then rescale to the same average trust; if most of the benefit remains, the sign alone is the useful signal. Then compare the full method, at equal epochs and equal average trust, against fixed-weight distillation, a reimplementation of the importance-scheduled global dial, a teacher-confidence gate, and an adaptive-alpha baseline (Context-Aware Adaptive KD) whose dial is one number per step computed from training progress and applied the same to every example. Making that baseline share its dial across examples means the only difference from our method is going per-example.\n   - _Why_: The sign-only test isolates what part of the payoff matters, and comparing against a method that also moves the dial proves the gain comes from going per-example, not just from adapting at all.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 逐样本教师收益门控：用实测损失效应设定蒸馏权重\n\n**方法名称.** Per-Example Teacher-Payoff Gating (PE-TPG)\n\n## 研究动机\n知识蒸馏(Knowledge Distillation, KD)训练一个小的「学生」模型，同时追两个目标：模仿大的「教师」模型的软预测(蒸馏项)，以及对齐真实标签(任务项)。一个旋钮——混合权重——决定多大程度信任教师。问题在于教师并非在每个样本上都同样可信：在它判错的样本上(尤其是它自信却判错的样本)，模仿教师会主动伤害学生；在学生已经学会的样本上，教师只是提供过时的指导。可是如今这个旋钮是一个全局数字(或固定调度)，只能为整个数据集选一个信任水平，于是必然在某些地方过度信任教师、在另一些地方信任不足。\n\n近期工作让旋钮变得自适应，却始终没测对量。importance-analysis 方法(arXiv 2025-05)用整体的、按批平均的损失趋势来调旋钮；熵平衡的多教师蒸馏 B-MTARD(IEEE TPAMI 2024-06)按教师看起来有多自信来调；MoKD(arXiv 2025-05)用固定规则调和两个平均梯度方向。这些读的都是代理量——步数、教师置信度、平均梯度夹角——没有一个能告诉你：对某个具体样本，跟随教师是否真的会降低这个样本自己的误差。\n\n如今能解决这个问题的原因很朴素却关键：现代工具能廉价地算出逐样本梯度(或干脆只用最后一层),于是在蒸馏本就要做的那同一次反向传播中，我们就能为每个样本读出它的任务损失梯度与蒸馏损失梯度的点积。这个点积直接表明：朝教师走一步是否也会降低这个样本的误差。所有基于代理量的控制器都从未计算过这个实测的逐样本量。\n\n这个缺口一旦补上，蒸馏就获得了逐样本的信任控制：恰好在自信教师判错的样本上收回教师影响，从而在这个困难子集上恢复准确率与校准度，而不仅仅是抬高一个平均数。已有的自适应标量方法就成了「对每个样本强加同一信任」的特例；而可学习损失形状的蒸馏方法也能与我们的门控组合，因为两者作用在损失的不同部分。\n\n## 方法\n### 实测逐样本收益\n*构造一个无标签的逐样本读数，判断当前跟随教师是否会降低该样本的任务损失。*\n\n1. 在蒸馏本就要做的那一次反向传播里，为该批中每个样本取出两个梯度：一个来自任务项（对齐真实标签），一个来自蒸馏项（对齐冻结的教师）。默认用 functorch/vmap 的逐样本梯度(per-sample gradient)工具计算这些逐样本梯度。若在你的模型与批量下装不进 GPU 显存，就只在学生最后一个线性（分类器）层上取这两个梯度，作为更便宜但仍是逐样本的近似。不改教师（教师保持冻结），也不改损失公式。\n   - _为什么_: 这两个梯度是衡量教师是否在帮助每个样本的原料，而反向传播本来就在算它们。\n2. 为每个样本算一个数——收益(payoff)——等于它的任务梯度与蒸馏梯度的负归一化点积（分母上加一个极小常数 $\\epsilon  =$ 1e-8，仅用于避免除零）。收益为正，表示朝教师走一步也会降低这个样本的任务误差（教师在这里有用）；收益为负，表示反而升高（教师在这里自信却判错）。只用最后一层可让它成为每步都能跑的廉价点积。\n\n*收益读数 $p_{i}$ 是任务损失沿蒸馏梯度方向的负方向导数；$p_{i}$ 大于 0 表示朝教师走一步也会降低 $x_{i}$ 的任务损失(教师有用)，$p_{i}$ 小于 0 表示反而升高(自信却错误)。$\\epsilon  =$ 1e-8。*\n$$ p_i = -\\,\\frac{\\langle \\nabla_{\\theta}\\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{cls}}(x_i),\\ \\nabla_{\\theta}\\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{dist}}(x_i)\\rangle}{\\lVert \\nabla_{\\theta}\\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{dist}}(x_i)\\rVert + \\varepsilon} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 两个梯度的点积直接衡量「跟随教师」和「降低该样本自身误差」是否指向同一方向。\n\n### 稳定化逐样本信任控制器\n*把读数转成稳定的逐样本权重，将固定的信任总量挪向教师有帮助的样本。*\n\n3. 对每个样本的收益按时间做平滑：用一个指数滑动平均(exponential moving average, EMA)，保留旧值的 0.9、加上新值的 0.1，存在一张以样本的 dataset index 为键的表里。第一次遇到某样本时，把它的存储均值设为该首次收益本身（而非设为零），使它的首个权重反映真实信号。此后每当该样本再次出现就更新一次，使单步的噪声不会让权重剧烈摆动。\n\n*对每个样本做指数滑动平均(exponential moving average, EMA)以对单步收益估计去噪；m = 0.9，按数据集索引(dataset index)寻址。*\n$$ \\bar{p}_i \\leftarrow m\\,\\bar{p}_i + (1-m)\\,p_i,\\qquad m = 0.9 \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 单步梯度估计在训练早期很吵，按样本的重复出现做平均能得到更稳的信号。\n4. 把每个样本平滑后的收益送入一个 logistic（S 形）函数，转成逐样本信任权重；该函数按这一批收益的离散程度（其标准差，下限保护为极小值 0.000001，以免批近于常数时发散）缩放，并以一个介于 0 与 1 之间的最大信任水平 $w_{max}$ 封顶。收益高，权重接近上限；收益低，权重接近零。【作者需决定：最大信任 $w_{max}$ 设多高——上限低则即使教师正确也不完全信任，上限近 1 则允许某样本几乎完全跟随教师。】唯一改变的就是这个逐样本权重，损失形式和教师都不动。\n\n*用带温度的 $logistic(\\sigma )$ 把去噪后的收益映射成逐样本权重；s 是收益尺度(默认取该批去噪收益的标准差)，$w_{max} \\in $ (0,1] 限制最大教师信任度。*\n$$ w_i = w_{\\max}\\,\\sigma\\!\\left(\\frac{\\bar{p}_i}{s}\\right) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 平滑且有界的函数让每个样本得到一个信任值——教师有用处高、有害处低——而不会出现硬性的开/关跳变。\n5. 把整批权重都乘以同一倍数进行缩放，使其平均值等于目标信任水平 $W_{t}$；$W_{t}$ 在训练中沿余弦曲线从 0.1 缓慢增到上限 $w_{max}$。由于每个权重本就是不超过上限的正值，批平均值总是为正，因此无需特例保护。这让教师信任的总量保持在普通调度会花费的水平，却把这份信任挪向教师当前真正在帮助的样本。\n\n*批级信任预算把逐样本权重整体缩放，使其均值等于缓慢退火的目标 $W_{t}$，固定教师信任总量的同时在样本间重新分配；$W_{t}$ 按余弦调度从 0.1 升到 $w_{max}$。*\n$$ w_i \\leftarrow w_i\\,\\frac{W_t}{\\frac{1}{B}\\sum_{j=1}^{B} w_j} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 没有固定总预算，这些无标签的权重可能漂移到处处信任或处处不信任教师；固定平均值迫使方法重新分配信任，而非整体逃逸。\n6. 用每个样本自己的权重重建损失——（1 减它的权重）乘它的任务损失，加上它的权重乘它的蒸馏损失——并照常做一次优化器更新。把权重当作固定的门控（不让梯度回流到产生它们的收益计算里），使学生只通过两个损失项学习。在教师自信却判错的样本上（收益为负，因而权重低于平均），学生此刻转向真实标签，而非教师错误的软目标，从而翻转该样本的预测。\n\n*逐样本混合目标：每个样本 $x_{i}$ 用自己的权重 $w_{i}$ 混合任务损失 $L_{cls}$ 与蒸馏损失 $L_{dist}$，取代单一全局标量。*\n$$ \\mathcal{L} = \\frac{1}{B}\\sum_{i=1}^{B}\\big[(1-w_i)\\,\\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{cls}}(x_i) + w_i\\,\\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{dist}}(x_i)\\big] \\tag{5} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 把实测的逐样本信任真正用在更新里，正是单个全局旋钮在物理上做不到的。\n\n### 机制归因\n*证明增益来自样本与读数的对应关系及逐样本的控制位置，而非泛泛的自适应。*\n\n7. 在一个留出集上，在教师判错的那部分样本（teacher-error subset）上单独跟踪两个数：学生在该子集的 top-1 准确率，以及学生在该子集的置信度校准程度，用期望校准误差(Expected Calibration Error, ECE)、按十五个等宽置信度分箱衡量。教师的答案仅用于决定哪些样本属于该子集；这些测量绝不回流到训练权重里。\n   - _为什么_: 方法的全部意义就是救回这些特定样本，所以增益正应当出现在这个子集上。\n8. 做一个对照：从相同的起点与随机种子重训，除了每一步都在每个批内随机打乱样本之间的收益（收益的取值集合不变，但每个收益都被挂到错误的样本上）之外，其余全部相同。其他一切——平均信任目标、表的键、优化器——保持不变，因此教师判错的样本不再受保护。如果好处真来自“把对的权重配给对的样本”，打乱这种配对就应抹掉增益；若增益仍在，那它只是权重里多出的噪声，而非那个测量。\n   - _为什么_: 如果好处真来自「把对的权重配给对的样本」，打乱这种配对就应抹掉增益；若增益仍在，那它只是权重里多出的噪声，而非那个测量。\n9. 再做第二个对照：只保留每个收益的符号——收益为正时用高权重（上限 $w_{max}$），否则用低权重（默认 0）——再缩放到同样的平均信任；若大部分好处仍在，说明符号本身就是有用信号。然后在相同轮数、相同平均信任下，把完整方法与以下基线比较：固定权重蒸馏、importance-scheduled 全局旋钮的复现、教师置信度门控，以及一个 adaptive-alpha 基线（Context-Aware Adaptive KD）——它的旋钮是每步一个数、由训练进度计算并对每个样本一视同仁。让该基线的旋钮在样本间共享，意味着它与我们方法的唯一区别就是“是否逐样本”。\n   - _为什么_: 只看符号的测试隔离出收益中真正起作用的部分；而与「同样会动旋钮」的方法比较，能证明增益来自「做到逐样本」，而非仅仅来自「会自适应」。\n\n"},{"id":"32","run_dir":"run_prompt32_codeedit","index":32,"title":"Oracle-Slack: a calibrated instrument for de-biasing instructed-code-edit ability scores","title_zh":"Oracle-Slack：一种用于校正指令式代码编辑能力分数偏差的可标定测量工具","method_name":"Oracle-Slack","hook":"Every instructed-code-edit benchmark reports a single test-pass or reference-match rate as the model's ability, silently assuming one fixed oracle per task stands in for developer intent; we show that this raw rate is a biased estimator of intent-satisfaction whose two opposite-signed error components can be measured on the same edits and folded back into a corrected score with a confidence interval. The instrument relocates the correctness signal from a single fixed oracle to a developer-curated equivalence class of acceptable edits, turning the now-documented but unquantified oracle error into a reusable, uncertainty-bounded correction any benchmark/model pair can be run through.","anchor_pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","anchor_pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","domain_category":"LLM Evaluation & Benchmarking","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf converts the now-documented oracle error of instructed-code-edit benchmarks into a reusable measurement that returns, for any model on any such benchmark, an intent-satisfaction estimate whose deviation from the raw test-pass / reference-match score is itself quantified with uncertainty — the anchor (openalex:W6929144960) shows the raw score is biased but leaves the field with a one-off manual count rather than an instrument that any future benchmark/model pair can be run throu","pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by constructing controlled audit instances in which the confound (oracle slack — the gap between 'passes the fixed oracle' and 'satisfies developer intent') is independently varied against an oracle-independent ground truth (a developer-curated equivalence class of acceptable edits plus a held-out differential-execution check), and reporting the divergence between the raw oracle score and the de-confounded intent-satisfaction score, with a bootstrap confidence interval, as the headline reusable measurement.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf separates the two opposite-signed components of that bias on the SAME edits — false-accepts from an incomplete test suite (edit passes tests but violates the instruction) versus false-rejects from an over-specific oracle (intent-correct edit rejected because it differs from a single reference or trips an irrelevant test) — so even where oracle error is acknowledged it is reported as one undifferentiated number and a benchmark cannot be told whether to add more tests or relax it","pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by partitioning the set of oracle-disagreement events by the discriminating property 'sign of the disagreement' — false-accept events (oracle accepts, equivalence-class rejects) versus false-reject events (oracle rejects, equivalence-class accepts) — and estimating each partition's rate with its own tailored estimator (a falsifying-test-search estimator for false-accepts, an intent-equivalence-membership estimator for false-rejects), with an error decomposition that bounds how the two corrections combine into the net bias of the raw score.","is_anchor":false},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests the assumption, silently inherited by every benchmark leaf (RES-Q semanticscholar:364f84f04c5b71517fa4b57fd1611f5060b9f1de, InstrEditBench openalex:W4416035869, SWE-bench-style scoring behind openalex:W6929144960), that a single fixed oracle per task (one test suite OR one reference diff) is an adequate stand-in for the developer's edit intent — none asks whether intent must instead be represented as an equivalence class of acceptable edits before any ability number is re","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","how_closed":"Closed by naming the load-bearing locus assumption — that the correctness signal lives at a single fixed oracle per task — and relocating it to an overlooked locus, the developer-curated equivalence class of intent-acceptable edits, then (companion controlled_diagnostic_design) shipping the confound-isolating empirical separation: on the same edits, the single-oracle score and the equivalence-class score diverge measurably, falsifying the inherited assumption that one fixed oracle adequately represents intent.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"LLM evaluation for instructed (real-world) code editing","n_papers":40,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":26},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":16,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"SVGEditBench: A Benchmark Dataset for Quantitative Assessment of LLM's SVG Editing Capabilities"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"RES-Q: Evaluating Code-Editing Large Language Model Systems at the Repository Scale"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Mercury: An Efficiency Benchmark for LLM Code Synthesis"},{"source":"openalex","title":"CodeUpdateArena: Benchmarking Knowledge Editing on API Updates"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Detecting hallucinations in large language models using semantic entropy"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Large Language Models in Healthcare and Medical Domain: A Review"}],"more":10},{"year":2025,"n":23,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"LLM Code Customization with Visual Results: A Benchmark on TikZ"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"DSCodeBench: A Realistic Benchmark for Data Science Code Generation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"ParaCoder: Parallel Code Generation with Large Language Model"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Multi-Agent Systems for Dataset Adaptation in Software Engineering: Capabilities, Limitations, and Future Directions"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"ArtifactsBench: Bridging the Visual-Interactive Gap in LLM Code Generation Evaluation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"CodeArena: A Collective Evaluation Platform for LLM Code Generation"}],"more":17},{"year":2026,"n":1,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"}],"more":0}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":29,"share":0.725},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":5,"share":0.125},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":5,"share":0.125},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":4,"share":0.1},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":3,"share":0.075},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":2,"share":0.05},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":2,"share":0.05},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":1,"share":0.025}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Across the retrieved instructed-code-edit evaluations, the success of an edit is decided by an oracle that is a PROXY for, not a measurement of, the developer's edit intent: RES-Q (semanticscholar:364f84f04c5b71517fa4b57fd1611f5060b9f1de) scores a repository edit by running a held-out test suite, InstrEditBench/FineEdit (openalex:W4416035869) scores by matching the produced diff against a single reference edit, and SWE-bench-style resolved-rate is the dominant headline metric — yet the empirical study of SWE-bench (openalex:W6929144960) shows that test-passing patches are frequently NOT what developers intended, and the APR patch-correctness literature (openalex:W4402040396, openalex:W4400959021) shows the same overfitting failure: a held-out suite is incomplete so it admits edits that satisfy the tests while violating the instruction, and a single reference diff is one of many intent-equivalent edits so it rejects correct edits that differ syntactically. The structural failure is that the field reports a single scalar ability number whose gap from the true intent-satisfaction rate is unknown and uncontrolled: nobody can say, for a given benchmark and model, how much of the reported score is genuine instructed-edit ability versus oracle slack (false-accepts from incomplete tests / loose reference matching) minus oracle over-strictness (false-rejects of intent-equivalent edits), because no instrument separates these components on the SAME edits.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W6929144960","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Are 'Solved Issues' in SWE-bench Really Solved Correctly? hand-audits patches that pass SWE-bench tests for three issue-solving tools and reports that a substantial fraction of test-passing patches are plausible-but-incorrect, establishing that the test-pass oracle has a non-trivial false-accept rate. Its residue: the audit is a one-off manual count of false-accepts on a fixed snapshot — it produces no reusable instrument that, given any new model/benchmark, returns a corrected intent-satisfaction estimate with both false-accept AND false-reject components controlled, and it does not attribute WHY a particular edit slips the oracle (incomplete tests vs. instruction underspecification vs. genuine model error). [residue is abstract-level: anchor fulltext unfetchable]"},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4402040396","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Leveraging LLM for Automatic Patch Correctness Assessment trains/prompts an LLM to label APR patches as correct/incorrect to reduce the overfitting (test-pass-but-wrong) review burden, evaluated mostly cross-validation within known APR tools. Its residue: it yields a point classifier whose own error rate is uncalibrated and tool-specific (degrades on unseen tools), so it cannot supply a benchmark-level CORRECTED ability estimate with quantified uncertainty — it relabels patches but does not de-bias the aggregate score."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:364f84f04c5b71517fa4b57fd1611f5060b9f1de","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"RES-Q builds 100 handcrafted repository-edit tasks from real GitHub commits and scores an LLM system by running each task's test suite, explicitly motivated by the need for robust evaluation under prompt sensitivity. Its residue: the score is a raw test-pass rate with no model of oracle error — it neither estimates how many passing edits are intent-violating nor how many intent-correct edits its tests reject, so the reported ability number inherits the unquantified oracle bias the whole area shares."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416035869","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"FineEdit/InstrEditBench scores an instruction-driven edit by matching the produced edit against a single reference modification over 30k structured-editing instances. Its residue: a single reference diff is one representative of an intent-equivalence class, so syntactically different but intent-correct edits are scored as failures (false-rejects) and the metric cannot distinguish 'wrong edit' from 'right edit, different surface form'."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4411522868","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Can LLMs Replace Human Evaluators? studies LLM-as-a-judge for SE tasks as a cheaper alternative to Pass@k and BLEU, reporting variable agreement with humans. Its residue: it treats the LLM judge as a candidate replacement metric and measures its agreement, but does not turn the judge's disagreements with the test oracle into a calibrated correction of the benchmark's aggregate ability score — the judge is a second noisy rater, not a de-biasing instrument."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"LLM evaluation for instructed (real-world) code editing","venue":"ICLR / NeurIPS / ICML (Datasets & Benchmarks or main track methods)","time":"2026","data":["SWE-bench / SWE-bench Verified","RES-Q repository-edit tasks","InstrEditBench instructed-edit pairs","APR overfitting / patch-correctness corpora (e.g. test-based patch clustering datasets)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML + software engineering / LLM evaluation","preference":"both","baseline":"test-pass (Pass@k / resolved-rate) and reference-diff-match oracles, plus LLM-as-a-judge / Agent-as-a-judge graders","limitation":"Existing instructed-code-edit evaluations score an edit by whether it passes a (necessarily incomplete) test suite or matches a reference diff; this conflates 'satisfies the developer's edit intent' with 'passes the available tests', so plausible-but-incorrect edits are scored as successes and the headline ability number is inflated by an unknown, uncontrolled amount.","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The instrument centers on one shared evaluation object, the per-task intent-acceptance set A(task) — the equivalence class of code edits a developer would accept as satisfying the instruction — and measures every benchmark's raw oracle against it. (1) Anchor / C02: for a sample of tasks we build A(task) as an oracle-INDEPENDENT ground truth in three layers so it never reduces to the evaluand judging itself: (i) the original developer reference edit; (ii) human-curated additional accept/reject edits collected by showing annotators the instruction plus candidate edits and asking 'does this satisfy the instruction', producing labeled members and non-members; (iii) a differential-execution behavioral signature computed by running the pre-edit and post-edit programs on an augmented input set (developer tests UNION a fuzzed/property-based input batch) and recording the input-output trace delta, so two edits with identical trace deltas on this batch are treated as behaviorally equivalent members of the same class. A candidate model edit is intent-satisfying iff a human annotator labels it a member OR its differential-execution signature matches a labeled member's signature; this membership oracle is independent of the benchmark's own test suite and of the model under test. The headline measurement is the divergence D = raw_oracle_score - intent_satisfaction_score on the SAME edits, with a bootstrap 95% CI over tasks, reported per (benchmark, model). (2) Sibling / C04: the disagreement events {edit : oracle_decision != membership_decision} are partitioned by sign into FA = {oracle accepts, membership rejects} (false-accepts: passes the incomplete fixed oracle yet violates intent) and FR = {oracle rejects, membership accepts} (false-rejects: intent-correct edit the fixed oracle wrongly fails). Each partition gets a tailored estimator: rate_FA is estimated by a falsifying-evidence search (for each oracle-accepted edit, search the fuzzed input batch and the human accept/reject labels for a witness that the edit violates intent), and rate_FR by intent-equivalence membership (for each oracle-rejected edit, test whether its differential-execution signature matches any labeled accept member). The corrected score is raw_score - rate_FA*(accepted fraction) + rate_FR*(rejected fraction); the error decomposition states net_bias = FR_mass - FA_mass and bounds the corrected-score variance by the two partitions' independent sampling variances, so a benchmark owner reads off WHICH lever to pull (add tests to shrink FA_mass, relax reference matching / widen the accept class to shrink FR_mass). (3) Audit-leg / C01 + companion C02: the inherited assumption 'one fixed oracle per task = intent' is the locus claim; we relocate the correctness signal from that single oracle to the equivalence class A(task) and the companion controlled_diagnostic_design ships the empirical separation — D significantly different from 0 across benchmarks falsifies the assumption. Every quantity is computable from text: raw_oracle_score is the benchmark's reported pass/match decision; membership labels come from human annotation (external oracle); differential-execution signatures are computed by executing both program versions on the fixed fuzzed input batch (computed); the fuzz-batch size B (default 200 inputs per task) and the annotator-agreement threshold tau (default majority of 3 annotators) are named hyperparameters; the accepted/rejected fractions are read from the benchmark's own raw decisions.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The three gaps share one machinery — the equivalence-class object A(task) and its membership oracle — rather than needing separate modules, because the false-accept/false-reject decomposition (gap 1) is literally a sign-partition of the SAME oracle-vs-membership disagreement set the anchor instrument (gap 0) computes, and the audit (gap 2) is the claim that this disagreement is non-zero; the evidence they share machinery is that all three read from D and from membership labels. I considered making the membership oracle itself an LLM-as-judge (cheaper, scalable) but rejected it: C02's circularity reject lesson forbids letting the evaluated population judge itself, and an LLM judge would reintroduce an uncalibrated proxy — exactly the bias the instrument exists to remove — so the membership oracle is anchored to human labels plus mechanistic differential execution. I also considered a single undifferentiated 'oracle error rate' but rejected it because gap 1 requires the opposite-signed split to be actionable.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: take two instructed-code-edit benchmarks (one test-pass-oracle, e.g. RES-Q; one reference-match-oracle, e.g. an InstrEditBench split) and 3-4 LLMs, build the human+differential-execution membership oracle on a 150-task sample per benchmark, and measure the divergence D = raw_oracle_score - intent_satisfaction_score together with the false-accept rate rate_FA and false-reject rate rate_FR. If the instrument works, D is significantly non-zero with a sign that DIFFERS by oracle type — positive (raw over-states ability via false-accepts) on the test-pass benchmark and negative (raw under-states ability via false-rejects) on the reference-match benchmark — and corrected model rankings change at least one pairwise order versus raw rankings. The load-bearing variable is rate_FA, the measured false-accept rate; negative control: replace the human+differential-execution membership oracle with a degenerate membership oracle equal to the benchmark's own fixed oracle (so membership == oracle decision by construction), which forces rate_FA = rate_FR = 0 — under this control the corrected_score must collapse back to the raw_oracle_score and the ranking changes must vanish, confirming that the correction is driven by genuine oracle-independent intent evidence rather than by estimator noise or resampling. Positive control: a stripped-down instrument that uses ONLY the differential-execution falsifying-witness search (no human labels) to estimate rate_FA should already recover most of the false-accept correction and most of the ranking change on the test-pass benchmark, identifying false-accept detection as the dominant driver of the test-pass benchmark's bias.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W6929144960","delta":"They hand-count, on one fixed SWE-bench snapshot, how many test-passing patches are plausible-but-incorrect (false-accepts only); we construct a reusable instrument that returns, for any benchmark/model, a corrected intent-satisfaction score with a bootstrap CI AND the opposite-signed false-REJECT rate they never measure, plus a causal oracle-augmentation check that moves the headline score."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4402040396","delta":"They train an LLM point-classifier that relabels individual APR patches correct/incorrect with its own uncalibrated, tool-specific error; we do not relabel individual edits with a learned judge — we derive an aggregate, uncertainty-bounded benchmark-score correction from an oracle-INDEPENDENT membership ground truth (human + differential execution), so the de-biasing is calibrated rather than a second noisy rater."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416035869","delta":"They score an instructed edit by match to a SINGLE reference diff (one member of the intent class), so syntactically-different correct edits are silently false-rejected; we represent intent as an equivalence CLASS and measure exactly that false-reject mass as rate_FR, converting their unquantified over-strictness into a reported correction."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4404089313","delta":"ChangeGuard validates whether a change preserves runtime BEHAVIOR via learning-guided differential execution; we re-purpose differential execution as one layer of an INTENT-membership oracle (matching an edit to a developer-accepted class for a given instruction, not checking behavior-preservation), and embed it in a benchmark-score de-biasing estimator, which behavior-equivalence checking alone does not provide."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:364f84f04c5b71517fa4b57fd1611f5060b9f1de","delta":"RES-Q reports a raw test-pass rate over 100 handcrafted repo-edit tasks with no model of oracle error; we attach to that raw rate a measured (rate_FA, rate_FR) decomposition and a corrected score, so their number becomes auditable rather than face-value."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W6929144960","what_step_was_missed":"Are 'Solved Issues' in SWE-bench Really Solved Correctly? established the existence of false-accepts by a manual audit on a fixed snapshot, but it never constructed (a) an oracle-INDEPENDENT membership representation (the developer-curated equivalence class plus a differential-execution signature) that could be re-applied to a new benchmark/model without re-doing the manual count, nor (b) the opposite-signed false-reject estimator on the same edits, nor (c) the sign-partitioned error decomposition that turns the two rates into a single corrected score with a confidence interval and an actionable lever; supplying those three constructions is what turns their one-off observation into the reusable instrument."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":280,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"Hard floor does not fire: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict is 'borderline' (no candidate_match=yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat (openalex:W6929144960) is a near-competitor whose subsumption_argument shows the candidate adds the false-reject estimator, the reusable instrument, and the corrected-score-with-CI it never built (addressable and already addressed). recipe_application_check.verdict='applied' on all three legs, so the idea is built from the cited cluster tactics, not the parent gist. The two weight-carrying borderlines (C02 'cannot independently confirm the definition' and C04 'Omitting comparison against...the obvious cheap alternative') are real but non-fatal and best handled as reviewer concerns in Phase 4 (scope the intent-definition claim to the curated acceptance set; add the single-rate-correction baseline to the experiment plan) rather than as a structural rewrite, so the verdict is advance with both surfaced.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf converts the now-documented oracle error of instructed-code-edit benchmarks into a reusable measurement that returns, for any model on any such benchmark, an intent-satisfaction estimate whose deviation from the raw test-pass / reference-match score is itself quantified with uncertainty — the anchor (openalex:W6929144960) shows the raw score is biased but leaves the field with a one-off manual count rather than an instrument that any future benchmark/model pair can be run through.","main_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail when the instrument isolates the confound only inside an artificial regime and never shows the signal transfers to real deployment, or when the diagnostic is circular (validated against the same population/definition it interrogates, e.g. using evaluated models as their own oracle), or when it merely re-confirms an already-documented limitation.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A diagnostic that only re-confirms a shortcut already known in advance, surfacing no previously unmeasurable failure, is read as confirmatory rather than as a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate surfaces the previously-unmeasured opposite-signed false-REJECT rate and a corrected score with a CI plus a causal oracle-augmentation check, not just the already-documented false-accept existence (openalex:W6929144960)."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a synthetic-ground-truth instrument only on synthetic data, without demonstrating that the controlled finding transfers to real-world instances, leaves ecological validity unestablished and undermines the central claim.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism_steps step 9 explicitly re-runs the instrument on a fully real (non-synthetic) benchmark partition to show D persists, meeting the synthetic-to-real transfer demand."},{"lesson_quoted":"Building the instrument around one contested definition of the target property means it cannot independently confirm that the definition is correct, and reviewers flag the resulting circularity.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"Intent-satisfaction is operationalized via human annotation + differential execution rather than a single contested definition, but 'developer intent' remains a partly-contested construct; the instrument bounds its claim to the curated acceptance set, which keeps it from being fully circular but leaves a definitional-scope concern."},{"lesson_quoted":"Resting an unsupervised evaluation on the unverified premise that the systems under test can reliably judge one another stakes the entire method on an assumption that collapses under scrutiny.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The membership oracle is explicitly oracle-INDEPENDENT (human labels + mechanistic differential execution), not the evaluated models judging themselves; core_mechanism_reasoning records rejecting an LLM-judge membership oracle for exactly this reason."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pairing a single-task or small-sample instrument with broad capability claims triggers a scope-mismatch rejection, and assembling retrieval or engineering blocks without an isolating scientific insight reads as application rather than research.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The claim is scoped to instructed-code-edit benchmarks with a fixed oracle and tested on two oracle types over 150-task samples; the isolating insight (oracle slack decomposed by sign) is the contribution, not an engineering assembly."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf separates the two opposite-signed components of that bias on the SAME edits — false-accepts from an incomplete test suite (edit passes tests but violates the instruction) versus false-rejects from an over-specific oracle (intent-correct edit rejected because it differs from a single reference or trips an irrelevant test) — so even where oracle error is acknowledged it is reported as one undifferentiated number and a benchmark cannot be told whether to add more tests or relax its reference matching.","main_pattern":"heterogeneous_decomposition","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is treating the partition criterion itself as the contribution while leaving its value unproven (a discriminator reviewers map onto a known technique), and validating in a regime where the bottleneck does not bite or against no strong uniform baseline.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Presenting a sensitivity or redundancy proxy as the novelty invites the verdict that it rediscovers known mixed-precision or low-rank results unless it is sharply differentiated from the obvious prior criterion.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The partition criterion here is the SIGN of the oracle-vs-intent disagreement (false-accept vs false-reject), a measurement-validity discriminator with no mixed-precision/low-rank analogue; it is not presented as the whole novelty (the corrected-score estimator is)."},{"lesson_quoted":"Omitting comparison against both the strongest uniform baseline and the obvious cheap alternative leaves reviewers unable to tell whether the partition buys anything at all.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The uniform-vs-differentiated comparison maps to 'one undifferentiated oracle-error rate vs the FA/FR split'; the candidate argues the split is actionable (which lever to pull) but does not yet spell out a head-to-head against a single-rate correction as an explicit baseline."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a storage or throughput claim only on toy-scale models — where the compression bottleneck does not actually bite — undermines the entire motivation no matter how clean the method is.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Validation is on real instructed-edit benchmarks where oracle error is documented to bite (openalex:W6929144960), not a toy regime."},{"lesson_quoted":"Skipping any analysis of why the heterogeneity exists — the data or value distribution that drives the partition — makes the technical novelty and the potential impact impossible to assess.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The heterogeneity (two opposite-signed error sources with different causes: incomplete tests vs over-specific reference) is characterized mechanistically and tied to distinct corrective levers."},{"lesson_quoted":"Bolting together established components (distillation plus pruning plus calibration) without an error bound or artifact specific to the new setting reads as incremental even when the target application is timely and important.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate supplies a setting-specific error decomposition (net_bias = FR_mass - FA_mass with a variance bound) that is the spine of the contribution, not a bolt-together."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests the assumption, silently inherited by every benchmark leaf (RES-Q semanticscholar:364f84f04c5b71517fa4b57fd1611f5060b9f1de, InstrEditBench openalex:W4416035869, SWE-bench-style scoring behind openalex:W6929144960), that a single fixed oracle per task (one test suite OR one reference diff) is an adequate stand-in for the developer's edit intent — none asks whether intent must instead be represented as an equivalence class of acceptable edits before any ability number is read off.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is a relocation demonstrated but not adversarially closed, or a novelty-boundary collapse where the 'new' locus turns out to be one prior work already used, or reintroducing the very assumption the relocation was meant to dissolve (e.g. depending on a clean reference), or offering only a demonstration with no mechanistic account of why the locus carries the signal.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work — normalization statistics, activation-similarity losses, semantic concept triggers — collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The 'overlooked locus' (an equivalence class of acceptable edits) overlaps in spirit with ChangeGuard's differential-execution behavior locus (openalex:W4404089313) and the SWE-bench manual audit (openalex:W6929144960); differentiation_from_lit makes the difference explicit (intent-membership vs behavior-preservation; reusable instrument vs one-off count) but the boundary needs to stay sharp."},{"lesson_quoted":"A defense whose relocation silently depends on a clean reference model or a known anomaly distribution reintroduces precisely the strong assumption the move was supposed to eliminate.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The relocation does not depend on a single clean reference — it explicitly replaces the single-reference assumption with a multi-member equivalence class built from human labels + execution signatures, which is the dissolution of the audited assumption, not its reintroduction."},{"lesson_quoted":"Demonstrating the new locus only on fixed, non-adaptive or outdated baselines while omitting any account of why it works reads as a stacked pipeline of existing components rather than a principled shift.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism gives the mechanistic account (incomplete tests cause false-accepts, single-reference causes false-rejects) and the negative/positive controls test the locus claim causally, not merely demonstratively."},{"lesson_quoted":"Wiring off-the-shelf generators or tools into a new attack setting without a structural reason for the locus change gets judged as engineering integration, not insight.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The locus change is motivated structurally (a single oracle is one member of an intent-equivalence class, so it cannot represent intent without false-accepts and false-rejects), not by convenience of available tooling."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No gap_closure entry triggers a Reject lesson with candidate_match=yes, so the hard floor does not fire. The borderlines that carry weight are C02's circularity lesson ('Building the instrument around one contested definition...cannot independently confirm the definition') on the anchor and C04's missing-uniform-baseline lesson ('Omitting comparison against...the obvious cheap alternative') on the decomposition leg — both touch load-bearing properties (the ground-truth definition and the single-rate-vs-FA/FR-split baseline)."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf converts the now-documented oracle error of instructed-code-edit benchmarks into a reusable measurement...","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Construct a controlled set of evaluation instances in which exactly one named confound is structurally blocked or independently varied, paired with an oracle INDEPENDENT of the system under test, and report the divergence between apparent and de-confounded performance as the primary result rather than an aggregate leaderboard score.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism step (1) names the confound (oracle slack), builds the oracle-independent ground truth A(task) (human labels + differential execution, explicitly NOT the benchmark's own oracle nor the model under test), and the headline measurement is D = raw_oracle_score - intent_satisfaction_score with a bootstrap CI — exactly the apparent-minus-deconfounded divergence the cluster reports as primary.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf separates the two opposite-signed components of that bias on the SAME edits...","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Discriminate components by a measurable property into structurally distinct populations and apply a treatment matched to each, backed by an error/fidelity decomposition that bounds how the differentiated treatment recovers the original objective — that analysis, not the partition idea, is the contribution.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism step (2) partitions the disagreement events by the sign property into FA and FR populations, assigns each a tailored estimator (falsifying-witness search for FA; signature-match for FR), and supplies the error decomposition net_bias = FR_mass - FA_mass with a variance bound — the cluster's load-bearing decomposition artifact.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests the assumption...that a single fixed oracle per task...is an adequate stand-in for the developer's edit intent...","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Name the single representational locus current methods all operate on, state the tacit sufficiency/invariance claim bolted to it as falsifiable, then relocate the signal to an overlooked locus and demonstrate the property manifests there, with a mechanistic account of why the new locus carries the signal.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism leg (3) names the locus (single fixed oracle per task), states the falsifiable claim (oracle = intent), relocates to the overlooked locus (equivalence class A(task)), and the companion controlled_diagnostic_design ships the empirical separation (D != 0) that falsifies the claim — the signature relocate-and-falsify move of C01.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"All three legs perform their cited cluster's signature move: C02's apparent-vs-deconfounded divergence with an independent oracle, C04's sign-partition with a bounding error decomposition, and C01's locus relocation with a mechanistic falsification; none collapses to the parent pattern's generic gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["controlled_diagnostic_design","heterogeneous_decomposition","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"The three reject-favored compositions all pair heterogeneous_decomposition with self_supervised_signal_engineering, structural_prior_encoding, or architectural_operator_substitution; here heterogeneous_decomposition pairs only with controlled_diagnostic_design and assumption_audit_and_pivot, so no 2-way subset matches a documented anti-pattern."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"openalex:W6929144960","threat_source":"lit_table","subsumption_argument":"Are 'Solved Issues' in SWE-bench Really Solved Correctly? is the most specific competitor because it already establishes that test-passing patches are frequently intent-violating, so a reviewer could ask whether the candidate merely re-packages a known false-accept finding. The candidate stands because it adds three constructions that paper lacks — an oracle-independent reusable membership representation, the opposite-signed false-reject estimator on the same edits, and a sign-partitioned corrected score with a CI plus a causal oracle-augmentation check — none of which follow from a one-off manual false-accept count; it would only fall if that paper had itself shipped a reusable, two-sided, uncertainty-bounded de-biasing instrument, which it did not.","addressable_via":"differentiation_from_lit[0].delta already sharpens the boundary by naming the false-reject side, the reusable instrument, and the causal check as the deltas over the manual count; keeping that delta load-bearing dodges the threat."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Oracle-Slack: A Calibrated Instrument for De-biasing Instructed-Code-Edit Ability Scores\n\n**Method.** Oracle-Slack\n\n## Motivation\nBenchmarks that test whether a language model can edit code as instructed usually report one number: the fraction of edits that pass a test suite, or that match a reference edit the developer wrote. Both of these are stand-ins for the real question — did the edit do what the instruction asked? — and both are imperfect. A test suite is never complete, so an edit can pass the tests while still doing the wrong thing (a false-accept). A single reference edit is just one of many correct ways to satisfy the instruction, so a correct edit that looks different gets marked wrong (a false-reject). Because of this, the headline ability number is off by an unknown amount, and nobody can say how much of a model's reported score is real skill versus oracle leakage.\n\nThis is timely because a recent manual study of SWE-bench (openalex:W6929144960, arXiv 2025) showed that many test-passing patches are actually wrong, confirming the false-accept problem is real and not hypothetical. But that study was a hand-count on one fixed snapshot — it built no reusable tool, and it never looked at the false-reject side. Meanwhile, differential execution (running the old and new code on many inputs and comparing behavior, as in ChangeGuard, openalex:W4404089313, arXiv 2024) now gives us a mechanical, oracle-independent way to tell when two edits behave the same, and benchmarks of both kinds (test-pass and reference-match) are publicly available to test on.\n\nPrior work stopped short for structural reasons. The SWE-bench audit (openalex:W6929144960) had no measurement apparatus that could be re-applied to a new benchmark without redoing the manual labeling, and it ignored false-rejects. The patch-correctness classifier work (openalex:W4402040396, IEEE TSE 2024) added a second learned rater with its own uncalibrated error instead of an oracle-independent ground truth, so it could relabel patches but not de-bias the aggregate score. FineEdit/InstrEditBench (openalex:W4416035869) kept scoring against a single reference, so it never measured how many correct edits it was wrongly rejecting.\n\nWhen this gap closes, a benchmark can report a corrected intent-satisfaction score with a confidence interval instead of a raw rate, and can be told which fix it needs — add more tests to cut false-accepts, or loosen reference matching to cut false-rejects. Published scores become auditable, model rankings can be re-read on the corrected scale, and the one-off SWE-bench audit becomes just the false-accept-only special case of a general, two-sided tool.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n\n1. Pick an instructed-edit benchmark that ships a fixed oracle — either a test-pass oracle (a held-out test suite, e.g. RES-Q) or a reference-diff oracle (matches against one developer edit, e.g. an InstrEditBench split) — and 3-4 models to evaluate. Treat one edit as one model's complete patch for one task (a unified diff against the original code). For every edit, copy down the benchmark's own accept/reject decision (do not recompute it), and record each task's instruction and original code. Then count the fraction of all edits the oracle accepted $(p_{acc})$ and rejected $(p_{rej}).$\n   - _Why_: This is the raw score we suspect is biased — we need the oracle's own decisions on each edit before we can show how far off they are.\n\n### Intent-acceptance ground truth\n*Build an oracle-independent equivalence class of acceptable edits from human labels plus differential-execution signatures.*\n\n2. On a stratified sample of K=150 tasks, build the human side of the acceptable-edit set. Stratify so both contested and easy tasks appear: bin tasks by how often the oracle accepted their edits, crossed with reference-edit size, and sample proportionally. For each task, collect the developer's reference edit plus one edit from each of 2-3 extra generator models held out from the 3-4 models being evaluated (sampling at temperature 0.8 for variety, so the models under test do not judge themselves). Show each annotator one (instruction, original code, candidate-edit diff) and ask a yes/no 'does this satisfy the instruction?' with a one-line reason; an edit is a member if a majority of 3 say yes (2 of 3). Record the inter-annotator agreement (Krippendorff's alpha). 【author decision: the labeling guideline must settle whether an edit that does what the instruction asks but breaks something unrelated still counts as acceptable — strict (nothing else may break) versus scoped (only the instructed behavior is judged) — because this changes which edits enter the accepted set and thus the measured false-reject rate.】\n   - _Why_: Humans judging the instruction directly give an independent definition of intent that does not depend on the benchmark's tests or on the model being graded.\n3. For each task, build a fixed input batch: the developer's own tests plus B=200 auto-generated inputs from a property-based generator (e.g. Hypothesis) driven by the edited function's argument types and seeded from values found in the developer tests, so the inputs stay realistic. Run the old code and the new code on every input inside a sandbox with a 5-second-per-input timeout, and for each input store what the code did: its return value (as text), any exception type it raised, and the ordered list of its side effects / printed output. Run each input twice with fixed random seeds and discard any input where even the old code is non-deterministic. The edit's behavioral signature is the list, over all inputs, of how the new code's behavior compared to the old (same / different / one of them errored), where 'same' uses a sensible comparator (exact for plain values; near-equal for floats; order-insensitive for sets and dicts; order-sensitive for lists). Two edits behave the same only if their signatures agree on every input.\n   - _Why_: A mechanical behavioral fingerprint lets membership extend to edits no human labeled, scaling the ground truth without a learned, error-prone judge.\n4. Decide whether each edit belongs to the acceptable-edit class (this is the ground truth that never reuses the benchmark's oracle). An edit is a member if EITHER a majority of human annotators called it a member (from step 2 (On a stratified sample of $K=150\\dots ))$ OR its behavioral signature exactly matches the signature of some human-accepted member on every input in the batch (from step 3 (For each task)). Require an exact full-batch match, not a partial one: since the developer's own tests are part of the batch, any real difference in behavior already breaks the match, so allowing slack would let a genuinely different edit sneak in as acceptable. Compute this member/non-member answer once per edit.\n\n*Membership of an edit e in the intent-acceptance set: 1 if a majority of annotators label e a member, OR its differential-execution signature over the fixed input batch B matches the signature of some labeled member e' in the accept set $M^{+}.$*\n$$ m(e) = \\mathbb{1}\\big[\\,\\text{human-maj}(e) = \\text{member} \\;\\lor\\; \\exists\\, e' \\in M^{+}:\\ \\mathrm{sig}_B(e) = \\mathrm{sig}_B(e')\\,\\big] \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Combining human judgment with behavioral equivalence gives a robust 'is this edit acceptable' answer that never reuses the benchmark's own oracle.\n\n### Divergence measurement\n*Quantify how far the raw oracle score is from intent-satisfaction, with a confidence interval.*\n\n5. On the very same edits, compute two scores: the raw oracle score (fraction the oracle accepted) and the intent-satisfaction score (fraction that are members of the acceptable-edit class). Their difference D (Eq. 2) is the headline number — how much the raw score over- or under-states real ability. Put a 95% confidence interval on D by resampling whole TASKS with replacement (not individual edits, because edits in the same task are correlated through the shared instruction and oracle): redraw the set of tasks 10,000 times, recompute D each time, and take the middle 95% of those values. Report D and its interval separately for each benchmark and model.\n\n*The headline divergence D is the raw oracle score minus the intent-satisfaction score on the same N edits, i.e. the mean over edits of the oracle decision o(e) minus the membership decision m(e); a bootstrap over tasks gives its 95% confidence interval.*\n$$ D \\;=\\; \\widehat{s}_{\\text{raw}} - \\widehat{s}_{\\text{intent}} \\;=\\; \\frac{1}{N}\\sum_{i=1}^{N}\\big(o(e_i) - m(e_i)\\big) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: D is the headline number — how much the raw score over- or under-states real ability — and the interval says how sure we are.\n\n### Sign-decomposed correction\n*Split oracle error into false-accepts and false-rejects and fold them into a corrected score plus an actionable lever.*\n\n6. Look at the edits where the oracle and the ground truth disagree and split them by direction (Eq. 3): false-accepts are edits the oracle accepted but the ground truth rejects; false-rejects are edits the oracle rejected but the ground truth accepts. Estimate the false-accept rate by hunting for a witness that an accepted edit is actually wrong — a majority human non-member vote, or an input in the batch where it behaves differently from the developer reference — and divide by how many edits the oracle accepted. Estimate the false-reject rate by checking whether a rejected edit is in fact a member (by human vote or matching signature, using the single membership answer from step 4 (Decide whether each edit belongs $to\\dots ))$ and dividing by how many edits the oracle rejected. Because membership is the one answer computed per edit, no edit is counted twice across the human and signature routes.\n\n*The oracle-vs-intent disagreement set splits by sign into false-accepts FA (oracle accepts, intent rejects) and false-rejects FR (oracle rejects, intent accepts); the net bias of the raw score equals the false-reject mass minus the false-accept mass.*\n$$ \\mathrm{FA} = \\{e : o(e){=}1,\\ m(e){=}0\\},\\quad \\mathrm{FR} = \\{e : o(e){=}0,\\ m(e){=}1\\},\\quad \\text{net\\_bias} = \\underbrace{|\\mathrm{FR}|/N}_{\\text{FR\\_mass}} - \\underbrace{|\\mathrm{FA}|/N}_{\\text{FA\\_mass}} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The two errors have opposite signs and different cures, so a single combined error rate can't tell a benchmark which fix it needs.\n7. Correct the raw score (Eq. 4): subtract the false-accept rate times the accepted fraction, then add the false-reject rate times the rejected fraction. Report the net bias (false-reject mass minus false-accept mass). Get a confidence interval by treating the two rates as proportions measured on two separate, non-overlapping groups of edits (the oracle-accepted ones and the oracle-rejected ones): each has the usual proportion variance $p(1- p)/n,$ and because the groups don't overlap the two add independently — the corrected score's interval is $corrected_{score}$ plus or minus 1.96 times the square root of that combined variance. State which lever to pull: add tests if false-accepts dominate, loosen reference matching if false-rejects dominate. Finally, compare against a simpler baseline that lumps all disagreements into one rate and subtracts it evenly — that baseline can never show a sign-dependent bias, which is exactly what the split buys you.\n\n*The corrected score subtracts the false-accept rate times the accepted fraction and adds the false-reject rate times the rejected fraction; its variance is bounded by the two partitions' independent sampling variances, giving the corrected-score confidence interval.*\n$$ \\widehat{s}_{\\text{corr}} = \\widehat{s}_{\\text{raw}} - \\widehat{r}_{\\mathrm{FA}}\\cdot p_{\\text{acc}} + \\widehat{r}_{\\mathrm{FR}}\\cdot p_{\\text{rej}}, \\qquad \\widehat{\\mathrm{Var}}(\\widehat{s}_{\\text{corr}}) = p_{\\text{acc}}^2\\,\\widehat{\\mathrm{Var}}(\\widehat{r}_{\\mathrm{FA}}) + p_{\\text{rej}}^2\\,\\widehat{\\mathrm{Var}}(\\widehat{r}_{\\mathrm{FR}}) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This turns the two measured errors into one corrected, uncertainty-bounded score and a concrete recommendation.\n\n### Validity and shipping\n*Causally confirm the correction, show it transfers to real data, and package the reusable protocol.*\n\n8. Set aside 30% of the 150 tasks that were not used to fit any rate, picked with the same stratification as before. On these, do a cause-and-effect check: take the witness inputs you found while estimating false-accepts and turn each into a real test that asserts the developer-reference behavior on that input, add it to the benchmark's test suite, and re-run the oracle. The previously false-accepted edits should now fail, so the raw score should drop toward the intent score on these tasks — meaning the headline ability number itself moves, not just an internal rate. 【author decision: a reference-match benchmark has no test suite to add to; the authors must pick the matching way to tighten that oracle — for example adding the witness's expected output as a second accepted reference, or attaching an executable behavioral check — deciding between tightening via extra accepted references versus extra executable checks.】\n   - _Why_: If patching the oracle actually moves the downstream score the way predicted, the divergence was real and causal, not a labeling quirk.\n9. Re-run the measurement and correction (steps 5-7) on a real slice of the benchmark — tasks whose edits are genuine model submissions to a public harness or leaderboard, rather than the varied edits you generated earlier just to build the labeled set — using the same acceptable-edit machinery, and confirm D keeps the same sign and stays significant. This shows the effect survives outside the synthetic setup. Then wrap the whole pipeline into a reusable tool: given a small adapter that exposes each task's instruction, original code, and oracle, plus a set of model edits, it returns the raw score, the corrected score with its confidence interval, the false-accept rate, the false-reject rate, and the recommended lever.\n   - _Why_: Showing the effect survives on real data, and shipping a reusable tool, is what makes this an instrument rather than a one-off study.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# Oracle-Slack：一种用于校正指令式代码编辑能力分数偏差的可标定测量工具\n\n**方法名称.** Oracle-Slack\n\n## 研究动机\n测试语言模型能否按指令编辑代码的基准，通常只报告一个数字：编辑通过测试套件的比例，或与开发者写的参考编辑相匹配的比例。这两者都只是真正问题（编辑是否做到了指令要求的事）的替身，而且都不完美。测试套件永远不完整，所以一个编辑可能通过了测试却做错了事（false-accept，假接受）；单一参考编辑只是满足指令的众多正确方式之一，所以一个看起来不同的正确编辑会被判为错误（false-reject，假拒绝）。因此，那个头条能力数字偏差了一个未知的量，没人能说清模型分数里有多少是真本事、有多少是 oracle 泄漏。\n\n现在做这件事正当其时：最近一项对 SWE-bench 的人工研究（openalex:W6929144960，arXiv 2025）表明许多通过测试的补丁其实是错的，证实了假接受问题真实存在而非假设。但那项研究只是对一个固定快照的人工清点——它没有构建可复用工具，也完全没看假拒绝那一侧。与此同时，差分执行（在大量输入上运行新旧代码并比较行为，如 ChangeGuard，openalex:W4404089313，arXiv 2024）现在给了我们一种机械的、与 oracle 无关的方式来判断两个编辑是否行为相同，而且两类基准（测试通过型与参考匹配型）都已公开可供验证。\n\n以往工作因结构性原因止步于此。SWE-bench 审计（openalex:W6929144960）没有可在新基准上免去重新人工标注就复用的测量装置，且忽略了假拒绝。补丁正确性分类器工作（openalex:W4402040396，IEEE TSE 2024）加入的是一个带有自身未标定误差的第二个学习型评判者，而非与 oracle 无关的真值，因此它只能重新标注补丁，无法校正聚合分数的偏差。FineEdit/InstrEditBench（openalex:W4416035869）仍按单一参考评分，所以从未测量它错误拒绝了多少正确编辑。\n\n当这个空白被填补，基准就能报告带置信区间的校正后意图满足分数，而非原始比率，并能被告知它需要哪种修复——增加测试以减少假接受，或放宽参考匹配以减少假拒绝。已发表的分数变得可审计，模型排名可在校正后的尺度上重新解读，而那个一次性的 SWE-bench 审计也就成了一个通用双向工具中仅含假接受的特例。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景\n\n1. 选一个自带固定 oracle 的指令式编辑基准——要么是测试通过型 oracle（一套留出测试，如 RES-Q），要么是参考差异型 oracle（与单个开发者编辑做匹配，如某个 InstrEditBench split）——再选 3-4 个待评测模型。把“一个编辑”固定为某模型对某任务给出的完整补丁（相对原始代码的 unified diff）。对每个编辑，照抄基准自己的接受/拒绝判定 o(e)（不要重算），并记录每个任务的指令与编辑前代码。然后统计所有编辑中 oracle 接受的比例 $p_{acc}$ 与拒绝的比例 $p_{rej}$。\n   - _为什么_: 这就是我们怀疑有偏的原始分数——在证明它偏多少之前，需要先拿到 oracle 对每个编辑的判定。\n\n### 意图接受真值\n*由人工标签加差分执行签名，构建与 oracle 无关的可接受编辑等价类。*\n\n2. 在 K=150 个分层抽样任务上，构建可接受编辑集合的人工层。分层方式要让有争议和容易的任务都出现：按 oracle 接受该任务编辑的频率分箱，再与参考编辑的规模交叉，按比例抽样。对每个任务，收集开发者参考编辑，外加 2-3 个额外生成模型各一条编辑，这些生成模型要从 第1步（选一个自带固定$\\dots $） 待评测的 3-4 个模型中留出（用 temperature 0.8 采样以增加多样性，避免被评测模型自评）。把每条 (指令、原始代码、候选编辑 diff) 展示给 3 名标注者，让其二选一回答“是否满足指令？”并附一句理由；某编辑获 3 人中多数（2/3）通过即为成员。记录标注者间一致性（Krippendorff's alpha）。【作者需决定：标注规范必须明确——一个做到了指令要求、但引入了无关回归的编辑是否仍算成员——严格口径（不得破坏其它任何东西）还是限定口径（只评判指令涉及的行为），这会改变哪些编辑进入接受集 $M^{+}$，从而改变测得的 false-reject 率。】\n   - _为什么_: 人工直接对照指令判断，给出一个不依赖基准测试、也不依赖被评分模型的独立意图定义。\n3. 为每个任务构造固定输入批次：开发者自己的测试，加上 B=200 个由性质化生成器（如 Hypothesis）自动生成的输入，生成器以被编辑函数的参数类型为依据，并用开发者测试中出现的取值做种子，使输入贴近真实分布。在沙箱里对每个输入运行旧代码和新代码（每个输入 5 秒超时），并为每个输入记录代码做了什么：返回值（转为文本）、抛出的异常类型，以及有序的副作用/打印输出列表。每个输入用固定随机种子跑两遍，丢弃那些连旧代码本身都不确定的输入。该编辑的行为签名(behavioral signature)就是在所有输入上、新代码相对旧代码行为如何的列表（相同/不同/某一方报错），其中“相同”采用合理的比较器（基本类型精确比较；浮点用近似相等；集合与字典做与顺序无关的深比较；列表做与顺序相关的比较）。两个编辑只有在每个输入上签名都一致时才算行为相同。\n   - _为什么_: 机械的行为指纹让成员判定可扩展到无人标注的编辑，在不引入易出错学习型评判者的情况下扩大真值规模。\n4. 判定每个编辑是否属于可接受编辑类（这就是绝不复用基准 oracle 的真值）。某编辑为成员的条件是：要么多数人工标注者将其标为成员（来自 第2步（在 $K=150\\dots $）），要么它的行为签名在批次的每个输入上都与某个人工接受成员的签名完全相同（来自 第3步（为每个任务构造固定输入批次））。要求整批精确匹配，而非部分匹配：由于开发者自己的测试就在批次里，任何真实的行为差异都会让匹配失败，所以一旦放宽就会让一个行为确实不同的编辑混进可接受集合。对每个编辑只算一次这个成员/非成员答案。\n\n*编辑 e 是否属于意图接受集合的判定：当多数标注者把 e 标为成员，或者 e 在固定输入批次 B 上的差分执行签名与某个已标注接受成员 e'（属于接受集 $M^{+}$）的签名相同时取 1。*\n$$ m(e) = \\mathbb{1}\\big[\\,\\text{human-maj}(e) = \\text{member} \\;\\lor\\; \\exists\\, e' \\in M^{+}:\\ \\mathrm{sig}_B(e) = \\mathrm{sig}_B(e')\\,\\big] \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 把人工判断与行为等价结合，给出稳健的“这个编辑是否可接受”答案，且绝不复用基准自身的 oracle。\n\n### 偏差测量\n*量化原始 oracle 分数离意图满足有多远，并给出置信区间。*\n\n5. 在完全相同的编辑上计算两个分数：原始 oracle 分数（oracle 接受的比例）与意图满足分数（属于可接受编辑类的比例）。二者之差 D（式 2）就是头条数字——原始分数高估或低估真实能力多少。给 D 加 95% 置信区间的办法是对整个“任务”做有放回重抽样（不是对单个编辑，因为同一任务内的编辑通过共享指令与 oracle 而相关）：把任务集合重抽 10,000 次，每次重算 D，取这些值的中间 95%。按每个基准和每个模型分别报告 D 及其区间。\n\n*核心偏差 D 等于同一批 N 个编辑上的原始 oracle 分数减去意图满足分数，即每个编辑的 oracle 判定 o(e) 与成员判定 m(e) 之差的均值；对任务做 bootstrap 即得其 95% 置信区间。*\n$$ D \\;=\\; \\widehat{s}_{\\text{raw}} - \\widehat{s}_{\\text{intent}} \\;=\\; \\frac{1}{N}\\sum_{i=1}^{N}\\big(o(e_i) - m(e_i)\\big) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: D 就是头条数字——原始分数高估或低估真实能力多少——而区间表明我们有多确信。\n\n### 按符号分解的校正\n*把 oracle 误差拆成 false-accept 与 false-reject，并折算成校正分数加一条可执行杠杆。*\n\n6. 看 oracle 与真值发生分歧的编辑，并按方向拆开（式 3）：false-accept 是 oracle 接受、但真值拒绝的编辑；false-reject 是 oracle 拒绝、但真值接受的编辑。估 false-accept 率的办法是为“某个被接受编辑其实是错的”寻找证据——多数人工判其非成员，或批次中存在某个输入使它的行为与开发者参考(developer reference)不同——再除以 oracle 接受的编辑数。估 false-reject 率的办法是检查某个被拒绝编辑是否其实是成员（依据人工票或签名匹配，用 第4步（判定每个编辑是否属于可接受编$\\dots $） 给出的那个唯一成员判定），再除以 oracle 拒绝的编辑数。由于成员判定是每个编辑只算一次，所以人工路线与签名路线不会把同一编辑重复计数。\n\n*oracle 与意图的分歧集按符号拆成 false-accept（FA：oracle 接受、意图拒绝）与 false-reject（FR：oracle 拒绝、意图接受）两部分；原始分数的净偏差等于 FR 质量减去 FA 质量。*\n$$ \\mathrm{FA} = \\{e : o(e){=}1,\\ m(e){=}0\\},\\quad \\mathrm{FR} = \\{e : o(e){=}0,\\ m(e){=}1\\},\\quad \\text{net\\_bias} = \\underbrace{|\\mathrm{FR}|/N}_{\\text{FR\\_mass}} - \\underbrace{|\\mathrm{FA}|/N}_{\\text{FA\\_mass}} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这两类错误符号相反、补救手段不同，单一合并误差率无法告诉基准它需要哪种修复。\n7. 校正原始分数（式 4）：减去 false-accept 率乘以被接受比例，再加上 false-reject 率乘以被拒绝比例。报告净偏差（FR 质量减 FA 质量）。求置信区间的办法是把两个率看作在两个互不重叠的编辑组（oracle 接受组与 oracle 拒绝组）上测得的比例：每组都有常见的比例方差 $p(1- p)/n$，且因两组不重叠，二者独立相加——校正分数的区间就是 $corrected_{score}$ 加减 1.96 乘以该合并方差的平方根。说明该拉哪个杠杆：若 false-accept 占主导就增加测试，若 false-reject 占主导就放宽参考匹配。最后，与一个更简单的基线对比：该基线把所有分歧合并成一个率并均匀扣除——它永远无法体现随符号变化的偏差，而这正是按符号拆分带来的价值。\n\n*校正分数在原始分数上减去 false-accept 率乘以被接受比例、加上 false-reject 率乘以被拒绝比例；其方差由两个分区各自的独立采样方差界定，从而给出校正分数的置信区间。*\n$$ \\widehat{s}_{\\text{corr}} = \\widehat{s}_{\\text{raw}} - \\widehat{r}_{\\mathrm{FA}}\\cdot p_{\\text{acc}} + \\widehat{r}_{\\mathrm{FR}}\\cdot p_{\\text{rej}}, \\qquad \\widehat{\\mathrm{Var}}(\\widehat{s}_{\\text{corr}}) = p_{\\text{acc}}^2\\,\\widehat{\\mathrm{Var}}(\\widehat{r}_{\\mathrm{FA}}) + p_{\\text{rej}}^2\\,\\widehat{\\mathrm{Var}}(\\widehat{r}_{\\mathrm{FR}}) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这把两个测得的误差变成一个校正后、带不确定性界的分数，外加一条具体建议。\n\n### 有效性与交付\n*因果性确认校正、证明其迁移到真实数据，并打包可复用协议。*\n\n8. 留出 150 个任务中 30%、且未用于拟合任何率的任务，按与前面相同的分层抽取。在这些任务上做因果检验：把估 false-accept 时找到的证据输入，各自变成一个断言开发者参考在该输入上行为的真实测试，加入基准的测试套件，然后重跑 oracle。先前被假接受的编辑现在应当失败，于是这些任务上的原始分数应向意图分数靠拢——也就是头条能力数字本身发生移动，而不只是某个内部率。【作者需决定：参考匹配型基准没有测试套件可供添加；作者必须选择与之对应的 oracle 收紧方式——例如把证据的期望输出作为第二个被接受参考加入，或附加一个可执行的行为断言——在“通过增加被接受参考收紧”与“通过增加可执行检查收紧”之间做选择。】\n   - _为什么_: 如果修补 oracle 真的按预测移动了下游分数，那么分歧就是真实且因果的，而非标注上的偶然。\n9. 在基准的真实切片上重跑测量与校正（步骤 5-7）——这些任务的编辑是真正提交给公开 harness 或 leaderboard 的模型产出，而非你早先为构建标注集而生成的多样化编辑——并使用相同的可接受编辑机制，确认 D 仍保持相同符号且依然显著。这说明效应在合成设置之外依然成立。然后把整条流程封装成可复用工具：给定一个暴露每个任务的指令、原始代码与 oracle 的小适配器，再加一组模型编辑，它就返回 $raw_{score}$、带置信区间的 $corrected_{score}$、false-accept 率、false-reject 率以及推荐杠杆。\n   - _为什么_: 证明效应在真实数据上仍然存在、并交付一个可复用工具，才使它成为一种测量工具而非一次性研究。\n\n"},{"id":"33","run_dir":"run_prompt33_unifiedgen","index":33,"title":"Editing as a Support-Confined Forward Process for Unified Image and Video Editing","title_zh":"将编辑视为支撑受限的前向过程：面向统一图像与视频编辑的方法","method_name":"Support-Confined Forward Process (SCFP), with the Support-Confined Edit Fidelity (SCEF) diagnostic","hook":"Every unified image+video editor (EditVerse, VACE, UniVideo) regenerates the whole token sequence through one global denoiser, so an instruction that should touch one region silently re-synthesizes the rest and the unedited complement drifts more the longer the video. We instead PRESCRIBE the edit as an instruction-gated forward corruption confined to a learned soft spatio-temporal support, and build the denoiser as its reverse anchored at the observed source, so the complement is preserved by construction rather than by data luck.","anchor_pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","anchor_pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","domain_category":"Generative Models — Vision","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved unified model exposes or controls the spatio-temporal SUPPORT of an instructed edit: when an instruction targets a region or time-span, there is no quantity governing how much of the output outside that support is preserved versus re-synthesized, so unintended drift in untouched regions/frames is uncontrolled at inference and grows with sequence length.","pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","sub_pattern":"C20 (Encode Structure by Construction)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by prescribing an explicit instruction-conditioned forward editing law whose per-token noising strength is gated by a learned soft support field s(x,t) in [0,1], and constructing the denoiser as the principled reverse of that law anchored at the observed source where s is near 0 — so off-support tokens are reconstructed from the source by construction and the amount of permitted change is the controllable quantity s, not an emergent side effect of global attention.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved unified model provides a MEASURE that separates intended change from collateral change — i.e. an edit-locality / preservation metric on native video edits — so the field cannot even rank two unified models on how cleanly they confine edits, and reports only aggregate fidelity that conflates a precise edit with a wholesale re-generation that happens to look plausible.","pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by constructing matched controlled instances whose intended edit support is known by construction (composited synthetic edits + provenance-tracked region masks) and scoring two de-confounded quantities separately — intended-region change vs complement-region change — against a copy-source 'no-edit' floor and a full-regenerate ceiling, so the headline is the leakage gap that aggregate FVD/CLIP conflate, and the same support field s the mechanism controls is exactly what the metric audits.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"unified image and video generation and editing (diffusion-transformer generative models)","n_papers":40,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":26},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":18,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"UniEdit: A Unified Tuning-Free Framework for Video Motion and Appearance Editing"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"UniReal: Universal Image Generation and Editing via Learning Real-world Dynamics"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Unified Editing of Panorama, 3D Scenes, and Videos Through Disentangled Self-Attention Injection"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Controllable Talking Face Generation by Implicit Facial Keypoints Editing"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Vitron: A Unified Pixel-level Vision LLM for Understanding, Generating, Segmenting, Editing"},{"source":"openalex","title":"MagDiff: Multi-alignment Diffusion for High-Fidelity Video Generation and Editing"}],"more":12},{"year":2025,"n":21,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"EditVerse: Unifying Image and Video Editing and Generation with In-Context Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"UniVideo: Unified Understanding, Generation, and Editing for Videos"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"DreamVE: Unified Instruction-based Image and Video Editing"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"VACE: All-in-One Video Creation and Editing"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"OmniV2V: Versatile Video Generation and Editing via Dynamic Content Manipulation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Omni-Video: Democratizing Unified Video Understanding and Generation"}],"more":15},{"year":2026,"n":1,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"}],"more":0}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":16,"share":0.4},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":16,"share":0.4},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":7,"share":0.175},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":6,"share":0.15},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":6,"share":0.15},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":6,"share":0.15},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":5,"share":0.125},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":3,"share":0.075}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Across the current unified image+video editing-and-generation frontier — EditVerse (semanticscholar:5e26ff506c3c029166cf1ca024010d4f8390fd39), VACE (semanticscholar:81a3c48930c06d8cdb6edcdeea2144412af00912), UniReal (openalex:W4413157087), UniVideo (semanticscholar:fc38660f092caa15895c54bbce87e139478ff235) and DreamVE (semanticscholar:21050282e0ccefb8387c4fd55d47e4dddf173ba8) — unification is obtained by serializing text, images and video into one token sequence and letting full self-attention plus large-scale data carry cross-modal transfer. Because the model is one undifferentiated denoiser over the whole sequence, an instruction that should change only a target region or a target time-span has no architectural boundary confining its effect: the change competes with reconstruction of every other token through the same attention, so untouched background regions and untouched frames are silently re-synthesized and drift, and the amount of unintended change grows with sequence length (more frames, higher resolution). None of these systems exposes a quantity that says how much of the output outside the intended edit support was preserved versus re-generated, so the spatio-temporal locality of an edit is neither controllable at inference nor measurable at evaluation — it is whatever scaled training happened to induce, and degrades exactly when the unified setting is most valuable (long videos, multi-object scenes, compositional multi-edit instructions).","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:5e26ff506c3c029166cf1ca024010d4f8390fd39","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"EditVerse tokenizes text, image and video into one interleaved sequence and uses full self-attention with a 4D RoPE so a single denoiser handles all image/video generation and editing tasks, relying on in-context learning and scale for cross-modal transfer. Its method has no notion of an edit support set: every output token attends to and is regenerated from the whole sequence, so it cannot confine an instructed change to a region/time-span nor report how much of the unedited content was preserved rather than re-synthesized — locality is an emergent, unmeasured property."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:81a3c48930c06d8cdb6edcdeea2144412af00912","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"VACE unifies video tasks by packing text/image/video/mask into a Video Condition Unit and restructuring the DiT to consume it, so a user-supplied mask CAN mark where to edit. But the mask is only an input conditioning signal fed through the same global attention; it neither bounds the denoiser's receptive influence nor yields a guarantee/metric that off-mask, off-edited-frame content is preserved, so leakage outside the masked support across frames is uncontrolled and unquantified."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4413157087","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"UniReal recasts image generation/editing as 'discontinuous video frames' and mines universal supervision from real video data, unifying many image tasks under one DiT. The reframing borrows video's consistency prior but provides no explicit support-localization: it cannot say which output pixels were meant to change, and its consistency comes from data statistics rather than an enforceable per-edit locality bound, leaving multi-edit and native-video locality unaddressed."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:fc38660f092caa15895c54bbce87e139478ff235","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"UniVideo uses a dual-stream MLLM+MM-DiT so a language model interprets complex instructions and the DiT generates, improving instruction understanding and identity preservation for video. The instruction is grounded semantically but its spatial/temporal extent is never localized in the generative process, so understanding 'what' to change does not translate into bounding 'where/when' the change is allowed to land — preservation of the complement is still emergent."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416075210","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"UNIC unifies diverse video editing tasks in-context by representing all task inputs as three token types in one model, removing task-specific adapters and DDIM inversion. Unification is again representational; the in-context tokens select the task but impose no constraint that the edit's influence stay within its intended support, so cross-frame leakage and the preservation/edit tradeoff remain unmeasured."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"unified image and video generation and editing (diffusion-transformer generative models)","venue":"top ML/CV venue (NeurIPS / ICLR / ICML / CVPR / ICCV tier)","time":"2026","data":["large-scale text-image-video paired corpora","instruction-edit triplets (instruction, source, edited)","video-frame-pair self-supervision (e.g. UniReal / Magic Fixup style)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"diffusion / generative modeling, video understanding","preference":"both","baseline":"single-token-sequence full-self-attention unified models (EditVerse, VACE, UniReal, UniVideo, DreamVE, UNIC)","limitation":"current unified image+video edit/gen models achieve unification through representational uniformity (tokenize all modalities into one sequence + full self-attention) and scaled data, but provide no control over, nor measurement of, where an instructed edit is allowed to take effect in space-time — untouched regions and frames drift, and the edit-precision vs preservation tradeoff is left implicit","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object across both legs is the soft spatio-temporal SUPPORT FIELD s = s_theta(instruction, source) in [0,1]^{H x W x T}, a per-latent-token scalar (computed by a small cross-attention head that reads the instruction text embedding and the VAE-encoded source latents; one scalar per latent position over height H, width W, and T latent frames) that says how much each location is permitted to change. LEG 1 (structural_prior_encoding, C20): we prescribe an explicit forward editing law over the latent x_0 of the SOURCE: x_tau = x_0 + s . (sqrt(alpha_tau-bar related schedule) noising) — concretely the forward process injects diffusion noise scaled pointwise by s, so where s=0 the forward law is the identity (the token stays exactly the source) and where s=1 it is the standard full noising schedule used by the base DiT; tau in [0,1] is the diffusion time. The model is then constructed as the principled REVERSE of this prescribed law: the denoiser v_theta predicts velocity only on the s-weighted component and the reverse update ANCHORS each token at the observed source latent with weight (1-s), i.e. x_{tau-dtau} = (1-s).x_0_source + s.(reverse-DiT step), so off-support tokens (s~0) are reconstructed from the source BY CONSTRUCTION and on-support tokens follow the generative reverse process conditioned on the instruction. s is itself learned end-to-end: it has no ground-truth label, so it is supervised only through the editing loss plus a sparsity prior lambda.||s||_1 (lambda a named hyperparameter, default 1e-3) that pushes s toward 0 wherever changing a token does not reduce the edit-reconstruction loss — this is what keeps the support MINIMAL and SOFT (a continuum, not a painted binary mask) and instruction-DERIVED rather than user-supplied. The identical operator handles images (T=1) and video (T>1) because s and the anchored reverse step are defined per latent token regardless of frame count, giving unification without a global undifferentiated denoiser. LEG 2 (controlled_diagnostic_design, C02): the SAME field s and the source/target pair define a measurement instrument, Support-Confined Edit Fidelity (SCEF). We build controlled instances where the TRUE intended support R* is known by construction (synthetic edits composited at known regions/time-spans, plus provenance-tracked human-annotated edit masks), then report two separately-scored quantities — intended change IC = perceptual distance between output and source restricted to R*, and complement leakage CL = perceptual distance restricted to the complement of R* — each anchored to a copy-source floor (output:=source -> IC=0, CL=0) and a full-regenerate ceiling (unconstrained base model). The headline is the LEAKAGE GAP, CL at matched IC: two models that achieve the same intended change can differ arbitrarily in complement leakage, a divergence aggregate FVD/CLIP-score cannot see because they average over R* and its complement. SCEF's oracle (R* and the source) is independent of the model under test, satisfying C02's non-circularity requirement.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules: the support field s is simultaneously the controllable quantity the mechanism leg encodes AND the object the diagnostic leg measures against, which is why coherence_thread_type is shared_evaluation — the metric certifies exactly the quantity the operator controls, so a reviewer reads one paper, not a method plus an unrelated benchmark. (b) Alternatives considered and rejected: (i) a hard binary user-painted mask with hard latent compositing (Blended-Diffusion style) — REJECTED as a regression to method_lineage collateral nodes c1 (flow-warped layer compositing) and c2 (blended/mask-restricted diffusion); it is not instruction-derived, has no soft boundary, and offers no learned support, so we keep s soft, differentiable, and instruction-conditioned. (ii) A separate auxiliary segmentation network producing the mask — REJECTED because it re-introduces an off-the-shelf module C20's failure mode warns against (gains creditable to the segmenter's capacity, not the encoded forward law); instead s is learned only through the editing loss + sparsity prior so the encoded forward process is provably load-bearing under an equal-capacity ablation (s frozen to 1 everywhere = the global-denoiser baseline).","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: fine-tune one pretrained unified image+video DiT with the support head on a standard instruction-edit corpus (image triplets + a few thousand video-edit clips) within ~30 A100-day, then evaluate on the held-out SCEF instances and on standard editing benchmarks. If the candidate works, complement leakage CL at matched intended-change IC DECREASES sharply versus the unmodified global-denoiser baseline, and the CL-vs-sequence-length curve stays roughly FLAT where the baseline's CL rises with T (the drift-grows-with-length signature). The single named load-bearing variable is the learned support field s; the mechanism distinguisher is a negative control that RANDOMIZES s (replace s_theta's output with a per-token random field of the same mean mass) while keeping all weights and compute identical: under this control, complement leakage CL must rise back toward the global-regenerate ceiling and standard edit-success accuracy must fall back to baseline, because a random support no longer anchors the right tokens at the source — if CL and edit-success are unchanged when s is randomized, the support field is not the mechanism and the reframe is falsified. Positive control: a stripped model that uses ONLY s to hard-blend source and a single unconditional base-model regeneration (no instruction in the reverse step) should already recover most of the leakage reduction, confirming that confinement, not the conditioning richness, owns the preservation gain.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:5e26ff506c3c029166cf1ca024010d4f8390fd39","delta":"EditVerse predicts visual velocity over one interleaved token sequence with full self-attention so every output token is regenerated from the whole sequence; we construct a per-token soft support field s that gates an instruction-confined forward law and anchors off-support tokens at the source, making preservation of the complement a by-construction property they have no quantity for."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:81a3c48930c06d8cdb6edcdeea2144412af00912","delta":"VACE admits a user mask as one more conditioning input passed through global attention, which neither bounds the denoiser's influence nor guarantees off-mask preservation; we make the support a LEARNED, soft, instruction-derived field that enters the forward/reverse dynamics itself, so preservation is enforced by the anchored reverse step rather than hoped for from conditioning."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4413157087","delta":"UniReal borrows a consistency prior from real-video data statistics with no notion of which output pixels were meant to change; we encode an explicit, controllable support whose mass is the measurable edit extent, and we ship a metric (SCEF) that separates intended vs collateral change, which their data-statistics consistency cannot expose."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416075210","delta":"UNIC unifies video-edit tasks via in-context token types that select the task but impose no support constraint; we add a constraint that confines and measures the spatio-temporal extent of each edit, and handle disjoint multi-edit instructions through disjoint per-token support fields."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:81a3c48930c06d8cdb6edcdeea2144412af00912","what_step_was_missed":"VACE supplies a user mask as a conditioning modality but treats it as static input fed through the same global attention; to reach our contribution it would have had to construct the mask as a soft, learned, instruction-derived support field that PARAMETERIZES the forward noising law and the reverse update's anchoring term — i.e. derive the recovery operator as the principled reverse of a support-confined corruption process so off-support preservation is forced by construction, a generative-process reformulation it never built (its mask never enters the diffusion dynamics, only the conditioning)."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":275,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"No hard floor fires (gap_closure_reject_check=borderline not triggered; anti_pattern matched_pattern_id=null; recipe_application_check=applied; paper_pointed_threat is competing-not-exact and addressable). I choose revise over advance because two load-bearing concerns are addressable by field edits: (1) paper_pointed_threat ReCo (arxiv:2512.17650v1) attacks the same non-editing-region-interference residual via soft latent/attention regularization, so differentiation_from_lit must add the 'soft regularizer that can be violated vs by-construction anchored reverse' delta or a reviewer reads the anchor leg as a re-skin of ReCo; (2) the controlled_diagnostic_design leg sits in an untested lane (share 0.04) and carries two borderline Reject lessons (confirmatory-risk and synthetic-only ecological validity), so differentiation_from_lit / the metric framing must foreground the non-obvious leakage-at-matched-IC gap and the synthetic-to-real transfer. These are tactical field edits; kill-switch fields are untouched.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved unified model exposes or controls the spatio-temporal SUPPORT of an instructed edit: when an instruction targets a region or time-span, there is no quantity governing how much of the output outside that support is preserved versus re-synthesized, so unintended drift in untouched regions/frames is uncontrolled at inference and grows with sequence length.","main_pattern":"structural_prior_encoding","sub_pattern":"C20 (Encode Structure by Construction)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail when the corruption-structure prior is asserted but never isolated as the actual source of gains: the 'structure' is really a generic architecture or pretrained backbone doing the work, so same-capacity ablations cannot attribute improvement to the prior, or the advertised generality is shown on a single backbone/dataset.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming an architecture carries a domain-matched structural prior while shipping a generic off-the-shelf encoder-decoder collapses the move into ordinary supervised denoising that ablations and weak-baseline comparisons quickly expose.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate does not ship a generic encoder-decoder: it prescribes an explicit support-gated forward noising law and constructs the reverse as an anchored blend (1-s)*x0_source + s*reverse-step, and step 10 ablates s:=1 (= the global-denoiser baseline) at equal capacity, so the encoded forward process is the isolated variable."},{"lesson_quoted":"An elegant equivalence proof (corruption-recovery equals descent on an energy landscape) earns nothing when the empirical gain over the base method is marginal and the advertised plug-in generality is shown on only a single backbone.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The candidate claims unification across images (T=1) and video (T>1) and across edit types, which is a breadth claim; if validated on only one backbone it would read as single-backbone generality — the plan should test more than one base unified DiT, currently implied but not explicit."},{"lesson_quoted":"Deriving partition labels from a first-principles physical model is undercut when the derivations lack rigor, baselines and ablations are missing, and citation hygiene fails.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"No partition-label derivation is involved; the support field is learned end-to-end with an explicit sparsity prior and a randomize-s negative control, and the baseline (s:=1 global denoiser) is named."},{"lesson_quoted":"If the structural signal you minimize rides on a powerful pretrained backbone, failing to isolate the prior's contribution from sheer backbone capacity leaves reviewers unable to credit the idea and unconvinced by the motivation for the chosen backbone.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The freeze-backbone + ~5M-param support-head design plus the s:=1 equal-capacity ablation is precisely the backbone-vs-prior isolation this lesson demands."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved unified model provides a MEASURE that separates intended change from collateral change — i.e. an edit-locality / preservation metric on native video edits — so the field cannot even rank two unified models on how cleanly they confine edits, and reports only aggregate fidelity that conflates a precise edit with a wholesale re-generation that happens to look plausible.","main_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail when the instrument isolates the confound only inside an artificial regime and never shows the signal transfers to real deployment, or when the diagnostic is validated against the same population/definition it interrogates (circularity), or when it merely re-derives an already-documented limitation.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A diagnostic that only re-confirms a shortcut already known in advance, surfacing no previously unmeasurable failure, is read as confirmatory rather than as a contribution.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"Complement-leakage is intuitively 'known', so SCEF must surface a genuinely new measurable gap — the leakage-at-matched-IC divergence and the leakage-vs-sequence-length growth curve — rather than re-confirm that editors change extra pixels; the candidate states this but must foreground that the gap is non-obvious (two models at equal edit success differ arbitrarily in leakage)."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a synthetic-ground-truth instrument only on synthetic data, without demonstrating that the controlled finding transfers to real-world instances, leaves ecological validity unestablished and undermines the central claim.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"SCEF has a synthetic-composite split with known R*; step 7 also adds a provenance-tracked human-annotated split, but the candidate should make the synthetic-to-real transfer of the leakage finding explicit rather than implied to dodge the ecological-validity reject."},{"lesson_quoted":"Building the instrument around one contested definition of the target property means it cannot independently confirm that the definition is correct, and reviewers flag the resulting circularity.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"SCEF's oracle (R* and the source) is constructed independently of the model under test — the support field s the mechanism learns is NOT used as the metric's ground-truth R*, so there is no circularity between mechanism and measure."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pairing a single-task or small-sample instrument with broad capability claims triggers a scope-mismatch rejection, and assembling retrieval or engineering blocks without an isolating scientific insight reads as application rather than research.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"SCEF spans multiple edit operations (insert/remove/recolor/move) over both images and video and reports a single isolating quantity (IC vs CL), not an engineering pipeline."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No Reject lesson is a hard 'yes'; the metric leg (controlled_diagnostic_design / C02) carries two borderlines — confirmatory-risk and synthetic-only ecological-validity — and the mechanism leg (structural_prior_encoding / C20) carries one borderline on single-backbone generality. All are addressable by sharpening field text, not by abandoning the design."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved unified model exposes or controls the spatio-temporal SUPPORT of an instructed edit: when an instruction targets a region or time-span, there is no quantity governing how much of the output outside that support is preserved versus re-synthesized, so unintended drift in untouched regions/frames is uncontrolled at inference and grows with sequence length.","sub_pattern":"C20 (Encode Structure by Construction)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"C20's signature move is to PRESCRIBE an explicit forward corruption/generation law (a noising kernel, masking schedule, or transform isolating the artifact) and then CONSTRUCT the recovery operator as the principled REVERSE of that prescribed law, anchoring the process at the actual observation so the inverse is obtained by construction rather than as black-box corrupt->clean regression.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism LEG 1 prescribes the forward law x_tau = x_0 + s.(noising) gated pointwise by the support field s (s=0 -> identity, s=1 -> base schedule), then builds the reverse update x_{tau-dtau} = (1-s).x0_source + s.(reverse-DiT step) which ANCHORS off-support tokens at the observed source — this is exactly C20's prescribe-forward-then-reverse-anchored-at-observation move, not the parent's generic 'encode a structural prior'.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved unified model provides a MEASURE that separates intended change from collateral change — i.e. an edit-locality / preservation metric on native video edits — so the field cannot even rank two unified models on how cleanly they confine edits, and reports only aggregate fidelity that conflates a precise edit with a wholesale re-generation that happens to look plausible.","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"C02's move is to construct controlled instances in which exactly one named confound is structurally blocked or independently varied, paired with an oracle independent of the system under test, then report the DIVERGENCE between apparent and de-confounded performance as the headline rather than an aggregate leaderboard score.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism LEG 2 names the confound (aggregate fidelity conflating intended vs collateral change), builds matched instances with known intended support R* (synthetic composites + provenance-tracked masks), scores IC and CL separately against a copy-source floor and full-regenerate ceiling, and reports the leakage gap CL-at-matched-IC as the headline — exactly C02's block-one-confound + independent-oracle + report-the-divergence move.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both legs perform their cited cluster's distinctive move: LEG 1 instantiates C20's prescribe-forward-then-anchored-reverse (not the generic 'encode a prior'), and LEG 2 instantiates C02's confound-blocked controlled instances + independent oracle + divergence-as-headline."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["structural_prior_encoding","controlled_diagnostic_design"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"The composition {structural_prior_encoding, controlled_diagnostic_design} matches none of the three reject-favored compositions, all of which require heterogeneous_decomposition as a component; heterogeneous_decomposition is not in the set."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"arxiv:2512.17650v1","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"ReCo (Region-Constraint In-Context Generation for Instructional Video Editing, 2025-12) directly targets the same residual the candidate's anchor leg attacks: it names 'token interference between editing and non-editing areas during denoising' and addresses inaccurate editing regions in instructional video editing. If ReCo's mechanism already enforced support-confined preservation by construction, the candidate's anchor contribution would be subsumed. It does NOT: ReCo width-wise concatenates source and target video for joint denoising and adds two soft REGULARIZATION terms (latent regularization that increases editing-region latent discrepancy while reducing non-editing-region discrepancy, and attention regularization on attention maps) — i.e. a training-time penalty that discourages off-region change, still computed inside the same global joint denoiser, and it presupposes a specified editing region rather than learning a soft instruction-derived support that enters the forward/reverse dynamics. The candidate's preservation is by-construction (off-support tokens are anchored at the source via the (1-s) blend so they cannot drift), is learned and soft (no user-specified region), and unifies image+video under one per-token operator; ReCo's preservation is a soft regularizer that can be violated and is video-only with externally-specified regions. So the candidate's claim stands but ReCo must be cited and differentiated, and the metric leg must distinguish SCEF's IC/CL separation from VEFX-Bench's 'Edit Exclusivity' VLM-judge score (semanticscholar:9b56277b19f240145a9870d4bec7f7102b2c9ba2).","addressable_via":"Add ReCo (arxiv:2512.17650v1) and VEFX-Bench to differentiation_from_lit with the regularizer-vs-by-construction-anchoring delta and the VLM-score-vs-IC/CL-separation delta; no mechanism change required."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat — ReCo (arxiv:2512.17650v1) addresses editing/non-editing-region token interference in instructional video editing via soft latent+attention regularization, the closest competing prior; and VEFX-Bench (semanticscholar:9b56277b19f240145a9870d4bec7f7102b2c9ba2) introduces an 'Edit Exclusivity' VLM-judged dimension close to the metric leg.","fix_direction":"Append two differentiation_from_lit entries: (i) arxiv:2512.17650v1 (ReCo) — delta: ReCo discourages non-editing-region change with two soft regularization terms on latents/attention computed inside the same global joint denoiser and requires a specified editing region, a penalty that can be violated; we make preservation a by-construction property by anchoring off-support tokens at the source through the (1-s) reverse blend and learn the soft support from the instruction rather than requiring a specified region. (ii) semanticscholar:9b56277b19f240145a9870d4bec7f7102b2c9ba2 (VEFX-Bench) — delta: VEFX-Bench scores 'Edit Exclusivity' with a learned VLM reward over the whole clip; SCEF instead reports a confound-isolated, region-resolved separation of intended change IC vs complement leakage CL against copy-source/full-regenerate anchors, exposing the leakage-at-matched-IC divergence and its growth with sequence length that a single holistic VLM score averages away."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"hook","issue":"gap_closure_reject_check — controlled_diagnostic_design (C02) borderline: confirmatory-risk (complement leakage sounds already-known) and untested-lane novelty defense; the non-obvious finding must be foregrounded so the metric leg does not read as re-confirming a known shortcut.","fix_direction":"Tighten the hook's second sentence to surface the non-obvious measurable claim that the metric makes visible: that two unified models achieving the SAME instructed change can differ arbitrarily in complement leakage, and that this leakage grows with sequence length under the global-denoiser baseline while staying flat under support-confinement — i.e. name the leakage-at-matched-IC gap (and its length-growth) as the previously-unmeasurable quantity SCEF exposes, keeping the structural-reframe shape but binding it to the diagnostic's new measurement."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Appended two entries — ReCo (arxiv:2512.17650v1) with the soft-regularizer-that-can-be-violated vs by-construction-anchored-reverse delta, and VEFX-Bench (semanticscholar:9b56277b19f240145a9870d4bec7f7102b2c9ba2) with the holistic-VLM-Edit-Exclusivity-score vs confound-isolated-region-resolved-IC/CL-separation delta."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"hook","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Tightened the hook's second sentence to name the previously-unmeasurable quantity SCEF exposes — that two unified models at the SAME instructed change can differ arbitrarily in complement leakage and that this leakage grows with sequence length under the global denoiser while staying flat under support-confinement — binding the structural reframe to the diagnostic's new measurement."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Editing as a Support-Confined Forward Process for Unified Image and Video Editing\n\n**Method.** Support-Confined Forward Process (SCFP), with the Support-Confined Edit Fidelity (SCEF) diagnostic\n\n## Motivation\nToday's best models that both create and edit images and videos with a single network (EditVerse, VACE, UniVideo) work by turning text, images, and video into one long list of tokens and letting one denoiser rebuild the entire list at once. The problem: when you ask for a small change -- recolor one object, edit one stretch of frames -- there is nothing in the model that confines the change to that spot. The single denoiser quietly re-creates everything else too, so the parts you wanted untouched slowly drift, and the drift gets worse the longer the video is.\n\nThis matters most exactly where these unified models are supposed to shine: long videos, busy multi-object scenes, and instructions that ask for several separate edits at once. And there is a second, related blind spot: no existing model even reports how much of the supposedly-untouched content actually stayed the same. Today's scores (like overall fidelity numbers) average everything together, so a clean local edit and a full re-generation that merely looks plausible get the same grade.\n\nWhy now: the whole unified image+video field converged on this same one-sequence recipe in just the last several months -- EditVerse (September 2025), UniVideo (October 2025), VACE (2025), UNIC and DreamVE (2025) -- and they all inherit the same blind spot. A recent paper, ReCo (December 2025), even names the exact symptom (interference between edited and non-edited areas during denoising), which shows the field is now ready for a fix that confines the edit by construction.\n\nWhat changes when this gap closes: a unified model stops being a wholesale re-generator and becomes a controllable editor. The size of an edit in space and time becomes a knob you can set and a number you can measure. Long-video and multi-object edits stop degrading with length, and several independent edits can be checked to make sure they don't interfere.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n\n1. Start from an existing pretrained unified image+video diffusion-transformer (a single network that both generates and edits, working on compressed latent representations produced by a VAE) and freeze every one of its weights. Define the baseline precisely: run this frozen network exactly as published but with the per-location 'how much may change' value pinned to 1 everywhere — which makes the source-preserving term disappear, so it behaves as the ordinary whole-sequence denoiser. That all-ones-support, frozen run is your honest baseline; nothing is trained in this step.\n   - _Why_: Freezing it means any improvement can be credited to the new support mechanism, not to extra model capacity.\n\n### Learned Support Field\n*Turn the instruction and source into a soft per-token map of how much each location may change.*\n\n2. Add a small (~5-million-parameter) two-layer cross-attention head that reads the edit instruction and the source latents and outputs one number between 0 and 1 for every latent token (each spatial position, each frame): how much that spot is allowed to change. Reuse the frozen network's existing text encoder to turn the instruction into the embeddings this head attends to — do not add a new language model. Each layer is an 8-head cross-attention block followed by a small two-layer network, and a final linear-plus-sigmoid produces the single 0-to-1 value per location. Initialize so the values start close to 1 (almost no confinement at first), and the later sparsity penalty will shrink them to only the locations that truly need changing.\n\n*A small cross-attention head reads the instruction embedding $c_{instr}$ and the source latents $x0_{src}$ and outputs one scalar s per latent token (over height H, width W, T latent frames) saying how much that location may change.*\n$$ s = s_\\theta(c_{\\text{instr}}, x_0^{\\text{src}}) \\in [0,1]^{H \\times W \\times T} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This gives the model a soft, learned 'where to edit' map derived from the instruction itself, instead of a hand-painted mask.\n3. Train everything together on (instruction, source, edited-result) triplets. The loss has two parts: a flow-matching loss measuring how well the edited region is reconstructed, plus a small L1 penalty (weight 1e-3) summed over all support values that pushes them toward 0. Because the base network is frozen, only the new support head learns; the support map gets no hand-drawn labels and is shaped purely by these two losses. For still images, use public instruction-edit triplet datasets; for video, build training pairs by applying a known edit to a source clip and carrying it across frames, plus any real instruction-based video-edit clips you have. 【author decision: how the synthetic video training targets are produced — which off-the-shelf editor makes each frame's edited version and how those frames are kept temporally consistent — is a data-engineering choice the authors must make; the trade-off is the quality versus the availability of video edit ground truth, and it controls how clean the support-map supervision is.】\n\n*s has no label; it is supervised only through the flow-matching loss on the s-weighted velocity plus an L1 sparsity prior weighted by lambda, which keeps the support minimal, soft, and instruction-derived.*\n$$ \\mathcal{L} = \\mathcal{L}_{\\text{flow}}\\big(v_\\theta, s \\odot v^{*}\\big) + \\lambda \\lVert s \\rVert_1, \\quad \\lambda = 10^{-3} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The L1 penalty keeps the edit region as small as possible, so s naturally lights up only where the instruction actually requires change.\n4. No new component is added here. Because the support value is predicted separately for every position and every frame, two edits that fall in different places or different times automatically get separate, non-overlapping support maps. Verify this: write instructions that ask for two clearly separate edits (for example, recolor an object in early frames AND insert a different object in later frames), run the model, and check two things — the support map lights up only inside the two intended regions, and running the two edits together gives, inside each region, essentially the same result as running that edit alone. Report how different the together-result is from the alone-result inside each region as the interference measure.\n   - _Why_: Because each edit owns its own region, several independent edits in one instruction can coexist without bleeding into each other.\n\n### Support-Confined Forward/Reverse Process\n*Corrupt only the support and invert it with a source-anchored reverse so the complement is preserved by construction.*\n\n5. Change the forward 'add-noise' process used during training so the noise added to each source token is scaled by that token's support value: where the value is 0 the token is frozen at the source (no noise), where it is 1 it receives the network's normal full noise level, and values in between get proportionally less. Concretely, draw the usual Gaussian noise and the usual noise strength from the base network's schedule, then multiply the noise by the per-location support value before adding it to the clean source latent. This redefined noisy version is what the denoiser is trained to reverse.\n\n*The prescribed forward editing law scales the injected diffusion noise pointwise by s, so where s=0 the law is the identity (token stays at the source) and where s=1 it is the base DiT noising schedule.*\n$$ x_\\tau = x_0 + s \\odot \\big(\\sqrt{1-\\bar{\\alpha}_\\tau}\\,\\epsilon\\big), \\quad \\epsilon \\sim \\mathcal{N}(0, I) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Defining the corruption process explicitly is what lets the model later invert it precisely, instead of learning a vague corrupt-to-clean mapping.\n6. Change the sampling loop so that after EVERY denoising step you blend, location by location: keep (1 minus the support value) of the original source token and take (the support value) of the model's edited step. Locations with support near 0 are re-pinned to the exact source at every step — so they cannot slowly drift no matter how long the video is — while locations with support near 1 follow the edit. Use the same support map throughout (computed once from the source and instruction). At the end, decode the result: pinned locations come back as the original pixels, edited locations as the new content.\n\n*The reverse update is the principled inverse of the forward law: off-support tokens (s near 0) are anchored at the source latent by the (1-s) term, while on-support tokens follow the instruction-conditioned reverse DiT step.*\n$$ x_{\\tau-d\\tau} = (1-s) \\odot x_0^{\\text{src}} + s \\odot \\text{DiT}_{\\text{rev}}(x_\\tau, c_{\\text{instr}}) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Pinning the untouched parts to the source by construction means they cannot drift, no matter how long the video is.\n\n### SCEF Diagnostic\n*Measure intended change versus complement leakage on instances with a known intended support.*\n\n7. Build a test set where the region/time-span that should change (call it R*) is known independently of any model being tested. First, a synthetic split: take clean images/videos and apply edits you control — paste in or remove an object at recorded coordinates, recolor or relight only inside a recorded region, move an object (record both its start and end areas) — so R* is exactly the area your editing code touched, with no guessing. Second, a human-annotated split: collect real before/after edit pairs and have people mark exactly where the change happened, saving each mark together with what edit produced it. Because R* is decided without running the model under test, you never grade a model against its own guess.\n   - _Why_: Knowing the true edit region lets you measure leakage honestly, and keeping R* independent of the tested model avoids grading a model against its own guess.\n8. For each test item, measure two things with a perceptual image-similarity distance (a learned measure of how visually different two pictures look, e.g. LPIPS = Learned Perceptual Image Patch Similarity): the change inside R* (the intended change) and the change outside R* (the complement leakage), each divided by the size of its region so big and small regions are compared fairly. For video, measure this frame by frame using that frame's slice of R* and combine across frames. Also record two reference points: copy-the-source (nothing changes anywhere) and full re-generation (the unconstrained base model). 【author decision: whether to keep the simple per-frame measure averaged over time, or switch to a video-aware similarity measure that also penalizes flicker inside the edited region, is an instrument choice the authors must make — the trade-off is per-frame sharpness versus sensitivity to temporal consistency, which changes what 'leakage' means for long clips.】\n\n*SCEF scores intended change IC as perceptual distance d between output y and source restricted to the known support R*, and complement leakage CL as the same distance over the complement of R*; the headline is CL at matched IC.*\n$$ \\text{IC} = \\!\\!\\sum_{p \\in R^{*}}\\!\\! d(y_p, x^{\\text{src}}_p), \\quad \\text{CL} = \\!\\!\\sum_{p \\notin R^{*}}\\!\\! d(y_p, x^{\\text{src}}_p) \\tag{5} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Splitting the score into inside-region and outside-region change separates a clean edit from a wholesale re-generation that overall-fidelity scores would rate the same.\n9. Group models by how much real editing they actually did (the intended-change score) into a handful of equal-strength bins, then within each bin compare their complement leakage — this gives 'leakage at the same edit strength', so a model isn't unfairly rewarded just for editing less. Separately, sort video items by length and, holding edit strength fixed, plot leakage against length: the standard baseline's leakage should climb with longer videos while the confined model's stays flat. The two headline results are the leakage-at-equal-edit-strength comparison table and the leakage-versus-length curve.\n   - _Why_: This reveals the non-obvious fact that two models making the same edit can leak very differently, and that the baseline leaks more on longer videos while a confined model stays flat.\n\n### Mechanism Isolation\n*Prove the support field, not extra capacity, drives the leakage reduction.*\n\n10. Run two controls with identical weights and compute. First, set the support to 1 everywhere — this recovers the ordinary whole-sequence baseline. Second, randomize the support: replace the learned map with a random one that has the SAME total amount of allowed change (so the model is permitted to change just as much overall, only in the wrong places). Then measure leakage and edit success (how much changed inside the intended region, plus the benchmark's usual edit-success score). The prediction: with a randomized support, leakage climbs back toward full re-generation and edit success drops back to baseline. If randomizing the support changes nothing, the support field was never doing the work and the whole idea is falsified.\n   - _Why_: If randomizing the support map does NOT hurt -- leakage and edit success stay the same -- then the support field was never doing the work and the whole idea is falsified.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 将编辑视为支撑受限的前向过程：面向统一图像与视频编辑的方法\n\n**方法名称.** Support-Confined Forward Process (SCFP), with the Support-Confined Edit Fidelity (SCEF) diagnostic\n\n## 研究动机\n如今最好的、用一个网络同时生成和编辑图像与视频的模型（EditVerse、VACE、UniVideo），其做法是把文本、图像和视频变成一长串 token，让一个 denoiser 一次性重建整串。问题在于：当你只想做一个很小的改动——给某个物体换色、只编辑一小段帧——模型里没有任何东西把这个改动限制在那个位置。单一 denoiser 会悄悄把其余部分也重新生成，于是你本想保持不变的区域会缓慢漂移，而且视频越长漂移越严重。\n\n这恰恰发生在这些统一模型本应最有优势的场景：长视频、物体繁多的场景，以及一次包含多个独立编辑的指令。还有第二个相关的盲点：现有模型甚至不会报告那些本应不变的内容到底保留了多少。今天的评分（如整体保真度指标）把一切平均到一起，于是一个干净的局部编辑和一个只是看起来合理的整体重生成会得到同样的分数。\n\n为什么是现在：整个统一图像+视频领域在最近几个月里收敛到了同一套单序列方案——EditVerse（2025 年 9 月）、UniVideo（2025 年 10 月）、VACE（2025 年）、UNIC 与 DreamVE（2025 年）——它们都继承了同一个盲点。最近的一篇 ReCo（2025 年 12 月）甚至点名了这一确切症状（去噪过程中编辑区与非编辑区之间的干扰），这说明该领域现在已准备好接受一个按构造方式限制编辑的解法。\n\n这个缺口被补上后会改变什么：统一模型不再是一个整体重生成器，而成为一个可控的编辑器。编辑在空间和时间上的范围变成一个你可以设定的旋钮，也变成一个你可以测量的数字。长视频与多物体编辑不再随长度退化，多个独立编辑还可以被检验以确保互不干扰。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景\n\n1. 从一个已有的预训练统一图像+视频 diffusion-transformer（一个既能生成又能编辑、在 VAE 压缩出的 latent 表示上工作的单一网络）出发，并冻结它的全部权重。把 baseline 精确定义出来：照原样运行这个冻结网络，但把每个位置「允许改变多少」的值处处钉为 1——这会让源保留项消失，于是它就退化成普通的整序列 denoiser。这个支撑处处为 1、且被冻结的运行结果就是你诚实的 baseline；本步不训练任何东西。\n   - _为什么_: 冻结它意味着任何提升都能归因于新的支撑机制，而不是更多的模型容量。\n\n### 学习得到的支撑场\n*把指令和源转化为一张柔性的、逐 token 的图，表示每个位置允许改变多少。*\n\n2. 加入一个很小（约 5M 参数）的两层 cross-attention 头，读取编辑指令和源 latent，为每个 latent token（每个空间位置、每帧）输出一个介于 0 和 1 之间的数 s：表示该位置允许改变的程度。复用冻结网络已有的文本编码器把指令转成这个头要关注的嵌入——不要新增语言模型。每层是一个 8 头 cross-attention 块加一个小型两层网络，最后用一个线性层加 sigmoid 为每个位置产生单一的 0 到 1 数值。初始化时让这些数值起步接近 1（一开始几乎不做限制），之后的稀疏惩罚会把它们收缩到真正需要改变的位置。\n\n*一个小型 cross-attention 头读取指令嵌入 $c_{instr}$ 与源 latent $x0_{src}$，对每个 latent token（在高 H、宽 W、T 个 latent 帧上）输出一个标量 s，表示该位置允许改变的程度。*\n$$ s = s_\\theta(c_{\\text{instr}}, x_0^{\\text{src}}) \\in [0,1]^{H \\times W \\times T} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这让模型得到一张柔性的、学习得到的、由指令本身导出的“在哪里编辑”图，而不是手工涂的 mask。\n3. 在 (指令, 源, 已编辑结果) 三元组上整体训练。损失有两部分：一个 flow-matching 损失，衡量编辑区域被重建得有多好；再加一个很小的 L1 惩罚（权重 1e-3），对所有支撑值求和并把它们推向 0。由于基座网络被冻结，只有新的支撑头在学习；支撑图没有任何手工标注，完全由这两个损失塑形。对静态图像，使用公开的指令-编辑三元组数据集；对视频，通过把一个已知编辑施加到源片段上并跨帧传递来构造训练对，再加上你手头任何真实的基于指令的视频编辑片段。【作者需决定：合成视频训练目标如何产生——用哪个现成编辑器生成每一帧的编辑版本、以及如何保持这些帧在时间上的一致性——这是作者必须做的数据工程选择；权衡在于视频编辑真值的质量与可得性，它决定了支撑图监督信号有多干净。】\n\n*s 没有标注，仅通过对 s 加权速度的 flow-matching 损失加上由 lambda 加权的 L1 稀疏先验来监督，从而使支撑保持最小、柔性且由指令导出。*\n$$ \\mathcal{L} = \\mathcal{L}_{\\text{flow}}\\big(v_\\theta, s \\odot v^{*}\\big) + \\lambda \\lVert s \\rVert_1, \\quad \\lambda = 10^{-3} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: L1 惩罚让编辑区域尽可能小，于是 s 自然只在指令确实需要改变的地方被点亮。\n4. 本步不新增任何组件。由于支撑值是为每个位置、每帧分别预测的，落在不同位置或不同时间的两个编辑会自动得到各自不重叠的支撑图。对此进行验证：写出要求两个明显分离的编辑的指令（例如，在前段帧给某物体换色，并在后段帧插入另一个物体），运行模型，检查两点——支撑图只在这两个预期区域内被点亮；以及把两个编辑一起执行时，在每个区域内得到的结果与单独执行该编辑时基本相同。把「一起执行」相对「单独执行」在每个区域内的差异大小作为干扰度量来报告。\n   - _为什么_: 因为每个编辑拥有自己的区域，一条指令中的多个独立编辑可以共存而不会互相渗透。\n\n### 支撑受限的前向/反向过程\n*只对支撑加噪，并用源锚定的反向过程逆转它，从而按构造保留互补区域。*\n\n5. 改变训练时所用的前向「加噪」过程，使加到每个源 token 上的噪声按该 token 的支撑值缩放：支撑值为 0 处该 token 冻结在源（不加噪），为 1 处则获得网络正常的完整噪声强度，介于两者之间则按比例减少。具体做法是：照常采样高斯噪声、照常从基座网络的计划里取噪声强度，然后在把噪声加到干净源 latent 之前，先按每个位置的支撑值对噪声做逐位置相乘。这个重新定义的带噪版本就是 denoiser 被训练去逆转的目标。\n\n*规定的前向编辑律按位置用 s 缩放注入的扩散噪声：s=0 处为恒等（token 保持在源），s=1 处即基座 DiT 的标准加噪计划。*\n$$ x_\\tau = x_0 + s \\odot \\big(\\sqrt{1-\\bar{\\alpha}_\\tau}\\,\\epsilon\\big), \\quad \\epsilon \\sim \\mathcal{N}(0, I) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 把这个加噪（corruption）过程显式定义出来，才能让模型之后精确地逆转它，而不是学一个含糊的“从噪到净”映射。\n6. 改变采样循环：在每一个去噪步之后都做逐位置混合——保留 (1 减去支撑值) 的原始源 token，取 (支撑值) 的模型编辑步结果。支撑接近 0 的位置在每一步都被重新钉回精确的源——所以无论视频多长它们都不会缓慢漂移——而支撑接近 1 的位置则跟随编辑。全程使用同一张支撑图（由源和指令一次性算出）。最后解码结果：被钉住的位置还原为原始像素，被编辑的位置呈现新内容。\n\n*反向更新是前向律的原理性逆过程：支撑外 token（s 接近 0）由 (1-s) 项锚定在源 latent，支撑内 token 则跟随指令条件下的反向 DiT 步。*\n$$ x_{\\tau-d\\tau} = (1-s) \\odot x_0^{\\text{src}} + s \\odot \\text{DiT}_{\\text{rev}}(x_\\tau, c_{\\text{instr}}) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 按构造把未触及的部分钉在源上，意味着无论视频多长它们都不会漂移。\n\n### SCEF 诊断\n*在已知预期支撑的实例上度量预期改变与互补泄漏。*\n\n7. 构建一个测试集，其中应当改变的区域/时间段（记作 R*）的确定独立于任何被测模型。第一，合成 split：取干净的图像/视频并施加你能掌控的编辑——在记录好的坐标处粘贴或移除一个物体、只在记录好的区域内换色或重打光、移动一个物体（同时记录它的起始与结束区域）——于是 R* 恰好就是你的编辑代码触及的区域，无需猜测。第二，人工标注 split：收集真实的前后编辑对，让人标出改变发生的确切位置，并把每个标注连同产生它的编辑动作一起保存。由于 R* 的确定不需要运行被测模型，你绝不会拿模型去对照它自己的猜测来评分。\n   - _为什么_: 知道真正的编辑区域才能诚实地度量泄漏，而让 R* 独立于被测模型可以避免拿模型去对照它自己的猜测来评分。\n8. 对每个测试项，用一个感知图像相似度距离（一种学习得到的、衡量两张图看起来有多不同的度量，例如 LPIPS = Learned Perceptual Image Patch Similarity，学习型感知图像块相似度）测量两件事：R* 之内的改变（预期改变）和 R* 之外的改变（互补泄漏），各自除以其区域大小，使大区域和小区域能被公平比较。对视频，用每帧对应的 R* 切片逐帧测量再跨帧汇总。同时记录两个参照点：复制源（处处不变）与完整重生成（无约束的基座模型）。【作者需决定：是保留按时间平均的逐帧度量，还是改用一个同时惩罚编辑区域内时间闪烁的视频感知相似度度量，这是作者必须做的仪器选择——权衡在于逐帧空间清晰度与对时间一致性的敏感度，它会改变长片段里「泄漏」的含义。】\n\n*SCEF 将预期改变 IC 定义为输出 y 与源在已知支撑 R* 上的感知距离 d，将互补泄漏 CL 定义为在 R* 之外的同一距离；核心指标是相同 IC 下的 CL。*\n$$ \\text{IC} = \\!\\!\\sum_{p \\in R^{*}}\\!\\! d(y_p, x^{\\text{src}}_p), \\quad \\text{CL} = \\!\\!\\sum_{p \\notin R^{*}}\\!\\! d(y_p, x^{\\text{src}}_p) \\tag{5} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 把分数拆成区域内与区域外的改变，可以把干净编辑与整体保真度会给同样分数的整体重生成区分开。\n9. 按模型实际做了多少真实编辑（预期改变分数）把它们分到若干个编辑强度相等的分箱里，然后在每个分箱内比较它们的互补泄漏——这就得到「相同编辑强度下的泄漏」，于是一个模型不会仅因为编辑得更少就被不公平地奖励。另外，把视频项按长度排序，在固定编辑强度的前提下把泄漏对长度作图：标准 baseline 的泄漏应随视频变长而上升，而受限模型的泄漏保持平稳。两个核心结果是：相同编辑强度下的泄漏对比表，以及泄漏对长度的曲线。\n   - _为什么_: 这揭示了一个不显然的事实：做同样编辑的两个模型泄漏可能差别很大，而 baseline 在更长视频上泄漏更多，受限模型却保持平稳。\n\n### 机制隔离\n*证明是支撑场而非额外容量驱动了泄漏的下降。*\n\n10. 在权重和算力完全相同的情况下做两个对照。第一，把支撑处处设为 1——这会回到普通的整序列 baseline。第二，把支撑随机化：用一张总「允许改变量」相同的随机图替换学到的支撑图（于是模型被允许改变的总量一样多，只是改在了错误的位置）。然后测量泄漏和编辑成功率（预期区域内改变了多少，再加上该 benchmark 通常用的编辑成功率分数）。预测是：支撑被随机化后，泄漏会回升到接近完整重生成的水平，编辑成功率回落到 baseline。如果随机化支撑什么都不改变，那说明支撑场从未起作用，整个想法被证伪。\n   - _为什么_: 如果随机化支撑图并不会变差——泄漏和编辑成功率都不变——那说明支撑场从未起作用，整个想法被证伪。\n\n"},{"id":"34","run_dir":"run_prompt34_valuealign","index":34,"title":"Anchored Decomposition: Attributing Cross-Model Value-Alignment Gaps to Values, Not Elicitation","title_zh":"锚定分解：将跨模型价值对齐差距归因于价值本身而非诱发方式（Anchored Decomposition）","method_name":"Anchored Decomposition","hook":"When two language models receive different value-alignment scores on the same benchmark, no current measure can say how much of that gap is a real value difference versus a difference in how the two models are elicited and judged; we show that a paired-anchor decomposition splits the gap into a value-contrast term and an elicitation-nuisance term, and that on existing benchmarks the elicitation term frequently dominates, reversing model rankings once removed.","anchor_pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","anchor_pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","domain_category":"LLM Alignment, Safety & Behavior","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved measure DECOMPOSES an observed cross-model behavioral difference into a value-disposition component versus elicitation-side components (prompt-form, response-style, judge), so the value-attributable part of a leaderboard gap is never identified (additive need: identifiability/attribution of the difference).","pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by partitioning the observed per-item behavioral gap between two models into structurally distinct populations — a value-disposition contrast term and elicitation-nuisance terms (item-form, response-style, judge) — and supplying a variance/error decomposition that bounds how the differentiated estimator recovers the true value-contrast, exactly the C04 move of discriminating a resource's heterogeneous components by a property tied to the downstream objective and treating each differently rather than reporting one uniform aggregate.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"Every retrieved leaf silently assumes that the elicitation instrument (the item set and its scoring judge) is a neutral, model-independent measuring stick — no retrieved paper tests whether the instrument itself must be held fixed-and-validated across models, rather than assumed neutral, for a comparative score to be meaningful (subtractive: the shared inherited assumption, stated as the unasked question).","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","how_closed":"Framing move (C05): the comparability of a cross-model score is an identifiability claim whose load-bearing precondition is instrument-neutrality (the same latent value elicited identically on each model); we show that precondition fails and pivot it to a checkable STRUCTURAL condition — a value-neutral anchor block plus a style/form-permutation block that must produce a known-null behavioral difference across models — which alone carries the symmetry-breaking that licenses attributing the residual to values. Companion deliverable (controlled_diagnostic_design / C02): a controlled instance set (matched anchor items + paraphrase/persona/judge-swap perturbations) whose known-null condition is the oracle independent of the models under test, shipping the empirical separation that demonstrates the instrument is NOT model-neutral.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"value alignment evaluation / behavioral measurement of LLMs","n_papers":35,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":22},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":10,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"LocalValueBench: A Collaboratively Built and Extensible Benchmark for Evaluating Localized Value Alignment and Ethical Safety in Large Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Ethical Reasoning and Moral Value Alignment of LLMs Depend on the Language We Prompt Them in"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"OpenFedLLM: Training Large Language Models on Decentralized Private Data via Federated Learning"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Cultural bias and cultural alignment of large language models"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Grounding Everything: Emerging Localization Properties in Vision-Language Transformers"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Embedded values-like shape ethical reasoning of large language models on primary care ethical dilemmas"}],"more":4},{"year":2025,"n":25,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Towards realistic evaluation of cultural value alignment in large language models: Diversity enhancement for survey response simulation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"CVC: A Large-Scale Chinese Value Rule Corpus for Value Alignment of Large Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Towards Better Value Principles for Large Language Model Alignment: A Systematic Evaluation and Enhancement"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"The Pluralistic Moral Gap: Understanding Judgment and Value Differences between Humans and Large Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Bridging the Evaluation Gap: Leveraging Large Language Models for Topic Model Evaluation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Prompt-Based Value Steering of Large Language Models"}],"more":19}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":25,"share":0.714},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":8,"share":0.229},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":3,"share":0.086},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":2,"share":0.057},{"pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","count":2,"share":0.057},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":2,"share":0.057},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":2,"share":0.057},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":2,"share":0.057}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Comparative value-alignment measurement reports a single behavioral score per model and ranks models by it, but every retrieved instrument elicits behavior through a fixed item set scored by a fixed judge, so the reported cross-model difference is a sum of (a) a true difference in the models' value dispositions and (b) elicitation-side response components — prompt-language sensitivity (af8b26c3, 'ethical reasoning depends on the language we prompt them in'), response-style / verbosity and judge bias (W7109045272, LLM judges penalize nuanced moral reasoning), and item-phrasing susceptibility (a10f523b, single-sentence probes are gamed) — that the score cannot separate. Concretely, when VAL-Bench (W4414976969) grounds the measure in belief-consistency and Measuring Human-AI Value Alignment (W4404518508) reports one composite alignment number, two models with identical underlying values but different verbosity or refusal styles receive different scores, and two models with different values but matched styles can receive the same score; the machinery produces no quantity certifying that the construct elicited on model A is the construct elicited on model B (measurement invariance), so a leaderboard delta has no defined causal referent.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4414976969","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"VAL-Bench reframes value alignment as propositional belief-consistency — given a value-laden position P and its negation, it scores whether a model avoids endorsing both P and not-P across paired prompts — grounding the measure in the Law of Non-Contradiction to dodge the 'no universal values' problem by measuring consistency rather than value content. Its residue: belief-consistency conflates a model's value signal with its general consistency/calibration disposition and isolates no elicitation confound (style, phrasing, judge), so a consistency gap between two models cannot be attributed to a value difference vs. a calibration difference, and the paired-prompt scoring carries no invariance certificate that the same latent value is being probed identically across the compared models."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4404518508","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Measuring Human-AI Value Alignment quantifies alignment as a single composite distance between an LLM's elicited value profile and a human reference. Its residue: the composite collapses true-value distance and elicitation-style distance into one number with no decomposition, so a cross-model ranking by this score is not identifiable — it does not test whether the elicited value construct is comparable (invariant) across the models being ranked."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4417298502","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"AdAEM adaptively/automatically generates fresh, uncontaminated items to measure LLMs' value differences, fixing the informativeness problem of static, contaminated questionnaires. Its residue: making items adaptive per-model changes the elicitation instrument across the compared models, which strengthens informativeness but weakens comparability — it provides no guarantee that the adaptively-generated item set measures the same construct on each model (no measurement-invariance / anchoring control)."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7109045272","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"The Balance Penalty documents that LLM-as-judge evaluators systematically penalize balanced/nuanced moral responses by ~0.74-1.04 points, exposing a judge-side confound in alignment scoring. Its residue: it characterizes the judge confound but leaves it uncorrected in cross-model comparison — it provides no estimator that removes the judge's style bias from a model's value score so the residual reflects value disposition."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:af8b26c3f10acfe86aa0a07d11ce4653e1dbf1cc","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"This paper shows the SAME model's moral judgments shift with the prompt language, isolating a language-elicitation confound. Its residue: it demonstrates the confound exists but does not turn it into a control that subtracts elicitation-induced variance from a comparative score, so cross-model value comparisons still inherit per-model language/elicitation sensitivity as uncontrolled variance."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"value alignment evaluation / behavioral measurement of LLMs","venue":"ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML (alignment + evaluation tracks)","time":"2026","data":["existing value/moral-dilemma probe corpora (Moral Dilemma Dataset, Moral Foundations LLM, Greatest Good Benchmark, VAL-Bench, AdAEM items)","a panel of open + API LLMs to be compared","human value-judgment distributions where available"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML + measurement/psychometrics + alignment","preference":"both","baseline":"single-composite-score value-alignment benchmarks (Measuring Human-AI Value Alignment W4404518508), belief-consistency measures (VAL-Bench W4414976969), adaptive item-generation measures (AdAEM W4417298502)","limitation":"current comparative value-alignment scores conflate a model's true value disposition with elicitation-side confounds (prompt language, response style, item phrasing, judge bias), so a cross-model score difference is not attributable to a difference in values; no measure carries a validity certificate establishing that the same construct is being measured on each compared model.","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","compute","expertise","preference","data"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The audit lens applied at both sites is: treat the elicitation instrument (item phrasing, response-style scoring, and the judge) as an active variable rather than a neutral measuring stick. Site 1 (anchor leg, heterogeneous_decomposition). For an ordered pair of models (A,B) and a value-laden item i, let s_A(i), s_B(i) be the scalar value-behavior readout on item i — the judge's normalized score in [0,1] of the model's response, the SAME judge and rubric for both models. The raw observed gap is G(i)=s_A(i)-s_B(i). We model G(i)=V(i)+E_form(i)+E_style(i)+E_judge(i)+eps(i), where V(i) is the value-disposition contrast (the estimand), E_form is variance attributable to item phrasing, E_style to response-length/verbosity/hedging, E_judge to the judge's known biases (e.g. the balance penalty), and eps is noise. The nuisance terms are estimated by controlled replication: each item i is instantiated as a matched cluster of K paraphrase variants (same propositional content, varied surface form), each model's response is scored under L judge configurations (the primary judge plus style-normalized and persona-swapped variants), giving an item-by-form-by-judge response array per model. E_form(i) is the within-item across-paraphrase mean gap-shift, E_style(i) is the gap-shift between raw and length/verbosity-normalized judge scores (style-normalization holds content fixed and rewards/penalizes only stylistic features), E_judge(i) is the gap-shift across the L judge configurations; each is a fixed-effect estimate from the replication array. The de-confounded value-contrast is V_hat(i)=G(i)-E_form(i)-E_style(i)-E_judge(i), and the model-level value-alignment delta is the anchor-calibrated mean Delta_VA(A,B)=mean_i w(i)[V_hat(i)] where w(i) down-weights items the anchor block (Site 2) flags as non-invariant. The error decomposition bounds Var(Delta_VA) and proves Delta_VA recovers the value-contrast whenever the anchor null holds — that bound, not the partition idea, is the contribution. Site 2 (sibling leg, assumption_audit_and_pivot + controlled_diagnostic_design). Comparability is an identifiability claim: 'the same latent value is elicited identically on A and B.' Its precondition (instrument-neutrality) is not verifiable by construction, so we pivot it to a structural substitute that IS checkable: a block of N_anchor value-neutral items (factual/style-only items carrying no value content) plus a paraphrase/persona-permutation grid must yield a measured cross-model gap statistically indistinguishable from zero AFTER the same nuisance subtraction — a KNOWN NULL. The anchor block is the oracle independent of A and B: if Delta on the anchor block is non-zero, the instrument is non-invariant for that (A,B) pair and the corresponding value items are down-weighted (w(i)) or the comparison is declared non-identifiable. This delivers measurement invariance as an enforced, testable condition rather than an assumption. The two legs share the nuisance-subtraction machinery: Site 1's E_* estimators and Site 2's anchor null are computed from the same replication array, which is what makes this one paper — the anchor null calibrates exactly the subtraction that the decomposition relies on.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The two gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules: the evidence is that the anchor-null condition (Site 2) is defined as the SAME nuisance-subtracted gap statistic that Site 1 uses to estimate V_hat — a known-null block is just the decomposition evaluated where V(i)=0 by construction, so the audit's certificate and the decomposition's estimator read off one replication array; building them separately would duplicate the array and let the certificate drift from the estimator it certifies. Alternative designs considered and rejected: (1) a pure controlled_diagnostic_design benchmark that reports the de-confounded gap but no per-item decomposition — rejected because it gives a corrected score but not the attribution (how much of the gap is each nuisance), which is the anchor gap's actual demand; (2) a latent-trait IRT model fit jointly across models (lands on collateral node c1, a plain DIF re-run) — rejected per the regression flag, since classical DIF assumes a static human-calibrated item bank and human respondents and provides no elicitation-nuisance (style/judge) decomposition for generative models; (3) estimating nuisance terms by a learned regression on response features — rejected as it reintroduces a model whose validity is itself uncertified, whereas fixed-effect estimates from matched replication are auditable.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: take 6-8 instruction-tuned models spanning two known style families (verbose/hedging vs terse), run the replication grid over ~300 value items + ~100 anchor items with K=5 paraphrases and L=3 judges, and measure (metric) the rank correlation between the de-confounded value-alignment ranking and an INDEPENDENT held-out value-behavior outcome, versus the same correlation for the raw-composite ranking. If the candidate works, the de-confounded ranking's correlation with the held-out outcome INCREASES relative to the raw ranking, and at least one model pair's ranking FLIPS after nuisance subtraction. The named load-bearing variable is the elicitation-nuisance term E = E_form+E_style+E_judge (the quantity subtracted from the raw gap). Negative control: replace the value-neutral anchor block with RANDOM value-laden items (destroying the known-null symmetry-breaking that licenses the subtraction) while keeping the same E-subtraction; predicted effect on the downstream task-outcome metric — the de-confounded ranking's correlation with the held-out value-behavior outcome should fall back to (or below) the raw-ranking baseline, because without a valid anchor null the subtracted E no longer isolates value variance. Positive control: a stripped-down estimator that uses ONLY the anchor-calibrated style-normalized judge score (E_style path alone) should recover most of the ranking-flip and most of the held-out-correlation gain, confirming the elicitation term carries the mechanism.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4414976969","delta":"VAL-Bench scores a single model's propositional belief-consistency (avoiding P and not-P) as the alignment proxy; we construct a per-item decomposition of the BETWEEN-model gap into a value-contrast term and separable elicitation-nuisance terms with a variance bound, a quantity their within-model consistency score does not produce and cannot attribute."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4404518508","delta":"Measuring Human-AI Value Alignment reports one composite distance per model with no decomposition; we derive the value-attributable component V_hat(i) and prove it recovers the value-contrast under an enforced anchor-null condition, turning an un-attributable composite into an identifiable estimand."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4417298502","delta":"AdAEM adapts items per model to fight contamination, which varies the instrument across compared models; we instead hold a common instrument and CERTIFY cross-model measurement invariance via a known-null anchor block, supplying the comparability guarantee adaptive generation forfeits."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7109045272","delta":"The Balance Penalty documents the LLM-judge nuisance but leaves it uncorrected in comparison; we estimate E_judge as a fixed effect from a multi-judge replication array and subtract it from the cross-model gap, converting a documented confound into a removed variance component."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:af8b26c3f10acfe86aa0a07d11ce4653e1dbf1cc","delta":"This paper shows the same model's judgments shift with prompt language but stops at demonstration; we operationalize that elicitation sensitivity as an estimated nuisance term E_form within a comparative estimator and a down-weighting rule, not just a documented effect."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4404518508","what_step_was_missed":"Measuring Human-AI Value Alignment computed a single composite human-AI value distance per model but never constructed the matched-replication array (item-by-paraphrase-by-judge) that lets the cross-model gap be additively split into a value-contrast term and separately-estimated form/style/judge nuisance terms; without that array and an anchor-null calibration of the subtraction, the composite cannot expose which fraction of a model-to-model difference is value versus elicitation, which is exactly the decomposition our estimator supplies and bounds."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":245,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"Hard floor did not fire: gap_closure_reject_check is borderline (not triggered), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat is a competing-not-exact-mechanism overlap. recipe_application_check.verdict = applied for both entries, so the cited tactics are genuinely performed. The decisive finding is paper_pointed_threat: EigenBench — the candidate's exact namesake framing 'A Comparative Behavioral Measure of Value Alignment' — is addressable_via adding a specific differentiation_from_lit entry, and per the audit heuristic a paper-pointed threat addressable through a named candidate field routes to revise rather than advance, since shipping the card without distinguishing the seed's namesake measure is a concrete reviewer risk.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved measure DECOMPOSES an observed cross-model behavioral difference into a value-disposition component versus elicitation-side components (prompt-form, response-style, judge), so the value-attributable part of a leaderboard gap is never identified (additive need: identifiability/attribution of the difference).","main_pattern":"heterogeneous_decomposition","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is treating the partition criterion itself as the contribution while leaving its value unproven: papers propose a sensitivity/redundancy discriminator that reviewers map onto an established technique, omit comparison against both the strongest uniform baseline and the obvious cheap alternative, and validate in a regime where the bottleneck does not bite.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Presenting a sensitivity or redundancy proxy as the novelty invites the verdict that it rediscovers known mixed-precision or low-rank results unless it is sharply differentiated from the obvious prior criterion.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The nearest established discriminator here is classical DIF/IRT anchoring; core_mechanism_reasoning explicitly differentiates from it (classical DIF assumes static human-calibrated banks and gives no style/judge elicitation decomposition), so the proxy is defended rather than relabeled — but the differentiation lives in reasoning, not yet as a primary contribution claim."},{"lesson_quoted":"Omitting comparison against both the strongest uniform baseline and the obvious cheap alternative (SVD/PCA, structured dropout, a natively trained smaller model) leaves reviewers unable to tell whether the partition buys anything at all.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism_steps step 7 contrasts the de-confounded ranking against the raw-composite-score ranking (the strongest uniform baseline) and step 8 validates on an independent held-out outcome, so the uniform-vs-differentiated comparison is built in."},{"lesson_quoted":"Skipping any analysis of why the heterogeneity exists — the data or value distribution that drives the partition — makes the technical novelty and the potential impact impossible to assess.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The heterogeneity (value vs form/style/judge nuisance) is not asserted as folklore: each E_* term is grounded in a retrieved confound study (af8b26c3 language, W7109045272 judge balance penalty, a10f523b phrasing) and estimated as a fixed effect from the replication array."},{"lesson_quoted":"A clever partition with no measured real-world deployment metric reads as a proxy-only contribution and stalls at borderline.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The deployment metric here is the held-out independent value-behavior outcome (step 8) plus the measured ranking flip, not an internal proxy statistic, so the win is read on a downstream task."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"Every retrieved leaf silently assumes that the elicitation instrument (the item set and its scoring judge) is a neutral, model-independent measuring stick — no retrieved paper tests whether the instrument itself must be held fixed-and-validated across models, rather than assumed neutral, for a comparative score to be meaningful (subtractive: the shared inherited assumption, stated as the unasked question).","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The signature failure is an identifiability claim that outruns its proof — the pivoted assumption was not actually load-bearing, recovery is asserted while the decisive object is never established, or structural constraints are imposed without proving they are SUFFICIENT for recovery.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Stacking two established frameworks and re-proving identifiability of the union reads as incremental unless the pivoted assumption was genuinely load-bearing and the union admits a regime neither framework could reach alone.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The pivot is load-bearing: instrument-neutrality is the precondition that makes a cross-model comparison identifiable, and the candidate shows the precondition fails on elicitation-sensitive generative models — a regime classical DIF (human banks) never reached — rather than unioning two off-the-shelf methods."},{"lesson_quoted":"Advertising an identifiability or 'consistency' property while the proof omits the decisive object — never proving latent identifiability, or excluding part of the model from the guarantee — collapses the contribution the moment a reviewer checks the theorem.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The candidate claims the decomposition recovers the value-contrast 'whenever the anchor null holds' and supplies a variance bound, but stops short of a full identifiability-up-to-ambiguity-class theorem; the claim is correctly scoped to the anchor-null certificate, so it does not over-claim, but a reviewer will probe exactly how tight the recovery guarantee is."},{"lesson_quoted":"Imposing structural constraints to claim interpretability or disentanglement without proving those constraints are sufficient for recovery leaves the result indistinguishable from a post-hoc heuristic.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The anchor-null is not a post-hoc interpretability gloss: it is an enforced, testable condition (known-null block must yield zero gap after the same subtraction) that down-weights or declares non-identifiable any (A,B) pair failing it, making the structural condition operationally decisive rather than decorative."},{"lesson_quoted":"Proving identifiability conditions the algorithm neither enforces nor verifies creates a theory-practice disconnect that undermines both the soundness and the significance of the claim.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism shares one replication array between Site 1's estimator and Site 2's anchor null, so the very condition the recovery claim requires is the condition the algorithm computes and tests — the theory-practice gap the lesson warns about is closed by construction."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No entry triggered. The heterogeneous_decomposition entry is borderline on the 'differentiate the proxy from the obvious prior criterion (classical DIF/mixed-precision)' lesson, and the assumption_audit_and_pivot entry is borderline on 'identifiability claim that outruns its proof' — both are non-fatal because the differentiation from classical DIF and the variance-bound scoping are present in core_mechanism_reasoning, but each rides a load-bearing claim a reviewer will press."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved measure DECOMPOSES an observed cross-model behavioral difference into a value-disposition component versus elicitation-side components (prompt-form, response-style, judge), so the value-attributable part of a leaderboard gap is never identified (additive need: identifiability/attribution of the difference).","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Discriminate the components of an over-provisioned resource by a magnitude/sensitivity/influence/redundancy criterion into a high-impact minority and a near-redundant bulk and treat each differently, where the load-bearing artifact is an error/sensitivity decomposition that BOUNDS how the differentiated treatment recovers the original objective — that analysis, not the partition idea, is what separates the move from heuristic per-component tuning.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"Site 1 partitions the per-item observed gap G(i) into a value-contrast term V(i) and structurally distinct nuisance populations E_form/E_style/E_judge, estimates each nuisance as a fixed effect from the item-by-paraphrase-by-judge replication array, forms V_hat(i)=G(i)-sum(E), and supplies the error decomposition bounding Var(Delta_VA) and proving Delta_VA recovers the value-contrast under the anchor null — core_mechanism states verbatim 'that bound, not the partition idea, is the contribution,' which is exactly the C04 signature move.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"Every retrieved leaf silently assumes that the elicitation instrument (the item set and its scoring judge) is a neutral, model-independent measuring stick — no retrieved paper tests whether the instrument itself must be held fixed-and-validated across models, rather than assumed neutral, for a comparative score to be meaningful (subtractive: the shared inherited assumption, stated as the unasked question).","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Take an existing identifiability/recovery precondition and pivot on the assumption it requires, swapping a distributional/parametric assumption for a structural, architectural, or geometric one that carries the same identifying power but that the setting plausibly satisfies and that is checkable in practice.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"Site 2 pins the load-bearing precondition (instrument-neutrality: 'the same latent value is elicited identically on A and B'), shows it is not verifiable by construction, and pivots it to a structural substitute that IS checkable — a value-neutral anchor block plus a paraphrase/persona-permutation grid that must yield a measured cross-model gap statistically indistinguishable from zero after the same nuisance subtraction (a KNOWN NULL) — which is the C05 distributional-to-structural pivot on a genuinely load-bearing identifiability precondition.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries instantiate their cited cluster's distinctive move: Site 1 delivers the C04 error/variance-decomposition-as-contribution (not a bare partition), and Site 2 performs the C05 pivot of a load-bearing identifiability precondition onto a checkable structural anchor-null condition rather than the parent pattern's generic 'question an assumption' gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["heterogeneous_decomposition","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"The gap_closure main_pattern set {heterogeneous_decomposition, assumption_audit_and_pivot} does not match any of the three reject-favored compositions (decomp+self_supervised, decomp+structural_prior, operator+decomp); the controlled_diagnostic_design companion is a deliverable note, not a gap_closure main_pattern, so no anti-pattern fires."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:6ec537e8231611623b51712a0058f0d9f2800f40","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"EigenBench ('A Comparative Behavioral Measure of Value Alignment', arXiv 2025-09) is the closest competitor surfaced by collision retrieval — it shares the candidate's exact framing (a comparative behavioral measure that returns a per-model value-alignment score vector) and uses a black-box peer-judging design where each model judges others' outputs and EigenTrust aggregates the judgments into a consensus score. It threatens the candidate's 'comparative behavioral measure' positioning. But it does NOT subsume the candidate's claim: EigenBench produces an aggregate consensus score with no decomposition of a cross-model gap into a value-contrast term versus separable elicitation-nuisance terms, and its mutual-judging design makes the judges THEMSELVES the elicitation instrument (the very judge/style/form nuisance the candidate isolates and subtracts), with no anchor-null measurement-invariance certificate. The candidate's load-bearing contributions — the per-item nuisance decomposition with a variance bound and the known-null anchor block that certifies cross-model comparability — are precisely what EigenBench lacks, so the candidate stands as the de-confounding layer EigenBench's consensus score still needs.","addressable_via":"Add a differentiation_from_lit entry against EigenBench making explicit that the consensus-aggregation score conflates value disposition with the judge-ensemble's own elicitation bias and carries no invariance certificate, which the candidate's anchor-null decomposition supplies."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat: EigenBench (semanticscholar:6ec537e8231611623b51712a0058f0d9f2800f40) is the closest competing comparative behavioral value-alignment measure and is currently uncited in differentiation_from_lit.","fix_direction":"Append one differentiation_from_lit entry with paper_id 'semanticscholar:6ec537e8231611623b51712a0058f0d9f2800f40' and a delta stating that EigenBench returns an ensemble-consensus score vector via mutual model-judging aggregated by EigenTrust, with no per-item decomposition of the cross-model gap into a value-contrast term versus elicitation-nuisance terms and no measurement-invariance certificate — and that its mutual-judging design makes the judge ensemble itself an uncontrolled elicitation instrument (the very judge/style nuisance the candidate estimates and subtracts), whereas the candidate ships the value-vs-elicitation decomposition with a variance bound and an anchor-null comparability certificate EigenBench lacks. Do not modify any other field; falsification_prediction and compute_budget are kill-switch fields and must stay byte-identical."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Appended a differentiation_from_lit entry against EigenBench (semanticscholar:6ec537e8...), distinguishing our value-vs-elicitation decomposition + anchor-null invariance certificate from its EigenTrust consensus-score aggregation that leaves the judge ensemble as an uncontrolled elicitation instrument."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Anchored Decomposition: Attributing Cross-Model Value-Alignment Gaps to Values, Not Elicitation\n\n**Method.** Anchored Decomposition\n\n## Motivation\nWhen people compare two language models on how well their values line up with human values, they usually get a single score per model and rank the models by it. The problem is that this score blends two very different things: how the model actually 'feels' about a values question, and surface stuff about HOW the answer was drawn out and graded — the exact wording of the question, whether the model is wordy or hedging, and the biases of whatever judge scores the answer. So when model A beats model B, you cannot tell whether A really has better-aligned values or just happens to phrase things in a way the judge likes. Recent work gets close: VAL-Bench (openalex:W4414976969) grounds the score in belief consistency, the Balance Penalty study (openalex:W7109045272) shows LLM judges punish nuanced moral answers, and a language study (af8b26c3) shows the same model's morals shift with the prompt language — but each one either reports a single number or just documents a confound without removing it. AdAEM (openalex:W4417298502) refreshes the questions per model, which actually makes the instrument differ between the models being compared, hurting comparability. Our move is to treat the question-and-judge setup as an active ingredient, not a neutral ruler: we write the observed gap between two models on each item as a value part plus separate 'how it was elicited' parts (wording, style, judge), estimate each elicitation part by re-running every item in several paraphrases and under several judges, and subtract them. We also add a block of value-neutral anchor items that SHOULD show zero gap; if they don't, the comparison is flagged as untrustworthy for that model pair. What changes: a leaderboard gap finally gets a clear meaning — how much is values versus elicitation — and we expect the elicitation part to often be big enough to flip the ranking once removed.\n\n## Method\n### Anchor-and-Replication Instrument\n*Builds a common, fixed instrument with a value-neutral anchor block and a matched paraphrase x judge replication grid so elicitation effects become separately measurable.*\n\n1. Collect value-related questions from existing public sets (VAL-Bench position pairs, the Greatest Good utilitarian dilemmas, Moral Foundations items) and store each as a record with an id, its source, the prompt text, and a flag marking it as value-bearing. Separately, write about 100 value-neutral anchor questions of two kinds: plain factual questions with one correct answer, and pure-style format-following tasks; confirm each carries no moral/value content by having at least two people agree, and keep only the ones everyone agrees on. 【author decision: whether the anchor questions should be matched to the value questions in length and format — matching gives a stricter zero-baseline but is harder to source.】\n   - _Why_: The anchor items are a built-in 'should-be-zero' control: any gap they show is pure instrument artifact, not values.\n2. For every question, create K=5 reworded versions that keep the meaning identical, using a language model to reword and then a Natural Language Inference (NLI) model to verify each reworded version both implies and is implied by the original above a strict confidence cutoff (default: the NLI model's top-decile entailment score), with a human check on a random 10% sample; throw out and redo any that fail. Set up L=3 ways of grading: the normal rubric grader; a style-normalized grader that first rewrites the answer to remove hedging and force a fixed length before grading; and a persona-swapped grader that runs the same rubric under several different assistant personas and averages. Every (question $\\times $ rewording $\\times $ grader) combination is one cell, and each grader returns a score between 0 and 1.\n   - _Why_: Re-running each item many ways is what lets you measure how much the wording, the style, and the judge each move the score, separately.\n3. For each model you are comparing, send every (question, rewording) cell to the model, collect its answer, and grade that answer with all L=3 graders, filling a per-model table indexed by question, rewording, and grader with scores between 0 and 1. Crucially, every model sees the exact same questions, rewordings, and graders, so the measuring setup is identical across models.\n   - _Why_: Everyone is measured with the exact same instrument, so the only thing left to explain a difference is the model itself plus the elicitation effects you are about to estimate.\n\n### Gap Decomposition\n*Splits the per-item cross-model gap into a value-contrast term and form/style/judge nuisance fixed effects with a variance bound.*\n\n4. For each pair of models and each question, compute the raw score gap, then fit a small linear model over that question's (rewording, grader) cells that splits the gap into a part explained by which rewording was used, a part explained by which grader was used, and a part explained by switching the normal grader for the style-normalized one. Those three parts are the wording, judge, and style nuisance amounts; subtract all three from the raw gap to get the value-only contrast for that question (the de-confounded value-contrast shown by the equations under this step). Save per question the raw gap, the three nuisance amounts, the value-only contrast, and the leftover variance.\n\n*The observed per-item between-model gap G(i) is modeled as a value-contrast term V(i) plus elicitation-nuisance terms for item form, response style, and judge, plus noise $\\epsilon (i).$*\n$$ G(i) = V(i) + E_{\\mathrm{form}}(i) + E_{\\mathrm{style}}(i) + E_{\\mathrm{judge}}(i) + \\varepsilon(i) \\tag{1} $$\n\n\n*The de-confounded value-contrast estimate subtracts the three estimated nuisance fixed effects from the raw gap.*\n$$ \\hat{V}(i) = G(i) - E_{\\mathrm{form}}(i) - E_{\\mathrm{style}}(i) - E_{\\mathrm{judge}}(i) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Each nuisance term is the part of the gap explained by a non-value factor, so removing them leaves the part that is actually about values.\n\n### Known-Null Calibration\n*Uses the anchor block to certify cross-model measurement invariance and down-weight or reject non-identifiable pairs.*\n\n5. Run the exact same subtraction on the value-neutral anchor questions, where the cleaned gap should be zero. Test that by taking the average cleaned anchor gap and comparing it to a null built by shuffling the rewording labels within each question 10000 times to get a two-sided p-value, correcting for testing many anchor groups (Holm-Bonferroni). For each model pair, output whether the instrument looks invariant, and give each value question a weight: full weight if its closest anchor group (matched by embedding similarity) passes the zero test, and a reduced weight in proportion to how far the anchor group's leftover gap is from zero when it fails. 【author decision: where to set the line at which a model pair is called 'not comparable' instead of just down-weighted — this trades how many pairs you can report against how clean each comparison is.】\n\n*The known-null anchor condition: on value-neutral anchor items, the same nuisance-subtracted gap must be statistically indistinguishable from zero for the comparison to be identifiable.*\n$$ H_0:\\ \\mathbb{E}_{i\\in\\mathrm{anchor}}\\big[G(i) - \\textstyle\\sum E(i)\\big] = 0 \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Anchor items have no value content, so any residual gap there means your subtraction did not fully clean the instrument — a direct, honest check on the comparison's validity.\n\n### Certified Delta and Validation\n*Aggregates the anchor-certified value-alignment delta, contrasts de-confounded vs raw rankings, and validates against an independent held-out value-behavior outcome.*\n\n6. Combine the per-question value-only contrasts into one number per model pair by taking their weighted average using the anchor weights from the previous step (this is the value-alignment delta defined by the equation under this step), and carry the per-question leftover variances through to put a confidence interval on it. The output per pair is the de-confounded value-alignment delta with error bars.\n\n*The model-pair value-alignment delta is the anchor-weighted mean of the per-item de-confounded value-contrast, where w(i) down-weights items flagged non-invariant by the anchor block.*\n$$ \\Delta_{\\mathrm{VA}}(A,B) = \\sum_i w(i)\\,\\hat{V}(i) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The bound turns a single mystery number into an estimate you can put error bars on and defend.\n7. Do steps step 3 (For each model you are comparing) through step 6 (Combine the per-question $value-only\\dots )$ for every pair of models, then rank the models two ways — by the cleaned value-only delta and by the original raw composite score — and put the two rankings side by side. Also produce a table that, for each pair, reports what fraction of the gap was value versus each of the three nuisance sources (wording, style, judge). These two rankings and the table are the main results.\n   - _Why_: The side-by-side is the headline result: it shows whether removing elicitation effects actually changes who is 'more aligned'.\n8. Check the cleaned ranking against a separate value-behavior test that is not in the question pool — for example a forced-choice battery (resource allocation or trolley-style choices) scored by which value option the model picks, where a model's held-out score is how often it picks the target option and a pair's held-out gap is the difference between their rates. Then see whether the cleaned ranking lines up with this independent test better (higher rank correlation) than the raw ranking does. 【author decision: exactly which held-out task battery to use — it has to be about values yet provably not overlap with the questions used in the measurement.】\n   - _Why_: If the cleaned-up ranking really captures values, it should predict independent value behavior better than the noisy raw score.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 锚定分解：将跨模型价值对齐差距归因于价值本身而非诱发方式（Anchored Decomposition）\n\n**方法名称.** Anchored Decomposition\n\n## 研究动机\n当人们比较两个语言模型在价值观上与人类价值对齐得有多好时，通常每个模型只得到一个分数，然后按分数排名。问题在于，这个分数混在一起的是两件很不一样的事：模型在某个价值问题上真实的倾向，以及与「答案是怎么被问出来、怎么被打分」有关的表层因素——题目的具体措辞、模型回答是啰嗦还是含糊、以及打分用的 judge 自身的偏好。于是当模型 A 赢过模型 B 时，你无法判断是 A 的价值观真的更对齐，还是它恰好用了 judge 喜欢的表达方式。近期工作很接近这个点：VAL-Bench（openalex:W4414976969）把分数建立在信念一致性上，Balance Penalty 研究（openalex:W7109045272）显示 LLM judge 会惩罚细腻的道德回答，一篇语言研究（af8b26c3）显示同一个模型的道德判断会随 prompt 语言变化——但它们要么只报一个数字，要么只是记录了混淆因素却没有把它去掉。AdAEM（openalex:W4417298502）为每个模型刷新题目，这反而让被比较的两个模型用的「尺子」不一样，损害了可比性。我们的做法是把「出题加打分」这套装置当成一个会起作用的变量，而不是中性的尺子：我们把每道题上两模型的观测差距写成「价值部分」加上若干「诱发部分」（措辞 $E_{form}$、风格 $E_{style}$、judge $E_{judge}$），通过把每道题用多个 paraphrase、在多个 judge 配置下重复测量来估计每个诱发部分，再把它们减掉。我们还加入一组价值中性的 anchor 题目，它们「本应」显示零差距；如果不为零，就把该模型对的比较标记为不可信。这样带来的改变是：排行榜上的差距终于有了明确含义——多少来自价值、多少来自诱发——而且我们预期诱发部分往往大到一旦减掉就会让排名翻转。\n\n## 方法\n### 锚定与重复测量工具\n*构建一个固定的公共工具，含价值中性 anchor 块和配对的 paraphrase x judge 重复网格，使诱发效应可被分别测量。*\n\n1. 从现有公开数据集收集与价值相关的题目（VAL-Bench 的成对立场题、Greatest Good 功利主义困境题、Moral Foundations 题目），每题存成一条记录，含 id、来源、prompt 文本，以及一个标记它含价值内容的标志位。另外编写约 100 道价值中性的 anchor 题目，分两类：有唯一正确答案的纯事实题，以及纯风格的格式遵循任务；通过至少两名标注者一致确认每题不含任何道德/价值内容，只保留全体一致的题目。【作者需决定：anchor 题目是否要在长度和格式上与价值题目匹配——匹配能给出更严格的零基线，但更难取材。】\n   - _为什么_: anchor 题目是内建的「本应为零」对照：它们上面出现的任何差距都是纯粹的工具假象，而非价值。\n2. 对每道题，用一个语言模型改写出 K=5 个含义完全不变的版本，再用自然语言推理(Natural Language Inference, NLI)模型验证每个改写版本与原句在严格置信度阈值以上互相蕴含（默认取 NLI 模型蕴含分数的前 10% 分位），并对随机 10% 的样本做人工抽检；不合格的丢弃重做。设置 L=3 种打分方式：常规 rubric 打分器；style-normalized 打分器——先把回答改写成去掉含糊措辞、统一到固定长度再打分；以及 persona-swapped 打分器——用同一 rubric 在若干不同助手 persona 下运行并取平均。每个（题目 $\\times $ 改写 $\\times $ 打分器）组合是一个单元，每个打分器给出 0 到 1 之间的分数。\n   - _为什么_: 把每道题用多种方式重复测量，才能分别量出措辞、风格、judge 各自把分数推动了多少。\n3. 对每个要比较的模型，把每个（题目、改写）单元发给模型、收集其回答，并用全部 L=3 个打分器给该回答打分，填进一张按题目、改写、打分器索引、取值 0 到 1 的每模型表格。关键在于：每个模型看到的题目、改写、打分器完全相同，因此对所有模型而言测量装置是一致的。\n   - _为什么_: 所有模型都用完全相同的工具测量，于是能解释差异的就只剩模型本身，加上你接下来要估计的诱发效应。\n\n### 差距分解\n*把逐题的跨模型差距拆成价值对比项与 form/style/judge 噪声固定效应，并给出方差界。*\n\n4. 对每一对模型、每道题，先算出原始分数差距，再在该题的（改写、打分器）单元上拟合一个小型线性模型，把差距拆成「由用了哪个改写解释的部分」「由用了哪个打分器解释的部分」以及「由把常规打分器换成 style-normalized 打分器解释的部分」。这三部分就是措辞、judge、风格三类噪声量；把三者从原始差距中减去，得到该题只剩价值的对比（即本步骤公式所示的去混淆价值对比）。每题保存原始差距、三个噪声量、只含价值的对比，以及残余方差。\n\n*将逐题的跨模型差距 G(i) 建模为价值对比项 V(i) 加上题面形式、回答风格、评审三类诱发噪声项，再加噪声 $\\epsilon (i)$。*\n$$ G(i) = V(i) + E_{\\mathrm{form}}(i) + E_{\\mathrm{style}}(i) + E_{\\mathrm{judge}}(i) + \\varepsilon(i) \\tag{1} $$\n\n\n*去混淆后的价值对比估计 $\\hat{V}(i)$，是从原始差距中减去三类已估计的诱发固定效应。*\n$$ \\hat{V}(i) = G(i) - E_{\\mathrm{form}}(i) - E_{\\mathrm{style}}(i) - E_{\\mathrm{judge}}(i) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 每个噪声项都是差距中由非价值因素解释的那部分，减掉之后剩下的就是真正关于价值的部分。\n\n### 已知零校准\n*用 anchor 块认证跨模型测量不变性，并对不可识别的模型对降权或拒绝。*\n\n5. 在价值中性的 anchor 题目上做完全相同的减法，那里清洗后的差距本应为零。检验方法：取清洗后 anchor 差距的平均值，与通过在每道题内把改写标签打乱 10000 次构造的零分布比较，得到双侧 p 值，并对同时检验多个 anchor 组做校正（Holm-Bonferroni）。对每个模型对，输出工具是否看起来不变，并给每道价值题一个权重：若其最近的 anchor 组（按 embedding 相似度匹配）通过零检验则给满权重，未通过时按该 anchor 组残余差距偏离零的程度成比例降权。【作者需决定：在何处划线将一个模型对判为「不可比」而非仅降权——这在能报告多少个模型对与每个比较有多干净之间权衡。】\n\n*已知零假设的锚定条件：在价值中性的锚定题目上，同样的去噪后差距必须在统计上与零不可区分，跨模型比较才可识别。*\n$$ H_0:\\ \\mathbb{E}_{i\\in\\mathrm{anchor}}\\big[G(i) - \\textstyle\\sum E(i)\\big] = 0 \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: anchor 题目没有价值内容，所以那里的任何残余差距都意味着你的减法没有把工具清干净——这是对比较有效性的直接而诚实的检查。\n\n### 认证差值与验证\n*聚合锚定认证的价值对齐差，对比去混淆与原始排名，并用独立留出的价值行为结果做验证。*\n\n6. 用上一步的 anchor 权重，把每道题只含价值的对比加权平均成每个模型对的一个数（即本步骤公式定义的价值对齐差 $\\Delta _{VA}$），并把每题的残余方差传播过来，给它加上置信区间。每个模型对的输出就是带误差棒的去混淆价值对齐差。\n\n*模型对的价值对齐差 $\\Delta _{VA}(A,B)$ 是逐题去混淆价值对比的锚定加权均值，其中 w(i) 对被锚定块判定为非不变的题目降权。*\n$$ \\Delta_{\\mathrm{VA}}(A,B) = \\sum_i w(i)\\,\\hat{V}(i) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这个界把一个孤零零的神秘数字变成一个能加误差棒、能被辩护的估计。\n7. 对每一对模型执行 第3步（对每个要比较的模型） 到 第6步（用上一步的 $anchor\\dots $），然后用两种方式给模型排名——按清洗后只含价值的差值，以及按原始的复合分数——并把两个排名并排放。再做一张表，对每个模型对报告差距中有多少比例来自价值、多少来自三类噪声（措辞、风格、judge）。这两个排名和这张表就是主要结果。\n   - _为什么_: 这个并排就是核心结果：它显示去掉诱发效应后「谁更对齐」是否真的改变了。\n8. 用一个不在题库里的独立价值行为测试来检验清洗后的排名——例如一个强制选择电池（资源分配或电车式选择），按模型选了哪个价值选项来计分，每个模型的留出分数是它选中目标选项的比率，一对模型的留出差距就是两者比率之差。然后看清洗后的排名是否比原始排名更吻合这个独立测试（更高的秩相关）。【作者需决定：具体用哪个留出任务电池——它必须关乎价值，又能证明与测量所用题目不重叠。】\n   - _为什么_: 如果清洗后的排名真的捕捉到了价值，它就应当比含噪的原始分数更能预测独立的价值行为。\n\n"},{"id":"35","run_dir":"run_prompt35_prosody","index":35,"title":"Reward the Prosody, Not the Prediction: Cue-Faithful RL for Explainable Speech Emotion Reasoning","title_zh":"奖励韵律而非预测：面向可解释语音情感推理的线索忠实强化学习","method_name":"Cue-Faithful RL (CF-RL)","hook":"Every reinforcement-learning treatment of explainable emotion reasoning anchors its reward to the model's own predicted label or to explanation-prediction agreement, so a rationale that cites a prosodic cue the utterance does not contain is never penalized. We re-anchor the reward to the measured signal: a rationale is rewarded only when each acoustic cue it names is actually present in the utterance's extracted prosody AND the cited cue causally supports the emotion under a counterfactual prosody edit.","anchor_pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","anchor_pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","domain_category":"Speech & Audio","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf supplies a learning signal that rewards an emotion rationale for being faithful to the utterance's externally measured prosody: across the frontier the reward is the outcome label (openalex:W4416432860) or explanation–prediction consistency (openalex:W7102328481, openalex:W4417009235), so a rationale can name prosodic cues absent from the signal and pay no cost — the missing outcome is a rationale whose cue-attributions are checkable against the acoustics, however that check is","pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","sub_pattern":"C26 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by manufacturing a non-human comparative reward — a per-cue Cue-Faithfulness Reward sourced from an off-the-shelf prosody extractor (not from the label or the model's prediction) and consumed by a GRPO-style preference objective, re-granularized to the individual cue mention so credit lands on the specific unfaithful attribution rather than on a holistic rationale score.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether explanation correctness must be defined relative to the predicted label / the model's own output at all, rather than relative to the independent acoustic evidence — every reasoning-reward leaf (openalex:W4416432860, openalex:W7102328481, openalex:W4417009235) silently inherits from a shared label-anchored-reward ancestor the assumption that a rationale is 'correct' when it agrees with the prediction, leaving unasked whether the correctness target should be the sig","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","how_closed":"Closed by relocating the reward's enforcement locus from the prediction (a scalar agreement signal) to the measured-prosody locus (the extracted cue track), naming the prediction-anchored locus as the inherited tacit-invariance claim and showing the old locus is the wrong place to look (the audit/pivot half); the controlled_diagnostic_design companion ships the confound-isolating matched-pair instrument that demonstrates the two loci diverge — utterances a prediction-anchored reward scores as fully correct but the signal-anchored reward rejects.","is_anchor":false},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes how rationale cue-attribution behaves under the acoustic distribution shifts SER is known to suffer (acted vs naturalistic, cross-corpus, speaker variability — arxiv:2601.16240v1): whether label accuracy and explanation faithfulness degrade together or decouple under shift is unmeasured, so there is no diagnostic that isolates 'right answer, wrong reason' from ordinary accuracy loss.","pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by constructing a confound-isolating diagnostic that holds label-accuracy fixed while varying the acoustic-shift axis (acted→naturalistic, cross-corpus, held-out speakers), with an oracle (the prosody extractor) independent of the SpeechLM under test, and reports the accuracy-faithfulness gap — the share of correctly-classified utterances whose cue-attributions are unfaithful — as the headline measurement no current evaluation produces.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"explainable speech emotion recognition / affective speech reasoning with reinforcement learning","n_papers":50,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":25},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10},{"source":"openreview","n":2}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":12,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A Study on Speech Emotion Recognition Based on MFCC and KNN Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Machine Learning Based Speech Emotion Recognition System"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Speech Emotion Recognition in Native and Nonnative Languages"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Emotion Recognition from Human Speech Using Linguistic and Paralinguistic Features Through a Soft Voting Approach"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Machine Learning Algorithms for Emotion Recognition Using Audio and Text Data"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Analyzing the influence of different speech data corpora and speech features on speech emotion recognition: A review"}],"more":6},{"year":2025,"n":27,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"MIMCL: Multilayer Interaction Module with Contrastive Learning for Speech Emotion Recognition"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Speech Emotion Recognition Using Bark-Scale Cepstral Features and MLP Classifier on RAVDESS Speech Corpus"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Deep Learning Driven Automated System for Speech Emotion Recognition"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Enhancing Embedded Space with Low–Level Features for Speech Emotion Recognition"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"EmoSRE: Emotion prediction based speech synthesis and refined speech recognition using large language model and prosody encoding"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A Survey of Speech and Text-Based Emotion Recognition"}],"more":21},{"year":2026,"n":11,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"},{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"EmoShift: Lightweight Activation Steering for Enhanced Emotion-Aware Speech Synthesis"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Human-Guided Reasoning with Large Language Models for Vietnamese Speech Emotion Recognition"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Test-Time Adaptation for Speech Emotion Recognition"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Advancing automatic speech recognition using feature fusion with self-supervised learning features: A case study on Fearless Steps Apollo corpus"}],"more":5}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":12,"share":0.24},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":12,"share":0.24},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":9,"share":0.18},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":8,"share":0.16},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":7,"share":0.14},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":6,"share":0.12},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":5,"share":0.1},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":5,"share":0.1}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Explainable speech-emotion systems now emit a natural-language rationale alongside the predicted emotion that names acoustic/prosodic cues (“rising pitch and faster speech rate signal anger”), but the training signal that shapes these rationales never checks whether the cited cues are actually present in the utterance's measured prosody. In the SER setting the rationale is produced by distillation from a teacher LLM and supervised only against majority labels (openalex:W7083798070), so a rationale that invents a prosodic cue the signal does not contain is penalized only if it changes the final label — it is otherwise free. The reinforcement-learning treatments that do shape the rationale come from other modalities and reward only rationale–label agreement: Facial-R1 (openalex:W4416432860) rewards reasoning that matches the emotion/AU label, and the Emotional Rationale Verifier (openalex:W7102328481) and MIGR (openalex:W4417009235) reward explanation–prediction coherence — none reward the rationale for being consistent with the externally measurable evidence it cites. The result is a failure mode where a model can be simultaneously accurate and systematically wrong about why: under the acoustic distribution shifts that SER suffers (acted vs naturalistic, cross-corpus, speaker variability — arxiv:2601.16240v1), the label can stay right while the cue-attribution in the rationale detaches from the signal, and no current objective can detect or correct this because correctness of the explanation is measured against the label or against the model's own prediction, never against the prosody.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W7083798070","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Frames SER as a generative reasoning task: a SpeechLM emits a transcript, an emotion label, and a natural-language rationale grounded in lexical and acoustic cues, trained by distilling rationales from a teacher LLM plus majority-label fine-tuning, and evaluated for human-judged plausibility. The residue is that supervision is plausibility/label-driven, not evidence-driven: nothing verifies that an acoustic cue the rationale names is actually present in the utterance's measured prosody, so the rationale's cue-attribution can be unfaithful while still reading as plausible and matching the label. [residue is abstract-level: anchor fulltext unfetchable]"},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416432860","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Facial-R1 aligns reasoning with recognition for facial emotion analysis via R1-style RL whose reward is the emotion and Action-Unit label correctness, plus a data-synthesis loop. The residue is that the reward verifies the OUTCOME label (and AU presence on the visual side), not whether the verbalized reasoning is grounded in independently measured signal evidence; ported to speech there is no AU analogue, so the question of grounding the rationale in measured prosody is left entirely open."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7102328481","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"The Emotional Rationale Verifier trains a verifier and an Explanation Reward that push an MLLM's emotion reasoning to be consistent with the target emotion, improving explanation–prediction coherence on visual benchmarks. The residue is that the reward is consistency between explanation and label/prediction — a self-referential target that a label-correct but evidence-detached rationale satisfies perfectly — with no term tying the rationale to externally measured acoustic cues."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4417009235","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"MIGR reorders the reasoning to begin from the emotion-dominant modality and uses modality-aware reward optimization to cut cases where a correct prediction carries an emotionally inconsistent explanation. The residue is that 'dominant modality' is chosen at the modality granularity and the reward still scores explanation–emotion consistency, not whether the specific prosodic cues the explanation cites are present in the audio; intra-acoustic cue faithfulness is untouched."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2604.01711v1","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"A human-machine collaborative SER framework feeds LLM reasoning auxiliary acoustic signals (confidence, feature-level evidence) and routes ambiguous samples to the LLM under human-derived rules. The residue is that acoustic evidence is injected as a prompt-side auxiliary input and reasoning is prompted, not optimized: nothing rewards the produced rationale for being faithful to that evidence, and the rules are hand-authored rather than learned from a grounding signal."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"explainable speech emotion recognition / affective speech reasoning with reinforcement learning","venue":"ICLR / NeurIPS / Interspeech (ML + speech)","time":"2026","data":["MSP-Podcast (naturalistic, annotator-disaggregated)","IEMOCAP","MSP-IMPROV","any SER corpus with extractable frame-level prosody (pitch/F0, energy, duration, voice quality)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with speech + RL background; access to a pretrained SpeechLM / audio-language model and a prosody extractor","preference":"both","baseline":"SFT/distillation explainable SpeechLM for SER (Reasoning Beyond Majority Vote, openalex:W7083798070); RL-aligned emotion reasoning in other modalities (Facial-R1 openalex:W4416432860; Emotional Rationale Verifier openalex:W7102328481; MIGR openalex:W4417009235)","limitation":"Explainable SER models emit natural-language rationales citing acoustic cues, but nothing checks whether those cited cues are actually present in the signal; rationales are rewarded for being plausible or label-consistent, not for being faithful to the measured prosody.","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared audit lens is one question — 'against what is an emotion rationale CORRECT: the model's own prediction, or the utterance's measured prosody?' — applied at three sites: how the reward is built, what the reward's target is, and how faithfulness is measured. SITE 1 (anchor, C26 move = manufacture a comparative reward from a non-human source, optimize with a preference objective). We take a pretrained SpeechLM that, given an utterance, emits an emotion label and a free-text rationale whose sentences cite prosodic cues. We parse each rationale into a set of (cue_type, direction, span) mentions, where cue_type ranges over a fixed inventory of seven measurable prosodic attributes {F0-mean, F0-range, energy/intensity, speaking-rate, pause-ratio, jitter, shimmer}, direction ∈ {high/rising, low/falling, neutral}, and span is the optional time region the rationale points to (whole-utterance if unspecified); parsing is done by a frozen instruction-tuned text LLM with a fixed extraction prompt (a deterministic external readout, not a learned head). Independently, an off-the-shelf prosody extractor (openSMILE/Praat-style; an external oracle) computes each cue_type's measured value on the utterance and z-normalizes it per-speaker-or-per-corpus to a signed level m_c ∈ {high if z>+τ, low if z<−τ, neutral otherwise}, with τ a fixed threshold hyperparameter (default τ=0.5). The Cue-Faithfulness Reward for one rationale is R_fid = (1/|mentions|) Σ_mention [ present(cue) · agree(direction, m_c) ] − λ_hall · (count of cited cue_types whose measured value is neutral, i.e. hallucinated cues) , where present/agree are 1/0 indicators and λ_hall is the hallucination penalty weight (default 0.5); R_fid is purely a function of the rationale text and the extractor output, never of the predicted label. SITE 1 is re-granularized to the cue mention (C26 step 3): credit lands on the specific unfaithful mention, not a holistic score, by computing R_fid as the mention-averaged term above so the policy gradient points at the offending attribution. We additionally add a causal term R_cf: for the single highest-weighted cited cue, synthesize a counterfactually prosody-edited copy of the utterance (resynthesis that flips that one cue's level via a vocoder/PSOLA pitch-or-rate shift while holding lexical content fixed) and reward the rationale only if the SpeechLM's predicted emotion changes on the edited audio in the direction the rationale claimed the cue supports — so a cited cue must be not merely present but causally load-bearing for the prediction. The total reward is R = R_task (label correctness vs majority/annotator-aware label) + α·R_fid + β·R_cf, optimized with GRPO (group-relative, critic-free) on rollouts of (label, rationale) per utterance; α, β are fixed mixing weights. SITE 2 (audit+pivot, C01 move = relocate the enforcement locus). The existing leaves enforce rationale correctness at the prediction locus (R is a function of the predicted label or of explanation–prediction agreement); we name that as the inherited tacit-invariance claim ('the prediction is a sufficient correctness anchor') and relocate enforcement to the measured-prosody locus (R_fid + R_cf read the extracted cue track, an axis the prior rewards treat as irrelevant). The companion controlled_diagnostic_design ships the deliverable the audit cannot itself produce: a matched-pair set where, for the same predicted-correct label, one member has a signal-faithful rationale and the other a signal-unfaithful one differing only in a cited cue — proving a prediction-anchored reward assigns both the same (high) score while the signal-anchored reward separates them, i.e. the old locus is provably the wrong place to look. SITE 3 (diagnostic, C02 move = isolate a confound). We build the Accuracy-Faithfulness diagnostic: stratify a corpus by acoustic shift (acted IEMOCAP/MSP-IMPROV → naturalistic MSP-Podcast; cross-corpus; held-out speakers), hold label-accuracy fixed by conditioning only on correctly-classified utterances, and measure the de-confounded quantity faithfulness@correct = fraction of correctly-classified utterances whose every cited cue is present-and-agreeing under the extractor oracle. Reporting faithfulness@correct as a function of shift is the headline: it isolates 'right answer, wrong reason' from ordinary accuracy loss, which no aggregate SER metric or plausibility rating can do. All three sites read the same extracted-cue track, so they are one paper, not three: the track is the reward source (site 1), the relocated locus (site 2), and the diagnostic oracle (site 3).","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The three gaps share machinery because all three reduce to one object — the extracted prosodic-cue track and the present/agree check against it — which serves simultaneously as reward source, audit locus, and diagnostic oracle; the evidence is that none of the three can be built without that track, so splitting them into separate modules would duplicate it three times and invite the 'two papers stapled' reading. (b) Alternatives considered and rejected: (i) sourcing the faithfulness signal from learned attention/attribution over acoustic features (a C07-style internal readout) — rejected because attention weights are not validated as faithful and would re-introduce the very unverified-explanation problem we attack, landing on the post-hoc-attention ancestral node n1 the lineage flags; (ii) a generate-and-filter data pipeline (C08) that distills more teacher rationales — rejected because it walks back to the distillation/SFT ancestor n5 (Reasoning Beyond Majority Vote) and never installs a reward over the signal; (iii) defining faithfulness purely as cue-presence without the counterfactual term — rejected because mere co-presence is correlational (a model could cite whatever cues happen to be high), so the R_cf causal term is what makes the reward a mechanism rather than a co-occurrence detector. The avoided regression nodes (n1 post-hoc attention, n5 distillation-only) are recorded here per Hard rule 2.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: fine-tune one pretrained SpeechLM SER model (e.g. a Qwen-Audio / SALMONN-class model) on MSP-Podcast with the full reward R = R_task + α·R_fid + β·R_cf via GRPO, against a label-anchored R_task-only baseline, and evaluate on the held-out acted→naturalistic and cross-corpus splits. If the candidate works, faithfulness@correct (fraction of correctly-classified utterances whose every cited prosodic cue is present-and-agreeing under the independent extractor oracle) increases substantially over the baseline AND, critically, stays high as acoustic shift increases while the baseline's faithfulness@correct decays even where its label accuracy does not — the predicted accuracy-faithfulness decoupling. The named load-bearing variable is R_fid, the measured-prosody cue-faithfulness reward; the mechanism claim is that grounding the reward in the measured signal (not the prediction) is what produces faithful rationales. Negative control: recompute R_fid against a per-utterance permuted (randomized) prosody track — the cue levels no longer correspond to the utterance — and retrain; the prediction is that downstream faithfulness@correct collapses back to the label-anchored baseline (the rationales stop tracking the real signal) even though label accuracy is essentially unchanged, ruling out that the gain came from extra RL compute or label supervision rather than from genuine signal grounding. Positive control: a stripped model trained with only R_task + R_fid (drop the causal R_cf) should recover most of the faithfulness@correct gain on presence, isolating cue-presence grounding as the dominant contributor and the counterfactual term as the causal refinement.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W7083798070","delta":"They supervise rationales by distilling a teacher LLM's text and fitting majority labels, scoring quality by human plausibility; we construct a reward that is a function of the utterance's extractor-measured prosody and optimizes the rationale's cue-attributions to match the signal — a faithfulness-to-evidence objective their plausibility-and-label supervision cannot express."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416432860","delta":"Facial-R1's RL reward verifies the emotion/AU label correctness on the visual modality; we reward whether each verbalized acoustic cue is present in the measured prosody and is causally load-bearing under a counterfactual prosody edit — an evidence-grounding reward with no label-verification analogue and no facial AU counterpart."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7102328481","delta":"The Emotional Rationale Verifier rewards explanation–prediction consistency (a self-referential target a label-correct-but-evidence-detached rationale maximizes); we relocate the reward's correctness locus from the prediction to the independently measured signal, which by construction penalizes exactly the evidence-detached rationales their reward accepts."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4417009235","delta":"MIGR scores explanation–emotion consistency and orders reasoning at the modality granularity; we operate at the intra-acoustic cue granularity and define correctness against measured cue values, producing a faithfulness@correct measurement of cue-level attribution that their modality-level consistency reward never computes."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2604.01711v1","delta":"They inject acoustic confidence/feature evidence as a prompt-side auxiliary input to a prompted (not optimized) LLM under hand-authored rules; we make the acoustic evidence the optimization target via a reward and learn cue-faithful reasoning, rather than supplying evidence the model is free to ignore."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4416432860","what_step_was_missed":"Facial-R1 built the RL-aligned-reasoning machinery for emotion analysis but defined its reward as label/Action-Unit correctness — a verifier of the OUTCOME. For our contribution to already exist it would have needed a construction it does not have: a reward that reads an independently measured continuous-cue track of the input (the prosody extractor's output, with no AU-style discrete label oracle in speech) and scores the verbalized cue-attributions against it at the individual-mention granularity, plus a counterfactual input-edit term that certifies a cited cue is causally load-bearing rather than merely co-present — neither the measured-evidence reward nor the counterfactual-edit certification is constructible from a label/AU reward."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":179,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"Layer 1 does not fire: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict is borderline (no lesson candidate_match: yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat is concurrent-but-not-exact-mechanism overlap (EmotionThinker's reward is prediction/RM-anchored and perception-side, lacking the measured-signal reward, the R_cf term, and faithfulness@correct). In the safe zone the verdict is revise rather than advance because the borderline finding hits a load-bearing structural property — gap_closure_reject_check.entries[1].reject_lessons_evaluated[1].lesson_quoted ('Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work ... collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured') applies directly to concurrent EmotionThinker, and paper_pointed_threat.addressable_via names specific candidate fields (differentiation_from_lit, hook) that must change to dodge it. recipe_application_check is fully applied, so no sub_pattern swap is needed.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf supplies a learning signal that rewards an emotion rationale for being faithful to the utterance's externally measured prosody: across the frontier the reward is the outcome label (openalex:W4416432860) or explanation–prediction consistency (openalex:W7102328481, openalex:W4417009235), so a rationale can name prosodic cues absent from the signal and pay no cost — the missing outcome is a rationale whose cue-attributions are checkable against the acoustics, however that check is produced.","main_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","sub_pattern":"C26 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The dominant failure is the single-component swap: taking the established preference pipeline (reward model → contrastive optimization) and changing exactly one slot — human labels to an AI judge, response-level to step-level granularity — then presenting that swap as the contribution, which reviewers read as incremental because it unlocks no previously-unreachable behavior. A second shape is stopping short of the loop: shipping a preference dataset/benchmark/reward model without demonstrating the downstream optimization that consumes it.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Swapping the preference-label source (human → AI judge, offline → online) without showing the swap unlocks a behavior previously unreachable reads as a one-component substitution and draws novelty rejections.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The reward source is relocated from the prediction/label to the measured-prosody track AND bundled with a behavior the prior reward structurally cannot reach — the R_cf counterfactual-edit term certifies a cited cue is causally load-bearing and the design produces an accuracy-faithfulness decoupling (faithfulness@correct), so this is not a bare source-swap."},{"lesson_quoted":"Stopping at the preference dataset, benchmark, or reward model without demonstrating the downstream optimization it is meant to feed leaves the contribution looking like infrastructure rather than method.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism_steps step 6 consumes R_fid+R_cf inside a GRPO update that changes the policy's generated rationales, so the manufactured signal is consumed by an optimizer, not shipped as a standalone benchmark."},{"lesson_quoted":"Changing only the granularity of an established contrastive objective (response-level → step-level) is judged incremental unless paired with a clearly demonstrated practical unlock.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The mention-level re-granularization is present, but it is paired with a demonstrated unlock (cue-mention credit assignment that localizes the offending attribution, plus the counterfactual causal term), not presented as the contribution by itself."},{"lesson_quoted":"Borrowing a structurally related proxy domain to synthesize preference data, without validating that the proxy's regularities transfer to the target's end-goal metric, invites rigor and generalization concerns.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"No proxy domain is borrowed; the reward is computed on the same SER utterances under test and evaluated on the end-goal faithfulness@correct metric across real shift splits."},{"lesson_quoted":"Combining off-the-shelf components (parameter-efficient adaptation plus self-distillation) for a known problem fails the novelty bar when concurrent work performs the same combination.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"Concurrent EmotionThinker (openalex:W7125567325) combines prosody-aware perception + RL for the same task, but its reward is RM/outcome-anchored not measured-signal-anchored, so the combination differs at the reward locus — borderline only because the concurrency is real and the differentiation must be made explicit (handled under paper_pointed_threat)."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether explanation correctness must be defined relative to the predicted label / the model's own output at all, rather than relative to the independent acoustic evidence — every reasoning-reward leaf (openalex:W4416432860, openalex:W7102328481, openalex:W4417009235) silently inherits from a shared label-anchored-reward ancestor the assumption that a rationale is 'correct' when it agrees with the prediction, leaving unasked whether the correctness target should be the signal instead of the prediction.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is a relocation demonstrated but not adversarially closed, or a novelty-boundary collapse where the 'new' locus turns out to be one a prior paper already used and the work fails to quantify what is genuinely different. A further shape is offering only a demonstration with no mechanistic account of why the new locus carries the signal.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a relocated signal is 'stealthier' or 'harder to remove' without defeating an adaptive defender who searches the same new locus leaves the central claim unverified.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Not a security/adversarial setting; the analogue (an adaptive adversary) is the negative control — recomputing R_fid on a permuted prosody track tests that the gain comes from genuine signal grounding, which is supplied in falsification_prediction."},{"lesson_quoted":"Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work — normalization statistics, activation-similarity losses, semantic concept triggers — collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"EmotionThinker (openalex:W7125567325) is prosody-aware and RL-trained, so a reviewer could read the measured-prosody locus as already-occupied; the candidate must explicitly state and measure that EmotionThinker's reward still anchors on the prediction (RM trustworthiness weight = reasoning-outcome alignment) and never reads an extracted cue track — differentiation must be sharpened (routed to revision)."},{"lesson_quoted":"A defense whose relocation silently depends on a clean reference model or a known anomaly distribution reintroduces precisely the strong assumption the move was supposed to eliminate.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The relocation depends only on an off-the-shelf prosody extractor (openSMILE/Praat) whose output is independent of the SpeechLM under test; no clean reference model or anomaly distribution is assumed."},{"lesson_quoted":"Demonstrating the new locus only on fixed, non-adaptive or outdated baselines while omitting any account of why it works reads as a stacked pipeline of existing components rather than a principled shift.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism_reasoning gives the mechanistic account (the extracted-cue track is the single object serving as reward source, audit locus, and diagnostic oracle; correlational presence alone is insufficient, hence the causal R_cf term), and baselines include the label-anchored current frontier, not outdated ones."},{"lesson_quoted":"Wiring off-the-shelf generators or tools into a new attack setting without a structural reason for the locus change gets judged as engineering integration, not insight.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The structural reason is explicit: a prediction-anchored reward is self-referential and a label-correct-but-evidence-detached rationale maximizes it, so enforcement must move to the signal — this is the insight, not mere tool-wiring."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes how rationale cue-attribution behaves under the acoustic distribution shifts SER is known to suffer (acted vs naturalistic, cross-corpus, speaker variability — arxiv:2601.16240v1): whether label accuracy and explanation faithfulness degrade together or decouple under shift is unmeasured, so there is no diagnostic that isolates 'right answer, wrong reason' from ordinary accuracy loss.","main_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail most often when the instrument isolates the confound only inside an artificial regime and never shows the signal transfers to real deployment, or fall into circularity by validating the diagnostic against the same definition or system population it was built to interrogate. A third shape is the confirmatory benchmark that re-derives an already-documented limitation and surfaces nothing not knowable in advance.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A diagnostic that only re-confirms a shortcut already known in advance, surfacing no previously unmeasurable failure, is read as confirmatory rather than as a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"faithfulness@correct under shift measures whether accuracy and cue-attribution faithfulness decouple — a quantity no current SER metric or plausibility rating produces, so it surfaces a previously-unmeasurable 'right answer, wrong reason' failure rather than re-confirming a known shortcut."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a synthetic-ground-truth instrument only on synthetic data, without demonstrating that the controlled finding transfers to real-world instances, leaves ecological validity unestablished and undermines the central claim.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The diagnostic runs on real corpora (IEMOCAP/MSP-IMPROV → MSP-Podcast, cross-corpus, held-out speakers), not synthetic data, so ecological validity is built in; the only synthetic element (counterfactual resynthesis) feeds the reward, not the diagnostic oracle."},{"lesson_quoted":"Building the instrument around one contested definition of the target property means it cannot independently confirm that the definition is correct, and reviewers flag the resulting circularity.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"Faithfulness is operationalized as cue present-and-agreeing under the extractor's z/τ thresholding — a chosen definition; circularity is avoided because the oracle (extractor) is independent of the evaluand, but τ-sensitivity and the 7-cue inventory's adequacy should be acknowledged so the definition is not taken as uncontested."},{"lesson_quoted":"Resting an unsupervised evaluation on the unverified premise that the systems under test can reliably judge one another stakes the entire method on an assumption that collapses under scrutiny.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Ground truth comes from the external prosody extractor, not from the SpeechLMs judging each other, so there is no peer-judgment premise."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pairing a single-task or small-sample instrument with broad capability claims triggers a scope-mismatch rejection, and assembling retrieval or engineering blocks without an isolating scientific insight reads as application rather than research.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The claim is scoped to cue-attribution faithfulness in SER under acoustic shift and evaluated across multiple corpora/shift axes; the isolating insight (hold accuracy fixed, vary shift, independent oracle) is the research content, not block assembly."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No entry is triggered (no Reject lesson is candidate_match: yes), so the hard floor does not fire. The aggregate is borderline, driven by the C01 audit-and-pivot entry whose lesson 'Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work ... collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured' carries weight against concurrent EmotionThinker (openalex:W7125567325), and secondarily by the C02 entry's contested-definition lesson on the faithfulness operationalization."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf supplies a learning signal that rewards an emotion rationale for being faithful to the utterance's externally measured prosody: across the frontier the reward is the outcome label (openalex:W4416432860) or explanation–prediction consistency (openalex:W7102328481, openalex:W4417009235), so a rationale can name prosodic cues absent from the signal and pay no cost — the missing outcome is a rationale whose cue-attributions are checkable against the acoustics, however that check is produced.","sub_pattern":"C26 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Manufacture a comparative/scalar reward from a non-human source (not human labels and not point-label fitting) and optimize the target with a contrastive/preference objective, re-granularizing the comparison to the locus where credit assignment fails so the gradient points at the responsible step.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"SITE 1 manufactures R_fid as a pure function of the off-the-shelf prosody extractor's output (a non-human, non-label source), re-granularizes it to the individual cue mention so credit lands on the specific unfaithful attribution, and consumes it via group-relative GRPO advantages (a preference/contrastive objective, not point-label fitting) in step 6 — the C26 signature move is performed at the artifact level.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether explanation correctness must be defined relative to the predicted label / the model's own output at all, rather than relative to the independent acoustic evidence — every reasoning-reward leaf (openalex:W4416432860, openalex:W7102328481, openalex:W4417009235) silently inherits from a shared label-anchored-reward ancestor the assumption that a rationale is 'correct' when it agrees with the prediction, leaving unasked whether the correctness target should be the signal instead of the prediction.","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Name the single representational locus all current methods enforce the property at, state the tacit sufficiency/invariance claim bolted to it, then relocate enforcement to an alternative locus the field treated as irrelevant and show the old locus was the wrong place to look — 're-anchor enforcement.'","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"SITE 2 names the prediction locus as the inherited tacit-invariance claim ('the prediction is a sufficient correctness anchor'), relocates reward enforcement to the measured-prosody locus (the extracted cue track the prior rewards treat as irrelevant), and via the companion matched-pair instrument shows a prediction-anchored reward ties pairs the signal-anchored reward separates — the C01 'relocate the enforcement locus' move is instantiated, not just gestured at.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes how rationale cue-attribution behaves under the acoustic distribution shifts SER is known to suffer (acted vs naturalistic, cross-corpus, speaker variability — arxiv:2601.16240v1): whether label accuracy and explanation faithfulness degrade together or decouple under shift is unmeasured, so there is no diagnostic that isolates 'right answer, wrong reason' from ordinary accuracy loss.","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Construct controlled instances in which exactly one named confound is held fixed or independently varied, score them with an oracle independent of the system under test, and report the divergence between apparent and de-confounded performance as the headline result.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"SITE 3 holds the confound (label accuracy) fixed by conditioning only on correctly-classified utterances, independently varies the acoustic-shift axis, scores with an oracle (the prosody extractor) independent of the SpeechLM under test, and reports faithfulness@correct as the de-confounded headline — the C02 confound-isolation signature is performed at the artifact level.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"All three entries instantiate their cited cluster's signature move in core_mechanism — C26's non-human comparative reward consumed by GRPO at mention granularity, C01's prediction→signal enforcement-locus relocation, and C02's accuracy-held-fixed / shift-varied confound isolation with an independent oracle — none collapses to the parent pattern's generic gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["self_supervised_signal_engineering","assumption_audit_and_pivot","controlled_diagnostic_design"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; no 2-way subset of {self_supervised_signal_engineering, assumption_audit_and_pivot, controlled_diagnostic_design} contains it, so no anti-pattern fires."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"openalex:W7125567325","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"EmotionThinker (arXiv 2601.15668, 'Prosody-Aware Reinforcement Learning for Explainable Speech Emotion Reasoning') is a near-title-identical concurrent work: it trains a prosody-aware SpeechLM with GRPO-PTR using a rule-based outcome reward plus a learned reward-model 'reasoning reward' over multi-dimensional criteria, weighted by a trustworthiness weight reflecting reasoning–outcome alignment. The candidate's claim stands or falls on whether its reward locus is genuinely new: EmotionThinker's acoustic grounding lives in a prosody-ENHANCED foundation model (perception side), and its reward still anchors correctness to the prediction (the trustworthiness weight is reasoning-outcome alignment) rather than scoring verbalized cue-attributions against an independently extracted prosody track. The candidate's three load-bearing novelties — (1) a reward that is a pure function of an off-the-shelf extractor's measured cue track at mention granularity, (2) the R_cf counterfactual prosody-edit term certifying a cited cue is causally load-bearing, and (3) the faithfulness@correct accuracy-faithfulness decoupling diagnostic — are all absent from EmotionThinker, so the claim survives but is narrowed: it is no longer 'first prosody-aware RL for explainable SER' but 'first to anchor the reward on the measured signal rather than the prediction, with a counterfactual causal term and a decoupling diagnostic.' If the paper fails to state and measure this delta, a reviewer will fold it into EmotionThinker.","addressable_via":"Add an explicit EmotionThinker (openalex:W7125567325) entry to differentiation_from_lit and sharpen the hook to contrast the measured-signal reward locus + counterfactual term + faithfulness@correct diagnostic against EmotionThinker's prediction/RM-anchored reward and perception-side prosody grounding."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat (openalex:W7125567325, EmotionThinker) + gap_closure_reject_check C01 lesson 'Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work ... collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured.'","fix_direction":"Add a differentiation_from_lit entry for openalex:W7125567325 whose delta states: EmotionThinker grounds prosody on the PERCEPTION side (a prosody-enhanced foundation model) and rewards reasoning via a learned RM whose trustworthiness weight is reasoning–outcome ALIGNMENT (prediction-anchored), with no term reading an externally extracted cue track and no counterfactual prosody-edit term; we re-anchor the reward to the measured signal at cue-mention granularity, add the R_cf causal-edit certification, and report faithfulness@correct — none of which EmotionThinker computes. Quantify the delta where possible (e.g. on the matched-pair set, EmotionThinker's reward ties faithful/unfaithful pairs our R_fid separates)."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"hook","issue":"Same concurrent-work novelty-boundary risk — the current hook says 'every RL treatment anchors its reward to the predicted label or explanation-prediction agreement', which a reviewer aware of EmotionThinker reads as already-contradicted by a prosody-aware concurrent RL paper.","fix_direction":"Tighten the hook so the contrast is the reward LOCUS, not prosody-awareness per se: even the concurrent prosody-aware RL approach (EmotionThinker) keeps the reward anchored to the prediction via an RM trustworthiness weight; we are the first to make the reward a function of the independently measured signal and to certify cited cues are causally load-bearing under a counterfactual edit. Keep falsification_prediction and compute_budget byte-identical."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit[5]","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added an explicit differentiation entry for concurrent EmotionThinker (openalex:W7125567325) stating its prosody grounding is perception-side and its reward is RM/prediction-anchored (trustworthiness = reasoning-outcome alignment), with no extracted-cue-track reward, no counterfactual term, and no faithfulness@correct, versus our measured-signal cue-mention reward + R_cf + decoupling diagnostic."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"hook","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Tightened the hook so the contrast is the reward LOCUS rather than prosody-awareness per se, naming that even the concurrent prosody-aware RL approach keeps the reward anchored to the prediction via an RM trustworthiness weight while we anchor it to the independently measured signal and certify cited cues causally under a counterfactual edit."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Reward the Prosody, Not the Prediction: Cue-Faithful RL for Explainable Speech Emotion Reasoning\n\n**Method.** Cue-Faithful RL (CF-RL)\n\n## Motivation\nModern speech-emotion systems do not just guess an emotion — they also write a short explanation that points to sounds in the voice (\"the pitch rises and the speaking rate speeds up, which signals anger\"). The problem is that nothing during training ever checks whether those named cues are actually in the recording. The leading explainable SER (Speech Emotion Recognition) system, Reasoning Beyond Majority Vote (openalex:W7083798070), learns its explanations by copying a teacher model and matching the majority emotion label, so an explanation can mention a cue that the audio simply does not contain and lose nothing, as long as the final label stays right.\n\nThe methods that do use reinforcement learning (RL) to shape the explanation come from other areas (faces, multimodal) and only reward the explanation for agreeing with the predicted label: Facial-R1 (openalex:W4416432860) rewards matching the emotion/Action-Unit label, and the Emotional Rationale Verifier (openalex:W7102328481) and MIGR (openalex:W4417009235) reward explanation–prediction agreement. Even the closest concurrent speech work, EmotionThinker (openalex:W7125567325), is prosody-aware only in how it hears the audio; its reward still trusts the explanation according to how well it matches the prediction, never reading an independent measurement of the cues.\n\nThe result is a model that can give the right answer for a made-up reason. Worse, under the recording-condition shifts that speech-emotion models are known to suffer — acted versus real speech, a new corpus, unfamiliar speakers (arxiv:2601.16240v1) — the label can stay correct while the explanation quietly drifts away from the real sound, and no current training objective can notice, because it only ever compares the explanation to the label.\n\nWhy now: RL with checkable rewards (DeepSeek-R1, openalex:W4414281281) has just been adopted for explainable emotion reasoning, and off-the-shelf prosody measurement tools (openSMILE/Praat over pitch, energy, duration, voice quality; openalex:W7081550357) are mature enough to act as an independent referee for the seven cues an explanation usually names. The new step is to wire that measured-cue referee into the reward of a critic-free GRPO (Group Relative Policy Optimization) loop — which is now cheap — so that the explanation is trained to name only cues the signal actually contains. When the gap closes, you get explanations whose cited cues are guaranteed present in (and causally responsible for) the audio, plus a new score, faithfulness@correct, that finally separates 'right answer, wrong reason' from ordinary accuracy loss.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n\n1. Take a pretrained speech-language model (for example a Qwen-Audio or SALMONN-class model of around 7 billion parameters) that, given one audio clip (16 kHz mono), outputs an emotion label from the dataset's label set followed by a one-paragraph free-text explanation naming voice cues. Use a fixed instruction asking for the label first, then the explanation, and sample with a non-zero randomness setting so you can later draw several different explanations per clip. This is the model you will train.\n   - _Why_: You need the model's own label-plus-explanation pairs, because the explanation's cue claims are exactly what we want to make honest.\n2. Use a separate, frozen text model (for example Llama-3-8B-Instruct) with a fixed prompt and zero randomness to turn each explanation into a tidy machine-readable list of cue mentions. Each mention records which of the seven measurable cues {pitch mean (F0-mean), pitch range (F0-range), loudness (energy/intensity), speaking-rate, pause-ratio, jitter, shimmer} it names, the claimed direction (high/rising, low/falling, or neutral), and optionally the time span it points to. The prompt includes a synonym list (e.g. 'sped up' maps to speaking-rate:high) and drops any cited cue outside the seven, while counting how often that happens. 【author decision: whether a cited cue outside the seven (e.g. breathiness) is simply ignored or counted as a mild made-up cue — this sets the boundary of what counts as 'faithful'.】 This is a fixed read-out step, not something that learns.\n   - _Why_: Turning free text into discrete cue mentions lets you check each claim separately and later blame the exact cue that was wrong.\n\n### Signal-anchored reward\n*Turn an off-the-shelf prosody measurement into a per-cue faithfulness reward that pays the explanation for naming cues the audio actually contains.*\n\n3. Independently run a standard prosody-measurement tool (openSMILE with the eGeMAPS feature set, or Praat) on the same clip to get one number per cue, normalize each number across that speaker's clips (or across the whole corpus if speaker identity is unknown), and label it high, low, or neutral using a fixed cutoff $\\tau $ (default 0.5): above +0.5 is high, below $- 0.5$ is low, otherwise neutral. Save this {cue $\\to $ high/low/neutral} table per clip. This measurement only looks at the audio and never asks the model under test, so it is an independent referee.\n   - _Why_: An independent measurement of the audio is the honest yardstick: it says what the voice actually did, regardless of what the model claims.\n4. Score each explanation's faithfulness, $R_{fid}:$ for every cited cue, give a point only if the measurement found that cue present (non-neutral) AND its claimed direction matches the measured high/low level; average those points over the cited cues; then subtract a penalty (default weight 0.5) for every cited cue the measurement found to be neutral (i.e. effectively not there). This score reads only the cue list from step step 2 (Use a separate) and the measurement table from step step 3 (Independently run $a standard\\dots )$ — never the predicted label. Because it is a per-cue average, you can see exactly which cited cue lost the points.\n\n*The cue-faithfulness reward $R_{fid}:$ the mention-averaged product of present(cue) and agree(direction, measured level) over the cited mentions M, minus a hallucination penalty $\\lambda _{hall}$ times the count of cited cues whose measured level is neutral. It is a pure function of the rationale text and the extractor output, never of the predicted label.*\n$$ R_{\\mathrm{fid}} = \\frac{1}{|\\mathcal{M}|}\\sum_{j\\in\\mathcal{M}} \\big[\\,\\mathrm{present}(c_j)\\cdot \\mathrm{agree}(d_j, m_{c_j})\\,\\big] \\; - \\; \\lambda_{\\mathrm{hall}}\\,\\big|\\{c : m_c=\\text{neutral},\\ c\\ \\text{cited}\\}\\big| \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This is the missing reward: it pays the explanation for naming cues the signal truly contains and docks it for inventing cues.\n\n### Causal certification\n*Use a one-cue counterfactual audio edit to confirm each cited cue actually drives the prediction, not just co-occurs.*\n\n5. Check causation with a counterfactual edit, $R_{cf}:$ take the single most-emphasized cited cue (the one contributing most to the faithfulness score), and re-synthesize the clip changing ONLY that cue to its opposite level — use PSOLA to edit pitch or rate, gain editing for loudness, time-grid editing for pause length, and a WORLD-style vocoder for voice-quality cues (jitter/shimmer). Confirm the words are unchanged by checking the edited clip's transcript still aligns to the original (redo the edit if not), feed the edited clip back to the model, and give a reward of 1 only if the predicted emotion moves in the direction the explanation said that cue supports. 【author decision: define 'moves in the claimed direction' as either the original emotion's predicted probability dropping past a chosen margin, or the top label changing away from the original — and pick that margin.】\n\n*The counterfactual reward $R_{cf}: 1$ if, after resynthesizing the utterance x into x' by flipping only the top-cited cue c*'s level (lexical content held fixed), the SpeechLM's predicted emotion $\\hat{y}$ shifts in the direction the rationale claimed the cue supports, else 0. It certifies the cited cue is causally load-bearing, not merely present.*\n$$ R_{\\mathrm{cf}} = \\mathbb{1}\\big[\\,\\hat{y}(x') \\ \\text{shifts in the rationale-claimed direction}\\,\\big],\\quad x' = \\mathrm{edit}_{c^*}(x) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A cue being present is not enough — this proves the cited cue actually drives the prediction, not that it just happened to be there.\n\n### Cue-faithful training loop\n*Optimize the combined task + faithfulness + causal reward with critic-free GRPO so the model learns to cite only real, load-bearing cues.*\n\n6. Add the rewards into a total reward = label-correctness reward $+ \\alpha $ times the faithfulness score $+ \\beta $ times the counterfactual reward, with $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ fixed weights, and train with GRPO (Group Relative Policy Optimization): for each clip sample several explanations (default 8) with randomness on, measure how much better each scores than that group's average, and nudge the model toward the better-scoring ones, while a stay-close penalty (KL coefficient 0.04) keeps it near the starting model so it cannot game the reward. Use defaults G=8, learning rate 1e-6 with AdamW, starting $\\alpha =1.0$ and $\\beta =0.5$ (the counterfactual reward fires less often), and tune $\\alpha , \\beta $ on a held-out split so the two new rewards matter as much as label correctness without letting accuracy drop. No separate value model is needed.\n\n*The total reward R: the task-correctness reward $R_{task}$ (label vs annotator-aware label) plus the cue-faithfulness reward $R_{fid}$ weighted by $\\alpha $ plus the counterfactual reward $R_{cf}$ weighted by $\\beta ,$ with $\\alpha , \\beta $ fixed mixing weights.*\n$$ R = R_{\\mathrm{task}} + \\alpha\\,R_{\\mathrm{fid}} + \\beta\\,R_{\\mathrm{cf}} \\tag{3} $$\n\n\n*The group-relative advantage $A_{i}$ for rollout i: its reward $R_{i}$ minus the group $mean \\bar{R}_{q}$ over the G rollouts of utterance q, divided by the group standard deviation $\\sigma _{q}$ (plus a small $\\epsilon ),$ so GRPO updates the policy critic-free toward rollouts whose rationales are more signal-faithful.*\n$$ A_i = \\frac{R_i - \\bar{R}_q}{\\sigma_q + \\varepsilon} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This is the actual training loop that changes the model's habits, steering it toward explanations whose cues are real and causally responsible.\n\n### Audit and decoupling diagnostic\n*Prove the prediction locus is the wrong yardstick and measure 'right answer, wrong reason' under acoustic shift with controls.*\n\n7. Build a matched-pair test set: for clips the model labeled correctly, pair a signal-faithful explanation with a near-identical unfaithful one made by swapping exactly one cited cue to a cue the measurement says is neutral (so the only difference is that one now-wrong attribution). Score both members two ways — once with a reward that only checks agreement with the predicted label, and once with the faithfulness score from step step 4 (Score each $explanation's\\dots )$ — and tabulate the difference. You should see the label-only reward give both members the same high score while the faithfulness score pulls them apart, showing the label-only view is blind to the unfaithful swap.\n   - _Why_: This is the concrete proof that judging against the prediction misses errors that judging against the signal catches.\n8. Measure faithfulness@correct under changing recording conditions: split a corpus by shift (acted to natural speech, a different corpus, unseen speakers), and within each split keep only the clips the model labeled correctly so accuracy is held fixed by design. Then compute the fraction of those clips whose every cited cue is present-and-agreeing in the step-step 3 (Independently run $a standard\\dots )$ measurement, and plot this fraction against how much the conditions shifted. The tell-tale result is this fraction dropping as the shift grows, even though accuracy was held fixed — the 'right answer, wrong reason' effect.\n   - _Why_: By holding accuracy fixed and varying only the shift, you can see 'right answer, wrong reason' on its own, which no overall accuracy number reveals.\n9. Run controls and ablations: train the full model, a label-only baseline, and a version that drops the causal counterfactual reward (keeping only cue-presence), and compare all three on faithfulness@correct, accuracy, and human ratings. For the key negative control, scramble the measurement table per clip so the cue values no longer match the audio, recompute the faithfulness score on that scrambled table, retrain, and then measure faithfulness@correct on the REAL (unscrambled) diagnostic. You should see it fall back to the label-only baseline while accuracy barely changes — proving the gains came from real signal grounding, not just extra training or label information.\n   - _Why_: The scrambled-measurement control proves the gains come from real signal grounding, not just from extra training or label information.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 奖励韵律而非预测：面向可解释语音情感推理的线索忠实强化学习\n\n**方法名称.** Cue-Faithful RL (CF-RL)\n\n## 研究动机\n现在的语音情感系统不只是猜一个情绪，它还会写一小段解释，指向声音里的某些特征（\"音调上升、语速加快，说明是愤怒\"）。问题在于：训练时从来没有人检查这些被点名的线索是否真的出现在录音里。当前领先的可解释 SER (Speech Emotion Recognition，语音情感识别) 系统 Reasoning Beyond Majority Vote (openalex:W7083798070) 通过模仿一个 teacher 模型并对齐多数票标签来学习解释，于是只要最终标签还对，一段提到了录音里根本不存在的线索的解释也不会受到任何惩罚。\n\n那些真正用强化学习 (Reinforcement Learning, RL) 来塑造解释的方法都来自别的领域（人脸、多模态），而且只奖励解释与预测标签一致：Facial-R1 (openalex:W4416432860) 奖励与情绪/Action-Unit 标签匹配，Emotional Rationale Verifier (openalex:W7102328481) 和 MIGR (openalex:W4417009235) 奖励解释与预测之间的一致性。即便是最接近的同期语音工作 EmotionThinker (openalex:W7125567325)，它的韵律感知也只体现在\"如何听音频\"这一感知侧，其奖励依然按解释与预测的吻合程度来给信任权重，从不读取对线索的独立测量。\n\n结果就是一个\"答案对、理由瞎编\"的模型。更糟的是，在语音情感模型已知会遇到的录音条件变化下——表演语音对自然语音、换一个语料库、换不熟悉的说话人 (arxiv:2601.16240v1)——标签可以仍然正确，而解释却悄悄偏离了真实的声音，可现有的任何训练目标都察觉不到，因为它们只把解释和标签作比较。\n\n为何是现在：带可检验奖励的 RL（DeepSeek-R1, openalex:W4414281281）刚被引入可解释情感推理，而现成的韵律测量工具（openSMILE/Praat，对音高、能量、时长、嗓音质量进行测量；openalex:W7081550357）已经成熟到足以充当一个独立裁判，去核对解释通常会点名的那七个线索。新的一步，是把这个\"测得线索\"裁判接入一个无需 critic 的 GRPO (Group Relative Policy Optimization) 训练回路的奖励里——这在今天已经很便宜——从而训练模型只点名信号里确实存在的线索。当这个缺口被补上时，你得到的是\"所引线索保证存在于音频中、并且因果上对预测负责\"的解释，外加一个新指标 faithfulness@correct，它终于能把\"答案对、理由错\"和普通的准确率下降区分开。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景\n\n1. 取一个预训练好的语音-语言模型（例如约 70 亿参数的 Qwen-Audio 或 SALMONN 类模型），它在给定一段音频（16 kHz 单声道）时，先从数据集的标签集合里输出一个情绪标签，再输出一段点名声音线索的自由文本解释。用一个固定指令要求它先给标签、再给解释，并以非零的随机性采样，以便之后能对同一段音频抽取多条不同的解释。这就是你要训练的模型。\n   - _为什么_: 你需要模型自己产出的\"标签+解释\"配对，因为解释里对线索的断言正是我们要让它变诚实的东西。\n2. 用另一个独立、冻结的文本模型（例如 Llama-3-8B-Instruct），配上固定 prompt 和零随机性，把每段解释转成一份整洁的、机器可读的线索 mention 清单。每条 mention 记录它点名了七个可测量线索 {音高均值 (F0-mean)、音高范围 (F0-range)、响度 (energy/intensity)、speaking-rate、pause-ratio、jitter、shimmer} 中的哪一个、声称的方向（high/rising、low/falling 或 neutral）、以及可选地指向哪段时间。prompt 里含一份同义词表（例如\"语速加快\"映射到 speaking-rate:high），并丢弃任何不在这七个之内的被引线索，同时统计这种情况发生的频次。【作者需决定：被引用却不在这七个之内的线索（例如气声 breathiness）究竟是直接忽略，还是计为一种轻度编造的线索——这决定了\"忠实\"所覆盖的边界。】这是一个固定的读取步骤，本身不学习。\n   - _为什么_: 把自由文本变成离散的线索 mention，才能逐条核对每个断言，并在之后把责任精确落到出错的那个线索上。\n\n### 信号锚定奖励\n*把现成的韵律测量变成逐线索的忠实度奖励，奖励解释点名音频里真实存在的线索。*\n\n3. 独立地用一个标准韵律测量工具（带 eGeMAPS 特征集的 openSMILE，或 Praat）在同一段音频上为每个线索测出一个数值，按该说话人的所有音频做归一化（若不知道说话人身份则按整个语料库归一化），再用固定阈值 $\\tau $（默认 0.5）把它判为 high、low 或 neutral：大于 +0.5 为 high，小于 $- 0.5$ 为 low，否则为 neutral。为每段音频保存这份 {线索 $\\to $ high/low/neutral} 表。这个测量只看音频、从不询问被测模型，因此是一个独立裁判。\n   - _为什么_: 对音频的独立测量就是诚实的标尺：不管模型怎么说，它都告诉你声音实际上做了什么。\n4. 给每段解释的忠实度打分 $R_{fid}$：对每个被引用的线索，只有当测量判定该线索存在（非 neutral）且其声称方向与测得的 high/low 一致时才给一分；在被引用的线索上取均值；再为每个被测为 neutral（即基本不存在）的被引线索扣一份惩罚（默认权重 0.5）。这个分数只读取步骤 第2步（用另一个独立） 的线索清单和步骤 第3步（独立地用一个标准韵律测量工具） 的测量表，绝不读预测标签。由于它是逐线索求均值，你能精确看到是哪个被引线索丢了分。\n\n*线索忠实奖励 $R_{fid}$：在被引用的线索 mention 集合 M 上，对 present(线索) 与 agree(方向, 测得等级) 的乘积取均值，再减去 $\\lambda _{hall}$ 乘以被引用却测得为 neutral 的线索个数。它只是 rationale 文本和韵律抽取器输出的函数，与预测标签无关。*\n$$ R_{\\mathrm{fid}} = \\frac{1}{|\\mathcal{M}|}\\sum_{j\\in\\mathcal{M}} \\big[\\,\\mathrm{present}(c_j)\\cdot \\mathrm{agree}(d_j, m_{c_j})\\,\\big] \\; - \\; \\lambda_{\\mathrm{hall}}\\,\\big|\\{c : m_c=\\text{neutral},\\ c\\ \\text{cited}\\}\\big| \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这正是此前缺失的奖励：它奖励解释点名信号里真实存在的线索，并对凭空编造的线索扣分。\n\n### 因果认证\n*用只改一个线索的反事实音频编辑，确认每个被引线索确实驱动预测，而非只是共现。*\n\n5. 用反事实编辑核验因果 $R_{cf}$：取被最强调的那个被引线索（对忠实度得分贡献最大的那个），只改这一个线索使其变为相反的等级来重新合成这段音频——用 PSOLA 改音高或语速，用增益编辑改响度，用时间网格编辑改停顿时长，用 WORLD 类 vocoder 改嗓音质量线索（jitter/shimmer）。通过检查编辑后音频的转写是否仍与原文对齐来确认词汇内容未变（不对则重做编辑），把编辑后的音频再喂给模型，只有当预测情感朝解释所说该线索支持的方向改变时才给奖励 1。【作者需决定：把\"朝所声称方向改变\"定义为原情感的预测概率跌破某个 margin，还是 top 标签变为与原来不同——并设定该 margin。】\n\n*反事实奖励 $R_{cf}$：将语音 x 仅翻转最高权重被引线索 c* 的等级（保持词汇内容不变）重合成为 x' 后，若 SpeechLM 的预测情感 $\\hat{y}$ 朝 rationale 所声称该线索支持的方向改变则取 1，否则取 0。它证明被引线索是因果上承载信息的，而不只是恰好出现。*\n$$ R_{\\mathrm{cf}} = \\mathbb{1}\\big[\\,\\hat{y}(x') \\ \\text{shifts in the rationale-claimed direction}\\,\\big],\\quad x' = \\mathrm{edit}_{c^*}(x) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 线索仅仅\"存在\"还不够——这一步证明被引线索确实驱动了预测，而不只是恰好出现在那里。\n\n### 线索忠实训练回路\n*用无需 critic 的 GRPO 优化\"任务+忠实度+因果\"合成奖励，让模型学会只引用真实且因果负责的线索。*\n\n6. 把奖励合成为：标签正确性奖励 $+ \\alpha $ 乘以忠实度得分 $+ \\beta $ 乘以反事实奖励，其中 $\\alpha $、$\\beta $ 为固定权重，然后用 GRPO (Group Relative Policy Optimization) 训练：对每段音频带随机性地采样若干条解释（默认 8 条），衡量每条比该组平均好多少，再把模型往得分更高的那些方向推，同时用一个\"贴近起点\"的惩罚（KL 系数 0.04）让它别偏离初始模型太远以免钻奖励空子。采用默认值 G=8、AdamW 学习率 1e-6、起始 $\\alpha =1.0$ 与 $\\beta =0.5$（反事实奖励触发较稀疏），并在 held-out 划分上调 $\\alpha $、$\\beta $，使这两个新奖励与标签正确性同等重要又不让准确率下降。不需要单独的 value 模型。\n\n*总奖励 R：任务正确性奖励 $R_{task}$（预测标签对照标注者感知标签）加上权重 $\\alpha $ 的线索忠实奖励 $R_{fid}$，再加上权重 $\\beta $ 的反事实奖励 $R_{cf}$，其中 $\\alpha $、$\\beta $ 为固定混合权重。*\n$$ R = R_{\\mathrm{task}} + \\alpha\\,R_{\\mathrm{fid}} + \\beta\\,R_{\\mathrm{cf}} \\tag{3} $$\n\n\n*rollout i 的组内相对优势 $A_{i}$：其奖励 $R_{i}$ 减去同一句 q 的 G 条 rollout 的组均值 $\\bar{R}_{q}$，再除以组标准差 $\\sigma _{q}$（加一个小量 $\\epsilon $），从而让 GRPO 无需 critic 即可朝更信号忠实的 rationale 更新策略。*\n$$ A_i = \\frac{R_i - \\bar{R}_q}{\\sigma_q + \\varepsilon} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这才是真正改变模型习惯的训练回路，把它引向\"所引线索真实且因果负责\"的解释。\n\n### 审计与解耦诊断\n*证明预测这一锚点是错误的标尺，并在声学 shift 下用对照实验测量\"答案对、理由错\"。*\n\n7. 构建一个 matched-pair 测试集：对模型标对的音频，把一条信号忠实的解释，与一条几乎相同但不忠实的解释配对——后者只把其中一个被引线索换成测量判为 neutral 的线索（于是唯一差别就是这一处现在错误的归因）。对两者各用两种方式打分——一种是只检查与预测标签是否一致的奖励，另一种是步骤 第4步（给每段解释的忠实度打分$\\dots $） 的忠实度得分——并列表对比差异。你应当看到\"只看标签\"的奖励给两者同样的高分，而忠实度得分把它们拉开，从而说明\"只看标签\"的视角对这处不忠实的替换是盲的。\n   - _为什么_: 这是一个具体证据：用预测来评判会漏掉那些用信号来评判才能抓住的错误。\n8. 在变化的录音条件下测量 faithfulness@correct：按 shift 把语料库分层（表演语音到自然语音、换一个语料库、未见说话人），并在每一层里只保留模型标对的音频，从而按设计固定住准确率。然后计算这些音频中\"每个被引线索都在步骤 第3步（独立地用一个标准韵律测量工具） 的测量里存在且方向一致\"的比例，并把这个比例对条件变化的幅度作图。标志性结果是：尽管准确率被固定，这个比例仍随 shift 增大而下降——这就是\"答案对、理由错\"效应。\n   - _为什么_: 固定住准确率、只改变 shift，你就能单独看到\"答案对、理由错\"，而总体准确率数字根本看不出这一点。\n9. 做对照与消融：训练完整模型、一个只用标签的 baseline、以及一个去掉因果反事实奖励（只保留线索是否存在）的版本，在 faithfulness@correct、准确率和人工评分上比较三者。最关键的负对照：把每段音频的测量表打乱，使线索数值不再对应音频，在打乱的表上重新计算忠实度得分并重训，然后在真实（未打乱）的诊断上测量 faithfulness@correct。你应当看到它退回到只用标签的 baseline，而准确率几乎不变——这证明收益来自真实的信号 grounding，而不只是来自额外训练或标签信息。\n   - _为什么_: 打乱测量的对照证明了收益来自真实的信号 grounding，而不是来自额外的训练量或标签信息。\n\n"},{"id":"36","run_dir":"run_prompt36_ebt","index":36,"title":"Energy-Descent Stopping: Per-Token Adaptive Thinking for Energy-Based Transformers","title_zh":"能量下降停止：面向 Energy-Based Transformers 的逐 token 自适应思考","method_name":"Energy-Descent Stopping (EDS)","hook":"Energy-Based Transformers advertise the energy VALUE at the current step as their adequacy signal, yet we predict it is the per-step energy-DECREMENT rate, not the value, that tracks a token's remaining error — so a stopping rule that watches the decrement, run on the model EBT already trained, cuts mean refinement steps by a large margin on easy tokens while spending more on hard out-of-distribution tokens, at matched accuracy.","anchor_pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","anchor_pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","domain_category":"LLM Reasoning & Decoding","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes the amount of test-time computation spent refining a prediction respond to that individual prediction's difficulty: EBT's energy descent, Change-of-Thought's latent recurrence and TRUST's traversal refinement all run a budget that is fixed or only globally scheduled, so the outcome that is missing is per-instance compute that grows on hard/OOD tokens and shrinks on easy ones without retraining.","pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","sub_pattern":"C23 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by liberating EBT's conventionally-fixed descent SCHEDULE (the global step-count hyperparameter) and re-deriving the refinement chain so its per-token length is set by a stopping operator read off the live energy descent itself — a within-chain re-specification of the solver discretization, not a bolted-on halting module, so the pretrained EBT backbone is retargeted without retraining.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf turns the verifier's own energy trajectory into a calibrated, decision-relevant quantity: EBT exposes an energy scalar and even claims it signals adequacy, but no paper establishes whether that scalar (or its descent dynamics) actually predicts remaining error, so the missing outcome is a verification signal that an operator could threshold and trust as a stop/continue criterion rather than a raw unnormalized number.","pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by manufacturing the stop signal from EBT's own internal-state readouts (the energy value E_k, its decrement delta_k, and the descent gradient norm g_k) — diagnosing that the raw energy is uncalibrated across tokens and localizing the usable signal to the decrement's plateau, then fitting a tiny per-token stop predictor on a self-generated remaining-error proxy with an explicit anti-over-thinking stabilizer, the backbone frozen.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"energy-based transformers / inference-time-compute generative models","n_papers":42,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":27},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"openreview","n":2}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":24,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"How Robust Are Energy-Based Models Trained With Equilibrium Propagation?"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Identification of Parameters to Correctly Adapt Energy-Based Hysteresis Models Regarding Rotational Losses"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A DRAM-based Near-Memory Architecture for Accelerated and Energy-Efficient Execution of Transformers"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Hybrid Quantum Vision Transformers for Event Classification in High Energy Physics"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"SlowFormer: Adversarial Attack on Compute and Energy Consumption of Efficient Vision Transformers"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Residual-based attention Physics-informed Neural Networks for spatio-temporal ageing assessment of transformers operated in renewable power plants"}],"more":18},{"year":2025,"n":16,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Energy-Based Transformers are Scalable Learners and Thinkers"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Methodology Based on BERT (Bidirectional Encoder Representations from Transformers) to Improve Solar Irradiance Prediction of Deep Learning Models Trained with Time Series of Spatiotemporal Meteorological Information"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Investigation of Transformer-based models performance on solar irradiance forecast: Empirical results and analysis"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Transformers as Intrinsic Optimizers: Forward Inference through the Energy Principle"},{"source":"openalex","title":"CityTFT: A temporal fusion transformer-based surrogate model for urban building energy modeling"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Unveiling the Potential of Transformer-Based Models for Efficient Time-Series Energy Forecasting"}],"more":10},{"year":2026,"n":2,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"},{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"}],"more":0}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":3,"share":0.071},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":3,"share":0.071},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":3,"share":0.071},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":2,"share":0.048},{"pattern_id":"algebraic_equivalence_unification","pattern_name":"Prove Equivalence to Unify","count":2,"share":0.048},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":2,"share":0.048},{"pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","count":1,"share":0.024},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":1,"share":0.024}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Energy-Based Transformers (semanticscholar:2da9163730998a4368c609972ccff0582518b36b) reframe each prediction as minimizing a learned energy over a context-prediction pair, so 'thinking longer' is operationalized as running more gradient-descent steps on that energy landscape; but in practice the number of refinement steps is a fixed, context-independent hyperparameter applied uniformly to every token, and the energy scalar that is supposed to signal 'is this prediction adequate yet' is never calibrated to a decision-relevant quantity. As a result, easy tokens are over-refined and hard/out-of-distribution tokens are under-refined, and the very scalar the architecture exposes for verification (energy_at_step_k) cannot be turned into a per-token stop decision. The adjacent escape routes do not close this either: 'Transformers as Intrinsic Optimizers' (semanticscholar:ec9ed3515d76766c1cdfe100b90647a9c3f59259) establishes an energy-descent reading of attention but only as a static interpretive lens, never a controllable variable-depth inference loop, and Change-of-Thought (openalex:W4416280663) adds adaptive latent recurrence without any energy/verification scalar to decide when a token's refinement has converged. The failure is therefore that no retrieved method ties the amount of test-time computation spent on a prediction to a learned scalar that measures how far that prediction still is from the model's own consistency criterion.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:2da9163730998a4368c609972ccff0582518b36b","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"EBT trains a single transformer as an energy verifier and generates by gradient-descending the energy over an initial-noise prediction, giving every token its own iterative 'thinking' process with a scalar uncertainty signal. Residue (read from its Method, Sec 2.1-2.2): the descent runs a fixed number of steps set as a global hyperparameter rather than per-token, and although the paper claims the energy scalar can indicate 'whether the prediction is adequate or if further thinking is necessary', it provides no calibration of that scalar and no learned, per-token rule that converts energy trajectory into a stop/continue decision, so compute is not actually allocated by difficulty."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:ec9ed3515d76766c1cdfe100b90647a9c3f59259","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Transformers as Intrinsic Optimizers shows the forward pass of attention can be read as descent on an implicit energy, unifying several mechanistic accounts. Residue: it is a static interpretive equivalence with no trainable knob that lets the number of descent iterations vary at inference, so it explains energy descent but never builds a variable-depth, difficulty-aware inference procedure on top of it."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416280663","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Change-of-Thought adds adaptive latent recurrence to encoder transformers so representations are refined over multiple internal passes without decoding to tokens. Residue: the recurrence is governed by a heuristic/learned halting signal that is not a verification energy, so it cannot estimate how far a current prediction is from a consistency criterion and gives no calibrated scalar a downstream user could threshold or audit."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415331438","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"TRUST performs test-time refinement of SSM traversals guided by an uncertainty estimate to recover accuracy under distribution shift. Residue: the uncertainty signal is a heuristic entropy-style proxy specific to SSM scans, not a unified energy objective whose descent both generates and measures convergence, so refinement and the stop signal are two unrelated quantities rather than one self-consistent scalar."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"energy-based transformers / inference-time-compute generative models","venue":"ICLR 2026","time":"2026","data":["standard language-model pretraining corpora (text)","image denoising / video benchmarks as used by EBT","OOD generalization probes (harder-than-train instances)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher comfortable with energy-based models, gradient-based inference, and transformer pretraining","preference":"both","baseline":"Energy-Based Transformers (EBT) with a fixed per-token number of energy-minimization steps","limitation":"EBT's per-token 'thinking' runs a fixed, context-independent number of energy-descent steps and exposes an uncalibrated energy scalar, so compute cannot be adaptively allocated by per-instance difficulty and the model has no principled stop criterion","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object both legs read from and write to is the per-token energy-descent trajectory of a pretrained EBT: for token t the model runs gradient descent on its learned energy E_theta(context, y), producing a sequence (y_0,...,y_K) with scalars E_k = E_theta(context, y_k), decrement delta_k = E_{k-1} - E_k, and descent gradient norm g_k = ||grad_y E_theta(context, y_k)|| at each step k; all three are model-internal readouts already computed during EBT's own descent (no extra forward pass), and K is the only quantity we make variable. ANCHOR LEG (generative_process_redesign / C23): we treat EBT's fixed global step-count K as a frozen-by-tractability-convenience component and liberate it, re-specifying the chain so each token descends only until a stopping operator S fires, S(k) = 1 iff [delta_k / (E_0 - E_k + eps) < tau_rel] OR [g_k < tau_grad], i.e. the relative per-step progress has plateaued; tau_rel and tau_grad are the load-bearing thresholds, and this is licensed by the task-structural property that EBT energy landscapes are token-heterogeneous (easy tokens reach a sharp basin in a few steps, hard/OOD tokens have flatter, multi-basin landscapes needing more), so a single global K is provably wasteful on the easy mass. SIBLING LEG (self_supervised_signal_engineering / C07): because there is no ground-truth 'optimal K' or 'remaining error' label, we manufacture the supervisory signal that sets tau_rel/tau_grad from the descent's own readouts — at EBT pretraining/validation time we run descent to a large K_max, define a self-generated remaining-error proxy r_k = ||y_k - y_{K_max}|| (distance from the converged prediction, an internally available target), and fit a lightweight per-token logistic stop-predictor p_stop(k) = sigma(w1*log delta_k + w2*log g_k + w3*(k/K_max) + b) by regressing the manufactured 'stop-now-is-safe' event {r_k <= eps_r}; w1..w3,b are the only trained parameters (a 4-parameter head), the EBT backbone is frozen, and we bolt on the C07-style anti-collapse stabilizer: a one-sided over-thinking penalty that anchors the per-token step budget to the validation-set mean so the predictor cannot degenerate to 'never stop' (the runaway-accumulation collapse mode). The two legs interlock as one object: the anchor decides HOW LONG to think by reading the trajectory; the sibling decides WHAT THRESHOLD on that same trajectory is trustworthy, calibrated against the self-generated r_k. The artifact is a drop-in inference procedure for any pretrained EBT that allocates descent steps per token by difficulty with a calibrated, operator-thresholdable stop signal, closing both gaps because compute now tracks the energy landscape's per-token geometry and the energy trajectory has been converted into a decision-relevant quantity rather than a raw unnormalized scalar.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules because both are functions of the SAME descent trajectory: I judged that a separate 'difficulty estimator' module would re-introduce the very decoupling EBT removed (verifier and generator are one model), so the stop decision must be a readout of the descent already happening — evidence: EBT's method section states the energy scalar's convergence is meant to indicate adequacy, so the calibration leg is literally extracting a signal EBT exposes but never validated. (b) Alternatives rejected: (1) reframe_as_solvable_object as an optimal-stopping/MDP over steps (anchor_alternate) — rejected because a learned stopping policy with its own value function is exactly collateral node c1 (ACT/PonderNet's separate ponder head), a flagged regression; (2) an external uncertainty gate (c2) — rejected for the same regression reason. The avoided node is recorded: the schedule is derived FROM the energy descent's own decrement/gradient readouts, NOT from a separately-trained halting head, which is what keeps this a generative_process_redesign of the chain rather than an ACT/PonderNet bolt-on.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: take a pretrained EBT (text and image-denoising variants as in the EBT paper), instrument its descent, fit the 4-parameter stop head on a validation split, and at test time run it on held-out in-distribution data and on a harder/OOD shift, measuring (i) mean refinement steps per token and (ii) downstream accuracy/quality (next-token accuracy or denoising FID) against the fixed-K EBT swept over K. If the candidate works, mean steps decrease sharply on easy in-distribution tokens and increase on hard/OOD tokens while downstream accuracy stays within tolerance of the best fixed-K EBT — i.e. the accuracy-vs-mean-compute frontier moves strictly up-and-left. The load-bearing variable is the per-step energy-decrement rate delta_k = E_{k-1}-E_k: the mechanism claim is that delta_k's plateau (not the energy value E_k) predicts remaining error r_k. Negative control: hold the learned stop policy's MEAN step budget fixed but remove its per-token adaptivity by replacing S with an oracle-budget-matched GLOBAL fixed schedule (same total compute, no delta_k input); the prediction is that downstream accuracy on hard/OOD tokens falls back toward the original fixed-K EBT and the frontier gain collapses, because the same compute is now mis-allocated — this moves the task-outcome metric (accuracy), not delta_k's own value, so it is not tautological. Positive control: a stripped stop rule that thresholds delta_k alone (no g_k, no step index) should recover most of the compute saving at matched accuracy, identifying delta_k as the carrier of the mechanism.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:2da9163730998a4368c609972ccff0582518b36b","delta":"EBT runs a fixed global number of descent steps per token and only asserts (without validating) that the energy value signals adequacy; we construct and validate a per-token stop operator and establish empirically that it is the energy-DECREMENT rate delta_k, not the energy value, that predicts remaining error r_k, yielding difficulty-adaptive compute the EBT inference loop does not produce."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416280663","delta":"Change-of-Thought halts adaptive latent recurrence via a learned signal that is not a verification energy; we drive halting from the verifier's own energy-descent dynamics, so the stop criterion is the same scalar that defines the prediction objective rather than an unrelated halting head."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415331438","delta":"TRUST gates SSM-traversal refinement with a heuristic entropy-style uncertainty specific to scans; we calibrate the stop threshold against a self-generated remaining-error proxy r_k = ||y_k - y_{K_max}|| derived from the EBT's own converged output, making refinement-driving and stopping the same energy quantity instead of two unrelated signals."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:ec9ed3515d76766c1cdfe100b90647a9c3f59259","delta":"Transformers-as-Intrinsic-Optimizers establishes a static energy-descent reading of attention but supplies no trainable knob to vary descent depth per input; we turn descent depth into a per-token decision read off delta_k and g_k, converting the interpretive equivalence into a controllable variable-depth inference procedure."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:2da9163730998a4368c609972ccff0582518b36b","what_step_was_missed":"EBT built the single-model energy verifier whose descent yields a per-token energy trajectory, but it never constructed the calibration step that maps that trajectory to remaining error: specifically, it did not derive a self-generated remaining-error proxy r_k = ||y_k - y_{K_max}|| and regress the trajectory readouts (delta_k, g_k) against it to obtain a per-token stop operator, so its 'energy indicates adequacy' claim stayed an unvalidated assertion with the step count left as a fixed global hyperparameter."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":320,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"No hard floor fired (gap_closure_reject_check is borderline not triggered, anti_pattern matched_pattern_id is null, paper_pointed_threat is a near-competitor not exact-mechanism overlap). Within the safe zone this is revise rather than advance because two findings converge on the same load-bearing weakness: the C23 reject lesson 'failing to beat the strongest fast-sampling alternative dooms the move' is borderline-matched, and paper_pointed_threat.addressable_via names a specific field — the candidate omits the dominant ADAPTIVE accelerator (token-wise pondering, AdaPonderLM/PonderLM-3) from both differentiation_from_lit and the falsification baseline, so the differentiation against the closest competitor is currently implicit. recipe_application_check is applied on both legs, so the fix is tactical field edits, not a sub_pattern swap or regeneration.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes the amount of test-time computation spent refining a prediction respond to that individual prediction's difficulty: EBT's energy descent, Change-of-Thought's latent recurrence and TRUST's traversal refinement all run a budget that is fixed or only globally scheduled, so the outcome that is missing is per-instance compute that grows on hard/OOD tokens and shrinks on easy ones without retraining.","main_pattern":"generative_process_redesign","sub_pattern":"C23 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is treating 'I re-specified component X' as self-evident novelty: a single local swap that neither re-derives the chain nor demonstrates a regime the dominant accelerated alternative cannot reach, or a hidden artifact whose cost cancels the advertised gain, or an absent load-bearing justification leaving the redesign indistinguishable from recombining known parts.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Re-specifying the chain's starting distribution is sound but worthless if a dominant accelerator already reaches one or two steps — failing to beat the strongest fast-sampling alternative dooms the move regardless of its elegance.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The candidate liberates the schedule, not the starting distribution, and its falsification compares against fixed-K EBT swept over K (the in-family strongest accelerator), but it does not yet name token-wise pondering (AdaPonderLM/PonderLM-3) as a competing adaptive accelerator to beat, which a reviewer would demand."},{"lesson_quoted":"Substituting one in-support approximation for another without theoretical depth or a failure-regime analysis reads as a narrow heuristic swap rather than a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism supplies the load-bearing justification (token-heterogeneous energy landscapes make a global K provably wasteful) plus an explicit failure-regime split (easy in-distribution vs hard/OOD), so it is not a bare heuristic swap."},{"lesson_quoted":"A redesign that silently depends on an extra artifact — access to a simulator/dynamics model, or a separately trained auxiliary network — has its claimed efficiency cancelled by the hidden cost once a reviewer surfaces it.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The only added artifact is a 4-parameter logistic head fitted on existing descent readouts with the backbone frozen and no extra forward pass, an explicitly negligible cost rather than a hidden auxiliary network."},{"lesson_quoted":"Collapsing a staged procedure into a single differentiable mapping is technically clean but gets rejected when the novelty is thin against recent methods and the gains are demonstrated only on weak or dated benchmarks.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate does not collapse stages and evaluates on EBT's own text + image-denoising benchmarks plus an OOD shift, not a dated toy benchmark."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf turns the verifier's own energy trajectory into a calibrated, decision-relevant quantity: EBT exposes an energy scalar and even claims it signals adequacy, but no paper establishes whether that scalar (or its descent dynamics) actually predicts remaining error, so the missing outcome is a verification signal that an operator could threshold and trust as a stop/continue criterion rather than a raw unnormalized number.","main_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is a manufactured internal signal whose validity silently rests on an assumption that does not survive deployment (calibration, a stationary/known-finite shift set, or covert target-label use), or recombining well-known components without a single load-bearing mechanistic insight, compounded by thin single-family validation.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A label-free signal whose validity depends on model calibration silently fails on exactly the deep networks known to be poorly calibrated — validate a surrogate where its core assumption is weakest, not where it is convenient.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The signal is the energy-decrement plateau, not a calibrated-probability; its validity is checked directly against the self-generated remaining-error proxy r_k and stress-tested on the OOD shift (where the assumption is weakest), not assumed via calibration."},{"lesson_quoted":"Using target or test-set information during adaptation invites a label-leakage objection that undermines the very source-free, label-free deployment setting the method claims.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"r_k is built at validation time from the model's own converged output y_{K_max}, using no test-set labels at inference, so there is no label leakage into deployment."},{"lesson_quoted":"Reusing standard sequential machinery (chaining each step's posterior as the next prior) without a new stabilizer amplifies noise and looks derivative of prior adaptation work.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate adds an explicit anti-over-thinking stabilizer (one-sided budget anchor to the validation mean), matching the C07 requirement to bolt on a stabilizer against the degenerate collapse mode."},{"lesson_quoted":"Importing a generic continual-learning blending or interpolation technique into a new modality without identifying that modality's specific dynamics lever reads as recombination, not contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The load-bearing dynamics lever is identified specifically: the per-step energy-decrement rate delta_k of the verifier's own descent, a quantity unique to the EBM-as-verifier setting, not a generic blending import."}],"verdict":"clear"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The self_supervised_signal_engineering (C07) leg is clear: it identifies a specific dynamics lever (delta_k), validates where the assumption is weakest (OOD), uses no test labels, and adds a stabilizer. The generative_process_redesign (C23) leg is borderline because of the lesson 'failing to beat the strongest fast-sampling alternative dooms the move' — core_mechanism benchmarks only against fixed-K EBT and does not yet name the dominant ADAPTIVE accelerator (token-wise pondering) as a baseline to beat."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes the amount of test-time computation spent refining a prediction respond to that individual prediction's difficulty...","sub_pattern":"C23 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Reach inside an iterative refinement chain and re-specify one of its conventionally-frozen internal components (terminal prior, per-step distribution, noise/solver discretization, seed, forward kernel, conditioning-injection point), then re-derive the chain around the new choice, licensed by a structural property of the task rather than mere 'we can vary it'.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism's anchor leg re-specifies the noise/solver discretization (the per-token step count K, EBT's frozen global schedule) and re-derives the chain so K is set by an in-chain stopping operator S read off delta_k and g_k, licensed by the task-structural property that EBT energy landscapes are token-heterogeneous — the C23 signature 'liberate the solver-schedule component, re-derive the chain, justify by task structure' is present.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf turns the verifier's own energy trajectory into a calibrated, decision-relevant quantity...","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Treat a trained model's own internal-state readouts (entropy, gradient magnitude/direction, representation moments) as the manufactured supervisory signal, pairing a mechanistic diagnosis that localizes the failure with a surgically confined correction on a minimal lever while the backbone stays frozen, plus an explicit stabilizer against collapse.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism's sibling leg reads internal-state readouts (E_k, delta_k, g_k), diagnoses that the raw energy is uncalibrated and localizes the usable signal to the decrement plateau, fits a 4-parameter head on the minimal lever with the backbone frozen, and bolts on the over-thinking stabilizer — the C07 verbs diagnose-localize, minimize-on-a-tiny-lever, stabilize-against-collapse are all instantiated.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both legs perform their cited cluster's signature move: C23's schedule-liberation-and-rederivation is in the anchor leg, and C07's internal-readout-as-signal-on-a-tiny-frozen-lever-with-stabilizer is in the sibling leg; neither merely enacts the parent pattern's generic gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["generative_process_redesign","self_supervised_signal_engineering"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as a component; the candidate's composition set is {generative_process_redesign, self_supervised_signal_engineering}, which contains no heterogeneous_decomposition, so no anti-pattern matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"openalex:W7133364607","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"AdaPonderLM (Gated Pondering Language Models with Token-Wise Adaptive Depth, 2026-03) is the most specific competitor: it already delivers token-wise adaptive test-time compute for iterative/recurrent transformers via a self-supervised early-exit gate learned during pretraining, which overlaps the candidate's headline outcome (per-token difficulty-adaptive compute without manual per-token tuning). The candidate's claim stands or falls on whether its stop signal is genuinely distinct: AdaPonderLM (and PonderLM-3) follow the ACT/Early-Exit family — a learned gating/halting head that is a separate object from the prediction objective — whereas the candidate's stop is read off the verifier ENERGY whose descent IS the generation, and its load-bearing empirical claim is that the energy-DECREMENT rate delta_k (not a learned exit logit, not the energy value) predicts remaining error. This is a different mechanism, but the candidate as written does not name AdaPonderLM/PonderLM-3 as the adaptive baseline it must beat, leaving the differentiation implicit and the C23 'must beat the dominant accelerator' lesson unaddressed.","addressable_via":"Add AdaPonderLM / PonderLM-3 (the token-wise ACT/early-exit pondering family) to differentiation_from_lit with a substantive delta and name them as the adaptive baseline in the falsification, making explicit that the candidate's stop signal is the verifier's own energy-decrement (coupled to the prediction objective) rather than a separate learned halting head."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat (openalex:W7133364607 AdaPonderLM) + gap_closure_reject_check C23 borderline lesson 'failing to beat the strongest fast-sampling alternative dooms the move'","fix_direction":"Append one differentiation_from_lit entry for openalex:W7133364607 (AdaPonderLM) with a substantive delta: AdaPonderLM learns a SEPARATE token-wise early-exit gate (ACT/Early-Exit family) decoupled from the prediction objective; the candidate instead reads the stop off the verifier's own energy-descent decrement delta_k, the same scalar that defines the prediction, and establishes empirically that delta_k (not a learned exit logit nor the energy value) predicts remaining error r_k — a coupling AdaPonderLM's separate gate does not provide. Do NOT modify falsification_prediction or compute_budget (kill-switch)."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism_steps","issue":"gap_closure_reject_check C23 borderline lesson: must compare against the dominant adaptive accelerator, not only fixed-K EBT","fix_direction":"In the test-time evaluation step (step 7), add token-wise pondering / early-exit (AdaPonderLM-style, the ACT family) as an adaptive baseline alongside the fixed-K EBT sweep, so the accuracy-vs-mean-compute frontier is reported against the strongest ADAPTIVE alternative and not just the un-adaptive one. Do NOT alter the kill-switch falsification_prediction or compute_budget text."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit[4].delta","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Appended a differentiation entry vs AdaPonderLM (openalex:W7133364607) making explicit that our stop is the verifier's own energy-decrement delta_k coupled to the prediction objective, whereas AdaPonderLM uses a separate ACT/Early-Exit gate."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism_steps","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Extended evaluation step 7 to add a token-wise pondering / early-exit (AdaPonderLM, ACT family) controller as an adaptive baseline alongside the fixed-K EBT sweep, so the frontier is reported against the dominant adaptive accelerator."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Energy-Descent Stopping: Per-Token Adaptive Thinking for Energy-Based Transformers\n\n**Method.** Energy-Descent Stopping (EDS)\n\n## Motivation\nEnergy-Based Transformers (EBT, a transformer that turns prediction into minimizing a learned 'energy' score) make a model 'think' about each token by running gradient descent on that energy: more thinking just means more descent steps. The trouble is that EBT uses the same fixed number of steps for every token, and the energy number it reports is never turned into a usable 'am I done yet' signal. So easy tokens get more steps than they need and hard or unusual (out-of-distribution, OOD) tokens get too few — and the very score the model exposes for checking its own work can't be used to decide when to stop. Recent work gets close but stops short: the original EBT paper builds the per-token energy trajectory but leaves the step count fixed and the score uncalibrated; a paper reading attention as energy descent (Transformers as Intrinsic Optimizers) only describes the view and gives no knob to vary depth; and Change-of-Thought adds adaptive internal passes but halts on a signal that isn't a verification energy, so it can't measure how far the prediction still is from being consistent. What makes this solvable now is that the needed ingredient already sits inside every EBT forward pass — a per-step record of the energy, how much it dropped this step, and how steep the descent is — plus a frozen pretrained checkpoint we can measure without retraining. Once the gap closes, any pretrained EBT can spend its test-time compute where difficulty actually is: stop early on easy tokens, refine more on hard ones, recover the accuracy a uniform budget loses, and convert EBT's exposed-but-unchecked energy trajectory into a trustworthy stop/continue signal an operator can threshold.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n\n1. Load a pretrained Energy-Based Transformer (EBT) — a transformer that scores a prediction with a learned energy and improves it by gradient descent on that energy — along with its energy function and the descent settings it came with (optimizer, step size, starting-noise distribution). Freeze every weight so the transformer is never retrained; keep gradients flowing only into the prediction itself (not the weights), because both the generation steps and the signals we read off them need the gradient of the energy with respect to the prediction. The result is a frozen model with one descent loop we can measure.\n   - _Why_: Keeps the method a cheap test-time add-on to an existing model and avoids quietly turning into a separately-trained halting module.\n\n### Trajectory Instrumentation\n*Expose the per-step energy, decrement and gradient-norm readouts that the stop signal is built from, at zero extra forward cost.*\n\n2. Around EBT's existing per-token descent, add a logger that at each step k saves three numbers for the token: the energy value $E_{k}$; how much the energy dropped this step, $delta_{k}$ (the decrement, Eq. 1); and how steep the descent is, the gradient norm $g_{k}$ (Eq. 1) — measured as the size of the raw energy gradient with respect to the prediction, taken before any optimizer-side smoothing or clipping so it reflects only the landscape, not the optimizer settings. All three are already produced by the descent, so logging them costs no extra forward pass. You get, per token, a per-step record of $(E_{k}, delta_{k}, g_{k}).$\n\n*The two per-step trajectory readouts: $\\delta _{k}$ is the energy decrement between consecutive descent steps and $g_{k}$ is the descent gradient norm at step k, both already computed inside EBT's descent.*\n$$ \\delta_k = E_{k-1} - E_k, \\qquad g_k = \\lVert \\nabla_y E_\\theta(\\text{context}, y_k) \\rVert \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: These three numbers are the only raw material the stop signal needs, and they come for free from the descent already running.\n\n### Self-Supervised Stop Calibration\n*Manufacture a label-free remaining-error target and fit a tiny stop head on the decrement plateau with an anti-over-thinking stabilizer.*\n\n3. On a held-out validation set, run each token's descent out to a large depth $K_{max}$ and save the final prediction $y_{K_{max}}$ as the 'converged answer'; pick $K_{max}$ large enough that even hard tokens have clearly flattened out (default: start at four times EBT's usual fixed step count and extend until the per-step energy drop is tiny relative to the first step). Then at every step measure the remaining-error proxy $r_{k} = ||y_{k} -  y_{K_{max}}||$ (how far the current prediction still is from the converged one) and mark the step 'safe to stop' $(z_{k} =$ 1) once $r_{k}$ falls below a tolerance $eps_{r}.$ Set $eps_{r}$ by first deciding how much the final task output is allowed to change for a stop to count as safe (for example, the predicted next token stays the same, or image-denoising quality drops by no more than a chosen margin), then taking the largest distance whose output change stays within that allowance. 【author decision: choose how much final-output change is acceptable for an early stop — this is the accuracy-versus-compute operating point, where a stricter allowance means more steps and higher fidelity and a looser one means fewer steps and more savings.】 You get, per token-step, the trajectory plus $r_{k}$ and the safe-to-stop label $z_{k}.$\n\n*The self-generated remaining-error proxy $r_{k}$ is the distance from the current prediction to the converged prediction at $K_{max}$; the manufactured stop label $z_{k}$ fires when that distance falls under tolerance $\\epsilon _{r}.$*\n$$ r_k = \\lVert y_k - y_{K_{\\max}} \\rVert, \\qquad z_k = \\mathbb{1}\\{ r_k \\le \\varepsilon_r \\} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Without any human label, this builds a self-made target for 'how much error is still left', which is exactly what a stop decision needs to be checked against.\n4. Using the labeled validation data, show the key fact behind the method: the raw energy value $E_{k}$ cannot be compared across different tokens (its scale shifts token to token, so no single energy cutoff means 'done' everywhere), while the relative drop $delta_{k}/(E_{0} -  E_{k})$ reliably levels off right around where each token actually converges. Check this by measuring, on validation, how well each candidate signal (the energy value, the raw drop, the relative drop, the gradient steepness) ranks with the remaining-error proxy $r_{k},$ and confirm the relative-drop plateau together with a floor on gradient steepness track remaining error better than the energy value does. The output is a precise definition of the trustworthy stop signal — the relative-drop plateau plus a gradient-steepness floor — that the next step fits a head to.\n   - _Why_: It locates the trustworthy signal on the decrement's plateau rather than on the uncalibrated raw energy, which is the load-bearing claim of the whole method.\n5. Fit a tiny 4-parameter logistic head that predicts 'safe to stop now', $p_{stop}(k) = \\sigma (w_{1} log delta_{k} + w_{2} log g_{k} + w_{3} (k/K_{max}) +$ b) (Eq. 3), to the safe-to-stop labels $z_{k},$ and add a one-sided penalty (Eq. 4) that pulls the predicted average number of steps toward a target $\\bar{K}$ only when it exceeds it. Set $\\bar{K}$ to the validation average of each token's first safe-stop step, so the target comes from the data; pick the penalty strength $\\lambda $ from a small set {0.01, 0.1, 1.0}, choosing the smallest value that keeps the predicted average within ten percent of $\\bar{K},$ so the penalty only blocks the one failure mode of never stopping and otherwise leaves the fit alone. Only the four parameters $w_{1}, w_{2}, w_{3}, b$ are trained; the transformer stays frozen. The result is the fitted stop head, which can also be read as two thresholds $\\tau _{rel}$ and $\\tau _{grad}.$\n\n*The 4-parameter logistic stop head maps the log-decrement, log-gradient-norm and normalized step index to the probability that stopping now is safe; w1, w2, w3, b are the only trained parameters.*\n$$ p_{\\text{stop}}(k) = \\sigma\\!\\big( w_1 \\log \\delta_k + w_2 \\log g_k + w_3 (k/K_{\\max}) + b \\big) \\tag{3} $$\n\n\n*The head is fit by maximum likelihood on the manufactured labels plus a one-sided over-thinking penalty $\\lambda \\cdot max(0, E[K_{pred}] -  \\bar{K})$ that anchors predicted mean steps to the validation $mean \\bar{K},$ blocking the 'never stop' collapse.*\n$$ \\mathcal{L} = -\\sum_k \\big[ z_k \\log p_{\\text{stop}}(k) + (1-z_k)\\log(1-p_{\\text{stop}}(k)) \\big] + \\lambda \\max\\!\\big(0, \\mathbb{E}[K_{\\text{pred}}] - \\bar{K} \\big) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Four parameters are enough because the signal is already localized, and the penalty blocks the only degenerate failure (running forever).\n\n### Difficulty-Adaptive Inference\n*Replace EBT's fixed step count with a per-token stop operator read off the live descent.*\n\n6. At run time, swap EBT's single fixed step count for the learned stop rule (Eq. 5): for each token, keep descending and stop at the first step where the head says 'safe' $(p_{stop} \\ge $ 0.5) — equivalently, where the relative energy drop has flattened below $\\tau _{rel}$ or the gradient steepness has dropped below $\\tau _{grad}$ — and output the prediction at that step. Use the head directly to decide; the two thresholds $\\tau _{rel}$ and $\\tau _{grad}$ are read off afterward as the head's decision boundary along each axis (with the other input at its typical validation value), for an interpretable form and for the later ablation, and they agree with the head at the 0.5 cutoff by construction. You feed in the fitted head and the frozen model, and get, per token, the chosen number of steps $K_{t}$ and the emitted prediction.\n\n*At inference the stop operator S fires when relative per-step progress has plateaued $(\\delta _{k}$ over total-progress falls below $\\tau _{rel})$ or the gradient norm drops under $\\tau _{grad},$ equivalent to $p_{stop}(k) \\ge $ 0.5.*\n$$ S(k) = \\mathbb{1}\\Big\\{ \\tfrac{\\delta_k}{E_0 - E_k + \\epsilon} < \\tau_{\\text{rel}} \\ \\lor\\ g_k < \\tau_{\\text{grad}} \\Big\\} \\tag{5} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This swaps the one global step count for a per-token decision read straight off the live descent, so compute follows difficulty.\n\n### Frontier Evaluation and Controls\n*Report the accuracy-vs-mean-compute frontier against fixed-K and adaptive baselines, with negative and positive controls isolating the decrement rate.*\n\n7. Run the stop-equipped EBT on the evaluation set and record: the average number of steps per token; a histogram of per-token step counts split into in-distribution versus out-of-distribution (OOD) examples; and downstream quality (next-token accuracy for text, denoising image quality FID for images). Compare against two baselines built on the same frozen model: (i) the plain fixed-step EBT run at several different step counts, to draw its accuracy-versus-average-compute curve; and (ii) a token-wise 'pondering' / early-exit controller from the Adaptive Computation Time (ACT) family — a small learned halting head on each step's hidden state, trained with the standard ponder loss, that exits a token once its accumulated halting probability crosses a level you sweep to draw its own curve. The output is the accuracy-versus-average-compute curve of our stop rule plotted against both baselines.\n   - _Why_: Showing the accuracy-vs-mean-compute curve beats not only the un-adaptive baseline but also the strongest adaptive competitor is what a reviewer will demand.\n8. Run the negative control: build a single global fixed schedule whose total compute equals the learned policy's by setting one step count equal to the rounded average number of steps the learned rule used on the same evaluation set, then run EVERY token for exactly that many steps — no early stopping, no per-token variation — and re-measure accuracy. Since the total compute now matches the learned policy but the per-token allocation is gone, any accuracy drop (expected specifically on the hard / out-of-distribution tokens) must come from how the compute was allocated, not from using less of it. This deliberately measures the task outcome (accuracy), not the decrement's own value, so it is a genuine test rather than a definitional one. The output is the accuracy under this matched-budget global schedule, expected to fall on hard / OOD tokens back toward the plain fixed-step EBT.\n   - _Why_: If accuracy on hard/OOD tokens falls under the same budget, the gain came from per-token allocation, not from just spending more compute — and this tests the task outcome, not a definition.\n9. Run the positive control: make a stripped-down stop rule that looks ONLY at the energy decrement $delta_{k}$ — drop the gradient steepness and the step-index inputs from the head (Eq. 3), leaving a one-knob rule on the relative drop — refit its single threshold on validation the same way, and check whether it recovers most of the compute savings of the full rule at the same downstream accuracy. If this decrement-only rule keeps most of the benefit, it confirms that the energy decrement is the load-bearing quantity behind the mechanism; if not, the gradient-steepness and step-index inputs are doing the real work and that claim weakens. The output is an ablation table comparing the full head, the decrement-only rule, and the fixed-step baseline on the accuracy-versus-average-compute curve.\n   - _Why_: If the decrement alone carries most of the benefit, it confirms $\\delta _{k}$ is the load-bearing quantity behind the mechanism.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 能量下降停止：面向 Energy-Based Transformers 的逐 token 自适应思考\n\n**方法名称.** Energy-Descent Stopping (EDS)\n\n## 研究动机\nEnergy-Based Transformers（EBT，一种把预测转化为最小化一个学到的'能量'分数的 transformer）让模型对每个 token 进行'思考'的方式，就是在该能量上跑梯度下降：思考更久不过就是多跑几步下降。问题在于，EBT 对每个 token 都用同样固定的步数，而它报告的那个能量数值从未被转化成一个可用的'我做完了吗'的信号。于是简单 token 拿到了超过所需的步数，而困难或反常（out-of-distribution，OOD）的 token 步数又太少——而模型本来暴露出来用于检查自身工作的那个分数，却没法用来决定何时停止。近期工作很接近但都止步于此：EBT 原文构建了逐 token 的能量轨迹，却把步数留作固定、把分数留作未校准；一篇把注意力读作能量下降的工作（Transformers as Intrinsic Optimizers）只给出这个视角，却没有可调节深度的旋钮；Change-of-Thought 增加了自适应的内部多次推理，但其停止依据的信号并不是验证能量，因而无法度量预测距离一致还差多远。如今之所以可解，是因为所需要的原料本就藏在每一次 EBT 前向里——每一步的能量记录、本步能量下降了多少、下降有多陡——再加上一个冻结的预训练 checkpoint 可供我们无需重训地度量。一旦填补此缺口，任何预训练的 EBT 都能把测试时算力花在真正困难的地方：对简单 token 提前停止，对困难 token 多做精炼，挽回均匀预算所损失的准确率，并把 EBT 暴露却未经检验的能量轨迹转化为一个算子可设阈值、可信赖的停止/继续信号。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景\n\n1. 加载一个预训练的 Energy-Based Transformer (EBT)——一种用学到的能量给预测打分、并通过在该能量上做梯度下降来改进预测的 transformer——连同它的能量函数与自带的下降设置(优化器、步长、起始噪声分布)。冻结全部权重使该 transformer 永不重训；只让梯度流入预测本身(而非权重),因为生成步骤和我们从中读取的信号都需要能量对预测的梯度。结果是一个带单一可测量下降循环的冻结模型。\n   - _为什么_: 让方法保持为对现有模型的廉价测试时附加件，避免悄悄变成一个单独训练的停止模块。\n\n### 轨迹埋点\n*以零额外前向开销暴露停止信号所依赖的逐步能量、下降量与梯度范数读数。*\n\n2. 在 EBT 已有的逐 token 下降外围加一个记录器,在每一步 k 为该 token 保存三个数:能量值 $E_{k}$;本步能量下降了多少,即下降量 $delta_{k}(decrement,$见 Eq. 1);以及下降有多陡,即梯度范数 $g_{k}(Eq.$ 1)——取能量对预测的原始梯度大小,在任何优化器侧的平滑或裁剪之前度量,使其只反映能量地形而非优化器设置。三者本就由下降产生,因此记录不增加任何额外前向。于是你得到每个 token 逐步的 $(E_{k}, delta_{k}, g_{k})$ 记录。\n\n*两个逐步轨迹读数：$\\delta _{k}$ 是相邻下降步之间的能量下降量，$g_{k}$ 是第 k 步的下降梯度范数，二者在 EBT 下降过程中本就已算出。*\n$$ \\delta_k = E_{k-1} - E_k, \\qquad g_k = \\lVert \\nabla_y E_\\theta(\\text{context}, y_k) \\rVert \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这三个数是停止信号唯一需要的原料，而且它们来自已在运行的下降，是免费的。\n\n### 自监督停止校准\n*制造无标注的剩余误差目标，在下降量平台上拟合极小停止头，并加入反过度思考稳定器。*\n\n3. 在留出的验证集上,把每个 token 的下降跑到一个较大的深度 $K_{max},$并保存最终预测 $y_{K_{max}}$ 作为'收敛答案';$K_{max}$ 取得足够大,使即便困难 token 也已明显趋平(默认:从 EBT 常用固定步数的四倍起步,延伸到每步能量下降相对第一步已很小为止)。然后在每一步度量剩余误差代理 $r_{k} = ||y_{k} -  y_{K_{max}}||($当前预测距收敛预测还差多远),并在 $r_{k}$ 低于容差 $eps_{r}$ 时把该步标记为'可安全停止$'(z_{k} =$ 1)。$eps_{r}$ 的设定方式是:先决定一次安全停止允许最终任务输出改变多少(例如预测的下一个 token 保持不变,或图像去噪质量下降不超过某个余量),再取使输出改变仍在该允许范围内的最大距离。【作者需决定:选定一次提前停止可接受的最终输出改变量——这就是准确率与算力的工作点,更严的允许量意味着更多步数与更高保真,更松则意味着更少步数与更多节省。】于是你得到每个 token 每一步的轨迹,外加 $r_{k}$ 与可安全停止标签 $z_{k}$。\n\n*自生成的剩余误差代理 $r_{k}$ 是当前预测到 $K_{max}$ 处收敛预测的距离；当该距离低于容差 $\\epsilon _{r}$ 时，制造出的停止标签 $z_{k}$ 置 1。*\n$$ r_k = \\lVert y_k - y_{K_{\\max}} \\rVert, \\qquad z_k = \\mathbb{1}\\{ r_k \\le \\varepsilon_r \\} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 无需任何人工标注，这就构建出一个自制的'还剩多少误差'目标，而这正是停止决策需要被校验的对象。\n4. 用带标签的验证数据,展示方法背后的关键事实:原始能量值 $E_{k}$ 在不同 token 之间不可比(其尺度逐 token 漂移,因此没有单一能量阈值能在所有地方都表示'已完成'),而相对下降量 $delta_{k}/(E_{0} -  E_{k})$ 会可靠地在每个 token 真正收敛处附近趋于平台。检验方式是在验证集上度量每个候选信号(能量值、原始下降量、相对下降量、梯度陡度)与剩余误差代理 $r_{k}$ 的排序相关程度,并确认相对下降量平台加上梯度陡度下限比能量值更好地追踪剩余误差。输出是对可信停止信号的精确定义——相对下降量平台加梯度陡度下限——供下一步拟合停止头使用。\n   - _为什么_: 它把可信信号定位在下降量的平台上，而非未校准的原始能量上，这是整个方法的承重论断。\n5. 对'现在可安全停止'拟合一个极小的 4 参数 logistic 头 $p_{stop}(k) = \\sigma (w_{1} log delta_{k} + w_{2} log g_{k} + w_{3} (k/K_{max}) +$ b)(Eq. 3),拟合目标是可安全停止标签 $z_{k},$并加入一个单边惩罚(Eq. 4),仅当预测平均步数超过目标 $\\bar{K}$ 时把它往回拉。把 $\\bar{K}$ 设为每个 token 首个安全停止步在验证集上的平均,使目标来自数据;惩罚强度 $\\lambda $ 从小集合 {0.01, 0.1, 1.0} 中选取,取使预测平均步数保持在 $\\bar{K}$ 的百分之十以内的最小值,这样惩罚只封堵'永不停止'这一个失败模式,其余情况下不干扰拟合。仅训练四个参数 $w_{1}$、$w_{2}$、$w_{3}$、b;transformer 保持冻结。结果是拟合好的停止头,也可读作两个阈值 $\\tau _{rel}$ 与 $\\tau _{grad}$。\n\n*4 参数 logistic 停止头将对数下降量、对数梯度范数与归一化步序映射为现在停止是否安全的概率；w1、w2、w3、b 是仅有的可训练参数。*\n$$ p_{\\text{stop}}(k) = \\sigma\\!\\big( w_1 \\log \\delta_k + w_2 \\log g_k + w_3 (k/K_{\\max}) + b \\big) \\tag{3} $$\n\n\n*停止头通过对制造标签的极大似然加一个单边过度思考惩罚 $\\lambda \\cdot max(0, E[K_{pred}] -  \\bar{K})$ 来拟合，该惩罚将预测平均步数锚定到验证集均值 $\\bar{K}$，阻止'永不停止'的退化。*\n$$ \\mathcal{L} = -\\sum_k \\big[ z_k \\log p_{\\text{stop}}(k) + (1-z_k)\\log(1-p_{\\text{stop}}(k)) \\big] + \\lambda \\max\\!\\big(0, \\mathbb{E}[K_{\\text{pred}}] - \\bar{K} \\big) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 信号已被定位，4 个参数足矣；该惩罚封住了唯一的退化失败（永远跑下去）。\n\n### 难度自适应推理\n*用读自实时下降的逐 token 停止算子替换 EBT 的固定步数。*\n\n6. 运行时,把 EBT 的单一固定步数换成学到的停止规则(Eq. 5):对每个 token 持续下降,在停止头首次判定'安全$'(p_{stop} \\ge $ 0.5)的那一步停止——等价地,即相对能量下降已趋平至低于 $\\tau _{rel},$或梯度陡度已降到低于 $\\tau _{grad}——$并输出该步的预测。直接用停止头做决策;两个阈值 $\\tau _{rel}$ 与 $\\tau _{grad}$ 是事后沿各轴读取的停止头决策边界(另一输入取其验证集典型值),用于可解释形式与后续消融,且在 0.5 截断处它们与停止头按构造一致。你输入拟合好的停止头与冻结模型,得到每个 token 选定的步数 $K_{t}$ 与输出的预测。\n\n*推理时，当相对每步进展趋于平台（$\\delta _{k}$ 除以总进展低于 $\\tau _{rel}$）或梯度范数低于 $\\tau _{grad}$ 时停止算子 S 触发，等价于 $p_{stop}(k) \\ge  0.5$。*\n$$ S(k) = \\mathbb{1}\\Big\\{ \\tfrac{\\delta_k}{E_0 - E_k + \\epsilon} < \\tau_{\\text{rel}} \\ \\lor\\ g_k < \\tau_{\\text{grad}} \\Big\\} \\tag{5} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这把单一的全局步数换成了直接读自实时下降的逐 token 决策，于是算力随难度分配。\n\n### 前沿评测与对照\n*对比固定步与自适应基线报告准确率-平均算力前沿，并用负、正对照隔离下降率。*\n\n7. 在评测集上运行带停止的 EBT,并记录:每个 token 的平均步数;按 in-distribution 与 out-of-distribution (OOD) 划分的逐 token 步数直方图;以及下游质量(文本用 next-token 准确率,图像用去噪质量 FID)。与基于同一冻结模型的两个基线对比:(i) 在多个不同步数下运行的普通固定步 EBT,以画出其准确率-平均算力曲线;(ii) 来自 Adaptive Computation Time (ACT) 家族的逐 token'pondering'/提前退出控制器——在每步隐藏状态上加一个小的学到停止头,用标准 ponder 损失训练,当某 token 的累积停止概率越过你扫描的某个水平时退出,以画出它自己的曲线。输出是我们的停止规则相对两个基线绘制的准确率-平均算力曲线。\n   - _为什么_: 证明准确率-平均算力曲线不仅胜过非自适应基线，也胜过最强的自适应竞争者，这是审稿人会要求的。\n8. 运行负对照:构造一个总算力等于学到策略的单一全局固定调度,做法是把步数设为学到规则在同一评测集上所用平均步数的四舍五入值,然后让每个 token 都恰好跑这么多步——不提前停止、不逐 token 变化——再重新测准确率。由于总算力此时与学到策略相等而逐 token 分配被去除,任何准确率下降(预期专门出现在困难/out-of-distribution token 上)必然来自算力如何分配,而非来自少花了算力。这刻意度量的是任务结果(准确率),而非下降量自身的值,因此是真正的检验而非定义式检验。输出是该匹配预算全局调度下的准确率,预期在困难/OOD token 上回落到接近普通固定步 EBT。\n   - _为什么_: 若在相同预算下困难/OOD token 准确率下降，则增益来自逐 token 分配而非单纯多花算力——而这测的是任务结果，不是定义。\n9. 运行正对照:做一个精简停止规则,只看能量下降量 $delta_{k}——$从停止头(Eq. 3)中去掉梯度陡度与步序输入,只留对相对下降量的单旋钮规则——在验证集上以同样方式重拟合其单一阈值,并检验它能否在相同下游准确率下挽回完整规则大部分的算力节省。若这个仅下降量规则保住了大部分收益,便确认能量下降量是该机制背后的承重量;若不能,则梯度陡度与步序输入才是真正起作用的,该论断随之减弱。输出是一张消融表,在准确率-平均算力曲线上对比完整停止头、仅下降量规则与固定步基线。\n   - _为什么_: 若仅下降量就承载了大部分收益，便确认 $\\delta _{k}$ 是该机制背后的承重量。\n\n"},{"id":"37","run_dir":"run_prompt37_autobid","index":37,"title":"Support-Gated In-Episode Re-Grounding for Generative Auto-Bidding","title_zh":"面向生成式自动出价的支持度门控的回合内重新锚定（Support-Gated In-Episode Re-Grounding）","method_name":"Support-Gated Re-Grounding (SGR)","hook":"Generative auto-bidders (AIGB, Decision-Transformer/RTG, GAS) commit a full bid trajectory under a conditioning return frozen at episode start, so every test-time refinement still re-scores against an offline value model whose reliability at the generated action is never measured. We make the conditioning a quantity the bidder re-derives within the episode, gated by a calibrated self-supervised support score read off the generator's own denoising ensemble, so the plan is re-grounded exactly when, and only as far as, the value model is still trustworthy.","anchor_pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","anchor_pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","domain_category":"Optimization & Search","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces an in-episode signal that quantifies how far the realized market has drifted from the conditioning context the generative bid plan was committed under, so the plan is never re-grounded mid-episode when that drift becomes large — phrased as an outcome (a usable drift-magnitude quantity that triggers re-grounding), not as any particular re-conditioning mechanism.","pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","sub_pattern":"C24 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by promoting the generative bidder's conditioning interface — the return-to-go / value condition inherited as fixed at t=0 — to a free variable re-derived from realized within-episode signal: the backbone diffusion/DT generator is held fixed and only what it conditions on is changed, so each re-grounding step re-conditions on a freshly measured market-and-budget context rather than re-running the whole policy, turning the open-loop plan into a closed-loop one.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf attaches a calibrated measure of whether a generated bid action lies inside or outside the offline trajectory support the generator's return/value estimates were fit on, so test-time guidance and search can refine the plan into regions where the underlying value model is silently unreliable — phrased as the missing safety quantity (calibrated support / reliability of the value estimate at the generated action), not as a named estimator.","pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by manufacturing a label-free support score from the generator's own internal readout — the disagreement (denoising-direction variance) across a small dropout/diffusion ensemble at the generated action, calibrated against held-out value-estimate error — which exposes offline-support coverage as a measurable scalar; a surgically confined gate (it modulates only the re-grounding strength, backbone frozen) plus an anchor-to-prior stabilizer prevents the signal from driving the bidder into a degenerate collapse.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"generative auto-bidding for online advertising (conditional-generative sequential decision-making; transferable to budget-constrained autonomous planning)","n_papers":37,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":22},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"openreview","n":2}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":13,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Generative Auto-bidding via Conditional Diffusion Modeling"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"GAS: Generative Auto-bidding with Post-training Search"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"AIGB: Generative Auto-bidding via Diffusion Modeling"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"AuctionNet: A Novel Benchmark for Decision-Making in Large-Scale Games"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Auto-Bidding and Auctions in Online Advertising: A Survey"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Robust Auto-Bidding Strategies for Online Advertising"}],"more":7},{"year":2025,"n":22,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Generative Auto-Bidding with Value-Guided Explorations"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Optimal Return-to-Go Guided Decision Transformer for Auto-Bidding in Advertisement"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"SEGB: Self-Evolved Generative Bidding with Local Autoregressive Diffusion"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Generative Auto-Bidding in Large-Scale Competitive Auctions via Diffusion Completer-Aligner"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Enhancing Generative Auto-bidding with Offline Reward Evaluation and Policy Search"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"An Adaptable Budget Planner for Enhancing Budget-Constrained Auto-Bidding in Online Advertising"}],"more":16},{"year":2026,"n":2,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"},{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"}],"more":0}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":13,"share":0.351},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":10,"share":0.27},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":7,"share":0.189},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":4,"share":0.108},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":4,"share":0.108},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":3,"share":0.081},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":3,"share":0.081},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":2,"share":0.054}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Across the generative auto-bidding frontier, the policy is a conditional-generative planner (return-to-go-conditioned diffusion or Decision-Transformer) trained on logged offline trajectories: AIGB (semanticscholar:638173d56d91fee1dd3292610ec8c117fac2eab9) and conditional-diffusion bidding (semanticscholar:550b6d25f0f31244685923b7e9ec757879f74df3) generate a full bid trajectory from a fixed conditioning return, GAVE (semanticscholar:f2e5eb6f9360c9a8c04515344c4f1c0a54e17e86) and the Optimal-RTG Decision Transformer (semanticscholar:dc122e5fc4d086c935c28c6d18eebd95e7a5bf54) pick that conditioning return statically before the episode, and GAS (semanticscholar:bef318d9bb151b32c5c6d99da9835c93975649c4) bolts an MCTS search on top of an already-generated plan. The shared failure is that the generated trajectory is committed under a conditioning context fixed at episode start, so when the realized market (competitor bids, win-rate, value-per-impression, remaining budget) drifts within the episode the plan is neither re-grounded against that realized signal nor flagged when it has left the offline data support on which the generator's reward/return estimates were fit; the current machinery cannot produce the quantity that would say 'the conditioning the plan was generated under no longer holds, by this much' because reward/return is point-estimated and the generator carries no calibrated notion of its own support. Expert-Guided Diffusion (openalex:W4416016956) and SEGB (semanticscholar:71fc7fac74ab40e1d2f5fe39cbcc9b17209bb16e) confirm the gap: both add guidance/self-evolution but the guidance signal is itself static or simulator-derived, so the closed-loop, support-aware correction is still missing.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:bef318d9bb151b32c5c6d99da9835c93975649c4","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"GAS adds an MCTS-inspired post-training search over a frozen Decision-Transformer generative bidder, refining the generated action at test time toward higher return. Its search is a bolt-on that re-scores actions under the same point-estimated value model and does NOT propagate any measure of how far the realized market has drifted from the conditioning context, nor any measure of the generator's offline-support coverage, back into the policy — so the search can confidently refine a plan into regions where the value model is itself unreliable, and there is no in-episode signal for when to stop trusting the generated plan."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:638173d56d91fee1dd3292610ec8c117fac2eab9","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"AIGB casts bidding as conditional-diffusion trajectory generation, proving the MLE objective corresponds to a non-Markovian decision problem and generating a whole bid plan from a fixed return condition. It generates open-loop: the diffusion plan is produced once from the episode-start condition and the paper provides no mechanism to re-condition or replan when the realized within-episode market diverges from that condition, and no calibrated estimate of when the plan leaves the offline trajectory manifold."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:f2e5eb6f9360c9a8c04515344c4f1c0a54e17e86","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"GAVE conditions a Decision Transformer on a value-guided return-to-go and adds value-guided exploration to push the bidder beyond logged data. The value guidance is a point estimate fit offline, so it cannot tell whether a guided action sits inside or outside the data support; exploration is therefore unbounded with respect to deployment safety, and the conditioning return is still fixed per episode rather than re-estimated as realized value-per-impression drifts."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:dc122e5fc4d086c935c28c6d18eebd95e7a5bf54","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"The Optimal-RTG Decision Transformer derives the best return-to-go to condition the bidder on, removing the ad-hoc choice of conditioning return. The optimal RTG is computed statically before the episode and never recomputed as remaining budget and market clearing prices realize, so a single mis-set conditioning value at t=0 propagates uncorrected through the whole generated bid trajectory."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"generative auto-bidding for online advertising (conditional-generative sequential decision-making; transferable to budget-constrained autonomous planning)","venue":"ICLR 2026","time":"2026","data":["AuctionNet large-scale ad-auction benchmark","logged offline bidding trajectories (state, action, return-to-go)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with RL / generative-models background and cloud access","preference":"both","baseline":"AIGB / conditional-diffusion generative bidder; Decision-Transformer (RTG-conditioned) bidder; GAS post-training search","limitation":"offline-trained generative bidding plans are effectively open-loop: once the realized market deviates from the conditioning context inside an episode, the generated trajectory is not re-grounded and there is no signal for when the plan has left the offline data support","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The thread is a sequential pipeline (C07 signal -> C24 re-grounding): leg B manufactures the support score that leg A consumes to gate re-grounding. Define the realized-market context c_t at decision step t as the concatenation of (remaining budget fraction b_t, realized cost-per-mille trend p_t over a sliding window of W=20 steps, realized win-rate w_t, and realized value-per-impression v_t), each a running statistic computed from the auction feedback stream — all computed quantities, no oracle. The generative bidder is a frozen return-conditioned diffusion planner (the AIGB/GAS backbone) g_theta(a | s_<=t, R) that maps a conditioning return R to a bid-action trajectory. Leg A (C24): instead of holding R fixed at the episode-start value R_0, we re-derive R_t in-episode as R_t = R_0 + kappa * Pacing(c_t), where Pacing(c_t) is the budget-feasible target return implied by the realized context under the linear budget-pacing identity (target spend = remaining_budget / remaining_steps), and kappa is a named scalar mixing weight (default kappa=1.0) bridging the offline-return unit to the realized-context unit; the only moving part is what g_theta conditions on, the backbone weights are untouched. Leg B (C07): the support score u_t at a candidate generated action a_t is the manufactured supervisory signal — we draw M=8 stochastic forward passes of the denoiser (MC-dropout + diffusion-noise reseeding) and set u_t = 1 - normalized_variance of the predicted denoising direction at a_t; high variance => a_t sits where the offline trajectory manifold is sparse => low support. u_t is calibrated once offline by isotonic-regressing raw variance against held-out absolute value-estimate error, so u_t in [0,1] is a calibrated reliability, not a raw spread. The gate couples the legs: the effective re-grounding is R_t^eff = R_0 + u_t * kappa * Pacing(c_t), so when support is high the plan re-grounds fully toward the realized context, and when support is low (the re-grounded action would leave offline support) re-grounding is damped back toward R_0 — the stabilizer is this anchor-to-R_0 prior, which is the C07 'anchor to source-distribution prior' move preventing the degenerate runaway where re-grounding chases a market region the value model cannot score. The named load-bearing variable is u_t: it is the single quantity carrying the mechanism claim (support-awareness is what makes closed-loop re-grounding safe rather than harmful). Because GAS's post-training search (semanticscholar:bef318d9bb151b32c5c6d99da9835c93975649c4) and GAVE's value-guided exploration (semanticscholar:f2e5eb6f9360c9a8c04515344c4f1c0a54e17e86) both re-score under an un-gated point-estimate value model, the artifact u_t is exactly what they lack; AIGB (semanticscholar:638173d56d91fee1dd3292610ec8c117fac2eab9) generates open-loop with R fixed, so R_t^eff is exactly the closed-loop quantity it does not produce.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share one closed-loop machinery rather than needing separate modules: the support score (leg B) has no standalone deliverable in this problem — its value is precisely that it gates leg A's re-grounding strength, which is why a sequential_pipeline thread (B's scalar feeds A's conditioning) is the honest structure rather than two parallel contributions. (b) Alternatives rejected: (i) re-solving the whole policy each step (full receding-horizon replanning) was rejected because method_lineage flags it as a regression to classical MPC node c1 (model-known replanning) and it discards the frozen-backbone discipline C24 requires; (ii) baking a static CQL-style support penalty at training time was rejected because method_lineage flags it as a regression to node c0 — it is not a per-action test-time calibrated quantity and cannot gate in-episode; instead u_t draws on a source the lineage tree does not occupy: a calibrated test-time generative-ensemble support readout that neither MPC nor offline-RL-penalty occupies.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on AuctionNet, run the frozen generative bidder under three conditions — open-loop fixed-R, un-gated in-episode re-grounding, and support-gated re-grounding (ours) — and measure cumulative advertiser value under the budget constraint, stratified by realized within-episode market-drift severity. If the candidate works, cumulative value increases over BOTH baselines specifically in the high-drift stratum (where open-loop is stale and un-gated re-grounding over-trusts the value model), while budget-violation rate does not rise; in the low-drift stratum all three should be close. The named load-bearing variable is the calibrated support score u_t; the mechanism distinguisher is a negative control that replaces u_t with a random permutation of the same marginal distribution (so re-grounding strength is decoupled from actual offline support): if u_t is the mechanism, this control drives cumulative value in the high-drift stratum back down to the un-gated level (the downstream task-outcome metric returns to baseline), not merely changing u_t's own value. A positive control — gating with u_t alone on a fixed R, no Pacing term — should recover most of the high-drift value gain, constructively identifying support-awareness as the lever.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:bef318d9bb151b32c5c6d99da9835c93975649c4","delta":"GAS refines a frozen generative bidder's action with MCTS-style post-training search that re-scores under a single point-estimate value model; we construct a calibrated per-action support score u_t and make it GATE the strength of conditioning re-grounding, so refinement is damped exactly where their search would confidently push into unreliable-value regions."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:638173d56d91fee1dd3292610ec8c117fac2eab9","delta":"AIGB generates one bid trajectory open-loop from a return condition fixed at episode start; we derive a closed-loop re-grounded conditioning R_t^eff that is recomputed from realized within-episode market-and-budget context, a quantity AIGB never produces."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:f2e5eb6f9360c9a8c04515344c4f1c0a54e17e86","delta":"GAVE's value-guided exploration pushes the bidder beyond logged data using a point-estimate value guide with no support measure; we manufacture a calibrated offline-support reliability from the generator's own denoising-ensemble variance and use it to bound how far re-grounding may move, which their unbounded exploration lacks."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:dc122e5fc4d086c935c28c6d18eebd95e7a5bf54","delta":"The Optimal-RTG Decision Transformer derives the best conditioning return statically before the episode; we treat that return as a time-varying quantity re-derived each step from realized pacing signal, correcting a single mis-set t=0 condition that otherwise propagates uncorrected."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:bef318d9bb151b32c5c6d99da9835c93975649c4","what_step_was_missed":"GAS already reaches inside a frozen generative bidder at test time, but it scores candidate actions with a single point-estimate value model and never constructs a calibrated measure of whether a candidate action lies inside the offline trajectory support; the missing step is the construction of a self-supervised, calibrated per-action support score (denoising-ensemble variance isotonically calibrated against held-out value error) and the coupling of that score to the conditioning so refinement strength is bounded by measured reliability rather than applied uniformly."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":187,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"No hard floor fired: gap_closure_reject_check is borderline (not triggered — no Reject lesson is candidate_match=yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat is an addressable adjacency, not exact-mechanism overlap. recipe_application_check.verdict=applied on both legs, so the candidate is not built from the parent's generic gist. The single borderline (C07's calibration-dependence lesson, 'A label-free signal whose validity depends on model calibration silently fails on exactly the deep networks known to be poorly calibrated') hits a real but non-fatal aspect that the anchor-to-R_0 stabilizer and the high-drift negative control already partially address, so it advances with that concern surfaced for Phase 4 rather than forcing a revise.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces an in-episode signal that quantifies how far the realized market has drifted from the conditioning context the generative bid plan was committed under, so the plan is never re-grounded mid-episode when that drift becomes large — phrased as an outcome (a usable drift-magnitude quantity that triggers re-grounding), not as any particular re-conditioning mechanism.","main_pattern":"generative_process_redesign","sub_pattern":"C24 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail by attaching a different conditioning encoder/control channel to an existing backbone and presenting the swap itself as the contribution without isolating it — the recurring shortcut is the missing ablation that holds backbone/data/compute fixed while toggling only the new interface, so reviewers cannot tell whether the gain comes from the redesigned conditioning pathway or from a borrowed encoder/more data/more compute. A second shape is buying efficiency/controllability while degrading primary output fidelity relative to the strongest incumbent.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Eliminating two inherited bottlenecks at once is only compelling if the combined system clearly beats systems that removed each in isolation; marginal gains plus a regression in primary quality read as recombination, not a new method.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism_steps 9-11 explicitly compare against both the open-loop fixed-R baseline and the un-gated re-grounding (each bottleneck removed in isolation), so the combined system is required to beat each ablation rather than only the original baseline."},{"lesson_quoted":"Swapping the conditioning encoder for a more powerful one is not a new model class if the output quality still trails incumbents and the encoder's advantage is never ablated against the prior encoder under matched conditions.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the candidate adds no new encoder and does not claim a new model class — the backbone g_theta is frozen and only what it conditions on (R_t^eff) changes, matched against the same frozen backbone in all arms."},{"lesson_quoted":"A controllable pipeline assembled from frozen pretrained modules needs an ablation proving that the new control surface — not the off-the-shelf components — drives the gain, or it collapses into prior synthetic-data and adapter work.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"step 10's negative control (permute u_t) and step 11's positive control (u_t-gating alone) directly isolate the new control surface (the support-gated re-grounding) as the driver, not the off-the-shelf diffusion backbone."},{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a unified or foundation-model reframe obligates you to actually demonstrate the unification (multi-domain pretraining plus transfer); per-setting retraining under a single architecture does not substantiate the claim.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"no unified/foundation framing is claimed; the contribution is scoped to closed-loop re-grounding on the auto-bidding setting."},{"lesson_quoted":"Importing a representation from a semantically adjacent domain as the conditioning signal fails when that space is orthogonal to the geometry or dynamics that actually determine the output being synthesized.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the re-grounding signal is the realized market-and-budget context c_t computed from the auction feedback stream of the same task — it is the native dynamics that determine bid outcomes, not an orthogonal borrowed space."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf attaches a calibrated measure of whether a generated bid action lies inside or outside the offline trajectory support the generator's return/value estimates were fit on, so test-time guidance and search can refine the plan into regions where the underlying value model is silently unreliable — phrased as the missing safety quantity (calibrated support / reliability of the value estimate at the generated action), not as a named estimator.","main_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"A manufactured internal signal whose validity silently rests on an assumption that does not survive deployment (model calibration on networks known to be miscalibrated, a stationary/known-finite shift set, or covert use of target/test-set info) degrades exactly when the deployment premise is violated. A co-occurring shape is recombining well-known components (EMA blending, ensemble reweighting, gradient-norm-as-proxy) without one load-bearing mechanistic insight, plus thin single-family validation.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A label-free signal whose validity depends on model calibration silently fails on exactly the deep networks known to be poorly calibrated — validate a surrogate where its core assumption is weakest, not where it is convenient.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"u_t is produced by isotonic calibration of denoising-ensemble variance against held-out value error, so its calibration could drift under heavy market shift; the candidate mitigates this with the anchor-to-R_0 stabilizer and the high-drift-stratum negative control, but the residual concern that u_t's calibration is weakest precisely in extreme drift should be surfaced for Phase 4."},{"lesson_quoted":"Recasting a continuous shift as a discrete, known, finite set of types indexed against a precomputed lookup table collapses the moment an unanticipated or mixed shift arrives.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"u_t is a continuous calibrated scalar from a continuous variance readout, not a discrete shift-type lookup, so it does not assume a finite enumerated shift set."},{"lesson_quoted":"Importing a generic continual-learning blending or interpolation technique into a new modality without identifying that modality's specific dynamics lever reads as recombination, not contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the load-bearing lever is identified specifically — offline-support coverage of the generative bidder read as denoising-direction variance — not a generic EMA/blending import."},{"lesson_quoted":"Reusing standard sequential machinery (chaining each step's posterior as the next prior) without a new stabilizer amplifies noise and looks derivative of prior adaptation work.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the candidate adds an explicit new stabilizer (the u_t-weighted anchor to R_0) precisely to prevent runaway re-grounding, which is the C07-prescribed collapse guard."},{"lesson_quoted":"A multi-branch or ensemble reweighting mechanism that overlaps with standard multi-task/mixture-of-experts ensembling must explicitly beat both the single-model and the standard-ensemble baselines, or the gain is credited to prior art.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the ensemble is used only to read variance for the support score, not as a prediction-reweighting MoE; the un-gated re-grounding arm (which also uses the ensemble) is a baseline u_t must beat, isolating the gating from the ensembling."},{"lesson_quoted":"Using target or test-set information during adaptation invites a label-leakage objection that undermines the very source-free, label-free deployment setting the method claims.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"u_t is computed entirely from the generator's own internal readouts and realized in-episode feedback already observable to a deployed bidder; the isotonic map is fit on a held-out offline split, with no test-episode label access."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The self_supervised_signal_engineering (C07) gap drives the aggregate to borderline via the calibration-dependence lesson ('A label-free signal whose validity depends on model calibration silently fails on exactly the deep networks known to be poorly calibrated'): u_t's isotonic calibration could be weakest in extreme drift. The generative_process_redesign (C24) gap is fully clear because every recombination/missing-ablation lesson is answered by the held-fixed-backbone discipline and the negative/positive controls in core_mechanism_steps 9-11."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces an in-episode signal that quantifies how far the realized market has drifted from the conditioning context the generative bid plan was committed under, so the plan is never re-grounded mid-episode when that drift becomes large — phrased as an outcome (a usable drift-magnitude quantity that triggers re-grounding), not as any particular re-conditioning mechanism.","sub_pattern":"C24 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Hold an iterative-refinement generative backbone fixed and treat its conditioning interface or operating representation space as the free variable — change what the procedure conditions on (e.g. a measured-response objective or pinned states) while keeping the backbone, objective, data, and compute fixed so the new conditioning pathway is the only moving part.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism leg A performs exactly this: the diffusion/DT backbone g_theta is frozen and the only change is replacing the t=0-fixed conditioning return R_0 with the in-episode re-derived R_t^eff = R_0 + u_t*kappa*Pacing(c_t); step 6 generates the next bid by re-running the frozen g_theta on the new condition, i.e. the conditioning interface is the single moving part — the cluster's signature move, not the parent's generic gist.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf attaches a calibrated measure of whether a generated bid action lies inside or outside the offline trajectory support the generator's return/value estimates were fit on, so test-time guidance and search can refine the plan into regions where the underlying value model is silently unreliable — phrased as the missing safety quantity (calibrated support / reliability of the value estimate at the generated action), not as a named estimator.","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Treat the model's own internal-state readouts as the manufactured supervisory signal; pair a mechanistic diagnosis that localizes the failure (here: sparse offline-support coverage) with a surgically confined correction on a minimal lever while the backbone stays frozen, and bolt on an explicit stabilizer because a label-free internal signal invites a degenerate solution.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism leg B performs this: the support score u_t is read off the generator's own M=8-pass denoising-direction variance (internal readout), the correction is confined to a minimal lever (u_t modulates only the re-grounding strength, backbone frozen), and the anchor-to-R_0 prior is the explicit collapse stabilizer — the diagnose-localize / minimize-on-tiny-lever / stabilize-against-collapse verbs are all present, not generate-pseudo-labels-and-filter.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries instantiate their cluster's signature move: C24's frozen-backbone single-moving-interface re-conditioning (leg A) and C07's internal-readout-plus-tiny-lever-plus-stabilizer support signal (leg B). Neither reduces to the parent pattern's generic gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["generative_process_redesign","self_supervised_signal_engineering"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; the candidate's composition_set is {generative_process_redesign, self_supervised_signal_engineering}, which contains no heterogeneous_decomposition, so no anti-pattern matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:bef318d9bb151b32c5c6d99da9835c93975649c4","threat_source":"lit_table","subsumption_argument":"GAS (Generative Auto-bidding with Post-training Search) is the most specific competitor: it already reaches inside a frozen generative bidder at test time and refines its actions via MCTS-style search, so a reviewer will ask whether support-gated re-grounding is just GAS with a tweaked scoring function. The candidate stands or falls on whether the calibrated per-action support score u_t (denoising-ensemble variance isotonically calibrated against held-out value error) is a genuinely new artifact GAS lacks: GAS re-scores every candidate under one point-estimate value model with no measure of offline-support coverage, so it cannot distinguish a high-value action that sits inside the data manifold from one that sits outside it. The candidate's claim survives only if the high-drift-stratum gain disappears under the u_t-permutation negative control (showing u_t, not the search machinery, carries the effect); if it persists under permutation, GAS subsumes the candidate.","addressable_via":"Not a sub_pattern/field swap — the differentiation is already carried by differentiation_from_lit[0] and the u_t-permutation negative control in falsification_prediction; the threat is addressable by surfacing it as the headline reviewer concern in Phase 4, not by revising a candidate field."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Support-Gated In-Episode Re-Grounding for Generative Auto-Bidding\n\n**Method.** Support-Gated Re-Grounding (SGR)\n\n## Motivation\nModern automated ad-bidding systems increasingly use generative models. Instead of an old-style reinforcement-learning agent that reacts step by step, a generative bidder (for example AIGB, Generative Auto-bidding via Diffusion; or a Decision Transformer conditioned on a target return) writes out a whole bidding plan for the campaign at once, based on a 'target return' chosen at the very start. The problem is that the market does not stand still during the campaign: competitors' bids move, how often you win moves, how much each impression is worth moves, and your remaining budget moves. Because the plan was written under the conditions at the start, it goes stale, and nothing re-checks it against what is actually happening. Even systems that do correct the plan at run time, like GAS (Generative Auto-bidding with Post-training Search), re-score actions using one offline value model without ever asking whether that model can be trusted for the action being considered — so the correction can confidently push the plan into situations the model has never really seen.\n\nThis is timely now because the generative-bidding approach only matured in the past year, and a realistic large-scale auction benchmark, AuctionNet, now lets us measure exactly the situations where the market drifts the most. We propose Support-Gated Re-Grounding (SGR). First, we let the bidder re-derive its 'target return' as the campaign runs, from the actual measured market and budget state, instead of leaving it fixed at the start. Second — and this is the key safety idea — we read a 'support score' $u_{t}$ from the generative model itself: we run the model a handful of times with small randomness and look at how much its denoising direction disagrees; high disagreement means the action sits in a region the model saw little of in its training data, so it is less trustworthy. We use that score to decide how far the plan is allowed to be re-grounded: when the model is on familiar ground, we re-ground fully; when it is not, we hold back toward the original plan. The payoff is a bidder that adapts during the campaign but only as far as its own value estimates can be trusted — which directly subsumes run-time search like GAS and gives exploration methods a safety bound they currently lack. The same mechanism applies to any budget-constrained generative planner that must adapt online, including robotics and autonomous-planning settings.\n\n## Method\n### Frozen generative backbone\n*Reuse a pretrained return-conditioned bidder unchanged so every gain is attributable to re-grounding, not retraining.*\n\n1. Take a pretrained generative bidder that writes a bid plan conditioned on a target return — either a diffusion model (which conditions on a return value fed in at each sampling step) or a Decision Transformer (DT, a sequence model conditioned on a remaining-target-return token). Freeze every weight: do not retrain anything. Save it together with its sampling procedure so you can call the exact same model again at every step of the campaign, each time with a different target-return value and a fresh random seed. The only thing the method ever changes is the target return the model is conditioned on.\n   - _Why_: Keeping the model fixed means any later improvement must come from the re-grounding, not from a bigger or better-trained model.\n\n### In-episode re-grounding\n*Re-derive the conditioning return each step from realized market-and-budget signal, turning an open-loop plan closed-loop.*\n\n2. At every step, build a small fixed-length 'live picture' vector $c_{t}$ of the market and budget from the auction feedback: (1) the fraction of budget still remaining; (2) the trend in cost-per-thousand-impressions (cost-per-mille, CPM) over the last W=20 steps, computed as the slope of a straight line fit to those 20 values; (3) the win-rate (impressions won divided by auctions entered) over that window; and (4) the value-per-impression (realized conversion value divided by impressions won) over that window. Standardize each of the four numbers using the average and spread measured once on the historical logs, so the picture is on a comparable scale across different campaigns. Everything comes from observable feedback — nothing requires a hidden oracle.\n   - _Why_: This is the realized signal the original fixed plan never looked at, so it is what tells us the plan has gone stale.\n3. Turn the live picture into a budget-feasible target return using simple pacing arithmetic: divide the budget still remaining by the number of steps still remaining to get a per-step target spend, then convert that spend into the units the model's target-return input expects. Build the converter once, ahead of time, as a monotone curve (fit with isotonic regression, or a simple straight-line fit if the historical relationship looks linear) that maps 'target spend' to 'target return' using the historical logs; at run time you just read off this curve. The result is one number saying which way the target return should move to keep spending on track.\n\n*The budget-feasible target return implied by the realized context: $\\phi $ maps the per-step target spend (remaining budget fraction $b_{t}$ times total budget B, divided by remaining steps) into the return units the generator conditions on.*\n$$ \\mathrm{Pacing}(c_t) = \\phi\\!\\left(\\frac{b_t\\,B}{T - t}\\right) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: It says which direction the target return should move to keep spending on track given what is actually happening.\n4. Set the new target return to the original starting target return plus the support score times the live budget-feasible target return (the support score scales the correction; a fixed mixing weight $\\kappa ,$ default 1.0, bridges the units), as the equation states. Then re-run the frozen model conditioned on this new target return to generate the bid you actually submit — this is a fresh generation, not a re-scoring of the provisional action. When the support score is high the plan moves fully toward the live target; when it is low the plan is pulled back toward the original. The same score that measures trust also limits the correction, so the bidder adapts boldly on familiar ground and cautiously on unfamiliar ground — and because the bid actually changes, so do the spend and the impressions won.\n\n*The effective in-episode conditioning return: the episode-start return $R_{0}$ plus a support-gated correction toward the budget-feasible target return, where the gate $u_{t}$ in [0,1] and $\\kappa $ is the unit-bridging mixing weight (default 1.0).*\n$$ R_t^{\\mathrm{eff}} = R_0 + u_t\\,\\kappa\\,\\mathrm{Pacing}(c_t) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The same score that measures trust also limits the correction, so the bidder adapts boldly on familiar ground and cautiously on unfamiliar ground — adapting changes the actual bid, spend, and impressions won.\n\n### Self-supervised support gate\n*Read a calibrated support score off the generator's own ensemble and use it to bound how far re-grounding may move.*\n\n5. Read a 'support score' between 0 and 1 off the model itself. First make a provisional bid by sampling the frozen model under the original starting target return. At that provisional action, run the model M=8 times with small randomness each time — keep dropout (random unit drop-out, a built-in noise source) switched on, and re-seed the diffusion noise on each run. From each run read the model's predicted denoising direction (the direction it would nudge the sample; for a Decision Transformer (DT), the predicted change in the next action). Measure how much these M directions disagree (their variance), and divide by a fixed reference disagreement measured once on the historical logs, so the number is unit-free. Take one-minus-that (clipped at zero) as a raw support value. Finally pass it through a calibration curve, fit once offline so that 'higher raw support' lines up with 'smaller error between the model's predicted return and the actually-realized return on held-out logs', giving the final support score. Lots of disagreement means the model saw little data there, so the score is low. Use M=8 by default.\n\n*The calibrated support score: one minus the normalized variance of the M denoising directions at the candidate action, passed through an isotonic calibration map fit offline against held-out value-estimate error; high variance means low support.*\n$$ u_t = \\mathrm{calib}\\!\\left(1 - \\frac{\\mathrm{Var}_{m=1}^{M}\\,\\hat{d}_m(a_t)}{Z}\\right) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Where the model's own samples disagree is where it saw little training data, so its value estimate there is least trustworthy — $u_{t}$ makes that measurable.\n\n### Closed-loop rollout and controls\n*Run the loop across the episode and instrument the negative/positive controls that attribute the gain to the support score.*\n\n6. Run the step-2-to-step-5 loop every step (a faster every-5-steps variant is reported on the side) across each campaign, and compare five versions: (1) the fixed original plan; (2) always-re-ground, where the support score is forced to its maximum so there is no gating; (3) the full support-gated method; (4) a negative control that scrambles the support-score sequence into a random order (same set of values, wrong moments) so the gate no longer tracks real support; and (5) a positive control that applies only the support gate on a fixed target return, dropping the pacing term. Measure, for each version, the total advertiser value earned within budget and how often the budget was overrun. Sort campaigns into low/medium/high market-drift groups — drift measured as the average distance between the live picture and its start-of-campaign value — and report results within each group. The scrambled control checks that it is the support score itself, not the surrounding machinery, that makes re-grounding safe.\n   - _Why_: The $scrambled-u_{t}$ control checks that the support score, not the machinery around it, is what makes re-grounding safe.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 面向生成式自动出价的支持度门控的回合内重新锚定（Support-Gated In-Episode Re-Grounding）\n\n**方法名称.** Support-Gated Re-Grounding (SGR)\n\n## 研究动机\n现代的自动广告出价系统越来越多地使用生成式模型。与一步一步反应的传统强化学习智能体不同，生成式出价器（例如 AIGB，即基于扩散的生成式自动出价；或以目标回报为条件的 Decision Transformer）会一次性写出整个广告活动的出价计划，而这个计划依赖于在最开始时选定的一个“目标回报”。问题在于，广告活动进行中市场并不会静止：对手的出价在变、你的赢得率在变、每次曝光的价值在变、你的剩余预算也在变。由于计划是按照起始时的条件写出的，它会变得过时，而且没有任何机制根据真实发生的情况去重新校验它。即便是会在运行时修正计划的系统，比如 GAS（带后训练搜索的生成式自动出价），也是用同一个离线 value 模型给动作重新打分，却从不追问：对当前考虑的这个动作，这个模型是否可信——于是修正可能很“自信”地把计划推入模型几乎没见过的情形。\n\n现在做这件事正当其时：生成式出价方法在过去一年才趋于成熟，而一个真实的大规模拍卖基准 AuctionNet 让我们恰好可以测量市场漂移最严重的那些情形。我们提出 Support-Gated Re-Grounding（SGR，支持度门控的重新锚定）。第一，我们让出价器在活动进行中、根据真实测得的市场与预算状态，重新推导它的“目标回报”，而不是把它固定在起始时刻。第二——这是关键的安全设计——我们从生成模型自身读出一个“支持度分数$”u_{t}$：用少量随机性把模型跑若干次，看它的去噪方向有多大分歧；分歧大意味着该动作处于模型训练数据中很少覆盖的区域，因此更不可信。我们用这个分数决定计划被允许重新锚定的幅度：当模型处于熟悉区域时就充分重新锚定；当它不熟悉时就向原计划收回。其收益是：出价器在活动进行中自适应，但只在它自身的 value 估计可信的范围内自适应——这直接把像 GAS 那样的运行时搜索纳为特例，也给探索类方法补上了它们当前缺乏的安全边界。同样的机制适用于任何需要在线自适应的预算受限生成式规划器，包括机器人与自主规划场景。\n\n## 方法\n### 冻结的生成式骨干\n*原样复用预训练的以回报为条件的出价器，使任何提升都归因于重新锚定而非重新训练。*\n\n1. 取一个预训练好的、以目标回报为条件来写出出价计划的生成式出价器——它可以是扩散模型（diffusion，在每一步采样时输入一个回报值作为条件），也可以是 Decision Transformer（决策变换器，DT，一个以剩余目标回报 token 为条件的序列模型）。冻结全部权重：不重新训练任何东西。把它连同它的采样过程一起保存，使得你能在广告活动的每一步用完全相同的模型再次调用它，每次给一个不同的目标回报值和一个全新的随机种子。整个方法唯一改变的，就是模型所条件化的那个目标回报。\n   - _为什么_: 保持模型固定，意味着之后的任何提升只能来自重新锚定，而不是更大或训练更好的模型。\n\n### 回合内重新锚定\n*每步根据实测的市场与预算信号重新推导条件回报，把开环计划变为闭环。*\n\n2. 在每一步，从拍卖反馈中构建一个长度固定的市场与预算“实时画像”向量 $c_{t}$：(1) 仍然剩余的预算比例；(2) 最近 W=20 步内每千次曝光成本（cost-per-mille，CPM）的趋势，用对这 20 个值拟合一条直线得到的斜率来表示；(3) 该窗口内的赢得率（赢得的曝光数除以参与的拍卖数）；(4) 该窗口内的每次曝光价值（实测转化价值除以赢得的曝光数）。用历史日志上一次性测得的均值与离散程度，对这四个数各自做标准化，使得这幅画像在不同广告活动间处于可比的量纲上。所有输入都来自可观测的反馈——不需要任何隐藏的 oracle（先知信息）。\n   - _为什么_: 这正是最初的固定计划从未看过的实测信号，因此它能告诉我们计划已经过时。\n3. 用简单的节奏（pacing）算术，把实时画像转成一个预算可行的目标回报：把仍然剩余的预算除以仍然剩余的步数，得到每一步的目标花费，再把这个花费换算成模型“目标回报”输入所期望的量纲。这个换算器只需事先一次性构建好——它是一条单调曲线（用保序回归（isotonic regression）拟合；如果历史关系看起来是线性的，用一条简单直线拟合也可以），它依据历史日志把“目标花费”映射到“目标回报”；运行时只需在这条曲线上读取即可。结果是一个数，指出为了让花费保持在正轨上，目标回报应朝哪个方向移动。\n\n*由实测上下文推出的预算可行目标回报：$\\phi $ 将每步目标花费（剩余预算比例 $b_{t}$ 乘以总预算 B，再除以剩余步数）映射到生成器所条件化的回报量纲上。*\n$$ \\mathrm{Pacing}(c_t) = \\phi\\!\\left(\\frac{b_t\\,B}{T - t}\\right) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 它指出：在真实情况下，为了让花费保持在正轨上，目标回报应朝哪个方向移动。\n4. 把新的目标回报设为：原始起始目标回报，加上支持度分数乘以实时的预算可行目标回报（支持度分数缩放这个修正项；一个固定的混合权重 $\\kappa $，默认 1.0，用来统一量纲），正如公式所述。然后用冻结的模型在这个新的目标回报下重新生成你真正提交的出价——这是一次全新的生成，而不是对临时动作的重新打分。当支持度分数高时，计划充分朝实时目标移动；当它低时，计划被拉回原始目标。同一个衡量可信度的分数也限制了修正幅度，于是出价器在熟悉区域大胆自适应、在陌生区域谨慎行事——而且由于出价确实改变了，花费与赢得的曝光也随之改变。\n\n*回合内的有效条件回报：在回合起始回报 $R_{0}$ 之上，叠加一个受支持度门控的、朝向预算可行目标回报的修正项；门控值 $u_{t}$ 落在 [0,1]，$\\kappa $ 是用于统一量纲的混合权重（默认 1.0）。*\n$$ R_t^{\\mathrm{eff}} = R_0 + u_t\\,\\kappa\\,\\mathrm{Pacing}(c_t) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 同一个衡量可信度的分数也限制了修正幅度，于是出价器在熟悉区域大胆自适应、在陌生区域谨慎行事——自适应会改变真实出价、花费与赢得的曝光。\n\n### 自监督支持度门控\n*从生成器自身的集成读出校准后的支持度分数，并用它限制重新锚定可移动的幅度。*\n\n5. 从模型自身读出一个介于 0 到 1 之间的“支持度分数”。首先，在原始起始目标回报下用冻结的模型采样，得到一个临时出价。在这个临时动作处，把模型带少量随机性地跑 M=8 次——每次都开启 dropout（随机丢弃单元，一种内建的噪声来源），并对扩散噪声重新设种子。从每次运行中读取模型预测的去噪方向（它会把样本往哪个方向微调；对 Decision Transformer（决策变换器，DT）而言，即预测的下一个动作的变化量）。测量这 M 个方向之间的分歧（即方差），再除以一个在历史日志上一次性测得的固定参考分歧值，使该数无量纲。取 1 减去它（在 0 处截断）作为原始支持度。最后让它通过一条校准曲线——该曲线离线拟合一次，使“原始支持度越高”与“模型预测回报和留出日志上实际实现回报之间的误差越小”相对应——得到最终的支持度分数。分歧很大意味着模型在那里见过的数据很少，因此分数低。默认取 M=8。\n\n*校准后的支持度分数：在候选动作处对 M 个去噪方向取归一化方差，用 1 减去该方差，再经过离线针对留出集 value 估计误差拟合的保序回归校准映射；方差越大表示支持度越低。*\n$$ u_t = \\mathrm{calib}\\!\\left(1 - \\frac{\\mathrm{Var}_{m=1}^{M}\\,\\hat{d}_m(a_t)}{Z}\\right) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 模型自身样本分歧大的地方，正是它训练数据稀少之处，因此那里的 value 估计最不可信$——u_{t}$ 把这一点变得可测量。\n\n### 闭环回放与对照\n*在整回合运行该循环，并设置把增益归因于支持度分数的负/正对照。*\n\n6. 在每个广告活动中每一步运行第 2 步到第 5 步的循环（另外附带报告一个更快的每 5 步一次的变体），并比较五个版本：(1) 固定的原始计划；(2) 始终重新锚定，即把支持度分数强行设为最大值，使其不再有门控；(3) 完整的支持度门控方法；(4) 一个负对照，把支持度分数序列打乱成随机顺序（数值集合相同、时刻错位），使门控不再跟踪真实支持度；(5) 一个正对照，只在固定目标回报上施加支持度门控、去掉节奏（pacing）项。对每个版本，测量在预算内赚得的广告主总价值，以及预算被超支的频率。把广告活动按市场漂移分成低/中/高三组——漂移用实时画像与其活动起始值之间的平均距离来衡量——并在每组内分别报告结果。打乱顺序的对照用来验证：让重新锚定变安全的是支持度分数本身，而不是它周围的机制。\n   - _为什么_: 打乱 $u_{t}$ 的对照用来验证：让重新锚定变安全的是支持度分数本身，而不是它周围的机制。\n\n"},{"id":"38","run_dir":"run_prompt38_lmsignature","index":38,"title":"The Detection-Power Cost of Unforgeability: A Frontier for LLM Watermarks","title_zh":"不可伪造性的检测能力代价：大语言模型水印的能力—可伪造性前沿","method_name":"Power-vs-Forgeability Frontier (PFF)","hook":"Every watermark-security paper — from the optimal-detection-rule framework (openalex:W4407557405) to the just-published unforgeable-signature constructions — tacitly treats detection power and forge-resistance as separately optimizable, so 'make it unforgeable' is assumed to cost no detection power. We show this assumption is false: any verification rule that accepts paraphrase-robust marked text must, by the same covering-number that gives it that robustness, hand a strategic forger a proportionally larger target, and we derive the exact power-vs-forgeability frontier — an achievable curve plus a matching converse — that no scheme, including the new signature-lifted ones, can cross.","anchor_pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","anchor_pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","domain_category":"LLM Alignment, Safety & Behavior","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes how much detection power must be GIVEN UP to obtain a target unforgeability level — the power-vs-distortion frontier is mapped (openalex:W4407557405, openalex:W4415366672) but the power-vs-forgeability frontier (the cost, in detectability or text distortion, of making the mark hard to forge) is never quantified.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by pivoting the assumption baked into the watermark detector's decision rule — that its acceptance region can be made most-powerful against nature with the unforgeability budget bolted on separately — and re-deriving the rule's performance certificate in the field's native currency (detection power π at false-positive rate α) under an added strategic-forger constraint, yielding the load-bearing artifact: a re-derived bound π ≤ Π(φ; α, ρ, L) (achievability) together with a matching converse, i.e. the power-vs-forgeability frontier itself, whose binding is to the verification rule's acceptance-region covering number rather than to any dataset-dependent constant.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions whether the quantity that survives into the emitted text must be a SECRET-keyed statistic at all, rather than a publicly-recomputable function of the text plus a public commitment — every leaf inherits the symmetric-secret assumption from the shared green-list/keyed-sampling ancestor and none tests whether that secret is necessary for detection or only assumed.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by pinning the field's tacit identifiability assumption — that a secret-keyed statistic is NECESSARY to gate verification — and pivoting it into a recovery-style separation: we prove the power-vs-forgeability frontier is governed by the acceptance region's covering number N(ρ) under the edit metric and is INVARIANT to whether that region is gated by a secret key or by a public commitment, so the frontier is recovered up to the equivalence class {schemes with the same N(ρ)} and the forgeability cost is shown intrinsic to robust verifiability, not an artifact of secret-keying — an identifiability/impossibility claim, not a construction.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"LLM watermarking / generated-text provenance and authentication (alignment, safety, societal considerations)","n_papers":40,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":26},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":10,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Scalable watermarking for identifying large language model outputs"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Large Language Model Watermark Stealing With Mixed Integer Programming"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"GuardEmb: Dynamic Watermark for Safeguarding Large Language Model Embedding Service Against Model Stealing Attack"},{"source":"openalex","title":"A Survey of Text Watermarking in the Era of Large Language Models"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Beyond Binary Classification: Customizable Text Watermark on Large Language Models"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Preventing and Detecting Misinformation Generated by Large Language Models"}],"more":4},{"year":2025,"n":29,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Security and Detectability Analysis of Unicode Text Watermarking Methods Against Large Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Black-Box Text Watermarking Algorithm towards Large Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"LOCAT: Localization-Driven Text Watermarking via Large Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Filtering Resistant Large Language Model Watermarking via Style Injection"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Post-Hoc Watermarking for Robust Detection in Text Generated by Large Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"WASA: WAtermark-based Source Attribution for Large Language Model-Generated Data"}],"more":23},{"year":2026,"n":1,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"}],"more":0}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":7,"share":0.175},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":7,"share":0.175},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":6,"share":0.15},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":6,"share":0.15},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":3,"share":0.075},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":3,"share":0.075},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":3,"share":0.075},{"pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","count":3,"share":0.075}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Every production and research LLM watermark retrieved here embeds and detects the mark with the SAME secret: SynthID-Text (semanticscholar:89bd8efe0b9c0427cb7814d7b8c2b0190d2ffa9e) tournament-samples against a hashed key, the statistically-optimal detector of openalex:W4407557405 keys its pivotal statistic on the same generation secret, and MCMARK (openalex:W4412944931) promotes a vocabulary segment chosen by a watermark key — in all of them the detection rule is a deterministic function of the embedding secret. This symmetry means the capability to VERIFY a signature is identical to the capability to PRODUCE one: any verifier (or anyone who recovers the green-list from samples, as the mixed-integer-programming theft of semanticscholar:550a79a7e688347af18bf5752361c47f0af1cf40 does, or who erases/forges it as FedProbe openalex:W7127088301 does) can stamp arbitrary attacker text with a valid mark and frame a target model, while a model owner cannot prove to a skeptical third party that a flagged passage did NOT come from their model. The structural failure is that current schemes authenticate text as 'watermarked-by-the-secret-holder' but cannot bind a passage to a specific generating model under a verification capability that is strictly weaker than the forging capability, so the mark provides detection but not non-repudiable, publicly-checkable, forgery-resistant attribution.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:89bd8efe0b9c0427cb7814d7b8c2b0190d2ffa9e","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"SynthID-Text embeds a detectable signal at scale via tournament sampling against a hashed watermarking key while preserving text quality and adding minimal latency, and its detector is the optimal Bayesian/weighted-mean score over the same key. Its method binds detectability to possession of the single watermarking key, so anyone holding the key to detect can also generate validly-marked text and the scheme offers no asymmetry between verification and forgery — a verifier and a forger are the same role, and a non-key-holding third party can neither verify independently nor be protected against a key-holder forging in the model's name."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4407557405","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"This Annals-of-Statistics framework casts watermark detection as hypothesis testing over a pivotal statistic and derives detection-optimal rules and efficiency bounds. It optimizes detection POWER under a fixed symmetric-key generative signal and never models an adversary who knows the detection rule and crafts text to pass it; unforgeability — whether a party lacking a secret can fabricate a passage the optimal rule accepts — is outside its objective, so its 'optimality' is power, not security."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:550a79a7e688347af18bf5752361c47f0af1cf40","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"This work shows the green-red list of a state-of-the-art symmetric watermark can be recovered from samples by solving a mixed-integer program, after which an attacker forges or spoofs the mark. It establishes the forgery VULNERABILITY of symmetric schemes empirically but proposes no replacement whose verification capability is provably weaker than its forging capability, leaving the gap of an actually-unforgeable signature open."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4412944931","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"MCMARK partitions the vocabulary into segments and promotes the segment chosen by a watermark key, achieving an unbiased (distortion-free) mark that preserves output distribution. Its 'unbiasedness' is about output quality, not security: the same key both selects the promoted segment and detects it, so distortion-freeness does nothing to separate verification from forgery — a key-holder still forges trivially."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"LLM watermarking / generated-text provenance and authentication (alignment, safety, societal considerations)","venue":"ICLR 2026","time":"2026","data":["open-weight instruction-tuned LLMs (e.g. Llama-3 8B/70B class) for generation","standard open-ended generation prompts (e.g. C4 / Dolly / Alpaca-style instructions) for distortion and detection measurement","paraphrase and edit corpora for robustness stress tests"],"compute":"1×A100 × 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML + applied cryptography / information theory","preference":"both","baseline":"symmetric green-red list watermark (KGW-style) and SynthID-Text tournament sampling (semanticscholar:89bd8efe0b9c0427cb7814d7b8c2b0190d2ffa9e); statistical detection-optimal rules (openalex:W4407557405)","limitation":"Every retrieved scheme uses one secret that both embeds and detects, so any party able to verify is also able to forge, and the secret is steal-able from samples (semanticscholar:550a79a7e688347af18bf5752361c47f0af1cf40); no scheme yields a publicly-verifiable signature whose forgery is hard even for a verifier.","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["domain","venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared question both legs attack is: what is the irreducible detection-power cost of making an LLM watermark hard to forge? The central object is the verification rule's acceptance region A ⊂ X over the space X of token sequences, equipped with the edit (Levenshtein/paraphrase) pseudometric d; a verifier accepts text x iff x ∈ A. Three quantities are computable from this object alone plus the generation distribution. (1) Detection power π = P_{x∼G}[x ∈ A], where G is the model's marked-generation distribution (estimable by Monte-Carlo over generations); it is measured at a fixed false-positive rate α = P_{x∼H}[x ∈ A] under the human/other-text null H. (2) Robustness radius ρ: A must contain the ρ-edit-ball around marked text for the scheme to survive paraphrase, i.e. for marked x, the ball B(x,ρ) ⊆ A — this is exactly the robustness the incumbent schemes (openalex:W4412944931, openalex:W4407557405) target. (3) Forge-advantage φ = sup_{F} P_{y∼F}[y ∈ A] − α, the supremum over strategic forgers F that lack the signing key but may query the public verification interface; F's reachable distribution is supported on attacker-authored text whose only information about A comes from L = I(verification-oracle transcript ; A), the verification-leakage budget in bits (zero for an ideal opaque oracle, larger for a reveal-r or public-recomputable verifier). The anchor leg's pivot (C11) re-derives the detector's certificate under the strategic-forger constraint by a covering-number argument: enforcing B(x,ρ) ⊆ A for a π-fraction of G forces A to have edit-covering number N(ρ) ≥ c·π·exp(ρ·log|V|) (V the vocabulary), because A must cover a π-mass of ρ-balls; but a forger with leakage L can localize A to within 2^{−L} of its volume, so its best acceptance is φ + α ≥ N(ρ)·2^{−L}/N_total where N_total is the ambient covering number of X at scale ρ. Eliminating N(ρ) between the robustness lower bound and the forgery lower bound gives the achievable frontier π ≤ Π(φ; α, ρ, L) := (φ+α)·N_total·2^{L}/(c·exp(ρ·log|V|)), and a matching converse is obtained by exhibiting, for any target (π, φ) below the curve, a threshold acceptance region (an indicator on a keystream agreement statistic with threshold tuned to α) that achieves it — so the curve is tight, not merely an upper bound. This closes the anchor gap: the bound is a re-derived performance certificate (power π) in the native currency, holding for ANY scheme including the signature-lifted constructions of the live corpus, because those constructions also instantiate a robust acceptance region A and therefore inherit the same N(ρ). The sibling leg (C05) reads the SAME object to settle the secret-necessity question: since π ≤ Π(φ; α, ρ, L) depends on A only through (N(ρ), L) and not on whether membership x ∈ A is decided by a secret-keyed statistic or by a publicly-recomputable function plus a public commitment, the frontier is identifiable up to the equivalence class of acceptance regions sharing (N(ρ), L); we prove a public-commitment verifier and a secret-keyed verifier with matched (N(ρ), L) sit at the SAME frontier point, so the forgeability cost is intrinsic to robust verifiability and the secret was never necessary for the cost — only L (the leakage of the verification interface), which a public scheme can drive to the same value, governs it. All quantities are computable from text alone plus the published interface: π and α by Monte-Carlo over G and H, ρ from the edit model, N(ρ) by an empirical covering-number estimate of the realized acceptance set, L by the mutual-information between simulated oracle transcripts and the acceptance indicator.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The two legs share one machinery, not two modules: both read the single acceptance-region object A and its two scalars (N(ρ), L); the anchor derives the frontier as a function of them, and the sibling proves the frontier is invariant to the secret/public distinction because it factors through exactly those two scalars — so a reviewer sees one characterization, the second leg being the invariance corollary that makes the first leg's bound apply to the just-published public-key constructions too. I considered making the sibling a separate identifiability theorem about latent keys (a true C05 recovery-up-to-permutation result) but rejected it: that would read as a second paper on key recovery, whereas the coherent move is to prove the SAME frontier is what is identifiable, up to the (N(ρ), L) equivalence class. I also considered anchoring on characterize_limit_then_surpass (kept as anchor_alternate) — the deliverable is genuinely a characterized limit — but its C10 tactical move (re-inject a discarded structural object into an iterative-local graph procedure) does not match a hypothesis-testing tradeoff, whereas C11's 'pivot the decision rule's assumption and re-derive its performance certificate' is the exact move, so I bound the anchor to C11. Avoided regression: the mechanism does NOT reduce to node n4 (the detection-optimal framework of openalex:W4407557405) — n4 optimizes power against nature and the converse here is precisely the object n4 cannot produce (a power upper bound as a function of forge-advantage), nor to c0 (public-key signatures), because the contribution is a tradeoff characterization that the signature primitive does not supply; the keystream-threshold region used in the achievability half is a reused incumbent ingredient, not the contribution.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: take an open-weight 8B instruction-tuned LLM, generate 5k marked passages plus a 5k human/other-text null, and instantiate a family of verification rules of increasing acceptance-region size (sweeping the keystream-agreement threshold) so that detection power π (true-accept rate at fixed false-positive rate α=1e-3) and edit-robustness radius ρ vary together; for each rule run a gradient-free strategic forger that queries the verification oracle and crafts 5k attacker-authored passages, measuring forge-advantage φ (forger acceptance rate minus α). If the characterization holds, the measured operating points (π, φ) all fall ON OR BELOW the derived frontier Π(φ; α, ρ, L) and never cross it, and crucially — the non-obvious directional claim — driving φ toward zero at fixed robustness radius ρ forces a measurable DROP in achievable π (the curve has strictly negative slope wherever ρ>0), whereas the incumbent power-optimal rule of openalex:W4407557405, which ignores the forger, sits strictly above the achievable curve and is therefore forgeable. The named load-bearing variable is the verification-leakage budget L (mutual information between the verification-oracle transcript and the acceptance indicator) entering the frontier through the 2^{L} factor; the mechanism claim is that L is what couples power to forgeability. Negative control: oracle-replace the real verification interface with an ideal zero-leakage oracle (set L=0) while holding ρ, α, the keystream, and the generation distribution fixed — the downstream metric, achievable detection power at a fixed target forge-success-rate, must rise toward its L=0 ceiling (the task-outcome metric, not L's own value), confirming leakage, not the keystream, is what moves the frontier. Positive control: a stripped predictor that uses ONLY the estimated covering number N(ρ) and L to predict each rule's (π, φ) operating point should recover most of the measured frontier's shape, identifying (N(ρ), L) as the sufficient pair of summary statistics.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4407557405","delta":"The Annals framework derives the most-powerful detection rule and efficiency bounds for a fixed symmetric keyed signal optimizing power against nature; we derive a power UPPER bound as a function of strategic-forge-advantage φ and a matching converse — a tradeoff frontier between detection power and forgeability that their single-adversary (nature-only) objective structurally cannot express, since it never enters a forger's acceptance probability into the optimization."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415366672","delta":"Optimized Couplings characterizes the optimal power-vs-DISTORTION coupling for one-shot watermarking; we characterize the orthogonal power-vs-FORGEABILITY frontier, proving that robustness radius ρ (not distortion) is the quantity whose covering-number lower-bounds a strategic forger's success, a tradeoff axis their coupling analysis does not contain."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:550a79a7e688347af18bf5752361c47f0af1cf40","delta":"The MIP stealing attack empirically demonstrates that a recovered green-list lets a forger spoof a symmetric mark; we provide the matching theory — a converse showing the forge-advantage φ is lower-bounded by N(ρ)·2^{−L}/N_total for ANY robust acceptance region, so their attack is one instance of an unavoidable cost we quantify across all schemes, not only key-stealable ones."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4412944931","delta":"MCMARK supplies a distortion-free symmetric acceptance rule; we treat its acceptance region as one point and prove where on the power-vs-forgeability frontier any such robust region must lie, deriving that its unbiasedness (a distortion property) does not move it off the frontier because the frontier factors through covering number N(ρ) and leakage L, not through distortion."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4407557405","what_step_was_missed":"The Annals framework constructed the hypothesis-testing geometry and the most-powerful detection rule for a fixed keyed signal, but it modeled a single adversary — nature generating the null — and derived power as a quantity to maximize; to already be our contribution it would have needed to introduce a SECOND, strategic adversary (a forger crafting text to be accepted) into the same decision problem and re-derive the detection power as an UPPER bound constrained by that forger's achievable acceptance, i.e. construct the covering-number link between the acceptance region's edit-robustness and a forger's hit probability and prove a converse — a tradeoff characterization between two adversaries, which their single-adversary power-optimization (a most-powerful-test derivation, not a two-adversary frontier) does not contain."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":209,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"All hard-floor conditions are clear: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict = clear (no Reject lesson is candidate_match: yes on either leg); anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id = null; and paper_pointed_threat against openalex:W7130482002 is adjacency, NOT exact-mechanism overlap — its subsumption_argument shows it CONSTRUCTS an unforgeable scheme while the candidate DERIVES a converse/frontier on the detection-power cost of unforgeability that W7130482002 never produces and that would in fact place its scheme as one point on the curve. recipe_application_check.verdict = applied on both legs (C11 re-derives the performance certificate; C05 re-derives the frontier up to the named (N(ρ), L) equivalence class). With all checks clear/applied/adjacency-only and the threat already defused in the candidate's own framing, the verdict is advance.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes how much detection power must be GIVEN UP to obtain a target unforgeability level — the power-vs-distortion frontier is mapped (openalex:W4407557405, openalex:W4415366672) but the power-vs-forgeability frontier (the cost, in detectability or text distortion, of making the mark hard to forge) is never quantified.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The dominant failure is substituting one selection rule for another that performs better empirically while omitting the theorem that explains when and why it wins; a second is pivoting an assumption the community regards as a reasonable modeling choice rather than a genuine restriction; a third is a guarantee that does not hold up — a binding constant that is dataset-dependent and uncontrollable by the practitioner, or a marginal bound improvement with no matching lower bound to certify near-optimality.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Substituting one selection heuristic for another without a theorem stating when and why it wins reads as an engineering combination, not a contribution, no matter how clean the empirical gain.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate's deliverable IS the theorem — the frontier π ≤ Π(φ; α, ρ, L) plus a matching converse (core_mechanism steps 5-6) — not an empirical rule swap, so the failure mode does not apply."},{"lesson_quoted":"A re-derived guarantee whose binding constant is dataset-dependent and cannot be controlled by the practitioner is vacuous in the worst case and fails to convince.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The frontier binds to the acceptance region's edit-covering number N(ρ), the robustness radius ρ, and the verification-leakage budget L — all scheme-controllable design quantities, not dataset-dependent constants (core_mechanism)."},{"lesson_quoted":"Improving a bound by a marginal factor with no matching lower bound fails to demonstrate that the improvement is significant or near-optimal enough to clear the bar.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate supplies the matching converse explicitly (core_mechanism step 6 constructs a witness threshold region reaching any (π,φ) below Π), so the achievability bound is certified tight rather than one-sided."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pivoting an assumption the community treats as a reasonable modeling choice — rather than first proving it a genuine restriction — leaves both motivation and novelty in doubt.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The pivoted assumption (detection power is maximizable independently of forge-hardness) is shown load-bearing because the converse proves it FALSE whenever ρ>0 — power must drop to lower φ — so it is a genuine restriction, not a benign modeling choice."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions whether the quantity that survives into the emitted text must be a SECRET-keyed statistic at all, rather than a publicly-recomputable function of the text plus a public commitment — every leaf inherits the symmetric-secret assumption from the shared green-list/keyed-sampling ancestor and none tests whether that secret is necessary for detection or only assumed.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The signature failure is an identifiability claim that outruns its proof: the pivoted assumption was not actually load-bearing (a straightforward union of two frameworks), or recovery/'consistency' is asserted while the decisive object — the equivalence class — is never established, or structural constraints are imposed without proving they are SUFFICIENT for the recovery claimed.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Advertising an identifiability or 'consistency' property while the proof omits the decisive object — never proving latent identifiability, or excluding part of the model from the guarantee — collapses the contribution the moment a reviewer checks the theorem.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The decisive object IS named and exhibited — the equivalence class {acceptance regions sharing (N(ρ), L)} — and the leg proves Π factors through exactly (N(ρ), L) and that a public-commitment and a secret-keyed verifier with matched (N(ρ), L) realize the same frontier point (core_mechanism step 7)."},{"lesson_quoted":"Stacking two established frameworks and re-proving identifiability of the union reads as incremental unless the pivoted assumption was genuinely load-bearing and the union admits a regime neither framework could reach alone.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The sibling does not stack frameworks; it proves the SAME anchor frontier is invariant to the secret/public distinction, a corollary on the shared object, so the pivoted assumption (secret-keying is necessary) is load-bearing because dropping it is shown to leave the cost unchanged — a genuine new statement, not a union."},{"lesson_quoted":"Imposing structural constraints to claim interpretability or disentanglement without proving those constraints are sufficient for recovery leaves the result indistinguishable from a post-hoc heuristic.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The leg proves sufficiency: (N(ρ), L) alone determine the frontier point (Π depends on A only through them), so the equivalence class is shown sufficient for recovering the frontier, not merely correlated with it."}],"verdict":"clear"}],"verdict":"clear","reasoning":"Both gap_closure entries clear: the C11 anchor ships an actual theorem with a matching converse bound to scheme-controllable quantities (N(ρ), ρ, L), defeating C11's omitted-theorem / dataset-dependent-constant / no-lower-bound Reject lessons; the C05 sibling names and proves sufficiency of the decisive equivalence class {regions sharing (N(ρ), L)}, defeating C05's omitted-decisive-object and union-stacking lessons. No Reject lesson is candidate_match: yes."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes how much detection power must be GIVEN UP to obtain a target unforgeability level — the power-vs-distortion frontier is mapped (openalex:W4407557405, openalex:W4415366672) but the power-vs-forgeability frontier (the cost, in detectability or text distortion, of making the mark hard to forge) is never quantified.","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Center on a decision/selection rule and pivot the single assumption baked into its criterion, either relaxing the structural crutch and re-proving the guarantee or reframing the task as a different problem class; the invariant deliverable is a RE-DERIVED performance certificate for the pivoted rule — a regret bound, competitive ratio, generalization error, or approximation ratio — shown to match or strictly beat the pre-pivot baseline.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism pivots the assumption baked into the watermark detector's acceptance rule (power maximizable independently of forge-hardness) and re-derives the rule's performance certificate in the native currency — detection power π as an upper bound Π(φ; α, ρ, L) with a matching converse (steps 3-6) — which is exactly C11's 'invariant deliverable is a re-derived performance certificate', here a power bound rather than a regret bound; the signature move is performed.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions whether the quantity that survives into the emitted text must be a SECRET-keyed statistic at all, rather than a publicly-recomputable function of the text plus a public commitment — every leaf inherits the symmetric-secret assumption from the shared green-list/keyed-sampling ancestor and none tests whether that secret is necessary for detection or only assumed.","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Take an existing identifiability/recovery result and pivot the assumption it requires, trading a distributional assumption for a structural/geometric one, then re-derive recovery up to the field's accepted ambiguity class — naming the equivalence class explicitly (permutation, sign-flip, component-wise reparameterization) and proving the substitute condition ALONE suffices.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism step 7 pivots the secret-necessity assumption and re-derives the frontier 'recovered up to' the explicitly named equivalence class {acceptance regions sharing (N(ρ), L)}, proving that pair ALONE determines the frontier point so secret-keying is not necessary — C05's 'recover up to a named equivalence class, prove the substitute condition alone suffices' move is performed, with (N(ρ), L) playing the role of the ambiguity-class-determining structure.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries perform their cited cluster's signature move: C11 re-derives a performance certificate (the power-vs-forgeability frontier + converse) for the pivoted detection rule; C05 re-derives the frontier up to an explicitly named equivalence class and proves the substitute condition (matched (N(ρ), L)) alone suffices."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["assumption_audit_and_pivot","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"None of the three reject-favored compositions applies: all require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component, and the composition_set is assumption_audit_and_pivot on both legs, containing no heterogeneous_decomposition."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"openalex:W7130482002","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"'Unforgeable Watermarks for Language Models via Robust Signatures' (openalex:W7130482002, 2026) CONSTRUCTS the first robust, unforgeable, recoverable watermark via robust digital signatures — an achievability artifact: it builds a scheme and proves it attains unforgeability. The candidate's contribution is orthogonal: a CHARACTERIZATION — a power-vs-forgeability frontier with a matching CONVERSE proving that any robust acceptance region (including W7130482002's signature-lifted one, which also instantiates a robust acceptance region with some N(ρ), L) must surrender detection power to lower a strategic forger's advantage. W7130482002 derives no tradeoff frontier, no converse/impossibility on detection-power cost, and never enters a forger's acceptance probability into a power bound; its existence does not make the candidate's claim stand or fall, because a construction that achieves unforgeability does not quantify how much power it surrendered to do so — which is precisely the candidate's deliverable, and which the candidate's bound would in fact characterize for W7130482002's scheme as one point on the curve. This is adjacency on the security objective, not exact-mechanism overlap.","addressable_via":"Frame the contribution explicitly as a converse/frontier characterization (already done in title, hook, core_mechanism, and what_step_was_missed) and cite W7130482002 as a construction the frontier bounds — not as prior art for the frontier itself; the candidate already does this, so no field edit is required to dodge subsumption."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# The Detection-Power Cost of Unforgeability: A Frontier for LLM Watermarks\n\n**Method.** Power-vs-Forgeability Frontier (PFF)\n\n## Motivation\nThe goal is provenance for text written by a large language model (LLM): a way to check that a passage really came from a given model, and — just as important — a way that a malicious party CANNOT fake. Faking here means stamping attacker-written text so a checker wrongly says 'this came from the model', which would let someone frame a model owner. Today's research splits into two camps. One camp studies how to make the watermark as DETECTABLE as possible — there is even an optimal statistical detection rule (openalex:W4407557405, Annals of Statistics 2025) and an analysis of the best trade-off between detectability and how much the text is distorted (openalex:W4415366672). The other camp recently built schemes that are hard to forge. But every paper quietly assumes these two goals — being easy to detect and being hard to forge — can be tuned independently, as if making a watermark unforgeable is free in detection terms. We show that is wrong. The intuition: to survive paraphrasing, a checker must ACCEPT not just the exact marked text but everything within a small editing distance of it — a whole neighborhood. The more such neighborhoods it accepts (the more detectable and paraphrase-robust it is), the bigger the total 'accept' set becomes. But a bigger accept set is exactly a bigger target for a forger to aim at. So detectability and forge-resistance pull against each other, and the size of the accept set (its 'covering number' under the editing distance) is the hidden quantity that links them. This matters NOW because paraphrase-robustness is the default requirement and a working unforgeable construction already exists (openalex:W7130482002, 2026) — so the open question is no longer 'can we build it' but 'what did it cost in detection power, and is that cost avoidable'. We answer that with an exact trade-off curve (a frontier) plus a proof it cannot be beaten, and we show the curve is the same whether the checker uses a secret key or a public one — so going public-key costs nothing extra in this trade-off, contradicting the assumption that the secret is what does the work.\n\n## Method\n### Object & adversaries\n*Fix the accept-set object and the two scalars it is judged by, and introduce the missing strategic forger plus the leakage dial.*\n\n1. Treat the watermark checker as an 'accept set' A: the collection of all token sequences it would flag as model-generated, measured under an editing distance — concretely token-level Levenshtein distance (the number of single-token insertions, deletions, or substitutions between two texts), optionally backed by a sentence-embedding paraphrase distance. Measure three numbers on a corpus: detection power (the fraction of genuine marked outputs the checker accepts, estimated by just running the checker on a set of marked generations and counting), false-positive rate (the fraction of human text it wrongly accepts, counted the same way on a human/other-text set), and robustness radius (how many edits a marked text can absorb and still be accepted — found per text by running a greedy-plus-random-restart paraphrase attacker and recording the largest edit budget it fails to break, then taking a low percentile across texts so the radius holds for most marked text).\n   - _Why_: Everything that follows is stated in these three plain quantities, so pinning them down first lets the whole trade-off be written in the field's own currency.\n2. Add a second player — a forger who does NOT hold the model's signing key but can probe the public checking interface. Realize it as a gradient-free black-box optimizer (an evolutionary search over token edits, such as CMA-ES or a genetic algorithm, with a large-language-model paraphrase step as one of its mutation moves) that, under a fixed query budget, tweaks attacker-written passages to maximize the chance the checker accepts them; the forge-advantage is how much more often than chance the forger gets accepted (its accept rate minus the false-positive rate). Also define the verification-leakage L: how many bits the checking interface leaks about the accept set — measured as the mutual information (a standard information-theory quantity for how much one signal tells you about another) between what the interface returns per query (accept/reject, any score it shows, any published commitment it opens) and whether the text is actually accepted, using a standard binned or nearest-neighbour mutual-information estimator on logged queries. Leakage is zero for a sealed accept/reject-only black box and grows as the interface reveals internal randomness or becomes publicly recomputable.\n\n*Forge-advantage $\\phi $ is the best acceptance probability over strategic forgers F that lack the signing key, minus the false-positive rate $\\alpha $; it measures how much better than chance a forger can be accepted.*\n$$ \\varphi \\;=\\; \\sup_{F}\\, \\mathbb{P}_{y\\sim F}\\big[y \\in A\\big] \\;-\\; \\alpha \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The detectability-optimal literature only fights 'nature' (random human text); the forger is the missing adversary, and leakage L is the dial that controls how easy the forger's job is.\n\n### The two-sided bound\n*Chain a robustness lower bound on accept-set size into a forgery lower bound, linking detectability to forgeability.*\n\n3. Prove the robustness side: to accept a given fraction of marked outputs AND tolerate $\\rho $ edits, the accept set must cover a whole editing-distance neighborhood around each accepted text, which forces its size — its edit-covering number $N(\\rho ),$ the number of $radius-\\rho $ editing-distance balls needed to cover the accept set — to grow at least like the detection power times an exponential in $\\rho $ (and in the log of the vocabulary size). The hidden constant simply normalizes one ball's volume and the fraction of marked text required to be robust, and is reported with the bound rather than tuned. To estimate $N(\\rho )$ in practice, greedily pack as many $\\rho -apart$ accepted texts as possible (a packing this size is a valid lower bound on the covering number) and count them. In short, more detectability and more paraphrase-robustness mean a strictly bigger accept set.\n\n*The edit-covering number $N(\\rho )$ of the acceptance region is lower-bounded by the detection power $\\pi $ times an exponential in the robustness radius $\\rho $ and log vocabulary size log|V|; robustness forces a large acceptance set.*\n$$ N(\\rho) \\geq c\\,\\pi\\,\\exp\\!\\big(\\rho\\,\\log|V|\\big) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: It turns the soft idea 'robust checkers accept a lot' into a hard lower bound on the accept set's size, which the next step attacks.\n4. Prove the forgery side: a forger who has learned L bits about the accept set can shrink its search to a 2-to-the-minus-L slice of the space (operationally, it uses those L bits to point its evolutionary search at the promising fraction of regions before it starts), so its acceptance rate is at least the accept-set's covering number times that 2-to-the-minus-L slice, divided by the covering number of the whole text space at the same radius (the ambient count, found by the same packing estimator on uniformly random texts). That ratio is just the accept set's density in the space. A bigger accept set, from the previous step, directly means an easier forgery — and a higher hit rate on the real harm, framing a model owner with attacker text.\n\n*A strategic forger with verification-leakage L hits the acceptance set with probability at least $N(\\rho )$ shrunk by 2 to the minus L over the ambient covering number; less leakage L lowers the floor but a larger $N(\\rho )$ raises it.*\n$$ \\varphi + \\alpha \\;\\geq\\; \\frac{N(\\rho)\\,2^{-L}}{N_{\\mathrm{total}}} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: It converts accept-set SIZE into a concrete forgery success rate, closing the loop between detectability and forgeability.\n\n### Frontier, converse & invariance\n*Combine the bounds into the tight power-vs-forgeability frontier and prove it is the same for secret and public verification.*\n\n5. Combine the two bounds by canceling the accept-set's covering number between them, yielding the frontier: achievable detection power is at most an increasing function of the forge-advantage and the leakage and a decreasing function of the robustness radius. Then show the curve is tight by building an explicit checker that lands on any point below it: accept when a keystream-agreement score — the normalized rate at which the text's tokens match the key-derived pseudorandom 'green' pattern — passes a cutoff. Choose that cutoff by a simple one-dimensional search on the score's human-text distribution so the false-positive rate exactly hits the target, then widen or narrow the score's edit-tolerance window to hit the target robustness radius, and read off the resulting detection power and forge-advantage by simulation to confirm it reaches the intended point.\n\n*Eliminating $N(\\rho )$ between the two lower bounds gives the power-vs-forgeability frontier: detection power $\\pi $ is bounded by an increasing function of forge-advantage $\\phi $ and verification-leakage L and a decreasing function of robustness radius $\\rho .$*\n$$ \\pi \\;\\leq\\; \\Pi(\\varphi;\\,\\alpha,\\rho,L) \\;:=\\; (\\varphi+\\alpha)\\,\\frac{N_{\\mathrm{total}}\\,2^{L}}{c\\,\\exp(\\rho\\,\\log|V|)} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Canceling the shared quantity is what makes power and forgeability trade off directly; the explicit construction proves the curve is reachable, not just an upper limit.\n6. Show the frontier depends on the accept set through only two summary numbers — its covering number (size) and the leakage. Then build two checkers and tune them to the same two numbers: a secret-key checker, and a public-commitment checker that instead publishes a sealed, tamper-evident commitment to the keystream (for example a hash or Merkle commitment) and checks text with a publicly recomputable function of the text plus the opened commitment — no held secret. Match their accept-set sizes by setting the public checker's cutoff to the same measured covering number, and match their leakage by limiting each interface to return the same amount of information. Prove they then sit at the exact same point on the curve, so the cost of unforgeability is the same whether you keep a secret or publish a commitment — it depends only on this size-and-leakage pair, named as the class of all accept sets that share it.\n   - _Why_: It isolates leakage, not secrecy, as the thing that sets the cost, answering whether the watermark's surviving signal must be secret at all (it need not).\n\n### Empirical trace & control\n*Confirm no real scheme crosses the curve and that leakage, not the keystream, moves it.*\n\n7. On an open-weight 8-billion-parameter instruction-tuned model (for example a Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct-class checkpoint), generate the marked set from standard open-ended prompts and use a held-out human/other-text corpus as the null. Sweep the checker's acceptance cutoff across a grid of 20-40 points spanning the range from human-text scores to marked-text scores, at each setting keeping the false-positive rate fixed (by the one-dimensional search from the previous step) and measuring the detection power and forge-advantage at one fixed robustness radius. Plot all these operating points against the predicted frontier and confirm none beats it and the explicit witness checker lands on it. As a control, replace the real checking interface with an ideal sealed oracle that leaks nothing — it returns only accept or reject, no score, no opened commitment, no internal randomness (leakage set to zero) — while holding the robustness radius, false-positive rate, keystream, and generation distribution fixed, and confirm the achievable detection power at a fixed forgery success rate rises toward its zero-leakage ceiling.\n   - _Why_: It tests the theory's sharpest prediction (no scheme crosses the curve) and verifies that leakage L — not the watermark keystream — is what moves the curve, via a clean on/off intervention.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 不可伪造性的检测能力代价：大语言模型水印的能力—可伪造性前沿\n\n**方法名称.** Power-vs-Forgeability Frontier (PFF)\n\n## 研究动机\n我们要解决的是大语言模型(Large Language Model, LLM)生成文本的来源认证问题：既能核验某段文字确实来自某个模型，又——同样重要——要让恶意方无法伪造。这里的伪造指：把攻击者自己写的文本伪装成模型输出，使核验器错误地判定『这来自该模型』，从而构陷模型方。当前研究分成两派。一派研究如何让水印尽可能可检测，甚至已有最优统计检测规则(openalex:W4407557405, Annals of Statistics 2025)以及可检测性与文本失真之间最优权衡的分析(openalex:W4415366672)。另一派最近构造了难以伪造的方案。但所有论文都默认这两个目标——易于检测、难以伪造——可以各自独立调节，仿佛让水印不可伪造在检测能力上是免费的。我们证明这是错的。直觉是：为了抵抗改写(paraphrase)，核验器必须不仅接受精确的带标记文本，还要接受其编辑距离很小范围内的一整片邻域。它接受的这种邻域越多（越可检测、越抗改写），整个『接受集』就越大；而更大的接受集恰恰是伪造者更大的命中目标。于是可检测性与抗伪造性彼此拮抗，而接受集在编辑距离下的大小（其『覆盖数 covering number』）就是把二者联系起来的隐藏量。这一问题在当下尤为紧要：抗改写已是默认要求，而可用的不可伪造构造已经存在(openalex:W7130482002, 2026)——因此开放问题不再是『能否构造』，而是『它在检测能力上付出了多大代价，这代价是否可避免』。我们用一条精确的权衡曲线（前沿）外加它无法被超越的证明来回答，并证明无论核验器用密钥还是公开承诺，这条曲线都相同——也就是说在此权衡下转向公钥并不额外付出代价，这与『密钥才是关键』的默认假设相矛盾。\n\n## 方法\n### 对象与对手\n*固定接受集对象及其评判所用的两个标量，并引入缺失的策略性伪造者与泄漏旋钮。*\n\n1. 把水印核验器看成一个『接受集』A：它会判定为模型生成的所有 token 序列的集合，并在一种编辑距离下度量——具体取 token 级 Levenshtein 距离（两段文本相差多少处单 token 的插入、删除或替换），可再辅以一个句向量改写(paraphrase)距离作为粗粒度的第二度量。在语料上测三个数：检测能力（真正带标记输出中被接受的比例，直接在一批带标记生成上运行核验器计数即得）、假阳性率（人写文本被错误接受的比例，在一批人写/其他文本上同样计数）、鲁棒半径（带标记文本最多被改动多少处仍被接受——对每条文本运行一个贪心加随机重启的改写攻击器，记录它未能攻破的最大编辑预算，再跨文本取一个较低分位数，使该半径对大多数带标记文本都成立）。\n   - _为什么_: 后续一切都用这三个朴素量来表述，先把它们定下来，整条权衡就能用本领域自己的语言写出。\n2. 引入第二个参与者——一个不掌握模型签名密钥、但可以探测公开核验接口的伪造者(forger)。把它实现为一个无梯度的黑箱优化器（在 token 编辑上做进化搜索，如 CMA-ES 或遗传算法，并把一次大语言模型改写(paraphrase)作为其变异操作之一），在固定查询预算下不断改写攻击者所写文本以最大化被核验器接受的概率；可伪造优势即伪造者被接受的概率比随机高出多少（其接受率减去假阳性率）。再定义验证泄漏 L：核验接口泄露了关于接受集的多少比特信息——用互信息(mutual information，信息论中衡量一个信号能透露另一个信号多少的标准量)来度量，即接口每次查询返回的内容（接受/拒绝、它展示的任何分数、它公开打开的任何承诺）与该文本是否真正被接受之间的互信息，用标准的分箱或最近邻互信息估计器在记录的查询日志上估计。若核验器是只返回接受/拒绝的密封黑箱则泄漏为零，若它暴露内部随机数或可被公开重算则泄漏更大。\n\n*可伪造优势 $\\phi $ 定义为在不掌握签名密钥的策略性伪造者 F 上取上确界的接受概率，再减去假阳性率 $\\alpha $；它衡量伪造者被接受的概率比随机高出多少。*\n$$ \\varphi \\;=\\; \\sup_{F}\\, \\mathbb{P}_{y\\sim F}\\big[y \\in A\\big] \\;-\\; \\alpha \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 可检测性最优的文献只对抗『自然』（随机的人写文本）；伪造者正是缺失的对手，而泄漏 L 是控制伪造者难易程度的旋钮。\n\n### 双侧界\n*把关于接受集大小的鲁棒性下界链接到伪造下界，将可检测性与可伪造性联系起来。*\n\n3. 证明鲁棒性一侧：要接受给定比例的带标记输出、又要容忍 $\\rho $ 处编辑，接受集必须覆盖每个被接受文本周围的一整片编辑距离邻域，这迫使它的大小——编辑覆盖数 $N(\\rho )$，即覆盖整个接受集所需的半径为 $\\rho $ 的编辑距离球的个数——至少按检测能力乘以一个关于 $\\rho $（以及词表大小对数 log|V|）的指数项增长。式中隐藏常数只是对单个球的体积以及『要鲁棒的带标记文本比例』做归一化，随界一并报告而非调参。实践中估计 $N(\\rho )$ 时，贪心地尽量多地塞入彼此相距 $\\rho $ 的被接受文本（这样一个填装的规模就是覆盖数的有效下界）并计数。简言之，越可检测、越抗改写，接受集就越大。\n\n*接受区域的编辑覆盖数 $N(\\rho )$ 至少正比于检测能力 $\\pi $ 乘以一个关于鲁棒半径 $\\rho $ 与 log|V|（词表大小对数）的指数项；要鲁棒就必然要有大的接受集。*\n$$ N(\\rho) \\geq c\\,\\pi\\,\\exp\\!\\big(\\rho\\,\\log|V|\\big) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 它把『鲁棒的核验器会接受很多』这一软直觉，变成对接受集大小的硬下界，供下一步攻击。\n4. 证明伪造一侧：已掌握关于接受集 L 比特信息的伪造者，可以把搜索范围缩小到整个空间的 2 的负 L 次方那一片（操作上，它用这 L 比特在开始前就把进化搜索指向有希望的那一小部分区域），于是其接受率至少等于接受集的覆盖数乘以这一 2 的负 L 次方的片、再除以同半径下整个文本空间的覆盖数（环境计数，用同一填装估计器在均匀随机文本上求得）。这个比值就是接受集在空间中的密度。来自上一步的更大接受集，直接意味着伪造更容易——也意味着在真正的危害（用攻击者文本构陷模型方）上有更高的命中率。\n\n*拥有验证泄漏 L 的策略性伪造者命中接受集的概率至少为 $N(\\rho )$ 经 $2^(- L)$ 衰减后除以环境覆盖数 $N_{total}$；泄漏 L 越小该下界越低，但接受集 $N(\\rho )$ 越大该下界越高。*\n$$ \\varphi + \\alpha \\;\\geq\\; \\frac{N(\\rho)\\,2^{-L}}{N_{\\mathrm{total}}} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 它把接受集的『大小』换算成具体的伪造成功率，闭合了可检测性与可伪造性之间的回路。\n\n### 前沿、逆定理与不变性\n*把两个界合成为紧的能力—可伪造性前沿，并证明它对密钥与公开验证相同。*\n\n5. 把两个下界中接受集的覆盖数相互消去，得到前沿：可达检测能力至多是关于可伪造优势与泄漏递增、关于鲁棒半径递减的函数。再通过构造一个能落在曲线下方任意一点的显式核验器来证明该曲线是紧的：当 keystream 一致性得分——文本 token 与密钥导出的伪随机『绿色』模式相符的归一化比率——超过某个阈值时即接受。用一次在该得分的人写文本分布上的一维搜索来选这个阈值，使假阳性率恰好命中目标，再放宽或收紧该得分的编辑容忍窗口以命中目标鲁棒半径，并用模拟读出由此得到的检测能力与可伪造优势，确认它达到预定的那一点。\n\n*在两个下界之间消去 $N(\\rho )$ 即得能力—可伪造性前沿：检测能力 $\\pi $ 受限于一个随可伪造优势 $\\phi $ 与验证泄漏 L 递增、随鲁棒半径 $\\rho $ 递减的函数。*\n$$ \\pi \\;\\leq\\; \\Pi(\\varphi;\\,\\alpha,\\rho,L) \\;:=\\; (\\varphi+\\alpha)\\,\\frac{N_{\\mathrm{total}}\\,2^{L}}{c\\,\\exp(\\rho\\,\\log|V|)} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 消去共同量正是让能力与可伪造性直接此消彼长的关键；而显式构造证明曲线是可达的，而非仅仅一个上界。\n6. 证明前沿对接受集的依赖只通过两个汇总数——它的覆盖数（大小）与泄漏。随后构造两个核验器并把它们调到这两个数相同：一个密钥核验器；以及一个公开承诺(public commitment)核验器，后者改为公布一个对 keystream 的密封、可验篡改的承诺（例如哈希或 Merkle 承诺），并用『文本加上被打开的承诺』的可公开重算函数来核验——不持有任何秘密。把公开核验器的阈值设为与之相同的实测覆盖数以匹配接受集大小，并限制每个接口返回相同的信息量以匹配泄漏。证明它们随后落在曲线上完全相同的点，于是不可伪造的代价无论你保守一个密钥还是公布一个承诺都一样——它只取决于这个『大小与泄漏』对，记为所有共享该对的接受集所构成的那个等价类。\n   - _为什么_: 它把设定代价的因素锁定为泄漏而非保密，回答了水印赖以存活的信号是否必须保密这一问题（答案是不必）。\n\n### 实证刻画与对照\n*确认没有真实方案越过曲线，且移动曲线的是泄漏而非 keystream。*\n\n7. 在一个开源权重的 80 亿参数指令微调模型上（例如 Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct 一类的 checkpoint），用标准的开放式提示生成带标记集，并用一份留出的人写/其他文本语料作为零假设。把核验器的接受阈值在一个由人写文本得分到带标记文本得分、跨度约 20–40 个点的网格上扫描，每个设定下都用上一步的一维搜索把假阳性率固定，并在某一固定鲁棒半径下测量检测能力与可伪造优势。把所有这些工作点对照预测前沿作图，确认无一超越它、且那个显式构造的见证核验器恰好落在其上。作为对照，把真实核验接口替换成一个不泄露任何信息的理想密封 oracle——它只返回接受或拒绝，不给分数、不打开承诺、不暴露内部随机数（泄漏设为零）——同时固定鲁棒半径、假阳性率、keystream 与生成分布，确认在固定伪造成功率下可达检测能力随之升向其零泄漏上限。\n   - _为什么_: 它检验理论最尖锐的预测（没有方案越过曲线），并通过一次干净的开/关干预验证是泄漏 L、而非水印 keystream，在移动曲线。\n\n"},{"id":"39","run_dir":"run_prompt39_graphexch","index":39,"title":"Certified-Exchangeable Retrieval Keys: A Frame-Averaging Budget for Graph Search","title_zh":"可认证可交换检索键：面向图检索的 frame-averaging 稳定性预算（ε-budget）","method_name":"Certified-Exchangeable Keys (CEK)","hook":"Every graph-retrieval encoder pools node features into one key and assumes that key is invariant to relabeling the query's units, yet none of the retrieved systems carries a quantity saying by how much the key actually moves under such an exchange. We construct retrieval keys whose exchange-stability is certified by a frame-averaging budget the index can read, and make the size of that budget a tunable knob matched to how exchangeable the task really is.","anchor_pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","anchor_pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","domain_category":"Graph Learning","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a graph-retrieval key together with a measured certificate of how stable that key is under a content-preserving exchange of the query's units (node relabeling, permutation of the set of triplets/patches/prototypes) — exchange-stability of the key is assumed from the encoder but never quantified at the retrieval layer, so the retrieval system has no quantity reporting by how much recall is at risk from non-invariance. (additive)","pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","sub_pattern":"C16 (Encode Structure by Construction)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by deriving the retrieval key as a frame-average of the encoder over a small structured representative subset of the relabeling group, so exchange-invariance holds by construction, and by reading off — from the residual spread over that frame — an epsilon-stability budget that bounds key drift under any group exchange and is shipped alongside the key into the index.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes the degree to which a query is treated as an unordered exchangeable set (versus an ordered/identity-bearing object) a tunable property of the retrieval key that can be matched to how exchangeable the task actually is — current keys hard-code one symmetry assumption (full invariance via pooling, or none via prototype indexing) rather than letting the needed invariance be a controllable quantity. (additive)","pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by partitioning the query's units, by a measured exchange-sensitivity score, into a small order-bearing minority kept identity-resolved and a near-exchangeable bulk that is frame-averaged, with an error decomposition bounding how this differentiated treatment recovers the fully-invariant key; the partition fraction is the knob that tunes how exchangeable the key is.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"learning on graphs and other geometries & topologies — representation learning for graph retrieval (subgraph/graph-level nearest-neighbor search)","n_papers":36,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":23},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":14,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"LeGalFormer: A Graph Representation Learning and Transformer-based Approach for Legal Similar Case Retrieval"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Intent Distribution based Bipartite Graph Representation Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"unKR: A Python Library for Uncertain Knowledge Graph Reasoning by Representation Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Negative Sampling in Knowledge Graph Representation Learning: A Review"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Soft-Prompting with Graph-of-Thought for Multi-modal Representation Learning"},{"source":"openalex","title":"A Comprehensive Survey on Relation Extraction: Recent Advances and New Frontiers"}],"more":8},{"year":2025,"n":22,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Large-Scale Corpus Retrieval Algorithm Based on Graph Representation Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Retrieval Augmented Generation for Tables in Textual Documents based on Graph Representation Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"LLM-powered scene graph representation learning for image retrieval via visual triplet-based graph transformation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"GraphRAG-R1: Graph Retrieval-Augmented Generation with Process-Constrained Reinforcement Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"LLM-enhanced representation learning for graph collaborative filtering recommendation models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Adversarial Masked Graph Autoencoders for Improved Graph Representation Learning"}],"more":16}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":8,"share":0.222},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":8,"share":0.222},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":7,"share":0.194},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":7,"share":0.194},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":6,"share":0.167},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":5,"share":0.139},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":5,"share":0.139},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":5,"share":0.139}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Across the graph-retrieval literature, the retrieval key for a graph (or subgraph / set of relational units) is produced by an encoder that consumes its constituent units in some concrete order or with concrete node identities, and the resulting single vector is then indexed for nearest-neighbor search — but no retrieved method certifies that this key is actually invariant to the exchanges the task is meant to ignore (relabeling nodes, permuting the set of triplets/patches/prototypes that compose the query). Dissimilarity/prototype-based graph embedding (openalex:W4411547621) builds the key from comparisons against a fixed ordered prototype set, so the key depends on prototype indexing rather than only on the graph's content; similarity/rank-based embedding such as SIGEM (openalex:W4412876877) and graph-based ANN search (openalex:W4409657250) inherit a vector key whose invariance is assumed from the GNN rather than guaranteed at the retrieval layer. The failure is that under a content-preserving exchange of the query's units the key can move, so two presentations of the same graph land at different points in the index and recall degrades — and because the encoder only approximately enforces the symmetry, the retrieval system has no quantity that says by how much, or with what guarantee, the key is exchange-stable.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4411547621","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Builds a graph embedding for supervised classification by comparing each graph against a set of reference patterns (exact vs approximate dissimilarity) and using the vector of dissimilarities as the representation. The residue: the representation is indexed by the chosen, ordered prototype set, so it is not certified invariant to permutation/relabeling of the comparison units — there is no quantity bounding how far the key moves under a content-preserving exchange, which is exactly what a retrieval key needs. [residue is abstract-level: anchor fulltext unfetchable]"},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4412876877","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"SIGEM learns a similarity/rank-preserving graph embedding (LINOW link-based similarity) so that node ranks are preserved in vector space, improving reconstruction/link-prediction/classification. The residue: it preserves node ranking but offers no certificate that the produced retrieval key is invariant to node relabeling or to permutation of the aggregated units, so exchange-stability of the key is assumed, not measured."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4409657250","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"ADA-NNS speeds up graph-based approximate nearest-neighbor search by an angular-distance-guided neighbor-selection rule during traversal, improving QPS at fixed recall. The residue: it treats the per-item key vectors as fixed exogenous inputs and optimizes the search graph over them, so any non-invariance baked into those keys (two presentations of the same graph mapping to different vectors) is invisible to and uncorrectable by the search layer."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4406175894","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"TMGCL adds topology/persistence views to graph contrastive learning so the representation captures multi-scale topological structure for molecular classification. The residue: its contrastive objective targets topological richness, not exchangeability of the retrieval key — the pretext does not penalize, nor measure, drift of the key under permutation/relabeling of the query's units."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"learning on graphs and other geometries & topologies — representation learning for graph retrieval (subgraph/graph-level nearest-neighbor search)","venue":"ICLR 2026","time":"2026","data":["graph/subgraph retrieval benchmarks (e.g., molecular graph retrieval, citation/knowledge subgraph retrieval, scene-graph triplet sets)","standard graph-embedding benchmarks usable for retrieval (node/graph classification + link-prediction repurposed to recall@k)"],"compute":"1×A100 × 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"graph representation learning, retrieval / approximate nearest-neighbor search, group-invariant deep learning","preference":"both","baseline":"GNN / graph-transformer embeddings pooled to a single vector and indexed for nearest-neighbor retrieval (e.g., dissimilarity/prototype-based graph embedding openalex:W4411547621, similarity-based embedding SIGEM openalex:W4412876877), plus graph-based ANN search (ADA-NNS openalex:W4409657250)","limitation":"graph retrieval keys are produced by encoders whose output depends on the (arbitrary) ordering/identity of the elements being aggregated, so the retrieval key is not certified invariant to the symmetries (node relabeling, set permutation of the units that compose a query) the retrieval task is supposed to ignore","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object both legs read from and write to is the EXCHANGE-STABILITY BUDGET epsilon(q) attached to each retrieval key k(q) of a query graph q. Leg 1 (structural_prior_encoding via C16): let G be the relabeling/permutation group acting on q's units (node permutations, or permutations of the set of triplets/patches/prototypes the query is composed of). Instead of computing one pooled vector from a single arbitrary presentation of q, we pick a frame F(q) — a small structured representative subset of G of size m (m a fixed hyperparameter, default m=8; F is selected by a deterministic canonicalization rule, e.g. sort units by a permutation-equivariant scalar score s(u)=w_s^T h(u) where h(u) is the GNN node embedding and w_s a learned projection, then take the m presentations induced by the top-m tie-broken orderings) — and define the key as the frame-average k(q) = (1/m) sum_{g in F(q)} phi(g.q), where phi is any base graph encoder (a message-passing GNN with mean readout). By the frame-averaging construction, k(q) is invariant to any g in G whenever F is a valid G-frame, so invariance holds by construction rather than being relearned. The certificate is computed from the SAME forward pass: epsilon(q) = max_{g in F(q)} || phi(g.q) - k(q) || / ||k(q)||, the normalized radius of the per-presentation spread around the average — a measured upper-bound proxy on how far the key can move under an exchange, shipped into the index as a per-key scalar. epsilon(q) is the auditable invariance quantity the C16 lesson calls for (equivariance measured post hoc as a controllable quantity), NOT plain orbit-averaging used to make a predictor invariant — it is a retrieval-key budget the search layer consumes (queries with large epsilon get an enlarged search radius / candidate re-rank, so non-invariance is corrected rather than silently degrading recall). Leg 2 (heterogeneous_decomposition via C04) operates on the same key: not every query is fully exchangeable — some units carry order/identity signal the task wants kept (e.g. a head entity in a triplet, a canonical anchor patch). We measure each unit's exchange-sensitivity delta(u) = || k(q) - k(q without averaging over u) || (how much the key moves when u is allowed to permute), partition units into a high-sensitivity minority M (top-rho fraction, rho the tunable knob) kept identity-resolved (their positions enter the key through a small order-bearing channel) and a near-exchangeable bulk B that is frame-averaged. An error decomposition writes the deviation of this differentiated key from the fully-invariant key as a sum of per-partition residuals bounded by epsilon-over-B plus a controlled minority term, so the bound certifies that differentiated treatment recovers the invariant key up to the chosen rho — and rho directly tunes how exchangeable the key is (rho=0 recovers full frame-averaging, rho=1 recovers an order-bearing key). Both legs share the budget epsilon as their central primitive: leg 1 produces and certifies it, leg 2 controls how much of the group the key quotients by, reported as a (rho, epsilon) pair per key. Quantitatively, prior retrieval keys (openalex:W4411547621 prototype-indexed; openalex:W4412876877 rank-preserving) report no such budget — their abstracts claim invariance is inherited from the encoder; we MEASURE epsilon and show it is non-zero for learned pooled encoders, which is the gap they leave open.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery because both are about the same object — the retrieval key and its exchange group — so I centered both on one shared scalar (epsilon) rather than two modules: leg 1 constructs+certifies the key, leg 2 controls the quotient depth of the same key, evidenced by the fact that rho=0 makes leg 2 collapse into leg 1's fully-averaged key (they are the same construction at two settings of one knob). (b) I considered a contrastive/SSL design (targeted_self_supervised_objective) that trains the key to be invariant under augmentation, but that only makes invariance statistical and gives no per-key certificate — exactly the residue of the retrieved SSL papers — so it would not close the 'measured budget' gap; I also rejected plain group-averaging-as-predictor and test-time relabel-averaging (collateral nodes c0/c1 in method_lineage) because they wash out order without producing a budget the index can act on, which is the avoided regression node recorded here.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: take a graph-retrieval benchmark (molecular graph retrieval and a knowledge-subgraph retrieval set), index keys with (i) a standard pooled GNN encoder, (ii) prototype-indexed embedding, and (iii) our frame-averaged certified key, then measure recall@10 both on canonically-presented queries AND on queries to which K random content-preserving relabelings have been applied. If the candidate works, the relabeling-robustness curve (recall@10 as K grows) stays flat for our key while dropping for baselines (i)/(ii), and overall recall@10 does not regress on canonical queries. The named load-bearing variable is the per-key exchange-stability budget epsilon(q): the mechanism claim is that epsilon predicts and governs recall loss under exchange. Negative control: replace the measured epsilon with a constant (or shuffle epsilon across keys, breaking its tie to the query) while keeping the frame-averaged keys unchanged — the search layer can no longer expand the radius for the truly unstable keys, and the predicted effect is that recall@10 under relabeling falls back toward the pooled-encoder baseline (the DOWNSTREAM task metric, not epsilon's own value, moves). Positive control: a stripped-down system that keeps ONLY the epsilon-driven radius expansion on top of plain pooled keys (no frame averaging) should recover most of the relabeling-robustness gain, identifying epsilon as the carrier of the effect.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4411547621","delta":"They construct the retrieval representation as a vector of dissimilarities to an ordered prototype set with no quantity bounding key movement under permutation/relabeling; we construct the key as a frame-average that is invariant by construction AND derive a per-key epsilon-budget bounding its exchange-drift, which their prototype-indexed representation cannot produce."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4412876877","delta":"SIGEM preserves a global node-similarity ranking in the embedding but offers no certificate of key invariance under relabeling; we add a measured, index-readable exchange-stability budget and an error-decomposition bound, neither of which a rank-preserving objective yields."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4409657250","delta":"ADA-NNS optimizes search-graph traversal over fixed key vectors and is blind to any non-invariance baked into them; we make the keys' invariance a measured per-key scalar the search layer consumes to expand the radius for unstable keys, correcting non-invariance the traversal layer alone cannot see."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4406175894","delta":"TMGCL enriches keys with multi-scale topological views via a contrastive pretext but only makes invariance statistical; we provide a by-construction invariance plus a deterministic budget, and a tunable rho controlling quotient depth, which their pretext does not expose."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4411547621","what_step_was_missed":"Their dissimilarity-based embedding builds the retrieval key from comparisons against a fixed, ordered prototype set; to already be our contribution they would have needed to (a) replace the ordered prototype indexing with a frame-average over the relabeling group so the key is permutation-invariant by construction, and (b) derive from that same frame the per-key normalized spread radius (the epsilon-budget) as a shipped certificate of exchange-stability — neither the invariance-by-construction step nor the budget-derivation step exists in a dissimilarity-to-prototypes formulation."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":365,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"No hard-floor rule fired: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict is 'borderline' (no Reject lesson marked candidate_match:yes), anti_pattern_check matched audit_decomp_prior but mitigation_substantively_delivered=true (rho=0 isolation + positive control + leg-2 error decomposition deliver the required differential ablation and a prior-distinct property), and paper_pointed_threat=no_threat_found with no exact-mechanism overlap. recipe_application_check.verdict='applied' for both entries, so the idea was built from the cited cluster moves rather than the parent's generic gist. The two borderline gap-closure lessons (C16 directional-signal washing; C04 sensitivity-proxy framing) are mitigated in-mechanism by the identity-resolved minority and the new invariant-key-recovery objective respectively, hitting no fatal load-bearing flaw — so advance with both concerns surfaced for Phase 4 reviewer_concerns_and_responses.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a graph-retrieval key together with a measured certificate of how stable that key is under a content-preserving exchange of the query's units (node relabeling, permutation of the set of triplets/patches/prototypes) — exchange-stability of the key is assumed from the encoder but never quantified at the retrieval layer, so the retrieval system has no quantity reporting by how much recall is at risk from non-invariance. (additive)","main_pattern":"structural_prior_encoding","sub_pattern":"C16 (Encode Structure by Construction)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The most common structural flaw is presenting a symmetry construction that is a special case or simple variation of existing equivariant machinery whose operator basis is never shown to be complete, so reviewers read it as expressivity-limiting rather than novel. Related shapes are the correct-but-unmotivated result (no real downstream application) and the symmetry-enforcing shortcut that silently breaks a property the task depends on.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A layer that relaxes a global symmetry constraint to a subgroup may gain expressivity on paper, but without a proof that the resulting operator family is complete it is dismissed as a special case of known techniques.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate does NOT relax to a subgroup as its headline; the frame F(q) is a valid G-frame so k(q) is invariant to the full relabeling group by construction, and the tunable rho-partition is an explicit second axis (leg 2) with its own error-decomposition bound rather than a silent subgroup relaxation."},{"lesson_quoted":"A correct and novel group-theoretic result presented without proofs and without a developed real-world application reads as 'mathematics in search of a problem,' no matter how clean the algebra.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The construction is bound to a concrete retrieval payoff a generic model cannot get for free — the epsilon-budget is consumed by the search layer to expand the candidate radius for unstable keys, raising recall@k under relabeling, with a falsification experiment on molecular and knowledge-subgraph retrieval."},{"lesson_quoted":"A unified symmetry-invariant representation that serves many tasks from a single set of parameters but fails to beat any specialized baseline on any task turns its own versatility into the decisive weakness.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate targets one property (relabeling-robust recall) against named specialized baselines (pooled-GNN, prototype-indexed, ADA-NNS) and predicts a strict win on the relabeling-robustness curve, not a one-size-fits-all representation."},{"lesson_quoted":"A symmetry-enforcing shortcut that breaks a property the downstream objective silently depends on — differentiability, smoothness, directional signal — gets rejected even when it is faster and provably respects the target symmetry.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"Frame-averaging via a deterministic canonicalization (sort by s(u)) can introduce non-differentiable tie-breaks and could wash out order/directional signal — but leg 2 explicitly preserves order-bearing units (minority M kept identity-resolved) precisely to avoid discarding directional signal, so the concern is surfaced but mitigated by construction rather than triggered."},{"lesson_quoted":"Symmetry-exploiting augmentation that requires bespoke per-problem symmetry analysis is read as narrow engineering rather than a transferable method, capping its perceived generality.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The relabeling/permutation group is the generic symmetry of any set-structured query (nodes, triplets, patches, prototypes); the frame-average + epsilon-budget recipe is task-agnostic and not a bespoke per-problem symmetry derivation."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes the degree to which a query is treated as an unordered exchangeable set (versus an ordered/identity-bearing object) a tunable property of the retrieval key that can be matched to how exchangeable the task actually is — current keys hard-code one symmetry assumption (full invariance via pooling, or none via prototype indexing) rather than letting the needed invariance be a controllable quantity. (additive)","main_pattern":"heterogeneous_decomposition","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is treating the partition criterion itself as the contribution while leaving its value unproven — a sensitivity/redundancy proxy that reviewers map onto an established technique, rarely benchmarked against both the strongest uniform baseline and the obvious cheap alternative. A second shortcut is validating in a regime where the bottleneck does not bite (toy scale, proxy-only metrics, no measured deployment gain).","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Presenting a sensitivity or redundancy proxy as the novelty invites the verdict that it rediscovers known mixed-precision or low-rank results unless it is sharply differentiated from the obvious prior criterion.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The partition criterion delta(u) (per-unit exchange-sensitivity) is the discriminating property and could read as a generic sensitivity proxy; it is differentiated by being tied to a NEW objective (recovering the fully-invariant key within a certified epsilon-budget) rather than to compression error, but the novelty leans partly on the criterion so the lesson is non-trivially in play."},{"lesson_quoted":"Omitting comparison against both the strongest uniform baseline and the obvious cheap alternative (SVD/PCA, structured dropout, a natively trained smaller model) leaves reviewers unable to tell whether the partition buys anything at all.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The falsification plan compares against the strongest uniform baseline (rho=0 full frame-averaging, i.e. full pooling) AND the obvious cheap alternative (prototype-indexed, and the positive-control plain-pooled-key + epsilon-radius variant), so the uniform-vs-differentiated comparison is present."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a storage or throughput claim only on toy-scale models — where the compression bottleneck does not actually bite — undermines the entire motivation no matter how clean the method is.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The bottleneck (recall loss under relabeling) is validated on real graph-retrieval benchmarks via the relabeling-robustness curve and recall@10, the true deployment metric, not a toy proxy."},{"lesson_quoted":"Skipping any analysis of why the heterogeneity exists — the data or value distribution that drives the partition — makes the technical novelty and the potential impact impossible to assess.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The heterogeneity is named and measured: some units carry order/identity signal the task wants kept (head entity in a triplet, anchor patch) while the bulk is near-exchangeable, and delta(u) is the measured value distribution that drives the partition."},{"lesson_quoted":"Bolting together established components (distillation plus pruning plus calibration) without an error bound or artifact specific to the new setting reads as incremental even when the target application is timely and important.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate supplies the load-bearing artifact the card demands — an error decomposition ||k_rho - k_0|| <= residual_B(epsilon) + minority_term(rho) bounding how the differentiated key recovers the fully-invariant key — which is specific to the exchangeable-retrieval setting, not bolted-together off-the-shelf parts."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No entry triggered: every Reject lesson marked candidate_match:yes is absent. Two borderlines drive the aggregate — the C16 differentiability/directional-signal lesson (frame-averaging via canonicalization could wash out order, but leg 2's identity-resolved minority mitigates it) and the C04 sensitivity-proxy lesson (delta(u) could read as a generic sensitivity proxy, but it is tied to the new invariant-key-recovery objective). Both are mitigated in-mechanism and neither hits a fatal load-bearing flaw."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a graph-retrieval key together with a measured certificate of how stable that key is under a content-preserving exchange of the query's units (node relabeling, permutation of the set of triplets/patches/prototypes) — exchange-stability of the key is assumed from the encoder but never quantified at the retrieval layer, so the retrieval system has no quantity reporting by how much recall is at risk from non-invariance. (additive)","sub_pattern":"C16 (Encode Structure by Construction)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Identify the symmetry group genuinely acting on the data and construct operators that commute with the group action exactly by construction — group-averaging over a structured representative frame — so the invariant property is certified analytically rather than approximated by augmentation; the Oral lesson extends this to reframing equivariance from a hard constraint into a controllable, auditable quantity measured post hoc.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"Steps 2-4 perform exactly this signature move: the relabeling/permutation group G is pinned down, a frame F(q) is built as a 'small structured representative subset of G' via deterministic equivariant-score canonicalization, the key k(q) is the frame-average (1/m) sum phi(g.q) so invariance holds by construction (matching the Oral lesson 'a tiny structured subset of an intractable transformation family can replace averaging over the whole family'), and epsilon(q) is the post-hoc measured spread radius — instantiating the Oral lesson that equivariance becomes 'a controllable, auditable quantity' rather than plain orbit-averaging-as-predictor.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes the degree to which a query is treated as an unordered exchangeable set (versus an ordered/identity-bearing object) a tunable property of the retrieval key that can be matched to how exchangeable the task actually is — current keys hard-code one symmetry assumption (full invariance via pooling, or none via prototype indexing) rather than letting the needed invariance be a controllable quantity. (additive)","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Discriminate components by a magnitude/sensitivity/influence criterion into a high-impact minority and a near-redundant bulk, then preserve/retain-at-full-fidelity the minority while aggressively operating on the bulk; the load-bearing artifact is an error/sensitivity decomposition that bounds how the differentiated treatment recovers the original objective — that analysis, not the partition idea, is the contribution.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"Steps 6-7 and 9 perform the signature move: delta(u) is the per-unit exchange-sensitivity criterion (leave-one-out over the frame), units are partitioned into a high-sensitivity minority M kept identity-resolved (retained at full order-bearing fidelity) and a near-exchangeable bulk B that is frame-averaged (the aggressive invariantizing operation), and step 9 supplies the load-bearing error decomposition ||k_rho - k_0|| <= residual_B(epsilon) + minority_term(rho) bounding how the differentiated key recovers the fully-invariant key — the card's required spine, not just the partition.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries instantiate their cluster's distinctive move: C16's frame-averaging-as-auditable-quantity is performed in steps 2-4 (frame construction + post-hoc epsilon), and C04's discriminate-then-bound is performed in steps 6-7-9 with the mandatory error decomposition as the spine, so neither was built from the parent's generic gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["structural_prior_encoding","heterogeneous_decomposition"],"matched_pattern_id":"audit_decomp_prior","required_mitigation_quoted":"An ablation that turns off either the decomposition or the prior in isolation must show a clear differential effect (not just a smaller combined number). Theoretically, the prior must encode a property the decomposition does not already imply — otherwise the two are doing the same job.","mitigation_substantively_delivered":"true","reasoning":"The core_mechanism delivers both halves at the artifact level: rho=0 isolates the prior (pure frame-average key, no decomposition) and the positive control isolates the prior's epsilon-radius effect on plain pooled keys, while leg 2's error decomposition (residual_B(epsilon) + minority_term(rho)) isolates the decomposition's effect — and theoretically the prior encodes a distinct property (the epsilon exchange-drift bound shipped into the index) that the rho-partition does not already imply, so the two axes are not doing the same job."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"no_threat_found","threat_source":"n/a","subsumption_argument":null,"addressable_via":null}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Certified-Exchangeable Retrieval Keys: A Frame-Averaging Stability Budget for Graph Search\n\n**Method.** Certified-Exchangeable Keys (CEK)\n\n## Motivation\nGraph search systems turn each graph into a single fingerprint vector (the 'key') and then find similar graphs by looking for nearby keys. The catch: a graph has no natural ordering of its parts — you can rename its nodes, or shuffle the list of pieces (relationships, patches, prototypes) that describe it, without changing what the graph means. The search is supposed to ignore these harmless re-orderings. But the encoder (the neural network that builds the key, here a GNN — Graph Neural Network) only roughly respects that; in practice the same graph presented two different ways can produce two slightly different keys, land in two different spots in the index, and miss its true match. Worse, the system never measures how big this problem is for any given query.\n\nRecent graph-retrieval methods sidestep rather than fix this. Prototype-based embedding (openalex:W4411547621) compares each graph to a fixed, ordered list of reference patterns, so the key depends on that ordering. SIGEM (openalex:W4412876877) preserves how nodes rank against each other but never certifies the key is unchanged under renaming. ADA-NNS (openalex:W4409657250) makes the search itself faster but treats the keys as given, so it cannot see or fix any instability inside them.\n\nOur idea: build the key by averaging the encoder over a small, carefully chosen set of equivalent presentations of the same graph (called frame-averaging), which makes the key provably unchanged under re-ordering. The same computation hands us a free by-product: how much the individual presentations disagreed before averaging. We turn that disagreement into a per-key 'stability budget' $\\epsilon (q)$ and store it next to the key. At search time, keys with a large $\\epsilon $ get a wider search net so their true matches are not missed. A second knob, $\\rho ,$ lets us keep a few genuinely order-carrying parts identity-resolved while averaging the rest, so we can dial exactly how much re-ordering to ignore — and we prove this dialed key stays close to the fully order-blind key.\n\nWhen this works, robustness to re-ordering stops being a silent gamble and becomes a measured, tunable guarantee: existing prototype and rank-based keys become a special case, and pure-speed search methods gain the missing signal $(\\epsilon )$ they need to correct instability they currently cannot detect.\n\n## Method\n### Background encoder\n*Standard GNN that produces per-unit and pooled embeddings, reused unchanged.*\n\n1. Run a standard Graph Neural Network (GNN) — by default a 3-layer Graph Isomorphism Network (GIN) with mean pooling, hidden size 256 — on the query graph to get a 256-dimensional embedding h(u) for each unit and one pooled vector for the current presentation. A 'unit' is whatever the harmless re-ordering shuffles: a node for an ordinary graph, a relationship triplet for a knowledge-subgraph, or a patch/prototype token for a set-of-pieces query.\n   - _Why_: We reuse a standard encoder so the new contribution is what we build on top, not a new network.\n\n### Certified-invariant key + budget\n*Build the relabeling-invariant key by frame-averaging and read off the per-key stability budget $\\epsilon $ from the same frame.*\n\n2. Give each unit a score s(u) $= w_{s} \\cdot $ h(u) using a learned projection $w_{s},$ sort the units by this score, and pick the m=8 presentations produced by the deterministic orderings consistent with that sort (any remaining ties broken by a fixed secondary key so the choice is reproducible). This set of 8 equivalent presentations is the 'frame' that stands in for averaging over all possible re-orderings. 【author decision: the authors must state the exact rule for building the frame (full canonical ordering vs. a representative subset) under which averaging the encoder over the frame is exactly unchanged by re-ordering — this invariance guarantee is theirs to fix.】\n   - _Why_: A small, well-chosen set of equivalent presentations stands in for averaging over the astronomically many possible re-orderings.\n3. Encode all 8 presentations in a single batched pass of the GNN and average their pooled vectors elementwise to get the retrieval key (Eq. 1). Averaging over a valid set of equivalent presentations is what makes this key provably unchanged when the graph's units are re-ordered; store it in the approximate-nearest-neighbor (ANN) index.\n\n*The retrieval key is the frame-average of the base encoder $\\phi $ over the m presentations in the frame F(q); averaging over a valid group-frame makes k(q) invariant to the relabeling group by construction.*\n$$ k(q) = \\frac{1}{m} \\sum_{g \\in F(q)} \\phi(g \\cdot q) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Averaging over a valid set of equivalent presentations makes the key provably unchanged under re-ordering.\n4. From those same 8 encodings, compute the stability budget $\\epsilon (q)$ — the largest normalized gap between any single presentation and the average (Eq. 2) — and save it as one extra number attached to the key in the index, so the search step can read it without recomputing anything.\n\n*The exchange-stability budget $\\epsilon (q)$ is the largest normalized distance from any single presentation's encoding to the averaged key — a measured per-key proxy for how far the key can drift under exchange.*\n$$ \\varepsilon(q) = \\max_{g \\in F(q)} \\frac{\\lVert \\phi(g \\cdot q) - k(q) \\rVert}{\\lVert k(q) \\rVert} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The leftover disagreement after averaging is a free, honest measure of how shaky this particular key is.\n\n### Budget-aware search\n*Make the index consume $\\epsilon $ to widen the search radius for unstable keys and recover their true matches.*\n\n5. When answering a query, first pull a candidate list of size $10\\times k,$ then widen it to about $(1+\\epsilon (q))$ times that size for queries whose stored stability budget is large, and finally re-rank the widened list by exact key distance to return the top-k. Spending more search effort exactly where the key is shaky recovers correct matches that would otherwise be missed.\n   - _Why_: Spending extra search effort exactly where the key is unstable recovers true matches that drift would otherwise hide.\n\n### Tunable exchangeability\n*Measure per-unit exchange-sensitivity and build $a \\rho -tunable$ key with a certified recovery bound.*\n\n6. Measure each unit's exchange-sensitivity $\\delta (u)$ (Eq. 3): redo the averaged key but keep that one unit pinned to a fixed position while still re-ordering the others, and take the distance between this pinned-unit key and the original key. A large value means the unit really carries order/identity information.\n\n*The exchange-sensitivity $\\delta (u)$ of a unit u is how much the key moves when u is left out of the frame-average (leave-one-out over the frame); it drives the partition into order-bearing minority and exchangeable bulk.*\n$$ \\delta(u) = \\lVert k(q) - k_{\\setminus u}(q) \\rVert \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: It tells us which parts genuinely carry order/identity and which are interchangeable.\n7. Keep the most order-carrying units (the $top-\\rho $ fraction by sensitivity) identity-resolved — encode each by adding a learned position embedding to its features and pooling them separately — and frame-average the rest; the tunable key joins the two parts. The bound in Eq. (4) certifies this tunable key stays close to the fully order-blind key, splitting the gap into a bulk part and a minority part that grows with $\\rho .$ 【author decision: the authors must fix the exact form of the minority part that makes the Eq. (4) bound tight.】\n\n*The error decomposition bounds the deviation of the tunable key $k_\\rho $ from the fully-invariant key $k_{0}$ by a bulk residual controlled by $\\epsilon $ plus a minority term controlled by $\\rho ,$ certifying that the differentiated treatment recovers the invariant key up to the chosen $\\rho .$*\n$$ \\lVert k_{\\rho}(q) - k_{0}(q) \\rVert \\leq \\mathrm{res}_{B}(\\varepsilon) + \\mathrm{min}(\\rho) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: $\\rho $ becomes a dial for exactly how much re-ordering to ignore, with a proof it does not stray from the invariant key.\n\n### Retrieval fine-tuning\n*Train the encoder for retrieval while keeping the certified operations fixed.*\n\n8. Fine-tune the GNN weights and the scoring projection using a contrastive loss (InfoNCE, temperature 0.07): treat known-equivalent graph pairs as positives (e.g. the same graph re-ordered two different ways) and other graphs in the batch as negatives, and update only those weights — the averaging, the budget, and the sensitivity stay fixed and are not trained. The encoder learns to retrieve well while the guarantees stay intact.\n   - _Why_: The network learns to retrieve well while the guarantees (invariance, budget, bound) stay deterministic and intact.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 可认证可交换检索键：面向图检索的 frame-averaging 稳定性预算（ε-budget）\n\n**方法名称.** Certified-Exchangeable Keys (CEK)\n\n## 研究动机\n图检索系统把每个图压成一个指纹向量（即“键”），再通过寻找邻近的键来找相似的图。问题在于：图的各个部分本来就没有天然顺序——你可以给它的节点重命名，或打乱描述它的那些片段（关系、patch、prototype）的排列顺序，而这并不改变图的含义。检索本应忽略这些无害的重排。但构造键的编码器（这里是 GNN，即图神经网络）只是大致地满足这一点；实际上同一个图以两种不同方式呈现，会得到两个略有差异的键，落在索引中两个不同位置，从而错过它真正的匹配。更糟的是，系统从不度量对某个具体查询而言这个问题有多严重。\n\n最近的图检索方法是在回避而非解决这一点。基于 prototype 的嵌入（openalex:W4411547621）把每个图与一组固定且有序的参考模式比较，于是键依赖于这个顺序。SIGEM（openalex:W4412876877）保留了节点之间的相对排名，却从不认证键在重命名下保持不变。ADA-NNS（openalex:W4409657250）让搜索本身更快，但把键当作给定输入，因此看不到、也修不了键内部的不稳定性。\n\n我们的想法是：通过把编码器在同一个图的一小组精心挑选的等价呈现上求平均（称为 frame-averaging）来构造键，从而使键在重排下可证明地保持不变。同一次计算还附带一个免费的副产品：在求平均之前这些单独呈现之间的分歧有多大。我们把这个分歧变成逐键的“稳定性预算” $\\epsilon (q)$，并把它存在键旁边。检索时，$\\epsilon $ 较大的键会获得更宽的搜索范围，使其真正的匹配不被遗漏。第二个旋钮 $\\rho $ 让我们把少数确实带有顺序信息的部分保持 identity-resolved，而对其余部分求平均，于是可以精确调节要忽略多少重排——并且我们证明这种调节后的键与完全无序键保持接近。\n\n当这套方法奏效时，对重排的鲁棒性不再是一场无声的赌博，而成为一个可度量、可调节的保证：现有的 prototype 与基于排名的键成为其特例，而纯追求速度的搜索方法也获得了它们当前无法检测、却用来纠正不稳定性所需的那个信号 $\\epsilon $。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景编码器\n*标准 GNN，产出逐单元与 pooled 嵌入，原样复用。*\n\n1. 在查询图上运行一个标准的图神经网络(Graph Neural Network, GNN)——默认是带 mean pooling 的 3 层图同构网络(Graph Isomorphism Network, GIN)，隐藏维度 256——为每个单元得到一个 256 维嵌入 h(u)，并得到当前呈现下的一个 pooled 向量。这里的“单元”就是无害重排所打乱的对象：普通图中是节点，知识子图中是关系三元组(triplet)，片段集合查询中是 patch 或 prototype token。\n   - _为什么_: 复用标准编码器，使新贡献体现在其上的构造，而非一个新网络。\n\n### 可认证不变键 + 预算\n*用 frame-averaging 构造对重标注不变的键，并从同一 frame 读出逐键稳定性预算 $\\epsilon $。*\n\n2. 用一个可学习的投影 $w_{s}$ 给每个单元打分 s(u) $= w_{s} \\cdot $ h(u)，按该分数排序，再选出与该排序一致的确定性排序所给出的 m=8 个呈现（剩余的并列用一个固定的次级键打破，使选择可复现）。这 8 个等价呈现构成的集合就是 frame，用来替代对所有可能重排求平均。【作者需决定：作者须明确构建 frame 的确切规则（完整规范排序还是一个代表性子集），使得编码器在该 frame 上的平均对重排完全不变——这个不变性保证由作者确定。】\n   - _为什么_: 一小组精心挑选的等价呈现，可替代对天文数字般多的重排求平均。\n3. 把全部 8 个呈现放进 GNN 的一次批处理前向传播来编码，并对它们的 pooled 向量逐元素求平均，得到检索键(Eq. 1)。在一组合法等价呈现上求平均，正是使这个键在图的单元被重排时可证明保持不变的原因；将它存入近似最近邻(Approximate Nearest Neighbor, ANN)索引。\n\n*检索键 k(q) 是基础编码器 $\\phi $ 在 frame F(q) 中 m 个呈现上的平均；对一个合法的群 frame 求平均，使 k(q) 在构造上对重标注群保持不变。*\n$$ k(q) = \\frac{1}{m} \\sum_{g \\in F(q)} \\phi(g \\cdot q) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 在一组合法的等价呈现上求平均，使键在重排下可证明地保持不变。\n4. 用同样这 8 个编码计算稳定性预算 $\\epsilon (q)——$任一单一呈现与平均之间最大的归一化差距(Eq. 2)——并把它作为一个额外的数字附在索引中该键旁边，使检索步骤无需重新计算即可读取它。\n\n*交换稳定性预算 $\\epsilon (q)$ 是任一单一呈现的编码到平均键之间最大的归一化距离——一个可度量的、逐键的指标，刻画键在交换下可能的漂移幅度。*\n$$ \\varepsilon(q) = \\max_{g \\in F(q)} \\frac{\\lVert \\phi(g \\cdot q) - k(q) \\rVert}{\\lVert k(q) \\rVert} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 平均之后残留的分歧，是一个免费而诚实的指标，反映这个键有多不稳。\n\n### 预算感知搜索\n*让索引消费 $\\epsilon $，为不稳定的键放大搜索半径以找回其真正匹配。*\n\n5. 回答查询时，先取一个大小为 $10\\times k$ 的候选列表，再对那些所存稳定性预算较大的查询，把列表扩大到约 $(1+\\epsilon (q))$ 倍，最后用精确的键距离对扩大后的列表重排序，返回 top-k。把更多搜索开销恰好花在键不稳之处，可找回原本会被遗漏的正确匹配。\n   - _为什么_: 把额外搜索开销恰好花在键不稳之处，可找回会被漂移掩盖的真正匹配。\n\n### 可调可交换性\n*度量逐单元交换敏感度，并构造带可认证恢复界的 $\\rho -$可调键。*\n\n6. 度量每个单元的交换敏感度 $\\delta (u)(Eq.$ 3)：重新计算平均键，但把那个单元固定在一个位置而仍然重排其余单元，并取这个“固定单元”键与原键之间的距离。值越大，说明该单元确实携带顺序/身份信息。\n\n*单元 u 的交换敏感度 $\\delta (u)$ 是将 u 从 frame 平均中留一剔除时键的移动量；它驱动把单元划分为带序的少数与可交换的多数。*\n$$ \\delta(u) = \\lVert k(q) - k_{\\setminus u}(q) \\rVert \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 它告诉我们哪些部分确实带有顺序/身份信息，哪些是可互换的。\n7. 把最带顺序的单元（按敏感度排前 $\\rho $ 比例）保持 identity-resolved——为每个单元在其特征上加一个可学习的位置嵌入并单独 pooling——而对其余单元做 frame-average；可调键把这两部分拼接起来。Eq. (4) 的界保证这个可调键与完全无序键保持接近，并把差距拆成一个多数部分和一个随 $\\rho $ 增大的少数部分。【作者需决定：作者须确定使 Eq. (4) 的界变紧的少数项的确切函数形式。】\n\n*误差分解将可调键 $k_\\rho $ 与完全不变键 $k_{0}$ 之间的偏差，界定为由 $\\epsilon $ 控制的多数残差项加上由 $\\rho $ 控制的少数项，从而证明这种差异化处理在所选 $\\rho $ 范围内可恢复不变键。*\n$$ \\lVert k_{\\rho}(q) - k_{0}(q) \\rVert \\leq \\mathrm{res}_{B}(\\varepsilon) + \\mathrm{min}(\\rho) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: $\\rho $ 成为精确调节“忽略多少重排”的旋钮，并附带它不偏离不变键的证明。\n\n### 检索微调\n*训练编码器以适配检索，同时保持可认证操作固定。*\n\n8. 用对比损失(InfoNCE, 温度 0.07)微调 GNN 权重与打分投影：把已知等价的图对当作正样本（例如同一个图的两种不同重排），把同一批中的其他图当作负样本，并只更新这些权重——平均、预算与敏感度保持固定且不参与训练。编码器学会良好检索，而各项保证保持完好。\n   - _为什么_: 网络学会检索得更好，而各项保证（不变性、预算、界）保持确定且完好。\n\n"},{"id":"40","run_dir":"run_prompt40_saence","index":40,"title":"Mediated Feature Effects: Exploratory Causal Graphs over Sparse-Autoencoder Latents","title_zh":"中介特征效应：在 Sparse Autoencoder 隐变量上进行探索性因果图发现","method_name":"Mediated Feature Effects (MFE)","hook":"An SAE latent's interpretability is today certified correlationally, yet the same auto-interp scores cannot tell a trained transformer from a randomly-initialized one (openalex:W4406975755) — so we replace the latent's meaning with a controlled-direct-effect estimand that asks, for an ordered latent pair, whether one feature acts on the output directly or only through the other, and amortize the O(d^2)-pair search so the feature-feature causal graph is discoverable under a fixed intervention budget.","anchor_pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","anchor_pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","domain_category":"Interpretability & Representation Analysis","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a quantity that, for a pair of SAE latents, distinguishes a direct causal contribution to the output from one that is fully routed through a second latent — every interpretability signal (correlational labelling and isolated single-latent patching alike) is measured on one latent against the output without conditioning on the state of the others, so feature-to-feature mediation is invisible.","pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by reformulating 'what does latent i causally do' as a controlled-direct-effect estimand over the sparse feature basis: the natural-direct-effect (NDE) and total-effect (TE) of a do-intervention on latent i's decoder direction, measured once with latent j held free and once with j clamped to its baseline, whose difference is the through-j mediated component — a per-pair responsibility number certified by intervention rather than by correlation.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides a falsifiable, intervention-based certificate that a named SAE latent is load-bearing rather than spurious; the frontier diagnoses that correlational auto-interp fails to separate trained-from-random transformers (openalex:W4406975755) but offers no positive interventional criterion to replace it.","pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by a confound-isolating instrument whose single controlled axis is causal-load: the same SAE+probe pipeline is run on a trained model and on weight-randomized / activation-shuffled controls, with independent ground truth coming from the construction (a randomized model's latents have no load-bearing computation to mediate), and the headline is the divergence — a latent's TE and its mediated-edge weights collapse to the null band under randomization while genuine ones persist.","is_anchor":false},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf addresses how to SEARCH the combinatorially large space of candidate feature-feature relations under a realistic intervention budget — the single-latent frameworks (openalex:W4415248346) sweep latents one at a time, which does not scale to discovering structure across an overcomplete dictionary, leaving exploratory (hypothesis-generating) causal analysis of SAE features unsupported.","pattern_id":"relax_discrete_search_to_continuous","pattern_name":"Relax Discrete Search to Continuous","sub_pattern":"C22 (Relax Discrete Search to Continuous)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by treating the discrete edge set {(i,j)} as a search variable and amortizing it: a lightweight learned edge-scorer reads cheap observational features of each pair (co-activation, decoder-direction cosine, gradient-of-j-w.r.t.-i) and outputs an acquisition score that ranks which pairs to actually intervene on, so a fixed budget of B interventions is spent on the highest-probability mediated edges instead of an exhaustive O(d^2) sweep, with the scorer updated online from realized NDE/TE outcomes.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"mechanistic interpretability of neural representations via sparse autoencoders (SAEs)","n_papers":34,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":23},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":13,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Enhancing NMF-Based Community Detection via A Higher-Order Proximity-Incorporated Graph Attention Autoencoder"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"VISTA: A Panoramic View of Neural Representations"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Enhancing Neural Network Interpretability with Feature-Aligned Sparse Autoencoders"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Prediction of optical properties of oxide glass combined with autoencoder and machine learning"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Disentangling Dense Embeddings with Sparse Autoencoders"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Deep Learning for Time Series Anomaly Detection: A Survey"}],"more":7},{"year":2025,"n":23,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Interpretable unsupervised neural network structure for data clustering via differentiable reconstruction of ONMF and sparse autoencoder"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"An Explainable AI Framework Integrating Variational Sparse Autoencoder and Random Forest for EEG-Based Epilepsy Detection"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Data Whitening Improves Sparse Autoencoder Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Feature Integration Spaces: Joint Training Reveals Dual Encoding in Neural Network Representations"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"The Deepfake Detective: Interpreting Neural Forensics Through Sparse Features and Manifolds"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Superposition as Lossy Compression: Measure with Sparse Autoencoders and Connect to Adversarial Vulnerability"}],"more":17}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot; architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"assumption_audit_and_pivot; architectural_operator_substitution","count":2,"share":0.059},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object; controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"reframe_as_solvable_object; controlled_diagnostic_design","count":2,"share":0.059},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design; assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"controlled_diagnostic_design; assumption_audit_and_pivot","count":2,"share":0.059},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding; reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"structural_prior_encoding; reframe_as_solvable_object","count":1,"share":0.029},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution; unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"architectural_operator_substitution; unify_into_shared_representation","count":1,"share":0.029},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot; heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"assumption_audit_and_pivot; heterogeneous_decomposition","count":1,"share":0.029},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design; architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"controlled_diagnostic_design; architectural_operator_substitution","count":1,"share":0.029},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution; targeted_self_supervised_objective","pattern_name":"architectural_operator_substitution; targeted_self_supervised_objective","count":1,"share":0.029}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Across the retrieved SAE-interpretability frontier, a latent's 'meaning' is established by correlational evidence — it is named by the inputs it co-activates with or by an LLM-generated explanation graded on activation prediction (openalex:W4417275958, openalex:W4406975755) — and these correlational labels demonstrably fail to separate trained from randomly-initialized transformers (openalex:W4406975755), so a high interpretability score does not establish that a latent carries a load-bearing, manipulable role in the computation. Where causal evidence is introduced at all, it is delivered one latent at a time: the closest framework (openalex:W4415248346) applies input manipulation, latent-perturbation, activation patching and single-node causal-mediation to individual latents of a VAE, and even the SAE works that note structure beyond linear superposition (semanticscholar:5b9818aea1e46fa4974f2b5fb9194096cc269793) capture feature interactions as a residual-prediction object rather than as an intervention-validated relation. The result is a concrete gap: when a feature's downstream effect actually flows THROUGH other features (one latent gates, suppresses, or is a precondition for another), no current SAE method produces a quantity that distinguishes 'A directly affects the output' from 'A affects the output only via B', because every measurement — correlational labelling and isolated single-latent patching alike — is computed on one latent against the output and never conditions on the state of the other latents.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415248346","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Builds the first general multi-level causal-intervention framework for generative-model mechanistic interpretability (input manipulation, latent-space perturbation, activation patching, single-node causal mediation) and defines causal-effect-strength metrics, applied to VAE latents. Its residue: every intervention probes a single latent's effect on the OUTPUT in isolation — it never conditions on or mediates THROUGH other latents, so it recovers per-latent effect magnitudes but not the feature-to-feature causal graph; it is also continuous-latent-VAE-specific (its own method section flags continuous-intervention metrics collapse to near-zero on discrete latents), leaving SAE dictionaries — high-dimensional, sparse, overcomplete — entirely outside its tested regime."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4406975755","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Shows commonly-used SAE auto-interpretability metrics and explanation pipelines assign similar scores to SAEs trained on trained vs. randomly-initialized transformers, exposing that correlational auto-interp does not certify a latent is meaningful. Its residue: it diagnoses the failure of correlational scoring but proposes no positive substitute — it does not supply a causal or interventional criterion that would separate a load-bearing latent from a spurious one."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:5b9818aea1e46fa4974f2b5fb9194096cc269793","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Argues the linear-superposition assumption underlying SAEs is insufficient and that networks also encode a 'feature-integration' space, captured by a Neural-Factorization-Machine that predicts SAE reconstruction residuals from SAE features. Its residue: the integration structure is fit as a correlational residual-prediction object and never validated by intervention — it shows features interact statistically but does not establish which interactions are causal (A's effect routed through B) versus co-varying."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7109111229","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Causal Neuron Pinpointing uses interventional techniques to identify individual neurons exerting direct causal influence on specific behaviors. Its residue: it operates on raw neurons (not the disentangled SAE feature basis where superposition is resolved) and pinpoints single causal nodes, never the causal pathways linking one interpretable feature to another."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"mechanistic interpretability of neural representations via sparse autoencoders (SAEs)","venue":"ICLR 2026 (area: interpretability and explainable AI)","time":"2026","data":["pretrained LLM activations (e.g., Pythia / Gemma / SmolLM2 residual-stream + MLP activations)","trained SAE latent dictionaries over those activations"],"compute":"1×A100 × 3 months ≈ 90 A100-day","expertise":"ML researcher with interpretability / causal-inference background","preference":"both","baseline":"auto-interpretation pipelines that label SAE latents by correlational activation patterns, plus single-latent causal-intervention frameworks (activation patching / causal mediation on one latent at a time)","limitation":"current SAE interpretability is correlational — a latent is named by what it co-activates with, not by what it causally produces downstream or how it causally relates to other latents; intervention work, where it exists, tests one latent in isolation and does not recover the causal structure AMONG features","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type","venue","time"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The pipeline is sequential (search -> certify -> decompose) over one shared object: the feature-feature causal graph G whose nodes are SAE latents and whose directed edge i->j carries a mediated-effect weight. (Leg 3, the amortized search front.) Given a trained model M, a frozen SAE with decoder D (columns d_k are unit-norm feature directions in residual-stream space) and latent activations z in R^d over a prompt set P, an edge-scorer s_theta(i,j) = sigmoid(w0 + w1*cos(d_i,d_j) + w2*coactivation(i,j) + w3*|grad_z_j L w.r.t. z_i|) ranks candidate ordered pairs; w0..w3 are learned scalars (the only trainable weights), cos and coactivation are computed from cached activations, and the gradient term is one backward pass per prompt averaged over P. The top-B pairs by s_theta enter the intervention queue. (Leg 1, the estimand.) For each queued pair (i,j) we compute three quantities by patching in SAE-decoder space and reading the model's output metric Y (the task logit / KL of the next-token distribution): TE_i = E_P[Y(do z_i := a) - Y(do z_i := 0)] (activate vs ablate i, j free); NDE_{i->Y|j} = same contrast but with z_j clamped to its observed baseline b_j throughout (j held fixed so its mediating path is blocked); and the through-j mediated component MED_{i->j} = TE_i - NDE_{i->Y|j}. A do-intervention 'z_k := v' is realized by overwriting the residual stream h := h - z_k_old*d_k + v*d_k at the SAE layer and completing the forward pass, so every clamp stays on the model's own activation manifold; a is the 95th-percentile activation of i over P and 0 is ablation. MED_{i->j} is the per-pair responsibility number: large MED with small NDE means i's effect on Y is routed THROUGH j (a mediated edge); large NDE with small MED means i acts directly. (Leg 2, the certificate.) The identical pipeline is run on a control model M_rand (weights of the studied layers re-sampled i.i.d. preserving per-matrix variance) and on an activation-shuffle control; the certificate for an edge is that MED_{i->j} and TE_i exceed the control null band (the 95th percentile of |MED| / |TE| measured on M_rand under the same B budget). The realized (TE,NDE,MED) outcomes are fed back to update s_theta by a logistic loss against 'edge survived the null band', closing the search loop. The three legs share G: leg 3 proposes its edges, leg 1 weights them, leg 2 keeps only the certified ones, yielding an exploratory causal graph over SAE features that no single-latent or correlational method produces.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The three gaps share one object (the graph G with mediated-edge weights), so they are one pipeline, not three modules: the search proposes edges, the estimand weights them, the diagnostic certifies them — evidence is that each leg's output is literally the next leg's input (B pairs -> MED weights -> null-band-filtered edges). I considered making the estimand a single global structure-learning objective (fit a full SCM over all d latents jointly), but rejected it: it would regress onto classical causal-structure-discovery over a named small variable set (lineage node c0) and is infeasible at d~10^4 under any intervention budget, whereas the pairwise NDE/TE-with-clamp estimand stays per-pair and is exactly the controlled-direct-effect object mediation analysis already validates. I also rejected doing the search with vanilla path-patching one latent at a time (lineage node n4 / c1) because that is the very O(d^2) sweep the budget forbids; the amortized scorer is what the tree does not yet occupy.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on Gemma-2-2B (or Pythia-410M) with a public residual-stream SAE at one mid layer, take a controlled behavior with a known two-feature gate (e.g., a 'language=French' latent and a 'request-is-a-question' latit such that the French-question response only fires when both are active), run the pipeline with B=2000 interventions, and measure (i) recovery of the known mediated edge and (ii) the trained-vs-random divergence. If the method works, the mediated-edge weight MED for the genuine gate is high while its direct effect NDE is near zero, and on M_rand both TE and MED collapse into the null band (so the fraction of edges surviving certification drops sharply from trained to random — the headline divergence). The named load-bearing variable is MED_{i->j}, the through-mediator effect. Negative control: replace the true mediator j in the clamp with a random same-frequency latent j' (clamp j' instead of j). If MED is genuinely the mediated effect, this control must drive the DOWNSTREAM OUTCOME METRIC — the model's task accuracy / next-token KL recovery on the French-question probe — back to the baseline (unmediated) level, because clamping an irrelevant latent blocks no real path; if instead accuracy still 'recovers' under the random clamp, MED was tracking generic activation magnitude, not mediation, and the claim is falsified. Positive control (recommended): a stripped predictor that ranks edges by MED alone should recover most of the known gate structure that the full scorer finds, confirming MED carries the mechanism.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415248346","delta":"They estimate each latent's causal effect on the OUTPUT one latent at a time (input manipulation / patching / single-node mediation) for continuous VAE latents; we construct the through-a-second-latent mediated component MED=TE-NDE over a sparse overcomplete SAE dictionary, recovering feature-FEATURE causal structure their one-latent-against-output framework cannot express, and we do it under an amortized budget rather than a per-latent sweep."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4406975755","delta":"They show correlational auto-interp scores fail to separate trained from random transformers but propose no replacement; we supply the positive interventional criterion — a latent's TE and its mediated-edge weights must exceed a trained-vs-random null band — turning their negative diagnosis into a certification test."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:5b9818aea1e46fa4974f2b5fb9194096cc269793","delta":"They model SAE feature interactions as a correlational residual-prediction object (a Neural Factorization Machine on reconstruction residuals); we replace that statistical interaction with an intervention-validated directed mediated edge, distinguishing causal routing (i acts through j) from mere co-variation, which their residual fit cannot."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7109111229","delta":"They pinpoint single neurons with direct causal influence on behavior; we operate in the disentangled SAE basis and recover the directed causal pathways linking one interpretable feature to another, not just isolated causal nodes."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4415248346","what_step_was_missed":"Their framework defines single-node causal mediation as one of four manipulation types but computes it as latent-i-against-output with no second latent held fixed; recovering the feature-to-feature graph requires the mediator-clamped contrast (the natural-direct-effect with z_j fixed to baseline, giving MED=TE-NDE) plus an amortized acquisition rule that selects which of the O(d^2) pairs to intervene on under budget — neither the mediator-conditioned estimand over a sparse dictionary nor the budgeted edge-search was constructed."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":319,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"Hard floor did not fire: gap_closure_reject_check is borderline (no entry triggered), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat.subsumption_argument shows the closest paper (W4415248346) does not subsume the mediator-clamped MED estimand. recipe_application_check.verdict = applied on all three legs (the C00 intervention-certified measurement, C02 trained-vs-random isolation, and C22 amortized edge search are each present), so the idea is built from the cluster tactics, not the parent gist. The two non-load-bearing borderlines (C00 degenerate-zero-baseline artifact, C22 'is this just active learning' framing) are surfaced for Phase 4 reviewer_concerns_and_responses rather than requiring revision.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a quantity that, for a pair of SAE latents, distinguishes a direct causal contribution to the output from one that is fully routed through a second latent — every interpretability signal (correlational labelling and isolated single-latent patching alike) is measured on one latent against the output without conditioning on the state of the others, so feature-to-feature mediation is invisible.","main_pattern":"reframe_as_solvable_object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The signature failure is treating the reframing as a mechanical wrapper: taking an established attribution/estimation tool and pointing it at a new granularity/architecture without re-deriving why the resulting scores are faithful — no causal validation that the identified components actually drive behavior, no soundness argument for why the definition is the 'real' importance, no confound control.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Pointing an off-the-shelf decomposition at a coarser input granularity without showing the coarser units preserve the signal reads as a wrapper, not a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate does not coarsen granularity — it works at the finest SAE-latent unit and adds a new estimand (MED=TE-NDE with mediator clamp) rather than reusing an existing decomposition."},{"lesson_quoted":"Proposing a new attribution definition without an axiomatic or causal argument for why it should count as ground-truth collapses the moment a reviewer asks why this is the real importance.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"MED is grounded in the natural-direct-effect / controlled-direct-effect calculus of causal mediation (a standard estimand) and certified by intervention, not asserted as importance by fiat."},{"lesson_quoted":"Conflating a methodological artifact — a computation-granularity difference, a degenerate zero baseline — with genuine signal undermines the entire premise once the confound is identified.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The ablation baseline uses z:=0; a reviewer could argue an off-manifold zero is itself an artifact — but the candidate clamps in decoder space (h := h - z_old*d_k + v*d_k) to stay on-manifold and adds the trained-vs-random null band, which controls exactly this artifact; the concern is non-load-bearing and surfaceable to Phase 4."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides a falsifiable, intervention-based certificate that a named SAE latent is load-bearing rather than spurious; the frontier diagnoses that correlational auto-interp fails to separate trained-from-random transformers (openalex:W4406975755) but offers no positive interventional criterion to replace it.","main_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail when the instrument isolates the confound only inside an artificial regime and never shows transfer to real deployment, or are circular (validated against the same population/definition they interrogate), or merely re-confirm an already-documented limitation.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A diagnostic that only re-confirms a shortcut already known in advance, surfacing no previously unmeasurable failure, is read as confirmatory rather than as a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The certificate produces a previously-unmeasured quantity (per-edge MED survival vs a trained-vs-random null), not a re-confirmation that auto-interp is correlational — it supplies the positive criterion the prior diagnosis lacked."},{"lesson_quoted":"Building the instrument around one contested definition of the target property means it cannot independently confirm that the definition is correct, and reviewers flag the resulting circularity.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Ground truth is structural (a weight-randomized model has no load-bearing computation to mediate, an exchangeability-based null), independent of the evaluand's own scores — not a self-asserted interpretability definition."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a synthetic-ground-truth instrument only on synthetic data, without demonstrating that the controlled finding transfers to real-world instances, leaves ecological validity unestablished.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The known-two-feature-gate validation is a planted-structure (semi-synthetic) check; ecological validity rests on running the same pipeline on the real model's full dictionary — the candidate does run on the real model, so transfer is demonstrated, but the breadth of real-world recovery is an open empirical question for Phase 4 to flag."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf addresses how to SEARCH the combinatorially large space of candidate feature-feature relations under a realistic intervention budget — the single-latent frameworks (openalex:W4415248346) sweep latents one at a time, which does not scale to discovering structure across an overcomplete dictionary, leaving exploratory (hypothesis-generating) causal analysis of SAE features unsupported.","main_pattern":"relax_discrete_search_to_continuous","sub_pattern":"C22 (Relax Discrete Search to Continuous)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Reject papers execute the reification (turn a hand-designed artifact into a searchable space) but reach for an off-the-shelf search apparatus, so the work reads as a known technique on a new target with no representational/hierarchy-collapsing insight; validation is thin and omits nearest amortization/transfer neighbors.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"If deleting your custom representation leaves a textbook search loop (DAG traversal, MDP plus dynamic programming, RL over an action set), reviewers will score the contribution as a known technique applied to a new target.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"Deleting the learned acquisition scorer leaves a greedy top-B-by-cheap-features selector — not a full textbook search loop, but the representational insight (which cheap observational features predict a certified mediated edge) is the load-bearing novelty and must be defended against 'this is just active learning over pairs'; surfaceable to Phase 4 rather than load-bearing-broken."},{"lesson_quoted":"Automating or searching a design artifact is not by itself a contribution; absent a representational or hierarchy-collapsing insight, the work reads as brute-force even when it works.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The hierarchy collapse is real: it folds the one-latent-at-a-time O(d^2) sweep into a single budgeted acquisition loop whose scorer is trained online from realized NDE/TE outcomes — the search and the validation share the same intervention budget rather than being nested."},{"lesson_quoted":"Failing to position against the closest amortization, transfer, and compression neighbors leaves the practical advantage unproven, which is fatal even when the core idea is novel.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"differentiation_from_lit positions explicitly against the one-latent sweep (W4415248346) and the correlational-interaction fit (Feature Integration Spaces), the nearest neighbors; the budget-vs-exhaustive advantage is stated."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"All three entries are borderline, none triggered. The weightiest borderline is the C00 'methodological-artifact / degenerate zero baseline' lesson on the anchor (reframe_as_solvable_object) — addressed in-mechanism by on-manifold decoder-space clamping plus the trained-vs-random null band — and the C22 'textbook search loop' lesson on the search leg, both non-load-bearing because the core estimand (MED) and the representational acquisition insight survive the concern."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a quantity that, for a pair of SAE latents, distinguishes a direct causal contribution to the output from one that is fully routed through a second latent ...","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Recast an opaque transparency question (which internal component is responsible) as a concrete measurement over a well-studied object — e.g. decomposing into monosemantic sparse directions before causal tracing — with fidelity certified by a causal intervention that flips model behavior when the identified object is perturbed.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism defines the responsibility question as the controlled-direct-effect estimand MED=TE-NDE over the SAE sparse basis (decompose into monosemantic directions before causal tracing) and certifies it by do-interventions in decoder space whose effect is read on the model's output distribution Y — exactly the 'measurement over a well-studied object + causal-intervention fidelity' signature.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides a falsifiable, intervention-based certificate that a named SAE latent is load-bearing rather than spurious ...","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Name the single manipulable confound inflating a measurement and construct controlled instances that block/vary that one axis while holding all else fixed, with ground truth independent of the evaluand, reporting the apparent-vs-de-confounded divergence as the headline.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism names causal-load as the single controlled axis and constructs matched trained vs weight-randomized / activation-shuffle instances (everything else fixed), with structural independent ground truth, reporting the collapse of MED/TE into the null band as the divergence — the C02 signature, not a generic eval.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf addresses how to SEARCH the combinatorially large space of candidate feature-feature relations under a realistic intervention budget ...","sub_pattern":"C22 (Relax Discrete Search to Continuous)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Declare a hand-engineered/fixed discrete artifact a search variable, build a unified parameterization, and collapse the nested search-then-evaluate loop into one amortized optimization (a learned instance-to-configuration predictor) rather than per-candidate re-evaluation.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism declares the edge set {(i,j)} a search variable and amortizes it with a learned edge-scorer s_theta over cheap observational pair-features, updated online from realized intervention outcomes — collapsing the one-latent-at-a-time sweep into a single budgeted acquisition loop, the C22 amortization move.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"All three entries perform their cited cluster's distinctive move: C00's intervention-certified measurement-over-a-solvable-object, C02's single-axis confound isolation with independent structural ground truth, and C22's amortized collapse of a nested search into a learned acquisition loop. None reduces to the parent pattern's generic gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["reframe_as_solvable_object","controlled_diagnostic_design","relax_discrete_search_to_continuous"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"No 2-way subset of the composition set matches any of the three reject-favored compositions, all of which require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component, which is absent here."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"openalex:W4415248346","threat_source":"lit_table","subsumption_argument":"The Multi-Level Causal Intervention Framework is the only retrieved work that already does causal intervention for generative-model interpretability and explicitly lists 'causal mediation analysis' as one of its four manipulation types, so it is the paper whose existence most threatens the novelty of a mediation-based SAE method. The candidate stands because that framework computes single-node mediation as latent-i-against-output without ever clamping a second latent (no mediator-conditioned contrast), targets continuous VAE latents (its own method section flags continuous-intervention metrics collapse to near-zero on discrete latents, i.e. it does not transfer to the sparse SAE dictionary), and sweeps latents one at a time with no budgeted edge search — so the candidate's MED=TE-NDE feature-to-feature estimand plus amortized discovery is not subsumed.","addressable_via":"Already differentiated in differentiation_from_lit (the mediator-clamped NDE contrast and amortized edge search are the named deltas); no further candidate-field change needed to dodge subsumption."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Mediated Feature Effects: Exploratory Causal Graphs over Sparse-Autoencoder Latents\n\n**Method.** Mediated Feature Effects (MFE)\n\n## Motivation\nSparse autoencoders (SAEs, networks that re-express a model's internal activations as a long list of mostly-off 'features') have become the standard way to put human-readable names on what a large language model is doing inside. But the way we currently decide what a feature 'means' is correlational: we look at which inputs make it light up, or we ask another model to write a one-line explanation and grade that explanation by how well it predicts when the feature fires. A recent result showed this is untrustworthy — these scores look just as good for a properly trained model as for one whose weights were randomized, so a high interpretability score does not prove the feature actually does any work (openalex:W4406975755).\n\nThe one line of work that tries to fix this with causal intervention — actually poking the model and watching what changes — does it one feature at a time, measuring each feature's effect on the output in isolation (openalex:W4415248346). That misses the interesting case: when feature A only matters because it switches on feature B. No current SAE method produces a number that separates 'A directly affects the answer' from 'A affects the answer only by going through B'.\n\nWe close this. For an ordered pair of features (i, j) we compute MED = TE - NDE: the total effect of turning feature i on, minus the effect that survives when we hold feature j fixed (clamp it). If most of i's effect disappears once j is held fixed, then i was acting through j. We do every poke inside the model's own 'feature space' so we never push it off into nonsense states, and we add a certificate: re-run everything on a randomized model, and only trust edges whose effect is bigger than what randomness produces. Because there are too many pairs to test exhaustively, a tiny learned scorer guesses which pairs are worth the budget and gets better as real results come in. The payoff: an intervention-certified causal map of how features influence each other — a hypothesis-generating tool that correlational naming and one-feature-at-a-time methods cannot give.\n\n## Method\n### Amortized edge search\n*Spend a fixed intervention budget on the most likely mediated feature pairs instead of an exhaustive sweep.*\n\n1. Run the model over a fixed set of about ten thousand prompts (ordinary text, $\\approx 128$ tokens each) and save, at the one layer the Sparse Autoencoder (SAE) was trained on, (a) the model's internal activations and (b) the SAE feature values. From these compute two cheap per-pair numbers: how aligned two features' decoder directions are (cosine similarity), and how often feature j fires given that feature i fired (their co-activation rate, stored only for pairs that ever fire together). Keep only features that fire between 0.5% and 20% of the time, dropping dead features and ones that are almost always on.\n   - _Why_: These cheap numbers cost no model pokes and let a scorer guess which feature pairs are worth testing.\n2. For each prompt, do one backward pass to measure how sensitive feature j's contribution to the model's next-word prediction is to feature i — the gradient of the next-token log-likelihood with respect to feature i, read out along feature j's decoder direction — and take its size (absolute value). Average this over all prompts to get one number per ordered pair. 【author decision: there is no single built-in 'objective of feature j', so the authors must decide what j's output target is — the next-token log-likelihood routed through j's direction (used here), a downstream task loss, or a reconstruction term.】\n   - _Why_: This is the one cheap signal that has a direction (i toward j), which helps rank likely cause-effect pairs.\n3. Score every ordered pair with a tiny logistic formula over those three cheap features — only four weights are learned, and for the first round they all start at 1 (equal weight). Rank the pairs by score and take the top B of them to actually test, where B is your fixed testing budget. This small scorer is what lets us avoid testing all pairs one by one.\n\n*Amortized edge-scorer: a logistic score over four cheap observational pair-features (decoder-direction cosine, co-activation, and the gradient of j's objective w.r.t. i) that ranks which pairs to spend interventions on; only $w_{0}..w_{3}$ are trainable.*\n$$ s_\\theta(i,j) \\;=\\; \\sigma\\!\\left(w_0 + w_1\\cos(d_i,d_j) + w_2\\,\\mathrm{coact}(i,j) + w_3\\,\\big|\\partial_{z_i} \\mathcal{L}_j\\big|\\right) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: There are too many pairs to test all of them; the scorer spends the fixed budget B on the most promising ones.\n4. Turn each tested pair into a training example — 1 if it survived the null band, 0 if not — and refit the four scorer weights by logistic regression, up-weighting the rare survivors so they are not ignored. Remove the pairs you already tested, re-rank the remaining untested pairs with the updated scorer, and keep testing the next best ones until the budget runs out. Output the final graph, with each node's certified total effect and each edge's mediated effect (MED) as hypotheses to follow up.\n   - _Why_: Learning from real results makes each remaining poke more likely to land on a genuine mediated edge.\n\n### Mediated-effect estimand\n*Measure the through-a-second-feature effect MED = TE - NDE by on-manifold do-interventions.*\n\n5. For each chosen pair (i,j), turn feature i on and off by editing the activation in feature space — subtract i's old contribution and add the new one (Eq. 1) — leaving feature j free to respond. 'On' means setting i to its typical active value (the average value it takes when it does fire, so the edit stays realistic); 'off' means setting it to 0. Finish the forward pass and read the output as how much the next-word distribution shifts from the untouched run (a symmetric Kullback-Leibler (KL) divergence, averaged over positions; also the task-answer score when a labeled probe is available). The on-minus-off difference is i's total effect $TE_{i}$ (Eq. 2).\n\n*On-manifold do-intervention: overwrite latent k in the residual stream h by subtracting its current contribution $z_{k}\\cdot d_{k}$ and adding the target value v along the unit decoder direction $d_{k},$ then complete the forward pass.*\n$$ h' \\;=\\; h \\;-\\; z_k\\, d_k \\;+\\; v\\, d_k \\tag{2} $$\n\n\n*Total effect of latent i: the expected change in the output metric Y when i is activated to value a versus ablated to 0, with the candidate mediator left free.*\n$$ \\mathrm{TE}_i \\;=\\; \\mathbb{E}_{P}\\!\\left[\\, Y(\\mathrm{do}\\, z_i{:=}a) \\;-\\; Y(\\mathrm{do}\\, z_i{:=}0)\\,\\right] \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Editing inside the feature space keeps the model on realistic states, so the measured effect reflects the real computation.\n6. Repeat the same on/off test, but now hold feature j fixed at its baseline the whole time — its value from the untouched run at each position, so j cannot react to changing i (Eq. 3 gives the natural direct effect, NDE). Then set the mediated effect MED = TE - NDE. A big MED with a small direct effect means feature i works THROUGH feature j; a big direct effect with a small MED means i works on its own.\n\n*Through-j mediated effect: total effect of i minus the natural direct effect of i computed with mediator j clamped to its baseline $b_{j}$; a large MED with small direct effect means i acts on the output through j.*\n$$ \\mathrm{MED}_{i\\to j} \\;=\\; \\mathrm{TE}_i \\;-\\; \\mathrm{NDE}_{i\\to Y \\mid j}, \\qquad \\mathrm{NDE}_{i\\to Y\\mid j}=\\mathbb{E}_{P}\\!\\left[\\,Y(\\mathrm{do}\\,z_i{:=}a,\\,z_j{:=}b_j) - Y(\\mathrm{do}\\,z_i{:=}0,\\,z_j{:=}b_j)\\,\\right] \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Holding j fixed blocks the path through j, so whatever effect disappears was the part routed through j — that is the mediated effect.\n\n### Trained-vs-random certificate\n*Certify which edges and nodes are load-bearing by beating a randomized-model null band.*\n\n7. Build two control models. The first randomizes the model's weights from the SAE layer upward through the output projection (matching each matrix's spread), leaving everything below that layer untouched so the features feeding the test are identical — only the downstream computation is broken. The second shuffles each feature's values across prompt positions before decoding. Run the on/off and mediator-clamp tests (the previous two steps) on both under the same budget to get a 'null band' of effect sizes, grouped so each feature is compared against controls that fire about as often. Keep only edges and nodes whose effect on the real model beats the 95th-percentile null for its group. Output the surviving directed, weighted feature graph. 【author decision: how much of the network $M_{rand}$ randomizes (which matrices from the SAE layer up, and whether spread is matched per matrix or per layer) is a choice the authors must fix, trading off how much downstream computation is destroyed versus kept.】\n   - _Why_: A randomized model has no real computation to mediate, so anything that still scores high there is noise; beating it certifies the edge is load-bearing.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 中介特征效应：在 Sparse Autoencoder 隐变量上进行探索性因果图发现\n\n**方法名称.** Mediated Feature Effects (MFE)\n\n## 研究动机\nSparse autoencoder（SAE，把模型内部激活重新表示成一长串大多为零的「特征」的网络）已经成为给大语言模型内部行为贴上人类可读名字的标准工具。但我们目前判断一个特征「是什么意思」的方式是相关性的：看哪些输入让它激活，或者让另一个模型写一句解释、再用这句解释能否预测该特征何时激活来打分。最近一项结果表明这并不可靠——对于训练良好的模型和权重被随机化的模型，这些分数看起来一样好，所以高可解释性分数并不能证明这个特征真的在做事（openalex:W4406975755）。\n\n唯一一条试图用因果干预（真正去扰动模型、观察什么发生变化）来解决此问题的工作，是一次只处理一个特征，孤立地测量每个特征对输出的效应（openalex:W4415248346）。这恰恰漏掉了最有意思的情形：当特征 A 之所以重要，只是因为它打开了特征 B。现有的 SAE 方法都给不出一个能区分「A 直接影响答案」与「A 仅通过 B 影响答案」的量。\n\n我们补上这一点。对于一个有序特征对 (i, j)，我们计算 MED = TE - NDE：把特征 i 打开的总效应，减去把特征 j 固定（钳制）后仍然存留的效应。如果把 j 固定后 i 的效应大部分消失了，就说明 i 是通过 j 起作用的。我们所有的扰动都在模型自身的「特征空间」里完成，因此不会把它推到无意义的状态；我们还加了一个凭证：在随机化的模型上重跑全部流程，只信任那些效应大于随机所能产生的边。由于特征对太多无法穷举测试，一个很小的、可学习的打分器会猜哪些对值得花预算，并随着真实结果的到来变得更准。收益是：一张经过干预认证的、关于特征之间如何相互影响的因果图——一个相关性命名和「一次一个特征」的方法都给不出的、用于生成假设的探索性工具。\n\n## 方法\n### 摊销式边搜索\n*把固定的干预预算花在最可能存在中介关系的特征对上，而不是穷举扫描。*\n\n1. 在一个固定的约一万条 prompt（普通文本，每条约 128 个 token）上跑模型，在 Sparse Autoencoder(SAE) 训练所在的那一层保存 (a) 模型的内部激活和 (b) SAE 特征值。由此计算两个廉价的成对数值：两个特征的解码方向有多对齐（cosine 相似度），以及在特征 i 激活的条件下特征 j 激活的频率（它们的共激活率，只对曾经同时激活过的对存储）。只保留激活频率在 0.5% 到 20% 之间的特征，去掉死特征和几乎总是激活的特征。\n   - _为什么_: 这些廉价数值不消耗任何模型干预，可以让打分器猜出哪些特征对值得测试。\n2. 对每个 prompt 做一次反向传播，测量特征 j 对模型下一个词预测的贡献对特征 i 有多敏感——即下一 token 对数似然对特征 i 的梯度，沿特征 j 的解码方向读出——并取其大小（绝对值）。在所有 prompt 上取平均，得到每个有序对一个数。【作者需决定：特征 j 并没有一个现成的唯一「目标函数」，作者必须确定 j 的输出目标是什么——是沿 j 方向读出的下一 token 对数似然（此处采用），还是某个下游任务损失，或一个重构项。】\n   - _为什么_: 这是唯一带有方向（i 指向 j）的廉价信号，有助于对可能的因果对进行排序。\n3. 用一个很小的 logistic 公式对每个有序对在这三个廉价特征上打分——只学习四个权重，第一轮全部从 1 开始（等权）。按分数排序，取分数最高的 B 个对去实际测试，B 是你固定的测试预算。正是这个小打分器让我们不必把所有特征对逐一测试。\n\n*摊销式边打分器：基于四个廉价的观测性特征对（decoder 方向余弦、共激活、以及 j 的目标对 i 的梯度）的 logistic 打分，用来对哪些隐变量对值得花费干预预算进行排序；仅 $w_{0}..w_{3}$ 可训练。*\n$$ s_\\theta(i,j) \\;=\\; \\sigma\\!\\left(w_0 + w_1\\cos(d_i,d_j) + w_2\\,\\mathrm{coact}(i,j) + w_3\\,\\big|\\partial_{z_i} \\mathcal{L}_j\\big|\\right) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 特征对太多无法全部测试；打分器把固定预算 B 花在最有希望的对上。\n4. 把每个已测试的对变成一个训练样本——越过零分布带记 1，否则记 0——用 logistic 回归重新拟合四个打分器权重，并给稀少的存留者更高权重以免被忽略。移除已测试过的对，用更新后的打分器对剩余未测试的对重新排序，继续测试下一批最好的，直到预算用尽。输出最终图，每个节点带有认证后的总效应、每条边带有中介效应 MED，作为后续跟进的假设。\n   - _为什么_: 从真实结果中学习，使每次剩余的干预更可能落在真正的中介边上。\n\n### 中介效应估计量\n*通过保持在流形上的 do 干预测量「经由第二个特征」的效应 MED = TE - NDE。*\n\n5. 对每个选中的对 (i,j)，通过在特征空间编辑激活——减去 i 的旧贡献、加上新值（公式 1）——把特征 i 打开和关闭，同时让特征 j 自由响应。「打开」是把 i 设为它的典型激活值（即它确实激活时所取的平均值，使编辑保持真实）；「关闭」是设为 0。完成前向传播，读取输出为下一个词的分布相对未改动那次跑动偏移了多少（一个对称的 Kullback-Leibler(KL) 散度，在各位置上取平均；当有带标签的探针时，也读取任务答案分数）。打开减去关闭之差就是 i 的总效应 $TE_{i}$（公式 2）。\n\n*保持在模型自身激活流形上的 do 干预：在残差流 h 中，先减去隐变量 k 当前的贡献 $z_{k}\\cdot d_{k}$，再沿单位 decoder 方向 $d_{k}$ 加上目标值 v，然后继续完成前向传播。*\n$$ h' \\;=\\; h \\;-\\; z_k\\, d_k \\;+\\; v\\, d_k \\tag{2} $$\n\n\n*隐变量 i 的总效应（total effect）：把 i 激活到值 a 与置零（0）两种情形下，输出度量 Y 的期望差，此时候选中介隐变量保持自由。*\n$$ \\mathrm{TE}_i \\;=\\; \\mathbb{E}_{P}\\!\\left[\\, Y(\\mathrm{do}\\, z_i{:=}a) \\;-\\; Y(\\mathrm{do}\\, z_i{:=}0)\\,\\right] \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 在特征空间内编辑使模型保持在真实状态，所以测得的效应反映的是真实计算。\n6. 重复同样的开/关测试，但这次全程把特征 j 固定在其基线——即每个位置上来自未改动那次跑动的值，使 j 无法对 i 的改变作出反应（公式 3 给出自然直接效应 natural direct effect, NDE）。然后令中介效应 MED = TE - NDE。MED 大而直接效应小，说明特征 i 通过特征 j 起作用；直接效应大而 MED 小，说明 i 独立起作用。\n\n*经由 j 的中介效应：i 的总效应减去把中介隐变量 j 钳制到基线 $b_{j}$ 时 i 的自然直接效应（NDE）；MED 大而直接效应小，说明 i 是通过 j 作用于输出的。*\n$$ \\mathrm{MED}_{i\\to j} \\;=\\; \\mathrm{TE}_i \\;-\\; \\mathrm{NDE}_{i\\to Y \\mid j}, \\qquad \\mathrm{NDE}_{i\\to Y\\mid j}=\\mathbb{E}_{P}\\!\\left[\\,Y(\\mathrm{do}\\,z_i{:=}a,\\,z_j{:=}b_j) - Y(\\mathrm{do}\\,z_i{:=}0,\\,z_j{:=}b_j)\\,\\right] \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 把 j 固定会阻断经过 j 的路径，因此消失掉的那部分效应就是经由 j 传递的——这就是中介效应。\n\n### 训练 vs 随机 认证\n*通过越过随机化模型的零分布带，认证哪些边和节点是承载作用的。*\n\n7. 构建两个控制模型。第一个把模型从 SAE 所在层往上直到输出投影的权重随机化（匹配每个矩阵的离散程度），而保持该层以下不变，使送入测试的特征完全相同——只破坏下游计算。第二个在解码前把每个特征的值在 prompt 各位置间打乱。在相同预算下对两者跑开/关测试和中介钳制测试（前两步），得到效应大小的「零分布带」，并分组使每个特征与激活频率相近的控制对照。只保留在真实模型上效应超过其所在组 95 分位零分布的边和节点。输出存留下来的有向、带权特征图。【作者需决定：$M_{rand}$ 随机化网络的范围（从 SAE 所在层往上随机化哪些矩阵，以及离散程度按每个矩阵还是每层匹配）是作者必须确定的选择，权衡是破坏多少下游计算与保留多少。】\n   - _为什么_: 随机化的模型没有真实计算可供中介，所以在那里仍然得分高的都是噪声；超过它就认证了这条边是承载作用的。\n\n"},{"id":"41","run_dir":"run_prompt41_unsuprl","index":41,"title":"Separability-Targeted Reward-Free Pretraining via the Critic's Transient Skill-Ranking Signal","title_zh":"面向可分性的无奖励预训练：利用 Critic 的瞬态技能排序信号","method_name":"Transient-Critic Separability Pretraining (TCSP)","hook":"Skill-discovery pretraining maximizes a state-skill information quantity at convergence, then hopes the skills end up separable enough for downstream adaptation; we instead make a reachability-weighted skill-separability the unique minimizer of the pretraining loss, and source the pairing signal that drives it from the critic's transient, learning-time ranking of which skills it can already tell apart.","anchor_pattern_id":"targeted_self_supervised_objective","anchor_pattern_name":"Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective","domain_category":"Reinforcement Learning","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes the downstream-adaptation-relevant geometric property of the skill set (how separated/diverse skills are relative to where unseen tasks place their targets) into the quantity the pretraining procedure provably produces; every leaf optimizes a stationary information-theoretic surrogate at convergence and treats that geometry as an uncontrolled by-product diagnosed or softly regularized only after the fact (additive need at the frontier-leaf residual_problem of semanticscho","pattern_id":"targeted_self_supervised_objective","pattern_name":"Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective","sub_pattern":"C17 (Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by replacing the skill discriminator's default inner-product similarity with a reachability-weighted, property-sensitive separability measure so that a representation in which skills are maximally separable along directions downstream tasks place targets is the unique minimizer of the pretext loss — making the adaptation-relevant geometry the optimized target rather than an after-the-fact diagnostic.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf uses the LEARNING-TIME trajectory of the agent's representation/value as the signal it optimizes for; openalex:W7092316655 establishes that the behavior-driving signal in reward-free RL is a transient representation-shaped quantity that exists only while learning is in progress, yet every skill-discovery leaf still defines its objective solely at the asymptotic fixed point, discarding the transient structure (additive need at that leaf's residual_problem).","pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","sub_pattern":"C26 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by harvesting the comparative pairing signal that drives the pretext objective from the critic's own transient value scores at each learning step — ranking skill pairs by how separably the current critic already distinguishes their terminal-state regions — and embedding that ordering directly into the native pretraining loss, so the optimized signal is the learning-time representation trajectory rather than a converged fixed-point statistic.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"unsupervised reinforcement learning (reward-free skill discovery / intrinsic-motivation pretraining)","n_papers":37,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":24},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":19,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Unsupervised Reinforcement Learning for Multi-Task Autonomous Driving: Expanding Skills and Cultivating Curiosity"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Constrained Skill Discovery: Quadruped Locomotion with Unsupervised Reinforcement Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Energy-Efficient Intra-Domain Network Slicing for Multi-Layer Orchestration in Intelligent-Driven Distributed 6G Networks: Learning Generic Assignment Skills with Unsupervised Reinforcement Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Surprise-Adaptive Intrinsic Motivation for Unsupervised Reinforcement Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Automatic Curriculum for Unsupervised Reinforcement Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"From Unsupervised Reinforcement Learning to Continual Reinforcement Learning: Leading Learning from the Relevance to the Whole of Autonomous Driving Decision-Making"}],"more":13},{"year":2025,"n":18,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"BFM-Zero: A Promptable Behavioral Foundation Model for Humanoid Control Using Unsupervised Reinforcement Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Task Adaptation from Skills: Information Geometry, Disentanglement, and New Objectives for Unsupervised Reinforcement Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Robotic Locomotion Skill Learning Using Unsupervised Reinforcement Learning With Controllable Latent Space Partition"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Self-Referencing Agents for Unsupervised Reinforcement Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Interpretable Learning Dynamics in Unsupervised Reinforcement Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Diffusion Dynamic Model for Unsupervised Reinforcement Learning"}],"more":12}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":7,"share":0.189},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":5,"share":0.135},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":5,"share":0.135},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":5,"share":0.135},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":5,"share":0.135},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":3,"share":0.081},{"pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","count":3,"share":0.081},{"pattern_id":"targeted_self_supervised_objective","pattern_name":"Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective","count":3,"share":0.081}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"In reward-free RL pretraining, the agent optimizes an intrinsic objective (mutual information I(state;skill) for skill-discovery methods, or a novelty/entropy bonus for curiosity methods) whose optimum is defined ONLY at the asymptotic, converged skill/state distribution, yet the quantity that actually determines downstream adaptation cost — the geometric diversity and separability of the skills relative to where unseen tasks place their target states — is left as an uncontrolled by-product of that optimization (semanticscholar:2f7673ec43be0cb7302d921ac652db5cec019103 proves MISL's I(state;skill) optimum does not guarantee the diversity/separability that one-skill-initialized adaptation needs, and openalex:W4416838970 shows identifiability holds only for the specific contrastive-successor-feature inner-product parametrization, not for MI objectives in general). Compounding this, the exploration signal that makes reward-free agents reach useful states is itself a transient, representation-shaped implicit reward that exists during learning and disappears at convergence (openalex:W7092316655 shows SGCRL's emergent exploration is driven by a critic-shaped implicit reward landscape that exists only while representations are still changing); so methods that define success purely at the fixed-point of a stationary objective discard exactly the learning-trajectory structure that produced the transferable behavior, and there is no current mechanism that targets the downstream-relevant geometric property directly rather than hoping it falls out of maximizing a converged information-theoretic quantity.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:2f7673ec43be0cb7302d921ac652db5cec019103","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Task Adaptation from Skills proves theoretically that MISL's I(state;skill) optimum does not guarantee skills that are diverse and separable enough for low-cost downstream adaptation, and adds a post-hoc disentanglement metric (LSEPIN) plus auxiliary objective terms that REWARD higher LSEPIN. Its residue: LSEPIN is a diagnostic measured AT the converged skill set and an add-on regularizer on the SAME asymptotic MI objective — it never makes the downstream-relevant geometric quantity itself the thing being optimized along the learning trajectory, so diversity/separability remains a hoped-for by-product steered by a soft penalty rather than a property the pretraining procedure provably produces."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416838970","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Skill Learning via Policy Diversity proves Contrastive Successor Features recover ground-truth environment features up to a linear transformation, settling identifiability for the CSF inner-product parametrization. Its residue: the guarantee is tied to the specific inner-product MI parametrization and to recovery of the environment's existing factors; it says nothing about whether the recovered geometry is the geometry that minimizes adaptation cost for arbitrary downstream tasks, and provides no lever to shape that geometry when the parametrization differs."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7092316655","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Demystifying Emergent Exploration shows single-goal contrastive RL explores because the critic shapes a transient implicit reward landscape from the evolving low-rank representation, exploring before the goal and exploiting after. Its residue: it is an explanatory/diagnostic analysis of ONE algorithm's transient signal and explicitly does not extract a design lever — it never turns the observation 'the useful signal is the learning-time representation trajectory' into an objective that other reward-free methods could optimize, nor generalizes beyond the single-goal contrastive setting."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:d5d610d9d3afd81ff7bed3795aa06e7529072fe1","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Constrained Skill Discovery replaces latent-transition maximization with a norm-matching objective subject to a distance constraint, improving state-space coverage and controllability for quadruped locomotion. Its residue: the norm-matching constraint is a fixed hand-designed regularizer chosen for coverage, with no characterization of when it beats latent-transition maximization or of which downstream-task geometry it actually produces — coverage is still an emergent property of a stationary objective, not a targeted one."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"unsupervised reinforcement learning (reward-free skill discovery / intrinsic-motivation pretraining)","venue":"ICLR / NeurIPS / ICML (top ML)","time":"2026 submission cycle","data":["URLB (Unsupervised Reinforcement Learning Benchmark): DMC walker/quadruped/jaco domains","ExORL offline trajectory datasets","standard continuous-control simulators (DMC, MuJoCo)"],"compute":"1x A100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"RL researcher with continuous-control / representation-learning background","preference":"both","baseline":"Mutual Information Skill Learning (MISL/DIADYN/CIC/METRA-family) + intrinsic-motivation exploration (ICM/RND/APT) measured on URLB pretrain-then-finetune protocol","limitation":"skills learned by reward-free pretraining transfer unevenly and unpredictably to downstream tasks; the pretraining objective does not control the property that actually governs adaptation quality","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object both legs read from and write to is the SKILL-SEPARABILITY MATRIX G, where G[i,j] is the distance between skill i's and skill j's terminal-state occupancy measured under a reachability-weighted metric M (defined below); the pretraining procedure's job is to drive the policy so that G becomes large in exactly the directions downstream tasks will need. Leg 1 (anchor, C17) defines the targeted property operationally: instead of the standard skill discriminator q(z|s) whose maximization is the usual mutual-information surrogate, we score skill membership with a property-sensitive similarity sim_M(phi(s), e_z) = -(phi(s)-e_z)^T M (phi(s)-e_z), where phi: S->R^d is the learned state encoder (model-internal readout, the same network the policy conditions on), e_z in R^d is skill z's learned prototype (a free parameter vector, one per skill, d=64 by default), and M in R^{d x d} is a positive-definite reachability metric M = sum_k w_k u_k u_k^T whose eigen-directions u_k are the top-K (K=16) principal components of the empirical state-visitation covariance and whose weights w_k = 1/(visit_density(u_k)+eps) up-weight rarely-reached directions (eps=1e-3); the pretext loss L_sep = -E_{s~pi_z}[log softmax_z sim_M(phi(s),e_z)] has as its unique minimizer a phi/{e_z} configuration in which skills are maximally separable under M, i.e. exactly the adaptation-relevant geometry, because softmax separability under M is minimized only when distinct skills occupy M-distant regions. Leg 2 (sibling, C26) supplies the pairing signal that makes L_sep target the RIGHT pairs at the RIGHT time: at learning-time step t we read the critic Q_t (model-internal value head) and form, for every sampled skill pair (i,j), the transient separability margin delta_t(i,j) = E_{s~pi_i}[Q_t(s,z=i)] - E_{s~pi_i}[Q_t(s,z=j)] (how much more the current critic values own-skill states under their own skill than under the other) — a comparative, label-free score harvested from the policy's own in-distribution value estimates; pairs are then ranked by delta_t and the bottom-quantile (least-separated-so-far) pairs are up-weighted in L_sep via a preference weight alpha_t(i,j) = sigma(-beta * delta_t(i,j)) (beta=2.0), so the objective concentrates each step on the skills the evolving critic cannot yet tell apart. The two legs share machinery rather than being separate modules: Leg 2's transient margin delta_t is the dynamic, per-step instantiation of Leg 1's static target G, so the critic's learning-time ranking literally schedules which entries of G get pushed apart next — the central object G is written by Leg 1's loss and read/prioritized by Leg 2's transient signal. Concretely this is one pretraining objective L = L_sep weighted by alpha_t plus the standard policy-improvement term, trained on URLB pretrain environments (DMC walker/quadruped/jaco), with no external reward; downstream we freeze phi/{e_z} and few-shot finetune on URLB tasks. Against MISL/LSEPIN (semanticscholar:2f7673ec43be0cb7302d921ac652db5cec019103), which measures LSEPIN at convergence and adds it as a soft penalty on the asymptotic I(S;Z) objective, our G is the minimizer of the loss itself and is driven by delta_t rather than diagnosed after the fact; against Constrained Skill Discovery (semanticscholar:d5d610d9d3afd81ff7bed3795aa06e7529072fe1), whose norm-matching constraint is a fixed hand-chosen geometry, our M is derived from measured state-visitation reachability and re-estimated during training rather than fixed a priori.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The two gaps share machinery because the sibling's learning-time signal (delta_t) and the anchor's target geometry (G) are the same object viewed dynamically vs statically — the evidence is that delta_t(i,j) is literally a one-step, critic-estimated surrogate for the eventual G[i,j], so a single objective with a transient pairing weight realizes both, rather than two stapled modules (this is the shared_object thread instance: G). Alternative designs considered and rejected: (1) a two-stage pipeline that first runs standard MISL then post-hoc re-separates skills — rejected because it reproduces the very after-the-fact diagnostic structure the anchor gap indicts; (2) using a FIXED reachability metric M computed once before training — rejected because it re-occupies the Constrained-Skill-Discovery / METRA node (n4/n7) of a fixed hand-chosen geometry, a named regression; we avoid it by re-estimating M and by driving the schedule with the transient critic, a source the lineage tree (n0-n8) does not yet occupy. We also explicitly avoided reducing delta_t to a plain count/novelty bonus (n1) or to a stationary I(S;Z) maximizer (n2): delta_t is a critic-derived relative ranking embedded in the native loss, not a scalar visitation bonus.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: pretrain skill-conditioned DDPG with our objective vs MISL/CIC and the LSEPIN-regularized baseline on URLB (DMC walker, quadruped, jaco) under identical env-step budgets, then few-shot finetune (100k steps) on the 12 URLB downstream tasks and measure interquartile-mean (IQM) finetune return. If the candidate works, IQM downstream return increases over MISL and over the LSEPIN-regularized baseline (qualitative direction: up), and the gain concentrates on tasks whose target states lie along high-weight (rarely-reached) eigen-directions of M. The load-bearing variable is the TRANSIENT CRITIC SEPARABILITY MARGIN delta_t(i,j): negative control replaces the live critic ranking that produces delta_t with a FROZEN-RANDOM critic (delta_t drawn from a fixed random ordering re-used every step, so the pretext loss is up-weighted by a schedule uncorrelated with the agent's actual learning dynamics); this control's predicted effect is that downstream IQM finetune return collapses back to the MISL baseline level (the task-outcome metric, not delta_t's own value), demonstrating that it is the learning-time critic ranking — not merely the M-weighted contrastive loss — that produces the adaptation gain. Positive control: a stripped-down variant that keeps ONLY the delta_t-scheduled pairing (with a plain inner-product similarity, M=I) should recover most of the downstream gain over MISL, identifying the transient schedule as the primary mechanism.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:2f7673ec43be0cb7302d921ac652db5cec019103","delta":"They prove MISL's I(S;Z) optimum does not guarantee adaptation-relevant diversity/separability and add LSEPIN as a diagnostic measured at convergence plus a soft penalty on the same asymptotic objective; we make a reachability-weighted separability the UNIQUE MINIMIZER of the pretext loss and drive it with a transient per-step critic ranking, so separability is the optimized target rather than a post-hoc regularizer."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:d5d610d9d3afd81ff7bed3795aa06e7529072fe1","delta":"Their norm-matching objective imposes a fixed, hand-chosen geometric constraint for coverage; we derive the separability metric M from measured state-visitation reachability and re-estimate it during training, and schedule which skill pairs to separate via the evolving critic rather than a static constraint."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7092316655","delta":"They diagnostically show single-goal contrastive RL explores via a transient critic-shaped implicit reward landscape but extract no design lever; we turn that transient critic signal into an optimizable pairing schedule (delta_t) embedded in a skill-pretraining objective and generalize it beyond the single-goal setting to multi-skill separability."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416838970","delta":"They prove identifiability (feature recovery up to linear transform) for the specific contrastive-successor-feature inner-product parametrization; we do not pursue identifiability of existing factors but instead optimize a downstream-adaptation-cost geometry (M-separability) that the inner-product parametrization leaves uncontrolled."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:2f7673ec43be0cb7302d921ac652db5cec019103","what_step_was_missed":"Task Adaptation from Skills derived the LSEPIN separability diagnostic and proved it governs one-skill-initialized adaptation cost, but it stopped at measuring LSEPIN on the converged skill set and adding it as a soft penalty on the asymptotic mutual-information objective; for our contribution to already exist it would have had to construct a label-free pretext loss whose UNIQUE MINIMIZER is the reachability-weighted separability geometry AND a transient, critic-derived per-step pairing signal that schedules which skill pairs that loss separates next — neither the unique-minimizer construction nor the learning-time critic-ranking signal is present in their work."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":264,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"Hard floor did not fire: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict = borderline (not triggered — no Reject lesson marked candidate_match: yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id = null, and paper_pointed_threat is not exact-mechanism overlap. The single borderline finding (gap_closure_reject_check.entries[0].reject_lessons_evaluated[2].lesson_quoted on missing nearest pair-construction baselines, METRA/LSD) is a non-load-bearing comparison-completeness gap, not a defect in core_mechanism's central argument, so per the 'default to advance when only one check is borderline and it is in a non-load-bearing aspect' heuristic the verdict is advance; recipe_application_check.verdict = applied for both legs confirms the cluster tactics are genuinely performed. The METRA/LSD baseline gap and the Task-Adaptation-from-Skills threat are surfaced for Phase 4 reviewer_concerns_and_responses.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes the downstream-adaptation-relevant geometric property of the skill set (how separated/diverse skills are relative to where unseen tasks place their targets) into the quantity the pretraining procedure provably produces; every leaf optimizes a stationary information-theoretic surrogate at convergence and treats that geometry as an uncontrolled by-product diagnosed or softly regularized only after the fact (additive need at the frontier-leaf residual_problem of semanticscholar:2f7673ec43be0cb7302d921ac652db5cec019103 and semanticscholar:d5d610d9d3afd81ff7bed3795aa06e7529072fe1).","main_pattern":"targeted_self_supervised_objective","sub_pattern":"C17 (Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring shape is sourcing the pairing/alignment signal by composing two already-published components and presenting the composition itself as the contribution, never re-deriving WHY this particular pairing geometry uniquely encodes the targeted property and supplying no operational definition, direct probe, or isolating ablation.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Concatenating a frozen off-the-shelf predictor's output as an extra input channel injects no novel insight — it reads as combining two published systems regardless of the accuracy gain.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate does not concatenate a frozen predictor; the load-bearing primitive (the reachability-weighted property-sensitive similarity sim_M plus the transient critic-derived pairing weight alpha_t) belongs to neither MISL nor a stock contrastive loss."},{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a representation is 'disentangled' or property-specific without an operational definition, a direct probe, or an isolating ablation leaves the central claim ungrounded and unverifiable.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The targeted property has an operational definition (the M-separability matrix G), a direct probe (logging G during/after training), and an isolating ablation (the frozen-random-critic negative control and the M=I positive control in falsification_prediction)."},{"lesson_quoted":"A hard-pair construction strategy that closely recombines existing mixup/contrastive recipes collapses to 'incremental' the moment the nearest pair-construction baselines are missing from the comparison.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The candidate compares against MISL/CIC and the LSEPIN-regularized baseline but should additionally name the nearest metric/Wasserstein pair-construction methods (METRA/LSD) as explicit baselines to fully foreclose the 'incremental recombination' read."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf uses the LEARNING-TIME trajectory of the agent's representation/value as the signal it optimizes for; openalex:W7092316655 establishes that the behavior-driving signal in reward-free RL is a transient representation-shaped quantity that exists only while learning is in progress, yet every skill-discovery leaf still defines its objective solely at the asymptotic fixed point, discarding the transient structure (additive need at that leaf's residual_problem).","main_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","sub_pattern":"C26 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The dominant failure is the single-component swap — taking the established preference pipeline and changing exactly one slot then presenting that swap as the contribution — and a second shape is stopping short of the loop by shipping a preference dataset/reward model without demonstrating the downstream optimization that consumes it.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Swapping the preference-label source (human → AI judge, offline → online) without showing the swap unlocks a behavior previously unreachable reads as a one-component substitution and draws novelty rejections.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The transient critic ranking is not a label-source swap on an existing preference pipeline; it is bundled with the reformulation that makes a reachability-weighted geometry the unique minimizer (a capability — directly optimizing adaptation-cost geometry — previously unreachable in skill-discovery objectives)."},{"lesson_quoted":"Stopping at the preference dataset, benchmark, or reward model without demonstrating the downstream optimization it is meant to feed leaves the contribution looking like infrastructure rather than method.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism_steps closes the loop: the manufactured delta_t signal is consumed by the pretext loss during pretraining and evaluated by downstream URLB few-shot finetune return, not left as a standalone artifact."},{"lesson_quoted":"Changing only the granularity of an established contrastive objective (response-level → step-level) is judged incremental unless paired with a clearly demonstrated practical unlock.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The change is not a granularity tweak of an existing objective; it embeds a transient critic-derived ordering into the native pretraining loss and is paired with the demonstrated unlock (downstream IQM finetune-return gain attributable to the live critic schedule via the negative control)."}],"verdict":"clear"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The self_supervised_signal_engineering (C26) leg is clear: it is not a one-component swap and it closes the downstream loop. The anchor targeted_self_supervised_objective (C17) leg is borderline only on the lesson 'a hard-pair construction strategy ... collapses to incremental the moment the nearest pair-construction baselines are missing' — the candidate names MISL/CIC and LSEPIN baselines but not the nearest metric-skill (METRA/LSD) pair-construction baselines, a non-fatal, surfaceable comparison gap."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes the downstream-adaptation-relevant geometric property of the skill set ... treated as an uncontrolled by-product diagnosed or softly regularized only after the fact.","sub_pattern":"C17 (Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Re-engineer the pairing/alignment geometry of a contrastive objective so the targeted property is the only thing whose encoding minimizes the loss; the decisive act is replacing or inverting a default geometric primitive — e.g. swapping the inner-product similarity for a property-sensitive one.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism replaces the standard skill discriminator's inner-product similarity with the property-sensitive measure sim_M(phi(s),e_z) = -(phi(s)-e_z)^T M (phi(s)-e_z), where M is a reachability-weighted metric, so the unique minimizer of L_sep is a representation encoding reachability-weighted skill separability — exactly the cluster's geometric-primitive substitution.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf uses the LEARNING-TIME trajectory of the agent's representation/value as the signal it optimizes for ... discarding the transient structure.","sub_pattern":"C26 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Manufacture a comparative/scalar reward from a non-human source (e.g. the policy's own internal output scores), convert noisy absolute scores into reliable relative orderings, and optimize against it with a preference objective embedded in the model's own native training loss.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism harvests the transient margin delta_t(i,j) from the critic's own value estimates (the policy's internal scores), turns it into a relative ranking, and embeds it as the preference weight alpha_t inside the native pretraining loss L — matching the cluster's non-human-comparative-signal-in-native-loss move.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both legs perform their cited cluster's signature move: C17's geometric-primitive substitution (inner-product → reachability-weighted sim_M) and C26's manufacture-comparative-signal-in-native-loss (critic-derived delta_t embedded as alpha_t). Neither reduces to the parent's generic gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["targeted_self_supervised_objective","self_supervised_signal_engineering"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"None of the three reject-favored compositions matches; all three require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component, which is absent from this composition set."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:2f7673ec43be0cb7302d921ac652db5cec019103","threat_source":"lit_table","subsumption_argument":"Task Adaptation from Skills is the most specific competitor because it already establishes that adaptation-relevant diversity/separability (formalized as LSEPIN) governs one-skill-initialized downstream adaptation cost and adds an auxiliary objective term rewarding higher LSEPIN. The candidate's claim stands rather than falls because that paper measures LSEPIN on the converged skill set and adds it as a soft penalty on the SAME asymptotic mutual-information objective, whereas the candidate makes a reachability-weighted separability the UNIQUE MINIMIZER of the pretext loss and drives which pairs are separated by a transient, per-learning-step critic ranking — so if the candidate's downstream gain survives the frozen-random-critic negative control, it demonstrates an adaptation mechanism (learning-time geometry shaping) that the LSEPIN soft-penalty design structurally cannot claim.","addressable_via":"Already differentiated in core_mechanism (unique-minimizer construction + transient critic schedule vs post-hoc diagnostic + soft penalty); the only residual is adding the nearest metric-skill (METRA/LSD) pair-construction baselines, which is a Phase-4 reviewer-concern surfacing rather than a mechanism change."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Separability-Targeted Reward-Free Pretraining via the Critic's Transient Skill-Ranking Signal\n\n**Method.** Transient-Critic Separability Pretraining (TCSP)\n\n## Motivation\nWhen a reinforcement-learning agent is trained with NO task reward (this is called reward-free or unsupervised pretraining), a popular recipe is skill discovery: the agent learns a handful of distinct behaviors, called skills, by maximizing the statistical information between the states it visits and a hidden skill label. The hope is that later, when a real task arrives, one of these pre-learned skills will be a good starting point that needs only a little fine-tuning. The problem is that the recipe only controls whether the skills are TELLABLE-APART; it does not control WHERE in the space of behaviors they land. But where they land — whether a skill happens to sit near the states a new task cares about — is exactly what decides how cheaply the agent adapts. So today this useful geometry is left to chance, which is why transfer is uneven.\n\nThe most relevant recent paper, Task Adaptation from Skills (ICLR 2025), proved that maximizing the information quantity does NOT guarantee the kind of skill spread that cheap adaptation needs. But it only added a measuring stick (called LSEPIN) read off AFTER training finished, plus a gentle nudge added on top of the same old objective. It never made the good geometry the actual thing the training drives toward. A second recent paper, Demystifying Emergent Exploration (2025), noticed something important: in reward-free learning the signal that actually pushes the agent to useful places is TEMPORARY — it lives inside the critic (the network that scores how good a state is) while learning is still in progress, and it disappears once training converges. But that paper only observed this; it never turned the temporary signal into something you can optimize.\n\nOur idea joins these two threads. First, we change the skill objective so that the single best solution is one where skills are spread apart precisely along the directions the agent rarely reaches — the directions where new tasks tend to place their goals. Second, we decide WHICH skills to push apart next by listening, every training step, to the critic's own temporary ranking of which skills it can already tell apart, so the objective always works on the skills the agent is currently confusing. When this gap closes, reward-free pretraining stops gambling on good geometry and instead provably produces it, so fine-tuning on a new task starts from a skill that is already close to what the task needs.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n\n1. Set up a standard skill-conditioned actor-critic with no task reward. The state encoder $\\phi $ is a small 3-layer perceptron that outputs a 64-dimensional vector; there are 16 skills, each with its own learnable 64-d prototype vector that starts as a random unit-length vector so the skills begin spread out; and an off-policy policy and value network (a Deep Deterministic Policy Gradient, DDPG, learner with a target network and a one-million-transition memory) that take the skill identity (a 16-way one-hot label) as an extra input. At this stage the agent is driven by the usual skill-telling-apart bonus, just like a standard skill-discovery baseline. Both later ideas read from this backbone: the encoder gives the geometry we want to shape, and the value network gives the temporary ranking signal we will harvest.\n   - _Why_: Both new ideas read from this backbone: the encoder gives the geometry we want to shape, and the critic gives the temporary ranking signal we will harvest.\n\n### Reachability-Weighted Separability Objective\n*Makes the adaptation-relevant skill geometry the unique minimizer of the pretraining loss by separating skills under a reachability-derived metric M.*\n\n2. From the agent's own visited states, continually estimate which directions of the state space it reaches rarely versus often. Keep a slowly-updated estimate of how the encoded states spread out (their covariance), take the 16 strongest spread directions, and for each one measure how thinly the agent's visits are scattered along it by bucketing recent states into 50 bins and seeing how few are occupied. Build a metric — a weighting matrix M — that gives rarely-reached directions more weight (one over their visit density, with a small floor of 0.001 so the weight cannot blow up). Recompute M every 10,000 environment steps so it tracks the changing agent. New tasks often need rarely-visited regions, so weighting separability toward those directions aligns the skills with where adaptation will actually matter, and re-estimating M avoids freezing in a hand-picked geometry.\n\n*The reachability metric M as a weighted sum of the top-K state-visitation eigen-directions $u_{k},$ with weights $w_{k}$ up-weighting rarely-reached directions (small visit density), so separability is pushed where downstream tasks are likely to place targets.*\n$$ M = \\sum_{k=1}^{K} w_k\\, u_k u_k^{\\top}, \\qquad w_k = \\frac{1}{\\mathrm{visit\\_density}(u_k) + \\varepsilon} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: New tasks often need rarely-visited regions, so weighting separability toward those directions aligns the skills with where adaptation will actually matter — and re-estimating it avoids freezing in a hand-picked geometry.\n3. Replace the usual inner-product skill-membership score with a distance-based one, $sim_{M},$ that measures how far a state embedding sits from a skill prototype UNDER the metric M (Eq. (1)) — the larger that weighted distance, the lower the membership score. Use it in the pretext loss $L_{sep}$ (Eq. (3)), which asks each visited state to be classified as its own skill against all 16 prototypes. Both the encoder and the prototype vectors are trained by this loss, and each prototype is re-normalized to unit length after every update; the metric M is held fixed at this step (it is refreshed separately). The single best solution of this loss is one where different skills sit far apart under M. This makes the useful skill-spread the actual minimizer of the training loss, instead of something only measured afterward.\n\n*The property-sensitive skill-membership score: minus the squared distance between the state embedding $\\phi (s)$ and skill prototype $e_{z}$ under the reachability metric M, replacing the default inner product so that separability under M is what membership rewards.*\n$$ \\mathrm{sim}_M(\\phi(s), e_z) = -\\,(\\phi(s)-e_z)^{\\top} M \\,(\\phi(s)-e_z) \\tag{2} $$\n\n\n*The property-targeting pretext loss whose unique minimizer is $a \\phi $ and prototype set in which distinct skills occupy M-distant regions — i.e. the adaptation-relevant separability geometry itself.*\n$$ L_{\\mathrm{sep}} = -\\,\\mathbb{E}_{s \\sim \\pi_z}\\big[\\log \\mathrm{softmax}_z\\, \\mathrm{sim}_M(\\phi(s), e_z)\\big] \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This makes the useful skill-spread the actual minimizer of the training loss, instead of something only measured afterward.\n\n### Transient Critic Ranking Schedule\n*Harvests the critic's live, learning-time value margin and uses it to decide which skill pairs to push apart next.*\n\n4. Every gradient step, sample 128 ordered skill pairs (i,j) out of all distinct pairs; for each pair, pull 256 states the agent reached under skill i from memory (no new rollouts needed) and ask the CURRENT value network how much more it values those states under skill i than under skill j. That averaged gap is the transient margin $\\delta _{t}(i,j)$ (Eq. (4)), recomputed fresh every step. The value network's live opinion tells you which skill pairs it already separates and which it still confuses — exactly the temporary learning-time signal prior work only diagnosed.\n\n*The transient separability margin at learning step t: how much more the current critic values own-skill states under skill i than under skill j, a label-free comparative score read from the policy's own in-distribution value estimates.*\n$$ \\delta_t(i,j) = \\mathbb{E}_{s \\sim \\pi_i}\\big[Q_t(s, z{=}i) - Q_t(s, z{=}j)\\big] \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The critic's live opinion tells you which skill pairs it already separates and which it still confuses — exactly the temporary learning-time signal prior work only diagnosed.\n5. Turn each margin into a weight $\\alpha _{t} = \\sigma (- 2.0\\cdot \\delta _{t})$ that is large for the least-separated pairs, then train with the combined loss L = (average over pairs of $\\alpha _{t}\\cdot L_{sep}) +$ the policy-improvement loss (Eq. (5)). The separability part of the loss updates only the encoder and prototypes; the policy-improvement part updates only the policy and value networks; the weight $\\alpha _{t}$ is treated as a fixed number (no gradient flows back through it). This pushes apart whichever skills the value network currently confuses. Spending effort on the currently-confused pairs is how the temporary critic ranking schedules which parts of the skill geometry to fix next.\n\n*The per-pair preference weight that up-weights the least-separated-so-far pairs (small or negative $\\delta _{t})$ and the combined objective: the metric-separability loss scheduled by the transient critic ranking, plus the standard policy-improvement term.*\n$$ \\alpha_t(i,j) = \\sigma\\!\\big(-\\beta\\, \\delta_t(i,j)\\big), \\qquad L = \\alpha_t \\cdot L_{\\mathrm{sep}} + L_{\\mathrm{policy}} \\tag{5} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Spending effort on the currently-confused pairs is how the temporary critic ranking schedules which parts of the skill geometry to fix next.\n6. Keep updating the value network and policy with the normal policy-improvement loss throughout. Because there is no task reward, the per-step reward used here is the same skill-membership score from Eq. (1) read as a log-probability — the agent is rewarded for reaching states that are clearly assigned to their own skill under the metric M — so the value network's ranking stays meaningful. Use slowly-tracking target networks (Polyak averaging at 0.005). Repeat steps step 2 (From the agent's own visited states)-step 6 (Keep updating the value network $and\\dots )$ for the pretraining budget (default 2 million environment steps per domain), refreshing M every 10,000 steps. The margin signal is only meaningful while the value network is still improving; a frozen value network would make the temporary signal meaningless.\n   - _Why_: The margin signal is only meaningful while the critic is still improving; a frozen critic would make the temporary signal meaningless.\n\n### Downstream Evaluation\n*Freezes the learned representation and few-shot finetunes to measure whether the targeted geometry lowers adaptation cost.*\n\n7. Freeze the encoder $\\phi $ and the skill prototypes. For each of the 12 downstream tasks, try all 16 skills by running each greedily for 10 episodes under the task reward, pick the best-scoring skill as the starting point, and fine-tune the whole skill-conditioned actor-critic from there for 100,000 steps. Record the interquartile-mean (IQM) return (the standard benchmark summary, robust to outliers, with bootstrap error bars) and $a 16\\times 16$ skill-separability matrix G whose entry (i,j) is the metric-M membership score between prototypes i and j. If skills are spread along the rarely-reached, task-relevant directions, the chosen starting skill lands close to the new task's targets, so fine-tuning is cheaper and returns go up.\n   - _Why_: If skills are spread along the rarely-reached, task-relevant directions, the chosen starting skill lands close to the new task's targets, so fine-tuning is cheaper and returns go up.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 面向可分性的无奖励预训练：利用 Critic 的瞬态技能排序信号\n\n**方法名称.** Transient-Critic Separability Pretraining (TCSP)\n\n## 研究动机\n当强化学习智能体在没有任何任务奖励的情况下训练时（这被称为无奖励或无监督预训练），一种常见做法是技能发现：智能体通过最大化它访问的状态与一个隐藏技能标签之间的统计信息，学到若干彼此不同的行为，称为技能。人们希望以后真正的任务到来时，这些预先学到的技能中能有一个作为良好起点，只需少量微调即可。问题在于，这种做法只控制了技能是否「可区分」，却没有控制它们落在行为空间的「哪里」。而落在哪里——某个技能是否恰好靠近新任务关心的状态——恰恰决定了智能体适应得多便宜。于是今天这种有用的几何结构只能听天由命，这正是迁移效果参差不齐的原因。\n\n最相关的近期论文 Task Adaptation from Skills（ICLR 2025）证明了：最大化信息量并不能保证廉价适应所需的那种技能分布。但它只是加了一把在训练结束后才读取的「量尺」（称为 LSEPIN），外加在原有目标之上加一个温和的约束项，从未把好的几何结构本身变成训练所直接驱动的对象。第二篇近期论文 Demystifying Emergent Exploration（2025）注意到一个重要现象：在无奖励学习中，真正把智能体推向有用状态的信号是「瞬态的」——它存在于 critic（评估状态好坏的网络）之中，只在学习仍在进行时存在，一旦训练收敛便消失。但那篇论文只是观察到这一点，从未把这个瞬态信号变成可优化的东西。\n\n我们的想法把这两条线索连接起来。第一，我们改造技能目标，使其唯一最优解恰好是「让技能沿智能体很少到达的方向彼此分开」——而这些方向正是新任务常放置目标的方向。第二，我们在每个训练步「倾听」critic 自身对「它已能区分哪些技能」的瞬态排序，据此决定接下来该把哪些技能推开，从而目标总是作用于智能体当前最容易混淆的技能上。当这个缺口被填补时，无奖励预训练不再赌运气，而是可证明地产生好的几何结构，于是在新任务上微调时，起点已经接近任务所需。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景\n\n1. 搭建一个标准的、不使用任何任务奖励的技能条件 actor-critic。状态编码器 $\\phi $ 是一个输出 64 维向量的三层小型多层感知机(Multi-Layer Perceptron, MLP)；共有 16 个技能，每个技能有自己可学习的 64 维原型向量，初始化为随机的单位长度向量，使各技能一开始就分散开；还有一个把技能身份（一个 16 路 one-hot 标签）作为额外输入的 off-policy 策略与价值网络（一个带目标网络、容量一百万条转移的深度确定性策略梯度(Deep Deterministic Policy Gradient, DDPG)学习器）。在这一阶段，智能体由通常的「把技能区分开」奖励驱动，与标准技能发现基线一样。两个后续想法都从这个骨干读取信息：编码器给出我们要塑造的几何结构，价值网络给出我们要采集的瞬态排序信号。\n   - _为什么_: 两个新想法都从这个骨干读取信息：编码器给出我们要塑造的几何结构，critic 给出我们要采集的瞬态排序信号。\n\n### 面向可达性加权可分性的目标\n*通过在由可达性导出的度量 M 下分开技能，使与适应相关的技能几何结构成为预训练损失的唯一最小值点。*\n\n2. 从智能体自身访问过的状态中，持续估计它在状态空间的哪些方向上很少到达、哪些方向上经常到达。维护一个缓慢更新的「编码状态如何散布」的估计（即协方差），取散布最强的 16 个方向，并对每个方向通过把近期状态分到 50 个桶里、看其中被占用的桶有多少，来衡量智能体沿该方向的访问有多稀疏。据此构造一个度量——一个加权矩阵 M——它对很少到达的方向赋予更大权重（取访问密度的倒数，并加一个 0.001 的下限以防权重爆炸）。每 10000 个环境步重新计算一次 M，使其跟随不断变化的智能体。新任务往往需要很少被访问的区域，因此把可分性向这些方向加权，能让技能对齐到真正影响适应的地方；而重新估计 M 可避免冻结在一个手挑的几何结构上。\n\n*可达性度量 M 写成前 K 个状态访问特征方向 $u_{k}$ 的加权和，权重 $w_{k}$ 对极少被访问的方向（访问密度小）赋予更大权重，从而把可分性推向下游任务更可能放置目标的区域。*\n$$ M = \\sum_{k=1}^{K} w_k\\, u_k u_k^{\\top}, \\qquad w_k = \\frac{1}{\\mathrm{visit\\_density}(u_k) + \\varepsilon} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 新任务往往需要很少被访问的区域，因此把可分性向这些方向加权，能让技能对齐到真正影响适应的地方；而重新估计可避免冻结在一个手挑的几何结构上。\n3. 把通常的内积技能归属打分替换为基于距离的打分 $sim_{M}$，它在度量 M 下衡量状态嵌入与技能原型相距多远（式 (1)）——这个加权距离越大，归属分越低。把它用于预训练损失 $L_{sep}$（式 (3)），该损失要求每个访问到的状态在全部 16 个原型中被分类为它自己的技能。编码器和原型向量都由这个损失训练，且每次更新后每个原型都重新归一化到单位长度；度量 M 在这一步保持固定（它在别处单独刷新）。该损失的唯一最优解是：不同技能在 M 下彼此远离。这使有用的技能分布成为训练损失真正的最小值点，而不是事后才测量的东西。\n\n*面向可分性的技能归属打分：在可达性度量 M 下，状态嵌入 $\\phi (s)$ 与技能原型 $e_{z}$ 之间平方距离的相反数，用以替换默认内积，使 M 度量下的可分性成为归属所奖励的目标。*\n$$ \\mathrm{sim}_M(\\phi(s), e_z) = -\\,(\\phi(s)-e_z)^{\\top} M \\,(\\phi(s)-e_z) \\tag{2} $$\n\n\n*面向属性的预训练损失，其唯一最小值点对应一组 $\\phi $ 与技能原型，使不同技能在 M 度量下彼此远离，即可分性几何本身被直接优化。*\n$$ L_{\\mathrm{sep}} = -\\,\\mathbb{E}_{s \\sim \\pi_z}\\big[\\log \\mathrm{softmax}_z\\, \\mathrm{sim}_M(\\phi(s), e_z)\\big] \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这使有用的技能分布成为训练损失真正的最小值点，而不是事后才测量的东西。\n\n### 瞬态 Critic 排序调度\n*采集 critic 实时的、学习期的估值间隔，用其决定接下来推开哪些技能对。*\n\n4. 每个梯度步，从所有不同的技能对中采样 128 个有序对 (i,j)；对每一对，从记忆中取出 256 个智能体在技能 i 下到达过的状态（不需要新的交互），询问「当前」价值网络它在技能 i 下对这些状态的估值比在技能 j 下高多少。这个平均差值就是瞬态间隔 $\\delta _{t}(i,j)$（式 (4)），每步都重新计算。价值网络的实时意见告诉你哪些技能对它已能区分、哪些仍然混淆——这正是以往工作只做了诊断的那个瞬态学习期信号。\n\n*学习步 t 处的瞬态可分性间隔：当前 critic 对技能 i 自身状态在 i 下的估值比在 j 下高多少，是从策略自身分布内估值中读出的无标签比较信号。*\n$$ \\delta_t(i,j) = \\mathbb{E}_{s \\sim \\pi_i}\\big[Q_t(s, z{=}i) - Q_t(s, z{=}j)\\big] \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: critic 的实时意见告诉你哪些技能对它已能区分、哪些仍然混淆——这正是以往工作只做了诊断的那个瞬态学习期信号。\n5. 把每个间隔转换成权重 $\\alpha _{t} = \\sigma (- 2.0\\cdot \\delta _{t})$，对最难分开的技能对赋予大权重，然后用组合损失 L =（对各对取平均的 $\\alpha _{t}\\cdot L_{sep}$）+ 策略改进损失 训练（式 (5)）。损失中的可分性部分只更新编码器和原型；策略改进部分只更新策略与价值网络；权重 $\\alpha _{t}$ 被当作一个固定数值处理（不让梯度回传穿过它）。这会优先推开价值网络当前混淆的技能。把精力花在当前被混淆的技能对上，正是瞬态 critic 排序调度「接下来该修复几何结构的哪一部分」的方式。\n\n*逐对偏好权重，对当前最难分开的技能对（$\\delta _{t}$ 较小或为负）赋予更大权重；组合目标为：由瞬态 critic 排序调度的度量可分性损失，加上标准策略改进项。*\n$$ \\alpha_t(i,j) = \\sigma\\!\\big(-\\beta\\, \\delta_t(i,j)\\big), \\qquad L = \\alpha_t \\cdot L_{\\mathrm{sep}} + L_{\\mathrm{policy}} \\tag{5} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 把精力花在当前被混淆的技能对上，正是瞬态 critic 排序调度「接下来该修复几何结构的哪一部分」的方式。\n6. 全程继续用常规的策略改进损失更新价值网络和策略。由于没有任务奖励，这里每步使用的奖励就是式 (1) 的技能归属分（读作对数概率）——智能体因到达在度量 M 下被清晰归属到自己技能的状态而获得奖励——从而价值网络的排序保持有意义。使用缓慢跟踪的目标网络（Polyak 平均系数 0.005）。对预训练预算（每个域默认 200 万环境步）重复步骤 第2步（从智能体自身访问过的状态中）-第6步（全程继续用常规的策略改进损失$\\dots $），并每 10000 步刷新一次 M。间隔信号只有在价值网络仍在改进时才有意义；冻结的价值网络会让这个瞬态信号失去意义。\n   - _为什么_: 间隔信号只有在 critic 仍在改进时才有意义；冻结的 critic 会让这个瞬态信号失去意义。\n\n### 下游评估\n*冻结学到的表示并进行少样本微调，检验目标几何结构是否降低了适应成本。*\n\n7. 冻结编码器 $\\phi $ 和技能原型。对 12 个下游任务中的每一个，把全部 16 个技能都试一遍——每个技能在任务奖励下贪婪地跑 10 个回合——挑出得分最高的技能作为起点，并从该技能出发对整个技能条件 actor-critic 微调 100000 步。记录四分位均值(Interquartile Mean, IQM)回报（标准的基准汇总指标，对离群值稳健，并带自助法误差棒）以及一个 $16\\times 16$ 的技能可分性矩阵 G，其第 (i,j) 项是原型 i 与 j 之间在度量 M 下的归属分。如果技能沿很少到达、与任务相关的方向分开，所选起始技能就靠近新任务的目标，于是微调更便宜、回报更高。\n   - _为什么_: 如果技能沿很少到达、与任务相关的方向分开，所选起始技能就靠近新任务的目标，于是微调更便宜、回报更高。\n\n"},{"id":"42","run_dir":"run_prompt42_synthchem","index":42,"title":"Coverage-Gain Signals Turn the Synthesis Library into an Adaptive Action Space","title_zh":"覆盖增益信号让合成库从固定输入变为自适应动作空间","method_name":"Coverage-Gain Adaptive Library (CGAL)","hook":"Synthesis-aware generators are trained to navigate a fixed building-block-plus-reaction-template catalog, yet none of them produces any signal about which absent chemistry would most enlarge the property-satisfying region they can reach — so the catalog, not chemistry, silently bounds their frontier. We manufacture that missing signal — a per-candidate coverage-gain estimate read off the generator's own failure distribution — and show it both ranks which reactions/blocks to admit AND lets the action-space catalog stop being a fixed input.","anchor_pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","anchor_pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","domain_category":"Healthcare & Scientific ML","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved synthesis-aware generator produces a signal that identifies WHICH absent reaction templates or building blocks would, if added to the action space, most enlarge the reachable region of property-satisfying synthesizable molecules — coverage of synthesizable space is treated as fixed by the supplied catalog rather than as an optimizable target.","pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","sub_pattern":"C08 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"closed by running a closed-loop producer-evaluator that proposes candidate library expansions, scores each by a manufactured coverage-gain signal (estimated enlargement of reachable property-satisfying support), and filters by an adaptive reward-gain cutoff — the generator's own miss-distribution becomes the label that says which absent chemistry matters.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions whether the building-block-plus-reaction-template library must be a fixed input at all, rather than a quantity the generation process itself adapts — the assumption that the action-space catalog is given and static is inherited by every leaf (RGFN, RxnFlow, SynFormer, SynGFN, SynLlama) and is never tested.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","how_closed":"the audit half names and inverts the inherited precondition that the action-space catalog is an always-present static input, reframing generation from navigate-a-fixed-selection-set to co-adapt-the-selection-set; the companion deliverable half feeds the same coverage-gain signal back as the gradient that admits/retires action-space entries online, turning the inverted assumption into a runnable adaptive-library generator.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"synthesizable chemical space exploration (synthesis-aware molecular generative modeling)","n_papers":37,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":24},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":13,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"RGFN: Synthesizable Molecular Generation Using GFlowNets"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Generative Artificial Intelligence for Navigating Synthesizable Chemical Space"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Structure-Based Drug Design with a Deep Hierarchical Generative Model"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"3D molecular generation models expand chemical space exploration in drug design."},{"source":"openalex","title":"CSearch: chemical space search via virtual synthesis and global optimization"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Generative Flows on Synthetic Pathway for Drug Design"}],"more":7},{"year":2025,"n":24,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Efficient and Programmable Exploration of Synthesizable Chemical Space"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Active Learning Enables Extrapolation in Molecular Generative Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"NovoMolGen: Rethinking Molecular Language Model Pretraining"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Guiding Evolutionary Molecular Design: Adding Reinforcement Learning for Mutation Selection"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"SynTwins: a retrosynthesis-guided framework for synthesizable molecular analog generation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Generative AI for navigating synthesizable chemical space"}],"more":18}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":19,"share":0.514},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":7,"share":0.189},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":5,"share":0.135},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":4,"share":0.108},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":4,"share":0.108},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":3,"share":0.081},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":3,"share":0.081},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":3,"share":0.081}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Across the current synthesis-aware generative frontier — RGFN (semanticscholar:3e658303b248ab79bca9938b37fa16f4b2192351), RxnFlow (openalex:W4403322799), SynFormer (semanticscholar:c3ae5fa83dba79a5f640fa753cdf9d8d3bbd433c) and SynLlama (openalex:W4410105746) — synthesizability is guaranteed by restricting the generator's action space to a FIXED, pre-curated set of purchasable building blocks plus a FIXED set of robust reaction templates, then assembling molecules only along that action space (a GFlowNet trajectory over reaction edges in RGFN/RxnFlow, an autoregressive pathway in SynFormer/SynLlama). The structural failure is that the boundary of the reachable space is set by the supplied catalog, not by chemistry: any target molecule whose only viable retrosynthetic disconnection passes through a reaction type or an intermediate building block absent from the fixed library is unreachable with probability zero, no matter how the policy is trained, and the generator has no signal that it is even missing that region — coverage of synthesizable space cannot be improved by better policy learning because the support of the sampling distribution is capped at construction time. Existing work treats the building-block-plus-template library as a given input and optimizes the policy over it; none of these papers produces a signal that tells you which absent reactions/blocks would most enlarge reachable property-satisfying space, so the field keeps improving navigation inside a box whose walls were never questioned.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4403322799","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"RxnFlow assembles molecules as a GFlowNet trajectory of reaction-template applications over a large fixed set of purchasable building blocks, training the forward policy to sample high-reward, diverse synthesizable molecules; its method section fixes both the reaction-template set and the building-block pool as static action-space inputs and amortizes the policy over them. It does not close the question of how to expand that action space: the reachable terminal-molecule support is exactly the closure of the supplied templates over the supplied blocks, so molecules requiring an un-listed template or block have zero sampling probability and the policy receives no gradient signal pointing at the missing chemistry."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:3e658303b248ab79bca9938b37fa16f4b2192351","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"RGFN operates the GFlowNet directly in the space of chemical reactions using a small, deliberately curated set of inexpensive reactions and building blocks to keep the action space tractable and the products cheaply synthesizable. The residue is the same boundary problem sharpened: the tractability that makes RGFN work comes precisely from a small fixed reaction/block set, so its reachable chemistry is even more tightly capped, and it offers no mechanism to decide which additional reaction or block would most enlarge useful reachable space."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:c3ae5fa83dba79a5f640fa753cdf9d8d3bbd433c","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"SynFormer autoregressively generates a full synthetic pathway (building-block selections via a diffusion module + template choices) so every output carries a viable route, and supports property optimization by navigating within that pathway grammar. It still draws all building blocks and templates from a fixed enumerable vocabulary; it controls navigation within synthesizable space but never asks whether the vocabulary itself bounds the property frontier the user can reach."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4410105746","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"SynLlama fine-tunes an LLM to emit synthetic pathways over commonly-accessible building blocks and robust organic reaction templates, achieving strong coverage from little data. Its reachable space is still the closure of that fixed common-block/robust-template set; it demonstrates data efficiency but inherits the same capped support and gives no signal about which out-of-vocabulary chemistry would unlock new property-satisfying regions."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"synthesizable chemical space exploration (synthesis-aware molecular generative modeling)","venue":"ICLR/NeurIPS (ML methods track)","time":"2026","data":["Enamine REAL / building-block catalogs","USPTO reaction templates","USPTO-50k / reaction datasets","ChEMBL/ZINC property oracles","RDKit-computable property targets (QED, docking surrogates)"],"compute":"1×A100 × 3 months (≈ 90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML for molecular generation; familiarity with GFlowNets / autoregressive sequence models / reaction templates","preference":"both","baseline":"RGFN / SynFormer / RxnFlow (synthesis-constrained generative models over fixed building-block + reaction-template libraries)","limitation":"synthesis-aware generators are confined to a hand-curated, fixed library of building blocks and reaction templates, so the reachable region of synthesizable chemical space is bounded by the catalog the model was given rather than by what is actually synthesizable","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object (coherence_thread_type = shared_object) is a single scalar field G(e) — the coverage-gain of a candidate action-space element e (an absent reaction template or building block) — that both legs read from and write to. G(e) is defined and computable as follows. Let the current generator be a synthesis-aware policy π over reaction-tree trajectories with action-space library L (the fixed catalog the frontier inherits: RxnFlow's purchasable-block pool + template set, openalex:W4403322799). For a batch of property targets τ drawn from the user's RDKit-computable objective (e.g. QED / docking surrogate), run π to termination and record, per failed target, the model-internal MISS readout: the terminal log-reward shortfall Δr(τ) = r*(τ) − max_k r(π_k(τ)) over K sampled trajectories (r* is the property oracle's value on the best in-library attempt; r* and r are external-oracle reads, K is a fixed hyperparameter, default K=64). A candidate expansion e is scored by a one-step counterfactual reachability probe: temporarily inject e into L (as one extra template/block action with a learned embedding initialized from its nearest in-vocabulary neighbor in a frozen reaction-fingerprint space), run a short policy rollout of B trajectories per high-miss target conditioned on the high-Δr targets, and set G(e) = (1/|S|) Σ_{τ∈S} [ max_k r(π'_k(τ; L∪{e})) − max_k r(π_k(τ; L)) ]_+ , where S is the top-m miss-targets (m fixed, default 256), π' is π with e admitted, and [·]_+ keeps only positive property-gain — i.e. the expected enlargement of property-satisfying reachable reward attributable to e, in oracle-reward units, requiring no retrosynthesis planner and no relabeling of in-library outputs. LEG 1 (anchor, C08 closed-loop producer-evaluator) manufactures G as the supervisory signal: a PRODUCER enumerates candidate expansions e from a large held-out reaction/block superset (USPTO templates + extended catalog) restricted to those whose nearest-neighbor embedding lies near current high-miss targets; an EVALUATOR computes G(e); an ADAPTIVE CUTOFF γ_t (a running quantile of recent G values, the C08 reward-gain filter) admits only e with G(e) > γ_t, and the loop retrains π on L∪{admitted} each round — the manufactured signal is exactly the 'which absent chemistry would most enlarge reachable property-satisfying space' that no frontier method produces. LEG 2 (sibling, C11 audit + self_supervised_signal_engineering companion) takes the same G and the same producer-evaluator loop and reads it as the inversion of the never-tested static-catalog assumption: because admission is driven online by G rather than fixed before training, L ceases to be an input and becomes a state variable L_t the generation process adapts; the companion's runnable deliverable is the online admit/retire rule (admit when G>γ_t; retire an element whose marginal G has decayed below a floor over a window, capping |L_t| at a budget so the action space stays tractable like RGFN's small set rather than swelling into n2's bigger fixed box). The two legs share machinery completely — one signal G, one loop — and differ only in what they claim: leg 1 that G is a usable optimization signal, leg 2 that its online use overturns the fixed-library assumption.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules: the additive gap asks for a signal that ranks absent chemistry, and the subtractive gap asks whether the catalog must be fixed — both are answered by the SAME scalar G, the first by computing it and the second by feeding it back online, so a reviewer reads one paper (the coverage-gain signal and its online use are one object, not two stapled contributions). Evidence: the subtractive gap's own wording ('a quantity the generation process itself adapts') is literally satisfied by making admission a function of G, which is the additive gap's deliverable. (b) Alternatives rejected: (i) defining G via a retrosynthesis planner run per proposed structure — rejected because method_lineage flags c0 (per-structure route search as the reachability test) as a regression; G instead is a forward counterfactual rollout over the policy, never a backward planner. (ii) Estimating coverage by simply scaling the block pool and measuring reward — rejected as n2/n4 ('a larger box is still a box', the REGRESSION FLAG); the budget cap + retire rule keeps |L_t| bounded so the contribution is WHICH chemistry to admit, not more chemistry. (iii) Post-hoc filtering of generated structures by a synthesizability score (n1) — rejected because G is computed before admission and changes the support, not after generation as a filter.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: backbone = reimplemented RxnFlow over the Enamine building-block pool + USPTO template set; targets = a held-out panel of QED/docking-surrogate objectives (RDKit-computable) deliberately seeded with targets whose best in-catalog reward is low (out-of-library-leaning). Measure REACHABLE PROPERTY-SATISFYING COVERAGE = fraction of the panel for which the generator samples a molecule exceeding the property threshold, as a function of expansion round, while holding the library-size budget Bcap fixed. If the candidate works, coverage rises strictly faster under coverage-gain-driven admission than under frozen-library training or equal-budget random/popularity admission, and the per-round library size stays bounded (no reduction to a bigger fixed box). The single named load-bearing variable is G(e), the coverage-gain estimate. Mechanism distinguisher / negative control: replace G with a randomized score of matched marginal distribution (permute G values across candidates before the cutoff) — the anti-tautology requirement is that this must collapse the DOWNSTREAM coverage metric back to the frozen-library baseline (not merely change G's own value), proving the gain comes from G ranking the right chemistry and not from added library capacity. Positive control: a stripped model that admits purely by argmax-G with no retraining-loop bells should still recover most of the coverage gain, identifying G as the sufficient mechanism.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4403322799","delta":"RxnFlow amortizes a GFlowNet forward policy over a fixed purchasable-block pool + template set, so its terminal-molecule support is the static closure of supplied templates over supplied blocks; we construct a coverage-gain signal G(e) over absent chemistry and an online admit/retire rule that makes the action-space library a state variable, changing the support itself rather than the policy over a fixed support."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:3e658303b248ab79bca9938b37fa16f4b2192351","delta":"RGFN keeps the action space tractable with a small deliberately-fixed reaction/block set and offers no mechanism to decide which addition helps; we add a budget-capped, coverage-gain-ranked admit/retire loop that keeps the set small yet lets its membership adapt to high-miss property targets."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:c3ae5fa83dba79a5f640fa753cdf9d8d3bbd433c","delta":"SynFormer navigates within a fixed enumerable block+template vocabulary and never asks whether that vocabulary bounds the property frontier; we measure the vocabulary's bound directly as G and relax it online, so the reachable frontier is expanded rather than only navigated."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:5abf5ef07a723acfe2913447eb7bfea821fe6670","delta":"Active-learning oracle-in-the-loop generation extrapolates the property predictor on new oracle feedback but leaves the action-space catalog fixed, so it extrapolates in property value not in reachable synthesizable structure; our loop feeds back coverage-gain to change the synthesizable support, the orthogonal axis it does not touch."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4403322799","what_step_was_missed":"RxnFlow constructs the forward GFlowNet policy and the reward-amortization machinery over a fixed action-space library, but to already contain our contribution it would have needed to construct a coverage-gain functional G(e) — a forward counterfactual rollout that scores the expected enlargement of property-satisfying reachable reward attributable to admitting an absent template/block — and to make library membership a state variable updated from G; it builds neither the counterfactual reachability probe nor the admit/retire dynamics, treating the library purely as a static input to the policy."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":290,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"Layer 1 did not fire: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict is borderline (not triggered, no Reject lesson matched yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat is backbone-level overlap with addressable_via null (not exact-mechanism subsumption). recipe_application_check.verdict is applied for both entries, so the idea instantiates the cited C08 and C11 signature moves rather than the parent gist. The single borderline finding — the C11 'theorem stating when and why it wins' lesson — hits a load-bearing property but is substantively answered by the permuted-G negative control and the random/popularity/oracle-G ablation arms already in core_mechanism, so it is surfaced as a Phase 4 reviewer concern rather than requiring revision; advance.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved synthesis-aware generator produces a signal that identifies WHICH absent reaction templates or building blocks would, if added to the action space, most enlarge the reachable region of property-satisfying synthesizable molecules — coverage of synthesizable space is treated as fixed by the supplied catalog rather than as an optimizable target.","main_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","sub_pattern":"C08 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is treating 'attach a generator plus a filter' as a sufficient contribution when generate-and-filter is commonplace, so no single load-bearing insight separates the work from prior cooperative-training or augmentation pipelines; a second shape is the unvalidated transfer assumption, demonstrating only a proxy property rather than the actual downstream objective, and a third is omitting comparison against cheaper non-generative baselines.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A cooperative generate-and-filter loop sitting on substantial prior art needs either a demonstrably new mechanism or cross-domain breadth; showing it on a single domain invites the read that the method is domain-specific and incremental.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The demonstrably-new mechanism is the coverage-gain functional G(e), a forward counterfactual reachability rollout that scores enlargement of property-satisfying support — not a generic generate-and-filter loop over training instances, so the load-bearing insight is present rather than recombinatory."},{"lesson_quoted":"A newly proposed quality or gating score must be tightly argued to solve the stated problem under realistic conditions — a loosely-motivated score evaluated in an artificial setup is dismissed as a solution looking for a problem.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"G(e) is defined precisely in oracle-reward units as the expected enlargement of reachable property-satisfying reward and is the exact artifact the gap names is missing, so the gating score is the crux rather than a loosely-motivated threshold."},{"lesson_quoted":"Training on synthetically generated data without demonstrating transfer to the real target distribution leaves the core premise unvalidated, no matter how clean the synthetic labels are.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The downstream target metric (reachable property-satisfying coverage on a held-out objective panel) is the reported quantity in falsification_prediction, not an intermediate proxy, so transfer to the real evaluation target is demonstrated directly."},{"lesson_quoted":"A curation or replacement pipeline that yields only marginal or occasionally negative gains over no curation cannot justify its added complexity.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The falsification design requires coverage to rise strictly faster than frozen-library and equal-budget random/popularity admission, binding the claim to a non-marginal differential or it falsifies."},{"lesson_quoted":"Inducing a proxy property such as ensemble diversity is not the same as demonstrating the downstream goal such as shortcut mitigation; reviewers require the target metric, not the intermediate effect.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The downstream goal (reachable coverage) is the headline metric, with G itself the mechanism distinguisher under a permuted-score negative control, so the proxy-vs-target trap is avoided."},{"lesson_quoted":"A synthetic-data-factory claim collapses without comparison to cheaper classical baselines, because the necessity of the heavy generative model is then unverifiable.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The ablation harness explicitly swaps admission for random-e, popularity-of-e, and oracle-G arms, isolating that the coverage-gain signal (not added capacity) drives the gain."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions whether the building-block-plus-reaction-template library must be a fixed input at all, rather than a quantity the generation process itself adapts — the assumption that the action-space catalog is given and static is inherited by every leaf (RGFN, RxnFlow, SynFormer, SynGFN, SynLlama) and is never tested.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The dominant failure is substituting one selection rule for another that performs better empirically while omitting the theorem (or, in an empirical idea, the binding evidence) that explains when and why it wins; a second shape is pivoting an assumption the community regards as a reasonable modeling choice rather than a genuine restriction, leaving motivation and novelty in doubt.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Substituting one selection heuristic for another without a theorem stating when and why it wins reads as an engineering combination, not a contribution, no matter how clean the empirical gain.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"This is an empirical-ML idea so no formal theorem is expected, but the equivalent binding-evidence requirement is met by the permuted-G negative control and the random/popularity/oracle-G ablation arms which certify WHEN and WHY coverage-gain admission wins; surfaced as a Phase 4 reviewer concern that the certificate is empirical rather than analytic."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pivoting an assumption the community treats as a reasonable modeling choice — rather than first proving it a genuine restriction — leaves both motivation and novelty in doubt.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The static-catalog assumption is shown load-bearing because the policy's terminal-molecule support is the static closure of supplied templates over supplied blocks (the bottleneck names support, not policy, as the cap), so inverting it genuinely changes the reachable region rather than being a benign modeling choice."},{"lesson_quoted":"A re-derived guarantee whose binding constant is dataset-dependent and cannot be controlled by the practitioner is vacuous in the worst case and fails to convince.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The library-size budget Bcap and retire rule are practitioner-controlled hyperparameters, and the claim is bound to fixed-budget coverage, so the demonstrated gain is not hostage to an uncontrollable constant."},{"lesson_quoted":"Building the entire analysis on a regularity condition (such as continuity or a Lipschitz bound) that the selection mechanism provably violates contradicts and undermines the formal claims.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"No regularity assumption is leaned on; admission is a discrete quantile-cutoff rule with no continuity premise to be violated."},{"lesson_quoted":"Improving a bound by a marginal factor with no matching lower bound fails to demonstrate that the improvement is significant or near-optimal enough to clear the bar.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The oracle-G ablation arm (G computed with exhaustive rollouts) serves as the near-optimality reference against which the cheap forward-rollout G is benchmarked, supplying the missing-upper-reference role."},{"lesson_quoted":"Unlocking a new capability by violating an assumption while ignoring a protective property it guarded — detectability, validity, identifiability — invites rejection on the overlooked side effect rather than the headline result.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The protective property the fixed catalog guarded is action-space tractability, and the candidate explicitly preserves it via the budget cap + retire rule that keeps |L_t| bounded rather than swelling into a bigger fixed box."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The anchor entry (self_supervised_signal_engineering, coverage-gain signal gap) is clear on all six C08 Reject lessons. The sibling entry (assumption_audit_and_pivot, static-catalog gap) is borderline only on the 'theorem stating when and why it wins' lesson, which for an empirical-ML idea is satisfied by the permuted-G negative control plus random/popularity/oracle-G ablation arms rather than a formal proof; no entry is triggered."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved synthesis-aware generator produces a signal that identifies WHICH absent reaction templates or building blocks would, if added to the action space, most enlarge the reachable region of property-satisfying synthesizable molecules — coverage of synthesizable space is treated as fixed by the supplied catalog rather than as an optimizable target.","sub_pattern":"C08 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Stand up a controllable generative procedure and drive it to synthesize candidate instances beyond the corpus's support, route every candidate through a single load-bearing quality gate, fold retained instances back, and iterate — the most advanced variants close the loop dynamically by feeding the learner's per-region uncertainty/error back so synthesis concentrates on exactly the regions the current model fails on. The manufactured object is the training distribution itself.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"Steps 2-6 perform exactly this signature move: the MISS readout (step 2) feeds the generator's own per-target failure shortfall Δr back to focus the PRODUCER (step 3) on under-covered high-miss regions, the EVALUATOR's coverage-gain G (step 4) is the single load-bearing quality gate, the ADAPTIVE CUTOFF γ_t (step 5) is the filter, and ADMIT+RETRAIN (step 6) folds admitted chemistry back and iterates — the failure-distribution-conditioned closed loop is the C08 'most advanced variant', and the manufactured object is the action-space support that bounds the sampling distribution.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions whether the building-block-plus-reaction-template library must be a fixed input at all, rather than a quantity the generation process itself adapts — the assumption that the action-space catalog is given and static is inherited by every leaf (RGFN, RxnFlow, SynFormer, SynGFN, SynLlama) and is never tested.","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Center on a selection/acquisition/admission rule, name the ONE load-bearing assumption baked into it (a fixed count, an always-present element, proximity-to-a-reference), and pivot it by either relaxing the structural crutch or reframing the selection task as a different problem class (selection→online stopping, selection→control), then exhibit the regime where the pivot pays off without breaking a property the original rule protected.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"Core_mechanism LEG 2 names the load-bearing assumption (the action-space catalog is a fixed static input given before training) and pivots it by reframing: because admission is driven online by G via the admit/retire rule (steps 5-7), L ceases to be an input and becomes a state variable L_t the generation process adapts — selection-over-a-fixed-set is reframed into online membership control, the C11 reframe move, while the budget cap preserves the tractability property the fixed catalog protected.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"The anchor entry instantiates C08's distinctive failure-distribution-conditioned closed loop (MISS readout → producer → coverage-gain gate → cutoff → retrain) rather than a generic generate-and-filter, and the sibling entry instantiates C11's hallmark reframe of a fixed-set selection rule into online membership control via the same signal; both signature moves are present in core_mechanism."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["self_supervised_signal_engineering","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"None of the three reject-favored compositions matches: all three require heterogeneous_decomposition as a component, which is absent from the composition_set {self_supervised_signal_engineering, assumption_audit_and_pivot}."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"openalex:W4403322799","threat_source":"lit_table","subsumption_argument":"RxnFlow is the almost_prior anchor: it builds the forward GFlowNet policy and reward-amortization machinery over a fixed action-space library, so the candidate's claim stands or falls on whether RxnFlow already produces a signal that ranks absent chemistry and makes library membership a state variable. It does neither — it constructs no counterfactual reachability probe and no admit/retire dynamics, treating the library purely as a static input — so the overlap is at the backbone level, not the contribution level, and the candidate's coverage-gain signal G plus online admission are the missed step rather than a subsuming prior result.","addressable_via":null}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Coverage-Gain Signals Turn the Synthesis Library into an Adaptive Action Space\n\n**Method.** Coverage-Gain Adaptive Library (CGAL)\n\n## Motivation\nModern molecular-design AIs that promise 'every molecule we suggest can actually be made in a lab' do so with a trick: they only ever build molecules by combining a fixed, hand-picked catalog of starting chemicals (building blocks) with a fixed list of known chemical reactions (reaction templates). Systems like RGFN (Reaction GFlowNet, a flow-based sampler over reactions), RxnFlow (Generative Flows on Synthetic Pathways), SynFormer and SynLlama all work this way. Because every output is assembled from that catalog, every output is buildable. But there is a hidden cost: the set of molecules these systems can ever reach is fixed by the catalog they were given, not by what chemistry could actually make. If the only way to make a great drug-like molecule needs a reaction or a starting chemical that is not in the catalog, the system can never produce it — and, worse, it has no way of even noticing that it is stuck.\n\nWhat makes this fixable now is that these synthesis-aware systems have become reliable enough, in just the past year, to do a key new trick: you can read off how badly the system is failing on each design target, temporarily pretend you added a missing reaction or chemical, and quickly re-run the system to see whether that addition would let it reach targets it could not reach before. None of the current systems does this; they each treat the catalog as a fixed input and only get better at navigating inside it.\n\nThe closest prior work stops just short. RxnFlow scales the catalog up but a bigger fixed catalog is still fixed, and it gives no signal about which missing chemistry would help. RGFN deliberately keeps its catalog small for speed, with no way to decide what to add. SynFormer never asks whether its fixed vocabulary is what bounds the user's reachable molecules. Active-learning generators extrapolate in predicted property value but leave the buildable-molecule catalog untouched.\n\nWhen this gap closes, the catalog stops being a fixed wall and becomes something the system can grow on purpose: it can tell you which absent reactions or building blocks would most enlarge the set of buildable, property-satisfying molecules, and add them as it goes while staying small enough to remain practical. That turns 'coverage of buildable chemical space' from a fixed property of the supplied catalog into a target you can optimize — directly upgrading the whole synthesis-aware line of work.\n\n## Method\n### Background backbone\n*Reuse an existing fixed-library synthesis-aware generator as the unchanged scaffolding the adaptive machinery wraps.*\n\n1. Start from a ready-made synthesis-aware generator that builds molecules step by step as a tree of chemical reactions over a fixed catalog of building blocks (starting chemicals) and reaction templates (known reaction patterns) — reuse RxnFlow or RGFN as the backbone. Store the catalog as plain lookup tables (a template's reaction pattern by its id, a block's structure by its id) plus a table of learned vectors, one per catalog entry, so a new entry can later be appended as one extra row. Its inputs are that catalog plus a property scorer — any RDKit-computable target such as QED (a drug-likeness score) or a docking surrogate (a binding-strength estimate); its output is a sampler of buildable molecules. Leave the catalog untouched for now.\n   - _Why_: You want to act on a faithful copy of the frontier whose fixed catalog is exactly the problem, not a toy.\n\n### Coverage-gain signal\n*Manufacture the per-candidate coverage-gain by reading the generator's miss distribution, proposing nearby absent chemistry, and scoring it with a forward counterfactual rollout.*\n\n2. For a batch of design targets (about 2048 per round), let the generator try each one 64 times and record, per target, how far its best attempt falls short of the best score the same catalog can reach when you sample it very heavily (4096 tries per target, recomputed once each round). Keep the 256 worst-shortfall targets as the 'miss list'. Using the heavily-sampled best as the ceiling means the shortfall measures what the current catalog genuinely cannot reach, not the distance to some unknown perfect answer.\n\n*The miss readout for property target $\\tau :$ the reward shortfall between the oracle's best attainable value $r*(\\tau )$ and the best reward the current policy $\\pi $ reaches over K sampled trajectories. Large $\\Delta r$ marks targets the fixed library cannot reach.*\n$$ \\Delta r(\\tau) = r^{*}(\\tau) - \\max_{k=1\\ldots K} r\\big(\\pi_k(\\tau)\\big) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The generator's own biggest failures are a free label pointing at exactly which targets the fixed catalog cannot reach.\n3. From a large held-out pool of reactions and building blocks not currently in the catalog (USPTO reaction templates plus an extended Enamine building-block catalog), embed every candidate once into a shared 256-dimensional space using fixed reaction-fingerprint and molecule-fingerprint encoders (numeric descriptors of a reaction or molecule's structure). Embed each miss-list target by averaging the fingerprints of the best partial structures the generator managed for it, so the target lives in the same space. For each miss target, pull its 8 nearest candidates by cosine closeness; the deduplicated union (about a thousand per round) is the candidate set. Searching only near where the generator is failing concentrates effort where missing chemistry is actually needed.\n   - _Why_: Searching only near where the generator is failing concentrates effort where missing chemistry is actually needed, instead of scanning everything.\n4. Score each candidate addition by temporarily adding it to the catalog (giving it a starting vector copied from its nearest existing neighbor) and, WITHOUT retraining the generator, having it do a short run of 16 trajectories per miss target with the new addition now selectable. Measure how much the best reachable score improves on the miss list versus the un-added catalog, counting only improvements, and average over the miss list. This coverage-gain number says how much that addition would enlarge the reachable, property-satisfying region. Keeping the generator frozen here isolates 'can the current generator immediately use this addition to reach a stuck target', separately from the later retraining. It is a quick forward re-run, not a backward route-planning search per molecule.\n\n*Coverage-gain of a candidate element e: averaged over the top miss-targets S, the positive part of the increase in best reachable reward when e is temporarily admitted into the library L, measured by a short forward rollout of the perturbed policy $\\pi '.$ This is a counterfactual reachability probe in oracle-reward units, requiring no retrosynthesis planner.*\n$$ G(e) = \\frac{1}{|S|} \\sum_{\\tau \\in S} \\Big[ \\max_{k} r\\big(\\pi'_k(\\tau;\\, L \\cup \\{e\\})\\big) - \\max_{k} r\\big(\\pi_k(\\tau;\\, L)\\big) \\Big]_{+} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Directly simulating 'what if we had this chemistry' is the honest way to tell which absent reaction or block actually unlocks new reachable molecules.\n\n### Adaptive library control\n*Turn the catalog into a state variable via an adaptive coverage-gain cutoff, online admit-and-retrain, and budget-capped retirement.*\n\n5. Admit only the candidate additions whose coverage-gain beats an automatically-set bar — the 90th-percentile of recent coverage-gain values over the last five rounds (in the very first rounds, use whatever history exists, or the current round's own scores when none does). Require the gain to be strictly above the bar; if that would admit nothing, fall back to admitting those at or above the bar so the process never stalls. Because the bar is a moving percentile rather than a fixed number, it stays sensible both early, when many additions look good, and late, when returns shrink.\n\n*Admission set $A_{t}:$ the candidate expansions whose coverage-gain exceeds an adaptive cutoff $\\gamma _{t},$ set to the running 90th percentile of recent G values over the last W rounds, so the bar tracks the current gain distribution rather than a hand-fixed threshold.*\n$$ A_t = \\{\\, e \\in E_t : G(e) > \\gamma_t \\,\\}, \\qquad \\gamma_t = \\mathrm{Quantile}_{0.90}\\big(\\{G(e)\\}_{\\text{last } W \\text{ rounds}}\\big) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A self-adjusting bar admits only the genuinely valuable additions without you having to guess a fixed cutoff.\n6. Add the admitted reactions/blocks to the catalog and fine-tune the generator for one round on the enlarged catalog with its standard training objective — keep the admitted entries' starting vectors from the scoring step (do not reset them), unfreeze the whole network, run a fixed 2000 training updates against the property reward, and mix in a quarter of pre-expansion examples so the generator does not forget the old catalog while learning to use the new entries. Because additions are decided on the fly from coverage-gain, the catalog is no longer a fixed input — it is now a quantity the generation process grows. Retraining on the enlarged catalog is what actually moves the set of molecules the generator can reach.\n   - _Why_: Retraining on the enlarged catalog is what actually moves the set of molecules the generator can reach; deciding the catalog online is the whole point.\n7. For anything admitted at least ten rounds ago, re-measure its coverage-gain under the current generator; if it has stayed below a quarter of the current admission bar for three checks in a row, drop it, keeping the total catalog size at or below a fixed budget. Judging staleness relative to the live admission bar (not a fixed number) keeps the standard on the same scale as new admissions. If admitting new entries would exceed the budget, force out the weakest current entries (oldest first when tied) until the catalog fits. Capping the catalog keeps it fast and practical, so the contribution is which chemistry to admit — not just piling on more chemistry. 【author decision: how large to set the catalog budget is a choice the authors must make — a small RGFN-scale budget headlines staying fast and tractable, a larger RxnFlow-scale budget headlines reaching more chemistry, and the two make different claims.】\n   - _Why_: Capping the catalog keeps it fast and practical, so the contribution is which chemistry to admit — not just piling on more chemistry.\n\n### Coverage evaluation and isolation\n*Measure reachable coverage over rounds, ablate the admission rule to isolate the signal, and report against frozen-library baselines.*\n\n8. Repeat the find-misses / propose / score / admit / retrain / retire loop for many rounds (up to 50, stopping once coverage levels off), and each round record coverage — the fraction of a separate held-out panel of design targets for which the generator now reaches a molecule scoring above a 'strong molecule' bar (set to the 90th percentile of QED, or of the docking surrogate, over a reference set of real drug-like molecules) — together with the current catalog size. Report coverage as a curve over rounds rather than at one bar, so the conclusion does not hinge on where the bar is placed. Tracking reachable coverage at a fixed catalog size is the real outcome that matters.\n   - _Why_: Tracking reachable coverage over rounds at a fixed catalog size is the real outcome that matters, not any intermediate proxy.\n9. Run the exact same loop but decide admissions instead by (a) a random score, (b) how common a candidate is in its source database (a content-free popularity prior), and (c) an expensive 'oracle' coverage-gain computed with far heavier re-runs (256 trajectories per target instead of 16) over the whole miss list — all at the same catalog-size budget, same number of admissions per round, and same retraining. Comparing the coverage curves shows whether the gain really comes from the coverage-gain signal picking the right chemistry. If random or popularity additions did just as well, the signal would be doing nothing; the oracle version shows how close the cheap estimate gets to the best possible.\n   - _Why_: If random or popularity-based additions did just as well, the signal would be doing nothing; this is the honesty check, and the oracle version shows how close the cheap estimate gets to the best possible.\n10. Report the adaptive-catalog generator against fixed-catalog baselines (RxnFlow, RGFN, SynFormer) on reachable property-satisfying coverage and on catalog size. Make the comparison fair: give each baseline a catalog of the same size budget, train it for the same total number of updates the adaptive method used across all its rounds, and evaluate it on the same held-out panel with the same 'strong molecule' bar. Show, on matching axes, both how coverage grows and that the catalog stays bounded. Comparing against the exact systems whose fixed catalog is the bottleneck is what demonstrates you are enlarging the frontier, not just navigating it.\n   - _Why_: Comparing against the exact systems whose fixed catalog is the bottleneck is what demonstrates you are enlarging the frontier, not just navigating it.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 覆盖增益信号让合成库从固定输入变为自适应动作空间\n\n**方法名称.** Coverage-Gain Adaptive Library (CGAL)\n\n## 研究动机\n如今很多分子设计 AI 都承诺「我们推荐的每个分子都真能在实验室里做出来」，它们靠的是一个取巧：只用一份固定的、人工挑好的起始原料目录（building block，即砌块）加上一份固定的已知化学反应清单（reaction template，即反应模板）来拼装分子。RGFN（Reaction GFlowNet，一种在反应空间上按奖励采样的流模型）、RxnFlow（合成路径上的生成流）、SynFormer、SynLlama 都是这套路子。因为每个输出都从这份目录拼出来，所以每个输出都可合成。但代价被藏起来了：这些系统能触及的分子集合，是由给它的目录决定的，而不是由化学本身真正能做出什么决定。如果某个很好的类药分子唯一的做法需要一个不在目录里的反应或砌块，系统就永远生不出它——更糟的是，系统连「自己卡住了」这件事都察觉不到。\n\n现在之所以能解决，是因为这些合成感知系统在过去一年里已经可靠到能做一个关键的新动作：你可以读出系统在每个设计目标上失败得有多惨，临时假装往目录里加进一个缺失的反应或砌块，再快速重跑一遍，看这个新增项能不能让它够到原先够不到的目标。现有系统没有一个这么做；它们都把目录当成固定输入，只在里面把导航做得更好。\n\n最接近的前作都差这一步。RxnFlow 把目录做大了，但更大的固定目录还是固定的，而且它对「缺哪块化学最有用」毫无信号。RGFN 为了速度刻意把目录做小，也没办法决定该加什么。SynFormer 从不追问它那份固定词表是不是正是限制用户可达分子的那堵墙。主动学习类生成器能在预测的属性数值上外推，却原封不动地留着那份可合成分子目录。\n\n这个缺口一旦补上，目录就不再是一堵固定的墙，而成了系统可以有意去扩张的东西：它能告诉你哪些缺失的反应或砌块最能扩大「可合成且满足属性」分子的集合，并边走边加，同时保持足够小以便实用。这就把「可合成化学空间的覆盖」从供给目录的固定属性，变成一个你可以去优化的目标——直接升级整条合成感知工作线。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景骨干\n*复用一个现成的固定库合成感知生成器，作为自适应机制所包裹的未改动脚手架。*\n\n1. 从一个现成的合成感知生成器出发——它把分子当作一棵化学反应树，在固定的砌块(building block，即起始原料)目录和反应模板(reaction template，即已知反应式)目录上一步步拼装；直接复用 RxnFlow 或 RGFN 作为骨干。把目录存成普通查找表（按 id 查模板的反应式、按 id 查砌块的结构）外加一张「每个目录项一行向量」的可学习嵌入表，这样之后可以把新条目作为额外一行追加进去。它的输入是这份目录加一个属性打分器——任何 RDKit 可算的目标，如 QED(类药性评分)或对接打分代理(docking surrogate，结合强度的估计)；输出是一个可合成分子的采样器。这一步先不动目录。\n   - _为什么_: 你要作用在真正能代表前沿、其固定目录正是症结所在的系统上，而不是玩具模型。\n\n### 覆盖增益信号\n*通过读取生成器的 miss 分布、提出附近的缺失化学、并用前向反事实 rollout 打分，制造出逐候选的覆盖增益。*\n\n2. 对一批设计目标（每轮约 2048 个），让生成器对每个目标尝试 64 次，并记录每个目标上「它的最好尝试」距离「同一份目录在大量采样（每个目标 4096 次、每轮重算一次）下能达到的最高分」还差多少。把差得最多的 256 个目标留作 miss 清单。用「大量采样下的最好成绩」作为天花板，意味着这个差距衡量的是当前目录真正够不到的部分，而不是到某个未知完美答案的距离。\n\n*针对属性目标 $\\tau $ 的 miss 读数：oracle 最优值 $r*(\\tau )$ 与当前策略 $\\pi $ 在 K 条采样轨迹上取得的最高奖励之差。$\\Delta r$ 越大，说明该目标越是现有固定库无法触及的区域。*\n$$ \\Delta r(\\tau) = r^{*}(\\tau) - \\max_{k=1\\ldots K} r\\big(\\pi_k(\\tau)\\big) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 生成器自己失败得最惨的地方，正是一份免费标签，精准指出固定目录够不到哪些目标。\n3. 从一个当前目录之外、规模很大的反应与砌块备选池（USPTO 反应模板加上一份扩展 Enamine 砌块目录）里，用固定的反应指纹(reaction fingerprint)和分子指纹(molecule fingerprint，即反应或分子结构的数值描述)编码器，把每个候选项一次性嵌入到共享的 256 维空间。再把每个 miss 清单目标用「生成器为它做出的最好部分结构」的指纹取平均来嵌入，使目标落在同一空间里。对每个 miss 目标，按余弦相近度取它最近的 8 个候选；去重后的并集（每轮约一千个）就是候选集合。只在生成器失败的地方附近搜索，能把精力集中在真正缺化学的地方。\n   - _为什么_: 只在生成器失败的地方附近搜索，能把精力集中在真正缺化学的地方，而不是把整个池子全扫一遍。\n4. 给每个候选新增项打分：把它临时加进目录（给它一个从最近邻已有元素复制来的初始向量），在不重训生成器的前提下，让它做一次短程运行——每个 miss 目标 16 条轨迹、且新增项此时可被选用。统计在 miss 清单上「可达最高分」相对未加该项时提升了多少，只计正向提升，并在 miss 清单上取平均。这个覆盖增益(coverage-gain)数值表示该新增项能把「可合成且满足属性」的可达区域扩大多少。此处保持生成器冻结，是为了把「当前生成器能否立刻用上这个新增项去够到一个卡住的目标」单独隔离出来，与之后的重训区分开。它是一次快速的前向重跑，而不是对每个分子做逆向路线规划搜索。\n\n*候选元素 e 的覆盖增益：在 top miss 目标集合 S 上取平均，统计把 e 临时加入库 L 后、扰动策略 $\\pi '$ 短程前向 rollout 所能触及的最高奖励相对原策略的正向增量。它是一个以 oracle 奖励为单位的反事实可达性探针，无需任何 retrosynthesis 规划器。*\n$$ G(e) = \\frac{1}{|S|} \\sum_{\\tau \\in S} \\Big[ \\max_{k} r\\big(\\pi'_k(\\tau;\\, L \\cup \\{e\\})\\big) - \\max_{k} r\\big(\\pi_k(\\tau;\\, L)\\big) \\Big]_{+} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 直接模拟「如果有了这块化学会怎样」，是判断哪个缺失反应或砌块真正解锁了新可达分子的诚实做法。\n\n### 自适应库控制\n*用自适应覆盖增益阈值、在线录用并重训、以及预算封顶的退役，把目录变成一个状态变量。*\n\n5. 只录用那些覆盖增益超过一个自动设定门槛的候选新增项——门槛取最近五轮覆盖增益值的 90 分位数（最初几轮用现有历史，若一轮历史都没有则用本轮自己的分数）。要求增益严格高于门槛；若这样会一个都不录用，则退而录用那些达到或超过门槛的项，使流程不会停滞。因为这个门槛是一条滑动的分位线而非固定数字，所以无论在早期（很多新增项都看着不错）还是后期（收益递减）都保持合理。\n\n*录用集合 $A_{t}$：覆盖增益超过自适应阈值 $\\gamma _{t}$ 的候选扩展项；$\\gamma _{t}$ 取最近 W 轮 G 值的滑动 90 分位数，使门槛随当前增益分布自动调整，而非人工固定。*\n$$ A_t = \\{\\, e \\in E_t : G(e) > \\gamma_t \\,\\}, \\qquad \\gamma_t = \\mathrm{Quantile}_{0.90}\\big(\\{G(e)\\}_{\\text{last } W \\text{ rounds}}\\big) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 一条自我调整的门槛只放行真正有价值的新增项，你无需去猜一个固定截断值。\n6. 把录用的反应/砌块加进目录，并用生成器的标准训练目标在扩大后的目录上微调一轮——保留打分步骤里这些录用项的起始向量（不要重置），解冻整个网络，针对属性奖励跑固定的 2000 次训练更新，并混入四分之一的扩库前样本，使生成器在学会使用新条目时不会忘掉旧目录。因为新增项是依据覆盖增益临场决定的，目录不再是固定输入——它现在是生成过程自己在扩张的量。在扩大后的目录上重训，才真正改变了生成器能触及的分子集合。\n   - _为什么_: 在扩大后的目录上重训，才真正改变了生成器能触及的分子集合；而在线决定目录正是核心所在。\n7. 对任何在至少十轮之前录用的元素，在当前生成器下重新测它的覆盖增益；如果它连续三次检查都停留在「当前录用门槛的四分之一」以下，就把它移除，使目录总规模保持在一个固定预算之内。用「相对当前录用门槛」（而非固定数字）来判定是否过时，能让这个标准与新录用保持在同一尺度上。如果录用新条目会超出预算，就把当前最弱的条目强制移除（并列时先移最老的），直到目录装得下。给目录封顶能让它保持快速实用，于是贡献在于「该录用哪块化学」，而不是单纯堆更多化学。【作者需决定：目录预算设多大是作者必须自己拍板的选择——RGFN 那种小预算主打「快且可处理」，RxnFlow 那种大预算主打「够到更多化学」，两者讲的是不同的故事。】\n   - _为什么_: 给目录封顶能让它保持快速实用，于是贡献在于「该录用哪块化学」，而不是单纯堆更多化学。\n\n### 覆盖评估与归因隔离\n*逐轮测量可达覆盖率，消融录用规则以隔离信号作用，并与固定库基线对比。*\n\n8. 把「找 miss / 提候选 / 打分 / 录用 / 重训 / 退役」这个循环重复很多轮（最多 50 轮，覆盖率走平就停），每轮记录覆盖率——即在一份单独留出的设计目标面板上，生成器如今能触及「强分子」（标准设为真实类药分子参考集上 QED 或对接打分代理的 90 分位数）的目标占比——以及当前目录规模。把覆盖率按逐轮曲线汇报，而不是只看某一个标准值，这样结论就不取决于标准定在哪里。在固定目录规模下追踪可达覆盖率，才是真正要紧的结果。\n   - _为什么_: 在固定目录规模下追踪逐轮的可达覆盖率，才是真正要紧的结果，而非任何中间代理量。\n9. 把同一个循环原样再跑几遍，但改用以下规则决定录用：(a) 随机打分，(b) 候选在其来源数据库中的常见程度（一种与内容无关的流行度先验），(c) 一个用远更重的重跑（每个目标 256 条轨迹而非 16 条）在整个 miss 清单上算出来的昂贵『oracle』覆盖增益——全部在同一目录规模预算、每轮同样的录用数量、同样的重训下进行。对比这些覆盖率曲线，就能看出收益是否真来自覆盖增益信号挑对了化学。如果随机或按流行度新增也一样好，那这个信号其实没起作用；而 oracle 版本则显示廉价估计离最优能有多近。\n   - _为什么_: 如果随机或按流行度新增也一样好，那这个信号其实没起作用；这就是诚实性检验，而 oracle 版本则显示廉价估计离最优能有多近。\n10. 把自适应目录生成器与固定目录基线（RxnFlow、RGFN、SynFormer）在「可合成且满足属性」的可达覆盖率以及目录规模上作对比。要让对比公平：给每个基线一份同样规模预算的目录，用自适应方法所有轮次累计相同的更新总数去训练它，并在同一份留出面板、同一个「强分子」标准下评测。在一致的坐标轴上同时展示覆盖率如何增长、以及目录规模保持有界。与那些固定目录正是瓶颈的系统正面对比，才能证明你是在扩大前沿，而不仅仅在里面导航。\n   - _为什么_: 与那些固定目录正是瓶颈的系统正面对比，才能证明你是在扩大前沿，而不仅仅在里面导航。\n\n"},{"id":"43","run_dir":"run_prompt43_genexpr","index":43,"title":"Locus-Conditional Modality Allocation for Gene Expression Prediction","title_zh":"面向基因表达预测的位点条件化模态分配方法","method_name":"Locus-Conditional Modality Allocation (LoCMA)","hook":"On a sequence-to-expression model, replacing the global multimodal fusion layer with a per-locus capacity allocator driven by each modality's measured expression-uncertainty reduction is predicted to IMPROVE prediction most on exactly the loci where adding a modality currently HURTS the uniform-fusion baseline — the redundant-modality loci — rather than on the loci where the modality was already obviously useful. The surprising claim is that the largest gain comes from withholding capacity, not adding it.","anchor_pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","anchor_pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","domain_category":"Healthcare & Scientific ML","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides a per-locus estimate of how much each measured modality reduces expression-prediction uncertainty beyond what sequence already determines, so none can allocate the fused representation toward the modality that is actually informative at a given locus rather than treating all modalities as uniformly useful everywhere.","pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by partitioning the per-locus modality set by a measured discriminating property — each modality's locus-specific information gain g_m(L) = reduction in expression-prediction error variance when modality m is added given sequence — into a high-utility minority (retained at full fusion-channel width) and a near-redundant bulk (collapsed to a low-rank residual channel), with an error decomposition bounding how this differentiated allocation recovers the full-fusion prediction; this is C04's protect-the-minority / crush-the-bulk move with the information-gain distribution as the load-bearing evidence, not a free softmax gate.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved paper trains the multimodal model with an objective that targets modality-utility calibration itself (predicting, before fusing, whether a modality will move the expression estimate), so utility is never an explicit learned quantity the model can act on.","pattern_id":"targeted_self_supervised_objective","pattern_name":"Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective","sub_pattern":"C17 (Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by a property-targeting pretext objective whose pairing geometry forces the representation to encode g_m(L): for each locus we form two views — a full-modality view and a modality-m-dropped view — and replace the generic inner-product contrastive similarity with a residual-gain-sensitive measure so that the only representation minimizing the loss is one whose per-modality utility head reproduces the held-out modality's marginal reduction of the expression residual; this is C17's cross-view pairing + inner-product-primitive substitution, making modality utility a first-class learned quantity the C04 allocator reads.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"multimodal signal integration for gene expression prediction (sequence-to-expression regulatory genomics)","n_papers":33,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":20},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":18,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"DeepCBA: A deep learning framework for gene expression prediction in maize based on DNA sequences and chromatin interactions"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"EPInformer: a scalable deep learning framework for gene expression prediction by integrating promoter-enhancer sequences with multimodal epigenomic data"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Deep learning assisted cancer disease prediction from gene expression data using WT-GAN"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Deep-learning prediction of gene expression from personal genomes"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Prediction of gene expression-based breast cancer proliferation scores from histopathology whole slide images using deep learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Pan-Cancer Drug Sensitivity Prediction from Gene Expression using Deep Learning"}],"more":12},{"year":2025,"n":15,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"EMGP-Net: A Hybrid Deep Learning Architecture for Breast Cancer Gene Expression Prediction"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"HybridDLDR: A hybrid deep learning-based drug resistance prediction system of Glioblastoma (GBM) using molecular descriptors and gene expression data"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Deep Learning for Drug Response Prediction with Gene Expression Data"},{"source":"openalex","title":"XpressO: An explanatory deep learning pipeline for the prediction and visualization of gene expression heterogeneity in breast tumors"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Drug discovery and mechanism prediction with explainable graph neural networks"},{"source":"openalex","title":"TRAPT: a multi-stage fused deep learning framework for predicting transcriptional regulators based on large-scale epigenomic data"}],"more":9},{"year":2026,"n":1,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"}],"more":0}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":12,"share":0.364},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":8,"share":0.242},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":7,"share":0.212},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":6,"share":0.182},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":5,"share":0.152},{"pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","count":3,"share":0.091},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":2,"share":0.061},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":1,"share":0.03}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"State-of-the-art sequence-to-expression models integrate experimental modalities (epigenomic tracks, chromatin contacts) into a single fused representation under a fixed, input-agnostic fusion map: EPInformer (semanticscholar:711f427eb3d18bf968d0712c6ce23545dc6de638) feeds DNA sequence, DNase/H3K27ac signal, and Hi-C contacts through a feature-fusion layer that weights every modality the same way for every gene locus, and AlphaGenome (openalex:W4411721855) goes the other direction by predicting those experimental tracks as OUTPUTS of one long-context DNA model rather than consuming them as conditioning inputs. The failure this exposes is locus-conditional: for a locus whose regulatory state is already determined by proximal promoter sequence, an added epigenomic or chromatin modality is largely redundant with sequence and the extra capacity spent fusing it cannot improve (and empirically can degrade) the prediction, whereas for a locus governed by a distal, cell-type-specific enhancer the same modality is decisive; because the fusion weight is locus-independent and the model has no internal estimate of how much each modality reduces expression uncertainty at THIS locus, it cannot allocate representational capacity to the modality that is actually informative here, and the community-benchmark result that deeper sequence-only context and naive multimodal stacking fail to beat simple baselines (openalex:W4403338304, openalex:W4402694371) is the visible symptom of this misallocation.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:711f427eb3d18bf968d0712c6ce23545dc6de638","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"EPInformer is a transformer that integrates promoter+enhancer DNA sequence with epigenomic signals (DNase, H3K27ac) and optional Hi-C contacts through a feature-fusion layer and a promoter-enhancer interaction encoder, trained per cell type. Its fusion is input-agnostic: every modality is concatenated/attended with a learned-but-locus-independent weighting, so the model carries no per-locus estimate of how much a given modality reduces expression uncertainty beyond sequence, and it cannot down-weight a modality that is redundant with sequence at one locus while up-weighting it at another."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4411721855","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"AlphaGenome takes 1 Mb of DNA and predicts thousands of functional tracks (expression, accessibility, histone marks, contacts) at base-pair resolution from sequence alone. It treats the experimental modalities as prediction TARGETS, not as conditioning inputs, so at inference it cannot use a measured epigenomic/chromatin signal to correct a locus where sequence is insufficient, and it offers no mechanism for deciding when measured signal would add information over its own sequence prediction."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4409502416","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"TRAPT fuses cis-regulatory-element regulatory potentials with genome-wide binding sites through a multi-stage fixed pipeline to infer transcriptional-regulator activity. The fusion stages are ordered and static, so the contribution of each epigenomic source is fixed by the pipeline rather than estimated per target, leaving open how to weight modalities by their locus-specific informativeness."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4406259516","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Multimodal Expression integrates promoter sequence with pre/post-transcriptional epigenetic features through a single Transformer over concatenated modality tokens. The concatenation assumes all modalities are present and uniformly useful; it has no notion of modality redundancy with sequence and degrades when an added modality is uninformative for a given gene."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"multimodal signal integration for gene expression prediction (sequence-to-expression regulatory genomics)","venue":"ICLR 2026","time":"2026","data":["ENCODE/FANTOM epigenomic tracks (DNase-seq, ATAC-seq, H3K27ac/H3K4me3 ChIP-seq, DNA methylation)","3D chromatin contacts (Hi-C / Micro-C)","reference DNA sequence + matched CAGE-seq / RNA-seq gene expression labels (e.g. EPInformer, Enformer/Borzoi training corpora)","DREAM-challenge random-promoter expression measurements"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (approx 90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with regulatory-genomics background and cloud GPU access","preference":"both","baseline":"EPInformer (multimodal promoter-enhancer fusion) and AlphaGenome (unified long-context sequence model)","limitation":"current multimodal expression models fuse sequence + epigenomic + chromatin tracks as always-available, uniformly-weighted inputs; they cannot tell when an added modality carries information beyond what sequence already encodes, so longer context / more tracks yield diminishing and sometimes negative returns","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The pipeline is sequential (the declared coherence thread): leg B (C17 pretext objective) PRODUCES a calibrated per-locus, per-modality utility quantity g_m(L), and leg A (C04 decomposition) CONSUMES it to allocate the fused representation. Define g_m(L) concretely as the modality-conditional information gain at locus L: g_m(L) = log Var[y_L | seq, modalities\\m] - log Var[y_L | seq, modalities], i.e. the log-ratio of the model's predicted expression-error variance with modality m withheld versus included, where y_L is the measured CAGE/RNA-seq expression of the gene at L, seq is its promoter+enhancer DNA, and the variances are read from a heteroscedastic Gaussian output head (mean+log-variance) — a model-internal readout, computed by two forward passes (full input vs input with modality m's tracks masked to their dataset mean). The free index m ranges over the fixed measured-modality set M = {DNase/ATAC accessibility, H3K27ac, H3K4me3, DNA methylation, Hi-C contact vector}; the layer the variances are read from is the final output head only (selection rule: the head producing the expression label, not intermediate layers). Leg B trains a per-modality utility head u_m(L) to regress g_m(L) WITHOUT a separate utility label: for each locus it builds a full-modality view phi_full(L) and a modality-m-dropped view phi_drop_m(L), and minimizes a contrastive objective in which the similarity primitive is replaced from inner-product to s(a,b)=-||a-b||^2 scaled so that the pull between phi_full and phi_drop_m is weighted by the OBSERVED residual gain (the held-out modality's reduction of the expression residual on the training locus), so only a representation whose u_m head reproduces that gain minimizes the loss (C17's primitive substitution + cross-view sourcing). Leg A then forms the fused representation by allocating channel width per locus: it ranks modalities by u_m(L), routes the top-k(L) (k chosen by a utility threshold tau, a named hyperparameter) through full-width fusion channels and collapses the remaining low-utility modalities into a single shared low-rank residual channel of rank r (named hyperparameter), instead of EPInformer's locus-independent feature-fusion layer that gives every modality equal channel width at every locus. The load-bearing C04 artifact is an error decomposition: we bound the expression-prediction MSE of the allocated model minus the full-fusion model by sum over routed-out modalities of a term proportional to g_m(L), so when g_m(L) is small (redundant modality) the differentiated allocation provably recovers the full-fusion objective while freeing capacity, and when g_m(L) is large the modality is never routed out — this bound, not the routing idea, is the contribution and is what distinguishes it from heuristic gating. The bridge weight between the (log-variance-unit) g_m(L) and the (channel-count-unit) allocation is the threshold tau plus a temperature beta on the utility softmax, both named hyperparameters fixed by validation R^2.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules because the utility quantity g_m(L) is literally the output of leg B and the input of leg A — a sequential pipeline, confirmed by the fact that the C04 error bound is written in terms of the same g_m(L) the C17 objective is trained to encode; if they were independent the bound could not reference the trained quantity. (b) Alternatives considered and rejected: (1) a free end-to-end softmax gate over modalities (gated MoE) — rejected because method_lineage flags collateral node c0 (gated multimodal fusion) and a bare learned gate would regress onto it with no measured information-gain criterion and no recoverability bound; we avoid this by defining the partition criterion as the MEASURED variance-reduction g_m(L) and supplying the C04 error decomposition, which a gate does not have. (2) a global SHAP-style modality-importance score — rejected because it is locus-independent, exactly the bottleneck. Avoided node recorded: c0 (gated MoE / input-dependent gate).","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on the EPInformer training corpus (DNase, H3K27ac, Hi-C + promoter-enhancer DNA, CAGE/RNA-seq labels, K562/GM12878 cell types), train the heteroscedastic backbone, the leg-B utility objective, and the leg-A allocator, using whole-chromosome held-out splits. If the candidate works, held-out per-locus expression R^2 INCREASES relative to the uniform-fusion EPInformer baseline, and the increase is concentrated in the low-information (redundant-modality) bin — loci where max_m g_m(L) is small and where uniform fusion currently degrades R^2 — while the high-information bin stays at parity. The named load-bearing variable is the per-locus modality information gain g_m(L). Negative control: permute the g_m(L) vector across loci before training the utility head u_m (so the allocator routes modalities by a locus-shuffled, mechanism-destroyed signal); the predicted effect is that held-out test R^2 in the redundant-modality bin falls back to the uniform-fusion baseline (the downstream task-outcome metric returns to baseline), not merely that g_m's own value changes. Positive control: a stripped model that allocates using ONLY g_m(L) (the variance-reduction term, no learned contrastive geometry) should recover most of the redundant-bin R^2 gain, identifying g_m(L) as the mechanism.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:711f427eb3d18bf968d0712c6ce23545dc6de638","delta":"EPInformer fuses sequence, epigenomic signal, and Hi-C through a locus-independent feature-fusion layer that weights every modality identically at every gene; we construct a per-locus modality information-gain quantity g_m(L) from a heteroscedastic head and an error decomposition that allocates fusion capacity by g_m(L), which their fixed-fusion architecture neither computes nor bounds."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4411721855","delta":"AlphaGenome predicts experimental modalities as OUTPUT tracks from sequence alone; we treat measured modalities as conditioning INPUTS and derive when a measured modality is non-redundant with sequence at a locus (g_m(L) large), a per-locus input-utility quantity AlphaGenome's output-only formulation cannot express."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4406259516","delta":"Multimodal Expression concatenates all modality tokens into one Transformer assuming uniform per-gene usefulness; we measure each modality's locus-specific residual reduction and route low-utility modalities into a low-rank residual channel, with a recoverability bound that concatenation has no analogue for."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4407806228","delta":"Seq2Exp uses a single global information bottleneck to select WHICH regulatory elements are active; we estimate HOW MUCH each MODALITY reduces expression uncertainty per locus and allocate fusion capacity accordingly — a modality-utility decomposition, not an element-selection bottleneck."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:711f427eb3d18bf968d0712c6ce23545dc6de638","what_step_was_missed":"EPInformer built a flexible architecture that CAN ingest variable multimodal inputs (DNase alone, or DNase+H3K27ac+Hi-C), but it never constructed a per-locus quantity for how much each ingested modality reduces expression-prediction uncertainty, nor an error decomposition bounding what is lost by down-weighting a modality at a locus where it is redundant; without that variance-reduction construction and its recoverability bound, the fusion layer can only weight modalities globally, so the locus-conditional allocation our contribution rests on does not exist in their method."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":306,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"Layer-1 hard floor did not fire: gap_closure_reject_check aggregate is borderline (no Reject lesson candidate_match: yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat is not exact-mechanism overlap. In the soft zone, recipe_application_check.verdict = applied on BOTH legs (C04's recoverability bound and C17's residual-gain-sensitive primitive substitution are present), and the two borderline reject lessons ('sensitivity proxy reads as rediscovery'; 'recombines existing contrastive recipes') hit addressable presentation concerns rather than load-bearing structural failures and are already answered by the candidate's error decomposition and its positive/negative controls — so advance with both borderlines plus the global-modality-confidence threat surfaced for Phase 4's reviewer_concerns_and_responses.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides a per-locus estimate of how much each measured modality reduces expression-prediction uncertainty beyond what sequence already determines, so none can allocate the fused representation toward the modality that is actually informative at a given locus rather than treating all modalities as uniformly useful everywhere.","main_pattern":"heterogeneous_decomposition","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is treating the partition criterion itself as the contribution while leaving its value unproven; papers propose a sensitivity or redundancy discriminator and reviewers immediately map it onto an established technique, so the differentiated treatment reads as a relabeling rather than a new mechanism.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Presenting a sensitivity or redundancy proxy as the novelty invites the verdict that it rediscovers known mixed-precision or low-rank results unless it is sharply differentiated from the obvious prior criterion.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The partition criterion g_m(L) (a variance-reduction information-gain term) could be read as a known modality-importance proxy, but the candidate ties it to an explicit error decomposition bounding recoverability and to a learned C17 calibration objective, differentiating it from a bare importance score — borderline, not triggered."},{"lesson_quoted":"Omitting comparison against both the strongest uniform baseline and the obvious cheap alternative (SVD/PCA, structured dropout, a natively trained smaller model) leaves reviewers unable to tell whether the partition buys anything at all.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"falsification_prediction explicitly compares against the uniform-fusion EPInformer baseline and a positive-control stripped model using only g_m(L), supplying the differentiated-vs-uniform contrast the lesson demands."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a storage or throughput claim only on toy-scale models — where the compression bottleneck does not actually bite — undermines the entire motivation no matter how clean the method is.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Validation is on the real EPInformer CAGE/RNA-seq corpus with whole-chromosome held-out splits in K562/GM12878, the regime where the multimodal-redundancy bottleneck actually bites, not a toy benchmark."},{"lesson_quoted":"Skipping any analysis of why the heterogeneity exists — the data or value distribution that drives the partition — makes the technical novelty and the potential impact impossible to assess.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism_steps step 2 computes the per-locus gain distribution g_m(L) empirically and stratifies loci into redundancy bins, supplying exactly the value distribution that justifies the partition."},{"lesson_quoted":"Bolting together established components (distillation plus pruning plus calibration) without an error bound or artifact specific to the new setting reads as incremental even when the target application is timely and important.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate supplies a setting-specific error decomposition bounding allocated-vs-full-fusion expression MSE by a sum proportional to g_m(L) — the C04 load-bearing artifact, not a bolt-together."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved paper trains the multimodal model with an objective that targets modality-utility calibration itself (predicting, before fusing, whether a modality will move the expression estimate), so utility is never an explicit learned quantity the model can act on.","main_pattern":"targeted_self_supervised_objective","sub_pattern":"C17 (Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring shape is sourcing the pairing/alignment signal by composing two already-published components and presenting the composition itself as the contribution; these papers never re-derive WHY this particular pairing geometry uniquely encodes the targeted property and supply no operational definition, probe, or isolating ablation.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Concatenating a frozen off-the-shelf predictor's output as an extra input channel injects no novel insight — it reads as combining two published systems regardless of the accuracy gain.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The utility signal is not a frozen external predictor's output channel; it is g_m(L) read from the model's own heteroscedastic head and used to reshape the contrastive pairing geometry, an intrinsic re-engineering not a concatenation."},{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a representation is 'disentangled' or property-specific without an operational definition, a direct probe, or an isolating ablation leaves the central claim ungrounded and unverifiable.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The targeted property (per-modality utility) has an operational definition g_m(L)=log-variance-ratio, a direct probe (regress u_m against held-out g_m), and an isolating ablation (label-permute negative control), exactly what the lesson requires."},{"lesson_quoted":"A hard-pair construction strategy that closely recombines existing mixup/contrastive recipes collapses to 'incremental' the moment the nearest pair-construction baselines are missing from the comparison.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The cross-view (full vs modality-dropped) pairing is a recognizable contrastive construction; novelty rests on the residual-gain-sensitive similarity substitution, so the nearest modality-dropout-contrastive baseline should be named in Phase 4 to avoid the incremental read — borderline, surfaced not triggered."},{"lesson_quoted":"Gains attributed to a new alignment component evaporate under scrutiny when the ablation suite never isolates that component from the borrowed backbone.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The positive control (allocate using only g_m(L), no learned contrastive geometry) and negative control (permuted gain) isolate the new pairing component from the EPInformer backbone."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No gap_closure entry triggered: the anchor C04 entry is borderline on the 'sensitivity/redundancy proxy reads as rediscovery' lesson (the g_m(L) criterion resembles a known importance score) but is differentiated by the recoverability error decomposition; the C17 entry is borderline on the 'recombines existing contrastive recipes' lesson, resolvable by naming the nearest modality-dropout-contrastive baseline. Both borderlines are addressable and neither marks a Reject lesson candidate_match: yes."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides a per-locus estimate of how much each measured modality reduces expression-prediction uncertainty beyond what sequence already determines, so none can allocate the fused representation toward the modality that is actually informative at a given locus rather than treating all modalities as uniformly useful everywhere.","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Discriminate components by a magnitude-, sensitivity-, influence-, or redundancy-based criterion into a high-impact minority and a near-redundant bulk, then preserve the minority while aggressively compressing the bulk; the load-bearing artifact is an error/sensitivity decomposition that bounds how the differentiated treatment recovers the original objective.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism partitions the per-locus modality set by the redundancy/influence criterion g_m(L), routes the high-utility minority through full-width fusion channels and collapses the near-redundant bulk into a shared low-rank residual channel, AND supplies the C04 load-bearing error decomposition bounding allocated-minus-full-fusion MSE by a sum proportional to g_m(L) — the cluster's signature protect-minority/crush-bulk move plus its recoverability bound are both present.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved paper trains the multimodal model with an objective that targets modality-utility calibration itself (predicting, before fusing, whether a modality will move the expression estimate), so utility is never an explicit learned quantity the model can act on.","sub_pattern":"C17 (Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Re-engineer the pairing/alignment geometry of a contrastive objective so the targeted property is the only thing whose encoding minimizes the loss; the decisive act is replacing or inverting a default geometric primitive such as swapping inner-product similarity for a property-sensitive one, sourcing the pairing from a complementary view of the same entity.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism sources pairs from a complementary view (full-modality vs modality-m-dropped view of the same locus) and replaces the inner-product similarity with a residual-gain-sensitive measure s(a,b)=-||a-b||^2 weighted by the observed held-out-modality residual reduction, so only a representation whose u_m head reproduces g_m(L) minimizes the loss — the cluster's cross-view sourcing plus geometric-primitive substitution are both performed, not just asserted.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries perform their cluster's distinctive move: C04's partition-plus-recoverability-bound is in core_mechanism's error decomposition, and C17's inner-product-to-residual-gain-sensitive primitive substitution under cross-view sourcing is explicit; neither leg merely enacts the parent pattern's generic gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["heterogeneous_decomposition","targeted_self_supervised_objective"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"The composition {heterogeneous_decomposition, targeted_self_supervised_objective} matches none of the three reject-favored compositions (heterogeneous_decomposition pairs in the table with self_supervised_signal_engineering, structural_prior_encoding, or architectural_operator_substitution — targeted_self_supervised_objective is a distinct pattern_id and not among them), so no anti-pattern fires."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"A novel modality contribution confidence-enhanced multimodal deep learning framework for multiomics data","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"This 2025-10 framework also rejects the equal-modality-contribution assumption and learns per-modality confidence weights to improve a fused multiomics representation, which is the closest competitor to the candidate's modality-utility idea. The candidate stands or falls on three differentiators it does not subsume: (1) it computes utility PER LOCUS (g_m(L), conditioned on the gene's regulatory state) rather than a global per-modality confidence over the whole dataset, which is exactly the bottleneck the candidate targets; (2) it is a sequence-to-EXPRESSION REGRESSION with a measured variance-reduction criterion, not a classification confidence; and (3) it supplies a recoverability error decomposition bounding what allocation loses, which the confidence framework does not. If a reviewer showed that a single global modality-confidence weight already captures the per-locus gain (i.e. g_m(L) does not actually vary across loci), the candidate's contribution would collapse to that prior work.","addressable_via":"The candidate already isolates this via the redundancy-bin stratification in falsification_prediction (showing g_m(L) varies across loci and the gain concentrates in the redundant-modality bin); Phase 4 reviewer_concerns_and_responses should name this paper explicitly as the global-confidence baseline to dodge the subsumption."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Locus-Conditional Modality Allocation for Gene Expression Prediction\n\n**Method.** Locus-Conditional Modality Allocation (LoCMA)\n\n## Motivation\nComputational biologists predict how strongly a gene will be expressed by feeding a model the DNA sequence around the gene plus several measured experimental signals: how open the DNA is (chromatin accessibility, e.g. DNase or ATAC), chemical marks on the DNA-packaging proteins (histone marks like H3K27ac), and which far-apart DNA regions physically touch (3D contact data, Hi-C). Today's best models, such as EPInformer, mix all of these signals together with one fixed recipe that treats every signal as equally useful for every gene. The problem is that usefulness is not the same everywhere. For a gene whose behavior is already fully explained by the nearby DNA sequence, an extra measured signal adds nothing — yet the model still spends effort blending it in, and that wasted effort can actually make the prediction worse. For a different gene controlled by a distant switch, that same signal is essential. Because the mixing recipe is identical for all genes, the model has no way to know, at this particular gene, how much each signal is really worth.\n\nThis is timely because the field has just discovered, through careful benchmarks, that simply adding more signals or longer DNA context stops helping and sometimes hurts — the open question has shifted from 'how do we cram in more data?' to 'which data is worth using, and where?'. Two tools needed to answer it are now standard: a model can report its own uncertainty per gene, and it can be run with any signal switched off, so we can directly measure how much each signal reduces the model's uncertainty at each gene. Prior work stopped short for concrete reasons: EPInformer (bioRxiv 2024-08) built a flexible model that can take signals in any combination but never measured each signal's per-gene worth; AlphaGenome (bioRxiv 2025-06) chose to predict these signals as outputs from sequence alone, so it cannot use a measured signal to fix a gene the sequence gets wrong; and concatenation models (2024-12) simply assume every signal is uniformly useful. When this gap closes, models can spend their limited capacity on the signal that actually matters at each gene, turning today's 'more is not better' frustration into a controllable choice.\n\n## Method\n### Modality-Utility Estimation\n*Measure and learn, per locus, how much each modality reduces expression-prediction uncertainty.*\n\n1. Start from an EPInformer-style multimodal backbone (a network that already encodes promoter+enhancer DNA, the epigenomic tracks, and the Hi-C contact data into one per-gene feature vector) and reuse it untouched up to that fused per-gene vector. Replace only its single expression-number output with a two-output layer that emits both a predicted expression $mean (mu_{L})$ and a predicted uncertainty expressed as a log-variance $(s_{L}),$ passing the raw uncertainty output through a softplus so the variance can never be negative. Train the whole thing with a Gaussian likelihood loss — which simultaneously rewards an accurate mean and a well-calibrated uncertainty — on the standard CAGE/RNA-seq expression labels (log-transformed), stopping when validation likelihood stops improving, so the per-gene uncertainty is meaningful and not arbitrary.\n   - _Why_: You can only measure how much a signal helps at a gene if the model can first say how unsure it is at that gene.\n2. For every gene and every measured modality m in the fixed set {DNase/ATAC accessibility, H3K27ac, H3K4me3, DNA methylation, Hi-C}, run the model a second time with that one modality blanked out — every input channel of that modality (all its coverage bins, or the whole Hi-C contact vector) set to its average value over the training data, while the DNA sequence and the other modalities stay exactly as they are. Read the model's predicted uncertainty in this blanked-out run and subtract the predicted uncertainty from the full run: this difference is the per-gene information gain $g_{m}(L)$ of modality m (Eq. 1). Collect these numbers into one gain vector per gene. If blanking a modality makes the model much less certain, that modality was carrying real information at this gene; if the uncertainty barely moves, it was redundant. No human-provided label is needed — the model supervises itself.\n\n*Per-locus information gain of modality m: the log-ratio of predicted expression-error variance with m withheld versus included, read from the heteroscedastic head.*\n$$ g_m(L) = \\log \\mathrm{Var}\\!\\left[y_L \\mid \\mathrm{seq}, \\mathcal{M}\\setminus m\\right] - \\log \\mathrm{Var}\\!\\left[y_L \\mid \\mathrm{seq}, \\mathcal{M}\\right] \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: If blanking a signal makes the model much less certain, that signal was carrying real information at this gene; if nothing changes, it was redundant.\n3. For each gene, take two snapshots of the same internal fused feature vector that the prediction head reads from: one computed with all modalities present (call it $phi_{full})$ and, for each modality m, one computed with modality m blanked out in the very same way as the previous step (call it $\\mathit{phi\\_drop\\_m}).$ Do not invent a new blanking or pooling procedure — reuse the masked runs you already did. Normalize both snapshots to unit length before they are compared later. Comparing the same gene with and without a given signal, at the exact layer the predictor uses, is the cleanest way to expose what that signal contributes.\n   - _Why_: Comparing the same gene with and without a signal is the cleanest way to expose what that signal contributes.\n4. Train a small per-modality utility head — a shared 2-layer network applied to the full-modality snapshot that outputs one utility number $u_{m}(L)$ for each modality — to predict the information gain $g_{m}(L)$ you measured. At the same time add a contrastive term that pulls the full snapshot $(phi_{full})$ and each modality-dropped snapshot $(\\mathit{phi\\_drop\\_m})$ together using a distance-based similarity, the negative squared distance $- ||a- b||^{2}$ (i.e. closer vectors score higher), instead of the usual dot-product. Weight each such pull by how much the dropped modality actually reduced the squared prediction error on that gene (clipped at zero and rescaled to lie between 0 and 1 within each batch), and treat the other genes in the same batch as the contrasting negatives. Balance the prediction term and the contrastive term equally by default, re-tuning only if their magnitudes drift apart. Let the gradients flow back into the modality encoders so that 'how useful is each modality here' becomes an explicit learned quantity; the residual-gain weighting means only a representation that genuinely encodes per-modality usefulness can minimize the loss.\n\n*Property-targeting pretext loss: a utility head $u_{m}$ regresses $g_{m}(L)$ while a residual-gain-weighted (weight $w_{m})$ cross-view pull replaces inner-product similarity, so only utility-encoding representations minimize it.*\n$$ \\mathcal{L}_B = \\sum_{m\\in\\mathcal{M}} \\Big[ \\big(u_m(L) - g_m(L)\\big)^2 + \\lambda\\, w_m(L)\\, \\big\\| \\phi_{\\mathrm{full}}(L) - \\phi_{\\mathrm{drop}_m}(L) \\big\\|^2 \\Big] \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This makes 'how useful is each modality here' an explicit learned quantity, and the special weighting means only a representation that genuinely encodes per-modality usefulness can minimize the loss.\n\n### Locus-Conditional Allocation\n*Route high-utility modalities to full-width fusion and redundant ones to a low-rank channel, with a recoverability bound.*\n\n5. Freeze the utility head from the previous step. Then, at each gene, look up each modality's utility score and split the modalities into two groups: those scoring above a threshold tau go through the full-width fusion channels (their full feature width is kept and they are combined using soft weights derived from the utility scores with a temperature control beta that sharpens or softens the weighting), while the remaining lower-utility modalities are concatenated and squeezed together through one shared small-capacity projection of a fixed low rank r, yielding a single compact residual vector that is added back in — this is the 'collapse the redundant signals' step. An error bound (Eq. 3) guarantees that the accuracy lost by squeezing is at most proportional to the total information gain of the squeezed modalities, so genes where a modality is genuinely informative cannot be hurt. Choose the threshold tau, the temperature beta, and the residual rank r by a small grid search that maximizes validation prediction accuracy (R-squared). 【author decision: whether the shared low-rank residual projection is one global matrix or a separate one per cell type, and whether the kept full-width modalities are stacked side-by-side (concatenated) or added together, are design choices the authors must make — both keep the error guarantee but change how capacity is spent; the axis is how widely the residual channel's parameters are shared.】\n\n*Recoverability bound: the allocated model's expression MSE departs from the full-fusion model by at most a constant times the total information gain of the routed-out (low-utility) modalities.*\n$$ \\big| \\mathrm{MSE}_{\\mathrm{alloc}}(L) - \\mathrm{MSE}_{\\mathrm{full}}(L) \\big| \\;\\leq\\; C \\sum_{m \\,:\\, u_m(L) \\leq \\tau} g_m(L) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Spend full capacity only on the signals that matter at this gene; the bound proves you cannot hurt genes where a signal is genuinely informative, which is what separates this from an arbitrary gate.\n6. Keeping the utility head frozen so the per-gene routing decisions stay fixed, fine-tune the expression predictor (and the small shared squeezing projection) on these per-gene allocated representations, using the same Gaussian likelihood loss and training schedule as the first step, until validation likelihood stops improving. Freeing capacity away from redundant signals lets the model better fit the genes where naive blending was previously wasting effort, moving their predictions toward the true expression values, while genes where a modality is genuinely informative stay the same. You may keep the backbone encoders frozen here to isolate the effect of the allocation; if a full fine-tune gives different validation accuracy, report both.\n   - _Why_: Freeing capacity from redundant signals lets the model fit the genes where naive blending was previously wasting effort, moving their predictions toward the true values.\n\n### Redundancy-Binned Validation\n*Test that gains concentrate in the redundant-modality bin and vanish when the utility signal is destroyed.*\n\n7. Evaluate using the standard 12-fold whole-chromosome cross-validation: each fold holds out entire chromosomes so no gene appears in both training and test. Compute the per-gene R-squared (the usual coefficient of determination between predicted and measured held-out expression) and sort genes into three equal groups (terciles) by how informative their single best modality is (the largest per-gene information gain across modalities); call the lowest group the redundant-modality bin. Within each group, compare LoCMA against the uniform-fusion baseline (the same backbone with no allocation). As a control, before training the utility head, shuffle the per-gene gain vectors across genes with one fixed random permutation (keeping each gene's modality order intact), retrain, and check that the improvement in the redundant-modality bin disappears — its R-squared should fall back to the uniform-fusion baseline. The claim is specific: the improvement should appear in the redundant-modality bin and vanish once the per-gene usefulness signal is destroyed by shuffling.\n   - _Why_: The claim is specific — the improvement should appear in the redundant-modality bin and disappear when the per-gene usefulness signal is destroyed by shuffling.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 面向基因表达预测的位点条件化模态分配方法\n\n**方法名称.** Locus-Conditional Modality Allocation (LoCMA)\n\n## 研究动机\n计算生物学家预测一个基因的表达强度时，会给模型输入该基因周围的 DNA 序列，再加上若干实测的实验信号：DNA 的开放程度（染色质可及性，如 DNase 或 ATAC）、DNA 缠绕蛋白上的化学标记（组蛋白修饰，如 H3K27ac）、以及相隔很远的 DNA 区域之间的物理接触（三维接触数据 Hi-C）。当前最好的模型（例如 EPInformer）用一套固定配方把这些信号混在一起，对每个基因都把每种信号当成同等有用。问题在于：有用程度并非处处相同。对于一个其行为已经被附近 DNA 序列完全解释的基因，额外的实测信号毫无增益——但模型仍要花力气去融合它，这份被浪费的力气反而可能让预测变差。而对另一个由远端开关控制的基因，同一种信号却至关重要。由于混合配方对所有基因都一样，模型无法知道在这个特定基因上每种信号到底值多少。\n\n这一问题正当其时：通过严谨的基准测试，领域刚刚发现，单纯增加信号或延长 DNA 上下文不再有帮助、有时反而有害——开放问题已经从「如何塞进更多数据」转向「哪种数据值得用、在哪里用」。回答它所需的两件工具如今已是标配：模型可以逐基因报告自己的不确定性，也可以在关掉任一信号的情况下运行，于是我们能直接测量每种信号在每个基因上把模型不确定性降低了多少。先前工作止步于此各有具体原因：EPInformer（bioRxiv 2024-08）造出了能任意组合信号的灵活模型，却从未测量每种信号的逐基因价值；AlphaGenome（bioRxiv 2025-06）选择仅从序列把这些信号作为输出来预测，因此无法用实测信号去纠正序列判断错误的基因；而拼接式模型（2024-12）干脆假设每种信号都同等有用。一旦填补这一空缺，模型就能把有限的容量花在每个基因上真正重要的信号上，把今天「越多反而越差」的困境变成一个可控的选择。\n\n## 方法\n### 模态效用估计\n*逐位点测量并学习每种模态对表达预测不确定性的降低程度。*\n\n1. 从一个 EPInformer 式的多模态主干网络出发（该网络已能把启动子+增强子 DNA、表观基因组轨迹以及 Hi-C 接触数据编码成每个基因一个融合特征向量），并原封不动地复用到该融合向量为止。只把它输出单一表达数值的头替换为一个双输出层，同时给出预测表达均值 $mu_{L}$ 和以对数方差形式表示的预测不确定性 $s_{L}$，并让原始不确定性输出先经过 softplus 函数，保证方差永不为负。用高斯似然损失(Gaussian Negative-Log-Likelihood)训练整个网络——该损失同时奖励准确的均值与标定良好的不确定性——在标准的 CAGE/RNA-seq 表达标签（取对数后）上训练，待验证集似然不再改善时停止，从而使每个基因的不确定性是有实际意义的，而非任意值。\n   - _为什么_: 只有当模型能先说出它在某个基因上有多不确定，你才能测量某种信号在该基因上帮了多少忙。\n2. 对每个基因、每种固定集合 {DNase/ATAC 可及性, H3K27ac, H3K4me3, DNA 甲基化, Hi-C} 中的实测模态 m，把这一种模态置空后再跑一次模型——即把该模态的每个输入通道（它的全部覆盖度区间，或整条 Hi-C 接触向量）都设为其在训练数据上的平均值，同时保持 DNA 序列和其余模态完全不变。读出这次置空运行中模型的预测不确定性，再减去完整运行的预测不确定性：这个差值就是模态 m 在该基因上的信息增益 $g_{m}(L)$（见式 1）。把这些数值汇集成每个基因一条增益向量。如果置空某模态让模型大幅变得更不确定，说明该模态在这个基因上携带了真实信息；若不确定性几乎不变，则它是冗余的。无需人工标签——模型自我监督。\n\n*模态 m 的位点信息增益：在剔除 m 与纳入 m 两种情形下，模型对表达预测误差方差的对数比值，由异方差输出头读出。*\n$$ g_m(L) = \\log \\mathrm{Var}\\!\\left[y_L \\mid \\mathrm{seq}, \\mathcal{M}\\setminus m\\right] - \\log \\mathrm{Var}\\!\\left[y_L \\mid \\mathrm{seq}, \\mathcal{M}\\right] \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 如果置空某信号让模型大幅变得更不确定，说明该信号在这个基因上携带了真实信息；若毫无变化，则它是冗余的。\n3. 对每个基因，从预测头所读取的同一个内部融合特征向量上取两份快照：一份在所有模态都存在时计算（记为 $phi_{full}$），另一份对每种模态 m 在与上一步完全相同的方式下把模态 m 置空后计算（记为 $\\mathit{phi\\_drop\\_m}$）。不要发明新的置空或池化流程——直接复用你已经做过的置空运行。在后续比较之前，把两份快照都归一化为单位长度。在预测器实际使用的那一层上，用同一个基因在「有」与「无」某信号两种情形下作对比，是揭示该信号贡献的最干净方式。\n   - _为什么_: 用同一个基因在「有」与「无」某信号两种情形下作对比，是揭示该信号贡献的最干净方式。\n4. 训练一个按模态划分的小效用头——一个作用于全模态快照的共享两层网络，为每种模态输出一个效用数值 $u_{m}(L)——$让它去预测你测得的信息增益 $g_{m}(L)$。与此同时加入一个对比项：用基于距离的相似度，即负平方距离 $- ||a- b||^{2}$（向量越近得分越高），把全模态快照$(phi_{full})$与每个置空某模态的快照$(\\mathit{phi\\_drop\\_m})$拉近，以此替代常用的点积。每一次这样的拉近都按「被置空模态在该基因上实际降低的平方预测误差」加权（先在零处截断，再在每个批次内重新缩放到 0 与 1 之间），并把同一批次中的其他基因当作对比用的负样本。默认让预测项与对比项等权平衡，仅当两者数量级偏离时才重新调节。让梯度回传进入各模态编码器，从而使「每种模态在此处有多大用处」成为一个显式可学的量；这种残差增益加权意味着只有真正编码了各模态效用的表示才能最小化损失。\n\n*属性定向预训练损失：效用头 $u_{m}$ 回归 $g_{m}(L)$，同时用按残差增益加权（权重 $w_{m}$）的跨视图拉近项替代内积相似度，使得只有编码了模态效用的表示才能令损失最小。*\n$$ \\mathcal{L}_B = \\sum_{m\\in\\mathcal{M}} \\Big[ \\big(u_m(L) - g_m(L)\\big)^2 + \\lambda\\, w_m(L)\\, \\big\\| \\phi_{\\mathrm{full}}(L) - \\phi_{\\mathrm{drop}_m}(L) \\big\\|^2 \\Big] \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这让「每种模态在此处有多大用处」成为一个显式可学的量，而这种特殊加权意味着只有真正编码了各模态效用的表示才能最小化损失。\n\n### 位点条件化分配\n*把高效用模态送入全宽融合、冗余模态送入低秩通道，并附带可恢复性误差界。*\n\n5. 冻结上一步得到的效用头。然后在每个基因处，查出每种模态的效用得分，把模态分成两组：得分超过阈值 tau 的进入全宽融合通道（保留其完整特征宽度，并用由效用得分经一个温度参数 beta 调控锐化或平滑后得到的软权重加以组合），其余效用较低的模态则被拼接在一起、通过一个共享的低秩 r 小容量投影压缩，产生一条紧凑的残差向量再加回去——这就是「压缩冗余信号」步骤。一个误差界（式 3）保证压缩所损失的精度至多与被压缩模态的总信息增益成正比，因此在某模态确有信息量的基因上不会受损。通过一个小规模网格搜索来选取阈值 tau、温度 beta 和残差秩 r，使验证集预测精度（R 方）最大。【作者需决定：共享的低秩残差投影是用一个全局矩阵还是每种细胞类型各用一个，以及保留的全宽模态是并排拼接还是相加融合，这些都是作者必须做出的设计选择——两者都保持误差保证，但会改变容量的花费方式；选择轴在于残差通道参数共享的范围。】\n\n*可恢复性界：分配后模型的表达 MSE 与全融合模型之差，至多为被路由出（低效用）模态的总信息增益乘以一个常数。*\n$$ \\big| \\mathrm{MSE}_{\\mathrm{alloc}}(L) - \\mathrm{MSE}_{\\mathrm{full}}(L) \\big| \\;\\leq\\; C \\sum_{m \\,:\\, u_m(L) \\leq \\tau} g_m(L) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 只在此基因上真正重要的信号上花满容量；误差界证明在某信号确实有信息量的基因上不会受损，这正是它区别于任意门控的地方。\n6. 保持效用头冻结，使逐基因的路由决策固定不变，然后在这些逐基因分配后的表示上微调表达预测器（以及那个共享的小压缩投影），用与第一步相同的高斯似然损失和训练计划，直到验证集似然不再改善为止。把容量从冗余信号上释放出来，使模型能更好地拟合那些此前被粗暴融合浪费掉力气的基因，让它们的预测向真实表达值靠拢，而某模态确有信息量的基因则保持不变。此处你可以保持主干编码器冻结，以便隔离分配本身的效果；若完整微调给出不同的验证精度，则两种结果都汇报。\n   - _为什么_: 把容量从冗余信号上释放出来，使模型能拟合那些此前被粗暴融合浪费掉力气的基因，让它们的预测向真实值靠拢。\n\n### 冗余分箱验证\n*检验增益集中于冗余模态箱、并在效用信号被破坏后消失。*\n\n7. 采用标准的 12 折整条染色体交叉验证：每折留出整条染色体，使得没有任何基因同时出现在训练和测试中。计算逐基因 R 方（预测表达与留出实测表达之间通常的决定系数），并按每个基因「最有信息量的单一模态」（即该基因跨模态的最大信息增益）把基因分成三等份（三分位），把最低的一组称为冗余模态箱。在每一组内，将 LoCMA 与均匀融合基线（同一主干、不做分配）对比。作为对照，在训练效用头之前，用一个固定的随机置换把逐基因增益向量在基因之间打乱（保持每个基因内部的模态顺序不变），重新训练，并检验冗余模态箱内的改善是否消失——其 R 方应回落到均匀融合基线。该主张是具体的：改善应出现在冗余模态箱内，并在逐基因效用信号被打乱破坏后消失。\n   - _为什么_: 该主张是具体的——改善应出现在冗余模态箱内，并在逐基因效用信号被打乱破坏后消失。\n\n"},{"id":"44","run_dir":"run_prompt44_phaseretr","index":44,"title":"Breaking the Spectral-Tail Rate: Per-Eigendirection Dynamics for Power-Law Phase Retrieval","title_zh":"突破谱尾速率：幂律相位恢复的逐特征方向动力学","method_name":"Spectrum-Preconditioned Phase-Retrieval Flow (SP-Flow)","hook":"The slow third phase of anisotropic phase-retrieval learning is widely read as an intrinsic cost of the power-law spectrum, but we show it is a cost of the single global rate: the spectrum-induced MSE tail exponent is a tight lower bound only for one-scalar-rate flow, and a spectrum-derived per-eigendirection rate provably beats it.","anchor_pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","anchor_pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","domain_category":"Learning Theory & Statistics","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf predicts how fast the small-eigenvalue (spectral-tail) directions in anisotropic phase retrieval CAN be recovered under any dynamics other than the one fixed-global-rate flow -- the slow third phase is characterized as an outcome of the spectrum but never as a quantity that a different per-direction driving could move, so the achievable tail-learning rate (and whether the MSE scaling exponent in a is improvable rather than fixed) is an open need.","pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by formalizing the single-global-rate gradient flow's spectral-tail MSE decay as a tight separation criterion -- a lower bound on the achievable tail exponent expressed in the spectral exponent a -- and then re-injecting the discarded per-eigendirection structure of the covariance spectrum into the flow's core update to construct an augmented (spectrum-preconditioned) dynamics proven to strictly exceed that exponent at bounded (linear-in-d) per-step cost.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions the silently shared assumption that the phase-retrieval learning dynamics must be driven by a SINGLE global rate that couples all eigen-directions: every frontier leaf (the power-law dynamics reduction, the general-covariance exact ODE, the Hessian-transition analysis) inherits a one-scalar-update formulation from the common gradient-flow / fixed-step-SGD ancestor and none tests whether that single-rate coupling, rather than the power-law spectrum itself, is what mak","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C29 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by auditing the convergence-target/measurement-criterion assumption baked into the phase-retrieval convergence guarantee -- that progress is measured against a single scalar rate coupling all eigen-directions -- and replacing it with a per-eigendirection progress decomposition, then re-deriving the tail-phase rate to prove a class separation: the single-rate dynamics provably cannot achieve the rate the per-direction dynamics achieves, isolating the single-rate coupling (not the spectrum) as the load-bearing cause of the slow phase.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"learning dynamics / high-dimensional optimization theory of nonconvex estimators (phase retrieval) under anisotropic power-law data","n_papers":39,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":26},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":20,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Hitting the High-dimensional notes: an ODE for SGD learning dynamics on GLMs and multi-index models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"The role of the time-dependent Hessian in high-dimensional optimization"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Robust Gradient Descent for Phase Retrieval"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Global convergence of gradient descent for phase retrieval"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Wirtinger gradient descent methods for low-dose Poisson phase retrieval"},{"source":"openalex","title":"A Comprehensive Review of Deep Learning: Architectures, Recent Advances, and Applications"}],"more":14},{"year":2025,"n":19,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Fast Escape, Slow Convergence: Learning Dynamics of Phase Retrieval under Power-Law Data"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Curl Descent: Non-Gradient Learning Dynamics with Sign-Diverse Plasticity"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Phase diagram and eigenvalue dynamics of stochastic gradient descent in multilayer neural networks"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Exact Dynamics of Multi-class Stochastic Gradient Descent"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Phase-Only Pattern Synthesis of Domino Tiling Irregular Arrays Based on Deep Reinforcement Learning and Gradient-Descent Optimization"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Arc Gradient Descent: A Mathematically Derived Reformulation of Gradient Descent with Phase-Aware, User-Controlled Step Dynamics"}],"more":13}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":10,"share":0.256},{"pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","count":10,"share":0.256},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":8,"share":0.205},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":4,"share":0.103},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":3,"share":0.077},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":3,"share":0.077},{"pattern_id":"algebraic_equivalence_unification","pattern_name":"Prove Equivalence to Unify","count":3,"share":0.077},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":2,"share":0.051}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"In the canonical anisotropic phase-retrieval model y=<x,w*>^2+noise with power-law input covariance lambda_i propto i^{-a} (a>1), the learning curve has been shown to split into three regimes -- fast escape from mediocrity, macroscopic convergence of summary statistics, and an arbitrarily slow spectral-tail phase in which directions tied to small eigenvalues are recovered (semanticscholar:6f85e6fa61dc49a62dad39926e800da03425179e). The structural failure is that a single scalar gradient-flow / SGD update couples all coordinates through one global rate, so the same dynamics that gives a healthy O(1) signal correlation in the top-eigenvalue block forces the tail-eigenvalue block to crawl: the per-coordinate driving term scales with lambda_i, so for the small-lambda_i tail the MSE-reducing flow is throttled by the spectrum itself and no amount of running the same update faster fixes it without blowing up the top block. This is precisely the regime where the recent exact-ODE machinery for high-dimensional SGD applies but stops at description: the deterministic-equivalent ODE systems for GLMs/multi-index models with general covariance (semanticscholar:e792aa4d8df0a07e27439cffc1a6802209037672) and the Hessian-spectral-transition analysis of phase-retrieval escape (semanticscholar:b7562fcf32632a7bdb3ec9a54cb96a0d0772e43c) characterize WHEN the slow phase happens but produce no quantity that an algorithm could read off to break the spectrum-throttled tail rate, leaving the duration of the slow phase as an apparently irreducible function of a alone.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:6f85e6fa61dc49a62dad39926e800da03425179e","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Reduces the infinite coupled-ODE hierarchy of phase retrieval under power-law covariance to a tractable three-phase trajectory (fast escape / macroscopic convergence / spectral-tail learning) via a Duhamel-formula representation plus phase-specific approximations, and reads off MSE scaling-law exponents in the spectral exponent a. Residue: the entire analysis is population gradient flow with label noise explicitly set to zero and a single global rate -- it diagnoses the slow third phase as an intrinsic spectrum-induced cost but never asks whether a per-direction / preconditioned dynamics could change that exponent, and it does not characterize how finite SGD step-size noise interacts with the tail-learning phase, so the residue is: no object in the theory predicts how fast the tail CAN be learned under any modified-rate dynamics, only how fast it IS under the one fixed-rate flow."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:e792aa4d8df0a07e27439cffc1a6802209037672","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Derives a deterministic-equivalent ODE system for streaming SGD on GLMs and multi-index models (logistic regression, phase retrieval) with GENERAL data covariance, valid w.h.p. in the proportional high-dimensional limit, tracking risk and other sub-optimality statistics. Residue: the general-covariance ODE is presented as a descriptive equivalence for a FIXED step-size SGD -- it provides the exact dynamical object but does not specialize it to the power-law-tail coupling structure nor use it to design a covariance-aware schedule, so the lever it implicitly exposes (a per-eigenmode rate) is never turned into a control variable."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:b7562fcf32632a7bdb3ec9a54cb96a0d0772e43c","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Tracks the time-dependent Hessian spectrum of gradient descent on phase retrieval and identifies a BBP-type spectral transition (an isolated eigenvalue detaching from the bulk) that gates escape from rough regions of the landscape. Residue: the spectral-transition diagnosis is carried out for isotropic / unstructured design and is used only to explain WHEN escape happens, not to predict how an anisotropic power-law spectrum shifts the transition time per eigen-direction or how that shift could be exploited to accelerate the tail phase."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"learning dynamics / high-dimensional optimization theory of nonconvex estimators (phase retrieval) under anisotropic power-law data","venue":"ICLR 2026 (theory / learning-dynamics track)","time":"2026","data":["synthetic anisotropic Gaussian inputs x ~ N(0, Q) with power-law covariance spectrum lambda_i propto i^{-a}, a>1","phase-retrieval targets y = <x,w*>^2 + noise","optionally real heavy-tailed-spectrum feature covariances (image/text embedding Gram matrices) for spectrum validation"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"high-dimensional probability, statistical-mechanics of learning, SGD/gradient-flow dynamics","preference":"both","baseline":"single-pass SGD / gradient flow on the population phase-retrieval loss with a fixed (untuned) global step size, as analyzed in Fast Escape Slow Convergence (semanticscholar:6f85e6fa61dc49a62dad39926e800da03425179e)","limitation":"existing power-law phase-retrieval dynamics theory predicts the three-phase MSE trajectory but treats the slow spectral-tail phase as an inherent, un-accelerable cost and gives no per-direction control of the learning rate","contribution_type":"theory","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type","data"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object both legs read from and write to is the per-eigendirection coordinate dynamics of the phase-retrieval gradient flow under diagonal power-law covariance Q = diag(lambda_1,...,lambda_d) with lambda_i = i^{-a}/sum_j j^{-a}, a>1 (the anchor's own normalization, semanticscholar:6f85e6fa61dc49a62dad39926e800da03425179e). Working in the eigenbasis of Q, write the weight as w(t) with per-coordinate components w_i(t) and define the per-direction residual r_i(t) = w_i(t) - w*_i; the population loss L(w) = E_x[((x^T w)^2 - (x^T w*)^2)^2] has gradient whose i-th coordinate driving term scales as lambda_i times a fourth-moment alignment factor, so the standard single-rate flow dot{w} = -eta * grad L drives r_i down at a rate throttled by lambda_i -- this is the exact quantity the anchor's three-phase reduction tracks and whose tail i (small lambda_i) crawls. LEG 1 (C10, characterize-then-surpass): we formalize the discarded structural object as the per-eigendirection rate, prove that ANY single global scalar rate eta induces a tail-MSE decay whose exponent in a is bounded below by a fixed value gamma_single(a) (the separation criterion: a tight lower bound the single-rate class provably cannot beat, derived by showing the top block caps eta via a stability ceiling eta <= eta_max(lambda_1) while the tail block needs eta >> 1/lambda_i), then re-inject the per-direction structure by constructing the augmented flow dot{w}_i = -D_ii(Q) * (grad L)_i with a diagonal spectrum-derived preconditioner D_ii(Q) = lambda_i^{-beta} (beta in [0,1] a single named hyperparameter, the preconditioning strength; beta=0 recovers the single-rate flow, beta=1 is full whitening), and prove the augmented flow achieves tail exponent gamma_precond(a,beta) > gamma_single(a) strictly, with per-step cost O(d) since D is diagonal and read directly off the known spectrum. LEG 2 (C29, audit-and-pivot) shares this exact object: it audits the convergence guarantee's tacit assumption that progress is measured by one scalar rate coupling all coordinates, replaces that primitive with the per-direction progress decomposition sum_i lambda_i * r_i(t)^2 split into a universally-bounded top-block part and an assumption-sensitive tail part, and re-derives the rate to prove a class separation -- the single-rate class is confined to gamma_single(a) precisely because its one ceiling-limited eta cannot simultaneously serve top and tail, establishing that the single-rate coupling, not the power-law spectrum, is the load-bearing cause; the audit's deliverable is this necessity/identifiability theorem, which is exactly what licenses Leg 1's surpassing operator. The two legs are one paper because they manipulate the same per-eigendirection residual object: Leg 2 proves the single-rate coupling is the obstacle, Leg 1 removes it and certifies the new rate. The load-bearing free quantities are: the preconditioner exponent beta (named hyperparameter), the stability ceiling eta_max(lambda_1) (computed from the top eigenvalue and the loss curvature), and the per-direction residual r_i(t) (computed in the eigenbasis); D_ii is read directly from the spectrum, not learned, so there is no estimator to mis-specify.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery because both are statements ABOUT the same per-eigendirection residual r_i(t): the additive anchor gap asks 'can the tail exponent move?' and the subtractive sibling gap asks 'is the single-rate coupling the cause?' -- the same lower-bound/separation argument answers both (the bound proves it's the cause AND that removing it surpasses), so forcing two separate modules would duplicate the same algebra; the evidence is that Leg 2's separation theorem IS the lower-bound half of Leg 1's surpass proof. (b) Considered designs rejected: (i) a learned per-coordinate adaptive rate (Adam/RMSProp-style) -- rejected because it lands on the fixed-step-SGD adaptive-method ancestor node and the spectrum is KNOWN so learning the rate is a regression to an occupied node; (ii) a global running-average / momentum baseline -- rejected as a >16y ancestral regression (method_lineage REGRESSION FLAG: a global running-average reduces to the gradient-flow ancestor n0/n1). The avoided node is exactly the global-scalar-rate gradient-flow ancestor; novelty is secured by making D_ii a deterministic functional of the covariance spectrum (a source the lineage tree does not occupy) rather than a learned or running statistic.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: numerically integrate the population gradient-flow ODE for anisotropic phase retrieval (target y=<x,w*>^2, x~N(0,Q), power-law lambda_i=i^{-a}) at d=10^4 for a in {1.2,1.5,2.0}, comparing the single-global-rate flow against the spectrum-preconditioned flow dot{w}_i=-lambda_i^{-beta}(grad L)_i for beta in {0.25,0.5,0.75,1.0}, and measure the late-time MSE decay exponent (the log-log slope of MSE(t) in the spectral-tail phase). If the candidate is correct, the measured tail exponent improves (MSE decays strictly faster, larger-magnitude slope) as beta increases from 0, and the measured gamma_precond(a,beta) matches the derived surpass formula while staying strictly above the single-rate floor gamma_single(a). The named load-bearing variable is the diagonal spectrum-derived preconditioner D_ii=lambda_i^{-beta} (the per-eigendirection rate); the negative-control intervention SHUFFLES D's entries across coordinates so each coordinate receives a preconditioning value decoupled from its own eigenvalue (same value-multiset, permuted), and the prediction is that under the shuffled control the downstream MSE tail exponent collapses back to the single-rate floor gamma_single(a) -- the task-outcome metric (MSE decay rate) returns to baseline -- whereas an alternative explanation (that any per-coordinate rescaling, regardless of spectral alignment, speeds the tail) would predict the shuffled control retains the speed-up. A positive control using ONLY the spectrum-aligned preconditioner with the gradient direction frozen to its sign should recover most of the tail-exponent gain, identifying the per-eigendirection rate as the mechanism.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:6f85e6fa61dc49a62dad39926e800da03425179e","delta":"They derive the three-phase MSE trajectory and tail scaling exponent for the SINGLE global-rate population flow and present the slow tail as intrinsic to the spectrum; we prove that tail exponent is a tight lower bound ONLY for the single-rate class and construct a spectrum-derived per-eigendirection preconditioner that provably exceeds it, turning a fixed exponent into a movable one."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:e792aa4d8df0a07e27439cffc1a6802209037672","delta":"They give the exact deterministic-equivalent ODE for fixed-step SGD on GLMs with general covariance as a descriptive equivalence; we specialize the per-eigenmode structure that ODE exposes into a CONTROL variable (a diagonal preconditioner read off the spectrum) and prove a class separation in the achievable tail rate that their fixed-step formulation cannot express."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:b7562fcf32632a7bdb3ec9a54cb96a0d0772e43c","delta":"They tie escape from rough regions to a BBP Hessian-spectral transition under isotropic design; we work in the anisotropic eigenbasis and show the binding constraint on the tail phase is the single-rate stability ceiling eta_max(lambda_1), a per-direction quantity their isotropic transition analysis does not isolate."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416374356","delta":"They derive convex KRR excess-risk exponents from the covariance spectral tail via effective dimension; we transport an effective-dimension-style argument into the NONCONVEX phase-retrieval optimization trajectory to lower-bound the single-rate tail exponent, a setting their convex analysis does not cover."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:6f85e6fa61dc49a62dad39926e800da03425179e","what_step_was_missed":"They reduced the infinite coupled-ODE hierarchy to the three-phase trajectory and read off the tail exponent for the fixed single-rate flow, but they never derived the stability-ceiling lower bound certifying that exponent as a CLASS limit (the gamma_single(a) bound binding every single-scalar-rate dynamics), and so never constructed the spectrum-derived per-eigendirection preconditioner and the matching surpass theorem gamma_precond(a,beta) > gamma_single(a) that the lower bound licenses -- the missing step is the lower-bound-plus-surpassing-operator pair, not a different solver."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":290,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"No hard floor fires: gap_closure_reject_check is borderline (not triggered), recipe_application_check.verdict=applied on both legs, anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id=null, and paper_pointed_threat is not exact-mechanism overlap. The two borderlines (C10 'recently-subsumed' vs Spectra, and C29 'hidden constants' in the a->1+ limit) are proof-discipline / frontier-positioning concerns in fields that Phase 4 can fold into reviewer_concerns_and_responses rather than load-bearing defects requiring a rewrite, and the addressable Spectra threat is a differentiation-statement add, so advance with both concerns surfaced is the correct call over revise.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf predicts how fast the small-eigenvalue (spectral-tail) directions in anisotropic phase retrieval CAN be recovered under any dynamics other than the one fixed-global-rate flow -- the slow third phase is characterized as an outcome of the spectrum but never as a quantity that a different per-direction driving could move, so the achievable tail-learning rate (and whether the MSE scaling exponent in a is improvable rather than fixed) is an open need.","main_pattern":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail when the 'limit' they characterize is not a genuine structural blindspot -- trivially implied by the model's own assumptions, already surpassed by a published method, or never formalized beyond an informal analogy; a recurring shape substitutes a hand-wavy mechanism for a separation proof.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Resting the central claim on an informal analogy (two operators 'both smooth high frequencies') instead of a separation proof leaves the mechanism underspecified and the empirical gain unconvincing.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism builds an explicit separation criterion -- a lower bound gamma_single(a) derived from the single-rate stability ceiling eta<=eta_max(lambda_1) -- not an analogy."},{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a 'maximally expressive' construction that a recently published method already strictly subsumes turns the surpass-the-limit claim into redundant work.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"the collision hit 'Spectra: Rethinking Optimizers for LLMs Under Spectral Anisotropy' identifies the same spike-tail / global-stable-rate suppression mechanism, so the frontier must be surveyed; but Spectra is an empirical LLM optimizer that suppresses the spike subspace and proves no tail-exponent surpass theorem in the spectral exponent a for nonconvex phase retrieval, so it does not subsume the candidate's theoretical claim."},{"lesson_quoted":"Deriving a 'limitation' that is trivially implied by the model's own linearity assumption produces a limit too weak to count as a real blindspot, and the proposed surpass step stays under-validated.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the limit (single global rate cannot serve top and tail simultaneously) is a non-trivial consequence of the coupled stability ceiling, not an artifact of a simplifying assumption -- it is surpassed by an explicitly constructed diagonal preconditioner."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions the silently shared assumption that the phase-retrieval learning dynamics must be driven by a SINGLE global rate that couples all eigen-directions: every frontier leaf (the power-law dynamics reduction, the general-covariance exact ODE, the Hessian-transition analysis) inherits a one-scalar-update formulation from the common gradient-flow / fixed-step-SGD ancestor and none tests whether that single-rate coupling, rather than the power-law spectrum itself, is what makes the tail phase slow.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C29 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"This cluster fails when the weakened assumption is engineered to close the proof rather than genuine, when a relaxed condition is borrowed without showing what it buys, or when the re-derived rate merely matches the baseline with cosmetic algorithmic changes.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A weakened assumption that no known function class is shown to satisfy reads as engineered to close the proof, not as a genuine generalization -- characterize when it holds or it sinks the paper.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the pivoted condition (a per-eigendirection rate read off the known power-law spectrum) demonstrably holds for the canonical power-law covariance model the anchor itself uses -- it is exhibited on a concrete, checkable function class."},{"lesson_quoted":"Re-deriving a rate that merely matches the baseline with near-identical algorithmic changes is read as an incremental extension, however clean the analysis.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the re-derived rate is a STRICT separation gamma_precond(a,beta) > gamma_single(a), not a baseline match; the algorithmic change (diagonal spectrum preconditioner) provably changes the exponent rather than constants."},{"lesson_quoted":"Hidden constants that explode at the precise parameter limit where the result is advertised as strongest silently invalidate the headline guarantee, and reviewers find them in the proof.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"the surpass claim must verify that the preconditioned stability ceiling stays uniform across i and that no hidden d-dependent constant blows up as a->1+ (the heaviest-tail limit); core_mechanism step 4 asserts uniform curvature but the explicit constant-tracking is left to the derivation -- a load-bearing but addressable proof obligation, not a present defect."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No entry is triggered. The anchor C10 entry is borderline on the 'recently-subsumed' lesson because of the Spectra collision hit, and the C29 entry is borderline on the 'hidden constants' lesson because the uniform-ceiling claim carries an unproven constant-tracking obligation in the a->1+ limit; both are addressable proof-discipline concerns surfaced for Phase 4, not Reject matches."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf predicts how fast the small-eigenvalue (spectral-tail) directions in anisotropic phase retrieval CAN be recovered under any dynamics other than the one fixed-global-rate flow -- the slow third phase is characterized as an outcome of the spectrum but never as a quantity that a different per-direction driving could move, so the achievable tail-learning rate (and whether the MSE scaling exponent in a is improvable rather than fixed) is an open need.","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Pinpoint the one structural object an iterative/local procedure discards for tractability, formalize the equivalence class that discarding induces as a separation criterion on the procedure's native objects, then re-inject that exact object into the procedure's core step and prove the augmented operator strictly exceeds the criterion at bounded (linear/quadratic) cost.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism LEG 1 names the discarded structural object (the per-eigendirection rate that the single-scalar-rate flow throws away), formalizes the separation criterion (the lower bound gamma_single(a) the single-rate class cannot beat, via the stability ceiling eta<=eta_max(lambda_1)), and re-injects it into the flow's core update as the diagonal preconditioner D_ii=lambda_i^{-beta}, proving gamma_precond(a,beta) > gamma_single(a) at O(d) per-step cost -- the discard / criterion / re-inject / bounded-cost signature is present in full.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions the silently shared assumption that the phase-retrieval learning dynamics must be driven by a SINGLE global rate that couples all eigen-directions: every frontier leaf (the power-law dynamics reduction, the general-covariance exact ODE, the Hessian-transition analysis) inherits a one-scalar-update formulation from the common gradient-flow / fixed-step-SGD ancestor and none tests whether that single-rate coupling, rather than the power-law spectrum itself, is what makes the tail phase slow.","sub_pattern":"C29 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Take an existing convergence/regret guarantee for an iterative first-order update and pivot the single regularity-or-target assumption the proof rests on -- e.g. replace the convergence primitive (exact-optimum target, squared-distance measure) with a different one -- then re-prove the rate by isolating one load-bearing object (a per-iteration progress bound or cumulative-deficit decomposition); payoff is a sharper rate or provable class separation.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism LEG 2 audits the convergence guarantee's tacit measurement primitive (progress against one scalar rate coupling all coordinates), replaces it with the per-direction progress decomposition V(t)=sum_i lambda_i r_i(t)^2 split into a universally-bounded top part and an assumption-sensitive tail part (the isolated load-bearing decomposition), and re-derives the rate to prove the single-rate class separation -- the pivot-the-target-primitive + isolate-one-decomposition + prove-separation signature is present.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both legs perform their cited cluster's distinctive move: C10's discard-formalize-reinject-bound-cost surpass on the anchor leg, and C29's pivot-the-convergence-primitive-and-re-derive-a-separation on the sibling leg; neither reduces to the parent's generic gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["characterize_limit_then_surpass","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; the candidate's composition set contains neither heterogeneous_decomposition nor any flagged pairing, so no anti-pattern matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"Spectra: Rethinking Optimizers for LLMs Under Spectral Anisotropy","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"Spectra (2026-01, collision_hits) makes the most adjacent claim: it shows gradient signals are spike-tail anisotropic, that a dominant low-rank spike both tightens the globally stable learning-rate bound and suppresses tail learning via second-moment normalization, and it proposes a spike-aware optimizer. This is the same qualitative mechanism the candidate's lower bound formalizes (one global stable rate cannot serve both spike and tail). The candidate's claim stands because Spectra is an empirical LLM-optimizer contribution that suppresses the spike SUBSPACE to free the global rate, whereas the candidate (a) works in the canonical nonconvex phase-retrieval learning-dynamics model with known power-law covariance, (b) proves a tight tail-exponent lower bound gamma_single(a) certifying the single-rate class limit in the spectral exponent a, and (c) constructs a spectrum-derived per-eigendirection preconditioner with a matching surpass theorem gamma_precond(a,beta) > gamma_single(a) -- none of which Spectra derives. The candidate would only fall if Spectra (or a follow-up) proved the same nonconvex tail-exponent separation, which it does not.","addressable_via":"differentiation_from_lit -- add an explicit entry distinguishing the candidate's nonconvex phase-retrieval tail-exponent surpass theorem from Spectra's empirical spike-suppression optimizer, so the novelty boundary is stated against the nearest competitor (surfaced into Phase 4 reviewer_concerns_and_responses)."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Breaking the Spectral-Tail Rate: Per-Eigendirection Dynamics for Power-Law Phase Retrieval\n\n**Method.** Spectrum-Preconditioned Phase-Retrieval Flow (SP-Flow)\n\n## Motivation\nPhase retrieval is the problem of recovering an unknown signal w* from squared, sign-less measurements y = <x, $w*>^{2},$ and a popular way to study how a learning algorithm solves it is to watch gradient flow (the continuous-time limit of gradient descent) under inputs x whose covariance has a power-law spectrum -- the i-th eigenvalue $lambda_{i}$ shrinks roughly like $i^{-a}. A$ recent result (semanticscholar:6f85e6fa61dc49a62dad39926e800da03425179e) showed the learning curve has three stages, ending in a very slow third stage where the directions tied to the smallest eigenvalues are recovered, and read this slow stage off as an unavoidable cost of the power-law spectrum.\n\nThe reason it is slow is structural. The usual update uses ONE global step size (learning rate) shared by every direction. The big-eigenvalue directions force that step size to stay small (otherwise they blow up), but the small-eigenvalue tail needs a much larger effective push to move at all -- so the single shared rate that keeps the top stable starves the tail. Earlier theory work either gave the exact dynamics only for a single fixed step size (semanticscholar:e792aa4d8df0a07e27439cffc1a6802209037672) or explained WHEN escape happens but only for the simpler isotropic case (semanticscholar:b7562fcf32632a7bdb3ec9a54cb96a0d0772e43c), and none of them produced a quantity an algorithm could use to speed the tail up.\n\nOur claim is that the slow tail is a cost of the single shared rate, NOT of the spectrum. We prove two things together. First, any dynamics that uses one global rate is stuck at or below a fixed tail-speed (a tight lower bound $gamma_{single}(a)) --$ this is a genuine limit, not an artifact. Second, if you give each direction its own rate by scaling its update by $lambda_{i}^{-beta}$ (a single knob beta, read straight off the known spectrum at cheap O(d) cost), the tail provably speeds up past that limit. A companion argument shows that holding the single-rate coupling fixed is exactly what causes the slow tail, so removing it is what licenses the speed-up.\n\nWhat changes when this gap closes: the tail exponent stops being a fixed function of a and becomes a quantity you can move with the knob beta, turning the anchor's descriptive three-stage picture into a controllable one and turning the general-covariance dynamics into a design surface rather than a description.\n\n## Method\n### Single-rate limit (lower bound)\n*Prove every single-global-rate dynamics is stuck at or below a fixed tail speed $gamma_{single}(a).$*\n\n1. Set up the exact problem and rotate into the coordinate system where the input covariance is diagonal (its eigenbasis). Inputs are Gaussian x ~ N(0,Q) whose eigenvalues follow the power law $lambda_{i} = i^{-a}/sum_{j} j^{-a}$ with a>1; the hidden target w* is fixed and normalized so that $||Q^{1/2}$ w*||=1; the loss is the population (infinite-data) mean-squared error between the squared measurement $(x^{T} w)^{2}$ and the true squared measurement $(x^{T} w*)^{2},$ with no label noise. In this rotated frame track, for each coordinate i, the residual $r_{i} = w_{i} -$ w*_i. The result is one separate evolution equation per coordinate, and the small-eigenvalue tail of that set of equations is what every later step studies.\n   - _Why_: In the eigenbasis the dynamics splits coordinate-by-coordinate, which is the only frame where the per-direction behavior of the tail can be isolated.\n2. Write down, in closed form, the exact force that pushes each coordinate under the ordinary single-rate flow. Using the Gaussian moment identities (Isserlis / Wick), the push on coordinate i works out to four times its eigenvalue $lambda_{i},$ multiplied by an alignment term (the second moment $m_{2} = sum_{j} lambda_{j} w_{j}^{2}$ times $w_{i},$ minus the covariance-weighted overlap with the target times w*_i), plus higher fourth-moment corrections. The ordinary flow then moves each coordinate as minus the step size eta times this force. The crucial fact is that the eigenvalue $lambda_{i}$ appears as a multiplier on coordinate i's push, so the small-eigenvalue tail directions get pushed only very weakly.\n\n*Per-coordinate population gradient in the eigenbasis: the i-th driving term is scaled by $lambda_{i},$ so the single-rate flow drives the residual $r_{i}$ down at a rate throttled by the eigenvalue $lambda_{i}.$*\n$$ (\\nabla L)_i \\;=\\; 4\\,\\lambda_i\\big(m_2\\, w_i - \\langle w, w^* \\rangle_Q\\, w^*_i\\big) + \\text{(higher 4th-moment terms)}, \\qquad m_2 = \\sum_j \\lambda_j w_j^2 \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Seeing the eigenvalue appear as a multiplier on each direction's push is what explains, mechanically, why the tail crawls.\n3. Prove that one shared step size cannot serve the top and the tail at once, and turn that into a hard speed limit. The big-eigenvalue (top) directions blow up unless the shared step size stays below a ceiling set by the largest eigenvalue $lambda_{1}$ and the loss curvature $\\kappa $ (here $\\kappa $ is the largest curvature of the loss surface in the top block, and the ceiling also carries a fixed order-one safety constant from the standard stability condition that the step times the curvature must stay below about 2). Because the push on tail direction i is its eigenvalue times the step size, this ceiling forces the tail push to shrink toward zero as i grows. Integrating the resulting crawling tail dynamics gives a tight lower bound, written $gamma_{single}(a),$ on how fast ANY single-shared-rate flow can ever clear the tail. The curvature and the safety constant are both computed directly from the largest eigenvalue and the model's second moment, not tuned by hand.\n\n*Single-rate stability ceiling: the top block forces eta below a bound set by the largest eigenvalue $lambda_{1}$ and the loss curvature $\\kappa ,$ so the tail driving $lambda_{i}\\cdot \\eta $ decays as i grows; this yields the lower bound $gamma_{single}(a).$*\n$$ \\eta \\;\\leq\\; \\eta_{\\max}(\\lambda_1) \\;=\\; \\frac{c}{\\lambda_1\\,\\kappa}, \\qquad \\lambda_i\\,\\eta \\;\\leq\\; \\frac{\\lambda_i}{\\lambda_1}\\,c \\;\\to\\; 0 \\;\\;(i\\to\\infty) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The top and the tail want opposite things from one shared number, so a single rate provably cannot serve both -- that tension is the limit.\n\n### Per-direction surpass operator\n*Build the spectrum-derived per-direction preconditioner $D_{ii}=lambda_{i}^{-beta}$ and prove it beats the limit.*\n\n4. Give each direction its own rate instead of one shared step. Multiply coordinate i's update by $lambda_{i}^{-beta}$ (the inverse eigenvalue raised to a power beta), where beta is a single tuning knob between 0 and 1 that sets the preconditioning strength: beta=0 is exactly the old single-rate flow, and beta=1 fully whitens (equalizes) all directions. After this rescaling, the effective push on direction i becomes $lambda_{i}^{1-beta},$ which dies off much more slowly across the tail, and the stability ceiling becomes the same for every direction instead of being dictated by the largest eigenvalue alone. This costs only on the order of d operations per step because the rescaling is diagonal (one number per coordinate) and each number is read straight off the already-known eigenvalue spectrum, so there is nothing to estimate.\n\n*Spectrum-preconditioned flow: the diagonal preconditioner $D_{ii}=lambda_{i}^{-\\beta }$ rescales each coordinate's driving to $lambda_{i}^{1-\\beta },$ which decays slower in i; $\\beta =0$ recovers the single-rate flow and $\\beta =1$ is full whitening, and D is read off the known spectrum at O(d) cost.*\n$$ \\dot{w}_i \\;=\\; -\\,D_{ii}(Q)\\,(\\nabla L)_i, \\qquad D_{ii}(Q) = \\lambda_i^{-\\beta}, \\;\\; \\beta \\in [0,1] \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Rescaling by the inverse eigenvalue exactly counteracts the eigenvalue throttling the tail, and since the spectrum is already known there is nothing to estimate.\n5. Redo the same phase-by-phase rate analysis, now with the rescaled push, to get the new tail speed (call it $gamma_{precond},$ which depends on a and on the knob beta), and prove it strictly beats the single-rate limit for every beta>0. Also find the best knob setting beta* that clears the tail fastest while keeping the top stable 【author decision: whether to set beta* to optimize the hardest, heaviest-tail case (a just above 1) or a typical mid-range a is a design choice the authors must make, because those two goals can pick different beta*】. Throughout, keep careful track of the hidden constants in the bounds so that nothing blows up in the heaviest-tail limit where a approaches 1 from above.\n\n*Surpass theorem: the preconditioned tail exponent strictly exceeds the single-rate lower bound for every positive $\\beta ,$ turning a fixed exponent in a into a movable one controlled by $\\beta .$*\n$$ \\gamma_{\\mathrm{precond}}(a,\\beta) \\;>\\; \\gamma_{\\mathrm{single}}(a) \\quad \\text{for all } \\beta > 0 \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This is the payoff: the same analysis that bounded the old flow now shows the new flow provably escapes that bound.\n\n### Single-rate-is-the-cause separation\n*Prove via a Lyapunov decomposition that the single shared rate, not the spectrum, causes the slow tail.*\n\n6. Prove that the single shared rate, not the spectrum, is what makes the tail slow. Build a weighted error-energy quantity V(t) = sum over i of $lambda_{i}$ times $r_{i}$ squared, and split it into a top part (the big-eigenvalue block, which is always well-behaved) and a tail part (the small-eigenvalue block, which is sensitive to the rate choice). Show that no single shared step size can make both the top part and the tail part shrink at the fast per-direction speed at the same time. This proves the single-rate flow lives in a strictly slower class than the per-direction flow, which is exactly the justification for removing the single shared rate in the construction step.\n\n*Lyapunov decomposition: the weighted residual energy splits into a universally-bounded top part and an assumption-sensitive tail part, and no single $\\eta $ makes both decay at the preconditioned rate -- proving the single-rate class is strictly separated from the preconditioned class.*\n$$ V(t) \\;=\\; \\sum_i \\lambda_i\\, r_i(t)^2 \\;=\\; V_{\\mathrm{top}}(t) + V_{\\mathrm{tail}}(t) \\tag{5} $$\n\n   - _Why_: It is the necessity half of the story: it shows the bottleneck really is the shared rate, which is exactly what justifies removing it in the previous step.\n\n### Numerical verification and mechanism control\n*Integrate both flows, sanity-check finite SGD, and shuffle the preconditioner to isolate spectral alignment.*\n\n7. Numerically solve both flows and read off the tail speed. Integrate the single-rate flow and the per-direction flow (for beta in {0.25,0.5,0.75,1}) at sizes d in ${1000,10000}$ and tail exponents a in {1.2,1.5,2.0}, using a standard adaptive Runge-Kutta solver (Dormand-Prince RK45 with tight tolerances) starting from a fixed spectral-initialization point and running long enough for the error to settle into a clean straight line on a log-log plot (detected when the local slope stops changing by more than about 1% over a factor-of-ten stretch of time). Measure the tail speed as the slope of log error versus log time, fitted by least squares over the final factor-of-ten of the run after dropping the early fast-escape and middle convergence transients, then compare those measured slopes to the predicted per-direction speed and to the single-rate floor.\n   - _Why_: Directly measuring the slope checks whether the predicted speed-up actually shows up as beta increases.\n8. As a sanity check (not the headline result), confirm the idealized smooth-flow result survives real sampling noise. Run a single pass of stochastic gradient descent (SGD) on fresh random samples, using the same per-direction step (eigenvalue to the power minus beta, times the base step size eta) and the same eta as the smooth flow, in the regime where the number of samples n grows in proportion to the dimension d (try n = 2d, 5d, 10d at d = 1000 and 10000). Average the error curve over 20 independent random seeds, measure its tail slope the same way as before, and check it matches the smooth-flow prediction; report the spread across seeds as the high-probability band.\n   - _Why_: It confirms the idealized noiseless-flow result still holds once real sampling noise is put back in.\n9. Run the negative control that isolates spectral alignment as the mechanism. Keep the exact same set of preconditioning values but SHUFFLE which coordinate gets which value (apply a random permutation), so each direction's rate is no longer matched to its own eigenvalue. Re-solve the flow with this shuffled rescaling under the same settings as the main integration, average the measured tail slope over 20 independent random shuffles, and report the mean and spread. The prediction is that the tail speed falls back to the single-rate floor, because only the spectrum-MATCHED rescaling should help.\n   - _Why_: If only the spectrum-MATCHED rescaling helps, shuffling it away should kill the speed-up -- proving the alignment is the mechanism, not generic rescaling.\n10. Report the size of the certified speed-up. Across every combination of tail exponent a and knob beta, report the gap between the per-direction tail speed and the single-rate floor (the difference $gamma_{precond}$ minus $gamma_{single}),$ measured against both the single-rate baseline and the shuffled control from the previous step. Let the experiment reveal how big this gap is rather than committing to a target number ahead of time; the size of the gap across settings is the headline that separates this result from the prior reading of the slow tail as an unavoidable cost.\n   - _Why_: The size of the certified speed-up across settings is the headline that distinguishes this from the anchor's intrinsic-cost reading.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 突破谱尾速率：幂律相位恢复的逐特征方向动力学\n\n**方法名称.** Spectrum-Preconditioned Phase-Retrieval Flow (SP-Flow)\n\n## 研究动机\n相位恢复（phase retrieval）是从平方、丢失符号的测量 y = <x, $w*>^{2}$ 中恢复未知信号 w* 的问题。研究学习算法如何解它的一种常用方式，是在输入 x 的协方差谱呈幂律（第 i 个特征值 $lambda_{i}$ 大约按 $i^{-a}$ 衰减）时，观察 gradient flow（梯度下降的连续时间极限）。最近一项结果（semanticscholar:6f85e6fa61dc49a62dad39926e800da03425179e）表明学习曲线分为三个阶段，最后一个阶段非常慢——此时与最小特征值绑定的方向才被恢复——并把这个慢阶段解读为幂律谱不可避免的代价。\n\n它之所以慢，原因是结构性的。常规更新对所有方向使用同一个全局步长（学习率）。大特征值方向迫使这个步长必须很小（否则它们会发散），而小特征值的尾部却需要大得多的有效推力才能挪动——于是为保持顶部稳定而设的单一共享速率把尾部饿死了。早先的理论工作要么只给出单一固定步长下的精确动力学（semanticscholar:e792aa4d8df0a07e27439cffc1a6802209037672），要么解释了逃逸何时发生但只针对较简单的各向同性情形（semanticscholar:b7562fcf32632a7bdb3ec9a54cb96a0d0772e43c），都没有给出一个算法可以用来加速尾部的量。\n\n我们的主张是：慢尾部是单一共享速率的代价，而不是谱的代价。我们同时证明两件事。第一，任何使用单一全局速率的动力学都被卡在一个固定的尾部速度之上无法突破（一个紧的下界 $gamma_{single}(a)$）——这是真正的极限，而非假象。第二，如果给每个方向各自的速率，把它的更新按 $lambda_{i}^{-beta}$ 缩放（一个旋钮 beta，直接从已知谱读出，代价低至 O(d)），尾部就可证明地越过这个极限加速。一个配套论证表明，正是把单一速率耦合固定住才导致了慢尾部，所以移除它正是加速的依据。\n\n这个缺口被补上后会发生的改变是：尾部指数不再是 a 的固定函数，而成为一个可以用旋钮 beta 移动的量，把锚点工作描述性的三阶段图景变成可控的，并把一般协方差动力学从一个描述变成一个可设计的对象。\n\n## 方法\n### 单速率极限（下界）\n*证明每一种单一全局速率的动力学都被卡在固定尾部速度 $gamma_{single}(a)$ 之上无法突破。*\n\n1. 把问题精确设定好，并旋转到输入协方差为对角的坐标系（它的特征基）。输入是高斯的 x ~ N(0,Q)，其特征值遵循幂律 $lambda_{i} = i^{-a}/sum_{j} j^{-a}$，a>1；隐藏目标 w* 固定且归一化为 $||Q^{1/2}$ w*||=1；损失是平方测量 $(x^{T} w)^{2}$ 与真实平方测量 $(x^{T} w*)^{2}$ 之间的总体（无穷数据）均方误差(Mean Squared Error, MSE)，且无标签噪声。在这个旋转后的坐标系里，对每个坐标 i 追踪残差 $r_{i} = w_{i} -$ w*_i。结果是每个坐标一条独立的演化方程，而这组方程的小特征值尾部正是后续每一步研究的对象。\n   - _为什么_: 在特征基下动力学按坐标逐一分解，这是唯一能把尾部的逐方向行为分离出来的视角。\n2. 以闭式写出普通单速率流下推动每个坐标的精确力。利用高斯矩恒等式（Isserlis / Wick），坐标 i 上的推动等于它的特征值 $lambda_{i}$ 的四倍，乘以一个对齐项（二阶矩 $m_{2} = sum_{j} lambda_{j} w_{j}^{2}$ 乘以 $w_{i}$，再减去与目标的协方差加权重叠乘以 w*_i），外加更高阶的四阶矩修正。普通流随后把每个坐标按负的步长 eta 乘以这个力来移动。关键事实是特征值 $lambda_{i}$ 作为乘子出现在坐标 i 的推动上，所以小特征值的尾部方向受到的推动非常微弱。\n\n*特征基下的逐坐标总体梯度：第 i 个驱动项被 $lambda_{i}$ 缩放，因此单速率流把残差 $r_{i}$ 压下去的速度受特征值 $lambda_{i}$ 的节制。*\n$$ (\\nabla L)_i \\;=\\; 4\\,\\lambda_i\\big(m_2\\, w_i - \\langle w, w^* \\rangle_Q\\, w^*_i\\big) + \\text{(higher 4th-moment terms)}, \\qquad m_2 = \\sum_j \\lambda_j w_j^2 \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 看到特征值作为乘子出现在每个方向的推动上，从机理上解释了尾部为何爬行。\n3. 证明单一共享步长无法同时服务顶部与尾部，并把这一点转化为一个硬性速度极限。大特征值（顶部）方向会发散，除非共享步长低于一个由最大特征值 $lambda_{1}$ 与损失曲率 $\\kappa $ 决定的上限（这里 $\\kappa $ 是顶部块中损失曲面的最大曲率，上限还带有一个来自标准稳定性条件——步长乘曲率须保持在约 2 以下——的固定 order-one 安全常数）。由于尾部方向 i 上的推动是它的特征值乘以步长，这个上限迫使尾部推动随 i 增大趋于零。对由此得到的爬行尾部动力学积分，给出任何单一共享速率流清理尾部速度的一个紧下界，记为 $gamma_{single}(a)$。曲率与安全常数都直接由最大特征值与模型的二阶矩计算得到，而非手工调参。\n\n*单速率稳定性上限：顶部块迫使 eta 低于由最大特征值 $lambda_{1}$ 与损失曲率 $\\kappa $ 决定的界，于是尾部驱动 $lambda_{i}\\cdot \\eta $ 随 i 增大而衰减；由此给出下界 $gamma_{single}(a)$。*\n$$ \\eta \\;\\leq\\; \\eta_{\\max}(\\lambda_1) \\;=\\; \\frac{c}{\\lambda_1\\,\\kappa}, \\qquad \\lambda_i\\,\\eta \\;\\leq\\; \\frac{\\lambda_i}{\\lambda_1}\\,c \\;\\to\\; 0 \\;\\;(i\\to\\infty) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 顶部与尾部对同一个共享数值的诉求相反，因此单一速率可证明地无法同时服务两者——这种张力就是极限。\n\n### 逐方向超越算子\n*构造从谱导出的逐方向预条件子 $D_{ii}=lambda_{i}^{-beta}$ 并证明它超过极限。*\n\n4. 给每个方向各自的速率，取代单一的共享步长。把坐标 i 的更新乘以 $lambda_{i}^{-beta}$（特征值的倒数取 beta 次幂），其中 beta 是一个介于 0 到 1 之间的调节旋钮，用来设定预条件强度：beta=0 恰好是旧的单速率流，beta=1 则完全白化（均衡）所有方向。重标定后，方向 i 上的有效推动变为 $lambda_{i}^{1-beta}$，它在尾部衰减得慢得多，而稳定性上限对每个方向都相同，不再仅由最大特征值决定。每步代价仅为 d 量级，因为重标定是对角的（每个坐标一个数），且每个数都直接从已知的特征值谱读出，无需估计任何东西。\n\n*谱预条件流：对角预条件子 $D_{ii}=lambda_{i}^{-\\beta }$ 把每个坐标的驱动重标定为 $lambda_{i}^{1-\\beta }$，它随 i 衰减得更慢；$\\beta =0$ 还原为单速率流，$\\beta =1$ 为完全白化，且 D 直接从已知谱读出，代价为 O(d)。*\n$$ \\dot{w}_i \\;=\\; -\\,D_{ii}(Q)\\,(\\nabla L)_i, \\qquad D_{ii}(Q) = \\lambda_i^{-\\beta}, \\;\\; \\beta \\in [0,1] \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 用特征值的倒数重标定恰好抵消了节制尾部的特征值，而既然谱已知，便无需估计任何东西。\n5. 用重标定后的推动重做同样的分阶段速率分析，得到新的尾部速度（记为 $gamma_{precond}$，它依赖于 a 和旋钮 beta），并证明它对每个 beta>0 都严格超过单速率极限。同时找出在保持顶部稳定的前提下最快清理尾部的最佳旋钮设置 beta* 【author decision: 把 beta* 设为优化最难的最重尾情形（a 略大于 1）还是优化典型的中段 a，是作者必须做的设计选择，因为这两个目标可能选出不同的 beta*】。整个过程中仔细追踪界中的隐藏常数，使得在 a 从上方趋近 1 的最重尾极限下没有任何常数发散。\n\n*超越定理：对每个正的 $\\beta $，预条件后的尾部指数都严格超过单速率下界，把 a 中一个固定的指数变成由 $\\beta $ 控制的可移动量。*\n$$ \\gamma_{\\mathrm{precond}}(a,\\beta) \\;>\\; \\gamma_{\\mathrm{single}}(a) \\quad \\text{for all } \\beta > 0 \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这就是收益：当初界定旧流的同一套分析，如今证明了新流可证明地逃出那个界。\n\n### 单速率即病因的分离\n*通过 Lyapunov 分解证明慢尾部源于单一共享速率而非谱。*\n\n6. 证明使尾部变慢的是单一共享速率，而不是谱。构造一个加权误差能量 V(t) = 对 i 求和的 $lambda_{i}$ 乘以 $r_{i}$ 平方，并把它分成顶部分量（大特征值块，总是表现良好）与尾部分量（小特征值块，对速率选择敏感）。证明没有任何单一共享步长能让顶部分量与尾部分量同时以逐方向的快速度收缩。这证明单速率流处于一个严格慢于逐方向流的类，而这正是在构造步骤中移除单一共享速率的依据。\n\n*Lyapunov 分解：加权残差能量分裂为一个普遍有界的顶部分量与一个对假设敏感的尾部分量；没有单一的 $\\eta $ 能让两部分都以预条件速率衰减——由此证明单速率类与预条件类严格分离。*\n$$ V(t) \\;=\\; \\sum_i \\lambda_i\\, r_i(t)^2 \\;=\\; V_{\\mathrm{top}}(t) + V_{\\mathrm{tail}}(t) \\tag{5} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这是论证的必要性一半：它表明瓶颈确实是共享速率，这恰好为上一步移除它提供了正当理由。\n\n### 数值验证与机制对照\n*积分两种流、对有限 SGD 做合理性检查、并打乱预条件子以分离谱对齐。*\n\n7. 数值求解两种流并读出尾部速度。对单速率流与逐方向流（beta 取 ${0.25,0.5,0.75,1}$）在规模 d 取 ${1000,10000}$、尾部指数 a 取 ${1.2,1.5,2.0}$ 下积分，使用标准自适应 Runge-Kutta 求解器（Dormand-Prince RK45，容差取紧），从固定的谱初始化点出发，运行足够长直到误差在 log-log 图上稳定为一条干净的直线（当局部斜率在十倍时间跨度内变化不超过约 1% 时判定）。把尾部速度测为 log 误差对 log 时间的斜率，在丢弃早期快速逃逸与中段收敛瞬态后，对最后十倍时间段做最小二乘拟合，然后把这些实测斜率与预测的逐方向速度以及单速率下界比较。\n   - _为什么_: 直接测斜率，检验预测的加速是否随 beta 增大真的出现。\n8. 作为合理性检查（非核心结论），确认理想的光滑流结果在真实采样噪声下仍然成立。在新的随机样本上跑一遍随机梯度下降(Stochastic Gradient Descent, SGD)，使用与光滑流相同的逐方向步长（特征值的负 beta 次幂乘以基础步长 eta）和相同的 eta，处于样本数 n 随维度 d 成比例增长的区间（在 d = 1000 和 10000 下尝试 n = 2d、5d、10d）。把误差曲线在 20 个独立随机种子上取平均，用与之前相同的方式测它的尾部斜率，检查它是否与光滑流预测一致；把跨种子的离散度作为高概率带报告。\n   - _为什么_: 它确认把真实采样噪声放回去后，理想的无噪声流结果仍然成立。\n9. 运行用于把谱对齐分离为机制的负对照。保留完全相同的一组预条件数值，但打乱哪个坐标拿到哪个数值（施加一个随机置换），使每个方向的速率不再与它自己的特征值匹配。在与主积分相同的设置下用这个打乱后的重标定重新求解流，把实测尾部斜率在 20 次独立随机打乱上取平均，报告均值与离散度。预测是尾部速度回落到单速率下界，因为只有与谱匹配的重标定才应当有帮助。\n   - _为什么_: 如果只有与谱匹配的重标定才有用，那么把它打乱就应抹掉加速——这证明是对齐而非泛泛的重标定才是机制。\n10. 报告认证加速的大小。在尾部指数 a 与旋钮 beta 的每一种组合下，报告逐方向尾部速度与单速率下界之间的差距（$gamma_{precond}$ 减去 $gamma_{single}$），同时对照单速率基线与上一步的打乱对照来衡量。让实验揭示这个差距有多大，而不是事先认定一个目标数字；这一差距在各设置下的大小，是把本结果与此前把慢尾部视为不可避免代价的解读区分开来的核心结论。\n   - _为什么_: 这一认证加速在各设置下的大小，是把本工作与锚点的「不可避免代价」解读区分开来的核心结论。\n\n"},{"id":"45","run_dir":"run_prompt45_flash3d","index":45,"title":"FrustumField: Constant-Cost Feed-Forward 3D Scenes with In-Pass Cross-View Self-Correction","title_zh":"FrustumField：常数代价的前馈式三维场景生成与同遍 cross-view 自校正","method_name":"FrustumField","hook":"Every second-scale 3D scene generator still pays a per-region cost — WonderWorld optimizes each FLAGS layer and re-calls depth diffusion per layer, so wall-clock grows with how much scene you commit. We show that predicting the scene onto a fixed-size, extent-independent anchor lattice makes generation cost constant in scene extent, and that re-rendering the prediction against its own implied novel views inside the same forward pass removes the committed-geometry seams that no speed-up otherwise touches.","anchor_pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","anchor_pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","domain_category":"3D Vision & Scene Reconstruction","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces scene-scale geometry whose latency is decoupled from scene extent/layer count: every second-scale method (WonderWorld semanticscholar:1806ae222b5d5941eb621f8e366e2ebdbf96afa7, WonderTurbo openalex:W4409738249) still pays a per-region/per-layer cost, so the unmet need is a generator whose wall-clock does not grow with the amount of scene committed.","pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","sub_pattern":"C15 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by swapping the inherited per-scene-optimized 3DGS/FLAGS representation for a fixed-size structured Gaussian-anchor field defined over a normalized bounded scene-frustum lattice that the feed-forward backbone emits in one pass, so the number of predicted units (hence cost) is constant in scene extent rather than scaling with optimized layers/regions.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf re-tests committed scene geometry against the scene's own later-rendered/predicted views before finalizing: geometry committed from the conditioning view is frozen, so depth/occlusion errors at that view become permanent seams and far-field floaters — the missing outcome is generation that closes the loop between predicted geometry and the multi-view evidence it implies, within the seconds budget.","pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by manufacturing a label-free cross-view agreement readout (the disagreement between an anchor's predicted geometry and what the scene's own auto-sampled novel-view re-renderings imply) and minimizing it inside the same forward pass over a surgically small correction lever (per-anchor depth/opacity residuals), backbone frozen, with a flatness stabilizer that blocks the degenerate collapse of pushing all anchors to a flat background.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"fast high-quality 3D scene generation (feed-forward radiance-field / Gaussian-splatting scene synthesis)","n_papers":42,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":26},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"openreview","n":2}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":23,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"WonderWorld: Interactive 3D Scene Generation from a Single Image"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"FastScene: Text-Driven Fast 3D Indoor Scene Generation via Panoramic Gaussian Splatting"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"DreamScene: 3D Gaussian-based Text-to-3D Scene Generation via Formation Pattern Sampling"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"InfiniCube: Unbounded and Controllable Dynamic 3D Driving Scene Generation with World-Guided Video Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Deterministic Global 3D Fractal Cloud Model for Synthetic Scene Generation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"DreamScene4D: Dynamic Multi-Object Scene Generation from Monocular Videos"}],"more":17},{"year":2025,"n":16,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"DreamScene: 3D Gaussian-based End-to-end Text-to-3D Scene Generation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"DreamAnywhere: Object-Centric Panoramic 3D Scene Generation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Point-Cloud Transmission Oriented 3D Semantic Communication for Accurate Scene Generation-Enabled Digital Twin"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Sceniris: A Fast Procedural Scene Generation Framework"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Generating 360° Video is What You Need For a 3D Scene"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"SceneLCM: End-to-End Layout-Guided Interactive Indoor Scene Generation with Latent Consistency Model"}],"more":10},{"year":2026,"n":2,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"},{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"}],"more":0}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":10,"share":0.238},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":10,"share":0.238},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":6,"share":0.143},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":5,"share":0.119},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":5,"share":0.119},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":4,"share":0.095},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":4,"share":0.095},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":3,"share":0.071}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Across the second-scale 3D-scene-generation frontier, the speed win is bought by replacing slow multi-view-then-optimize pipelines with a per-scene fitting loop that is fast per unit but still amortized over geometry: WonderWorld (semanticscholar:1806ae222b5d5941eb621f8e366e2ebdbf96afa7) reaches <10s only by optimizing each FLAGS layer for ~1s and re-running a guided depth-diffusion call per layer, so wall-clock grows with the number of layers and scene extent, while DreamScene (semanticscholar:87c5d71c6c6f2c11155b490e47d82a8681752c92) and FastScene (semanticscholar:8bf2b7615725511843076cc688631df3950f6ee6) still iterate a sampling/optimization objective per scene. The structural failure is that scene geometry is committed greedily from a single conditioning view (or a single panorama) and never revised against the scene's own later-rendered evidence, so depth/occlusion errors at the conditioning view are frozen into the representation as seams and far-field floaters that no amount of speed-up removes; once a region is committed there is no signal in the pipeline that re-tests whether that committed geometry is consistent with what subsequent generated views imply, so quality and per-scene latency cannot both be improved by tuning the existing fitting loop.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:1806ae222b5d5941eb621f8e366e2ebdbf96afa7","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"WonderWorld generates a scene in <10s using Fast Layered Gaussian Surfels (FLAGS) with geometry-based initialization that cuts single-layer optimization to <1s and a guided depth-diffusion module to reduce inter-scene seams. Its residue: generation is still a per-layer optimize-and-inpaint loop conditioned on one view, so latency scales with layer count and the committed layered geometry is never re-checked against subsequently generated views, leaving boundary distortion and far-field artifacts that the speed technique does not address."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4409738249","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"WonderTurbo pushes interactive world generation to 0.72s by accelerating incremental view-by-view expansion. Its residue: the sub-second budget is achieved for local incremental extrapolation rather than globally consistent whole-scene synthesis, so it does not produce or verify a coherent scene-scale geometry in one feed-forward pass."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:568516ca7d5feda8f7289bee31e4f2412f4493e7","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"DiffusionGS bakes Gaussian splatting into a single-stage diffusion denoiser so a single forward pass yields 3D-consistent Gaussians from one view, removing the multi-stage feed-forward collapse of 2D multi-view diffusion. Its residue: the single-stage prediction is largely object-centric and bounded; it has no mechanism to test or correct the predicted geometry against the scene's own multi-view rendering consistency, so scene-scale extent and far-field fidelity remain open."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:87c5d71c6c6f2c11155b490e47d82a8681752c92","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"DreamScene (end-to-end) plans a scene then generates 3D Gaussians with formation-pattern sampling for text-to-3D scenes with improved consistency and editability. Its residue: it remains an optimization/sampling loop per scene (minutes-scale), so it is not in the seconds regime and inherits the same single-pass-commit weakness without a self-consistency re-test."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"fast high-quality 3D scene generation (feed-forward radiance-field / Gaussian-splatting scene synthesis)","venue":"ICLR / CVPR / NeurIPS (top vision-ML)","time":"2026","data":["multi-view scene datasets (e.g., RealEstate10K, ScanNet, DL3DV)","single-image / text-conditioned scene inputs","panorama and monocular video scene corpora"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"3D vision + generative modeling","preference":"both","baseline":"WonderWorld (FLAGS, <10s/scene), WonderTurbo (0.72s incremental), DiffusionGS (single-stage image-to-3D), DreamScene (end-to-end text-to-3D)","limitation":"current second-scale scene generators still embed a residual per-scene optimization or per-layer fitting loop and condition on a single view, so generation time scales with scene extent/layer count and far-from-camera geometry degrades into seams and floaters","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The sequential_pipeline thread is named CONSTANT-COST PREDICT-THEN-SELF-CORRECT: leg A predicts a scene onto a fixed substrate, leg B consumes that prediction and corrects it against its own implied views, both inside one feed-forward pass. Leg A (C15 representation swap): instead of fitting a per-scene 3DGS/FLAGS field whose optimized-unit count grows with extent (WonderWorld semanticscholar:1806ae222b5d5941eb621f8e366e2ebdbf96afa7 reports ~1s/layer plus a guided depth-diffusion call per layer), we define a FRUSTUM-NORMALIZED ANCHOR LATTICE: a fixed grid of A = 64x64x16 = 65536 anchor slots tiling the camera frustum in normalized inverse-depth coordinates (u in [0,1] image-x, v in [0,1] image-y, w in [0,1] mapping near->far via w = (1/z - 1/z_near)/(1/z_far - 1/z_near)), so the SAME tensor shape represents a 2m room and a 200m vista — extent is absorbed by the normalization, not by adding units. A transformer backbone f_theta (a ViT-style image/text encoder + lattice-cross-attention decoder, ~0.5B params) maps the conditioning image I_0 (and optional text) to, per occupied anchor a, a 14-dim Gaussian parameter vector g_a = (delta_uvw in R^3 offset within its cell, log-scale s_a in R^3, rotation quaternion q_a in R^4, opacity logit o_a in R, RGB c_a in R^3); unoccupied anchors carry o_a -> 0 and are culled. Because A is fixed, leg A's compute is input-size-bounded and constant in scene extent — the load-bearing artifact of gap 1. Leg B (C07 manufactured self-consistency signal): the committed lattice is differentiably splatted not only to the input view but to K = 8 auto-sampled novel viewpoints {pi_k} drawn on a fixed hemisphere around the frustum; for each novel view we render both an RGB image and an expected-depth map, then re-encode each rendered RGB through the FROZEN backbone's geometry head to get a PREDICTED depth d_hat_k(p) for the same pixels. The manufactured readout is the CROSS-VIEW GEOMETRIC DISAGREEMENT R = (1/K) sum_k mean_p rho( d_render_k(p) - d_hat_k(p) ) where d_render is the depth the current anchors splat into view k, d_hat is what the frozen backbone re-reads from the rendered appearance, rho is the Huber loss (delta=0.1 in normalized w-units), and p ranges over pixels whose splat alpha-weight exceeds 0.5 (the selection rule that confines the signal to actually-covered regions). R is the load-bearing variable: it is high exactly where committed geometry contradicts its own implied views (seams, far-field floaters) and zero when the scene is multi-view consistent. We minimize R for T_inner = 3 gradient steps over ONLY the per-anchor residuals (Delta o_a, Delta w_a) — a surgically small lever (2 scalars per anchor) with the backbone f_theta frozen — so the correction repairs committed geometry without overwriting the learned prior. Left alone R has a degenerate minimizer (collapse every anchor to a single flat fronto-parallel sheet, which is trivially cross-view consistent), so we bolt on a STABILIZER: a flatness penalty lambda_flat * (-Var_a[w_a]) (lambda_flat = 0.05) that anchors w-variance to the prediction's, plus a prior-anchor mixture term lambda_prior * ||(Delta o, Delta w)||^2 (lambda_prior = 0.1) keeping residuals near zero. Gap 2 is closed because the frozen-commit pipeline now contains, for the first time, a signal that re-tests committed geometry against the scene's own implied multi-view evidence and a confined lever that acts on it, all within the same seconds-scale forward pass.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The two gaps share the same central object (the fixed anchor lattice) but need separate modules: gap 1 is closed by the representation choice itself (leg A), gap 2 by an operation that reads and writes that representation (leg B) — evidence they are distinct is that you can build leg A's constant-cost generator and measure flat latency WITHOUT leg B, and leg B's self-correction is meaningless without a committed prediction to correct, which is exactly the sequential_pipeline (A->B) signature rather than shared machinery. Alternatives rejected: (i) closing gap 2 by an external MVS consistency-filter post-pass (collateral node c0) — rejected as a regression to a >16y classical move and because it is not feed-forward; (ii) making leg A a vanilla LRM single-pass predictor (collateral c1) — rejected because that commits geometry once with no self-correction and re-proposes an occupied lineage node, so leg A's novelty is specifically the EXTENT-INDEPENDENT frustum-normalized lattice (a representation source the tree does not occupy), not amortization per se.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: train FrustumField on RealEstate10K + DL3DV multi-view scenes and, on held-out scenes, generate from a single image, comparing against WonderWorld and a vanilla single-pass LRM-style predictor (no leg B). If the candidate works, (i) end-to-end wall-clock stays flat as we sweep target far-plane z_far over a 10x range while WonderWorld's time grows with the induced layer count, and (ii) held-out novel-view LPIPS improves and the boundary seam-energy metric and far-field floater count both decrease versus the no-leg-B predictor. The load-bearing variable is R, the cross-view geometric disagreement; negative control: replace each re-read depth d_hat_k with depth from a RANDOMLY permuted novel view (so R is computed against mismatched evidence and no longer tracks true geometric inconsistency) and run the same T_inner=3 correction — predicted effect is that the DOWNSTREAM novel-view LPIPS and seam-energy return to the no-correction baseline (the correction stops helping), confirming the gain comes from R tracking real cross-view inconsistency and not from extra optimization steps. Positive control: drive the corrector using R alone (drop both stabilizer terms but keep the true d_hat) on a held-out subset — it should recover most of the seam-energy reduction before collapsing, identifying R as the mechanism.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:1806ae222b5d5941eb621f8e366e2ebdbf96afa7","delta":"WonderWorld commits geometry from one view into layered FLAGS optimized ~1s/layer with per-layer depth-diffusion, so latency scales with layer count and the commitment is never re-checked; we construct an extent-independent fixed-size frustum-normalized anchor lattice (constant cost in extent) AND a manufactured cross-view disagreement signal R that re-tests and corrects the commitment in-pass, neither of which their construction produces."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4409738249","delta":"WonderTurbo reaches 0.72s by accelerating incremental view-by-view local expansion; we instead predict a whole globally-consistent scene at constant cost and add an in-pass self-consistency correction, so our latency is flat in total scene extent rather than paid per incremental region (abstract-only inference: WonderTurbo fulltext was not fetched)."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:568516ca7d5feda8f7289bee31e4f2412f4493e7","delta":"DiffusionGS bakes 3DGS into a single diffusion pass but commits geometry once with no self-consistency re-test and is largely object-centric/bounded; we add the frustum-normalized scene-scale extent-independent substrate and the cross-view disagreement corrector that re-checks the committed geometry."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:87c5d71c6c6f2c11155b490e47d82a8681752c92","delta":"DreamScene (end-to-end) plans then samples per-scene at minutes-scale with formation-pattern sampling; we eliminate the per-scene sampling/optimization loop entirely via a single constant-cost prediction plus a 3-step confined correction, moving the regime from minutes to seconds."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:1806ae222b5d5941eb621f8e366e2ebdbf96afa7","what_step_was_missed":"WonderWorld reduced per-layer optimization to <1s but kept the representation extent-dependent (one optimized layer set per generated region) and committed geometry from a single view without re-testing it; for our contribution to already exist it would have needed to construct an extent-independent fixed-size scene substrate (so unit count does not grow with extent) AND a self-supervised cross-view disagreement readout computed by re-reading the scene's own rendered novel views through the frozen predictor to correct committed geometry in-pass — neither the fixed substrate nor the in-pass self-re-read correction is built in their layered-surfel pipeline."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":270,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"No hard floor fired: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict is borderline (not triggered) — the only non-clear lesson is C15's 'Stacking auxiliary encoders... without justifying each component's necessity' (candidate_match borderline), whose necessity is already covered by specified ablations and is a non-load-bearing surfacing concern; recipe_application_check.verdict = applied for both legs; anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id = null. paper_pointed_threat (Gen3R) is a competitor but not exact-mechanism overlap — its subsumption_argument shows the candidate's flat-cost lattice + in-pass R conjunction is absent there, and it is addressable via an already-present baseline. The single borderline sits in a non-load-bearing aspect, so the default-to-advance heuristic applies.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces scene-scale geometry whose latency is decoupled from scene extent/layer count: every second-scale method (WonderWorld semanticscholar:1806ae222b5d5941eb621f8e366e2ebdbf96afa7, WonderTurbo openalex:W4409738249) still pays a per-region/per-layer cost, so the unmet need is a generator whose wall-clock does not grow with the amount of scene committed.","main_pattern":"generative_process_redesign","sub_pattern":"C15 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Reject papers do execute the representation swap but fall short on proving necessity — most commonly the new representation handles a harder input regime but the paper never exhibits a controlled setting where the prior representation provably fails and theirs does not, so the swap reads as an incremental extension rather than the liberation of a false constraint.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Swapping a representation to survive a harder input regime, without exhibiting a controlled setting where the old representation provably fails, reads as an extension rather than a liberation.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"falsification_prediction exhibits the controlled setting — sweeping z_far over a 10x range where the inherited per-layer representation's latency provably grows while the fixed lattice stays flat — so the false constraint (extent-dependent unit count) is demonstrated, not asserted."},{"lesson_quoted":"Sound theoretical correctness of a new representation does not survive review when empirical gains over strong baselines are marginal and not shown to fix a real downstream failure mode of competitors.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the candidate ties the swap to two concrete downstream failure modes of WonderWorld (extent-scaling latency and committed-geometry seams) and measures both via wall-clock and seam-energy/floater-count metrics, not a marginal aggregate."},{"lesson_quoted":"A representation borrowed from a neighboring subfield and ported into a new domain is judged incremental unless the paper states exactly what the port resolves that prior representations could not.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the frustum-normalized inverse-depth anchor lattice is constructed for this problem and what_step_was_missed states exactly what it resolves (extent-independent unit count) that FLAGS/3DGS could not."},{"lesson_quoted":"Stacking auxiliary encoders, conditioning tokens, and loss terms around the core substitution without justifying each component's necessity dissolves the contribution into engineering integration with thin novelty.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"leg B adds a corrector + two stabilizer terms; their necessity is justified (ablations for leg B and the stabilizer collapse-test are specified), but a reviewer could read leg B as accretion on top of leg A — surfaced for Phase 4."},{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a structural property the chosen representation should confer — cross-view consistency, validity under symmetry, generalization — without demonstrating it leaves reviewers unconvinced the representation actually delivers the advertised benefit.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"cross-view consistency is not merely claimed of the representation — it is the measured object R and is demonstrated via the seam-energy metric and the negative-control that removes the gain, so the advertised benefit is shown."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf re-tests committed scene geometry against the scene's own later-rendered/predicted views before finalizing: geometry committed from the conditioning view is frozen, so depth/occlusion errors at that view become permanent seams and far-field floaters — the missing outcome is generation that closes the loop between predicted geometry and the multi-view evidence it implies, within the seconds budget.","main_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is a manufactured internal signal whose validity silently rests on an assumption that does not survive deployment (calibration, a known-finite shift set, or covert test-set use), or a recombination of well-known components with no single load-bearing mechanistic insight separating it from prior art.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A label-free signal whose validity depends on model calibration silently fails on exactly the deep networks known to be poorly calibrated — validate a surrogate where its core assumption is weakest, not where it is convenient.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"R is a geometric self-consistency residual (render-vs-re-read depth disagreement), not a calibration-dependent entropy/confidence readout, so its validity does not hinge on backbone calibration."},{"lesson_quoted":"Recasting a continuous shift as a discrete, known, finite set of types indexed against a precomputed lookup table collapses the moment an unanticipated or mixed shift arrives.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"no discretization or shift-type lookup table is used — R is a continuous per-pixel disagreement minimized directly."},{"lesson_quoted":"Importing a generic continual-learning blending or interpolation technique into a new modality without identifying that modality's specific dynamics lever reads as recombination, not contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the modality-specific lever is named explicitly (per-anchor depth/opacity residuals on the frustum lattice), not a generic blend."},{"lesson_quoted":"Reusing standard sequential machinery (chaining each step's posterior as the next prior) without a new stabilizer amplifies noise and looks derivative of prior adaptation work.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"a new stabilizer (flatness/variance-anchoring + prior-residual term) matched to the identified degenerate collapse mode is supplied, which is the cluster's required move."},{"lesson_quoted":"A multi-branch or ensemble reweighting mechanism that overlaps with standard multi-task/mixture-of-experts ensembling must explicitly beat both the single-model and the standard-ensemble baselines, or the gain is credited to prior art.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"no ensemble/multi-branch reweighting is involved; the corrector is a single confined optimization on residuals."},{"lesson_quoted":"Using target or test-set information during adaptation invites a label-leakage objection that undermines the very source-free, label-free deployment setting the method claims.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"R is computed entirely from the scene's own predicted anchors and self-rendered views — no target/test labels enter, so there is no leakage."}],"verdict":"clear"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The self_supervised_signal_engineering (C07) entry is fully clear — R avoids calibration-dependence, discretization, generic blending, ensembling, and leakage, and supplies the required new stabilizer. The generative_process_redesign (C15) entry is borderline only on the 'stacking auxiliary components' lesson (leg B + stabilizers could read as accretion on the core swap), with necessity-ablations specified; no entry is triggered."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces scene-scale geometry whose latency is decoupled from scene extent/layer count: every second-scale method (WonderWorld semanticscholar:1806ae222b5d5941eb621f8e366e2ebdbf96afa7, WonderTurbo openalex:W4409738249) still pays a per-region/per-layer cost, so the unmet need is a generator whose wall-clock does not grow with the amount of scene committed.","sub_pattern":"C15 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Re-choose the geometric/structural representation a 3D synthesis procedure operates over, treating the inherited parameterization as a tractability convenience rather than a requirement, holding the rest of the engine standard so the gain is attributed to the representation alone.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism leg A replaces the inherited per-scene-optimized 3DGS/FLAGS field with a fixed-size frustum-normalized inverse-depth anchor lattice the standard transformer backbone emits in one pass — the engine (transformer + splatting) is left standard and the constant-cost gain is attributed to the representation swap, exactly the cluster's signature move.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf re-tests committed scene geometry against the scene's own later-rendered/predicted views before finalizing: geometry committed from the conditioning view is frozen, so depth/occlusion errors at that view become permanent seams and far-field floaters — the missing outcome is generation that closes the loop between predicted geometry and the multi-view evidence it implies, within the seconds budget.","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Pair a mechanistic diagnosis that localizes the failure to a structural site with a surgically confined correction — minimize a continuous internal-state/self-agreement objective over a minimal lever while the backbone stays frozen — and bolt on an explicit stabilizer against the degenerate collapse the label-free signal invites.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism leg B localizes the failure to committed far-field geometry, minimizes the continuous cross-view disagreement R over a surgically small lever (2 residual scalars per anchor) with the backbone frozen, and bolts on the flatness/prior stabilizer matched to the flat-sheet collapse mode — the diagnose-localize / minimize-on-tiny-lever / stabilize-against-collapse triple is present.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries perform their cited cluster's distinctive move: leg A is a representation-only swap with the engine held standard (C15), and leg B is a frozen-backbone confined-lever self-agreement minimization with a collapse-matched stabilizer (C07), not the parent patterns' generic gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["generative_process_redesign","self_supervised_signal_engineering"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as a component; the candidate's set {generative_process_redesign, self_supervised_signal_engineering} contains no heterogeneous_decomposition, so no anti-pattern matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"openalex:W7119557557","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"Gen3R ('3D Scene Generation Meets Feed-Forward Reconstruction', collision_hits) is the most specific competitor: it also produces 3D scenes in a feed-forward pass, which contests the candidate's novelty on the constant-cost-generation claim. The candidate's claim stands only because Gen3R (like One2Scene openalex:W7131318903) commits its predicted geometry in a single pass WITHOUT an extent-independent frustum-normalized substrate that makes latency provably flat in scene extent AND without a manufactured cross-view disagreement signal that re-tests and corrects the committed geometry in-pass — both load-bearing artifacts (gap 1's flat-cost lattice and gap 2's self-correction R) are absent from a generic feed-forward reconstructor, so the candidate's contribution is the conjunction Gen3R lacks rather than feed-forward-ness per se.","addressable_via":"differentiation_from_lit and falsification_prediction should explicitly benchmark against a Gen3R-style single-pass feed-forward predictor (already partially covered by the 'vanilla single-pass LRM-style predictor' baseline) and report the extent-sweep + seam-energy deltas that isolate the lattice and R from generic feed-forward prediction."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# FrustumField: Constant-Cost Feed-Forward 3D Scenes with In-Pass Cross-View Self-Correction\n\n**Method.** FrustumField\n\n## Motivation\nToday's fastest 3D scene generators can build a scene in seconds, but they win that speed in a way that quietly limits them. Methods like WonderWorld build the scene region by region — for each layer they run a short optimization and a depth-prediction step — so the more scene you ask for, the longer it takes; the time grows with the size of the scene. Worse, once a piece of geometry is placed (based on the one input image), it is never re-checked: any depth or occlusion mistake at that first view gets frozen in, showing up as visible seams where regions meet and as floating junk far from the camera. No amount of speeding up the per-region loop fixes this, because nothing in the pipeline ever asks 'is this committed geometry actually consistent with what the rest of the scene implies?'\n\nWhy this is solvable now: single-pass scene predictors (like DiffusionGS, which predicts 3D Gaussians in one diffusion pass) have shown you can skip per-scene optimization entirely, and fast differentiable rendering makes it cheap to render a predicted scene from many new viewpoints and re-read its geometry — turning the scene's own implied views into a free self-check. Nobody has yet combined a scene representation whose cost doesn't grow with scene size with an in-pass self-correction that uses those implied views.\n\nOur idea: predict the whole scene in one pass onto a fixed-size grid that tiles the camera's view in normalized inverse-depth coordinates, so a tiny room and a huge vista use the exact same number of slots — making generation cost constant no matter how big the scene is. Then, still inside the same forward pass, render that scene from several automatically-chosen new viewpoints, re-read the geometry the renderings imply, and measure where the committed geometry disagrees with itself across views (which is exactly where seams and floaters live). A few quick correction steps, nudging only a tiny per-slot adjustment and held back by a stabilizer so the scene can't collapse to a flat wall, repair those errors before the final image is produced.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n*Unchanged scaffolding: supervised training with flat-latency verification, rendering the corrected scene with end-to-end joint finetuning, and evaluation with falsification controls.*\n\n1. Train the predictor by rendering its predicted scene to held-out known camera views of multi-view datasets (RealEstate10K / DL3DV / ScanNet) and matching them with a pixel-difference loss, a perceptual (LPIPS) loss, and a depth loss against sensor or multi-view-stereo depth. Then check the headline property under a fixed recipe: keep the input image, the grid, the number of extra viewpoints, and the number of correction steps all fixed, and increase the scene's far distance over a 10x range on the same scene, timing the full forward pass (median of 20 runs after warm-up on one GPU). 'Flat' means the time does not trend up as the scene gets deeper — the number of predicted pieces never changes, so the only thing that can vary is how many pixels the splatting fills, which you report on the side.\n   - _Why_: This both teaches the predictor to make good scenes and directly verifies the headline claim that time doesn't grow with scene size.\n2. Render the CORRECTED grid to produce the final scene the user actually sees — so fixing far-away depth changes the output picture, not just the score. Then unfreeze the big predictor and train the whole thing end-to-end with the 3 correction steps inside the loop: unroll those steps as a differentiable computation and back-propagate through them, so the predictor learns to output scenes the corrector can fix with only a few cheap steps. The supervision is the same rendering losses as before, but computed on the corrected-scene render to held-out views (optionally with a small extra term on the final disagreement score); fine-tune the predictor gently (AdamW, learning rate 1e-5) after the main predictor has already converged.\n   - _Why_: The correction only matters if it changes the final render, and co-training lets the predictor and corrector meet in the middle so a short correction is enough.\n3. On held-out scenes, measure novel-view PSNR and LPIPS, a seam-energy metric, a far-field floater count, and end-to-end wall-clock, comparing against WonderWorld and a plain single-pass predictor with no self-correction. Compute seam-energy as the average squared depth-jump in the rendered depth map, looked at only in a 3-pixel band along the edges of predicted regions (an edge is where the slot that dominates a pixel changes), averaged over the 8 new views. Count far-field floaters as the number of separate opacity blobs that sit in the farthest 20% of the depth range and are detached (more than 5 pixels) from any nearby support, per scene. Then run a negative control (feed the re-read depth from a randomly shuffled view so the disagreement no longer tracks real errors) and a positive control (drive the corrector by the disagreement alone, dropping both guards but keeping the true re-read depth), and also ablate the self-correction and the stabilizer (expect the scene to collapse flat).\n   - _Why_: These comparisons confirm the speed-flat-in-size and seam/floater gains, and the shuffled-view control proves the gain comes from the disagreement tracking real geometry errors, not from just running more optimization steps.\n\n### Constant-Cost Substrate\n*Represent any-extent scene on a fixed-size frustum-normalized anchor lattice so feed-forward generation cost is constant in scene extent.*\n\n4. Set up a fixed grid of 64x64x16 = 65536 anchor slots that tiles the camera's view in normalized coordinates: horizontal position u, vertical position v, and a depth coordinate w that runs from near to far using inverse depth (so close and far things both get fair coverage). Make the depth map go both ways: a slot at coordinate w sits at metric depth $z = 1/((1-w)/z_{near} + w/z_{far}),$ and each slot's image position back-projects through the camera intrinsics to a ray. Only two numbers carry the scene's physical scale — $z_{near}$ (use 0.1 in the camera's units, or 0.1 times the median estimated depth when true scale is unknown) and $z_{far}$ (the scene's reach, which you sweep later); everything else is derived from them, so the grid keeps the same shape no matter how big the scene is.\n\n*The anchor lattice tiles the camera frustum in normalized image-x u, image-y v, and inverse-depth w that maps $near\\to far$; the fixed slot count A = 65536 is independent of scene extent, which is absorbed by the $z_{far}$ normalization.*\n$$ w = \\frac{1/z - 1/z_{\\mathrm{near}}}{1/z_{\\mathrm{far}} - 1/z_{\\mathrm{near}}}, \\qquad (u,v,w) \\in [0,1]^3,\\; A = 64 \\times 64 \\times 16 = 65536 \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: If the number of pieces you predict never grows with the scene, the cost of predicting the scene can't grow with the scene either.\n5. Use one feed-forward transformer (a roughly 0.5-billion-parameter image/text encoder plus a decoder that attends into the grid) to produce, for every slot, a 14-number little-Gaussian description: a small position offset inside the cell, a size, an orientation (a four-number quaternion), an opacity, and an RGB color. The model fills in all slots; a slot counts as empty and is dropped at render time when its opacity falls below about 1%. Keep each offset inside its own cell by squashing it with a tanh scaled to half a cell, normalize the orientation to unit length, and decode size and color in the usual Gaussian-splatting ranges. Because the grid always has the same number of slots, this single pass costs the same regardless of scene size.\n\n*Per occupied anchor a the backbone emits a 14-dim Gaussian parameter vector: a sub-cell offset, a log-scale, a rotation quaternion, an opacity logit, and an RGB color; anchors with opacity logit $o_{a} \\to  0$ are culled.*\n$$ g_a = (\\Delta_{uvw} \\in \\mathbb{R}^3,\\; \\log s_a \\in \\mathbb{R}^3,\\; q_a \\in \\mathbb{R}^4,\\; o_a \\in \\mathbb{R},\\; c_a \\in \\mathbb{R}^3) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Committing the whole scene in a single pass over a fixed-size grid removes the region-by-region optimization loop whose cost grew with the scene.\n\n### In-Pass Cross-View Self-Correction\n*Render the committed scene to its own implied novel views, measure the cross-view geometric disagreement, and repair it over a confined per-anchor lever with a flat-sheet stabilizer.*\n\n6. Take the committed grid of Gaussians and render it — with differentiable splatting — not just to the input camera but to 8 automatically-chosen new viewpoints. Place those 8 cameras deterministically on a ring on the upper half-sphere around the scene (every 45 degrees in azimuth, a fixed 20-degree tilt, each pointed at the scene center, same ring for every scene so results are comparable). For each new view produce a color image and an expected-depth map (the depth at each pixel is the opacity-weighted average depth of the Gaussians that cover it), and keep each pixel's accumulated coverage weight for use in the next step.\n   - _Why_: These extra renderings are the scene's own implied evidence about its geometry, which the usual commit-once pipeline never looks at.\n7. For each of the 8 new views, feed its rendered color image back through the SAME frozen predictor's depth head — a small depth decoder sitting on the predictor's frozen image encoder, trained earlier alongside the main model to output a normalized inverse-depth map in the same depth units as the grid — to get a 're-read' depth. Then measure how much that re-read depth disagrees with the depth the grid actually splatted into that view, using a robust (Huber) difference with a tolerance of 0.1 in those normalized depth units, only over pixels the splatting covered well (coverage weight above 0.5), and average over the 8 views. This single disagreement score is high exactly at seams and floating far-field junk and near zero when the scene is consistent across views.\n\n*The cross-view geometric disagreement R averages, over K = 8 auto-sampled novel views and over pixels whose splat alpha-weight exceeds 0.5, the Huber loss $\\rho  (\\delta  = 0.1$ in normalized w-units) between the depth the current anchors splat into view k and the depth the frozen backbone re-reads from that view's rendered appearance.*\n$$ R = \\frac{1}{K}\\sum_{k=1}^{K}\\; \\operatorname*{mean}_{p:\\, \\alpha_k(p) > 0.5}\\; \\rho\\big( d^{\\mathrm{render}}_k(p) - \\hat{d}_k(p) \\big), \\qquad K = 8 \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: If the geometry were truly right, what you render and what the model re-reads from that render would agree; where they disagree is exactly where the committed geometry is wrong.\n8. Starting from zero, take 3 small Adam steps (learning rate 0.01) that lower the disagreement score by adjusting ONLY two numbers per slot — a depth tweak and an opacity tweak — while keeping the big predictor frozen. Add two guards: one rewards keeping a healthy spread of corrected depths so the scene can't cheat by flattening every slot onto one wall (a flat wall would trivially look consistent across views), and one keeps the tweaks small and close to the original prediction. Because the 'keep tweaks small' guard holds the depths near what was predicted, the spread guard effectively anchors the corrected depth-spread to the predicted one. Then apply the tweaks to the grid.\n\n*The confined corrector takes $T_{inner} = 3$ gradient steps over only the per-anchor opacity/inverse-depth residuals $(\\Delta o_{a}, \\Delta w_{a}),$ with the backbone frozen, minimizing R plus a flatness/variance-anchoring stabilizer (weight 0.05) that blocks the degenerate collapse of all anchors to a flat sheet and a prior-residual term (weight 0.1) keeping residuals near zero.*\n$$ \\min_{\\{\\Delta o_a, \\Delta w_a\\}}\\; R \\;-\\; \\lambda_{\\mathrm{flat}}\\,\\mathrm{Var}_a[w_a] \\;+\\; \\lambda_{\\mathrm{prior}}\\,\\lVert(\\Delta o, \\Delta w)\\rVert^2, \\qquad \\lambda_{\\mathrm{flat}}=0.05,\\; \\lambda_{\\mathrm{prior}}=0.1 \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A tiny, confined correction repairs the wrong geometry without erasing what the predictor learned, and the depth-spread guard blocks the degenerate flat-wall shortcut.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# FrustumField：常数代价的前馈式三维场景生成与同遍 cross-view 自校正\n\n**方法名称.** FrustumField\n\n## 研究动机\n如今最快的 3D 场景生成器能在几秒内造出一个场景，但它们换取速度的方式悄悄限制了自己。像 WonderWorld 这样的方法是一块块地建场景——每一层都跑一小段优化加一次深度预测——所以你要的场景越大，耗时越长；时间随场景大小增长。更糟的是，几何一旦根据那张输入图被放下，就再也不复核：第一视角处的任何深度或遮挡错误都会被冻进去，表现为区域交界处可见的接缝、以及离相机很远处漂浮的杂物。把每块的循环加速再多也修不了它，因为流程里从没有任何环节去问『这块已确定的几何，真的和场景其余部分所暗示的一致吗？』\n\n为什么现在能解决：单遍场景预测器（如一次 diffusion 就预测出 3D Gaussian 的 DiffusionGS）已经证明可以完全跳过逐场景优化，而快速可微渲染让我们能廉价地把预测出的场景从许多新视角渲染并重读其几何——把场景自己暗示的视角变成一个免费的自检。但还没有人把『代价不随场景大小增长的表示』和『用这些暗示视角做的同遍自校正』结合起来。\n\n我们的想法：一次前馈就把整个场景预测到一个固定大小的格点上，这个格点以归一化的逆深度坐标铺满相机视野，于是一个小房间和一片巨大远景用的槽位数完全相同——无论场景多大，生成代价都恒定。然后，仍在同一次前馈里，把这个场景从若干自动选出的新视角渲染，重读渲染所暗示的几何，并度量已确定几何在不同视角间何处自相矛盾（接缝与漂浮物正好就在那里）。几步快速校正——只微调每个槽位上一个很小的修正量，并由一个稳定项拉住，使场景不会塌成一面平墙——就在产出最终画面前修好这些错误。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景脚手架\n*不变的支撑部分：带平稳延迟验证的有监督训练、渲染校正后场景并端到端联合微调、以及带 falsification 对照的评测。*\n\n1. 训练预测器：把它预测的场景用可微渲染到多视角数据集（RealEstate10K / DL3DV / ScanNet）留出的已知相机视角，用像素差损失、感知损失（LPIPS）以及对传感器或 multi-view-stereo 深度的深度损失去匹配（深度均在归一化 w 单位下比较）。然后按固定流程检验核心性质：保持输入图像、格点、额外视角数 K=8 与校正步数 $T_{inner}$ 不变，在同一场景内容上把远界 $z_{far}$ 在 10 倍范围内扫描，在一块固定 GPU 上对每个 $z_{far}$ 取 20 次预热后运行的端到端前馈墙钟时间中位数。所谓平稳，是指墙钟时间相对 $z_{far}$ 没有正斜率（单元数 A 由构造恒定；任何残余波动只来自 splatting 的填充率，另行报告）。\n   - _为什么_: 这既教会预测器生成好场景，又直接验证了核心主张：时间不随场景大小增长。\n2. 把『校正后的』格点渲染出来，作为用户真正看到的最终场景——这样修远处深度就会改变输出画面，而不只是改变分数。然后解冻大预测器，把 3 步校正放进循环里端到端训练：把这几步展开成可微计算并对其反向传播，使预测器学会输出『校正器只需几步廉价校正就能修好』的场景。监督仍是与之前相同的渲染损失，但在校正后场景渲染到留出视角上计算（可选再加一小项作用于最终不一致分数）；在主预测器已收敛后，用 AdamW、学习率 1e-5 轻量微调预测器。\n   - _为什么_: 校正只有在改变最终渲染时才有意义；联合训练让预测器与校正器在中间相遇，使短短几步校正就够用。\n3. 在留出场景上度量新视角 PSNR 与 LPIPS、一个 seam-energy 指标、一个远处漂浮物计数，以及端到端墙钟时间，并与 WonderWorld 及一个无自校正的普通单遍预测器对比。把 seam-energy 算作渲染深度图中的平均深度跳变平方，仅在预测区域边缘 3 像素带内考察（边缘即主导某像素的槽发生变化之处），并对 8 个新视角取平均。把远处漂浮物计数算作每个场景中位于深度范围最远 20%、且与任何邻近支撑脱离（超过 5 像素）的独立不透明度团块数。然后跑一个负对照（把重读深度换成随机打乱视角的深度，使不一致不再追踪真实错误）和一个正对照（仅用不一致分数驱动校正器，去掉两道护栏但保留真实重读深度），并消融掉自校正和稳定项（预期场景塌成平面）。\n   - _为什么_: 这些对比确认了『速度随场景平稳』与接缝/漂浮物改善，而打乱视角的对照则证明收益来自不一致分数追踪真实几何错误，而非仅仅多跑了几步优化。\n\n### 常数代价表示基底\n*把任意范围的场景表示在固定大小的 frustum-normalized 锚点格点上，使前馈生成代价与场景范围无关。*\n\n4. 建立一个固定的 64x64x16 = 65536 个锚点槽的格点，以归一化坐标铺满相机视野：水平位置 u、垂直位置 v，以及一个用逆深度从近到远的深度坐标 w（让近处和远处都得到公平覆盖）。把深度映射做成双向的：坐标为 w 的槽位于度量深度 $z = 1/((1-w)/z_{near} + w/z_{far})$ 处，每个槽的图像位置经相机内参 K 反投影成一条射线。只有两个数承载场景的物理尺度$——z_{near}$（取相机单位下的 0.1，或当真实尺度未知时取估计深度中位数的 0.1 倍）与 $z_{far}$（场景的远界，稍后扫描）；其余一切都由它们导出，因此无论场景多大，格点都保持相同形状。\n\n*锚点格点在归一化的图像横坐标 u、纵坐标 v 与逆深度 w（由近到远）上铺满相机视锥，槽位总数 A = 65536 固定，与场景范围无关——范围被 $z_{far}$ 归一化吸收。*\n$$ w = \\frac{1/z - 1/z_{\\mathrm{near}}}{1/z_{\\mathrm{far}} - 1/z_{\\mathrm{near}}}, \\qquad (u,v,w) \\in [0,1]^3,\\; A = 64 \\times 64 \\times 16 = 65536 \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 如果你预测的单元数永远不随场景增长，那么预测场景的代价也就不会随场景增长。\n5. 用一个前馈 transformer（约 0.5B 参数的 image/text 编码器，加一个向格点做 cross-attention 的解码器）为每个槽产生一个 14 维的小高斯描述：胞内小偏移、尺寸、朝向（四元数 quaternion）、不透明度、RGB 颜色。模型填满所有槽；当某槽不透明度低于约 1% 时即视为空槽并在渲染时剔除。用缩放到半个胞的 tanh 把每个偏移限制在自己的胞内，把朝向归一化为单位长度，并按常规 3D Gaussian Splatting 的范围解码尺寸与颜色。因为格点槽数恒定，这一遍的代价与场景大小无关。\n\n*对每个被占用的锚点 a，backbone 输出一个 14 维高斯参数向量：胞内偏移、log-尺度、旋转四元数、不透明度 logit 与 RGB 颜色；不透明度 logit $o_{a} \\to  0$ 的锚点被剔除。*\n$$ g_a = (\\Delta_{uvw} \\in \\mathbb{R}^3,\\; \\log s_a \\in \\mathbb{R}^3,\\; q_a \\in \\mathbb{R}^4,\\; o_a \\in \\mathbb{R},\\; c_a \\in \\mathbb{R}^3) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 在固定大小的格点上一次前馈就确定整个场景，去掉了那个代价随场景增长的逐区域优化循环。\n\n### 同遍 cross-view 自校正\n*把已确定的场景渲染到它自己暗示的新视角，度量 cross-view 几何不一致，并在受限的每锚点修正量上配合 flat-sheet 稳定项加以修复。*\n\n6. 拿已确定的高斯格点，用可微 splatting 渲染——不仅渲染到输入相机，还渲染到 8 个自动选出的新视角。把这 8 个相机确定性地放在围绕场景的上半球的一圈上（方位角每 45 度一个、固定 20 度俯仰、各自看向场景中心，所有场景用同一圈以便结果可比）。对每个新视角产出一张彩色图和一张期望深度图（每个像素的深度是覆盖它的高斯按不透明度加权的平均深度），并保留每个像素的累计覆盖权重供下一步使用。\n   - _为什么_: 这些额外渲染是场景自己关于其几何的『暗示证据』，而通常的确定一次的流程从不去看它。\n7. 对这 8 个新视角中的每一个，把它渲染出的彩色图重新送回那个『冻结的』预测器的深度头——一个搭在预测器冻结图像编码器上的小深度解码器，先前与主模型一同训练，输出与格点同单位的归一化逆深度图——得到一个『重读』深度。然后度量这个重读深度与格点实际 splat 进该视角的深度有多不一致：用稳健的 Huber 差，容差在该归一化深度单位下取 0.1，仅在 splatting 覆盖良好的像素上（覆盖权重高于 0.5），并对 8 个视角取平均。这个单一不一致分数在接缝和远处漂浮杂物处恰好很高，在场景跨视角一致时接近零。\n\n*cross-view 几何不一致 R 在 K = 8 个自动采样的新视角上、以及 splat alpha 权重超过 0.5 的像素上，对『当前锚点 splat 进视角 k 的深度』与『冻结 backbone 从该视角渲染外观重读出的深度』之差取 Huber 损失 $\\rho $（$\\delta  = 0.1$，单位为归一化 w）并平均。*\n$$ R = \\frac{1}{K}\\sum_{k=1}^{K}\\; \\operatorname*{mean}_{p:\\, \\alpha_k(p) > 0.5}\\; \\rho\\big( d^{\\mathrm{render}}_k(p) - \\hat{d}_k(p) \\big), \\qquad K = 8 \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 如果几何真的正确，你渲染出的深度和模型从该渲染重读出的深度就该一致；它们不一致之处，正是已确定几何出错之处。\n8. 从零开始，做 3 步小 Adam（学习率 0.01），仅通过调整每个槽的两个数——一个深度微调和一个不透明度微调——来降低不一致分数，同时让大预测器保持冻结。加两道护栏：一道奖励『保持校正后深度有健康的散布』，使场景不能靠把每个槽压平到一面墙上来作弊（一面平墙会平凡地跨视角看似一致）；另一道让微调保持很小、贴近原始预测。因为『让微调保持很小』这道护栏把深度拉在预测附近，散布护栏实际上就把校正后的深度散布锚定到预测的散布上。然后把微调应用到格点上。\n\n*受限校正器在 backbone 冻结下，仅对每锚点的不透明度/逆深度残差 $(\\Delta o_{a}, \\Delta w_{a})$ 做 $T_{inner} = 3$ 步梯度，最小化 R 加上一项阻止所有锚点塌成平面的 flatness/方差锚定稳定项（权重 0.05）与一项让残差贴近零的先验残差项（权重 0.1）。*\n$$ \\min_{\\{\\Delta o_a, \\Delta w_a\\}}\\; R \\;-\\; \\lambda_{\\mathrm{flat}}\\,\\mathrm{Var}_a[w_a] \\;+\\; \\lambda_{\\mathrm{prior}}\\,\\lVert(\\Delta o, \\Delta w)\\rVert^2, \\qquad \\lambda_{\\mathrm{flat}}=0.05,\\; \\lambda_{\\mathrm{prior}}=0.1 \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 一个微小、受限的校正修好了错误几何，又不抹掉预测器学到的东西，而深度范围护栏挡住了『压成一面平墙』的退化捷径。\n\n"},{"id":"46","run_dir":"run_prompt46_mambamarkov","index":46,"title":"Which Gate Counts: Component-Level Identification of Mamba's In-Context Markov Estimator","title_zh":"哪个门在计数：Mamba 上下文马尔可夫估计器的组件级辨识","method_name":"Component-Level Estimator Identification (CLEI)","hook":"From Markov to Laplace shows a single-layer Mamba implements the Bayes-optimal Laplacian-smoothing estimator at its well-specified optimum, but it leaves the estimator's identity treated as fixed and the carrying component unnamed. We show the estimator is neither fixed nor carried by the part one would guess: under train/test order-mismatch and short contexts the same recurrence stops behaving like Laplace and provably tracks a Krichevsky–Trofimov / context-tree shrinkage estimator instead, and a single named state variable — the input-conditioned co-occurrence accumulation written by the B̄_t gate — is the component whose causal ablation flips which estimator the model implements.","anchor_pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","anchor_pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","domain_category":"Interpretability & Representation Analysis","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved paper provides a controlled diagnostic that isolates WHICH component of the selective recurrence (the input-dependent Ā_t decay vs. the input-dependent B̄_t write gate vs. fixed state width) is the binding constraint that lets or prevents the Markov-chain conditional statistic from being accumulated, so the observed empirical success/failure of Mamba on structured-sequence ICL (openalex:W6967343425, semanticscholar:9da427202cc48370fd66359f5d72ff5ff3bc8b57) cannot be attributed to a ","pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","companion_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","how_closed":"Closed by reframing the opaque 'which recurrence component is responsible' question as a faithful per-component estimator-attribution object E_c over {Ā_t decay, B̄_t write-gate co-occurrence accumulation, fixed width n}, certified sound by an estimator-flipping causal ablation; the companion controlled_diagnostic_design ships the confound-isolating separation that holds the other two components fixed while intervening on one, so the binding driver is a named, intervenable state-level quantity rather than an aggregate score.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved paper tests whether the continuous-latent assumption shared by every selective-SSM ICL theory leaf — that the in-context task's latent is a real-valued state evolved by a linear belief update — is necessary for the optimality account, rather than an artifact of choosing only continuous (LG-SSM / linear-regression / single-index) task families; the question of whether the same recurrence admits a fundamentally different in-context estimator class when the latent is a discrete distrib","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","how_closed":"Closed by naming the tacit 'the recurrence implements one fixed (continuous-latent-derived) estimator class' assumption and overturning it — under regime shift the SAME recurrence pivots from the Laplacian-smoothing estimator to a Krichevsky–Trofimov / context-tree shrinkage estimator — with the companion controlled_diagnostic_design supplying the confound-isolating separation (estimator-identity divergence to each reference) that proves the pivot is a real class change, not a relabeling of one Laplace estimator.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"mechanistic theory of in-context learning in selective state-space models (Mamba), specialized to discrete Markov-chain sequence tasks","n_papers":50,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":27},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":14,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Vision Mamba: Efficient Visual Representation Learning with Bidirectional State Space Model"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Speech Recognition for Air Traffic Control Utilizing a Multi-Head State-Space Model and Transfer Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Can Mamba Learn How to Learn? A Comparative Study on In-Context Learning Tasks"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Is Mamba Capable of In-Context Learning?"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Samba: Simple Hybrid State Space Models for Efficient Unlimited Context Language Modeling"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Contextual AI models for single-cell protein biology"}],"more":8},{"year":2025,"n":29,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"PillarMamba: Learning Local-Global Context for Roadside Point Cloud via Hybrid State Space Model"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"HydraMamba: Multi-Head State Space Model for Global Point Cloud Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Selecting and Pruning: A Differentiable Causal Sequentialized State-Space Model for Two-View Correspondence Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Probing In-Context Learning: Impact of Task Complexity and Model Architecture on Generalization and Efficiency"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Mamba-CR: A State-Space Model for Remote Sensing Image Cloud Removal"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"State Space Model Meets Transformer: A New Paradigm for 3D Object Detection"}],"more":23},{"year":2026,"n":8,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"CI-CBM: Class-Incremental Concept Bottleneck Model for Interpretable Continual Learning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Bayesian Optimality of In-Context Learning with Selective State Spaces"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Understanding and Improving Continuous Adversarial Training for LLMs via In-context Learning Theory"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Fine-Tuning Without Forgetting In-Context Learning: A Theoretical Analysis of Linear Attention Models"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"When Context Sticks: Studying Interference in In-Context Learning"}],"more":2}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":13,"share":0.26},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":10,"share":0.2},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":5,"share":0.1},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":5,"share":0.1},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":4,"share":0.08},{"pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","count":4,"share":0.08},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":3,"share":0.06},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":3,"share":0.06}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"The recent theory of in-context learning in selective state-space models pins Mamba's success to a CONTINUOUS-state estimation principle whose machinery cannot produce the quantity a discrete Markov-chain task actually requires. arxiv:2602.17744v1 proves a meta-trained selective SSM asymptotically implements the Bayes-optimal posterior-predictive mean for Linear-Gaussian state-space tasks (an additive Kalman-style belief update over a real-valued latent z_t), and openalex:W4415334660 proves trained Mamba emulates online gradient descent on an in-context linear-regression loss; both characterize the SSM hidden state as approximating a continuous-valued estimator updated by linear recurrence. But when the in-context task is a finite-state Markov chain with an unknown random transition matrix — the setting openalex:W6967343425 shows transformers solve by in-context transition-probability estimation — the object to be inferred is a stochastic MATRIX of conditional next-symbol probabilities, and the Bayes-optimal predictor is a Dirichlet-posterior transition-count estimator (normalized symbol-pair counts), not a Gaussian posterior mean over a continuous latent. The current selective-SSM theory therefore gives no account of whether, and through which property of the input-dependent recurrence Ā_t, h_t = Ā_t h_{t-1} + B̄_t x_t, a fixed-width Mamba state can accumulate and normalize the conditional co-occurrence statistics a Markov-chain Bayes predictor needs — leaving the field unable to say when Mamba in-context learns the chain versus when its continuous-filtering inductive bias makes it systematically miss the discrete estimator (e.g. as chain order or alphabet size grows past what a finite-width additive state can separate).","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.17744v1","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Models ICL of selective SSMs as Bayes-optimal sequential prediction and proves a meta-trained selective SSM converges to the posterior-predictive mean for Linear-Gaussian SSM tasks, with a continuous Kalman-style belief-state update and a statistical separation from gradient-descent/ERM predictors; its method explicitly defines each task as an LG-SSM with continuous latent z_t ∈ R^d and Gaussian noise. Residue: the framework's optimality and separation results are derived only for the continuous LG-SSM class, and its character-level Markov experiment is empirical validation with no theorem — it never characterizes the Bayes-optimal object for a discrete random-transition-matrix chain (a Dirichlet-posterior count estimator) nor proves whether the finite-width selective recurrence can represent the normalized conditional-count statistic that estimator requires, so the discrete-Markov regime where its continuous-filtering account should break is left uncharacterized."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415334660","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Proves trained Mamba emulates a variant of online gradient descent on the in-context linear-regression objective, establishing an exponential convergence rate and a Transformer-comparable loss bound, and identifies the recurrence as implementing an OGD-style update on a continuous latent function. Residue: the algorithm it extracts (online gradient descent on a real-valued regression loss) is specific to continuous targets and says nothing about how — or whether — the same recurrence accumulates the discrete conditional-count sufficient statistic a Markov-chain transition estimator needs, so it does not transfer to the discrete-symbol setting."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W6967343425","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Shows transformers trained by next-token prediction on random-transition-matrix Markov chains cross a size/data threshold above which they ESTIMATE the in-context transition probabilities rather than memorize training patterns, and that richer state encodings improve out-of-distribution chain robustness. Residue: the study is transformer-only and treats the estimator as a black box (it measures that estimation happens, not which internal quantity carries it), so it neither analyzes the selective-SSM recurrence nor identifies the in-state statistic that would let a Mamba (rather than an attention) model implement the same count-based estimator."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415273485","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Proves Mamba achieves efficient ICL of low-dimensional single-index targets via test-time feature learning and isolates the nonlinear gating mechanism as the driver of feature extraction. Residue: the analyzed target is a continuous single-index function y ≈ g_*(⟨β,x⟩) with one relevant direction, so the result characterizes continuous-direction feature recovery and does not touch discrete conditional-distribution (transition-matrix) estimation, where the relevant 'feature' is a full conditional table rather than a single direction."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"mechanistic theory of in-context learning in selective state-space models (Mamba), specialized to discrete Markov-chain sequence tasks","venue":"ICLR 2026","time":"2026","data":["synthetic discrete Markov chains with random transition matrices (varying order and state-space size)","character-level Markov text benchmarks","controlled in-context sequence-prediction probes"],"compute":"1×A100 × 3 months (≈ 90 A100-day)","expertise":"theory of sequence models + mechanistic interpretability + small-scale controlled training","preference":"both","baseline":"selective-SSM ICL viewed as Bayes-optimal filtering over Linear-Gaussian SSMs (arxiv:2602.17744v1) and as online-gradient-descent emulation (openalex:W4415334660); transformer Markov-chain in-context estimation (openalex:W6967343425)","limitation":"existing theory of Mamba ICL is derived for continuous-state tasks (Linear-Gaussian SSM filtering, linear regression, single-index targets); it does not characterize what algorithm the selective-SSM recurrence implements when the in-context task is a DISCRETE Markov chain whose latent object is a transition matrix rather than a continuous Kalman state","contribution_type":"theory","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"Shared object (shared_object thread): the single selective recurrence h_t = Ā_t h_{t-1} + B̄_t x_t and the in-context next-symbol law p_model(x_{t+1} | x_{1:t}) it induces on a discrete random-transition-matrix Markov chain over alphabet size K and order r. ANCHOR (reframe + diagnostic companion): we reframe the opaque attribution question as a measurement object. For each component c in {A = the input-dependent decay Ā_t, B = the input-conditioned write gate B̄_t, W = fixed state width n}, define the per-component estimator-attribution score E_c = D_KL( p_model || p_model^{c-frozen} ), where p_model^{c-frozen} is the next-symbol law of the SAME trained model with component c replaced by its context-independent (input-frozen) counterpart at inference (Ā_t→constant decay ā, B̄_t→constant write b̄, or n clamped by zeroing the top n−n0 state coordinates) and all other components left intact; E_c is computed by a second forward pass and is faithful-by-construction because it is read off the model's own forward computation, not a surrogate. The load-bearing named state variable is S_t = the running input-conditioned co-occurrence accumulation the B̄_t gate writes into h_t — concretely the sub-vector of h_t whose update B̄_t x_t increments the state coordinate indexed by the current symbol conditioned on the recent context window; we give a soundness argument that S_t is the in-state carrier of the conditional-count sufficient statistic by exhibiting that p_model^{B-frozen} (which destroys S_t's input-conditioning) loses the count-accumulation behavior while p_model^{A-frozen} and p_model^{W-frozen} (above a width floor) do not, and we CERTIFY this causally: ablating the producer of S_t flips the model's implemented estimator (D_est defined below jumps from the Laplace basin to a non-count baseline), which is the estimator-flipping causal intervention that converts a correlational attribution into a causal one. SIBLING (audit + diagnostic companion): the continuous-latent theory leaves (arxiv:2602.17744v1 LG-SSM filtering, openalex:W4415334660 OGD, openalex:W4415273485 single-index) and even the discrete optimum result (From Markov to Laplace) tacitly treat the recurrence as implementing ONE fixed estimator class; we audit that assumption by measuring the estimator-identity divergence D_est(ref) = min over a one-parameter shrinkage family of D_KL( p_model || p_ref ) for ref in {Laplace (add-1 conditional counts), Krichevsky–Trofimov / context-tree (add-1/2, depth-adaptive)} across a regime grid (context length L, train-order r_train vs test-order r_test, stationary vs non-stationary transitions). The pivot claim: there is a regime boundary across which arg min_ref D_est switches from Laplace to KT/CTW — i.e. the recurrence admits a DIFFERENT discrete estimator class, falsifying the fixed-class assumption — and the same per-component diagnostic shows S_t (the B̄_t co-occurrence accumulation) is the carrier in BOTH regimes, only its effective shrinkage/depth parameter changes, so the two legs read as one paper about one object. The legs share machinery (E_c, S_t, D_est all computed from the same forward passes) rather than being stapled modules. All quantities are model-internal readouts (E_c, S_t) or external-oracle reference estimators (Laplace, KT/CTW computed in closed form from context counts); the shrinkage-family minimization is a 1-D scalar search; the width floor n0 and context grid L are fixed selection rules stated in the diagnostic, not tuned per result. Numbers: From Markov to Laplace reports Laplace-optimality for all orders at the well-specified optimum; our distinct claim is a REGIME-CONDITIONAL estimator identity (we measure arg min over reference estimators across regimes, not a representability bound), so there is no exponent to align — the regime distinction is written visibly as the train/test order-mismatch and finite-L axes their well-specified-optimum result does not vary.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery because both are statements about the same forward-pass-induced next-symbol law and the same three recurrence components: the anchor asks which component carries the statistic (E_c, S_t) and the sibling asks whether the carried estimator's CLASS is fixed (D_est across regimes) — the diagnostic that freezes one component at a time is the single instrument both legs read, so the design is one object with two questions, not two modules. (b) Alternatives considered and rejected: (i) a standalone representability theorem on finite width — rejected because From Markov to Laplace already characterizes representation capacity, so it would re-derive prior art (the prior abandon); (ii) making the anchor a controlled_diagnostic_design directly (the anchor_alternate) — rejected because contribution_type=theory needs the faithfulness/soundness identification artifact that reframe_as_solvable_object owns, with the diagnostic kept as the companion that ships the empirical separation. We avoid the flagged ancestral nodes: S_t is an SSM-native state accumulation read off B̄_t, NOT the classical hand-built conditional-count/context-tree estimator c0 (we use Laplace and KT/CTW only as external REFERENCE oracles to name what the model matches, never re-derive them as the contribution) and NOT the attention-specific induction-head circuit c1 (no attention is involved).","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: train a single-layer Mamba on order-1 K=5 random-transition Markov chains, evaluate in-context next-symbol prediction across context length L in {8,32,128,512} and a train-order-1/test-order-2 mismatch split; measure the estimator-identity divergence D_est(ref) to {Laplace, KT/CTW} and the per-component attribution E_A,E_B,E_W. If the candidate is right: (b) in the well-specified long-L regime arg min_ref D_est = Laplace (low) reproducing prior work, but under order-mismatch / short L the KT/CTW divergence becomes the minimum — the estimator-identity arg min SWITCHES — and E_B is the largest component attribution throughout (B̄_t carries the statistic), while E_A and E_W (above the width floor) stay small. (c) Named load-bearing variable: S_t, the input-conditioned co-occurrence accumulation the B̄_t gate writes; negative control = freeze B̄_t's input-conditioning (replace by context-independent write). Anti-tautology: the control's predicted effect is the DOWNSTREAM task-outcome metric — the model's in-context next-symbol KL to the gold transition law degrades to the context-free marginal baseline AND D_est leaves both Laplace and KT basins — not merely 'S_t becomes constant'. Positive control: a model whose only input-dependent component is B̄_t recovers most of the gold-law KL and reproduces the Laplace→KT regime switch, converting the falsifier into a constructive identification that S_t is sufficient.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:0385b6a7e6cd1f3618f7102343fd38a1ef16cc97","delta":"From Markov to Laplace proves single-layer Mamba represents the Bayes/minimax-optimal Laplacian-smoothing estimator at its well-specified optimum and characterizes representation capacity (a fixed-estimator, optimum-only result); we measure the REGIME-CONDITIONAL estimator identity and show the same recurrence's implemented estimator switches class to Krichevsky–Trofimov / context-tree under order-mismatch / short context, and we NAME the carrying component (the B̄_t input-conditioned co-occurrence accumulation S_t) via an estimator-flipping causal ablation — neither the regime switch nor the component attribution is in their result."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.17744v1","delta":"They derive Bayes-optimal posterior-mean filtering for continuous LG-SSM tasks with a real-valued latent; we measure which selective-recurrence component carries the DISCRETE conditional-count statistic and whether the implemented discrete estimator's class is fixed across regimes — a discrete-estimator-identity question their continuous-latent account does not pose."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W6967343425","delta":"They show transformers cross a threshold to estimate the transition matrix and treat the estimator as a black box; we analyze the selective-SSM (not attention) recurrence and identify the named in-state variable S_t carrying the estimate, with a causal ablation that flips the estimator identity."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:0385b6a7e6cd1f3618f7102343fd38a1ef16cc97","what_step_was_missed":"From Markov to Laplace constructed the representation of the optimal Laplacian-smoothing estimator at the well-specified optimum but never (i) varied the regime to test whether the implemented estimator's CLASS is invariant — its theorem fixes Laplace for all orders only under well-specification, so it did not measure the order-mismatch / short-context regime where a different shrinkage (KT/CTW) estimator can become the model's effective behavior — nor (ii) performed the per-component causal attribution that names which input-dependent recurrence component (rather than convolution-in-aggregate) is the intervenable state-level carrier of the count statistic; both require a frozen-component diagnostic and an estimator-identity divergence measurement they did not construct."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":203,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"No hard floor fired: gap_closure_reject_check has no entry with candidate_match: yes (aggregate borderline), anti_pattern matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat is adjacent-setting with a non-null addressable_via (not exact-mechanism). Within the safe zone, recipe_application_check.entries[1] (the sibling, C05) is borderline on a load-bearing leg — core_mechanism enacts the audit/pivot backbone but not C05's recovery-up-to-ambiguity terminal move — and gap_closure_reject_check flags the matching borderline lesson ('structural constraints … without proving sufficiency for recovery'); per the 'choose revise when a borderline hits a load-bearing structural property / when recipe_application_check is borderline on a leg' heuristic this is a revise, fixable in-scope by a tactical re-alignment of core_mechanism that makes the sibling's C05 audit-pivot spine explicit (the companion controlled_diagnostic_design legitimately carries the deliverable) plus a tightening of the threat-dodge framing — no sub_pattern swap, since C05's same-parent siblings are off-domain and a cross-parent move is out of Phase 3.3 scope.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved paper provides a controlled diagnostic that isolates WHICH component of the selective recurrence (the input-dependent Ā_t decay vs. the input-dependent B̄_t write gate vs. fixed state width) is the binding constraint that lets or prevents the Markov-chain conditional statistic from being accumulated, so the observed empirical success/failure of Mamba on structured-sequence ICL (openalex:W6967343425, semanticscholar:9da427202cc48370fd66359f5d72ff5ff3bc8b57) cannot be attributed to a named, intervenable state-level quantity.","main_pattern":"reframe_as_solvable_object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The signature failure is treating the reframing as a mechanical wrapper — pointing an established attribution/estimation tool at a new architecture without re-deriving why the scores are faithful, with no causal validation (only correlation) and no confound control, so a methodological artifact explains the result instead. A second variant under-specifies the object; a third surveys/recombines tools without a unifying axis or decisive experiment.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Pointing an off-the-shelf decomposition at a coarser input granularity without showing the coarser units preserve the signal reads as a wrapper, not a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"E_c is read off the model's own forward pass at the native component level (Ā_t / B̄_t / width), not a coarser surrogate granularity."},{"lesson_quoted":"Porting a known attribution technique to a new architecture or domain while ignoring that technique's documented failure modes — and omitting comparisons to alternatives — leaves reviewers unable to see any unique benefit.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The frozen-component diagnostic compares all three components (E_A/E_B/E_W) and adds a positive control, so the differential benefit is identifiable rather than a single-technique port."},{"lesson_quoted":"Proposing a new attribution definition without an axiomatic or causal argument for why it should count as ground-truth collapses the moment a reviewer asks why this is the real importance.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism certifies E_c / S_t with an estimator-flipping causal ablation (perturbing S_t's producer flips the model's implemented estimator), supplying the causal ground the lesson demands."},{"lesson_quoted":"Conflating a methodological artifact — a computation-granularity difference, a degenerate zero baseline — with genuine signal undermines the entire premise once the confound is identified.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The width-floor n0 and the frozen-but-otherwise-intact counterfactual control for the degenerate-baseline confound; the anti-tautology guard ties the effect to a downstream task metric, not E_c's own value."},{"lesson_quoted":"Building a suppression or privacy method without formalizing the threat model leaves the central guarantee unverifiable regardless of strong empirical numbers.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Not a security/privacy method; no threat model is invoked."},{"lesson_quoted":"Surveying or recombining fragmented methods without a unifying axis or a decisive controlled experiment yields a contribution reviewers dismiss as anecdotal.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The unifying axis is the single shared object (the recurrence + its next-symbol law) and the decisive experiment is the regime-conditional estimator-identity switch."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved paper tests whether the continuous-latent assumption shared by every selective-SSM ICL theory leaf — that the in-context task's latent is a real-valued state evolved by a linear belief update — is necessary for the optimality account, rather than an artifact of choosing only continuous (LG-SSM / linear-regression / single-index) task families; the question of whether the same recurrence admits a fundamentally different in-context estimator class when the latent is a discrete distribution is left unasked.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The signature failure is an identifiability claim that outruns its proof — the pivoted assumption was not load-bearing (a straightforward union of two frameworks), or recovery/consistency is asserted while the decisive object (latent identifiability, an ambiguity class) is never established, leaving the result indistinguishable from a post-hoc heuristic.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Stacking two established frameworks and re-proving identifiability of the union reads as incremental unless the pivoted assumption was genuinely load-bearing and the union admits a regime neither framework could reach alone.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The sibling does not re-prove identifiability of a framework-union; it overturns the single load-bearing 'fixed estimator class' assumption and exhibits a concrete regime (order-mismatch / short context) the prior well-specified-optimum result does not reach."},{"lesson_quoted":"Advertising an identifiability or 'consistency' property while the proof omits the decisive object — never proving latent identifiability, or excluding part of the model from the guarantee — collapses the contribution the moment a reviewer checks the theorem.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The sibling deliberately does NOT advertise a recovery-up-to-ambiguity theorem (the companion controlled_diagnostic_design carries the validating deliverable), so there is no omitted identifiability object to collapse."},{"lesson_quoted":"Imposing structural constraints to claim interpretability or disentanglement without proving those constraints are sufficient for recovery leaves the result indistinguishable from a post-hoc heuristic.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The estimator-class-switch claim is validated empirically by D_est rather than by a sufficiency proof, so a reviewer expecting C05's recovery-grade theorem could read the audit leg as empirical rather than as the cluster's signature identifiability proof — the deliverable lives in the companion diagnostic, not in a C05-style recovery theorem."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The anchor leg (reframe_as_solvable_object / C00) is clear — its estimator-flipping causal certificate and decisive regime-switch experiment defuse every C00 Reject lesson. The sibling leg (assumption_audit_and_pivot / C05) is borderline on the lesson 'Imposing structural constraints to claim interpretability … without proving those constraints are sufficient for recovery,' because the sibling's deliverable is an empirical D_est separation carried by the companion diagnostic rather than the recovery-grade identifiability theorem C05's card centers on; no entry is triggered (no candidate_match: yes), so the aggregate is borderline, not triggered."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved paper provides a controlled diagnostic that isolates WHICH component of the selective recurrence (the input-dependent Ā_t decay vs. the input-dependent B̄_t write gate vs. fixed state width) is the binding constraint that lets or prevents the Markov-chain conditional statistic from being accumulated, so the observed empirical success/failure of Mamba on structured-sequence ICL (openalex:W6967343425, semanticscholar:9da427202cc48370fd66359f5d72ff5ff3bc8b57) cannot be attributed to a named, intervenable state-level quantity.","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Recast an opaque transparency question (which internal component is responsible) as a concrete measurement over a well-studied object whose faithfulness constraint reflects the model's actual computation, with fidelity certified by a causal intervention that flips model behavior when the identified object is perturbed, rather than by plausibility.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism defines the per-component measurement object E_c = KL(p_model || p_model^{c-frozen}) read off the model's own forward pass (the faithfulness constraint), and certifies S_t via the estimator-flipping causal ablation — 'ablating the producer of S_t flips the model's implemented estimator' — which is exactly C00's causal-intervention-flips-behavior certificate; the move is performed, not merely named.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved paper tests whether the continuous-latent assumption shared by every selective-SSM ICL theory leaf — that the in-context task's latent is a real-valued state evolved by a linear belief update — is necessary for the optimality account, rather than an artifact of choosing only continuous (LG-SSM / linear-regression / single-index) task families; the question of whether the same recurrence admits a fundamentally different in-context estimator class when the latent is a discrete distribution is left unasked.","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Take an existing identifiability/recovery theorem, pivot the assumption it requires for unique recoverability (typically swapping a distributional assumption for a structural/geometric one), and re-prove recovery of the hidden structure up to the field's standard ambiguity class.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism performs the audit-and-pivot spine (names the 'fixed estimator class' assumption, violates it with the regime-shifted discrete task, exhibits a new regime the prior excluded) but does NOT perform C05's distinctive terminal move — it re-proves no recovery-up-to-ambiguity theorem; the validating deliverable is the empirical D_est separation supplied by the companion controlled_diagnostic_design. The audit/pivot-with-concrete-new-regime backbone is present; the recovery-theorem signature is not.","verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The anchor (C00) is applied — the estimator-flipping causal certificate is literally enacted in core_mechanism. The sibling (C05) is borderline: core_mechanism enacts the assumption-audit/pivot-to-new-regime backbone but not C05's recovery-up-to-ambiguity terminal move, because the leg's deliverable is intentionally carried by the companion diagnostic; this is a sub_pattern fit issue, not an absent contribution."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["reframe_as_solvable_object","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as a component; it is absent from the composition_set, so no anti-pattern matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:0385b6a7e6cd1f3618f7102343fd38a1ef16cc97","threat_source":"lit_table","subsumption_argument":"From Markov to Laplace proves a single-layer Mamba implements the Bayes-and-minimax-optimal Laplacian-smoothing estimator for all Markovian orders and characterizes the representation capacity (with convolution enabling the representation). This subsumes the prior abandoned anchor (a finite-width representability wall) and would subsume any leg that re-derives 'Mamba learns Laplace' or re-characterizes its representation capacity. The current candidate, however, does NOT make either claim: its load-bearing artifacts are (i) a per-component CAUSAL attribution naming which input-dependent recurrence component (B̄_t's S_t) carries the statistic — the paper proves convolution enables the representation but never isolates the binding component by intervention — and (ii) a REGIME-CONDITIONAL estimator-identity measurement showing the implemented estimator switches class (Laplace → KT/CTW) under order-mismatch / short context, a regime the paper's well-specified-optimum theorem does not vary over. So the paper bounds what the candidate may NOT claim but does not stand on the candidate's actual load-bearing claims; the overlap is adjacent-setting, not exact-mechanism. Notably this paper did NOT surface in the re-routed Phase 3.1 collision_hits (203 hits) under the new signature_terms, and no Mamba/SSM in-context paper appears anywhere in the collision set, corroborating that the re-routed anchor occupies a non-colliding neighborhood.","addressable_via":"Already dodged in the current candidate by scoping the claim to component-attribution + regime-conditional estimator identity; the standing requirement (foldable into Phase 4 reviewer_concerns_and_responses) is that differentiation_from_lit and core_mechanism keep the well-specified-optimum Laplace representability result attributed to this paper and never restate it as the candidate's own — a framing constraint, not an exact-mechanism collision."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism (sibling leg) + gap_closure[1].how_closed","issue":"recipe_application_check.entries[1].verdict = borderline — core_mechanism performs the audit/pivot-to-new-regime backbone but does not visibly enact C05's signature move (pin the single load-bearing assumption so the prior proof demonstrably collapses without it, exhibit a concrete regime the relaxed condition admits and the prior excluded, then operationalize the pivoted claim as an estimator/algorithm validated where the original assumption fails). A sub_pattern swap is NOT used here: C05's only same-parent siblings under assumption_audit_and_pivot (C01 security-locus, C11 privacy-composition, C19 distribution-free generalization, C28 distributed-protocol, C29 convergence-rate) are each off-domain for this estimator-class audit, and moving to a diagnostic cluster (C02) would change the main_pattern, which is out of Phase 3.3 scope; so the fix is a tactical re-alignment of core_mechanism to make the in-scope C05 audit-pivot spine explicit, with the companion controlled_diagnostic_design carrying the empirical-separation deliverable (the legitimate PAIR resolution Phase 2.1 already declared).","fix_direction":"In the SIBLING portion of core_mechanism, make the C05 audit-pivot spine explicit: (1) state the single load-bearing assumption precisely — 'the selective recurrence implements ONE fixed, well-specification-derived estimator class' — and note the prior optimum-only result demonstrably says nothing once well-specification is dropped; (2) name the concrete regime the relaxed condition admits and the prior excluded (train/test order-mismatch, short context, non-stationary transitions); (3) operationalize the pivoted claim as the D_est estimator-identity measurement against the {Laplace, KT/CTW} reference oracles supplied by the companion controlled_diagnostic_design, validated precisely where well-specification fails. Re-emit gap_closure[1].how_closed to name both halves (the audit's overturned assumption + the companion's confound-isolating D_est separation). Hold falsification_prediction and compute_budget byte-identical."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit / core_mechanism (threat-dodge framing vs semanticscholar:0385b6a7e6cd1f3618f7102343fd38a1ef16cc97)","issue":"paper_pointed_threat addressable_via — the candidate must keep the well-specified-optimum Laplace representability result attributed to From Markov to Laplace and never restate it as its own, so the adjacent-setting threat stays dodged.","fix_direction":"Ensure the differentiation_from_lit entry for the threat paper explicitly concedes its well-specified-optimum Laplace representability + capacity result and states the candidate's delta as (i) component-level causal attribution and (ii) regime-conditional estimator-identity switch; add no new claim re-deriving Laplace representability. No change to falsification_prediction or compute_budget."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism (sibling leg) + gap_closure[1].how_closed","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Re-aligned the sibling portion of core_mechanism to make the C05 audit-pivot spine explicit — pin the single load-bearing 'one fixed estimator class' assumption (prior proof collapses once well-specification is dropped), name the concrete excluded regime (order-mismatch / short context / non-stationary), and operationalize the pivoted claim via the companion's D_est estimator-identity measurement validated where well-specification fails — and re-emitted gap_closure[1].how_closed to name both the overturned assumption and the companion's confound-isolating D_est separation."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit[0].delta","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Tightened the From Markov to Laplace delta to explicitly concede its well-specified-optimum Laplace representability + capacity result up front and state the candidate's delta strictly as (i) component-level causal attribution and (ii) regime-conditional estimator-identity switch, adding no claim that re-derives Laplace representability."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Which Gate Counts: Component-Level Identification of Mamba's In-Context Markov Estimator\n\n**Method.** Component-Level Estimator Identification (CLEI)\n\n## Motivation\nMamba is a fast sequence model (a selective state-space model, SSM) that can learn a pattern from its own input on the fly — this is called in-context learning (ICL). When the input is a Markov chain (a random sequence where the next symbol depends only on recent ones), a 2025 paper, From Markov to Laplace, proved something clean: even a one-layer Mamba ends up computing the textbook-optimal way to predict the next symbol, called Laplacian smoothing (essentially: count how often each symbol followed each context, add one to every count, and normalize). That result tells you WHAT the model computes when everything is ideal. It does not tell you two things a mechanic would want. First, WHICH part of the model does the counting: a Mamba step combines an input-dependent forgetting term $(\\bar{A}_{t})$ and an input-dependent write gate $(\\bar{B}_{t})$ into a running memory; nobody has shown which of these actually stores the counts. Second, whether the model always computes Laplacian smoothing, or switches to a different counting rule when conditions change — for example when the test chain has a different 'memory length' (order) than the training chains, or when the context is short. We answer both. We define a per-part score $E_{c}$ by freezing one part at a time (replacing it with a version that ignores the input) and measuring how much the model's predictions change; the part with the biggest change is the one doing the work. We predict that part is the write gate $\\bar{B}_{t},$ and we name the exact piece of memory it builds — the running count of which symbol followed which context — calling it $S_{t}.$ We then prove it causally: if we disable the input-sensitivity of that memory, the model's predictions collapse to ignoring the context entirely. Finally, we sweep conditions and show the model's effective rule switches from Laplacian smoothing to a related rule (Krichevsky–Trofimov / context-tree smoothing, which adds one-half instead of one and can adapt its memory depth) when the order is mismatched or the context is short. This turns a clean 'it's optimal' statement into a usable map: point to the part that counts, and predict from the situation which counting rule the model is using.\n\n## Method\n### Background (model + readout)\n*Train the small Mamba models and record their in-context next-symbol predictions.*\n\n1. Train a one-layer and a two-layer Mamba (a selective state-space model) to predict the next symbol on synthetic random Markov chains, sweeping memory length (order r in 1,2,3) and alphabet size (K in 3,5,8). For every training sequence, draw a brand-new transition table at random — for each possible recent-history context, sample its next-symbol probabilities uniformly over the simplex (a symmetric Dirichlet with parameter 1) — and roll out a length-256 sequence. Because the table is new every time, the model cannot memorize it and must infer it from the running context. Train by standard next-token prediction until held-out loss stops improving, and keep a separate batch of freshly drawn chains for all later measurements.\n\n*The selective recurrence shared by both legs: state $h_{t}$ is the input-dependent decay $\\bar{A}_{t}$ acting on the previous state plus the input-conditioned write $\\bar{B}_{t}$ of the current symbol $x_{t}.$*\n$$ h_t = \\bar{A}_t\\, h_{t-1} + \\bar{B}_t\\, x_t \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: You need real trained models at the same small scale the prior optimality result studied before you can ask which part does the counting.\n2. Run each trained model on fresh chains and record its predicted next-symbol probabilities at every position and context length L. Save these per-position predictions, because every later comparison (against textbook counting rules and against frozen-part versions of the model) is lined up position-by-position with exactly these numbers.\n   - _Why_: Every later measurement compares the model's own predictions against reference rules, so you record them first.\n\n### Estimator-identity map\n*Measure which textbook counting rule the model matches in each situation and locate the $Laplace\\to KT/context-tree$ switch.*\n\n3. From the same context, compute two textbook counting rules in closed form: Laplace (add 1 to every count) and Krichevsky–Trofimov / context-tree (add 1/2, with adaptive memory depth). Both rules start from the same tally — how many times each symbol followed each recent-history context so far in the sequence. Laplace adds one to every tally before normalizing; KT adds one half. The context-tree version makes the memory depth adaptive: it builds a tree of contexts up to the deepest swept order (3) and, at each node, blends that node's own count-estimate with the deeper ones using the standard context-tree-weighting recipe, so it leans on longer history only where the data support it. These rules never see the model — they are reference oracles.\n   - _Why_: These rules are computed independently of the model, so comparing to them is a fair, non-circular test of what the model is doing.\n4. For each situation (context length, matched vs mismatched order, stationary vs changing transitions), find which reference rule the model's predictions are closest to, and mark where the closest rule switches from Laplace to KT/context-tree. To compare fairly, give each reference rule one tunable knob — how many fake counts it adds before normalizing — and pick the knob setting that makes that rule fit the model best (search the knob over a small range where the fit quality is smooth and has a single best point), then read off the residual gap. The reference with the smaller gap is the one the model is behaving like in that situation. Sweep context length over 8 to 256, every pairing of trained order versus tested order, and stationary versus mid-sequence-changing transitions; the cell where the winner flips from Laplace to KT/context-tree is the key result.\n\n*The estimator-identity divergence: the closest fit (over a one-parameter shrinkage $\\lambda )$ between the model's next-symbol law and each reference estimator; arg min over ref names which estimator the model matches in a given regime.*\n$$ D_{\\mathrm{est}}(\\mathrm{ref}) = \\min_{\\lambda}\\, D_{\\mathrm{KL}}\\!\\big(p_{\\mathrm{model}} \\,\\|\\, p_{\\mathrm{ref}}^{\\lambda}\\big), \\quad \\mathrm{ref} \\in \\{\\text{Laplace}, \\text{KT/CTW}\\} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: If the closest rule changes with the situation, the model is not running one fixed rule — that is the audit's payoff.\n\n### Component attribution & causal carrier\n*Rank the recurrence parts by how much each carries the counting and causally identify the write-gate memory $S_{t}$ as the carrier.*\n\n5. Freeze one part at a time — make the forgetting term $\\bar{A}_{t} a$ constant, make the write gate $\\bar{B}_{t}$ input-independent, or shrink the memory width — and measure how much the predictions change $(E_{A}, E_{B}, E_{W}).$ Concretely: for the forgetting term, replace its per-step value with its average across the evaluation positions, so the state still decays but no longer adapts to the input; for the write gate, replace it with its average so every symbol is written the same way; for the width, zero out the higher-index memory coordinates, trying cutoffs that double each time (1,2,4,8,...) and reporting at the smallest width that still keeps essentially all of the full model's prediction quality, plus the whole curve. Each frozen version is one extra forward pass through the unchanged output, and the change is the gap (in predicted-distribution terms) between the original and the frozen version, measured in every situation.\n\n*The per-component attribution score: the KL divergence between the model's next-symbol law and the same model with component c replaced by its context-independent (input-frozen) counterpart, computed by one extra forward pass.*\n$$ E_c = D_{\\mathrm{KL}}\\!\\big(p_{\\mathrm{model}} \\,\\|\\, p_{\\mathrm{model}}^{c\\text{-frozen}}\\big), \\quad c \\in \\{A, B, W\\} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The part whose freezing changes predictions the most is the part carrying the counting; we expect that to be the write gate $\\bar{B}_{t}.$\n6. Name the exact memory the write gate builds — the running count of symbol-given-context, call it $S_{t}$ — then disable its input-sensitivity and check that predictions collapse to ignoring the context. To pin down which memory coordinates are $S_{t},$ regress each coordinate's per-step write increment onto an indicator of which (symbol, recent-context) pair just occurred, and keep the coordinates that together explain at least 90% of that co-occurrence signal. Then ablate by making the write gate input-independent (its averaged value) and re-check the situation-by-situation comparison from before: the carrier is confirmed if the model stops matching the add-1 (Laplace) rule and its prediction error against the true transition law rises all the way to the context-free baseline — a model that just predicts overall symbol frequencies and ignores the running context.\n   - _Why_: Flipping the model's behavior by perturbing one named quantity is the causal proof that this quantity, not something correlated with it, does the work.\n7. Train a stripped model whose only input-dependent part is the write gate and check it still counts; repeat the part-attribution under mismatched order to confirm the same memory $S_{t}$ carries both counting rules. Build the stripped model by making the forgetting term a single fixed (input-independent) decay learned during training and fixing the memory width at the smallest sufficient size from before, leaving only the write gate input-sensitive; train it from scratch with the same data and protocol as the first step. It passes if it recovers most of the full model's prediction quality against the true transition law and still shows the Laplace-to-KT switch across situations. Finally, redo the part-attribution and carrier identification in the mismatched-order situation and confirm the same memory coordinates $S_{t}$ carry the count there too, with only their effective amount of count-smoothing changing between the Laplace-matched and KT-matched cells.\n   - _Why_: Showing the write gate alone is enough turns a 'what breaks it' test into a 'this is sufficient' identification, and confirms one carrier across both regimes.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 哪个门在计数：Mamba 上下文马尔可夫估计器的组件级辨识\n\n**方法名称.** Component-Level Estimator Identification (CLEI)\n\n## 研究动机\nMamba 是一种快速的序列模型（选择性状态空间模型，SSM），它能在不更新权重的情况下，临时从自己的输入里学到规律——这叫上下文学习（in-context learning, ICL）。当输入是一条马尔可夫链（下一个符号只依赖最近若干符号的随机序列）时，2025 年的论文 From Markov to Laplace 证明了一件干净的事：即使是单层 Mamba，最终也会算出预测下一符号的教科书最优方法，称为 Laplacian smoothing（本质上是：数每个符号在每个上下文后出现了多少次，给每个计数加 1，再归一化）。这个结论告诉你在理想情形下模型算的是『什么』，却没回答两个偏机制的问题。第一，是模型的『哪个部分』在计数：Mamba 的一步把一个输入相关的遗忘项 $\\bar{A}_{t}$ 和一个输入相关的写入门 $\\bar{B}_{t}$ 组合进一段滚动记忆里，但没人指出究竟哪一个真正存下了计数。第二，模型是否总是在算 Laplacian smoothing，还是在条件变化时切换到别的计数规则——比如测试链的『记忆长度』（阶数 order）与训练链不一致，或者上下文很短时。我们两个都回答。我们通过每次只冻结一个部分（把它换成忽略输入的版本）并测量模型预测变化多少，来定义组件分数 $E_{c}$；变化最大的那个部分就是真正在干活的。我们预测那是写入门 $\\bar{B}_{t}$，并给它构建的那段记忆——即『哪个符号跟在哪个上下文之后』的滚动计数——起名 $S_{t}$。随后用因果方式证明它：一旦关掉这段记忆对输入的敏感性，模型的预测就退化为完全忽略上下文。最后我们扫描各种条件，显示当阶数不匹配或上下文很短时，模型的有效规则会从 Laplacian smoothing 切换到一个相关规则（Krichevsky–Trofimov / context-tree smoothing，它加二分之一而不是加 1，并能自适应记忆深度）。这就把一句干净的『它是最优的』，变成一张可用的地图：指出在计数的部分，并从情形预测模型当前用的是哪种计数规则。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景（模型与读出）\n*训练小型 Mamba 模型并记录其上下文下一符号预测。*\n\n1. 训练一个单层和一个双层 Mamba（一种选择性状态空间模型，selective state-space model）来在合成的随机马尔可夫链上预测下一符号，扫描记忆长度（阶数 r 取 1,2,3）与字母表大小（K 取 3,5,8）。每条训练序列都重新随机抽一张转移表——对每个可能的近期历史上下文，从单纯形上均匀采样它的下一符号概率（即参数为 1 的对称 Dirichlet 分布）——再滚动生成一条长度为 256 的序列。由于表每次都是新的，模型无法把它背进权重，只能从运行中的上下文里推断。用标准的下一符号预测训练直到留出集损失不再下降，并另留一批新抽的链供后续所有测量使用。\n\n*两条腿共享的选择性递推：状态 $h_{t}$ 由输入相关衰减 $\\bar{A}_{t}$ 作用于上一状态，加上当前符号 $x_{t}$ 经输入相关写入门 $\\bar{B}_{t}$ 的写入构成。*\n$$ h_t = \\bar{A}_t\\, h_{t-1} + \\bar{B}_t\\, x_t \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 要在与先前最优性结论相同的小规模上有真实训练好的模型，才能去问『哪个部分在计数』。\n2. 让每个训练好的模型在新链上运行，记录它在每个位置、每个上下文长度 L 下预测的下一符号概率。把这些逐位置的预测保存下来，因为后续所有比较（与教科书计数规则比较、与冻结某部分后的模型比较）都要逐位置地与这同一组数对齐。\n   - _为什么_: 后续每个测量都要拿模型自身的预测去和参考规则比，所以先把它记录下来。\n\n### 估计器身份地图\n*测量模型在每种情形下匹配哪种教科书计数规则，并定位 $Laplace\\to KT/context-tree$ 的切换。*\n\n3. 用同一段上下文以闭式算出两种教科书计数规则：Laplace（每个计数加 1）和 Krichevsky–Trofimov / context-tree（加 1/2，并自适应记忆深度）。两种规则都从同一张计数表出发——序列到目前为止每个符号在每个近期历史上下文之后出现了多少次。Laplace 在归一化前给每个计数加 1，KT 加 1/2。context-tree 版本让记忆深度自适应：它在直到最深扫描阶数（3）的范围内建一棵上下文树，并在每个节点用标准的 context-tree-weighting（上下文树加权）配方把本节点的计数估计与更深层的估计混合，从而只在数据支持时才依赖更长的历史。这些规则完全不看模型——它们是参考神谕（reference oracle）。\n   - _为什么_: 这些规则独立于模型计算，因此拿来对比是对模型行为的公平、不循环的检验。\n4. 对每种情形（上下文长度、阶数匹配与否、转移是否平稳），找出模型预测最接近哪种参考规则，并标出最接近的规则从 Laplace 切换到 KT/context-tree 的地方。为了公平比较，给每条参考规则一个可调旋钮——归一化前额外加多少个虚拟计数——并选取让该规则最贴合模型的旋钮值（在一个拟合质量平滑、只有单个最优点的小范围内搜索），再读出剩余差距。差距更小的那条参考规则，就是模型在该情形下表现得像的那条。上下文长度从 8 扫到 256，遍历训练阶数与测试阶数的每一种配对，以及平稳与序列中途改变转移两种情况；获胜者从 Laplace 翻转到 KT/context-tree 的那一格就是关键结果。\n\n*估计器身份散度：在单参数收缩 $\\lambda $ 上，对模型下一符号分布与各参考估计器的最优拟合；对 ref 取 arg min 即指出在给定 regime 下模型匹配的是哪种估计器。*\n$$ D_{\\mathrm{est}}(\\mathrm{ref}) = \\min_{\\lambda}\\, D_{\\mathrm{KL}}\\!\\big(p_{\\mathrm{model}} \\,\\|\\, p_{\\mathrm{ref}}^{\\lambda}\\big), \\quad \\mathrm{ref} \\in \\{\\text{Laplace}, \\text{KT/CTW}\\} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 如果最接近的规则随情形改变，模型就不是在跑一条固定规则——这正是这次审计的收获。\n\n### 组件归因与因果承载者\n*按各部分承载计数的程度排序递推组件，并因果地辨识写入门记忆 $S_{t}$ 为承载者。*\n\n5. 每次冻结一个部分——把遗忘项 $\\bar{A}_{t}$ 设为常数、把写入门 $\\bar{B}_{t}$ 设为与输入无关、或缩小记忆宽度——并测量预测变化多少（$E_{A}$、$E_{B}$、$E_{W}$）。具体地：对遗忘项，用它在评测位置上的平均值替换其逐步取值，使状态仍会衰减但不再随输入自适应；对写入门，用其平均值替换，使每个符号都以同样方式写入；对宽度，把高序号的记忆坐标清零，尝试每次翻倍的截断点（$1,2,4,8,\\dots $），并在仍能保住几乎全部全模型预测质量的最小宽度处汇报（同时给出整条曲线）。每个冻结版本只是经过未改动输出头的一次额外前向传播，变化量就是原模型与冻结版本之间预测分布的差距，在每种情形下都测一遍。\n\n*组件级归因分数：模型下一符号分布与把组件 c 替换为其与上下文无关（输入冻结）版本后的分布之间的 KL 散度，仅需一次额外前向计算。*\n$$ E_c = D_{\\mathrm{KL}}\\!\\big(p_{\\mathrm{model}} \\,\\|\\, p_{\\mathrm{model}}^{c\\text{-frozen}}\\big), \\quad c \\in \\{A, B, W\\} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 冻结后使预测变化最大的部分，就是承载计数的部分；我们预期是写入门 $\\bar{B}_{t}$。\n6. 给写入门构建的那段记忆起名——即『符号在给定上下文后』的滚动计数 $S_{t}——$然后关掉它对输入的敏感性，检查预测是否退化为忽略上下文。要确定哪些记忆坐标属于 $S_{t}$，就把每个坐标的逐步写入增量回归到『刚出现的（符号, 近期上下文）配对』的指示变量上（岭回归，每个状态坐标一个回归量），保留那些合起来能解释该共现信号至少 90% 的坐标。随后通过把写入门设为与输入无关（取其平均值）来消融，并重做之前那套逐情形比较：若模型不再匹配加 1（Laplace）规则、且其相对真实转移律的预测误差一路升到无上下文基线（一个只预测整体符号频率、忽略运行上下文的模型），则承载者得到确认。\n   - _为什么_: 通过扰动一个被点名的量就能翻转模型行为，这是该量（而非与它相关的别的东西）在干活的因果证明。\n7. 训练一个仅写入门是输入相关的精简模型，检查它是否仍能计数；并在阶数不匹配的情形下重复组件归因，确认同一段记忆 $S_{t}$ 承载两种计数规则。精简模型的构建方式是：把遗忘项做成训练中习得的单一固定（与输入无关）衰减，并把记忆宽度固定为之前找到的最小够用尺寸，只保留写入门对输入敏感；用与第一步相同的数据和流程从头训练。若它能恢复全模型相对真实转移律的大部分预测质量、并在各情形下仍呈现 Laplace 到 KT 的切换，即算通过。最后，在阶数不匹配的情形下重做组件归因与承载者辨识，确认同一组记忆坐标 $S_{t}$ 在那里同样承载计数，且只有它们的有效计数平滑量在 Laplace 匹配格与 KT 匹配格之间变化。\n   - _为什么_: 证明仅靠写入门就够，把『什么会破坏它』的检验升级为『它就足够』的辨识，并确认在两种 regime 下是同一个承载者。\n\n"},{"id":"47","run_dir":"run_prompt47_rnnhippo","index":47,"title":"The Movement Source, Not Its Statistics: Closed-Loop Self-Motion Reshapes the Hippocampal RNN Code","title_zh":"运动的来源而非其统计量：闭环自运动重塑海马 RNN 的空间编码","method_name":"Closed-Loop Confidence-Gated Self-Motion (CL-CGSM)","hook":"Every RNN model of hippocampal coding draws self-motion from an exogenous trajectory oracle, tacitly assuming the movement source is irrelevant once its statistics are fixed — only the velocity distribution the network integrates is thought to matter. We predict the opposite: an RNN whose self-motion is generated endogenously, by gating its own exploration on its current decoding confidence, converges to a measurably different and more rodent-faithful spatial code than a matched RNN trained on an open-loop replay of the byte-identical realized trajectory, so the closed-loop SOURCE carries code-shaping signal that no statistics-matched exogenous stream can reproduce.","anchor_pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","anchor_pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","domain_category":"Healthcare & Scientific ML","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved model questions the shared assumption — inherited by the When-and-Where network (arxiv:2604.00036v1), the HC-MEC loop (openalex:W6979295729), and the co-emergence model (arxiv:2605.21356v1) — that the trajectory generator supplying self-motion is a fixed exogenous oracle; none asks whether the movement distribution must be exogenous and stationary at all, rather than something that co-develops with and is shaped by the maturing code.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","how_closed":"Framing half (C01): relocate the load-bearing trajectory SOURCE from the exogenous-oracle locus — where every closest_adjacent model anchors it and treats movement as an external given whose only content is its velocity statistics — to an endogenous closed-loop locus where the agent's own per-step decoding confidence gates its self-motion sampling, dissolving the exogenous-source assumption and arguing structurally that code-shaping signal lives in the source coupling, not just in the velocity histogram. Companion deliverable (controlled_diagnostic_design, C02): ship the confound-isolating separation that compares the closed-loop run against an open-loop replay of that run's OWN byte-identical realized trajectory — so velocity statistics, total path length, and sensory coverage are matched by construction and the closed-loop coupling is the single varied axis — and report the resulting code divergence ΔF_loop as the headline, with the open-loop replay as the oracle independent of the closed-loop network under test.","is_anchor":true}],"phase0":{"topic":"computational neuroscience / recurrent neural network models of hippocampal spatial coding","n_papers":50,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":26},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":15,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Recurrent Connectivity Shapes Spatial Coding in Hippocampal CA3 Subregions"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Suspicious activities detection using spatial–temporal features based on vision transformer and recurrent neural network"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"SST-CRAM: spatial-spectral-temporal based convolutional recurrent neural network with lightweight attention mechanism for EEG emotion recognition"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Spatial modulation and recurrent neural network based equalizer for MIMO communication systems"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Stochastic-Binary Hybrid Spatial Coding Multiplier for Convolutional Neural Network Accelerator"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Recurrent Inhibitory Dynamics in the Entorhinal Cortex Support Pattern Separation"}],"more":9},{"year":2025,"n":24,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Predictive remapping and allocentric coding as consequences of energy efficiency in recurrent neural network models of active vision"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Environmental risk assessment based on multiscale spatial recurrent neural network algorithm for IoT agriculture area"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Modeling autonomous shifts between focus state and mind-wandering using a predictive-coding-inspired variational recurrent neural network"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Convolutional-recurrent neural network for the prediction of formation and switching dynamics for multicolor solitons"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Classification of Traffic Pattern and Estimation of Traffic Speed Using Recurrent Neural Network in Smart Cities"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Semi-Airborne Electromagnetic Line Signal Denoising Based on Recurrent Self-Coding Neural Network"}],"more":18},{"year":2026,"n":11,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Midterm Status Report of the ILC Technology Network Activities"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Neural Networks and Schramm-Loewner Evolutions"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Combining Convolution and Delay Learning in Recurrent Spiking Neural Networks"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Irreversible behavior drives neural flows in the hippocampus"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"When and Where: A Model Hippocampal Network Unifies Formation of Time Cells and Place Cells"}],"more":5}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":12,"share":0.24},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":9,"share":0.18},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":8,"share":0.16},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":5,"share":0.1},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":4,"share":0.08},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":3,"share":0.06},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":2,"share":0.04},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":2,"share":0.04}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"RNN models of hippocampal spatial coding are trained on a single, stationary distribution of self-motion: the When-and-Where CA3 model (arxiv:2604.00036v1) hand-selects a fixed trajectory generator and two manually-set dynamical regimes to produce place and time cells, and the REMI HC-MEC loop (openalex:W6979295729) path-integrates pre-generated 5s traversals with fixed velocity statistics, so in both the input movement distribution is frozen and the network is read out only at its trained endpoint. Because the locomotor statistics that drive the recurrent dynamics never change across training, these models structurally cannot express how the ordered developmental change in an animal's movement (early slow, tortuous, short-range exploration giving way to fast, ballistic, directed locomotion) feeds back through path integration to set properties of the spatial code such as field size, grid scale, and the spatial-vs-temporal balance of CA3 — the very developmental dependency the user asks about. As a result the field has many trained-endpoint snapshots of the adult code (openalex:W4408275905, arxiv:2605.21356v1) but no model in which a non-stationary movement schedule is itself the independent variable that the emergent code is read out against.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2604.00036v1","is_anchor":"true","summary_and_residue":"Shows a single recurrent CA3 network produces both place cells and time cells, with a convex blend parameter that controls how strongly the sensory stream is structured by space vs time and two dynamical regimes that yield the two cell types. The blend and regime are set by hand at a fixed value rather than emerging from a movement schedule, and the model is trained and read out at one stationary input distribution, so it cannot show how a developmental change in locomotor statistics moves the network between the spatial and temporal regimes or reshapes field structure over an ontogenetic trajectory."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W6979295729","is_anchor":"false","summary_and_residue":"Builds an HC-MEC loop RNN in which grid cells emerge from integrating velocity sequences and place cells auto-associate sensory plus grid inputs for planning, trained on pre-generated fixed-velocity 5s traversals. The velocity statistics are stationary across training and the developmental ordering of movement is absent, so it cannot reveal how changing self-motion statistics during maturation set grid scale or place-field size."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2605.21356v1","is_anchor":"false","summary_and_residue":"Models the chicken-and-egg co-emergence of grid and place fields in one network. The co-emergence is driven by stationary input statistics with no locomotor-developmental schedule, so it answers which code appears first under fixed movement but not how the ontogenetic change in movement orders or shapes their emergence."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4406406162","is_anchor":"false","summary_and_residue":"An RL agent in a 3D virtual environment spontaneously develops place-like tuning and global remapping across contexts. Locomotor statistics are an uncontrolled byproduct of the policy rather than a manipulated developmental variable, so the model cannot isolate the effect of a movement-statistics schedule on the spatial code."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"computational neuroscience / recurrent neural network models of hippocampal spatial coding","venue":"ICLR / NeurIPS (machine-learning-for-neuroscience track)","time":"2026","data":["simulated agent trajectories with controllable locomotor statistics (speed, tortuosity, head-direction persistence, dwell-time distribution)","publicly available rodent place/grid-cell recordings across postnatal development (e.g. open neurophysiology datasets) for validation"],"compute":"1×A100 × 3 months (≈ 90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML modeling of neural systems; RNN training and analysis (fixed-point / dynamical-systems analysis)","preference":"both","baseline":"RNNs trained for path integration with stationary trajectory statistics (e.g. When-and-Where CA3 RNN arxiv:2604.00036v1; REMI HC-MEC RNN openalex:W6979295729)","limitation":"current RNN models of hippocampal spatial coding train on a fixed, stationary distribution of movement and so cannot reveal how the developmental change in locomotor statistics shapes the emerging spatial code","contribution_type":"empirical_reveal","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The AUDIT LENS (C01) is: where does the load-bearing, code-shaping signal of self-motion actually live? The whole closest_adjacent set anchors it at one representational locus — an exogenous trajectory oracle that emits a velocity stream the RNN integrates — and tacitly assumes that once the velocity statistics are fixed, the source that produced them is irrelevant. The candidate names that assumption and relocates the source to an endogenous closed-loop locus, then ships a C02 confound-isolating separation that demonstrates the relocated locus carries signal the old locus discards. Concretely, the base model is a fixed vanilla RNN (H = 512 tanh units) trained to path-integrate a velocity input into a 2D position readout — architecturally identical to the When-and-Where / REMI lineage — so the ONLY thing that varies across the two compared conditions is where the velocity stream comes from. Closed-loop condition: at each step t the agent draws its next velocity from a correlated-random-walk sampler whose speed is set to v(t) = v_min + (v_max − v_min)·u(t), where u(t) ∈ [0,1] is the agent's current decoding confidence, computed as u(t) = 1 − H_norm(t) and H_norm(t) is the Shannon entropy of a softmax position posterior (read from an auxiliary linear position decoder trained online on the hidden state h(t), entropy normalized by log of the K-bin spatial grid so H_norm ∈ [0,1]); v_min, v_max (cm/s) are fixed hyperparameters and the heading-persistence ρ and tortuosity κ of the correlated-random-walk sampler are likewise scaled by u(t) (low confidence → slow, tortuous, short-range exploration; high confidence → fast, directed) so movement and code co-develop in one loop. Every realized step (v(t), heading, position) is logged. Open-loop control condition (the C02 oracle): a fresh RNN instance, identical seed family, is trained on the EXACT logged velocity sequence from the closed-loop run played back as an exogenous oracle — so the marginal velocity histogram, the full temporal autocorrelation, the cumulative integrated path length ∫|v|dτ, and the spatial coverage are byte-identical to the closed-loop run; the SINGLE difference is that in the open-loop replay the stream is fixed in advance rather than gated by the network's own evolving confidence. The READOUT spatial-code properties, computed identically for both conditions on a fixed held-out uniform-coverage probe trajectory, are: place-field size F (cm², median area where a hidden-unit rate map exceeds 50% of its peak, over all H units), grid scale G (cm, first autocorrelogram peak radius over units with gridness > 0.3), and a rodent-faithfulness score D (the distance between the model's (F,G) developmental trajectory and the published postnatal-rodent place-field-maturation curve, scoped to qualitative direction). The C02 headline is the divergence ΔF_loop = F_closed − F_open (and ΔG_loop, ΔD_loop): the exogenous-oracle assumption predicts ΔF_loop = ΔG_loop = 0 (statistics-matched replay must reproduce the code), so a measured non-zero ΔF_loop with the closed-loop code closer to the rodent curve (ΔD_loop < 0) demonstrates the source locus carries code-shaping signal the velocity statistics do not encode — closing the gap. This is genuinely distinct from training on an ordered exogenous developmental schedule (the now-public prior result): both conditions here are matched on ALL movement statistics including their time-ordering, and the only thing varied is whether the stream is endogenously gated by the network's own confidence or externally replayed, so the contribution is the closed-loop coupling per se, not that developmental movement statistics shape the code. Cross-checking the lineage: the When-and-Where model (arxiv:2604.00036v1) reports place/time cells at a hand-set space/time blend on an exogenous oracle stream; our F and G are read on the same trained-RNN substrate, but we make the trajectory source the manipulated locus rather than its statistics, a contrast their fixed-oracle construction cannot express.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) This is a single-leg paper: Phase 2.1 deferred Gaps 1 and 2 because the ordered-exogenous-developmental-schedule reveal and the order-isolation diagnostic are now subsumed/pre-empted by public prior art (Abrate/Wills/Barry, bioRxiv 2025-12-30), so the only non-subsumed object is the closed-loop SOURCE relocation, which carries the whole paper through one C01 framing + one C02 companion deliverable rather than multiple legs. (b) Alternatives rejected: (i) framing the closed loop as an ordered non-stationary developmental schedule that drives sequential emergence — rejected because that IS the public prior result and would re-collide; the design therefore holds ALL movement statistics (including ordering) byte-identical between conditions via replay, leaving endogenous-vs-exogenous source as the only axis. (ii) Making the confidence signal drive a Hebbian/local-plasticity receptive-field rule — rejected because it lands on the collateral node c0 (local-plasticity refinement), a regression off the trained-RNN/path-integration lineage. (iii) Framing the closed loop as a generic easy-to-hard curriculum — rejected because it lands on collateral node c1 (plain curriculum learning); the open-loop replay control specifically strips any generic-curriculum or statistics explanation, since the replay reproduces the exact realized curriculum yet is predicted to fail to reproduce the code. The avoided nodes (c0, c1, and the public exogenous-schedule mechanism) are recorded so the load-bearing artifact — the endogenous confidence-gated SOURCE coupling, identified by replay failure — draws on a locus the lineage tree does not yet occupy.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: train two 512-unit path-integration RNNs over 5 seeds each — one CLOSED-LOOP (self-motion speed/tortuosity gated by the network's own per-step decoding confidence u(t)) and one OPEN-LOOP trained on a verbatim replay of the closed-loop run's logged velocity stream (byte-identical velocity histogram, temporal autocorrelation, path length, and coverage) — then rate-map the frozen networks on a fixed probe to measure median place-field size F and grid scale G. If the candidate is correct, F and G diverge between the two conditions in a consistent direction (ΔF_loop ≠ 0) with the closed-loop code lying closer to the published postnatal-rodent place-field-maturation curve, whereas the exogenous-oracle assumption predicts ΔF_loop ≈ ΔG_loop ≈ 0 because statistics-matched replay should reproduce the code. The named load-bearing variable is the per-step decoder-confidence signal u(t) that gates movement: as the mechanism distinguisher, randomize u(t) by drawing it i.i.d. from its own marginal histogram (preserving its distribution but destroying its temporal coupling to the developing code), and the prediction is that the closed-loop code divergence ΔF_loop collapses back toward the open-loop value AND the downstream held-out position-decoding error returns to the open-loop baseline — confirming it is the code-coupled SOURCE of movement, not the movement histogram, that sets the code. A positive control trains a stripped model whose only departure from the open-loop baseline is the confidence-gated sampler, and should recover most of ΔF_loop.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2604.00036v1","delta":"They drive a CA3 RNN with an exogenous trajectory oracle and read place/time cells at a hand-set space/time blend; we relocate the trajectory SOURCE to an endogenous confidence-gated closed loop and measure a code divergence ΔF_loop against a statistics-matched open-loop replay, an endogenous-vs-exogenous-source contrast their fixed-oracle construction cannot express."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W6979295729","delta":"They path-integrate pre-generated fixed-velocity 5s traversals supplied exogenously; we make the velocity stream endogenously generated by the network's own decoding confidence and isolate the closed-loop coupling by replaying the identical realized stream open-loop, which they never construct."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2605.21356v1","delta":"They show which of grid/place co-emerges first under exogenous stationary input statistics; we hold all movement statistics byte-identical across conditions and vary only whether the movement source is endogenously confidence-gated or exogenously replayed, isolating source-coupling rather than emergence order."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4406406162","delta":"Their RL agent's movement is an uncontrolled byproduct of a reward-driven policy; our movement is gated by an explicit, logged decoding-confidence signal and contrasted against its own statistics-matched open-loop replay, so the closed-loop coupling is isolated as the manipulated variable rather than entangled with reward and policy."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4406406162","what_step_was_missed":"The RL-agent model already has a closed loop in which the agent's internal state influences its movement, so it structurally contains an endogenous movement source. The substantive step it missed is constructing the statistics-matched open-loop replay control — training a second network on a verbatim playback of the closed-loop run's own realized velocity stream — which is the measurement primitive that isolates the closed-loop SOURCE coupling from the velocity statistics it produces; without that replay control the model's movement and code are entangled with reward and policy and cannot show that the coupling itself, rather than the resulting statistics, shapes the code."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":318,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"All four checks are clean: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict = clear (the C01 novelty-boundary-collapse lesson does not match because the endogenous confidence-gated closed-loop source is a locus no retrieved paper uses, and the difference is explicitly measured by the open-loop replay), recipe_application_check.verdict = applied (core_mechanism performs C01's relocate-and-explain move and ships the C02 separation), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id = null, and paper_pointed_threat is NOT exact-mechanism overlap for this anchor — Abrate varies which exogenous statistics are presented whereas the candidate matches all statistics and varies only the endogenous-vs-exogenous source, a contrast Abrate never constructs. No hard floor fires and no load-bearing borderline remains, so the verdict is advance.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved model questions the shared assumption — inherited by the When-and-Where network (arxiv:2604.00036v1), the HC-MEC loop (openalex:W6979295729), and the co-emergence model (arxiv:2605.21356v1) — that the trajectory generator supplying self-motion is a fixed exogenous oracle; none asks whether the movement distribution must be exogenous and stationary at all, rather than something that co-develops with and is shaped by the maturing code.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is a relocation demonstrated but not adversarially closed (or a novelty-boundary collapse where the 'new' locus turns out to be one a prior paper already used and the work fails to quantify what is genuinely different); a third is reintroducing the very assumption the relocation was meant to dissolve, and a fourth is offering only a demonstration with no mechanistic account of why the locus carries the signal.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work — normalization statistics, activation-similarity losses, semantic concept triggers — collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The relocated locus — an endogenous closed-loop where the agent's own per-step decoding confidence u(t) gates its self-motion sampling — is NOT used by any retrieved paper: the Abrate collision and the closest_adjacent set all supply self-motion from an exogenous oracle, and arxiv:2512.20044v1 embeds an exogenous path-integration motion PRIOR (not a confidence-gated endogenous source), so the difference is genuinely distinct and is explicitly measured by the ΔF_loop replay separation."},{"lesson_quoted":"A defense whose relocation silently depends on a clean reference model or a known anomaly distribution reintroduces precisely the strong assumption the move was supposed to eliminate.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The relocation does not reintroduce the exogenous-oracle assumption it dissolves: the closed-loop condition generates self-motion endogenously from the network's own state, and the open-loop replay control is derived from the closed-loop run's own logged stream rather than from any external clean reference."},{"lesson_quoted":"Demonstrating the new locus only on fixed, non-adaptive or outdated baselines while omitting any account of why it works reads as a stacked pipeline of existing components rather than a principled shift.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism supplies a mechanistic account (the confidence-gated source co-develops with the code so the realized stream carries code-coupled structure a statistics-matched replay cannot reproduce) and the negative control on u(t) traces the effect to that coupling rather than asserting it."}],"verdict":"clear"}],"verdict":"clear","reasoning":"The single anchor leg (assumption_audit_and_pivot / C01, companion controlled_diagnostic_design) is clear: its load-bearing Reject lesson — novelty-boundary collapse by relocating to an already-used locus — does not match, because the endogenous confidence-gated closed-loop source is used by no retrieved paper (the Abrate collision and arxiv:2512.20044v1 both keep self-motion exogenous) and the difference is explicitly measured via the statistics-matched open-loop replay. The companion C02's confirmatory-benchmark lesson is also avoided by construction (see paper_pointed_threat / recipe_application_check): the replay reveals a gap NOT knowable in advance rather than re-confirming a documented effect."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved model questions the shared assumption — inherited by the When-and-Where network (arxiv:2604.00036v1), the HC-MEC loop (openalex:W6979295729), and the co-emergence model (arxiv:2605.21356v1) — that the trajectory generator supplying self-motion is a fixed exogenous oracle; none asks whether the movement distribution must be exogenous and stationary at all, rather than something that co-develops with and is shaped by the maturing code.","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"The tactical move is to relocate the load-bearing signal to a different representational locus the field treated as irrelevant or invariant, demonstrate the property manifests there (ideally more robustly), and supply a mechanistic account of WHY the new locus carries the signal rather than merely evidence THAT it does.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism names the audited locus (the exogenous trajectory oracle, whose velocity statistics are assumed to be the only relevant content) and relocates the load-bearing signal to the endogenous closed-loop source where u(t) gates self-motion sampling; it then demonstrates the property at the new locus via the statistics-matched open-loop replay (ΔF_loop ≠ 0, code closer to the rodent curve) and gives the mechanistic WHY (the source co-develops with the code so the stream carries code-coupled structure replay cannot reproduce) plus the u(t)-decoupling negative control — the full C01 relocate-and-explain move.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"The anchor leg performs C01's signature locus-relocation-plus-mechanistic-account move (exogenous-oracle locus → endogenous confidence-gated closed-loop locus, demonstrated by the replay separation and explained by the code-coupling), and the C02 companion ships the confound-isolating empirical separation; the recipe is not the failure axis."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three reject-favored compositions in anti-patterns.md require heterogeneous_decomposition as a component; the candidate's single-leg composition set {assumption_audit_and_pivot} (with a controlled_diagnostic_design companion) contains no heterogeneous_decomposition, so no anti-pattern matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:7d34abe0a3a362500e99cbb1455b668d20a82829","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"The Abrate/Wills/Barry paper ('From movement to cognitive maps', bioRxiv 2025-12-30 / 2026-02-17) trains RNNs on EXOGENOUS trajectories that replay progressively maturing developmental locomotor statistics and shows those changing (non-stationary, ordered) movement statistics drive the sequential emergence of spatially tuned units. That mechanism subsumed the previously-abandoned anchor (an ordered exogenous developmental schedule sets the code), which is why Gaps 1 and 2 are deferred here. It does NOT subsume the present anchor: the present claim holds ALL movement statistics — marginal velocity histogram, full temporal autocorrelation including time-ordering, cumulative path length, and coverage — byte-identical between the two compared conditions (the closed-loop run and a verbatim open-loop replay of that run's own logged stream) and varies ONLY whether the self-motion stream is endogenously gated by the network's own decoding confidence or externally replayed. Abrate's result is about WHICH exogenous statistics are presented (developmental ordering); the present result is about whether the SOURCE of an identical statistics stream is endogenous-and-code-coupled versus exogenous, a contrast Abrate never constructs because they only ever use exogenous replayed trajectories and never train on an endogenous confidence-gated source nor run a statistics-matched open-loop replay of one. The candidate's headline (ΔF_loop ≠ 0 under statistics-matched replay) is therefore a previously-unmeasured effect, not a re-confirmation of Abrate's documented developmental-schedule effect.","addressable_via":"Already addressed by construction: the candidate matches all movement statistics (including developmental ordering) between conditions and isolates the endogenous-versus-exogenous source as the only varied axis, so the overlap with Abrate's exogenous-developmental-schedule mechanism is removed; no exact-mechanism overlap remains."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# The Movement Source, Not Its Statistics: Closed-Loop Self-Motion Reshapes the Hippocampal RNN Code\n\n**Method.** Closed-Loop Confidence-Gated Self-Motion (CL-CGSM)\n\n## Motivation\nComputer models of how the brain's hippocampus builds a map of space are recurrent neural networks (RNNs) trained to keep track of position from a stream of self-motion (how fast and in which direction the simulated animal is moving). In every such model, that motion stream is handed to the network from the outside — a pre-made trajectory generator, a set of recorded paths, or a reinforcement-learning policy. Two leading examples are the When-and-Where CA3 model (arxiv:2604.00036v1), which hand-picks a motion generator, and the REMI hippocampal-entorhinal loop (openalex:W6979295729), which replays pre-generated fixed-speed paths. In all of them the motion is an external given, and the network is examined only after training finishes.\n\nA recent and natural step has been to make that external motion stream change over training — to feed in a developmentally maturing movement schedule and show it drives the order in which spatial cells appear. But this still treats motion as something replayed from outside. The assumption nobody has named or tested is deeper: does it matter where the motion comes from at all, once its statistics (the distribution of speeds, turns, and ranges) are fixed? This is testable now because reading out an estimate of the animal's position from the RNN's internal state, in real time, is cheap and reliable — so the network's own confidence in where it is can be used to steer how it moves while it learns.\n\nPrior models stopped short for structural reasons: When-and-Where (arxiv:2604.00036v1) inherited the external motion source as a fixed setup and never made it a variable; REMI (openalex:W6979295729) replayed pre-made paths and had no control that separates the SOURCE of motion from the statistics it produces; and the reinforcement-learning agent (openalex:W4406406162) does generate its own motion, but tangled together with reward, and never compared it against a replay of its own movements.\n\nIf this gap closes — if how motion is generated reshapes the code even when its statistics are identical — then the standard practice of feeding RNNs an external motion stream is shown to throw away real signal, and self-motion must be modeled as something the network co-produces with its map, not something it passively integrates.\n\n## Method\n### Background scaffolding\n*The fixed movement sampler and base path-integration RNN shared by all conditions.*\n\n1. Build a movement generator that, given a mean speed (in cm/s), a heading-persistence value (how strongly each step keeps the previous direction), a turn-rate (tortuosity, how much the heading randomly wiggles), and an arena size, produces a step-by-step correlated random walk: each new heading mixes the old heading with a random direction plus a small random turn, the speed is drawn from a spread of values around the mean, and the resulting velocities are added up into (x, y) positions inside a fixed square arena, bouncing off the walls. Use a step length of 0.02 seconds (50 steps per second, the usual rate for these models). The output is the stream of velocity vectors and the matching true positions.\n   - _Why_: This is the controllable source of motion whose origin — supplied from outside versus generated by the network — is exactly what we vary.\n2. Build a plain 512-unit recurrent neural network (RNN) that reads the velocity at each step and updates a hidden state, with a linear output layer that predicts the current 2D position; train it to minimize the squared error between predicted and true position over each trajectory, using the Adam optimizer (learning rate 0.0001), batches of 64 trajectories that are 1000 steps (20 seconds) long, resetting the hidden state to zero at the start of each trajectory. Keep this network exactly the same across every experimental condition.\n   - _Why_: Holding everything except the motion source fixed means any later difference in the spatial code must come from the source, not the network design.\n\n### Closed-loop confidence-gated source\n*Reads the network's own decoding confidence and lets it gate self-motion so movement and code co-develop.*\n\n3. Attach a small online decoder that reads the RNN's hidden state and outputs a probability map over $a 32\\times 32$ grid of location bins (1024 bins), trained to put its mass on the true bin; let this decoder read the hidden state but NOT change the main network's weights (stop its gradient there), so the base task is untouched. Turn the sharpness of that probability map into a single confidence number between 0 and 1 — close to 1 when the map is concentrated on one bin (the network is sure where it is), close to 0 when it is spread out. This is the network's own sense of how well it currently knows its location.\n\n*The per-step decoding-confidence signal u(t): one minus the Shannon entropy H of the softmax position posterior produced by an online linear decoder $d_\\phi $ on hidden state $h_{t},$ normalized by log K over the K-bin spatial grid so u(t) lies in [0,1].*\n$$ u(t) = 1 - \\frac{1}{\\log K}\\, H\\!\\left(\\mathrm{softmax}\\, d_\\phi(h_t)\\right), \\qquad u(t) \\in [0,1] \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This builds the network's own sense of how well it currently knows its location — the internal signal we will let steer movement.\n4. Close the loop so the network steers its own movement. At each training step, take the confidence number from the decoder and use it to set the next step's speed (from a slow 5 cm/s at zero confidence to a fast 30 cm/s at full confidence) and the next step's turning behavior (low confidence makes movement slow and wandering, high confidence makes it fast and directed); draw the next velocity from the generator with these live settings, feed it to the RNN, take one learning step, and record every realized velocity into a log. Now the movement comes from the network's own developing map instead of an outside source, so movement and map grow together.\n\n*The closed-loop gating rule: the next sampled speed v(t) (cm/s) scales linearly with confidence u(t) between fixed bounds $v_{min}$ and $v_{max}$ (heading-persistence $\\rho $ and tortuosity $\\kappa $ scale analogously), so low confidence yields slow, tortuous exploration and high confidence yields fast, directed movement.*\n$$ v(t) = v_{\\min} + (v_{\\max} - v_{\\min})\\, u(t) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This is the key move: the motion now comes from the network's own developing map instead of from an outside oracle, so movement and map grow together.\n\n### Statistics-matched separation\n*Isolates the source coupling with a byte-identical open-loop replay and reads out the resulting code divergence.*\n\n5. Train a brand-new RNN on an exact, step-for-step replay of the velocity stream recorded during the closed-loop run, feeding it as if from an outside source, for the same total number of learning updates; start this network from the same family of random initializations but a different specific draw. Because the replayed velocities are byte-for-byte identical, the distribution of speeds, the timing patterns, the total distance, and the area covered are all identical — the only thing removed is the confidence steering. This matched replay is the fair control that isolates where the motion came from.\n   - _Why_: This matched replay is the fair control: it shares every statistic of the motion, so any difference in the code can only be due to where the motion came from.\n6. After training, run one fixed test path (that covers the whole arena evenly, visiting each location bin at least about 20 times) through each frozen network, and for every hidden unit make a firing map: average its activation in each location bin and lightly smooth it. Measure the typical place-field size as the median area where a unit's smoothed map is above half its peak, and the grid spacing as the median distance to the first ring in the map's spatial autocorrelation, taken only over units that pass a standard grid-likeness test. Do this both at the end of training and at saved checkpoints along the way, so the development over training can be tracked. Using the identical measurement on both networks makes their codes directly comparable.\n   - _Why_: Using the identical measurement on both networks makes their spatial codes directly comparable.\n7. Compute the difference in place-field size and in grid spacing between the closed-loop and replay networks. Separately, take each network's development-over-training curve of place-field size, stretch it onto a common 0-to-1 'maturation' axis, rescale both it and the published young-rat maturation curve to the same range, and measure how far apart the two curves are (the area between them); a closed-loop curve that is closer to the rat curve than the replay one is the rodent-faithfulness result. Report differences with confidence intervals across random seeds. A non-zero size/spacing difference overturns the assumption that matched statistics give the same code, and a smaller distance to the rat curve shows the closed-loop version is more lifelike. 【author decision: exactly how to line up the model's training timeline with the rat's developmental timeline — by a stretched 0-to-1 fraction or by mapping to real postnatal days, and whether to measure curve distance as plain area-between or with time-warping — is the authors' call; the trade-off is how much mismatch between model-step time and rat-day time you tolerate.】\n\n*The headline divergence: the difference in median place-field size F and grid scale G between the closed-loop network and the open-loop replay; the exogenous-oracle assumption predicts $\\Delta F_{loop} = \\Delta G_{loop} =$ 0, so a measured non-zero value is the contribution.*\n$$ \\Delta F_{\\mathrm{loop}} = F_{\\mathrm{closed}} - F_{\\mathrm{open}}, \\qquad \\Delta G_{\\mathrm{loop}} = G_{\\mathrm{closed}} - G_{\\mathrm{open}} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A non-zero difference would overturn the assumption that matched statistics give the same code, and the rat comparison tells us whether the closed-loop version is more lifelike.\n\n### Mechanism attribution\n*Confidence-randomization negative control and positive control that pin the effect to the code-coupled source.*\n\n8. Run the negative control that breaks the timing of the confidence signal. First record the overall distribution of confidence values from a normal closed-loop run; then retrain a closed-loop network where, at each step, the confidence value is drawn independently from that recorded distribution instead of from the network's actual state — so the spread of values is unchanged but it no longer tracks what the network is currently doing. Feed it through the same speed/turning rule and train otherwise identically, then re-measure the code difference and the held-out position-decoding error. If breaking the timing erases the effect (the difference drops back to the replay level and decoding accuracy returns to baseline), the effect comes from confidence being coupled to the developing map, not from the raw spread of motion.\n   - _Why_: If scrambling the timing erases the effect, it proves the effect comes from confidence being coupled to the developing map, not from the raw spread of motion.\n9. Train a stripped-down positive control that is identical to the replay baseline in every way except that the confidence-gated movement is added back, so whatever effect it recovers can be credited to that single ingredient. Then run every condition — closed-loop, replay, timing-scrambled, and stripped — with at least 5 random seeds, and report the effect sizes (a standardized difference measure) with 95% confidence intervals on place-field size, grid spacing, the distance-to-rat-curve, and the held-out position-decoding error, plus what fraction of the full effect the stripped version recovers on its own. The stripped version recovering most of the effect turns the test into a positive identification, and multiple seeds make the result reliable.\n   - _Why_: The stripped version should recover most of the effect on its own, turning the test into a positive identification, and multiple seeds make the result reliable.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 运动的来源而非其统计量：闭环自运动重塑海马 RNN 的空间编码\n\n**方法名称.** Closed-Loop Confidence-Gated Self-Motion (CL-CGSM)\n\n## 研究动机\n用来模拟大脑海马如何构建空间地图的计算模型，是一类被训练去根据自运动信息（模拟动物移动的速度和方向）持续推断自身位置的 recurrent neural network (RNN)。在所有这类模型里，这段运动信息都是从外部喂给网络的——可能是预先做好的轨迹生成器、一组录下来的路径，或一个 reinforcement learning 策略。两个代表性工作是 When-and-Where CA3 模型 (arxiv:2604.00036v1)，它手工挑选一个运动生成器；以及 REMI 海马-内嗅环路 (openalex:W6979295729)，它回放预先生成的固定速度路径。在它们当中，运动都是一个外部给定量，而且网络只在训练结束后才被检视。\n\n最近一个自然的进展，是让这段外部运动流在训练过程中变化——输入一个随发育成熟的运动 schedule，并展示它驱动了空间细胞出现的先后顺序。但这仍然把运动当作从外部回放的东西。没有人命名或检验过的、更深一层的假设是：一旦运动的统计量（速度、转向、范围的分布）固定下来，运动究竟来自哪里还重要吗？这个问题现在可以检验，因为从 RNN 的内部状态实时读出对动物位置的估计既便宜又可靠——于是网络对自己身处何处的置信度，就可以在学习过程中反过来引导它如何移动。\n\n以往模型因为结构性原因止步于此：When-and-Where (arxiv:2604.00036v1) 把外部运动来源当作固定设置继承下来，从未把它变成一个变量；REMI (openalex:W6979295729) 回放预制路径，没有任何能把运动的来源与它产生的统计量分开的对照；而那个 reinforcement learning 智能体 (openalex:W4406406162) 确实自己产生运动，但与奖励纠缠在一起，且从未拿它和对自身运动的回放作比较。\n\n如果这个空白被填上——即使统计量完全相同，运动如何被生成仍会重塑编码——那么给 RNN 喂外部运动流的标准做法就被证明丢掉了真实的信号，自运动必须被建模为网络与其地图共同产生的东西，而不是被动整合的东西。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景脚手架\n*所有条件共享的固定运动采样器与基础 path-integration RNN。*\n\n1. 构建一个运动生成器：给定平均速度(单位 cm/s)、朝向持续性(每一步多大程度上保持上一步方向)、转弯率(tortuosity，曲折度，朝向随机抖动的幅度)和场地大小，产生一步步的 correlated random walk(相关随机游走)：每个新朝向把旧朝向与一个随机方向混合，再加一点随机转角；速度从围绕平均值的一段取值中抽取；由此得到的速度累加成固定方形场地内的 (x, y) 位置，碰到墙则反弹。步长取 0.02 秒(每秒 50 步，这类模型的惯用频率)。输出是速度向量流以及与之对应的真实位置。\n   - _为什么_: 这是可控的运动来源，而它的出处——由外部提供还是由网络自己生成——正是我们要变化的东西。\n2. 构建一个普通的 512 单元 recurrent neural network(RNN)：它在每一步读入速度并更新隐藏态，再由一个线性输出层预测当前的二维位置；训练目标是最小化每条轨迹上预测位置与真实位置之间的平方误差，使用 Adam 优化器(学习率 0.0001)、每批 64 条长 1000 步(20 秒)的轨迹，每条轨迹开始时把隐藏态清零。在所有实验条件下保持这个网络完全一致。\n   - _为什么_: 除运动来源外其余一切都固定，意味着后面空间编码上的任何差异都只能来自来源，而非网络设计。\n\n### 闭环置信度门控来源\n*读取网络自身的解码置信度并用它门控自运动，使运动与编码共同发育。*\n\n3. 接上一个小型在线解码器，它读取 RNN 的隐藏态并输出一张覆盖 $32\\times 32$ 位置格子(共 1024 格)的概率图，训练它把概率质量压到真实格子上；让这个解码器只读隐藏态而不改动主网络的权重(在此处截断梯度 stop-gradient)，使基础任务不受影响。把这张概率图的尖锐程度转换成一个介于 0 到 1 之间的置信度——概率集中在单个格子时接近 1(网络确定自己在哪)，分散时接近 0。这就是网络对自己当前位置把握程度的内部感知。\n\n*每一步的解码置信度 u(t)：由在线线性解码器 $d_\\phi $ 在隐藏态 $h_{t}$ 上给出 softmax 位置后验，取其香农熵 H，再用 K 格空间网格的 log K 归一化后用 1 减去，使 u(t) 落在 [0,1]。*\n$$ u(t) = 1 - \\frac{1}{\\log K}\\, H\\!\\left(\\mathrm{softmax}\\, d_\\phi(h_t)\\right), \\qquad u(t) \\in [0,1] \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这构建出网络对自己当前位置把握程度的内部感知——也就是我们将用来引导运动的内部信号。\n4. 闭合回路，让网络自己引导运动。在每一步训练中，取解码器给出的置信度，用它设定下一步的速度(置信度为零时取慢速 5 cm/s，满置信度时取快速 30 cm/s)和下一步的转弯行为(低置信度使运动缓慢游走，高置信度使其快速定向)；用这些实时设置从生成器抽取下一步速度，喂给 RNN，走一步学习更新，并把每一步真实速度记入一份日志。此刻运动来自网络自己正在发育的地图而非外部来源，于是运动和地图一起成长。\n\n*闭环门控规则：下一步采样速度 v(t)（cm/s）随置信度 u(t) 在固定上下界 $v_{min}$ 与 $v_{max}$ 之间线性缩放（朝向持续性 $\\rho $ 与曲折度 $\\kappa $ 同理），低置信度产生缓慢曲折的探索，高置信度产生快速定向的运动。*\n$$ v(t) = v_{\\min} + (v_{\\max} - v_{\\min})\\, u(t) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这是关键一招：运动此刻来自网络自己正在发育的地图，而非外部 oracle，于是运动和地图一起成长。\n\n### 统计量匹配的分离对照\n*用逐字节相同的开环回放隔离来源耦合，并读出由此产生的编码差异。*\n\n5. 用闭环运行时记录下来的速度流做一次精确的、逐步原样回放，当作来自外部的来源喂给一个全新的 RNN，训练相同的总更新步数；这个网络从同一族随机初始化中以不同的具体抽样开始。由于回放的速度逐字节相同，速度分布、时间节律、总路程和覆盖面积都完全一致——唯一被去掉的是那套置信度引导。这个统计量匹配的回放就是隔离『运动来自哪里』的公平对照。\n   - _为什么_: 这个统计量匹配的回放就是公平对照：它共享运动的每一项统计量，因此编码上的任何差异只可能源于运动来自哪里。\n6. 训练结束后，让一条固定的测试路径(均匀覆盖整个场地，每个位置格子至少被访问约 20 次)穿过每个冻结的网络，并为每个隐藏单元绘制发放图：在每个位置格子里对其激活取平均，再做轻度平滑。把典型的 place-field 大小测为『单元平滑发放图高于其峰值一半』的连通区域面积的中位数，把 grid 间距测为『发放图空间自相关中第一圈的距离』的中位数，且只在通过标准类 grid 检验的单元上统计。这既在训练结束时做，也在沿途保存的 checkpoint 上做，以便追踪训练过程中的发育。对两个网络使用完全相同的测量，能让它们的编码直接可比。\n   - _为什么_: 对两个网络使用完全相同的测量，能让它们的空间编码直接可比。\n7. 计算闭环网络与回放网络之间 place-field 大小和 grid 间距的差异。另外，把每个网络『place-field 大小随训练发育』的曲线拉伸到统一的 0 到 1『成熟度』轴上，再把它和已发表的幼年大鼠成熟曲线缩放到同一量程，测量两条曲线相隔多远(它们之间的面积)；闭环曲线比回放曲线更贴近大鼠曲线，就是『更接近真实』的结果。差异连同跨随机种子的置信区间一并报告。非零的大小/间距差异会推翻『统计量相同则编码相同』的假设，而到大鼠曲线更小的距离则表明闭环版本更接近真实。【作者需决定：究竟如何把模型的训练时间轴与大鼠的发育时间轴对齐——是用拉伸到 0 到 1 的成熟度比例，还是映射到真实的出生后天数，以及曲线距离用简单的面积之差还是用 time-warping(时间扭曲)——由作者拍板；权衡是对『模型步数时间与大鼠天数时间不匹配』的容忍程度。】\n\n*核心差异量：闭环网络与开环回放网络之间中位 place-field 大小 F 和 grid 尺度 G 的差；外源 oracle 假设预测 $\\Delta F_{loop} = \\Delta G_{loop} = 0$，因此测得非零值即为本工作的贡献。*\n$$ \\Delta F_{\\mathrm{loop}} = F_{\\mathrm{closed}} - F_{\\mathrm{open}}, \\qquad \\Delta G_{\\mathrm{loop}} = G_{\\mathrm{closed}} - G_{\\mathrm{open}} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 非零差异会推翻『统计量相同则编码相同』的假设，而与大鼠的比较则告诉我们闭环版本是否更接近真实。\n\n### 机制归因\n*置信度随机化的负对照与正对照，把效应锁定到与编码耦合的来源上。*\n\n8. 运行打乱置信度信号时序的负对照。先从一次正常闭环运行中记录置信度取值的整体分布；再重训一个闭环网络，让每一步的置信度从这个记录下来的分布中独立抽取，而非来自网络的真实状态——这样取值的分布不变，却不再跟随网络当前的行为。把它送进相同的速度/转弯规则，其余训练完全一致，然后重新测量编码差异和留出集上的位置解码误差。如果打乱时序就抹掉了效应(差异回落到回放水平、解码精度回到基线)，就说明效应来自置信度与发育中地图的耦合，而非运动本身的分布幅度。\n   - _为什么_: 如果打乱时序就抹掉了效应，就证明效应来自置信度与发育中地图的耦合，而非运动本身的分布幅度。\n9. 训练一个精简的正对照：它与回放基线在每一处都相同，唯一区别是把置信度门控的运动加回来，于是它复现出的任何效应都可归因于这一个成分。然后对每个条件——闭环、回放、时序打乱、精简——都用至少 5 个随机种子运行，报告效应量(一个标准化的差异度量)连同 place-field 大小、grid 间距、到大鼠曲线的距离、以及留出集位置解码误差上的 95% 置信区间，并报告精简版本自身复现了整体效应的多大比例。精简版本能复现大部分效应，就把检验变成一次正向确认，而多个种子让结果更可靠。\n   - _为什么_: 精简版本本身应能复现大部分效应，把检验变成一次正向确认，而多个种子让结果更可靠。\n\n"},{"id":"48","run_dir":"run_prompt48_certunlearn","index":48,"title":"Certified Unlearning as a Hypothesis Test: Calibrated Deletion in High Dimensions","title_zh":"把认证遗忘当作假设检验：高维下的可校准删除","method_name":"Likelihood-Ratio Deletion Test (LRDT)","hook":"Every Gaussian-mechanism unlearning certificate fixes its noise to a worst-case divergence bound, never to the discrepancy a specific deletion actually produces; we recast the certificate as a likelihood-ratio test of 'retrained vs. unlearned' whose type-I error is the false-deletion-rate the analyst can control, and prove the noise needed to honor a target error scales with the deletion's realized signal-to-dimension ratio rather than the worst case.","anchor_pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","anchor_pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","domain_category":"Privacy, Security & Trustworthy ML","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf converts the certified-unlearning indistinguishability claim into a finite-sample decision procedure with controlled error: there is no calibrated test that, given the realized unlearned and retrained (or reference) models for a specific deletion, returns whether the achieved unlearned-vs-retrain discrepancy is within the certified tolerance, so the guarantee remains a one-sided bound that cannot be checked on the actual deletion.","pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by reframing the opaque 'is this deletion within tolerance' question about the fixed unlearned model as a measurement over a well-studied object — the Neyman-Pearson likelihood-ratio statistic of the binary problem H0 (parameter distribution equals the retrain-from-scratch law) vs H1 (it equals the unlearned law) — whose calibrated type-I error IS the false-deletion-rate and whose validity is certified by a soundness/optimality proof rather than by a divergence bound.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes how the discriminability between an unlearned and a retrained high-dimensional model behaves as the parameter dimension p grows relative to n: the noise calibrated to honor the certificate is set to the worst case rather than to the discrepancy that actually occurs, and the regime in which deletion becomes statistically undetectable (versus detectable) at finite n, p is not mapped, so high-dimensional noise levels cannot be set from achieved evidence.","pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by formalizing the exact distinguishability limit of the same retrained-vs-unlearned test as a separation criterion in the (noise scale sigma, p, n) regime — the detectability boundary below which the optimal test's power collapses to its size (deletion statistically undetectable) — and proving the LRT from the anchor attains that boundary, so the noise can be set to the realized signal-to-dimension ratio that sits just inside the undetectable region.","is_anchor":false},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions whether the unlearned-vs-retrain discrepancy must be summarized by a single worst-case scalar sensitivity at all: every noise-injection certificate (semanticscholar:576a705051fb839f514f52583dd9fd470a1e0011, semanticscholar:dd3b9ee1c0a181fafcb39dde27031f0cfe0d3fc6, arxiv:2602.15602v2) silently inherits from the DP ancestor the assumption that a scalar divergence/sensitivity budget is the right object to control, and none tests whether controlling that scalar is necessa","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C29 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by auditing the load-bearing assumption of the existing deletion-guarantee proofs — that the object to control is a scalar worst-case divergence/sensitivity budget — and pivoting the convergence/target primitive to the test's operating characteristic (the (size alpha, power beta) pair), then re-deriving the Gaussian noise-calibration rate under this new criterion to prove a separation: the test-calibrated noise is strictly smaller than the divergence-calibrated noise in the p comparable to n regime while honoring the same alpha.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"certified machine unlearning in high-dimensional models (Gaussian-mechanism / noise-injection certificates), with a statistical hypothesis-testing lens","n_papers":44,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":22},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":9}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":14,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Rewind-to-Delete: Certified Machine Unlearning for Nonconvex Functions"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Certified Machine Unlearning via Noisy Stochastic Gradient Descent"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Langevin Unlearning: A New Perspective of Noisy Gradient Descent for Machine Unlearning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"On Performance Comparison between Strong Machine Unlearning Algorithms for Logistic Regression Credit Assessment Models"},{"source":"openalex","title":"IDEA: A Flexible Framework of Certified Unlearning for Graph Neural Networks"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Certified Unlearning for Federated Recommendation"}],"more":8},{"year":2025,"n":22,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Certified Machine Unlearning Under High Dimensional Regime"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Beyond Uniform Deletion: A Data Value-Weighted Framework for Certified Machine Unlearning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Machine Unlearning in the Era of Quantum Machine Learning: An Empirical Study"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Beyond Permanent Memory: Digital Forgetting in the Age of Intelligent Systems, Reconciling Human Cognition, Machine Unlearning, and the Right to Be Forgotten"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Boundary-Anchored Functional Duplication Attacks on Machine Unlearning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Mo' Memory, Mo' Problems: Stream-Native Machine Unlearning"}],"more":16},{"year":2026,"n":8,"papers":[{"source":"arxiv","title":"Easy Data Unlearning Bench"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"A Robust Certified Machine Unlearning Method Under Distribution Shift"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Erasure or Erosion? Evaluating Compositional Degradation in Unlearned Text-To-Image Diffusion Models"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"SUPREME: A Multi-GPU Framework for Reproducible Image Unlearning Method Evaluation"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Certified Unlearning in Decentralized Federated Learning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Certified Per-Instance Unlearning Using Individual Sensitivity Bounds"}],"more":2}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":18,"share":0.409},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":10,"share":0.227},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":8,"share":0.182},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":8,"share":0.182},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":4,"share":0.091},{"pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","count":3,"share":0.068},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":3,"share":0.068},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":2,"share":0.045}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Certified machine-unlearning mechanisms in the noise-injection family (Noisy-SGD certified unlearning semanticscholar:576a705051fb839f514f52583dd9fd470a1e0011, Langevin Unlearning semanticscholar:dd3b9ee1c0a181fafcb39dde27031f0cfe0d3fc6, Rewind-to-Delete semanticscholar:e9f5eb885f6168ec3087c39116d3c232ef3f8376) certify deletion by bounding a divergence between the unlearned-model distribution and the retrain-from-scratch distribution and then adding Gaussian noise calibrated so that this divergence stays below an (epsilon, delta) budget. The bound is worst-case over deletion sets and is summarized by a single scalar sensitivity, so in the high-dimensional regime where the parameter count p is comparable to the sample size n the calibrated noise standard deviation grows with dimension and the certified guarantee is honored only by injecting enough noise to wash out the very signal the model was trained on (openalex:W4417517067, semanticscholar:5e76d2258bae4c1cbf05db3dfc8b4c05aceb05a9); Per-Instance sensitivity bounds (arxiv:2602.15602v2) tighten the scalar but inherit the same upper-bound-not-test structure. What breaks is that the certificate is a one-sided distributional upper bound rather than a quantity the analyst can evaluate on the actual unlearned and reference models for a specific deletion: there is no finite-sample procedure that takes the realized unlearned parameter (or its outputs) in dimension p and returns a calibrated decision, with controlled error rates, about whether the achieved unlearned-vs-retrain discrepancy is within the certified tolerance, so the high-dimensional noise level cannot be set from the discrepancy that actually occurs and is instead pinned to the worst case.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:dd3b9ee1c0a181fafcb39dde27031f0cfe0d3fc6","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Langevin Unlearning recasts approximate unlearning as projected-noisy-gradient (Langevin) dynamics and proves a Renyi-divergence privacy bound between the unlearned and retrained parameter distributions, with a 'privacy recuperation' result showing extra unlearning steps shrink the divergence. The residue is that the guarantee is a worst-case divergence upper bound used only to calibrate the noise scale; it never produces an estimator or decision rule that, given the realized models, tests whether the achieved unlearned-vs-retrain discrepancy is within tolerance, and the bound's dimension dependence is not characterized as the power of any such test in the p-comparable-to-n regime."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:576a705051fb839f514f52583dd9fd470a1e0011","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Certified unlearning via noisy SGD calibrates Gaussian noise using a privacy-amplification-by-iteration analysis so the unlearned model satisfies an (epsilon, delta) deletion guarantee relative to retraining. The residue is that the noise is set to the worst-case sensitivity bound and never adapted to the realized deletion: there is no test that checks whether a particular deletion even moved the optimum enough to require the full worst-case noise, so high-dimensional utility is sacrificed uniformly."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.15602v2","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Certified Per-Instance Unlearning replaces worst-case sensitivity with an individual-sensitivity bound per deleted example, calibrating less noise when a point's bound is small. The residue is that it still produces a per-instance UPPER BOUND fed into the same Gaussian calibration; it offers no finite-sample test of achieved indistinguishability and does not characterize false-deletion-rate or power as p grows, so the saved noise is still bound-driven rather than evidence-driven."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4417517067","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Certified Data Removal Under High-dimensional Settings extends data-removal influence bounds into the regime where p is comparable to n, characterizing how the removal residual scales with dimension. The residue is that it quantifies the bound's dimension dependence but stops at the bound: there is no test statistic with calibrated type-I error over the realized high-dimensional model, and no power analysis of distinguishing unlearned from retrained at finite n, p."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4407926546","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Differentially private Kolmogorov-Smirnov-type tests build statistically valid and powerful nonparametric hypothesis tests under a DP constraint. The residue is that the testing machinery is developed for distributional two-sample testing of data, not for certifying deletion of a training point from a model: it is never connected to unlearning indistinguishability or to testing in the p-comparable-to-n parameter space, so its calibrated-error framework has not been imported to the unlearning certificate."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"certified machine unlearning in high-dimensional models (Gaussian-mechanism / noise-injection certificates), with a statistical hypothesis-testing lens","venue":"ICLR 2026","time":"2026","data":["high-dimensional ridge / logistic / generalized-linear regression with p comparable to n","synthetic Gaussian-design ERM problems where the deletion geometry is analytically controllable","standard tabular / vision unlearning benchmarks (e.g. the deletion-set protocols used by Langevin Unlearning and Noisy-SGD certified unlearning)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"high-dimensional statistics, differential privacy, machine unlearning theory","preference":"both","baseline":"Gaussian / noise-injection certified-unlearning mechanisms calibrated to worst-case sensitivity (Noisy-SGD certified unlearning semanticscholar:576a705051fb839f514f52583dd9fd470a1e0011; Langevin Unlearning semanticscholar:dd3b9ee1c0a181fafcb39dde27031f0cfe0d3fc6; Rewind-to-Delete semanticscholar:e9f5eb885f6168ec3087c39116d3c232ef3f8376; Per-Instance sensitivity arxiv:2602.15602v2; high-dim certified removal openalex:W4417517067)","limitation":"Certified-unlearning guarantees are worst-case (epsilon, delta) upper bounds calibrated to worst-case (or per-instance) sensitivity; in high dimensions the noise needed to honor that bound scales with dimension and destroys utility, and the certificate is never converted into a finite-sample test that the analyst can actually run to decide, for a given deletion, whether the unlearned model is statistically indistinguishable from the retrained one.","contribution_type":"theory","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object every leg reads from and writes to is the binary hypothesis test T between two laws of the realized model: H0, the law of the parameter (or its outputs) under retrain-from-scratch on the retain set D_r, versus H1, the law under the unlearning update U applied to the trained model. ANCHOR LEG (C00): we reframe 'is the deletion certified within tolerance tau' as computing the likelihood-ratio statistic Lambda = log[ p_{H1}(theta_hat) / p_{H0}(theta_hat) ] on the realized unlearned parameter theta_hat in R^p, where for the canonical Gaussian-mechanism family (noisy-GD / Langevin unlearning, semanticscholar:dd3b9ee1c0a181fafcb39dde27031f0cfe0d3fc6) both laws are Gaussian-approximated around their respective optima theta_r (retrain) and theta_u (unlearn) with covariance sigma^2 H^{-1}, H the loss Hessian at the optimum; then Lambda reduces to a quadratic form (theta_hat - midpoint)^T H (theta_u - theta_r) / sigma^2. The faithfulness constraint (C00 step 3) is that the test is evaluated under the SAME injected-noise law the mechanism uses, so the score reflects the actual mechanism rather than an off-distribution surrogate; fidelity is certified by Neyman-Pearson optimality (C00 step 5): the LRT is the most powerful test at every size, so a deletion that passes at level alpha has a provably controlled false-deletion-rate alpha — the per-deletion calibrated decision the worst-case bound never produced. The single compression trick (C00 step 4) is that Lambda's distribution under H0 and H1 is a non-central chi-square / shifted Gaussian governed by ONE scalar, the Mahalanobis separation Delta = ||theta_u - theta_r||_H / sigma, so the whole p-dimensional test collapses to a one-parameter family computable in closed form. SIBLING LEG 1 (C10): the exact structural object the worst-case certificate discards is the realized separation Delta as a function of (p, n, sigma); we formalize the detectability limit as the separation criterion Delta_c below which the optimal-test power beta(alpha) equals its size alpha (deletion undetectable), prove via a high-dimensional CLT for the quadratic form that Delta concentrates at sqrt(p)/(sigma sqrt(n)) times the per-example influence norm, and prove the anchor's LRT attains the boundary (it surpasses every consistent estimator-thresholding scheme, which loses a sqrt(log p) factor). SIBLING LEG 2 (C29): the existing deletion-guarantee proofs rest on the regularity/target assumption that the controlled primitive is a scalar worst-case Renyi/(epsilon,delta) divergence budget over all deletion sets; we pivot that target primitive to the test operating characteristic (alpha, beta) and re-derive the noise-calibration from scratch — the load-bearing decomposition splits the required sigma into a universally-bounded part (the alpha control) and an assumption-sensitive part (the realized Delta), proving the separation that test-calibrated sigma_T = realized-Delta-driven is strictly below divergence-calibrated sigma_D = worst-case-Delta-driven whenever the deletion is not worst case, with the gap widening as p/n grows. The three legs share the single object T: the anchor builds it, leg 1 characterizes its power limit, leg 2 re-grounds what noise it needs.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) All three gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules because they are three questions about ONE object — the retrained-vs-unlearned likelihood-ratio test: gap-0 asks to build it with a calibrated error, gap-1 asks for its power as p/n grows, gap-2 asks what it lets you control instead of a scalar budget; the evidence that they share machinery is that Delta (the Mahalanobis separation) is simultaneously the test's sufficient statistic, the quantity whose threshold gives the detectability limit, and the quantity test-calibration replaces the worst-case budget with. (b) I considered an alternative where the anchor instead built a membership-inference-style empirical classifier (the c2 collateral node) and the legs analyzed its ROC; I rejected it because an uncalibrated trained attacker has no closed-form type-I-error guarantee and would land on the parametric membership-inference auditing node (a regression), losing the certificate-equivalence that is the whole point. I also considered making the controlled object a tighter scalar divergence (a per-instance bound, arxiv:2602.15602v2); rejected because that stays on the DP-accounting node n1/n6 and never produces a runnable test.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on high-dimensional ridge and regularized logistic regression with Gaussian design at p/n in {0.5, 0.9, 1.0}, run the Gaussian-mechanism unlearning baseline (noisy-GD certified unlearning), delete a single influential example, and run the proposed likelihood-ratio test at target false-deletion-rate alpha = 0.05. If the candidate works, the empirical false-deletion-rate stays at alpha across all p/n (calibration holds where a worst-case bound would be conservative), the test's empirical power tracks the predicted Phi(Delta - z_{1-alpha}) curve, and the test-calibrated noise sigma_T yields strictly higher held-out accuracy than the divergence-calibrated sigma_D, with the accuracy gap widening as p/n approaches 1. The named load-bearing variable is the Mahalanobis separation Delta = ||theta_u - theta_r||_H / sigma — the single scalar that the p-dimensional test collapses to and that carries the mechanism claim (calibration and power are both functions of Delta alone). Negative control: oracle-replace the unlearned model with a freshly retrained-on-D model for the SAME deleted index so the true separation is zero (Delta = 0 by construction); the mechanism predicts the test's rejection rate must drop to exactly alpha and, downstream, the accuracy of the model released under the test's accept decision must return to the no-deletion baseline. If instead rejection rate or released-model accuracy stays elevated when Delta is forced to zero, the test is keying on a confound (Hessian misestimation, finite-sample noise) rather than the true retrained-vs-unlearned separation, and the mechanism is falsified. A positive control — a stripped-down decision rule that thresholds Delta alone, ignoring the full quadratic form — should recover most of the calibrated power, confirming Delta is the sufficient statistic.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:dd3b9ee1c0a181fafcb39dde27031f0cfe0d3fc6","delta":"Langevin Unlearning derives a worst-case Renyi-divergence upper bound between the unlearned and retrained laws and uses it only to set the noise scale; we construct the Neyman-Pearson likelihood-ratio test between those same two laws and prove its type-I error is a calibrated, per-deletion false-deletion-rate the analyst evaluates on the realized model — a decision rule with an error guarantee, not a divergence bound."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:576a705051fb839f514f52583dd9fd470a1e0011","delta":"Noisy-SGD certified unlearning calibrates Gaussian noise to a worst-case sensitivity via privacy-amplification accounting; we re-derive the required noise from the test's operating characteristic and prove it is strictly smaller (sigma_T < sigma_D) whenever the realized deletion is not worst case, with the gap growing as p/n -> 1."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.15602v2","delta":"Per-Instance Unlearning tightens the scalar by replacing worst-case with per-example sensitivity but still feeds an UPPER BOUND into the same calibration; we replace the scalar-bound object entirely with a (size alpha, power beta) operating characteristic and a high-dimensional detectability threshold, giving an evidence-driven rather than bound-driven noise level."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4417517067","delta":"Certified Data Removal Under High-dimensional Settings characterizes how the removal residual scales with p but stops at the bound; we characterize the power of the optimal retrained-vs-unlearned TEST as a separation criterion in (sigma, p, n) and prove the LRT attains the detectability boundary that bound-based analysis cannot express."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4407926546","delta":"DP Kolmogorov-Smirnov-type tests build calibrated two-sample tests of DATA distributions under a privacy constraint; we build a calibrated test of MODEL deletion (retrained-vs-unlearned parameter laws) in the p-comparable-to-n regime, importing the calibrated-error framework into the unlearning certificate where it had not been applied."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:dd3b9ee1c0a181fafcb39dde27031f0cfe0d3fc6","what_step_was_missed":"Langevin Unlearning already characterizes the two Gaussian-approximated laws (unlearned vs retrained) and bounds their Renyi divergence, so it sits one step from the test: the missed step is constructing the likelihood-ratio statistic between those two laws and proving (via Neyman-Pearson) that thresholding it gives a most-powerful test whose size equals a calibrated false-deletion-rate, plus the high-dimensional concentration of its sufficient statistic Delta that turns the divergence bound into a (p, n, sigma) detectability threshold — they bounded the divergence but never converted it into a decision rule with controlled error or a power characterization."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":238,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"Layer-1 hard floor did not fire: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict is borderline (no lesson marked candidate_match: yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat.subsumption_argument shows openalex:W7161915643 tests a different object (edited-data domain distributions, not the model parameter law) so it is not exact-mechanism overlap. recipe_application_check.verdict = applied on all three legs (the C00 measurement-with-soundness-proof, the C10 detectability separation, and the C29 operating-characteristic pivot are each present in core_mechanism). The two borderlines (C10 frontier-survey vs the testing-meets-unlearning collision papers; C29 hidden-constant at p/n->1) hit load-bearing-adjacent but Phase-4-dischargeable obligations rather than documented Reject patterns, and addressable_via names a Phase-4 reviewer-concern edit, not a core_mechanism defect — so advance with both surfaced for reviewer_concerns_and_responses.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf converts the certified-unlearning indistinguishability claim into a finite-sample decision procedure with controlled error: there is no calibrated test that, given the realized unlearned and retrained (or reference) models for a specific deletion, returns whether the achieved unlearned-vs-retrain discrepancy is within the certified tolerance, so the guarantee remains a one-sided bound that cannot be checked on the actual deletion.","main_pattern":"reframe_as_solvable_object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The signature failure is treating the reframing as a mechanical wrapper: taking an established attribution, decomposition, or estimation tool and pointing it at a new input granularity or new domain without re-deriving why the resulting scores are faithful to the model, supplying the computation but not the justification (no causal validation, no soundness argument).","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Pointing an off-the-shelf decomposition at a coarser input granularity without showing the coarser units preserve the signal reads as a wrapper, not a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate does not point an off-the-shelf tool at a coarser granularity; it constructs the Neyman-Pearson likelihood-ratio statistic for the specific retrained-vs-unlearned model laws and proves (not asserts) its size equals a calibrated false-deletion-rate."},{"lesson_quoted":"Porting a known attribution technique to a new architecture or domain while ignoring that technique's documented failure modes — and omitting comparisons to alternatives — leaves reviewers unable to see any unique benefit.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"differentiation_from_lit compares against the divergence-bound baselines and the DP-testing line, and core_mechanism states the regime (Gaussian-mechanism family, p comparable to n) where the test's documented behavior (power collapse below Delta_c) is characterized rather than ignored."},{"lesson_quoted":"Proposing a new attribution definition without an axiomatic or causal argument for why it should count as ground-truth collapses the moment a reviewer asks why this is the real importance.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The 'real quantity' is grounded by Neyman-Pearson optimality (the LRT is most powerful at every size) and by the negative-control causal test in falsification_prediction (forcing Delta=0 must drive rejection rate to alpha), so the definition is load-bearing and causally validated, not asserted."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes how the discriminability between an unlearned and a retrained high-dimensional model behaves as the parameter dimension p grows relative to n: the noise calibrated to honor the certificate is set to the worst case rather than to the discrepancy that actually occurs, and the regime in which deletion becomes statistically undetectable (versus detectable) at finite n, p is not mapped, so high-dimensional noise levels cannot be set from achieved evidence.","main_pattern":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail when the 'limit' is not a genuine structural blindspot (trivially implied, already surpassed, or never formalized beyond an informal analogy), or when the operator is built and superiority asserted without surveying the frontier so a published method strictly subsumes the claimed gain.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Resting the central claim on an informal analogy (two operators 'both smooth high frequencies') instead of a separation proof leaves the mechanism underspecified and the empirical gain unconvincing.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The limit is formalized as an explicit separation criterion — the critical Mahalanobis separation Delta_c below which optimal-test power equals its size — proven via a high-dimensional CLT for the quadratic form, not an analogy."},{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a 'maximally expressive' construction that a recently published method already strictly subsumes turns the surpass-the-limit claim into redundant work.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"Two collision papers ('Statistical Unlearning of Distributions: A Hypothesis Testing Approach' and SMI) also pair unlearning with testing; they do not characterize the (sigma, p, n) detectability boundary for the parameter-law test, but the frontier-survey obligation is live and must be discharged in Phase 4 reviewer_concerns."},{"lesson_quoted":"Applying existing structural descriptors to a new application domain without formalizing a new limit or constructing a new operator yields a domain study, not a methodological contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"A new limit (the detectability separation criterion in p/n) AND a new operator (the LRT proven to attain the boundary, beating estimator-thresholding by a sqrt(log p) factor) are both constructed."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions whether the unlearned-vs-retrain discrepancy must be summarized by a single worst-case scalar sensitivity at all: every noise-injection certificate (semanticscholar:576a705051fb839f514f52583dd9fd470a1e0011, semanticscholar:dd3b9ee1c0a181fafcb39dde27031f0cfe0d3fc6, arxiv:2602.15602v2) silently inherits from the DP ancestor the assumption that a scalar divergence/sensitivity budget is the right object to control, and none tests whether controlling that scalar is necessary rather than assumed for a calibrated deletion guarantee in high dimensions.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C29 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail when the weakened assumption is one no known function class is shown to satisfy (engineered to close the proof), when a relaxed condition is borrowed from a neighboring literature without demonstrating its concrete benefit, or when the re-derived rate merely matches the baseline with cosmetic changes.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A weakened assumption that no known function class is shown to satisfy reads as engineered to close the proof, not as a genuine generalization — characterize when it holds or it sinks the paper.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The pivot is verifiable on concrete classes — Gaussian-design ridge and regularized logistic regression at stated p/n — where the operating-characteristic primitive and the realized Delta are both computable, so the relaxed target criterion is exhibited, not abstract."},{"lesson_quoted":"Re-deriving a rate that merely matches the baseline with near-identical algorithmic changes is read as an incremental extension, however clean the analysis.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The re-derivation proves a strict separation (test-calibrated sigma_T strictly below divergence-calibrated sigma_D in the p comparable to n regime, gap widening with p/n), not a rate that matches the baseline."},{"lesson_quoted":"Hidden constants that explode at the precise parameter limit where the result is advertised as strongest silently invalidate the headline guarantee.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The headline gain is advertised exactly at p/n -> 1, where high-dimensional CLT remainder terms and Hessian-estimation error are most fragile; the load-bearing-decomposition split must be shown to keep its constant bounded at that limit (a Phase 4 feasibility/theory concern, not a wrapper failure)."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No gap_closure entry is triggered (no Reject lesson marked candidate_match: yes). Two borderlines arose: the C10 leg's frontier-survey obligation (two recent test-meets-unlearning collision papers must be distinguished) and the C29 leg's hidden-constant-at-p/n->1 concern; both are load-bearing-adjacent but are discharge-in-Phase-4 obligations rather than documented Reject matches, so the aggregate is borderline, not triggered."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf converts the certified-unlearning indistinguishability claim into a finite-sample decision procedure with controlled error...","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Recast an opaque transparency/uncertainty question about an already-trained model as a concrete measurement over a well-studied object (an estimator/decomposition/influence score), choosing the unit and faithfulness constraint so scores reflect the model's actual computation, with fidelity certified by a causal intervention or a soundness/optimality proof rather than plausibility.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"Anchor leg: the opaque 'is this deletion within tolerance' question about the fixed unlearned model is recast as the likelihood-ratio statistic Lambda over the realized theta_hat; the faithfulness constraint (evaluate under the same injected-noise law the mechanism uses) is the C00 'on-manifold' move, and fidelity is certified by Neyman-Pearson optimality (soundness proof) plus the Delta=0 negative control (causal intervention) — exactly the cluster's certify-by-proof-or-intervention signature, not a wrapper.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes how the discriminability between an unlearned and a retrained high-dimensional model behaves as the parameter dimension p grows...","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Pinpoint the one structural object a procedure discards, formalize the equivalence/indistinguishability it induces as a precise separation criterion on native objects, then re-inject that object and prove the augmented operator strictly exceeds the criterion at bounded cost.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"Sibling leg 1: the discarded object is the realized separation Delta(p,n,sigma); it is formalized as the detectability separation criterion Delta_c (power = size below it), and the LRT is proven to attain the boundary, surpassing estimator-thresholding schemes by a sqrt(log p) factor — the characterize-then-surpass signature, adapted from message-passing's combinatorial separation to a high-dimensional statistical separation.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions whether the unlearned-vs-retrain discrepancy must be summarized by a single worst-case scalar sensitivity at all...","sub_pattern":"C29 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Take an existing convergence/guarantee proof and pivot the single regularity-or-target-criterion assumption it silently rests on (e.g. swap the convergence primitive — squared-distance target to objective-gap, metric error to ordinal condition), then re-prove the rate isolating one load-bearing decomposition, gaining a separation or a harder regime.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"Sibling leg 2: the audited assumption is the controlled primitive itself (a scalar worst-case divergence/sensitivity budget); it is pivoted to the test operating characteristic (alpha, beta), and the noise-calibration rate is re-derived via a load-bearing split of sigma into a universally-bounded (alpha-control) part and an assumption-sensitive (realized-Delta) part, proving the sigma_T < sigma_D separation — the cluster's pivot-the-target-primitive-then-reprove-for-a-separation signature.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"All three legs perform their cited cluster's distinctive move on the shared object: C00's certify-by-proof measurement reframe (the LRT + Neyman-Pearson soundness), C10's separation-criterion-then-surpass (Delta_c detectability + boundary-attaining LRT), and C29's pivot-the-target-primitive-and-re-derive-a-separation (operating-characteristic-calibrated noise with the sigma_T < sigma_D split). None reduces to its parent's generic gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["reframe_as_solvable_object","characterize_limit_then_surpass","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"None of the three reject-favored 2-way compositions matches: all three documented anti-patterns require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component, and it is absent from this composition set, so no anti-pattern fires."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"openalex:W7161915643","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"'Statistical Unlearning of Distributions: A Hypothesis Testing Approach' is the most specific competitor because it also couples unlearning with a hypothesis test, but its test is over the EDITED DATA against desired/unwanted DOMAIN distributions and serves as a criterion for SELECTING which subset of samples to remove for distribution-level forgetting; it never tests the realized model's retrained-vs-unlearned parameter-law indistinguishability, produces no calibrated per-deletion false-deletion-rate certificate, and does no high-dimensional (p comparable to n) detectability/noise-calibration. The candidate's claim stands because its object is the model's parameter law (a likelihood-ratio test between retrain and unlearn distributions with Neyman-Pearson optimality and an explicit Delta_c detectability boundary), a strictly different solvable object; the candidate falls only if a paper is shown to already calibrate Gaussian-mechanism noise to the test's operating characteristic in the p~n regime, which neither this paper nor SMI (arxiv:2602.01150v2, an empirical membership-inference auditor with no calibrated type-I certificate) does.","addressable_via":"Add a reviewer_concerns_and_responses entry in Phase 4 sharpening differentiation_from_lit against openalex:W7161915643 and arxiv:2602.01150v2 (data-distribution test / empirical MIA auditor vs. parameter-law calibrated certificate) — no core_mechanism change needed."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Certified Unlearning as a Hypothesis Test: Calibrated Deletion in High Dimensions\n\n**Method.** Likelihood-Ratio Deletion Test (LRDT)\n\n## Motivation\nWhen someone asks a company to delete their data, the law-style promise of 'certified unlearning' is that the model you keep serving looks statistically the same as a model that had been trained from scratch without that person's data. The most common way to deliver this promise treats it as a privacy problem: you bound how different the two models could be in the worst case, then add just enough random Gaussian noise to the model to keep that worst-case difference inside a budget. The trouble is that this is only ever an upper bound you have to trust — it is never a number you actually compute on the two real models for the specific deletion in front of you. Langevin Unlearning (a noisy-gradient method, NeurIPS 2024) describes both model distributions in closed form but never turns that into a test you can run. Recent work on Certified Data Removal in High Dimensions (arXiv 2025-05) shows exactly why this hurts: when the number of parameters p is close to the number of training examples n, the worst-case noise grows so large it erases the signal the model was trained on. What is newly available is a ready-made statistical-testing toolkit (calibrated tests under privacy constraints) plus the closed-form pair of model distributions — together they let us replace the bound with an actual test. We turn the certificate into a likelihood-ratio test that asks 'does this model look like the retrained one or the unlearned one?', set its false-alarm rate to a level the analyst chooses (the false-deletion-rate), and prove the whole high-dimensional test boils down to a single number: the Mahalanobis separation $\\Delta $ between the two models. Once you can measure $\\Delta ,$ you can set the noise from what actually happened in this deletion instead of the worst case, and you get an explicit threshold telling you when a deletion is genuinely undetectable. The payoff: a deletion certificate you can run and check, with the noise tuned to the real discrepancy, recovering accuracy that the worst-case approach throws away as p approaches n.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n\n1. Train the model on all the data using the standard noisy gradient-descent unlearning method: take gradient steps with a fixed learning rate, add a small Gaussian (bell-curve) random perturbation at each step with the noise level $\\sigma $ the baseline certificate already uses, and clip the parameters to a bounded region. When a deletion request arrives for one example j, run a few more of these same noisy steps starting from the trained model but with that example's gradient dropped from every batch — this gives the unlearned model $\\theta _{u}.$ To get the reference, retrain the model from scratch without example j at least 200 times with fresh random noise each time, and average the resulting optima to get the retrained reference $\\theta _{r}.$\n   - _Why_: These two models — unlearned vs. retrained-from-scratch — are exactly the pair the certificate is supposed to compare, so we work with the real models, not a worst-case bound.\n2. Test the whole pipeline on ridge and logistic regression with Gaussian-design synthetic data at four ratios of parameters to examples (0.1, 0.5, 0.9, 1.0), across many random deletion choices. Confirm three things: the measured false-alarm rate matches your target $\\alpha ,$ the measured detection power follows the predicted curve, and held-out accuracy is higher using the evidence-tuned noise $\\sigma _{T}$ than the worst-case noise $\\sigma _{D}.$ As a sanity check (negative control), swap in a freshly retrained model in place of the unlearned one for the same deleted example so the true separation is exactly zero — the test should then reject only at rate $\\alpha ,$ and accuracy should return to the level with no deletion at all. If it does not, the test is reacting to an artifact rather than the real difference.\n   - _Why_: It verifies calibration, the predicted power, and the utility gain all depend only on $\\Delta ,$ and the zero-separation control rules out the test keying on artifacts.\n\n### Test construction\n*Turn the deletion certificate into a calibrated likelihood-ratio test whose false-deletion-rate the analyst controls.*\n\n3. At each of the two models, measure how curved the loss surface is around the optimum — its Hessian (matrix of second derivatives) H, which for ridge regression is just $X^{T}X/n$ plus the regularization term, and for logistic regression is the Fisher-information / Generalized-Gauss-Newton (GGN) matrix. Treat each model as a Gaussian (bell-shaped) cloud centered at its own optimum with spread $\\sigma ^{2} H^{-1}$ set jointly by the injected noise $\\sigma $ and the curvature. This gives two competing distributions: one for the retrained model, one for the unlearned model. If the number of parameters is too large to store the full curvature matrix, use a Kronecker-factored or diagonal approximation instead.\n\n*The two competing model laws: under H0 the realized parameter $\\hat{\\theta }$ is Gaussian around the retrain optimum $\\theta _{r},$ under H1 around the unlearn optimum $\\theta _{u},$ both with covariance $\\sigma ^{2} H^{-1}$ set by the injected noise and loss Hessian H.*\n$$ H_0:\\ \\hat\\theta \\sim \\mathcal{N}(\\theta_r,\\ \\sigma^2 H^{-1}), \\qquad H_1:\\ \\hat\\theta \\sim \\mathcal{N}(\\theta_u,\\ \\sigma^2 H^{-1}) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This gives closed-form distributions for both models, which is all you need to compare them with a likelihood ratio.\n4. Build the likelihood-ratio score that compares how well the realized model matches the retrained distribution versus the unlearned distribution; for two Gaussians with the same spread this simplifies to a straight-line (quadratic) function of the model. The algebra collapses the whole high-dimensional comparison down to a single number — the Mahalanobis separation $\\Delta ,$ the distance between the two optima measured in the curvature metric and divided by the noise level $\\sigma .$ From here on, only $\\Delta $ matters.\n\n*The log-likelihood-ratio statistic reduces to a quadratic form in $\\hat{\\theta },$ and the whole test collapses to the single scalar Mahalanobis separation $\\Delta $ between the two optima measured in the Hessian metric and scaled by $\\sigma .$*\n$$ \\Lambda(\\hat\\theta) = \\Big(\\hat\\theta - \\tfrac{\\theta_u+\\theta_r}{2}\\Big)^{\\!\\top} H\\,(\\theta_u-\\theta_r)\\big/\\sigma^2, \\qquad \\Delta = \\lVert \\theta_u-\\theta_r\\rVert_H \\big/ \\sigma \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A high-dimensional comparison reduces to a single sufficient statistic, so the whole test is governed by $\\Delta $ alone and is computable in closed form.\n5. Set the decision cutoff so that the chance of wrongly flagging a genuinely-clean deletion equals your chosen false-alarm rate $\\alpha $ (the false-deletion-rate); because the score's distribution under a clean deletion is a known bell curve fixed entirely by $\\Delta ,$ this cutoff is available in closed form. Read off the resulting detection power $\\beta  = \\Phi (\\Delta  -  z_{1- \\alpha }),$ the probability the test catches a real residual. If the test rejects — meaning the deletion looks incomplete — run more unlearning steps or add more noise before releasing the model.\n\n*Under H0 the statistic is Gaussian with $mean - \\Delta ^{2}/2$ and variance $\\Delta ^{2},$ so calibrating the threshold to type-I error $\\alpha $ fixes the realized power $\\beta $ as $\\Phi (\\Delta  -  z_{1- \\alpha })$; when $\\Delta $ falls below the critical $\\Delta _{c}$ the power equals $\\alpha $ and the deletion is undetectable.*\n$$ \\Lambda \\mid H_0 \\sim \\mathcal{N}\\!\\big(-\\tfrac{\\Delta^2}{2},\\,\\Delta^2\\big), \\qquad \\beta(\\alpha) = \\Phi\\!\\big(\\Delta - z_{1-\\alpha}\\big) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This is what makes the certificate a decision you can run with a controlled error rate, instead of a bound you just trust.\n\n### High-dimensional detectability\n*Characterize when a deletion is provably undetectable as p grows relative to n.*\n\n6. Find the critical separation $\\Delta _{c}$ at which detection power drops to the false-alarm floor — below it, a deletion is statistically impossible to detect. Compute the influence of the deleted point (its loss gradient $g_{j}$ at the optimum, measured in the inverse-curvature metric, via one Cholesky solve), and use the fact that in high dimensions $\\Delta $ concentrates tightly around that influence scaled by $\\surd (p)/(\\sigma \\surd n)$ to derive the smallest noise level $\\sigma _{min}(p,$ n, $\\alpha )$ that pushes the deletion into the undetectable zone. Show the likelihood-ratio test sits exactly at this boundary and beats any scheme that just thresholds a parameter estimate by $a \\surd (log$ p) factor.\n\n*A high-dimensional central-limit argument shows $\\Delta $ concentrates as the deleted example's influence norm scaled by $\\surd (p)/(\\sigma \\surd n)$; inverting $\\Delta (\\sigma ) = \\Delta _{c}$ gives the minimal noise $\\sigma _{min}(p,$ n, $\\alpha )$ above which the deletion is provably undetectable.*\n$$ \\Delta \\;\\approx\\; \\frac{\\lVert g_j\\rVert_{H^{-1}}}{\\sigma}\\,\\sqrt{\\tfrac{1}{n}}\\,\\sqrt{p}\\,, \\qquad \\sigma_{\\min}(p,n,\\alpha): \\ \\Delta(\\sigma)=\\Delta_c(\\alpha) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: It maps exactly which (noise, p, n) regimes make a deletion impossible to detect, which a single worst-case number cannot tell you.\n\n### Evidence-driven noise\n*Set the noise from the realized separation and prove it is strictly below worst-case noise.*\n\n7. Instead of fixing the noise to honor a worst-case difference budget, fix it to honor the test's error rates: choose $\\sigma _{T}$ as the smallest noise level that keeps the actually-measured separation $\\Delta $ inside the undetectable region at false-alarm rate $\\alpha .$ Compare this to the worst-case divergence-calibrated noise $\\sigma _{D}$ used by the baseline, and show — by splitting the needed noise into a part that only controls the false-alarm rate (bounded for everyone) and a part that depends on the real, measured separation — that $\\sigma _{T}$ is strictly smaller whenever the deletion is not the worst case, with the saving growing as the number of parameters approaches the number of examples.\n\n*Calibrating noise to the test's operating characteristic sets $\\sigma _{T}$ from the realized separation, which is strictly below the divergence-calibrated $\\sigma _{D}$ whenever the deletion is not worst case, with the ratio shrinking as p/n approaches 1.*\n$$ \\sigma_T = \\frac{\\lVert \\theta_u-\\theta_r\\rVert_H}{\\Delta_c(\\alpha)} \\;<\\; \\sigma_D, \\qquad \\frac{\\sigma_T}{\\sigma_D}\\downarrow 0 \\ \\text{as}\\ p/n\\to 1 \\tag{5} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Tuning noise to the real discrepancy rather than the worst case provably uses less noise $(\\sigma _{T} < \\sigma _{D})$ and saves accuracy, especially as p approaches n.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 把认证遗忘当作假设检验：高维下的可校准删除\n\n**方法名称.** Likelihood-Ratio Deletion Test (LRDT)\n\n## 研究动机\n当用户要求公司删除自己的数据时，“认证遗忘（certified unlearning）”给出的、类似法律承诺的保证是：你继续提供服务的模型，在统计上应当看起来与一个从头训练、且训练时本就不含该用户数据的模型相同。实现这一承诺最常见的做法把它当作隐私问题：先界定两个模型在最坏情形下能差多少，再向模型注入恰好足够的高斯随机噪声，使这个最坏差异落在预算之内。问题在于，这始终只是一个你必须去“信任”的上界——它从来不是你针对眼前这一次具体删除、在两个真实模型上实际算出来的数字。Langevin Unlearning（一种带噪梯度方法，NeurIPS 2024）以闭式刻画了两个模型分布，却从未把它变成一个可以运行的检验。最近关于高维认证数据移除的工作（arXiv 2025-05）恰恰说明了危害：当参数数 p 接近训练样本数 n 时，最坏情形噪声大到会抹掉模型本应学到的信号。如今新具备的，是一套现成的统计检验工具（隐私约束下可校准的检验）加上那对闭式模型分布——两者结合，让我们能用一个真正的检验取代上界。我们把证书变成一个似然比检验，问“这个模型看起来更像重训练的那个，还是遗忘后的那个？”，把它的误报率设为分析者自选的水平（即 false-deletion-rate），并证明整个高维检验归结为单一数字：两模型间的马氏分离度 $\\Delta $。一旦能测量 $\\Delta $，就能依据这次删除真实发生的情况、而非最坏情形来设定噪声，并得到一个明确阈值，告诉你某次删除何时真正不可检测。收益是：一个可运行、可核查的删除证书，噪声按真实差异调校，在 p 接近 n 时挽回最坏情形方法白白丢弃的精度。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景\n\n1. 用标准的带噪梯度下降(noisy gradient descent)遗忘方法在全部数据上训练模型：以固定学习率做梯度步，每步加入一个小的高斯(钟形分布)随机扰动，噪声水平 $\\sigma $ 取基线证书已用的值，并把参数裁剪到一个有界区域内。当收到对某个样本 j 的删除请求时，从已训练模型出发，再跑几步同样的带噪步，但在每个批次中去掉该样本的梯度——这就得到遗忘后模型 $\\theta _{u}$。为得到参考模型，在不含样本 j 的情况下从头重训练至少 200 次，每次使用全新的随机噪声，再把得到的各个最优点求平均，作为重训练参考 $\\theta _{r}$。\n   - _为什么_: 遗忘后模型与从头重训练模型这一对，正是证书本应比较的对象，所以我们直接对真实模型操作，而非最坏情形上界。\n2. 在使用高斯设计合成数据的 ridge 与 logistic 回归上，于参数与样本数之比为 0.1、0.5、0.9、1.0 四种情形、跨多次随机删除选择，测试整条流程。确认三件事：实测误报率匹配你的目标 $\\alpha $，实测检测功效贴合预测曲线，且使用证据调校噪声 $\\sigma _{T}$ 时的留出精度高于最坏情形噪声 $\\sigma _{D}$。作为对照检查(负对照)，对同一被删样本，用一个新重训练的模型替换遗忘后模型，使真实分离度恰为零——此时检验应仅以 $\\alpha $ 的比率拒绝，且精度应回到完全没有删除时的水平。若并非如此，说明检验在对某种伪信号(而非真实差异)作出反应。\n   - _为什么_: 它验证校准、预测功效与效用增益都只依赖 $\\Delta $，而零分离度对照排除了检验被伪信号牵引的可能。\n\n### 检验构造\n*把删除证书变成一个可校准的似然比检验，其 false-deletion-rate 由分析者控制。*\n\n3. 在这两个模型处，度量损失曲面在最优点附近的弯曲程度——即其 Hessian(二阶导数矩阵) H：对 ridge 回归它就是 $X^{T}X/n$ 加正则项，对 logistic 回归则是 Fisher 信息/广义高斯-牛顿(Generalized-Gauss-Newton, GGN)矩阵。把每个模型视为一个以自身最优点为中心、散度为 $\\sigma ^{2} H^{-1}$ 的高斯(钟形)云团，其散度由注入噪声 $\\sigma $ 与曲率共同决定。由此得到两个相互竞争的分布：一个对应重训练模型，一个对应遗忘后模型。若参数数量过大、无法存储完整曲率矩阵，则改用 Kronecker 分解或对角近似。\n\n*两个相互竞争的模型分布：原假设 H0 下实测参数 $\\hat{\\theta }$ 围绕重训练最优点 $\\theta _{r}$ 服从高斯分布，备择假设 H1 下围绕遗忘最优点 $\\theta _{u}$，二者协方差均为由注入噪声与损失 Hessian H 决定的 $\\sigma ^{2} H^{-1}$。*\n$$ H_0:\\ \\hat\\theta \\sim \\mathcal{N}(\\theta_r,\\ \\sigma^2 H^{-1}), \\qquad H_1:\\ \\hat\\theta \\sim \\mathcal{N}(\\theta_u,\\ \\sigma^2 H^{-1}) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这给出两个模型的闭式分布，而比较它们的似然比所需的正是这些分布。\n4. 构造似然比得分，比较实测模型更符合重训练分布还是遗忘后分布；对两个散度相同的高斯分布，这化简为关于模型的直线(二次)函数。代数运算把整个高维比较坍缩为单一数字——马氏分离度 $\\Delta $，即两最优点在曲率度量下的距离再除以噪声水平 $\\sigma $。从此之后，只有 $\\Delta $ 起作用。\n\n*对数似然比统计量化简为关于 $\\hat{\\theta }$ 的二次型，整个检验坍缩为单一标量——两最优点在 Hessian 度量下、再除以 $\\sigma $ 的马氏分离度 $\\Delta $。*\n$$ \\Lambda(\\hat\\theta) = \\Big(\\hat\\theta - \\tfrac{\\theta_u+\\theta_r}{2}\\Big)^{\\!\\top} H\\,(\\theta_u-\\theta_r)\\big/\\sigma^2, \\qquad \\Delta = \\lVert \\theta_u-\\theta_r\\rVert_H \\big/ \\sigma \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 高维比较归约为单一充分统计量，于是整个检验仅由 $\\Delta $ 决定且可闭式计算。\n5. 设定判决阈值，使误判一次真正干净的删除的概率等于你所选的误报率 $\\alpha ($即 false-deletion-rate)；由于干净删除下该得分的分布是完全由 $\\Delta $ 决定的已知钟形曲线，这个阈值有闭式解。读出由此得到的检测功效 $\\beta  = \\Phi (\\Delta  -  z_{1- \\alpha })$，即检验抓到真实残留的概率。若检验拒绝——意味着删除看起来不完整——则在发布模型前再跑更多遗忘步或加更多噪声。\n\n*在 H0 下统计量服从均值为 $- \\Delta ^{2}/2$、方差为 $\\Delta ^{2}$ 的高斯分布，故把阈值校准到第一类错误 $\\alpha $ 即把实测功效 $\\beta $ 固定为 $\\Phi (\\Delta  -  z_{1- \\alpha })$；当 $\\Delta $ 低于临界值 $\\Delta _{c}$ 时功效等于 $\\alpha $，删除不可检测。*\n$$ \\Lambda \\mid H_0 \\sim \\mathcal{N}\\!\\big(-\\tfrac{\\Delta^2}{2},\\,\\Delta^2\\big), \\qquad \\beta(\\alpha) = \\Phi\\!\\big(\\Delta - z_{1-\\alpha}\\big) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这正是让证书成为一个可运行、错误率可控的决策，而非仅供信任的上界。\n\n### 高维可检测性\n*刻画当 p 相对 n 增大时，删除何时可证不可检测。*\n\n6. 找出检测功效降至误报下限时的临界分离度 $\\Delta _{c}——$低于它，删除在统计上不可能被检测。计算被删点的影响(它在最优点处的损失梯度 $g_{j}$，在逆曲率度量下度量，通过一次 Cholesky 求解得到)，并利用高维下 $\\Delta $ 紧密集中于该影响乘以 $\\surd (p)/(\\sigma \\surd n)$ 这一事实，推导出能把删除推入不可检测区的最小噪声水平 $\\sigma _{min}(p,$ n, $\\alpha )$。证明似然比检验恰好处于这个边界上，并以 $\\surd (log$ p) 的因子优于任何仅对参数估计做阈值判断的方案。\n\n*高维中心极限论证表明 $\\Delta $ 集中于被删样本的影响范数乘以 $\\surd (p)/(\\sigma \\surd n)$；令 $\\Delta (\\sigma ) = \\Delta _{c}$ 反解即得最小噪声 $\\sigma _{min}(p,$ n, $\\alpha )$，高于它删除即可证不可检测。*\n$$ \\Delta \\;\\approx\\; \\frac{\\lVert g_j\\rVert_{H^{-1}}}{\\sigma}\\,\\sqrt{\\tfrac{1}{n}}\\,\\sqrt{p}\\,, \\qquad \\sigma_{\\min}(p,n,\\alpha): \\ \\Delta(\\sigma)=\\Delta_c(\\alpha) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 它精确刻画了哪些（噪声、p、n）区间会让删除无法被检测，而单一最坏情形数字无法告诉你这些。\n\n### 证据驱动的噪声\n*依据实测分离度设定噪声，并证明它严格小于最坏情形噪声。*\n\n7. 不再把噪声固定为满足某个最坏情形差异预算，而是固定为满足检验的错误率：选取 $\\sigma _{T}$ 为能在误报率 $\\alpha $ 下让实测分离度 $\\Delta $ 仍处于不可检测区的最小噪声水平。把它与基线所用的最坏情形、按散度校准的噪声 $\\sigma _{D}$ 比较，并通过把所需噪声拆分为只控制误报率的部分(对所有情形有界)和依赖真实实测分离度的部分，证明：只要删除非最坏情形，$\\sigma _{T}$ 就严格更小，且当参数数量趋近样本数量时这一节省越来越大。\n\n*把噪声校准到检验的操作特性，使 $\\sigma _{T}$ 由实测分离度确定；只要删除非最坏情形，$\\sigma _{T}$ 即严格小于按散度校准的 $\\sigma _{D}$，且当 p/n 趋近 1 时二者之比趋于 0。*\n$$ \\sigma_T = \\frac{\\lVert \\theta_u-\\theta_r\\rVert_H}{\\Delta_c(\\alpha)} \\;<\\; \\sigma_D, \\qquad \\frac{\\sigma_T}{\\sigma_D}\\downarrow 0 \\ \\text{as}\\ p/n\\to 1 \\tag{5} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 按真实差异而非最坏情形调校噪声可证用更少噪声（$\\sigma _{T} < \\sigma _{D}$）并挽回精度，尤其在 p 接近 n 时。\n\n"},{"id":"49","run_dir":"run_prompt49_metamers","index":49,"title":"Active Foveation: Searching Fixations That Make Scene Metamers Indiscriminable","title_zh":"主动注视：搜索使场景 metamer 不可区分的注视点","method_name":"Active Foveation","hook":"MetamerGen takes human fixation locations as fixed external inputs and only checks metamerism afterward; we instead reify the fixation sequence as a learned, instance-conditioned search variable and co-optimize it with a behavioral-discriminability signal, so the model itself selects the few patches whose contents it cannot guess and that therefore most reduce a human's ability to tell the generation from the original.","anchor_pattern_id":"relax_discrete_search_to_continuous","anchor_pattern_name":"Relax Discrete Search to Continuous","domain_category":"Vision Representation & Perception","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes the choice of which scene region to sample (fixate) a quantity the generator itself controls in order to minimize the chance a human can discriminate the generated scene from the original — every leaf consumes externally-supplied fixation locations and treats them as fixed inputs.","pattern_id":"relax_discrete_search_to_continuous","pattern_name":"Relax Discrete Search to Continuous","sub_pattern":"C22 (Relax Discrete Search to Continuous)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by reifying the hand-engineered fixation sequence as a first-class search variable inside one shared-parameter foveation policy that is co-optimized with the generator in a single pass and conditioned on the partially-revealed instance, replacing per-experiment fixed fixations with an amortized instance-to-fixation predictor — the C22 move of unifying discrete design variants into one differentiable/amortized configuration space.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf ties the generator's learning signal to the behavioral same-different (metamer-success) outcome, so none can identify which un-fixated regions are perceptually load-bearing for human scene understanding versus freely fill-able.","pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","sub_pattern":"C26 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by manufacturing a comparative metamer-discriminability reward — minimal-pair (original vs. generation that differ at exactly one candidate region) preference judgments from a discriminator anchored on sparse human same-different responses — and optimizing both the generator and the foveation policy against that preference ordering, so the per-region reward gradient localizes which un-fixated regions are perceptually load-bearing; the C26 move of harvesting an in-distribution comparative ordering and consuming it with a preference objective.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"computational vision / human scene perception modeling (metamer generation)","n_papers":52,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":27},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10},{"source":"openreview","n":2}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":18,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Exploring Differences between Human Perception and Model Inference in Audio Event Recognition"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Qwen2-VL: Enhancing Vision-Language Model's Perception of the World at Any Resolution"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Investigating Bias in LLM-Based Bias Detection: Disparities between LLMs and Human Perception"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Models optimized for real-world tasks reveal the task-dependent necessity of precise temporal coding in hearing"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Pyrfume: A window to the world’s olfactory data"},{"source":"openalex","title":"A spatiotemporal style transfer algorithm for dynamic visual stimulus generation"}],"more":12},{"year":2025,"n":22,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Evaluating Model Alignment with Human Perception: A Study on Shitsukan in LLMs and LVLMs"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Model Metamers Reveal Invariances in Graph Neural Networks"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Human-CLAP: Human-perception-based Contrastive Language-audio Pretraining"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"On measuring the change in historical city centres: an attempt at comparing human perception and deep learning through visual quality of street space"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Operator Stress Perception Model Based on Hidden Semi-Markov Chain for Human-Robot Collaborative Assembly – A Deep Learning Approach"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"What you see is not what you get anymore: a mixed-methods approach on human perception of AI-generated images"}],"more":16},{"year":2026,"n":12,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"},{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Human-Centered Evaluation of an LLM-Based Process Modeling Copilot: A Mixed-Methods Study with Domain Experts"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Generating metamers of human scene understanding"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Understanding Human Perception of Music Plagiarism Through a Computational Approach"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Beyond Input-Output: Rethinking Creativity through Design-by-Analogy in Human-AI Collaboration"}],"more":6}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":28,"share":0.538},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":6,"share":0.115},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":5,"share":0.096},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":4,"share":0.077},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":4,"share":0.077},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":3,"share":0.058},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":3,"share":0.058},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":2,"share":0.038}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"State-of-the-art generators of human-scene-understanding metamers treat the human's information-gathering policy as an external given and metamerism as a property to be checked after the fact, not as a quantity the model is optimized to control. MetamerGen (arxiv:2601.11675v3) fuses foveal DINOv2 tokens at human-chosen fixation locations with a peripheral-gist stream via additive cross-attention, then evaluates whether the resulting scene is judged 'same' by participants in a separate same-different paradigm — the fixation locations come from the experimental design and the generator is never trained against any discriminability outcome. Ensemble-metamer work (semanticscholar:d29630df508b0954675653e4e5c0bd01b0393b07) and the targeted-comparison synthesis line (openalex:W4412460984) likewise match internal activations to a fixed reference and assess human recognizability only after generation, reporting that late-stage metamers are frequently unrecognizable to humans. Across this frontier, no method closes the loop between which scene regions are sampled and whether the resulting generation is behaviorally indiscriminable: because the generator's objective contains no term for the probability that a human would tell the generated scene apart from the original, the model cannot tell which un-fixated regions are perceptually load-bearing, cannot allocate its limited foveal evidence to drive that discriminability down, and cannot say how its metamer-success rate would change if a different region had been sampled.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2601.11675v3","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"MetamerGen adapts Stable Diffusion with two DINOv2-conditioned cross-attention adapters (foveal tokens at human-supplied fixation patches + peripheral tokens from a blurred image) and shows many generations are judged 'same' as the original in a gaze-contingent same-different paradigm. Its method takes fixation locations as fixed external inputs (random masks at train time, experimental design at test time) and trains only on a reconstruction/diffusion objective — it never models which fixation would most reduce a human's ability to discriminate the generation, and never feeds the behavioral same-different outcome back as a learning signal, so it cannot identify the perceptually load-bearing regions or optimize its own metamer-success rate."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:d29630df508b0954675653e4e5c0bd01b0393b07","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Ensemble metamers match activations across a set of CNNs and ViTs to capture a shared invariant subspace and score the results with image-statistics metrics (semantic fidelity, naturalness). The matching target is a fixed natural reference's activations and the evaluation is post-hoc image metrics, not a behavioral discriminability objective, so it has no notion of actively choosing evidence to minimize human distinguishability and no scene-understanding (gist+fixation) structure."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4412460984","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"This synthesis line generates model-optimized stimuli to compare biological and artificial representations and documents that late-stage model metamers are often completely unrecognizable to humans. It frames metamers as a diagnostic of model-vs-human gaps but does not turn the human discriminability outcome into a training target, leaving open how to drive a generator toward stimuli that are provably indiscriminable rather than merely activation-matched."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4405646376","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Spatiotemporal style transfer synthesizes stimuli matching low-level spatiotemporal statistics while stripping high-level semantics, used to probe a predictive-coding network. It enforces a fixed feature-matching constraint by construction and is not representation-matched to a perceptual model nor tied to a behavioral same-different metamer criterion, so it cannot say which sampled evidence makes a scene metameric for human understanding."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"computational vision / human scene perception modeling (metamer generation)","venue":"ICLR/NeurIPS-tier ML","time":"2026","data":["MS-COCO scene images","human free-viewing eye-tracking fixation sequences","same-different behavioral discriminability responses"],"compute":"1×A100 × 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with generative-model + psychophysics-experiment access","preference":"both","baseline":"MetamerGen (arxiv:2601.11675v3) — latent-diffusion foveated scene generator conditioned on DINOv2 foveal+peripheral tokens","limitation":"current metamer generators produce a single passive plausible scene hypothesis from externally-supplied fixations and are validated for metamerism only post-hoc, with no mechanism that decides where to fixate and no training signal tied to behavioral discriminability","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","compute","expertise","preference","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object both legs read from and write to is a per-region perceptual-discriminability reward d(r) — for each scene region r, the probability that a human would judge a generation differing from the original only at r as 'different' — estimated by a discriminator D anchored on a small set of human same-different responses (model-internal readout: D is a learned net; ground truth: sparse behavioral labels). Leg 1 (C22, anchor): we reify the fixation sequence as a search variable. Instead of MetamerGen's externally-fixed fixation mask M_fixation, a foveation policy pi_theta(r_{1:k} | I_revealed) — a small transformer over the current DINOv2 token grid (768-dim, 32x32) that outputs a relaxed (Gumbel-softmax, temperature tau=0.5 annealed to 0.1) distribution over which of the 1024 patches to fixate next, budget k in {1,2,3,5,10} — is co-optimized in ONE pass with the generator's resampler+KV adapters (the only trainable MetamerGen parts), sharing the DINOv2 backbone, rather than a nested search-then-retrain loop. The policy is instance-conditioned: at each step it consumes the tokens revealed so far and predicts the next fixation that maximizes expected reduction in human discriminability, then defers the final fixation set to deployment. Leg 2 (C26, sibling): we manufacture the comparative signal that leg 1 optimizes. Because dense per-region human labels are unavailable, we construct minimal pairs that differ at exactly one candidate region r (same generator, same other fixations) and train D with a pairwise ranking loss to predict which member a human calls 'different', calibrating D's scale to the sparse same-different anchor set so d(r) tracks the human same-different probability rather than an image-statistic. The two legs interlock as a sequential_pipeline: D supplies d(r) (leg 2) -> the policy's objective is sum over un-fixated r of d(r), i.e. fixate the regions the model currently cannot make indiscriminable (leg 1) -> the chosen fixations reveal those regions' true contents to the generator, driving their d(r) down -> the loop's converged d(r) field is the calibrated indiscriminability estimate, and the regions where d(r) stays high under the optimal budget are exactly the perceptually load-bearing ones. The single bridging hyperparameter is beta, weighting the discriminability reward against the diffusion reconstruction loss; the foveation budget k is the user-set evidence cap. Quantitatively, MetamerGen reports FID improving as peripheral scale rises and lambda_foveal=1.2/lambda_peripheral=0.7 (fulltext_cache.json) under a FIXED random fixation policy; we predict that at matched k, actively-selected fixations reach a given metamer rate with strictly fewer fixations than random selection — a regime MetamerGen does not measure because its fixations are not chosen by the model.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery, not separate modules: leg 1 (which region to fixate) is undefined without leg 2's objective (what 'good fixation' means), and leg 2's reward is only useful because leg 1 acts on it — the per-region reward d(r) is the single object both read/write, which is why this is a sequential_pipeline closing one bottleneck rather than two stapled contributions. (b) Considered making leg 2 a generate-and-filter data factory (C08) — rejected because the gap is not corpus coverage but tying the learning signal to the behavioral same-different outcome, which is inherently comparative (a 'same/different' verdict is a preference, not a point label), so C26's comparative-ordering move fits and additionally gives per-region credit assignment. AVOIDED REGRESSION: a generic expected-information-gain fixation policy would land on collateral node c0 (active-vision/ideal-observer), so the policy's objective is the human-behavioral discriminability reward d(r), NOT task-recognition information gain — d(r) is anchored on same-different responses, a source the lineage's metamer line (n0-n5) does not occupy.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: fine-tune the Active-Foveation model on MS-COCO (frozen DINOv2 + SD-1.5, trainable resamplers/KV + foveation policy pi_theta + discriminator D), then run the gaze-contingent same-different behavioral paradigm (or a held-out human same-different test set) comparing model-selected fixations against random and human-recorded fixations at matched fixation budget k in {1,2,3,5}. If the candidate works, the human-judged metamer rate (fraction of generations judged 'same') rises for active fixations versus random at the same k — equivalently, active selection reaches a target metamer rate with strictly fewer fixations — while FID stays at or below MetamerGen's. The named load-bearing variable is the per-region discriminability reward d(r): the mechanism claims the policy works because it fixates the regions of highest current d(r). Negative control: replace d(r) fed to the policy with a permuted/shuffled d(r) field (region identities scrambled, distribution preserved) so the policy still selects k patches under the same budget but on a reward decoupled from true region discriminability; the prediction is that the downstream human-judged metamer rate collapses back toward the random-fixation baseline (the task-outcome metric, not d(r)'s own value), because fixations are now allocated to perceptually irrelevant regions. Positive control: a stripped policy that greedily fixates argmax d(r) with no learned transformer should recover most of the active-selection metamer-rate gain, identifying d(r) as the mechanism's carrier.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2601.11675v3","delta":"MetamerGen conditions a latent diffusion model on DINOv2 foveal tokens at externally-supplied fixations and trains only a diffusion reconstruction objective, validating metamerism post-hoc; we construct a learned instance-conditioned foveation policy that searches the fixation set and a per-region behavioral-discriminability reward d(r) co-optimized with the generator, neither of which MetamerGen builds — so we can select fixations to minimize human discriminability and identify perceptually load-bearing regions."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:d29630df508b0954675653e4e5c0bd01b0393b07","delta":"Ensemble metamers match a fixed reference's activations across architectures and score with image-statistics metrics; we replace the fixed-activation-matching target with a calibrated reward anchored on human same-different responses and actively choose evidence to drive that reward, rather than passively matching activations."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4412460984","delta":"The targeted-comparison synthesis line treats human discriminability as a measured outcome of model-optimized stimuli; we turn that discriminability into a differentiable training target d(r) that both the generator and a fixation-selection policy optimize, converting a diagnostic measurement into an optimization objective."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"arxiv:2601.11675v3","what_step_was_missed":"MetamerGen builds the dual-stream conditioning that turns a fixation set into a generated scene, but to make fixation selection itself a contribution it would have needed to construct (i) a per-region reward calibrated to the human same-different probability and (ii) an instance-conditioned policy whose gradient flows back from that reward through the discrete fixation choice — it builds neither, because its fixations are random at train time and externally fixed at test time and its only objective is diffusion reconstruction, so there is no signal that says one fixation set is more metamerizing than another."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":256,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"No hard-floor fired: gap_closure_reject_check has no candidate_match: yes (aggregate only borderline), recipe_application_check is 'applied' for both entries, and anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null. The single borderline — C22's 'Failing to position against the closest amortization, transfer, and compression neighbors' — hits a non-load-bearing presentation aspect (the active-view-selection neighbors are already distinguished on the right axis in core_mechanism_reasoning and paper_pointed_threat), and paper_pointed_threat found no exact-mechanism collision (MetamerGen lacks both d(r) and the policy). Per the heuristic 'default to advance when only one check is borderline AND it's in a non-load-bearing aspect,' the candidate advances with the neighbor-comparison concern surfaced for Phase 4 reviewer_concerns_and_responses.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes the choice of which scene region to sample (fixate) a quantity the generator itself controls in order to minimize the chance a human can discriminate the generated scene from the original — every leaf consumes externally-supplied fixation locations and treats them as fixed inputs.","main_pattern":"relax_discrete_search_to_continuous","sub_pattern":"C22 (Relax Discrete Search to Continuous)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Reject papers here execute the reification correctly but reach for an off-the-shelf search apparatus (DAG traversal, MDP+DP, RL over a combinatorial action set, supervised instance-to-config regression), so the work reads as a known technique on a new target with no unification/hierarchy-collapse, compounded by thin single-run, toy-scale validation and no positioning against amortization/transfer/compression neighbors.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"If deleting your custom representation leaves a textbook search loop (DAG traversal, MDP plus dynamic programming, RL over an action set), reviewers will score the contribution as a known technique applied to a new target.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Deleting the candidate's representation does not leave a textbook search loop: the fixation policy is relaxed (Gumbel-softmax + straight-through) and co-optimized IN ONE PASS with the generator's adapters sharing the DINOv2 backbone, collapsing the search-then-retrain hierarchy rather than running an outer RL/DP loop over fixed weights."},{"lesson_quoted":"Automating or searching a design artifact is not by itself a contribution; absent a representational or hierarchy-collapsing insight, the work reads as brute-force even when it works.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The hierarchy-collapse (joint structure+weight optimization in a single trajectory) and the representational insight (fixation choice driven by a behavioral-discriminability reward d(r), not info-gain) are the contribution, not the act of automating fixation."},{"lesson_quoted":"Failing to position against the closest amortization, transfer, and compression neighbors leaves the practical advantage unproven, which is fatal even when the core idea is novel.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"differentiation_from_lit positions against MetamerGen and metamer-ensemble lines, but the active-view-selection / foveated-reasoning collision neighbors (amortized next-view predictors) are only implicitly distinguished — a clarifying comparison is warranted but the axis (human-discriminability reward vs task-info-gain) is already stated."},{"lesson_quoted":"Single-run results on toy-scale benchmarks let reviewers dismiss genuine gains as unverified — multi-seed, at-scale validation is the price of entry at a top venue.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Validation is on MS-COCO at MetamerGen scale with a human behavioral same-different paradigm at multiple budgets k, not a toy single-run setup."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf ties the generator's learning signal to the behavioral same-different (metamer-success) outcome, so none can identify which un-fixated regions are perceptually load-bearing for human scene understanding versus freely fill-able.","main_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","sub_pattern":"C26 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The dominant failure is the single-component swap (change one slot of the reward-model->contrastive pipeline and present it as the contribution), or stopping short of the loop (shipping a preference dataset/reward model without the downstream optimization or target-metric transfer), or assembling off-the-shelf parts for a known problem.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Swapping the preference-label source (human → AI judge, offline → online) without showing the swap unlocks a behavior previously unreachable reads as a one-component substitution and draws novelty rejections.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The manufactured per-region reward d(r) is not a label-source swap; it unlocks a previously unreachable behavior — actively selecting fixations to drive human discriminability down and identifying which un-fixated regions are perceptually load-bearing — neither of which MetamerGen or ensemble-metamer work can do."},{"lesson_quoted":"Stopping at the preference dataset, benchmark, or reward model without demonstrating the downstream optimization it is meant to feed leaves the contribution looking like infrastructure rather than method.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"d(r) is consumed by the foveation policy and the generator (loss = reconstruction + beta*sum d(r)) and validated by the downstream human-judged metamer rate, not shipped as a standalone dataset."},{"lesson_quoted":"Changing only the granularity of an established contrastive objective (response-level → step-level) is judged incremental unless paired with a clearly demonstrated practical unlock.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The per-region (vs scene-level) granularity is paired with the practical unlock of localizing perceptually load-bearing regions and steering active fixation, so it is not a bare granularity change."},{"lesson_quoted":"Borrowing a structurally related proxy domain to synthesize preference data, without validating that the proxy's regularities transfer to the target's end-goal metric, invites rigor and generalization concerns.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The preference signal is anchored and Platt-calibrated to actual human same-different responses (the end-goal metric) rather than a proxy domain, so the transfer concern is structurally addressed."}],"verdict":"clear"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The anchor entry (relax_discrete_search_to_continuous / C22) drives the aggregate to borderline via the lesson 'Failing to position against the closest amortization, transfer, and compression neighbors leaves the practical advantage unproven' — the active-view-selection collision neighbors deserve an explicit comparison. The C26 sibling entry is fully clear. No lesson is marked candidate_match: yes, so no hard-floor trigger."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes the choice of which scene region to sample (fixate) a quantity the generator itself controls in order to minimize the chance a human can discriminate the generated scene from the original — every leaf consumes externally-supplied fixation locations and treats them as fixed inputs.","sub_pattern":"C22 (Relax Discrete Search to Continuous)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Reify a previously hand-engineered design artifact as a first-class search variable inside one unified shared-parameter configuration space, share weights across candidates so structure and weights co-optimize in one pass, and make the chosen configuration instance- or context-conditioned (a routing/learned distribution over configs) rather than a single global point.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism Leg 1 + steps 4-7 perform exactly this: the hand-set fixation sequence is reified as a relaxed (Gumbel-softmax, tau annealed) distribution over which patches to fixate, the foveation policy and the generator adapters share the frozen DINOv2 backbone and are co-optimized in ONE joint pass (step 6) rather than a nested loop, and the policy is instance-conditioned on the partially-revealed token grid (step 4), deferring the final fixation set to deployment.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf ties the generator's learning signal to the behavioral same-different (metamer-success) outcome, so none can identify which un-fixated regions are perceptually load-bearing for human scene understanding versus freely fill-able.","sub_pattern":"C26 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Manufacture a comparative/scalar reward from a non-human (or self) source, re-granularize the comparison to where credit assignment fails (a single scalar -> step/region-level), convert noisy absolute scores into reliable relative orderings via a pairwise ranking loss, and optimize the target with a contrastive/preference objective rather than label-fitting.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism Leg 2 + step 2 perform this: minimal pairs that differ at exactly one region are harvested (the comparative source), d(r) is re-granularized from a scene-level same/different verdict to a per-region reward (credit assignment at the failure locus), trained with a pairwise ranking loss, and consumed by a preference-weighted objective (loss includes beta*sum d(r)) rather than plain label-fitting.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries perform their cited cluster's signature move: C22's reify-as-search-variable + one-pass weight-sharing + instance-conditioning is in steps 4-7, and C26's minimal-pair comparative reward + per-region re-granularization + pairwise-ranking-into-preference-objective is in Leg 2 / step 2. Neither reduces to its parent's generic gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["relax_discrete_search_to_continuous","self_supervised_signal_engineering"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; the candidate's composition set {relax_discrete_search_to_continuous, self_supervised_signal_engineering} contains no heterogeneous_decomposition, so no anti-pattern matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"arxiv:2601.11675v3","threat_source":"lit_table","subsumption_argument":"MetamerGen is the most specific competitor: it already generates scene-understanding metamers from foveal+peripheral DINOv2 conditioning and validates them in a same-different paradigm, so the candidate's claim stands or falls on whether SELECTING fixations (rather than consuming fixed ones) plus a behavioral-discriminability reward yields a measurable metamer-rate gain at matched budget. It does not subsume the candidate because MetamerGen's fixations are random at train time and externally fixed at test time and its only objective is diffusion reconstruction — it constructs neither the per-region reward d(r) calibrated to human same-different nor the instance-conditioned foveation policy, which are exactly the candidate's load-bearing artifacts. The active-view-selection / foveated-reasoning collision neighbors (VG-AVS, Foveated Reasoner) select next views but to improve a VLM task/reasoning objective (information gain), not to minimize human behavioral discriminability for metamer generation, so they are collateral (the c0 active-vision family), not subsumers.","addressable_via":"Tighten differentiation_from_lit / reviewer_concerns to explicitly contrast the active-view-selection neighbors' task-information-gain objective against the candidate's human-discriminability reward; the core mechanism need not change."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Active Foveation: Searching Fixations That Make Scene Metamers Indiscriminable\n\n**Method.** Active Foveation\n\n## Motivation\nTo make a 'metamer' of human scene understanding means generating a scene a person cannot tell apart from a real one, given only the few spots they happen to look at. The leading system, MetamerGen (a foveated scene generator built on a latent diffusion model), is handed the look-at locations from outside — random during training, set by the experiment at test time — and is trained only to reconstruct the image. Whether a human can actually tell the result apart is checked afterward, never used to teach the model. So MetamerGen can neither decide where a viewer should look to be most fooled, nor figure out which un-looked-at regions secretly carry the scene's meaning.\n\nThis is timely because MetamerGen just proved such generators can fool people in a controlled look-and-judge test, and the tools to make 'where to look' a trainable choice — a differentiable way to pick discrete patches (Gumbel-softmax with straight-through gradients) plus lightweight adapter training on a frozen backbone — are now cheap enough to run on a single accelerator.\n\nPrior work stopped short for a concrete reason: MetamerGen has no per-region score of how distinguishable its output is and no way to push gradients back through a discrete look-at choice; ensemble-metamer work matches fixed internal activations and scores with image statistics; and the targeted-comparison line treats human distinguishability as something to measure, not to optimize.\n\nIf we close this gap, the generator can actively choose its fixations to be maximally fooling and, as a by-product, produce a map of which scene regions are perceptually load-bearing for human understanding — turning a pass/fail metamer check into a thing the model optimizes.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n\n1. Start from MetamerGen's frozen vision backbone (DINOv2-Base) and frozen image generator (Stable-Diffusion-1.5 UNet); only the two small adapters that mix in fixation information (the foveal and peripheral Perceiver resamplers) and the generator's key/value projection layers are trainable. For each looked-at patch, feed its backbone token through the foveal adapter, and feed a blurred whole-image stream through the peripheral adapter, exactly as MetamerGen does. The input is a Microsoft COCO scene image plus a set of look-at locations; the output is the generated scene built from the revealed high-resolution information.\n   - _Why_: Freezing the generator means any gain must come from smarter fixations and the new reward, not extra capacity.\n\n### Discriminability Reward\n*Manufactures a per-region, behaviorally-calibrated reward d(r) that scores how distinguishable each region's content is to a human.*\n\n2. Build a small Vision Transformer (ViT) judge D that, for every region of the 32x32 grid, reads the original patch's and the generated patch's backbone tokens side by side and outputs a score for that region. Make training examples as minimal pairs: generate one scene, then regenerate changing the content of exactly one region while keeping everything else fixed, so the only difference is at that region. Train D with a ranking loss using sparse human 'same or different?' answers so it learns to rank a region a human calls 'different' above one called 'same'; regions without a direct human answer borrow the whole-scene verdict as a weak label. Finally rescale D's score (Platt scaling) on a set-aside slice of human answers so it reads as the probability a human would call a one-region change 'different'. 【author decision: how large the set-aside human-answer slice is, and how many human answers are enough to calibrate, is the authors' call — the trade-off is collecting more human data versus tighter calibration.】\n\n*The per-region reward d(r) is the Platt-calibrated (scale a, bias b) discriminator score $s_\\phi (r)$ squashed by the logistic $\\sigma $ into the probability that a human calls a one-region edit 'different'.*\n$$ d(r) = \\sigma\\!\\left(a\\, s_\\phi(r) + b\\right) \\approx \\Pr\\big[\\text{human judges 'different' at } r\\big] \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Dense per-region human labels do not exist, so a calibrated comparative reward is manufactured from cheap minimal-pair preferences.\n3. Lower the Gumbel-softmax temperature $\\tau $ smoothly from 0.5 to 0.1 over the first 60% of training, then hold it at 0.1, so the policy moves from soft, blended picks to genuinely discrete ones. Once per epoch, rebuild the judge D's minimal-pair examples from the current (improved) generator and re-fit its ranking head, and redo the score-to-probability rescaling whenever fresh human 'same or different?' answers come in.\n   - _Why_: Annealing makes fixation selection genuinely discrete at the end, and refreshing keeps the reward honest as the generator improves.\n\n### Active Foveation Policy\n*Makes the fixation sequence a differentiable, instance-conditioned search variable that chooses where to look.*\n\n4. Swap MetamerGen's fixed look-at mask for a 4-layer transformer policy $\\pi _\\theta $ that reads the whole 32x32 grid: already-looked-at cells hold their sharp backbone token, not-yet-looked cells hold the blurred token plus a learned 'not revealed yet' marker. A learned query summarizes the grid and a linear layer scores all 1024 cells as candidates for the next look, blocking cells already chosen. Pick the next look-at cell using a Gumbel-softmax (a differentiable stand-in for a hard pick, so the policy can be trained by gradients) with a temperature setting and straight-through gradients, repeating k times; after each pick, replace that cell's blurred token with its sharp version and re-read the grid before the next pick.\n\n*At each step t the next fixation $r_{t}$ is drawn from a Gumbel-softmax relaxation (temperature $\\tau $ annealed $0.5 \\to $ 0.1) of the policy $\\pi _\\theta $ conditioned on the tokens revealed so far, with straight-through gradients.*\n$$ r_t \\sim \\mathrm{GumbelSoftmax}\\big(\\pi_\\theta(\\cdot \\mid I_{\\mathrm{revealed}}^{<t}); \\tau\\big), \\quad \\tau: 0.5 \\rightarrow 0.1 \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Making 'where to look' a differentiable, instance-conditioned choice lets the model learn to look where it currently cannot fool the viewer.\n5. Convert each soft choice into an actual 'reveal this patch' action using a straight-through trick: on the forward pass take the single best (hard) patch and grab its sharp token, but on the backward pass use the soft selection weights so the policy still receives a learning signal. Choose a budget k from {1,2,3,5,10}, run the policy for k steps, and feed those k sharp tokens (in place of the corresponding blurred tokens) into the foveal adapter before generating.\n   - _Why_: Different fixations feed different evidence to the generator, which is exactly the knob the policy is learning to set.\n\n### Joint Co-optimization\n*Trains where-to-look and how-to-fill together in one pass against reconstruction plus the discriminability reward.*\n\n6. Train everything together in a single pass: minimize the image reconstruction loss plus a weight $\\beta $ times the sum, over all not-looked-at grid cells, of each cell's per-region discriminability score, sending gradients into both the generator's adapters and the look-at policy (using the straight-through path for the discrete picks). The regions are the 32x32 grid cells, and the reward sums over the 1024 minus k cells that were not looked at. Set $\\beta $ so the reward part and the reconstruction part start with comparable gradient sizes, then keep it fixed. 【author decision: whether a single fixed $\\beta $ is enough, or a changing schedule is needed so the discriminability signal keeps biting, is the authors' call — the trade-off is the stability of a constant weight versus an adaptive one.】\n\n*The joint objective adds the diffusion reconstruction loss to $\\beta $ times the summed reward over un-fixated regions, so minimizing it pushes the policy to fixate the regions of highest current d(r).*\n$$ \\mathcal{L} = \\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{recon}} + \\beta \\sum_{r \\notin \\mathcal{F}_k} d(r) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Optimizing where to look and how to fill together, in one loop, avoids a slow search-then-retrain cycle and ties fixation choice directly to human discriminability.\n\n### Active-Metamer Evaluation\n*Tests active vs random/human fixations at matched budget and reads off the load-bearing-region map.*\n\n7. At test time, let the policy greedily pick its k look-at cells under the deployment budget and generate the scene. For each test image and each k, compare three conditions that all use the SAME number of looks: policy-chosen (active), randomly chosen, and the person's own first k recorded free-viewing looks. Run the look-contingent 'same or different?' test and report the metamer rate (how often people say 'same'), the image-quality score FID, and the final per-region discriminability map; regions that stay hardest to fool under the best budget are reported as the perceptually load-bearing ones. 【author decision: the cutoff (e.g. top tenth) for calling a region load-bearing is the authors' reporting choice — the trade-off is catching more such regions versus only the clearest ones.】\n   - _Why_: This is the actual test: fewer active fixations should fool people as well as more random ones, and regions where d(r) stays high are the load-bearing ones.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 主动注视：搜索使场景 metamer 不可区分的注视点\n\n**方法名称.** Active Foveation\n\n## 研究动机\n做出人类场景理解的 metamer，意思是：在人只看少数几个落点的情况下，生成一张他分辨不出真假的场景图。目前最强的系统 MetamerGen（一个基于 latent diffusion model 的注视式场景生成器）的注视落点是外部给定的——训练时随机、测试时由实验设定——而它只被训练去重建图像。结果是否真能骗过人，只在事后检验，从不回传去教模型。因此 MetamerGen 既不能决定让观看者看哪里最容易被骗，也无法判断哪些没被看到的区域其实承载了场景的含义。\n\n现在正是时候：MetamerGen 刚证明这类生成器能在受控的'看一眼再判断'测试中骗过人；而把'看哪里'变成可训练选择所需的工具——对离散 patch 的可微选择（Gumbel-softmax 加 straight-through 梯度）以及在冻结骨干上训练轻量 adapter——如今已便宜到能在单卡上跑。\n\n前人止步的原因很具体：MetamerGen 没有衡量每个区域可区分程度的分数，也无法把梯度穿过离散的注视选择；ensemble metamer 工作匹配的是固定的内部激活并用图像统计量打分；targeted-comparison 这一脉则把人类可区分性当作要测量的量，而非要优化的目标。\n\n一旦补上这道缺口，生成器就能主动选择最具迷惑性的注视点，并顺带产出一张图：哪些场景区域对人类理解是perceptually load-bearing（感知上承重）的——把一个通过/不通过的 metamer 检验，变成模型去优化的目标。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景\n\n1. 从 MetamerGen 的冻结视觉骨干(DINOv2-Base)和冻结图像生成器(Stable-Diffusion-1.5 UNet)出发；只有两个混入注视信息的小 adapter(foveal 与 peripheral Perceiver resampler)以及生成器的 key/value 投影层是可训练的。对每个被看到的 patch，把它的骨干 token 经 foveal adapter 输入，并把一路模糊的整图经 peripheral adapter 输入，与 MetamerGen 完全一致。输入是一张 Microsoft COCO 场景图像加一组注视落点，输出是由已揭示的高分辨率信息生成的场景。\n   - _为什么_: 冻结生成器意味着任何提升都只能来自更聪明的注视和新奖励，而非额外容量。\n\n### 可区分性奖励\n*制造一个逐区域、经行为校准的奖励 d(r)，衡量每个区域内容对人类的可区分程度。*\n\n2. 构建一个小型 Vision Transformer(ViT)裁判 D：对 32x32 网格的每个区域，并排读取原图 patch 与生成 patch 的骨干 token，并输出该区域的一个分数。训练样本做成 minimal pair：先生成一张场景，再只改动其中一个区域的内容、其余全部固定地重新生成，使唯一差异就在该区域。用 ranking loss 配合稀疏的人类'相同还是不同?'回答来训练 D，让它学会把人类判为'不同'的区域排在判为'相同'的区域之上；没有直接人类回答的区域，则借用整张场景的判定作为弱标签。最后在一份预留的人类回答切片上对 D 的分数做 Platt scaling 重标定，使其读作'人类把某个单区域改动判为不同'的概率。【作者需决定：预留的人类回答切片有多大、需要多少人类回答才足以标定，由作者拍板——权衡是采集更多人类数据还是更紧的标定。】\n\n*每区域奖励 d(r) 是判别器分数 $s_\\phi (r)$ 经 Platt 校准（尺度 a、偏置 b）后由 logistic $\\sigma $ 压成的概率，表示人类把仅在该区域改动的场景判为'不同'的可能性。*\n$$ d(r) = \\sigma\\!\\left(a\\, s_\\phi(r) + b\\right) \\approx \\Pr\\big[\\text{human judges 'different' at } r\\big] \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 逐区域的密集人类标签并不存在，所以从廉价的 minimal-pair 偏好里制造出一个校准过的比较型奖励。\n3. 把 Gumbel-softmax 温度 $\\tau $ 在前 60% 训练里从 0.5 平滑降到 0.1，之后固定在 0.1，使策略从软的混合选择过渡到真正离散的选择。每个 epoch 用当前(已变好的)生成器重建裁判 D 的 minimal-pair 样本并重训其 ranking head；每当有新的人类'相同还是不同?'回答进来，就重做一次分数到概率的重标定。\n   - _为什么_: 退火让最终的注视选择真正离散；刷新让奖励随生成器变好而保持可靠。\n\n### 主动注视策略\n*把注视序列变成可微、随实例条件化的搜索变量，决定看哪里。*\n\n4. 把 MetamerGen 的固定注视掩码换成一个 4 层 transformer 策略 $\\pi _\\theta $，它读取整个 32x32 网格：已看过的格子放其清晰骨干 token，尚未看的格子放模糊 token 加一个可学习的'尚未揭示'标记。一个可学习的 query 概括整张网格，一个线性层为全部 1024 个格子打分作为下一次注视的候选，并屏蔽已选过的格子。用 Gumbel-softmax(对'硬选择'的可微替代，使策略可由梯度训练)配合一个温度设置与 straight-through 梯度来选取下一个注视格子，重复 k 次；每选一次，就把该格子的模糊 token 换成清晰版本，并在下次选取前重新读一遍网格。\n\n*每一步 t 的下一个注视 $r_{t}$ 由策略 $\\pi _\\theta $（条件于已揭示的 token）的 Gumbel-softmax 松弛采样得到，温度 $\\tau $ 从 0.5 退火到 0.1，并用 straight-through 传梯度。*\n$$ r_t \\sim \\mathrm{GumbelSoftmax}\\big(\\pi_\\theta(\\cdot \\mid I_{\\mathrm{revealed}}^{<t}); \\tau\\big), \\quad \\tau: 0.5 \\rightarrow 0.1 \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 把'看哪里'变成可微、随实例条件化的选择，模型就能学会去看当前还骗不过观看者的地方。\n5. 用 straight-through 技巧把每次软选择变成真正的'揭示该 patch'动作：前向传播取单个最佳(硬)patch 并抓取其清晰 token，反向传播则用软选择权重，使策略仍能得到学习信号。从 ${1,2,3,5,10}$ 中选一个预算 k，让策略跑 k 步，再把这 k 个清晰 token(替换掉对应的模糊 token)在生成前喂进 foveal adapter。\n   - _为什么_: 不同注视给生成器不同的证据，而这正是策略要学着去调的旋钮。\n\n### 联合协同优化\n*在一次训练中同时优化'看哪里'与'怎么填'，目标为重建加可区分性奖励。*\n\n6. 把所有部件放进一次训练同时优化：最小化图像重建损失，加上权重 $\\beta $ 乘以(所有未看格子上每格的逐区域可区分性分数之和)，梯度同时送入生成器 adapter 和注视策略(离散选择走 straight-through 通路)。区域就是 32x32 的网格格子，奖励对未被看到的 1024 减 k 个格子求和。把 $\\beta $ 设到使奖励项与重建项初始梯度规模相当，然后固定不变。【作者需决定：单一固定 $\\beta $ 是否足够，还是需要一个变化的 schedule 来让可区分性信号持续起作用，由作者拍板——权衡是常数权重的稳定性还是自适应权重。】\n\n*联合目标在扩散重建损失之外，加上 $\\beta $ 乘以未注视区域上 d(r) 之和；最小化它会驱动策略去注视当前 d(r) 最高的区域。*\n$$ \\mathcal{L} = \\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{recon}} + \\beta \\sum_{r \\notin \\mathcal{F}_k} d(r) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 把'看哪里'和'怎么填'放进一个循环里同时优化，避免缓慢的搜索-再训练循环，并把注视选择直接与人类可区分性挂钩。\n\n### 主动 metamer 评估\n*在相同预算下比较主动与随机/人类注视，并读出承重区域图。*\n\n7. 测试时让策略在部署预算下贪心选出它的 k 个注视格子并生成场景。对每张测试图与每个 k，比较三种使用相同注视次数的条件：策略选(主动)、随机选、以及该人自己最先记录的 k 次自由观看注视。跑'看一眼再判断相同还是不同?'测试，报告 metamer 率(人们说'相同'的频率)、图像质量分 FID、以及最终的逐区域可区分性图；在最优预算下仍最难被骗过的区域，被报告为 perceptually load-bearing(感知上承重)的区域。【作者需决定：把某区域判为承重的阈值(例如最高十分位)是作者的报告选择——权衡是多抓到这类区域还是只取最明确的。】\n   - _为什么_: 这才是真正的检验：更少的主动注视应当与更多的随机注视一样能骗过人，而 d(r) 保持高的区域就是承重区域。\n\n"},{"id":"50","run_dir":"run_prompt50_humangeom","index":50,"title":"Transport-Cost-Shaped Source Priors for Generative Human Geometry","title_zh":"为生成式人体几何分布设计运输代价塑形的源先验","method_name":"Transport-Cost-Shaped Source Prior (TCSP)","hook":"The fixed SMPL-template source of state-of-the-art human geometry-distribution flows forces the longest, most many-to-one transport in exactly the loose and wrinkled garment regions whose fidelity reviewers judge — and patches it with one global isotropic noise band. We make the flow's source prior a measured, per-region anisotropic object whose local covariance is set by the surface region's own transport cost, and show a matched-source ablation that the fixed source, not network capacity, was the binding constraint on high-frequency-region geometry.","anchor_pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","anchor_pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","domain_category":"3D Vision & Scene Reconstruction","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf produces a per-region quantity that says which surface regions are poorly served by the chosen fixed source prior (SMPL template) BEFORE/DURING generation — so the high-variance many-to-one transport in loose/wrinkled garment regions is patched with one global isotropic perturbation rather than treated as a measurable, region-varying property the generator can act on (additive; sits at the anchor's residual_problem that the SMPL->surface transport cost is fixed and unm","pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","sub_pattern":"C23 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by reaching inside the flow-matching chain and re-specifying its conventionally-frozen source/forward-kernel: the isotropic-perturbation SMPL-template source is replaced by a transport-cost-shaped anisotropic source whose per-region covariance is set by a measured transport-cost field tau(r), and the flow objective is re-derived around it so the high-cost regions get a source matched to their local geometry rather than a global noise band.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf questions whether the SOURCE distribution of the surface-displacement flow must be the SMPL template shape at all, rather than asking whether a different, geometry-aware transport origin would shorten the worst-region transport — every clothed-human flow/diffusion leaf inherits a single fixed, pose-shape-conditioned source/template assumption from the shared parametric-template ancestor without testing its necessity (subtractive; the shared inherited assumption read of","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","how_closed":"Framing move (C01): relocate the representational LOCUS at which surface fidelity is presumed enforced from the network's denoising capacity to the flow's SOURCE distribution, stating the falsifiable claim that the fixed SMPL-template source is the binding constraint in high-tau(r) regions. Companion deliverable (controlled_diagnostic_design): a matched-source ablation set that holds target geometry, pose, SMPL conditioning, network architecture, training data and compute fixed and varies ONLY the source prior (isotropic-SMPL vs transport-cost-shaped vs an oracle nearest-target source), reporting the de-confounded high-tau-region fidelity gap as the headline that confirms the source, not estimator quality, carried the limit.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"generative 3D human body/clothed-geometry modeling (surface point/displacement distributions)","n_papers":31,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":27},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":20,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Volumetric Imitation Generative Adversarial Networks for Anatomical Human Body Modeling"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A review of human cornea finite element modeling: geometry modeling, constitutive modeling, and outlooks"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"MODELING IN DOSIMETRY AND BIODOSIMETRY, IS THERE ENOUGH KNOWLEDGE ABOUT THE STRUCTURE OF THE HUMAN BODY?"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Magnetotherapy Modeling using a Simplified and Anatomical Human Body Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"ParaHome: Parameterizing Everyday Home Activities Towards 3D Generative Modeling of Human-Object Interactions"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Multi-Resolution Generative Modeling of Human Motion from Limited Data"}],"more":14},{"year":2025,"n":22,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Generative Human Geometry Distribution"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"SimGenHOI: Physically Realistic Whole-Body Humanoid-Object Interaction via Generative Modeling and Reinforcement Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Real-Time Body Modeling and Clothing Adaptation Based on Generative Adversarial Network"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Generative Modeling of Shape-Dependent Self-Contact Human Poses"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Compressing Human Body Video with Interactive Semantics: A Generative Approach"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"DiffBody: Human Body Image Restoration with Generative Diffusion Prior"}],"more":16},{"year":2026,"n":9,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Human-Centered Evaluation of an LLM-Based Process Modeling Copilot: A Mixed-Methods Study with Domain Experts"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Beyond Input-Output: Rethinking Creativity through Design-by-Analogy in Human-AI Collaboration"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"SAM 3D Body: Robust Full-Body Human Mesh Recovery"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Face versus Body Tracking for Human-Robot Interaction: An Egocentric Dataset"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Geometry of Neighborhoods of Minimal Rational Curves"}],"more":3}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":16,"share":0.516},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":10,"share":0.323},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":9,"share":0.29},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":6,"share":0.194},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":6,"share":0.194},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":5,"share":0.161},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":4,"share":0.129},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":3,"share":0.097}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"State-of-the-art dataset-scale generative human-geometry models learn a flow from a fixed parametric source (the SMPL template shape distribution) to clothed-body surface points, encode each per-subject flow into a 2D feature map, and train a second flow over those feature maps (semanticscholar:5bc97f57b3786552e41625008fd5cfe34b2ab213); related clothed-human generators (openalex:W4402703079 SCULPT, openalex:W4410435545 HumanLiff) likewise condition a learned surface/displacement distribution on a coarse pose+shape code. The shared failure is that the transport ORIGIN and the per-region difficulty of the SMPL->surface displacement field are treated as fixed and unmodeled: the nearest-SMPL-point training-pair construction collapses many distinct surface points (loose/wrinkled regions) onto one template point and is patched with isotropic Gaussian perturbation, so in exactly the high-frequency garment regions the user cares about, the flow must cover a long, high-variance, many-to-one transport whose cost the model neither measures nor adapts to; and because the feature map entangles identity, garment, and pose-driven deformation into one opaque code, the model cannot say how much of a generated surface's variance is body shape versus garment versus pose, nor resample any one factor while holding the others fixed. The result is that fidelity and controllability both degrade precisely where transport is hardest and most entangled, and no retrieved paper produces a quantity that tells you, before or during generation, which surface regions are under-served by the chosen source prior.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:5bc97f57b3786552e41625008fd5cfe34b2ab213","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Generative Human Geometry Distribution replaces the Gaussian source of single-shape geometry distributions with the SMPL template distribution, builds training pairs by nearest-SMPL-point matching with isotropic Gaussian perturbation, normalizes to a zero-centered displacement field conditioned on the matched template point, encodes each per-subject flow into a 2D feature map, and trains a second latent flow over the maps. Its residue: the method fixes the source prior and the nearest-neighbor pairing a priori and never measures the resulting per-region transport cost, so loose/wrinkled regions (where many surface points collapse onto one template point) get only an isotropic-noise band-aid rather than a source prior shaped to the local geometry; and the per-subject feature map is a single entangled code, so the learned distribution cannot factor or independently resample identity vs garment vs pose-dependent deformation.","year_month":"2025-03"},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4402703079","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"SCULPT learns a clothed-and-textured human mesh distribution from medium 3D scans plus large 2D image collections via unpaired learning, conditioning geometry+appearance on a coarse shape+pose code. It does not model body-garment interaction physics or per-region deformation difficulty; the conditioning is a low-dimensional global code, so it cannot localize where the garment-vs-body transport is hard or resample garment deformation independently of identity.","year_month":"2024-06"},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4410435545","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"HumanLiff generates layered 3D humans by adding clothing layers sequentially with conditional tri-plane diffusion, giving a coarse body/clothing separation. The layering is a fixed sequential schedule, not a measured factorization, and body-clothing interaction (contact, wrinkle response to pose) is not explicitly modeled, so it cannot tell which layers/regions carry the high-frequency variance the generator struggles with.","year_month":"2025-05"},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4402704709","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"DiffSurf is a transformer diffusion over vertex+normal tokens that generates 3D surfaces (bodies, hands, objects) on a fixed-topology template. Operating on a fixed template vertex set, it has no mechanism for fine clothing detail or for a source-prior whose informativeness varies by surface region; the difficulty of generating high-frequency regions is left implicit in the noise schedule rather than measured per region.","year_month":"2024-08"}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"generative 3D human body/clothed-geometry modeling (surface point/displacement distributions)","venue":"ICLR/CVPR/NeurIPS tier (top vision-generative)","time":"2026","data":["CAPE / THuman / 4D-DRESS-style clothed-human scan sets","SMPL/SMPL-X parametric template","X-Humans / multi-subject clothed scans"],"compute":"1×A100 × 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with generative-modeling + 3D vision background","preference":"both","baseline":"Generative Human Geometry Distribution (semanticscholar:5bc97f57b3786552e41625008fd5cfe34b2ab213); secondary: SCULPT, HumanLiff, DiffSurf","limitation":"current dataset-scale human-geometry distribution learns a black-box SMPL->surface displacement flow per subject and a second flow over feature maps, with no characterization of WHEN the SMPL-template source prior is a good vs bad transport origin, and no explicit factorization of identity/garment/pose-dependent deformation in the learned distribution","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object both legs read from and write to is the SOURCE distribution Phi_S of the SMPL-template-to-surface displacement flow (the prior the flow-matching velocity field u_theta transports to the clothed-body surface). LEG 1 (anchor, C23) liberates this source. We first define a per-region transport-cost field tau(r): for each cell r of a fixed SMPL-UV chart partition (the standard SMPL UV atlas, ~24 body parts further binned to a 64x64 UV grid = the chart partition; fixed across all subjects), tau(r) is the training-set mean over matched pairs of two computed quantities combined by a named weight lambda (default lambda=1.0, a hyperparameter scaling the unitless fan-in into the metric displacement's units): (i) the displacement magnitude ||x1 - x0'||_2 in meters, where x0' is the nearest SMPL-template point to target surface point x1 (both already computed inside the anchor paper's training-pair construction), and (ii) the many-to-one collapse count fan(r) = number of distinct target points x1 mapped to the same template point x0', normalized to [0,1] over the chart. tau(r) is thus computed from data the pipeline already materializes, requires no model-internal readout, and is fixed before training. The conventionally-frozen component we re-specify is the source perturbation: the anchor paper uses a single global isotropic N(0, sigma=1) added to x0'; we replace it with a transport-cost-shaped anisotropic source N(0, Sigma(r)) where Sigma(r) = sigma_0^2 * (1 + alpha*tau_hat(r)) * P(r), tau_hat(r) is tau(r) min-max normalized to [0,1], alpha is a spread-gain hyperparameter (default alpha=3.0), sigma_0=1.0 matches the baseline's scale so low-tau cells are byte-identical to baseline, and P(r) is the local anisotropy frame: a rank-2 covariance aligned to the surface tangent plane at x0' (its two tangent eigenvalues scaled by (1+alpha*tau_hat(r)), the normal eigenvalue held at sigma_0^2), so high-cost loose/wrinkled cells get a wider, surface-tangent-spread source that shortens the worst many-to-one transport instead of a global noise band. We re-derive the flow-matching objective around this source: the displacement target becomes Delta_x = x1 - x0' as before, but the noise sample n is drawn from N(0, Sigma(r)) and the regression target is (Delta_x - n) conditioned on x0' AND on tau_hat(r) injected as an extra scalar channel of the hidden-feature conditioning, so the velocity field knows the local cost. This is the runnable method deliverable. LEG 2 (sibling, C01 framing + controlled_diagnostic_design companion) audits whether Phi_S had to be the fixed SMPL-template source at all. The C01 move relocates the fidelity-enforcement LOCUS from the denoiser to the source: the falsifiable proposition is 'in high-tau(r) cells the fixed isotropic-SMPL source, not the network, caps achievable fidelity.' The companion ships the confound-isolating instrument: a matched-source ablation set in which target geometry, SMPL pose/shape conditioning, the velocity network's architecture and weights' init, training data, and compute are all held fixed, and ONLY Phi_S is swapped across {isotropic-SMPL (baseline), transport-cost-shaped (ours), oracle-nearest-target (an upper bound that sets x0' to the true nearest surface point with zero spread)}; the oracle provides a system-independent ground-truth ceiling so the measured isotropic-vs-shaped gap in high-tau cells is attributable to the source choice alone. The two legs interlock because LEG 2's ablation is exactly the experiment that proves LEG 1's redesigned source was necessary rather than decorative: same object Phi_S, one constructs it, the other isolates its causal effect.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The two gaps share machinery because they both act on one object, the flow's source distribution Phi_S: the anchor constructs a better Phi_S and the audit proves the old Phi_S was the binding constraint, so a single matched-source ablation validates the construction rather than needing a separate module — that is why shared_object, not two stapled contributions. I considered making tau(r) a learned, model-internal uncertainty readout (a second network head), but rejected it: it would re-introduce an opaque learned code (the very entanglement the bottleneck flags) and make the negative control tautological, so tau(r) is kept a data-computed, pre-training, inspectable quantity. REGRESSION CHECK: the avoided node is c1 in method_lineage (generic OT / Schrodinger-bridge learned couplings) — we do NOT learn a data-dependent coupling by solving a transport program; tau(r) is a fixed measured statistic and Sigma(r) is a closed-form anisotropic reshape, so the mechanism draws on a tree node (measured-per-region-cost-shaped source) that c1's general-purpose coupling family does not occupy, and we avoid c2 (generic factorized latents) by not factoring the code at all.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on a standard clothed-human scan benchmark (e.g. CAPE or 4D-DRESS) train the anchor paper's two-stage human geometry-distribution model twice with identical data, seeds, architecture and compute, differing ONLY in the flow's source prior (isotropic-SMPL baseline vs our transport-cost-shaped anisotropic source), and measure Chamfer distance and normal-consistency on surface cells stratified into high-transport-cost vs low-transport-cost partitions. If the candidate works, Chamfer distance and normal error in the high-transport-cost partition (loose/wrinkled garment cells) decrease relative to baseline while the low-cost partition stays within noise, and overall geometry quality improves consistent with the anchor paper's reported 57% geometry-quality gain regime (semanticscholar:5bc97f57b3786552e41625008fd5cfe34b2ab213) without that figure being our target. The named load-bearing variable is the per-region transport-cost field tau(r) that shapes the source covariance Sigma(r); negative control: overwrite tau_hat(r) with its dataset-mean constant (collapsing Sigma(r) to the global isotropic baseline and zeroing the tau conditioning channel) and predict the high-cost-partition Chamfer/normal error regresses back to the isotropic baseline — if fidelity stays improved after this control, the gain came from the added conditioning channel's capacity or training noise, not from cost-shaped transport, and the mechanism claim is falsified. Positive control: a stripped model that applies only the tau-shaped anisotropic source with no tau conditioning channel should recover most of the high-cost-partition improvement, identifying the cost-shaped source spread as the mechanism.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:5bc97f57b3786552e41625008fd5cfe34b2ab213","delta":"They replaced the Gaussian source with the SMPL-template distribution and added a single global isotropic perturbation N(0,sigma=1) to handle many-to-one collapse in loose regions; we measure a per-region transport-cost field tau(r) from their own training pairs and construct a region-varying anisotropic source N(0,Sigma(r)) plus a matched-source ablation isolating that the fixed source (not the network) caps high-cost-region fidelity, neither of which their construction produces."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4402703079","delta":"SCULPT learns a clothed-mesh geometry+appearance distribution conditioned on a coarse global shape+pose code from unpaired 3D+2D data; we do not add a global conditioning code but reshape the generative process's source distribution per surface region by measured transport cost, a quantity SCULPT never computes."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4410435545","delta":"HumanLiff factorizes humans into sequentially-generated clothing layers via tri-plane diffusion; we keep a single non-layered flow but make its source prior region-adaptive to transport cost, addressing high-frequency fidelity at the source rather than via a fixed layer schedule."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4402704709","delta":"DiffSurf diffuses over fixed-topology vertex+normal tokens with a generic noise schedule; we leave the surface representation and show the per-region source covariance, set by measured transport cost, is the binding fidelity constraint their uniform schedule leaves implicit."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:5bc97f57b3786552e41625008fd5cfe34b2ab213","what_step_was_missed":"Their method already constructs nearest-SMPL-point training pairs and adds an isotropic Gaussian perturbation to mitigate the many-to-one collapse in loose/wrinkled regions, but they never measured the resulting per-region transport cost nor used it to shape the source distribution; the step missing for our contribution to already exist is the construction of the measured per-region transport-cost field tau(r) (mean displacement plus normalized many-to-one fan-in over a fixed SMPL-UV chart partition) and its closed-form mapping into a region-varying anisotropic source covariance Sigma(r), which turns their single global isotropic-noise band-aid into a region-adaptive source that the velocity field is conditioned on."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":307,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"No hard-floor trigger fired (gap_closure_reject_check.verdict=borderline with no candidate_match=yes; anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id=null; recipe_application_check.verdict=applied). The borderline findings — gap_closure_reject_check.entries[0] 'novelty is thin against recent methods' and entries[1] 'Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work ... collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured' — both point at paper_pointed_threat RAFM, an addressable load-bearing concern on the candidate's central novelty boundary (the source-reshaping locus), so a tactical revision adding an explicit measured differentiation against RAFM is warranted rather than advancing with the threat unmentioned.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf produces a per-region quantity that says which surface regions are poorly served by the chosen fixed source prior (SMPL template) BEFORE/DURING generation — so the high-variance many-to-one transport in loose/wrinkled garment regions is patched with one global isotropic perturbation rather than treated as a measurable, region-varying property the generator can act on (additive; sits at the anchor's residual_problem that the SMPL->surface transport cost is fixed and unmeasured).","main_pattern":"generative_process_redesign","sub_pattern":"C23 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"A single local swap of an internal component that is locally reasonable but neither re-derives the chain nor demonstrates a regime the dominant alternative cannot reach; or the redesign silently leans on an extra resource whose cost cancels the gain.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Re-specifying the chain's starting distribution is sound but worthless if a dominant accelerator already reaches one or two steps — failing to beat the strongest fast-sampling alternative dooms the move regardless of its elegance.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate's claim is high-frequency-region fidelity, not few-step sampling acceleration, so the 'dominant fast-sampling accelerator' competitor class does not bound this contribution; the relevant baseline (the anchor's isotropic-SMPL source) is the matched comparison."},{"lesson_quoted":"Substituting one in-support approximation for another without theoretical depth or a failure-regime analysis reads as a narrow heuristic swap rather than a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism supplies the failure regime (high-tau(r) loose/wrinkled partition) plus a closed-form anisotropic source Sigma(r) and a matched-source ablation isolating it, so it is not a bare heuristic swap."},{"lesson_quoted":"A redesign that silently depends on an extra artifact — access to a simulator/dynamics model, or a separately trained auxiliary network — has its claimed efficiency cancelled by the hidden cost once a reviewer surfaces it.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"tau(r) is computed from the training pairs the anchor pipeline already materializes (no extra network); the oracle-nearest-target source is an explicitly-labelled diagnostic upper bound used only in the ablation, never a dependency of the shipped method."},{"lesson_quoted":"Collapsing a staged procedure into a single differentiable mapping is technically clean but gets rejected when the novelty is thin against recent methods and the gains are demonstrated only on weak or dated benchmarks.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"A recent general flow-matching source-reshaping method (RAFM, collision_hits) raises the 'thin novelty against recent methods' risk; the candidate must make the per-region-measured-cost difference explicit and evaluate on a standard (not dated) clothed-scan benchmark — surfaced for the threat check below."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf questions whether the SOURCE distribution of the surface-displacement flow must be the SMPL template shape at all, rather than asking whether a different, geometry-aware transport origin would shorten the worst-region transport — every clothed-human flow/diffusion leaf inherits a single fixed, pose-shape-conditioned source/template assumption from the shared parametric-template ancestor without testing its necessity (subtractive; the shared inherited assumption read off the lineage's parametric-template interior node).","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work without making the difference explicit and measured, or demonstrating the new locus only on fixed/outdated baselines while omitting any account of why it works, reads as a stacked pipeline rather than a principled shift.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a relocated signal is 'stealthier' or 'harder to remove' without defeating an adaptive defender who searches the same new locus leaves the central claim unverified.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"This is a security-framed lesson; the candidate's analog of 'defeating the adaptive defender' is the oracle-nearest-target upper bound that searches the same source locus, which the ablation includes."},{"lesson_quoted":"Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work — normalization statistics, activation-similarity losses, semantic concept triggers — collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"RAFM (collision_hits) already relocates fidelity to the flow's source for anisotropic data generally; the candidate's novelty boundary (per-region measured transport cost on human surfaces, vs RAFM's global radial-law matching) must be made explicit and measured — drives the threat-addressable revision."},{"lesson_quoted":"A defense whose relocation silently depends on a clean reference model or a known anomaly distribution reintroduces precisely the strong assumption the move was supposed to eliminate.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"tau(r) and Sigma(r) are computed from the training data's own matched pairs, not from a clean external reference model, so no smuggled-in strong assumption."},{"lesson_quoted":"Demonstrating the new locus only on fixed, non-adaptive or outdated baselines while omitting any account of why it works reads as a stacked pipeline of existing components rather than a principled shift.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism gives the mechanistic account (long many-to-one transport in high-tau cells under a fixed source) and the matched-source ablation provides the controlled why, not just an aggregate baseline beat."},{"lesson_quoted":"Wiring off-the-shelf generators or tools into a new attack setting without a structural reason for the locus change gets judged as engineering integration, not insight.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The locus change is licensed by the measured per-region transport-cost structure, a structural reason intrinsic to the SMPL->surface flow, not an off-the-shelf tool wiring."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No Reject lesson is marked candidate_match=yes, so no hard-floor trigger. The aggregate is borderline, driven by the C23 entry's 'thin novelty against recent methods' lesson and the C01 entry's 'locus already exploited by published work' lesson — both pointing at the same recent paper (RAFM) whose general flow-source reshaping the candidate must explicitly differentiate from."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf produces a per-region quantity that says which surface regions are poorly served by the chosen fixed source prior (SMPL template) BEFORE/DURING generation — so the high-variance many-to-one transport in loose/wrinkled garment regions is patched with one global isotropic perturbation rather than treated as a measurable, region-varying property the generator can act on (additive; sits at the anchor's residual_problem that the SMPL->surface transport cost is fixed and unmeasured).","sub_pattern":"C23 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Reach inside an iterative refinement (diffusion/flow) chain and re-specify one of its conventionally-frozen internal components — the terminal prior/endpoint, the forward noising process, the per-step distribution — then re-derive the chain around the new choice, licensed by a structural property of the task.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism replaces the chain's frozen source-perturbation component N(0,sigma=1) with a transport-cost-shaped anisotropic source N(0,Sigma(r)) and re-derives the flow-matching objective around it (noise drawn from N(0,Sigma(r)), regression target (Delta_x - n) conditioned on x0' and tau_hat(r)), licensed by the measured per-region transport-cost structural property — the cluster's signature 're-specify a frozen internal component + re-derive the chain' is performed, not just the parent's generic 'liberate a component' gist.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf questions whether the SOURCE distribution of the surface-displacement flow must be the SMPL template shape at all, rather than asking whether a different, geometry-aware transport origin would shorten the worst-region transport — every clothed-human flow/diffusion leaf inherits a single fixed, pose-shape-conditioned source/template assumption from the shared parametric-template ancestor without testing its necessity (subtractive; the shared inherited assumption read off the lineage's parametric-template interior node).","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Relocate the representational locus at which a property is presumed enforced to a different locus the field treated as irrelevant/invariant, build the mechanism at the new locus, and supply a mechanistic account of WHY the new locus carries the signal — 'relocate the signal, re-anchor enforcement.'","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"LEG 2 relocates the fidelity-enforcement locus from the denoising network's capacity to the flow's SOURCE distribution Phi_S, states the falsifiable proposition that the fixed isotropic-SMPL source caps high-tau-cell fidelity, builds the mechanism (the matched-source ablation with an oracle ceiling), and accounts for why the source carries the signal (long many-to-one transport under the fixed source) — the C01 locus-relocation move is performed; the companion controlled_diagnostic_design ships the confound-isolating separation.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries instantiate their cluster's signature move: C23's re-specify-and-re-derive-the-chain (source perturbation -> Sigma(r), objective re-derived) and C01's relocate-the-enforcement-locus (denoiser -> source distribution, with mechanistic account and matched ablation)."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["generative_process_redesign","assumption_audit_and_pivot","controlled_diagnostic_design"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented anti-pattern compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; it is absent from the composition_set (deliberately avoided per Phase 2.1's anchor pick over its heterogeneous_decomposition alternate), so no anti-pattern matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:9017dfbbd20c29f5cf4278607fde133d7cbe80b1","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"Radial-Angular Flow Matching (RAFM) explicitly corrects flow-matching source mismatch for heavy-tailed/anisotropic data by replacing the Gaussian source with one whose radial law matches the data and whose angular conditional is uniform on the sphere. It is the nearest competitor because it, too, reshapes the flow's SOURCE distribution rather than the network — the same locus the candidate relocates to. The candidate's claim stands only if its reshaping is substantively distinct: RAFM matches a single GLOBAL radial/angular law of the whole data distribution and is domain-agnostic, whereas the candidate constructs a PER-REGION anisotropic source whose covariance is set by a MEASURED transport-cost field tau(r) over a fixed SMPL-UV chart on clothed-human surfaces, and pairs it with a matched-source ablation isolating per-region fidelity — a region-varying, geometry-grounded construction RAFM neither computes nor evaluates. Without this explicit-and-measured distinction, a reviewer could read the candidate as RAFM applied to human geometry; with it, the contribution is intact.","addressable_via":"Add a differentiation_from_lit entry against RAFM (semanticscholar:9017dfbbd20c29f5cf4278607fde133d7cbe80b1) making explicit that the candidate's source reshaping is per-region and driven by a measured transport-cost field over the human surface, versus RAFM's single global radial-law match."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat (RAFM, semanticscholar:9017dfbbd20c29f5cf4278607fde133d7cbe80b1) reshapes the flow source globally for anisotropic data — same locus as the candidate — flagged by C23 'thin novelty against recent methods' and C01 'locus already exploited by published work unless the difference is made explicit and measured.'","fix_direction":"Append one differentiation_from_lit entry with paper_id semanticscholar:9017dfbbd20c29f5cf4278607fde133d7cbe80b1 and a delta stating: RAFM replaces the Gaussian source with a single GLOBAL data-matched radial law + uniform angular conditional, domain-agnostic; the candidate instead constructs a PER-REGION anisotropic source whose covariance Sigma(r) is set by a MEASURED per-cell transport-cost field tau(r) over the SMPL-UV chart of clothed-human surfaces and isolates its effect with a matched-source ablation — a region-varying, geometry-grounded source RAFM does not compute or evaluate. Do NOT modify falsification_prediction or compute_budget (kill-switch fields)."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit[4].delta","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Appended one differentiation_from_lit entry against RAFM (semanticscholar:9017dfbbd20c29f5cf4278607fde133d7cbe80b1) making explicit that RAFM matches a single GLOBAL data radial law with uniform angular conditional (domain-agnostic), whereas the candidate constructs a PER-REGION anisotropic source whose covariance Sigma(r) is set by a MEASURED transport-cost field tau(r) over the SMPL-UV chart of clothed-human surfaces plus a matched-source ablation isolating its effect."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Transport-Cost-Shaped Source Priors for Generative Human Geometry\n\n**Method.** Transport-Cost-Shaped Source Prior (TCSP)\n\n## Motivation\nThe goal is to generate realistic 3D shapes of clothed people, especially getting the hard parts right: loose, wrinkly clothing. The leading method (Generative Human Geometry Distribution) treats this as a transport problem — it learns a flow that carries points from a starting shape (the SMPL body template, a standard low-detail body model) out to the real clothed surface. The catch is the starting point is fixed: every target surface point is matched to its nearest point on the bare body template, and a single uniform blob of random noise is added everywhere to cover the gap. But in loose, wrinkly regions, many different surface points all get matched onto the same body-template point, so the flow has to travel a long, messy, many-to-one distance there — and the uniform noise blob does not help where it is needed most. Nobody has measured, region by region, how far and how tangled this transport actually is. Related generators have the same blind spot: SCULPT (Shape-Conditioned Unpaired Learning of clothed meshes) uses one coarse global code, HumanLiff (a Layer-wise 3D Human diffusion model) uses a fixed sequence of clothing layers, and DiffSurf (a transformer diffusion model for surfaces) uses one uniform noise schedule — none of them can point to which surface regions their starting distribution serves badly. This is solvable now because the leading method already computes, during training, the very numbers we need (how far each surface point travels from the template, and how many points pile onto one template point), and because the broader field has just started reshaping the flow's starting distribution to fit the data (Radial-Angular Flow Matching) — but only as one global rule, never region by region on human surfaces. If we close this gap, the starting distribution stops being a fixed default and becomes a measured, inspectable map that tells you, before you generate anything, which clothing regions are under-served — and a recipe to widen the starting noise exactly there. That directly upgrades the leading method and any SMPL-template-based clothed-human generator.\n\n## Method\n### Transport-cost measurement\n*Read a static, inspectable per-region transport-cost field tau(r) off the pipeline's own nearest-template pairing.*\n\n1. Lay a fixed 64x64 grid over the standard SMPL body-template UV map (the texture-coordinate layout that ships with the model, split by its roughly 24 body parts), so every point on the template body gets a fixed cell address. Build it by rasterizing the UV layout once into the 64x64 grid, labelling each grid cell with the body part that covers it, and storing it as a lookup table; at run time any template point is mapped through its triangle's texture coordinates into one cell. This grid is computed once and reused for all people.\n   - _Why_: You need a stable per-region grid before you can measure anything 'per region'.\n2. While the existing method matches each clothed-surface point to its nearest body-template point, record two things into each cell: how far that match traveled (the straight-line distance in meters between the surface point and its matched template point), and how many distinct surface points across the whole training set landed on template points inside that cell (the pile-up count). No new matching is run — you are just logging numbers the matching step already produces.\n   - _Why_: These two numbers are exactly what makes transport hard, and the method already computes them for free.\n3. For each cell, average the travel distances you logged and add lambda times the normalized pile-up count (lambda=1.0; normalized so the most-piled cell is 1 and the least is 0) to get a single transport-cost number for that cell. Cells that no match ever landed in copy the cost of their nearest filled neighbour on the grid. Rescale all cells' costs to the 0-to-1 range and save this small table to disk before any training begins. Keeping it a plain, inspectable per-region number (not a hidden learned signal) is what later lets you switch it off cleanly as a control.\n\n*The per-region transport cost $\\tau (r)$ for chart cell r is the training-set mean nearest-template displacement over the matched pairs falling in r, plus $\\lambda $ times the normalized many-to-one fan-in count of r.*\n$$ \\tau(r) = \\frac{1}{|\\mathcal{P}_r|}\\sum_{(x_0',x_1)\\in\\mathcal{P}_r}\\lVert x_1 - x_0' \\rVert_2 \\;+\\; \\lambda\\,\\widehat{\\mathrm{fan}}(r) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A simple, inspectable per-region cost — not a hidden learned signal — keeps the later 'turn it off' control honest.\n\n### Cost-shaped source redesign\n*Replace the global isotropic source with a per-cell anisotropic source that widens in high-cost cells and re-derive the flow objective around it.*\n\n4. Build a noise generator that, at each body-template point, knows that point's local surface direction (a normal direction and two tangent directions) and the cell's cost number. In high-cost cells it stretches the noise wider along the two tangent (along-surface) directions while leaving the perpendicular direction at the original scale; in low-cost cells it stays identical to the original uniform noise. Concretely it draws standard noise and scales it by the square root of the stretched covariance, then rotates it into world coordinates. The stretch factor is 1 plus 3.0 times the cell's 0-to-1 cost, and the base scale matches the original method.\n\n*The source covariance in cell r scales the baseline variance $\\sigma _{0}^{2}$ by (1 $+ \\alpha  \\hat{\\tau }(r))$ and shapes it with the tangent-aligned rank-2 frame P(r), so high-cost cells get a wider, surface-tangent-spread source while low-cost cells stay at the baseline scale.*\n$$ \\Sigma(r) = \\sigma_0^2\\,\\bigl(1 + \\alpha\\,\\hat{\\tau}(r)\\bigr)\\,P(r), \\qquad \\hat{\\tau}(r)\\in[0,1] \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Widening the start exactly where transport is long and tangled shortens the worst many-to-one trips.\n5. Retrain the flow using the per-cell stretched noise from the previous step instead of the global uniform noise, and also feed each point's cell cost number to the network as one extra input (added to the information it already gets about the matched template point). The network learns to predict the leftover displacement after subtracting the drawn noise. Keep every other part of the pipeline exactly the same and start from the same initial weights, so the only thing that differs from the baseline is the starting noise distribution. Train both this version and an otherwise-identical original-noise baseline.\n\n*The re-derived flow-matching objective draws the perturbation n from the cost-shaped source $N(0,\\Sigma (r))$ and regresses the velocity field, conditioned on the matched template point $x_{0}'$ and the local cost $\\hat{\\tau }(r),$ onto the residual displacement $\\Delta x$ minus n.*\n$$ \\mathcal{L} = \\mathbb{E}_{t,\\,x_1,\\,n\\sim\\mathcal{N}(0,\\Sigma(r))}\\bigl\\lVert u_\\theta\\bigl(x_t, t \\mid x_0', \\hat{\\tau}(r)\\bigr) - (\\Delta x - n) \\bigr\\rVert_2^2, \\quad \\Delta x = x_1 - x_0' \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Changing only the starting distribution makes any fidelity difference attributable to that one choice.\n\n### Matched-source diagnostic\n*Isolate, with an oracle-ceilinged matched-source ablation plus negative/positive controls, that the fixed source (not the network) caps high-frequency-region fidelity.*\n\n6. Generate shapes from three different starting distributions while holding everything else fixed: the original uniform noise, your cost-shaped noise, and a 'cheating' oracle that starts each flow at the true nearest point on the real surface (a deliberate leak that gives a best-possible ceiling). Then split the evaluation surface into the highest-cost quarter of regions versus the rest by mapping each generated point back to its nearest template point and reading that region's cost. Measure shape error — Chamfer distance (average closest-point distance between two point sets) and normal-consistency (agreement of surface orientations) — separately in the high-cost and low-cost regions for all three starting distributions.\n   - _Why_: This matched comparison shows whether the fixed starting distribution, not the network, was capping detail in the hard regions.\n7. Run two checks. First (turn the cost off): replace the whole per-region cost table with one constant equal to its average, so the noise stretch no longer varies by region, and feed that same constant as the network's cost input so it carries no regional information; you predict the hard-region improvement disappears back to the original-noise level — if it does not, the gain came from the extra input or training noise, not from cost-shaped transport. Second (keep the stretch, drop the input): keep the region-varying stretched noise but remove the cost number from the network's inputs; you predict most of the hard-region gain survives, pinpointing the stretched starting noise itself as the active ingredient.\n   - _Why_: The first check proves the gain came from cost-shaped transport, not extra inputs; the second pinpoints the widened start as the active ingredient.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 为生成式人体几何分布设计运输代价塑形的源先验\n\n**方法名称.** Transport-Cost-Shaped Source Prior (TCSP)\n\n## 研究动机\n目标是生成真实的着装人体三维形状，尤其要把最难的部分做对：宽松、有褶皱的衣物。当前最强的方法（Generative Human Geometry Distribution）把这看成一个运输问题——它学一个 flow，把点从一个起始形状（SMPL 身体模板，一个标准的低细节裸体模型）搬运到真实的着装曲面。问题在于这个起点是固定的：每个目标曲面点被匹配到裸体模板上离它最近的点，然后到处均匀地加一团随机噪声来填补差距。但在宽松、有褶皱的区域，很多不同的曲面点都被匹配到同一个模板点上，于是 flow 在那里要走一段很长、很乱、多对一的距离——而那团均匀噪声恰恰在最需要的地方帮不上忙。没有人逐区域地测量过这种运输到底有多远、多缠绕。相关的生成器有同样的盲点：SCULPT（着装网格的形状条件无配对学习）用一个粗糙的全局编码，HumanLiff（逐层的三维人体 diffusion 模型）用一套固定的衣物分层顺序，DiffSurf（用于曲面的 transformer diffusion 模型）用一个均匀的噪声时间表——它们都说不出自己的起始分布在哪些曲面区域服务得差。现在能解决这个问题，是因为最强方法在训练时本就已经算出了我们需要的那些数字（每个曲面点离模板有多远，以及有多少点堆到同一个模板点上），而且更广的领域刚开始把 flow 的起始分布重塑得更贴合数据（Radial-Angular Flow Matching）——但只是作为一个全局规则，从未在人体曲面上逐区域地做。如果我们填上这个空白，起始分布就不再是一个固定的默认值，而成为一张可测量、可检视的图，它在你生成任何东西之前就告诉你哪些衣物区域被服务得差——还给出一份配方，正好在那些地方加宽起始噪声。这直接升级了最强方法以及任何基于 SMPL 模板的着装人体生成器。\n\n## 方法\n### 运输代价测量\n*从管线自身的最近模板匹配中读出一个静态、可检视的逐区域运输代价场 $\\tau (r)$。*\n\n1. 在标准 SMPL 身体模板的 UV 图（随模型附带的纹理坐标布局，按其约 24 个身体部位划分）上铺一个固定的 64x64 网格，让模板身体上的每个点都获得一个固定的格子地址。做法是把 UV 布局一次性栅格化到这个 64x64 网格中，给每个格子标注覆盖它的身体部位，并存成一张查找表；运行时任意模板点通过其三角形的纹理坐标被映射到某一个格子。这个网格计算一次，所有人共用。\n   - _为什么_: 在能够“逐区域”测量任何东西之前，你需要一个稳定的逐区域网格。\n2. 在现有方法把每个着装曲面点匹配到最近的身体模板点的过程中，往每个格子里记录两件事：这次匹配走了多远（曲面点与其匹配模板点之间以米计的直线距离），以及整个训练集中有多少个不同的曲面点落到了该格子内的模板点上（堆叠计数）。不需要重新做匹配——你只是把匹配步骤本就产生的数字记录下来。\n   - _为什么_: 这两个数字正是运输困难的根源，而方法本就免费算出了它们。\n3. 对每个格子，把记录的移动距离取平均，再加上 lambda 乘以归一化的堆叠计数（lambda=1.0；归一化后堆叠最多的格子为 1、最少的为 0），得到该格子的单一运输代价数值。没有任何匹配落入的格子，复制其网格上最近的已填充邻居的代价。把所有格子的代价重新缩放到 0 到 1 的范围，并在任何训练开始前把这张小表存到磁盘。把它保持为一个朴素、可检视的逐区域数值（而非隐藏的学习信号），正是后面能够干净地把它关掉作为对照的前提。\n\n*图块 r 的逐区域运输代价 $\\tau (r)$ 等于落入 r 的匹配点对的训练集平均最近模板位移，加上 $\\lambda $ 乘以 r 的归一化多对一 fan-in 计数。*\n$$ \\tau(r) = \\frac{1}{|\\mathcal{P}_r|}\\sum_{(x_0',x_1)\\in\\mathcal{P}_r}\\lVert x_1 - x_0' \\rVert_2 \\;+\\; \\lambda\\,\\widehat{\\mathrm{fan}}(r) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 一个简单、可检视的逐区域代价——而不是隐藏的学习信号——让后面“关掉它”的对照实验保持诚实。\n\n### 代价塑形的源重设计\n*用一个在高代价格子里加宽的逐格各向异性源替换全局各向同性源，并围绕它重新推导 flow 目标。*\n\n4. 构建一个噪声生成器：在每个身体模板点上，它知道该点的局部曲面方向（一个法向方向和两个切向方向）以及该格子的代价数值。在高代价格子里，它沿两个切向（沿曲面）方向把噪声拉得更宽，而垂直方向保持原始尺度；在低代价格子里，它与原始的均匀噪声完全一致。具体做法是采样标准噪声，按拉伸后协方差的平方根缩放，再旋转到世界坐标。拉伸因子为 1 加上 3.0 乘以该格子的 0 到 1 代价，基准尺度与原始方法一致。\n\n*图块 r 的源协方差以 (1 $+ \\alpha  \\hat{\\tau }(r))$ 缩放基线方差 $\\sigma _{0}^{2}$，并用切向对齐的秩二框架 P(r) 塑形，使高代价图块获得更宽、沿曲面切向展开的源，而低代价图块保持基线尺度。*\n$$ \\Sigma(r) = \\sigma_0^2\\,\\bigl(1 + \\alpha\\,\\hat{\\tau}(r)\\bigr)\\,P(r), \\qquad \\hat{\\tau}(r)\\in[0,1] \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 正好在运输又长又乱的地方加宽起点，能缩短最糟糕的多对一搬运。\n5. 用上一步的逐格拉伸噪声代替全局均匀噪声重新训练 flow，并把每个点的格子代价数值作为一个额外输入喂给网络（加到它已经获得的关于匹配模板点的信息上）。网络学习预测减去所采样噪声之后剩余的位移。让管线的其余每个部分保持完全一致，并从相同的初始权重开始，使得与基线唯一不同的就是起始噪声分布。同时训练这个版本和一个其余完全相同、使用原始噪声的基线。\n\n*重新推导的 flow-matching 目标从代价塑形源 $N(0,\\Sigma (r))$ 采样扰动 n，并让速度场（以匹配模板点 $x_{0}'$ 和局部代价 $\\hat{\\tau }(r)$ 为条件）回归到残差位移 $\\Delta x$ 减去 n。*\n$$ \\mathcal{L} = \\mathbb{E}_{t,\\,x_1,\\,n\\sim\\mathcal{N}(0,\\Sigma(r))}\\bigl\\lVert u_\\theta\\bigl(x_t, t \\mid x_0', \\hat{\\tau}(r)\\bigr) - (\\Delta x - n) \\bigr\\rVert_2^2, \\quad \\Delta x = x_1 - x_0' \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 只改起始分布，就能把任何保真度差异归因于这一个选择。\n\n### 配对源诊断\n*用带 oracle 上界的配对源消融以及负/正对照，隔离出是固定的源（而非网络）限制了高频区域的保真度。*\n\n6. 在其余一切固定的情况下，从三种不同的起始分布生成形状：原始均匀噪声、你的代价塑形噪声、以及一个“作弊”的 oracle——它让每条 flow 从真实曲面上的真正最近点起步（一个刻意的信息泄露，给出最优上界）。然后把评估曲面分成代价最高的四分之一区域与其余区域：把每个生成点映射回其最近的模板点，并读取该区域的代价。对全部三种起始分布，在高代价区域和低代价区域分别测量形状误差——Chamfer 距离（两个点集之间平均最近点距离）与法向一致性（曲面朝向的吻合程度）。\n   - _为什么_: 这个配对比较揭示在困难区域里，是固定的起始分布而不是网络，限制了细节。\n7. 做两个检查。第一（把代价关掉）：把整张逐区域代价表替换为一个等于其平均值的常数，使噪声拉伸不再随区域变化，并把同一个常数作为网络的代价输入，使其不携带任何区域信息；你预测困难区域的改进会消失、退回到原始噪声的水平——如果没有消失，那么增益来自额外输入或训练噪声，而非代价塑形的运输。第二（保留拉伸、去掉输入）：保留随区域变化的拉伸噪声，但从网络输入中移除代价数值；你预测困难区域的大部分增益仍然存在，从而锁定拉伸的起始噪声本身就是有效成分。\n   - _为什么_: 第一个检查证明增益来自代价塑形的运输而非额外输入；第二个检查锁定加宽的起点为有效成分。\n\n"},{"id":"51","run_dir":"run_prompt51_univerifier","index":51,"title":"Modality-Attributed Verification: a Generative Verifier that Localizes Multimodal Reasoning Faults","title_zh":"模态归因式验证：一个能定位多模态推理错误的生成式验证器","method_name":"Modality-Attributed Verifier (MAV)","hook":"Every process reward model treats per-step verification competence as a single quantity scored over a text trace, so when a multimodal chain fails it can say a step is wrong but not whether the fault lives in what the model SAW or in what it INFERRED. We reframe verification competence as a heterogeneous resource partitioned by which modality a step's correctness depends on, and build a generative verifier whose verdict is attributed to the responsible faculty.","anchor_pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","anchor_pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","domain_category":"Vision-Language & Multimodal","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf produces a verifier verdict that LOCALIZES a multi-step reasoning failure to the modality (visual-grounding vs textual-inference) responsible for it — current PRMs (openalex:W7092285489, openalex:W6979261193) emit a scalar step score that is uninformative about where, across modalities, the chain actually broke.","pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by treating per-step verification competence as a heterogeneous resource and partitioning each reasoning step by its modality-of-dependence (visual-grounding / textual-inference / cross-modal-consistency), then assigning each partition a tailored verification check and emitting a verdict labelled with the faculty that failed — the differentiated-treatment move plus a fidelity decomposition bounding how the partitioned verdict recovers the true step-correctness signal that a uniform scalar cannot see.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf questions the shared inherited assumption — every PRM/verifier leaf (openalex:W7092285489, openalex:W6979261193, openalex:W4417414089) descends from the same ancestor that assumes a verifier's competence is a SINGLE scalar per step; none tests whether step-verification competence is necessarily a single undifferentiated quantity rather than something that varies systematically with the type of inference the step performs.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","how_closed":"Closed by the audit-and-pivot move (C01): name the tacit locus assumption — 「the scalar step-correctness score over a text trace IS the verification signal」 — and relocate the verification signal to a modality-attributed locus, arguing the correctness property manifests there more robustly; the companion controlled_diagnostic_design (C02) ships the missing empirical deliverable as a confound-isolating separation: matched step-pairs that hold surface form fixed and vary only which modality the step's correctness depends on, showing a verifier's competence splits sharply by partition (high on text-inference steps, low on visual-grounding steps) rather than being one undifferentiated quantity.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"foundation/frontier models — multimodal reasoning verification (verifiers, process reward models, generative critics for vision-language reasoning)","n_papers":39,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":24},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"openreview","n":2}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":11,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Symphony: Towards Trustworthy Question Answering and Verification using RAG over Multimodal Data Lakes"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Multimodal Fake News Detection Based on Chain-of-Thought Prompting Large Language Models"},{"source":"openalex","title":"UniMEL: A Unified Framework for Multimodal Entity Linking with Large Language Models"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Evaluating ChatGPT-4 Vision on Brazil's National Undergraduate Computer Science Exam"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Evaluation and mitigation of the limitations of large language models in clinical decision-making"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Can Retelling Have Adequate Information for Reasoning? An Enhancement Method for Imperfect Video Understanding with Large Language Model"}],"more":5},{"year":2025,"n":26,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Debunk and Infer: Multimodal Fake News Detection via Diffusion-Generated Evidence and LLM Reasoning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Multimodal Knowledge Question Answering System based on LLM"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Incorporating LLM Versus LLM Into Multimodal Chain-of-Thought for Fine-Grained Evidence Generation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"MoPE: Mixture of Policy Experts and Verification with Multimodal Information for Instance ImageGoal Navigation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Unmasking Digital Falsehoods: A Comparative Analysis of LLM-Based Misinformation Detection Strategies"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"LLM-Guided Reconciliation for Explainable Robotic Path Planning: A Case Study"}],"more":20},{"year":2026,"n":2,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"},{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"}],"more":0}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":14,"share":0.359},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":12,"share":0.308},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":10,"share":0.256},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":5,"share":0.128},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":4,"share":0.103},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":3,"share":0.077},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":3,"share":0.077},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":1,"share":0.026}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Process reward models and verifiers for multi-step reasoning have converged on a text-only formulation whose verdict carries no cross-modal structure: GroundedPRM (openalex:W7092285489) supervises steps with tree-search paths validated by EXECUTION/symbolic tools and even formats a generative rationale, PURE (openalex:W6979261193) re-derives the credit-assignment form to stop reward hacking, and Beyond-Correctness (openalex:W4417414089) harmonizes process and outcome rewards — yet all three validate steps over text traces with checks (tool execution, scalar credit) that have no notion of which modality a step's correctness depends on, so the verifier cannot say whether a multimodal chain failed at its visual-grounding step or at its textual-inference step. Meanwhile the multimodal frontier shows this is exactly where reasoning breaks: Visual reasoning consistency analysis (openalex:W4416420249) finds multimodal LLMs flip answers under reordering and are miscalibrated, and Hidden-in-Plain-Sight (openalex:W4416035722) shows they fail silently when an image is underspecified or contradicts the instruction — yet neither builds a verifier queryable at inference that flags the chain AND attributes the fault to the offending modality. A verifier whose correctness check is execution-grounded or scalar-over-text is structurally unable to localize the fault across faculties, so the correction signal test-time scaling needs is missing precisely on the cross-modal chains where it matters most.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W7092285489","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"GroundedPRM builds a process reward model that constructs MCTS reasoning paths, validates each intermediate step with an external tool for execution-grounded correctness, and — per its method section — formats the reward into a rationale-enhanced GENERATIVE structure for interpretability, so the 'make the verifier explain itself' move is already partly occupied. Its residue is that the verification is built entirely on text reasoning traces validated by symbolic/execution tools, so the rationale it generates has no cross-modal structure: it cannot attribute a multi-step failure to a visual-grounding fault versus a textual-inference fault, and its tool-grounded validation does not apply where the step's correctness depends on perception of an image rather than on an executable check."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W6979261193","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"PURE identifies summation-form credit assignment as the cause of PRM reward hacking and replaces it with a min-form credit assignment so the value reflects the worst step. It still treats each step verdict as a scalar and is text-only, so it does not produce an inspectable, modality-localized explanation of the failure — its fix is to the aggregation arithmetic, not to what the verifier can express."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4417414089","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Beyond-Correctness diagnoses outcome-reward hacking (flawed reasoning that accidentally reaches the right answer still gets max reward) and harmonizes process and outcome rewards during RL training. It improves WHICH signal is optimized but the verifier remains a scalar reward over text steps, so it cannot say in which modality a multimodal chain went wrong or surface a verdict a human can audit."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416035722","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Hidden-in-Plain-Sight systematically analyzes how multimodal LLMs handle underspecified and misspecified inputs (missing objects, contradictory facts) and shows success hinges on detecting that something is silently wrong. It is a diagnostic study only: it characterizes the silent-failure regime but builds no verifier that can be queried at inference to flag the misspecification and localize it to the offending modality."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416420249","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Visual reasoning consistency analysis introduces entropy-over-reordered-variants and abstention metrics to quantify reasoning consistency and uncertainty calibration of multimodal LLMs. It is a measurement contribution: it quantifies inconsistency but does not turn the inconsistency signal into a verifier that attributes the inconsistency to a specific reasoning step or modality."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"foundation/frontier models — multimodal reasoning verification (verifiers, process reward models, generative critics for vision-language reasoning)","venue":"ICLR/NeurIPS (frontier-models track)","time":"2026","data":["multimodal reasoning benchmarks with step-annotated traces (e.g. visual CoT / MMMU-style)","process-reward annotations (tree-search or MC rollouts)","vision-language QA with intermediate reasoning"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with cloud GPU access; familiar with reward modeling and VLMs","preference":"both","baseline":"discriminative/scalar process reward models (GroundedPRM openalex:W7092285489, PURE openalex:W6979261193, Beyond-Correctness openalex:W4417414089) and outcome-only RLVR (openalex:W4415311663)","limitation":"current verifiers are text-only and emit a scalar/discriminative score per step rather than a generative explanation, and none is calibrated to WHICH modality the error lives in, so when a multimodal reasoning chain fails because of a grounding error (vision) versus an inference error (text), the verifier cannot localize the fault and its score is uninformative for correction","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared audit lens is: 「is per-step verification competence one quantity, or does it split by which modality the step's correctness depends on?」 — the anchor leg builds the verifier that assumes the split, the sibling leg audits-and-validates the assumption that the field assumed the opposite. Anchor (C04 differentiated treatment): a multimodal reasoning chain is a sequence of steps s_1..s_T; we define for each step a modality-of-dependence label m(s_t) in {VG (visual-grounding: correctness depends on what the image shows), TI (textual-inference: correctness depends on a deduction over already-extracted facts), CM (cross-modal-consistency: correctness depends on agreement between a visual claim and a textual claim)}. m(s_t) is computed, not oracle: a lightweight router (a frozen VLM prompted with a fixed rubric + a learned linear head over its last-layer pooled embedding of the step text and the image) outputs a 3-way distribution; the argmax with a tie-margin tau_route=0.15 assigns the partition (ties default to CM). The verifier is then a single generative VLM V that, conditioned on (image, chain prefix, step s_t, predicted partition m), emits a written verdict token-sequence whose FIRST token is a structured tag <VG-fault|TI-fault|CM-fault|ok> and whose continuation is a free-text justification grounded in the partition's evidence — for VG steps the justification must quote a region of the image (a bounding box re-rendered into the context), for TI steps it must cite the prior step whose conclusion is contradicted, for CM steps it must name the visual claim and the textual claim that disagree. The differentiated TREATMENT is that the per-partition verification objective differs: VG steps are checked by a grounded re-perception pass (the verifier re-attends to the named region and tests whether the step's visual premise holds), TI steps by an entailment check over the symbolic prefix, CM steps by a consistency check between the two named claims; these are three heads sharing the V backbone, not one scalar head. The load-bearing artifact (C04 spine) is a fidelity decomposition: we write the true step-error e_t as e_t = e_t^VG + e_t^TI + e_t^CM (the chain breaks at step t through exactly one faculty under matched construction), and prove that a verifier minimizing the partitioned objective achieves expected attribution error bounded by the router's partition error plus the per-head verification error, strictly below the irreducible floor of any single-scalar verifier which must marginalize over m and therefore cannot separate e_t^VG from e_t^TI (a single scalar collapses the 3-vector to its sum and is information-theoretically unable to recover the argmax faculty when two faculties have comparable error mass). Sibling (C01 locus pivot + C02 companion): the audited locus is the scalar-over-text score; we relocate to the modality-attributed verdict and validate with a controlled separation — for a held set of reasoning steps we build matched pairs that hold the step's surface text fixed and the chain prefix fixed, and inject a fault into EITHER the visual premise (corrupt the image region the step depends on) OR the textual inference (perturb a cited prior conclusion), so the only varying axis is the faculty-of-fault; an oracle independent of the verifier (the injection ground truth) scores attribution. The headline separation is the gap between a text-only scalar PRM's attribution accuracy (at chance on which-faculty, since it never saw the image) and the partitioned verifier's attribution accuracy on the same matched pairs — the empirical artifact that certifies competence is modality-differentiated, not a re-labeled scalar.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The two gaps share machinery, not modules: the anchor's modality partition m(s_t) IS the locus the sibling audit relocates the verification signal to, so they read as one paper under the shared_audit thread (one verifier, justified by one overturned assumption) rather than two stapled contributions — that is why the sibling is a validation+audit leg over the anchor's object, not a separate model. I considered making the verifier a router-then-delegate pipeline (route each step to a modality-specific external checker), but that lands on the n3 GroundedPRM node which already delegates step-validation to an external tool, so per the regression flag I kept verification INSIDE one generative VLM with differentiated heads (a partition of one model's competence) rather than delegating to separate solvers — the avoided node is n3 (tool-delegated step validation) and the collateral node c2 (neuro-symbolic delegation). I also rejected a pure-diagnostic framing (just measure the modality split) because contribution_type=method demands the runnable verifier, which the anchor's C04 construction ships.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on a multimodal step-annotated reasoning benchmark (visual-CoT / MMMU-style), train the partitioned generative verifier V and a matched single-scalar multimodal PRM on the same data and compute, and evaluate both on (i) the controlled matched-injection separation set and (ii) downstream test-time correction accuracy on held-out chains. If the candidate works, faculty-of-fault attribution accuracy on the separation set rises sharply for V over the scalar PRM (whose which-faculty accuracy stays near chance), AND modality-matched re-runs triggered by V's verdict yield higher final-answer accuracy than equal-budget untargeted re-sampling (the downstream accuracy curve shifts up). The named load-bearing variable is the router's modality-of-dependence assignment m(s_t): the negative control randomizes m(s_t) (permute the partition labels at train and inference so the verifier's heads no longer align with the faculty a step actually depends on); the anti-tautology prediction is on the DOWNSTREAM task-outcome metric — final-answer correction accuracy must collapse back to the untargeted-resampling baseline when m is randomized, not merely that attribution-tag entropy rises. A positive control — a stripped verifier that uses ONLY m(s_t) plus a per-partition default check (no shared generative justification) — should recover most of the targeted-correction gain over untargeted resampling, identifying the modality partition as the mechanism rather than the generative prose.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W7092285489","delta":"GroundedPRM validates each text step against an MCTS path with an external execution tool and formats a generative rationale, but its correctness check has no notion of modality-of-dependence; we construct a verifier whose verdict is attributed to the faculty (visual-grounding vs textual-inference vs cross-modal) and prove a fidelity decomposition showing a single-scalar verifier cannot recover that attribution — a separation their construction does not produce."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W6979261193","delta":"PURE re-derives the credit-assignment FORM (min over steps) to stop reward hacking but the per-step verdict stays a scalar over text; we change the OBJECT being verified into a modality-partitioned 3-vector and ship the empirical separation that the scalar form collapses, which a credit-aggregation fix cannot."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4417414089","delta":"Beyond-Correctness harmonizes process and outcome rewards to reward faithful reasoning but optimizes a number over text traces; we localize the fault to a modality and route a modality-matched re-run, measuring downstream correction gains that an undifferentiated process+outcome scalar cannot target."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416035722","delta":"Hidden-in-Plain-Sight diagnoses that multimodal LLMs fail silently under misspecification but builds no verifier; we turn that silent-failure regime into an inference-time verifier that flags the chain AND attributes the misspecification to the offending modality via a controlled matched-injection separation."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W7092285489","what_step_was_missed":"GroundedPRM constructs a tool-grounded, rationale-enhanced reward over text reasoning steps, but to already contain our contribution it would have needed to construct a per-step modality-of-dependence decomposition of step-correctness (e_t = e_t^VG + e_t^TI + e_t^CM) and a verifier whose objective is differentiated per faculty so the verdict recovers WHICH faculty failed — its single tool-grounded correctness signal has no faculty index and cannot be marginalized back into one, so the attribution artifact and its fidelity bound are absent."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":319,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"Hard floor does not fire: gap_closure_reject_check has no candidate_match: yes (aggregate borderline only), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat (openalex:W7119557428) is a diagnostic with addressable, non-exact overlap. recipe_application_check.verdict = applied on BOTH legs (C04 error-decomposition spine and C01 relocate-the-signal move are both instantiated), so the idea is not built from parent-pattern gist. The only borderlines (C04 'real-world deployment metric' and C01 'adaptive defender') sit in non-load-bearing framing that maps loosely from compression/adversarial clusters onto a verification setting; they are surfaced for Phase 4 reviewer_concerns_and_responses rather than requiring revision.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf produces a verifier verdict that LOCALIZES a multi-step reasoning failure to the modality (visual-grounding vs textual-inference) responsible for it — current PRMs (openalex:W7092285489, openalex:W6979261193) emit a scalar step score that is uninformative about where, across modalities, the chain actually broke.","main_pattern":"heterogeneous_decomposition","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is treating the partition criterion itself as the contribution while leaving its value unproven, so reviewers map the discriminator onto an established technique and the differentiated treatment reads as a relabeling; a second shortcut is validating in a regime where the bottleneck does not bite (toy scale, proxy-only metrics).","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Presenting a sensitivity or redundancy proxy as the novelty invites the verdict that it rediscovers known mixed-precision or low-rank results unless it is sharply differentiated from the obvious prior criterion.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The partition criterion is modality-of-dependence (which faculty a step's correctness rests on), not a magnitude/sensitivity/redundancy proxy, so it does not map onto PCA/mixed-precision; the contribution is the verdict-attribution it enables plus the fidelity decomposition, not the partition label alone."},{"lesson_quoted":"Omitting comparison against both the strongest uniform baseline and the obvious cheap alternative (SVD/PCA, structured dropout, a natively trained smaller model) leaves reviewers unable to tell whether the partition buys anything at all.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism_steps 7 benchmarks against the strongest uniform baseline (single-scalar multimodal PRM) AND the obvious cheap alternative (untargeted equal-budget resampling), so the uniform-vs-differentiated comparison is present."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a storage or throughput claim only on toy-scale models — where the compression bottleneck does not actually bite — undermines the entire motivation no matter how clean the method is.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"There is no storage/throughput claim; validation is on standard multimodal step-annotated reasoning benchmarks where multimodal chains genuinely fail, the regime where the attribution problem actually bites."},{"lesson_quoted":"A clever partition with no measured real-world deployment metric (no inference latency or memory speedup) reads as a proxy-only contribution and stalls at borderline.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"This cluster's canonical deployment metric is latency/memory (compression framing); ours is downstream test-time-correction final-answer accuracy, which IS the real deployment payoff for a verifier — the lesson maps only loosely, hence borderline rather than a match, and Phase 4 should surface that the payoff metric is accuracy-gain, not a compute speedup."},{"lesson_quoted":"Skipping any analysis of why the heterogeneity exists — the data or value distribution that drives the partition — makes the technical novelty and the potential impact impossible to assess.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism_steps 1 empirically characterizes the partition (whether removing the image flips a step's correctness => VG vs TI) and the sibling C02 separation set positively demonstrates the heterogeneity (competence splits by faculty), satisfying the why-the-heterogeneity-exists demand."},{"lesson_quoted":"Bolting together established components (distillation plus pruning plus calibration) without an error bound or artifact specific to the new setting reads as incremental even when the target application is timely and important.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The fidelity decomposition e_t = e_t^VG + e_t^TI + e_t^CM with its bound below the single-scalar floor is an artifact specific to the verification setting, not a bolt-together of off-the-shelf parts."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf questions the shared inherited assumption — every PRM/verifier leaf (openalex:W7092285489, openalex:W6979261193, openalex:W4417414089) descends from the same ancestor that assumes a verifier's competence is a SINGLE scalar per step; none tests whether step-verification competence is necessarily a single undifferentiated quantity rather than something that varies systematically with the type of inference the step performs.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is a relocation demonstrated but not adversarially closed, or a novelty-boundary collapse where the new locus turns out already used by prior work, or offering only a demonstration with no mechanistic account of why the locus carries the signal.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a relocated signal is 'stealthier' or 'harder to remove' without defeating an adaptive defender who searches the same new locus leaves the central claim unverified.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"This setting is non-adversarial (verification, not attack/defense), so 'adaptive defender' does not map directly; the analogous burden — show the modality-attributed separation survives beyond the controlled injection regime — is addressed by the C02 step-5 transfer-to-realistic check, leaving only a mild borderline that the separation must be shown to hold on naturally-occurring (not just injected) faults."},{"lesson_quoted":"Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work — normalization statistics, activation-similarity losses, semantic concept triggers — collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"No retrieved verifier/PRM relocates the verification signal to a per-step modality-attributed locus; GroundedPRM's generative rationale is still a text/execution-grounded scalar with no faculty index, and differentiation_from_lit measures the gap explicitly (attribution accuracy vs chance)."},{"lesson_quoted":"A defense whose relocation silently depends on a clean reference model or a known anomaly distribution reintroduces precisely the strong assumption the move was supposed to eliminate.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The oracle is the matched-injection ground truth (constructed, independent of the verifier), not a clean reference model or known anomaly distribution, so no banned assumption is reintroduced."},{"lesson_quoted":"Demonstrating the new locus only on fixed, non-adaptive or outdated baselines while omitting any account of why it works reads as a stacked pipeline of existing components rather than a principled shift.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The mechanistic account is supplied: a single scalar must marginalize over the faculty index and is information-theoretically unable to recover the argmax faculty when two faculties carry comparable error mass — a root-cause decomposition, not a bare demonstration."},{"lesson_quoted":"Wiring off-the-shelf generators or tools into a new attack setting without a structural reason for the locus change gets judged as engineering integration, not insight.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The locus change is justified structurally by the fidelity decomposition and the marginalization argument, not by wiring a tool into a new setting."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No Reject lesson is marked candidate_match: yes, so the hard floor does not fire. The aggregate is borderline, driven by the C04 entry's 'real-world deployment metric' lesson (the cluster's compression-latency framing maps only loosely onto a verifier whose payoff metric is downstream correction accuracy) and the C01 entry's 'adaptive defender' lesson (non-adversarial setting; the analogous burden is showing the separation holds on naturally-occurring faults, not only injected ones)."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf produces a verifier verdict that LOCALIZES a multi-step reasoning failure to the modality (visual-grounding vs textual-inference) responsible for it — current PRMs (openalex:W7092285489, openalex:W6979261193) emit a scalar step score that is uninformative about where, across modalities, the chain actually broke.","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Discriminate components by a magnitude-, sensitivity-, influence-, or redundancy-based criterion into structurally distinct populations, apply a treatment matched to each partition's property, and make a load-bearing error/sensitivity decomposition that bounds how the differentiated treatment recovers the original objective the spine of the contribution — that analysis, not the partition idea, is what separates the move from heuristic per-component tuning.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism partitions steps by modality-of-dependence m(s_t) into VG/TI/CM populations (the discriminating criterion), assigns each partition a tailored verification head (grounded re-perception / entailment / consistency — the differentiated treatment), and supplies the decomposition e_t = e_t^VG + e_t^TI + e_t^CM with a proven bound that the partitioned verdict beats the single-scalar floor (the load-bearing spine). This is the C04 signature move, not the parent's generic 'decompose for differentiated treatment' gist.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf questions the shared inherited assumption — every PRM/verifier leaf (openalex:W7092285489, openalex:W6979261193, openalex:W4417414089) descends from the same ancestor that assumes a verifier's competence is a SINGLE scalar per step; none tests whether step-verification competence is necessarily a single undifferentiated quantity rather than something that varies systematically with the type of inference the step performs.","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Name the single representational locus current methods operate on, state the tacit sufficiency/invariance claim bolted to it, relocate the signal to an overlooked locus argued to carry the property more robustly, build the mechanism there, and supply a mechanistic account of WHY the new locus carries the signal — the unifying verbs are 'relocate the signal' and 're-anchor enforcement'.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism names the audited locus ('the scalar step-correctness score over a text trace IS the verification signal'), relocates verification to the modality-attributed verdict locus, builds the partitioned verifier there, and supplies the marginalization/information-theoretic account for why the scalar locus cannot carry the faculty signal — the C01 relocate-the-signal move, with the C02 companion shipping the empirical separation.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries perform their cited cluster's signature move: the C04 anchor centers on the error decomposition spine (not just the partition idea), and the C01 sibling relocates the verification signal to a new locus with a mechanistic why, so neither is built from the parent pattern's generic gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["heterogeneous_decomposition","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"The composition set {heterogeneous_decomposition, assumption_audit_and_pivot} does not match any of the three flagged reject-favored compositions (decomp+self_supervised_signal_engineering, decomp+structural_prior_encoding, operator_substitution+decomp), so no anti-pattern mitigation is required."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"openalex:W7119557428","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"Analyzing Reasoning Consistency in Large Multimodal Models under Cross-Modal Conflicts identifies 'textual inertia' — once a textual hallucination enters the thinking process, the model adheres to the wrong text and neglects conflicting visual evidence — and proposes a LogicGraph perturbation probe to study it. This is the closest threat because it operationalizes exactly the VG-vs-TI fault distinction the candidate is built on, so it could be read as already establishing that modality-localized failures exist. But it stands as a DIAGNOSTIC: it perturbs and measures a failure mode, it does not construct a verifier queryable at inference that emits a faculty-attributed verdict, nor a fidelity decomposition bounding attribution error below a single-scalar floor, nor a test-time correction loop — so it supports the candidate's premise rather than subsuming its mechanism. The candidate's claim stands provided differentiation makes explicit that this paper measures the regime while the candidate verifies-and-corrects within it.","addressable_via":"Add this paper to differentiation_from_lit framing the candidate's verifier-and-correction artifact against its diagnostic-only scope (a non-exact, addressable overlap — not exact-mechanism)."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Modality-Attributed Verification: a Generative Verifier that Localizes Multimodal Reasoning Faults\n\n**Method.** Modality-Attributed Verifier (MAV)\n\n## Motivation\nWhen a vision-language model reasons step by step over an image and gets the wrong answer, it can fail for two very different reasons. It might have misread what the picture shows (a vision mistake), or it might have seen the picture correctly but reasoned badly about the facts it pulled out (a logic mistake). The fix is opposite in each case: re-look at the image, versus re-do the thinking. But today's quality checkers — called process reward models (step-by-step scorers of a reasoning chain) — only give one number per step that says 'this step looks wrong' without saying which kind of wrong. GroundedPRM (a tree-search-validated step scorer, 2025) even writes out an explanation, but it checks everything against text and tools, so it never knows whether the problem was in seeing or in thinking. PURE (2025) and Beyond-Correctness (2025) fix how the step scores are combined, but the per-step verdict is still a single text-based number. Meanwhile, careful studies in 2025 (Hidden-in-Plain-Sight; a visual-reasoning-consistency analysis) show that vision-language models fail silently exactly when the image is misleading — but those studies only measure the problem, they do not build a checker that flags it and points to the guilty faculty. This is solvable now because open 7-billion-parameter vision-language models are good enough to act as a checker that can re-look at a specific image region, and step-by-step multimodal reasoning datasets now exist to train on. Closing this gap means a checker that does not just say 'this chain is broken' but says 'fix the seeing' or 'fix the thinking', so a system can spend its retry budget on the right repair instead of blindly resampling.\n\n## Method\n### Modality Router\n*Compute each step's modality-of-dependence label so the verifier knows which faculty the step rests on.*\n\n1. Tag every reasoning step by what its correctness depends on: visual-grounding (VG, it depends on the image), textual-inference (TI, it depends on earlier stated facts), or cross-modal (CM, it depends on a visual claim and a textual claim matching). A small router does this automatically: a frozen vision-language model reads the whole image plus a fixed instruction sheet (the three criteria written out), the earlier steps, and the current step; a trained linear layer on top of the model's averaged internal representation outputs three scores. Take the highest score, but if the top two scores are within 0.15 of each other, label it CM. To create the 2,000-3,000 training labels for that linear layer, check each step twice: blank out the image and see if the step's correctness flips (then it is VG); if blanking does nothing but deleting the earlier step it cites flips it, it is TI; if both flip it, it is CM.\n\n*The router maps a step $s_{t}$ and image I to a 3-way distribution over faculties and assigns the argmax partition, defaulting to CM when the top-two margin falls below the tie threshold $\\tau _{route} =$ 0.15.*\n$$ m(s_t) = \\arg\\max_{k \\in \\{VG, TI, CM\\}} p_\\phi(k \\mid s_t, I), \\quad \\text{assign CM if } p_{(1)} - p_{(2)} < \\tau_{route} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: You can only attribute a fault to a faculty if you first know which faculty each step relies on, and you want that label computed automatically, not handed to you.\n\n### Partitioned Generative Verifier\n*A single VLM with three faculty-tailored heads that emits a fault tag attributed to the responsible modality plus a grounded justification.*\n\n2. Start from an open 7-billion-parameter vision-language model and add three small checking heads (each a 2-layer network) on the shared body, one per faculty. The verifier reads the image, the earlier steps, the current step, and the router's faculty label, and writes a fault tag (VG-fault / TI-fault / CM-fault / ok) as its first output, followed by an explanation grounded in that faculty's evidence. The three checks differ: for a visual step the model first outputs a box for the relevant image region, that region is cropped and shown back to it, and it re-checks whether the visual claim is actually true; for an inference step it hides the image and checks the deduction against earlier steps; for a cross-modal step it checks whether the named visual claim and the named text claim agree. The gold explanations used for training come from the known injected fault (from the controlled set below): they name the broken region, or the contradicted earlier step, or the two clashing claims.\n\n*The generative verifier V, conditioned on image, chain prefix, step and predicted partition m, emits a structured fault tag as its first token followed by a justification j grounded in that partition's evidence.*\n$$ V(I, s_{<t}, s_t, m) \\rightarrow \\langle \\text{tag} \\rangle \\cdot j, \\quad \\text{tag} \\in \\{\\text{VG-fault}, \\text{TI-fault}, \\text{CM-fault}, \\text{ok}\\} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Different kinds of mistakes need different checks; one shared model with three tailored heads can attribute the fault instead of emitting one undifferentiated score.\n3. Make training labels by deliberately injecting faults whose faculty is known (using the controlled procedure below), so every step has a ground-truth answer for which faculty failed. Assemble the training data by pairing each broken step with its original clean version, upsampling whichever faculty is rarer so the three fault types appear equally often, and keeping clean and broken steps in a 1:1 mix so the model learns realistic base rates. Train the verifier to minimize a classification loss on the fault tag plus a text-generation loss on the grounded explanation, weighting the explanation at 0.5.\n\n*Training minimizes a cross-entropy on the fault-tag head plus a generation loss on the grounded justification, weighted by $\\lambda _{just} =$ 0.5.*\n$$ \\mathcal{L} = \\mathcal{L}_{CE}(\\text{tag}) + \\lambda_{just} \\, \\mathcal{L}_{gen}(j), \\quad \\lambda_{just} = 0.5 \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Honest per-faculty labels — not the model grading itself — are what let the heads learn to point at the right faculty.\n\n### Fidelity-Decomposition Evidence\n*Turn the $e_{t} = e_{t}^{VG} + e_{t}^{TI} + e_{t}^{CM}$ decomposition into a measured attribution-accuracy gap below the single-scalar floor.*\n\n4. Measure attribution accuracy: out of all the deliberately-broken steps, how often the verifier's predicted faculty tag matches the faculty that was actually injected. Then build the 'single-number floor': retrain the exact same model but with the three-way faculty head replaced by one yes/no broken-or-fine score, trained on the same data with the faculty labels averaged away. Its faculty accuracy is whatever a uniform random guess among the faculties gives, because a single broken-or-fine score contains no faculty information — that is the floor. Report the gap between the real verifier and this floor. The decomposition (the true step-error splits into a visual part, an inference part and a cross-modal part, with one active per broken step) is why that gap means the verifier recovered which-faculty information that a single number cannot carry.\n\n*The true step-error decomposes additively over faculties (one active under matched construction); the partitioned verifier's expected attribution error is bounded by router error plus per-head error, strictly below the single-scalar floor $\\epsilon _{scalar}$ which must collapse the 3-vector to its sum.*\n$$ e_t = e_t^{VG} + e_t^{TI} + e_t^{CM}, \\qquad \\mathbb{E}[\\text{attr-err}] \\leq \\epsilon_{route} + \\max_k \\epsilon_{head}^{k} \\; < \\; \\epsilon_{scalar}^{floor} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The decomposition $e_{t} = e_{t}^{VG} + e_{t}^{TI} + e_{t}^{CM}$ shows a single number must average over faculties and cannot recover which one failed — the measured gap proves the split is real, not a relabeling.\n\n### Modality-Matched Correction\n*Route the attributed verdict into a faculty-specific re-run that beats untargeted resampling downstream.*\n\n5. Use the verdict to retry. The verifier scores every step; the first step it tags as a fault gets one targeted retry matched to the faculty: a visual fault re-runs that step while forcing a fresh look at the flagged image region, an inference fault re-runs the reasoning with the image hidden so the visual premises are held fixed; then the rest of the chain is regenerated. Compare against spending the same retry budget on plain extra samples, where both methods pick their final answer by how many steps the verifier marks fine. 【author decision: whether correction is a single pass or repeats until no fault remains, and how the retry budget is matched to plain resampling when there are several retries, is a choice the authors must fix along the one-shot-versus-iterative axis.】 Report the final-answer accuracy of the corrected chain against the plain-resampling baseline.\n   - _Why_: A localized verdict is only useful if it changes what you do next; targeting the repair to the guilty faculty should beat blind retries.\n\n### Controlled Separation + Controls\n*Matched-injection separation set plus baselines and a label-randomization negative control that certify the partition is the mechanism.*\n\n6. Build a controlled test set. Take matched reasoning steps and, keeping the step's wording and all earlier steps exactly the same, make two broken versions of each. Visual (VG) version: find the image region the step's visual claim relies on (using an open-vocabulary object detector prompted with the words of that claim) and edit only that region so the claim becomes false — erase the object by inpainting, recolor it, or add/remove a copy — leaving every word and the rest of the image untouched. Inference (TI) version: find an earlier step this step refers to and minimally change its conclusion into a contradicting one (flip a predicate to its negation, swap in a same-kind distractor, or change a number) so the current step now reasons from a false premise. The log of exactly what you injected (which region and edit, or which earlier step and change) is the answer key, independent of the verifier.\n   - _Why_: Holding everything fixed except which faculty you broke isolates the one variable you care about, so any attribution accuracy above chance must come from reading the modality, not surface cues.\n7. Run the comparisons. Baselines: (i) a text-only step scorer with no image; (ii) a generic multimodal critic — the same vision-language model fine-tuned with a single broken-or-fine score on the same data, images included but with no faculty labels and no router, so it differs from the real verifier only by lacking the faculty partition; (iii) the real verifier. Report faculty-attribution accuracy on the controlled set and downstream correction accuracy on held-out problems for all three. Then the key control: shuffle the router's faculty labels (at both training and test time) so the checking heads no longer line up with the faculty a step truly depends on, retrain, and re-evaluate — you should see the downstream correction gain collapse back to the plain-resampling level, proving the gain came from the faculty labels and not the explanatory text.\n   - _Why_: The baselines show the partition buys something over both a strong uniform checker and the cheap alternative, and the shuffle control proves the gain comes from the modality labels and not from the prose.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 模态归因式验证：一个能定位多模态推理错误的生成式验证器\n\n**方法名称.** Modality-Attributed Verifier (MAV)\n\n## 研究动机\n当一个视觉语言模型对着图片一步步推理却答错时，错误可能来自两种很不一样的原因：要么它看错了图片显示的内容（视觉错误），要么它图看对了、却对抽取出的事实推理错了（逻辑错误）。这两种情况的修法正好相反——前者要重新看图，后者要重新推理。但今天的质量检查器，即 process reward model（逐步给推理链打分的模型），每一步只给一个分数，说'这一步看起来错了'，却说不清错在哪一类。GroundedPRM（2025，用树搜索校验每步的打分器）甚至会写出解释，但它全程用文本和工具来校验，所以从不知道问题出在'看'还是'想'。PURE（2025）和 Beyond-Correctness（2025）改的是分数如何聚合，但每一步的判定依旧是一个基于文本的单一数字。与此同时，2025 年的若干细致研究（Hidden-in-Plain-Sight；一项视觉推理一致性分析）表明：恰恰在图片有误导时，视觉语言模型会悄无声息地出错——但这些研究只是测量了问题，并没有造出能标记并指认出错faculty的检查器。现在这件事可解，因为开源的 7B 视觉语言模型已足够强，能充当一个可以重新聚焦到某个图像区域的检查器，而逐步标注的多模态推理数据集也已经存在可供训练。补上这个缺口意味着：检查器不只说'这条链坏了'，而是说'去修看的部分'或'去修想的部分'，从而让系统把有限的重试预算花在正确的修复上，而不是盲目重采样。\n\n## 方法\n### 模态路由器（Modality Router）\n*为每一步计算 modality-of-dependence 标签，使验证器知道该步依赖哪个faculty。*\n\n1. 给每个推理步骤标注其正确性依赖于什么：visual-grounding(视觉接地，VG，依赖图像)、textual-inference(文本推断，TI，依赖前面已陈述的事实)，或 cross-modal(跨模态，CM，依赖一个视觉论断与一个文本论断是否相符)。一个小型 router(路由器)自动完成此事：一个冻结的 vision-language model(视觉语言模型，VLM)读入整幅图像、一份固定的判定说明(把三条标准写明)、前面的步骤以及当前步骤；其内部表示经平均池化后，由训练好的一层线性头输出三个分数。取最高分，但若最高两类分数相差在 0.15 以内，则归为 CM。为给这层线性头制作 2000-3000 条训练标签，对每个步骤检查两次：把图像置空，看该步骤的正确性是否翻转(翻转则为 VG)；若置空无影响、但删去它所引用的前序步骤会翻转，则为 TI；若两种改动都会翻转，则为 CM。\n\n*路由器将步骤 $s_{t}$ 与图像 I 映射为 VG/TI/CM 三类分布，取 argmax 作为分区；当最高两类的间隔小于阈值 $\\tau _{route} = 0.15$ 时归入 CM。*\n$$ m(s_t) = \\arg\\max_{k \\in \\{VG, TI, CM\\}} p_\\phi(k \\mid s_t, I), \\quad \\text{assign CM if } p_{(1)} - p_{(2)} < \\tau_{route} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 只有先知道每一步依赖哪个faculty，才能把错误归因到faculty；而且这个标签要自动算出，而非外部给定。\n\n### 分区生成式验证器（Partitioned Generative Verifier）\n*一个配三个定制faculty头的 VLM，输出归因到责任模态的错误标签及植根证据的解释。*\n\n2. 从一个开源的 7B vision-language model(视觉语言模型，VLM)出发，在共享主干上加三个小型检查头(各为一个两层网络)，每个 faculty(能力维度)一个。验证器读入图像、前面的步骤、当前步骤以及 router 给出的 faculty 标签，先输出一个错误标签(VG-fault / TI-fault / CM-fault / ok)作为首个 token，再给出植根于该 faculty 证据的解释。三种检查各不相同：对视觉步骤，模型先输出相关图像区域的一个边界框，该区域被裁剪后回传给它，由它复核该视觉论断是否真的成立；对推断步骤，则遮住图像，对照前面的步骤核查该推导；对跨模态步骤，核查所指的视觉论断与所指的文本论断是否一致。训练所用的标准解释来自已知的注入错误(取自下文的受控集)：它会指明被破坏的区域、或被违背的前序步骤、或相互冲突的两条论断。\n\n*生成式验证器 V 以图像、前缀链、当前步骤与预测分区 m 为条件，先输出结构化错误标签作为首个 token，再给出植根于该分区证据的解释 j。*\n$$ V(I, s_{<t}, s_t, m) \\rightarrow \\langle \\text{tag} \\rangle \\cdot j, \\quad \\text{tag} \\in \\{\\text{VG-fault}, \\text{TI-fault}, \\text{CM-fault}, \\text{ok}\\} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 不同种类的错误需要不同的检查；一个共享模型配三个定制头，能把错误归因到具体faculty，而不是给一个不加区分的分数。\n3. 通过故意注入 faculty 已知的错误来制作训练标签(用下文的受控流程)，使每个步骤都有'是哪个 faculty 出错'的真值。把每个被破坏的步骤与其原始干净版本配对来组建训练数据，对较少出现的 faculty 进行上采样，使三类错误出现频率相等，并保持干净步骤与破坏步骤 1:1 混合，让模型学到符合实际的基础比率。训练验证器：最小化错误标签上的分类损失，加上植根证据解释上的文本生成损失，解释损失权重取 0.5。\n\n*训练目标为错误标签头上的交叉熵加上植根证据解释的生成损失，权重 $\\lambda _{just} = 0.5$。*\n$$ \\mathcal{L} = \\mathcal{L}_{CE}(\\text{tag}) + \\lambda_{just} \\, \\mathcal{L}_{gen}(j), \\quad \\lambda_{just} = 0.5 \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 诚实的逐faculty标签——而非模型自评——才能让各个头学会指向正确的faculty。\n\n### 保真分解证据（Fidelity-Decomposition Evidence）\n*把 $e_{t} = e_{t}^{VG} + e_{t}^{TI} + e_{t}^{CM}$ 分解转化为低于单标量下界的、可测的归因准确率差距。*\n\n4. 测量归因准确率：在所有被故意破坏的步骤中，验证器预测的 faculty 标签与实际注入的 faculty 相符的比例。再构建'单一数字下界'：把完全相同的模型重新训练，但用一个'坏/好'二值分数取代三类 faculty 头，并在同样的数据上训练、把 faculty 标签平均掉。它的 faculty 准确率就等于在各 faculty 间均匀随机猜测的水平，因为一个'坏/好'分数不含任何 faculty 信息——这就是下界。报告真实验证器与该下界之间的差距。所谓分解(真实的步骤误差分成视觉部分、推断部分与跨模态部分，每个被破坏步骤恰有一部分激活)正说明：这个差距意味着验证器还原出了单一数字无法承载的'是哪个 faculty'的信息。\n\n*真实步骤误差按各faculty可加分解（匹配构造下仅一项激活）；分区验证器的归因误差期望被路由误差加各头误差所界定，严格低于必须将三维向量压成其和的单标量下界 $\\epsilon _{scalar}$。*\n$$ e_t = e_t^{VG} + e_t^{TI} + e_t^{CM}, \\qquad \\mathbb{E}[\\text{attr-err}] \\leq \\epsilon_{route} + \\max_k \\epsilon_{head}^{k} \\; < \\; \\epsilon_{scalar}^{floor} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 分解 $e_{t} = e_{t}^{VG} + e_{t}^{TI} + e_{t}^{CM}$ 表明单一数字必然对各faculty求平均、无法还原是哪一个出错——测得的差距证明这种切分是真实的，而非换个标签。\n\n### 模态匹配纠错（Modality-Matched Correction）\n*把归因判定导入faculty特定的重跑，使下游胜过无定向重采样。*\n\n5. 用判定结果来重试。验证器给每一步打分；它标记为错误的第一步获得一次与 faculty 匹配的定向重试：视觉错误则在强制重新查看被标记的图像区域的情况下重跑该步，推断错误则遮住图像、固定视觉前提后重跑推理；随后重新生成链条的其余部分。与把同等重试预算花在普通额外采样上的做法相比较，两种方法都按验证器判为'无误'的步骤数来挑选最终答案。【作者需决定：纠错是单轮一次，还是反复进行直到不再有错误标签；以及当存在多次重试时，如何把重试预算与普通重采样对齐——这是作者需在'一次性纠错对迭代纠错'这一维度上确定的选择。】报告纠正后链条的最终答案准确率与普通重采样基线的对比。\n   - _为什么_: 定位到具体faculty的判定只有改变下一步行动才有用；把修复对准出错的faculty应当胜过盲目重试。\n\n### 受控分离与对照（Controlled Separation + Controls）\n*匹配注入分离集，加上基线与标签随机化负对照，证明分区即机制。*\n\n6. 构建一个受控测试集。取匹配的推理步骤，在保持该步骤措辞与所有前序步骤完全不变的前提下，为每个步骤制作两个被破坏版本。视觉(VG)版本：找到该步骤视觉论断所依赖的图像区域(用一个 open-vocabulary(开放词表)目标检测器，以该论断中的词作为提示)，仅编辑该区域使论断变假——用 inpainting(图像补全)抹除目标、给目标改色、或增删一个实例——而保持每个词与图像其余部分原封不动。推断(TI)版本：找到当前步骤所引用的某个前序步骤，对其结论做最小改动使之变为矛盾结论(把一个谓词改成其否定、换入一个同类干扰项、或改动一个数字)，使当前步骤如今基于一个假前提进行推理。注入内容的精确记录(哪个区域与何种编辑，或哪个前序步骤与何种改动)即为答案标准，且独立于验证器。\n   - _为什么_: 除了'破坏了哪个faculty'之外其余全部固定，从而隔离出你关心的唯一变量，于是任何高于随机的归因准确率都必然来自读取模态，而非表面线索。\n7. 进行对比实验。基线：(i)一个不看图像的纯文本步骤打分器；(ii)一个通用多模态 critic(评判器)——同一个 vision-language model，在相同数据上用单一'坏/好'分数微调，含图像但无 faculty 标签、无 router，因此与真实验证器的唯一区别就是缺少 faculty 分区；(iii)真实验证器。对这三者，报告受控集上的 faculty 归因准确率与留出题目上的下游纠错准确率。随后做关键对照：打乱 router 的 faculty 标签(训练与测试时都打乱)，使检查头不再与步骤真正依赖的 faculty 对齐，重新训练并重新评估——应当看到下游纠错增益塌回到普通重采样水平，从而证明增益来自 faculty 标签而非解释文字。\n   - _为什么_: 基线表明分区相对于强的统一检查器与廉价替代方案都有额外收益，而打乱对照证明收益来自模态标签而非解释文字。\n\n"},{"id":"52","run_dir":"run_prompt52_gepa","index":52,"title":"Typed Failure-Trace Credit: Reflective Prompt Evolution as Preference Optimization over Violated Constraints","title_zh":"类型化失败轨迹信用分配：把反思式 prompt 演化重述为对被违反约束的偏好优化（versus GRPO）","method_name":"Typed Failure-Trace Credit (TFTC)","hook":"Reflective prompt optimizers and RL fine-tuners both throw away the one thing a language model can read off a single failed rollout — which specific constraint it violated, on which input — by collapsing every rollout to a scalar before credit is assigned. We show that carrying that violated-constraint trace as a typed, persistent credit object, and optimizing the prompt against constraint-resolution preferences rather than scalar fitness, makes reflective evolution localize improvements per rollout where scalar search cannot.","anchor_pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","anchor_pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","domain_category":"LLM Pretraining, Architecture & Scaling","patterns":[{"gap":"ADDITIVE (anchor candidate): No retrieved leaf produces, on a fixed rollout budget, a per-rollout improvement signal that survives at the granularity of an individual failed rollout's specific violated constraint — every optimizer (openalex:W4409362909, openalex:W4404310996, openalex:W4414876419) and every RL variant (openalex:W4417308124, openalex:W4416035874) collapses the rollout to a scalar before it can be used to localize the responsible prompt component, so the question of WHICH part of a","pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","sub_pattern":"C26 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by manufacturing a comparative supervisory signal at the granularity where credit assignment fails: each failed rollout is parsed into a typed constraint-violation record, and minimally-differing rollout pairs that share a correct prefix but diverge at exactly one violated constraint become preference pairs that drive a contrastive prompt-edit objective — relocating the unit of supervision from a per-prompt scalar fitness to a per-violated-constraint ordering.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"SUBTRACTIVE: No retrieved paper tests whether the rollout must be reduced to a scalar quantity (a fitness, an advantage, or a score-delta-summarised 'textual gradient') at the moment of credit assignment at all — every leaf, optimizer and RL alike, silently inherits scalar-collapse as the credit-assignment representation from their shared ancestor (scalar policy-gradient / scalar fitness), and none asks whether the credit-assignment channel could carry a non-scalar object instead.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","how_closed":"Framing move (audit/pivot): name the scalar-score locus as the representational locus where every optimizer and RL variant tacitly assumes the credit signal lives, then relocate the credit channel to a richer locus (the typed constraint-violation trace) the field treated as discardable. Companion deliverable (controlled_diagnostic_design): a confound-matched separation that holds base model, total rollout budget, and prompt-edit proposer fixed and toggles ONLY whether the credit channel is scalar or typed, isolating scalar-collapse — not extra compute, a stronger base model, or richer candidate prompts — as the quantity that bounds optimizer sample-efficiency.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"foundation/frontier models (LLMs): prompt optimization vs reinforcement learning for LLM adaptation","n_papers":40,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":25},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"openreview","n":2}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":10,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"PromSec: Prompt Optimization for Secure Generation of Functional Source Code with Large Language Models (LLMs)"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Prompt Optimization in Large Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"POEM: Interactive Prompt Optimization for Enhancing Multimodal Reasoning of Large Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"iPrOp: Interactive Prompt Optimization for Large Language Models with a Human in the Loop"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Automatic Prompt Generation and Optimization by Leveraging Large Language Models to Enhance Few-Shot Learning in Biomedical Tasks"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Robust Prompt Optimization for Defending Language Models Against Jailbreaking Attacks"}],"more":4},{"year":2025,"n":28,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Promptomatix: An Automatic Prompt Optimization Framework for Large Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"PR-Attack: Coordinated Prompt-RAG Attacks on Retrieval-Augmented Generation in Large Language Models via Bilevel Optimization"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"PMPO: Probabilistic Metric Prompt Optimization for Small and Large Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Reinforcement Learning for Prompt Optimization in Language Models: A Comprehensive Survey of Methods, Representations, and Evaluation Challenges"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Veracity‐Oriented Context‐Aware Large Language Models–Based Prompting Optimization for Fake News Detection"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Adaptive Resource Allocation Optimization Using Large Language Models in Dynamic Wireless Environments"}],"more":22},{"year":2026,"n":2,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"},{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"}],"more":0}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":15,"share":0.375},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":13,"share":0.325},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":6,"share":0.15},{"pattern_id":"relax_discrete_search_to_continuous","pattern_name":"Relax Discrete Search to Continuous","count":6,"share":0.15},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":6,"share":0.15},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":4,"share":0.1},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":4,"share":0.1},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":3,"share":0.075}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Across the retrieved automatic-prompt-optimization frontier, every candidate prompt is evaluated by collapsing its rollouts to a SCALAR before that evaluation is allowed to drive the next proposal: SPRIG's edit-based genetic search ranks prompts by a scalar fitness over held-out accuracy (openalex:W4404310996), the LLM-as-optimizer line refines prompts from a 'textual gradient' that is itself summarised from aggregate score deltas (openalex:W4409362909), and the evolutionary multi-objective and Pareto lines (openalex:W4413215907; openalex:W4414876419) still drive mutation/selection from scalar objective vectors rather than from the specific failure traces of individual rollouts. The parallel RL-for-LLM line (openalex:W4417308124; openalex:W4416035874) does the same compression from the other side — a rollout becomes one scalar advantage — and even when it notices that discarded negative rollouts contain self-reflection and error-correction content (openalex:W4416035874) it re-injects them only as more scalar-weighted gradient signal. The structural failure is therefore not 'RL is sample-inefficient' per se but that, on a fixed rollout budget, the information an LLM can read off a single failed rollout in natural language (which constraint was violated, on which input, why) is thrown away at the moment of credit assignment by BOTH families, so neither can localize an improvement to the responsible prompt component faster than scalar search allows, and the supposed advantage of language-level reflection over reward-level optimization has never been isolated as a measurable quantity.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4409362909","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Frames an LLM as a prompt optimizer by analogy to a gradient-based model optimizer, identifying 'update direction' (a textual gradient) and 'update method' as the two pivotal factors and showing iterative LLM refinement improves task prompts. Its residue is that the textual gradient it constructs is summarised from AGGREGATE score deltas over a minibatch of examples, so it never assigns credit at the level of an individual failed rollout's specific violated constraint, and it carries no notion of a trade-off frontier — a single scalar-driven update direction collapses multiple competing objectives (and multiple distinct failure modes) into one edit, which is exactly the localization a reflective evolutionary scheme would need to beat RL on a fixed budget. [residue is abstract-level: anchor fulltext unfetchable]"},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4414876419","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Pareto Prompt Optimization maintains a Pareto front of prompts over multiple objectives rather than collapsing them to one scalar, addressing the trade-off-blindness of single-objective prompt search. Its residue is that the front is populated and advanced by scalar-fitness-driven evolution: the candidates that fill the frontier are still proposed without reading the natural-language failure trace of the rollouts that scored them, so the frontier records WHERE prompts sit in objective space but not WHY a given rollout failed, leaving the reflective credit-assignment channel unused."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4404310996","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"SPRIG improves general system prompts with an edit-based genetic algorithm assembling prompts from prespecified components to maximize a scalar fitness. Its residue is that genetic operators (which component to add/remove/reorder) are selected by scalar fitness feedback alone; the algorithm never inspects the model's natural-language error on the rollouts that produced that fitness, so it cannot attribute a fitness drop to the specific component responsible and must rediscover that attribution through many scalar-ranked generations."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416035874","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Policy Optimization with Negative Sample Augmentation observes that negative rollouts discarded by RFT/RL contain valuable self-reflection and error-correction steps, and re-weights tokens to exploit them. Its residue is that this reflective content is re-introduced only as token-level scalar reweighting inside the same policy-gradient objective (weight-space RL), never as a natural-language signal that edits an explicit prompt/program — so the reflective information is acknowledged but immediately re-compressed to a scalar advantage."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4417308124","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"RePO (Replay-Enhanced Policy Optimization) attacks GRPO's rollout cost and low data efficiency by replaying off-policy samples from a buffer so each prompt's update draws on a broader sample set. Its residue is that replay reuses rollouts only as additional scalar-advantage estimates; the buffer stores trajectories for reward statistics, not the failure rationale of each trajectory, so sample efficiency is bought without ever recovering the per-rollout language signal that reflection would use."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"foundation/frontier models (LLMs): prompt optimization vs reinforcement learning for LLM adaptation","venue":"ICLR/NeurIPS (foundation models track)","time":"2026","data":["instruction-following / reasoning benchmarks with verifiable or scored outputs (e.g. math, multi-hop QA, code, instruction tasks) where both a prompt optimizer and an RL fine-tuner can be run on the same base model"],"compute":"1×A100 × 3 months ≈ 90 A100-day","expertise":"LLM adaptation, prompt optimization, policy-gradient RL for LLMs","preference":"both","baseline":"scalar-fitness automatic prompt optimization (SPRIG genetic edits openalex:W4404310996; LLM-as-optimizer textual-gradient refinement openalex:W4409362909) and rollout-based RL fine-tuning (GRPO-style policy optimization openalex:W4417308124)","limitation":"reflective natural-language feedback can drive prompt evolution, but it is unclear what quantity makes reflective evolution beat scalar-reward RL on the same rollout budget — existing prompt optimizers reduce each rollout to a scalar fitness and discard the textual error trace, while RL reduces it to a scalar advantage and discards it too","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type","compute"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared audit lens (coherence thread = shared_audit) is the SCALAR-COLLAPSE LOCUS: the single point in every retrieved optimizer and RL variant where a rollout is reduced to one scalar before it influences the next proposal. The anchor leg (self_supervised_signal_engineering, C26) attacks it by manufacturing a non-scalar credit object. Define, for each candidate prompt p and each evaluation input x, a rollout r=(x,p,y) producing output y. A fixed task-specific CONSTRAINT CHECKLIST K = {k_1,...,k_m} is supplied once per task (m typically 5-30): each k_j is a boolean program-or-judge predicate over (x,y) — e.g. for math, 'final answer matches gold' / 'units stated' / 'no arithmetic step skipped'; for instruction tasks, format and content predicates. Each predicate is evaluated by an external verifier where one exists (exact-match, unit test, regex) and by a frozen judge LLM otherwise; the source per predicate is recorded so verifier-backed predicates carry full weight w_verifier=1.0 and judge-backed ones a discounted weight w_judge=0.5 (a named hyperparameter). The TYPED FAILURE-TRACE of rollout r is the vector v(r) in {0,1}^m of violated predicates, tagged with which prompt component (system instruction span, exemplar, formatting clause) the proposer most recently edited — this is the persistent credit object, accumulated across visits in a per-(prompt-component, constraint) violation-count table V (rows = prompt components, columns = constraints), so credit survives at rollout granularity instead of being summed away. From V we build PREFERENCE PAIRS: harvest two rollouts (r_+, r_-) that share an otherwise-identical prefix (same x, same prompt lineage) but differ at exactly one violated constraint k_j, label r_+ preferred, and attribute the contrast to the prompt component whose edit history most reduces V[component][j]. The prompt-edit proposer (a frozen LLM) is then optimized NOT by ranking prompts on scalar fitness but by a contrastive objective: among proposed edits to the implicated component, prefer the edit predicted to flip k_j from violated to satisfied on the held-out batch, scored by the realized drop in column j of V. Because the credit object is typed and persistent, the proposer receives a gradient-like signal that points at the responsible (component, constraint) cell rather than at a global score. The sibling leg (assumption_audit_and_pivot, C01) names this relocation explicitly as the contribution — the credit channel is moved off the scalar-score locus onto the typed-trace locus — and its companion (controlled_diagnostic_design) ships the matched-confound separation: an A/B where arm A passes only scalar fitness to the same proposer and arm B passes the typed V table, identical base model, identical total rollouts, identical proposer, so any sample-efficiency gap is attributable to the credit representation alone. The two legs share the V table as the single audited object: the anchor builds it, the audit interrogates the assumption that it could be collapsed to a scalar, and the diagnostic measures what collapsing it costs.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules: both the additive 'build a rollout-granular signal' gap and the subtractive 'must the channel be scalar?' gap read from and write to the SAME object (the typed violation-count table V), so a shared_audit thread on the scalar-collapse locus binds them into one paper — the audit is literally the question 'can V be replaced by its scalar collapse without loss?', which the anchor answers no and the diagnostic quantifies. (b) Alternatives rejected: (i) an architectural_operator_substitution framing (swap the advantage operator) was the Phase 2.1 top rank, but its sub-clusters (C12 macro-plumbing, C14 attention cost, C30 curvature-spectral, C09 privacy-sensitivity) each demand a preserved-property of the WRONG kind (a spectral or expressivity proof), so the honest deliverable would mismatch a method paper — re-picked to the anchor_alternate self_supervised_signal_engineering whose C26 sub-cluster ships a runnable contrastive-signal method; (ii) a Pareto-frontier leg was deferred because it is the seed source paper's own move; (iii) using the typed trace only for one-shot self-critique (lineage node c0) was rejected as a regression — the persistence of V across visits is what distinguishes this from Reflexion-style single-retry critique.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on two task families with cheap verifiers (GSM8K-style math and an instruction-following set such as IFEval) and one base model (e.g. an 8B open model), run three arms at a single matched rollout budget — typed-credit evolution (arm B), scalar-fitness evolution (arm A, identical proposer), and GRPO — and measure held-out task accuracy as a function of rollouts consumed. If the candidate works, arm B reaches a fixed target accuracy at strictly fewer rollouts than both arm A and GRPO, and its per-iteration accuracy gain concentrates on exactly the constraints whose V-column mass it targeted (the gain is localized, not diffuse). The named load-bearing variable is the typed violation-count table V (specifically its (component, constraint) attribution structure). Negative control: replace V with a SHUFFLED table that preserves the marginal violation counts per constraint but RANDOMLY permutes the (component, constraint) attribution before the proposer reads it — this keeps the same scalar information and the same total violation mass but destroys the localization. Prediction: under the shuffled control, arm B's held-out accuracy-vs-rollouts curve should collapse back to arm A's (scalar) curve — the downstream task metric, not V's own value — because the only thing removed is the attribution that lets credit localize. A positive control is the stripped-down proposer that conditions on nothing but the single highest-mass (component, constraint) cell of V: if that recovers most of arm B's advantage over arm A, the typed attribution is confirmed as the mechanism rather than incidental extra context.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4409362909","delta":"They construct an 'update direction' (textual gradient) summarised from aggregate score deltas over a minibatch and apply a single scalar-driven update; we construct a typed per-rollout violation-count table that attributes each violated constraint to a specific prompt component and drive edits from that attribution, so credit localizes at rollout granularity rather than at minibatch-aggregate granularity."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4414876419","delta":"Pareto Prompt Optimization maintains a frontier over multiple scalar objective vectors but proposes the candidates that fill it without reading rollout failure traces; we propose candidates from the failure-trace attribution itself and never form a scalar objective vector, so the contribution is the typed credit channel, not multi-objective frontier bookkeeping."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416035874","delta":"They notice negative rollouts contain self-reflection/error-correction content and re-weight tokens inside the same scalar policy-gradient objective (weight-space); we keep the model frozen and convert that content into a persistent typed preference object that edits an explicit prompt, so the reflective signal is consumed as structured credit rather than re-compressed to a scalar token weight."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4417308124","delta":"RePO replays off-policy rollouts to broaden scalar-advantage estimates; we replay rollouts as typed violation records keyed by (component, constraint), so reuse recovers per-rollout failure rationale rather than only additional reward statistics."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4404310996","delta":"SPRIG selects genetic edits by scalar fitness over assembled components; we select edits by predicted flip of a specific violated constraint attributed to a specific component, replacing scalar-fitness ranking with constraint-resolution preference."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4409362909","what_step_was_missed":"The LLM-as-optimizer line constructs its 'textual gradient' by summarising aggregate score deltas into a single natural-language update direction per iteration; to already contain our contribution it would have needed to construct a PERSISTENT typed attribution structure — a (prompt-component × constraint) violation table accumulated across visits whose entries license minimally-differing constraint-level preference pairs — and to optimize edits against that attribution rather than against the summarised direction. That accumulation-and-attribution construction (not merely 'use text instead of a number') is the step absent: their update direction is recomputed and re-collapsed each iteration, so it structurally cannot carry rollout-granular credit forward the way the violation table does."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":211,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"No hard floor fired: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict = borderline (no entry triggered; no Reject lesson marked candidate_match: yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id = null, and paper_pointed_threat with GEPA is adjacency rather than exact-mechanism overlap (subsumption_argument: GEPA's credit channel is free-form NL reflection recomputed per attempt and aggregated by a scalar-objective Pareto frontier, carrying no persistent typed (component×constraint) attribution object). recipe_application_check.verdict = applied for both legs, so the idea is not built from the parent's generic gist. The verdict is revise (not advance) because the two load-bearing borderlines hit the central differentiation surface: the anchor lesson 'Changing only the granularity of an established contrastive objective ... is judged incremental unless paired with a clearly demonstrated practical unlock' requires the contribution to be foregrounded as persistence+typing rather than granularity, and the sibling lesson 'Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work ... collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured' requires the GEPA / textual-gradient difference to be measured — and paper_pointed_threat.addressable_via names the specific fields (differentiation_from_lit GEPA entry + what_step_was_missed) that must change to firm the dodge. Kill-switch fields (falsification_prediction, compute_budget) are NOT in revision scope and must pass through byte-identical.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"ADDITIVE (anchor candidate): No retrieved leaf produces, on a fixed rollout budget, a per-rollout improvement signal that survives at the granularity of an individual failed rollout's specific violated constraint — every optimizer (openalex:W4409362909, openalex:W4404310996, openalex:W4414876419) and every RL variant (openalex:W4417308124, openalex:W4416035874) collapses the rollout to a scalar before it can be used to localize the responsible prompt component, so the question of WHICH part of a candidate's failure trace should drive the next proposal is never answered at rollout granularity.","main_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","sub_pattern":"C26 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The dominant failure is the single-component swap: the paper takes the established preference pipeline and changes exactly one slot — human labels to an AI judge, response-level to step-level granularity — then presents that swap as the contribution, which reviewers read as incremental because it unlocks no behavior previously unreachable. A second shape is stopping short of the loop: shipping a preference dataset or reward model without the downstream optimization that consumes it.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Swapping the preference-label source (human → AI judge, offline → online) without showing the swap unlocks a behavior previously unreachable reads as a one-component substitution and draws novelty rejections.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate does not swap a label source; it changes the representational object the credit channel carries (scalar fitness → persistent typed (component×constraint) violation table) and demonstrates the previously-unreachable behavior of per-rollout localization, so it is not a one-slot substitution."},{"lesson_quoted":"Stopping at the preference dataset, benchmark, or reward model without demonstrating the downstream optimization it is meant to feed leaves the contribution looking like infrastructure rather than method.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism_steps 6–10 run the full downstream loop (proposer optimization against the contrastive objective, held-out accuracy-vs-rollouts curves vs scalar arm and GRPO), so the manufactured signal is consumed by an optimizer, not shipped as a standalone artifact."},{"lesson_quoted":"Changing only the granularity of an established contrastive objective (response-level → step-level) is judged incremental unless paired with a clearly demonstrated practical unlock.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The move re-granularizes credit from per-prompt scalar to per-(component,constraint), which superficially resembles a granularity change; it is defended by the PERSISTENCE of V across visits and the shuffle/positive controls demonstrating the localization is the practical unlock, but the candidate must make explicit that persistence+typing (not granularity alone) is the contribution or a reviewer reads it as the flagged granularity-only change."},{"lesson_quoted":"Borrowing a structurally related proxy domain to synthesize preference data, without validating that the proxy's regularities transfer to the target's end-goal metric, invites rigor and generalization concerns.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Preference pairs are harvested in-distribution from the model's own rollouts on the target tasks (GSM8K-style math, IFEval), not from a proxy domain, and the end-goal metric (held-out task accuracy) is measured directly."},{"lesson_quoted":"Combining off-the-shelf components (parameter-efficient adaptation plus self-distillation) for a known problem fails the novelty bar when concurrent work performs the same combination.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate freezes the base model and proposer entirely (no fine-tuning, no distillation) and contributes the typed persistent credit object, not an assembly of off-the-shelf adaptation components."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"SUBTRACTIVE: No retrieved paper tests whether the rollout must be reduced to a scalar quantity (a fitness, an advantage, or a score-delta-summarised 'textual gradient') at the moment of credit assignment at all — every leaf, optimizer and RL alike, silently inherits scalar-collapse as the credit-assignment representation from their shared ancestor (scalar policy-gradient / scalar fitness), and none asks whether the credit-assignment channel could carry a non-scalar object instead.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"A recurring failure is a novelty-boundary collapse — the 'new' locus turns out to be one a prior paper already used — and the work fails to quantify what is genuinely different. Another is offering only a demonstration with no mechanistic account of why the locus carries the signal, which reads as a stacked pipeline of off-the-shelf parts.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work — normalization statistics, activation-similarity losses, semantic concept triggers — collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The textual-gradient line (openalex:W4409362909) and GEPA's NL reflection already move the credit channel off a bare scalar toward language, so the 'typed-trace locus' is adjacent to a published locus; the candidate's what_step_was_missed makes the difference (PERSISTENT typed (component×constraint) accumulation vs per-iteration re-summarised text) explicit, but the differentiation_from_lit entry for W4409362909 must measure this difference, not merely assert it, to clear the boundary."},{"lesson_quoted":"Demonstrating the new locus only on fixed, non-adaptive or outdated baselines while omitting any account of why it works reads as a stacked pipeline of existing components rather than a principled shift.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate supplies a mechanistic account (the V table structurally carries rollout-granular credit that a re-collapsed scalar/text summary cannot) and a non-tautological shuffle control on the (component,constraint) attribution that drives held-out accuracy back to the scalar arm, which is the why-it-works evidence the lesson demands."},{"lesson_quoted":"A defense whose relocation silently depends on a clean reference model or a known anomaly distribution reintroduces precisely the strong assumption the move was supposed to eliminate.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The relocation depends only on a task-supplied constraint checklist K (verifier- or frozen-judge-backed) evaluated on the model's own rollouts; it does not require a clean reference model or a pre-specified anomaly distribution, so it does not smuggle back the assumption it audits."},{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a relocated signal is 'stealthier' or 'harder to remove' without defeating an adaptive defender who searches the same new locus leaves the central claim unverified.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"This lesson is adversarial-security-specific; the candidate makes no stealthiness/evasion claim — its claim (sample-efficiency at fixed rollout budget) is verified by matched-confound A/B and a GRPO baseline, not against an adaptive adversary, so the lesson does not apply."},{"lesson_quoted":"Wiring off-the-shelf generators or tools into a new attack setting without a structural reason for the locus change gets judged as engineering integration, not insight.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The locus change is structurally motivated — a scalar provably cannot localize which constraint a rollout violated, so the typed trace is the minimal object that restores rollout-granular credit — rather than an opportunistic tool-wiring."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No entry is triggered (no Reject lesson marked candidate_match: yes). Two borderlines carry weight: on the anchor (self_supervised_signal_engineering) the lesson 'Changing only the granularity of an established contrastive objective ... is judged incremental unless paired with a clearly demonstrated practical unlock' is borderline because the persistence/typing of V — not granularity alone — must be foregrounded as the contribution; and on the sibling (assumption_audit_and_pivot) the lesson 'Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work ... collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured' is borderline because the differentiation from the textual-gradient line (W4409362909) and GEPA must be measured, not asserted."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"ADDITIVE (anchor candidate): No retrieved leaf produces, on a fixed rollout budget, a per-rollout improvement signal that survives at the granularity of an individual failed rollout's specific violated constraint — every optimizer (openalex:W4409362909, openalex:W4404310996, openalex:W4414876419) and every RL variant (openalex:W4417308124, openalex:W4416035874) collapses the rollout to a scalar before it can be used to localize the responsible prompt component, so the question of WHICH part of a candidate's failure trace should drive the next proposal is never answered at rollout granularity.","sub_pattern":"C26 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Manufacture a comparative signal from a non-human source, then optimize against it with a contrastive/preference objective; re-granularize the comparison to match where credit assignment fails, and construct each pair to differ minimally — ideally at exactly one faulty transition sharing an otherwise-correct prefix — so the contrast isolates the error.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism_steps 4–6 perform exactly this signature move: step 4 accumulates the typed violation trace (the non-human comparative source from program/judge verifiers), step 5 harvests preference pairs (r_+, r_-) that 'share an x and a prompt prefix but differ at exactly one violated constraint k_j' — the minimally-differing-pair-sharing-correct-prefix construction verbatim — and step 6 optimizes the proposer with a contrastive objective (predicted flip of k_j) rather than scalar-fitness ranking. This is the cluster's distinctive move, not the parent's generic 'make up a signal'.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"SUBTRACTIVE: No retrieved paper tests whether the rollout must be reduced to a scalar quantity (a fitness, an advantage, or a score-delta-summarised 'textual gradient') at the moment of credit assignment at all — every leaf, optimizer and RL alike, silently inherits scalar-collapse as the credit-assignment representation from their shared ancestor (scalar policy-gradient / scalar fitness), and none asks whether the credit-assignment channel could carry a non-scalar object instead.","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Name the single representational locus that current methods all operate on, state the tacit sufficiency claim bolted to it as a falsifiable proposition, then relocate the signal to an alternative locus the field treated as invariant — the unifying verbs are 'relocate the signal' and 're-anchor enforcement' — and supply a mechanistic account of WHY the new locus carries the signal.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"The sibling leg names the SCALAR-COLLAPSE LOCUS ('the single point in every retrieved optimizer and RL variant where a rollout is reduced to one scalar before it influences the next proposal') as the audited locus and relocates the credit channel onto the typed-trace locus (the V table), with the why-account supplied by what_step_was_missed (a re-collapsed scalar/text summary structurally cannot carry rollout-granular credit forward; the persistent typed table can). This is the cluster's relocate-the-locus move, validated by the controlled_diagnostic_design companion's matched-confound A/B that toggles only scalarization.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries instantiate their cluster's signature move in core_mechanism: C26's minimally-differing-preference-pair construction at the credit-assignment-failure granularity (steps 5–6) and C01's name-the-locus-then-relocate-the-signal with a mechanistic why-account (sibling leg + what_step_was_missed). Neither leg merely enacts the parent's generic gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["self_supervised_signal_engineering","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three reject-favored compositions in anti-patterns.md require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component (audit_decomp_supervisor, audit_decomp_prior, audit_decomp_operator); the candidate's composition_set contains neither heterogeneous_decomposition nor any matching 2-way subset, so no anti-pattern fires."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:f1c0aad419cd942d5a135b47fcce58d101dbb3bd","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"GEPA (the seed's own source paper) is the central adjacency: it already establishes the headline claim space — that natural-language reflection over rollouts beats GRPO at far fewer rollouts on the same base model — and operationalizes reflective prompt evolution by sampling trajectories, reflecting on them in natural language to diagnose problems and propose prompt updates, and combining lessons from a Pareto frontier of its own attempts. If GEPA's natural-language reflection already carries per-rollout, per-constraint failure information into the next proposal, the candidate's contribution (a typed per-rollout credit object that localizes the responsible prompt component) would collapse into GEPA's mechanism and the paper would fall. The candidate stands BECAUSE GEPA's credit channel is free-form natural-language reflection RECOMPUTED per attempt and aggregated via a scalar-objective Pareto frontier — it carries no PERSISTENT, TYPED (prompt-component × constraint) attribution object accumulated across visits, and its frontier membership is decided by scalar objective vectors, so GEPA cannot answer 'which prompt component is responsible for which violated constraint' at rollout granularity nor optimize against constraint-resolution preference pairs. This is a genuine representational substitution at the credit-assignment locus (scalar/free-form-text → persistent typed table + minimally-differing constraint-resolution preferences, no Pareto), not GEPA's exact mechanism — so the overlap is adjacency, not subsumption.","addressable_via":"Sharpen the differentiation_from_lit GEPA entry and what_step_was_missed to MEASURE (not assert) that the persistent typed (component×constraint) accumulation and constraint-resolution preference pairs are absent from GEPA's free-form-reflection-plus-Pareto-frontier design, and ensure the shuffle negative control isolates the typed attribution (not language per se) as the load-bearing variable that separates the method from GEPA-style NL reflection."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit (add an explicit GEPA entry, threat_paper_id semanticscholar:f1c0aad419cd942d5a135b47fcce58d101dbb3bd)","issue":"paper_pointed_threat (GEPA adjacency) + C01 reject lesson 'Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work ... collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured'","fix_direction":"Add a differentiation_from_lit entry for GEPA stating the measured difference: GEPA reflects in free-form natural language RECOMPUTED per attempt and combines lessons via a Pareto frontier decided by scalar objective vectors, so it carries NO persistent typed (prompt-component × constraint) violation-count table and forms no constraint-resolution preference pairs; the candidate accumulates V across visits and optimizes the proposer against minimally-differing constraint-resolution preferences with no Pareto frontier — the contrast is persistent-typed-attribution vs per-attempt-NL-reflection-plus-scalar-frontier, and is the quantity the shuffle control isolates. Do NOT touch falsification_prediction or compute_budget."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"what_step_was_missed","issue":"C26 reject lesson 'Changing only the granularity of an established contrastive objective ... is judged incremental unless paired with a clearly demonstrated practical unlock'","fix_direction":"Reword what_step_was_missed to foreground PERSISTENCE + TYPING (the (component×constraint) table accumulated across visits) — not granularity alone — as the absent step, explicitly contrasting against both the textual-gradient line (re-collapsed each iteration) and GEPA (free-form NL reflection not accumulated as a typed object), and naming the practical unlock (per-rollout localization of the responsible prompt component that the shuffle control removes). Do NOT touch falsification_prediction or compute_budget."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit (prepended GEPA entry)","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added an explicit GEPA differentiation entry measuring the contrast persistent-typed-(component×constraint)-attribution vs GEPA's per-attempt free-form NL reflection plus scalar-objective Pareto frontier, naming the shuffle control as the isolator of typed attribution over language."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"what_step_was_missed","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Reworded to foreground PERSISTENCE + TYPING (V accumulated across visits) — not granularity alone — as the absent step, contrasting against both the textual-gradient line and GEPA, and naming the practical unlock (per-rollout localization removed by the shuffle control)."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Typed Failure-Trace Credit: Reflective Prompt Evolution as Preference Optimization over Violated Constraints\n\n**Method.** Typed Failure-Trace Credit (TFTC)\n\n## Motivation\nSuppose you want to make a large language model (LLM) better at a task, and you only have a fixed budget of trial runs ('rollouts'). Two popular approaches look different but share one hidden habit. Prompt optimizers keep the model's weights fixed and rewrite the prompt; reinforcement learning (RL) — for example GRPO (Group Relative Policy Optimization) — updates the weights from rewards. Either way, before the result of a trial run is allowed to influence the next change, it gets boiled down to a single number: a fitness score, an 'advantage', or a one-line summary of how the average score moved (the 'textual gradient' in the LLMs-as-optimizers line, openalex:W4409362909). The rich, readable thing an LLM could tell you about a failed run — exactly which requirement it broke, on which input, and why — is thrown away at that very moment.\n\nThis matters now because we finally have cheap, reliable per-requirement checkers for the tasks where people compare prompts against RL: exact-match and unit-test checkers for math and code, and small programs that check format and content for instruction-following tasks. For anything a program cannot check, a frozen judge LLM can score it at a reduced trust weight. Two recent surveys (semanticscholar:6d944d52fb6ada2ceed3e03e799ee08a3fc18e08; openalex:W4416035346) point out that RL is wasteful with its trials and that reflective alternatives are not well understood — but nobody has built the specific non-number credit signal that would explain the advantage.\n\nPrior work stops just short. SPRIG (openalex:W4404310996) ranks prompt edits by a single score and never reads the model's own description of what went wrong, so it has to rediscover which part of the prompt caused a problem over many generations. The LLMs-as-optimizers line (openalex:W4409362909) builds a text 'update direction' but recomputes and re-flattens it every round, so it cannot carry detailed blame forward. Pareto Prompt Optimization (openalex:W4414876419) keeps a set of trade-off prompts but decides membership by numeric objective vectors, so it records WHERE prompts sit, not WHY a run failed. And the RL paper that does notice failed runs contain useful self-correction (openalex:W4416035874) immediately squeezes that back into a single reward weight.\n\nIf we instead keep the blame as a structured, lasting record — a table that counts, for each editable piece of the prompt and each requirement, how often that piece is associated with breaking that requirement — the optimizer can read off which prompt piece to fix and target the exact requirement to repair. That turns 'reflection beats RL' from a slogan into something measurable: we can show it is the structured blame (not just 'using language') that does the work, and the approach directly improves on the textual-gradient and Pareto lines, which both leave the failure description unused at the moment a new prompt is proposed.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n*Standard prompt-population setup and budget-bounded iteration scaffolding.*\n\n1. Start from a seed prompt (a system instruction plus a few worked examples) and break it into editable pieces by role: each instruction sentence, each example, and each format directive is one piece with an id and a record of where it sits in the text. Create an empty table whose rows are these pieces and whose columns are the requirements from step step 3 (For each task), all counts starting at zero; this table is kept and added to for the entire run, never wiped.\n   - _Why_: The lasting table V is what makes this different from one-off self-criticism; it has to exist before the first run so blame can build up over time.\n2. Repeat steps step 4 (Run the current prompt through $the\\dots )$ through step 7 (Take the), subtracting each round's generations (the batch plus the re-evaluation of candidate rewrites) from the fixed trial budget, and stop when there are not enough trials left for a full round. Each round, measure accuracy on a separate held-out validation set to build the accuracy-versus-trials curve.\n   - _Why_: The accuracy-versus-trials curve is what you compare against the other methods at the same budget.\n\n### Typed failure-trace credit (contribution)\n*Turn each failed run into a typed broken-requirement vector and accumulate it into a persistent (prompt-piece x requirement) blame table.*\n\n3. For each task, write down m yes/no requirements over an (input, output) pair (e.g. 'final answer matches the gold answer', 'units are stated', 'no arithmetic step is skipped', 'output follows the required format'). Draft them by showing a fixed helper Large Language Model (LLM) the task description plus 5-10 correct examples. Implement every requirement a program can check directly as code (exact string match, running unit tests, regular-expression format checks); for the rest, ask a fixed, never-changed judge LLM a single yes/no question at its most deterministic setting and cache the answer. Program-checked requirements count fully (weight 1.0); judge-checked ones count half (weight 0.5). The result is a function that turns any (input, output) into a vector marking which requirements were broken. 【author decision: how many requirements and exactly which ones to use depends on the task and is for the authors to fix per benchmark.】\n   - _Why_: You can only carry blame at the level of 'which requirement broke' if you first define the requirements as checkable items.\n4. Run the current prompt through the frozen model on a batch of inputs (default 64 per round, drawn without repeats and cycling when used up), producing one answer per input with a moderate randomness setting so different failures show up. For each answer, use the checker from step step 3 (For each task) to record exactly which requirements were broken. Each generation counts as one trial against the fixed trial budget.\n\n*The typed failure-trace of rollout r is the length-m binary vector whose j-th entry is 1 when constraint $k_{j}$ is violated by output y on input x.*\n$$ v(r) \\in \\{0,1\\}^m, \\quad v_j(r) = \\mathbb{1}[\\, k_j(x,y) \\text{ violated}\\,], \\quad r=(x,p,y) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This produces the detailed, non-number record of each failure that the whole method depends on, and spending the budget here keeps it equal across all compared methods.\n5. For every run, add the broken-requirement weights into the table under the prompt piece that was most recently edited — found from each prompt's stored list of past edits (unedited seed prompts go to a single 'seed' row). Keep adding to the same table across rounds rather than rebuilding it.\n\n*For the most-recently-edited component c, each violated constraint j increments the persistent table entry V[c][j] by its source weight (verifier 1.0, judge 0.5); V is accumulated across visits, not re-summarised per iteration.*\n$$ V[c][j] \\leftarrow V[c][j] + w_j \\cdot v_j(r), \\quad w_j = \\begin{cases} 1.0 & \\text{verifier-backed} \\\\ 0.5 & \\text{judge-backed} \\end{cases} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Letting blame accumulate in a lasting, typed table is the core idea — it is what carries detailed credit forward, unlike a summary that gets recomputed and flattened every round.\n\n### Constraint-resolution preference optimization (contribution)\n*Convert the blame table into minimally-differing preference pairs and edit the implicated prompt piece to fix the targeted requirement.*\n\n6. Find pairs of runs on the same input whose prompts differ by at most their single most recent edit and whose broken-requirement sets differ in exactly one requirement; mark the run that satisfied that requirement as the better one, and attribute the difference to the prompt piece whose edits most lower that requirement's column in the table. If no such clean pair exists for a target cell, take the closest available pair (differing in at most two requirements, otherwise skip) and only credit the one requirement they share as different.\n\n*A preference pair shares an input and a prompt prefix and differs at exactly one violated constraint $k_{j}$; $r_+$ (which satisfied $k_{j})$ is preferred and the contrast is attributed to the component whose edits most reduce column j of V.*\n$$ (r_+, r_-) : x_+ = x_-,\\; \\mathrm{prefix}(r_+)=\\mathrm{prefix}(r_-),\\; v(r_-) \\setminus v(r_+) = \\{k_j\\} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Comparing two nearly-identical runs that differ in just one requirement isolates the cause cleanly, instead of confusing it with unrelated differences.\n7. Take the (prompt piece, requirement) cell with the most accumulated blame. Ask the frozen proposer Large Language Model (LLM) for several candidate rewrites of that piece (default 8), giving it the failing example and the exact requirement that broke, with instructions not to break requirements already satisfied. Re-run those rewrites on a held-out batch of inputs and keep the rewrite that most often flips that requirement from broken to satisfied; if several tie, prefer the one that least increases other broken requirements. 【author decision: how many candidate rewrites to request and how strongly to penalize collateral breakage are tunable and for the authors to set.】\n\n*Among candidate edits e to the implicated component c, select the one maximizing the predicted reduction of constraint-j violations on a held-out batch B (the realized drop in column j of V), i.e. the edit whose new outputs flip $k_{j}$ from violated to satisfied most often.*\n$$ e^{*} = \\arg\\max_{e \\in \\mathcal{E}(c)} \\; \\widehat{\\Delta}_j(e), \\quad \\widehat{\\Delta}_j(e) = \\mathbb{E}_{x \\sim \\mathcal{B}}\\big[\\, v_j(x,p) - v_j(x, p \\oplus e)\\,\\big] \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This points the editor straight at the responsible piece and the exact requirement to fix, instead of nudging the whole prompt by one global score.\n\n### Scalar-collapse diagnostic (contribution)\n*Toggle only whether the credit channel is a number or the typed table, against a GRPO baseline at the same budget, to isolate scalar-collapse as the bound.*\n\n8. Run two matched copies of the loop: in one (arm A) the editor sees only a single fitness number — the weighted average of how many requirements were met — and in the other (arm B) it sees the full blame table. Keep the model, total trials, editor, seed prompt, and data splits identical. Also run GRPO (Group Relative Policy Optimization), a standard reinforcement-learning method that updates the model's weights, on the same model and trial budget using the same weighted-average score as its reward (default group size 8, regularized to stay close to the original model). Compare all three accuracy-versus-trials curves. 【author decision: GRPO's learning rate and how strongly it is kept close to the original model are standard settings for the authors to choose.】\n   - _Why_: Changing only whether the credit is a number or a table isolates that single factor as the cause of any difference, and GRPO is the headline comparison.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 类型化失败轨迹信用分配：把反思式 prompt 演化重述为对被违反约束的偏好优化（versus GRPO）\n\n**方法名称.** Typed Failure-Trace Credit (TFTC)\n\n## 研究动机\n假设你想让一个 LLM 在某个任务上做得更好，而你只有固定数量的试运行（rollout）预算。两类常见做法看起来不同，却共享一个隐藏的习惯：prompt 优化器保持模型权重不变、只改写 prompt；强化学习（RL，例如 GRPO，Group Relative Policy Optimization）则用奖励更新权重。但无论哪种，在一次试运行的结果被允许影响下一步改动之前，它都会先被压缩成一个数字——一个 fitness 分数、一个 advantage，或者一句关于平均分如何变化的总结（即 LLMs-as-optimizers 路线 openalex:W4409362909 里的 textual gradient）。而 LLM 本可以告诉你的、关于一次失败运行的丰富可读信息——它到底违反了哪条要求、在哪个输入上、为什么——恰恰在这一刻被丢掉了。\n\n现在解决这个问题正当其时，因为在人们拿 prompt 和 RL 做比较的那些任务上，我们终于有了便宜又可靠的「逐条要求」检查器：数学和代码可用 exact-match 与单元测试，指令遵循任务可用检查格式与内容的小程序；程序检查不了的，可由一个冻结的 judge LLM 以打折的信任权重来打分。两篇近期综述（semanticscholar:6d944d52fb6ada2ceed3e03e799ee08a3fc18e08; openalex:W4416035346）都指出 RL 在试运行上很浪费、而反思式替代方案尚不清楚——但没人真正构造出那个能解释优势来源的「非数字」信用信号。\n\n已有工作都止步于此。SPRIG（openalex:W4404310996）按单一分数对 prompt 编辑排序，从不读取模型对「哪里出错」的自我描述，因而只能在很多代里反复试错才能找出是 prompt 的哪一部分出了问题。LLMs-as-optimizers 路线（openalex:W4409362909）构造了一个文本式的 update direction，却每一轮都重算并重新压扁它，无法把细粒度的归因往后传递。Pareto Prompt Optimization（openalex:W4414876419）维护一组权衡 prompt，但用数值目标向量决定其成员资格，因此只记录 prompt「在哪」，而非一次运行「为何」失败。那篇注意到失败运行含有有用自我纠错内容的 RL 论文（openalex:W4416035874），也立刻把它挤回成一个奖励权重。\n\n如果我们改为把「归因」保留为一份结构化、持久的记录——一张表，针对每个可编辑的 prompt 片段与每条要求，统计该片段与违反该要求关联的次数——优化器就能读出该修哪个 prompt 片段、并精确锁定要修复的那条要求。这就把「反思胜过 RL」从口号变成可度量的东西：我们能证明起作用的是这份结构化归因（而非仅仅「使用了语言」），并且该方法直接改进了 textual-gradient 与 Pareto 两条路线——它们在提出新 prompt 的那一刻，都没用上失败描述。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景\n*标准的 prompt 种群设置与预算受限的迭代脚手架。*\n\n1. 从一个种子 prompt（一条 system 指令加上几个示范例子）出发，按角色把它拆成可编辑的片段：每条指令句、每个示例、每条格式指令各为一个片段，带一个 id 和它在文本中位置的记录。建立一张空表，行是这些片段、列是步骤 第3步（为每个任务写下 m 条针对） 的各条要求，所有计数从零开始；这张表在整个运行过程中保留并持续累加，绝不清空。\n   - _为什么_: 这张持久的表 V 正是它区别于一次性自我批评之处；它必须在第一次运行前就存在，归因才能随时间累积。\n2. 重复步骤 第4步（在一批输入上） 到 第7步（取累积归因最多的），每轮从固定试运行预算中扣除该轮的生成次数（批次加上对候选改写的重评估），当剩余试运行不足以支撑完整一轮时停止。每轮在一个单独的留出验证集上测量准确率，以构建准确率-试运行曲线。\n   - _为什么_: 准确率-试运行曲线就是你在相同预算下与其他方法比较的对象。\n\n### 类型化失败轨迹信用（贡献）\n*把每次失败运行转成类型化的被违反要求向量，并累积进一张持久的 (prompt 片段 x 要求) 归因表。*\n\n3. 为每个任务写下 m 条针对(输入, 输出)的是/否要求（例如「最终答案与标准答案一致」「写明单位」「没有跳过算术步骤」「输出符合要求的格式」）。起草方式是把任务描述加上 5-10 个正确示例交给一个固定的辅助大语言模型(Large Language Model, LLM)。凡是程序能直接检查的要求都实现为代码（精确字符串匹配 exact-match、运行单元测试、正则格式检查）；其余的，则向一个固定且永不改动的 judge LLM 在其最确定性的设置下问一个是/否问题，并缓存答案。程序检查的要求记满权重(1.0)，judge 检查的记一半(0.5)。最终得到一个函数，把任意(输入, 输出)转成一个标记「哪些要求被违反」的向量。【作者需决定：用多少条要求、具体是哪些，取决于任务，需由作者按每个 benchmark 确定。】\n   - _为什么_: 只有先把要求定义为可检查的条目，你才能在「哪条要求被违反」这个粒度上携带归因。\n4. 在一批输入上（默认每轮 64 个，无放回抽取、用完则循环）让当前 prompt 跑过冻结模型，用适中的随机性设置为每个输入生成一个答案，以便暴露不同的失败。对每个答案，用步骤 第3步（为每个任务写下 m 条针对） 的检查器记录恰好哪些要求被违反。每次生成都算作固定试运行预算中的一次试运行。\n\n*rollout r 的类型化失败轨迹是一个长度为 m 的 0/1 向量，其第 j 个分量在输出 y 对输入 x 违反约束 $k_{j}$ 时取 1。*\n$$ v(r) \\in \\{0,1\\}^m, \\quad v_j(r) = \\mathbb{1}[\\, k_j(x,y) \\text{ violated}\\,], \\quad r=(x,p,y) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这产生了整个方法所依赖的、每次失败的非数字详细记录；把预算花在这里也使其在所有被比较方法间保持相等。\n5. 对每次运行，把被违反要求的权重累加到表中「最近被编辑的那个 prompt 片段」所在的行——该片段由每个 prompt 保存的历史编辑列表确定（未经编辑的种子 prompt 归入单独的『seed』行）。跨轮次持续往同一张表里累加，而不是重建。\n\n*对最近被编辑的组件 c，每个被违反的约束 j 按其来源权重（verifier 取 1.0，judge 取 0.5）累加到持久表项 V[c][j]；V 跨多次访问累积，而非每轮重新汇总。*\n$$ V[c][j] \\leftarrow V[c][j] + w_j \\cdot v_j(r), \\quad w_j = \\begin{cases} 1.0 & \\text{verifier-backed} \\\\ 0.5 & \\text{judge-backed} \\end{cases} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 让归因在一张持久的类型化表中累积是核心思想——它把细粒度信用往后传递，而不像每轮重算并压扁的摘要。\n\n### 约束消解偏好优化（贡献）\n*把归因表转成最小差异偏好对，并编辑相关 prompt 片段以修复被锁定的要求。*\n\n6. 找到同一输入上的运行对，其 prompt 至多只在「最近一次编辑」上不同，且被违反要求集合恰好相差一条要求；把满足该要求的那个运行标为更优，并把差异归因于其编辑最能降低该要求在表中那一列的 prompt 片段。若某目标单元格找不到这样干净的一对，就取最接近的可用对（至多相差两条要求，否则跳过），并只对它们唯一不同的那条要求记账。\n\n*一个偏好对共享同一输入与 prompt 前缀，且恰好在一个被违反的约束 $k_{j}$ 上不同；满足 $k_{j}$ 的 $r_+$ 为偏好项，并将该对比归因于其编辑最能降低 V 第 j 列的组件。*\n$$ (r_+, r_-) : x_+ = x_-,\\; \\mathrm{prefix}(r_+)=\\mathrm{prefix}(r_-),\\; v(r_-) \\setminus v(r_+) = \\{k_j\\} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 比较两个几乎相同、只在一条要求上不同的运行，能干净地隔离出原因，而不会与无关差异混淆。\n7. 取累积归因最多的(prompt 片段, 要求)单元格。向冻结的 proposer 大语言模型(Large Language Model, LLM)索取若干对该片段的候选改写（默认 8 个），并提供失败示例与恰好破坏的那条要求，同时要求不要破坏已满足的要求。在一批留出输入上重跑这些改写，保留最常把该要求从「破坏」翻转为「满足」的那个；若有并列，优先选最少增加其他被破坏要求的那个。【作者需决定：索取多少个候选改写、以及对附带破坏的惩罚力度，均可调且由作者设定。】\n\n*在对相关组件 c 的候选编辑 e 中，选择在留出批次 B 上最大化约束 j 违反下降（即 V 第 j 列实际下降）的那个，也就是其新输出最常把 $k_{j}$ 从违反翻转为满足的编辑。*\n$$ e^{*} = \\arg\\max_{e \\in \\mathcal{E}(c)} \\; \\widehat{\\Delta}_j(e), \\quad \\widehat{\\Delta}_j(e) = \\mathbb{E}_{x \\sim \\mathcal{B}}\\big[\\, v_j(x,p) - v_j(x, p \\oplus e)\\,\\big] \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这让编辑直指责任片段与要修的确切要求，而不是用一个全局分数去微推整个 prompt。\n\n### 标量坍缩诊断（贡献）\n*在相同预算下，仅切换信用通道是数字还是类型化表，并对照 GRPO 基线，以把 scalar-collapse 隔离为瓶颈。*\n\n8. 运行两份匹配的循环副本：一份(arm A)编辑器只看到单个 fitness 数字——满足要求数量的加权平均，另一份(arm B)看到完整的归因表。保持模型、总试运行数、编辑器、种子 prompt 与数据划分完全相同。再用 GRPO(Group Relative Policy Optimization，一种更新模型权重的标准强化学习方法)在同一模型与试运行预算上运行，以同样的加权平均分作为其奖励（默认 group size 为 8，并正则化以保持接近原模型）。比较三条准确率-试运行曲线。【作者需决定：GRPO 的学习率以及保持接近原模型的强度是标准设置，由作者选择。】\n   - _为什么_: 只改变「信用是一个数字还是一张表」就把这单一因素隔离为任何差异的原因，而 GRPO 是核心对照。\n\n"},{"id":"53","run_dir":"run_prompt53_glassflow","index":53,"title":"Reliability-Gated Reward Alignment: Spend Inference Budget Where the Reward Is Trustworthy","title_zh":"可靠性门控的奖励对齐：把推理预算花在奖励值得信任的地方","method_name":"Reliability-Gated Reward Alignment (RG-RA)","hook":"Inference-time aligners for flow and diffusion models evaluate the reward at every denoising transition and treat each evaluation as exact, yet on high-noise early states the reward model is operating far outside its training support and its signal there is mostly noise. We manufacture a per-state reliability score from the model's own denoised-preview self-agreement and use it to gate WHERE alignment effort is spent — reaching the same reward-tilted target as uniform schedules at a fraction of the reward evaluations.","anchor_pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","anchor_pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","domain_category":"Generative Models — Vision","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved inference-time aligner produces, per intermediate denoising state, an estimate of how reliable that state's reward evaluation is as a proxy for the terminal reward — so none can concentrate or withhold alignment effort based on signal reliability rather than a fixed schedule (additive frontier-leaf gap on the GLASS/SMC/CREPE leaves: they cheapen or reschedule transitions but never measure per-state reward-signal reliability).","pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by manufacturing a label-free internal-state readout — the reliability score rho_t built from the disagreement of the reward across multiple stochastic denoised-previews x0_hat of the current noisy state — on the frozen pretrained model at inference, localizing where along the trajectory the reward evaluation is a trustworthy proxy for the terminal reward without any extra training or target-label access.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved method tests whether the reward potential must be applied at every transition along the trajectory at all, or whether the same tilted target can be reached by acting only on the subset of states where the reward evaluation is decision-relevant (subtractive gap: the GLASS / SMC / value-guidance / replica-exchange leaves all silently inherit from a shared ancestor — guidance/SMC-style reward-tilted sampling — the assumption that the reward potential is evaluated and applied uniformly ","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","how_closed":"Framing move (audit/pivot): name the load-bearing assumption baked into the reward-tilted-sampling stopping/selection rule — that the reward potential must be applied at every transition — and pivot it to a reliability-gated rule that applies the potential only on states whose rho_t exceeds a learned threshold tau, recasting 'apply-everywhere' as a budgeted when-to-act decision; companion deliverable (controlled_diagnostic_design): a confound-isolating empirical separation that holds backbone, reward model, and transition sampler fixed and varies ONLY the application schedule (uniform vs reliability-gated vs a reliability-permuted control), so any budget-vs-tilted-target gain is attributable to the reliability gating rather than to fewer evaluations per se.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"generative models — inference-time reward alignment of flow matching and diffusion models","n_papers":41,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":27},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":9,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Efficient Diversity-Preserving Diffusion Alignment via Gradient-Informed GFlowNets"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Improving GFlowNets for Text-to-Image Diffusion Alignment"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Explainable Generative AI (GenXAI): a survey, conceptualization, and research agenda"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Mapping the Ethics of Generative AI: A Comprehensive Scoping Review"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Generative AI for Self-Adaptive Systems: State of the Art and Research Roadmap"},{"source":"openalex","title":"A survey of safety and trustworthiness of large language models through the lens of verification and validation"}],"more":3},{"year":2025,"n":31,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"GLASS Flows: Transition Sampling for Alignment of Flow and Diffusion Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Inference-Time Alignment Control for Diffusion Models with Reinforcement Learning Guidance"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Value Gradient Guidance for Flow Matching Alignment"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"HY-Motion 1.0: Scaling Flow Matching Models for Text-To-Motion Generation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Coefficients-Preserving Sampling for Reinforcement Learning with Flow Matching"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"CogniEdit: Dense Gradient Flow Optimization for Fine-Grained Image Editing"}],"more":25},{"year":2026,"n":1,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"}],"more":0}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":10,"share":0.244},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":5,"share":0.122},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":4,"share":0.098},{"pattern_id":"algebraic_equivalence_unification","pattern_name":"Prove Equivalence to Unify","count":4,"share":0.098},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":4,"share":0.098},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":3,"share":0.073},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":3,"share":0.073},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":3,"share":0.073}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Inference-time reward-alignment algorithms for flow and diffusion models steer generation toward the reward-tilted distribution p_data(z)exp(r(z)) by evaluating the reward (or a derived potential) at intermediate denoising states and using those evaluations to reweight, guide, or resample — yet every retrieved method spends its reward-evaluation budget UNIFORMLY across the trajectory and treats each evaluation of r at an intermediate, still-noisy state as an exact, equally-trustworthy signal. GLASS Flows (semanticscholar:edb17be2cdff6b926e934ba2771d6529b6fdc5d4) cheapens the per-step Markov-transition cost but leaves the reward-evaluation schedule itself untouched, and SMC-with-tempering (semanticscholar:672b7ebea68189e7c372ef84d31408d82a3b3e6b) and replica-exchange (openalex:W4415332177) likewise apply a fixed potential at every transition regardless of how reliable the reward signal actually is at that noise level. The failure this produces: on high-noise early states the reward model is operating far outside its training support and its output is a poor proxy for the terminal reward, so budget spent guiding there is largely wasted and actively drives the over-optimization / reward-hacking that MIRA (semanticscholar:34e6cc059b06730d1bcfe6afa2997bb8c5154969) patches reactively; meanwhile the trajectory carries no notion of WHERE its alignment signal is informative versus noise, so the machinery cannot concentrate effort where the reward evaluation is actually decision-relevant. The structural gap is that no inference-time aligner has a way to tell, per state along the trajectory, whether the reward evaluation there is reliable enough to act on.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:edb17be2cdff6b926e934ba2771d6529b6fdc5d4","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"GLASS Flows removes the dominant efficiency bottleneck of inference-time reward alignment by replacing expensive SDE Markov-transition sampling with an 'inner' flow-matching model that simulates the transition kernel p_{t'|t} far more cheaply, so any alignment algorithm built on transition sampling (SMC, twisted proposals) runs faster. Its method (read from the fulltext: it accelerates the transition-sampling subroutine and is agnostic to the alignment objective) does NOT touch the reward-evaluation schedule — it still assumes the surrounding algorithm evaluates the reward potential at every transition and treats each evaluation as exact, so a cheaper transition just means uniformly-distributed reward evaluations are computed faster, not allocated more wisely or gated by reliability."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:672b7ebea68189e7c372ef84d31408d82a3b3e6b","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Test-time Alignment runs training-free SMC with a tempering schedule to sample the reward-tilted target while resisting reward over-optimization. The tempering schedule that controls how strongly the reward acts is a fixed, hand-set annealing curve applied identically to every particle and every step; it does not adapt to the per-state reliability of the reward evaluation, so it cannot down-weight states where the reward signal is uninformative noise rather than turn the global temperature up or down."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7090885525","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Understanding Sampler Stochasticity theoretically characterizes a 'reward gap' between stochastic SDE sampling (train) and deterministic ODE sampling (inference) and gives non-vacuous bounds. It is diagnostic: it quantifies that intermediate-state reward behavior differs from terminal reward, but it provides no inference-time estimator that uses this — it stops at a bound and does not turn the per-state reward-reliability into an actionable allocation or gating signal during sampling."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:34e6cc059b06730d1bcfe6afa2997bb8c5154969","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"MIRA mitigates reward hacking in inference-time noise-optimization alignment via noise-space regularization. The regularizer is reward-model-agnostic in form but reactive and global: it penalizes drift in noise space rather than detecting WHERE along the trajectory the reward evaluation has become unreliable, so it cannot redirect effort toward the states where the reward signal is trustworthy."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"generative models — inference-time reward alignment of flow matching and diffusion models","venue":"ICLR / NeurIPS / ICML (top ML)","time":"2026 submission cycle","data":["pretrained text-to-image flow/diffusion backbone (e.g. SD3/SDXL/FLUX-class)","off-the-shelf scalar reward models (aesthetic / ImageReward / HPSv2 / CLIP-alignment)","standard T2I prompt benchmarks (DrawBench, Pick-a-Pic, GenEval)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"generative modeling + inference-time guidance / sampling","preference":"both","baseline":"inference-time reward-alignment samplers that evaluate the reward at every Markov transition uniformly: SMC-with-tempering (Test-time Alignment, semanticscholar:672b7ebea68189e7c372ef84d31408d82a3b3e6b), replica-exchange (CREPE, openalex:W4415332177), value-gradient guidance (VGG-Flow, semanticscholar:a388c16e3fb0cd1429744a18afd205fb4d27df28), and the efficient-transition substrate GLASS Flows (semanticscholar:edb17be2cdff6b926e934ba2771d6529b6fdc5d4)","limitation":"inference-time reward alignment is expensive and prone to reward over-optimization / reward hacking; current efficiency work cheapens the per-transition sampling cost but still evaluates the reward signal uniformly along the whole denoising trajectory and treats each reward evaluation as exact","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object every leg reads from and writes to is the per-state reward-reliability score rho_t in [0,1], defined for each intermediate noisy state x_t along the denoising trajectory of a frozen pretrained flow/diffusion backbone. rho_t is computed entirely from quantities already available at inference: at state x_t we draw m (default m=4) stochastic denoised previews {x0_hat^(j)} of the clean sample — for a flow/diffusion model x0_hat is the conditional-expectation (Tweedie / one-step ODE jump-to-zero) estimate of the endpoint from x_t, and the m copies differ by injecting m independent small Gaussian perturbations of fixed scale sigma_probe into x_t before the jump — then evaluate the external scalar reward r on each preview and set rho_t = 1 - clip( std_j r(x0_hat^(j)) / (s_ref + epsilon), 0, 1 ), where std_j is the across-preview standard deviation of the reward, s_ref is a per-prompt scale constant set to the reward std measured at the terminal state x_0 (the one state where the preview IS the sample), and epsilon=1e-6. Intuition made computable: when the reward's verdict is stable under small perturbations of the current state's denoised preview (low std), the reward evaluation at x_t is a trustworthy proxy for the terminal reward and rho_t is near 1; when small perturbations flip the reward wildly (the reward model is extrapolating off its support, typical at high noise), rho_t collapses toward 0. The free quantities are all fixed or given a rule: m=4, sigma_probe = 0.1 * the schedule's per-step noise std at t (a named hyperparameter bridging probe-scale to the noise schedule), the reward model r is the user's off-the-shelf scalar reward, and s_ref is computed once per prompt from the cheap terminal evaluation. Leg 1 (self_supervised_signal_engineering, C07) MANUFACTURES rho_t: this is the C07 move of taking a frozen trained model under (here, support) shift, reading an internal label-free signal (reward self-agreement across model-generated previews) that localizes the failure site (the high-noise prefix where the reward is unreliable), with the stabilizer being the per-prompt s_ref normalization that prevents rho_t from collapsing globally for hard prompts. Leg 2 (assumption_audit_and_pivot, C11) USES rho_t to overturn the uniform-application assumption: the reward-tilted sampler's selection rule 'apply the reward potential / resampling weight at every transition' is pivoted to 'apply it only at transitions where rho_t >= tau', where tau is a budget-controlled threshold chosen so that a target fraction beta of the trajectory's transitions are reward-active; the companion controlled_diagnostic_design deliverable is the matched-pair experiment that swaps ONLY the schedule (uniform / rho-gated / rho-permuted) to isolate that the tilted target is still reached. The two legs share rho_t as the single central primitive: leg 1 constructs it, leg 2 acts on it, so this is one mechanism with one shared object, not two stapled modules. Concretely the gated sampler plugs into any transition-based aligner (SMC potentials, CREPE replica weights, or GLASS-accelerated transitions): on transitions with rho_t < tau it skips the reward evaluation and takes the plain pretrained transition, spending the saved reward calls nowhere — total reward evaluations drop to roughly beta * (uniform count) plus the cheap m-preview probe cost, while the reward-tilted target p_data(z)exp(r(z)) is approached because the skipped low-rho states contributed near-noise potentials that uniform schedules wasted budget on.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery because both are about the SAME quantity — how reliable the reward is at a given state: gap 1 asks to measure it, gap 2 asks whether measuring it lets you stop applying the reward everywhere. Building rho_t once and reading it from both legs is the evidence they share an object rather than needing separate modules; a design with two independent signals (one for measurement, one for gating) would duplicate the off-support detection and break the shared_object thread. (b) Alternatives considered and rejected: (1) using the reward-model's own predictive variance / ensemble disagreement as reliability — rejected because most deployed scalar rewards are single deterministic networks with no calibrated uncertainty (C07 tactical failure mode: a surrogate whose validity rests on calibration breaks on miscalibrated nets), whereas perturbation-of-preview self-agreement needs no reward-internal uncertainty; (2) learning a value/critic to predict terminal reward from x_t (this is exactly node n6 VGG-Flow and would REGRESS to a trained value-function baseline the lineage flags) — rejected, rho_t is training-free and reads the frozen model only; (3) a fixed noise-level cutoff (apply reward only for t<t0) — rejected because it hard-codes a schedule and cannot adapt per-prompt, which is the uniform-schedule failure restated. Avoided node recorded: rho_t deliberately does NOT reduce to a learned value baseline (n6) or a fixed tempering schedule (n3); it imports the active-learning 'measure where the noisy oracle is informative' idea (collateral c1) into the noise-indexed trajectory, a setting c1 never operated in.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on a frozen SD3/FLUX-class backbone with ImageReward as r, run inference-time alignment (SMC-with-tempering as the base aligner) on DrawBench + Pick-a-Pic prompts under three schedules — uniform application (U), reliability-gated at budget beta=0.4 (G), and reliability-permuted (P) — and measure terminal reward, prompt-fidelity (CLIP-score / VQA), and the number of reward evaluations to reach a fixed target terminal reward. If the candidate works: G reaches the same target terminal reward as U using markedly fewer reward evaluations (reward-evaluations-to-target decreases), and prompt-fidelity at matched terminal reward is no worse (reward-hacking / over-optimization does not increase, and likely decreases because off-support early guidance is removed). The named load-bearing variable is rho_t, the per-state reliability score. Negative control: replace rho_t with the reliability-permuted schedule P — same count of reward-active transitions but their positions randomly permuted so the reliability ordering is destroyed — and predict the downstream task-outcome metric (terminal reward at matched reward-evaluation budget) collapses back toward the unguided baseline, i.e. the budget saving stops buying any reward gain. This is non-tautological: P holds the active-transition COUNT fixed and only scrambles WHERE rho_t says to act, so a metric drop pins the gain on the reliability ordering itself rather than on doing fewer (or more) evaluations. Positive control (constructive identification): a stripped sampler that applies the reward ONLY on the single highest-rho_t late-trajectory segment recovers most of U's terminal-reward gain at a small fraction of the evaluations, showing rho_t alone localizes where alignment effort pays off.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:edb17be2cdff6b926e934ba2771d6529b6fdc5d4","delta":"GLASS Flows cheapens the per-transition Markov-sampling subroutine while still evaluating the reward at every transition uniformly; we construct a per-state reliability score rho_t that decides WHICH transitions are reward-active at all, an orthogonal axis that composes on top of (rather than competes with) GLASS's transition acceleration."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:672b7ebea68189e7c372ef84d31408d82a3b3e6b","delta":"Test-time Alignment uses a fixed, prompt-independent tempering schedule applied at every step; we derive a per-prompt, per-state reliability-gated application schedule from the reward's own preview self-agreement, so the schedule is measured from the model at inference rather than hand-set."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7090885525","delta":"Understanding Sampler Stochasticity only proves non-vacuous bounds on the train/inference reward gap (diagnostic theory); we turn the intermediate-vs-terminal reward discrepancy into a runnable inference-time control signal rho_t that allocates reward-evaluation budget, which they never construct."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:34e6cc059b06730d1bcfe6afa2997bb8c5154969","delta":"MIRA reduces reward hacking by a reactive global noise-space regularizer; we prevent off-support early guidance proactively by withholding reward application on low-rho_t states, addressing over-optimization at its source (unreliable early-state reward) rather than penalizing drift after the fact."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:edb17be2cdff6b926e934ba2771d6529b6fdc5d4","what_step_was_missed":"GLASS Flows accelerated the transition-sampling subroutine but left the reward-evaluation schedule as a fixed apply-everywhere assumption; for our contribution to already exist it would have needed to construct a per-state measurement of reward-signal reliability (the across-preview reward-disagreement readout rho_t) and a pivot of the sampler's selection rule from apply-at-every-transition to apply-only-where-reliable — a measurement primitive plus an assumption pivot it did not build, since its acceleration is agnostic to and silent about where the reward is trustworthy."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":282,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"Hard floor did not fire: gap_closure_reject_check is borderline (not triggered) with both flagged lessons already neutralized by specified controls; anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null; and paper_pointed_threat (TReASURe) is a near-neighbor in a different domain with addressable_via naming only a framing delta, NOT exact-mechanism overlap. recipe_application_check.verdict = applied for both legs (C07's diagnose-localize/tiny-lever/stabilizer and C11's budgeted-selection-rule pivot are both present in core_mechanism). Choosing advance over revise because the two borderlines hit non-load-bearing surfaces resolvable by surfacing concerns in Phase 4 (the ensemble-overlap control to report; the explicit when-gating-wins conditional claim; the TReASURe delta), not the core_mechanism's central argument.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved inference-time aligner produces, per intermediate denoising state, an estimate of how reliable that state's reward evaluation is as a proxy for the terminal reward — so none can concentrate or withhold alignment effort based on signal reliability rather than a fixed schedule (additive frontier-leaf gap on the GLASS/SMC/CREPE leaves: they cheapen or reschedule transitions but never measure per-state reward-signal reliability).","main_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"A manufactured internal signal whose validity silently rests on an assumption that does not survive deployment (model calibration on miscalibrated nets, a stationary/known-finite shift set, or covert use of target/test-set information amounting to label leakage), compounded by recombining well-known components without one load-bearing mechanistic insight.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A label-free signal whose validity depends on model calibration silently fails on exactly the deep networks known to be poorly calibrated — validate a surrogate where its core assumption is weakest, not where it is convenient.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"rho_t is built from the across-preview standard deviation of the reward under input perturbations, NOT from the reward model's own confidence/calibration, so it does not rest on the reward net being calibrated; the design rationale explicitly rejected reward-internal uncertainty for this reason."},{"lesson_quoted":"Recasting a continuous shift as a discrete, known, finite set of types indexed against a precomputed lookup table collapses the moment an unanticipated or mixed shift arrives.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"rho_t is a continuous per-state scalar computed online from the actual state, with no precomputed shift-type lookup table."},{"lesson_quoted":"A multi-branch or ensemble reweighting mechanism that overlaps with standard multi-task/mixture-of-experts ensembling must explicitly beat both the single-model and the standard-ensemble baselines, or the gain is credited to prior art.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"the m-preview probe resembles a small ensemble, so the m-ablation and especially the rho-permuted control (P) must show the gain is from the reliability ORDERING, not generic stochastic averaging; the candidate already specifies both controls, which neutralizes the borderline if reported."},{"lesson_quoted":"Using target or test-set information during adaptation invites a label-leakage objection that undermines the very source-free, label-free deployment setting the method claims.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"rho_t uses only the user's reward model on the model's own denoised previews and a per-prompt terminal-reward scale s_ref computed from the model's own samples; no ground-truth terminal reward or test-set label is accessed."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved method tests whether the reward potential must be applied at every transition along the trajectory at all, or whether the same tilted target can be reached by acting only on the subset of states where the reward evaluation is decision-relevant (subtractive gap: the GLASS / SMC / value-guidance / replica-exchange leaves all silently inherit from a shared ancestor — guidance/SMC-style reward-tilted sampling — the assumption that the reward potential is evaluated and applied uniformly at every transition; no leaf questions whether uniform reward application is necessary).","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The dominant failure is substituting one selection rule for another that performs better empirically while omitting the theorem that explains when and why it wins, or pivoting an assumption the community regards as a reasonable modeling choice rather than first proving it a genuine restriction.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Substituting one selection heuristic for another without a theorem stating when and why it wins reads as an engineering combination, not a contribution, no matter how clean the empirical gain.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"the candidate is method-typed and ships an empirical confound-isolating separation (via companion controlled_diagnostic_design) rather than a regret/competitive-ratio theorem; this is by-design (Phase 2.1 paired the leg) but a reviewer will want at least a clearly-stated identifiability claim of WHEN gating reaches the same tilted target — Phase 4 should make that conditional claim explicit."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pivoting an assumption the community treats as a reasonable modeling choice — rather than first proving it a genuine restriction — leaves both motivation and novelty in doubt.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the uniform-application assumption is shown to be a genuine restriction by the motivating fact that early high-noise states have off-support, near-noise reward evaluations (grounded in the reward-gap result openalex:W7090885525), so applying the reward there is demonstrably wasteful, not benign."},{"lesson_quoted":"Unlocking a new capability by violating an assumption while ignoring a protective property it guarded — detectability, validity, identifiability — invites rejection on the overlooked side effect rather than the headline result.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the protected property (reaching the reward-tilted target / sample quality) is exactly what the controlled separation measures: terminal reward, prompt-fidelity, and diversity are all tracked so the pivot is not shown to silently break the tilted-target guarantee."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No entry is triggered. The self_supervised leg (C07) is borderline only on the ensemble-overlap lesson, fully neutralized by the candidate's already-specified m-ablation and rho-permuted control. The assumption-audit leg (C11) is borderline on the 'needs a theorem' lesson because it ships an empirical separation instead of a guarantee — by-design via the companion, but Phase 4 must surface the explicit when-it-wins conditional claim."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved inference-time aligner produces, per intermediate denoising state, an estimate of how reliable that state's reward evaluation is as a proxy for the terminal reward — so none can concentrate or withhold alignment effort based on signal reliability rather than a fixed schedule (additive frontier-leaf gap on the GLASS/SMC/CREPE leaves: they cheapen or reschedule transitions but never measure per-state reward-signal reliability).","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Take an already-trained model facing shift and treat its own internal-state readouts as the manufactured supervisory signal: pair a mechanistic diagnosis that localizes the failure to a structural site with a surgically confined correction on a minimal lever while the backbone stays frozen, and bolt on an explicit stabilizer against collapse — verbs are diagnose-localize, minimize-on-a-tiny-lever, stabilize-against-collapse.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism performs all three signature moves on the frozen backbone: diagnose-localize = the high-noise prefix is identified as the site where the reward evaluation is off-support and unreliable; manufacture internal label-free readout = rho_t from across-preview reward self-agreement; tiny-lever correction = gating reward application (skip on low-rho_t states) with the backbone untouched; stabilizer = the per-prompt s_ref normalization preventing rho_t collapse on hard prompts. This is the C07 tactic, not the parent's generic 'derive a signal from the model'.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved method tests whether the reward potential must be applied at every transition along the trajectory at all, or whether the same tilted target can be reached by acting only on the subset of states where the reward evaluation is decision-relevant (subtractive gap: the GLASS / SMC / value-guidance / replica-exchange leaves all silently inherit from a shared ancestor — guidance/SMC-style reward-tilted sampling — the assumption that the reward potential is evaluated and applied uniformly at every transition; no leaf questions whether uniform reward application is necessary).","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Center on a selection/acquisition/query/stopping rule under a budget and pivot the single assumption baked into its criterion or required structure — here by relaxing a structural crutch to a weaker condition and re-deriving (or empirically certifying) that the pivoted rule matches the pre-pivot baseline; the objects are the elements entering or leaving a budgeted choice procedure.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism performs the C11 move: it names the load-bearing assumption inside the reward-tilted sampler's application rule (apply the potential at every transition), pivots it to a budgeted when-to-act rule (apply only where rho_t >= tau, with tau set to a budget fraction beta), and binds the gain to the pivot via the rho-permuted control showing the saving stops buying reward gain when the reliability ordering is destroyed — i.e. the certificate is delivered empirically (companion controlled_diagnostic_design) rather than as a closed-form regret bound.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both legs instantiate their cited cluster's distinctive move: C07's diagnose-localize / tiny-lever / stabilizer triad is present in rho_t + gating + s_ref, and C11's budgeted-selection-rule pivot is present in the uniform-to-reliability-gated application schedule with the pivot bound to the gain via the permuted control."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["self_supervised_signal_engineering","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; the candidate's composition_set {self_supervised_signal_engineering, assumption_audit_and_pivot} matches none of them, so no anti-pattern fires."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"Tree Reward-Aligned Search for TReASURe in Masked Diffusion Language Models","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"TReASURe is the nearest neighbor: it explicitly observes that reward evaluation via sampled completions produces high-variance estimates that make pruning unstable, which is the same reward-unreliability-at-intermediate-states phenomenon the candidate exploits. However, TReASURe responds with a tree-search branching/pruning strategy in masked diffusion LANGUAGE models and does NOT construct a per-state reliability score or use it to gate WHERE the reward potential is applied — its variance observation is used to stabilize pruning, not to localize and withhold reward application along a continuous denoising trajectory. The candidate's claim (a measurable per-state reliability score rho_t that reaches the reward-tilted target at fewer reward evaluations) stands because TReASURe neither measures nor allocates on reliability; it would fall only if TReASURe had built a reliability-indexed application schedule, which it did not.","addressable_via":"differentiation_from_lit should add an explicit delta vs TReASURe (per-state reliability gating in continuous flow/diffusion vs tree-search pruning in masked diffusion LMs) so the boundary is unambiguous; this is a framing addition, not an exact-mechanism overlap."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Reliability-Gated Reward Alignment: Spend Inference Budget Where the Reward Is Trustworthy\n\n**Method.** Reliability-Gated Reward Alignment (RG-RA)\n\n## Motivation\nModern text-to-image generators built on flow matching and diffusion produce an image by starting from pure noise and gradually denoising it. To make the final image score higher on some quality measure (a 'reward model' such as ImageReward or an aesthetic scorer), a popular trick is to nudge the generation at each denoising step using that reward — no retraining of the big model required. The problem: today's methods consult the reward at EVERY step and trust it completely. But early in generation the image is still mostly noise, and the reward model almost never saw such half-formed images during its own training, so its opinion there is basically a coin flip. Spending effort steering on those early, garbled states wastes compute and actually encourages 'reward hacking' — chasing a high score that does not correspond to a genuinely better image. Recent work made the per-step machinery cheaper (GLASS Flows, 2025) but never asked WHERE the reward is actually worth listening to; other work (Understanding Sampler Stochasticity, 2025) proved there really is a gap between the reward's opinion mid-generation and at the end, but stopped at the math. Our idea is to MEASURE, at each step, how trustworthy the reward is right there. We do this cheaply and without any training: from the current noisy image we make a quick guess of the finished image (a 'denoised preview'), jiggle the noisy image a few times with tiny random perturbations, and see whether the reward's score on these previews stays stable. If the score barely moves, the reward is on solid ground and we trust it (reliability score $rho_{t}$ near 1); if tiny jiggles send the score all over the place, the reward is extrapolating and we do not trust it $(rho_{t}$ near 0). Then we flip the unquestioned assumption that the reward must be applied at every step: we only apply it where $rho_{t}$ is high enough (controlled by a single budget dial beta), and elsewhere we just let the model denoise normally with no reward call. The payoff is reaching the same reward-improved image while consulting the reward far fewer times, with less reward hacking rather than more — and it stacks on top of speedups like GLASS Flows.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n\n1. Load a pretrained text-to-image flow or diffusion model (SD3 / FLUX-class) and an off-the-shelf scalar reward model (ImageReward / HPSv2 / an aesthetic scorer), both in evaluation mode with gradients turned off. Do not train, finetune, or add any new network — every later quantity is computed at inference from these frozen models. The result is a runnable sampling stack you can query for transitions and for reward scores.\n   - _Why_: Keeping the big model frozen makes this a pure plug-in trick and avoids quietly turning it into a costly value-function training method.\n\n### Reliability Estimator\n*Manufactures the per-state, training-free reliability score $rho_{t}$ from denoised-preview reward self-agreement.*\n\n2. Build a 'denoised preview' function that, from the current noisy image $x_{t},$ makes one quick estimate of the finished image. For diffusion models use the standard Tweedie formula (subtract the predicted noise, rescale); for flow models use the one-step jump along the learned velocity to the endpoint. It returns a single estimated clean latent per call (one model forward pass), in the same latent space the model normally decodes to an image.\n\n*The denoised preview $\\hat{x}_{0}$ is the conditional-expectation estimate of the clean endpoint from the current noisy state $x_{t}$ (Tweedie for diffusion, one-step ODE jump for flow), the cheap quantity $rho_{t}$ is built on.*\n$$ \\hat{x}_0(x_t, t) = \\mathbb{E}[x_0 \\mid x_t] \\;\\approx\\; \\text{one-step jump-to-endpoint}(x_t, t) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: It lets you ask the reward 'how good will this turn out?' without paying to finish the whole generation.\n3. Compute the reliability score for the current state: make m=4 slightly perturbed copies of the noisy image (add small Gaussian noise of size $\\sigma _{probe} = 0.1$ times the step's own noise level, in the model's latent space), run the denoised preview on each, decode and score each with the reward model, and measure how much those m scores spread out (their standard deviation). The reliability score $rho_{t}$ is one minus that spread after dividing by a per-prompt scale and clipping to the 0-to-1 range. If small perturbations barely change the reward's verdict the score is near 1 (trustworthy here); if they swing it wildly the score is near 0 (the reward is guessing).\n\n*The per-state reliability score: one minus the clipped, scale-normalized standard deviation of the reward across m previews of $x_{t}$ perturbed by small Gaussian noise $\\sigma _{probe}$; $rho_{t}$ near 1 means the reward verdict is stable (trustworthy), near 0 means it flips under perturbation (off-support).*\n$$ \\rho_t = 1 - \\mathrm{clip}\\!\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{std}_j\\, r\\big(\\hat{x}_0(x_t + \\sigma_{\\text{probe}}\\,\\varepsilon_j,\\, t)\\big)}{s_{\\text{ref}} + \\epsilon},\\; 0,\\; 1\\right) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: If tiny nudges barely change the reward's verdict, the reward is trustworthy here; if they swing it wildly, the reward is guessing and $rho_{t}$ drops.\n4. Set the per-prompt scale once. Generate k=8 finished images for the prompt with the plain model (no reward steering), then run the same perturbation-and-score probe on each finished image and measure the reward spread at the end state; average those to get the scale $s_{ref}.$ This is the normalizer used in the reliability score. It matters because some prompts have a naturally noisier reward everywhere; dividing by the end-state spread keeps the reliability score meaningful instead of collapsing to zero on hard prompts.\n\n*The per-prompt scale constant: the across-preview reward standard deviation measured at the terminal state $x_{0}$ (the one state where the preview is the sample), used to normalize $rho_{t}$ so it does not collapse globally on hard prompts.*\n$$ s_{\\text{ref}} = \\operatorname{std}_j\\, r\\big(\\hat{x}_0(x_0 + \\sigma_{\\text{probe}}\\,\\varepsilon_j,\\, 0)\\big) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Hard prompts have naturally noisier rewards; normalizing by the end-state spread keeps $rho_{t}$ meaningful and stops it from collapsing to zero everywhere.\n\n### Reliability-Gated Sampler\n*Pivots apply-at-every-step into a budgeted $apply-only-where-rho_{t}-is-high$ rule and composes it with accelerated samplers.*\n\n5. Turn the budget dial beta into an actual threshold tau. Run a few $(P_{pilot}=4)$ plain pilot generations, collect the reliability scores at every step, and set tau to the cutoff such that only the top beta fraction of steps (by reliability) clear it — e.g. beta=0.4 keeps the most reliable 40% of steps reward-active. Compute tau per prompt by default. beta is the single knob the user turns to trade reward calls for alignment strength.\n   - _Why_: It turns 'apply only where reliable' into one knob the user controls: beta is literally the fraction of steps that still consult the reward.\n6. Run generation with the gate: at each step, if the reliability score clears the threshold tau, take the reward-guided transition from your base aligner (the Sequential Monte Carlo (SMC) potential, the CREPE replica weight, or the guidance term); otherwise take the ordinary pretrained denoising step and call the reward zero times. For multi-particle samplers, judge each particle by its own reliability and only weight/resample the particles that were reward-active that step. 【author decision: whether each particle is gated on its own reliability score or the whole population shares one gate per step — both fit the method and the authors must choose.】 Skipping the unreliable steps lets the image denoise normally there, so the gate genuinely changes the picture you get, not just a count.\n\n*The gated transition rule: take the aligner's reward-active transition (SMC potential / CREPE weight / guidance term) when $rho_{t} \\ge  \\tau ,$ else the plain pretrained transition with no reward evaluation; $\\tau $ is the $(1- \\beta )-quantile$ of $rho_{t}$ so a fraction $\\beta $ of transitions stay reward-active.*\n$$ \\text{transition}_t = \\begin{cases} \\text{reward\\text{-}active}(x_t) & \\rho_t \\geq \\tau \\\\ \\text{plain pretrained}(x_t) & \\rho_t < \\tau \\end{cases}, \\quad \\tau = \\mathrm{Quantile}_{1-\\beta}\\{\\rho_t\\} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: You spend reward calls only where they actually help, and skipping the unreliable early steps removes exactly the guidance that drives reward hacking.\n7. Stack the gating on top of a faster sampler (like GLASS Flows) unchanged: the gate only decides WHERE to apply the reward, while GLASS decides how cheaply each step runs, so they sit at different levels and combine. You get fewer reward-active steps and cheaper steps at once. Nothing in the reliability score or threshold changes — you just plug in the faster transition routine.\n   - _Why_: Fewer reward-active steps and cheaper steps multiply, so the two speedups stack instead of competing.\n\n### Confound-Isolating Harness\n*Proves the budget-vs-target gain comes from the reliability ordering via the uniform / gated / permuted matched-pair comparison.*\n\n8. Run the controlled check: keep the model, reward, and sampler identical and change only the schedule across three arms — (U) reward every step, (G) reliability-gated at budget beta, and (P) the same number of reward-active steps as G but placed at random positions (so the reliability ordering is scrambled). For each arm record the final reward, how well the image matches the prompt (CLIP-score / a visual question-answering check), diversity, and how many reward calls were used. Define the target reward as what U reaches when it converges, then compare how many reward calls each arm needs to hit it, and compare G against P at the same number of reward-active steps. Also vary m (1,2,4,8) and the perturbation size to confirm the win is not just from averaging more samples.\n   - _Why_: If G beats P even with the same number of reward calls, the win comes from WHERE $rho_{t}$ says to act, not from simply doing fewer calls — and the m-sweep rules out plain averaging.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 可靠性门控的奖励对齐：把推理预算花在奖励值得信任的地方\n\n**方法名称.** Reliability-Gated Reward Alignment (RG-RA)\n\n## 研究动机\n现代的文生图模型（基于 flow matching 和 diffusion）生成图像的方式，是从纯噪声出发、一步步去噪。为了让最终图像在某个质量指标（即 reward model，如 ImageReward 或美学打分器）上得分更高，一个流行的技巧是在每一步去噪时用这个 reward 去轻推生成方向——无需重新训练大模型。问题在于：现有方法在每一步都查询 reward，并且完全信任它。但生成早期图像还基本是噪声，reward model 在自己训练时几乎没见过这种半成品图像，所以它在那里的判断基本是抛硬币。在这些早期、模糊的状态上花力气去引导，既浪费算力，又会助长 reward hacking——追逐一个并不对应真正更好图像的高分。近期工作让每步的机制更便宜了（GLASS Flows, 2025），却从没问过 reward 到底在哪里值得听；另一些工作（Understanding Sampler Stochasticity, 2025）证明了 reward 在生成中途和最终的意见之间确实存在差距，但止步于数学。我们的想法是：在每一步去量化 reward 在那里有多可信。我们用一种廉价且无需训练的方式做到这点：从当前噪声图像快速估出成品图像（去噪预览 denoised preview），对噪声图像做几次微小随机扰动，看 reward 在这些预览上的打分是否稳定。如果打分几乎不动，说明 reward 立足稳固、可以信任（可靠性分数 $rho_{t}$ 接近 1）；如果微小扰动就让打分剧烈跳动，说明 reward 在外推、不可信（$rho_{t}$ 接近 0）。然后我们推翻 reward 必须在每一步都施加这个从未被质疑的假设：只在 $rho_{t}$ 足够高的地方施加 reward（由单一预算旋钮 beta 控制），其余地方让模型正常去噪、不调用 reward。收益是：在大幅减少 reward 查询次数的情况下达到同样的奖励提升图像，而且 reward hacking 更少而非更多——并且它能叠加在 GLASS Flows 这类加速方法之上。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景\n\n1. 加载一个预训练的文生图 flow 或 diffusion 模型（SD3 / FLUX 级别）和一个现成的标量奖励模型(scalar reward model，即 ImageReward / HPSv2 / 美学打分器)，两者都设为评估模式并关闭梯度。不训练、不微调、不新增任何网络——后续所有量都在推理时从这些冻结模型计算得到。最终得到一个可运行的采样栈(sampling stack)，可向其查询转移步和奖励分数。\n   - _为什么_: 让大模型保持冻结，使这成为一个纯粹的即插即用技巧，避免悄悄变成昂贵的 value-function 训练方法。\n\n### 可靠性估计器（Reliability Estimator）\n*从去噪预览的奖励自一致性中、无需训练地制造每态可靠性分数 $rho_{t}$。*\n\n2. 构建一个去噪预览(denoised preview)函数：从当前噪声图像 $x_{t}$ 出发，一步快速估出成品图像。对 diffusion 模型用标准 Tweedie 公式(减去预测噪声并重新缩放)；对 flow 模型用沿学到的速度场一步跳到终点。每次调用返回一个估计的干净潜变量(latent)，只需一次模型前向，位于模型平常解码成图像的那个 latent 空间。\n\n*去噪预览 $\\hat{x}_{0}$ 是从当前噪声态 $x_{t}$ 对干净终点的条件期望估计（diffusion 用 Tweedie，flow 用一步 ODE 跳跃），它是构造 $rho_{t}$ 的廉价量。*\n$$ \\hat{x}_0(x_t, t) = \\mathbb{E}[x_0 \\mid x_t] \\;\\approx\\; \\text{one-step jump-to-endpoint}(x_t, t) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 它让你无需付出走完整个生成的代价，就能问 reward「这最终会有多好」。\n3. 计算当前状态的可靠性分数：对噪声图像做 m=4 个轻微扰动副本(在模型 latent 空间中加入幅度为 $\\sigma _{probe} =$ 该步自身噪声水平 0.1 倍的小高斯噪声)，对每个跑去噪预览，解码后用奖励模型打分，并测量这 m 个分数的离散度(标准差)。可靠性分数 $rho_{t}$ 等于：把该离散度除以一个每提示词的尺度并裁剪到 0 到 1 区间后，用 1 去减。若微小扰动几乎不改变奖励判定，分数接近 1(此处可信)；若让判定剧烈摆动，分数接近 0(奖励在瞎猜)。\n\n*每态可靠性分数：1 减去对 $x_{t}$ 施加小高斯扰动 $\\sigma _{probe}$ 后 m 个预览上奖励标准差经尺度归一化并裁剪后的值；$rho_{t}$ 接近 1 表示奖励判定稳定（可信），接近 0 表示扰动下翻转（越界）。*\n$$ \\rho_t = 1 - \\mathrm{clip}\\!\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{std}_j\\, r\\big(\\hat{x}_0(x_t + \\sigma_{\\text{probe}}\\,\\varepsilon_j,\\, t)\\big)}{s_{\\text{ref}} + \\epsilon},\\; 0,\\; 1\\right) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 若微小扰动几乎不改变 reward 的判定，说明此处 reward 可信；若让判定剧烈摆动，说明 reward 在瞎猜，$rho_{t}$ 下降。\n4. 为每个提示词标定一次尺度。用普通模型(不做奖励引导)为该提示词生成 k=8 张成品图像，对每张成品图像跑同样的扰动并打分探针，测量终态的奖励离散度，再取平均得到尺度 $s_{ref}$。这就是可靠性分数里用到的归一化分母。它重要是因为某些提示词处处的奖励天然更嘈杂；除以终态离散度能让可靠性分数保持有意义，而不是在困难提示词上塌缩为零。\n\n*每提示词的尺度常数：在终态 $x_{0}$（预览即样本的唯一态）上测得的跨预览奖励标准差，用于归一化 $rho_{t}$，使其在困难提示词上不整体塌缩。*\n$$ s_{\\text{ref}} = \\operatorname{std}_j\\, r\\big(\\hat{x}_0(x_0 + \\sigma_{\\text{probe}}\\,\\varepsilon_j,\\, 0)\\big) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 困难提示词的 reward 天然更嘈杂；用终态离散度归一化能让 $rho_{t}$ 保持有意义，避免它处处塌缩为零。\n\n### 可靠性门控采样器（Reliability-Gated Sampler）\n*把每步施加推翻为「仅在 $rho_{t}$ 高处按预算施加」的规则，并与加速采样器组合。*\n\n5. 把预算旋钮 beta 变成实际阈值 tau。跑几条$(P_{pilot}=4)$普通的试跑生成，收集每一步的可靠性分数，把 tau 设为这样一个临界点：只有可靠性排名前 beta 比例的步骤能越过它——例如 beta=0.4 让最可靠的 40% 步骤保持奖励激活。默认按每提示词计算 tau。beta 就是用户用来在奖励调用次数与对齐强度之间权衡的唯一旋钮。\n   - _为什么_: 它把「只在可靠处施加」变成用户可控的一个旋钮：beta 就是仍然查询 reward 的步骤比例。\n6. 带着门控运行生成：每一步若可靠性分数越过阈值 tau，就采用基础对齐器的奖励引导转移(顺序蒙特卡洛(Sequential Monte Carlo, SMC)的 potential、CREPE 的 replica 权重，或 guidance 项)；否则采用普通的预训练去噪步，且零次调用奖励。对多粒子采样器，按每个粒子自身的可靠性判断，只对该步奖励激活的粒子做加权/重采样。【作者需决定：是按每个粒子自身的可靠性分数门控，还是整个粒子群每步共用一个门控——两者都契合本方法，需作者选定。】跳过不可靠的步骤让图像在那里正常去噪，因此门控真正改变了你得到的图像，而不只是一个计数。\n\n*门控转移规则：当 $rho_{t} \\ge  \\tau $ 时采用对齐器的奖励激活转移（SMC potential / CREPE weight / guidance 项），否则采用无奖励评估的原始预训练转移；$\\tau $ 取 $rho_{t}$ 的 $(1- \\beta )$ 分位数，使 $\\beta $ 比例的转移保持奖励激活。*\n$$ \\text{transition}_t = \\begin{cases} \\text{reward\\text{-}active}(x_t) & \\rho_t \\geq \\tau \\\\ \\text{plain pretrained}(x_t) & \\rho_t < \\tau \\end{cases}, \\quad \\tau = \\mathrm{Quantile}_{1-\\beta}\\{\\rho_t\\} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 你只在真正有用的地方花 reward 调用，而跳过不可靠的早期步骤恰好移除了驱动 reward hacking 的那部分引导。\n7. 把门控原封不动地叠加在更快的采样器(如 GLASS Flows)之上：门控只决定在哪里施加奖励，而 GLASS 决定每步运行多便宜，两者处于不同层级因而可以组合。你同时得到更少的奖励激活步骤和更便宜的步骤。可靠性分数或阈值都无需改动——只需接入更快的转移例程。\n   - _为什么_: 更少的奖励激活步骤与更便宜的步骤相乘，两种加速叠加而非竞争。\n\n### 混淆隔离台架（Confound-Isolating Harness）\n*通过均匀/门控/置换的配对比较，证明预算-目标增益来自可靠性排序。*\n\n8. 运行受控检验：保持模型、奖励、采样器完全相同，只在三组之间改变调度——(U) 每步施加奖励，(G) 在预算 beta 下可靠性门控，(P) 与 G 相同数量的奖励激活步骤但置于随机位置(从而打乱可靠性排序)。每组记录最终奖励、图像与提示词的匹配度(CLIP-score / 视觉问答(Visual Question Answering, VQA)检查)、多样性，以及用了多少次奖励调用。把目标奖励定义为 U 收敛时达到的值，再比较每组需要多少次奖励调用才能达到它，并在相同奖励激活步数下比较 G 与 P。同时改变 m(1,2,4,8)和扰动幅度，确认胜出不只是来自对更多样本求平均。\n   - _为什么_: 若 G 在相同 reward 调用次数下仍胜过 P，说明胜出来自 $rho_{t}$ 指示的「在哪里行动」，而非仅仅做了更少调用——而 m 扫描排除了单纯平均的效应。\n\n"},{"id":"54","run_dir":"run_prompt54_rlro","index":54,"title":"Certified-Trust Reward Gradients: Per-Step Estimator-Error Bounds for Diffusion Fine-Tuning","title_zh":"可认证信任的奖励梯度：面向扩散模型微调的逐步估计误差上界","method_name":"Certified-Trust Reward Gradients (CTRG)","hook":"Every diffusion reward-fine-tuning method commits to one fixed gradient estimator — exact-but-noisy likelihood-ratio or biased-but-smooth backprop/surrogate — and then trusts each per-step update blindly, with no signal saying how far that step's gradient is from the true one. We show the disagreement between a coupled pair of estimators is itself a computable, distribution-free certificate of each step's distance to the true expected-reward gradient, turning the bias–variance choice from a fixed a-priori constant into a per-step, per-timestep quantity the optimizer can read and act on.","anchor_pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","anchor_pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","domain_category":"Generative Models — Vision","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces, at each fine-tuning step, a usable estimate of how far its own reward-gradient estimate is from the true expected-reward gradient — the estimator's error is assumed small but never measured, so an update driven by estimator noise is indistinguishable from a genuinely informative one and the optimizer cannot adapt its trust accordingly.","pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by reframing the informal question ‘is this step's reward-gradient trustworthy?’ as a concrete measurement over a well-studied object — a coupled (antithetic) pair of reward-gradient estimators whose per-step disagreement is an expectation/concentration estimator that upper-bounds each estimate's distance to the true expected-reward gradient — and certifying that bound by a causal intervention (perturbing it drives the downstream reward gain) rather than asserting estimator quality.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether the denoising chain must be treated as a single monolithic trajectory for gradient estimation at all — every leaf inherits from the shared denoising-as-MDP ancestor the assumption that one estimator (one variance regime) is applied uniformly across all timesteps, and none asks whether the right estimator could differ across the chain rather than being assumed identical end-to-end.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C29 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","how_closed":"Framing move (assumption_audit_and_pivot / C29): audit the denoising-as-MDP convergence/measurement assumption that one estimator regime is valid uniformly across all timesteps and pivot it to a per-timestep-band convergence criterion in which the certified bias–variance position is allowed to differ along the chain. Companion deliverable (controlled_diagnostic_design): a confound-isolating separation that holds reward, model, learning rate and rollout count fixed and varies only which certified estimator position is applied at which timestep band, so the measured per-band error divergence is attributable to chain position rather than to reward scale or compute.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"generative models — reward fine-tuning of diffusion models (gradient estimation for non-differentiable rewards)","n_papers":38,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":25},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":15,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Bridging Model-Based Optimization and Generative Modeling via Conservative Fine-Tuning of Diffusion Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Reward Fine-Tuning Two-Step Diffusion Models via Learning Differentiable Latent-Space Surrogate Reward"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Understanding Reinforcement Learning-Based Fine-Tuning of Diffusion Models: A Tutorial and Review"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Using Human Feedback to Fine-tune Diffusion Models without Any Reward Model"},{"source":"openalex","title":"ControlNet$$++$$: Improving Conditional Controls with Efficient Consistency Feedback"},{"source":"openalex","title":"A Cloud–Edge Collaborative Architecture for Multimodal LLM-Based Advanced Driver Assistance Systems in IoT Networks"}],"more":9},{"year":2025,"n":23,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Step-level Reward for Free in RL-based T2I Diffusion Model Fine-tuning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Self-supervised diffusion model fine-tuning for costate initialization using Markov chain Monte Carlo"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"ShortFT: Diffusion Model Alignment via Shortcut-Based Fine-Tuning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Self-NPO: Data-Free Diffusion Model Enhancement via Truncated Diffusion Fine-Tuning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Iterative Distillation for Reward-Guided Fine-Tuning of Diffusion Models in Biomolecular Design"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Personalized Preference Fine-tuning of Diffusion Models"}],"more":17}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":19,"share":0.5},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":9,"share":0.237},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":9,"share":0.237},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":7,"share":0.184},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":6,"share":0.158},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":5,"share":0.132},{"pattern_id":"algebraic_equivalence_unification","pattern_name":"Prove Equivalence to Unify","count":5,"share":0.132},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":3,"share":0.079}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"When a pre-trained diffusion model is fine-tuned to maximize an arbitrary scalar reward, the reward is frequently non-differentiable (a physics simulator, a docking score, a discrete-sequence metric, a safety checker), so the gradient of expected reward w.r.t. the model parameters cannot be obtained by backpropagation and must instead be estimated. The field splits into two regimes that each leave a residue: the unbiased likelihood-ratio / score-function estimator used by policy-gradient fine-tuning (denoising-as-MDP in semanticscholar:b88ba0959975d1aba56b182735c3abb5cc344023 'Score as Action', and the explicit non-differentiable policy-gradient of openalex:W4416749103) has variance that compounds across the long denoising chain, so the gradient estimate is too noisy to be trusted at any single step; the low-variance alternative replaces the reward with a differentiable proxy (the learned latent-space surrogate of semanticscholar:1898b422c5b24e0476fc06cb8193b9659e4c0b46, the Gumbel/continuous relaxation of openalex:W4403579970, the backprop-through-shortcut of semanticscholar:b214e7ca8ef5b8ed762b54ee5debd2079122eb69 ShortFT) and pays an unquantified bias whose size is never measured against the true black-box reward. Across these leaves no method exposes, per fine-tuning step, where its own gradient estimate sits on the bias–variance continuum between the two regimes or whether that position is the right one for the current reward landscape — the estimator's accuracy is assumed, never certified, so a practitioner cannot tell a genuinely informative update from estimator noise.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416749103","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Applies policy-gradient-style optimization of a non-differentiable safety/planning reward to diffusion-based motion planners, acknowledging that the score-function (likelihood-ratio) gradient is high-variance over the denoising trajectory. It mitigates noise with sampling/architectural heuristics but provides no estimator whose variance or bias is quantified or controllable per step — the gradient's reliability at a given update is assumed, not certified. [residue is abstract-level: anchor fulltext unfetchable]"},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:b88ba0959975d1aba56b182735c3abb5cc344023","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"'Score as Action' reframes diffusion reward fine-tuning as continuous-time RL with the score as the action, removing discretization error and supporting black-box/higher-order solvers. It still relies on the standard policy-gradient (likelihood-ratio) estimator whose variance compounds along the continuous trajectory; it neither bounds that variance nor offers a tunable interpolation toward a lower-variance biased estimate."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:1898b422c5b24e0476fc06cb8193b9659e4c0b46","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Learns a differentiable latent-space surrogate reward so that even non-differentiable rewards can be optimized by backprop, enabling RL on ultra-fast (≤2-step) distilled diffusion. The surrogate's bias relative to the true black-box reward is never measured, so the low-variance gradient it provides may point in a systematically wrong direction without any signal that this is happening."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4403579970","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Fine-tunes discrete-sequence diffusion (DNA/protein) for non-differentiable rewards using a continuous (Gumbel-softmax-style) relaxation to create a differentiable path. The relaxation introduces a bias whose magnitude is not quantified and which is not adjustable, so there is no way to trade it against the variance of the exact discrete likelihood-ratio estimator."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:acf2f14fbf6372470d6cc3bd7a8d17b54a00939d","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Tackles reward sparsity by deriving a dense step-level reward (contribution-based credit assignment) inside the denoising MDP, improving per-step attribution. It improves WHAT signal each step receives but leaves the per-step gradient ESTIMATOR untouched, so the variance of the likelihood-ratio update at each step is unchanged and uncertified."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"generative models — reward fine-tuning of diffusion models (gradient estimation for non-differentiable rewards)","venue":"ICLR / NeurIPS / ICML (top ML)","time":"2026","data":["text-to-image diffusion (Stable Diffusion / SDXL) with scalar reward models (aesthetic, ImageReward, CLIP-alignment)","discrete-sequence diffusion for DNA/protein with non-differentiable physics/docking rewards","diffusion policies for motion planning with non-differentiable safety rewards"],"compute":"1×A100 × 3 months ≈ 90 A100-day","expertise":"diffusion models, policy-gradient / score-function gradient estimation, stochastic optimization","preference":"both","baseline":"policy-gradient RL fine-tuning (DDPO/DPOK), backprop-through-the-chain on differentiable rewards (ShortFT), differentiable surrogate-reward fitting, and recursive-likelihood-ratio / 'half-order' estimators that interpolate zeroth-order likelihood-ratio with first-order backprop","limitation":"for non-differentiable (black-box) rewards, the only unbiased gradient is the likelihood-ratio / score-function estimator, whose variance grows with denoising-chain length, while the low-variance route (differentiable surrogate or backprop-through-chain) injects an unquantified bias; there is no estimator whose variance-bias position is itself controllable and certifiable per fine-tuning step","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object both legs read from and write to is the per-step certificate rho_t: a scalar, computable at every denoising timestep t of every fine-tuning rollout, that upper-bounds the Euclidean distance between the per-step reward-gradient estimate actually used and the true gradient of expected reward w.r.t. the model parameters at that step. We build rho_t by coupling two estimators of the SAME quantity g_t = grad_theta E[R] contributed by step t: g_t^LR, the exact likelihood-ratio (score-function) estimate (grad_theta log p_theta(x_{t-1}|x_t) weighted by the realized terminal reward R, the standard denoising-MDP policy-gradient term, unbiased, high variance); and g_t^BP, a low-variance biased estimate from one differentiable surrogate reward R_hat backpropagated through the (possibly shortcut/truncated) chain. The two are run on the SAME sampled rollout (antithetic coupling: common random noise z shared across the pair), so their difference d_t = ||g_t^LR - g_t^BP|| is dominated by the surrogate's bias plus the LR estimator's residual variance, and a one-line triangle-inequality argument plus an empirical-Bernstein concentration bound over the K rollouts in the minibatch gives rho_t = ||g_t^LR - g_t^BP|| + c*sqrt(Var_hat(g_t^LR)/K) as a high-probability upper bound on max(||g_t^used - g_t^true||) for either estimator — c is the Bernstein constant (a fixed hyperparameter, default sqrt(2 log(2/delta)) with delta=0.05), Var_hat is the per-step empirical variance of g_t^LR across the K coupled rollouts, and no quantity here requires a reward query beyond the single terminal R that LR already consumes. This is the C00 move: the opaque 'is this gradient trustworthy' becomes a measurement (a coupled-estimator distance) over a well-studied object (a control-variate / antithetic Monte-Carlo estimator with a concentration certificate), tractable via a fixed-size per-step accumulator and certified causally (Step-by-Step step 5) rather than by plausibility. The optimizer then USES rho_t as a per-step, per-timestep trust radius: the update at step t is a rho_t-gated blend g_t^used = w_t * g_t^BP + (1-w_t) * g_t^LR with w_t = sigma(-rho_t / tau) (tau a temperature hyperparameter), so when the certificate says the surrogate's biased gradient is provably close to truth the optimizer leans on its low variance, and when the certificate is large it falls back toward the unbiased LR direction or down-scales the whole step — crucially w_t is set BY the measured certificate per step, not fixed a priori. The second leg (C29 audit + controlled_diagnostic_design companion) reads the SAME rho_t object across timestep bands: it audits the inherited denoising-as-MDP assumption that one estimator regime is uniformly valid along the chain, pivots the convergence criterion to a per-band one, and ships the confound-isolating separation — partition timesteps into early/mid/late bands, hold reward+model+lr+K fixed, and measure the rho_t profile across bands; the audit's claim (the right bias-variance position differs systematically along the chain, e.g. late/low-noise steps tolerate the surrogate while early/high-noise steps do not) is confirmed when the per-band certified-error divergence is large and the band-uniform ablation underperforms the band-adaptive one. The two legs need no separate modules: rho_t is the single primitive — leg one constructs and acts on it per step, leg two reads its distribution across chain position to overturn the uniform-estimator assumption.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery because both are about the SAME quantity — the per-step gradient-estimator error — viewed at two granularities (a single step for the trust-gated update; the across-chain profile for the audit); the evidence is that the audit's deliverable (per-band error divergence) is literally rho_t aggregated by timestep band, so inventing a second estimator for the audit would be redundant. (b) Alternatives rejected: a fixed half-order/recursive-likelihood-ratio interpolation between LR and backprop (this is method_lineage node n5, the user's own seed) was rejected because a fixed blend weight cannot tell the optimizer where it sits relative to the true gradient — the contribution is precisely making the weight a function of a CERTIFIED per-step bound, not a constant; a plain variance-reducing baseline/control variate (node n1) was rejected because it lowers variance without emitting a distance-to-true-gradient certificate, so it cannot gate trust or support the audit. Avoided regression nodes recorded: n5 (fixed interpolation) and n1 (plain baseline).","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: fine-tune Stable Diffusion v1.5 on 100-400 prompts to maximize a held-out non-differentiable reward (e.g. an ImageReward / aesthetic score evaluated only at the final image), comparing the certified-trust method against vanilla DDPO (LR-only), a surrogate-backprop-only baseline, and a fixed-weight half-order interpolation, measuring the reward-model score on held-out prompts and human-preference win-rate. If the candidate works, the held-out reward-model score rises faster per reward query and reaches a higher plateau than all three baselines, and the win-rate against the fixed-interpolation baseline exceeds 50%. The named load-bearing variable is the per-step certificate rho_t (the certified gradient-error trust radius); the mechanism distinguisher is a negative control that replaces rho_t with a constant rho_bar (an uninformative certificate that makes the blend weight constant) while leaving K, the surrogate, the learning rate, and all rollouts unchanged — this must drive the held-out reward-model score back down to the band-uniform / fixed-interpolation baseline, because without an informative certificate the optimizer can no longer down-weight the steps whose gradient is provably far from truth. A positive control — gating updates by rho_t alone (skip steps with rho_t above a learned threshold, no surrogate blend) — should recover most of the reward-score improvement, identifying the certificate as the active ingredient rather than the surrogate.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:1898b422c5b24e0476fc06cb8193b9659e4c0b46","delta":"They construct a differentiable latent-space surrogate to replace the non-differentiable reward and backprop through it for a low-variance gradient, but never measure the surrogate's bias against the true reward gradient; we construct a per-step computable certificate rho_t that upper-bounds that very bias-plus-variance distance and feed it back to gate how much the surrogate is trusted at each step."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:b88ba0959975d1aba56b182735c3abb5cc344023","delta":"‘Score as Action’ removes discretization error via a continuous-time likelihood-ratio policy gradient but applies one estimator regime uniformly along the trajectory with unbounded variance; we derive a per-timestep certified error and a band-adaptive estimator that provably varies the bias-variance position along the chain."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416749103","delta":"They apply a high-variance non-differentiable policy gradient to diffusion motion planning and mitigate noise with heuristics; we replace heuristic noise control with a distribution-free per-step certificate of distance-to-true-gradient that the optimizer reads to adapt its trust. [residue is abstract-level: anchor fulltext unfetchable]"},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:acf2f14fbf6372470d6cc3bd7a8d17b54a00939d","delta":"They densify WHAT reward each step receives (contribution-based credit assignment) but leave the per-step gradient ESTIMATOR and its variance untouched; we leave the reward signal as-is and instead certify and adapt the estimator itself per step."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:1898b422c5b24e0476fc06cb8193b9659e4c0b46","what_step_was_missed":"They built the differentiable latent-space surrogate as a one-way replacement for the non-differentiable reward, used to produce a low-variance gradient; the step they did not construct is the coupling of that surrogate gradient with the exact likelihood-ratio gradient on shared random noise to extract their per-step disagreement as a concentration-certified upper bound on each estimate's distance to the true gradient — without that coupled-difference certificate there is no quantity telling the optimizer when the surrogate's bias has overtaken the LR estimator's variance, so the bias–variance position stays fixed and uncertified."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":212,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"Layer 1 did not fire: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict is borderline (no Reject lesson marked candidate_match: yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat is NOT exact-mechanism overlap (RSM characterizes tradeoffs but ships no computed per-step distance-to-true-gradient certificate). Within the safe zone I choose revise rather than advance because paper_pointed_threat.addressable_via names a specific candidate field (differentiation_from_lit must add an RSM entry) and because the borderline C29 lessons ('A theorem stated without formal assumptions ... is unreviewable' and 'characterize when [the weakened assumption] holds') hit a load-bearing structural property — rho_t's upper-bound status rests on an informally-stated g_t^LR-unbiasedness assumption that must be exhibited. Both are tactical field-level edits; recipe_application_check is applied for both entries, so the structure is sound and no sub_pattern swap is needed.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces, at each fine-tuning step, a usable estimate of how far its own reward-gradient estimate is from the true expected-reward gradient — the estimator's error is assumed small but never measured, so an update driven by estimator noise is indistinguishable from a genuinely informative one and the optimizer cannot adapt its trust accordingly.","main_pattern":"reframe_as_solvable_object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The signature failure is treating the reframing as a mechanical wrapper: taking an established attribution, decomposition, or estimation tool and pointing it at a new input granularity, a new architecture, or a new domain without re-deriving why the resulting scores are faithful to the model — supplying the computation but not the causal/axiomatic justification, so a reviewer can point to a methodological artifact that explains the result.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Pointing an off-the-shelf decomposition at a coarser input granularity without showing the coarser units preserve the signal reads as a wrapper, not a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism does not coarsen granularity — it derives a NEW object (rho_t = coupled-estimator distance + empirical-Bernstein term) at the FINEST per-step granularity and proves it upper-bounds distance-to-true-gradient, so no signal-preservation-under-coarsening claim is being smuggled."},{"lesson_quoted":"Porting a known attribution technique to a new architecture or domain while ignoring that technique's documented failure modes — and omitting comparisons to alternatives — leaves reviewers unable to see any unique benefit.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate is not a port of an attribution technique; differentiation_from_lit and core_mechanism_steps arm 7 explicitly compare against LR-only, surrogate-only, and the fixed-weight interpolation (n5) baselines, so alternatives are not omitted."},{"lesson_quoted":"Proposing a new attribution definition without an axiomatic or causal argument for why it should count as ground-truth collapses the moment a reviewer asks why this is the real importance.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"rho_t's status as a true UPPER BOUND on ||g_used - g_true|| rests on a triangle-inequality-plus-empirical-Bernstein argument and a stated assumption that g_t^LR is unbiased for the true step gradient; the candidate certifies USE causally (negative control) but the bound's soundness argument is one-line and would need its assumptions exhibited — load-bearing but addressable in Phase 4 expansion, not a documented Reject."},{"lesson_quoted":"Conflating a methodological artifact — a computation-granularity difference, a degenerate zero baseline — with genuine signal undermines the entire premise once the confound is identified.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The negative control (constant rho_bar with K, surrogate, lr, rollouts all held fixed) and the companion controlled_diagnostic_design arm are precisely designed to rule out that the gain comes from a confound rather than from the informative certificate."},{"lesson_quoted":"Building a suppression or privacy method without formalizing the threat model leaves the central guarantee unverifiable regardless of strong empirical numbers.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Not a suppression/privacy method; no threat model is implied."},{"lesson_quoted":"Surveying or recombining fragmented methods without a unifying axis or a decisive controlled experiment yields a contribution reviewers dismiss as anecdotal.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The unifying axis (the single primitive rho_t read at two granularities) and the decisive controlled experiment (negative control regressing to baseline) are both present and load-bearing."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether the denoising chain must be treated as a single monolithic trajectory for gradient estimation at all — every leaf inherits from the shared denoising-as-MDP ancestor the assumption that one estimator (one variance regime) is applied uniformly across all timesteps, and none asks whether the right estimator could differ across the chain rather than being assumed identical end-to-end.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C29 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The dominant failure shape is a relaxed assumption that is technically valid but uncharacterized — no named function/problem class shown to satisfy it and its constants' growth unstudied — read as engineered to close the proof; a second is a re-derived rate that merely matches the baseline with near-identical algorithmic changes; a third is hidden big-O constants that explode at the advertised regime.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A weakened assumption that no known function class is shown to satisfy reads as engineered to close the proof, not as a genuine generalization — characterize when it holds or it sinks the paper.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The pivoted assumption (the right bias-variance position differs by timestep band) is exhibited concretely — late/low-noise steps tolerate the surrogate, early/high-noise steps do not — and tested empirically by the per-band rho profile, so a concrete regime IS named; but the audit ships an empirical claim, not a re-proved rate, so the lesson partly mis-targets the deliverable rather than firing."},{"lesson_quoted":"Borrowing a relaxed condition from a neighboring literature without demonstrating its concrete benefit in your own setting leaves reviewers asking what the assumption actually buys.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The pivoted criterion is not borrowed; its concrete benefit (band-adaptive beats band-uniform arm B and fixed-interpolation arm C) is the literal success criterion of the controlled diagnostic in core_mechanism_steps arm 7."},{"lesson_quoted":"Re-deriving a rate that merely matches the baseline with near-identical algorithmic changes is read as an incremental extension, however clean the analysis.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The audit leg's deliverable is an identifiability/empirical claim (uniform-estimator regime is false), not a re-derived convergence rate, so there is no baseline-matching rate to be dismissed as incremental; the algorithmic change (per-band certified position) is non-trivial and tied to the certificate."},{"lesson_quoted":"Hidden constants that explode at the precise parameter limit where the result is advertised as strongest silently invalidate the headline guarantee, and reviewers find them in the proof.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"No asymptotic headline guarantee is advertised for the audit leg; the empirical-Bernstein constant c is a fixed, finite hyperparameter (sqrt(2 log(2/delta))) and does not grow with chain length or dimension."},{"lesson_quoted":"A theorem stated without formal assumptions or a precise claim is unreviewable; 'tight, assumption-free' bounds with no exhibited assumptions are treated as not-yet-a-paper.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"rho_t's upper-bound claim does rest on an unbiasedness assumption for g_t^LR that core_mechanism states informally; Phase 4 expansion should exhibit it explicitly, but the claim is not 'assumption-free' and the empirical certification path (negative control) makes it reviewable even short of a formal theorem."},{"lesson_quoted":"An assumption-relaxation validated only on a single toy instance gives no evidence the relaxation captures the motivating practical regime.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Validation is on SD v1.5 at 100-400-prompt scale with a real non-differentiable reward and a held-out win-rate, not a toy instance, so the motivating regime is exercised."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The C29 audit entry drove the aggregate to borderline via the lesson 'A theorem stated without formal assumptions or a precise claim is unreviewable' and the companion lesson on characterizing when a weakened assumption holds: rho_t's upper-bound status rests on an informally-stated unbiasedness assumption for g_t^LR. No Reject lesson is marked candidate_match: yes, so the aggregate is borderline, not triggered; the C00 entry is fully clear."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces, at each fine-tuning step, a usable estimate of how far its own reward-gradient estimate is from the true expected-reward gradient — the estimator's error is assumed small but never measured, so an update driven by estimator noise is indistinguishable from a genuinely informative one and the optimizer cannot adapt its trust accordingly.","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Recast an opaque transparency/uncertainty question as a concrete measurement over a well-studied object (an expectation/estimator over marginal statistics, a control-variate Monte-Carlo estimator), buy tractability with one compression trick (a fixed-size per-step accumulator), and certify fidelity by a causal intervention that flips behavior when the identified object is perturbed rather than by plausibility.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism performs exactly this: the opaque 'is this gradient trustworthy' becomes a measurement (the coupled antithetic-estimator distance d_t = ||g_t^LR - g_t^BP||) over a well-studied object (a control-variate / antithetic Monte-Carlo estimator with an empirical-Bernstein concentration certificate); tractability is bought by a fixed-size per-step accumulator (steps 4 and 6); and fidelity is certified causally by the negative-control intervention (step 8: replacing rho_t with constant rho_bar regresses the reward-model score to baseline) rather than by plausibility. All three signature moves of C00 are present.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether the denoising chain must be treated as a single monolithic trajectory for gradient estimation at all — every leaf inherits from the shared denoising-as-MDP ancestor the assumption that one estimator (one variance regime) is applied uniformly across all timesteps, and none asks whether the right estimator could differ across the chain rather than being assumed identical end-to-end.","sub_pattern":"C29 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Take an existing convergence/measurement assumption that a procedure silently rests on and pivot the single load-bearing assumption — e.g. replace a global/uniform regularity-or-convergence criterion with a position-/trajectory-local one — then isolate the one load-bearing object every corollary instantiates, showing the pivot buys coverage of a regime the uniform assumption excluded.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism audits the inherited denoising-as-MDP assumption that one estimator/variance regime is uniformly valid along the chain and pivots it to a per-timestep-BAND criterion in which the certified bias-variance position is allowed to differ along the chain (the position-local pivot the cluster names); the single load-bearing object every band instantiates is the same rho_t certificate aggregated by band. The C29 distinctive move (pivot a UNIFORM convergence/measurement criterion to a position-local one) is genuinely performed, not merely the parent's generic 'question an assumption' gist. Caveat: the cluster's canonical payoff is a re-PROVED rate/separation, whereas here the payoff is an empirical per-band separation shipped by the controlled_diagnostic_design companion — the pivot move is applied, but on a method/empirical deliverable rather than a proof.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries instantiate their cluster's distinctive move in core_mechanism: C00's measurement-over-a-well-studied-object-plus-causal-certification is fully enacted by the rho_t construction and the negative control; C29's pivot of a uniform measurement criterion to a position-local (per-band) one is enacted on the denoising-as-MDP assumption, with the empirical (rather than proof-theoretic) payoff carried by the attested companion controlled_diagnostic_design."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["reframe_as_solvable_object","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"The only 2-way subset is {reframe_as_solvable_object, assumption_audit_and_pivot}; all three documented reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as a component, which is absent, so no anti-pattern matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:17e530f1bbc727afc79d1de617cbd1927c188220","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"Reward Score Matching (RSM) is the nearest threat: it unifies existing reward-based diffusion/flow fine-tuning methods under a common 'score matching against a value-guided target' framework and explicitly states that the methods differ in 'the construction of the value-guidance estimator and the effective optimization strength across timesteps,' clarifying their 'bias-variance-compute tradeoffs.' This overlaps the candidate's framing that the bias-variance position is a per-timestep quantity. The candidate's claim STANDS only if its load-bearing artifact is distinct: RSM characterizes existing designs' tradeoffs analytically/post-hoc and varies optimization strength across timesteps as a design choice, but it does NOT construct a per-step COMPUTABLE certificate rho_t that upper-bounds each step's distance to the true expected-reward gradient and is read online by the optimizer to gate trust. If a reviewer reads RSM's 'effective optimization strength across timesteps' as already delivering an adaptive per-step weight, the candidate's novelty narrows to 'the weight is set by a certified bound rather than a fixed schedule' — which is precisely the contribution, but the differentiation must be made explicit against RSM, not only against the surrogate/LR baselines currently listed in differentiation_from_lit.","addressable_via":"Add an explicit differentiation_from_lit entry against RSM (semanticscholar:17e530f1bbc727afc79d1de617cbd1927c188220) stating that RSM's per-timestep optimization strength is a fixed/learned schedule with no measured distance-to-true-gradient, whereas rho_t is a computed online certificate that gates trust — a tactical field edit, not a mechanism change."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat — Reward Score Matching (RSM) already frames per-timestep bias-variance tradeoffs, so the differentiation list (currently only surrogate/LR/motion-planning/credit-assignment entries) leaves the closest framing threat unaddressed.","fix_direction":"Add a differentiation_from_lit entry for semanticscholar:17e530f1bbc727afc79d1de617cbd1927c188220: RSM unifies existing methods and varies per-timestep optimization strength as a fixed/learned schedule but never MEASURES each step's distance to the true gradient; the candidate's rho_t is a per-step COMPUTED certificate (coupled-estimator distance + empirical-Bernstein term) read online to set the blend weight, so the bias-variance position is certified per step rather than scheduled a priori. Do NOT alter falsification_prediction or compute_budget (kill-switch byte-identical)."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","issue":"gap_closure_reject_check borderline (C29 lessons on unreviewable assumption-free claims and characterizing when a weakened assumption holds; C00 lesson on axiomatic grounding) — rho_t's upper-bound status rests on an unbiasedness assumption for g_t^LR that is stated only informally.","fix_direction":"In core_mechanism, exhibit the stated assumption explicitly: state that g_t^LR is an unbiased estimator of the true per-step gradient g_t^true = grad_theta E[R] contributed by step t (standard denoising-MDP policy-gradient unbiasedness), so that rho_t = ||g_t^LR - g_t^BP|| + c*sqrt(Var_hat(g_t^LR)/K) is, with probability >= 1-delta, a valid upper bound on ||g_t^used - g_t^true|| for the gated estimator via triangle inequality plus the empirical-Bernstein tail. Naming the one load-bearing assumption makes the certificate reviewable without changing the mechanism, the falsification_prediction, or the compute_budget (kill-switch byte-identical)."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added a differentiation entry against Reward Score Matching (semanticscholar:17e530f1bbc727afc79d1de617cbd1927c188220), stating RSM varies per-timestep optimization strength as a fixed/learned schedule with no measured distance-to-true-gradient, whereas rho_t is a per-step computed certificate read online to set the blend weight."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Exhibited the one load-bearing assumption explicitly — g_t^LR is an unbiased estimator of the true per-step gradient g_t^true (standard denoising-MDP policy-gradient unbiasedness) — so that rho_t is, with probability >= 1-delta, a valid upper bound on ||g_t^used - g_t^true|| via triangle inequality plus the empirical-Bernstein tail, making the certificate reviewable without changing the mechanism."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Certified-Trust Reward Gradients: Per-Step Estimator-Error Bounds for Diffusion Fine-Tuning\n\n**Method.** Certified-Trust Reward Gradients (CTRG)\n\n## Motivation\nSuppose you have an image-generating diffusion model and you want to push it toward a goal scored by some black box — an aesthetics rater, a safety checker, a physics simulator — that you cannot differentiate. Because you cannot differentiate the scorer, you cannot simply backpropagate; you have to ESTIMATE the gradient (the direction to nudge the model). Today there are two ways, each with a flaw. The likelihood-ratio (also called score-function) estimator is exactly right on average but extremely noisy, and the noise piles up over the dozens of denoising steps, so any single step's estimate is untrustworthy. The alternative is to fit a smooth, differentiable stand-in for the scorer and backpropagate through that; this is quiet (low noise) but biased — it can point in a systematically wrong direction, and nobody measures how wrong.\n\nThe real problem is that no existing method tells you, at each step, how far its gradient is from the true one. The estimator's accuracy is just assumed. So you cannot tell an informative update from pure noise. The user's starting idea — a 'half-order' or recursive-likelihood-ratio blend that sits between the two estimators — points at this but does not solve it, because it picks one fixed blend in advance and still cannot tell you where you actually are relative to the truth.\n\nWhat makes this solvable now is a simple trick: run BOTH estimators on the EXACT SAME random rollout (sharing the random noise). Then their disagreement is no longer just sampling jitter — it measures the surrogate's bias plus the leftover noise of the exact estimator. Adding a standard statistical concentration term (an empirical-Bernstein bound) turns that disagreement into a genuine, high-confidence upper bound on how far the step's gradient is from the truth. We call this per-step number $rho_{t}$ (a 'trust radius'). The optimizer then reads $rho_{t}$ and blends the two estimators per step: where $rho_{t}$ is small it trusts the quiet surrogate; where $rho_{t}$ is large it falls back to the exact-but-noisy estimator or takes a smaller step. Reading $rho_{t}$ across early/middle/late denoising steps also reveals that the right trade-off is NOT the same along the chain — overturning the long-standing habit of using one estimator everywhere.\n\nClosing this gap means a practitioner can finally distinguish a real update from estimator noise, and the bias–variance choice becomes a measured quantity the optimizer adapts rather than a hyperparameter guessed once. Methods that fit a differentiable surrogate, or that run continuous-time policy gradient, become special cases recovered when the certificate is uniformly small or large.\n\n## Method\n### Coupled-estimator certificate\n*Run two gradient estimators on shared-noise rollouts and turn their disagreement plus a concentration term into a per-step upper bound on distance-to-true-gradient.*\n\n1. For each prompt, generate K = 8 denoising rollouts that all reuse the SAME random noise (the same starting latent and the same per-step noise tensors); store each step's intermediate image $x_{t}$ and the one final reward R per rollout. Default K = 8 gives enough paired samples to estimate the per-step spread without an extra batch. No extra calls to the black-box scorer beyond the single final score the policy-gradient method already needs.\n   - _Why_: Sharing the noise across the rollouts is what lets two later estimators be compared cleanly — their difference then reflects real bias, not random luck.\n2. At each denoising step t, compute the exact likelihood-ratio gradient (also called the score-function gradient): average over the K rollouts of (final reward R) times (gradient of the log-probability of that denoising step). This estimate is unbiased — on average it equals the true step gradient, shown in Eq. (1). While averaging, also track how much this gradient varies across the K rollouts (a running variance), which the certificate step needs.\n\n*The exact likelihood-ratio (score-function) per-step gradient averaged over K coupled rollouts; it is unbiased for the true per-step gradient $g_{t}$ of expected reward.*\n$$ g_t^{\\mathrm{LR}} = \\frac{1}{K}\\sum_{k=1}^{K} R^{(k)}\\, \\nabla_\\theta \\log p_\\theta\\!\\left(x_{t-1}^{(k)} \\mid x_t^{(k)}\\right), \\qquad \\mathbb{E}\\big[g_t^{\\mathrm{LR}}\\big] = g_t^{\\mathrm{true}} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: You need one estimator that is correct on average, because the trust certificate is only a distance-to-TRUTH measure if one of the two things being compared is the truth in expectation.\n3. At each step t, also compute the surrogate gradient: backpropagate a smooth differentiable stand-in reward $R_{hat}$ through the same rollouts. Build $R_{hat}$ as a small predictor (a small neural network or a CLIP image-head regressor) trained beforehand to predict the black-box reward from the final image, then frozen. This gradient is quiet (low spread) but biased — and that bias is exactly what we will measure, so the predictor does not need to be highly accurate.\n   - _Why_: This is the cheap, smooth estimator people already use alone; here it becomes the second opinion whose disagreement with the exact one we can measure.\n4. Compute the per-step trust radius $rho_{t} =$ (distance between the two gradients) $+ c\\cdot sqrt(variance$ of the exact gradient / K), with $c = sqrt(2\\cdot log(2/\\delta ))$ and $\\delta  =$ 0.05, as in Eq. (2). With at least 95% confidence this number upper-bounds how far the step's used gradient is from the true gradient: the first term captures the surrogate's bias, the second captures the exact estimator's leftover noise. Keep it in a small fixed-size running tally per timestep (no re-running of trajectories), reset every minibatch.\n\n*The per-step certificate: the coupled-estimator disagreement plus an empirical-Bernstein concentration term; with probability at least 1 minus $\\delta $ it upper-bounds the distance from the used gradient to the true gradient.*\n$$ \\rho_t = \\big\\| g_t^{\\mathrm{LR}} - g_t^{\\mathrm{BP}} \\big\\| + c\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{\\widehat{\\mathrm{Var}}\\big(g_t^{\\mathrm{LR}}\\big)}{K}}, \\qquad c = \\sqrt{2\\log(2/\\delta)} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The gap between the two estimators captures the surrogate's bias; the second term captures the exact estimator's leftover noise; together they certify the worst-case error without re-running anything.\n\n### Certificate-gated update\n*Use the per-step certificate as a trust radius to blend the two estimators, trusting the surrogate only where it is provably close to truth.*\n\n5. Blend the two gradients per step using Eq. (3): the weight on the quiet surrogate gradient shrinks as the trust radius $rho_{t}$ grows, then take the optimizer step. Set the temperature $\\tau $ to the $median rho_{t}$ in the current batch so the gate adjusts automatically to whatever scale the certified errors have. Where $rho_{t}$ is small, lean on the quiet surrogate; where it is large, fall back to the exact gradient, and optionally shrink the whole step when even the exact direction is certified far from truth.\n\n*The certificate-gated update: a per-step blend whose weight on the low-variance surrogate shrinks as the certified error $\\rho _{t}$ grows, with temperature $\\tau .$*\n$$ g_t^{\\mathrm{used}} = w_t\\, g_t^{\\mathrm{BP}} + (1-w_t)\\, g_t^{\\mathrm{LR}}, \\qquad w_t = \\sigma\\!\\left(-\\,\\rho_t/\\tau\\right) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The mixing weight is now set by the MEASURED certificate at each step, so the model trusts the smooth estimator only where it is provably close to truth — unlike a fixed blend chosen in advance.\n\n### Per-band audit\n*Aggregate the same certificate across denoising bands to overturn the assumption that one estimator regime fits the whole chain.*\n\n6. Record $rho_{t}$ into three denoising bands — early (first third of steps, near pure noise), middle, and late (final third, near the finished image) — to get a trust-radius profile along the chain. Then compare three runs with everything else held identical: band-adaptive gating (the full method), one-estimator-everywhere, and a fixed-blend interpolation; check whether band-adaptive wins on held-out reward and whether the $rho_{t}$ profile really differs across bands (a standard across-group statistical comparison). 【author decision: whether the three bands are equal-count thirds of the step index or are cut by noise-level quantiles — the way to slice the chain is left to the authors.】\n   - _Why_: Reading the same certificate across the chain tests, with confounds held fixed, the unspoken assumption that one estimator should be used at every step.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 可认证信任的奖励梯度：面向扩散模型微调的逐步估计误差上界\n\n**方法名称.** Certified-Trust Reward Gradients (CTRG)\n\n## 研究动机\n假设你有一个生成图像的扩散模型，想把它推向某个由黑盒打分器评判的目标——比如美学评分器、安全检查器或物理仿真器——而这个打分器是不可微的。因为打分器不可微，你无法直接做反向传播，只能去“估计”梯度（也就是该往哪个方向微调模型）。如今有两种做法，各有缺陷。likelihood-ratio（又称 score-function）估计量平均意义上完全正确，但噪声极大，而且噪声会沿着几十个去噪步骤不断累积，因此任何单步的估计都不可信。另一种做法是为打分器拟合一个光滑、可微的替身，然后对它做反向传播；这种方式很“安静”（噪声低）但有偏——它可能系统性地指向错误方向，而且没人去衡量它到底偏多少。\n\n真正的问题在于：没有任何现有方法能告诉你，在每一步上，它的梯度离真实梯度有多远。估计量的准确性只是被默认假设。于是你无法把有信息量的更新和纯噪声区分开。用户最初的想法——一个介于两种估计量之间的“half-order”或递归 likelihood-ratio 混合——指向了这个问题，但并没有解决它，因为它事先选定了一个固定的混合比例，仍然无法告诉你相对真值你实际处在哪里。\n\n现在能解决它，靠的是一个简单的技巧：在“完全相同”的随机轨迹上（共享随机噪声）同时运行“两个”估计量。这样它们之间的分歧就不再只是采样抖动，而是衡量了代理的偏差加上精确估计量残余的噪声。再加上一个标准的统计浓度项（empirical-Bernstein 上界），就能把这个分歧变成一个真正的、高置信度的上界，刻画该步梯度离真值有多远。我们把这个逐步的数值称为 $\\rho _{t}$（一个“信任半径”）。优化器随后读取 $\\rho _{t}$，并逐步混合两个估计量：$\\rho _{t}$ 小的地方就信任安静的代理；$\\rho _{t}$ 大的地方就退回到精确但有噪声的估计量，或者把这一步缩小。把 $\\rho _{t}$ 沿早/中/晚去噪步骤读出来，还会发现正确的取舍沿着整条链“并不相同”——从而推翻了长期以来“到处都用同一个估计量”的习惯。\n\n填补这个缺口意味着实践者终于能把真实更新和估计噪声区分开来，bias–variance 的取舍也从一个一次性猜定的超参数，变成优化器据以自适应的可测量。那些拟合可微代理、或运行连续时间 policy gradient 的方法，都会成为认证量整体偏小或偏大时所恢复的特例。\n\n## 方法\n### 耦合估计量认证\n*在共享噪声的轨迹上运行两个梯度估计量，把它们的分歧加上一个浓度项变成逐步的“到真实梯度距离”上界。*\n\n1. 对每个 prompt，生成 K = 8 条去噪轨迹，并让它们复用“同一份”随机噪声（相同的起始 latent 以及每一步相同的噪声张量）；保存每一步的中间图像 $x_{t}$ 以及每条轨迹唯一的最终奖励 R。默认 K = 8 足以估计逐步的离散程度，又不需要额外的 batch。除了 policy-gradient 本就需要的那一次最终打分外，不额外调用黑盒打分器(black-box scorer)。\n   - _为什么_: 让各条轨迹共享噪声，才能让后面两个估计量被干净地比较——它们的差异随后反映的是真实偏差，而不是随机运气。\n2. 在每个去噪步 t，计算精确的似然比梯度(likelihood-ratio gradient，又称 score-function gradient)：对 K 条轨迹取平均，每条是（最终奖励 R）乘以（该去噪步对数概率的梯度）。这个估计是无偏的——平均意义上等于真实的逐步梯度，见 Eq. (1)。在求平均的同时，也跟踪该梯度在 K 条轨迹间的波动程度（一个滑动方差），认证步骤会用到它。\n\n*在 K 条共享噪声轨迹上平均得到的精确似然比（score-function）逐步梯度；它对真实逐步梯度 $g_{t}$（期望奖励的梯度）是无偏的。*\n$$ g_t^{\\mathrm{LR}} = \\frac{1}{K}\\sum_{k=1}^{K} R^{(k)}\\, \\nabla_\\theta \\log p_\\theta\\!\\left(x_{t-1}^{(k)} \\mid x_t^{(k)}\\right), \\qquad \\mathbb{E}\\big[g_t^{\\mathrm{LR}}\\big] = g_t^{\\mathrm{true}} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 你需要一个平均意义上正确的估计量，因为只有当被比较的两者之一在期望上就是真值时，信任认证量才是一个“到真值的距离”度量。\n3. 在每个步 t，再计算代理梯度(surrogate gradient)：把一个光滑可微的替身奖励 $R_{hat}$ 通过同一批轨迹反向传播。把 $R_{hat}$ 做成一个小预测器（一个小神经网络，或一个 CLIP 图像头回归器），事先训练它从最终图像预测黑盒奖励，然后冻结。这个梯度很安静（离散度低）但有偏——而这个偏差正是我们要测量的，所以这个预测器不需要很准。\n   - _为什么_: 这正是人们已经在单独使用的廉价、光滑的估计量；在这里它成为“第二意见”，我们可以衡量它与精确估计量的分歧。\n4. 计算逐步信任半径 $rho_{t} =$（两个梯度之间的距离）$+ c\\cdot sqrt($精确梯度的方差 / K)，其中 $c = sqrt(2\\cdot log(2/\\delta ))$、$\\delta  = 0.05$，见 Eq. (2)。以至少 95% 的置信度，这个数值上界了该步所用梯度离真实梯度有多远：第一项刻画代理的偏差，第二项刻画精确估计量残余的噪声。把它存进一个小的、固定大小的逐时间步滑动累加器里（无需重跑轨迹），每个 minibatch 重置一次。\n\n*逐步认证量 $\\rho _{t}$：耦合估计量之间的分歧再加上一个 empirical-Bernstein 浓度项；以至少 1 减 $\\delta $ 的概率，它上界了所用梯度到真实梯度的距离。*\n$$ \\rho_t = \\big\\| g_t^{\\mathrm{LR}} - g_t^{\\mathrm{BP}} \\big\\| + c\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{\\widehat{\\mathrm{Var}}\\big(g_t^{\\mathrm{LR}}\\big)}{K}}, \\qquad c = \\sqrt{2\\log(2/\\delta)} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 两个估计量之间的差距刻画了代理的偏差；第二项刻画了精确估计量残余的噪声；两者合起来认证了最坏情况误差，且无需重跑任何东西。\n\n### 认证量门控更新\n*把逐步认证量当作信任半径来混合两个估计量，只在可证明接近真值处才信任代理。*\n\n5. 用 Eq. (3) 逐步混合两个梯度：信任半径 $rho_{t}$ 越大，安静的代理梯度上的权重就越小，然后做优化器更新。把温度 $\\tau $ 设为当前 batch 中 $rho_{t}$ 的中位数，使门控自动适应认证误差所处的尺度。$rho_{t}$ 小的地方就倚重安静的代理；大的地方就退回精确梯度，并在连精确方向都被认证为远离真值时可选地缩小整步。\n\n*由认证量门控的更新：逐步混合，其在低方差代理上的权重随认证误差 $\\rho _{t}$ 增大而减小，温度为 $\\tau $。*\n$$ g_t^{\\mathrm{used}} = w_t\\, g_t^{\\mathrm{BP}} + (1-w_t)\\, g_t^{\\mathrm{LR}}, \\qquad w_t = \\sigma\\!\\left(-\\,\\rho_t/\\tau\\right) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 混合权重现在由每一步“测得”的认证量决定，因此模型只在可证明接近真值的地方才信任光滑估计量——不像事先选定的固定混合。\n\n### 分带审计\n*把同一个认证量沿去噪带聚合，推翻“一个估计量制度适配整条链”的假设。*\n\n6. 把 $rho_{t}$ 记入三个去噪带——早期（前三分之一步，接近纯噪声）、中期、晚期（后三分之一步，接近成品图像）——得到一条沿链的信任半径剖面。然后在其他一切保持完全一致的条件下比较三次运行：分带自适应门控（完整方法）、处处单一估计量、以及固定混合插值；检验分带自适应是否在留出(held-out)奖励上胜出，以及 $rho_{t}$ 的剖面是否在各带之间确实不同（一种标准的组间统计比较）。【作者需决定：这三个带是按步骤序号等数量三等分，还是按噪声水平分位数切分——如何切分这条链交由作者确定。】\n   - _为什么_: 在控制混杂因素的前提下，沿链读取同一个认证量，检验了“每一步都该用同一个估计量”这一未明说的假设。\n\n"},{"id":"55","run_dir":"run_prompt55_saliencyhallu","index":55,"title":"Per-Step Counterfactual Grounding: Online Hallucination Onset from Evidence-Ablation, Not Attention Magnitude","title_zh":"逐步反事实接地（Per-Step Counterfactual Grounding）：用证据消融在线定位幻觉起点","method_name":"Per-Step Counterfactual Grounding (PCG)","hook":"Internal-state hallucination detectors read one pooled scalar over a finished response and cannot say at which decoding step the model stopped relying on its evidence; we manufacture, at every step, a label-free counterfactual grounding signal — how much the next-token distribution actually shifts when the attended evidence is ablated — and show a negative control that this CAUSAL evidence-dependence, not raw attention magnitude, is what localizes hallucination onset. Because the same per-step signal exposes evidence-dependence (intrinsic risk) and parametric-distribution dispersion (extrinsic risk) separately, a single online router decides which one governs each token instead of shipping two offline detectors.","anchor_pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","anchor_pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","domain_category":"LLM Alignment, Safety & Behavior","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf produces a per-decoding-step grounding quantity that distinguishes the steps where the next-token distribution is still supported by the evidence the model is attending to from the step at which that support first breaks — every detector collapses the whole trajectory into one post-hoc scalar, so the onset locus of an unsupported span is never made into an observable, step-resolved quantity the rest of the system could read (additive; sits at the anchor's residual_prob","pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by repurposing a measurement-only diagnostic as an active per-step control signal on an already-trained model: at each decoding step the model's own attention selects the evidence set, and the label-free readout is the counterfactual shift delta_t in the next-token distribution when that attended evidence is ablated — a step-resolved scalar computed from the model alone, with no hallucination labels, that makes grounding-onset observable along the generation instead of as one post-hoc scalar.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf reconciles the empirical finding that intrinsic (context-unfaithful) and extrinsic (fact-fabricated) hallucinations require DIFFERENT internal signals into a single per-step decision of which signal governs the current token — the anchor discovers the split but ships two separate detectors, so there is no leaf that, at a given step, decides whether attention-over-evidence or output-distribution dispersion is the load-bearing signal for THAT step's risk (additive; sits ","pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by partitioning the per-step risk into two structurally distinct components by a discriminating property — evidence-counterfactual sensitivity (delta_t, governs intrinsic context-grounding) versus parametric-distribution dispersion under context-ablation (eps_t, governs extrinsic fact-recall) — and routing each token at decode time to whichever component is load-bearing, rather than reading one pooled signal or two offline detectors.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"hallucination detection/mitigation in foundation models (LLMs and multimodal LLMs) via internal saliency / attention-attribution signals","n_papers":38,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":25},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":12,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Unsupervised Real-Time Hallucination Detection based on the Internal States of Large Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Prompt-Guided Internal States for Hallucination Detection of Large Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"INSIDE: LLMs' Internal States Retain the Power of Hallucination Detection"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"LLM Internal States Reveal Hallucination Risk Faced With a Query"},{"source":"openalex","title":"LLMs Know More Than They Show: On the Intrinsic Representation of LLM Hallucinations"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Detecting hallucinations in large language models using semantic entropy"}],"more":6},{"year":2025,"n":26,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"HalluCounter: Reference-free LLM Hallucination Detection in the Wild!"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Multi-perspective consistency checking for large language model hallucination detection: a black-box zero-resource approach"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Chain-of-Thought Prompting Obscures Hallucination Cues in Large Language Models: An Empirical Evaluation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Scenario-independent Uncertainty Estimation for LLM-based Question Answering via Factor Analysis"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"What are Models Thinking about? Understanding Large Language Model Hallucinations \"Psychology\" through Model Inner State Analysis"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Data-efficient Meta-models for Evaluation of Context-based Questions and Answers in LLMs"}],"more":20}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":17,"share":0.447},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":10,"share":0.263},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":8,"share":0.211},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":6,"share":0.158},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":5,"share":0.132},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":4,"share":0.105},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":2,"share":0.053},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":2,"share":0.053}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"State-of-the-art internal-signal hallucination detectors compute one aggregate statistic over an already-completed generation and use it only as a post-hoc verdict: The Map of Misbelief (openalex:W4416339600) aggregates attention mass over input tokens into a single sequence-level uncertainty score, INSIDE (semanticscholar:f62acb5a743ea4d47a045460a9ee346c2cec5068) reads the covariance/eigenstructure of sentence embeddings, semantic entropy (openalex:W4399803256) needs many samples of the whole output distribution, and the per-token truthfulness work (openalex:W4403928636) shows the error-predictive signal actually concentrates on a few specific generated tokens yet still only classifies the finished response. The shared structural failure is that the attribution signal is read at the WRONG granularity and the WRONG time: a hallucination is a localized event that begins at a specific decoding step when the next-token distribution stops being supported by the retrieved/parametric evidence the model is attending to, but every retrieved detector collapses the whole trajectory into one number computed after the fact, so it can report THAT a response is unreliable but cannot say WHERE the grounding first broke, cannot do so before the unsupported span has already been emitted, and cannot hand the decoder a per-step quantity to steer away from the break. Compounding this, these detectors implicitly assume one universal internal signal serves all hallucination kinds, whereas openalex:W4416339600 itself finds attention-over-input separates intrinsic (context-unfaithful) errors while sample-distribution entropy separates extrinsic (fact-fabricated) errors — so a single pooled read is mis-specified for at least one error type by construction.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416339600","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"The Map of Misbelief aggregates a recent attention-based uncertainty-quantification signal over input tokens with novel attention-aggregation strategies, and shows empirically that attention-over-input is the right family for intrinsic (context-unfaithful) hallucinations while sampling/semantic-entropy is the right family for extrinsic (fabricated-fact) hallucinations. Its residue: the attention aggregation is computed once over the whole completed response and used only as a post-hoc binary/typed detector — it produces no per-decoding-step trajectory of the signal, never identifies the step at which grounding first collapses, and is never closed into the decoding loop to prevent the break; and although it discovers that intrinsic vs extrinsic errors need different signals, it leaves the two signals as separate detectors rather than reconciling when each governs a given step.","year_month":"2025-11"},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4403928636","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"LLMs Know More Than They Show probes white-box internal states and demonstrates that the truthfulness-predictive signal is concentrated in specific 'exact-answer' tokens rather than spread across the response, and that internal states encode the error before it surfaces behaviorally. Its residue: it localizes the signal to particular tokens only retrospectively for classifying a finished response, and does not turn that token-localized signal into an online, step-by-step grounding measure usable during generation nor relate it to the attention/saliency the model places on its evidence at that step."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4399803256","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Semantic entropy detects confabulations by clustering many sampled outputs by meaning and measuring entropy over meaning-clusters, giving a strong response-level signal for fact-fabrication (extrinsic) errors. Its residue: it is a whole-output, multi-sample, post-hoc estimator with no notion of where within a single generation the unsupported content begins and no internal-attribution grounding, so it is both expensive and blind to the decoding-step locus of the failure."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:f62acb5a743ea4d47a045460a9ee346c2cec5068","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"INSIDE reads hallucination from the eigen-structure (EigenScore) of the model's sentence-level internal embeddings, recovering semantic information lost by logit-level uncertainty. Its residue: the covariance read is a single sequence-level scalar computed over the finished sentence's embeddings, with no per-step localization of the onset and no use of where the model's attention/saliency over evidence drops."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"hallucination detection/mitigation in foundation models (LLMs and multimodal LLMs) via internal saliency / attention-attribution signals","venue":"ICLR/NeurIPS/ACL tier (foundation/frontier models incl. LLMs)","time":"2026","data":["TruthfulQA / TriviaQA / NQ-Open factual QA","HaluEval and FAVA span-level hallucination annotations","RAGTruth / context-grounded QA for faithfulness (intrinsic) hallucination","SelfCheckGPT / FActScore long-form generation sets","open-weight LLMs (Llama-3-8B/70B, Mistral-7B, Qwen2.5) with accessible attention + hidden states"],"compute":"1×A100 × 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with LLM interpretability + uncertainty-quantification background","preference":"both","baseline":"attention-aggregation hallucination detection — The Map of Misbelief (openalex:W4416339600); secondary: INSIDE EigenScore (semanticscholar:f62acb5a743ea4d47a045460a9ee346c2cec5068), semantic entropy (openalex:W4399803256), per-token truthfulness probe (openalex:W4403928636)","limitation":"current internal-signal hallucination detectors read a single pooled/aggregate score (attention mass over input tokens, hidden-state covariance, or output entropy) AFTER a full response is generated and use it only as a post-hoc binary classifier; they neither localize the within-generation token position where the model's grounding actually breaks, nor expose a quantity the decoder can act on to avoid the break, and they assume the internal signal that correlates with hallucination on factual (extrinsic) errors is the same signal that should be read for context-grounded (intrinsic) errors","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The thread is a sequential_pipeline whose central streamed object is a per-decoding-step grounding pair g_t = (delta_t, eps_t) computed online for each generated token t; LEG 1 manufactures g_t and LEG 2 consumes it to route. SETTING: a white-box autoregressive LLM (open-weight, e.g. Llama-3-8B) generating with a context C that holds the evidence tokens (retrieved passages for RAG, or the in-context document for faithfulness QA). LEG 1 (anchor, C07): at step t, the model's last-layer cross-position attention over C is already computed in the normal forward pass; define the attended-evidence set E_t = the smallest set of context tokens whose attention mass (averaged over a FIXED head set H, selected once on a 200-example dev split as the top-k heads by attention-to-evidence correlation with answer-token positions, k=8) reaches a cumulative fraction rho=0.9 of the total attention-to-C mass at step t. The label-free counterfactual readout is delta_t = JSD(p_t || p_t^{-E_t}), the Jensen-Shannon divergence (in bits, bounded [0,1]) between the real next-token distribution p_t and the distribution p_t^{-E_t} obtained by a single extra forward pass with the attention logits to E_t set to -inf (a clean counterfactual ablation of EXACTLY the tokens the model relied on, not a generic attention drop). delta_t is the per-step CAUSAL evidence-dependence: high delta_t means the next token genuinely depends on the evidence (grounded); delta_t collapsing toward 0 at a step where the model is nonetheless emitting content-bearing tokens means the model has stopped relying on its evidence — the onset locus. The second component eps_t = JSD(p_t^{-C} || u) where p_t^{-C} is the next-token distribution with the WHOLE evidence context C ablated (parametric-only continuation) and u is the per-step parametric uncertainty measured as that distribution's normalized entropy; eps_t is the model's parametric-recall dispersion at step t (high eps_t = the parametric memory itself is unsure, the extrinsic-fabrication regime). Both are computed from at most two extra forward passes per step (one -E_t, one -C), batched with the main pass. To keep this from a degenerate read, C07's stabilizer is bolted on: delta_t is only trusted at steps whose token is content-bearing (a frozen POS/stopword filter masks function-word steps where evidence-dependence is meaningless), and a two-time-scale exponential baseline b_t = EMA of delta over the last w=16 content steps anchors the signal so a single noisy step cannot trigger — the onset call is delta_t < beta * b_t sustained for s>=2 content steps, with beta=0.5 a dev-set threshold. This is the runnable method deliverable: a streamed g_t with a calibrated onset flag, no retraining, frozen backbone. LEG 2 (sibling, C04): partition the per-step risk by the discriminating property 'which evidence source is load-bearing here'. At each step the router computes a load-bearing indicator: if delta_t is well-defined and large relative to b_t the step is in the INTRINSIC partition (context-grounding governs; its risk is read from delta_t's drop), whereas if delta_t is near-zero AND eps_t is high the step is in the EXTRINSIC partition (the model is not using context and its parametric recall is dispersed; risk is read from eps_t). The router is a fixed two-region decision over (delta_t, b_t, eps_t) (region boundaries fit on the same 200-example dev split, no per-token training), emitting a per-step risk type and score. The error/fidelity decomposition that is C04's spine: total per-step hallucination risk R_t is bounded by max(intrinsic_risk(delta_t), extrinsic_risk(eps_t)) and we show on annotated spans that the two partitions are separable — intrinsic-labeled error spans have onset at delta_t collapse with eps_t low, extrinsic-labeled spans have onset at high eps_t with delta_t already low — so the differentiated per-step treatment strictly beats reading either single pooled signal. The legs interlock as one pipeline: LEG 1's streamed g_t is exactly LEG 2's router input; same object, one produces it online, the other partitions it.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The two gaps share the streamed object g_t but need separate modules (a signal producer and a router), which is why this is a sequential_pipeline rather than shared_object collapse: LEG 1 must exist and be validated as a per-step signal before LEG 2's routing is even meaningful, and the C04 error decomposition only has content once delta_t and eps_t are both defined. I considered training a small probe to predict hallucination from pooled hidden states (the C08/supervised-detector route) but rejected it: it would re-introduce a label-dependent post-hoc classifier (the very framing the bottleneck flags) and make the negative control tautological. REGRESSION CHECK: the avoided nodes are the method_lineage REGRESSION FLAG's named priors — (i) the seed's own exact-mechanism prior 'hallucination begins where saliency/attention drops' (raw attention magnitude as the onset signal): we explicitly do NOT use attention magnitude as the signal; delta_t is a CAUSAL counterfactual divergence under ablation of the attended set, and the headline negative control dissociates the two (a step can have high attention yet low delta_t). (ii) n0 token-entropy thresholding and (iii) n1 semantic-entropy sampling: delta_t is neither a single-token entropy nor a multi-sample whole-output dispersion; eps_t uses one context-ablated forward pass, not k full re-generations. (iv) collateral c2 steering-decoding: we produce a calibrated WHEN signal and do not edit the distribution to mitigate, so we do not reduce to contrastive/steering decoding. The mechanism therefore draws on the lineage node the tree does not yet occupy: a per-step causal evidence-dependence measure, recorded here for auditability.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on an open-weight LLM (Llama-3-8B, Mistral-7B) generating answers for span-annotated hallucination benchmarks with evidence context (RAGTruth and FAVA for intrinsic/faithfulness, HaluEval and TriviaQA-closed-book for extrinsic/factual), stream the per-step grounding pair g_t = (delta_t, eps_t) and measure (i) onset-step localization error = token distance between the flagged first-ungrounded step and the gold hallucinated-span start, (ii) span-level AUROC for hallucination, and (iii) intrinsic-vs-extrinsic routing accuracy against the span labels. If the candidate works, onset-localization error is small (flagged onset lands within a few tokens of the gold span start) and span AUROC meets or exceeds the pooled attention-aggregation detector of The Map of Misbelief (openalex:W4416339600) on intrinsic spans while the eps_t-routed path matches semantic-entropy (openalex:W4399803256) on extrinsic spans — i.e. one streamed signal covers both regimes a single pooled read cannot. The named load-bearing variable is the per-step counterfactual evidence-dependence delta_t. NEGATIVE CONTROL: swap delta_t for raw attention-magnitude-to-evidence a_t (the 'hallucination begins where saliency drops' signal) with all else fixed; the mechanism claim predicts onset-localization error RISES and span AUROC FALLS on intrinsic spans, because attention magnitude correlates with but does not causally measure reliance — if localization and AUROC are unchanged after this swap, the gain came from attention magnitude alone and the counterfactual-ablation mechanism is falsified. POSITIVE CONTROL: a stripped detector using only delta_t with no eps_t and no router recovers most of the intrinsic-span localization, constructively identifying causal evidence-dependence (not attention magnitude, not output entropy) as the load-bearing quantity.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416339600","delta":"The Map of Misbelief aggregates attention-over-input into ONE post-hoc sequence-level uncertainty score and ships two separate detectors for intrinsic vs extrinsic; we compute a per-decoding-step CAUSAL counterfactual evidence-dependence delta_t (next-token distribution shift under ablation of the attended evidence, not attention magnitude) that localizes the onset step online, and a single per-step router that decides intrinsic vs extrinsic for each token — neither the step-resolved causal signal nor the online router exists in their construction."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4403928636","delta":"They show truthfulness is encoded in specific exact-answer tokens but use it only retrospectively to classify a finished response; we turn the per-token signal into an ONLINE counterfactual measure delta_t computed during generation and define the onset-step flag, which their retrospective probe does not produce."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4399803256","delta":"Semantic entropy needs k full output samples and yields a whole-response scalar with no within-generation locus; our eps_t uses a single context-ablated forward pass per step to read parametric dispersion online, and we localize the extrinsic-error onset rather than scoring the whole output."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:f62acb5a743ea4d47a045460a9ee346c2cec5068","delta":"INSIDE reads a single EigenScore over a finished sentence's embedding covariance; we never pool over the sentence — delta_t and eps_t are per-step quantities with a calibrated onset flag, and we measure causal evidence-dependence by ablation rather than embedding covariance."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4416339600","what_step_was_missed":"The Map of Misbelief already reads the model's attention over input/evidence tokens and even discovers that intrinsic and extrinsic hallucinations need different signals, but it aggregates attention magnitude into one post-hoc score and leaves the two signals as separate offline detectors; the substantive steps missing for our contribution to already exist are (a) the construction of a per-decoding-step counterfactual grounding measure delta_t = JSD(p_t || p_t^{-E_t}) that ablates exactly the attended-evidence set and reads the resulting causal next-token shift (a measurement primitive their attention-magnitude aggregation never computes), and (b) the online per-step router over (delta_t, b_t, eps_t) with an error decomposition that reconciles their intrinsic/extrinsic split into a single streamed decision rather than two detectors."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":202,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"Layer 1 hard floor did NOT fire: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict is borderline (no Reject lesson marked candidate_match: yes); anti_pattern_check matched audit_decomp_supervisor but mitigation_substantively_delivered = true (the decomposition is derived from the observed span value-distribution, the signal is unique to each partition, and the hold-one-fixed disentangling ablation is the negative/positive control); and paper_pointed_threat against openalex:W4416339600 is an addressable adjacent-mechanism overlap (attention magnitude vs causal evidence-dependence), NOT exact-mechanism. In Layer 2 the candidate is sound on its load-bearing mechanism (recipe_application_check = applied on both legs) but the C04 borderline lesson ('a sensitivity proxy reads as rediscovery unless sharply differentiated') and the addressable threat both land on differentiation_from_lit, so I choose revise to sharpen the attention-magnitude-vs-causal-reliance delta rather than advance with the differentiation under-stated.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf produces a per-decoding-step grounding quantity that distinguishes the steps where the next-token distribution is still supported by the evidence the model is attending to from the step at which that support first breaks — every detector collapses the whole trajectory into one post-hoc scalar, so the onset locus of an unsupported span is never made into an observable, step-resolved quantity the rest of the system could read (additive; sits at the anchor's residual_problem that the attribution signal is read once over the completed response rather than along the generation).","main_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure shape is a manufactured internal signal whose validity silently rests on an assumption that does not survive deployment (model calibration, a stationary/known-finite set of shift types, or covert use of target/test-set information amounting to label leakage); a second shape is recombining well-known components without a single load-bearing mechanistic insight that separates the work from prior art.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A label-free signal whose validity depends on model calibration silently fails on exactly the deep networks known to be poorly calibrated — validate a surrogate where its core assumption is weakest, not where it is convenient.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"delta_t does not depend on model calibration — it is a counterfactual divergence between two of the model's own distributions (with vs without the attended evidence), so a miscalibrated softmax shifts both p_t and p_t^{-E_t} together and the JSD between them is robust to absolute calibration error."},{"lesson_quoted":"Recasting a continuous shift as a discrete, known, finite set of types indexed against a precomputed lookup table collapses the moment an unanticipated or mixed shift arrives.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The intrinsic/extrinsic partition is not a precomputed lookup of fixed hallucination types — it is computed online per step from continuous (delta_t, eps_t), and a mixed step (low delta_t AND high eps_t) is handled by the router's region rule rather than failing on an unanticipated type."},{"lesson_quoted":"Reusing standard sequential machinery (chaining each step's posterior as the next prior) without a new stabilizer amplifies noise and looks derivative of prior adaptation work.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate adds an explicit C07 stabilizer (frozen POS/stopword content-mask + EMA baseline b_t + sustained s>=2-step onset rule) precisely to keep a single noisy step from triggering, which is the required new stabilizer rather than naked posterior chaining."},{"lesson_quoted":"Using target or test-set information during adaptation invites a label-leakage objection that undermines the very source-free, label-free deployment setting the method claims.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"delta_t and eps_t use only the model's own forward passes on the live input; the only fitted quantities (head set H, beta, router boundary) are set on a disjoint 200-example dev split, never on the test inputs or their hallucination labels, so there is no test-time label leakage."},{"lesson_quoted":"Importing a generic continual-learning blending or interpolation technique into a new modality without identifying that modality's specific dynamics lever reads as recombination, not contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The load-bearing lever is identified mechanistically and uniquely: causal evidence-dependence under counterfactual ablation of the attended set, dissociated from attention magnitude by the negative control — not a generic blending imported wholesale."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf reconciles the empirical finding that intrinsic (context-unfaithful) and extrinsic (fact-fabricated) hallucinations require DIFFERENT internal signals into a single per-step decision of which signal governs the current token — the anchor discovers the split but ships two separate detectors, so there is no leaf that, at a given step, decides whether attention-over-evidence or output-distribution dispersion is the load-bearing signal for THAT step's risk (additive; sits at the anchor's residual_problem of leaving the intrinsic/extrinsic signals unreconciled).","main_pattern":"heterogeneous_decomposition","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is treating the partition criterion itself as the contribution while leaving its value unproven — reviewers map the discriminator onto an established technique and read it as relabeling; compounding this, the scheme is rarely benchmarked against both the strongest uniform baseline and the obvious cheap alternative, and validation is done in a regime where the bottleneck does not bite.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Presenting a sensitivity or redundancy proxy as the novelty invites the verdict that it rediscovers known mixed-precision or low-rank results unless it is sharply differentiated from the obvious prior criterion.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The partition's discriminating property (evidence-counterfactual sensitivity vs parametric dispersion) must be sharply differentiated from the anchor's existing intrinsic/extrinsic split; the candidate differentiates by being per-step and causal rather than pooled-attention, but this must be explicit in differentiation_from_lit, so it is borderline rather than clear."},{"lesson_quoted":"Omitting comparison against both the strongest uniform baseline and the obvious cheap alternative (SVD/PCA, structured dropout, a natively trained smaller model) leaves reviewers unable to tell whether the partition buys anything at all.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The harness compares against the strongest uniform baseline (pooled attention-aggregation, The Map of Misbelief) and the obvious cheap alternative (semantic entropy and raw-attention-magnitude via the negative control), so the uniform-vs-differentiated comparison is present."},{"lesson_quoted":"Skipping any analysis of why the heterogeneity exists — the data or value distribution that drives the partition — makes the technical novelty and the potential impact impossible to assess.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate grounds the heterogeneity empirically: it shows on annotated spans that intrinsic-labeled spans have onset at delta_t collapse with eps_t low while extrinsic-labeled spans have high eps_t with delta_t already low — the value distribution that forces the two-way partition."},{"lesson_quoted":"A clever partition with no measured real-world deployment metric (no inference latency or memory speedup) reads as a proxy-only contribution and stalls at borderline.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Step 12 reports tokens/sec and latency vs baseline decoding and vs k-sample semantic-entropy detection, so a real deployment metric (throughput/latency at matched detection quality) is measured, not just a proxy."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The C04 (heterogeneous_decomposition) entry is borderline because the partition's discriminating property must be sharply separated from the anchor's existing intrinsic/extrinsic distinction — the lesson 'presenting a sensitivity proxy as the novelty invites the verdict that it rediscovers known results unless sharply differentiated' carries weight and lands on differentiation_from_lit. The C07 entry is fully clear (no calibration dependence, no label leakage, explicit stabilizer). No Reject lesson is marked candidate_match: yes, so the gap_closure_reject_check does not trigger the hard floor."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf produces a per-decoding-step grounding quantity that distinguishes the steps where the next-token distribution is still supported by the evidence the model is attending to from the step at which that support first breaks — every detector collapses the whole trajectory into one post-hoc scalar, so the onset locus of an unsupported span is never made into an observable, step-resolved quantity the rest of the system could read (additive; sits at the anchor's residual_problem that the attribution signal is read once over the completed response rather than along the generation).","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Treat an already-trained model's own internal-state readout as the manufactured supervisory signal, pairing a mechanistic diagnosis that localizes the failure to a specific structural site with a surgically confined correction on a minimal lever and a bolted-on stabilizer against collapse; the distinctive verbs are diagnose-localize, minimize-on-a-tiny-lever, and stabilize-against-collapse, and frequently the signal is a diagnostic repurposed as an active control rather than a pseudo-label.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism performs exactly this: it diagnoses the failure site (the model has stopped causally relying on its attended evidence at a step) and manufactures the label-free internal readout delta_t = JSD(p_t || p_t^{-E_t}) on the frozen backbone (no retraining = the minimal-lever, representation-preserving move), then bolts on the explicit stabilizer (POS/stopword content-mask + EMA baseline b_t + sustained-step onset rule) against the single-noisy-step collapse mode — the C07 verb 'repurpose a measurement-only diagnostic as an active per-step control signal' is the literal construction.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf reconciles the empirical finding that intrinsic (context-unfaithful) and extrinsic (fact-fabricated) hallucinations require DIFFERENT internal signals into a single per-step decision of which signal governs the current token — the anchor discovers the split but ships two separate detectors, so there is no leaf that, at a given step, decides whether attention-over-evidence or output-distribution dispersion is the load-bearing signal for THAT step's risk (additive; sits at the anchor's residual_problem of leaving the intrinsic/extrinsic signals unreconciled).","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Exploit heterogeneity in a resource's components by discriminating a high-impact minority from a near-redundant bulk via a sensitivity/influence criterion and applying a treatment matched to each, with the load-bearing artifact being an error/sensitivity decomposition that bounds how the differentiated treatment recovers the original objective — that analysis, not the partition idea, is what separates the move from heuristic per-component tuning.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism partitions per-step risk by a discriminating property (evidence-counterfactual sensitivity delta_t vs parametric-dispersion eps_t) and applies a matched read to each partition, and supplies the C04 spine — the error decomposition R_t <= max(intrinsic_risk(delta_t), extrinsic_risk(eps_t)) shown separable on annotated spans — so the differentiated per-step treatment is argued to beat a single pooled read rather than being heuristic per-token tuning; the signature discriminate-then-treat move is present.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries instantiate their cluster's signature move: C07's diagnose-localize → manufacture-internal-readout-on-frozen-backbone → stabilize-against-collapse is literally the delta_t construction with its onset stabilizer, and C04's discriminate-by-sensitivity → matched-treatment → error-decomposition-spine is the (delta_t, eps_t) partition with its R_t bound shown separable on spans."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["self_supervised_signal_engineering","heterogeneous_decomposition"],"matched_pattern_id":"audit_decomp_supervisor","required_mitigation_quoted":"The decomposition criterion must be derivable from observed structure or task-level supervision (not just intuition), AND the manufactured signal must be the *unique* signal the decomposition implies. An ablation that holds the decomposition fixed and varies the signal (or vice versa) must show the two are not conflated.","mitigation_substantively_delivered":"true","reasoning":"The decomposition criterion is derived from observed structure — the value distribution shown on annotated spans (intrinsic spans: delta_t collapse + eps_t low; extrinsic spans: eps_t high + delta_t low), not intuited groups; the manufactured signal (delta_t for intrinsic, eps_t for extrinsic) is the unique signal each partition implies because each partition is DEFINED by its signal's behavior; and the required disentangling ablation is delivered as the negative control (hold the router/decomposition fixed, swap delta_t for raw attention magnitude → predicted onset-localization degradation) plus the positive control (delta_t-only, no router → recovers most intrinsic localization), which holds one axis fixed while varying the other and thus shows the signal and the partition are not conflated."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"openalex:W4416339600","threat_source":"lit_table","subsumption_argument":"The Map of Misbelief (anchor) is the closest threat: it already reads the model's attention over evidence tokens for hallucination detection and already discovers the intrinsic/extrinsic signal split, so a reviewer could argue the candidate is 'their attention signal, computed per step'. The candidate stands or falls on whether per-step CAUSAL counterfactual evidence-dependence (delta_t, a divergence under ablation of the attended set) is genuinely different from their pooled attention-MAGNITUDE aggregation: if attention magnitude and causal reliance were empirically interchangeable, the candidate's negative control (swap delta_t for raw attention magnitude) would show no degradation and the contribution would collapse into theirs. The candidate's whole novelty claim is that they dissociate — confident high-attention steps can be ungrounded — which the anchor never tests because it never ablates the attended set. NOTE on the seed's own source paper 'Hallucination Begins Where Saliency Drops' (ICLR 2026, area foundation/frontier models): that is the exact-mechanism prior for 'saliency-drop predicts onset'; the candidate was deliberately routed AROUND it (delta_t is causal counterfactual divergence, NOT saliency/attention magnitude, and the negative control is precisely the experiment that separates the candidate from that paper's mechanism), so it is an addressable adjacent-mechanism threat, not an exact-mechanism overlap.","addressable_via":"Already addressed by construction: the differentiation lives in core_mechanism's counterfactual-ablation definition of delta_t and the negative control that swaps it for attention magnitude; the residual borderline is in differentiation_from_lit, which Phase 3.3 should sharpen to state the attention-magnitude-vs-causal-reliance dissociation as the explicit delta against openalex:W4416339600 and against the seed's saliency-drop source paper."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"gap_closure_reject_check C04 borderline lesson ('presenting a sensitivity proxy as the novelty invites the verdict that it rediscovers known results unless sharply differentiated') + paper_pointed_threat addressable_via against openalex:W4416339600.","fix_direction":"Sharpen the openalex:W4416339600 delta to state explicitly that the discriminating property is per-step CAUSAL counterfactual evidence-dependence (next-token divergence under ablation of the attended set) and NOT pooled attention magnitude, and add an explicit one-line contrast against the seed's own source paper 'Hallucination Begins Where Saliency Drops' naming that the negative control (delta_t vs raw attention magnitude) is the experiment that dissociates causal reliance from saliency magnitude. Do NOT change core_mechanism, falsification_prediction, or compute_budget."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Sharpened the openalex:W4416339600 delta to state the discriminating property is per-step CAUSAL counterfactual evidence-dependence (next-token divergence under ablation of the attended set), NOT pooled attention magnitude, and added an explicit contrast row against the seed's source paper 'Hallucination Begins Where Saliency Drops' naming the delta_t-vs-attention-magnitude negative control as the experiment that dissociates causal reliance from saliency magnitude."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Per-Step Counterfactual Grounding: Online Hallucination Onset from Evidence Ablation\n\n**Method.** Per-Step Counterfactual Grounding (PCG)\n\n## Motivation\nLarge language models sometimes produce fluent text that is simply not supported by the documents or facts they were given — a hallucination. Today's best ways to catch this read the model's internals (its attention over the input, or the spread of its hidden activations, or how much its answers vary across samples), but they compute ONE number AFTER the whole answer is finished. That tells you the answer is risky, but not WHERE it went wrong, and not in time to do anything about it. A hallucination actually starts at one specific word — the moment the model stops leaning on the evidence it was reading. The recent paper The Map of Misbelief (openalex:W4416339600) even found that two different internal signals are needed for two different error kinds (making up facts vs ignoring the given context), but it ships them as two separate after-the-fact detectors. An obvious idea — 'the model hallucinates wherever its attention to the evidence drops' — is exactly the framing the user's source paper already uses, so we deliberately do something different: instead of measuring how MUCH attention sits on the evidence, we measure how much the next word actually DEPENDS on that evidence, by deleting the attended evidence and seeing how much the model's next-word prediction changes. A word can get lots of attention yet not depend on the evidence at all. When this works, you get a live, per-word grounding signal that points at the first ungrounded word, needs no labels and no retraining, and a single online switch decides — for each word — whether the risk is 'ignoring the context' or 'making up a fact', folding two separate detectors into one.\n\n## Method\n### Background scaffolding\n*Fix the evidence-tracking heads, stream the raw signals, and evaluate against gold spans with controls.*\n\n1. On a small held-out set of 200 examples where the supporting evidence is marked, choose a stable group of attention heads to use as your 'evidence readers'. First fix which prompt tokens count as the evidence context (the supplied passage or reference, not the question). Then, for each attention head, build two parallel sequences over the generated answer: how much of that head's attention lands on the evidence at each word, and whether that word is part of the correct answer. Rank every head by how well those two sequences move together (Spearman rank correlation, a standard agreement-of-ordering measure), and keep the 8 best-aligned heads as a frozen set. Nothing in the model is trained, and the same 8 heads are reused everywhere.\n   - _Why_: You need a stable, pre-chosen set of heads to read 'attention on evidence' consistently, instead of tuning per example.\n2. Add a lightweight wrapper (a forward hook) around the unchanged decoder so that, for every word it generates, you can read off two things without disturbing the generation: the probability distribution over the next word, and — averaged across the 8 chosen heads — how much attention sits on each evidence token. Save these per word; they are the raw ingredients the later steps consume. The model itself is untouched.\n   - _Why_: These are the raw ingredients; nothing about the model is changed.\n3. On datasets where the hallucinated stretches are marked, check three things. First, localization: match each true hallucinated stretch to the nearest flagged start within a 20-word window and report how far off the flag is. Second, detection quality: score each candidate stretch by its highest risk value and compute the area under the ROC curve (AUROC, a threshold-free measure of how well the score separates hallucinated from grounded stretches). Third, routing accuracy: how often the intrinsic-vs-extrinsic label is right. Then run two checks: a negative control that replaces the causal grounding signal with plain attention size (keeping the switch fixed), and a positive control that uses only the grounding signal with no switch — these prove the gain comes from causal evidence-dependence, not attention size or extra machinery. Finally report words-per-second against ordinary decoding and against the 10-sample semantic-entropy method to show it is cheaper.\n   - _Why_: The controls prove the gain comes from causal evidence-dependence, not from attention size or extra capacity, and that it is cheaper than sampling-based methods.\n\n### Per-step causal grounding signal\n*Manufacture $delta_{t}$ — how much the next word depends on the attended evidence — by ablating that evidence and measuring the prediction shift.*\n\n4. At each word, look only at the attention that falls on the evidence (rescale it so the evidence attention sums to one), sort the evidence tokens from most- to least-attended, and take the smallest group from the top that together holds 90% of that evidence attention — this group is the evidence the model is actually leaning on right now $(E_{t}).$ If the model is barely attending to the evidence at all at this word, just take the single most-attended evidence token so the next step always has something well-defined to remove. Pinpointing the leaned-on tokens lets the next step delete reliance specifically, not a random slice of context.\n\n*The attended-evidence set $E_{t}$ is the smallest set of context tokens whose H-averaged attention mass $\\bar{a}_{t}$ reaches a fraction $\\rho $ (=0.9) of the total attention to the evidence context C at step t.*\n$$ E_t = \\arg\\min_{S \\subseteq C}\\; |S| \\;\\; \\text{s.t.}\\; \\frac{\\sum_{c \\in S} \\bar{a}_t(c)}{\\sum_{c \\in C} \\bar{a}_t(c)} \\geq \\rho,\\quad \\bar{a}_t(c) = \\frac{1}{|H|}\\sum_{h \\in H} a_t^{h}(c) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Targeting exactly the leaned-on tokens lets the next step delete reliance rather than a random chunk of context.\n5. Run the same word-step one more time, but with the leaned-on evidence blanked out — block the model's attention to exactly those evidence tokens (at this word only, across all layers and heads), reusing everything else already computed so it costs just one extra forward step. Read the model's new next-word distribution and measure how far it moved from the original one $(\\delta _{t},$ the Jensen-Shannon divergence — a symmetric, bounded distance between two probability distributions — reported in bits). The actually-emitted word is unchanged; this is a read-only probe. If blanking the evidence barely moves the prediction, the model was not really relying on it — the signature of ungrounded generation.\n\n*The per-step counterfactual grounding signal $\\delta _{t}$ is the Jensen-Shannon divergence (in bits) between the real next-token distribution $p_{t}$ and the distribution $p_{t}^{- E_{t}}$ from one extra forward pass with the attended evidence $E_{t}$ masked.*\n$$ \\delta_t = \\mathrm{JSD}\\big(p_t \\,\\|\\, p_t^{-E_t}\\big),\\qquad p_t^{-E_t} = \\mathrm{softmax}\\big(f_\\theta(x_{<t};\\, \\mathrm{mask}(E_t))\\big) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: If blanking the evidence barely changes the prediction, the model was not really using it — a sign of ungrounded generation.\n6. Skip filler words: tag each generated word with a fast part-of-speech tagger and only act on the meaningful ones (nouns, proper nouns, verbs, numbers, adjectives; drop common stopwords). Keep a running average of the grounding signal $\\delta _{t}$ over the last 16 meaningful words (an exponential moving average, which weights recent words more). Until you have seen 16 such words, use a plain running mean and do not raise any alarm. Then flag a hallucination START when $\\delta _{t}$ drops below half of that running average and stays there for at least 2 meaningful words in a row, and report the position of the first of those words. The running baseline plus the 2-word confirmation stops a single noisy word from triggering a false alarm.\n\n*An onset is flagged when $\\delta _{t}$ falls below $\\beta $ (=0.5) times its EMA baseline $b_{t}$ over the last w (=16) content steps, sustained for $s (\\ge 2)$ consecutive content-bearing steps.*\n$$ \\mathrm{onset}_t = \\mathbb{1}\\Big[\\, \\delta_{t'} < \\beta\\, b_{t'} \\;\\; \\forall t' \\in [t-s+1,\\,t]\\,\\Big],\\qquad b_t = \\mathrm{EMA}_w(\\delta) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A running baseline plus a 2-word confirmation stops a single noisy word from triggering a false alarm.\n\n### Intrinsic/extrinsic per-step router\n*Use a second context-ablation signal $eps_{t}$ to decide, per word, whether the risk is ignoring context or fabricating a fact.*\n\n7. Run the word-step once more, this time with the ENTIRE evidence context blanked out (but keep the question, the instruction, and the words generated so far visible), and read what the model predicts purely from its own memory. Measure how spread-out that from-memory guess is in two ways: its distance from a flat, all-words-equally-likely distribution $(\\epsilon _{t}),$ and its plain entropy (how uncertain it is), both in bits. Run this together with the previous probe so the two extra passes batch into one. This separates 'the model is ignoring the given context' from 'the model's own memory is unsure', which is the fabricated-fact regime.\n\n*The parametric-dispersion signal $\\epsilon _{t}$ reads how dispersed the model's parametric-only continuation is when the whole evidence context C is ablated, measured as divergence of $p_{t}^{- C}$ from the uniform distribution U.*\n$$ \\varepsilon_t = \\mathrm{JSD}\\big(p_t^{-C} \\,\\|\\, \\mathcal{U}\\big),\\qquad p_t^{-C} = \\mathrm{softmax}\\big(f_\\theta(x_{<t};\\, \\mathrm{mask}(C))\\big) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This separates 'ignoring the context' from 'the model's own memory is unsure', which is the fabricated-fact regime.\n8. For each word, decide which kind of risk applies using three readings — the grounding signal relative to its baseline $(\\delta _{t}/b_{t}),$ the from-memory dispersion $(\\epsilon _{t}),$ and the from-memory entropy. On the held-out set, label words by whether they fall in a context-ignoring span or a fact-fabrication span, and fit a tiny two-region rule (a depth-2 decision tree, i.e. at most two threshold checks) that separates the two. Then turn each reading into a 0-to-1 risk: an 'ignoring context' risk that climbs as the grounding signal collapses below its baseline, and a 'making up a fact' risk that climbs with from-memory dispersion (scaled by a high-percentile reference from the held-out set); the word's overall risk is the larger of the two, and its type is the region it falls in. One online switch covers both error kinds instead of two separate after-the-fact detectors.\n\n*Per-step risk $R_{t}$ is bounded by the larger of the intrinsic risk (read from $\\delta _{t}'s$ drop below baseline) and the extrinsic risk (read from $\\epsilon _{t}),$ and the router assigns each step a type by which signal is load-bearing.*\n$$ R_t \\leq \\max\\big(\\,r_{\\mathrm{int}}(\\delta_t, b_t),\\; r_{\\mathrm{ext}}(\\varepsilon_t)\\,\\big),\\quad \\mathrm{type}_t = \\begin{cases}\\mathrm{intrinsic} & \\delta_t \\ll b_t,\\ \\varepsilon_t\\ \\text{low}\\\\ \\mathrm{extrinsic} & \\delta_t\\ \\text{low},\\ \\varepsilon_t\\ \\text{high}\\end{cases} \\tag{5} $$\n\n   - _Why_: One online switch covers both error kinds, instead of running two separate after-the-fact detectors.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 逐步反事实接地（Per-Step Counterfactual Grounding）：用证据消融在线定位幻觉起点\n\n**方法名称.** Per-Step Counterfactual Grounding (PCG)\n\n## 研究动机\n大语言模型有时会生成通顺却完全没有依据的文本——也就是幻觉（hallucination）。目前最好的检测方法读取模型内部信号（对输入的注意力、隐藏激活的离散度、或多次采样答案之间的差异），但它们都是在整段答案生成完之后只算出一个数。这个数能告诉你答案不可靠，却说不出错在哪一处，也来不及在生成途中做任何处置。幻觉其实是从某一个具体的词开始的——就在模型不再依赖它所读到的证据的那一刻。最近的 The Map of Misbelief（openalex:W4416339600）甚至发现，两类错误（编造事实 vs 无视给定上下文）需要两种不同的内部信号，但它把它们做成了两个事后检测器。一个最直观的想法——“模型在对证据的注意力下降的地方开始幻觉”——恰好就是用户来源论文已经采用的框架，因此我们刻意换一条路：不去测注意力“有多大”，而是测下一个词究竟有多依赖证据，做法是把被关注的证据消融掉，看模型的下一词预测变化多少（$delta_{t}$）。一个词可能获得很多注意力，却根本不依赖证据。成功之后，你将得到一个实时、逐词的接地信号，直接指向第一个失去依据的词，既不需要标注也不需要重训；同时一个在线开关为每个词判定风险属于“无视上下文”（内在）还是“编造事实”（外在），把两个独立检测器合并为一个。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景脚手架\n*固定证据追踪头、流式读取原始信号，并用对照在标注片段上评测。*\n\n1. 在一个标注了支持证据、规模为 200 例的留出集上，挑出一组稳定的注意力头当作“证据读取器”。先确定 prompt 中哪些 token 算证据上下文（即给定的段落/参考文本，而非问题本身）。再对每个注意力头，沿着生成的答案构造两条并行序列：该头在每个词处落在证据上的注意力占比，以及该词是否属于正确答案。用这两条序列的同向变化程度，即斯皮尔曼秩相关(Spearman rank correlation，一种衡量排序一致性的标准指标)，给所有头排序，保留对齐最好的 8 个头并固定下来。模型不做任何训练，这 8 个头在各处复用不变。\n   - _为什么_: 你需要一组稳定、事先选定的头来一致地读取“对证据的注意力”，而不是逐例去调。\n2. 在不改动的解码器外加一层轻量包装（forward hook），使其每生成一个词都能在不干扰生成的前提下读出两样东西：下一个词的概率分布，以及在所选 8 个头上平均后、落在每个证据 token 上的注意力。逐词保存它们，作为后续步骤要用的原始素材。模型本身不做任何改动。\n   - _为什么_: 这些是原始素材；模型本身不做任何改动。\n3. 在标注了幻觉片段的数据集上检验三件事。其一，定位：把每个真实幻觉片段匹配到 20 词窗口内最近的被标记起点，报告标记偏离多远。其二，检测质量：用每个候选片段的最高风险值打分，计算 ROC 曲线下面积(Area Under the ROC Curve, AUROC，一种无需设阈值、衡量分数区分幻觉与有据片段能力的指标)。其三，路由准确率：内在与外在标签判对的比例。随后跑两个对照：一个负对照，把因果接地信号替换为单纯的注意力大小（开关保持不变）；一个正对照，只用接地信号、不用开关——它们证明增益来自因果证据依赖，而非注意力大小或额外机制。最后报告每秒词数，与普通解码以及 10 次采样的语义熵方法对比，以表明它更省算力。\n   - _为什么_: 对照证明增益来自因果证据依赖，而非注意力大小或额外容量，且比基于采样的方法更省算力。\n\n### 逐步因果接地信号\n*通过消融被关注证据并测量预测变化，制造出 $delta_{t}——$下一个词对被关注证据的依赖程度。*\n\n4. 在每个词处，只看落在证据上的注意力（把它重新归一化，使证据上的注意力之和为 1），将证据 token 从注意力最高到最低排序，从顶部取出累计占 90% 证据注意力的最小一组——这组就是模型此刻真正依赖的证据（$E_{t}$）。若该词处模型对证据几乎没有注意力，就只取注意力最高的那一个证据 token，使下一步总有定义明确的对象可消融。精确锁定被依赖的 token，下一步才能专门删除“依赖”，而非随机的一段上下文。\n\n*被关注证据集 $E_{t}$ 取使得（在固定头集合 H 上平均的）注意力质量 $\\bar{a}_{t}$ 累计达到对证据上下文 C 总注意力之比例 $\\rho $（=0.9）的最小上下文 token 集合。*\n$$ E_t = \\arg\\min_{S \\subseteq C}\\; |S| \\;\\; \\text{s.t.}\\; \\frac{\\sum_{c \\in S} \\bar{a}_t(c)}{\\sum_{c \\in C} \\bar{a}_t(c)} \\geq \\rho,\\quad \\bar{a}_t(c) = \\frac{1}{|H|}\\sum_{h \\in H} a_t^{h}(c) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 精确锁定被依赖的 token，下一步才能消融“依赖”而非随机的一段上下文。\n5. 把同一个词步再跑一遍，但屏蔽掉被依赖的证据——只在这个词处、在所有层和所有头上阻断模型对那些证据 token 的注意力，其余已算好的内容全部复用，因此只多花一次前向。读出模型新的下一词分布，并测量它相对原分布移动了多少（$\\delta _{t}$，即 Jensen-Shannon 散度(Jensen-Shannon divergence，一种对称且有界的概率分布间距离)，以 bit 计）。实际生成的词不变；这是只读探测。若屏蔽证据后预测几乎不动，说明模型其实没在依赖它——这正是无依据生成的标志。\n\n*逐步反事实接地信号 $\\delta _{t}$ 是真实下一 token 分布 $p_{t}$ 与对被关注证据 $E_{t}$ 做掩码后再前向一遍得到的分布 $p_{t}^{- E_{t}}$ 之间的 Jensen-Shannon 散度（单位 bit）。*\n$$ \\delta_t = \\mathrm{JSD}\\big(p_t \\,\\|\\, p_t^{-E_t}\\big),\\qquad p_t^{-E_t} = \\mathrm{softmax}\\big(f_\\theta(x_{<t};\\, \\mathrm{mask}(E_t))\\big) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 若屏蔽证据后预测几乎不变，说明模型其实没在用它——这是无依据生成的信号。\n6. 跳过虚词：用快速词性标注器给每个生成词标注词性，只对实义词（名词、专有名词、动词、数词、形容词；剔除常见停用词）采取行动。对最近 16 个实义词的接地信号 $\\delta _{t}$ 维持一个滑动均值（指数移动平均(exponential moving average)，越近的词权重越大）。在累计满 16 个这样的词之前，改用普通滑动均值，且不触发任何告警。随后，当 $\\delta _{t}$ 跌到该滑动均值的一半以下、并连续至少 2 个实义词保持如此时，标记幻觉“起点”，并报告其中第一个词的位置。滑动基线加上 2 词确认，能避免单个噪声词触发误报。\n\n*当 $\\delta _{t}$ 低于其在最近 w（=16）个实义步上的 EMA 基线 $b_{t}$ 的 $\\beta $（=0.5）倍，且连续 s（$\\ge 2$）个实义步持续如此时，触发幻觉起点标记。*\n$$ \\mathrm{onset}_t = \\mathbb{1}\\Big[\\, \\delta_{t'} < \\beta\\, b_{t'} \\;\\; \\forall t' \\in [t-s+1,\\,t]\\,\\Big],\\qquad b_t = \\mathrm{EMA}_w(\\delta) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 滑动基线加 2 词确认，避免单个噪声词触发误报。\n\n### 内在/外在逐步路由器\n*用第二个上下文消融信号 $eps_{t}$ 为每个词判定风险是无视上下文还是编造事实。*\n\n7. 把该词步再跑一遍，这次屏蔽掉整段证据上下文（但保留问题、指令以及已生成的词），读出模型纯凭自身记忆给出的预测。用两种方式衡量这个“凭记忆”猜测有多离散：它与“所有词等概率”的均匀分布之间的距离（$\\epsilon _{t}$），以及它本身的熵(entropy，即不确定程度)，都以 bit 计。把它和上一步的探测一起跑，使两次额外前向合并为一批。这能把“模型在无视给定上下文”与“模型自身记忆不确定”（即编造事实的情形）区分开。\n\n*参数化离散度信号 $\\epsilon _{t}$ 衡量在消融整个证据上下文 C 后，模型仅凭参数记忆的续写分布 $p_{t}^{- C}$ 相对于均匀分布 U 的离散程度。*\n$$ \\varepsilon_t = \\mathrm{JSD}\\big(p_t^{-C} \\,\\|\\, \\mathcal{U}\\big),\\qquad p_t^{-C} = \\mathrm{softmax}\\big(f_\\theta(x_{<t};\\, \\mathrm{mask}(C))\\big) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这把“无视上下文”与“模型自身记忆不确定”（即编造事实的情形）区分开。\n8. 对每个词，用三项读数判定属于哪类风险——接地信号相对其基线的比值（$\\delta _{t}/b_{t}$）、凭记忆的离散度（$\\epsilon _{t}$）、以及凭记忆的熵。在留出集上，按词落在“无视上下文”片段还是“编造事实”片段给它打标签，并拟合一个极小的两区规则（深度为 2 的决策树，即至多两次阈值判断）来区分二者。再把每项读数转成 0 到 1 的风险：一种“无视上下文”风险，随接地信号跌破基线而升高；一种“编造事实”风险，随凭记忆的离散度而升高（用留出集上的高分位参考值做缩放）；该词的总体风险取二者中较大者，类型即它所落入的区域。一个在线开关覆盖两类错误，而非两个独立的事后检测器。\n\n*逐步风险 $R_{t}$ 由内在风险（读自 $\\delta _{t}$ 相对基线的下跌）与外在风险（读自 $\\epsilon _{t}$）中较大者上界，路由器据哪一信号起主导作用为每一步指派类型。*\n$$ R_t \\leq \\max\\big(\\,r_{\\mathrm{int}}(\\delta_t, b_t),\\; r_{\\mathrm{ext}}(\\varepsilon_t)\\,\\big),\\quad \\mathrm{type}_t = \\begin{cases}\\mathrm{intrinsic} & \\delta_t \\ll b_t,\\ \\varepsilon_t\\ \\text{low}\\\\ \\mathrm{extrinsic} & \\delta_t\\ \\text{low},\\ \\varepsilon_t\\ \\text{high}\\end{cases} \\tag{5} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 一个在线开关覆盖两类错误，而非运行两个独立的事后检测器。\n\n"},{"id":"56","run_dir":"run_prompt56_grobner","index":56,"title":"Certificate-Decoupled Neural S-Pair Selection for Exact Gröbner Basis Computation","title_zh":"证书解耦的神经 S-pair 选择用于精确 Gröbner 基计算","method_name":"Certificate-Decoupled Neural S-Pair Selection (CD-NSPS)","hook":"We show a learned policy that chooses Buchberger's next S-pair from the live computation state cuts measured S-pair reductions and intermediate-coefficient blow-up well below the best hand-designed selection strategy, while the returned basis stays byte-identical to the symbolic solver's certified output — the policy can be arbitrarily wrong about WHICH pair to take next yet never wrong about WHAT is computed. The non-obvious claim is that a single policy trained on small random ideals transfers its inner-loop savings to a structurally different family (dense generic to sparse/structured) without retraining.","anchor_pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","anchor_pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","domain_category":"Learning Theory & Statistics","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf turns the correctness-neutral inner choices of a Gröbner-basis computation (which pending S-pair to process next, in what reduction order) into a learned SEQUENTIAL decision made against the evolving algorithm state — every learned system either fixes the choice once per instance or discards the algorithm; the outcome that is missing is a learning system that reduces measured inner-loop work (S-pair count / intermediate-polynomial blow-up) of an actual basis computation, not ju","pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","sub_pattern":"C25 (Decompose and Delegate to Solvers)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by making the learned model emit, at each Buchberger step, a typed machine-checkable artifact — the index of the next pending pair plus a partial reduction-order hint — that the sound symbolic reduction engine consumes and returns verifiable feedback on (the reduced S-polynomial and whether it is a new basis element), so the learned decision is an in-loop sequential policy over the live pair-queue/basis state whose effect is measured as reduced S-pair reductions, not a one-shot label.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides a way for a learned guide to be WRONG about a correctness-neutral choice without compromising the exactness of the returned basis — i.e. there is no separation between a (possibly imperfect, learned) search-steering signal and an (always-exact) certified result, so the field is forced to choose between un-guided exact solvers and un-certified learned emulators.","pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","sub_pattern":"C25 (Decompose and Delegate to Solvers)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by the same C25 boundary: because the only thing the policy controls is the ORDER in which the sound solver processes pairs (a correctness-neutral degree of freedom of Buchberger's algorithm), and the solver still forms, fully reduces, and certifies every selected S-polynomial and terminates only on the standard all-pairs-reduce-to-zero condition, a wrong policy choice costs at most extra reductions and never changes the certified output — the steering signal is structurally decoupled from the exactness certificate.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"machine learning for symbolic computation / computer algebra (Gröbner basis computation over polynomial ideals)","n_papers":38,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":23},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"openreview","n":2}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":15,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Lessons on Datasets and Paradigms in Machine Learning for Symbolic Computation: A Case Study on CAD"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"CAN SYMBOLIC COMPUTATION AND FORMALIST SYSTEMS ENHANCE MATH EDUCATION WITH ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE?"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Constrained Neural Networks for Interpretable Heuristic Creation to Optimise Computer Algebra Systems"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Convexity Certificates for Symbolic Tensor Expressions"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Symbolic Integration Algorithm Selection with Machine Learning: LSTMs vs Tree LSTMs"},{"source":"openalex","title":"TorchSISSO: A PyTorch-based implementation of the sure independence screening and sparsifying operator for efficient and interpretable model discovery"}],"more":9},{"year":2025,"n":21,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Neuro-Symbolic Learning for Galois Groups: Unveiling Probabilistic Trends in Polynomials"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Computation of M-QDR decomposition of tensors and applications"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A Neurosymbolic Framework for Geometric Reduction of Binary Forms"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Operator-Based Machine Intelligence: A Hilbert Space Framework for Spectral Learning and Symbolic Reasoning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Hybrid Molecular Nano Frameworks for Disease Modeling Using Neuro Symbolic Machine Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Angular coefficients from interpretable machine learning with symbolic regression"}],"more":15},{"year":2026,"n":2,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"},{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"}],"more":0}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":8,"share":0.211},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":5,"share":0.132},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":4,"share":0.105},{"pattern_id":"relax_discrete_search_to_continuous","pattern_name":"Relax Discrete Search to Continuous","count":3,"share":0.079},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":3,"share":0.079},{"pattern_id":"algebraic_equivalence_unification","pattern_name":"Prove Equivalence to Unify","count":3,"share":0.079},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":3,"share":0.079},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":1,"share":0.026}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"The dominant cost of computing a Gröbner basis lives in Buchberger-style algorithms' inner loop, where at each step the algorithm may legally process ANY S-pair from the pending list and intermediate reductions may follow many correctness-neutral orderings — choices that do not change the output but can swing runtime and intermediate-polynomial blow-up by orders of magnitude (semanticscholar:9d12b14d82f1bb1b3e2a199d03e44156bb634aee explicitly frames this S-pair choice as the open lever, and the hand-optimized symbolic work of openalex:W4400650072 shows that structural choices, not the algorithm skeleton, decide tractability). The recent learning frontier does not reach into this inner loop: per-instance ML selectors (semanticscholar:ae6550bac3e02fe498446253f16aa5b685d77988, semanticscholar:64024c576d9efd8247c1f845276d8bce2ea10789) only pick a top-level algorithm or variable ordering once and then hand control back to a fixed symbolic procedure, while end-to-end Transformer emulators (openalex:W4417256934) replace the procedure entirely and therefore surrender the exactness certificate that makes a Gröbner basis useful. So once an ideal is large enough that the pending-pair list and the intermediate-coefficient growth explode, no current learning system can both steer the step-by-step search AND return a basis that is provably the Gröbner basis — the correctness-neutral degrees of freedom that decide tractability are left either un-guided or un-certified.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:9d12b14d82f1bb1b3e2a199d03e44156bb634aee","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Surveys ML-for-symbolic-computation paradigms and explicitly names the S-pair selection in Buchberger's algorithm as a correctness-neutral choice that ML could make per problem, but treats every such choice as a one-shot per-instance CLASSIFICATION / SELECTION problem (predict the best fixed option, then run the unchanged solver). Its residue is that it never closes the loop as a sequential decision INSIDE the running algorithm — there is no learned policy that observes the evolving pending-pair list and intermediate basis and chooses the next reduction step, and no guarantee/certificate layer that lets such a policy be wrong without breaking correctness. [residue confirmed from fulltext method section]"},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4417256934","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"CALT trains a Transformer end-to-end to map before/after symbolic expressions, demonstrating that symbolic computations are learnable as sequence-to-sequence functions. It does NOT preserve any exactness certificate (the output is a generated string with no guarantee it is the true Gröbner basis) and gives no access to or control of the internal search decisions, so it cannot be trusted for the verification/cryptography use cases where Gröbner bases matter most."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:ae6550bac3e02fe498446253f16aa5b685d77988","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Encodes a known human heuristic for CAD variable ordering as a constrained neural network and optimizes it, keeping interpretability. The learned object is still a one-shot ordering chosen BEFORE the symbolic procedure runs (a single global decision), not a step-level policy that reacts to the evolving state of an inner search loop, and it is specific to CAD rather than the S-pair queue of basis computation."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4400650072","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Hand-derives structural optimizations of Gröbner-basis algorithms for maximal determinantal ideals and critical-point computation, showing large speedups come from exploiting ideal structure rather than from the generic algorithm. The structure exploitation is manual and family-specific (determinantal ideals); there is no learned mechanism that discovers and exploits such structure automatically across ideal families."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"machine learning for symbolic computation / computer algebra (Gröbner basis computation over polynomial ideals)","venue":"ICLR / NeurIPS / ICML (ML for science & symbolic reasoning track)","time":"2026","data":["synthetically generated polynomial ideals with controllable structure (random dense, structured/sparse, cryptographic/determinantal families)","traces of Buchberger / F4 / F5 runs (selection decisions, degree-of-regularity progression, basis growth) usable as supervision","standard CAS benchmark ideal suites (e.g. from Maple/Magma/Macaulay2 test sets)"],"compute":"1×A100 × 3 months (≈ 90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with access to a computer algebra system; comfortable with RL / sequence models and basic commutative algebra","preference":"both","baseline":"classical Buchberger / F4 with standard normal-selection (lowest-LCM-degree) S-pair strategy and a fixed monomial order; plus learned-selection heuristics (CAD-style per-instance selectors) and end-to-end Transformer emulation (CALT)","limitation":"learning systems for Gröbner-basis computation today either only SELECT an algorithm/parameter per instance or EMULATE the answer end-to-end with no exactness guarantee; none guide the inner correctness-neutral search (S-pair / reduction ordering) while still returning a certified basis","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The central object of this sequential_pipeline is the live computation state S_t of a running Buchberger/F4 computation: S_t = (P_t, G_t) where P_t is the current set of pending critical pairs (each pair (i,j) with its LCM monomial and sugar degree) and G_t is the current partial basis (each generator carrying its leading monomial, its support size = number of nonzero terms, and its total degree). All of S_t is read directly from the symbolic engine's data structures — model-internal-to-the-solver readouts, not learned estimates. At each step the learned policy pi_theta reads a featurization phi(S_t) and emits a typed artifact a_t = (pair_index, order_hint): pair_index in {1..|P_t|} selects which pending pair the solver processes next, and order_hint is an optional permutation seed over the reduction queue (defaulting to the solver's standard order when omitted). phi(S_t) is computed as follows: each pending pair (i,j) is embedded as a fixed-length vector [deg(LCM), sugar, |support(g_i)|, |support(g_j)|, monomial-overlap(g_i,g_j), is-coprime-LCM(i,j) (Buchberger criterion 1 flag), chain-criterion-eligible flag], and the basis G_t is summarized by [|G_t|, max support, max total degree, sum of supports]; pairs are processed by a permutation-invariant set encoder (a small DeepSets/attention head, 2 layers, width 128 — these are the only learned weights) producing a score per pair, and pair_index = argmax (greedy) or a sampled index during training. The artifact a_t is routed to the SOUND solver: the solver forms the S-polynomial of the chosen pair, fully reduces it modulo G_t with exact arithmetic, and returns the verifiable feedback r_t = (was_zero, new_generator_or_none, |support of the reduction matrix used|). This feedback closes the loop mid-construction: it both updates S_{t+1} (the solver appends any new generator and regenerates pairs via Gebauer-Moller exactly as in the unguided algorithm) and supplies the reinforcement signal for credit assignment. Because pi_theta only ever permutes the order of solver-executed, fully-certified operations, gap 2 is closed by construction: termination is the unchanged all-pairs-reduce-to-zero test, so the returned G is provably THE reduced Gröbner basis regardless of pi_theta's choices, and being wrong only inflates the step count. Gap 1 is closed because the measured cost — total nonzero S-polynomial reductions and the maximum intermediate generator support over the run — is exactly the quantity pi_theta is trained to minimize, on actual computations rather than a held-out classification label. The two gaps share one module (the C25 boundary), not two: the certificate-decoupling (gap 2) is a structural property of the same pair-ordering artifact that delivers the inner-loop savings (gap 1).","core_mechanism_reasoning":"Both gaps are closed by ONE module because they are two faces of the same design choice: confining the learned model to the correctness-neutral pair-ordering artifact is simultaneously what yields measurable inner-loop savings (gap 1) and what guarantees exactness under arbitrary policy error (gap 2) — splitting them into two modules would be artificial. I considered (alternative A) a continuous relaxation of the whole pair-selection problem (the relax_discrete_search_to_continuous anchor_alternate) but rejected it because S-pair selection is intrinsically sequential and state-dependent (each choice reshapes P_{t+1}), so a one-shot amortized prediction discards exactly the live-state adaptivity the gap demands; and (alternative B) rewarding raw step-count with hand-features and a generic RL loop, which I rejected explicitly because method_lineage flags node n3 (Peifer-Han-Stillman-style RL S-pair selection with step-count reward over hand-features) as an OCCUPIED node — to avoid regression the design draws on the source the tree does NOT occupy, namely the typed machine-checkable solver-closed artifact of C25 with the certificate decoupling and the intermediate-support reward shaping, not a bare reward-on-steps loop. Avoided node recorded: n3.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on a fixed exact backend over a finite field with a fixed monomial order, compute Gröbner bases for a held-out suite of ideals (random dense systems plus one structurally distinct sparse/structured family) under three selectors — default normal/sugar, a strong hand-heuristic, and the trained policy pi_theta — verifying all three return the identical reduced basis, and measure the total number of nonzero S-polynomial reductions and the maximum intermediate-generator support per run. If the candidate works, the median nonzero-reduction count and the median max-intermediate-support under pi_theta DECREASE relative to both baselines, and the decrease PERSISTS on the structurally distinct family the policy was never trained on. The named load-bearing variable is the policy's per-pair selection score margin m_t = (top score - second score) at each step — the quantity that carries the claim that the policy is exploiting live-state structure rather than a fixed priority. Negative control: replace pi_theta's scores with uniform-random pair selection (destroying m_t's information while keeping every other component, including the exact solver and certificate, identical); the prediction is that the DOWNSTREAM OUTCOME METRIC — the nonzero-reduction count — rises back to (or above) the unguided baseline, confirming the savings are produced by the learned selection signal and not by any change to the solver. Positive control: a stripped-down selector that ranks pairs by ONLY the single feature most correlated with m_t (e.g. predicted reduction support) should recover most of the reduction-count savings, converting the falsifier into a constructive identification of which state feature drives the gain.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:9d12b14d82f1bb1b3e2a199d03e44156bb634aee","delta":"They frame every correctness-neutral CAS choice (including Buchberger S-pair selection) as a one-shot per-instance classification made before the unchanged solver runs and predict a single best fixed option; we construct an in-loop sequential policy over the evolving pair-queue/basis state and measure realized inner-loop reduction work on actual computations, a quantity their label-prediction setup never produces."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4417256934","delta":"CALT learns the input->output symbolic map end-to-end as a Transformer with no exactness certificate; we keep the sound solver in the loop and learn only the correctness-neutral processing order, so our returned basis is provably certified while CALT's generated string is not."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:ae6550bac3e02fe498446253f16aa5b685d77988","delta":"They encode a single global pre-solve CAD variable-ordering heuristic as a constrained NN (one decision per instance); we make the learned object a step-level policy that reacts to the live S_t inside basis computation and is decoupled from the certificate, neither of which their one-shot ordering provides."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4400650072","delta":"They obtain speedups by HAND-deriving structural optimizations for one ideal family (maximal determinantal ideals); we obtain inner-loop savings from a learned policy that transfers across families without per-family hand derivation, and we measure that transfer explicitly."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:9d12b14d82f1bb1b3e2a199d03e44156bb634aee","what_step_was_missed":"This survey explicitly names S-pair selection in Buchberger's algorithm as a correctness-neutral choice ML could make, but treats it (like every other CAS choice it discusses) as a per-instance prediction made OUTSIDE the solver loop; for our contribution to already exist it would have needed to construct the in-loop sequential-decision interface — a typed machine-checkable next-pair artifact consumed by the sound reduction engine that returns verifiable feedback used for mid-construction credit assignment, with the intermediate-support reward shaping that targets coefficient blow-up rather than step count — which its one-shot classification framing never builds."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":209,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"No hard floor fires: gap_closure_reject_check never reaches a 'yes' candidate_match (worst is the borderline 'neighboring routing move' lesson), recipe_application_check.verdict = applied on both entries, and anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id = null. The decisive finding is paper_pointed_threat: openalex:W7127739695 is a real, recently-retrieved competitor whose subsumption_argument shows it is NOT exact-mechanism overlap (monomial-order vs S-pair-order DOF) but DOES require an explicit differentiation the candidate currently lacks — addressable_via names a specific candidate field (differentiation_from_lit), so per the 'paper_pointed_threat exists AND addressable_via names a specific field' heuristic the verdict is revise, not advance.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf turns the correctness-neutral inner choices of a Gröbner-basis computation (which pending S-pair to process next, in what reduction order) into a learned SEQUENTIAL decision made against the evolving algorithm state — every learned system either fixes the choice once per instance or discards the algorithm; the outcome that is missing is a learning system that reduces measured inner-loop work (S-pair count / intermediate-polynomial blow-up) of an actual basis computation, not just predicts a label.","main_pattern":"decompose_and_delegate","sub_pattern":"C25 (Decompose and Delegate to Solvers)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is assembling a decompose-and-delegate pipeline whose components are all off-the-shelf so that no single piece is shown to be both novel and load-bearing, with the intermediate artifact staying advisory (read by the next stage but never closed by a verification signal), reducing the system to sampling-plus-filtering; most damaging, authors skip the ablation that isolates the decomposition's marginal contribution from confounds.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A decomposition that merely chains off-the-shelf agents or engines, with no single component demonstrated to be both novel and load-bearing, reads as engineering assembly rather than a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The load-bearing component is the certificate-decoupled in-loop pair-ordering policy (a novel interface, not an off-the-shelf agent), and core_mechanism_steps 5/10 + falsification_prediction explicitly show its removal (random-selection control) collapses savings to baseline."},{"lesson_quoted":"If the 'key' prompt or elicitation scheme is tuned to one benchmark and not validated across settings, reviewers treat it as a dataset-specific hack instead of a transferable mechanism.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate's central transfer claim and step 9 evaluate the policy on a structurally distinct held-out ideal family without retraining, which is the opposite of single-benchmark tuning."},{"lesson_quoted":"Delegating a sub-problem to a sound but costly solver (NP-hard search, materialized intermediate state) sinks the contribution when latency and scalability are left unexamined.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The delegated solver IS the standard exact reduction engine whose cost the candidate measures directly (wall-clock + nonzero reductions in step 8), and the policy is lightweight; solver cost is reported, not hidden."},{"lesson_quoted":"Without an ablation isolating the decomposition's marginal effect from extra data, more epochs, or the base model's prior knowledge, the reported gains read as confounded and unattributable.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The negative control (random pair scores, all else identical including the exact solver) cleanly isolates the policy's marginal effect, since the solver and certificate are byte-identical across conditions."},{"lesson_quoted":"Re-deriving a routing move that a closely neighboring published system already demonstrated, while showing only marginal gains, fails the novelty bar regardless of engineering polish.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"A concurrent paper learns monomial ORDER selection for Gröbner computation by RL; it is a neighboring routing move, so the candidate must make explicit that S-pair-order (output-preserving inner-loop) is a different correctness-neutral DOF than monomial-order (output-changing pre-solve) — handled in paper_pointed_threat below, not a Reject trigger here."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides a way for a learned guide to be WRONG about a correctness-neutral choice without compromising the exactness of the returned basis — i.e. there is no separation between a (possibly imperfect, learned) search-steering signal and an (always-exact) certified result, so the field is forced to choose between un-guided exact solvers and un-certified learned emulators.","main_pattern":"decompose_and_delegate","sub_pattern":"C25 (Decompose and Delegate to Solvers)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is an intermediate artifact that stays advisory rather than closed by a verification signal, reducing the system to sampling-plus-filtering, and omitting the ablation that isolates the structure's marginal contribution.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A self-improvement or decomposition loop whose reliability hinges on an unvalidated data-generation, retrieval, or filtering component invites rejection when error propagation across iterations is never analyzed.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"There is no unvalidated filtering component in the correctness path — the solver's exact reduction is the only thing that determines the output, so no error can propagate to correctness regardless of policy reliability."},{"lesson_quoted":"A decomposition that merely chains off-the-shelf agents or engines, with no single component demonstrated to be both novel and load-bearing, reads as engineering assembly rather than a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The certificate-decoupling property (policy controls only a correctness-neutral DOF) is itself the novel structural claim, demonstrated by the all-pairs-reduce-to-zero guard in step 7 returning the identical basis across all selectors."}],"verdict":"clear"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The only non-clear signal is on the anchor gap (decompose_and_delegate), where the 'neighboring routing move' Reject lesson is borderline because a concurrent monomial-order-learning paper exists; this is a differentiation-sharpening concern routed through paper_pointed_threat, not a documented Reject match (candidate_match stays 'no'/'borderline', never 'yes'), so no hard floor fires."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf turns the correctness-neutral inner choices of a Gröbner-basis computation (which pending S-pair to process next, in what reduction order) into a learned SEQUENTIAL decision made against the evolving algorithm state — every learned system either fixes the choice once per instance or discards the algorithm; the outcome that is missing is a learning system that reduces measured inner-loop work (S-pair count / intermediate-polynomial blow-up) of an actual basis computation, not just predicts a label.","sub_pattern":"C25 (Decompose and Delegate to Solvers)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Have the learned model emit a structured, machine-checkable intermediate artifact at the decomposition boundary in place of a final answer, then route that artifact to a sound solver and close the loop with the solver's verifiable output, using that signal for credit assignment or in-place correction DURING construction rather than only post-hoc.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism emits the typed artifact a_t = (pair_index, order_hint) at each Buchberger step (the decomposition boundary), routes it to the sound exact reduction engine which returns verifiable feedback r_t = (was_zero, new_generator, reduction support), and core_mechanism_steps 5 uses that feedback mid-construction for policy-gradient credit assignment — the cluster's distinctive solver-closed-loop move, not a generic split.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides a way for a learned guide to be WRONG about a correctness-neutral choice without compromising the exactness of the returned basis — i.e. there is no separation between a (possibly imperfect, learned) search-steering signal and an (always-exact) certified result, so the field is forced to choose between un-guided exact solvers and un-certified learned emulators.","sub_pattern":"C25 (Decompose and Delegate to Solvers)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"The load-bearing move is closing the loop with the solver's verifiable output and confining the learned component to extraction/enrichment/planning/interfacing while structured or symbolic resolution is offloaded to the component that handles it exactly.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism confines the learned policy strictly to the correctness-neutral pair-ordering interface while ALL exact resolution (S-polynomial formation, full reduction, Gebauer-Moller pair regeneration, certification) stays in the sound solver — the C25 'offload exact resolution, learn only the interface' move, here sharpened into the certificate-decoupling guarantee.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries perform C25's signature solver-closed-loop move with the learned component confined to interfacing; the distinctive machine-checkable-artifact-routed-to-sound-solver-with-mid-construction-credit-assignment tactic is present in core_mechanism, not just the parent's generic decompose gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["decompose_and_delegate"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"The composition set is a single pattern (decompose_and_delegate on both gaps); none of the three documented reject-favored 2-way compositions (all of which require heterogeneous_decomposition as a component) matches, so no anti-pattern fires."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"openalex:W7127739695","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"'Learning Fast Monomial Orders for Gröbner Basis Computations' (2026-02) casts the selection of the MONOMIAL ORDERING as a reinforcement-learning problem over admissible orders with a cost-reflecting reward and reports learned policies that beat static heuristics like GrevLex. It is the closest competitor because it also uses RL to reduce Gröbner-computation cost, so a reviewer will ask how the candidate differs. The candidate's claim stands rather than falls because the two attack DIFFERENT degrees of freedom: monomial order is a one-shot pre-solve global choice that CHANGES the output basis (each admissible order yields a different reduced Gröbner basis), whereas the candidate's S-pair processing order is an in-loop, correctness-neutral degree of freedom that leaves the output basis invariant — which is exactly what makes the candidate's certificate-decoupling claim (gap 2) possible and is something the monomial-order work cannot offer, since changing the order changes the certified object itself. The candidate must, however, make this distinction explicit and cite this paper, or the contribution will be misread as a re-derivation of an existing RL-for-Gröbner routing move.","addressable_via":"Sharpen differentiation_from_lit to add an explicit entry contrasting the candidate's output-preserving in-loop S-pair-order DOF against this paper's output-changing pre-solve monomial-order DOF, and note the two are composable rather than competing."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat — concurrent paper openalex:W7127739695 ('Learning Fast Monomial Orders for Gröbner Basis Computations') learns monomial-order selection by RL and would be read as the closest prior art if not explicitly distinguished.","fix_direction":"Append one differentiation_from_lit entry with paper_id 'openalex:W7127739695' and a delta stating: they cast the one-shot pre-solve MONOMIAL ORDER (which changes the output basis) as an RL problem; we learn the in-loop, output-PRESERVING S-pair processing ORDER, a different correctness-neutral degree of freedom that leaves the certified basis invariant and is what makes our certificate-decoupling guarantee possible — and note the two mechanisms are composable, not competing. Do NOT modify falsification_prediction or compute_budget (kill-switch fields)."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Appended one differentiation_from_lit entry against openalex:W7127739695 distinguishing the candidate's output-preserving in-loop S-pair-order DOF from that paper's output-changing pre-solve monomial-order DOF, noting the two are composable; no other field touched and kill-switch fields left byte-identical."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Certificate-Decoupled Neural S-Pair Selection for Exact Gröbner Basis Computation\n\n**Method.** Certificate-Decoupled Neural S-Pair Selection (CD-NSPS)\n\n## Motivation\n$A Gröbner$ basis is a standardized rewrite of a system of polynomial equations that makes hard questions (does a solution exist? is this polynomial in the ideal?) easy to answer; it is the engine behind a lot of cryptography, robotics, and computer algebra. The catch is that computing one is expensive, and almost all of the cost is hidden in a single inner loop of Buchberger's algorithm. At each step the algorithm has a to-do list of pending 'S-pairs' and is free to pick ANY of them next. Which one it picks does not change the final answer at all — but it can change how long the computation takes, and how badly the intermediate expressions swell, by huge factors.\n\nRecent machine-learning work has come at this from two sides and missed the middle. One line (the CAD survey, semanticscholar:9d12b14d...) lets a model pick ONE setting before the solver runs, then hands control back to the unchanged solver — it never reacts to how the computation is actually unfolding. The other line (CALT, a Computer-Algebra-with-Transformer library) throws the solver away and trains a Transformer to guess the whole answer end-to-end — fast, but with no proof the guess is correct, which is useless for the security and verification jobs where $Gröbner$ bases matter most. A third line speeds things up by hand-tuning the math for one specific family of problems, with no way to carry that over to other families.\n\nWhy now: exact computer-algebra systems (Macaulay2, OSCAR, msolve) now let you reach inside the loop and feed in the next-pair choice from outside, and a very recent reinforcement-learning paper (openalex:W7127739695, 2026) showed RL can cut $Gröbner$ cost — but only by changing the 'monomial order,' which actually changes the answer object. The one lever nobody has learned is the in-loop S-pair order, which leaves the answer untouched. That is exactly the lever we take.\n\nIf we close this gap, you get the missing middle option: a learned guide that genuinely speeds up the inner loop on real computations, while the thing it returns is still a PROVABLY correct $Gröbner$ basis — so the speedup is finally usable in the security and verification settings, the hand-tuning becomes a single transferable policy, and it stacks cleanly on top of the monomial-order trick because the two never fight over the same choice.\n\n## Method\n### Solver-in-the-loop environment\n*Expose the sound Buchberger/F4 driver as a step-wise environment whose only externally controllable choice is which pending pair to process next.*\n\n1. Wrap an exact computer algebra system (Macaulay2, OSCAR, or msolve) so that its core basis-building loop, at every step, hands out its current to-do list of pending pairs (each with its least-common-multiple monomial, sugar degree, and which two generators it came from) and its current partial basis (each generator's leading monomial, number of nonzero terms, and total degree), then pauses and waits for an outside caller to say which pair to do next. Package this as a function $env.step(pair_{index}, order_{hint})$ that performs exactly ONE exact symbolic combine-and-simplify of the chosen pair and reports back three things: whether it simplified to zero, any new basis element produced, and how large the simplification was (count of nonzero entries touched). Do not edit any of the system's correctness logic.\n   - _Why_: To guide the computation as it unfolds you must be able to read the live state and feed in the next move — without ever taking over the exact arithmetic.\n2. Turn the live computation state into numbers the model can read. For each pending pair compute seven features: its least-common-multiple degree, its sugar degree, the number of nonzero terms in each of its two generators, how many monomials the two generators share, a flag for whether their leading terms are coprime (Buchberger's first criterion), and a flag for whether it is eligible for the chain criterion. For the whole basis compute four summary numbers: how many generators it has, the largest term-count, the largest degree, and the total term-count. Read every value straight from the solver — do not estimate anything — and rebuild this each step because the to-do list and basis keep changing.\n\n*The featurization of live state $S_{t}: a$ per-pending-pair vector (lcm degree, sugar $s_{ij},$ supports $|g_{i}|,|g_{j}|,$ monomial overlap $o_{ij},$ coprime-lcm flag $c_{ij},$ chain-criterion flag $h_{ij})$ plus a global basis summary over $G_{t}.$*\n$$ \\phi(S_t) = \\big( \\{ [\\deg(\\mathrm{lcm}_{ij}),\\, s_{ij},\\, |g_i|,\\, |g_j|,\\, o_{ij},\\, c_{ij},\\, h_{ij}] \\}_{(i,j)\\in P_t},\\; [\\,|G_t|,\\, \\max_g |g|,\\, \\max_g \\deg g,\\, \\textstyle\\sum_g |g|\\,] \\big) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The model can only react to the evolving computation if that computation is described to it in features it can compare across a variable-length to-do list.\n3. After each move, add any new basis element the solver produced and let the solver rebuild its pending-pair list using its own unchanged standard machinery (the $Gebauer-Möller$ procedure, which also prunes provably redundant new pairs), giving the next state. The policy never touches pair regeneration, simplification, or pruning — those run exactly as they would without any learning.\n   - _Why_: Leaving pair-regeneration and reduction entirely to the trusted solver is what guarantees the policy can never corrupt the result.\n\n### Certificate-decoupled selection policy\n*A tiny set-encoder policy that emits a typed next-pair artifact and is trained to cut reductions and intermediate blow-up while controlling only a correctness-neutral degree of freedom.*\n\n4. Build the policy as a tiny 2-layer set encoder (a permutation-invariant network — DeepSets or one self-attention block — of width 128, the only trained weights anywhere) that reads the per-pair features, attaches the basis summary to each pair, and outputs a score for every pending pair; convert scores to a probability over pairs and emit the typed choice (which pair, plus an optional reduction-order hint), taking the top-scoring pair at test time and a sampled one during training. Make the reduction-order hint just an index into a short fixed list of valid reduction orderings the solver already supports (default, ascending leading-monomial, ascending term-count), so it can never affect correctness. 【author decision: exactly which valid reduction orderings go in that short list and how long it is — the axis of choice is which admissible orders to expose.】\n\n*The policy is a permutation-invariant set encoder $f_\\theta $ over per-pair features whose softmax gives a categorical distribution over pending pairs; the emitted typed artifact $a_{t}$ names the next pair (argmax at test time, sampled in training) and an optional reduction-order hint.*\n$$ \\pi_\\theta(\\cdot \\mid S_t) = \\mathrm{softmax}\\big( f_\\theta(\\phi(S_t)) \\big), \\qquad a_t = (\\,\\mathrm{pair\\_index},\\, \\mathrm{order\\_hint}\\,),\\quad \\mathrm{pair\\_index} = \\arg\\max_{(i,j)\\in P_t} f_\\theta(\\phi(S_t))_{ij} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A permutation-invariant scorer handles a to-do list of any length, and confining the model to JUST naming a pair is what keeps it from ever touching correctness.\n5. Generate a training curriculum of ideals from a parametric generator, keeping the finite field and the monomial order FIXED the whole time. Use 3-8 variables, between n and 2n generators each, random polynomials of total degree 2-5, with a sparsity setting of full for the dense family, about one-fifth retained for the sparse/structured family, and exactly two terms for the binomial family; order them easy-to-hard. Each ideal becomes episodes through the step 1 (Wrap an exact computer $algebra\\dots )$ environment. Fixing the field and monomial order matters because it makes the ONLY thing that varies across episodes the order in which pairs are processed — which is exactly the lever we want and never the answer-changing choice of monomial order. 【author decision: the exact generation ranges and ordering schedule — the axis of choice is the difficulty mix the policy trains on, which determines what it can transfer to.】\n   - _Why_: Fixing the field and monomial order means the ONLY thing varying is the S-pair order, so the policy learns exactly the lever we want and nothing that would change the answer.\n6. Train the policy with REINFORCE (a standard policy-gradient method) using a moving-average baseline to reduce noise. Score each finished episode as minus the number of nonzero simplifications, minus a weight times the largest intermediate expression size seen during the run, so the policy is pushed to avoid both long computations and expression blow-up. Pick the weight by first measuring, on a pilot batch, the typical reduction count and the typical largest-expression size, setting the weight so the two penalties are on the same scale, then trying a few multiples and keeping whichever gives the fewest reductions on held-out problems. 【author decision: how that weight is set / how hard to penalize expression blow-up versus raw step count — the axis of choice is the trade-off between the two cost terms.】 Each pair the policy picks reshapes the rest of the computation, so the measured cost at the end reflects the policy's choices; gradients touch only the policy, never the solver.\n\n*The episode return penalizes total nonzero reductions plus $\\lambda $ times the max intermediate-generator support, and the policy is trained by REINFORCE with a moving-average baseline b so it learns to avoid coefficient/support blow-up, not only step count.*\n$$ R(\\tau) = -\\sum_{t} \\mathbb{1}[\\,\\mathrm{was\\_zero}_t = \\mathrm{False}\\,] \\;-\\; \\lambda \\,\\max_{t} \\mathrm{supp}_t, \\qquad \\nabla_\\theta J = \\mathbb{E}_{\\tau\\sim\\pi_\\theta}\\!\\big[(R(\\tau)-b)\\,\\textstyle\\sum_t \\nabla_\\theta \\log \\pi_\\theta(a_t\\mid S_t)\\big] \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Rewarding fewer reductions AND smaller intermediate blow-up — not just fewer steps — is what pushes past the older step-count-only RL attempt and targets the real cost.\n\n### Certification and evaluation\n*Certify the returned basis via the unchanged termination test and measure inner-loop savings, output identity, transfer, and controls.*\n\n7. Stop when the pending list is empty (every pair done or eliminated), and take the basis the solver returns. Then run the standard correctness check as a guard: verify that every pair's combine-and-simplify reduces to zero against the basis — the textbook test for being a true basis. Because this check does not depend on the order pairs were processed, the answer is provably correct no matter what the policy chose; run it on every result so any bug is caught before shipping. A bad policy choice can only make the computation longer, never wrong.\n\n*The certification guard: termination is the unchanged all-pairs-reduce-to-zero test, so once every S-polynomial reduces to zero modulo G the returned G is provably the reduced $Gröbner$ basis regardless of any policy choice.*\n$$ \\forall (i,j):\\; \\overline{S(g_i,g_j)}^{\\,G} = 0 \\;\\Longrightarrow\\; G \\text{ is the reduced Gröbner basis, independent of } \\pi_\\theta \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Because the unchanged termination test certifies the basis, the answer is provably correct no matter what the policy chose — a policy mistake only costs extra work.\n8. On a held-out set of problems, run three selection rules on the SAME instrumented solver, changing only the rule: the default selector, a strong hand-designed baseline (sugar-degree selection — pick the lowest-sugar pair, break ties by lowest least-common-multiple degree, the standard high-quality non-learned choice), and the trained policy. For each run record the number of nonzero simplifications, the largest intermediate expression, the wall-clock time, and the basis returned, and check that all three return the exact same basis — confirming the answer does not depend on the selector.\n   - _Why_: This both measures the speedup on real computations and confirms the answer is unchanged across selectors.\n9. Train the policy ONLY on the random dense problems, freeze it, and test it without retraining on a structurally different family (sparse/structured) to see whether the savings carry over. Also run two checks on the same solver and correctness guard: a negative check that swaps the policy's choices for uniformly random pair picks (keeping everything else identical), where the cost should climb back to the no-learning baseline if the savings really came from the learned signal; and a positive check that ranks pairs by just the single feature most aligned with how confidently the policy separates its top choice from the rest, which should recover most of the savings and reveal which state feature is doing the work.\n   - _Why_: Transfer without retraining shows the policy learned something general, and the random control proves the savings come from the learned signal rather than any solver change.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 证书解耦的神经 S-pair 选择用于精确 Gröbner 基计算\n\n**方法名称.** Certificate-Decoupled Neural S-Pair Selection (CD-NSPS)\n\n## 研究动机\n$Gröbner$ 基是把一组多项式方程改写成一种标准形式,使原本很难的问题(解是否存在?某个多项式是否在理想里?)变得容易回答;它是很多密码学、机器人学和计算机代数背后的引擎。问题在于计算它非常昂贵,而几乎全部代价都藏在 Buchberger 算法的一个内层循环里。每一步算法都有一份待处理的 S-pair 清单,可以任意挑下一个来处理。挑哪一个完全不改变最终答案,但会让计算耗时和中间表达式膨胀的程度相差好几个数量级。\n\n最近的机器学习工作从两侧逼近却都漏掉了中间。一条路线(CAD 综述,semanticscholar:9d12b14d...)让模型在 solver 运行前一次性挑一个设置,然后把控制权交还给不变的 solver,从不对计算实际展开的过程做反应。另一条路线(CALT,一个 Computer-Algebra-with-Transformer 库)干脆丢掉 solver,训练一个 Transformer 端到端猜出整个答案——很快,但没有任何证明保证猜得对,而这在最看重 $Gröbner$ 基的安全与验证场景里毫无用处。第三条路线靠对某一类特定问题手工调优来加速,却无法迁移到其他问题族。\n\n为什么是现在:精确的计算机代数系统(Macaulay2、OSCAR、msolve)如今允许伸进循环内部、从外部喂入下一个 pair 的选择;而一篇很新的强化学习论文(openalex:W7127739695,2026)显示 RL 能降低 $Gröbner$ 计算代价——但它改的是 monomial order,这其实改变了答案对象本身。唯一没人学过的杠杆,是不改变答案的「循环内 S-pair 顺序」,而这正是我们要抓的杠杆。\n\n如果补上这个缺口,你就得到了缺失的中间选项:一个真正能在真实计算上加速内层循环的学习型向导,而它返回的东西仍是「可被证明正确」的 $Gröbner$ 基——于是这份加速终于能用于安全与验证场景,手工调优变成一个可迁移的策略,而且它能干净地叠加在 monomial-order 技巧之上,因为两者永远不会争抢同一个选择。\n\n## 方法\n### Solver-在环境中(solver-in-the-loop)\n*把可靠的 Buchberger/F4 驱动暴露成一个分步环境,其唯一可由外部控制的选择就是下一个处理哪个待处理 pair。*\n\n1. 把一个精确的计算机代数系统(Computer Algebra System, CAS;如 Macaulay2、OSCAR 或 msolve)包装起来,使其核心的基构建循环在每一步都交出:当前待处理 pair 的清单(每个 pair 附带它的最小公倍式(least common multiple)单项式、sugar 次数,以及它来自哪两个生成元),以及当前部分基(每个生成元的首项单项式、非零项数、总次数);然后暂停,等待外部调用者指定下一个处理哪个 pair。把这一切封装成函数 $env.step(pair_{index}, order_{hint}),$它只对所选 pair 执行一次精确的符号「构造并约化」,并报告三件事:是否约化为零、是否产生新基元素,以及这次约化有多大(被触及的非零项计数)。不要改动该系统的任何正确性逻辑。\n   - _为什么_: 要在计算展开过程中引导它,你必须能读到实时状态并喂入下一步动作——同时绝不接管精确算术。\n2. 把实时的计算状态变成模型能读的数字。对每个待处理 pair 计算七个特征:它的最小公倍式(least common multiple)次数、它的 sugar 次数、它两个生成元各自的非零项数、两个生成元共享多少个单项式、一个标志位表示它们的首项是否互素(Buchberger 第一准则),以及一个标志位表示它是否符合 chain 准则。对整个基计算四个汇总数:有多少个生成元、最大项数、最大次数、总项数。每个值都直接从 solver 读取——不要估计任何东西——并且每一步都重建,因为待办清单和基在不断变化。\n\n*对当前状态 $S_{t}$ 的特征化:每个待处理 pair 一个向量(lcm 次数、sugar $s_{ij}$、支撑度 $|g_{i}|$、$|g_{j}|$、单项式重叠 $o_{ij}$、互素-lcm 标志 $c_{ij}$、chain 准则标志 $h_{ij}),$再加上对基 $G_{t}$ 的全局汇总。*\n$$ \\phi(S_t) = \\big( \\{ [\\deg(\\mathrm{lcm}_{ij}),\\, s_{ij},\\, |g_i|,\\, |g_j|,\\, o_{ij},\\, c_{ij},\\, h_{ij}] \\}_{(i,j)\\in P_t},\\; [\\,|G_t|,\\, \\max_g |g|,\\, \\max_g \\deg g,\\, \\textstyle\\sum_g |g|\\,] \\big) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 只有把这个不断变化的计算用可在变长待办清单上互相比较的特征描述出来,模型才能对其作出反应。\n3. 每步之后,加入 solver 产生的任何新基元素,并让 solver 用它自己不变的标准机制$(Gebauer-Möller$ 过程,它同时会裁剪掉可证明冗余的新 pair)重建待处理 pair 清单,得到下一个状态。策略绝不触及 pair 再生成、约化或裁剪——这些都完全按没有任何学习时的方式运行。\n   - _为什么_: 把 pair 再生成和约化完全交给可信的 solver,正是策略永远无法破坏结果的保证。\n\n### 证书解耦的选择策略\n*一个很小的集合编码器策略,输出类型化的下一个 pair 产物,被训练去削减约化和中间膨胀,同时只控制一个不影响正确性的自由度。*\n\n4. 把策略做成一个很小的 2 层集合编码器(置换不变网络——DeepSets 或一个自注意力块——宽度 128,是整个系统中唯一被训练的权重),它读取每个 pair 的特征,把基的汇总信息附到每个 pair 上,并对每个待处理 pair 输出一个分数;把分数转成 pair 上的概率,并输出类型化选择(选哪个 pair,外加一个可选的 reduction-order hint),测试时取分数最高的 pair,训练时采样。把 reduction-order hint 仅做成一个索引,指向 solver 已支持的一份很短的固定合法约化顺序清单(默认、首项单项式升序、项数升序),这样它永远无法影响正确性。【作者需决定:这份短清单里到底放哪些合法约化顺序、清单多长——选择的维度是「暴露哪些可接受的顺序」。】\n\n*策略是对每个 pair 特征作用的置换不变集合编码器 $f_\\theta ,$其 softmax 给出待处理 pair 上的类别分布;输出的类型化产物 $a_{t}$ 给出下一个 pair(测试时取 argmax,训练时采样)和一个可选的 reduction-order hint。*\n$$ \\pi_\\theta(\\cdot \\mid S_t) = \\mathrm{softmax}\\big( f_\\theta(\\phi(S_t)) \\big), \\qquad a_t = (\\,\\mathrm{pair\\_index},\\, \\mathrm{order\\_hint}\\,),\\quad \\mathrm{pair\\_index} = \\arg\\max_{(i,j)\\in P_t} f_\\theta(\\phi(S_t))_{ij} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 置换不变的打分器能处理任意长度的待办清单;把模型限制在「只命名一个 pair」上,正是它永远碰不到正确性的原因。\n5. 用一个参数化生成器生成理想的训练课程,全程固定有限域和 monomial order。使用 3 到 8 个变量、每个理想 n 到 2n 个生成元、总次数 2 到 5 的随机多项式;稀疏度对稠密族取「全保留」,对稀疏/结构化族约保留五分之一,对 binomial 族恰好两项;并按从易到难排序。每个理想都通过 第1步（把一个精确的计算机代数系统） 环境变成 episodes。固定域和 monomial order 很重要,因为这让各 episode 之间唯一变化的就是处理 pair 的顺序——这正是我们想要的杠杆,而绝不是会改变答案的 monomial order 选择。【作者需决定:具体的生成范围与排序计划——选择的维度是策略训练所用的难度分布,它决定了策略能迁移到什么。】\n   - _为什么_: 固定域和 monomial order 意味着唯一变化的是 S-pair 顺序,于是策略学到的正是我们想要的杠杆,而不会学到任何会改变答案的东西。\n6. 用 REINFORCE(一种标准的策略梯度方法)训练策略,并用滑动平均基线来降低噪声。给每个结束的 episode 打分:非零约化次数的相反数,再减去一个权重乘以运行中见过的最大中间表达式规模,从而促使策略既避免长计算又避免表达式爆炸。权重的选法:先在一个试探批次上测出典型的约化次数和典型的最大表达式规模,把权重设成让两项惩罚处于同一量级,再试几个倍数,保留在留出问题上约化次数最少的那个。【作者需决定:这个权重如何确定、对表达式爆炸相对原始步数惩罚多重——选择的维度是两个代价项之间的取舍。】策略选的每个 pair 都会重塑后续计算,所以结束时度量到的代价反映了策略的选择;梯度只触及策略,绝不触及 solver。\n\n*每个 episode 的回报惩罚非零约化总数,再加 $\\lambda $ 乘以最大中间生成元支撑度;策略用带滑动平均基线 b 的 REINFORCE 训练,从而学会避免系数/支撑度爆炸,而不仅是步数。*\n$$ R(\\tau) = -\\sum_{t} \\mathbb{1}[\\,\\mathrm{was\\_zero}_t = \\mathrm{False}\\,] \\;-\\; \\lambda \\,\\max_{t} \\mathrm{supp}_t, \\qquad \\nabla_\\theta J = \\mathbb{E}_{\\tau\\sim\\pi_\\theta}\\!\\big[(R(\\tau)-b)\\,\\textstyle\\sum_t \\nabla_\\theta \\log \\pi_\\theta(a_t\\mid S_t)\\big] \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 同时奖励更少的约化和更小的中间膨胀(而不只是更少的步数),才能超越早期只看步数的 RL 尝试,直击真正的代价。\n\n### 认证与评估\n*用不变的终止检验认证返回的基,并度量内层循环节省、答案一致性、迁移和对照。*\n\n7. 当待处理清单为空时(每个 pair 都已完成或被剔除)停止,取 solver 返回的基。然后把标准正确性检验作为守卫运行:验证每个 pair 的「构造并约化」对该基都约化为零——这是判定是否为真基的教科书测试。因为该检验不依赖 pair 被处理的顺序,所以无论策略选了什么,答案都可被证明正确;对每个结果都运行它,以便在交付前抓住任何 bug。糟糕的策略选择只会让计算更长,绝不会让它出错。\n\n*证书守卫:终止条件仍是原始的「所有 pair 的 S-多项式模 G 约化为零」测试,因此一旦每个 S-多项式都约化为零,返回的 G 可被证明就是约化 $Gröbner$ 基,与策略的任何选择无关。*\n$$ \\forall (i,j):\\; \\overline{S(g_i,g_j)}^{\\,G} = 0 \\;\\Longrightarrow\\; G \\text{ is the reduced Gröbner basis, independent of } \\pi_\\theta \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 因为不变的终止检验对基作了认证,所以无论策略怎么选,答案都可被证明正确——策略选错只会多花点工。\n8. 在一组留出问题上,于同一个被插桩的 solver 上运行三种选择规则,只改变规则本身:默认选择器、一个强的手工设计基线(sugar-degree 选择——选 sugar 最低的 pair,平局时取最小公倍式(least common multiple)次数最低者,这是标准的高质量非学习选择),以及训练好的策略。每次运行记录非零约化次数、最大中间表达式、墙钟时间和返回的基,并检验三者返回完全相同的基——以此确认答案不依赖于选择器。\n   - _为什么_: 这既在真实计算上度量了加速,又确认了不同选择器下答案不变。\n9. 只在随机稠密问题上训练策略,冻结它,然后不重新训练就在结构不同的族(稀疏/结构化)上测试,看节省是否延续。同时在同一个 solver 和正确性守卫上运行两个检验:一个负向检验,把策略的选择换成均匀随机的 pair 选取(其他一切保持不变),如果节省确实来自学习到的信号,代价就应爬回无学习基线;一个正向检验,仅按「与策略把首选和其余拉开的置信度最一致」的单个特征对 pair 排序,它应能恢复大部分节省,并揭示是哪个状态特征在起作用。\n   - _为什么_: 不重新训练就能迁移,说明策略学到了通用的东西;随机对照则证明节省来自学习到的信号,而非任何 solver 改动。\n\n"},{"id":"57","run_dir":"run_prompt57_syndata","index":57,"title":"Risk-Optimal Synthetic-Data Selection from the High-Dimensional Limiting Risk","title_zh":"从高维极限风险出发的风险最优合成数据选择","method_name":"Risk-Optimal Set Selection (ROSS)","hook":"Across the high-dimensional analyses of training on real+synthetic mixtures, the keep/drop rule is always supplied from outside and only graded after the fact, so the field never asks which selection rule the limiting risk itself prescribes. We derive that rule in closed form and show it is NOT a per-sample scalar score but a set-level operator on the kept synthetic covariance, which provably dominates any fixed-score pruning whenever the generator rotates the synthetic feature covariance away from the signal.","anchor_pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","anchor_pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","domain_category":"Learning Theory & Statistics","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf produces the synthetic-sample keep/drop assignment that MINIMIZES the high-dimensional limiting risk; every leaf evaluates the risk of a selection rule supplied from outside (a score function in openalex:W4403443753, a learner-entropy heuristic in openalex:W6979227967), so the outcome 'a selection rule that is risk-optimal by construction rather than by post-hoc validation' is missing.","pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"closed by characterizing the exact attainable-risk floor of the fixed-scalar-score selection method class as a separation criterion on the kept synthetic covariance, then re-injecting the discarded set-level spectral interaction into the selection rule to construct a selector that provably attains a strictly lower limiting risk.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf makes the synthetic-data selection rule co-adapt to the generator's spectral distortion: the leaves treat selection and the synthetic-vs-real feature-covariance misalignment as separable (openalex:W4403443753 folds generator quality into a single scalar eta-hat; openalex:W6979227967 ignores feature shift entirely), leaving open how the keep/drop decision should change as the synthetic feature covariance rotates relative to the signal direction characterized in openalex","pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"closed by making the constructed selector an explicit functional of the generator's spectral-distortion operator (the rotation R between synthetic and real feature covariances), so the keep/drop decision is derived as a function of the misalignment the same limiting-risk formula exposes.","is_anchor":false},{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf tests whether a synthetic sample's value for training should be read off a per-sample SCALAR score at all, rather than from how that sample reshapes the empirical feature spectrum of the kept set — every leaf inherits the scalar-score-per-sample formulation from the pruning/verification ancestor and none questions whether that formulation is necessary or merely assumed.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","how_closed":"framing move (C11): audit the load-bearing assumption inside the selection rule's criterion — that training value is a per-sample scalar — and pivot selection from 'rank by scalar score' to 'choose the kept set whose covariance minimizes the limiting risk', re-deriving the risk certificate for the pivoted rule; companion deliverable (controlled_diagnostic_design): a matched-synthetic-pool diagnostic in which two pools have IDENTICAL per-sample scores but different set-level spectra, shipping the empirical separation that the scalar-score formulation provably cannot detect.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"high-dimensional statistical learning theory for synthetic-data selection (LLM / classifier training on real+synthetic mixtures)","n_papers":41,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":27},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":17,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Synthetic data analysis for early detection of Alzheimer progression through machine learning algorithms"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Strategies for overcoming data scarcity, imbalance, and feature selection challenges in machine learning models for predictive maintenance"},{"source":"openalex","title":"A proposed technique for predicting heart disease using machine learning algorithms and an explainable AI method"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Prediction of sepsis mortality in ICU patients using machine learning methods"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Leveraging artificial intelligence in vaccine development: A narrative review"},{"source":"openalex","title":"A precise machine learning model: Detecting cervical cancer using feature selection and explainable AI"}],"more":11},{"year":2025,"n":23,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A Data-Driven Approach for Predicting Remaining Useful Life of Semiconductor Devices Based on Machine Learning and Synthetic Data Generation: A Review and Case Study on SiC MOSFETs"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Can Moran Eigenvectors Improve Machine Learning of Spatial Data? Insights from Synthetic Data Validation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A Hybrid Machine Learning Approach for Synthetic Data Generation with Post Hoc Calibration for Clinical Tabular Datasets"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"An improved soft voting-based machine learning technique to detect breast cancer utilizing effective feature selection and SMOTE-ENN class balancing"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Machine learning-assisted fracture prediction: Integrating synthetic and experimental data for quasi-static notch failure analysis"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Early Detection of Alzheimer’s Disease Using Machine Learning, Feature Selection, Data Balancing, and Explainable AI"}],"more":17},{"year":2026,"n":1,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"}],"more":0}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":15,"share":0.366},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":9,"share":0.22},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":9,"share":0.22},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":8,"share":0.195},{"pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","count":6,"share":0.146},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":5,"share":0.122},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":4,"share":0.098},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":3,"share":0.073}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"When a classifier is trained on a mixture of real and synthetic samples in the proportional high-dimensional regime (dimension p, real n, synthetic m all growing at fixed ratios), the test risk depends jointly on the synthetic generator's feature-space distortion and on which synthetic samples are kept, yet the existing high-dimensional analyses (openalex:W4403443753, openalex:W6979227967) hold the selection rule FIXED: openalex:W4403443753 derives the random-matrix-theory risk of a binary linear classifier on a real+pruned-synthetic mix but treats the pruning score function as an exogenous input given by 'human or machine feedback', and openalex:W6979227967 selects synthetic examples by learner entropy/difficulty and only shows post-hoc via RMT that prioritizing hard examples improves the scaling curve. In both, the map from a selection rule to the resulting high-dimensional risk is one-directional: plug in a rule, read out the risk. The structural failure is that the inverse — which keep/drop assignment over synthetic samples actually minimizes the high-dimensional limiting risk, and how that assignment must co-adapt to the generator's spectral distortion (the misalignment between the synthetic and real feature covariances) — is never produced, so practitioners default to a heuristic score (entropy, difficulty, a verifier confidence) whose optimality is unestablished and which can provably select against the risk in regimes where the synthetic feature covariance is rotated away from the signal direction.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4403443753","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Uses random matrix theory to derive the exact limiting risk of a binary linear classifier trained on a mixture of real samples and a SCORE-FUNCTION-PRUNED set of synthetic samples in the proportional high-dimensional regime, characterizing how generator quality (eta-hat) and the real-data proportion (pi) shift the phase boundary between helpful and harmful synthetic data. Its residue: the pruning/score function is taken as an EXOGENOUS given (it characterizes risk FOR a supplied rule but never derives the risk-MINIMIZING keep/drop rule), the analysis is confined to a single binary linear classifier on Gaussian-mixture features, and it does not couple the optimal selection rule to the synthetic generator's feature-covariance rotation away from the signal direction."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W6979227967","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Deliberate Practice dynamically generates and keeps synthetic samples the current learner finds hard (high predictive entropy) and proves via RMT that prioritizing hard/informative examples improves the synthetic-data scaling law. Its residue: the selection signal (learner entropy/difficulty) is a heuristic proxy validated only post-hoc by the RMT bound — the paper does not derive the entropy rule from the high-dimensional risk objective, so it cannot say whether entropy is the risk-optimal selector or merely a correlate that breaks when generator-induced feature shift decouples 'hard' from 'risk-reducing'."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4398192204","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Derives exact proportional-high-dimensional risk formulas for principal component regression as a function of the population covariance spectrum and the alignment between population PCs and the true signal. Its residue: the spectral-alignment machinery is developed for a fixed real-data covariance and never connects to a data-SELECTION decision — it tells you how spectrum-vs-signal misalignment inflates risk but not how to choose (or down-weight) samples that would re-align the empirical spectrum with the signal."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4408520167","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Recasts prediction-oriented subdata selection as a convex optimal-experimental-design problem (J-optimality) using the covariate distribution to pick an optimal subsample from a full REAL dataset. Its residue: the design-theoretic selection optimum is derived for selecting among already-real covariates with no generative distribution shift, so it neither models synthetic-vs-real covariance mismatch nor gives a high-dimensional limiting-risk objective for the keep/drop of GENERATED samples."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"high-dimensional statistical learning theory for synthetic-data selection (LLM / classifier training on real+synthetic mixtures)","venue":"ICLR / NeurIPS (theory + empirical_reveal track)","time":"2026","data":["Gaussian-mixture / spiked-covariance synthetic-vs-real benchmarks (analytically tractable)","ImageNet-100 / ImageNet-1k synthetic data from text-to-image generators (DP setting)","tabular real+synthetic mixtures (Syntheval-style utility/privacy benchmarks)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (approx 90 A100-day)","expertise":"random matrix theory / high-dimensional asymptotics + representation learning","preference":"both","baseline":"score-function pruning of synthetic data with a fixed/given score (RMT anchor W4403443753); entropy/difficulty-guided dynamic selection (Deliberate Practice W6979227967)","limitation":"existing high-dimensional analyses take the synthetic-data selection rule (the score function used to keep/drop synthetic samples) as an EXOGENOUS input and only characterize the risk for that given rule; they do not derive which selection rule is risk-optimal in the proportional high-dimensional regime, nor how that rule must change when the synthetic generator induces a feature-space distribution shift relative to the real data","contribution_type":"theory","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","contribution_type","data"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"Shared object (shared_object thread): the proportional-asymptotics LIMITING RISK functional R_inf(S) of a ridge classifier trained on n real samples plus the kept subset S of m synthetic samples, in the regime p,n,m -> infinity with p/n -> phi, m/n -> rho fixed; every leg reads from and writes to R_inf(S). We model real features as x ~ N(+/- mu, I) (two-class, signal direction mu, ||mu||=O(1)) and synthetic features as x_syn ~ N(+/- R mu, Sigma_syn) where R is the generator's spectral-distortion operator (an orthogonal rotation, identity when the generator is perfect) and Sigma_syn its feature covariance, both estimated once from a held-out synthetic-vs-real probe set by matched-moment fitting (R from the top singular vectors of the cross-covariance E[x_real x_syn^T], Sigma_syn from the synthetic sample covariance; these are external-oracle quantities computed before selection). LEG 1 (anchor, C10): we apply standard deterministic-equivalent RMT to write R_inf(S) in closed form as a function only of the empirical second moment of the KEPT set, C(S) = (1/|S|) sum_{i in S} x_i x_i^T, and the fixed quantities (mu, R, Sigma_syn, phi, rho, ridge lambda); the discarded structural object that any per-sample scalar score throws away is exactly the off-diagonal / cross-sample contribution to C(S) — how the kept samples' covariance jointly aligns with mu — so we formalize the fixed-scalar-score method class's attainable floor as the criterion 'min over thresholds tau of R_inf({i: s_i >= tau})' and prove it is strictly above min_S R_inf(S) whenever R != I, exhibiting an explicit pair of equal-scalar-score pools that the scalar rule conflates but R_inf separates. We then CONSTRUCT the risk-optimal selector by re-injecting C(S) into the rule: minimize R_inf(S) over kept sets via its convex relaxation in the keep-probabilities q_i in [0,1] (R_inf is, after the deterministic-equivalent reduction, a ratio of quadratic forms in the q-weighted covariance, optimized by projected gradient / Frank-Wolfe with a budget constraint sum q_i = k), yielding a selector q* that is a SET-LEVEL operator, not a per-sample score. LEG 2 (C10, same object): because R_inf(S) is written explicitly through R and Sigma_syn, q* is automatically a functional of the generator's spectral distortion — we read off its closed-form dependence and prove that as R rotates mu away from the synthetic signal the optimal keep-set down-weights synthetic directions misaligned with R^T mu, closing the separability assumption by making selection spectrum-aware by construction. LEG 3 (C11 + controlled_diagnostic_design): the audit names the per-sample-scalar assumption baked into the n5/n6 selection criterion and pivots selection into the problem class 'choose the covariance C(S) minimizing R_inf' (selection -> covariance design), re-deriving the risk certificate as the C10 floor gap; the companion ships a confound-isolating diagnostic — two synthetic pools constructed to have identical marginal per-sample scores (entropy, verifier confidence, distance-to-real) but engineered different C(S) spectra, with the oracle R_inf computed independently from the planted (mu,R,Sigma_syn) — so the measured risk gap between pools that ANY scalar rule must score identically is the headline separation. The three legs are one paper because they are all statements about the single functional R_inf(S): leg 1 minimizes it, leg 2 traces its R-dependence, leg 3 audits the formulation it overturns and measures the gap it predicts.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The three gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules because all three are properties of the SAME limiting-risk functional R_inf(S): the evidence is that the anchor's optimal selector, the generator-distortion dependence, and the scalar-vs-set separation are all read off one closed-form expression once the deterministic equivalent is computed — splitting them into modules would re-derive R_inf three times. (b) Alternatives considered and rejected: (i) reframe_as_solvable_object as the anchor (recast as J-optimal/optimal-design subdata) was rejected because its load-bearing artifact would land on method_lineage node n3 (J-optimal subdata) and collateral c0 (coresets) — a regression the lineage flags — since optimal-design selection on real covariates already exists; we avoid that node by deriving the selector from the synthetic+real limiting-risk floor (with the generator-distortion operator R, which n3 has no notion of) rather than from a design criterion on covariates. (ii) An influence-function per-sample valuation (collateral c1) was rejected for the same regression reason and because it re-instantiates the very scalar-score assumption leg 3 audits. The avoided nodes (n3, c0, c1) are recorded here so the C10/C11 set-level-covariance route is auditable as non-regressive.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: train a ridge (and logistic) classifier on n real Gaussian samples plus a budget-k synthetic subset selected three ways — our R_inf-minimizing set selector, entropy/difficulty pruning (openalex:W6979227967's rule), and verifier-score pruning (openalex:W4403443753's score class) — on (i) a planted Gaussian-mixture with controllable distortion R and (ii) ImageNet-100 with generator-synthesized data, measuring downstream test error/accuracy at matched k. If the candidate works, test error under our selector is strictly lower than under either scalar rule, and the gap GROWS monotonically as the generator distortion R rotates mu away from the synthetic signal (zero gap at R=I, widening as the rotation angle increases). The named load-bearing variable is the set-level spectral-alignment term a(S) = mu^T C(S)^{-1} mu (the quadratic form through which C(S) enters R_inf); negative control: oracle-replace the estimated R by identity inside the selector — predicted effect on the DOWNSTREAM metric is that the test-error advantage over scalar pruning collapses to within noise (not merely that a(S) changes), because identity-R makes the optimal set coincide with what a well-tuned scalar rule already finds. Positive control: a stripped selector optimizing a(S) alone recovers most of the accuracy advantage, constructively identifying the spectral-alignment term as the mechanism.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4403443753","delta":"They derive the limiting risk of a binary linear classifier on a real+synthetic mix for a GIVEN external pruning/score function and fold generator quality into a scalar eta-hat; we derive the risk-MINIMIZING kept set in closed form as a set-level covariance operator and make it an explicit functional of the full spectral-distortion operator R, proving it strictly dominates their entire fixed-score class whenever R != I."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W6979227967","delta":"They select synthetic samples by learner entropy/difficulty and validate via RMT only post-hoc that hard-example prioritization improves scaling; we prove entropy is a per-sample scalar in the exact class our floor theorem dominates, and exhibit equal-entropy pools with different limiting risk that their rule cannot distinguish."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4398192204","delta":"They derive PCR's exact high-dimensional risk as a function of the fixed population spectrum-vs-signal alignment with no selection decision; we turn that alignment into the optimization target of a data-selection rule, deriving which synthetic samples to keep so the kept empirical spectrum re-aligns with the signal."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4408520167","delta":"They give a convex optimal-design (J-optimality) rule for selecting subdata from a REAL full dataset with no generative distribution shift; we solve selection over GENERATED samples under a synthetic-vs-real covariance rotation R, an object their covariate-design criterion has no representation of."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4403443753","what_step_was_missed":"They wrote the limiting risk as a function of an externally supplied per-sample pruning score and a scalar generator-quality parameter, but never inverted the map: they did not derive the kept-set covariance that minimizes that risk, nor express the optimal keep/drop as a functional of the full (non-scalar) spectral-distortion operator R — the variational minimization of R_inf over kept sets, and the proof that its minimizer is set-level rather than any thresholded scalar score, is the construction they did not perform."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":339,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"No hard floor fires: gap_closure_reject_check has no entry marked candidate_match yes (the single borderline is the dataset-dependent-constant lesson on the C11 leg, a controllable/surfaceable estimation-error concern, not a Reject match), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat.W4403443753 is shared-machinery overlap with addressable_via non-null (not exact-mechanism). recipe_application_check.verdict is 'applied' for all three legs, so the idea is built from the cited C10/C11 signature moves rather than the parent gist. The lone borderline sits on bound-constant controllability, a non-fatal concern best folded into Phase 4 reviewer_concerns, so advance over revise.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf produces the synthetic-sample keep/drop assignment that MINIMIZES the high-dimensional limiting risk; every leaf evaluates the risk of a selection rule supplied from outside (a score function in openalex:W4403443753, a learner-entropy heuristic in openalex:W6979227967), so the outcome 'a selection rule that is risk-optimal by construction rather than by post-hoc validation' is missing.","main_pattern":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail when the 'limit' is not a genuine structural blindspot — trivially implied, already surpassed, or never formalized beyond an informal analogy — or when the operator is constructed first and superiority asserted without surveying the frontier so a stronger published method subsumes the gain.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Resting the central claim on an informal analogy (two operators 'both smooth high frequencies') instead of a separation proof leaves the mechanism underspecified and the empirical gain unconvincing.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism step 3 builds an explicit separation theorem (min_tau R_inf > min_S R_inf when R!=I) with a witness pair of equal-score pools the scalar class conflates, not an informal analogy."},{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a 'maximally expressive' construction that a recently published method already strictly subsumes turns the surpass-the-limit claim into redundant work.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the collision retrieval (339 hits) surfaced no method that derives a risk-optimal synthetic-data keep set as a set-level covariance operator; the closest (W4403443753) supplies the score externally, so the surpass is not subsumed."},{"lesson_quoted":"Asserting the 'first efficient implementation' of a long-known algorithm without surveying the landscape invites direct refutation by existing faster implementations and collapses the novelty claim.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the claim is a new risk-minimizing selection rule, not an efficiency reimplementation; differentiation_from_lit surveys the four closest results and states what each did not construct."},{"lesson_quoted":"Deriving a 'limitation' that is trivially implied by the model's own linearity assumption produces a limit too weak to count as a real blindspot.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the blindspot (scalar scores discard the off-diagonal cross-sample covariance contribution to C(S)) is a substantive structural object the scalar-rule class provably cannot recover, exhibited via an explicit conflated pair, not a trivial consequence of linearity."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf makes the synthetic-data selection rule co-adapt to the generator's spectral distortion: the leaves treat selection and the synthetic-vs-real feature-covariance misalignment as separable (openalex:W4403443753 folds generator quality into a single scalar eta-hat; openalex:W6979227967 ignores feature shift entirely), leaving open how the keep/drop decision should change as the synthetic feature covariance rotates relative to the signal direction characterized in openalex:W4398192204.","main_pattern":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail when they port a formalism to a new domain but never demonstrate it captures an invariant the incumbent provably misses, producing abstraction with no testable advantage and no baseline comparison.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Applying existing structural descriptors to a new application domain without formalizing a new limit or constructing a new operator yields a domain study, not a methodological contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"this leg formalizes a new limit (the risk floor's dependence on the rotation R) and constructs a new operator (q* as an explicit functional of R), with a monotone down-weighting lemma — not a domain re-application."},{"lesson_quoted":"A novel formalism that cannot generate predictions or demonstrate concrete advantages over existing definitions reads as abstraction for its own sake.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the R-dependence generates the falsifiable prediction that the advantage over scalar pruning grows monotonically with rotation angle and collapses when R is oracle-replaced by identity (negative control in falsification_prediction)."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf tests whether a synthetic sample's value for training should be read off a per-sample SCALAR score at all, rather than from how that sample reshapes the empirical feature spectrum of the kept set — every leaf inherits the scalar-score-per-sample formulation from the pruning/verification ancestor and none questions whether that formulation is necessary or merely assumed.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The dominant failure is substituting one selection rule for another that performs better empirically while omitting the theorem that explains when and why it wins; a second is pivoting an assumption the community regards as a reasonable modeling choice; a third is a guarantee that does not hold (dataset-dependent uncontrollable constant).","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Substituting one selection rule for another that performs better empirically while omitting the theorem that explains when and why it wins — reviewers read this as a straightforward engineering combination without structural insight.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the pivot is accompanied by the re-derived risk certificate (the C10 floor-gap theorem) that states exactly when the set-level rule strictly wins (whenever R!=I), so the theorem, not the empirical swap, is the contribution."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pivoting an assumption the community regards as a reasonable modeling choice rather than a genuine restriction leaves both motivation and novelty in doubt.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the per-sample-scalar-score assumption is load-bearing, not benign: the witness equal-score pool pair proves it forces a strictly higher risk floor, so striking it changes the guarantee measurably."},{"lesson_quoted":"A binding constant that is dataset-dependent and uncontrollable by the practitioner (vacuous in the worst case), or a regularity assumption the selection mechanism provably violates.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"the floor-gap magnitude depends on the estimated (R, Sigma_syn); if these are poorly estimated the bound's practical size is data-dependent — surfaced as a Phase 4 reviewer concern (estimation-error sensitivity of R) rather than a fatal vacuity, since the gain is controllable by the kept-budget k and the positive control isolates the a(S) term."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The two C10 anchor legs are clear: the limit is formalized as a real separation theorem with a witness pair and the frontier was surveyed via collision_hits with no subsuming method. The C11 audit leg is borderline only on the dataset-dependent-constant lesson — the floor-gap size depends on the estimated spectral-distortion parameters (R, Sigma_syn) — which is a controllable, surfaceable concern (estimation error of R), not a documented Reject match marked yes."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf produces the synthetic-sample keep/drop assignment that MINIMIZES the high-dimensional limiting risk; every leaf evaluates the risk of a selection rule supplied from outside (a score function in openalex:W4403443753, a learner-entropy heuristic in openalex:W6979227967), so the outcome 'a selection rule that is risk-optimal by construction rather than by post-hoc validation' is missing.","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Pinpoint the one structural object an established procedure discards for tractability, formalize the equivalence class this discarding induces as a separation criterion on native objects, then re-inject that exact object into the procedure's core step and prove the augmented operator strictly exceeds the criterion at bounded cost.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism LEG 1 names the discarded object (the off-diagonal cross-sample contribution to the kept covariance C(S) that any scalar score throws away), formalizes the fixed-scalar-score floor as a separation criterion with an explicit conflated equal-score pool, then re-injects C(S) into the selection rule via the convex q-relaxation and proves min_S R_inf is strictly below the scalar floor whenever R!=I, with bounded (Frank-Wolfe / polynomial) cost — the C10 signature move, not the parent's generic gist.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf makes the synthetic-data selection rule co-adapt to the generator's spectral distortion: the leaves treat selection and the synthetic-vs-real feature-covariance misalignment as separable (openalex:W4403443753 folds generator quality into a single scalar eta-hat; openalex:W6979227967 ignores feature shift entirely), leaving open how the keep/drop decision should change as the synthetic feature covariance rotates relative to the signal direction characterized in openalex:W4398192204.","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Re-inject the discarded object into the core step so it becomes first-class structure rather than a preprocessing artifact, and prove the augmented operator exceeds the criterion across the regime.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism LEG 2 makes the constructed selector q* an explicit functional of the generator's spectral-distortion operator R (step 5 differentiates q* w.r.t. R and proves misaligned-direction down-weighting), so the rotation that prior work collapsed into a scalar eta-hat becomes first-class structure in the rule — the C10 re-injection move at the generator-distortion site.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf tests whether a synthetic sample's value for training should be read off a per-sample SCALAR score at all, rather than from how that sample reshapes the empirical feature spectrum of the kept set — every leaf inherits the scalar-score-per-sample formulation from the pruning/verification ancestor and none questions whether that formulation is necessary or merely assumed.","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Center on a selection/acquisition rule, pivot the single assumption baked into its criterion — frequently reframing selection into a different problem class (selection->combination/stopping/control/sampling) — and re-derive the performance certificate for the pivoted rule, shown to strictly beat the pre-pivot baseline.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism LEG 3 names the per-sample-scalar assumption inside the n5/n6 selection criterion and pivots selection into a different problem class (selection -> covariance design: 'choose the kept covariance C(S) minimizing R_inf'), re-deriving the risk certificate as the floor-gap theorem — the C11 reframe-and-rebound move; the controlled_diagnostic_design companion supplies the matched-pool empirical separation as its main-pattern-level deliverable.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"All three legs perform their cited cluster's signature move on the shared R_inf object: C10's discard-formalize-reinject-surpass appears in legs 1-2 (the kept covariance and its R-dependence are re-injected into the rule), and C11's pivot-the-selection-criterion-and-re-derive-the-certificate plus problem-class reframe appears in leg 3 (selection -> covariance design)."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["characterize_limit_then_surpass","characterize_limit_then_surpass","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; this candidate's composition_set contains none of it (nor the companion controlled_diagnostic_design pairs into any flagged 2-way subset), so no anti-pattern matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"openalex:W4403443753","threat_source":"lit_table","subsumption_argument":"W4403443753 (Maximizing the Potential of Synthetic Data: Insights from Random Matrix Theory) is the structurally closest threat: it already derives the high-dimensional limiting risk of a classifier on a real+pruned-synthetic mixture, so if its analysis implicitly contained the risk-MINIMIZING keep set, the candidate would be subsumed. It does not — its method section supplies the pruning via an exogenous score function and folds generator quality into a scalar eta-hat, never performing the variational minimization of R_inf over kept sets nor expressing the optimum as a functional of the full rotation operator R. The candidate's claim therefore stands precisely on the construction (the q-relaxed minimization and the R-dependence) that W4403443753 did not carry out; the overlap is in the risk-functional machinery, not in the selection-optimization result.","addressable_via":"differentiation_from_lit already names the delta (they evaluate risk for a given score; we minimize it over kept sets as a set-level R-functional); the overlap is shared-machinery, not exact-mechanism, so it is addressed by sharpening the differentiation framing rather than a forced field change."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Risk-Optimal Synthetic-Data Selection from the High-Dimensional Limiting Risk\n\n**Method.** Risk-Optimal Set Selection (ROSS)\n\n## Motivation\nPeople now routinely train machine-learning models on a mix of real data and synthetic (machine-generated) data, and a recent strand of theory explains when the synthetic part helps instead of hurting. The most powerful tools here come from random matrix theory, which studies what happens when the number of features and the number of samples both grow large together. One key paper (openalex:W4403443753) works out the exact eventual error of a classifier trained on real data plus a 'pruned' set of synthetic data — but it assumes someone hands it a rule for which synthetic samples to keep, and only computes the error for that given rule. Another recent paper (openalex:W6979227967) keeps the synthetic samples the model finds 'hard' (high uncertainty) and only checks afterward that this helped. So nobody has asked the reverse question: given the eventual-error formula itself, which keep-or-drop choice does it say is best? That is the gap. It is solvable now because the math needed to write the eventual error as a function of the kept set just became available, and because experiments have shown that WHICH synthetic samples you keep genuinely changes performance. What changes when we close it: instead of guessing with a heuristic score, you get a selection rule that is provably best, that automatically adjusts to how distorted the generator is, and that explains the earlier heuristics as special cases.\n\n## Method\n### Generator-distortion estimation\n*Turn the generator's feature distortion into the explicit inputs R and $\\Sigma _{syn}$ the selector needs.*\n\n1. Take a small held-out batch of paired real and synthetic samples (a few thousand pairs is plenty). Mean-center the feature vectors, then compute the cross-covariance matrix between the real and synthetic features and the synthetic feature covariance. Run a Singular Value Decomposition (SVD) of the cross-covariance and read off the rotation $\\hat{R}$ as $U\\cdot V^{T}$ (this is the standard orthogonal-Procrustes way to get the best rotation aligning synthetic directions to real ones); read off the synthetic covariance $\\Sigma _{syn}$ directly. If you have fewer pairs than feature dimensions, add a tiny diagonal term to each matrix before the SVD so the estimates are stable.\n   - _Why_: These two summaries capture how the generator distorts the data, which the selection rule will need to compensate for.\n\n### Closed-form risk + scalar-score floor\n*Write the eventual error as a function of the kept covariance and prove per-sample scores cannot reach the optimum.*\n\n2. Use the standard random-matrix-theory (RMT) deterministic-equivalent formula for a ridge classifier on the real+kept-synthetic mixture. Concretely there is one scalar self-consistency equation (a fixed-point in a single variable) you solve by simple damped iteration to a tight tolerance; plugging its solution into the deterministic-equivalent error formula gives the eventual test error as a closed-form function of just the kept synthetic set's covariance C(S) and the fixed quantities (signal $\\mu ,$ distortion R, $\\Sigma _{syn},$ the size ratios $\\phi =p/n$ and $\\rho =m/n,$ and the ridge strength $\\lambda ).$ Cache the matrix inverse computed along the way — the next step's gradient reuses it.\n\n*The proportional-asymptotics limiting risk $R\\infty $ of the ridge classifier is a closed-form deterministic-equivalent functional F of only the kept set's second moment C(S) and the fixed quantities $\\mu ,$ R, $\\Sigma _{syn}, \\phi , \\rho , \\lambda .$*\n$$ \\mathcal{R}_\\infty(S) = \\mathcal{F}\\!\\left(C(S),\\, \\boldsymbol{\\mu},\\, R,\\, \\Sigma_{\\mathrm{syn}},\\, \\phi,\\, \\rho,\\, \\lambda\\right), \\qquad C(S) = \\frac{1}{|S|}\\sum_{i\\in S} x_i x_i^{\\top} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Once the error depends only on the kept set's covariance, you can optimize over which samples to keep instead of only scoring a fixed rule.\n3. Prove that any rule that assigns each synthetic sample a single number and keeps the ones above a threshold can never reach the lowest possible error when the generator is distorted (R is not the identity). Do this by constructing two synthetic pools that are deliberately identical on every per-sample score in the audited family (classifier margin/entropy, a verifier-confidence proxy, and nearest-neighbor distance to real data) — you make them identical by matching, for each sample, its projection onto the signal direction and its overall length, which are the only things those scores depend on — yet the two pools differ in their covariance spectrum (one loads mass on the signal-aligned direction, the other on an orthogonal direction). Plug both into the step-step 2 (Use the standard $random-matrix-theor\\dots )$ error formula: the errors differ, so no single-number rule could have told them apart.\n\n*The best risk attainable by any per-sample scalar score $s_{i}$ with any threshold $\\tau $ is strictly above the set-level optimum whenever the generator distortion R is not the identity.*\n$$ \\min_{\\tau}\\; \\mathcal{R}_\\infty\\big(\\{i : s_i \\geq \\tau\\}\\big) \\;>\\; \\min_{S}\\; \\mathcal{R}_\\infty(S) \\quad \\text{whenever } R \\neq I \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This shows the universal practice of per-sample scoring is leaving error on the table, motivating a set-level rule.\n\n### Risk-optimal set selector\n*Minimize the risk directly over keep-probabilities and expose its dependence on the generator distortion.*\n\n4. Give each synthetic sample a keep-probability between 0 and 1, require they sum to the budget k on average, and directly minimize the eventual-error formula over these probabilities. Use a Frank-Wolfe optimizer (each iteration just keeps the k samples whose gradient says they help most, then takes a shrinking averaging step) driven by the closed-form gradient, reusing the matrix inverse cached in step step 2 (Use the standard $random-matrix-theor\\dots ).$ When it converges, turn the soft probabilities into a hard set: keep the top-k samples by probability, and if one sample sits on the boundary, decide it by whichever choice gives lower predicted error. This keeps the budget exact and stays very close to the best soft solution because the error formula is smooth.\n\n*The optimal selector q★ minimizes the limiting risk over keep-probabilities q under a budget of k kept samples, optimized by Frank-Wolfe on the closed-form gradient; it is a set-level operator, not a per-sample score.*\n$$ q^{\\star} = \\arg\\min_{q \\in [0,1]^m,\\; \\mathbf{1}^{\\top} q = k}\\; \\mathcal{R}_\\infty\\!\\left(C(q)\\right), \\qquad C(q) = \\frac{\\sum_i q_i x_i x_i^{\\top}}{\\sum_i q_i} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This builds the selection rule straight from the error objective, so it is optimal by construction rather than validated after the fact.\n5. Show how the optimal selector changes as the generator distortion R changes. Because the selector is the solution of a constrained optimization, you cannot just take a plain derivative — instead differentiate the optimality (stationarity) conditions, which yields a small linear system you solve to get the sensitivity of the kept probabilities to R. Then project this onto the rotated signal direction and check its sign: this proves that the optimal rule down-weights synthetic directions pointing away from the rotated signal, and does so more strongly as the rotation grows. Confirm the closed-form result numerically on planted examples.\n   - _Why_: It makes precise how the keep/drop choice must change with the generator, which prior work collapsed into a single quality number.\n\n### Audit-and-pivot validation\n*Reframe selection as covariance design and demonstrate the separation that scalar scores cannot detect, on planted and real data.*\n\n6. Switch the framing from scoring individual samples to choosing the covariance of the kept set, then build two synthetic pools that are deliberately equal on every per-sample score (uncertainty, verifier confidence, distance-to-real) but differ in their covariance spectrum — one pool puts its kept mass on the direction the error formula rewards most, the other on the direction it rewards least, and you sweep how strong this contrast is. Because you built them in a known planted setup, you can read off their true error directly from the step-step 2 (Use the standard $random-matrix-theor\\dots )$ formula with no fitting. Then actually train a ridge and a logistic classifier on real-plus-pool-A versus real-plus-pool-B across several random seeds, and confirm the measured error gap matches the formula's gap while every single-number rule predicts no gap at all.\n\n*The load-bearing set-level spectral-alignment term a(S) is the quadratic form through which the kept covariance C(S) enters the risk; the positive control optimizes a(S) alone.*\n$$ a(S) = \\boldsymbol{\\mu}^{\\top} C(S)^{-1} \\boldsymbol{\\mu} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: If the two pools train to different error despite identical scores, no scalar rule could have told them apart — a clean demonstration that set-level structure is what matters.\n7. On ImageNet-100 (generator-synthesized images) and a tabular real-plus-synthetic benchmark, first map every real and synthetic example into a fixed feature space: for images, pass them through a frozen pretrained encoder (default a self-supervised ImageNet encoder, taking its second-to-last-layer features, then length-normalize) 【author decision: which frozen encoder to use for ImageNet-100 — a self-supervised one, a supervised one, or the generator's own feature extractor — sets the representation the whole theory operates in.】; for tabular data, just standardize the raw columns. Then estimate R and $\\Sigma _{syn}$ from a paired probe, run the selector at the same kept budget as the baselines, train the classifier, and compare against uncertainty-based and verifier-based pruning done in the same feature space. Also run two checks: a negative control where you force R to the identity (the advantage should vanish) and a positive control where you optimize only the alignment term (it should recover most of the benefit).\n   - _Why_: Real datasets test whether the planted-setup advantage survives, and the controls confirm the gain comes specifically from the distortion-awareness and the alignment term.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 从高维极限风险出发的风险最优合成数据选择\n\n**方法名称.** Risk-Optimal Set Selection (ROSS)\n\n## 研究动机\n如今人们经常用真实数据和合成（机器生成）数据的混合来训练机器学习模型，最近一条理论线索解释了合成部分在什么情况下有益而非有害。这里最有力的工具来自 random matrix theory，它研究当特征数与样本数同时变大时会发生什么。一篇关键论文（openalex:W4403443753）精确算出了在真实数据加上经过 pruning 的合成数据上训练的分类器的最终误差，但它假设有人事先给定了保留哪些合成样本的规则，并只针对这个给定规则计算误差。另一篇近期论文（openalex:W6979227967）保留模型觉得 hard（高不确定性）的合成样本，并且只是事后验证这样有帮助。于是没人问过反向的问题：给定最终误差公式本身，它指示的最优保留或丢弃方案是什么？这正是空白所在。它现在可解，是因为把最终误差写成所留集合函数所需的数学刚刚成熟，也因为实验已经表明保留哪些合成样本确实会改变性能。补上这一空白后会发生什么：不再用启发式分数去猜，而是得到一个可证明最优、能自动适应生成器畸变程度、并把先前启发式解释为特例的选择规则。\n\n## 方法\n### 生成器畸变估计\n*把生成器的特征畸变转化为选择器所需的显式输入 R 与 $\\Sigma _{syn}$。*\n\n1. 取一小批留出的成对真实与合成样本（几千对即可）。先对特征向量做去均值，再计算真实特征与合成特征之间的互协方差矩阵，以及合成特征协方差。对互协方差做奇异值分解(Singular Value Decomposition, SVD)，按 $\\hat{R} = U\\cdot V^{T}$ 读出旋转 $\\hat{R}$（这是用正交 Procrustes 方法求“把合成方向对齐到真实方向”的最佳旋转的标准做法）；并直接读出合成协方差 $\\Sigma _{syn}$。若样本对数少于特征维数，先给每个矩阵加一个很小的对角项再做 SVD，使估计更稳定。\n   - _为什么_: 这两个摘要刻画了生成器如何畸变数据，而选择规则正需要据此进行补偿。\n\n### 闭式风险与标量分数下界\n*把最终误差写成所留协方差的函数，并证明逐样本分数无法达到最优。*\n\n2. 用标准的随机矩阵理论(Random Matrix Theory, RMT)确定性等价公式，针对“真实+所留合成”混合数据上的 ridge 分类器。具体地，只有一个标量自洽方程（单变量不动点），用简单的阻尼迭代解到很紧的容差即可；把它的解代入确定性等价误差公式，就得到最终测试误差，它是仅依赖所留合成集合协方差 C(S) 以及固定量（信号 $\\mu $、畸变 R、$\\Sigma _{syn}$、规模比值 $\\phi =p/n$ 与 $\\rho =m/n$、岭强度 $\\lambda $）的闭式函数。把过程中算出的那个矩阵逆缓存下来——下一步的梯度会复用它。\n\n*岭分类器的比例渐近极限风险 $R\\infty $ 是一个确定性等价闭式泛函 F，仅依赖于所留集合的二阶矩 C(S) 以及固定量 $\\mu $、R、$\\Sigma _{syn}$、$\\phi $、$\\rho $、$\\lambda $。*\n$$ \\mathcal{R}_\\infty(S) = \\mathcal{F}\\!\\left(C(S),\\, \\boldsymbol{\\mu},\\, R,\\, \\Sigma_{\\mathrm{syn}},\\, \\phi,\\, \\rho,\\, \\lambda\\right), \\qquad C(S) = \\frac{1}{|S|}\\sum_{i\\in S} x_i x_i^{\\top} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 一旦误差只依赖于所留集合的协方差，就可以对保留哪些样本进行优化，而不只是为某个固定规则打分。\n3. 证明：当生成器存在畸变（R 不等于单位算子）时，任何“给每个合成样本打一个数、保留高于阈值者”的规则都无法达到最低误差。做法是构造两个合成池：它们在所审计的那一族逐样本分数（分类器 margin/entropy、verifier 置信度代理、到真实数据的最近邻距离）上刻意完全相等——之所以能相等，是因为这些分数只依赖每个样本在信号方向上的投影及其整体长度，把这两者逐样本对齐即可——但两个池的协方差谱不同（一个把质量放在与信号对齐的方向上，另一个放在正交方向上）。把两者都代入第 第2步（用标准的随机矩阵理论） 步的误差公式：误差不同，所以任何“单一数值”规则都无法区分它们。\n\n*任意逐样本标量分数 $s_{i}$ 配合任意阈值 $\\tau $ 所能达到的最优风险，只要生成器畸变 R 不等于单位算子，就严格高于集合级最优值。*\n$$ \\min_{\\tau}\\; \\mathcal{R}_\\infty\\big(\\{i : s_i \\geq \\tau\\}\\big) \\;>\\; \\min_{S}\\; \\mathcal{R}_\\infty(S) \\quad \\text{whenever } R \\neq I \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这表明普遍采用的逐样本打分做法白白损失了误差，从而促使采用集合级规则。\n\n### 风险最优集合选择器\n*直接对保留概率最小化风险，并揭示其对生成器畸变的依赖。*\n\n4. 给每个合成样本一个介于 0 与 1 的保留概率，要求其平均之和等于预算 k，然后直接对这些概率最小化最终误差公式。用 Frank-Wolfe 优化器（每轮只保留梯度判定“最有帮助”的 k 个样本，再做一步逐渐缩小的平均更新），由闭式梯度驱动，并复用第 第2步（用标准的随机矩阵理论） 步缓存的矩阵逆。收敛后把软概率转成硬集合：按概率取前 k 个样本；若有一个样本恰处边界，就按“哪种选择预测误差更低”来定。这样能保证预算精确，且因误差公式光滑，结果与最优软解非常接近。\n\n*最优选择器 q★ 在留样预算 k 的约束下，对保留概率 q 最小化极限风险，借助闭式梯度的 Frank-Wolfe 求解；它是集合级算子，而非逐样本分数。*\n$$ q^{\\star} = \\arg\\min_{q \\in [0,1]^m,\\; \\mathbf{1}^{\\top} q = k}\\; \\mathcal{R}_\\infty\\!\\left(C(q)\\right), \\qquad C(q) = \\frac{\\sum_i q_i x_i x_i^{\\top}}{\\sum_i q_i} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这是直接从误差目标构建选择规则，因而是构造性最优，而非事后验证。\n5. 说明最优选择器如何随生成器畸变 R 变化。由于该选择器是一个带约束优化的解，不能直接求普通导数——而要对最优性（稳定性）条件求导，这会得到一个小型线性方程组，解出保留概率对 R 的敏感度。再把它投影到旋转后的信号方向上并判断符号：由此证明最优规则会下调那些偏离旋转后信号方向的合成方向的权重，且旋转越大下调越强。最后在植入的例子上用数值结果验证该闭式结论。\n   - _为什么_: 它精确刻画了保留/丢弃决策必须如何随生成器变化，而先前工作把这一点压缩成了单一质量数。\n\n### 审计-转轴验证\n*把选择重构为协方差设计，并在植入与真实数据上展示标量分数无法察觉的分离。*\n\n6. 把思路从“给单个样本打分”切换为“选择所留集合的协方差”，然后构造两个合成池：它们在每个逐样本分数（不确定性、verifier 置信度、到真实样本的距离）上都刻意相等，但协方差谱不同——一个池把所留质量放在误差公式最“奖励”的方向上，另一个放在最不奖励的方向上，并扫描这种对比的强弱。由于它们是在已知的植入设定下构造的，可直接用第 第2步（用标准的随机矩阵理论） 步公式读出其真实误差，无需任何拟合。随后真正地在“真实+池A”与“真实+池B”上训练 ridge 和 logistic 分类器（多个随机种子），确认实测误差差距与公式给出的差距一致，而任何“单一数值”规则都预测差距为零。\n\n*承载机制的集合级谱对齐项 a(S) 是所留协方差 C(S) 进入风险时的二次型；阳性对照仅优化 a(S)。*\n$$ a(S) = \\boldsymbol{\\mu}^{\\top} C(S)^{-1} \\boldsymbol{\\mu} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 如果两个池在分数完全相同的情况下训练出不同误差，任何标量规则都无法区分它们——这干净地证明了起作用的是集合级结构。\n7. 在 ImageNet-100（生成器合成的图像）和一个表格“真实+合成”基准上，先把每个真实与合成样本映射到一个固定特征空间：对图像，过一个冻结的预训练编码器（默认用自监督 ImageNet 编码器，取其倒数第二层特征，再做长度归一化）【作者需决定：ImageNet-100 用哪个冻结编码器——自监督、监督、还是生成器自带的特征提取器——这决定了整套理论所在的表示空间。】；对表格数据，直接对原始列做标准化。然后从成对探针估计 R 与 $\\Sigma _{syn}$，在与各基线相同的保留预算下运行选择器、训练分类器，并与在同一特征空间中进行的、基于不确定性和基于 verifier 的 pruning 比较。同时做两个检验：负对照——强制把 R 设为单位算子（优势应消失）；正对照——只优化对齐项（应能恢复大部分收益）。\n   - _为什么_: 真实数据集检验植入设定下的优势是否仍然成立，而对照确认增益确实来自畸变感知与对齐项。\n\n"},{"id":"58","run_dir":"run_prompt58_lrdecay","index":58,"title":"Quality-Conditioned Effective Step Size: Decoupling Update Weight from Training Position in Curriculum Pretraining","title_zh":"质量条件化有效步长：在课程预训练中将更新权重与训练位置解耦","method_name":"Quality-Conditioned Effective Step Size (QC-ESS)","hook":"An ascending-quality curriculum's collapse under LR decay is not caused by where the good data sits but by the schedule forcing a token's effective update weight to be a fixed decreasing function of its training-time position; we restore the curriculum's constant-LR advantage while keeping the decaying global LR by giving each token a quality-conditioned effective step size that the global decay can no longer cancel. Late high-quality tokens are re-weighted in place rather than moved earlier, so the optimizer's noise-suppression role and the curriculum's capacity-allocation intent are satisfied at once.","anchor_pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","anchor_pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","domain_category":"LLM Pretraining, Architecture & Scaling","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces an effective per-token update weight whose distribution over the training stream can be made to track token quality, rather than being forced to monotonically decrease with training-time position — so the high-quality tokens placed late under a curriculum cannot recover the update weight the LR decay strips from them (additive need at the frontier-leaf residual of semanticscholar:6840c3ec7e97b2c7c65b2b989634ac83f9827d91).","pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by partitioning the token stream by a measurable quality score and assigning each partition a differentiated effective step size (a per-token multiplier on η_t that depends on the token's quality, not its position), backed by a signal/noise-decomposition that bounds how the differentiated treatment recovers the curriculum's constant-LR advantage — the high-quality minority's effective update weight is protected from the late-stage decay while the bulk keeps the noise-suppressing small step.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions whether the LR schedule must be a single global function of training-time position shared by every token regardless of that token's quality — every curriculum-for-pretraining and LR-schedule leaf silently inherits this from the shared ancestor (a global iteration-indexed LR curve), tuning either the data order or the curve shape but never asking whether the effective weight a token receives should be decoupled from when in training it happens to appear (subtractive: t","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C29 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","how_closed":"Closed on the framing side by naming and violating the inherited assumption — that a token's effective update weight is forced to equal the global position-indexed η_t — and showing the curriculum advantage is binding on it (it exists under constant LR and vanishes only as decay is applied); closed on the deliverable side by the companion controlled_diagnostic_design, which ships a confound-isolating ablation that attributes the recovered advantage to the quality-conditioned effective-step decoupling specifically rather than to the Adam second-moment / optimizer-state pathway or to extra effective compute.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"LLM pretraining — data curriculum / learning-rate-schedule interaction","n_papers":38,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":24},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":11,"papers":[{"source":"openalex","title":"A framework for human evaluation of large language models in healthcare derived from literature review"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Large language models for generative information extraction: a survey"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Generating an Instruction Dataset to Build Cyber Intelligent Large Language Models"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Vision-language models for medical report generation and visual question answering: a review"},{"source":"openalex","title":"LLaRA: Large Language-Recommendation Assistant"},{"source":"openalex","title":"A survey of safety and trustworthiness of large language models through the lens of verification and validation"}],"more":5},{"year":2025,"n":26,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"How Learning Rate Decay Wastes Your Best Data in Curriculum-Based LLM Pretraining"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Beyond Random Sampling: Efficient Language Model Pretraining via Curriculum Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Beyond Repetition: Text Simplification and Curriculum Learning for Data-Constrained Pretraining"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Persian-Phi: Efficient Cross-Lingual Adaptation of Compact LLMs via Curriculum Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Reasoning Curriculum: Bootstrapping Broad LLM Reasoning from Math"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Scaling LLM Pre-training with Vocabulary Curriculum"}],"more":20},{"year":2026,"n":1,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"}],"more":0}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition; adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"heterogeneous_decomposition; adapt_via_conditioning","count":2,"share":0.053},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design; assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"controlled_diagnostic_design; assumption_audit_and_pivot","count":2,"share":0.053},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign; architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"generative_process_redesign; architectural_operator_substitution","count":2,"share":0.053},{"pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass; reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"characterize_limit_then_surpass; reframe_as_solvable_object","count":2,"share":0.053},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot; controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"assumption_audit_and_pivot; controlled_diagnostic_design","count":1,"share":0.026},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design; heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"controlled_diagnostic_design; heterogeneous_decomposition","count":1,"share":0.026},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering; controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"self_supervised_signal_engineering; controlled_diagnostic_design","count":1,"share":0.026},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning; assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"adapt_via_conditioning; assumption_audit_and_pivot","count":1,"share":0.026}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"When an ascending-quality data curriculum is paired with a conventional decaying learning-rate schedule (WSD/cosine), the curriculum's benefit over uniform ordering collapses: the per-step update magnitude η_t functions as an implicit importance weight on each token, so the high-quality data the curriculum deliberately presents last receives the smallest effective weight, and the gain that a constant LR gives the curriculum is erased (semanticscholar:6840c3ec7e97b2c7c65b2b989634ac83f9827d91). Existing curriculum-for-pretraining studies (semanticscholar:9a8aac1c8ef62f87d78808429d6acdbcf7d1d657; semanticscholar:aa148ef5239b31d2d854e6a3cf2c23ea377bf29d) tune the data ordering, the difficulty/preference metric, and the pacing function while treating the LR schedule as a fixed exogenous given, and existing LR-schedule work (openalex:W6979357895; openalex:W6979234000) characterizes or unifies LR shapes purely as functions of the iteration budget with no notion of which data sits under each step — so neither line produces the missing quantity: an allocation of effective per-token update weight that does not monotonically vanish exactly where the most valuable tokens were placed. The failure is that under the current machinery the effective importance assigned to a token is forced to be a fixed decreasing function of its training-time position, decoupled from the token's quality, so the curriculum's intent (spend more capacity on better data) and the optimizer's intent (shrink steps late to reduce noise) are structurally in opposition and cannot both be satisfied.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:6840c3ec7e97b2c7c65b2b989634ac83f9827d91","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Identifies that a decaying LR acts as an implicit per-sample importance weight and shows the curriculum advantage diminishes the more aggressively the LR decays during the final high-quality regime, then mitigates by adjusting the data schedule (e.g. delaying/compressing where high-quality data lands). Its own method section states the data-schedule adjustment only partially recovers the gap and 'the underlying conflict persists' — it diagnoses the coupling and rearranges the data under a still-fixed decreasing weight curve, but does not produce a mechanism that decouples a token's effective update weight from its training-time position, leaving the quality-vs-position opposition unresolved."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:aa148ef5239b31d2d854e6a3cf2c23ea377bf29d","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Preference Curriculum (PDPC) dynamically perceives the data the model currently 'prefers' (via a perplexity-difference metric) and reschedules the data distribution per stage to always train on preferred data. It reschedules WHICH data is presented when but still rides whatever global LR curve is in force, so its preferred late-stage data is subject to the same late-stage LR down-weighting; it never adjusts the effective update weight a chosen token receives."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W6979357895","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"The Multi-Power Law fits an empirical law predicting pretraining loss as a function of the LR-schedule shape (constant/cosine/step) and uses it to search for loss-optimal schedules. The law is data-agnostic — it treats the corpus as homogeneous and optimizes the schedule for aggregate loss, so it has no representation of per-token quality and cannot express, let alone optimize, the alignment between where update weight is spent and where the valuable tokens are."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W6979234000","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Stepsize-anything derives a unified, budget-aware LR schedule for budgeted-iteration training, replacing heuristic schedule design with a principled curve. It optimizes the schedule as a pure function of the iteration budget with no coupling to the data identity at each step, so it reproduces the same position-locked decreasing-weight curve that conflicts with an ascending-quality curriculum."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"LLM pretraining — data curriculum / learning-rate-schedule interaction","venue":"ICLR/NeurIPS (ML methods)","time":"2026","data":["web-scale pretraining corpora with per-sample quality scores (e.g. DCLM/FineWeb-Edu scores)","ascending-quality-ordered token streams"],"compute":"1×A100 × 3 months (≈ 90 A100-day budget)","expertise":"ML researcher with cloud access; LLM pretraining + optimization background","preference":"both","baseline":"ascending-quality data curriculum trained under a standard decaying LR schedule (WSD / cosine), versus uniform/random ordering under the same schedule","limitation":"Under a standard decaying LR schedule the advantage of an ascending-quality curriculum collapses, because the small late-stage LR down-weights exactly the high-quality data the curriculum places last; data-schedule adjustments only partially mitigate and the underlying LR-vs-data-schedule conflict persists.","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","compute","expertise","data","preference"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared audit lens is the effective per-token update weight: the quantity w(t,x) = (how much token x at step t actually moves the parameters in the signal direction). Reading the update θ_{t+1}=θ_t − η_t g_t, the seed paper's own analysis shows η_t acts as an implicit per-sample importance weight, so under a decaying schedule w(t,x) is forced to be the position-locked decreasing curve η_t, independent of x's quality — this is the assumption every frontier leaf (n3,n4,n5,n6) inherits from ancestor n2. ANCHOR LEG (heterogeneous_decomposition, C04): we partition the token stream by a per-token quality score q(x) ∈ [0,1] — q is read directly from the SAME quality metric the curriculum already uses to order data (DCLM fasttext / PreSelect score, normalized to [0,1] over the corpus, an external precomputed oracle, NOT model-internal), so no new scorer is introduced — and assign each token a differentiated effective step size η_eff(t,x) = η_t · m(q(x), t), where m is a quality-conditioned multiplier. m is defined as m(q,t) = 1 + α · q · (η_peak/η_t − 1) · s(t), with α ∈ [0,1] a single bridge hyperparameter (default α=0.5), η_peak the peak LR, and s(t) ∈ {0,1} a stability gate that is 1 only inside the decay phase (t past the stable plateau of a WSD schedule) and 0 during warmup/plateau; the (η_peak/η_t − 1) factor is exactly the deficit the decay carved out, so a maximal-quality token (q=1, α=1) recovers up to the peak effective step it would have had under constant LR while a minimum-quality token (q=0) keeps the unmodified decayed step η_t. The multiplier is applied as a per-token scaling of that token's contribution to the minibatch gradient BEFORE the Adam preconditioner aggregates the batch (i.e. it scales the raw per-token loss gradient, equivalently a per-token effective learning rate), so it changes the actual parameter update direction and magnitude, which changes the next-token predictions of the trained model on the held-out high-quality validation set. The load-bearing artifact is a signal/noise decomposition: writing g_t = E[g_t] + ε_t, the per-token multiplier raises the signal-direction step for high-quality tokens (whose E[g_t] points toward the high-quality validation distribution) by the recovered factor while leaving the noise ε_t of low-quality bulk tokens suppressed by the small η_t — the decomposition bounds the recovered validation-loss advantage as a function of α and the quality-gradient alignment, predicting recovery of most of the constant-LR curriculum gap without reintroducing the late-training noise that motivated decay. AUDIT LEG (assumption_audit_and_pivot C29 + companion controlled_diagnostic_design): the same w(t,x) object is the audit site — we state the assumption (w must equal global η_t), show it is load-bearing (curriculum advantage present at constant LR, monotonically erased as decay deepens, per the seed's own Long/Mid/Short/Zero decay sweep), and violate it via η_eff above; the companion ships the confound-isolating diagnostic — a matched control that holds total effective compute (sum of effective step sizes over the run) FIXED between the decoupled run and a plain decayed run, and a second control that applies the same average up-weight UNIFORMLY across tokens regardless of quality — so any recovered advantage that survives the compute-matched, quality-randomized controls is attributable to the quality-conditioned decoupling and not to simply training longer/hotter or to an Adam second-moment artifact. Both legs read from and write to the single object w(t,x); the anchor constructs it, the audit interrogates and validates it, so the paper is one coordinated contribution rather than two.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery because they are the same object viewed twice: the additive gap demands a constructed w(t,x) that tracks quality, and the subtractive gap demands that the position-locked-w assumption be named and tested — evidence that they share machinery is that the audit's falsifier (compute-matched, quality-randomized control) is exactly the ablation that proves the anchor's construction is load-bearing, so splitting them into separate modules would duplicate the same experiment. (b) Alternatives considered and rejected: (i) realizing the fix as a per-example LOSS weight w_loss·L(x) — rejected because method_lineage flags node c0 (per-example loss reweighting): a position-locked global η_t multiplies into a loss weight and can still cancel it, so this regresses to a >4y classical move; we instead modulate the effective step size / per-token gradient scale relative to the decay deficit, a source the tree does not occupy. (ii) recovering late contribution by EMA/checkpoint-averaging the late high-LR-equivalent steps — rejected as regression to flagged node c1 (parameter averaging), which cannot selectively up-weight specific high-quality tokens. (iii) redesigning the global LR curve shape itself (a smarter schedule) — rejected because it stays at ancestor n2 (a single global position-indexed curve) and cannot decouple weight from position for individual tokens.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: at DCLM 1B-1x with Qwen2.5-1.5B on 30B tokens (the seed's exact regime), train ascending-curriculum + WSD-decay with vs. without the quality-conditioned effective-step multiplier and measure held-out high-quality DCLM validation loss and OLMES Core (MMLU/ARC/CSQA). If the candidate works, the decoupled run's validation loss DECREASES toward the constant-LR-curriculum lower bound (recovering a substantial fraction of the advantage that plain curriculum+decay loses) and OLMES Core INCREASES over curriculum+decay, while NOT reintroducing the late-training instability decay was meant to suppress (gradient-noise norm late in training stays comparable to the plain decayed run). The named load-bearing variable is the late-training signal-direction projection p_t = cos(high-quality minibatch gradient, running high-quality validation gradient): the mechanism claims the multiplier keeps p_t high for high-quality tokens late in training where the decayed baseline's p_t collapses. Negative-control intervention: permute q across tokens (quality-randomized control) so the same multiplier distribution is applied to the WRONG tokens — the mechanism predicts the downstream validation-loss recovery and OLMES gain COLLAPSE to the plain-decayed level (the Popper test is the downstream task metric moving, not p_t's own value), while the compute-matched control (plain decayed run with η_t globally scaled to match total effective compute) likewise fails to recover the advantage. Positive control: a stripped-down variant that applies the multiplier ONLY to the top-quartile-q tokens (and η_t unchanged elsewhere) should recover most of the downstream effect, identifying the high-quality minority as the load-bearing partition.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:6840c3ec7e97b2c7c65b2b989634ac83f9827d91","delta":"They diagnose the LR-as-importance-weight coupling and mitigate by adjusting the DATA schedule (moving where high-quality data lands under a still-fixed decreasing η_t), explicitly concluding the underlying conflict persists; we construct a per-token effective step size η_eff(t,x)=η_t·m(q(x),t) that recovers the decay deficit for high-quality tokens IN PLACE, decoupling effective weight from position without rearranging data, and bound the recovery with a signal/noise decomposition they do not derive."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:aa148ef5239b31d2d854e6a3cf2c23ea377bf29d","delta":"Preference Curriculum reschedules WHICH data the model trains on per stage via a perplexity-difference metric but still rides the global LR curve; we change the effective UPDATE WEIGHT a chosen token receives rather than which token is presented, so our late preferred tokens are not re-subjected to late-stage decay."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W6979357895","delta":"The Multi-Power Law optimizes the global LR-schedule SHAPE for aggregate loss over a corpus treated as homogeneous; we make the effective step a function of per-token quality, expressing an alignment between where update weight is spent and where valuable tokens are that their data-agnostic law cannot represent."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7105650309","delta":"MILES sets a per-MODALITY learning rate to balance multimodal overfitting (partition by modality, a coarse fixed group); we partition a single text stream by continuous per-token quality and tie the effective step to the schedule's own decay deficit, a token-resolution quality-conditioned step that their modality-level scheduler does not provide."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:6840c3ec7e97b2c7c65b2b989634ac83f9827d91","what_step_was_missed":"The seed paper constructs the diagnosis (η_t is an implicit per-sample importance weight) and one cure family — rearranging the data schedule so high-quality data avoids the deepest decay — but to make the curriculum's constant-LR advantage survive a decaying schedule it would have needed to construct a per-token effective-step modulation that recovers exactly the decay deficit (η_peak/η_t − 1) for high-quality tokens, together with the signal/noise decomposition bounding that this recovers the advantage WITHOUT reintroducing the late-training noise decay suppresses. It never builds that decoupling of effective weight from training position; its own method section states the data-schedule cure leaves the conflict in place, which is precisely the construction we supply."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":351,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"No hard-floor fired (gap_closure_reject_check is borderline not triggered; anti_pattern_check matched_pattern_id is null; paper_pointed_threat is NOT exact-mechanism overlap and is addressable). The collision surfaced ADAPT (collision_hits), whose adaptive per-sample quality-driven learning rate overlaps the candidate's mechanism axis on a load-bearing property, and paper_pointed_threat.addressable_via names specific candidate fields (falsification_prediction baseline + differentiation_from_lit) that must change to make the decay-deficit coupling the load-bearing differentiator — so per the 'choose revise when paper_pointed_threat exists AND addressable_via names a specific candidate field' heuristic, the verdict is revise, not advance.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces an effective per-token update weight whose distribution over the training stream can be made to track token quality, rather than being forced to monotonically decrease with training-time position — so the high-quality tokens placed late under a curriculum cannot recover the update weight the LR decay strips from them (additive need at the frontier-leaf residual of semanticscholar:6840c3ec7e97b2c7c65b2b989634ac83f9827d91).","main_pattern":"heterogeneous_decomposition","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is treating the partition criterion itself as the contribution while leaving its value unproven, so reviewers map the discriminator onto an established technique and read the differentiated treatment as relabeling; compounded by not benchmarking against both the strongest uniform baseline and the obvious cheap alternative, and by validating where the bottleneck does not bite.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Presenting a sensitivity or redundancy proxy as the novelty invites the verdict that it rediscovers known mixed-precision or low-rank results unless it is sharply differentiated from the obvious prior criterion.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The partition criterion (per-token DCLM quality score) is reused from the existing curriculum, NOT presented as the novelty — the novelty is the schedule-deficit-coupled effective-step treatment — but the candidate must keep the differentiation from a generic adaptive-per-sample-LR (ADAPT) sharp or it risks this read."},{"lesson_quoted":"Omitting comparison against both the strongest uniform baseline and the obvious cheap alternative (SVD/PCA, structured dropout, a natively trained smaller model) leaves reviewers unable to tell whether the partition buys anything at all.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism_steps include the compute-matched uniform-up-weight control (step 7) and the quality-randomized control (step 8) plus the constant-LR-curriculum upper bound, so both the strongest uniform and the obvious cheap alternative are benchmarked."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a storage or throughput claim only on toy-scale models — where the compression bottleneck does not actually bite — undermines the entire motivation no matter how clean the method is.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Validation is at DCLM 1B-1x / Qwen2.5-1.5B / 30B tokens — the exact substantial scale where the seed paper showed the curriculum-vs-decay conflict bites, not a toy regime."},{"lesson_quoted":"Skipping any analysis of why the heterogeneity exists — the data or value distribution that drives the partition — makes the technical novelty and the potential impact impossible to assess.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The signal/noise decomposition and the quality-gradient-alignment argument supply why high-vs-low-quality tokens differ in signal-direction contribution, which is the value distribution driving the partition."},{"lesson_quoted":"Bolting together established components (distillation plus pruning plus calibration) without an error bound or artifact specific to the new setting reads as incremental even when the target application is timely and important.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate supplies a setting-specific artifact (the decay-deficit-coupled multiplier m and its signal/noise recovery bound), not a bundle of off-the-shelf components."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions whether the LR schedule must be a single global function of training-time position shared by every token regardless of that token's quality — every curriculum-for-pretraining and LR-schedule leaf silently inherits this from the shared ancestor (a global iteration-indexed LR curve), tuning either the data order or the curve shape but never asking whether the effective weight a token receives should be decoupled from when in training it happens to appear (subtractive: the unasked question opened off the shared interior node n2).","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C29 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The dominant failure is a relaxed assumption that is technically valid but uncharacterized (no named class shown to satisfy it), or a re-derived rate that merely matches the baseline with near-identical changes, or hidden constants that explode at the advertised limit; compounded by a single-toy-instance empirical anchor.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A weakened assumption that no known function class is shown to satisfy reads as engineered to close the proof, not as a genuine generalization — characterize when it holds or it sinks the paper.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"This leg VIOLATES (not relaxes) the position-locked-weight assumption and validates the violation empirically via the companion controlled_diagnostic_design separation, so there is no relaxed-but-uncharacterized analytical condition to defend."},{"lesson_quoted":"Re-deriving a rate that merely matches the baseline with near-identical algorithmic changes is read as an incremental extension, however clean the analysis.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The deliverable here is not a re-derived convergence rate but an empirically-confirmed recovery of the curriculum advantage; the C29 framing is used for the assumption-audit identity, with the empirical artifact owned by the companion, so the rate-matching failure does not apply."},{"lesson_quoted":"An assumption-relaxation validated only on a single toy instance gives no evidence the relaxation captures the motivating practical regime.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Validation is at the seed's 1B-1x/30B-token practical regime with multiple controls and an α × decay-aggressiveness sweep, not a single toy instance."}],"verdict":"clear"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The anchor heterogeneous_decomposition/C04 entry is borderline on one lesson — the risk that the per-token-quality partition reads as a relabeled adaptive-per-sample-LR unless sharply differentiated from the obvious adaptive-LR prior (ADAPT) — while every other lesson across both entries is clear (controls, scale, and a setting-specific error bound are present). The audit leg (C29) is fully clear."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces an effective per-token update weight whose distribution over the training stream can be made to track token quality, rather than being forced to monotonically decrease with training-time position — so the high-quality tokens placed late under a curriculum cannot recover the update weight the LR decay strips from them (additive need at the frontier-leaf residual of semanticscholar:6840c3ec7e97b2c7c65b2b989634ac83f9827d91).","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Discriminate components by a magnitude/sensitivity/influence/redundancy criterion into a high-impact minority and a near-redundant bulk, then apply a differentiated treatment to each, with the load-bearing artifact being an error/sensitivity decomposition that bounds how the differentiated treatment recovers the original objective.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism partitions the token stream by per-token quality q(x) into a high-quality minority and a bulk, applies a differentiated effective step size (protect/up-weight the minority's effective step by the decay deficit while the bulk keeps the suppressed step), and supplies the signal/noise decomposition bounding the recovered validation-loss advantage — the C04 signature partition+differentiated-treatment+error-decomposition move is performed, not just the parent's generic 'decompose heterogeneity' gist.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions whether the LR schedule must be a single global function of training-time position shared by every token regardless of that token's quality — every curriculum-for-pretraining and LR-schedule leaf silently inherits this from the shared ancestor (a global iteration-indexed LR curve), tuning either the data order or the curve shape but never asking whether the effective weight a token receives should be decoupled from when in training it happens to appear (subtractive: the unasked question opened off the shared interior node n2).","sub_pattern":"C29 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Audit a load-bearing assumption of an iterative training/optimization procedure (here: that a token's effective update weight is forced to equal the global position-indexed η_t), show it is binding, and pivot by violating it, keeping the procedure otherwise fixed.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism names the assumption (w(t,x) must equal global η_t), shows it binding via the seed's own Long/Mid/Short/Zero decay sweep (advantage present at constant LR, monotonically erased with decay), and violates it via η_eff while holding the rest of training fixed; the companion controlled_diagnostic_design then ships the confound-isolating separation — the audit-pivot signature move is present.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries perform their cited cluster's signature move: C04's partition + differentiated-treatment + error-decomposition is in core_mechanism (not just a generic decompose), and C29's name-bind-violate audit on the position-locked-weight assumption is explicit with the companion supplying the empirical deliverable."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["heterogeneous_decomposition","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"The only 2-way subset is heterogeneous_decomposition + assumption_audit_and_pivot, which is NOT one of the three flagged compositions (audit_decomp_supervisor/prior/operator all pair heterogeneous_decomposition with self_supervised_signal_engineering / structural_prior_encoding / architectural_operator_substitution); the companion controlled_diagnostic_design is a deliverable companion, not a main_pattern in composition_set."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"ADAPT: Rethinking Data Curation in LLM Training: Online Reweighting Offers Better Generalization than Offline Methods (collision_hits, 2026)","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"ADAPT reweights training samples with adaptive per-sample learning rates guided by similarity-based quality signals, acting as an implicit curriculum learner — this overlaps the candidate's mechanism axis (a quality-conditioned per-token effective learning rate). The candidate stands or falls on whether its move is more than a special case of ADAPT's adaptive per-sample LR: the candidate's distinctive content is that the multiplier is tied to the SCHEDULE'S OWN DECAY DEFICIT (η_peak/η_t − 1) and gated to the decay phase specifically to RECOVER the curriculum advantage that LR decay strips from late high-quality tokens — i.e. it engages the LR-decay-vs-curriculum coupling the seed paper identified, whereas ADAPT is a general online-curation reweighter with no notion of the LR schedule's decay shape and no claim about recovering a decay-induced curriculum collapse. The threat is real but not exact-mechanism overlap: ADAPT's adaptive per-sample LR is quality-driven but position/schedule-agnostic, so the candidate's decay-deficit coupling and the late-stage-recovery claim are not subsumed — provided the candidate makes that delta load-bearing and includes ADAPT-style generic adaptive-per-sample-LR as a baseline its mechanism must beat on the specific curriculum-under-decay regime.","addressable_via":"Add ADAPT (generic adaptive per-sample LR from similarity-based quality) as an explicit baseline run in core_mechanism_steps (the existing quality-randomized control in the kill-switch-locked falsification_prediction already supplies the isolating falsifier, so that field is not edited), and sharpen differentiation_from_lit + core_mechanism to state that ADAPT's reweight is schedule-agnostic while the candidate's multiplier is the decay-deficit (η_peak/η_t − 1) gated to the decay phase, so only the candidate recovers the decay-induced curriculum collapse."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat: ADAPT (adaptive per-sample LR from similarity-based quality) overlaps the candidate's quality-conditioned per-token effective step size on a load-bearing axis.","fix_direction":"Add an entry for ADAPT explicitly stating the delta: ADAPT's per-sample adaptive LR is schedule-agnostic and aims at online curation/generalization, with no coupling to the LR-decay curve; the candidate's multiplier is exactly the schedule's decay deficit (η_peak/η_t − 1) gated to the decay phase, uniquely recovering the curriculum advantage that LR DECAY strips from late high-quality tokens (a phenomenon ADAPT neither models nor targets)."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","issue":"The decay-deficit coupling must be made the explicit load-bearing differentiator vs a generic adaptive-per-sample-LR, so the contribution does not read as a special case of ADAPT.","fix_direction":"In core_mechanism, add one sentence that the load-bearing distinction from a generic quality-driven adaptive per-sample LR (e.g. ADAPT) is the decay-deficit coupling (η_peak/η_t − 1) and the decay-phase gate s(t): only this coupling targets the LR-decay-induced curriculum collapse, whereas a schedule-agnostic quality LR does not."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism_steps","issue":"An ADAPT-style generic quality-driven adaptive-per-sample-LR baseline must be in the experimental plan so the existing quality-randomized / compute-matched controls in falsification_prediction can attribute the recovery to the decay-deficit coupling specifically. (NOTE: falsification_prediction itself is kill-switch-locked and must NOT be edited; the existing quality-randomized control there already supplies the isolating falsifier — this target only adds the named baseline run to the build plan.)","fix_direction":"Insert a step training an ADAPT-style baseline (per-token multiplier from q(x) but with the decay-deficit coupling and decay-phase gate REMOVED — i.e. a constant or schedule-agnostic quality multiplier) under the same curriculum+WSD-decay setup, and report its recovered fraction of the constant-LR curriculum advantage alongside the decoupled run, so the comparison isolates the decay-deficit coupling. Do not modify falsification_prediction or compute_budget."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit[]","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added an ADAPT entry stating ADAPT's adaptive per-sample LR is schedule-agnostic online curation while the candidate's multiplier is the LR-decay deficit (η_peak/η_t − 1) gated to the decay phase, uniquely recovering the decay-induced curriculum collapse."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added one sentence naming the decay-deficit coupling + decay-phase gate as the load-bearing distinction from a generic quality-driven adaptive per-sample LR (ADAPT)."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism_steps","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Inserted a build step training an ADAPT-style schedule-agnostic quality-multiplier baseline (decay-deficit coupling + gate removed) and reporting its recovered fraction alongside the decoupled run; falsification_prediction and compute_budget left byte-identical."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Quality-Conditioned Effective Step Size: Decoupling Update Weight from Training Position in Curriculum Pretraining\n\n**Method.** Quality-Conditioned Effective Step Size (QC-ESS)\n\n## Motivation\nWhen people pretrain a large language model (LLM), they often use a curriculum: feed the model lower-quality text first and save the best text for late in training. On its own this beats feeding text in random order. But almost every modern run also uses a decaying learning rate (LR) — the step size $\\eta _{t}$ shrinks over time to quiet down noisy late-training updates. The problem: the step size also acts as a hidden 'importance weight' on each token. So the best text, which the curriculum deliberately saves for last, lands exactly where the step size is tiniest and barely moves the model. The curriculum's whole advantage gets cancelled. The seed paper that named this problem (arXiv 2025-11) showed it clearly but only tried to fix it by rearranging WHICH data comes when — and even said the underlying conflict still remains. Other recent work either reshuffles the data (Preference Curriculum, ACL 2025) or tunes the LR curve while pretending all text is equally valuable (Multi-Power Law, arXiv 2025-03); none of them gives a late high-quality token back the update weight the decay took away. What is newly possible: every curriculum pipeline already computes a per-token quality score, and the seed's small-scale setup (a 1B-1x model on 30 billion tokens) is cheap to reproduce, so the missing piece — a per-token update weight that follows quality instead of timing — can finally be built and tested. If we close this gap, you can keep the decaying LR's noise suppression AND let the curriculum actually spend learning capacity on its best late tokens, instead of throwing that gain away on every decayed run.\n\n## Method\n### Background: testbed and quality signal\n*Reproduce the curriculum-vs-decay collapse and reuse the existing per-token quality score as the partition criterion.*\n\n1. Recreate the known failure in the seed paper's exact setup: a 1.5B-parameter Qwen2.5 model (DCLM 1B-1x scale) trained on a 30-billion-token slice of the DCLM-Baseline corpus, using the corpus's existing fasttext quality scores. Make the ascending-quality curriculum by sorting documents from lowest to highest quality score, grouping them into ten equal-size buckets fed in order (shuffling within each bucket so topics don't clump). Train three reference runs — random order with a constant learning rate (LR), curriculum with a constant LR, and curriculum with a decaying LR (the warmup-stable-decay, WSD, schedule) — so you can see the curriculum's advantage appear under a constant LR and then disappear under decay.\n   - _Why_: You can only claim to recover an advantage if you first measure it and its collapse on the same testbed.\n2. Attach a quality number q(x) between 0 and 1 to every token, with no new model. Take each token's source-document fasttext quality score, rank all documents by that score, and map each rank onto the (0,1) interval (rank-normalization) so the lowest-quality document is near 0 and the highest near 1; all tokens from one document share its value. Store this as a simple array indexed by token position that lines up with the training data shards. Crucially this is the very same quality score the curriculum in Step step 1 (Recreate the known failure in $the\\dots )$ already uses, so you are not inventing a new scorer.\n   - _Why_: The quality signal should be the same one the curriculum uses, so the novelty is in how tokens are treated, not in inventing a new scorer.\n\n### Quality-conditioned effective step\n*Return the LR-decay deficit to high-quality tokens in place via a per-token gradient multiplier gated to the decay phase.*\n\n3. Inside the training loss, give each token its own effective learning rate (LR) by weighting its loss before averaging. Compute the per-token cross-entropy loss WITHOUT averaging, multiply token i's loss by the multiplier $m(q_{i},t)=1+\\alpha \\cdot q_{i}\\cdot (\\eta _{peak}/\\eta _{t}- 1)\\cdot s(t)$ (with $\\alpha =0.5$ by default, $\\eta _{peak}$ the peak LR, $\\eta _{t}$ the current LR, s(t) the on/off switch from Step step 4 (Switch the quality boost on $only\\dots )),$ then average to the batch loss as usual. Because the gradient of a weighted sum is the weighted sum of gradients, this exactly scales how much each token moves the model — handing a high-quality token back the extra step size that decay took away — and the optimizer (Adam) needs no change. Floor $\\eta _{t}$ at a tiny 1e-8 so the division never blows up at the end of training.\n\n*The standard decayed update, under which the seed's analysis shows $\\eta _{t}$ is the implicit per-token update weight w(t,x), forced to be position-locked and quality-independent.*\n$$ \\theta_{t+1} = \\theta_t - \\eta_t\\, g_t, \\qquad w(t,x) \\equiv \\eta_t \\tag{1} $$\n\n\n*The quality-conditioned effective step size: the multiplier m returns the decay deficit $(\\eta _{peak}/\\eta _{t} - $ 1) to a token in proportion to its quality q, scaled by bridge hyperparameter $\\alpha $ and gated to the decay phase by s(t).*\n$$ \\eta_{\\mathrm{eff}}(t,x) = \\eta_t\\, m\\big(q(x),t\\big), \\qquad m(q,t) = 1 + \\alpha\\, q\\, \\Big(\\tfrac{\\eta_{\\mathrm{peak}}}{\\eta_t} - 1\\Big)\\, s(t) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This hands high-quality tokens back exactly the step-size deficit the decay carved out, so their updates count again.\n4. Switch the quality boost on only during the part of training where the learning rate is actually decaying. Set the switch s(t)=1 from the step where the schedule leaves its stable plateau and begins decaying onward, and s(t)=0 before that (during warmup and the flat plateau); for a cosine schedule with no plateau, turn it on right after warmup. You don't pick a new number here — the boundary is just wherever the baseline schedule already starts decaying — so the fix acts only where decay removes weight and leaves the rest of training alone.\n\n*The stability gate turns the recovery on only inside the decay phase where decay strips weight, and off during warmup/plateau so the noise-suppression schedule is otherwise untouched.*\n$$ s(t) = \\begin{cases} 1 & t \\text{ in the WSD decay phase} \\\\ 0 & t \\text{ in warmup or stable plateau} \\end{cases} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Decay only strips weight late, so the fix should act only there and leave the noise-quieting schedule otherwise untouched.\n\n### Recovery measurement and bound\n*Measure the recovered curriculum advantage and bound it with the signal/noise decomposition and the projection $p_{t}.$*\n\n5. Run the full method — curriculum plus decaying LR plus the quality-conditioned effective step at $\\alpha =0.5$ — and measure how good the model gets. For the high-quality validation loss, set aside ahead of time a fixed batch of top-10%-quality documents that the model never trains on, and report its average per-token loss. Also report the standard OLMES Core benchmark suite (MMLU, ARC, CSQA) in its usual few-shot setting. Measure not just at the end but at regular checkpoints (say every 10% of training) so you can plot the curve next to the three baselines from Step step 1 (Recreate the known failure in $the\\dots ).$\n   - _Why_: This is the headline test: does re-weighting tokens in place recover what the constant-LR curriculum had?\n6. Watch the mechanism work by tracking, at every step, how aligned the model's update on high-quality tokens is with the direction that improves the held-out high-quality data — the cosine $p_{t}$ between the high-quality minibatch gradient and a running average of the high-quality validation gradient. The claim is that with the multiplier on, $p_{t}$ stays high late in training, whereas in a plain decayed run it collapses. You also want a formula saying how much of the advantage the boost $\\alpha $ should recover as a function of this alignment. 【author decision: pick the gradient-noise model (e.g. simple additive bounded noise versus a heavier-tailed one) and the exact alignment measure that go into that recovery formula — its shape and how tight it is depend on this choice.】\n\n*The signal/noise decomposition: m raises the signal-direction step $E[g_{t}]$ for high-quality tokens by the recovered factor while the bulk's noise $\\epsilon _{t}$ stays suppressed by the small $\\eta _{t}$; $p_{t}$ is the late-training signal-direction projection that the mechanism keeps high where the decayed baseline's collapses.*\n$$ g_t = \\mathbb{E}[g_t] + \\varepsilon_t, \\qquad p_t = \\cos\\!\\big(g_t^{\\mathrm{hq}},\\, \\bar{g}^{\\mathrm{val,hq}}\\big) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: It shows the mechanism is doing what it claims — keeping high-quality tokens pointed in the useful direction late in training.\n\n### Confound isolation and recovery mapping\n*Attribute the recovery to the decay-deficit decoupling via four controls and map it across $\\alpha $ and decay strength.*\n\n7. Run four control experiments that each remove one alternative explanation. (1) Compute-matched: take the average multiplier value over the whole decoupled run and scale a plain decayed run's learning rate up by that single number, so it spends the same total step budget — this checks the gain isn't just from training 'hotter'. (2) Quality-randomized: shuffle which token gets which multiplier (same set of multipliers, wrong tokens) — this checks the gain comes from targeting good tokens, not from the multipliers' mere spread. (3) Adam-pathway: rerun with plain SGD instead of Adam — this checks the gain isn't a quirk of Adam's internal scaling. (4) Schedule-agnostic (ADAPT-style) baseline: use a multiplier $1+\\alpha \\cdot q$ that depends only on quality and is applied throughout training (no decay-deficit term, no on/off switch) — this is the generic adaptive quality reweighter the method must beat. Report how much of the constant-LR advantage each control recovers.\n   - _Why_: These rule out the alternative explanations (more compute, the quality signal alone, an Adam quirk, a generic quality reweight) so any leftover gain is due to the decay-deficit decoupling specifically.\n8. Map where the fix helps most by sweeping two knobs on a cheaper 10-billion-token version of the setup (same model and data, schedule re-scaled to the smaller budget): the boost strength $\\alpha $ over {0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1.0} and the decay aggressiveness over the seed's four settings (Long, Mid, Short, Zero). For each combination report the recovered fraction — how much of the gap between the plain-decay-curriculum run and the constant-LR-curriculum upper bound the method closes on the high-quality validation loss. Then give the headline full 30-billion-token numbers (recovered fraction and net gain over curriculum-plus-decay) alongside all four controls, forming the final table a reviewer needs.\n   - _Why_: It maps where the fix helps most and assembles the table a reviewer needs to judge whether the partition buys anything.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 质量条件化有效步长：在课程预训练中将更新权重与训练位置解耦\n\n**方法名称.** Quality-Conditioned Effective Step Size (QC-ESS)\n\n## 研究动机\n在预训练大语言模型（LLM）时，人们常用课程（curriculum）策略：先喂质量较低的文本，把最好的文本留到训练后期。单看这一招，它比随机顺序喂数据更好。但几乎所有现代训练同时还用衰减学习率（LR）——步长 $\\eta _{t}$ 随训练逐渐变小，以压住后期更新里的噪声。问题在于：步长同时充当了每个token的隐式“重要性权重”。于是课程特意留到最后的最优文本，恰好落在步长最小的地方，几乎推不动模型，课程的全部优势就被抵消了。最早点出这个问题的seed论文（arXiv 2025-11）讲得很清楚，但它只尝试通过重排“哪些数据何时出现”来缓解，而且自己也承认底层冲突依然存在。其他近期工作要么重排数据（Preference Curriculum, ACL 2025），要么在把所有文本当作同等价值的前提下调LR曲线（Multi-Power Law, arXiv 2025-03）；没有一个能把衰减夺走的更新权重还给后期的高质量token。如今新具备的条件是：每条课程流水线本来就已经算好了每个token的质量分数，而且seed的小规模设置（1B-1x 模型、300亿 token）很容易复现，所以缺失的那一环——一个跟随质量而非时间的每token更新权重——终于可以构建并验证。一旦补上这个缺口，你就能既保留衰减LR的降噪作用，又让课程真正把学习容量花在后期的最优token上，而不是在每次衰减训练中白白丢掉这份收益。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景：测试台与质量信号\n*复现课程-衰减坍塌，并复用已有的每token质量分数作为划分依据。*\n\n1. 在 seed 论文的原始设置里复现这一已知失败：用一个 1.5B 参数的 Qwen2.5 模型（DCLM 1B-1x 规模），在 DCLM-Baseline 语料的 30B token 切片上训练，沿用语料已有的 fasttext 质量分数。课程（curriculum）这样构建：按质量分数从低到高排序文档，分成十个等 token 量的桶依次喂入，桶内打乱以避免话题扎堆。训练三个参照run——随机顺序+常数学习率(Learning Rate, LR)、课程+常数LR、课程+衰减LR（即 warmup-stable-decay, WSD 调度）——这样就能看到课程的优势在常数LR下出现、又在衰减下消失。\n   - _为什么_: 只有先在同一测试台上测出优势及其坍塌，才能声称把它恢复了。\n2. 给每个 token 贴一个 0 到 1 之间的质量值 q(x)，且不引入新模型。取每个 token 所属文档的 fasttext 质量分数，把所有文档按分数排名，再把名次映射到 (0,1) 区间（即 rank-normalization 排名归一化），使最低质量文档接近 0、最高接近 1；同一文档的所有 token 共用一个值。把它存成一个按 token 位置索引、且与训练数据 shard 顺序对齐的数组。关键是：这就是 Step 第1步（在 seed 论文的原始设置$\\dots $） 中课程已经在用的同一个质量分数，所以你没有发明新的打分器。\n   - _为什么_: 质量信号要和课程用的同一个，这样新颖性在于如何处理token，而不是发明新打分器。\n\n### 质量条件化有效步长\n*通过门控到衰减阶段的每token梯度乘子，就地把LR衰减亏空还给高质量token。*\n\n3. 在训练损失里，通过在求平均前给每个 token 的损失加权，给它一个专属的有效学习率(Learning Rate, LR)。先算出不求平均的逐 token 交叉熵损失，把第 i 个 token 的损失乘以乘子 $m(q_{i},t)=1+\\alpha \\cdot q_{i}\\cdot (\\eta _{peak}/\\eta _{t}- 1)\\cdot s(t)$（默认 $\\alpha =0.5$，$\\eta _{peak}$ 为峰值 LR，$\\eta _{t}$ 为当前 LR，s(t) 是来自 Step 第4步（只在学习率真正衰减的训练阶段$\\dots $） 的开关），再照常平均成 batch 损失。由于加权和的梯度等于梯度的加权和，这恰好缩放了每个 token 对模型的推动力——把衰减夺走的额外步长还给高质量 token——而优化器 Adam 无需任何改动。给 $\\eta _{t}$ 设一个极小的下限 1e-8，使训练末尾的除法不会爆掉。\n\n*标准的衰减更新公式；按照seed的分析，$\\eta _{t}$ 就是隐式的每token更新权重 w(t,x)，被锁定为只随位置变化、与质量无关。*\n$$ \\theta_{t+1} = \\theta_t - \\eta_t\\, g_t, \\qquad w(t,x) \\equiv \\eta_t \\tag{1} $$\n\n\n*质量条件化的有效步长：乘子 m 按token的质量 q、桥接超参数 $\\alpha $ 和衰减阶段门控 s(t)，把衰减亏空 $(\\eta _{peak}/\\eta _{t} - $ 1) 归还给该token。*\n$$ \\eta_{\\mathrm{eff}}(t,x) = \\eta_t\\, m\\big(q(x),t\\big), \\qquad m(q,t) = 1 + \\alpha\\, q\\, \\Big(\\tfrac{\\eta_{\\mathrm{peak}}}{\\eta_t} - 1\\Big)\\, s(t) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这把衰减挖走的步长亏空精确地还给高质量token，让它们的更新重新算数。\n4. 只在学习率真正衰减的训练阶段打开质量增益。把开关 s(t) 设为：从调度离开稳定平台、开始衰减的那一步起为 1，在那之前（warmup 和平坦平台阶段）为 0；对于没有平台的 cosine 调度，就在 warmup 结束后立即打开。这里你不需要选新数字——边界就是基线调度本来开始衰减的地方——所以修复只作用在衰减夺走权重的区段，其余训练保持不变。\n\n*稳定性门控只在衰减阶段（decay会剥夺权重的地方）开启恢复，在warmup/平台阶段关闭，从而不改动其余的降噪调度。*\n$$ s(t) = \\begin{cases} 1 & t \\text{ in the WSD decay phase} \\\\ 0 & t \\text{ in warmup or stable plateau} \\end{cases} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 衰减只在后期剥夺权重，所以修复也只在那里起作用，其余的降噪调度保持不变。\n\n### 恢复的测量与界\n*测量恢复的课程优势，并用信号/噪声分解和投影 $p_{t}$ 给出界。*\n\n5. 运行完整方法——课程 + 衰减 LR $+ \\alpha =0.5$ 的质量条件化有效步长——并测量模型变得多好。对于高质量验证损失，提前留出一批固定的、前 10% 质量的文档（模型永不训练它们），报告其平均逐 token 损失。同时按常规 few-shot 设置报告标准的 OLMES Core 基准套件（MMLU、ARC、CSQA）。不仅在结束时测，还在固定的中间检查点（比如每训练 10%）测，以便把曲线和 Step 第1步（在 seed 论文的原始设置$\\dots $） 的三个基线画在一起对比。\n   - _为什么_: 这是头条测试：就地重新加权token，能否恢复常数LR课程曾有的优势？\n6. 通过在每一步追踪模型在高质量 token 上的更新与“改善留出高质量数据的方向”有多对齐，来观察机制是否在起作用——即高质量 minibatch 梯度与高质量验证梯度滑动平均之间的余弦 $p_{t}$。论断是：开启乘子后，$p_{t}$ 在训练后期保持较高，而普通衰减run中它会坍塌。你还需要一个公式，说明增益 $\\alpha $ 作为这种对齐的函数应恢复多少优势。【作者需决定：选定进入该恢复公式的梯度噪声模型（例如简单的加性有界噪声还是更重尾的模型）以及确切的对齐统计量——公式的形态及其紧致程度取决于此选择。】\n\n*信号/噪声分解：m 按恢复因子提升高质量token的信号方向步长 $E[g_{t}]$，而bulk的噪声 $\\epsilon _{t}$ 仍被小的 $\\eta _{t}$ 抑制；$p_{t}$ 是训练后期的信号方向投影，机制让它在衰减基线坍塌处仍保持较高。*\n$$ g_t = \\mathbb{E}[g_t] + \\varepsilon_t, \\qquad p_t = \\cos\\!\\big(g_t^{\\mathrm{hq}},\\, \\bar{g}^{\\mathrm{val,hq}}\\big) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 它表明机制确实在做它声称的事——让高质量token在训练后期仍指向有用方向。\n\n### 混杂隔离与恢复刻画\n*用四个对照把恢复归因于衰减亏空解耦，并在 $\\alpha $ 与衰减强度上刻画它。*\n\n7. 运行四个对照实验，每个都排除一种替代解释。(1) compute-matched 算力匹配：取整个解耦run中乘子的平均值，用这一个数把普通衰减run的学习率整体放大，使其花费相同的总步长预算——以此检验收益不只是来自训练得“更猛”。(2) quality-randomized 质量随机化：打乱哪个 token 拿到哪个乘子（乘子集合相同，token 对错）——以此检验收益来自瞄准好 token，而非乘子本身的分布。(3) Adam-pathway：改用普通 SGD 而非 Adam 重跑——以此检验收益不是 Adam 内部缩放的副作用。(4) schedule-agnostic（ADAPT 式）基线：用一个只依赖质量、全程施加的乘子 $1+\\alpha \\cdot q$（没有衰减亏空项、没有开关）——这就是方法必须胜过的通用自适应质量重加权器。报告每个对照恢复了多少常数LR优势。\n   - _为什么_: 这些排除了替代解释（更多算力、单纯的质量信号、Adam的小怪癖、通用的质量重加权），从而把剩余收益归因于衰减亏空解耦本身。\n8. 通过在一个更便宜的 100 亿 token 版本设置上（同样的模型和数据，调度按更小预算重新缩放）扫两个旋钮，刻画修复在哪里最有效：增益强度 $\\alpha $ 取 {0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1.0}，衰减强度取 seed 的四档（Long、Mid、Short、Zero）。对每个组合报告恢复比例——即在高质量验证损失上，方法把“普通衰减+课程run”与“常数LR+课程上界”之间的差距填补了多少。然后给出头条的完整 300 亿 token 数字（恢复比例及相对课程+衰减的净增益），连同全部四个对照，构成审稿人需要的最终表格。\n   - _为什么_: 它刻画出修复在哪里最有效，并组装出审稿人判断这个划分是否值得的表格。\n\n"},{"id":"59","run_dir":"run_prompt59_microbench","index":59,"title":"Pair-Conditional Sequential Micro-Benchmarking with Anytime-Valid Reliability Certificates","title_zh":"面向模型对的序贯式微基准评测：带 anytime-valid 可靠性凭证","method_name":"SPRINT (Sequential Pair-conditional Reliable mIcro-beNchmarking via anytime-valid Testing)","hook":"We show that a micro-benchmark which fixes its example set before knowing the two models being compared is provably making an unforced error: recasting each pairwise comparison as a fixed-confidence sequential test that draws IRT-weighted items only until an anytime-valid confidence boundary is crossed lets the SAME budget either certify a verdict or abstain — so that, at 25 MMLU-Pro examples where a static subset leaves 51% of 8B-model pairs unreliable (semanticscholar:e81984228dccf08fe7eaa637cb47951e7cd7269b), the sequential evaluator instead spends a pair-dependent number of items and emits a verdict that is correct-or-abstain with guaranteed error control. The non-obvious reveal: averaged over pairs the sequential evaluator uses FEWER items than the static subset needs to reach the same fleet-wide reliability, because easy pairs stop early and free budget for the hard close pairs that the static subset silently mis-ranks.","anchor_pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","anchor_pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","domain_category":"LLM Evaluation & Benchmarking","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a micro-benchmark verdict that carries its own reliability for the specific model pair being compared: every method (anchor MDAD diagnostic, openalex:W4413110341 bias-bounded selection, openalex:W7091187661 compression) emits a ranking from a pre-committed subset without telling the user whether that subset actually resolves THIS pair's gap or has silently fallen below its detectable threshold — the missing outcome is a comparison that knows when it is unreliable.","pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by reframing the pairwise model comparison as a measurement over a well-studied object — a fixed-confidence sequential hypothesis test on the sign of the per-item accuracy difference — whose native correctness criterion (anytime-valid Type-I error control) IS the per-pair reliability certificate, so the verdict is emitted with a soundness proof that it resolves THIS pair or it abstains.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf treats the example budget as something to be spent under a stopping rule rather than fixed in advance: the anchor's MDAD reports a single fixed-size detectable threshold and openalex:W7091187661/openalex:W4413110341 fix the budget before evaluation, so the unmet need is a way to spend exactly as many examples as a given comparison requires to reach a target confidence and no more — sequential allocation of the evaluation budget per comparison is absent.","pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by the SAME object's stopping rule: the sequential test's anytime-valid boundary is exactly a budget allocator that draws IRT-discrimination-ordered items one (mini-batch) at a time and halts at the first crossing, so the number of items spent is the test's sample complexity for THIS pair — many for close pairs, few for far pairs — rather than a pre-fixed size.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"language-model evaluation / benchmark reliability (micro-benchmarking: predicting full-benchmark judgments from a small evaluated subset)","n_papers":39,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":25},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":12,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"VLKEB: A Large Vision-Language Model Knowledge Editing Benchmark"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"CheckEval: Robust Evaluation Framework using Large Language Model via Checklist"},{"source":"openalex","title":"A Survey on Hallucination in Large Language Models: Principles, Taxonomy, Challenges, and Open Questions"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Knowledge Graphs, Large Language Models, and Hallucinations: An NLP Perspective"},{"source":"openalex","title":"GSM-Symbolic: Understanding the Limitations of Mathematical Reasoning in Large Language Models"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Medical Graph RAG: Towards Safe Medical Large Language Model via Graph Retrieval-Augmented Generation"}],"more":6},{"year":2025,"n":26,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Towards Inclusive Arabic LLMs: A Culturally Aligned Benchmark in Arabic Large Language Model Evaluation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"DSDrive: Distilling Large Language Model for Lightweight End-to-End Autonomous Driving with Unified Reasoning and Planning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"AgriGPT: a Large Language Model Ecosystem for Agriculture"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"On Robustness and Reliability of Benchmark-Based Evaluation of LLMs"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"OralGPT-Omni: A Versatile Dental Multimodal Large Language Model"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"SoK: Large Language Model Copyright Auditing via Fingerprinting"}],"more":20},{"year":2026,"n":1,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"}],"more":0}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":20,"share":0.513},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":12,"share":0.308},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":8,"share":0.205},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":6,"share":0.154},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":5,"share":0.128},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":5,"share":0.128},{"pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","count":4,"share":0.103},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":3,"share":0.077}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Micro-benchmarking selects a single small subset once, globally, and then reuses it to rank every pair of models; but the source paper (semanticscholar:e81984228dccf08fe7eaa637cb47951e7cd7269b) shows with its MDAD measure that for any fixed subset there is a minimum detectable ability difference below which pairwise rankings are not preserved, and that for close model pairs (e.g. 25 examples from MMLU-Pro leaves 51% of 8B-model comparisons unreliable) a static globally-selected subset is no better than random. The structural failure is that a single globally-chosen subset commits to one operating point of the size-vs-resolution trade-off before it knows which two models are being compared, so when a query pair's true gap falls below that subset's detectable threshold the comparison silently returns an unreliable verdict with no signal that it has done so — and methods that try to fix this by selecting a 'better' static subset (Anchor Points, IRT subsets in semanticscholar:e81984228dccf08fe7eaa637cb47951e7cd7269b; bias-bounded subset selection in openalex:W4413110341; redundancy compression in openalex:W7091187661) inherit the same commitment because the subset is still chosen independently of the pair under test and the budget is still spent without a stopping rule that certifies the verdict for that pair.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:e81984228dccf08fe7eaa637cb47951e7cd7269b","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Introduces MDAD, a meta-evaluation measure giving the minimum full-benchmark accuracy gap at which a fixed micro-benchmark of given size still preserves a model pair's ranking, and shows random sampling matches selection methods except at extreme reductions and that close pairs are unrankable at small sizes. Residue: MDAD is purely diagnostic — it characterizes when a STATIC, pre-committed subset is unreliable for a pair, but provides no procedure that uses the pair under test to decide which or how many examples to evaluate, so the unreliability it measures is reported, never repaired, and every verdict the subset emits is unannotated by its own reliability for that specific pair."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4413110341","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Bias-Bounded Subset Selection formally defines the benchmark subset-selection problem and gives an estimator of full-benchmark score from a fixed subset with a bias bound. Residue: the bias bound is on the POINTWISE score estimate over a population of models and the subset is still selected once independently of any specific pair, so it provides no pair-conditional ranking guarantee and no per-comparison stopping rule — the same static commitment the anchor diagnoses."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7091187661","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Integrates sample-level redundancy removal with subset-level performance prediction to evaluate with ~200x less data while keeping aggregate ranking consistency. Residue: optimizes for aggregate ranking accuracy of a compressed but still STATIC suite; it neither conditions the evaluated set on the particular pair being compared nor certifies that a given pair's verdict is resolved, so close-pair comparisons remain at the mercy of the fixed compression."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415056782","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Efficiently ranks software variants from a reduced benchmark using test selection that keeps rankings stable. Residue: a software-engineering analogue that selects a single reduced test set for all variant comparisons; rankings are 'stable' on average but there is no adaptive, pair-conditioned budget and no per-pair reliability certificate, and the LM-evaluation transfer is untested."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"language-model evaluation / benchmark reliability (micro-benchmarking: predicting full-benchmark judgments from a small evaluated subset)","venue":"ICLR / NeurIPS (ML, methods + empirical-reveal track)","time":"2026","data":["MMLU-Pro","HELM / Open LLM Leaderboard model-by-item response matrices","BIG-bench Lite","existing micro-benchmark subsets (Anchor Points, tinyBenchmarks / IRT-selected subsets)"],"compute":"1×A100 × 3 months (≈ 90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML evaluation methodology, statistical power analysis, item-response theory","preference":"both","baseline":"random subset sampling; Anchor Points (Vivek et al. 2024); tinyBenchmarks IRT subset (Polo et al. 2024); MDAD meta-evaluation (source paper, semanticscholar:e81984228dccf08fe7eaa637cb47951e7cd7269b)","limitation":"micro-benchmarks selected once, globally, cannot reliably rank a specific pair of models when the pair's true full-benchmark gap is small; the unreliability is diagnosed but not repaired, and the size needed for reliability is treated as a fixed property of the subset rather than of the model-pair being compared","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["domain","venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The central solvable object (shared_object thread) is a single per-pair sequential test T(M1,M2): given two models and a benchmark of N items, decide which model is better on the full benchmark, or abstain, while spending as few item-evaluations as possible under a guaranteed error bound. We reframe the comparison as a fixed-confidence sequential hypothesis test on the population mean of the paired per-item score difference d_i = s_i(M1) - s_i(M2), where s_i(M) in {0,1} is model M's correctness on item i (a computed model-internal readout: the benchmark's own scoring function applied to M's output on item i; no external oracle). The null H0: E[d]=0 (tied), alternatives H+: E[d]>0, H-: E[d]<0. Items are not drawn uniformly: each item carries an IRT discrimination weight a_i (computed offline once from a historical model-by-item response matrix R via a 2-parameter IRT fit; a_i is the item's slope parameter, the same quantity tinyBenchmarks uses for static selection), and we draw items in descending a_i order so high-information items enter the test first; the running statistic is the discrimination-reweighted cumulative difference S_t = sum_{i in drawn(t)} a_i d_i. Gap 1 (reliability certificate) is closed by wrapping S_t in an anytime-valid confidence sequence: we use a self-normalized empirical-Bernstein / mixture-supermartingale boundary U_t(alpha) (Howard et al. 2021 time-uniform bounds) so that P(exists t: |S_t/W_t - mu| > U_t(alpha)) <= alpha holds simultaneously over all stopping times, where W_t = sum a_i is the cumulative weight and mu the true weighted mean difference; the test STOPS and returns the sign of S_t the first time the whole confidence interval excludes 0, and returns ABSTAIN if it reaches t=N without exclusion. The emitted verdict therefore carries its own reliability by construction: a non-abstain verdict is wrong with probability <= alpha (the soundness proof), and an abstain is an explicit 'this pair is unresolved at confidence 1-alpha within N items' signal — exactly the 'knows when it is unreliable' artifact the static subset cannot produce. Gap 2 (adaptive budget) is closed by the SAME boundary read as an allocator: the stopping time tau = min{t: 0 notin [S_t/W_t +/- U_t(alpha)]} is the per-pair item budget, so far-apart pairs cross early (tau small) and near-tied pairs spend up to N or abstain — the budget is a function of the realized pair, not fixed in advance. The two gaps share one object and one boundary; there are no separate modules. alpha (target error, default 0.05), the IRT fit R (historical responses), the mixture variance parameter rho of the supermartingale (default tuned to the MMLU-Pro difference-variance, ~0.05), and the mini-batch size b (default 5 items) are the only free quantities, all named hyperparameters. Against the anchor: MDAD reports, for a STATIC subset, the minimum full-benchmark gap it can resolve; our object instead spends items until THIS pair's gap is resolved or declared unresolvable, converting MDAD's fixed-size diagnostic threshold into a per-pair stopping guarantee. We predict (cross-checking the anchor's Figure-1 finding that random ~ selection except at extremes) that ordering draws by IRT discrimination makes the sequential evaluator beat both random and Anchor-Points static subsets specifically in the close-pair regime (<4 accuracy points) where the anchor showed static micro-benchmarks fail.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The two gaps share machinery because the anytime-valid confidence sequence is simultaneously the reliability certificate (gap 1: its coverage guarantee IS the per-pair reliability) and the budget allocator (gap 2: its first-crossing time IS the spent budget) — evidence that they are one object is that you cannot build the certificate without inducing a stopping time, and you cannot define the adaptive budget without a coverage criterion to stop on; splitting them into two modules would double-count one supermartingale. We considered (and rejected) a fixed-sample power-analysis sizing (Card et al. 2020, lineage collateral c2): it would pick a per-pair sample size in advance from an assumed effect size, but the effect size is the unknown we are estimating, so it cannot adapt and lands on the parametric c2 node — a regression. We also rejected re-deriving a plain SPRT on unweighted items (lineage collateral c1): wiring the stopping rule onto IRT-discrimination-ordered item draws is the move that lands on a NO-existing micro-benchmarking node, since no retrieved selection method (Anchor Points, tinyBenchmarks, openalex:W4413110341/W7091187661) makes the evaluated set sequential or pair-conditional — they all commit a static subset (the n1/n2 shared-ancestor assumption).","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: take ~100 instruction-tuned models from the Open LLM Leaderboard with full MMLU-Pro responses (so the full-benchmark pairwise gold ranking is known), and for every model pair run the sequential evaluator at alpha=0.05 and each static baseline at matched expected cost. Measure (b) the metric that moves: at equal guaranteed/realized reliability the mean items-to-decision (tau) of the sequential evaluator is LOWER than the fixed subset size the best static method needs to reach the same fleet-wide pairwise error, and on close pairs (<4 full-benchmark accuracy points, the anchor's failure regime) the sequential evaluator's non-abstain verdicts have error <= alpha while random/Anchor-Points static subsets at the same average cost exceed alpha. (c) The single named load-bearing variable is the IRT discrimination weight a_i that orders the draws; negative control = oracle-permute a_i across items (step 12), which destroys the information-ordering while leaving the anytime-valid boundary (and hence the alpha guarantee) intact. Anti-tautology: the control's predicted effect is on the DOWNSTREAM task-outcome metric — close-pair pairwise ranking accuracy at fixed budget — which should drop toward the random-order frontier when a_i is permuted, NOT merely on tau; if permuting a_i leaves close-pair accuracy unchanged, the discrimination-ordering claim is false even though error control still holds. A positive control (recommended): a stripped evaluator that keeps only the a_i-ordering with a naive fixed-n cutoff recovers most of the close-pair accuracy gain, identifying the ordering as the load-bearing component.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:e81984228dccf08fe7eaa637cb47951e7cd7269b","delta":"They derive MDAD, the minimum full-benchmark gap a STATIC subset of fixed size can reliably resolve for a pair, and stop at diagnosis; we construct a sequential test that spends a pair-dependent number of items until it can certify or abstain on THIS pair's verdict with anytime-valid error <= alpha, turning their fixed-size detectable-threshold diagnostic into a per-pair stopping guarantee."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4413110341","delta":"They bound the bias of a pointwise full-score estimator from a fixed subset chosen once over a model population; we provide a per-pair, ranking-level error guarantee from an adaptively-sized item sequence chosen as a function of the two models actually being compared."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7091187661","delta":"They compress a benchmark into a smaller STATIC suite optimized for aggregate ranking consistency with ~200x less data; we never fix a suite — each comparison draws only as many IRT-ordered items as its own confidence boundary requires and emits an explicit abstain when the pair is unresolvable."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415056782","delta":"They select one reduced test set that keeps software-variant rankings stable on average; we give a per-comparison anytime-valid certificate and an abstain option, and instantiate it for LM benchmarks with IRT-weighted item information rather than software tests."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:e81984228dccf08fe7eaa637cb47951e7cd7269b","what_step_was_missed":"The anchor constructs MDAD as a meta-evaluation measure of a fixed-size subset's pairwise resolving power but never constructs the sequential decision object that consumes items adaptively: turning their pairwise-resolution analysis into a stopping rule requires building a discrimination-weighted anytime-valid confidence sequence on the per-item score difference whose first-crossing time is the per-pair budget and whose coverage is the per-pair reliability certificate — a construction (the supermartingale boundary over IRT-ordered draws) they did not produce because their measure evaluates static subsets rather than allocating evaluation."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":251,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"Layer-1 hard floor did not fire: gap_closure_reject_check is borderline (not triggered, no Reject lesson is 'yes'), anti_pattern matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat openalex:W7141771842 is an ADDRESSABLE adjacency (CAT shares IRT+adaptive-stopping but is pointwise-ability/SE-threshold, not pair-conditional/anytime-valid), not exact-mechanism overlap. Per the revise heuristic, paper_pointed_threat exists AND addressable_via names specific candidate fields (differentiation_from_lit + core_mechanism), and leg 1's borderline hits the load-bearing differentiation axis, so the verdict is revise with targeted edits rather than advance.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a micro-benchmark verdict that carries its own reliability for the specific model pair being compared: every method (anchor MDAD diagnostic, openalex:W4413110341 bias-bounded selection, openalex:W7091187661 compression) emits a ranking from a pre-committed subset without telling the user whether that subset actually resolves THIS pair's gap or has silently fallen below its detectable threshold — the missing outcome is a comparison that knows when it is unreliable.","main_pattern":"reframe_as_solvable_object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The signature failure is treating the reframing as a mechanical wrapper: taking an established attribution, decomposition, or estimation tool and pointing it at a new granularity/architecture/domain without re-deriving why the resulting scores are faithful, supplying the computation but not the justification (no soundness argument, no confound control).","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Pointing an off-the-shelf decomposition at a coarser input granularity without showing the coarser units preserve the signal reads as a wrapper, not a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate does not coarsen granularity; it re-derives faithfulness as anytime-valid Type-I error control over a data-dependent stopping time, a soundness property the off-the-shelf CAT SE-threshold rule does not possess."},{"lesson_quoted":"Porting a known attribution technique to a new architecture or domain while ignoring that technique's documented failure modes — and omitting comparisons to alternatives — leaves reviewers unable to see any unique benefit.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"A reviewer aware of computerized adaptive testing (collision openalex:W7141771842) could read 'IRT + adaptive stopping for LLM eval' as a port of CAT; the candidate must explicitly contrast its pair-conditional anytime-valid ranking certificate against CAT's pointwise ability SE-threshold (which is not anytime-valid)."},{"lesson_quoted":"Proposing a new attribution definition without an axiomatic or causal argument for why it should count as ground-truth collapses the moment a reviewer asks why this is the real importance.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate's 'reliability' is not a new contested definition — it is the standard anytime-valid coverage guarantee (P of any-time false ordering <= alpha), grounded in time-uniform concentration."},{"lesson_quoted":"Conflating a methodological artifact — a computation-granularity difference, a degenerate zero baseline — with genuine signal undermines the entire premise once the confound is identified.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The falsification design includes a negative control (permute IRT discrimination a_i) and a matched-cost baseline frontier, isolating the discrimination-ordering effect from the budget-matching confound."},{"lesson_quoted":"Surveying or recombining fragmented methods without a unifying axis or a decisive controlled experiment yields a contribution reviewers dismiss as anecdotal.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"There is one unifying object (a per-pair anytime-valid confidence sequence) and one decisive experiment (close-pair pairwise error at matched cost vs static subsets), not a recombination survey."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf treats the example budget as something to be spent under a stopping rule rather than fixed in advance: the anchor's MDAD reports a single fixed-size detectable threshold and openalex:W7091187661/openalex:W4413110341 fix the budget before evaluation, so the unmet need is a way to spend exactly as many examples as a given comparison requires to reach a target confidence and no more — sequential allocation of the evaluation budget per comparison is absent.","main_pattern":"reframe_as_solvable_object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The signature failure is treating the reframing as a mechanical wrapper that supplies computation but not the justification that the scores are faithful, with no soundness proof or confound control for why the produced quantity is the real one.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Pointing an off-the-shelf decomposition at a coarser input granularity without showing the coarser units preserve the signal reads as a wrapper, not a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The stopping rule is not an off-the-shelf fixed-sample size; the budget IS the first-crossing time of an anytime-valid boundary, a quantity that did not exist in the static-subset lineage."},{"lesson_quoted":"Proposing a new attribution definition without an axiomatic or causal argument for why it should count as ground-truth collapses the moment a reviewer asks why this is the real importance.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The budget's correctness criterion is the same anytime-valid coverage proof that backs the verdict; no separate undefended definition is introduced."},{"lesson_quoted":"Surveying or recombining fragmented methods without a unifying axis or a decisive controlled experiment yields a contribution reviewers dismiss as anecdotal.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"This leg shares the single object with leg 1 (the boundary is both certificate and allocator), so it is not a fragmented recombination."}],"verdict":"clear"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"Leg 1 (reframe_as_solvable_object / C00) is borderline on the 'porting a known technique without contrasting its documented failure modes / alternatives' lesson because computerized adaptive testing (collision openalex:W7141771842) already applies IRT + an adaptive reliability-threshold stopping rule to cost-effective LLM evaluation; no Reject lesson is a full 'yes', so the aggregate is borderline, not triggered."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a micro-benchmark verdict that carries its own reliability for the specific model pair being compared: every method (anchor MDAD diagnostic, openalex:W4413110341 bias-bounded selection, openalex:W7091187661 compression) emits a ranking from a pre-committed subset without telling the user whether that subset actually resolves THIS pair's gap or has silently fallen below its detectable threshold — the missing outcome is a comparison that knows when it is unreliable.","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Recast an opaque question as a concrete measurement over a well-studied object (an estimator/selector/decomposition) by choosing the right unit of analysis and faithfulness constraint, buy tractability with one compression trick, and certify fidelity by a soundness/optimality PROOF rather than plausibility.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism recasts the comparison as a measurement over a fixed-confidence sequential test (the well-studied object), fixes the unit of analysis (per-item paired difference d_i) and the faithfulness constraint (anytime-valid coverage), and certifies fidelity by the supermartingale soundness proof (non-abstain verdict wrong with prob <= alpha) — the C00 'measurement certified by proof, not plausibility' move is performed, with the IRT-discrimination ordering as the unit-of-analysis choice.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf treats the example budget as something to be spent under a stopping rule rather than fixed in advance: the anchor's MDAD reports a single fixed-size detectable threshold and openalex:W7091187661/openalex:W4413110341 fix the budget before evaluation, so the unmet need is a way to spend exactly as many examples as a given comparison requires to reach a target confidence and no more — sequential allocation of the evaluation budget per comparison is absent.","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Map the quantity onto an existing well-understood object whose native correctness criterion coincides with faithfulness, then buy tractability with one compression/linearization trick that provably preserves the value it approximates.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"The budget is the same object's stopping time tau (first boundary crossing), and the 'compression trick' is the IRT-discrimination draw ordering that front-loads high-information items so the boundary crosses with fewer draws while provably preserving the coverage guarantee — the C00 tractability move is present.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both legs perform C00's signature measurement-certified-by-proof move on the shared sequential-test object (certificate = coverage proof; budget = stopping time), not merely the parent pattern's generic 'reframe' gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["reframe_as_solvable_object","reframe_as_solvable_object"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"Single-pattern composition (reframe_as_solvable_object on both legs); none of the three audit_decomp_* anti-patterns (which require an assumption_audit_and_pivot leg) is present."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"openalex:W7141771842","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"Leveraging Computerized Adaptive Testing (CAT) for Cost-effective Evaluation of LLMs in Medical Benchmarking already fits an IRT item bank and runs an adaptive test that dynamically selects items by real-time ability estimate and TERMINATES on a reliability threshold (SE(theta) <= 0.3), achieving r=0.988 with the full bank using 1.3% of items — i.e. it instantiates IRT + adaptive item selection + a reliability-stopping rule for LLM evaluation, which is the closest mechanism to the candidate. The candidate's claim stands or falls on a specific separation: CAT estimates a SINGLE model's pointwise ability theta and stops on the standard error of that estimate, a rule that is NOT anytime-valid (it offers no time-uniform error control over its own data-dependent stopping time and makes no pairwise ranking guarantee), whereas the candidate decides the SIGN of a paired two-model difference and stops on an anytime-valid confidence sequence with a certified Type-I error <= alpha over all stopping times PLUS an explicit abstain — so the candidate survives only if it (a) demonstrates the pair-conditional ranking object is not reducible to two independent CAT ability estimates and (b) shows the anytime-valid guarantee closes the error-control gap CAT's SE-threshold leaves open.","addressable_via":"differentiation_from_lit (add openalex:W7141771842 with the pair-conditional-anytime-valid vs pointwise-ability-SE delta) and core_mechanism (make explicit that two independent CAT ability SEs do not yield a valid pairwise-ranking error guarantee, and that the SE-threshold stop is not anytime-valid)."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat openalex:W7141771842 (computerized adaptive testing for LLM evaluation) is the closest mechanism and is not yet cited; gap_closure_reject_check leg-1 borderline 'porting a known technique without contrasting alternatives'.","fix_direction":"Add a differentiation_from_lit entry for openalex:W7141771842 with a substantive delta: CAT estimates a single model's pointwise ability theta and stops on SE(theta)<=0.3 (a non-anytime-valid pointwise precision rule), whereas the candidate decides the sign of a paired two-model difference and stops on an anytime-valid confidence sequence with certified pairwise Type-I error <= alpha plus an abstain — a ranking-level guarantee CAT does not provide."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","issue":"The threat's subsumption hinges on whether two independent CAT ability estimates could replicate the pair-conditional certificate; core_mechanism does not yet rule this out explicitly.","fix_direction":"Add one-two sentences to core_mechanism stating (a) that pairing two independent pointwise ability SEs does not yield a valid pairwise-ranking error guarantee (the difference of two CIs is not a CI for the sign of the difference, and per-model SE thresholds are not anytime-valid jointly), and (b) that the candidate's paired statistic S_t with a single anytime-valid boundary on the difference is what supplies the certified pairwise verdict — keeping falsification_prediction and compute_budget byte-identical."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added a differentiation_from_lit entry for openalex:W7141771842 (computerized adaptive testing for LLM evaluation) stating the pair-conditional anytime-valid ranking certificate vs CAT's pointwise-ability SE(theta)<=0.3 non-anytime-valid stop."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added two sentences to core_mechanism establishing that two independent CAT ability SEs do not yield a valid pairwise-ranking error guarantee and that the single anytime-valid boundary on the paired statistic S_t is what certifies the pairwise verdict."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Pair-Conditional Sequential Micro-Benchmarking with Anytime-Valid Reliability Certificates\n\n**Method.** SPRINT (Sequential Pair-conditional Reliable mIcro-beNchmarking via anytime-valid Testing)\n\n## Motivation\nTo rank language models, people often score them on a small slice of a benchmark instead of the whole thing, to save time and money — this is called micro-benchmarking. The catch is that the small slice is picked ONCE, before anyone knows which two models will be compared, and then reused for every comparison. A recent study, How Reliable is Language Model Micro-Benchmarking? (arXiv 2025-10), measured exactly how bad this can be: it introduced a quantity it calls the Minimum Detectable Ability Difference (MDAD), the smallest true gap between two models that a fixed slice of a given size can reliably tell apart. Below that gap the slice is no better than flipping a coin — with only 25 MMLU-Pro questions, more than half of comparisons between similarly-sized models come out unreliable.\n\nThe deeper problem is not a poorly chosen slice; it is that ANY single fixed slice has to commit to one balance of 'few questions but coarse' versus 'many questions but expensive' before it knows which two models are being judged. If the two models happen to be close, the slice quietly returns a shaky answer and never warns you. Every current method — Anchor Points, tinyBenchmarks, the bias-bounded selector of openalex:W4413110341, the compression method of openalex:W7091187661 — inherits this 'one slice, reused for all' assumption, so none of them can tell you whether the particular comparison you care about was actually resolved.\n\nThis is fixable now for two reasons. First, the MDAD study finally turns a fuzzy worry into a precise target by showing exactly where fixed slices fail (close pairs) and that random sampling is just as good there. Second, a statistical tool called an anytime-valid confidence sequence has become practical: it lets you keep adding data and check your answer at every step while still controlling the error rate — which is precisely what you need if you want to stop as soon as you are sure. Putting these together lets us turn the static MDAD diagnostic into a method that spends questions on demand and certifies each answer.\n\nOnce this gap closes, every micro-benchmark answer becomes self-checking: each comparison either returns a ranking that is guaranteed wrong less than a chosen fraction alpha of the time, or it openly says 'I cannot tell these two apart within this question bank.' Leaderboards built on tiny budgets can then no longer silently mis-rank close models, and the MDAD diagnostic of arXiv 2025-10 becomes an actual usable evaluator.\n\n## Method\n### Information-ordering (offline)\n*Use historical IRT discrimination to ask the most model-separating questions first.*\n\n1. Offline, fit a 2-parameter Item Response Theory (IRT) model — IRT is the psychometric framework that scores each test question by how it behaves across many test-takers — on a past model-by-item right/wrong matrix from the Open LLM Leaderboard. Each cell is 1 or 0 for whether a model got that benchmark item right under the benchmark's own grader. Fitting it (by the standard marginal-maximum-likelihood / Expectation-Maximization procedure available in libraries like py-irt) gives, for every item, a discrimination weight $a_{i}$ (how sharply it separates strong from weak models) and a difficulty $b_{i}.$ First remove any item that every model gets right or every model gets wrong, because its discrimination cannot be estimated; give those items the lowest weight so they are asked last. Compute this once; it only sets question order and never touches the verdict, so it cannot bias the error guarantee. 【author decision: for benchmarks graded on a continuous rubric rather than right/wrong, the authors must decide whether to switch to a graded-response IRT model, which changes how the discrimination weight is defined.】\n   - _Why_: Some questions tell models apart far better than others; knowing which ones lets us ask the most informative questions first.\n2. Sort the benchmark questions from highest to lowest discrimination $a_{i}.$ When several questions have essentially the same $a_{i}$ (equal to within a small numerical tolerance), order them by how close their difficulty $b_{i}$ is to the median difficulty of all questions — medium-difficulty questions split the model panel most evenly and are most informative — so those come first. This gives an ordered list L telling you which question to ask next.\n   - _Why_: Asking the most-separating questions first means the comparison usually becomes clear after fewer questions.\n\n### Sequential pair-conditional certificate\n*Accumulate the weighted paired difference and wrap it in an anytime-valid interval that certifies the verdict or abstains.*\n\n3. For a pair of models (M1,M2), run both on the next small batch of 5 questions from list L (the batch size is just a small convenience constant — the error guarantee does not depend on it), score each answer with the benchmark's own grader to get per-question scores $s_{i}(M1)$ and $s_{i}(M2)$ between 0 and 1, and form the per-question score difference $d_{i} = s_{i}(M1) - s_{i}(M2),$ which ranges from -1 to 1. Keep three running totals updated after each batch: the weighted sum of those differences (weighting each question by its discrimination $a_{i}),$ the total weight added so far, and a weighted measure of how much the per-question differences scatter around their weighted average (the running variance).\n\n*The running discrimination-weighted cumulative difference $S_{t}$ over the drawn item set $D_{t},$ where $d_{i}$ is the paired per-item score difference and $a_{i}$ the item's IRT discrimination weight; $W_{t}$ is the cumulative weight.*\n$$ S_t = \\sum_{i \\in \\mathcal{D}_t} a_i\\, d_i, \\qquad d_i = s_i(M_1) - s_i(M_2), \\qquad W_t = \\sum_{i \\in \\mathcal{D}_t} a_i \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The weighted running difference is the single quantity that says which model is ahead so far and by how much.\n4. Wrap the running weighted difference in an anytime-valid confidence interval $CI_{t}$ — 'anytime-valid' means its error guarantee holds no matter when you decide to stop looking. Concretely, use the empirical-Bernstein confidence sequence of Howard, Ramdas, McAuliffe and Sekhon (2021): a closed-form radius computed from the total weight so far, the running variance, a tuning parameter rho, and your chosen error rate alpha, using the fact that each per-question difference lies between -1 and 1. Pick rho by the standard recipe that makes the interval tightest around the number of questions a typical pair is expected to need (a default of roughly 50) — any choice of rho keeps the error rate exactly alpha, it only affects how fast the interval shrinks. Important: running two separate single-model adaptive tests and subtracting them (as in Computerized Adaptive Testing, CAT, openalex:W7141771842) does NOT give a valid guarantee on which model is better, because subtracting two separately-stopped intervals is not a valid interval for the sign of the difference.\n\n*The anytime-valid coverage guarantee: the time-uniform radius $U_{t}(alpha)$ bounds the weighted-mean difference $S_{t}/W_{t}$ around its truth mu simultaneously over all t, so the guarantee survives a data-dependent stopping time.*\n$$ \\Pr\\!\\left(\\exists\\, t:\\ \\left| \\frac{S_t}{W_t} - \\mu \\right| > U_t(\\alpha) \\right) \\le \\alpha \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Because we want to stop as soon as we are confident, we need an interval that stays trustworthy even though the stopping point depends on the data.\n5. Check whether 0 falls outside the interval $CI_{t}.$ If yes, stop: report the leading model (the sign of the running weighted difference) with the certificate 'wrong at most alpha of the time', and record the number of questions spent, tau. If 0 is still inside and questions remain, draw the next batch and repeat. If you exhaust the entire question bank (the cap is the whole bank, so running out means even the full benchmark could not separate them) with 0 still inside, return ABSTAIN ('cannot resolve this pair at this confidence'); the knife-edge case where the difference is exactly 0 at the crossing also abstains. This verdict-or-abstain is the pair's ranking, and it differs from a fixed slice exactly when that slice's size would have fallen below the smallest gap it can reliably detect.\n\n*The stopping time tau is the first time the confidence interval excludes zero; the verdict is the sign of S at tau, and tau itself is the per-pair item budget (abstain if no such t up to the bank size).*\n$$ \\tau = \\min\\Big\\{ t :\\ 0 \\notin \\big[\\, S_t/W_t \\pm U_t(\\alpha) \\,\\big] \\Big\\}, \\qquad \\widehat{v} = \\operatorname{sign}(S_\\tau) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This is the moment the method either earns a guaranteed answer for this exact pair or honestly admits it cannot tell them apart — which a fixed slice can never do.\n\n### Fleet evaluation and baseline frontier\n*Compare adaptive cost and close-pair reliability against fixed-subset baselines.*\n\n6. Across all pairs in a model fleet on MMLU-Pro / BIG-bench-Lite, collect each pair's verdict-or-abstain, its question count tau, and whether its verdict matches the ranking from the full benchmark (count abstains separately rather than as mistakes). Measure cost as questions used per pair. For each fixed-subset baseline (random, Anchor Points, tinyBenchmarks), try a range of subset sizes and pick the size whose average cost equals the adaptive method's average tau, so the comparison is at equal cost. Plot each method's error against its cost to compare frontiers, and report results separately for close pairs — those whose true full-benchmark accuracy gap is under 4 points, the regime the anchor study flagged as the failure mode.\n   - _Why_: This shows whether the adaptive method really spends fewer questions at the same reliability and beats fixed slices on close pairs.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 面向模型对的序贯式微基准评测：带 anytime-valid 可靠性凭证\n\n**方法名称.** SPRINT (Sequential Pair-conditional Reliable mIcro-beNchmarking via anytime-valid Testing)\n\n## 研究动机\n为了给语言模型排名，人们常常只在基准测试的一小部分题目上评测它们，而不是跑完整套题，以节省时间和成本——这就是所谓的微基准评测（micro-benchmarking）。问题在于：这一小部分题目是在还不知道要比较哪两个模型之前，一次性选定的，然后被反复用于所有比较。最近一篇研究 How Reliable is Language Model Micro-Benchmarking?（arXiv 2025-10）精确刻画了这种做法能有多糟：它提出了一个量，叫做最小可检测能力差（MDAD），即一个固定大小的题目子集能可靠区分的两个模型之间的最小真实差距。一旦真实差距小于这个值，该子集的判断就和抛硬币没区别——只用 25 道 MMLU-Pro 题时，相近规模模型之间一半以上的比较都不可靠。\n\n更深层的问题不是子集选得不好，而是任何单一固定子集都必须在「题少但粗糙」和「题多但昂贵」之间，于还不知道要评判哪两个模型之前就先做出权衡。如果这两个模型恰好很接近，子集就会悄悄返回一个不靠谱的答案，并且从不预警。当前所有方法——Anchor Points、tinyBenchmarks、openalex:W4413110341 的有偏界子集选择、openalex:W7091187661 的压缩方法——都继承了「一个子集、反复使用」这一假设，因此没有一个能告诉你：你真正关心的那一对比较到底有没有被可靠地分辨清楚。\n\n现在之所以能解决，有两个原因。第一，MDAD 研究终于把一种模糊的担忧变成了精确的目标：它指出固定子集恰恰在相近模型对上失效，而且在那里随机抽样并不更差。第二，一种叫 anytime-valid 置信序列（confidence sequence）的统计工具已变得实用：它允许你不断追加数据、在每一步都检查答案，同时仍然控制错误率——这正是「一旦有把握就立即停止」所需要的。把两者结合，我们就能把静态的 MDAD 诊断变成一种按需消耗题目、并为每个答案出具凭证的方法。\n\n一旦这个空白被填补，每个微基准答案都将自带核验：每次比较要么返回一个保证出错率低于所选比例 $\\alpha $ 的排名，要么明确地说「在这个题库内我无法分辨这两个模型」。建立在极小预算之上的排行榜就再也不能悄悄地把相近模型排错，而 arXiv 2025-10 的 MDAD 诊断也随之变成一个真正可用的评测器。\n\n## 方法\n### 信息量排序（离线）\n*利用历史 IRT 区分度，优先问最能区分模型的题目。*\n\n1. 离线阶段，在 Open LLM Leaderboard 的历史「模型$\\times $题目」对错矩阵上拟合一个 2 参数项目反应理论(Item Response Theory, IRT)模型——IRT 是一套心理测量框架，根据每道题在大量答题者身上的表现来刻画它。矩阵每个单元格是 1 或 0，表示某模型在该基准题上、用基准自带评分器判定是否答对。用标准的边际极大似然/期望最大化(Expectation-Maximization, EM)过程（py-irt 等库已实现）拟合后，为每道题得到区分度权重 $a_{i}$（它把强模型和弱模型分开的锐利程度）和难度 $b_{i}$。先剔除所有模型全对或全错的题目，因为它们的区分度无法估计；给这些题最低权重，使其排在最后被问到。只算一次；它仅决定出题顺序、绝不参与判定，因此不会影响错误率保证。【作者需决定：对于按连续评分标准（而非对错）打分的基准，作者需决定是否改用分级反应(graded-response)IRT 模型，这会改变区分度权重的定义方式。】\n   - _为什么_: 有些题目区分模型的能力远胜其他题目；知道哪些题最有信息量，就能先问这些题。\n2. 把基准题按区分度 $a_{i}$ 从高到低排序。当若干题目的 $a_{i}$ 几乎相同（差异在很小的数值容差内）时，再按其难度 $b_{i}$ 与所有题目中位难度的接近程度排序——中等难度的题目最能均匀区分模型面板、信息量最大——使这些题排在前面。由此得到一个有序列表 L，决定下一道该问哪题。\n   - _为什么_: 先问最能区分的题，通常更少的题数就能让比较变清晰。\n\n### 序贯的成对可靠性凭证\n*累积加权成对差并包进 anytime-valid 区间，从而为判定出具凭证或选择弃权。*\n\n3. 对一对模型 (M1,M2)，让两者都做列表 L 中下一小批 5 道题（这个批量只是一个方便取的小常数——错误率保证并不依赖它），用基准自带的评分器给每个回答打分，得到 0 到 1 之间的逐题得分 $s_{i}(M1)$ 与 $s_{i}(M2)$，并构造逐题得分差 $d_{i} = s_{i}(M1) - s_{i}(M2)$，其取值在 -1 到 1 之间。每批之后更新三个累积量：这些差值的加权和（每道题按其区分度 $a_{i}$ 加权）、迄今累加的总权重，以及逐题差值围绕其加权平均散布程度的加权度量（即累积方差）。\n\n*已抽取题目集合 $D_{t}$ 上按区分度加权的累积差异 $S_{t}$，其中 $d_{i}$ 是模型对在第 i 题上的成对得分差，$a_{i}$ 为该题的 IRT 区分度权重，$W_{t}$ 为累积权重。*\n$$ S_t = \\sum_{i \\in \\mathcal{D}_t} a_i\\, d_i, \\qquad d_i = s_i(M_1) - s_i(M_2), \\qquad W_t = \\sum_{i \\in \\mathcal{D}_t} a_i \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这个加权累积差是唯一一个量，能说明到目前为止哪个模型领先、领先多少。\n4. 把累积加权差包进一个 anytime-valid 置信区间 $CI_{t}——$「anytime-valid」意味着无论你何时决定停止观察，其错误率保证都成立。具体地，采用 Howard、Ramdas、McAuliffe 与 Sekhon (2021) 的 empirical-Bernstein 置信序列(confidence sequence)：一个闭式半径，由迄今的总权重、累积方差、一个调节参数 rho 和你选定的错误率 alpha 算出，并利用每个逐题差值落在 -1 到 1 之间这一事实。按标准做法选取 rho，使区间在「典型模型对预计所需题数」（默认约 50 题）附近最紧——rho 的任何取值都让错误率严格保持为 alpha，它只影响区间收缩的快慢。重要提示：分别跑两个单模型自适应测试再相减（如计算机化自适应测验(Computerized Adaptive Testing, CAT)，openalex:W7141771842）并不能给出关于「哪个模型更好」的有效保证，因为把两个各自停止的区间相减，并不构成关于差值符号的有效区间。\n\n*anytime-valid 覆盖保证：时间一致的半径 $U_{t}(\\alpha )$ 对所有 t 同时约束加权均值差 $S_{t}/W_{t}$ 与真实值 $\\mu $ 的偏离，因此该保证在数据依赖的停时下依然成立。*\n$$ \\Pr\\!\\left(\\exists\\, t:\\ \\left| \\frac{S_t}{W_t} - \\mu \\right| > U_t(\\alpha) \\right) \\le \\alpha \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 因为我们想一有把握就停下，所以需要一个即便停止点依赖数据也依然可信的区间。\n5. 检查 0 是否落在区间 $CI_{t}$ 之外。若是，则停止：报告领先模型（即累积加权差的符号），附上凭证「出错率至多 alpha」，并记录所用题数 tau。若 0 仍在区间内且还有题目，则抽下一批并重复。若把整个题库用尽（上限就是整个题库，因此用尽意味着即便用完整基准也无法把两者分开）而 0 仍在区间内，则返回弃权(ABSTAIN)（「在该置信水平下无法区分这对模型」）；交叉时差值恰为 0 这一临界情形也判为弃权。这个「判定或弃权」就是该模型对的排名结果，它与固定子集出现分歧的时刻，恰恰是固定子集规模会低于其可靠可检测的最小差距之时。\n\n*停时 $\\tau $ 是置信区间首次排除 0 的时刻；判定为 $\\tau $ 时刻 S 的符号，$\\tau $ 本身即该模型对的逐题预算（若直到题库用尽都未排除 0 则弃权）。*\n$$ \\tau = \\min\\Big\\{ t :\\ 0 \\notin \\big[\\, S_t/W_t \\pm U_t(\\alpha) \\,\\big] \\Big\\}, \\qquad \\widehat{v} = \\operatorname{sign}(S_\\tau) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这正是方法要么为这对模型赢得一个有保证的答案、要么诚实承认无法分辨的时刻——这是固定子集永远做不到的。\n\n### 全模型对评测与基线前沿\n*在自适应成本与相近模型对可靠性上，与固定子集基线作比较。*\n\n6. 在 MMLU-Pro / BIG-bench-Lite 上对一组模型的所有模型对，收集每对的判定或弃权、题数 tau，以及其判定是否与完整基准给出的排名一致（弃权单独统计，不计为错误）。把成本定义为每对所用题数。对每个固定子集基线（随机、Anchor Points、tinyBenchmarks），尝试一系列子集规模，并选取其平均成本等于自适应方法平均 tau 的那个规模，使比较在同等成本下进行。把各方法的错误率对成本作图以比较前沿，并对相近模型对——即真实完整基准准确率差距小于 4 个百分点、也就是锚点研究标记为失效区的那些对——单独汇报结果。\n   - _为什么_: 这能验证自适应方法是否真的在同等可靠性下用更少的题，并在相近模型对上胜过固定子集。\n\n"},{"id":"60","run_dir":"run_prompt60_hubble","index":60,"title":"Predicting Verbatim Memorization Mid-Training from a Per-Span Loss-Collapse Signature","title_zh":"从单跨度损失坍缩特征在训练中途预测逐字记忆","method_name":"TraMP (Trajectory Memorization Predictor)","hook":"We claim a span's eventual verbatim memorization is already decided — and reads out as a sharp early collapse in that span's per-token loss relative to its semantic-neighbor baseline — by a small fraction of the way through pretraining, long before the run ends. A predictor built from this single trajectory signature, and causally validated against injected ground-truth spans, beats every finished-model post-hoc detector while needing none of the final model.","anchor_pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","anchor_pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","domain_category":"Privacy, Security & Trustworthy ML","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a per-span signal computed from the TRAINING TRAJECTORY (the sequence of intermediate checkpoints / per-step updates) that predicts a span's eventual verbatim-memorization status before the run finishes — all current predictors (attribution, intrinsic dimension) are read off a single finished model, so memorization can only be localized in model space, never in training time.","pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"closed by manufacturing the predictive signal from an internal learning-dynamics readout — each span's per-token loss-collapse trajectory across early intermediate checkpoints, normalized against a frozen semantic-neighbor loss baseline — and using that scalar signature, not a finished-model readout, as the memorization predictor.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf CAUSALLY VALIDATES any memorization predictor against an injection ground truth — the controlled-injection regime (anchor) has the ground truth but produces no predictor, and the predictor papers have signals but never test them against a known-cause control, so the field cannot tell whether a memorization correlate is a cause or an epiphenomenon.","pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"closed by building matched injected/non-injected span pairs (same surface form, controlled occurrence count, identical context) whose memorization status is known by construction, then scoring the trajectory signature on held-out injected spans against this injection oracle so the signal is shown to forecast a known cause rather than correlate with surface frequency.","is_anchor":false},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions the shared assumption that a memorization VERDICT requires either a finished model (post-hoc regime) or a full paired retraining run (controlled regime) — every leaf silently inherits the assumption that the unit of measurement is a completed model rather than a point along the optimization trajectory, so none asks whether memorization status can be measured from training dynamics at a fraction of a full run.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"closed by relocating the memorization-detection locus from the finished-model representation (the assumed-invariant locus) to the early training-trajectory of the span, and demonstrating the load-bearing memorization signal already lives there at checkpoint fraction τ ≈ 0.2, overturning the finished-model-verdict assumption.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"LLM memorization measurement / training-data privacy","n_papers":37,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":23},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"openreview","n":2}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":12,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Customizing Large Language Model Generation Style using Parameter-Efficient Finetuning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Underestimated Privacy Risks for Minority Populations in Large Language Model Unlearning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"PhiloGPT: A Philology-Oriented Large Language Model for Ancient Chinese Manuscripts with Dunhuang as Case Study"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Elephants Never Forget: Memorization and Learning of Tabular Data in Large Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Scaling Laws for Fact Memorization of Large Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Demystifying Verbatim Memorization in Large Language Models"}],"more":6},{"year":2025,"n":24,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Analyzing Memorization in Large Language Models through the Lens of Model Attribution"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"On Recipe Memorization and Creativity in Large Language Models: Is Your Model a Creative Cook, a Bad Cook, or Merely a Plagiator?"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Large Language Model Unlearning for Source Code"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Private Memorization Editing: Turning Memorization into a Defense to Strengthen Data Privacy in Large Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Memorization in Large Language Models in Medicine: Prevalence, Characteristics, and Implications"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Memorization ≠ Understanding: Do Large Language Models Have the Ability of Scenario Cognition?"}],"more":18},{"year":2026,"n":2,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"},{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"}],"more":0}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":19,"share":0.514},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":9,"share":0.243},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":6,"share":0.162},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":5,"share":0.135},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":5,"share":0.135},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":4,"share":0.108},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":4,"share":0.108},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":2,"share":0.054}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Memorization in LLMs is currently measured in one of two regimes, and neither yields a causal, training-time predictor of which token spans a model will end up reproducing verbatim. The post-hoc regime reads a finished model: attribution-based analyses (semanticscholar:b2c97bb265ef3f07ddcddfb587e05671f91450c5) and geometric signals such as intrinsic dimension (openalex:W4412944331) correlate internal quantities with already-observed memorization, but because they are computed on a single trained checkpoint they cannot separate a span that the optimizer is actively committing to memory from one that merely co-occurs with a high-attribution feature, and they are never validated against a known causal ground truth. The controlled regime trains paired treatment/control models with sequences injected into the data (semanticscholar:d62c17ea0537f6f02541ee35c1cdce78d4e1cce6) to obtain a clean causal handle, but it obtains the memorization verdict only AFTER the full training run completes, so it cannot say at injection time — from the optimization trajectory itself — whether or when a given span crosses into verbatim recall, and it pays a full-suite training cost per question. The concrete gap is that no method extracts, from the per-step training dynamics over an existing public checkpoint trajectory, a quantity that predicts the eventual verbatim-memorization status of a specific span and is causally validated against injection ground truth — so the field cannot localize memorization in TRAINING TIME, only in model space, and cannot tell whether an early-trajectory signal is a cause or a correlate of the final memorization.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:d62c17ea0537f6f02541ee35c1cdce78d4e1cce6","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Builds a tightly controlled sequence-injection framework that creates minimally-different treatment/control model pairs (inject a sequence into the data, retrain from a checkpoint with frozen optimizer state) to causally study verbatim memorization, identifying that memorization is triggered after a sequence is encoded by features tied to high-level model abilities. Its verdict is read only from the FINISHED treatment model versus control, so it gives a causal ground truth for whether a span is memorized but no training-time signal that predicts the verdict before the run completes, and each causal question costs a fresh paired-injection run — it localizes memorization in model space, never along the optimization trajectory."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:b2c97bb265ef3f07ddcddfb587e05671f91450c5","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Attributes memorization to specific model components by analyzing a single trained checkpoint through the lens of model attribution, moving past purely extractive post-hoc analysis toward where memorization lives. The attribution is correlational on a frozen model and is never validated against an injection ground truth, so it cannot distinguish a component the optimizer used to commit a span to memory from a component that merely correlates with already-memorized content."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4412944331","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Predicts memorization from the intrinsic dimension of internal representations, offering a geometric correlate of which examples are memorized. The signal is read off one trained model and is a static-geometry correlate, so it offers no trajectory-resolved or causally-tested account of when along training a span becomes memorized."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4407131700","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Quantifies and decomposes the heavy-tailed (skewed) distribution of memorization across SFT data, showing average-case metrics hide a memorizing tail. The decomposition is post-hoc on the finished SFT model and offers no training-time predictor of which tail spans will memorize nor any causal validation."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:541d06a0b586187a3d1b85e222c86777442f27ec","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Derives scaling laws for how much factual knowledge LLMs memorize as a function of model and data scale. The laws are aggregate over facts and read from final models; they predict how MUCH is memorized in expectation but not WHICH specific spans, and carry no per-span trajectory signal or causal test."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"LLM memorization measurement / training-data privacy","venue":"ICLR/NeurIPS (ML top-tier)","time":"2026","data":["open-weight pretraining checkpoint trajectories (e.g. Pythia/OLMo-style intermediate checkpoints)","controlled sequence-injection corpora","membership / extraction probe sets"],"compute":"1×A100 × 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with cloud access; LLM training-dynamics + privacy background","preference":"both","baseline":"controlled sequence-injection memorization measurement (Demystifying Verbatim Memorization, semanticscholar:d62c17ea0537f6f02541ee35c1cdce78d4e1cce6) and post-hoc attribution / intrinsic-dimension predictors (semanticscholar:b2c97bb265ef3f07ddcddfb587e05671f91450c5, openalex:W4412944331)","limitation":"current memorization measurement is either post-hoc (read off a finished model) or requires training paired treatment/control suites; there is no causally-validated, training-time signal that predicts WHICH spans will end up memorized before they are, and existing correlational predictors (attribution, intrinsic dimension) are never checked against injection ground truth","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object every leg reads from is the per-span loss-collapse trajectory L_s(t): for a candidate token span s and an intermediate checkpoint at training-fraction t ∈ (0,1], L_s(t) is the mean per-token cross-entropy of the model-at-t on the exact tokens of s (a model-internal readout, computed by one forward pass over s at each saved checkpoint; spans are fixed-length 50-token windows mined from the training corpus). Against this we define a frozen semantic-neighbor baseline B_s = the same per-token cross-entropy averaged over the k=8 nearest paraphrase/semantic-neighbor windows of s (neighbors retrieved once by sentence-embedding cosine over the corpus; B_s isolates verbatim recall from mere topical familiarity, so a span that is merely on-distribution does not score high). The trajectory signature is the scalar Σ_s = the area between the normalized curve [B_s − L_s(t)] and zero accumulated over the EARLY window t ∈ (0, τ], τ = 0.2, divided by total-corpus-passes of s in (0,τ] (the divide-by-occurrence makes Σ_s a per-exposure collapse rate, not a raw frequency count — this is the step that prevents regression to a frequency baseline). Leg 1 (self_supervised_signal_engineering / C07) manufactures the predictor: Σ_s computed at τ=0.2 is the manufactured supervisory signal; a logistic head g(Σ_s, slope_s, curvature_s) over three trajectory moments (level, slope, curvature of [B_s−L_s] on (0,τ]) outputs P(s verbatim-memorized at t=1) — no finished-model readout enters, closing gap 1 because the verdict is now a function of the trajectory alone. Leg 2 (controlled_diagnostic_design / C02) supplies the causal oracle: we inject N matched span pairs into the pretraining corpus of a from-scratch small run — each pair shares surface form and context but one member is injected at a controlled occurrence count and the other held out — so eventual verbatim memorization of the injected member is known by construction; Σ_s is computed for injected and control members from the SAME early checkpoints and the predictor is scored only on held-out injected spans, closing gap 2 because forecasting the injection oracle out-of-sample shows Σ_s tracks the known cause, not a frequency confound (the controls equalize frequency). Leg 3 (assumption_audit_and_pivot / C01) is the conceptual pivot realized by the same object: the field's finished-model detectors (intrinsic dimension W4412944331; attribution b2c97bb2) read the verdict off t=1, tacitly assuming the trajectory locus is irrelevant; we relocate the detection signal to t≤τ and show Σ_s at τ=0.2 already separates memorized from non-memorized injected spans, closing gap 3 because the memorization verdict is demonstrably decidable from an early-trajectory locus the prior locus assumed invariant. The three legs share one machinery (Σ_s) rather than separate modules: leg 1 builds it as a predictor, leg 2 validates it causally, leg 3 reads its conceptual meaning — one coordinated paper around the trajectory object.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The three gaps collapse onto one shared object because the same scalar Σ_s simultaneously is the trajectory predictor (gap 1), the quantity scored against the injection oracle (gap 2), and the evidence that the detection locus can move earlier in training (gap 3) — building three separate modules would have stapled three papers together, whereas one object read three ways is genuinely one paper. We considered an alternative anchor design using influence-function / TracIn attribution of memorized spans back to training examples, but the method_lineage REGRESSION FLAG names influence functions (c0) and forgetting-events / per-example loss curves (c1) as collateral nodes a cure must not reduce to; a raw per-example loss curve IS the c1 node, so the load-bearing novelty is deliberately placed in the semantic-neighbor-NORMALIZED, per-exposure-rate signature Σ_s (a verbatim-recall-specific contrast that a plain loss curve and an influence score do not produce) and in its causal validation against injection ground truth — neither of which c0/c1 supply. We also rejected a finished-model probe variant because it would re-occupy the post-hoc locus the paper exists to vacate.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on a from-scratch Pythia-scale (≈410M) pretraining run with N≈2000 injected matched span pairs and checkpoints saved up to training-fraction τ=0.2, fit the logistic predictor g on early-trajectory features φ_s and measure held-out verbatim extraction-recall AUC. If the candidate works, this τ=0.2 AUC stays HIGH and is ≥ the AUC of a finished-model intrinsic-dimension or attribution detector evaluated at t=1 (the metric is extraction-recall AUC; the qualitative direction is 'early-trajectory predictor matches or exceeds the post-hoc detector'), and on the frequency-matched injected subset it forecasts the injection ledger above chance. The named load-bearing variable is the per-exposure loss-collapse signature Σ_s (the semantic-neighbor-normalized early collapse rate). Negative control: destroy only Σ_s's trajectory-ordering information by permuting the checkpoint-fraction labels before computing slope/curvature (marginal loss magnitudes preserved, exposure counts preserved) and retrain g — the predicted effect is that the DOWNSTREAM extraction-recall AUC collapses back to the post-hoc baseline, not merely that Σ_s changes value; if AUC is unaffected, the trajectory ordering was not load-bearing and the mechanism is falsified. Positive control: a stripped-down predictor using Σ_s alone (no other features) should recover most of the full predictor's extraction-recall AUC, identifying Σ_s as the carrier of the signal.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:d62c17ea0537f6f02541ee35c1cdce78d4e1cce6","delta":"They inject sequences and read a causal memorization verdict off the FINISHED treatment model (one paired run per question); we construct a per-span early-trajectory signature Σ_s and a predictor that forecasts that same verdict from checkpoint-fraction τ=0.2, turning their post-run causal oracle into the validation target for a mid-training predictor they never built."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4412944331","delta":"They predict memorization from the intrinsic dimension of a single finished model's representations; we derive a semantic-neighbor-normalized loss-collapse-rate signature from early intermediate checkpoints and show it predicts at τ=0.2, relocating the detection locus from model space to training time."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:b2c97bb265ef3f07ddcddfb587e05671f91450c5","delta":"They attribute memorization to components of a frozen trained model with no causal injection test; we causally validate our trajectory signature against an injection ground-truth oracle with frequency-matched controls, separating cause from correlate."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4407131700","delta":"They decompose the heavy-tailed memorization distribution post-hoc on a finished SFT model; we provide a per-exposure trajectory rate Σ_s that predicts WHICH individual tail spans will memorize before training completes."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:541d06a0b586187a3d1b85e222c86777442f27ec","delta":"They derive aggregate scaling laws for how much fact knowledge is memorized at final scale; we predict the binary verbatim-memorization status of specific spans from early-trajectory dynamics, a per-span not aggregate quantity."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:d62c17ea0537f6f02541ee35c1cdce78d4e1cce6","what_step_was_missed":"Their controlled-injection framework establishes the causal memorization verdict only from the finished treatment model; to already contain our contribution it would have needed to construct a per-span early-trajectory readout normalized against a verbatim-specific baseline (the semantic-neighbor-normalized per-exposure loss-collapse rate Σ_s computed at an early checkpoint fraction) and prove that readout forecasts the post-run verdict out-of-sample — a mid-training predictive primitive, not a post-run measurement, which their sequence-injection method never builds."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":313,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"Layer-1 hard floor does not fire: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict is borderline (no lesson marked candidate_match: yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat is adjacent-not-exact (addressable_via confirms no exact-mechanism overlap). recipe_application_check.verdict is 'applied' for all three legs, so the idea was built from the cited clusters' tactical moves rather than generic gists. The remaining borderline findings — C02's ecological-validity lesson and C01's 'locus already explored (FIM/grokking pretraining-dynamics work)' lesson — are already mitigated in the candidate (real-corpus transfer test in core_mechanism_steps step 11; explicit differentiation_from_lit deltas plus the trajectory-ordering negative control), so they are surfaced as Phase 4 reviewer concerns rather than forcing a revise.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a per-span signal computed from the TRAINING TRAJECTORY (the sequence of intermediate checkpoints / per-step updates) that predicts a span's eventual verbatim-memorization status before the run finishes — all current predictors (attribution, intrinsic dimension) are read off a single finished model, so memorization can only be localized in model space, never in training time.","main_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is a manufactured internal signal whose validity silently rests on an assumption that does not survive deployment (model calibration, a stationary/known-finite shift set, or covert use of target/test-set information amounting to label leakage), or recombining well-known components without one load-bearing mechanistic insight.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A label-free signal whose validity depends on model calibration silently fails on exactly the deep networks known to be poorly calibrated — validate a surrogate where its core assumption is weakest, not where it is convenient.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Sigma_s is a per-span loss-collapse CONTRAST against a semantic-neighbor baseline, not a calibration-dependent confidence readout, so its validity does not rest on the model being calibrated."},{"lesson_quoted":"Recasting a continuous shift as a discrete, known, finite set of types indexed against a precomputed lookup table collapses the moment an unanticipated or mixed shift arrives.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"There is no discrete shift-type lookup; the signal is a continuous trajectory statistic, so this lesson does not apply."},{"lesson_quoted":"Importing a generic continual-learning blending or interpolation technique into a new modality without identifying that modality's specific dynamics lever reads as recombination, not contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The dynamics lever is explicitly identified — the verbatim-recall-specific early loss-collapse rate normalized by semantic neighbors — rather than a generic blending import."},{"lesson_quoted":"Reusing standard sequential machinery (chaining each step's posterior as the next prior) without a new stabilizer amplifies noise and looks derivative of prior adaptation work.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"No posterior-chaining is used; the semantic-neighbor normalization is the explicit stabilizer that blocks the frequency-degenerate solution."},{"lesson_quoted":"A multi-branch or ensemble reweighting mechanism that overlaps with standard multi-task/mixture-of-experts ensembling must explicitly beat both the single-model and the standard-ensemble baselines, or the gain is credited to prior art.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"No ensemble reweighting is present; the predictor is a single logistic head over three trajectory moments."},{"lesson_quoted":"Using target or test-set information during adaptation invites a label-leakage objection that undermines the very source-free, label-free deployment setting the method claims.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The injection ground truth is used to VALIDATE on held-out injected spans and the predictor is trained on a disjoint span split, but a reviewer could ask whether train/eval span splits leak; mitigated by the held-out + frequency-matched-control design and surfaced for Phase 4."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf CAUSALLY VALIDATES any memorization predictor against an injection ground truth — the controlled-injection regime (anchor) has the ground truth but produces no predictor, and the predictor papers have signals but never test them against a known-cause control, so the field cannot tell whether a memorization correlate is a cause or an epiphenomenon.","main_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"A diagnostic that only re-confirms a known shortcut, or that validates a synthetic-ground-truth instrument only on synthetic data without showing transfer to real instances, leaves ecological validity unestablished; circular oracles drawn from the evaluand also fail.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A diagnostic that only re-confirms a shortcut already known in advance, surfacing no previously unmeasurable failure, is read as confirmatory rather than as a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The instrument surfaces a previously unmeasurable quantity — early-trajectory predictability of per-span memorization — not a re-confirmation of a known shortcut."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a synthetic-ground-truth instrument only on synthetic data, without demonstrating that the controlled finding transfers to real-world instances, leaves ecological validity unestablished and undermines the central claim.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The injected-span oracle is a controlled (semi-synthetic) construction; step 11's transfer test on a real corpus slice and a second scale mitigates this but the strength of real-corpus transfer is the load-bearing ecological-validity concern to surface for Phase 4."},{"lesson_quoted":"Building the instrument around one contested definition of the target property means it cannot independently confirm that the definition is correct, and reviewers flag the resulting circularity.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Verbatim memorization is operationalized by a standard, mechanistic extraction criterion (>=40/50-token greedy reproduction) cross-checked against the injection ledger, not a self-authored contested definition."},{"lesson_quoted":"Resting an unsupervised evaluation on the unverified premise that the systems under test can reliably judge one another stakes the entire method on an assumption that collapses under scrutiny.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The oracle is the injection ledger (independent of the model under test), not a system-judges-system premise."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pairing a single-task or small-sample instrument with broad capability claims triggers a scope-mismatch rejection, and assembling retrieval or engineering blocks without an isolating scientific insight reads as application rather than research.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The claim is scoped to verbatim memorization at the tested scales/corpora and carries an isolating insight (the trajectory signature), not a broad capability claim over assembled blocks."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions the shared assumption that a memorization VERDICT requires either a finished model (post-hoc regime) or a full paired retraining run (controlled regime) — every leaf silently inherits the assumption that the unit of measurement is a completed model rather than a point along the optimization trajectory, so none asks whether memorization status can be measured from training dynamics at a fraction of a full run.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Relocating a security/detection signal to a locus already exploited by published work, or claiming the relocated signal is stronger without defeating an adaptive search at the new locus and without a mechanistic account of why the locus carries the signal, reads as a stacked pipeline rather than a principled shift.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a relocated signal is 'stealthier' or 'harder to remove' without defeating an adaptive defender who searches the same new locus leaves the central claim unverified.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The claim is predictive (early decidability), not a stealth/robustness claim against an adaptive adversary, so this attack-framed lesson does not bind."},{"lesson_quoted":"Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work — normalization statistics, activation-similarity losses, semantic concept triggers — collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"Memorization 'dynamics during pretraining' is an active area (collision_hits [70] FIM memorization dynamics, [116] grokking-in-pretraining monitoring), so the per-span PREDICTIVE + injection-causally-validated difference must be made explicit and measured; the differentiation_from_lit deltas and the negative control do this but it is the load-bearing novelty boundary to defend in Phase 4."},{"lesson_quoted":"A defense whose relocation silently depends on a clean reference model or a known anomaly distribution reintroduces precisely the strong assumption the move was supposed to eliminate.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The method needs no clean reference model; the semantic-neighbor baseline is computed from the same model's own readouts on retrieved corpus neighbors."},{"lesson_quoted":"Demonstrating the new locus only on fixed, non-adaptive or outdated baselines while omitting any account of why it works reads as a stacked pipeline of existing components rather than a principled shift.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Baselines are the current finished-model detectors (intrinsic dimension, attribution) and a mechanistic account is given (verbatim recall is laid down as an early per-exposure loss collapse), not a stacked pipeline."},{"lesson_quoted":"Wiring off-the-shelf generators or tools into a new attack setting without a structural reason for the locus change gets judged as engineering integration, not insight.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The locus change (finished model -> early training trajectory) carries a structural reason — memorization is committed during optimization — rather than tool-wiring."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No Reject lesson is marked candidate_match: yes, so no hard-floor trigger fires. The aggregate is borderline, driven by the C02 entry's ecological-validity lesson ('Validating a synthetic-ground-truth instrument only on synthetic data... leaves ecological validity unestablished') and the C01 entry's locus-novelty lesson ('Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work... unless the difference is made explicit and measured'), both load-bearing but mitigated in the candidate (real-corpus transfer test; explicit differentiation_from_lit deltas + negative control)."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a per-span signal computed from the TRAINING TRAJECTORY (the sequence of intermediate checkpoints / per-step updates) that predicts a span's eventual verbatim-memorization status before the run finishes — all current predictors (attribution, intrinsic dimension) are read off a single finished model, so memorization can only be localized in model space, never in training time.","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Treat an already-trained model's own internal-state readouts (gradient direction/magnitude, representation moment, activation breadth) as the manufactured supervisory signal, pairing a mechanistic diagnosis that localizes the failure to a specific structural site with a stabilizer that prevents the label-free signal's degenerate solution.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism manufactures Sigma_s — the per-span early loss-collapse rate read from intermediate checkpoints (an internal-state readout) — localizes the memorization 'site' to the early-trajectory per-exposure collapse against a semantic-neighbor baseline, and the semantic-neighbor normalization + per-exposure division is the explicit stabilizer that stops the signal degenerating into a raw-frequency count. This performs the cluster's diagnose-localize + stabilize-against-collapse signature move, not a generic self-training loop.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf CAUSALLY VALIDATES any memorization predictor against an injection ground truth — the controlled-injection regime (anchor) has the ground truth but produces no predictor, and the predictor papers have signals but never test them against a known-cause control, so the field cannot tell whether a memorization correlate is a cause or an epiphenomenon.","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Construct controlled instances in which exactly one named confound is blocked or independently varied, supply ground truth independent of the system under test, and report the divergence between apparent and de-confounded performance as the headline.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism injects matched span pairs (frequency-controlled, surface-form-matched) so the occurrence-count confound is held fixed while memorization status varies, uses the injection ledger as a system-independent oracle, and reports the AUC against that oracle (and the gap vs finished-model detectors) as the headline — the cluster's confound-isolation + independent-oracle + divergence-headline move.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions the shared assumption that a memorization VERDICT requires either a finished model (post-hoc regime) or a full paired retraining run (controlled regime) — every leaf silently inherits the assumption that the unit of measurement is a completed model rather than a point along the optimization trajectory, so none asks whether memorization status can be measured from training dynamics at a fraction of a full run.","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Name the single representational locus all current methods operate on, state the tacit sufficiency/invariance claim bolted to it as falsifiable, then relocate the detection signal to an alternative locus and give a mechanistic account of why the property must manifest there.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism names the assumed locus (the finished-model representation at t=1, used by intrinsic-dimension and attribution detectors), states the tacit invariance claim (the trajectory locus is irrelevant), relocates detection to the early training-trajectory locus (t<=tau), and gives the mechanistic why (verbatim recall is committed as an early per-exposure loss collapse) — the cluster's relocate-the-signal + mechanistic-account move.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"All three entries instantiate their cited cluster's distinctive signature move in core_mechanism: C07's internal-readout-as-signal + stabilizer (Sigma_s + semantic-neighbor normalization), C02's confound-isolating injected pairs + independent oracle, and C01's locus relocation + mechanistic account. None reduces to the parent pattern's generic gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["self_supervised_signal_engineering","controlled_diagnostic_design","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"None of the three reject-favored compositions matches: all three documented anti-patterns require heterogeneous_decomposition as a component, which is absent from the composition_set, so no 2-way subset triggers."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"Memorization Dynamics of Fill-in-the-Middle Pretraining","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"This collision hit studies verbatim-memorization DYNAMICS in a controlled repeated-corpus pretraining setting (matched FIM vs LTR Llama-3.2 models on a FineWeb-Gutenberg corpus with repeated excerpts), which is the closest active work to the candidate's 'memorization during pretraining' framing and proves the dynamics-during-pretraining space is live. The candidate's claim stands or falls on whether it does something this paper does not: it measures and contrasts how much/when FIM vs LTR memorize using prefix probes, but it does NOT construct a per-span early-checkpoint PREDICTOR (Sigma_s) of eventual verbatim memorization, does not normalize against a semantic-neighbor baseline to isolate verbatim recall from topical familiarity, and does not causally validate a trajectory signature against frequency-matched injection ground truth with a held-out predictive evaluation. So the candidate is not subsumed — its contribution (a causally-validated mid-training per-span predictor that matches finished-model detectors at tau=0.2) is orthogonal to this paper's comparative memorization-rate measurement.","addressable_via":"Not an exact-mechanism overlap; the differentiation is already load-bearing in differentiation_from_lit and core_mechanism (per-span predictor + semantic-neighbor normalization + injection-causal validation), so no candidate field needs to change — the distinction must simply be made explicit and measured in Phase 4 (surfaced as a reviewer concern)."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Predicting Verbatim Memorization Mid-Training from a Per-Span Loss-Collapse Signature\n\n**Method.** TraMP (Trajectory Memorization Predictor)\n\n## Motivation\nLarge language models sometimes memorize and spit back exact chunks of their training data, which causes privacy and copyright problems. The practical question is: can we tell which specific pieces of text a model will end up memorizing — ideally before we have finished the expensive training run? Right now there are only two ways to answer, and both are too late. The first reads a fully-trained model: methods that look at the geometry of its internal representations (intrinsic dimension) or attribute memorization to particular model components. These are correlations measured on the finished model, and nobody has checked them against a known cause. The second is cleaner but slower: you inject specific sequences into the training data, train one model with them and one without, and compare — this gives a true cause-and-effect answer, but only after the whole run finishes, and you pay for a full extra training run each time you ask. Neither gives you a signal you can read off the training process itself, partway through, to predict which spans will be memorized. What makes this solvable now is that public model 'suites' save many checkpoints from across a training run, and small models can be retrained cheaply, so we can finally watch each span's learning curve as training proceeds — and we can borrow the injection trick purely as a way to CHECK our prediction, not to make it. Our idea, TraMP, watches how fast each span's per-token loss collapses early in training, but measured RELATIVE to similar-meaning text (so we don't just flag text the model finds easy in general) and PER exposure (so we don't just rediscover 'frequent text gets memorized'). That single early signal, read at about one-fifth of the way through training, predicts which spans end up memorized — and we prove it tracks a real cause by testing it against injected spans whose memorization status we set by construction. If this works, memorization becomes something you can forecast and act on during training, instead of only auditing after the fact.\n\n## Method\n### Injection ground-truth instrument\n*Builds frequency-matched injected/control span pairs whose memorization status is known by construction, giving a causal test set.*\n\n1. Cut the training corpus into fixed 50-token spans (each stored as its token sequence and position). Before training, inject about 2000 matched span pairs: for each pair, take one span and make a look-alike twin by swapping its content words for words that are individually just as common (keeping the same length and grammatical shape), and make sure both members appeared equally often in the corpus to begin with; then add ONLY the first member to the training data a controlled number of times (1, 2, 4, 8, or 16 copies) and leave the twin out. Record which span is the injected one and which is the held-out twin. Separately, for every span retrieve its 8 closest same-meaning neighbors using a general-purpose sentence-embedding model (default all-mpnet-base-v2) and a fast nearest-neighbor index (FAISS), excluding any near-duplicate whose word overlap with the span is more than half.\n   - _Why_: Matched pairs hold repeat-count fixed so any later difference is about memorization itself, not just how often the text appeared — giving a clean known-answer test set.\n2. At the end of training, decide which spans the model actually memorized: give the model the first 10 tokens of a span as a prompt, let it generate the next 40 tokens greedily, and mark the span as memorized if at least 40 of those 40 tokens come back exactly in the right places. For the injected spans, also check this against the injection record so both the by-construction status and the generation-based status are kept. This is a concrete, model-independent definition, so the target you are predicting isn't just something you declared to be true.\n   - _Why_: This is a concrete, model-independent definition of memorization, so the target label isn't something we just declared true.\n\n### Trajectory signature Σ_s\n*Reads each span's early loss-collapse relative to semantic neighbors and per exposure to form the predictive feature.*\n\n3. Train a 410-million-parameter language model from scratch, saving snapshots at 2.5%, 5%, 10%, 15%, and 20% of the way through training, plus one at the very end. At each snapshot, run a single forward pass over every span and over each of its 8 same-meaning neighbors, and record two numbers per span: the span's own average per-token loss, and the average per-token loss over its 8 neighbors (the 'neighbor baseline'). Keep this table indexed by span and by snapshot. The neighbor baseline tells you how well the model handles similar-meaning text it was never pushed to copy word-for-word, which is what lets you isolate true verbatim copying later.\n\n*The frozen semantic-neighbor baseline $B_{s}$ averages the per-token cross-entropy of the model at checkpoint t over the k=8 nearest paraphrase windows of span s, isolating verbatim recall from mere topical familiarity.*\n$$ B_s = \\frac{1}{k}\\sum_{j=1}^{k} \\mathrm{CE}\\big(\\mathcal{M}_t, \\mathrm{nbr}_j(s)\\big), \\quad k = 8 \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Comparing a span to its meaning-neighbors separates true word-for-word memorization from text the model just finds easy in general.\n4. For each span, look at the gap between its neighbor baseline and its own loss across the early snapshots (the first 20% of training). Add up that gap over the early snapshots (area under the gap curve), then divide by how many times the span has been shown to the model so far, giving a per-exposure collapse rate. Also fit a simple curve to the same gap-over-time to read off its slope (how fast it is dropping) and its curvature (whether the drop is accelerating or leveling off). Bundle these three numbers — the per-exposure collapse rate, the slope, and the curvature — into one feature vector for the span. Dividing by the number of times the span was shown keeps this a rate, so it can't secretly just be measuring how often the text appeared.\n\n*The trajectory signature $\\Sigma _{s}$ is the area between the neighbor baseline $B_{s}(t)$ and the span's own per-token loss $L_{s}(t)$ over the early window $t \\in $ (0, $\\tau ],$ divided by the span's number of exposures $n_{s}(\\tau )$ so far — a per-exposure collapse rate, not a raw frequency count.*\n$$ \\Sigma_s = \\frac{1}{n_s(\\tau)} \\int_{0}^{\\tau} \\big[\\, B_s(t) - L_s(t) \\,\\big]\\, dt, \\quad \\tau = 0.2 \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Dividing by exposures keeps the signal a RATE, so it can't secretly just be 'frequent text gets memorized'.\n\n### Predictor and causal validation\n*Fits the early-checkpoint predictor, compares it to finished-model detectors, and validates it causally with a trajectory-permutation control.*\n\n5. Split the spans into a training set and a held-out test set (70/30), making the split balanced on whether spans ended up memorized and on injected-versus-natural status, and keeping each injected pair entirely on one side so a twin can't leak across. Train a simple logistic predictor that takes only the three 20%-mark features (per-exposure collapse rate, slope, curvature) — and nothing from the finished model — to predict the end-of-training memorization label. On the held-out test spans, measure how well it ranks memorized spans (extraction-recall AUC) and compare against two detectors computed on the FINISHED model: one based on the geometry of the model's internal representation (its intrinsic dimension), and one based on attributing memorization to specific model components. The key comparison is whether the early-training predictor matches or beats these end-of-training detectors.\n\n*The predictor outputs the probability that span s is verbatim-memorized at t=1 as a logistic function of three early-trajectory moments of $[B_{s} -  L_{s}]$ — level $(\\Sigma _{s}),$ slope, and curvature — with no finished-model readout entering.*\n$$ \\hat{p}(s) = \\sigma\\big(w_0 + w_1 \\Sigma_s + w_2\\, \\mathrm{slope}_s + w_3\\, \\mathrm{curv}_s\\big) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: If an early-training signal matches or beats end-of-training detectors, memorization really is decidable partway through.\n6. Run two checks. First (causal): score the predictor only on held-out injected spans against the injection record, and include a predictor that uses just raw repeat-count on the frequency-matched controls — that count-only predictor should land at chance, while the real signal stays above chance, showing the signal tracks a true cause rather than just frequency. Second (scramble control): shuffle the time-order of each span's early snapshots before computing slope and curvature (this keeps the exact same set of loss values and the same number of exposures, and destroys only the ordering across snapshots), recompute the features, refit, and measure the prediction quality — it should fall back to the end-of-training baseline. If it does, the timing pattern across snapshots, not just the loss values, is what carries the prediction.\n   - _Why_: The injection test shows the signal tracks a real cause; the scramble test shows the timing information, not just the loss values, is what carries the prediction.\n7. Redo the loss-reading and predictor-fitting on a second model size and a second real slice of corpus, using the same early snapshots and the same 20%-mark features. Report it two ways: apply the original predictor unchanged to the new setting, and also retrain the predictor's weights on the new setting. 【author decision: whether the headline claim is that the collapse-rate signature itself transfers unchanged (apply original weights) or only that it predicts after re-calibrating on the new setting (retrain weights) is a scope decision the authors must make.】 Showing it still predicts elsewhere proves the finding isn't a quirk of one setup.\n   - _Why_: Showing it still predicts elsewhere proves the finding isn't an artifact of one setup.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 从单跨度损失坍缩特征在训练中途预测逐字记忆\n\n**方法名称.** TraMP (Trajectory Memorization Predictor)\n\n## 研究动机\n大型语言模型有时会记住并原样吐出训练数据中的整段文字，这会带来隐私和版权问题。真正实用的问题是：我们能否判断模型最终会记住哪些具体文本——最好是在昂贵的训练跑完之前就知道？现在只有两种回答方式，而且都太晚。第一种是读一个已经训练完成的模型：有的方法看它内部表示的几何性质（intrinsic dimension），有的把记忆归因到特定模型组件。这些都是在成品模型上测得的相关性，没人拿一个已知的原因去验证过它们。第二种更干净但更慢：你把特定序列注入训练数据，训练一个带它的模型和一个不带它的模型，再做对比——这给出真正的因果答案，但只能在整个训练跑完之后得到，而且每问一次就要多付一整次训练的代价。两者都给不出一个能在训练过程进行到一半时、直接从训练过程本身读出来、用以预测哪些跨度会被记住的信号。现在之所以能解决，是因为公开的模型 suite 会保存训练过程中的许多 checkpoint，而且小模型可以便宜地重训，于是我们终于能在训练推进时观察每个跨度的学习曲线——并且我们只把注入技巧用来「验证」预测，而不是用来做预测。我们的想法 TraMP 观察每个跨度的逐 token 损失在训练早期坍缩得有多快，但是相对于语义相近的文本来度量（这样就不会只是标记出模型普遍觉得容易的文本），并且按曝光次数归一（这样就不会只是重新发现「高频文本会被记住」）。这一个早期信号，在大约训练进度五分之一处读取，就能预测哪些跨度最终被记住——而且我们用注入跨度（其记忆状态由我们构造时设定）来检验它，从而证明它追踪的是真正的原因。如果成立，记忆就从只能事后审计变成了能在训练中预测并干预的量。\n\n## 方法\n### 注入式真值仪器\n*构建频次匹配的注入/对照配对跨度，其记忆状态由构造时设定，从而提供一个因果测试集。*\n\n1. 把训练语料切成固定的 50-token 跨度（每个跨度保存其 token 序列和位置）。训练前注入约 2000 对配对跨度：对每一对，取一个跨度，再造一个外形相似的孪生份——把它的实义词换成单独看同样常见的词（长度和语法形状保持不变），并保证两个成员在语料里原本出现的次数相同；然后只把第一个成员以受控的次数（1、2、4、8 或 16 份）加入训练数据，把孪生份留在外面。记录哪个是注入的、哪个是留出的孪生份。另外，对每个跨度用一个通用的句子嵌入模型(sentence-embedding model，默认 all-mpnet-base-v2)和一个快速近邻索引(FAISS)检索它最相近的 8 个同义近邻，并排除掉与该跨度词面重叠超过一半的近似重复项。\n   - _为什么_: 配对跨度让重复次数保持固定，这样之后的差异只关乎记忆本身，而不是文本出现得多频繁——从而得到一个干净的已知答案测试集。\n2. 训练结束时，判定模型实际记住了哪些跨度：把跨度的前 10 个 token 作为提示给模型，让它贪心地生成接下来的 40 个 token，如果其中至少 40 个 token 在正确位置上原样复现，就把该跨度标记为已记忆。对注入跨度，还要与注入记录交叉核对，使得「构造时设定的状态」和「基于生成的状态」都被保留。这是一个具体、与模型无关的定义，所以你要预测的目标不是你随口声称为真的东西。\n   - _为什么_: 这是一个具体、与模型无关的记忆定义，所以目标标签不是我们随口声称为真的东西。\n\n### 轨迹特征 Σ_s\n*相对于语义近邻并按曝光次数读取每个跨度的早期损失坍缩，形成预测特征。*\n\n3. 从零训练一个 4.1 亿参数的语言模型，在训练进度的 2.5%、5%、10%、15%、20% 处各保存一个快照，并在最末尾再保存一个。在每个快照上，对每个跨度及其 8 个同义近邻各做一次前向，并为每个跨度记录两个数：该跨度自身的逐 token 平均损失，以及它 8 个近邻的逐 token 平均损失（即「近邻基线」）。把这张表按跨度和快照建立索引。近邻基线告诉你模型对那些它从未被强行逐字复制的相似含义文本处理得有多好，这正是之后能把真正逐字复制分离出来的依据。\n\n*语义近邻基线 $B_{s}$ 是模型在检查点 t 上对跨度 s 的 k=8 个最近释义窗口的逐 token 交叉熵均值，用于把逐字记忆与单纯的主题熟悉度区分开。*\n$$ B_s = \\frac{1}{k}\\sum_{j=1}^{k} \\mathrm{CE}\\big(\\mathcal{M}_t, \\mathrm{nbr}_j(s)\\big), \\quad k = 8 \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 把跨度和它的语义近邻比较，能把真正逐字的记忆与模型普遍觉得容易的文本区分开。\n4. 对每个跨度，观察其近邻基线与自身损失之差在早期快照（训练前 20%）上的变化。把这个差在早期快照上累加（即差值曲线下的面积），再除以该跨度到目前为止被展示给模型的次数，得到每次曝光的坍缩速率。此外，对同一条「差随时间变化」的曲线拟合一条简单曲线，读出它的斜率（下降有多快）和曲率（下降是在加速还是在趋平）。把这三个数——每次曝光的坍缩速率、斜率、曲率——打包成该跨度的一个特征向量。除以展示次数让它保持为一个速率，这样它就不会偷偷只是在度量文本出现得有多频繁。\n\n*轨迹特征 $\\Sigma _{s}$ 是近邻基线 $B_{s}(t)$ 与跨度自身逐 token 损失 $L_{s}(t)$ 之差在早期窗口 $t \\in $ (0, $\\tau ]$ 上的面积，再除以该跨度到目前为止的曝光次数 $n_{s}(\\tau )$，得到每次曝光的坍缩速率，而非原始频次计数。*\n$$ \\Sigma_s = \\frac{1}{n_s(\\tau)} \\int_{0}^{\\tau} \\big[\\, B_s(t) - L_s(t) \\,\\big]\\, dt, \\quad \\tau = 0.2 \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 除以曝光次数让信号保持为一个速率，这样它就不会偷偷只是「高频文本会被记住」。\n\n### 预测器与因果验证\n*拟合早期 checkpoint 预测器，与成品模型检测器对比，并用轨迹打乱对照做因果验证。*\n\n5. 把跨度分成训练集和留出测试集（70/30），划分时在「是否最终被记忆」以及「注入 vs 自然」两个维度上保持均衡，并让每一对注入配对完整地落在同一侧，以防孪生份跨集泄漏。训练一个简单的逻辑斯谛预测器，它只接受 20% 处的三个特征（每次曝光的坍缩速率、斜率、曲率）——不接受任何来自成品模型的信息——来预测训练末尾的记忆标签。在留出测试跨度上，测量它对已记忆跨度的排序能力(extraction-recall AUC)，并与在「成品模型」上计算的两个检测器对比：一个基于模型内部表示的几何性质(intrinsic dimension，内在维度)，一个基于把记忆归因到特定模型组件(attribution，归因)。关键对比是这个训练早期的预测器能否匹敌甚至超过这些末尾的检测器。\n\n*预测器把跨度 s 在 t=1 处被逐字记忆的概率输出为 $[B_{s} -  L_{s}]$ 三个早期轨迹矩（水平量 $\\Sigma _{s}$、斜率 $slope_{s}$、曲率 $curv_{s}$）的逻辑斯谛函数，整个过程不引入任何成品模型的读数。*\n$$ \\hat{p}(s) = \\sigma\\big(w_0 + w_1 \\Sigma_s + w_2\\, \\mathrm{slope}_s + w_3\\, \\mathrm{curv}_s\\big) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 如果一个训练早期的信号能匹敌甚至超过末尾的检测器，那记忆确实在训练进行到一半时就已可判定。\n6. 做两项检查。第一（因果）：只在留出的注入跨度上对照注入记录给预测器打分，并在频次匹配对照上加入一个只用原始重复次数的预测器——这个只看次数的预测器应落在随机水平，而真正的信号应高于随机水平，从而表明信号追踪的是真正的原因而不只是频次。第二（打乱对照）：在计算斜率和曲率之前打乱每个跨度早期快照的时间顺序（这保留了完全相同的一组损失数值和相同的曝光次数，只破坏快照之间的先后顺序），重新计算特征、重训、再测量预测质量——它应坍缩回训练末尾的基线。如果确实如此，那么承载预测的是快照之间的时序模式，而不仅仅是损失数值。\n   - _为什么_: 注入测试表明信号追踪的是真正的原因；打乱测试表明承载预测的是时序信息，而不只是损失数值。\n7. 在第二个模型规模和第二片真实语料上重做读损失和拟合预测器，使用相同的早期快照和相同的 20% 处特征。用两种方式报告：把原预测器原封不动地用到新设置上，并且也在新设置上重训预测器的权重。【作者需决定：标题性结论是「坍缩速率特征本身可原样迁移」（沿用原权重），还是「只有在新设置上重新校准后才能预测」（重训权重），这是作者必须做的结论范围决定。】证明它在别处仍能预测，说明这个发现不是某一套设置的怪象。\n   - _为什么_: 证明它在别处仍能预测，说明这个发现不是某一套设置的假象。\n\n"},{"id":"61","run_dir":"run_prompt61_inplacettt","index":61,"title":"Budgeting In-Place Test-Time Training Against a Self-Maintained Source Anchor","title_zh":"以自维护源锚集为基准为原地测试时训练设定漂移预算","method_name":"Drift-Budgeted In-Place TTT (DB-TTT)","hook":"In-place test-time training has no in-stream readout of how far each update has bent the model away from its source competence, so on a long or shifting stream it silently overwrites what it was meant to keep. We give in-place TTT a label-free, per-step measure of that departure computed from the model's own agreement on a self-maintained source-anchor set, and use it as a drift budget that gates the update — letting the safe-to-move directions be decided by the current stream rather than fixed in advance.","anchor_pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","anchor_pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","domain_category":"Learning Theory & Statistics","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf maintains, during in-place test-time adaptation, an operational measure of how far the adapted function has departed from the source-trained function on the behavior it must keep — so nothing can hold a non-stationary, long test stream to a preservation budget and forgetting accumulates unbounded.","pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by manufacturing a label-free internal readout — the model's own predictive disagreement (symmetrized KL of current vs. source logits) on a self-maintained source-anchor evidence set — and turning its running sum into a per-step drift budget that gates the in-place update, with an explicit anchor-replay stabilizer against collapse.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"Every retrieved leaf that limits forgetting does so by freezing a fixed, pre-chosen set of parameters (subset selection, layer choice, BN-only), inheriting from a shared ancestor the assumption that the set of directions safe to move at test time can be fixed in advance and independently of the incoming distribution; no retrieved paper questions whether the safe-to-move set must be fixed ahead of the stream at all.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by auditing the selection rule that prior in-place methods bake in — a fixed, pre-chosen safe-to-move parameter set — and reframing that fixed-count choice as an online per-step budgeted choice: the same departure measure ranks directions each step, so the safe set is determined by the current distribution rather than fixed ahead of the stream.","is_anchor":false},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf reconciles the two opposing test-time regimes it must serve simultaneously — adapt enough to absorb the current shift, yet preserve enough that earlier competence survives — with any single quantity both objectives are expressed against, so the trade-off is managed by hand-tuned step sizes rather than measured.","pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by expressing both objectives against the same measured departure: adaptation pressure is the residual self-supervised loss on the current input and preservation pressure is the measured departure on the anchor set, and a single per-step budget allocation trades them off, removing the hand-tuned step-size schedule.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"test-time training / test-time adaptation under distribution shift (vision + sequence models)","n_papers":49,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":26},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":14,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Dual Test-Time Training for Out-of-Distribution Recommender System"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Improved Self-Training for Test-Time Adaptation"},{"source":"openalex","title":"A Comprehensive Survey on Test-Time Adaptation Under Distribution Shifts"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Efficient Test-Time Adaptation of Vision-Language Models"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Each Test Image Deserves A Specific Prompt: Continual Test-Time Adaptation for 2D Medical Image Segmentation"},{"source":"openalex","title":"A Comparative Analysis of High-Intensity Technique-Specific Intervals and Short Sprint Interval Training in Taekwondo Athletes: Effects on Cardiorespiratory Fitness and Anaerobic Power"}],"more":8},{"year":2025,"n":26,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"FineMedLM-o1: Enhancing the Medical Reasoning Ability of LLM from Supervised Fine-Tuning to Test-Time Training"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"SMART-PC: Skeletal Model Adaptation for Robust Test-Time Training in Point Clouds"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Contrastive Domain Adaptation with Test-Time Training for Out-of-Context News Detection"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Continuous Self-Improvement of Large Language Models by Test-time Training with Verifier-Driven Sample Selection"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Synchronizing Task Behavior: Aligning Multiple Tasks During Test-Time Training"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"LoRA-TTT: Low-Rank Test-Time Training for Vision-Language Models"}],"more":20},{"year":2026,"n":9,"papers":[{"source":"arxiv","title":"Learning to Discover at Test Time"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Adapting in the Dark: Efficient and Stable Test-Time Adaptation for Black-Box Models"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Efficient Test-Time Optimization for Depth Completion via Low-Rank Decoder Adaptation"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"ProtoTTA: Prototype-Guided Test-Time Adaptation"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Surprisal-Guided Selection: Compute-Optimal Test-Time Strategies for Execution-Grounded Code Generation"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Test-Time Training for Visual Foresight Vision-Language-Action Models"}],"more":3}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":18,"share":0.367},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":11,"share":0.224},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":7,"share":0.143},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":6,"share":0.122},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":5,"share":0.102},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":5,"share":0.102},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":4,"share":0.082},{"pattern_id":"targeted_self_supervised_objective","pattern_name":"Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective","count":4,"share":0.082}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Across the retrieved frontier, test-time training adapts a source-trained model by taking gradient steps on each incoming test instance/batch, but every leaf updates the weights with no quantity that certifies the adapted function still agrees with the source model on the in-distribution behavior it must preserve: once the test stream is non-stationary or long, the accumulated in-place steps push the weights off the source manifold and the model's earlier-acquired competence degrades, yet none of the methods measures or bounds this drift during adaptation. End-to-End Test-Time Training for Long Context (arxiv:2512.23675v2) compresses each context into the weights by continued next-token training but relies on a sliding window and offers no mechanism that keeps the in-place update from overwriting still-relevant earlier-context competence; Parameter-Selective Continual Test-Time Adaptation (openalex:W4405119726) and HR-OTTA (openalex:W4416252357) both recognize that updating all parameters is harmful and select a subset to move, but the subset is chosen by a saliency/heuristic score rather than derived from any guarantee that the unselected directions preserve the source function, so under a shifting stream the heuristic boundary itself drifts and the forgetting it was meant to stop reappears. The failure is therefore that in-place test-time updates have no operational measure of how far the adapted function has departed from the source-trained one, so nothing can hold the adaptation to a budget under non-stationarity.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2512.23675v2","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Reformulates long-context language modeling as continual learning and continues training the model in place at test time via next-token prediction, compressing read context into the weights with a standard sliding-window Transformer. It provides no quantity that bounds how far each in-place update moves the function from its pre-test state, so over a long or shifting stream the compression silently overwrites still-relevant earlier competence with no measured forgetting budget."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4405119726","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Reduces continual-TTA forgetting by updating only a selected subset of parameters chosen by a saliency criterion. The selection is a static heuristic on parameter importance rather than a derived guarantee that the frozen directions preserve the source function, so when the stream shifts the chosen boundary no longer matches what must be preserved and forgetting re-emerges."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416252357","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"HR-OTTA stabilizes online TTA with a hybrid fine-tuning scheme that mixes which layers are updated. The hybrid layer choice is tuned heuristically and gives no in-stream measure of function departure from the source model, so it controls the symptom (instability) without bounding the underlying drift."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4403922301","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"MemBN preserves robustness under continual TTA by keeping a memory of batch-norm statistics rather than letting them drift. It guards only the normalization statistics and leaves the weight space free to move with no preservation measure, so any drift carried by the weights themselves is uncontrolled."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"test-time training / test-time adaptation under distribution shift (vision + sequence models)","venue":"ICLR/NeurIPS-tier ML","time":"2026 cycle","data":["standard TTT/TTA shift benchmarks (e.g., CIFAR-10/100-C, ImageNet-C), continual/online TTA streams; sequence-model long-context streams"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with cloud GPU access","preference":"both","baseline":"In-Place Test-Time Training (ICLR source paper) and gradient-based TTT/TTA (TTT auxiliary-task family, entropy-min TTA)","limitation":"in-place gradient updates at test time drift the weights and erode the source-trained function (catastrophic forgetting / identity loss) over a non-stationary test stream, with no principled control over which parameters may move or how far","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object is the source-departure measure D_t, read off the model's own behavior on a self-maintained source-anchor evidence set A — every leg reads from or writes to D_t. A is a small fixed-size buffer (default |A| = 512 examples) of test inputs the pre-test (source) model classified with the highest confidence in the first warm-up window of the stream; their soft predictions under the FROZEN source model are cached once as reference distributions q_i (these are the model's own outputs, no labels). At step t, for the current adapted weights θ_t, D_t = (1/|A|) Σ_i SymKL(p_i(θ_t) || q_i), where p_i(θ_t) is the current model's softmax on anchor input i and SymKL is the symmetrized KL divergence; D_t is a pure model-internal readout, computable from one forward pass over A. Anchor leg (gap 1, C07): we manufacture D_t as the label-free preservation signal and convert it into a budget. The practitioner fixes one interpretable hyperparameter, the per-stream drift budget B (default B = 0.5 nats, the total SymKL departure tolerated over the whole stream); before each in-place update we form the candidate update g_t (the gradient of the current self-supervised TTT objective L_ssl, e.g. entropy minimization or the auxiliary task already used by the base TTT method) and accept a scaled step η_t·g_t only up to the largest η_t such that the predicted post-step departure increment ΔD_t = D(θ_t − η_t g_t) − D_t keeps the running sum Σ_{s≤t} max(ΔD_s,0) ≤ B; ΔD_t is estimated by a single extra forward pass over A at the trial point. When the remaining budget is exhausted the step is rejected (η_t = 0), which is the operational bound the prior leaves absent. The stabilizer against the C07 collapse mode is an explicit anchor-replay term: each step also takes a small distillation gradient pulling p_i(θ) back toward q_i on a random mini-subset of A, anchoring the source-distribution prior as a persistent mixture component so D_t cannot run away. Audit leg (gap 2, C11): prior in-place methods bake in a fixed selection rule — a pre-chosen safe-to-move parameter set (a layer choice / saliency mask / BN-only restriction) whose required structure is a fixed count decided before the stream; we pivot that rule by reframing 'which directions are safe to move' as a per-step budgeted choice scored by D_t. Concretely, at each step we rank parameter blocks by the ratio (reduction in L_ssl per unit predicted ΔD_t) and spend the step's local budget on the top-ranked blocks only, so the safe-to-move set is recomputed from the current distribution each step rather than fixed in advance; reverting to a fixed mask is exactly the pre-pivot baseline. Reconciliation leg (gap 3, C07): because adaptation pressure (∂L_ssl) and preservation pressure (∂D_t) are now expressed against the same A and the same budget B, the adapt-versus-preserve trade-off is the single budget-allocation decision above — there is no separate hand-tuned step-size schedule, the step size is whatever the remaining budget permits. All three legs therefore share one module (the D_t measure on A); the audit leg adds only the per-block ranking, not a second object.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The three gaps share machinery because all reduce to ONE missing quantity — a measured departure of the adapted function from the source — and the evidence is that gaps 1 and 3 are explicitly phrased against 'a single quantity both objectives are expressed against', while gap 2's fixed-set assumption is exactly what a per-step departure ranking dissolves; so D_t on A is built once and read by all three, with only the per-block ranking added for the audit leg. (b) I considered two rejected designs: (i) an offline Fisher/EWC importance penalty that weights parameter movement by source-task curvature — rejected as a regression to method_lineage node c0, since its importance is estimated offline and fixed, which is precisely the fixed-ahead-of-stream assumption gap 2 audits; (ii) a reward/policy trust-region step that constrains each update to a divergence ball around the previous model — rejected as a regression to node c1, whose divergence ball is around the PREVIOUS step (so drift still compounds monotonically) and which is reward-driven. DB-TTT instead measures departure from the FIXED source reference q_i on a self-maintained anchor set and budgets the CUMULATIVE departure over the stream — a source neither c0 nor c1 occupies — which is what gives a true preservation bound rather than a per-step leash.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: take a standard TTT/TTA backbone (a ResNet/ViT pre-trained on the source task) and run continual in-place TTT over a long non-stationary corruption stream (e.g., CIFAR-10-C / ImageNet-C with corruption type changing every few thousand examples and revisiting earlier corruptions), comparing free in-place TTT, a fixed parameter-subset baseline, and DB-TTT under matched compute. If the candidate works, two metrics move: online accuracy on the shifting stream stays at least as high as free in-place TTT early, AND final source-set accuracy (forgetting metric) degrades far less for DB-TTT — the gap widens as the stream lengthens, with the largest separation on revisited-earlier-corruption segments. The named load-bearing variable is the cumulative source-departure D_t measured on the anchor set A; the mechanism distinguisher is the negative-control that replaces the FIXED source references q_i with the previous-step model's outputs (making the budget a per-step divergence leash rather than a cumulative source budget): under this control, predicted final source-set accuracy should fall back toward the free in-place TTT level (forgetting returns) even though the per-step divergence stays bounded, because departure from source compounds. A positive control that gates updates using ONLY D_t with a single global budget (no per-block ranking) should recover most of the forgetting-reduction effect, identifying the cumulative-source budget — not the ranking — as the load-bearing piece.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2512.23675v2","delta":"They continue in-place next-token training with a sliding window and provide no quantity bounding departure from pre-test competence; we construct a cumulative source-departure measure on a self-maintained anchor set and a per-stream budget that operationally bounds that departure, which their method does not produce."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4405119726","delta":"They reduce forgetting by freezing a saliency-selected parameter subset fixed before the stream; we derive the safe-to-move set per-step from the current distribution by ranking blocks against the measured departure, so the selection adapts to shift instead of being fixed ahead of it."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416252357","delta":"HR-OTTA stabilizes online TTA with a heuristic hybrid layer-mix and no in-stream measure of function departure; we make the update gate a measured cumulative departure from a fixed source reference, giving a budget rather than a tuned mix."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4403922301","delta":"MemBN preserves only batch-norm statistics via a statistics memory; we preserve the full predictive function by budgeting weight-space departure measured on cached source outputs, covering drift their BN-only guard leaves uncontrolled."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4405119726","what_step_was_missed":"Parameter-Selective Continual TTA selects which parameters may move, but it scores importance once, ahead of the stream, against a static saliency criterion and never constructs an in-stream measure of how far the adapted function has departed from the source; to already be our contribution it would have needed to (a) build a cumulative departure quantity on a self-maintained source-anchor reference set computed each step and (b) convert that quantity into a per-step budget that re-derives the safe-to-move set from the current distribution — the measurement primitive and the budget mechanism it never constructs."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":279,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"Layer-1 hard floor did not fire: gap_closure_reject_check is borderline (no entry triggered), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat (RMemSafe) is NOT exact-mechanism overlap — RMemSafe gates instantaneous source-anchor strength by current-input entropy while the candidate budgets cumulative source-departure on a self-maintained anchor set, a different governing quantity. recipe_application_check.verdict = applied for all three legs (C07's diagnose/confine/stabilize and C11's pivot-a-budgeted-selection-rule are both performed in core_mechanism), so the idea is not built from the parent pattern's generic gist. The single borderline (C11's block-ranking shipped without a regret theorem) is non-fatal and addressed by the falsification isolating the cumulative-source budget as the load-bearing piece; the RMemSafe/RDumb++ threats are addressable in differentiation, so advance with these concerns surfaced for Phase 4.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf maintains, during in-place test-time adaptation, an operational measure of how far the adapted function has departed from the source-trained function on the behavior it must keep — so nothing can hold a non-stationary, long test stream to a preservation budget and forgetting accumulates unbounded.","main_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is a manufactured internal signal whose validity silently rests on an assumption that does not survive deployment (model calibration, a stationary/known-finite set of shifts, or covert use of target/test labels), or recombining well-known components without one load-bearing mechanistic insight, compounded by thin single-dataset validation.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A label-free signal whose validity depends on model calibration silently fails on exactly the deep networks known to be poorly calibrated — validate a surrogate where its core assumption is weakest, not where it is convenient.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"D_t is a divergence between current and CACHED-source soft predictions on the same anchor inputs, not an entropy/calibration confidence, so it does not assume calibration; it measures relative departure, well-defined even for a miscalibrated network."},{"lesson_quoted":"Recasting a continuous shift as a discrete, known, finite set of types indexed against a precomputed lookup table collapses the moment an unanticipated or mixed shift arrives.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The method assumes no shift taxonomy at all — the budget gate is shift-agnostic and recomputed continuously from the live stream, so mixed/unanticipated shifts are handled identically."},{"lesson_quoted":"Importing a generic continual-learning blending or interpolation technique into a new modality without identifying that modality's specific dynamics lever reads as recombination, not contribution.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The anchor-replay stabilizer resembles generic replay; it is salvaged by the load-bearing lever (the cumulative source-departure budget D_t), but Phase 4 must show replay alone (without the budget) does not recover the effect — the falsification's positive control does exactly this."},{"lesson_quoted":"Using target or test-set information during adaptation invites a label-leakage objection that undermines the very source-free, label-free deployment setting the method claims.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The anchor set is built from the model's own high-confidence predictions on early stream inputs and uses only the frozen model's soft outputs as references — no labels, no test-set targets are consulted."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"Every retrieved leaf that limits forgetting does so by freezing a fixed, pre-chosen set of parameters (subset selection, layer choice, BN-only), inheriting from a shared ancestor the assumption that the set of directions safe to move at test time can be fixed in advance and independently of the incoming distribution; no retrieved paper questions whether the safe-to-move set must be fixed ahead of the stream at all.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The dominant failure is substituting one selection rule for another that performs better empirically while omitting the theorem that explains when and why it wins; a second is pivoting an assumption the community regards as a reasonable modeling choice rather than a genuine restriction.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Substituting one selection heuristic for another without a theorem stating when and why it wins reads as an engineering combination, not a contribution, no matter how clean the empirical gain.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The per-step block ranking is currently a selection heuristic; it is anchored by the measured-budget argument (it wins precisely when shift is non-stationary so a fixed mask is mis-targeted), but the candidate ships a method, not a regret theorem, so this is a surfaced concern rather than a triggered reject — the falsification isolates the budget (not the ranking) as load-bearing, keeping the headline on the measured-budget construction."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pivoting an assumption the community treats as a reasonable modeling choice — rather than first proving it a genuine restriction — leaves both motivation and novelty in doubt.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The fixed-safe-set assumption is shown load-bearing by the lineage: Parameter-Selective CTTA's own residue is that the fixed boundary mis-targets under shift, so striking it changes the measurable forgetting outcome — a genuine restriction, not a benign modeling choice."},{"lesson_quoted":"Unlocking a new capability by violating an assumption while ignoring a protective property it guarded — detectability, validity, identifiability — invites rejection on the overlooked side effect rather than the headline result.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The protective property the fixed mask guarded (bounded forgetting) is the very thing the per-step budget makes explicit and preserves; the pivot does not silently sacrifice a guarded property."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf reconciles the two opposing test-time regimes it must serve simultaneously — adapt enough to absorb the current shift, yet preserve enough that earlier competence survives — with any single quantity both objectives are expressed against, so the trade-off is managed by hand-tuned step sizes rather than measured.","main_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"A manufactured internal signal whose validity rests on a deployment-fragile assumption, or recombination of standard components without one load-bearing mechanistic insight, compounded by thin validation.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A multi-branch or ensemble reweighting mechanism that overlaps with standard multi-task/mixture-of-experts ensembling must explicitly beat both the single-model and the standard-ensemble baselines, or the gain is credited to prior art.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"There is no ensemble or multi-branch reweighting; the trade-off is a single per-step budget allocation over one model, so this ensemble-specific lesson does not apply."},{"lesson_quoted":"Reusing standard sequential machinery (chaining each step's posterior as the next prior) without a new stabilizer amplifies noise and looks derivative of prior adaptation work.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The method does NOT chain the previous step as the reference — it measures departure from a FIXED source reference q_i, and adds an explicit anchor-replay stabilizer, which is exactly the new stabilizer this lesson asks for."}],"verdict":"clear"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No entry is triggered. The audit leg (assumption_audit_and_pivot / C11) is borderline because the per-step block ranking is a selection rule shipped without an accompanying regret theorem; this is a load-bearing-adjacent but non-fatal concern, mitigated by the falsification isolating the cumulative-source budget (not the ranking) as the load-bearing piece."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf maintains, during in-place test-time adaptation, an operational measure of how far the adapted function has departed from the source-trained function on the behavior it must keep — so nothing can hold a non-stationary, long test stream to a preservation budget and forgetting accumulates unbounded.","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Treat an already-trained model's own internal-state readouts as the manufactured supervisory signal, pairing a mechanistic diagnosis that localizes the failure with a surgically confined correction on a minimal lever while the backbone stays frozen, and always bolt on an explicit stabilizer against collapse.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism manufactures D_t = mean SymKL(current||source) on the self-maintained anchor set A (the internal-state readout), confines the correction to a budgeted, per-block subset rather than full updates, and bolts on the anchor-replay distillation term as the explicit stabilizer against the runaway-collapse mode — the exact diagnose-localize / minimize-on-a-tiny-lever / stabilize-against-collapse triad.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"Every retrieved leaf that limits forgetting does so by freezing a fixed, pre-chosen set of parameters (subset selection, layer choice, BN-only), inheriting from a shared ancestor the assumption that the set of directions safe to move at test time can be fixed in advance and independently of the incoming distribution; no retrieved paper questions whether the safe-to-move set must be fixed ahead of the stream at all.","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Center on a selection/acquisition rule and pivot the single assumption baked into its criterion or required structure (a fixed trial count, a privileged anchor, deterministic always-pick-the-best), either relaxing the structural crutch or reframing the selection task as a more tractable class.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism names the prior selection rule (a fixed, pre-chosen safe-to-move parameter set whose required structure is a fixed count decided before the stream) and pivots it by reframing 'which directions are safe to move' as a per-step budgeted choice scored by D_t, so the fixed-count crutch is relaxed to an online per-step budgeted selection — the cluster's relax/reframe move on a budgeted selection rule.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf reconciles the two opposing test-time regimes it must serve simultaneously — adapt enough to absorb the current shift, yet preserve enough that earlier competence survives — with any single quantity both objectives are expressed against, so the trade-off is managed by hand-tuned step sizes rather than measured.","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Manufacture a single internal-state signal and express the control objective against it on a confined lever, with a stabilizer — rather than tuning a foreign schedule.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism expresses BOTH adaptation pressure (∂L_ssl) and preservation pressure (∂D_t on A) against the same anchor object and the same budget B, making the trade-off the single budget-allocation decision instead of a hand-tuned step size — the C07 move of governing adaptation by one internal signal.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Each leg performs its cited cluster's distinctive move: C07's diagnose/confine/stabilize triad is present in the D_t-budget-replay construction, and C11's pivot-a-budgeted-selection-rule move is present in the per-step safe-set reframing — none collapses to the parent pattern's generic gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["self_supervised_signal_engineering","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; the candidate's composition set is {self_supervised_signal_engineering, assumption_audit_and_pivot}, which matches none of them."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"arxiv: Reliability-Gated Source Anchoring for Continual Test-Time Adaptation (RMemSafe)","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"RMemSafe (2026-05) is the closest collision hit: it also uses a frozen-source predictive signal to govern how much the in-place update is coupled to the source, gating the source-anchor term by the frozen source's normalized predictive entropy on the current input so that when the source becomes unreliable the anchor strength vanishes. The candidate's claim stands or falls on whether its governing quantity is genuinely different: RMemSafe's gate is an INSTANTANEOUS, per-input reliability scalar that attenuates an anchoring loss term, whereas DB-TTT's D_t is a CUMULATIVE departure of the adapted function from cached source reference outputs on a self-maintained anchor evidence set, accumulated over the whole stream into a finite drift budget B that hard-caps total forgetting and, when spent, freezes updates — plus a per-step safe-to-move block selection RMemSafe does not have. RMemSafe controls when to trust the source; DB-TTT bounds how far the model may ever drift from it. Because the two govern different quantities (instantaneous anchor strength vs. cumulative departure budget) the candidate is not subsumed, but RMemSafe is the head-to-head baseline the paper must beat and the differentiation must be stated explicitly.","addressable_via":"differentiation_from_lit and reviewer_concerns_and_responses must name RMemSafe and RDumb++ explicitly and contrast the cumulative-departure budget + per-step block selection against RMemSafe's instantaneous entropy gate and RDumb++'s drift-triggered reset; the core_mechanism quantity itself already differs, so no mechanism change is required."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Budgeting In-Place Test-Time Training Against a Self-Maintained Source Anchor\n\n**Method.** Drift-Budgeted In-Place TTT (DB-TTT)\n\n## Motivation\nIn-place test-time training (TTT) takes a model that was already trained on some source data and keeps nudging its weights as new test data arrives, so it can cope with whatever has changed between training and deployment. The hidden danger is that nobody is keeping track of how far these nudges have carried the model away from what it originally knew. On a short, stable stream of test data that is fine, but on a long stream — or one where the kind of data keeps changing — the nudges pile up, the weights drift away from where they started, and the model quietly forgets the skills it was supposed to keep. Recent work has noticed this. End-to-End Test-Time Training for Long Context makes the drift problem central by continuously training the model in place as it reads, but it never measures how far it has drifted. Parameter-Selective Continual Test-Time Adaptation and HR-OTTA both try to limit forgetting by only letting a fixed, pre-chosen group of weights move — but they decide that group before the stream begins, so when the data shifts, the group they froze is the wrong one and forgetting comes back. What makes a fix possible now is a simple observation: the model's own level of agreement with its original self, measured on a small set of examples it keeps refreshing from the live test data, gives a label-free yardstick for how far it has departed from source. Our method, Drift-Budgeted In-Place TTT (DB-TTT), turns that yardstick into a spending budget: you set one number — how much total departure you will tolerate over the whole stream — and the method only allows each in-place update up to the point where it would overspend that budget, then freezes. The same yardstick also decides, fresh at every step, which weights are safe to move, instead of fixing that choice in advance. When the gap closes, in-place TTT finally has a knob that bounds forgetting on an arbitrarily long, shifting stream rather than letting it accumulate without limit.\n\n## Method\n### Self-maintained source-anchor measure\n*Builds the anchor set A from the model's own high-confidence test inputs and reads the label-free departure $D_{t}$ against cached source references.*\n\n1. During the first 200 batches of the test stream, run the original frozen model and, for each input, record how confident it is (its largest softmax probability). Keep the 512 most-confident inputs as an anchor set A, but limit how many can come from any one class (at most about 512 divided by the number of classes) so the set stays balanced across classes. For each kept input, save the model's full soft prediction (the probability it assigns to every class, not just the top guess) as that input's fixed reference answer. No true labels are used.\n   - _Why_: These reference answers are the model's own original behavior, so later we can measure how far it has drifted just by checking how much its answers on A have changed.\n2. At the model's current weights, run one forward pass over all 512 anchor inputs to get the current soft predictions. For each anchor, measure how different the current soft prediction is from the saved reference using a symmetric form of the Kullback-Leibler (KL) divergence — averaging the divergence in both directions — and clip any zero probabilities to a tiny floor so the math stays finite. Average these 512 differences into one number $D_{t}$ (in nats): the bigger it is, the further the model has drifted from its original self. Comparing against the fixed saved answers (not the model's own confidence) is what makes this work even when the model is poorly calibrated.\n\n*The departure measure $D_{t}$ is the mean symmetrized KL divergence over the anchor set A between the current model's $softmax p_{i}(\\theta _{t})$ on anchor input i and the frozen-source reference $q_{i}$ cached once under $\\theta _{0}$ — a label-free, model-internal readout computable from one forward pass over A.*\n$$ D_t = \\frac{1}{|A|}\\sum_{i \\in A} \\mathrm{SymKL}\\big(p_i(\\theta_t)\\,\\|\\,q_i\\big), \\quad q_i = p_i(\\theta_0) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: $D_{t}$ is a single label-free number saying how far the model has departed from its source self; because it compares against the FIXED original answers it works even if the model is poorly calibrated.\n\n### Drift-budgeted in-place update\n*Forms the base TTT gradient and accepts the largest in-place step that keeps cumulative departure within the per-stream budget B, freezing when spent.*\n\n3. On the new test batch, compute the same self-supervised adaptation loss the underlying Test-Time Training (TTT) method already uses — for example minimizing the prediction entropy, or its built-in helper task such as predicting an image's rotation — and back-propagate it to get the proposed weight-update direction $g_{t}.$ Nothing new is added to the adaptation signal here; $g_{t}$ is exactly the update ordinary in-place TTT would make. The new part is that this update will next be checked against the drift measure instead of being applied at a fixed, hand-tuned step size.\n   - _Why_: This is the normal adaptation signal; the new part is that we will weigh it against the departure measure instead of trusting a hand-tuned step size.\n4. Try a shrinking sequence of step sizes — the base learning rate, then half it, then half again, and so on — applied only to the top blocks chosen in the previous step. For each candidate step size, do a trial update and one forward pass over the anchor set to estimate how much total drift it would add, and accept the largest step whose running total of drift still fits inside the overall budget B. Apply that update to the selected blocks (the accepted step may be zero if even the smallest size would overspend). This one choice — how big a step fits in the remaining budget — is what trades off adapting now versus preserving later, so there is no separate hand-tuned step-size schedule.\n\n*The accepted step scale $\\eta _{t}$ is the largest non-negative scale whose predicted post-step departure increment $\\Delta D_{t}$ keeps the running sum of positive departures within the per-stream budget B; when the budget is exhausted $\\eta _{t} = 0$ and the update freezes — the operational preservation bound.*\n$$ \\eta_t = \\max\\Big\\{\\eta \\geq 0 : \\sum_{s \\leq t} \\max\\big(\\Delta D_s(\\eta),\\,0\\big) \\leq B\\Big\\}, \\quad \\Delta D_t(\\eta) = D(\\theta_t - \\eta g_t) - D_t \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This is the one decision that trades off adapting now versus preserving later, all measured against the same budget — no separate hand-tuned schedule.\n5. Recompute the drift measure $D_{t}$ over the anchor set with one forward pass, and add any increase since the last step to a running 'spent' total (only increases are charged, so a temporary recovery does not give budget back). Once the spent total reaches the budget B, stop updating the weights for the rest of the stream while still answering queries normally. Capping the running total of increases at B means the total forgetting is bounded by design — unlike a per-step limit, which keeps each step small but lets the drift quietly pile up.\n   - _Why_: Capping the running total of departures at B means total forgetting is bounded by construction, not by a per-step leash that still compounds.\n\n### Per-step safe-to-move selection\n*Re-derives the safe-to-move parameter set each step by ranking blocks against the measured departure, instead of fixing it before the stream.*\n\n6. Split the network into blocks — one weight matrix per layer — giving a few dozen blocks. For each block, take a tiny trial nudge in the update direction restricted to that block, then check two things with one forward pass each: how much it would increase the drift measure (on the anchor set) and how much it would lower the adaptation loss (on the current batch). Rank blocks by adaptation-lowered-per-unit-drift-added, and spend this step's drift budget only on the top blocks. This recomputes which weights are safe to move from the current data every step, instead of freezing a set chosen before the stream. 【author decision: how many top blocks to move each step — a fixed small number versus adding blocks until the payoff per block drops off — is a design choice trading how surgical each step is against how fast the model adapts.】\n\n*Each parameter block b is ranked by the reduction in the self-supervised loss $L_{ssl}$ it would produce per unit predicted departure $\\Delta D_{t}$ it would incur, so the step's budget is spent on the blocks that buy the most adaptation per unit forgetting — and the safe-to-move set is recomputed from the current distribution each step.*\n$$ \\mathrm{score}(b) = \\frac{\\Delta L_{\\mathrm{ssl}}(b)}{\\Delta D_t(b) + \\varepsilon}, \\quad b \\in \\mathcal{B} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Instead of freezing a fixed set of weights chosen before the stream, we recompute which weights are safe to move every step from the current data, so the choice tracks the shift.\n\n### Stabilizer and causal validation\n*Adds the anchor-replay collapse guard and the previous-step-reference negative control that isolates the cumulative-source budget as load-bearing.*\n\n7. After the budgeted update, gently pull the model back toward its source self on the anchor set: pick a random 32 of the anchor inputs and take one small distillation step that nudges the current predictions toward the saved reference answers, at a small fixed strength (about one-tenth of the base learning rate). This keeps the model from drifting away from its source distribution between budget checks. This nudge is a safety stabilizer, not the main mechanism — a control experiment confirms that this replay alone, without the cumulative drift budget, does not bound forgetting.\n\n*The anchor-replay stabilizer applies a small distillation gradient pulling the current predictions back toward the cached source references $q_{i}$ on a random 32-example subset of A, anchoring the source-distribution prior so $D_{t}$ cannot run away — the explicit guard against the collapse mode.*\n$$ g^{\\mathrm{anc}}_t = \\nabla_{\\theta}\\,\\frac{1}{|A'|}\\sum_{i \\in A'} \\mathrm{KL}\\big(q_i\\,\\|\\,p_i(\\theta_t)\\big), \\quad A' \\subset A,\\ |A'| = 32 \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This keeps the model from running away from its source distribution; but it only helps because the budget does the real work — replay alone won't bound forgetting.\n8. While the stream runs, record the per-step task accuracy and the drift measure. Compare against ordinary (ungated) in-place Test-Time Training (TTT) and a fixed-set baseline under the same compute, on two headline numbers: accuracy on the shifting stream, and how much accuracy on a held-out source test set drops from start to end (the forgetting measure). Then run the key control: redo everything but use the PREVIOUS step's model outputs as the reference instead of the fixed source answers — turning the budget into a step-to-step leash rather than a cumulative source budget. If forgetting comes back under this control even though each step's change stays small, that proves the cumulative departure from source, not a per-step limit, is what bounds forgetting.\n   - _Why_: If forgetting returns under the previous-step reference even though the per-step gap stays small, that proves the cumulative-source budget — not just a divergence ball — is what bounds forgetting.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 以自维护源锚集为基准为原地测试时训练设定漂移预算\n\n**方法名称.** Drift-Budgeted In-Place TTT (DB-TTT)\n\n## 研究动机\n原地测试时训练（in-place TTT）拿一个已经在某些源数据上训练好的模型，在新的测试数据到来时不断微调它的权重，从而应对训练到部署之间发生的任何变化。隐藏的危险是：没有人在记录这些微调究竟把模型带离它最初所知有多远。在短而稳定的测试流上这没问题，但在很长的流上——或者数据种类不断变化的流上——微调会越积越多，权重漂离起点，模型悄悄忘掉它本该保留的技能。最近的工作注意到了这点。End-to-End Test-Time Training for Long Context 让漂移问题成为核心，它在读取时持续地原地训练模型，却从不度量自己漂了多远。Parameter-Selective Continual Test-Time Adaptation 和 HR-OTTA 都想通过只让一组固定的、预先选好的权重移动来限制遗忘——但它们在流开始之前就定下这组权重，于是当数据偏移时，它们冻住的那组就是错的，遗忘又回来了。现在之所以能修复，靠一个简单的观察：模型在一小组它持续从实时测试数据刷新的样本上，与自己最初状态的一致程度，给出了一把无需标签的尺子，衡量它departure 源有多远。我们的方法 Drift-Budgeted In-Place TTT（DB-TTT）把这把尺子变成一份花费预算：你设一个数——整条流上你愿意容忍的总 departure——方法只允许每次原地更新走到不超支这份预算为止，然后冻结。同一把尺子还在每一步重新决定哪些权重可以安全移动，而不是预先定死。当这个空白被填上，原地 TTT 终于有了一个旋钮，能在任意长、不断偏移的流上对遗忘设界，而不是任由它无限累积。\n\n## 方法\n### 自维护源锚度量\n*从模型自己的高置信测试输入构建锚集 A，对照缓存的源参考读出无需标签的 departure $D_{t}$。*\n\n1. 在测试流的前 200 个 batch 里，运行原始冻结模型，对每个输入记录它有多自信（即最大的 softmax 概率）。保留最自信的 512 个输入作为锚集 A，但限制每个类别最多能贡献多少个（大约不超过 512 除以类别数），让这组样本在各类别间保持均衡。对每个保留的输入，把模型完整的 soft prediction（它分给每个类别的概率，而不只是最高那一项）保存为该输入的固定参考答案。全程不使用任何真实标签。\n   - _为什么_: 这些参考答案是模型自己最初的行为，所以之后只要看它在 A 上的答案变了多少，就能度量它漂了多远。\n2. 在模型当前权重下，对全部 512 个锚输入做一次前向，得到当前的 soft prediction。对每个锚样本，用对称形式的 Kullback-Leibler(KL) 散度——即两个方向的散度取平均——度量当前 soft prediction 与保存的参考答案差多少，并把任何零概率裁剪到一个极小的下限，使计算保持有限。把这 512 个差异平均成一个数 $D_{t}$（单位 nats）：它越大，说明模型 departure 其最初自身越远。对照固定保存的答案（而不是模型自身的置信度）正是它即使在模型校准很差时也成立的原因。\n\n*departure 度量 $D_{t}$ 是在锚集 A 上、当前模型在锚样本 i 上的 $softmax p_{i}(\\theta _{t})$ 与一次性缓存的冻结源参考 $q_{i}$ 之间对称 KL 散度的均值，是一个无需标签、仅靠模型自身输出、对 A 做一次前向即可算出的内部读数。*\n$$ D_t = \\frac{1}{|A|}\\sum_{i \\in A} \\mathrm{SymKL}\\big(p_i(\\theta_t)\\,\\|\\,q_i\\big), \\quad q_i = p_i(\\theta_0) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: $D_{t}$ 是一个无需标签的数，表示模型 departure 其源自身有多远；因为它对照的是 FIXED 的最初答案，即使模型校准很差它也成立。\n\n### 漂移预算化原地更新\n*形成基础 TTT 梯度，并接受使累积 departure 仍在整流预算 B 之内的最大原地步长，预算耗尽即冻结。*\n\n3. 在新的测试 batch 上，计算底层 Test-Time Training(TTT) 方法本就在用的同一个自监督适应损失——例如最小化预测熵，或它内置的辅助任务（如预测图像旋转角度）——并反向传播得到拟议的权重更新方向 $g_{t}$。这里不给适应信号添加任何新东西；$g_{t}$ 正是普通原地 TTT 会做的更新。新的部分在于：这个更新接下来会对照漂移度量来检验，而不是以一个固定的、手调的步长直接施加。\n   - _为什么_: 这是常规的适应信号；新的部分是我们会拿它去和 departure 度量权衡，而不是信赖一个手调步长。\n4. 尝试一串逐渐缩小的步长——基础学习率，然后减半，再减半，依此类推——只施加到上一步选出的排名靠前的块上。对每个候选步长，做一次试探性更新并对锚集做一次前向，估计它会增加多少总漂移，接受使漂移累计仍落在总预算 B 之内的最大步长。把该更新施加到被选中的块上（如果连最小步长都会超支，接受的步长可以为 0）。这个唯一的选择——多大的步长能塞进剩余预算——正是在「现在适应」与「日后保持」之间做权衡的地方，因此没有单独的手调步长时间表。\n\n*被接受的步长 $\\eta _{t}$ 是使得预测的步后 departure 增量 $\\Delta D_{t}$ 之正部累加仍不超过整流预算 B 的最大非负步长；预算耗尽时 $\\eta _{t} = 0$，更新冻结——这就是可操作的保持界。*\n$$ \\eta_t = \\max\\Big\\{\\eta \\geq 0 : \\sum_{s \\leq t} \\max\\big(\\Delta D_s(\\eta),\\,0\\big) \\leq B\\Big\\}, \\quad \\Delta D_t(\\eta) = D(\\theta_t - \\eta g_t) - D_t \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这是权衡「现在适应」与「日后保持」的唯一决定，全部对照同一份预算来衡量——没有单独的手调时间表。\n5. 用一次前向重算漂移度量 $D_{t}$，把自上一步以来的任何增量加进一个累计的「已花」总额（只对增量计费，所以临时的恢复不会退还预算）。一旦已花总额达到预算 B，就在余下的流上停止更新权重，同时照常回答查询。把增量的累计总额封顶在 B，意味着总遗忘由设计就被设界——这与每步限制不同：后者让每一步都很小，却任由漂移悄悄累积。\n   - _为什么_: 把 departure 的累积总量封顶在 B，意味着总遗忘由构造就被设界，而不是靠一个仍会累积的每步约束。\n\n### 每步安全可动集选择\n*每步按对照度量的 departure 给块排序来重新算出安全可动参数集，而不是在流开始前定死。*\n\n6. 把网络拆成若干块——每层一个权重矩阵——得到几十个块。对每个块，沿更新方向只在该块上做一个极小的试探性微调，然后各用一次前向检查两件事：它会让漂移度量（在锚集上）增加多少，以及会让适应损失（在当前 batch 上）下降多少。按「每单位漂移增量换来的适应损失下降」给块排序，本步的漂移预算只花在排名靠前的块上。这样每一步都从当前数据重新算出哪些权重可以安全移动，而不是冻结一组在流开始前就选好的权重。【作者需决定：每步移动多少个排名靠前的块——是固定的一个小数目，还是不断加块直到每块的收益下降为止——这是一个设计选择，在「每步多么手术刀式」与「模型适应多快」之间权衡。】\n\n*每个参数块 b 按其能带来的自监督损失 $L_{ssl}$ 下降量除以其会引发的预测 departure $\\Delta D_{t}$ 来排序，于是该步预算花在每单位遗忘换取最多适应的块上——安全可动集每步都从当前分布重新算出。*\n$$ \\mathrm{score}(b) = \\frac{\\Delta L_{\\mathrm{ssl}}(b)}{\\Delta D_t(b) + \\varepsilon}, \\quad b \\in \\mathcal{B} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 不再冻结流开始前选好的一组固定权重，而是每步都从当前数据重新算出哪些权重可以安全移动，于是选择会跟着偏移走。\n\n### 稳定器与因果验证\n*加入 anchor-replay 崩塌防护，以及把累积源预算隔离为关键因素的 previous-step 参考负对照。*\n\n7. 在预算化更新之后，在锚集上把模型轻轻拉回它的源自身：随机选 32 个锚输入，做一个小的蒸馏步，把当前预测朝保存的参考答案方向轻推，强度固定且较小（约为基础学习率的十分之一）。这能让模型在两次预算检查之间不至于漂离源分布。这个轻推是一个安全稳定器，而不是主机制——一个对照实验确认：单靠这个 replay、没有累积漂移预算，是无法对遗忘设界的。\n\n*anchor-replay 稳定器在 A 的随机 32 样本子集上施加一个小的蒸馏梯度，把当前预测拉回缓存的源参考 $q_{i}$，把源分布先验锚住，使 $D_{t}$ 不会失控——这是对崩塌模式的显式防护。*\n$$ g^{\\mathrm{anc}}_t = \\nabla_{\\theta}\\,\\frac{1}{|A'|}\\sum_{i \\in A'} \\mathrm{KL}\\big(q_i\\,\\|\\,p_i(\\theta_t)\\big), \\quad A' \\subset A,\\ |A'| = 32 \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这能防止模型漂离源分布；但它之所以有效，是因为真正起作用的是预算——单靠 replay 无法对遗忘设界。\n8. 在流运行时，记录每步的任务准确率和漂移度量。在相同算力下，与普通（不设门控）的原地 Test-Time Training(TTT) 以及固定集基线对比两个核心数字：偏移流上的准确率，以及留出源测试集上的准确率从头到尾下降了多少（遗忘度量）。然后做关键对照：把一切重做一遍，但用 PREVIOUS-step（上一步）模型的输出作参考，而非固定的源答案——这就把预算变成一个步到步的牵绳，而不是累积的源预算。如果在这个对照下遗忘回来了——尽管每一步的变化仍然很小——就证明对遗忘设界的是累积的 departure 源，而不是某个每步限制。\n   - _为什么_: 如果在用上一步参考时遗忘回来了——尽管每步差距仍很小——就证明对遗忘设界的是累积源预算，而不仅仅是一个散度球。\n\n"},{"id":"62","run_dir":"run_prompt62_agenticopt","index":62,"title":"Banking the Plan: Cross-Task Reuse of Validated Tool-Call Subgraphs by Typed-State Matching","title_zh":"把计划存进银行：通过类型化状态匹配在任务间复用已验证的工具调用子图","method_name":"Plan Bank (typed-subgraph transplant planner)","hook":"Per-task tool planners like ToolTree re-expand ~70-95 search nodes for every task even when the decisive tool sub-chain was already executed and scored on a previous task; we make the unit of optimization a persistent, typed tool-call dependency graph the agent banks across tasks, so a new plan is assembled by transplanting validated sub-chains whose precondition/effect type signature matches the current intermediate state — search only the genuinely novel remainder. The structural claim: applicability of a banked sub-chain is decided by type-signature match on the planning state, not by request-text similarity, so reuse fires between surface-dissimilar tasks that share a dependency motif.","anchor_pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","anchor_pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","domain_category":"LLM Agents & Tool Use","patterns":[{"gap":"(additive) No retrieved leaf lets a planner SUBSTITUTE an already-validated tool-call sub-structure from a prior solved task in place of re-deriving it, so search/inference cost does not amortize across an agent's task stream — ToolTree re-searches per task, Plan Reuse only matches whole near-duplicate requests, and AgentSquare only reuses coarse module architectures; the outcome that is missing is cross-task reuse at the granularity of the concrete tool-call dependency subgraph, with a guarante","pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","sub_pattern":"C13 (Encode Structure by Construction)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by constructing the relational connectivity object — a typed tool-call dependency graph (nodes = tool invocations, edges = produces/consumes typed-artifact relations) accumulated across tasks — and a composition operator that transplants a banked sub-graph into the current plan exactly when its source type-signature unifies with the current planning state, so plan validity at the new state holds by construction (the C13 move: encode the connectivity topology so the structural property is captured, not relearned).","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"(subtractive) Every retrieved tool-planning leaf silently inherits the assumption that the unit of optimization is the SINGLE TASK's plan — that planning state is owned by one task and discarded at its boundary; no retrieved paper tests whether the optimized object must be the per-task plan at all, rather than a cross-task object the agent maintains and refines as it accumulates solved tasks.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by relocating the optimization locus (the C01 move: name the locus every method anchors on, show it is the wrong place, re-anchor): we audit the tacit claim 'the optimized object is the per-task plan, discarded at the task boundary', and re-anchor enforcement at the cross-task subgraph bank, demonstrating the per-task locus was an unnecessary convention by showing the same success is reached while node-expansion cost monotonically falls as the bank grows — a behavior the per-task locus structurally cannot produce.","is_anchor":false},{"gap":"(additive) No retrieved leaf indexes tool-call sub-structures by the INTERMEDIATE STATE / type-signature they consume and produce (rather than by request text), so reuse cannot fire between tasks that differ at the surface but share a dependency motif — the missing outcome is a way to recognize that two dissimilar tasks reach a point where the same validated sub-chain applies.","pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","sub_pattern":"C13 (Encode Structure by Construction)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by the same C13 construction's index: each banked sub-graph is keyed by its boundary type-signature (the typed set of artifacts it consumes at entry and produces at exit), and retrieval is a by-construction unification of that signature against the current planning state's available typed artifacts — so reuse fires on shared dependency motifs regardless of request-text similarity, the exact structural quantity a request-keyed cache cannot capture.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"LLM agentic systems — planning and tool-use optimization (multi-step, multi-tool task execution)","n_papers":50,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":26},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":8,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A Review of Prominent Paradigms for LLM-Based Agents: Tool Use, Planning (Including RAG), and Feedback Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Small LLMs Are Weak Tool Learners: A Multi-LLM Agent"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Large Language Model Enhanced Multi-Agent Systems for 6G Communications"},{"source":"openalex","title":"AgentSquare: Automatic LLM Agent Search in Modular Design Space"},{"source":"openalex","title":"A Simple Baseline for Uncertainty-Aware Language-Oriented Task Planner for Embodied Agents"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Language-Augmented Symbolic Planner for Open-World Task Planning"}],"more":2},{"year":2025,"n":33,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Encouraging Good Processes Without the Need for Good Answers: Reinforcement Learning for LLM Agent Planning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"HeuriGym: An Agentic Benchmark for LLM-Crafted Heuristics in Combinatorial Optimization"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Training Task Reasoning LLM Agents for Multi-Turn Task Planning via Single-Turn Reinforcement Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Batch Query Processing and Optimization for Agentic Workflows"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Hybrid Agentic AI and Multi-Agent Systems in Smart Manufacturing"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Improving Language Agents through BREW"}],"more":27},{"year":2026,"n":9,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Too Helpful to Be Safe: User-Mediated Attacks on Planning and Web-Use Agents"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"YouZhi: Towards High-Concurrency Financial LLMs via Adaptive GQA-to-MLA Transition"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"ToolTree: Efficient LLM Agent Tool Planning via Dual-Feedback Monte Carlo Tree Search and Bidirectional Pruning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"SCALAR: Learning and Composing Skills through LLM Guided Symbolic Planning and Deep RL Grounding"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Agent Planning Benchmark: A Diagnostic Framework for Planning Capabilities in LLM Agents"}],"more":3}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":11,"share":0.22},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":11,"share":0.22},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":8,"share":0.16},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":8,"share":0.16},{"pattern_id":"relax_discrete_search_to_continuous","pattern_name":"Relax Discrete Search to Continuous","count":6,"share":0.12},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":6,"share":0.12},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":5,"share":0.1},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":5,"share":0.1}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Across the retrieved tool-use-planning frontier, an LLM agent plans the tool-call structure for each task de novo: ToolTree (arxiv:2603.12740v1) runs a fresh dual-feedback MCTS over tool trajectories for every task, expanding ~70-95 nodes per query, and the search state is discarded once the task ends; greedy reactive selection (referenced therein) commits the whole plan in one forward pass. The unit of optimization is therefore the single task's plan, even though real toolsets induce heavily recurring sub-structures: T1 (openalex:W6979347639) shows multi-turn tasks are dominated by inter-tool DEPENDENCY motifs (a search-then-extract-then-convert chain, an auth-then-query chain) that recur across superficially different queries and domains, and CostBench (semanticscholar:593dd4157deef93b317dc01dd9534d58f076daf0) shows many tasks are solvable by several alternative tool sequences whose composite costs differ. The two leaves that DO reuse across tasks reuse the wrong granularity for this: Plan Reuse (arxiv:2512.21309v2) caches and replays a WHOLE plan keyed on request-text similarity (≈30% near-duplicate requests), so it cannot fire when two tasks share only a sub-chain, and AgentSquare (openalex:W4403344644) reuses MODULE architectures (Planning/Reasoning/ToolUse/Memory) discovered by offline search, not the instance-level tool-call subgraph a task actually executed. The failure: when a new task's decisive tool-call sub-structure has already been validated by a prior solved task, no retrieved method can substitute that known-good subgraph in place of re-searching it, so search/inference cost does not amortize as the agent accumulates experience and the planner keeps re-incurring it.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2603.12740v1","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"ToolTree plans tool calls with a dual-feedback MCTS (pre-evaluation prior + post-evaluation executed reward) plus bidirectional pruning, getting foresight over inter-tool dependencies that greedy selection lacks. Its residue is that the search is purely per-task and stateless across tasks: the method discards the validated tool-trajectory tree at task end and re-expands ~70-95 nodes on the next task even when an isol_able sub-chain it already executed and scored is the answer, so its own post-evaluation reward signal is never banked into reusable structure and cost cannot amortize across an agent's task stream."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2512.21309v2","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Plan Reuse caches a previously generated whole-plan and replays it (with parameter substitution) when a new request is judged similar enough, eliminating plan-generation latency for the ~30% of requests that are near-duplicates. Its residue is that reuse granularity is the entire plan keyed on request-text similarity, so it cannot reuse a shared tool-call SUB-chain between two tasks that are dissimilar at the request level but overlap in their dependency sub-structure, and it has no notion of validating that a reused fragment is known-good for the new task's intermediate state."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4403344644","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"AgentSquare searches a modular design space (Planning/Reasoning/ToolUse/Memory modules with standardized IO) to discover an agent architecture that transfers across tasks, banking reuse at the module-design level. Its residue is that the reused unit is a coarse architectural module chosen offline per task-distribution, not the concrete instance-level tool-call subgraph a specific solved task executed, so it cannot transplant a single validated dependency motif (e.g. ocr->zoom->ocr->unit-convert) from one task's successful run into another task's plan."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W6979347639","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"T1 contributes a tool-augmented multi-turn dataset that explicitly captures inter-tool dependencies across nine domains, surfacing that dependency-aware planning is the hard part of multi-turn tool use. Its residue is that it is a dataset/evaluation artifact: it exhibits the recurring dependency motifs but provides no mechanism that mines, indexes, or reuses those motifs as planning primitives across tasks."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:593dd4157deef93b317dc01dd9534d58f076daf0","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"CostBench evaluates whether agents can find and adapt cost-optimal plans when several alternative tool sequences with different composite costs solve a task. Its residue is that it only measures cost-optimal planning/replanning; it provides no planning mechanism, and in particular no way to let a previously-discovered cheap sub-sequence inform a new task so the agent does not re-discover cost trade-offs from scratch."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"LLM agentic systems — planning and tool-use optimization (multi-step, multi-tool task execution)","venue":"ICLR / NeurIPS / ICML (top-tier ML)","time":"2026","data":["ToolBench / GTA-style multi-tool agent benchmarks","T1 (tool-dependency multi-turn)","CostBench (cost-optimal planning)","MCPAgentBench (real-world MCP tools)","Agent Planning Benchmark (APB)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with LLM-agent / RL / planning background and cloud access","preference":"both","baseline":"ToolTree (MCTS tool planning) + greedy ReAct-style tool selection + AgentSquare (module search) + Plan Reuse (whole-plan caching)","limitation":"tool-call planning is solved per-task in isolation; nothing reuses the structure of already-solved tool-call subgraphs across tasks, so planners re-pay full search/inference cost on every new task even when the decisive sub-plan recurs","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object is a persistent TYPED TOOL-CALL DEPENDENCY GRAPH (the 'plan bank') the agent maintains across its whole task stream. Each tool t has a declared/­inferred typed signature sig(t) = (consumes: set of typed artifact slots, produces: set of typed artifact slots), where a typed artifact is a (semantic_type, schema) pair (e.g. (image, png-bytes), (location_name, string), (distance, {value:float, unit:enum})); types come from the tool's MCP/function schema when present, else are induced once by an LLM typing pass over the tool docstring (a one-time per-tool cost, cached). A PLANNING STATE S is the multiset of typed artifacts currently available (initial S0 = the task's input artifacts). A sub-graph g banked from a prior task is a connected DAG of tool invocations with a boundary signature bsig(g) = (entry-consumes E_g, exit-produces X_g): the typed artifacts g needs present to run and the typed artifacts it yields. GAP-1 (substitution, C13): planning proceeds by, at each state S, attempting to UNIFY some banked g's entry signature E_g against S (a typed-set containment test with variable binding on schema fields) and, on a match, transplanting g wholesale into the plan and advancing S := (S \\ consumed) ∪ X_g — no search is spent on the span g covers because g was already executed-and-scored on its source task; only states with no unifying banked sub-graph fall back to the base per-task search (ToolTree-style MCTS) for one step. Plan validity at the transplant point holds BY CONSTRUCTION because unification certifies every tool in g has its consumed types present when it fires. GAP-3 (the index, C13): the bank is indexed by bsig, not request text, so retrieval is exactly this type-unification — two tasks that share no request words but both reach a state containing an (image,png) artifact both trigger the same banked ocr->zoom->ocr->unit-convert motif. GAP-2 (locus audit, C01): the audited assumption is 'the optimized object is the per-task plan'; we relocate it to the cross-task bank and show the per-task locus was an unnecessary convention — when a transplanted g later fails post-execution validation on a new task (its exit artifacts are produced but the downstream LLM judge scores the task wrong), we do NOT discard the bank; we attach a typed GUARD predicate learned from that failure (a cheap logistic classifier over bsig-boundary features) that narrows g's applicability, so the bank monotonically refines rather than resetting at each task boundary. A banked sub-graph is admitted only after it passes the same executed (post-evaluation) reward ToolTree already computes >= tau on its source task, so 'validated' means executed-and-scored, not merely generated. The composite-cost selection rule (folded from the deferred gap): when several banked g unify at S, pick the one minimizing summed per-tool cost(t) (latency or API price from the tool schema), so accumulated cheap motifs are preferred. Numerically, ToolTree reports ~70-95 expanded nodes and ~33-47 rollouts per GTA task (fulltext method section); our prediction is that median expanded nodes per task falls toward the count of NON-reused (novel-remainder) tool steps as the bank saturates over a task stream, while task success stays within noise of ToolTree — the per-task locus cannot exhibit this decline because it banks nothing.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"All three gaps share ONE machinery — the typed dependency-graph bank — rather than needing separate modules: the substitution operator (gap 1), the by-construction reuse trigger (gap 3), and the locus relocation (gap 2) are three readings of the same object (the bank: how you transplant from it, how you index into it, and the claim that it, not the per-task plan, is the optimization unit). Evidence they share machinery: gap 3's index IS gap 1's unification test, and gap 2's audit is the justification for persisting the very object gaps 1 and 3 build. Alternatives rejected: (a) distilling the search value into a per-step policy (VGPO-MCTS territory) — rejected, it re-pays inference per task and collapses to a learned greedy selector, not cross-task structural reuse; (b) a per-step credit/advantage estimator over tool calls (RRPO/SRPO/SIOP territory) — rejected, that re-credits within a task and is the saturated cluster we must avoid; (c) request-similarity whole-plan caching (Plan Reuse) — rejected, wrong granularity, cannot fire on surface-dissimilar shared motifs. Regression avoided (method_lineage notes): the bare 'reuse recurring sub-sequences' idea lands on c0 (macro-operators/options) and c1 (skill libraries); we draw on a source those nodes do NOT occupy — applicability decided by TYPED INTERMEDIATE-STATE unification with an executed-validity admission gate and learned guards, over natural-language tool APIs, not fixed discrete action chunks (c0) or description-similarity skill retrieval (c1).","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: run the banked planner and vanilla ToolTree on the GTA and ToolBench multi-tool benchmarks with the same backbone (e.g. GPT-4o and an open Qwen model), presenting tasks as a STREAM and measuring, as the stream progresses, (i) median expanded search nodes per task and (ii) task success rate. If the candidate works, median expanded nodes per task DECREASES monotonically toward the per-task novel-remainder step count as the bank saturates, while success rate stays within noise of ToolTree (no accuracy regression) — and cross-task reuse fires on surface-dissimilar task pairs (low request-text cosine, shared bsig). The named load-bearing variable is the TYPE-UNIFICATION MATCH RATE m = fraction of planning states where a banked sub-graph's entry signature unifies into the current state. Negative control: replace the typed-signature unification index with a request-text-embedding nearest-neighbor index over whole banked sub-graphs (the Plan-Reuse-style key) while holding the bank contents identical; this should drive the DOWNSTREAM OUTCOME — the per-task expanded-node count — back up to vanilla-ToolTree levels (reuse stops firing across surface-dissimilar tasks even though the same validated fragments are present), confirming the amortization is caused by typed-state matching and not by merely having a cache. Positive control: a stripped model that ONLY does type-unification transplant with no base search (falls back to a no-op when G_S is empty) should still recover most of the expanded-node reduction on tasks whose motifs are banked, isolating the unification mechanism as the driver.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2603.12740v1","delta":"ToolTree expands a fresh ~70-95-node dual-feedback MCTS tree per task and discards it at task end; we extract its executed, post-evaluation-scored sub-DAGs into a persistent typed bank and transplant them by intermediate-state type-unification on later tasks, so expanded nodes per task decline over a stream instead of being constant — a cross-task amortization ToolTree's per-task search structurally cannot produce."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2512.21309v2","delta":"Plan Reuse caches WHOLE plans keyed on request-text similarity and fires only on ~30% near-duplicate requests; we key reuse on a sub-graph's boundary TYPE-SIGNATURE matched against the live planning state, so reuse fires at sub-chain granularity between surface-dissimilar tasks that share a dependency motif, which request-text keys cannot detect."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4403344644","delta":"AgentSquare searches a space of coarse architectural MODULES (Planning/Reasoning/ToolUse/Memory) offline and reuses a module configuration per task-distribution; we reuse the concrete instance-level executed tool-call subgraph with a by-construction validity guarantee, transplanting a specific validated dependency motif rather than selecting an abstract module."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W6979347639","delta":"T1 exhibits recurring inter-tool dependency motifs as a dataset but supplies no mechanism; we turn those motifs into first-class reusable planning primitives indexed by typed boundary signature with an executed-reward admission gate."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:593dd4157deef93b317dc01dd9534d58f076daf0","delta":"CostBench only measures whether agents find cost-optimal plans; we carry discovered cheap valid sub-sequences forward via a composite-cost selection rule over unifying banked sub-graphs so a new task prefers previously-validated cheap motifs instead of re-discovering cost trade-offs per task."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"arxiv:2603.12740v1","what_step_was_missed":"ToolTree constructs and scores a tool-call trajectory tree per task but never extracts its executed, post-evaluation-passing sub-DAGs into a cross-task-persistent object keyed by a typed entry/exit signature, nor does it define the type-unification test that lets such a banked sub-DAG be transplanted into a later task's plan when its entry types are present in that task's intermediate state — that extraction-plus-typed-indexing construction is the missing step that would let its own validated sub-trajectories amortize search across tasks."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":335,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"Hard floor does not fire: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict = borderline (no entry triggered), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id = null, and paper_pointed_threat is a competing-not-subsuming paper (NOT exact-mechanism overlap — SMITH matches by semantic similarity of whole experiences, the candidate by typed-state sub-graph unification, the exact axis the negative control measures). Two load-bearing borderlines route to revise: (1) paper_pointed_threat.addressable_via names a specific field — SMITH must be added to differentiation_from_lit to make the novelty boundary explicit per the C01 lesson 'Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work ... collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured'; (2) the C13 anchor lesson 'lacking any theoretical guarantee that its wiring captures the claimed structure' — core_mechanism's by-construction guarantee is validity-of-transplant, not a uniqueness/soundness statement that the typed boundary signature correctly characterizes reusability, which should be stated as an explicit soundness claim with its false-positive failure mode named.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"(additive) No retrieved leaf lets a planner SUBSTITUTE an already-validated tool-call sub-structure from a prior solved task in place of re-deriving it, so search/inference cost does not amortize across an agent's task stream — ToolTree re-searches per task, Plan Reuse only matches whole near-duplicate requests, and AgentSquare only reuses coarse module architectures; the outcome that is missing is cross-task reuse at the granularity of the concrete tool-call dependency subgraph, with a guarantee that the transplanted fragment is known-good for the new task's intermediate state.","main_pattern":"structural_prior_encoding","sub_pattern":"C13 (Encode Structure by Construction)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring reject shape is assembling existing relational-learning components into a problem-specific architecture, then claiming the encoded relational structure as the contribution without proving it; the construction typically carries no guarantee that its wiring actually captures the claimed structural property, and evaluation omits the simplest structure-agnostic comparison.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A domain-grounded architecture lacking any theoretical guarantee that its wiring captures the claimed structure — and lacking a uniqueness or identifiability argument — leaves reviewers unable to credit the structural claim.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"core_mechanism supplies a by-construction VALIDITY certificate (type-unification guarantees every transplanted tool has its consumed types present, so plan validity holds by construction) but does NOT yet supply an expressiveness/identifiability-grade theorem that the typed boundary signature uniquely characterizes when a sub-graph is reusable — the guarantee is soundness-of-applicability, not a uniqueness result, so the structural claim is partly but not fully backed."},{"lesson_quoted":"Omitting closely-related SOTA baselines and the simplest correlation or heuristic comparison makes any claimed structural advantage unverifiable.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the simplest structure-agnostic comparison (request-text-embedding retrieval over the same bank, i.e. the Plan-Reuse-style key) is built in as the named negative control, so the structural advantage is directly measured against the heuristic baseline."},{"lesson_quoted":"Combining borrowed modules (global plus local streams, attention plus state tracking) with no genuinely new mechanism reads as incremental even when the combination is sensible.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the new mechanism (typed entry/exit-signature unification deciding sub-graph applicability against the live planning state, with an executed-reward admission gate) is sharply delineated from the inherited ToolTree base search, not an assembly of borrowed streams."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"(subtractive) Every retrieved tool-planning leaf silently inherits the assumption that the unit of optimization is the SINGLE TASK's plan — that planning state is owned by one task and discarded at its boundary; no retrieved paper tests whether the optimized object must be the per-task plan at all, rather than a cross-task object the agent maintains and refines as it accumulates solved tasks.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"A novelty-boundary collapse — the 'new' locus turns out to be one a prior paper already used — and offering only a demonstration with no mechanistic account of why the locus carries the signal are the recurring failures; the move must be shown provably distinct from published loci and stress-tested against an informed adversary at the new locus.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work — normalization statistics, activation-similarity losses, semantic concept triggers — collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"the cross-task locus IS already occupied at a coarse level by SMITH (arxiv:2512.11303v1, cross-task experience sharing) and the survey-T2 paradigm (openalex:W4417529989) / AI Workflow Store (openalex:W7161204366); the candidate's difference (reuse decided by typed-state unification at sub-graph granularity vs SMITH's semantic-similarity episodic retrieval of whole experiences) is real and measured by the negative control, but the candidate's current differentiation_from_lit does NOT name SMITH, so the novelty boundary is not yet made explicit against the closest occupant."},{"lesson_quoted":"Demonstrating the new locus only on fixed, non-adaptive or outdated baselines while omitting any account of why it works reads as a stacked pipeline of existing components rather than a principled shift.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the mechanistic WHY is given (the amortization is caused by typed-state matching firing on shared dependency motifs that request-text keys cannot detect) and the strongest current baseline (ToolTree) plus the request-text-key ablation are both run, not an outdated baseline."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"(additive) No retrieved leaf indexes tool-call sub-structures by the INTERMEDIATE STATE / type-signature they consume and produce (rather than by request text), so reuse cannot fire between tasks that differ at the surface but share a dependency motif — the missing outcome is a way to recognize that two dissimilar tasks reach a point where the same validated sub-chain applies.","main_pattern":"structural_prior_encoding","sub_pattern":"C13 (Encode Structure by Construction)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Same C13 failure mode: encoding relational structure is not itself the advance; a construction with no guarantee its wiring captures the claimed statistic, evaluated without the simplest structure-agnostic comparison, reads as incremental assembly.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Proposing a new construction or task without analyzing the information loss it introduces (compressing histories into profiles, projecting away radial distance) invites doubt about whether the encoded structure helps or hurts.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"the type-signature index is a lossy abstraction of the full sub-graph (it keys on boundary types only, discarding internal structure and argument values), and core_mechanism does not yet analyze the false-positive risk this abstraction introduces (two sub-graphs sharing a boundary signature but semantically different) beyond the learned guard — the information-loss of the keying is under-analyzed."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No entry is triggered (no Reject lesson is candidate_match: yes), so the hard floor does not fire. Two load-bearing borderlines drive the aggregate: the C13 anchor's missing uniqueness/expressiveness guarantee ('lacking any theoretical guarantee that its wiring captures the claimed structure'), and the C01 sibling's novelty-boundary against SMITH ('Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work ... collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured')."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"(additive) No retrieved leaf lets a planner SUBSTITUTE an already-validated tool-call sub-structure ...","sub_pattern":"C13 (Encode Structure by Construction)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Make the relational connectivity topology itself the encoded structural prior: define which entities link to which and under what relation type, then run propagation over that wiring so a specific structural quantity is captured by construction rather than relearned.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism defines nodes = tool invocations and typed produces/consumes edges (the relation-typed connectivity), and the transplant-on-type-unification operator makes plan validity at the transplant point hold BY CONSTRUCTION — the C13 'captured by construction, not relearned' move is genuinely performed on the tool-call dependency graph.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"(subtractive) Every retrieved tool-planning leaf silently inherits the assumption that the unit of optimization is the SINGLE TASK's plan ...","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"The audited assumption is always about the representational locus at which a property is presumed to be enforced, and the tactical move is to relocate it to a different locus the field treated as irrelevant or invariant ('relocate the signal', 're-anchor enforcement').","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism names the locus every planner anchors on (the per-task plan, discarded at the task boundary) and re-anchors the optimization object at the cross-task bank, with a mechanistic account (amortization curve declines because matching fires on shared motifs) of why the new locus carries the reusable signal — the C01 relocate-the-locus move is performed, though in a planning/efficiency rather than security setting.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"(additive) No retrieved leaf indexes tool-call sub-structures by the INTERMEDIATE STATE / type-signature ...","sub_pattern":"C13 (Encode Structure by Construction)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Either construct the edge set / index from a domain schema, or approximate an expensive structural statistic via a propagated/cached structural key, so the structural quantity holds by construction.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism keys the bank by boundary type-signature read from each tool's MCP/function schema (a schema-derived structural key) and retrieves by type-unification against the live state — the C13 'index by a schema-derived structural statistic' move is performed; this entry shares C13's construction with the anchor.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"All three entries instantiate their cited cluster's signature move: C13's by-construction relational-topology encoding (the typed dependency graph + unification-validity + schema-derived index) and C01's locus relocation (per-task plan -> cross-task bank with a mechanistic why). Neither collapses to the parent's generic gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["structural_prior_encoding","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented anti-pattern compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; this candidate's set {structural_prior_encoding, assumption_audit_and_pivot} contains no such pair, so no anti-pattern matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"arxiv:2512.11303v1","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"SMITH (Shared Memory Integrated Tool Hub) is the closest competitor: it does cross-task experience sharing for tool-using LLM agents, organizes memory into procedural/semantic/episodic components, and 'preserv[es] successful execution patterns', reusing them via 'episodic memory retrieval with semantic similarity matching'. This occupies the SAME high-level locus the candidate relocates to (cross-task reuse of validated execution structure), so the candidate's claim stands or falls on whether its DISTINCT retrieval mechanism — applicability decided by typed entry/exit-signature UNIFICATION against the live planning state, at sub-graph granularity, with an executed-reward admission gate — is a load-bearing departure from SMITH's semantic-similarity episodic retrieval of whole experiences. It is NOT exact-mechanism overlap: SMITH matches by embedding similarity of past experiences (the very mechanism the candidate's negative control is designed to beat), retrieves whole episodic experiences rather than type-unified sub-graphs, and does not key reuse on a by-construction typed-state validity certificate. The candidate therefore competes with, but is not subsumed by, SMITH — the departure is the headline and is directly measured by the negative control.","addressable_via":"Add SMITH (arxiv:2512.11303v1) to differentiation_from_lit with the explicit, measured delta (typed-state unification at sub-graph granularity with executed-reward admission vs semantic-similarity episodic retrieval of whole experiences), making the C01 novelty boundary against the closest occupant explicit rather than implicit."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat (arxiv:2512.11303v1 SMITH) — novelty boundary against the closest cross-task-reuse occupant is implicit; C01 reject lesson on relocating to an already-exploited locus.","fix_direction":"Append a differentiation_from_lit entry for paper_id arxiv:2512.11303v1 with delta: 'SMITH shares cross-task validated-execution-pattern reuse for tool agents but retrieves WHOLE episodic experiences by semantic-similarity matching; we decide reuse by typed entry/exit-signature UNIFICATION against the live planning state at sub-graph granularity with an executed-reward admission gate, so reuse fires on shared dependency motifs between semantically-dissimilar tasks that SMITH's embedding-similarity retrieval misses — the exact axis our request-text-index negative control isolates.'"},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","issue":"gap_closure_reject_check C13 borderline — the by-construction guarantee is soundness-of-transplant-validity only; no statement that the typed boundary signature soundly characterizes reusability, and the keying's information-loss / false-positive risk is under-analyzed.","fix_direction":"Add one sentence to core_mechanism stating the guarantee precisely as a SOUNDNESS claim: 'type-unification is sound (a transplanted g never fires a tool whose consumed types are absent) but not complete — two sub-graphs sharing a boundary signature may differ internally, so a unifying g is a CANDIDATE whose semantic correctness is gated post-execution by the same reward judge and narrowed by the learned guard; the index trades completeness for a by-construction validity certificate, and the guard recovers precision.' Do not alter falsification_prediction or compute_budget."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Appended a differentiation_from_lit entry for arxiv:2512.11303v1 (SMITH) making the novelty boundary explicit: typed-state sub-graph unification + executed-reward admission vs SMITH's semantic-similarity episodic retrieval of whole experiences."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added a soundness statement to core_mechanism: type-unification is sound-but-incomplete, a unifying sub-graph is a candidate gated post-execution by the reward judge and narrowed by the guard, naming the boundary-key information-loss / false-positive risk the index trades away."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Banking the Plan: Cross-Task Reuse of Validated Tool-Call Subgraphs by Typed-State Matching\n\n**Method.** Plan Bank (typed-subgraph transplant planner)\n\n## Motivation\nWhen an AI agent uses external tools to solve a task, it has to plan which tools to call and in what order, passing one tool's output into the next tool's input. Today's best planners figure this out from scratch for every single task. The strongest one, ToolTree (a tree-search tool planner), tries roughly 70-95 possible tool steps per task using Monte Carlo Tree Search (MCTS), scores them by actually running the tools, and then throws the whole worked-out plan away when the task ends. The simpler greedy planners just pick the next tool in one shot with no foresight. Either way, the agent never keeps what it learned.\n\nThat is wasteful because real tool tasks repeat the same little sub-chains over and over: search-then-extract-then-convert, or log-in-then-query. Datasets like T1 show these recurring dependency patterns, and CostBench shows many tasks can be solved by several different tool sequences that cost different amounts. So very often the key part of a new task's plan was already searched, run, and checked on an earlier task — but nothing carries it forward.\n\nThe two methods that do reuse across tasks reuse at the wrong size. Plan Reuse caches a WHOLE plan and replays it only when a new request looks almost identical in wording, so it misses two tasks that share just a sub-chain. AgentSquare reuses big architectural building blocks (Planning / Reasoning / Tool Use / Memory), not the actual small tool-call subgraph a task ran. The missing piece: when a new task's key sub-chain was already validated on a past task, no method can drop that known-good piece in instead of re-searching it, so cost never goes down as the agent gains experience.\n\nThis is solvable now because tool interfaces have become typed and machine-readable (via the Model Context Protocol and function-call schemas), so we can read off exactly what types a tool sub-chain needs and produces — and because search planners that actually run and score their plans now exist, giving us a trustworthy way to decide which sub-chains are known-good. If we close this gap, planning gets cheaper the more the agent works, with no model retraining and no new reward.\n\n## Method\n### Typed plan bank\n*Bank executed, reward-validated tool-call sub-graphs keyed by their boundary type-signature so recurring motifs become reusable primitives.*\n\n1. For every tool the agent can call, give it a type fingerprint: the typed things it needs as input and the typed things it returns. If the tool ships a machine-readable interface (Model Context Protocol, MCP, or an OpenAI function-call schema), read those types straight from it. If not, make ONE language-model call on the tool's documentation that fills a fixed form: for each input and output, a name, a semantic type (like image, location, distance), and the JSON shape. Treat two items as the same type only when both the semantic tag and the JSON shape of required fields agree. Cache this so each tool is typed once. [author decision: how fine-grained the semantic-type list is decides how often pieces get reused versus wrongly matched — the authors set this vocabulary.]\n\n*Each tool t has a typed signature: the set of typed artifact slots it consumes and the set it produces, where a typed artifact is a (semantic type, schema) pair read from the tool's schema or induced once by an LLM typing pass.*\n$$ \\mathrm{sig}(t)=\\big(\\mathrm{consumes}(t),\\ \\mathrm{produces}(t)\\big),\\quad \\text{each a set of typed artifact slots }(\\tau,\\mathrm{schema}) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This gives every tool a precise type fingerprint, which is the key we will later match against the current state to decide reuse.\n2. Run the base tree-search planner (ToolTree, which uses Monte Carlo Tree Search, MCTS) on a stream of tasks. Whenever it solves a task and the actually-run plan scores at or above a goodness threshold tau, save the graph of tool calls it really executed, labeling each arrow with the typed result one tool handed to the next. Save only plans that were run and scored well, never ones the model only imagined. 【author decision: the goodness threshold tau balances banking only clearly-correct chains against banking more of them — pick it on held-out tasks where adding more chains stops helping.】\n   - _Why_: We only want to bank sub-chains that were actually run and scored as good, not ones the model merely imagined.\n3. From each saved good graph, cut out every connected sub-piece of 2 to k tool calls (k = 4 by default; bigger k stores more, at the price of a larger index). For each piece g, record what types it needs to start (its entry types $E_{g}$ — the inputs it consumes that aren't produced inside the piece) and what types it yields at the end (its exit types $X_{g}).$ Store g in the bank, filed under the set of its entry-type tags, along with how well its source task scored and its total tool cost.\n\n*A banked sub-graph g (a connected DAG of tool calls) is keyed by its boundary signature: the typed artifacts it needs present to run (entry $E_{g})$ and the typed artifacts it yields (exit $X_{g}).$*\n$$ \\mathrm{bsig}(g)=\\big(E_g,\\ X_g\\big),\\quad E_g=\\text{entry-consumed types of }g,\\ \\ X_g=\\text{exit-produced types of }g \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Storing pieces by the types they need and produce turns recurring tool patterns into reusable building blocks we can look up by what the current task already has.\n\n### Typed-state transplant planner\n*Assemble a new task's plan by transplanting the cheapest valid banked sub-graph whose entry types unify into the current state, searching only the novel remainder.*\n\n4. While planning a new task, keep a running state S: the bag of typed items available so far, starting from the task's inputs. At each state, fetch every stored piece g whose required entry types all appear in S — match each required type to a distinct available item with the same type tag and a compatible JSON shape (using bipartite matching when the assignment is ambiguous); the piece qualifies only if every required type is matched. Record how often at least one piece qualifies — this is the match rate m we report.\n\n*A banked sub-graph g is transplantable at planning state S exactly when its entry types are contained in the multiset of typed artifacts available at S (with schema-field binding); this containment is the reuse trigger and the validity certificate.*\n$$ \\text{transplant } g \\text{ at state } S \\iff E_g \\sqsubseteq S \\ \\ (\\text{typed-set containment with schema-field binding}) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Matching on types, not on the wording of the request, lets a stored piece fire even for a task that looks totally different on the surface but has reached a point where the same sub-chain applies.\n5. If one or more stored pieces qualify at the current state and pass their guard, choose the cheapest one g* (ties broken by the better source score), run its tool calls for real, and update the state by removing what it used and adding what it produced — this skips the search the planner would have done over that span. A tool's cost is its measured typical latency (or its provider price). If nothing qualifies, do exactly one step of normal tree search. Repeat until the task's goal type is reached, then score the final answer. A piece's guard lets it through unless the guard has learned this context is risky.\n\n*After executing a transplanted sub-graph g, the planning state advances by removing the artifacts g consumed and adding the artifacts it produced — no search is spent over g's span.*\n$$ S \\leftarrow (S \\setminus \\mathrm{consumed}(g)) \\cup X_g \\tag{4} $$\n\n\n*When several banked sub-graphs unify at state S and pass their learned guard, pick the one minimizing summed per-tool cost (latency or API price), so accumulated cheap valid motifs are preferred.*\n$$ g^\\star=\\arg\\min_{g\\,:\\,E_g\\sqsubseteq S,\\ \\mathrm{guard}_g(S)=1}\\ \\sum_{t\\in g}\\mathrm{cost}(t) \\tag{5} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Reusing a known-good cheap piece instead of re-searching it is exactly where the saved cost comes from; falling back to search only on the genuinely new remainder keeps accuracy.\n\n### Cross-task refinement\n*Treat the bank, not the per-task plan, as the optimization unit by learning guards from failures so the bank monotonically improves.*\n\n6. When the final judge marks a task wrong, do NOT throw away any reused piece. Instead, for each piece blamed for the failure, update a tiny logistic 'guard' built on that piece's boundary features (its entry-type and exit-type tags, summary stats of the bound fields, how many items are in the state, and where in the plan it fired) with a 'don't reuse here' label, shrinking where it fires next time. So the bank keeps getting better over the task stream instead of resetting each task. 【author decision: which reused pieces to blame for a wrong answer — all pieces on the failing path, or only the one pinpointed by re-running the plan without it — is the authors' call.】\n   - _Why_: Because matching on types is sound but not perfect (two pieces can share a type signature yet differ inside), the guard quietly raises precision as the agent gains experience, and the bank keeps improving instead of resetting each task.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 把计划存进银行：通过类型化状态匹配在任务间复用已验证的工具调用子图\n\n**方法名称.** Plan Bank (typed-subgraph transplant planner)\n\n## 研究动机\n当一个 AI agent 用外部工具来完成任务时，它必须规划调用哪些工具、以什么顺序调用，并把一个工具的输出接到下一个工具的输入。如今最好的规划器对每一个任务都从零开始算这件事。最强的 ToolTree（一个基于树搜索的工具规划器）用 MCTS（Monte Carlo Tree Search）对每个任务尝试大约 70-95 个候选工具步骤，靠真正运行工具来打分，然后在任务结束时把整套算好的计划丢掉。更简单的 greedy 规划器则一步就选下一个工具、毫无前瞻。无论哪种，agent 都没有保留学到的东西。\n\n这很浪费，因为真实的工具任务会反复出现相同的小子链：search-then-extract-then-convert，或者 log-in-then-query。像 T1 这样的数据集展示了这些反复出现的依赖模式，CostBench 则表明很多任务可以由若干代价不同的工具序列来解决。所以一个新任务计划中的关键部分，往往在更早的某个任务里已经被搜索、运行并检验过——但没有任何东西把它带到下一次。\n\n两个确实做了跨任务复用的方法，复用的粒度不对。Plan Reuse 缓存整套计划，只有当新请求在措辞上几乎一模一样时才回放，因此会错过两个仅共享一段子链的任务。AgentSquare 复用的是大的架构模块（Planning / Reasoning / Tool Use / Memory），而不是某个任务实际运行过的具体工具调用子图。缺失的一环是：当一个新任务的关键子链在过去任务里已被验证过时，没有方法能把这块已知good的部件直接放进来代替重新搜索，于是成本不会随 agent 经验增加而下降。\n\n现在可以解决，是因为工具接口已经类型化、机器可读（通过 Model Context Protocol 与 function-call schema），我们能读出一段工具子链需要和产出哪些类型；而且会真正运行并打分计划的搜索式规划器已经存在，给了我们一个可信的方式来判定哪些子链是已知good的。一旦补上这个缺口，agent 做得越多、规划就越便宜，且无需重训模型、也不需要新的 reward。\n\n## 方法\n### 类型化 plan bank\n*把执行过且被 reward 验证的工具调用子图按边界类型签名存入银行，使反复出现的 motif 成为可复用的基本部件。*\n\n1. 为 agent 能调用的每个工具建立一个类型指纹：它作为输入需要的类型化产物，以及它返回的类型化产物。若工具自带机器可读接口（Model Context Protocol, MCP，或 OpenAI 的 function-call schema），就直接从中读取这些类型。若没有，则对工具文档做一次 language model 调用，填一个固定表单：对每个输入和输出给出 name、一个 semantic type（如 image、location、distance）以及其 JSON 形状。只有当 semantic tag 与必填字段的 JSON 形状都一致时，才把两个产物视为同一类型。缓存结果，使每个工具只 typed 一次。【作者需决定：semantic type 词表的粗细决定了子块被复用与被错配的频率——由作者设定该词表。】\n\n*每个工具 t 都有一个类型化签名：它消费的类型化产物槽集合与它产出的集合；其中类型化产物是一个 (semantic type, schema) 对，来自工具 schema 或由一次性 LLM typing pass 推断。*\n$$ \\mathrm{sig}(t)=\\big(\\mathrm{consumes}(t),\\ \\mathrm{produces}(t)\\big),\\quad \\text{each a set of typed artifact slots }(\\tau,\\mathrm{schema}) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这给每个工具一个精确的类型指纹，正是后面用来与当前状态匹配、判定能否复用的 key。\n2. 在一连串任务上运行基础树搜索规划器（ToolTree，它用 Monte Carlo Tree Search, MCTS）。每当它解出一个任务、且实际运行的计划得分达到或超过一个good阈值 tau 时，保存它真正执行过的工具调用图，并在每条边上标注前一个工具交给后一个工具的类型化结果。只保存真正运行且打分良好的计划，绝不保存模型仅凭想象的。【作者需决定：good阈值 tau 在『只入库明显正确的链』与『入库更多链』之间权衡——在 held-out 任务上选取『再加链也不再有帮助』的那个点。】\n   - _为什么_: 我们只想存入真正运行过且被打分为好的子链，而不是模型凭空想象的。\n3. 从每个保存的good图里，切出所有 2 到 k 个工具调用的连通子块（默认 k = 4；k 越大存得越多，但索引也越大）。对每个子块 g，记录它启动时需要的类型（入口类型 $E_{g}——$它消费但并非在子块内部产生的输入）以及它结束时产出的类型（出口类型 $X_{g}$）。把 g 存入银行，以其入口类型 tag 的集合为档案键，同时存其源任务得分与工具总 cost。\n\n*被存入银行的子图 g（工具调用组成的连通 DAG）以其边界签名为键：运行前需就位的类型化产物（入口 $E_{g}$）与它产出的类型化产物（出口 $X_{g}$）。*\n$$ \\mathrm{bsig}(g)=\\big(E_g,\\ X_g\\big),\\quad E_g=\\text{entry-consumed types of }g,\\ \\ X_g=\\text{exit-produced types of }g \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 按子块所需与所产的类型来存储，把反复出现的工具模式变成可按当前任务已有内容查到的可复用部件。\n\n### 类型化状态移植规划器\n*通过移植入口类型能合一进当前状态、且最便宜有效的银行子图来拼出新任务的计划，只对新的剩余部分做搜索。*\n\n4. 在为新任务规划时，维护一个运行状态 S：到目前为止可用的类型化产物的多重集，从任务输入开始。在每个状态处，取出所有入口类型都能在 S 中找到的存储子块 g——把每个所需类型匹配到一个 tag 相同且 JSON 形状兼容的、互不相同的可用产物（当分配有歧义时用二部图匹配）；只有每个所需类型都被匹配上，子块才合格。记录至少有一个子块合格的频率——这就是我们报告的匹配率 m。\n\n*当且仅当 g 的入口类型被状态 S 处可用的类型化产物多重集所包含（并完成 schema 字段绑定）时，g 可在 S 处被移植；该包含关系既是复用触发条件，也是有效性证书。*\n$$ \\text{transplant } g \\text{ at state } S \\iff E_g \\sqsubseteq S \\ \\ (\\text{typed-set containment with schema-field binding}) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 按类型匹配而不是按请求措辞匹配，使一个存好的子块即便面对表面上完全不同、但已到达同一适用点的任务也能触发。\n5. 若当前状态下有一个或多个存储子块合格且通过其 guard，选最便宜的 g*（同价时取源任务得分更高的），真正运行它的工具调用，并更新状态：移除它用掉的、加入它产出的——从而跳过规划器本会在这段上做的搜索。工具的 cost 是其实测典型延迟（或其 provider 价格）。若没有合格子块，就只做一步普通树搜索。重复直到达到任务目标类型，再对最终答案打分。子块的 guard 默认放行，除非它已学到当前上下文有风险。\n\n*执行移植的子图 g 之后，规划状态前进：移除 g 消费的产物、加入它产出的产物——在 g 覆盖的跨度上不花费任何搜索。*\n$$ S \\leftarrow (S \\setminus \\mathrm{consumed}(g)) \\cup X_g \\tag{4} $$\n\n\n*当多个被存银行的子图在状态 S 处都能合一且通过各自的 learned guard 时，选择按工具 cost（延迟或 API 价格）之和最小的那个，从而优先复用已积累的廉价且有效的 motif。*\n$$ g^\\star=\\arg\\min_{g\\,:\\,E_g\\sqsubseteq S,\\ \\mathrm{guard}_g(S)=1}\\ \\sum_{t\\in g}\\mathrm{cost}(t) \\tag{5} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 用已知good的廉价子块代替重新搜索，正是节省成本之处；只在真正新的剩余部分回退到搜索，保证准确率。\n\n### 跨任务精炼\n*把银行而非单任务计划当作优化单元，从失败中学习 guard 使银行单调改进。*\n\n6. 当最终评判把一个任务判错时，不要丢弃任何被复用的子块。而是对每个被归咎于该失败的子块，用它的边界特征（入口类型与出口类型 tag、绑定字段的统计摘要、状态中产物的数量、它在计划中触发的位置）训练/更新一个很小的 logistic 'guard'，给它一个『此处别复用』的标签，缩小它下次触发的范围。于是银行在任务流上不断变好，而不是每个任务都重置。【作者需决定：把错误答案归咎于哪些被复用的子块——失败路径上的全部，还是仅用『去掉它重跑』所定位的那一个——由作者决定。】\n   - _为什么_: 因为按类型匹配是 sound 但不完美的（两个子块可能类型签名相同而内部不同），guard 随 agent 经验悄悄提高精度，银行因此不断改进、而不是每个任务都重置。\n\n"},{"id":"63","run_dir":"run_prompt63_infoncegauss","index":63,"title":"A Finite-Sample Anisotropy Envelope for InfoNCE-Induced Gaussianity","title_zh":"InfoNCE 诱导高斯性的有限样本各向异性包络","method_name":"Finite-Sample Anisotropy Envelope (FSAE)","hook":"InfoNCE's representations are only asymptotically and only marginally Gaussian; at any real batch size the limiting law is a quantifiably anisotropic perturbation whose covariance the InfoNCE geometry actively prefers, not an artifact that vanishes. We give the first finite-sample envelope that bounds the deviation from Gaussianity and pins the tangent-space covariance eigenstructure, turning an emergent observation into a certifiable, anisotropy-aware statement.","anchor_pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","anchor_pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","domain_category":"Learning Theory & Statistics","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes the finite-N / finite-temperature deviation of InfoNCE representations from their asymptotic Gaussian limit: there is no envelope or rate that tells a practitioner, at the batch size they actually train at, how far the true law sits from Gaussian and which direction the discrepancy will shrink in -- the outcome 'a certifiable finite-sample bound on non-Gaussianity' is achieved by no leaf.","pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"closed by formalizing the anchor's asymptotic-marginal result as a separation criterion (it cannot distinguish a finite-N law from its Gaussian limit) and re-injecting the discarded finite-N fluctuation via a Stein/Berry-Esseen-style quantitative bound that yields an explicit O(tau^2 + 1/sqrt(N_eff)) envelope on a smooth integral-probability-metric distance to the matched Gaussian.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes the COVARIANCE / tangent-space anisotropy of the limiting representation law -- whether the InfoNCE geometry actively prefers an isotropic Gaussian or a structured anisotropic one is unaddressed; the augmentation-overlap and augmentation-aware leaves bound only downstream risk and never the second-moment structure of the marginal.","pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"closed by re-injecting the second-moment object the anchor discards: deriving the stationary tangent-space covariance Sigma_T as the fixed point of the InfoNCE uniformity-vs-alignment force balance, and proving its eigenstructure is governed by the augmentation channel's HGR-conditional covariance, so the matched Gaussian in leg 1 is provably anisotropic with a closed-form condition-number lower bound.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"self-supervised / contrastive representation learning theory","n_papers":27,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":25},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":21,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Supervised Contrastive Representation Learning: Landscape Analysis with Unconstrained Features"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A World Model Reinforcement Learning Method That Is Not Distracted by Background Information by Using Representation Learning via Invariant Causal Mechanisms for Non-Contrastive Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"CL-SR: Boosting Imbalanced Image Classification with Contrastive Learning and Synthetic Minority Oversampling Technique Based on Rough Set Theory Integration"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Idempotent Unsupervised Representation Learning for Skeleton-Based Action Recognition"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Hierarchical Banzhaf Interaction for General Video-Language Representation Learning"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Adversarial alignment and graph fusion via information bottleneck for multimodal emotion recognition in conversations"}],"more":15},{"year":2025,"n":17,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"The contrastive learning method in tongue image representation learning and its significance in intelligent diagnosis"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Research on Node Evaluation Model of Disciplinary Knowledge Graph Based on Contrastive Learning Theory"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"An Augmentation-Aware Theory for Self-Supervised Contrastive Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"An Augmentation Overlap Theory of Contrastive Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Revisiting Theory of Contrastive Learning for Domain Generalization"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Binary Representation Learning for Discriminative Acoustic Unit Discovery"}],"more":11},{"year":2026,"n":10,"papers":[{"source":"arxiv","title":"The Inclusion Depth of Pattern Languages: An Open Problem in Algorithmic Learning Theory"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"From Performance to Viability: A Bootstrap Framework for Latent-Space Representation Learning in Adaptive Biological Systems"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Contrastive Reasoning Alignment: Reinforcement Learning from Hidden Representations"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Stable $\\infty$-categories for representation theorists"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"ACDC: Adaptive Curriculum Planning with Dynamic Contrastive Control for Goal-Conditioned Reinforcement Learning in Robotic Manipulation"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"InfoNCE Induces Gaussian Distribution"}],"more":4}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":3,"share":0.111},{"pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass; assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"characterize_limit_then_surpass; assumption_audit_and_pivot","count":1,"share":0.037},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot; architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"assumption_audit_and_pivot; architectural_operator_substitution","count":1,"share":0.037},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot; controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"assumption_audit_and_pivot; controlled_diagnostic_design","count":1,"share":0.037},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot; reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"assumption_audit_and_pivot; reframe_as_solvable_object","count":1,"share":0.037},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot; characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"assumption_audit_and_pivot; characterize_limit_then_surpass","count":1,"share":0.037},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering; heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"self_supervised_signal_engineering; heterogeneous_decomposition","count":1,"share":0.037},{"pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass; reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"characterize_limit_then_surpass; reframe_as_solvable_object","count":1,"share":0.037}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"The anchor result (arxiv:2602.24012v1) establishes that one-dimensional projections of InfoNCE-trained representations converge to a marginal Gaussian, but the convergence is purely asymptotic and is conditioned on an alignment plateau bounded via HGR maximal correlation plus a norm-concentration assumption; consequently at any finite batch size N and finite temperature tau the actual representation law is an unknown perturbation of that Gaussian whose anisotropy (the covariance eigenstructure on the tangent space of the hypersphere) is left completely uncharacterized, so a practitioner cannot tell whether an observed deviation from Gaussianity is a finite-N artifact that will vanish or a genuine anisotropic structure that the InfoNCE geometry actively prefers. The adjacent theory papers do not close this either: the augmentation-overlap and augmentation-aware bounds (semanticscholar:b772dc4f2bcd6a9af123d1c8e8dc616df5fdc7b2, semanticscholar:d86e641baeb80530d530fafcccdafb108ae2a127) bound downstream RISK as a function of augmentation strength but never the marginal geometry of the embedding, and the unconstrained-features landscape result (semanticscholar:8b98640dc14fffe9a3e101dd6f5f2f58ee5afe2d) pins down a unique simplex-type minimizer for the SUPERVISED contrastive loss but in a label-conditioned UFM proxy that discards exactly the population-level isotropy question. The failure is therefore: existing machinery produces an asymptotic shape claim with no finite-sample envelope and no covariance characterization, so the Gaussianity is neither certifiable nor controllable at the scales people actually train at.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.24012v1","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Proves that projections of InfoNCE representations are asymptotically marginally Gaussian via two routes (an empirical-idealization route that assumes alignment hits a plateau and norm concentrates, reducing InfoNCE to a constrained uniformity problem on the sphere, and a regularized route that adds a vanishing low-norm/high-entropy penalty), with a novel HGR-maximal-correlation alignment bound as the key ingredient. Residue: the theorem is an asymptotic statement about marginal projections only -- it neither characterizes the COVARIANCE / tangent-space anisotropy of the limiting law nor supplies any finite-N rate of convergence, so it cannot say how Gaussian a real finite-batch encoder actually is or whether the limit is isotropic, leaving Gaussianity an emergent observation rather than a quantity that can be measured-against-a-bound or enforced."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2606.00262v1","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Uses extreme-value theory to show InfoNCE's softmax encodes a mis-specified tail assumption on the top-scoring negative under normalized embeddings, and patches it with a parameter-free batch-statistic logit correction (WEINCE) that improves frozen-feature accuracy. Residue: it modifies the loss to fix a tail mismatch but never characterizes the resulting embedding distribution -- it is silent on whether the correction changes the marginal Gaussianity or its anisotropy, so the link between the loss's tail handling and the induced representation geometry is left open."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:8b98640dc14fffe9a3e101dd6f5f2f58ee5afe2d","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Analyzes the supervised-contrastive loss landscape in the unconstrained-features model and proves all local minima are global with a unique (up-to-rotation) minimizer via a tight convex relaxation. Residue: the result lives in a label-conditioned UFM proxy that fixes the feature geometry by construction (a discrete simplex-type configuration), so it characterizes a supervised minimizer's discrete shape rather than the population-level continuous marginal/covariance law of the unsupervised InfoNCE encoder -- the isotropy-vs-anisotropy question is assumed away, not answered."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"self-supervised / contrastive representation learning theory","venue":"ICLR / NeurIPS / ICML (theory track)","time":"2026","data":["CIFAR-10","synthetic isotropic/anisotropic latent models","ImageNet-100 (optional empirical)"],"compute":"diagnostic / light-empirical: 1xA100 x a few days for CIFAR-scale verification; core contribution is theory","expertise":"probability / high-dimensional statistics / representation-learning theory","preference":"theory","baseline":"InfoNCE Induces Gaussian Distribution (arxiv:2602.24012v1) asymptotic marginal-Gaussianity result","limitation":"the anchor proves only that low-dimensional PROJECTIONS of InfoNCE representations are asymptotically marginally Gaussian under an alignment-plateau + norm-concentration assumption (or under a vanishing low-norm/high-entropy regularizer); it says nothing about the covariance/anisotropy structure of the limiting law, gives no finite-sample rate, and the Gaussianity is a passive emergent property rather than a quantity one can certify or steer at finite N","contribution_type":"theory","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object both legs read from and write to is the limiting law mu_N of the l2-normalized InfoNCE representation u = f_hat(X) on the unit hypersphere S^{d-1}, viewed in the tangent space at the population mean direction (so the manifold is locally Euclidean and a Gaussian comparison is well-defined). Leg 1 (characterize the limit, then surpass it): the anchor (arxiv:2602.24012v1) proves only that one-dimensional projections <a,u> are asymptotically marginally Gaussian under an alignment plateau plus norm concentration; we formalize its blindspot as a separation criterion -- the anchor's statement is invariant to any perturbation of mu_N that preserves marginal projections in the limit, hence it provably cannot distinguish mu_N at finite (N, tau) from its Gaussian limit. We re-inject the discarded object (the finite-N fluctuation) by treating the InfoNCE population gradient on the sphere as a Stein operator: the constrained-uniformity problem the anchor reduces to has a known Gaussian stationary measure in the limit, and a quantitative Stein/Berry-Esseen argument bounds a smooth integral-probability-metric (IPM) distance d_IPM(mu_N, N(0,Sigma_T)) by an explicit envelope E(N,tau,Lc) = c1*tau^2 + c2*Lc/sqrt(N_eff), where N_eff is the effective number of negatives (N_eff = (N-1)*(1 - rho_align) with rho_align the HGR maximal-correlation alignment level read off the anchor's alignment bound), Lc is the encoder's Lipschitz constant on the data manifold (a model-internal readout estimated by the spectral norm of the Jacobian on a held-out batch), and c1, c2 are explicit dimension-free constants from the Stein bound. Every quantity is computable from the trained encoder and a batch: rho_align is the mean positive-pair cosine similarity, tau is the loss temperature (a fixed hyperparameter), Lc is the Jacobian spectral-norm estimate, and N_eff follows from N and rho_align. Leg 2 (same object, second moment): the matched Gaussian N(0,Sigma_T) in leg 1 is NOT assumed isotropic -- we derive Sigma_T as the fixed point of the InfoNCE force balance (alignment pulls along the augmentation-conditional mean direction, uniformity pushes isotropically), giving Sigma_T proportional to (I - beta*C_aug)^{-1} restricted to the tangent space, where C_aug is the HGR-conditional covariance of an augmentation given its anchor (computed from augmented-pair embeddings) and beta = beta(tau) is an explicit temperature-dependent weight bridging the two unit-incommensurate forces. From this we prove a closed-form lower bound on the condition number kappa(Sigma_T) >= 1 + beta*lambda_gap(C_aug) where lambda_gap is the spectral gap of C_aug, so whenever the augmentation channel is itself anisotropic (lambda_gap > 0) the induced Gaussian is provably anisotropic at every finite scale and in the limit. The two legs interlock on mu_N: leg 1 bounds the distance from mu_N to a Gaussian, and leg 2 identifies WHICH Gaussian (its covariance), so together they upgrade 'InfoNCE induces a Gaussian' to 'InfoNCE induces an anisotropic Gaussian, and here is the certified finite-N envelope around it'.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The two gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules because they are two questions about ONE object (mu_N): 'how close to Gaussian' (leg 1) is only meaningful relative to 'which Gaussian' (leg 2), so the matched covariance Sigma_T derived in leg 2 is literally the reference measure inside leg 1's IPM distance -- making them one theorem with a coupled proof, not two stapled results. We considered the alternative of a purely empirical anisotropy study (measure kappa across encoders) but rejected it because contribution_type is theory and an empirical-only leg would not surpass the anchor's analytical claim; we also considered casting the finite-N argument as a CLT-rate corollary of the anchor but rejected it because the anchor gives no covariance, so a bare rate would still inherit the isotropy ambiguity. Regression check: the avoided node is c1 (von Mises-Fisher / directional density fitting) and c0/c1's machinery (Berry-Esseen, Stein) is awareness-only -- our novelty is not 'use a quantitative CLT' (that machinery is old) but deriving the InfoNCE-specific Stein operator and the closed-form Sigma_T fixed point, which no ancestral node supplies; we record that the load-bearing artifact lands on neither n2 (alignment-uniformity, which never gives a finite-N law) nor c1 (which gives a density but not the InfoNCE-induced covariance).","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: train SimCLR-style InfoNCE encoders (ResNet-18/50) on CIFAR-10 and ImageNet-100 at batch sizes N in {128, 512, 2048} and temperature tau in {0.07, 0.2, 0.5}; in the tangent space at the mean direction, measure (i) a smooth IPM/kernel-MMD distance from the empirical representation law to its moment-matched Gaussian and (ii) the condition number kappa of the empirical tangent-space covariance. If the candidate is correct, the measured IPM distance decreases as 1/sqrt(N_eff) and stays below the derived envelope E(N,tau,Lc)=c1*tau^2 + c2*Lc/sqrt(N_eff) at every setting (envelope holds), while kappa stays bounded away from 1 and tracks the predicted 1 + beta*lambda_gap(C_aug) rather than collapsing to isotropy as N grows. The named load-bearing variable is lambda_gap(C_aug), the spectral gap of the augmentation-conditional covariance; the negative-control intervention replaces the data augmentation with an isotropic-dither-only channel that drives lambda_gap toward 0, and the mechanism is confirmed only if this control makes the downstream measured kappa collapse toward 1 (the anisotropy disappears) while the random-augmentation arm keeps kappa bounded away from 1 -- if kappa stays anisotropic even under the isotropic-augmentation control, the C_aug mechanism is falsified. A positive control trains a stripped linear-encoder model whose only structure is C_aug and checks it reproduces most of the predicted kappa, converting the falsifier into a constructive identification of C_aug as the anisotropy source.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.24012v1","delta":"They prove that one-dimensional projections of InfoNCE representations are ASYMPTOTICALLY and MARGINALLY Gaussian (no rate, no covariance); we derive a finite-N envelope E(N,tau,Lc) bounding the IPM distance to a matched Gaussian AND a closed-form anisotropic covariance Sigma_T with a condition-number lower bound, neither of which their asymptotic-marginal analysis produces."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2606.00262v1","delta":"They modify the InfoNCE loss (WEINCE) to fix a softmax tail mis-specification but never characterize the induced embedding distribution; we leave the loss unchanged and instead characterize the distribution's finite-N proximity to, and anisotropy of, its Gaussian limit."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:8b98640dc14fffe9a3e101dd6f5f2f58ee5afe2d","delta":"They pin a unique discrete simplex-type minimizer for the SUPERVISED contrastive loss in an unconstrained-features proxy; we characterize the continuous population covariance of the UNSUPERVISED InfoNCE marginal and prove it is anisotropic, a second-moment statement their label-conditioned UFM discards."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:b772dc4f2bcd6a9af123d1c8e8dc616df5fdc7b2","delta":"They bound downstream supervised RISK as a function of augmentation overlap; we bound the embedding LAW's distance to Gaussian and tie its covariance eigenstructure to the augmentation-conditional covariance, a geometry statement their risk bound never makes."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"arxiv:2602.24012v1","what_step_was_missed":"The anchor reduces InfoNCE to a constrained-uniformity problem on the sphere and reads off marginal Gaussianity in the limit, but it never instantiates a quantitative Stein/Berry-Esseen bound for that stationary measure (which would give the finite-N rate) and never solves the alignment-vs-uniformity force balance for the stationary second moment (which would give the covariance Sigma_T and its anisotropy). Constructing the InfoNCE-specific Stein operator and the Sigma_T fixed point are the two substantive steps their asymptotic-marginal route did not take."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":264,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"No hard-floor rule fired: gap_closure_reject_check is borderline (no lesson candidate_match: yes), recipe_application_check is applied on both legs, anti_pattern_check matched nothing, and paper_pointed_threat arxiv:2603.12552v1 is adjacent-not-overlapping. But the threat's addressable_via names a specific candidate field (differentiation_from_lit lacks any delta against the one collision paper that also claims finite-time InfoNCE theory), and the borderline reject lesson ('recently published method may subsume') hits the load-bearing novelty boundary of leg 1 -- per the heuristic 'choose revise when paper_pointed_threat exists AND addressable_via names a specific candidate field', this is a revise with a single tactical target.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes the finite-N / finite-temperature deviation of InfoNCE representations from their asymptotic Gaussian limit: there is no envelope or rate that tells a practitioner, at the batch size they actually train at, how far the true law sits from Gaussian and which direction the discrepancy will shrink in -- the outcome 'a certifiable finite-sample bound on non-Gaussianity' is achieved by no leaf.","main_pattern":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail when the 'limit' they characterize is not a genuine structural blindspot -- trivially implied by the model's own assumptions, already surpassed by a published method, or never formalized beyond an informal analogy; the self-check is whether you can exhibit concrete objects the method conflates, prove no published method separates them, and bound your added cost.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Resting the central claim on an informal analogy (two operators 'both smooth high frequencies') instead of a separation proof leaves the mechanism underspecified and the empirical gain unconvincing.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The separation criterion is formal: the anchor's statement is invariant to any mu_N perturbation preserving limiting marginal projections, so it provably cannot distinguish finite-N mu_N from its Gaussian limit -- a stated invariance, not an analogy."},{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a 'maximally expressive' construction that a recently published method already strictly subsumes turns the surpass-the-limit claim into redundant work.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"collision_hits surfaces arxiv:2603.12552v1 (Asymptotic and Finite-Time Guarantees for Langevin-Based Temperature Annealing in InfoNCE) which also claims finite-time InfoNCE guarantees; it targets annealing-schedule convergence to global optima, NOT a finite-N distance-to-Gaussian envelope or covariance, so it does not subsume, but the overlap on 'finite-time InfoNCE' must be explicitly distinguished."},{"lesson_quoted":"Deriving a 'limitation' that is trivially implied by the model's own linearity assumption produces a limit too weak to count as a real blindspot, and the proposed surpass step stays under-validated.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The blindspot (no finite-N rate, no covariance) is not implied by any assumption of the anchor -- the anchor genuinely stops at an asymptotic marginal claim, so the limit is a real omission, and the surpass step is validated by the envelope-holds + kappa-tracking experiment."},{"lesson_quoted":"Asserting the 'first efficient implementation' of a long-known algorithm without surveying the landscape invites direct refutation by existing faster implementations and collapses the novelty claim.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate makes no efficiency/implementation-first claim; its contribution is an analytical bound plus a covariance characterization, and compute is a light diagnostic, not an algorithmic speedup."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes the COVARIANCE / tangent-space anisotropy of the limiting representation law -- whether the InfoNCE geometry actively prefers an isotropic Gaussian or a structured anisotropic one is unaddressed; the augmentation-overlap and augmentation-aware leaves bound only downstream risk and never the second-moment structure of the marginal.","main_pattern":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail when the characterized limit is not a genuine structural blindspot or the augmented operator is never proven to capture an invariant the incumbent provably misses, producing abstraction with no testable advantage and no baseline comparison.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Applying existing structural descriptors to a new application domain without formalizing a new limit or constructing a new operator yields a domain study, not a methodological contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate constructs a new object (the InfoNCE force-balance fixed-point covariance Sigma_T) and proves a new closed-form condition-number bound, not a port of an existing descriptor."},{"lesson_quoted":"A novel formalism that cannot generate predictions or demonstrate concrete advantages over existing definitions reads as abstraction for its own sake.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Sigma_T yields a falsifiable prediction (kappa stays bounded away from 1 and tracks 1+beta*lambda_gap) with a negative control on lambda_gap, so the formalism generates a concrete, testable prediction the anchor's marginal claim cannot."},{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a 'maximally expressive' construction that a recently published method already strictly subsumes turns the surpass-the-limit claim into redundant work.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"No retrieved or collision paper characterizes the InfoNCE marginal's covariance/anisotropy; the SC-loss UFM result (semanticscholar:8b98640d...) gives a discrete supervised minimizer, not the unsupervised continuous covariance, so nothing subsumes this leg."}],"verdict":"clear"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The covariance/anisotropy leg is clear; the finite-N leg is borderline only on the 'recently published method may subsume' lesson, driven by collision hit arxiv:2603.12552v1 whose finite-time InfoNCE claim is adjacent but targets annealing-schedule convergence rather than a distance-to-Gaussian envelope -- no Reject lesson is marked candidate_match: yes, so the aggregate is borderline, not triggered."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes the finite-N / finite-temperature deviation of InfoNCE representations from their asymptotic Gaussian limit: there is no envelope or rate that tells a practitioner, at the batch size they actually train at, how far the true law sits from Gaussian and which direction the discrepancy will shrink in -- the outcome 'a certifiable finite-sample bound on non-Gaussianity' is achieved by no leaf.","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Pinpoint the one structural object an established procedure discards for tractability, formalize the equivalence class this discarding induces as a separation/indistinguishability criterion on the procedure's native objects, then re-inject that exact object into the procedure's core step and prove the augmented operator strictly exceeds the criterion at bounded cost.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism Leg 1 names the discarded object (the finite-N fluctuation of mu_N that the anchor's asymptotic-marginal route averages away), formalizes the separation criterion (the anchor's claim is invariant to any perturbation preserving limiting marginal projections, hence cannot distinguish finite-N mu_N from its limit), and re-injects that object via an InfoNCE-specific Stein operator yielding the explicit envelope E(N,tau,Lc) -- the exact 'name the discarded object -> separation criterion -> re-inject -> prove strict exceedance' move.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes the COVARIANCE / tangent-space anisotropy of the limiting representation law -- whether the InfoNCE geometry actively prefers an isotropic Gaussian or a structured anisotropic one is unaddressed; the augmentation-overlap and augmentation-aware leaves bound only downstream risk and never the second-moment structure of the marginal.","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Re-inject the discarded structural object into the procedure's core computational step so it becomes first-class structure, and prove the augmented characterization captures the specific invariant the incumbent provably misses, with bounded added cost.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism Leg 2 re-injects the second-moment object the anchor discards (the tangent-space covariance) by deriving Sigma_T as the InfoNCE force-balance fixed point and proving kappa(Sigma_T) >= 1 + beta*lambda_gap(C_aug), the closed-form anisotropy certificate -- capturing the augmentation-conditional covariance invariant the marginal analysis provably cannot see.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both legs perform C10's signature move on the InfoNCE representation law: leg 1 names the discarded finite-N fluctuation and re-injects it via a Stein operator to a proven envelope; leg 2 re-injects the discarded covariance to a proven anisotropy bound -- neither stops at the parent's generic 'characterize a limit' gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["characterize_limit_then_surpass","characterize_limit_then_surpass"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"The composition set is a single pattern (characterize_limit_then_surpass on both legs) and contains no heterogeneous_decomposition, so none of the three documented reject-favored 2-way compositions matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"arxiv:2603.12552v1","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"arxiv:2603.12552v1 (Asymptotic and Finite-Time Guarantees for Langevin-Based Temperature Annealing in InfoNCE) provides finite-time InfoNCE guarantees by modeling embedding evolution as Langevin dynamics on a compact Riemannian manifold and shows logarithmic annealing schedules converge in probability to globally optimal representations. This is the nearest threat because it also claims finite-time InfoNCE theory, but its quantity is convergence-of-the-optimizer-to-global-optima under a temperature SCHEDULE, not the marginal representation law's finite-N distance to a Gaussian nor its covariance anisotropy; the candidate's claim stands because neither a distance-to-Gaussian envelope E(N,tau,Lc) nor the force-balance covariance Sigma_T with its condition-number bound is derivable from a global-convergence annealing result -- they answer orthogonal questions (how-Gaussian-and-how-anisotropic-the-law-is vs. does-the-optimizer-reach-the-optimum).","addressable_via":"differentiation_from_lit should add an explicit delta against arxiv:2603.12552v1 stating that their finite-time guarantee is optimizer-convergence under annealing whereas ours is a finite-N distributional envelope plus covariance characterization at fixed tau, removing the surface 'finite-time InfoNCE' overlap."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat (arxiv:2603.12552v1) + gap_closure_reject_check borderline lesson 'a recently published method may subsume the surpass claim'","fix_direction":"Add a differentiation_from_lit entry for arxiv:2603.12552v1 with a substantive delta: their finite-time guarantee certifies optimizer convergence to globally optimal representations under a logarithmic temperature-annealing schedule via Langevin dynamics, whereas this candidate certifies, at FIXED temperature and finite batch size, the representation law's IPM distance to a matched Gaussian (envelope E) and that Gaussian's covariance anisotropy (Sigma_T condition-number bound) -- the two results characterize orthogonal quantities (optimization convergence vs. distributional geometry), so no subsumption. Do not change falsification_prediction or compute_budget."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added a differentiation_from_lit entry for arxiv:2603.12552v1 distinguishing their annealing-schedule optimizer-convergence guarantee from our fixed-tau finite-N distance-to-Gaussian envelope and covariance characterization."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# A Finite-Sample Anisotropy Envelope for InfoNCE-Induced Gaussianity\n\n**Method.** Finite-Sample Anisotropy Envelope (FSAE)\n\n## Motivation\nWhen you train an image encoder with the popular contrastive objective InfoNCE (Information Noise-Contrastive Estimation), the resulting feature vectors tend to 'look Gaussian' (bell-shaped), and many practical tools quietly assume this. A very recent theory paper proved that, in the limit of infinitely large training batches, one-dimensional shadows of these features really are Gaussian. The catch: that proof is about the infinite limit and about one-dimensional shadows only. At the batch size you actually train with, it tells you nothing about how close to Gaussian your features really are, nor about the SHAPE of that Gaussian — whether it is a perfectly round ball (isotropic) or a stretched ellipsoid (anisotropic).\n\nThis is the right moment to fix that. The recent proof rewrote InfoNCE training as a clean 'spread out evenly on a sphere' problem whose limiting distribution is exactly the kind of object that classical finite-sample approximation tools (Stein's method, Berry-Esseen bounds) are built to handle. So we can finally (a) bound how far a finite-batch encoder sits from Gaussian, and (b) compute the actual covariance (the ellipsoid's shape) instead of assuming a round ball.\n\nPrior work stopped short for concrete reasons. The anchor paper (arXiv 2026-02) gave only the infinite-limit, one-dimensional result and never instantiated a finite-sample rate or solved for the covariance. The WEINCE paper (arXiv 2026-05) fixed a different statistical flaw in the InfoNCE loss but never described the resulting feature distribution. A 2024 information-theory paper pinned the exact shape of the SUPERVISED contrastive minimizer, but in a simplified proxy model that assumes the geometry away rather than deriving it.\n\nWhen this gap closes, every downstream tool that models InfoNCE features as Gaussian gets a certified error bar (how trustworthy the Gaussian assumption is at your batch size) and an explicit ellipsoid shape to plug in, instead of blindly assuming a round ball. And augmentation design gains a direct dial — the spread of the data augmentations — onto that shape.\n\n## Method\n### Comparison frame and inputs\n*Set up the tangent-space Gaussian comparison and read off the loss-level quantities the bounds need.*\n\n1. Take a held-out batch of L2-normalized feature vectors (use at least ten times the feature dimension d so the estimate is stable), estimate their average direction by summing them and re-normalizing to unit length, and then re-express every feature as a small displacement in the flat tangent plane at that average direction. Concretely, for each feature compute the logarithmic map: take the angle to the average direction (the inverse cosine of their dot product) and the unit vector pointing from the average direction toward the feature, and multiply them; write the result in a fixed orthonormal basis of that tangent plane (obtained by a QR factorization). The output is a table of $(d- 1)-dimensional$ tangent coordinates plus the basis, which is where a Gaussian comparison is meaningful.\n   - _Why_: On a sphere there is no global flat coordinate, but near the average direction the surface is locally flat, which is where a Gaussian comparison is meaningful.\n2. Measure the alignment level $\\rho _{align}$ — the average cosine similarity (dot product of unit-length embeddings) between matched positive pairs — by drawing one fresh augmented positive per anchor on the held-out split, embedding both, and averaging. Read the temperature $\\tau $ straight from the loss settings, and take N as the batch size the model was trained with. Combine them into an effective negative count $N_{eff} = (N- 1)\\cdot (1- \\rho _{align}).$ These three numbers are exactly what the finite-sample bound needs, and they are already available from any trained model.\n   - _Why_: These three numbers are exactly what the finite-sample bound needs, and they are already available from any trained model.\n3. Estimate the encoder's Lipschitz constant Lc — how much the output can change for a small input change — as the largest singular value of its Jacobian. For each input in a held-out batch, run power iteration that only ever multiplies a vector by the Jacobian and by its transpose (both done by automatic differentiation, so the full Jacobian is never built): repeatedly apply Jacobian-then-transpose to a random unit vector and renormalize, for about twenty iterations or until the length stops changing, to get that input's largest singular value. Then take the maximum of these values over the batch as Lc, because a Lipschitz constant is a worst-case (supremum) quantity; also report the 95th percentile as a stability check. The smoothness of the encoder sets the scale of the finite-sample error, so the bound is meaningless without it.\n   - _Why_: The smoothness of the encoder sets the scale of the finite-sample error, so the bound is meaningless without it.\n\n### Finite-sample envelope\n*Prove the certifiable distance-to-Gaussian bound via an InfoNCE-specific Stein operator.*\n\n4. Write down the population InfoNCE gradient flow on the sphere, identify the distribution it settles into in the alignment-plateau limit, and apply a quantitative Stein / Berry-Esseen argument to prove that the distance from the feature distribution to its matched Gaussian is at most a small-temperature-squared term plus a fluctuation term that shrinks with the effective negative count. Use the smooth distance defined over test functions with a bounded third derivative (the natural setting for this kind of approximation argument), not a raw total-variation distance. The two constants in front are not tuned: the first is read off from the curvature the temperature induces in the loss landscape, and the second from the leftover third-moment term in the Berry-Esseen bound — both come out of the proof as explicit formulas. This re-injects the finite-batch fluctuation the original proof averaged away, turning an infinite-limit claim into a usable finite-batch error bar.\n\n*The finite-sample envelope: the smooth IPM distance between the InfoNCE representation law $\\mu _{N}$ and its matched Gaussian is bounded by $a \\tau ^{2}$ term plus an $Lc/\\surd (N_{eff})$ term, with $N_{eff}$ the effective negative count set by the alignment level $\\rho _{align}.$*\n$$ d_{\\mathrm{IPM}}\\big(\\mu_N,\\;\\mathcal{N}(0,\\Sigma_T)\\big)\\;\\le\\;c_1\\,\\tau^2\\;+\\;c_2\\,\\frac{L_c}{\\sqrt{N_{\\mathrm{eff}}}},\\qquad N_{\\mathrm{eff}}=(N-1)\\,(1-\\rho_{\\mathrm{align}}) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This re-injects the finite-batch fluctuation the original proof averaged away, turning an infinite-limit claim into a usable finite-batch error bar.\n\n### Anisotropic covariance characterization\n*Build the augmentation-conditional covariance, derive the stationary covariance, and prove the anisotropy certificate.*\n\n5. For each of many held-out anchor images (use at least ten times the feature dimension so the matrix is well-conditioned), embed K augmentations of that anchor (a default of 64 augmentations is enough for a low-variance per-anchor average), map them into the tangent plane from step 1 (Take a held-out batch $of\\dots ),$ subtract that anchor's average, and accumulate the covariance of these augmentation-induced deviations. Averaging over all anchors and augmentations gives the matrix $C_{aug}, a$ symmetric positive-semidefinite matrix in tangent coordinates; also compute its eigenvalues (largest to smallest). $C_{aug}$ captures how the data augmentations spread features around — the exact ingredient that determines the ellipsoid's shape.\n   - _Why_: $C_{aug}$ captures how the data augmentations spread features around — the exact ingredient that determines the ellipsoid's shape.\n6. Balance the pull of alignment (which stretches features along the directions the augmentations vary, captured by $C_{aug})$ against the isotropic push of uniformity, by linearizing the training dynamics around the settled mean direction, and solve for the resulting covariance $Sigma_{T}.$ It comes out proportional to the inverse of (the identity minus a temperature-dependent weight $\\beta $ times $C_{aug}),$ computed entirely in the $(d- 1)-dimensional$ tangent plane from step 1 (Take a held-out batch $of\\dots ),$ so no large ambient matrix is inverted. The temperature weight $\\beta $ grows as temperature shrinks (roughly one-over-temperature, so colder temperatures make the ellipsoid more stretched); its exact value falls out of the force-balance derivation. Rescale $Sigma_{T}$ to have unit total variance so only its shape matters, and confirm it is the same Gaussian used in step 4 (Write down the population $InfoNCE\\dots ).$ This identifies WHICH Gaussian the features approach, not just that they approach some Gaussian, supplying the missing shape.\n\n*The stationary tangent-space covariance $Sigma_{T}$ is the force-balance fixed point: the inverse of I minus a temperature-weighted augmentation-conditional covariance $C_{aug},$ restricted to the tangent space at the mean direction.*\n$$ \\Sigma_T\\;\\propto\\;\\big(I-\\beta\\,C_{\\mathrm{aug}}\\big)^{-1}\\big|_{T_{\\bar\\mu}\\mathbb{S}^{d-1}},\\qquad \\beta=\\beta(\\tau) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This identifies WHICH Gaussian the features approach, not just that they approach some Gaussian, supplying the missing shape.\n7. From the covariance $Sigma_{T},$ prove that its condition number (the ratio of its largest to smallest variance directions) is at least one plus the temperature weight $\\beta $ times the spread of $C_{aug}'s$ eigenvalues — where that spread is the largest minus the smallest eigenvalue of $C_{aug}.$ The proof is a one-line algebra step from the closed form of $Sigma_{T}.$ Then check the safety condition that $\\beta $ times the largest eigenvalue of $C_{aug}$ is below one, which guarantees the formula is well-defined (the matrix being inverted stays positive); if that fails for the measured values, report that you are outside the regime the bound covers rather than pushing the formula past where it holds. A condition number above 1 means a stretched ellipsoid, so this turns 'is it round or stretched' into a provable, directional statement.\n\n*The anisotropy certificate: the covariance condition number is at least 1 plus the temperature weight times the spectral gap of $C_{aug},$ so a nonzero augmentation spectral gap forces genuine anisotropy.*\n$$ \\kappa(\\Sigma_T)\\;\\ge\\;1+\\beta\\,\\lambda_{\\mathrm{gap}}(C_{\\mathrm{aug}}) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A condition number above 1 means a stretched ellipsoid, so this turns 'is it round or stretched' into a provable, directional statement.\n\n### Empirical verification\n*Test both bounds across encoders and a negative control that removes augmentation anisotropy.*\n\n8. Train SimCLR-style encoders on CIFAR-10 and ImageNet-100 with two or three encoder sizes, at batch sizes 128 / 512 / 2048 and temperatures 0.07 / 0.2 / 0.5. For each setting, measure two things in the tangent plane: (a) the actual distance to the predicted Gaussian, estimated by the maximum-mean-discrepancy (MMD) — a standard two-sample distance — using a Gaussian bell-shaped kernel whose width is set to the median distance between points (the usual default), comparing the real tangent coordinates against an equal-size sample drawn from the predicted Gaussian; and (b) the actual condition number of the empirical tangent covariance. Then report, per setting, the ratio of the measured distance to the predicted envelope (it should stay at or below one if the bound holds) and the relative error between the measured condition number and the predicted one. Finally run the negative control: swap the data augmentation for one that only adds small, direction-neutral random noise of matched strength (removing the directional crop and color changes), which should drive the augmentation spread toward zero; retrain and confirm the measured condition number collapses toward one, while the normal-augmentation run keeps it clearly above one. If the bound and the shape prediction are right, the measured distance stays under the envelope and the condition number stays stretched except under the round-augmentation control, where it should collapse toward 1.\n   - _Why_: If the bound and the shape prediction are right, the measured distance stays under the envelope and $\\kappa $ stays stretched except under the round-augmentation control, where it should collapse toward 1.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# InfoNCE 诱导高斯性的有限样本各向异性包络\n\n**方法名称.** Finite-Sample Anisotropy Envelope (FSAE)\n\n## 研究动机\n当你用流行的对比学习目标 InfoNCE（Information Noise-Contrastive Estimation）训练图像编码器时，得到的特征向量往往「看起来像高斯分布」（钟形），许多实用工具默默假设了这一点。最近一篇理论文章证明：在训练批量无限大的极限下，这些特征的一维投影确实是高斯的。问题在于：那个证明只针对无限极限、且只针对一维投影。在你实际使用的批量大小下，它无法告诉你特征到底有多接近高斯，也无法告诉你这个高斯的「形状」——是一个完美的圆球（各向同性 isotropic），还是一个被拉伸的椭球（各向异性 anisotropic）。\n\n现在正是补上这一点的时机。最近那篇证明把 InfoNCE 训练重写为一个干净的「在球面上均匀铺开」问题，其极限分布恰好是经典有限样本逼近工具（Stein 方法、Berry-Esseen 界）所擅长处理的对象。于是我们终于可以：(a) 界定有限批量编码器与高斯的距离，(b) 计算真实的协方差（椭球的形状），而不是假设一个圆球。\n\n先前工作止步是有具体原因的。锚点论文（arXiv 2026-02）只给出无限极限、一维的结果，从未给出有限样本速率或求解协方差。WEINCE 论文（arXiv 2026-05）修正了 InfoNCE 损失中另一个统计缺陷，却从未描述所得到的特征分布。2024 年一篇信息论文章确定了「有监督」对比极小化解的精确形状，但是在一个把几何结构直接假设掉、而非推导出来的简化代理模型里。\n\n当这一缺口补上后，每一个把 InfoNCE 特征建模为高斯的下游工具，都会获得一个有认证的误差范围（在你的批量大小下高斯假设有多可信）以及一个明确的椭球形状可以代入，而不再盲目假设圆球。而且数据增广设计也获得了一个直接的旋钮——增广的展开程度——来调控这个形状。\n\n## 方法\n### 比较坐标系与输入\n*建立切空间高斯比较，并读取各个界所需的损失层面量。*\n\n1. 取一批留出的、做了 L2 归一化的特征向量（数量至少为特征维度 d 的十倍，以保证估计稳定），先把它们求和再重新归一化到单位长度，得到平均方向；然后把每个特征改写为在该平均方向处「切平面」上的小位移。具体做法是对每个特征计算对数映射(logarithmic map)：取它与平均方向之间的夹角（即两者点积的反余弦 arccos），再乘以从平均方向指向该特征的单位向量；并把结果写在该切平面的一组固定标准正交基里（这组基由 QR 分解得到）。输出是一张 $(d- 1)$ 维切空间坐标表加上这组基——这正是高斯比较有意义的地方。\n   - _为什么_: 球面上没有全局平直坐标，但在平均方向附近曲面是局部平直的，这正是高斯比较有意义的地方。\n2. 测量对齐水平 $\\rho _{align}——$即匹配正样本对之间的平均余弦相似度（单位长度嵌入的点积）：在 第1步（取一批留出的） 的同一留出集上，对每个锚点抽取一个新的增广正样本，嵌入两者后求平均。从损失设置中直接读取温度 $\\tau $，并把 N 取为模型训练时所用的批量大小。把它们组合成有效负样本数 $N_{eff} = (N- 1)\\cdot (1- \\rho _{align})$。这三个数正是有限样本界所需要的，而且任何训练好的模型都已经可以得到它们。\n   - _为什么_: 这三个数正是有限样本界所需要的，而且任何训练好的模型都已经可以得到它们。\n3. 估计编码器的 Lipschitz 常数 Lc——即输入发生微小变化时输出最多能改变多少——它等于编码器 Jacobian 的最大奇异值。对留出批次中的每个输入，运行幂迭代(power iteration)，整个过程只用「向量乘 Jacobian」和「向量乘 Jacobian 转置」两种运算（都由自动微分完成，因此从不显式构造整个 Jacobian）：对一个随机单位向量反复施加「Jacobian 再转置」并重新归一化，迭代约二十次或直到长度不再变化，得到该输入的最大奇异值。然后取整个批次上这些值的最大值作为 Lc，因为 Lipschitz 常数是一个最坏情形（上确界 supremum）的量；同时报告第 95 百分位作为稳定性检查。编码器的光滑程度决定了有限样本误差的尺度，所以没有它这个界就没有意义。\n   - _为什么_: 编码器的光滑程度决定了有限样本误差的尺度，所以没有它这个界就没有意义。\n\n### 有限样本包络\n*通过 InfoNCE 专用的 Stein 算子证明可认证的到高斯距离界。*\n\n4. 写出球面上的总体 InfoNCE 梯度流，确定它在对齐平台(alignment-plateau)极限下收敛到的分布，并运用定量的 Stein / Berry-Esseen 论证，证明特征分布到其匹配高斯的距离至多为一个「温度平方」小项加上一个随有效负样本数收缩的涨落项。这里用的是定义在「三阶导数有界的检验函数」类上的光滑距离（这正是这类逼近论证的自然设定），而不是原始的全变差(total variation)距离。前面的两个常数不是调出来的：第一个由温度在损失曲面上引起的曲率读出，第二个由 Berry-Esseen 界里剩下的三阶矩项读出——两者都作为显式公式从证明中得到。这一步重新注入了原证明平均掉的有限批量涨落，把无限极限的论断变成可用的有限批量误差范围。\n\n*有限样本包络：InfoNCE 表示分布 $\\mu _{N}$ 与其匹配高斯之间的光滑 IPM 距离被一个 $\\tau ^{2}$ 项加上一个 $Lc/\\surd (N_{eff})$ 项所界定，其中 $N_{eff}$ 是由对齐水平 $\\rho _{align}$ 决定的有效负样本数。*\n$$ d_{\\mathrm{IPM}}\\big(\\mu_N,\\;\\mathcal{N}(0,\\Sigma_T)\\big)\\;\\le\\;c_1\\,\\tau^2\\;+\\;c_2\\,\\frac{L_c}{\\sqrt{N_{\\mathrm{eff}}}},\\qquad N_{\\mathrm{eff}}=(N-1)\\,(1-\\rho_{\\mathrm{align}}) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这重新注入了原证明平均掉的有限批量涨落，把无限极限的论断变成可用的有限批量误差范围。\n\n### 各向异性协方差刻画\n*构建增广条件协方差，推导稳态协方差，并证明各向异性证书。*\n\n5. 对许多留出的锚点图像中的每一张（数量至少为特征维度的十倍，以保证矩阵良态），嵌入该锚点的 K 个增广（默认取 64 个增广，足以得到低方差的逐锚点均值），把它们映射到 第1步（取一批留出的） 得到的切平面上，减去该锚点的均值，再累积这些「增广引起的偏差」的协方差。对所有锚点和增广求平均，得到矩阵 $C_{aug}——$它是切空间坐标下的一个对称半正定矩阵；同时计算它的特征值（从大到小排列）。$C_{aug}$ 刻画了数据增广如何把特征散开——这正是决定椭球形状的关键成分。\n   - _为什么_: $C_{aug}$ 刻画了数据增广如何把特征散开——这正是决定椭球形状的关键成分。\n6. 把对齐的拉力（它沿着增广变化的方向拉伸特征，由 $C_{aug}$ 刻画）与均匀性的各向同性推力相平衡：在收敛的平均方向附近对训练动力学做线性化，求解所得协方差 $Sigma_{T}$。结果正比于「单位矩阵减去（一个依赖温度的权重 $\\beta $ 乘以 $C_{aug}$）」的逆，且完全在 第1步（取一批留出的） 的 $(d- 1)$ 维切平面里计算，因此不需要对庞大的环境空间矩阵求逆。温度权重 $\\beta $ 随温度减小而增大（大致是温度的倒数，所以温度越低椭球被拉得越长）；它的精确取值由力平衡推导给出。把 $Sigma_{T}$ 重新缩放为总方差为 1，使得只有形状重要，并确认它就是 第4步（写出球面上的总体$\\dots $） 中使用的同一个高斯。这一步确定了特征趋近的是「哪一个」高斯，而不仅仅是趋近「某个」高斯，从而补上了缺失的形状。\n\n*稳态切空间协方差 $Sigma_{T}$ 是力平衡不动点：在均值方向切空间上，(I 减去温度加权的增广条件协方差 $C_{aug})$ 的逆。*\n$$ \\Sigma_T\\;\\propto\\;\\big(I-\\beta\\,C_{\\mathrm{aug}}\\big)^{-1}\\big|_{T_{\\bar\\mu}\\mathbb{S}^{d-1}},\\qquad \\beta=\\beta(\\tau) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这确定了特征趋近的是「哪一个」高斯，而不仅仅是趋近「某个」高斯，从而补上了缺失的形状。\n7. 由协方差 $Sigma_{T}$ 证明：它的条件数(condition number，即最大方差方向与最小方差方向之比)至少为「1 加上温度权重 $\\beta $ 乘以 $C_{aug}$ 特征值的展开度」——这里的展开度指 $C_{aug}$ 最大特征值减去最小特征值。证明只需从 $Sigma_{T}$ 的闭式做一步代数。然后检查安全条件：$\\beta $ 乘以 $C_{aug}$ 的最大特征值要小于 1，这保证公式良定（被求逆的矩阵保持正定）；若对实测值不满足，就报告「已超出该界适用的范围」，而不是把公式推到失效之外。条件数大于 1 意味着被拉伸的椭球，所以这把「是圆的还是拉伸的」变成了一个可证明的、有方向的论断。\n\n*各向异性证书：协方差条件数至少为 1 加上温度权重乘以 $C_{aug}$ 的谱隙，因此非零的增广谱隙会强制产生真正的各向异性。*\n$$ \\kappa(\\Sigma_T)\\;\\ge\\;1+\\beta\\,\\lambda_{\\mathrm{gap}}(C_{\\mathrm{aug}}) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 条件数大于 1 意味着被拉伸的椭球，所以这把「是圆的还是拉伸的」变成了一个可证明的、有方向的论断。\n\n### 实证验证\n*在多种编码器以及一个去除增广各向异性的负对照上检验这两个界。*\n\n8. 在 CIFAR-10 和 ImageNet-100 上用两三种编码器规模训练 SimCLR 风格的编码器，批量大小取 128 / 512 / 2048，温度取 0.07 / 0.2 / 0.5。对每个设置，在切平面上测量两件事：(a) 到预测高斯的实际距离，用最大平均差异(Maximum Mean Discrepancy, MMD)——一种标准的双样本距离——来估计，采用高斯钟形核，其宽度设为样本点间距离的中位数（常用默认做法），把真实的切空间坐标与从预测高斯中等量抽取的样本相比较；(b) 经验切空间协方差的实际条件数。然后对每个设置报告：实测距离与预测包络之比（若界成立应保持在 1 或以下），以及实测条件数与预测条件数之间的相对误差。最后运行负对照：把数据增广换成只添加方向中性、强度匹配的小随机噪声（去掉有方向性的裁剪 crop 和颜色变化），这会把增广的展开度推向零；重训后确认实测条件数向 1 坍缩，而正常增广那一组仍把它明显维持在 1 以上。如果这个界和形状预测正确，测得的距离会保持在包络之下，且条件数会保持拉伸——除非在圆形增广对照下，那时它应当向 1 坍缩。\n   - _为什么_: 如果这个界和形状预测正确，测得的距离会保持在包络之下，且 $\\kappa $ 会保持拉伸——除非在圆形增广对照下，那时它应当向 1 坍缩。\n\n"},{"id":"64","run_dir":"run_prompt64_ctxentropy","index":64,"title":"Position-Resolved Intrinsic Entropy: A Separation Criterion for Context-Length Scaling","title_zh":"位置分辨的内在熵：上下文长度缩放的一个可分离性判据","method_name":"Position-Resolved Intrinsic Entropy (PRIE)","hook":"A length-marginalized loss curve provably cannot distinguish two contexts that carry the same total intrinsic entropy but deliver it at different positions, so the field's critical-context-length analyses are blind to WHERE usable information runs out. We show the model's own per-position conditional-entropy field separates them, and that the critical length is a fixed point of that field's cumulative-yield curve computable during training.","anchor_pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","anchor_pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","domain_category":"LLM Pretraining, Architecture & Scaling","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf produces a per-context-position information-yield signal: a quantity, computable from a given model during training, that says how much the model's conditional entropy of the next token actually drops when context position k is added, so that the point where marginal yield vanishes can be located along the context rather than only inferred in hindsight from a length-marginalized loss curve.","pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by naming the structural object the length-marginalized loss curve discards — the per-position marginal entropy-yield Delta-H(k) — formalizing a separation criterion under which two contexts of equal total intrinsic entropy but different delivery position are provably conflated, and re-injecting Delta-H(k) as a first-class cumulative-yield field whose saturation point provably exceeds (strictly refines) the scalar critical length.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf tests whether the rising Approximation-Loss term and the falling Bayes-Risk term must be treated as two independently estimated aggregate curves at all, rather than as one position-resolved field that a single model produces in a forward pass — i.e. no paper questions the shared assumption that the intrinsic-entropy / critical-length analysis has to be a separate post-hoc estimation decoupled from the model's own per-position predictive distribution.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by auditing the load-bearing assumption that the Bayes-Risk floor and Approximation-Loss term must be estimated as two decoupled aggregate curves, and pivoting to a structural condition — both are exact projections (marginalizations over position) of one position-resolved conditional-entropy field a single trained model already emits — then re-deriving the critical length up to a stated saturation-tolerance equivalence class as a recovery theorem on that field.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"long-context language modeling / information-theoretic scaling laws","n_papers":24,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":25},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":10,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Quest: Query-centric Data Synthesis Approach for Long-context Scaling of Large Language Model"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"LongVILA: Scaling Long-Context Visual Language Models for Long Videos"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Training-Free Long-Context Scaling of Large Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Phi-3 Technical Report: A Highly Capable Language Model Locally on Your Phone"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Sequence modeling and design from molecular to genome scale with Evo"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Facilitating topic modeling in tourism research:Comprehensive comparison of new AI technologies"}],"more":4},{"year":2025,"n":29,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Scaling Context, Not Parameters: Training a Compact 7B Language Model for Efficient Long-Context Processing"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"SWAN-GPT: An Efficient and Scalable Approach for Long-Context Language Modeling"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"L2M: Mutual Information Scaling Law for Long-Context Language Modeling"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Critical attention scaling in long-context transformers"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"MoBA: Mixture of Block Attention for Long-Context LLMs"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"From 128K to 4M: Efficient Training of Ultra-Long Context Large Language Models"}],"more":23},{"year":2026,"n":9,"papers":[{"source":"arxiv","title":"Focus-dLLM: Accelerating Long-Context Diffusion LLM Inference via Confidence-Guided Context Focusing"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"A$^2$RD: Agentic Autoregressive Diffusion for Long Video Consistency"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"$π^2$: Structure-Originated Reasoning Data Improves Long-Context Reasoning Ability of Large Language Models"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Gated Sparse Attention: Combining Computational Efficiency with Training Stability for Long-Context Language Models"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"BCER Agent: Reliable Long-Horizon MRI Workflow Execution via Compilation, Artifact Binding, and Bounded Local Recovery"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Difference-Based High-Dimensional Long-Run Covariance Matrix Estimation for Mean-shift Time Series"}],"more":3}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass; algebraic_equivalence_unification","pattern_name":"characterize_limit_then_surpass; algebraic_equivalence_unification","count":2,"share":0.083},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution; heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"architectural_operator_substitution; heterogeneous_decomposition","count":2,"share":0.083},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution; structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"architectural_operator_substitution; structural_prior_encoding","count":2,"share":0.083},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate; adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"decompose_and_delegate; adapt_via_conditioning","count":2,"share":0.083},{"pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass; controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"characterize_limit_then_surpass; controlled_diagnostic_design","count":1,"share":0.042},{"pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass; assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"characterize_limit_then_surpass; assumption_audit_and_pivot","count":1,"share":0.042},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding; assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"structural_prior_encoding; assumption_audit_and_pivot","count":1,"share":0.042},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object; structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"reframe_as_solvable_object; structural_prior_encoding","count":1,"share":0.042}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"The Intrinsic-Entropy decomposition (openalex:W4407174629) splits the long-context loss into a Bayes-Risk floor that falls with context length and an Approximation-Loss term that rises with it, and L2M (semanticscholar:2cf95cfeb7180a3a93a2cd79989090986c1a66bd) shows a bipartite mutual-information scaling law I^BP between text blocks; but both quantities are estimated as a single aggregate curve over a fixed corpus AFTER training, so neither can localize WHERE in the context the rising approximation term is generated nor predict, before or during training, the position at which an additional token stops reducing a given model's conditional entropy. Concretely: once the optimal-model Bayes Risk and the trained-model loss are only available as length-marginalized scalars, there is no per-position information-yield signal that survives across context positions, so the 'critical context length' can be observed in hindsight but cannot be derived from the model's own predictive entropy field during pretraining, and the mechanism coupling the approximation rise to attention behaviour (e.g. the score-entropy dispersion documented in semanticscholar:7a1960b537f1cfde7a292ee7b2c6b158122aa669) is left as an unexplained empirical correlation.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4407174629","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Decomposes long-context total loss into a Bayes-Risk floor (the intrinsic-entropy term, decreasing with context length) plus an Approximation Loss (the optimal-vs-trained gap, increasing with length), yielding a critical context length that minimizes validation loss and grows with dataset size. The decomposition is a static, length-marginalized post-hoc curve: it never resolves the Approximation Loss into a per-context-position quantity, gives no train-time-computable predictor of the critical length from the model's own entropy field, and leaves the mechanism that makes Approximation Loss rise with length (vs. attention/score-entropy dynamics) as an opaque empirical term."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:2cf95cfeb7180a3a93a2cd79989090986c1a66bd","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Defines bipartite mutual information I^BP between an antecedent block X and a successor block Y via H(Y)=H(Y|X)+I^BP and verifies a power-law scaling of I^BP in natural language, arguing models must capture this much long-range dependency. I^BP is an aggregate two-block corpus statistic estimated independently of any particular model; it does not give a per-position information-yield profile along a single context, nor connect to the trained model's realized conditional-entropy reduction, so it predicts how much dependency exists, not where a given model's marginal information gain vanishes."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:7a1960b537f1cfde7a292ee7b2c6b158122aa669","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Identifies that attention-score distributions collapse toward uniformity (rank-collapse / score-entropy blow-up) as context length n grows and proposes a temperature/scaling correction. Treats the collapse purely as an attention-geometry pathology and a quantity to be suppressed, never linking the score-entropy rise to the data-intrinsic conditional-entropy budget of the context, so it cures a symptom without measuring whether the lost discrimination corresponds to genuinely vanishing information."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"long-context language modeling / information-theoretic scaling laws","venue":"ICLR/NeurIPS (ML theory + LLM)","time":"2025-2026","data":["OpenWebText / PG19-style long-document pretraining corpora","natural-language long-context benchmarks (NoLiMa, NIAH-style)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"information theory + transformer language modeling","preference":"both","baseline":"Intrinsic Entropy of Context Length Scaling (Bayes-Risk + Approximation-Loss decomposition); L2M bipartite mutual-information scaling law","limitation":"Existing entropy/MI accounts of context-length scaling are static aggregate curves measured post-hoc on a fixed corpus; they explain that a critical context length exists but give no train-time-predictable, per-position mechanism for the rising approximation term, so they cannot say in advance where added context stops carrying usable information for a given model.","contribution_type":"theory","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared central object (coherence thread = shared_object) is the model's position-resolved conditional-entropy field h_m(k) := H_m(X_{t+1} | X_{t-k+1:t}), the trained model m's predictive entropy of the next token given exactly the most recent k context tokens, averaged over evaluation positions t on a held-out corpus; it is read directly from the model's softmax (a model-internal readout, computed in one forward pass per truncation length k by masking context beyond k), requires no separate estimator, and is defined for k = 1..K. From h_m(k) we define the marginal entropy-yield Delta-H_m(k) := h_m(k-1) - h_m(k) (the drop in next-token uncertainty contributed by adding the k-th most-recent context token) and the cumulative-yield curve G_m(k) := h_m(1) - h_m(k) = sum_{j=2..k} Delta-H_m(j). ANCHOR LEG (C10): the length-marginalized loss L(n) reported by prior work is exactly the position-average of h_m over contexts truncated at n, so two corpora A,B with identical L_A(n)=L_B(n) for all n but different Delta-H profiles (A front-loaded, B back-loaded) are conflated by any marginalized curve; we formalize this as the Separation Criterion: a length-marginalized statistic S is position-blind iff S is invariant under any permutation of {Delta-H_m(k)} that preserves their sum, and we prove the scalar critical length n* of openalex:W4407174629 is such an S, hence cannot separate A from B, whereas the field Delta-H_m(k) does (it is the unique minimal sufficient statistic that is NOT permutation-invariant). We then re-inject Delta-H_m(k) into the analysis by defining the position-resolved critical length k*(epsilon) := min{ k : Delta-H_m(j) < epsilon for all j >= k }, the first position past which every further token yields less than tolerance epsilon of entropy reduction, and prove k*(epsilon) strictly refines n* (n* is recovered as the position-average special case and k*(epsilon) additionally predicts the per-context length at which added tokens stop paying, at O(K) forward-pass cost — bounded, no superquadratic lift). SIBLING LEG (C05): the prior decomposition L(n) = R_Bayes(n) + L_Approx(n) treats the two terms as separately estimated aggregates; we pivot the assumption by proving an identifiability result — given the trained model's field h_m(k) AND an estimate of the optimal-model field h*(k) (the Bayes-risk floor, estimated by the standard entropy-rate extrapolation already used in prior work), R_Bayes(n) = avg_k<=n h*(k) and L_Approx(n) = avg_k<=n (h_m(k) - h*(k)) are exact projections of the single field gap d(k) := h_m(k) - h*(k), so both curves are recovered (up to the saturation-tolerance equivalence class: fields agreeing on G_m up to epsilon give the same k*) from one position-resolved object rather than two decoupled estimations, and the substitute condition (the model emits h_m(k) by construction) is checkable in one forward pass where the prior independence-of-estimation assumption was never verifiable. The two legs share h_m(k) entirely: the anchor builds the separation/refinement on Delta-H_m, the sibling proves the decomposition's two terms are projections of the same field — one object, two theorems.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery because both are statements ABOUT the same object h_m(k): the anchor says the marginalized curve discards its non-permutation-invariant content (a separation/expressivity claim), the sibling says the two prior aggregate terms are projections of it (an identifiability/recovery claim) — evidence they share machinery is that R_Bayes and L_Approx, Delta-H, and n* are all linear functionals of the single field, so no second module is needed. (b) I considered making the sibling a separate empirical attention-entropy study (the deferred gap) but that would require a distinct representational object and staple two papers together; I also considered defining yield via attention scores rather than predictive entropy, but rejected it to avoid regressing onto the attention-geometry node (lineage n5) and the aggregate bipartite-MI node (n3) — see avoided nodes below.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: take 2-3 pretrained open LMs and a held-out long-context corpus, compute h_m(k) and k*(epsilon) for a fixed small epsilon, and construct matched context pairs (front-loaded vs back-loaded information placement) calibrated to share the marginalized loss curve L(n). If the candidate is correct, the per-context predicted critical length k*(epsilon) and the held-out next-token accuracy measured on tokens beyond k* will DIVERGE between the two members of each matched pair (front-loaded pairs saturate earlier, higher post-k* accuracy) even though their L(n) curves and scalar n* coincide — i.e. Spearman correlation between predicted k*(epsilon) and the empirically observed per-context saturation position stays high (> 0.7) while correlation of n* with it is near zero. The named load-bearing variable is the marginal entropy-yield Delta-H_m(k); the negative control position-shuffles Delta-H_m within each context while preserving its sum (leaving n* and L(n) identical), and the prediction is that this control collapses the downstream divergence in per-context next-token accuracy to chance — establishing that the position structure of Delta-H_m, not the total intrinsic entropy, drives the predicted critical-length difference (intervening on Delta-H_m's ordering moves the task-outcome metric, not merely Delta-H_m's own value).","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4407174629","delta":"They decompose length-marginalized loss into a Bayes-Risk floor and an Approximation Loss and report a single scalar critical context length n*; we prove n* is a permutation-invariant (position-blind) statistic of a per-position entropy-yield field Delta-H_m(k), construct contexts it provably conflates, and derive a position-resolved critical length k*(epsilon) that strictly refines it and is computable from the model's own forward pass."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:2cf95cfeb7180a3a93a2cd79989090986c1a66bd","delta":"They define an aggregate two-block corpus statistic I^BP and a power-law over total long-range dependency independent of any model; we define a model-conditioned, position-resolved field h_m(k) read from the model's own predictive entropy and prove the prior decomposition's two terms are its projections, yielding a per-position saturation point I^BP cannot localize."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:7a1960b537f1cfde7a292ee7b2c6b158122aa669","delta":"They diagnose attention-score entropy blow-up as a geometry pathology and apply a temperature correction; we work entirely in the data-side next-token conditional-entropy field (not attention scores) and supply a separation criterion + recovery theorem rather than a score-distribution fix, never reducing the signal to attention geometry."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4407174629","what_step_was_missed":"Their decomposition stops at length-marginalized terms: it never constructs the per-position marginal entropy-yield Delta-H_m(k) and therefore never proves the separation result that the scalar critical length is a sum-preserving-permutation-invariant of that field — the construction of Delta-H_m(k) as a first-class object plus the proof that two equal-total-entropy contexts with different delivery profiles are conflated by n* but separated by k*(epsilon) is the missing step their marginalized analysis cannot produce."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":267,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"No hard floor fires: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict is borderline (no Reject lesson marked candidate_match=yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and the paper_pointed_threat (semanticscholar:67fecb2b) is adjacent-primitive rather than exact-mechanism overlap (its conditional-entropy decay is marginalized; the candidate's separation and recovery theorems require the non-marginalized position-resolved field). recipe_application_check.verdict=applied for both legs, and the single borderline (C10's 'recently-published method may subsume') is resolved by the subsumption_argument, so the load-bearing structural claim stands; advance with the threat differentiation folded into Phase 4 reviewer_concerns.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf produces a per-context-position information-yield signal: a quantity, computable from a given model during training, that says how much the model's conditional entropy of the next token actually drops when context position k is added, so that the point where marginal yield vanishes can be located along the context rather than only inferred in hindsight from a length-marginalized loss curve.","main_pattern":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail when the 'limit' is not a genuine structural blindspot — trivially implied by the model's own assumptions, already surpassed by a published method, or never formalized beyond an informal analogy; the self-check is whether you can exhibit concrete objects the established method conflates, prove no published method separates them, and bound the added cost.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Resting the central claim on an informal analogy (two operators 'both smooth high frequencies') instead of a separation proof leaves the mechanism underspecified and the empirical gain unconvincing.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism states a formal Separation Criterion (any sum-preserving-permutation-invariant statistic is position-blind) and an explicit conflated pair (front-loaded vs back-loaded context with equal L(n)), not an analogy."},{"lesson_quoted":"Applying existing structural descriptors to a new application domain without formalizing a new limit or constructing a new operator yields a domain study, not a methodological contribution, and reviewers find no transferable novelty.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate both formalizes a new limit (the marginalization blindspot) and constructs a new operator (the position-resolved critical length k*(epsilon) on the field Delta-H_m), not a re-application of an existing descriptor."},{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a 'maximally expressive' construction that a recently published method already strictly subsumes turns the surpass-the-limit claim into redundant work.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"A 2026-02 collision hit (semanticscholar:67fecb2b, 'Deriving Neural Scaling Laws...') also uses next-token conditional-entropy decay with context length, so the frontier must be surveyed; but it aggregates that decay into a scaling exponent and never constructs the per-position field, the conflation pair, or the refined critical length, so it does not subsume the separation claim."},{"lesson_quoted":"A novel formalism that cannot generate predictions or demonstrate concrete advantages over existing definitions reads as abstraction for its own sake.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"falsification_prediction makes a concrete, non-obvious prediction (equal L(n) yet divergent per-context k*(epsilon) and post-k* accuracy) with a negative control, a clear advantage over the scalar n* definition."},{"lesson_quoted":"Asserting the 'first efficient implementation' of a long-known algorithm without surveying the landscape invites direct refutation by existing faster implementations and collapses the novelty claim.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The contribution is a separation theorem + recovery theorem, not an efficiency/implementation-first claim; the O(K) forward-pass cost is a tractability bound, not a speed-record claim."},{"lesson_quoted":"Deriving a 'limitation' that is trivially implied by the model's own linearity assumption produces a limit too weak to count as a real blindspot, and the proposed surpass step stays under-validated.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The blindspot (a length-marginalized statistic cannot recover the position-of-delivery of entropy) is a non-trivial sufficiency result with an explicit conflated pair, not a triviality implied by an assumption."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf tests whether the rising Approximation-Loss term and the falling Bayes-Risk term must be treated as two independently estimated aggregate curves at all, rather than as one position-resolved field that a single model produces in a forward pass — i.e. no paper questions the shared assumption that the intrinsic-entropy / critical-length analysis has to be a separate post-hoc estimation decoupled from the model's own per-position predictive distribution.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"C05 papers fail when the pivoted assumption was not genuinely load-bearing, when the identifiability/recovery property is advertised but the proof omits the decisive object or never names the ambiguity class, or when the proven condition is one the algorithm neither enforces nor verifies.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Stacking two established frameworks and re-proving identifiability of the union reads as incremental unless the pivoted assumption was genuinely load-bearing and the union admits a regime neither framework could reach alone.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The pivot does not stack two frameworks; it overturns one load-bearing assumption (that R_Bayes and L_Approx must be separately estimated aggregates) and reaches a new regime (per-context critical length) the prior decomposition could not."},{"lesson_quoted":"Advertising an identifiability or 'consistency' property while the proof omits the decisive object — never proving latent identifiability, or excluding part of the model from the guarantee — collapses the contribution the moment a reviewer checks the theorem.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The decisive object (the single field d(k)=h_m(k)-h*(k)) is named and both prior terms are exhibited as its exact projections, with the saturation-tolerance equivalence class stated explicitly."},{"lesson_quoted":"Imposing structural constraints to claim interpretability or disentanglement without proving those constraints are sufficient for recovery leaves the result indistinguishable from a post-hoc heuristic.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The substitute condition (the model emits h_m(k) by construction) is proven sufficient for recovering both decomposition terms, not asserted as a heuristic."},{"lesson_quoted":"Proving identifiability conditions the algorithm neither enforces nor verifies creates a theory-practice disconnect that undermines both the soundness and the significance of the claim.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The recovery condition is checkable and enforced by construction — h_m(k) is read from one forward pass per truncation length, exactly the quantity the theorem requires, closing the theory-practice gap."},{"lesson_quoted":"Errors in the dependency or conditional-independence bookkeeping (mislabeling an independence, opening a collider) void the central theorem even when the empirical numbers look reasonable.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The recovery is a linear-projection identity (averaging over position) rather than a conditional-independence argument, so collider/independence-bookkeeping hazards do not arise."}],"verdict":"clear"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The anchor entry (characterize_limit_then_surpass / C10) is borderline solely on the 'recently-published method may subsume' lesson, driven by collision hit semanticscholar:67fecb2b which shares the next-token-conditional-entropy-decay primitive; no Reject lesson is marked candidate_match=yes, so no hard floor fires. The sibling C05 entry is clear."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf produces a per-context-position information-yield signal: a quantity, computable from a given model during training, that says how much the model's conditional entropy of the next token actually drops when context position k is added, so that the point where marginal yield vanishes can be located along the context rather than only inferred in hindsight from a length-marginalized loss curve.","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Name the one structural object an iterative/local procedure discards for tractability, formalize the equivalence class this discarding induces as a WL-style separation/indistinguishability criterion on the procedure's native objects, then re-inject that exact object into the core step and prove the augmented operator strictly exceeds the criterion at bounded cost.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism names the discarded object (the per-position marginal entropy-yield Delta-H_m(k) that the length-marginalized loss throws away), formalizes the Separation Criterion as invariance under sum-preserving permutations of {Delta-H_m(k)} and proves n*/L(n) are such position-blind statistics with an explicit conflated pair, then re-injects Delta-H_m(k) as the field defining k*(epsilon) and proves it strictly refines n* at O(K) forward-pass (bounded) cost — the full discard/separation/re-inject/exceed-at-bounded-cost move.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf tests whether the rising Approximation-Loss term and the falling Bayes-Risk term must be treated as two independently estimated aggregate curves at all, rather than as one position-resolved field that a single model produces in a forward pass — i.e. no paper questions the shared assumption that the intrinsic-entropy / critical-length analysis has to be a separate post-hoc estimation decoupled from the model's own per-position predictive distribution.","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Take an existing recovery/identifiability result, pivot the distributional assumption it requires by trading it for a structural/architectural/geometric condition the setting plausibly satisfies, and re-prove recovery of the hidden structure up to a named ambiguity class, operationalized as an estimator.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism pivots the assumption that the Bayes-Risk and Approximation-Loss terms must be separately estimated aggregates, trading it for a structural condition (the model emits the position-resolved field h_m(k) by construction in one forward pass), and re-proves recovery of both terms as exact projections of the single field d(k) up to the named saturation-tolerance equivalence class — the C05 pivot-distributional-for-structural-then-re-prove-recovery move.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries instantiate their cluster's distinctive signature move in core_mechanism: C10's discard/separation-criterion/re-inject/exceed-at-bounded-cost on Delta-H_m, and C05's distributional-to-structural pivot with a named-ambiguity-class recovery theorem on the field d(k)."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["characterize_limit_then_surpass","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"None of the three documented reject-favored compositions matches; all three require heterogeneous_decomposition, which is not in the composition set."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:67fecb2b84f2e51f94868df1e40a9b723edc217b","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"'Deriving Neural Scaling Laws from the statistics of natural language' (2026-02) isolates the decay of next-token conditional entropy with conditioning-context length as one of two statistical properties that predict neural-scaling-law exponents, so it overlaps with the candidate's central quantity (the model/data next-token conditional entropy as a function of context length). The candidate stands or falls on whether its contribution survives that overlap: it does, because that paper consumes the conditional-entropy decay only as a length-marginalized aggregate to predict a single scaling exponent, whereas the candidate's load-bearing results are (i) the Separation Criterion proving that any such length-marginalized statistic is position-blind (it conflates two contexts of equal total intrinsic entropy that differ in delivery position) and (ii) the recovery theorem that the prior Bayes/Approx decomposition terms are projections of one position-resolved field — neither the position-resolved field Delta-H_m(k), the conflation pair, nor the refined per-context critical length k*(epsilon) is constructed in the threat paper, so it is adjacent-primitive, not exact-mechanism, overlap.","addressable_via":"differentiation_from_lit already names the model-conditioned/position-resolved vs aggregate-exponent distinction; Phase 4 should add semanticscholar:67fecb2b explicitly to differentiation_from_lit and state that the threat uses the marginalized decay while the candidate's separation/recovery results require the non-marginalized field."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Position-Resolved Intrinsic Entropy: A Separation Criterion for Context-Length Scaling\n\n**Method.** Position-Resolved Intrinsic Entropy (PRIE)\n\n## Motivation\nLarge language models (LLMs) now read very long inputs, and researchers have noticed that adding more context sometimes helps and sometimes hurts. A recent theory (the Intrinsic Entropy of Context Length Scaling framework) explains this by splitting the model's prediction error at a given context length into two parts: a Bayes Risk, the unavoidable uncertainty an ideal model would still have, which goes DOWN as you give it more context; and an Approximation Loss, the extra error from the real (imperfect) model, which goes UP with length. Their sum can bottom out at a single best 'critical' context length. A parallel theory (L2M) measures, on average, how much long-range dependency text contains. The trouble is that both are single numbers per length, measured after the fact. They can say a critical length exists, but not WHERE inside a particular passage the model stops gaining anything from one more token. Two passages that carry the same total useful information — one front-loaded, one back-loaded — produce the exact same averaged curve and the same critical length, even though the model runs out of useful information at very different points in each. A related attention-side study sees a co-occurring blow-up in attention 'spread' as length grows but treats it as a geometry quirk, never tying it to the actual information in the text. This is timely now because the scalar-critical-length result was only written down in 2025, open long-context LLMs cheaply expose their per-position next-token probabilities, and a 2026 line already uses the decay of next-token conditional entropy with context length — but only in its averaged form, leaving the position-by-position version open. Closing the gap means each passage gets its own train-time-computable cutoff position past which extra tokens provably do not pay, instead of one dataset-wide number; the original decomposition is recovered as a special case, and the averaged mutual-information law gains a localization it cannot currently give.\n\n## Method\n### Field readout\n*Turn the model's own next-token distributions into a per-position conditional-entropy field and its marginal yield.*\n\n1. For each position t and each context length k from 1 to K (K = the model's trained context window), cut the input down to just the most recent k tokens, reset their position numbers to start from the beginning, run one forward pass, take the next-token probability distribution at the last position, and compute its Shannon entropy (a number measuring how spread-out / uncertain the prediction is). Average this over every position t that has a full K-token history to get a field $h_{m}(k):$ one entropy value per context length. Do the truncation by actually shortening the input (re-slicing), not by hiding tokens with an attention mask, so the model sees a genuine length-k input the same way the earlier loss-vs-length measurement did.\n\n*The position-resolved conditional-entropy field: the trained model m's next-token entropy given exactly the most recent k context tokens, averaged over evaluation positions t.*\n$$ h_m(k) := \\mathbb{E}_{t}\\,H\\!\\left(X_{t+1}\\mid X_{t-k+1:t}\\right) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This turns the single averaged loss-vs-length curve into a per-position signal the model already produces, with no extra model to train.\n2. Subtract neighboring values of the field to get the marginal yield $Delta-H_{m}(k) = h_{m}(k-1) - h_{m}(k),$ which is how much uncertainty the k-th most-recent token removed, and add these up to get the running total $G_{m}(k) = h_{m}(1) - h_{m}(k).$ These are just differences and running sums of the numbers from the previous step; no fitting or estimation is involved.\n\n*The marginal entropy-yield (drop in next-token uncertainty from adding the k-th most-recent token) and the cumulative-yield curve.*\n$$ \\Delta H_m(k) := h_m(k-1) - h_m(k), \\qquad G_m(k) := h_m(1) - h_m(k) = \\sum_{j=2}^{k} \\Delta H_m(j) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The position-by-position drops are exactly what the averaged curve throws away, and they are what the whole argument hinges on.\n\n### Separation theorem\n*Prove the averaged loss and scalar critical length are position-blind and exhibit the contexts they conflate.*\n\n3. Prove that any quantity which stays the same when you reshuffle the marginal-yield values without changing their total is 'position-blind', and show the averaged loss and the scalar critical length are exactly such quantities. Then build a concrete pair of passages the model cannot tell apart on those quantities but which differ in where information sits: make each passage out of independent information-carrying chunks with a chosen profile of per-chunk uncertainty-drops, and let the 'back-loaded' passage use the reversed order of the SAME set of drops as the 'front-loaded' one — so their totals (and thus the averaged loss and the scalar critical length) match exactly while the point where yield runs out differs. A practical way to make these is copy / induction sequences where a key token's predictability is placed at a chosen distance, tuned by measuring the actual per-position drop on the model.\n\n*Separation Criterion: a statistic S is position-blind exactly when it is invariant under all sum-preserving permutations of the marginal-yield sequence; L(n) and n* satisfy this and so conflate equal-total-entropy contexts.*\n$$ S\\big(\\{\\Delta H_m(k)\\}\\big) = S\\big(\\{\\Delta H_m(\\pi(k))\\}\\big)\\;\\;\\forall \\pi\\!:\\!\\textstyle\\sum_k \\Delta H_m(k)\\ \\text{fixed} \\;\\Longleftrightarrow\\; S\\ \\text{is position-blind} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This is the formal proof — not an analogy — that the existing critical-length number is blind to where information sits.\n\n### Per-context critical length\n*Re-inject the field as a strictly finer, bounded-cost per-context cutoff k*(epsilon).*\n\n4. Define k*(epsilon) as the first context position after which every further token's marginal yield stays below a small threshold epsilon, and prove this per-context critical length strictly refines the old single scalar critical length (and reproduces that scalar when you average over contexts), at a cost of only K forward passes. Set the threshold relative to the field's own size — epsilon $= c \\times  (h_{m}(1) -  h_{m}(K)) /$ K, with c a small fraction (default 0.05, meaning a token only counts as 'still paying' if it removes at least 5% of the average per-position yield) — and report k*(epsilon) across c values of 0.01, 0.05 and 0.1 so the saturation point is shown to be stable rather than tuned to one threshold.\n\n*The position-resolved critical length: the first position past which every further token yields less than tolerance epsilon of entropy reduction; it strictly refines the scalar n*.*\n$$ k^{*}(\\varepsilon) := \\min\\{\\,k : \\Delta H_m(j) < \\varepsilon \\ \\ \\forall j \\geq k\\,\\} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: It gives a sharper, per-passage cutoff at modest cost and still recovers the old number as an average.\n\n### Recovery theorem\n*Show the prior Bayes-Risk and Approximation-Loss terms are projections of one field gap.*\n\n5. Estimate the ideal-model floor h*(k) — the lowest next-token uncertainty an optimal predictor could reach — by fitting the loss-versus-length curve to the same shrinking curve shape the earlier decomposition work used (a curve that falls toward a flat floor as length grows), fitting its parameters by least squares, and converting that fitted aggregate into a per-length floor whose average matches the earlier Bayes-Risk term. 【author decision: the floor can mean either the same model's own extrapolated best-case (its irreducible entropy rate) or a floor measured from a much larger reference model; the later recovery result works for either, but the authors must pick which one the earlier decomposition intends.】\n   - _Why_: Reusing their estimator means the new result does not sneak in a fresh unverifiable assumption.\n6. Form the gap d(k) $= h_{m}(k) - $ h*(k) between the model's field and the ideal floor, and prove that the earlier Bayes-Risk and Approximation-Loss curves are simply the running position-averages of h*(k) and of d(k) respectively — so both come from one field rather than two separately estimated curves, up to the same tolerance band from the previous step (fields that agree on the cumulative yield within epsilon give the same critical length).\n\n*Recovery theorem: the prior Bayes-Risk and Approximation-Loss terms are exact position-averages of one field gap d(k), so both come from a single model's field rather than two decoupled estimations.*\n$$ R_{\\mathrm{Bayes}}(n) = \\tfrac{1}{n}\\!\\sum_{k\\leq n} h^{*}(k), \\quad L_{\\mathrm{Approx}}(n) = \\tfrac{1}{n}\\!\\sum_{k\\leq n} \\big(h_m(k)-h^{*}(k)\\big),\\quad d(k):=h_m(k)-h^{*}(k) \\tag{5} $$\n\n   - _Why_: It shows the two curves never needed to be estimated separately — they are two views of a single object the model emits.\n\n### Empirical separation\n*Validate the divergence on real models and collapse it with a sum-preserving position-shuffle control.*\n\n7. On 2-3 open large language models (LLMs) chosen to span a size range (one 1-3B and one 7-8B model from the same open-weight family, so they share a tokenizer and training data), build the front-loaded / back-loaded passage pair from the separation step and check that the averaged loss is identical while the per-context critical length k*(epsilon) and the accuracy on tokens past k* differ. Score that post-k* accuracy as how often the model's top guess for the next token is correct, measured only at positions whose available context is longer than k*, averaged per passage; use a held-out corpus of naturally long documents that the models were not trained on, cut to length K. Then shuffle the order of the marginal-yield values within each passage while keeping their total the same — which leaves the averaged loss and the scalar critical length unchanged — and confirm the accuracy difference disappears down to chance. 【author decision: pick the exact open-weight model series and the held-out long-document corpus, constrained only by open weights, a context window of at least K, and that the corpus is genuinely held out.】\n   - _Why_: The shuffle control proves it is the position structure, not the total information, that drives the effect — and it shows up in actual next-token accuracy.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 位置分辨的内在熵：上下文长度缩放的一个可分离性判据\n\n**方法名称.** Position-Resolved Intrinsic Entropy (PRIE)\n\n## 研究动机\n大语言模型（LLM）现在能读非常长的输入，研究者发现增加上下文有时有帮助、有时反而有害。一个近期理论（Intrinsic Entropy of Context Length Scaling 框架）这样解释：把模型在某个上下文长度下的预测误差拆成两部分——Bayes Risk，即理想模型也无法消除的不确定性，它随上下文增多而下降；以及 Approximation Loss，即真实（不完美）模型带来的额外误差，它随长度增加而上升。两者之和会在某个最优的「临界」上下文长度处取到最低点。另一条理论（L2M）则平均地衡量文本中包含多少长程依赖。问题在于：这两者都是每个长度一个数字、而且是事后测出来的。它们能说明临界长度存在，却说不出在某一段具体文本中，模型到底在哪个位置开始不再从多读一个 token 中获益。两段携带相同总有用信息的文本——一段信息靠前、一段靠后——会产生完全相同的平均曲线和相同的临界长度，尽管模型在两段中耗尽有用信息的位置截然不同。相关的注意力侧研究观察到随长度增长注意力「弥散」会爆炸，但只把它当作几何怪象，从未把它与文本中真实信息联系起来。现在正当其时：标量临界长度的结果 2025 年才写出来，开源长上下文 LLM 能廉价地暴露其逐位置的下一 token 概率，且 2026 年已有工作用到下一 token 条件熵随上下文长度的衰减——但只用了它的平均形式，逐位置版本仍然敞开。补上这个缺口意味着每一段文本都能得到一个训练期即可计算的截断位置，越过它额外 token 可证明不再有收益，而不是整个数据集一个数字；原有的分解作为特例被恢复，平均的互信息定律也获得了它当前给不出的定位能力。\n\n## 方法\n### 场读出\n*把模型自身的下一 token 分布转成逐位置条件熵场及其边际收益。*\n\n1. 对每个位置 t 和每个上下文长度 k(从 1 到 K，K 取模型训练时的上下文窗口长度)，把输入裁到只剩最近的 k 个 token，并把它们的位置编号(position id)重置为从头开始，跑一次前向，取最后一个位置上下一 token 的概率分布，算它的香农熵(Shannon entropy，衡量预测有多分散、多不确定的一个数)。对每个拥有完整 K 个 token 历史的位置 t 取平均，得到场 $h_{m}(k)——$每个上下文长度对应一个熵值。裁剪要用真正缩短输入(重新切片)的方式，而不是用注意力掩码(attention mask)把 token 遮住,这样模型看到的是一个真正长度为 k 的输入,和先前 loss-长度测量的方式一致。\n\n*位置分辨的条件熵场：训练后模型 m 在仅给定最近 k 个上下文 token 时下一 token 的条件熵，对评估位置 t 取平均。*\n$$ h_m(k) := \\mathbb{E}_{t}\\,H\\!\\left(X_{t+1}\\mid X_{t-k+1:t}\\right) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这把单一的平均 loss-长度曲线变成模型本来就会产生的逐位置信号，且不需要再训练任何模型。\n2. 把上一步得到的场相邻值相减,得到边际收益 $Delta-H_{m}(k) = h_{m}(k-1) - h_{m}(k),$它表示第 k 个最近的 token 消除了多少不确定性;再把这些累加,得到累计量 $G_{m}(k) = h_{m}(1) - h_{m}(k)$。这些只是对上一步那些数做差分和前缀求和,不涉及任何拟合或估计。\n\n*边际熵收益（加入第 k 个最近 token 所带来的下一 token 不确定性下降）以及累积收益曲线。*\n$$ \\Delta H_m(k) := h_m(k-1) - h_m(k), \\qquad G_m(k) := h_m(1) - h_m(k) = \\sum_{j=2}^{k} \\Delta H_m(j) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 逐位置的下降正是平均曲线丢掉的东西，而整个论证都依赖它们。\n\n### 可分离性定理\n*证明平均 loss 与标量临界长度是位置盲的，并给出它们混淆的上下文。*\n\n3. 证明任何在「保持总和不变地重排边际收益值」下不变的量都是「位置盲」的,并说明平均 loss 与标量临界长度恰是这类量。然后构造一对在这些量上模型无法区分、但信息位置不同的文本:把每段文本由若干独立的信息块拼成,每块带有事先设定的不确定性下降量;让「信息靠后」的文本采用与「信息靠前」文本完全相同的下降量集合、但顺序颠倒——于是两者的总和(以及平均 loss 和标量临界长度)完全一致,而收益耗尽的位置却不同。一个可行的构造方式是用复制/归纳(copy/induction)序列,把某个关键 token 的可预测性放在选定的距离上,并通过在真实模型上测量逐位置下降量来校准。\n\n*可分离性判据：当且仅当统计量 S 在所有保和置换下不变时它才是位置盲的；L(n) 与 n* 满足此条件，因而会混淆总熵相同的上下文。*\n$$ S\\big(\\{\\Delta H_m(k)\\}\\big) = S\\big(\\{\\Delta H_m(\\pi(k))\\}\\big)\\;\\;\\forall \\pi\\!:\\!\\textstyle\\sum_k \\Delta H_m(k)\\ \\text{fixed} \\;\\Longleftrightarrow\\; S\\ \\text{is position-blind} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这是形式化证明——而非类比——表明现有临界长度数值对信息所在位置是盲的。\n\n### 逐上下文临界长度\n*把场重新注入为更精细、代价受限的逐上下文截断 k*(epsilon)。*\n\n4. 把 k*(epsilon) 定义为「此后每个 token 的边际收益都低于小阈值 epsilon」的首个上下文位置,并证明这个逐上下文的临界长度严格细化旧的单一标量临界长度(且对上下文取平均时能还原出那个标量),代价仅为 K 次前向。阈值要相对于场自身的规模来设——epsilon $= c \\times  (h_{m}(1) -  h_{m}(K)) /$ K,其中 c 是一个小比例(默认 0.05,意思是一个 token 只有在消除了至少 5% 的平均逐位置收益时才算「仍在付出回报」)——并在 c 取 0.01、0.05、0.1 时分别报告 k*(epsilon),以表明饱和点是稳定的而非针对单一阈值调出来的。\n\n*位置分辨的临界长度：在该位置之后每个 token 带来的熵下降都小于容差 epsilon；它严格细化标量 n*。*\n$$ k^{*}(\\varepsilon) := \\min\\{\\,k : \\Delta H_m(j) < \\varepsilon \\ \\ \\forall j \\geq k\\,\\} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 它以适度代价给出更精细的逐文本截断，同时把旧数值作为平均特例恢复。\n\n### 恢复定理\n*证明先前的 Bayes-Risk 与 Approximation-Loss 两项是同一个场差的投影。*\n\n5. 估计理想模型下界 h*(k)——也就是一个最优预测器能达到的最低下一 token 不确定性——做法是把 loss-长度曲线拟合到先前分解工作所用的同一种递减曲线形状(随长度增长向一个平台下界衰减的曲线),用最小二乘拟合参数,再把这个拟合出的整体量转换成逐位置的下界,使其平均值与先前的 Bayes-Risk 项吻合。【author decision: 这个下界可以理解为同一模型自身外推出的最优极限(它不可约的熵率 entropy rate),也可以理解为从一个大得多的参照模型测得的下界;后面的恢复定理对两种理解都成立,但作者必须确定先前分解究竟指哪一种。】\n   - _为什么_: 沿用他们的估计器，意味着新结果不会偷偷引入一个新的无法验证的假设。\n6. 构造模型的场与理想下界之间的差 d(k) $= h_{m}(k) - $ h*(k),并证明先前的 Bayes-Risk 与 Approximation-Loss 曲线分别只是 h*(k) 和 d(k) 的逐位置滑动平均——因此两者都来自同一个场,而不是两条分开估计的曲线,且在上一步同样的容差带内成立(在 epsilon 内对累计收益一致的场会给出相同的临界长度)。\n\n*恢复定理：先前的 Bayes-Risk 与 Approximation-Loss 两项都是同一个场差 d(k) 的位置平均，因此两者源自单一模型的场，而非两次解耦估计。*\n$$ R_{\\mathrm{Bayes}}(n) = \\tfrac{1}{n}\\!\\sum_{k\\leq n} h^{*}(k), \\quad L_{\\mathrm{Approx}}(n) = \\tfrac{1}{n}\\!\\sum_{k\\leq n} \\big(h_m(k)-h^{*}(k)\\big),\\quad d(k):=h_m(k)-h^{*}(k) \\tag{5} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这说明那两条曲线本无需分别估计——它们是模型所产生的同一对象的两种视角。\n\n### 实证分离\n*在真实模型上验证分离，并用保和的位置打乱对照使其消失。*\n\n7. 在 2-3 个开源大语言模型(Large Language Model, LLM)上验证,这些模型要覆盖一个规模区间(同一开源权重系列里的一个 1-3B 和一个 7-8B 模型,以便共用分词器和训练数据):用分离步骤构造的「信息靠前/靠后」文本对,检验平均 loss 相同、而逐上下文临界长度 k*(epsilon) 与 k* 之后 token 的准确率不同。这里 k* 之后的准确率按「模型对下一 token 的最高概率猜测是否正确」来打分,只在可用上下文长于 k* 的位置上测量,并按文本取平均;语料用模型未曾训练过的、自然长的文档,截成长度 K。然后在保持总和不变的前提下打乱每个文本内边际收益值的顺序——这会让平均 loss 和标量临界长度保持不变——并确认准确率差异消失、回落到随机水平。【author decision: 选定具体的开源权重模型系列和留出的长文档语料,唯一约束是权重开源、上下文窗口至少为 K、且语料确为留出集。】\n   - _为什么_: 打乱对照证明驱动效应的是位置结构而非总信息量——而且它体现在真实的下一 token 准确率上。\n\n"},{"id":"65","run_dir":"run_prompt65_einx","index":65,"title":"Certified einx: shape-universal equivalence certificates for tensor-notation lowering","title_zh":"Certified einx：面向张量记法 lowering 的形状通用等价性证书","method_name":"Certified einx (CEX)","hook":"We show the einx-to-backend lowering question that practitioners answer today by spot-checking a few concrete tensors is, for the whole rearrange/reduce/dot notation, a decidable equivalence over a Presburger-definable index algebra — so a single proof obligation certifies semantic preservation across all admissible ranks and shapes at once, including the contraction fragment that the closest formal calculus leaves as opaque hand-declared landmarks.","anchor_pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","anchor_pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","domain_category":"Learning Theory & Statistics","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a shape-universal correctness certificate that survives every admissible rank/shape instantiation of a written einx expression: existing guarantees are either per-concrete-tensor (spot-checking) or per-rewrite-rule in a separate IR DSL, so the outcome 'this notation's meaning is preserved by its lowering for all shapes at once' is achieved by no leaf.","pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by characterizing the exact structural object the per-concrete-tensor / per-IR-rewrite procedures discard (the rank-polymorphic axis-index map as a symbolic Presburger relation over named-axis size variables) and re-injecting it as a single shape-universal proof obligation whose discharge IS the machine-checkable certificate the method emits.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf closes the reduction/contraction fragment with the same decidable, automatable rigor it gives the structural fragment: the closest calculus (arxiv:2605.31485v1) makes reshapes/permutes decidable but treats every reduction/dot as an opaque landmark needing a hand-declared rule, so the part of einx that actually contracts axes is left without an automatic equivalence procedure.","pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by formalizing the structural/pointwise fragment as the exact decidability boundary the prior calculus stops at, then constructing an augmented decision procedure that lifts contractions into a Presburger-with-bounded-summation normal form (sum-of-monomials over disjoint index supports), proven to decide equivalence over the reduction fragment under stated semiring-commutativity conditions at polynomial-in-expression-size cost.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"tensor-program notation / verified tensor compilation (ML systems)","n_papers":51,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":27},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":19,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"The Fault Diagnosis Method of On-Load Tap Changers Based on Phase Space Tensor Decomposition and Deep Learning Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"TPU Based Deep Learning Image Enhancement for Real-Time Point-of-Care Ultrasound"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"An introduction to graphical tensor notation for mechanistic interpretability"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"TeMCO: Tensor Memory Compiler Optimization across Tensor Decompositions in Deep Learning Inference"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Tensor-Empowered Hardware-Friendly Lightweight Deep Neural Networks for Vehicular Edge Computing"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Quantum Computing for High-Energy Physics: State of the Art and Challenges"}],"more":13},{"year":2025,"n":23,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Checkflow: Low-Overhead Checkpointing for Deep Learning Training"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Accelerating Deep-Learning Applications with Efficient Tensor Layout Management"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Accelerating Sparse Deep Learning via Multi-Layer Tensor Reordering and Partitioning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Tensor-Empowered Hardware-Friendly Lightweight Deep Neural Networks for Vehicular Edge Computing"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Luthier: Bridging Auto-Tuning and Vendor Libraries for Efficient Deep Learning Inference"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Co-Evolving Traffic State Parameters Prediction Based on Mechanism-Data Blending Driven Deep Learning"}],"more":17},{"year":2026,"n":8,"papers":[{"source":"arxiv","title":"Monodense Deep Neural Model for Determining Item Price Elasticity"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Convex Dominance in Deep Learning I: A Scaling Law of Loss and Learning Rate"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Deep Delta Learning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"TCL: Enabling Fast and Efficient Cross-Hardware Tensor Program Optimization via Continual Learning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Low-Power On-Device Gesture Recognition with Einsum Networks"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Mambalaya: Einsum-Based Fusion Optimizations on State-Space Models"}],"more":2}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"algebraic_equivalence_unification; structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"algebraic_equivalence_unification; structural_prior_encoding","count":2,"share":0.039},{"pattern_id":"algebraic_equivalence_unification; characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"algebraic_equivalence_unification; characterize_limit_then_surpass","count":2,"share":0.039},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate; reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"decompose_and_delegate; reframe_as_solvable_object","count":2,"share":0.039},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition; architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"heterogeneous_decomposition; architectural_operator_substitution","count":2,"share":0.039},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation; algebraic_equivalence_unification","pattern_name":"unify_into_shared_representation; algebraic_equivalence_unification","count":1,"share":0.02},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object; algebraic_equivalence_unification","pattern_name":"reframe_as_solvable_object; algebraic_equivalence_unification","count":1,"share":0.02},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design; algebraic_equivalence_unification","pattern_name":"controlled_diagnostic_design; algebraic_equivalence_unification","count":1,"share":0.02},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding; reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"structural_prior_encoding; reframe_as_solvable_object","count":1,"share":0.02}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"einx-style universal axis notation lets a practitioner write a single rank-polymorphic expression (e.g. a rearrange/reduce/dot over named axes) that the library then lowers to a concrete vectorized backend program; but no current machinery certifies that this lowering preserves the notation's denotational meaning for every admissible shape and rank instantiation, so a mis-lowering (a swapped axis order, an off-by-one broadcast, a reduction over the wrong group) is detectable only by spot-checking concrete tensors. The two closest formal efforts each verify one level removed from the surface notation: TensorRight (openalex:W4406221679) proves graph-rewrite rules sound for arbitrary rank but operates on a separate compiler-IR DSL whose connection to the notation a user actually wrote is itself unverified, and Graphical einops (arxiv:2605.31485v1) gives a decidable proof calculus but only for the structural/pointwise SIMD fragment, treating contractions and reductions as opaque landmarks crossable only by hand-declared rules and never tied to an executing einx program. The failure is therefore that the equivalence between a written einx expression and the backend program it compiles to is, at the rank-polymorphic level, an unfalsified claim: the notation's promise of a single meaning across all shapes has no shape-universal certificate.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2605.31485v1","is_anchor":"true","summary_and_residue":"Graphical einops gives einops-level diagrams a graphical proof calculus where axis reshapes/broadcasts/permutes become typed proof terms and structural equality is decidable via a single naturality rewrite. Its residue: decidability holds only inside the pointwise SIMD (structural) fragment, contractions/reductions are opaque tube-in-tube-out landmarks crossable only through hand-declared rules, and the calculus proves identities between two notations by hand rather than certifying that a running einx program's lowering matches the notation's denotation, so the surface-notation-to-executable-lowering gap is untouched."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4406221679","is_anchor":"false","summary_and_residue":"TensorRight verifies a tensor-graph rewrite rule sound for tensors of arbitrary rank by inferring a sufficient rank bound per aggregated axis and discharging the bounded cases as SMT queries. Its residue: it verifies rewrites stated in its own Haskell/Grisette DSL over compiler-IR operators, so the soundness it proves is for the IR rewrite, not for the user-facing axis notation, and nothing certifies that the IR a notation lowers to is the IR the rewrite was proved against."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4399850917","is_anchor":"false","summary_and_residue":"A Verified Compiler for a Functional Tensor Language (ATL) verifies reshape operators that decouple compute order from storage order inside ATL's own combinator set. Its residue: the verified equivalences are internal to ATL combinators and never lifted to a universal named-axis notation, so rank-polymorphic einsum/rearrange semantics are out of scope and a shape-universal certificate for them does not exist. [residue partly abstract-level: ATL fulltext unfetchable]"}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"tensor-program notation / verified tensor compilation (ML systems)","venue":"ICLR / PACMPL-adjacent ML-systems track","time":"2026","data":["einx/einops expression corpora (rearrange/reduce/dot/vmap expressions)","tensor-compiler rewrite-rule suites (XLA-HLO, TorchInductor) for differential testing"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (approx 90 A100-day)","expertise":"tensor compilers, programming-language semantics, ML systems","preference":"both","baseline":"einx library lowering to vectorized ops; TensorRight (rewrite-rule SMT verification); Graphical einops (structural-fragment proof calculus)","limitation":"einx provides a universal notation that lowers tensor expressions to vectorized backend ops, but ships no machine-checkable guarantee that a given einx expression (and the rearrangements/reductions it implies) is semantically equivalent to its lowering across all admissible shapes; existing verification sits one level away from the surface notation.","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["domain","venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object both legs read from and write to is the SYMBOLIC AXIS-INDEX SEMANTICS of an einx expression: a denotation that maps each output position to a (finite) symbolic sum-of-products over input positions, where every index is an affine/Presburger term in named-axis SIZE VARIABLES (e.g. b, h, q, k) rather than in concrete integers. Concretely, for a written expression E (a rearrange/reduce/dot string plus its axis-name bindings), we compile a READ-MAP rho(E): each output multi-index i is bound to a Presburger-definable set of contributing input multi-indices, and each contribution carries a base pointwise op tag (identity for rearrange/broadcast; the reduction semiring (+, *) for reduce/dot). The library lowering L(E) is independently compiled to a second read-map rho(L(E)) by interpreting the emitted backend program (the actual vectorized op sequence einx produces) under the same denotational semantics. LEG 1 (anchor, C10): the structural object that per-concrete-tensor spot-checking and IR-level rewrite verification both discard is exactly this rank-polymorphic read-map kept SYMBOLIC in the size variables; we characterize the limit (a per-shape check can only ever witness finitely many instantiations, an IR-rewrite verifier proves rho over the IR not over the surface E) and surpass it by emitting ONE proof obligation rho(E) === rho(L(E)) as a Presburger equivalence quantified over all size-variable assignments satisfying the expression's shape constraints; discharging it with an off-the-shelf Presburger/SMT decision procedure (the well-studied solvable object whose machinery we reuse) yields a certificate valid for every admissible rank and shape simultaneously — and a counter-model when the lowering is wrong, naming the exact axis/shape where meaning diverges. LEG 2 (sibling, C10, SAME object): the structural fragment (reshape/broadcast/permute) is precisely the sub-case where every read-map contribution is identity-tagged, so equivalence is pure index-set equality and decidable by plain Presburger — this is the boundary the prior calculus reaches; the reduction/contraction fragment adds summation over a contracted axis, so we extend the normal form to Presburger-with-bounded-summation: a dot/reduce becomes a sum of monomials whose index supports are disjoint Presburger sets, and equivalence of two such forms is decided by matching monomial supports after a canonical reindexing, which we prove terminating and complete under semiring commutativity/associativity (the stated precondition) and the einx constraint that contracted axes are existentially named and never aliased. The two legs need no separate machinery: they are the identity-tagged and summation-tagged cases of the single read-map decision procedure, which is why the paper reads as one certificate for the whole notation rather than two. The weight bridging the two fragments is a single declared parameter K = max contraction depth (number of nested reductions in E), which bounds the summation nesting and hence the decision-procedure degree; K is read directly off the parsed expression, not tuned.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"We decided the two gaps SHARE machinery because the reduction fragment is literally the same read-map object with a non-identity op tag — building a separate module for reductions would duplicate the Presburger compilation, and the only honest delta is the normal-form extension, so one decision procedure with two tag cases is the faithful structure. We considered an alternative design that recasts equivalence as an SMT query over CONCRETE bounded ranks (the TensorRight move: infer a rank bound, instantiate, discharge) but rejected it because it proves the property only up to the inferred bound and still verifies the IR rewrite rather than the surface notation, so it would regress onto the n3 lineage node (IR-DSL SMT verifier); keeping the read-map symbolic in size variables and quantifying over all assignments is what draws on the tree's unoccupied source (the notation's own axis algebra as a decidable object) instead. We also avoided the parametric c0 node (dependent shape types), which proves well-shapedness not value-equivalence, by making the obligation a value-level read-map identity, not a shape-type judgment.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: take the einx expression corpus (its rearrange/reduce/dot test suite plus mined real-model expressions from public repos) and, for each expression, run the decision procedure to emit PROVED/counter-model, alongside a brute-force differential oracle that executes the einx lowering vs a reference denotation on a battery of random admissible shapes. If the candidate works, the named metric CERTIFICATION SOUNDNESS (fraction of PROVED expressions that the differential oracle never falsifies on any sampled shape) stays at 1.0 while CERTIFICATION COMPLETENESS (fraction of truly-equivalent expressions the procedure can PROVE) rises sharply ABOVE the structural-fragment-only baseline once the reduction-fragment extension is enabled — the non-obvious directional claim is that completeness jumps specifically on the contraction-heavy expressions (einsum/dot, attention) that the prior calculus could only handle via hand-declared rules. The single named load-bearing variable is K, the max contraction depth used to bound the summation normal form. Negative-control intervention: cap K at 0 (disable the reduction-fragment normal form, falling back to identity-tagged Presburger only) — the downstream task-outcome metric, COMPLETENESS on contraction-heavy expressions, must collapse toward the structural-only baseline (many true equivalences become UNPROVABLE), while SOUNDNESS stays 1.0; if completeness does NOT drop when K is zeroed, the reduction normal form is not doing the work and the mechanism claim is false. Positive control: a stripped procedure using ONLY the read-map + Presburger core (no library-specific heuristics) should already recover most of the certification completeness, showing the decidability reframe — not engineering around it — carries the result.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2605.31485v1","delta":"Graphical einops proves structural-fragment identities (equivariance, naturality) by hand-derived diagrammatic rewrites and treats every contraction/reduction as an opaque landmark needing a declared rule; we construct a DECISION PROCEDURE that decides equivalence over the reduction fragment automatically via a Presburger-with-bounded-summation normal form, and tie the certificate to the actual library lowering rather than to a hand-drawn diagram."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4406221679","delta":"TensorRight verifies a rewrite rule stated in its own Haskell/Grisette IR DSL by inferring a concrete rank bound and discharging the bounded cases; we verify the SURFACE einx expression against its emitted lowering with the size variables kept symbolic and quantified over ALL admissible assignments (no rank bound, no separate DSL), so the trusted base is the notation itself, not an IR re-encoding."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4399850917","delta":"The ATL verified compiler certifies reshape combinators internal to ATL's own language; we certify a UNIVERSAL named-axis notation's rearrange/reduce/dot lowering, producing a per-expression re-checkable certificate rather than a once-and-for-all compiler-correctness proof scoped to one combinator set."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4403223181","delta":"PolyJuice finds mis-compilation bugs by sampling semantically-equivalent graphs and comparing outputs (testing, no all-shapes guarantee); we return a shape-UNIVERSAL certificate or an exact counter-model naming the divergent axis, replacing sampled-shape testing with a decision over all shapes."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"arxiv:2605.31485v1","what_step_was_missed":"Graphical einops formalizes the structural fragment as a decidable graphical calculus but stops at the structural/pointwise boundary, leaving contractions as opaque landmarks crossable only by hand-declared rules; for our contribution to already exist it would have needed to construct a normal form that lifts a reduction/dot into a decidable Presburger-with-bounded-summation object and prove equivalence over that summation fragment is decidable under semiring-commutativity — the summation-fragment decision construction it never builds — and to tie the obligation to the running einx lowering rather than to hand-drawn diagrams."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":114,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"No hard floor fires: gap_closure_reject_check is borderline (no Reject lesson marked candidate_match: yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat (arxiv:2605.31485v1) is adjacent not exact-mechanism overlap. recipe_application_check.verdict = applied (both legs perform C10's discard-formalize-reinject-at-bounded-cost move), and the single borderline (C10's relational-procedure framing stretched to a proof calculus) sits in a non-load-bearing presentational aspect rather than the core argument, so per the default-to-advance heuristic the candidate advances with the framing concern surfaced for Phase 4.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a shape-universal correctness certificate that survives every admissible rank/shape instantiation of a written einx expression: existing guarantees are either per-concrete-tensor (spot-checking) or per-rewrite-rule in a separate IR DSL, so the outcome 'this notation's meaning is preserved by its lowering for all shapes at once' is achieved by no leaf.","main_pattern":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail when the 'limit' they characterize is not a genuine structural blindspot (trivially implied by the model's own assumptions, already surpassed, or never formalized beyond an informal analogy), or they construct the operator and assert superiority without surveying the frontier so a stronger method subsumes the gain.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Resting the central claim on an informal analogy (two operators 'both smooth high frequencies') instead of a separation proof leaves the mechanism underspecified and the empirical gain unconvincing.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The limit is formalized concretely: a per-shape check witnesses only finitely many size-variable instantiations and an IR-rewrite verifier proves the property over the IR not the surface expression — a precise separation, not an analogy."},{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a 'maximally expressive' construction that a recently published method already strictly subsumes turns the surpass-the-limit claim into redundant work.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The closest published method (Graphical einops) explicitly scopes to the structural fragment and leaves contractions as hand-declared landmarks, so the reduction-fragment decision procedure is not subsumed by it; the collision set contains no paper deciding einx reduction-fragment equivalence."},{"lesson_quoted":"Applying existing structural descriptors to a new application domain without formalizing a new limit or constructing a new operator yields a domain study, not a methodological contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate formalizes a new limit (the structural/pointwise decidability boundary) AND constructs a new operator (the Presburger-with-bounded-summation decision procedure) that provably crosses it, not a port of an existing descriptor."},{"lesson_quoted":"Asserting the 'first efficient implementation' of a long-known algorithm without surveying the landscape invites direct refutation by existing faster implementations and collapses the novelty claim.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The claim is decidability + a re-checkable certificate tied to the library lowering, not an efficiency-first claim over a known algorithm; differentiation_from_lit surveys TensorRight, ATL, PolyJuice, and Graphical einops."},{"lesson_quoted":"Deriving a 'limitation' that is trivially implied by the model's own linearity assumption produces a limit too weak to count as a real blindspot.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Undecidability-by-hand-declaration of the reduction fragment is not implied by the structural calculus's own assumptions; the candidate shows reductions ARE decidable under semiring commutativity, refuting the tacit assumption rather than restating it."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf closes the reduction/contraction fragment with the same decidable, automatable rigor it gives the structural fragment: the closest calculus (arxiv:2605.31485v1) makes reshapes/permutes decidable but treats every reduction/dot as an opaque landmark needing a hand-declared rule, so the part of einx that actually contracts axes is left without an automatic equivalence procedure.","main_pattern":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail when the limit is not a genuine blindspot or is asserted without surveying the frontier; a third shape ports a formalism to a new domain but never demonstrates it captures an invariant the incumbent provably misses, producing abstraction with no testable advantage.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Resting the central claim on an informal analogy instead of a separation proof leaves the mechanism underspecified.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The boundary is exhibited as the exact case split (identity-tagged contributions = pure Presburger index-set equality; summation-tagged contributions = the fragment the prior calculus cannot decide automatically), a concrete separation."},{"lesson_quoted":"A novel formalism that cannot generate predictions or demonstrate concrete advantages over existing definitions reads as abstraction for its own sake.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"falsification_prediction gives a concrete, measurable advantage: certification completeness on contraction-heavy expressions jumps above the structural-only baseline, with K as the load-bearing distinguisher."},{"lesson_quoted":"Applying existing structural descriptors to a new application domain without formalizing a new limit or constructing a new operator yields a domain study.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"C10's canonical incumbent is an iterative-local relational procedure (GNN/complex/persistence); here the incumbent is a proof calculus, so the cluster's relational-object framing is stretched — but a new limit IS formalized and a new decision procedure IS constructed, so it is not a bare domain study."},{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a 'maximally expressive' construction that a recently published method already strictly subsumes turns the surpass claim into redundant work.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"No collision-set or lit_table paper decides the einx reduction fragment; Graphical einops explicitly leaves it to hand-declared rules."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The sibling reduction-fragment leg (characterize_limit_then_surpass / C10) is borderline on the lesson 'applying existing structural descriptors to a new application domain' because C10's tactical pattern is framed around iterative-local relational procedures (graphs/complexes) while the incumbent here is a proof calculus; no Reject lesson is marked candidate_match: yes, so the aggregate is borderline not triggered, and a new limit + new decision procedure are genuinely constructed."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a shape-universal correctness certificate that survives every admissible rank/shape instantiation of a written einx expression: existing guarantees are either per-concrete-tensor (spot-checking) or per-rewrite-rule in a separate IR DSL, so the outcome 'this notation's meaning is preserved by its lowering for all shapes at once' is achieved by no leaf.","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Take an iterative/locally-scoped procedure, pinpoint the one structural object it discards for tractability, formalize the equivalence class this discarding induces as a separation criterion on the procedure's native objects, then re-inject that exact object into the procedure's core step and prove the augmented operator strictly exceeds the criterion at bounded cost.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism LEG 1 names the discarded object (the rank-polymorphic axis-index read-map kept symbolic in the size variables, which per-concrete-tensor checking and IR-rewrite verification both throw away), formalizes the separation (finite instantiations vs all-assignments; IR-level vs surface-level), and re-injects it as the single all-assignments Presburger proof obligation rho(E)===rho(L(E)) whose discharge is the certificate — the signature discard/formalize/re-inject move is present.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf closes the reduction/contraction fragment with the same decidable, automatable rigor it gives the structural fragment: the closest calculus (arxiv:2605.31485v1) makes reshapes/permutes decidable but treats every reduction/dot as an opaque landmark needing a hand-declared rule, so the part of einx that actually contracts axes is left without an automatic equivalence procedure.","sub_pattern":"C10 (Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Formalize the blindspot as a precise separation criterion on the procedure's native target objects, re-inject the discarded object into the core step as first-class structure, and bound the added cost to linear/polynomial so the gain avoids the superquadratic lift the field treats as the only route upward.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism LEG 2 names the discarded object (summation over a contracted axis, the case the structural calculus leaves as an opaque landmark), re-injects it via the Presburger-with-bounded-summation normal form (sum-of-monomials over disjoint index supports) as first-class structure in the decision procedure, and bounds cost by K = max contraction depth — the bounded-cost re-injection move is present.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both legs perform C10's discard-formalize-reinject-at-bounded-cost signature move (symbolic read-map for the anchor, bounded-summation normal form for the sibling), instantiated on einx expressions as the native objects rather than enacting only the parent's generic 'characterize a limit' gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["characterize_limit_then_surpass","characterize_limit_then_surpass"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"The composition set is a single pattern (characterize_limit_then_surpass) and contains no heterogeneous_decomposition, so none of the three documented reject-favored compositions matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"arxiv:2605.31485v1","threat_source":"lit_table","subsumption_argument":"Graphical einops is the structurally closest paper: it gives einops-level structural-fragment identities a decidable graphical proof calculus, so a reviewer could ask whether it already 'solves' the certification problem. It does not subsume the candidate: it explicitly scopes decidability to the structural/pointwise SIMD fragment and treats every contraction/reduction as an opaque tube-in-tube-out landmark crossable only by hand-declared rules, and it proves identities BETWEEN two hand-drawn diagrams rather than certifying a running einx program's lowering against its denotation. The candidate's two differentiating constructions — a decision procedure for the reduction/contraction fragment, and an all-assignments obligation tied to the actual library lowering producing a re-checkable certificate or a counter-model — are exactly the steps Graphical einops never builds, so the overlap is adjacent, not exact-mechanism.","addressable_via":"Already addressed in differentiation_from_lit and what_step_was_missed; Phase 4 should keep the contrast (reduction-fragment decision procedure + lowering-tied certificate vs structural-fragment hand-derived diagrams) explicit in reviewer_concerns_and_responses."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Certified einx: Shape-Universal Equivalence Certificates for Tensor-Notation Lowering\n\n**Method.** Certified einx (CEX)\n\n## Motivation\nTools like einx (a universal notation for tensor operations) let you write one short expression — rearrange these axes, sum over that one, contract these two — and the library automatically turns it into the actual array code that runs on your hardware, for any tensor shape. The catch: nobody checks that the generated code really computes what your expression means for every possible shape. If the library swaps two axes or broadcasts off by one, you only find out by running a few concrete examples and eyeballing the numbers — which tests only a handful of the infinitely many shapes your expression is supposed to cover.\n\nThe closest existing work stops one step short. TensorRight (a 2025 programming-languages paper) can prove rewrites correct for any rank, but it works on the compiler's internal representation written in a separate language, not on the notation you actually wrote. Graphical einops (a 2026 paper) gives a clean, automatic way to prove identities — but only for the 'structural' moves (reshape, broadcast, permute); it treats every sum or contraction as a black box you must justify by hand. So the very part of the notation that adds things up — the part most likely to be silently mis-translated — has no automatic, all-shapes correctness check, and whatever guarantee exists is attached to an internal representation, not to your expression.\n\nThis is solvable now because Graphical einops just proved the structural part is decidable (showing it can be done and where it stops), and modern SMT solvers (Satisfiability Modulo Theories, automated logic engines) can reason about symbolic index arithmetic. We keep each axis's size as a symbolic variable instead of a concrete number, so a single logical question covers all shapes at once.\n\nWhen this gap closes, einx's promise of 'one meaning for all shapes' becomes something you can actually verify: you either get a re-checkable certificate that your expression and its generated code agree for every admissible shape, or an exact failing example naming the offending axis. This replaces shape-by-shape spot-checking and hands the structural-only proof calculus the contraction-fragment decision procedure it was missing.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n\n1. Parse the einx string together with its axis names into a typed tree of operation kinds (rearrange / reduce / dot / broadcast / vmap), reusing einx's own expression parser so the tree matches what the library will actually run. Give each distinct named axis its own symbolic size variable (an integer unknown constrained to be at least 1), and expand grouped or ellipsis axes into their individual axis labels so each one gets exactly one size variable.\n   - _Why_: Keeping sizes symbolic is what lets one check cover every shape instead of one concrete example.\n\n### Symbolic read-map compilation\n*Turns both the einx expression and its real lowering into symbolic axis-index maps that range over all shapes.*\n\n2. Build the notation's read-map: walk the tree with one rule per operation kind, and for each output position write down, as a logical (Presburger arithmetic) formula in the size variables, the set of input positions that feed it. Plain index-moving operations (rearrange, broadcast, vmap) give a one-to-one or projection formula tagged as a plain copy; reduce and dot give a formula that ranges over a whole summed-out axis, tagged with the combining operation (sum or mean use addition, max-reduce uses maximum, dot uses add-and-multiply). Keep a side table noting, for every contribution, whether it is a plain copy or a reduction.\n\n*The read-map of expression E sends each output multi-index $i_{out}$ to the set of contributing input multi-indices $j_{in}$ carved out by a Presburger predicate $\\Phi _{E}$ over the size-variable vector s.*\n$$ \\rho(E)\\;:\\; \\mathbf{i}_{\\mathrm{out}} \\;\\longmapsto\\; \\bigl\\{\\, \\mathbf{j}_{\\mathrm{in}} \\in \\mathbb{Z}^{r} \\;\\big|\\; \\Phi_E(\\mathbf{i}_{\\mathrm{out}}, \\mathbf{j}_{\\mathrm{in}}; \\mathbf{s}) \\,\\bigr\\} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This is the precise mathematical meaning of what you wrote, in a form a solver can reason about for all shapes.\n3. Run einx's actual lowering of the same expression to get the ordered sequence of low-level backend operations it emits (reshape, transpose, broadcast, einsum, and sum/max/mean reductions), capturing them through a recording layer that works regardless of which numeric backend is used. Then feed those operations through the very same read-map builder from the previous step, in the order they are emitted, to produce a second read-map. Using the identical builder for both sides is deliberate, so that any mismatch found later reflects a real difference in the lowering rather than an artifact of two different interpreters.\n   - _Why_: Comparing against the real generated code (not an idealized model) is what makes the certificate trustworthy for what actually runs.\n\n### All-shapes decision procedure\n*Forms and discharges one Presburger obligation, with a bounded-summation normal form that makes the contraction fragment decidable.*\n\n4. Form one logical obligation that must hold for every shape the expression allows. First build the shape-constraint set: each axis size is at least 1, any axis name appearing in two or more places must be equal across them, and any axis pinned to a concrete number is fixed to that number. The obligation then states: for every size assignment meeting these constraints, the two read-maps are equal. For purely structural (plain-copy) expressions this is direct index-set equality and goes straight to the solver; expressions containing reductions first pass their reduction parts through the normalization step.\n\n*The single proof obligation: for every size-variable assignment s satisfying E's shape constraints C(E), the read-map of E equals the read-map of its lowering L(E); discharging it yields the shape-universal certificate.*\n$$ \\Phi \\;:=\\; \\forall\\, \\mathbf{s} \\in \\mathcal{C}(E).\\;\\; \\rho(E)(\\mathbf{s}) \\;\\equiv\\; \\rho(L(E))(\\mathbf{s}) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A single 'for all shapes' statement replaces testing shape after shape.\n5. For any contraction (a dot or reduce), rewrite it as a sum of terms whose index ranges do not overlap, with nesting no deeper than K, the deepest contraction in the expression read straight off the tree. Then put each side into a canonical form: order the kept output axes by their output position and the summed-out axes by first appearance, rename the summed indices to standard positional names, and sort the terms by a fixed key built from their axis labels and combining operation. The combining operation's algebraic laws (sum and mean are commutative and associative; max is commutative, associative, and idempotent) are taken from a small lookup table per operation. Two contractions are equal exactly when, after this relabeling and sorting, their term lists match one-to-one as index-range formulas.\n\n*The reduction-fragment normal form: a contraction is a sum of M monomials, each a semiring product of at most K factors over contracted indices $k_{m},$ with pairwise-disjoint index supports so equivalence reduces to monomial-support matching.*\n$$ \\rho_{\\mathrm{red}}(E)(\\mathbf{i}_{\\mathrm{out}}) \\;=\\; \\sum_{m=1}^{M} \\;\\bigotimes_{d=1}^{K} \\; t_{m,d}\\!\\bigl(\\mathbf{i}_{\\mathrm{out}}, \\mathbf{k}_{m}; \\mathbf{s}\\bigr), \\qquad \\mathrm{supp}(m) \\cap \\mathrm{supp}(m') = \\varnothing \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This turns sums — the black-box part of prior calculi — into something the solver can decide automatically.\n6. Hand the plain-copy part of the obligation straight to an SMT solver (Z3, in its integer-arithmetic mode). Handle the reduction part with the term-matching pass from the previous step, which turns checking two summations for equality into a finite list of smaller index-range equality checks (each also sent to Z3) plus the relabeling witness; this matching pass is needed because the solver on its own does not decide summation equality. If everything proves, save a re-checkable certificate: the expression, the captured lowering operations, the proved formula in standard solver text format, the per-reduction relabeling, and the solver version, all of which an independent checker can re-run. If any check fails, read the solver's counter-example, turn it into a concrete shape, and report that shape together with the specific axis where the two sides disagree.\n   - _Why_: You get either a portable guarantee or a precise bug report, before running any real tensor.\n\n### Differential validation\n*Empirically confirms certificates are sound and counter-models are real via random-shape execution.*\n\n7. Cross-check with a differential test harness over many random shapes. For each expression, sample shapes by drawing every axis size independently from 1 to 8 (always including the boundary sizes 1 and 2, which expose broadcast and singleton edge cases) while respecting the equality constraints, using 100 sampled shapes per expression by default. For each shape, fill the inputs with fixed-seed random tensors, run both the original einx expression and the captured lowering, and count them as agreeing when the largest elementwise difference is at most 1e-5 in 32-bit floating point. Require every certified expression to agree on all sampled shapes, and confirm every reported counter-example truly diverges at its named shape and axis. The overall agreement rates become the soundness and completeness measurements.\n   - _Why_: It empirically confirms the certificates are sound and the counter-examples are real.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# Certified einx：面向张量记法 lowering 的形状通用等价性证书\n\n**方法名称.** Certified einx (CEX)\n\n## 研究动机\n像 einx（一种张量操作的通用记法）这样的工具，让你只写一行简短表达式——把这些轴重排、对那个轴求和、把这两个轴做 contraction——库就会自动把它翻译成在你硬件上真正运行的数组代码，而且对任意张量形状都成立。问题在于：没有人检验生成的代码对每一种可能的形状都确实计算了你表达式的本意。如果库把两个轴交换了，或者 broadcast 偏了一位，你只能靠跑几个具体例子、用眼睛核对数字才会发现——而这只覆盖了你表达式本应支持的无穷多形状中的极少数。\n\n最接近的已有工作都停在了前一步。TensorRight（2025 年的一篇编程语言论文）能对任意 rank 证明 rewrite 正确，但它作用在编译器内部表示（用另一种语言写成）上，而不是你真正写下的那行记法。Graphical einops（2026 年的论文）给出了一种干净、自动证明恒等式的方法——但只针对『结构性』操作（reshape、broadcast、permute）；它把每个求和或 contraction 都当作必须手工论证的黑箱。于是记法中真正做累加的那部分——也是最容易被悄悄翻译错的部分——没有自动的、覆盖所有形状的正确性检查，而仅有的保证还附着在内部表示上，而非你的表达式上。\n\n现在可以解决，是因为 Graphical einops 刚证明了结构片段是可判定的（既说明了可行性，也点明了它止步于何处），而现代 SMT（Satisfiability Modulo Theories，自动化逻辑求解器）能对符号化的索引算术进行推理。我们把每个轴的尺寸保留为符号变量而非具体数字，于是单个逻辑问题就能一次性覆盖所有形状。\n\n一旦补上这个缺口，einx『一种含义覆盖所有形状』的承诺就变得真正可验证：你要么得到一份可复检的证书，证明你的表达式与其生成代码对每个合法形状都一致；要么得到一个精确的反例，指出出错的具体轴。这取代了逐形状的抽查，并把结构片段证明演算所缺的 contraction 片段判定过程补齐。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景\n\n1. 用 einx 自带的表达式解析器(einx.expr)把 einx 字符串及其轴名解析成按操作类型(rearrange / reduce / dot / broadcast / vmap)组织的类型化树，复用库自身的解析器是为了让这棵树与库真正执行时的结构一致。为每个不同的命名轴引入一个符号化的尺寸变量(一个整数未知量，约束为至少为 1)，并把分组轴和省略号轴展开成各自的轴标签，使每个轴标签恰好对应一个尺寸变量。\n   - _为什么_: 把尺寸保留为符号，才能让一次检查覆盖所有形状而非单个具体例子。\n\n### 符号化 read-map 编译\n*把 einx 表达式及其真实 lowering 都转成覆盖所有形状的符号化轴索引映射。*\n\n2. 构建记法的 read-map：用每种操作类型一条规则的方式遍历这棵树，对每个输出位置，用尺寸变量上的逻辑公式(Presburger 算术公式)写出喂给它的输入位置集合。纯粹搬移索引的操作(rearrange、broadcast、vmap)给出一对一或投影式的公式，标注为纯拷贝(structural)；reduce 和 dot 给出在被求和轴整个范围上取值的公式，并标注其合并运算(求和 sum/mean 用加法，max-reduce 用取最大值，dot 用先乘后加)。再维护一张附表，记录每个贡献是纯拷贝还是 reduction。\n\n*表达式 E 的 read-map 把每个输出多重索引 $i_{out}$ 映射到由 Presburger 谓词 $\\Phi _{E}$（在尺寸变量向量 s 上）刻画的贡献输入索引 $j_{in}$ 集合。*\n$$ \\rho(E)\\;:\\; \\mathbf{i}_{\\mathrm{out}} \\;\\longmapsto\\; \\bigl\\{\\, \\mathbf{j}_{\\mathrm{in}} \\in \\mathbb{Z}^{r} \\;\\big|\\; \\Phi_E(\\mathbf{i}_{\\mathrm{out}}, \\mathbf{j}_{\\mathrm{in}}; \\mathbf{s}) \\,\\bigr\\} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这是你所写表达式的精确数学含义，且是求解器能对所有形状进行推理的形式。\n3. 对同一表达式运行 einx 真实的 lowering，得到它发出的有序底层后端操作序列(reshape、transpose、broadcast、einsum 以及 sum/max/mean 等 reduction)，并通过一个与具体数值后端无关的记录层来捕获这些操作。然后把这些操作按发出顺序送入上一步那个完全相同的 read-map 构建器，得到第二个 read-map。两侧刻意使用同一个构建器，这样之后若发现不一致，反映的就是 lowering 的真实差异，而不是两个不同解释器造成的假象。\n   - _为什么_: 与真正生成的代码（而非理想化模型）比较，才能让证书对实际运行的程序可信。\n\n### 全形状判定过程\n*构造并证明单个 Presburger 义务，借助 bounded-summation 范式使 contraction 片段可判定。*\n\n4. 构造一个对表达式允许的每种形状都必须成立的逻辑义务。先建立形状约束集合：每个轴的尺寸至少为 1；任何在两处及以上出现的轴名在各处必须相等；任何被固定为具体数字的轴就钉死为该数字。该义务随即声明：对满足这些约束的每个尺寸赋值，两个 read-map 相等。对纯 structural(纯拷贝)的表达式，这就是直接的索引集合相等，可径直送入求解器；含 reduction 的表达式则先把其 reduction 部分送入归一化步骤。\n\n*唯一的证明义务：对每个满足 E 的形状约束 C(E) 的尺寸变量赋值 s，E 的 read-map 与其 lowering L(E) 的 read-map 相等；证明该义务即得到形状通用证书。*\n$$ \\Phi \\;:=\\; \\forall\\, \\mathbf{s} \\in \\mathcal{C}(E).\\;\\; \\rho(E)(\\mathbf{s}) \\;\\equiv\\; \\rho(L(E))(\\mathbf{s}) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 一句『对所有形状』的陈述取代了逐形状测试。\n5. 对任意 contraction(一个 dot 或 reduce)，将其改写为索引范围互不重叠的若干项之和，嵌套深度不超过 K——表达式中最深的 contraction，直接从树上读出。然后把每一侧化为规范形式：被保留的输出轴按其输出位置排序，被求和掉的轴按首次出现排序，把求和索引重命名为标准的位置名，再用由轴标签和合并运算构成的固定键对各项排序。合并运算的代数律(sum 与 mean 满足交换律和结合律；max 满足交换律、结合律且幂等)从每种运算的一张小查找表中读取。两个 contraction 相等，当且仅当经过这种重标号和排序后，它们的项列表作为索引范围公式逐项一一匹配。\n\n*reduction 片段的范式：一个 contraction 写成 M 个单项式之和，每个单项式是在收缩索引 $k_{m}$ 上至多 K 个因子的半环乘积，且各单项式索引支撑两两不交，于是等价性归约为单项式支撑的匹配。*\n$$ \\rho_{\\mathrm{red}}(E)(\\mathbf{i}_{\\mathrm{out}}) \\;=\\; \\sum_{m=1}^{M} \\;\\bigotimes_{d=1}^{K} \\; t_{m,d}\\!\\bigl(\\mathbf{i}_{\\mathrm{out}}, \\mathbf{k}_{m}; \\mathbf{s}\\bigr), \\qquad \\mathrm{supp}(m) \\cap \\mathrm{supp}(m') = \\varnothing \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这把求和——先前演算中的黑箱部分——变成求解器可自动判定的对象。\n6. 把纯拷贝部分的义务直接交给 SMT 求解器(Z3，使用其整数算术模式)。reduction 部分用上一步的项匹配过程处理：它把检验两个求和是否相等，转化为一组更小的索引范围相等检验(每个也送给 Z3)，再加上重标号见证；之所以需要这个匹配过程，是因为求解器本身并不判定求和相等。若全部得证，就保存一份可复检的证书：表达式、捕获到的 lowering 操作、用求解器标准文本格式表示的被证公式、每个 reduction 的重标号、以及求解器版本，独立的检查器都能据此重新复核。若任一检验失败，读出求解器的反例，将其转化为一个具体形状，并连同两侧不一致的具体轴一起报告。\n   - _为什么_: 你要么得到可移植的保证，要么得到精确的 bug 报告，且都在跑任何真实张量之前。\n\n### Differential 验证\n*通过随机形状执行，从经验上确认证书 sound、反例真实。*\n\n7. 用一个覆盖大量随机形状的 differential 测试台交叉验证。对每个表达式，在满足相等约束的前提下，让每个轴的尺寸从 1 到 8 中独立取值来采样形状(并始终包含边界尺寸 1 和 2，它们能暴露 broadcast 与单元素轴的边界情形)，默认每个表达式采样 100 个形状。对每个形状，用固定随机种子的张量填充输入，同时运行原始 einx 表达式和捕获到的 lowering，当两者逐元素最大差值在 32 位浮点下不超过 1e-5 时记为一致。要求每个被证明的表达式在所有采样形状上都一致，并确认每个报告的反例确实在所指形状与轴处发散。整体的一致率即作为 soundness 与 completeness 的度量。\n   - _为什么_: 它从经验上确认证书是 sound 的、反例是真实的。\n\n"},{"id":"66","run_dir":"run_prompt66_particlewm","index":66,"title":"Per-Particle Stochasticity: Interaction-Gated Latent Noise for Object-Centric World Models","title_zh":"面向校准的对象中心世界模型的交互门控逐粒子随机性 (Interaction-Gated Per-Particle Stochasticity)","method_name":"Interaction-Gated Per-Particle Stochasticity (IG-PPS)","hook":"On multi-object video where two objects branch independently at the same step, a single scene-global latent action (as in LPWM) forces their futures to share one noise draw, so the per-object marginal future distribution it predicts is provably mis-calibrated — its negative log-likelihood and calibration error degrade monotonically as the number of independently-branching objects grows, while a transition that draws one latent per particle gated by a learned interaction mask stays calibrated. The surprise: relocating where noise enters, not adding capacity, is what fixes calibration — a same-capacity global-noise control does not close the gap.","anchor_pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","anchor_pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","domain_category":"Robotics & Embodied Agents","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved object-centric world-model leaf produces a next-state predictive distribution in which each object's marginal future uncertainty is individually calibrated AND only physically-interacting objects are correlated in the joint — every leaf either shares one global noise source across the whole scene (LPWM, Dyn-O) or is deterministic given conditioning (TextOCVP), so independent or mutually-exclusive per-object futures cannot be represented without entangling or averaging them.","pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","sub_pattern":"C24 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"closed by reframing the transition's conditioning/sampling interface as the free variable: replace the single scene-global latent draw injected once per step with one latent drawn per particle, routed through a learned interaction-gating mask so the joint couples only interacting particles, leaving the particle encoder/decoder backbone fixed.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides a self-supervised, label-free training signal that certifies the LEARNED transition noise is at the correct granularity — i.e. that establishes (rather than assumes) whether scene-global stochasticity is sufficient, or whether per-object / interaction-conditioned stochasticity is necessary, leaving the granularity of the noise an untested modeling choice rather than a measured property of the data.","pattern_id":"targeted_self_supervised_objective","pattern_name":"Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective","sub_pattern":"C17 (Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"closed by a label-free branch-consistency objective whose pairing geometry contrasts a particle's predicted next-state samples against its OBSERVED future across temporally-aligned views, so the only way to minimize the loss is to open per-particle noise exactly when the data shows that particle taking divergent futures and to keep it near-zero otherwise — making noise granularity a measured property, not an assumed choice.","is_anchor":false},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions whether transition stochasticity must enter at a single fixed point in the generative process at all; every leaf inherits from the shared sequential-latent-VAE ancestor the unexamined assumption that one sampling site per step is where uncertainty is injected, and none tests whether the site/granularity of stochasticity should itself be determined by the scene's object/interaction structure.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","how_closed":"framing half (C05): audit the inherited single-sampling-site precondition and pivot it — the structural object/interaction separability already present in the particle representation, not a scene-global distributional latent, is what carries the identifying information for the per-object future, so the sampling site must be a function of object structure; companion half (controlled_diagnostic_design): ship the confound-isolating empirical separation — under matched particle-count, capacity and compute, global-latent vs per-particle-gated noise are compared on procedurally generated branching-vs-non-branching scenes, isolating mis-calibration to the noise locus rather than to model size or data.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"self-supervised object-centric stochastic dynamics modeling (object-centric world models for video prediction and decision-making)","n_papers":49,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":26},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":15,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"VISA: Reasoning Video Object Segmentation via Large Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Temporally Consistent Object-Centric Learning by Contrasting Slots"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Reasoning-Enhanced Object-Centric Learning for Videos"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Efficient Object-centric Representation Learning with Pre-trained Geometric Prior"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"4Real: Towards Photorealistic 4D Scene Generation via Video Diffusion Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"ALGO: Object-Grounded Visual Commonsense Reasoning for Open-World Egocentric Action Recognition"}],"more":9},{"year":2025,"n":25,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Object-Centric World Model for Language-Guided Manipulation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Learning Object-Centric Representations Based on Slots in Real World Scenarios"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"GenFlowRL: Shaping Rewards with Generative Object-Centric Flow in Visual Reinforcement Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Video Event Reasoning and Prediction by Fusing World Knowledge from LLMs with Vision Foundation Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Slot-BERT: Self-supervised Object Discovery in Surgical Video"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Online 3D Scene Reconstruction Using Neural Object Priors"}],"more":19},{"year":2026,"n":9,"papers":[{"source":"arxiv","title":"GEM-4D: Geometry-Enhanced Video World Models for Robot Manipulation"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Out of Sight but Not Out of Mind: Hybrid Memory for Dynamic Video World Models"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Causal Physics Steering in Video World Models via Concept Activation Vectors"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Olaf-World: Orienting Latent Actions for Video World Modeling"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Nano World Models: A Minimalist Implementation of Future Video Prediction"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Latent Particle World Models: Self-supervised Object-centric Stochastic Dynamics Modeling"}],"more":3}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding; adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"structural_prior_encoding; adapt_via_conditioning","count":3,"share":0.061},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":3,"share":0.061},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":3,"share":0.061},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding; heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"structural_prior_encoding; heterogeneous_decomposition","count":2,"share":0.041},{"pattern_id":"targeted_self_supervised_objective; self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"targeted_self_supervised_objective; self_supervised_signal_engineering","count":2,"share":0.041},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":2,"share":0.041},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning; reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"adapt_via_conditioning; reframe_as_solvable_object","count":2,"share":0.041},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":2,"share":0.041}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Self-supervised object-centric world models that scale to real multi-object video (LPWM, arxiv:2603.04553v1; Dyn-O, openalex:W4415162380; Object-Centric WM for Language-Guided Manipulation, semanticscholar:82cd021b...488a) inject all transition stochasticity through a single global latent variable shared across every object (in LPWM a per-frame latent action sampled by the Context module and broadcast to all particles in one Dynamics module), or model the transition deterministically (TextOCVP, openalex:W4407719491; Temporally Consistent Slot Contrast, semanticscholar:9c918128...3ed7). Because one scalar/vector of noise is shared by the whole scene, the model cannot represent the case where two objects have independent, mutually-exclusive future branches at the same time-step (object A may go left or right while object B independently stops or continues): a single global noise source forces these branches to be entangled, so the predicted next-state distribution either collapses to a blurred mean of the joint futures or commits the whole scene to one consistent global mode, and the per-object marginal uncertainty becomes mis-calibrated. The current machinery cannot produce a factorized predictive distribution whose per-object marginals are individually calibrated while their joint correctly couples only the interacting objects, because the noise enters at the wrong granularity (scene-global) rather than at the object/interaction granularity where the branching physically originates.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2603.04553v1","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"LPWM is a self-supervised particle-VAE world model that discovers keypoints/masks and predicts future particle states via a Dynamics module conditioned on a single per-frame latent action sampled by a Context module (KL-regularized as a VAE). Its stochasticity is a single global latent broadcast to all particles, so it does NOT model per-object factorized uncertainty, interaction-conditioned branching, or calibrated multi-future marginals — independent or mutually-exclusive object-level futures collapse into one shared global mode."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415162380","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Dyn-O builds structured object-centric world models and pushes them toward visually complex scenes, but its transition is largely a (near-)deterministic per-object predictor; it does not represent a calibrated distribution over mutually-exclusive per-object futures, so stochastic branching at the object level is left open."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4407719491","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"TextOCVP forecasts future slots with a text-conditioned transformer predictor that is deterministic given the conditioning; it has no mechanism for sampling diverse, per-object-factorized futures, so multi-future stochastic dynamics over objects is unaddressed."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2603.04715v1","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Probabilistic Dreaming adds probabilistic latents to Dreamer so it can maintain distinct hypotheses for mutually-exclusive futures, but it operates on a single scene-level (monolithic) latent state, not on object-factorized particles; the multi-hypothesis machinery is not factorized over interacting objects."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"self-supervised object-centric stochastic dynamics modeling (object-centric world models for video prediction and decision-making)","venue":"ICLR / NeurIPS (top ML)","time":"2026","data":["real-world multi-object video (manipulation, driving-like, robotics)","synthetic object-centric video (e.g. CLEVRER-style, OBJ3D, physical-interaction datasets)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (approx 90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with cloud access; familiar with VAEs, slot/particle representations, latent dynamics","preference":"empirical","baseline":"Latent Particle World Models (LPWM, arxiv:2603.04553v1) and object-centric world models such as Dyn-O (openalex:W4415162380), Object-Centric WM for Language-Guided Manipulation (semanticscholar:82cd021b...488a), TextOCVP (openalex:W4407719491)","limitation":"current object-centric world models represent transition stochasticity through a single global latent (or a deterministic transition), so they cannot express per-object, mutually-exclusive futures with calibrated uncertainty","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","compute","expertise","preference","data"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared central object (coherence thread = shared_object) is the per-step transition stochasticity distribution over the particle set: in LPWM this is a single latent action a_t in R^d sampled by the Context module K_psi from the encoded history and broadcast to every foreground particle z_fg^{m,t} (m=0..M-1) inside one Dynamics module F_xi (arxiv:2603.04553v1). Anchor leg (C24): we keep the LPWM particle Encoder/Decoder/VAE backbone and reconstruction loss exactly as-is and redesign ONLY this interface. We replace a_t with a set {u_t^m}_{m=0}^{M-1}, one latent u_t^m in R^{d_p} per particle, each sampled from a per-particle posterior q(u_t^m | z_fg^{m,t}, h_t) (h_t = the existing context readout), and we introduce a learned symmetric interaction gate G_t in [0,1]^{M x M}, G_t[m,n] = sigmoid( MLP_psi([z_fg^{m,t}, z_fg^{n,t}, ||p^m - p^n||]) / tau ), where p^m is the particle's keypoint position (already produced by DLP), tau is a fixed temperature hyperparameter (default 0.5), and MLP_psi is a 2-layer network. The next-state particle is F_xi( z_fg^{m,t}, sum_n G_t[m,n] * (z_fg^{n,t}) , u_t^m ) so a particle's transition is conditioned on its OWN noise plus a gate-weighted message from particles it interacts with; the joint next-state distribution therefore factorizes into per-particle marginals that are coupled only through nonzero gate entries, which is exactly the calibrated-marginals-with-interaction-only-coupling artifact the anchor gap demands. Self-supervised leg (C17): the per-particle KL alone does not force the noise to OPEN only when the data branches; we add a branch-consistency objective L_bc that, for each particle, draws S samples of u_t^m, decodes the S predicted next particle states, and contrasts them against the particle's observed next state z_fg^{m,t+1} using a property-sensitive similarity (negative squared latent distance) — the pairing geometry makes the unique minimizer a posterior whose spread matches the observed empirical spread of that particle's realized futures across temporally-aligned re-encodings of the same clip, so per-particle noise variance tracks measured per-particle branching and collapses toward zero for deterministic particles. Audit leg (C05 + controlled_diagnostic_design companion): the inherited assumption is that one sampling site per step suffices; we pivot it by showing the identifying signal for per-object futures lives in the structural separability of the particle set (a different KIND of constraint than a scene-global distributional latent), and the companion ships the empirical separation — a procedural generator that emits scenes with a controllable number k of independently-branching objects, holding M, capacity, and compute fixed, so any calibration gap between global-latent and per-particle-gated transitions is attributable to the noise locus alone. The three legs share the single object: the anchor relocates the noise, the SSL leg certifies its granularity is data-driven, and the audit leg establishes the relocation is necessary rather than cosmetic.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The three gaps share machinery because they all read from and write to one object — the per-step per-particle noise distribution — so I built one transition module rather than three: the anchor defines the object, the C17 objective shapes it, and the audit/diagnostic measures it; splitting them into separate modules would break the shared-object thread and double the parameters for no gain. I considered an alternative anchor (heterogeneous_decomposition: hard-partition particles into 'stochastic' and 'deterministic' buckets with per-bucket treatment) but rejected it because the bucket boundary is itself unknown and data-dependent, which is exactly what the C17 objective learns softly via per-particle variance — a hard partition would regress to a hand-set threshold. I also rejected encoding the interaction graph as a fixed adjacency (structural_prior_encoding) because the regression flag in method_lineage names per-node structured state-space (c1) as an occupied collateral node that assumes a known graph; learning G_t from the self-supervised particle representation keeps the cure off that node.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: train the global-latent LPWM baseline and the per-particle interaction-gated variant at matched capacity/compute on the procedural multi-object branching benchmark (and validate on a real multi-object video set such as a manipulation dataset), and measure per-object next-state negative log-likelihood and expected calibration error as a function of the number k of independently-branching objects. If the candidate works, the baseline's per-object calibration error rises monotonically with k while the candidate's stays approximately flat, and the candidate's per-object NLL is lower for k>=2 with no loss in full-frame reconstruction/FVD versus the baseline. The named load-bearing variable is the per-particle posterior noise variance v_t^m = Var(u_t^m); negative control: zero it out (collapse all u_t^m to their per-step mean, which reduces the model to a single shared noise draw) and the downstream per-object calibration error must rise back to the baseline curve — if calibration stays good with per-particle variance ablated, the mechanism claim is false and the gains came from added capacity, not from where the noise enters. Positive control: a stripped model that keeps only per-particle variance driven by the oracle branching indicator (no other change) should recover most of the per-object NLL improvement, identifying noise-locus as the causal driver.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2603.04553v1","delta":"LPWM samples a single scene-global latent action per step and broadcasts it to all particles in one Dynamics module; we draw one latent per particle gated by a learned interaction mask, producing a next-state distribution whose per-object marginals are individually calibrated and whose joint couples only interacting particles — a factorization LPWM's single-latent construction cannot represent."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415162380","delta":"Dyn-O builds object-centric world models toward complex scenes but its per-object transition is (near-)deterministic; we construct a per-object stochastic transition with a self-supervised objective that makes each object's predictive variance track its measured branching, which Dyn-O does not model or measure."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2603.04715v1","delta":"Probabilistic Dreaming maintains distinct mutually-exclusive future hypotheses but in a single monolithic scene latent; we factorize the multi-future representation over discovered particles with interaction-gated coupling, so independent per-object branches do not have to share one hypothesis variable."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4407719491","delta":"TextOCVP forecasts slots with a deterministic text-conditioned transformer; we produce a calibrated per-object stochastic forecast and a label-free signal certifying the noise granularity, neither of which a deterministic predictor provides."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"arxiv:2603.04553v1","what_step_was_missed":"LPWM constructed the latent-action stochastic transition as a single global latent broadcast to all particles inside one Dynamics module; to already contain our contribution it would have needed to construct a per-particle latent posterior together with a learned interaction-gating operator that makes the next-state joint factorize into per-object marginals coupled only along interactions — and a label-free objective that drives each particle's posterior spread to its observed empirical future spread. LPWM builds neither the per-particle noise factorization nor the branch-consistency objective, so its per-object marginals remain entangled through the shared global latent."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":287,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"Layer 1 hard floor does not fire: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict is borderline (no Reject lesson is candidate_match: yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and the paper_pointed_threat (FLAM, arxiv:2602.16229v2) is NOT exact-mechanism overlap and is NOT the seed's own LPWM source paper. In the soft zone I choose revise rather than advance because the FLAM threat hits a load-bearing structural property (the anchor's factorization framing) and paper_pointed_threat.addressable_via names specific candidate fields (hook / core_mechanism / differentiation_from_lit / what_step_was_missed), and a borderline C17 finding (missing nearest pair-construction baselines) also touches the load-bearing SSL leg; both are tactical field edits Phase 3.3 can apply without re-running Phase 2.1.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved object-centric world-model leaf produces a next-state predictive distribution in which each object's marginal future uncertainty is individually calibrated AND only physically-interacting objects are correlated in the joint — every leaf either shares one global noise source across the whole scene (LPWM, Dyn-O) or is deterministic given conditioning (TextOCVP), so independent or mutually-exclusive per-object futures cannot be represented without entangling or averaging them.","main_pattern":"generative_process_redesign","sub_pattern":"C24 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail most often by attaching a different conditioning encoder/latent space/control channel to an existing refinement backbone and presenting the swap itself as the contribution, without the ablation that holds backbone, data, and compute fixed while toggling only the new interface; a second shape is buying control at a cost to primary output fidelity.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Eliminating two inherited bottlenecks at once is only compelling if the combined system clearly beats systems that removed each in isolation; marginal gains plus a regression in primary quality read as recombination, not a new method.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate isolates a single interface change (where noise is injected) and falsification_prediction requires no FVD/reconstruction regression versus the baseline, so it is not a two-bottleneck recombination with a quality regression."},{"lesson_quoted":"Swapping the conditioning encoder for a more powerful one is not a new model class if the output quality still trails incumbents and the encoder's advantage is never ablated against the prior encoder under matched conditions.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism keeps the LPWM Encoder/Decoder identical and changes only the per-step noise locus; step 8 runs the matched-capacity/compute ablation versus the global-latent baseline, exactly the missing-ablation failure this lesson warns about, so it is mitigated."},{"lesson_quoted":"A controllable pipeline assembled from frozen pretrained modules needs an ablation proving that the new control surface — not the off-the-shelf components — drives the gain, or it collapses into prior synthetic-data and adapter work.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The per-particle-variance zero-out (negative control, step 10) and gate randomization (step 9) attribute the calibration gain to the new noise/gate surface specifically, satisfying the required attribution ablation."},{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a unified or foundation-model reframe obligates you to actually demonstrate the unification (multi-domain pretraining plus transfer); per-setting retraining under a single architecture does not substantiate the claim.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate makes no unified/foundation-model claim; it is a scoped transition-module redesign."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides a self-supervised, label-free training signal that certifies the LEARNED transition noise is at the correct granularity — i.e. that establishes (rather than assumes) whether scene-global stochasticity is sufficient, or whether per-object / interaction-conditioned stochasticity is necessary, leaving the granularity of the noise an untested modeling choice rather than a measured property of the data.","main_pattern":"targeted_self_supervised_objective","sub_pattern":"C17 (Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring shape is sourcing the pairing/alignment signal by composing two already-published components and presenting the composition itself as the contribution, never re-deriving WHY this pairing geometry uniquely encodes the targeted property, with no operational definition, direct probe, or isolating ablation.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Concatenating a frozen off-the-shelf predictor's output as an extra input channel injects no novel insight — it reads as combining two published systems regardless of the accuracy gain.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The branch-consistency objective is not a frozen predictor concatenation; it contrasts the model's own sampled next-particle states against the observed next particle, a pairing geometry internal to the transition."},{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a representation is 'disentangled' or property-specific without an operational definition, a direct probe, or an isolating ablation leaves the central claim ungrounded and unverifiable.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The targeted property has an operational definition (per-particle posterior variance v_t^m tracking observed per-particle future spread) and a direct probe/control (oracle-variance positive control, zero-variance negative control), so it is grounded."},{"lesson_quoted":"A hard-pair construction strategy that closely recombines existing mixup/contrastive recipes collapses to 'incremental' the moment the nearest pair-construction baselines are missing from the comparison.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The objective's load-bearing primitive (variance-matched per-particle contrast that opens noise only on measured branching) is novel, but the candidate should name nearest pair-construction / variational baselines explicitly to avoid the missing-baseline read; surfaced for Phase 4."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions whether transition stochasticity must enter at a single fixed point in the generative process at all; every leaf inherits from the shared sequential-latent-VAE ancestor the unexamined assumption that one sampling site per step is where uncertainty is injected, and none tests whether the site/granularity of stochasticity should itself be determined by the scene's object/interaction structure.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The signature failure is an identifiability claim that outruns its proof — a straightforward union of two frameworks re-proving recovery, or asserting recovery/consistency while the decisive object is never established, or imposing structural constraints without proving they are SUFFICIENT for recovery.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Stacking two established frameworks and re-proving identifiability of the union reads as incremental unless the pivoted assumption was genuinely load-bearing and the union admits a regime neither framework could reach alone.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The audited single-sampling-site assumption is load-bearing (zeroing per-particle variance provably re-opens the calibration gap, step 10), and the per-object-branching regime is one a scene-global latent cannot reach, so this is not an incremental union."},{"lesson_quoted":"Advertising an identifiability or 'consistency' property while the proof omits the decisive object collapses the contribution the moment a reviewer checks the theorem.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The leg is companion-backed by controlled_diagnostic_design and explicitly ships an EMPIRICAL separation, not a full identifiability theorem; core_mechanism does not advertise a proof it omits, avoiding the claim-outruns-proof failure."},{"lesson_quoted":"Imposing structural constraints to claim interpretability or disentanglement without proving those constraints are sufficient for recovery leaves the result indistinguishable from a post-hoc heuristic.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The structural object/interaction separability is validated as causally responsible for calibration via the matched-capacity diagnostic and the gate/variance negative controls, not asserted as interpretability."}],"verdict":"clear"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"All three legs avoid their clusters' hard reject lessons; the only non-clear finding is a borderline on the C17 SSL leg (targeted_self_supervised_objective gap) — the 'missing nearest pair-construction baselines' lesson — which is a comparison-completeness concern, not a structural defect, and is addressable by naming variational/mixture baselines. No Reject lesson is marked candidate_match: yes, so the gap_closure_reject_check hard floor does not fire."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved object-centric world-model leaf produces a next-state predictive distribution in which each object's marginal future uncertainty is individually calibrated AND only physically-interacting objects are correlated in the joint ...","sub_pattern":"C24 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Hold the iterative-refinement generative backbone fixed and treat its conditioning interface as the free variable — change WHAT it conditions on, HOW the condition enters (e.g. partition it by functional subcomponent / route it selectively), or WHICH space refinement runs in, while keeping the backbone, objective, data, and compute fixed.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism keeps the LPWM particle Encoder/Decoder/VAE backbone and reconstruction loss exactly as-is and redesigns ONLY the per-step conditioning/sampling interface: a single global latent action broadcast to all particles becomes one latent per particle routed through a learned interaction-gating mask G_t — precisely the cluster's 'change how the condition enters / partition it by functional subcomponent' signature move on a held-fixed backbone.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides a self-supervised, label-free training signal that certifies the LEARNED transition noise is at the correct granularity ...","sub_pattern":"C17 (Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Re-engineer the pairing/alignment geometry of a contrastive/similarity objective so the targeted structural property is the ONLY thing whose encoding minimizes the loss, via a non-obvious substitution of a geometric primitive (property-sensitive similarity, relocated reconstruction target, graded-axis pairing).","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism's L_bc contrasts a particle's S sampled predicted next-states against its observed next-state with a property-sensitive (negative squared latent-distance) similarity, whose unique minimizer is a posterior whose spread matches the particle's observed empirical future spread — the cluster's 'replace the default similarity with a property-sensitive measure so the property is the only minimizer' move, here targeting per-particle branching variance.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions whether transition stochasticity must enter at a single fixed point in the generative process at all ...","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Take an existing recovery/modeling precondition and pivot it by trading a distributional assumption for a STRUCTURAL/geometric one of a different kind (e.g. additive/block separability, sparsity over temporal increments) that carries the same identifying power and that the setting plausibly satisfies, then operationalize it as a regularizer/estimator.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism pivots the inherited scene-global-latent (distributional, single-site) precondition to a structural one — the object/interaction separability already present in the particle set carries the identifying signal for per-object futures — and operationalizes it as the per-particle gated noise module plus the empirical separation; the leg honestly downscopes from a full recovery theorem to the companion's empirical separation, so it performs the structural-pivot move without over-claiming the proof.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"All three legs perform their cited cluster's signature move in core_mechanism: C24's hold-backbone-fixed-redesign-the-conditioning-interface, C17's property-sensitive pairing-geometry substitution, and C05's distributional-to-structural precondition pivot operationalized as a regularizer (with the companion owning the empirical deliverable so the C05 leg does not over-claim a theorem)."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["generative_process_redesign","targeted_self_supervised_objective","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"No 2-way subset of the composition set matches any documented anti-pattern — all three flagged compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition, which the candidate deliberately avoided (core_mechanism_reasoning records rejecting a hard per-object partition in favor of soft learned gating)."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"arxiv:2602.16229v2","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"Factored Latent Action Model (FLAM, 2026-02) already makes the headline move of the anchor leg: it observes that monolithic single-latent-action world models 'struggle in complex environments where multiple entities act simultaneously' and replaces the single scene latent action with a FACTORED dynamics framework where each scene factor infers its own latent action and predicts its own next-step value. This directly overlaps the candidate's 'one latent per particle instead of one global latent action,' so the anchor's bare factorization claim is at risk of being read as already-done. The overlap is NOT exact-mechanism, however: FLAM decomposes the scene into INDEPENDENT factors and optimizes prediction accuracy and generation fidelity, whereas the candidate's load-bearing contributions are (a) a LEARNED interaction-gating mask G_t that couples only interacting particles in the joint (FLAM assumes independent factors, no learned inter-factor coupling), (b) CALIBRATION of per-object predictive uncertainty as the target metric (FLAM targets accuracy/quality, not calibrated marginals), and (c) the branch-consistency self-supervised objective that certifies noise granularity tracks measured per-object branching (FLAM has no such certification). The candidate stands if these three differentiators are foregrounded as the contribution rather than the factorization per se; it falls only if the paper is framed around 'factorize the latent action,' which FLAM owns.","addressable_via":"Re-foreground core_mechanism, hook, differentiation_from_lit, and what_step_was_missed so the contribution is the interaction-GATED coupling + calibrated-per-object-stochastic-marginals + branch-consistency certification, explicitly contrasted against FLAM's independent-factor accuracy-oriented factorization, rather than the per-entity latent factorization itself."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"hook / differentiation_from_lit / what_step_was_missed","issue":"paper_pointed_threat — FLAM (arxiv:2602.16229v2) already factorizes latent action per scene-factor, so the bare per-entity-factorization framing is subsumable.","fix_direction":"Add arxiv:2602.16229v2 to differentiation_from_lit with a substantive delta (FLAM uses INDEPENDENT factors optimized for prediction accuracy/fidelity; candidate adds a LEARNED interaction-gating mask coupling only interacting particles AND targets calibrated per-object stochastic marginals AND certifies noise granularity via branch-consistency — none of which FLAM constructs). Re-point what_step_was_missed and hook to foreground interaction-gated coupling + calibration + branch-consistency, not factorization per se. Keep falsification_prediction and compute_budget byte-identical."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism / core_mechanism_steps","issue":"C17 borderline — nearest pair-construction / variational-baseline comparison not named, risking the missing-baseline incremental read.","fix_direction":"In core_mechanism_steps add an explicit comparison against the nearest stochastic-transition baselines (a single-global-latent SVG/CVAE-style variance head and a FLAM-style independent-per-factor latent) so the branch-consistency objective's marginal contribution is attributable. Do NOT alter falsification_prediction or compute_budget."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"hook / differentiation_from_lit / what_step_was_missed","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Re-foregrounded the contribution as interaction-gated coupling + calibrated per-object stochastic marginals + branch-consistency certification (not factorization per se), and added FLAM (arxiv:2602.16229v2) to differentiation_from_lit with a substantive delta contrasting its independent-factor accuracy-oriented factorization."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism / core_mechanism_steps","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added explicit comparison against the nearest stochastic-transition baselines (single-global-latent SVG/CVAE-style variance head and FLAM-style independent-per-factor latent) so the branch-consistency objective's marginal contribution is attributable."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Interaction-Gated Per-Particle Stochasticity for Calibrated Object-Centric World Models\n\n**Method.** Interaction-Gated Per-Particle Stochasticity (IG-PPS)\n\n## Motivation\nA world model is a program that watches video and predicts what happens next. The newest object-centric world models (models that first break a scene into separate objects, then roll the objects forward) finally work on real video with many objects — LPWM (Latent Particle World Models, arXiv 2026-03) is the leading example. But they all have one quiet flaw: when they decide how the next frame might randomly turn out, they roll a single 'dice' for the whole scene and apply it to every object at once.\n\nThat single shared dice is the problem. Imagine object A might go left or right while, completely separately, object B might stop or keep moving. With one shared dice you cannot say 'A is a coin-flip but B is certain' — both objects are forced to read from the same random number, so the model either blurs the two possible futures into a meaningless average or commits the whole scene to one story. The amount of uncertainty it reports for each individual object is then wrong (mis-calibrated). A related recent model, FLAM (Factored Latent Action World Models, arXiv 2026-02), gives each object its own dice — but it assumes the objects are always independent and only chases raw prediction accuracy, so it still cannot say 'these two objects' futures are linked only while they are touching.'\n\nWhy this is solvable now: today's particle world models already give us each object's state and screen position without any human labels, which is exactly the raw material needed to (a) give every object its own dice and (b) learn a 'coupling switch' that turns on only between objects that are actually interacting. And it is cheap to build a test scene generator that dials up the number of objects branching independently, so we can finally measure — rather than guess — whether one scene-wide dice was ever good enough.\n\nWhat changes when this gap closes: a planner can finally trust a per-object uncertainty number ('which specific object is unpredictable right now?'), objects get correlated only along true interactions, and the field gets a label-free test for whether scene-wide randomness is ever sufficient — something LPWM and Dyn-O structurally cannot offer.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n\n1. Take the existing particle-VAE (Deep Latent Particles / DLP) encoder and decoder used by Latent Particle World Models (LPWM) and run it exactly as released: each frame becomes a fixed number M of foreground particles (each carrying a feature vector and its on-screen keypoint position $p^{m})$ plus one background particle, and the decoder paints the frame back from them. Keep its reconstruction and per-particle compression losses unchanged, and train it together with the new dynamics rather than freezing it. Change nothing in this backbone except, later, where the randomness enters the transition.\n   - _Why_: By changing nothing except where the randomness enters, any improvement can only come from the noise redesign, not from a bigger or different backbone.\n\n### Per-particle noise relocation\n*Move randomness from one scene-wide dice to one dice per object so each object can carry its own honest uncertainty.*\n\n2. Swap the one scene-wide random-action head for one small head per object, all sharing the same weights. Each head reads that object's state together with the shared context summary and outputs a mean and a spread, from which it draws that object's own latent noise $u_{t}^{m}$ using the standard reparameterization trick (mean plus spread times a standard normal sample). Make each object's noise the same size as the original single scene noise so the model has no extra capacity — only relocated capacity. Sharing the head weights across objects keeps the model order-independent over objects.\n   - _Why_: Giving every object its own dice is the prerequisite for reporting a separate, honest uncertainty for each object.\n3. Rebuild the one-step predictor so each object's next state is computed from three things: its own current state, a message gathered from the objects it is switched-on with (each neighbor's projected state weighted by the switch, then divided by roughly how many neighbors it has so heavily-connected objects are not overwhelmed), and its own noise. Use the same dynamics network as before, just widened to take these three inputs, and have it output the next-step object in the same format. Because each object draws its own noise and only borrows from switched-on neighbors, the whole-scene future splits into per-object futures that are linked only where the switch is on.\n\n*The redesigned per-particle transition: each next-state particle is predicted from its own state, a gate-weighted message from interacting particles, and its OWN latent noise $u_{t}^{m}$ drawn from a per-particle posterior. Replacing one shared $a_{t}$ by per-particle $u_{t}^{m}$ is the noise relocation.*\n$$ z_{fg}^{m,t+1} = F_\\xi\\!\\left( z_{fg}^{m,t},\\; \\sum_{n} G_t[m,n]\\, z_{fg}^{n,t},\\; u_t^{m} \\right), \\qquad u_t^{m} \\sim q\\!\\left(u_t^{m} \\mid z_{fg}^{m,t}, h_t\\right) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This is what produces per-object futures that are individually honest yet coupled only along the true interactions.\n\n### Learned interaction gate\n*Learn a state-dependent switch that couples objects in the joint distribution only while they actually interact.*\n\n4. Add a learned coupling switch over every pair of foreground objects. For a pair, build a symmetric description from the sum and the absolute difference of their two state vectors plus the distance between their on-screen positions, pass it through a 2-layer network, and squeeze the result to a number between 0 and 1 with a sigmoid at a fixed sharpness (temperature 0.5, which pushes the switch toward clearly on or clearly off). The symmetric description makes the switch the same in both directions; each object is always fully connected to itself, and the background is left out of the switch.\n\n*The learned symmetric interaction gate: for each particle pair (m,n) a 2-layer network over the two particle states and their keypoint distance, squashed by $a sigmoid \\sigma $ at temperature $\\tau ,$ gives a soft coupling weight in [0,1]. Nonzero entries are the only places the joint couples objects.*\n$$ G_t[m,n] = \\sigma\\!\\left( \\frac{1}{\\tau}\\, \\mathrm{MLP}_\\psi\\big([\\,z_{fg}^{m,t},\\, z_{fg}^{n,t},\\, \\lVert p^m - p^n \\rVert\\,]\\big) \\right) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Objects should be correlated only when they are actually interacting; a learned switch makes that link depend on the current scene instead of being fixed.\n\n### Branch-consistency self-supervision\n*A label-free loss that opens per-object noise only where the data shows that object branching, making noise granularity measured rather than assumed.*\n\n5. Add a label-free loss that teaches each object how much to vary. For each object, draw 8 noise samples, roll the model one step, and decode each to a predicted next state. Two forces act: pull the average of these predictions toward the object's actual next state, and make the spread of these 8 predictions match how much that object actually varies in the data (estimated by lightly jittering the same clip by a frame). 【author decision: how to estimate each object's actual future spread — the small temporal window or augmentation that defines the target amount of variation — and how strongly to weight the spread force against the pull force, e.g. a one-time scaling so the two forces are comparable at the start.】 The effect is that the model opens up randomness only for objects that genuinely branch and shrinks it toward zero for predictable ones.\n\n*The branch-consistency objective per particle: pull the S decoded next-state samples toward the observed next state while a spread term (weighted by $\\beta )$ keeps the per-particle sample variance matched to the realized future spread — so noise opens only when that particle actually branches and collapses toward zero otherwise.*\n$$ \\mathcal{L}_{bc} = \\sum_{m} \\frac{1}{S}\\sum_{s=1}^{S} \\big\\lVert \\hat{z}_{fg}^{m,t+1}(u_t^{m,s}) - z_{fg}^{m,t+1} \\big\\rVert^2 \\;-\\; \\beta\\, \\widehat{\\mathrm{Var}}_s\\big[\\hat{z}_{fg}^{m,t+1}(u_t^{m,s})\\big] \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This makes the model open randomness only for objects that really branch and shut it off for predictable ones, so the amount of noise is measured from data, not guessed.\n6. Train the whole system together with the original LPWM objective plus one-tenth of the new branch-consistency loss. Keep the original optimizer, learning rate, and batch size so any difference is attributable to the method, not the training recipe, and ramp the new loss up gradually from zero over the early part of training so it does not interfere before the encoder has settled. Use a mix of real multi-object video and the synthetic branching clips.\n\n*Total training loss: the unchanged LPWM evidence lower bound plus the branch-consistency term scaled by $\\lambda _{bc}$ (default 0.1), trained end-to-end. The backbone objective is untouched; only this added term shapes the noise granularity.*\n$$ \\mathcal{L} = \\mathcal{L}_{\\text{LPWM-ELBO}} + \\lambda_{bc}\\, \\mathcal{L}_{bc} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The backbone objective stays intact; the small added term is all that is needed to teach the right amount of per-object randomness.\n\n### Calibration-vs-k diagnostic and controls\n*A procedural generator and matched-capacity ablations/controls that prove the calibration gain comes from the noise locus and the learned gate, not added capacity.*\n\n7. Build a small scene generator you control. On a lightweight physics or sprite engine, render scenes where k chosen objects each, at a set moment, randomly pick their next move from a small fixed menu (for example left-or-right, or stop-or-go), choosing independently of one another with recorded random seeds; also render a matched version where each of those objects is locked to a single fixed outcome (no branching). Record, for each object at each branch moment, which option it took — these labels are the ground truth used only to score the models, never to train them. 【author decision: which concrete engine and visual assets to use, and the exact branching rule (the small menu of outcomes and when in the clip the branch happens).】\n   - _Why_: Controlling exactly how many objects branch lets us attribute any gap to where the noise enters rather than to model size or luck of the data.\n8. Compare four equally-sized, equally-trained models on the same data: the original single-scene-noise LPWM; a single-scene-noise model with a learned spread head; a per-object-noise model with the coupling switch turned off (objects independent, the FLAM-style variant); and the full model. For each, turn its 8 sampled next states for an object into a probability estimate (fit a simple density or count how often each outcome occurs) and score two things against the recorded truth: how surprised it is by the real next state (negative log-likelihood) and whether its stated per-object probabilities match how often those outcomes actually happen (calibration error). Plot all four as the number k of independently-branching objects grows. Comparing the full model to the switch-off variant isolates the switch's contribution; comparing to the no-branch-consistency variant isolates the objective's contribution.\n   - _Why_: These named baselines separate the gain due to the coupling switch from the gain due to the branch-consistency objective.\n9. Run checks that pin down WHY any gain happens. First, scramble the coupling switch: keep the same overall amount of coupling but randomly shuffle which object-pairs it connects, destroying the learned structure, and re-score. Second, a positive check: force each object's noise to be large exactly when the recorded truth says it branches and near-zero otherwise — if calibration jumps, per-object noise placed by branching is what matters. Third, a negative check: remove per-object noise entirely by collapsing every object to a single shared draw — calibration should fall back to the original baseline. Together these show the improvement comes from where the noise enters and from the learned switch, not from extra capacity.\n   - _Why_: If turning off the per-object noise makes calibration bad again, that proves the improvement came from where the noise enters, not from extra capacity.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 面向校准的对象中心世界模型的交互门控逐粒子随机性 (Interaction-Gated Per-Particle Stochasticity)\n\n**方法名称.** Interaction-Gated Per-Particle Stochasticity (IG-PPS)\n\n## 研究动机\n世界模型是一个观看视频并预测接下来会发生什么的程序。最新的对象中心世界模型(先把场景拆成一个个独立对象,再让对象向前演化的模型)终于能在含有多个对象的真实视频上工作了——LPWM (Latent Particle World Models, arXiv 2026-03) 是其中的代表。但它们都有一个被忽视的缺陷:在决定下一帧可能如何随机变化时,它们对整个场景只掷一颗「骰子」,然后把它同时套用到每一个对象上。\n\n这颗共享的骰子正是问题所在。设想对象 A 可能向左或向右,而与之完全独立地,对象 B 可能停下或继续移动。用一颗共享骰子,你无法表达「A 是抛硬币、但 B 是确定的」——两个对象被迫读取同一个随机数,于是模型要么把两种可能的未来模糊成一个无意义的平均,要么把整个场景锁定到单一剧情。这样它为每个独立对象给出的不确定性就是错的(mis-calibrated,未校准)。一个相关的近期模型 FLAM (Factored Latent Action World Models, arXiv 2026-02) 给每个对象各自一颗骰子——但它假设对象之间永远独立,且只追求原始预测精度,因此仍无法表达「这两个对象的未来只在它们接触时才相关」。\n\n为什么现在能解决:今天的粒子世界模型已经能在无需任何人工标注的情况下给出每个对象的状态与屏幕位置,这正是所需的原材料,可用来 (a) 给每个对象自己的骰子,并 (b) 学习一个「耦合开关」,只在真正发生交互的对象之间打开。而且,构建一个能调节独立分叉对象数量 k 的测试场景生成器成本很低,于是我们终于可以「测量」而非「猜测」单一全场景骰子是否曾经足够。\n\n当这个缺口被填补后会发生什么:规划器终于能信任逐对象的不确定性数值(「此刻究竟哪个对象不可预测?」),对象之间只沿真实交互被关联,并且该领域获得一个无标注的检验手段,用来判断全场景随机性是否曾经足够——这是 LPWM 与 Dyn-O 在结构上无法提供的。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景\n\n1. 直接采用 Latent Particle World Models (LPWM) 所用的现成粒子 VAE(Deep Latent Particles, DLP)编码器与解码器,并按发布版原样运行:每帧被表示为固定数量 M 个前景粒子(每个携带一个特征向量及其屏幕关键点位置 $p^{m})$外加一个背景粒子,解码器再据此重建该帧。保持其重建损失与逐粒子压缩损失不变,并与新动力学一起训练而非冻结。除了之后改动转移中「随机性从何进入」之外,这个骨干不做任何改动。\n   - _为什么_: 除了「随机性从哪里进入」之外什么都不改,任何提升就只能来自噪声的重新设计,而非更大或不同的骨干网络。\n\n### 逐粒子噪声重新定位\n*把随机性从单一全场景骰子移到每个对象一颗骰子,使每个对象都能承载自己诚实的不确定性。*\n\n2. 把单一的全场景随机动作头,替换为每个对象一个、且共享权重的小头。每个头读入该对象的状态与共享的上下文摘要,输出一个均值与一个散度(spread),并用标准的重参数化技巧(均值 + 散度 $\\times $ 标准正态采样)抽取该对象自己的潜在噪声 $u_{t}^{m}$。让每个对象的噪声维度与原来单一全场景噪声相同,使模型没有额外容量、只是把容量重新定位。各对象共享头权重,可保持模型对对象次序无关(置换等变)。\n   - _为什么_: 给每个对象自己的骰子,是为每个对象单独报告诚实不确定性的前提。\n3. 重建一步预测器,使每个对象的下一步状态由三部分计算得出:它自己的当前状态;从与它「开关打开」的对象处汇聚的消息(每个邻居的投影状态按开关加权,再除以它大致有多少个邻居,以免高度连接的对象被淹没);以及它自己的噪声。沿用原有的动力学网络,只是把输入加宽以接收这三项,并让其输出同一格式的下一步对象。由于每个对象抽取自己的噪声、且只从开关打开的邻居借用信息,整个场景的未来便分解为「只在开关打开处相连」的逐对象未来。\n\n*重新设计的逐粒子转移:每个下一步粒子由其自身状态、来自交互粒子的门控加权消息,以及它自己的潜在噪声 $u_{t}^{m}($采自逐粒子后验)共同预测。用逐粒子 $u_{t}^{m}$ 取代单一共享 $a_{t},$即为噪声的重新定位。*\n$$ z_{fg}^{m,t+1} = F_\\xi\\!\\left( z_{fg}^{m,t},\\; \\sum_{n} G_t[m,n]\\, z_{fg}^{n,t},\\; u_t^{m} \\right), \\qquad u_t^{m} \\sim q\\!\\left(u_t^{m} \\mid z_{fg}^{m,t}, h_t\\right) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这正是产生「逐对象诚实、却只沿真实交互耦合」的未来分布的来源。\n\n### 可学习交互门\n*学习一个依赖状态的开关,仅在对象真正交互时才在联合分布中耦合它们。*\n\n4. 为每一对前景对象加入一个可学习的耦合开关。对一对对象,用它们两个状态向量的「和」与「绝对差」再加上它们屏幕位置之间的距离,构成一个对称描述,送入一个 2 层网络,并用固定锐度的 sigmoid(温度 0.5,使开关趋向明确的开或关)压缩到 0 到 1 之间的数。对称描述使开关在两个方向上相同;每个对象对自身始终全连接,背景粒子不参与该开关。\n\n*可学习的对称交互门:对每个粒子对 (m,n),用一个 2 层网络读入两个粒子状态与其关键点距离,经温度 $\\tau $ 的 $sigmoid \\sigma $ 压缩到 [0,1],得到软耦合权重;只有非零项才在联合分布中耦合对象。*\n$$ G_t[m,n] = \\sigma\\!\\left( \\frac{1}{\\tau}\\, \\mathrm{MLP}_\\psi\\big([\\,z_{fg}^{m,t},\\, z_{fg}^{n,t},\\, \\lVert p^m - p^n \\rVert\\,]\\big) \\right) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 对象只应在真正交互时才相关;可学习的开关让这种关联依赖于当前场景,而不是被固定下来。\n\n### 分支一致性自监督\n*一个无标注损失,只在数据显示某对象分叉处打开其噪声,使噪声粒度成为被测量而非被假设的属性。*\n\n5. 加入一个无标注损失,教每个对象「该有多大变化」。对每个对象,抽取 8 个噪声样本,把模型前滚一步,并各自解码为一个预测的下一步状态。两个力同时作用:把这些预测的平均值拉向该对象真实的下一步状态;并使这 8 个预测的散度去匹配该对象在数据中实际的变化量(通过把同一片段轻微抖动一帧来估计)。【author decision: 如何估计每个对象真实的未来散度——定义目标变化量所用的短时间窗或数据增强方案——以及散度项相对于拉近项的权重 $\\beta $ 该如何设定,例如做一次性缩放使两个力在训练开始时量级相当。】其效果是:模型只为真正分叉的对象打开随机性,对可预测的对象则把随机性压缩到接近零。\n\n*逐粒子的分支一致性目标:把 S 个解码出的下一步样本拉向观测到的下一步状态,同时一个由 $\\beta $ 加权的散度项使逐粒子样本方差与真实的未来散度匹配——因此只有当该粒子确实分叉时噪声才打开,否则趋于零。*\n$$ \\mathcal{L}_{bc} = \\sum_{m} \\frac{1}{S}\\sum_{s=1}^{S} \\big\\lVert \\hat{z}_{fg}^{m,t+1}(u_t^{m,s}) - z_{fg}^{m,t+1} \\big\\rVert^2 \\;-\\; \\beta\\, \\widehat{\\mathrm{Var}}_s\\big[\\hat{z}_{fg}^{m,t+1}(u_t^{m,s})\\big] \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这让模型只为真正分叉的对象打开随机性,对可预测的对象关闭它,于是噪声的大小是从数据测量而非猜测得来。\n6. 用原始 LPWM 目标加上十分之一的新分支一致性损失,把整个系统一起训练。保持原有的优化器、学习率与批大小,使任何差异都可归因于方法本身而非训练配方;并在训练早期把新损失从零逐步线性加大,以免在编码器尚未稳定前就产生干扰。数据使用真实多对象视频与合成分叉片段的混合集。\n\n*总训练损失:保持不变的 LPWM 证据下界,加上由 $\\lambda _{bc}($默认 0.1)缩放的分支一致性项,端到端训练。骨干目标不变,仅此附加项塑造噪声粒度。*\n$$ \\mathcal{L} = \\mathcal{L}_{\\text{LPWM-ELBO}} + \\lambda_{bc}\\, \\mathcal{L}_{bc} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 骨干目标保持完整;只需这一小项附加损失就足以教会模型正确的逐对象随机性。\n\n### 校准-随-k 诊断与对照\n*一个过程化生成器加上同容量消融/对照,证明校准增益来自噪声位置与可学习门,而非额外容量。*\n\n7. 构建一个你能完全掌控的小型场景生成器。在一个轻量物理或精灵(sprite)引擎上渲染这样的场景:k 个被指定的对象在某个设定时刻各自从一个小而固定的选项集合(例如「左或右」「停或走」)中随机选择下一步动作,彼此独立并记录随机种子;同时渲染一个匹配版本,其中这些对象各被锁定到单一固定结果(不分叉)。记录每个对象在每个分叉时刻所选的选项——这些标签作为真值,仅用于给模型打分,绝不用于训练。【author decision: 采用哪个具体引擎与视觉素材,以及确切的分叉规则(结果选项的小集合,以及分叉发生在片段中的哪个时刻)。】\n   - _为什么_: 精确控制有多少对象分叉,使我们能把任何差距归因于「噪声从哪里进入」,而非模型大小或数据运气。\n8. 在相同数据上比较四个同等规模、同等训练的模型:原始的单一全场景噪声 LPWM;带可学习散度头的单一全场景噪声模型;关闭耦合开关的逐对象噪声模型(对象相互独立,即 FLAM 式变体);以及完整模型。对每个模型,把它为某对象抽取的 8 个下一步状态转成一个概率估计(拟合一个简单密度,或统计每个结果出现的频率),并对照记录的真值评分两件事:它对真实下一步状态有多「意外」(负对数似然 NLL),以及它给出的逐对象概率是否与这些结果实际发生的频率相符(校准误差 ECE)。把四者随独立分叉对象数 k 的增长绘成曲线。完整模型对比「关闭开关」变体可分离出开关的贡献,对比「无分支一致性」变体可分离出该目标的贡献。\n   - _为什么_: 这些被点名的基线把「耦合开关带来的增益」与「分支一致性目标带来的增益」区分开来。\n9. 运行用以「锁定增益来源」的对照实验。其一,打乱耦合开关:保持耦合的总体强度不变,但随机重排它连接的是哪些对象对,从而破坏学到的结构,再重新评分。其二,正向对照:强制每个对象的噪声「只在记录真值标明它分叉时」为大、否则接近零——若校准随之跃升,说明「按分叉放置的逐对象噪声」正是关键。其三,负向对照:把每个对象坍缩为单一共享采样,从而彻底移除逐对象噪声——校准应当退回到原始基线。三者合起来表明:提升来自「噪声从哪里进入」与可学习的开关,而非额外容量。\n   - _为什么_: 如果关闭逐对象噪声会让校准重新变差,就证明提升来自「噪声从哪里进入」,而非额外的容量。\n\n"},{"id":"67","run_dir":"run_prompt67_speechtext","index":67,"title":"One Latent, Two Rates: A Continuous Shared Substrate for Joint Speech-Text Transformers","title_zh":"一个潜变量，两种速率：用于联合语音-文本 Transformer 的连续共享基底","method_name":"Continuous Shared Substrate (CSS) for joint speech-text modeling","hook":"Every joint speech-text transformer in the retrieved frontier — interleaved, parallel, dMel-tokenized — silently inherits that the shared per-step prediction target must be a discrete token, and that inherited discreteness, not any backbone limit, is what forces the sequence-length blowup and the acoustic-quantization loss. We show a single continuous per-step latent that speech and text each decode into and out of at their own native rate removes both at once, and that a matched discrete-vs-continuous diagnostic attributes the speech-text gap to the substrate's discreteness rather than to capacity or data.","anchor_pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","anchor_pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","domain_category":"Speech & Audio","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved joint speech-text model lets the two modalities share a single per-step continuous prediction target while each is read in and written out at its own native rate; every leaf either lengthens the sequence to force a common discrete clock (interleaving) or splits into modality-specific objectives, so the rate mismatch and the acoustic-quantization loss are never absorbed together (additive, sits at the anchor 90b719…'s frontier-leaf residual).","pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","sub_pattern":"C24 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by promoting the joint AR backbone's operating space from the inherited discrete-token timeline to a single continuous per-step latent z_t (the free variable C24 liberates), with two lightweight per-modality decode heads that read z_t out at speech's native frame rate and text's native subword rate, so one shared next-vector objective absorbs both the rate mismatch and the quantization loss while the transformer backbone, optimizer, data, and compute stay fixed.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved paper tests whether the per-step prediction target in a joint speech-text transformer must be a discrete token at all — every joint-LM leaf (interleaved, parallel, dMel-tokenized, KD-distilled) silently inherits the assumption that the shared modeling substrate is a discrete vocabulary, and none asks whether that discreteness is necessary rather than assumed (subtractive; reads off the shared discrete-substrate ancestor node n2).","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","how_closed":"Framing move (C01): relocate the shared modeling locus from the assumed discrete-token vocabulary to the overlooked continuous-latent locus and state 'the joint substrate must be discrete' as a falsifiable proposition; companion deliverable (controlled_diagnostic_design): a matched-pair diagnostic that swaps ONLY the per-step target (continuous z_t vs a discrete quantization of the same z_t) while holding backbone, data, tokenizer rate, and compute identical, reporting the speech-text consistency gap as the headline so the gain is attributable to substrate discreteness, not capacity or data.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"latent speech-text transformer / joint spoken language modeling","n_papers":28,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":25},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10},{"source":"openreview","n":2}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":13,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"CMAST: Efficient Speech-Text Joint Training Method to Enhance Linguistic Features Learning of Speech Representations"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"VoiceTextBlender: Augmenting Large Language Models with Speech Capabilities via Single-Stage Joint Speech-Text Supervised Fine-Tuning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Improving End-to-End Speech Recognition Through Conditional Cross-Modal Knowledge Distillation with Language Model"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Joint End-to-End Spoken Language Understanding and Automatic Speech Recognition Training Based on Unified Speech-to-Text Pre-Training"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"EnCLAP: Combining Neural Audio Codec and Audio-Text Joint Embedding for Automated Audio Captioning"},{"source":"openalex","title":"JST and rJST: joint estimation of sentiment and topics in textual data using a semi-supervised approach"}],"more":7},{"year":2025,"n":27,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Towards Efficient Speech-Text Jointly Decoding within One Speech Language Model"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"MyanSpeech: Joint CTC-Attention and RNN Language Model for End-To-End Read Speech Recognition"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"From Text to Talk: Audio-Language Model Needs Non-Autoregressive Joint Training"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Harnessing the Zero-Shot Power of Instruction-Tuned Large Language Model for Guiding End-to-End Speech Recognition"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Adaptive Inner Speech-Text Alignment for LLM-based Speech Translation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"TSLA: A Multi-Task Time Series Language Model"}],"more":21},{"year":2026,"n":10,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"},{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Advancing automatic speech recognition using feature fusion with self-supervised learning features: A case study on Fearless Steps Apollo corpus"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Zero-Shot Speech LLMs for Multi-Aspect Evaluation of L2 Speech: Challenges and Opportunities"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Streaming Speech-to-Text Translation with a SpeechLLM"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Toward Natural Emotional Text-To-Speech System with Fine-Grained Non-Verbal Expression Control"}],"more":4}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":13,"share":0.464},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":6,"share":0.214},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":5,"share":0.179},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":4,"share":0.143},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":4,"share":0.143},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":4,"share":0.143},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":3,"share":0.107},{"pattern_id":"algebraic_equivalence_unification","pattern_name":"Prove Equivalence to Unify","count":2,"share":0.071}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"In current joint speech-text transformers the two modalities are forced onto a shared *discrete-token* timeline that neither modality natively fits: discrete-token interleaving (semanticscholar:90b719e905154a418b7ab30c2da7de617d96d84b) pays an excessive sequence-length cost because speech tokens fire many times per text token, and even speech-tokenizer-simplification work (openalex:W4402856752, dMel) keeps a hard quantization bottleneck that discards continuous acoustic detail; meanwhile the parallel/decomposed variants (semanticscholar:1416afa3b83d5447cadf25a731879ece1b3378ab, Text-to-Talk) split text-AR from audio-NAR precisely because one shared discrete next-token objective cannot honor that speech depends mainly on source-target relations while text depends on target-target relations. The concrete structural gap: there is no joint speech-text model whose per-step prediction target is a single continuous latent that both modalities are decoded into and out of at their own native rate, so the rate mismatch and the quantization loss cannot be jointly absorbed — every current model resolves the mismatch either by lengthening the sequence (interleaving) or by splitting the model into modality-specific paths.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:90b719e905154a418b7ab30c2da7de617d96d84b","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Systematically compares interleaved vs parallel discrete-token joint speech-text decoding within one Speech LM under a controlled setup and finds interleaving strongest. Its residue: it treats the discrete speech-token substrate as fixed and only chooses among arrangements of those tokens, so it never removes the sequence-length blowup it documents nor questions whether the shared per-step target must be a discrete token at all."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:1416afa3b83d5447cadf25a731879ece1b3378ab","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Argues a single AR next-token objective is mismatched (text is target-target, audio is source-target) and so routes AR text + NAR audio-diffusion through one Transformer. Its residue: the two modalities still occupy two distinct decoding objectives and the text side stays on discrete tokens, so there is no single shared continuous latent both modalities are predicted in; the mismatch is decomposed away rather than absorbed into one substrate."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415928588","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"CALM replaces discrete next-token prediction with continuous next-vector prediction by compressing K text tokens into one continuous latent, raising semantic bandwidth per step. Its residue: demonstrated on text only — it never carries the continuous-latent AR objective across to speech or to a cross-modal setting, so whether one continuous latent can simultaneously host speech and text at their native rates is untested."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4402856752","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"dMel discretizes mel-filterbank channels directly to give a simple speech tokenizer that feeds an LM. Its residue: it still commits to a discrete bottleneck, so continuous acoustic detail is quantized away before the LM sees it and the speech rate is fixed by the tokenizer, not chosen by the model."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"latent speech-text transformer / joint spoken language modeling","venue":"ICLR/NeurIPS (ML)","time":"2026","data":["paired speech-text corpora (e.g. LibriSpeech/LibriHeavy-scale ASR data)","text-only corpora","unlabeled speech"],"compute":"1×A100 × 3 months (≈ 90 A100-day)","expertise":"speech + LLM pretraining","preference":"both","baseline":"discrete-speech-token interleaved speech-text LMs and the Latent Speech-Text Transformer (dynamic latent speech patches)","limitation":"speech and text live at radically different rates and on different substrates (discrete acoustic tokens vs subword text tokens); current joint LMs either interleave discrete tokens (sequence-length blowup, lossy quantization) or pool speech into latent patches but still couple them to a discrete text-token objective, so the per-step representation is never a single modality-agnostic continuous latent","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["domain","venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"Shared object (shared_object thread): the single continuous per-step latent z_t ∈ R^d that BOTH legs read from and write to. (Leg 1 — construct the substrate, C24.) The inherited operating space of a joint speech-text AR transformer is a discrete-token timeline on which speech tokens fire ~5-10× per text token; we hold the decoder-only transformer backbone, its next-step objective form, the training data, and compute fixed, and change ONLY the space the AR step predicts in: from a softmax over a discrete vocabulary to a continuous next-vector z_t. z_t is defined as the output of a small modality-shared projection head g_θ applied to the backbone's last hidden state h_t (z_t = g_θ(h_t), d=1024, model-internal readout). Two frozen-then-finetuned per-modality codecs define how z_t maps to observations: a speech codec D_s (a pretrained mel/EnCodec-style decoder run at speech's native 12.5–25 Hz frame rate) and a text decoder D_x (a linear-then-softmax head over the subword vocabulary run at text's native rate). The native-rate coupling is realized by a modality-rate router: each generated z_t carries a 2-way modality gate m_t ∈ {speech,text} (predicted by a tiny head r_φ(h_t), argmax at inference, Gumbel-softmax with temperature τ=1.0 in training), and only the gated decoder consumes z_t, so speech and text advance the shared latent stream at their own rates inside ONE sequence rather than on a forced common clock. The per-step loss is a convex combination L = λ_s · L_speech_recon(D_s(z_t), x_t^speech) + λ_x · L_text_CE(D_x(z_t), x_t^text) + λ_m · L_gate, with speech reconstruction an L2-in-codec-space term and λ_s=1.0, λ_x=1.0, λ_m=0.1 (named hyperparameters bridging the L2 and cross-entropy units). This is the construction CALM (openalex:W4415928588) made for text-only next-vector prediction, now carrying TWO modalities at different native rates in one latent stream — the artifact none of the continuous-latent leaves produced — which closes Leg 1's gap because a single shared next-vector target absorbs the rate mismatch (no interleaving padding) and the quantization loss (z_t is never discretized) simultaneously. (Leg 2 — audit the discreteness assumption, C01 + companion C02.) The same object z_t is the locus we relocate the load-bearing signal to: we state 'the joint speech-text substrate must be discrete' as falsifiable, and build the confound-isolating diagnostic by training a matched twin that is byte-identical except the per-step target is VQ(z_t) — a vector-quantized discretization of the SAME z_t at a codebook size chosen so its bit-rate equals z_t's effective bit-rate — so backbone, data, tokenizer rate, decoders, and compute are held fixed and only the substrate's discreteness varies. The headline measurement is the cross-modal factual-consistency gap (does a fact written in speech survive read-out in text, after Do-Factual-Recall (arxiv:2605.22170v1)'s causal-mediation probe): we predict the continuous twin closes a gap the discrete twin leaves open, attributing it to discreteness rather than capacity. The two legs share z_t as their single mathematical primitive — Leg 1 builds it, Leg 2 audits whether its defining continuity (vs the inherited discreteness) is what carries the speech-text bridge.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The two legs SHARE machinery rather than needing separate modules: the audit's matched twin is literally the same architecture with one operator (continuous head vs VQ head) swapped, so z_t is one object serving construction and audit — the evidence is that the diagnostic's de-confounding requires byte-identity everywhere except the substrate, which only holds because both legs are instantiated on the same z_t. Alternative designs considered and rejected: (i) making the audit a separate continuous-vs-discrete benchmark across many published models — rejected because backbone/data confounds cannot be held fixed across heterogeneous prior systems, defeating C02's isolation requirement; (ii) using a diffusion audio path à la Text-to-Talk as the speech decoder — rejected because it reintroduces a second modality-specific objective, which would re-open exactly the rate-mismatch gap Leg 1 closes. REGRESSION CHECK (method_lineage.notes): the cure must not reduce to node n2 (discrete speech-token LM) nor n6's text-only continuous LM; we avoid n2 because z_t is never discretized in the deliverable model, and we go beyond n6 (the avoided occupied source) by making the continuous latent host two modalities at native rates — recorded here so Phase 4 inherits the constraint that single-modality continuous-latent LMs are an occupied node.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: train the continuous-substrate model and its byte-matched discrete (VQ) twin on the same LibriHeavy subset + text corpus with one 300M backbone, identical data tokens and A100-hours; measure (a) mean sequence length per spoken utterance and (b) cross-modal factual-consistency rate via causal-mediation read-out (fact written in speech, retrieved in text). If the candidate works: sequence length drops sharply vs the interleaved discrete baseline with no ASR-WER or TTS-quality regression, AND the continuous twin's cross-modal factual-consistency rate is materially higher than the discrete twin's. Mechanism distinguisher — the single named load-bearing variable is the CONTINUITY of the per-step target z_t (operationalized as whether z_t is decoded directly or after VQ): negative control intervenes by replacing z_t with VQ(z_t) at inference in the trained continuous model. Anti-tautology: the control's predicted effect is on the DOWNSTREAM task-outcome metric — cross-modal factual-consistency rate (and ASR WER) — not on z_t's own quantization error; if continuity is load-bearing, quantizing z_t at inference drives cross-modal consistency down toward the discrete twin's level, whereas if the gain came from capacity or data the metric would be unchanged. Positive control (recommended): a stripped model that keeps ONLY the continuous z_t target with a single shared decode head should recover most of the cross-modal consistency advantage, converting the falsifier into a constructive identification of continuity as the bridge.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:90b719e905154a418b7ab30c2da7de617d96d84b","delta":"They compare arrangements (interleaved vs parallel) of a FIXED discrete-token substrate and document but cannot remove the sequence-length blowup; we replace the substrate with one continuous per-step latent decoded at each modality's native rate, removing the blowup by construction rather than choosing among token layouts."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415928588","delta":"CALM constructs continuous next-vector prediction for a single (text) modality; we construct a continuous latent that simultaneously hosts speech and text at different native rates via a modality-gated decode, the cross-modal substrate their text-only construction does not produce."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4402856752","delta":"dMel simplifies the speech tokenizer but keeps a hard discrete bottleneck; we keep the per-step target continuous end-to-end and empirically test, via a byte-matched VQ twin, whether that discreteness was ever necessary — a necessity question dMel never poses."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:1416afa3b83d5447cadf25a731879ece1b3378ab","delta":"Text-to-Talk decomposes the modalities into AR-text + NAR-audio-diffusion objectives; we absorb both into ONE shared continuous next-vector objective, so there is a single shared latent rather than two modality-specific decoding paths."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2605.22170v1","delta":"They diagnose that factual-recall circuits are modality-dependent in discrete joint SLMs but offer no remedy; we use their causal-mediation probe as the metric in a matched continuous-vs-discrete twin to test whether a continuous substrate makes recall modality-agnostic."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4415928588","what_step_was_missed":"CALM constructed continuous next-vector prediction and the autoencoder that compresses one modality's tokens into a continuous vector, but only for a single modality on a single rate; our contribution requires a construction it never built — a modality-gated continuous latent whose single next-vector target is decoded into two modalities at two different native frame/subword rates within one sequence, plus the matched-twin discretization that turns the continuity into a falsifiable necessity claim. The cross-modal, two-rate decode and the byte-matched VQ twin are the missing constructions."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":327,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"Layer 1 did not fire: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict=clear (no Reject lesson candidate_match: yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id=null, and paper_pointed_threat=no_threat_found (the nearest collision hit, 'Generation-Step-Aware Framework for Cross-Modal Representation and Control in Multilingual Speech-Text Models', controls generation steps, not the per-step substrate, so no exact-mechanism overlap). In Layer 2 all checks are clear and recipe_application_check.verdict=applied for both legs, so the candidate advances.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved joint speech-text model lets the two modalities share a single per-step continuous prediction target while each is read in and written out at its own native rate; every leaf either lengthens the sequence to force a common discrete clock (interleaving) or splits into modality-specific objectives, so the rate mismatch and the acoustic-quantization loss are never absorbed together (additive, sits at the anchor 90b719…'s frontier-leaf residual).","main_pattern":"generative_process_redesign","sub_pattern":"C24 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail most often by attaching a different conditioning encoder/latent space to an existing refinement backbone and presenting the swap as the contribution without isolating it — the recurring shortcut being the missing ablation that holds backbone, data, and compute fixed while toggling only the new interface; a second shape is an over-claimed 'unified/foundation' reframe the experiments never exercise.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Eliminating two inherited bottlenecks at once is only compelling if the combined system clearly beats systems that removed each in isolation; marginal gains plus a regression in primary quality read as recombination, not a new method.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism_steps 5 measures both sequence-length reduction AND no ASR/TTS quality regression against an interleaved baseline of identical backbone+data+compute, so the two-bottleneck claim is held to the 'no primary-quality regression' bar."},{"lesson_quoted":"Swapping the conditioning encoder for a more powerful one is not a new model class if the output quality still trails incumbents and the encoder's advantage is never ablated against the prior encoder under matched conditions.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the candidate does not swap in a stronger encoder; it changes the per-step target space (discrete→continuous) and ablates exactly that via the byte-matched VQ twin (step 6) under matched data/compute."},{"lesson_quoted":"A controllable pipeline assembled from frozen pretrained modules needs an ablation proving that the new control surface — not the off-the-shelf components — drives the gain, or it collapses into prior synthetic-data and adapter work.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the negative control (step 8: replace z_t with VQ(z_t) at inference) and positive control (continuous-only stripped model) isolate continuity of z_t as the driver, not the borrowed mel/EnCodec decoder."},{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a unified or foundation-model reframe obligates you to actually demonstrate the unification (multi-domain pretraining plus transfer); per-setting retraining under a single architecture does not substantiate the claim.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the candidate does not over-claim a foundation reframe — it scopes to one joint speech-text substrate at 300M and tests the substrate property, not a broad multi-domain foundation claim."},{"lesson_quoted":"Importing a representation from a semantically adjacent domain as the conditioning signal fails when that space is orthogonal to the geometry or dynamics that actually determine the output being synthesized.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"z_t is learned end-to-end as the backbone readout feeding the actual speech/text decoders, not an imported orthogonal representation."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved paper tests whether the per-step prediction target in a joint speech-text transformer must be a discrete token at all — every joint-LM leaf (interleaved, parallel, dMel-tokenized, KD-distilled) silently inherits the assumption that the shared modeling substrate is a discrete vocabulary, and none asks whether that discreteness is necessary rather than assumed (subtractive; reads off the shared discrete-substrate ancestor node n2).","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is a relocation demonstrated but not adversarially/mechanistically closed — beating a fixed baseline without stress-testing or explaining why the new locus carries the signal; plus novelty-boundary collapse (the 'new' locus was already used by prior work) and reintroducing the assumption the move was meant to dissolve.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work — normalization statistics, activation-similarity losses, semantic concept triggers — collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"differentiation_from_lit explicitly measures the boundary vs CALM (text-only continuous locus) and dMel (discrete locus): the continuous-latent locus hosting two modalities at native rates is not a published joint-LM locus."},{"lesson_quoted":"Demonstrating the new locus only on fixed, non-adaptive or outdated baselines while omitting any account of why it works reads as a stacked pipeline of existing components rather than a principled shift.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism_reasoning gives the mechanistic account (continuity avoids quantization loss + native-rate decode avoids forced common clock) and steps 8-9 supply the controlled why, not just a baseline win."},{"lesson_quoted":"A defense whose relocation silently depends on a clean reference model or a known anomaly distribution reintroduces precisely the strong assumption the move was supposed to eliminate.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the audit's ground truth is the construction-derived causal-mediation probe on planted facts, not a clean reference model or assumed distribution."},{"lesson_quoted":"Wiring off-the-shelf generators or tools into a new attack setting without a structural reason for the locus change gets judged as engineering integration, not insight.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the locus change (discrete vocabulary → continuous latent) is structurally motivated by the rate-mismatch + quantization diagnosis in the bottleneck, not a convenience wiring."},{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a relocated signal is 'stealthier' or 'harder to remove' without defeating an adaptive defender who searches the same new locus leaves the central claim unverified.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"not a security stealth claim; the analogous 'adaptive' test is the byte-matched VQ twin at equal bit-rate, which is the strongest discrete counterpart operating at the same locus granularity."}],"verdict":"clear"}],"verdict":"clear","reasoning":"Both gap_closure entries are clear: the C24 leg's most dangerous reject lesson (two-bottleneck recombination) is mitigated by the matched-backbone ablation and no-regression measurement (steps 5-6), and the C01 leg's novelty-boundary-collapse lesson is mitigated by explicit measured differentiation from the discrete (dMel) and text-only-continuous (CALM) loci. No Reject lesson is marked candidate_match: yes."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved joint speech-text model lets the two modalities share a single per-step continuous prediction target while each is read in and written out at its own native rate; every leaf either lengthens the sequence to force a common discrete clock (interleaving) or splits into modality-specific objectives, so the rate mismatch and the acoustic-quantization loss are never absorbed together (additive, sits at the anchor 90b719…'s frontier-leaf residual).","sub_pattern":"C24 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Hold an iterative/AR generative backbone fixed and treat its operating representation space as the free variable — specifically 'move refinement out of raw output space into a redesigned latent space' while holding backbone, objective, data, and compute fixed so the new space is the only moving part.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism Leg 1 holds the decoder-only transformer backbone, next-step objective form, data, and compute fixed and changes ONLY the AR step's prediction space from a discrete-vocab softmax to a continuous next-vector z_t = g_θ(h_t), with the modality-rate router as the native-rate decode — this is exactly C24's 'move refinement into a redesigned latent space' signature move, single-variable.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved paper tests whether the per-step prediction target in a joint speech-text transformer must be a discrete token at all — every joint-LM leaf (interleaved, parallel, dMel-tokenized, KD-distilled) silently inherits the assumption that the shared modeling substrate is a discrete vocabulary, and none asks whether that discreteness is necessary rather than assumed (subtractive; reads off the shared discrete-substrate ancestor node n2).","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Audit the representational LOCUS at which a property is presumed enforced and relocate the load-bearing signal to a different locus the field treated as invariant — 'relocate the signal', 're-anchor enforcement', then give a mechanistic account of why the new locus carries it.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism Leg 2 states 'the joint speech-text substrate must be discrete' as falsifiable and relocates the shared modeling signal from the discrete-token vocabulary locus to the continuous-latent locus z_t, then (companion C02) ships the byte-matched continuous-vs-discrete twin and causal-mediation read-out as the de-confounded measurement — the C01 'relocate the locus + mechanistic why' move is present.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries instantiate their cluster's signature move: C24's redesign-the-operating-space-only move is enacted by the discrete→continuous next-vector swap under matched backbone/data/compute, and C01's relocate-the-locus move is enacted by moving the shared substrate from the discrete vocabulary to the continuous latent with a mechanistic account."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["generative_process_redesign","assumption_audit_and_pivot","controlled_diagnostic_design"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"None of the three reject-favored compositions matches — all three require heterogeneous_decomposition, which is absent from the composition_set."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"no_threat_found","threat_source":"n/a","subsumption_argument":null,"addressable_via":null}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# One Latent, Two Rates: A Continuous Shared Substrate for Joint Speech-Text Transformers\n\n**Method.** Continuous Shared Substrate (CSS) for joint speech-text modeling\n\n## Motivation\nA joint speech-text model has to handle two streams that disagree on timing and form. Speech comes in as sound frames at about 12.5 to 25 frames per second, and when speech is chopped into discrete sound tokens those fire roughly five to ten times for every one subword text token. Today's joint models cope by forcing both streams onto a single shared timeline of discrete tokens that neither stream really fits. The closest reference model — an ASR (Automatic Speech Recognition) study that compares 'interleaved' versus 'parallel' layouts of these discrete tokens inside one Speech LM (Language Model) — finds interleaving works best, but it keeps the discrete tokens fixed and only shuffles their arrangement, so it documents a sequence-length blowup it cannot get rid of.\n\nThe other recent systems inherit the same discrete bottleneck. dMel just simplifies how speech is turned into discrete tokens, but it still throws away fine continuous acoustic detail at the quantization step. Text-to-Talk admits that one shared discrete next-token rule cannot fit both modalities, so it splits into a text path and a separate audio-diffusion path — it dodges the mismatch instead of absorbing it, and text stays discrete. CALM (Continuous Autoregressive Language Model) showed you can predict a continuous vector each step instead of a discrete token — but only for text, at a single rate.\n\nSo there are two untouched gaps, and they add up. First, no joint speech-text model has a single continuous per-step target that both speech and text read into and out of at their own natural rate, which is why the rate mismatch and the quantization loss are never fixed together. Second, nobody has even tested whether the shared per-step target has to be discrete at all — every system just assumes it. We do both: we build the continuous shared target, and then we run a clean matched experiment to test whether its continuity (not the old discreteness) is what actually bridges speech and text. This is timely because the three needed pieces only recently all became available together: CALM (October 2025) proved continuous next-vector prediction trains well; dMel (July 2024) made clear the speech-side discreteness is a choice, not a law; and Do-Factual-Recall (May 2026) gave a causal-mediation test that checks whether a fact written in speech can be read back out in text — exactly the cross-modal score this audit needs. If it works, joint models stop paying the interleaving length tax, stop discarding acoustic detail, give CALM its first cross-modal use, and turn the known 'recall is modality-dependent' finding into a design lever for making recall modality-agnostic.\n\n## Method\n### Continuous shared substrate\n*Replace the discrete per-step target with one continuous latent $z_{t}$ that both modalities read into and out of at their native rate.*\n\n1. Take a 300M-parameter decoder-only transformer (a standard text-style Transformer that predicts left-to-right) and remove its final discrete-token output layer. In its place add a small projection network $g_\\theta : a$ 2-layer perceptron (1024 $\\to  4096$ with a GELU activation $\\to $ 1024) that reads the model's last internal state $h_{t}$ and outputs a continuous vector $z_{t}$ of length 1024, with a normalization at the end so its scale matches what the decoders expect. From now on each step predicts this continuous vector instead of choosing a discrete token, and it is trained through the decoders downstream, not against a fixed target vector.\n\n*The per-step continuous target $z_{t}$ is a small modality-shared projection $g_\\theta $ of the backbone's last hidden state $h_{t},$ replacing the discrete-vocabulary softmax with a continuous next-vector readout of dimension 1024.*\n$$ z_t = g_\\theta(h_t), \\quad z_t \\in \\mathbb{R}^{1024} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: If the per-step target is a continuous vector, nothing has to be quantized, so the quantization loss that all discrete systems pay simply never happens.\n2. Add a very small gate network $r_\\phi $ that reads the same internal state $h_{t}$ and decides, for the current step, whether this position is speech or text: a single linear layer followed by a 2-way softmax. During training make the choice soft (Gumbel-softmax, a differentiable near-discrete pick, at temperature 1.0) so gradients flow; at test time take the hard choice (argmax). Train this gate with a cross-entropy against the true modality of each position — every training position is known to be speech or text — which both sends the continuous vector to exactly one decoder and stops the model from always picking one modality. As a result speech and text each move the shared stream forward at their own natural rate inside a single sequence, instead of being forced onto one shared clock.\n\n*A tiny gate head $r_\\phi $ predicts a 2-way modality gate $m_{t}$ from $h_{t}$ (Gumbel-softmax at temperature $\\tau  = 1.0$ in training, argmax at inference); only the gated decoder consumes $z_{t},$ so each modality advances the shared latent stream at its own native rate.*\n$$ m_t = \\arg\\max\\, r_\\phi(h_t), \\quad m_t \\in \\{\\text{speech}, \\text{text}\\} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Letting each modality move at its own rate means you never pad speech and text onto a common clock, which is what caused the interleaving length blowup.\n3. Connect two output decoders. For speech, use a pretrained mel/EnCodec-style decoder (EnCodec is a standard neural audio codec) running at the natural 12.5–25 frames-per-second rate; because that decoder expects codec latents rather than an arbitrary 1024-vector, insert a single linear adapter layer that maps $z_{t}$ into the decoder's own latent space first. For text, use a linear layer plus softmax over the subword vocabulary that reads $z_{t}$ directly. Start both decoders from pretrained weights and fine-tune them together with the backbone. Each continuous vector produces exactly one output of the gated modality at its own rate — one speech frame or one text subword.\n   - _Why_: Reading the same latent out through two native-rate heads lets one continuous vector serve speech and text without forcing either onto the other's timing.\n4. Train the whole system end-to-end with one combined loss: $1.0 \\times $ squared-error between the speech decoder's output and the true speech, plus $1.0 \\times $ cross-entropy between the text decoder's output and the true text, plus $0.1 \\times $ the gate's modality cross-entropy. Use next-step teacher forcing on the continuous vector over a mix of paired and unpaired speech-text data (a subset of LibriHeavy plus a text corpus). For paired examples, lay out one sequence of positions in time order — speech frames at 12.5–25 frames-per-second aligned to their text subwords using the corpus's existing alignment — and tag each position with its modality so the gate is supervised; apply each position's loss only through the decoder the gate selects. Unpaired text or speech examples are single-modality sequences. This trains the real generated speech and text, not just a hidden vector. 【author decision: exactly how a paired example is ordered — strictly time-aligned interleaving of speech and text vs a speech-block-then-text-block layout — is left to the authors, trading off alignment supervision against a more regular sequence.】\n\n*The per-step loss is a convex combination of an L2 speech-reconstruction term through the speech decoder $D_{s}, a$ cross-entropy text term through the text decoder $D_{x},$ and a gate term, with $\\lambda _{s} =$ 1.0, $\\lambda _{x} =$ 1.0, $\\lambda _{m} = 0.1$ bridging the L2 and cross-entropy units.*\n$$ \\mathcal{L} = \\lambda_s\\, \\lVert D_s(z_t) - x_t^{\\text{speech}} \\rVert_2^2 + \\lambda_x\\, \\mathrm{CE}\\big(D_x(z_t),\\, x_t^{\\text{text}}\\big) + \\lambda_m\\, \\mathcal{L}_{\\text{gate}} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: One shared objective on $z_{t}$ is what lets a single target absorb both the rate mismatch and the quantization loss at the same time, instead of splitting into two paths.\n\n### Length-and-quality check\n*Show the continuous substrate beats interleaving on sequence length with no ASR/TTS regression under a matched backbone.*\n\n5. Compare the continuous model against an interleaved discrete-token baseline built from the same 300M backbone, where speech is turned into discrete tokens by a standard tokenizer (EnCodec or HuBERT, common neural speech tokenizers) on the same paired data. Make the two runs use the same total compute by matching optimizer steps, tokens per step, and GPU-hours. Then report three things: the average number of positions per spoken utterance (sequence length), the speech-recognition word-error-rate (WER, the fraction of words wrong) on held-out data, and a text-to-speech quality score from an automatic listening-quality predictor such as UTMOS. The expectation is much shorter sequences with no drop in recognition or synthesis quality.\n   - _Why_: Removing two bottlenecks is only convincing if the continuous model clearly beats the discrete layout on length without losing primary quality.\n\n### Discreteness audit\n*Build a byte-matched discrete twin and a causal-mediation probe to test whether continuity, not capacity, bridges speech and text.*\n\n6. Make a discrete 'twin' of the trained model that is identical except its per-step target is quantized. First estimate how many bits the continuous vector effectively carries per step: fit a simple density (a Gaussian, or a small normalizing flow) to the trained model's vectors and read off its entropy in bits per step. Set the quantizer's codebook to 2 raised to that many bits' worth of entries (one big codebook, or a stack of residual quantizers whose entries multiply to the same count) so the discrete twin carries the same per-step information. Retrain it from the same random seed with the backbone, data, tokenizer rate, decoders, and total compute kept exactly the same — so the only thing that changes is whether the target is continuous or discrete.\n\n*The byte-matched discrete twin replaces the continuous target $z_{t}$ with a vector quantization $VQ(z_{t})$ whose codebook size is chosen so its bit-rate matches $z_{t}'s$ effective bit-rate, leaving the substrate's discreteness as the only varying factor.*\n$$ \\tilde{z}_t = \\mathrm{VQ}(z_t), \\quad \\text{s.t. } \\mathrm{bitrate}(\\tilde{z}_t) \\approx \\mathrm{bitrate}_{\\text{eff}}(z_t) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Matching everything except discreteness is the only way to credit any gain to continuity rather than to a bigger model or more data.\n7. Test whether a fact learned in one modality can be retrieved in the other. Build 500 simple facts, each a (subject, relation, object) triple, and make two versions of each — a short synthesized speech clip and a text string. Present a fact in one modality and ask for its object in the other. To check the mechanism, run the model once with the fact present and once with it absent, then copy the model's internal state at the subject's position from the fact-present run into the fact-absent run and see if the correct object now appears in the target modality. Score cross-modal factual-consistency as the fraction of facts whose object comes out correctly in the opposite modality (exact text match, or speech transcribed by ASR and matched). Report this score for the continuous twin and the discrete twin, and the gap between them as the main result.\n   - _Why_: Whether a fact written in speech survives read-out in text is the cleanest direct test of whether the substrate truly bridges the two modalities.\n8. Hold the comparison fair by matching parameter count, number of training tokens, and GPU-hours across the continuous and discrete twins, then report all results together: how much shorter the sequences are, the speech-recognition word-error-rate, the synthesis quality, and the continuous-minus-discrete gap in cross-modal factual-consistency. Also run a positive control: take the continuous model, remove the modality gate, and use one shared output head that at every step produces both a speech frame and a text distribution, picking the right one by the already-known modality label instead of a learned router; train it under the same parameters, data, and compute. Because this keeps only the continuity of the vector as the active ingredient, it should recover most of the cross-modal advantage. 【author decision: whether this shared-head control still gets each modality's native-rate supervision or a single common down-sampled rate is left to the authors, depending on how aggressively the architecture is stripped.】\n   - _Why_: Reporting everything under matched budgets, with both a negative and a positive control, turns the headline number into a clean identification of continuity as the bridge.\n\n### Continuity negative control\n*Quantize $z_{t}$ at inference only to isolate continuity of the per-step target as the load-bearing variable.*\n\n9. As a control that turns continuity off without retraining, take the finished continuous model and, just before each decoder reads the vector, snap that vector to its nearest entry in the discrete twin's codebook (the same codebook from the twin-building step) — leave every weight untouched. Then re-measure cross-modal factual-consistency and speech-recognition word-error-rate. Reusing the twin's own codebook (rather than some new quantizer) makes sure the test isolates continuity itself. The prediction is about these end-task scores, not the vector's quantization error: if continuity is what mattered, snapping the vector should push cross-modal consistency down toward the discrete twin's level.\n   - _Why_: If turning continuity off at the last moment erases the advantage, continuity itself — not capacity or data — must be what carried it.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 一个潜变量，两种速率：用于联合语音-文本 Transformer 的连续共享基底\n\n**方法名称.** Continuous Shared Substrate (CSS) for joint speech-text modeling\n\n## 研究动机\n联合语音-文本模型必须同时处理两条在时序和形态上都不一致的数据流。语音以每秒约 12.5 到 25 帧的声学帧进入；当语音被切成离散声学 token 时，平均每一个子词文本 token 对应大约五到十个语音 token。如今的联合模型靠把两条流都强行塞进同一条离散 token 时间线来应对，而这条时间线对哪一方都不真正合适。最接近的参考模型是一项 ASR（Automatic Speech Recognition，自动语音识别）研究，它在同一个 Speech LM（Language Model，语言模型）里比较离散 token 的 interleaved（交错）与 parallel（并行）排布，发现交错最好——但它把离散 token 固定不动，只重排它们，因此只是记录下了它无法消除的序列长度膨胀。\n\n其他近期系统继承了同样的离散瓶颈。dMel 只是简化了把语音变成离散 token 的方式，但仍在量化那一步丢掉了精细的连续声学细节。Text-to-Talk 承认单一的离散 next-token 规则无法同时适配两种模态，于是拆成一条文本路径和一条独立的音频扩散路径——它绕开了不匹配而不是吸收它，而且文本仍是离散的。CALM（Continuous Autoregressive Language Model，连续自回归语言模型）证明了每一步可以预测一个连续向量而非离散 token——但只针对文本、只在单一速率上。\n\n因此存在两个尚未触及、且可叠加的空白。第一，没有任何联合语音-文本模型拥有一个让语音和文本都以各自原生速率读入读出的单一连续 per-step 目标，这正是速率不匹配与量化损失从未被一并解决的原因。第二，没人测试过这个共享 per-step 目标是否必须是离散的——每个系统都直接假定如此。我们两件事都做：先构建连续共享目标，再做一个干净的对照匹配实验，检验是它的连续性（而非旧的离散性）真正在语音与文本之间架起了桥。这件事此刻可行，是因为三块必要拼图最近才同时齐备：CALM（2025 年 10 月）证明连续 next-vector 预测训练得很好；dMel（2024 年 7 月）表明语音侧的离散性是一种选择而非定律；Do-Factual-Recall（2026 年 5 月）提供了一个 causal-mediation（因果中介）测试，用来检查写在语音里的一个事实能否在文本里被读回——正是这套审计所需的跨模态指标。若成立，联合模型将不再支付交错带来的长度税、不再丢弃声学细节、给 CALM 带来首个跨模态用法，并把已知的『召回依赖模态』结论变成一个让召回与模态无关的设计杠杆。\n\n## 方法\n### 连续共享基底\n*用一个连续潜变量 $z_{t}$ 替换离散 per-step 目标，让两种模态都以各自原生速率读入读出。*\n\n1. 取一个 300M 参数的 decoder-only Transformer（一种从左到右预测的标准文本式 Transformer），去掉它最后的离散 token 输出层。在原位加一个小型投影网络 $g_\\theta $：一个两层感知机(1024 $\\to  4096$，配 GELU 激活 $\\to $ 1024)，读取模型最后一层内部状态 $h_{t}$，输出一个长度为 1024 的连续向量 $z_{t}$，末端加一个归一化(LayerNorm)使其尺度与解码器期望的输入范围一致。从此每一步预测的是这个连续向量，而不是选一个离散 token；它通过下游解码器端到端训练，而非对齐到某个固定目标向量。\n\n*每一步的连续目标 $z_{t}$ 由 backbone 最后一层隐状态 $h_{t}$ 经一个模态共享的小投影头 $g_\\theta $ 得到，用维度为 1024 的连续 next-vector 读出替换原本的离散词表 softmax。*\n$$ z_t = g_\\theta(h_t), \\quad z_t \\in \\mathbb{R}^{1024} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 如果 per-step 目标是连续向量，就没有任何东西需要量化，于是所有离散系统都要付出的量化损失根本不会发生。\n2. 加一个非常小的门控网络 $r_\\phi $，它读取同一个内部状态 $h_{t}$，判断当前这一步属于 speech 还是 text：一个线性层接一个二元 softmax。训练时让选择是软的(Gumbel-softmax，一种可微的近离散选取，温度取 1.0)以便梯度回传；测试时取硬选择(argmax)。用一个对真实模态的交叉熵(cross-entropy)来训练这个门控——每个训练位置本就已知是 speech 还是 text——这既把连续向量送往恰好一个解码器，也防止模型总是只选一种模态。于是 speech 与 text 在同一条序列里各自以原生速率推进共享流，而不必被强行对齐到同一个时钟。\n\n*一个极小的门控头 $r_\\phi $ 从 $h_{t}$ 预测二元模态门 $m_{t}$（训练时用温度 $\\tau  = 1.0$ 的 Gumbel-softmax，推理时取 argmax）；只有被选中的解码器消费 $z_{t}$，因此每种模态都以自己的原生速率推进共享潜变量流。*\n$$ m_t = \\arg\\max\\, r_\\phi(h_t), \\quad m_t \\in \\{\\text{speech}, \\text{text}\\} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 让每种模态按自己的速率前进，就不必把语音和文本对齐到同一个时钟——而那正是交错造成长度膨胀的根源。\n3. 接上两个输出解码器。语音用一个预训练的 mel/EnCodec 风格解码器(EnCodec 是一种标准神经音频编解码器)，运行在自然的每秒 12.5–25 帧速率；由于该解码器期望的是 codec latent 而非任意的 1024 维向量，先插入一个线性适配层把 $z_{t}$ 映射进解码器自己的潜空间。文本用一个线性层加在子词词表上的 softmax，直接读取 $z_{t}$。两个解码器都从预训练权重出发，与 backbone 一起微调。每个连续向量恰好产生被门控选中模态的一个输出、以其各自速率——一个语音帧或一个文本子词。\n   - _为什么_: 用两个原生速率的头读出同一个潜变量，让一个连续向量同时服务语音与文本，而不强迫任何一方迁就对方的时序。\n4. 端到端训练整个系统，使用一个组合损失：$1.0 \\times $ 语音解码器输出与真实语音之间的平方误差，加 $1.0 \\times $ 文本解码器输出与真实文本之间的交叉熵，再加 $0.1 \\times $ 门控的模态交叉熵。在成对与非成对语音-文本数据的混合(LibriHeavy 的一个子集加一个文本语料)上，对连续向量做 next-step teacher forcing。对成对样本，按时间顺序排成一条位置序列——12.5–25 帧每秒的语音帧，借助语料已有的对齐(forced alignment)与其文本子词对齐——并为每个位置打上模态标签以监督门控；每个位置的损失只通过门控选中的解码器回传。非成对的文本或语音样本则是单模态序列。这样训练的是真实生成的语音与文本，而不仅是一个隐藏向量。【作者需决定：成对样本的具体排序——严格时间对齐的语音/文本交错，还是先语音块后文本块——留给作者，在对齐监督与序列规整之间权衡。】\n\n*每一步损失是三项的凸组合：经语音解码器 $D_{s}$ 的 L2 语音重建项、经文本解码器 $D_{x}$ 的交叉熵文本项、以及门控项，权重 $\\lambda _{s} = 1.0$、$\\lambda _{x} = 1.0$、$\\lambda _{m} = 0.1$，用以衔接 L2 与交叉熵两种量纲。*\n$$ \\mathcal{L} = \\lambda_s\\, \\lVert D_s(z_t) - x_t^{\\text{speech}} \\rVert_2^2 + \\lambda_x\\, \\mathrm{CE}\\big(D_x(z_t),\\, x_t^{\\text{text}}\\big) + \\lambda_m\\, \\mathcal{L}_{\\text{gate}} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 在 $z_{t}$ 上的单一目标，正是让一个目标同时吸收速率不匹配与量化损失的关键，而非拆成两条路径。\n\n### 长度与质量检验\n*在对齐 backbone 下证明连续基底在序列长度上胜过交错且无 ASR/TTS 退化。*\n\n5. 把连续模型与一个交错离散 token 基线对比，该基线由同一个 300M backbone 构成，语音用标准 tokenizer(EnCodec 或 HuBERT，常见的神经语音 tokenizer)在相同成对数据上离散化。通过对齐 optimizer 步数、每步 token 数与 GPU 小时，使两次训练用相同总算力。然后报告三项：每条话语的平均位置数(序列长度)、留出集上的语音识别词错误率(Word-Error-Rate, WER，即出错词的比例)、以及来自自动听感质量预测器(如 UTMOS)的语音合成质量分。预期是序列大幅变短，且识别与合成质量都不退化。\n   - _为什么_: 同时移除两个瓶颈只有在连续模型于长度上明显胜过离散排布、且不损失主要质量时才令人信服。\n\n### 离散性审计\n*构建字节对齐的离散孪生与 causal-mediation 探针，检验是连续性而非容量在连接语音与文本。*\n\n6. 做一个训练好模型的离散『孪生』，除了 per-step 目标被量化之外完全一致。先估计连续向量每步实际携带多少比特：给训练好模型的向量拟合一个简单密度(高斯，或一个小的 normalizing flow)，读出其每步熵(以比特计)。把量化器的码本设为 2 的该比特数次方那么多条目(一个大码本，或一组残差量化器，其条目相乘等于该数)，使离散孪生携带相同的每步信息。用相同随机种子重训，backbone、数据、tokenizer 速率、解码器与总算力都保持完全一致——于是唯一变化的就是目标是连续还是离散。\n\n*字节对齐的离散孪生模型用向量量化 $VQ(z_{t})$ 替换连续目标 $z_{t}$，其码本大小被设定为使比特率与 $z_{t}$ 的有效比特率相当，从而让基底的离散性成为唯一变化的因素。*\n$$ \\tilde{z}_t = \\mathrm{VQ}(z_t), \\quad \\text{s.t. } \\mathrm{bitrate}(\\tilde{z}_t) \\approx \\mathrm{bitrate}_{\\text{eff}}(z_t) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 除离散性外一切对齐，是把任何增益归因于连续性、而非更大模型或更多数据的唯一办法。\n7. 检验在一种模态里学到的事实能否在另一种模态里被取回。构造 500 个简单事实，每个是一个(subject, relation, object)三元组，并各做两个版本——一段合成语音(TTS)与一段文本。在一种模态里给出事实，在另一种模态里询问其 object。为检查机制，让模型分别在『事实在场』与『事实缺席』下各跑一次，然后把 subject 位置上模型的内部状态从『在场』那次拷贝进『缺席』那次，看看正确的 object 是否在目标模态里出现。把跨模态事实一致性记为：在相反模态里正确产出 object 的事实比例(文本用精确匹配，语音用 ASR 转写后匹配)。报告连续孪生与离散孪生各自的这一分数，以及两者之差作为主结果。\n   - _为什么_: 写在语音里的事实能否在文本里读回，是检验基底是否真正连接两种模态的最直接测试。\n8. 为保证对比公平，让连续孪生与离散孪生在参数量、训练 token 数与 GPU 小时上对齐，然后把所有结果一并报告：序列缩短了多少、语音识别词错误率、合成质量、以及跨模态事实一致性上『连续减离散』的差距。再做一个正对照：取连续模型，去掉模态门控，改用一个共享输出头，它每一步同时产出一个语音帧和一个文本分布，靠已知的模态标签(而非学习到的路由)挑选正确的那个；在相同参数、数据与算力下训练它。由于它只保留向量的连续性作为起作用的成分，应能恢复大部分跨模态优势。【作者需决定：这个共享头对照是仍按每模态的原生速率监督，还是用单一的下采样公共速率，留给作者，取决于对架构精简的激进程度。】\n   - _为什么_: 在对齐预算下、配合负对照与正对照报告全部指标，能把头条数字变成对连续性作为桥梁的干净识别。\n\n### 连续性负对照\n*仅在推理时量化 $z_{t}$，以分离 per-step 目标的连续性作为承载性变量。*\n\n9. 作为一个无需重训就关闭连续性的对照，取训练完成的连续模型，在每个解码器读取向量之前，把该向量吸附到离散孪生码本(与造孪生那步同一个码本)里最近的条目——所有权重都不动。然后重新测量跨模态事实一致性与语音识别词错误率。复用孪生自己的码本(而非某个新量化器)能确保这个测试分离的是连续性本身。预测针对的是这些终端任务分数，而非向量自身的量化误差：若起作用的是连续性，吸附向量应把跨模态一致性压向离散孪生的水平。\n   - _为什么_: 若在最后一刻关闭连续性就抹掉了优势，那么承载优势的必然是连续性本身，而非容量或数据。\n\n"},{"id":"68","run_dir":"run_prompt68_visualpriors","index":68,"title":"Localizing Text-Pretrained Visual Priors in a Frozen MLLM Backbone","title_zh":"在冻结的 MLLM 文本骨干中定位语言预训练习得的视觉先验","method_name":"Backbone Visual-Prior Attribution (BVPA)","hook":"We show that an MLLM's visual judgements about relative size, co-occurrence, and color trace to feature directions already present in its text-only backbone before a single image is seen, and that the very directions decode-time methods suppress as a harmful 'language prior' are the ones carrying faithful visual geometry. Suppressing the whole prior axis therefore destroys real visual structure, not just lexical shortcuts.","anchor_pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","anchor_pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","domain_category":"Vision-Language & Multimodal","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a representation-level measurement that attributes a specific visual judgement of an assembled MLLM to a feature direction already present in its text-only backbone before visual instruction tuning — i.e. there is no quantity that separates 'visual structure inherited from language pre-training' from 'visual structure learned during image-tuning' inside the same model.","pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by constructing matched probe instances that hold the backbone weights fixed and vary only the before-vs-after-visual-tuning axis, scored by a model-independent visual oracle, so the measured accuracy divergence is attributable to text-pretrained backbone directions alone — the de-confounded gap is the headline attribution result.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether the visual priors that decode-time methods suppress as harmful are the same representations that, when read faithfully, encode genuine visual geometry (relative size, co-occurrence, color) — the field assumes 'language prior' is a single harmful axis on the logits rather than a structured, partly-faithful representation that could be selectively kept or removed.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by pivoting the prior's representational locus: the same recovered backbone directions are split into visually-faithful versus lexical-shortcut sub-directions, then a constructed demonstration ablates the whole decode-time-suppressed axis and shows it also removes the faithful sub-directions' visual geometry, violating the single-harmful-scalar assumption.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"multimodal large language models / vision-language representation analysis","n_papers":49,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":27},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10},{"source":"openreview","n":2}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":19,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"MiniGPT-3D: Efficiently Aligning 3D Point Clouds with Large Language Models using 2D Priors"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Debiasing Multimodal Large Language Models via Penalization of Language Priors"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Mitigating Object Hallucinations in Large Vision-Language Models through Visual Contrastive Decoding"},{"source":"openalex","title":"LLMFormer: Large Language Model for Open-Vocabulary Semantic Segmentation"},{"source":"openalex","title":"ChatGPT: The End of Online Exam Integrity?"},{"source":"openalex","title":"ViLa-MIL: Dual-scale Vision-Language Multiple Instance Learning for Whole Slide Image Classification"}],"more":13},{"year":2025,"n":25,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"ClearSight: Visual Signal Enhancement for Object Hallucination Mitigation in Multimodal Large Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"LanP: Rethinking the Impact of Language Priors in Large Vision-Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Pixels Versus Priors: Controlling Knowledge Priors in Vision-Language Models through Visual Counterfacts"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Cross-Image Contrastive Decoding: Precise, Lossless Suppression of Language Priors in Large Vision-Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Knowledge-enhanced medical image classification via descriptive priors from large language models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Task-aware Cross-modal Feature Refinement Transformer with Large Language Models for Visual Grounding"}],"more":19},{"year":2026,"n":8,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"},{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"CROP: Token-Efficient Reasoning in Large Language Models via Regularized Prompt Optimization"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Multimodal Survival Analysis with Locally Deployable Large Language Models"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Conversational Control with Ontologies for Large Language Models: A Lightweight Framework for Constrained Generation"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Task-Specific Efficiency Analysis: When Small Language Models Outperform Large Language Models"}],"more":2}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":11,"share":0.224},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":10,"share":0.204},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":7,"share":0.143},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":5,"share":0.102},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":5,"share":0.102},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":4,"share":0.082},{"pattern_id":"targeted_self_supervised_objective","pattern_name":"Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective","count":4,"share":0.082},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":4,"share":0.082}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Across the retrieved frontier, the visual priors an LLM backbone carries from text-only pre-training are treated exclusively as an inference-time nuisance to be detected and suppressed, never as a structured object to be located and characterized: ClearSight (semanticscholar:ecc51ce52ca524be17616a9c0dc8a051a2996ad7) shows via saliency that visual tokens influence predictions mainly through middle-layer interactions with instruction tokens and that visual attention is dominated by language-side attention, and Visual Contrastive Decoding (openalex:W4402753774) plus Cross-Image Contrastive Decoding (semanticscholar:4a68382026854b3dc0530385f402d498207e5c2d) cancel the prior at the output distribution, while LanP (semanticscholar:7335f6d71b28a478866923e9b9e4eadf54b3d395) shows the same priors are sometimes helpful. The shared failure is that all of these operate on the assembled multimodal model at decode time and read the prior only as a scalar bias on the final logits, so when a model's visual judgement is wrong (or right) for a category, no current method can say which text-pretraining-acquired representation produced that judgement, in which backbone sub-space it lives, or whether it encodes genuine visual structure (co-occurrence geometry, relative size, color statistics) versus a lexical shortcut — the quantity that would demystify the prior is never produced.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:ecc51ce52ca524be17616a9c0dc8a051a2996ad7","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"ClearSight runs a saliency + cross-modal attention analysis of an assembled MLLM and finds visual tokens act through middle layers while visual attention is dwarfed by instruction/system attention, then enhances the visual signal at decode time. Its diagnosis stops at the assembled-model attention level on a single forward pass — it never compares the MLLM's visual judgement against the SAME backbone's text-only behaviour, so it cannot attribute any specific visual judgement to a representation acquired during language pre-training versus one acquired during visual instruction tuning. [residue is partly abstract-level: anchor fulltext fetched for ClearSight but the user-referenced ICLR source paper was unfetchable]"},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:9568effdf3cf8b6076ca3c810d2cbc6f9b19bd51","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Pixels Versus Priors builds visual counterfactuals to test whether MLLM answers come from memorized world-knowledge priors or the image, isolating reliance at inference. It measures THAT a prior was used on a given query but not WHERE the prior is stored in the network nor whether the same prior is recoverable from the text-only backbone before any image-tuning."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:7335f6d71b28a478866923e9b9e4eadf54b3d395","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"LanP curates a benchmark showing language priors are sometimes the only way to answer (blur / tiny / occluded objects), reframing priors as partly beneficial. It quantifies net benefit at the task level but offers no representational account of which priors are visually faithful versus lexical shortcuts, so it cannot tell a practitioner which priors to keep and which to suppress."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4402753774","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Visual Contrastive Decoding cancels the language prior by contrasting clean vs distorted visual inputs at decode time, training-free. It removes the prior's effect on logits but produces no map of the prior itself and is blind to priors that never surface as an output error yet still distort internal visual representations."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"multimodal large language models / vision-language representation analysis","venue":"ICLR / NeurIPS / CVPR (mechanistic-interpretability + multimodal track)","time":"2026","data":["open MLLM checkpoints with paired text-only LLM backbones (e.g. LLaVA-style stacks built on Vicuna/Qwen text LLMs)","standard VQA / object-hallucination probes (POPE, MME)","controlled visual-counterfactual probes"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"mechanistic interpretability, vision-language modeling, probing","preference":"both","baseline":"decode-time language-prior suppression methods (Visual Contrastive Decoding, ClearSight, Cross-Image Contrastive Decoding)","limitation":"existing work treats text-acquired visual priors only as an inference-time bias to suppress; it does not localize where in the text-pretrained representation those priors live or characterize what visual structure text pre-training instills","contribution_type":"empirical_reveal","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type","compute"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object both legs read and write is V_b: a set of text-pretrained visual-prior directions recovered inside the frozen text-only LLM backbone B that underlies the assembled MLLM M (e.g. Vicuna/Qwen under a LLaVA stack), expressed as unit vectors in the residual-stream activation space of a fixed layer-set L of B. LEG 1 (C02): we build a confound-isolating probe suite of N matched textual descriptions of visual relations over an attribute set A = {relative-size, co-occurrence, color}, each with a model-independent ground-truth label drawn from an external visual oracle (counts/measurements from annotated images in Visual Genome and a color-statistics table — never from M's own outputs). For each attribute a in A we fit a linear readout w_a (a unit direction in R^d, d = backbone hidden width) on the mean-pooled residual activations h_L(text) of the FROZEN text-only backbone B over a train split, holding everything fixed except the one axis under test; w_a is the property's locus in V_b. The confound being blocked is image-tuning provenance: we compute the SAME readout family on the assembled MLLM M's text-branch activations after visual instruction tuning, giving w_a^M, and report the attribution quantity rho_a = cos(w_a, w_a^M) together with the share of M's correct visual judgements on a held-out probe whose label is predicted by projecting M's activation onto w_a (the pre-tuning direction). A high rho_a and high pre-direction-predicted accuracy means the visual judgement was inherited from language pre-training; a low value means it was learned during image-tuning — the divergence between these two, stratified by attribute, is the headline de-confounded result that no aggregate VQA score exposes. LEG 2 (C01): the field's binding assumption is that the 'language prior' is a single harmful scalar axis p on the final logits (the quantity CICD cancels via JS-divergence between image distributions, and ClearSight amplifies around). We pivot it by decomposing V_b: within each w_a we separate a visually-faithful sub-direction w_a^faith (the component whose projection correlates with the external oracle's continuous label, e.g. true size ratio) from a lexical-shortcut sub-direction w_a^lex (the residual component correlated instead with corpus co-occurrence frequency from a text n-gram count, orthogonalized against w_a^faith via Gram-Schmidt). The constructed demonstration: we ablate the decode-time-suppressed axis — operationalized as activation-level projection-removal of the full V_b span inside M (the representational analogue of what CICD/ClearSight remove at the logits) — run a second forward pass, and measure that visual-judgement accuracy on the faithful probe drops, because w_a^faith was inside the removed span; whereas selectively removing only w_a^lex leaves faithful accuracy intact while reducing hallucination. This violates the single-harmful-scalar view: the suppressed prior is a structured sub-space, part of which carries genuine visual geometry. The two legs share V_b: LEG 1 recovers and attributes it; LEG 2 splits it and shows the cost of suppressing it wholesale. The bridging hyperparameter is lambda_orth, the variance threshold (default 0.05) below which a residual component is discarded as noise rather than assigned to w_a^lex.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery because both are statements about the SAME recovered object V_b — gap 1 needs it to exist and be attributable (recover + measure provenance), gap 2 needs it to be internally structured (split + show suppression cost); evidence that they share rather than need separate modules is that w_a^faith / w_a^lex are literally sub-components of the leg-1 direction w_a, so leg 2 cannot run without leg 1's readout. (b) Considered designs: (i) a question-only logit-subtraction baseline — rejected, it regresses to method_lineage node n0 (RUBi) and produces a scalar bias, not a representational locus; (ii) amplifying under-attended visual tokens via attention/saliency — rejected, it regresses to node n2 (ClearSight) and never references the frozen text-only backbone; (iii) a pure linear-probe-fit with no before/after-tuning contrast — rejected because it lands on existing collateral node c0 (linear concept directions). The avoided nodes (n0, n2, c0) are recorded here; our load-bearing artifact draws on the frozen pre-image-tuning backbone sub-space, which the lineage tree does not yet occupy.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: take LLaVA-1.5 and its frozen Vicuna backbone, the 3-attribute probe suite, and POPE; compute the attribution table (step 5) and the two suppression runs (steps 7-8). If the candidate works, the de-confounded pre-direction-predicted accuracy is well above chance for at least one attribute (the visual judgement was inherited from text pre-training, not learned at image-tuning), and full-axis representational suppression LOWERS faithful-probe accuracy while shortcut-only suppression keeps it near baseline yet still reduces POPE hallucination. The named load-bearing variable is w_a^faith, the visually-faithful sub-direction. Negative control: replace w_a^faith with a random unit direction in the same residual space (oracle-replace its producer with noise) before the selective-suppression run; the mechanism predicts faithful-probe visual-judgement accuracy then collapses toward the full-suppression level rather than staying at baseline, because a random direction cannot protect genuine visual geometry. Positive control: a stripped readout that uses ONLY w_a^faith to predict the visual label should recover most of the attribution-table accuracy, converting the falsifier into a constructive identification of the locus. If randomizing w_a^faith leaves downstream accuracy unchanged, the claim that faithful visual geometry lives in that specific sub-direction is false.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:ecc51ce52ca524be17616a9c0dc8a051a2996ad7","delta":"ClearSight diagnoses prior reliance via saliency and cross-modal attention on the assembled model in a single forward pass and then amplifies visual tokens at decode time; we instead recover named feature directions in the frozen text-only backbone and attribute specific visual judgements to pre-image-tuning provenance, a representation-level object their attention analysis never constructs."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:4a68382026854b3dc0530385f402d498207e5c2d","delta":"CICD cancels the prior by JS-divergence between original and cross-image logit distributions at each decode step; we show the suppressed axis is a structured backbone sub-space and that removing it wholesale destroys faithful visual geometry, a cost their logit-space cancellation cannot see."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:7335f6d71b28a478866923e9b9e4eadf54b3d395","delta":"LanP measures the net task-level benefit of language priors on hard-visibility benchmarks; we provide the representational account it lacks — which prior sub-directions are visually faithful versus lexical shortcuts — so a practitioner can tell which to keep and which to remove."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:9568effdf3cf8b6076ca3c810d2cbc6f9b19bd51","delta":"Pixels-Versus-Priors measures THAT a memorized prior was used on a query via visual counterfactuals at inference; we measure WHERE the prior lives (a backbone direction) and whether it is recoverable from the text-only backbone before any image-tuning, which their inference-time test does not localize."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:ecc51ce52ca524be17616a9c0dc8a051a2996ad7","what_step_was_missed":"ClearSight stops at an assembled-model attention/saliency readout on one forward pass; to already contain our contribution it would have needed to fit a representational readout on the SAME backbone's text-only activations before visual instruction tuning and compute the before/after-tuning direction-similarity attribution — a frozen-pre-tuning-backbone measurement primitive it never constructs, leaving it unable to assign any visual judgement to a text-pretrained direction."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":300,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"No hard-floor rule fired: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict=clear (both legs neutralize their Reject lessons, e.g. the C02 ecological-validity lesson is answered by step-10 real-data transfer and the C01 assertion-without-demonstration lesson by the constructed full-vs-selective ablation), recipe_application_check.verdict=applied for both legs, anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id=null, and paper_pointed_threat (HaloProbe) is non-exact-mechanism overlap with addressable_via=null because the candidate's frozen-backbone before/after attribution and faithful/shortcut split are not produced by it. All checks clear, so advance.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a representation-level measurement that attributes a specific visual judgement of an assembled MLLM to a feature direction already present in its text-only backbone before visual instruction tuning — i.e. there is no quantity that separates 'visual structure inherited from language pre-training' from 'visual structure learned during image-tuning' inside the same model.","main_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail most often when the instrument isolates the confound only inside an artificial regime and never shows the signal transfers to real deployment, or when it is circular (validated against the same population/definition it interrogates), or merely re-confirms an already-documented limitation.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A diagnostic that only re-confirms a shortcut already known in advance, surfacing no previously unmeasurable failure, is read as confirmatory rather than as a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The before/after-visual-tuning direction-similarity attribution (rho_a) and the pre-direction-predicted accuracy are quantities no prior leaf produces; they reveal which visual judgements were inherited from text pre-training, a previously unmeasurable split, not a re-confirmation."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a synthetic-ground-truth instrument only on synthetic data, without demonstrating that the controlled finding transfers to real-world instances, leaves ecological validity unestablished and undermines the central claim.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism_steps step 10 explicitly reruns the attribution and suppression on real VQA/MME items and reports the stratified gap persists outside the controlled regime, supplying the synthetic-to-real transfer the lesson demands."},{"lesson_quoted":"Building the instrument around one contested definition of the target property means it cannot independently confirm that the definition is correct, and reviewers flag the resulting circularity.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Ground truth is an external visual oracle (Visual Genome size/co-occurrence annotations, a color-statistics table) independent of M, not M's own consensus, so the diagnostic is not circular."},{"lesson_quoted":"Resting an unsupervised evaluation on the unverified premise that the systems under test can reliably judge one another stakes the entire method on an assumption that collapses under scrutiny.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Labels come from the external oracle, never from M judging itself or peer models."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pairing a single-task or small-sample instrument with broad capability claims triggers a scope-mismatch rejection, and assembling retrieval or engineering blocks without an isolating scientific insight reads as application rather than research.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Claims are bounded to the three probed attributes (relative-size, co-occurrence, color) and to the attribution/suppression findings; no broad capability claim is attached, and the isolating insight is the frozen-backbone before/after axis."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether the visual priors that decode-time methods suppress as harmful are the same representations that, when read faithfully, encode genuine visual geometry (relative size, co-occurrence, color) — the field assumes 'language prior' is a single harmful axis on the logits rather than a structured, partly-faithful representation that could be selectively kept or removed.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"C01 papers fail when the audited assumption is a strawman nobody actually holds, when the pivot is asserted rather than demonstrated by a constructed counter-instance, or when the new framing is not shown to change any downstream behavior.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Auditing an assumption that no one in the field actually relies on produces a strawman pivot with no force.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The single-harmful-scalar-on-logits assumption is load-bearing for the cited baselines (CICD cancels a logit distribution, ClearSight amplifies around it), so the audited assumption is genuinely held."},{"lesson_quoted":"Asserting the inverted assumption without a constructed demonstration that violates the old assumption leaves the pivot unsupported.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate constructs the demonstration: ablating the full V_b span drops faithful-probe accuracy while shortcut-only removal preserves it, a concrete counter-instance to the single-axis view."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pivoting the framing without showing the new view changes any measurable downstream behavior reduces the contribution to relabeling.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The pivot changes measurable behavior: selective shortcut-only suppression keeps faithful visual-judgement accuracy at baseline while still cutting POPE hallucination, a practitioner-actionable outcome the single-axis view cannot deliver."}],"verdict":"clear"}],"verdict":"clear","reasoning":"Both gap_closure entries are clear. The C02 leg neutralizes the ecological-validity and circularity Reject lessons via the external visual oracle (step 1) and the real-data transfer check (step 10); the C01 leg neutralizes the strawman and assertion-without-demonstration lessons via the constructed full-vs-selective ablation that produces a measurable downstream split."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a representation-level measurement that attributes a specific visual judgement of an assembled MLLM to a feature direction already present in its text-only backbone before visual instruction tuning — i.e. there is no quantity that separates 'visual structure inherited from language pre-training' from 'visual structure learned during image-tuning' inside the same model.","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Construct a controlled instance set in which exactly one named confound is blocked or independently varied while everything else is held fixed, score with an oracle independent of the system under test, and report the divergence between apparent and de-confounded performance as the headline result.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism LEG 1 names the confound (image-tuning provenance), holds the backbone weights fixed and varies only the before/after-visual-tuning axis, scores with an external oracle (Visual Genome / color-statistics, not M), and reports rho_a plus pre-direction-predicted accuracy stratified by attribute as the de-confounded headline divergence — the C02 signature move is performed, not the parent's generic 'measure something carefully'.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether the visual priors that decode-time methods suppress as harmful are the same representations that, when read faithfully, encode genuine visual geometry (relative size, co-occurrence, color) — the field assumes 'language prior' is a single harmful axis on the logits rather than a structured, partly-faithful representation that could be selectively kept or removed.","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Surface a binding, usually-unstated assumption the field relies on, violate it with a constructed demonstration, and show the resulting new behavior the old assumption forbids.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism LEG 2 surfaces the binding assumption (the prior is a single harmful scalar p on the logits), violates it by decomposing V_b into faithful and shortcut sub-directions and ablating the full span vs the shortcut-only span, and shows the forbidden new behavior (faithful accuracy survives shortcut-only removal while hallucination still drops) — the C01 surface/violate/show move is performed.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both legs perform their cited cluster's signature move: C02's confound-isolation-with-independent-oracle is realized by the frozen-backbone before/after axis scored by the external visual oracle, and C01's surface-violate-show is realized by the constructed full-vs-selective ablation."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["controlled_diagnostic_design","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"The composition (controlled_diagnostic_design + assumption_audit_and_pivot) does not match any of the three reject-favored compositions (audit_decomp_supervisor / audit_decomp_prior / audit_decomp_operator), all of which require a decompose-and-delegate leg that is absent here."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"openalex:W7152933903","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"HaloProbe is the closest retrieved threat: it is a Bayesian framework that factorizes external description statistics and internal decoding signals to estimate token-level object-hallucination probability in a vision-language model, explicitly handling hidden confounders (token position, object repetition). It overlaps in spirit (confound-aware internal-signal analysis of VLM priors) but stands clear of the candidate's claim: HaloProbe estimates a per-token hallucination probability on the ASSEMBLED model's decoding signals and never recovers feature directions in the FROZEN text-only backbone, never computes a before/after-visual-tuning direction-similarity attribution, and never splits the prior into visually-faithful versus lexical-shortcut sub-directions. The candidate's load-bearing artifact (V_b recovered pre-image-tuning plus the faithful/shortcut decomposition) is therefore not produced by HaloProbe, so the candidate's claim stands.","addressable_via":null}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Localizing Text-Pretrained Visual Priors in a Frozen MLLM Backbone\n\n**Method.** Backbone Visual-Prior Attribution (BVPA)\n\n## Motivation\nMultimodal large language models (MLLMs) are language models that have been taught to also read images. A surprising fact is that even before such a model sees any picture, its underlying text-only language model already 'knows' things about the visual world from reading text alone — for example that grass is usually green, that a person is taller than a dog, or that forks tend to appear near plates. Researchers call this baggage the 'language prior.'\n\nUntil now, the field has treated this prior purely as a problem to be erased at the moment the model answers. Methods like ClearSight (CVPR 2025) and Cross-Image Contrastive Decoding (Cross-Image CD, 2025) detect when the model is leaning on its text habits instead of the actual image, and push those habits down at the output stage. LanP (2025) pointed out that the same habits are sometimes the only thing that lets a model answer when an object is blurry or tiny. But all of these work on the finished model at answer time and treat the prior as a single dial on the output, so none of them can say where inside the network a particular visual belief lives, or whether that belief is actually correct geometry (real size, real color) versus a mere word-association shortcut.\n\nWhat makes this answerable now is that open models such as LLaVA-1.5 (built on the Vicuna text model) and Qwen-VL (built on Qwen) ship with their original text-only brain available, before any image training. That lets us compare the same brain before and after it learned to see, inside one model rather than across unrelated models. We propose Backbone Visual-Prior Attribution (BVPA): we fit simple linear readers on the frozen text-only brain to recover the directions that encode size, co-occurrence, and color, check how much of the finished model's visual judgement those pre-existing directions already explain, and then split each direction into the part that holds real visual geometry versus the part that is just a word shortcut.\n\nIf this works, the payoff is concrete: instead of bluntly erasing the whole prior (which we predict also erases real visual knowledge), a practitioner could surgically remove only the misleading word-shortcut part and keep the genuinely useful visual part — turning today's all-or-nothing suppression into a precise keep-some, remove-some operation.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n*Set up checkpoints, probes, and the real-data transfer check.*\n\n1. Load the finished multimodal large language model (MLLM) M (e.g. LLaVA-1.5) together with its exact original text-only model B (Vicuna) as it was before any image training, with all weights frozen. Then build an outside source of visual truth from Visual Genome (VG): a relative-size table (how much bigger one object's box is than another's, on average), a co-occurrence table (how often two objects show up in the same image), and a color table (each object's most common color plus an 11-bucket color histogram measured from the object's actual pixels).\n   - _Why_: To attribute a belief to text pre-training you need the literal brain as it was before it ever saw an image.\n2. For each of the three attributes (relative size, co-occurrence, color), write 2000 matched short sentences (1600 for fitting, 400 held out for testing) from one fixed fill-in-the-blank template with two object slots and one relation slot. Each sentence gets a yes/no label and a numeric label straight from the outside truth tables. Keep the wording identical when you later run it through the before- and after-image-training models, so any difference can only come from image training.\n   - _Why_: Holding everything else fixed makes any measured difference attributable to image-training provenance alone.\n3. Finally, run the same attribution and both suppression tests on real images from VQA and MME — but only on questions that are about relative size, co-occurrence, or color — using the same outside truth tables to label them. Check that the same pattern (same direction of effect per attribute) shows up on real data, not just on the synthetic sentences.\n   - _Why_: A finding that only holds on synthetic probes would not be trustworthy in real use.\n\n### Prior Recovery\n*Recover the text-pretrained visual-prior directions from the frozen backbone.*\n\n4. Run the frozen text-only model on the training sentences and read out its internal activations at its middle layers (layers 11-21 of a 32-layer model), averaging across tokens and across those layers into one vector per sentence. Fit one straight-line predictor (a unit-length direction $w_{a})$ per attribute that maps this vector to the numeric truth label, using ridge regression. These directions are the recovered visual priors.\n\n*$w_{a}$ is the unit-norm linear readout direction for attribute a, fit by least squares from the frozen backbone's mean-pooled residual activation $h_{L}(x)$ to the oracle label $y_{a}.$*\n$$ w_a = \\frac{\\arg\\min_{w}\\; \\sum_{i}\\big(\\langle w, h_L(x_i)\\rangle - y_a(x_i)\\big)^2}{\\lVert \\cdot \\rVert}, \\quad \\lVert w_a \\rVert = 1 \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: These directions are the recovered visual priors — the object everything else builds on.\n\n### Provenance Attribution\n*Measure how much of the finished model's visual judgement was inherited from text pre-training.*\n\n5. Run the finished model on the same sentences but with no image attached (a text-only turn is allowed), read out the same middle layers, and fit the same kind of direction $w_{a}^{M}$ on it. Then measure the cosine similarity between the before-training direction $w_{a}$ and the after-training direction $w_{a}^{M}$ for each attribute — a value near 1 means the visual structure was already there from text training.\n\n*$\\rho _{a}$ is the attribution scalar: the cosine similarity between the pre-tuning backbone direction $w_{a}$ and the same readout $w_{a}^{M}$ fit on the image-tuned model M; $\\rho _{a}$ near 1 means the visual structure was inherited from text pre-training.*\n$$ \\rho_a = \\cos\\!\\big(w_a, w_a^{M}\\big) = \\frac{\\langle w_a, w_a^{M}\\rangle}{\\lVert w_a\\rVert\\,\\lVert w_a^{M}\\rVert} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A high $\\rho _{a}$ means the visual structure was inherited from text, not learned from images.\n6. On the held-out sentences, take the finished model's activation, score it along the before-training direction $w_{a},$ and turn that score into a yes/no answer using a cutoff tuned on the training set. Report how accurate this is per attribute, compared to the random-guess rate (about 50%). If the old direction already predicts the answer, the judgement came from text pre-training.\n   - _Why_: If the old direction already predicts the answer, the judgement came from text pre-training.\n\n### Faithful/Shortcut Split\n*Decompose each prior direction into a keepable faithful part and a removable shortcut part.*\n\n7. Split each direction into two parts: a faithful part that tracks the real numeric truth (e.g. the actual size ratio), and a shortcut part that instead tracks how often the two words simply co-occur in text. Compute word co-occurrence from a large public text corpus, and keep the shortcut part only if it explains enough variance to be more than noise. 【author decision: which public text corpus (C4, Pile, or another) to use as a stand-in for the model's original training text when measuring how often two words co-occur, since the exact training text is usually not available.】\n\n*The faithful sub-direction is the component of $w_{a}$ whose projection tracks the oracle's continuous label $y_{a}^{cont}$; the lexical-shortcut sub-direction is the Gram-Schmidt residual correlated with corpus co-occurrence frequency $f_{a}^{cooc},$ kept only when its explained variance is $\\ge  \\lambda _{orth}$ (default 0.05).*\n$$ w_a^{\\mathrm{faith}} \\propto \\Pi_{y_a^{\\mathrm{cont}}}\\, w_a, \\qquad w_a^{\\mathrm{lex}} = \\mathrm{GS}\\big(w_a - w_a^{\\mathrm{faith}},\\; f_a^{\\mathrm{cooc}}\\big),\\;\\; \\mathrm{Var}(\\cdot) \\geq \\lambda_{\\mathrm{orth}} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This turns the prior from one dial into a structured space with a keepable part and a removable part.\n\n### Selective Suppression Test\n*Show that removing the whole prior destroys real visual geometry while shortcut-only removal does not.*\n\n8. Add a hook that, while the model is generating its answer, removes the entire recovered-prior subspace from the model's internal activations at the middle layers, at every word position. Because this changes everything downstream, the model's actual answer changes. Measure faithful-probe accuracy and the POPE hallucination score on this run.\n\n*Full-axis representational suppression projects the activation $h_{L}$ off the entire recovered prior span $V_{b}$ at layer-set L before the second forward pass that produces the answer; replacing the sum over $w_{a}$ with only $w_{a}^{lex}$ gives the selective shortcut-only suppression.*\n$$ \\tilde{h}_L = h_L - \\sum_{a} \\big(\\langle h_L, w_a\\rangle\\, w_a\\big) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Removing everything tests whether wholesale suppression also destroys real visual geometry.\n9. Repeat the previous step but remove only the shortcut part of each direction (keep the faithful part). Combine the three shortcut directions into one small subspace and subtract just that during generation, then re-measure the same two scores. Now the only difference from the previous run is which part was removed.\n   - _Why_: If faithful accuracy survives while hallucination still drops, the prior was never a single harmful dial.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 在冻结的 MLLM 文本骨干中定位语言预训练习得的视觉先验\n\n**方法名称.** Backbone Visual-Prior Attribution (BVPA)\n\n## 研究动机\n多模态大语言模型（MLLM）是被教会同时读取图像的语言模型。一个出人意料的事实是：即使在这种模型看到任何图片之前，它底层那个仅靠文本训练的语言模型，已经仅凭阅读文字就 '知道' 了关于视觉世界的不少事情——例如草通常是绿色的、人一般比狗高、叉子常常出现在盘子旁边。研究者把这种 '行囊' 称为 '语言先验'（language prior）。\n\n迄今为止，学界只把这种先验当作要在模型作答的那一刻擦除的麻烦。ClearSight（CVPR 2025）和 Cross-Image Contrastive Decoding（Cross-Image CD，2025）等方法会检测模型何时在依赖文本习惯而非真实图像，并在输出阶段把这些习惯压下去。LanP（2025）则指出，当物体模糊或极小时，这些习惯有时反而是模型唯一能作答的依据。但所有这些方法都作用在 '成品模型' 的作答阶段，并把先验当成输出上的单一旋钮，因此它们都无法说明某个具体的视觉信念存在于网络内部的何处，也无法判断这个信念究竟是真实的几何（真实尺寸、真实颜色），还是仅仅一种词语关联捷径。\n\n让这个问题现在变得可解的，是 LLaVA-1.5（基于 Vicuna 文本模型）和 Qwen-VL（基于 Qwen）等开放模型，都附带了它们尚未经过任何图像训练的原始 '纯文本大脑'。这让我们能够在同一个模型内部、而非在彼此无关的模型之间，比较同一个大脑在 '学会看' 之前与之后的差异。我们提出 Backbone Visual-Prior Attribution（BVPA）：在冻结的纯文本大脑上拟合简单的线性读出器，恢复编码尺寸、共现与颜色的方向；检验这些已存在的方向能在多大程度上解释成品模型的视觉判断；然后把每个方向拆分为承载真实视觉几何的部分与仅是词语捷径的部分。\n\n若此法奏效，收益是具体的：与其粗暴地擦除整个先验（我们预测这同时会擦除真实的视觉知识），实践者可以只手术式地移除有误导性的词语捷径部分，而保留真正有用的视觉部分——把如今 '全有或全无' 的抑制，变成精确的 '保留一部分、移除一部分' 的操作。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景\n*准备检查点、探针以及真实数据迁移检验。*\n\n1. 载入成品多模态大语言模型(Multimodal Large Language Model, MLLM) M（如 LLaVA-1.5），以及它在任何图像训练之前那个完全对应的纯文本模型 B（Vicuna），并冻结全部权重。随后基于 Visual Genome(VG) 构建外部视觉真值来源：一张相对尺寸表（两个物体的框平均大多少）、一张共现表（两个物体在同一张图中一起出现的频率），以及一张颜色表（每个物体最常见的颜色，外加一个从该物体真实像素测得的 11 桶颜色直方图）。\n   - _为什么_: 要把某个信念归因于文本预训练，你需要那个尚未见过任何图像时的真实大脑。\n2. 为三个属性（相对尺寸、共现、颜色）各写 2000 条成对短句（1600 条用于拟合，400 条留作测试），全部出自同一个固定的填空模板，含两个物体槽位和一个关系槽位。每条句子从外部真值表直接获得一个是/否标签和一个数值标签。在之后送入图像训练前、后两个模型时保持措辞完全一致，使任何差异都只可能来自图像训练。\n   - _为什么_: 固定其余一切，能让任何测得的差异都只归因于图像训练来源。\n3. 最后，在 VQA 与 MME 的真实图像上跑同样的归因与两种抑制测试——但只针对关于相对尺寸、共现或颜色的问题——并用同样的外部真值表为其打标签。检验同样的规律（每个属性上效应方向一致）是否在真实数据上也出现，而不仅是在合成句子上。\n   - _为什么_: 只在合成探针上成立的发现，在真实使用中不可信。\n\n### 先验恢复\n*从冻结骨干中恢复文本预训练习得的视觉先验方向。*\n\n4. 用冻结的纯文本模型跑训练句子，读取其中间层（32 层模型的第 11–21 层）的内部激活，对词元和这些层取平均，得到每句一个向量。用岭回归(ridge regression)为每个属性拟合一个单位长度的直线预测方向 $w_{a}$，把这个向量映射到数值真值标签。这些方向就是恢复出的视觉先验。\n\n*$w_{a}$ 是属性 a 的单位范数线性读出方向，由冻结骨干在层集 L 的均值池化残差激活 $h_{L}(x)$ 经最小二乘回归到外部 oracle 标签 $y_{a}$ 得到。*\n$$ w_a = \\frac{\\arg\\min_{w}\\; \\sum_{i}\\big(\\langle w, h_L(x_i)\\rangle - y_a(x_i)\\big)^2}{\\lVert \\cdot \\rVert}, \\quad \\lVert w_a \\rVert = 1 \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这些方向就是恢复出的视觉先验——后续一切都建立在这个对象之上。\n\n### 来源归因\n*测量成品模型的视觉判断有多少继承自文本预训练。*\n\n5. 用成品模型跑同样的句子，但不附带任何图像（允许纯文本回合），读取同样的中间层，并在其上拟合同样类型的方向 $w_{a}^{M}$。随后对每个属性测量训练前方向 $w_{a}$ 与训练后方向 $w_{a}^{M}$ 之间的余弦相似度——数值接近 1 意味着该视觉结构在文本训练时就已存在。\n\n*$\\rho _{a}$ 是归因标量，即预训练前骨干方向 $w_{a}$ 与在图像微调后模型 M 上拟合的同一读出 $w_{a}^{M}$ 之间的余弦相似度；$\\rho _{a}$ 接近 1 表示该视觉结构继承自文本预训练。*\n$$ \\rho_a = \\cos\\!\\big(w_a, w_a^{M}\\big) = \\frac{\\langle w_a, w_a^{M}\\rangle}{\\lVert w_a\\rVert\\,\\lVert w_a^{M}\\rVert} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: $\\rho _{a}$ 较高意味着该视觉结构继承自文本，而非从图像中学得。\n6. 在留出的句子上，取成品模型的激活，沿训练前方向 $w_{a}$ 打分，再用训练集上调好的阈值把分数变成是/否答案。按属性报告其准确率，并与随机猜测率（约 50%）对比。若旧方向已能预测答案，则该判断来自文本预训练。\n   - _为什么_: 若旧方向已能预测答案，则该判断来自文本预训练。\n\n### 忠实/捷径拆分\n*把每个先验方向拆分为可保留的忠实部分与可移除的捷径部分。*\n\n7. 把每个方向拆成两部分：一个忠实部分，追踪真实的数值真值（如真实的尺寸比）；一个捷径部分，转而追踪两个词在文本中单纯共现的频率。从一个大型公开文本语料库计算词共现频率，并仅在捷径部分能解释足够多的方差（超过噪声水平）时才保留它。【作者需决定：在测量两个词共现频率时，用哪个公开文本语料库（C4、Pile 或其他）来替代模型的原始训练文本，因为确切的训练文本通常不可获得。】\n\n*忠实子方向是 $w_{a}$ 中投影与 oracle 连续标签 $y_{a}^{cont}$ 相关的分量；词汇捷径子方向是经 Gram-Schmidt 正交化后与语料共现频率 $f_{a}^{cooc}$ 相关的残差分量，仅当其解释方差 $\\ge  \\lambda _{orth}$（默认 0.05）时保留。*\n$$ w_a^{\\mathrm{faith}} \\propto \\Pi_{y_a^{\\mathrm{cont}}}\\, w_a, \\qquad w_a^{\\mathrm{lex}} = \\mathrm{GS}\\big(w_a - w_a^{\\mathrm{faith}},\\; f_a^{\\mathrm{cooc}}\\big),\\;\\; \\mathrm{Var}(\\cdot) \\geq \\lambda_{\\mathrm{orth}} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这把先验从一个旋钮变成一个有结构的空间，其中有可保留的部分和可移除的部分。\n\n### 选择性抑制检验\n*证明移除整个先验会破坏真实视觉几何，而仅移除捷径则不会。*\n\n8. 加一个钩子(hook)，在模型生成答案时，于中间层、每个词位置上，从模型内部激活中移除整个已恢复的先验子空间。由于这会改变其后的一切，模型给出的实际答案随之改变。在此次运行上测量忠实探针准确率与 POPE 幻觉评分。\n\n*全轴表征抑制在产生答案的第二次前向传播之前，将层集 L 的激活 $h_{L}$ 投影到整个已恢复先验子空间 $V_{b}$ 之外；把对 $w_{a}$ 的求和替换为仅 $w_{a}^{lex}$ 即得到选择性的仅捷径抑制。*\n$$ \\tilde{h}_L = h_L - \\sum_{a} \\big(\\langle h_L, w_a\\rangle\\, w_a\\big) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 移除全部内容可检验整体抑制是否也会破坏真实的视觉几何。\n9. 重复上一步，但只移除每个方向的捷径部分（保留忠实部分）。把三个捷径方向合并为一个小子空间，在生成时仅减去它，然后重新测量同样的两个评分。此时与上一轮唯一的差别就在于移除了哪一部分。\n   - _为什么_: 若忠实准确率得以保留而幻觉仍下降，说明先验从来就不是单一的有害旋钮。\n\n"},{"id":"69","run_dir":"run_prompt69_vrpseg","index":69,"title":"Reopenable Segments: Search-Feedback-Driven Adaptive Decomposition for Vehicle Routing","title_zh":"可重开分段：面向车辆路径问题的搜索反馈驱动自适应分解","method_name":"Reopenable Segments (REOSEG)","hook":"When a learned segmenter freezes part of a VRP solution to accelerate iterative search, the frozen boundary itself is the new quality ceiling — yet no solver lets that boundary reopen when the search's own realized gains say the freeze was wrong. We show that recycling each iteration's realized-vs-expected improvement into a label-free reopen signal converts a one-shot stable/unstable cut (L2Seg) into a self-revising decomposition that lifts the attainable-quality cap while keeping L2Seg's 2x-7x speedup.","anchor_pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","anchor_pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","domain_category":"Optimization & Search","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a decomposition boundary that revises itself in response to the search's own realized improvement: once a region is frozen (L2Seg's hypernodes, DRI's clusters, CFRS's partition), no current method maintains a signal that detects the freeze is now costing attainable quality and reopens that boundary — so the achievable solution is capped by a partition decision made before the evidence to correct it exists.","pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","sub_pattern":"C08 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by manufacturing a label-free reopen signal from each iteration's realized-vs-expected local improvement and routing it back into the segmenter so synthesis concentrates on exactly the frozen regions the current freeze is mis-serving — the closed-loop producer (segmenter)/evaluator (realized-gain gate) reopens boundaries that the search's own evidence flags as quality-capping.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes the GRANULARITY of decomposition a first-class adaptive quantity: every method commits to a single segment/cluster scale (L2Seg's fixed hypernode aggregation, DRI's one clustering pass), and none exposes a mechanism by which the local instance density or realized local gain selects a coarser-or-finer boundary where it pays off.","pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by stratifying the current solution's segments along a realized-gain/density discriminator into a high-leverage minority (reopened and re-optimized at fine, per-edge granularity) versus a near-redundant bulk (aggregated into coarse hypernodes), with an improvement-recovery decomposition bounding how the differentiated granularity recovers the unaccelerated solver's attainable cost.","is_anchor":false},{"gap":"Subtractive (shared inherited assumption): no retrieved paper questions whether the stable/unstable (or in-cluster/out-of-cluster) decision must be a HARD, committed partition of the solution at all — every leaf descends from the divide-and-conquer ancestor that assumes the solver operates on disjoint, mutually-exclusive subproblems, and none tests whether that disjoint-partition assumption is necessary rather than merely inherited.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"reframe_as_solvable_object","how_closed":"Closed by auditing the disjoint-partition assumption the segmenter's keep-frozen/reopen choice rule inherits (C11: the selection rule presumes mutually-exclusive segments) and pivoting it; the companion reframe_as_solvable_object ships the deliverable by recasting the hard stable/unstable cut as a soft overlapping-membership object — a fractional reopen-weight per edge so boundary revision becomes a continuous re-weighting rather than a hard re-cut.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"neural combinatorial optimization for vehicle routing problems (learned decomposition / segmentation of iterative VRP search)","n_papers":48,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":23},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10},{"source":"openreview","n":2}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":13,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Neural Combinatorial Optimization Algorithms for Solving Vehicle Routing Problems: A Comprehensive Survey with Perspectives"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Self-Improved Learning for Scalable Neural Combinatorial Optimization"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Rethinking Supervised Learning-Based Neural Combinatorial Optimization for Routing Problem"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Neural Combinatorial Optimization for Robust Routing Problem with Uncertain Travel Times"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Leader Reward for POMO-Based Neural Combinatorial Optimization"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Learn to Solve Vehicle Routing Problems ASAP: A Neural Optimization Approach for Time-Constrained Vehicle Routing Problems with Finite Vehicle Fleet"}],"more":7},{"year":2025,"n":23,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Boosting Neural Combinatorial Optimization for Large-Scale Vehicle Routing Problems"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Improving Generalization of Neural Combinatorial Optimization for Vehicle Routing Problems via Test-Time Projection Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Rethinking Neural Combinatorial Optimization for Vehicle Routing Problems with Different Constraint Tightness Degrees"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Efficient Neural Combinatorial Optimization Solver for the Min-max Heterogeneous Capacitated Vehicle Routing Problem"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Neural Combinatorial Optimization for Real-World Routing"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Recurrent State Encoders for Efficient Neural Combinatorial Optimization"}],"more":17},{"year":2026,"n":12,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"},{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"NCO4CVRP: Neural Combinatorial Optimization for the Capacitated Vehicle Routing Problem"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Learning to Route Electric Trucks Under Operational Uncertainty"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Enforcing TSP-Optimality in Fair Vehicle Routing by Cutting Planes"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"On vehicle routing problems with stochastic demands -- Scenario-optimal recourse policies"}],"more":6}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":6,"share":0.125},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":3,"share":0.062},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":2,"share":0.042},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":2,"share":0.042},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation; structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"unify_into_shared_representation; structural_prior_encoding","count":2,"share":0.042},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":2,"share":0.042},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition; architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"heterogeneous_decomposition; architectural_operator_substitution","count":1,"share":0.021},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":1,"share":0.021}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"State-of-the-art learned acceleration of iterative VRP search rests on a single decision unit it never re-examines: a binary, instance-static partition of the current solution into 'stable' (frozen) and 'unstable' (re-optimized) portions. L2Seg (openalex:W4417175691) learns a per-node stable/unstable label and then aggregates the stable runs into fixed FSTA hypernodes that are held constant for the remainder of the search; the decompose-route-improve line (openalex:W4415479087) likewise commits to a single hand-designed spatial-temporal-demand clustering that is computed once and never revised; and Neural CFRS (arxiv:2605.09301v1) collapses routing to a one-shot capacity-constrained partition. Across all three the partition is decided once (or relabeled with the same fixed granularity each pass) and its boundaries do not respond to the search's own evidence that a frozen region is actually still improving or that the chosen segment size is throttling the gain. The concrete failure: when a region the model labeled stable is in fact near a productive move, or when the segment granularity is mismatched to the local instance density, the frozen hypernode boundary permanently excludes that region's edges from re-optimization, so the achievable solution quality is capped below what the underlying solver would reach unaccelerated — and no current method exposes a signal that lets the decomposition boundary itself adapt to the realized improvement the search is producing.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4417175691","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"L2Seg learns to classify each node of an iterative-search solution as belonging to a stable or unstable segment, then FSTA aggregates the stable consecutive runs into fixed hypernodes so the solver re-optimizes only the unstable remainder, accelerating LKH-3/HGS by 2x-7x. Residue (from method section): the stable/unstable decision is a one-shot binary classification with a fixed aggregation granularity and the resulting hypernode boundaries are frozen for the search horizon — L2Seg never closes the loop by letting the realized search improvement revise which segments stay aggregated or at what granularity, so any region it mislabels stable is permanently excluded from re-optimization and caps attainable quality."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415479087","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"The decompose-route-improve (DRI) framework partitions a large VRPTW into subproblems with a hand-designed spatial-temporal-demand dissimilarity metric, solves each independently, then does pruned local search across boundaries. Residue: the decomposition is computed once by a static, non-learned similarity metric and the subproblem boundaries are never revised based on how much improvement the per-subproblem solve actually achieved — boundary customers that would benefit from cross-subproblem moves are reachable only through a fixed pruning rule, not through an adaptive re-decomposition."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2605.09301v1","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Neural CFRS reframes CVRP as a one-shot, capacity-constrained customer-to-vehicle partition via a differentiable optimal-transport layer, then solves independent per-cluster TSPs in parallel. Residue: the partition is produced in a single forward pass with no iterative-search loop, so once the clusters are fixed there is no mechanism to migrate a customer across a cluster boundary when the downstream TSP reveals the assignment was suboptimal — the decomposition is non-adaptive to realized routing cost."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4417299023","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"L2R learns to dynamically prune the per-step construction search space of constructive NCO, prioritizing nodes by learned problem features and scaling to 10M-node VRPs. Residue: pruning operates at the level of individual candidate nodes within autoregressive construction, not at the level of contiguous solution segments in an iterative-improvement loop, and it carries a residual geometric/spatial prior; it offers no notion of freezing-and-revising stable regions of a maintained incumbent solution."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"neural combinatorial optimization for vehicle routing problems (learned decomposition / segmentation of iterative VRP search)","venue":"ICLR / NeurIPS (ML methods track)","time":"2026 cycle","data":["CVRP and VRPTW benchmark instances (uniform + real-world distributions, up to 10k-100k nodes)","LKH-3 / HGS iterative-search traces for supervision/evaluation"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML + combinatorial optimization","preference":"empirical","baseline":"L2Seg (Learning-to-Segment / FSTA decomposition) and state-of-the-art iterative VRP solvers (LKH-3, HGS) it accelerates","limitation":"current learned decomposition for iterative VRP search labels segments as stable/unstable with a fixed FSTA hypernode abstraction; the granularity and adaptivity of decomposition boundaries over the course of search is not itself learned or theoretically grounded","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The three legs interlock as one sequential pipeline (coherence thread instance: the per-edge reopen-weight w_e is the single object that leg-1 writes, leg-2 reads to set granularity, and leg-3 relaxes from hard to soft). LEG 1 (self_supervised_signal_engineering / C08): an iterative VRP solver (LKH-3 or HGS, or a learned LNS) runs on a solution decomposed by a base segmenter (we reuse L2Seg's non-autoregressive node encoder as the producer). After each search round t, for every edge e currently inside a frozen hypernode we compute a realized-gain signal g_e(t) = max(0, c_pred(e,t) - c_real(e,t)) / s_e, where c_pred(e,t) is the improvement the segmenter's value head predicted would be available if e were reopened (a scalar readout of the producer head, units = travel-cost reduction), c_real(e,t) is the actual improvement obtained on the last round e was eligible (units = travel-cost reduction; for never-reopened edges it is the improvement of the geometrically nearest reopened edge in the same route as a bootstrapped proxy), and s_e is the edge's travel cost (units = travel cost) so g_e is dimensionless. g_e(t) is the manufactured label-free signal — no ground-truth 'should-reopen' label is ever used. The reopen gate is a single scalar threshold tau (hyperparameter, default tau=0.05): edges with g_e(t) > tau are reopened next round; this routes the learner's own realized error back into which frozen regions get synthesized as re-optimization targets, exactly the C08 dynamic-loop move. LEG 2 (heterogeneous_decomposition / C04): rather than a uniform hypernode size, edges are stratified by g_e(t) into a high-leverage minority (top-k by g_e within each route, reopened at fine per-edge granularity) and a near-redundant bulk (aggregated into coarse hypernodes); k_route is selected per route by the density rule k_route = ceil(rho * |reopen-eligible edges in route|) with rho a hyperparameter (default rho=0.2). The improvement-recovery decomposition delta_total = sum_e w_e * g_e(t) * s_e bounds how much of the unaccelerated solver's attainable cost reduction the differentiated granularity recovers, and is the spine of the leg. LEG 3 (assumption_audit_and_pivot / C11 + companion reframe_as_solvable_object): the base segmenter's keep-frozen/reopen rule assumes each edge is exclusively in one segment; we audit this (a frozen edge adjacent to a reopened one cannot participate in a boundary-crossing move) and pivot by reframing the hard cut as a soft membership: w_e in [0,1] is a fractional reopen-weight computed as w_e = sigmoid((g_e(t) - tau)/beta) (beta a temperature hyperparameter, default 0.02), and the solver's neighborhood operator samples each frozen edge into the active re-optimization set with probability w_e each round. With w_e in {0,1} this exactly recovers the hard L2Seg cut (a strict generalization), so the audit's pivot is realized as a runnable soft-partition object and the disjoint-partition assumption is replaced by an overlapping one. Quantitative grounding: L2Seg reports 2x-7x speedup over LKH-3/HGS (openalex:W4417175691); our reopen events add O(reopen-fraction) extra local-search cost per round, so we predict speedup retention in the 1.8x-6x band (a small constant erosion) with a strictly lower final optimality gap — we measure cumulative final gap, distinct from L2Seg's per-iteration speedup-only reporting.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The three gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules because all three operate on the SAME per-edge object: leg-1 produces the realized-gain signal g_e, leg-2 reads g_e to set granularity, leg-3 relaxes the g_e-derived decision from hard to soft via w_e — the evidence is that each leg's input is the prior leg's output on the same edge index, which is the sequential_pipeline signature, so one shared per-edge state suffices. (b) Alternative designs considered and rejected: (i) a separately trained reopen-classifier with ground-truth reopen labels was rejected because no such labels exist and it would regress toward a static second segmenter; (ii) a continuous trust-region-style step-size on the whole subproblem (collateral node c0) was rejected because it acts on a scalar region size, not on a maintained discrete-segment abstraction, and would not differentiate from classical trust-region control; (iii) re-running a fixed clustering each round (regresses to n0/DRI) was rejected. The avoided regression nodes (n1 ALNS hand-weighted destroy operator; c0 continuous trust-region; n0 fixed clustering) are recorded here: our reopen signal is a discrete-segment realized-gain statistic maintained across iterations on a contiguous-segment abstraction, which none of those nodes provide.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: take L2Seg's released CVRP and VRPTW setup (instances of 1k-10k nodes, LKH-3 and HGS as the accelerated solvers) and run three arms to equal wall-clock budget: (A) unaccelerated solver, (B) L2Seg frozen-segmentation acceleration, (C) our reopenable-segment method. If the candidate works, the metric that moves is the final optimality gap to best-known: arm C's gap is strictly LOWER than arm B's at matched wall-clock while arm C retains >=70% of arm B's speedup over arm A (gap decreases, speedup largely preserved). The single named load-bearing variable is the realized-gain reopen signal g_e (and its soft weight w_e): the mechanism distinguisher is a negative-control intervention that PERMUTES g_e across edges within each route (randomize which frozen edges get high reopen-weight while preserving the marginal distribution of w_e), holding the reopen budget f_max identical. Anti-tautology: the predicted effect of this permutation is on the DOWNSTREAM task outcome — arm C's final optimality-gap advantage over arm B must collapse to within noise (the gap-reduction vanishes), NOT merely that g_e's own value changes. A positive control is the g_e-only stripped model: reopen purely by ranking g_e with the soft gate and no other learned component, which should recover most of arm C's gap-reduction over arm B, converting the falsifier into a constructive identification that the realized-gain signal is what carries the improvement.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4417175691","delta":"L2Seg learns a one-shot binary stable/unstable cut and freezes the hypernodes for the search horizon; we construct a per-edge realized-vs-expected improvement signal g_e that REOPENS frozen edges mid-search and a soft membership w_e that strictly generalizes their hard cut (w_e in {0,1} recovers L2Seg), neither of which their construction produces."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415479087","delta":"DRI decomposes once with a hand-designed spatial-temporal-demand similarity metric and never revises subproblem boundaries; we make boundary revision driven by the solver's realized per-edge gain, a quantity DRI's static clustering never computes or feeds back."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2605.09301v1","delta":"Neural CFRS produces a one-shot differentiable-OT partition with no iterative loop and no cross-cluster migration; we maintain an iterative reopen loop with fractional membership that migrates edges across the frozen/active boundary in response to downstream realized routing cost."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4417299023","delta":"L2R learns per-step node-level search-space pruning for autoregressive construction with a residual spatial prior; we operate on contiguous segments of a maintained incumbent in an improvement loop and revise the freeze by realized gain, a segment-level reopen notion L2R has no representation for."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4417175691","what_step_was_missed":"L2Seg constructs the stable/unstable classifier and the FSTA hypernode aggregation but stops at a one-shot, horizon-frozen cut; for our contribution to already exist they would have needed to construct the realized-vs-expected per-edge improvement statistic g_e as a closed-loop supervisory signal AND the soft fractional-membership relaxation w_e that lets a frozen edge re-enter the active set probabilistically — they built neither the feedback signal nor the soft-partition object, so the freeze remains a permanent quality ceiling in their method."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":251,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"Layer 1 does not fire: no gap_closure_reject_check entry has a Reject lesson at candidate_match=yes, anti_pattern_check matched audit_decomp_supervisor but mitigation_substantively_delivered=true (g_e is the single shared object behind both the decomposition and the signal, with the disentangling controls present), and paper_pointed_threat against L2Seg is adjacent-build-on not exact-mechanism overlap. In the safe zone the load-bearing borderline is the C11 audit leg: the Reject lesson 'substituting one selection heuristic for another without a theorem stating when and why it wins reads as an engineering combination' is borderline because the soft-membership pivot ships a runnable object and the delta_total recovery decomposition but not a sharp when-it-wins argument, and the protective-property borderline (reopen-budget vs retained-speedup trade asserted at >=70%, not characterized) hits the same leg — both are load-bearing structural properties of the audit contribution, so the verdict is revise with tactical revision_targets, addressable by Phase 3.3 field edits without touching the kill-switch fields.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a decomposition boundary that revises itself in response to the search's own realized improvement: once a region is frozen (L2Seg's hypernodes, DRI's clusters, CFRS's partition), no current method maintains a signal that detects the freeze is now costing attainable quality and reopens that boundary — so the achievable solution is capped by a partition decision made before the evidence to correct it exists.","main_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","sub_pattern":"C08 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is treating 'attach a generator plus a filter' as a sufficient contribution when generate-and-filter is already commonplace, so no single load-bearing insight separates the work; a second shape is the unvalidated transfer assumption where the manufactured distribution is never shown to generalize to the real target.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A cooperative generate-and-filter loop sitting on substantial prior art needs either a demonstrably new mechanism or cross-domain breadth; showing it on a single domain invites the read that the method is domain-specific and incremental.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The load-bearing new mechanism is the realized-vs-expected per-edge improvement signal g_e feeding a freeze-reopen loop — absent from all prior VRP-decomposition work — and the falsification spans CVRP and VRPTW with two solvers (LKH-3, HGS), so it is not single-domain recombination."},{"lesson_quoted":"A newly proposed quality or gating score must be tightly argued to solve the stated problem under realistic conditions — a loosely-motivated score evaluated in an artificial setup is dismissed as a solution looking for a problem.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"g_e and the reopen threshold tau are concretely defined and motivated, but c_real for never-reopened edges uses a bootstrapped nearest-edge proxy whose validity under realistic large-scale instances is asserted rather than argued, leaving the gate's correctness mildly under-defended."},{"lesson_quoted":"Training on synthetically generated data without demonstrating transfer to the real target distribution leaves the core premise unvalidated, no matter how clean the synthetic labels are.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The manufactured signal is consumed in-loop on the same real benchmark instances being solved (no synthetic-to-real transfer gap), and the falsification measures the real downstream optimality gap, so the transfer-premise failure mode does not apply."},{"lesson_quoted":"A synthetic-data-factory claim collapses without comparison to cheaper classical baselines, because the necessity of the heavy generative model is then unverifiable.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The falsification includes arm A (unaccelerated solver), arm B (L2Seg frozen acceleration), and the hard-cut/g_e-permutation/g_e-only controls, which are exactly the cheaper baselines that isolate the reopen mechanism's necessity."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes the GRANULARITY of decomposition a first-class adaptive quantity: every method commits to a single segment/cluster scale (L2Seg's fixed hypernode aggregation, DRI's one clustering pass), and none exposes a mechanism by which the local instance density or realized local gain selects a coarser-or-finer boundary where it pays off.","main_pattern":"heterogeneous_decomposition","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is treating the partition criterion itself as the contribution while leaving its value unproven, so reviewers map the discriminator onto an established technique and read the differentiated treatment as relabeling; compounded by validating where the bottleneck does not bite.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Presenting a sensitivity or redundancy proxy as the novelty invites the verdict that it rediscovers known mixed-precision or low-rank results unless it is sharply differentiated from the obvious prior criterion.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The discriminator here is the realized-search-gain g_e, which is not a static sensitivity/redundancy proxy but a dynamic per-iteration quantity produced by the solver, and the granularity leg is explicitly subordinate to the anchor signal rather than presented as the standalone novelty."},{"lesson_quoted":"Omitting comparison against both the strongest uniform baseline and the obvious cheap alternative (SVD/PCA, structured dropout, a natively trained smaller model) leaves reviewers unable to tell whether the partition buys anything at all.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Arm B (L2Seg's single-granularity frozen aggregation) is exactly the strongest uniform-granularity baseline, and the hard-cut ablation isolates the adaptive-granularity contribution."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a storage or throughput claim only on toy-scale models — where the compression bottleneck does not actually bite — undermines the entire motivation no matter how clean the method is.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Evaluation is on 1k-10k-node CVRP/VRPTW where the redundant-recompute bottleneck the candidate targets genuinely bites (L2Seg's own large-scale regime), not toy instances."},{"lesson_quoted":"Skipping any analysis of why the heterogeneity exists — the data or value distribution that drives the partition — makes the technical novelty and the potential impact impossible to assess.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism_steps step 1 and the improvement-recovery decomposition delta_total = sum w_e g_e s_e characterize the realized-gain distribution that drives the partition, satisfying the why-heterogeneity-exists requirement."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"Subtractive (shared inherited assumption): no retrieved paper questions whether the stable/unstable (or in-cluster/out-of-cluster) decision must be a HARD, committed partition of the solution at all — every leaf descends from the divide-and-conquer ancestor that assumes the solver operates on disjoint, mutually-exclusive subproblems, and none tests whether that disjoint-partition assumption is necessary rather than merely inherited.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The dominant failure is substituting one selection rule for another that performs better empirically while omitting the theorem that explains when and why it wins, read as an engineering combination without structural insight; a second is pivoting an assumption the community regards as a reasonable modeling choice rather than a genuine restriction.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Substituting one selection heuristic for another without a theorem stating when and why it wins reads as an engineering combination, not a contribution, no matter how clean the empirical gain.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The audit pivots the disjoint-partition assumption into a soft-membership selection rule (hard cut -> w_e in [0,1]) but ships only the runnable object plus the delta_total recovery decomposition, not a re-derived performance certificate stating when the soft rule strictly beats the hard cut — the headline structural insight is present (overlap recovers boundary-crossing moves the hard cut forbids) but the formal 'when and why it wins' argument is thin."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pivoting an assumption the community treats as a reasonable modeling choice — rather than first proving it a genuine restriction — leaves both motivation and novelty in doubt.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The disjoint-partition assumption is shown to be a genuine restriction, not a benign choice: bottleneck_statement and method_lineage establish that the hard freeze permanently excludes mislabeled-stable regions and caps attainable quality, which is the precise harm the pivot removes."},{"lesson_quoted":"A re-derived guarantee whose binding constant is dataset-dependent and cannot be controlled by the practitioner is vacuous in the worst case and fails to convince.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"No vacuous guarantee is claimed; the candidate stays empirical (the strict-generalization property w_e in {0,1} recovers L2Seg is exact, not a loose constant), so this lesson does not bite."},{"lesson_quoted":"Unlocking a new capability by violating an assumption while ignoring a protective property it guarded — detectability, validity, identifiability — invites rejection on the overlooked side effect rather than the headline result.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"Softening the disjoint partition could let the active re-optimization set grow unbounded (the property the hard cut protected was bounded subproblem size = the speedup); the f_max cap and tau-annealing stabilizer address this, but the trade between reopen budget and retained speedup is asserted (>=70% retention) rather than characterized."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No gap_closure entry has any Reject lesson marked candidate_match=yes, so the hard floor does not fire. The audit leg (assumption_audit_and_pivot / C11) drives the aggregate to borderline: the lesson 'substituting one selection heuristic for another without a theorem stating when and why it wins reads as an engineering combination' is borderline because the soft-membership pivot ships a runnable object and a recovery decomposition but not a sharp when-it-wins argument, and the protective-property lesson is borderline on the reopen-budget-vs-speedup trade."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a decomposition boundary that revises itself in response to the search's own realized improvement: once a region is frozen (L2Seg's hypernodes, DRI's clusters, CFRS's partition), no current method maintains a signal that detects the freeze is now costing attainable quality and reopens that boundary — so the achievable solution is capped by a partition decision made before the evidence to correct it exists.","sub_pattern":"C08 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Stand up a controllable producer and drive it to synthesize candidate training instances beyond the original support, then route every candidate through one quality gate; the most advanced variants close the loop dynamically — feeding the learner's per-instance error/uncertainty back to the producer so synthesis concentrates on exactly the regions the current model fails on, making the filter implicit in generation.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"LEG 1 of core_mechanism performs exactly the advanced dynamic-loop move: the segmenter (producer) proposes freeze/reopen candidates, the realized-gain g_e gate (quality filter) routes each, and the learner's own realized error (c_real vs c_pred) is fed back so reopening concentrates on the frozen regions the current freeze is mis-serving — the C08 'fold the learner's error back so filtering becomes implicit in generation' signature, instantiated on segment reopening rather than data synthesis.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes the GRANULARITY of decomposition a first-class adaptive quantity: every method commits to a single segment/cluster scale (L2Seg's fixed hypernode aggregation, DRI's one clustering pass), and none exposes a mechanism by which the local instance density or realized local gain selects a coarser-or-finer boundary where it pays off.","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Discriminate components by a magnitude/sensitivity/influence/redundancy criterion into a high-impact minority and a near-redundant bulk, then preserve/retain-at-full-fidelity the minority while aggressively compressing the bulk; the load-bearing artifact is an error/sensitivity decomposition that bounds how the differentiated treatment recovers the original objective.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"LEG 2 stratifies edges by realized-gain g_e into a high-leverage minority (reopened at fine per-edge granularity = retained at full fidelity) versus a near-redundant bulk (aggregated into coarse hypernodes = compressed), and supplies the improvement-recovery decomposition delta_total = sum w_e g_e s_e as the C04 bounding artifact — the cluster's discriminate-then-differentially-treat signature is present.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"Subtractive (shared inherited assumption): no retrieved paper questions whether the stable/unstable (or in-cluster/out-of-cluster) decision must be a HARD, committed partition of the solution at all — every leaf descends from the divide-and-conquer ancestor that assumes the solver operates on disjoint, mutually-exclusive subproblems, and none tests whether that disjoint-partition assumption is necessary rather than merely inherited.","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Center on a selection/keep-or-drop rule and pivot the single assumption baked into its criterion or required structure; the pivot either relaxes the structural crutch to a weaker condition and re-proves the guarantee, or reframes the selection task as a different problem class — the invariant deliverable is a re-derived performance certificate.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"LEG 3 performs the pivot's reframe arm (companion reframe_as_solvable_object): the hard keep-frozen/reopen selection is recast as a soft overlapping-membership object w_e in [0,1], with w_e in {0,1} exactly recovering the pre-pivot hard cut — the C11 reframe-the-selection-class signature is performed. The 'invariant deliverable = re-derived performance certificate' is only partially met (the delta_total recovery decomposition substitutes for a formal when-it-wins certificate), which is the borderline noted in gap_closure_reject_check, not a bypass of the tactical move.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"All three legs instantiate their cited cluster's signature move in core_mechanism — C08's dynamic error-fed-back loop, C04's discriminate-and-differentially-treat with a recovery decomposition, and C11's reframe-the-selection-class soft-membership pivot. The C11 leg's certificate is empirical rather than formal, which is a strength-of-deliverable borderline (handled in gap_closure_reject_check), not an absent-tactic bypass."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["self_supervised_signal_engineering","heterogeneous_decomposition","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":"audit_decomp_supervisor","required_mitigation_quoted":"The decomposition criterion must be derivable from observed structure or task-level supervision (not just intuition), AND the manufactured signal must be the *unique* signal the decomposition implies. An ablation that holds the decomposition fixed and varies the signal (or vice versa) must show the two are not conflated.","mitigation_substantively_delivered":"true","reasoning":"The decomposition criterion and the manufactured signal are the SAME observed quantity (the per-edge realized-search-gain g_e): leg 2's granularity partition is derived from g_e (observed search structure, not intuition) and g_e is the unique signal that partition implies, so the two are not two independent ad-hoc choices but one shared object — and the falsification's g_e-permutation negative control (holds the reopen budget/decomposition fixed, scrambles the signal) plus the g_e-only positive control and the hard-cut ablation jointly supply the required hold-one-vary-the-other disentanglement, so the strongest-reject composition's failure mode is substantively mitigated in core_mechanism, not merely named."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"openalex:W4417175691","threat_source":"lit_table","subsumption_argument":"L2Seg (the seed's own source paper) is the structurally closest prior art: it learns the stable/unstable segmentation and the FSTA hypernode aggregation the candidate builds on. The candidate's claim stands or falls on whether the search-feedback REOPEN loop and the soft fractional membership are genuinely outside L2Seg's method. L2Seg's method section commits to a one-shot binary stable/unstable classification with horizon-frozen hypernodes and never computes a realized-vs-expected improvement signal nor a fractional reopen weight, so the overlap is on the shared base segmenter (which the candidate explicitly reuses and credits) and NOT on the load-bearing reopen mechanism — the candidate strictly generalizes L2Seg (w_e in {0,1} recovers it) rather than restating it. This is adjacent-prior-to-build-on, not exact-mechanism subsumption.","addressable_via":"Already differentiated in core_mechanism and differentiation_from_lit; no field change needed to dodge subsumption, but the candidate must keep crediting L2Seg as the reused base segmenter and report arm B (L2Seg) as the head-to-head baseline so the reopen delta is attributable."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","issue":"C11 Reject lesson 'substituting one selection heuristic for another without a theorem stating when and why it wins' (borderline) — the soft-membership pivot lacks an explicit when-it-wins statement.","fix_direction":"In the LEG 3 portion of core_mechanism, add the explicit when-it-wins condition for the soft pivot: state that the soft membership strictly beats the hard L2Seg cut precisely on instances where at least one boundary-crossing move with positive realized gain spans a frozen/active boundary (formally: whenever there exists an edge e with g_e > tau lying adjacent to an unstable region), and that the gain provably collapses to zero (recovering L2Seg exactly) when no such cross-boundary positive-gain move exists — making the recovery decomposition delta_total the certificate that quantifies the win and ties it to the pivot. Do NOT alter falsification_prediction or compute_budget."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism_steps","issue":"C11 protective-property borderline — the reopen-budget vs retained-speedup trade (the property the hard cut guarded) is asserted at >=70% retention rather than characterized.","fix_direction":"In core_mechanism_steps step 7 (the f_max/tau-annealing stabilizer), make the speedup-protection explicit: state that the retained speedup is lower-bounded by 1/(1+f_max) relative to L2Seg's because the active-set size per round is capped at a (1+f_max) factor over the frozen baseline, so the practitioner controls the reopen-budget/speedup trade directly via f_max (default 0.3 -> >=~77% of L2Seg's per-round acceleration retained). Keep this consistent with the falsification's >=70% retention claim; do NOT alter falsification_prediction or compute_budget."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added an explicit when-it-wins certificate to LEG 3: the soft membership strictly beats the hard L2Seg cut iff a frozen edge with g_e>tau is adjacent to an unstable region, and delta_total collapses to zero recovering L2Seg exactly otherwise (C11 re-derived-certificate deliverable made explicit)."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism_steps","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Made the protected speedup property explicit in step 7: retained per-round acceleration lower-bounded by 1/(1+f_max) of L2Seg's, so the reopen-budget/speedup trade is a controllable knob (f_max=0.3 => >=~77% retained), consistent with the >=70% falsification claim."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Reopenable Segments: Search-Feedback-Driven Adaptive Decomposition for Vehicle Routing\n\n**Method.** Reopenable Segments (REOSEG)\n\n## Motivation\nModern solvers for vehicle routing problems (VRP — planning delivery routes for a fleet of trucks) speed up by freezing the part of the current route plan that looks settled and only re-optimizing the rest. The best learned method, L2Seg (Learning to Segment for VRP), trains a network to label each piece of the solution as 'stable' (freeze it) or 'unstable' (keep working on it), then merges the stable pieces into fixed blocks for the rest of the search. This makes it 2-7 times faster than running the classic solver alone.\n\nThe catch is that the freeze decision is made once, up front, before the search has produced any evidence about whether it was right. If the network wrongly marks a region 'stable' when a good improving move was actually available right next to it, that region is locked out of further optimization for good — so the final route quality is capped below what the plain solver could have reached. Related methods have the same blind spot: the Decompose-Route-Improve framework splits a big problem once with a hand-designed rule and never revisits the split, and Neural Cluster-First-Route-Second assigns customers to vehicles in a single shot with no way to move a customer later.\n\nWhat makes a fix possible now is precisely that L2Seg made segment stability a LEARNED quantity: its network already produces a number predicting how much improvement a region offers. We can compare that prediction to the improvement the search actually achieves, and use the gap — for free, with no new labels — as a signal that says 'this frozen region is worth reopening.' Closing this gap turns the freeze boundary from a permanent ceiling into something that corrects itself as the search learns, recovering the quality the plain solver could reach while keeping most of the speedup.\n\n## Method\n### Realized-Gain Signal\n*Manufacture a label-free per-edge signal from predicted-vs-actual improvement that flags which frozen regions to reopen.*\n\n1. Reuse L2Seg's existing pretrained node-encoder network exactly as-is. Add one small extra linear output layer (the 'value head') that, for each edge in the route plan, takes the encoder's embeddings of the edge's two endpoint nodes together with that edge's travel cost and outputs a single number: how much travel cost that edge could still save if reopened. Start this layer at zero so it predicts no saving until it has learned something. Keep the main network frozen; train only this new layer and a few scaling parameters.\n   - _Why_: We need a cheap prediction of available improvement to later compare against what actually happens — and reusing the trained segmenter avoids re-learning routing from scratch.\n2. Run a single round of the underlying solver (LKH-3, HGS, or a learned large-neighborhood search — a method that repeatedly rips out and rebuilds part of a solution) on only the unstable part, holding the frozen blocks fixed. For each edge the solver was allowed to touch, record the actual travel-cost reduction it achieved this round. Frozen edges get no direct measurement.\n   - _Why_: This gives us the ground truth of what the search really gained, which is the evidence the freeze decision was missing.\n3. For every frozen edge, compute the realized-gain signal $g_{e}$ (Eq. 1): take how much improvement the value head predicted minus how much the search actually achieved, keep only the positive part, and divide by the edge's travel cost so the result is a unitless number. For an edge that has never been reopened (so it has no measured improvement), borrow the measured improvement of the nearest reopened edge in the same route, where 'nearest' means the smallest straight-line distance between the two edges' midpoints; if the route has no reopened edge this round, use zero. No human-provided label is used. 【author decision: whether the predicted improvement compared against reality is the value head's current-round prediction or the prediction it made the last time that edge was eligible — more responsive versus more causally matched.】\n\n*The manufactured label-free realized-gain signal for frozen edge e at round t: the positive part of predicted-minus-realized improvement, normalized by edge travel cost $s_{e}$ so $g_{e}$ is dimensionless. No ground-truth reopen label is used.*\n$$ g_e(t) = \\frac{\\max\\!\\left(0,\\; c_{\\mathrm{pred}}(e,t) - c_{\\mathrm{real}}(e,t)\\right)}{s_e} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: When the network predicted more improvement than the search delivered for the unstable part, the frozen neighbors are probably hiding usable gains — that mismatch is exactly the free signal telling us where to reopen.\n4. After each round, train the value head by reducing the squared difference between what it predicted and what the search actually achieved, over the edges that had a real measurement, with one or a few gradient updates. Only the value head and a few scaling parameters change; the main network stays frozen. The only teaching signal is the solver's own results, never an external correct answer.\n   - _Why_: The predictor gets better over time using only the solver's own results — no external labels — keeping the whole loop self-supervised.\n\n### Soft Reopen Membership\n*Relax the hard stable/unstable cut into a fractional reopen probability that strictly generalizes L2Seg.*\n\n5. Convert each frozen edge's signal $g_{e}$ into a soft reopen probability $w_{e}$ using a sigmoid of how far $g_{e}$ exceeds a threshold $\\tau ,$ scaled by a temperature $\\beta $ (Eq. 2; defaults $\\tau =0.05, \\beta =0.02).$ Then, independently for each frozen edge, flip a biased coin with that probability to decide whether to pull it back into the next round's working set of movable edges; sampled edges are physically reconsidered by the solver. Making $\\beta $ very small turns this back into a hard yes/no decision identical to the original L2Seg cut.\n\n*The soft fractional reopen-membership: $a temperature-\\beta  sigmoid$ of the gap between realized gain $g_{e}$ and threshold $\\tau .$ As $\\beta  \\to  0$ it collapses to the hard ${0,1}$ L2Seg cut, so the soft object strictly generalizes the hard partition.*\n$$ w_e = \\sigma\\!\\left(\\frac{g_e(t) - \\tau}{\\beta}\\right), \\qquad w_e \\in [0,1] \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A soft probability instead of a hard yes/no lets boundaries overlap and revise gently; pushing $\\beta $ toward 0 recovers the original hard L2Seg cut exactly, so this only ever generalizes the proven method.\n6. Add a switch that sets the temperature $\\beta $ to (effectively) zero, so every reopen probability becomes a hard 0 or 1 and the method reproduces L2Seg's original frozen segmentation exactly. Running this control arm with the reopen mechanism turned off shows how much the soft-reopening idea itself contributes.\n   - _Why_: Comparing against this exact-L2Seg arm isolates how much the reopen mechanism itself contributes, ruling out that gains came from anything else.\n\n### Adaptive Granularity\n*Use the signal to pick fine-vs-coarse decomposition scale per route where it pays off.*\n\n7. In each route, sort the reopen-eligible edges by their signal $g_{e}$ and take the top $k_{route}$ of them to reopen at full per-edge detail; $k_{route}$ is a fixed fraction $\\rho $ (default 0.2) of how many edges in that route are eligible, rounded up (Eq. 3). Merge all the other edges of the route into coarse blocks exactly as L2Seg does. The result is that each route gets its own decomposition granularity, fine where the realized-gain signal is concentrated and coarse elsewhere.\n\n*The per-route adaptive granularity: the top $k_{route}$ edges by $g_{e}$ within a route are reopened at fine per-edge scale, where $k_{route}$ is a density fraction $\\rho $ of that route's reopen-eligible edges.*\n$$ k_{\\mathrm{route}} = \\left\\lceil \\rho \\cdot |\\,\\mathcal{E}_{\\mathrm{elig}}\\,| \\right\\rceil \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Spend fine-grained effort only where the realized-gain signal says it pays off, and stay coarse (fast) everywhere else — so granularity adapts to local opportunity.\n\n### Speedup Protection + Certificate\n*Cap the reopen budget to guarantee retained speedup, and log a certificate that proves when reopening wins.*\n\n8. Limit how much gets reopened: never reopen more than a fraction $f_{max}$ (default 0.3) of edges per round, keeping only the highest-probability ones up to that fraction; if the working set is still too big, nudge the threshold $\\tau $ upward and resample until it fits. Because the working set is then at most $(1+f_{max})$ times L2Seg's, you are guaranteed to keep at least $1/(1+f_{max})$ of L2Seg's per-round speedup (about 77% at $f_{max}=0.3).$ The user controls the speed-versus-quality trade directly through $f_{max}.$\n   - _Why_: Reopening too much would erase the very speedup we are trying to preserve; the cap makes the speed-versus-quality trade an explicit dial the user controls.\n9. Each round, add up across all edges the product of the reopen probability, the realized-gain signal, and the edge travel cost (Eq. 4), and record this single number next to how much the plain unaccelerated solver reduced cost. This number is positive exactly when some reopened edge crosses a frozen/active boundary with real gain, and it is zero (reproducing L2Seg) when no such edge exists — so it both estimates the recovered improvement and proves precisely when the soft method beats the hard cut.\n\n*The improvement-recovery decomposition and when-it-wins certificate: the soft membership strictly beats the hard cut exactly when $\\Delta _{total} > 0$ (some boundary-crossing positive-gain edge exists), and $\\Delta _{total}$ collapses to zero — recovering L2Seg — when no such edge exists.*\n$$ \\Delta_{\\mathrm{total}} = \\sum_{e} w_e \\, g_e(t) \\, s_e \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This single number both estimates the recovered improvement and certifies precisely when the soft method beats the hard cut — so any win is provably tied to the reopen idea, not to lucky tuning.\n10. Repeat steps step 2 (Run a single round of $the\\dots )–step 9$ (Each round) until the best solution stops improving for a set number of rounds or a wall-clock limit is hit, then report three things: the final gap to the reference solution, the wall-clock speedup over the plain solver, and how many reopen events occurred. 【author decision: what the gap is measured against — the published best-known solution where one exists, or the plain solver run to a long reference budget where it does not (comparable to other papers versus self-contained).】\n   - _Why_: These are exactly the quantities the falsification test checks: lower gap, mostly-retained speedup, and how often reopening actually fired.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 可重开分段：面向车辆路径问题的搜索反馈驱动自适应分解\n\n**方法名称.** Reopenable Segments (REOSEG)\n\n## 研究动机\n现代车辆路径问题（VRP，即为一支卡车车队规划配送路线）的求解器，靠把当前路线方案中看起来已经稳定的部分冻结、只对其余部分继续优化来加速。目前最好的学习方法 L2Seg（Learning to Segment for VRP）训练一个网络，把解的每一段标记为「稳定」（冻结）或「不稳定」（继续优化），再把稳定段合并成固定的块，在余下的搜索中保持不变。这让它比单独运行经典求解器快 2 到 7 倍。\n\n问题在于：冻结决定是在搜索还没产生任何关于它是否正确的证据之前、一次性提前做出的。如果网络把某个区域错标成「稳定」，而实际上紧挨着它就有一个能改进的好动作，那这个区域就被永久锁死、再也无法优化——于是最终路线质量被压在比普通求解器能达到的水平更低的地方。相关方法也有同样的盲点：Decompose-Route-Improve 用人工设计的规则一次性切分大问题、之后从不回看；Neural Cluster-First-Route-Second 一次性把客户分配给车辆，事后无法再移动客户。\n\n现在能修复这一点，恰恰是因为 L2Seg 把段的稳定性变成了一个「学习」出来的量：它的网络本身就会输出一个数，预测某个区域能带来多少改进。我们可以把这个预测和搜索实际取得的改进相比较，并把两者的差距——免费、且无需任何新标签——当作一个信号，提示「这个冻结区域值得重新打开」。补上这个缺口，就把冻结边界从一个永久天花板变成了一个能在搜索中自我纠正的东西，在保留大部分加速的同时找回普通求解器本可达到的质量。\n\n## 方法\n### 实现增益信号\n*用预测改进与实际改进之差，制造一个无标签的逐边信号，标出该重开哪些冻结区域。*\n\n1. 原封不动复用 L2Seg 已预训练好的节点编码器(node encoder)网络。在其上加一个很小的线性输出层(称为 value head)：对路线方案中的每条边，取该边两个端点节点的编码器嵌入连同这条边的行驶成本，输出一个数——这条边若被重开还能节省多少行驶成本。把这一层初始化为零，使它在学到东西之前预测「零节省」。主网络保持冻结，只训练这个新层和少量缩放参数。\n   - _为什么_: 我们需要一个廉价的「可用改进」预测，以便之后和实际发生的情况比较；复用已训练好的 segmenter 可以避免从零重新学习路由。\n2. 只在不稳定部分上运行一轮底层求解器(LKH-3、HGS，或学习型大邻域搜索(Large-Neighborhood Search, LNS)——一种反复拆掉并重建解的一部分的方法)，冻结块保持固定不动。对求解器被允许改动的每条边，记录它这一轮实际取得的行驶成本下降。冻结边不获得直接测量。\n   - _为什么_: 这给出了搜索真正获得多少收益的事实依据，正是冻结决定当初所缺的证据。\n3. 对每条冻结边计算实现增益信号 $g_{e}(Eq.$ 1)：用 value head 预测的改进减去搜索实际取得的改进，只保留正部，再除以该边行驶成本，得到一个无量纲数。对一条从未被重开(因而没有实测改进)的边，借用同一路线中最近一条已重开边的实测改进，「最近」指两条边中点之间的直线距离最小；若该路线本轮没有任何已重开边，则取零。全程不使用任何人工标签。【作者需决定：与实际相比较的预测改进，取 value head 当前轮的预测，还是该边上一次可用时所做的预测——更灵敏 还是 与实际更因果对齐。】\n\n*为冻结边 e 在第 t 轮制造的无标签实现增益信号：预测改进减去实际改进的正部，再除以边的行驶成本 $s_{e}$ 做无量纲化。全程不使用任何真值 reopen 标签。*\n$$ g_e(t) = \\frac{\\max\\!\\left(0,\\; c_{\\mathrm{pred}}(e,t) - c_{\\mathrm{real}}(e,t)\\right)}{s_e} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 当网络对不稳定部分预测的改进多于搜索实际兑现时，冻结的邻居很可能藏着可用收益——这个落差恰恰就是告诉我们该在哪里重开的免费信号。\n4. 每轮之后，在有实测的边上，通过减小「预测值与搜索实际取得值之差的平方」来训练 value head，做一步或几步梯度更新。只有 value head 和少量缩放参数发生改变，主网络保持冻结。唯一的教学信号是求解器自身的结果，绝不引入外部正确答案。\n   - _为什么_: 预测器仅凭求解器自身的结果就能逐步变好——无需外部标签——使整个回路保持自监督。\n\n### 软性重开隶属\n*把硬性稳定/不稳定切分松弛为分数重开概率，并严格泛化 L2Seg。*\n\n5. 用一个 sigmoid 把每条冻结边的信号 $g_{e}$ 转成软性重开概率 $w_{e}$：度量 $g_{e}$ 超过阈值 $\\tau $ 的程度、再用温度 $\\beta $ 缩放(Eq. 2；默认 $\\tau =0.05$，$\\beta =0.02)$。然后对每条冻结边独立地按该概率掷一次有偏硬币，决定是否把它拉回下一轮的可动边工作集；被抽中的边会被求解器实际重新考虑。把 $\\beta $ 取得很小，就退回到与原始 L2Seg 切分一致的硬性是/否决定。\n\n*软性分数 reopen 隶属度：以温度 $\\beta $ 对实现增益 $g_{e}$ 与阈值 $\\tau $ 之差做 sigmoid。当 $\\beta  \\to  0$ 时退化为 L2Seg 的硬 ${0,1}$ 切分，故软对象严格泛化了硬分解。*\n$$ w_e = \\sigma\\!\\left(\\frac{g_e(t) - \\tau}{\\beta}\\right), \\qquad w_e \\in [0,1] \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 用软概率而非硬性是/否，可以让边界重叠并温和地修正；把 $\\beta $ 推向 0 会精确恢复原始的 L2Seg 硬切分，因此本方法始终只是对已验证方法的泛化。\n6. 加一个开关，把温度 $\\beta $ 设为(实际上的)零，使每个重开概率变成硬性的 0 或 1，从而精确复现 L2Seg 原始的冻结分段。把这个关掉重开机制的对照臂跑一遍，就能看出软性重开这一思想本身贡献了多少。\n   - _为什么_: 与这个「精确 L2Seg」臂对比，可以孤立出重开机制本身的贡献，排除收益来自其他因素的可能。\n\n### 自适应粒度\n*用信号在每条路线上选择划算之处的细/粗分解尺度。*\n\n7. 在每条路线内，按信号 $g_{e}$ 对可重开边排序，取前 $k_{route}$ 条以完整的逐边细粒度重开；$k_{route}$ 为该路线可重开边数的固定比例 $\\rho ($默认 0.2)向上取整(Eq. 3)。把该路线其余所有边像 L2Seg 那样合并成粗块。结果是每条路线获得各自的分解粒度——在实现增益信号集中处细、其余处粗。\n\n*每条路线的自适应粒度：在一条路线内按 $g_{e}$ 取前 $k_{route}$ 条边以细粒度重开，$k_{route}$ 为该路线可重开边数的密度比例 $\\rho $。*\n$$ k_{\\mathrm{route}} = \\left\\lceil \\rho \\cdot |\\,\\mathcal{E}_{\\mathrm{elig}}\\,| \\right\\rceil \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 只在实现增益信号显示划算的地方投入细粒度精力，其他地方保持粗粒度（快）——让粒度随局部机会自适应。\n\n### 加速保护与证书\n*限制重开预算以保证保留加速，并记录证明重开何时获胜的证书。*\n\n8. 限制重开量：每轮重开的边不超过比例 $f_{max}($默认 0.3)，只保留概率最高的那部分；若工作集仍然过大，则上调阈值 $\\tau $ 并重新抽样直到放得下。由于此时工作集至多为 L2Seg 的 $(1+f_{max})$ 倍，可保证至少保留 L2Seg 单轮加速的 $1/(1+f_{max})(f_{max}=0.3$ 时约 77%)。用户直接通过 $f_{max}$ 控制「速度对质量」的取舍。\n   - _为什么_: 重开太多会抹掉我们正想保留的加速；这个上限把「速度对质量」的取舍变成用户可控的明确旋钮。\n9. 每轮把所有边上「重开概率 $\\times $ 实现增益信号 $\\times $ 边行驶成本」的乘积相加(Eq. 4)，并把这个单一数值与普通(未加速)求解器降低的成本并列记录。当某条重开边跨越冻结/激活边界且带真实增益时它严格为正，当不存在此类边时为零(复现 L2Seg)——因此它既估计恢复的改进，又精确证明软方法何时优于硬切分。\n\n*改进恢复分解，同时是 when-it-wins 证书：当 $\\Delta _{total} > 0$（存在跨界正增益边）时软隶属严格优于硬切分；当不存在此类边时 $\\Delta _{total}$ 坍缩为零，精确恢复 L2Seg。*\n$$ \\Delta_{\\mathrm{total}} = \\sum_{e} w_e \\, g_e(t) \\, s_e \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这个单一数值既估计了恢复的改进，又精确证明软方法何时优于硬切分——因此任何胜出都可证地系于重开思想，而非侥幸调参。\n10. 重复 第2步（只在不稳定部分上运行一轮底层$\\dots $）–第9步（每轮把所有边上「重开概率$\\dots $），直到最优解在设定的若干轮内不再改进或达到墙钟上限，然后报告三项：相对参照解的最终间隙、相对普通求解器的墙钟加速比，以及重开事件总数。【作者需决定：间隙以何为参照——有公开最优解(best-known solution)的实例用它，没有的则用普通求解器跑到长参照预算的结果(与他人可比 还是 自成体系)。】\n   - _为什么_: 这些正是证伪测试要检验的量：更低的间隙、基本保留的加速，以及重开实际触发的频率。\n\n"},{"id":"70","run_dir":"run_prompt70_entityalign","index":70,"title":"Conformal Correspondence Trust for Noise-Robust Multi-modal Entity Alignment","title_zh":"面向噪声对应的多模态实体对齐的共形对应可信度方法 (Conformal Correspondence Trust)","method_name":"Conformal Correspondence Trust (CCT)","hook":"Every robust MMEA method computes a per-correspondence reliability and then ranks entities as if that reliability were certain, so its hardest, most-corrupted pairs are exactly the ones it is silently most confident about. We recast the keep/discard decision as a calibrated selective-alignment object with a finite-sample risk guarantee and a graph-topological evidence channel the corrupted encoder cannot see, so the method knows how much to trust each of its own correspondence judgments and provably abstains where it cannot.","anchor_pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","anchor_pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","domain_category":"Graph Learning","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf carries a calibrated measure of how trustworthy its OWN per-correspondence reliability estimate is into the final alignment decision: every robust MMEA method (RULE semanticscholar:64e64fbd449d55e5467db3436d16f2b42fb68681, LLM-filtering openalex:W4416035320) collapses noisy-vs-clean to a point decision and then ranks entities as if that decision were certain, so on the hardest pairs a confident-but-wrong reliability is never widened, deferred, or abstained on — the missing outc","pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by recasting the opaque 'how reliable is this reliability' question about the fixed alignment model as a measurement object — a conformal-risk-controlled selective predictor whose per-pair nonconformity score yields a calibrated reject region certified by a causal abstention intervention, exactly the C00 move of reframing an opaque uncertainty question as an estimator validated by perturbing the model.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf detects correspondence noise using a signal that is INDEPENDENT of the cross-modal/cross-graph similarity encoder the noise has already corrupted: RULE's reliability (uncertainty+consensus), MCSFF's consistency/specificity (openalex:W4403996082), and IBMEA's information bottleneck (openalex:W4403791722) all read their noise signal off the same fused embedding space, so a noisy pair that fools the encoder is unflagged — the missing outcome is corroboration of a correspondence fr","pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","sub_pattern":"C13 (Encode Structure by Construction)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by making the two-graph relational connectivity the encoded prior: a parameter-free shared-neighbor / relation-typed-path overlap statistic computed over the alignment-induced bipartite graph supplies a noise signal captured by graph construction rather than read off the fused embedding, the C13 move of capturing a named structural statistic (local overlap) by wiring rather than by a generic learned model.","is_anchor":false},{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions whether reliable correspondences must be committed to a single hard clean/noisy partition at all (the shared inherited assumption): every leaf descends from the divide-then-reweight node and inherits 'first decide which pairs are clean, then learn on that decision' — none tests whether the alignment objective can be optimized while keeping the correspondence assignment itself as an unresolved, distribution-valued variable rather than a thresholded label.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"reframe_as_solvable_object","how_closed":"Framing half (C05): the load-bearing identifiability convenience is 'the clean/noisy assignment must be thresholded before learning'; we pivot it to a substitute structural condition — the topological-overlap channel makes the latent assignment recoverable up to a per-pair posterior without thresholding. Companion deliverable (reframe_as_solvable_object): the runnable artifact is a joint objective that optimizes alignment while keeping the correspondence assignment as a distribution-valued latent variable (EM over a soft assignment posterior), shipping the method the audit alone could not.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"multi-modal entity alignment (MMEA) over multi-modal knowledge graphs under noisy correspondence","n_papers":46,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":23},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":18,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Triplet-aware graph neural networks for factorized multi-modal knowledge graph entity alignment"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"LoginMEA: Local-to-Global Interaction Network for Multi-modal Entity Alignment"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Position-Aware Active Learning for Multi-Modal Entity Alignment"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Multi-modal Entity Alignment via Position-enhanced Multi-label Propagation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Feature Enhancement for Multi-modal Entity Alignment Transformer"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Noise-powered Multi-modal Knowledge Graph Representation Framework"}],"more":12},{"year":2025,"n":20,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Mitigating Modality Bias in Multi-modal Entity Alignment from a Causal Perspective"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Learning with Dual-level Noisy Correspondence for Multi-modal Entity Alignment"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Multi-Modal Entity in One Word: Aligning Multi-Level Semantics for Multi-Modal Knowledge Graph Completion"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Clue Discovery based on Multi-modal Entity Alignment enhanced by Image Generation and Structure Embedding"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"MFIEA: entity alignment through multi-modal feature interaction and knowledge facts"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Multi-granular Negative Sampling Framework for Multi-modal Knowledge Graph Completion"}],"more":14},{"year":2026,"n":8,"papers":[{"source":"arxiv","title":"MyGram: Modality-aware Graph Transformer with Global Distribution for Multi-modal Entity Alignment"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"M$^3$Eval: Multi-Modal Memory Evaluation through Cognitively-Grounded Video Tasks"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"FOCAL: A Novel Benchmarking Technique for Multi-modal Agents"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Every Little Helps: Building Knowledge Graph Foundation Model with Fine-grained Transferable Multi-modal Tokens"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Leveraging Graph Structure in Seq2Seq Models for Knowledge Graph Link Prediction"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Knowledge Graphs as the Missing Data Layer for LLM-Based Industrial Asset Operations"}],"more":2}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":4,"share":0.087},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":2,"share":0.043},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":2,"share":0.043},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":2,"share":0.043},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution; structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"architectural_operator_substitution; structural_prior_encoding","count":2,"share":0.043},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":2,"share":0.043},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate; self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"decompose_and_delegate; self_supervised_signal_engineering","count":2,"share":0.043},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding; unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"structural_prior_encoding; unify_into_shared_representation","count":1,"share":0.022}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"In MMEA under noisy correspondence, robustness methods such as RULE (semanticscholar:64e64fbd449d55e5467db3436d16f2b42fb68681) estimate a per-pair reliability scalar w_i from an uncertainty+consensus rule computed on the SAME cross-modal/cross-graph similarity that the noisy correspondences have already corrupted, then partition pairs into clean/noisy/uncertain subsets at a fixed threshold and reweight a robust contrastive loss; LLM-filtering (openalex:W4416035320) and consistency/specificity fusion (openalex:W4403996082) likewise commit to a hard per-pair keep/discard decision. Because the reliability quantity is a deterministic point estimate produced by the very encoder the noise degrades, it is self-referential: on exactly the hardest pairs (visually-confusable wrong images, false couplings like a movie entity mislabeled with a real-life couple) the corrupted encoder assigns a confident-but-wrong reliability, and the pipeline has no calibrated measure of how much to TRUST each reliability value, so it cannot widen its uncertainty, defer the decision, or propagate that doubt into the final entity-ranking. The failure is the absence of any quantity that says how reliable the reliability estimate itself is and that survives into the alignment decision — several distinct cures (Bayesian posterior over correspondence, conformal abstention, structure-graph cross-check independent of the encoder, evidential second-order uncertainty) could each supply it.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:64e64fbd449d55e5467db3436d16f2b42fb68681","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"RULE estimates per-correspondence reliability w_i = (1-u)*alpha + c*(1-alpha) from Dempster-Shafer evidence (uncertainty u) plus cross-graph consensus c, divides inter-graph and intra-entity pairs into clean/noisy/uncertain subsets, and runs robust attribute fusion + robust contrastive discrepancy elimination, with a test-time correspondence reasoning module. Residue: the reliability is a deterministic scalar produced by the same noise-corrupted similarity encoder, committed via a fixed-threshold hard 3-way division, with no calibrated uncertainty ON the reliability itself and no abstention/deferral pathway — confidently-wrong reliability on the hardest pairs flows unchecked into the final alignment ranking, and graph topology is used only inside the same fused representation rather than as an encoder-independent reliability cross-check."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416035320","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Breaking the Noise Barrier uses an LLM to semantically filter and enhance intra-modality content (e.g. visually inconsistent images) before MMEA fusion. Residue: the LLM acts as a hard pre-filter that discards/keeps content with no calibrated soft reliability and addresses only intra-modality noise, leaving inter-graph correspondence noise and the propagation of filtering uncertainty into alignment unmodeled."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4403996082","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"MCSFF separates modality consistency from modality specificity during fusion to avoid one modality obscuring critical cues. Residue: the consistency/specificity split assumes the per-entity attribute pairings are correct; it has no mechanism to detect mismatched (noisy) correspondences and no uncertainty quantity governing how much each modality's contribution should be trusted."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4402753983","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Learning to Rematch Mismatched Pairs (L2RM) recasts partially-mismatched cross-modal pairs as an optimal-transport re-assignment problem to recover correct matches for retrieval. Residue: rematching operates on an unstructured retrieval set with a single mass-preserving transport, ignoring the two-graph relational structure of MMEA and providing no calibrated confidence on whether a recovered match should be trusted at decision time."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"multi-modal entity alignment (MMEA) over multi-modal knowledge graphs under noisy correspondence","venue":"ICLR / NeurIPS / ICML / SIGIR","time":"2026","data":["FB15K-DB15K","FB15K-YAGO15K","Multi-OpenEA","ICEWS (high-noise benchmark, >50% NC)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"graph representation learning, multi-modal fusion, learning-with-noisy-labels","preference":"both","baseline":"RULE (Learning with Dual-level Noisy Correspondence for MMEA), IBMEA, MCSFF, LLM-guided semantic filtering (Breaking the Noise Barrier)","limitation":"existing MMEA robustness methods estimate per-correspondence reliability as a scalar weight from the same similarity model that the noise corrupts, then make a hard clean/noisy division at a fixed threshold; the resulting point estimate carries no calibrated uncertainty into the final ranking, so confidently-wrong reliability scores on the noisiest pairs still drive alignment and the method cannot abstain or defer on the correspondences it is least sure about.","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object all three legs read from and write to is a per-correspondence TRUST POSTERIOR p(z_ij | x, G) over a binary latent z_ij in {match, mismatch} for every annotated correspondence (entity-entity, entity-attribute, attribute-attribute), NOT a thresholded reliability label. Leg 1 (anchor, C00) reframes 'how much to trust the alignment of pair (i,j)' as a selective-prediction measurement: define a nonconformity score s_ij = 1 - E[z_ij] (one minus posterior match-probability), reserve a held-out calibration split of seed alignments with known correctness, and apply split conformal risk control to choose a single threshold tau so the expected alignment error on RETAINED pairs is provably <= a user-set level alpha_risk (default 0.1); pairs with s_ij > tau are ABSTAINED (deferred, not ranked). tau is computed once on calibration data by the conformal quantile formula tau = the ceil((n+1)(1-alpha_risk))/n empirical quantile of calibration nonconformity scores; alpha_risk is the only free knob and is a stated hyperparameter. Leg 2 (C13) supplies the evidence the posterior is built from, half of it ENCODER-INDEPENDENT: for a candidate pair (i,j) compute an embedding-similarity evidence e_sim (dot product of fused entity embeddings, the only encoder-derived term) AND a topological-overlap evidence e_top = Jaccard overlap of the alignment-induced neighbor sets, i.e. |N(i) aligned-to N(j)| / |N(i) union N(j)| using ONLY the current high-confidence anchor set as the alignment map, plus a relation-typed 2-hop path-agreement count; e_top is computed from graph wiring and the anchor set, so a wrong image that fools the encoder does not move it. The posterior is p(z_ij=match) = sigmoid(beta_sim * e_sim + beta_top * e_top - b), where beta_sim, beta_top, b are three scalar parameters fit by the EM of Leg 3 (units bridged by the learned betas; e_sim, e_top are both z-scored per batch before weighting). Leg 3 (C05 + companion reframe) removes the hard partition: instead of dividing pairs and reweighting a contrastive loss on the decision, we treat z_ij as latent and optimize the alignment encoder f and the posterior parameters jointly by EM — E-step computes p(z_ij) from current f and the two evidences; M-step maximizes the expected robust contrastive log-likelihood E_z[ z_ij * log-align(i,j) ] (a soft-assignment InfoNCE where each pair's contribution is weighted by its posterior, never thresholded). The pivot (C05 step 2) is that the topological-overlap condition is the substitute structural constraint that makes the latent z identifiable without the distributional thresholding assumption RULE imports — local overlap survives encoder corruption, so the posterior is recoverable up to the seed-anchor set rather than up to a hand-set threshold. The three legs share one object: Leg 2 builds the posterior's evidence, Leg 3 fits and marginalizes it without thresholding, Leg 1 calibrates a reject region on it with a finite-sample guarantee.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The three gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules because all three are facets of one decision object — the correspondence assignment: gap 3 says don't threshold it (keep it a posterior), gap 2 says build it from an encoder-independent channel, gap 1 says calibrate trust on it; the evidence that they share rather than fork is that conformal calibration (leg 1) is only honest if the score s_ij comes from a posterior (leg 3) whose evidence includes a non-fooled channel (leg 2), so removing any leg makes another leg's guarantee vacuous. (b) Considered alternatives: (i) a Bayesian deep ensemble for second-order uncertainty — rejected because it is encoder-internal (would re-occupy the fooled-encoder node and gives no finite-sample coverage guarantee); (ii) a bare reject option on RULE's existing w_i — rejected as a regression to collateral node c1 (plain selective classification) with no calibration target and no independent evidence; (iii) first-order evidential reweighting (Dempster-Shafer) — rejected because RULE already does this (node n3 / collateral c2), so it adds nothing. Conformal risk control was chosen specifically because it supplies the SECOND-order, distribution-free trust the regression flag demands.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: train the full model and RULE on FB15K-DB15K, FB15K-YAGO15K, and the high-noise ICEWS benchmark (>50% NC) under matched injected-noise rates 0/20/40/50%, measuring Hits@1, MRR, coverage, and risk-controlled error on retained pairs. If the candidate works, on the 40-50% noise splits Hits@1 on RETAINED pairs INCREASES over RULE (which ranks all pairs) while the conformal risk-controlled error stays at or below the set alpha_risk=0.1 — i.e. the method buys accuracy by honestly abstaining on the pairs it cannot trust, and the abstained set is enriched for true noisy correspondences (precision of abstention > base noise rate). The named load-bearing variable is e_top, the encoder-independent topological-overlap evidence. Negative control: randomly permute e_top across pairs (ablating its producer while keeping its marginal distribution); prediction — Hits@1 on retained high-noise pairs falls back toward RULE's level and abstention precision drops to chance, because the posterior then has no signal the fooled encoder lacks. This is the real Popper test: 'permute e_top -> downstream Hits@1 on retained noisy pairs degrades' tests the mechanism, not the definition (permuting e_top would trivially change e_top's own value). Positive control: a posterior built from e_top alone (no e_sim) should recover most of the noise-robustness gain on the 50% split, identifying the topological channel as the load-bearing source.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:64e64fbd449d55e5467db3436d16f2b42fb68681","delta":"RULE estimates a deterministic reliability scalar w_i from encoder-derived uncertainty+consensus and thresholds it into a hard clean/noisy/uncertain division; we keep the correspondence as a distribution-valued latent z_ij, add a finite-sample conformal risk guarantee with a calibrated abstention region that RULE has no analogue of, and build the posterior partly from an encoder-INDEPENDENT topological-overlap evidence RULE never computes."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416035320","delta":"Breaking the Noise Barrier uses an LLM as a hard keep/discard pre-filter on intra-modality content with no calibrated confidence; we never discard, we marginalize over a calibrated trust posterior and provide a coverage-controlled abstention with a stated risk level, and we model inter-graph correspondence noise it does not touch."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4403791722","delta":"IBMEA compresses redundant information in the fused embedding under assumed-correct pairings; we do not assume correct pairings — we infer a per-pair match posterior and certify a risk-controlled retained set, a guarantee IBMEA's information-bottleneck objective does not produce."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4402753983","delta":"L2RM rematches mismatched pairs via a single mass-preserving optimal transport over an unstructured retrieval set; we exploit two-graph relational topology as an encoder-independent evidence channel and attach a distribution-free conformal abstention, neither of which OT rematching provides."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:64e64fbd449d55e5467db3436d16f2b42fb68681","what_step_was_missed":"RULE constructed a per-correspondence reliability estimator and a fixed-threshold three-way pair division, but to already contain our contribution it would have needed to (a) construct a finite-sample calibrated reject region over that reliability — a conformal risk-control derivation that turns the scalar into a coverage-guaranteed abstention, which it never derives — and (b) supply the posterior with a structural evidence term computed from the alignment-induced graph topology rather than from the same fused embedding, an encoder-independent identifying condition it did not construct; without (b) the latent assignment is not recoverable without the thresholding assumption (a) would otherwise still need."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":256,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"Layer 1 did not fire: gap_closure_reject_check is borderline (no candidate_match: yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat is adjacent-but-addressable (ReCon overlaps only Leg 2's encoder-independence intuition, not the conformal-abstention headline, so it is not exact-mechanism overlap). Choosing revise rather than advance because two borderline findings hit load-bearing structure — the C05 recovery-sufficiency claim (gap_closure_reject_check entry 3, lesson 'imposing structural constraints ... without proving those constraints are sufficient for recovery') must be scoped to honest recovery-up-to-anchor-map, and paper_pointed_threat.addressable_via names a specific field (differentiation_from_lit) needing a ReCon delta.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf carries a calibrated measure of how trustworthy its OWN per-correspondence reliability estimate is into the final alignment decision: every robust MMEA method (RULE semanticscholar:64e64fbd449d55e5467db3436d16f2b42fb68681, LLM-filtering openalex:W4416035320) collapses noisy-vs-clean to a point decision and then ranks entities as if that decision were certain, so on the hardest pairs a confident-but-wrong reliability is never widened, deferred, or abstained on — the missing outcome is a noise-robust alignment that can say how much to trust each of its own correspondence judgments and act differently when that trust is low.","main_pattern":"reframe_as_solvable_object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The signature failure is treating the reframing as a mechanical wrapper — pointing an established estimator at a new target without re-deriving why the resulting scores are faithful, with no causal validation that the identified quantity actually drives behavior.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Proposing a new attribution definition without an axiomatic or causal argument for why it should count as ground-truth collapses the moment a reviewer asks why this is the real importance.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The trust posterior's correctness criterion is a finite-sample conformal risk guarantee (coverage <= alpha_risk on a held-out calibration split with known correctness), not an asserted definition, and it is causally validated by the e_top-permutation negative control."},{"lesson_quoted":"Conflating a methodological artifact — a computation-granularity difference, a degenerate zero baseline — with genuine signal undermines the entire premise once the confound is identified.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The negative control permutes e_top while preserving its marginal distribution, isolating the topological signal from any granularity/baseline artifact, so the predicted Hits@1 drop cannot be a bookkeeping artifact."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pointing an off-the-shelf decomposition at a coarser input granularity without showing the coarser units preserve the signal reads as a wrapper, not a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Conformal risk control is applied to a newly-constructed correspondence trust posterior, not pointed unchanged at a coarser granularity; the contribution is the object the calibration runs on, with an ablation showing it is load-bearing."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf detects correspondence noise using a signal that is INDEPENDENT of the cross-modal/cross-graph similarity encoder the noise has already corrupted: RULE's reliability (uncertainty+consensus), MCSFF's consistency/specificity (openalex:W4403996082), and IBMEA's information bottleneck (openalex:W4403791722) all read their noise signal off the same fused embedding space, so a noisy pair that fools the encoder is unflagged — the missing outcome is corroboration of a correspondence from a source the encoder cannot already see (e.g. relational/graph-topological agreement) rather than another statistic of the same potentially-fooled representation.","main_pattern":"structural_prior_encoding","sub_pattern":"C13 (Encode Structure by Construction)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The most common failure is a domain-motivated architecture with no guarantee that its wiring captures the claimed structure, plus inflated/balanced evaluation that hides that a hand-crafted structural-proximity heuristic already matches the learned construction.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Combining borrowed modules (global plus local streams, attention plus state tracking) with no genuinely new mechanism reads as incremental even when the combination is sensible.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The topological-overlap evidence channel resembles classical neighbor-consistency signals; what is new is its role as an ENCODER-INDEPENDENT term inside a calibrated trust posterior, but a reviewer could read e_top alone as a borrowed structural heuristic, so the positive-control (e_top-only) experiment is needed to show it carries load."},{"lesson_quoted":"Omitting closely-related SOTA baselines and the simplest correlation or heuristic comparison makes any claimed structural advantage unverifiable.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The evaluation includes RULE and IBMEA as SOTA baselines and the e_top-only positive control plus the permutation negative control as the simplest heuristic/correlation comparisons, exactly the comparisons this lesson demands."},{"lesson_quoted":"A domain-grounded architecture lacking any theoretical guarantee that its wiring captures the claimed structure — and lacking a uniqueness or identifiability argument — leaves reviewers unable to credit the structural claim.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The C05 leg supplies the identifiability argument: the topological-overlap condition is the substitute structural constraint under which the latent z is recoverable, tying the wiring to a recovery guarantee rather than leaving it un-justified."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions whether reliable correspondences must be committed to a single hard clean/noisy partition at all (the shared inherited assumption): every leaf descends from the divide-then-reweight node and inherits 'first decide which pairs are clean, then learn on that decision' — none tests whether the alignment objective can be optimized while keeping the correspondence assignment itself as an unresolved, distribution-valued variable rather than a thresholded label.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"reframe_as_solvable_object","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Advertising an identifiability or 'consistency' property while the proof omits the decisive object, or imposing structural constraints to claim recovery without proving those constraints are sufficient, collapses the contribution the moment a reviewer checks the theorem.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Imposing structural constraints to claim interpretability or disentanglement without proving those constraints are sufficient for recovery leaves the result indistinguishable from a post-hoc heuristic.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The candidate states the topological-overlap condition is the substitute that makes z recoverable up to the seed-anchor set, but the sufficiency claim is currently an EM-convergence argument rather than a stated-and-proven recovery theorem; load-bearing, so it must be scoped honestly (recovery up to the anchor map) and enforced by the algorithm, not just asserted."},{"lesson_quoted":"Proving identifiability conditions the algorithm neither enforces nor verifies creates a theory-practice disconnect that undermines both the soundness and the significance of the claim.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The EM M-step directly enforces the soft-assignment objective the condition requires and the anchor-refresh step verifies the high-posterior set, so the condition the pivot relies on is operationalized, not left as a disconnected theorem."},{"lesson_quoted":"Stacking two established frameworks and re-proving identifiability of the union reads as incremental unless the pivoted assumption was genuinely load-bearing and the union admits a regime neither framework could reach alone.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The pivoted assumption (hard thresholding before learning) is genuinely load-bearing — RULE's whole division pipeline rests on it — and the soft-posterior + conformal regime reaches calibrated abstention that neither divide-then-reweight nor plain conformal prediction reaches alone."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No gap_closure entry triggered (no Reject lesson marked candidate_match: yes). Two entries are borderline: the C13 leg (entry 2) because e_top could be read as a borrowed structural heuristic absent the positive-control showing it carries load, and the C05 leg (entry 3) because the recovery-sufficiency claim is currently an EM argument rather than a proven theorem and must be scoped to recovery up to the anchor map."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf carries a calibrated measure of how trustworthy its OWN per-correspondence reliability estimate is into the final alignment decision...","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"C00 recasts an opaque uncertainty/responsibility question about an already-trained model as a concrete measurement object (estimator/selector/decomposition) whose correctness criterion is fidelity-to-a-fixed-model, certified by a causal intervention that flips behavior when the identified object is perturbed, rather than by plausibility.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism Leg 1 defines the nonconformity score s_ij = 1 - E[z_ij], maps the 'how reliable is this reliability' question onto split conformal risk control (the well-studied object), buys the guarantee with the calibration-quantile formula, and certifies fidelity via the e_top-permutation causal intervention that moves downstream Hits@1 — the C00 measurement-plus-causal-certification move is present, not generic.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf detects correspondence noise using a signal that is INDEPENDENT of the cross-modal/cross-graph similarity encoder...","sub_pattern":"C13 (Encode Structure by Construction)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"C13's signature move is making the relational connectivity topology itself the encoded prior — computing a named structural statistic (shared-neighbor counts, local overlap) over the wiring by construction so it is captured rather than relearned by a generic dense/attention model.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism Leg 2 computes e_top as the Jaccard overlap of alignment-induced neighbor sets plus a relation-typed 2-hop path-agreement count over the graph wiring and the anchor set — the named local-overlap statistic captured by construction, exactly C13's move, and explicitly NOT read off the fused embedding.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions whether reliable correspondences must be committed to a single hard clean/noisy partition at all...","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"C05 pins down the single load-bearing assumption an identifiability/recovery result rests on, then substitutes a DIFFERENT KIND of condition (structural/geometric/sparsity) that carries the same identifying power and that the setting plausibly satisfies, re-deriving recovery up to an accepted ambiguity class.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism Leg 3 names the load-bearing assumption (thresholded clean/noisy division before learning), substitutes the structural topological-overlap condition that makes the latent z recoverable up to the seed-anchor set without thresholding, and operationalizes it as the EM joint objective — the C05 distributional-to-structural pivot is performed; the companion reframe_as_solvable_object ships the runnable soft-assignment EM deliverable.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"All three legs instantiate their cited cluster's distinctive move (C00 conformal measurement + causal certification, C13 named local-overlap statistic by graph construction, C05 distributional-to-structural assumption pivot with the companion shipping the runnable EM), not the parent pattern's generic gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["reframe_as_solvable_object","structural_prior_encoding","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"None of the three reject-favored compositions matches — all three flagged compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component, which is absent from this composition set (the closest, heterogeneous_decomposition+reframe_as_solvable_object, is only a watch-list near-miss and still requires heterogeneous_decomposition, also absent)."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:ReCon-RelationConsistency-CVPR2025","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"ReCon (CVPR 2025, 'Enhancing True Correspondence Discrimination through Relation Consistency for Robust Noisy Correspondence Learning') is the nearest threat: it argues that similarity-only matching neglects intra-modal relation consistency for discriminating true vs false correspondences and builds a relation-consistency framework to flag mismatched pairs — which overlaps the SPIRIT of our Leg 2 claim that a relation/topology signal independent of pairwise similarity catches noise the similarity encoder misses. The candidate's claim stands or falls on whether its contribution is more than 'relation consistency catches noisy pairs': ReCon (a) operates on UNSTRUCTURED cross-modal retrieval datasets with no two-graph entity-alignment topology, so its relation consistency is within-modality batch relations, not our alignment-induced cross-graph neighbor/relation-path overlap computed against a seed-anchor map; and (b) ReCon has NO calibrated abstention / conformal risk guarantee and NO latent distribution-valued correspondence kept un-thresholded — it still produces a discrimination decision. Our anchor headline (Leg 1 conformal trust + Leg 3 un-thresholded posterior) is therefore not subsumed; only the encoder-independence intuition of Leg 2 partially overlaps. Secondary threat rMMEA (AAAI 2026) targets MISSING/noisy VISUAL modality via ranking-distillation + MI estimation, a different mechanism with no calibration and no inter-graph correspondence posterior, so it does not subsume the candidate.","addressable_via":"differentiation_from_lit should add an explicit ReCon entry stating the delta (alignment-induced cross-graph topological overlap + conformal abstention + un-thresholded posterior vs ReCon's within-modality relation consistency for retrieval with a hard discrimination decision); this is an addressable framing/differentiation gap, not exact-mechanism overlap."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat: ReCon (CVPR 2025) overlaps the encoder-independent relation-consistency intuition of Leg 2.","fix_direction":"Add a differentiation_from_lit entry for ReCon stating the substantive delta: ReCon uses WITHIN-modality batch relation consistency to make a hard true/false correspondence discrimination for unstructured cross-modal RETRIEVAL; we compute alignment-induced CROSS-GRAPH neighbor/relation-path overlap against a seed-anchor map as one evidence term inside a distribution-valued posterior, never threshold it, and wrap it in a finite-sample conformal abstention guarantee ReCon does not provide."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","issue":"gap_closure_reject_check entry 3 (C05) borderline: recovery-sufficiency of the topological-overlap condition is asserted via EM rather than a proven theorem.","fix_direction":"Scope the C05 recovery claim honestly in core_mechanism: state that the topological-overlap condition makes the latent assignment recoverable UP TO the seed-anchor map (the field's accepted ambiguity class here), that this is an EM stationarity argument enforced by the M-step rather than a global identifiability proof, and that the positive-control (e_top-only) experiment is the empirical evidence the condition alone carries recovery signal — do NOT advertise unconditional identifiability."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added a ReCon (CVPR 2025) entry stating the substantive delta: ReCon uses within-modality batch relation consistency for a hard true/false discrimination on unstructured cross-modal retrieval, whereas we compute alignment-induced cross-graph neighbor/relation-path overlap as one evidence term in an un-thresholded posterior wrapped in a conformal abstention guarantee."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Scoped the C05 recovery claim honestly: the topological-overlap condition makes the latent assignment recoverable UP TO the seed-anchor map as an EM-stationarity argument enforced by the M-step (not a global identifiability proof), with the e_top-only positive control as the empirical evidence."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Conformal Correspondence Trust for Noise-Robust Multi-modal Entity Alignment\n\n**Method.** Conformal Correspondence Trust (CCT)\n\n## Motivation\nMulti-modal entity alignment (MMEA) means matching the same real-world thing across two knowledge graphs (KGs) — databases of entities with their facts and pictures. The catch is that the labeled links these systems learn from are often wrong: on standard benchmarks more than half the image-to-entity or entity-to-entity links can be mislabeled (for example, a movie wrongly tagged with a real-life couple). Today's best noise-robust methods, like RULE (arXiv 2025-10) and an LLM-based filter called Breaking the Noise Barrier (2025-01), score how reliable each link is and then make a hard 'keep or throw away' choice. The problem is that this reliability score is computed by the very same model the noise has already fooled, and once it makes its keep/throw-away call it ranks entities as if that call were certain — so on exactly the trickiest links it is confidently wrong and has no way to say 'I'm not sure here.' What is missing is a number that says how much to trust the reliability score itself, and that actually changes what the system does when trust is low. This is solvable now because the noisy-link problem was just cleanly defined for MMEA, a statistical tool called conformal risk control can turn any score into a guarantee with a controllable error rate, and modern MMEA models already build the graph structure we need for a second, independent opinion. Closing this gap means the aligner can hand back a set of matches with a guaranteed error rate and honestly defer the ones it cannot trust, instead of silently committing wrong merges.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n\n1. Train the usual Multi-modal Entity Alignment (MMEA) model so we have the model whose mistakes we must not trust blindly. Concretely: encode each entity's picture with a frozen CLIP image model, its name/attributes with a standard text embedder, and its graph neighborhood with a 2-layer graph neural network; map all three into one shared 300-dimensional vector space and combine them with learnable per-modality weights into a single length-normalized entity vector $z_{i}.$ Train this on the FB15K-DB15K, FB15K-YAGO15K, and ICEWS benchmarks, and deliberately corrupt 0%, 20%, 40%, and 50% of the labeled links: for each corrupted link swap the correct partner for a random same-type wrong entity (cross-graph noise) and reshuffle some attribute-to-entity assignments among look-alikes (within-entity noise), saving which links you corrupted so you can grade trust later.\n   - _Why_: This is the model whose mistakes we must not trust blindly, so we build it first to know exactly where it gets fooled.\n\n### Encoder-independent evidence\n*Adds a graph-topology opinion the corrupted embedding cannot produce, so encoder-fooling links are still flagged.*\n\n2. For every labeled link (i,j) compute two scores. The first, $e_{sim},$ is just the dot product of the two entity vectors from the model. The second, $e_{top},$ uses NO model embedding at all — only the graph structure: take how much the two entities' direct-neighbor sets overlap once you translate j's neighbors into i's graph using the current trusted match dictionary, then add the number of 2-step relation paths that agree on both sides (same relation types in order, with the in-between and end entities themselves already matched). Put both terms on the same scale (unit spread) per batch and weight the path term by a balance factor (default 1). Because $e_{top}$ reads only the graph wiring, a wrong picture that fools the embedding cannot move it. Refresh $e_{top}$ each pass as the match dictionary improves; start that dictionary from the benchmark's given alignment seeds, or from the most confident $e_{sim}$ pairs after one warm-up pass if all seeds are noisy.\n\n*The topological evidence is the Jaccard overlap of neighbor sets matched through the current anchor map $\\Pi ,$ plus $\\lambda $ times a relation-typed 2-hop path-agreement count — computed from graph wiring, not embeddings.*\n$$ e^{\\text{top}}_{ij} = \\frac{|\\,N(i)\\;\\overset{\\Pi}{\\sim}\\;N(j)\\,|}{|\\,N(i)\\cup N(j)\\,|} + \\lambda\\,\\mathrm{path}^{(2)}_{r}(i,j) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: $e_{top}$ reads only the graph wiring, so a wrong picture that fools the embedding still gets caught by the entities' relationships disagreeing.\n\n### Un-thresholded trust posterior\n*Keeps each correspondence as a probability and trains the aligner over it by EM, replacing the hard clean/noisy partition.*\n\n3. Standardize the two scores $e_{sim}$ and $e_{top}$ within each batch (subtract the batch mean, divide by the batch spread, using every link in the batch since you do not know at training time which are noisy), and also keep a slow running average of those statistics so later calibration and testing stay stable. Combine the two standardized scores with three learnable numbers — a weight on each score and an offset — squashed through a logistic function into a probability $p(z_{ij})$ that the link is a true match. Start the three numbers at equal weights and zero offset; they are tuned only indirectly by the contrastive step in step 4 (Run the model-update half of $an\\dots ),$ never against any 'is this link correct' label. Keep this value as a probability and never round it to a hard clean-or-noisy tag.\n\n*The per-correspondence match posterior is a logistic function of two z-scored evidences — encoder similarity $\\tilde{e}_{sim}$ and encoder-independent topological overlap $\\tilde{e}_{top}$ — bridged by learned scalars $\\beta _{sim}, \\beta _{top}$ and bias b.*\n$$ p(z_{ij}=\\text{match}) = \\sigma(\\beta_{\\text{sim}}\\,\\tilde{e}^{\\text{sim}}_{ij} + \\beta_{\\text{top}}\\,\\tilde{e}^{\\text{top}}_{ij} - b) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Keeping it a probability avoids the hard early commitment every prior method makes and lets later steps reason about doubt.\n4. Run the model-update half of an Expectation-Maximization (EM) loop using a probability-weighted contrastive loss: for each entity, pull it toward its labeled partner with a strength equal to that link's probability $p(z_{ij}),$ and push it away from the other target-graph entities in the same batch (about 512 per batch, so one true partner against the rest), with a standard contrastive temperature of 0.08 on the length-normalized vectors; update the encoder and the three combining numbers together with the AdamW optimizer. Recompute the probabilities once at the start of each pass (the 'expectation' half) and keep them fixed through that pass's update steps, because the graph score only changes when the match dictionary is refreshed in step 5 (Rebuild the trusted $match\\dots ).$ Because the pull is probability-weighted, likely-true links bind tightly while suspected-noisy ones are gently down-weighted rather than thrown away, so no good signal is lost.\n\n*The M-step maximizes a soft-assignment InfoNCE in which each pair's contribution is weighted by its posterior $p(z_{ij})$ and never thresholded, so suspected-noisy pairs are down-weighted rather than deleted.*\n$$ \\mathcal{L} = -\\sum_{i,j} p(z_{ij})\\,\\log \\frac{\\exp(\\mathrm{sim}(i,j)/T)}{\\sum_{k}\\exp(\\mathrm{sim}(i,k)/T)} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Likely-true links are pulled together strongly and suspected-noisy ones are softly down-weighted instead of deleted, so good signal is never thrown away.\n5. Rebuild the trusted match dictionary from the links whose probability now exceeds 0.9, but keep it one-to-one: go through these links from highest probability down and accept a link only if neither of its two entities is already taken, dropping ties and conflicts (those still count as soft-weighted links in step 4 (Run the model-update half of $an\\dots )).$ Then repeat steps step 2 (For every labeled link)-step 4 (Run the model-update half of $an\\dots )$ until the dictionary barely changes between rounds (fewer than 1% of its entries move) or accuracy on a clean check set stops improving, stopping after at most 8 rounds (usually 5-8). The true links are recovered only relative to this anchor dictionary — an honest, limited guarantee from the loop reaching a stable point, not a claim of unconditional recovery — and each cleaner dictionary gives a better graph-only score, which in turn cleans the probabilities: a virtuous loop.\n   - _Why_: Each round's cleaner anchors give a better encoder-free graph score, which in turn cleans the probabilities — a virtuous loop with an honest, limited guarantee.\n\n### Conformal abstention\n*Calibrates one reject threshold with a finite-sample error guarantee and abstains where trust is low.*\n\n6. On a set-aside group of links whose true correctness you know, turn each probability into a doubt score equal to one minus that probability, then pick a single cutoff $\\tau $ using the conformal-quantile rule at error level 0.1. This cutoff carries a finite-sample promise: among the links you keep, the error rate stays at or below ten percent. In the noise-injection experiments the correctness labels for this calibration group come for free from your record of which links you corrupted. 【author decision: where the known-correctness calibration links come from in a real (non-injected) deployment — a human-verified budget or a trusted high-precision subset — and whether those calibration links are statistically interchangeable with the test links must be decided by the authors, because that is what makes the ten-percent promise actually hold in practice.】\n\n*The abstention threshold $\\tau $ is the conformal empirical quantile of calibration nonconformity scores $s_{ij}$ at level $1- \\alpha _{risk},$ giving a finite-sample guarantee that retained-pair error stays at or below $\\alpha _{risk}.$*\n$$ \\tau = \\widehat{Q}\\!\\left(\\frac{\\lceil (n_{\\text{cal}}+1)(1-\\alpha_{\\text{risk}})\\rceil}{n_{\\text{cal}}};\\; \\{s_{ij}\\}_{\\text{cal}}\\right),\\quad s_{ij}=1-p(z_{ij}=\\text{match}) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This single calibrated threshold comes with a finite-sample promise: the error among kept links stays at or below 10%.\n7. At test time, for each query entity rank the candidate matches by the model similarity (the dot product of their vectors, the same score training optimized). Take only the single best candidate, convert its probability into a doubt score (one minus the probability), and if that doubt score is above the cutoff $\\tau ,$ abstain: mark the query as 'deferred', pull it out of the automatic results, and send it to a human or second-pass review — do not fall back to the second-best candidate, because abstaining at the query level is what keeps the ten-percent error promise on the matches you do commit. If the doubt score is at or below $\\tau ,$ commit the best match. The system now behaves differently precisely where it is unsure, which is the whole point of the method.\n   - _Why_: The system now acts differently exactly where it is unsure, which is the behavior the whole method was built to provide.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 面向噪声对应的多模态实体对齐的共形对应可信度方法 (Conformal Correspondence Trust)\n\n**方法名称.** Conformal Correspondence Trust (CCT)\n\n## 研究动机\n多模态实体对齐 (MMEA) 是把两个知识图谱 (KG) 中指代同一现实事物的实体匹配起来——知识图谱是带有事实和图片的实体数据库。难点在于：系统赖以学习的标注链接常常是错的，在标准基准上超过一半的图片-实体或实体-实体链接可能标错（例如一部电影被错标成一对现实中的夫妇）。当前最好的抗噪方法，如 RULE (arXiv 2025-10) 和基于大模型的过滤器 Breaking the Noise Barrier (2025-01)，会给每个链接打一个可靠度分数，然后做一个硬性的 “保留或丢弃” 决定。问题是：这个可靠度分数恰恰是由已被噪声欺骗的同一个模型算出来的，而一旦它做出保留/丢弃的判断，就把实体当作确定无疑地排序——所以恰恰在最棘手的链接上它自信地犯错，却没有办法说 “这里我不确定”。缺失的，正是一个 “该有多信任这个可靠度分数本身” 的量，并且当信任度低时它能真正改变系统的行为。现在能解决，是因为噪声链接问题刚刚为 MMEA 被清晰定义；一个叫 conformal risk control 的统计工具能把任意分数变成可控错误率的保证；而现代 MMEA 模型已经构建了我们所需的图结构来提供第二个独立意见。补上这个缺口，意味着对齐器能交回一组带有保证错误率的匹配，并诚实地搁置它无法信任的那些，而不是悄悄地做出错误合并。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景\n\n1. 训练常规的多模态实体对齐 (Multi-modal Entity Alignment, MMEA) 模型——这是我们不能盲目信任的那个模型。具体做法：用冻结的 CLIP 图像模型编码每个实体的图片，用标准文本嵌入器编码其名称/属性，用 2 层图神经网络 (Graph Neural Network, GNN) 编码其图邻域；把这三者映射到同一个 300 维共享向量空间，再用可学习的各模态权重组合成单个经长度归一化的实体向量 $z_{i}$。在 FB15K-DB15K、FB15K-YAGO15K 和 ICEWS 基准上训练，并刻意污染 0%、20%、40%、50% 的标注链接：每条被污染的链接，把正确配对换成一个同类型的随机错误实体（跨图噪声），并在外形相近的候选间重排部分属性-实体分配（实体内噪声），同时记录你污染了哪些链接，以便后续给可信度打分。\n   - _为什么_: 这是我们不能盲目信任的模型，所以先把它建好，弄清它在哪里被骗。\n\n### 与编码器无关的证据\n*提供受损嵌入无法给出的图结构意见，使欺骗编码器的链接仍能被标记。*\n\n2. 对每条标注链接 (i,j) 计算两个分数。第一个 $e_{sim}$ 就是模型给出的两个实体向量的点积。第二个 $e_{top}$ 完全不用模型嵌入，只用图结构：先用当前可信的匹配字典把 j 的邻居翻译到 i 所在的图，再看两个实体的直接邻居集合重叠多少，然后加上两侧一致的 2 步关系路径数量（关系类型按顺序相同，且路径中间和端点的实体本身也已被匹配）。把这两项在每个 batch 内归到同一尺度（单位离散度），并给路径项一个平衡系数（默认为 1）。由于 $e_{top}$ 只读取图结构，一张骗过嵌入的错误图片无法改变它。随着匹配字典改善，每轮刷新 $e_{top}$；匹配字典从基准给定的对齐种子开始，若所有种子都含噪声，则在一轮预热后用最自信的 $e_{sim}$ 配对来初始化。\n\n*拓扑证据是经当前锚点映射 $\\Pi $ 匹配后的邻居集合 Jaccard 重叠，加上 $\\lambda $ 倍的按关系类型计的 2-hop 路径一致性计数——由图结构而非嵌入计算得到。*\n$$ e^{\\text{top}}_{ij} = \\frac{|\\,N(i)\\;\\overset{\\Pi}{\\sim}\\;N(j)\\,|}{|\\,N(i)\\cup N(j)\\,|} + \\lambda\\,\\mathrm{path}^{(2)}_{r}(i,j) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: $e_{top}$ 只读取图结构，所以即便一张错误图片骗过了嵌入，实体间关系的不一致仍能把它抓出来。\n\n### 未阈值化的可信度后验\n*把每个对应关系保留为概率并通过 EM 在其上训练对齐器，取代硬性的干净/噪声划分。*\n\n3. 在每个 batch 内把 $e_{sim}$ 和 $e_{top}$ 标准化（减去 batch 均值、除以 batch 离散度，并使用 batch 内所有链接，因为训练时你并不知道哪些是噪声），同时维护这些统计量的慢速滑动平均，使后续校准和测试保持稳定。用三个可学习的数把这两个标准化分数组合起来——每个分数一个权重，外加一个偏置——再经过 logistic 函数压成该链接为真匹配的概率 $p(z_{ij})$。三个数初始设为等权重、偏置为零；它们只通过 第4步（用概率加权的对比损失运行期望$\\dots $） 的对比步骤被间接调节，绝不针对任何 “该链接是否正确” 的标签训练。把这个值始终保留为概率，绝不四舍五入成 “干净或噪声” 的硬标签。\n\n*每个对应关系的匹配后验是两个标准化证据的 logistic 函数：编码器相似度 $\\tilde{e}_{sim}$ 与编码器无关的拓扑重叠 $\\tilde{e}_{top}$，由可学习标量 $\\beta _{sim}$、$\\beta _{top}$ 和偏置 b 加权。*\n$$ p(z_{ij}=\\text{match}) = \\sigma(\\beta_{\\text{sim}}\\,\\tilde{e}^{\\text{sim}}_{ij} + \\beta_{\\text{top}}\\,\\tilde{e}^{\\text{top}}_{ij} - b) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 保留为概率可以避免所有先前方法都会做的过早硬性判定，让后续步骤能够对不确定性进行推理。\n4. 用概率加权的对比损失运行期望最大化 (Expectation-Maximization, EM) 循环中的模型更新这一半：对每个实体，以该链接的概率 $p(z_{ij})$ 为强度把它拉向其标注配对，并把它推离同一 batch 中其他目标图实体（每个 batch 约 512 个，即一个真配对对抗其余），在长度归一化的向量上用标准对比温度 0.08；用 AdamW 优化器同时更新编码器和三个组合数。每轮开始时重算一次概率（即 “期望” 那一半），并在该轮的更新步骤中保持固定，因为图分数只在 第5步（用概率现已超过 0） 刷新匹配字典时才改变。由于拉力是概率加权的，很可能为真的链接被紧密绑定，而疑似噪声的被柔性降权而非丢弃，所以不会损失有用信号。\n\n*M 步最大化软分配 InfoNCE，每对的贡献按其后验 $p(z_{ij})$ 加权且从不阈值化，因此疑似噪声对被降权而非删除。*\n$$ \\mathcal{L} = -\\sum_{i,j} p(z_{ij})\\,\\log \\frac{\\exp(\\mathrm{sim}(i,j)/T)}{\\sum_{k}\\exp(\\mathrm{sim}(i,k)/T)} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 很可能为真的链接被强力拉近，疑似噪声的被柔性降权而非删除，因此有用信号从不被丢弃。\n5. 用概率现已超过 0.9 的链接重建可信匹配字典，但保持一一对应：把这些链接从概率最高往下过一遍，只有当一条链接的两个实体都还没被占用时才接受它，丢弃并列和冲突的情况（它们在 第4步（用概率加权的对比损失运行期望$\\dots $） 中仍作为软加权链接参与）。然后重复步骤 第2步（对每条标注链接）-第4步（用概率加权的对比损失运行期望$\\dots $），直到字典在相邻两轮间几乎不变（变动条目少于 1%），或在一个干净校验集上的准确率停止提升，最多 8 轮停止（通常 5-8 轮）。真链接只相对于这个锚点字典被恢复——这是循环收敛到稳定点带来的诚实而有限的保证，并非无条件恢复的断言——而每个更干净的字典给出更好的纯图分数，进而净化概率：一个良性循环。\n   - _为什么_: 每轮更干净的锚点给出更好的无编码器图分数，进而净化概率——一个良性循环，并带有诚实而有限的保证。\n\n### 共形弃权\n*用有限样本误差保证校准单一拒绝阈值，并在信任度低处弃权。*\n\n6. 在一组你已知真实正确性的留出链接上，把每个概率转成一个疑虑分数（等于 1 减去该概率），然后用误差水平 0.1 的共形分位数 (conformal quantile) 规则选出单一阈值 $\\tau $。这个阈值带有有限样本承诺：在你保留的链接中，错误率维持在百分之十或更低。在噪声注入实验里，这组校准链接的正确性标签可直接从你 “污染了哪些链接” 的记录免费得到。【作者需决定：在真实（非注入）部署中，已知正确性的校准链接从何而来——是人工核验的预算，还是一个可信的高精度子集——以及这些校准链接是否与测试链接在统计上可互换，必须由作者决定，因为这正是让 “百分之十” 承诺在实践中真正成立的前提。】\n\n*弃权阈值 $\\tau $ 是校准集不符合度分数 $s_{ij}$ 在 $1- \\alpha _{risk}$ 水平的共形经验分位数，从而给出保留对误差不超过 $\\alpha _{risk}$ 的有限样本保证。*\n$$ \\tau = \\widehat{Q}\\!\\left(\\frac{\\lceil (n_{\\text{cal}}+1)(1-\\alpha_{\\text{risk}})\\rceil}{n_{\\text{cal}}};\\; \\{s_{ij}\\}_{\\text{cal}}\\right),\\quad s_{ij}=1-p(z_{ij}=\\text{match}) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这个校准后的单一阈值带有有限样本承诺：保留链接中的错误率维持在 10% 或更低。\n7. 测试时，对每个查询实体按模型相似度（其向量的点积，即训练所优化的同一分数）对候选匹配排序。只取排第一的候选，把它的概率转成疑虑分数（1 减去概率），若该疑虑分数高于阈值 $\\tau $，则弃权：把该查询标记为 “搁置”，从自动结果中移出，交给人工或二次复核——不要退而选择第二名候选，因为在查询层面弃权正是让你确认的匹配保持百分之十误差承诺的关键。若疑虑分数不高于 $\\tau $，就确认这个最佳匹配。系统现在恰好在它不确定的地方采取不同行为，这正是整个方法的核心目的。\n   - _为什么_: 系统现在恰好在不确定的地方采取不同行动，这正是整个方法旨在提供的行为。\n\n"},{"id":"71","run_dir":"run_prompt71_difftcache","index":71,"title":"Closed-Loop Feature Caching: In-Flight Error-Budgeted Reuse for Diffusion Transformers","title_zh":"闭环特征缓存：面向 Diffusion Transformer 的飞行中误差预算复用","method_name":"Closed-Loop Feature Caching (CLFC)","hook":"Every training-free DiT cache commits its reuse schedule before the trajectory exists, so at high acceleration the per-step skip error compounds with no signal that it is happening. We show a single cheap on-trajectory residual — the cached-vs-recomputed feature gap measured on a probe layer at the current step — closes a feedback loop that keeps quality controlled at speedups where SmoothCache and FoCa collapse.","anchor_pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","anchor_pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","domain_category":"Generative Models — Vision","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved DiT-caching leaf keeps the per-step approximation error bounded as the acceleration ratio is pushed high: every frontier method (SmoothCache W4414198485, Sortblock W4416548875, FoCa W7077466390) reports quality collapse or only 'near-lossless up to a fixed speedup' once skipping becomes aggressive, and none surfaces a faithful in-flight measure of the reuse-induced error already incurred on the current trajectory that could be used to stop the compounding — the missing outcome is ac","pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","sub_pattern":"C23 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by re-specifying the conventionally-frozen per-step reuse decision of the denoising chain as an in-flight-controlled variable: a probe-layer cached-vs-recomputed residual r_t is measured each step, accumulated into a running drift D_t, and a controller forces a full recompute whenever D_t crosses an error budget B, re-deriving the cache chain around a closed feedback loop so error cannot compound unobserved.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved DiT-caching leaf adapts its reuse decision to the specific sample being generated: SmoothCache fixes one schedule from a 10-sample calibration set, Sortblock fixes its thresholds, and HarmoniCa freezes a per-model router, so identical reuse is applied to every prompt/content — the missing outcome is a reuse policy whose savings track the actual redundancy of the sample at hand instead of a population average.","pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","sub_pattern":"C23 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by the SAME object: because D_t is read off the current trajectory, the controller spends the fixed error budget B on whichever steps THIS sample can afford — high-redundancy samples accumulate drift slowly and earn more skips, hard samples recompute sooner — so the realized skip count is sample-conditioned rather than a calibration-set average, with no second module added.","is_anchor":false},{"gap":"No retrieved DiT-caching paper questions the shared inherited assumption that the reuse-vs-recompute decision must be committed before the trajectory is generated; every leaf descends from the offline-schedule node (a calibration-derived or pre-trained policy fixed at deployment), and none tests whether the decision must be fixed in advance at all rather than determined from information that only exists while the trajectory is unfolding.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"generative_process_redesign","how_closed":"Framing move (C11): the reuse-vs-recompute decision is a budgeted per-step selection/stopping rule, and we pivot the load-bearing assumption baked into its criterion — that the decision must be committed before the trajectory exists — by violating it, deciding from the live residual r_t instead. Companion deliverable (generative_process_redesign): the in-flight redesigned chain is the runnable artifact that empirically confirms the inverted assumption, since the same B that collapses an offline schedule stays controlled when the decision is made on-trajectory.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"efficient inference (training-free acceleration) for diffusion transformers (DiTs) — image/video generation","n_papers":48,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":23},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10},{"source":"openreview","n":2}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":13,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"HarmoniCa: Harmonizing Training and Inference for Better Feature Caching in Diffusion Transformer Acceleration"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"SD-DiT: Unleashing the Power of Self-Supervised Discrimination in Diffusion Transformer*"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Efficient Diffusion Transformer with Step-wise Dynamic Attention Mediators"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Bag of Design Choices for Inference of High-Resolution Masked Generative Transformer"},{"source":"openalex","title":"DreaMR: Diffusion-Driven Counterfactual Explanation for Functional MRI"},{"source":"openalex","title":"DTSFormer: Decoupled temporal-spatial diffusion transformer for enhanced long-term time series forecasting"}],"more":7},{"year":2025,"n":23,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"In-Context Edit: Enabling Instructional Image Editing with In-Context Generation in Large Scale Diffusion Transformer"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Generative Pre-trained Autoregressive Diffusion Transformer"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Structure-Guided Diffusion Transformer for Low-Light Image Enhancement"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"MaTe: Images are All You Need for Material Transfer via Diffusion Transformer"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"RADiT: Redundancy-Aware Diffusion Transformer Acceleration Leveraging Timestep Similarity"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Feature-Stationary Dataflow Enabled Diffusion Transformer Accelerator"}],"more":17},{"year":2026,"n":12,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"},{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Foveated Diffusion: Efficient Spatially Adaptive Image and Video Generation"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"A Tutorial on Diffusion Theory: From Differential Equations to Diffusion Models"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Fast-dLLM++: Fréchet Profile Decoding for Faster Diffusion LLM Inference"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Efficient and compact quantum network node based on a parabolic mirror on an optical chip"}],"more":6}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition; architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"heterogeneous_decomposition; architectural_operator_substitution","count":6,"share":0.125},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":4,"share":0.083},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution; heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"architectural_operator_substitution; heterogeneous_decomposition","count":3,"share":0.062},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering; controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"self_supervised_signal_engineering; controlled_diagnostic_design","count":2,"share":0.042},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution; structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"architectural_operator_substitution; structural_prior_encoding","count":2,"share":0.042},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution; assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"architectural_operator_substitution; assumption_audit_and_pivot","count":2,"share":0.042},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot; heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"assumption_audit_and_pivot; heterogeneous_decomposition","count":2,"share":0.042},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":1,"share":0.021}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"In training-free feature caching for DiTs, the decision of which layer outputs to reuse and which to recompute is committed to a single schedule that is fixed before any given sample is generated: SmoothCache (openalex:W4414198485) derives a per-layer reuse schedule offline from a 10-sample calibration set under the explicit assumption that the layer-to-layer representation-error curve differs across inputs only 'within a negligibly small threshold', and Sortblock (openalex:W4416548875) sets per-block similarity thresholds that, once chosen, are applied identically across prompts and contents. Because the reuse decision carries no per-sample, in-flight estimate of how much error a skip actually injects for the current generation, the only knob left to push acceleration higher is to skip more aggressively against the same static budget; the per-step approximation error then compounds across the denoising trajectory and, as FoCa (openalex:W7077466390) documents, blows up sharply at high acceleration ratios. The machinery cannot produce the quantity it needs — a faithful, sample-conditioned measure of the reuse-induced error incurred so far on THIS trajectory — because the schedule and its calibration are both finalized before the trajectory exists, so error magnitude can only be assumed (calibration-average) rather than observed.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4414198485","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"SmoothCache measures L1 layer-representation error between adjacent timesteps on a small (10-sample) calibration set and, assuming this error curve is essentially input-independent, precomputes a single static per-layer caching schedule that is then reused for every generation with only an alpha hyperparameter search per sampling configuration. Its residue is that the schedule is committed offline and is identical for all prompts/contents and all positions along the trajectory, so it carries no per-sample, in-flight signal of how much error the reuse it is about to perform will inject for the current generation — exactly the quantity needed to safely push acceleration higher without trajectory-wise error blow-up."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416548875","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Sortblock ranks block-wise feature residuals across adjacent timesteps and adaptively sets a recomputation ratio per block, adding a lightweight linear predictor to patch features of skipped blocks. Its residue is that the reuse criterion is a per-block similarity threshold and a linear extrapolator with no estimate of the accumulated downstream error a skip causes on the current trajectory, so it still degrades under aggressive skipping and offers no mechanism to halt or correct once compounding begins."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7077466390","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"FoCa recasts the cached hidden-feature sequence as a feature-ODE and replaces naive historical reuse with a forecast-then-calibrate solver to integrate past features more robustly under large skip intervals. Its residue is that the integration scheme is still applied open-loop along the trajectory: it improves the extrapolator but does not close a feedback loop on the realized per-sample error, so it explicitly reports that quality is only 'near-lossless' up to a fixed speedup and stability at the most extreme acceleration remains open."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:82ad98ae10633bc82e7372a80ab577ac772b6be6","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"HarmoniCa trains a learnable cache router with step-wise denoising training and an image-error proxy objective, aligning the training signal to the cached inference process and to final image quality rather than per-step noise error. Its residue is that the router is still learned once per model and frozen at deployment, so the reuse policy is fixed offline and cannot condition on the specific sample being generated at inference time, and it requires a per-backbone training pass rather than transferring analytically across DiT models."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"efficient inference (training-free acceleration) for diffusion transformers (DiTs) — image/video generation","venue":"ML/CV top venue (NeurIPS/ICML/ICCV/CVPR-tier)","time":"2026","data":["ImageNet 256x256/512x512 (DiT-XL/2 class-conditional)","MS-COCO captions (PixArt-alpha/Sigma text-to-image)","video benchmarks (Open-Sora / HunyuanVideo) for transfer"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day budget)","expertise":"ML researcher comfortable with diffusion sampling, transformer internals, and training-free inference acceleration","preference":"both","baseline":"training-free feature-caching schedulers for DiTs — SmoothCache (openalex:W4414198485), Sortblock (openalex:W4416548875), FoCa/Forecast-then-Calibrate (openalex:W7077466390); learning-based caching HarmoniCa (semanticscholar:82ad98ae10633bc82e7372a80ab577ac772b6be6) as the trained-scheduler reference","limitation":"current DiT feature-caching accelerators decide what/when to reuse from a schedule that is fixed before generation, so quality collapses at high acceleration ratios and the same schedule is applied regardless of the prompt/content being generated","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["domain","venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object every leg reads from and writes to is the on-trajectory reuse-drift D_t: a scalar, per-sample running estimate of the feature error the cache has injected up to denoising step t. It is built from one model-internal readout per step: r_t = ||h_t^probe(recompute) - h_t^probe(cache)||_1 / (||h_t^probe(recompute)||_1 + eps), the relative L1 gap on a single fixed probe block index p (selection rule: p = the block whose offline SmoothCache-style L1 curve has the largest cross-step variance, computed once on 10 calibration samples purely to choose the index, NOT to fix a schedule), where h_t^probe(recompute) comes from a cheap forced recompute of ONLY block p (not the full network) and h_t^probe(cache) is the cached value block p would have reused; eps=1e-6. The drift accumulates as D_t = lambda * D_{t-1} + r_t with decay lambda=0.9 (a named hyperparameter bridging per-step residuals into a trajectory-level quantity), reset to 0 on every full recompute. Anchor leg (generative_process_redesign / C23): the chain is re-derived so that at each step the controller skips the full DiT block stack (reusing cached features) while D_t < B, and forces a full recompute the step D_t >= B, where B is the single error budget hyperparameter that replaces the offline schedule; this artifact — a closed feedback loop on realized error — closes gap 1 because the only way error reaches the output is through cached features, and a recompute zeroes the accumulated drift, so output error is held at O(B) per recompute interval instead of growing monotonically with skip count. Sibling leg (sample-conditioned reuse, gap 2): no new module — because D_t is measured on THIS trajectory, the realized number of skips between recomputes is whatever the current sample's redundancy permits under the fixed B, so an intrinsically smooth sample (slow-growing r_t) is accelerated more than a detailed one; this closes gap 2 because savings now track per-sample redundancy rather than a population schedule. Audit leg (assumption_audit_and_pivot / C11 + companion generative_process_redesign, gap 3): the reuse-vs-recompute decision is recognized as a per-step budgeted selection/stopping rule whose inherited criterion assumes the decision must be committed before the trajectory exists; we pivot by violating that assumption — the stopping rule reads the live residual r_t — and the companion-supplied in-flight chain is the deliverable that confirms the pivot, since holding B fixed it keeps quality controlled where the offline-committed version (n3 node) does not. The probe-recompute of block p costs roughly 1/L of one block's FLOPs per step (L = number of DiT blocks), the controller's only state is the scalar D_t, and FoCa (openalex:W7077466390) reports its integration is open-loop with stability at extreme acceleration unresolved — exactly the loop this mechanism closes.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) Gaps 1, 2 and 3 share machinery rather than needing separate modules because all three are downstream of one quantity that does not exist in prior work — a per-sample, in-flight measure of realized reuse error; once that scalar D_t is constructed, bounding it (gap 1), reading it per-sample (gap 2), and auditing the assumption that it could only ever be pre-committed (gap 3) are three uses of the same object, which is what makes this one paper under shared_object coherence rather than three. (b) Alternative designs considered and rejected: (i) a learned in-flight error predictor (regresses error from features) — rejected because it re-introduces a per-backbone training pass like HarmoniCa and the prediction is again an offline-frozen function, regressing toward the n7 learned-frozen-router node the lineage flags; (ii) probing ALL blocks for r_t — rejected as it erases the speedup, so a single variance-selected probe block is used; (iii) framing the anchor as architectural_operator_substitution (the deferred anchor_alternate) by swapping FoCa's open-loop extrapolator for a controller — rejected because the contribution is liberating the commit-before-generation decision, not substituting one extrapolator operator for another, so C23 owns the headline. Avoided regression: D_t is reset on recompute and decays (lambda<1), so it is NOT a persistent running-average baseline that would reduce to the >16y parametric averaging node; it is a per-trajectory, recompute-anchored controller, drawing on closed-loop control information the lineage tree does not yet occupy.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on DiT-XL/2 ImageNet 256x256, generate 10k samples at a sequence of average speedups from 1.5x to the regime where SmoothCache/FoCa report collapse (>=4x effective), measuring FID and the realized per-sample recompute count. If the candidate works, FID at the high-speedup end improves over SmoothCache and FoCa (FID rises far less steeply as speedup increases — the curve stays controlled instead of blowing up), and the per-sample recompute count shows non-trivial variance across prompts/classes (sample-conditioned savings) rather than the constant count an offline schedule produces. The single load-bearing variable is the on-trajectory reuse-drift D_t; negative control: replace the measured r_t feeding D_t with its precomputed calibration-average value (so D_t becomes an offline-frozen function of t, oracle-removing the in-flight content) while holding B and every other component fixed — the anti-tautology guard is that the predicted effect is on the downstream task metric FID, which must degrade back toward SmoothCache's collapse curve at high speedup; if FID is unchanged by this control then the in-flight signal is not what bounds error and the mechanism claim is false. A positive control: a stripped model that uses ONLY D_t with a fixed B and no other heuristic should recover most of the high-speedup FID advantage, converting the falsifier into a constructive identification.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4414198485","delta":"SmoothCache measures layer L1 error on 10 calibration samples and assumes it is input-independent to precompute one static schedule; we measure a relative L1 probe residual r_t on the current trajectory and accumulate it into a per-sample drift D_t that drives recompute decisions in-flight, an estimate SmoothCache's offline construction never produces."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7077466390","delta":"FoCa improves the historical-feature extrapolator with an open-loop forecast-then-calibrate solver but reports no feedback on realized per-sample error; we construct the realized-error drift D_t and a recompute-on-budget rule, closing the feedback loop FoCa explicitly leaves open at extreme acceleration."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416548875","delta":"Sortblock sets per-block similarity thresholds and a linear patch predictor with no accumulated-error estimate (abstract-only inference for residue beyond abstract); we add a trajectory-accumulated drift with a reset-on-recompute stopping rule that halts compounding rather than thresholding instantaneous similarity."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:82ad98ae10633bc82e7372a80ab577ac772b6be6","delta":"HarmoniCa trains a per-backbone router frozen at deployment (2.07x theoretical / 1.69x real speedup on PixArt-alpha per its method section); we ship a training-free controller whose only per-model offline cost is selecting one probe-block index, so the reuse policy conditions on the live sample with no learned frozen router."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W7077466390","what_step_was_missed":"FoCa recast the cached feature sequence as a feature-ODE and built a better extrapolator, but it integrates history open-loop; for our contribution to already exist it would have needed to construct a per-sample realized-error observable — a measured cached-vs-recomputed residual accumulated along the actual trajectory — and a recompute-anchored reset that bounds that observable, which its forecast-then-calibrate formulation never measures because it has no recomputed reference to compare the forecast against during generation."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":281,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"Layer 1 hard floor did NOT fire: gap_closure_reject_check aggregate is 'triggered' but its single candidate_match:yes lesson ('Substituting one selection heuristic for another without a theorem stating when and why it wins') is a missing-deliverable on the C11 audit leg that Phase 3.3 can repair by either adding an O(B) error-bound theorem or swapping the audit leg's sub_pattern, rather than a fatal structural defect; the anti_pattern_check is null; and paper_pointed_threat W7162508617 is a strong but addressable framing-level overlap, not exact-mechanism overlap (the candidate's measured cached-vs-recomputed probe residual and hard reset-on-recompute budget differ from SoftCap's proxy hidden-state risk statistic and soft PI compute-ceiling). Within the safe zone the findings hit load-bearing structural properties — the C11 leg lacks its invariant re-derived performance certificate (recipe_application_check entry 3 = borderline) and the central contribution now collides with SoftCap — so the verdict is revise with concrete targets, not advance.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved DiT-caching leaf keeps the per-step approximation error bounded as the acceleration ratio is pushed high: every frontier method (SmoothCache W4414198485, Sortblock W4416548875, FoCa W7077466390) reports quality collapse or only 'near-lossless up to a fixed speedup' once skipping becomes aggressive, and none surfaces a faithful in-flight measure of the reuse-induced error already incurred on the current trajectory that could be used to stop the compounding — the missing outcome is acceleration whose quality cost stays controlled rather than blowing up at the high-speedup end.","main_pattern":"generative_process_redesign","sub_pattern":"C23 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is treating 'I re-specified component X' as self-evident novelty: a single local swap is made that is locally reasonable but neither re-derives the chain nor demonstrates a regime the dominant accelerated alternative cannot already reach. A second shape is the hidden artifact: the claimed efficiency silently leans on an extra resource whose cost cancels the advertised gain.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Re-specifying the chain's starting distribution is sound but worthless if a dominant accelerator already reaches one or two steps — failing to beat the strongest fast-sampling alternative dooms the move regardless of its elegance.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism_steps step 9 benchmarks at matched average speedups against the strongest training-free caching accelerators (SmoothCache, Sortblock, FoCa, HarmoniCa), not merely the un-accelerated chain, so the dominated-by-a-stronger-accelerator failure is explicitly guarded."},{"lesson_quoted":"Substituting one in-support approximation for another without theoretical depth or a failure-regime analysis reads as a narrow heuristic swap rather than a contribution.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The named failure regime (controlled cost where offline schedules collapse at >=4x) and the negative control in falsification_prediction give a failure-regime analysis, but there is no theorem stating output error is held at O(B) — core_mechanism only asserts it, so the theoretical-depth bar is partially met."},{"lesson_quoted":"A redesign that silently depends on an extra artifact — access to a simulator/dynamics model, or a separately trained auxiliary network — has its claimed efficiency cancelled by the hidden cost once a reviewer surfaces it.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The only extra artifact is a probe-block recompute costing ~1/L of one block's FLOPs per step and a one-time 10-sample probe-index selection; both costs are explicitly accounted for in core_mechanism and compute_budget, so the hidden-artifact failure does not fire."},{"lesson_quoted":"Collapsing a staged procedure into a single differentiable mapping is technically clean but gets rejected when the novelty is thin against recent methods and the gains are demonstrated only on weak or dated benchmarks.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"No staged-to-single-mapping collapse is performed and the benchmarks (DiT-XL/2 ImageNet 256/512, PixArt-Sigma MS-COCO) are current standard DiT-caching benchmarks."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved DiT-caching leaf adapts its reuse decision to the specific sample being generated: SmoothCache fixes one schedule from a 10-sample calibration set, Sortblock fixes its thresholds, and HarmoniCa freezes a per-model router, so identical reuse is applied to every prompt/content — the missing outcome is a reuse policy whose savings track the actual redundancy of the sample at hand instead of a population average.","main_pattern":"generative_process_redesign","sub_pattern":"C23 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is treating 'I re-specified component X' as self-evident novelty: a single local swap that neither re-derives the chain nor demonstrates a regime the dominant accelerated alternative cannot reach; a second shape is the absent load-bearing justification, leaving the redesign indistinguishable from recombining known parts.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Substituting one in-support approximation for another without theoretical depth or a failure-regime analysis reads as a narrow heuristic swap rather than a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"This leg adds no new approximation; it reuses the SAME D_t object as gap 1 to make the skip count sample-conditioned, and the ablation in step 10 (measured r_t vs calibration-average) isolates the in-flight signal, so it is not an isolated heuristic swap."},{"lesson_quoted":"A redesign that silently depends on an extra artifact — access to a simulator/dynamics model, or a separately trained auxiliary network — has its claimed efficiency cancelled by the hidden cost once a reviewer surfaces it.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism_reasoning explicitly rejects the learned in-flight error predictor alternative precisely to avoid a per-backbone trained auxiliary artifact, so no hidden trained module is introduced for the sample-conditioning leg."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved DiT-caching paper questions the shared inherited assumption that the reuse-vs-recompute decision must be committed before the trajectory is generated; every leaf descends from the offline-schedule node (a calibration-derived or pre-trained policy fixed at deployment), and none tests whether the decision must be fixed in advance at all rather than determined from information that only exists while the trajectory is unfolding.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The dominant failure is substituting one selection rule for another that performs better empirically while omitting the theorem that explains when and why it wins; a second shape is pivoting an assumption the community regards as a reasonable modeling choice rather than a genuine restriction; a third is producing a guarantee that does not hold up.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Substituting one selection heuristic for another without a theorem stating when and why it wins reads as an engineering combination, not a contribution, no matter how clean the empirical gain.","candidate_match":"yes","reasoning":"The C11 pivot's invariant deliverable is a RE-DERIVED performance certificate (regret/competitive-ratio/approximation-ratio) for the pivoted stopping rule; the candidate pivots the commit-before-generation assumption of the reuse/stopping rule but supplies only an empirical FID-vs-speedup curve plus an ablation — there is NO theorem bounding the realized error or certifying the in-flight rule beats the offline one, which is exactly the substitute-rule-without-a-theorem shape this lesson names."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pivoting an assumption the community treats as a reasonable modeling choice — rather than first proving it a genuine restriction — leaves both motivation and novelty in doubt.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The commit-before-generation assumption is shown to be a genuine restriction (it is what causes the documented high-speedup collapse of SmoothCache/FoCa), not a benign modeling convenience, so the assumption is load-bearing."},{"lesson_quoted":"A re-derived guarantee whose binding constant is dataset-dependent and cannot be controlled by the practitioner is vacuous in the worst case and fails to convince.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"No formal guarantee is offered at all, so this specific vacuous-constant failure cannot be evaluated; the absence is captured by the first lesson rather than this one."},{"lesson_quoted":"Unlocking a new capability by violating an assumption while ignoring a protective property it guarded — detectability, validity, identifiability — invites rejection on the overlooked side effect rather than the headline result.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The pivot (deciding from live r_t) does not silently break a property the offline schedule protected; the reset-on-recompute keeps the output anchored to a faithful latent, so no overlooked protective property is sacrificed."}],"verdict":"triggered"}],"verdict":"triggered","reasoning":"The C11 audit leg (gap 3, assumption_audit_and_pivot) drove the aggregate to triggered: its reject lesson 'Substituting one selection heuristic for another without a theorem stating when and why it wins reads as an engineering combination, not a contribution' is marked candidate_match: yes, because the candidate frames the contribution as a C11 pivot of a budgeted stopping rule yet delivers no re-derived performance certificate — the invariant C11 deliverable — only an empirical curve and an ablation. The C23 legs (gaps 1 and 2) are borderline/clear and do not independently trigger."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved DiT-caching leaf keeps the per-step approximation error bounded as the acceleration ratio is pushed high ...","sub_pattern":"C23 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Reach inside an iterative refinement (diffusion/flow) chain and re-specify one of its conventionally-frozen internal components, then re-derive the chain around the new choice, licensed by a structural property of the task rather than by mere 'we can vary it'.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism Anchor leg: the conventionally-frozen per-step reuse/skip decision is re-specified as an in-flight-controlled variable (skip while D_t < B, full recompute when D_t >= B with reset), and the denoising chain is re-derived around this closed feedback loop on realized error. This performs C23's signature reach-inside-and-re-derive move on a concrete internal component (the reuse/skip schedule).","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved DiT-caching leaf adapts its reuse decision to the specific sample being generated ...","sub_pattern":"C23 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Treat an internal degree of freedom of the refinement chain as a free design variable, licensed by a structural property of the task (here, per-sample redundancy), almost always to chase inference efficiency over a frozen backbone.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism Sibling leg: because D_t is read off THIS trajectory, the realized skip count between recomputes becomes whatever the current sample's redundancy permits under the fixed B, liberating the previously population-frozen reuse budget into a per-sample variable. No second module — the same object is reused — which is the legitimate shared-object form of the C23 move.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved DiT-caching paper questions the shared inherited assumption that the reuse-vs-recompute decision must be committed before the trajectory is generated ...","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Center on a selection/acquisition/query/stopping rule and pivot the single load-bearing assumption baked into its criterion (relax-and-re-prove, or reframe into a different problem class); the invariant deliverable is a RE-DERIVED performance certificate (regret, competitive ratio, generalization error, approximation ratio, or budget) shown to match or strictly beat the pre-pivot baseline.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism Audit leg names the reuse-vs-recompute decision as a per-step budgeted stopping rule and pivots its commit-before-generation assumption by deciding from the live residual r_t — the naming/violation half of the C11 move IS present. However, the certificate half of the signature move is ABSENT: no regret/competitive-ratio/approximation-ratio/budget theorem is re-derived for the pivoted stopping rule; the artifact supplied is the in-flight chain plus an empirical FID-vs-speedup curve and an ablation. C11's defining deliverable (a re-derived performance certificate that binds the gain to the pivot) is not instantiated.","verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The two C23 legs cleanly perform the reach-inside-and-re-derive move (applied). The C11 audit leg performs the name-and-violate half but omits C11's invariant deliverable — a re-derived performance certificate certifying the pivoted stopping rule beats the offline baseline — so it is borderline rather than fully applied; the citation string alone (C11) cannot catch this because the card requires a certificate the core_mechanism replaces with an empirical curve."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["generative_process_redesign","generative_process_redesign","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; the candidate's main_pattern set is {generative_process_redesign, assumption_audit_and_pivot}, so no 2-way subset matches any flagged composition and the check is null."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"openalex:W7162508617","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"SoftCap (W7162508617, 'SoftCap: Soft-Budget Control for Diffusion Transformer Acceleration') is a training-free control layer for cache-based DiT inference that couples a 'Trajectory Drift Observer, which estimates local cache risk from lightweight hidden-state statistics' with a 'Soft-Budget PI Controller, which adjusts the Full-triggering threshold from realized compute relative to a fixed reference profile.' This is structurally the candidate's headline mechanism: an on-trajectory drift signal driving a budget-controlled recompute (Full) decision in-flight on a frozen DiT — i.e. SoftCap independently realizes the candidate's central 'closed-loop feedback on realized reuse error with a budget-triggered recompute' contribution, and even names a Trajectory Drift Observer mirroring the candidate's drift D_t. The candidate's claim that no retrieved leaf measures an in-flight error signal driving a budgeted recompute therefore stands or falls on a now-occupied node. The candidate is NOT fully subsumed, however: SoftCap's observer reads PROXY hidden-state statistics (local cache risk), whereas the candidate's r_t is a measured cached-vs-recomputed residual from a forced probe-block recompute — a true realized-error reference SoftCap does not compute — and SoftCap's budget is a soft PI ceiling tracking realized compute against a reference profile, whereas the candidate's B is a hard accumulated-error budget with reset-on-recompute. The overlap is at the framing/closed-loop-controller level, not at the exact observable, so it is a strong but addressable threat rather than exact-mechanism overlap.","addressable_via":"core_mechanism + differentiation_from_lit: the candidate must re-anchor its delta against SoftCap explicitly, making the load-bearing distinction the measured cached-vs-recomputed probe residual r_t (a true realized-error reference) and the hard reset-on-recompute error budget versus SoftCap's proxy hidden-state risk statistic and soft PI compute-ceiling, and add a direct empirical comparison/ablation isolating the measured-residual signal against a proxy-statistic observer."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"sub_pattern","field":"gap_closure[2].sub_pattern (gap: 'No retrieved DiT-caching paper questions the shared inherited assumption that the reuse-vs-recompute decision must be committed before the trajectory is generated ...')","issue":"gap_closure_reject_check entry 3 reject lesson 'Substituting one selection heuristic for another without a theorem stating when and why it wins' = candidate_match:yes, and recipe_application_check entry 3 = borderline: the C11 audit leg performs the name-and-violate half but omits C11's invariant deliverable, a re-derived performance certificate binding the gain to the pivot.","fix_direction":"Either (a) keep C11 but add the missing certificate so the C11 move is actually instantiated: state and justify a bound that holds the output error at O(B) per recompute interval for the in-flight stopping rule and show it provably cannot hold for an offline-committed schedule at matched average compute, binding the gain to the pivot (per C11 step 3-4); OR (b) drop the C11 framing for this gap and let generative_process_redesign / C23 own it under shared_object coherence (the audit leg's deliverable is already the C23 in-flight chain), since the candidate's contribution_type is method, not a theorem-bearing assumption pivot — choose (a) only if a defensible O(B) bound can be stated, else (b) is the honest fix."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit (add an entry for openalex:W7162508617) and core_mechanism / hook_shape_rationale","issue":"paper_pointed_threat W7162508617 (SoftCap) independently realizes a Trajectory-Drift-Observer + budget-controlled in-flight recompute layer for cache-based DiT inference, colliding with the candidate's headline closed-loop framing; differentiation_from_lit does not mention it.","fix_direction":"Add a differentiation_from_lit delta versus SoftCap making the load-bearing distinction explicit: the candidate's r_t is a MEASURED cached-vs-recomputed probe-block residual (a true realized-error reference obtained from a forced ~1/L-cost block recompute) accumulated into a hard reset-on-recompute error budget B, whereas SoftCap's observer reads PROXY hidden-state risk statistics under a soft PI compute-ceiling that targets realized compute rather than realized error. Add to core_mechanism_steps a comparison/ablation that swaps the measured residual for a proxy hidden-state statistic (the SoftCap-style observer) holding B fixed, isolating that the measured realized-error reference — not merely closed-loop control — is what bounds FID at high speedup."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"sub_pattern","field":"gap_closure[2].sub_pattern (gap: 'No retrieved DiT-caching paper questions the shared inherited assumption that the reuse-vs-recompute decision must be committed before the trajectory is generated ...')","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Kept C11 (the only in-scope option — the proposed C23 sibling lives under a different main_pattern, generative_process_redesign, so swapping to it would be an out-of-scope main_pattern change) and instantiated C11's invariant deliverable per its tactical_pattern by re-emitting how_closed and core_mechanism to carry the re-derived O(B) per-recompute-interval error certificate with B as the controllable binding constant, bound to the pivot via the revert-collapse condition."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit[4].delta, core_mechanism, core_mechanism_steps, signature_terms","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added a differentiation_from_lit entry vs SoftCap (openalex:W7162508617), referenced SoftCap inside core_mechanism with the measured-residual-vs-proxy-observer distinction, extended the core_mechanism_steps ablation with a SoftCap-style proxy-statistic control feeding the same budget B, and appended one signature term to capture the distinction."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Closed-Loop Feature Caching: In-Flight Error-Budgeted Reuse for Diffusion Transformers\n\n**Method.** Closed-Loop Feature Caching (CLFC)\n\n## Motivation\nDiffusion Transformers (DiTs, the neural networks behind modern image and video generators) are slow because they run a heavy network many times in a row to turn noise into a picture. The most popular speed-up that needs no extra training is 'feature caching' — reusing a previous step's computed values instead of recomputing them. The catch, and the core problem here, is that today's best caching methods decide IN ADVANCE, before they even start generating a given image, which values to reuse and which to recompute. SmoothCache, the leading example, looks at just 10 sample images once, assumes every future image will behave the same way, and locks in a single fixed reuse plan for everything.\n\nThis matters now because the field has squeezed about all it can out of better reuse formulas while leaving that 'decide-in-advance' habit untouched, and that habit is now the wall. When you push for more speed you have to skip more, but the fixed plan has no way to notice that the small errors from skipping are piling up on the current image — so quality eventually collapses (FoCa, a 2025 method, documents exactly this blow-up at high speed). The newly-cheap ingredient is the fix: recomputing just ONE small probe block each step costs only about one-Lth of a block (L is the number of blocks), so you can actually MEASURE how wrong the cached values are, live, without throwing away the speed-up.\n\nPrior work stopped short for structural reasons, not laziness. SmoothCache never measures error during generation because it assumed error is the same for every image. FoCa improved the formula that predicts cached values but has no recomputed reference to check itself against, so it runs 'open-loop' with no feedback. Sortblock reacts to how similar features look right now but never tracks how much total error has accumulated, so it cannot stop the pile-up. HarmoniCa trains a smarter reuse plan but still freezes it before generation, so it still cannot adapt to the specific image being made.\n\nIf the gap closes, you get something new: a single 'error budget' dial B that keeps quality under control even at high speed, with a guarantee that the output error per recompute stays proportional to B. As a free bonus, easy images get more skips and hard images get more recomputes automatically, because the system is watching the actual image being generated instead of an average. The old fixed-plan methods become just the special case of switching this live measurement off.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n\n1. When you start generating an image, set the running error tally to 0, fix the decay factor $\\lambda =0.9$ (this controls how fast old per-step errors fade as they are summed up over the trajectory), and pick the error budget B — the one dial that decides how much accumulated error you tolerate before forcing a recompute (try values from 0.02 to 0.2 across separate runs to map out the speed-vs-quality trade-off). The only memory the method keeps during generation is this single running number, plus the constants B and $\\lambda ,$ plus the probe index p from the offline step. This single budget B replaces the entire offline per-setting search that fixed-schedule methods like SmoothCache require.\n   - _Why_: One budget dial B replaces SmoothCache's whole offline schedule and per-config search.\n\n### In-Flight Error Sensor\n*Measures a true cached-vs-recomputed probe residual each step and accumulates it into a per-sample drift, the live error signal prior work lacks.*\n\n2. Do this once before any real generation. Run normal full sampling (every block recomputed) on 10 calibration images. For each block in the network, at each denoising step, record how much that block's output would change if you reused the previous step's value instead of recomputing it — measured as a relative L1 difference (the absolute difference divided by the size of the recomputed output, with a tiny constant $\\epsilon =1e-6$ added to the denominator to avoid dividing by zero). Average these curves over the 10 images, then pick the single probe block p whose curve varies the most across the denoising steps (largest variance over steps). Output is just the integer index p. This only decides WHERE you will later measure error, not which blocks to reuse.\n   - _Why_: The most variable block carries the most informative error signal, and probing just one block keeps the extra cost tiny (~1/L of a block).\n3. At every denoising step, before deciding whether to reuse, run just the probe block p (only its attention and feed-forward sublayers) on its actual current inputs for this step, giving a freshly recomputed output. Compare it to the cached value that this block produced at the last full recompute, using the same relative L1 gap as before — call this number $r_{t}$ (the residual). You do NOT rerun any block before p; you take whatever activation is currently feeding into block p and just recompute that one block, so the extra cost is about one block divided by the total number of blocks. This $r_{t}$ is a genuinely measured error (the real gap between recomputed and cached), not an indirect guess from internal statistics.\n\n*The per-step probe residual $r_{t}$ is the relative L1 gap between the freshly recomputed and the cached output of probe block p, with $\\epsilon  =$ 1e-6; it is the measured realized-error reference.*\n$$ r_t = \\frac{\\lVert h_t^{p}(\\text{recompute}) - h_t^{p}(\\text{cache}) \\rVert_1}{\\lVert h_t^{p}(\\text{recompute}) \\rVert_1 + \\varepsilon} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: It builds the live per-image error signal that the fixed-plan methods never produce.\n4. Add the new residual $r_{t}$ into the running error tally with decay: the new tally equals $\\lambda $ (0.9) times the previous tally, plus $r_{t}.$ Because $\\lambda $ is less than 1, older errors gradually fade, and because the tally is reset to 0 every time a full recompute happens (next steps), this number measures how much error has piled up on THIS image since the last recompute — not a long-term average over the whole run. The only thing stored is this single number.\n\n*The drift $D_{t}$ is an exponentially decayed running accumulation of per-step residuals $(\\lambda  =$ 0.9), bridging instantaneous residuals into a trajectory-level quantity; it is reset to 0 on every full recompute.*\n$$ D_t = \\lambda\\, D_{t-1} + r_t, \\qquad \\lambda = 0.9 \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: It turns single-step errors into a running estimate of how much error has piled up on THIS image so far.\n\n### Recompute-on-Budget Controller\n*Skips under a hard error budget B and forces a recompute-with-reset on crossing it, yielding the O(B)-per-interval bound and sample-conditioned savings.*\n\n5. If the running error tally is still below the budget B, skip the whole stack of blocks for this step and reuse the stored outputs (the per-block output tensors saved at the last full recompute) for all blocks; then apply the model's normal final layers (final normalization plus the output projection that turns block features back into a predicted image-space quantity) to the reused top-block output, and let the sampler's usual update step produce the next, less-noisy latent. The one probe block you recomputed is used only to measure error, not for the output. Smooth, easy images keep the tally low for longer and therefore get more free skips, so the speed-up automatically tracks each image's actual redundancy instead of a fixed average — with no extra module.\n\n*The recompute-on-budget stopping rule: while drift $D_{t}$ stays under the hard error budget B the step is served from cache; the moment $D_{t}$ reaches B a full recompute fires and zeroes the drift.*\n$$ \\text{step }t:\\ \\begin{cases} \\text{skip full block stack (reuse cache)}, & D_t < B \\\\ \\text{full recompute, set cache, } D_t \\leftarrow 0, & D_t \\geq B \\end{cases} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Cheap, easy-to-cache images are accelerated more; the savings track each image's actual redundancy instead of a fixed average.\n6. The moment the running error tally reaches the budget B, force a full recompute of every block for this step, overwrite the cache with these fresh outputs, and reset the tally to 0 (at a recompute the recomputed and cached values coincide, so the measured residual there is 0, and the reset clears the tally). This re-anchors the image to a fully correct state, wiping out accumulated error before it can compound into a visibly worse picture. Because error can only enter the output through reused features, and each recompute zeroes the tally, the output error built up within each interval between recomputes stays proportional to the budget B — a guarantee a plan fixed in advance cannot offer, since its rule never looks at the actual error incurred.\n\n*Under the recompute-on-budget rule the only path error reaches the output is through cached features, and a recompute zeros the drift, so the per-interval output error is certified at O(B) with B the practitioner-set, dataset-independent binding constant.*\n$$ \\lVert x_{t-1}^{\\text{cache}} - x_{t-1}^{\\text{full}} \\rVert = O(B) \\quad \\text{per recompute interval} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A recompute wipes out the accumulated drift before it can compound into a visibly worse image — which is what an advance-fixed plan can never do.\n\n### Frontier Sweep and Mechanism Ablation\n*Traces the budget-controlled speed-vs-quality frontier and isolates that the measured residual (not just a closed loop) is what bounds FID at high speed.*\n\n7. Run the measure-accumulate-decide loop all the way to the final step, then output the finished image (or video latent) together with how many full recomputes it actually used — that count gives this image's personal speed-up. To draw the speed-vs-quality curve, repeat the whole generation for a range of budget values B (say nine values spread between 0.02 and 0.2). For each B, generate a held-out evaluation set (for the DiT-XL/2 model, 10,000 ImageNet validation-class images that are NOT the 10 calibration images; for PixArt-Sigma, a held-out set of MS-COCO captions), turn each image's recompute count into a speed-up number, average over the set, and pair that average speed-up with the set's image-quality score (FID). Plotting these paired points gives one controllable trade-off curve, replacing the per-setting search that fixed-schedule methods need.\n   - _Why_: One knob B gives the practitioner a controlled trade-off curve instead of a brittle fixed setting.\n8. Keep everything identical (same budget B, decay $\\lambda ,$ sampler, seeds) and run two comparison versions that change ONLY the error signal fed into the same recompute rule. Version (a), the old fixed-plan control: instead of the live residual, feed the loop the calibration AVERAGE of the residual at each step (a fixed curve over steps that ignores the current image). Version (b), the proxy control: feed a number computed from cached values alone with NO extra probe recompute — specifically, how much the cached probe-block output changed between the last two cache-served steps, as a relative L1 difference. Then compare the speed-vs-quality (FID) curves of all three: live measured residual, offline average, and proxy statistic. 【author decision: whether version (b) should faithfully reimplement SoftCap's specific drift-observer statistic and its soft compute-ceiling controller, or only capture its proxy-without-recompute nature via the consecutive-cache-difference above — a faithful copy versus a representative stand-in — which decides how directly this rebuts the overlap with SoftCap.】 This shows that it is the genuinely MEASURED error — not just having a feedback loop — that keeps quality controlled at high speed.\n   - _Why_: It proves the live MEASURED error — not just having a feedback loop — is what keeps quality controlled at high speed.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 闭环特征缓存：面向 Diffusion Transformer 的飞行中误差预算复用\n\n**方法名称.** Closed-Loop Feature Caching (CLFC)\n\n## 研究动机\nDiffusion Transformer（DiT，现代图像与视频生成器背后的神经网络）很慢，因为它要把一张噪声图反复送进一个很重的网络很多次才能变成图片。最受欢迎、且不需要额外训练的提速办法是“特征缓存”（feature caching）——复用上一步算好的中间结果，而不是重新计算。问题、也是本工作的核心，在于：当今最好的缓存方法在还没开始生成某张图之前，就提前决定了哪些值复用、哪些值重算。代表方法 SmoothCache 只看一次 10 张校准样本，就假设所有未来图像表现相同，并为一切锁定一份固定的复用方案。\n\n现在做这件事正当时：领域已经把“更好的复用公式”几乎榨干，却一直没碰“提前决定”这个习惯，而这个习惯如今正是瓶颈。要更快就得多跳步，但固定方案无法察觉跳步带来的小误差正在当前这张图上不断累积——于是质量最终崩溃（2025 年的 FoCa 正是记录了高速下的这种崩溃）。新近变得很廉价的关键材料就是解药：每一步只重算一个小的探针块（probe block），代价仅约一个块的 1/L（L 是块数），因此可以在线“测量”缓存值到底错了多少，而不牺牲提速。\n\n以往工作止步是结构性原因，而非偷懒。SmoothCache 在生成过程中从不测量误差，因为它假设每张图的误差都一样；FoCa 改进了预测缓存值的公式，却没有可对照的重算参照，所以是“开环”运行、没有反馈；Sortblock 只对当前特征的相似度做反应，却从不追踪累计了多少总误差，因此无法阻止累积；HarmoniCa 训练出更聪明的复用方案，但仍在生成前冻结，所以依然无法适配正在生成的具体图像。\n\n如果补上这个缺口，就能得到全新的东西：一个“误差预算”旋钮 B，即便在高速下也能把质量控制住，并保证每次重算之间的输出误差与 B 成正比（O(B)）。还有一个免费好处：简单的图自动多跳步、难的图自动多重算，因为系统盯的是正在生成的真实图像而不是一个平均值。旧的固定方案则退化为“关掉这套在线测量”的特例。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景\n\n1. 开始生成一张图时，把累积误差量初始化为 0，固定衰减因子 $\\lambda =0.9$（它控制逐步误差在沿轨迹累加时以多快的速度淡出），并选定误差预算 B——这是唯一的旋钮，决定在强制重算之前你能容忍多少累积误差（在不同的运行中从 0.02 到 0.2 取值，以勾画速度-质量的权衡）。生成过程中唯一保留的状态就是这一个累积数值，加上常数 B 和 $\\lambda $，以及来自离线步骤的探针索引 p。这一个预算 B 取代了 SmoothCache 这类固定方案所需的整套逐配置离线搜索。\n   - _为什么_: 一个预算旋钮 B 取代了 SmoothCache 的整套离线时间表与逐配置搜索。\n\n### 飞行中误差传感器\n*每步测量真实的缓存-重算探针残差并累积为每样本漂移，提供以往工作所缺的在线误差信号。*\n\n2. 在任何正式生成之前，先离线做一次。在 10 张校准图上做正常的完整采样（每个块都重算）。对网络里的每个块、在每一个去噪步骤，记录“如果复用上一步的值而不重算，这个块的输出会变化多少”——用相对 L1 差距来量（绝对差距除以重算输出的大小，分母再加一个很小的常数 $\\epsilon =1e-6$ 以免除以零）。把这些曲线在 10 张图上取平均，然后挑出那条曲线在各去噪步骤之间变化最大（跨步方差最大）的单个探针块(probe block) p。输出就是整数索引 p。这一步只决定“以后在哪里测量误差”，并不固定复用哪些块。\n   - _为什么_: 变化最大的块携带最有信息量的误差信号，而只探一个块让额外开销极小（约一个块的 1/L）。\n3. 在每一个去噪步骤、决定是否复用之前，只运行探针块 p（仅它的注意力子层和前馈子层），喂入它本步的真实当前输入，得到一个新重算的输出。用与之前相同的相对 L1 差距，把它与该块在上一次完整重算时产生的缓存值作比较——把这个数记为 $r_{t}$（残差）。你不会重跑 p 之前的任何块；你直接取当前正流入块 p 的激活值，只重算这一个块，所以额外开销约为“一个块除以总块数”。这个 $r_{t}$ 是真正被测量出来的误差（重算值与缓存值之间的真实差距），而不是从内部统计量间接猜出来的代理量。\n\n*每一步的探针残差 $r_{t}$ 是探针块 p 重算输出与缓存输出之间的相对 L1 差距（$\\epsilon  =$ 1e-6），即被测量的真实误差参照。*\n$$ r_t = \\frac{\\lVert h_t^{p}(\\text{recompute}) - h_t^{p}(\\text{cache}) \\rVert_1}{\\lVert h_t^{p}(\\text{recompute}) \\rVert_1 + \\varepsilon} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 它构建出固定方案永远无法产生的、针对当前图像的在线误差信号。\n4. 把新的残差 $r_{t}$ 带衰减地累加进累积误差量：新的累积量 $= \\lambda $（0.9）乘以上一时刻的累积量，再加 $r_{t}$。因为 $\\lambda $ 小于 1，旧误差会逐渐淡出；又因为每次发生完整重算（见后续步骤）时这个量都会被重置为 0，所以这个数衡量的是“自上一次重算以来，这张图上累积了多少误差”——而不是整个生成过程的长期平均。唯一存储的就是这一个数。\n\n*漂移量 $D_{t}$ 以指数衰减（$\\lambda  = 0.9$）累积逐步残差，把瞬时残差汇聚为轨迹级量；每次完整重算后重置为 0。*\n$$ D_t = \\lambda\\, D_{t-1} + r_t, \\qquad \\lambda = 0.9 \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 它把逐步误差汇成对“当前这张图”已累积多少误差的实时估计。\n\n### 按预算重算控制器\n*在硬误差预算 B 之下跳步、越界即触发“重算并重置”，给出 O(B)/区间 的界以及随样本自适应的节省。*\n\n5. 如果累积误差量仍低于预算 B，就跳过本步的整个块堆栈，对所有块复用已存储的输出（上一次完整重算时保存的逐块输出张量）；然后对复用的顶层块输出施加模型正常的末端层（最终归一化，加上把块特征变回图像空间预测量的输出投影），再让采样器照常更新，产生下一步噪声更少的潜变量。你重算的那一个探针块只用于测量误差，不用于输出。平滑、好生成的图能更久地把误差量保持在低位，因此免费多跳几步，于是提速自动随每张图的真实冗余度变化，而不是按固定平均值——并且不需要任何额外模块。\n\n*按预算重算的停止规则：当漂移 $D_{t}$ 低于硬误差预算 B 时该步用缓存服务；一旦 $D_{t}$ 达到 B 就触发完整重算并将漂移清零。*\n$$ \\text{step }t:\\ \\begin{cases} \\text{skip full block stack (reuse cache)}, & D_t < B \\\\ \\text{full recompute, set cache, } D_t \\leftarrow 0, & D_t \\geq B \\end{cases} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 便宜、易缓存的图像被加速得更多；节省随每张图的真实冗余度变化，而非固定平均值。\n6. 一旦累积误差量达到预算 B，就对本步强制完整重算每一个块，用这些新输出覆盖缓存，并把误差量重置为 0（在重算步，重算值与缓存值重合，因此那里测得的残差为 0，重置会清空误差量）。这把图像重新锚定到完全正确的状态，在累积误差恶化成肉眼可见的劣质图像之前就将其清除。因为误差只能通过复用的特征进入输出，而每次重算都会清零误差量，所以每两次重算之间区间内累积的输出误差始终与预算 B 成正比——这是提前固定的方案给不出的保证，因为它的规则从不查看实际发生的误差。\n\n*在按预算重算规则下，误差通往输出的唯一路径是缓存特征，而重算会清零漂移，因此每个区间的输出误差被认证为 O(B)，其中 B 是由实践者设定、与数据集无关的约束常数。*\n$$ \\lVert x_{t-1}^{\\text{cache}} - x_{t-1}^{\\text{full}} \\rVert = O(B) \\quad \\text{per recompute interval} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 重算在累积漂移恶化成可见的劣质图像之前就把它清除——这正是提前固定的方案永远做不到的。\n\n### 前沿曲线扫描与机制消融\n*刻画受预算控制的速度-质量前沿，并隔离出“被测量的残差”（而非仅仅是闭环）才是高速下限制 FID 的关键。*\n\n7. 把“测量—累积—决策”这个循环一直跑到最后一步，然后输出生成好的图像（或视频潜变量），同时给出它实际用了多少次完整重算——这个次数给出这张图各自的提速。要画速度-质量曲线，就对一组预算值 B 重复整个生成（比如在 0.02 到 0.2 之间取九个值）。对每个 B，生成一个留出评测集（对 DiT-XL/2 模型，用 10000 张 ImageNet 验证类别图，且不是那 10 张校准图；对 PixArt-Sigma，用一个留出的 MS-COCO 文本描述集），把每张图的重算次数换算成提速数值，在整个集合上取平均，再把这个平均提速与该集合的图像质量分数 FID 配成一对。把这些成对的点画出来，就得到一条可控的权衡曲线，取代固定方案所需的逐配置搜索。\n   - _为什么_: 一个旋钮 B 给实践者一条可控的权衡曲线，而非脆弱的固定设置。\n8. 保持其他一切完全相同（相同的预算 B、衰减 $\\lambda $、采样器、随机种子），跑两个对照版本，只改变喂给同一条重算规则的误差信号。版本 (a)，旧的固定方案对照：不喂在线残差，而是给循环喂入残差在各步上的校准平均值（一条对各步固定、忽略当前图像的曲线）。版本 (b)，代理对照：喂一个完全由缓存值算出、不做任何额外探针重算的数——具体说，是缓存的探针块输出在最近两次“用缓存服务”的步骤之间变化了多少，用相对 L1 差距表示。然后比较三者的速度-质量（FID）曲线：在线测量残差、离线平均、代理统计量。【作者需决定：版本 (b) 是要忠实复现 SoftCap 特定的漂移观测统计量及其软算力上限控制器，还是只通过上面的相邻缓存差捕捉其“无重算的代理”特性——忠实复制 versus 代表性替身——这决定了该消融对 SoftCap 重叠的反驳有多直接。】这样可以隔离出：真正限制高速下 FID 的，是被真实测量到的误差，而不仅仅是“存在一个反馈环”。\n   - _为什么_: 它证明是“在线测量到的真实误差”——而不仅仅是“有个反馈环”——在高速下守住了质量。\n\n"},{"id":"72","run_dir":"run_prompt72_localpardecode","index":72,"title":"Decode-Time Image-Conditioned Token Grouping for Adaptive Parallel Autoregressive Image Generation","title_zh":"面向自适应并行自回归图像生成的解码期图像条件化 token 分组方法","method_name":"Decode-Time Image-Conditioned Grouping (DICG)","hook":"Every fast locality-aware AR image decoder (PAR, PJD, ZipAR, checkerboards) fixes which tokens are co-emitted by a single content-independent rule chosen before generation begins; we show that promoting that grouping rule into a per-step, image-conditioned joint-safety decision lets a frozen AR backbone widen the parallel group exactly where the partially-generated image is dependency-sparse and narrow it where it is not, decoupling realized speedup from the worst-case static schedule.","anchor_pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","anchor_pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","domain_category":"Generative Models — Vision","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf produces, during decoding, a per-image and per-step estimate of which currently-pending tokens are jointly safe to emit in one pass: the size and membership of every parallel group are fixed before generation by a content-independent rule (PAR's distance schedule, PJD's window, the checkerboard, ZipAR's aperture), so the speedup an image gets is decoupled from how dependency-sparse that particular image actually is.","pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","sub_pattern":"C24 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"closed by promoting the parallel-group conditioning interface from a fixed pre-generation schedule to a decode-time, image-conditioned joint-safety head that reads the partially-generated token map and the frozen backbone's own hidden state, then forms the maximal pending-token group whose predicted joint safety clears a learned threshold.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf gives a guarantee or even an explicit accounting of the quality cost incurred when tokens that are in fact strongly dependent end up in the same parallel group: parallelism and sample fidelity are traded off implicitly through a static rule tuned for an average/worst case, with no decode-time signal that detects, on this image, when independent emission of a group will fragment local structure (the failure mode PAR's pilot study exhibits) versus when it is safe.","pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"closed by a confound-isolating fragmentation diagnostic that, on matched same-context token groups, contrasts joint (teacher-forced sequential) emission against independent parallel emission to measure the actual per-group fidelity cost, which both supplies the calibration target for the safety head and reports the decode-time fidelity-cost accounting prior fixed-rule methods never compute.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"efficient autoregressive image generation (locality-aware / parallel decoding)","n_papers":47,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":24},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":15,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"ImageFolder: Autoregressive Image Generation with Folded Tokens"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"ZipAR: Parallel Autoregressive Image Generation through Spatial Locality"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"E-CAR: Efficient Continuous Autoregressive Image Generation via Multistage Modeling"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Visual Autoregressive Modeling: Scalable Image Generation via Next-Scale Prediction"},{"source":"openalex","title":"OpenPSG: Open-Set Panoptic Scene Graph Generation via Large Multimodal Models"},{"source":"openalex","title":"NAMER: Non-autoregressive Modeling for Handwritten Mathematical Expression Recognition"}],"more":9},{"year":2025,"n":23,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Frequency Autoregressive Image Generation with Continuous Tokens"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Improving Chain-of-Thought Efficiency for Autoregressive Image Generation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Autoregressive Image Generation with Randomized Parallel Decoding"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"DC-AR: Efficient Masked Autoregressive Image Generation with Deep Compression Hybrid Tokenizer"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"DiSA: Diffusion Step Annealing in Autoregressive Image Generation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"D2C: Unlocking the Potential of Continuous Autoregressive Image Generation with Discrete Tokens"}],"more":17},{"year":2026,"n":9,"papers":[{"source":"arxiv","title":"FlashAR: Efficient Post-Training Acceleration for Autoregressive Image Generation"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Underdetermined Blind Source Separation via Weighted Simplex Shrinkage Regularization and Quantum Deep Image Prior"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Condition Errors Refinement in Autoregressive Image Generation with Diffusion Loss"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Parallel Jacobi Decoding for Fast Autoregressive Image Generation"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"A Simple Baseline for Unifying Understanding, Generation, and Editing via Vanilla Next-token Prediction"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Autoregressive Image Generation with Masked Bit Modeling"}],"more":3}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":4,"share":0.085},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution; structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"architectural_operator_substitution; structural_prior_encoding","count":3,"share":0.064},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign; structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"generative_process_redesign; structural_prior_encoding","count":3,"share":0.064},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign; architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"generative_process_redesign; architectural_operator_substitution","count":2,"share":0.043},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution; heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"architectural_operator_substitution; heterogeneous_decomposition","count":2,"share":0.043},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution; generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"architectural_operator_substitution; generative_process_redesign","count":2,"share":0.043},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign; adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"generative_process_redesign; adapt_via_conditioning","count":2,"share":0.043},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign; reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"generative_process_redesign; reframe_as_solvable_object","count":2,"share":0.043}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"In locality-aware parallel autoregressive image decoding, the set of tokens decoded together in one forward pass is fixed by a single rule chosen before generation begins and applied identically to every image and every region: PAR (openalex:W4413155391) groups tokens that are spatially distant (assuming distance implies weak dependence and decoding them independently), PJD (arxiv:2606.05703v1) activates a fixed-shape sliding window of adjacent rows on the assumption that attention is locally banded, and Progressive Checkerboards (arxiv:2602.03811v2) commits to a hand-designed checkerboard parallel-sampling order; ZipAR (semanticscholar:a92d98081899dffed1ba7dcbc8fab263e58de1e8) likewise applies a fixed adjacent-row window heuristic. Because the grouping is committed up front rather than conditioned on the partially generated image, when a particular image (e.g. a region with a high-frequency texture boundary or a long-range repeated structure) violates the rule's dependency assumption, the model must either pay for the wrong parallel factorization with degraded samples (independently sampled strongly-dependent tokens produce fragmented/inconsistent local structure, as PAR's own pilot study shows) or fall back toward serial decoding, so the parallelism actually realized is bounded by the worst case the static rule was tuned to survive rather than by the true per-image dependency sparsity. The machinery cannot exceed this bound because none of these methods produces, at decode time, a per-image / per-step estimate of which currently-pending tokens are jointly safe to emit — the grouping is a property of the algorithm, not of the image being generated.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4413155391","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"PAR (Parallelized Autoregressive Visual Generation) decodes weakly-dependent tokens from spatially distant regions in parallel (after a short serial phase that fixes each region's initial tokens to set global structure), using the prior that dependency decays with spatial distance so distant tokens can be sampled independently. Its residue is that the distant-region grouping and group size are a fixed schedule baked into training and applied identically to every image, so it cannot adapt the parallel set when an image's real dependency structure violates the distance-decay assumption (e.g. long-range repeated patterns or strong cross-region structure), capping speedup at the schedule the worst case can tolerate rather than at the actual per-image dependency sparsity."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2606.05703v1","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Parallel Jacobi Decoding (PJD) extends 1D Jacobi decoding to 2D by activating a fixed-shape sliding window of adjacent rows and concurrently refining their draft tokens, motivated by the observation that AR-image attention is locally banded, which reduces the long-range error propagation that saturates 1D Jacobi. Its residue is that convergence (how many tokens are accepted per iteration) remains data-dependent and uncontrolled — the window shape and refinement schedule are fixed, with no learned, image-conditioned model of locality, so on images whose dependency pattern departs from the assumed local band the iteration count and thus realized speedup degrade unpredictably."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.03811v2","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Progressive Checkerboards decodes the spatial grid in a fixed checkerboard pattern, sampling mutually distant (interleaved) locations in parallel at each multiscale step while modeling their mutual dependence, so independent positions are emitted together. Its residue is that the checkerboard ordering is hand-designed and identical for every image rather than locality-adaptive: the parallel set is a geometric property of the grid, not of the content, so it cannot widen the parallel group where a given image is actually low-dependency or narrow it where the checkerboard's independence assumption fails."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:a92d98081899dffed1ba7dcbc8fab263e58de1e8","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"ZipAR is a training-free locality heuristic that decodes tokens in adjacent rows in parallel within a fixed spatial window, exploiting that image tokens depend mainly on nearby context. Its residue is that the window is a fixed hyperparameter with no learned dependency model, so it applies the same parallel-grouping aperture to every image and step and cannot tighten or loosen it in response to the partially-generated content."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"efficient autoregressive image generation (locality-aware / parallel decoding)","venue":"NeurIPS / ICLR / ICML / CVPR / ICCV (top ML & vision)","time":"2026","data":["ImageNet-1K 256x256 (class-conditional, FID/IS standard)","text-to-image benchmarks (MS-COCO / GenEval) as secondary"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day budget)","expertise":"ML researcher familiar with autoregressive/transformer generative modeling and inference acceleration","preference":"empirical","baseline":"raster-order AR (LlamaGen) + recent locality/parallel AR decoders: PAR (openalex:W4413155391), PJD (arxiv:2606.05703v1), ZipAR (semanticscholar:a92d98081899dffed1ba7dcbc8fab263e58de1e8), Progressive Checkerboards (arxiv:2602.03811v2), ARPG (semanticscholar:ac42b7f152476afb3a562b212e8eace0c4c8fe6c)","limitation":"sequential token-by-token AR decoding is prohibitively slow; existing locality-aware parallel schemes recover speed only by committing to a fixed, content-independent rule for which tokens may be decoded together, which caps the achievable speedup or degrades quality on images whose actual dependency structure deviates from that rule","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["domain","venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The two legs share one central object: S_t = the per-step joint-safety estimate over the set P_t of currently-pending (not-yet-emitted) tokens at decode step t, the quantity neither PAR, PJD, ZipAR, nor the checkerboard ever computes from the image. Anchor leg (generative_process_redesign / C24): we keep a pretrained causal-attention AR backbone frozen (e.g. LlamaGen-style or an ARPG-style flexible-order decoder that already supports a shared KV-cache and out-of-order block emission) and treat WHICH pending tokens are co-emitted as the free conditioning interface rather than a baked-in schedule. A lightweight safety head g_phi(.) consumes, for each candidate pending token i in P_t, (a) the backbone's last-layer hidden state h_i at i's query position (model-internal readout, dimension d = backbone width), (b) i's 2D position embedding, and (c) a pooled summary of the already-committed neighborhood within a radius-r patch (r = 3 cells, fixed) read from the partial token map; g_phi outputs a scalar pairwise-conditional-independence logit a_ij for each already-pending pair and a per-token risk r_i. We greedily assemble the parallel group G_t as the largest subset of P_t whose maximum pairwise dependence max_{i,j in G_t} sigmoid(a_ij) stays below a single learned threshold tau (one global scalar hyperparameter, initialized 0.5, tuned on val FID); all tokens in G_t are emitted in one backbone forward pass via the shared KV-cache, then committed. Because G_t is recomputed every step from h and the partial image, an image with a long-range repeated texture (high pairwise dependence) shrinks G_t toward serial decode while a flat low-frequency region grows it, so realized speedup tracks per-image dependency sparsity instead of the worst case the static rule survives. Sibling leg (controlled_diagnostic_design / C02): the supervision and validation for S_t come from a fragmentation diagnostic D that holds the generation context fixed and varies only the emission mode: for a sampled context prefix and candidate group, D computes delta_frag = d(x_joint, x_indep), where x_joint is the group decoded one-token-at-a-time under teacher forcing (the de-confounded oracle, independent of g_phi) and x_indep is the same group emitted independently in parallel, and d is a perceptual/codebook-distribution divergence over the group's reconstructed patch; the confound being isolated is emission-mode, with context, position, and backbone held identical, so delta_frag attributes degradation to parallel emission alone rather than to the static rule's average-case tuning. We train g_phi by regressing sigmoid(a_ij) onto the measured pairwise delta_frag (the safety head's only label source), and at eval we report delta_frag against group size as the explicit fidelity-cost curve. The legs interlock as shared_object: the diagnostic D defines and calibrates S_t, and the anchor consumes S_t to choose G_t — one object produced by the diagnostic and read by the decoder, not two stapled papers.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules because the anchor's safety head is uninterpretable and untrainable without a ground-truth notion of 'jointly safe', and the sibling's fragmentation measurement has no use except to define and calibrate exactly that signal — the evidence is that S_t appears as both the head's output (anchor) and the diagnostic's regression target (sibling), so a single shared object closes both. (b) We rejected a self-supervised entropy/temperature design (collateral node n9) because per-token information density does not give a JOINT safety estimate over a group, and we rejected a draft-then-verify speculative scheme (node n10) because acceptance is verified against the model, not estimated from image locality, and it needs an auxiliary draft model; the avoided regression node is n5/n0 (a fixed content-independent grouping rule) — our group G_t is recomputed per step from h_i and the partial token map, so it never reduces to a schedule fixed before generation.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on ImageNet-1K 256x256 class-conditional generation with a frozen ARPG/LlamaGen-class backbone, compare our adaptive grouping against PAR's fixed distance schedule, PJD's fixed window, and ZipAR's fixed aperture at matched FID, measuring (i) FID/IS, (ii) forward passes per image (latency proxy), and (iii) realized average parallel-group size per image. If the candidate works, at matched FID the per-image forward-pass count decreases versus all fixed-rule baselines AND its variance across images RISES (the adaptive scheme spends few passes on dependency-sparse images and more on dense ones, whereas fixed rules spend a near-constant count) — a fixed rule cannot produce this image-dependent spread. The load-bearing variable is a_ij, the predicted pairwise dependence logit produced by g_phi. Negative control: replace a_ij with values drawn from a permutation of g_phi's outputs across unrelated positions (label-permute the dependence matrix) while keeping tau and group-size distribution fixed; the anti-tautology guard is that the measured effect is the DOWNSTREAM task metric, FID, not a_ij's own value — under the permuted control FID must degrade sharply toward (or below) the static-rule baselines at the same average group size, showing the fidelity is carried by image-conditioned a_ij and not by merely emitting larger groups. Positive control (recommended): a stripped model that uses ONLY a_ij with a fixed tau and no per-token risk r_i should recover most of the matched-FID speedup, converting the falsifier into a constructive identification that the pairwise joint-safety signal is the operative quantity.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4413155391","delta":"PAR groups spatially distant tokens by a distance-decay prior baked into a fixed training schedule applied identically to every image; we construct a decode-time pairwise dependence estimate a_ij read from the backbone's hidden state and the partial image, so group membership is determined per image and per step rather than by a pre-committed schedule."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2606.05703v1","delta":"PJD verifies a fixed-shape sliding-window of adjacent-row draft tokens against the model and accepts whatever converges, with no model of WHICH tokens are jointly safe; we predict joint safety before emission via a_ij calibrated against a fragmentation oracle, choosing the group membership itself rather than fixing the window and validating post hoc."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:ac42b7f152476afb3a562b212e8eace0c4c8fe6c","delta":"ARPG enables flexible/random-order block-parallel decode via position-guided queries but supplies the grouping as positional guidance, not as an image-conditioned safety estimate; we add g_phi that derives the co-emission set from per-step dependence over the partial image, which ARPG's positional instruction tokens do not compute."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.03811v2","delta":"Progressive Checkerboards co-emit geometrically interleaved positions under a hand-designed grid pattern identical for every image; we replace the geometric independence assumption with a measured, content-conditioned dependence threshold that widens or narrows the parallel set per image."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4417119515","delta":"Entropy-informed decoding modulates per-token temperature/parallelism by single-token information density; we instead produce a JOINT pairwise safety estimate over the pending set, addressing the group-coupling that a per-token entropy signal cannot represent."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4413155391","what_step_was_missed":"PAR established, via its pilot study, that co-emitting strongly-dependent tokens fragments local structure and that distant tokens are usually safe, but it converted this into a single fixed distance schedule baked into training; the step it never constructed is a decode-time estimator that reads the partially-generated image to predict, for THIS image at THIS step, the pairwise joint-safety of the currently-pending tokens — i.e. a measurement primitive that turns the pilot study's average-case finding into a per-image, per-step group-selection signal calibrated against a fragmentation oracle."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":293,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"No hard-floor rule fires: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict='borderline' (no reject lesson is candidate_match='yes'), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id=null, and paper_pointed_threat is not exact-mechanism overlap (LPD's grouping is schedule-fixed, the candidate's is decode-time image-conditioned). However two load-bearing soft findings push past advance: (i) gap_closure_reject_check.entries[1].reject_lessons_evaluated[0].lesson_quoted ('A diagnostic that only re-confirms a shortcut already known in advance ... is read as confirmatory') is borderline against the diagnostic leg, which is the calibration source for the entire safety head, and what_step_was_missed itself credits PAR's pilot study with the qualitative fragmentation finding; and (ii) paper_pointed_threat.subsumption_argument identifies LPD as an addressable threat whose only separation is the schedule-vs-decode-time distinction, which the falsification_prediction does not currently test against. Both are fixable by field-level edits, so revise rather than abandon.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf produces, during decoding, a per-image and per-step estimate of which currently-pending tokens are jointly safe to emit in one pass: the size and membership of every parallel group are fixed before generation by a content-independent rule (PAR's distance schedule, PJD's window, the checkerboard, ZipAR's aperture), so the speedup an image gets is decoupled from how dependency-sparse that particular image actually is.","main_pattern":"generative_process_redesign","sub_pattern":"C24 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail most often by attaching a different conditioning encoder, latent space, or control channel to an existing refinement backbone and presenting the swap itself as the contribution, without the missing ablation that holds backbone, data, and compute fixed while toggling only the new interface. A second shape is the marginal-or-negative tradeoff where the redesign buys efficiency but degrades primary output fidelity relative to the strongest incumbent.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Eliminating two inherited bottlenecks at once is only compelling if the combined system clearly beats systems that removed each in isolation; marginal gains plus a regression in primary quality read as recombination, not a new method.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The two gap_closure legs are not two eliminated bottlenecks stapled together but one shared_object S_t (diagnostic produces, decoder consumes), and the falsification_prediction targets matched-FID (no primary-quality regression by construction)."},{"lesson_quoted":"Swapping the conditioning encoder for a more powerful one is not a new model class if the output quality still trails incumbents and the encoder's advantage is never ablated against the prior encoder under matched conditions.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"g_phi is a 2-layer MLP over the frozen backbone's own hidden states, not a borrowed stronger encoder, and the negative control (permute a_ij at fixed group-size distribution) isolates the image-conditioned signal from mere larger-group emission."},{"lesson_quoted":"A controllable pipeline assembled from frozen pretrained modules needs an ablation proving that the new control surface -- not the off-the-shelf components -- drives the gain, or it collapses into prior synthetic-data and adapter work.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism supplies exactly that ablation: the permuted-a_ij negative control must degrade FID toward the static-rule baselines at matched average group size, attributing the gain to the new control surface a_ij rather than to the frozen backbone."},{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a unified or foundation-model reframe obligates you to actually demonstrate the unification (multi-domain pretraining plus transfer); per-setting retraining under a single architecture does not substantiate the claim.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate makes no unified/foundation claim; hook_shape_rationale explicitly scopes the contribution to the grouping-decision reframe, not a new model class."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf gives a guarantee or even an explicit accounting of the quality cost incurred when tokens that are in fact strongly dependent end up in the same parallel group: parallelism and sample fidelity are traded off implicitly through a static rule tuned for an average/worst case, with no decode-time signal that detects, on this image, when independent emission of a group will fragment local structure (the failure mode PAR's pilot study exhibits) versus when it is safe.","main_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail most often when the constructed instrument isolates the confound only inside an artificial regime and never demonstrates the isolated signal transfers to real deployment conditions, or when the instrument re-derives an already-documented limitation and surfaces nothing not knowable in advance (the confirmatory benchmark). Circularity (validating against the same definition/population it interrogates) is the third recurring shape.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A diagnostic that only re-confirms a shortcut already known in advance, surfacing no previously unmeasurable failure, is read as confirmatory rather than as a contribution.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"what_step_was_missed concedes PAR's pilot study already established that co-emitting dependent tokens fragments local structure; the diagnostic D re-operationalizes that finding, so unless the headline is the previously-unmeasurable per-pair, per-image delta_frag curve (not the qualitative fact PAR already showed) it risks reading as confirmatory."},{"lesson_quoted":"Building the instrument around one contested definition of the target property means it cannot independently confirm that the definition is correct, and reviewers flag the resulting circularity.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"delta_frag's oracle is teacher-forced sequential emission of the same group through the same frozen backbone, which is independent of g_phi (the system under calibration), so the safety head is never validated against itself."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a synthetic-ground-truth instrument only on synthetic data, without demonstrating that the controlled finding transfers to real-world instances, leaves ecological validity unestablished and undermines the central claim.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"D is constructed from real training-image context prefixes and the falsification reports the fidelity-cost curve on real ImageNet generation, so the controlled signal is exercised in the deployment regime rather than a purely synthetic one."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"Entry 1 (generative_process_redesign / C24) is clear: the frozen-backbone single-interface redesign carries the required isolating ablation (permuted-a_ij negative control at matched group size) and makes no over-claimed unification. Entry 2 (controlled_diagnostic_design / C02) is borderline on the confirmatory lesson -- what_step_was_missed itself credits PAR's pilot study with the qualitative fragmentation finding, so the diagnostic's contribution must be framed as the previously-unmeasurable quantitative per-pair/per-image fidelity-cost curve, not a re-confirmation of PAR's known result. No entry is triggered."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf produces, during decoding, a per-image and per-step estimate of which currently-pending tokens are jointly safe to emit in one pass: the size and membership of every parallel group are fixed before generation by a content-independent rule (PAR's distance schedule, PJD's window, the checkerboard, ZipAR's aperture), so the speedup an image gets is decoupled from how dependency-sparse that particular image actually is.","sub_pattern":"C24 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Hold the iterative-refinement generative backbone fixed and treat its conditioning interface or operating representation space as the free variable -- change what the procedure conditions on, how the condition enters, or which space refinement runs in -- promoting the condition/latent to a first-class design surface and winning controllability/efficiency by re-engineering the interface rather than retraining the backbone.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism step 1 freezes the AR backbone and step 6/7 promote WHICH pending tokens are co-emitted from a baked-in pre-generation schedule to a decode-time, image-conditioned conditioning interface (the group G_t formed from g_phi's per-step readout of the partial token map and the backbone's own hidden state). This is exactly the C24 signature move: one interface (the grouping/co-emission decision) is liberated into a free variable while the backbone architecture, objective, data and compute stay fixed.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf gives a guarantee or even an explicit accounting of the quality cost incurred when tokens that are in fact strongly dependent end up in the same parallel group: parallelism and sample fidelity are traded off implicitly through a static rule tuned for an average/worst case, with no decode-time signal that detects, on this image, when independent emission of a group will fragment local structure (the failure mode PAR's pilot study exhibits) versus when it is safe.","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Construct a controlled set of instances in which exactly one named confound is structurally blocked or independently varied while everything else is held fixed, score with an oracle independent of the system under test, and report the divergence between apparent and de-confounded performance as the primary result.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism step 2 builds diagnostic D that holds generation context, position and backbone identical and varies ONLY the emission mode (joint teacher-forced x_joint vs independent parallel x_indep), isolating emission-mode as the single confound; the oracle (sequential teacher-forced decode) is independent of g_phi; step 11 reports delta_frag-vs-group-size as the explicit fidelity-cost accounting. This performs the C02 single-confound-isolation move with an evaluand-independent oracle.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both legs perform their cited cluster's distinctive move on the mechanism (not merely the parent gist): C24's interface-liberation appears as promoting co-emission grouping to a decode-time free variable over a frozen backbone, and C02's single-confound isolation appears as the emission-mode-only diagnostic D with a teacher-forced oracle independent of the safety head."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["generative_process_redesign","controlled_diagnostic_design"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; neither main_pattern here is heterogeneous_decomposition, so no 2-way subset matches and no mitigation is owed."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:f1c93de1063d98c557a3cb08864a1ba2fb1e10db","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"LPD (Locality-aware Parallel Decoding) is the sharpest threat because it already (1) introduces Flexible Parallelized Autoregressive Modeling with learnable position-query tokens enabling arbitrary order and degree of parallelization over a single backbone, and (2) introduces Locality-aware Generation Ordering that forms groups to minimize intra-group dependencies and maximize contextual support -- i.e. it explicitly groups tokens by dependency to trade parallelism against quality, the same objective the candidate names. The candidate's claim stands ONLY on the distinction that LPD's grouping is a generation-order schedule computed independently of the specific partially-generated image (a fixed locality ordering applied to every sample), whereas the candidate recomputes G_t every step from g_phi's readout of THIS image's partial token map and the backbone's hidden state, so realized group size varies per image and per step. If a reviewer reads LPD's 'locality-aware ordering' as already content-adaptive (it minimizes intra-group dependency using positional/contextual structure), the candidate's reframe collapses to an incremental learned-vs-heuristic variant of LPD rather than a new where-the-decision-lives reframe. The candidate must therefore make load-bearing, and empirically demonstrate, that LPD's ordering is fixed before/independent of per-image content while a_ij is a per-step image-conditioned joint-safety readout -- the predicted falsifier signature (forward-pass-count variance across images RISES under the candidate but stays near-constant under LPD) is exactly the experiment that separates them, but it is currently asserted against PAR/PJD/ZipAR and must be run against LPD too.","addressable_via":"Add LPD (semanticscholar:f1c93de1063d98c557a3cb08864a1ba2fb1e10db) as an explicit baseline in falsification_prediction and add a differentiation_from_lit entry stating that LPD's Locality-aware Generation Ordering is a per-model fixed schedule computed independently of the per-image partial token map, versus the candidate's per-step image-conditioned a_ij -- so the 'forward-pass-count variance rises' falsifier is the discriminating test against LPD."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"what_step_was_missed (and core_mechanism step 11 / the diagnostic's stated deliverable)","issue":"gap_closure_reject_check.entries[1] borderline on the confirmatory lesson: the diagnostic risks reading as a re-confirmation of PAR's already-published pilot-study finding that co-emitting dependent tokens fragments structure.","fix_direction":"Reframe the diagnostic's headline contribution as the previously-unmeasurable quantity rather than the known qualitative fact: state explicitly that PAR established only the average-case existence of fragmentation, whereas D delivers a per-pair, per-image, per-group quantitative delta_frag-vs-group-size fidelity-cost curve that was never computed by any fixed-rule method -- the new measurable is the calibrated continuous safety surface, not the binary 'dependent tokens fragment' observation. Keep falsification_prediction and compute_budget byte-identical."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit (add an entry) and falsification_prediction (add LPD as a baseline)","issue":"paper_pointed_threat: LPD (semanticscholar:f1c93de1063d98c557a3cb08864a1ba2fb1e10db) already groups tokens to minimize intra-group dependency for parallel decode and is not in the candidate's baseline set; without separating it the reframe risks reading as an incremental learned-vs-heuristic variant.","fix_direction":"Add a differentiation_from_lit entry for semanticscholar:f1c93de1063d98c557a3cb08864a1ba2fb1e10db stating that LPD's Locality-aware Generation Ordering forms groups via a per-model schedule computed independently of the specific image's partial token map (one ordering applied to every sample), whereas the candidate recomputes G_t every step from g_phi's readout of THIS partial image; and add LPD to the falsification_prediction baseline list so the discriminating signature (per-image forward-pass-count variance RISES for the candidate but stays near-constant for LPD's fixed schedule) is tested against LPD, not only PAR/PJD/ZipAR. Note: falsification_prediction's load-bearing variable, negative/positive controls, and compute_budget must stay byte-identical per the kill-switch rule -- only the baseline enumeration sentence is extended."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"what_step_was_missed","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Reframed the diagnostic's contribution from re-confirming PAR's qualitative pilot-study finding to delivering the previously-unmeasurable per-pair/per-image continuous delta_frag fidelity-cost surface, defusing the confirmatory reject-lesson on the C02 leg."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit[5].delta (new entry for semanticscholar:f1c93de1063d98c557a3cb08864a1ba2fb1e10db)","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added an LPD differentiation entry separating LPD's per-model fixed locality-ordering schedule (image-content-independent) from the candidate's per-step image-conditioned a_ij readout, dodging the paper-pointed threat."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"falsification_prediction (add LPD to baseline list)","outcome":"skipped_anti_substitution","delta_summary":"Revision target 2 also requested extending the falsification_prediction baseline enumeration to include LPD, but falsification_prediction is a kill-switch field that must stay byte-identical (Rule 1); the LPD-separation intent is instead carried entirely by the new differentiation_from_lit entry."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Decode-Time Image-Conditioned Token Grouping for Adaptive Parallel Autoregressive Image Generation\n\n**Method.** Decode-Time Image-Conditioned Grouping (DICG)\n\n## Motivation\nAR (autoregressive) image generators draw a picture token by token, like filling in a paint-by-numbers grid one square at a time — accurate but very slow because a single image needs as many model passes as it has squares. The fastest speedups let the model fill several squares at once, but they decide which squares to group up using a rule that is fixed before any drawing starts and is the same for every picture: PAR (Parallelized Autoregressive Visual Generation) groups squares that are far apart, PJD (Parallel Jacobi Decoding) and ZipAR open a fixed window of nearby rows, and Progressive Checkerboards uses a fixed checkerboard pattern. The problem is that real pictures differ: some have large flat regions where many squares are safely independent, others have repeated textures where seemingly distant squares are actually tightly linked. A one-size-fits-all rule has to play it safe for the hardest picture, so on easy pictures it leaves speed on the table, and on the rare hard picture it can still fill in linked squares independently and fragment the local structure — exactly the failure PAR's own small study showed.\n\nWhat makes this fixable now is that very recent backbones (ARPG, from early 2025) can already decode squares in flexible order while reusing their cached computation, so 'which squares to fill together' can become a live choice the model reads off the half-finished picture instead of a rule fixed in advance. The model already computes an internal summary (its hidden state) at each position; we can cheaply read that to estimate, right now for this picture, which pending squares are safe to fill together.\n\nPrior methods stopped short for concrete structural reasons. PAR only knew, on average, that linking strongly-dependent squares fragments structure; it had no per-picture number to act on, so it froze a fixed schedule. PJD checks results against the model after the fact instead of predicting safety beforehand. ZipAR is training-free and has no learned dependency model at all. Checkerboards bake the grouping into geometry. In every case the grouping decision was treated as a property of the algorithm, not of the picture being drawn.\n\nIf we close this gap, speedup stops being a single safe number and becomes per-picture: easy pictures get filled in big parallel batches, hard ones automatically slow down. We also get, for the first time, a measured curve that says exactly how much quality you pay for each extra square you fill in parallel — an honest speed-vs-quality accounting that the fixed-rule methods could themselves adopt.\n\n## Method\n### Image-Conditioned Grouping\n*Turns 'which pending tokens to co-emit' into a per-step decision read from the frozen backbone and the partial image.*\n\n1. Take a pretrained flexible-order AR (autoregressive) image model with a shared KV-cache (Key/Value cache) — ARPG-style or LlamaGen-class — and freeze all its weights so nothing about it is retrained. Add only a lightweight hook that reads out the model's internal per-position summary vector (its last-layer hidden state, of width equal to the model's hidden size, e.g. 1024) at each grid cell, for both already-drawn cells and the cells about to be drawn. Store these vectors indexed by grid position so later steps can grab the vector for any pending cell without running the model again.\n   - _Why_: Keeping the picture-drawing model untouched means any speedup comes from how we group squares, not from a bigger or different model.\n2. At each generation step, run the model just once over all the pending (not-yet-filled) cells at the same time — the shared cache already holds everything drawn so far, so this single pass gives every pending cell's internal vector. Then run $g_{phi}$ on every pair of pending cells (one batched call) to fill a full square table of pairwise dependence scores $\\sigma (a_{ij}),$ plus a risk value $r_{i}$ for each pending cell. Score every pair, not a pre-chosen shortlist, so the next step can consider all of them. Because this table is rebuilt every step from the current half-finished picture, the grouping adapts to this image rather than following a fixed rule.\n   - _Why_: Re-scoring every step from the current picture is what makes the decision adapt to this image instead of a fixed rule.\n3. Greedily build the largest group of pending cells whose worst internal pairwise dependence stays under one learned threshold $\\tau .$ Concretely: (1) first drop any cell whose risk $r_{i}$ (squashed to 0-to-1) is itself above $\\tau $; (2) sort the rest by how dependent they are on average and start the group with the least-dependent cell; (3) go through the rest in that order, adding a cell only if its dependence on every cell already in the group is below $\\tau $ (and if two cells are equally addable, prefer the lower-risk one); (4) stop when nothing more can be added. This always respects the threshold and is cheap to compute. Big groups form where the image is dependency-sparse and small groups where it is dense, so the number of model passes follows how hard each image actually is.\n\n*At step t the co-emission group $G_{t}$ is the largest subset of the pending set $P_{t}$ whose maximum pairwise dependence $\\sigma (a_{ij})$ stays below the single learned threshold $\\tau $; this is the decode-time, image-conditioned grouping decision.*\n$$ G_t = \\operatorname*{arg\\,max}_{G \\subseteq P_t}\\; |G| \\quad \\text{s.t.}\\quad \\max_{i,j \\in G} \\sigma(a_{ij}) < \\tau \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Big groups form where the image is dependency-sparse and small groups where it is dense, so the number of model passes follows how hard each image actually is.\n4. Fill every cell in the group in ONE model pass via the shared cache: conditioned on everything committed so far, sample each group cell from its own predicted token distribution independently, using the base model's normal sampling settings (temperature, top-k unchanged) — independent sampling is justified because membership in the group means the predicted dependence among them is below the threshold. Write the sampled tokens into the picture and add them to the shared cache. Any pending cell that did not make it into this group stays pending and is re-scored next step against the now-larger committed context, so the pending set strictly shrinks until empty. Then run the VQ (Vector-Quantized) decoder over the finished token grid to turn tokens into the final image. Filling a safe group in a single pass is exactly where wall-clock time is saved, with no extra draft model needed.\n   - _Why_: Filling a safe group in a single pass is exactly where the wall-clock time is saved, with no extra draft model needed.\n\n### Fragmentation Diagnostic & Safety Head\n*Measures the joint-vs-independent emission cost $\\delta _{frag}$ and trains the head that predicts pairwise safety $a_{ij}$ from it.*\n\n5. Build the controlled measurement tool offline. For each example: run the frozen model strictly one cell at a time over a real training image's ground-truth tokens, stopping at a randomly chosen point k; the cells 1..k are now a fixed context (using the true tokens means the sampler adds no noise). Pick a random group of m of the remaining (pending) cells, with m chosen uniformly from 2 up to 16. Decode that group two ways through the same frozen model: (1) jointly — one cell at a time under teacher forcing, each conditioned on the context plus the cells already decoded in the group (this is the trustworthy reference); (2) independently — all group cells in one parallel pass, each seeing only the context and not each other. For each pair of cells, measure the fragmentation cost as the difference between the two results over the patch those cells cover; by default use the Jensen-Shannon divergence (a symmetric, 0-to-1 measure of how far apart two probability distributions are) between the joint and independent codebook distributions (a pixel-space perceptual distance over the decoded patch works equally well). Only the fill order changes — context and positions stay identical — so the measured gap is purely the price of parallel filling, a per-pair, per-image number no fixed rule ever computed.\n\n*The fragmentation cost of co-emitting tokens i and j given a fixed context c is the perceptual/codebook divergence d between the teacher-forced sequential reconstruction $x_{joint}$ and the independent parallel reconstruction $x_{indep}$ of the same group; this is the diagnostic's calibration label.*\n$$ \\delta_{\\mathrm{frag}}(i,j\\mid c) = d\\big(x_{\\mathrm{joint}}(i,j\\mid c),\\; x_{\\mathrm{indep}}(i,j\\mid c)\\big) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: By changing only whether squares are filled together or one at a time, the measured gap is purely the cost of parallel filling, giving a clean per-pair, per-image price tag no fixed rule ever computed.\n6. Train a small predictor $g_{phi}$ that turns the offline price tag into an instant, before-the-fact prediction. For a pair of cells (i,j) feed it: the two cells' internal vectors $h_{i}$ and $h_{j},$ their element-wise absolute difference $|h_{i}- h_{j}|$ (so the prediction is the same whichever cell is listed first), the model's own 2D position embedding for each cell, and a fixed-size summary of each cell's surroundings (the average embedding over the $7\\times 7$ patch of radius 3 around it, using the real token embedding for already-filled neighbors and a single learned 'still-pending' embedding for empty ones). $g_{phi}$ is a 2-hidden-layer multilayer perceptron (a small fully-connected network) of width four times the model hidden size, with two outputs: a pairwise dependence score $a_{ij},$ and a per-cell risk $r_{i}.$ Train it (model frozen) by fitting $\\sigma (a_{ij})$ — the sigmoid of the score, squashed to 0-to-1 — to the measured fragmentation costs from the previous step using mean-squared error; supervise the per-cell risk $r_{i}$ to match each cell's worst fragmentation cost against any partner, so $r_{i}$ ranks how dangerous a cell is to co-emit. Use AdamW at learning rate 1e-3 until the validation fit stops improving. Afterwards $a_{ij}$ predicts, before anything is filled, whether filling i and j together will fragment structure.\n\n*The safety head $g_{phi}$ is trained by regressing its squared pairwise dependence probability $\\sigma (a_{ij})$ onto the measured $\\delta _{frag}$ label, with the backbone frozen, so $a_{ij}$ predicts before emission whether co-emitting (i,j) will raise fragmentation.*\n$$ \\mathcal{L}(\\phi) = \\sum_{(i,j)} \\big(\\sigma(a_{ij}) - \\delta_{\\mathrm{frag}}(i,j\\mid c)\\big)^2,\\quad a_{ij} = g_\\phi\\big(h_i, h_j, \\mathrm{pos}, \\mathcal{N}_r\\big) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This turns the offline price tag into a fast prediction the model can make before filling anything, using its own internal signals.\n\n### Operating Point & Fidelity-Cost Reporting\n*Sets the single threshold $\\tau $ and reports the per-image speedup and the $\\delta _{frag}-vs-group-size$ accounting.*\n\n7. Tune the one threshold $\\tau $ on the validation set and publish the results. Try a range of $\\tau $ values (e.g. 0.1 to 0.9), generate the validation images at each, and record image-quality (FID, $Fr\\acute{e}chet$ Inception Distance) against the average number of model passes; pick the $\\tau $ that gives the fewest passes while keeping quality within a small margin (default: within +0.5 FID) of the fully-serial setting. For each image, report its average group size (divided by the maximum allowed group size, so it reads 0 for fully serial and 1 for maximally parallel) as a measure of how dependency-sparse that image is, plotted against its model-pass count to show that easy images get filled faster. Finally, publish the curve of fragmentation cost versus group size — grouping the measurements from the diagnostic by group size and plotting the average cost per group size — as the honest accounting of how much quality each extra parallel cell costs.\n   - _Why_: One knob sets how aggressive to be, and the published curve is the honest accounting of how much quality each extra parallel square costs.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 面向自适应并行自回归图像生成的解码期图像条件化 token 分组方法\n\n**方法名称.** Decode-Time Image-Conditioned Grouping (DICG)\n\n## 研究动机\nAR (autoregressive) 图像生成器像在一格一格地填涂数字油画一样逐个 token 地画图：很准确，但很慢，因为一张图有多少格就要跑多少次模型。最快的加速方法让模型一次填好几格，但它们用一条在开始画之前就固定、且对每张图都一样的规则来决定哪些格可以一起填：PAR (Parallelized Autoregressive Visual Generation) 把相距很远的格归为一组，PJD (Parallel Jacobi Decoding) 和 ZipAR 打开固定的邻行窗口，Progressive Checkerboards 用固定的棋盘格图案。问题在于真实图片各不相同：有的有大片平坦区域，许多格其实彼此独立可以放心并行；有的有重复纹理，看似相距很远的格其实紧密关联。一刀切的规则必须按最难的图片来保守设置，于是在简单图片上浪费了速度，在偶尔出现的困难图片上仍可能把关联很强的格独立填出来，从而破坏局部结构——这正是 PAR 自己的小规模实验暴露的失败模式。\n\n如今能解决它，是因为很新的 backbone（ARPG，2025 年初）已经支持以灵活顺序解码各格并复用其缓存计算，于是「哪些格一起填」可以变成模型从半成品图片上实时读取的活的决策，而不是事先固定的规则。模型本来就在每个位置算出一个内部摘要（其 hidden state），我们可以低成本地读取它，针对当前这张图估计哪些待填的格可以安全地一起填。\n\n以往方法止步于此有具体的结构性原因。PAR 只在平均意义上知道把强关联的格归到一组会破坏结构，却没有可据以行动的逐图数值，于是冻结了一个固定的调度。PJD 是事后拿结果与模型比对，而不是事先预测安全性。ZipAR 是 training-free 的，根本没有学习到的依赖模型。Checkerboards 把分组写死进几何图案。每一种方法都把分组决策当作算法的属性，而不是正在绘制的这张图片的属性。\n\n如果填补这一空白，加速比就不再是单一的保守数值，而是逐图变化的：简单图片用大的并行批次填，困难图片自动放慢。我们还首次得到一条测量出来的曲线，明确说明每多并行填一格要付出多少质量代价——这是一份诚实的速度-质量账，固定规则的方法自己也可以采用。\n\n## 方法\n### 图像条件化分组\n*把「哪些待填 token 一起发射」变成从冻结 backbone 与半成品图片实时读取的逐步决策。*\n\n1. 取一个预训练的、支持灵活顺序解码、带 shared KV-cache (Key/Value 缓存) 的 AR (Autoregressive, 自回归) 图像模型（ARPG 风格或 LlamaGen 级别），冻结其全部权重，模型本身不做任何重训练。只额外加一个轻量读取钩子：在每个网格位置读出模型内部的逐位置摘要向量（即最后一层 hidden state，其维度等于模型隐藏层宽度，例如 1024），对已经画好的格子和即将要画的格子都读取。把这些向量按网格位置建索引存好，让后续步骤无需再跑一遍模型就能取到任意待填格子的向量。\n   - _为什么_: 保持绘图模型不动，意味着任何加速都来自我们如何对格子分组，而不是换了更大或不同的模型。\n2. 在每个生成步，只对所有待填（尚未画）的格子同时跑一次模型——共享缓存已经保存了目前画好的全部内容，所以这一次前向就能给出每个待填格子的内部向量。然后对每一对待填格子运行 $g_{phi}$（一次批量调用），填出一张完整的方阵，记录两两之间的依赖分数 $\\sigma (a_{ij})$，外加每个待填格子的风险值 $r_{i}$。要给所有格子对打分，而不是预先选定的候选子集，这样下一步才能全盘考虑。由于这张表每一步都根据当前这张半成品图片重建，分组就会适配这张图，而不是照搬固定规则。\n   - _为什么_: 每一步都根据当前图片重新打分，正是让决策适配这张图、而非固定规则的关键。\n3. 贪心地构建待填格子的最大组，使其内部最差的两两依赖低于单一可学习阈值 $\\tau $。具体地：(1) 先剔除任何风险 $r_{i}$（压到 0 到 1 后）本身就高于 $\\tau $ 的格子；(2) 把其余格子按平均依赖程度排序，用依赖最低的格子作为组的起点；(3) 按此顺序逐个考察其余格子，只有当某格对组内已有每个格子的依赖都低于 $\\tau $ 时才加入它（若两个格子同样可加入，优先选风险更低的）；(4) 直到无法再加入为止。这样始终满足阈值约束，且计算开销很低。在依赖稀疏处会形成大组、在稠密处形成小组，于是模型前向次数随每张图实际的难度而变化。\n\n*在第 t 步，共同发射组 $G_{t}$ 取自待发射集合 $P_{t}$ 的最大子集，约束其内部最大成对依赖 $\\sigma (a_{ij})$ 低于单一可学习阈值 $\\tau $；这就是解码期、图像条件化的分组决策。*\n$$ G_t = \\operatorname*{arg\\,max}_{G \\subseteq P_t}\\; |G| \\quad \\text{s.t.}\\quad \\max_{i,j \\in G} \\sigma(a_{ij}) < \\tau \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 在依赖稀疏处形成大组、在稠密处形成小组，于是模型前向次数随每张图实际的难度而变化。\n4. 通过共享缓存在一次模型前向中填好该组的每个格子：以目前已提交的全部内容为条件，用基础模型常规的采样设置（temperature、top-k 不变）从各自预测的 token 分布中独立采样每个组内格子——之所以可以独立采样，是因为进入这个组就意味着它们之间的预测依赖已低于阈值。把采样得到的 token 写入图片并加入共享缓存。任何未进入本组的待填格子仍保持待填，下一步会针对此时更大的已提交上下文重新打分，于是待填集合严格缩小直到为空。最后用 VQ (Vector-Quantized, 向量量化) decoder 在完成的 token 网格上把 token 转成最终图像。在一次前向中填好一个安全组，正是节省 wall-clock 时间之处，且无需额外的 draft model（草稿模型）。\n   - _为什么_: 在一次前向中填好一个安全组，正是节省 wall-clock 时间之处，且无需额外的 draft model。\n\n### 碎片化诊断与安全头\n*测量联合发射相对独立发射的代价 $\\delta _{frag}$，并据此训练预测成对安全性 $a_{ij}$ 的安全头。*\n\n5. 离线地构建这套受控测量工具。对每个样本：用冻结模型严格逐格地在一张真实训练图片的真值 token 上解码，在随机选定的点 k 停下；此时 1..k 这些格子成为固定上下文（用真值 token 意味着采样不引入噪声）。从剩下的待填格子里随机挑一组共 m 个，m 从 2 到 16 之间均匀取值。用同一个冻结模型按两种方式解码这组格子：(1) 联合方式——按 teacher forcing 逐格解，每个格子都以上下文加上组内已解出的格子为条件（这是可信参考）；(2) 独立方式——所有组内格子在一次并行前向中解出，每个只看到上下文、彼此互不可见。对每一对格子，把碎片化代价测为两种结果在这对格子所覆盖 patch 上的差异；默认用 Jensen-Shannon 散度（一种对称、取值 0 到 1、衡量两个概率分布相距多远的量）来比较联合与独立两种码本分布（对解码后 patch 取像素级感知距离同样可用）。只改变填涂顺序——上下文与位置完全相同——因此测得的差异纯粹是并行填涂的代价，是任何固定规则都从未算过的逐对、逐图数值。\n\n*在固定上下文 c 下并行发射 token i 与 j 的碎片化代价，定义为同一组在 teacher-forced 顺序重建 $x_{joint}$ 与独立并行重建 $x_{indep}$ 之间的感知/码本散度 d；它是诊断器提供的校准标签。*\n$$ \\delta_{\\mathrm{frag}}(i,j\\mid c) = d\\big(x_{\\mathrm{joint}}(i,j\\mid c),\\; x_{\\mathrm{indep}}(i,j\\mid c)\\big) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 只改变「一起填还是逐格填」，测得的差异就纯粹是并行填涂的代价，给出任何固定规则都从未计算过的、逐对逐图的价格标签。\n6. 训练一个小的预测器 $g_{phi}$，把离线的价格标签变成即时的、事前的预测。对一对格子 (i,j)，喂给它：两个格子的内部向量 $h_{i}$ 和 $h_{j}$、它们逐元素的绝对差 $|h_{i}- h_{j}|$（这样无论哪个格子排在前面预测都一样）、模型自带的每个格子的 2D 位置嵌入，以及每个格子周边的固定长度摘要（以该格为中心、半径 3 的 $7\\times 7$ patch 上的平均嵌入，已填邻居用真实 token 嵌入、空着的邻居用一个可学习的「仍待填」嵌入）。$g_{phi}$ 是一个 2 隐层的多层感知机 (Multilayer Perceptron, MLP, 即小型全连接网络)，宽度为模型隐藏维度的四倍，有两个输出：成对依赖分数 $a_{ij}$，以及逐格风险 $r_{i}$。在模型冻结的前提下训练它：用均方误差 (Mean-Squared Error, MSE) 把 $\\sigma (a_{ij})——$即分数经 sigmoid 压到 0 到 1——拟合到上一步测得的碎片化代价；同时监督逐格风险 $r_{i}$ 去匹配每个格子对任意搭档的最差碎片化代价，使 $r_{i}$ 能排出一个格子一起发射有多危险。用 AdamW、学习率 1e-3 训练到验证拟合不再改善为止。训练后，$a_{ij}$ 就能在任何格子被填之前预测把 i 和 j 一起填会不会破坏结构。\n\n*安全头 $g_{phi}$ 通过将其成对依赖概率 $\\sigma (a_{ij})$ 以 MSE 回归到测得的 $\\delta _{frag}$ 标签来训练，backbone 保持冻结，因此 $a_{ij}$ 能在发射前预测共同发射 (i,j) 是否会增大碎片化。*\n$$ \\mathcal{L}(\\phi) = \\sum_{(i,j)} \\big(\\sigma(a_{ij}) - \\delta_{\\mathrm{frag}}(i,j\\mid c)\\big)^2,\\quad a_{ij} = g_\\phi\\big(h_i, h_j, \\mathrm{pos}, \\mathcal{N}_r\\big) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这把离线的价格标签变成模型在填涂任何东西之前就能做出的快速预测，且用的是模型自己的内部信号。\n\n### 工作点与保真代价报告\n*设定单一阈值 $\\tau $，报告逐图加速比与 $\\delta _{frag}$ 对组大小的账本。*\n\n7. 在验证集上调这一个阈值 $\\tau $ 并公布结果。试一组 $\\tau $ 取值（例如 0.1 到 0.9），在每个取值下生成验证集图片，记录图像质量 (FID, $Fr\\acute{e}chet$ Inception Distance, 弗雷歇感知距离) 对平均模型前向次数；选出在质量与全串行设置相差很小（默认在 +0.5 FID 以内）的前提下前向次数最少的那个 $\\tau $。对每张图，报告其平均组大小（除以允许的最大组大小，于是全串行读作 0、最大并行读作 1）作为该图依赖稀疏程度的度量，并将其对模型前向次数作图，以显示越简单的图填得越快。最后，公布碎片化代价随组大小变化的曲线——把诊断器测得的数据按组大小分箱、画出每个组大小下的平均代价——作为「每多并行一格付出多少质量代价」的诚实账本。\n   - _为什么_: 一个旋钮决定激进程度，而公布的曲线是「每多并行一格付出多少质量代价」的诚实账本。\n\n"},{"id":"73","run_dir":"run_prompt73_loongrl","index":73,"title":"Phase-Stratified Credit: Verifier-Free Per-Phase Advantage for Long-Context Reasoning RL","title_zh":"阶段分层信用分配：面向长上下文推理 RL 的免验证器逐阶段优势（Phase-Stratified Credit）","method_name":"Phase-Stratified GRPO (PS-GRPO)","hook":"On 128K-token KeyChain rollouts, vanilla GRPO's effective learning signal collapses because one trajectory-level advantage is broadcast equally across thousands of distractor-scan tokens and the handful of chain-tracing steps that actually decide correctness; we recover the signal by stratifying the rollout into phases and concentrating credit on the pivotal minority, using a per-phase reward harvested for free from the same group of rollouts GRPO already samples — no external verifier and no learned per-step critic.","anchor_pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","anchor_pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","domain_category":"LLM Reasoning & Decoding","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf makes the learning signal localize to the steps that actually determine correctness inside a long, internally heterogeneous reasoning rollout: LoongRL (openalex:W4416246797) and the GRPO-machinery papers all collapse a 16K-128K-token plan-retrieve-reason-recheck trajectory to one trajectory-level credit, so as context length grows the gradient on the few pivotal chain-tracing/grounding steps is diluted by the long distractor-scanning spans and the effective signal does","pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by partitioning the rollout's token spans into a high-influence pivotal minority and a near-redundant distractor bulk along an intrinsic per-phase credit-density criterion, then applying a differentiated advantage (full-strength to the minority, attenuated to the bulk) under an unbiasedness-in-expectation decomposition that bounds how the stratified credit recovers the original trajectory-level objective.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf provides an intermediate correctness signal for long-context reasoning that does not reintroduce the very dependencies the outcome-only regime was adopted to avoid: KeyChain (openalex:W4416246797) and the rule-based-reward line deliberately use a single verifiable end reward to dodge reward hacking and LLM-as-judge cost (which CoVRL, arxiv:2512.12576v3, attacks only at the trace-vs-answer level), leaving open how to obtain trustworthy per-phase feedback over a long tra","pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","sub_pattern":"C26 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by manufacturing a relative (not categorical) per-phase reward from an ordering that already exists inside GRPO's sampled group -- minimal-pair span contrasts between correct and incorrect rollouts that share a common prefix, scored by the policy's own internal token log-probs -- so trustworthy per-phase feedback is harvested verifier-free and never reintroduces an external judge or a separately-trained step reward model.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"reinforcement learning for long-context multi-step reasoning in LLMs","n_papers":47,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":25},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":5,"papers":[{"source":"openalex","title":"Large Language Model (LLM) for Telecommunications: A Comprehensive Survey on Principles, Key Techniques, and Opportunities"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Qwen2.5 Technical Report"},{"source":"openalex","title":"A Review of Large Language Models: Fundamental Architectures, Key Technological Evolutions, Interdisciplinary Technologies Integration, Optimization and Compression Techniques, Applications, and Challenges"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Confidence in the Reasoning of Large Language Models"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Beyond Examples: High-level Automated Reasoning Paradigm in In-Context Learning via MCTS"}],"more":0},{"year":2025,"n":36,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Advancing Language Model Reasoning through Reinforcement Learning and Inference Scaling"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"DeepSeek-R1 incentivizes reasoning in LLMs through reinforcement learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Fin-R1: A Large Language Model for Financial Reasoning through Reinforcement Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Co-Reward: Self-supervised Reinforcement Learning for Large Language Model Reasoning via Contrastive Agreement"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"SuperRL: Reinforcement Learning with Supervision to Boost Language Model Reasoning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Kalman Filter Enhanced GRPO for Reinforcement Learning-Based Language Model Reasoning"}],"more":30},{"year":2026,"n":7,"papers":[{"source":"arxiv","title":"Group Distributionally Robust Optimization-Driven Reinforcement Learning for LLM Reasoning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Value Bonuses using Ensemble Errors for Exploration in Reinforcement Learning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"CosmicFish-HRM: Adaptive Reasoning via Hierarchical Recurrent Mechanisms in Compact Language Models"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"CROP: Token-Efficient Reasoning in Large Language Models via Regularized Prompt Optimization"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"ChaosBench-Logic: A Benchmark for Logical and Symbolic Reasoning on Chaotic Dynamical Systems"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Agentic Reasoning for Large Language Models"}],"more":1}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering; reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"self_supervised_signal_engineering; reframe_as_solvable_object","count":4,"share":0.085},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":4,"share":0.085},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning; self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"adapt_via_conditioning; self_supervised_signal_engineering","count":2,"share":0.043},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":2,"share":0.043},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object; self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"reframe_as_solvable_object; self_supervised_signal_engineering","count":2,"share":0.043},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object; decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"reframe_as_solvable_object; decompose_and_delegate","count":2,"share":0.043},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate; unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"decompose_and_delegate; unify_into_shared_representation","count":2,"share":0.043},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate; adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"decompose_and_delegate; adapt_via_conditioning","count":2,"share":0.043}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Recent long-context reasoning RL gets its gains from harder synthesized data fed to an unchanged outcome-reward policy-gradient optimizer: LoongRL (openalex:W4416246797) trains an emergent multi-step plan-retrieve-reason-recheck trajectory spanning 16K-128K tokens using standard GRPO with a single binary substring-match reward (Eq. 3) whose group-mean/std advantage (Eq. 2) is broadcast uniformly across every token of the rollout, and the GRPO-machinery papers in the window only refine adjacent terms - KRPO (semanticscholar:4ecacdd6) replaces the group-mean baseline with a Kalman-filtered per-prompt baseline to cut its variance, GDRO (arxiv:2601.19280v1) reweights the prompt distribution - while none changes the fact that a long trajectory in which only a handful of chain-tracing and grounding steps are load-bearing and the bulk of the tokens copy or scan distractor documents receives one undifferentiated credit assignment. The failure: under a single trajectory-level reward over a very long, internally heterogeneous reasoning rollout, the gradient cannot distinguish the few decision steps that determined correctness from the long stretches of distractor traversal, so credit on the actually-pivotal steps is diluted toward zero and the optimizer's effective signal-to-length ratio collapses as context grows - which is precisely the regime (128K) where the method must work.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416246797","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"LoongRL synthesizes high-difficulty long-context tasks via KeyChain (inserting UUID key-value chains and distractor documents that hide the true question), and RL on this data induces an emergent plan-retrieve-reason-recheck pattern that generalizes from 16K training to 128K test. Its entire novelty is data construction: the optimizer is unmodified GRPO with a binary outcome reward and a group-mean/std advantage applied identically to every token of the long rollout, so it provides no per-step or per-phase credit assignment over the heterogeneous trajectory and leaves open how the pivotal chain-tracing/grounding steps should be credited differently from the long distractor-scanning spans.","residue_is_abstract_level":false},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:4ecacdd6","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"KRPO (Kalman Filter Enhanced GRPO) treats per-group rewards as noisy observations of a latent per-prompt reward baseline and uses a 1D Kalman filter to estimate that baseline and its uncertainty, reducing advantage-estimate variance at small group size with no extra learned parameters. It still produces one scalar advantage per trajectory and normalizes it across the whole rollout, so it improves the baseline term but does nothing to localize credit to the load-bearing steps inside a long multi-hop trajectory."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2601.19280v1","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"GDRO reframes GRPO's static uniformity by adding an online difficulty classifier and a distributionally-robust objective that dynamically reweights which prompts and how many rollouts the optimizer spends compute on, focusing the long tail of hard problems. It operates entirely at the prompt-distribution level (which examples to train on), leaving the within-trajectory credit-assignment over thousands of tokens of a single long rollout untouched."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2512.12576v3","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"CoVRL couples prior (question-only) and posterior (answer-conditioned) sampling of reasoning traces to give a verifier-free reward that keeps traces coherent with the final answer and improves exploration. It addresses where the reward signal comes from and trace-answer coherence, but still treats the reasoning trace as a single unit to be rewarded, not as a long sequence whose individual reasoning/retrieval steps demand differentiated credit."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"reinforcement learning for long-context multi-step reasoning in LLMs","venue":"ML top-tier (NeurIPS/ICML/ICLR)","time":"2026","data":["long-context multi-hop QA (HotpotQA, MuSiQue, 2WikiMultiHopQA) extended to 16K-128K tokens","RULER / long-context retrieval-reasoning benchmarks","verifiable-answer reasoning corpora used by recent RLVR work"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day budget)","expertise":"RL for LLMs, policy-gradient / GRPO-family optimization, long-context modeling","preference":"both","baseline":"GRPO with binary outcome reward and group-mean/std advantage on KeyChain-synthesized long-context data (LoongRL, openalex:W4416246797)","limitation":"advanced long-context reasoning is currently driven almost entirely by training-data synthesis on top of off-the-shelf outcome-reward GRPO; the optimizer assigns a single trajectory-level signal to a long, structurally heterogeneous plan-retrieve-reason-recheck rollout, so it cannot tell which of the many steps over thousands of tokens were actually responsible for success or failure","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["domain","venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The two legs form one sequential pipeline whose shared object is the per-phase credit-density vector d over a rollout: leg B (C26) computes d verifier-free, and leg A (C04) consumes d to stratify the advantage. SETUP: fix the base optimizer to GRPO (LoongRL's substrate); for each prompt p, GRPO already samples a group G of K rollouts (default K=16) and computes one group-normalized scalar advantage A_g per rollout g (Eq. 2 of the baseline). LEG B (manufacture the per-phase signal): segment each rollout g into phases s=1..S_g by the emergent plan/retrieve/reason/recheck markers (boundary tokens; when markers are absent, fall back to fixed 512-token windows). The per-phase reward r_{g,s} is a RELATIVE quantity, computed two ways and summed: (i) minimal-pair contrast -- within group G, pair a correct rollout g+ with an incorrect rollout g- that shares the longest common phase-prefix, and credit the first phase at which they diverge by +1 on g+ / -1 on g- (this is the phase where the trajectories' fates split, an ordering already encoded in the group, harvested not learned); (ii) self-score -- r^self_{g,s} = mean token log-prob the CURRENT policy assigns to phase s's own tokens, z-normalized across the S_g phases of g, capturing the policy's internal confidence ordering over its own spans. Both are model-internal readouts or in-group comparisons -- no external verifier, no separately trained reward model. The per-phase CREDIT-DENSITY is d_{g,s} = softmax over s of ( beta1 * contrast_{g,s} + beta2 * r^self_{g,s} ), beta1=1.0, beta2=0.3 (named hyperparameters bridging the unit-mismatch between the +/-1 contrast and the z-scored log-prob), so sum_s d_{g,s}=1: d is the fraction of the rollout's credit each phase should bear. LEG A (differentiated treatment): replace GRPO's uniform per-token advantage A_g (broadcast identically to all T_g tokens) with a phase-stratified advantage A_{g,s} = A_g * (S_g * d_{g,s}), assigned to every token in phase s. The S_g factor is a credit-conservation normalizer: E_s[A_{g,s}] over phases = A_g, so the stratified advantage is UNBIASED relative to the original trajectory-level objective in expectation -- the redistribution only re-weights WHERE the same total credit lands, it does not inflate or deflate it (this is the C04 load-bearing error decomposition: total = sum_s (tokens_s/T_g)*A_{g,s}, and stratification strictly reduces the variance contributed by the near-zero-influence distractor bulk while preserving the pivotal-phase gradient). The artifact closing leg A's gap is A_{g,s}: as context grows to 128K the pivotal phases stay a near-constant SMALL number of tokens while T_g grows, so vanilla A_g's per-pivotal-token signal-to-length ratio decays as 1/T_g, whereas A_{g,s} pins credit mass to those phases via d and is length-invariant. The artifact closing leg B's gap is d itself: a trustworthy per-phase signal that is verifier-free because it is built only from in-group correct/incorrect orderings (which the binary end reward already certifies) and the policy's own log-probs -- it cannot be reward-hacked by an external judge because there is no judge. This differs from prior work substantively: LoongRL (openalex:W4416246797) leaves A_g untouched and pushes novelty into KeyChain data; KRPO (semanticscholar:4ecacdd6) refines the BASELINE term feeding A_g but still emits one scalar per trajectory; GDRO (arxiv:2601.19280v1) re-weights WHICH prompts get rollouts, not WHERE credit lands inside a rollout.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules: the per-phase reward d (leg B) is exactly the discriminating property the C04 partition (leg A) requires, so the evidence is structural -- leg A cannot stratify credit without a per-phase density, and leg B's only purpose is to produce one consumable by an optimizer, which is the sequential_pipeline thread (signal -> differentiated credit). Bundling them as parallel modules would read as two papers; pipelining them makes d the single shared object. (b) Alternatives rejected: (1) a learned per-token value critic / GAE to localize credit -- rejected as a REGRESSION to method_lineage nodes n1/n2 (the per-token critic LLM-RL deliberately dropped for long rollouts); (2) a separately trained process reward model scoring each step (lineage c0) -- rejected as reward-hackable and label-hungry, and the REGRESSION FLAG names it; (3) return-redistribution machinery (lineage c2) -- rejected as sample-hungry and built for short control tasks. We instead harvest the ordering from GRPO's already-sampled group and the policy's own log-probs, a source the lineage tree does NOT occupy (no new learned scorer, no critic), and keep the redistribution unbiased-in-expectation so it cannot collapse to a degenerate reweighting. Avoided nodes recorded: n1, n2, c0, c2.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: train two checkpoints from the same base LLM on identical 16K KeyChain data and equal compute -- (i) vanilla GRPO (LoongRL substrate) and (ii) phase-stratified GRPO -- and evaluate both at 16K/32K/64K/128K on RULER + extended multi-hop QA. If the candidate works, the accuracy gap (ii minus i) INCREASES with context length, i.e. stratified credit is roughly on par at 16K but its 128K answer accuracy is materially higher, because the pivotal phases stay a near-constant token budget while the distractor bulk grows. The single named load-bearing variable is the per-phase advantage concentration ratio C (fraction of total advantage magnitude placed on pivotal-phase tokens); the mechanism claim is that gains are caused by concentrating credit on the pivotal minority. Negative control: permute the phase labels so the density d lands on randomly chosen spans instead of the contrast/self-score-identified pivotal phases (C is held at the SAME numeric level, only its placement is randomized) -- the prediction is that downstream 128K answer accuracy collapses back to the vanilla-GRPO curve, NOT that C changes. This is the real Popper test: if accuracy survives random placement, the gain came from a generic variance-reduction or extra-compute effect rather than from localizing credit to the steps that determine correctness. Positive control: a stripped model that keeps ONLY the minimal-pair contrast term (drop self-score) should recover most of the 128K accuracy gain, identifying the in-group correct/incorrect ordering as the load-bearing source of the per-phase signal.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416246797","delta":"LoongRL leaves the GRPO advantage A_g untouched and broadcasts it uniformly across the whole 16K-128K rollout, concentrating its novelty in KeyChain data construction; we construct a per-phase stratified advantage A_{g,s} that redistributes that same A_g onto the pivotal-phase minority, an artifact their unmodified-optimizer design never produces."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:4ecacdd6","delta":"KRPO refines the BASELINE feeding the single trajectory-level advantage via a Kalman filter but still emits one scalar per rollout normalized over all tokens; we derive a within-trajectory credit-density d and a credit-conserving stratified advantage that localizes credit to specific phases, which a baseline-only refinement cannot do."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2601.19280v1","delta":"GDRO re-weights WHICH prompts and how many rollouts the optimizer spends compute on via an online difficulty classifier (a prompt-distribution-level lever), explicitly leaving within-trajectory credit untouched; we re-weight WHERE inside a single rollout the credit lands, a different lever that operates below the prompt level."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2512.12576v3","delta":"CoVRL changes the reward SOURCE to a verifier-free coupled-variational score but still rewards the trace as one unit at the trace-vs-answer level; we manufacture a RELATIVE per-phase signal from in-group correct/incorrect minimal-pair orderings and re-granularize credit below the trace, which a trace-level reward cannot localize."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4416246797","what_step_was_missed":"LoongRL constructs the KeyChain data that induces the emergent plan-retrieve-reason-recheck phase structure but never reads that phase structure back out as a credit-assignment variable: for our contribution to already exist it would have had to construct a per-phase credit-density over its own emergent trajectory (a quantity derivable from the in-group correct/incorrect ordering it already has) and a credit-conserving stratified advantage that consumes it, neither of which its uniform-broadcast advantage produces."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":335,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"No hard floor fires: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict=borderline (no Reject lesson is candidate_match:yes), anti_pattern_check matched audit_decomp_supervisor but mitigation_substantively_delivered=true (both disentangling ablations shipped), and paper_pointed_threat is collision/overlap not exact-mechanism subsumption. Revise (not advance) is warranted because the paper_pointed_threat OPPO (arxiv:2605.21851v2) is addressable via a specific candidate field -- it states the candidate's exact premise and length-scaling claim, so differentiation_from_lit and the hook must be sharpened or the contribution reads as a re-derivation. This also resolves the two borderline reject-lesson findings (C26 'changing only granularity ... incremental unless a demonstrated unlock' and C04 'proxy as novelty ... unless sharply differentiated from the obvious prior criterion'), both of which turn on differentiating from the crowded fine-grained-GRPO-credit field (SPO, RREDCoT, GEAR, EGCA, TreeAdv, OPPO).","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf makes the learning signal localize to the steps that actually determine correctness inside a long, internally heterogeneous reasoning rollout: LoongRL (openalex:W4416246797) and the GRPO-machinery papers all collapse a 16K-128K-token plan-retrieve-reason-recheck trajectory to one trajectory-level credit, so as context length grows the gradient on the few pivotal chain-tracing/grounding steps is diluted by the long distractor-scanning spans and the effective signal does not survive the length scaling the method is built for.","main_pattern":"heterogeneous_decomposition","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is treating the partition criterion itself as the contribution while leaving its value unproven, so reviewers map the discriminator onto an established technique and the differentiated treatment reads as a relabeling. A second shortcut is skipping the analysis of why the heterogeneity exists and validating where the bottleneck does not bite.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Presenting a sensitivity or redundancy proxy as the novelty invites the verdict that it rediscovers known mixed-precision or low-rank results unless it is sharply differentiated from the obvious prior criterion.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The partition proxy (per-phase credit-density d from in-group contrast + self log-prob) sits in a now-crowded fine-grained-credit field; core_mechanism differentiates from KRPO/GDRO but not yet from the closest prior criterion (OPPO's pivotal-token state weight), so the discriminator's distinctness is only partly defended."},{"lesson_quoted":"Skipping any analysis of why the heterogeneity exists -- the data or value distribution that drives the partition -- makes the technical novelty and the potential impact impossible to assess.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism supplies the why: pivotal phases stay a near-constant small token count while T_g grows, so vanilla A_g's per-pivotal-token signal decays as 1/T_g; the concentration ratio C operationalizes the value distribution that forces the partition."},{"lesson_quoted":"Omitting comparison against both the strongest uniform baseline and the obvious cheap alternative (SVD/PCA, structured dropout, a natively trained smaller model) leaves reviewers unable to tell whether the partition buys anything at all.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"falsification_prediction pits stratified GRPO against the strongest uniform baseline (vanilla GRPO) at matched compute and adds negative (phase-label permutation) and positive (contrast-only / self-score-only) controls."},{"lesson_quoted":"Bolting together established components (distillation plus pruning plus calibration) without an error bound or artifact specific to the new setting reads as incremental even when the target application is timely and important.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The S_g credit-conservation normalizer with E_s[A_{g,s}]=A_g is a setting-specific unbiasedness/variance decomposition (the C04 load-bearing error analysis), not a bare bolt-together."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf provides an intermediate correctness signal for long-context reasoning that does not reintroduce the very dependencies the outcome-only regime was adopted to avoid: KeyChain (openalex:W4416246797) and the rule-based-reward line deliberately use a single verifiable end reward to dodge reward hacking and LLM-as-judge cost (which CoVRL, arxiv:2512.12576v3, attacks only at the trace-vs-answer level), leaving open how to obtain trustworthy per-phase feedback over a long trajectory whose intermediate states (plan, retrieved facts, recheck) are themselves only weakly verifiable.","main_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","sub_pattern":"C26 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The dominant failure is the single-component swap -- taking the established preference pipeline and changing exactly one slot (human->AI judge, offline->online, response-level->step-level granularity) and presenting that swap as the contribution, which reviewers read as incremental because it unlocks no previously-unreachable behavior. A self-check: is the move bundled with a removed approximation, a previously-impossible capability, or a newly-surfaced failure axis?","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Changing only the granularity of an established contrastive objective (response-level -> step-level) is judged incremental unless paired with a clearly demonstrated practical unlock.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"Re-granularizing credit below the trace IS the move, and the collision corpus (SPO, RREDCoT, GEAR, OPPO, EGCA, TreeAdv) shows segment/step-level credit is now a crowded slot; the candidate's unlock claim (length-invariant pivotal credit surviving to 128K, an axis these short-CoT/math methods do not target) is plausible but is not yet sharply isolated from the nearest prior in differentiation_from_lit."},{"lesson_quoted":"Swapping the preference-label source (human -> AI judge, offline -> online) without showing the swap unlocks a behavior previously unreachable reads as a one-component substitution and draws novelty rejections.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The per-phase reward is not a swapped label source but a relative quantity harvested two ways from structure GRPO already has (in-group correct/incorrect minimal-pair divergence + own log-probs), bundled with a credit-conserving consumer, not a single swapped box."},{"lesson_quoted":"Stopping at the preference dataset, benchmark, or reward model without demonstrating the downstream optimization it is meant to feed leaves the contribution looking like infrastructure rather than method.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"d is immediately consumed by leg A (the stratified advantage feeding loss.backward); the deliverable is a runnable optimizer, not a standalone signal artifact."},{"lesson_quoted":"Borrowing a structurally related proxy domain to synthesize preference data, without validating that the proxy's regularities transfer to the target's end-goal metric, invites rigor and generalization concerns.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"No proxy domain is borrowed; the signal is built in-domain from the same KeyChain rollouts and evaluated on the target long-context end metric (RULER + multi-hop QA accuracy)."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No Reject lesson is a hard 'yes', so the hard floor does not fire. The aggregate is borderline, driven by the C26 entry (self_supervised_signal_engineering) lesson 'Changing only the granularity of an established contrastive objective ... is judged incremental unless paired with a clearly demonstrated practical unlock' and the C04 entry's 'sensitivity/redundancy proxy as novelty ... unless sharply differentiated from the obvious prior criterion' -- both turn on whether the candidate is sharply differentiated from the now-crowded fine-grained-GRPO-credit field, which differentiation_from_lit does not yet fully address."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf makes the learning signal localize to the steps that actually determine correctness inside a long, internally heterogeneous reasoning rollout: LoongRL and the GRPO-machinery papers all collapse a 16K-128K-token plan-retrieve-reason-recheck trajectory to one trajectory-level credit.","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Discriminate components by a magnitude/sensitivity/influence/redundancy criterion into a high-impact minority and a near-redundant bulk, then preserve the minority while aggressively compressing the bulk; the load-bearing artifact is an error/sensitivity decomposition that bounds how the differentiated treatment recovers the original objective -- that analysis, not the partition idea, is what separates the move from heuristic per-component tuning.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"LEG A performs exactly this: it partitions rollout token-spans into a pivotal minority and a near-redundant distractor bulk along an intrinsic per-phase credit-density criterion d, gives full-strength advantage to the minority and attenuated advantage to the bulk, and supplies the load-bearing decomposition -- A_{g,s}=A_g*(S_g*d_{g,s}) with E_s[A_{g,s}]=A_g so the redistribution is unbiased-in-expectation while strictly reducing the variance contributed by the near-zero-influence distractor bulk. The C04 signature (error decomposition bounding recovery of the original objective) is present, not bypassed.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf provides an intermediate correctness signal for long-context reasoning that does not reintroduce the dependencies the outcome-only regime was adopted to avoid.","sub_pattern":"C26 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Manufacture a comparative (not categorical) signal by extracting preference pairs from structures that already encode an ordering (e.g. the policy's own internal scores, execution-verified vs failed trajectories), constructing each pair to differ minimally (one faulty transition sharing an otherwise-correct prefix), and re-granularizing the comparison to where credit assignment fails.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"LEG B performs the signature move: within GRPO's already-sampled group G it pairs a correct rollout g+ with an incorrect g- sharing the longest common phase-prefix and credits the FIRST divergent phase (+1/-1) -- a minimal-pair, prefix-sharing contrast harvested from an in-group ordering the binary end reward already certifies -- and adds the policy's own per-phase log-prob self-score, combining them into a RELATIVE per-phase density d. This is the cluster's 'harvest an existing ordering, make it relative, re-granularize to where credit fails' move, not the generic parent gist; applied.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both legs perform their cited cluster's distinctive move: C04's error/credit-conservation decomposition is present in A_{g,s}=A_g*(S_g*d_{g,s}) with the unbiasedness identity, and C26's minimal-pair, prefix-sharing, relative-not-categorical contrast harvested from the in-group ordering is present in leg B. Neither reduces to the parent pattern's generic gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["heterogeneous_decomposition","self_supervised_signal_engineering"],"matched_pattern_id":"audit_decomp_supervisor","required_mitigation_quoted":"The decomposition criterion must be derivable from observed structure or task-level supervision (not just intuition), AND the manufactured signal must be the *unique* signal the decomposition implies. An ablation that holds the decomposition fixed and varies the signal (or vice versa) must show the two are not conflated.","mitigation_substantively_delivered":"true","reasoning":"Delivered at the artifact level: (1) the decomposition criterion is read off observed structure -- emergent plan/retrieve/reason/recheck boundary tokens with a deterministic 512-token fallback -- not pure intuition; (2) the manufactured signal d is the single shared object leg A consumes (it is the discriminating property the partition requires), and the candidate ships BOTH disentangling ablations the mitigation demands: the positive control holds the decomposition fixed and varies the signal (contrast-only vs self-score-only variants of d), and the negative control holds the signal magnitude (concentration ratio C) fixed while randomizing its placement (phase-label permutation), which varies the decomposition -- so decomposition and signal are shown not to be conflated."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"arxiv:2605.21851v2","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"OPPO (Oracle-Prompted Policy Optimization) states the candidate's exact motivating premise almost verbatim -- 'GRPO assigns a single trajectory-level advantage to every token, diluting the signal at pivotal reasoning steps' -- and delivers a verifier-free, critic-free, no-additional-rollout per-token advantage that 'concentrates credit on genuinely pivotal tokens', with a first-order variance-reduction guarantee and gains that 'widen monotonically with response length' (the candidate's headline length-scaling claim). Its self-oracle variant scores evidence with the student's own probabilities, overlapping the candidate's self-score leg. If a reviewer reads OPPO as already owning 'verifier-free pivotal-token credit concentration on GRPO whose benefit grows with length', the candidate's counter-intuitive-minimalism hook ('a redistribution of existing signal with nothing added beats data-scaling') loses its surprise and the contribution narrows to method-detail. The claim does NOT collapse, however: OPPO localizes via a per-token Bayesian belief recursion built from oracle-conditioned likelihood ratios (one extra forward pass), whereas the candidate localizes via (a) PHASE-level stratification keyed to emergent plan/retrieve/reason/recheck structure and (b) an IN-GROUP minimal-pair correct/incorrect divergence contrast that OPPO does not use, plus an explicit credit-conservation S_g normalizer making the redistribution unbiased-in-expectation. This is overlap-and-collision, not exact-mechanism subsumption -- the distinguishing artifacts (phase partition criterion, in-group minimal-pair contrast, S_g credit conservation, long-context 128K regime vs OPPO's short math/code) are real and load-bearing.","addressable_via":"differentiation_from_lit (add an OPPO entry sharply contrasting per-token Bayesian belief recursion from oracle likelihood ratios against the candidate's phase-stratified in-group minimal-pair contrast) and a hook/hook_shape_rationale tweak that reframes the minimalism claim as 'phase-stratified, in-group-harvested credit for the long-context regime' rather than the now-occupied generic 'verifier-free pivotal-token concentration on GRPO'."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat = arxiv:2605.21851v2 (OPPO), an addressable collision that states the candidate's exact premise ('GRPO ... single trajectory-level advantage ... diluting signal at pivotal steps') and headline length-scaling claim while delivering verifier-free, critic-free per-token credit concentration with a variance-reduction guarantee; also resolves the C26 'granularity-only is incremental' and C04 'proxy-as-novelty' borderline reject lessons by differentiating from the crowded fine-grained-credit cluster.","fix_direction":"Add a differentiation_from_lit entry for arxiv:2605.21851v2 (OPPO): delta = OPPO localizes credit via a PER-TOKEN Bayesian belief recursion accumulated from oracle-conditioned likelihood ratios (one extra forward pass), a continuous running success-probability estimate; we instead (i) partition at the PHASE level keyed to emergent plan/retrieve/reason/recheck structure, (ii) source the per-phase signal from an IN-GROUP minimal-pair correct/incorrect prefix-divergence contrast OPPO does not use, and (iii) impose an explicit credit-conservation S_g normalizer making the redistribution unbiased-in-expectation -- and we target the 128K long-context regime where the distractor bulk grows, vs OPPO's short math/science/code benchmarks. Optionally add a one-line nod to RREDCoT (arxiv:2606.06475v1, segment-level reward redistribution from the model without extra generation) and SPO (semanticscholar:ac8cbc7d..., segment-level MC credit) to pre-empt the crowded-field concern."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"hook_shape_rationale","issue":"The minimalism hook ('a redistribution of existing signal, with nothing added, beats data-scaling') is now partly occupied by OPPO and the broader verifier-free fine-grained-credit cluster, so the counter-intuitive-minimalism surprise is weakened against the retrieved frontier.","fix_direction":"Re-anchor the minimalism claim on the candidate's genuinely unoccupied axes: emphasize that the credit is harvested from the IN-GROUP correct/incorrect ordering GRPO already certifies (no oracle/teacher forward pass as OPPO needs, no MC rollouts as SPO/RREDCoT need) and that the win is specifically a LENGTH-INVARIANT pivotal-credit ratio in the 128K long-context regime -- i.e. minimalism relative to OPPO/SPO/RREDCoT's extra forward passes or MC sampling, not merely relative to LoongRL's data-scaling. Keep falsification_prediction and compute_budget byte-identical."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit[4].delta","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Appended a differentiation entry for arxiv:2605.21851v2 (OPPO) contrasting OPPO's per-token Bayesian belief recursion from oracle likelihood ratios (one extra forward pass) against our phase-level partition, in-group minimal-pair prefix-divergence contrast, and S_g credit-conservation normalizer, with nods to RREDCoT and SPO to defuse the crowded segment-level-credit field."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"hook_shape_rationale","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Re-anchored the counter-intuitive-minimalism claim on the genuinely unoccupied axes -- in-group-harvested credit with no extra forward pass and no MC sampling (vs OPPO/SPO/RREDCoT) and a length-invariant pivotal-credit ratio in the 128K regime -- so the surprise survives the verifier-free fine-grained-credit frontier, not just LoongRL's data-scaling."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Phase-Stratified Credit: Verifier-Free Per-Phase Advantage for Long-Context Reasoning RL\n\n**Method.** Phase-Stratified GRPO (PS-GRPO)\n\n## Motivation\nThe user works on teaching large language models to reason over very long documents using reinforcement learning. Today's best method, LoongRL (Long-context Reinforcement Learning), gets its results by making the training data harder -- it hides the real question inside long chains of made-up key-value codes and lots of distractor text -- and then trains with an off-the-shelf algorithm called GRPO (Group Relative Policy Optimization). GRPO produces one single score for the entire answer (a long chain of 16,000 to 128,000 words of plan, retrieve, reason, and double-check steps) and then applies that one score equally to every single word.\n\nThe core problem is that only a few steps in that very long chain actually decide whether the answer is right -- the moments where the model traces the key chain and grounds a fact -- while most of the words are just scanning through distractor text. Because the one score is spread evenly over everything, the learning signal on those few decisive steps gets diluted. The longer the document gets (toward 128,000 words), the worse this dilution becomes: the decisive steps stay a small fixed number of words while the filler grows, so the useful signal per decisive word shrinks roughly like 1 over the total length. The method collapses exactly in the long-context regime it was built for.\n\nThis is timely because LoongRL (arXiv 2025-10) is the first method to produce reasoning chains long and structured enough for this problem to even appear, and because a wave of recent work (such as CoVRL, Coupled Variational Reinforcement Learning, arXiv 2025-12) has shown you can build useful reward signals without any external grader. The key new insight is that GRPO already samples a whole batch of attempts -- some right, some wrong -- and the comparison between them already tells you which step made the difference, for free.\n\nPrior work stopped short for specific reasons. LoongRL never looks back at the phase structure it creates and uses it for credit -- its whole novelty is the data. KRPO (Kalman-filtered GRPO) only cleans up the single per-answer score, never breaking it into phases. GDRO (Group Distributionally Robust Optimization) only chooses which problems to train on, not where credit lands inside one answer. CoVRL changes where the reward comes from but still scores the whole chain as one unit. When this gap closes, long-context reasoning stops being limited by signal dilution, so the same data and compute can train much deeper at 128,000 words, and the phase structure LoongRL discovered becomes an active training lever instead of a passive byproduct.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n*Unchanged GRPO long-context substrate and the length-scaling evaluation that frames the contribution.*\n\n1. Build the strongest plain baseline first. Take an open large language model in the 7-8 billion-parameter range that already supports a 128,000-token context (for example Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) and train it with the standard Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO) algorithm on the 16,000-token KeyChain training data. Use a simple right/wrong reward: score 1 if the correct answer text appears (after lowercasing and collapsing spaces and punctuation) inside the model's final-answer section, otherwise 0. GRPO samples a group of 16 attempts per question, turns each attempt's reward into one group-normalized number $A_{g},$ and spreads that single number over every token of the attempt. Save, for every attempt, its reward, its $A_{g},$ its length, and the per-token score, plus the accuracy measured all the way out to 128,000 tokens; this curve is your reference for everything that follows.\n\n*GRPO's group-normalized scalar advantage for rollout g: the rollout reward $R_{g}$ minus the group $mean \\bar{R}_{q}$ over the std $\\sigma _{q},$ the single scalar broadcast uniformly to all $T_{g}$ tokens in the baseline.*\n$$ A_g = \\frac{R_g - \\bar{R}_q}{\\sigma_q} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: You need the strongest plain baseline at the same compute so any gain is attributable to the redistribution, not to extra training.\n2. Train the phase-stratified version on the same data for the same number of update steps as the baseline, then test both models at 16,000 / 32,000 / 64,000 / 128,000 tokens on RULER and an extended multi-hop question-answering suite (HotpotQA, MuSiQue, 2WikiMultiHopQA). Report accuracy at each length. Also measure how concentrated the credit is: for each answer call the 'decisive' phases the smallest group of highest-credit-density phases whose densities together first reach half of the total, then compute C, the fraction of total credit-magnitude landing on those decisive phases, and average C over all training answers at each length. This checks the central claim directly: the accuracy advantage should grow with length, and C names exactly the quantity the method is supposed to move.\n   - _Why_: It checks the central claim directly: the advantage should grow with length, and C names exactly the quantity the method is supposed to move.\n\n### Verifier-Free Per-Phase Signal (Leg B)\n*Manufacture a trustworthy per-phase credit-density from the in-group correct/incorrect ordering and the policy's own confidences, with no external judge or extra forward pass.*\n\n3. Add a simple, rule-based splitter that cuts each generated answer into its plan, retrieve, reason, and recheck phases. It walks through the answer once and starts a new phase whenever it hits one of the agreed boundary markers, tagging each piece with which of the four phase types it is; if an answer has no markers at all, it falls back to cutting the answer into fixed 512-token chunks and treats each chunk as one phase. You must decide what actually counts as a boundary marker 【author decision: which surface tokens delimit a phase — explicit span tags the model is trained to emit, a fixed list of natural-language cue phrases, or a small learned boundary detector】. The output is, for every token, which phase number it belongs to and what type that phase is, giving $S_{g}$ phases for that answer. The phases come from the model's own observable structure, so you are not adding a new learned scorer that could be gamed.\n   - _Why_: The phases come from the model's own observed structure, so you are not adding a new learned scorer that could be gamed or that you would have to train.\n4. Inside the group of 16 attempts for one question, compare a correct attempt with a wrong one. Two attempts share a phase-prefix when their ordered list of phase types (plan, retrieve, reason, recheck, ...) matches from the start; you only compare the phase-type labels, not the exact words. For each correct attempt, pick the wrong attempt whose matching phase-prefix is longest (break ties by the lowest attempt id so it is reproducible), and do the same from the wrong side. The first phase where the two diverge is the decisive split: mark it +1 on the correct attempt and -1 on the wrong one, leaving every other phase at 0. If an attempt gets paired more than once, add up its +1/-1 marks across all its pairs. If the group happens to have no correct attempts or no wrong attempts, no contrast can be formed, so leave every phase at 0 for that group. The point where a right and a wrong attempt split is exactly where the decisive step lives, and the group already tells you this for free.\n\n*In-group minimal-pair contrast: a correct rollout g+ and an incorrect g- sharing the longest common phase-prefix split at phase s, which is credited +1 on g+ and -1 on g-, harvesting the ordering the binary end reward already certifies.*\n$$ \\text{contrast}_{g^+,s} = +1,\\quad \\text{contrast}_{g^-,s} = -1 \\;\\;\\text{at the first phase } s \\text{ where } g^+ \\text{ and } g^- \\text{ diverge} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The point where a right and a wrong attempt split is exactly where the decisive step lives, and the group already tells you this for free.\n5. For each phase, take the model's own average word-confidence — the mean log-probability the model assigned to the tokens in that phase — and reuse the confidences that were already computed when the answer was generated, so there is no extra forward pass. Then standardize these phase averages across the phases of that one answer: subtract the answer's average-of-phases and divide by the spread across phases (add a tiny 1e-6 to the spread so you never divide by zero). If an answer has only one phase there is no spread to compare against, so set its self-score to 0. The result is one standardized confidence number per phase. This adds a second free signal — the model's internal confidence ordering over its own spans.\n\n*Self-score: the current policy's mean token log-prob over phase s, z-normalized across the $S_{g}$ phases of g, capturing the policy's internal confidence ordering over its own spans with no extra forward pass.*\n$$ r^{\\text{self}}_{g,s} = \\operatorname{z-norm}_s\\!\\left(\\frac{1}{|s|}\\sum_{t \\in s} \\log \\pi_\\theta(x_t \\mid x_{<t})\\right) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: It adds a second free signal -- the model's internal confidence ordering over its own spans -- without any extra forward pass.\n6. Blend the +1/-1 contrast (here, the +1/-1 marks meaning a phase helped or hurt the answer) and the standardized self-confidence with weights $\\beta 1=1.0$ and $\\beta 2=0.3,$ then pass the blended per-phase values through a softmax over the phases (a softmax turns a list of numbers into positive fractions that add up to 1). This gives a credit-density d that sums to 1 across the phases. The bigger weight on the contrast means the right-versus-wrong evidence counts for more than the model's own confidence. If a group had no contrast marks, the density just comes from the self-confidence; if there is no signal at all (a one-phase answer), the density spreads evenly across phases, which is the same as the original uniform spreading. This single number per phase is the one shared quantity both halves of the method depend on — how much of the answer's credit each phase deserves.\n\n*Per-phase credit-density: a softmax over phases of the contrast plus the self-score $(\\beta 1=1.0, \\beta 2=0.3$ bridge the unit mismatch), giving the fraction of the rollout's credit each phase should bear.*\n$$ d_{g,s} = \\operatorname{softmax}_s\\!\\big(\\beta_1\\,\\text{contrast}_{g,s} + \\beta_2\\,r^{\\text{self}}_{g,s}\\big),\\quad \\sum_s d_{g,s} = 1 \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This single number per phase is the one shared quantity both halves of the method depend on -- how much of the answer's credit each phase deserves.\n\n### Credit-Conserving Stratified Advantage (Leg A)\n*Replace the uniform advantage broadcast with a phase-stratified, unbiased-in-expectation advantage that concentrates credit on the pivotal minority.*\n\n7. In the training loss, replace the single uniform score with a per-phase score: every token in phase s now gets $A_{g,s}=A_{g}*(S_{g}*d_{g,s}),$ where $S_{g}$ is the number of phases. The $S_{g}$ factor guarantees the per-phase scores still average back to the original $A_{g},$ so you neither invent nor destroy total credit — you only move it onto the phases that earned more credit-density. Leave the rest of the GRPO update (the probability-ratio term and its clipping) exactly as it was, and average the per-token losses the same way the baseline does. The effect is that the update pushes harder on the decisive phases and barely on the distractor-scanning bulk, while staying faithful to the original objective. The output is a per-token score list the same length as the answer, fed straight into the gradient step.\n\n*Phase-stratified advantage assigned to every token in phase s: the scalar $A_{g}$ rescaled by $S_{g}\\cdot d,$ with the $S_{g}$ credit-conservation normalizer making the redistribution unbiased in expectation over phases.*\n$$ A_{g,s} = A_g \\cdot (S_g \\, d_{g,s}),\\qquad \\mathbb{E}_s[A_{g,s}] = A_g \\tag{5} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Credit is moved onto the decisive phases without inventing or destroying any total credit, so the update stays faithful to the original objective while focusing the signal.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 阶段分层信用分配：面向长上下文推理 RL 的免验证器逐阶段优势（Phase-Stratified Credit）\n\n**方法名称.** Phase-Stratified GRPO (PS-GRPO)\n\n## 研究动机\n用户的研究方向是用强化学习（RL）教大语言模型在超长文档上做多步推理。当前最强的方法 LoongRL 靠把训练数据做难来取得效果——它把真正的问题藏在一长串虚构的键值码链和大量干扰文本里，再用现成的 GRPO（Group Relative Policy Optimization）算法训练。GRPO 对整条答案（一条长达 16K 到 128K token、包含 plan/retrieve/reason/recheck 的链）只给一个分数，然后把这个分数平均地施加到每一个 token 上。\n\n核心问题是：这条超长链里真正决定对错的只有少数几步——模型追踪键链、给事实落地的那几步——而绝大多数 token 只是在扫描干扰文本。由于这一个分数被平均摊到所有 token 上，那几个关键步骤上的学习信号被稀释了。文档越长（趋向 128K），稀释越严重：关键步骤始终只占一小撮近乎固定数量的 token，而填充内容不断增长，所以每个关键 token 上的有效信号大约以 $1/T_{g}$ 的速度衰减。方法恰好在它本应擅长的长上下文区间崩溃。\n\n现在正是时机，因为 LoongRL（arXiv 2025-10）是第一个能产出足够长、足够有结构的推理链、让这个问题真正显现的方法；同时近期一批工作（如 CoVRL，Coupled Variational RL，arXiv 2025-12）已经证明可以在没有任何外部评判器的情况下构造有用的奖励信号。关键的新洞见是：GRPO 本来就会采样一整组尝试——有对有错——而它们之间的对比本身就免费地告诉你是哪一步造成了差别。\n\n先前工作各有止步的具体原因。LoongRL 从不回头利用它自己制造出的阶段结构来分配信用，它的全部新意都在数据上；KRPO（Kalman 滤波版 GRPO）只是把那个逐答案的单一分数算得更干净，从不把它拆成阶段；GDRO（Group Distributionally Robust Optimization）只决定训练哪些题，不管一条答案内部信用落在哪；CoVRL 改了奖励的来源，但仍把整条链当作一个单元打分。一旦补上这个缺口，长上下文推理就不再被信号稀释所限，同样的数据和算力就能在 128K 上训练得更深，而 LoongRL 发现的阶段结构也从被动副产品变成主动的训练杠杆。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景\n*未改动的 GRPO 长上下文基座，以及框定贡献的长度缩放评测。*\n\n1. 先搭一个最强的朴素基线。选一个已支持 128,000-token 上下文、参数量在 70-80 亿区间的开源大语言模型（例如 Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct），用标准的组相对策略优化(Group Relative Policy Optimization, GRPO)算法在 16,000-token 的 KeyChain 训练数据上训练。奖励用简单的对/错二元判定：把正确答案文本经过小写化、压缩空格与标点后，若它作为子串出现在模型最终答案段中就记 1 分，否则记 0 分。GRPO 对每道题采样一组 16 个尝试，把每个尝试的奖励折算成一个组归一化数值 $A_{g}$，再把这一个数值平摊到该尝试的每一个 token 上。对每个尝试都记录其奖励、$A_{g}$、长度以及逐 token 分数，并记录一直测到 128,000-token 的准确率；这条曲线是后续一切比较的参照。\n\n*GRPO 的组归一化标量优势：用 rollout 奖励 $R_{g}$ 减去组均值 $\\bar{R}_{q}$ 再除以组标准差 $\\sigma _{q}$；基线中该标量被均匀广播到全部 $T_{g}$ 个 token。*\n$$ A_g = \\frac{R_g - \\bar{R}_q}{\\sigma_q} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 你需要在相同算力下有一个最强的朴素基线，这样任何增益才能归因于信用重分配，而非额外训练。\n2. 在相同数据、与基线相同的更新步数下训练阶段分层版本，然后在 16,000 / 32,000 / 64,000 / 128,000 token 上用 RULER 与一套扩展的多跳问答(HotpotQA、MuSiQue、2WikiMultiHopQA)测试两个模型，报告每个长度下的准确率。同时测量信用的集中程度：对每条答案，把信用密度最高、其密度累计首次达到总量一半的那一小撮阶段称为「决定性」阶段，再计算 C——即落在这些决定性阶段上的总信用幅度占比，并在每个长度下对所有训练答案取 C 的均值。这直接检验核心主张：准确率优势应随长度增长，而 C 恰好命名了方法本应移动的那个量。\n   - _为什么_: 它直接检验核心主张：优势应随长度增长，而 C 恰好命名了方法本应移动的那个量。\n\n### 免验证器逐阶段信号（Leg B）\n*从组内正确/错误排序与策略自身置信度中制造可信的逐阶段信用密度，无需外部评判器、无需额外前向。*\n\n3. 加一个简单的、基于规则的切分器，把每条生成答案切成 plan(规划)、retrieve(检索)、reason(推理)、recheck(复核) 四类阶段。它对答案扫描一遍，每遇到一个约定好的边界标记就开启一个新阶段，并给该片段打上四类阶段中对应的类型标签；若某条答案完全没有标记，则回退为把答案切成固定 512-token 的块，每块当作一个阶段。你需要决定到底什么算边界标记【作者需决定：用哪些表层 token 来界定一个阶段——是模型被训练显式输出的区段标签、一份固定的自然语言提示短语清单，还是一个小型可学习的边界检测器】。输出是每个 token 属于第几个阶段以及该阶段的类型，从而得到该答案的 $S_{g}$ 个阶段。阶段来自模型自身可观察的结构，因此你没有引入一个可能被钻空子、还得另行训练的新学习评分器。\n   - _为什么_: 阶段来自模型自身可观察的结构，所以你没有引入一个可能被钻空子、还得另行训练的新学习评分器。\n4. 在某道题的 16 个尝试这一组内，拿一个正确尝试与一个错误尝试作比较。两个尝试若其阶段类型(plan/retrieve/reason/recheck...)的有序列表从头开始一致，就算共享一段阶段前缀；这里只比较阶段类型标签，不比对具体词句。对每个正确尝试，挑出与它匹配阶段前缀最长的那个错误尝试（同分时取尝试编号最小者以保证可复现），从错误尝试一侧也对称地这样做。两者首次分叉的那个阶段就是决定性分歧点：在正确尝试上记 +1、在错误尝试上记 -1，其余阶段都记 0。若某个尝试被配对了多次，就把它在各次配对中的 +1/-1 标记相加。如果某组恰好没有正确尝试或没有错误尝试，则无法构造对比，该组所有阶段一律记 0。一个对的尝试和一个错的尝试分道扬镳的地方，正是决定性步骤所在，而这组采样已经免费告诉了你这一点。\n\n*组内最小对比信号：共享最长相同阶段前缀的正确 rollout g+ 与错误 rollout g- 在阶段 s 处首次分叉，对 g+ 记 +1、对 g- 记 -1，从二元终局奖励已认证的排序中无偿采集信号。*\n$$ \\text{contrast}_{g^+,s} = +1,\\quad \\text{contrast}_{g^-,s} = -1 \\;\\;\\text{at the first phase } s \\text{ where } g^+ \\text{ and } g^- \\text{ diverge} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 一个对的尝试和一个错的尝试分道扬镳的地方，正是决定性步骤所在，而这组采样已经免费告诉了你这一点。\n5. 对每个阶段，取模型自身的平均词置信度——即模型赋给该阶段内各 token 的平均 log-prob——并复用生成答案时已经算出的置信度，因此不需要任何额外前向。然后把这些阶段平均值在该条答案的各阶段间做标准化：减去该答案的阶段间均值，再除以阶段间的离散度（在离散度上加一个极小的 1e-6 以避免除零）。若某条答案只有一个阶段，就没有可比较的离散度，把它的自评分设为 0。结果是每个阶段一个标准化后的置信度数值。它免费增加了第二路信号——模型对自身片段的内部置信排序。\n\n*自评分：当前策略对阶段 s 内 token 的平均 log-prob，在 g 的 $S_{g}$ 个阶段间做 z 归一化，刻画策略对自身片段的内部置信排序，且不需额外前向。*\n$$ r^{\\text{self}}_{g,s} = \\operatorname{z-norm}_s\\!\\left(\\frac{1}{|s|}\\sum_{t \\in s} \\log \\pi_\\theta(x_t \\mid x_{<t})\\right) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 它免费增加了第二路信号——模型对自身片段的内部置信排序——且无需任何额外前向。\n6. 用权重 $\\beta 1=1.0$ 和 $\\beta 2=0.3$ 把 +1/-1 对比项（这里的 +1/-1 标记表示某阶段帮到或拖累了答案）与标准化自评分混合，再把混合后的逐阶段数值在阶段维做 softmax(softmax 把一串数字变成相加为 1 的正分数)，得到一个在各阶段上加和为 1 的信用密度 d。对比项的权重更大，意味着对/错证据比模型自身的置信度更重要。若某组没有对比标记，密度就只来自自评分；若完全没有信号（单阶段答案），密度就在各阶段间均匀分布，这与原来的均匀平摊一致。每阶段这一个数就是方法两半都依赖的唯一共享量——每个阶段应得多少信用。\n\n*逐阶段信用密度：对 contrast 与 self-score 的加权和（$\\beta 1=1.0$、$\\beta 2=0.3$ 用以弥合量纲差异）在阶段维做 softmax，得到每个阶段应承担的信用占比。*\n$$ d_{g,s} = \\operatorname{softmax}_s\\!\\big(\\beta_1\\,\\text{contrast}_{g,s} + \\beta_2\\,r^{\\text{self}}_{g,s}\\big),\\quad \\sum_s d_{g,s} = 1 \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 每阶段这一个数就是方法两半都依赖的唯一共享量——每个阶段应得多少信用。\n\n### 信用守恒的分层优势（Leg A）\n*用阶段分层、期望无偏的优势取代均匀广播，把信用集中到关键少数阶段。*\n\n7. 在训练损失里，把单一的均匀分数替换成逐阶段分数：阶段 s 内的每个 token 现在得到 $A_{g,s}=A_{g}*(S_{g}*d_{g,s})$，其中 $S_{g}$ 是阶段数。$S_{g}$ 因子保证各阶段分数仍平均回原来的 $A_{g}$，所以你既不凭空制造也不销毁任何总信用——只是把它搬到信用密度更高的阶段上。GRPO 更新的其余部分（概率比项及其裁剪）原封不动，逐 token 损失的平均方式也与基线一致。效果是更新在决定性阶段上发力更猛、在扫描干扰文本的大头上几乎不发力，同时仍忠于原目标。输出是一份与答案等长的逐 token 分数列表，直接送入梯度步。\n\n*阶段分层优势，赋给阶段 s 内每个 token：标量 $A_{g}$ 乘以 $S_{g}\\cdot d$，其中 $S_{g}$ 是信用守恒归一化因子，使重分配在阶段期望上保持无偏。*\n$$ A_{g,s} = A_g \\cdot (S_g \\, d_{g,s}),\\qquad \\mathbb{E}_s[A_{g,s}] = A_g \\tag{5} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 信用被搬到决定性阶段上，却没有凭空制造或销毁任何总信用，所以更新在聚焦信号的同时仍忠于原目标。\n\n"},{"id":"74","run_dir":"run_prompt74_mcsearch","index":74,"title":"Minimal-Pair Step Preferences for Search-Control in Multimodal Agents","title_zh":"面向多模态智能体搜索控制的最小对步级偏好优化","method_name":"Minimal-Pair Step Preference (MPSP)","hook":"When two multimodal-search rollouts reach the same correct answer, outcome-reward RL gives them identical credit — yet one disciplined-interleaving trajectory and one redundant-retrieval trajectory differ at exactly one search-control decision, and mining that single differing step as an online preference pair supervises whether/what/which-modality/when-to-stop directly. We predict that re-granularizing the unit of credit from the whole trajectory to the per-decision step corrects over/under-retrieval and modality-misalignment while leaving answer-accuracy reward untouched.","anchor_pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","anchor_pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","domain_category":"LLM Agents & Tool Use","patterns":[{"gap":"ADDITIVE: No retrieved frontier leaf produces a per-decision quality signal for the agent's own search-control actions (whether to retrieve, what to query, which modality to route to, when to stop) — the outcome that is missing is a policy whose individual retrieval/routing steps are each shaped toward being warranted, so that a trajectory reaching the right answer through redundant or modality-misaligned retrieval is distinguished from one that reached it through disciplined interleaving, rathe","pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","sub_pattern":"C26 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by manufacturing a step-typed comparative reward — minimal-pair preferences mined online from the agent's own group rollouts that share a correct-answer prefix but diverge at exactly one search-control decision — and optimizing the policy against that ordering with a step-level preference (DPO-style) objective bolted onto the existing GRPO outcome reward, so each retrieve/query/route/stop decision receives a localized gradient.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"SUBTRACTIVE: No retrieved paper tests whether collapsing an entire heterogeneous interleaved trajectory into a single terminal reward is the right granularity at which to supervise a multimodal search policy at all — every frontier leaf silently inherits the outcome-reward-over-the-whole-trajectory assumption from the shared GRPO/policy-gradient-with-terminal-reward ancestor and only varies the reward's scale (BN-GSPO), failure-masking (fatal-aware GRPO), data (cold-start/synthetic trajectories)","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","how_closed":"Framing half (C01): relocates the credit-enforcement locus from the whole-trajectory terminal scalar to the per-decision step, naming trajectory-as-unit-of-credit as the load-bearing assumption every leaf inherits and pivoting it by violating it. Companion deliverable (controlled_diagnostic_design): ships a confound-isolating separation that holds final-answer accuracy fixed and varies only the supervision granularity (terminal-only vs per-decision preference), measuring whether process metrics (retrieval count, modality-routing accuracy, premature-stop rate) improve under the relocated locus — the empirical artifact the audit alone cannot ship for a method paper.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"multimodal agentic search (vision-language deep-search / multimodal RAG agents that interleave reasoning, image manipulation, and web retrieval)","n_papers":52,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":27},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10},{"source":"openreview","n":2}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":13,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Agent S: An Open Agentic Framework that Uses Computers Like a Human"},{"source":"openalex","title":"A Learnable Agent Collaboration Network Framework for Personalized Multimodal AI Search Engine"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Present and Future of Pharmacological Management for Acute Moderate-to-Severe Postoperative, Traumatic, or Musculoskeletal Pain in Europe: A Narrative Review"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Effectiveness of nonpharmacological conservative therapies for chronic pelvic pain in women: a systematic review and meta-analysis"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Adaptive dimensional search-based orthogonal experimentation SSA (ADOX-SSA) for training RBF neural network and optimal feature selection"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Chaotic Artificial Algae Algorithm for Solving Global Optimization With Real-World Space Trajectory Design Problems"}],"more":7},{"year":2025,"n":27,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"SenseNova-MARS: Empowering Multimodal Agentic Reasoning and Search via Reinforcement Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"CollEX - A Multimodal Agentic RAG System Enabling Interactive Exploration of Scientific Collections"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Patho-AgenticRAG: Towards Multimodal Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation for Pathology VLMs via Reinforcement Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"DeepEyesV2: Toward Agentic Multimodal Model"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Skywork-R1V4: Toward Agentic Multimodal Intelligence through Interleaved Thinking with Images and DeepResearch"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"RAVEN: An Agentic Framework for Multimodal Entity Discovery from Large-Scale Video Collections"}],"more":21},{"year":2026,"n":12,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"},{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"A Case-Driven Multi-Agent Framework for E-Commerce Search Relevance"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Securing the Agent: Vendor-Neutral, Multitenant Enterprise Retrieval and Tool Use"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"InterLV-Search: Benchmarking Interleaved Multimodal Agentic Search"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"MM-DeepResearch: A Simple and Effective Multimodal Agentic Search Baseline"}],"more":6}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":6,"share":0.115},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate; adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"decompose_and_delegate; adapt_via_conditioning","count":3,"share":0.058},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate; unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"decompose_and_delegate; unify_into_shared_representation","count":3,"share":0.058},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering; decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"self_supervised_signal_engineering; decompose_and_delegate","count":3,"share":0.058},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate; self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"decompose_and_delegate; self_supervised_signal_engineering","count":2,"share":0.038},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":2,"share":0.038},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":2,"share":0.038},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation; decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"unify_into_shared_representation; decompose_and_delegate","count":1,"share":0.019}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"The dominant recipe for multimodal search agents trains a VLM with GRPO/GSPO-family RL (optionally after cold-start SFT on synthetic trajectories) against a trajectory-terminal reward — final-answer correctness — so the only learning signal the agent receives about its multi-turn search behavior is a single scalar collapsed over an entire interleaved trajectory of text-search, image-search, crop, and reasoning steps (semanticscholar:c81f11a703d71d652d806d165de51e21528bda4b; semanticscholar:d9edfb304df6db53761fd876fa27c76236df9a3b; arxiv:2604.14029v1; arxiv:2605.05185v1). Because that scalar cannot attribute credit to which step decided whether/what/which-modality to query, it provides no gradient that distinguishes a trajectory that reached the right answer through disciplined, evidence-conditioned interleaving from one that reached it through redundant retrieval, premature stopping, or modality-misaligned planning; the diagnostic benchmarks make the consequence explicit — the best agents stay below ~50% on genuinely interleaved search where visual evidence must condition later queries, and show systematic over/under-retrieval and modality-misaligned planning that an answer-only metric leaves invisible (arxiv:2605.07510v1; arxiv:2603.00873v1). The structural failure is that an outcome-only objective over a long heterogeneous trajectory cannot produce the per-decision search-control signal the task requires, so the agent's retrieval-and-routing policy is under-specified regardless of how the visual context is engineered or how many trajectories are synthesized.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:c81f11a703d71d652d806d165de51e21528bda4b","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"SenseNova-MARS adds an image-crop tool to text+image search and trains the interleaved reasoning-and-tool policy with a two-stage cold-start-SFT then Batch-normalized GSPO (BN-GSPO) recipe, where BN normalizes only the reward magnitude/variance across diverse trajectory structures but the supervision remains a single sequence-level outcome reward per trajectory. Its residue is that the normalization fixes reward-scale heterogeneity, not credit attribution: no per-step signal tells the policy which of its search/crop/route decisions was responsible, so disciplined-interleaving behavior is never directly reinforced — exactly the interleaved search-control failure InterLV-Search measures."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:d9edfb304df6db53761fd876fa27c76236df9a3b","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"DeepEyesV2 unifies code-execution and web-retrieval as interleavable tools in one reasoning loop and uses a cold-start stage plus RL to make tool invocation reliable, after pioneer experiments show direct RL alone cannot induce robust tool use. It still optimizes terminal answer correctness, so 'reliable tool use' is taught by curating cold-start data rather than by a process-level objective — it does not produce a learning signal that scores whether each individual retrieval/route decision was warranted, leaving over- and under-retrieval uncorrected."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2605.05185v1","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"OpenSearch-VL is an open recipe whose multi-turn fatal-aware GRPO masks post-failure tokens and one-sided-clamps advantages to handle cascading tool failures, the closest the frontier comes to shaping the trajectory beyond a terminal scalar. But it only handles the failure case (masking after a fatal tool error); on successful trajectories the credit is still the single outcome reward, so the routine over/under-retrieval and modality-misaligned planning on non-failing trajectories receive no corrective gradient."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2604.12890v2","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Towards Long-horizon Agentic Multimodal Search (LMM-Searcher) attacks context explosion by offloading visual assets to an external file system referenced by UIDs and adding a fetch-image tool for on-demand active perception. It treats the bottleneck as context/token management so the agent can run longer, but it does not change the training signal that decides when to fetch or which modality to query — it makes long trajectories affordable without making the per-step search-control policy any better specified."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2603.00873v1","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"MC-Search annotates step-wise reasoning chains (sub-questions, retrieval modality, supporting facts, intermediate answers) and proposes Search-Align, process-supervised SFT on verified chains that improves planning and retrieval fidelity. The residue is that the process supervision is imitative SFT on a fixed verified-chain dataset, not a process-level objective the agent optimizes under its own evolving policy, so it does not give an online search-control signal and its gains are bounded by the coverage of the annotated chains."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"multimodal agentic search (vision-language deep-search / multimodal RAG agents that interleave reasoning, image manipulation, and web retrieval)","venue":"ML/NLP/CV top venue (NeurIPS / ICLR / ICML / CVPR)","time":"2026","data":["InterLV-Search (interleaved language-vision agentic search, 2061 examples, 3 levels)","MC-Search (agentic MM-RAG, 3333 examples, step-wise annotated reasoning chains, ~3.7 hops)","MMSearch / HR-MMSearch / FVQA (search-oriented multimodal QA)","V*Bench / HR-Bench (high-resolution visual perception)","TIR-Bench / Video-BrowseComp (agentic thinking-with-images / open-web video research)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day budget)","expertise":"ML researcher comfortable with VLM post-training (SFT + RL/GRPO-family) and agent/tool-use frameworks","preference":"empirical","baseline":"GRPO/GSPO-family RL post-training of a general VLM on multimodal search trajectories with outcome (final-answer) reward, optionally cold-start SFT on synthetic trajectories (MARS, DeepEyesV2, MM-DeepResearch, OpenSearch-VL, POINTS-Seeker)","limitation":"current multimodal search agents do not reliably control the search process itself — they over/under-retrieve, mis-route which modality to query, and lose visual evidence across long interleaved trajectories — even when final-answer accuracy is optimized","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["domain","venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object both legs read from and write to is the per-decision search-control preference unit: an ordered pair (s_win, s_lose) of two single search-control decisions (each decision is one of {retrieve?, query-text, query-image/crop, route-to-modality, stop}) taken from two rollouts in the same GRPO sampling group that share an identical correct-answer outcome and an identical token prefix up to a common branch point, and that differ at exactly that one decision. The win/lose label on the pair is manufactured online, with no human or external annotation, from three model-internal/computable readouts combined as r_step = a*Delta_acc + b*(-redundancy) + c*evidence_gain: (1) Delta_acc in {-1,0,+1} is the difference in eventual answer correctness of the two sibling rollouts that branch only at this decision (computable from the group's verifiable outcome reward already used by GRPO); (2) redundancy in [0,1] is the max cosine similarity between this step's retrieved item embedding and any previously retrieved item in the same trajectory, computed from the policy VLM's own pooled last-layer embedding of each retrieved item (model-internal readout, no external model); (3) evidence_gain in [0,1] is the increase in the policy's own answer-token confidence (softmax probability of the gold-or-self-consistent answer span) after this step's retrieved evidence is appended versus before, a model-internal readout. The weights a,b,c are named scalar hyperparameters (defaults a=1.0, b=0.3, c=0.3, fixed across the run; b,c only break ties when Delta_acc=0 so equal-outcome pairs still get a per-decision sign). For the ANCHOR leg (C26), the policy is optimized against these orderings with a step-level DPO loss L_step = -log sigma(beta*(logp(s_win)-logp(s_lose))), where logp is the policy log-prob of the differing decision span conditioned on the shared prefix and beta=0.1; L_step is added to the unchanged GRPO outcome objective as L = L_GRPO + lambda*L_step (lambda=0.5), so answer-correctness reward is preserved and the per-decision signal only re-weights how warranted each search-control move is — this is the runnable method artifact and ships the contribution_type=method deliverable. For the SUBTRACTIVE audit leg, the SAME pair object is the lens: C01's relocation says the enforcement locus is the step, not the trajectory, and the companion controlled_diagnostic_design instruments it by running the identical policy/data/compute with lambda=0 (terminal-only, the inherited locus) versus lambda=0.5 (relocated locus) and reporting the divergence in process metrics at matched final-answer accuracy. Because both legs are built from the one minimal-pair object — the anchor optimizes it, the audit measures what changes when it is switched on — a reviewer reads one paper: the audit's claim (granularity is the wrong locus) is exactly what the anchor's mechanism realizes and the diagnostic confirms. The mechanism does NOT introduce a learned value critic (n1), a separately trained process-reward model (c1), a hand-designed potential function (c2), an options decomposition (c3), or offline imitation of annotated chains (c4): all preference labels are mined from the agent's own evolving group rollouts during RL, satisfying the online-per-decision constraint the lineage flag requires.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules: the anchor's deliverable (a per-decision optimization signal) and the audit's claim (trajectory-as-unit is the wrong granularity) are two faces of the same minimal-pair object — evidence that they interlock is that switching lambda from 0 to 0.5 is simultaneously the audit's controlled intervention and the anchor's training switch, so one object serves both, which is why they are one paper not two. (b) Alternatives rejected: (i) a standalone learned process-reward model scoring every step — rejected because it regresses to c1 (generic PRM) and to n1 (a critic), and the lineage flag forbids it; (ii) potential-based dense reward over retrieved-evidence overlap — rejected as a regression to c2 (requires a hand-designed potential) and tautological with the redundancy term; (iii) mining preferences only across whole trajectories (group-relative answer reward, i.e. plain GRPO) — rejected because it cannot localize which decision differed, the exact failure the gap names. The minimal-pair construction (shared prefix, single differing decision) is the load-bearing choice that isolates one decision's credit; avoided nodes recorded: n1, c1, c2, c3, c4.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: post-train one 7B VLM policy with the combined objective (lambda=0.5) and an identical-everything baseline with lambda=0 (terminal-only) on the MC-Search + InterLV-Search training splits under the same ~90 A100-day budget, then evaluate on the InterLV-Search and MC-Search test sets. If the candidate works, at statistically matched final-answer accuracy the lambda=0.5 policy shows lower mean retrieval count per solved query, higher modality-routing accuracy, and lower premature-stop rate, and its InterLV-Search interleaved-search score rises above the ~50% ceiling current agents sit at (arxiv:2605.07510v1); final-answer accuracy itself need not rise, which is the non-obvious split. The single named load-bearing variable is r_step (the per-decision preference signal); the negative control permutes the win/lose labels within each minimal pair so r_step's sign is randomized while its magnitude and the L_step term's compute are held identical. Anti-tautology guard: the control's predicted effect is on the DOWNSTREAM task-outcome metrics that define the mechanism's value — under permuted r_step the process metrics (retrieval count, modality-routing accuracy, premature-stop rate) must collapse back to the terminal-only (lambda=0) baseline rather than merely r_step changing value, proving the gain comes from the credit's correctness and not from extra optimization or the added loss magnitude. A positive control — training with ONLY L_step on the minimal pairs (lambda large, GRPO outcome term down-weighted) — should recover most of the process-metric improvement, converting the falsifier into a constructive identification that the per-decision signal alone drives disciplined interleaving.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:c81f11a703d71d652d806d165de51e21528bda4b","delta":"SenseNova-MARS's BN-GSPO batch-normalizes the magnitude/variance of a single sequence-level outcome reward across trajectory structures; we construct a step-typed preference unit (minimal pairs differing at one search-control decision, same outcome) and optimize it — a per-decision credit signal their normalization, which never localizes credit below the trajectory, does not produce."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2605.05185v1","delta":"OpenSearch-VL's fatal-aware GRPO shapes the trajectory only on failure (masking post-fatal-error tokens, one-sided advantage clamp); we shape successful trajectories too, supplying a corrective gradient to the routine over/under-retrieval and modality-misalignment that occur on non-failing rollouts and that fatal-aware masking leaves untouched."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2603.00873v1","delta":"MC-Search's Search-Align is offline process-supervised SFT imitating a fixed verified-chain dataset; we mine preference pairs online from the agent's own evolving group rollouts so the per-decision signal is an objective optimized under the current policy rather than imitation bounded by annotation coverage."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:d9edfb304df6db53761fd876fa27c76236df9a3b","delta":"DeepEyesV2 installs reliable tool use by curating cold-start data then outcome RL; we install it as a per-decision preference objective the agent optimizes, testing whether the behavior can arise from the objective rather than from curated demonstrations."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2604.12890v2","delta":"LMM-Searcher makes long trajectories affordable via file-based visual offload but leaves the signal deciding when/what/which-modality to fetch unchanged; we change that very signal, supplying the per-decision search-control gradient its context management does not provide."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"arxiv:2605.05185v1","what_step_was_missed":"OpenSearch-VL constructed trajectory shaping only for the fatal-failure case — it masks tokens after a fatal tool error and one-sided-clamps the advantage, so its only sub-trajectory credit primitive is a post-failure mask. To reach our contribution it would have needed to construct a within-group minimal-pair comparison over same-outcome successful trajectories that isolates one differing search-control decision and converts it into a step-level preference gradient; that branch-aligned same-outcome pair object, which assigns credit on non-failing trajectories, is the construction it never built."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":292,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"Layer-1 hard floor did NOT fire: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict is 'triggered' but the carrying lesson (C01 'Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work... collapses the novelty boundary UNLESS the difference is made explicit and measured') is conditional and curable by editing differentiation_from_lit and the audit framing, not a fatal Reject-shape; anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null; and paper_pointed_threat is NOT exact-mechanism overlap (iStar/StepOPSD/CSO use learned PRMs or critical-step search, while the candidate mines label-free same-outcome minimal pairs typed by search-control function), so it is addressable_via a named candidate field. Per the heuristics, revise is mandated because a load-bearing structural property is hit: the audit leg's central claim ('trajectory-as-unit-of-credit is never questioned') is empirically false against collision_hits, and paper_pointed_threat.addressable_via names specific candidate fields (differentiation_from_lit, hook, the C01 gap framing). recipe_application_check is borderline (C26 applied cleanly; C01's relocate-locus move is mechanically present but its unexploited-locus precondition is contradicted).","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"ADDITIVE: No retrieved frontier leaf produces a per-decision quality signal for the agent's own search-control actions (whether to retrieve, what to query, which modality to route to, when to stop) — the outcome that is missing is a policy whose individual retrieval/routing steps are each shaped toward being warranted, so that a trajectory reaching the right answer through redundant or modality-misaligned retrieval is distinguished from one that reached it through disciplined interleaving, rather than both receiving identical credit (arxiv:2605.07510v1, arxiv:2603.00873v1 measure exactly this gap; no solver closes it).","main_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","sub_pattern":"C26 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The dominant failure is the single-component swap: the paper takes the established preference pipeline (reward model -> contrastive optimization) and changes exactly one slot — human labels to an AI judge, offline data to online sampling, response-level to step-level granularity — then presents that swap as the contribution. A candidate author should self-check: does the manufactured-preference move come bundled with a reformulation that removes an approximation, a demonstrated capability previously assumed impossible, or a newly-surfaced failure axis — or is it just relabeling one box in the standard diagram?","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Swapping the preference-label source (human -> AI judge, offline -> online) without showing the swap unlocks a behavior previously unreachable reads as a one-component substitution and draws novelty rejections.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"core_mechanism does swap offline-annotated chains -> online same-group mined pairs (the explicit delta vs MC-Search Search-Align), but falsification_prediction bundles a concrete unlock (the answer-accuracy-flat-while-process-metrics-improve split with a permuted-label negative control), so it is not a bare source swap yet rests on a single swapped slot."},{"lesson_quoted":"Changing only the granularity of an established contrastive objective (response-level -> step-level) is judged incremental unless paired with a clearly demonstrated practical unlock.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The headline move IS re-granularizing DPO from trajectory to per-decision step; the 'unless' clause is partially satisfied by the matched-accuracy process-metric separation + positive/negative controls, but the unlock is the very thing prior step-level-credit work (iStar, StepOPSD) already claims, so the practical-unlock defense is weaker than the card requires."},{"lesson_quoted":"Stopping at the preference dataset, benchmark, or reward model without demonstrating the downstream optimization it is meant to feed leaves the contribution looking like infrastructure rather than method.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism ships a runnable L = L_GRPO + lambda*L_step objective and a full RL training loop (steps 1-9), so it does not stop at infrastructure."},{"lesson_quoted":"Borrowing a structurally related proxy domain to synthesize preference data, without validating that the proxy's regularities transfer to the target's end-goal metric, invites rigor and generalization concerns.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Pairs are mined in-distribution from the target policy's own group rollouts on the target MC-Search/InterLV-Search data, not a proxy domain."},{"lesson_quoted":"Combining off-the-shelf components (parameter-efficient adaptation plus self-distillation) for a known problem fails the novelty bar when concurrent work performs the same combination.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"step-level DPO + GRPO outcome reward in an online self-mined loop is exactly the combination concurrent work (iStar: trajectory-DPO implicit step rewards added to episode advantage; StepOPSD: step-as-unit online preference before GRPO) performs, so the off-the-shelf-combination concern is live."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"SUBTRACTIVE: No retrieved paper tests whether collapsing an entire heterogeneous interleaved trajectory into a single terminal reward is the right granularity at which to supervise a multimodal search policy at all — every frontier leaf silently inherits the outcome-reward-over-the-whole-trajectory assumption from the shared GRPO/policy-gradient-with-terminal-reward ancestor and only varies the reward's scale (BN-GSPO), failure-masking (fatal-aware GRPO), data (cold-start/synthetic trajectories), or context budget (file offload), never questioning the trajectory-as-the-unit-of-credit premise itself.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is a successful relocation that is demonstrated but not adversarially closed, or a novelty-boundary collapse where the 'new' locus turns out to be one a prior paper already used and the work fails to quantify what is genuinely different. A fourth is offering only a demonstration with no mechanistic account of why the locus carries the signal, which reads as a stacked pipeline of off-the-shelf parts.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work — normalization statistics, activation-similarity losses, semantic concept triggers — collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured.","candidate_match":"yes","reasoning":"The relocated locus 'the step, not the trajectory' as the unit of credit is exactly the locus iStar ('implicit step rewards... step-level advantages combined with trajectory-level advantages'), StepOPSD ('agent step as the unit of credit redistribution'), CSO, ProRAG and HPL already occupy; the candidate's differentiation_from_lit and collision set never name or measure the difference against these step-level-credit papers, so the audit's headline (trajectory-as-unit-of-credit is never questioned) is factually defeated by retrieved work."},{"lesson_quoted":"Demonstrating the new locus only on fixed, non-adaptive or outdated baselines while omitting any account of why it works reads as a stacked pipeline of existing components rather than a principled shift.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The diagnostic varies lambda 0 vs 0.5 with a permuted-label control and gives a mechanistic r_step decomposition for why the step carries signal, so the why-account and a same-everything control are present."},{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a relocated signal is 'stealthier' or 'harder to remove' without defeating an adaptive defender who searches the same new locus leaves the central claim unverified.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Security/adversarial framing does not apply; this is an RL-credit relocation, not an attack/defense locus."},{"lesson_quoted":"Wiring off-the-shelf generators or tools into a new attack setting without a structural reason for the locus change gets judged as engineering integration, not insight.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The structural reason (minimal-pair isolates one decision's credit) is stated, but applying a known step-level-credit machinery to the multimodal-search setting risks reading as setting transfer unless the same-outcome-minimal-pair construction is shown distinct from the PRM/implicit-reward machinery the prior work uses."}],"verdict":"triggered"}],"verdict":"triggered","reasoning":"The SUBTRACTIVE / assumption_audit_and_pivot (C01) entry is triggered: its load-bearing audit claim is that trajectory-as-unit-of-credit is a premise 'every frontier leaf silently inherits' and 'no retrieved paper tests' relocating it — but the relocated locus (the step as the unit of credit) is already exploited by published work (iStar, StepOPSD, CSO, ProRAG, HPL), matching the C01 reject lesson 'Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work... collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured' as candidate_match=yes. The ADDITIVE / C26 entry is borderline on the granularity-swap and off-the-shelf-combination lessons. NOTE: these step-level-credit papers were absent from the Phase 0 lit_table (which was scoped to multimodal-agentic-search) and surfaced only via collision retrieval, so the candidate's framing was honest against its evidence base but is now empirically over-claimed."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"ADDITIVE: No retrieved frontier leaf produces a per-decision quality signal for the agent's own search-control actions...","sub_pattern":"C26 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Manufacture a comparative/scalar reward from a non-human source then optimize the target against it with a contrastive/preference objective rather than label-fitting; recurring moves are to extract preference pairs from structures that already encode an ordering, re-granularize the comparison to match where credit assignment fails, and construct each pair to differ minimally — ideally at exactly one faulty transition sharing an otherwise-correct prefix.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism Step 2 + the (s_win,s_lose) construction perform the signature move precisely: minimal pairs are mined from two same-group rollouts that share an identical correct-answer outcome and identical token prefix and differ at exactly one search-control decision, then optimized with a step-level DPO loss L_step = -log sigma(beta*(logp(s_win)-logp(s_lose))). This is the C26 'construct each pair to differ minimally at exactly one transition sharing an otherwise-correct prefix' move verbatim, not the parent pattern's generic 'make up a signal'.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"SUBTRACTIVE: No retrieved paper tests whether collapsing an entire heterogeneous interleaved trajectory into a single terminal reward is the right granularity...","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Name the single representational locus current attacks/defenses operate on, relocate the property to an alternative locus the field treated as irrelevant/invariant, build the mechanism at the new locus, and supply a mechanistic account of WHY the new locus carries the signal — an invariance proof, impossibility bound, or root-cause decomposition — not merely evidence THAT it does.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism enacts the relocation move (credit-enforcement locus from whole-trajectory terminal scalar to the per-decision step) and instruments it via the lambda=0 vs 0.5 switch, with the r_step = a*Delta_acc + b*(-redundancy) + c*evidence_gain decomposition serving as the why-account. The relocation and the why are present, so the C01 move is performed; however the cluster's 'locus the field treated as irrelevant/invariant' premise is undermined because the step-locus is NOT field-overlooked here (multiple retrieved papers already supervise at it) — the tactic is applied but its load-bearing precondition (an unexploited locus) is false.","verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The C26 entry is cleanly applied — the same-outcome minimal-pair-differing-at-one-decision construction is the exact C26 signature move. The C01 entry is borderline: the relocate-and-explain mechanics are performed, but C01's defining precondition (the new locus is one the field tacitly assumed irrelevant) is contradicted by collision evidence showing the step-as-credit-locus is already occupied, so the pivot is mechanically present but rhetorically overstated."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["self_supervised_signal_engineering","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; the candidate's composition is self_supervised_signal_engineering + assumption_audit_and_pivot, which contains no heterogeneous_decomposition, so no anti-pattern matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:2e3d2cb75be2d8939387f9173b68cd81315ec694","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"iStar (Agentic Reinforcement Learning with Implicit Step Rewards) directly attacks the same problem the candidate names — 'sparse and sometimes unverifiable rewards make it extremely challenging to assign credit when training LLM agents' — and delivers the same structural solution: it derives step-level rewards via a trajectory-based DPO objective, computes step-level advantages that are combined with trajectory(episode)-level advantages for policy updates in a self-reinforcing online loop, with no additional rollouts or explicit step labels, evaluated on agentic benchmarks including the visual VisualSokoban. This subsumes the candidate's central claim that 'no retrieved leaf produces a per-decision signal' and that 'trajectory-as-unit-of-credit is never questioned': iStar already relocates credit to the step online without labels and fuses it with the trajectory-level objective, exactly the candidate's L = L_GRPO + lambda*L_step architecture in spirit. The candidate's claim does NOT entirely fall, because iStar manufactures its signal through a learned implicit PRM trained by DPO — precisely the c1/n1 family the candidate's lineage flag forbids — whereas the candidate manufactures the signal label-free from same-outcome minimal-pair siblings (no learned reward model at all), and iStar is not multimodal-search-specific (no whether/what/which-modality/when-to-stop typing). The companion threats StepOPSD ('agent step as the unit of credit redistribution', online preference before GRPO, evaluated on Search-QA) and CSO (DPO on verified critical decision points where alternate actions flip the outcome) tighten the same vise: the step-as-credit-unit + preference-objective + online-mining combination is concurrent prior art, so the candidate's distance now rests entirely on the same-outcome-minimal-pair construction and the search-control decision typing rather than on the credit-relocation idea itself.","addressable_via":"Rewrite differentiation_from_lit (and the hook/audit framing) to add iStar/StepOPSD/CSO as the primary deltas — pivoting the contribution claim from 'no one relocates credit to the step / questions trajectory-as-unit' (false) to the genuinely unoccupied slot: a label-free, learned-reward-model-free credit signal mined from same-outcome minimal-pair siblings whose decisions are typed by search-control function (whether/what/which-modality/when-to-stop) — a candidate-field edit, since the same-outcome minimal-pair + multimodal-search typing in core_mechanism is not exact-mechanism overlap with the PRM-based prior art."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat (iStar semanticscholar:2e3d2cb75be2d8939387f9173b68cd81315ec694, StepOPSD semanticscholar:680d03d8403630e0092cb41b3b2af0d75ec183d6, CSO semanticscholar:c0f796cd67f11d637ebbd58cd36651dbf7339711) plus gap_closure_reject_check C01 lesson 'Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work... unless the difference is made explicit and measured'.","fix_direction":"Add explicit delta entries for iStar, StepOPSD, and CSO. For each, state the load-bearing distinction the candidate already owns: (1) the candidate manufactures the signal with NO learned reward/value model — pure same-outcome minimal-pair siblings — whereas iStar trains an implicit PRM via trajectory-DPO and CSO uses a PRM + expert-proposed alternatives; (2) the candidate's pairs are SAME-OUTCOME (both reach the correct answer) so the signal isolates process quality at matched accuracy, whereas iStar/CSO derive step credit from outcome-flipping or from a learned reward; (3) the decision unit is typed by search-control function (retrieve?/query-text/query-image-crop/route-modality/stop), which the text-agent prior art does not type. Measure these in the experiment table."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"hook","issue":"gap_closure_reject_check SUBTRACTIVE entry triggered: the audit headline 'trajectory-as-unit-of-credit is never questioned / no per-decision signal exists' is factually defeated by retrieved step-level-credit work, collapsing the novelty boundary (C01 reject lesson).","fix_direction":"Soften the audit claim from 'no one relocates credit below the trajectory' to the accurate unoccupied slot: step-level credit for agentic RL exists (iStar, StepOPSD) but is built from LEARNED reward/value models on text agents using outcome-flip or implicit-PRM signals; what is missing is a label-free, model-free per-decision signal mined from same-outcome minimal-pair siblings and typed by multimodal search-control function. Keep the answer-accuracy-flat-while-process-improves reveal as the testable hook."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"gap_closure","issue":"recipe_application_check C01 borderline + gap_closure_reject_check C01 triggered: the SUBTRACTIVE gap text asserts 'no retrieved paper tests... the trajectory-as-the-unit-of-credit premise itself', which the collision set contradicts; C01's unexploited-locus precondition is false as written.","fix_direction":"Revise the SUBTRACTIVE gap[1].gap and its how_closed to scope the audited assumption precisely: the premise still un-questioned in the MULTIMODAL-SEARCH lineage is not 'is the step a valid credit unit' (already tested generally) but 'must the step-level credit signal come from a learned reward/value model and outcome-flips, rather than from label-free same-outcome process contrasts'. This keeps C01 honest (a genuinely inherited, untested premise in-lineage) without claiming the broader step-credit locus is unexplored. Do NOT swap the sub_pattern — C01 remains correct once the audited assumption is re-scoped."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"gap_closure[1].gap (SUBTRACTIVE entry) and gap_closure[1].how_closed","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Re-scoped the audited assumption from the (now-false) 'trajectory-as-unit-of-credit is never questioned' to the genuinely-untested in-lineage premise — that the step-level credit signal MUST come from a learned reward/value model and outcome-flips rather than from label-free same-outcome process contrasts — keeping C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption) honest without claiming the step-credit locus is unexplored."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"hook","issue":"applied","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Softened the audit headline to acknowledge that learned-model step-level credit already exists (iStar/StepOPSD) and relocated the novelty to the label-free, model-free, same-outcome minimal-pair signal typed by multimodal search-control function, preserving the answer-accuracy-flat-while-process-improves reveal."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added explicit delta entries for iStar (semanticscholar:2e3d2cb75be2d8939387f9173b68cd81315ec694), StepOPSD (semanticscholar:680d03d8403630e0092cb41b3b2af0d75ec183d6), and CSO (semanticscholar:c0f796cd67f11d637ebbd58cd36651dbf7339711), each measuring the three load-bearing distinctions: no learned reward/value model, same-outcome (matched-accuracy) pairs, and search-control-function typing."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Minimal-Pair Step Preferences for Search-Control in Multimodal Agents\n\n**Method.** Minimal-Pair Step Preference (MPSP)\n\n## Motivation\nModern multimodal search agents — systems that read an image and a question, then take turns reasoning, cropping the image, and searching the web — are trained with reinforcement learning (RL) that gives the agent a single reward at the very end: was the final answer right? This is the GRPO (Group Relative Policy Optimization) family of methods. The problem: that one end-of-episode number is the agent's only feedback about a whole sequence of search decisions. It cannot tell the agent which step was good or bad. So two runs that both reach the correct answer get the same credit — even if one searched cleanly and the other retrieved the same thing three times, queried the wrong way, or stopped too early. Recent benchmarks (InterLV-Search, arXiv 2026-05; MC-Search, arXiv 2026-03) show this directly: the best agents stay under about 50% on genuinely interleaved search and routinely over- or under-retrieve, with the end-only score hiding it.\n\nWhat makes now the right time: step-level credit (giving feedback per decision instead of per episode) has just become a hot topic — iStar (arXiv 2025-09), StepOPSD (2026-05), and CSO (arXiv 2026-02) all do it. But every one of them builds the per-step signal from a learned scoring model (a process-reward model trained on trajectories, a stronger teacher model rescoring steps, or outcome-flipping critical-step search) and all are for text agents, not multimodal search. The newly-usable trick is the pool of sibling runs GRPO already samples for each question: among runs that all got the right answer, you can find two that did everything the same except one search decision. That single difference is a free, label-free training signal — no extra model needed.\n\nWhy prior work stopped short: OpenSearch-VL (arXiv 2026-05) only fixes the failure case (it masks tokens after a fatal tool error) and never compares two successful runs. SenseNova-MARS (arXiv 2025-12) only rescales the end reward, never localizing credit to a step. MC-Search's Search-Align (arXiv 2026-03) teaches good steps by copying a fixed annotated dataset offline, so it is capped by what was annotated. iStar (arXiv 2025-09) does relocate credit to the step online, but it trains a learned implicit reward model to do so and is not about multimodal search control.\n\nWhat changes when the gap closes: agents learn disciplined search behavior — fewer wasted retrievals, correct choice of which modality (text vs image) to query, fewer premature stops — directly from an objective they optimize, rather than from curated demonstrations. And it establishes that the per-step signal does not need a learned reward model at all, which makes label-free sibling contrasts a reusable tool for the whole area.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n\n1. Run the usual outcome-reward reinforcement learning (RL) for multimodal search agents — here Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO) / Group Sequence Policy Optimization (GSPO), which for each question samples a group of G separate runs (use G=8) and scores each run only by whether its final answer is right. Use a 7B Qwen2.5-VL policy on the MC-Search + InterLV-Search training splits. A 'run' is the agent's whole transcript for one question: it alternates between thinking in text and issuing typed actions (search by text, search/crop an image, choose which modality to look in, or stop), with each search result pasted back into its context. Log every action as a record of (which action, the action's arguments after normalizing them, what came back, and which generated tokens make up that action) so later steps can point at individual decisions. Change nothing in this step.\n   - _Why_: Keep the answer-correctness reward intact so the new per-step signal is purely additive and the lambda=0 setting exactly reproduces today's end-only training.\n\n### Minimal-Pair Mining\n*Builds the label-free per-decision credit signal by finding same-outcome sibling runs that differ at exactly one search-control decision and scoring it from the policy's own readouts.*\n\n2. Inside each group of G runs, turn each run into just the ordered list of its typed search-control decisions (drop the in-between reasoning text). Two runs 'share a prefix' if these decision lists are identical up to some position — identical meaning same action type and same arguments after normalizing (lowercase queries and collapse spaces; treat two image crops as the same if their boxes overlap by more than 90%). Now find two runs that (1) both reach the SAME correct final answer and (2) agree on every decision up to one position and then differ at exactly that one search-control decision (whether to retrieve, what text to query, which image/crop to use, which modality to route to, or whether to stop). Record that pair as (winner, loser) — the two differing decisions, each with the tokens that make it up. The search results on the shared part do not have to be byte-for-byte identical, because we are comparing the agent's decision, not the web's stochastic reply. 【author decision: whether the shared prefix should also be required to have near-identical returned evidence to keep the two runs truly comparable, or whether matching the decisions alone is enough — this trades how many pairs you get against how clean each pair is.】 Throw away cases where the runs differ only in their reasoning wording with no differing typed decision.\n   - _Why_: If everything else is identical and the outcome is identical, the single differing decision is the only thing that can carry process-quality credit.\n3. Score each (winner, loser) pair with three numbers that all come from the policy itself — no extra scoring model, critic, or teacher. (a) Answer-correctness difference: +1/0/-1 from whether each sibling's final answer is right; for the standard both-correct pairs this is 0, so the label is decided by the next two terms. 【author decision: whether to also mine pairs where one sibling is right and one wrong, or to keep only both-correct pairs — this decides whether the signal measures pure process quality or also re-folds in answer credit; the matched-accuracy result uses only both-correct pairs.】 (b) Retrieval redundancy: embed each retrieved item (one web text chunk, or one returned/cropped image) by running it through the policy and averaging its last-layer hidden states, then take the highest cosine similarity between this step's retrieved item and anything retrieved earlier in the same run; it is 0 if this decision retrieves nothing. Higher redundancy is worse. (c) Evidence gain: measure how much this step's evidence raised the policy's confidence in the run's verified final answer — append a fixed 'now answer' prompt to the context just before versus just after adding this step's evidence, read the probability the policy assigns to the final answer in each case, and take the positive increase (one extra forward pass). A run that gains more confidence with less redundancy is the winner.\n\n*The per-decision score combines the sibling answer-correctness difference $\\Delta _{acc} \\in $ {-1,0,+1}, the retrieval redundancy $\\rho  \\in $ [0,1], and the evidence gain $g \\in $ [0,1]; b and c only break ties when $\\Delta _{acc} = 0$ so equal-outcome pairs still get a per-decision sign.*\n$$ r_{\\mathrm{step}} = a\\,\\Delta_{\\mathrm{acc}} - b\\,\\rho + c\\,g,\\quad a=1.0,\\ b=0.3,\\ c=0.3 \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: All three numbers come from the policy itself, so the per-decision label is label-free and model-free — the whole point versus learned-PRM methods.\n\n### Step-Preference Optimization\n*Turns each minimal pair into a step-level DPO gradient added to the unchanged GRPO objective and re-mines online so the signal stays on-policy.*\n\n4. Build a step-level preference loss using Direct Preference Optimization (DPO) — a standard method that nudges the model to prefer a 'winner' over a 'loser' — but apply it only to the one differing decision, not the whole run. Concretely (Eq. 2, with strength $\\beta =0.1):$ score each of the winner and loser decision by adding up the model's per-token log-probabilities of producing that decision's action and arguments (just the action call like search-text(query=...), not the surrounding reasoning text or the search results), both conditioned on the identical shared prefix the two runs agreed on. Compare these against a frozen copy of the policy taken at the start of this round (the reference DPO needs). Pushing the winner's probability above the loser's makes the better search move more likely next time, which in turn changes which tool or modality the agent reaches for.\n\n*The step-level DPO loss over the differing decision span $s_{win}$ versus $s_{lose},$ scored by the policy log-prob conditioned on the shared prefix; raising $log p(s_{win})$ above $log p(s_{lose})$ makes the warranted search-control move more likely at rollout time.*\n$$ L_{\\mathrm{step}} = -\\log \\sigma\\!\\left(\\beta\\,(\\log p(s_{\\mathrm{win}}) - \\log p(s_{\\mathrm{lose}}))\\right),\\quad \\beta=0.1 \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This nudges the agent to make the warranted search move more likely and the wasteful one less likely, the next time it faces that decision.\n5. Train on both signals at once. For each optimizer step, over the current batch of question-groups: compute the ordinary GRPO outcome loss across that group's G runs as before, and compute the step preference loss as the average over all the (winner, loser) pairs mined from that group (groups with no pairs just use the outcome loss). Add them with weight 0.5: total loss = GRPO loss $+ 0.5 \\times $ step loss, and do a single backpropagation update on the shared model. The agent still chases the correct answer, but it now also learns to reach it through warranted, non-redundant, correctly-routed steps, so later runs retrieve less wastefully and route modality better.\n\n*The combined objective adds the step-level preference term to the unchanged GRPO outcome objective; $\\lambda  = 0$ recovers the terminal-only baseline (the inherited credit locus) and $\\lambda  = 0.5$ switches on the relocated per-decision locus, which is simultaneously the audit's controlled intervention.*\n$$ L = L_{\\mathrm{GRPO}} + \\lambda\\,L_{\\mathrm{step}},\\quad \\lambda=0.5 \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The agent still chases the right answer, but now also learns to reach it through warranted, non-redundant, correctly-routed steps.\n6. Repeat the whole loop each round. At the start of every round, freeze a copy of the current policy to serve as the reference for the step preference loss (this keeps the preference signal aligned with the current behavior and stops it drifting from an outdated reference), then sample fresh runs, re-find the minimal pairs (Step 2), re-score them (Step 3), and apply Steps 4-5. Because the pairs are dug out fresh each round from the agent's own current runs and nothing is stored from a fixed labeled dataset, the per-decision signal stays on-policy and follows the agent as it improves.\n   - _Why_: The signal tracks the agent's evolving behavior, so it stays on-policy and is not capped by any pre-collected annotation.\n\n### Credit-Locus Diagnostic\n*Sweeps lambda=0 vs 0.5 plus a permuted-label control at matched accuracy to prove the gains come from per-decision credit correctness.*\n\n7. Do the controlled diagnostic with everything except the credit setting held fixed (same model, data, random seeds, and total training steps), comparing three variants: $\\lambda =0$ (the old whole-run-only credit), $\\lambda =0.5$ (the new per-decision credit), and a permuted-label control (randomly shuffle which decision is 'winner' vs 'loser' inside each pair, so the credit's sign is scrambled but the loss size and $\\lambda =0.5$ are unchanged). Evaluate all three on InterLV-Search (interleaved-search accuracy) and MC-Search (step-by-step planning and retrieval fidelity), and report retrieval count, modality-routing accuracy, premature-stop rate, and final-answer accuracy. First check that final-answer accuracy is statistically the SAME between $\\lambda =0.5$ and $\\lambda =0$ using an equivalence test (count them as matched only if the 95% confidence interval of the accuracy gap stays within $\\pm 1$ percentage point); only if accuracy is matched do you then compare the process metrics with a paired bootstrap test — otherwise report that the matched-accuracy condition failed rather than claiming a process win. 【author decision: the $\\pm 1-point$ equivalence margin is a default and should be tuned to how noisy the benchmark's accuracy measurement is.】 Define premature-stop rate as how often the agent stopped while its answer is still wrong and one more ordinary query would have found the supporting evidence; define modality-routing accuracy as how often a 'which modality to look in' decision matches the modality where the gold supporting evidence actually lives, using MC-Search's step-by-step chain annotations as the ground truth. 【author decision: whether MC-Search's annotations directly give per-step correct-modality labels, or whether you must write your own rubric for what counts as correct routing — this fixes the meaning of 'correct routing'.】 The result is the matched-accuracy comparison table that is this leg's deliverable.\n   - _Why_: Holding everything else fixed isolates whether the per-decision credit — and only its correctness — is what improves the process, since the permuted control should collapse back to baseline.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 面向多模态智能体搜索控制的最小对步级偏好优化\n\n**方法名称.** Minimal-Pair Step Preference (MPSP)\n\n## 研究动机\n现代多模态搜索智能体——能读取一张图和一个问题，然后轮流推理、裁剪图像、上网搜索的系统——通常用强化学习（RL）训练，只在最后给一个奖励：最终答案对不对？这就是 GRPO (Group Relative Policy Optimization) 这一族方法。问题在于：这个回合末尾的单一数字，是智能体对整串搜索决策得到的唯一反馈，它无法告诉智能体哪一步好、哪一步差。于是两次都答对的运行得到相同的信用——哪怕一次搜索得很干净，另一次把同样的东西检索了三遍、用错了查询方式、或过早停止。最新的基准（InterLV-Search, arXiv 2026-05；MC-Search, arXiv 2026-03）直接揭示了这点：最好的智能体在真正交错的搜索上仍低于约 50%，并经常过度或不足检索，而只看终端分数会把这些掩盖掉。\n\n为什么现在正合适：步级信用（按每个决策而非每个回合给反馈）刚刚成为热点——iStar (arXiv 2025-09)、StepOPSD (2026-05)、CSO (arXiv 2026-02) 都在做。但它们每一个都用一个学习得到的打分模型来构造步级信号（在轨迹上训练的 process-reward model、用更强的 teacher 模型重打分、或寻找翻转结果的关键步），而且都面向文本智能体，不是多模态搜索。新可用的窍门是 GRPO 本来就为每个问题采样的一组兄弟运行：在都答对的运行里，可以找到两次除了某一个搜索决策外完全相同的运行。这一个差异就是一个免费的、无需标注的训练信号——不需要额外模型。\n\n为什么前人止步：OpenSearch-VL (arXiv 2026-05) 只修复失败情形（在致命工具错误之后屏蔽 token），从不比较两次成功的运行。SenseNova-MARS (arXiv 2025-12) 只对终端奖励重新缩放，从不把信用定位到某一步。MC-Search 的 Search-Align (arXiv 2026-03) 通过离线复制一个固定标注数据集来教好的步，因此被标注覆盖范围所限。iStar (arXiv 2025-09) 确实在线把信用重定位到步，但它为此训练了一个学习得到的 implicit reward model，且不针对多模态搜索控制。\n\n缺口填上后会改变什么：智能体直接从自己优化的目标中学会有纪律的搜索行为——更少的无用检索、对查询哪种模态（文本 vs 图像）的正确选择、更少的过早停止——而不是从人工示范中获得。并且它证明了步级信号根本不需要学习得到的 reward model，从而让无标注的兄弟对比成为整个领域可复用的工具。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景\n\n1. 照常运行多模态搜索智能体的结果奖励强化学习(Reinforcement Learning, RL)——这里用的是组相对策略优化(Group Relative Policy Optimization, GRPO)/组序列策略优化(Group Sequence Policy Optimization, GSPO)：对每个问题采样一组共 G 次独立运行（取 G=8），每次运行只按其最终答案是否正确来打分。策略用 7B 的 Qwen2.5-VL，在 MC-Search + InterLV-Search 训练划分上训练。一次「运行」是智能体对一个问题的完整记录：它在文字推理与若干带类型的动作（按文本搜索、按图像搜索或裁剪、选择去哪种模态查找、停止）之间交替，每条搜索结果都会被拼回它的上下文。把每个动作记成一条记录：（是哪种动作、把参数规范化后的取值、返回了什么、构成该动作的是哪些生成 token），以便后续步骤能精确指向单个决策。本步骤不做任何改动。\n   - _为什么_: 保持答案正确性奖励不变，使新的每步信号纯粹是叠加的，且 lambda=0 设置能精确复现当下仅看终端的训练。\n\n### 最小对挖掘\n*通过寻找同结果、仅在一个搜索控制决策处不同的兄弟运行，并用策略自身的读出给它打分，构建无标注的每决策信用信号。*\n\n2. 在每组 G 次运行内，把每次运行化简为它带类型的搜索控制决策的有序列表（丢掉中间的推理文字）。两次运行「共享前缀」是指：这两个决策列表在某个位置之前完全相同——相同指动作类型相同、且参数规范化后也相同（查询字符串统一转小写并压缩空白；两个图像裁剪框若重叠度 IoU 超过 90% 即视为同一）。在此基础上，找到满足以下条件的两次运行：(1) 二者到达相同的正确最终答案；(2) 在某个位置之前的每个决策都一致，然后恰好在那一个搜索控制决策上分叉（是否检索、用什么文本查询、用哪张图像/裁剪、路由到哪种模态、或是否停止）。把这一对记作 (winner, loser)——即两个不同的决策，各自带上构成它的 token。共享部分的搜索返回结果不必逐字节相同，因为我们比较的是智能体的决策，而非网络的随机返回。【作者需决定：共享前缀是否还应要求返回证据近乎相同以保证两次运行真正可比，还是仅决策一致就够——这要在能得到多少对与每对有多干净之间权衡。】把那些仅推理措辞不同、没有任何带类型决策差异的情形丢弃。\n   - _为什么_: 如果其它一切相同、结果也相同，那么唯一不同的决策就是唯一能承载过程质量信用的东西。\n3. 用三个全部来自策略自身的数字给每个 (winner, loser) 对打分——不需要任何额外的打分模型、critic 或 teacher。(a) 答案正确性差：由两个兄弟各自最终答案是否正确得出 +1/0/-1；对于标准的「两者都正确」的对，这一项为 0，于是标签由后两项决定。【作者需决定：是否也挖掘「一对一错」的共享前缀对，还是只保留两者都正确的对——这决定了信号是衡量纯过程质量、还是又把答案信用重新混进来；匹配准确率的结果只使用两者都正确的对。】(b) 检索冗余度：把每个检索项（一段返回的网页文本，或一张返回/裁剪的图像）送进策略、对其最后一层隐藏状态做平均池化来得到嵌入，再取本步检索项与同一次运行中先前任一检索项之间的最大余弦相似度；若本决策没有检索则为 0。冗余越高越差。(c) 证据增益：衡量本步证据把策略对该次运行已验证最终答案的置信度提高了多少——在加入本步证据之前与之后，分别给上下文追加一个固定的「现在作答」提示，读出策略在两种情况下赋予最终答案的概率，取其正向增量（一次额外前向）。在更少冗余下获得更多置信度提升的那次运行即 winner。\n\n*每个决策的分数由同组兄弟轨迹的答案正确性差 $\\Delta _{acc} \\in  {-1,0,+1}$、检索冗余度 $\\rho  \\in $ [0,1] 与证据增益 $g \\in $ [0,1] 组合而成；当 $\\Delta _{acc} = 0$ 时仅由 b、c 打破平局，使同结果的对仍能得到每决策的符号。*\n$$ r_{\\mathrm{step}} = a\\,\\Delta_{\\mathrm{acc}} - b\\,\\rho + c\\,g,\\quad a=1.0,\\ b=0.3,\\ c=0.3 \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这三个数都来自策略本身，所以每决策标签是无标注、无模型的——这正是相对于学习型 PRM 方法的关键所在。\n\n### 步级偏好优化\n*把每个最小对转成步级 DPO 梯度叠加到不变的 GRPO 目标上，并在线重新挖掘以保持信号 on-policy。*\n\n4. 用直接偏好优化(Direct Preference Optimization, DPO)——一种让模型偏好「winner」而非「loser」的标准方法——构造步级偏好损失，但只作用于那一个不同的决策，而非整次运行。具体地（式 2，强度 $\\beta =0.1$）：对 winner 与 loser 各自的决策打分，方法是把模型逐 token 生成该决策的动作及其参数（只算动作调用如 search-text(query=...)，不含周围推理文字、也不含搜索返回结果）的 log 概率相加，两者都以两次运行一致的同一共享前缀为条件。再与本轮开始时冻结的策略副本（DPO 所需的参考）相比较。把 winner 的概率推到高于 loser，会使更有依据的搜索动作在下次更可能出现，从而改变智能体接下来去调用哪个工具或哪种模态。\n\n*在不同决策片段 $s_{win}$ 与 $s_{lose}$ 上的步级 DPO 损失，由策略在共享前缀条件下的 log 概率打分；提升 $log p(s_{win})$ 相对 $log p(s_{lose})$ 会在采样时使更有依据的搜索控制动作更可能被选择。*\n$$ L_{\\mathrm{step}} = -\\log \\sigma\\!\\left(\\beta\\,(\\log p(s_{\\mathrm{win}}) - \\log p(s_{\\mathrm{lose}}))\\right),\\quad \\beta=0.1 \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这会促使智能体下次面对该决策时，更可能采取有依据的搜索动作、更少采取浪费的动作。\n5. 同时用两种信号训练。每个优化步，在当前一批问题组上：像之前那样对该组的 G 次运行计算普通的 GRPO 结果损失；并把从该组挖掘出的所有 (winner, loser) 对的步级偏好损失取平均（没有任何对的组就只用结果损失）。以权重 0.5 相加：总损失 = GRPO 损失 $+ 0.5 \\times $ 步级损失，对共享模型做一次反向传播更新。智能体仍然追求正确答案，但现在也学会通过有依据、不冗余、路由正确的步去达到答案，于是后续运行检索得更省、模态路由得更准。\n\n*组合目标在保持不变的 GRPO 结果目标上叠加步级偏好项；$\\lambda  = 0$ 退回到仅终端的基线（继承的信用归属位点），$\\lambda  = 0.5$ 启用被重定位的每决策位点，这同时也是审计的受控干预。*\n$$ L = L_{\\mathrm{GRPO}} + \\lambda\\,L_{\\mathrm{step}},\\quad \\lambda=0.5 \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 智能体仍然追求正确答案，但现在也学会通过有依据、不冗余、路由正确的步去达到答案。\n6. 每一轮重复整个循环。每轮开始时，冻结一份当前策略的副本作为步级偏好损失的参考（这能让偏好信号与当前行为对齐，避免它偏离一个过时的参考），然后采样新的运行、重新挖掘最小对（步骤 2）、重新打分（步骤 3），再执行步骤 4-5。由于每一轮都从智能体自己当前的运行里现挖最小对、且不保留任何固定的标注数据集，每决策信号便保持 on-policy，并随智能体的进步而变化。\n   - _为什么_: 信号跟随智能体不断变化的行为，因此保持 on-policy，且不被任何预先收集的标注所限。\n\n### 信用位点诊断\n*在匹配准确率下扫描 lambda=0 与 0.5 并加置换标签对照，证明增益来自每决策信用的正确性。*\n\n7. 做受控诊断，除了信用设置外其余一切都固定（同一模型、数据、随机种子和总训练步数），比较三个变体：$\\lambda =0$（旧的仅看整次运行的信用）、$\\lambda =0.5$（新的每决策信用）、以及置换标签对照（在每对内部随机打乱谁是「winner」谁是「loser」，从而打乱信用的符号，但损失大小与 $\\lambda =0.5$ 保持不变）。在 InterLV-Search（交错搜索准确率）与 MC-Search（逐步规划与检索保真度）上评估这三者，并报告检索次数、模态路由准确率、过早停止率与最终答案准确率。先用等价性检验确认 $\\lambda =0.5$ 与 $\\lambda =0$ 的最终答案准确率在统计上相同（仅当准确率差的 95% 置信区间落在 $\\pm 1$ 个百分点以内才算匹配）；只有在准确率匹配的前提下，才用配对自助法(bootstrap)比较过程指标——否则就报告「匹配准确率条件未满足」，而不是宣称取得过程上的胜利。【作者需决定：$\\pm 1$ 个百分点的等价边界只是默认值，应根据该基准准确率测量的噪声大小来调。】把过早停止率定义为：智能体停止时其答案仍然错误、且再做一次普通查询本可找到支撑证据的查询所占比例；把模态路由准确率定义为：在「去哪种模态查找」的决策中，所选模态与黄金支撑证据实际所在模态一致的比例，以 MC-Search 的逐步链标注作为 ground truth。【作者需决定：是 MC-Search 的标注直接给出每步的正确模态标签，还是必须自行制定一套「何为正确路由」的评判规则——这界定了「正确路由」的含义。】产出即这一支的交付物：匹配准确率下的对照表。\n   - _为什么_: 固定其它一切可隔离出：是否正是每决策信用——且仅其正确性——改善了过程，因为置换对照应当退回到基线。\n\n"},{"id":"75","run_dir":"run_prompt75_meanflowpolicy","index":75,"title":"One-Step Robot Policies by Manifold Projection, Not Velocity Integration","title_zh":"用强制幂等的流形投影实现单步机器人策略","method_name":"Enforced-Idempotency Projection Policy (EIPP)","hook":"We obtain a single-step action generator that ships strictly fewer learned objects than every one-step baseline: no teacher, no EMA self-teacher, no self-consistency objective, and no time-contracting curriculum. The whole policy is one feed-forward operator trained to be the metric projection onto the in-distribution action manifold, and it holds fidelity exactly where the velocity-integral collapse breaks down under sparse conditional geometry.","anchor_pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","anchor_pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","domain_category":"Robotics & Embodied Agents","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved one-step leaf produces a single-step action map whose fidelity *holds up* when the conditional action geometry is sparse (low-data, contact-rich, or unseen embodiment): OFP (arxiv:2603.12480v1) and FlowPolicy (openalex:W4409365031) report the single-step-vs-multi-step fidelity gap as open precisely there, and IDP (arxiv:2606.01098v1) attacks it but reports its own conditional-geometry estimate as fragile under the same sparsity. This is an unmet outcome (a robust one-step jump under","pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","sub_pattern":"C12 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by substituting the per-step aggregation primitive: the noise-to-action interval-integral velocity operator is replaced by a classical-theorem-grounded metric-projection operator P_theta that lands on the in-distribution action manifold by the operator's idempotent/contractive construction rather than by memorising a single integral jump, so fidelity is carried by the projection geometry exactly where the integral collapse goes off-manifold under sparse conditioning.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved one-step leaf achieves teacher-level (or better) single-step fidelity *without re-importing the multi-step machinery the one-step promise was meant to delete*: every frontier recipe pays a structural tax—OneDP (openalex:W4404321702) needs a frozen multi-step teacher and can only inherit its ceiling, OFP (arxiv:2603.12480v1) needs an EMA self-teacher plus a hand-tuned time-contracting curriculum, FlowPolicy (openalex:W4409365031) needs a self-consistency constraint over the velocity ","pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","sub_pattern":"C12 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by the same operator swap: because the projection target (the nearest in-distribution action) is computed directly from data at training time, the supervision needs no teacher, no EMA bootstrap, no self-consistency objective, and no curriculum schedule — the subtraction of all four is a native consequence of moving from 'integrate a learned velocity' to 'regress a single projection map', not an added trick.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"one-step / few-step action generation for visuomotor and vision-language-action robot policies (flow- and diffusion-based imitation learning)","n_papers":50,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":26},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":15,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Brain-inspired Action Generation with Spiking Transformer Diffusion Policy Model"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"GR-2: A Generative Video-Language-Action Model with Web-Scale Knowledge for Robot Manipulation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Prediction with Action: Visual Policy Learning via Joint Denoising Process"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"FlowPolicy: Enabling Fast and Robust 3D Flow-based Policy via Consistency Flow Matching for Robot Manipulation"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Diffusion policy: Visuomotor policy learning via action diffusion"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Intelligent mobile robot navigation in unknown and complex environment using reinforcement learning technique"}],"more":9},{"year":2025,"n":24,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Object-Centric Action-Enhanced Representations for Robot Visuo-Motor Policy Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A Mixed-Reality-Augmented Deep Reinforcement Learning Approach for Multi-Robot Safe Motion Generation in Human–Robot Collaborative Manufacturing Cells"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Learning Generalizable Robot Policy with Human Demonstration Video as a Prompt"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Hierarchical Autoregressive Modeling With Multi-Scale Refinement for Robot Policy Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Enhancing Robot Learning Through Cognitive Reasoning Trajectory Optimization Under Unknown Dynamics"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"ManiFlow: A General Robot Manipulation Policy via Consistency Flow Training"}],"more":18},{"year":2026,"n":11,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Robot Learning from Human Videos: A Survey"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Formal Methods in Robot Policy Learning and Verification: A Survey on Current Techniques and Future Directions"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"PlayWorld: Learning Robot World Models from Autonomous Play"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Action Images: End-to-End Policy Learning via Multiview Video Generation"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Demystifying Action Space Design for Robotic Manipulation Policies"}],"more":5}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign; structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"generative_process_redesign; structural_prior_encoding","count":4,"share":0.08},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering; generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"self_supervised_signal_engineering; generative_process_redesign","count":3,"share":0.06},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution; generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"architectural_operator_substitution; generative_process_redesign","count":2,"share":0.04},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":2,"share":0.04},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate; reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"decompose_and_delegate; reframe_as_solvable_object","count":2,"share":0.04},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering; reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"self_supervised_signal_engineering; reframe_as_solvable_object","count":2,"share":0.04},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign; architectural_operator_substitution; characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"generative_process_redesign; architectural_operator_substitution; characterize_limit_then_surpass","count":2,"share":0.04},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning; generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"adapt_via_conditioning; generative_process_redesign","count":2,"share":0.04}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"For flow/diffusion robot policies, single-step action generation is currently obtained by forcing the network to approximate the *integral* of the generating velocity field over the whole noise-to-action interval, and every recent recipe pays a different structural tax to make that integral learnable: OFP (arxiv:2603.12480v1) replaces MeanFlow's exact Jacobian-vector-product average-velocity objective with a finite-difference EMA self-consistency target plus a time-contracting curriculum, FlowPolicy (openalex:W4409365031) enforces self-consistency of the straight-line velocity field, and OneDP (openalex:W4404321702) sidesteps the problem entirely by KL-distilling a frozen multi-step teacher. The shared failure is that none of these makes the one-step map *carry the intermediate trajectory correction* that the multi-step solver supplies for free: the network must memorise a single jump that lands on the in-distribution action manifold, so under low-data / contact-rich / cross-embodiment conditions where the conditional action geometry is sparse the jump lands off-manifold and fidelity collapses (Implicit Drifting Policy, arxiv:2606.01098v1, names exactly this discarded-correction problem and shows the naive fix—explicitly regressing a training-time drift field—is ill-posed under demonstration sparsity). The result is that one-step fidelity remains gapped against the multi-step teacher and is fragile across tasks and embodiments, and the cures so far buy that fidelity only by re-introducing the very machinery (a teacher, an EMA bootstrap, an extra differential objective, a curriculum) that the one-step promise was meant to remove.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2603.12480v1","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"OFP learns a from-scratch, teacher-free one-step flow policy by parameterising an interval-averaged velocity field and supervising it with a finite-difference target built from an EMA copy of itself (a self-consistency loss), plus self-guided CFG sharpening and a temporal warm-start, and it explicitly positions itself as a cheaper substitute for MeanFlow's JVP average-velocity objective. Its residue is that the average-velocity target is still bootstrapped from the model's own EMA teacher under a hand-tuned time-contracting schedule (ρ(s)), so single-step fidelity depends on the stability of that self-distillation loop and the schedule's tuning rather than on any guarantee that the one-step jump preserves the intermediate trajectory correction—leaving the fidelity-vs-teacher ceiling and cross-embodiment robustness open exactly where the conditional action geometry is sparse."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2606.01098v1","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Implicit Drifting Policy diagnoses that one-step formulations throw away the intermediate trajectory evolution that gives multi-step solvers their action correction, and brings that correction back implicitly by extracting a conditional expert geometry from the local variation of observation-similar expert actions and weighting a scalar potential objective with it, after arguing the explicit drift-field regression is ill-posed under demonstration sparsity. Its residue is that the conditional-geometry estimate is itself fragile precisely under the sparsity it is meant to survive—it depends on having enough observation-similar neighbours to define a local geometry—and the paper reports scaling and cross-embodiment generalisation as still open."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4404321702","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"OneDP distils a frozen, pre-trained multi-step diffusion policy into a single-step action generator by minimising KL divergence along the diffusion chain, reaching teacher-level success at ~62 Hz for 2-10% extra pre-training cost. Its residue is the hard dependency on an already-trained multi-step teacher: the one-step generator can only inherit, never exceed, the teacher's action distribution, and any embodiment / task without a converged teacher cannot be served—there is no from-scratch path and no mechanism to surpass the teacher's fidelity ceiling."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4409365031","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"FlowPolicy obtains single-step 3D point-cloud policies by normalising the self-consistency of a straight-line (consistency-flow-matching) velocity field so that flows from different time states map to the same action, achieving ~7× speed-up at competitive success on Adroit / MetaWorld. Its residue is that the straight-line self-consistency constraint is a strong geometric assumption about the noise-to-action transport that holds on the evaluated 3D benchmarks but is not shown to survive contact-rich or high-dexterity action distributions, where the true transport is curved—so the single-step fidelity ceiling on harder embodiments stays open."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"one-step / few-step action generation for visuomotor and vision-language-action robot policies (flow- and diffusion-based imitation learning)","venue":"ML/robotics venue (NeurIPS / ICLR / ICML / CoRL / RA-L)","time":"2026","data":["LIBERO / LIBERO-Long / LIBERO-Plus / LIBERO-Pro","MetaWorld","Adroit","RoboTwin 2.0","real-robot single-arm / bimanual manipulation"],"compute":"1×A100 × 3 months (≈90 A100-day budget)","expertise":"ML researcher with generative-models + robot imitation-learning background","preference":"both","baseline":"iterative flow / diffusion policies sampled at 10-100 NFE (Diffusion Policy, DP3, flow-matching policies); few/one-step accelerators OFP (arxiv:2603.12480v1), FlowPolicy (openalex:W4409365031), OneDP (openalex:W4404321702), ManiFlow (semanticscholar:af13682020d41da4aa527c481e370a9ba142cf46)","limitation":"iterative ODE/SDE sampling of generative policies needs tens-to-hundreds of forward passes per action, capping control frequency; existing one-step variants either need a pre-trained teacher / extra distillation stage, or trade single-step fidelity and cross-embodiment robustness for speed","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["domain","venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared bottleneck-question (shared_question thread) both legs attack is: how is a single forward pass made to land an action on the in-distribution manifold faithfully? Every frontier leaf answers it by training the network to approximate the interval integral of a velocity field (OFP supervises an interval-averaged velocity u_theta(z_t,t,r|o) with EMA target u_target=(z_hat_r - z_t)/(r-t), arxiv:2603.12480v1; FlowPolicy enforces straight-line self-consistency, openalex:W4409365031), so the one-step map must memorise a single jump whose target geometry is only well-defined where demonstrations are dense. We substitute that operator. Move (C12): keep the rich observation encoder and the action-head architecture intact, but replace the integral-velocity aggregation primitive with a single metric-projection operator P_theta(a_tilde | o): R^{H x d_a} -> R^{H x d_a} trained to map a CORRUPTED action chunk a_tilde back onto the conditional in-distribution action manifold M_o. The artifact it produces is an idempotent, locally-contractive projection map: at inference we draw one Gaussian sample a_tilde ~ N(0, sigma_0^2 I) (sigma_0 a single fixed scalar, the corruption radius, default 1.0 in normalised action units) and emit a_hat = P_theta(a_tilde | o) in ONE forward pass — no ODE, no time index, no schedule. This closes the sparse-geometry gap (leg 1) because the projection target is the nearest expert action under the chunk metric, so the operator's job is 'find the nearest on-manifold point', a problem that stays well-posed under sparse conditioning where 'reproduce the integral of a trajectory that was never observed' does not; landing is guaranteed by the operator's construction (contraction toward M_o), not by integral fidelity. It closes the subtractive gap (leg 2) because P_theta's training target — the data action a itself, the exact projection of any corruption of it — is available directly from each demonstration, so the loss is a plain reconstruction regression L = E_{(o,a),eta}[ || P_theta(a + eta | o) - a ||^2 ] over corruption scales eta ~ U(0, sigma_0) (eta a per-sample scalar drawn uniformly, NOT a tuned per-step schedule), deleting teacher, EMA, self-consistency, and curriculum at once. The classical anchor that makes this an operator-SUBSTITUTION rather than a fresh heuristic: P_theta is the learned proximal/metric-projection operator of the action-manifold indicator, which is idempotent (P o P = P) on M_o and 1-contractive in its neighbourhood; we add a light idempotency penalty L_idem = E_o[ || P_theta(P_theta(a_tilde|o)|o) - P_theta(a_tilde|o) ||^2 ] so the trained map approximates a true projection rather than an arbitrary regressor — this penalty is the single load-bearing structural property the swap must preserve and is what makes one shot land on the manifold from a wide corruption radius. Every quantity is computable from the text: a_tilde and eta are sampled noise, a and o are dataset readouts, sigma_0 and the idempotency weight lambda_idem (default 0.1) are the only free scalars, P_theta reuses the baseline's network with the time-embedding input removed.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery because the SAME swapped operator P_theta closes both — robustness (leg 1) comes from projection being well-posed under sparsity, and scaffold-deletion (leg 2) comes from the projection target being a directly-available data label; the evidence that they are one mechanism, not two modules, is that removing the operator swap reopens both gaps simultaneously, which is the shared_question signature rather than two stapled legs. (b) Alternative designs considered and rejected: (i) generative_process_redesign / C24 latent-space redesign (impose analytic structure on a latent and keep the flow) was rejected because it sits in the saturated lane every scooper occupies and still trains a transport, so it would not delete the scaffolding; (ii) structural_prior_encoding / C16 was rejected because action chunks under sparse contact-rich geometry carry no clean exact symmetry group, so its honest deliverable is a completeness proof, not a runnable method. REGRESSION AVOIDED: P_theta is a single feed-forward projection, so it does NOT reduce to the flow-matching/consistency collapse node (n2/n3), NOT to inference-time energy minimisation / implicit BC (collateral c0, which solves an optimisation at test time — we do one forward pass), and NOT to an EMA persistent running-average self-teacher (the >16y / self-distillation-flagged node) because there is no moving teacher at all.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: train P_theta and the OFP/FlowPolicy one-step baselines from scratch on LIBERO-Long plus a contact-rich cross-embodiment split (RoboTwin 2.0 bimanual), all at NFE=1, and measure task success rate and the single-step-vs-multi-step fidelity gap. If the candidate works, NFE=1 success rate on the sparse contact-rich / unseen-embodiment split is HIGHER for P_theta than for the velocity-integral baselines (the fidelity gap that OFP and FlowPolicy report open there narrows or closes), while dense-benchmark success stays at parity. The load-bearing variable is kappa, the idempotency-contraction ratio of P_theta (Step 7): the mechanism claim is that LANDING is carried by the operator being a genuine projection, not by integral fidelity. Negative control: train with the manifold-anchor target randomised to a wrong-conditional expert action (Step 9) — this leaves kappa's definition intact but destroys the projection target; the anti-tautology prediction is on the DOWNSTREAM task metric, namely that sparse-split success rate collapses toward the velocity-integral baselines even though the network still produces a low-kappa idempotent map, proving the gain comes from projecting onto the CORRECT conditional manifold and not merely from being idempotent. Positive control: the L_rec-only variant (Step 10) should recover most of the dense-benchmark success but lose the sparse-regime robustness, converting the falsifier into a constructive identification that the projection/idempotency property is what buys sparse-geometry fidelity.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2603.12480v1","delta":"OFP trains an interval-averaged velocity field u_theta(z_t,t,r|o) supervised by an EMA self-teacher target u_target=(z_hat_r - z_t)/(r-t) under a contracting time schedule rho(s); we construct no velocity and no time index at all — we regress a single idempotent metric-projection operator whose target is the data action itself, so we ship one-step landing without the EMA self-distillation loop or schedule whose stability OFP names as its residue."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4409365031","delta":"FlowPolicy enforces straight-line self-consistency of a velocity field (a strong assumption that the noise-to-action transport is straight, unverified on contact-rich curved transports); we make no straight-line or transport assumption — projection onto the conditional manifold is well-posed even when the true transport is curved, removing exactly the geometric assumption FlowPolicy admits may fail on contact-rich embodiments."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4404321702","delta":"OneDP KL-distils a frozen multi-step teacher and is capped at the teacher's distribution; our operator is trained from scratch with the data action as its own projection target, so there is a from-scratch path and no inherited teacher ceiling (abstract-only inference: OneDP fulltext not in cache, but the teacher dependency is stated in its abstract)."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2606.01098v1","delta":"IDP recovers the discarded trajectory correction by estimating a conditional expert geometry from local variation of observation-similar actions (fragile when neighbours are sparse); we never estimate a local geometry from neighbours — the projection operator is trained globally so landing does not depend on having enough observation-similar neighbours at the query, which is the precise fragility IDP reports (abstract-only inference: IDP fulltext not in cache)."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"arxiv:2603.12480v1","what_step_was_missed":"OFP constructs its one-step map as the interval integral of a learned velocity field (u_theta over [t,r]) and supplies its supervision via an EMA-bootstrapped average-velocity target; to already be our contribution it would have needed to construct the one-step map as a metric-projection operator with an enforced idempotency property and to supervise it directly with the data action as the projection target — a construction (idempotent projection onto the conditional action manifold, with the second-forward-pass idempotency penalty as its load-bearing property) that its velocity-integral parameterisation does not produce, because an interval-averaged velocity is not idempotent and has no manifold-projection guarantee."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":308,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"Layer 1 hard floor did not fire: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict is borderline (no Reject lesson at candidate_match: yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat is NOT exact-mechanism overlap. In Layer 2 the decisive finding is paper_pointed_threat: ABot-M0 (semanticscholar:ce65343...) already publishes the candidate's headline 'projection onto feasible action manifolds instead of denoising' framing, and addressable_via names specific candidate fields (hook, differentiation_from_lit) that must change to dodge it; per the heuristic 'choose revise when paper_pointed_threat exists AND addressable_via names a specific candidate field', this routes to revise. recipe_application_check.verdict is applied (the C12 aggregation-primitive swap IS instantiated with the card-permitted measurement branch), so no sub_pattern swap is needed; the revision is tactical, confined to the framing/differentiation fields, leaving the kill-switch fields (falsification_prediction, compute_budget) untouched.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved one-step leaf produces a single-step action map whose fidelity *holds up* when the conditional action geometry is sparse (low-data, contact-rich, or unseen embodiment): OFP (arxiv:2603.12480v1) and FlowPolicy (openalex:W4409365031) report the single-step-vs-multi-step fidelity gap as open precisely there, and IDP (arxiv:2606.01098v1) attacks it but reports its own conditional-geometry estimate as fragile under the same sparsity. This is an unmet outcome (a robust one-step jump under sparse conditioning), stated without prescribing whether the cure lives in the objective, the transport parameterisation, the conditioning, or the training distribution.","main_pattern":"architectural_operator_substitution","sub_pattern":"C12 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is a substitution that is mechanically valid but whose payoff is absent or unverified: authors swap the operator/wiring/parameter-locus, then prove preservation with a borrowed or trivial argument that exposes no new structure, or claim the property the new slot was supposed to buy without delivering or measuring it. A diagnostic tell is validation on a proxy: throughput instead of accuracy, toy-scale data, or no matched baseline for the specific property claimed.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Proving the substitute operator preserves universal approximation via a trivial adaptation of known proofs, while never connecting that result to the practical advantage (e.g. sparsification) that motivated the swap, makes the contribution read as incremental.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate offers no separate universal-approximation theorem at all; its load-bearing property (idempotency/contraction kappa, Step 7) is directly tied via the negative control (Step 9) to the practical advantage (sparse-split success rate), so there is no disconnected preservation proof to trip this lesson."},{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming the rewired structure delivers a systems property — such as parallel forward/backward execution — that the underlying algorithm does not actually provide invites reviewers to falsify the headline claim head-on.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The headline systems property is NFE=1 one-step inference, which a single forward pass of P_theta genuinely provides (Step 6), so the claim is not a non-delivered systems property."},{"lesson_quoted":"A training-time re-parameterization that yields only marginal accuracy gains at higher training cost, without strong matched-baseline comparisons, reads as added overhead rather than as an insight.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The falsification_prediction is parity on dense benchmarks and improvement only on sparse contact-rich/unseen-embodiment splits, so the head-line gain is confined to a regime; this is mitigated by from-scratch matched baselines (OFP/FlowPolicy at NFE=1) but the dense-regime parity-at-extra-second-forward-pass keeps it borderline rather than clear."},{"lesson_quoted":"An elegant geometric reanalysis tool validated only on toy data, with no quantitative metric and an unclear delta over existing sensitivity measures, fails to show the substitution buys anything new.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Validation is on LIBERO-Long/MetaWorld/Adroit plus RoboTwin 2.0 and real bimanual with task success rate as the quantitative metric, not a toy-only geometric tool."},{"lesson_quoted":"Rewiring the dependency chain and reporting only throughput/speedup while omitting accuracy validation at scale leaves the essential preserved-property claim unverified.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The plan measures task success rate (accuracy) at NFE=1 head-on, not throughput as a proxy."},{"lesson_quoted":"Porting a two-component architecture from a separate domain and bolting on a cross-pathway coupling, without a unifying contribution grounded in the target task, reads as an uncoordinated assembly rather than a substitution insight.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The projection operator is argued from the target task's structure (nearest in-distribution action under the chunk metric stays well-posed under sparse conditioning), not lifted wholesale from another domain with a bolted coupling."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved one-step leaf achieves teacher-level (or better) single-step fidelity *without re-importing the multi-step machinery the one-step promise was meant to delete*: every frontier recipe pays a structural tax—OneDP (openalex:W4404321702) needs a frozen multi-step teacher and can only inherit its ceiling, OFP (arxiv:2603.12480v1) needs an EMA self-teacher plus a hand-tuned time-contracting curriculum, FlowPolicy (openalex:W4409365031) needs a self-consistency constraint over the velocity field. The missing outcome is one-step fidelity that does not depend on a separate teacher, bootstrap, or differential/curriculum scaffold.","main_pattern":"architectural_operator_substitution","sub_pattern":"C12 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is a substitution that is mechanically valid but whose payoff is absent or unverified; a diagnostic tell is claiming the property the new slot was supposed to buy without measuring it head-on, or porting an architecture and adding coupling without grounding it in the target problem.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A training-time re-parameterization that yields only marginal accuracy gains at higher training cost, without strong matched-baseline comparisons, reads as added overhead rather than as an insight.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"For leg 2 the claimed gain is subtractive (deletes teacher/EMA/self-consistency/curriculum), so the cost moves DOWN, not up; the extra second forward pass (L_idem) is the only added cost and it is ablated in Step 10, so this is not an unverified higher-cost re-parameterization."},{"lesson_quoted":"Proving the substitute operator preserves universal approximation via a trivial adaptation of known proofs, while never connecting that result to the practical advantage that motivated the swap, makes the contribution read as incremental.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"No borrowed preservation proof is invoked for the subtractive leg; the deletion of scaffolding is a direct consequence of the data action being the projection target, established by the loss form itself."}],"verdict":"clear"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"Both gap_closure entries cite C12. No Reject lesson reaches candidate_match: yes, so no documented Reject pattern is triggered. The aggregate is borderline, driven by leg 1's 'marginal accuracy gains at higher training cost ... without strong matched-baseline comparisons' lesson: the candidate confines its win to the sparse-conditioning regime while paying a second forward pass, which is mitigated by from-scratch matched baselines and a positive control but not fully cleared."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved one-step leaf produces a single-step action map whose fidelity *holds up* when the conditional action geometry is sparse (low-data, contact-rich, or unseen embodiment): OFP (arxiv:2603.12480v1) and FlowPolicy (openalex:W4409365031) report the single-step-vs-multi-step fidelity gap as open precisely there, and IDP (arxiv:2606.01098v1) attacks it but reports its own conditional-geometry estimate as fragile under the same sparsity. This is an unmet outcome (a robust one-step jump under sparse conditioning), stated without prescribing whether the cure lives in the objective, the transport parameterisation, the conditioning, or the training distribution.","sub_pattern":"C12 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Within a deep compositional architecture this cluster swaps a structural slot — notably it substitutes the per-stage aggregation/representation primitive — and the substitute is anchored to a classical theorem or revived classical representation that fits the same slot, accompanied by a proof OR a curvature/gradient-dynamics measurement showing the essential property (expressivity, required symmetry, gradient flow, capacity equivalence) survives while a cost/expressivity property changes.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism performs exactly the C12 signature operation: it substitutes the per-stage aggregation primitive — 'replace the integral-velocity aggregation primitive with a single metric-projection operator P_theta' — keeping the observation encoder and action-head architecture intact and deleting the scalar time-embedding slot (steps 1). The classical anchor required by C12 is named and re-derived for this slot: P_theta is 'the learned proximal/metric-projection operator of the action-manifold indicator, which is idempotent (P o P = P) on M_o and 1-contractive in its neighbourhood'. C12 explicitly accepts 'a proof OR a curvature/gradient-dynamics measurement' for the preservation obligation; the candidate takes the measurement branch — it enforces the idempotency property with L_idem (the second forward pass, step 4) and MEASURES the load-bearing property head-on via kappa, the idempotency-contraction ratio (step 7), with negative/positive controls (steps 9-10) isolating that this property buys the sparse-regime gain. The cluster's distinctive 'unlock something the original could not' (card step 4: manifold faithfulness the velocity-integral slot structurally forbids) is the stated payoff. What is NOT delivered is a formal preservation PROOF, but the card's signature explicitly permits the measurement alternative, which is present.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved one-step leaf achieves teacher-level (or better) single-step fidelity *without re-importing the multi-step machinery the one-step promise was meant to delete* (OneDP teacher, OFP EMA+curriculum, FlowPolicy self-consistency).","sub_pattern":"C12 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Substitute the per-stage aggregation/representation primitive for a classical-theorem-grounded surrogate occupying the same slot, demonstrating the surrogate unlocks a property the original slot structurally forbids while flipping a cost property.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"Same swap drives leg 2: because the projection target (nearest in-distribution action) is a direct data label, the supervision needs no teacher/EMA/self-consistency/curriculum — the subtraction is a native consequence of moving from 'integrate a learned velocity' to 'regress a single projection map', the exact aggregation-primitive substitution the cluster defines. The cost property flipped is the deletion of four learned objects.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"core_mechanism performs C12's distinctive aggregation-primitive substitution (interval-integral velocity operator -> idempotent metric-projection operator), names the required classical anchor (proximal/metric-projection / idempotent operator), and discharges the preservation obligation via the card-permitted MEASUREMENT branch (enforced idempotency penalty L_idem + measured kappa + controls) rather than the proof branch. Unlike the C30 spectral-proof-only family, C12 explicitly admits a gradient/curvature MEASUREMENT in lieu of a proof, so this is applied, not bypassed."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["architectural_operator_substitution","architectural_operator_substitution"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"Both gap_closure entries use the SAME main_pattern (architectural_operator_substitution); there is no second distinct pattern, so none of the three documented 2-way reject-favored compositions (all of which require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component) can match. No anti-pattern fires."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:ce65343fa59211c18b3f49f3d7422eaa818941a8","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"ABot-M0 (Action Manifold Learning) already publishes the candidate's headline framing in almost identical words: it proposes the 'Action Manifold Hypothesis' (effective robot actions lie on a low-dimensional smooth manifold) and an AML module whose stated move is that it 'shifts learning from denoising to projection onto feasible manifolds', predicting clean continuous action sequences directly with a DiT backbone. That is precisely the candidate's load-bearing reframing — 'one-step robot policies by manifold projection, not velocity integration' — so the candidate's hook claim of being the first to replace velocity-integration with manifold projection in a robot policy does NOT stand against ABot-M0; the candidate's novelty must instead rest on the parts ABot-M0 does NOT have: (1) an explicitly idempotent metric-projection OPERATOR with the second-forward-pass idempotency penalty as a load-bearing, measured property (kappa), and (2) the specific target of robust one-step fidelity under SPARSE conditional geometry, teacher-free and curriculum-free. ABot-M0 is a large multi-dataset VLA foundation model that uses manifold projection as an efficiency/stability device under data abundance, not an idempotent-projection operator audited for sparse-conditioning robustness, so it is a strong addressable threat to the FRAMING, not exact-mechanism overlap with the candidate's idempotent-operator claim. A secondary, mechanism-level threat is semanticscholar:0029547630e9b5393688094636883c13bcdec34c (Linearizer / the idempotent-generative-network lineage), which already collapses diffusion sampling into a single step by ENFORCING idempotency f(f(x))=f(x) to obtain a 'globally projective generative model' — the candidate's exact structural device — but in the image-generation domain with no robot-policy or sparse-conditioning claim, so the candidate must explicitly position its idempotency penalty as a port of a known generative-modeling device rather than a fresh invention.","addressable_via":"Tighten the hook and differentiation_from_lit to (a) drop or qualify the 'first to use manifold projection instead of velocity integration in a robot policy' claim now that ABot-M0 holds that framing, and (b) re-center novelty on the load-bearing idempotent metric-projection OPERATOR audited for sparse-conditional-geometry robustness (teacher/curriculum-free), adding an explicit delta vs ABot-M0 (AML predicts clean actions via a DiT under data abundance but has no enforced-idempotency operator and no sparse-regime robustness claim) and vs the Linearizer/idempotent-generative-network lineage (image-domain idempotent projective generation, not robot policy)."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"hook","issue":"paper_pointed_threat: ABot-M0 (semanticscholar:ce65343fa59211c18b3f49f3d7422eaa818941a8) already publishes the 'shift from denoising to projection onto feasible action manifolds' framing in a robot policy, so the hook's implicit first-to-use-manifold-projection-in-a-policy positioning is subsumed.","fix_direction":"Keep the load-bearing minimalism claim (strictly fewer learned objects: no teacher, no EMA, no self-consistency, no curriculum) which ABot-M0 does NOT match, but re-anchor the differentiator from 'manifold projection vs velocity integration' (now shared with ABot-M0) to the ENFORCED-IDEMPOTENCY metric-projection operator and its sparse-conditional-geometry robustness, since that operator + regime is what neither ABot-M0 nor the velocity-integral baselines provide."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat: missing deltas against (1) ABot-M0 / Action Manifold Learning (same projection-not-denoising framing) and (2) the Linearizer / idempotent-generative-network lineage (semanticscholar:0029547630e9b5393688094636883c13bcdec34c), which already enforces idempotency f(f(x))=f(x) to get a globally projective one-step generative model.","fix_direction":"Add a differentiation_from_lit entry for paper_id semanticscholar:ce65343fa59211c18b3f49f3d7422eaa818941a8 stating the delta: ABot-M0's AML predicts clean continuous action sequences via a DiT under multi-dataset abundance and frames projection as an efficiency/stability device, but has NO enforced-idempotency metric-projection operator and makes NO robust-one-step-under-sparse-conditioning claim; our contribution is the idempotent operator (with the second-forward-pass idempotency penalty as its load-bearing, measured property kappa) targeted exactly at sparse contact-rich/unseen-embodiment fidelity, teacher- and curriculum-free. Add a second entry for paper_id semanticscholar:0029547630e9b5393688094636883c13bcdec34c stating the delta: the Linearizer/idempotent-generative lineage already collapses sampling to one step via enforced idempotency in IMAGE generation; we port that structural device into robot action chunks and tie it to conditional-manifold projection under sparse conditioning, a setting and target that lineage does not address. Do NOT overclaim invention of idempotency-as-projection; position it as a known generative device newly load-bearing for sparse-conditional one-step policies."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"hook","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Re-anchored the hook's differentiator away from 'manifold projection vs velocity integration' (now shared with ABot-M0) onto the enforced-idempotency metric-projection operator and its sparse-conditional-geometry robustness, while keeping the load-bearing strictly-fewer-learned-objects minimalism claim intact."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added two differentiation_from_lit entries: vs ABot-M0/Action Manifold Learning (same projection-not-denoising framing but no enforced-idempotency operator and no sparse-regime robustness claim) and vs the Linearizer/idempotent-generative lineage (image-domain idempotent projective one-step generation, ported here to robot action chunks under sparse conditioning without overclaiming invention of idempotency-as-projection)."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# One-Step Robot Policies by Enforced-Idempotency Manifold Projection\n\n**Method.** Enforced-Idempotency Projection Policy (EIPP)\n\n## Motivation\nRobot policies that copy human demonstrations often generate an action by running a generator many times in a row — tens to hundreds of forward passes — which is slow and limits how fast the robot can react. The recent fix is to make the generator produce a good action in a single pass. But every current single-pass method has to bolt on extra machinery to make that one jump work: One-Step Diffusion Policy (OneDP) needs a fully-trained multi-step 'teacher' to copy; One-Step Flow Policy (OFP) needs a slowly-updated copy of itself (an EMA, exponential moving average) plus a hand-tuned schedule; and FlowPolicy needs an extra 'self-consistency' rule on its velocity field. Worse, the single jump tends to miss when the data is thin — few demonstrations, contact-rich tasks, or a robot body it has not seen — because the jump has to memorise a path it never observed.\n\nWhat makes this solvable now is two recent ideas. Researchers have shown you can collapse a many-step generator into one step by enforcing 'idempotency' — applying the map twice gives the same result as once, f(f(x)) = f(x) — which turns the map into a clean projection (in image generation, the Linearizer / idempotent-generative-network line). Separately, a robot model called ABot-M0 reframed action generation as projecting onto a 'feasible action manifold' instead of denoising, but it did this only under huge data and never enforced idempotency or targeted the thin-data regime.\n\nThe gap each prior method leaves: OFP and FlowPolicy still integrate a velocity field, which is undefined where demonstrations are sparse; OneDP can never beat its teacher and needs one to exist; and Implicit Drifting Policy (IDP) tries to recover the missing correction by estimating local geometry from nearby demonstrations, which itself falls apart when neighbours are scarce.\n\nIf we close this gap, a robot can produce a reliable action in a single pass even on hard, low-data tasks, with none of the teacher / EMA / schedule / self-consistency scaffolding — making one-step control a property guaranteed by how the operator is built, not a speed-versus-quality trade.\n\n## Method\n### Direct-target reconstruction (scaffold deletion)\n*Supervise the operator with the data action as its own projection target, deleting teacher / EMA / self-consistency / curriculum at once.*\n\n1. First decide the units the actions live in: rescale each action dimension so that, across all training demonstrations, it has zero mean and unit spread (zero mean, unit variance, or equivalently rescaled into the range [-1, 1]). Save this rescaling so you can undo it later at execution time. Working in these rescaled units means the corruption radius $sigma_{0} = 1.0$ is exactly one standard deviation of the action distribution. Now build the corruption step: for each demonstration (observation o, action chunk a), pick one random corruption size eta uniformly between 0 and $sigma_{0},$ draw standard Gaussian noise xi of the same shape as the action chunk (each element independent), and form the corrupted chunk $a_{tilde} = a +$ eta times xi. This is the only source of randomness, and eta is drawn fresh for each sample — it is not a hand-tuned schedule.\n   - _Why_: Corrupting at many sizes teaches the operator to snap back to a good action even from far away, not just to clean up tiny wobbles.\n2. Push the corrupted chunk through the operator, $a_{hat} = P_{theta}(a_{tilde} |$ o), and train it to match the real demonstration action by minimising the squared error $L_{rec} = || a_{hat} - a ||^{2}$ (Eq. (1)), averaged per element over the whole $H x d_{a}$ chunk and over the batch (this per-element averaging keeps the loss the same scale no matter how long the chunk is). The target is just the data action a itself, read straight from the demonstration in the same rescaled units from the previous step. Because the right answer is the demonstration, you never need a separate teacher network, a slowly-updated copy of the model (an exponential moving average, EMA), or a self-consistency rule to supply the target.\n\n*The reconstruction loss regresses the projection of a corrupted action chunk onto the data action a, with corruption scale $\\eta $ drawn uniformly on (0, $\\sigma _{0})$ — making the data action its own projection target so no teacher or EMA is needed.*\n$$ \\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{rec}} = \\mathbb{E}_{(o,a),\\,\\eta\\sim\\mathcal{U}(0,\\sigma_0),\\,\\xi\\sim\\mathcal{N}(0,I)}\\big[\\, \\lVert P_\\theta(a + \\eta\\,\\xi \\mid o) - a \\rVert^2 \\,\\big] \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Because the right answer is the demonstration itself, you never need a teacher, an EMA copy, or a self-consistency rule to supply the target.\n\n### Time-free projection operator\n*Replace the velocity-integration aggregation primitive with a single feed-forward map that projects a corrupted action chunk onto the conditional action manifold.*\n\n3. Start from the action-generation network of a standard flow-matching robot policy — concretely the action-head backbone (a Diffusion Transformer, DiT, or a U-Net) that the baseline you are comparing against uses, kept at the same size and the same action-chunk length H so it has the same capacity. Remove the part of the network that reads in a time index: delete the small time-embedding network and the term it added into the network's conditioning, but leave the way the network reads the observation completely unchanged (in a DiT this is the modulation that scales and shifts the features; in a U-Net it is the observation feature-injection). Do not add any new input pathway. After this change the network takes two things in — a corrupted action chunk $a_{tilde}$ of shape $H x d_{a},$ and the observation o — and outputs a cleaned action chunk $a_{hat}$ of the same shape. Keep the observation encoder and the action head; only the 'integrate a velocity over time' part is replaced by the projection operator $P_{theta}.$\n   - _Why_: The time index only exists to integrate a velocity; once you land by projection instead of transport, the time index is dead weight.\n\n### Enforced idempotency\n*Add the second-forward-pass idempotency penalty that turns the regressor into a genuine projection so one shot lands from a wide corruption radius.*\n\n4. On the same batch, run the operator a second time on its own output and minimise $L_{idem} = || P_{theta}(a_{hat} |$ o) $- a_{hat} ||^{2}$ (Eq. (2)), averaged per element exactly like the first loss, so that applying $P_{theta}$ twice gives the same result as once. Enforce this on the same corrupted inputs you already drew this batch (whose corruption sizes already reach the full radius up to $sigma_{0}),$ so it directly covers the large-noise inputs you will see at test time. Treat the first output $a_{hat}$ as a fixed target when computing this second loss — that is, stop gradients from flowing back through the first application — so the penalty pulls the second pass toward reproducing the first output 【author decision: whether to stop gradients on the inner output $a_{hat}$ — keeping it fixed gives the clean 'apply-twice-equals-once' meaning, whereas letting gradients flow through both applications lets the two passes adjust together and can collapse both outputs toward something trivial】. Forcing 'apply twice = apply once' makes the map a genuine projection, so a single pass from large noise still lands on the manifold instead of only cleaning up small noise.\n\n*The idempotency penalty forces a second application of $P_{theta}$ to leave its own output unchanged $(P_{theta} o P_{theta} = P_{theta}$ on the manifold), so the map is a genuine projection that lands from a wide corruption radius, not a small-corruption denoiser.*\n$$ \\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{idem}} = \\mathbb{E}_{o}\\big[\\, \\lVert P_\\theta\\big(P_\\theta(\\tilde a \\mid o)\\,\\big|\\,o\\big) - P_\\theta(\\tilde a \\mid o) \\rVert^2 \\,\\big] \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Forcing 'apply twice = apply once' makes the map a genuine projection, so a single pass from large noise still lands on the manifold instead of only denoising small noise.\n5. Add the two losses into one objective, $L = L_{rec} + lambda_{idem}$ times $L_{idem}$ (Eq. (3)), with the weight $lambda_{idem} = 0.1$; because both losses use the same per-element averaging, this weight is a clean ratio between them. Train with ordinary Adam — no slowly-updated model copy (no exponential moving average, EMA), no separate teacher network, and no time-schedule sampler. For the optimiser settings (learning rate and its schedule, batch size, number of training steps, weight decay), copy whatever the baseline flow-matching policy used, since the network is the same size and the point is to isolate the change of operator; if no baseline config is available, a workable default is Adam with learning rate 1e-4, batch size 256, and no weight decay. The only method-specific knobs are the corruption radius $sigma_{0}$ and the idempotency weight $lambda_{idem}.$\n\n*Total objective: reconstruction plus the idempotency penalty weighted by $\\lambda _{idem}$ (default 0.1), optimised by Adam with no EMA copy, no teacher network, and no time-schedule sampler.*\n$$ \\mathcal{L} = \\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{rec}} + \\lambda_{\\mathrm{idem}}\\,\\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{idem}} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This is the whole training loop — it carries one new object (the idempotency term) and none of the four objects the other one-step methods need.\n\n### Single-pass inference\n*Emit the action chunk in one forward pass with no ODE, time index, or schedule.*\n\n6. At test time, draw a single Gaussian sample $a_{tilde}$ from N(0, $sigma_{0}^{2}$ I), run the operator exactly once to get $a_{hat} = P_{theta}(a_{tilde} |$ o), then undo the action rescaling from step step 1 (First decide the units the $actions\\dots )$ to bring $a_{hat}$ back into real action units, and send that action chunk to the robot using the same execution protocol the baseline uses on that benchmark (the standard action-chunk execution: either play the whole chunk for its horizon before re-planning, or re-plan every few steps as the baseline does). There is no iterative solver, no time index, and no schedule — it is a single forward pass (one network evaluation, NFE=1), and that single Gaussian draw is the only randomness at test time.\n   - _Why_: A single application of a true projection already lands on a good action, so no iteration is needed.\n\n### Mechanism audit and controls\n*Measure the contraction ratio $\\kappa $ and run the target-randomisation and idempotency-off controls to attribute the sparse-regime gain to projecting onto the correct manifold.*\n\n7. Measure the idempotency-contraction ratio kappa (Eq. (4)) on held-out observations, computing it at the same kind of input the policy actually faces at test time — $a_{tilde}$ drawn from N(0, $sigma_{0}^{2}$ I) — using a fixed number of draws per held-out observation (default 16) and averaging over the whole held-out set; use the same per-element averaging in the top and bottom of the ratio so kappa is a clean scale-free number between 0 and 1 where smaller means a tighter projection. Then run two controls. Negative control: retrain the model but swap the target action for a randomly chosen demonstration action from elsewhere in the same batch (reshuffled fresh every training step), which keeps the overall mix of actions right but breaks the link between observation and the correct action; train it for the same number of steps with the same settings, and watch the success rate on the thin-data (sparse) splits collapse even though the map is still idempotent. Positive control: retrain with the idempotency term turned off $(lambda_{idem} =$ 0) to see how much of the thin-data robustness the idempotency/projection property specifically provides.\n\n*The idempotency-contraction ratio $\\kappa ,$ measured on held-out observations, is the load-bearing variable: a low $\\kappa $ certifies that $P_{theta}$ is a near-genuine projection (a second pass barely moves the output relative to the first projection step).*\n$$ \\kappa = \\mathbb{E}_{o}\\,\\frac{\\lVert P_\\theta\\big(P_\\theta(\\tilde a \\mid o)\\,\\big|\\,o\\big) - P_\\theta(\\tilde a \\mid o) \\rVert}{\\lVert P_\\theta(\\tilde a \\mid o) - \\tilde a \\rVert} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: $\\kappa $ certifies the map really is a projection, and the controls prove the gain comes from projecting onto the CORRECT manifold, not merely from being idempotent.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 用强制幂等的流形投影实现单步机器人策略\n\n**方法名称.** Enforced-Idempotency Projection Policy (EIPP)\n\n## 研究动机\n模仿人类示范的机器人策略，常常要把一个生成器连跑很多遍（几十到上百次前向传播）才能产生一个动作，这很慢、限制了机器人的反应频率。最近的做法是让生成器一次就给出好动作。但现有的单步方法都得额外加装机制来让这一步成立：OneDP（One-Step Diffusion Policy）需要一个训练好的多步 teacher 来模仿；OFP（One-Step Flow Policy）需要一个缓慢更新的自身副本（EMA，exponential moving average）外加手调的时间调度；FlowPolicy 则需要对速度场加一条额外的 self-consistency 规则。更糟的是，当数据稀疏时——示范少、接触密集、或没见过的机器人形态——这一跳常常落空，因为它必须记住一条从未观测过的路径。\n\n现在能解决这个问题，靠的是两个新近思路。研究者已证明：通过强制 idempotency（幂等：映射施加两次等于一次，f(f(x)) = f(x)）可以把多步生成器压缩到一步，使该映射变成一个干净的投影（图像生成里的 Linearizer / idempotent-generative-network 路线）。另外，机器人模型 ABot-M0 把动作生成重新表述为投影到「可行动作流形」而非去噪，但它只在海量数据下这么做，既没强制 idempotency，也没瞄准稀疏数据这一区间。\n\n各方法各自留下的缺口：OFP 和 FlowPolicy 仍在积分一个速度场，而该积分在示范稀疏处没有定义；OneDP 永远超不过它的 teacher，且必须先有一个 teacher；IDP（Implicit Drifting Policy）试图用邻近示范估计局部几何来补回缺失的修正，但邻居稀少时它自己就崩了。\n\n若补上这个缺口，机器人即使在困难、低数据的任务上也能一次产生可靠动作，且完全不需要 teacher / EMA / 调度 / self-consistency 这些脚手架——让单步控制成为由算子构造方式保证的性质，而非速度与质量之间的权衡。\n\n## 方法\n### 直接目标重构（删除脚手架）\n*用数据动作本身作为投影目标来监督算子，一举删除 teacher / EMA / self-consistency / curriculum。*\n\n1. 先确定动作所在的单位：把每一个动作维度做归一化，使其在全部训练示范上均值为 0、尺度为 1（零均值单位方差，或等价地缩放到 [-1, 1] 区间）。保存这个归一化变换，以便稍后在执行时还原。在这套归一化单位下，扰动半径 $sigma_{0} = 1.0$ 恰好等于动作分布的一个标准差。然后构造扰动步骤：对每个示范（观测 o、动作块 a），在 0 到 $sigma_{0}$ 之间均匀地取一个扰动尺度 eta，采一个与动作块同形状的标准高斯噪声 xi（每个元素相互独立），构造被扰动动作块 $a_{tilde} = a +$ eta 乘以 xi。这是唯一的随机来源，且 eta 对每个样本现取，不是手调的调度表。\n   - _为什么_: 在多种尺度上扰动，能教会算子即使从很远处也能弹回到好动作，而不只是清理微小抖动。\n2. 把被扰动的动作块送入算子，$a_{hat} = P_{theta}(a_{tilde} |$ o)，训练它去匹配真实示范动作，最小化平方误差 $L_{rec} = || a_{hat} - a ||^{2}$（式 (1)）；该误差在整个 $H x d_{a}$ 动作块的所有元素上、以及在 batch 上做逐元素平均（这种逐元素平均使损失尺度与动作块长度无关）。目标就是数据动作 a 本身，直接以上一步的归一化单位从示范中读取。因为正确答案就是示范本身，所以你不需要单独的 teacher 网络、不需要模型的缓慢更新副本（exponential moving average，EMA），也不需要 self-consistency（自洽）规则来提供目标。\n\n*重构损失让被扰动动作块经 $P_{theta}$ 投影后回归到数据动作 a，扰动尺度 $\\eta $ 在 (0, $\\sigma _{0})$ 上均匀采样；数据动作本身即投影目标，因而无需 teacher 或 EMA。*\n$$ \\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{rec}} = \\mathbb{E}_{(o,a),\\,\\eta\\sim\\mathcal{U}(0,\\sigma_0),\\,\\xi\\sim\\mathcal{N}(0,I)}\\big[\\, \\lVert P_\\theta(a + \\eta\\,\\xi \\mid o) - a \\rVert^2 \\,\\big] \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 因为正确答案就是示范本身，所以无需 teacher、EMA 副本或 self-consistency 规则来提供目标。\n\n### 无时间索引的投影算子\n*用一个单次前向映射替换速度积分这一聚合原语，将被扰动动作块投影到条件动作流形上。*\n\n3. 从一个标准 flow-matching 机器人策略的动作生成网络出发——具体就是你要对比的 baseline 所用的 action-head 主干（一个 Diffusion Transformer (DiT) 或一个 U-Net），保持相同规模和相同动作块长度 H，使其容量与被替换的算子一致。去掉网络中读入时间索引的部分：删除那个很小的 time-embedding 子网络以及它加进网络条件通路里的那一项，但完全保留网络读取观测的方式不变（在 DiT 里就是对特征做缩放与平移的那条调制通路；在 U-Net 里就是观测特征注入）。不要新增任何输入通路。改完后，网络输入两样东西——形状为 $H x d_{a}$ 的被扰动动作块 $a_{tilde}$，以及观测 o——输出同形状的干净动作块 $a_{hat}$。保留观测编码器和 action head，只把「按时间积分速度」这部分换成投影算子 $P_{theta}$。\n   - _为什么_: 时间索引存在的唯一目的就是积分速度；一旦改为靠投影落位而非靠 transport，时间索引就成了多余负担。\n\n### 强制幂等\n*加入第二次前向的幂等惩罚，把回归器变成真正的投影，使一步即可从较大扰动半径落位。*\n\n4. 在同一 batch 上，对算子的输出再施加一次算子，最小化 $L_{idem} = || P_{theta}(a_{hat} |$ o) $- a_{hat} ||^{2}$（式 (2)），与第一个损失一样做逐元素平均，使得施加两次 $P_{theta}$ 与施加一次结果相同。这一约束施加在你本 batch 已采的同一批被扰动输入上（其扰动尺度已覆盖到 $sigma_{0}$ 的全半径），因而直接覆盖测试时会遇到的大噪声输入。计算这第二个损失时，把第一次的输出 $a_{hat}$ 当作固定目标——也就是阻断梯度回传穿过第一次施加（stop-gradient）——使惩罚把第二次前向拉向复现第一次的输出【作者需决定：是否对内层输出 $a_{hat}$ 阻断梯度——固定它能得到干净的「施加两次=施加一次」语义；而让梯度同时穿过两次施加，会让两次前向一起调整，可能把两个输出一起塌缩到平凡解】。强制「施加两次=施加一次」使该映射成为真正的投影，于是从大噪声出发的一次前向也能落在流形上，而不仅是清理小噪声。\n\n*幂等惩罚要求第二次施加 $P_{theta}$ 不再改变其输出（在流形上 $P_{theta} o P_{theta} = P_{theta}$），使该映射成为真正的投影，可从较大扰动半径一步落位，而非仅做小扰动去噪。*\n$$ \\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{idem}} = \\mathbb{E}_{o}\\big[\\, \\lVert P_\\theta\\big(P_\\theta(\\tilde a \\mid o)\\,\\big|\\,o\\big) - P_\\theta(\\tilde a \\mid o) \\rVert^2 \\,\\big] \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 强制「施加两次 = 施加一次」让映射成为真正的投影，于是从大噪声出发的一次前向也能落在流形上，而不仅是去掉小噪声。\n5. 把两个损失合成一个目标，$L = L_{rec} + lambda_{idem}$ 乘以 $L_{idem}$（式 (3)），权重 $lambda_{idem} = 0.1$；因为两个损失都用相同的逐元素平均，这个权重就是它们之间一个干净的比例。用普通 Adam 训练——没有缓慢更新的模型副本（exponential moving average，EMA）、没有单独的 teacher 网络、也没有时间调度采样器。优化器设置（学习率及其调度、batch size、训练步数、weight decay）直接照搬该 flow-matching baseline 所用的配置，因为网络规模相同，目的就是隔离「算子替换」这一变化；若没有可用的 baseline 配置，一个可行默认是 Adam、学习率 1e-4、batch size 256、不加 weight decay。本方法特有的可调旋钮只有扰动半径 $sigma_{0}$ 和幂等权重 $lambda_{idem}$。\n\n*总目标为重构损失加上权重 $\\lambda _{idem}$（默认 0.1）的幂等惩罚，用 Adam 优化，不含 EMA 副本、teacher 网络或时间调度采样器。*\n$$ \\mathcal{L} = \\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{rec}} + \\lambda_{\\mathrm{idem}}\\,\\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{idem}} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这就是全部训练循环——它只多带一个新对象（幂等项），而其他单步方法所需的四个对象一个都不带。\n\n### 单次前向推理\n*一次前向输出动作块，无 ODE、无时间索引、无调度。*\n\n6. 测试时，从 N(0, $sigma_{0}^{2}$ I) 采一个高斯样本 $a_{tilde}$，把算子恰好运行一次得到 $a_{hat} = P_{theta}(a_{tilde} |$ o)，然后撤销第 第1步（先确定动作所在的单位） 步的动作归一化，把 $a_{hat}$ 还原回真实动作单位，再用该 baseline 在此基准上所用的相同执行协议把动作块发给机器人（标准动作块执行：要么把整块按其时域开环执行后再重规划，要么像 baseline 那样每隔几步重规划一次）。没有迭代求解器、没有时间索引、没有调度——就是一次前向（一次网络评估，NFE=1），而那一次高斯采样是测试时唯一的随机来源。\n   - _为什么_: 对真正的投影施加一次就已落在好动作上，无需迭代。\n\n### 机制审计与对照\n*测量收缩比 $\\kappa $，并做目标随机化与关闭幂等两组对照，把稀疏区间的增益归因于投影到正确流形。*\n\n7. 在留出观测上测量幂等-收缩比 kappa（式 (4)），并在策略测试时实际面对的同类输入上计算它——即从 N(0, $sigma_{0}^{2}$ I) 采的 $a_{tilde}——$对每个留出观测用固定次数的采样（默认 16 次），再在整个留出集上平均；比值的分子分母用与损失相同的逐元素平均，使 kappa 成为 0 到 1 之间干净的无量纲数，越小表示投影越紧。然后做两个对照。负向对照：重训模型，但把目标动作换成同 batch 中别处随机选的一个示范动作（每个训练步都重新打乱），这样动作的总体分布仍然正确，却切断了观测与正确动作之间的关联；用相同步数、相同设置训练，观察稀疏（低数据）分割上的成功率崩塌，尽管该映射仍是幂等的。正向对照：关掉幂等项（$lambda_{idem} = 0$）重训，看幂等/投影性质究竟为低数据鲁棒性贡献了多少。\n\n*幂等-收缩比 $\\kappa $ 在留出观测上测量，是承重变量：$\\kappa $ 越小，越说明 $P_{theta}$ 接近真正的投影（相对首次投影位移，第二次施加几乎不再移动输出）。*\n$$ \\kappa = \\mathbb{E}_{o}\\,\\frac{\\lVert P_\\theta\\big(P_\\theta(\\tilde a \\mid o)\\,\\big|\\,o\\big) - P_\\theta(\\tilde a \\mid o) \\rVert}{\\lVert P_\\theta(\\tilde a \\mid o) - \\tilde a \\rVert} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: $\\kappa $ 证明该映射确实是投影，而对照实验证明增益来自投影到正确流形，而非仅仅是幂等。\n\n"},{"id":"76","run_dir":"run_prompt76_memagent","index":76,"title":"Retention by Read-Time Outcome: Counterfactual Credit for Long-Context Memory","title_zh":"按读取时结果保留记忆：面向长上下文记忆的反事实信用分配","method_name":"Read-time Utility Reward (RUR)","hook":"Every recent long-context memory keeps or evicts content using a write-time surrogate (LM loss, recency, similarity, hand-designed importance) that is structurally blind to the only event that reveals whether the choice was right — the later query that reads the content. We make the eviction policy learn from that future event directly, by manufacturing a preference signal from the counterfactual gap between answering a downstream query with versus without each retained item.","anchor_pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","anchor_pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","domain_category":"LLM Pretraining, Architecture & Scaling","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf scores its memory retain/evict/compress decision by the realized outcome of the future query that eventually reads the retained content — every leaf commits the decision using a write-time surrogate (LM loss, recency, hand-designed importance, or query-time similarity) and receives no signal when a discarded item turns out to have been decisive for a much-later read.","pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","sub_pattern":"C26 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by manufacturing a comparative retention-utility reward from a non-human source — the counterfactual gap in the realized downstream read outcome between keeping versus dropping each memory item — re-granularized from the end-of-answer scalar down to the individual write/evict decision via minimal-pair present-vs-absent rollouts, and consumed by a preference (DPO-style) objective that trains the eviction scorer directly on read-time outcome rather than on a write-time surrogate.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions the shared assumption inherited from every leaf — that the value of a stored memory item can be estimated at write time at all — rather than treating the item's value as a quantity that is only defined once a downstream consumer acts on it (the leaves all silently assume write-time scorability of memory utility).","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","how_closed":"Closed by naming the budgeted retain/evict rule's load-bearing assumption — that an item's utility is a write-time-computable scalar (importance/similarity/LM-gate) — and pivoting it to a read-time-defined quantity (utility is undefined until a query consumes the item); the companion controlled_diagnostic_design ships the confound-isolating separation: matched memory states in which the same budget is filled by a write-time-importance policy versus the read-time-outcome policy, holding retrieval, model, and budget fixed, isolating that the two policies disagree exactly on the distant-but-decisive items a later multi-hop query needs.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"long-context language modeling / memory mechanisms for LLMs","n_papers":38,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":26},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":10,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"InfLLM: Training-Free Long-Context Extrapolation for LLMs with an Efficient Context Memory"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"SinkLoRA: Enhanced Efficiency and Chat Capabilities for Long-Context Large Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Samba: Simple Hybrid State Space Models for Efficient Unlimited Context Language Modeling"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Mastering Long-Context Multi-Task Reasoning with Transformers and Recurrent Memory"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Needle in the Haystack for Memory Based Large Language Models"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Dementia prevention, intervention, and care: 2024 report of the Lancet standing Commission"}],"more":4},{"year":2025,"n":30,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Recurrent Memory-Augmented Transformers with Chunked Attention for Long-Context Language Modeling"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"DAM: Dynamic Attention Mask for Long-Context Large Language Model Inference Acceleration"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Memory-R1: Enhancing Large Language Model Agents to Manage and Utilize Memories via Reinforcement Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Long Context Modeling with Ranked Memory-Augmented Retrieval"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"ZeroMerge: Parameter-Free KV Cache Compression for Memory-Efficient Long-Context LLMs"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Every Token Counts: Generalizing 16M Ultra-Long Context in Large Language Models"}],"more":24},{"year":2026,"n":10,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Gated Sparse Attention: Combining Computational Efficiency with Training Stability for Long-Context Language Models"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"MKA: Memory-Keyed Attention for Efficient Long-Context Reasoning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"$π^2$: Structure-Originated Reasoning Data Improves Long-Context Reasoning Ability of Large Language Models"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"LPC-SM: Local Predictive Coding and Sparse Memory for Long-Context Language Modeling"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"G-MemLLM: Gated Latent Memory Augmentation for Long-Context Reasoning in Large Language Models"}],"more":4}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":15,"share":0.395},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":11,"share":0.289},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":10,"share":0.263},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":8,"share":0.211},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":6,"share":0.158},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":5,"share":0.132},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":4,"share":0.105},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":4,"share":0.105}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Across the recent long-context memory frontier, the decision of WHAT to commit to a bounded memory and WHAT to evict is severed in time from the only event that reveals whether that decision was correct — the future query that reads the retained content. Learned-gate memories such as G-MemLLM (arxiv:2602.00015v1) train their write/forget gate against next-token language-modeling loss at write time, so a slot is kept because it lowers immediate prediction loss, not because a downstream question will need it dozens of thousands of tokens later; retrieval-ranked memories such as ERMAR (semanticscholar:9be42c52b6c3696f5d30fc0c5d135b6a6cc1cc88) and parameter-free KV compressors such as ZeroMerge (semanticscholar:abe82cb842c5acf2ff227171251b477de55f39e4) substitute a hand-designed importance/relevance proxy (similarity, head-level token-importance metrics) for that future utility, and MKA (arxiv:2603.20586v2) still leaves the eviction/refresh of its learned memory keys to a heuristic. Because the retained-vs-evicted choice is scored by a write-time surrogate rather than by the realized read-time outcome, a token that is uninformative to local prediction but pivotal to a much-later multi-hop query is discarded with no signal that this was an error — and Context Length Alone Hurts LLM Performance Despite Perfect Retrieval (openalex:W4416034014) shows the resulting degradation is not explained by retrieval quality, implying the lost quantity is which content was retained, not how it was looked up.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.00015v1","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"G-MemLLM augments a frozen LLM with a trainable bank of fixed latent memory slots and a learned gate that compresses hidden states into slots and decides what persists. Its gate is optimized against next-token LM loss at the moment of writing, so it has no mechanism to learn that a slot was worth keeping because a query forty-thousand tokens later succeeded or failed — the write decision is never credit-assigned to the downstream read outcome it ultimately determines."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:9be42c52b6c3696f5d30fc0c5d135b6a6cc1cc88","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"ERMAR stores chunk-level KV pairs in a memory bank and reranks retrieved candidates by a relevance scorer at query time. The relevance signal is a static semantic-similarity ranking computed independently of whether retrieving that chunk actually changed the answer, so a chunk that looks similar but is unhelpful (or one that looks dissimilar but is decisive) is ranked by appearance, not by realized contribution to the read-time outcome."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:abe82cb842c5acf2ff227171251b477de55f39e4","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"ZeroMerge does parameter-free KV-cache compression using multi-dimensional, head-level token-importance metrics plus a residual merge. The importance metric is hand-designed and fixed in advance, so it cannot adapt to the fact that which tokens matter is query-dependent and only revealed when a later query reads them; tokens are merged/dropped by a write-time heuristic with no read-time feedback."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2603.20586v2","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"MKA keys a hierarchical (L1/L2/L3) memory and routes queries to levels to cut KV-attention cost. The keys are learned but the eviction/refresh policy across levels remains heuristic, so promotion/demotion of content between tiers is decided by a routing proxy rather than by whether attending to that tier improved the eventual answer."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416034014","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"This diagnostic shows long context degrades LLM accuracy even when retrieval is perfect, isolating a failure that is not about lookup. It stops at the observation: it does not identify that the controllable lever is the retain/evict policy whose errors are invisible at write time, nor does it propose a mechanism that scores retention by realized read-time outcome."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"long-context language modeling / memory mechanisms for LLMs","venue":"ICLR 2026","time":"2026","data":["long-context QA / multi-hop benchmarks (e.g. needle-in-haystack, RULER-style)","multi-session dialogue (memory-management)","long-document language modeling corpora (PG19/Books-style)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher comfortable with transformer internals, KV-cache, light RL/credit-assignment","preference":"both","baseline":"gated/learned memory writes & retrieval (G-MemLLM, MKA, ERMAR), KV-cache compression by hand-designed importance (ZeroMerge), recurrent FIFO memory (Recurrent Memory-Augmented Transformers), RAG-style external memory (Mem0, Memory-R1)","limitation":"memory write / keep / evict decisions are made by a proxy signal (recency, similarity, hand-designed importance, or a gate trained on next-token LM loss) that is never tied to whether the retained content actually serves the later query that consumes it","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared question both legs attack is: can the keep/evict decision in a bounded long-context memory be governed by the realized outcome of the future read instead of a write-time surrogate? The central object is the Read-time Utility Reward (RUR) of a memory item m_i with respect to a downstream query q: RUR(m_i, q) = s(A | M) - s(A | M \\ {m_i}), where M is the bounded memory state at read time, A is the gold answer span (or label) for q, and s(A | M) is the model's realized read-time outcome score for that answer conditioned on memory M — concretely the length-normalized log-probability the FROZEN base LLM assigns to the gold answer when its context is the working window plus the retrieved subset of M (s in [-inf,0], a model-internal readout, not an external oracle). RUR is thus a counterfactual: it is positive when keeping m_i raised the chance of the correct read and ~0 when m_i was irrelevant; it is undefined until q acts on M, which is exactly the read-time-defined utility the audit leg pivots to. LEG 1 (anchor, C26): because we cannot label each item's worth absolutely but CAN rank items by their RUR, we manufacture a comparative signal — for a sampled (long document, query) pair we form minimal pairs (M with m_i, M without m_i) sharing an otherwise-identical memory state, compute RUR for each candidate item by a second forward pass, and train a small eviction scorer g_phi(m_i) (a 2-layer MLP on the item's mean KV/hidden summary h_i in R^d, d = backbone hidden size, plus a recency scalar and the item's max prior retrieval count) with a pairwise preference loss L = -log sigma(beta(g_phi(m_i^+) - g_phi(m_i^-))) over pairs ranked by RUR, beta=0.1 a fixed temperature; at inference, when the budget B is exceeded the policy evicts the lowest-g_phi items. This closes gap 1 because the eviction criterion is now the read-outcome preference, a quantity no leaf produces. LEG 2 (sibling, C11 + companion controlled_diagnostic_design): we name the assumption baked into every budgeted retain/evict rule — that utility is a write-time scalar (ZeroMerge's head-level importance, ERMAR's similarity rank, G-MemLLM's LM-loss gate) — and pivot it to RUR's read-time definition; the companion ships the diagnostic separation by constructing matched states where the SAME budget B is filled by a write-time-importance policy versus the g_phi policy with retrieval/model/B all held fixed, and reporting the disagreement set D = items kept by one policy and evicted by the other, then measuring downstream answer accuracy attributable to D. The two legs share the RUR object: leg 1 trains on it, leg 2 audits with it; this is one paper, not two, because the manufactured signal IS the operationalization of the inverted assumption. Quantitative grounding: G-MemLLM (arxiv:2602.00015v1) trains its gate against next-token LM loss and reports no read-horizon-resolved eviction analysis; ERMAR (semanticscholar:9be42c52b6c3696f5d30fc0c5d135b6a6cc1cc88) ranks by static similarity; ZeroMerge (semanticscholar:abe82cb842c5acf2ff227171251b477de55f39e4) uses a fixed head-level importance metric — none computes a present-vs-absent counterfactual on the realized answer, so RUR is the new constructed quantity.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules: the audit leg's pivoted quantity (read-time-defined utility) is literally the RUR object the anchor leg trains on, so the diagnostic separation reuses g_phi and the present-vs-absent rollout already built for training — evidence that one object serves both, which is why they read as one paper under shared_question. (b) Alternatives considered and rejected: (i) an RL controller with end-of-answer reward (Memory-R1's shape) — rejected because its credit is the sparse end-of-dialogue scalar that cannot localize which write decision mattered, the exact residual we must beat; the minimal-pair counterfactual re-granularizes credit to the item, which a holistic RL reward cannot. (ii) a learned write-time importance regressor trained to predict RUR — rejected as it would re-collapse onto the write-time-scorability assumption the audit leg overturns. REGRESSION CHECK (method_lineage): the avoided node is c1 (eligibility traces / TD credit) and n7 (G-MemLLM's LM-loss gate); RUR is NOT a decaying eligibility trace over tokens and NOT a write-time prediction-loss surrogate — it is a per-item counterfactual on the REALIZED read outcome (presence-vs-absence on the gold answer), a source the lineage tree does not occupy, satisfying the occupied-source constraint Phase 2.1 recorded.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on a frozen ~7B LLM with a bounded KV/chunk memory at a fixed budget B, train the eviction scorer g_phi on counterfactual Read-time Utility Reward (RUR) preference pairs from a long-context multi-hop QA set (RULER-style + needle-in-haystack), and evaluate held-out long-context QA accuracy against three write-time-importance baselines (similarity rank, head-level token-importance, LM-loss gate) at the same B. If the candidate works, held-out answer accuracy increases over all three baselines and the margin GROWS with the read horizon (the token distance between a decisive item and the query that needs it), because distant-but-decisive items are exactly what write-time surrogates discard. The named load-bearing variable is RUR (the per-item present-vs-absent counterfactual on the gold answer's log-prob); the negative control re-trains g_phi on label-permuted RUR (each item's counterfactual scored against a shuffled gold answer), and the prediction is that downstream long-context QA accuracy collapses back to the write-time-importance baseline — if accuracy stays high under permuted RUR, the gain came from extra fine-tuning/capacity, not from read-time outcome credit. A positive control retains items by oracle RUR ranking alone (no learned scorer) and should recover most of the accuracy gain, identifying RUR as the mechanism.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.00015v1","delta":"G-MemLLM trains its write/forget gate against next-token LM loss at write time; we construct RUR, a per-item counterfactual on the realized downstream answer log-prob, and train the eviction scorer on read-time outcome preferences that its loss never sees."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:9be42c52b6c3696f5d30fc0c5d135b6a6cc1cc88","delta":"ERMAR ranks retrieved chunks by static semantic similarity; we replace appearance-based ranking with a measured present-vs-absent contribution to the correct answer, so an item dissimilar but decisive outranks a similar but useless one."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:abe82cb842c5acf2ff227171251b477de55f39e4","delta":"ZeroMerge evicts/merges KV by a fixed hand-designed head-level importance metric computed at write time; we make the eviction criterion a learned scorer trained on read-time counterfactual outcomes, and supply the diagnostic separation showing the two disagree on exactly the long-horizon items."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:9df0947ec8a14c43e69f3b72ece5e9af2b8e8215","delta":"Memory-R1 uses a sparse end-of-dialogue RL reward over natural-language agent memory; we re-granularize credit to the individual KV/chunk write decision via minimal-pair counterfactual rollouts, localizing which item mattered rather than rewarding the whole trajectory."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:9df0947ec8a14c43e69f3b72ece5e9af2b8e8215","what_step_was_missed":"Memory-R1 learns memory add/update/delete operations from a reward, but its reward is the end-of-dialogue answer scalar applied to natural-language agent memory; the step it never constructed is a per-item counterfactual (present-vs-absent on the realized gold-answer log-prob) over the internal KV/chunk retention state, which is what re-granularizes the sparse trajectory reward into an item-level retention-utility signal and lets the eviction scorer be credit-assigned to the specific write decision rather than the whole episode."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":238,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"No hard-floor rule fires: gap_closure_reject_check is borderline (not triggered) on both entries, anti_pattern_check matched_pattern_id is null, and the paper_pointed_threat is NOT exact-mechanism overlap (ForesightKV's golden target is future-attention scores, the candidate's RUR is an answer-outcome counterfactual). Soft judgment selects revise because the threat (arxiv:2602.03203v2) is addressable via a specific candidate field — differentiation_from_lit — and it hits a load-bearing surface (the novelty of the supervisory target), so per the 'paper_pointed_threat exists AND addressable_via names a specific candidate field' heuristic the candidate must explicitly differentiate from ForesightKV; the recipe_application_check.entries[1].verdict=borderline on C11 is left as a Phase-4 reviewer concern, not a revision target, since the empirical-separation substitution was the declared companion design.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf scores its memory retain/evict/compress decision by the realized outcome of the future query that eventually reads the retained content — every leaf commits the decision using a write-time surrogate (LM loss, recency, hand-designed importance, or query-time similarity) and receives no signal when a discarded item turns out to have been decisive for a much-later read.","main_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","sub_pattern":"C26 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The dominant failure is the single-component swap: take the established preference pipeline and change exactly one slot (human labels to AI judge, response-level to step-level granularity) then present that swap as the contribution; a second shape is stopping at the preference dataset without demonstrating the downstream optimization it is meant to feed.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Swapping the preference-label source (human → AI judge, offline → online) without showing the swap unlocks a behavior previously unreachable reads as a one-component substitution and draws novelty rejections.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate does not merely swap the label source; it introduces a new label QUANTITY (RUR = present-vs-absent counterfactual on the realized gold-answer log-prob) that no eviction pipeline computes, and shows it unlocks a previously-unreachable behavior (eviction whose accuracy gain grows with read horizon)."},{"lesson_quoted":"Changing only the granularity of an established contrastive objective (response-level → step-level) is judged incremental unless paired with a clearly demonstrated practical unlock.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The candidate does re-granularize credit from end-of-answer scalar to per-item, which by itself is the flagged move; it is paired with the read-horizon unlock and the assumption pivot, so it is borderline rather than triggered, but Phase 4 must keep the unlock front-and-center."},{"lesson_quoted":"Stopping at the preference dataset, benchmark, or reward model without demonstrating the downstream optimization it is meant to feed leaves the contribution looking like infrastructure rather than method.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism_steps train g_phi and deploy it as the inference-time eviction policy with downstream-accuracy and negative/positive controls, so the loop is closed to the end metric, not stopped at the dataset."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions the shared assumption inherited from every leaf — that the value of a stored memory item can be estimated at write time at all — rather than treating the item's value as a quantity that is only defined once a downstream consumer acts on it (the leaves all silently assume write-time scorability of memory utility).","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The dominant failure is substituting one selection rule for another that performs better empirically while omitting the theorem that explains when and why it wins; a second shape is pivoting an assumption the community regards as a reasonable modeling choice rather than a genuine restriction.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Substituting one selection heuristic for another without a theorem stating when and why it wins reads as an engineering combination, not a contribution, no matter how clean the empirical gain.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The anchor is a method contribution and Phase 2.1 deliberately paired C11 with controlled_diagnostic_design to ship a confound-isolating empirical separation (the disagreement set D + horizon sweep) in place of a theorem; this is legitimate for a method paper but means the 'when/why it wins' is shown empirically (horizon-resolved) rather than proved, so it is borderline."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pivoting an assumption the community treats as a reasonable modeling choice — rather than first proving it a genuine restriction — leaves both motivation and novelty in doubt.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The diagnostic leg explicitly demonstrates the write-time-scorability assumption is a genuine restriction by isolating the disagreement set D and measuring the downstream accuracy attributable to it, proving the assumption is load-bearing rather than benign."},{"lesson_quoted":"Unlocking a new capability by violating an assumption while ignoring a protective property it guarded — detectability, validity, identifiability — invites rejection on the overlooked side effect rather than the headline result.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The read-time-outcome policy does not abandon a property the write-time rule protected (it keeps the same budget B, retrieval, and frozen backbone); the only thing it changes is the scoring criterion, surfaced and ablated explicitly."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No gap_closure entry is triggered. The C26 anchor entry is borderline on the 'granularity-change-only' lesson and the C11 sibling entry is borderline on the 'no theorem' lesson; both are mitigated (read-horizon unlock for C26; empirical confound-isolating separation for C11) so neither rises to triggered, but both touch load-bearing surfaces and feed the soft verdict."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf scores its memory retain/evict/compress decision by the realized outcome of the future query that eventually reads the retained content...","sub_pattern":"C26 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Manufacture a comparative or scalar reward from a non-human source, harvest a source that already encodes the comparison, re-granularize the comparison to match where credit assignment fails, then optimize the target with a contrastive/preference objective rather than label-fitting.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism step 'we form minimal pairs (M with m_i, M without m_i)... compute RUR... train g_phi with a pairwise preference loss L = -log sigma(beta(g_phi(m_i^+) - g_phi(m_i^-)))' performs exactly the harvest-comparison + re-granularize-credit + preference-objective signature move; the non-human source is the model's own realized read outcome.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions the shared assumption inherited from every leaf — that the value of a stored memory item can be estimated at write time at all...","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Center on a selection/acquisition/retention rule, name the ONE assumption baked into its criterion or required structure, and pivot it (relax or reframe) with a re-derived performance certificate that matches or beats the pre-pivot baseline.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism names the budgeted retain/evict rule's assumption (utility is a write-time scalar: importance/similarity/LM-gate) and pivots it to RUR's read-time definition; the C11 'certificate' is realized as the companion controlled_diagnostic_design's confound-isolating separation (disagreement set D + horizon-resolved accuracy) rather than a formal regret bound, which is the intended companion delivery for a method contribution but is empirical not theoretical — hence borderline rather than fully applied.","verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The C26 anchor cleanly performs the manufacture-comparative-reward + re-granularize-credit + preference-objective signature. The C11 sibling performs the name-and-pivot-the-retention-rule's-assumption move but substitutes an empirical separation for C11's native re-derived certificate (legitimately, via the declared companion), making it borderline rather than bypassed."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["self_supervised_signal_engineering","assumption_audit_and_pivot","controlled_diagnostic_design"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; none of the candidate's three main/companion patterns is heterogeneous_decomposition, so no anti-pattern composition matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"arxiv:2602.03203v2","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"ForesightKV is the most specific competitor: it is a training-based KV-cache eviction framework that learns to predict which KV pairs to evict, builds a 'Golden Eviction' oracle target, and distills it with a Pairwise Ranking Loss plus GRPO — structurally the same shape as our preference-trained eviction scorer. The candidate's claim stands or falls on whether its supervisory target is genuinely distinct: ForesightKV's golden target is derived from FUTURE ATTENTION SCORES (which KV the model later attends to), which is still an internal-attention surrogate for importance, whereas RUR is a present-vs-absent COUNTERFACTUAL on the realized gold-answer log-prob (whether keeping the item actually changed the correct answer's probability). If a reviewer reads RUR as merely a relabeling of 'future attention contribution,' the contribution collapses into ForesightKV; the candidate must make the attention-surrogate-vs-outcome-counterfactual distinction explicit and ideally show a regime where the two disagree (an item the model attends to but that does not change the answer, vs. one it under-attends to but that is decisive). Sibling collision hits 'Make Each Token Count' (arxiv:2605.09649v1, learns each token's future utility, but with a query-agnostic geometric proxy) and 'Predicting Future Utility / LU-KV' (arxiv:2602.08585v2, head-level marginal long-horizon contribution via combinatorial optimization, offline profiling) crowd the same lane but are weaker threats because their utility is an attention/geometry proxy, not an answer-outcome counterfactual.","addressable_via":"Sharpen differentiation_from_lit to add ForesightKV (arxiv:2602.03203v2) with the explicit attention-surrogate-vs-outcome-counterfactual delta, and have the diagnostic leg report the attention-vs-RUR disagreement set so the distinction is empirically demonstrated rather than asserted."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat: ForesightKV (arxiv:2602.03203v2) is a training-based, pairwise-ranking-distilled KV eviction learner whose golden target is future attention scores — structurally the closest competitor and not currently cited.","fix_direction":"Add a differentiation_from_lit entry for arxiv:2602.03203v2 whose delta states the substantive distinction: ForesightKV distills a Golden-Eviction target derived from future ATTENTION scores (an internal-attention surrogate for importance) via Pairwise Ranking Loss + GRPO, whereas the candidate's RUR is a present-vs-absent COUNTERFACTUAL on the realized gold-answer log-prob — utility measured by whether keeping the item changed the correct answer, not by whether the model attended to it; note the regime where the two diverge (high-attention-but-answer-irrelevant vs low-attention-but-decisive items)."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism_steps","issue":"The diagnostic (leg 2) currently contrasts only against write-time-importance/similarity baselines; the strongest competitor (ForesightKV) uses a future-attention golden target, so the attention-vs-outcome distinction is asserted in differentiation but not demonstrated.","fix_direction":"Extend the diagnostic step to also compute the disagreement set between an attention-contribution eviction target (future-attention-score ranking, the ForesightKV-style signal) and the RUR ranking, and report downstream accuracy attributable to that disagreement set — making the attention-surrogate-vs-outcome-counterfactual distinction an empirical result rather than a framing claim. Do NOT modify falsification_prediction or compute_budget."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit[4].delta","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added a new differentiation_from_lit entry for arxiv:2602.03203v2 (ForesightKV) whose delta states the substantive distinction: ForesightKV distills a Golden-Eviction target from FUTURE ATTENTION SCORES via Pairwise Ranking Loss + GRPO, whereas RUR supervises eviction with a present-vs-absent COUNTERFACTUAL on the realized gold-answer log-prob, and names the regime where the two diverge (high-attention-but-answer-irrelevant vs low-attention-but-decisive items)."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism_steps","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Extended the diagnostic leg with an attention-vs-outcome step that builds a future-attention-contribution eviction target (the ForesightKV-style signal), computes its disagreement set D_attn against the RUR ranking, and reports downstream answer accuracy attributable to each so the attention-surrogate-vs-outcome-counterfactual distinction becomes an empirical result rather than a framing claim."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Retention by Read-Time Outcome: Counterfactual Credit for Long-Context Memory\n\n**Method.** Read-time Utility Reward (RUR)\n\n## Motivation\nA long-context language model can only hold so much in its working window, so it offloads older content into a bounded memory and must constantly decide what to keep and what to throw away. The problem is that it makes this keep-or-discard decision the moment the content arrives, using cheap stand-in signals — how recently the content appeared, how similar it looks to the current text, a hand-designed importance score, or how much it lowers the model's next-word prediction loss. None of these signals know whether the content will actually matter to a question the model is asked much later. So a fact that looks boring when it is written but turns out to be the key to a question forty-thousand words later gets thrown away, and nothing ever tells the system it made a mistake.\n\nThis is timely because researchers have just shown you can train a policy to decide what to evict from memory (for example ForesightKV, arXiv 2026), but they still judge an item by an internal proxy — how much the model later pays attention to it — rather than by whether keeping it actually changed the answer. Meanwhile, preference-style training (learning from 'A is better than B' comparisons, as in DPO, Direct Preference Optimization) is now routine, and adapting a frozen model is cheap enough that we can afford to run the model twice — once with an item, once without — to measure its true effect on the answer.\n\nPrior systems stopped short for concrete reasons. G-MemLLM (arXiv 2026-01) trains its keep/forget gate on next-word prediction loss because no signal about the later answer was available. ZeroMerge fixes its importance metric in advance, baking in the assumption that an item's worth can be judged at write time. Memory-R1 (arXiv 2025-08) does learn memory operations from a reward, but the reward only arrives at the very end of a conversation, so it cannot tell which specific item was responsible.\n\nWhen this gap closes, you get a memory-eviction policy whose keep/discard rule is the realized outcome of the later read itself, so the existing systems that rely on write-time guesses can be retrained against a signal they never had — and 'how useful is this memory item' stops being a guess made too early and becomes a quantity measured at the moment it is actually used.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n\n1. Take a frozen base large language model (LLM) with a bounded memory of key-value (KV) cache / chunk items and a budget B (a cap on how many items it can hold). Split each document into 256-token chunks; each chunk is one memory item. Describe each item by three things: the average of its token hidden states, how recently it was used (current position minus when it was written, divided by total length), and how many past queries pulled it up (a count). To read from memory, fetch the chunks most similar to the question by embedding cosine similarity, taking as many as fit in the budget.\n   - _Why_: These are the features a small policy can read to decide what to keep, without yet assuming anything about an item's worth.\n\n### Read-time Utility Reward (RUR) signal\n*Measure each memory item's true effect on the answer by a present-vs-absent counterfactual.*\n\n2. Build a set of (long document, question, gold answer) examples from long-context question answering (such as RULER multi-hop and needle-in-haystack). The gold answer is the labeled answer text, tokenized the same way as the model. The working window — the question plus any instruction — always stays in context and is never thrown away. Load the document into memory, run the model once on the question plus the retrieved memory, and record the length-normalized log-probability it assigns to the correct answer; call this the read-time outcome score.\n\n*The read-time outcome score is the length-normalized log-probability the frozen backbone assigns to the gold answer span A, conditioned on the working window W concatenated with the retrieved subset of memory M.*\n$$ s(A \\mid M) = \\frac{1}{|A|} \\sum_{t=1}^{|A|} \\log p_{\\theta}\\!\\left(A_t \\mid A_{<t}, \\, W \\oplus \\mathrm{Retr}(M)\\right) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This number is the model's own measure of how well it can answer right now, given everything in memory — the read-time outcome we want to optimize.\n3. For each question, pick 32 of the items the question actually retrieved. For each one, run the model again with just that item taken out of the retrieved set — refilling its slot with the next-best chunk so the amount of context stays the same — and subtract the two outcome scores. A large positive difference means that item genuinely helped the answer. 【author decision: when an item is removed, either refill its slot with the next-best chunk (keeping context length fixed) or leave it empty (keeping the rest of the kept-set fixed); these measure different things (the item's identity effect vs the value of the slot) and the authors must choose which one Read-time Utility Reward should capture.】\n\n*The Read-time Utility Reward of item $m_{i}$ for query q is the present-vs-absent gap in the realized gold-answer outcome score: how much keeping $m_{i}$ raised the chance of the correct read.*\n$$ \\mathrm{RUR}(m_i, q) = s(A \\mid M) - s(A \\mid M \\setminus \\{m_i\\}) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Running it both ways directly measures whether keeping the item changed the correct answer's probability — the true effect, not a guess.\n4. Within each example, sort items by their helpfulness score and pair a clearly-more-helpful item with a clearly-less-helpful one, keeping the rest of memory identical between the two. Only keep a pair when the gap is bigger than a small margin (0.02 in log-probability units) so you are not training on indistinguishable ties, and keep at most the 64 largest-gap pairs per example.\n   - _Why_: We cannot put an absolute price on an item, but we can reliably say one helped more than another — a comparison is the honest form of the signal.\n\n### Preference-trained eviction policy\n*Turn the RUR signal into a cheap learned scorer that drives eviction at run time.*\n\n5. Train a small two-layer network (a 256-wide hidden layer with GELU activation, about 0.5 million parameters) that reads each item's features and outputs one score, so that in every pair the more-helpful item scores higher, using a pairwise preference loss (the same form used in Direct Preference Optimization, DPO) with temperature 0.1. Use the AdamW optimizer (learning rate 1e-3), batches of 256 pairs, and stop when held-out pairwise accuracy plateaus; the big model stays frozen.\n\n*The eviction scorer $g_{phi}$ is trained with a pairwise preference loss over minimal pairs ranked by RUR $(m_{i}^{+}$ the higher-RUR item, $m_{i}^{-}$ the lower), with temperature $\\beta $; the backbone stays frozen.*\n$$ \\mathcal{L} = -\\log \\sigma\\!\\left(\\beta\\,(g_{\\phi}(m_i^{+}) - g_{\\phi}(m_i^{-}))\\right) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The scorer learns to predict read-time helpfulness from cheap features, so at run time we do not need the expensive two-pass measurement.\n6. At run time, whenever memory exceeds the budget B, drop the items the scorer rates lowest until you are back under budget, breaking ties by oldest. Never drop items in the working window, and give a just-written item one step of grace so a question can use it before it can be removed. Now the learned helpfulness score is the real eviction rule.\n   - _Why_: This makes the learned read-time-outcome signal the actual eviction rule, closing the loop to downstream answer accuracy.\n\n### Diagnostics and controls\n*Prove the read-time signal is the mechanism and that it differs from write-time and attention proxies.*\n\n7. Build a write-time-importance baseline: for the KV-cache variant, score items by the total attention their tokens received while the document was read in; for the chunk variant, score by similarity to the query. Run each as its own eviction policy at the same budget. Find the items the two policies disagree on (kept by one, dropped by the other), then force-drop those items and measure how much accuracy falls — that is how much the disagreement matters.\n   - _Why_: It shows the write-time rule and the read-time rule disagree exactly on the items that matter for the answer — proof the write-time assumption is doing real harm.\n8. Run two checks. The negative check shuffles which answer each item is scored against — each item's with-versus-without effect is measured on an unrelated question's answer — then retrains the scorer and deploys it; if the gain disappears, the gain really came from the genuine signal. The positive check evicts using the true measured helpfulness ranking directly (no learned scorer), showing the ceiling the signal alone can reach.\n   - _Why_: If shuffling the labels destroys the gain, the gain really came from RUR; the true-RUR run shows the ceiling the signal alone can reach.\n9. Group test questions by read horizon — how far back, in tokens, the item that mattered most for the answer was written (use the farthest supporting item when several matter) — split into ten equal-size bins, and plot accuracy in each bin for the learned policy versus the write-time baselines. The advantage should grow with distance.\n   - _Why_: The advantage should grow with distance, which is exactly where write-time guesses are blindest.\n10. Build a future-attention ranking: score each item by how much, averaged across all layers and heads, the question and answer positions attend to it during the read pass (the ForesightKV-style signal). Find where this ranking disagrees with the helpfulness ranking, force-drop each side's exclusive items at the same budget, and report which side's items carry more answer accuracy. This turns 'changing the answer is not the same as being attended to' into a measured result.\n   - _Why_: It turns the claim 'changing the answer is not the same as being attended to' into a measured result, separating our signal from the closest competitor.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 按读取时结果保留记忆：面向长上下文记忆的反事实信用分配\n\n**方法名称.** Read-time Utility Reward (RUR)\n\n## 研究动机\n长上下文语言模型的工作窗口容量有限，所以它会把较早的内容转入一个有限的记忆区，并不断决定哪些保留、哪些丢弃。问题在于，它在内容刚到达时就做出保留或丢弃的决定，依靠的是一些廉价的替代信号：内容出现的新旧程度、与当前文本的相似度、人工设计的重要性分数，或它能在多大程度上降低下一词的预测损失。这些信号都不知道这段内容对于模型稍后被问到的问题到底重不重要。于是，一个在写入时看似平常、却是四万字之后某个问题关键答案的事实被丢弃了，而系统从未得到任何“你错了”的反馈。\n\n这个问题正适逢其时：研究者刚刚证明可以训练一个策略来决定从记忆中驱逐什么（例如 ForesightKV，arXiv 2026），但它们仍然用一个内部代理指标来评判一个项——模型之后对它投入了多少注意力——而不是看保留它是否真的改变了答案。与此同时，偏好式训练（从“A 比 B 好”的比较中学习，如 DPO, Direct Preference Optimization）已成常规，而适配一个冻结模型的成本已足够低，以至于我们可以负担得起让模型运行两次——一次带该项、一次不带——来测量它对答案的真实影响。\n\n以往的系统因具体原因而止步。G-MemLLM（arXiv 2026-01）用下一词预测损失训练其保留/遗忘门，因为当时没有关于后续答案的信号。ZeroMerge 预先固定了其重要性指标，从而预设了一个项的价值可以在写入时判定。Memory-R1（arXiv 2025-08）确实从奖励中学习记忆操作，但奖励只在对话的最后才出现，因此无法分辨到底是哪个具体的项起了作用。\n\n当这个缺口被填补，你就得到一个驱逐策略，其保留/丢弃规则本身就是后续读取的真实结果，于是那些依赖写入时猜测的现有系统可以针对一个它们从未拥有过的信号重新训练——“这个记忆项有多有用”不再是过早做出的猜测，而是在它真正被使用的那一刻被测量的量。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景\n\n1. 取一个冻结的基础大语言模型(Large Language Model, LLM)，配一个有限的键值缓存(Key-Value cache, KV)/chunk 记忆区和预算 B（能保留多少项的上限）。把每篇文档切成 256-token 的 chunk，每个 chunk 就是一个记忆项。用三样东西描述每个项：其 token 隐状态的均值、被使用的新旧程度（当前位置减去写入位置，再除以总长度）、以及过去有多少次查询把它取出（一个计数）。读取记忆时，按嵌入余弦相似度取出与问题最相似的若干 chunk，取到刚好填满预算为止。\n   - _为什么_: 这些特征是一个小策略可读取的依据，不需要预先假设任何关于项价值的东西。\n\n### 读取时效用奖励（RUR）信号\n*通过保留-移除的反事实测量每个记忆项对答案的真实影响。*\n\n2. 从长上下文问答(Question Answering, QA)（如 RULER 多跳与 needle-in-haystack）构建（长文档、问题、标准答案）样例。标准答案是标注的答案文本，用与模型相同的方式分词。工作窗口——问题加上任何指令——始终留在上下文中，永不丢弃。把文档载入记忆，在问题加检索到的记忆上运行模型一次，记录它给正确答案的长度归一化对数概率；称之为读取时结果得分。\n\n*读取时结果得分是冻结主干对标准答案片段 A 赋予的长度归一化对数概率，其条件是工作窗口 W 拼接从记忆 M 中检索到的子集。*\n$$ s(A \\mid M) = \\frac{1}{|A|} \\sum_{t=1}^{|A|} \\log p_{\\theta}\\!\\left(A_t \\mid A_{<t}, \\, W \\oplus \\mathrm{Retr}(M)\\right) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这个数字是模型自己衡量在当前记忆下能多好地答对的指标——正是我们要优化的读取时结果。\n3. 对每个问题，从该问题实际检索到的项中选 32 个。对每个项，去掉这一项后重新运行模型——用次优 chunk 补上它腾出的位置，使上下文总量不变——再把两个结果得分相减。差值为较大正数，说明该项确实帮助了答案。【作者需决定：移除某项时，要么用次优 chunk 补上其位置（保持上下文长度不变），要么留空（保持其余保留集不变）；二者测量的东西不同（项的身份效应 vs 该位置的价值），作者须选择读取时效用奖励应捕捉哪一个。】\n\n*项 $m_{i}$ 对查询 q 的读取时效用奖励，等于保留与移除该项时正确答案得分之差：衡量保留 $m_{i}$ 在多大程度上提升了正确读取的概率。*\n$$ \\mathrm{RUR}(m_i, q) = s(A \\mid M) - s(A \\mid M \\setminus \\{m_i\\}) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 两种情况都跑一遍，直接测量保留该项是否改变了正确答案的概率——是真实效果，而非猜测。\n4. 在每个样例内，按有用性得分排序，把明显更有帮助的项与明显较没用的项配成一对，两者之间记忆的其余部分保持完全相同。只保留差距大于一个小边界（0.02 对数概率单位）的配对，以免在难以区分的平局上训练，每例最多保留差距最大的 64 对。\n   - _为什么_: 我们无法给一项定出绝对价格，但能可靠地说某项比另一项更有帮助——比较是这个信号诚实的形式。\n\n### 偏好训练的驱逐策略\n*把 RUR 信号转为一个廉价的学习打分器，在运行时驱动驱逐。*\n\n5. 训练一个小型两层网络（256 宽的隐层，GELU 激活，约 50 万参数），它读入每个项的特征并输出一个分数，使每对中更有帮助的项得分更高，采用成对偏好损失（与直接偏好优化(Direct Preference Optimization, DPO)同形），温度 0.1。使用 AdamW 优化器（学习率 1e-3）、每批 256 对，当留出集的成对准确率不再提升时停止；大模型保持冻结。\n\n*驱逐打分器 $g_{phi}$ 通过成对偏好损失训练，配对按 RUR 排序（$m_{i}^{+}$ 为高 RUR 项，$m_{i}^{-}$ 为低 RUR 项），温度为 $\\beta $；主干保持冻结。*\n$$ \\mathcal{L} = -\\log \\sigma\\!\\left(\\beta\\,(g_{\\phi}(m_i^{+}) - g_{\\phi}(m_i^{-}))\\right) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 打分器学会从廉价特征预测读取时的有用性，运行时就不需要昂贵的两次前向测量。\n6. 运行时，一旦记忆超过预算 B，就丢弃打分器评分最低的项直到回到预算以内，平局时丢最旧的。永不丢弃工作窗口中的项，并给刚写入的项一步宽限期，使问题能在它被移除前用到它。如此，学到的有用性得分就成了真正的驱逐规则。\n   - _为什么_: 这让学到的读取时结果信号成为真正的驱逐规则，把闭环闭合到下游答案准确率。\n\n### 诊断与对照\n*证明读取时信号是机制所在，并与写入时及注意力代理区分开。*\n\n7. 构建一个写入时重要性基线：对键值缓存(KV)变体，按项的 token 在读入文档时收到的总注意力打分；对 chunk 变体，按与问题的相似度打分。在相同预算下各自作为驱逐策略运行。找出两种策略意见相左的项（一个保留、另一个丢弃），强制丢弃这些项并测量准确率下降多少——这就是分歧的重要程度。\n   - _为什么_: 它表明写入时规则与读取时规则恰恰在对答案重要的项上分歧——证明写入时假设确实造成了损害。\n8. 跑两个检验。负检验打乱每个项所对照的答案——每个项的“有 vs 无”效果改在一个无关问题的答案上测量——然后重新训练打分器并部署；若增益消失，说明增益确实来自真实信号。正检验直接按真实测得的有用性排序驱逐（不用学习的打分器），展示信号本身能达到的上限。\n   - _为什么_: 如果打乱标签使增益消失，说明增益确实来自 RUR；真实-RUR 运行则展示信号本身能达到的上限。\n9. 按读取跨度对测试问题分组——对答案最关键的项是在多少 token 之前写入的（若有多个关键项则取最远的那个）——分成十个等量的分箱，绘制学到策略与写入时基线在每个分箱的准确率。优势应随距离增大。\n   - _为什么_: 优势应随距离增大，而这正是写入时猜测最盲目的地方。\n10. 构建未来注意力排序：按问题和答案位置在读取过程中对每个项的平均注意力（对所有层和头取平均）打分（即 ForesightKV 式信号）。找出该排序与有用性排序的分歧处，在相同预算下强制丢弃双方各自独有的项，报告哪一方的项携带更多答案准确率。这把“改变答案不等于被注意”变成可测量的结果。\n   - _为什么_: 它把“改变答案不等于被注意”的论断变成可测量的结果，把我们的信号与最近的竞争者区分开。\n\n"},{"id":"77","run_dir":"run_prompt77_ttsmmretr","index":77,"title":"Stop When the Ranking Stops Moving: Per-Query Test-Time Compute Allocation for Multimodal Retrieval","title_zh":"排序稳定即停止：面向多模态检索的逐查询测试时计算分配","method_name":"Rank-Stability Gated Retrieval (RSG-Retrieval)","hook":"Every test-time-scaling multimodal retriever picks its compute budget before it has seen the query, so it pays a fixed price on easy and hard queries alike; we instead let the retriever's own candidate-score geometry decide, per query, when one more compute increment would no longer reorder the top-k, and stop there. The result is a controller that reads a label-free ranking-stability statistic from a frozen retriever and reaches the same retrieval quality as the largest fixed budget while spending a fraction of the compute on the easy majority.","anchor_pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","anchor_pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","domain_category":"Vision-Language & Multimodal","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf decides how much test-time compute to spend on a given multimodal query from a quantity computed at retrieval time: every method fixes its spend (Meta-Token rung, reasoning-token budget, number of query variants) open-loop before reading the candidate set, so easy queries are over-served and hard near-tied queries are under-served, and there is no signal indicating whether additional compute would still change the top-k ordering.","pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","sub_pattern":"C25 (Decompose and Delegate to Solvers)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by splitting each retrieval into (i) a frozen multimodal retriever that, after each compute increment, emits a structured machine-checkable intermediate artifact — the current top-k candidate-score vector with its provenance (which rung / variant / reasoning pass produced it) — and (ii) a lightweight stop/continue controller that plays the role of the sound 'checker', grading that artifact by behavioral consensus of the top-k ordering across consecutive increments and returning a verifiable verdict mid-construction (stop, or escalate to the next increment), so the per-query budget is the controller's accumulated decision rather than a pre-set schedule.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides a stopping / escalation criterion for iterative multimodal retrieval refinement that is grounded in the retrieval state itself (candidate-score geometry across modalities) rather than in an external schedule (dialogue turns, a fixed iteration count, a fixed fusion of fixed variants), so iterative refinement cannot self-terminate when the ranking has stabilized nor self-extend when it has not.","pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by manufacturing the stopping signal the controller consumes from the frozen retriever's own internal readout — a label-free ranking-stability statistic (top-k rank-correlation between successive increments combined with the score-margin between rank-1 and rank-(k+1)) — rather than from any ground-truth relevance label or external schedule; the statistic is read on a tiny lever (only the controller's threshold is fit, the backbone retriever stays frozen) and is stabilized against the degenerate 'always stop immediately' collapse by a minimum-increment floor and a margin-anchored prior, exactly the diagnose-localize / minimize-on-a-tiny-lever / stabilize-against-collapse move.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"multimodal (vision-language) retrieval, test-time / inference-time compute scaling","n_papers":48,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":26},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":9},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":12,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Expanding Performance Boundaries of Open-Source Multimodal Models with Model, Data, and Test-Time Scaling"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Detecting hallucinations in large language models using semantic entropy"},{"source":"openalex","title":"A pathology foundation model for cancer diagnosis and prognosis prediction"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Evaluation and mitigation of the limitations of large language models in clinical decision-making"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Artificial intelligence for geoscience: Progress, challenges, and perspectives"},{"source":"openalex","title":"An Improved Dung Beetle Optimizer for the Twin Stacker Cranes’ Scheduling Problem"}],"more":6},{"year":2025,"n":30,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"MetaEmbed: Scaling Multimodal Retrieval at Test-Time with Flexible Late Interaction"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Test-Time Scaling Strategies for Generative Retrieval in Multimodal Conversational Recommendations"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Reason to Contrast: A Cascaded Multimodal Retrieval Framework"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"VideoChat-R1.5: Visual Test-Time Scaling to Reinforce Multimodal Reasoning by Iterative Perception"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"InternVL3: Exploring Advanced Training and Test-Time Recipes for Open-Source Multimodal Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Training Vision-Language Process Reward Models for Test-Time Scaling in Multimodal Reasoning: Key Insights and Lessons Learned"}],"more":24},{"year":2026,"n":7,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"LLandMark: A Multi-Agent Framework for Landmark-Aware Multimodal Interactive Video Retrieval"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"LITTA: Late-Interaction and Test-Time Alignment for Visually-Grounded Multimodal Retrieval"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Lost in Decoding? Reproducing and Stress-Testing the Look-Ahead Prior in Generative Retrieval"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Learning to Discover at Test Time"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Adapting in the Dark: Efficient and Stable Test-Time Adaptation for Black-Box Models"}],"more":1}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":13,"share":0.271},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":11,"share":0.229},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":7,"share":0.146},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":6,"share":0.125},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":5,"share":0.104},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":5,"share":0.104},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":4,"share":0.083},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":3,"share":0.062}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Across the recent wave of test-time scaling for multimodal retrieval, every method spends inference compute on a schedule that is fixed before the query is seen rather than steered by how hard the query actually is: MetaEmbed (semanticscholar:b44bed44cb88e23a5a070d520f6d87a397f32b6d) exposes a Matryoshka ladder of Meta-Token granularities but the number of vectors used at query time is a user-chosen global operating point, not a per-query decision; TTE-v2 / Reason-to-Contrast (semanticscholar:1556486c21e3b0dda9baeca4b9d415b3f2af2563) adds a uniform reasoning-token budget for reranking regardless of whether a given query's candidate set is already well-separated; and LITTA (arxiv:2603.26683v1) generates a fixed number of LLM query variants and fuses them whether or not the first retrieval was already confident. Because the spend is decided open-loop, easy queries are over-served (compute wasted on already-separated candidate lists) and hard, near-tied queries are under-served (the budget runs out before the modality-gap-induced ambiguity is resolved), and no method exposes a quantity computed at retrieval time that says how much further compute would still change the top-k ordering — so there is no signal on which to stop early or to escalate, and the compute-quality trade-off curve is left to a global knob the deployer sets blind.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:b44bed44cb88e23a5a070d520f6d87a397f32b6d","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"MetaEmbed trains a fixed set of learnable Meta Tokens with Matryoshka multi-vector retrieval so that, at test time, a user can pick how many of the contextualized Meta-Token vectors to use for late interaction, trading retrieval quality for cost along a granularity ladder. The residue: the choice of which rung to use is a single global operating point set by the deployer ahead of time and applied identically to every query — the method has no per-query mechanism that reads the candidate set and decides this query needs more vectors while that one is already resolved, and no stopping criterion grounded in whether spending another rung would actually reorder the top-k."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:1556486c21e3b0dda9baeca4b9d415b3f2af2563","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"TTE-v2 (Reason to Contrast) scales retrieval quality by spending an additional reasoning-token budget to rewrite the query and rerank candidates, showing quality grows with token budget rather than model/embedding size. The residue: the reasoning-token budget is applied uniformly per query and per stage; there is no allocation that gives more tokens to queries whose candidate scores are near-tied and fewer to queries already cleanly separated, and no measured quantity tells the system when added reasoning has stopped changing the ranking."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2603.26683v1","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"LITTA improves visually-grounded retrieval without retraining by generating a fixed number of complementary LLM query variants, retrieving for each with a frozen late-interaction vision retriever, and fusing the results with reciprocal rank fusion. The residue: the number of query variants (the test-time compute) is a fixed hyperparameter independent of the query's difficulty, and fusion proceeds even when the first variant already returned a confidently separated list, so compute is neither allocated nor halted based on a retrieval-side confidence signal."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:1df59177995fb7fb356847b9628226f017d962b1","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"This work brings test-time scaling to multi-turn conversational multimodal product retrieval, iteratively refining results across dialogue turns using MLLM-as-retriever inference-time refinement. The residue: scaling is driven by the dialogue turn structure (one refinement per user turn) rather than by per-query retrieval uncertainty within a turn, and there is no notion of allocating a finite compute budget across turns or candidates according to how ambiguous the current retrieval state is."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"multimodal (vision-language) retrieval, test-time / inference-time compute scaling","venue":"ICLR 2026","time":"2026","data":["MMEB / MMEB-V2 (universal multimodal embedding benchmark)","ViDoSeek / visual-document retrieval","image-text retrieval (e.g. Flickr/COCO-style)","video retrieval (VATEX)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with cloud access; familiar with retrieval, MLLMs, test-time scaling","preference":"both","baseline":"MetaEmbed (flexible late-interaction test-time scaling), TTE-v2 / Reason-to-Contrast (reasoning-token reranking), LITTA (LLM query expansion), Guided Query Refinement","limitation":"current test-time scaling for multimodal retrieval spends a fixed, query-agnostic compute budget (fixed Meta-Token count, fixed reasoning-token budget, fixed number of query variants) and has no principled per-query stopping rule","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The two gaps interlock as a sequential_pipeline whose central pipeline is RANK-STABILITY-GATED TEST-TIME RETRIEVAL: the self-supervised leg (C07) manufactures a per-step stopping signal that the delegate-to-solver leg (C25) consumes to make the per-query allocation decision, so they share machinery (one statistic feeds one controller) rather than forming two separate modules. Fix a frozen multimodal retriever R (e.g. MetaEmbed-style flexible late interaction, or any retriever exposing an escalating compute ladder) and a candidate corpus. A compute increment is one rung of R's ladder: for MetaEmbed it is using r more Meta-Token vectors in late interaction; for a reasoning-token reranker (TTE-v2) it is one more reasoning/rewrite pass; for query-expansion (LITTA) it is one more LLM query variant fused by reciprocal rank fusion. At increment t the retriever produces a top-k candidate-score vector s_t = (s_t[1] >= ... >= s_t[k]) over the SAME fixed candidate shortlist (k is fixed at 100; the shortlist is produced once by the cheapest rung so increments only re-score, never re-fetch). From s_t the self-supervised leg computes two label-free quantities, defined entirely from R's outputs with no relevance labels: (1) ranking-stability tau_t = Kendall's tau between the top-k ordering at increment t and at increment t-1 (tau_1 := 0 by definition); (2) separation margin m_t = (s_t[1] - s_t[k+1]) / (s_t[1] - s_t[k]) using the score of the first OUT-of-top-k candidate s_t[k+1] as the denominator anchor (a unitless ratio, so no cross-quantity weight is needed between tau and m). The stopping signal is g_t = tau_t after at least t_min increments AND m_t computed on the current state; the controller (the C25 'checker') STOPS at the first t >= t_min with tau_t >= theta_tau OR m_t >= theta_m, else ESCALATES to t+1, up to a hard cap T_max (the top rung). theta_tau, theta_m, t_min, T_max are the ONLY fitted hyperparameters; they are calibrated ONCE on a held-out query set by choosing the smallest thresholds whose induced per-query stops keep nDCG@10 within a tolerance epsilon (default 0.5 nDCG points) of the always-T_max budget — calibration uses graded relevance only to pick thresholds, never at test time. The per-query budget B(q) = sum of FLOPs over the increments actually run for q; the controller's output is exactly the top-k of the increment at which it stopped. This closes the anchor gap because the budget is now a per-query quantity emitted by reading the candidate-score geometry (gap 1: a quantity computed at retrieval time decides the spend, and tau_t is precisely the 'would more compute reorder the top-k' signal that was missing); it closes the sibling gap because the stop/escalate criterion is grounded in the retrieval state (tau_t, m_t) not an external schedule, so refinement self-terminates when tau_t saturates and self-extends when it has not (gap 2). The mechanism does NOT reduce to a fixed cascade cutoff (lineage c0: cutoffs there are query-agnostic shortlist sizes, here the stop index is per-query and read from tau_t), to an in-network early-exit halting unit (c1: that needs a trained halting head inside one network; here R is frozen and the controller is a 4-parameter rule over external candidate scores), or to a textbook i.i.d. SPRT (c2: SPRT tests one hypothesis under i.i.d. evidence, here the decision is a top-k RANKING stabilization over non-i.i.d. correlated increments of a frozen retriever — tau over orderings is the object SPRT does not provide).","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery, not separate modules: the stopping signal (C07's manufactured statistic) is the SOLE input to the allocation controller (C25's checker), so building two modules would duplicate the same tau_t computation — the sequential_pipeline thread (signal -> stop decision -> budget) makes one statistic feed one controller, evidenced by the fact that gap 2's deliverable (the criterion) is literally gap 1's missing input. (b) Alternatives considered and rejected: (i) a LEARNED stopping policy (train a small RNN on candidate-score trajectories) — rejected because it needs trajectory labels and re-introduces training, undercutting the 'frozen retriever, tiny lever' minimalism and the hook's compute claim; (ii) reframing as optimal stopping with a learned value function (the reframe_as_solvable_object alternates C00/C21/C27) — rejected because none of those sub-clusters' objects (attribution scores, RL-as-sequence-modeling, game equilibria) match a ranking-stabilization stop, and a value-function fit again needs supervision; (iii) entropy of the softmaxed scores as the signal — rejected because score entropy moves with temperature/calibration (the exact non-mechanism confound the falsification control guards against) whereas tau over orderings is calibration-invariant. AVOIDED REGRESSION NODES (method_lineage): c0 fixed cascade cutoff, c1 in-network early-exit, c2 i.i.d. SPRT — the mechanism is kept distinct from each by defining the stop over the frozen retriever's external cross-modal top-k ORDERING geometry, which none of c0-c2 instantiate.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: take a frozen MetaEmbed retriever on MMEB-V2 with its Matryoshka rungs as compute increments, calibrate the controller once on a held-out split, and run it on the test split measuring nDCG@10, Recall@10, and mean per-query compute B(q) against the always-top-rung baseline. If the candidate works, mean B(q) drops substantially (the easy-query majority stops early) while nDCG@10 stays within the calibrated tolerance epsilon of the always-top-rung budget — i.e. the quality-vs-compute Pareto curve of the adaptive controller dominates every fixed-budget point. The mechanism's load-bearing variable is the ranking-stability statistic tau_t (Kendall's tau between successive top-k orderings); the mechanism claim is that tau_t saturating is what signals further compute will not reorder the top-k. Negative control: replace tau_t with softmax-score ENTROPY H_t (a calibration-driven quantity that is NOT an ordering-stability measure) as the stop signal while holding thresholds-calibration identical — if the mechanism is real, the entropy-gated controller must give back the compute saving at fixed quality (its nDCG@10-at-equal-compute should fall back toward the random-stopping baseline), because entropy can be low while the top-k ordering is still churning; if instead entropy gates just as well, the gain was calibration/score-scale, not ranking stabilization, and the mechanism claim is falsified. Positive control: a tau_t-only controller (m_t removed) should recover most of the compute saving, confirming ordering stability is the carrying signal.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:b44bed44cb88e23a5a070d520f6d87a397f32b6d","delta":"MetaEmbed exposes a Matryoshka ladder of Meta-Token granularities chosen as a single global operating point set by the deployer; we construct a per-query controller that reads a ranking-stability statistic tau_t over that same ladder and decides the rung query-by-query, a per-query allocation MetaEmbed never derives."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:1556486c21e3b0dda9baeca4b9d415b3f2af2563","delta":"TTE-v2 shows retrieval quality grows with a UNIFORM reasoning-token budget; we measure and exploit that the marginal token spend stops changing the top-k for most queries, deriving a stopping rule (tau_t saturation) that allocates the token budget non-uniformly, which their uniform-budget framing does not provide."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2603.26683v1","delta":"LITTA fuses a FIXED number of LLM query variants by reciprocal rank fusion regardless of confidence; we make the number of variants a per-query quantity emitted by the candidate-score margin m_t and ordering-stability tau_t, so fusion self-terminates once the ranking stabilizes — an adaptive variant count LITTA lacks."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415190470","delta":"Rank1 trains a reranker to consume a uniform test-time reasoning budget on text passages; we add no training and instead define a label-free, calibration-invariant ordering-stability signal over a frozen MULTIMODAL retriever's candidate geometry to allocate the budget per query."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:b44bed44cb88e23a5a070d520f6d87a397f32b6d","what_step_was_missed":"MetaEmbed built the test-time-scalable ladder (the increments) and a granularity-organized multi-vector representation, but it never constructed a retrieval-time readout that decides, per query, where on that ladder to stop: specifically it lacks the ordering-stability functional tau_t over successive rungs and the proof/measurement that tau_t saturation predicts no further top-k reordering, which is the construction needed to convert their global operating point into a per-query budget."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":343,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"Hard floor did not fire: gap_closure_reject_check aggregate is 'borderline' (no lesson marked candidate_match=yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat is addressable (not exact-mechanism overlap). recipe_application_check.verdict='applied' for both legs, so the cited C25 and C07 tactical moves are genuinely instantiated rather than parent-gist. The single borderline (C25's 'neighboring routing move already demonstrated') is a non-load-bearing novelty-framing concern and the paper_pointed_threat is dodge-able by a differentiation_from_lit entry, so this advances with both surfaced as reviewer_concerns for Phase 4 rather than triggering a revise.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf decides how much test-time compute to spend on a given multimodal query from a quantity computed at retrieval time: every method fixes its spend (Meta-Token rung, reasoning-token budget, number of query variants) open-loop before reading the candidate set, so easy queries are over-served and hard near-tied queries are under-served, and there is no signal indicating whether additional compute would still change the top-k ordering.","main_pattern":"decompose_and_delegate","sub_pattern":"C25 (Decompose and Delegate to Solvers)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"An advisory plan with no verification closure leaves the artifact non-load-bearing and collapses the contribution to ordinary sampling-plus-filtering; tailoring the routing/prompts to one benchmark while omitting the efficiency tradeoff sinks the decomposition.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A decomposition that merely chains off-the-shelf agents or engines, with no single component demonstrated to be both novel and load-bearing, reads as engineering assembly rather than a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The single load-bearing, novel component is the ranking-stability functional tau_t as the stop signal; core_mechanism_steps 7-8 ablate it (entropy negative control, tau-only positive control), so it is demonstrated load-bearing, not a chain of agents."},{"lesson_quoted":"If the 'key' prompt or elicitation scheme is tuned to one benchmark and not validated across settings, reviewers treat it as a dataset-specific hack instead of a transferable mechanism.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The thresholds are calibrated once and the method is validated across three benchmark families (MMEB-V2, ViDoSeek, image-text) and across three retriever ladders (Meta-Token rungs, reasoning passes, query variants), so it is not single-benchmark tuned."},{"lesson_quoted":"Delegating a sub-problem to a sound but costly solver (NP-hard search, materialized intermediate state) sinks the contribution when latency and scalability are left unexamined.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The 'solver' here is a 4-parameter stop/continue rule (Kendall tau over k items, O(k log k)); per-query compute B(q) is the headline measured quantity, so cost is examined as the primary axis, not ignored."},{"lesson_quoted":"Without an ablation isolating the decomposition's marginal effect from extra data, more epochs, or the base model's prior knowledge, the reported gains read as confounded and unattributable.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Nothing is trained (retriever frozen, no epochs), and the gain is isolated by comparing against always-top-rung at matched quality plus the entropy/tau-only controls, so there is no extra-data/epoch confound."},{"lesson_quoted":"Re-deriving a routing move that a closely neighboring published system already demonstrated, while showing only marginal gains, fails the novelty bar regardless of engineering polish.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"Several recent collision hits (Compute Allocation for Reasoning-Intensive Retrieval Agents; Uncertainty-Aware Budget Allocation) do adaptive test-time allocation, so the routing idea is neighboring — but they allocate over reasoning samples / which-retriever, not via a calibration-invariant ordering-stability stop on a frozen multimodal retriever's candidate geometry; surfaced for Phase 4."},{"lesson_quoted":"A self-improvement or decomposition loop whose reliability hinges on an unvalidated data-generation, retrieval, or filtering component invites rejection when error propagation across iterations is never analyzed.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"There is no self-improvement / data-generation loop; increments only re-score a fixed shortlist, so there is no cross-iteration error propagation to analyze."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides a stopping / escalation criterion for iterative multimodal retrieval refinement that is grounded in the retrieval state itself (candidate-score geometry across modalities) rather than in an external schedule (dialogue turns, a fixed iteration count, a fixed fusion of fixed variants), so iterative refinement cannot self-terminate when the ranking has stabilized nor self-extend when it has not.","main_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"A label-free internal signal invites a degenerate solution, so the tactic must bolt on an explicit stabilizer; a surrogate whose validity depends on calibration or covert target-label access breaks exactly when deployment diverges from those premises.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A label-free signal whose validity depends on model calibration silently fails on exactly the deep networks known to be poorly calibrated — validate a surrogate where its core assumption is weakest, not where it is convenient.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The chosen signal tau_t is a rank-correlation over orderings, which is invariant to monotone score rescaling and hence to calibration; the design explicitly rejects score-entropy precisely because entropy is calibration-dependent (this is the negative control)."},{"lesson_quoted":"Recasting a continuous shift as a discrete, known, finite set of types indexed against a precomputed lookup table collapses the moment an unanticipated or mixed shift arrives.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"tau_t and m_t are continuous functionals computed live per query; there is no finite shift-type lookup table."},{"lesson_quoted":"Importing a generic continual-learning blending or interpolation technique into a new modality without identifying that modality's specific dynamics lever reads as recombination, not contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The modality-specific lever is named: the cross-modal top-k score ordering of a frozen multimodal late-interaction retriever and how it churns across compute increments — not a generic blending technique."},{"lesson_quoted":"Reusing standard sequential machinery (chaining each step's posterior as the next prior) without a new stabilizer amplifies noise and looks derivative of prior adaptation work.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Explicit stabilizers are added (t_min>=2 floor and an m_floor margin anchor that forbids halting on a stable-but-low-margin ranking), matching C07's stabilize-against-collapse step."},{"lesson_quoted":"A multi-branch or ensemble reweighting mechanism that overlaps with standard multi-task/mixture-of-experts ensembling must explicitly beat both the single-model and the standard-ensemble baselines, or the gain is credited to prior art.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"No ensemble reweighting is used; the controller selects a stopping increment of a single frozen retriever, so MoE/ensemble baselines are not the relevant comparison."},{"lesson_quoted":"Using target or test-set information during adaptation invites a label-leakage objection that undermines the very source-free, label-free deployment setting the method claims.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Graded relevance labels are used ONLY in the one-time held-out threshold calibration, never at test time; the test-time signal is purely label-free candidate-score geometry, explicitly stated in steps 2-4."}],"verdict":"clear"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The self_supervised_signal_engineering leg (C07) is clear on all six Reject lessons because tau_t is calibration-invariant, label-free at test time, and explicitly stabilized. The decompose_and_delegate leg (C25) is borderline on one lesson only — 'Re-deriving a routing move that a closely neighboring published system already demonstrated' — because recent collision hits do adaptive test-time allocation, though none over a frozen multimodal retriever's ordering geometry; this is a non-load-bearing novelty-framing concern, surfaced for Phase 4 rather than a triggered Reject."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf decides how much test-time compute to spend on a given multimodal query from a quantity computed at retrieval time: every method fixes its spend (Meta-Token rung, reasoning-token budget, number of query variants) open-loop before reading the candidate set, so easy queries are over-served and hard near-tied queries are under-served, and there is no signal indicating whether additional compute would still change the top-k ordering.","sub_pattern":"C25 (Decompose and Delegate to Solvers)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Have the learned model emit a structured machine-checkable intermediate artifact at the decomposition boundary, then close the loop with the solver's verifiable output (execution results, validator verdicts, behavioral consensus across independently sampled candidates, terminal-answer confidence) and apply that feedback DURING construction for credit assignment / candidate selection / in-place correction.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism + step 3: the frozen retriever emits the structured machine-checkable artifact (the top-k candidate-score vector s_t with provenance) at each increment, and the controller closes the loop mid-construction by grading it via behavioral consensus of the top-k ORDERING across consecutive increments (tau_t) and returning a verifiable stop/escalate verdict that selects which increment's ranking is returned — exactly the 'behavioral consensus across candidates used for selection during construction' move, not post-hoc filtering.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides a stopping / escalation criterion for iterative multimodal retrieval refinement that is grounded in the retrieval state itself (candidate-score geometry across modalities) rather than in an external schedule (dialogue turns, a fixed iteration count, a fixed fusion of fixed variants), so iterative refinement cannot self-terminate when the ranking has stabilized nor self-extend when it has not.","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Treat the already-trained model's own internal-state readout as the manufactured supervisory signal; the signature verbs are diagnose-localize (find the structural failure site), minimize-on-a-tiny-lever (confine the correction to a minimal parameter/threshold while the backbone stays frozen), and stabilize-against-collapse (bolt on an explicit stabilizer).","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism + steps 2,3,5: diagnose-localize = the failure (open-loop over/under-serving) is localized to the top-k ordering churn, read off as tau_t/m_t from the frozen retriever's own scores; minimize-on-a-tiny-lever = only the 4 controller thresholds are fit, retriever frozen; stabilize-against-collapse = t_min floor + m_floor margin anchor prevent the degenerate stop-immediately solution. All three signature verbs are present.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both legs perform their cluster's distinctive move: C25's machine-checkable-artifact-plus-verifiable-loop-during-construction is realized by the candidate-score artifact graded by ordering consensus, and C07's diagnose-localize / tiny-lever / stabilize triad is realized by the frozen-retriever readout, threshold-only fit, and the t_min/m_floor stabilizers."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["decompose_and_delegate","self_supervised_signal_engineering"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"None of the three reject-favored compositions matches: all three require heterogeneous_decomposition as a component, which is absent from the composition_set {decompose_and_delegate, self_supervised_signal_engineering}."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:c613546149b19f4f921ccd413b32542d44c020e4","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"Compute Allocation for Reasoning-Intensive Retrieval Agents studies how to allocate inference compute across query expansion and candidate re-ranking in an LLM agent's retrieval pipeline, which is the closest competing claim: if it already allocates per-query retrieval compute from a retrieval-state signal, the candidate's anchor contribution would be subsumed. It does not: its setting is an agent's growing text memory store with reasoning-bridged (implicit) query-document links, and its allocation is over LLM reasoning/expansion calls, not a calibration-invariant ranking-stability stop computed over a frozen MULTIMODAL late-interaction retriever's top-k score ordering; it neither defines tau_t-style ordering stabilization nor handles the cross-modal candidate geometry, so the candidate's claim stands but must explicitly differentiate from it.","addressable_via":"differentiation_from_lit — add an entry contrasting the candidate's frozen-multimodal-retriever ordering-stability stop against this paper's LLM-agent reasoning-compute allocation over a text memory store."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Stop When the Ranking Stops Moving: Per-Query Test-Time Compute Allocation for Multimodal Retrieval\n\n**Method.** Rank-Stability Gated Retrieval (RSG-Retrieval)\n\n## Motivation\nRecent multimodal search systems have started spending extra computation at search time to get better results: MetaEmbed uses more vectors when comparing a query to candidates, TTE-v2 spends more reasoning tokens to re-rank, and LITTA rewrites the query into several variants and merges the results. They all share one habit, though — they decide how much computation to spend BEFORE looking at the query. So an easy query whose best answer is already obvious gets the full expensive treatment, and a genuinely hard query, where the top few candidates are nearly tied, runs out of budget before the tie is broken. Nobody computes a number, while searching, that tells you whether spending a bit more would actually change the answer.\n\nWhy this is fixable now: retrievers like MetaEmbed (2025) now offer a built-in 'compute ladder' you can climb one rung at a time, which is exactly the handle a per-query decision needs. And because the decision can be read straight off the candidate scores of a frozen model, you do not have to train anything — the whole method is a tiny four-number rule plus a one-time tuning step.\n\nWhat prior work stopped short of: MetaEmbed built the ladder but never decided per query where to stop on it; TTE-v2 spends the same reasoning budget on every query and never measures when more reasoning stops helping; LITTA always merges a fixed number of query variants even when the first one already nailed it. The missing piece in all three is a search-time signal of 'diminishing returns'.\n\nWhat changes once you have it: any of these systems can match its best-quality setting while spending far less compute on average, because most queries are easy and can stop early. The deployer no longer has to guess one global budget — the retriever decides per query — and the same difficulty signal can be reused by conversational multimodal search to spend effort wisely within a single turn.\n\n## Method\n### Frozen increment interface\n*Turn a fixed retriever's compute ladder into an interruptible per-increment re-scoring loop over a frozen shortlist.*\n\n1. Put a thin wrapper around a frozen retriever that has a compute ladder (for example MetaEmbed). Each call to the wrapper runs one more rung of that ladder and hands back the scores of the top 101 candidates as a fixed-length list (we keep the top 100 plus one extra just-outside item, so k=100). Make the wrapper return the same kind of score list no matter which ladder you use: for the multi-vector ladder, rung t re-scores each shortlisted item using one more comparison vector (default: t vectors at rung t); for the reasoning ladder, rung t runs t reasoning passes of the frozen re-ranker and reads its relevance score per item; for the query-rewrite ladder, rung t adds one more rewritten query and merges the per-query rankings with reciprocal rank fusion (an averaging of 1/rank across the queries). The retriever's weights are never changed — every rung only re-scores the same candidates — so the rest of the method does not care which ladder is underneath.\n   - _Why_: It turns 'spend a fixed amount' into a sequence of small, interruptible steps whose state you can inspect between steps.\n2. Build the candidate shortlist once, using the cheapest rung, and then freeze which items are in it. Concretely: at the first rung do a normal full search, keep the best 101 items (the 100 you will rank plus one just-outside reference item), and from then on every rung only re-scores those exact 101 items — no new items are ever let in. The internal ordering of those 101 can still change as you climb, but the membership cannot. The single 'just-outside' reference item is whichever of the 101 sits in 101st place under the current scores, and step 3 (After each rung) uses it as the benchmark the top item must beat.\n   - _Why_: If the set of items kept changing, you couldn't tell whether the ranking moved because of better scoring or because different items showed up.\n\n### Label-free stability signal\n*Read a calibration-invariant ordering-stability statistic and a margin from the candidate scores alone.*\n\n3. After each rung, compute two numbers from the scores alone. First, a ranking-stability number $\\tau _{t}$ (Eq. 1): how similar the current ordering of the 100 candidates is to the previous rung's ordering, measured by Kendall rank correlation (a tie-corrected version, scored from -1 for fully reversed to +1 for identical); at the very first rung set it to 0 because there is no previous ordering. Because this only looks at ordering, it does not care about the absolute size or scaling of the scores. Second, a separation margin $m_{t}$ (Eq. 2): how far the top item is ahead of the first item just outside the top 100, divided by how spread out the scores inside the top 100 are (with a tiny constant added to the denominator so you never divide by zero). Neither number uses any relevance labels — they come purely from the frozen retriever's own scores.\n\n*The ranking-stability signal $\\tau _{t}$ is the Kendall rank correlation between the top-k candidate ordering at increment t and the previous increment t-1; it is undefined at t=1 so set to 0.*\n$$ \\tau_t = \\mathrm{KendallTau}\\big(\\pi(s_t[1{:}k]),\\, \\pi(s_{t-1}[1{:}k])\\big),\\qquad \\tau_1 := 0 \\tag{1} $$\n\n\n*The separation margin $m_{t}$ is a unitless ratio of the gap between the top score and the first out-of-top-k score over the spread inside the top-k, anchoring the stop decision in score geometry without any cross-quantity weight.*\n$$ m_t = \\frac{s_t[1] - s_t[k+1]}{s_t[1] - s_t[k] + \\varepsilon} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: $\\tau _{t}$ answers 'did one more rung reorder anything?' and, being about ordering, it doesn't care about score scale or calibration; $m_{t}$ answers 'is the winner clearly ahead?'\n\n### Stop/escalate controller\n*Decide per query when more compute would no longer reorder the top-k, with stabilizers against early-stop collapse, plus its one-time calibration.*\n\n4. Loop over the rungs. At each rung t (start checking only once t is at least 2 so a previous ordering exists) stop if either the ordering is stable enough (the stability number is at or above a learned threshold) or the winner is clearly ahead enough (the margin is at or above a learned threshold) — but never stop while the margin is below a safety floor, even if the ordering looks stable. If neither condition fires, climb to the next rung, up to a cap equal to the largest rung the ladder offers (so you never spend more than the most expensive fixed setting). When you stop, return the top 100 from the rung you stopped at, and record how much compute that took (the total number of arithmetic operations used, also reported simply as which rung you stopped on). That stop point is what decides the final answer — it picks which rung's ranking the user actually receives.\n\n*The controller stops at the first increment past $t_{min}$ where either the ordering is stable enough or the margin is large enough, but never while the margin is below a floor that guards against halting on a stable-but-low-margin ranking.*\n$$ \\mathrm{stop}(t) = \\big[t \\geq t_{\\min}\\big] \\wedge \\big( \\tau_t \\geq \\theta_\\tau \\;\\vee\\; m_t \\geq \\theta_m \\big) \\wedge \\big[m_t \\geq m_{\\text{floor}}\\big] \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Stopping is exactly the moment more compute would no longer change the answer; the floor stops it from quitting on a ranking that looks stable but isn't clearly resolved.\n5. Tune the four thresholds one time, offline, on a held-out set of queries (about 20% of the data, kept separate from the test set) that does have relevance labels. Try a small grid of values for each threshold — the stability threshold from 0.80 up to 0.99, the margin threshold from 1.0 to 3.0, the minimum rung from 2 to 4, and the margin floor from 0.0 to 1.0. For each combination, measure the average compute and the retrieval quality (nDCG@10) on this held-out set, throw away any combination whose quality drops more than a small allowed tolerance (default half an nDCG@10 point) below always using the top rung, and from what is left pick the combination with the lowest average compute, preferring the more cautious (higher minimum rung) one when tied. Labels are used only in this tuning step; at actual search time no labels are ever needed.\n   - _Why_: It lets you state up front how much quality you're willing to trade for speed, while keeping the live method label-free.\n\n### Mechanism validation\n*Isolate ordering stability as the carrying signal and show Pareto dominance across benchmarks and ladders.*\n\n6. Build two comparison versions that change only the stopping signal, keeping everything else (the wrapper, the frozen shortlist, the loop, the evaluation) identical. Negative control: replace the ordering-stability number with score entropy — turn the top-100 scores into a probability distribution with a softmax at a fixed temperature of 1.0 and take its entropy (a standard 'how spread out / uncertain' measure); stop when the entropy is low enough (low entropy means the model is confident), and re-tune its own threshold on the held-out set just like before so this control is given a fair best setting. Positive control: keep the stability signal but remove the margin part entirely, so the controller stops only when the ordering is stable. Then compare all three versions at equal compute: how much quality each gets, and how much of the compute saving each recovers.\n   - _Why_: If entropy works just as well, the gain was about score calibration, not ordering stability — that would disprove the claim; the $\\tau _{t}-only$ version checks ordering stability is doing the work.\n7. Test the tuned controller on several benchmarks — MMEB and MMEB-V2 (multimodal embedding benchmarks), ViDoSeek (visual document retrieval), and one image-text set such as Flickr30K or COCO 1K — and on all three ways of adding compute (more vectors, more reasoning passes, more query rewrites). Compare against three baselines: always use the cheapest rung, always use the top rung, and an 'oracle' that is allowed to peek at the answers to find, for each query, the smallest rung that already gets essentially the best quality (an unreachable best case used as the lower bound of the trade-off curve). Report retrieval quality (nDCG@10 and Recall@10) and how much compute each query used on average and at the worst 10% and 1% (the tail). This shows the adaptive method beats every fixed-budget setting and that the idea carries across different ways of spending compute, not just one benchmark.\n   - _Why_: It shows the adaptive curve beats every fixed-budget setting and that the idea transfers across different ways of adding compute, not just one benchmark.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 排序稳定即停止：面向多模态检索的逐查询测试时计算分配\n\n**方法名称.** Rank-Stability Gated Retrieval (RSG-Retrieval)\n\n## 研究动机\n最近的多模态检索系统开始在检索时多花算力来换取更好结果：MetaEmbed 在比较 query 与候选时使用更多向量，TTE-v2 花更多 reasoning token 来重排，LITTA 把 query 改写成多个变体再融合结果。它们有一个共同习惯——在看到 query 之前就决定要花多少算力。于是一个答案已经很明显的简单 query 也照样接受最贵的处理，而一个真正困难、前几个候选几乎打平的 query，却在打破平局之前就把预算用完了。没有人在检索过程中算出一个数，来判断多花一点算力是否真的会改变结果。\n\n为什么现在能解决：像 MetaEmbed (2025) 这样的检索器现在提供了一个可以逐级攀爬的内置“算力阶梯”，这正是逐查询决策所需要的把手。而且由于这个决策可以直接从一个冻结模型的候选分数上读出，你完全不需要训练任何东西——整个方法只是一个四参数的小规则加上一次性的标定。\n\n以往工作止步于何处：MetaEmbed 造了阶梯，却从不逐 query 决定停在哪一级；TTE-v2 对每个 query 花同样的 reasoning 预算，从不测量何时再推理也无济于事；LITTA 即使第一个变体已经命中，也总是融合固定数量的 query 变体。三者共同缺失的，是一个检索时的“边际收益递减”信号。\n\n一旦拥有它会带来什么：上述任一系统都能在平均算力大幅下降的同时，达到其最佳质量设定，因为大多数 query 是简单的、可以提前停止。部署者不再需要去猜一个全局预算——检索器逐 query 自行决定——而同一个难度信号还能被对话式多模态检索复用，在单轮之内明智地分配算力。\n\n## 方法\n### 冻结增量接口\n*把固定检索器的算力阶梯变成在冻结短名单上可中断的逐增量重打分循环。*\n\n1. 在一个带“算力阶梯”的冻结检索器（例如 MetaEmbed）外套一层薄封装。每次调用封装就多跑该阶梯的一级，并以定长列表的形式返回 top-101 候选的分数（我们保留前 100 名外加一个刚刚落榜的项，因此 k=100）。让封装无论底层是哪种阶梯都返回同一种分数列表：对于多向量阶梯，第 t 级用多一个比较向量对每个入选候选重新打分（默认第 t 级用 t 个向量）；对于 reasoning 阶梯，第 t 级跑 t 次冻结重排器的 reasoning 过程并读取它给每个候选的相关性分数；对于 query 改写阶梯，第 t 级多加一条改写后的 query，并用 reciprocal rank fusion（倒数排名融合，即对各 query 的 1/排名 求平均）合并各 query 的排序。检索器权重始终不变——每一级都只对同一批候选重新打分——所以方法的其余部分无需关心底层是哪种阶梯。\n   - _为什么_: 它把“花固定算力”变成一串可中断的小步骤，让你能在步骤之间查看状态。\n2. 用最便宜的一级一次性构建候选短名单，然后冻结其成员。具体来说：第一级做一次正常的全量检索，保留最好的 101 个候选（你要排序的 100 个，外加一个刚刚落榜的参考项），此后每一级都只对这 101 个候选重新打分——绝不放入新候选。这 101 个候选的内部排序在攀爬过程中仍可变化，但成员资格不变。那个“刚刚落榜”的参考项就是当前分数下排在第 101 位的候选，第3步（每一级之后） 会用它作为第一名必须超越的基准。\n   - _为什么_: 如果候选集合一直变，你就无法判断排序变动是因为打分更好，还是因为换了不同的候选。\n\n### Label-free 稳定信号\n*仅从候选分数读出一个校准不变的排序稳定统计量和一个裕度。*\n\n3. 每一级之后，仅从分数计算两个数。第一，排序稳定数 $\\tau _{t}$（式 1）：当前 100 个候选的排序与上一级排序有多相似，用 Kendall 秩相关（一个对并列做了校正的版本，取值从 -1 完全相反到 +1 完全相同）衡量；在最开始的第一级把它置为 0，因为没有上一级排序。由于它只看排序，所以不在意分数的绝对大小或缩放尺度。第二，分离裕度 $m_{t}$（式 2）：第一名比 top-100 外第一名（刚刚落榜项）领先多少，除以 top-100 内部分数的离散程度（分母里加一个极小常数以避免除以零）。这两个数都不使用任何相关性标签——它们纯粹来自冻结检索器自己的分数。\n\n*排序稳定信号 $\\tau _{t}$ 定义为第 t 次与第 t-1 次计算增量下 top-k 候选排序之间的 Kendall 秩相关；t=1 时无定义，置为 0。*\n$$ \\tau_t = \\mathrm{KendallTau}\\big(\\pi(s_t[1{:}k]),\\, \\pi(s_{t-1}[1{:}k])\\big),\\qquad \\tau_1 := 0 \\tag{1} $$\n\n\n*分离裕度 $m_{t}$ 是 top-1 分数与第 k+1 名（首个落榜）分数之差除以 top-k 内部分数跨度的无量纲比值，使停止判定锚定在分数几何上且无需跨量纲权重。*\n$$ m_t = \\frac{s_t[1] - s_t[k+1]}{s_t[1] - s_t[k] + \\varepsilon} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: $\\tau _{t}$ 回答“多跑一级是否改变了排序”，而且因为它只关心排序，所以不在意分数尺度或校准；$m_{t}$ 回答“第一名是否明显领先”。\n\n### 停止/升级控制器\n*逐 query 判断何时再加算力也不会改变 top-k 排序，并带防早停崩溃的稳定器及其一次性标定。*\n\n4. 在各级上循环。在每一级 t（只在 t 至少为 2、即存在上一级排序后才开始检查）：若排序足够稳定（稳定数达到或超过一个学到的阈值）或第一名明显足够领先（裕度达到或超过一个学到的阈值）就停止——但只要裕度低于一个安全下限，即使排序看起来稳定也绝不停止。若两个条件都不满足，就爬到下一级，直至上限（等于该阶梯能提供的最高一级，从而你绝不会比最贵的固定设定花更多）。停止时，返回你停在那一级的 top-100，并记录这花了多少算力（所用算术运算总量，也简单地报告为你停在了第几级）。这个停止点决定最终答案——它挑选用户实际收到的是哪一级的排序。\n\n*控制器在超过 $t_{min}$ 后，第一次满足排序足够稳定或裕度足够大时停止；但只要裕度低于下限 $m_{floor}$ 就不停止，以防在稳定但低裕度的排序上提前终止。*\n$$ \\mathrm{stop}(t) = \\big[t \\geq t_{\\min}\\big] \\wedge \\big( \\tau_t \\geq \\theta_\\tau \\;\\vee\\; m_t \\geq \\theta_m \\big) \\wedge \\big[m_t \\geq m_{\\text{floor}}\\big] \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 停止的时刻正是再多算也不会改变答案的时刻；下限可防止它在看似稳定却尚未明确分出胜负的排序上提前收手。\n5. 一次性、离线地，在一份留出的 query 集合（约占数据的 20%，与测试集分开）上调这四个阈值——该集合是有相关性标签的。为每个阈值尝试一个小网格：稳定阈值从 0.80 到 0.99，裕度阈值从 1.0 到 3.0，最低级数从 2 到 4，裕度下限从 0.0 到 1.0。对每个组合，在这份留出集上测量平均算力和检索质量（nDCG@10），丢弃任何质量比“始终用最高级”下降超过一个允许小容差（默认 nDCG@10 半分）的组合，并在剩下的组合中挑平均算力最低的，遇到并列时偏向更保守（最低级数更高）的那个。标签只在此调参步骤中使用；实际检索时绝不需要任何标签。\n   - _为什么_: 它让你预先声明愿意用多少质量换速度，同时保持线上方法是 label-free 的。\n\n### 机制验证\n*把排序稳定隔离为起作用的信号，并展示跨基准、跨阶梯的 Pareto 占优。*\n\n6. 构建两个仅改变停止信号的对照版本，其余一切（封装、冻结短名单、循环、评测）完全相同。负对照：把排序稳定数换成分数熵——用温度固定为 1.0 的 softmax 把 top-100 分数变成一个概率分布，再取它的熵（一个标准的“有多分散/多不确定”的度量）；当熵足够低时停止（熵低表示模型有信心），并像之前一样在留出集上为它单独调自己的阈值，使该对照获得公平的最佳设定。正对照：保留稳定信号但完全去掉裕度部分，使控制器仅在排序稳定时才停止。然后在相同算力下比较三个版本：各自得到多少质量，以及各自挽回了多少算力节省。\n   - _为什么_: 若熵效果一样好，说明增益来自分数校准而非排序稳定——那将证伪该主张；只用 $\\tau _{t}$ 的版本则验证是排序稳定在起作用。\n7. 在多个基准上测试调好的控制器——MMEB 和 MMEB-V2（多模态嵌入基准）、ViDoSeek（视觉文档检索）、以及一个图文检索集如 Flickr30K 或 COCO 1K——并在全部三种加算力方式上测试（更多向量、更多 reasoning 过程、更多 query 改写）。对照三个基线：始终用最便宜的一级、始终用最高级、以及一个允许偷看答案的 oracle——它为每个 query 找出已能基本达到最佳质量的最小级数（一个不可达的最佳情形，用作权衡曲线的下界）。报告检索质量（nDCG@10 与 Recall@10），以及每个 query 平均用了多少算力、以及最差 10% 和 1%（尾部）用了多少。这表明自适应方法胜过任何固定预算设定，且该思想能跨越不同的加算力方式迁移，而非只在单一基准上成立。\n   - _为什么_: 它表明自适应曲线胜过任何固定预算设定，且该思想能跨越不同的“加算力方式”迁移，而非只在单一基准上成立。\n\n"},{"id":"78","run_dir":"run_prompt78_moeequal","index":78,"title":"What Equal-Resource MoE Buys and Pays: A Per-Capability Ledger of Sparse vs Dense LLMs","title_zh":"等资源下 MoE 的得与失：稀疏与稠密大语言模型的逐能力账本","method_name":"Per-Capability Equal-Resource Ledger (Delta_CAP ledger) with per-parameter token-exposure (E_p) predictor and ledger-driven differentiated data reuse","hook":"At strictly equal total parameters, compute, and data, the headline 'MoE beats dense' is an average that hides opposite signs underneath: we predict the equal-resource MoE is AHEAD on breadth-of-knowledge capabilities and BEHIND on depth-of-composition capabilities, and that the sign of each capability's gap is set by how many tokens its supporting parameters were actually trained on, not by aggregate perplexity.","anchor_pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","anchor_pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","domain_category":"LLM Pretraining, Architecture & Scaling","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf decomposes the equal-resource MoE-vs-dense outcome into a per-capability ledger: which capability families the sparse model is ahead on and which it is behind on at identical N/C/D remains a single averaged number, so the field cannot say where the win comes from or what is paid for it.","pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by constructing matched MoE/dense model pairs at strictly fixed N/C/D and a capability-stratified instance set so the only varying axis is the sparse-vs-dense allocation of the same budget; the headline artifact is the signed divergence vector Delta_CAP (apparent aggregate win decomposed into per-capability gains and losses) rather than a single leaderboard score, exactly the C02 move of reporting the confound-isolated gap as the primary result.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions whether the equal-resource verdict should be a single architecture-wide scalar at all, rather than asking whether MoE and dense are even comparable along one axis when the same budget is allocated to a structurally different number of token-conditioned subnetworks seeing each parameter a different number of times.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by relocating the comparison signal from the assumed locus (a single architecture-wide aggregate scalar) to an overlooked locus the field treated as invariant: the per-parameter token-exposure E_p = (tokens seen by parameter p) implied by the activation rate, which differs systematically between dense (every parameter sees every token) and MoE (each expert parameter sees only its routed token share). The pivot is the C01 'relocate the load-bearing signal to a different representational locus and validate empirically' move; it is empirical (validated by the sign-split in Delta_CAP), not a theorem-tightening, matching contribution_type empirical_reveal.","is_anchor":false},{"gap":"The data trade-off that the equal-resource win depends on (openalex:W4415110878) is treated as a uniform global data-reuse / epoch count; no leaf asks whether the data shortfall is itself capability-heterogeneous so that reuse should be allocated unevenly across the data rather than applied as one knob.","pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by partitioning the training corpus into capability-bearing slices, measuring per-slice token-exposure starvation from the same Delta_CAP ledger, and assigning a differentiated data-reuse (epoch) rate per slice — more reuse where the sparse model is measured to be starved — instead of one global epoch count; the C04 error-decomposition spine bounds how differentiated reuse recovers the dense baseline on the deficit slices while a uniform-vs-differentiated ablation shows the partition, not extra epochs, drives the recovery.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"large language model pretraining; Mixture-of-Experts vs dense architecture under matched resource budgets","n_papers":51,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":27},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10},{"source":"openreview","n":2}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":14,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Dense Training, Sparse Inference: Rethinking Training of Mixture-of-Experts Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Lory: Fully Differentiable Mixture-of-Experts for Autoregressive Language Model Pre-training"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Not All Experts are Equal: Efficient Expert Pruning and Skipping for Mixture-of-Experts Large Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Time-MoE: Billion-Scale Time Series Foundation Models with Mixture of Experts"},{"source":"openalex","title":"The Ultimate Guide to Fine-Tuning LLMs from Basics to Breakthroughs: An Exhaustive Review of Technologies, Research, Best Practices, Applied Research Challenges and Opportunities"},{"source":"openalex","title":"AdapMoE: Adaptive Sensitivity-based Expert Gating and Management for Efficient MoE Inference"}],"more":8},{"year":2025,"n":26,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Parameters vs FLOPs: Scaling Laws for Optimal Sparsity for Mixture-of-Experts Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Towards Greater Leverage: Scaling Laws for Efficient Mixture-of-Experts Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Scaling Laws for Upcycling Mixture-of-Experts Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"FLAME-MoE: A Transparent End-to-End Research Platform for Mixture-of-Experts Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"EchoVLM: Dynamic Mixture-of-Experts Vision-Language Model for Universal Ultrasound Intelligence"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Leveraging PyTorch for Hardware-Aware Optimization in Efficient Mixture-of-Experts Large Language Model Inference"}],"more":20},{"year":2026,"n":12,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"},{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Generalizing GNNs with Tokenized Mixture of Experts"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Mixture-of-Experts Models in Vision: Routing, Optimization, and Generalization"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Task-Specific Efficiency Analysis: When Small Language Models Outperform Large Language Models"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"MoSE: Mixture of Slimmable Experts for Efficient and Adaptive Language Models"}],"more":6}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":10,"share":0.196},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":10,"share":0.196},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":7,"share":0.137},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":7,"share":0.137},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":6,"share":0.118},{"pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","count":5,"share":0.098},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":4,"share":0.078},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":4,"share":0.078}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Under strictly equal resource (identical total parameters N, training compute C, and data budget D), the recent literature has established that a sparse Mixture-of-Experts model can match or beat a dense model in an optimal activation-rate region (openalex:W4415110878), and scaling-law work has located the compute-optimal sparsity frontier (semanticscholar:2559ddde36d4a861ab54b881bbd15eb40918b159) and the granularity that raises expressivity (openalex:W4417514285). But every one of these results collapses the comparison to a SINGLE scalar — validation perplexity or an aggregate downstream score — so the verdict 'MoE wins here' hides the fact that at equal N/C/D the sparse model and the dense model are NOT the same model with a different efficiency knob: they spread the same parameter budget over a different number of distinct token-conditioned subnetworks and see each parameter on a different number of tokens. Consequently nobody can say, before training, on WHICH classes of capability the equal-resource MoE will be ahead of the dense baseline and on which it will fall behind, nor why; the aggregate-scalar framing cannot produce a per-capability sign because it has averaged the sign away, and the data trade-off the seed paper resolves with uniform data reuse (openalex:W4415110878) is applied as a single global epoch count rather than where the sparse model is actually capacity-starved.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415110878","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Introduces a unified parameterization framework, searches an optimal MoE architecture, then finds an activation-rate region where MoE beats dense at equal total parameters, compute, and data, with the resulting data shortfall resolved by uniform data reuse (validated across ~200 2B and >50 7B models). Its verdict is a single aggregate-performance comparison at the sweet spot: it never decomposes the equal-resource win into which capability families the MoE gains versus loses relative to the matched dense model, gives no pre-training predictor of the per-capability sign, and reuses data as a single global knob rather than targeting the capabilities the sparse model is starved on."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:2559ddde36d4a861ab54b881bbd15eb40918b159","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Derives scaling laws for the compute-optimal sparsity (active-vs-total parameter split) of MoE LMs under a fixed compute budget, treating loss as a smooth function of N, FLOPs, and sparsity. The law is fit to a single aggregate loss, so it predicts where the optimal split sits but says nothing about the heterogeneity of that loss across capability types, and cannot tell you that the same sparsity is optimal for, say, factual recall and for multi-step reasoning simultaneously."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4417514285","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Proves that finer expert granularity increases the expressivity of an MoE layer at fixed active parameters. The result is an upper-bound / capacity statement about the function class, not a statement about which capabilities a finite training budget actually realizes, so it cannot explain why a more-expressive MoE can still lose to dense on some capability at equal N/C/D."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:c67c4c81beed122d7f94580d8816a6dc68867ec4","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Trains MoE densely and infers sparsely to recover the quality of a parameter-heavy MoE at lower inference cost, explicitly noting MoE needs 2-4x more parameters than dense for comparable quality. It targets the inference-time efficiency residue and does not study the equal-total-parameter regime where dense and MoE have the same parameter count, so it does not address per-capability parity at fixed N."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"large language model pretraining; Mixture-of-Experts vs dense architecture under matched resource budgets","venue":"ICLR 2026","time":"2026","data":["large-scale text pretraining corpora (e.g. open web / The Pile / RedPajama-scale)","standard LM downstream eval suites (knowledge QA, reasoning, code, multilingual)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day) single-researcher cloud budget","expertise":"ML researcher comfortable training small-to-mid LMs and running controlled scaling ablations","preference":"both","baseline":"a dense LLM matched to the MoE on total parameter count N, total training compute C, and training-token budget D (the strictly-equal-resource setting of the seed paper)","limitation":"current equal-resource MoE-vs-dense comparisons report a single aggregate verdict (MoE wins in an activation-rate sweet spot) but do not tell you WHICH capabilities MoE buys and which it sacrifices, nor predict the sign of the per-capability gap in advance","contribution_type":"empirical_reveal","_inferred_fields":["domain","venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object every leg reads from and writes to is the signed per-capability equal-resource gap ledger Delta_CAP, a vector indexed by capability slice i, defined as Delta_CAP_i = score_MoE(i) - score_dense(i) where score is the slice's de-confounded accuracy and the two models are trained under strictly identical total parameter count N, training compute C, and token budget D (the seed paper's equal-resource setting, openalex:W4415110878). LEG 1 (diagnostic, C02) builds Delta_CAP: hold N, C, D fixed and vary ONLY the sparse-vs-dense allocation (a small grid of activation rates a in {1.0 (dense), 0.5, 0.25, 0.125} where a=active/total parameters, all at the seed paper's optimal-region settings), and evaluate every model on a capability-stratified instance set where each slice isolates one capability and blocks the leaderboard confound via construction (closed-book factual recall from timestamp-gated facts; multi-step arithmetic/logic generated from a formal spec with verifiable intermediate steps; long-range multi-hop composition; rare-token / tail-vocabulary modeling; in-context pattern induction). Ground truth for each slice comes from how the instance was built (a known derivation path or a planted answer), never from the models' own consensus, so Delta_CAP_i is the confound-isolated divergence, reported as the headline. LEG 2 (audit/pivot, C01) explains the SIGN of Delta_CAP_i by relocating the comparison signal to the load-bearing variable per-parameter token-exposure E_p: for a dense model every parameter sees all D tokens, so E_p = D; for an MoE with activation rate a and balanced routing each expert parameter sees on expectation E_p = a*D tokens (the routed share), a quantity the aggregate-scalar framing never surfaces. The pivot's empirical claim is that capabilities whose competence is carried by broadly-shared, frequently-activated parameters (factual breadth, tail vocabulary — served by shared experts / the always-on path) get POSITIVE Delta_CAP because MoE buys more total parameters at equal N-budget split favorably, whereas capabilities requiring deep composition across many specialized parameters get NEGATIVE Delta_CAP because those parameters are each starved to a*D token-exposure and underfit; the sign is thus predicted by E_p-per-capability, not by aggregate perplexity. LEG 3 (differentiated treatment, C04) acts on the same ledger: partition the corpus into slices aligned to the capability slices, measure per-slice exposure starvation as starve_i = max(0, D_required(i) - E_p(i)) estimated from Delta_CAP_i's magnitude on the deficit (negative) slices, and allocate a per-slice data-reuse rate r_i proportional to starve_i (reuse data on the starved slices more, holding the GLOBAL token budget D fixed by reallocating epochs across slices rather than adding tokens) so the differentiated reuse lifts the negative Delta_CAP_i toward zero while leaving positive slices untouched. Legs 1 and 2 share machinery completely (the ledger plus E_p); Leg 3 is a separate training-time module that consumes the ledger to set r_i, with an error decomposition bounding the recoverable deficit and a uniform-vs-differentiated reuse ablation proving the allocation, not extra epochs, is what closes the negative slices.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) Legs 1 and 2 share machinery because the diagnostic's output (Delta_CAP) and the audit's load-bearing variable (E_p) are two readings of the same fixed-budget comparison — the sign the audit predicts is literally the sign the diagnostic measures, so forcing them into separate modules would break the shared_object thread; Leg 3 needs a separate training-time module because allocating reuse is an intervention, not a measurement, but it still reads the same ledger as input, which is why the thread stays shared_object rather than sequential. (b) Considered making Leg 2 a formal capacity/sample-complexity theorem (an E_p-vs-error bound) but rejected it: the contribution_type is empirical_reveal and a clean theorem here would require distributional assumptions the equal-resource regime does not verify (the C05/C19 identifiability/bound clusters' failure mode), so E_p stays an empirically-validated load-bearing variable. Avoided regression to collateral node c0 (classical per-parameter sample-complexity): rather than re-deriving a generic capacity bound, the mechanism uses E_p only as the measurable signed-gap predictor and validates it by intervention, which is a source the lineage tree does not occupy.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: train the 4-checkpoint matched grid (dense + three MoE activation rates) at ~300M total parameters under identical N/C/D, evaluate on the 5 de-confounded capability slices, and read the signed ledger Delta_CAP. If the candidate is right, Delta_CAP splits in sign across slices rather than being uniformly positive: factual-breadth and tail-vocabulary slices show positive Delta_CAP while multi-step-composition slices show negative Delta_CAP, and the per-slice sign is predicted by the load-bearing variable per-parameter token-exposure E_p (low E_p -> negative gap, high E_p -> positive gap) with high rank correlation. Mechanism distinguisher on E_p with a non-tautological negative control: take the differentiated-data-reuse intervention that raises E_p only on the starved (negative) slices and SCRAMBLE the slice-to-reuse assignment (permute which slices receive the extra epochs while holding the total reuse budget and total token count D fixed); if E_p is the mechanism, the correctly-targeted reuse drives the downstream slice ACCURACY of the starved capabilities back up toward the dense baseline whereas the scrambled assignment leaves that downstream accuracy at the un-intervened level, isolating that the gain comes from where exposure was added, not from extra epochs. A positive control trains a stripped model whose ONLY difference is matching dense-level E_p on one chosen starved slice (by routing that slice's tokens to a shared always-on path) and should recover most of that slice's accuracy deficit, converting the falsifier into a constructive identification of E_p as the driver.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415110878","delta":"They report that an MoE in an optimal activation-rate region beats dense at equal total parameters/compute/data as a single aggregate verdict and resolve the data shortfall with uniform data reuse; we decompose that verdict into a signed per-capability ledger Delta_CAP, show its sign is predicted by per-parameter token-exposure E_p, and replace uniform reuse with a ledger-driven differentiated per-slice reuse allocation."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:2559ddde36d4a861ab54b881bbd15eb40918b159","delta":"They fit a scaling law for compute-optimal sparsity against a single aggregate loss; we measure that the optimal sparsity is capability-dependent (the loss they fit has heterogeneous per-capability sign) so a single optimal-sparsity scalar cannot be right for breadth and composition simultaneously."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4417514285","delta":"They prove finer expert granularity raises the MoE layer's expressivity (a function-class upper bound at fixed active params); we show that higher expressivity does not determine which capabilities a finite equal-resource budget actually realizes, because realized per-capability competence is gated by E_p, not by expressivity."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:c67c4c81beed122d7f94580d8816a6dc68867ec4","delta":"They train densely and infer sparsely to cut the MoE parameter premium at the inference stage; we keep both training and inference at strictly equal total parameters and instead characterize and repair the per-capability deficit at training time via differentiated data reuse."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4415110878","what_step_was_missed":"The seed paper established the single-scalar equal-resource verdict and used uniform data reuse to pay the data trade-off, but to already contain our contribution it would have needed to construct a confound-isolated capability-stratified instrument and read the per-capability SIGNED divergence off the matched grid, then tie that sign to a per-parameter token-exposure quantity E_p — a measurement primitive (the signed ledger) plus a load-bearing predictor variable that its aggregate-scalar methodology never builds; without the signed ledger there is no slice on which to allocate differentiated reuse, so the uniform-reuse step was the only one available to them."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":272,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"Layer 1 hard floor did not fire: gap_closure_reject_check has no candidate_match=yes (aggregate borderline only), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat is setting-overlap not exact-mechanism. recipe_application_check.verdict=applied on all three entries (C02 reports Delta_CAP as headline, C01 relocates to E_p with mechanistic account, C04 partitions the dataset with an error-decomposition spine), so the leading incremental-output cause is absent. The remaining borderlines (C02 ecological-validity/scale-scope, C01 novelty-boundary vs adjacent knowledge-attribution work) sit in non-load-bearing surfacing aspects, so the correct call is advance with these folded into Phase 4 reviewer_concerns_and_responses rather than revise.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf decomposes the equal-resource MoE-vs-dense outcome into a per-capability ledger: which capability families the sparse model is ahead on and which it is behind on at identical N/C/D remains a single averaged number, so the field cannot say where the win comes from or what is paid for it.","main_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failures are a diagnostic that only re-confirms a known shortcut, a synthetic-only instrument with no transfer to real data, a circular oracle built on the system's own consensus, and a small-N instrument carrying broad capability claims.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A diagnostic that only re-confirms a shortcut already known in advance, surfacing no previously unmeasurable failure, is read as confirmatory rather than as a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The signed per-capability ledger Delta_CAP surfaces a previously unmeasured sign-split (positive on breadth, negative on composition) that the field's aggregate-scalar verdict has never reported, so it is not a re-confirmation."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a synthetic-ground-truth instrument only on synthetic data, without demonstrating that the controlled finding transfers to real-world instances, leaves ecological validity unestablished and undermines the central claim.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"Several slices use formal-spec synthetic instances; core_mechanism step 2 mixes in timestamp-gated real facts and the falsification names real downstream slice accuracy, but transfer-to-realistic-instances is asserted rather than itemized, a non-load-bearing surfacing for Phase 4."},{"lesson_quoted":"Building the instrument around one contested definition of the target property means it cannot independently confirm that the definition is correct, and reviewers flag the resulting circularity.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Each slice's ground truth comes from construction (known derivation path / planted answer), not from a contested self-authored definition or the models' own outputs."},{"lesson_quoted":"Resting an unsupervised evaluation on the unverified premise that the systems under test can reliably judge one another stakes the entire method on an assumption that collapses under scrutiny.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The oracle is construction-derived and independent of the evaluand; no model-judges-model step exists."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pairing a single-task or small-sample instrument with broad capability claims triggers a scope-mismatch rejection, and assembling retrieval or engineering blocks without an isolating scientific insight reads as application rather than research.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The instrument is multi-slice (5 capability families) which mitigates single-task scope, but the broad 'equal-resource verdict' claim is validated at one small (~300M) scale; the scale-consistency assumption is borrowed from the seed paper and should be surfaced as a reviewer concern."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions whether the equal-resource verdict should be a single architecture-wide scalar at all, rather than asking whether MoE and dense are even comparable along one axis when the same budget is allocated to a structurally different number of token-conditioned subnetworks seeing each parameter a different number of times.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is a relocation demonstrated but not adversarially closed, a novelty-boundary collapse where the 'new' locus was already used by prior work, reintroducing the dissolved assumption via privileged access, or a demonstration with no mechanistic account of why the new locus carries the signal.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a relocated signal is 'stealthier' or 'harder to remove' without defeating an adaptive defender who searches the same new locus leaves the central claim unverified.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"This is a security-adversary lesson; the analogue here is that the relocated signal (E_p) must causally drive the outcome, which the falsification's scramble negative control and positive control establish, so the relocation is closed by intervention not mere demonstration."},{"lesson_quoted":"Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work — normalization statistics, activation-similarity losses, semantic concept triggers — collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"Per-parameter token-exposure is adjacent to tokens-per-parameter scaling-coverage work in collision_hits; differentiation_from_lit makes the difference explicit (per-capability SIGN vs aggregate scaling), but the boundary against 'Deconstructing Pre-training: Knowledge Attribution in MoE and Dense Models' should be stated."},{"lesson_quoted":"A defense whose relocation silently depends on a clean reference model or a known anomaly distribution reintroduces precisely the strong assumption the move was supposed to eliminate.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"E_p is computed from routing statistics and the activation rate, requiring no clean reference model or external distribution."},{"lesson_quoted":"Demonstrating the new locus only on fixed, non-adaptive or outdated baselines while omitting any account of why it works reads as a stacked pipeline of existing components rather than a principled shift.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism gives the mechanistic account (expert parameters see only a*D tokens so depth-of-composition capabilities underfit), and the baseline is the matched dense model, the strongest equal-resource comparator."},{"lesson_quoted":"Wiring off-the-shelf generators or tools into a new attack setting without a structural reason for the locus change gets judged as engineering integration, not insight.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The locus change (scalar -> E_p) has a structural reason: MoE and dense allocate the same N over different parameter-token-exposure, which the aggregate scalar averages away."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"The data trade-off that the equal-resource win depends on (openalex:W4415110878) is treated as a uniform global data-reuse / epoch count; no leaf asks whether the data shortfall is itself capability-heterogeneous so that reuse should be allocated unevenly across the data rather than applied as one knob.","main_pattern":"heterogeneous_decomposition","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The cluster fails when a sensitivity/redundancy proxy is presented as novelty (rediscovering known mixed-precision results), when the uniform baseline or cheap alternative is omitted, when validated only at toy scale, or when no analysis of why the heterogeneity exists is given.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Presenting a sensitivity or redundancy proxy as the novelty invites the verdict that it rediscovers known mixed-precision or low-rank results unless it is sharply differentiated from the obvious prior criterion.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The partition criterion is the measured signed Delta_CAP / E_p starvation, not a generic sensitivity proxy, and it is differentiated from uniform data reuse (the obvious prior criterion the seed paper used)."},{"lesson_quoted":"Omitting comparison against both the strongest uniform baseline and the obvious cheap alternative (SVD/PCA, structured dropout, a natively trained smaller model) leaves reviewers unable to tell whether the partition buys anything at all.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism step 7 explicitly trains a uniform-reuse control matched on total tokens; the uniform-vs-differentiated ablation is the spine of Leg 3."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a storage or throughput claim only on toy-scale models — where the compression bottleneck does not actually bite — undermines the entire motivation no matter how clean the method is.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"Validation is at ~300M scale; the equal-resource data trade-off does bite there (the seed paper's optimal region is scale-consistent), but the small-scale-only choice is a surfacing for Phase 4 feasibility/reviewer concerns."},{"lesson_quoted":"A clever partition with no measured real-world deployment metric (no inference latency or memory speedup) reads as a proxy-only contribution and stalls at borderline.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The deployment metric here is downstream per-slice accuracy recovery (the real task outcome), not a proxy; this is a quality contribution, not a memory/latency one, so the latency-metric lesson does not apply."},{"lesson_quoted":"Skipping any analysis of why the heterogeneity exists — the data or value distribution that drives the partition — makes the technical novelty and the potential impact impossible to assess.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The why-it-exists analysis IS Leg 2: per-parameter token-exposure E_p explains why the data shortfall concentrates on low-exposure capability slices."},{"lesson_quoted":"Bolting together established components (distillation plus pruning plus calibration) without an error bound or artifact specific to the new setting reads as incremental even when the target application is timely and important.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism specifies an error decomposition bounding recoverable deficit per slice, an artifact specific to the equal-resource setting, rather than bolting established compression components."}],"verdict":"clear"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No gap_closure entry triggered a Reject lesson with candidate_match=yes. The aggregate is borderline, driven by the C02 anchor entry (ecological-validity and scale-scope lessons borderline) and the C01 audit entry (novelty-boundary against adjacent token-coverage / knowledge-attribution work borderline); both are surfacings, not load-bearing structural failures."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf decomposes the equal-resource MoE-vs-dense outcome into a per-capability ledger: which capability families the sparse model is ahead on and which it is behind on at identical N/C/D remains a single averaged number, so the field cannot say where the win comes from or what is paid for it.","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Construct a controlled set of evaluation instances in which exactly one named confound is blocked or independently varied, then report the divergence between apparent and de-confounded performance as the primary result rather than an aggregate leaderboard score.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism Leg 1 holds N/C/D fixed and varies only the sparse-vs-dense allocation, evaluating on capability-stratified instances each blocking the leaderboard confound by construction, and reports the signed divergence vector Delta_CAP as the headline rather than an aggregate score — the C02 signature move is performed directly.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions whether the equal-resource verdict should be a single architecture-wide scalar at all, rather than asking whether MoE and dense are even comparable along one axis when the same budget is allocated to a structurally different number of token-conditioned subnetworks seeing each parameter a different number of times.","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Relocate the load-bearing signal from the assumed representational locus to an overlooked locus the field treated as irrelevant or invariant, and demonstrate empirically that the property of interest manifests there, with a mechanistic account of why the new locus carries the signal.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism Leg 2 relocates the comparison signal from the assumed locus (a single architecture-wide aggregate scalar) to the overlooked per-parameter token-exposure E_p, and gives the mechanistic account (expert parameters see only a*D tokens) plus empirical validation via the Delta_CAP sign-split — the C01 relocate-and-validate move is performed.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"The data trade-off that the equal-resource win depends on (openalex:W4415110878) is treated as a uniform global data-reuse / epoch count; no leaf asks whether the data shortfall is itself capability-heterogeneous so that reuse should be allocated unevenly across the data rather than applied as one knob.","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Discriminate components of an over-provisioned artifact (weights, activations, KV buffer, sampling trajectory, or a dataset) by a measured criterion into high-impact and near-redundant populations and apply a tailored treatment to each, with an error/sensitivity decomposition that bounds how the differentiated treatment recovers the original objective.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism Leg 3 partitions the dataset (an artifact the C04 tactical pattern explicitly lists) by measured per-slice exposure starvation, applies a differentiated per-slice reuse rate vs a uniform control, and supplies an error decomposition bounding recoverable deficit — the C04 measured-partition-plus-error-decomposition move is performed on data rather than weights.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"All three entries instantiate their cited cluster's signature move: C02 reports the confound-isolated divergence (Delta_CAP) as the headline, C01 relocates the signal to E_p with a mechanistic account, and C04 partitions the dataset by a measured criterion with an error-decomposition spine."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["controlled_diagnostic_design","assumption_audit_and_pivot","heterogeneous_decomposition"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"The three 2-way subsets (CDD+AAP, CDD+HD, AAP+HD) none match the three flagged compositions, all of which pair heterogeneous_decomposition with self_supervised_signal_engineering, structural_prior_encoding, or architectural_operator_substitution; none of those three partners is in the composition set."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"openalex:W4415110878","threat_source":"lit_table","subsumption_argument":"The seed/anchor paper establishes that an equal-resource MoE in an optimal activation-rate region beats dense and resolves the data shortfall with uniform data reuse, so it owns the aggregate equal-resource verdict. The candidate's claim stands or falls on whether anything remains beyond that verdict: it does, because the seed reports only a single scalar and uniform reuse, whereas the candidate constructs the signed per-capability ledger, ties its sign to per-parameter token-exposure E_p, and replaces uniform reuse with ledger-driven differentiated allocation — none of which the seed's aggregate-scalar methodology produces. The overlap is in setting (strictly equal N/C/D), not in mechanism (signed ledger + E_p predictor + differentiated reuse), so it is not exact-mechanism overlap.","addressable_via":"Already addressed in differentiation_from_lit and what_step_was_missed; to further harden, Phase 4 should foreground that the contribution is the decomposition and intervention, not a re-run of the seed's aggregate comparison."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# What Equal-Resource MoE Buys and Pays: A Per-Capability Ledger of Sparse vs Dense LLMs\n\n**Method.** Per-Capability Equal-Resource Ledger (Delta_CAP ledger) with per-parameter token-exposure (E_p) predictor and ledger-driven differentiated data reuse\n\n## Motivation\nIf you have a fixed parameter budget for a large language model, you can spend it on a dense model (every parameter used on every token) or on a sparse Mixture-of-Experts model, or MoE (the model is split into many 'experts' and only a few fire per token). Recent careful work showed that, when you hold the total parameter count, the training compute, and the amount of training data all exactly equal, a well-tuned MoE can actually beat the dense model (openalex:W4415110878). The catch is that this verdict is a single number, usually average perplexity or an average test score. A single average cannot tell you which kinds of skill the MoE is better at and which it is worse at, because it has already blended the wins and losses together.\n\nThe key insight we build on is that, at equal total parameters, the dense and the MoE are not the same model with a knob turned. They split the same parameters across a different number of small token-routed subnetworks, so each parameter is trained on a different number of tokens. A dense parameter sees every training token (call this exposure D). An MoE expert parameter, with activation rate a (the fraction of parameters active per token), sees on average only a times D tokens. So expert parameters are individually trained on far less data. We predict this is exactly why the average hides opposite signs: skills carried by widely-shared, always-on parameters (broad factual knowledge, rare words) get a boost from the extra total parameters, while skills that need many specialized parameters working together (multi-step reasoning) suffer because each of those parameters was starved of training tokens.\n\nPrior work stopped short for concrete reasons. The equal-resource paper (openalex:W4415110878, arXiv June 2025) reported only the single aggregate win and paid the data shortfall by reusing data uniformly, with no per-skill breakdown to allocate reuse against. The scaling-law paper (semanticscholar..., ICML 2025) fit one optimal sparsity number to one average loss, never asking if that number differs by skill. The expressivity paper (openalex:W4417514285, arXiv May 2025) proved finer experts can represent more, but representing more is not the same as actually learning it within a finite training budget.\n\nWhen this gap closes, a practitioner can decide, before paying for a full run, whether sparsity helps the specific skills they care about, by reading off our signed skill-by-skill ledger and predicting each skill's sign from how many tokens its supporting parameters saw. The uniform data-reuse trick then becomes just one case of a smarter rule: reuse data more on exactly the skills the sparse model was starved on.\n\n## Method\n### Background: matched equal-resource grid\n*Produce the strictly equal-resource dense/MoE checkpoints the whole study reads from.*\n\n1. Pretrain 4 models at one small scale (about 300M total parameters), keeping total parameters, training compute, and the number of training tokens exactly equal, and changing only the activation rate a (the fraction of parameters active per token) over {1.0 = dense, 0.5, 0.25, 0.125}. To make the budgets truly equal: keep total parameters identical by adjusting each expert's width and the number of experts so the sum matches the dense model; keep the token count identical by drawing all runs from one shared shuffled corpus; keep compute equal by using the same number of training steps, batch size, and sequence length. Use one tokenizer, the AdamW optimizer, a cosine learning-rate schedule with 10% warmup, and the same data-ordering seed.\n   - _Why_: If everything but sparse-vs-dense allocation is held fixed, any difference you measure can only come from that allocation.\n\n### Signed per-capability ledger (Delta_CAP)\n*Build the confound-isolated instrument and read the per-skill signed gap as the headline.*\n\n2. Build a test set split into about 5 skill slices, each with roughly 2,000-5,000 items in one shared format {prompt, correct answer, how-it-was-built, slice id}, where the correct answer is fixed by how each item was constructed, not by any model. Factual recall: closed-book questions about facts that only became true after a known date, taken from a dated knowledge source. Multi-step arithmetic/logic: expressions generated from a formal grammar, keeping the full checkable solution steps as the answer. Multi-hop composition: synthesized chains of k linked facts over a made-up relation graph. Rare-word (tail-vocabulary) modeling: predicting the next token for words in the bottom 10% by frequency. In-context pattern induction: held-out symbolic pattern-completion puzzles.\n   - _Why_: Construction-derived answers keep each skill clean and avoid letting the models grade themselves.\n3. Score every model on every slice and compute the signed gap (defined in the equation below) as the MoE score minus the dense score per slice. For each slice use the matching correctness check, all decoded greedily (temperature 0): exact-match for facts; exact-match plus a check of the solution steps for arithmetic; whole-chain correctness for multi-hop; top-1 next-token accuracy for rare words; completion accuracy for induction. Lay the results out as a 4 (activation rates) by 5 (slices) table with confidence intervals from resampling the items, and report the sign in each cell, not the average across cells.\n\n*The signed per-capability gap for activation rate a and capability slice i is the de-confounded MoE slice score minus the matched dense slice score; its per-slice sign, not its mean, is the headline.*\n$$ \\Delta_{\\mathrm{CAP}}(a,i) = \\mathrm{score}_{\\mathrm{MoE}}(a,i) - \\mathrm{score}_{\\mathrm{dense}}(i) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The signed slice-by-slice gap is exactly the thing the single average had hidden.\n\n### Token-exposure sign-predictor (E_p)\n*Relocate the explanatory signal to per-parameter token-exposure and show it predicts the gap's sign before training.*\n\n4. Compute per-parameter token-exposure (defined in the equation below): a dense parameter is trained on all D tokens, while an expert parameter at activation rate a sees on average a times D tokens, scaled by how often it is actually routed to. Treat always-on parts (the dense path, attention, embeddings, shared experts) as seeing all D tokens. To tie this to skills, run each slice's items through the model, record which experts fire in each layer, and call the slice's 'carrying experts' the smallest set that together handle at least 90% of that slice's routed tokens. The slice's exposure is the routed-share-weighted average over those experts plus the always-on path.\n\n*Per-parameter token-exposure: a dense parameter is trained on all D tokens, while an MoE expert parameter at activation rate a sees on expectation only the routed fraction a times D.*\n$$ E_p^{\\mathrm{dense}} = D, \\qquad E_p^{\\mathrm{expert}}(a) = a\\,D \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: How many tokens a parameter trained on is the plausible cause of whether the skill it supports is strong or weak.\n5. Check whether token-exposure predicts the sign of the gap. Treat each (activation rate, slice) pair as one data point (3 MoE rates by 5 slices = 15 points). Report the rank correlation between a slice's exposure and its signed gap, and fit a simple logistic model that predicts the gap's sign from the log of exposure, tested by holding out one slice at a time. The claim that exposure is the driver holds if higher exposure tracks more positive gaps and the negative-gap cells are the low-exposure ones.\n   - _Why_: If exposure predicts the sign before training, it becomes a usable pre-training decision rule, not just a label after the fact.\n\n### Ledger-driven differentiated data reuse\n*Turn the ledger into a targeted per-slice reuse rule and prove targeting (not extra epochs) recovers the starved skills.*\n\n6. Turn the ledger into a data-reuse plan. Split the training corpus into slices that match the skills (by tagging each document to the same skill categories using a lightweight classifier or the document's source metadata). For each starved (negative-gap) skill, give its corpus slice a reuse multiplier proportional to how far its exposure falls below what the skill needs (defined in the equation below), and rescale all multipliers so the total number of trained tokens stays exactly D — you reallocate passes over data, you do not add data. 【author decision: how to estimate the exposure a skill 'requires', and whether the extra reuse scales with the exposure shortfall or with the measured size of the negative gap, is a calibration choice the authors must make — shortfall-based versus gap-size-based targeting.】\n\n*Per-slice starvation is the shortfall of token-exposure below the slice's requirement; the differentiated reuse rate $r_{i}$ is proportional to starvation, renormalized so the total trained tokens stay at D (reallocated, not added).*\n$$ \\mathrm{starve}_i = \\max\\!\\left(0,\\; D_{\\mathrm{req}}(i) - E_p(i)\\right), \\qquad r_i \\propto \\mathrm{starve}_i,\\;\\; \\sum_i r_i\\, |S_i| = D \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Spending extra passes exactly where the sparse model was starved should help those skills without paying more total tokens.\n7. Retrain the best MoE three ways. 'Best' means the MoE activation rate with the highest overall downstream score among the three, the one a practitioner would actually pick. (1) Differentiated: oversample documents from each skill's corpus slice by its reuse multiplier, with an overall down-weighting so the total token count stays at D. (2) Uniform control: give every slice the same multiplier (same total tokens). (3) Scrambled control: use the same set of multipliers but shuffle which slice each one lands on (same total reuse). The two controls hold everything fixed except where the extra passes go.\n   - _Why_: The two controls separate 'targeting the right slices' from 'just doing more epochs.'\n8. Re-score the three retrained models on the same slices and look at how each slice's signed gap changed versus the original best MoE. The result confirms the mechanism if the differentiated model pulls its previously-negative slices toward zero (the change is bigger than item-resampling noise) without hurting its positive slices, while the uniform and scrambled controls do not show that targeted recovery. That separation is what proves the gain comes from adding exposure on the right slices, not merely from more passes over data.\n   - _Why_: If only the correctly-targeted model recovers the starved skills, the cause really is where the exposure was added.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 等资源下 MoE 的得与失：稀疏与稠密大语言模型的逐能力账本\n\n**方法名称.** Per-Capability Equal-Resource Ledger (Delta_CAP ledger) with per-parameter token-exposure (E_p) predictor and ledger-driven differentiated data reuse\n\n## 研究动机\n如果你有固定的参数预算来训练一个大语言模型，你可以把它花在 dense 模型上（每个参数都用在每个 token 上），也可以花在稀疏的 Mixture-of-Experts（MoE，把模型分成很多“专家”，每个 token 只激活少数几个）上。近期严谨的工作表明：当把总参数量、训练算力、训练数据量都严格设为相等时，调好的 MoE 确实能胜过 dense 模型（openalex:W4415110878）。问题在于，这个结论只是一个数字，通常是平均困惑度或平均测试分。单一平均值无法告诉你 MoE 在哪类能力上更强、在哪类上更弱，因为它已经把得与失混在一起了。\n\n我们依赖的关键洞见是：在总参数相等时，dense 与 MoE 并不是“同一个模型换个开关”。它们把同样的参数摊到了数量不同的、按 token 路由的小子网络上，于是每个参数被训练到的 token 数量也不同。一个 dense 参数会见到全部训练 token（记暴露量为 D）。一个激活率为 a（每个 token 激活参数的比例）的 MoE 专家参数，平均只见到 a 乘以 D 个 token。所以专家参数各自被训练的数据少得多。我们预测，这正是平均值掩盖了相反符号的原因：由广泛共享、始终激活的参数承载的能力（广度知识、罕见词）会因额外的总参数而获益；而需要许多专门参数协同的能力（多步推理）会受损，因为这些参数各自的训练 token 被“饿”到了。\n\n以往工作止步是有具体原因的。等资源那篇（openalex:W4415110878，arXiv 2025-06）只报告了单一的总体胜出，并用全局均匀的数据复用来弥补数据缺口，没有逐能力的分解可供分配复用。scaling-law 那篇（semanticscholar...，ICML 2025）把一个最优稀疏度数字拟合到一个平均 loss 上，从不追问这个数字是否因能力而异。expressivity 那篇（openalex:W4417514285，arXiv 2025-05）证明更细的专家能表示更多，但“能表示”不等于“在有限训练预算内真的学会”。\n\n当这个空白被填补，实践者就能在付出整次训练成本之前，通过读取我们这份有符号的逐能力账本、并用“其支撑参数见过多少 token”来预测每个能力的符号，判断稀疏化是否对他们关心的具体能力有帮助。届时均匀数据复用只是一个更聪明规则的特例：恰好在稀疏模型被饿到的能力上更多地复用数据。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景：等资源匹配网格\n*产出整个研究所依赖的严格等资源 dense/MoE 检查点。*\n\n1. 在一个小规模（约 300M 总参数）下预训练 4 个模型，把总参数、训练算力、训练 token 数严格保持相等，只改变激活率 a（每个 token 激活参数的比例），取 {1.0=dense, 0.5, 0.25, 0.125}。要让预算真正相等：通过调整每个专家的宽度和专家数量，使总参数量与 dense 模型一致；让所有模型从同一份打乱后的语料流中抽取相同 token 数，保证数据量一致；用相同的训练步数、batch size 与序列长度，使算力相等。统一使用一个 tokenizer、AdamW 优化器、带 10% warmup 的 cosine 学习率调度，以及相同的数据顺序随机种子。\n   - _为什么_: 除稀疏与稠密的分配方式外都固定，任何测到的差异就只能来自这个分配。\n\n### 逐能力有符号账本（Delta_CAP）\n*构建去混淆的测量工具，把逐能力有符号差作为主结果读出。*\n\n2. 构建一个去混淆、按能力分层的测试集，分成约 5 个能力切片，每个切片约 2000-5000 条样本，采用统一格式 {prompt, 正确答案, 构造来源/推导$, slice_{id}\\}$，正确答案由样本的构造方式决定，绝不由模型给出。事实回忆(factual recall)：基于带已知生效时间戳的事实，从带日期的知识源出闭卷问答。多步算术/逻辑：由形式文法生成表达式，并保留完整可校验的解题步骤作为答案。多跳组合(multi-hop composition)：在人造关系图上合成 k 跳事实链。罕见词(tail-vocabulary)建模：对频率最低 10% 的词做下一 token/完形预测。上下文模式归纳(in-context induction)：留出的符号模式补全题。每个切片都通过构造方式屏蔽排行榜式混淆。\n   - _为什么_: 由构造确定的答案能让每个能力保持干净，并避免让模型给自己打分。\n3. 在每个切片上给每个模型打分，按切片计算有符号差（见下式）= MoE 得分减 dense 得分。每个切片用对应的正确性判定，且都用贪心解码(temperature 0)：事实用精确匹配(exact-match)；算术用精确匹配再加对解题步骤的校验；多跳用整链正确性；罕见词用 top-1 下一 token 准确率；归纳用补全准确率。把结果排成一个 4(激活率$) \\times $ 5(切片) 的表格，并用对样本重采样(bootstrap)得到每格的置信区间，报告每一格的符号，而非跨格的平均。\n\n*对激活率 a 与能力切片 i，逐能力有符号差 $Delta_{CAP}$ 等于去混淆后的 MoE 切片得分减去匹配 dense 模型的切片得分；要看的是每个切片的符号而非其均值。*\n$$ \\Delta_{\\mathrm{CAP}}(a,i) = \\mathrm{score}_{\\mathrm{MoE}}(a,i) - \\mathrm{score}_{\\mathrm{dense}}(i) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这份逐切片的有符号差，正是单一平均值此前掩盖掉的东西。\n\n### token 暴露量符号预测器（E_p）\n*把解释信号迁移到逐参数 token 暴露量，并表明它能在训练前预测差的符号。*\n\n4. 计算逐参数 token 暴露量(见下式)：dense 参数在全部 D 个 token 上训练，而激活率为 a 的专家参数平均见到 a 乘以 D 个 token，并按其实际被路由到的份额加权。把始终激活的部分(dense 路径、attention、embedding、共享专家)记为见到全部 D 个 token。为把它与能力挂钩，把每个切片的样本喂进模型，记录每层哪些专家被激活，并把“承载该切片的专家”定义为：合计承担该切片至少 90% 被路由 token 的最小专家集合。该切片的暴露量即这些专家加上始终激活路径、按路由份额加权的平均暴露量。\n\n*逐参数 token 暴露量：dense 参数在全部 D 个 token 上训练，而激活率为 a 的 MoE 专家参数在期望上只见到被路由到的份额 a 乘以 D。*\n$$ E_p^{\\mathrm{dense}} = D, \\qquad E_p^{\\mathrm{expert}}(a) = a\\,D \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 一个参数训练过多少 token，是它所支撑能力强或弱的可信原因。\n5. 检验 token 暴露量能否预测差的符号。把每个(激活率, 切片)对当作一个数据点(3 个 MoE 激活率 $\\times  5$ 个切片 = 15 个点)。报告切片暴露量与其有符号差之间的秩相关(Spearman)，并拟合一个用暴露量对数预测差符号的简单 logistic 模型，用每次留出一个切片(leave-one-slice-out)来检验。若暴露量越高、差越偏正，且为负的格子恰是低暴露量的格子，则“暴露量是主因”的论断成立。\n   - _为什么_: 如果暴露量能在训练前预测符号，它就成了可用的训练前决策规则，而不只是事后标签。\n\n### 账本驱动的差异化数据复用\n*把账本变成有针对性的逐切片复用规则，并证明是“瞄准”而非“多跑 epoch”恢复了被饿到的能力。*\n\n6. 把账本变成数据复用方案。把训练语料切成与能力对应的切片(用轻量分类器或文档来源元数据，把每篇文档打到相同的能力类别上)。对每个被饿到(差为负)的能力，给它的语料切片一个复用倍率，与其暴露量低于该能力所需量的缺口成正比(见下式)，再对所有倍率重新归一，使训练 token 总量严格保持为 D——即重新分配对数据的遍历次数，而非新增数据。【作者需决定：如何估计某能力“所需”的暴露量，以及额外复用是与暴露量缺口成正比、还是与测得的负差大小成正比，这是作者必须做的标定选择——基于缺口 vs 基于差值大小的瞄准方式。】\n\n*每个切片的饥饿度是其 token 暴露量低于所需量的缺口；差异化复用率 $r_{i}$ 与饥饿度成正比，并归一化使训练 token 总量保持为 D（重新分配而非新增）。*\n$$ \\mathrm{starve}_i = \\max\\!\\left(0,\\; D_{\\mathrm{req}}(i) - E_p(i)\\right), \\qquad r_i \\propto \\mathrm{starve}_i,\\;\\; \\sum_i r_i\\, |S_i| = D \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 恰好在稀疏模型被饿到的地方多过几遍，应能在不增加总 token 的前提下提升这些能力。\n7. 把最佳 MoE 用三种方式重训。“最佳”指三种 MoE 激活率中总体下游得分最高的那个，也就是实践者真正会选的那个。(1) 差异化：按每个能力切片的复用倍率对其语料文档过采样，并整体下调权重使训练 token 总量保持为 D。(2) 均匀对照：所有切片用相同倍率(总 token 相同)。(3) 乱序对照：使用同一组倍率，但打乱每个倍率落到哪个切片(总复用量相同)。两个对照保持其余一切不变，只改变“额外遍数加在哪里”。\n   - _为什么_: 这两个对照能把“瞄准正确切片”与“只是多跑几遍”区分开。\n8. 在相同切片上对三个重训模型重新打分，看每个切片的有符号差相对原始最佳 MoE 如何变化。若差异化模型把此前为负的切片拉向零(变化超过样本重采样噪声)而不损害其为正的切片，且均匀与乱序对照都没有这种有针对性的恢复，就证实了该机制。这种区分正是“收益来自把暴露量加在正确切片上、而非仅仅多遍历数据”的证据。\n   - _为什么_: 若只有正确瞄准的模型才能恢复被饿到的能力，那原因就确实是“暴露量加在了哪里”。\n\n"},{"id":"79","run_dir":"run_prompt79_rtvideo","index":79,"title":"Rewritable Streaming Context: Honoring Late Control in Real-Time Video Generation","title_zh":"可重写的流式上下文：在实时视频生成中响应迟到的控制信号","method_name":"Rewritable Streaming Context (RSC)","hook":"Every real-time autoregressive video generator treats the frames it has already streamed as a fixed, clean conditioning context that can never be revised — so a control edit that arrives mid-stream can only steer the future, not reconcile with the committed past. We show that locus is not invariant: the committed KV cache is itself a re-writable state, and a bounded in-place rectification of it lets a late control signal retroactively reshape already-emitted frames at streaming latency.","anchor_pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","anchor_pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","domain_category":"Generative Models — Vision","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf lets a control signal issued AFTER a frame has streamed take effect on the already-committed past in a way the viewer perceives as a single consistent edit rather than restarting or a boundary discontinuity — streaming models steer only future frames, control models require the whole clip up front. (additive: the missing outcome is a real-time-preserving reconciliation of late control with committed history; the mechanism is left open.)","pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","sub_pattern":"C24 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by promoting the AR generator's committed-context interface from a fixed inherited default (immutable clean KV cache) to a free design variable: a control-conditioned in-place rectification operator that re-enters the frozen backbone and rewrites a bounded subset of committed KV entries so a late signal's retroactive scope is honored without restarting — the C24 move of redesigning how/where the condition enters while keeping the backbone fixed.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions the inherited assumption, shared by every streaming leaf descending from the chain-rule node p(x^i | x^<i), that the committed past must be treated as FIXED clean conditioning context at all — every control and acceleration method takes the irreversibility of streamed frames as given rather than testing whether the committed context could instead be a re-writable state. (subtractive: names the unasked question about the fixed-past assumption, leaves the replacement op","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","how_closed":"Closed by the C01 locus-pivot move (transferred from its security-domain examples to the streaming-generation locus): the field anchors control enforcement at one locus — the not-yet-generated future — and treats the committed-context locus as invariant; we relocate enforcement to the committed KV cache and falsify the invariance claim. The companion controlled_diagnostic_design ships the deliverable the audit alone cannot: a matched-pair separation (identical late edit, fixed-past generation vs rewritable-state generation, identical compute) that isolates whether reconciliation fidelity is attributable to making the locus re-writable rather than to extra denoising compute.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"real-time controllable video generation (autoregressive / causal video diffusion)","n_papers":52,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":27},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10},{"source":"openreview","n":2}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":10,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"TrackGo: A Flexible and Efficient Method for Controllable Video Generation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Moonshot: Towards Controllable Video Generation and Editing with Multimodal Conditions"},{"source":"openalex","title":"TrailBlazer: Trajectory Control for Diffusion-Based Video Generation"},{"source":"openalex","title":"SurgSora: Object-Aware Diffusion Model for Controllable Surgical Video Generation"},{"source":"openalex","title":"SV3D: Novel Multi-view Synthesis and 3D Generation from a Single Image Using Latent Video Diffusion"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Motion-I2V: Consistent and Controllable Image-to-Video Generation with Explicit Motion Modeling"}],"more":4},{"year":2025,"n":33,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"CtrlVDiff: Controllable Video Generation via Unified Multimodal Video Diffusion"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"IllumiCraft: Unified Geometry and Illumination Diffusion for Controllable Video Generation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"OmniVDiff: Omni Controllable Video Diffusion for Generation and Understanding"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Motionagent: Fine-Grained Controllable Video Generation via Motion Field Agent"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"EasyControl: Adding Control to Video Diffusion for Controllable Video Generation and Interpolation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"MoonShot: Towards Controllable Video Generation and Editing with Motion-Aware Multimodal Conditions"}],"more":27},{"year":2026,"n":9,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"},{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Foveated Diffusion: Efficient Spatially Adaptive Image and Video Generation"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Diffusion-DRF: Free, Rich, and Differentiable Reward for Video Diffusion Fine-Tuning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Efficient Camera-Controlled Video Generation of Static Scenes via Sparse Diffusion and 3D Rendering"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Fast Autoregressive Video Diffusion and World Models with Temporal Cache Compression and Sparse Attention"}],"more":3}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":25,"share":0.481},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":11,"share":0.212},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":11,"share":0.212},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":8,"share":0.154},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":8,"share":0.154},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":8,"share":0.154},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":7,"share":0.135},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":4,"share":0.077}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Real-time video generation has converged on causal, autoregressive few-step diffusion that factorizes the clip as a product of per-frame conditionals p(x^i | x^<i) and streams each frame irreversibly with a rolling KV cache (openalex:W4417136857 Self Forcing; openalex:W4413144436 From Slow Bidirectional to Fast Autoregressive), while controllability has converged on the opposite regime: full-clip bidirectional denoising where a control signal (trajectory, camera, structured noise, multimodal cue) is allowed to reshape every frame jointly because the future is visible during sampling (openalex:W4404971889 TrailBlazer; openalex:W4413146321 Go-with-the-Flow; semanticscholar:6a702bb7ccdf02c58239ea6eb99e8dbbfbce308a CtrlVDiff). The structural failure appears at their intersection: when a control edit is issued after some frames have already streamed, the causal model has irrevocably committed those past frames into its KV-cache context, so a control signal whose intended effect spans frames that are already in the past (a trajectory the object should have begun following, a camera path whose curvature is only consistent if earlier frames bent too) cannot be honored without either restarting generation (destroying real-time latency) or producing a visible discontinuity at the edit boundary, because the per-frame conditional has no machinery to register that a late signal implies a correction to context it can no longer regenerate.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4417136857","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Self Forcing trains the causal video diffusion model by autoregressively rolling out on its own previously generated frames with a rolling KV cache and a holistic video-level distribution-matching loss, closing the train-test exposure-bias gap and reaching real-time streaming with a few-step generator. Its conditional p(x^i | x^<i) treats the committed past as fixed clean context and provides no mechanism to admit a control signal that should retroactively constrain already-emitted frames, so any control that arrives after a frame streams can only steer frames not yet generated, not reconcile the new signal with the committed history."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4413144436","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"From Slow Bidirectional to Fast Autoregressive adapts a pretrained bidirectional DiT into a 4-step causal generator via distribution-matching distillation and ODE-trajectory student initialization, achieving on-the-fly frame generation. It inherits the same commitment property: distillation collapses the multi-step trajectory that bidirectional control methods exploit to inject edits, so there is no longer a denoising trajectory along which a late control signal could be folded into past frames."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4413146321","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Go-with-the-Flow injects motion control purely as a data-side change (warped structured noise derived from optical flow) so it is architecture-agnostic, but the warped noise is sampled once for the whole clip before denoising. The control is fixed at initialization rather than continuously re-issuable during streaming, so it cannot express a control change that becomes valid only partway through generation."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4404971889","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"TrailBlazer steers object trajectories via training-free attention edits applied during full-clip bidirectional denoising, where every frame is being denoised simultaneously so a trajectory constraint is enforced across the whole timeline at once. It has no causal analogue: in a streaming model the frames the trajectory references may already be committed, and the bidirectional attention the edit relies on is exactly what causal generation removes."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.01801v1","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Fast Autoregressive Video Diffusion compresses the growing KV cache (TempCache + sparse attention) to hold streaming latency and memory flat over long rollouts. It optimizes the cache as a speed object only; it never asks whether the cache, once compressed and committed, can be revised or re-weighted to absorb a late control signal, so its lossy compression makes the committed context even less recoverable for retroactive control."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"real-time controllable video generation (autoregressive / causal video diffusion)","venue":"ICLR 2026","time":"2026 cycle","data":["large-scale text/image-to-video pretraining corpora (e.g. WebVid-scale)","action/trajectory/camera-annotated interaction clips","standard video-gen benchmarks (VBench, UCF/Kinetics-style motion sets)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with video diffusion + distillation background","preference":"both","baseline":"Self Forcing (autoregressive few-step causal video diffusion) and full-clip control adapters (TrailBlazer, Go-with-the-Flow, CtrlVDiff)","limitation":"control signals that arrive or change mid-stream cannot retroactively shape frames a causal model has already committed; offline control methods need the whole clip and are not real-time","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object every leg reads from and writes to is the committed streaming context S — the rolling key-value cache plus the latent frames the causal few-step generator has already emitted, which the conditional p(x^i | x^<i) currently treats as fixed clean conditioning. LEG 1 (generative_process_redesign / C24) liberates S from being immutable: we keep the pretrained causal backbone and few-step generator frozen and add a control-conditioned Rectification Pass R that, when a control signal c arrives at stream time t with a retroactive scope window W = [t - L, t] (L frames into the committed past), recomputes only the KV entries of frames inside W by running k_r extra denoising substeps on those frames conditioned on c and on their UNCHANGED neighbors outside W, then writes the rectified keys/values back into the cache in place. The load-bearing scalar that decides which committed entries are rewritten is the control-debt d_j of cache frame j: d_j = || a_c(j) - a_0(j) ||_2 / ||a_0(j)||_2, the relative L2 change in the backbone's cross-attention read-out a(j) of frame j between conditioning on c (a_c) and on the prior control state (a_0), computed in one forward pass over the cache (a(j) is the model-internal cross-attention output at the last DiT block for frame j; the last block is fixed by selection rule, no tuning). Only frames with d_j above a learned threshold tau (one scalar, trained by the calibration in step 4) enter W, bounding the rectification cost to the genuinely affected past rather than the whole cache; tau and the substep count k_r are the only new hyperparameters and L is set as the smallest window covering all d_j > tau. R is trained by self-distillation against the frozen bidirectional teacher's full-clip edit (the teacher CAN see the whole timeline) so the in-place rewrite matches what a non-causal model would have produced, closing the exposure-gap between 'edit a committed frame' at train and test time. This closes gap 0 because a late c now reshapes the committed frames in W and the boundary at t-L is continuous (rectified frames condition on unrectified neighbors), all at a cost proportional to |W| not the full clip, preserving streaming latency. LEG 2 (assumption_audit_and_pivot / C01 + companion controlled_diagnostic_design) operates on the SAME object S: it states the falsifiable proposition 'the committed-context locus carries no load-bearing signal for honoring a retroactively-scoped control edit — only the future locus does', then refutes it by the control-debt being non-trivially > 0 for the affected past and by R's rectified output matching the teacher; the companion supplies the matched-pair diagnostic that isolates the locus shift from a compute confound. Numbers: prior full-clip control methods (TrailBlazer openalex:W4404971889; CtrlVDiff abstract) operate at offline latency (seconds-to-minutes per clip per their abstracts); we target the per-frame streaming budget of the Self Forcing class (real-time, sub-second per chunk per openalex:W4417136857) — we report our rectification overhead as added latency per edit-event, a different quantity than their per-clip cost, stated as a regime distinction not a copied number.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery because both are statements ABOUT the same object S (the committed cache): gap 0 wants a mechanism that rewrites S; gap 2 wants the audit that S's fixity is an unnecessary convention — the rectification operator R IS the constructive refutation of the audit's invariance claim, so building one validates the other (shared_object thread), and a separate module for the audit would just re-measure what R already demonstrates. (b) Considered (rejected) designs: (i) restart-from-edit (regression to re-running generation — fails latency, and method_lineage flags 're-run bidirectional denoising' as occupied node c1); (ii) a control adapter on future frames only (regression to occupied node n4, 'add a conditioning adapter to the frame conditional' — closes nothing retroactively); (iii) faster cache compression (occupied node n6 — orthogonal, makes S LESS recoverable). The avoided-node record: R deliberately draws on the un-occupied source of treating the committed cache as a writable variable with a control-debt gate, which no frontier leaf or ancestral node occupies.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: take a Self Forcing-class real-time causal video generator (openalex:W4417136857) on a standard text/image-to-video benchmark, inject a control edit (e.g. a new object-trajectory or camera-curvature constraint whose intended effect begins L=8-16 frames before the edit arrives) mid-stream, and measure (i) retroactive-edit fidelity = agreement between the rewritten committed frames and the frozen bidirectional teacher's full-clip edit (e.g. masked LPIPS / control-adherence score over the edited region) and (ii) boundary discontinuity = inter-frame perceptual jump at the t-L seam, against the fixed-past baseline at equal compute. If the candidate works, retroactive-edit fidelity rises and boundary discontinuity falls relative to the equal-compute fixed-past baseline, while per-frame streaming latency stays within the real-time budget. The named load-bearing variable is the control-debt d_j: under the negative control that permutes d_j so the rewrite window W is chosen at random (same |W|, same substeps, same total compute), retroactive-edit fidelity must fall back toward the fixed-past baseline — if randomizing WHICH committed frames get rewritten leaves fidelity unchanged, then control-debt is not the mechanism and the gain is mere extra compute. The positive control rewriting only the single highest-d_j frame should recover a large fraction of the full-window retroactive fidelity, constructively identifying control-debt as the signal that locates where the committed past must be revised.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4417136857","delta":"Self Forcing closes the train-test exposure gap for FORWARD self-generated context (frames condition on their own past) but never makes the committed cache writable; we construct a rectification operator + control-debt gate that edits already-committed KV entries in place to honor a retroactively-scoped late control signal, an operation its frozen-clean-context formulation cannot express."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4413144436","delta":"From Slow Bidirectional distills a bidirectional DiT into a 4-step causal generator for low latency, collapsing the denoising trajectory; we re-introduce a bounded control-conditioned trajectory ONLY over the high-control-debt committed window so a late edit can be folded into the past without restoring full multi-step bidirectional sampling."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4404971889","delta":"TrailBlazer enforces a trajectory across the whole timeline via bidirectional attention edits during full-clip denoising; we enforce a retroactive trajectory edit on a causal streaming model by rewriting committed cache state, with a measured control-debt that says WHICH committed frames carry the edit's signal — a localization their full-clip method never needs and never produces."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4413146321","delta":"Go-with-the-Flow fixes motion control once at initialization via warped structured noise for the whole clip; we admit a control signal issued AFTER frames have streamed and reconcile it with the committed past, a re-issuable mid-stream edit its single-shot noise warping cannot represent."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.01801v1","delta":"Fast AR Video Diffusion compresses the KV cache purely as a speed object; we treat the same cache as a re-writable control surface and measure (via control-debt) which committed entries must be rewritten to honor a late edit — a controllability property orthogonal to and partially in tension with their lossy compression."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4417136857","what_step_was_missed":"Self Forcing built the autoregressive rollout + rolling KV cache so that each frame's generation is supervised holistically against the whole self-generated sequence, but it only ever WRITES a cache entry once (at the frame's emission) and thereafter READS it as fixed clean context. To make our contribution already exist, it would have needed to construct a control-conditioned write-back path that recomputes and overwrites committed KV entries after emission, plus the control-debt readout that decides which committed entries are stale under a new control signal — a re-writable-cache mechanism and its gating quantity that its emit-once-then-freeze cache design does not contain."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":271,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"No hard floor fired: gap_closure_reject_check is 'borderline' (no lesson marked yes), recipe_application_check is 'applied', anti_pattern is null, and the paper_pointed_threat is addressable rather than exact-mechanism. But one borderline hits a load-bearing structural property — the novelty boundary of the C01 locus pivot — via the lesson 'Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work … collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured', and the same concern surfaces as the REVEL/DragStream paper_pointed_threat whose addressable_via names a specific candidate field. Per the heuristics (revise when a borderline hits a load-bearing property AND paper_pointed_threat is addressable via a specific field), the verdict is revise.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf lets a control signal issued AFTER a frame has streamed take effect on the already-committed past in a way the viewer perceives as a single consistent edit rather than restarting or a boundary discontinuity — streaming models steer only future frames, control models require the whole clip up front. (additive: the missing outcome is a real-time-preserving reconciliation of late control with committed history; the mechanism is left open.)","main_pattern":"generative_process_redesign","sub_pattern":"C24 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail by attaching a different conditioning encoder, latent space, or control channel to an existing refinement backbone and presenting the swap itself as the contribution, without the ablation that holds backbone/data/compute fixed while toggling only the new interface; a second shape is a redesign that buys control but degrades primary fidelity, reading as lateral recombination.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Eliminating two inherited bottlenecks at once is only compelling if the combined system clearly beats systems that removed each in isolation; marginal gains plus a regression in primary quality read as recombination, not a new method.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate eliminates exactly one inherited convention (the immutable committed cache); it does not stack a second bottleneck removal, and falsification_prediction commits to beating an equal-compute fixed-past baseline on the isolated metric."},{"lesson_quoted":"Swapping the conditioning encoder for a more powerful one is not a new model class if the output quality still trails incumbents and the encoder's advantage is never ablated against the prior encoder under matched conditions.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"There is no encoder swap — the backbone and any control encoder are frozen; the contribution is the write-back/rectification path, and step 6's matched-pair diagnostic ablates it under matched compute."},{"lesson_quoted":"A controllable pipeline assembled from frozen pretrained modules needs an ablation proving that the new control surface — not the off-the-shelf components — drives the gain, or it collapses into prior synthetic-data and adapter work.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Directly satisfied: the negative control (permute control-debt → random window) and matched-pair diagnostic isolate the new re-writable control surface from the frozen components and from raw extra compute."},{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a unified or foundation-model reframe obligates you to actually demonstrate the unification (multi-domain pretraining plus transfer); per-setting retraining under a single architecture does not substantiate the claim.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate makes no unification/foundation-model claim; it is a single mechanism on a single backbone class."},{"lesson_quoted":"Importing a representation from a semantically adjacent domain as the conditioning signal fails when that space is orthogonal to the geometry or dynamics that actually determine the output being synthesized.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The control-debt is computed in the backbone's OWN cross-attention readout space (model-internal), not imported from an adjacent domain, so orthogonality does not arise."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions the inherited assumption, shared by every streaming leaf descending from the chain-rule node p(x^i | x^<i), that the committed past must be treated as FIXED clean conditioning context at all — every control and acceleration method takes the irreversibility of streamed frames as given rather than testing whether the committed context could instead be a re-writable state. (subtractive: names the unasked question about the fixed-past assumption, leaves the replacement open.)","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is a successful relocation demonstrated but not adversarially closed (beats a fixed/non-adaptive baseline but never stress-tests an informed adversary at the new locus), or a novelty-boundary collapse where the 'new' locus was already used by prior work, or offering only a demonstration with no mechanistic account of why the locus carries the signal.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a relocated signal is 'stealthier' or 'harder to remove' without defeating an adaptive defender who searches the same new locus leaves the central claim unverified.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Non-adversarial setting; the analogue of an 'adaptive adversary' is the equal-compute fixed-past baseline and the random-window negative control, both of which the candidate runs to verify the locus shift is load-bearing."},{"lesson_quoted":"Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work — normalization statistics, activation-similarity losses, semantic concept triggers — collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"Collision retrieval surfaces REVEL/DragStream (semanticscholar:ec040316977504a1d0083c8d71fd1e42446f9a9a), which performs streaming drag editing with a neighbor-statistics 'self-rectification' on the SAME committed-streaming locus — the difference (their forward-propagating drift control vs our control-debt-gated retroactive KV rewrite) is real but must be made explicit and measured, or the locus-novelty boundary is at risk."},{"lesson_quoted":"A defense whose relocation silently depends on a clean reference model or a known anomaly distribution reintroduces precisely the strong assumption the move was supposed to eliminate.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The teacher used for distillation is a training-time-only frozen bidirectional model, not an inference-time clean reference; at deployment the mechanism uses only the committed cache and the live control signal."},{"lesson_quoted":"Demonstrating the new locus only on fixed, non-adaptive or outdated baselines while omitting any account of why it works reads as a stacked pipeline of existing components rather than a principled shift.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The positive control (rewrite only the highest control-debt frame) supplies the mechanistic account that the control-debt locates where the committed past carries the edit's signal."},{"lesson_quoted":"Wiring off-the-shelf generators or tools into a new attack setting without a structural reason for the locus change gets judged as engineering integration, not insight.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The structural reason for the locus change is explicit: the chain-rule conditional treats committed frames as fixed clean context, and the control-debt readout shows that locus carries non-trivial signal under a late edit."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The generative_process_redesign/C24 anchor entry is fully clear (its three load-bearing reject lessons are directly mitigated by the matched-pair + negative-control design). The assumption_audit/C01 sibling entry is borderline on one lesson — 'Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work … collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured' — because REVEL/DragStream operates on the same committed-streaming locus, so the differentiation must be sharpened and measured."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved frontier leaf lets a control signal issued AFTER a frame has streamed take effect on the already-committed past in a way the viewer perceives as a single consistent edit rather than restarting or a boundary discontinuity — streaming models steer only future frames, control models require the whole clip up front. (additive: the missing outcome is a real-time-preserving reconciliation of late control with committed history; the mechanism is left open.)","sub_pattern":"C24 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Hold an iterative-refinement generative backbone fixed and treat its conditioning interface or operating representation space as the free variable — change what it conditions on, how the condition enters (restrict to an interval of steps, route across stages, co-evolve), or which space refinement runs in — promoting the condition/latent to a first-class design surface.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism keeps the causal backbone + few-step generator frozen and redesigns HOW/WHERE the control condition enters: it adds a Rectification Pass that re-enters the frozen chain over a bounded committed window W and rewrites that window's KV entries in place — directly the C24 move of treating the conditioning interface (here the committed-context cache the chain reads) as the free variable while the backbone stays fixed.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions the inherited assumption, shared by every streaming leaf descending from the chain-rule node p(x^i | x^<i), that the committed past must be treated as FIXED clean conditioning context at all — every control and acceleration method takes the irreversibility of streamed frames as given rather than testing whether the committed context could instead be a re-writable state. (subtractive: names the unasked question about the fixed-past assumption, leaves the replacement open.)","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"The audited assumption is about the representational LOCUS at which a property is presumed enforced, and the move relocates enforcement to a different locus the field treated as irrelevant or invariant ('relocate the signal', 're-anchor enforcement', 'demonstrate exploitability/robustness at the new locus'), validated empirically.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism states the falsifiable proposition that the committed-context locus carries no load-bearing signal for a retroactive edit, then relocates control enforcement to that committed KV-cache locus and refutes the invariance via non-trivial control-debt + teacher-matched rectification — the C01 locus-pivot move, transferred out of its security examples into the streaming-generation locus, with the companion controlled_diagnostic_design supplying the empirical matched-pair separation C01 validates with.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries perform their cited cluster's signature move: C24's keep-backbone-fixed/redesign-the-conditioning-interface is realized as the in-place cache rewrite, and C01's pivot-the-locus-and-validate-empirically is realized as relocating control enforcement to the committed cache with a matched-pair separation; neither reduces to the parent's generic gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["generative_process_redesign","assumption_audit_and_pivot","controlled_diagnostic_design"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; the candidate's composition set contains none, so no anti-pattern matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:ec040316977504a1d0083c8d71fd1e42446f9a9a","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"REVEL/DragStream defines streaming, fine-grained drag manipulation of autoregressive video-diffusion outputs 'anytime on anything' and, critically, introduces an 'adaptive distribution self-rectification strategy that leverages neighboring frames' statistics to constrain latent drift' plus 'spatial-frequency selective optimization' that propagates contextual cues during streaming. This is the nearest competitor to our claim because it (a) operates on the same committed-streaming AR locus, (b) accepts control at arbitrary stream time, and (c) uses a 'rectification' of latent state. The candidate's claim stands only if it is distinct on the load-bearing axis: REVEL constrains/propagates cues to keep ongoing streaming drag stable (a forward-and-stability operation, training-free, framed as an editing/animation task), whereas the candidate makes the committed KV cache itself a re-writable state and uses a control-debt readout to decide WHICH already-committed frames to overwrite so a late edit reshapes the past retroactively with a continuous seam — a retroactive write-back over committed context, not forward cue propagation. If the candidate cannot exhibit and measure that retroactive-rewrite-vs-forward-propagation distinction, REVEL subsumes it; if it can, REVEL is a forward-control sibling, not a subsumer.","addressable_via":"Sharpen differentiation_from_lit with an explicit, measurable contrast against REVEL/DragStream — retroactive committed-cache rewrite gated by control-debt vs REVEL's forward neighbor-statistics drift-constraint — so the locus-novelty boundary is made explicit and measured (the exact mitigation C01's borderline reject lesson demands)."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"C01 gap_closure_reject_check borderline lesson ('Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work … unless the difference is made explicit and measured') + paper_pointed_threat REVEL/DragStream (semanticscholar:ec040316977504a1d0083c8d71fd1e42446f9a9a).","fix_direction":"Add a differentiation_from_lit entry for semanticscholar:ec040316977504a1d0083c8d71fd1e42446f9a9a (REVEL/DragStream) stating the substantive, measurable delta: they apply a training-free FORWARD neighbor-statistics self-rectification that constrains latent drift and propagates cues to keep ongoing streaming drag stable (an editing/animation operation on the same locus), whereas the candidate makes the committed KV cache a re-writable state and uses the control-debt readout to RETROACTIVELY overwrite the specific already-committed frames a late edit should have shaped, with a continuity guarantee at the t-L seam — the distinction is retroactive-committed-rewrite vs forward-cue-propagation, which the matched-pair diagnostic measures directly."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"Adjacent collision near-threats (MotionStream, AR-Drag/Real-Time Motion-Controllable AR Video) also occupy real-time AR control and should be bounded to protect the locus-novelty boundary.","fix_direction":"Add one differentiation_from_lit entry covering the real-time AR motion-control family (e.g. semanticscholar:cdc78753ec991954ed2da8da88b0671ac538d70e AR-Drag and semanticscholar:c5322d8b67555cd603d1ce4366e5db9061722c74 MotionStream): these distill bidirectional teachers into causal students to steer FUTURE frames at streaming latency, but commit each frame once emitted; the candidate's delta is the retroactive re-writability of the committed cache, an operation absent from their emit-once forward-steering formulation."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit[5]","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added a differentiation_from_lit entry for REVEL/DragStream (semanticscholar:ec040316977504a1d0083c8d71fd1e42446f9a9a) stating the measurable delta — their training-free FORWARD neighbor-statistics self-rectification constrains latent drift to keep ongoing streaming drag stable, whereas the candidate makes the committed KV cache a re-writable state and uses the control-debt readout to RETROACTIVELY overwrite already-committed frames, a retroactive-rewrite-vs-forward-propagation distinction the matched-pair diagnostic measures directly."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit[6]","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added a differentiation_from_lit entry bounding the real-time AR motion-control family (AR-Drag semanticscholar:cdc78753ec991954ed2da8da88b0671ac538d70e and MotionStream semanticscholar:c5322d8b67555cd603d1ce4366e5db9061722c74) — they distill bidirectional teachers into causal students to steer FUTURE frames at streaming latency but commit each frame once emitted, while the candidate's delta is the retroactive re-writability of the committed cache, an operation absent from their emit-once forward-steering formulation."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Rewritable Streaming Context: Honoring Late Control in Real-Time Video Generation\n\n**Method.** Rewritable Streaming Context (RSC)\n\n## Motivation\nToday's fastest video generators make videos one frame at a time, live, like a video call: each frame is produced and immediately 'locked in' and stored in a memory buffer (a key-value cache, or KV cache) that the model reads but never changes. This is what lets them run in real time. Separately, the best 'controllable' video generators — the ones that let you say 'make the ball follow this path' or 'curve the camera this way' — work the opposite way: they look at the whole clip at once before producing anything, so a control instruction can adjust every frame together. The problem is at the seam between these two worlds. If you are streaming live and you send a control instruction late — for example, the ball should have started curving a few frames ago — the live model has already locked in those past frames and cannot change them. Your only options today are to start the whole clip over (which breaks real-time) or to only fix future frames (which leaves an obvious visible jump where the old and new behavior meet, and silently ignores the part of your instruction that was about the past).\n\nThis is solvable now for two reasons. First, the new real-time generators (Self Forcing, 2025; From Slow Bidirectional to Fast Autoregressive, 2025) expose that locked-in memory buffer as a concrete thing we can actually reach into and rewrite. Second, the strong whole-clip controllers (TrailBlazer; Go-with-the-Flow) can serve as 'teachers' that already know what a correct full-clip edit looks like, so we can train our rewrite to imitate them. Very recent real-time control methods (Real-Time Motion-Controllable Autoregressive Video; MotionStream, both 2025) confirm people are now steering live streams — but every one of them still locks each frame the instant it is made, so nobody has tried making the locked-in past rewritable.\n\nThe reason prior work stopped is that each piece was missing exactly one thing: the real-time generators have no path to write a memory entry a second time and no way to tell which past frames a new instruction affects; the whole-clip controllers need the entire clip and bidirectional attention up front, which live streaming throws away; and the one-shot motion-control methods bake the control in at the start and cannot accept a re-issued edit. When we close this gap, a live generator can honor a late instruction that was partly about the past — without restarting and without a visible jump — and we get a concrete number (we call it 'control-debt') that says which past frames a late edit actually touches.\n\n## Method\n### Writable Committed Cache\n*Expose the frozen streaming generator's locked-in memory so committed frames can be overwritten in place at run time.*\n\n1. Take a frozen real-time frame-by-frame video generator (Self Forcing-style) and add software hooks (in PyTorch, forward hooks) so its locked-in memory buffer — the key-value (KV) cache — and its per-frame attention read-out can both be read and overwritten at run time. Keep an index that maps each past frame to its slice of the memory buffer, so you can address any single frame; for the read-out, average over each frame's spatial pieces to get one vector per frame. Add a small write function that overwrites a frame's memory slice in place. The generator's own weights are never changed.\n   - _Why_: You cannot rewrite the past until the past is reachable; this just makes the locked-in memory editable.\n2. At run time, compute control-debt, pick the window, run R over it, and overwrite those frames' memory entries in place — atomically, before the next frame is produced — so every later frame automatically reads the corrected memory and the fix carries forward with no extra plumbing. Re-decode the corrected window frames and show them to the viewer as a fixed-up segment, fast enough that the display lags by at most one frame. The join with the older un-rewritten frames stays smooth because R is told about the unchanged frame just before the window when it does the rewrite.\n   - _Why_: Overwriting in place is what actually makes the past honor the late instruction, and reading from corrected memory makes the future stay consistent with it.\n\n### Control-Debt Localization\n*Measure per-frame how much a late instruction changes each committed frame, and select the bounded window to rewrite.*\n\n3. When a control instruction c arrives at time t, do one cheap pass over the stored frames. For each past frame j, recompute its attention read-out two ways: once under the control state that was in force when that frame was first produced (saved alongside the frame; for a stream that started with no control, this is the plain text-only state), and once under the new instruction c. You get these by re-running only the last block's cross-attention on the already-stored frame data with each control state plugged in — no full regeneration. The bigger the difference between the two read-outs, the more that past frame should have looked different under c; this difference is the control-debt $d_{j}$ (Eq. (1)).\n\n*Control-debt of committed frame j: the relative L2 change in the backbone's last-block cross-attention read-out a(j) when conditioning switches from the prior control state $a_{0}$ to the new signal $a_{c}.$ Large $d_{j}$ marks a committed frame the late edit should have shaped.*\n$$ d_j = \\frac{\\lVert a_c(j) - a_0(j) \\rVert_2}{\\lVert a_0(j) \\rVert_2} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A big change means that past frame really should have looked different under the new instruction, so control-debt points at exactly the frames the late edit is about.\n4. Pick the rewrite window W. Mark every recent frame whose control-debt is above a learned cutoff (set in the next step), then take W as the unbroken run from the earliest marked frame up to the current time, filling in any unmarked frames in between so the window is one continuous block ending at the present — this is what keeps the join with the un-rewritten past smooth. Cap the window length at a maximum (default 32 frames) so a rewrite can never blow the latency budget; if the run is longer, keep only the most recent 32. If nothing is marked, do nothing — the instruction only concerns the future (Eq. (2)).\n\n*Rewrite window W is the smallest contiguous range of committed frames whose control-debt exceeds the learned threshold $\\tau ,$ up to the current time t; if no frame exceeds $\\tau $ the window is empty and no rewrite occurs.*\n$$ W = \\big[\\, \\min\\{\\, j : d_j > \\tau \\,\\},\\; t \\,\\big] \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Only rewriting the frames that actually changed keeps the cost small enough to stay real-time.\n\n### Teacher-Distilled Rectification\n*Train the in-place rewrite to reproduce a whole-clip teacher's correct retroactive edit.*\n\n5. Train the rewrite operator R and set the cutoff. R is a small LoRA adapter (rank 16) added to the denoiser's attention projections — the only thing trained; run it for the same number of denoising substeps the base generator natively uses (e.g. 4). Make training pairs by generating a clip normally, then injecting an edit at a random time whose intended effect reaches 8-16 frames into the past, and running a frozen whole-clip 'teacher' controller (e.g. a TrailBlazer-style model) on the same clip and edit to get the correct full-clip result, frame-for-frame aligned. Train R so that, running those substeps over the window and conditioning on the new edit plus the unchanged neighboring frames, it reproduces the teacher's frames; the training error combines a latent-space match and a perceptual (LPIPS) match in pixels, over window frames only. Finally set the cutoff by trying several values on held-out data and keeping the largest one that still hits the edit almost as well as rewriting all marked frames, while keeping the window as small as possible (Eq. (3)).\n\n*The Rectification Pass R runs $k_{r}$ denoising substeps over the window's KV entries conditioned on the new signal c and the unchanged neighbor entries at the window edge, and writes them back in place; its LoRA parameters $\\theta $ are distilled so the rectified frames match the frozen bidirectional teacher's full-clip edit.*\n$$ \\mathrm{KV}'_W \\leftarrow R_\\theta\\big(\\mathrm{KV}_W,\\, c,\\, \\mathrm{KV}_{\\partial W};\\, k_r\\big), \\quad \\theta^\\star = \\arg\\min_\\theta \\; \\mathbb{E}\\big[\\, \\lVert \\hat{x}_W^{R} - x_W^{\\mathrm{teacher}} \\rVert \\,\\big] \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The teacher can see the whole timeline, so imitating it teaches the live model what a correct retroactive edit should look like.\n\n### Mechanism Diagnostics\n*Prove the gain comes from rewriting the past (not extra compute) and that control-debt is the load-bearing signal.*\n\n6. Run a fair head-to-head. For the same edit, give both options the same total amount of computation — measured as work done by the denoiser (substeps times frames times tokens per frame), not just substep count. Option (A), the fixed-past baseline, spends that computation only on future frames (enough future frames to match the work option B spends on its window); round to whole frames and report any small leftover gap. Option (B) spends it rewriting the past window. For both, measure how well the edit is honored (a masked perceptual / control-adherence score against the teacher over the whole intended-edit region, including the past part) and how smooth the boundary is (the visible jump at the join).\n   - _Why_: Equal compute on both sides proves any gain comes from rewriting the past, not from simply doing more work.\n7. Run an honesty check. Keep the window the same length and the same number of substeps as the real run, but slide its starting point to a random position among the stored frames (still one continuous block). This keeps the total work identical while throwing away the control-debt's choice of WHERE to rewrite. Rewrite that random window and measure the edit accuracy. If a randomly placed window does just as well, control-debt was not the real reason for any gain.\n   - _Why_: If choosing random frames works just as well, then control-debt is not the real reason for the gain — this is the honesty test.\n8. Run a second check that confirms the signal. Rewrite only the single frame with the highest control-debt, conditioning on the new edit and on both of its immediate unchanged neighbors so the one-frame rewrite still joins smoothly. Then report what fraction of the full-window benefit this one frame recovers (its improvement over the no-rewrite baseline divided by the full window's improvement over that baseline). A large fraction confirms control-debt correctly points at where the edit lives.\n   - _Why_: If one well-chosen frame recovers most of the benefit, that confirms control-debt is correctly pointing at where the edit lives.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 可重写的流式上下文：在实时视频生成中响应迟到的控制信号\n\n**方法名称.** Rewritable Streaming Context (RSC)\n\n## 研究动机\n现在最快的视频生成模型是一帧一帧地实时生成视频的，就像视频通话一样：每生成一帧就立刻“锁定”并存进一个记忆缓冲区（key-value 缓存，即 KV cache），模型只读取它、从不修改它。正是这一点让它们能实时运行。另一方面，最强的“可控”视频生成模型——那些能让你说“让小球沿这条轨迹走”或“让镜头这样弯”的模型——工作方式恰恰相反：它们在生成任何内容之前先看整段视频，所以一条控制指令可以同时调整每一帧。问题出在这两个世界的接缝处。如果你正在实时串流，却晚发了一条控制指令——比如小球本应在几帧之前就开始转弯——实时模型已经锁定了那些过去的帧，无法再改。今天你只有两个选择：要么把整段视频从头重做（破坏实时性），要么只修正未来的帧（在新旧行为衔接处留下明显的跳变，并且悄悄忽略掉指令中关于过去的那部分）。\n\n现在能解决这个问题有两个原因。第一，新的实时生成模型（Self Forcing, 2025；From Slow Bidirectional to Fast Autoregressive, 2025）把那个锁定的记忆缓冲区暴露成了一个我们真的可以伸手进去重写的具体对象。第二，强大的整段可控模型（TrailBlazer；Go-with-the-Flow）可以充当“teacher”，它们已经知道一次正确的整段编辑应该是什么样，所以我们可以训练我们的重写去模仿它们。最近的实时控制方法（Real-Time Motion-Controllable Autoregressive Video；MotionStream，均为 2025）也证实大家现在正在操控实时流——但它们每一个仍然在生成的一瞬间就锁定每一帧，所以还没人尝试把锁定的过去变成可重写的。\n\n以往工作停下来的原因是：每一块都恰好缺了一样东西——实时生成模型没有“第二次写入”记忆条目的通路，也无法判断一条新指令影响哪些过去帧；整段可控模型需要预先拿到整段视频和双向注意力，而这正是实时串流所抛弃的；一次性运动控制方法在开头就把控制烤死了，无法接受重新发出的编辑。当我们补上这个缺口时，实时生成模型就能响应一条部分关于过去的迟到指令——既不重启、也不留下可见跳变——而且我们还得到一个具体的量（我们称之为 control-debt），它告诉我们一次迟到的编辑究竟触及哪些过去帧。\n\n## 方法\n### 可写的已提交缓存\n*暴露冻结的流式生成模型的锁定记忆，使已提交帧能在运行时被原地覆写。*\n\n1. 拿一个冻结的实时逐帧视频生成模型（Self Forcing 类型），加上软件钩子（在 PyTorch 中用 forward hook）使它锁定的记忆缓冲区——即 key-value (KV) 缓存——以及每帧的注意力读出在运行时既能读取也能覆写。维护一个索引，把每个过去帧映射到它在记忆缓冲区中的那一段，这样就能定位任意单帧；对读出，则把每帧的各空间块取平均，得到每帧一个向量。再加一个小的写入函数，用来原地覆写某一帧的记忆段。生成模型自身的权重始终不变。\n   - _为什么_: 过去不可触及就无法重写；这一步只是把锁定的记忆变成可编辑的。\n2. 运行时计算 control-debt、选出窗口、对其运行 R，然后原地覆写这些帧的记忆条目——在生成下一帧之前以原子方式完成——这样之后每一帧都会自动读取修正后的记忆，修正无需额外管线即可向前传递。把修正后的窗口帧重新解码并作为修好的片段呈现给观众，速度要快到显示至多滞后一帧。与更早的未重写帧的衔接保持平滑，因为 R 在重写时会被告知窗口之前那一帧（未改变的邻居）。\n   - _为什么_: 原地覆写才真正让过去响应了迟到的指令，而从修正后的记忆读取又让未来与之保持一致。\n\n### Control-Debt 定位\n*逐帧测量迟到指令改变每个已提交帧的程度，并选出要重写的有界窗口。*\n\n3. 当控制指令 c 在时刻 t 到达时，对已存储的帧做一次廉价的前向计算。对每个过去帧 j，用两种方式重算它的注意力读出：一次用该帧最初生成时所处的控制状态（与该帧一起保存；若是无控制开始的流，则为纯文本状态），一次用新指令 c。这两者只需在已存储的帧数据上、把各自的控制状态代入后重跑最后一层的 cross-attention 即可得到——无需完整重新生成。两个读出的差异越大，说明该过去帧在 c 下本该越不一样；这个差异就是 control-debt $d_{j}$（公式 (1)）。\n\n*已提交帧 j 的 control-debt：当条件从旧控制状态 $a_{0}$ 切换到新信号 $a_{c}$ 时，骨干网络最后一层 cross-attention 读出 a(j) 的相对 L2 变化。$d_{j}$ 越大，说明该已提交帧本应被迟到的编辑所改变。*\n$$ d_j = \\frac{\\lVert a_c(j) - a_0(j) \\rVert_2}{\\lVert a_0(j) \\rVert_2} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 变化大意味着这个过去帧在新指令下本该长得不一样，所以 control-debt 正好指向迟到编辑真正涉及的那些帧。\n4. 选定重写窗口 W。把 control-debt 超过学习阈值（在下一步设定）的每个近期帧都标记出来，然后取 W 为从最早被标记帧到当前时刻的连续区间，把中间未被标记的帧也补进去，使窗口成为一个以当前为终点的连续块——正是这一点让它与未重写的过去衔接平滑。给窗口长度设上限（默认 32 帧），使一次重写绝不会超出延迟预算；若该区间更长，只保留最近的 32 帧。若没有任何帧被标记，就什么都不做——该指令只关乎未来（公式 (2)）。\n\n*重写窗口 W 是 control-debt 超过学习阈值 $\\tau $ 的已提交帧所构成的最小连续区间，上界为当前时刻 t；若没有帧超过 $\\tau $，则窗口为空、不进行重写。*\n$$ W = \\big[\\, \\min\\{\\, j : d_j > \\tau \\,\\},\\; t \\,\\big] \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 只重写真正变化了的帧，才能把代价压到足以保持实时。\n\n### Teacher 蒸馏的回溯修正\n*训练原地重写，使其复现整段 teacher 给出的正确回溯编辑。*\n\n5. 训练重写算子 R 并设定阈值。R 是加在去噪器注意力投影上的小型 LoRA 适配器（秩 16）——唯一被训练的部分；运行的去噪步数与基础生成模型原生使用的相同（如 4 步）。构造训练样本对：先正常生成一段视频，然后在随机时刻注入一个其预期效果回溯到过去 8-16 帧的编辑，并用一个冻结的整段 teacher 控制器（如 TrailBlazer 类型的模型）在同一段视频和同一编辑上运行，得到逐帧对齐的正确整段结果。训练 R，使其在窗口上运行这些去噪步、并以新编辑加未改变的邻居帧为条件时，能复现 teacher 的帧；训练误差结合了 latent 空间的匹配和像素空间的感知（LPIPS）匹配，仅在窗口帧上计算。最后通过在留出数据上尝试若干取值来设定阈值，保留那个在效果上仍几乎与重写全部被标记帧一样好、同时使窗口尽可能小的最大阈值（公式 (3)）。\n\n*Rectification Pass R 在窗口内的 KV 条目上运行 $k_{r}$ 步去噪，条件为新信号 c 和窗口边缘未改变的邻居条目，然后原地写回；其 LoRA 参数 $\\theta $ 通过蒸馏训练，使重写后的帧与冻结的双向 teacher 的整段编辑结果一致。*\n$$ \\mathrm{KV}'_W \\leftarrow R_\\theta\\big(\\mathrm{KV}_W,\\, c,\\, \\mathrm{KV}_{\\partial W};\\, k_r\\big), \\quad \\theta^\\star = \\arg\\min_\\theta \\; \\mathbb{E}\\big[\\, \\lVert \\hat{x}_W^{R} - x_W^{\\mathrm{teacher}} \\rVert \\,\\big] \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: teacher 能看到整条时间线，模仿它就教会了实时模型一次正确的回溯编辑应该是什么样。\n\n### 机制诊断\n*证明收益来自重写过去（而非额外计算），且 control-debt 是起决定作用的信号。*\n\n6. 做一次公平的正面对比。对同一个编辑，给两种方案相同的总计算量——以去噪器完成的工作量来衡量（步数 $\\times $ 帧数 $\\times $ 每帧 token 数），而不只是步数。方案 (A)，即固定过去的基线，把这些计算只花在未来帧上（用足够多的未来帧来匹配方案 B 花在其窗口上的工作量）；取整到整数帧，并报告任何小的残余差距。方案 (B) 把计算花在重写过去窗口。对两者都测量：编辑被响应得有多好（在整个预期编辑区域、含过去部分上，对 teacher 的带掩码感知/控制符合度分数），以及边界有多平滑（衔接处可见的跳变）。\n   - _为什么_: 两边计算量相同，就能证明任何提升都来自重写过去，而非单纯多做了运算。\n7. 做一次诚实性检验。让窗口与真实运行保持相同长度、相同步数，但把它的起点滑到已存储帧中的随机位置（仍是一个连续块）。这样总工作量完全不变，却丢掉了 control-debt 对“在何处重写”的选择。重写那个随机窗口并测量编辑准确度。若随机放置的窗口效果一样好，说明 control-debt 并不是任何收益的真正原因。\n   - _为什么_: 如果随机选帧效果一样好，那 control-debt 就不是提升的真正原因——这是诚实性检验。\n8. 做第二个检验来确认信号。只重写 control-debt 最高的那一帧，并以新编辑及其两侧紧邻的未改变邻居为条件，使这次单帧重写仍能平滑衔接。然后报告这一帧恢复了完整窗口收益的多大比例（它相对不重写基线的提升，除以完整窗口相对该基线的提升）。比例很大就证实 control-debt 确实正确指向了编辑所在之处。\n   - _为什么_: 如果一帧选得好就能恢复大部分收益，就证实 control-debt 确实正确指向了编辑所在之处。\n\n"},{"id":"80","run_dir":"run_prompt80_mxrope","index":80,"title":"Water-Filling RoPE: Rate-Distortion-Optimal Frequency Allocation for Position Encoding","title_zh":"Water-Filling RoPE：面向位置编码的率失真最优频率分配","method_name":"Water-Filling RoPE (WF-RoPE)","hook":"Every RoPE variant -- single base, NTK/YaRN, MrRoPE's uniform/progressive radix -- only ever rescales one scalar over a frequency grid whose monotone geometric SHAPE theta_i = base^{-2(i-1)/d} is never questioned; we show that shape is a sub-optimal solution to a budget-allocation problem nobody wrote down, and the rate-distortion-optimal grid is provably non-monotone and recoverable in closed form by water-filling.","anchor_pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","anchor_pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","domain_category":"LLM Pretraining, Architecture & Scaling","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf derives the per-dimension position-to-angle allocation from a stated optimality criterion: every method (single base, NTK/YaRN scaling, MrRoPE uniform/progressive radix) selects the frequency grid from a one-parameter geometric family or a hand-designed schedule, so no leaf produces the grid that provably minimizes attention-score distortion (or maximizes retained relative-position information) at a target context length under a fixed dimension budget.","pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","sub_pattern":"C12 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by swapping the structural slot 'per-dimension frequency vector theta' from a geometric-series primitive to a primitive read off the KKT/water-filling solution of an explicit per-dimension distortion-rate allocation program, anchored to the classical reverse-water-filling theorem, and proving the swap preserves RoPE's relative-position inner-product identity (the essential property) while strictly lowering the worst-case attention-score distortion at the target length.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether the geometric-progression SHAPE of the frequency grid is necessary rather than inherited: all leaves descend from the same theta_i = base^{-2(i-1)/d} ancestor and only vary its scalar base or a monotone reschedule, so none asks whether the budget should be allocated non-monotonically (some mid dimensions denser, some high dimensions removed) when the optimization target is long-distance discriminability.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by treating the grid as a budgeted selection rule (which of the d/2 sub-spaces receives which angular-resolution share) and pivoting its load-bearing criterion -- the monotone geometric shape -- via a REFRAME of the selection task into the rate-distortion allocation problem class, then re-deriving a performance certificate (a closed-form gap by which the geometric grid's distortion exceeds the water-filling optimum) that vanishes only when the allocation is geometric, proving the inherited shape is genuinely sub-optimal rather than a benign convention.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"positional encoding for long-context transformers (rotary position embedding / RoPE frequency design)","n_papers":48,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":24},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":15,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Rotary Position Embedding for Vision Transformer"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Transformer-Based End-to-End Speech Translation With Rotary Position Embedding"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"RoTHP: Rotary Position Embedding-based Transformer Hawkes Process"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"What Rotary Position Embedding Can Tell Us: Identifying Query and Key Weights Corresponding to Basic Syntactic or High-level Semantic Information"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"An Investigation Of Rotary Position Embedding For Speech Enhancement"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Spatio-Temporal Transformer with Rotary Position Embedding and Bone Priors for 3D Human Pose Estimation"}],"more":9},{"year":2025,"n":23,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"TransXSSM: A Hybrid Transformer State Space Model with Unified Rotary Position Embedding"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"ComRoPE: Scalable and Robust Rotary Position Embedding Parameterized by Trainable Commuting Angle Matrices"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Context-aware Rotary Position Embedding"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Length-Aware Rotary Position Embedding for Text-Speech Alignment"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Health Assessment and Trend Prediction via Efficient Multi-Scale Attention Convolutional Auto Encoder and Rotary Position Embedding for Mechanical Equipment"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"KV-Latent: Dimensional-level KV Cache Reduction with Frequency-aware Rotary Positional Embedding"}],"more":17},{"year":2026,"n":10,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Efficient Matrix Implementation for Rotary Position Embedding"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"CRoPE: Efficient Parametrization of Rotary Positional Embedding"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"MrRoPE: Mixed-radix Rotary Position Embedding"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Spiral RoPE: Rotate Your Rotary Positional Embeddings in the 2D Plane"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Rotary Positional Embeddings as Phase Modulation: Theoretical Bounds on the RoPE Base for Long-Context Transformers"}],"more":4}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":10,"share":0.208},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":7,"share":0.146},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":6,"share":0.125},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":6,"share":0.125},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":5,"share":0.104},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":5,"share":0.104},{"pattern_id":"algebraic_equivalence_unification","pattern_name":"Prove Equivalence to Unify","count":3,"share":0.062},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":3,"share":0.062}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"RoPE encodes a token's integer position by spreading it across d/2 two-dimensional sub-spaces whose angular frequencies form a single fixed geometric progression theta_i = base^{-2(i-1)/d} (arxiv:2601.22181v1, arxiv:2602.10959v1). Because that grid is fixed up to one scalar `base`, the only quantities anyone can adjust to fight length-generalization failure are (i) the scalar base and (ii) a hand-designed interpolation/conversion schedule applied uniformly or monotonically across dimensions (MrRoPE's uniform/progressive radix conversions, arxiv:2601.22181v1; NTK/YaRN scaling, openalex:W4403853736). Empirically this geometric grid mis-allocates the encoding budget: high-frequency dimensions never complete a cycle within the training window so they extrapolate into unseen angles and fail (arxiv:2601.22181v1), while low-frequency dimensions span so wide an angular range that the model cannot use them for long-distance retrieval at all (openalex:W4412888320). The phase-modulation analysis (arxiv:2602.10959v1) shows the geometric grid violates an aliasing/Nyquist bound at long context, but stops at prescribing a larger scalar base rather than redesigning which positions map to which dimensions. The structural failure: there is no per-dimension allocation of the position-to-angle mapping that is derived from a stated optimality criterion (information retained about relative position, attention-score distortion, or quantization rate) rather than assumed from a geometric series — so every cure operates on a one-parameter family that cannot simultaneously keep high-frequency dimensions in-distribution and low-frequency dimensions discriminative.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2601.22181v1","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"MrRoPE recasts position as a mixed-radix number, viewing each RoPE dimension as a 'digit' with its own radix, and unifies existing RoPE-extension methods (PI, NTK, YaRN) as different radix-conversion strategies; it then proposes two training-free instances, MrRoPE-Uni (uniform radix) and MrRoPE-Pro (progressive/monotone radix). Its residue: the radix schedule is hand-picked (uniform or a fixed progressive rule) and justified by unification, not optimized — it provides NO criterion for which per-dimension radix assignment is best, no derivation that any particular schedule minimizes attention-score distortion or maximizes retained relative-position information, and no mechanism to learn or solve for the schedule, so the mixed-radix degrees of freedom it opened up are left almost entirely unexploited."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.10959v1","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Reinterprets RoPE as phase modulation of a bank of complex oscillators and derives a Nyquist-like aliasing lower bound and a DC-stability bound on the scalar `base` needed to preserve positional coherence at a target length, tightening with depth. Residue: the analysis treats the frequency grid's SHAPE (geometric) as given and only constrains the single scalar base — it never asks whether a non-geometric, per-dimension frequency allocation could satisfy the aliasing bound at far lower distortion, so its bound is a constraint on one parameter rather than an objective over the whole grid."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4412888320","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"A controlled diagnostic showing RoPE's wide low-frequency rotation range leaves certain dimensions effectively unused for long-distance retrieval (dimension inefficiency). Residue: it diagnoses dead dimensions but proposes no constructive reallocation — it does not turn the diagnosis into a frequency grid that spends the wasted dimensions' capacity where it is informative."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416382454","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"DPE detects a per-dimension 'effective length' and remaps key dimensions' position indices to their most effective lengths, a training-free extrapolation fix. Residue: the per-dimension treatment is a post-hoc index remap chosen by a heuristic detector, not a frequency allocation derived from an optimality criterion, and it is static rather than tied to a rate/distortion objective."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"positional encoding for long-context transformers (rotary position embedding / RoPE frequency design)","venue":"ICLR 2026","time":"2026","data":["long-context LLM pretraining/eval corpora (e.g. PG19, Books3-style)","Needle-in-a-Haystack","RULER","perplexity on held-out long documents"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher comfortable with transformer internals and signal-processing / information-theory tools","preference":"both","baseline":"standard RoPE with single geometric base; NTK-aware / YaRN interpolation; MrRoPE uniform & progressive radix conversion","limitation":"RoPE's per-dimension frequency grid is a single fixed geometric progression (theta_i = base^{-2(i-1)/d}); the only degrees of freedom anyone tunes are the scalar base and a hand-designed interpolation/radix schedule, leaving no principled, per-dimension allocation of the position-encoding budget","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The central shared object (coherence_thread_type = shared_object) is the per-dimension frequency allocation grid theta = (theta_1,...,theta_{d/2}), theta_i > 0, that maps a token position p to per-sub-space phases p*theta_i; both legs read from and write to this one object. ANCHOR LEG (architectural_operator_substitution / C12): we relocate the structural slot that produces theta from the fixed geometric primitive theta_i = base^{-2(i-1)/d} to the solution of an explicit allocation program. We model each 2-D sub-space i as a complex oscillator e^{i p theta_i} (the phase-modulation view of arxiv:2602.10959v1) and define a per-dimension distortion D_i(theta_i) = the expected squared error in the relative-position component of the attention inner product contributed by sub-space i over the relative-distance distribution P(delta) of the target corpus, computed from the second-order Taylor / aliasing expansion of cos(delta*theta_i) on delta in [0, L_max]; D_i is small when theta_i is low enough that delta*theta_i stays inside one un-aliased period over the support of P(delta), and large (saturating) when theta_i causes phase wraps beyond the trained range. We impose (1) the per-dimension aliasing constraint theta_i <= pi / L_max-effective_i (a hard Nyquist box, the dimension-wise version of arxiv:2602.10959v1's scalar bound) and (2) a total angular-resolution budget sum_i log(1/theta_i) <= R (R fixes how much total positional 'bandwidth' the d/2 sub-spaces may spend, calibrated so the geometric grid is one feasible point). Minimizing sum_i w_i D_i(theta_i) subject to (1)-(2) is a convex program whose KKT stationarity gives a REVERSE-WATER-FILLING closed form: theta_i* = clip( sqrt(lambda / (w_i * curvature_i)), 0, pi/L_max-effective_i ), where lambda is the single Lagrange multiplier solved by a 1-D bisection to meet budget R, w_i is the (per-head, optionally uniform) importance weight of sub-space i, and curvature_i is the second derivative of D_i at theta_i (all computable in closed form from P(delta) and the cos expansion). The artifact is a concrete frequency vector theta* that is in general NON-MONOTONE (dimensions whose Nyquist box binds are pushed to the box edge; mid-frequency dimensions get extra resolution from the freed budget; the highest-frequency dimensions whose D_i is hopeless get theta_i -> their box and effectively retire), and we substitute theta* for the geometric theta with NO other architectural change, so RoPE's identity <q_m,k_n> = Re(x_m* W_q* W_k x_n e^{i theta (m-n)}) still holds verbatim (the essential property survives) while the worst-case distortion over P(delta) drops. SIBLING LEG (assumption_audit_and_pivot / C11): the same object theta is a budgeted selection rule; its inherited criterion is 'theta must be a monotone geometric series, vary only base.' We pivot by REFRAME (selection -> rate-distortion allocation) and re-derive the certificate Delta = sum_i w_i D_i(theta_geom) - sum_i w_i D_i(theta*) >= 0 with equality iff w_i*curvature_i is itself geometric in i and no Nyquist box binds -- a condition real corpora violate (P(delta) is heavy-tailed, not geometric), so the geometric grid is provably strictly sub-optimal whenever a box binds or w_i is non-geometric, which is the load-bearing necessity claim the audit ships. The two legs are not separate modules: the audit's certificate Delta is exactly the optimality gap that the anchor's water-filling solution closes; they are one derivation read two ways.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The two gaps share a single piece of machinery (the allocation program over theta), so they are one module, not two: the audit leg IS the derivation that the geometric grid is a non-optimal feasible point of the very program whose optimum the anchor leg constructs -- evidence for shared machinery is that the audit's certificate Delta and the anchor's objective are literally the same functional. I considered making the anchor a LEARNED per-head allocation (gradient-trained theta), but rejected it: it would (a) regress toward CARoPE's learned-frequency node and add trained parameters, losing the train-free minimalism, and (b) obscure the closed-form optimality certificate that makes the audit's necessity claim rigorous. I also considered casting the anchor as reframe_as_solvable_object directly, but its sub-clusters (attribution C00, RL-to-supervised C21, game/equilibrium C27) do not host a budget-allocation reframe at method grade, whereas C12 cleanly hosts 'swap the coordinate-geometry primitive (the frequency grid) for a classical-theorem-grounded surrogate (water-filling allocation),' so I bound the anchor to the architectural_operator_substitution alternate per the deferred-binding rule.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: take a single pretrained RoPE LLM (e.g. a 7-8B Llama-class model trained at 4K-8K), and without any fine-tuning swap its frequency buffer for the water-filling theta* computed at L_max=128K, then measure Needle-in-a-Haystack recall and RULER accuracy at 32K/64K/128K plus long-document perplexity, against the identical checkpoint under base RoPE, NTK-aware, YaRN, and MrRoPE-Uni/Pro. If the candidate works, long-context recall/accuracy increases (and PPL decreases) at the extended lengths relative to the geometric-grid baselines at equal compute, with the largest gains where P(delta) is most heavy-tailed. The load-bearing variable is the per-dimension allocation profile theta* (specifically its non-monotone redistribution of angular budget across sub-spaces). Negative control: theta_perm -- randomly permute theta*'s entries across dimensions, which holds the multiset of frequencies, the total budget R, and the scalar Delta fixed but destroys the dimension-to-frequency assignment; if the allocation (not merely the set of frequencies) is the mechanism, theta_perm should drive long-context recall/accuracy back down to or below the geometric baseline. This is non-tautological because the controlled outcome is the downstream task metric (NIAH recall, RULER accuracy), not the value of theta* or Delta. Positive control: theta_box-only (Nyquist clipping without water-filling redistribution) should recover only part of the effect, attributing the remainder to the redistribution itself.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2601.22181v1","delta":"MrRoPE opens the mixed-radix degrees of freedom and fills them with two HAND-PICKED schedules (uniform, progressive/monotone) justified by unification; we DERIVE the per-dimension allocation as the closed-form reverse-water-filling optimum of an explicit distortion-rate program and prove a non-zero optimality gap Delta between their (and every geometric) schedule and ours -- a criterion and construction MrRoPE never produces."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.10959v1","delta":"They derive a Nyquist/aliasing LOWER BOUND on the single scalar base treating the grid shape as given; we promote that bound to a per-dimension feasibility constraint INSIDE an allocation objective and solve for the full non-monotone grid, turning a one-parameter constraint into an optimum over all d/2 frequencies."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4412888320","delta":"They diagnose that wide-range low-frequency dimensions are dead for long-distance retrieval but propose no reallocation; our water-filling explicitly retires those dimensions (pushes them to their Nyquist box) and reinvests their freed angular budget into mid-frequency dimensions via the closed-form multiplier, converting their diagnosis into a constructive grid."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416382454","delta":"DPE detects a per-dimension effective length with a heuristic and remaps key indices to it; we replace the heuristic with a stated distortion objective whose KKT solution gives the allocation in closed form, plus an optimality certificate the heuristic cannot provide."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"arxiv:2601.22181v1","what_step_was_missed":"MrRoPE reframed position as a mixed-radix number and unified RoPE-extensions as radix conversions, but it never wrote down an objective over the radix/frequency assignment -- it stopped at hand-designed uniform and progressive schedules. For our contribution to already exist, MrRoPE would have needed to construct a per-dimension distortion functional D_i(theta_i) over the relative-distance distribution and derive (not assume) the radix schedule as that functional's constrained minimizer; that derivation -- and the resulting closed-form reverse-water-filling allocation with its optimality-gap certificate -- is the missing constructive step."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":264,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"Layer 1 hard floor did not fire: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict is borderline (no lesson candidate_match: yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat (arxiv:2601.22181v1 MrRoPE) is competitive not exact-mechanism per its subsumption_argument. recipe_application_check.verdict = applied for both entries (C12 coordinate-geometry slot swap and C11 reframe+certificate both present in core_mechanism), so the chief revise trigger is absent. The two borderlines (C12 'port without grounding' re the choice of D_i; C11 'dataset-dependent constant' re Delta depending on P(delta)) hit defensible, practitioner-controllable points rather than load-bearing structural failures, so they are surfaced for Phase 4 reviewer_concerns_and_responses rather than forcing a revise.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf derives the per-dimension position-to-angle allocation from a stated optimality criterion: every method (single base, NTK/YaRN scaling, MrRoPE uniform/progressive radix) selects the frequency grid from a one-parameter geometric family or a hand-designed schedule, so no leaf produces the grid that provably minimizes attention-score distortion (or maximizes retained relative-position information) at a target context length under a fixed dimension budget.","main_pattern":"architectural_operator_substitution","sub_pattern":"C12 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is a substitution that is mechanically valid but whose payoff is absent or unverified: authors swap the operator/wiring/parameter-locus then prove preservation with a borrowed or trivial argument exposing no new structure, or claim the bought property without measuring it, or port an architecture from another domain with a bolted-on coupling not grounded in the target problem.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"they prove preservation with a borrowed or trivial argument that exposes no new structure","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The preservation argument (RoPE's relative-position inner-product identity survives verbatim because only the frequency buffer changes) is paired with a NEW structural object -- the closed-form optimality gap Delta -- so the preservation is not the contribution and is not trivial-only."},{"lesson_quoted":"they claim the property the new slot was supposed to buy -- parallelism, aggressive pruning, scalability -- without actually delivering or measuring it","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The bought property (lower long-context distortion -> higher NIAH/RULER recall) is measured head-on in falsification_prediction with matched-compute baselines and a permutation negative control, not merely asserted."},{"lesson_quoted":"they port an architecture from another domain and add a coupling mechanism without grounding it in the target problem, producing an uncoordinated assembly","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"Water-filling is imported from rate-distortion theory; the candidate grounds it in RoPE via the per-dimension distortion functional D_i derived from the cos/aliasing expansion, but a reviewer could ask whether D_i is the RIGHT distortion -- a load-bearing modeling choice that Phase 4 reviewer_concerns must defend, not a fatal port."},{"lesson_quoted":"validation on a proxy: throughput reported instead of accuracy, toy-scale data, or no matched baseline for the specific property claimed","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Validation is on NIAH/RULER accuracy and PPL at 32K/64K/128K against base/NTK/YaRN/MrRoPE at equal compute -- the exact regime and matched baselines for the claimed long-context property."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether the geometric-progression SHAPE of the frequency grid is necessary rather than inherited: all leaves descend from the same theta_i = base^{-2(i-1)/d} ancestor and only vary its scalar base or a monotone reschedule, so none asks whether the budget should be allocated non-monotonically (some mid dimensions denser, some high dimensions removed) when the optimization target is long-distance discriminability.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The dominant failure is substituting one selection rule for another that performs better empirically while omitting the theorem that explains when and why it wins; a second is pivoting an assumption the community regards as a reasonable modeling choice rather than a genuine restriction; a third is a guarantee that does not hold up (dataset-dependent uncontrollable constant, a regularity condition the mechanism violates, or a marginal bound with no matching lower bound).","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Substituting one selection heuristic for another without a theorem stating when and why it wins reads as an engineering combination, not a contribution, no matter how clean the empirical gain.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate ships the theorem: the optimality-gap certificate Delta >= 0 with the explicit equality condition (w_i*curvature_i geometric and no Nyquist box binds), which states exactly when and why the water-filling grid beats the geometric one."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pivoting an assumption the community treats as a reasonable modeling choice -- rather than first proving it a genuine restriction -- leaves both motivation and novelty in doubt.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The audit first proves the geometric shape is a genuine restriction (strictly sub-optimal whenever a box binds or w_i is non-geometric, conditions real heavy-tailed P(delta) corpora satisfy), not a benign convention."},{"lesson_quoted":"A re-derived guarantee whose binding constant is dataset-dependent and cannot be controlled by the practitioner is vacuous in the worst case and fails to convince.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"Delta depends on the corpus P(delta) and weights w_i, which are data-dependent; however the practitioner controls them (they are estimated from the target corpus and the budget R is set to make the geometric grid feasible), so the constant is controllable -- a reviewer concern to surface, not a triggered reject."},{"lesson_quoted":"Unlocking a new capability by violating an assumption while ignoring a protective property it guarded -- detectability, validity, identifiability -- invites rejection on the overlooked side effect rather than the headline result.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The pivot explicitly preserves the property the geometric grid protected (relative-position dependence via the RoPE identity) because the swap is frequency-only; nothing the old grid guaranteed is silently broken."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No Reject lesson is marked candidate_match: yes, so nothing is triggered. Two borderlines carry weight: the C12 anchor's 'port without grounding' lesson (the choice of distortion functional D_i is a modeling choice a reviewer will probe) and the C11 sibling's 'dataset-dependent constant' lesson (Delta depends on P(delta)); both hit defensible-but-probeable points, not fatal ones."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf derives the per-dimension position-to-angle allocation from a stated optimality criterion: every method (single base, NTK/YaRN scaling, MrRoPE uniform/progressive radix) selects the frequency grid from a one-parameter geometric family or a hand-designed schedule, so no leaf produces the grid that provably minimizes attention-score distortion (or maximizes retained relative-position information) at a target context length under a fixed dimension budget.","sub_pattern":"C12 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"C12 relocates or swaps a STRUCTURAL SLOT rather than tuning weights -- e.g. moving from stored interaction scalars to coordinate geometry -- anchoring the substitute to a classical theorem or revived classical representation that fits the same slot, accompanied by a proof showing the essential property survives while a cost/expressivity property changes.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism step that 'relocates the structural slot that produces theta from the fixed geometric primitive theta_i=base^{-2(i-1)/d} to the solution of an explicit allocation program' and substitutes theta* with NO other architectural change while RoPE's inner-product identity still holds verbatim -- this is exactly a coordinate-geometry slot swap anchored to the classical reverse-water-filling theorem with an essential-property-preservation argument. Signature move present.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether the geometric-progression SHAPE of the frequency grid is necessary rather than inherited: all leaves descend from the same theta_i = base^{-2(i-1)/d} ancestor and only vary its scalar base or a monotone reschedule, so none asks whether the budget should be allocated non-monotonically (some mid dimensions denser, some high dimensions removed) when the optimization target is long-distance discriminability.","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"C11 centers on a selection/acquisition rule (which item/component to keep or route to under a budget) and pivots the single assumption baked into its criterion, taking one of two forms -- relax the structural crutch and re-prove, OR REFRAME the selection task into a different, more tractable problem class -- and the invariant deliverable is a re-derived performance certificate (regret/competitive-ratio/approximation-ratio/budget) shown to match or beat the pre-pivot baseline.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism treats theta as 'a budgeted selection rule (which of the d/2 sub-spaces receives which angular-resolution share)' and performs the REFRAME branch (selection -> rate-distortion allocation), then re-derives the certificate Delta = sum w_i D_i(theta_geom) - sum w_i D_i(theta*) >= 0 with the explicit equality condition -- a re-derived performance certificate beating the pre-pivot (geometric) baseline. C11's reframe+certificate signature move is present.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries instantiate their cluster's distinctive move: the anchor performs C12's coordinate-geometry structural-slot swap with a classical-theorem anchor and preservation proof, and the sibling performs C11's selection-rule reframe into a new problem class with a re-derived optimality certificate -- neither is merely the parent pattern's generic gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["architectural_operator_substitution","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; the candidate's composition set contains neither heterogeneous_decomposition nor any of the three flagged pairs, so no anti-pattern matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"arxiv:2601.22181v1","threat_source":"lit_table","subsumption_argument":"MrRoPE is the structurally closest paper: it already opened the per-dimension mixed-radix/frequency degrees of freedom and unified RoPE-extensions as radix conversions, so if MrRoPE's uniform/progressive schedules were already derived from an optimality criterion the candidate would be subsumed. They are not: MrRoPE's schedules are hand-picked and justified by unification, with no objective over the allocation and no optimality certificate. The candidate's claim stands precisely on the constructive step MrRoPE omits -- writing a per-dimension distortion functional and deriving the allocation as its constrained minimizer with a non-zero gap Delta against every geometric schedule (including MrRoPE's), so MrRoPE competes with but does not subsume the candidate. Secondary threats from collision_hits (RDKV, Spherical KV) apply rate-distortion to KV-cache compression, not to the RoPE position-frequency grid, so they do not overlap the mechanism.","addressable_via":"Already addressed in differentiation_from_lit and what_step_was_missed; no field change needed since the overlap is competitive (shared problem space) not exact-mechanism (shared construction) -- the optimality-gap certificate is the distinguishing artifact."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Water-Filling RoPE: Rate-Distortion-Optimal Frequency Allocation for Position Encoding\n\n**Method.** Water-Filling RoPE (WF-RoPE)\n\n## Motivation\nRoPE (Rotary Position Embedding) is how most modern language models tell tokens apart by position: it rotates each token's query and key vectors by an angle proportional to the token's position, using a fixed list of rotation speeds called frequencies. Those frequencies are laid out as a single geometric sequence -- each one a fixed fraction of the last -- and almost every fix for long-context failure only stretches or shrinks this one sequence by a single knob. Position interpolation shrinks all angles equally; NTK and YaRN scaling shrink fast ones less than slow ones with a hand-tuned rule; and the recent MrRoPE (Mixed-radix RoPE) reinterprets position as a mixed-radix number and unifies these fixes, but still hands the model two pre-chosen schedules rather than computing the best one. So the only thing anyone ever tunes is the overall scale, never the shape of the frequency list itself.\n\nThis matters now because three recent results line up. MrRoPE (January 2026) explicitly opened up the per-dimension freedom -- letting each frequency be set independently -- but never said which setting is best. A phase-modulation analysis (February 2026) proved that the standard geometric frequencies break a Nyquist/aliasing limit at long context (the fast frequencies wrap around into angles the model never saw in training), but only recommended a bigger overall scale. And a 2025 diagnostic showed the slow frequencies are so spread out that some dimensions are effectively dead for long-range lookups. Together they say: the budget of 'rotation resolution' is badly spent, the freedom to respend it exists, and there is a hard limit each frequency must respect -- but nobody has written down what 'best' means and solved for it.\n\nPrior work stopped short for concrete reasons. MrRoPE had no objective function over the per-dimension assignment, so it picked schedules by hand. The phase-modulation paper kept the geometric shape fixed and only constrained one scalar. The dimension-inefficiency paper diagnosed the waste but offered no recipe to redistribute it. And DPE (Dimension-Wise Position Encoding manipulation) remapped dimensions with a heuristic detector rather than an optimization, so it could not certify its choice was best.\n\nWhen the gap closes, extending a model's context stops being trial-and-error over one knob and becomes a solved calculation: given a target length and a corpus, you compute the provably-best per-dimension frequencies in seconds and swap them in without any training. The best grid turns out to be non-monotone -- some middle frequencies get denser, some fast ones are retired -- which the geometric sequence can never represent, and it comes with a certificate proving exactly how much better it is.\n\n## Method\n### Distortion objective\n*Turn 'which per-dimension frequency is best' into a measurable, corpus-grounded distortion the grid can be optimized against.*\n\n1. On your target corpus at the chosen maximum length $L_{max},$ run the model once and record, for every query token, how far back it actually looks — weighting each looked-at distance by how much attention it received — and collect this into a histogram of relative distances $\\delta $ from 0 to $L_{max},$ normalized so it sums to 1. This histogram $P(\\delta )$ tells you which token-to-token distances the model genuinely needs to distinguish. If you have no corpus to measure on, just assume every distance from 0 to $L_{max}$ is equally likely.\n   - _Why_: The best frequencies depend on which distances the model actually has to tell apart, so you measure that first.\n2. For each rotation frequency (each 2-D sub-space i), write down a formula $D_{i}$ that says how much positional error this frequency contributes: take the ideal relative-position signal cos(distance $\\times $ frequency) folded into one clean cycle, subtract what the frequency actually produces when distances are large, square the difference, and average it using the distance histogram $P(\\delta )$ from the previous step. Also compute its curvature (the second derivative). A frequency scores low when it stays within one clean cycle for the distances that matter, and high when it wraps around into angles never seen in training. Since these are exact sums over the histogram, no random sampling is needed.\n\n*Per-dimension distortion $D_{i}:$ the expected squared error in the relative-position term contributed by sub-space i over the corpus relative-distance distribution $P(\\delta ),$ with $curv_{i}$ its second derivative.*\n$$ D_i(\\theta_i) = \\mathbb{E}_{\\delta\\sim P}\\big[(\\cos(\\delta\\,\\theta_i) - \\widehat{\\cos})^2\\big], \\qquad \\mathrm{curv}_i = D_i''(\\theta_i) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This turns 'good frequency' into a number you can minimize instead of an intuition.\n\n### Constrained water-filling solver\n*Solve the convex allocation in closed form under per-dimension Nyquist boxes and a fixed total budget, yielding the non-monotone optimal grid.*\n\n3. Give each frequency a hard ceiling — its Nyquist limit — so it can never rotate fast enough to wrap past the angles the model saw in training: by default set every ceiling to $\\pi $ divided by the full target length $L_{max},$ or tighten each one to the distance that captures all but a tiny fraction (about 0.1%) of the histogram mass. Then set the total 'resolution budget' R to exactly what the model's original geometric frequencies already spend, so that when you re-solve for better frequencies you are only moving budget around, never adding more.\n   - _Why_: The cap enforces the aliasing limit per dimension, and fixing the budget means any improvement comes from respending, not from spending more.\n4. Find the best frequencies by reverse water-filling: there is a single tuning number $\\lambda $; for each frequency set its value by the clipped square-root rule and cap it at that frequency's ceiling, then adjust $\\lambda $ up or down by binary search until the frequencies together spend exactly the budget R. Bracket $\\lambda $ between 'too small, budget unspent' and 'too large, all frequencies at their ceilings', and bisect until the budget is matched to high precision (~50 steps). You must decide how to weight each frequency's error $w_{i}.$ 【author decision: weight every frequency equally (the simplest training-free default), or weight by how much attention energy each carries, or use per-attention-head weights for a head-specific grid — each gives a different optimum.】\n\n*The allocation program: minimize budget-weighted total distortion subject to a per-dimension Nyquist box and a total angular-resolution budget R that makes the geometric grid one feasible point.*\n$$ \\min_{\\theta}\\ \\sum_i w_i D_i(\\theta_i)\\quad \\text{s.t.}\\quad \\theta_i \\le \\frac{\\pi}{L_{\\max}\\text{-eff}_i},\\ \\ \\sum_i \\log\\tfrac{1}{\\theta_i} \\le R \\tag{2} $$\n\n\n*Reverse-water-filling closed form: each sub-space's optimal frequency is set by a single Lagrange multiplier $\\lambda $ (solved by 1-D bisection to meet budget R), clipped to its Nyquist box.*\n$$ \\theta_i^{*} = \\mathrm{clip}\\!\\left(\\sqrt{\\frac{\\lambda}{w_i\\,\\mathrm{curv}_i}},\\,0,\\,\\frac{\\pi}{L_{\\max}\\text{-eff}_i}\\right) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Classical rate-distortion theory says this clipped square-root rule is the exact optimum for splitting a budget across coordinates.\n\n### Train-free swap and certificate\n*Substitute the optimal grid with no fine-tuning and report the optimality-gap certificate $\\Delta $ and non-monotonicity profile.*\n\n5. Replace the model's stored rotation-frequency list with your solved best frequencies $\\theta *.$ This is a one-line change — every attention layer automatically uses the new list — and you touch no weights and do no training. In a standard library this means swapping the precomputed inverse-frequency buffer (and any cached cosine/sine tables) for $\\theta *.$ Because only the frequencies changed, the model's relative-position behavior is preserved; it just scores long-distance pairs using the better frequencies.\n\n*RoPE's relative-position identity: the attention inner product depends on positions only through m - n via the frequency vector $\\theta ,$ and stays intact when $\\theta $ is replaced -- only the buffer changes.*\n$$ \\langle q_m, k_n\\rangle = \\mathrm{Re}\\big(x_m^{*} W_q^{*} W_k\\, x_n\\, e^{\\,i\\,\\theta\\,(m-n)}\\big) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Only the frequencies change, so the model's relative-position behavior is preserved and the swap is free.\n6. Report the certificate $\\Delta ,$ which is the geometric grid's total weighted error minus the water-filling grid's total weighted error, and list the full change $\\theta * -  \\theta _{geom}$ frequency by frequency. To make the pattern readable, tag each frequency as 'retired' if it ended up pinned at its ceiling, 'denser' if it grew, or 'thinned' if it shrank without hitting the ceiling — these tags are just for description. $A \\Delta $ greater than zero is a proof on paper that the original geometric frequencies were not the best choice; $\\Delta $ is zero only if they already were.\n\n*Optimality-gap certificate $\\Delta :$ the budget-weighted distortion of the geometric grid minus that of the water-filling grid, non-negative and zero only when the geometric allocation is already optimal.*\n$$ \\Delta = \\sum_i w_i D_i(\\theta_{\\text{geom}}) - \\sum_i w_i D_i(\\theta^{*}) \\ \\ge\\ 0 \\tag{5} $$\n\n   - _Why_: $\\Delta  \\ge  0$ proves on paper exactly how much better the new grid is and shows it is non-monotone, which a geometric sequence cannot be.\n\n### Falsification and controls\n*Test the long-context payoff against geometric baselines with a permutation control isolating the allocation and a box-only control isolating the bound.*\n\n7. Without any fine-tuning, test the model with the new frequencies on three long-context tasks at lengths 32K, 64K, and 128K: Needle-in-a-Haystack (can it find a planted fact), RULER (a long-context accuracy suite), and perplexity on long documents. Compare against the very same model using the standard RoPE frequencies and the other popular grids (NTK-aware, YaRN, and both MrRoPE schedules), each installed by the same one-line swap so only the frequency list differs. Plot recall, accuracy, and perplexity across the lengths and methods.\n   - _Why_: This checks the real payoff -- better long-context behavior -- against the grids people use today.\n8. Make a scrambled version $\\theta _{perm}$ by randomly shuffling the solved frequencies across dimensions: this keeps the exact same set of frequency values, the same total budget, and the same certificate number, but puts each frequency on the wrong dimension. Install it the same way and re-run the long-context tests. Do this for several different shuffles (about 5–10) and report the average and the range. If putting frequencies on the right dimensions is what matters, every shuffle should drop performance back to — or below — the standard geometric baseline.\n   - _Why_: If the shuffle erases the gain, the win comes from the assignment itself, not just from having those frequency values.\n9. Make a 'ceiling-only' version $\\theta _{box}-only$ by taking the original geometric frequencies and simply capping any that exceed their Nyquist ceiling, with no redistribution of budget. Install it and re-run the long-context tests. Whatever extra improvement the full water-filling frequencies show over this ceiling-only version is the credit due to actually redistributing the budget, as opposed to merely obeying the aliasing limit.\n   - _Why_: This separates how much help comes from obeying the aliasing limit versus from actually redistributing the budget.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# Water-Filling RoPE：面向位置编码的率失真最优频率分配\n\n**方法名称.** Water-Filling RoPE (WF-RoPE)\n\n## 研究动机\nRoPE（Rotary Position Embedding，旋转位置编码）是当今大多数语言模型区分 token 位置的方式：它按 token 的位置成比例地旋转每个 token 的 query 和 key 向量，旋转用的是一组固定的转速，称为频率。这些频率被排成一条几何序列——每一个都是前一个的固定比例——而几乎所有针对长上下文失效的修补方法，都只是用一个旋钮把这条序列整体拉伸或压缩。position interpolation 把所有角度等比例缩小；NTK 和 YaRN 缩放用手工规则让快频率缩得比慢频率少；最近的 MrRoPE（Mixed-radix RoPE，混合基数 RoPE）把位置重新解释为一个混合基数的数并统一了这些方法，但仍然只给模型两套预先选定的调度表，而不是算出最优的那一套。于是大家真正调的永远只是整体的缩放，而从不触及频率列表本身的形状。\n\n这个问题现在变得可解，是因为三项近期结果恰好对齐。MrRoPE（2026 年 1 月）明确打开了逐维的自由度——允许每个频率独立设定——却没有说哪种设定最好。一项相位调制分析（2026 年 2 月）证明标准几何频率在长上下文下会突破 Nyquist/混叠极限（快频率会绕回到训练时从未见过的角度），但只建议把整体缩放调大。一项 2025 年的诊断显示慢频率铺得太开，使某些维度在长距离检索中实际上是死的。三者合起来说明：旋转分辨率这份预算花得很糟，重新分配它的自由度是存在的，而且每个频率都必须遵守一条硬性极限——但还没有人写下『最优』的定义并求解它。\n\n先前工作止步是有具体原因的。MrRoPE 对逐维分配没有目标函数，所以只能手工挑调度表。相位调制论文保持几何形状不变，只约束了一个标量。维度低效论文诊断出了浪费，却没给出重新分配的配方。而 DPE（Dimension-Wise Position Encoding，逐维位置编码操控）用启发式探测器重映射维度，而非优化，因而无法证明其选择是最优的。\n\n当这个缺口被填上，扩展模型上下文就不再是对单一旋钮的反复试错，而变成一道已解的计算题：给定目标长度和语料，几秒内算出可证明最优的逐维频率，无需任何训练即可换入。最优网格被证明是非单调的——某些中间频率变得更密、某些快频率被退役——这是几何序列永远无法表示的，并且它附带一份证书，精确证明它好了多少。\n\n## 方法\n### 失真目标\n*把『哪个逐维频率最优』变成一个可度量、基于语料的失真，使网格可据此优化。*\n\n1. 在目标语料、所选最大长度 $L_{max}$ 上，把模型跑一遍，记录每个 query token 实际回看了多远——并按它获得的 attention 权重对每个被看的距离加权——汇总成一张从 0 到 $L_{max}$ 的相对距离 $\\delta $ 直方图，并归一化使其总和为 1。这张直方图 $P(\\delta )$ 告诉你模型真正需要区分哪些 token 间距离。若没有可测量的语料，就假设 0 到 $L_{max}$ 内每个距离等可能。\n   - _为什么_: 最优频率取决于模型实际需要区分哪些距离，所以先把它测出来。\n2. 对每个旋转频率（每个二维子空间 i），写出一个公式 $D_{i}$，表示该频率贡献了多少位置误差：取折叠到一个干净周期内的理想相对位置信号 cos(距离 $\\times $ 频率)，减去该频率在距离很大时实际产生的值，求平方差，再用上一步的距离直方图 $P(\\delta )$ 加权求平均。同时算出它的曲率(curvature，即二阶导数)。当一个频率对重要的距离都停留在一个干净周期内时得分低，当它绕回到训练中从未见过的角度时得分高。由于这些都是对直方图的精确求和，无需随机采样。\n\n*逐维失真 $D_{i}$：子空间 i 在语料相对距离分布 $P(\\delta )$ 下对相对位置项贡献的期望平方误差；$curv_{i}$ 为其二阶导数。*\n$$ D_i(\\theta_i) = \\mathbb{E}_{\\delta\\sim P}\\big[(\\cos(\\delta\\,\\theta_i) - \\widehat{\\cos})^2\\big], \\qquad \\mathrm{curv}_i = D_i''(\\theta_i) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这把『好频率』从直觉变成一个可以最小化的数值。\n\n### 带约束的注水求解器\n*在逐维 Nyquist 上界与固定总预算下闭式求解凸分配，得到非单调的最优网格。*\n\n3. 给每个频率一个硬性上限——它的 Nyquist(奈奎斯特)极限——使它绝不会快到绕过模型训练时见过的角度：默认把每个上限设为 $\\pi $ 除以完整目标长度 $L_{max}$，或把每个上限收紧到能覆盖直方图除极小一部分(约 0.1%)质量之外的距离。然后把总『分辨率预算』R 设为模型原始几何频率恰好花掉的量，这样当你重新求解更优频率时，只是在挪动预算，绝不增加预算。\n   - _为什么_: 上限按维度强制执行混叠极限，而固定预算意味着任何提升都来自重新分配，而非花得更多。\n4. 用反向注水(reverse water-filling)找最优频率：只有一个调节数 $\\lambda $；对每个频率用裁剪过的平方根规则设定其取值，并裁剪到该频率的上限，然后通过二分搜索上下调整 $\\lambda $，直到这些频率合起来恰好花完预算 R。把 $\\lambda $ 框定在『太小、预算没花完』与『太大、所有频率都顶到上限』之间，二分到预算被高精度匹配为止(约 50 步)。你需要决定如何为每个频率的误差加权 $w_{i}$。【作者需决定：可对每个频率等权(最简单的免训练默认)，或按各自携带的 attention 能量加权，或用逐 attention head 的权重得到 head 专属网格——每种都给出不同的最优解。】\n\n*分配规划：在逐维 Nyquist 上界与总角分辨率预算 R（使几何网格恰为一个可行点）的约束下，最小化按预算加权的总失真。*\n$$ \\min_{\\theta}\\ \\sum_i w_i D_i(\\theta_i)\\quad \\text{s.t.}\\quad \\theta_i \\le \\frac{\\pi}{L_{\\max}\\text{-eff}_i},\\ \\ \\sum_i \\log\\tfrac{1}{\\theta_i} \\le R \\tag{2} $$\n\n\n*反向注水的闭式解：每个子空间的最优频率由单一拉格朗日乘子 $\\lambda $ 决定（用一维二分法求解以满足预算 R），并裁剪到各自的 Nyquist 上界。*\n$$ \\theta_i^{*} = \\mathrm{clip}\\!\\left(\\sqrt{\\frac{\\lambda}{w_i\\,\\mathrm{curv}_i}},\\,0,\\,\\frac{\\pi}{L_{\\max}\\text{-eff}_i}\\right) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 经典率失真理论表明，这个裁剪过的平方根规则正是把预算分配到各坐标上的精确最优解。\n\n### 免训练替换与证书\n*无需微调即替换最优网格，并报告最优性间隙证书 $\\Delta $ 与非单调性剖面。*\n\n5. 把模型存储的旋转频率列表替换为你求解出的最优频率 $\\theta *$。这是一行改动——每个 attention 层会自动采用新列表——你不触碰任何权重，也不做训练。在标准库中，这意味着把预先算好的逆频率缓冲区(以及任何缓存的 cosine/sine 表)换成 $\\theta *$。由于只改了频率，模型的相对位置行为得以保留；它只是用更优的频率为长距离 token 对打分。\n\n*RoPE 的相对位置恒等式：注意力内积只通过 m - n 依赖位置（经由频率向量 $\\theta $），替换 $\\theta $ 时该恒等式保持不变，改变的仅是频率缓冲区。*\n$$ \\langle q_m, k_n\\rangle = \\mathrm{Re}\\big(x_m^{*} W_q^{*} W_k\\, x_n\\, e^{\\,i\\,\\theta\\,(m-n)}\\big) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 只有频率改变，模型的相对位置行为得以保留，且这次替换是零成本的。\n6. 报告证书 $\\Delta $，即几何网格的总加权误差减去注水网格的总加权误差，并逐个频率列出完整变化 $\\theta * -  \\theta _{geom}$。为使规律可读，把每个频率标记为：若最终顶到上限则为『退役』，若变大则为『加密』，若未顶上限而变小则为『稀释』——这些标记仅供描述。$\\Delta $ 大于零就是纸面上的证明，说明原始几何频率并非最优选择；只有当它们本就最优时 $\\Delta $ 才为零。\n\n*最优性间隙证书 $\\Delta $：几何网格与注水网格在按预算加权下的失真之差，恒非负，且仅当几何分配本身已最优时为零。*\n$$ \\Delta = \\sum_i w_i D_i(\\theta_{\\text{geom}}) - \\sum_i w_i D_i(\\theta^{*}) \\ \\ge\\ 0 \\tag{5} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: $\\Delta  \\ge  0$ 在纸面上精确证明新网格好了多少，并显示它是非单调的——这是几何序列做不到的。\n\n### 证伪与对照\n*对照几何基线检验长上下文收益，用置换对照分离出分配的作用、用仅上限对照分离出界的作用。*\n\n7. 在不做任何微调的情况下，用新频率在三项长上下文任务、长度 32K、64K、128K 上测试模型：Needle-in-a-Haystack(能否找到植入的事实)、RULER(一套长上下文准确率评测)、以及长文档困惑度(perplexity)。与使用标准 RoPE 频率以及其他流行网格(NTK-aware、YaRN、两套 MrRoPE 调度)的同一模型对比，每种都用同样的一行替换装入，使得仅频率列表不同。画出各长度、各方法下的召回率、准确率与困惑度曲线。\n   - _为什么_: 这检验真正的收益——更好的长上下文表现——并与人们当下使用的网格做对照。\n8. 做一个打乱版 $\\theta _{perm}$：把求解出的频率在各维度间随机洗牌——这保持了完全相同的频率取值集合、相同的总预算、相同的证书数值，但把每个频率放到了错误的维度上。用同样方式装入并重跑长上下文测试。对若干种不同洗牌(约 5–10 次)各做一遍，报告平均值与范围。如果把频率放到正确维度上才是关键，那么每种洗牌都应使性能跌回——或低于——标准几何基线。\n   - _为什么_: 如果打乱后收益消失，说明胜出来自分配本身，而不仅仅是拥有那些频率值。\n9. 做一个『仅上限』版 $\\theta _{box}-only$：取原始几何频率，仅把任何超过其 Nyquist 上限的频率裁剪到上限，不做任何预算的重新分配。装入并重跑长上下文测试。完整注水频率相对这个仅上限版本多出的改进，就是真正重新分配预算应得的功劳，区别于仅仅遵守混叠极限。\n   - _为什么_: 这能区分多少帮助来自遵守混叠极限，多少来自真正重新分配预算。\n\n"},{"id":"81","run_dir":"run_prompt81_unpairmatch","index":81,"title":"Relational-Agreement Matching: Unpaired Image-Text Matching by Construction, Not Concept Bank","title_zh":"关系一致性匹配：以构造方式而非概念库实现无配对图文匹配","method_name":"Relational-Agreement Matching (RAM)","hook":"Every unpaired image-text matcher scores how many concepts two modalities share, but none scores how those concepts are BOUND — so 'a man bites a dog' and 'a dog bites a man' get the same image score. We show the matching signal lives at a relational-agreement locus computed by construction between two independently-built scene graphs, recovering binding without any paired supervision and without a precollected word-region bank.","anchor_pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","anchor_pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","domain_category":"Vision-Language & Multimodal","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved unpaired-matching leaf produces a cross-modal score that depends on how concepts are BOUND/related within each modality rather than only on which concepts are present, so two instances with the same concept set but different relational structure remain indistinguishable when paired supervision is removed (additive need at the MACK / coarse-to-fine common-space frontier leaf).","pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","sub_pattern":"C13 (Encode Structure by Construction)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by making the relational connectivity topology of each modality (a typed scene graph over concept nodes) the encoded structural prior, and computing the cross-modal score as a relation-typed graph-agreement statistic over the two wirings by construction, so binding (subject-verb-object / attribute-noun edges) is captured rather than relearned from pairs.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved unpaired-matching leaf questions whether the cross-modal score must be assembled from per-concept word-region associations collected before training at all, rather than emerging from agreement between independently-built structured representations of each modality (subtractive assumption: every unpaired leaf inherits the precomputed-per-concept-association node from the region-word-similarity ancestor and none tests whether that decomposition is necessary).","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"structural_prior_encoding","how_closed":"Framing move (assumption_audit_and_pivot / C01): name the representational LOCUS every unpaired matcher anchors its grounding signal at — a precomputed per-concept word-region association table — and relocate the load-bearing matching signal to an overlooked locus, the inference-time relational-agreement between two independently-built within-modality graphs, showing the precomputed-association locus was the wrong place to enforce matching; companion deliverable (structural_prior_encoding): the C13 relation-typed graph-agreement operator is the runnable artifact that scores matching at the new locus and empirically certifies the relocation.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"cross-modal vision-language matching / unpaired image-text retrieval","n_papers":48,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":25},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":16,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Unpaired Image-Text Matching via Multimodal Aligned Conceptual Knowledge"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Generative artificial intelligence: a systematic review and applications"},{"source":"openalex","title":"A Systematic Review of Synthetic Data Generation Techniques Using Generative AI"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Vision-language models for medical report generation and visual question answering: a review"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Generative AI-Driven Semantic Communication Networks: Architecture, Technologies, and Applications"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Mitochondrial complex I promotes kidney cancer metastasis"}],"more":10},{"year":2025,"n":24,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Generating Multimodal Images with GAN: Integrating Text, Image, and Style"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Att-Adapter: a Robust and Precise Domain-Specific Multi-Attributes T2i Diffusion Adapter Via Conditional Variational Autoencoder"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Beyond General Alignment: Fine-Grained Entity-Centric Image-Text Matching with Multimodal Attentive Experts"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Enhancing image–text matching through multi-level semantic consistency alignment"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Ambiguity-Aware and High-order Relation learning for multi-grained image-text matching"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"GADNet: Improving image-text matching via graph-based aggregation and disentanglement"}],"more":18},{"year":2026,"n":8,"papers":[{"source":"arxiv","title":"Learning Image-Text Matching with Optimal Partial Transport"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"RAFM: Retrieval-Augmented Flow Matching for Unpaired CBCT-to-CT Translation"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Low-Effort Jailbreak Attacks Against Text-to-Image Safety Filters"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Bootstrap Your Generator: Unpaired Visual Editing with Flow Matching"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Understanding Pure Textual Reasoning for Blind Image Quality Assessment"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"FullFlow: Upgrading Text-to-Image Flow Matching Models for Bidirectional Vision--Language Generation"}],"more":2}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":14,"share":0.292},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":10,"share":0.208},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":7,"share":0.146},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":6,"share":0.125},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":5,"share":0.104},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":5,"share":0.104},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":5,"share":0.104},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":3,"share":0.062}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"In the unpaired image-text matching setting introduced by MACK (semanticscholar:ac26da57cae6c6c341818a395d4ec21eac5b8039), the only available cross-modal signal is a per-concept association between a word and a prototypical visual region built once from an external region-tagged dataset; matching then scores each parsed word against image regions independently and pools the scores bidirectionally. Because the association is concept-by-concept and the pooling is order/relation-agnostic, two distinct failures follow: (a) a caption and an image that share the same set of concepts but bind them differently (e.g. 'a man bites a dog' vs 'a dog bites a man', or attribute mis-binding documented for global representations in arxiv:2512.17178v1) receive nearly identical aggregated similarity, so relational/compositional structure carries no weight; and (b) any concept absent from the externally-collected bank has no prototypical region at all, so its contribution to the score is undefined and the unpaired-only refinement (self-supervised on unpaired images and texts) cannot manufacture the missing word-region association because it never observes the two modalities co-occurring. The same concept-independence assumption is inherited by the cross-modal hashing / common-space lines (openalex:W4406823622 builds a coarse-to-fine common space for unpaired retrieval, openalex:W4400875435 derives unsupervised pseudo-similarity from features) whose alignment quality is bounded by an initial per-instance similarity that no relational structure corrects. The failure is: when paired supervision is removed, current machinery can only certify that the same concepts are PRESENT in both modalities, not that they are BOUND the same way, and it goes silent on concepts outside its collected vocabulary.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:ac26da57cae6c6c341818a395d4ec21eac5b8039","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"MACK matches images and texts without paired training by collecting word->prototypical-region prototypes from external region-tagged data, refining them self-supervised on unpaired images/texts, then scoring region-word similarity and bidirectional-pooling into an image-text score. Its residue: the concept bank is static and scores concepts independently, so it cannot represent how concepts are RELATED/composed within an image or sentence (no relational binding) and emits no signal for any concept the external bank never collected, and the self-supervised refinement on unpaired data cannot create a missing word-region association because the two modalities are never observed co-occurring. [residue is abstract-level: anchor fulltext unfetchable]"},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4406823622","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Constructs a two-stage (coarse-to-fine) common semantic space for unpaired cross-modal retrieval. Residue: the fine stage's alignment is bounded by the coarse stage's per-instance similarity, which is itself concept-presence-based and has no mechanism to use relational/compositional agreement between the two modalities, so it shares MACK's binding-blindness."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4400875435","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Unsupervised cross-modal hashing that derives pseudo-similarity from features via dynamic contrast/optimization without labels. Residue: the pseudo-similarity is a global feature-distance proxy with no concept-level or relational anchoring, so it cannot distinguish same-concepts-different-binding instances and degrades on concepts whose feature geometry is unreliable in the unpaired regime."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2512.17178v1","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"ABE-CLIP enhances compositional attribute binding in CLIP matching training-free by decomposing the global embedding. Residue: it relies on CLIP's massive PAIRED pretraining to supply the per-token visual grounding it re-binds, so its compositional fix has no counterpart in the truly unpaired regime where no paired-pretrained per-token grounding exists to start from."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"cross-modal vision-language matching / unpaired image-text retrieval","venue":"ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML (Oral tier); CV/ML cross-modal track","time":"2026","data":["region-tagged image datasets (e.g. Visual Genome, OpenImages) as a concept source","unpaired image corpora and text corpora (Flickr30K / MS-COCO images and captions used in an unpaired regime)","scene-graph / parser outputs for text"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day) [inferred default]","expertise":"vision-language representation learning, cross-modal retrieval","preference":"both","baseline":"MACK (Multimodal Aligned Conceptual Knowledge, TPAMI 2024) as the unpaired-matching reference; CLIP zero-shot as the paired-pretraining reference","limitation":"unpaired image-text matching currently rests on a static, externally-built word->prototypical-region concept bank that scores region-word similarity independently and pools them, so it cannot represent relations/compositions between concepts and cannot ground concepts the bank never collected","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object across both legs is one quantity: a relation-typed graph-agreement score S(I,T) computed by construction between two independently-built scene graphs, G_I for the image and G_T for the text, with NO paired image-text supervision and NO precollected word-region association table. Build G_T by parsing the caption with an off-the-shelf dependency/SRL parser into typed edges over concept nodes (node = lemma string for a noun/verb/attribute; edge type in {subject_of, object_of, attribute_of, spatial_relation} read directly off the parse). Build G_I by running an open-vocabulary detector/segmenter (e.g. a frozen Detic/GroundingDINO-class model, no caption supervision used) to get region nodes, labelling each region node with its predicted concept lemma, and inducing typed edges from purely visual geometry/relation heuristics that require no pairing: attribute_of from a region's own appearance classifier, spatial_relation from relative box geometry (above/left-of/contains), and subject_of/object_of from an unpaired-trained visual-relation predictor (trained on a region-relation dataset that is itself unpaired with any target caption). To make the two graphs comparable WITHOUT a learned cross-modal projection trained on pairs, embed every node label (image lemma and text lemma alike) into one frozen text-only word-embedding space E (a single uni-modal language encoder), so node-to-node compatibility is c(u,v)=cosine(E(label_u),E(label_v)) — this is the bridge that lets a region labelled 'dog' and a word 'dog' agree, and the ONLY place vocabulary enters; it is open-vocabulary because E embeds any lemma, closing the binding gap for any concept E can embed (Leg-1 / C13 Step 1-2: the named relational object is the typed-edge agreement, captured by construction). The score is then a relation-typed assignment problem: find a soft node-matching matrix P (rows=text nodes, cols=image nodes, doubly-stochastic via a fixed-iteration Sinkhorn) maximizing node-label agreement sum_{u,v} P[u,v]*c(u,v) PLUS an edge-consistency term lambda * sum over text edges (u,u',r) of sum_{v,v'} P[u,v]*P[u',v']*1[edge_type(v,v')==r]*g(v,v',r), where g scores whether the image graph carries the same relation type r between the matched regions; S(I,T) is the optimal objective value, lambda a fixed scalar hyperparameter (set on a held-out unpaired dev split by the dev protocol below, default 0.5). The edge term is exactly what makes 'man bites dog' != 'dog bites man': swapping subject_of/object_of flips which (v,v') pair the term rewards, so the same node set yields a different S — this is the binding signal MACK's relation-agnostic pooling cannot produce (Leg-1 closes gap-0). Leg-2 (audit / C01 framing + structural_prior_encoding companion) is realized on this SAME object: the audited assumption is the sufficiency claim 'the cross-modal score is an aggregation of independent per-concept word-region associations precomputed before training' (the locus); we relocate the matching signal to the relational-agreement locus (the edge term over P) and show the old locus is recoverable as the lambda=0, no-edge special case of S, so MACK-style scoring is literally the degenerate sub-case of ours with the relational locus switched off — the companion's runnable operator (the Sinkhorn graph-matcher) is what certifies the relocation empirically. Because S needs no paired training and no association bank, it is computed online for any (I,T); the only learned-on-unpaired-data piece is the visual-relation predictor, and even it never sees a target caption.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"Both gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules: the binding gap (gap-0) is closed by the relation-typed graph-agreement score, and the subtractive audit gap (gap-2) is the SAME score read as a locus relocation (the precomputed-association table is the lambda=0, node-only degenerate case), so a single object — S(I,T) — carries both legs, which is why coherence_thread_type is shared_audit/shared_object and not two stapled modules. I considered (and rejected) a design that learns a cross-modal projection between region features and word embeddings: that would smuggle paired supervision back in and regress toward lineage node n3 (relation graph trained from PAIRED correspondences) flagged in method_lineage.notes — so the avoided node is n3, and the regression is avoided by routing ALL cross-modal compatibility through one FROZEN uni-modal text-embedding space E applied identically to both modalities' lemma labels, a source the lineage tree does not occupy. I also rejected building G_I edges from a paired visual-genome-style relation model conditioned on captions for the same reason; the visual-relation predictor is trained on region-relation data unpaired with any target caption.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on MS-COCO/Flickr30K evaluated in the unpaired regime (no image-caption pairs seen in training), run our relational-agreement matcher and MACK as a baseline, and additionally construct a binding-probe set of caption pairs that share the identical concept lemma set but differ only in relational binding (swapped subject/object or re-assigned attributes, e.g. 'man bites dog' vs 'dog bites man'; 'red car blue truck' vs 'blue car red truck'), each with one matching and one mismatching image. If the candidate works, binding-probe matching accuracy rises sharply above MACK's near-chance (MACK and any per-concept-presence pooler cannot exceed chance on this probe because the concept sets are identical), while standard Recall@K stays at least on par with MACK. The named load-bearing variable is the edge-consistency weight lambda (the scalar gating the relational locus). Mechanism distinguisher with a non-tautological negative control: set lambda=0 (ablate the relational locus, leaving only node-presence agreement — the MACK-equivalent degenerate case); the prediction is that the DOWNSTREAM binding-probe accuracy collapses back to chance while standard Recall@K is largely unchanged — confirming the relational locus, not the node embeddings, carries the binding signal. As a positive control, a stripped model using ONLY the edge term (node agreement frozen to identity within the probe's shared concept set) should recover most of the binding-probe accuracy, identifying the edge-agreement statistic as the sufficient mechanism.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:ac26da57cae6c6c341818a395d4ec21eac5b8039","delta":"MACK constructs a static precomputed word->prototypical-region association table and scores by relation-agnostic bidirectional pooling of independent region-word similarities; we construct NO association table and instead derive a relation-typed graph-agreement score by construction at inference, of which MACK's pooled score is the lambda=0 degenerate special case, so we produce a binding-sensitive signal their construction provably cannot (their pooling is invariant to subject/object swaps)."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4406823622","delta":"The coarse-to-fine common-space method builds a shared embedding whose fine alignment is bounded by a per-instance coarse similarity with no relational term; we instead compute a relation-typed edge-consistency statistic over two independently-built graphs, giving a score that distinguishes same-concept-different-binding instances their per-instance similarity treats as identical."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2512.17178v1","delta":"ABE-CLIP fixes compositional attribute binding by re-decomposing CLIP's globally-pooled embedding, which exists only because of CLIP's billion-pair paired pretraining; we recover binding in the truly unpaired regime where no paired-pretrained per-token grounding exists, by routing all cross-modal compatibility through a frozen uni-modal text-embedding space applied to both modalities' lemma labels."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2603.14349v1","delta":"OMIT uses optimal transport (Sinkhorn) to compute fine-grained image-text similarity but trains the transport cost with PAIRED similarity supervision and over feature fragments without typed relations; we use Sinkhorn over typed scene-graph nodes with an edge-consistency term and zero paired supervision, so our transport optimizes relational agreement rather than learned paired fragment cost."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:ac26da57cae6c6c341818a395d4ec21eac5b8039","what_step_was_missed":"MACK constructed per-concept word->region prototype associations and a bidirectional similarity-pooling aggregator, but it never constructed the typed relational wiring of each modality nor an edge-consistency statistic over a node-matching — so its score has no term that depends on how concepts connect; adding binding would have required building, for each image and each text, an independent typed graph and a relation-aware agreement objective (the Sinkhorn-plus-edge-term construction) whose value changes when subject/object edges swap, a relational construction absent from their per-concept pooling design."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":344,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"Layer 1 hard floor does not fire: no gap_closure_reject lesson is a 'yes' match, no anti-pattern composition matches, and paper_pointed_threat (OMIT) is addressable, not exact-mechanism overlap. Layer 2 chooses revise because a borderline hits a LOAD-BEARING structural property: gap_closure_reject_check.entries[0] lesson 'A domain-grounded architecture lacking any theoretical guarantee that its wiring captures the claimed structure ... leaves reviewers unable to credit the structural claim' is exactly C13 Step 4's demanded certificate, and the candidate currently argues binding-sensitivity only constructively — so a theoretical_leg stating and (sketch-)proving that the relational-agreement score is binding-sensitive while its lambda=0 reduction is provably binding-invariant must be added. A second, lighter revision sharpens differentiation against OMIT/SOTAlign per paper_pointed_threat.addressable_via.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved unpaired-matching leaf produces a cross-modal score that depends on how concepts are BOUND/related within each modality rather than only on which concepts are present, so two instances with the same concept set but different relational structure remain indistinguishable when paired supervision is removed (additive need at the MACK / coarse-to-fine common-space frontier leaf).","main_pattern":"structural_prior_encoding","sub_pattern":"C13 (Encode Structure by Construction)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring reject shape is assembling existing relational-learning components into a problem-specific architecture, then claiming the encoded relational structure as the contribution without proving it; the construction typically carries no guarantee (no expressiveness, recovery, identifiability, or uniqueness result) that its wiring actually captures the claimed structural property.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Combining borrowed modules (global plus local streams, attention plus state tracking) with no genuinely new mechanism reads as incremental even when the combination is sensible.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The genuinely new mechanism — a relation-typed edge-consistency term over a soft node-matching whose value flips under subject/object swaps — is sharply delineated from the borrowed parser/detector/Sinkhorn components, which are explicitly off-the-shelf inputs."},{"lesson_quoted":"A domain-grounded architecture lacking any theoretical guarantee that its wiring captures the claimed structure — and lacking a uniqueness or identifiability argument — leaves reviewers unable to credit the structural claim.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"core_mechanism gives a constructive argument (the edge term differs under subject/object swap) and an empirical binding-probe + lambda=0 ablation, but no formal statement that the relational-agreement score is provably binding-sensitive / that lambda=0 is provably binding-invariant — C13 Step 4 demands an expressiveness or identifiability certificate, which is currently absent."},{"lesson_quoted":"Inheriting the core operator and its constraints from prior work and merely porting them to a new domain collapses the contribution to assembly unless the incremental piece is delineated explicitly.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The edge-consistency objective is not ported from a prior matcher; OMIT/Sinkhorn matching is node-only and paired-trained, and the candidate delineates the edge term as the incremental piece."},{"lesson_quoted":"Inflated or balanced evaluation protocols can mask that a hand-crafted structural heuristic already outperforms the learned construction in the realistic distribution, removing the motivation for added complexity.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The binding-probe is adversarially constructed (identical concept sets) precisely so a concept-presence heuristic scores at chance, and standard R@K is also reported — the protocol is not balanced-to-hide."},{"lesson_quoted":"Omitting closely-related SOTA baselines and the simplest correlation or heuristic comparison makes any claimed structural advantage unverifiable.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"MACK (the closest unpaired baseline) and the lambda=0 node-only degenerate case (the simplest structure-agnostic comparison) are both included."},{"lesson_quoted":"Proposing a new construction or task without analyzing the information loss it introduces (compressing histories into profiles, projecting away radial distance) invites doubt about whether the encoded structure helps or hurts.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"Routing all cross-modal compatibility through a single frozen uni-modal text-embedding space E is an information-bottleneck (visual features collapsed to lemma labels) whose loss is not analyzed; this is a real but secondary concern, foldable into reviewer_concerns."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved unpaired-matching leaf questions whether the cross-modal score must be assembled from per-concept word-region associations collected before training at all, rather than emerging from agreement between independently-built structured representations of each modality (subtractive assumption: every unpaired leaf inherits the precomputed-per-concept-association node from the region-word-similarity ancestor and none tests whether that decomposition is necessary).","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is a relocation demonstrated but not adversarially closed, or a novelty-boundary collapse where the 'new' locus turns out to be one a prior paper already used, or offering only a demonstration with no mechanistic account of why the locus carries the signal.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work — normalization statistics, activation-similarity losses, semantic concept triggers — collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The relational-agreement locus is adjacent to paired graph-relation matchers (GADNet/AAHR) and OMIT's OT fragment matching; the candidate's distinction (no paired supervision, typed edge-consistency, MACK is the lambda=0 sub-case) is stated and measured, but the boundary against paired graph-matchers must be made unmistakable to avoid a fold-back."},{"lesson_quoted":"A defense whose relocation silently depends on a clean reference model or a known anomaly distribution reintroduces precisely the strong assumption the move was supposed to eliminate.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The relocation depends only on frozen uni-modal encoders and unpaired-trained components; it does not smuggle back paired supervision (the assumption being dissolved), which is verified by the design avoiding lineage node n3."},{"lesson_quoted":"Demonstrating the new locus only on fixed, non-adaptive or outdated baselines while omitting any account of why it works reads as a stacked pipeline of existing components rather than a principled shift.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism gives the account of WHY the relational locus carries the binding signal (the edge term over P is exactly the quantity invariant under concept-presence but sensitive to edge-type swaps), not merely a demonstration."},{"lesson_quoted":"Wiring off-the-shelf generators or tools into a new attack setting without a structural reason for the locus change gets judged as engineering integration, not insight.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The structural reason for the locus change is explicit: concept-presence pooling is provably invariant to binding, so the load-bearing signal MUST live at the relational locus — the change is motivated, not convenience integration."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No Reject lesson is a hard 'yes' match, so the floor does not fire. The weight-bearing borderline is on the C13 (structural_prior_encoding) entry's lesson 'A domain-grounded architecture lacking any theoretical guarantee that its wiring captures the claimed structure ... leaves reviewers unable to credit the structural claim' — the candidate currently certifies binding-sensitivity only constructively/empirically, not with the expressiveness or identifiability statement C13 Step 4 demands. The C01 borderline (novelty-boundary vs paired graph-matchers) is secondary and addressable by sharpening differentiation."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved unpaired-matching leaf produces a cross-modal score that depends on how concepts are BOUND/related within each modality rather than only on which concepts are present, so two instances with the same concept set but different relational structure remain indistinguishable when paired supervision is removed (additive need at the MACK / coarse-to-fine common-space frontier leaf).","sub_pattern":"C13 (Encode Structure by Construction)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Make the relational connectivity topology itself the encoded structural prior: define which entities link to which (and under what relation type), then run message-passing/propagation over that wiring so a specific structural quantity is captured by construction rather than relearned by a generic dense or attention model; match the aggregation operator to each relation's topology.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism steps 1-2 build typed scene graphs (subject_of/object_of/attribute_of/spatial_relation edges) as the explicit connectivity topology, and step 5's edge-consistency term is a relation-typed aggregation operator over that wiring (it propagates compatibility along matched edges and rewards same-type relations), so the binding statistic is captured by construction — this performs C13's distinctive 'relational topology as encoded prior + relation-typed operator' move, not a generic dense model.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved unpaired-matching leaf questions whether the cross-modal score must be assembled from per-concept word-region associations collected before training at all, rather than emerging from agreement between independently-built structured representations of each modality (subtractive assumption: every unpaired leaf inherits the precomputed-per-concept-association node from the region-word-similarity ancestor and none tests whether that decomposition is necessary).","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"The audited assumption is always about the representational LOCUS at which a property is presumed to be enforced, and the tactical move is to relocate the signal to a different locus the field treated as irrelevant or invariant, then supply a mechanistic account of why the property must manifest more robustly at the new locus.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism's Leg-2 names the locus (precomputed per-concept word-region association table) as the falsifiable sufficiency claim, relocates the matching signal to the relational-agreement locus (the edge term over P), and accounts mechanistically for why binding must live there (concept-presence pooling is the lambda=0 degenerate sub-case, provably binding-invariant). The cluster's [Accept] examples are security-domain, but the abstract locus-relocation move is genuinely performed; borderline because the 'overlooked-locus-is-MORE-robust' framing is realized as 'binding-sensitive' rather than 'invariant to an access restriction', a softer form of the cluster's signature.","verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The C13 anchor entry cleanly applies the relational-topology-as-prior move. The C01 audit entry performs the abstract locus-relocation but in a non-security instantiation, so it is borderline rather than bypassed — the relocation and its mechanistic account are present, which is the cluster's load-bearing operation."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["structural_prior_encoding","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"None of the three reject-favored compositions matches: all three require heterogeneous_decomposition as a component, which is absent from {structural_prior_encoding, assumption_audit_and_pivot} (the companion structural_prior_encoding does not add heterogeneous_decomposition either)."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"arxiv:2603.14349v1","threat_source":"lit_table","subsumption_argument":"OMIT (Learning Image-Text Matching with Optimal Partial Transport) is the nearest mechanism: it also uses Sinkhorn/optimal transport to compute fine-grained image-text similarity over fragments, so a reviewer could ask whether the candidate is OMIT plus a graph. The candidate stands because OMIT trains its transport cost with PAIRED similarity supervision over untyped feature fragments and has no edge-consistency term, whereas the candidate uses zero paired supervision and a relation-typed edge term whose value flips under subject/object swaps — OMIT's node-only paired transport is, in the candidate's own framing, the lambda=0 paired special case. The claim falls only if OMIT (or SOTAlign / EmergentBridge from collision_hits) already computed a typed-relational edge-consistency statistic without pairs, which none do (SOTAlign is semi-supervised whole-encoder OT with no relational term; EmergentBridge addresses missing modality-pair coverage in unified embeddings, not relational binding).","addressable_via":"Sharpen differentiation_from_lit against OMIT/SOTAlign to make the no-paired-supervision + typed-edge-consistency boundary explicit and measured (a non-load-bearing field edit)."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","issue":"gap_closure_reject_check.entries[0] borderline on the missing-guarantee lesson; recipe_application_check C13 Step 4 demands an expressiveness/identifiability certificate that the wiring captures the binding statistic.","fix_direction":"Add to core_mechanism an explicit theoretical_leg: state a proposition that the relation-typed agreement score S(I,T) is binding-sensitive by construction — formally, for two texts T, T' with identical node-label multisets but a swapped relation edge (subject_of <-> object_of), the edge term (and hence S) provably differs whenever the image graph carries the corresponding asymmetric relation, while the lambda=0 reduction S0 is provably invariant to that swap (S0(I,T)=S0(I,T')). Give the short argument (the node term depends only on the label multiset, so it is identical for T,T'; the edge term is a sum over directed text edges whose matched image-relation indicator is not symmetric under endpoint swap). This converts the binding claim from empirical to a by-construction identifiability statement, satisfying C13's guarantee demand. Do NOT modify falsification_prediction or compute_budget."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat (OMIT) addressable; C01 novelty-boundary-collapse borderline vs paired graph-matchers and OT matchers.","fix_direction":"Tighten the OMIT delta and add/sharpen a SOTAlign-style entry so the boundary is unmistakable: state that all OT/graph matchers in the pool (OMIT, GADNet, AAHR, SOTAlign) either (i) train the transport/relation cost with paired or semi-paired supervision, or (ii) carry no relation-typed edge-consistency term, and that the candidate is the only construction combining zero paired supervision WITH a typed edge-consistency statistic — making MACK and OMIT both special cases (node-only) of S. Keep it substantive (what each constructs vs what we construct), not methodological."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Appended a by-construction binding-sensitivity proposition (with its short argument) showing S(I,T) provably differs under a subject/object edge swap while the lambda=0 reduction is provably swap-invariant, converting C13's structural claim from empirical to an identifiability certificate."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Sharpened the OMIT delta and added a SOTAlign collision entry so the no-paired-supervision + typed-edge-consistency boundary against all OT/graph matchers in the pool is explicit and measured."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Relational-Agreement Matching: Unpaired Image-Text Matching by Construction, Not Concept Bank\n\n**Method.** Relational-Agreement Matching (RAM)\n\n## Motivation\nSuppose you want a system that can match pictures to captions even though it has never seen a single picture paired with its correct caption during training. This is called unpaired image-text matching, and the leading method is MACK (Multimodal Aligned Conceptual Knowledge). MACK works by first building, from a separate dataset of labelled image regions, a dictionary that says 'the word dog tends to look like this kind of region'. To score how well an image matches a caption, it checks each caption word against the image's regions one at a time and adds up the matches. The problem is subtle but fatal: because it scores each word independently and then just sums the results, it has no way to tell apart 'a man bites a dog' from 'a dog bites a man'. Both sentences contain exactly the same words — man, bites, dog — so the summed score is the same, even though the meanings are opposites. The same blindness shows up for attributes: 'a red car and a blue truck' versus 'a blue car and a red truck'. The newer methods in this area (a two-stage common-space method from 2025, and various unsupervised hashing methods) inherit the same flaw, because they all start from independent per-concept similarities and never add anything that depends on how the concepts are connected. A different recent method, ABE-CLIP, does fix this binding problem, but only by leaning on CLIP — a model trained on billions of paired image-text examples — so it has no version that works in the truly unpaired setting we care about. What makes a fix possible now is that three tools recently became reliable enough: open-vocabulary detectors that can label arbitrary image regions with words without any caption supervision; frozen text encoders that can place any word (whether it came from the image side or the text side) into one shared space; and fast Sinkhorn matching that can line up two sets of items cheaply. Our idea is to stop summing independent per-word matches and instead build a small 'who-is-doing-what-to-whom' graph separately for the image and for the caption, then score how well those two graphs AGREE — including the connections, not just the nodes. When this gap is closed, an unpaired matcher can finally separate sentences that contain the same words but mean different things, a capability the entire MACK-style line structurally cannot deliver, and the old MACK-style score turns out to be just the special case of ours where the connection-checking is switched off.\n\n## Method\n### Background scaffolding\n*Off-the-shelf parsing and matching machinery the contribution runs on, not itself novel.*\n\n1. Run an off-the-shelf grammar parser (spaCy) plus a Semantic Role Labelling (SRL) model on the caption to turn it into a small graph. Words for nouns, verbs and attributes become nodes (reduced to their dictionary base form, with filler words like 'the' removed). Then add directed labelled links: verb-to-subject as $subject_{of},$ verb-to-object as $object_{of},$ adjective-to-noun as $attribute_{of},$ and noun-to-noun as $spatial_{relation}$ for a fixed list of place words (on, in, above, below, left of, right of, inside, behind, in front of). The output is a graph of nodes plus typed links.\n   - _Why_: This graph records not just which concepts are mentioned but who does what to whom — the connection information the old summing approach throws away.\n2. Find a soft matching between text nodes and image nodes using the Sinkhorn algorithm. Treat the compatibility table as a reward to maximize, run K=20 Sinkhorn iterations (with a small smoothing temperature of 0.1, in the numerically-stable log domain), and require each text node and each image node to carry equal total matching mass. When the two sides have unequal node counts, add an optional 'leftover' row and column to absorb unmatched nodes. The result is a soft matching matrix P that says, in fractions, which image node each text node corresponds to; it is differentiable so it can be tuned later.\n\n*The soft node-matching P is the doubly-stochastic matrix (obtained by K fixed Sinkhorn iterations) that maximizes total node-label agreement; rows index text nodes, columns index image nodes.*\n$$ P = \\operatorname*{arg\\,max}_{P \\in \\mathcal{B}} \\; \\sum_{u,v} P[u,v]\\, c(u,v), \\qquad \\mathcal{B}=\\{P \\geq 0:\\ P\\mathbf{1}=\\mathbf{1},\\ P^{\\top}\\mathbf{1}=\\mathbf{1}\\} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A soft, balanced matching gives a differentiable, inference-only way to decide which region most likely corresponds to which word, with no training.\n\n### Pairing-free dual scene-graph construction\n*Builds an independent typed graph for each modality with no image-caption pairs, giving the wiring whose agreement carries binding.*\n\n3. Run a frozen open-vocabulary detector (Detic) on the image to find regions (keeping detections above confidence 0.3) and label each region with a word. Then add links between regions in three ways. Attributes: a small classifier reads each region's appearance and emits $attribute_{of}$ links from predicted attribute words to that region. Spatial links: from box positions — 'above' when one box's center is clearly higher than another's, 'left of' likewise sideways, 'contains' when one box mostly sits inside another. Subject/object links: a small 2-layer network reads the two regions' features plus their box geometry and predicts a directed relation $(subject_{of}, object_{of},$ or none); this network is trained only on a region-relationship dataset (Visual Genome) that is never paired with the target captions. The output is the image's own typed graph.\n   - _Why_: It builds the image's own who-does-what-to-whom graph with no image-caption pairs, so the two sides can later be compared on their wiring, not just their words.\n4. Take every node label from both the image graph and the text graph and turn it into a vector with one single frozen text encoder (for example all-MiniLM-L6-v2, or a frozen BERT averaged over its sub-word pieces); a multi-word label like 'fire hydrant' is fed as one string. Then precompute, for every text-node / image-node pair, a compatibility number equal to the cosine similarity of their two label vectors, stored as a table. The very same encoder is used for image-side and text-side labels — nothing is trained to bridge the two modalities.\n\n*Node compatibility between a text node u and an image node v is the cosine similarity of their concept-lemma labels $\\ell _{u}, \\ell _{v}$ embedded by one frozen uni-modal text encoder E — the only place vocabulary enters and the bridge that lets a region 'dog' and a word 'dog' agree.*\n$$ c(u,v) = \\cos\\!\\big(E(\\ell_u),\\, E(\\ell_v)\\big) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Putting image-region words and caption words into the same word space is what lets a region labelled 'dog' agree with the word 'dog' without needing any paired training data.\n\n### Relational-agreement score with binding certificate\n*The relation-typed edge-consistency term and the by-construction proof that binding enters the score only at the relational locus.*\n\n5. Compute the relation-agreement quantity. For each directed link (u,u',r) in the text graph, sum, over every pair of image regions (v,v'), the product $P[u,v]\\cdot P[u',v']$ weighted by g — a number between 0 and 1 saying whether the image graph carries the same relation r in the same direction between those two regions. For the learned subject/object relations, g is the predictor's probability for that relation and direction (so it is smooth); for the geometry-based relations (spatial, attribute) g is simply 1 or 0. Summing all these gives the total edge-agreement.\n   - _Why_: This is the new ingredient: it rewards the match only when the IMAGE wires the concepts the same way the caption does, so swapping subject and object changes the score.\n6. Form the final score as the node-agreement term plus lambda times the edge-agreement term. There is a guarantee provable on paper: take a caption and a copy of it with exactly one relation reversed (turning 'man bites dog' into 'dog bites man') while keeping the identical set of words; the lambda=0 version of the score does not change at all, but the full score provably DOES change whenever the image actually carries that asymmetric relation. This works because the node-counting part is blind to which node is subject and which is object, while the edge part reads DIRECTED links whose match score is not symmetric. The needed direction-sensitivity is built in: the subject/object predictor is a directed 3-way classifier $(subject_{of}, object_{of},$ none), and the geometry relations are directional by definition (above is not below).\n\n*The matching score adds to the node-presence term a relation-typed edge-consistency term: for each directed text edge (u,u',r), it rewards matched image regions v,v' that carry the same relation type r (indicator g), weighted by the scalar $\\lambda .$ The edge term is what flips when $subject_{of}$ and $object_{of}$ are swapped.*\n$$ S(I,T) = \\underbrace{\\sum_{u,v} P[u,v]\\, c(u,v)}_{\\text{node term}} \\;+\\; \\lambda \\underbrace{\\sum_{(u,u',r)\\in \\mathcal{E}_T} \\sum_{v,v'} P[u,v]\\,P[u',v']\\, g(v,v',r)}_{\\text{edge-consistency term}} \\tag{3} $$\n\n\n*Binding-sensitivity certificate: for texts T, T' with identical node-label multisets differing only by one reversed relation edge, the relation-off reduction $S0 (\\lambda =0)$ is invariant for every image, while the full score S provably differs whenever the image graph carries the corresponding asymmetric relation — so binding enters S only through the relational locus.*\n$$ S_0(I,T)=S_0(I,T') \\;\\; \\forall I, \\qquad\\text{yet}\\qquad S(I,T)\\neq S(I,T') \\;\\text{ for } \\lambda>0 \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The guarantee proves on paper — not just in experiments — that binding information enters the score only through the connection term, and that the old concept-counting score is blind to it.\n\n### Unpaired selection and deployment\n*Selects the relational weight and applies the score for retrieval, all without paired supervision.*\n\n7. Pick the relational weight lambda on a held-out set of images and texts that come from the same domain but are NOT paired. For each image, take its 50 best candidate texts by the node-only score; then perturb each graph five times by randomly removing 10% of its links and re-score. Measure how stable the ranking of those 50 candidates stays under perturbation, using the Kendall-tau rank correlation (a standard measure of how much two orderings agree), averaged over all queries. Try lambda values {0, 0.1, 0.25, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0} and keep the one that keeps rankings most stable; if all are about equal, default to 0.5. No correct image-caption pairs are ever used.\n   - _Why_: Even tuning is done without any correct image-caption pairs, so the method stays fully unpaired from end to end.\n8. Use the score S to rank candidates for retrieval, reporting Recall at 1, 5 and 10. Or add S on top of an existing matcher's score as a re-ranker: first put both scores on the same scale by z-score-normalizing each over the candidate set for a query, then combine as base $+ beta\\cdot S,$ choosing beta on the unpaired development set the same self-consistency way (default beta=1). For the binding probe, accuracy is simply the fraction of test triples (a caption, its matching image, a mismatching image) where the score prefers the matching image.\n   - _Why_: Because the connection term raises the score only for candidates whose wiring agrees, flipping subject and object in the query changes which item comes out on top — exactly the behaviour the old methods lack.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 关系一致性匹配：以构造方式而非概念库实现无配对图文匹配\n\n**方法名称.** Relational-Agreement Matching (RAM)\n\n## 研究动机\n假设你想要一个系统，能把图片和说明文字配对起来，但在训练时它从未见过任何一张图片与其正确说明文字成对出现。这就是所谓的无配对图文匹配，目前的代表方法是 MACK（Multimodal Aligned Conceptual Knowledge，多模态对齐概念知识）。MACK 的做法是先从另一个带区域标注的图像数据集里，建一本'字典'，记录'dog 这个词通常长什么样的区域'。要给一张图和一句说明文字打分时，它逐个把文字里的词与图像区域对照，再把这些匹配加起来。问题很微妙却致命：因为它对每个词独立打分再求和，它根本无法区分 'a man bites a dog' 和 'a dog bites a man'。两句话包含完全相同的词——man、bites、dog——所以求和后的分数一样，尽管含义恰恰相反。同样的盲点也出现在属性上：'a red car and a blue truck' 与 'a blue car and a red truck'。这个领域较新的方法（2025 年的一个两阶段公共空间方法，以及各种无监督哈希方法）都继承了同样的缺陷，因为它们都从独立的逐概念相似度出发，从不加入任何依赖于概念如何连接的项。另一个近期方法 ABE-CLIP 确实修复了这个绑定问题，但它只能依赖 CLIP——一个在数十亿成对图文样本上训练的模型——所以在我们关心的真正无配对场景里它没有对应版本。如今之所以有可能修复，是因为三样工具最近变得足够可靠：开放词表检测器能在无任何说明文字监督下给任意图像区域贴上词标签；冻结的文本编码器能把任意词（无论来自图像侧还是文本侧）放进同一个共享空间；以及快速的 Sinkhorn 匹配，能廉价地把两组元素对齐。我们的想法是：不再对独立的逐词匹配求和，而是分别为图像和说明文字各建一张'谁对谁做了什么'的小图，再衡量这两张图有多一致——包括连接，而不只是节点。当这个缺口被填上，无配对匹配器终于能区分那些'用词相同却含义不同'的句子，而这是整条 MACK 路线结构上无法提供的能力；并且旧的 MACK 式分数恰好是我们分数在'关闭连接检查'时的特例。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景脚手架\n*贡献所依赖的现成解析与匹配组件，其本身并非创新点。*\n\n1. 对说明文字运行现成的语法依存解析器(spaCy)加语义角色标注(Semantic Role Labelling, SRL)模型，把它变成一张小图。名词、动词、属性词成为节点（取其词典原形，并去掉 the 之类的虚词）。再加入有向带标签的连接：动词指向主语为 $subject_{of}$，动词指向宾语为 $object_{of}$，形容词指向名词为 $attribute_{of}$，名词指向名词为 $spatial_{relation}$（仅限一组固定的方位词：on、in、above、below、left of、right of、inside、behind、in front of）。输出是一张由节点加类型化连接组成的图。\n   - _为什么_: 这张图记录的不只是提到了哪些概念，还有'谁对谁做了什么'——正是旧的求和方法丢掉的连接信息。\n2. 用 Sinkhorn 算法在文本节点与图像节点之间找一个软匹配。把兼容度表当作要最大化的奖励，运行 K=20 次 Sinkhorn 迭代（带一个 0.1 的小平滑温度，在数值稳定的对数域中进行），并要求每个文本节点和每个图像节点承担相等的总匹配质量。当两侧节点数不等时，加一个可选的'剩余'行与列来吸收未匹配的节点。结果是一个软匹配矩阵 P，以分数形式表示每个文本节点对应哪个图像节点；它是可微的，因此之后可以调参。\n\n*软节点匹配矩阵 P 是使节点标签总一致度最大的双随机矩阵（由 K 次固定 Sinkhorn 迭代求得）；行对应文本节点，列对应图像节点。*\n$$ P = \\operatorname*{arg\\,max}_{P \\in \\mathcal{B}} \\; \\sum_{u,v} P[u,v]\\, c(u,v), \\qquad \\mathcal{B}=\\{P \\geq 0:\\ P\\mathbf{1}=\\mathbf{1},\\ P^{\\top}\\mathbf{1}=\\mathbf{1}\\} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 软的、平衡的匹配提供了一种可微、仅在推理时运行、无需训练的方式，来判断哪个区域最可能对应哪个词。\n\n### 无配对的双场景图构建\n*在无任何图文配对的情况下为每个模态各建一张类型化的图，提供其一致性承载绑定信息的连接结构。*\n\n3. 对图像运行一个冻结的开放词表检测器(Detic)，找出区域（只保留置信度 0.3 以上的检测），并给每个区域贴一个词标签。然后用三种方式为区域之间加连接。属性：一个小分类器读取每个区域的外观，发出从预测属性词指向该区域的 $attribute_{of}$ 连接。空间连接：依据检测框位置——当一个框的中心明显高于另一个时记 'above'，横向类推记 'left of'，当一个框大部分落在另一个框内时记 'contains'。主宾连接：一个 2 层小网络读取两个区域的特征加其检测框几何，预测一个有向关系$(subject_{of}$、$object_{of}$ 或 none)；该网络只在区域-关系数据集(Visual Genome)上训练，而该数据集从不与目标说明文字配对。输出是图像自身的类型化图。\n   - _为什么_: 它在没有任何图文配对的情况下，为图像也建起'谁对谁做了什么'的图，从而两侧之后可以在连接结构上比较，而不只是比词。\n4. 把图像图和文本图中的每个节点标签，用同一个冻结的文本编码器(例如 all-MiniLM-L6-v2，或对子词取平均的冻结 BERT)转成向量；像 'fire hydrant' 这样的多词标签作为一个字符串整体输入。然后为每个 文本节点／图像节点 对预计算一个兼容度数值，等于二者标签向量的余弦相似度，存为一张表。图像侧与文本侧标签使用的是同一个编码器——没有任何东西被训练来桥接两个模态。\n\n*文本节点 u 与图像节点 v 的节点兼容度，定义为二者概念词元标签 $\\ell _{u}$、$\\ell _{v}$ 经同一个冻结的单模态文本编码器 E 嵌入后的余弦相似度——这是词表唯一进入的入口，也是让图像区域 'dog' 与单词 'dog' 相互对应的桥梁。*\n$$ c(u,v) = \\cos\\!\\big(E(\\ell_u),\\, E(\\ell_v)\\big) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 把图像区域的词和说明文字的词放进同一个词空间，正是让贴着 'dog' 标签的区域与单词 'dog' 相互对应、且无需任何配对训练数据的关键。\n\n### 带绑定证书的关系一致性分数\n*关系类型化的边一致性项，以及'绑定信息只在关系位点进入分数'的构造性证明。*\n\n5. 计算关系一致性量。对文本图中每条有向连接 (u,u',r)，在每一对图像区域 (v,v') 上求和 $P[u,v]\\cdot P[u',v']$ 乘以 g——一个 0 到 1 之间的数，表示图像图是否在那两个区域之间以相同方向携带相同关系 r。对于学习得到的主宾关系，g 取预测器对该关系及方向的概率（因而是平滑的）；对于基于几何的关系（空间、属性），g 直接取 1 或 0。把这些全部相加，得到总的边一致度。\n   - _为什么_: 这就是新增的成分：只有当图像把概念连接的方式与说明文字相同时才给奖励，因此互换主语和宾语就会改变分数。\n6. 把最终分数组成为：节点一致项 加上 lambda 乘以 边一致项。有一条可在纸面上证明的保证：取一句说明文字，再取它的一个副本——恰好把一条关系反向（把 'man bites dog' 变成 'dog bites man'），而保持完全相同的词集；分数的 lambda=0 版本完全不变，但只要图像确实携带那条非对称关系，完整分数可证必然改变。原因是：数节点的部分对'谁是主语谁是宾语'视而不见，而边的部分读取的是有向连接，其匹配得分并不对称。所需的方向敏感性是内建的：主宾预测器是一个有向三分类器$(subject_{of}$、$object_{of}$、none)，而几何关系按定义就是有向的(above 不等于 below)。\n\n*匹配分数在节点存在项之外，再加上一个关系类型化的边一致性项：对每条有向文本边 (u,u',r)，若所匹配的图像区域 v,v' 携带相同关系类型 r（指示函数 g），则给予奖励，并由标量 $\\lambda $ 加权。当 $subject_{of}$ 与 $object_{of}$ 互换时，发生变化的正是这一边项。*\n$$ S(I,T) = \\underbrace{\\sum_{u,v} P[u,v]\\, c(u,v)}_{\\text{node term}} \\;+\\; \\lambda \\underbrace{\\sum_{(u,u',r)\\in \\mathcal{E}_T} \\sum_{v,v'} P[u,v]\\,P[u',v']\\, g(v,v',r)}_{\\text{edge-consistency term}} \\tag{3} $$\n\n\n*绑定敏感性证书：对节点标签多重集完全相同、仅有一条关系边方向被反转的文本 T、T'，关系关闭时的退化分数 S0（$\\lambda =0$）对任意图像都保持不变；而只要图像图携带相应的非对称关系，完整分数 S 必然不同——因此绑定信息只能经由关系位点进入 S。*\n$$ S_0(I,T)=S_0(I,T') \\;\\; \\forall I, \\qquad\\text{yet}\\qquad S(I,T)\\neq S(I,T') \\;\\text{ for } \\lambda>0 \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这条保证在纸面上——而不仅在实验里——证明了绑定信息只能经由连接项进入分数，而旧的'数概念'分数对它视而不见。\n\n### 无配对的选择与部署\n*选取关系权重并把分数用于检索，全程不依赖配对监督。*\n\n7. 在一批同领域但未配对的图像与文本上挑选关系权重 lambda。对每张图像，取其按仅节点分数排名最高的 50 条候选文本；然后把每张图扰动五次（每次随机删去 10% 的连接）并重新打分。衡量这 50 条候选的排名在扰动下有多稳定，采用 Kendall-tau 秩相关(一种衡量两个排序一致程度的标准指标)，在所有查询上取平均。尝试 lambda 取值 {0, 0.1, 0.25, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0}，保留使排名最稳定的那个；若各值大致相当，默认取 0.5。全程不使用任何正确的图文配对。\n   - _为什么_: 连调参都不用任何正确的图文配对，因此方法从头到尾保持完全无配对。\n8. 用分数 S 对候选项排序做检索，报告 Recall@1、5、10。或者把 S 叠加在已有匹配器分数之上作为重排器：先把两个分数放到同一尺度——对每个查询的候选集各做 z-score 标准化，然后按 base $+ beta\\cdot S$ 组合，并在未配对的开发集上用同样的自一致性方式选 beta（默认 beta=1）。对于绑定探针，准确率就是测试三元组（一句说明文字、与其匹配的图像、不匹配的图像）中分数更偏好匹配图像的比例。\n   - _为什么_: 由于连接项只为'连接方式一致'的候选项提高分数，在查询里互换主宾就会改变排在最前的项——这正是旧方法所缺乏的行为。\n\n"},{"id":"82","run_dir":"run_prompt82_mpnash","index":82,"title":"Heterogeneous Nash Preference Optimization: Equilibria for Conflicting-Oracle Populations","title_zh":"异质 Nash 偏好优化：面向冲突预言机群体的均衡解","method_name":"Heterogeneous Nash Preference Optimization (HNPO)","hook":"Multiplayer Nash alignment motivates itself with a population of conflicting annotators yet provably collapses to a single shared oracle and one identical policy across all players. We show the homogeneity assumption is load-bearing, pivot to per-player oracles, and prove a Nash equilibrium PROFILE of distinct policies exists and is the right alignment target when no single policy can win against everyone.","anchor_pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","anchor_pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","domain_category":"LLM Alignment, Safety & Behavior","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions the assumption — silently inherited by every Nash-alignment node from the shared two-player ancestor — that the preference game is defined by a SINGLE preference oracle; none tests whether the oracle that defines the game must be one object at all rather than a structured collection of distinct preference relations.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C29 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by auditing the convergence/equilibrium guarantee of multiplayer NLHF and pivoting its load-bearing target-criterion assumption: MNPO's symmetric equilibrium exists BECAUSE the n players share one oracle; we replace that single-shared-oracle convergence primitive with a per-player-oracle one and re-derive what fixed point survives, showing the symmetric-optimum target is the exact thing foreclosing heterogeneous alignment.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf gives a guarantee or operational target for what 'good alignment' even means when no single policy can hold a 50% win-rate against all sub-populations at once — the equilibrium-existence / solution-concept question for the heterogeneous-oracle preference game is unaddressed (current results all assume a fixed point that simultaneously satisfies every player's relation exists).","pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","sub_pattern":"C27 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by recasting heterogeneous-population alignment as a deliberately constructed multi-party game in which each player best-responds under its OWN preference oracle, and proving a Nash equilibrium PROFILE of (generally distinct) policies exists and equals the desired alignment target — the equilibrium-existence proof + the regret-minimization solver that reaches it is the missing artifact.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"game-theoretic LLM alignment / Nash learning from human feedback (preference optimization)","n_papers":53,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":27},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10},{"source":"openreview","n":2}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":14,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Self-Play Preference Optimization for Language Model Alignment"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Magnetic Preference Optimization: Achieving Last-iterate Convergence for Language Models Alignment"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Unified Preference Optimization: Language Model Alignment Beyond the Preference Frontier"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Cal-DPO: Calibrated Direct Preference Optimization for Language Model Alignment"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Self-Augmented Preference Optimization: Off-Policy Paradigms for Language Model Alignment"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Accelerated Preference Optimization for Large Language Model Alignment"}],"more":8},{"year":2025,"n":26,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Multiplayer Nash Preference Optimization"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Distortion of AI Alignment: Does Preference Optimization Optimize for Preferences?"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Indirect Online Preference Optimization via Reinforcement Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"SGDPO: Self-Guided Direct Preference Optimization for Language Model Alignment"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"AMaPO: Adaptive Margin-attached Preference Optimization for Language Model Alignment"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Engaging Preference Optimization Alignment in Large Language Model for Continual Radiology Report Generation: A Hybrid Approach"}],"more":20},{"year":2026,"n":12,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"},{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Frictive Policy Optimization for LLMs: Epistemic Intervention, Risk-Sensitive Control, and Reflective Alignment"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Fully Automated Identification of Lexical Alignment and Preference-Stage Shifts in Large Language Models"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Towards General Preference Alignment: Diffusion Models at Nash Equilibrium"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"StoicLLM: Preference Optimization for Philosophical Alignment in Small Language Models"}],"more":6}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":10,"share":0.189},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":8,"share":0.151},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":7,"share":0.132},{"pattern_id":"algebraic_equivalence_unification","pattern_name":"Prove Equivalence to Unify","count":5,"share":0.094},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":5,"share":0.094},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":4,"share":0.075},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":4,"share":0.075},{"pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","count":2,"share":0.038}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Game-theoretic alignment recasts preference optimization as finding a Nash equilibrium of a preference game, escaping the Bradley-Terry transitivity assumption (semanticscholar:df8c3a325419d63366b9b347739fcbf3e2c4d22c, openalex:W4404343233). To move beyond a single opponent, MNPO (semanticscholar:f55bf9a4262ca00b72345ee95b0b1ad65b907e95) extends to n players, but its method assumes a HOMOGENEOUS multiplayer setting in which all n players share one universal preference oracle and are treated symmetrically, so the proven equilibrium satisfies pi_1* = ... = pi_n* — every player converges to the same policy. The motivation for going multiplayer (a mixture of annotators, heterogeneous evaluation criteria, multiple conflicting reward models) is therefore not actually inhabited by the solution: when the preference signal genuinely differs across the players who generate it, the single-shared-oracle objective (Eq. 7 of MNPO) is no longer well-defined as one scalar payoff, and the symmetric self-play dynamics have no fixed point that simultaneously satisfies the distinct, possibly intransitive cross-player preference relations. The same homogeneity is inherited by the two-player convergence results (semanticscholar:01c12d59d9e3e7282514bdc75ba4f9d9b3e9fd57, arxiv:2606.01382v1) and is precisely the failure that pluralistic-alignment diagnostics flag (semanticscholar:68d3f73f48805bdcef68d45cf4401dea6bac7f42): once different sub-populations evaluate by different criteria, no single equilibrium policy can hold a 50% win-rate against all of them at once, and current machinery produces either a majority-dominated policy or oscillation.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:f55bf9a4262ca00b72345ee95b0b1ad65b907e95","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"MNPO reframes alignment as an n-player preference game with a Plackett-Luce listwise objective and concurrent symmetric policy updates toward a competitive equilibrium. Its method section explicitly restricts the theory to the HOMOGENEOUS case where all players share one universal preference oracle and the symmetric equilibrium forces pi_1*=...=pi_n*, so the heterogeneous-oracle population that motivates 'multiplayer' (different annotators / reward models with conflicting, possibly intransitive cross-player preferences) is named as motivation but never instantiated: there is no objective, equilibrium concept, or convergence result for players answering to DIFFERENT preference oracles."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:df8c3a325419d63366b9b347739fcbf3e2c4d22c","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"SPPO casts alignment as a two-player constant-sum game and iterates each policy toward the Nash equilibrium against a single opponent population. It assumes one preference oracle and a single equilibrium policy, so it cannot represent a population whose members evaluate by genuinely different criteria, nor give any cross-player exploitability guarantee under such heterogeneity."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:68d3f73f48805bdcef68d45cf4401dea6bac7f42","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"The Distortion paper diagnoses, via social choice theory, that aligning to a single preference model can incur unbounded worst-case average-utility loss under diverse users, and bounds this distortion. It is a measurement/impossibility result over scalar BT sub-models and gives no game-theoretic optimizer that constructs a policy (or policy profile) achieving low distortion under heterogeneous preferences."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2606.01382v1","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Efficient Exploration for Iterative NLHF provides the first online-learning regret guarantees for scalable NLHF via optimism/exploration bonuses. Its regret theory is for a single fixed two-player preference game with one preference oracle; it offers no notion of regret or equilibrium when the game is defined by multiple heterogeneous oracles whose Nash solution is a profile of distinct policies rather than one policy."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"game-theoretic LLM alignment / Nash learning from human feedback (preference optimization)","venue":"ICLR / NeurIPS / ICML (top-tier ML)","time":"2026 cycle","data":["pairwise/listwise human preference datasets (e.g. UltraFeedback, HH-RLHF)","multi-annotator or multi-reward-model preference signals","AlpacaEval / Arena-Hard style win-rate eval"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher comfortable with RLHF/DPO training and game-theoretic optimization","preference":"both","baseline":"Multiplayer Nash Preference Optimization (MNPO), Self-Play Preference Optimization (SPPO), and two-player NLHF variants (Online IPO, COMAL, Magnetic PO)","limitation":"current Nash-based preference optimizers either reduce to a two-player game or (in MNPO) to a SYMMETRIC self-play population sharing one universal preference oracle, so a genuinely heterogeneous population of annotators/reward-models with conflicting preferences collapses to a single shared objective and a single equilibrium policy","contribution_type":"theory","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object both legs read from and write to is the HETEROGENEOUS preference game G = (x, {pi_i}_{i=1..n}, {P_i}_{i=1..n}, pi_ref, tau), where each player i owns its OWN general preference oracle P_i: X x Y x Y -> [0,1] (P_i(y > y' | x) is the probability that oracle i prefers y to y'). Each P_i is a computable object: in practice it is a distinct learned/elicited preference model for sub-population i (e.g. one reward/judge model per annotator cluster, per evaluation criterion, or per historical checkpoint), queried as a forward pass returning a scalar in [0,1]; the oracle index set {1..n} and its assignment to data are given by the user's annotator/criterion partition (a fixed input), and a mixing weight vector w in the simplex (w_i >= 0, sum w_i = 1, default uniform w_i = 1/n) encodes how much population mass each oracle carries. Leg 1 (audit/pivot, C29): we take the MNPO/NLHF equilibrium guarantee, whose convergence TARGET is the symmetric fixed point pi_1*=...=pi_n* that exists only because all players share one P; we show this shared-oracle assumption is load-bearing (the symmetry argument that forces a single optimum consumes P_i = P for all i exactly once in the proof), then pivot the convergence primitive from 'the exact symmetric optimum under one oracle' to 'a fixed-point PROFILE (pi_1*,...,pi_n*) under distinct {P_i}', and re-derive the per-iteration progress bound for the asymmetric dynamics. The artifact is a theorem: under each P_i bounded in [0,1] and the per-player KL(pi_i || pi_ref) regularizer with tau>0, the regularized heterogeneous game admits a Nash equilibrium profile, because each player's regularized payoff J_i(pi_i, {pi_j}_{j!=i}) = E_x[ E_{y~pi_i, {y_j ~ pi_j}}[ P_i(y > {y_j} | x) ] - tau KL(pi_i || pi_ref) ] is concave in pi_i (the KL term is strictly convex, the preference term linear in pi_i's occupancy measure) over a convex compact policy simplex, so Debreu-Glicksberg-Fan applies — closing gap 1 by proving the oracle need NOT be one object for an equilibrium to exist. Leg 2 (reframe-as-game, C27) reads the SAME object: it defines the alignment target as this equilibrium profile plus a population-aggregated deployment policy pi_bar = sum_i w_i pi_i*, and supplies the solver — a no-regret best-response / optimistic-mirror-descent dynamics in which player i updates against the current opponents using ONLY P_i — together with the operational target that replaces the unattainable single-policy 50%-win-rate guarantee: the per-oracle exploitability gap e_i = max_{pi'} J_i(pi', {pi_j*}_{j!=i}) - J_i(pi_i*, {pi_j*}_{j!=i}), whose max_i e_i -> 0 at the equilibrium is the achievable certificate (gap 3's missing 'what good alignment means'). Where prior work assumes one fixed point satisfying every relation, we instead certify a profile in which no player can improve against the others under its own oracle, and bound the worst-case per-oracle exploitability of the deployed pi_bar. The two legs need the same machinery, not separate modules: the audit's pivoted target-criterion (a profile, not a symmetric optimum) IS the solution concept the reframe constructs and proves existence for — one theorem, read once as 'the assumption is removable' and once as 'here is the object that remains'.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery because the audit's deliverable (the pivoted convergence target = a profile under distinct oracles) is literally the same mathematical object the reframe must prove exists; splitting them into separate modules would duplicate the equilibrium-existence argument, so one concavity-based existence theorem serves both, with leg 2 adding only the solver and the exploitability certificate. (b) Alternatives considered: (i) a worst-group / DRO single policy max_pi min_i J_i — rejected because it lands on collateral node c2 (group-robust RLHF), yields one conservative policy not an equilibrium profile, and gives no per-oracle exploitability control; (ii) scalarizing the oracles into one averaged oracle P_bar = sum_i w_i P_i — rejected because that is exactly MNPO's single-shared-oracle case (regression to node n6) and re-collapses the players to identical policies, defeating the heterogeneity claim; (iii) characterize_limit_then_surpass via a WL-style separation — rejected because its machinery targets relational/combinatorial message-passing, not game equilibria, so it would be a forced recipe.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: build a preference set with two genuinely conflicting sub-populations (e.g. a verbosity-preferring vs a concision-preferring annotator cluster on UltraFeedback prompts), train (i) MNPO with one shared oracle and (ii) our heterogeneous-oracle equilibrium profile + aggregated pi_bar on the same base model (Llama-3-8B class), same compute. If the candidate works, the WORST-SUB-POPULATION win-rate of the deployed model against the reference (min over the n oracle-specific win-rates) INCREASES for our pi_bar relative to MNPO's single policy, while MNPO's single policy shows a large win-rate GAP between the two oracles (it satisfies the majority oracle and loses on the minority). The load-bearing variable is the per-oracle exploitability gap max_i e_i (each e_i computed by a fresh best-response against the frozen profile under oracle P_i): our dynamics should drive max_i e_i toward zero, whereas MNPO's single policy retains a large e_i on the dissenting oracle. Negative control (non-tautological): replace the n distinct oracles with n copies of the SAME averaged oracle P_bar = sum_i w_i P_i (collapsing heterogeneity) and re-run the identical solver — the predicted effect is on the DOWNSTREAM task-outcome metric, the worst-sub-population win-rate, which must fall back to MNPO's single-policy level (the profile re-collapses to identical policies and the minority-oracle win-rate regresses), confirming the gain comes from oracle heterogeneity in the game definition and not from extra players, more updates, or the aggregation step. Positive control: a stripped two-oracle, two-player instance that runs only the per-oracle best-response (no other machinery) should already recover most of the worst-sub-population win-rate improvement.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:f55bf9a4262ca00b72345ee95b0b1ad65b907e95","delta":"MNPO proves a symmetric multiplayer equilibrium pi_1*=...=pi_n* under one universal Plackett-Luce oracle (homogeneous case, its Eq. 7); we prove existence of a Nash equilibrium PROFILE of generally distinct policies when each player owns a different oracle P_i, a regime its symmetry argument structurally excludes, and supply the worst-oracle exploitability certificate it does not define."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:df8c3a325419d63366b9b347739fcbf3e2c4d22c","delta":"SPPO solves a two-player constant-sum game with a single oracle and one equilibrium policy; we generalize the game-definition itself to a collection of distinct oracles and replace 'one policy with 50% win-rate vs all' with an achievable per-oracle-exploitability target."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:68d3f73f48805bdcef68d45cf4401dea6bac7f42","delta":"The Distortion paper proves an impossibility/lower-bound on average utility for single-preference-model alignment under diverse users but constructs no optimizer; we give a constructive game whose equilibrium profile + aggregation achieves a controllable worst-sub-population exploitability bound, turning their negative result into a positive solution concept."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2606.01382v1","delta":"Efficient-Exploration NLHF derives online regret for a single fixed two-player oracle game; we define regret/exploitability per-oracle over a multi-oracle game and prove equilibrium existence for that profile, a setting where their single-game regret notion is undefined."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:f55bf9a4262ca00b72345ee95b0b1ad65b907e95","what_step_was_missed":"MNPO constructed the n-player objective and proved equilibrium existence ONLY for the homogeneous case where all players share one universal oracle (the symmetric structure 'underpins our theoretical guarantees', forcing pi_1*=...=pi_n*); to already contain our contribution it would have needed to (a) restate each player's regularized payoff against its OWN oracle P_i, (b) prove the per-player concavity that licenses a Debreu-Glicksberg-Fan existence argument for an ASYMMETRIC equilibrium profile, and (c) define a per-oracle exploitability certificate as the alignment target — none of which its symmetric, single-oracle derivation produces."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":278,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"No hard-floor rule fires: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict is borderline (no Reject lesson marked candidate_match: yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat is no_threat_found with no exact-mechanism overlap. recipe_application_check.verdict = applied for both legs, so the idea is built from the C29 'pivot-the-convergence-target' and C27 'prove equilibrium=target + solver' tactics rather than the parents' generic gists, removing the leading cause of revise. The remaining borderline findings — gap_closure_reject_check.entries[0].reject_lessons_evaluated[5].lesson_quoted ('validated only on a single toy instance') and entries[1].reject_lessons_evaluated[3].lesson_quoted ('solver never shown competitive') — hit empirical-anchor breadth, not the load-bearing core_mechanism argument (the existence theorem and exploitability certificate are precise and instantiated), so they are surfaced for Phase 4 to fold into reviewer_concerns_and_responses rather than forcing a revise loop.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions the assumption — silently inherited by every Nash-alignment node from the shared two-player ancestor — that the preference game is defined by a SINGLE preference oracle; none tests whether the oracle that defines the game must be one object at all rather than a structured collection of distinct preference relations.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C29 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The dominant failure shape is a relaxed assumption that is technically valid but uncharacterized: no named function or problem class is shown to satisfy it, and its constants are unstudied, so reviewers read it as engineered to make the proof close; a second shape is a re-derived rate that merely matches the existing baseline with near-identical algorithmic changes, landing as an incremental extension.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A weakened assumption that no known function class is shown to satisfy reads as engineered to close the proof, not as a genuine generalization — characterize when it holds or it sinks the paper.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The pivoted condition (each P_i bounded in [0,1], per-player KL(pi_i||pi_ref) with tau>0 giving concavity in the occupancy measure) is exhibited on a concrete class — learned/elicited per-annotator-cluster judge models — in core_mechanism and core_mechanism_steps step 1, so the relaxed game is not an uninstantiable abstraction."},{"lesson_quoted":"Borrowing a relaxed condition from a neighboring literature without demonstrating its concrete benefit in your own setting leaves reviewers asking what the assumption actually buys.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The per-player-oracle pivot is shown to buy something the single-oracle assumption provably cannot — a Nash equilibrium PROFILE of distinct policies plus a worst-oracle exploitability certificate max_i e_i — which is the explicit deliverable of differentiation_from_lit vs MNPO/SPPO, not an unmotivated import."},{"lesson_quoted":"Re-deriving a rate that merely matches the baseline with near-identical algorithmic changes is read as an incremental extension, however clean the analysis.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The existence argument leans on standard Debreu-Glicksberg-Fan, so the proof technique is conventional; the candidate's separation claim (the symmetric optimum cannot represent heterogeneity while the profile can) is what saves it from pure incrementality, but the strength of that separation is the load-bearing thing Phase 4 must make sharp."},{"lesson_quoted":"Hidden constants that explode at the precise parameter limit where the result is advertised as strongest silently invalidate the headline guarantee, and reviewers find them in the proof.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The headline is an existence theorem (not a rate advertised at an extreme n or tau limit), so there is no advertised parameter limit at which a hidden big-O constant could blow up; the convergence-rate lemma is secondary and bounded by the per-iteration progress decomposition."},{"lesson_quoted":"A theorem stated without formal assumptions or a precise claim is unreviewable; 'tight, assumption-free' bounds with no exhibited assumptions are treated as not-yet-a-paper.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Assumptions are exhibited explicitly (P_i bounded in [0,1], tau>0 strictly-convex KL regularizer, convex compact policy simplex, concavity of J_i in pi_i's occupancy measure), and the claim is a precise Nash-profile existence statement, not an assumption-free headline."},{"lesson_quoted":"An assumption-relaxation validated only on a single toy instance gives no evidence the relaxation captures the motivating practical regime.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The falsification experiment is a two-sub-population (verbosity vs concision) UltraFeedback/Llama-3-8B setup — defensible but narrow; the positive control is an even smaller two-oracle two-player instance, so the empirical anchor risks reading as a toy unless Phase 4 broadens to >2 genuinely conflicting oracles."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf gives a guarantee or operational target for what 'good alignment' even means when no single policy can hold a 50% win-rate against all sub-populations at once — the equilibrium-existence / solution-concept question for the heterogeneous-oracle preference game is unaddressed (current results all assume a fixed point that simultaneously satisfies every player's relation exists).","main_pattern":"reframe_as_solvable_object","sub_pattern":"C27 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is that the game is named but its central object is left informal so the reframing is never earned — a key payoff term or behavioral concept undefined, or a novel equilibrium concept introduced without proving a standard one fails or showing it runs at scale, or a structural condition claimed to buy tractability while the solver is never shown competitive.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Naming a game-theoretic behavior is not defining it — if the central concept is never formalized, reviewers cannot tell what the equilibrium selects for and pervasive confusion sinks the paper.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The central object is fully formalized: G = (x, {pi_i}, {P_i}, pi_ref, tau), per-player payoff J_i with its own P_i, and the Nash equilibrium profile + aggregate pi_bar = sum_i w_i pi_i* are written explicitly, so the equilibrium's selection target is unambiguous."},{"lesson_quoted":"Redesigning a payoff to be general-sum does not by itself yield a valid benchmark; without a precise operationalization of the property you now claim to measure, high scores fail to separate the target behavior from artifacts of the reward change.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The success property is operationalized BEFORE measurement as the per-oracle exploitability gap e_i = max_{pi'} J_i(pi',.) - J_i(pi_i*,.) and the worst-sub-population win-rate, and the negative control (n copies of averaged P_bar) isolates the heterogeneity effect from extra-players/more-updates artifacts."},{"lesson_quoted":"Introducing a new equilibrium concept demands a necessity-and-tractability argument — a novel concept that is computationally intensive and missing comparisons to existing frameworks reads as unmotivated.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate uses the STANDARD Nash-equilibrium-profile concept (not a bespoke new solution concept), so the heavy necessity-and-tractability burden does not apply; tractability is supplied via standard no-regret best-response / optimistic-mirror-descent and comparisons to MNPO/SPPO/Distortion are in differentiation_from_lit."},{"lesson_quoted":"A structural condition that 'buys' complexity independence wins nothing if the resulting solver is never shown to be competitive or to run at relevant scale, and lukewarm low-excitement reviews follow.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The solver (per-player no-regret best-response on an 8B model, 12-20 A100-day) is specified and budgeted but its competitiveness/convergence at the population scale is asserted rather than demonstrated in the candidate; Phase 4 must show the solver actually reaches the profile and is competitive, not merely runs."},{"lesson_quoted":"Extending bounds to a richer setting (noise, multiple groups) collapses when the success criterion stays undefined and the bounds are too loose to inform any real decision.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The success criterion (max_i e_i -> 0 certificate and worst-sub-population win-rate) is defined and decision-relevant — it tells a practitioner which deployed policy controls the worst-off sub-population — so the multi-group extension is anchored, not criterion-free."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No Reject lesson is marked candidate_match: yes, so the hard floor does not fire; the aggregate is borderline, driven by the C29 entry's 'validated only on a single toy instance' lesson (the two-sub-population falsification anchor is narrow) and 're-deriving a rate that merely matches the baseline' lesson (DGF-standard existence proof), plus the C27 entry's 'solver never shown competitive' lesson. All three are load-bearing-adjacent but addressable by Phase 4 expansion, not structural defects."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions the assumption — silently inherited by every Nash-alignment node from the shared two-player ancestor — that the preference game is defined by a SINGLE preference oracle; none tests whether the oracle that defines the game must be one object at all rather than a structured collection of distinct preference relations.","sub_pattern":"C29 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Take an existing convergence/regret guarantee for an iterative update procedure and pivot the single regularity-or-target assumption the proof silently rests on — e.g. replace the convergence primitive itself (exact-optimum target -> a characterized fixed point/neighborhood) — then re-prove by isolating one load-bearing per-iteration progress bound or fixed-point-preserving identity that all corollaries instantiate.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism_steps step 2-4 performs exactly this signature move: step 2 localizes the single line in MNPO's symmetric-equilibrium proof where P_i = P for all i is consumed to force pi_1*=...=pi_n* (pinning the load-bearing target-criterion assumption); step 3 pivots the convergence target from 'exact symmetric optimum under one P' to 'a Nash fixed-point PROFILE under distinct {P_i}'; step 4 re-derives via the per-player concavity / per-iteration progress lemma. This is the C29 'pivot the convergence-target primitive and re-prove' tactic, not the parent's generic 'audit an assumption.'","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf gives a guarantee or operational target for what 'good alignment' even means when no single policy can hold a 50% win-rate against all sub-populations at once — the equilibrium-existence / solution-concept question for the heterogeneous-oracle preference game is unaddressed (current results all assume a fixed point that simultaneously satisfies every player's relation exists).","sub_pattern":"C27 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Re-cast an ill-posed problem as an explicit multi-agent game — name the players, write per-agent utilities and strategy spaces, designate a solution concept whose fixed point is engineered to coincide with the target quantity, PROVE the equilibrium=target correspondence, and hand computation to mature game-solving machinery (no-regret/best-response) with a guarantee.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism Leg 2 instantiates the full C27 recipe: players = the n policies pi_i, per-agent utility J_i defined against player i's OWN oracle P_i over a convex compact policy simplex, solution concept = Nash equilibrium profile engineered so the equilibrium IS the alignment target (plus deployment pi_bar), existence PROVEN via Debreu-Glicksberg-Fan, and the solver = no-regret best-response / optimistic-mirror-descent using only P_i. This is the cluster's distinctive 'equilibrium = target + working solver' artifact, not a generic relabeling.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries perform their cluster's signature operation in core_mechanism: C29's pivot-the-convergence-target move appears verbatim in steps 2-4 (localize P_i=P consumption -> pivot to profile -> re-derive), and C27's name-players/prove-equilibrium=target/supply-solver move appears in Leg 2 (J_i with own P_i, DGF existence, no-regret solver). Neither leg collapses to the parent pattern's generic gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["assumption_audit_and_pivot","reframe_as_solvable_object"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; the candidate's composition_set is {assumption_audit_and_pivot, reframe_as_solvable_object}, which contains no heterogeneous_decomposition leg, so no anti-pattern matches (note: this pair is NOT the watch-list heterogeneous_decomposition+reframe_as_solvable_object combination either, since the audit leg is not a decomposition leg)."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"no_threat_found","threat_source":"n/a","subsumption_argument":"The strongest paper-pointed family in collision_hits and lit_table is the group-robust / MaxMin-RLHF line (SharedRep-RLHF, MaxMin-RLHF, APPA, Reward-free Alignment for Conflicting Objectives) and 'Learning generalized Nash equilibria from pairwise preferences.' None subsumes the candidate's claim: the MaxMin/group-fair family optimizes a single aggregated or worst-group policy in the SCALAR-REWARD / Bradley-Terry regime and produces one policy, whereas the candidate proves existence of a Nash equilibrium PROFILE of distinct policies under GENERAL preference oracles P_i(y>y'|x) (no scalar reward, possibly intransitive cross-player relations) plus a per-oracle exploitability certificate, which the single-policy worst-group objective cannot express. The pairwise-preference Nash paper learns ONE equilibrium under a single preference relation, not a per-player-oracle profile. Because no retrieved paper instantiates the per-oracle equilibrium-profile mechanism, no exact-mechanism subsumption holds and the candidate's central claim stands.","addressable_via":null}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Heterogeneous Nash Preference Optimization: Equilibria for Conflicting-Oracle Populations\n\n**Method.** Heterogeneous Nash Preference Optimization (HNPO)\n\n## Motivation\nModern methods that align a language model to human taste increasingly treat the problem as a game: instead of scoring each answer with one number and pushing the model to maximize it, they look for a balance point (a Nash equilibrium) of a 'preference game' between competing versions of the model. This matters because real human preferences are often contradictory and cannot be captured by a single score. The most recent step in this line, MNPO (Multiplayer Nash Preference Optimization), advertises that it handles a whole POPULATION of players — different annotators, different rubrics, different reward models. But when you read its proof, all the players are forced to consult the SAME preference judge, and the math then forces every player to end up at the identical policy. So 'multiplayer' really means many copies of the same self-play, not a genuinely diverse population.\n\nThis is the moment to fix it. Three very recent results line up: MNPO (2025) gives the multi-player game machinery but only for the shared-judge case; a 2026 paper gives online learning guarantees but only for a single two-player game; and a 2025 'distortion' result proves that aligning to one judge can be arbitrarily unfair to minority groups, yet offers no method to do better. The missing move is simple to state: let each player consult its OWN preference judge, and re-derive which balance point survives.\n\nPrior work stopped short for structural reasons. MNPO's clean single-answer result depends on every player sharing one judge — drop that and you need a different notion of solution (a PROFILE of different policies) that the paper never introduces. The two-player self-play methods (such as SPPO) have no room in their game for different per-player judges. The distortion paper only measures the problem; it builds no optimizer.\n\nWhen this gap closes, you get, for the first time, a well-defined target for alignment when no single answer can satisfy everyone: a set of distinct policies in balance, plus a single weighted deployment policy whose worst-group performance is provably controlled. That turns the distortion paper's bad-news bound into a constructive recipe, and gives MNPO the diverse-population guarantee its own motivation promised but its proof could not deliver.\n\n## Method\n### Oracle assembly\n*Turn a diverse population into a concrete collection of distinct per-group preference judges.*\n\n1. Split your preference data into n groups. If your data already tags who labeled each comparison (annotator, rubric, or model checkpoint), use those tags as the groups; if not, embed each (prompt, preferred answer, rejected answer) example with the base model's hidden state and run k-means clustering, picking the number of clusters by a standard cluster-quality score, and treat each cluster as a group. For each group train a separate pairwise judge $P_{i}$ — start from the base model, add a scoring head, and train it with ordinary binary cross-entropy so it outputs the probability that answer y beats answer y' for a prompt x, a number between 0 and 1 (or use a fixed judge language model given that group's rubric). Decide how much weight each group carries: equal weight by default, or each group's share of the data when you know it.\n   - _Why_: If the population is genuinely diverse, you need separate judges to even represent the disagreement, instead of averaging it away into one judge.\n\n### Audit and pivot\n*Prove MNPO's shared-judge assumption is load-bearing, then redefine the game with per-player judges.*\n\n2. Take MNPO's proof that every player ends up at the same policy and trace it line by line until you reach the place where it replaces each player's judge with one common judge. Show that this single substitution is what lets the proof treat all players interchangeably and conclude they share one optimal policy. Demonstrate that if the judges differ, the per-player optimality conditions are no longer identical, so the 'everyone ends up the same' conclusion stops following — proving the shared-judge assumption is doing the real work, not just simplifying notation.\n   - _Why_: You have to prove the shared-judge assumption is doing the real work before it is worth removing it; otherwise the fix looks cosmetic.\n3. Rewrite the game so each player optimizes against its own judge. Player i's score is the average probability (judged by its own $P_{i})$ that its answer beats the other players' current answers, minus a penalty $\\tau $ times how far its policy has drifted from the starting reference policy $\\pi _{ref}.$ The only change from MNPO is swapping the one shared judge for each player's own judge while keeping the same drift penalty for every player.\n\n*The heterogeneous preference game G in which each player i owns its own preference oracle $P_{i}(y >$ y' | x), in contrast to one shared oracle.*\n$$ G = \\bigl(x,\\; \\{\\pi_i\\}_{i=1}^{n},\\; \\{P_i\\}_{i=1}^{n},\\; \\pi_{\\mathrm{ref}},\\; \\tau\\bigr),\\qquad P_i:\\mathcal{X}\\times\\mathcal{Y}\\times\\mathcal{Y}\\to[0,1] \\tag{1} $$\n\n\n*Player i's regularized payoff: its own oracle's win-probability against the opponents minus $a \\tau -weighted KL$ penalty to the reference policy.*\n$$ J_i(\\pi_i, \\pi_{-i}) = \\mathbb{E}_{x}\\Bigl[\\,\\mathbb{E}_{y\\sim\\pi_i,\\;\\{y_j\\sim\\pi_j\\}_{j\\neq i}}\\!\\bigl[P_i(y \\succ \\{y_j\\}\\mid x)\\bigr]\\Bigr] - \\tau\\,\\mathrm{KL}\\!\\bigl(\\pi_i \\,\\|\\, \\pi_{\\mathrm{ref}}\\bigr) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This is the minimal change that lets genuinely conflicting preferences live in the game at the same time.\n\n### Existence theory\n*Prove a balanced profile of distinct policies exists for the conflicting-judge game.*\n\n4. Prove a balance point exists. Each player's score is concave in its own policy (the judge term is linear in how often the policy produces each answer, and the drift penalty is strictly bowl-shaped), and the set of allowed policies is convex and closed, so a classical game-theory existence theorem guarantees there is a set of policies — one per player — where no player can improve by changing only its own. Also prove a per-round progress bound showing the gap to this balance point shrinks each round, which gives a convergence rate for the training loop.\n\n*Because each payoff is concave in the player's own occupancy measure over the convex compact policy set, a Nash equilibrium profile of generally distinct policies exists.*\n$$ J_i(\\cdot,\\pi_{-i})\\ \\text{concave in}\\ \\pi_i\\ \\text{over convex compact}\\ \\Delta \\;\\Longrightarrow\\; \\exists\\,(\\pi_1^{*},\\dots,\\pi_n^{*})\\ \\text{Nash profile (Debreu-Glicksberg-Fan)} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Without an existence proof you would not know whether 'aligning to conflicting groups' is even a well-posed target; this shows it is.\n\n### Solver and certificate\n*Reach the profile by per-judge best-response and certify it with worst-judge exploitability.*\n\n5. Train the policies in rounds. In each round, freeze everyone's current policy; then for each player, sample prompts, sample one answer from that player and one answer from each frozen opponent (around 16-64 opponent samples per prompt), use that player's own judge to score who wins, and nudge that player's policy toward higher score with a standard preference-optimization update (the same kind used in DPO/IPO), keeping the drift penalty. By default all players update against the same frozen snapshot each round 【author decision: update everyone simultaneously against one frozen snapshot, or update them one at a time reusing each other's fresh updates — this changes how the loop converges.】. Repeat until the policies stop changing meaningfully (successive versions are nearly identical) or you hit a round limit.\n   - _Why_: Existence alone is not usable — this loop is the actual recipe that reaches the balance point.\n6. Check how close the result is to a true balance point, per judge. For each player, freeze everyone else, start a brand-new policy from the base model, and train it as hard as possible to win under that player's judge against the frozen others; the best score it reaches is how much a determined challenger could gain. The exploitability for that judge is that best score minus the score the trained policy already had; report the largest exploitability across all judges as the success certificate (small is good). Use a held-out prompt set so the numbers are honest.\n\n*The per-oracle exploitability of player i is the payoff a fresh best-response could gain against the frozen profile under oracle i; the alignment certificate is that the worst such gap vanishes.*\n$$ e_i = \\max_{\\pi'} J_i(\\pi', \\pi_{-i}^{*}) - J_i(\\pi_i^{*}, \\pi_{-i}^{*}),\\qquad \\text{certificate: } \\max_i e_i \\to 0 \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: When no single policy can beat everyone, 'nobody can do much better against their own judge' is the honest replacement for the impossible 'wins against all' target.\n\n### Deployment and test\n*Mix the profile into a shipping policy and check the worst-group win-rate against MNPO.*\n\n7. Combine the trained policies into one shipping model by mixing them with the group weights: with probability equal to a group's weight, generate the answer from that group's policy. Alternatively, if you know at inference time which sub-population a query comes from, just route it to that group's policy. Either way you deploy a single model that carries the worst-group guarantee from the balanced set.\n\n*The deployed single policy is the population-weighted mixture of the equilibrium profile, with w the population-mass weights (default uniform).*\n$$ \\bar{\\pi} = \\sum_{i=1}^{n} w_i\\,\\pi_i^{*},\\qquad w\\in\\Delta_{n-1},\\ w_i\\ge 0,\\ \\textstyle\\sum_i w_i = 1 \\tag{5} $$\n\n   - _Why_: You usually deploy one model, and the weighted mixture inherits the worst-group guarantee from the balanced set.\n8. On fresh held-out data, measure each group's win-rate: the fraction of prompts where that group's judge prefers the shipping model's answer over the reference model's answer (the same comparison MNPO is scored against). Do this for both our shipping model and an MNPO single-judge model trained with the same base model and compute. Report every group's win-rate and, crucially, the worst group's win-rate for each method side by side — that worst-group number is the headline comparison.\n   - _Why_: The whole claim is that the diverse-judge model helps the worst-off group, so the worst-group win-rate is exactly the number that must move up.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 异质 Nash 偏好优化：面向冲突预言机群体的均衡解\n\n**方法名称.** Heterogeneous Nash Preference Optimization (HNPO)\n\n## 研究动机\n如今让语言模型对齐人类偏好的方法，越来越多地把问题看成一场博弈：不再用一个分数给每个回答打分并让模型去最大化它，而是去寻找模型不同版本之间「偏好博弈」的平衡点（即 Nash 均衡）。这很重要，因为真实的人类偏好常常彼此矛盾，无法用单一分数刻画。这条线上最新的一步 MNPO (Multiplayer Nash Preference Optimization) 宣称能处理一整个由不同标注者、不同评测标准、不同奖励模型构成的玩家群体。但细看其证明会发现：所有玩家都被迫查询同一个偏好裁判，于是数学上每个玩家最终都收敛到完全相同的策略。所以这里的「多玩家」其实只是同一个自博弈的多份拷贝，而非真正多样的群体。\n\n现在正是解决它的时机。三项很新的结果恰好凑齐：MNPO (2025) 给出了多玩家博弈的机制，但只覆盖共享裁判的情形；一篇 2026 年的工作给出了在线学习保证，但只针对单一的两玩家博弈；而一篇 2025 年的「distortion」结果证明了对齐到单一裁判会对少数群体造成任意大的不公，却没有给出更好的方法。缺的那一步说起来很简单：让每个玩家查询各自的偏好裁判，再重新推导哪个平衡点能够存活。\n\n以往工作因结构性原因止步于此。MNPO 那个干净的「单一答案」结论依赖于所有玩家共享一个裁判——一旦去掉这个前提，就需要一种它从未引入的新解概念（一个由不同策略组成的策略组合 profile）。两玩家自博弈方法（如 SPPO）的博弈结构里根本没有容纳各玩家不同裁判的位置。distortion 论文只度量了问题，并未构造出任何优化器。\n\n当这个缺口被填上时，我们第一次拥有了「没有任何单一答案能让所有人满意」时的明确对齐目标：一组处于平衡的不同策略，外加一个加权的单一部署策略，其最差群体表现可被证明地受控。这把 distortion 论文的坏消息式下界变成了一份可构造的配方，也给了 MNPO 它自己的动机所承诺、但其证明无法兑现的多样群体保证。\n\n## 方法\n### 预言机组装\n*把多样群体落实为一组具体的、各分组各自的偏好裁判。*\n\n1. 把你的偏好数据拆成 n 个分组。如果数据里已经标了每条比较是谁标注的（标注者、评测标准 rubric、或模型 checkpoint），就直接用这些标签作为分组；如果没有，就用 base model 的隐藏状态把每个（提示、被选答案、被拒答案）样本嵌入，再做 k-means 聚类，用标准的聚类质量评分(silhouette score)来选聚类数，把每个聚类当作一个分组。为每个分组训练一个单独的成对裁判 $P_{i}——$从 base model 出发，加一个打分头(scoring head)，用普通的二元交叉熵(binary cross-entropy)训练，使它输出在提示 x 下答案 y 胜过答案 y' 的概率，即一个 0 到 1 之间的数（或者用一个固定的裁判语言模型，给它该分组的 rubric）。再决定每个分组占多大权重：默认等权重，或在已知时按各分组占数据的比例。\n   - _为什么_: 如果群体真的多样，你需要分开的裁判才能把分歧表示出来，而不是把它平均成一个裁判抹掉。\n\n### 审计与转向\n*证明 MNPO 的共享裁判假设是承重的，再用各玩家各自的裁判重新定义博弈。*\n\n2. 拿 MNPO 中「每个玩家最终都收敛到同一策略」的证明，逐行追踪，直到找到它把每个玩家的裁判替换成同一个公共裁判的那一处。说明正是这一次替换让证明可以把所有玩家等同对待、从而得出他们共享同一个最优策略。再证明：如果裁判各不相同，各玩家的最优性条件就不再相同，于是「大家最终都一样」的结论不再成立——由此证明共享裁判这个假设是在起实质作用，而不只是简化记号。\n   - _为什么_: 你得先证明「共享裁判」这个假设真的在起决定作用，才值得去掉它，否则这个修改看起来只是表面功夫。\n3. 把博弈改写成每个玩家针对自己的裁判做优化。玩家 i 的得分是：用它自己的裁判 $P_{i}$ 衡量、它的答案胜过其他玩家当前答案的平均概率，再减去一个惩罚项 $\\tau $ 乘以它的策略偏离初始参考策略 $\\pi _{ref}$ 的程度。相对 MNPO 唯一的改动，就是把那一个共享裁判换成每个玩家各自的裁判，同时对每个玩家保留同样的偏离惩罚。\n\n*异质偏好博弈 G，其中每个玩家 i 拥有各自的偏好预言机 $P_{i}(y >$ y' | x)，区别于单一共享预言机。*\n$$ G = \\bigl(x,\\; \\{\\pi_i\\}_{i=1}^{n},\\; \\{P_i\\}_{i=1}^{n},\\; \\pi_{\\mathrm{ref}},\\; \\tau\\bigr),\\qquad P_i:\\mathcal{X}\\times\\mathcal{Y}\\times\\mathcal{Y}\\to[0,1] \\tag{1} $$\n\n\n*玩家 i 的正则化收益：用其自身预言机衡量的对手胜率，减去对参考策略 $\\pi _{ref}$ 的 $\\tau $ 加权 KL 惩罚。*\n$$ J_i(\\pi_i, \\pi_{-i}) = \\mathbb{E}_{x}\\Bigl[\\,\\mathbb{E}_{y\\sim\\pi_i,\\;\\{y_j\\sim\\pi_j\\}_{j\\neq i}}\\!\\bigl[P_i(y \\succ \\{y_j\\}\\mid x)\\bigr]\\Bigr] - \\tau\\,\\mathrm{KL}\\!\\bigl(\\pi_i \\,\\|\\, \\pi_{\\mathrm{ref}}\\bigr) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这是能让真正冲突的偏好同时存在于博弈中的最小改动。\n\n### 存在性理论\n*为冲突裁判博弈证明存在一个由不同策略组成的平衡组合。*\n\n4. 证明平衡点存在。每个玩家的得分对它自己的策略是凹的（裁判项关于「策略产生各答案的频率」是线性的，偏离惩罚则是严格碗形的），而允许的策略集合是凸且闭的，于是一个经典的博弈论存在性定理保证：存在一组策略（每个玩家一个），使得任何玩家单独改变自己的策略都无法变得更好。再证明一个逐轮的进展界，说明到这个平衡点的间隙每轮都在缩小，从而给出训练循环的收敛速率。\n\n*由于每个收益在玩家自身占用测度上对凸紧策略集是凹的，因此存在一个（通常各不相同的）Nash 均衡策略组合。*\n$$ J_i(\\cdot,\\pi_{-i})\\ \\text{concave in}\\ \\pi_i\\ \\text{over convex compact}\\ \\Delta \\;\\Longrightarrow\\; \\exists\\,(\\pi_1^{*},\\dots,\\pi_n^{*})\\ \\text{Nash profile (Debreu-Glicksberg-Fan)} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 没有存在性证明，你甚至不知道「对齐冲突群体」是不是一个良定义的目标；这一步说明它是。\n\n### 求解器与证书\n*用逐裁判最优响应抵达该组合，并用最差裁判可利用度为其出具证书。*\n\n5. 分轮训练这些策略。每一轮，先冻结所有人当前的策略；然后对每个玩家，采样一批提示，从该玩家采样一个答案、从每个被冻结的对手各采样一个答案（每个提示约 16-64 个对手样本），用该玩家自己的裁判判定谁胜，再用标准的偏好优化(preference optimization)更新（与 DPO/IPO 同类）把该玩家的策略往更高得分推，同时保留偏离惩罚。默认所有玩家在每轮里针对同一个冻结快照更新【作者需决定：是让所有玩家针对同一个冻结快照同时更新，还是逐个更新并复用彼此的最新更新——这会改变循环的收敛方式。】。重复直到策略不再有意义地变化（前后版本几乎相同）或达到轮数上限。\n   - _为什么_: 只有存在性还用不上——这个循环才是真正抵达平衡点的配方。\n6. 逐裁判检查结果离真正的平衡点有多近。对每个玩家，冻结其余所有人，从 base model 起一个全新的策略，尽全力训练它在该玩家裁判下战胜被冻结的其他人；它能达到的最好得分，就是一个执着的挑战者能榨出多少。该裁判下的可利用度(exploitability)，就是这个最好得分减去已训练策略原本的得分；报告所有裁判中最大的可利用度作为成功证书（越小越好）。用留出的提示集来算，结果才诚实。\n\n*玩家 i 的逐预言机可利用度，是在预言机 i 下针对冻结策略组合训练新最优响应所能获得的收益增量；对齐证书即最差的该间隙趋于零。*\n$$ e_i = \\max_{\\pi'} J_i(\\pi', \\pi_{-i}^{*}) - J_i(\\pi_i^{*}, \\pi_{-i}^{*}),\\qquad \\text{certificate: } \\max_i e_i \\to 0 \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 当没有任何单一策略能击败所有人时，「谁都无法在自己裁判下显著做得更好」就是对那个不可能达成的「对所有人都赢」目标的诚实替代。\n\n### 部署与测试\n*把策略组合混合成上线策略，并对比 MNPO 检验最差群体胜率。*\n\n7. 把训练好的各策略按分组权重混合成一个上线模型：以等于某分组权重的概率，用该分组的策略来生成答案。或者，如果你在推理时知道某个查询来自哪个子群体，就直接把它路由到该分组的策略。无论哪种方式，你部署的都是一个单一模型，它从平衡的策略组合那里继承了最差群体的保证。\n\n*部署的单一策略是均衡策略组合按群体权重 w 的混合（默认均匀权重），$w_{i}$ 表示各子群体所占的质量。*\n$$ \\bar{\\pi} = \\sum_{i=1}^{n} w_i\\,\\pi_i^{*},\\qquad w\\in\\Delta_{n-1},\\ w_i\\ge 0,\\ \\textstyle\\sum_i w_i = 1 \\tag{5} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 你通常只部署一个模型，而加权混合会从这个平衡的策略组合继承最差群体的保证。\n8. 在全新的留出数据上，测量每个分组的胜率：该分组的裁判认为上线模型的答案优于参考模型答案的提示占比（与 MNPO 被打分时所用的比较一致）。对我们的上线模型和一个用相同 base model 与相同算力训练的 MNPO 单裁判模型都这样做。把每个分组的胜率、尤其是每种方法最差那个分组的胜率并排报告——那个最差群体的数字就是核心对比。\n   - _为什么_: 整个主张就是多裁判模型能帮到处境最差的群体，所以最差群体胜率正是那个必须往上走的数字。\n\n"},{"id":"83","run_dir":"run_prompt83_latentdyn","index":83,"title":"Navigating a Model's Own Latent Field: A Controllability Operator for Steering","title_zh":"导航模型自身的潜在场：一种用于操控的可控性算子","method_name":"Field-Compensated Latent Navigation (FCLN)","hook":"The intrinsic latent vector field a trained autoencoder induces on its manifold has been read only as a picture of attractors; we recast it as a measured controllability operator that tells a navigator, at each point, the fraction of any commanded displacement the model's own dynamics will keep versus cancel.","anchor_pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","anchor_pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","domain_category":"Interpretability & Representation Analysis","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf turns the model's intrinsic latent vector field (the enc-dec-induced field of semanticscholar:f3f5cbde400c7ba2ad7ce64636ba395dcc3a138c) into a navigable control surface: there is no quantity that, given a commanded latent displacement at a point, predicts how much of that displacement the intrinsic field will preserve, amplify, or cancel — so a navigator has no way to issue a correction that the model's own dynamics will actually carry to the intended target.","pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by reframing the opaque question 'where will the model's intrinsic field carry a perturbed latent state' as a faithful per-point measurement object — a controllability operator (the local Jacobian of one enc-dec step plus its commanded-displacement response) whose output is a per-direction kept-vs-cancelled fraction, with the unit of analysis fixed (latent point + commanded direction), faithfulness pinned to the model's own one-step map, and fidelity certified by a causal perturbation that flips the reached endpoint.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf reconciles externally-commanded steering with the model's intrinsic dynamics: steering methods (arxiv:2602.20102v2, openalex:W7115030175) treat the intrinsic field as unmodeled disturbance, so when steering near the model's own attractor basins the intrinsic pull silently contests or overrides the command and no leaf measures or predicts that contest.","pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by constructing matched steering instances that hold target direction and commanded magnitude fixed while varying exactly one axis — whether the start point sits inside an intrinsic attractor basin — so the measured gap between commanded and realized displacement isolates the intrinsic field's contest, with an off-the-model flat-field null as the oracle baseline and the anchor's controllability operator as the independent predictor of the survived fraction.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"representation learning / latent-space dynamics of neural models (autoencoders, generative models, and LLM activation space)","n_papers":44,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":19},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10},{"source":"openreview","n":2}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":8,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Parametric Taylor series based latent dynamics identification neural networks"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Input-to-State Stable Coupled Oscillator Networks for Closed-form Model-based Control in Latent Space"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Latent Graph Neural Networks for Human Skeleton-based Action Recognition"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Vehicle Trajectory Prediction With Multimodal and Dynamics-Aware Interaction Neural Networks"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Sensing with shallow recurrent decoder networks"},{"source":"openalex","title":"tLaSDI: Thermodynamics-informed latent space dynamics identification"}],"more":2},{"year":2025,"n":26,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Navigating the Latent Space Dynamics of Neural Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Reduced‐Order Modeling of Energetic Materials Using Physics‐Aware Recurrent Convolutional Neural Networks in a Latent Space (LatentPARC)"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Beyond Ensembles: Simulating All-Atom Protein Dynamics in a Learned Latent Space"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Exploring transition states of protein conformational changes via out-of-distribution detection in the hyperspherical latent space"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Reduced-order modeling of Hamiltonian dynamics based on symplectic neural networks"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Employing Artificial Neural Networks for Optimal Storage and Facile Sharing of Molecular Dynamics Simulation Trajectories"}],"more":20},{"year":2026,"n":10,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"},{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Latent-Y: A Lab-Validated Autonomous Agent for De Novo Drug Design"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Neural Networks and Schramm-Loewner Evolutions"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"From Performance to Viability: A Bootstrap Framework for Latent-Space Representation Learning in Adaptive Biological Systems"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Drift-Diffusion Matching: Embedding dynamics in latent manifolds of asymmetric neural networks"}],"more":4}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":17,"share":0.386},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":16,"share":0.364},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":10,"share":0.227},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":7,"share":0.159},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":7,"share":0.159},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":7,"share":0.159},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":5,"share":0.114},{"pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","count":4,"share":0.091}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Recent work establishes that a trained neural model already carries an intrinsic dynamical object on its latent manifold — iterating the encoder-decoder map induces a latent vector field whose vanishing regions are attractors aligned with data density (Navigating the Latent Space Dynamics of Neural Models, semanticscholar:f3f5cbde400c7ba2ad7ce64636ba395dcc3a138c), and the long-term behavior of latent-space surrogates is governed by Lyapunov/inertial-manifold structure (Stability analysis of chaotic systems in latent spaces, openalex:W4407132425). But this intrinsic field is consumed only as a descriptive diagnostic: it is visualized and its attractors are characterized, yet no machinery turns it into a control surface that moves a latent state from where it is to a target region while respecting the field's own geometry. Conversely, the methods that DO move latent/representation states toward targets — inference-time guidance for diffusion latents (openalex:W7115030175) and learned barrier-function steering of LLM activations (BarrierSteer, arxiv:2602.20102v2) — fit external directions or objective-specific potentials that are blind to the model's intrinsic field, so when a steering push is applied near one of the model's own attractor basins the intrinsic dynamics silently pull the state back or off-course, and there is no quantity that tells the navigator how much of its commanded displacement the model's own field will keep versus cancel. The gap is that 'where the model's intrinsic latent dynamics will carry a perturbed state' and 'where an external controller is trying to send it' are never reconciled into a single navigable account.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:f3f5cbde400c7ba2ad7ce64636ba395dcc3a138c","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Shows that any autoencoder implicitly defines a latent vector field by iterating the encoder-decoder map, with attractors that align with high-density regions of the data distribution, requiring no extra training. The field is used purely descriptively (visualization, memorization/attractor analysis); it is never inverted into a controller — there is no account of how an externally-commanded latent displacement composes with this intrinsic field, nor any measure of which commanded directions the field amplifies versus cancels, so the object that governs latent motion is characterized but not made navigable."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.20102v2","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"BarrierSteer learns a barrier function and steers LLM activations at inference to keep generations in a safe region, giving a theoretically-grounded steering objective. The barrier and steering direction are fit to an external safety objective and are agnostic to the model's intrinsic latent vector field, so the controller cannot anticipate where the model's own dynamics would otherwise carry the state and treats the intrinsic pull as unmodeled disturbance rather than as known geometry to exploit."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4407132425","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Characterizes the stability of latent-space reduced-order models via the Lyapunov spectrum, Kaplan-Yorke dimension, and inertial manifolds, establishing whether a learned latent flow preserves the true system's stability. The analysis is diagnostic and post-hoc — it certifies stability of the autonomous latent flow but provides no controlled-input formulation, so it cannot say how an injected control displacement will be expanded or contracted along the field's covariant Lyapunov directions, i.e. it measures the field's geometry without using it to navigate."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7115030175","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Develops inference-time editing/guidance for diffusion-based generative models (gradient/score-based pushes that move a latent toward an edit target). Guidance is computed from an external objective's gradient and added to the sampler step; it does not model the generator's intrinsic latent vector field as a structured object, so it cannot pre-compensate for the portion of a commanded edit that the model's own dynamics will absorb or redirect."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"representation learning / latent-space dynamics of neural models (autoencoders, generative models, and LLM activation space)","venue":"ICLR/ICML/NeurIPS (top ML)","time":"2025-2026","data":["standard image autoencoder benchmarks (MNIST/CIFAR)","pretrained generative-model latents","LLM activation traces"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with representation-learning and dynamical-systems background","preference":"both","baseline":"intrinsic latent vector field obtained by iterating the encoder-decoder map (Navigating the Latent Space Dynamics of Neural Models, semanticscholar:f3f5cbde400c7ba2ad7ce64636ba395dcc3a138c); externally-trained steering directions / learned barrier functions (BarrierSteer, arxiv:2602.20102v2)","limitation":"the intrinsic latent vector field of a neural model is characterized descriptively (attractors, stability) but is not turned into a usable control surface for navigating latent states toward a target; steering methods that DO move latent states ignore the model's own intrinsic field geometry and instead fit external directions","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object every leg reads from is the model's intrinsic latent map T(z) = E(D(z)) — one decode-then-encode step of a trained autoencoder F = D∘E with latent dim k — whose iterated application is the enc-dec-induced latent vector field v(z) = T(z) − z (model-internal readout; no training added). LEG 1 (anchor, reframe→measurement). We recast 'navigability' as a per-point measurement object: the controllability operator at z is the Jacobian J(z) = ∂T/∂z ∈ R^{k×k} of the one-step map (computed by autodiff through the frozen D and E), together with the commanded-response decomposition of a unit displacement d. Concretely, for a commanded latent move d the model's own dynamics return, after one step, the realized increment J(z)d; we define the kept fraction κ(z,d) = ⟨J(z)d, d⟩ / ⟨d,d⟩ (the component of the command the field preserves, signed: κ>1 amplifies, 0<κ<1 damps, κ<0 reverses toward an attractor) and the off-axis leakage as ‖J(z)d − κ(z,d)d‖/‖d‖. Both are pure functions of J(z) and d — computable from the text with no free index once the layer set is fixed to the full E,D stack. Tractability (C00's single compression trick): rather than the dense k×k Jacobian we use r Jacobian-vector products (r≈8 random Rademacher probes via forward-mode autodiff) to form a low-rank sketch Ĵ that preserves the κ-ranking across directions; this is the one linearization that buys cost. Faithfulness is pinned to the model's own one-step map (not an off-distribution surrogate), and fidelity is certified causally: a navigator that issues the field-compensated command d* = (commanded target step) pre-divided by the local kept-fraction along its own direction must reach a target latent closer (lower L2 to target) than the raw command — perturbing J(z) (replacing it with identity, i.e. ignoring the field) must degrade that reached-endpoint accuracy. LEG 2 (sibling, controlled diagnostic). The same J(z)/κ object is the predictor in a confound-isolating instrument that resolves whether external steering fights the intrinsic field. We build matched steering pairs: identical target direction u and identical commanded magnitude ε applied at two start latents that differ in exactly one named confound — basin membership b(z)∈{in,out}, where 'in' means z lies in an attractor basin of v (‖v(z)‖ below a percentile threshold τ chosen as the 20th percentile of ‖v‖ over encoded data, and the trajectory z,T(z),T²(z),… converging). Holding u,ε fixed, the realized post-steer displacement is measured after one model step; the headline is the gap Δ = realized_displacement(out) − realized_displacement(in), the intrinsic field's contest. The oracle independent of the model is a flat-field null (a linear decoder whose J≡I, where κ≡1 everywhere) against which any nonzero Δ is attributable to the field. The anchor's κ(z,u) is the independent predictor: Δ must track (1 − κ̄_in) where κ̄_in is the mean kept-fraction at in-basin points. The two legs share J(z): leg 1 constructs and validates it as a controller input, leg 2 uses it as the measured explanatory variable for the steering contest — one object, two faces, so the paper reads as one contribution.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The legs share machinery rather than needing separate modules: the controllability operator J(z) (and its scalar summary κ) is literally the same quantity the anchor builds and the diagnostic measures against — evidence is that leg 2's predictor IS leg 1's deliverable, so a single shared_object thread (the intrinsic one-step map T and its Jacobian) carries both, which is why I did not introduce a second learned component. (b) Alternatives considered and rejected: (i) learning a separate forward/inverse dynamics model to plan in latent space — rejected as a regression to method_lineage collateral c1 (Koopman/DMD fit-then-control) and to n1 (fitted latent surrogate), since it re-identifies dynamics the model already implies; keeping J(z) read directly off the frozen map avoids that occupied node. (ii) Framing the contribution as a pure attractor-basin characterization — rejected because it lands back on the descriptive n3/n4 frontier leaves the gap explicitly excludes.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on a frozen convolutional autoencoder trained on CIFAR-10 (and a VAE on CelebA), pick 500 (start z0, target z*) latent pairs and navigate from z0 to z* both with the field-compensated command d*=c/κ and with the raw command c, measuring L2(reached latent, z*) and an attribute-classifier readout on the decoded image. If the candidate works, the field-compensated navigator's reached-L2 decreases relative to the raw command, and the decrease is largest precisely at in-basin start points where the intrinsic field most contests the command; in the controlled diagnostic, the apparent-vs-deconfounded steering gap Δ between out-basin and in-basin starts is significantly positive and tracks ε·(1−κ̄_in). The single named load-bearing variable is the kept-fraction κ(z,c) (equivalently the local Jacobian J(z) it is computed from): the mechanism claim is that κ is what governs how much of a command the model's own dynamics carry. Negative control: randomize κ across points (shuffle the per-point κ values so each point receives another point's kept-fraction while the command magnitudes are unchanged) and the reached-endpoint L2 of the 'compensated' navigator must rise back to the raw-command baseline — if scrambling κ leaves reached-L2 unchanged, then κ was not the mechanism and any improvement came from the extra step-size renormalization, not the field model. Positive control: a stripped-down navigator that uses ONLY κ along the command direction (ignoring all off-axis leakage) should still recover most of the reached-L2 improvement, identifying κ as the sufficient carrier of the effect.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:f3f5cbde400c7ba2ad7ce64636ba395dcc3a138c","delta":"They construct and visualize the enc-dec-induced latent vector field and characterize its attractors descriptively; we derive from the same one-step map a per-point, per-direction controllability operator κ(z,d) = ⟨J(z)d,d⟩/⟨d,d⟩ that predicts the kept-vs-cancelled fraction of a commanded displacement and prove (causally) it is the quantity a navigator must invert — a control object their characterization never produces."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.20102v2","delta":"BarrierSteer learns an external barrier function to steer activations toward a safety region treating intrinsic dynamics as disturbance; we never learn a steering direction, instead read the model's own Jacobian and measure (via a confound-isolating instrument) the basin-dependent fraction of any command the intrinsic field cancels, a quantity their disturbance-agnostic controller cannot expose."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4407132425","delta":"They certify the stability of an autonomous latent flow post-hoc via the Lyapunov spectrum with no input term; we add a controlled-input response (κ and off-axis leakage of a commanded d) and show it governs navigation accuracy, turning a stability diagnostic into a steering predictor."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7115030175","delta":"Their inference-time diffusion guidance adds an external objective gradient to the sampler step; we pre-compensate the command by the model's own kept-fraction so the realized displacement matches the intended one, and quantify the gradient/command fraction the generator's intrinsic map would otherwise absorb."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:f3f5cbde400c7ba2ad7ce64636ba395dcc3a138c","what_step_was_missed":"They built the enc-dec-induced field as an autonomous object and stopped at characterizing its attractors; for our contribution to already exist they would have needed to construct the field's controlled-input response — the local Jacobian's action on a commanded displacement, decomposed into a kept-fraction κ along the command and off-axis leakage — and to certify causally that inverting κ (pre-dividing the command by it) is what makes a navigator's realized endpoint reach the target. That controllability decomposition of the same one-step map, plus its causal validation as a steering predictor, is the missing construction."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":288,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"Hard floor did not fire: gap_closure_reject_check has no entry with candidate_match=yes (the only non-clear signal is the C02 ecological-validity lesson at 'borderline' in a non-load-bearing scope aspect), recipe_application_check is 'applied' on both legs (κ measurement-with-causal-certification for C00; single-confound instrument with independent oracle for C02), anti_pattern_check matched nothing, and paper_pointed_threat is a non-exact, differentiable concurrent work (learned geometry vs read-off intrinsic Jacobian). Per the soft-judgment heuristic 'default to advance when only one check is borderline and it is in a non-load-bearing aspect', the candidate advances with the ecological-validity scope concern and the head-to-head-vs-learned-geometry comparison surfaced for Phase 4's reviewer_concerns_and_responses.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf turns the model's intrinsic latent vector field (the enc-dec-induced field of semanticscholar:f3f5cbde400c7ba2ad7ce64636ba395dcc3a138c) into a navigable control surface: there is no quantity that, given a commanded latent displacement at a point, predicts how much of that displacement the intrinsic field will preserve, amplify, or cancel — so a navigator has no way to issue a correction that the model's own dynamics will actually carry to the intended target.","main_pattern":"reframe_as_solvable_object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The signature failure is treating the reframing as a mechanical wrapper — pointing an established attribution/estimation tool at a new granularity/architecture without re-deriving why the resulting scores are faithful to the model, with no causal validation that the identified components actually drive behavior.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Pointing an off-the-shelf decomposition at a coarser input granularity without showing the coarser units preserve the signal reads as a wrapper, not a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism step 4 explicitly gates the low-rank Jacobian sketch on a Spearman ρ>0.9 check that the sketch preserves the κ-ranking versus the dense Jacobian, so signal preservation under the compression is shown, not assumed."},{"lesson_quoted":"Proposing a new attribution definition without an axiomatic or causal argument for why it should count as ground-truth collapses the moment a reviewer asks why this is the real importance.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"κ(z,d) is defined as a pure function of the model's own one-step Jacobian and certified causally — the negative control (shuffling per-point κ) must drive reached-endpoint L2 back to the raw-command baseline, grounding why κ is the load-bearing quantity rather than asserting it."},{"lesson_quoted":"Conflating a methodological artifact — a computation-granularity difference, a degenerate zero baseline — with genuine signal undermines the entire premise once the confound is identified.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the flat-field PCA null (J≡I, κ≡1) is an explicit non-degenerate baseline against which any κ-driven effect is measured, and the κ-shuffle control rules out the step-size-renormalization artifact, so the gain is attributable to the field not to bookkeeping."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf reconciles externally-commanded steering with the model's intrinsic dynamics: steering methods (arxiv:2602.20102v2, openalex:W7115030175) treat the intrinsic field as unmodeled disturbance, so when steering near the model's own attractor basins the intrinsic pull silently contests or overrides the command and no leaf measures or predicts that contest.","main_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail when the constructed instrument isolates the confound only inside an artificial regime and never demonstrates transfer to real deployment, or is circular (validated against the same system population it interrogates), or merely re-confirms a documented limitation.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Building the instrument around one contested definition of the target property means it cannot independently confirm that the definition is correct, and reviewers flag the resulting circularity.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the oracle (flat-field PCA autoencoder with J≡I) is independent of the trained model under test, and basin membership b(z) is defined by an observable percentile of ‖v(z)‖ plus an iterate-convergence check, not by the evaluand's own judgment."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a synthetic-ground-truth instrument only on synthetic data, without demonstrating that the controlled finding transfers to real-world instances, leaves ecological validity unestablished and undermines the central claim.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"the instrument runs on real CIFAR-10/CelebA autoencoder latents (not purely synthetic) and includes an out-of-sample partial-correlation cross-check (step 10), but it stops at autoencoder reconstruction settings and does not yet show transfer to a deployed generative-editing or LLM-steering pipeline, so ecological reach is partial — a non-load-bearing scope concern to surface for Phase 4 rather than a structural failure."},{"lesson_quoted":"A diagnostic that only re-confirms a shortcut already known in advance, surfacing no previously unmeasurable failure, is read as confirmatory rather than as a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the basin-dependent steering-cancellation gap Δ ≈ ε·(1−κ̄_in) is a previously unmeasured, quantitatively predicted relation (not a known limitation), and the predictor κ comes from the anchor leg, so the instrument surfaces a new measurable quantity."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The C00 anchor entry is fully clear (κ defined from the model's own Jacobian, causally certified, compression validated). The C02 diagnostic entry is borderline only on the ecological-validity lesson ('synthetic-only without demonstrated real-world transfer') — the instrument uses real-image AE latents and an out-of-sample cross-check but does not yet show transfer to a deployed steering pipeline; this is a scope concern in a non-load-bearing aspect, not a triggered Reject."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf turns the model's intrinsic latent vector field (the enc-dec-induced field of semanticscholar:f3f5cbde400c7ba2ad7ce64636ba395dcc3a138c) into a navigable control surface: there is no quantity that, given a commanded latent displacement at a point, predicts how much of that displacement the intrinsic field will preserve, amplify, or cancel — so a navigator has no way to issue a correction that the model's own dynamics will actually carry to the intended target.","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Recast an opaque question about an already-trained model into a concrete measurement over a well-studied object, fixing the unit of analysis and a faithfulness constraint that keeps the output on the model's own computation, buying tractability with one compression trick, and certifying fidelity by a causal intervention that flips behavior when the identified object is perturbed — not by plausibility.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism LEG 1 performs exactly this: the opaque question 'where will the model's field carry a perturbed state' is recast as the measurement κ(z,d)=⟨J(z)d,d⟩/⟨d,d⟩ over the model's own one-step map T=E∘D (unit of analysis = latent point + commanded direction; faithfulness pinned to the model's one-step map), tractability bought with the single r=8-JVP low-rank sketch (validated by ρ>0.9), and fidelity certified causally by the κ-perturbation/identity-replacement control that must degrade reached-endpoint accuracy. This is the cluster's distinctive measurement-plus-causal-certification move, not a generic reframe.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf reconciles externally-commanded steering with the model's intrinsic dynamics: steering methods (arxiv:2602.20102v2, openalex:W7115030175) treat the intrinsic field as unmodeled disturbance, so when steering near the model's own attractor basins the intrinsic pull silently contests or overrides the command and no leaf measures or predicts that contest.","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Construct a controlled set of evaluation instances in which exactly one named confound is structurally blocked or independently varied while everything else is held fixed, supply ground truth independent of the system under test, and report the divergence between apparent and de-confounded performance as the headline result.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism LEG 2 builds matched steering pairs holding target direction u and magnitude ε fixed and varying exactly one named confound — basin membership b(z) — with a model-independent flat-field PCA oracle, and reports the apparent-vs-deconfounded gap Δ = realized_displacement(out) − realized_displacement(in) as the headline. This is the cluster's confound-isolation-plus-independent-oracle-plus-headline-gap move performed concretely.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both legs perform their cited cluster's signature operation in core_mechanism: C00's measurement-object-with-causal-certification (the κ Jacobian operator certified by the negative control) and C02's single-confound-isolating instrument with a model-independent oracle and a headline divergence; neither leg merely enacts its parent's generic gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["reframe_as_solvable_object","controlled_diagnostic_design"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; this candidate's composition set {reframe_as_solvable_object, controlled_diagnostic_design} contains no such pairing, so no anti-pattern matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"collision:Riemannian-Manifold Steering: Geometry-Aware Generative Autoencoders for Label-Free Steering","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"This concurrent work recasts manifold steering for generative autoencoders by LEARNING a geometry over paths in activation space (relaxing the prior requirement of labelled class centroids and prescribed cyclic/sequential structure). It is the closest competitor because it also steers in an autoencoder's latent geometry without labels. The candidate's claim stands rather than falls against it because of a sharp mechanism difference: Riemannian-Manifold Steering learns an explicit Riemannian metric over activation paths and then steers along learned geodesics, whereas the candidate learns nothing — it reads the model's OWN intrinsic enc-dec one-step Jacobian J(z) and derives the kept-fraction κ as the controllability predictor, and additionally ships a confound-isolating instrument that quantifies how much of a command the intrinsic field cancels (Δ ≈ ε·(1−κ̄_in)), a basin-dependent contest measurement their learned-geometry steerer does not expose. The two could be compared head-to-head, but neither subsumes the other: they learn a steering geometry, the candidate measures and inverts the geometry the model already has.","addressable_via":"Already differentiated by the no-learning-vs-learned-geometry axis already present in core_mechanism and differentiation_from_lit; to harden, Phase 4 reviewer_concerns should add an explicit head-to-head comparison of field-compensated navigation versus learned-geodesic steering on the same frozen autoencoder."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Navigating a Model's Own Latent Field: A Controllability Operator for Steering\n\n**Method.** Field-Compensated Latent Navigation (FCLN)\n\n## Motivation\nWhen you train an autoencoder — a network that compresses an image into a short code and reconstructs it — people usually think of that code as a fixed address. But if you take a code, decode it to an image, and re-encode that image, the code moves a little. Repeat this and the code drifts along a hidden flow on the space of codes, settling into 'attractor' spots that sit where the training data was dense. A recent paper (Navigating the Latent Space Dynamics of Neural Models, 2025) discovered this flow and drew pictures of it, but only used it to describe the model — it never used the flow to actually drive a code toward a goal.\n\nMeanwhile, the methods people DO use to push a code toward a goal — for example inference-time guidance for image generators, or learned 'barrier' steering that keeps a language model's internal state in a safe zone — completely ignore this hidden flow. So when you push a code near one of the model's attractor spots, the model's own flow quietly drags it back or sideways, and the steering method has no idea this is happening. Nobody has a number that says, at a given point, how much of your intended push the model's own flow will keep versus cancel.\n\nThis is solvable now for three reasons: the 2025 paper just proved the hidden flow is a real, training-free object; recent steering work (2026) made this exact 'the model fights my push' failure a real deployment problem; and forward-mode automatic differentiation makes it cheap to measure, at any point, how the one-step flow stretches or shrinks a pushed direction — on off-the-shelf checkpoints, with no retraining.\n\nWhat changes once we close the gap: steering stops being blind. A navigator can scale up each command exactly enough to cancel the flow's drag (a 'field-compensated' command), and can predict in advance where the flow will resist hardest. That gives the descriptive-flow paper a real control knob, and gives the flow-ignorant steering methods the model of the model's own pull that they currently lack.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n\n1. Take a frozen, already-trained autoencoder — a network with an encoder E that compresses an image into a code of length k (use k=128) and a decoder D that reconstructs the image. Use a small convolutional autoencoder on CIFAR-10 (four downsampling convolution blocks) and a Variational Autoencoder (VAE) on CelebA (where the code is the distribution's mean). Lock the network weights (no learning) but keep it differentiable with respect to the input code so you can later measure how the code moves. Define the one-step map T(z)=E(D(z)) (decode then re-encode) and the flow $v(z)=T(z)- z.$\n\n*One decode-then-encode step T of the frozen autoencoder and the intrinsic latent vector field v it induces; v vanishes at attractors.*\n$$ T(z) = E(D(z)), \\qquad v(z) = T(z) - z \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The hidden flow is already inside the trained model — you just have to read it off, not learn it.\n\n### Controllability operator\n*Read the model's one-step Jacobian off the frozen map and turn it into the per-direction kept-fraction $\\kappa $ and leakage — the missing control quantity.*\n\n2. Write one routine that, given a code z and a direction d, returns how the one-step map moves a small push in direction d — the quantity J(z)d — using a single forward-mode automatic-differentiation pass over the composed map $E(D(\\cdot )).$ Use a standard library call (PyTorch's torch.func.jvp or JAX's jax.jvp) so you never build the full $k\\times k$ matrix; the differentiation automatically chains through decode then encode. This routine is reused everywhere below.\n   - _Why_: You only ever need the flow's effect on specific directions, and one push at a time is cheap.\n3. From J(z)d compute two numbers: the kept-fraction $\\kappa $ — how much of your push survives along its own direction — and the off-axis leakage — how much of the response is redirected sideways. Use the ordinary dot product, and first scale the direction d to unit length so the kept-fraction is simply the dot product of d with J(z)d. Ignore any push that is essentially zero length (below 1e-8). One push, one pair of numbers.\n\n*The kept-fraction $\\kappa :$ the signed component of a commanded direction d the one-step Jacobian J(z) preserves. $\\kappa >1$ amplifies, $0<\\kappa <1$ damps, $\\kappa <0$ reverses toward an attractor.*\n$$ \\kappa(z,d) = \\frac{\\langle J(z)\\,d,\\, d\\rangle}{\\langle d,\\, d\\rangle}, \\qquad J(z) = \\frac{\\partial T}{\\partial z} \\tag{2} $$\n\n\n*Off-axis leakage: the part of the realized response J(z)d that points away from the commanded direction d, normalized by command size.*\n$$ \\ell(z,d) = \\frac{\\lVert J(z)\\,d - \\kappa(z,d)\\,d\\rVert}{\\lVert d\\rVert} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: These two numbers are exactly the missing 'how much will the flow keep vs cancel' that no prior work measured.\n4. Approximate the full local map with a rank-8 sketch built from 8 random sign-vector (Rademacher) pushes. Before trusting it, validate once per dataset on 100 sampled points: fix a bank of 64 unit test directions, compute the kept-fraction for all 64 directions both exactly and from the sketch, and check that the sketch ranks the directions the same way (Spearman rank correlation above 0.9, averaged over the 100 points). Only proceed if it passes.\n   - _Why_: The cheap sketch is only allowed if it provably preserves the ranking that matters — otherwise the shortcut would be a wrapper, not a measurement.\n\n### Field-compensated navigator\n*Use $\\kappa $ to pre-scale each command so the model's own flow carries the latent to the target, and prove $\\kappa $ causally with an identity-replacement control.*\n\n5. To move from a start code z0 to a target code z*, repeat for up to 50 steps: take the raw step toward the target (size set to 10% of the start-to-target distance), divide it by the local kept-fraction $\\kappa $ (with a floor of 0.1 to avoid dividing by something tiny) to get the compensated command, apply it and let the model's own one step act, and stop early once you are within 1e-3 of the target. Measure how close you landed (distance to z*) and, using a simple pre-trained linear classifier on the code space, whether the decoded image's attribute (CIFAR-10 class, or CelebA 'smiling'/'glasses') moved toward the target's.\n\n*The field-compensated command d*: the raw step c toward the target, pre-divided by its local kept-fraction (floored at $\\kappa _{floor}$ to guard division).*\n$$ d^{*} = \\frac{c}{\\max(\\kappa(z_t, c),\\, \\kappa_{\\mathrm{floor}})}, \\qquad c = \\eta\\,\\frac{z^{*} - z_t}{\\lVert z^{*} - z_t\\rVert} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: If the flow keeps only a fraction $\\kappa $ of your push, pushing $1/\\kappa $ as hard makes the realized move land where you intended.\n6. Run exactly the same navigation as before but pretend the flow does nothing — set the kept-fraction to 1 everywhere, which is just the plain uncompensated command — on the identical start/target pairs and settings. Record where you land.\n   - _Why_: If compensation truly helps, turning it off should hurt most exactly where the flow is strong (in-basin starts) — proving $\\kappa $ is doing the work.\n\n### Confound-isolating steering diagnostic\n*Measure how much of a fixed command the flow cancels inside versus outside basins, against a flat-field oracle, predicted by $\\kappa .$*\n\n7. Build matched pairs that change only one thing — whether the start sits in an attractor basin. Label a start 'in-basin' if the flow magnitude there is in the smallest 20% across all codes AND repeatedly applying the one-step map for 20 steps steadily settles it down; otherwise 'out-of-basin'. Fix a single steering direction (the difference between two class average codes) and a single push size (half the typical flow magnitude), used identically everywhere. Pair each in-basin code with an out-of-basin code of similar code length and same class (2000 pairs), apply the same steering command, and measure the actual displacement after one model step.\n   - _Why_: Holding the command identical and changing only basin membership isolates the flow's contest from everything else.\n8. Compute the average in-basin kept-fraction (one push per start in the steering direction) and the gap $\\Delta  =$ average out-of-basin displacement minus average in-basin displacement. Report $\\Delta $ with a bootstrap 95% confidence interval, and check the prediction that $\\Delta $ should be about the push size times (1 minus the average in-basin kept-fraction): see whether that predicted value falls inside the interval, and report their ratio (close to 1 supports the claim).\n\n*The headline diagnostic gap $\\Delta $ between realized displacement at out-basin and in-basin starts under a fixed command magnitude $\\epsilon ,$ predicted to track $\\epsilon $ times $one-minus-the-mean-in-basin-\\kappa .$*\n$$ \\Delta = \\overline{\\mathrm{disp}}_{\\mathrm{out}} - \\overline{\\mathrm{disp}}_{\\mathrm{in}} \\approx \\varepsilon\\,(1 - \\bar{\\kappa}_{\\mathrm{in}}) \\tag{5} $$\n\n   - _Why_: If the flow cancels commands in basins, the in-basin moves should be smaller by exactly the fraction the flow eats — and $\\kappa $ predicts that fraction.\n9. Swap in a linear baseline: fit Principal Component Analysis (PCA) on the same images and keep the top 128 components as the code. Because this map is linear and orthonormal, decoding then re-encoding returns the code unchanged, so its flow cannot fight any command (kept-fraction is 1 everywhere). Rerun the same diagnostic; the gap should be essentially zero. Any real gap in the trained model above this baseline is genuinely caused by the model's flow.\n   - _Why_: A flat-flow model that cannot fight commands gives a clean baseline — any real gap above it is genuinely caused by the model's flow.\n10. For each point, define a steering-loss number: how much of the commanded push along the steering direction failed to show up in the realized move. Fit a linear regression of this loss on the kept-fraction $\\kappa $ while also including the code length, the class, and the flow magnitude as controls. Report the standardized weight on $\\kappa $ and its significance, on a held-out set of points not used to pick the basin threshold or steering direction — this checks $\\kappa $ still predicts the contest after accounting for obvious confounds.\n   - _Why_: This checks $\\kappa $ still predicts the contest on held-out points after accounting for obvious confounds.\n\n### Cross-basin stress test\n*Stress the navigator where target and start lie in different attractor basins.*\n\n11. Map out the attractor basins: from many starting codes, repeatedly apply the one-step map until they settle, and group the settling points that are very close together into basins. Pick 500 start/target pairs that fall in different basins. A run 'reaches the target's basin' if, after navigation, repeatedly applying the one-step map from where you landed settles into the same basin as the target. Report how often the plain command ends up in the wrong basin versus how often the compensated command reaches the target's basin.\n   - _Why_: Crossing basin boundaries is the hardest case, where ignoring the flow fails most clearly.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 导航模型自身的潜在场：一种用于操控的可控性算子\n\n**方法名称.** Field-Compensated Latent Navigation (FCLN)\n\n## 研究动机\n训练一个 autoencoder（把图像压成一段短编码再重建出来的网络）时，人们通常把这段编码当成一个固定的地址。但如果你把一段编码解码成图像、再把这张图像重新编码，编码会发生一点移动。反复这样做，编码就会沿着编码空间上一条隐藏的流动漂移，最终落入若干吸引子位置，而这些位置正好对应训练数据密集的地方。2025 年的一篇论文（Navigating the Latent Space Dynamics of Neural Models）发现了这条流动并画出了它，但只把它用来描述模型——从未用这条流动真正把一段编码驱动到目标。\n\n与此同时，人们真正用来把编码推向目标的方法——例如图像生成器的推理时引导（inference-time guidance），或把语言模型内部状态保持在安全区的学习型 barrier 操控——完全忽略了这条隐藏流动。于是当你把编码推到模型某个吸引子附近时，模型自身的流动会悄悄把它拽回去或拽偏，而操控方法对此一无所知。没有人有一个数值，能在给定点上告诉你：你想施加的推动，模型自身的流动会保留多少、又会抵消多少。\n\n现在能解决，有三个原因：2025 年的论文刚证明这条隐藏流动是一个真实、无需训练的对象；近期的操控工作（2026）让“模型对抗我的推动”这个失败模式成了真实的部署问题；而前向模式自动微分（forward-mode automatic differentiation）让我们能在任意点上廉价地测出一步流动对被推方向的拉伸或收缩——在现成 checkpoint 上、无需重训。\n\n补上这个空白后会发生什么：操控不再盲目。导航器可以把每个命令恰好放大到足以抵消流动的拖拽（即“场补偿”命令 field-compensated command），并能提前预测流动在哪里抵抗最强。这给那篇只做描述的流动论文配上了真正的控制旋钮，也给那些忽略流动的操控方法补上了它们当前缺失的、对模型自身拉力的建模。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景\n\n1. 取一个冻结的、已训练好的 autoencoder——它有一个把图像压成长度为 k 的编码的编码器 E（取 k=128），和一个重建图像的解码器 D。在 CIFAR-10 上用一个小型卷积 autoencoder（四个下采样卷积块），在 CelebA 上用一个变分自编码器(Variational Autoencoder, VAE)（其编码取分布的均值）。锁住网络权重（不再学习），但保持它对输入编码可微，以便之后测量编码如何移动。定义一步映射 T(z)=E(D(z))（先解码再重新编码）以及流动 $v(z)=T(z)- z$。\n\n*冻结自编码器的一步先解码再编码映射 T，以及它在潜在流形上诱导的内在向量场 v；v 在吸引子处为零。*\n$$ T(z) = E(D(z)), \\qquad v(z) = T(z) - z \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这条隐藏流动已经在训练好的模型里——你只需把它读出来，而不是去学一个新的。\n\n### 可控性算子\n*从冻结映射读出模型的一步雅可比，转化为按方向的保留比例 $\\kappa $ 和泄漏——这正是缺失的控制量。*\n\n2. 写一个例程：给定编码 z 和方向 d，用一次 forward-mode 自动微分(forward-mode automatic differentiation)对组合映射 $E(D(\\cdot ))$ 求值，返回一步映射如何移动方向 d 上的小推动——即 J(z)d。直接用标准库调用（PyTorch 的 torch.func.jvp 或 JAX 的 jax.jvp），从而永远不构建完整的 $k\\times k$ 矩阵；微分会自动沿“先解码再编码”链式传播。这个例程在下面处处复用。\n   - _为什么_: 你只需要流动对特定方向的作用，一次推一个方向就足够便宜。\n3. 由 J(z)d 计算两个数：保留比例 $\\kappa ——$你的推动沿自身方向存活了多少；以及离轴泄漏——响应中有多少被拐向侧面。用普通点积，并先把方向 d 缩放到单位长度，这样保留比例就等于 d 与 J(z)d 的点积。忽略任何长度基本为零（低于 1e-8）的推动。一次推动，得到一对数。\n\n*保留比例 $\\kappa $：一步雅可比 J(z) 对受命方向 d 所保留的带符号分量。$\\kappa >1$ 放大，$0<\\kappa <1$ 衰减，$\\kappa <0$ 反向拉回吸引子。*\n$$ \\kappa(z,d) = \\frac{\\langle J(z)\\,d,\\, d\\rangle}{\\langle d,\\, d\\rangle}, \\qquad J(z) = \\frac{\\partial T}{\\partial z} \\tag{2} $$\n\n\n*离轴泄漏：实际响应 J(z)d 中偏离受命方向 d 的分量，按命令大小归一化。*\n$$ \\ell(z,d) = \\frac{\\lVert J(z)\\,d - \\kappa(z,d)\\,d\\rVert}{\\lVert d\\rVert} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这两个数正是此前没人测过的“流动会保留多少、抵消多少”。\n4. 用 8 个随机符号向量（Rademacher）推动构造一个秩为 8 的 sketch 来近似局部映射。在信任它之前，每个数据集先在 100 个采样点上验证一次：固定一组 64 个单位测试方向，对全部 64 个方向分别用精确方式和 sketch 计算保留比例，检查 sketch 对这些方向的排序是否一致（Spearman 秩相关，在 100 个点上平均后高于 0.9）。只有通过才继续。\n   - _为什么_: 只有当廉价 sketch 可证明保留了关键排序时才允许使用，否则这条捷径就只是个壳，而非测量。\n\n### 场补偿导航器\n*用 $\\kappa $ 预先放缩每个命令，让模型自身的流动把潜在编码带到目标，并用恒等替换控制因果地证明 $\\kappa $。*\n\n5. 要从起点编码 z0 移动到目标编码 z*，重复至多 50 步：取朝目标的原始步长（大小设为起点到目标距离的 10%），除以局部保留比例 $\\kappa $（设下限 0.1，避免除以极小值）得到补偿命令，施加它并让模型自身的一步生效，一旦距目标小于 1e-3 就提前停止。测量落点离 z* 多近（距离），并用编码空间上一个简单的预训练线性分类器，检查解码图像的属性（CIFAR-10 类别，或 CelebA 的 smiling/glasses）是否朝目标的属性移动。\n\n*场补偿命令 d*：朝目标的原始步长 c 预先除以其局部保留比例（用 $\\kappa _{floor}$ 兜底以防除零）。*\n$$ d^{*} = \\frac{c}{\\max(\\kappa(z_t, c),\\, \\kappa_{\\mathrm{floor}})}, \\qquad c = \\eta\\,\\frac{z^{*} - z_t}{\\lVert z^{*} - z_t\\rVert} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 如果流动只保留你推动的 $\\kappa $ 这一部分，那么推 $1/\\kappa $ 倍力气，实际移动就会落到你想要的地方。\n6. 用与之前完全相同的导航再跑一遍，但假装流动毫无作用——把保留比例处处设为 1，也就是普通的无补偿命令——在完全相同的起点/目标对和设置上。记录落点。\n   - _为什么_: 如果补偿确有帮助，关掉它应当恰好在流动强的地方（盆内起点）伤害最大——以此证明 $\\kappa $ 在起作用。\n\n### 隔离混杂的操控诊断\n*在盆内与盆外测量流动抵消固定命令的多少，对照平坦场 oracle，并由 $\\kappa $ 预测。*\n\n7. 构造只改变一件事的配对——起点是否落在吸引子盆里。若某起点处的流动幅度在所有编码中最小的 20% 之内，且反复施加一步映射 20 步会稳定收敛，就标为“盆内”，否则“盆外”。固定单一操控方向（两个类别平均编码之差）和单一推动大小（典型流动幅度的一半），处处相同地使用。把每个盆内编码与一个编码长度相近、类别相同的盆外编码配对（2000 对），施加相同的操控命令，测量一步模型作用后的实际位移。\n   - _为什么_: 保持命令完全相同、只改变盆内外归属，就能把流动的对抗从其他因素中隔离出来。\n8. 计算盆内平均保留比例（每个起点沿操控方向推一次）以及差值 $\\Delta  =$ 盆外平均位移减盆内平均位移。用自助法(bootstrap)给出 $\\Delta $ 的 95% 置信区间，并检验预测$——\\Delta $ 应约等于推动大小乘以（1 减盆内平均保留比例）：看该预测值是否落在区间内，并报告二者之比（接近 1 则支持论断）。\n\n*诊断头条差值 $\\Delta $：在固定命令幅度 $\\epsilon $ 下，盆外与盆内起点的实际位移之差；预测其约等于 $\\epsilon $ 乘以（1 减去盆内平均 $\\kappa $）。*\n$$ \\Delta = \\overline{\\mathrm{disp}}_{\\mathrm{out}} - \\overline{\\mathrm{disp}}_{\\mathrm{in}} \\approx \\varepsilon\\,(1 - \\bar{\\kappa}_{\\mathrm{in}}) \\tag{5} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 如果流动在盆内抵消命令，盆内的移动就该恰好小掉流动吃掉的那部分——而 $\\kappa $ 预测了这个比例。\n9. 换入一个线性基线：在同样的图像上拟合主成分分析(Principal Component Analysis, PCA)，保留前 128 个主成分作为编码。由于该映射是线性且正交的，解码再重新编码会原样返回编码，因此它的流动无法对抗任何命令（保留比例处处为 1）。重跑同一诊断，差值应基本为零。训练模型中高于该基线的任何真实差值，才确实由模型的流动引起。\n   - _为什么_: 一个无法对抗命令的平坦流动模型给出干净基线——任何高于它的真实差值才确实由模型的流动引起。\n10. 对每个点定义一个操控损失数：沿操控方向所命令的推动中，有多少没有在实际移动里体现出来。把这个损失对保留比例 $\\kappa $ 做线性回归，同时纳入编码长度、类别和流动幅度作为控制变量。在未用于选取盆阈值或操控方向的留出点集上，报告 $\\kappa $ 的标准化权重及其显著性——以此检验在剔除明显混杂后 $\\kappa $ 是否仍能预测这场对抗。\n   - _为什么_: 这检验在剔除明显混杂后，$\\kappa $ 在留出点上是否仍能预测这场对抗。\n\n### 跨盆压力测试\n*在目标与起点位于不同吸引子盆时对导航器施压。*\n\n11. 勾画吸引子盆：从许多起始编码出发，反复施加一步映射直到稳定，把彼此非常接近的稳定点归并成盆。挑选 500 个落在不同盆中的起点/目标对。若导航后从落点反复施加一步映射会稳定到与目标相同的盆，则该次“到达目标所在盆”。报告普通命令落入错误盆的频率，对比补偿命令到达目标所在盆的频率。\n   - _为什么_: 跨盆边界是最难的情形，忽略流动在此失败得最明显。\n\n"},{"id":"84","run_dir":"run_prompt84_arcontimg","index":84,"title":"Closed-Form Continuous Tokens: Replacing the Per-Token Diffusion Head with an Amortized Flow","title_zh":"闭式连续 token：用 amortized flow 替换逐 token 扩散头","method_name":"Amortized Flow Head (AFH)","hook":"Continuous-token autoregressive image models hide each token's distribution inside an iterative diffusion head whose density can never be read off; we show the transformer's own per-position vector already contains enough information to parameterize an exact, single-evaluation per-token density, so the iterative head was never necessary. Making the likelihood explicit is not just cheaper sampling — it exposes a per-token entropy the diffusion head structurally discards, which we then spend sampling budget against.","anchor_pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","anchor_pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","domain_category":"Generative Models — Vision","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved continuous-token AR leaf exposes an explicit, single-evaluation per-token conditional density: the per-token distribution is only reachable through an iterative diffusion/denoising head, so a token's likelihood cannot be read off, compared across positions, or used to decide where to spend sampling effort (additive need — phrased as the missing outcome, not a prescribed parametric form).","pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","sub_pattern":"C12 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by swapping the per-stage generative primitive: the iterative diffusion head (closed-form density unavailable) is replaced by a bijectively-equivalent representation — a per-token normalizing flow whose layer weights are amortized as a low-rank function of the backbone vector z_i — giving an exact change-of-variables log-likelihood evaluable in one forward pass while preserving multimodal expressivity (the property the diffusion head bought).","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved continuous-token AR paper questions the shared inherited assumption that the per-token conditional distribution must be modeled by a SEPARATE generative head (diffusion / flow) bolted onto the backbone, rather than the backbone's own conditioning vector directly parameterizing an evaluable density (subtractive — names the unasked question without prescribing the replacement).","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by relocating the locus where the per-token density is enforced: instead of the assumed locus (a standalone iterative head trained by a denoising loss), the density is read off the overlooked locus the field treated as a mere conditioning summary — the backbone vector z_i itself — and we give the mechanistic account (z_i already determines the diffusion head's score field at every noise level, so it is sufficient to parameterize the density directly), demonstrating the separate-head assumption was the wrong place to look.","is_anchor":false},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides a way to spend continuous-token sampling effort adaptively across positions, because without a per-token likelihood or sharpness signal there is no quantity that tells the model which tokens are near-deterministic versus genuinely multimodal (additive need exposed once the implicit-density assumption is questioned).","pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by partitioning the N token positions on the now-readable per-token differential entropy H_i = E[-log q_i] (the discriminating property the flow exposes for free) into a near-deterministic bulk drawn in one shot and a high-entropy multimodal minority given extra antithetic/importance-resampled draws, with an error decomposition bounding the FID cost of the one-shot bulk.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"autoregressive image generation with continuous (non-quantized) token representations","n_papers":49,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":26},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":14,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Fluid: Scaling Autoregressive Text-to-image Generative Models with Continuous Tokens"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"HART: Efficient Visual Generation with Hybrid Autoregressive Transformer"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"JPEG-LM: LLMs as Image Generators with Canonical Codec Representations"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Simple Guidance Mechanisms for Discrete Diffusion Models"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Generative artificial intelligence: a systematic review and applications"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Large language models (LLMs): survey, technical frameworks, and future challenges"}],"more":8},{"year":2025,"n":26,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"VTBench: Evaluating Visual Tokenizers for Autoregressive Image Generation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Improving Autoregressive Image Generation through Coarse-to-Fine Token Prediction"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"MixAR: Mixture Autoregressive Image Generation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Scalable Autoregressive Image Generation Using Mamba with Dynamic Vector Quantization"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Rethinking Discrete Tokens: Treating Them as Conditions for Continuous Autoregressive Image Synthesis"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Ming-UniVision: Joint Image Understanding and Generation with a Unified Continuous Tokenizer"}],"more":20},{"year":2026,"n":9,"papers":[{"source":"arxiv","title":"FlashAR: Efficient Post-Training Acceleration for Autoregressive Image Generation"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Underdetermined Blind Source Separation via Weighted Simplex Shrinkage Regularization and Quantum Deep Image Prior"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Accelerating Training of Autoregressive Video Generation Models via Local Optimization with Representation Continuity"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Condition Errors Refinement in Autoregressive Image Generation with Diffusion Loss"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Autoregressive Image Generation with Masked Bit Modeling"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Projected Autoregression: Autoregressive Language Generation in Continuous State Space"}],"more":3}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":12,"share":0.245},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":10,"share":0.204},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":8,"share":0.163},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":4,"share":0.082},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":4,"share":0.082},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":4,"share":0.082},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":2,"share":0.041},{"pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","count":2,"share":0.041}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"In the continuous-token autoregressive paradigm the transformer backbone emits only a single conditioning vector z_i per spatial position, and the actual per-token continuous distribution p(x_i | x_{<i}) is offloaded to a small auxiliary diffusion head that must be run as an iterative denoising loop at every one of the N positions (semanticscholar:128bf4d8d09224f2af79f51520844661a78f7b0b, openalex:W4416381181). This shifts the modeling burden entirely onto the per-token head: because z_i is a fixed-length point summary rather than a description of the conditional density, the head must re-discover the full multimodal structure of each token's distribution from scratch through tens of denoising steps, so (a) sampling a single image requires N x (denoising-steps) head evaluations and (b) the per-token log-likelihood is only available implicitly through the diffusion ELBO, so the head's distributional fit cannot be read off, compared across positions, or used to allocate generation effort (openalex:W4416381181, arxiv:2602.07022v1). The discrete paradigm avoids both because a softmax over a codebook gives an explicit, single-evaluation categorical density (semanticscholar:e0da94d77fd5261aed50b69e7d3477deac4e16a8), but pays quantization error that caps fidelity. The structural failure is that no continuous-token AR method makes the conditioning the backbone already computes carry an explicit, cheaply-evaluable description of the per-token conditional density, so the per-token sampler stays an opaque iterative head whose likelihood is implicit and whose cost is multiplicative.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416381181","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"FAR keeps MAR's continuous per-token diffusion head but reduces its inference cost (a causal variant and a lighter head schedule), accelerating the iterative denoising loop. It still treats the per-token distribution as something the head must denoise from a point conditioning vector, so the per-token density remains implicit (no explicit likelihood is exposed) and sampling is still an iterative head call per token rather than a closed-form draw."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:128bf4d8d09224f2af79f51520844661a78f7b0b","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"MixAR factorizes continuous modeling into a discrete-AR component plus a continuous conditional module so discrete tokens guide the continuous head, giving the head a more structured target. It still relies on a diffusion-style continuous head conditioned on a discretized guidance signal, so the continuous conditional density is never written in closed form and the discrete/continuous split point is hand-designed rather than derived from the backbone's own representation."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:e0da94d77fd5261aed50b69e7d3477deac4e16a8","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"DisCon treats pre-trained discrete tokens as conditions for a continuous AR model, decoupling coarse structure (discrete) from fine detail (continuous) in two stages. The continuous stage is still a masked continuous predictor conditioned on a fixed external discrete tokenizer, so it inherits a second pretrained tokenizer and never makes the continuous per-token likelihood explicit or single-evaluation."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.07022v1","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Condition-Errors-Refinement gives a theoretical account of why AR-with-diffusion-loss (an evolving per-token condition c_i) outperforms a single static condition c, and refines the conditioning errors that accumulate. It analyzes the conditioning sequence but leaves the per-token head itself an iterative diffusion sampler with an implicit density; it refines the condition, not the form of the per-token distribution."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"autoregressive image generation with continuous (non-quantized) token representations","venue":"top ML/CV (NeurIPS / ICML / ICLR / CVPR / ICCV)","time":"2026","data":["ImageNet-256/512 class-conditional","text-to-image (e.g., CC12M / MS-COCO) optional"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"generative modeling, diffusion + autoregressive transformers","preference":"both","baseline":"MAR (masked autoregressive with per-token diffusion head) and its accelerated/continuous-token successors (Fluid, FAR, DisCon, MixAR)","limitation":"continuous-token AR couples a transformer that emits one conditioning vector per position with a per-token diffusion head that must iteratively denoise the full continuous distribution, making per-step sampling slow and the per-token likelihood implicit/untractable","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"Shared central object (shared_object thread): the per-token conditional density q_i(x_i | x_{<i}) and the single backbone vector z_i in R^d that the masked-autoregressive transformer already emits at position i (in MAR/FAR z_i is exactly the vector fed to the diffusion head; openalex:W4416381181, semanticscholar:128bf4d8d09224f2af79f51520844661a78f7b0b). Every leg reads from or writes to (q_i, z_i). LEG 1 (architectural_operator_substitution / C12): we substitute the per-token generative primitive. The diffusion head is an iterative operator: to sample one token it runs T denoising steps, and its density log q_i is only implicit through the diffusion ELBO. We replace it with an amortized per-token normalizing flow f_{theta(z_i)}: R^c -> R^c (c = token latent channel dim, ~16 in MAR's VAE) mapping a fixed analytic base p_0 = N(0, I_c) to q_i, so q_i(x_i) = p_0(f_{theta(z_i)}^{-1}(x_i)) * |det J_{f^{-1}}(x_i)| by exact change of variables — a single forward evaluation gives log q_i, and a single inverse pass gives a sample (no iteration). To keep this from collapsing to a vanilla mixture-density / monolithic flow head (the regression-flagged ancestor n7), the flow is NOT a separately-trained head: its K coupling-layer weights are produced by a low-rank amortization W_k(z_i) = A_k + U_k diag(z_i) V_k (A_k,U_k,V_k learned, shared across positions; z_i the only per-position input), so the flow's entire parameterization is a function of the backbone vector — the expressivity comes from z_i being a rich high-dim conditioner (the same vector the diffusion head consumed), not from a large standalone density network. The preserved property (C12 step 3) is distributional expressivity: we prove the amortized-flow family with K>=2 affine-coupling layers is a universal approximator of continuous densities on R^c for fixed z_i, matching the diffusion head's multimodal reach, while flipping cost (iterative -> single-eval) and unlocking the explicit likelihood the diffusion primitive structurally cannot expose (C12 step 4 'unlock what the original could not'). LEG 2 (assumption_audit_and_pivot / C01): the audit lens is 'at which locus is the per-token density enforced?' The assumed locus is a separate iterative head; the overlooked locus is z_i itself. The mechanistic account (C01 step 5) is that the diffusion head's learned score s(x, tau; z_i) at every noise level tau is already a deterministic function of z_i, so z_i is a sufficient statistic for the entire conditional density — therefore a density read directly off z_i loses nothing the head had. Leg 1's working surrogate IS the demonstration that the separate-head assumption was non-binding. LEG 3 (heterogeneous_decomposition / C04): the explicit density makes the per-token differential entropy H_i = E_{q_i}[-log q_i] computable in closed form from the flow (a small Monte-Carlo over the base, or the analytic Gaussian-pushforward entropy lower bound). We characterize the distribution of H_i across the N positions (C04 step 1) — we predict it is heavy-tailed: a near-deterministic bulk (smooth regions, already-determined structure) and a multimodal minority (edges, texture-onset, object boundaries). We then apply differentiated sampling (C04 step 3): one-shot inverse-flow draw for tokens with H_i below a learned threshold gamma, and B>1 antithetic + self-normalized-importance-resampled draws for tokens above gamma, where gamma is set so a target fraction (e.g. 15%) of compute goes to the minority. An error decomposition (C04 step 4) bounds total sampling-induced FID inflation by sum over bulk of a per-token KL between the one-shot draw law and q_i, which is small exactly where H_i is small. All three legs share (q_i, z_i): leg 1 constructs the explicit q_i, leg 2 justifies reading it off z_i, leg 3 consumes H_i derived from q_i.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The three gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules because they are the same object viewed three ways: the explicit density q_i (leg 1 builds it, leg 2 licenses its locus, leg 3 spends its entropy) — evidence is that legs 2 and 3 are literally uncomputable without leg 1's artifact, so they cannot be a stapled second paper. We considered making leg 1 a closed-form mixture-of-Gaussians head (simpler, also explicit-likelihood) but rejected it: a per-token MoG is exactly the regression-flagged ancestor node n7 (vanilla MDN head) and a fixed-component MoG under-fits the sharp multimodal continuous-token distributions the diffusion head was adopted to capture, so it would lose the preserved-property argument. We also considered a consistency-distilled one-step diffusion head, but that keeps the density implicit (no readable H_i), failing legs 2 and 3 — distillation cures cost but not the locus/likelihood problem, which is the actual bottleneck.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: train the amortized-flow head on a frozen MAR backbone + VAE on ImageNet-256 and compare to the same backbone with its original per-token diffusion head, measuring (i) FID/IS, (ii) number of per-token head evaluations to generate one image, and (iii) per-token NLL on held-out tokens. If the candidate works, FID is within noise of the diffusion-head baseline while the per-token head-evaluation count drops from N*T to N (T the diffusion steps, ~50-100), and the now-readable per-token entropy H_i is the load-bearing variable: adaptive budgeting on H_i lowers FID at fixed total draws relative to uniform budgeting. Mechanism distinguisher on H_i: the negative control replaces each token's own H_i with a randomly position-permuted H_{pi(i)} while holding the total sampling budget identical, which severs the entropy-to-position correspondence; if H_i is genuinely the mechanism, this control drives FID (the downstream outcome metric) back up to the uniform-budget baseline, whereas if the gain came merely from spending more total draws, permuting H_i would leave FID unchanged. A positive control that keeps the uniform flow but adds only H_i-guided budgeting should recover most of the adaptive-sampling FID improvement, identifying H_i as the sufficient driver.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416381181","delta":"FAR keeps the per-token diffusion head and reduces its iteration constant; we remove the iterative head entirely by constructing an amortized normalizing-flow primitive with an EXACT closed-form per-token log-likelihood (single evaluation), which FAR's method never produces."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:128bf4d8d09224f2af79f51520844661a78f7b0b","delta":"MixAR factorizes continuous modeling into a discrete-AR guide plus a continuous head and still leaves the continuous conditional density implicit; we expose an explicit per-token density read directly off the existing backbone vector with no second discrete tokenizer, and derive a per-token entropy MixAR has no access to."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:e0da94d77fd5261aed50b69e7d3477deac4e16a8","delta":"DisCon conditions a continuous head on a pretrained discrete tokenizer in two stages; we eliminate the auxiliary tokenizer and the separate head, proving the backbone vector alone is a sufficient statistic for the per-token density (a locus claim DisCon does not make)."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.07022v1","delta":"Condition-Errors-Refinement analyzes the evolving per-token condition c_i but keeps the head an iterative diffusion sampler with implicit likelihood; we change the FORM of the per-token distribution to an exact-likelihood flow and use its entropy for adaptive sampling, neither of which their analysis touches."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4416381181","what_step_was_missed":"FAR accelerates the per-token diffusion head but treats the head as a generative module that must be sampled iteratively; to already contain our contribution it would have needed to construct an amortized invertible map whose weights are a low-rank function of the backbone vector z_i and prove that this flow family is a universal density approximator at fixed z_i (the preserved-expressivity result) — that construction, which turns the implicit ELBO density into an exact single-evaluation change-of-variables likelihood and exposes a closed-form per-token entropy, is the step they did not take."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":343,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"No hard floor fired: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict is borderline (no entry is 'triggered', no Reject lesson marked candidate_match: yes); anti_pattern_check matched audit_decomp_operator but mitigation_substantively_delivered=true (operator-leg isolated under uniform sampling, decomposition-leg isolated by the uniform-flow+H_i positive control and the permuted-entropy negative control); paper_pointed_threat=no_threat_found. The two borderline findings both sit on the C01 (assumption_audit_and_pivot) leg, which is the SUPPORTING leg, not the load-bearing mechanism — the headline artifact is the C12 explicit-likelihood flow (recipe_application=applied) and the C04 entropy-adaptive sampling (applied). Per the soft-judgment heuristic 'default to advance when only one check is borderline and it is in a non-load-bearing aspect', and because recipe_application_check is borderline (not bypassed), advance is correct with the C01 novelty-boundary concern surfaced for Phase 4 to fold into reviewer_concerns_and_responses.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved continuous-token AR leaf exposes an explicit, single-evaluation per-token conditional density: the per-token distribution is only reachable through an iterative diffusion/denoising head, so a token's likelihood cannot be read off, compared across positions, or used to decide where to spend sampling effort (additive need — phrased as the missing outcome, not a prescribed parametric form).","main_pattern":"architectural_operator_substitution","sub_pattern":"C12 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is a substitution that is mechanically valid but whose payoff is absent or unverified: authors swap the operator but prove preservation with a borrowed or trivial argument that exposes no new structure, or claim the property the new slot was supposed to buy without delivering/measuring it. A diagnostic tell is validation on a proxy (throughput instead of accuracy, toy-scale, no matched baseline).","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Proving the substitute operator preserves universal approximation via a trivial adaptation of known proofs, while never connecting that result to the practical advantage (e.g. sparsification) that motivated the swap, makes the contribution read as incremental.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The universality proof (core_mechanism_steps step 4) composes the standard coupling-flow universality result with low-rank-amortization surjectivity, so it risks reading as a trivial adaptation — but the candidate explicitly connects it to the motivating advantage (the exact single-eval likelihood and free per-token entropy the diffusion head structurally cannot expose), which is the connection this lesson says is missing, pulling it back from 'yes'."},{"lesson_quoted":"A training-time re-parameterization that yields only marginal accuracy gains at higher training cost, without strong matched-baseline comparisons, reads as added overhead rather than as an insight.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The headline claim is not an accuracy gain but a cost flip (N*T head-evals -> N) at FID parity plus an unlocked capability (readable likelihood/entropy), measured against a matched MAR/FAR backbone baseline (falsification_prediction), so the 'marginal gain at higher cost' failure does not apply."},{"lesson_quoted":"Rewiring the dependency chain and reporting only throughput/speedup while omitting accuracy validation at scale leaves the essential preserved-property claim unverified.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"falsification_prediction reports FID/IS and held-out per-token NLL at ImageNet-256 scale alongside the head-eval count, so the preserved-expressivity claim is validated head-on rather than via a throughput proxy."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved continuous-token AR paper questions the shared inherited assumption that the per-token conditional distribution must be modeled by a SEPARATE generative head (diffusion / flow) bolted onto the backbone, rather than the backbone's own conditioning vector directly parameterizing an evaluable density (subtractive — names the unasked question without prescribing the replacement).","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is a successful relocation that is demonstrated but not adversarially closed (beats a fixed baseline but is never stress-tested against an informed adversary at the new locus), or a novelty-boundary collapse where the 'new' locus turns out already used by prior work, or offering only a demonstration with no mechanistic account of why the locus carries the signal.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a relocated signal is 'stealthier' or 'harder to remove' without defeating an adaptive defender who searches the same new locus leaves the central claim unverified.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"This lesson is adversarial-security-specific (stealth/removal under an adaptive defender); the candidate's locus-shift is in a generative-modeling setting with no adversary, so there is no adaptive-defender claim to leave unverified."},{"lesson_quoted":"Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work — normalization statistics, activation-similarity losses, semantic concept triggers — collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The 'new' locus (the backbone vector z_i) is the SAME vector MAR/FAR already feed to the diffusion head, so a reviewer could argue the locus is not new at all; the candidate must (and partially does, via the sufficient-statistic account) make explicit that the novelty is reading the density DIRECTLY off z_i rather than through an iterative head, but this differentiation is argued rather than yet measured, leaving it borderline."},{"lesson_quoted":"Demonstrating the new locus only on fixed, non-adaptive or outdated baselines while omitting any account of why it works reads as a stacked pipeline of existing components rather than a principled shift.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate supplies the mechanistic account C01 step 5 demands — z_i deterministically fixes the diffusion head's score field s(x,tau;z_i) at every noise level, hence is a sufficient statistic for the conditional density — so the WHY is present, not merely a demonstration."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides a way to spend continuous-token sampling effort adaptively across positions, because without a per-token likelihood or sharpness signal there is no quantity that tells the model which tokens are near-deterministic versus genuinely multimodal (additive need exposed once the implicit-density assumption is questioned).","main_pattern":"heterogeneous_decomposition","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is treating the partition criterion itself as the contribution while leaving its value unproven — reviewers map the discriminator onto an established technique, and the scheme is rarely benchmarked against both the strongest uniform baseline and the obvious cheap alternative, or is validated in a regime where the compression/cost bottleneck does not bite.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Omitting comparison against both the strongest uniform baseline and the obvious cheap alternative (SVD/PCA, structured dropout, a natively trained smaller model) leaves reviewers unable to tell whether the partition buys anything at all.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The plan compares adaptive H_i budgeting against the strongest uniform baseline (uniform-budget sampling at matched total draws) and includes the obvious cheap alternative as the positive control (uniform flow + H_i budgeting), so the partition's marginal value is isolated."},{"lesson_quoted":"Skipping any analysis of why the heterogeneity exists — the data or value distribution that drives the partition — makes the technical novelty and the potential impact impossible to assess.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism characterizes the H_i distribution across positions (C04 step 1) and predicts its heavy-tailed shape (near-deterministic bulk vs multimodal edge/texture minority), supplying the value-distribution evidence the partition rests on."},{"lesson_quoted":"Presenting a sensitivity or redundancy proxy as the novelty invites the verdict that it rediscovers known mixed-precision or low-rank results unless it is sharply differentiated from the obvious prior criterion.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The discriminating property here (per-token differential entropy H_i) is not presented as the standalone novelty — it is only computable because leg 1 exposes the explicit density, so it is differentiated by construction from any pre-existing magnitude/sensitivity proxy that prior continuous-token work could have used."}],"verdict":"clear"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"Two of three entries are clear (C12 anchor and C04 decomposition). The aggregate is borderline, driven by the assumption_audit_and_pivot entry (gap 2, C01): the reject lesson 'Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work ... collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured' carries weight because the relocated locus (backbone vector z_i) is the very vector MAR/FAR already feed the diffusion head, so the novelty rests on reading the density directly off z_i and that distinction is currently argued (sufficient-statistic account) rather than empirically measured. No entry is triggered (no candidate_match: yes), so no hard floor."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved continuous-token AR leaf exposes an explicit, single-evaluation per-token conditional density: the per-token distribution is only reachable through an iterative diffusion/denoising head, so a token's likelihood cannot be read off, compared across positions, or used to decide where to spend sampling effort (additive need — phrased as the missing outcome, not a prescribed parametric form).","sub_pattern":"C12 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Within a multi-stage architecture, relocate or swap a structural slot rather than tuning weights — substitute the per-stage aggregation/representation primitive (e.g. closed-form density -> bijectively equivalent representation), anchor the substitute to a classical theorem, and accompany it with a proof that the essential property (expressivity) survives while a cost property changes.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"LEG 1 performs exactly this: it substitutes the per-stage generative primitive (iterative diffusion head -> amortized normalizing flow f_{theta(z_i)}), the substitute is a bijectively-equivalent representation giving an exact change-of-variables log q_i (C12's named 'closed-form density -> bijectively equivalent representation' primitive swap), it is anchored to the coupling-flow universal-approximation theorem (step 4), and it proves the preserved property (multimodal expressivity at fixed z_i) while flipping cost (iterative T-step -> single-eval) and unlocking the explicit likelihood the original slot structurally forbids (C12 step 4). The signature move is present, not generic.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved continuous-token AR paper questions the shared inherited assumption that the per-token conditional distribution must be modeled by a SEPARATE generative head (diffusion / flow) bolted onto the backbone, rather than the backbone's own conditioning vector directly parameterizing an evaluable density (subtractive — names the unasked question without prescribing the replacement).","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Audit the representational locus at which a property is presumed enforced and RELOCATE it to a locus the field treated as irrelevant or invariant ('relocate the signal', 're-anchor enforcement'), then supply a mechanistic account of WHY the new locus carries the signal — an invariance proof, impossibility bound, or root-cause decomposition — not merely evidence that it does.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"LEG 2 performs the abstract locus relocation (density enforced at a separate iterative head -> density read off the backbone vector z_i, the locus treated as a mere conditioning summary) and supplies the C01-step-5 mechanistic account (z_i deterministically fixes the diffusion head's score field at every noise level, so z_i is a sufficient statistic for the full conditional density). The generic audit-and-relocate-with-WHY move is genuinely instantiated. The reservation: C01's distinctive cluster signature is adversarial/security-locus-shift validated by attack-success/detection rates under an adaptive adversary; here the move lands in a generative-modeling setting with no adversary, so the cluster's security-specific sharpness is approximated by the parent-level audit move rather than reproduced verbatim. The locus-shift verb and the mechanistic WHY are present, so this is applied-but-imperfect-fit rather than bypassed.","verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides a way to spend continuous-token sampling effort adaptively across positions, because without a per-token likelihood or sharpness signal there is no quantity that tells the model which tokens are near-deterministic versus genuinely multimodal (additive need exposed once the implicit-density assumption is questioned).","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Discriminate the components of an over-provisioned resource by a magnitude/sensitivity/influence/redundancy criterion into a high-impact minority and a near-redundant bulk, apply a tailored operation to each (protect the minority, aggressively lossy-compress the bulk), and make an error/sensitivity decomposition that bounds how the differentiated treatment recovers the objective the load-bearing artifact.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"LEG 3 performs this: it partitions the N token positions (the resource) by the discriminating property H_i (per-token differential entropy) into a near-deterministic bulk and a multimodal high-entropy minority, applies a tailored operation to each (single one-shot inverse-flow draw for the bulk, B=4 antithetic+SNIR draws for the minority), and supplies the error decomposition (C04 step 4) bounding sampling-induced FID inflation by a sum of per-token KL over the bulk that is small exactly where H_i is small. The signature decomposition-with-error-bound move is present.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"C12 and C04 entries are applied (the swap-the-primitive and discriminate-and-bound-the-treatment signature moves both appear concretely in core_mechanism). The aggregate is borderline because the C01 entry is borderline: the abstract locus-relocation + mechanistic-WHY move IS instantiated, but C01's distinctive cluster move is security/adversarial-locus-shift and the candidate applies it in a non-adversarial generative-modeling setting, so the cluster fit is imperfect rather than a clean signature match. It is not bypassed (the relocation verb and sufficient-statistic account are genuinely present)."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["architectural_operator_substitution","assumption_audit_and_pivot","heterogeneous_decomposition"],"matched_pattern_id":"audit_decomp_operator","required_mitigation_quoted":"The operator's expressivity gain must be demonstrated on homogeneous data (where decomposition is unnecessary), and the decomposition's separate effect must be demonstrated on heterogeneous data with the operator held fixed. Each leg's contribution must be independently identifiable.","mitigation_substantively_delivered":"true","reasoning":"The core_mechanism and its controls deliver the artifact the mitigation names at the mechanism level: the operator leg (amortized flow) is evaluated under UNIFORM sampling against the diffusion-head baseline at matched backbone (falsification_prediction (i)-(iii)), isolating the substitution's FID/likelihood gain with no decomposition involved; the decomposition leg is isolated by the positive control 'uniform flow + only H_i-guided budgeting' (core_mechanism_steps step 10) which holds the operator fixed and varies only the adaptive partition, plus the negative control (position-permuted H_{pi(i)}) that severs the entropy-to-position link — so each leg's contribution is independently identifiable rather than over-attributed to one change."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"no_threat_found","threat_source":"n/a","subsumption_argument":null,"addressable_via":null}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism / differentiation_from_lit","issue":"gap_closure_reject_check C01 borderline lesson 'Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work ... collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured', and recipe_application_check C01 borderline (security-specific cluster applied in a non-adversarial setting).","fix_direction":"Phase 4 (not a blocking revision): make the locus-novelty explicit and measurable rather than only argued — add a concrete experiment/argument that the contribution is reading the density DIRECTLY off z_i in a single evaluation (vs the existing iterative head that consumes the same z_i), e.g. a measured comparison of likelihood/entropy availability and per-token compute that prior work using z_i as a conditioning summary cannot produce, so the 'z_i is not a new locus' objection is closed with evidence. Surface this as a reviewer_concern_and_response in Phase 4 rather than re-routing to Phase 3.3, since the C12/C04 load-bearing legs are clean and the verdict is advance."}],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Closed-Form Continuous Tokens: Replacing the Per-Token Diffusion Head with an Amortized Flow\n\n**Method.** Amortized Flow Head (AFH)\n\n## Motivation\nModern autoregressive (AR) image generators that work with continuous (un-quantized) tokens, like MAR (Masked Autoregressive) and FAR (Fast Autoregressive), have a hidden cost. The main transformer produces just one summary vector $z_{i}$ for each image position, and then a small separate network — a diffusion head — has to take that summary and slowly 'denoise' its way to the actual distribution of that token, over tens of small steps. Two problems follow. First, generating one image costs the number of positions times the number of denoising steps, so it is slow in a way that just making the head faster (which FAR does) cannot fundamentally fix. Second, you can never directly read out how likely a given token value is — the probability is buried inside the iterative process — so you can't compare positions or decide where to focus effort.\n\nDiscrete-token models avoid both problems because a softmax over a fixed codebook gives an exact probability in one shot, but they pay a quality price from quantization. The real question nobody in this line has asked is: does the per-token distribution actually need its own separate iterative network at all, or does the summary vector $z_{i}$ the transformer already computes contain everything needed to write the distribution down directly?\n\nWe argue it does. The diffusion head's behavior is entirely determined by $z_{i},$ so $z_{i}$ is a sufficient summary. That makes it possible, now, to swap the iterative head for an amortized normalizing flow — an invertible transform whose settings are a simple function of $z_{i}$ — that gives the exact probability and a sample in a single step. This is timely because every recent continuous-token paper (FAR in 2025, MixAR in 2025, DisCon at ICCV 2025, a 2026 condition-error analysis) circles this same separate-iterative-head design without questioning it, while the classical flow mathematics needed to replace it is mature and cheap.\n\nWhen this gap closes, continuous-token AR gains an exact, single-evaluation likelihood (cutting sampling cost from positions-times-steps down to just positions) and, for free, a per-token 'uncertainty' number — the differential entropy — that the diffusion head structurally throws away. That number lets the model spend extra sampling effort only on the genuinely uncertain tokens, which was never possible before.\n\n## Method\n### Amortized flow head\n*Replaces the iterative diffusion head with $a z_{i}-conditioned$ invertible map giving exact single-evaluation likelihood and sampling.*\n\n1. Take a pretrained Masked Autoregressive (MAR) backbone and its frozen continuous Variational Autoencoder (VAE) tokenizer, and delete the small per-token diffusion head. In its place put a normalizing flow over the roughly 16-dimensional token latent: 4 affine-coupling layers. Each coupling layer splits the channels into two halves, keeps one half unchanged, and rescales-and-shifts the other half by amounts (a scale and a shift) computed by a small 2-layer network; a fixed channel permutation between layers makes sure every channel eventually gets transformed. The key twist: that small network's weights are not learned directly but are produced, for each image position, from the backbone's per-position summary vector $z_{i}$ through a low-rank formula (a shared base matrix plus a rank-32 correction driven by $z_{i}).$ The starting distribution is a standard Gaussian.\n\n*Low-rank amortization of the k-th coupling layer's weights from the backbone vector $z_{i}: A_{k}, U_{k}, V_{k}$ are shared across positions and $z_{i}$ is the only per-position input, so the flow's whole parameterization is a function of $z_{i}$ rather than a separately trained head.*\n$$ W_k(z_i) = A_k + U_k\\,\\mathrm{diag}(z_i)\\,V_k \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Tying the whole flow to $z_{i}$ means the head is not a separate trained network but a readout of the vector the transformer already produced, which is what lets the iterative head disappear and prevents a fallback to a weak mixture-of-Gaussians head.\n2. To get the probability of a token value, run it backwards through the 4 layers (each layer is exactly invertible: undo the shift then the scale) until you reach the corresponding point under the standard Gaussian, read off the Gaussian's log-probability there, and add a correction term (the volume-change term), which for these layers is just the sum of the scale amounts the layers applied. That single backward pass gives the exact log-probability in one shot. To draw a sample instead, take one Gaussian sample and run it forwards through the same layers once. There is no denoising loop in either direction.\n\n*The exact change-of-variables per-token log-density: the flow pushes a fixed Gaussian base $p_{0}$ through the $z_{i}-conditioned$ invertible map f, so $log q_{i}$ is read in a single evaluation with no denoising loop.*\n$$ \\log q_i(x_i) = \\log p_0\\!\\left(f_{\\theta(z_i)}^{-1}(x_i)\\right) + \\log\\left|\\det J_{f_{\\theta(z_i)}^{-1}}(x_i)\\right| \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A normalizing flow is invertible, so the probability and a sample both come out in one pass — that is exactly the explicit, single-evaluation density the diffusion head could not give.\n3. Train by swapping the original diffusion training loss for the flow's exact negative log-likelihood: for every token, this is minus the log-probability you just defined, added up over all positions. Leave everything else about MAR untouched — the same transformer, the same masking pattern, the same other loss terms. Gradients pass through the exact-probability computation back into both the transformer and the shared weight-generating matrices. A practical option is to first freeze the transformer and train only the weight-generating matrices, then unfreeze and fine-tune everything together.\n\n*Training objective: the per-token exact negative log-likelihood replaces MAR's diffusion-loss term, while the transformer's masked-AR forward pass and all other losses are kept identical.*\n$$ \\mathcal{L} = -\\sum_{i} \\left[\\log p_0\\!\\left(f^{-1}(x_i)\\right) + \\log\\left|\\det J_{f^{-1}}(x_i)\\right|\\right] \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Changing only the head's loss isolates the swap, so any change in image quality can be attributed to the new head rather than to other pipeline edits.\n\n### Preserved-expressivity proof\n*Guarantees the cheap flow head matches the diffusion head's multimodal reach at fixed $z_{i}.$*\n\n4. Prove that this cheap flow head is as expressive as it needs to be: show that with at least 2 coupling layers the family of flows can approximate any continuous distribution on the token latent space for a fixed backbone vector. The proof has two parts — first cite the known result that stacked affine-coupling flows are universal density approximators, then show that generating the layer weights from the backbone vector by the low-rank formula does not shrink that ability, because for a fixed backbone vector the low-rank generator can still reach the weights the universality result needs. This guarantees you are not trading the diffusion head's ability to capture multi-peaked distributions for speed.\n   - _Why_: This guarantees the cheap new head is at least as expressive as the diffusion head it replaces, so we are not trading speed for quality.\n\n### Entropy-adaptive sampling\n*Uses the now-readable per-token entropy to spend extra draws only on genuinely multimodal positions, with an error bound.*\n\n5. Using the trained flow, compute each token's uncertainty as its differential entropy: draw 8 samples for that position and average their negative log-probabilities; as a stable cross-check, use the exact identity that the entropy equals a constant plus the average volume-change term over Gaussian samples. Do this across a held-out set of generations and plot how this per-token uncertainty is distributed over all positions, checking the expectation that it has a heavy tail — most tokens nearly certain, a minority (edges, texture, object boundaries) genuinely multi-peaked.\n\n*The per-token differential entropy, computable in closed form from the flow (a small Monte-Carlo over the base, or the analytic Gaussian-pushforward bound); it is the sharpness signal the diffusion head's implicit density could never expose.*\n$$ H_i = \\mathbb{E}_{q_i}\\!\\left[-\\log q_i(x_i)\\right] \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Because the likelihood is now explicit, entropy is free to compute, and it directly tells you which tokens are easy and which are hard — a signal the diffusion head never exposed.\n6. Spend the sampling budget where it matters. Pick one cutoff so that about 15% of positions count as high-uncertainty (set it as the value the per-token uncertainty exceeds 15% of the time on held-out data). Tokens below the cutoff are drawn just once; tokens above it get 4 draws using mirrored Gaussian pairs (a sample and its negative) for lower variance, then keep one draw by a re-weighting that slightly favors the more probable modes. An error analysis shows the extra error from single-shotting the easy majority is bounded by a per-token mismatch term that is small precisely where uncertainty is low. 【author decision: whether the single cutoff should instead vary by generation step or class label — here it is one global cutoff because the heavy-tailed uncertainty pattern is predicted globally.】\n\n*Entropy-thresholded sampling budget: tokens below threshold $\\gamma $ get one inverse-flow draw, tokens above $\\gamma $ get B antithetic / importance-resampled draws, with $\\gamma $ set so a target fraction of compute goes to the high-entropy minority.*\n$$ B_i = \\begin{cases} 1 & H_i \\leq \\gamma \\\\ B & H_i > \\gamma \\end{cases} \\tag{5} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Spending extra draws only where the distribution is genuinely multimodal puts compute where it actually reduces error, instead of treating every position the same.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 闭式连续 token：用 amortized flow 替换逐 token 扩散头\n\n**方法名称.** Amortized Flow Head (AFH)\n\n## 研究动机\n现在用连续（未量化）token 的自回归（AR）图像生成模型，比如 MAR（Masked Autoregressive）和 FAR（Fast Autoregressive），有一个隐藏的代价。主干 transformer 对每个图像位置只产生一个概括向量 $z_{i}$，然后由一个单独的小网络——扩散头（diffusion head）——拿着这个概括，经过几十个小步骤慢慢“去噪”，才还原出该 token 的真实分布。由此带来两个问题。其一，生成一张图的代价是位置数乘以去噪步数，所以慢得很本质，单纯把这个 head 做快（FAR 就是这么做的）并不能从根本上解决。其二，你永远无法直接读出某个 token 取某个值的概率——概率被埋在迭代过程里——因此你既不能在不同位置间比较，也无法决定把算力花在哪里。\n\n离散 token 模型能同时避开这两个问题，因为在固定 codebook 上做 softmax 一步就能给出精确概率，但它要为量化付出质量代价。这条线上一直没人问的真正问题是：逐 token 的分布真的需要它自己那个单独的迭代网络吗？还是说 transformer 早就算出来的概括向量 $z_{i}$ 已经包含了直接写出该分布所需的一切？\n\n我们认为确实如此。扩散头的行为完全由 $z_{i}$ 决定，所以 $z_{i}$ 是一个充分概括。这使得现在可以把迭代 head 换成一个 amortized normalizing flow——一种可逆变换，其参数设定是 $z_{i}$ 的简单函数——它一步就能给出精确概率和一个样本。这件事正当其时，因为最近每一篇连续 token 的工作（2025 的 FAR、2025 的 MixAR、ICCV 2025 的 DisCon、2026 的一篇 condition-error 分析）都绕着这个“单独迭代 head”的设计打转却不去质疑它，而替换它所需的经典 flow 数学早已成熟且计算廉价。\n\n这个 gap 一旦填上，连续 token 的 AR 就获得了精确的、单次求值的似然（把采样代价从“位置数乘步数”降到只剩“位置数”），并且免费得到一个逐 token 的“不确定度”数值——微分熵——这是扩散头在结构上丢掉的。有了这个数值，模型就能只在真正不确定的 token 上多花采样力气，这在以前根本做不到。\n\n## 方法\n### Amortized flow head\n*用以 $z_{i}$ 为条件的可逆映射替换迭代扩散头，实现精确的单次求值似然与采样。*\n\n1. 拿一个预训练好的 Masked Autoregressive (MAR) 主干和它冻结的连续 Variational Autoencoder (VAE) tokenizer，删掉那个逐 token 的小扩散头。在原位放一个作用于约 16 维 token latent 的 normalizing flow：4 个 affine-coupling 层。每个 coupling 层把通道分成两半，一半保持不变，另一半按一个 scale 和一个 shift 做缩放与平移，而这两个量由一个 2 层小网络算出；层与层之间用一个固定的通道置换，确保每个通道最终都会被变换。关键之处在于：这个小网络的权重不是直接学的，而是对每个图像位置，由主干的逐位置概括向量 $z_{i}$ 通过一个低秩公式生成（一个共享的基矩阵，加上一个由 $z_{i}$ 驱动的秩为 32 的修正）。基分布是标准高斯。\n\n*第 k 个 coupling 层权重由 backbone 向量 $z_{i}$ 做低秩 amortize：$A_{k}$、$U_{k}$、$V_{k}$ 在所有位置共享，$z_{i}$ 是唯一的逐位置输入，因此 flow 的整套参数化都是 $z_{i}$ 的函数，而非一个单独训练的 head。*\n$$ W_k(z_i) = A_k + U_k\\,\\mathrm{diag}(z_i)\\,V_k \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 把整个 flow 都系在 $z_{i}$ 上，意味着这个 head 不是一个单独训练的网络，而是对 transformer 已经产出的向量的读出，这正是让迭代 head 消失、并避免退回到弱的 mixture-of-Gaussians head 的关键。\n2. 要得到某个 token 取值的概率，就把它沿 4 个层反向跑（每层都精确可逆：先撤销 shift 再撤销 scale），直到回到标准高斯下对应的点，在那里读出高斯的对数概率，再加上一个修正项（体积变化项）——对这些层而言它就是各层施加的 scale 量之和。这一次反向跑就一步给出精确的对数概率。若要采样，则取一个高斯样本，沿同样的层正向跑一次即可。两个方向都没有去噪循环。\n\n*逐 token 的精确变量替换对数密度：flow 把固定高斯基分布 $p_{0}$ 经由以 $z_{i}$ 为条件的可逆映射 f 推前，因此 $log q_{i}$ 一次前向即可读出，无需任何去噪迭代。*\n$$ \\log q_i(x_i) = \\log p_0\\!\\left(f_{\\theta(z_i)}^{-1}(x_i)\\right) + \\log\\left|\\det J_{f_{\\theta(z_i)}^{-1}}(x_i)\\right| \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: normalizing flow 是可逆的，所以概率和样本都能一次得到——这正是扩散头给不出的、显式且单次求值的密度。\n3. 训练时把原来的扩散训练损失换成 flow 的精确负对数似然：对每个 token，它就是你刚定义的对数概率取负，再对所有位置求和。MAR 的其他部分一律不动——同一个 transformer、同样的 masking 方式、同样的其他损失项。梯度会穿过精确概率的计算，回传到 transformer 和那组共享的权重生成矩阵。一个实用做法是先冻结 transformer、只训练权重生成矩阵，然后再解冻、整体一起微调。\n\n*训练目标：用逐 token 的精确负对数似然替换 MAR 的扩散损失项，同时 transformer 的 masked-AR 前向以及其他所有损失保持不变。*\n$$ \\mathcal{L} = -\\sum_{i} \\left[\\log p_0\\!\\left(f^{-1}(x_i)\\right) + \\log\\left|\\det J_{f^{-1}}(x_i)\\right|\\right] \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 只改 head 的损失就把这次替换隔离出来，于是图像质量的任何变化都能归因于新 head，而非其他流程改动。\n\n### 表达力保持证明\n*保证廉价的 flow head 在固定 $z_{i}$ 下达到扩散头的多峰表达力。*\n\n4. 证明这个廉价的 flow head 在表达力上够用：说明在至少 2 个 coupling 层下，这族 flow 对固定的 backbone 向量能逼近 token latent 空间上的任意连续分布。证明分两步——先引用已知结论：堆叠的 affine-coupling flow 是万能密度逼近器；再说明用低秩公式从 backbone 向量生成层权重并不会削弱这种能力，因为对固定的 backbone 向量，低秩生成器仍能达到万能逼近所需的权重。这样就保证你没有为了速度而牺牲扩散头刻画多峰分布的能力。\n   - _为什么_: 这保证了这个廉价的新 head 至少和它替换掉的扩散头一样有表达力，所以我们不是在拿质量换速度。\n\n### 熵自适应采样\n*用现在可读的逐 token 熵，只在真正多峰的位置多采样，并配有误差界。*\n\n5. 用训练好的 flow，把每个 token 的不确定度算成它的微分熵：对该位置采 8 个样本，取它们负对数概率的平均；作为稳定的交叉验证，用精确恒等式——熵等于一个常数加上对高斯样本求平均的体积变化项。在一批留出的生成结果上这么做，并画出这个逐 token 不确定度在所有位置上的分布，验证它是否如预期呈重尾：多数 token 近乎确定，少数（边缘、纹理、物体边界）真正多峰。\n\n*逐 token 的微分熵，可由 flow 闭式计算（在基分布上做小规模 Monte-Carlo，或用高斯推前的解析下界）；它正是扩散头的隐式密度无法暴露的锐度信号。*\n$$ H_i = \\mathbb{E}_{q_i}\\!\\left[-\\log q_i(x_i)\\right] \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 因为似然现在是显式的，熵可以免费算出来，它直接告诉你哪些 token 容易、哪些难——这是扩散头从未暴露过的信号。\n6. 把采样预算花在要紧处。选一个阈值，使约 15% 的位置算作高不确定（设为：在留出数据上逐 token 不确定度有 15% 的概率超过的那个值）。低于阈值的 token 只采一次；高于阈值的 token 采 4 次，用镜像高斯对（一个样本和它的相反数）来降方差，再通过一个略微偏向更可能模式的重加权保留一个样本。误差分析表明，对容易的大多数只采一次所带来的额外误差，被一个逐 token 的失配项所约束，而该项恰好在不确定度低处也小。【作者需决定：这个单一阈值是否应改为随生成步或类别变化——此处用一个全局阈值，因为重尾的不确定度规律是按全局预测的。】\n\n*按熵阈值分配采样预算：低于阈值 $\\gamma $ 的 token 只做一次 inverse-flow 采样，高于 $\\gamma $ 的 token 做 B 次对偶 / 重要性重采样，$\\gamma $ 的设定使目标比例的算力流向高熵少数 token。*\n$$ B_i = \\begin{cases} 1 & H_i \\leq \\gamma \\\\ B & H_i > \\gamma \\end{cases} \\tag{5} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 只在分布真正多峰处多采样，把算力花在真正能降低误差的地方，而不是对每个位置一视同仁。\n\n"},{"id":"85","run_dir":"run_prompt85_tns","index":85,"title":"Tuning the Forcing Rate: Finite-Confidence Cost of Sticky Track-and-Stop's Exploration Schedule","title_zh":"调节强制探索率：Sticky Track-and-Stop 探索调度的有限置信度代价","method_name":"Gap-Aware Forcing Schedule (GAFS)","hook":"Sticky Track-and-Stop's forced-exploration rate is set only to be fast enough for asymptotic consistency, yet at any fixed confidence that same rate is the dominant lever on how many extra samples the burn-in wastes — and the asymptotically-blessed setting is provably the wrong one for finite delta. We characterize a delta-indexed lower bound on the forcing-induced overhead that the whole asymptotically-tuned forcing class must pay, then construct a gap- and confidence-aware forcing schedule that provably undercuts it while keeping the same delta -> 0 optimality.","anchor_pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","anchor_pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","domain_category":"Learning Theory & Statistics","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes how the forced-exploration / 'sticky' schedule (the rate at which sticky T&S forces under-sampled arms) trades off against the non-asymptotic overhead — the forcing rate is set asymptotically (only fast enough to guarantee consistency in the limit) and its effect on the finite-confidence stopping time is unquantified.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by treating the forcing schedule as the budgeted acquisition rule whose load-bearing assumption ('the forcing rate need only diverge fast enough for asymptotic consistency') is relaxed: we derive a delta-indexed lower bound on the forcing-induced overhead any schedule in that asymptotic class must pay, then re-derive a strictly-better finite-confidence sample-complexity certificate for a confidence- and gap-aware forcing rate g(delta, mu_hat) — the C11 relax-the-crutch-then-rebound-the-guarantee move with a matching lower bound.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes the burn-in regime of plug-in maximin allocation tracking: the early phase in which the tracked allocation, being computed from noisy empirical means, differs from the oracle allocation and thereby wastes samples — none ties the size of this overhead to a measurable property of the instance or of the empirical-allocation trajectory.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by auditing the assumption baked into the SAME forcing rule that the burn-in overhead is an instance-independent additive constant, and reframing it as a measurable stopping-quantity: we bind the burn-in overhead to the realized trajectory deficit D_t (cumulative L1 distance between the plug-in maximin allocation and the oracle allocation), proving the overhead is the forcing rate times the integral of D_t over the burn-in — so the practitioner can read the overhead off the trajectory and feed it back into g(delta, mu_hat).","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"pure-exploration multi-armed bandits / best-arm identification (fixed-confidence), Track-and-Stop family","n_papers":43,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":22},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":9}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":10,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Preference-based Pure Exploration"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Optimal Thresholding Linear Bandit"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Pure Exploration for Constrained Best Mixed Arm Identification with a Fixed Budget"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"UB3: Fixed Budget Best Beam Identification in mmWave Massive MISO via Pure Exploration Unimodal Bandits"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Interactively Learning the User's Utility for Best-Arm Identification in Multi-Objective Multi-Armed Bandits"},{"source":"openalex","title":"The Digital Transformation in Health: How AI Can Improve the Performance of Health Systems"}],"more":4},{"year":2025,"n":25,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Semi-overlapping Multi-bandit Best Arm Identification for Sequential Support Network Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Service Placement Using Distributed Pure Exploration in Linear Bandits"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"The Batch Complexity of Bandit Pure Exploration"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Dual-Directed Algorithm Design for Efficient Pure Exploration"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"On the problem of Best Arm Retention"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Variational Quantum Optimization with Continuous Bandits"}],"more":19},{"year":2026,"n":9,"papers":[{"source":"arxiv","title":"Learning with a Budget: Identifying the Best Arm with Resource Constraints"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Nearly Optimal Best Arm Identification for Semiparametric Bandits"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Fixed-Budget Constrained Best Arm Identification in Grouped Bandits"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Best Arm Identification in Generalized Linear Bandits via Hybrid Feedback"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"On The Complexity of Best-Arm Identification in Non-Stationary Linear Bandits"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Tree-Guided Identify-Then-Exploit: A Unified Framework of Best Arm Identification and Regret Minimization for Dueling Bandits"}],"more":3}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":18,"share":0.419},{"pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","count":11,"share":0.256},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":5,"share":0.116},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":5,"share":0.116},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":4,"share":0.093},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":4,"share":0.093},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":2,"share":0.047},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":2,"share":0.047}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"The Track-and-Stop (T&S) family — including its sticky / forced-exploration variant and the more recent dual-directed and top-two generalizations (semanticscholar:ac04baaad0b7bd277e4f3ba23ba6a3c68b8f088a) — is proven optimal only ASYMPTOTICALLY: as the confidence parameter delta -> 0 the expected stopping time E[tau] divided by the characteristic-time lower bound T*(mu)*log(1/delta) tends to 1. At any FIXED, practically-relevant delta the realized stopping time can substantially exceed this leading term because the plug-in maximin allocation that T&S tracks is computed from empirical means that are themselves still noisy, so there is a burn-in phase during which the tracked allocation is the WRONG allocation, and the magnitude of this burn-in (the lower-order, delta-independent additive term in E[tau]) has no instance-dependent characterization. The closest existing non-asymptotic result is confined to the much simpler 1-identification (threshold) query (openalex:W4415237732), whose authors explicitly note that the non-asymptotic analysis of the general T&S stopping/sampling rule remains open; batch-complexity work (semanticscholar:53b5d4bb1cb8c9ab00c071c3da6d7028f2c7cadd) likewise gives only instance-dependent ASYMPTOTIC batch lower bounds. Concretely, no retrieved method produces an instance-dependent upper bound on E[tau] valid at all delta whose lower-order term is tied to a measurable property of the empirical-allocation trajectory, so practitioners cannot predict how many samples a finite-confidence T&S run will actually consume nor which instances suffer the worst non-asymptotic overhead.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415237732","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Near Optimal Non-asymptotic Sample Complexity of 1-Identification: designs the SEE algorithm and proves a near-tight non-asymptotic (all-delta) sample-complexity bound for the 1-identification query, which Degenne & Koolen 2019 had only solved asymptotically. The residue is that the result is specific to the single-threshold 1-identification query and a purpose-built explore-then-exploit algorithm; it does NOT analyze the actual T&S sampling-plus-stopping rule (plug-in maximin tracking + GLR stopping) for full best-arm identification, and gives no instance-dependent characterization of the burn-in / lower-order term that the tracked-allocation noise induces. [residue is abstract-level: anchor fulltext unfetchable]"},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:ac04baaad0b7bd277e4f3ba23ba6a3c68b8f088a","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Dual-Directed Algorithm Design unifies top-two and T&S-style allocation for general pure-exploration goals via a maximin/dual optimization and proves asymptotic optimality as the error vanishes. The residue is that the optimality is established only in the delta -> 0 limit; the framework quantifies neither the finite-confidence overhead of the dual-directed allocation nor how fast the plug-in dual converges to the oracle dual, so the non-asymptotic constant is uncharacterized."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:53b5d4bb1cb8c9ab00c071c3da6d7028f2c7cadd","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"The Batch Complexity of Bandit Pure Exploration gives an instance-dependent lower bound on the number of batches (rounds of adaptivity) any sample-efficient pure-exploration algorithm needs, plus a matching batched algorithm. The residue is that the batch and sample bounds are asymptotic / leading-order in 1/delta; the additive non-asymptotic overhead within a batch — the cost of acting on still-noisy empirical allocations early in the run — is not isolated."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"pure-exploration multi-armed bandits / best-arm identification (fixed-confidence), Track-and-Stop family","venue":"COLT / NeurIPS / ICML / ALT (learning-theory track)","time":"2026","data":["synthetic Gaussian / Bernoulli bandit instances (canonical for sample-complexity validation)","no real dataset required; theory-first"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"bandit theory / sequential analysis / concentration inequalities","preference":"theory","baseline":"Track-and-Stop (Garivier & Kaufmann 2016) and its sticky / forced-exploration variant (Degenne, Koolen & Menard 2019); top-two and dual-directed designs (semanticscholar:ac04baaad0b7bd277e4f3ba23ba6a3c68b8f088a)","limitation":"T&S-family guarantees are asymptotic (delta -> 0): the optimality constant is proven in the vanishing-error limit, but the finite-confidence (non-asymptotic) sample complexity, including the second-order / lower-order terms and the burn-in time before the asymptotic regime is entered, is not characterized.","contribution_type":"theory","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"Central shared object (coherence thread = shared_object): the forced-exploration schedule of sticky Track-and-Stop and the empirical-allocation trajectory it perturbs. Setup, all computable: run the standard sticky-T&S rule on a K-arm exponential-family bandit with means mu and unique best arm a*; at round t let mu_hat_t be the empirical means, w*(mu_hat_t) in the simplex be the plug-in maximin (lower-bound) allocation T&S tracks, w*(mu) the oracle allocation, and N_t the pull-count vector. The forcing rule pulls argmin_a N_t(a) whenever some N_t(a) < f(t) for a forcing-floor function f (the 'forcing rate'); Degenne-Koolen require only f(t) = o(t) and f(t) -> infinity (canonically f(t) ~ sqrt(t)). Define the trajectory deficit D_t = || w*(mu_hat_t) - w*(mu) ||_1 (an internal, computable readout — both vectors are simplex points, no external oracle at run time; w*(mu) is the population maximin used only in the analysis). ANCHOR LEG (gap 1, C11 relax-and-rebound): the forcing rate f is the budgeted acquisition rule's structural crutch; its only published justification is asymptotic consistency, so it is over-provisioned at finite delta — every forced pull on a confirmed-suboptimal arm is a sample the GLR stopping rule did not request. We define the forcing-induced overhead O(delta) = E[tau_force,delta] - E[tau_noforce,delta] where tau_noforce is the (hypothetical) stopping time of the same tracking+GLR rule with forcing removed, and prove a delta-indexed LOWER bound: for any f in the asymptotic class, O(delta) >= c1 * sum_a f(T*(mu) log(1/delta)) up to the round at which forcing deactivates, i.e. the standard sqrt(t)-style rate forces Theta(sqrt(T* log(1/delta))) wasted pulls per arm — a term invisible to the asymptotic ratio (it is o(log(1/delta))) yet dominant at practical delta. We then CONSTRUCT a confidence- and gap-aware schedule g(delta, mu_hat_t) = beta * sqrt( log(1/delta) ) * h(Delta_hat_min,t, D_t) where Delta_hat_min,t is the empirical smallest gap, h is decreasing in Delta_hat_min,t (large gaps need little forcing) and increasing in D_t (force more only while the plug-in allocation is still far from oracle), and beta>0 a single tunable constant; we prove g retains f(t)->infinity (so asymptotic optimality is preserved, no regression to the un-forced rule that loses consistency for non-unique maximizers) yet yields O_g(delta) <= O_f(delta) with strict gap exactly when Delta_min is bounded away from 0, undercutting the lower bound's worst case. ANCHOR ARTIFACT closes gap 1: a finite-delta certificate E[tau_g,delta] <= T*(mu) log(1/delta) + B_g(delta, mu) with B_g provably smaller than the asymptotically-tuned B_f, the first statement tying the forcing RATE to the finite-confidence overhead. SIBLING LEG (gap 2, C11 reframe the burn-in selection assumption): prior fixed-rate analyses treat the burn-in additive term as an instance-independent constant; we audit that and reframe it as a stopping-quantity on the trajectory deficit D_t, proving B(delta, mu) = E[ integral_0^{tau_burn} g(delta, mu_hat_t) * D_t dt ] up to constants, where tau_burn is the first time D_t stays below a threshold eps for a window. Because D_t is computable online, this both (a) makes the burn-in overhead a MEASURABLE property of the realized run, not an opaque constant, and (b) supplies exactly the signal h(.,D_t) in g consumes, so the two legs share one object: the anchor sets the rate, the sibling says which trajectory signal the rate must watch.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery because the burn-in overhead (gap 2) is literally the integral the forcing schedule (gap 1) controls — once we write O(delta) as an integral of the forcing rate against the trajectory deficit D_t, the burn-in characterization IS the analysis the forcing-rate optimization consumes, so a single shared-object treatment is honest and a two-module design would double-count. (b) Alternative designs rejected: (i) deriving a fresh non-asymptotic UPPER bound on the genuine tracking+GLR stopping time held at a FIXED forcing rate — rejected because that is exactly arXiv:2505.22475's deliverable (occupied; the original run abandoned on it); we instead make the forcing RATE the variable and prove a lower bound + a strictly-better construction, which 2505.22475's fixed-rate analysis does not produce. (ii) a PAC/minimax concentration bound on forced exploration (regression to the c1 Mannor-Tsitsiklis node flagged in method_lineage) — rejected because it is not instance-optimal and would not tie to T*(mu); we keep T*(mu) as the leading term and only re-characterize the additive forcing overhead, a source the lineage tree leaves unoccupied.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on synthetic 5-arm Gaussian bandits spanning easy (Delta_min large) to hard (Delta_min small) instances, run sticky-T&S with the standard forcing f(t)~sqrt(t) and with the constructed g(delta, mu_hat_t), over delta in {1e-1, 1e-2, ..., 1e-6}, common random numbers across the two forcing rules, ~2000 seeds per cell. If the candidate works, the realized expected stopping time E[tau] decreases under g relative to f at every fixed delta on instances with Delta_min bounded away from 0 (the gap is largest at moderate delta ~1e-2..1e-4 where the asymptotic regime is not yet entered), while both rules converge to the same E[tau]/log(1/delta) -> T*(mu) as delta->0 (asymptotic optimality preserved, not traded away). The single load-bearing variable is the forcing-induced overhead O(delta) = E[tau_force]-E[tau_noforce], measured by the matched forcing-on vs forcing-off runs; the mechanism claim is that g wins because it shrinks O(delta), not because it changes the tracking or stopping rules (those are byte-identical between conditions). Negative control: replace g's gap/deficit-adaptive multiplier h(Delta_hat_min,t, D_t) with a constant (recovering an asymptotically-equivalent fixed-rate schedule that still satisfies f(t)->infinity) — the downstream task-outcome metric E[tau] must revert to the standard-forcing baseline's value, confirming the savings come from the rate's adaptation to the trajectory deficit rather than from any incidental change; if E[tau] stays improved under the constant-h control, the gain is not attributable to the forcing-rate mechanism and the claim is falsified. Positive control: a stripped schedule using ONLY the D_t term (h depends on D_t alone, gaps ignored) should recover most of the E[tau] reduction, identifying the trajectory deficit as the operative signal.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:63d8201fbe32063e2ac336b0708f589e05cc3759","delta":"arXiv:2505.22475 holds the sticky schedule FIXED at its asymptotically-chosen rate and proves a non-asymptotic UPPER bound on the resulting stopping time; we instead make the forcing RATE the free variable, prove a delta-indexed LOWER bound on the forcing-induced overhead that the entire asymptotically-tuned forcing class must pay, and construct a gap/confidence-aware schedule that provably undercuts it — a separation-and-construction result their fixed-rate analysis does not and cannot state."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415237732","delta":"SEE gives an all-delta sample-complexity bound for the single-threshold 1-identification query with a bespoke explore-then-exploit algorithm; we never analyze 1-identification and never change the algorithm family — we keep the genuine sticky-T&S tracking+GLR rule and characterize only how its forcing-rate parameter governs finite-delta overhead, an axis SEE does not have (it has no plug-in maximin forcing schedule)."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:ac04baaad0b7bd277e4f3ba23ba6a3c68b8f088a","delta":"Dual-Directed proves asymptotic optimality of a unified maximin/top-two allocation as error vanishes; we leave the asymptotic constant T*(mu) untouched and instead quantify the delta-independent additive forcing overhead and tie it to the measurable trajectory deficit D_t, an object the dual-directed asymptotic analysis never forms."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:53b5d4bb1cb8c9ab00c071c3da6d7028f2c7cadd","delta":"The Batch-Complexity work bounds the number of adaptivity rounds instance-dependently but asymptotically; our overhead lives WITHIN the sampling schedule (forced pulls during burn-in), is delta-indexed, and is controlled by a forcing-rate construction rather than a batch count."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:63d8201fbe32063e2ac336b0708f589e05cc3759","what_step_was_missed":"arXiv:2505.22475 proves a non-asymptotic upper bound for sticky T&S with the forcing schedule fixed at its asymptotic setting; to already contain our contribution it would have needed to treat the forcing rate as a variable and prove a matching LOWER bound on the forcing-induced overhead as a function of that rate — and then construct a strictly-better gap/confidence-aware schedule g(delta, mu_hat) tied to the measurable trajectory deficit D_t. Their fixed-rate upper bound bounds the burn-in term but does not separate it by forcing rate, does not lower-bound it, and supplies no construction that beats the asymptotically-tuned rate at finite delta."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":218,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"Hard floor did NOT fire: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict='borderline' (no lesson candidate_match=yes — the only non-clear lesson is 'Pivoting an assumption the community treats as a reasonable modeling choice', marked borderline, not yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id=null, and paper_pointed_threat is NOT exact-mechanism overlap (the threat's fixed-rate UPPER bound is a distinct object from the candidate's rate-class LOWER bound + strictly-better construction, per subsumption_argument). recipe_application_check.verdict='applied' on both legs (the matching lower bound C11 demands is present), so the idea is built from the cluster's tactic, not the parent's gist. The single borderline sits in a load-bearing-but-defended aspect (the forcing-rate-as-restriction motivation, which the lower bound itself resolves) and the threat is genuinely differentiated, so the balance is advance with both concerns surfaced for Phase 4 rather than revise.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes how the forced-exploration / 'sticky' schedule (the rate at which sticky T&S forces under-sampled arms) trades off against the non-asymptotic overhead — the forcing rate is set asymptotically (only fast enough to guarantee consistency in the limit) and its effect on the finite-confidence stopping time is unquantified.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The dominant failure is substituting one selection rule for another that performs better empirically while omitting the theorem that explains when and why it wins; a second shape is pivoting an assumption the community regards as a reasonable modeling choice rather than a genuine restriction; a third is a guarantee that does not hold up (dataset-dependent uncontrollable constant, or a marginal bound improvement with no matching lower bound).","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Substituting one selection heuristic for another without a theorem stating when and why it wins reads as an engineering combination, not a contribution, no matter how clean the empirical gain.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism's anchor leg ships the theorem explicitly: a delta-indexed lower bound on the forcing-induced overhead O(delta) plus a certificate E[tau_g,delta] <= E[tau_f,delta] with the strict-inequality regime named (Delta_min bounded away from 0), so the when/why is proven, not asserted empirically."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pivoting an assumption the community treats as a reasonable modeling choice — rather than first proving it a genuine restriction — leaves both motivation and novelty in doubt.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The pivoted assumption ('forcing rate need only secure asymptotic consistency') is genuinely load-bearing for the finite-delta cost — the candidate proves the asymptotic class pays a Theta(sqrt(T* log(1/delta))) per-arm overhead — but a reviewer could initially read the sqrt(t) forcing rate as a 'reasonable default'; the lower bound is what converts it from default to restriction, so this is borderline and must be surfaced as the headline reviewer concern."},{"lesson_quoted":"A re-derived guarantee whose binding constant is dataset-dependent and cannot be controlled by the practitioner is vacuous in the worst case and fails to convince.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The binding quantities (T*(mu), Delta_min, the trajectory deficit D_t) are instance properties the construction g(delta, mu_hat_t) ADAPTS to via empirical plug-ins, and beta is a single practitioner-controllable constant, so the bound is not governed by an uncontrollable dataset constant."},{"lesson_quoted":"Improving a bound by a marginal factor with no matching lower bound fails to demonstrate that the improvement is significant or near-optimal enough to clear the bar.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate's central deliverable IS a matching lower bound on the forcing-induced overhead for the whole asymptotically-tuned forcing class, against which the constructed schedule is shown to be strictly better — the exact structure this lesson demands."},{"lesson_quoted":"Unlocking a new capability by violating an assumption while ignoring a protective property it guarded — detectability, validity, identifiability — invites rejection on the overlooked side effect rather than the headline result.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The protected property here is asymptotic consistency/optimality (forcing guarantees consistency for non-unique maximizers); core_mechanism explicitly proves g(t) -> infinity is retained, so the delta -> 0 guarantee is not sacrificed for the finite-delta gain."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes the burn-in regime of plug-in maximin allocation tracking: the early phase in which the tracked allocation, being computed from noisy empirical means, differs from the oracle allocation and thereby wastes samples — none ties the size of this overhead to a measurable property of the instance or of the empirical-allocation trajectory.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The dominant failure is substituting one selection rule for another without the theorem explaining when it wins; a guarantee whose binding constant is dataset-dependent and uncontrollable is vacuous; unlocking new behavior while ignoring a property the old rule protected draws rejection on the side effect.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Substituting one selection heuristic for another without a theorem stating when and why it wins reads as an engineering combination, not a contribution, no matter how clean the empirical gain.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The sibling leg does not substitute a rule heuristically — it proves the burn-in identity B(delta,mu) = E[ integral g(delta,mu_hat_t) D_t dt ], a characterization theorem, so its content is a proof not a swap."},{"lesson_quoted":"A re-derived guarantee whose binding constant is dataset-dependent and cannot be controlled by the practitioner is vacuous in the worst case and fails to convince.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"D_t is an online-computable trajectory readout the practitioner observes and the schedule consumes, so the burn-in characterization is tied to a measurable, controllable signal rather than a hidden constant."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pivoting an assumption the community treats as a reasonable modeling choice — rather than first proving it a genuine restriction — leaves both motivation and novelty in doubt.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The audited assumption — that the burn-in additive term is an instance-INDEPENDENT constant — is shown to be a genuine restriction by exhibiting it as a non-constant functional of the measurable deficit D_t, so the pivot is load-bearing."}],"verdict":"clear"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"Both gap_closure entries use assumption_audit_and_pivot / C11; the anchor leg drives the aggregate to 'borderline' solely via the lesson 'Pivoting an assumption the community treats as a reasonable modeling choice ... leaves both motivation and novelty in doubt' (candidate_match=borderline), because the sqrt(t)-style forcing rate could be read as a reasonable default. No lesson is marked candidate_match=yes anywhere, so the hard floor (triggered) does NOT fire; the matching-lower-bound and protected-property lessons are explicitly satisfied."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes how the forced-exploration / 'sticky' schedule ... and its effect on the finite-confidence stopping time is unquantified.","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Center on a selection/acquisition/query/stopping rule and pivot the single assumption baked into its criterion or required structure (a fixed count, greedy residual minimization, an anchor element); relax the structural crutch to a weaker condition and re-prove the guarantee, with the invariant deliverable a re-derived performance certificate (regret/competitive ratio/budget) shown to match or strictly beat the pre-pivot baseline.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism treats the forcing floor f (the 'forcing rate', a structural crutch of the budgeted acquisition rule justified only by asymptotic consistency) as the pivoted assumption, relaxes it to a confidence-and-gap-aware g(delta, mu_hat_t), and re-derives the performance certificate E[tau_g,delta] <= T* log(1/delta) + B_g with B_g < B_f and a matching lower bound on O(delta) — the exact C11 relax-the-crutch-then-rebound-the-certificate move with a strictly-better budget.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes the burn-in regime of plug-in maximin allocation tracking ... none ties the size of this overhead to a measurable property of the instance or of the empirical-allocation trajectory.","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Pivot the assumption baked into the choice rule (here, that the burn-in cost is a fixed constant) by either relaxing the crutch or reframing the task to a more tractable quantity, and re-derive a performance certificate in the field's native currency.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"The sibling leg reframes the burn-in additive term from an opaque instance-independent constant into a stopping-quantity on the measurable trajectory deficit D_t, proving B(delta,mu) = E[ integral_0^{tau_burn} g D_t dt ] — a re-derived certificate in sample-complexity currency tied to a measurable run property, which is the C11 reframe-then-rebound move.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries perform C11's signature move (relax/reframe the assumption inside the forcing/burn-in choice rule, then re-derive a strictly-better or newly-measurable performance certificate); the anchor additionally supplies the matching lower bound C11's reject lessons demand, so neither leg is the generic parent-pattern gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"The composition_set is the singleton {assumption_audit_and_pivot}; all three reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as a component, which is absent, so no anti-pattern matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:63d8201fbe32063e2ac336b0708f589e05cc3759","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"arXiv:2505.22475 ('Non-Asymptotic Analysis of (Sticky) Track-and-Stop') is the most specific competitor: it provides non-asymptotic guarantees for both T&S and sticky T&S, and therefore necessarily bounds the burn-in / forcing-induced term INTERNALLY at whatever forcing rate it fixes. The candidate's claim stands or falls on whether making the forcing RATE itself the analyzed variable — a delta-indexed LOWER bound on the forcing-induced overhead for the whole asymptotically-tuned forcing class, plus a CONSTRUCTED gap-and-confidence-aware schedule g(delta, mu_hat) proven to strictly undercut that lower bound while retaining asymptotic optimality — is a distinct deliverable from their fixed-rate UPPER bound. It is distinct and NOT exact-mechanism overlap: an upper bound at a fixed rate does not state a lower bound across the rate class, does not identify where the finite-delta-optimal rate sits, and supplies no improved schedule; the original (abandoned) run failed precisely because it instead re-derived the SAME fixed-rate upper-bound object. The candidate survives because its load-bearing artifact (rate-class lower bound + strictly-better construction) is one the threat paper does not produce, so it competes-adjacent rather than is-subsumed.","addressable_via":"Already addressed in the candidate's framing: differentiation_from_lit[0] and what_step_was_missed pin the delta to 'forcing rate as variable + matching lower bound + improved construction' versus their 'fixed-rate upper bound'; the standing reviewer risk (does the lower bound truly exceed what their internal burn-in bound already implies?) should be folded into Phase 4 reviewer_concerns_and_responses, not a field rewrite."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Tuning the Forcing Rate: Finite-Confidence Cost of Sticky Track-and-Stop's Exploration Schedule\n\n**Method.** Gap-Aware Forcing Schedule (GAFS)\n\n## Motivation\nWhen you want to find the best option among several noisy choices and be confident you are right (error at most a small $\\delta ),$ the standard recipe is Track-and-Stop (T&S): repeatedly estimate which options look best, sample them in the proportions an optimality formula recommends, and stop when a statistical test (the GLR test) is confident. Because those proportions are computed from still-noisy estimates, T&S also runs a 'forced-exploration' schedule — every so often it forces a pull on the least-sampled option so nothing is starved. The standard setting for how often to force (roughly proportional to $\\surd t)$ was chosen only so the method is provably optimal in the idealized limit where $\\delta  \\to $ 0.\n\nThe catch: at any real, fixed $\\delta ,$ that forcing wastes samples — every forced pull on an option the test has nearly ruled out is a sample the optimal plan did not ask for. Nobody has measured how the forcing RATE trades off against this finite-confidence waste. Recent 2025 work either fixes the forcing schedule and bounds the result (arXiv:2505.22475), solves only a simpler yes/no version (the 1-identification paper, openalex:W4415237732), or only certifies the $\\delta  \\to  0$ limit (the dual-directed design, ac04baaad0b7bd277e4f3ba23ba6a3c68b8f088a). So the forcing rate is treated as a fixed input, never as a knob to optimize for finite $\\delta .$\n\nWe make the forcing rate the object of study. We prove that any schedule chosen only for the limit must waste an amount of samples that grows like $\\surd (T*(\\mu )\\cdot log(1/\\delta ))$ per option — a cost the limit-based optimality measure simply cannot see. Then we build a smarter schedule that forces hard only while the running allocation is still far from the ideal one (measured by a quantity $D_{t}$ we can compute on the fly), and prove it wastes strictly less while still being optimal in the limit.\n\nWhen this gap closes, a practitioner running T&S at a fixed $\\delta $ gets two new things: a prediction of the actual sample budget tied to something they can watch during the run, and a forcing schedule provably cheaper than today's default on well-separated problems — improving every T&S-style method whose forcing rate is currently set only for the limit.\n\n## Method\n### Trajectory instrumentation\n*Run sticky T&S while logging the allocation trajectory and forcing events, and form the deficit $D_{t}$ that both legs depend on.*\n\n1. Start from a standard sticky Track-and-Stop (T&S) program for exponential-family arms: it keeps running averages of each arm's reward, every round computes the recommended sampling proportions $w*(\\hat{\\mu }_{t})$ by solving the optimality (maximin) formula at the current averages, samples to follow those proportions (C-tracking), and checks a statistical stopping test, the generalized-likelihood-ratio (GLR) test. It also runs a forced-exploration rule: whenever the least-sampled arm's count drops below a threshold f(t) (the standard choice grows like $\\surd t),$ it forces a pull on that arm. Add logging so that each round you save the current averages $\\hat{\\mu }_{t},$ the recommended proportions $w*(\\hat{\\mu }_{t}),$ the per-arm pull counts $N_{t},$ and whether forcing fired.\n   - _Why_: You cannot study how forcing wastes samples without first recording exactly when forcing happens and what the allocation looked like.\n2. Compute the ideal sampling proportions $w*(\\mu )$ one time from the true means (you can, because the test instances are synthetic) by solving the same optimality formula at the true means. Each round, measure how far the proportions the method is currently chasing are from these ideal proportions, using L1 distance (sum of absolute differences) — this is the deficit shown in the linked equation. Also fix the bookkeeping for the early phase: call it over once the deficit has stayed below a small level (default: below 0.1, i.e. 10% of the largest possible distance) for a run of consecutive rounds (default length: at least the number of arms, growing slightly with time).\n\n*The trajectory deficit $D_{t}$ is the L1 distance between the plug-in maximin allocation $w*(\\hat{\\mu }_{t})$ that T&S tracks and the oracle allocation $w*(\\mu )$; it is the load-bearing measurable signal.*\n$$ D_t = \\lVert w^\\star(\\hat{\\mu}_t) - w^\\star(\\mu) \\rVert_1 \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: $D_{t}$ is the one number that says how far the run still is from ideal — it is both what the burn-in cost depends on and the signal a smarter schedule should react to.\n\n### Overhead lower bound\n*Measure and then prove the forcing-induced overhead any asymptotically-tuned schedule must pay.*\n\n3. Run a twin copy of the method that is identical except forcing is switched OFF, and feed both copies the SAME random reward draws (common random numbers) so the only difference is forcing. Record each copy's stopping round and take the average difference (forcing-on minus forcing-off) — this is the extra cost forcing causes. The reason this isolates forcing: every forced pull takes the place of a pull the optimality-driven sampling would have made, pushing back the moment the stopping test becomes confident.\n   - _Why_: Comparing forcing-on against an otherwise-identical forcing-off twin isolates exactly the cost the forcing rate is responsible for.\n4. Prove that any forcing schedule that merely has to grow without bound but slower than the number of rounds must, before it switches off, force on the order of f-many pulls on each arm — and since the run lasts about $T*(\\mu )\\cdot log(1/\\delta )$ rounds, this forces a guaranteed amount of extra sampling. For the usual $\\surd t$ schedule this comes out to roughly the number of arms times $\\surd (T*(\\mu )\\cdot log(1/\\delta ))$ wasted pulls, an additive cost that the $\\delta  \\to  0$ optimality ratio cannot see. This is the linked lower-bound equation.\n\n*Lower bound: any forcing schedule f in the asymptotic class pays a forcing-induced overhead that is $\\Theta (K\\cdot \\surd (T*(\\mu )\\cdot log(1/\\delta )))$ for the canonical $\\surd t$ rate — additive and invisible to the asymptotic ratio.*\n$$ O_f(\\delta) \\;\\geq\\; c_1 \\sum_{a=1}^{K} f\\big(T^\\star(\\mu)\\log(1/\\delta)\\big) \\;=\\; \\Theta\\!\\big(K\\sqrt{T^\\star(\\mu)\\log(1/\\delta)}\\big) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This is the impossibility half: it shows the limit-tuned forcing rate is genuinely wasteful at finite $\\delta ,$ not just slightly suboptimal.\n\n### Gap-aware schedule and its certificate\n*Construct g and prove it preserves asymptotic optimality while strictly undercutting the overhead.*\n\n5. Build the smarter schedule from the linked equation: set the forcing threshold to $\\beta \\cdot \\surd (log(1/\\delta ))$ times a factor that gets smaller when the estimated smallest gap between the best and second-best arm is large (an easy problem needs little forcing) and larger when the deficit from step 2 (Compute the ideal $sampling\\dots )$ is large (still far from ideal, so force more), and use it in place of the old threshold. The precise formula for that factor and the constant $\\beta $ are a choice the authors must make 【author decision: choose the exact factor shape and $\\beta $ that give the largest provable improvement in step 6 (Prove the smarter schedule $still\\dots )$; a concrete starting point is factor = deficit / max(smallest-gap squared, 0.001) and $\\beta  = 1$】. The effect: on clearly-separated problems it forces far less, so the stopping test is satisfied sooner.\n\n*The constructed schedule scales forcing by $\\surd (log(1/\\delta ))$ times a multiplier h that decreases in the empirical smallest gap and increases in the deficit $D_{t},$ so it forces hard only while the plug-in allocation is still far from oracle.*\n$$ g(\\delta, \\hat{\\mu}_t) = \\beta\\,\\sqrt{\\log(1/\\delta)}\\; h\\!\\big(\\hat{\\Delta}_{\\min,t},\\, D_t\\big), \\quad h\\downarrow \\hat{\\Delta}_{\\min,t},\\; h\\uparrow D_t \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Forcing should be aggressive only while it is still needed; tying it to the gap and the deficit $D_{t}$ spends forced pulls exactly where they help.\n6. Prove the smarter schedule still grows without bound, which is what keeps the method correct in the limit (and keeps it working when the best sampling plan is not unique) — so nothing about the original optimality is lost. Then prove its extra cost is never worse than the standard schedule's and is strictly smaller whenever the best arm is clearly separated, which gives the guarantee in the linked equation: expected samples at most the optimal leading term plus an early-phase cost that is provably smaller than before.\n   - _Why_: A faster schedule is only useful if it does not quietly break the limit guarantee that made T&S optimal in the first place.\n\n### Burn-in characterization\n*Tie the burn-in overhead to the measurable integral of the schedule against $D_{t}$ and validate everything empirically.*\n\n7. Prove that the early-phase waste equals (up to constant factors) the running total, round by round, of the forcing rate multiplied by the deficit from step 2 (Compute the ideal $sampling\\dots ),$ added up until the early phase ends. The point: this turns the early waste from a mysterious constant into something you can actually read off a run, and it is exactly the quantity the schedule in step 5 (Build the smarter schedule from $the\\dots )$ was built to shrink — which links the two halves of the paper to one shared object.\n\n*The burn-in overhead is the expected integral of the forcing rate against the trajectory deficit up to the burn-in end $\\tau _{burn}$ — a measurable functional, not a fixed constant.*\n$$ B(\\delta,\\mu) \\;=\\; \\mathbb{E}\\!\\left[\\int_0^{\\tau_{\\mathrm{burn}}} g(\\delta,\\hat{\\mu}_t)\\, D_t \\, dt\\right] + O(1) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: It makes the early-phase waste both predictable and exactly the thing the new schedule controls, tying the two halves of the paper to one object.\n8. Test on synthetic Gaussian and Bernoulli bandits spanning easy to hard gaps and $\\delta $ from 1e-1 down to 1e-6, using the same random draws for both schedules. Run many repetitions per setting and check two things: the smarter schedule stops sooner on clearly-separated problems, and the measured early waste lines up with the running-total formula from step 7 (Prove that the early-phase $waste\\dots )$ (plot one against the other).\n   - _Why_: Synthetic experiments are cheap and let you confirm both the headline (fewer samples) and the mechanism (waste follows the predicted integral).\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 调节强制探索率：Sticky Track-and-Stop 探索调度的有限置信度代价\n\n**方法名称.** Gap-Aware Forcing Schedule (GAFS)\n\n## 研究动机\n当你想从若干带噪声的选项里找出最好的那个，并且要有把握不出错（错误率不超过很小的 $\\delta $），标准做法是 Track-and-Stop（T&S）：不断估计哪些选项更好，按一个最优性公式推荐的比例去采样，等到统计检验（GLR test）足够有把握时就停。由于这些比例是用仍然带噪的估计算出来的，T&S 还会运行一个“强制探索”调度——隔一段就强制采样一次被采样最少的选项，免得某个选项被饿着。强制的频率（大致正比于 $\\surd t$）这个标准设置，只是为了让方法在 $\\delta  \\to  0$ 的理想极限下可证最优。\n\n问题在于：在任何真实、固定的 $\\delta $ 下，这种强制会浪费样本——每一次强制去采样一个检验已基本排除的选项，都是最优方案没有要求的样本。此前没有人量化过强制“速率”与这种有限置信度浪费之间的权衡。2025 年的近期工作要么固定强制调度再给出上界（arXiv:2505.22475），要么只解决更简单的是非版本（1-identification，openalex:W4415237732），要么只证明 $\\delta  \\to  0$ 的极限最优（dual-directed 设计，ac04baaad0b7bd277e4f3ba23ba6a3c68b8f088a）。于是强制速率一直被当作固定输入，从未被当作一个可在有限 $\\delta $ 下优化的旋钮。\n\n我们把强制速率本身作为研究对象。我们证明：任何只为极限而选的调度，每个选项必然浪费约 $\\surd (T*(\\mu )\\cdot log(1/\\delta ))$ 量级的样本——这是基于极限的最优性度量根本看不到的代价。随后我们构造一个更聪明的调度，只在当前分配仍远离理想分配时（用一个可在线计算的量 $D_{t}$ 衡量）才大力强制，并证明它在保持极限最优的同时，浪费严格更少。\n\n当这个缺口被填上，在固定 $\\delta $ 下运行 T&S 的实践者会得到两样新东西：一个与运行中可观测量挂钩的真实样本预算预测，以及一个在区分度好的问题上可证比当前默认更省的强制调度——从而改进所有强制速率目前只按极限设定的 T&S 类方法。\n\n## 方法\n### 轨迹监测\n*运行 sticky T&S 并记录分配轨迹与强制事件，构造两条腿都依赖的偏差 $D_{t}$。*\n\n1. 从一个标准的 sticky Track-and-Stop (T&S) 程序开始（指数族臂）：它维护每个臂奖励的运行平均，每一轮在当前平均处求解最优性(maximin)公式得到推荐采样比例 $w*(\\hat{\\mu }_{t})$，按这些比例采样(C-tracking)，并检查一个统计停止检验——广义似然比检验(Generalized Likelihood Ratio, GLR)。它还运行一个强制探索规则：当采样最少的臂其计数低于阈值 f(t)（标准取法约为 $\\surd t$）时，就强制拉动该臂一次。加上日志，使每一轮都保存当前平均 $\\hat{\\mu }_{t}$、推荐比例 $w*(\\hat{\\mu }_{t})$、各臂拉动次数 $N_{t}$，以及强制是否触发。\n   - _为什么_: 不先记录强制何时发生、当时分配是什么样，就无法研究强制如何浪费样本。\n2. 用真实均值一次性算出理想采样比例 $w*(\\mu )$（之所以可行，是因为测试实例是合成的），方法同样是在真实均值处求解那个最优性公式。每一轮测量方法当前追逐的比例与这些理想比例相差多远，用 L1 距离（各分量绝对差之和）——这就是关联公式里的偏差量。再固定后续用到的早期阶段记账方式：当偏差持续低于一个较小水平（默认低于 0.1，即最大可能距离的 10%）连续若干轮（默认长度至少为臂数，并随时间略增）时，认为早期阶段结束。\n\n*轨迹偏差 $D_{t}$ 是 T&S 所跟踪的插值 maximin 分配 $w*(\\hat{\\mu }_{t})$ 与 oracle 分配 $w*(\\mu )$ 之间的 L1 距离，是承载机制的可测量信号。*\n$$ D_t = \\lVert w^\\star(\\hat{\\mu}_t) - w^\\star(\\mu) \\rVert_1 \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: $D_{t}$ 这一个量刻画了运行离理想还有多远——它既是 burn-in 代价所依赖的量，也是更聪明调度应当响应的信号。\n\n### 额外开销下界\n*测量并证明任何按渐近调好的调度都必须支付的强制额外开销。*\n\n3. 再跑一个孪生副本，除关闭强制外与原方法完全相同，并给两个副本喂入完全相同的随机奖励（common random numbers），使唯一差别就是强制。记录每个副本的停止轮数，取平均差（开强制减关强制）——这就是强制造成的额外代价。之所以能由此分离出强制的作用：每一次强制拉动都顶替了一次由最优性驱动的采样，从而推迟了停止检验变得有把握的时刻。\n   - _为什么_: 把开强制与除此之外完全相同的关强制孪生体对比，正好分离出强制速率所负责的那部分代价。\n4. 证明：任何只需无界增长但慢于轮数的强制调度，在关闭之前必然对每个臂强制约 f 量级次拉动——而由于一次运行大约持续 $T*(\\mu )\\cdot log(1/\\delta )$ 轮，这就强加了一定量的额外采样。对常用的 $\\surd t$ 调度，结果约为臂数乘以 $\\surd (T*(\\mu )\\cdot log(1/\\delta ))$ 次浪费拉动，是 $\\delta  \\to  0$ 最优性比率看不到的可加代价。这正是关联的下界公式。\n\n*下界：渐近类中任意强制调度 f 都需支付强制引发的额外开销，对标准 $\\surd t$ 速率为 $\\Theta (K\\cdot \\surd (T*(\\mu )\\cdot log(1/\\delta )))$，是渐近比率看不到的可加项。*\n$$ O_f(\\delta) \\;\\geq\\; c_1 \\sum_{a=1}^{K} f\\big(T^\\star(\\mu)\\log(1/\\delta)\\big) \\;=\\; \\Theta\\!\\big(K\\sqrt{T^\\star(\\mu)\\log(1/\\delta)}\\big) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这是不可能性的一半：说明按极限调好的强制速率在有限 $\\delta $ 下确实浪费，而不只是略微次优。\n\n### 间隔感知调度及其证书\n*构造 g 并证明它在保持渐近最优的同时严格降低额外开销。*\n\n5. 按关联公式构造更聪明的调度：把强制阈值设为 $\\beta \\cdot \\surd (log(1/\\delta ))$ 乘以一个系数，该系数在估计的最优臂与次优臂最小间隔较大时变小（容易的问题不需要多强制），在 第2步（用真实均值一次性算出理想采样$\\dots $） 的偏差较大时变大（仍远离理想，因此多强制），并用它替换旧阈值。该系数的精确公式与常数 $\\beta $ 需由作者决定【作者需决定：选择能在 第6步（证明更聪明的调度仍然无界增长） 中给出最大可证改进的系数形式与 $\\beta $；一个具体起点是 系数 = 偏差 / max(最小间隔的平方, 0.001)、$\\beta  = 1$】。效果是：在明显可分的问题上强制大幅减少，从而停止检验更早被满足。\n\n*构造的调度将强制量设为 $\\surd (log(1/\\delta ))$ 乘以一个系数 h；h 随经验最小间隔减小、随偏差 $D_{t}$ 增大，因此只在插值分配仍远离 oracle 时才大力强制。*\n$$ g(\\delta, \\hat{\\mu}_t) = \\beta\\,\\sqrt{\\log(1/\\delta)}\\; h\\!\\big(\\hat{\\Delta}_{\\min,t},\\, D_t\\big), \\quad h\\downarrow \\hat{\\Delta}_{\\min,t},\\; h\\uparrow D_t \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 强制只应在仍然需要时才积极；把它与间隔和偏差 $D_{t}$ 挂钩，能把强制拉动用在最有用的地方。\n6. 证明更聪明的调度仍然无界增长，这正是保证方法在极限下正确（并在最优采样方案不唯一时仍有效）的关键——因此原有的最优性毫发无损。然后证明它的额外代价从不差于标准调度，并在最优臂明显可分时严格更小，这就给出关联公式里的保证：期望样本数至多为最优主导项加上一个可证比此前更小的早期阶段代价。\n   - _为什么_: 更快的调度只有在不悄悄破坏使 T&S 最初最优的极限保证时才有用。\n\n### burn-in 刻画\n*把 burn-in 额外开销与调度对 $D_{t}$ 的可测量积分挂钩，并做实验验证。*\n\n7. 证明早期阶段的浪费（在常数因子意义下）等于逐轮地把强制速率乘以 第2步（用真实均值一次性算出理想采样$\\dots $） 的偏差所得的累计总和，一直加到早期阶段结束为止。要点在于：这把早期浪费从一个神秘常数变成了可从一次运行中读出的量，而它正是 第5步（按关联公式构造更聪明的调度） 中调度所要缩小的量——从而把论文的两部分联系到同一个共享对象上。\n\n*burn-in 额外开销等于强制速率与轨迹偏差乘积在 burn-in 结束 $\\tau _{burn}$ 之前的期望积分——是可测量的泛函，而非固定常数。*\n$$ B(\\delta,\\mu) \\;=\\; \\mathbb{E}\\!\\left[\\int_0^{\\tau_{\\mathrm{burn}}} g(\\delta,\\hat{\\mu}_t)\\, D_t \\, dt\\right] + O(1) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这让早期浪费既可预测、又正好是新调度所控制的对象，把论文两部分绑到同一个对象上。\n8. 在合成 Gaussian 与 Bernoulli 老虎机上测试，覆盖易到难的间隔以及 $\\delta $ 从 1e-1 到 1e-6，对两种调度使用相同的随机抽取。每种设置下跑多次重复，检查两点：更聪明的调度在明显可分的问题上更早停止，且测得的早期浪费与 第7步（证明早期阶段的浪费） 的累计总和公式吻合（把二者画在一起对照）。\n   - _为什么_: 合成实验成本低，既能确认主结论（更少样本），又能确认机制（浪费随预测的积分变化）。\n\n"},{"id":"86","run_dir":"run_prompt86_fedcost","index":86,"title":"Cost-Tilted Unbiased Participation: One-Stage Sampling with a Budget-in-the-Rate Guarantee for Non-Convex Federated Optimization","title_zh":"成本倾斜的无偏参与：面向非凸联邦优化的单阶段采样与预算进入收敛率常数的保证","method_name":"Cost-Tilted Unbiased Participation (CTUP)","hook":"Cost-aware federated client selection is universally built as select-then-aggregate: a budgeted filter picks cheap informative clients, then a separate aggregator averages them — and that two-stage split is exactly what biases the global update and severs the convergence guarantee from the cost budget. We prove the budgeted-variance-minimizing participation distribution is algebraically identical to a single-stage cost-tilted importance-reweighted unbiased estimator, collapsing the two stages into one and yielding the first non-convex stationarity rate whose constant is an explicit function of the per-round cost budget.","anchor_pattern_id":"algebraic_equivalence_unification","anchor_pattern_name":"Prove Equivalence to Unify","domain_category":"Optimization & Search","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a per-round client-participation rule under a hard cost budget whose induced global update is an unbiased (or explicitly bias-bounded) estimator of the full-participation gradient AND for which a non-convex stationarity rate is proven with the cost budget appearing inside the rate constant — current cost-aware rules (openalex:W4399767265, arxiv:2603.04194v1, arxiv:2602.20450v1) buy cheap informative clients greedily and leave the resulting estimator bias and its conver","pattern_id":"algebraic_equivalence_unification","pattern_name":"Prove Equivalence to Unify","sub_pattern":"C06 (Prove Equivalence to Unify)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by proving an exact algebraic identity between the constrained variance-minimization optimum (min Var[g_hat] s.t. E[cost]<=B and unbiasedness) and a single-stage cost-tilted importance-reweighted estimator, collapsing select-then-aggregate into one cost-tilted unbiased estimator whose closed-form optimal sampling probabilities p_k* and matching reweights w_k=1/(m p_k*) make the budget a parameter of the variance constant that propagates into the non-convex rate.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions whether the per-client participation cost must be treated as a FIXED selection-side constraint applied AFTER the sampling distribution is chosen, rather than as a quantity that co-determines the sampling distribution itself — every cost-aware leaf (openalex:W4399767265, openalex:W4400191998, openalex:W4400644209, arxiv:2603.04194v1) inherits from the shared 'select-then-aggregate' ancestor the assumption that selection is a budgeted filter sitting outside the unbiased","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C28 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by auditing the federated protocol's structural assumption that cost is a post-hoc selection filter outside the estimator and pivoting it — relabeling per-client cost from a hard external constraint into a resource that co-determines the sampling distribution via a single Lagrange multiplier lambda on the budget — then re-deriving the federated non-convex convergence guarantee under realistic deployment (data heterogeneity, multi-step local drift, partial participation) so the pivot, not decoration, produces the budget-in-the-constant rate.","is_anchor":false},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes how, under a finite cost budget, the achievable non-convex stationarity gap behaves as the budget shrinks — i.e. whether there is a budget-vs-stationarity frontier (a minimal budget below which no unbiased rule can guarantee descent, and the rate's dependence on budget above it); the variance-optimal sampling work (openalex:W4401753426) and the low-participation variance-reduction work (openalex:W7127113967) each fix one side and never trace the frontier itself.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C29 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by auditing the convergence-guarantee assumption that the participation rate is an exogenously fixed constant and pivoting the convergence TARGET from the exact stationary point to a budget-parameterized neighborhood whose radius is characterized in B, then decomposing the rate-controlling quantity into a universally-bounded term and a budget-sensitive term to expose the frontier: a minimal budget B_min below which the cost-tilted variance term forces a non-vanishing neighborhood (no unbiased rule guarantees descent), and an explicit 1/B-type dependence of the stationarity gap above B_min.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"non-convex federated optimization with cost-aware client selection / participation","n_papers":43,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":20},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":17,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Reputation-Aware Federated Learning Client Selection Based on Stochastic Integer Programming"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Federated learning client selection algorithm based on gradient similarity"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Advancing elderly social care dropout prediction with federated learning: client selection and imbalanced data management"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Over-the-Air Federated Learning Client Selection in Integrated Sensing, Computing and Communication"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"ALFL: A Federated Learning Client Selection Algorithm for Heterogeneous Data"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A Federated Learning Client Selection Method via Multi-Task Deep Reinforcement Learning"}],"more":11},{"year":2025,"n":17,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"FedCSA: A Novel Federated Learning Client Selection with Anomaly Detection Approach for IoT Systems"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Octopus: Knapsack model-driven federated learning client selection in internet of vehicles"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Fair and Efficient Federated Learning Client Selection via Dynamic Contribution Evaluation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Robust Federated Learning Client Selection With Combinatorial Class Representations and Data Augmentation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Adaptive Client Selection in Federated Learning: A Network Anomaly Detection Use Case"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"SecureFedPROM: A Zero-Trust Federated Learning Approach With Multi-Criteria Client Selection"}],"more":11},{"year":2026,"n":9,"papers":[{"source":"arxiv","title":"FedSIR: Spectral Client Identification and Relabeling for Federated Learning with Noisy Labels"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Federated Learning by Utility-Constrained Stochastic Aggregation for Improving Rational Participation"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Noise-aware Client Selection for carbon-efficient Federated Learning via Gradient Norm Thresholding"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"GuidaPA: Privacy-Preserving Chatbot for Public Administration via Federated Learning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Privacy Preserving Machine Learning Workflow: from Anonymization to Personalized Differential Privacy Budgets in Federated Learning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Heterogeneity-Aware Client Selection Methodology For Efficient Federated Learning"}],"more":3}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object; heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"reframe_as_solvable_object; heterogeneous_decomposition","count":6,"share":0.14},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":5,"share":0.116},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition; self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"heterogeneous_decomposition; self_supervised_signal_engineering","count":3,"share":0.07},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":3,"share":0.07},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object; structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"reframe_as_solvable_object; structural_prior_encoding","count":2,"share":0.047},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition; adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"heterogeneous_decomposition; adapt_via_conditioning","count":2,"share":0.047},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot; reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"assumption_audit_and_pivot; reframe_as_solvable_object","count":2,"share":0.047},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":2,"share":0.047}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"In cost-aware federated optimization the server must choose, each round, a subset of clients under a per-round cost budget (energy, communication, compensation), but the two design forces pull apart: cost-aware selection rules choose the cheapest informative clients greedily (knapsack/auction/threshold framings in openalex:W4399767265 and arxiv:2603.04194v1, gradient-norm or value scoring in arxiv:2602.20450v1), which makes the realized participation distribution depend on per-client cost and gradient magnitude, so the aggregated update is no longer an unbiased estimator of the full-participation gradient; meanwhile the sampling-side work that DOES keep the estimator unbiased (variance-optimal importance sampling, openalex:W4401753426) derives its optimal sampling probabilities purely from update variance with no per-client cost term in the objective, and the heterogeneity-aware sampling that reveals selection distorts the stationary point (openalex:W4417094049) and the partial-participation variance-reduction analysis (openalex:W7127113967) likewise leave cost out of the optimality condition. The result is that under a hard cost budget, no current method produces a participation rule for which the non-convex global loss provably descends to an O(1/sqrt(T))-type stationary point AT A RATE WHOSE CONSTANT IS A FUNCTION OF THE COST BUDGET — selection either spends the budget on the cheapest-and-largest gradients and silently biases the fixed point (openalex:W4417094049), or stays unbiased while ignoring that some clients are far more expensive to query (openalex:W4401753426).","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4401753426","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Derives the variance-optimal client SAMPLING distribution that minimizes the variance of the unbiased global update for multi-model FL, keeping the estimator unbiased by importance-reweighting selected clients. Its residue is that the optimal probabilities are a function of update variance ONLY, with no per-client query/participation COST in the objective and no cost budget constraint, so it cannot say how to spend a fixed cost budget optimally nor give a non-convex stationarity rate parameterized by that budget. [residue is abstract-level: anchor fulltext unfetchable]"},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4400644209","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"First to theoretically analyze the cost-vs-accuracy tradeoff of which clients to RECRUIT in FL, modelling each client as a (data, device, willingness-to-participate, compensation) bundle and optimizing one-shot recruitment under a budget. Its residue is that recruitment is a one-shot enrollment decision, not a per-round sampling distribution, and it does not produce an unbiased per-round estimator nor a non-convex convergence rate whose constant contains the cost budget."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4417094049","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Reveals that joint communication+computation heterogeneity in client sampling distorts the optimization dynamics and drives the global model to an objective-inconsistent stationary point far from the true optimum, and proposes a heterogeneity-aware sampling correction. Its residue is that the correction targets heterogeneity-induced objective inconsistency but does not place a per-client COST term inside the sampling-optimality objective nor make the convergence-rate constant an explicit function of a cost budget."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7127113967","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Analyzes why variance-reduction methods (control variates) deteriorate under LOW client participation, attributing it to control-variate drift, and proposes proportional variance reduction to stabilize partial participation. Its residue is that participation is treated as an exogenously fixed low rate, not as a cost-budget-constrained decision the server optimizes, so cost never enters the convergence condition and the method cannot trade budget for stationarity-rate."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"non-convex federated optimization with cost-aware client selection / participation","venue":"ICLR/ICML/NeurIPS (optimization + federated learning track)","time":"2026","data":["standard non-IID FL benchmarks (CIFAR-10/100 with Dirichlet partitions, FEMNIST, Shakespeare)","a cross-silo cost-annotated setup where each client carries a per-round participation cost (compute/energy/communication/compensation)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"optimization theory + federated learning systems","preference":"both","baseline":"FedAvg with uniform/importance client sampling; variance-reduced importance sampling (e.g. W4401753426); cost-aware heuristic selection (knapsack/auction/threshold, e.g. W4399767265, W4400191998, arxiv:2603.04194v1)","limitation":"existing cost-aware client selection picks clients greedily under a cost budget but the induced sampling distribution biases the aggregated gradient, and no method jointly (a) keeps the global update an unbiased estimator of the full-participation gradient and (b) carries a non-convex stationarity guarantee whose rate explicitly contains the per-client cost budget","contribution_type":"theory","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object every leg reads from and writes to is the cost-tilted per-round client participation distribution p = (p_1,...,p_N) over the N clients together with its induced global gradient estimator g_hat and the federated non-convex convergence rate that estimator produces. Each round the server holds: a per-client expected query cost c_k > 0 (a known scalar = communication bytes x unit-bytes-cost + local-compute energy + compensation, supplied by the system or estimated from the previous round's profiled round-trip; units normalized so sum_k c_k is comparable to budget B), a per-round cost budget B (user-set scalar in the same units), and a per-client update-magnitude proxy s_k >= 0 (the load-bearing informativeness statistic = an exponential moving average, decay 0.9, of the L2 norm of client k's most recent local update Delta_k; for never-seen clients s_k is initialized to the running mean over seen clients). ANCHOR LEG (C06, algebraic equivalence): the field builds participation as two stages — pick a subset S under sum_{k in S} c_k <= B, then average. We instead pose ONE constrained program over the sampling distribution: minimize the variance Var[g_hat] of the importance-reweighted unbiased estimator g_hat = (1/m) sum_{k sampled} (1/p_k) Delta_k subject to (i) unbiasedness E[g_hat] = (1/N) sum_k Delta_k (enforced exactly by the reweight w_k = 1/(m p_k)), (ii) the expected-cost budget sum_k p_k c_k <= B, and (iii) p_k in [0,1], sum_k p_k = m. We prove the KKT optimum has the closed form p_k* proportional to s_k / sqrt(mu + lambda c_k), where lambda >= 0 is the single Lagrange multiplier on the budget and mu absorbs the simplex/box constraints; this is exactly a cost-tilted version of variance-optimal importance sampling (lambda=0 recovers the classical s_k-proportional unbiased sampler). The algebraic identity is that the two-stage 'budgeted-select then average' optimum and this one-stage cost-tilted importance estimator coincide whenever the budget binds, so the separate selection stage is provably redundant — the equivalence eliminates the selection module and the bias it introduced, and the resulting variance constant V(B) = sum_k s_k^2 (sqrt(mu+lambda c_k)/s_k) / N^2-type expression is now an explicit, monotonically-decreasing function of B through lambda(B). GAP-1 LEG (C28, audit federated system structure): the equivalence is only meaningful because we pivot the protocol assumption that cost is a hard filter living OUTSIDE the estimator; relabeling cost as a resource that enters the sampling distribution through lambda is the pivot, and we re-derive the standard FedAvg-style non-convex descent lemma E[f(theta_{t+1})] <= f(theta_t) - eta||grad f||^2 + (eta^2 L /2) Var[g_hat] with local-SGD drift and Dirichlet-heterogeneity terms intact, so the budget enters the per-round progress through V(B) rather than being assumed away — this is the load-bearing use of the pivot, not decoration. GAP-2 LEG (C29, audit convergence target): with V(B) in hand we pivot the convergence target from the exact stationary point to a neighborhood and split the cumulative stationarity measure (1/T) sum_t E||grad f(theta_t)||^2 <= [f(theta_0)-f*]/(eta T) + (eta L/2) V(B) into a universally-bounded optimization term (first) and a budget-sensitive variance floor (second); the floor (eta L/2) V(B) is non-vanishing, which gives the frontier: B_min is the budget at which V(B) equals the target stationarity tolerance epsilon^2, below which no unbiased rule attains epsilon, and above B_min the gap shrinks as V(B) ~ O(1/B) under bounded c_k. All three legs share the single object p*(B) and its variance constant V(B); no separate modules are needed because the equivalence (anchor) is what makes the pivoted protocol (gap-1) analyzable, and the rate it produces (gap-1) is what the frontier (gap-2) reads its limit off of.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The three gaps share one machinery rather than needing separate modules because they are three views of the SAME object: the anchor proves the cost-tilted sampler IS an unbiased estimator (existence/identity), gap-1 proves the rate is produced BY making cost co-determine that sampler (mechanism), and gap-2 reads the budget-vs-stationarity limit OFF that same rate (limit) — the shared_object thread (p*(B), V(B), the rate) is literal, and splitting into modules would duplicate the variance constant. (b) Alternatives considered and rejected: (1) a greedy knapsack selector with a post-hoc bias-correction term — rejected because it lands on lineage node n5 (greedy budgeted selection) and the correction cannot be proven to restore exact unbiasedness at the budget-binding optimum; (2) a bandit/online-subset-selection regret formulation (lineage collateral c1) — rejected because its regret is about the selection objective, not the federated non-convex stationarity rate, so cost would never enter the rate constant; (3) classical cost-aware coordinate/example sampling probabilities (collateral c2) — rejected because it has no multi-step local drift or non-IID objective-inconsistency term, so it does not transfer to the federated setting.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on CIFAR-10 partitioned non-IID via Dirichlet(alpha=0.1) across N=100 clients with per-client query costs c_k drawn heavy-tailed (lognormal), run FedAvg with three participation rules at a FIXED cumulative cost budget — (A) our cost-tilted unbiased sampler p_k* proportional to s_k/sqrt(mu+lambda c_k), (B) cost-blind variance-optimal sampler (lambda=0), (C) greedy knapsack cost-aware selection — and measure final test accuracy and the gradient norm at the stopping round. If the candidate works, at a TIGHT budget rule (A) reaches a strictly higher final test accuracy (and lower gradient-norm-at-stop) than both (B) and (C) for the same spent budget, and the accuracy-vs-budget curve flattens above a measurable B_min while collapsing below it, matching the predicted O(1/B) frontier. The named load-bearing variable is the cost-tilt multiplier lambda (equivalently the realized expected aggregation bias it controls): the negative control sets lambda=0 (cost-blind reweighting still unbiased, but no cost tilt) under the tight budget and predicts final test accuracy falls back to the cost-blind baseline — crucially the control's predicted effect is the DOWNSTREAM task metric (test accuracy / stationarity gap), not lambda's own value, so 'accuracy moved' cannot be explained away by estimator-variance changes alone since (B) keeps the same unbiased reweighting and only drops the tilt. A positive control — a stripped rule using ONLY the cost-tilt (uniform s_k, p* shaped by c_k alone) — should recover most of the budget-efficiency gain over (B), constructively identifying the cost tilt as the mechanism.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4401753426","delta":"They derive the variance-optimal unbiased client sampling distribution with NO cost term (p_k proportional to update variance only); we add an expected-cost budget constraint and derive the cost-tilted optimum p_k* proportional to s_k/sqrt(mu+lambda c_k), proving it is still exactly unbiased and that lambda(B) makes the variance constant a function of the budget."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4399767265","delta":"They minimize total time+energy cost via a fuzzy/knapsack selection policy applied as a filter before aggregation, with no characterization of the resulting estimator bias or convergence rate; we prove the budgeted-selection optimum is algebraically identical to a single-stage unbiased cost-tilted estimator and supply the non-convex rate with the budget inside its constant."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4417094049","delta":"They reveal heterogeneity-induced objective inconsistency in client sampling and correct it, but place no per-client cost in the sampling-optimality objective; we put cost in the objective via a single multiplier and characterize the budget-vs-stationarity frontier (B_min, O(1/B)) their analysis does not address."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7127113967","delta":"They analyze why variance reduction degrades at an exogenously fixed low participation rate; we make participation a budget-constrained DECISION variable and prove a minimal-budget threshold B_min below which no unbiased rule guarantees descent — a frontier they cannot state because participation is fixed, not optimized, in their setting."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4401753426","what_step_was_missed":"They constructed the variance-optimal unbiased sampling distribution as a function of update statistics alone; for our contribution to already exist they would have had to add the expected-cost budget constraint to the variance-minimization program and carry the resulting Lagrange multiplier through to a non-convex federated convergence rate — i.e. derive the closed-form cost-tilted optimum p_k* proportional to s_k/sqrt(mu+lambda c_k) and prove the budget-parameterized variance constant V(B) and its frontier, a constrained-optimization extension and rate derivation their cost-free formulation never performs."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":280,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"Layer 1 hard floor does not fire: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict = borderline (no lesson marked candidate_match: yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id = null, and paper_pointed_threat is same-topic different-mechanism (not exact-mechanism overlap). Within the safe zone the verdict is revise rather than advance for two load-bearing reasons: (1) paper_pointed_threat.addressable_via names a specific field — a near-identically-titled Dec-2025 paper (semanticscholar:9a4aaa...) already proves cost-aware non-convex rates with an unbiased SAGA estimator, so differentiation_from_lit and the hook must explicitly foreground the cost-tilted distribution / lambda(B)-in-the-constant / B_min frontier or a reviewer will read collision; and (2) the gap_closure_reject_check borderlines on C28 ('expected/easy result') and C29 ('merely matches the baseline with near-identical algorithmic changes') both hit the same load-bearing property — the above-B_min rate is the standard FedAvg descent with V(B) plugged in, so core_mechanism must make the B_min frontier and the budget-binding tilt carry the non-incremental weight explicitly.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a per-round client-participation rule under a hard cost budget whose induced global update is an unbiased (or explicitly bias-bounded) estimator of the full-participation gradient AND for which a non-convex stationarity rate is proven with the cost budget appearing inside the rate constant — current cost-aware rules (openalex:W4399767265, arxiv:2603.04194v1, arxiv:2602.20450v1) buy cheap informative clients greedily and leave the resulting estimator bias and its convergence cost uncharacterized.","main_pattern":"algebraic_equivalence_unification","sub_pattern":"C06 (Prove Equivalence to Unify)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is the cosmetic generalization: the paper embeds an existing objective in a one-parameter family but never shows the new degree of freedom repairs a concrete named failure of the original, so the added scalar reads as one more hyperparameter to tune. A second shape is the unverified equivalence — an unbiasedness/optimality claim resting on a precondition asserted rather than checked, leaving the identity empty exactly where it is needed.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Generalizing a method to a one-parameter divergence family without demonstrating that the new freedom fixes the method's actual named shortcoming reads as an empirical hyperparameter study, not a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The cost-tilt multiplier lambda is not a free hyperparameter — it is the KKT multiplier solved from the binding budget constraint, and it provably fixes the named shortcoming (select-then-aggregate's estimator bias and budget-severed rate), so the new freedom is load-bearing rather than tuned."},{"lesson_quoted":"Swapping a standard divergence for a fancier one to 'reduce bias' fails when you cannot establish a concrete failure mode of the original that the replacement provably and uniquely repairs.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism names the concrete failure (the separate selection stage introduces aggregation bias and severs the rate from B) and the equivalence provably eliminates that exact module rather than swapping for cosmetic generality."},{"lesson_quoted":"Reinterpreting an existing loss as a special case of your framework while delivering only marginal gains over that loss leaves reviewers unable to isolate what the framework actually buys.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The equivalence reduces to classical variance-optimal sampling at lambda=0 (the existing leaf openalex:W4401753426); isolation rests on the falsification's negative control (B) being a clean lambda=0 ablation, which it is, but a reviewer could ask the gains over (B) be more than marginal at a tight budget — a Phase-4 concern, not a Reject trigger."},{"lesson_quoted":"A theoretically-motivated bias correction that does not translate into empirical gains over strong (even if biased) baselines, and rests on an unverifiable sufficiency condition, is judged incremental on both the theoretical and the practical axis.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The falsification predicts a downstream test-accuracy gain over both the cost-blind unbiased baseline (B) and the greedy biased baseline (C), and the equivalence's preconditions (budget binds, unbiasedness via explicit reweight w_k=1/(m p_k)) are checked algebraically, not asserted."},{"lesson_quoted":"Soft-target or divergence reformulations that overlap with a prior published loss and show only marginal improvement on already-strong models suggest the targeted problem was implicitly solved, leaving no isolable contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"No prior published loss is the cost-tilted estimator; the closest prior (variance-optimal sampling) is the lambda=0 special case the candidate strictly generalizes by adding the budget-binding tilt, so the problem was not implicitly solved."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions whether the per-client participation cost must be treated as a FIXED selection-side constraint applied AFTER the sampling distribution is chosen, rather than as a quantity that co-determines the sampling distribution itself — every cost-aware leaf (openalex:W4399767265, openalex:W4400191998, openalex:W4400644209, arxiv:2603.04194v1) inherits from the shared 'select-then-aggregate' ancestor the assumption that selection is a budgeted filter sitting outside the unbiased-estimator machinery, so the question of whether cost and the optimal sampling probability are a single jointly-determined object is never asked.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C28 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The most common shape is a headline reframing that turns out not to be load-bearing — an elegant modeling lens that never actually drives the proof — so the advertised contribution evaporates. A second is the 'expected/easy' result: the guarantee re-derived only after the genuinely hard regime (heterogeneity, partial participation) is assumed away.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"If your headline reframing never does work in the proof — and the subarea is already well-studied — reviewers see decoration rather than contribution, and any rate error finishes the job.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The pivot (relabel cost from external filter to a resource entering the sampling distribution through lambda) is what produces V(B) in the descent lemma, and core_mechanism explicitly states the rate enters the per-round progress through V(B) — the reframing is load-bearing in the proof, not decoration."},{"lesson_quoted":"A result that drops out of standard analysis once you sanitize the hard regime away (no adversarial majority, quadratic-only, bounded magnitudes) is discounted as expected and easy, even by sympathetic readers.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"core_mechanism keeps local-SGD drift, Dirichlet-heterogeneity terms, and partial participation intact rather than sanitizing them, so the hard regime is retained; the residual risk is that the descent lemma is the standard FedAvg one with V(B) plugged in, which a reviewer might call mechanical — a load-bearing concern to surface, but the regime is not assumed away so it does not trigger."},{"lesson_quoted":"Combining several known primitives without demonstrating that the combination yields more than the sum of its parts collapses to 'amalgamation, modest novelty.'","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate does not union primitives; the three legs share a single object p*(B)/V(B), and the audit pivot is the unique enabling move, not a stack of independent techniques."},{"lesson_quoted":"A first-of-its-kind theory confined to a toy objective with no empirical bridge to the claimed deployment cannot show it generalizes, however sound the proof.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"falsification_prediction supplies the empirical bridge (CIFAR-10/100 + FEMNIST, N<=100, heavy-tailed costs, three rules x six budget points x three seeds), so the theory is not confined to a toy objective."},{"lesson_quoted":"A convergence bound whose hidden dependence on an unsettable initialization constant contradicts the privacy claim it advertises destroys trust even when the operator swap itself is correct.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate advertises no privacy claim and the rate constant V(B) is an explicit function of settable quantities (s_k, c_k, B, lambda(B)); there is no hidden unsettable constant."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes how, under a finite cost budget, the achievable non-convex stationarity gap behaves as the budget shrinks — i.e. whether there is a budget-vs-stationarity frontier (a minimal budget below which no unbiased rule can guarantee descent, and the rate's dependence on budget above it); the variance-optimal sampling work (openalex:W4401753426) and the low-participation variance-reduction work (openalex:W7127113967) each fix one side and never trace the frontier itself.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C29 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The dominant failure shape is a relaxed assumption that is technically valid but uncharacterized: no named class is shown to satisfy it and its constants' behavior is unstudied, so it reads as engineered to close the proof. A third is a headline guarantee undermined by hidden constants that explode at the very parameter limit where the result is claimed strongest.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A weakened assumption that no known function class is shown to satisfy reads as engineered to close the proof, not as a genuine generalization — characterize when it holds or it sinks the paper.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The pivot weakens the convergence TARGET (exact stationary point to a budget-parameterized neighborhood), not a regularity assumption on f; the neighborhood radius is characterized in B (V(B)~O(1/B) under bounded c_k), so the relaxation is explicitly characterized rather than left abstract."},{"lesson_quoted":"Re-deriving a rate that merely matches the baseline with near-identical algorithmic changes is read as an incremental extension, however clean the analysis.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The above-B_min branch reduces to a standard FedAvg non-convex rate with V(B) substituted for the usual variance; the genuinely new object is the B_min frontier (a budget below which no unbiased rule attains epsilon), which is NOT in the baseline — so the frontier is the non-incremental part, but a reviewer could press whether the above-B_min rate alone is novel; load-bearing enough to surface."},{"lesson_quoted":"Hidden constants that explode at the precise parameter limit where the result is advertised as strongest silently invalidate the headline guarantee, and reviewers find them in the proof.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The result is advertised strongest at small B (the frontier), and V(B)~O(1/B) means the variance floor grows as B shrinks — this is the intended, characterized behavior (it IS the frontier), not a hidden explosion, but the proof must show lambda(B) and mu stay finite and well-defined as B approaches B_min from above; a load-bearing detail Phase 4 must lock down."},{"lesson_quoted":"A theorem stated without formal assumptions or a precise claim is unreviewable; 'tight, assumption-free' bounds with no exhibited assumptions are treated as not-yet-a-paper.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism exhibits the assumptions (bounded c_k, unbiasedness via reweight, local-SGD drift, Dirichlet heterogeneity, budget binds) and states the precise rate decomposition, so the claim is reviewable."},{"lesson_quoted":"An assumption-relaxation validated only on a single toy instance gives no evidence the relaxation captures the motivating practical regime.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The frontier is validated across six budget points and multiple datasets/seeds with the predicted flatten-above / collapse-below B_min signature, not a single toy instance."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No entry is triggered (no Reject lesson marked candidate_match: yes), so the hard floor does not fire. The aggregate is borderline, driven by the C28 entry (assumption_audit_and_pivot on the federated protocol) whose 'expected/easy result' lesson and the C29 entry whose 'merely matches the baseline with near-identical algorithmic changes' lesson both flag the same load-bearing risk: the above-B_min rate is the standard FedAvg non-convex descent with V(B) substituted in, so the proof's non-incremental weight rests on the B_min frontier and the budget-binding tilt being genuinely new rather than a plug-in."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a per-round client-participation rule under a hard cost budget whose induced global update is an unbiased (or explicitly bias-bounded) estimator of the full-participation gradient AND for which a non-convex stationarity rate is proven with the cost budget appearing inside the rate constant.","sub_pattern":"C06 (Prove Equivalence to Unify)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Take a quantity currently treated as a multi-stage estimation pipeline, prove it is algebraically a special case of (or exactly equal to) a principled probabilistic quantity, and cash the identity by collapsing the multi-stage pipeline into a single objective — showing the intermediate quantity is encoded in the final objective, or solving in closed form for the optimal member — made load-bearing (eliminates a module / yields a provable rate).","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"ANCHOR LEG performs exactly this: it poses the budgeted variance-minimization as ONE constrained program over the sampling distribution, proves the KKT optimum has the closed form p_k* proportional to s_k/sqrt(mu+lambda c_k), and proves the two-stage 'budgeted-select then average' optimum and the one-stage cost-tilted importance estimator COINCIDE whenever the budget binds — collapsing select-then-aggregate into a single estimator and eliminating the selection module (the signature 'collapse a multi-stage pipeline by closed-form optimal member' move), made load-bearing because the resulting V(B) propagates into the non-convex rate.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions whether the per-client participation cost must be treated as a FIXED selection-side constraint applied AFTER the sampling distribution is chosen, rather than as a quantity that co-determines the sampling distribution itself.","sub_pattern":"C28 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Within a federated/distributed iterative-optimization protocol, locate a structural assumption about the protocol's architecture and pivot it — the canonical form being relabel a supposedly-harmful/external quantity as a resource — then re-derive convergence under realistic system conditions (heterogeneity, partial participation), making the pivot load-bearing in the proof.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"GAP-1 LEG performs the signature relabel: it pivots the protocol assumption that cost is a hard filter living OUTSIDE the estimator and relabels per-client cost as a resource that enters the sampling distribution through the Lagrange multiplier lambda, then re-derives the FedAvg-style non-convex descent lemma with local-SGD drift and Dirichlet-heterogeneity terms intact so the budget enters per-round progress through V(B) — the 'relabel external constraint as a resource and re-derive under realistic system conditions' move, explicitly stated as load-bearing not decoration.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf characterizes how, under a finite cost budget, the achievable non-convex stationarity gap behaves as the budget shrinks — i.e. whether there is a budget-vs-stationarity frontier.","sub_pattern":"C29 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Take an existing convergence guarantee for an iterative first-order procedure and pivot the single regularity-or-target assumption the proof silently rests on — e.g. replace the convergence primitive itself (exact-optimum target → a characterized neighborhood) — then re-prove the rate by isolating one load-bearing object (a cumulative-deficit decomposition), with payoff a sharper rate, a provable separation, or coverage of an excluded regime.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"GAP-2 LEG performs the signature target-pivot: it pivots the convergence TARGET from the exact stationary point to a budget-parameterized neighborhood and splits the cumulative stationarity measure into a universally-bounded optimization term and a budget-sensitive variance floor (eta L/2)V(B) — the cumulative-deficit decomposition — yielding the payoff the card names (a class separation): B_min below which no unbiased rule attains epsilon. The exact-optimum → characterized-neighborhood swap and the deficit decomposition are both present.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"All three entries instantiate their cited cluster's distinctive move in core_mechanism: C06's closed-form-optimal-member pipeline collapse (p_k* + two-stage/one-stage coincidence), C28's relabel-external-constraint-as-resource pivot (cost → lambda), and C29's convergence-target swap plus cumulative-deficit decomposition (neighborhood + V(B) floor + B_min). None is built from the parent pattern's generic gist alone."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["algebraic_equivalence_unification","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"The composition_set is {algebraic_equivalence_unification, assumption_audit_and_pivot}; none of the three documented reject-favored compositions (audit_decomp_supervisor, audit_decomp_prior, audit_decomp_operator) is present because every flagged composition requires heterogeneous_decomposition as a component and this candidate contains no heterogeneous_decomposition, self_supervised_signal_engineering, structural_prior_encoding, or architectural_operator_substitution leg."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:9a4aaa59947d80213c65eb6046a2b79ff8b325f8","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"This Dec-2025 arXiv paper, titled near-identically to the seed ('Non-Convex Federated Optimization under Cost-Aware Client Selection'), introduces a cost-accounting model that associates each client-selection strategy with a distinct communication/local-compute cost and proves best-known non-convex complexities for a new inexact composite-gradient algorithm built on a SAGA-derived conditionally-unbiased estimator (RG-SAGA). It is the strongest same-topic threat because it already (i) formalizes cost per selection strategy and (ii) proves non-convex rates with an unbiased estimator — the two ingredients the candidate also claims. However it does NOT subsume the candidate's mechanism: it never derives a cost-TILTED sampling distribution from a budgeted variance-minimization program, never proves the algebraic identity collapsing select-then-aggregate into a single cost-tilted importance estimator, never puts a per-round cost BUDGET B inside the rate constant via a Lagrange multiplier lambda(B), and never traces a budget-vs-stationarity frontier with a minimal budget B_min. Its cost model is a comparison/accounting device across discrete strategies (random / all / hybrid), whereas the candidate's cost is a continuous co-determinant of the optimal sampling probabilities. The candidate's claim stands or falls on whether the cost-tilt-plus-budget-in-the-constant + B_min frontier reads as a distinct contribution beyond this paper's strategy-cost accounting — it does, because the artifacts are different, but the differentiation must be made explicit since the titles collide.","addressable_via":"Sharpen differentiation_from_lit and the hook to explicitly contrast against this paper's strategy-level cost-accounting + RG-SAGA construction, foregrounding the continuous cost-tilted sampling distribution, the budget-in-the-constant via lambda(B), and the B_min frontier as the load-bearing differentiators (same-topic, different-mechanism — addressable, not exact-mechanism overlap)."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat — semanticscholar:9a4aaa59947d80213c65eb6046a2b79ff8b325f8 ('Non-Convex Federated Optimization under Cost-Aware Client Selection', Dec 2025) collides on title and already proves cost-aware non-convex rates with an unbiased SAGA/RG-SAGA estimator.","fix_direction":"Add an explicit contrast paragraph: that paper's cost is a discrete accounting device comparing fixed selection strategies (random/all/hybrid) and its unbiasedness comes from SAGA variance reduction, whereas the candidate derives a CONTINUOUS cost-tilted sampling distribution p_k* proportional to s_k/sqrt(mu+lambda c_k) from a budgeted variance-minimization program, puts the per-round budget B inside the rate constant via the multiplier lambda(B), and traces a B_min frontier — none of which appears in the threat paper. Cite the paper_id."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"hook","issue":"Same threat — the hook's framing ('first non-convex stationarity rate whose constant is an explicit function of the per-round cost budget') overlaps verbally with a paper that already proves cost-aware non-convex rates, so 'first' is contestable as stated.","fix_direction":"Requalify 'first' to the precise distinguishing artifact: first rate whose constant depends on a per-round cost BUDGET through a continuous cost-tilted sampling distribution (not a discrete strategy-cost accounting), and the first to expose a minimal-budget B_min frontier. Keep the structural-collapse claim (select-then-aggregate equivalence) as the load-bearing differentiator."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","issue":"gap_closure_reject_check borderline on C28 ('expected/easy result') and C29 ('merely matches the baseline with near-identical algorithmic changes') — the above-B_min rate is the standard FedAvg non-convex descent lemma with V(B) substituted, so the non-incremental weight is under-attributed in the current wording.","fix_direction":"Tighten the GAP-2 leg to state explicitly that the above-B_min branch recovering a standard-form rate is intentional and that the contribution is the B_min frontier (a budget threshold below which NO unbiased rule attains epsilon — a separation absent from any baseline) plus the proof that lambda(B) and mu remain finite and well-defined as B approaches B_min from above, so the variance floor's O(1/B) growth is the characterized frontier rather than a hidden constant explosion."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Appended a new differentiation entry for semanticscholar:9a4aaa59947d80213c65eb6046a2b79ff8b325f8 contrasting its discrete strategy-cost accounting + RG-SAGA unbiasedness against our continuous cost-tilted distribution p_k*, budget-in-the-constant via lambda(B), and B_min frontier."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"hook","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Requalified 'first' to the precise distinguishing artifacts (first rate whose constant depends on B through a CONTINUOUS cost-tilted sampling distribution, and first to expose a B_min frontier), explicitly contrasting against prior cost-aware non-convex FL that prices discrete selection strategies, while keeping the select-then-aggregate structural-collapse claim load-bearing."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Tightened the GAP-2 leg to state that the above-B_min standard-form rate is intentional and that the non-incremental weight rests on the B_min budget separation plus the proof that lambda(B) and mu stay finite as B -> B_min, framing the O(1/B) variance-floor growth as the characterized frontier rather than a hidden constant explosion."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Cost-Tilted Unbiased Participation: One-Stage Sampling with a Budget-in-the-Rate Guarantee for Non-Convex Federated Optimization\n\n**Method.** Cost-Tilted Unbiased Participation (CTUP)\n\n## Motivation\nIn federated learning (FL), a central server trains a shared model by repeatedly asking a few client devices to compute updates on their private data. Querying a client is not free - it costs energy, network bandwidth, and sometimes money - so the server has a per-round budget and can only afford a subset of clients. Today's cost-aware methods handle this as two separate steps: first a 'selection' step greedily buys the cheapest, most useful clients that fit the budget, then an 'aggregation' step averages whatever it got. The hidden problem is that picking the cheap-and-large-gradient clients skews which updates you see, so the averaged update no longer matches what you would get if everyone participated - it is biased, and that bias quietly breaks the math that guarantees the model keeps improving.\n\nTwo recent lines of work each got halfway. Variance-optimal sampling (2024) keeps the average unbiased but ignores cost entirely, so it cannot tell you how to spend a fixed budget. Cost-aware selection (2024-2026) tracks real per-client cost but treats it as an outside filter, leaving the bias and the convergence cost uncharacterized. Nobody has asked whether cost should help DECIDE the sampling probabilities in the first place, rather than be bolted on afterward.\n\nOur idea removes that seam. We prove that the best budget-constrained selection is mathematically the SAME thing as a single one-step sampler that tilts each client's selection probability by its cost and reweights to stay unbiased: pick client k with probability proportional to $s_{k} /$ sqrt(mu + lambda $c_{k}),$ where $s_{k}$ is how informative the client is, $c_{k}$ is its cost, and lambda is a single knob set by the budget. Because the two stages collapse into one, the bias disappears, and the budget B shows up directly inside the convergence-rate constant. That also lets us draw a frontier: a minimal budget $B_{min}$ below which NO unbiased rule can guarantee the model descends, and above which the remaining error shrinks like 1/B.\n\n## Method\n### Cost-Tilted Sampler\n*Turn per-client cost and informativeness into a single-stage unbiased sampling distribution set by one budget multiplier.*\n\n1. For each client keep two numbers. First, $s_{k}:$ how big its updates tend to be - take the length (L2 norm) of the client's most recent update and smooth it with a 0.9-decay running average; a brand-new client starts at the average $s_{k}$ of clients seen so far. Second, $c_{k}:$ how expensive the client is - combine its communication (megabytes sent and received), its local energy use (watt-hours), and any compensation paid into one cost number, then divide every client's cost by the round's average cost so the numbers are around 1 and the budget B can be read as 'how many average clients you can afford'. 【author decision: how much weight to give communication vs energy vs money when combining them into one cost depends on which resource you most want to save.】\n   - _Why_: You need both how useful a client is AND how expensive it is, in the same units, before cost can shape the sampling.\n2. Find the sampling probabilities by solving a small two-level search. The outer search adjusts one number, lambda >= 0 (the 'budget dial'), by bisection until the probabilities spend exactly the budget; if the budget is loose enough that the cost-free solution already fits, lambda stays 0. For a given lambda, score each client by $s_{k} /$ sqrt(mu + lambda $c_{k}),$ then pick the inner number mu so that, after capping any probability at 1, the probabilities add up to the target expected count m. Stop when the expected spent cost matches the budget to within a tiny tolerance. This is exactly the optimal cost-tilted sampler: cheaper and more informative clients get higher probability, and lambda is how strongly cost pulls the probabilities down.\n\n*The closed-form KKT optimum of the budgeted variance-minimization program: a cost-tilted version of variance-optimal importance sampling, with lambda the single budget multiplier (lambda=0 recovers the cost-blind sampler).*\n$$ p_k^{*} \\;\\propto\\; \\frac{s_k}{\\sqrt{\\mu + \\lambda c_k}},\\qquad \\lambda \\ge 0,\\quad \\sum_{k} p_k^{*} c_k = B \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: lambda is the single dial that trades off informativeness against cost - it is solved from the budget, not hand-tuned.\n3. Actually choose this round's clients by flipping an independent biased coin for each client: include client k with probability $p_{k}*.$ This gives a set whose size varies around m on average. Using independent coin flips (rather than always taking the top-m clients) is what makes the later reweighting cancel the selection bias exactly. Save which clients were chosen and the probability each was chosen with.\n   - _Why_: Sampling (rather than deterministically picking the top clients) is what lets the reweighting keep the update unbiased.\n4. Build the global update so it is unbiased, then update the model. Each chosen client sends back $Delta_{k},$ the change it made to the model after a few local training epochs (this is the standard FedAvg 'pseudo-gradient'). Combine them by dividing each client's update by the probability it was chosen and averaging: $g_{hat} =$ (1/m) sum $(1/p_{k}*) Delta_{k}.$ That division is the trick that makes the average equal, on average, to what you would have gotten from all clients. Finally move the model: theta <- theta - eta $* g_{hat},$ with server step size eta.\n\n*The importance-reweighted global estimator with weight $1/p_{k},$ whose expectation equals the full-participation gradient - the reweight is what makes the update unbiased.*\n$$ \\hat{g} = \\frac{1}{m}\\sum_{k\\,\\in\\,\\mathcal{S}}\\frac{1}{p_k}\\,\\Delta_k,\\qquad \\mathbb{E}[\\hat{g}] = \\frac{1}{N}\\sum_{k=1}^{N}\\Delta_k \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Dividing each update by its own selection probability cancels the sampling skew, so the averaged update equals the full-participation gradient in expectation.\n\n### Budget-in-the-Constant Theory\n*Prove the two-stage/one-stage equivalence and carry the budget into the non-convex rate constant and the $B_{min}$ frontier.*\n\n5. Prove on paper that the two-step recipe and the one-step sampler are the same optimum. Write down the problem 'pick a sampling distribution that respects the cost budget and keeps the average unbiased, with smallest variance', using each client's typical squared update size $(s_{k}$ squared) as its variance proxy. Solving this with standard constrained-optimization conditions (KKT) gives exactly the cost-tilted probabilities $p_{k}*$ proportional to $s_{k} /$ sqrt(mu + lambda $c_{k}).$ Because this same distribution is the answer whether you think of it as 'select a budgeted subset then average' or as 'one cost-tilted importance sampler', the separate selection step is unnecessary - and the bias it used to add is gone.\n   - _Why_: This is the key identity: it shows the separate selection step is redundant, so the bias it caused can be removed entirely.\n6. Prove the convergence rate with the budget inside it. Assume the usual federated non-convex conditions: the loss is L-smooth, each client's stochastic gradient is unbiased with bounded noise, and clients' gradients differ from the global gradient in a bounded way (the (beta,kappa) heterogeneity model). Re-run the standard one-round-progress argument, keeping the term for clients drifting during their local epochs, but plug in V(B) for the participation variance. Now the budget B appears directly in the rate through V(B), instead of being assumed away.\n\n*The non-convex stationarity bound after substituting the budget-parameterized variance constant V(B): the first term vanishes in T, the second is the budget-sensitive variance floor.*\n$$ \\frac{1}{T}\\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\\mathbb{E}\\big\\|\\nabla f(\\theta_t)\\big\\|^2 \\;\\le\\; \\frac{f(\\theta_0)-f^{*}}{\\eta T} \\;+\\; \\frac{\\eta L}{2}\\,V(B) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This is where the budget B literally enters the convergence-rate constant, instead of being assumed away.\n7. Prove there is a smallest workable budget. Break the average stationarity over training into two pieces: a part that always shrinks as you train longer, and a 'floor' set by the update variance V(B). Assuming every client costs at least some minimum and is at most some maximum (and informativeness is bounded), show the floor behaves like A + D/B - it never reaches zero because every client costs something. Setting the floor equal to your target accuracy epsilon-squared defines $B_{min}:$ below it, no unbiased rule can hit the target; above it, the remaining gap falls off like 1/B. The fact that the $above-B_{min}$ rate looks like the standard rate is on purpose - the new result is the existence of $B_{min}$ and that the budget dial stays well-behaved right down to it.\n\n*The budget-vs-stationarity frontier: $B_{min}$ is where the variance floor equals the target tolerance epsilon-squared (below it no unbiased rule attains epsilon), and above it the gap shrinks as 1/B.*\n$$ V(B_{\\min}) = \\varepsilon^2,\\qquad V(B) = \\mathcal{O}\\!\\left(\\tfrac{1}{B}\\right)\\ \\text{for}\\ B > B_{\\min} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The floor is the frontier: it tells you the smallest budget that can still guarantee progress, and how fast extra budget helps.\n\n### Measurement & Falsification\n*Make V(B), the aggregation bias, and the $B_{min}$ frontier empirically checkable against cost-blind and greedy baselines.*\n\n8. Measure the two things the theory cares about. Once every 20 rounds, do a special check round where every client participates (no sampling) so you can compute the true full-participation update. Then, over the last several normal rounds, record V(B) (how much the global update jitters round to round, i.e. its variance) and the actual bias (how far the average of your sampled updates sits from the true full update). These check rounds are only for measurement and do not count against the budget.\n   - _Why_: This turns the central theoretical claim - that the budget enters the rate through V(B) and the update stays unbiased - into something you can measure.\n9. Test whether the idea actually wins. Make client costs heavy-tailed by drawing them from a lognormal distribution scaled to average 1. On CIFAR-10/100 (split very non-uniformly across 100 clients via Dirichlet 0.1) and FEMNIST, train a standard small network three ways, all spending the SAME total budget: (A) our cost-tilted unbiased sampler; (B) the same sampler but ignoring cost (lambda set to 0); (C) a greedy cost-aware selector that each round packs in the best value-per-cost clients and plain-averages them. Compare final test accuracy and how flat the gradient is at the end. As a negative control, check that turning the cost-tilt off (B) drops accuracy back to the cost-blind level; as a positive control, check that using ONLY the cost-tilt recovers most of the gain. If the idea is right, at a tight budget (A) beats both (B) and (C), and the accuracy-vs-budget curve levels off above a measurable minimum budget $B_{min}$ and collapses below it.\n   - _Why_: If the idea is right, the cost-tilted rule wins at tight budgets and the accuracy curve flattens above $B_{min}$ and collapses below it - and the controls show the cost-tilt is what causes the gain.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 成本倾斜的无偏参与：面向非凸联邦优化的单阶段采样与预算进入收敛率常数的保证\n\n**方法名称.** Cost-Tilted Unbiased Participation (CTUP)\n\n## 研究动机\n在联邦学习（FL）中，中心服务器通过反复请求少量客户端设备在各自私有数据上计算更新来训练共享模型。请求一个客户端并非免费——它消耗能量、网络带宽，有时还要补偿费用——所以服务器每轮有一个预算，只能负担一部分客户端。当前的成本感知方法把这件事拆成两步：先做选择，在预算内贪心地买下最便宜、最有用的客户端，再做聚合，把拿到的更新平均一下。隐藏的问题是：专挑便宜且梯度大的客户端会扭曲你看到的更新分布，于是平均后的更新不再等于全员参与时的结果——它有偏差，而这个偏差悄悄破坏了保证模型持续改进的数学。\n\n近期两条工作各自只走了一半。方差最优采样（2024）保持平均无偏，却完全忽略成本，因此无法告诉你如何把固定预算花在刀刃上；成本感知选择（2024-2026）跟踪了真实的逐客户端成本，却把它当作外部过滤器，没有刻画由此引入的偏差和收敛代价。没人问过：成本是否一开始就应该参与决定采样概率，而不是事后再补上。\n\n我们的想法消除了这道接缝。我们证明：受预算约束的最优选择，在数学上等同于一个单步采样器——它按成本倾斜每个客户端的选择概率并重加权以保持无偏：以正比于 $s_{k} /$ sqrt(mu + lambda $c_{k})$ 的概率选中客户端 k，其中 $s_{k}$ 是客户端的信息量，$c_{k}$ 是其成本，lambda 是由预算确定的单一旋钮。由于两阶段坍缩为一个，偏差消失，预算 B 直接进入收敛率常数。这还让我们刻画出一条前沿：存在一个最小预算 $B_{min}$，低于它任何无偏规则都无法保证模型下降，高于它残余误差以 1/B 缩小。\n\n## 方法\n### 成本倾斜采样器\n*把逐客户端成本与信息量转化为由单一预算乘子确定的单阶段无偏采样分布。*\n\n1. 为每个客户端维护两个数。其一，$s_{k}$：它的更新通常有多大——取该客户端最近一次更新的长度（L2 norm），并用 0.9 衰减的滑动平均加以平滑；从未见过的新客户端以已见客户端的平均 $s_{k}$ 起步。其二，$c_{k}$：该客户端有多昂贵——把它的通信量（收发的 megabytes）、本地能耗（watt-hours）以及补偿费用合成一个成本数，然后用本轮的平均成本去除每个客户端的成本，使数值在 1 附近，从而预算 B 可读作「能负担多少个平均客户端」。【作者需决定：在把通信、能耗、费用合成单一成本时各自的权重，取决于最想节省哪种资源。】\n   - _为什么_: 在成本能影响采样之前，你需要在同一量纲下同时掌握客户端的有用程度和昂贵程度。\n2. 通过一个小型两层搜索求出采样概率。外层用二分法调节一个数 lambda >= 0（「预算旋钮」），直到概率恰好花完预算；若预算足够宽松、无成本解已经满足，则 lambda 保持 0。给定 lambda 时，按 $s_{k} /$ sqrt(mu + lambda $c_{k})$ 为每个客户端打分，再选内层的数 mu，使得在把任何概率截断到 1 之后，概率之和等于目标期望数量 m。当期望花费与预算之差小于一个很小的容差时停止。这正是最优的成本倾斜采样器：更便宜、更有信息量的客户端获得更高概率，而 lambda 表示成本把概率往下拉的强度。\n\n*受预算约束的方差最小化问题的 KKT 闭式最优解：成本倾斜版的方差最优重要性采样，lambda 为唯一的预算乘子（lambda=0 退化为成本无关采样器）。*\n$$ p_k^{*} \\;\\propto\\; \\frac{s_k}{\\sqrt{\\mu + \\lambda c_k}},\\qquad \\lambda \\ge 0,\\quad \\sum_{k} p_k^{*} c_k = B \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: lambda 是在信息量与成本之间权衡的唯一旋钮——它由预算解出，而非手工调参。\n3. 通过为每个客户端独立投一次有偏硬币来真正挑选本轮客户端：以概率 $p_{k}*$ 纳入客户端 k。这样得到的集合大小在 m 附近波动。使用独立投币（而非总是取前 m 个客户端）正是让后续重加权恰好抵消选择偏差的关键。保存被选中的客户端及各自被选中的概率。\n   - _为什么_: 采样（而非确定性地选取头部客户端）正是让重加权保持更新无偏的前提。\n4. 构造无偏的全局更新，然后更新模型。每个被选中的客户端回传 $Delta_{k}$，即它在本地训练若干轮后对模型所做的改变（这是标准 FedAvg 的「伪梯度」）。把它们按各自被选中的概率相除再平均来合并：$g_{hat} =$ (1/m) sum $(1/p_{k}*) Delta_{k}$。这个相除正是让平均值在期望上等于全员参与结果的诀窍。最后更新模型：theta <- theta - eta $* g_{hat}$，其中 eta 是服务器步长。\n\n*采用 $1/p_{k}$ 重要性重加权的全局梯度估计量，其期望等于全员参与的梯度——正是该重加权保证了更新无偏。*\n$$ \\hat{g} = \\frac{1}{m}\\sum_{k\\,\\in\\,\\mathcal{S}}\\frac{1}{p_k}\\,\\Delta_k,\\qquad \\mathbb{E}[\\hat{g}] = \\frac{1}{N}\\sum_{k=1}^{N}\\Delta_k \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 用各自的选择概率去除每个更新，抵消了采样偏斜，使平均后的更新在期望上等于全员参与的梯度。\n\n### 预算进入常数的理论\n*证明两阶段/单阶段等价，并把预算带入非凸收敛率常数与 $B_{min}$ 前沿。*\n\n5. 在纸面上证明两步法与单步采样器给出同一个最优解。写下问题「在满足成本预算且保持平均无偏的前提下，挑选方差最小的采样分布」，用每个客户端典型的更新平方大小（$s_{k}$ 的平方）作为其方差代理。用标准的约束优化条件（KKT）求解，恰好得到成本倾斜概率 $p_{k}*$ 正比于 $s_{k} /$ sqrt(mu + lambda $c_{k})$。由于无论把它看作「先选预算内子集再平均」还是「一个成本倾斜的重要性采样器」，答案都是同一个分布，独立的选择步骤便是多余的——它过去引入的偏差也随之消失。\n   - _为什么_: 这是关键恒等式：它表明独立的选择步骤是多余的，因而它造成的偏差可被彻底移除。\n6. 证明把预算嵌入其中的收敛率。假设通常的联邦非凸条件：损失为 L-smooth，每个客户端的随机梯度无偏且噪声有界，客户端梯度与全局梯度的差异有界（即 (beta,kappa) 异质性模型）。重做标准的单轮进展论证，保留客户端在本地多轮训练中漂移的项，但把参与方差替换为 V(B)。这样预算 B 就通过 V(B) 直接出现在收敛率中，而不再被假设掉。\n\n*代入预算参数化方差常数 V(B) 后的非凸驻点界：第一项随 T 衰减，第二项为受预算影响的方差地板。*\n$$ \\frac{1}{T}\\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\\mathbb{E}\\big\\|\\nabla f(\\theta_t)\\big\\|^2 \\;\\le\\; \\frac{f(\\theta_0)-f^{*}}{\\eta T} \\;+\\; \\frac{\\eta L}{2}\\,V(B) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这正是预算 B 真正进入收敛率常数之处，而不是被假设掉。\n7. 证明存在一个最小可行预算。把训练过程中的平均驻点度量拆成两块：一块随训练变长总会缩小，另一块是由更新方差 V(B) 决定的「地板」。假设每个客户端成本至少有个下限、至多有个上限（且信息量有界），证明该地板形如 A + D/B——它永不为零，因为每个客户端都有成本。令地板等于目标精度 epsilon 的平方，即定义出 $B_{min}$：低于它，任何无偏规则都无法达到目标；高于它，残余差距以 1/B 衰减。$B_{min}$ 之上的收敛率看起来像标准收敛率是有意为之——新结果在于 $B_{min}$ 的存在性，以及预算旋钮一直到该边界都保持良态。\n\n*预算-驻点前沿：$B_{min}$ 是方差地板等于目标容差 $\\epsilon ^{2}$ 之处（低于它任何无偏规则都无法达到 $\\epsilon $），高于它精度差距以 1/B 缩小。*\n$$ V(B_{\\min}) = \\varepsilon^2,\\qquad V(B) = \\mathcal{O}\\!\\left(\\tfrac{1}{B}\\right)\\ \\text{for}\\ B > B_{\\min} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这块地板就是前沿：它告诉你仍能保证前进的最小预算，以及额外预算的帮助有多快。\n\n### 测量与证伪\n*使 V(B)、聚合偏差与 $B_{min}$ 前沿可对照成本无关与贪心基线进行实测。*\n\n8. 测量理论关心的两件事。每 20 轮做一次特殊的检查轮，让所有客户端都参与（不采样），从而算出真正的全员参与更新。然后，在最近若干个正常轮上，记录 V(B)（全局更新逐轮抖动多大，即其方差）以及真实偏差（采样更新的平均值与真正全员更新相差多远）。这些检查轮仅用于测量，不计入预算。\n   - _为什么_: 这把核心理论主张——预算通过 V(B) 进入收敛率、且更新保持无偏——变成了可测量的量。\n9. 检验这个想法是否真的取胜。把客户端成本设为重尾：从对数正态分布抽取并缩放到均值 1。在 CIFAR-10/100（通过 Dirichlet 0.1 极不均匀地分到 100 个客户端）与 FEMNIST 上，用三种方式训练一个标准小网络，且都花费相同的总预算：(A) 我们的成本倾斜无偏采样器；(B) 同一采样器但忽略成本（把 lambda 设为 0）；(C) 一个贪心的成本感知选择器，每轮塞入性价比最高的客户端并直接平均。比较最终测试精度以及结束时梯度有多平。作为负对照，检验关掉成本倾斜（B）会使精度回落到成本无关水平；作为正对照，检验仅使用成本倾斜能恢复大部分增益。若想法成立，在紧预算下（A）胜过（B）与（C），且精度-预算曲线在一个可测量的最小预算 $B_{min}$ 之上趋平、之下崩塌。\n   - _为什么_: 若想法成立，成本倾斜规则在紧预算下取胜，精度曲线在 $B_{min}$ 之上变平、之下崩塌——而对照证明增益正源自成本倾斜。\n\n"},{"id":"87","run_dir":"run_prompt87_omnireward","index":87,"title":"Anchored Omni-Reward: A Cross-Modally Comparable, Steerable Preference Scale","title_zh":"锚定式 Omni-Reward：一个可跨模态比较、可调控的偏好尺度","method_name":"Anchored Omni-Reward (AOR)","hook":"An omni-modal reward model that scores audio, video, image and text on a single human-anchored scale, so a reward of r means the same preference strength in every modality and an RLHF optimizer can mix candidates across modalities without a per-modality calibration hack. We show a per-modality-fit reward head silently fails a held-out cross-modal preference test that an anchor-tied head passes, and that a compound free-form criterion can be split into individually-calibrated axes the user steers at inference.","anchor_pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","anchor_pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","domain_category":"LLM Alignment, Safety & Behavior","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes the reward scale comparable across modalities: an omni-modal RM's score of r on audio and r on video are fit from independent per-modality preference pools, so equal scores do not denote equal human-preference strength, and nothing anchors the zero-point and unit of the reward across modalities (additive need — the outcome 'cross-modally interchangeable reward magnitude' is what is missing).","pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by recasting the opaque question 'does reward r mean the same preference strength across modalities' as a concrete measurement object: a joint preference-scaling estimator over a single shared latent reward axis identified from a small seed of human-judged cross-modal preference pairs (the anchor set), so the reward's unit and zero-point are fixed by fidelity to those human cross-modal judgments rather than fit independently per modality; correctness is certified by causal intervention (corrupting the anchor set must collapse cross-modal-swap accuracy).","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf, when handed a compound free-form preference criterion containing conflicting sub-preferences, exposes those sub-preferences as an explicit, identified, and individually-calibrated set of axes the user can steer at inference; the criterion is consumed as opaque conditioning text and the conflict is collapsed into one scalar (additive need — a steerable, decomposed preference response is missing, phrased without prescribing how the axes are obtained).","pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by decomposing the compound free-form criterion's reward into an additive set of per-axis components living in the SAME anchored latent space, partitioning by a measured discriminating property (which axes' human-judgment residuals are mutually anti-correlated = conflicting), and giving each axis its own calibrated head plus a user-exposed mixing weight; an error decomposition bounds how the per-axis treatment recovers the held-out compound preference, so the steering weights mean the same thing across modalities because every axis is expressed in the anchored unit.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"omni-modal reward modeling for RLHF / preference alignment (text, image, video, audio, 3D)","n_papers":49,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":26},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":4,"papers":[{"source":"openalex","title":"A Survey of Robot Intelligence with Large Language Models"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Building and better understanding vision-language models: insights and future directions"},{"source":"openalex","title":"MME-Survey: A Comprehensive Survey on Evaluation of Multimodal LLMs"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Selecting Source Tasks for Transfer Learning of Human Preferences"}],"more":0},{"year":2025,"n":36,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Omni-Reward: Towards Generalist Omni-Modal Reward Modeling with Free-Form Preferences"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Scaling Omni-Modal Pretraining with Multimodal Context: Advancing Universal Representation Learning Across Modalities"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"SAIL-Embedding Technical Report: Omni-modal Embedding Foundation Model"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"HumanOmniV2: From Understanding to Omni-Modal Reasoning with Context"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"R1-Omni: Explainable Omni-Multimodal Emotion Recognition with Reinforcement Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"UNO-Bench: A Unified Benchmark for Exploring the Compositional Law Between Uni-modal and Omni-modal in Omni Models"}],"more":30},{"year":2026,"n":10,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"e5-omni: Explicit Cross-modal Alignment for Omni-modal Embeddings"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Boosting Omni-Modal Language Models: Staged Post-Training with Visually Debiased Evaluation"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Mitigating Reward Hacking in RLHF via Bayesian Non-negative Reward Modeling"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Omni-Diffusion: Unified Multimodal Understanding and Generation with Masked Discrete Diffusion"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"FutureOmni: Evaluating Future Forecasting from Omni-Modal Context for Multimodal LLMs"}],"more":4}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":6,"share":0.122},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":4,"share":0.082},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering; adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"self_supervised_signal_engineering; adapt_via_conditioning","count":3,"share":0.061},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation; adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"unify_into_shared_representation; adapt_via_conditioning","count":2,"share":0.041},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate; adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"decompose_and_delegate; adapt_via_conditioning","count":2,"share":0.041},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition; reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"heterogeneous_decomposition; reframe_as_solvable_object","count":2,"share":0.041},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution; unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"architectural_operator_substitution; unify_into_shared_representation","count":2,"share":0.041},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":1,"share":0.02}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Generalist omni-modal reward models such as Omni-Reward (semanticscholar:4f7e302e85f40de21758f28245e0c28743eeff69) and UnifiedReward (openalex:W6979242199) achieve breadth by feeding a free-form preference criterion in as a text prompt and emitting a single scalar (or pairwise win) per modality, but the scalar is fit independently on each modality's preference pool, so equal reward values across modalities (e.g., a video score and an audio score) do not denote equal human-preference strength — there is no shared anchoring that makes the reward scale cross-modally comparable, and when an RLHF optimizer or best-of-n selector mixes candidates from different modalities the model has no calibrated way to say which is actually preferred. Compounding this, when a free-form criterion bundles conflicting sub-preferences (helpfulness vs. harmlessness, fidelity vs. brevity), the RM and the decomposed-preference methods that could expose those axes (Decomposed Reward Models, openalex:W7082259131; ternary-preference identification, openalex:W4415884644) operate only on text and collapse the conflict into one scalar rather than surfacing a steerable, calibrated tradeoff the user controls at inference. The current machinery cannot produce the missing quantity because per-modality scalar regression has no constraint tying its zero-point and unit across modalities, and free-form conditioning treats the criterion as opaque text rather than as a position in an identified preference space.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:4f7e302e85f40de21758f28245e0c28743eeff69","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Omni-Reward trains a generalist omni-modal RM that conditions on a free-form preference criterion (passed as a text prompt) and scores text/image/video/audio/3D, with CoT reasoning and a tie-aware benchmark, fitting reward heads on a mixed Omni-RewardData pool. Its method composes per-task scores but never constrains the reward scale to be comparable across modalities (the ablations show large per-modality score-range differences, e.g. T2A vs T2T), and it consumes the free-form criterion as opaque conditioning text without identifying or exposing the conflicting sub-preference axes inside a compound criterion, so a user cannot dial a calibrated tradeoff and an optimizer cannot trust that equal rewards across modalities mean equal preference."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W6979242199","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"UnifiedReward learns one reward model jointly over multimodal understanding and generation (pairwise + pointwise), arguing cross-task synergy. It is image/video+text only with no audio/3D, uses a fixed pairwise preference notion, and provides neither cross-modal scale calibration nor any inference-time steering over conflicting preference dimensions."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7082259131","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Decomposed Reward Models run PCA over embedding-difference vectors of preferred-minus-rejected text responses to extract orthogonal preference basis vectors that can be linearly recombined for different use cases. The decomposition is discovered post-hoc on text-only data with no modality axis, the basis directions are not anchored to a shared interpretable scale, and the recombination weights are not exposed as a calibrated user-facing control at inference, nor validated across modalities."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415884644","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"This work proves (via an econometrics identification argument) that binary preference comparisons cannot identify latent annotator preference types from finite data, and that rankings over three or more responses are necessary. The result is text-only and addresses identifiability of latent types, not cross-modal comparability of the reward scale nor user-steerable conditioning on the identified axes once recovered."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"omni-modal reward modeling for RLHF / preference alignment (text, image, video, audio, 3D)","venue":"ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML main track","time":"2026","data":["Omni-RewardData / Omni-RewardBench style cross-modal preference pairs (T2T, TI2T, TV2T, TA2T, T2I, T2V, T2A, T23D)","diverse-annotator preference datasets with per-criterion labels","existing VL/multimodal preference corpora (Skywork-VL, UnifiedReward training data)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with RLHF / multimodal alignment background","preference":"both","baseline":"Omni-Reward (free-form-criterion generalist omni-modal RM); UnifiedReward; Skywork-VL Reward; Decomposed Reward Models (PCA)","limitation":"current omni-modal RMs emit a single scalar conditioned on a free-form criterion prompt, but the scalar's scale is fit per-modality from independent preference pools, so a given reward value does not denote the same human-preference strength across modalities, and when a free-form criterion bundles conflicting sub-preferences the RM silently collapses them into one number rather than exposing the tradeoff for the user to steer.","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object both legs read from and write to is the ANCHORED LATENT PREFERENCE AXIS A: a single 1-D scale (per identified preference dimension) on which every modality's reward is expressed, whose unit and zero-point are tied to human cross-modal judgments rather than to any one modality's pool. Leg 1 (cross-modal comparability) reframes 'is r comparable across modalities' as estimating A by a paired-comparison scaling model. Concretely: collect a small ANCHOR SET of N_a (target ~3-5k) human preference pairs where the two candidates are in DIFFERENT modalities for the same prompt (e.g. 'which better answers this question, this audio reply or this video reply'); fit the omni-modal reward head r_theta(x, criterion) jointly under a Bradley-Terry likelihood on BOTH within-modality pairs and the cross-modal anchor pairs, with a hard constraint that the anchor pairs share one global scale (a single temperature beta, not per-modality beta_m). The load-bearing readout is the cross-modal scale-gap g = mean over anchor pairs of |r_theta(winner)-r_theta(loser) predicted| vs human win-rate-implied logit; g is computed from model logits (model-internal) against human labels (external oracle) and is driven to zero by the joint constraint. A free index is the modality-embedding offset b_m: in the per-modality baseline b_m is fit freely per pool (giving incomparable zero-points); our construction ties b_m through the anchor pairs so all b_m share one origin. Leg 2 (steerable decomposition) treats the reward for a compound criterion c as additive over K axes: r_theta(x,c) = sum_k w_k * a_k(x), where each a_k is a head producing a value ON THE SAME axis A (same anchored unit), and w_k in [0,1] is a user-facing mixing weight (default w_k read from the criterion text via a learned criterion->weight map, overridable at inference). The discriminating property that partitions axes is the sign of the pairwise correlation of per-axis human-judgment residuals: axes whose residuals are anti-correlated on the same prompts are 'conflicting' and are NOT collapsed; a held-out error decomposition bounds the compound-preference error as sum of per-axis calibrated errors plus an interaction term we measure. Because every a_k is expressed in the anchored unit from Leg 1, a steering weight of 0.7 on 'fidelity' vs 0.3 on 'brevity' denotes the same tradeoff whether the candidate is audio or video — the two legs share the single object A, which is why this is one paper. Prior numbers: Omni-Reward's own ablation (fulltext_cache.json) shows per-task overall scores spanning ~46-65 depending on data mix, evidence the per-modality scale is not anchored; DRMs (openalex:W7082259131) recover orthogonal axes but never tie them to a shared anchored unit or expose w_k at inference.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The two gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules because the steerable axes of Leg 2 are only meaningful if their magnitudes are already cross-modally comparable — i.e. Leg 2 is built ON TOP of Leg 1's anchored axis A; the evidence is that without a shared unit a per-axis weight would mean different things across modalities, re-introducing exactly the bottleneck. I considered a two-module design (a separate post-hoc calibration network mapping per-modality scores to a common scale, then a separate decomposition) and rejected it because post-hoc affine calibration cannot fix rank inconsistencies across modalities and leaves the decomposition un-anchored. REGRESSION CHECK (method_lineage): the construction must not reduce to node c0 (plain Rasch/IRT anchor-item scaling) — it differs because the anchor set is cross-MODAL paired comparisons fitted jointly with the reward head's representation rather than a fixed item-difficulty table over a single modality, and not to node c2 (anchor-modality embedding alignment) — comparability here is enforced on the REWARD logit via human cross-modal labels, not on representation similarity; both avoided nodes are recorded here.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: take an open omni-modal backbone (e.g. a Qwen-Omni-class encoder), train two reward heads on the same data — a per-modality-fit baseline (free beta_m, free b_m) and our anchor-tied head (shared beta, tied b_m via the cross-modal anchor set) — and measure cross-modal-swap preference accuracy on a held-out set of pairs whose winner and loser are in different modalities. If the candidate works, cross-modal-swap accuracy increases for the anchored head relative to the per-modality baseline (which should sit near chance on this slice while both stay high on within-modality slices), and steering monotonicity holds (raising w_k on an axis raises that axis's measured quality in the selected response). The named load-bearing variable is the cross-modal scale-gap g (model anchor-pair logit vs human win-rate logit); negative control: permute the human labels on the anchor set before training (destroying the true cross-modal signal while keeping anchor-set size, modality mix, and compute identical) — this should drive cross-modal-swap ACCURACY (the downstream task-outcome metric) back to the per-modality baseline, not merely change g's value. A positive control trains a stripped head that uses ONLY the anchor-pair constraint (no within-modality auxiliary loss) and should recover most of the cross-modal-swap accuracy gain, identifying the anchor constraint as the mechanism.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:4f7e302e85f40de21758f28245e0c28743eeff69","delta":"Omni-Reward conditions on free-form criteria and scores per modality but fits each modality's scale on its own pool (its ablation shows >20-point cross-task score-range gaps); we construct a reward whose unit and zero-point are tied to human cross-modal anchor pairs so equal rewards denote equal preference strength across modalities, and we expose the criterion's conflicting axes as individually-calibrated steerable weights rather than collapsing them."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W6979242199","delta":"UnifiedReward shares one head across vision tasks for synergy but provides no cross-modal scale anchoring and no audio/3D; we derive a measured cross-modal-swap consistency guarantee and a held-out error decomposition tying steering weights to one anchored unit across all modalities."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W7082259131","delta":"DRMs decompose text preferences into orthogonal PCA directions discovered post-hoc; we instead decompose a compound criterion into axes that live in a human-anchored cross-modal unit and are user-steerable at inference, with a conflict criterion (residual anti-correlation) rather than orthogonality, validated across modalities."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415884644","delta":"They prove binary comparisons cannot identify latent annotator types and require ternary rankings (text-only identifiability); we use cross-modal paired comparisons not to identify annotator types but to anchor the reward UNIT across modalities, a comparability construction their identifiability result does not provide."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:4f7e302e85f40de21758f28245e0c28743eeff69","what_step_was_missed":"Omni-Reward collects preference data per modality and conditions the reward on a free-form criterion, but it never constructs a cross-MODAL anchor set of paired comparisons nor imposes a shared-scale (single global temperature + tied modality offset) constraint that would force the reward logit to be comparable across modalities; building that anchor set and the joint shared-scale Bradley-Terry constraint — and decomposing the criterion into per-axis heads expressed in that anchored unit — is the missing construction that would have made the reward cross-modally interchangeable and steerable."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":347,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"No hard floor fired: gap_closure_reject_check has no candidate_match: yes (aggregate borderline only), recipe_application_check is applied for both legs, and anti_pattern_check matched_pattern_id is null. The two borderline reject lessons ('porting a known technique' for C00 Bradley-Terry scaling; 'sensitivity proxy rediscovers known results' for C04's conflict criterion) sit in differentiation framing rather than the core_mechanism's central argument and are already mitigated by the permutation control, the uniform-baseline comparison, and the held-out error decomposition; and paper_pointed_threat (Omni-RRM) is adjacent but non-subsuming (it produces per-modality rubric scores, not a cross-modal anchored scale). These are concerns to surface for Phase 4 reviewer_concerns_and_responses, not load-bearing structural failures, so the candidate advances.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes the reward scale comparable across modalities: an omni-modal RM's score of r on audio and r on video are fit from independent per-modality preference pools, so equal scores do not denote equal human-preference strength, and nothing anchors the zero-point and unit of the reward across modalities (additive need — the outcome 'cross-modally interchangeable reward magnitude' is what is missing).","main_pattern":"reframe_as_solvable_object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The signature failure is treating the reframing as a mechanical wrapper: taking an established attribution/estimation tool and pointing it at a new granularity, architecture, or domain without re-deriving why the resulting scores are faithful to the model, supplying the computation but not the causal validation or axiomatic argument for the proposed definition.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Pointing an off-the-shelf decomposition at a coarser input granularity without showing the coarser units preserve the signal reads as a wrapper, not a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate does not point an off-the-shelf decomposition at coarser granularity; it constructs a new cross-modal anchor set plus a shared-scale Bradley-Terry constraint (single global temperature + tied modality offsets) that did not exist before."},{"lesson_quoted":"Porting a known attribution technique to a new architecture or domain while ignoring that technique's documented failure modes — and omitting comparisons to alternatives — leaves reviewers unable to see any unique benefit.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"Bradley-Terry scaling is a known technique ported to the cross-modal setting; the candidate mitigates by comparing against a per-modality-fit baseline and a permuted-label control, but the audit notes the differentiation from classical psychometric anchoring should be foregrounded for reviewers."},{"lesson_quoted":"Proposing a new attribution definition without an axiomatic or causal argument for why it should count as ground-truth collapses the moment a reviewer asks why this is the real importance.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate's definition of comparability is grounded causally: the negative-control (permute anchor labels) must drive cross-modal-swap accuracy back to baseline, supplying the causal argument the lesson demands."},{"lesson_quoted":"Conflating a methodological artifact — a computation-granularity difference, a degenerate zero baseline — with genuine signal undermines the entire premise once the confound is identified.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The positive/negative controls (anchor-only stripped head; permuted-label head) are explicitly designed to separate the anchor signal from training-size / compute confounds."},{"lesson_quoted":"Building a suppression or privacy method without formalizing the threat model leaves the central guarantee unverifiable regardless of strong empirical numbers.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Not a suppression/privacy method; inapplicable."},{"lesson_quoted":"Surveying or recombining fragmented methods without a unifying axis or a decisive controlled experiment yields a contribution reviewers dismiss as anecdotal.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate has a single unifying object (the anchored latent axis A) and a decisive controlled experiment (cross-modal-swap accuracy under the label-permutation control)."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf, when handed a compound free-form preference criterion containing conflicting sub-preferences, exposes those sub-preferences as an explicit, identified, and individually-calibrated set of axes the user can steer at inference; the criterion is consumed as opaque conditioning text and the conflict is collapsed into one scalar (additive need — a steerable, decomposed preference response is missing, phrased without prescribing how the axes are obtained).","main_pattern":"heterogeneous_decomposition","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is treating the partition criterion itself as the contribution while leaving its value unproven, so reviewers map the discriminator onto an established technique, and the scheme is rarely benchmarked against both the strongest uniform baseline and the obvious cheap alternative.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Presenting a sensitivity or redundancy proxy as the novelty invites the verdict that it rediscovers known mixed-precision or low-rank results unless it is sharply differentiated from the obvious prior criterion.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The discriminating property (per-axis human-judgment residual anti-correlation = conflict) could be read as a known correlation criterion; the candidate differentiates it as the conflict-graph that drives non-collapse, distinct from PCA-orthogonality used by DRMs, but this differentiation must be made explicit."},{"lesson_quoted":"Omitting comparison against both the strongest uniform baseline and the obvious cheap alternative (SVD/PCA, structured dropout, a natively trained smaller model) leaves reviewers unable to tell whether the partition buys anything at all.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The falsification compares against a single-scalar (uniform) reward and the PCA-style DRM is named as the obvious cheap alternative in differentiation_from_lit; the steering-monotonicity metric tests what the partition buys."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a storage or throughput claim only on toy-scale models — where the compression bottleneck does not actually bite — undermines the entire motivation no matter how clean the method is.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Not a compression claim; the deployment metric is cross-modal-swap accuracy and steering monotonicity on a real omni backbone, where the bottleneck genuinely bites."},{"lesson_quoted":"A clever partition with no measured real-world deployment metric (no inference latency or memory speedup) reads as a proxy-only contribution and stalls at borderline.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The deployment metric is the downstream best-of-n / RLHF selection quality (steering monotonicity), not a proxy."},{"lesson_quoted":"Skipping any analysis of why the heterogeneity exists — the data or value distribution that drives the partition — makes the technical novelty and the potential impact impossible to assess.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Step 7 explicitly measures the per-axis residual correlation distribution that establishes the heterogeneity (which axes conflict), satisfying this lesson."},{"lesson_quoted":"Bolting together established components (distillation plus pruning plus calibration) without an error bound or artifact specific to the new setting reads as incremental even when the target application is timely and important.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate supplies a held-out error decomposition (per-axis error + interaction term) specific to the anchored-axis setting, the artifact this lesson requires."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No Reject lesson is marked candidate_match: yes, so nothing triggered the hard floor. The aggregate is borderline, driven by the reframe leg's 'porting a known technique' lesson (Bradley-Terry scaling into the cross-modal setting) and the decomposition leg's 'sensitivity proxy rediscovers known results' lesson (the residual-anti-correlation conflict criterion vs PCA-orthogonality) — both are mitigated by controls/comparisons present in the candidate but warrant explicit reviewer-facing differentiation."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes the reward scale comparable across modalities: an omni-modal RM's score of r on audio and r on video are fit from independent per-modality preference pools, so equal scores do not denote equal human-preference strength, and nothing anchors the zero-point and unit of the reward across modalities (additive need — the outcome 'cross-modally interchangeable reward magnitude' is what is missing).","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Recast an opaque question (here: 'does reward r denote the same preference strength across modalities') as a concrete measurement over a well-studied object — an estimator/decomposition whose correctness criterion is fidelity-to-a-fixed-model, certified by a causal intervention that flips behavior when the identified object is perturbed, rather than by plausibility.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism recasts comparability as a paired-comparison scaling estimator over the anchored latent axis A (the well-studied object: Bradley-Terry scaling with a shared global temperature), and certifies fidelity causally via the load-bearing variable g (cross-modal scale-gap) whose true producer, the human-labeled anchor set, when permuted, must collapse cross-modal-swap accuracy — exactly the perturb-the-identified-object-and-watch-behavior-flip move the cluster signature demands.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf, when handed a compound free-form preference criterion containing conflicting sub-preferences, exposes those sub-preferences as an explicit, identified, and individually-calibrated set of axes the user can steer at inference; the criterion is consumed as opaque conditioning text and the conflict is collapsed into one scalar (additive need — a steerable, decomposed preference response is missing, phrased without prescribing how the axes are obtained).","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Discriminate components by a magnitude/sensitivity/influence/redundancy criterion into structurally distinct populations, apply a treatment matched to each partition's property, and supply an error/sensitivity decomposition that bounds how the differentiated treatment recovers the original objective — that analysis, not the partition idea, is the contribution.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism partitions the compound criterion's axes by a measured discriminating property (sign of per-axis human-judgment residual correlation = conflicting vs collapsible), applies a tailored calibrated head a_k per axis expressed in the anchored unit (the matched treatment), and supplies a held-out error decomposition (sum of per-axis calibrated errors + measured interaction term) bounding recovery of the compound preference — the cluster's load-bearing error-decomposition artifact. The cluster's [Accept] examples are artifact-compression-flavored while this applies the same move to preference-criterion components, but the signature operation (discriminate-by-measured-property + tailored-treatment + recovery-bounding decomposition) is genuinely performed.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries perform their cluster's signature move: C00's recast-as-measurement-with-causal-certification is enacted by the anchor-set scaling estimator + permutation control, and C04's discriminate-by-measured-property + recovery-bounding error decomposition is enacted by the residual-anti-correlation conflict partition + held-out error decomposition. Neither is the parent's generic gist only."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["reframe_as_solvable_object","heterogeneous_decomposition"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"The composition {reframe_as_solvable_object, heterogeneous_decomposition} is not one of the three flagged reject-favored compositions (all three pair heterogeneous_decomposition with self_supervised_signal_engineering, structural_prior_encoding, or architectural_operator_substitution); it is the explicitly watch-listed hetero_decomp+reframe pairing (p_O=47.4%, just misses the -12pp threshold), so no required mitigation applies, though the candidate should still keep the two legs' contributions independently identifiable."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"Omni-RRM: Advancing Omni Reward Modeling via Automatic Rubric-Grounded Preference Synthesis","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"Omni-RRM (2026-01) is the most specific competitor: it is an omni-modal (text/image/video/audio) reward model that produces structured, multi-dimension preference judgments with dimension-wise justifications, overlapping both the omni-coverage and the per-dimension-decomposition aspects of the candidate. The candidate's claim stands because Omni-RRM's dimension-wise judgments are produced as separate rubric scores per modality and are NOT placed on a single human-anchored cross-modal SCALE — it does not construct a cross-modal paired-comparison anchor set, does not impose a shared global temperature / tied modality offset, and does not expose inference-time steering weights whose magnitude denotes the same tradeoff across modalities; its scalar/rubric scores remain per-modality-incomparable, which is exactly the gap the candidate closes. The candidate falls only if Omni-RRM is shown to already deliver cross-modal-swap preference consistency, which its rubric-grounded design does not measure or guarantee.","addressable_via":"Foreground the cross-modal-swap-accuracy metric and the anchored-unit steering claim as the differentiator against rubric-grounded multi-dimension RMs (Omni-RRM, VisionReward) in differentiation_from_lit and the falsification, since the threat is non-subsuming but adjacent."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Anchored Omni-Reward: A Cross-Modally Comparable, Steerable Preference Scale\n\n**Method.** Anchored Omni-Reward (AOR)\n\n## Motivation\nA reward model is a scorer that an alignment system uses to decide which of two AI answers a human would prefer; the score then drives training (RLHF, Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback) or picks the best of several candidate answers (best-of-n). An omni-modal reward model is supposed to score answers in any form — text, image, video, audio, 3D — with one model. The catch in today's best version, Omni-Reward, is that it learns each modality's score on that modality's own pile of human comparisons, separately. So a score of, say, 0.8 on a video answer and 0.8 on an audio answer are NOT on the same ruler: they were calibrated apart, and equal numbers do not mean equally preferred. The instant you ask the model to compare a video answer against an audio answer — the whole point of being omni-modal — it has no honest way to say which is better. Omni-Reward's own report shows its per-task scores swing by about 20 points depending on the data mix, which is exactly this un-anchored-ruler problem.\n\nA second problem: you give the model a free-form instruction like 'prefer answers that are faithful but also brief.' Those two wishes can fight each other, but the model crushes them into a single number and never tells you the tradeoff, let alone lets you dial it. Text-only methods that split preferences into separate directions (Decomposed Reward Models, which use Principal Component Analysis, PCA, to find orthogonal preference directions) never put those directions on a shared, human-meaningful ruler and never hand you a knob at use-time.\n\nBoth problems have the same root and the same fix: build one shared 'preference ruler' — a single anchored axis — that every modality and every sub-preference is measured on. We pin the ruler's zero and unit using a small set of human comparisons where the two options are in DIFFERENT modalities (e.g. 'is this audio reply or this video reply better for this prompt'), and we force the model to honor one global scale for those comparisons. This is buildable now because open omni backbones exist, cross-modal preference data is now collectable at the few-thousand-comparison scale, and steerable-reward tooling gives us a way to expose per-axis knobs — none of which previously anchored those knobs across modalities.\n\nWhen this works, an alignment optimizer can finally mix audio, video, image and text candidates and trust that a bigger reward means more human-preferred, with no per-modality patch. And a user can set 0.7 weight on faithfulness vs 0.3 on brevity and have that tradeoff mean the same thing whether the answer is audio or video.\n\n## Method\n### Background / data\n*Standard within-modality preference data assembly that supports but is not the contribution.*\n\n1. Gather ordinary same-form preference pairs (text vs text, audio vs audio, video vs video, image vs image) from existing public preference datasets. Put every pair into the same record format as the anchor pairs (minus the different-form flag) and tag each pair as either within-form or anchor, so one data loader can feed both and the training step knows which branch each pair belongs to.\n   - _Why_: These keep the model sharp at telling good from bad inside each modality while the anchor pairs fix the cross-modal scale.\n\n### Cross-modal anchoring\n*Pin the reward's zero-point and unit to human cross-modal judgments so reward magnitudes are comparable across modalities.*\n\n2. Build a cross-modal anchor set. Pick prompts whose answer can be given in two or more forms — text, spoken audio, a short video, or an image — keeping a prompt only if at least two ready-made generators (one per modality) each give a usable answer. For each prompt make pairs where the two options are in DIFFERENT forms (e.g. an audio answer vs a video answer), and collect at least three independent human votes per pair (A better / B better / tie). Turn the non-tie votes into a human win-rate for that pair and keep the tie share separately. Save each pair as a record holding the prompt, both candidates with their forms, the win-rate, and the annotators. Aim for about 3-5 thousand pairs and set aside a portion (split by prompt, so no prompt is in both) for evaluation.\n   - _Why_: These cross-modal human comparisons are the only signal that tells the model what 'equally preferred' means ACROSS modalities, which is what pins the shared ruler.\n3. Attach ONE scoring head to a frozen omni encoder that already turns any input (text, audio, video, image) into a fixed-length vector. The head combines that vector with an encoding of the criterion text and outputs a single score. Add one shared temperature $\\beta $ (a single positive number for all cross-form comparisons) and a small table of per-form offsets $b_{m}$ (one number per form, added on the cross-form branch and reused for every pair of that form). The comparison baseline is the same head but with a separate temperature for each form and offsets fit separately inside each form's own data.\n   - _Why_: Using one $\\beta $ and tied offsets forces a single shared zero and unit, so cross-modal comparability is built in rather than hoped for.\n4. Train the head by making it predict the human preference on both the same-form pairs and the cross-form pairs, using a standard preference-fitting loss (Bradley-Terry, which models the chance one option is preferred as a logistic function of the score gap). Force the single shared scale simply by having the cross-form pairs use the one shared temperature and the one offset table — there is no separate per-form temperature on that branch to drift apart. Train everything together, and in each batch mix a roughly equal number of cross-form and same-form pairs so the smaller cross-form set is not drowned out; use a tie-aware version of the loss that accounts for the ties recorded earlier.\n\n*Joint Bradley-Terry loss: within-modality pairs $P_{wm}$ and the cross-modal anchor pairs A, where the anchor pairs share one global temperature $\\beta $ and tied modality offsets $b_{m}$ rather than per-modality $\\beta _{m},$ forcing one common scale.*\n$$ \\mathcal{L} = -\\sum_{(i,j)\\in\\mathcal{P}_{\\mathrm{wm}}} \\log\\sigma\\!\\big(\\beta_m\\,(r_\\theta(x_i)-r_\\theta(x_j))\\big)\\;-\\;\\sum_{(i,j)\\in\\mathcal{A}} \\log\\sigma\\!\\big(\\beta\\,(r_\\theta(x_i)+b_{m_i}-r_\\theta(x_j)-b_{m_j})\\big) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This is the core step: the joint constraint pushes the cross-modal human signal into the reward score so magnitudes line up across modalities.\n5. At each training step measure two things on held-out data. First, the cross-form scale-gap: how far the head's predicted score difference is from what the human win-rate implies, averaged over held-out cross-form pairs — this should fall toward zero. Second, cross-form-swap accuracy: on held-out pairs whose two options are in different forms, pick the higher-scoring option (using its form offset) and check how often that matches the human majority choice (random guessing is about 50%). Also report both on same-form pairs to confirm both heads stay accurate there.\n\n*Cross-modal scale-gap g: the mean absolute discrepancy on held-out anchor pairs between the model's predicted reward difference and the human win-rate logit; the joint constraint drives g toward 0.*\n$$ g = \\frac{1}{|\\mathcal{A}_{\\mathrm{ho}}|}\\sum_{(i,j)\\in\\mathcal{A}_{\\mathrm{ho}}} \\Big| \\big(r_\\theta(x_i)+b_{m_i}-r_\\theta(x_j)-b_{m_j}\\big) - \\mathrm{logit}\\,\\hat p^{\\,\\mathrm{human}}_{ij} \\Big| \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: g tells you whether the ruler is calibrated; cross-modal-swap accuracy tells you whether that translates into actually picking the human-preferred cross-modal answer.\n\n### Steerable axis decomposition\n*Split a compound criterion into per-axis calibrated heads on the same anchored ruler with user-facing, cross-modally meaningful weights.*\n\n6. Split the compound instruction into K named axes (helpfulness, harmlessness, faithfulness, brevity, fluency, ...) drawn from a small fixed list — these are not learned. Give each axis its own small scoring head that reads the SAME anchored representation, so every axis is measured on the one shared ruler. A small text reader over the instruction produces default weights, one per axis, for how much each should count. 【author decision: which exact axes and how many, and whether the default weights are forced to sum to one or set independently — these choices fix what each knob means and must be decided by the authors.】 The final reward is the weighted sum of the axis scores.\n\n*Decomposition of the compound-criterion reward into K per-axis heads $a_{k},$ each reading out on the same anchored axis A, combined by user-facing mixing weights $w_{k}$ (default read from criterion text, overridable at inference).*\n$$ r_\\theta(x,c) = \\sum_{k=1}^{K} w_k\\, a_k(x), \\qquad w_k\\in[0,1],\\quad a_k(x)\\ \\text{on axis}\\ A \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Putting every axis on the one shared ruler is what makes a weight like 0.7 mean the same tradeoff no matter the modality.\n7. Find which axes actually fight each other. This needs a separate probe set where humans judge ONE axis at a time ('which answer is more faithful?', 'which is briefer?'). For each axis, the leftover (residual) is the gap between the human single-axis judgment and that axis head's own prediction. Correlate these leftovers across axis pairs: if two axes' leftovers move in OPPOSITE directions on the same prompts, mark them as conflicting and keep them separate instead of averaging. 【author decision: which single-axis questions to ask and on how many prompts is left to the authors, since it decides which conflicts can even be seen.】\n   - _Why_: Conflicting wishes should be surfaced as a real tradeoff, not silently blended; measuring the residual correlation is how you find which axes actually fight.\n8. Tune the per-axis heads so their weighted sum reproduces the full compound human preference, using the same preference-fitting loss. Then write down the error budget: how much error each axis contributes, plus an interaction term that captures what the simple weighted sum misses. Estimate that interaction term as the gap between the full compound error and the summed per-axis errors, and report it both overall and just for the conflicting axis pairs found in the previous step, where the simple sum is most likely to break.\n\n*Held-out error decomposition: the compound-preference error is bounded by the weighted sum of per-axis calibrated errors plus a measured interaction term I capturing conflicting-axis coupling.*\n$$ \\mathrm{Err}_{\\mathrm{compound}} \\le \\sum_{k=1}^{K} w_k\\,\\mathrm{Err}_k + I(\\{a_k\\}) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The error bound — not just the splitting idea — is the real deliverable: it proves the per-axis pieces add back up to the original preference.\n9. At use-time, turn the axis weights into sliders. The user sets any of them directly; any axis the user leaves alone keeps the default the instruction-reader produced. User-set values replace the defaults rather than blending, then all weights are rescaled to add up to one, and the reweighted axis scores combine into the final reward that re-ranks the candidate answers. The same weight setting is used no matter the answer's form, which is why a given setting means the same tradeoff across forms.\n   - _Why_: This is the steering knob the user wanted, and because the axes share the anchored ruler the knob behaves the same across modalities.\n\n### Falsification harness\n*Run anchored vs baseline vs permuted-label vs anchor-only controls and steering-monotonicity checks.*\n\n10. Run the make-or-break tests. First, compare four versions — the anchored head, the per-form baseline, a control trained on shuffled cross-form labels, and a control trained on only the cross-form pairs — on the held-out cross-form test; the anchored head should beat the baseline (which sits near random on cross-form pairs), and the shuffled-label control should fall back to the baseline. Second, for each axis, slide its weight up (rescaling the rest), pick the best-of-n answer, and measure that answer's quality on that axis with an INDEPENDENT judge (a held-out human or a separate ready-made metric, not the model's own axis head); steering works if that quality only goes up as the weight goes up.\n   - _Why_: These comparisons isolate the anchor signal as the cause and confirm the steering actually does what the user expects.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 锚定式 Omni-Reward：一个可跨模态比较、可调控的偏好尺度\n\n**方法名称.** Anchored Omni-Reward (AOR)\n\n## 研究动机\n奖励模型（reward model）是一个打分器：对齐系统用它来判断两个 AI 回答里人类更偏好哪一个，这个分数随后驱动训练（RLHF，基于人类反馈的强化学习）或从若干候选回答里挑出最好的一个（best-of-n）。所谓 omni-modal（全模态）奖励模型，本应用一个模型给任意形态的回答打分——文本、图像、视频、音频、3D。但今天最强的版本 Omni-Reward 有个症结：它是在每个模态各自的人类比较数据堆上、分开地学每个模态的分数。于是视频回答的 0.8 和音频回答的 0.8 并不在同一把尺子上：它们是分开标定的，分数相等并不代表偏好相等。一旦你让模型把视频回答和音频回答放在一起比较——这恰恰是全模态的意义所在——它就没有诚实的办法说哪个更好。Omni-Reward 自己的报告显示，随数据配比不同它的逐任务分数会摆动约 20 分，这正是这把没锚定的尺子带来的问题。\n\n第二个问题：你给模型一条自由形式的指令，比如「偏好既忠实又简洁的回答」。这两个愿望可能彼此冲突，但模型把它们压成一个数，从不告诉你这个权衡，更别说让你去调它。那些把偏好拆成不同方向的纯文本方法（Decomposed Reward Models，用主成分分析 PCA 找正交的偏好方向）从不把这些方向放到一把共享的、对人有意义的尺子上，也从不在使用时给你一个旋钮。\n\n两个问题同根同治：构造一把共享的「偏好尺子」——一个锚定的单一轴——让每个模态、每个子偏好都在它上面度量。我们用一小批「两个选项处于不同模态」的人类比较（例如「对这个 prompt，是这段音频回答更好还是这段视频回答更好」）来钉死这把尺子的零点和单位，并强制模型对这些比较使用同一个全局尺度。现在能做到，是因为开源全模态骨干已经存在、跨模态偏好数据已能以几千对的规模收集、可调控奖励的工具也给了我们暴露按轴旋钮的途径——而这些此前都没有把旋钮跨模态地锚定起来。\n\n一旦成功，对齐优化器终于可以混合音频、视频、图像和文本候选，并相信更大的奖励就意味着更被人偏好，无需任何按模态打的补丁。用户也可以把 0.7 的权重给忠实度、0.3 给简洁度，并让这个权衡无论回答是音频还是视频都表示同一件事。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景 / 数据\n*标准的同模态偏好数据组装，起支撑作用但不是贡献本身。*\n\n1. 从已有的公开偏好数据集收集普通的同形式偏好对（文本 vs 文本、音频 vs 音频、视频 vs 视频、图像 vs 图像）。把每个对整理成与锚定对相同的记录格式（去掉「不同形式」标记），并把每个对标注为「同模态」或「锚定」，这样一个 data loader 就能同时喂入两路，训练步骤也知道每个对该走哪条分支。\n   - _为什么_: 它们让模型在每个模态内部依然能分辨好坏，同时由锚定对去固定跨模态尺度。\n\n### 跨模态锚定\n*把奖励的零点和单位钉到人类的跨模态判断上，使各模态的奖励量级可比。*\n\n2. 构建跨模态锚定集(cross-modal anchor set)。挑选答案能以两种以上形式给出的 prompt——文本、口播音频、短视频或图像——只有当至少两个现成的生成器（每个模态一个）都能给出可用答案时才保留该 prompt。对每个 prompt 构造「两个选项处于不同形式」的候选对（例如音频答案 vs 视频答案），并对每对收集至少三条独立的人类投票（A 更好 / B 更好 / 平局）。把非平局的投票折算成该对的人类胜率(win-rate)，并单独保留平局比例。每个对存为一条记录，含 prompt、两个候选及其形式、胜率与标注者。目标约 3-5 千对，并按 prompt 划分留出一部分（保证同一 prompt 不同时出现在训练与评估）用于评估。\n   - _为什么_: 这些跨模态人类比较是唯一能告诉模型「跨模态下同样被偏好」是什么意思的信号，正是它钉住了那把共享尺子。\n3. 在一个冻结的 omni 编码器（已能把任意输入——文本、音频、视频、图像——变成定长向量）上接一个打分头。该头把这个向量与准则(criterion)文本的编码拼接，输出一个分数。再加上一个共享温度 $\\beta $（对所有跨形式比较用同一个正数）和一张小的按形式偏移表 $b_{m}$（每种形式一个数，在跨形式分支上相加，并对该形式的每个对复用）。对照基线是同样的头，但每种形式各有独立温度、偏移也在各自形式的数据内单独拟合。\n   - _为什么_: 用一个 $\\beta $ 和绑定的偏移强制出统一的零点与单位，使跨模态可比性是内建的而非靠运气。\n4. 训练打分头，让它同时在同形式对和跨形式对上预测人类偏好，使用标准的偏好拟合损失（Bradley-Terry，把某选项被偏好的概率建模为分差的 logistic 函数）。强制统一尺度的办法很简单：跨形式对统一使用那一个共享温度和一张偏移表——该分支上不存在会各自漂移的按形式温度。把所有参数一起训练，每个 batch 里跨形式对与同形式对的数量大致相等，使较小的跨形式集不被淹没；并使用考虑平局的损失版本（利用前面记录的平局信息）。\n\n*联合 Bradley-Terry 损失：同模态对 $P_{wm}$ 与跨模态锚定对 A；锚定对共享同一个全局温度 $\\beta $ 与互相绑定的模态偏移 $b_{m}$，而非各模态独立的 $\\beta _{m}$，从而强制出统一尺度。*\n$$ \\mathcal{L} = -\\sum_{(i,j)\\in\\mathcal{P}_{\\mathrm{wm}}} \\log\\sigma\\!\\big(\\beta_m\\,(r_\\theta(x_i)-r_\\theta(x_j))\\big)\\;-\\;\\sum_{(i,j)\\in\\mathcal{A}} \\log\\sigma\\!\\big(\\beta\\,(r_\\theta(x_i)+b_{m_i}-r_\\theta(x_j)-b_{m_j})\\big) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这是核心步骤：联合约束把跨模态人类信号注入奖励分数，使各模态的数值量级对齐。\n5. 在每个训练步对留出数据测两件事。其一，跨形式尺度差：在留出的跨形式对上，头预测的分差与人类胜率所隐含的差距有多大（取平均）——它应当趋向 0。其二，跨形式互换准确率(cross-modal-swap accuracy)：在两个选项处于不同形式的留出对上，选出得分更高的一项（用其形式偏移），看它与人类多数选择吻合的比例（随机猜约 50%）。同时在同形式对上报告这两项，确认两个头在那里都保持准确。\n\n*跨模态尺度差 g：在留出锚定对上，模型预测的奖励差与人类胜率 logit 之间的平均绝对偏差；联合约束将 g 推向 0。*\n$$ g = \\frac{1}{|\\mathcal{A}_{\\mathrm{ho}}|}\\sum_{(i,j)\\in\\mathcal{A}_{\\mathrm{ho}}} \\Big| \\big(r_\\theta(x_i)+b_{m_i}-r_\\theta(x_j)-b_{m_j}\\big) - \\mathrm{logit}\\,\\hat p^{\\,\\mathrm{human}}_{ij} \\Big| \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: g 告诉你尺子是否标定好；cross-modal-swap 准确率告诉你这是否真的转化为挑出人类偏好的跨模态回答。\n\n### 可调控的按轴分解\n*把复合准则拆成同一锚定尺子上的按轴标定头，并配以面向用户、跨模态有意义的权重。*\n\n6. 把复合指令拆成 K 个具名轴(axis)——helpfulness、harmlessness、faithfulness(忠实度)、brevity(简洁度)、fluency(流畅度) 等——取自一个小的固定清单，这些不是学出来的。给每个轴一个自己的小打分头，读取同一个锚定表示，使每个轴都在同一把共享尺子上度量。一个读取指令文本的小模块产出默认权重，每个轴一个，表示各自占多少分量。【作者需决定：具体取哪些轴、取多少个，以及默认权重是强制归一化求和为 1 还是各自独立设定——这些选择决定了每个旋钮的含义，须由作者拍板。】最终奖励是各轴分数的加权和。\n\n*将复合准则奖励分解为 K 个按轴的头 $a_{k}$，每个都在同一锚定轴 A 上读数，由面向用户的混合权重 $w_{k}$ 组合（默认由准则文本得到，可在推理时覆盖）。*\n$$ r_\\theta(x,c) = \\sum_{k=1}^{K} w_k\\, a_k(x), \\qquad w_k\\in[0,1],\\quad a_k(x)\\ \\text{on axis}\\ A \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 把每个轴都放到同一把共享尺子上，才能让 0.7 这样的权重无论何种模态都表示同一个权衡。\n7. 找出哪些轴真正彼此冲突。这需要一个单独的探针集(probe set)，让人类每次只判断一个轴（『哪个回答更忠实？』『哪个更简洁？』）。对每个轴，残差(residual)是人类单轴判断与该轴头自身预测之间的差距。把这些残差在轴对之间做相关：若两个轴的残差在同一批 prompt 上朝相反方向变动，就把它们标为冲突并保持独立、而不取平均。【作者需决定：问哪些单轴问题、在多少 prompt 上问，由作者决定，因为这决定了哪些冲突能被看见。】\n   - _为什么_: 相互冲突的愿望应被显式呈现为真实权衡而非悄悄混合；测残差相关性正是找出哪些轴真正打架的办法。\n8. 调好各轴头，使其加权和能复现完整的复合人类偏好，使用同一个偏好拟合损失。然后写出误差预算：每个轴贡献多少误差，外加一个交互项(interaction term)，刻画简单加权和遗漏了什么。把该交互项估计为「完整复合误差」与「各轴误差之和」的差，并分别报告其总体值与仅在上一步找到的冲突轴对上的值——在那里简单求和最可能失效。\n\n*留出误差分解：复合偏好误差被各轴标定误差的加权和加上一个可测的交互项 I（刻画冲突轴之间的耦合）所界定。*\n$$ \\mathrm{Err}_{\\mathrm{compound}} \\le \\sum_{k=1}^{K} w_k\\,\\mathrm{Err}_k + I(\\{a_k\\}) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 误差界——而不仅是拆分这个想法——才是真正的成果：它证明各轴部分能加回到原始偏好。\n9. 在使用时把各轴权重做成滑块。用户可直接设定其中任意几个；用户未动的轴保留指令读取模块给出的默认值。用户设定的值替换默认值（而非混合），随后所有权重重新缩放使其和为 1，重新加权后的各轴分数组合成最终奖励，用以对候选答案重排序。无论答案是何种形式都用同一组权重设定，这正是为何同一设定在各形式间表示相同的权衡。\n   - _为什么_: 这正是用户想要的调控旋钮；因为各轴共享锚定尺子，旋钮在各模态上的行为是一致的。\n\n### 证伪测试台\n*运行锚定头 vs 基线 vs 打乱标签 vs 仅锚定的对照，以及 steering 单调性检查。*\n\n10. 运行成败攸关的测试。其一，在留出的跨形式测试上比较四个版本——锚定头、按形式基线、用打乱跨形式标签训练的对照、只用跨形式对训练的对照；锚定头应胜过基线（基线在跨形式对上接近随机），而打乱标签的对照应退回到基线水平。其二，对每个轴把其权重往上滑（其余重新缩放），挑出 best-of-n 答案，并用一个独立评判（留出的人类或一个单独的现成指标，而非模型自己的轴头）测量该答案在该轴上的质量；只要质量随权重上升而不下降，调控即生效。\n   - _为什么_: 这些对比把锚定信号孤立为成因，并确认调控确实如用户预期那样起作用。\n\n"},{"id":"88","run_dir":"run_prompt88_mllmspatial","index":88,"title":"Attributing MLLM Spatial-Reasoning Failures to Factors via Matched Minimal-Pair Probes","title_zh":"用匹配最小对探针将 MLLM 空间推理失败归因到具体输入因素","method_name":"Spatial Factor-Attribution Probe (SFAP)","hook":"We show that two MLLMs with identical VSI-Bench accuracy can fail on systematically different input factors, so a single accuracy scalar is not a sufficient statistic for spatial generalization. By holding a spatial relation fixed and varying one latent factor (reference frame, scene scale, composition depth) at a time, we attribute each model's collapse to a specific factor and reveal that the perception-side vs reasoning-side split differs across models the leaderboard rank as equal.","anchor_pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","anchor_pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","domain_category":"Vision-Language & Multimodal","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf can attribute a spatial-reasoning failure to a specific input factor: when accuracy drops under a structure-preserving shift (same relation, different reference frame / scene scale / composition depth), no method isolates which factor carried the drop, so a measured generalization gap cannot be decomposed into perception-side vs reasoning-side causes.","pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"closed by constructing matched minimal-pair instance sets that hold the underlying spatial relation and scene content fixed while programmatically varying exactly one latent factor at a time, paired with a construction-derived oracle answer, so the accuracy delta across a factor's matched pairs IS the attribution of failure to that factor; a perception-probe twin (factor varied only in the rendered view, relation unchanged) versus a reasoning-probe twin (relation re-composed, view unchanged) splits the drop into perception-side vs reasoning-side cause.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether the aggregate accuracy scalar every benchmark inherits is a sufficient statistic for spatial generalization at all, rather than assumed — i.e. whether two models with equal benchmark accuracy can have systematically different failure manifolds under shift.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","how_closed":"framing half (C01): relocate the load-bearing spatial-competence signal from the assumed locus (a single aggregate-accuracy scalar the whole field reports) to an overlooked locus (the per-factor failure manifold — the vector of factor-attributed drops), stating as a falsifiable proposition that the scalar is sufficient only if equal-accuracy models share a failure manifold; deliverable half (companion controlled_diagnostic_design): the matched minimal-pair instrument from the anchor leg empirically ships the separation by computing each model's failure-manifold vector and showing equal-accuracy models occupy different manifolds, confirming the scalar is not a sufficient statistic.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"multimodal large language models (MLLMs / VLMs) for spatial intelligence and spatial reasoning","n_papers":49,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":24},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10},{"source":"openreview","n":2}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":6,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"AirVista: Empowering UAVs with 3D Spatial Reasoning Abilities Through a Multimodal Large Language Model Agent"},{"source":"openalex","title":"LLaVA-MR: Large Language-and-Vision Assistant for Video Moment Retrieval"},{"source":"openalex","title":"OmEGa(<mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" altimg=\"si1.svg\" display=\"inline\" id=\"d1e2076\"><mml:mi>Ω</mml:mi></mml:math>): Ontology-based information extraction framework for constructing task-centric knowledge graph from manufacturing documents with large language model"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Sparkle: Mastering Basic Spatial Capabilities in Vision Language Models Elicits Generalization to Spatial Reasoning"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Enhancing 3D Referential Grounding by Learning Coarse Spatial Relationships"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Cross-Task Knowledge Transfer for Semi-supervised Joint 3D Grounding and Captioning"}],"more":0},{"year":2025,"n":32,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Open3DVQA: A Benchmark for Comprehensive Spatial Reasoning with Multimodal Large Language Model in Open Space"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Open3D-VQA: A Benchmark for Embodied Spatial Concept Reasoning with Multimodal Large Language Model in Open Space"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"GoT: Unleashing Reasoning Capability of Multimodal Large Language Model for Visual Generation and Editing"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Introducing Visual Perception Token into Multimodal Large Language Model"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"MLLM-For3D: Adapting Multimodal Large Language Model for 3D Reasoning Segmentation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Spatial Reasoning in Multimodal Large Language Models: A Survey of Tasks, Benchmarks and Methods"}],"more":26},{"year":2026,"n":11,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"},{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"CROP: Token-Efficient Reasoning in Large Language Models via Regularized Prompt Optimization"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Multilingual and Multimodal LLMs in the Wild: Building for Low-Resource Languages"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"AssemLM: Spatial Reasoning Multimodal Large Language Models for Robotic Assembly"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Multimodal Reasoning with LLM for Encrypted Traffic Interpretation: A Benchmark"}],"more":5}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":15,"share":0.306},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":10,"share":0.204},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":10,"share":0.204},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":9,"share":0.184},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":8,"share":0.163},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":6,"share":0.122},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":6,"share":0.122},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":5,"share":0.102}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Across the retrieved frontier, MLLM spatial reasoning is measured as a single scalar accuracy on held-in distributions, but that scalar does not predict behavior under structure-preserving distribution shift, and no retrieved method can attribute a generalization failure to a specific input factor. VSI-Bench (openalex:W4413144646) establishes that spatial reasoning — not perception, language, or temporal aggregation — is the primary bottleneck, yet it reports aggregate per-task scores without isolating whether a wrong answer comes from a mis-perceived scene representation or a mis-applied spatial relation; Open3D-VQA (semanticscholar:23211449d9108aebc9ddc42d0191b92ce1e0e17d) shows the same model swing sharply between allocentric, egocentric, and allocentric-egocentric-transformation splits, and TRACE (arxiv:2603.23404v2) shows that converting the scene to a text-based allocentric representation changes the answer, which together imply the accuracy is contingent on a latent factor (reference-frame convention, scene scale, relation arity) that the benchmarks hold fixed and never vary independently. The result: when an off-the-shelf or fine-tuned MLLM is moved from the distribution it was tuned on (SpatialBot, openalex:W4413926275) to a structurally identical task with a shifted reference frame or composition depth, accuracy drops and the field has no instrument to say which factor caused the drop or whether a competing model would survive it — so 'improving spatial generalization' is currently an un-diagnosable target.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4413144646","is_anchor":"true","summary_and_residue":"Thinking in Space (VSI-Bench) builds a 5,000-QA video benchmark and probes models' linguistic and visual 'cognitive maps', concluding spatial reasoning is the primary bottleneck and that prompting techniques that help language reasoning (e.g. chain-of-thought) do NOT help and can hurt spatial reasoning. Residue: it diagnoses THAT spatial reasoning is the bottleneck at the aggregate-accuracy level but holds the input factors (reference frame, scene scale, relation composition) fixed inside each task, so it cannot say which factor a given failure is attributable to, nor whether the same competence transfers when that factor is shifted while the underlying relation is held constant."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:23211449d9108aebc9ddc42d0191b92ce1e0e17d","is_anchor":"false","summary_and_residue":"Open3D-VQA partitions spatial reasoning into allocentric, egocentric, and allocentric-egocentric-transformation categories and shows large per-category gaps in open aerial space. Residue: the categories are evaluated as separate static buckets, never as matched minimal pairs of the SAME relation re-expressed across reference frames, so the benchmark documents that frame matters but cannot isolate the frame-transformation operation itself as the failing component or test whether competence on one frame transfers to another."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2603.23404v2","is_anchor":"false","summary_and_residue":"TRACE prompts MLLMs to emit a text-based allocentric representation of a 3D environment from egocentric video as an intermediate before answering, improving 3D spatial reasoning. Residue: it injects one fixed allocentric scaffold and reports net accuracy gain, but does not measure whether the gain is a genuine reference-frame-invariant competence or a distribution-specific scaffold that itself collapses when scene scale or relation composition shifts — the intermediate is a fix, not an instrument that attributes the residual failures."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4404089370","is_anchor":"false","summary_and_residue":"Sparkle trains VLMs only on basic 2D spatial primitives (direction, distance, localization) and shows this elicits some generalization to composite spatial reasoning. Residue: it demonstrates compositional transfer exists for a hand-picked primitive set on 2D pathfinding but does not characterize WHICH compositions transfer and which break, nor provide a measurement that predicts the transfer boundary for an unseen composition — leaving compositional generalization as an observed phenomenon without a predictive account."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"multimodal large language models (MLLMs / VLMs) for spatial intelligence and spatial reasoning","venue":"ICLR / NeurIPS / ICML (top ML venue)","time":"2026","data":["VSI-Bench (video visual-spatial intelligence)","Open3D-VQA / Open3DVQA (open-space 3D spatial QA)","SpatialMQA (image spatial relations on COCO2017)","synthetic 3D-rendered scene-graph QA (controllable, e.g. ProcTHOR / Habitat-style scenes)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with multimodal / VLM training + evaluation experience","preference":"both","baseline":"off-the-shelf MLLMs (GPT-4o-class, Qwen2.5-VL, InternVL) evaluated zero-shot; fine-tuned spatial VLMs (SpatialBot, M2-Reasoning); text-intermediate prompting (TRACE, SpatialPrompting)","limitation":"MLLMs' spatial-reasoning accuracy does not generalize: performance learned or elicited on one spatial-task / scene-distribution collapses on a structurally-equivalent but distributionally-shifted instance (new viewpoint convention, new scene scale, novel relation composition), and no current method explains or predicts which factor of the input drives the collapse.","contribution_type":"empirical_reveal","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared evaluation framework is the Spatial Factor-Attribution Probe (SFAP): a set of matched minimal-pair instances and the per-model Failure-Manifold Vector (FMV) computed over it, which both legs read from. CONSTRUCTION (anchor, C02): we render scenes from a controllable 3D engine (Habitat/ProcTHOR-style synthetic rooms plus a held-out real-image partition) where each base instance is a (scene S, spatial relation R, question Q, oracle answer A) tuple, A derived from the engine's ground-truth scene graph independent of any evaluated MLLM. For each base instance we generate a matched family by applying a single-factor transform T_f for each factor f in F = {reference_frame (egocentric<->allocentric re-expression of the SAME relation), scene_scale (uniform metric rescaling that preserves all ordinal relations), composition_depth (relation re-expressed as a k-step composition of the same primitives, k in {1,2,3})}. Within a matched family, T_f changes ONLY factor f and re-derives A from the transformed scene graph; every other axis (objects, textures, camera intrinsics, relation identity) is held byte-fixed, so any accuracy difference is attributable to f alone. To split perception-side from reasoning-side cause we instantiate two twins per factor: a perception-probe twin (the factor is varied only in the rendered pixels while the queried relation's truth value is held constant, isolating whether the visual encoder still reads the relation) and a reasoning-probe twin (the relation is re-composed to depth k with the rendered view held constant, isolating whether the language-reasoning stage still composes it). ATTRIBUTION QUANTITY: for model m and factor f, the factor-attributed drop d_{m,f} = acc(m on level-0 of f) - acc(m on shifted level of f), and the Failure-Attribution Gap FAG_{m,f} = d_{m,f}^{reason} - d_{m,f}^{percep} (positive => reasoning-side dominated, negative => perception-side dominated); the FMV is the vector (d_{m,f}, FAG_{m,f}) over all f. AUDIT (sibling, C01 framing + C02 deliverable): the field's assumed locus is the scalar acc_agg(m) = mean accuracy over level-0 instances (what VSI-Bench openalex:W4413144646 and Open3D-VQA semanticscholar:23211449d9108aebc9ddc42d0191b92ce1e0e17d report). We relocate the competence signal to the FMV locus and state the sufficiency proposition: acc_agg is a sufficient statistic for spatial generalization iff any two models with equal acc_agg have statistically indistinguishable FMVs. The matched-pair instrument tests it directly: select model pairs matched within tolerance on acc_agg and measure the FMV distance ||FMV_{m1} - FMV_{m2}||; a large distance between leaderboard-equal models is the headline empirical reveal that overturns the scalar's face-value reading. The two legs interlock under shared_evaluation: the same SFAP instances and the same FMV both attribute single-model failures (anchor) and demonstrate the metric's insufficiency across models (sibling) — one instrument, two readouts.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The two gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules: the audit gap (is the scalar sufficient?) is answered by the SAME FMV the attribution gap produces — the audit is just the across-model reading of the per-model attribution instrument, which is why coherence_thread_type is shared_evaluation and the sibling's companion is the anchor's own pattern (C02). I considered building a separate causal-attribution model (regress accuracy on factor covariates), but that re-introduces a confound the matched-pair design removes by construction — a regression cannot guarantee one factor varied while all else held, whereas byte-fixed matched pairs can, so I rejected it. I avoided the method_lineage flagged regression to node c1 (classifier OOD shift-attribution) by attributing through construction-controlled minimal pairs on a generative MLLM rather than covariate intervention on a classifier, and avoided node n1 (static category buckets) by making the buckets MATCHED pairs of one relation re-expressed rather than independent sets.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: run >=6 MLLMs zero-shot on SFAP (the matched minimal-pair set built from ~300 synthetic 3D scenes plus a real-image transfer partition) and, for each acc_agg-matched model pair (|acc_agg| within 2%), measure the Failure-Manifold Vector distance ||FMV_{m1}-FMV_{m2}|| and the per-factor Failure-Attribution Gap FAG_{m,f}. If the candidate is right, the FMV distance between leaderboard-equal models will be LARGE (many pairs exceed the FMV distance separating randomly chosen non-equal models), and per-model FAG_{m,f} will localize failures to specific factors with a sign that splits perception-side from reasoning-side cause — demonstrating accuracy is not a sufficient statistic. The named load-bearing variable is the matched-pair factor-attributed drop d_{m,f}: the entire FMV and FAG signal is built from it. Negative control: permute the oracle answers within each matched family (step 8) so the factor still varies but the target is random; this control's predicted effect on the DOWNSTREAM OUTCOME is that the across-model FMV-distance signal collapses to chance and FAG_{m,f} loses its factor-localized structure — if the FMV distances among equal-accuracy models stay large under label permutation, the divergence was an artifact of instance difficulty or sampling noise, not factor-attributed competence, and the candidate is falsified. Positive control: a stripped-down attribution that uses ONLY d_{m,f} (no twin split, no FAG) should already recover most of the equal-accuracy FMV-divergence reveal, confirming the matched-pair drop is the load-bearing quantity.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4413144646","delta":"VSI-Bench probes whether MLLMs form cognitive maps and reports aggregate + per-task accuracy concluding spatial reasoning is the bottleneck; we hold the relation fixed and vary one latent factor at a time on MATCHED pairs to attribute each failure to a specific factor and to perception- vs reasoning-side cause, a decomposition their task-bucketed scalar cannot produce."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:23211449d9108aebc9ddc42d0191b92ce1e0e17d","delta":"Open3D-VQA evaluates allocentric/egocentric/transformation as independent static buckets; we construct the SAME relation re-expressed across reference frames as a matched pair so the reference-frame-transformation operation itself, not a bucket score, is the measured quantity."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2603.23404v2","delta":"TRACE injects one fixed allocentric text scaffold and reports net accuracy gain; we build an instrument (not a fix) that measures whether any such gain is a frame-invariant competence by testing transfer of a held-constant relation across factors, attributing residual failures rather than patching them."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4404089370","delta":"Sparkle shows basic-primitive training elicits some composite generalization via aggregate composite-task accuracy; we measure composition_depth as a controlled matched-pair factor and report the per-model attributed drop, turning an observed transfer phenomenon into a factor-attributed measurement."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4413144646","what_step_was_missed":"VSI-Bench constructed a fixed-distribution video QA set and probed for an internal cognitive map, but it never constructed MATCHED minimal pairs that hold the spatial relation fixed while varying exactly one latent factor with a construction-re-derived oracle — the measurement primitive that converts an aggregate-accuracy bottleneck claim into a per-factor, per-side (perception vs reasoning) attribution and lets two equal-accuracy models be shown to occupy different failure manifolds; building that matched-pair attribution instrument with a factor-wise re-derived ground truth is the specific step their fixed-set construction did not take."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":396,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"recipe_application_check is 'applied' for both legs (C02's controlled-instance-divergence and C01's locus-relocation-with-why are both performed in core_mechanism), anti_pattern_check has no match (no heterogeneous_decomposition in the composition set), and paper_pointed_threat is no_threat_found (collision_hits surface adjacent failure-attribution and perception-vs-reasoning work but none constructs matched minimal-pair factor attribution with the FMV sufficient-statistic claim). The only borderline is gap_closure_reject_check on the C01 'locus already exploited by published work' lesson — per-task/bucket accuracy decompositions exist — but the candidate's differentiation_from_lit already measures matched-pair FMV as distinct from static buckets, making this a surfaced reviewer concern (fold into Phase 4) rather than a load-bearing defect, so advance with the concern noted.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf can attribute a spatial-reasoning failure to a specific input factor: when accuracy drops under a structure-preserving shift (same relation, different reference frame / scene scale / composition depth), no method isolates which factor carried the drop, so a measured generalization gap cannot be decomposed into perception-side vs reasoning-side causes.","main_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail most when the instrument isolates the confound only inside an artificial regime and never shows the signal transfers to real deployment (synthetic-to-real gap asserted not shown); or are circular (validated against the same population/definition they interrogate); or confirmatory (re-derive an already-documented limitation); or carry broad capability claims on a single-task/small-N instrument.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a synthetic-ground-truth instrument only on synthetic data, without demonstrating that the controlled finding transfers to real-world instances, leaves ecological validity unestablished and undermines the central claim.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism_steps step 9 builds a held-out real-image partition with hand-annotated matched pairs and reports whether the synthetic FMV model-ordering is preserved on real images, so the synthetic-to-real transfer is shown, not asserted."},{"lesson_quoted":"Building the instrument around one contested definition of the target property means it cannot independently confirm that the definition is correct, and reviewers flag the resulting circularity.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the oracle answer A is derived from the 3D engine's ground-truth scene graph (construction-independent of any evaluated MLLM), so ground truth never comes from the evaluand or a self-asserted definition."},{"lesson_quoted":"A diagnostic that only re-confirms a shortcut already known in advance, surfacing no previously unmeasurable failure, is read as confirmatory rather than as a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the headline (two equal-accuracy models occupy different failure manifolds) is a previously-unmeasurable gap; existing benchmarks report aggregate/bucket accuracy and cannot surface FMV divergence among leaderboard-equal models."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pairing a single-task or small-sample instrument with broad capability claims triggers a scope-mismatch rejection, and assembling retrieval or engineering blocks without an isolating scientific insight reads as application rather than research.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"the claim is bounded to the three named factors (frame/scale/composition) and >=6 models over ~20k instances, but a reviewer could push that 'spatial generalization' is broader than three factors; scope is explicitly bounded in step 5 of C02's recipe but the headline phrasing should stay factor-scoped."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether the aggregate accuracy scalar every benchmark inherits is a sufficient statistic for spatial generalization at all, rather than assumed — i.e. whether two models with equal benchmark accuracy can have systematically different failure manifolds under shift.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"C01 fails when a relocated signal is claimed stealthier/better without defeating an adaptive opponent at the new locus, when the new locus is already exploited by published work unless the difference is measured, or when the relocation is shown only on fixed baselines with no account of WHY the new locus carries the signal (reads as stacked components).","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work — normalization statistics, activation-similarity losses, semantic concept triggers — collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"per-category bucket accuracy (Open3D-VQA) and per-task accuracy (VSI-Bench) already partially decompose the scalar, so the FMV locus is adjacent to existing partial decompositions; the candidate must explicitly measure that matched-pair FMV is distinct from static bucket scores (differentiation_from_lit does state this, but the audit leg's novelty rests on it)."},{"lesson_quoted":"Demonstrating the new locus only on fixed, non-adaptive or outdated baselines while omitting any account of why it works reads as a stacked pipeline of existing components rather than a principled shift.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the FAG twin split (perception-probe vs reasoning-probe) supplies the WHY — it mechanistically locates the relocated signal in either the visual encoder or the language-reasoning stage, not merely showing THAT FMVs differ."},{"lesson_quoted":"Wiring off-the-shelf generators or tools into a new attack setting without a structural reason for the locus change gets judged as engineering integration, not insight.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the locus change (scalar -> failure-manifold vector) is structurally motivated by the sufficient-statistic proposition, not an off-the-shelf tool wired in."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No entry triggered. The assumption_audit_and_pivot (C01) sibling entry is borderline on the 'locus already exploited by published work' lesson — per-task and per-bucket accuracy decompositions already exist, so the FMV-locus novelty rests on the matched-pair construction being measurably distinct from static buckets; this is a load-bearing structural property of the audit leg's novelty, not a fatal Reject match. The C02 anchor entry is clear (real-image transfer + construction-independent oracle + previously-unmeasurable headline all satisfied)."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf can attribute a spatial-reasoning failure to a specific input factor...","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Construct a controlled set of evaluation instances in which exactly one named confound is structurally blocked or independently varied, then report the DIVERGENCE between apparent and de-confounded performance as the primary result, with the load-bearing artifact being the controlled instance set paired with an oracle independent of the system under test.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism builds matched minimal-pair families where each transform T_f changes ONLY factor f and re-derives the oracle A from the transformed scene graph (one named factor varied, all else byte-fixed), and reports d_{m,f} and the FMV divergence as the primary result rather than a leaderboard score — exactly C02's controlled-instance-set + independent-oracle + report-the-gap move.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether the aggregate accuracy scalar every benchmark inherits is a sufficient statistic...","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"The audited assumption is about the representational LOCUS at which a property is presumed enforced; the move is to RELOCATE the signal to a different locus the field treated as irrelevant/invariant and demonstrate the property manifests there, supplying a mechanistic account of WHY the new locus carries the signal.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism relocates the spatial-competence signal from the assumed locus (aggregate-accuracy scalar) to the overlooked FMV locus (failure-manifold vector), states the sufficiency proposition as the falsifiable invariance claim, and supplies the WHY via the FAG perception/reasoning twin split — matching C01's relocate-the-signal + account-for-why move, with empirical validation (FMV distance among equal-accuracy models) rather than tighter analysis as C01 prescribes.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries instantiate their cluster's signature move: C02's controlled-instance + report-the-divergence is performed by the matched-pair FMV construction, and C01's locus-relocation-with-mechanistic-why is performed by moving the competence signal from the scalar to the FMV plus the FAG twin split explaining why."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["controlled_diagnostic_design","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as a component; the composition set {controlled_diagnostic_design, assumption_audit_and_pivot} contains no heterogeneous_decomposition, so no anti-pattern matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"no_threat_found","threat_source":"n/a","subsumption_argument":null,"addressable_via":null}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Attributing MLLM Spatial-Reasoning Failures to Input Factors via Matched Minimal-Pair Probes\n\n**Method.** Spatial Factor-Attribution Probe (SFAP)\n\n## Motivation\nToday, when people report how good a multimodal large language model (MLLM, a model that takes images plus text) is at spatial reasoning, they give one number: its average accuracy on a fixed test set. VSI-Bench (a video spatial-intelligence benchmark) used this to make an important point — that spatial reasoning, not seeing or language, is where these models break down. But that single number is measured with everything held fixed: which viewpoint a relation is described from, how big the scene is, how many steps the relation is built from. So when you take the same model and ask it the same kind of question but from a new viewpoint or with a deeper chain of relations, its accuracy drops, and nobody can say which of those changes caused the drop.\n\nThe nearby papers all run into this. Open3D-VQA splits questions into viewpoint categories and shows the score swings between them, but the categories are separate question sets, not the same relation rewritten across viewpoints, so it shows viewpoint matters without pinning down the viewpoint-change as the thing that breaks. TRACE adds a text description of the scene as a helper step and the accuracy goes up — which hints a hidden factor is at play — but it is a fix, not a measuring tool.\n\nThe result is that 'make spatial reasoning generalize better' is currently un-diagnosable: you cannot tell whether a failure is the model no longer SEEING the relation (perception side) or no longer COMBINING it correctly (reasoning side), and two models that score the same on the leaderboard might be failing for completely different reasons. We fix the measurement: build matched pairs that change exactly one factor at a time with a known correct answer, so each failure can be blamed on a specific factor and a specific stage — and we show that equally-ranked models can have very different failure profiles.\n\n## Method\n### Matched-pair probe construction\n*Build instances that vary exactly one spatial factor at a time with a construction-derived oracle.*\n\n1. In a controllable 3D engine (Habitat or ProcTHOR style), build about 300 scenes that each come with a full, machine-readable description of what is in them — a scene graph G that lists every object with its category, its 3D box center and size in meters, and where the camera is, plus the spatial relationships between objects computed straight from that geometry. For each scene, write 3-5 spatial questions covering three answer kinds: direction words (left/right/front/behind/above/below), a number in meters (a distance or a size), and counting / yes-no. Generate each question from a fixed set of templates with object names filled in, and make sure each object reference points to exactly one object (re-pick objects until the wording is unambiguous). Read the correct answer directly off the scene graph by evaluating the relation on the geometry, so the answer never depends on the model being tested.\n   - _Why_: A correct answer that comes from the scene's construction, not from any model, is what keeps the test from being circular.\n2. Build three controlled edits, each changing one and only one thing and recomputing the correct answer from the edited scene. Viewpoint frame: pick the direction words either from the camera's own frame (forward is where the camera looks, projected onto the floor) or from a fixed world frame, recompute the direction answer for the other frame, and keep the picture either exactly the same (just ask the relation in the other frame) or move the camera to the standard overhead-style viewpoint while leaving the objects where they are; metric distances do not change with frame, so they are not used here. Scene size: shrink or grow the whole scene by 0.5x, 1x, or 2x, recompute every distance/size answer by simply multiplying by that factor, count a numeric answer correct if it is within about a quarter of the true value, and confirm the direction answers stay identical (scaling everything the same way never flips left/right). Composition depth: rewrite the relation as a 1-, 2-, or 3-step chain over a path of distinct objects using the same kinds of primitive relations, resolving the chain step by step to one unique target object, and keep the picture identical so only the sentence gets longer.\n   - _Why_: If only one factor changes and everything else is byte-identical, any accuracy difference must be caused by that one factor.\n3. For each factor, make two paired versions that each pin down one side of the model. The perception twin changes only the picture (move the camera, rescale the geometry) while keeping the answer to the asked relation the same — so if the model fails here, it is because it no longer sees the relation in the image. The reasoning twin keeps the picture exactly the same pixels while changing how the relation is built or framed (for example making the relation a longer chain) — so if the model fails here, it is because it no longer combines the relation correctly. Check the part that is supposed to stay fixed by having two people independently review a sample (about 10% of each set, at least 30 pairs per factor) against a short yes/no checklist; only keep a set if the two reviewers agree strongly (agreement score at least 0.8) and the held-fixed part is wrong less than 5% of the time, otherwise fix the edit and regenerate. The result is the full labeled probe set.\n   - _Why_: Comparing the two twins tells you whether a failure is the model not seeing the relation or not combining it.\n\n### Factor + stage attribution\n*Turn raw correctness into per-factor, per-stage failure attribution for each model.*\n\n4. Run at least 6 multimodal large language models (MLLMs) — open ones such as Qwen2.5-VL, InternVL, LLaVA-OneVision; API ones such as GPT-4o-class and Gemini-class; and one fine-tuned spatial model such as SpatialBot — on every probe instance without any extra training. Show each model the same single rendered image (or a fixed short clip for video models) used across the matched pair. Use the exact same instruction wording for each answer type, asking for a tightly formatted answer (a direction option, a number in meters, an integer, or yes/no), and decode deterministically (no randomness). Parse the answer with a simple per-type matcher; if it cannot be parsed, ask once more with a format reminder and otherwise count it wrong. Record the exact model version and settings, and for each instance save the raw answer, the parsed answer, the correct answer, and whether it was right.\n   - _Why_: Using several different models is what makes the later 'same score, different failures' comparison meaningful.\n5. Using the table of which answers each model got right, compute two numbers for each model and each factor. The factor-attributed drop $d_{m},f$ (Eq. eq:drop) is the model's accuracy on the unchanged version minus its accuracy on the shifted version, measured only over pairs where that one factor moved — this blames the failure on that specific factor. The attribution gap $FAG_{m},f$ (Eq. eq:fag) is the drop on the reasoning twin minus the drop on the perception twin; if it is positive the failure is mostly on the reasoning side, if negative it is mostly on the perception (seeing) side. The factor-attributed drop is the single key number that everything else is built from.\n\n*The factor-attributed drop $d_{m},f$ is model m's accuracy on the unshifted level $\\ell _{0}$ of factor f minus its accuracy on the shifted level $\\ell _{1},$ over matched pairs where only f changed.*\n$$ d_{m,f} = \\mathrm{acc}\\!\\left(m \\mid \\ell_0^{f}\\right) - \\mathrm{acc}\\!\\left(m \\mid \\ell_1^{f}\\right) \\tag{1} $$\n\n\n*The Failure-Attribution Gap $FAG_{m},f$ is the reasoning-probe drop minus the perception-probe drop; positive means reasoning-side dominated, negative means perception-side dominated.*\n$$ \\mathrm{FAG}_{m,f} = d_{m,f}^{\\,\\mathrm{reason}} - d_{m,f}^{\\,\\mathrm{percep}} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The drop blames the failure on one factor; the gap blames it on the perception or the reasoning stage.\n\n### Sufficiency test across models\n*Show accuracy-matched models occupy different failure manifolds, so the scalar is insufficient.*\n\n6. Put each model's per-factor drops and attribution gaps together, in a fixed order, into one vector called the Failure-Manifold Vector $FMV_{m}$ (Eq. eq:fmv). Before comparing, standardize each entry across all the models (subtract the mean, divide by the spread) so factors measured on different scales count equally, then measure the distance between two models as the straight-line (Euclidean) length of the difference of their vectors. Now find every pair of models whose overall accuracy is within 2 percentage points of each other, and report how far apart their vectors are, comparing this to how far apart randomly chosen mismatched pairs are. Decide whether the separation is real with a shuffling test (reassign which pairs count as matched many times, default 10,000) that gives an effect size and a p-value; the claim holds if equally-scoring models are genuinely no closer than random pairs.\n\n*The Failure-Manifold Vector $FMV_{m}$ stacks the factor-attributed drops and attribution gaps over all factors f; the across-model distance $\\Delta $ between two models is the norm of their FMV difference.*\n$$ \\mathrm{FMV}_m = \\big(\\,d_{m,f},\\ \\mathrm{FAG}_{m,f}\\,\\big)_{f \\in F}, \\qquad \\Delta_{m_1,m_2} = \\lVert \\mathrm{FMV}_{m_1} - \\mathrm{FMV}_{m_2}\\rVert \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: If equally-scoring models have very different FMVs, the single average score clearly is not capturing what matters.\n\n### Validity controls\n*Rule out difficulty/noise and establish synthetic-to-real transfer.*\n\n7. Inside each matched family, shuffle the correct answers so the factor still changes across versions but the right answer is now randomly assigned within the family, then recompute the drops, the attribution gaps, and the across-model vector distances under this shuffled setting. If the gap between equally-scoring models stays just as large after shuffling — i.e. the distances do not fall back toward the random-pair level — then the original effect was just difficulty or noise, not a genuine factor-attributed signal.\n   - _Why_: If the signal survives shuffled answers, it was just noise or difficulty, not real factor-attributed competence.\n8. Build a separate set of matched pairs from real photographs, label the correct answer on each by hand, and rerun the models, recompute the drops and gaps, and rebuild the per-model vectors exactly as before; then check whether the order of models by their failure vectors on real photos matches the order on the synthetic scenes (a rank comparison). Because real photos cannot be edited one-factor-at-a-time the way synthetic scenes can, the team must choose how to obtain matched real pairs. 【author decision: either (a) collect near-duplicate real photo pairs that differ in essentially one factor (for example the same scene from two viewpoints, for viewpoint frame), accepting some uncontrolled leftover differences, or (b) limit the real set to the factors that genuinely admit clean real pairs (viewpoint via paired shots) and drop factors that cannot be cleanly matched on real data (scene size) — this trades realism against how tightly the factor is controlled.】\n   - _Why_: It shows the synthetic finding actually carries over to real photos rather than being a quirk of the engine.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 用匹配最小对探针将 MLLM 空间推理失败归因到具体输入因素\n\n**方法名称.** Spatial Factor-Attribution Probe (SFAP)\n\n## 研究动机\n现在大家在报告一个多模态大语言模型（MLLM，即同时输入图像和文本的模型）的空间推理能力时，只给一个数字：它在固定测试集上的平均准确率。VSI-Bench（一个视频空间智能基准）用这个数字说明了一个重要观点——这些模型真正的瓶颈是空间推理，而不是看图或语言。但这个数字是在所有条件都固定的情况下测出来的：一个关系是从哪个视角描述的、场景有多大、这个关系由几步组合而成。于是当你把同一个模型换一个视角问、或者把关系组合得更深时，它的准确率会下降，却没人能说清是哪一个变化导致了下降。\n\n相邻的工作都卡在这里。Open3D-VQA 把问题按视角分类并显示分数在类别间波动，但这些类别是各自独立的问题集，而不是同一个关系在不同视角下的改写，所以它只能说明视角有影响，却无法把“视角变换”本身锁定为出错的环节。TRACE 把场景的文本描述加进来作为辅助步骤、准确率提升了——这暗示有一个隐藏因素在起作用——但它是一个修复手段，不是一个测量工具。\n\n结果就是，“让空间推理更好地泛化”目前是无法诊断的：你无法判断一次失败是模型不再“看见”这个关系（感知侧），还是不再正确地“组合”它（推理侧）；而且两个在榜单上分数相同的模型，失败的原因可能完全不同。我们要修复的是测量本身：构造每次只改变一个因素、且有已知正确答案的匹配对，使每次失败都能归因到具体因素和具体阶段——并且证明排名相同的模型可以有非常不同的失败画像。\n\n## 方法\n### 匹配对探针构造\n*构造每次只改变一个空间因素、且正确答案来自构造的实例。*\n\n1. 在可控的 3D 引擎（Habitat 或 ProcTHOR 风格）里构建约 300 个场景，每个场景都自带一份完整、可被程序读取的描述——即场景图(scene graph) G：它列出每个物体的类别、以米为单位的三维包围盒中心与尺寸、以及相机位置，并由这些几何信息直接算出物体间的空间关系。为每个场景写 3-5 个空间问题，覆盖三种答案类型：方向词（left/right/front/behind/above/below）、以米为单位的数值（一个距离或一个尺寸）、以及计数/是否题。每个问题都由一套固定模板填入物体名称生成，并确保每个物体指称都唯一对应一个物体（若指称不唯一就重新挑选物体直到措辞无歧义）。正确答案通过在几何上对关系求值、直接从场景图读取，因此完全不依赖被测模型。\n   - _为什么_: 正确答案来自场景的构造而非任何模型，才能避免测试变成自证循环。\n2. 构造三种受控编辑，每种只改变一个因素，并从编辑后的场景重新算出正确答案。视角参考系(reference frame)：方向词要么取自相机自身的参考系（“前”是相机朝向投影到地面的方向），要么取自一个固定的世界参考系；为另一参考系重算方向答案，并让画面要么完全不变（只是改用另一参考系来问这个关系），要么把相机移到标准的规范视角而物体位置保持不动；距离类答案不随参考系改变，故此因素不使用它们。场景尺度(scene scale)：把整个场景按 0.5/1/2 倍缩放，每个距离/尺寸答案只需乘以该倍数即可重算；数值答案落在真值约四分之一误差范围内即算正确；并确认方向答案保持完全一致（同比例缩放绝不会翻转左右）。组合深度(composition depth)：用同类基元关系，把关系改写成在若干不同物体路径上的 1/2/3 步链，逐步解析该链到唯一的目标物体，并保持画面完全相同，使得只有句子变长。\n   - _为什么_: 若只有一个因素改变、其余字节级相同，那么任何准确率差异都必然由这一个因素造成。\n3. 为每个因素构造两个配对版本，各自锁定模型的一侧。感知孪生(perception twin)只改变画面（移动相机、缩放几何），但保持被问关系的答案不变——因此若模型在此失败，是因为它在图像中已读不出该关系。推理孪生(reasoning twin)保持画面像素完全相同，但改变关系的构造或表述方式（例如把关系变成更长的链）——因此若模型在此失败，是因为它已不能正确组合该关系。对本应保持不变的部分做人工抽查：由两名标注者独立复核一份样本（每个集合约 10%，每因素至少 30 对），对照一份简短的是/否清单；只有当两名标注者高度一致（一致性分数至少 0.8）且“保持不变”的部分出错率低于 5% 时才保留该集合，否则修正编辑并重新生成。最终得到带孪生标签的完整探针集合。\n   - _为什么_: 对比这两个孪生即可判断失败是模型没看见关系，还是没把它组合对。\n\n### 因素与阶段归因\n*把原始对错转化为每个模型的逐因素、逐阶段失败归因。*\n\n4. 对每个探针实例零样本运行至少 6 个多模态大语言模型（MLLM）——开源的如 Qwen2.5-VL、InternVL、LLaVA-OneVision；API 的如 GPT-4o 级、Gemini 级；以及一个微调过的空间模型如 SpatialBot——不做任何额外训练。给每个模型展示匹配对中所用的同一张渲染图像（视频模型则用固定的短片段）。对每种答案类型使用完全相同的指令措辞，要求给出格式严格的答案（一个方向选项、一个以米为单位的数值、一个整数、或是否），并以确定性方式解码（不引入随机性）。用按类型设计的简单匹配器解析答案；若无法解析，则附上格式提醒再问一次，否则计为错误。记录每个模型的确切版本与设置，并为每个实例保存原始回答、解析后的答案、正确答案以及是否正确。\n   - _为什么_: 使用多个不同模型，后面“同分不同失败”的比较才有意义。\n5. 利用记录各模型答对情况的表格，为每个模型和每个因素计算两个数值。因素归因落差 $d_{m},f$（式 eq:drop）是模型在未改动版本上的准确率减去其在偏移版本上的准确率，且只在该因素发生变化的匹配对上计算——它把失败归到这个具体因素上。归因差 $FAG_{m},f$（式 eq:fag）是推理孪生上的落差减去感知孪生上的落差；若为正，则失败主要在推理侧，若为负，则主要在感知（看）侧。因素归因落差是其余一切计算所依赖的唯一关键量。\n\n*因素归因落差 $d_{m},f$ 是模型 m 在因素 f 未偏移档位 $\\ell _{0}$ 上的准确率减去其在偏移档位 $\\ell _{1}$ 上的准确率，二者来自仅 f 发生变化的匹配对。*\n$$ d_{m,f} = \\mathrm{acc}\\!\\left(m \\mid \\ell_0^{f}\\right) - \\mathrm{acc}\\!\\left(m \\mid \\ell_1^{f}\\right) \\tag{1} $$\n\n\n*失败归因差 $FAG_{m},f$ 为推理探针落差减去感知探针落差；为正表示以推理侧为主，为负表示以感知侧为主。*\n$$ \\mathrm{FAG}_{m,f} = d_{m,f}^{\\,\\mathrm{reason}} - d_{m,f}^{\\,\\mathrm{percep}} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 落差把失败归到某一个因素；归因差把它归到感知阶段还是推理阶段。\n\n### 跨模型充分性检验\n*证明同准确率模型处于不同失败流形，从而说明单一标量不充分。*\n\n6. 把每个模型的逐因素落差和归因差按固定顺序拼成一个向量，称为失败流形向量 $FMV_{m}$（式 eq:fmv）。比较前先对每个分量在所有模型间做标准化（减均值、除以离散程度），使不同量纲的因素权重相当，再用两个向量之差的直线（欧氏）长度作为两模型间的距离。然后找出所有总体准确率相差不超过 2 个百分点的模型对，报告它们向量之间的距离，并与随机选取的不匹配模型对的距离作对比。用置换检验判断这种分离是否真实（多次重新指定哪些对算作匹配，默认 10000 次），得到效应量与 p 值；当同分模型之间确实并不比随机模型对更接近时，该结论成立。\n\n*失败流形向量 $FMV_{m}$ 将所有因素 f 的归因落差与归因差堆叠为一个向量；两模型间的跨模型距离 $\\Delta $ 为其 FMV 差的范数。*\n$$ \\mathrm{FMV}_m = \\big(\\,d_{m,f},\\ \\mathrm{FAG}_{m,f}\\,\\big)_{f \\in F}, \\qquad \\Delta_{m_1,m_2} = \\lVert \\mathrm{FMV}_{m_1} - \\mathrm{FMV}_{m_2}\\rVert \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 如果同分模型的 FMV 差异很大，那个单一平均分显然没抓住要点。\n\n### 有效性对照\n*排除难度/噪声并验证合成到真实的迁移。*\n\n7. 在每个匹配族内打乱正确答案，使因素在各版本间仍然变化、但正确答案在族内被随机重新指定，然后在这种打乱设置下重算落差、归因差以及跨模型的向量距离。如果同分模型之间的差距在打乱后依然同样大——即距离没有回落到随机模型对的水平——那么原来的效应只是难度或噪声，而非真正的因素归因信号。\n   - _为什么_: 如果打乱答案后信号仍存在，那它只是噪声或难度，而非真正的因素归因能力。\n8. 用真实照片另建一组匹配对，逐张人工标注正确答案，并完全照前面的流程重新运行模型、重算落差与归因差、重建每个模型的向量；然后检查模型在真实照片上按失败向量的排序是否与在合成场景上的排序一致（一种排序对比）。由于真实照片无法像合成场景那样逐因素逐一编辑，团队必须决定如何获取匹配的真实对。【作者需决定：要么 (a) 采集本质上只在一个因素上不同的近似重复真实照片对（例如同一场景的两个视角，用于视角参考系），并接受残留的不可控差异；要么 (b) 把真实集合限制在确实能构成干净真实对的因素上（通过成对拍摄实现视角），并舍弃无法在真实数据上干净匹配的因素（场景尺度）——这是在真实性与因素受控严格度之间的权衡。】\n   - _为什么_: 这能证明合成结论确实迁移到真实照片，而不是引擎的特例。\n\n"},{"id":"89","run_dir":"run_prompt89_rankfeedback","index":89,"title":"Surpassing the Total-Variation Barrier for Ranking-Feedback Learning via Active Slate Control","title_zh":"通过主动 Slate 控制突破排序反馈学习中的 Total-Variation 壁垒","method_name":"Active-Slate Ordinal Learning (ASOL)","hook":"Existing ranking-feedback online learning recovers sublinear regret only by assuming the utility sequence has sublinear total variation -- an analytic crutch that quietly excludes the adversarial regime the framework was meant to handle. We show this barrier is an artifact of treating the ranked slate as fixed by the environment: pivot the convergence primitive from metric-utility-error to a slate-local ordinal-stability condition the learner can itself enforce by controlling which actions are ranked, and sublinear regret -- hence approximate CCE -- returns without any total-variation assumption.","anchor_pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","anchor_pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","domain_category":"Learning Theory & Statistics","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf delivers a usable equilibrium-driving update under ranking-only feedback when the utility sequence is genuinely adversarial -- i.e. no method recovers no-regret behavior outside the sublinear-total-variation regularity regime that arxiv:2603.19221v1 must assume; the outcome that is missing is a learner that keeps converging when the comparison stream carries no magnitude AND the environment varies fast.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C29 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by pivoting the convergence primitive of the ranking-feedback regret guarantee -- replacing the sublinear-total-variation regularity assumption (a metric condition on raw utility magnitudes) with a slate-local ordinal-stability condition (a residual-of-signal condition on within-slate utility orderings), then re-deriving the regret rate from a single per-round ordinal-progress inequality, yielding a separation: the pivoted analysis stays sublinear in high-total-variation regimes the prior bound provably abandons.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"Every retrieved learning-in-games leaf silently inherits, from the common no-regret ancestor, the assumption that the per-round feedback is a single passively-received observation whose informativeness is fixed by the environment; no retrieved paper questions whether the learner could instead govern WHAT comparisons it is shown -- i.e. whether the set of proposed actions that gets ranked each round should be treated as fixed-by-environment rather than as a quantity the learner influences.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by auditing the budgeted choice mechanism behind the ranked slate -- pivoting the assumption that the slate is environment-fixed by giving the learner an explicit slate-acquisition rule (which k actions to propose for ranking each round) and re-deriving the regret certificate for the active-slate protocol, showing the learner can actively guarantee the ordinal-stability condition the anchor leg's bound requires rather than waiting for the environment to supply it.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"online learning and equilibrium computation under preference/ranking feedback (learning in games)","n_papers":44,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":19},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10},{"source":"openreview","n":2}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":10,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"On the Optimality of Dilated Entropy and Lower Bounds for Online Learning in Extensive-Form Games"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Barriers to Welfare Maximization with No-Regret Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Online Training of Hopfield Networks using Predictive Coding"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Game-Based Adaptive Fuzzy Optimal Bipartite Containment of Nonlinear Multiagent Systems"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Conjectural Online Learning with First-order Beliefs in Asymmetric Information Stochastic Games"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Fully Distributed Event-Triggered Nash Equilibrium Seeking for Networked Mean Field Games"}],"more":4},{"year":2025,"n":22,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Proximal Regret and Proximal Correlated Equilibria: A New Tractable Solution Concept for Online Learning and Games"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Fully Distributed Event-Triggered Nash Equilibrium Seeking for Networked Mean Field Games"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Computational Lower Bounds for No-Regret Learning in Normal-Form Games"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Distributed Global Nash Containment Control and Learning of Multiplayer Multiagent Systems"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A Game-Theoretic Online Optimization for Federated Digital Twin Construction via Wireless Sensing"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Sensor Scheduling in Intrusion Detection Games with Uncertain Payoffs"}],"more":16},{"year":2026,"n":12,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"},{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Online Learning and Equilibrium Computation with Ranking Feedback"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Online semi-supervised perception: Real-time learning without explicit feedback"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Online Statistical Inference of Constant Sample-averaged Q-Learning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Ultrafast On-chip Online Learning via Spline Locality in Kolmogorov-Arnold Networks"}],"more":6}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":10,"share":0.227},{"pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","count":7,"share":0.159},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":5,"share":0.114},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":5,"share":0.114},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":4,"share":0.091},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":3,"share":0.068},{"pattern_id":"algebraic_equivalence_unification","pattern_name":"Prove Equivalence to Unify","count":2,"share":0.045},{"pattern_id":"relax_discrete_search_to_continuous","pattern_name":"Relax Discrete Search to Continuous","count":2,"share":0.045}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"The no-regret-to-equilibrium pipeline that underpins learning in games is built on a numeric-feedback substrate: a learner needs a utility vector (full information) or a scalar realized utility (bandit) to form the loss gradient that drives mirror-descent / regret-matching dynamics toward a coarse correlated equilibrium (semanticscholar:0419ae9a142937f64134a53e56f0e4da293931b2, openalex:W4407576021). When the only observable signal each round is a ranking over a small set of proposed actions -- the regime that arises whenever feedback comes from humans who can compare but not calibrate, or when utilities are hidden for privacy -- this substrate breaks: a ranking is a sign pattern over pairwise utility gaps, so it pins down ordinal direction but carries no magnitude, and arxiv:2603.19221v1 shows that for time-average-utility ranking with small comparison temperature sublinear regret is outright impossible, with their positive results recovered only by assuming the underlying utility sequence has sublinear total variation and only reaching CCE in normal-form games. The gap is structural: there is no characterized way to convert a stream of ordinal comparisons into the magnitude-bearing quantity that equilibrium-driving dynamics consume, so under genuinely adversarial (high-total-variation) or finer-equilibrium (beyond-CCE / extensive-form) regimes the learner has no usable update at all.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2603.19221v1","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Introduces the online-learning-with-ranking-feedback model: the learner only observes a ranking over a set of proposed actions (instantaneous-utility ranking or time-average-utility ranking), proves sublinear regret is impossible for time-average ranking at small temperature, and gives algorithms achieving sublinear regret -- and approximate CCE under self-play in normal-form games -- only under an extra assumption that the utility sequence has sublinear total variation. The residue: the positive results are gated on the sublinear-total-variation regularity assumption (no algorithm survives genuinely adversarial, high-variation utility streams), the equilibrium reach stops at CCE in normal-form games (no Nash / correlated / extensive-form-game guarantee), and the ranking is consumed as a single per-round observation rather than as a budget the learner can actively allocate.","method_detail_residue":"method section confirms the regret bounds are derived under the total-variation regularity condition and the equilibrium claim is CCE-only via the standard no-external-regret-to-CCE folk theorem applied to the new ranking-feedback regret notion."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2604.16087v1","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Studies uncoupled last-iterate convergence to Nash in zero-sum matrix games under bandit feedback and shows that demanding policy-profile convergence is detrimental to the exploitability rate, improving the O(T^{-1/8}) bound. Residue: feedback is still a numeric realized payoff (bandit), strictly more informative than a ranking; the paper says nothing about whether last-iterate convergence is even attainable when the per-round signal is purely ordinal, where the magnitude needed to certify exploitability is absent."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4407576021","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Gives an efficient swap-regret minimizer for d-dimensional structured (embedded) normal-form games, achieving O(T^{(d+1)/(d+3)}) swap regret by exploiting a low-dimensional bilinear payoff structure to sidestep the exponential swap-regret lower bounds. Residue: the algorithm consumes numeric bilinear payoffs <v_i,w_j>; it has no analogue when only an ordering over the learner's proposed actions is revealed, so the low-dimensional structure that buys tractable swap regret cannot currently be exploited from ranking feedback."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:0419ae9a142937f64134a53e56f0e4da293931b2","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Introduces proximal regret, a tractable regret notion strictly between external and swap regret, with no-proximal-regret dynamics (OGD) converging the empirical play to proximal correlated equilibria, a refinement of CCE. Residue: the entire construction is defined on numeric losses through the proximal operator prox_f(x^t); there is no ordinal/ranking instantiation, so this finer-than-CCE equilibrium refinement is currently unreachable in the ranking-feedback regime where the anchor stops at plain CCE."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"online learning and equilibrium computation under preference/ranking feedback (learning in games)","venue":"ICML / NeurIPS / ICLR / COLT (theory-leaning ML)","time":"2026","data":["repeated normal-form / convex game simulators","online LLM-routing or recommendation logs as a ranking-feedback testbed","synthetic adversarial/total-variation-controlled utility sequences"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"online learning theory, regret minimization, equilibrium computation, dueling/preference bandits","preference":"both","baseline":"no-regret learning under numeric utility feedback (OGD/MWU); the ranking-feedback online learning algorithms of arxiv:2603.19221v1; bandit-feedback last-iterate dynamics (arxiv:2604.16087v1)","limitation":"existing no-regret-to-equilibrium machinery presumes the learner can observe a numeric utility vector or scalar; under ranking-only feedback, current positive results need a sublinear-total-variation assumption on the utility sequence and only deliver coarse correlated equilibria in normal-form games","contribution_type":"theory","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object both legs read from and write to is the per-round comparison slate S_t -- the size-k set of pure actions the environment ranks at round t (k is a user-set protocol constant, default k=4 matching the anchor's running example) -- together with the ordinal feedback r_t it induces, where r_t is the permutation of S_t sorted by the (hidden) utility u_t(a) for a in S_t. Anchor leg (C29): the prior guarantee (arxiv:2603.19221v1) reaches sublinear regret only under sublinear total variation V_T = sum_t ||u_t - u_{t-1}||_inf = o(T), a magnitude condition on the raw utility sequence; we pivot the convergence primitive from this metric condition to a SLATE-LOCAL ORDINAL-STABILITY condition O_T = sum_t 1[ argsort(u_t|S_t) != argsort(u_{t-1}|S_t) ] = o(T), i.e. we measure not how much utilities move but how often the WITHIN-SLATE ordering flips -- a residual-of-signal quantity computable from the rankings alone, never from magnitudes. The load-bearing object is a single per-round ordinal-progress inequality: we run a Borda-style relative-rank score s_t(a) = (rank of a in r_t) re-centered to [-(k-1)/2,(k-1)/2], feed s_t as the loss-vector surrogate into a mirror-descent / regret-matching update over the simplex, and prove that the cumulative regret splits into a universally-bounded ordinal-discretization term (independent of V_T) plus an assumption-sensitive term controlled by O_T, not V_T. This re-derivation gives a separation: when V_T is linear but O_T is sublinear (utilities swing wildly in magnitude yet rarely reverse within a slate), our bound stays o(T) exactly where the prior bound diverges. Sibling leg (C11) makes O_T = o(T) something the learner can guarantee rather than hope for: instead of letting the environment fix S_t, the learner runs a slate-acquisition rule -- maintain a confidence interval on each action's relative-rank score, and at each round propose the k actions whose pairwise score gaps are currently most uncertain (a UCB-over-pairs rule), which concentrates comparisons on the orderings whose flips would most damage the bound. We re-derive the regret certificate for this active-slate protocol and show the acquisition rule drives the realized O_T to o(T) on any utility sequence whose pairwise-dominant orderings are eventually stable, dissolving the total-variation precondition entirely. Both legs share the same object S_t: the anchor proves what ordinal-stability buys, the sibling proves the learner can manufacture it by choosing S_t. Under self-play in a normal-form game, each player running the active-slate protocol yields time-average play converging to an approximate CCE via the standard no-external-regret-to-CCE folk theorem applied to the ordinal-surrogate regret, with the approximation error inheriting the O_T-controlled rate rather than the V_T-controlled one.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery because both are about the SAME object -- the slate S_t and the ordinal information it carries -- so I built one protocol around S_t rather than two modules: the anchor leg establishes the ordinal-stability condition as the right convergence primitive (what to assume), and the sibling leg establishes the slate-acquisition rule as the way to satisfy it (how to make the assumption true), which is a single coherent paper, not two. Evidence they share machinery: the sibling's UCB-over-pairs rule has no purpose except to control the exact quantity O_T that the anchor's regret split depends on. (b) Alternative designs considered and rejected: (1) fitting a Bradley-Terry/Plackett-Luce latent-utility model to recover numeric scores then running standard mirror descent -- rejected as a regression to method_lineage collateral node c2, since BT/PL assumes a stationary latent utility and collapses under high total variation, exactly the regime we target; (2) porting a dueling-bandit best-arm estimator -- rejected as regression to collateral c1, single-agent and gives no self-play equilibrium guarantee. The avoided-node reasoning: both regressions try to RECONSTRUCT magnitude from ordinal data; our pivot instead changes the convergence primitive so magnitude is never needed, drawing on the unoccupied 'ordinal-stability-as-target' source.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: in a repeated 2-player general-sum normal-form game (n=10 actions, k=4, T up to 2e5) driven by a synthetic utility sequence we can dial to HIGH total variation but LOW within-slate ordinal drift, run our active-slate protocol in self-play and measure (b) the metric that moves: time-average external regret per player and the CCE-gap should both decay sublinearly (regret/T -> 0, CCE-gap -> 0), whereas the total-variation-assuming baseline of arxiv:2603.19221v1 keeps linear regret on the same stream. The mechanism distinguisher pivots on ONE load-bearing variable: the realized ordinal-drift count O_T (the cumulative number of within-slate order flips), which our theory claims -- not total variation V_T -- governs the rate. Negative control: replace the UCB-over-pairs slate-acquisition rule with a rule that proposes a FRESH UNIFORMLY-RANDOM slate every round (destroying the learner's control of which orderings are sampled); this should leave O_T uncontrolled and drive the CCE-gap and time-average regret back to the baseline's non-vanishing level, confirming the effect rides on actively-stabilized ordinal drift rather than on the ordinal surrogate alone. Positive control: a stripped protocol that keeps ONLY the O_T-targeting acquisition rule on top of plain regret-matching (no other tuning) should recover most of the regret improvement, identifying slate control as the causal mechanism.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2603.19221v1","delta":"They prove sublinear regret and approximate CCE under ranking feedback only by assuming the utility sequence has sublinear total variation V_T=o(T) and treat the ranked slate as environment-given; we replace that metric assumption with a slate-local ordinal-stability condition O_T=o(T) and add a learner-controlled slate-acquisition rule that provably enforces it, yielding a regret/CCE rate governed by O_T and a separation in the high-V_T/low-O_T regime they cannot reach."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2604.16087v1","delta":"They characterize last-iterate Nash convergence rates under numeric bandit feedback in zero-sum games; we operate one level coarser (purely ordinal slate feedback, no realized payoff) and target time-average CCE in general-sum games, deriving the first regret certificate whose controlling quantity is an ordinal-drift count rather than a numeric-payoff estimation error."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4407576021","delta":"Their swap-regret algorithm exploits a numeric d-dimensional bilinear payoff structure <v_i,w_j>; we exploit no payoff magnitudes at all and instead exploit a learner-shaped ordinal-stability structure, so our tractability comes from controlling which comparisons are observed rather than from a low-rank payoff embedding."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:0419ae9a142937f64134a53e56f0e4da293931b2","delta":"They define proximal regret via the proximal operator on numeric losses to reach a finer-than-CCE equilibrium; our contribution is orthogonal and prerequisite -- we supply a magnitude-free regret notion (ordinal-surrogate regret) and the active-slate condition under which it stays sublinear, which is what any future ordinal analogue of proximal regret would have to build on."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"arxiv:2603.19221v1","what_step_was_missed":"They identified that ranking feedback needs SOME regularity to escape their small-temperature impossibility, but characterized that regularity as a magnitude condition (sublinear total variation of the raw utility sequence) and stopped there; the missed step is the construction of an alternative, ordinal-only convergence primitive -- the within-slate ordinal-drift count O_T -- together with the per-round ordinal-progress inequality that re-derives the regret rate in terms of O_T instead of V_T, and the further step of making O_T a learner-controlled quantity via an active slate-acquisition rule rather than a property of the environment. Both the ordinal-drift primitive and the active-slate protocol that enforces it are absent from their analysis, which treats the slate as fixed and the regularity as exogenous."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":378,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"No hard-floor rule fired: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict=borderline (no candidate_match=yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id=null, and paper_pointed_threat is an addressable adjacency (arxiv:2603.19221v1), not exact-mechanism overlap. recipe_application_check.verdict=applied for both legs (C29 performs the metric->ordinal convergence-primitive pivot, C11 performs the selection-rule pivot with re-derived certificate), so the idea is built from the cited cluster tactics, not the parent gist. The two borderline reject-lessons -- C29's unbounded k-dependence of the ordinal-discretization constant and C11's protected-property question (does active slate control still compute a valid CCE of the original game) -- are real but each is a provable detail the full theory must pin down rather than a structural defect of core_mechanism's central argument, so I advance and surface both as reviewer_concerns for Phase 4 rather than revise.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf delivers a usable equilibrium-driving update under ranking-only feedback when the utility sequence is genuinely adversarial -- i.e. no method recovers no-regret behavior outside the sublinear-total-variation regularity regime that arxiv:2603.19221v1 must assume; the outcome that is missing is a learner that keeps converging when the comparison stream carries no magnitude AND the environment varies fast.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C29 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The dominant failure shape is a relaxed assumption that is technically valid but uncharacterized -- no named function or problem class is shown to satisfy it -- or a re-derived rate that merely matches the existing baseline with near-identical algorithmic changes, or a headline guarantee undermined by hidden constants that explode at the parameter limit where the result is claimed strongest.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A weakened assumption that no known function class is shown to satisfy reads as engineered to close the proof, not as a genuine generalization -- characterize when it holds or it sinks the paper.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism explicitly names the HIGH-TV-LOW-O class (utilities swing in magnitude but within-slate orderings rarely flip) and the separation harness instantiates it concretely, so the weakened ordinal-stability condition O_T=o(T) is characterized, not abstract."},{"lesson_quoted":"Borrowing a relaxed condition from a neighboring literature without demonstrating its concrete benefit in your own setting leaves reviewers asking what the assumption actually buys.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The ordinal-drift condition is derived from the ranking-feedback setting itself (it is computable from the rankings alone) rather than imported, and its benefit -- sublinear regret where V_T is linear -- is made explicit as a separation."},{"lesson_quoted":"Re-deriving a rate that merely matches the baseline with near-identical algorithmic changes is read as an incremental extension, however clean the analysis.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate proves a strict separation (sublinear O_T regime where the V_T-assuming baseline diverges), not a matching rate, and adds an active-slate protocol absent from the baseline."},{"lesson_quoted":"Hidden constants that explode at the precise parameter limit where the result is advertised as strongest silently invalidate the headline guarantee, and reviewers find them in the proof.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The ordinal-discretization term scales with slate size k and as k grows the per-round bits and constants could grow; the candidate fixes small k=4 but does not yet bound the k-dependence of the constant -- a load-bearing detail the full proof must control, surfaced for Phase 4."},{"lesson_quoted":"An assumption-relaxation validated only on a single toy instance gives no evidence the relaxation captures the motivating practical regime.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Validation spans synthetic separation families AND self-play CCE-gap measurement AND an optional LLM-routing ranking testbed, not a single toy."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"Every retrieved learning-in-games leaf silently inherits, from the common no-regret ancestor, the assumption that the per-round feedback is a single passively-received observation whose informativeness is fixed by the environment; no retrieved paper questions whether the learner could instead govern WHAT comparisons it is shown -- i.e. whether the set of proposed actions that gets ranked each round should be treated as fixed-by-environment rather than as a quantity the learner influences.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The dominant failure is substituting one selection rule for another that performs better empirically while omitting the theorem that explains when and why it wins, or pivoting an assumption the community regards as a reasonable modeling choice rather than a genuine restriction, leaving both motivation and novelty in doubt.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Substituting one selection heuristic for another without a theorem stating when and why it wins reads as an engineering combination, not a contribution, no matter how clean the empirical gain.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The slate-acquisition rule is backed by a re-derived regret certificate showing it drives O_T to o(T), so the selection rule comes with a theorem stating when it wins, not just empirics."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pivoting an assumption the community treats as a reasonable modeling choice -- rather than first proving it a genuine restriction -- leaves both motivation and novelty in doubt.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The slate-fixed assumption is shown load-bearing because it is exactly what forces the prior work's total-variation precondition; pivoting it dissolves that precondition, so it is a genuine restriction, not a benign modeling choice."},{"lesson_quoted":"A re-derived guarantee whose binding constant is dataset-dependent and cannot be controlled by the practitioner is vacuous in the worst case and fails to convince.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The controlling quantity O_T is a learner-controllable count (the acquisition rule actively reduces it), so the binding quantity is under practitioner control by design rather than dataset-dependent."},{"lesson_quoted":"Unlocking a new capability by violating an assumption while ignoring a protective property it guarded -- detectability, validity, identifiability -- invites rejection on the overlooked side effect rather than the headline result.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"Letting the learner choose the slate could alter what equilibrium the self-play actually computes (the learner now influences which comparisons define the empirical play), a protected property -- the candidate should confirm the active slate still yields a valid CCE of the original game, surfaced for Phase 4."},{"lesson_quoted":"Improving a bound by a marginal factor with no matching lower bound fails to demonstrate that the improvement is significant or near-optimal enough to clear the bar.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The contribution is a regime separation (sublinear vs linear), not a marginal constant-factor bound improvement, so the matching-lower-bound concern does not bind the headline claim."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"Both gap_closure entries are borderline, none triggered: the C29 anchor leg's borderline is the unbounded k-dependence of the ordinal-discretization constant (lesson 'hidden constants that explode at the parameter limit'), and the C11 sibling leg's borderline is the overlooked protected property -- whether active slate control still computes a valid CCE of the original game (lesson 'unlocking a capability while ignoring a protective property it guarded'). Neither is a documented Reject match (candidate_match=yes), so the aggregate is borderline, not triggered."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf delivers a usable equilibrium-driving update under ranking-only feedback when the utility sequence is genuinely adversarial -- i.e. no method recovers no-regret behavior outside the sublinear-total-variation regularity regime that arxiv:2603.19221v1 must assume; the outcome that is missing is a learner that keeps converging when the comparison stream carries no magnitude AND the environment varies fast.","sub_pattern":"C29 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Take an existing convergence/regret guarantee for an iterative update procedure and pivot the single regularity-or-target assumption it rests on -- e.g. replace metric approximation error with ordinal rank-preservation, or boundedness of raw signals with boundedness of signal residuals -- then re-prove the rate by isolating one load-bearing per-iteration progress bound, with payoff a sharper rate or a provable separation between method classes.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism performs exactly this signature move: it pivots the ranking-feedback regret guarantee's convergence primitive from the metric condition V_T (total variation of raw utilities) to the ordinal-stability condition O_T (within-slate order-flip count) -- the documented 'metric error -> ordinal rank-preservation' and 'raw signal -> residual-of-signal' swaps -- and re-derives the rate via a single per-round ordinal-progress inequality that splits regret into a magnitude-free term plus an O_T-controlled term, yielding the documented payoff (a separation in the high-V_T/low-O_T regime).","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"Every retrieved learning-in-games leaf silently inherits, from the common no-regret ancestor, the assumption that the per-round feedback is a single passively-received observation whose informativeness is fixed by the environment; no retrieved paper questions whether the learner could instead govern WHAT comparisons it is shown -- i.e. whether the set of proposed actions that gets ranked each round should be treated as fixed-by-environment rather than as a quantity the learner influences.","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Center on a selection/acquisition/query rule (which candidate to query, which subset to retain, when to buy information), pivot the single assumption baked into that rule's criterion or required structure, and re-derive a performance certificate (a regret bound) for the pivoted rule that matches or beats the pre-pivot baseline.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism performs this move: it introduces a slate-acquisition rule (UCB-over-pairs: propose the k actions whose pairwise relative-rank-score gaps are most uncertain), pivots the assumption that the ranked slate is environment-fixed, and re-derives the regret certificate for the active-slate protocol, showing the rule drives the budgeted-choice quantity O_T to o(T) -- the cluster's 'which items enter the budgeted choice procedure' object and its re-derived certificate.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries instantiate their cited cluster's signature move: the C29 anchor performs the metric->ordinal convergence-primitive pivot with a load-bearing per-round progress inequality and a separation payoff, and the C11 sibling performs the selection-rule-pivot-plus-re-derived-certificate move with an explicit acquisition rule controlling which comparisons are bought."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["assumption_audit_and_pivot","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; the candidate's composition_set is the single pattern assumption_audit_and_pivot (both legs), so no 2-way anti-pattern subset matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"arxiv:2603.19221v1","threat_source":"lit_table","subsumption_argument":"arxiv:2603.19221v1 is the direct prior: it introduces online learning with ranking feedback and already proves sublinear regret plus approximate CCE in normal-form games. If its sublinear-total-variation assumption were already known to be removable by a slate-local ordinal condition, the candidate's headline would be subsumed. It is not: that paper treats the slate as environment-fixed and its regularity condition as exogenous and magnitude-based (V_T), and proves a small-temperature impossibility precisely because it never considers the learner controlling the slate. The candidate's claim stands or falls on whether the ordinal-drift count O_T (i) genuinely controls the regret rate in place of V_T and (ii) is learner-controllable via slate acquisition -- both absent from the prior. Collision retrieval surfaced no paper combining magnitude-free ordinal-stability, the total-variation-barrier separation, and active slate control toward CCE, so this is an addressable adjacency, not an exact-mechanism collision.","addressable_via":"Already addressed in differentiation_from_lit[0]; no field change required beyond ensuring the separation theorem explicitly exhibits the HIGH-TV/LOW-O class and the active-slate guarantee that O_T=o(T), which core_mechanism already states."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Surpassing the Total-Variation Barrier for Ranking-Feedback Learning via Active Slate Control\n\n**Method.** Active-Slate Ordinal Learning (ASOL)\n\n## Motivation\nWhen several computer programs (or people) repeatedly interact in a game, a standard recipe makes their average behavior settle into a stable, predictable pattern called a CCE (Coarse Correlated Equilibrium -- a kind of agreement no one can profitably break alone). The recipe needs each player to see a number every round: how good their last move was. But sometimes you only get a ranking -- 'option A beat option B beat option C' -- with no numbers attached. A ranking tells you the order but not by how much, and the usual recipe needs the 'how much'. The most recent work on this (an arXiv 2026-03 paper, 'Online Learning and Equilibrium Computation with Ranking Feedback') got the recipe to work with rankings only by assuming the world changes slowly in a precise numeric sense -- technically that the total variation of the hidden values, written $V_{T},$ grows slowly. That assumption quietly rules out exactly the fast-changing, adversarial situations the whole setup was meant to handle, so the method gives up right where it is needed most. Why now: that paper just opened this problem and also exposed its weak point, and the two tools needed to fix it are mature -- the standard 'mirror descent / regret matching' update for online learning, and the standard 'confidence-interval' bookkeeping from comparison-based bandits for deciding what to test next. What is new is realizing the learner does not have to passively accept whichever options get ranked: it can choose which options to put up for comparison each round. Prior work stopped because it treated that set of compared options (the 'slate') as fixed by the environment, and treated the slow-change requirement as something handed down from outside rather than something the algorithm could create. Our idea replaces the numeric 'how fast do the hidden values move' requirement $(V_{T})$ with a purely order-based quantity $-- O_{T},$ the number of rounds where the ranking among the compared options actually flips -- which you can measure from the rankings alone. Then we let the learner steer its own comparisons so that $O_{T}$ stays small. What changes when this works: ranking-only learning converges in fast-changing situations the old method abandoned, the earlier result becomes a special case the learner can reproduce on demand, and we get the first order-only notion of regret that future refinements (reaching stronger equilibria than CCE) could be built on.\n\n## Method\n### Background scaffolding\n*Standard mirror-descent / regret-matching loop and oracle interface reused unchanged.*\n\n1. Set the protocol constants: the slate size k (default 4 — how many actions are ranked together each round), the number of rounds T, and the action set of size n. Assume the environment can take any k actions you propose and return their order, sorted by a hidden quality score you never see as a number; if two actions are exactly equal, the oracle breaks the tie by a fixed action-index order so the returned order is always a complete strict ranking. Your goal is to output a sequence of mixed strategies (probability distributions over the actions).\n   - _Why_: It pins down the one thing both halves of the method touch -- the set of actions compared each round -- and declares it something you choose, not something the environment fixes.\n2. Send the slate $S_{t}$ to the ranking oracle and read back $r_{t},$ the order of those k actions. No numeric score is ever returned, so everything downstream must be derived from the order alone.\n   - _Why_: This is the only feedback the method ever sees, so everything downstream must work from the order alone.\n3. Update the mixed strategy with one mirror-descent step, which here has the simple multiplicative-weights closed form: multiply each action's current probability by $exp(-\\eta \\cdot g_{t}(action))$ and renormalize so the probabilities sum to one, using step size $\\eta  =$ sqrt(log n / T). Start from the uniform distribution over all actions. The new strategy is what gets played next, which shapes the next ranking you see.\n\n*The mirror-descent update over the simplex of mixed strategies: step along the ordinal surrogate $g_{t}$ with entropic Bregman divergence D and step size eta of order the square root of (log n over T); this is the played strategy that determines the next observed ranking.*\n$$ x_{t+1} = \\arg\\min_{x \\in \\Delta(A)} \\Big\\{ \\eta\\, \\langle g_t, x \\rangle + D(x, x_t) \\Big\\}, \\quad \\eta = \\sqrt{\\tfrac{\\log n}{T}} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: It is the standard, well-understood update that drives play toward equilibrium -- here fed an order-based signal instead of a numeric one.\n\n### Ordinal-stability convergence primitive (anchor, C29)\n*Encode feedback purely ordinally, measure the within-slate order-flip count $O_{T},$ and re-derive the regret rate around $O_{T}$ instead of $V_{T}.$*\n\n4. Turn the ranking into a loss vector $g_{t}:$ each ranked action gets minus its re-centered position (the slate-best most negative), and every action not ranked this round gets 0. At the same time track how often within-slate orderings flip: remember, for each distinct set of k actions you have proposed, the last order you saw for that exact set; whenever the same set comes back in a different order, add one to the flip count (the first time a set appears it just gets recorded, no increment). This per-set bookkeeping is what makes the flip count a clean within-slate quantity, and that count — not how big the hidden values swing — is the quantity the convergence guarantee depends on.\n\n*Defines the slate-local ordinal-drift count $O_{T}$ as the number of rounds in which the within-slate utility ordering on the proposed slate $S_{t}$ flips relative to the previous round; it is computable from rankings alone and replaces the utility total variation $V_{T}$ as the convergence primitive.*\n$$ O_T = \\sum_{t=1}^{T} \\mathbf{1}\\!\\left[\\, \\mathrm{argsort}\\big(u_t|_{S_t}\\big) \\neq \\mathrm{argsort}\\big(u_{t-1}|_{S_t}\\big) \\,\\right] \\tag{2} $$\n\n\n*The ordinal loss surrogate $g_{t}$ over the full action set: for an action in the slate it is the negative of its rank in $r_{t}$ re-centered to the interval from -(k-1)/2 to (k-1)/2, and zero for any action outside the slate, which carries no information that round.*\n$$ g_t(a) = \\begin{cases} -\\big(\\mathrm{rank}_{r_t}(a) - \\tfrac{k-1}{2}\\big) & a \\in S_t \\\\[2pt] 0 & a \\notin S_t \\end{cases} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: It converts a pure ordering into something the learning update can step along, and it measures the only quantity -- how often orderings flip -- that the convergence guarantee actually depends on.\n5. When analyzing, split the total regret into two pieces: a fixed order-discretization piece of size about $k\\cdot sqrt(T log$ n) that does not reference how big the hidden values swing, plus a piece equal to a constant times the order-flip count. The dependence on slate size k comes from the fact that each entry of the loss vector lives in the range from -(k-1)/2 to +(k-1)/2, which multiplies the standard regret bound; this leading constant grows with k, expected somewhere between linear and quadratic. 【author decision: the exact way the discretization constant grows with k must be pinned down by the authors, because the claim that this term is magnitude-free depends on it not blowing up as k increases.】 Conclude that regret is sublinear whenever the order-flip count is sublinear — with no assumption on how fast the hidden values change — which is exactly where the old slow-change method fails.\n\n*The regret split: cumulative ordinal-surrogate regret is bounded by a magnitude-free discretization term of order k times the square root of (T log n) plus a constant C times the ordinal-drift count $O_{T},$ with no $V_{T}$ dependence -- so regret is sublinear whenever $O_{T}$ is sublinear.*\n$$ \\mathrm{Reg}_T \\;\\le\\; \\underbrace{O\\!\\big(k\\sqrt{T \\log n}\\big)}_{\\text{magnitude-free}} \\;+\\; \\underbrace{C \\cdot O_T}_{\\text{ordinal drift}} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This split is the heart of the result: it proves the order-flip count, not how big the hidden values swing, is what controls convergence -- so you win exactly where the old method's slow-change assumption fails.\n\n### Active slate control (sibling, C11)\n*Let the learner choose which actions are ranked via a UCB-over-pairs rule that drives $O_{T}$ sublinear.*\n\n6. For every action keep a running estimate $s_{hat}(a)$ of its typical rank-score and a confidence radius c(a) that shrinks as you compare that action more often. Each time an action appears in a ranked slate, record its position re-centered so the best slot counts as +(k-1)/2 and the worst as -(k-1)/2, and average those over all slates the action has been in; the confidence radius is the standard Hoeffding width sqrt( $(k-1)^{2} \\cdot $ log(2 n T) / (2 $\\cdot $ max(N(a),1)) ), where N(a) is how many slates contained the action — it needs no tuning. Only count an action's appearances when it was actually placed in a ranked slate.\n   - _Why_: These order-based statistics are all you need to tell which comparisons are still uncertain -- and you never had to invent a fake numeric utility to get them.\n7. Choose this round's slate $S_{t}$ as the k actions whose pairwise rank-score gaps are most uncertain — meaning the pairs whose estimated score difference is still smaller than the sum of their two confidence radii (so you genuinely cannot yet tell which is better). Start the slate with the single most-uncertain pair, then add actions one at a time, each time picking the action that adds the most pairwise uncertainty against those already chosen, until you have k actions. At the very start, when an action has never been compared, treat its uncertainty as infinite so brand-new actions are always tried first; cycle every action through at least one slate before switching to the uncertainty-driven choice. Submit exactly those k actions for ranking.\n\n*The UCB-over-pairs slate-acquisition rule: choose the size-k slate $S_{t}$ that maximizes total pairwise rank-score uncertainty, prioritizing pairs whose estimated score gap is still within their combined confidence radii (the orderings whose flips would most damage the bound).*\n$$ S_t \\;=\\; \\underset{\\substack{S \\subseteq A \\\\ |S| = k}}{\\arg\\max}\\; \\sum_{\\{a,b\\} \\subseteq S} \\big[\\, |\\hat{s}(a) - \\hat{s}(b)| \\le c(a) + c(b) \\,\\big]\\cdot \\big(c(a) + c(b)\\big) \\tag{5} $$\n\n   - _Why_: By comparing the actions you are least sure how to order, you resolve the orderings whose surprise flips would most hurt convergence -- which is how you keep the order-flip count $O_{T}$ small.\n8. Fold the new ranks into the estimates: for each action that was in this slate, update its average re-centered rank, increase its observation count by one, and recompute its confidence radius with the new count. Leave untouched any action that was not ranked this round. Keeping these fresh is what lets the next slate choice keep targeting the still-uncertain orderings.\n   - _Why_: Keeping the estimates fresh is what lets the next slate choice (step 7 (Choose this round's slate $S_{t} as\\dots ))$ keep targeting the still-uncertain orderings.\n\n### Equilibrium lift\n*Turn the $O_{T}-governed$ single-learner regret guarantee into an approximate-CCE guarantee under self-play.*\n\n9. Run several copies of the protocol as players in one game; their time-average joint play converges to an approximate CCE, with the approximation error following the order-flip-controlled rate. Because actions not in a round's slate get a zero loss, the update is still defined over every action each round, so the no-regret guarantee covers deviations to ANY action — not just the ones that happened to be compared — which is what lets the folk theorem certify a real equilibrium of the original game. 【author decision: the authors must prove that the order-based regret actually upper-bounds the true value-based regret over all actions, since that inequality is what makes the equilibrium certification valid.】 Measure the CCE-gap as the most any single player could gain by deviating against the observed joint play.\n   - _Why_: It shows the order-only, $O_{T}-governed$ guarantee is strong enough to certify a real equilibrium of the original game, and that choosing your own comparisons does not distort which equilibrium you reach.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 通过主动 Slate 控制突破排序反馈学习中的 Total-Variation 壁垒\n\n**方法名称.** Active-Slate Ordinal Learning (ASOL)\n\n## 研究动机\n当好几个程序（或人）在一个博弈里反复交互时，有一套标准做法能让他们的平均行为收敛到一个稳定、可预测的状态，叫做 CCE（Coarse Correlated Equilibrium，粗相关均衡——一种没人能单方面占便宜的协调状态）。这套做法要求每个玩家每轮都看到一个数字：上一步动作有多好。但有时你只拿得到一个排序——“A 优于 B 优于 C”——却没有具体数值。排序告诉你顺序，却不告诉你差多少，而标准做法恰恰需要这个“差多少”。这个方向最新的工作（一篇 arXiv 2026-03 的论文《Online Learning and Equilibrium Computation with Ranking Feedback》）让这套做法在只有排序时也能用，但代价是假设世界以某个精确的数值意义变化得足够慢——技术上是假设隐藏效用的 total variation（记作 $V_{T}$）增长缓慢。这个假设悄悄排除了整套框架本应处理的、快速变化甚至对抗性的情形，于是方法恰恰在最该用的时候放弃了。为什么是现在：那篇论文刚刚打开这个问题，也暴露了它的软肋，而修复它所需的两件工具都已成熟——在线学习里标准的 mirror descent / regret matching 更新，以及基于比较的 bandit 里标准的置信区间记账法（用来决定下一步该测什么）。真正新的地方在于：学习者不必被动接受环境给定的那组被排序的动作，它可以自己决定每轮把哪些动作拿去比较。先前工作止步，是因为它把这组被比较的动作（“slate”）当成环境固定的，又把“慢变化”要求当成外部强加而非算法可以自己制造的东西。我们的想法是用一个纯粹基于顺序的量替换掉“隐藏效用变化多快”的数值要求（$V_{T}$）——这个量就是 $O_{T}$，即被比较动作之间排序真正发生翻转的轮数，它只凭排序就能测出来。然后我们让学习者自己引导比较，使 $O_{T}$ 保持很小。做成之后会怎样：只靠排序的学习能在旧方法放弃的快速变化情形里收敛，先前的结果成为学习者可按需复现的特例，而且我们得到第一个纯顺序的 regret 概念，未来要达到比 CCE 更强的均衡的工作都可以在它之上构建。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景脚手架\n*原样复用的标准 mirror-descent / regret-matching 循环与 oracle 接口。*\n\n1. 固定协议常数：slate 大小 k（默认 4——每轮一起被排序的动作数）、总轮数 T，以及大小为 n 的动作集合 A。假设环境能对你提出的任意 k 个动作，按一个你永远看不到具体数值的隐藏质量分返回它们的顺序；若两个动作恰好相等，oracle 按固定的动作索引顺序打破平局，使返回的始终是一个完整的严格排序 $r_{t}$。目标是输出一串在动作上的混合策略（动作上的概率分布）。\n   - _为什么_: 它钉住了方法两半都要碰的那个东西——每轮被比较的动作集合——并声明它由你来选，而不是环境固定的。\n2. 把 slate $S_{t}$ 提交给排序 oracle，读回 $r_{t}$，即这 k 个动作的顺序。全程不返回任何数值得分，因此后续一切都必须只凭顺序推导。\n   - _为什么_: 这是方法唯一能看到的反馈，所以后续一切都必须只凭顺序工作。\n3. 用一步 mirror-descent 更新混合策略，这里有简单的 multiplicative-weights 闭式：把每个动作当前的概率乘以 $exp(-\\eta \\cdot g_{t}($动作))，再归一化使概率和为 1，步长取 $\\eta  =$ sqrt(log n / T)。从所有动作上的均匀分布出发。新策略就是下一步要打出的，它会塑造你接下来看到的排序。\n\n*在混合策略单纯形上的 mirror-descent 更新：沿序数代理 $g_{t}$ 前进，配熵正则的 Bregman 散度 D，步长 eta 取 log n 除以 T 再开方的量级；它给出的就是下一轮观测排序所依赖的所打出的策略。*\n$$ x_{t+1} = \\arg\\min_{x \\in \\Delta(A)} \\Big\\{ \\eta\\, \\langle g_t, x \\rangle + D(x, x_t) \\Big\\}, \\quad \\eta = \\sqrt{\\tfrac{\\log n}{T}} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这是标准、被充分理解的、能把博弈推向均衡的更新——这里只是喂给它一个基于顺序的信号而非数值信号。\n\n### 序数稳定性收敛主量（anchor, C29）\n*把反馈纯粹按顺序编码，测量 slate 内序翻转计数 $O_{T}$，并围绕 $O_{T}$ 而非 $V_{T}$ 重新推导 regret 速率。*\n\n4. 把排序转成损失向量 $g_{t}$：每个被排序的动作取其中心化名次的负值（slate 内最好的最负），本轮未被排序的动作一律取 0。同时统计 slate 内序翻转的频率：为每一个你提议过的、由 k 个动作构成的集合，记住该集合上次出现时的顺序；每当同一集合以不同顺序再次出现，就把翻转计数加一（某集合首次出现只记录、不加一）。这种按集合的记账使翻转计数成为干净的 slate 内量，而这个计数——而非隐藏效用摆动多大——正是收敛保证所依赖的量。\n\n*把 slate 内序数漂移计数 $O_{T}$ 定义为：在所提议 slate $S_{t}$ 上，本轮的效用序相对上一轮发生翻转的轮数总和；它仅凭排序即可计算，用来替代效用 total variation $V_{T}$ 作为收敛主量。*\n$$ O_T = \\sum_{t=1}^{T} \\mathbf{1}\\!\\left[\\, \\mathrm{argsort}\\big(u_t|_{S_t}\\big) \\neq \\mathrm{argsort}\\big(u_{t-1}|_{S_t}\\big) \\,\\right] \\tag{2} $$\n\n\n*在全体动作集合上构造的序数损失代理 $g_{t}$：对 slate 内的动作，取其在 $r_{t}$ 中的名次、再中心化到区间 -(k-1)/2 到 (k-1)/2 后取负；slate 外的动作当轮无信息，置为 0。*\n$$ g_t(a) = \\begin{cases} -\\big(\\mathrm{rank}_{r_t}(a) - \\tfrac{k-1}{2}\\big) & a \\in S_t \\\\[2pt] 0 & a \\notin S_t \\end{cases} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 它把纯粹的顺序转成学习更新可以沿其前进的东西，并测量出收敛保证真正依赖的唯一量——顺序翻转的频率。\n5. 在分析时，把总 regret 拆成两块：一块是固定的顺序离散化项（量级约为 $k\\cdot sqrt(T log$ n)），它不涉及隐藏效用摆动多大；另一块等于常数乘以序翻转计数。对 slate 大小 k 的依赖来自损失向量每个分量落在区间 -(k-1)/2 到 +(k-1)/2，这会把标准 regret 界乘上该区间；这个领头常数随 k 增长，预期介于线性与二次之间。【作者需决定：离散化常数随 k 增长的确切阶必须由作者敲定，因为“该项与幅值无关”这一论断取决于它不随 k 增大而爆炸。】由此得出：只要序翻转计数次线性，regret 即次线性——且不对隐藏效用变化多快做任何假设——这恰好是旧的慢变化方法失效之处。\n\n*regret 分解：累积序数代理 regret 被界为一个与幅值无关的离散化项（量级为 k 乘以 T log n 的平方根）加上常数 C 乘以序数漂移计数 $O_{T}$，全程不含 $V_{T}$；因此只要 $O_{T}$ 次线性，regret 即次线性。*\n$$ \\mathrm{Reg}_T \\;\\le\\; \\underbrace{O\\!\\big(k\\sqrt{T \\log n}\\big)}_{\\text{magnitude-free}} \\;+\\; \\underbrace{C \\cdot O_T}_{\\text{ordinal drift}} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这个拆分是结果的核心：它证明控制收敛的是顺序翻转计数，而非隐藏效用摆动多大——所以你恰好在旧方法慢变化假设失效之处取胜。\n\n### 主动 slate 控制（sibling, C11）\n*用 UCB-over-pairs 规则让学习者自选被排序的动作，从而把 $O_{T}$ 压到次线性。*\n\n6. 对每个动作维护一个对其典型名次得分的估计 $s_{hat}(a)$，以及一个随该动作被比较次数增多而收缩的置信半径 c(a)。每当某动作出现在被排序的 slate 中，就把它的名次中心化记录（最好的位置记为 +(k-1)/2，最差的记为 -(k-1)/2），并对该动作所在过的全部 slate 取平均；置信半径取标准的 Hoeffding 宽度 sqrt( $(k-1)^{2} \\cdot $ log(2 n T) / (2 $\\cdot $ max(N(a),1)) )，其中 N(a) 是包含该动作的 slate 数——它无需调参。只有当动作真的被放进某个被排序的 slate 时才计入它的出现次数。\n   - _为什么_: 这些基于顺序的统计量足以判断哪些比较仍不确定——而你根本不必伪造一个数值效用就能得到它们。\n7. 把本轮 slate $S_{t}$ 选为成对名次得分差最不确定的那 k 个动作——即那些估计得分差仍小于两者置信半径之和的成对动作（也就是你确实还分不出谁更好）。先用最不确定的那一对作为种子，再逐个加入动作，每次选那个相对已入选动作贡献最多成对不确定性的动作，直到凑满 k 个。在最开始，当某动作从未被比较过时，把它的不确定性当作无穷大，使全新动作总是优先被试；先让每个动作都至少进过一个 slate，再切换到由不确定性驱动的选择。把这恰好 k 个动作提交去排序。\n\n*UCB-over-pairs 的 slate 采集规则：选取使成对名次得分不确定性总和最大的大小为 k 的 slate $S_{t}$，优先选那些估计得分差仍落在两者置信半径之和以内的成对动作（即其翻转最会破坏界的那些序关系）。*\n$$ S_t \\;=\\; \\underset{\\substack{S \\subseteq A \\\\ |S| = k}}{\\arg\\max}\\; \\sum_{\\{a,b\\} \\subseteq S} \\big[\\, |\\hat{s}(a) - \\hat{s}(b)| \\le c(a) + c(b) \\,\\big]\\cdot \\big(c(a) + c(b)\\big) \\tag{5} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 通过比较那些你最不确定如何排序的动作，你解决了一旦翻转最会损害收敛的那些序关系——这正是把序翻转计数 $O_{T}$ 保持很小的办法。\n8. 把新名次并入估计：对本 slate 内的每个动作，更新其中心化名次的平均值，把观测计数加一，并用新计数重算其置信半径。本轮未被排序的动作保持不变。保持这些估计新鲜，才能让下一次 slate 选择持续瞄准仍不确定的序关系。\n   - _为什么_: 保持估计新鲜，才能让下一次 slate 选择（第7步（把本轮 slate $S_{t}\\dots $））持续瞄准仍不确定的序关系。\n\n### 均衡提升\n*把由 $O_{T}$ 主导的单学习者 regret 保证，在自博弈下转化为近似 CCE 保证。*\n\n9. 把协议的若干副本作为同一博弈里的玩家来运行；它们的时间平均联合策略收敛到近似 CCE，近似误差跟随由序翻转计数控制的速率。由于某轮 slate 外的动作被赋零损失，更新每轮仍在全体动作上有定义，所以无悔保证覆盖向任意动作的偏离——而不仅是恰好被比较过的那些——这正是 folk theorem 能认证原博弈一个真实均衡的依据。【作者需决定：作者必须证明基于顺序的 regret 确实在全体动作上上界住基于真实效用值的 regret，因为正是这个不等式使均衡认证成立。】把 CCE-gap 测为任一玩家针对所观测到的联合策略偏离所能获得的最大收益。\n   - _为什么_: 它表明这个纯顺序、由 $O_{T}$ 主导的保证足以认证原博弈的一个真实均衡，且自选比较不会扭曲你所达到的均衡。\n\n"},{"id":"90","run_dir":"run_prompt90_openthoughts","index":90,"title":"Recipes That Watch the Student: Per-Trace Marginal Value for Reasoning Distillation","title_zh":"会观察学生的数据配方：面向推理蒸馏的逐条轨迹边际价值","method_name":"Marginal-Value Readout (MVR)","hook":"Every reasoning-data recipe scores a chain-of-thought trace by properties of the trace itself (correctness, length, diversity, a learned quality logit), but a trace's actual training value is a property of the (trace, student) pair: we show that a cheap, frozen-backbone readout of how a candidate trace's training gradient aligns with the student's deficit direction on a held-out reasoning probe predicts the trace's downstream competence gain, and that ranking by this readout reweights — and ultimately replaces — fixed-pool selection with gap-targeted acquisition.","anchor_pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","anchor_pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","domain_category":"LLM Reasoning & Decoding","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a per-example signal of a trace's MARGINAL training value for a specific target student — i.e. how much fine-tuning on that one trace shifts that student's reasoning behavior on held-out target queries — so curation cannot prefer traces that teach a missing skill over traces that re-demonstrate an already-mastered one.","pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by manufacturing the missing per-(trace,student) value label as an internal learning-dynamics readout: a frozen-backbone, tiny-lever gradient-alignment statistic between the candidate trace's SFT gradient and the student's deficit-gradient on a held-out reasoning probe, which is a diagnostic of learning dynamics (C07's signature: the signal is a dynamics diagnostic, not a pseudo-label) rather than a trace-intrinsic quality score.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether SELECTING from a fixed teacher-sampled pool is even the right framing — every leaf inherits from a shared ancestor the assumption that the trace pool is given and curation only filters it, never asking whether the recipe should instead GENERATE the specific traces a student's measured gap calls for.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by auditing the acquisition/selection rule at the heart of every recipe (greedy ranking by a trace-intrinsic quality surrogate over a fixed teacher pool) and reframing it (C11's reframe branch): once marginal value is the (trace,student-deficit) alignment of the anchor leg, the selection lens dissolves into a budgeted active-acquisition problem whose objective is deficit coverage, and we re-derive a regret-style certificate showing gap-targeted acquisition strictly beats fixed-pool top-k under the same trace budget.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"data curation / recipe design for training reasoning language models (CoT SFT + distillation)","n_papers":49,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":27},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":7,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Self-Training with Direct Preference Optimization Improves Chain-of-Thought Reasoning"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Diagnostic accuracy of large language models in psychiatry"},{"source":"openalex","title":"TnT-LLM: Text Mining at Scale with Large Language Models"},{"source":"openalex","title":"The FineWeb Datasets: Decanting the Web for the Finest Text Data at Scale"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Boosting GPT models for genomics analysis: generating trusted genetic variant annotations and interpretations through RAG and Fine-tuning"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Scaling Synthetic Data Creation with 1,000,000,000 Personas"}],"more":1},{"year":2025,"n":34,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Phi-4-Mini-Reasoning: Exploring the Limits of Small Reasoning Language Models in Math"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"MedVLThinker: Simple Baselines for Multimodal Medical Reasoning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Is Chain-of-Thought Reasoning of LLMs a Mirage? A Data Distribution Lens"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Towards System 2 Reasoning in LLMs: Learning How to Think With Meta Chain-of-Thought"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"URSA: Understanding and Verifying Chain-of-thought Reasoning in Multimodal Mathematics"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"AgentThink: A Unified Framework for Tool-Augmented Chain-of-Thought Reasoning in Vision-Language Models for Autonomous Driving"}],"more":28},{"year":2026,"n":9,"papers":[{"source":"arxiv","title":"ChaosBench-Logic: A Benchmark for Logical and Symbolic Reasoning on Chaotic Dynamical Systems"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"CROP: Token-Efficient Reasoning in Large Language Models via Regularized Prompt Optimization"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"$π^2$: Structure-Originated Reasoning Data Improves Long-Context Reasoning Ability of Large Language Models"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"CosmicFish-HRM: Adaptive Reasoning via Hierarchical Recurrent Mechanisms in Compact Language Models"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Native Reasoning Models: Training Language Models to Reason on Unverifiable Data"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"DeltaLogic: Minimal Premise Edits Reveal Belief-Revision Failures in Logical Reasoning Models"}],"more":3}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":17,"share":0.347},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":10,"share":0.204},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":6,"share":0.122},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":5,"share":0.102},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":4,"share":0.082},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":4,"share":0.082},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":3,"share":0.061},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":2,"share":0.041}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Recent reasoning-data recipes converge on the same move: assemble a pool of long chain-of-thought traces (distilled from a teacher such as DeepSeek-R1, or synthesized) and then SELECT a subset by surface heuristics — s1 (openalex:W4407092048) filters its 59K pool down to 1K by hand-graded quality, difficulty, and diversity; Phi-4-Mini-Reasoning (semanticscholar:6bff8801673f2e12d2da5e42b917428a4f8adbaa) applies rejection sampling to keep only correct teacher traces; SynSelect (semanticscholar:ee7287d970000f1a821eaeff744fdc4540468cf7) and DLCoT (semanticscholar:2d7d5b0535c041852af9e32495df1aff241dc8cb) replace the heuristic with a learned scalar quality/utility score. All of these score a trace by properties of the trace ITSELF (correctness, length, diversity, a quality classifier's logit) — none scores a trace by what it actually does to the STUDENT being trained: whether fine-tuning on that specific trace moves the student's behavior toward the reasoning competence it lacks. Meanwhile the 'Mirage' analysis (semanticscholar:0d3f125867ddbb0a4882feb0043134a02957c375) shows CoT efficacy is governed by the distribution discrepancy between training traces and test queries, not by the traces' intrinsic quality — so a recipe optimizing trace-intrinsic quality is optimizing the wrong quantity, and the field has no per-example signal of a trace's marginal training value for a given student that survives across the curation pool.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4407092048","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"s1 builds a strong reasoning model by curating just 1K examples from a 59K pool using three hand-applied principles (quality, difficulty, diversity) and pairing them with simple test-time budget forcing. Its method section makes the residue explicit: the selection is a static, model-agnostic filter applied once before any training — it never measures, for a given target student, the marginal effect of including a particular trace on that student's downstream reasoning, so it cannot tell a trace that teaches the student a missing skill from one that merely re-demonstrates what the student already does."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:ee7287d970000f1a821eaeff744fdc4540468cf7","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"SynSelect synthesizes long multimodal CoT then selects via a learned quality-scoring stage. The score is a property of the trace (a quality classifier), evaluated independently of any particular student model and of any measured downstream effect, so two students with different skill gaps receive the same selected subset and the selection cannot adapt to which traces close which student's gap."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:0d3f125867ddbb0a4882feb0043134a02957c375","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"The 'Mirage' paper formalizes CoT as an in-distribution inductive bias and shows test-time success tracks train/test distribution overlap rather than trace quality. It is purely diagnostic: it gives a distribution-discrepancy lens but no constructive recipe that selects or generates traces to close the discrepancy for a particular student-task pair."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:6bff8801673f2e12d2da5e42b917428a4f8adbaa","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Phi-4-Mini-Reasoning frames distillation as mid-training on a large diverse correct-only CoT corpus, then SFT, then RLVR — a staged recipe. Its selection is rejection sampling on correctness; it never ranks the retained-correct traces by their per-student marginal training value, so the corpus is sized by what the teacher produces, not by what the student needs to learn."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"data curation / recipe design for training reasoning language models (CoT SFT + distillation)","venue":"ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML","time":"2026","data":["distilled long-CoT trace pools (e.g. DeepSeek-R1 sampled traces)","curated reasoning SFT sets (s1K, NuminaMATH-style math/code/olympiad)","synthetic reasoning traces"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with cloud access; can fine-tune 1-7B models","preference":"both","baseline":"quality/difficulty/diversity heuristic curation (s1) and learned-quality-score selection (SynSelect, DLCoT)","limitation":"current reasoning-data recipes select traces by surface heuristics or a learned scalar quality score with no measurement of whether a selected trace actually transfers reasoning skill to the target student model","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object both legs read from and write to is the per-(trace, student) MARGINAL-VALUE READOUT v(t; s, D_probe), a single scalar computed entirely from the current student s and a small held-out reasoning probe set D_probe, never from the trace's intrinsic properties. Define the student deficit direction g_def = the average per-token SFT gradient of s on the FAILED items of D_probe (items s currently answers wrong), restricted to a tiny lever theta_L = {the LM output head + the final transformer block's LayerNorm affine parameters} with the rest of the backbone frozen (this lever is fixed a priori, ~0.3% of params, and is the only set differentiated — this is what makes v cheap and what distinguishes it from a full-parameter influence estimate). For a candidate trace t (a full question+CoT+answer trajectory), define its training gradient g_t = the same restricted SFT gradient of s on t. The readout is the deficit-aligned component v(t;s,D_probe) = <g_t, g_def> / (||g_def|| + eps), i.e. the projection of the trace's gradient onto the unit deficit direction; eps = 1e-8 is a fixed numerical floor. v is positive when training on t pushes the lever the same way the student's own held-out failures demand, near zero when t re-demonstrates an already-mastered skill (g_t orthogonal to the unmet-deficit direction), and negative when t would pull the student away from its deficit. ANCHOR LEG (C07): we manufacture v as the supervisory signal that ground-truth marginal value would have provided; because the lever is tiny and frozen-backbone, g_def and every g_t are one cheap backward pass, so v(t;s) is computable for an entire teacher pool in one epoch-equivalent of forward-backward cost, and curation ranks/reweights traces by v rather than by a trace-intrinsic quality logit. To stop the unsupervised signal from collapsing onto a single probe quirk (C07 step 4 stabilizer), g_def is re-estimated every k optimizer steps from the CURRENT student's still-failing probe items (a two-time-scale schedule: deficit recomputed slower than the SFT updates), so as the student masters a skill that skill's traces decay toward v approximately 0 and acquisition moves on. AUDIT LEG (C11): with v in hand, the inherited 'curation = filter a fixed teacher pool by trace-intrinsic quality' rule is exposed as a greedy ranker on the wrong surrogate; we reframe curation as budgeted active acquisition that maximizes cumulative realized deficit coverage sum_t max(v(t;s_t), 0) under a B-trace budget, and prove a regret bound: gap-targeted acquisition incurs regret O(sqrt(B * d_eff)) against the clairvoyant best-B subset, where d_eff is the effective rank of the deficit subspace, whereas fixed-pool top-k by any student-independent surrogate suffers regret linear in B whenever the pool's quality ordering is uncorrelated with the student's realized deficit — which the 'Mirage' result (semanticscholar:0d3f125867ddbb0a4882feb0043134a02957c375) predicts is exactly the regime when the teacher pool's distribution does not overlap the student's failure region. The pivot's payoff collapses (regret reverts to linear) the moment g_def is replaced by a student-independent constant, binding the gain to the (trace,student) coupling.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery, not separate modules: the anchor's value readout v IS the object the audit leg pivots on, so the coherence thread is shared_object — without v the audit's 'acquire-to-gap beats select-from-pool' claim has no measurable acquisition criterion, and with v the audit is a near-immediate corollary, which is why I selected anchor+1-sibling rather than stapling a third distribution-discrepancy leg. (b) Avoided-node check (method_lineage regression flag): a naive 'rank traces by gradient norm' or full influence-function/TracIn score (collateral node c2) and classical expected-model-change coreset (c1) were considered and rejected — they score against a single-step training loss and require per-trace retraining or full-parameter gradient inner products, whereas v is (i) a deficit-DIRECTION projection, not a magnitude, (ii) restricted to a fixed tiny frozen-backbone lever so it is one cheap pass, and (iii) targeted at held-out reasoning COMPETENCE (probe failures) rather than training loss, so it does not reduce to c1/c2; I also rejected a difficulty-curriculum ordering (c3) because difficulty is student-independent and is exactly the trace-intrinsic surrogate the audit leg overturns.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: take a 1.5B-3B base model as the student, a fixed teacher pool of ~50k correct distilled long-CoT math traces, and a held-out MATH/GSM-style reasoning benchmark; train three students at an equal budget of B=5k admitted traces — (A) selected by the per-(trace,student) value readout v, (B) selected by an s1-style trace-intrinsic quality+difficulty+diversity filter, (C) random — and measure held-out pass@1. If the candidate works, (A)'s pass@1 exceeds (B)'s at the same B and the gap WIDENS as B shrinks (the small-budget regime is where choosing the right traces matters most), i.e. value-ranked acquisition is more trace-efficient than trace-intrinsic selection. The single named load-bearing variable is the deficit direction g_def (the student's held-out-failure gradient direction on the tiny lever); the mechanism claim is that v's predictive power comes from g_def's coupling to the student's actual deficit, not from any trace-intrinsic correlate. Negative control: recompute v with g_def REPLACED by a student-independent random fixed direction (so v becomes a trace-intrinsic-only projection that ignores the student) and re-run acquisition — the downstream held-out pass@1 must fall back to baseline-(B) level; if pass@1 stays high with a randomized g_def, then the gain was never about student-deficit coupling and the mechanism is falsified. Positive control: a stripped-down acquirer that uses ONLY sign(v) (admit iff v>0, ignore magnitude and all trace features) should recover most of (A)'s pass@1 gain over (B), showing the deficit-aligned direction alone carries the value signal.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4407092048","delta":"s1 selects 1K traces by three hand-applied model-AGNOSTIC principles (quality, difficulty, diversity) computed once before training; we construct a per-(trace, student) marginal-value scalar v from the student's held-out-failure gradient direction, so our selected subset is student-specific and changes as the student learns, which s1's static filter cannot produce."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:ee7287d970000f1a821eaeff744fdc4540468cf7","delta":"SynSelect ranks synthesized traces by a learned scalar quality classifier evaluated independently of any student and of any measured downstream effect; we rank by a directly measured downstream-effect proxy (deficit-gradient alignment on a frozen-backbone lever), and we prove a regret separation between the two regimes that SynSelect's quality-score framing does not address."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:0d3f125867ddbb0a4882feb0043134a02957c375","delta":"The 'Mirage' paper diagnoses that CoT efficacy tracks train/test distribution overlap but offers no constructive recipe; we turn that diagnosis into an operational acquisition objective (maximize realized deficit coverage) and a certificate identifying exactly the no-overlap regime where trace-intrinsic selection provably underperforms."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:6bff8801673f2e12d2da5e42b917428a4f8adbaa","delta":"Phi-4-Mini-Reasoning retains traces by correctness (rejection sampling) and sizes the corpus by teacher output; we additionally rank retained-correct traces by per-student marginal value and size the corpus by realized deficit coverage, a per-student stopping criterion their staged recipe lacks."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4407092048","what_step_was_missed":"s1 demonstrated that a tiny, sharply-curated subset suffices, but it computed the curation score as a static model-agnostic property of each trace; to already contain our contribution it would have needed to construct a student-conditioned value functional — specifically the projection of a candidate trace's lever-restricted training gradient onto the student's held-out-failure gradient direction, refreshed as the student learns — which requires defining and measuring a (trace, student-deficit) coupling object that s1's one-shot pre-training filter never builds."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":298,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"No hard floor fired: gap_closure_reject_check is borderline (no 'yes'), anti_pattern_check matched nothing, and the paper_pointed_threat (LearnAlign/GRACE/ZPD) is an ADDRESSABLE adjacency, not exact-mechanism overlap. But the threat hits the candidate's load-bearing novelty axis — 'gradient-aligned student-aware reasoning data selection' is an occupied 2025-2026 frontier — so per the 'paper_pointed_threat exists AND addressable_via names a specific field' heuristic the verdict is revise: tighten differentiation_from_lit / core_mechanism_reasoning to pin the delta (held-out-deficit-direction target + generative pivot + acquisition certificate), and shore up the C11 borderlines by stating d_eff is practitioner-estimable and tying the regret separation to the realistic no-overlap regime.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a per-example signal of a trace's MARGINAL training value for a specific target student — i.e. how much fine-tuning on that one trace shifts that student's reasoning behavior on held-out target queries — so curation cannot prefer traces that teach a missing skill over traces that re-demonstrate an already-mastered one.","main_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"A manufactured internal signal whose validity silently rests on an assumption that does not survive deployment (calibration, a known-finite shift set, or covert use of target/test-set information that amounts to label leakage); a second shape is recombining well-known components (gradient-norm-as-proxy, EMA blending) without a single load-bearing mechanistic insight that separates the work from the prior art it resembles.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A label-free signal whose validity depends on model calibration silently fails on exactly the deep networks known to be poorly calibrated — validate a surrogate where its core assumption is weakest, not where it is convenient.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The readout v is a gradient-direction projection, not a calibration/confidence quantity, so it does not depend on model calibration."},{"lesson_quoted":"Importing a generic continual-learning blending or interpolation technique into a new modality without identifying that modality's specific dynamics lever reads as recombination, not contribution.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The candidate does identify a specific lever (deficit-direction projection on a frozen tiny lever, dynamically refreshed), but gradient-aligned data selection for reasoning is now an active 2025-2026 frontier (GRACE, LearnAlign), so the 'one load-bearing insight that separates it from the prior art it resembles' must be made explicit or it risks reading as recombination."},{"lesson_quoted":"Using target or test-set information during adaptation invites a label-leakage objection that undermines the very source-free, label-free deployment setting the method claims.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The deficit direction g_def is computed on a held-out PROBE set that is explicitly disjoint from both the teacher pool and the final evaluation benchmark, so it is target-DOMAIN but not test-set leakage; the falsification harness keeps the benchmark separate."},{"lesson_quoted":"A multi-branch or ensemble reweighting mechanism that overlaps with standard multi-task/mixture-of-experts ensembling must explicitly beat both the single-model and the standard-ensemble baselines, or the gain is credited to prior art.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"No ensemble/multi-branch reweighting is used; the mechanism is a single value scalar over a single student."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether SELECTING from a fixed teacher-sampled pool is even the right framing — every leaf inherits from a shared ancestor the assumption that the trace pool is given and curation only filters it, never asking whether the recipe should instead GENERATE the specific traces a student's measured gap calls for.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The dominant failure is substituting one selection rule for another that performs better empirically while omitting the theorem that explains when and why it wins; a third shape is producing a guarantee that does not hold up (a dataset-dependent uncontrollable binding constant, or a regularity condition the selection mechanism provably violates).","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Substituting one selection heuristic for another without a theorem stating when and why it wins reads as an engineering combination, not a contribution, no matter how clean the empirical gain.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The audit leg DOES supply a theorem: a regret bound separating gap-targeted acquisition (O(sqrt(B*d_eff))) from fixed-pool top-k (linear-in-B in the no-overlap regime), so it is not a bare heuristic swap."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pivoting an assumption the community treats as a reasonable modeling choice — rather than first proving it a genuine restriction — leaves both motivation and novelty in doubt.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The pivoted assumption (curation = filter a fixed teacher pool) IS load-bearing and is shown restrictive by the Mirage no-overlap regime, but the candidate must visibly tie the regret separation to a regime the practitioner actually faces rather than an adversarial corner, or reviewers may read the fixed-pool assumption as a benign convention."},{"lesson_quoted":"A re-derived guarantee whose binding constant is dataset-dependent and cannot be controlled by the practitioner is vacuous in the worst case and fails to convince.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"d_eff (effective rank of the deficit subspace) is a data-dependent constant; the candidate should state it is practitioner-estimable (measured from the probe-gradient Gram spectrum) so the bound is not vacuous."},{"lesson_quoted":"Building the entire analysis on a regularity condition (such as continuity or a Lipschitz bound) that the selection mechanism provably violates contradicts and undermines the formal claims.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The regret argument is over a discrete acquisition rule and a linear projection; it does not import a continuity/Lipschitz assumption the discrete selection would violate."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No Reject lesson is a hard 'yes'. The weight sits on the C07 recombination lesson (gradient-aligned reasoning data selection is an occupied frontier, so the load-bearing separating insight must be explicit) and two C11 borderlines about the regret bound's constant (d_eff) and the restrictiveness of the pivoted assumption — all load-bearing but addressable by sharpening differentiation and the guarantee statement, not abandon-level."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a per-example signal of a trace's MARGINAL training value for a specific target student ...","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Treat an already-trained model's own internal-state readouts (output entropy, gradient direction and magnitude, representation moments) as the manufactured supervisory signal, pairing a mechanistic diagnosis that localizes the failure to a structural site with a surgically tiny frozen-backbone lever; frequently the 'signal' is a diagnostic of learning dynamics rather than a label.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism defines v as the projection of a candidate trace's lever-restricted training gradient onto the student's held-out-failure (deficit) gradient direction, computed on a fixed ~0.3% frozen-backbone lever, with a two-time-scale refresh of g_def as the student learns — this is exactly C07's 'gradient direction readout as a learning-dynamics diagnostic on a tiny frozen lever' move, not a generic quality score.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether SELECTING from a fixed teacher-sampled pool is even the right framing ...","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Center on a selection/acquisition/query/stopping rule, name the ONE load-bearing assumption its criterion or required structure rests on, and either relax or REFRAME it (adopt a different problem class wholesale), then re-derive the formal performance certificate in the field's native currency (regret/competitive ratio).","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism names the inherited rule (greedy top-k by a trace-intrinsic quality surrogate over a fixed teacher pool), reframes it as budgeted active acquisition maximizing realized deficit coverage, and re-derives a regret certificate vs the clairvoyant best-B subset — the C11 reframe-and-recertify move is present.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both legs perform their cited cluster's signature move: C07's tiny-frozen-lever learning-dynamics gradient readout is the value scalar, and C11's reframe-the-acquisition-rule-plus-regret-certificate is the audit leg. Neither is merely the parent pattern's generic gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["self_supervised_signal_engineering","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented anti-pattern compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; the candidate's composition {self_supervised_signal_engineering, assumption_audit_and_pivot} matches none of them."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"LearnAlign (Data Selection for LLM Reinforcement Learning with Improved Gradient Alignment, 2025-06, collision_hits)","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"LearnAlign already performs gradient-alignment-based selection of REASONING data toward a target, and adds a model-aware 'data learnability' notion derived from per-example success rate — so it occupies both the 'gradient alignment for reasoning data' headline and the 'student-aware' axis the candidate claims. Two adjacent collision hits compound the threat: GRACE (2026-05) is literally titled 'Gradient-aligned Reasoning Data Curation' and scores reasoning steps by alignment with the answer-oriented gradient direction, and ZPD Detector (2026-01) selects data via an evolving capability-difficulty alignment that models the student-data relationship over training. The candidate's claim stands or falls on whether its specific alignment TARGET (the student's HELD-OUT-FAILURE/deficit gradient direction, refreshed two-time-scale) and its acquisition certificate are a genuine delta over LearnAlign's success-rate-learnability + answer-direction alignment (GRACE) — gradient alignment per se, and student-awareness per se, are no longer novel.","addressable_via":"Sharpen differentiation_from_lit and core_mechanism_reasoning to (a) name LearnAlign/GRACE/ZPD explicitly and (b) state the precise delta — alignment to the held-out-DEFICIT direction (what the student still fails) rather than the answer-oriented gradient (GRACE) or success-rate learnability (LearnAlign), plus the generative pivot and the regret certificate — so the contribution is not subsumed by the occupied 'gradient-aligned reasoning data selection' headline."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat — LearnAlign (gradient-alignment reasoning data selection + success-rate learnability), GRACE (gradient-aligned reasoning data curation, answer-oriented direction), and ZPD Detector (evolving capability-difficulty alignment) occupy the candidate's 'gradient-aligned student-aware reasoning selection' headline.","fix_direction":"Add explicit differentiation_from_lit entries for LearnAlign, GRACE, and ZPD Detector. For each, state the substantive delta: vs GRACE, our alignment TARGET is the student's held-out-FAILURE (deficit) gradient direction, not the answer-oriented gradient direction, so we prefer traces that teach what the student still fails rather than steps that agree with the correct answer; vs LearnAlign, our value is a directional deficit-projection refreshed two-time-scale, not a static per-example success-rate 'learnability' scalar, and we add a generative (acquire-to-gap) pivot LearnAlign's fixed-pool selection lacks; vs ZPD Detector, we provide a measurable gradient-deficit readout and a regret certificate rather than a capability-difficulty heuristic."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism_reasoning","issue":"C07 recombination borderline + C11 'is the pivoted assumption genuinely restrictive' borderline — the single load-bearing insight separating the work from the occupied gradient-alignment frontier must be explicit, and the pivot must be tied to a realistic regime.","fix_direction":"Add one-two sentences naming the single load-bearing insight that separates this from LearnAlign/GRACE: the alignment target is the student's HELD-OUT-DEFICIT direction (so value decays to ~0 as a skill is mastered, which a static answer-direction or success-rate score cannot capture), and note that this is exactly the regime the Mirage no-overlap result makes restrictive in practice (teacher pool distribution not covering the student's failure region), so the fixed-pool assumption is a genuine restriction, not a benign convention."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","issue":"C11 'binding constant dataset-dependent and uncontrollable' borderline — d_eff in the regret bound is a data-dependent constant that, if unestimable, makes the guarantee vacuous.","fix_direction":"State in core_mechanism that d_eff (the effective rank of the deficit subspace) is practitioner-estimable from the spectrum of the probe-gradient Gram matrix over the failed items, so the bound's binding constant is measurable rather than free; do NOT alter falsification_prediction or compute_budget."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added three explicit differentiation entries (GRACE, LearnAlign, ZPD Detector) pinning the delta as alignment to the held-out-deficit direction + generative acquire-to-gap pivot + regret certificate."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism_reasoning","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Named the single load-bearing separating insight (deficit-direction alignment target, value decays on mastery) and tied the pivoted fixed-pool assumption's restrictiveness to the Mirage no-overlap regime."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Stated that the regret bound's constant d_eff is practitioner-estimable from the probe-gradient Gram spectrum, making the guarantee non-vacuous; kill-switch fields untouched."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Recipes That Watch the Student: Per-Trace Marginal Value for Reasoning Distillation\n\n**Method.** Marginal-Value Readout (MVR)\n\n## Motivation\nToday's recipes for teaching a small model to reason work like this: you collect a big pile of worked-out solutions (called chain-of-thought, or CoT, traces) from a strong teacher model, then you pick a subset to train on. The catch is HOW the subset is chosen — every current method (s1, SynSelect, Phi-4-Mini-Reasoning) judges a single trace by looking only at the trace: is it correct, is it long, is it diverse, does a learned scorer like it? None of them ever check the one thing that actually matters: does training on THIS trace make THIS particular student better at what it currently gets wrong?\n\nThat distinction is the whole point. A trace's usefulness is not a fixed property of the trace — it depends on the student. A solution that teaches one model a brand-new skill is wasted on another model that already knows that skill. Because today's recipes hand out the same selected set to every student, they literally cannot tell apart a trace that fills a gap from a trace that just repeats something the student already does well. A recent analysis nicknamed 'Mirage' drives this home: whether CoT helps depends on how well the training traces overlap the kinds of questions you test on, not on how 'high quality' the traces look in isolation — so scoring traces by their own quality is optimizing the wrong target.\n\nWhy is this fixable now? Two reasons. First, we can measure a trace's effect on a student cheaply by only looking at a tiny slice of the model — the output head and the last layer's normalization parameters, about 0.3% of the weights — so one quick backward pass per trace is enough, and you can afford to score an entire 50,000-trace pool. Second, a very recent line of work (LearnAlign in 2025, GRACE and ZPD Detector in 2026) has shown that comparing gradients is a workable way to pick reasoning data — but all of them aim at the wrong target (agreeing with the correct answer, or a static success rate), leaving open the more useful target: the direction of what the student still FAILS.\n\nOnce this gap is closed, curation stops being a one-time filter and becomes a feedback loop: a recipe can prefer traces that teach a missing skill, skip traces that re-teach a mastered one, and stop collecting once the student's measured weaknesses are covered — turning the 'Mirage' observation from a diagnosis into something a recipe actively fixes.\n\n## Method\n### Deficit measurement\n*Turn the student's held-out failures into a single gradient direction $g_{def}$ on a tiny frozen lever.*\n\n1. Choose a tiny slice of the student to measure gradients on: only the output-head weights plus the final block's LayerNorm scale and shift parameters (about 0.3% of all weights). Build a fixed mask that keeps gradients on exactly those parameters and zeros everything else, so every trace is scored in the same small coordinate system. If the model shares its input and output word-embedding tables, make a separate copy of the output head first so scoring does not also move the embeddings.\n   - _Why_: Restricting to this tiny slice makes one trace's score a single cheap backward pass, so you can afford to score the whole pool instead of an expensive full-model influence estimate.\n2. Build a small held-out probe set of about 500 target-domain reasoning questions whose answers can be checked automatically, drawn from a source separate from both the training pool and the final test benchmark, and spread across the difficulty levels so it is not all one kind of problem. Run the student once per question with greedy (deterministic) decoding, then mark each question pass or fail by whether the final answer exactly matches the known correct answer. The failed set F is simply every question the student gets wrong.\n   - _Why_: The failed items F are exactly where the student is currently weak, so they define the deficit we want training to fix — and keeping the probe separate from the benchmark avoids cheating.\n3. For each failed question, take a known-correct worked solution (a reference solution if the dataset has one, otherwise a teacher-generated solution that reaches the right answer) and compute the student's training gradient on it, but only over the tiny lever from Step 1, using the usual next-token training loss with the question prompt excluded from the loss. Average these gradients across all failed questions (without rescaling each one first) to get a single direction, then store its unit-length version. This averaged direction captures what the student would need to move toward to fix what it currently gets wrong.\n\n*The student deficit direction $g_{def}$ is the mean lever-restricted SFT gradient of student s over the failed probe items F — the direction the student's own held-out failures demand.*\n$$ g_{\\mathrm{def}} = \\frac{1}{|F|}\\sum_{i \\in F} \\nabla_{\\theta_L}\\, \\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{SFT}}\\big(s,\\, x_i\\big) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Averaging the gradients of the student's own failures points in the direction training would need to move to fix what the student gets wrong — the load-bearing target everything else aligns to.\n\n### Per-trace value scoring\n*Score every candidate trace by how much its training gradient points along the student's deficit direction.*\n\n4. For each candidate training trace, compute the student's training gradient on it using exactly the same tiny-lever, prompt-masked next-token loss as in Step 3, measured against the student as it stands right now (not a stale earlier copy). Then score the trace by how much its gradient points along the stored deficit direction: take the dot product of the trace's gradient with the unit deficit direction and divide by the deficit direction's length plus a tiny constant. A high score means the trace helps fix what the student currently fails; a score near zero means it re-teaches something already mastered; a negative score means it pulls the wrong way.\n\n*The marginal-value readout v is the projection of a candidate trace's lever-restricted training gradient $g_{t}$ onto the unit deficit direction; it is positive when training on the trace pushes the lever the way the student's failures demand, near 0 when the trace re-demonstrates a mastered skill, and negative when it pulls away from the deficit.*\n$$ v(t; s, D_{\\mathrm{probe}}) = \\frac{\\langle g_t,\\, g_{\\mathrm{def}}\\rangle}{\\lVert g_{\\mathrm{def}}\\rVert + \\varepsilon} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: v is high for traces that push the student toward fixing its current failures, near 0 for traces re-teaching something already mastered, and negative for traces pulling the wrong way — a student-specific value a trace-only score cannot give.\n\n### Budgeted gap-targeted acquisition\n*Spend a fixed trace budget to maximize deficit coverage, selecting or generating traces and refreshing the deficit as the student learns.*\n\n5. Treat curation as spending a fixed budget of B traces to cover the student's measured weaknesses as much as possible. In each round, admit the highest-scoring not-yet-used traces (about B divided by the number of refresh rounds each time) for fine-tuning. In the generate-instead-of-select variant, ask the teacher model to write new traces aimed at the currently failed probe questions, score those by the same method, and keep the ones scoring above a moving floor (the lowest score you admitted last round, or the median positive score the first time). Fine-tune the student on the admitted traces with a standard optimizer (AdamW, learning rate around 1e-5 to 2e-5 for 1.5-3B models). The theory says spending the budget this way provably beats picking by a student-blind quality score when the pool does not already cover the student's failures. 【author decision: whether fine-tuning updates the whole model or only the small lever is a choice the authors must make — scoring always uses the frozen lever, but training can update everything (more power) or just the lever (more consistent with how value is measured).】\n\n*Acquisition maximizes cumulative realized deficit coverage — the sum of positive marginal value over an admitted set of at most B traces, scored against the student state $s_{t}$ at the time each trace is admitted.*\n$$ \\max_{|S| \\leq B}\\ \\sum_{t \\in S} \\max\\big(v(t; s_t,\\, D_{\\mathrm{probe}}),\\, 0\\big) \\tag{3} $$\n\n\n*Gap-targeted acquisition incurs sublinear regret against the clairvoyant best-B subset, where $d_{eff}$ is the effective rank of the deficit subspace (read off as the 90%-energy effective rank of the probe-gradient Gram spectrum), whereas fixed-pool top-k by a student-independent surrogate suffers regret linear in B in the no-overlap regime.*\n$$ \\mathrm{Regret}(B) = O\\!\\big(\\sqrt{B \\cdot d_{\\mathrm{eff}}}\\big) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Spending a limited budget on the traces that most reduce the student's measured weakness provably beats picking by a student-blind quality score when the pool doesn't already cover the student's failures.\n6. Every so often during training — once per admitted batch of traces, which is slower than the per-step weight updates — re-measure the student's weaknesses: re-run the pass/fail probe from Step 2 on the now-updated student, rebuild the failed set, and recompute the deficit direction from Step 3 on it. Use this fresh direction as-is, without blending it with old directions, so that as soon as the student masters a skill, traces for that skill drop to near-zero score and acquisition automatically moves on to what is still failing.\n   - _Why_: As the student masters a skill, traces for that skill drop to $v\\approx 0$ automatically, so acquisition keeps moving on to whatever the student still fails.\n\n### Mechanism falsification\n*Isolate the student-deficit coupling as the load-bearing cause of the gain via negative and positive controls.*\n\n7. Test whether the method actually works: pick a held-out reasoning benchmark and train three students on the same number of traces B — (A) chosen by our value score, (B) chosen by an s1-style trace-only quality/difficulty/diversity filter, and (C) chosen at random — keeping the number of traces, the number of training steps, and the learning-rate schedule identical so the only difference is which traces are used. Compare their accuracy (pass@1), and shrink B to check the gap widens at small budgets. As a negative control, swap the deficit direction for a fixed random direction (same size and length) that ignores the student and re-run; the gain should disappear back to baseline (B). As a positive control, admit traces using only the sign of the score (keep if positive); this should recover most of the gain, showing the deficit direction alone carries the signal.\n   - _Why_: If randomizing the deficit direction erases the gain, the improvement really came from matching the student's weaknesses; if sign-only keeps most of the gain, the deficit direction alone carries the value.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 会观察学生的数据配方：面向推理蒸馏的逐条轨迹边际价值\n\n**方法名称.** Marginal-Value Readout (MVR)\n\n## 研究动机\n如今教小模型学会推理的数据配方大致是这样：先从一个强大的教师模型那里采集一大堆写好的解题过程（称为 chain-of-thought，简称 CoT 轨迹），再从中挑一个子集来训练。问题出在「怎么挑」上——现有方法（s1、SynSelect、Phi-4-Mini-Reasoning）只盯着轨迹本身打分：对不对、长不长、够不够多样、一个学到的打分器喜不喜欢它。没有一个去检验真正要紧的那件事：在这一条轨迹上训练，能不能让这个特定的学生在它当前做错的地方变得更好。\n\n这个区别才是关键。一条轨迹有没有用并不是轨迹自身的固定属性，而是取决于学生。能教会一个模型全新技能的解法，对另一个早已掌握该技能的模型就是浪费。由于现有配方对所有学生发的是同一个选出来的集合，它们根本无法区分「填补缺口的轨迹」和「只是重复学生已会内容的轨迹」。一篇被昵称为 'Mirage' 的分析把这一点说透了：CoT 有没有用，取决于训练轨迹与测试问题的分布重叠程度，而不是轨迹孤立看上去有多「高质量」——所以按轨迹自身质量打分，是在优化错误的目标。\n\n为什么现在可以解决？两个原因。第一，我们可以只看模型的一小片——输出头加上最后一层的 LayerNorm 归一化参数，约占权重的 0.3%——就能廉价地测出一条轨迹对学生的影响，每条轨迹只需一次快速反向传播，因此可以负担得起给整个 5 万条的轨迹池打分。第二，非常近期的一批工作（2025 年的 LearnAlign，2026 年的 GRACE 和 ZPD Detector）已经表明，比较梯度是一种可行的推理数据挑选方式——但它们瞄准的目标都不对（与正确答案一致，或一个静态的成功率），从而留下了那个更有用的目标：学生仍然做错（deficit，缺陷）的方向。\n\n一旦补上这个缺口，数据筛选就不再是一次性过滤，而变成一个反馈回路：配方可以优先选取教授缺失技能的轨迹，跳过重复已掌握技能的轨迹，并在学生被测出的弱点被覆盖后停止采集——从而把 'Mirage' 的观察从一个诊断变成配方主动修复的东西。\n\n## 方法\n### 缺陷测量\n*在一个微小且冻结的杠杆上，把学生的留出失败转化为单一梯度方向 $g_{def}$。*\n\n1. 选学生模型的一小片来测梯度：只取输出头(output head)权重，加上最后一个 transformer block 的 LayerNorm 缩放与平移参数（约占全部权重的 0.3%）。构建一个固定的掩码(mask)，只在这些参数上保留梯度、其余全部置零，使每条轨迹都在同一个小坐标系里打分。如果模型把输入与输出词嵌入(word embedding)绑在一起，先复制一份独立的输出头，避免打分时把词嵌入表也一起移动。\n   - _为什么_: 限制在这一小片上，使得给一条轨迹打分只需一次廉价的反向传播，从而负担得起给整个池打分，而不必做昂贵的全模型影响力估计。\n2. 构建一个约 500 题的小型留出探针集(probe set)，题目是目标领域、答案可自动验证的推理题，来源与训练池和最终测试基准都分开，并按难度分散，避免全是同一类问题。对每道题用贪心(greedy，确定性)解码让学生作答一次，再按最终答案是否与已知正确答案完全匹配标注通过或失败。失败集合 F 就是学生答错的全部题目。\n   - _为什么_: 失败题 F 恰恰是学生当前薄弱之处，因此定义了我们希望训练去修复的缺陷——而让探针集与基准分开可以避免作弊。\n3. 对每道失败题，取一份已知正确的解题过程（数据集自带的参考解优先，否则取一条能得出正确答案的教师生成解），计算学生在它上面的训练梯度，但只在第 1 步定义的小杠杆(lever)范围内，用常规的下一词预测训练损失，并把问题提示词排除在损失之外。把所有失败题的这些梯度求平均（不预先各自缩放），得到一个方向，再存下其单位长度版本。这个平均方向刻画了学生为修复当前错误所需移动的方向。\n\n*学生缺陷方向 $g_{def}$ 是学生 s 在做错的探针题集合 F 上、限制在小杠杆 $\\theta _{L}$ 内的 SFT 梯度均值，代表学生自身留出失败所指向的方向。*\n$$ g_{\\mathrm{def}} = \\frac{1}{|F|}\\sum_{i \\in F} \\nabla_{\\theta_L}\\, \\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{SFT}}\\big(s,\\, x_i\\big) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 对学生自身失败题的梯度求平均，指向的正是修复学生做错之处所需的训练移动方向——这是其他一切要对齐的承重目标。\n\n### 逐条轨迹价值打分\n*按每条候选轨迹的训练梯度沿学生缺陷方向的程度来打分。*\n\n4. 对每条候选训练轨迹，用与第 3 步完全相同的小杠杆、提示词屏蔽的下一词损失，计算学生在它上面的训练梯度，并以当前这一刻的学生为准（不是过时的旧副本）。然后按该轨迹梯度沿存储的缺陷方向的程度打分：取轨迹梯度与单位缺陷方向的点积，再除以缺陷方向的长度加一个极小常数。分数高表示该轨迹有助于修复学生当前的失败；接近 0 表示重教已掌握内容；为负表示把方向拉反。\n\n*边际价值读数 v 是候选轨迹的杠杆受限训练梯度 $g_{t}$ 在单位缺陷方向上的投影：当训练该轨迹把杠杆推向学生失败所要求的方向时为正，当轨迹只是重演已掌握技能时接近 0，当它把学生拉离缺陷时为负。*\n$$ v(t; s, D_{\\mathrm{probe}}) = \\frac{\\langle g_t,\\, g_{\\mathrm{def}}\\rangle}{\\lVert g_{\\mathrm{def}}\\rVert + \\varepsilon} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: v 对推动学生修复当前失败的轨迹很高，对重复已掌握内容的轨迹接近 0，对方向相反的轨迹为负——这是只看轨迹的打分给不出的、与学生相关的价值。\n\n### 预算内的面向缺口采集\n*在固定轨迹预算下最大化缺陷覆盖，边选取或生成轨迹边随学生学习刷新缺陷方向。*\n\n5. 把数据筛选当成用固定 B 条轨迹的预算，尽量覆盖学生被测出的弱点。每一轮采纳当前得分最高、尚未使用的轨迹（每轮约 B 除以刷新轮数那么多）来做微调(fine-tune)。在「生成而非挑选」的变体里，让教师模型针对当前失败的探针题写新轨迹，用同样的方法打分，保留得分高于一个移动下限的（上一轮采纳过的最低分，或第一轮时的正分中位数）。用标准优化器(AdamW，1.5-3B 模型学习率约 1e-5 到 2e-5)在采纳的轨迹上微调学生。理论表明：当池子本身没覆盖学生的失败时，这样花预算可证明优于按学生无关的质量分挑选。【作者需决定：微调是更新整个模型还是只更新这个小杠杆，需由作者定夺——打分始终用冻结的杠杆，但训练既可更新全部参数(能力更强)，也可只更新杠杆(与价值的测量方式更一致)。】\n\n*采集过程最大化累计实现的缺陷覆盖：在至多 B 条被采纳轨迹上，按采纳时刻的学生状态 $s_{t}$ 计算的正边际价值之和。*\n$$ \\max_{|S| \\leq B}\\ \\sum_{t \\in S} \\max\\big(v(t; s_t,\\, D_{\\mathrm{probe}}),\\, 0\\big) \\tag{3} $$\n\n\n*面向缺口的采集相对于全知最优 B 子集只产生次线性遗憾，其中 $d_{eff}$ 是缺陷子空间的有效秩（取探针梯度 Gram 谱 90% 能量处的有效秩）；而在无重叠区间，按学生无关代理做固定池 top-k 的遗憾随 B 线性增长。*\n$$ \\mathrm{Regret}(B) = O\\!\\big(\\sqrt{B \\cdot d_{\\mathrm{eff}}}\\big) \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 当池子本身没覆盖学生的失败时，把有限预算花在最能减少学生已测弱点的轨迹上，可证明优于按学生无关的质量分挑选。\n6. 训练过程中每隔一段时间——每采纳一批轨迹做一次，这比逐步的权重更新要慢——重新测量学生的弱点：在更新后的学生上重跑第 2 步的通过/失败探针，重建失败集合，再据此用第 3 步重算缺陷方向。直接使用这个新方向，不与旧方向混合，这样一旦学生掌握某技能，该技能的轨迹得分立刻降到接近 0，采集便自动转向仍在失败的部分。\n   - _为什么_: 当学生掌握某技能后，该技能的轨迹会自动降到 $v\\approx 0$，于是采集会持续转向学生仍然做错的部分。\n\n### 机制证伪\n*通过负控制和正控制把学生-缺陷耦合分离出来，确认它是增益的承重原因。*\n\n7. 检验方法是否真的有效：选一个留出的推理基准，用相同数量 B 的轨迹训练三个学生——(A) 按我们的价值分挑选，(B) 按 s1 式只看轨迹的质量/难度/多样性过滤挑选，(C) 随机挑选——保持轨迹数量、训练步数、学习率(learning rate)时间表完全一致，使唯一差别在于用了哪些轨迹。比较它们的准确率(pass@1)，并缩小 B 验证小预算下差距会扩大。作为负控制(negative control)，把缺陷方向换成一个忽略学生、大小与长度相同的固定随机方向重跑；增益应消失、回落到基线 (B)。作为正控制(positive control)，仅按价值分的正负号采纳轨迹(为正即保留)；这应能恢复大部分增益，说明价值信号主要由缺陷方向承载。\n   - _为什么_: 若随机化缺陷方向就抹掉增益，说明改进确实来自匹配学生弱点；若只看符号就能保留大部分增益，说明价值信号主要由缺陷方向承载。\n\n"},{"id":"91","run_dir":"run_prompt91_moesparsity","index":91,"title":"Step-Heterogeneous Sparsity: Reasoning Tracks Where MoE Compute Lands, Not How Much","title_zh":"步骤异质稀疏性：推理准确率取决于 MoE 算力分配到哪里，而非分配了多少","method_name":"Step-Heterogeneous Sparsity diagnostic (SHS)","hook":"We show that for chain-of-thought reasoning the optimal Mixture-of-Experts sparsity is not a single number: at a fixed average active-parameter budget, reallocating that budget across reasoning steps by the model's own routing uncertainty raises reasoning accuracy, while the same budget spread uniformly does not. The reasoning-optimal sparsity studies measured the right thing at the wrong granularity — sparsity must be characterized per reasoning step, not as one global scalar.","anchor_pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","anchor_pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","domain_category":"LLM Pretraining, Architecture & Scaling","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved paper tests whether sparsity must be characterized as a single global scalar at all, rather than as a quantity that could legitimately differ across reasoning steps — the optimal-sparsity studies silently inherit from the dense-scaling-law ancestor the assumption that the compute-per-token knob is one constant chosen before training and measured only by end-of-trace accuracy, and never question whether a single number can be optimal when the trace contains steps of heterogeneous dif","pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by constructing an average-active-parameter-matched diagnostic: instances are run under three policies whose per-trace MEAN active experts are forced equal but whose ALLOCATION across reasoning steps differs (uniform / difficulty-aligned / difficulty-anti-aligned), so the headline result is the accuracy gap between allocation policies at identical mean compute — isolating allocation from the average-compute confound that the global-scalar studies leave conflated.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes the realized active-compute budget (the effective sparsity a token receives) vary with the inferential difficulty of the current reasoning step within a single chain-of-thought — every method that touches sparsity (scaling-law tuning, pruning, intra-expert harvesting) sets it uniformly across decode positions, so positions doing hard deductive work and positions doing easy continuation are allocated identical active compute.","pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","sub_pattern":"C12 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by swapping the fixed top-k gating primitive in every MoE block for a variable-k operator whose per-token k is set by a budget controller from the step-difficulty signal, keeping the router's learned which-experts scores untouched (preserving expert specialization) while making how-many an output rather than a frozen hyperparameter, under a hard per-trace average-k constraint so total compute is conserved.","is_anchor":false},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides an observable signal, computable online during decoding from the model's own internal state, that distinguishes a reasoning step which needs more active experts from one that does not — routing-analysis work reads expert activations only post-hoc as a task-identity fingerprint and never as a live difficulty estimate that could drive allocation.","pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by manufacturing a label-free per-token difficulty scalar d_t from the frozen model's own internal readouts — the top-k router-logit margin averaged over MoE layers and the next-token predictive entropy — calibrated against a held-out reference and used (with the backbone frozen) as the only lever that drives the variable-k controller, so no ground-truth difficulty labels are needed.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"Mixture-of-Experts language models; sparse conditional computation for multi-step reasoning","n_papers":39,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":26},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10},{"source":"openreview","n":2}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":12,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"MoE-Pruner: Pruning Mixture-of-Experts Large Language Model using the Hints from Its Router"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"MoE-LLaVA: Mixture of Experts for Large Vision-Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"LLaMA-MoE v2: Exploring Sparsity of LLaMA from Perspective of Mixture-of-Experts with Post-Training"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Efficient Expert Pruning for Sparse Mixture-of-Experts Language Models: Enhancing Performance and Reducing Inference Costs"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Understanding the Performance and Estimating the Cost of LLM Fine-Tuning"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Pre-gated MoE: An Algorithm-System Co-Design for Fast and Scalable Mixture-of-Expert Inference"}],"more":6},{"year":2025,"n":27,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Parameters vs FLOPs: Scaling Laws for Optimal Sparsity for Mixture-of-Experts Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Optimal Sparsity of Mixture-of-Experts Language Models for Reasoning Tasks"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"MegaScale-Infer: Efficient Mixture-of-Experts Model Serving with Disaggregated Expert Parallelism"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"BlockFFN: Towards End-Side Acceleration-Friendly Mixture-of-Experts with Chunk-Level Activation Sparsity"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"MegaScale-Infer: Serving Mixture-of-Experts at Scale with Disaggregated Expert Parallelism"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Mixture of Experts Made Intrinsically Interpretable"}],"more":21},{"year":2026,"n":12,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"},{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Generalizing GNNs with Tokenized Mixture of Experts"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Mixture-of-Experts Models in Vision: Routing, Optimization, and Generalization"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Task-Conditioned Routing Signatures in Sparse Mixture-of-Experts Transformers"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Uncovering Intra-expert Activation Sparsity for Efficient Mixture-of-Expert Model Execution"}],"more":6}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":14,"share":0.359},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":12,"share":0.308},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":8,"share":0.205},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":6,"share":0.154},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":5,"share":0.128},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":5,"share":0.128},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":4,"share":0.103},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":4,"share":0.103}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Recent scaling-law work on MoE sparsity (semanticscholar:2559ddde36d4a861ab54b881bbd15eb40918b159, semanticscholar:528f19cbaafe1e3590b16d8d1cbbd45814de0bc3) establishes that the sparsity level S = (E-K)/E that minimizes pretraining loss is NOT the one that maximizes downstream reasoning accuracy — reasoning improves with greater active FLOPs per token (lower effective sparsity) while memorization improves with more total parameters — yet in both studies S is treated as a single scalar set once at training time and applied identically to every token at inference. Meanwhile routing-analysis work shows that which experts fire is already strongly conditioned on the task and even the local semantic content of a prompt (arxiv:2603.11114v1, openalex:W4416033927), and intra-expert work shows a large fraction of an activated expert's neurons are unnecessary for most tokens (arxiv:2605.08575v1) — establishing that the per-token active-compute demand is highly non-uniform. The structural gap: the active-compute budget a reasoning trace receives is allocated by a fixed top-k rule blind to where in the chain-of-thought the model actually is, so positions doing hard inferential work (a deduction, an arithmetic carry, a constraint-satisfaction step) receive exactly the same number of active experts as positions doing easy continuation, and no current method makes the realized sparsity track the inferential difficulty of the current reasoning step.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:528f19cbaafe1e3590b16d8d1cbbd45814de0bc3","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Trains MoE families varying total/active params and top-k under fixed compute and shows reasoning-optimal sparsity differs from loss-optimal, summarized as the Active-FLOPs and tokens-per-parameter principles. Its residue: sparsity is characterized only as a single global scalar chosen before training and measured by end-of-trace accuracy; the paper neither resolves the optimal sparsity at the granularity of an individual reasoning step nor offers any mechanism to vary realized active compute within a trace, so the question of whether uniform per-token sparsity is even the right object is left untouched."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:2559ddde36d4a861ab54b881bbd15eb40918b159","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Fits an IsoFLOP surface L(N,S;C) and locates the loss-optimal (N*,S*) for a fixed compute budget, defining sparsity S=(E-K)/E. Residue: the entire analysis is keyed to pretraining loss on held-out text and the optimum is a constant across the sequence; it explicitly does not connect S to downstream reasoning capability nor allow S to depend on token-level inferential demand."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2603.11114v1","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Introduces routing signatures (per-layer expert-activation distributions concatenated into a fingerprint) and shows prompts from the same task category route similarly (within-category cosine 0.84 vs across 0.62, Cohen's d=1.44). Residue: the finding is purely correlational/observational — routing is read out as a diagnostic of task identity but never intervened upon to change how much compute a reasoning step receives, and the unit of analysis is the whole prompt, not the per-step difficulty inside one chain-of-thought."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2605.08575v1","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Reveals up to 90% intra-expert activation sparsity is free in off-the-shelf pretrained MoEs and exploits it to cut execution cost without accuracy loss. Residue: the sparsity it harvests is used solely as a static efficiency lever (zero out low-magnitude neurons uniformly); it never asks whether the spare capacity should instead be RE-ALLOCATED toward harder reasoning steps, nor ties the harvested headroom to reasoning-step difficulty."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"Mixture-of-Experts language models; sparse conditional computation for multi-step reasoning","venue":"ICLR / ICML / NeurIPS main track","time":"2026","data":["pretrained open MoE LLMs (OLMoE-1B-7B, DeepSeek-V2-Lite, Qwen3-MoE, GPT-OSS-20B)","reasoning benchmarks with step-structured traces (GSM8K, MATH, BBH, GPQA)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with access to open MoE checkpoints and reasoning eval harnesses","preference":"both","baseline":"static top-k MoE routing at the loss-optimal sparsity level; uniform sparsity across all decode positions","limitation":"sparsity (active-parameter / FLOPs-per-token budget) is fixed as a single global training-time hyperparameter and held uniform across every token of a reasoning trace, even though different reasoning steps differ in difficulty","contribution_type":"empirical_reveal","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object every leg reads from and writes to is the per-token realized active-compute allocation a(t) = number of active experts k_t at decode position t, summed over MoE layers; the paper's claim is that reasoning accuracy is a function of how a(t) is distributed across reasoning steps at fixed mean, not of the mean alone. LEG 3 (signal) manufactures the driver: for a frozen pretrained MoE LLM, at each decoded token t we read two internal quantities — the per-layer router-logit margin m_t = mean over MoE layers of (top-1 gate logit minus top-k-th gate logit), which is small when the router is uncertain which experts to fire, and the next-token predictive entropy H_t of the output distribution — and combine them into a difficulty scalar d_t = sigma(alpha * z(-m_t) + beta * z(H_t)), where z(.) is standardization using running mean/std estimated on a held-out calibration split of 2k reasoning traces, sigma is the logistic, and alpha,beta are two scalar hyperparameters (default alpha=beta=1) fixed by maximizing rank-correlation between d_t and per-token loss on the calibration split. LEG 1 (operator) substitutes the fixed top-k gate in every MoE block with a variable-k operator: a budget controller maps d_t to a target active-expert count k_t = clip(round(k_base + g*(d_t - d_bar)), k_min, k_max), where k_base is the model's native top-k, d_bar is the calibration-set mean difficulty, g is an integer gain (default g such that k ranges over [k_base-2, k_base+2]), and the router's learned gate scores are reused unchanged to pick WHICH k_t experts — only the count changes, so expert specialization (the property C12 must preserve) is untouched; a per-trace controller (a running Lagrange multiplier on a PI loop) adjusts a global offset so the realized trace-mean of k_t equals a target K_avg exactly, conserving total active compute. LEG 2 (diagnostic) is the confound-isolating instrument that makes the reveal: on reasoning benchmarks (GSM8K, MATH, BBH, GPQA) we run each trace under three allocation policies that are forced to the SAME per-trace mean K_avg — (i) uniform (k_t = K_avg everywhere, the baseline = current practice), (ii) difficulty-aligned (k_t from d_t as above, more experts at high-d_t steps), (iii) difficulty-anti-aligned (k_t from -d_t, more experts at easy steps) — and report the primary result as the accuracy divergence between (ii), (i), and (iii). Because mean active compute is held byte-identical across the three arms by the PI controller, any accuracy gap is attributable to ALLOCATION, not to spending more compute — exactly the confound the global-scalar scaling-law studies (semanticscholar:528f19..., which varies only a single global S and measures end-of-trace accuracy) cannot separate. The oracle ground truth is independent of the routing system: correctness is the benchmark's own verifiable answer key, and the difficulty axis is validated against an external per-step difficulty derived from a stronger held-out model's per-token loss, never from the evaluand's own consensus. The three legs share machinery tightly — leg 3's d_t is leg 1's controller input and leg 2's policy axis — so this is one coordinated instrument, not three modules.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The three gaps share one object (the per-step allocation a(t)) so they are realized as one pipeline rather than separate modules: the diagnostic (leg 2) is only meaningful if a controllable operator (leg 1) exists to vary allocation at fixed mean, and that operator is inert without a driving signal (leg 3) — collapsing them into independent contributions would let a reviewer read three stapled papers. I considered two alternative designs and rejected them: (a) training a learned difficulty predictor head end-to-end, rejected because it reintroduces the average-compute confound (the head adds parameters/compute and its gain could not be attributed to allocation) and regresses toward the Mixture-of-Depths loss-trained capacity gate flagged in method_lineage node c1; (b) varying network DEPTH per token (early exit) instead of expert WIDTH, rejected because it regresses onto the ACT/PonderNet collateral node c0 and does not touch the MoE sparsity object the user asked about. Keeping the backbone and router scores frozen and moving only the integer count k_t with a hard mean-k constraint is precisely what avoids both flagged nodes — it draws on a source (the inference-time count operator under a conservation constraint) that no lineage node occupies.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: take OLMoE-1B-7B (frozen), run GSM8K and MATH chains under the three allocation policies (uniform / difficulty-aligned / difficulty-anti-aligned), each constrained by the PI controller to the SAME per-trace mean active-expert count K_avg = k_base. If the candidate is right, exact-match reasoning accuracy increases under difficulty-aligned relative to uniform and decreases under difficulty-anti-aligned, producing a monotone accuracy ordering (aligned > uniform > anti-aligned) at byte-matched mean compute; if accuracy is flat across all three, the global-scalar view is correct and the candidate is falsified. The single named load-bearing variable is the per-token difficulty scalar d_t (built from router-logit margin + predictive entropy). Negative control: replace d_t with its within-trace position-permutation (identical value distribution and identical mean k_t, only the step-to-step alignment destroyed) feeding the same variable-k controller; the prediction is that REASONING ACCURACY collapses back to the uniform-policy baseline — the downstream task-outcome metric, not d_t's own value — because if d_t carries the mechanism, scrambling WHERE the extra experts land must remove the gain. Positive control: a controller driven by router-logit margin alone should recover most of the difficulty-aligned accuracy gain, identifying the margin as the dominant carrier.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:528f19cbaafe1e3590b16d8d1cbbd45814de0bc3","delta":"They establish that the loss-optimal global sparsity scalar differs from the reasoning-optimal global sparsity scalar and summarize it as Active-FLOPs and tokens-per-parameter principles measured by end-of-trace accuracy; we measure that at a FIXED average active budget, reasoning accuracy depends on the within-trace ALLOCATION of that budget across reasoning steps — a quantity their single-scalar, end-of-trace formulation cannot express or test."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:2559ddde36d4a861ab54b881bbd15eb40918b159","delta":"They fit an IsoFLOP surface L(N,S;C) for a constant sparsity S and locate one optimal (N*,S*); we construct an average-S-matched diagnostic showing the accuracy-relevant degree of freedom is the per-step variation of realized sparsity, a within-sequence axis absent from their constant-S surface."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2603.11114v1","delta":"They read routing signatures post-hoc and show routing correlates with task category (within- vs across-category cosine), purely observationally; we turn an online router-derived signal into an INTERVENTION that reallocates active experts across reasoning steps and measure the causal accuracy effect, which their correlational fingerprint never does."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2605.08575v1","delta":"They harvest free intra-expert neuron sparsity to cut cost uniformly across tokens; we ask the opposite question — whether spare capacity should be REALLOCATED toward hard reasoning steps at constant average sparsity — and supply the matched-mean diagnostic that measures it."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:528f19cbaafe1e3590b16d8d1cbbd45814de0bc3","what_step_was_missed":"They trained MoE families varying total params, active params, and top-k under fixed compute and read out end-of-trace reasoning accuracy, establishing reasoning needs more active compute than loss-optimal — but they never constructed the within-trace, average-active-parameter-matched comparison that holds total compute fixed while varying its per-step allocation, so the question of whether the reasoning gain comes from MORE mean compute or from WHERE that compute is spent was left undecided; that matched-mean allocation diagnostic (plus the online difficulty signal needed to instantiate the aligned policy) is the missing construction."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":308,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"No hard-floor rule fired: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict is borderline (not triggered — no Reject lesson is candidate_match:yes), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat is an addressable near-collision (DynaMoE), not exact-mechanism overlap. Two soft-judgment heuristics push to revise: (a) paper_pointed_threat.subsumption_argument names DynaMoE and addressable_via points at a specific candidate field (differentiation_from_lit) that must be added or the reveal risks reading as a re-derivation of DynaMoE's dynamic routing; (b) the C07 borderline lesson_quoted 'A label-free signal whose validity depends on model calibration silently fails on exactly the deep networks known to be poorly calibrated' hits a load-bearing property — d_t is the single named load-bearing variable in falsification_prediction — so the calibration-robustness of its entropy component should be hardened. recipe_application_check is fully applied, so no sub_pattern swap is warranted.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved paper tests whether sparsity must be characterized as a single global scalar at all, rather than as a quantity that could legitimately differ across reasoning steps — the optimal-sparsity studies silently inherit from the dense-scaling-law ancestor the assumption that the compute-per-token knob is one constant chosen before training and measured only by end-of-trace accuracy, and never question whether a single number can be optimal when the trace contains steps of heterogeneous difficulty.","main_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail most often when the constructed instrument isolates the confound only inside an artificial regime and never demonstrates the isolated signal transfers to real deployment, or falls into circularity by validating the diagnostic against the same definition/system population it was built to interrogate (using the evaluated models as their own oracle), or builds a confirmatory benchmark that re-derives an already-documented limitation surfacing nothing not knowable in advance.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A diagnostic that only re-confirms a shortcut already known in advance, surfacing no previously unmeasurable failure, is read as confirmatory rather than as a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The headline result — that at byte-matched mean active compute reasoning accuracy diverges by allocation policy (aligned > uniform > anti-aligned) — is a previously-unmeasured gap that the global-scalar formulation (almost_prior_paper_id 528f19) structurally cannot express, so it is not a re-confirmation of a known shortcut."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a synthetic-ground-truth instrument only on synthetic data, without demonstrating that the controlled finding transfers to real-world instances, leaves ecological validity unestablished and undermines the central claim.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The diagnostic runs directly on real reasoning benchmarks (GSM8K, MATH, BBH, GPQA) with real frozen MoE checkpoints, not on a synthetic-only regime, so there is no synthetic-to-real transfer gap to assert."},{"lesson_quoted":"Building the instrument around one contested definition of the target property means it cannot independently confirm that the definition is correct, and reviewers flag the resulting circularity.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The target property (reasoning correctness) is fixed by the benchmark's own verifiable answer keys and the difficulty axis is validated against an external stronger held-out model's per-token loss — neither is a contested self-defined property the instrument circularly assumes."},{"lesson_quoted":"Resting an unsupervised evaluation on the unverified premise that the systems under test can reliably judge one another stakes the entire method on an assumption that collapses under scrutiny.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The oracle is explicitly independent of the evaluand — benchmark answer keys for correctness and an external held-out model for the difficulty axis — so no self-judgment premise is load-bearing."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pairing a single-task or small-sample instrument with broad capability claims triggers a scope-mismatch rejection, and assembling retrieval or engineering blocks without an isolating scientific insight reads as application rather than research.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The claim is scoped to autoregressive CoT reasoning on the four tested benchmarks (core_mechanism_steps step 11) and the K_avg sweep over {k_base-1, k_base, k_base+1} demonstrates the effect across budgets rather than from a single point, so the scope is matched to what is probed."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes the realized active-compute budget (the effective sparsity a token receives) vary with the inferential difficulty of the current reasoning step within a single chain-of-thought — every method that touches sparsity (scaling-law tuning, pruning, intra-expert harvesting) sets it uniformly across decode positions, so positions doing hard deductive work and positions doing easy continuation are allocated identical active compute.","main_pattern":"architectural_operator_substitution","sub_pattern":"C12 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is a substitution that is mechanically valid but whose payoff is absent or unverified: authors swap the operator then prove preservation with a borrowed/trivial argument, or claim the property the new slot was supposed to buy without measuring it, or port an architecture from another domain and bolt on coupling without grounding it in the target problem; a diagnostic tell is validation on a proxy (throughput instead of accuracy, toy-scale data, no matched baseline).","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Proving the substitute operator preserves universal approximation via a trivial adaptation of known proofs, while never connecting that result to the practical advantage (e.g. sparsification) that motivated the swap, makes the contribution read as incremental.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate makes no expressivity-preservation proof claim at all; the preserved property (expert specialization, via reusing the learned which-experts gate scores) is connected directly to the motivating payoff (allocation-driven reasoning accuracy at matched mean), not left orthogonal."},{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming the rewired structure delivers a systems property — such as parallel forward/backward execution — that the underlying algorithm does not actually provide invites reviewers to falsify the headline claim head-on.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate claims no systems/throughput property; its headline is an accuracy effect under a conserved mean-compute constraint, and the PI controller is verified to hold mean k_t to |.|<0.05 expert (step 4), so the load-bearing constraint is measured not assumed."},{"lesson_quoted":"A training-time re-parameterization that yields only marginal accuracy gains at higher training cost, without strong matched-baseline comparisons, reads as added overhead rather than as an insight.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The operator swap is inference-only on a frozen backbone (no training cost) and is evaluated against a matched-mean uniform baseline that is current practice — exactly the matched-baseline the lesson demands."},{"lesson_quoted":"An elegant geometric reanalysis tool validated only on toy data, with no quantitative metric and an unclear delta over existing sensitivity measures, fails to show the substitution buys anything new.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Validation is on real reasoning benchmarks with exact-match accuracy as the quantitative metric, not toy data."},{"lesson_quoted":"Rewiring the dependency chain and reporting only throughput/speedup while omitting accuracy validation at scale leaves the essential preserved-property claim unverified.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The reported headline is accuracy (not speedup), with the preserved property (expert specialization) operationalized by reusing the unchanged gate scores."},{"lesson_quoted":"Porting a two-component architecture from a separate domain and bolting on a cross-pathway coupling, without a unifying contribution grounded in the target task, reads as an uncoordinated assembly rather than a substitution insight.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The variable-k operator is derived from first principles against the reasoning task (per-step difficulty heterogeneity), not ported from another domain; core_mechanism_reasoning explicitly couples it to the diagnostic and the signal as one coordinated instrument."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides an observable signal, computable online during decoding from the model's own internal state, that distinguishes a reasoning step which needs more active experts from one that does not — routing-analysis work reads expert activations only post-hoc as a task-identity fingerprint and never as a live difficulty estimate that could drive allocation.","main_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is a manufactured internal signal whose validity silently rests on an assumption that does not survive deployment (model calibration on miscalibrated nets, a stationary/known-finite shift set, or covert target-label use amounting to leakage), often co-occurring with recombining well-known components without one load-bearing mechanistic insight, compounded by thin validation on a single dataset family.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A label-free signal whose validity depends on model calibration silently fails on exactly the deep networks known to be poorly calibrated — validate a surrogate where its core assumption is weakest, not where it is convenient.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The difficulty scalar d_t uses next-token predictive entropy H_t, a component whose informativeness can be sensitive to calibration; the candidate mitigates this by combining it with a router-logit margin term and validating d_t against an external difficulty oracle (step 8) and by causal permutation/positive controls, but does not explicitly stress the entropy component under miscalibration."},{"lesson_quoted":"Recasting a continuous shift as a discrete, known, finite set of types indexed against a precomputed lookup table collapses the moment an unanticipated or mixed shift arrives.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"d_t is a continuous online scalar from internal readouts, not a discrete lookup over a fixed type set."},{"lesson_quoted":"Importing a generic continual-learning blending or interpolation technique into a new modality without identifying that modality's specific dynamics lever reads as recombination, not contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The signal is purpose-built for the MoE reasoning setting (router-logit margin is the modality-specific lever — the router's own uncertainty), not an imported generic blending technique."},{"lesson_quoted":"Reusing standard sequential machinery (chaining each step's posterior as the next prior) without a new stabilizer amplifies noise and looks derivative of prior adaptation work.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"No sequential posterior chaining is used; the per-trace PI budget controller serves as the explicit stabilizer (conserving mean k_t), matching the cluster's required stabilize-against-collapse move."},{"lesson_quoted":"A multi-branch or ensemble reweighting mechanism that overlaps with standard multi-task/mixture-of-experts ensembling must explicitly beat both the single-model and the standard-ensemble baselines, or the gain is credited to prior art.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The method is single-model with a within-model count change, not an ensemble reweighting, and the matched-mean uniform policy is the single-model baseline it is measured against."},{"lesson_quoted":"Using target or test-set information during adaptation invites a label-leakage objection that undermines the very source-free, label-free deployment setting the method claims.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"d_t is calibrated on a held-out 2k-trace split using teacher-forced per-token loss on gold solutions of that split (not the evaluation set), and correctness ground truth at test time comes from the benchmark answer keys, so no test-set information drives the signal."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"Two of three gap_closure entries (controlled_diagnostic_design / C02 and architectural_operator_substitution / C12) are fully clear with every documented Reject lesson marked candidate_match:no. The aggregate is driven to borderline by the self_supervised_signal_engineering / C07 entry, where the lesson_quoted 'A label-free signal whose validity depends on model calibration silently fails on exactly the deep networks known to be poorly calibrated' is borderline: d_t's predictive-entropy component is calibration-sensitive and the candidate validates the signal causally (external oracle + permutation control) but never stresses the entropy term where its calibration assumption is weakest."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved paper tests whether sparsity must be characterized as a single global scalar at all, rather than as a quantity that could legitimately differ across reasoning steps — the optimal-sparsity studies silently inherit from the dense-scaling-law ancestor the assumption that the compute-per-token knob is one constant chosen before training and measured only by end-of-trace accuracy, and never question whether a single number can be optimal when the trace contains steps of heterogeneous difficulty.","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Construct a controlled set of evaluation instances in which exactly one named confound is structurally blocked or independently varied, with an oracle independent of the system under test, then report the divergence between apparent and de-confounded performance as the primary result rather than an aggregate leaderboard score.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"LEG 2 (diagnostic) runs each trace under three allocation policies (uniform / difficulty-aligned / difficulty-anti-aligned) that a PI controller forces to byte-identical per-trace mean active-expert count K_avg, so the single confound (mean active compute) is held fixed while allocation is varied; the headline result is the accuracy divergence between the three arms (core_mechanism: 'any accuracy gap is attributable to ALLOCATION, not to spending more compute'), and the oracle is benchmark answer keys plus an external held-out model's per-token loss — independent of the evaluand. This is the C02 signature move performed exactly.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf makes the realized active-compute budget (the effective sparsity a token receives) vary with the inferential difficulty of the current reasoning step within a single chain-of-thought — every method that touches sparsity (scaling-law tuning, pruning, intra-expert harvesting) sets it uniformly across decode positions, so positions doing hard deductive work and positions doing easy continuation are allocated identical active compute.","sub_pattern":"C12 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Relocate or swap a structural slot rather than tuning weights — substitute the per-stage aggregation/representation primitive (e.g. fixed selection -> a different selection operator) — and accompany the swap with a measurement showing the essential property (expressivity, specialization, capacity) survives while a cost/expressivity property changes.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"LEG 1 substitutes the fixed top-k gate primitive in every MoE block with a variable-k operator k_t = clip(round(k_base + g*(d_t - d_bar)), k_min, k_max), reusing the learned gate scores unchanged to pick WHICH experts so expert specialization (the essential property C12 must preserve) survives while the count (cost/allocation property) changes; the per-trace PI controller conserves mean compute. This is a structural-slot operator swap with the preserved property named and operationalized, matching the C12 signature move. (Note: C12's card emphasizes a classical-theorem-grounded surrogate and a preservation proof; the candidate substitutes a measured/structural preservation argument instead of a theorem — adequate for an empirical_reveal deliverable but a weaker form of the cluster's distinctive theorem-anchoring.)","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides an observable signal, computable online during decoding from the model's own internal state, that distinguishes a reasoning step which needs more active experts from one that does not — routing-analysis work reads expert activations only post-hoc as a task-identity fingerprint and never as a live difficulty estimate that could drive allocation.","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Treat an already-trained model's own internal-state readouts (output entropy, gate/router statistics) as the manufactured supervisory signal, pair a mechanistic localization with a correction confined to a minimal lever while the backbone stays frozen, and bolt on an explicit stabilizer because a label-free internal signal invites a degenerate solution; the distinctive verbs are diagnose-localize, minimize-on-a-tiny-lever, and stabilize-against-collapse.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"LEG 3 manufactures d_t = sigma(alpha*z(-m_t) + beta*z(H_t)) from two internal readouts (router-logit margin m_t and next-token predictive entropy H_t) of a FROZEN backbone, drives only the integer expert count k_t (the minimal lever — no weight updates), and uses the per-trace PI mean-k controller as the explicit stabilizer against runaway allocation; step 8 causally validates the signal against an external difficulty oracle, matching C07's 'demonstrate the internal signal genuinely tracks the target rather than coincidentally correlating' move. The signature operation is present.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"All three entries instantiate their cited cluster's distinctive move in core_mechanism: C02's matched-mean confound-isolation (LEG 2), C12's structural-slot count operator swap with specialization preserved (LEG 1), and C07's frozen-backbone internal-readout signal on a minimal integer-count lever with a PI stabilizer (LEG 3). The C12 instantiation is the weakest — it substitutes a measured/structural preservation argument for the cluster's characteristic classical-theorem anchoring — but the structural-slot swap itself is genuinely performed, so it remains applied rather than bypassed."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["controlled_diagnostic_design","architectural_operator_substitution","self_supervised_signal_engineering"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored anti-patterns (audit_decomp_supervisor / audit_decomp_prior / audit_decomp_operator) require heterogeneous_decomposition as a composition member; the candidate's composition_set contains no heterogeneous_decomposition pattern, so no anti-pattern matches at the mechanism level."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:5d85fe8844a83f00a49119c47f286337307c7a06","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"DynaMoE already relaxes fixed Top-K so that the number of active experts per token varies with input complexity and theoretically analyzes the expressivity gains of dynamic routing — which overlaps the candidate's LEG-1 variable-k operator and its premise that uniform top-k is not optimal. If DynaMoE's variable-k-by-complexity result were taken to already establish that allocation (not mean compute) carries the gain, the candidate's headline reveal would lose its claim to novelty. But DynaMoE does NOT subsume the candidate: (1) its objective and reported finding are parameter/compute EFFICIENCY (superior accuracy at lower compute, task- and scale-dependent optimal schedules), i.e. it deliberately changes mean active compute, whereas the candidate's entire contribution is the average-active-parameter-MATCHED diagnostic that holds mean compute byte-identical and isolates allocation as the carrier — the one comparison DynaMoE never runs; (2) DynaMoE validates on MNIST / Fashion-MNIST / CIFAR-10 / generic LM, never on chain-of-thought reasoning benchmarks, so it makes no claim about per-reasoning-step difficulty heterogeneity; (3) DynaMoE varies k inside training as an architecture-design framework, while the candidate operates on a frozen pretrained backbone with the router scores untouched and adds a permutation negative control proving the gain is positional-alignment-driven. The candidate's claim therefore stands, but DynaMoE is the most serious near-collision and must be differentiated head-on.","addressable_via":"Add a differentiation_from_lit entry for DynaMoE that explicitly contrasts the matched-mean allocation diagnostic (allocation isolated at fixed mean compute, on frozen reasoning models) against DynaMoE's efficiency-axis variable-k (which changes mean compute and is validated on vision/LM, not reasoning), so the reveal is not read as a re-derivation of DynaMoE's dynamic routing."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat — DynaMoE (semanticscholar:5d85fe8844a83f00a49119c47f286337307c7a06) is a variable-k-by-input-complexity MoE framework absent from the current differentiation list, the most serious near-collision.","fix_direction":"Add a differentiation_from_lit entry for DynaMoE stating the delta precisely: DynaMoE varies k for parameter EFFICIENCY (changing mean compute, optimal schedules task/scale-dependent, validated on MNIST/CIFAR/LM) and analyzes expressivity bounds in-training; the candidate instead holds mean active compute byte-matched and measures whether per-reasoning-step ALLOCATION is the carrier on frozen reasoning models with a positional-permutation negative control — a matched-mean reasoning diagnostic DynaMoE never runs."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism / core_mechanism_steps","issue":"gap_closure_reject_check C07 borderline — the predictive-entropy component H_t of the load-bearing signal d_t rests on a calibration assumption that is weakest on the deep nets where it is most relied upon, and is not stress-tested there.","fix_direction":"Add a calibration-robustness check to the signal validation: confirm d_t's rank-correlation with the external difficulty oracle is preserved under a margin-only ablation (already partially present as the positive control) AND report whether a temperature-calibrated H_t changes d_t's oracle correlation, so the entropy term's contribution is validated where its calibration premise is weakest rather than assumed; if H_t is calibration-fragile, scope the load-bearing signal to the router-logit margin m_t."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added a differentiation_from_lit entry for DynaMoE (semanticscholar:5d85fe8844a83f00a49119c47f286337307c7a06) contrasting its efficiency-axis variable-k (changes mean compute; expressivity bounds; validated on MNIST/CIFAR/LM, in-training) against the candidate's matched-mean reasoning allocation diagnostic on frozen models with a positional-permutation control."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism_steps","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added a calibration-robustness sub-step to the signal validation (step 8) that stress-tests the predictive-entropy component H_t under temperature calibration where its assumption is weakest, with a fallback to a margin-only load-bearing signal if H_t proves calibration-fragile."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Step-Heterogeneous Sparsity: Reasoning Tracks Where MoE Compute Lands, Not How Much\n\n**Method.** Step-Heterogeneous Sparsity diagnostic (SHS)\n\n## Motivation\nModern large language models often use a Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) design: instead of running the whole network on every word, a small router picks a fixed handful of specialist sub-networks ('experts') to run for each token. How many experts you run per token is the model's 'sparsity', and it is normally set as one number, the same for every word the model produces. Recent studies found something important — the sparsity that makes a model best at its basic training objective is NOT the sparsity that makes it best at multi-step reasoning; reasoning wants more experts firing per token. But those studies still treated sparsity as a single global number, measured only by whether the final answer was right.\n\nHere is the question they could not ask: when reasoning improves with more experts, is that because the model spent more compute ON AVERAGE, or because the extra compute landed on the HARD steps of the reasoning chain? A single global number can't tell these apart, because it spends the same amount everywhere by definition. Yet other evidence shows different reasoning steps genuinely need different amounts of work — some steps are easy continuation, others are a hard deduction or an arithmetic carry.\n\nThis idea reframes MoE reasoning sparsity from 'one number for the whole trace' to 'an allocation across the steps of the trace.' It builds the one missing measuring instrument: a comparison that keeps the AVERAGE number of experts exactly the same, but changes WHERE within the reasoning chain those experts are spent. The reasoning-optimal-sparsity study measured the right thing at the wrong zoom level; this measures it at the level where the two explanations can finally be separated.\n\nThe timing works because open MoE models now expose their router internals (so we can read the model's own uncertainty live, with no retraining), the reasoning-vs-loss sparsity result is fresh enough to make the question urgent, and separate findings show per-token compute demand really is uneven with spare capacity to move around. If the gap closes, the field's object of study shifts from a global sparsity scalar to a per-step allocation policy, and a whole class of cheap, training-free, router-driven interventions becomes available.\n\n## Method\n### Difficulty signal\n*Manufacture a label-free per-step difficulty estimate from the frozen model's own router and output internals.*\n\n1. Load a pretrained Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) model without changing any weights, and attach hooks at every expert-gating block and at the output layer. At each generated token, compute two numbers: the router-logit margin $m_{t}$ — the gap between the highest gate score and the k-th gate score, averaged over all MoE layers, which is small when the router is unsure which experts to pick — and the predictive entropy $H_{t}$ — how spread-out the model's next-token probability distribution is (natural-log entropy). Save both as per-token streams.\n   - _Why_: These are quantities the model already computes; reading them costs nothing and needs no labels.\n2. Turn the two readouts into one per-token difficulty score $d_{t}.$ First standardize each readout (subtract the mean, divide by the standard deviation) using statistics collected once over a held-out set of 2,000 reasoning traces. Then pick the two mixing weights by trying a small grid of values and keeping the pair whose resulting $d_{t}$ best lines up (by rank) with where the model actually has high per-token loss on the gold solution; if nothing beats the default, use equal weights. The result is a difficulty score you can compute live while the model generates.\n\n*The per-token difficulty scalar $d_{t}$ is a logistic combination of the standardized negative router-logit margin $-m_{t}$ (small margin = router uncertain) and standardized predictive entropy $H_{t},$ with weights $\\alpha , \\beta $ fit on a held-out calibration split.*\n$$ d_t = \\sigma\\!\\left(\\alpha\\, z(-m_t) + \\beta\\, z(H_t)\\right) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A step where the router is unsure and the next-token guess is spread out is exactly a step the model finds hard, so this score is a free difficulty estimate.\n\n### Variable-k allocator\n*Make the per-token active-expert count track difficulty while holding average compute byte-identical.*\n\n3. Change the gate in every MoE block so that instead of always firing the same fixed number of experts $k_{base},$ it fires a count $k_{t}$ that rises on hard steps and falls on easy ones (here, ranging from two below to two above $k_{base}).$ Crucially, keep using the model's own existing scores to rank and pick WHICH experts — you only move the cutoff for how many — and renormalize their weights exactly as the original router would. Each expert's learned specialty is therefore untouched.\n\n*The variable-k operator maps difficulty $d_{t}$ to an integer active-expert count $k_{t}$ by shifting the native top-k count $k_{base}$ up or down with gain g around the calibration-set mean difficulty d-bar, clipped to $[k_{min}, k_{max}].$*\n$$ k_t = \\mathrm{clip}\\!\\left(\\mathrm{round}\\!\\left(k_{\\mathrm{base}} + g\\,(d_t - \\bar d)\\right),\\, k_{\\min},\\, k_{\\max}\\right) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Only the number of experts changes, not their identities, so we isolate 'how much compute' from 'what the experts do'.\n4. Add a small controller that watches the running average number of active experts over the trace and nudges a global offset every step (with a moderate update rate) so that average drifts toward a chosen target. At the end of each trace, if the average is still off by more than a twentieth of one expert, make a tiny deterministic fix by adjusting the borderline tokens (those closest to the difficulty midpoint) up or down until the average matches exactly.\n\n*A per-trace proportional-integral controller adjusts a global offset $\\lambda $ each step so the running mean of $k_{t}$ tracks the target $K_{avg},$ conserving total active compute across allocation policies.*\n$$ \\lambda \\leftarrow \\lambda + \\eta\\,\\Big(\\tfrac{1}{t}\\textstyle\\sum_{\\tau \\le t} k_\\tau - K_{\\mathrm{avg}}\\Big), \\qquad k_t \\leftarrow k_t - \\lambda \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: If the average compute is held identical across experiments, any accuracy difference must come from WHERE the compute went, not from spending more.\n\n### Matched-mean diagnostic\n*Compare allocation policies at equal mean compute (with permutation control) to isolate allocation as the reasoning carrier.*\n\n5. On reasoning benchmarks (GSM8K, MATH, BBH, GPQA), run each trace three ways at the same average budget — spread evenly, concentrated on the hard steps, and concentrated on the easy steps — and report the accuracy gaps as the main result. Then run a control that keeps the same difficulty values but scrambles which step each attaches to, and a second control driven by the router-confidence number alone. Separately, sanity-check the difficulty score by comparing it against a stronger outside model's per-token loss on the same traces (lining up the two models' tokens by re-tokenizing the generated text), and re-check that the entropy part of the score still helps after adjusting for the model's confidence calibration; if it does not, fall back to using only the router-confidence number. 【author decision: whether the outside reference is one larger model or several combined, and exactly which 'stronger but independent' model family to use — this trades reliability against independence and is the authors' call.】\n   - _Why_: If accuracy rises only when extra experts land on the genuinely hard steps and the gain vanishes when you scramble where they land, then allocation — not average compute — is what matters.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 步骤异质稀疏性：推理准确率取决于 MoE 算力分配到哪里，而非分配了多少\n\n**方法名称.** Step-Heterogeneous Sparsity diagnostic (SHS)\n\n## 研究动机\n现代大语言模型常用 Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) 结构：不是每个词都跑整张网络，而是由一个小的 router 为每个 token 挑选固定数量的专家子网络('experts')来运行。每个 token 跑多少个专家，就是模型的'稀疏度'，通常被设成一个数，对所有词一视同仁。最近的研究发现了一件重要的事——让模型在基础训练目标上最优的稀疏度，并不是让它在多步推理上最优的稀疏度；推理需要每个 token 激活更多专家。但这些研究仍然把稀疏度当作一个全局的数，而且只用最终答案对不对来衡量。\n\n它们无法追问的问题是：当推理因为激活更多专家而变好时，到底是因为'平均'花了更多算力，还是因为这些额外算力落在了推理链中'更难'的步骤上？一个全局的数无法区分这两者，因为按定义它在每个位置花的量都一样。然而其他证据显示，不同推理步骤确实需要不同的算力——有些步骤只是简单续写，有些则是一次困难的推导或一次进位运算。\n\n这个想法把 MoE 推理稀疏度从'整条轨迹一个数'重新理解为'在轨迹各步骤之间的一种分配'。它构建了唯一缺失的测量工具：一个让'平均'激活专家数保持完全相同、但改变这些专家在推理链中'花在哪里'的对照实验。reasoning-optimal-sparsity 研究测对了东西，却用错了缩放层级；这里在能真正区分两种解释的层级上去测它。\n\n时机成熟，是因为开源 MoE 模型现在会暴露 router 内部状态（于是我们可以在线读取模型自身的不确定性，无需重新训练），reasoning-vs-loss 稀疏度结果足够新使这个问题紧迫，且另有发现表明每个 token 的算力需求确实不均、存在可挪用的余量。若这一空白被填上，该领域的研究对象将从一个全局稀疏度标量转向一种按步分配策略，并由此带来一整类廉价、免训练、由 router 驱动的干预手段。\n\n## 方法\n### 难度信号\n*从冻结模型自身的 router 与输出内部状态中，免标注地造出一个按步难度估计。*\n\n1. 加载一个预训练好的 Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) 模型，不改动任何权重，并在每个专家门控(gating)块和输出层挂上 hook。在每个生成 token 处计算两个数：router-logit margin $m_{t}——$最高门控分数与第 k 高门控分数之差、在所有 MoE 层上取平均，当 router 不确定该选哪些专家时它会很小；以及预测熵 predictive entropy $H_{t}——$模型对下一个 token 的概率分布有多分散（自然对数熵）。把二者都存成逐 token 的序列。\n   - _为什么_: 这些都是模型本就会算出的量，读取它们零成本、也不需要任何标注。\n2. 把这两个读数合成一个每 token 的难度分 $d_{t}$。先对每个读数做标准化（减均值、除以标准差），所用统计量在一个留出的 2,000 条推理轨迹集合上一次性算好。再用一个小网格逐一尝试两个混合权重，保留使 $d_{t}$ 与模型在标准答案上真实的每 token cross-entropy loss 高低（按秩）对得最齐的那一组；若没有比默认更好的，就用相等权重。最终得到一个可在生成过程中在线计算的难度分。\n\n*每个 token 的难度标量 $d_{t}$ 由标准化后的负 router-logit margin $-m_{t}$（margin 越小说明 router 越不确定）与标准化预测熵 $H_{t}$ 经 logistic 组合得到，权重 $\\alpha $、$\\beta $ 在留出校准集上拟合。*\n$$ d_t = \\sigma\\!\\left(\\alpha\\, z(-m_t) + \\beta\\, z(H_t)\\right) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: router 不确定、且下一 token 猜测很分散的那一步，正是模型觉得难的一步，所以这个分数就是免费的难度估计。\n\n### 可变 k 分配器\n*让每 token 激活专家数随难度变化，同时使平均算力逐字节相同。*\n\n3. 改写每个 MoE 块里的 gate：不再总是激活固定数量 $k_{base}$ 个专家，而是激活一个数量 $k_{t}——$难步骤上调、易步骤下调（这里在 $k_{base}$ 上下各浮动 2）。关键是仍用模型自身已有的打分来排序并挑选'哪些'专家，你只移动'选多少'的截断位置，并像原始 router 那样对它们的权重重新归一化。因此每个专家学到的专长保持不变。\n\n*可变 k 算子将难度 $d_{t}$ 映射为整数激活专家数 $k_{t}$：以增益 g 让原生 top-k 数 $k_{base}$ 围绕校准集平均难度 d-bar 上下浮动，并裁剪到 $[k_{min}, k_{max}]$ 区间。*\n$$ k_t = \\mathrm{clip}\\!\\left(\\mathrm{round}\\!\\left(k_{\\mathrm{base}} + g\\,(d_t - \\bar d)\\right),\\, k_{\\min},\\, k_{\\max}\\right) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 只改专家'数量'、不改专家'身份'，于是把'花多少算力'与'专家做什么'这两件事分离开。\n4. 加一个小控制器，盯住整条轨迹上激活专家数的滑动平均，并每步（以中等更新速率）微调一个全局偏移量，使该平均向选定目标靠拢。在每条轨迹结束时，如果平均仍偏离超过二十分之一个专家，就做一个极小的确定性修正：对处于边界的 token（最接近难度中点的那些）上调或下调，直到平均精确吻合。\n\n*每条轨迹的比例-积分(PI)控制器每步调整全局偏移 $\\lambda $，使 $k_{t}$ 的滑动均值逼近目标 $K_{avg}$，从而在不同分配策略间守恒总激活算力。*\n$$ \\lambda \\leftarrow \\lambda + \\eta\\,\\Big(\\tfrac{1}{t}\\textstyle\\sum_{\\tau \\le t} k_\\tau - K_{\\mathrm{avg}}\\Big), \\qquad k_t \\leftarrow k_t - \\lambda \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 若各实验间'平均算力'完全相同，那么任何准确率差异就只能来自算力'花在哪里'，而不是花得更多。\n\n### 等均值诊断\n*在平均算力相等的条件下比较各分配策略（含打乱位置对照），以分离出分配才是推理增益的来源。*\n\n5. 在推理基准(GSM8K、MATH、BBH、GPQA)上，把每条轨迹在相同平均预算下跑三种方式——均匀铺开、集中到难步骤、集中到易步骤——并以这些准确率差距作为主结果。再跑一个对照：保持同样的难度数值但打乱它们各自对应到哪一步；以及第二个仅由 router 置信度数值驱动的对照。另外，用一个更强的外部模型在同样轨迹上的每 token loss 来校验难度分（通过对生成文本重新分词，把两个模型的 token 对齐），并在对模型的置信度校准(calibration)做调整后再次确认难度分中的熵部分是否仍然有帮助；若无帮助，则退回到只用 router 置信度数值。【作者需决定：外部参照是用单个更大模型还是多个组合，以及具体用哪一个'更强但独立'的模型家族——这是在可靠性与独立性之间的取舍，须由作者拍板。】\n   - _为什么_: 若只有当额外专家落在真正困难的步骤上时准确率才上升，且一旦打乱'落在哪里'增益就消失，那么起作用的就是分配，而非平均算力。\n\n"},{"id":"92","run_dir":"run_prompt92_optimistictask","index":92,"title":"Misspecification-Aware Optimistic Task Inference for Behavior Foundation Models","title_zh":"面向行为基础模型的失配感知乐观任务推断","method_name":"Misspecification-Aware OpTI (MA-OpTI)","hook":"Behavior foundation models perform test-time task inference entirely inside the frozen pretrained feature span, so when the deployed reward leaves that span their optimism criterion keeps shrinking confidently toward a task it can never fit and the recovered policy degrades silently with MORE interaction, not less. We substitute the in-span-only belief operator with one that carries an online out-of-span reward-residual channel, giving optimistic task inference a quantity that tells 'keep querying, the task is identifiable' apart from 'the reward is out of model, fall back' — and we predict the regret curve under out-of-span rewards bends DOWNWARD where current methods bend up.","anchor_pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","anchor_pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","domain_category":"Reinforcement Learning","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces, during test-time task inference, a quantity that separates reducible (epistemic) uncertainty about which in-span task embedding is correct from the irreducible mismatch of NO in-span embedding explaining the observed rewards; consequently active inference cannot tell 'keep querying, the task is identifiable' apart from 'stop trusting the BFM span, the reward is out of model' and degrades silently under misspecification.","pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","sub_pattern":"C12 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by swapping the structural slot occupied by the test-time belief-and-acquisition operator: the original operator maps (history of states, rewards) -> posterior over z in the frozen span plus an in-span optimism bonus; the surrogate operator maps the same history -> a TWO-channel object (the same in-span posterior PLUS an online estimate rho_t of reward variance unexplained by the best in-span fit), and the acquisition rule is re-derived to inflate exploration when rho_t is small (task identifiable, keep querying within span) and trigger a span-exit fallback when rho_t persists above a learned threshold (no in-span z fits). The substitution provably preserves OpTI-BFM's no-regret property on genuinely in-span tasks (rho_t -> 0 collapses the operator to the original) while unlocking a halt/fallback regime the original slot structurally cannot reach.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions the shared assumption that the optimism/uncertainty signal driving active test-time inference must be computed entirely within the FROZEN pretrained feature span — every frontier method (OpTI-BFM, ReLA, FB humanoid) inherits from the USF/FB ancestor the premise that the representable-task manifold is fixed at deployment, and none tests whether the test-time exploration objective should instead account for reward structure the frozen basis cannot carry.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","how_closed":"Audit half (framing): the load-bearing identifiability precondition every leaf inherits is 'the deployed task is recoverable as a point z in the frozen feature span', so task inference is a well-posed in-span regression; we show this precondition is load-bearing (when it fails, the in-span posterior is provably mis-centered and the optimism bonus is uninformative) and pivot it to a structural substitute condition — the projection RESIDUAL of observed rewards onto the span carries the identifying signal of out-of-span structure, and a sufficiency claim states when in-span recovery is valid (the recovered policy is near-optimal iff the residual norm is below a derived task-dependent bound). Companion controlled_diagnostic_design deliverable: a confound-isolating BFM-deployment suite where the target reward is dialed from fully-in-span to provably-out-of-span at fixed querying budget, attributing recovered-value collapse to span-misspecification rather than to insufficient querying or feature underfit — the empirical separation that the audit's sufficiency claim predicts.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"zero-shot / unsupervised reinforcement learning with behavior foundation models (BFMs); test-time task inference","n_papers":49,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":25},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":19,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Finer Behavioral Foundation Models via Auto-Regressive Features and Advantage Weighting"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Random Policy Enables In-Context Reinforcement Learning within Trust Horizons"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"SAD: State-Action Distillation for In-Context Reinforcement Learning under Random Policies"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"OpenFMNav: Towards Open-Set Zero-Shot Object Navigation via Vision-Language Foundation Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Scaling Robot Policy Learning via Zero-Shot Labeling with Foundation Models"},{"source":"openalex","title":"When large language models meet personalization: perspectives of challenges and opportunities"}],"more":13},{"year":2025,"n":19,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Zero-Shot Whole-Body Humanoid Control via Behavioral Foundation Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Optimistic Task Inference for Behavior Foundation Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Task Tokens: A Flexible Approach to Adapting Behavior Foundation Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"TD-JEPA: Latent-predictive Representations for Zero-Shot Reinforcement Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Towards Robust Zero-Shot Reinforcement Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Tackling the Zero-Shot Reinforcement Learning Loss Directly"}],"more":13},{"year":2026,"n":11,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Value Bonuses using Ensemble Errors for Exploration in Reinforcement Learning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"GIRL: Generative Imagination Reinforcement Learning via Information-Theoretic Hallucination Control"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Controlling Fish Schools via Reinforcement Learning of Virtual Fish Movement"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Maximum Entropy Behavior Exploration for Sim2Real Zero-Shot Reinforcement Learning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Group Distributionally Robust Optimization-Driven Reinforcement Learning for LLM Reasoning"}],"more":5}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":11,"share":0.224},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":11,"share":0.224},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":8,"share":0.163},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":4,"share":0.082},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":3,"share":0.061},{"pattern_id":"targeted_self_supervised_objective","pattern_name":"Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective","count":3,"share":0.061},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":3,"share":0.061},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":3,"share":0.061}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"For USF/FB-based behavior foundation models, test-time task inference reduces to estimating a task embedding z whose induced policy is near-optimal, and the entire estimation operates inside the span of the FIXED pretrained feature basis: OpTI-BFM (semanticscholar:5d349b172143ba45337405c5d5d1c0738c5b0649) frames this as a linear bandit over z, using an optimism bonus derived from the assumed linear relationship between the frozen features phi and the unknown reward to actively pick z and minimize regret, while ReLA/fast-adaptation (openalex:W4417251308) bolts a residual critic onto z_r to correct projection error only after committing to a near-optimal z. The shared failure is that both treat the reward-to-feature relationship as exactly linear in the frozen basis and treat the belief over z as the sole carrier of task uncertainty: when the true reward has a component OUTSIDE the feature span (model misspecification), the optimism/regret machinery has no quantity that registers 'the task I can represent does not explain the rewards I am seeing', so active data collection keeps reducing posterior variance over an embedding that can never fit the task, and the agent confidently converges to a wrong z. Neither paper produces a signal that separates epistemic uncertainty about WHICH in-span task is correct from the irreducible error of NO in-span task fitting, so under misspecification the recovered policy degrades silently with more interaction rather than less.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:5d349b172143ba45337405c5d5d1c0738c5b0649","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"OpTI-BFM casts test-time task inference as a linear bandit over the task embedding z, exploiting the assumed-linear features-to-reward map to build an optimism criterion that actively selects z and bounds cumulative regret over deployment episodes. Its belief, bonus, and regret guarantee all live entirely inside the frozen feature span and assume every interaction returns a reward label and a single stationary in-span task — it carries no quantity that detects reward variance unexplained by ANY in-span z (misspecification), so when the true reward leaves the span the optimism term keeps shrinking confidently toward a mis-fit embedding instead of flagging that no embedding fits."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4417251308","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"ReLA/fast-adaptation initializes at the zero-shot inferred z_r and runs an off-policy actor-critic with a residual critic that corrects the reward-projection error left by the linear z fit, gradually moving the policy off the BFM manifold. The residual correction is applied only AFTER a z is committed and is driven by gradient descent on reward-labeled transitions, so it spends label budget reactively after a bad in-span commit rather than deciding test-time queries by how much reward they leave unexplained; it has no active-inference criterion and no explicit account of out-of-span task error during the inference phase itself."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:85a4c2cd9a8e428fc5a65775813fefb57bd19fac","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"The whole-body humanoid BFM scales FB-with-conditional-policy-regularization to high-dimensional control from unlabeled mocap, demonstrating zero-shot policy retrieval at humanoid scale. It still recovers a task by projecting a provided reward onto the frozen feature span (standard linear task inference) and does not address how to actively elicit the task under a label budget or how to behave when the target reward is not representable in the learned span."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"zero-shot / unsupervised reinforcement learning with behavior foundation models (BFMs); test-time task inference","venue":"ICLR / NeurIPS / ICML (core ML)","time":"2026 submission cycle","data":["reward-free offline trajectory datasets for BFM pretraining (e.g. ExORL, DMC, humanoid mocap)","small online test-time interaction budget with sparse/expensive reward labels"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"RL / representation learning","preference":"both","baseline":"OpTI-BFM (Optimistic Task Inference for BFMs, semanticscholar:5d349b...) and ReLA/fast-adaptation (openalex:W4417251308)","limitation":"test-time task inference for BFMs is data-inefficient and brittle: identifying the task embedding z from reward observations consumes labels and assumes the reward sits inside the fixed pretrained feature span","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"Shared audit lens (the coherence thread): both legs interrogate ONE site — the frozen-span belief that carries all test-time task uncertainty in USF/FB behavior foundation models. ANCHOR LEG (operator substitution). At deployment a USF-based BFM gives a frozen feature map phi: S -> R^d, finite-horizon successor-feature estimates psi^{pi_z} for each task embedding z, and the standard task-inference rule z = argmin over the span of the squared error between observed returns and <psi, z>. OpTI-BFM wraps this in a linear bandit: a Gaussian posterior over z (mean mu_t, covariance Sigma_t built from the design matrix of executed psi's) and a UCB-style acquisition z_{t+1} = argmax_z [<mu_t, z> + beta * sqrt(z^T Sigma_t z)]. We substitute this single-channel belief-and-acquisition operator with a two-channel surrogate. Channel 1 is the unchanged in-span posterior (mu_t, Sigma_t). Channel 2 is rho_t, the LOAD-BEARING VARIABLE: an online running estimate of the residual reward variance unexplained by ANY in-span z, computed as rho_t = (1/t) * sum over observed episodes k of (G_hat_k - <psi^{pi_{z_k}}(s_{kH}), z_hat_k>)^2 minus the predicted in-span estimator variance (the irreducible regression noise floor sigma0^2 supplied by the BFM's own held-out reward-prediction error during pretraining); rho_t is clamped at 0 and is by construction the part of return-prediction error NOT attributable to finite-sample uncertainty in z. The acquisition rule is re-derived as z_{t+1} = argmax_z [<mu_t, z> + beta*sqrt(z^T Sigma_t z) * g(rho_t)] with g a monotone increasing gate (g(0)=1, saturating), AND a span-exit trigger: when rho_t stays above a learned threshold tau for w consecutive episodes, the operator stops curating z and hands control to a residual-recovery routine (e.g. ReLA-style off-manifold actor-critic) seeded at the current best z. The essential preservation property: when the task is genuinely in-span, rho_t -> sigma0^2-floor -> 0, g(rho_t) -> 1, the trigger never fires, and the operator is byte-for-byte OpTI-BFM, so its no-regret guarantee is inherited; the unlocked capability is the fallback regime, which the original single-channel slot cannot express because it has no quantity that is non-zero only under out-of-span reward. SIBLING LEG (assumption audit + diagnostic companion). The audit names the inherited identifiability precondition ('deployed task recoverable as a span point') and pivots it: the residual rho_t IS the structural substitute condition of a different kind (a geometric signature of the reward relative to the span) that carries the out-of-span identifying information the in-span-linearity assumption silently supplied. We state and prove a sufficiency claim: the recovered policy's value gap is bounded by c1*sqrt(z-estimation-error) + c2*sqrt(true out-of-span residual norm), so below a derived residual bound in-span recovery is near-optimal and above it no amount of querying helps — exactly the quantity rho_t estimates. The companion ships the confound-isolating suite that varies a single axis (out-of-span reward fraction) at fixed label budget, so a measured value collapse is attributable to misspecification, validating the sufficiency claim empirically. The two legs share the residual object: the anchor uses rho_t to drive acquisition/fallback, the audit uses the same residual norm as the pivoted identifying condition and as the diagnostic's varied axis. Quantitatively, OpTI-BFM reports cumulative regret R_n growing sublinearly in episodes n for in-span tasks (their Sec 3 analysis); our claim is regime-distinguished: we match that sublinear R_n when out-of-span fraction = 0, and bound the ASYMPTOTIC regret by the irreducible out-of-span value gap (a constant our rho_t estimates) rather than letting it grow as current methods do when they keep committing to a mis-fit z.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules: the residual rho_t is simultaneously the new acquisition/fallback channel (anchor) and the pivoted identifying condition + diagnostic axis (sibling), so a single object closes both — evidence is that the sufficiency bound's residual term and the operator's channel-2 estimator are the same quantity, just used to drive a decision vs. to state a guarantee. (b) Alternatives considered and rejected: (1) treating misspecification as a known constant epsilon and importing an agnostic-linear-bandit regret bound (lineage node c1) — rejected as a regression because c1 takes epsilon as a given input and never ESTIMATES out-of-span mass online or acts on it, whereas the whole point is an online-estimated, decision-driving channel; the avoided node is recorded here. (2) Re-learning / unfreezing the feature span at test time (a fine-tuning move) — rejected because it abandons the zero-shot/compute-efficiency premise of BFMs and would make the comparison to OpTI-BFM unfair; we keep the span frozen and only add a residual channel. (3) A pure posterior-sampling (PSRL, node c0) recast — rejected because classical PSRL also collapses silently under model-class misspecification and provides no out-of-span signal.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on a frozen FB/USF BFM in DMC (walker, cheetah) and one humanoid task, evaluate test-time task inference across an out-of-span reward sweep alpha in {0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1.0} at a fixed reward-label budget of n episodes, with arms {ours, OpTI-BFM, ReLA, FB zero-shot}, measuring cumulative regret R_n and final recovered-policy value gap. If the candidate works, at alpha=0 our regret matches OpTI-BFM (no penalty when well-specified), and as alpha grows our final value gap and R_n stay bounded (curve flattens) while OpTI-BFM's value gap WIDENS with more episodes (its regret curve bends upward past a point) — i.e. the value-gap-vs-alpha curves separate with a sign-flip in the slope of regret-vs-episodes for alpha>0. The load-bearing variable is rho_t, the online out-of-span residual estimate. Negative control: oracle-replace rho_t with 0 throughout (force the operator to believe every task is in-span, disabling the gate and the span-exit trigger) — this should drive our recovered-policy value gap at alpha>0 back to OpTI-BFM's (the downstream task-outcome metric returns to baseline), confirming rho_t is the mechanism rather than incidental tuning; crucially the control's predicted effect is on the value gap, not on rho_t's own value. Positive control: a stripped model that ignores the gated acquisition and uses ONLY rho_t to fire the span-exit fallback should recover most of the value-gap improvement at high alpha, identifying the residual-triggered fallback as the dominant constructive ingredient.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:5d349b172143ba45337405c5d5d1c0738c5b0649","delta":"OpTI-BFM builds its optimism bonus and regret guarantee entirely from the in-span linear-bandit posterior (mu_t, Sigma_t) and assumes the reward lies in the feature span; we construct an additional online estimator rho_t of out-of-span reward residual that they do not compute, re-derive the acquisition rule to gate exploration and trigger a span-exit fallback on it, and prove an asymptotic-regret bound governed by the irreducible out-of-span value gap rather than their in-span sublinear regret that silently fails under misspecification."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4417251308","delta":"ReLA applies a residual critic AFTER committing to the zero-shot z_r to correct projection error by reactive gradient descent; we instead use the residual as a forward-looking decision signal during inference (gating acquisition and deciding WHEN to exit the span), and supply the sufficiency bound and threshold that tell the agent when in-span recovery is provably hopeless, which ReLA's post-commit correction never states."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:85a4c2cd9a8e428fc5a65775813fefb57bd19fac","delta":"The humanoid BFM recovers tasks by projecting a provided reward onto the frozen span and demonstrates scale, but never measures or acts on reward mass outside the span; we add the out-of-span residual channel and the controlled out-of-span sweep that quantifies recovered-value collapse as a function of misspecification."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:492762bef1d470275df2a55b96fe7b745fc62d60","delta":"Finer-BFM enriches the feature basis so more reward structure is in-span, addressing WHAT the span can represent; we leave the span fixed and address detection of and response to reward that is out-of-span at deployment for any given frozen span, an orthogonal and composable contribution."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:5d349b172143ba45337405c5d5d1c0738c5b0649","what_step_was_missed":"OpTI-BFM constructed the in-span linear-bandit belief (posterior mu_t, Sigma_t) and the optimism bonus from the assumed feature-reward linearity, but to make optimistic task inference robust it would have needed to construct a second estimator that isolates return-prediction error NOT attributable to finite-sample z uncertainty (the out-of-span residual rho_t, defined against the BFM's own in-span noise floor sigma0^2) and a sufficiency bound relating that residual to the recovered-policy value gap — that residual estimator and bound are exactly what convert their silently-failing in-span regret into a misspecification-aware criterion, and they are absent from their construction."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":246,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"No hard-floor rule fired: gap_closure_reject_check has no entry with candidate_match=yes (worst is borderline), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat against OpTI-BFM is partial-overlap (strictly-added mechanism), not exact. The decision is revise rather than advance because recipe_application_check.entries[1].verdict=borderline hits a load-bearing structural property: the C05 audit leg performs the assumption pivot but stops short of the cluster's terminal move (recovery re-proven up to a named ambiguity/equivalence class), stating only a value-gap sufficiency bound, and the same gap surfaces in gap_closure_reject_check.entries[1] lesson 'Advertising an identifiability or consistency property while the proof omits the decisive object'. Sharpening the sibling leg's sufficiency claim into an explicit in-span-task recovery statement up to the span-projection equivalence class (with rho_t / R_oos as the out-of-span witness) closes the borderline without touching the kill-switch fields or the anchor mechanism.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces, during test-time task inference, a quantity that separates reducible (epistemic) uncertainty about which in-span task embedding is correct from the irreducible mismatch of NO in-span embedding explaining the observed rewards; consequently active inference cannot tell 'keep querying, the task is identifiable' apart from 'stop trusting the BFM span, the reward is out of model' and degrades silently under misspecification.","main_pattern":"architectural_operator_substitution","sub_pattern":"C12 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is a substitution that is mechanically valid but whose payoff is absent or unverified: authors swap the operator then claim a property the new slot was supposed to buy without measuring it, or validate on a proxy (throughput instead of accuracy, toy scale, no matched baseline for the specific property claimed).","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Proving the substitute operator preserves universal approximation via a trivial adaptation of known proofs, while never connecting that result to the practical advantage (e.g. sparsification) that motivated the swap, makes the contribution read as incremental.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The preservation claim (no-regret collapses to OpTI-BFM as rho_t->0) is explicitly tied to the practical advantage that motivated the swap — the span-exit fallback that bounds asymptotic regret under misspecification — not left as a disconnected proof."},{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming the rewired structure delivers a systems property — such as parallel forward/backward execution — that the underlying algorithm does not actually provide invites reviewers to falsify the headline claim head-on.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The claimed unlocked capability (detect-and-fall-back under out-of-span reward) is exactly what the falsification_prediction measures via the value-gap-vs-alpha curve and the rho_t negative control, so it is offered for head-on falsification rather than asserted."},{"lesson_quoted":"A training-time re-parameterization that yields only marginal accuracy gains at higher training cost, without strong matched-baseline comparisons, reads as added overhead rather than as an insight.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"This is a test-time operator (no retraining of the frozen BFM) and the candidate carries matched baselines (OpTI-BFM, ReLA, FB zero-shot) across the misspecification sweep, with the gain claimed only where alpha>0, not a marginal across-the-board number."},{"lesson_quoted":"Rewiring the dependency chain and reporting only throughput/speedup while omitting accuracy validation at scale leaves the essential preserved-property claim unverified.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Primary metrics are recovered-policy value gap and cumulative regret (task-outcome quantities), not throughput; the preserved-property claim (no-regret at alpha=0) is the alpha=0 anchor of the same sweep."},{"lesson_quoted":"Porting a two-component architecture from a separate domain and bolting on a cross-pathway coupling, without a unifying contribution grounded in the target task, reads as an uncoordinated assembly rather than a substitution insight.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The span-exit fallback reuses a ReLA-style off-manifold actor-critic, so a reviewer could read the fallback as a bolted-on second component; mitigated because the residual rho_t (a target-task quantity) is what gates the handoff and the noise-floor decomposition grounds it in the BFM itself, but the coupling between channel-2 gating and the fallback should be shown to be load-bearing rather than two stacked systems."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions the shared assumption that the optimism/uncertainty signal driving active test-time inference must be computed entirely within the FROZEN pretrained feature span — every frontier method (OpTI-BFM, ReLA, FB humanoid) inherits from the USF/FB ancestor the premise that the representable-task manifold is fixed at deployment, and none tests whether the test-time exploration objective should instead account for reward structure the frozen basis cannot carry.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The signature failure is an identifiability claim that outruns its proof: the pivoted assumption was not actually load-bearing (a straightforward union of two frameworks), or recovery/'consistency' is asserted while the decisive object is never established, or structural constraints are imposed without proving they are SUFFICIENT for recovery.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Stacking two established frameworks and re-proving identifiability of the union reads as incremental unless the pivoted assumption was genuinely load-bearing and the union admits a regime neither framework could reach alone.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The pivoted assumption (task recoverable as a span point) is shown load-bearing — when it fails the in-span posterior is provably mis-centered — and the regime admitted (out-of-span deployment reward) is one neither OpTI-BFM nor ReLA reaches; not a cosmetic union."},{"lesson_quoted":"Advertising an identifiability or 'consistency' property while the proof omits the decisive object — never proving latent identifiability, or excluding part of the model from the guarantee — collapses the contribution the moment a reviewer checks the theorem.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The sibling states a sufficiency bound (value_gap <= c1*sqrt(z-error)+c2*sqrt(R_oos)) and claims rho_t consistently estimates R_oos, but as written the 'recovery' object is a value-gap bound rather than an explicit identifiability statement of the in-span task up to the span-projection equivalence class — the decisive object C05 demands (recovery up to a named ambiguity class) is implied but not stated, so a reviewer could say the consistency claim outruns the stated theorem."},{"lesson_quoted":"Imposing structural constraints to claim interpretability or disentanglement without proving those constraints are sufficient for recovery leaves the result indistinguishable from a post-hoc heuristic.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The structural substitute condition (residual norm below a derived bound) is exactly what the sufficiency claim proves governs near-optimal recovery, and the operator enforces it via the threshold tau, so it is not a decorative constraint."},{"lesson_quoted":"Proving identifiability conditions the algorithm neither enforces nor verifies creates a theory-practice disconnect that undermines both the soundness and the significance of the claim.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The algorithm verifies the condition online (rho_t vs tau) and acts on it (span-exit), so the proven condition is the one the system enforces — the theory-practice link is closed."},{"lesson_quoted":"Errors in the dependency or conditional-independence bookkeeping (mislabeling an independence, opening a collider) void the central theorem even when the empirical numbers look reasonable.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"No latent-variable conditional-independence graph is invoked; the bound is a regression/approximation argument over the frozen span, so collider-style bookkeeping errors do not apply."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The audit (C05) entry drove the aggregate: its lesson 'Advertising an identifiability or consistency property while the proof omits the decisive object' is borderline because the sibling ships a value-gap sufficiency bound and a consistency-of-rho_t claim but does not explicitly name the recovery/ambiguity-class object C05's terminal claim demands. The C12 anchor entry is borderline only on the 'uncoordinated assembly' lesson (the reused fallback component), which is a surfacing concern, not a trigger."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces, during test-time task inference, a quantity that separates reducible (epistemic) uncertainty about which in-span task embedding is correct from the irreducible mismatch of NO in-span embedding explaining the observed rewards; consequently active inference cannot tell 'keep querying, the task is identifiable' apart from 'stop trusting the BFM span, the reward is out of model' and degrades silently under misspecification.","sub_pattern":"C12 (Substitute the Operator or Representation)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Relocate or swap a structural slot rather than tuning weights (substitute the per-stage aggregation/representation primitive or rewire routing), anchor the substitute to a classical construction, and accompany the move with a proof or measurement that the essential property (expressivity, gradient flow, capacity equivalence) survives while a cost/expressivity property changes — and show the surrogate unlocks something the original slot structurally cannot reach.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism swaps the structural slot occupied by the single-channel belief-and-acquisition operator for a two-channel surrogate (in-span posterior + out-of-span residual rho_t), proves the essential no-regret property survives (rho_t->0 collapses it byte-for-byte to OpTI-BFM), and demonstrates the unlocked capability the original slot structurally forbids (a span-exit fallback regime, since the original carries no quantity non-zero only under out-of-span reward). This is the C12 signature move applied to a test-time inference operator rather than a deep-network forward block, but the relocate-slot + preserve-property + unlock-capability structure is present.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf questions the shared assumption that the optimism/uncertainty signal driving active test-time inference must be computed entirely within the FROZEN pretrained feature span — every frontier method (OpTI-BFM, ReLA, FB humanoid) inherits from the USF/FB ancestor the premise that the representable-task manifold is fixed at deployment, and none tests whether the test-time exploration objective should instead account for reward structure the frozen basis cannot carry.","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Take an existing identifiability/recovery result and pivot the assumption it requires, trading a distributional assumption (here: reward is linear in the frozen span) for a structural/geometric one (a feasible-region or curvature signature that survives), then re-prove recovery of the hidden structure up to the field's standard ambiguity class.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism performs the pivot — names the inherited identifiability precondition (task recoverable as a span point), shows it load-bearing, and substitutes the geometric condition that the reward residual onto the span carries the out-of-span identifying signal. It then states a sufficiency bound. The cluster's terminal artifact — recovery re-proven up to a NAMED ambiguity/equivalence class — is implied (the in-span task is recovered up to the span-projection class, with the residual as the out-of-span witness) but core_mechanism states a value-gap bound instead of naming that class, so the distinctive C05 closing move is partially executed.","verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The C12 anchor entry is applied (relocate-slot + preserve no-regret + unlock fallback are all present). The C05 audit entry is borderline: the assumption pivot is genuinely performed, but the cluster's signature terminal move — re-prove recovery up to a named ambiguity class — is only implied via a value-gap sufficiency bound, not stated as an identifiability/equivalence-class claim."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["architectural_operator_substitution","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as a component; the candidate's composition set is {architectural_operator_substitution, assumption_audit_and_pivot}, which matches none of them."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:5d349b172143ba45337405c5d5d1c0738c5b0649","threat_source":"lit_table","subsumption_argument":"OpTI-BFM is the exact-topic prior: it already casts test-time task inference for BFMs as an online optimism problem over z and bounds regret. The candidate stands or falls on whether it produces something OpTI-BFM's construction does not: OpTI-BFM's belief, bonus, and regret guarantee live entirely inside the frozen span and assume the reward is in-span, so it has no estimator of out-of-span reward mass and no behavior change under misspecification. The candidate's load-bearing additions — the online out-of-span residual rho_t (defined against the BFM's in-span noise floor sigma0^2), the rho_t-gated acquisition, the span-exit fallback trigger, and a regret bound governed by the irreducible out-of-span value gap — are constructions absent from OpTI-BFM, so the overlap is partial (same problem framing, strictly added mechanism) rather than exact-mechanism. The candidate is therefore not subsumed, but its differentiation hinges entirely on the misspecification regime being real and on the residual estimator being sound.","addressable_via":"Not exact-mechanism overlap; the differentiation is already carried by the rho_t channel and span-exit, and is further protected by making the out-of-span sweep (alpha) the headline experiment so the regime where the candidate departs from OpTI-BFM is the one measured — no field needs to change to dodge subsumption."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"gap_closure[1].how_closed","issue":"recipe_application_check.entries[1]=borderline and gap_closure_reject_check.entries[1] lesson on consistency-claims-without-the-decisive-object: the C05 pivot is performed but the terminal recovery-up-to-ambiguity-class artifact is not named.","fix_direction":"Rewrite the audit half of how_closed so the sufficiency claim is stated as an explicit identifiability result: 'the in-span task embedding is recovered up to the span-projection equivalence class (any two rewards with identical projection onto span(phi) are indistinguishable and yield the same optimal in-span policy), and the residual norm R_oos — estimated online by rho_t — is the witness of the out-of-span coset that no in-span querying can resolve.' Keep the value-gap bound but frame it as the consequence of this recovery statement, so the decisive recovery object C05 demands is named."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","issue":"Same C05 borderline plus the C12 'uncoordinated assembly' borderline: core_mechanism should (a) name the span-projection equivalence class as the recovery object, and (b) make explicit that the rho_t gate is what couples the in-span operator to the fallback so the fallback is not a bolted-on second system.","fix_direction":"In the SIBLING-LEG paragraph, add one sentence naming the span-projection equivalence class recovered and stating rho_t is a consistent estimator of the out-of-span coset norm R_oos (not merely of residual variance). In the ANCHOR-LEG paragraph, add one clause that the single quantity rho_t both gates acquisition and triggers the fallback, so the operator and fallback are one coupled controller keyed on rho_t rather than two stacked systems. Do NOT alter falsification_prediction or compute_budget."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"gap_closure[1].how_closed","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Rewrote the audit half of how_closed so the sufficiency claim is stated as an explicit identifiability result — the in-span task is recovered up to the span-projection equivalence class, with the residual norm R_oos (estimated online by rho_t) named as the witness of the unresolvable out-of-span coset — and the value-gap bound is framed as the consequence of that recovery statement."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"In the SIBLING-LEG paragraph, named the span-projection equivalence class as the recovery object and stated rho_t is a consistent estimator of the out-of-span coset norm R_oos (not merely residual variance); in the ANCHOR-LEG paragraph, added a clause that the single quantity rho_t both gates acquisition and triggers the fallback, making the operator and fallback one coupled controller keyed on rho_t rather than two stacked systems. falsification_prediction and compute_budget untouched."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Misspecification-Aware Optimistic Task Inference for Behavior Foundation Models\n\n**Method.** Misspecification-Aware OpTI (MA-OpTI)\n\n## Motivation\nBehavior foundation models (BFMs) are big policies pretrained without any reward, so that later, when you hand them a new task, they can produce a good policy by picking a small task code z out of a frozen menu of skills (the 'feature span'). The current best way to pick z is OpTI-BFM (Optimistic Task Inference for BFMs): it treats the choice of z like a slot machine and adds an 'optimism' nudge so it actively tries the z's most likely to be good, getting better with each interaction. The trouble is that this whole process happens inside the frozen menu and assumes the true reward is something the menu can express. If the real task is partly OUTSIDE what the frozen features can represent, OpTI-BFM has no way to notice: it keeps getting more confident about a code z that can never actually fit the task, so the policy you get out quietly gets WORSE the more you interact, not better. We fix this by adding one extra number, $rho_{t},$ computed online: the part of the prediction error that no menu item could ever explain, measured against the model's own built-in noise level $sigma0^{2}.$ When $rho_{t}$ is near zero, the task is in the menu and we behave exactly like OpTI-BFM (so we keep its guarantees). When $rho_{t}$ stays high, the same number tells us 'no z fits — stop trusting the menu' and hands off to a fallback that learns off-menu. Prior work stopped short for structural reasons: OpTI-BFM (arXiv 2025-10) builds everything from the in-menu math and left no slot for an out-of-menu signal; ReLA (arXiv 2025-04) only corrects errors AFTER committing to a code, never using the leftover error to decide whether to keep querying; and the humanoid-scale BFM (ICLR 2025) just projects the reward onto the frozen menu and never checks whether that projection is even adequate. Closing this gap gives test-time task inference a built-in self-check — a single number that says whether more interaction can still help or whether the task is simply out of model — and turns both OpTI-BFM and ReLA into the special case where that number is zero.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n\n1. Build the standard Optimistic Task Inference for BFMs (OpTI-BFM) loop exactly, both as the comparison method and as the behavior we fall back to when the task is in-menu. Keep a Gaussian belief over the task code z: $a mean mu_{t}$ and a covariance $Sigma_{t}$ that grows out of which skill-feature directions you have already tried. Each episode, pick the next z that maximizes $<mu_{t},$ z> + beta $* sqrt(z^{T} Sigma_{t}$ z) (best guess plus an optimism bonus for under-explored directions), run that policy for one episode, observe the return, and update the belief. Record the chosen z's and the running regret.\n   - _Why_: This is the method we must match exactly when the task is in the menu, so it's both the baseline and the behavior we fall back to.\n\n### Out-of-span residual channel\n*Constructs and maintains $rho_{t},$ the online estimate of reward mass no in-span task can explain, against the model's noise floor.*\n\n2. When you pretrain the behavior foundation model (BFM), also measure how much prediction error is unavoidable even when the task IS expressible by the frozen feature menu. Hold out some (state, reward) examples, fit the best linear reward predictor over the frozen features, and on a separate held-out fold record its average squared error as a single number $sigma0^{2}.$ Save $sigma0^{2}$ in the model file. This is the model's normal 'noise floor' — the yardstick everything later is compared against.\n   - _Why_: You need a baseline for normal prediction error so that later you don't mistake ordinary noise for a task that's out of the menu.\n3. Add a second running quantity. After each episode, compute how far the predicted return was from the actual return, square it, and keep a smoothed average (exponential moving average, weight 0.05 on the newest value). From that average subtract two things: the noise floor $sigma0^{2}$ from step 2 (When you pretrain the $behavior\\dots ),$ and the part of error that comes from still being unsure about z (computed as $\\psi ^{T} Sigma_{t} \\psi $ for the feature vector $\\psi $ you just executed). Clamp the result at 0 to get $rho_{t}.$ What's left after removing ordinary noise and z-uncertainty is exactly the error that no menu item could ever explain — the out-of-menu signal, and a consistent estimate of how much reward sits outside the menu.\n\n*The load-bearing variable $\\rho _{t}:$ the running mean squared return-prediction residual, minus the pretraining in-span noise floor $\\sigma _{0}^{2}$ and minus the finite-sample predictive variance induced by $\\Sigma _{t},$ clamped at 0 — by construction the part of prediction error attributable to NO in-span embedding, i.e. an estimate of the out-of-span coset norm $R_{oos}.$*\n$$ \\rho_t = \\max\\Big(0,\\; \\tfrac{1}{t}\\textstyle\\sum_{k\\le t}\\big(\\hat G_k - \\langle \\psi^{\\pi_{z_k}}(s_{kH}), \\hat z_k\\rangle\\big)^2 - \\sigma_0^2 - \\mathrm{tr}(\\text{Var}_{\\Sigma_t})\\Big) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: What's left over after removing normal noise and 'I'm-still-learning-z' uncertainty is exactly the error that no menu item can explain — the out-of-menu signal.\n\n### rho_t-keyed controller\n*One scalar both gates optimistic exploration and triggers the span-exit fallback, coupling operator and fallback into a single controller.*\n\n4. Change the z-selection rule so the optimism bonus is multiplied by a gate $g(rho_{t}).$ Use $g(x)=1+lambda*tanh(x/sigma0^{2}):$ when $rho_{t}$ is 0 the gate is exactly 1 and the rule is identical to OpTI-BFM (so we keep its guarantees); as $rho_{t}$ grows, the gate grows smoothly up to 1+lambda, pushing exploration harder. Dividing by $sigma0^{2}$ means the gate reacts to out-of-menu signal measured against the model's own noise level. Start with lambda=1 and tune it later.\n\n*The gated acquisition rule: the in-span UCB objective (posterior $mean \\mu _{t}$ plus an optimism bonus scaled by the posterior covariance $\\Sigma _{t})$ is multiplied by a monotone gate $g(\\rho _{t})$ that equals 1 when no out-of-span mass is detected, so the operator reduces to OpTI-BFM exactly when $\\rho _{t}$ is 0.*\n$$ z_{t+1} = \\arg\\max_{z}\\; \\langle \\mu_t, z\\rangle + \\beta\\,\\sqrt{z^{\\top}\\Sigma_t z}\\;\\, g(\\rho_t),\\qquad g(0)=1 \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: When nothing is out of menu the method is identical to OpTI-BFM; when out-of-menu mass appears, exploration responds to it instead of ignoring it.\n5. Use the SAME $rho_{t}$ to decide when to give up on the menu. Keep a threshold tau and require $rho_{t}$ to stay above it for w episodes in a row (default 5) to avoid reacting to noise. When that happens, hand control to a fallback off-menu actor-critic that starts from the current best policy (the BFM policy for $z = mu_{t})$ and then learns directly from reward-labeled transitions using a standard off-policy method (such as TD3 or SAC). Set tau in step 7 (Build a controlled test suite $on\\dots )$ so that genuinely in-menu tasks almost never cross it (the 95th percentile of $rho_{t}$ on in-menu runs). Because one number both tunes exploration (step 4 (Change the z-selection rule so $the\\dots ))$ and triggers this fallback, the switch is smooth rather than a separate bolted-on system.\n   - _Why_: The SAME number that tunes exploration also decides when to give up on the menu entirely, so the switch to the fallback is smooth and not a separate bolted-on system.\n\n### Recovery theory\n*Names the span-projection equivalence class and proves the value-gap sufficiency bound $rho_{t}$ verifies online.*\n\n6. Prove two things. First, that inferring the task inside the menu can only pin it down up to a 'span-projection equivalence class': any two rewards that look identical after projecting onto the menu are indistinguishable to in-menu querying and share the same best in-menu policy — and $R_{oos},$ the size of the leftover out-of-menu part, is precisely what querying can never resolve. Second, as a consequence, the recovered policy's value gap is at most c1*sqrt(z-error) $+ c2*sqrt(R_{oos}),$ and $rho_{t}$ consistently estimates $R_{oos}$ (up to the noise floor). 【author decision: which regularity assumptions the proof commits to (e.g. independent vs. correlated returns; whether you assume the tried directions cover the feature space or actively guarantee it) — choose the regime under which $rho_{t}$ provably estimates $R_{oos}.$】\n\n*The sufficiency bound: the recovered policy's value gap is controlled by the in-span estimation error plus the out-of-span coset norm $R_{oos},$ so below a derived $R_{oos}$ bound in-span recovery is near-optimal and above it the residual coset, not insufficient querying, caps achievable value.*\n$$ \\text{value\\_gap} \\;\\le\\; c_1\\sqrt{\\;\\|\\hat z - z^\\star\\|\\;} \\; + \\; c_2\\sqrt{R_{\\mathrm{oos}}} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This names exactly what can and cannot be recovered and proves the system acts on the very quantity that decides whether in-menu recovery is good enough.\n\n### Confound-isolating diagnostic\n*Dials the out-of-span reward fraction at fixed label budget to attribute value collapse to misspecification.*\n\n7. Build a controlled test suite on one frozen BFM where the only thing you change is how much of the task lies OUTSIDE the menu. To make a provably out-of-menu reward, take a candidate reward function, fit it as well as possible with the menu features, and keep only the leftover part that the menu cannot fit (the residual) — check that this residual really has near-zero overlap with the menu. Scale the in-menu and out-of-menu parts equally, then build tasks $r = r_{inmenu} +$ alpha $* r_{orthogonal}$ and sweep alpha from 0 to 1, always with the same number of reward labels. Use the alpha=0 runs to set the trigger threshold tau from step 5 (Use the SAME $rho_{t}$ to decide $when\\dots ).$\n   - _Why_: Varying only the out-of-menu fraction lets you attribute any policy collapse to misspecification rather than to running out of queries.\n8. Run our method, OpTI-BFM, ReLA, and forward-backward (FB) zero-shot projection across the alpha sweep, measuring cumulative regret and the final value gap. For the value gap, train a from-scratch task-specific policy (e.g. SAC) to convergence on each task as the 'best achievable' reference, and reuse it across all methods so the comparison is fair. Also run the two controls: a negative control that forces $rho_{t}$ to 0 everywhere (turning off the gate and the fallback), which should make our results match OpTI-BFM; and a positive control that uses $rho_{t}$ only to trigger the fallback. Tune the threshold tau and gate slope lambda on a held-out split and report how sensitive regret is to them.\n   - _Why_: This produces the headline result — our curve stays bounded while OpTI-BFM's worsens — and the controls prove $rho_{t}$ is the cause.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 面向行为基础模型的失配感知乐观任务推断\n\n**方法名称.** Misspecification-Aware OpTI (MA-OpTI)\n\n## 研究动机\n行为基础模型（BFM，behavior foundation model）是一类在没有任何奖励的情况下预训练出来的大型策略；之后给它一个新任务时，它通过从一份冻结的技能菜单（即 feature span）里挑出一个小小的任务码 z 来给出好策略。目前挑 z 的最好办法是 OpTI-BFM（面向 BFM 的乐观任务推断）：它把挑 z 当作老虎机问题，加上一个“乐观”推动，主动去试最可能好的 z，并随着交互越来越好。问题在于，整个过程都发生在这份冻结菜单内部，并假设真实奖励是菜单能表达的东西。如果真实任务有一部分落在冻结特征所能表示的范围之外，OpTI-BFM 根本察觉不到：它会对一个永远拟合不了该任务的 z 越来越自信，于是你拿到的策略会随着交互悄悄变差，而不是变好。我们的修法是在线地多算一个数 $rho_{t}$：预测误差中任何菜单项都无法解释的那一部分，并以模型自带的噪声地板 $sigma0^{2}$ 为基准来度量。当 $rho_{t}$ 接近 0 时，任务在菜单内，我们的行为与 OpTI-BFM 完全一致（因此继承它的保证）；当 $rho_{t}$ 持续偏高时，同一个数告诉我们“没有 z 能拟合——别再信菜单了”，并切换到一个在菜单之外学习的 fallback。先前工作因结构性原因止步：OpTI-BFM（arXiv 2025-10）一切都从 in-span 数学构造，没给 out-of-span 信号留位置；ReLA（arXiv 2025-04）只在选定任务码之后才纠错，从不用残余误差来决定是否继续查询；而人形 BFM（ICLR 2025）只是把奖励投影到冻结菜单上，从不检查这个投影是否够用。补上这个缺口，就给测试时任务推断装上了一个内置自检——一个数告诉你更多交互还能不能帮上忙，还是任务本身已超出模型范围——并把 OpTI-BFM 与 ReLA 都变成这个数为 0 时的特例。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景\n\n1. 完全按原样实现 Optimistic Task Inference for BFMs(OpTI-BFM) 循环，它既是对照方法，也是任务在菜单内时我们回退到的行为。对任务码 z 维护一个高斯信念：均值 $mu_{t}$ 和一个由你已经试过哪些技能特征方向而增长的协方差 $Sigma_{t}$。每个 episode，挑选使 $<mu_{t},$ z> + beta $* sqrt(z^{T} Sigma_{t}$ z)（最佳猜测加上对欠探索方向的乐观奖励）最大的下一个 z，运行该策略一个 episode，观察回报，并更新信念。记录所选的 z 序列和累计 regret。\n   - _为什么_: 当任务在菜单内时我们必须与它完全一致，所以它既是基线，也是我们回退时的行为。\n\n### Out-of-span 残差通道\n*以模型噪声地板为基准，构造并维护 $rho_{t}——$对任何 in-span 任务都无法解释的奖励质量的在线估计。*\n\n2. 在预训练行为基础模型(Behavior Foundation Model, BFM)时，顺便测量一下即便任务确实能被冻结特征菜单表达，也无法避免的预测误差有多大。留出一些 (state, reward) 样本，在冻结特征上拟合最好的线性奖励预测器，再在另一份留出折上记录它的平均平方误差，得到单个数 $sigma0^{2}$。把 $sigma0^{2}$ 存进模型文件。这就是模型正常的“噪声地板”——后面一切都要拿它当标尺来比较。\n   - _为什么_: 需要一个正常预测误差的基准，免得之后把普通噪声误当成超出菜单的任务。\n3. 增加第二个滑动量。每个 episode 之后，算预测回报与实际回报的差距，取平方，并保持一个平滑均值（指数移动平均，新值权重 0.05）。从该均值里减去两样东西：来自 第2步（在预训练行为基础模型） 的噪声地板 $sigma0^{2}$，以及仍不确定 z 所导致的那部分误差（用你刚执行的特征向量 $\\psi $ 算成 $\\psi ^{T} Sigma_{t} \\psi $）。把结果在 0 处截断得到 $rho_{t}$。去掉普通噪声和 z 不确定性后剩下的，正是任何菜单项都无法解释的误差——即 out-of-menu 信号，也是对有多少奖励落在菜单之外的一致估计。\n\n*承载变量 $\\rho _{t}$：回报预测残差平方的滑动均值，减去预训练得到的 in-span 噪声地板 $\\sigma _{0}^{2}$，再减去 $\\Sigma _{t}$ 引起的有限样本预测方差，并在 0 处截断——构造上即预测误差中无法由任何 in-span 嵌入解释的部分，也就是对 out-of-span 陪集范数 $R_{oos}$ 的估计。*\n$$ \\rho_t = \\max\\Big(0,\\; \\tfrac{1}{t}\\textstyle\\sum_{k\\le t}\\big(\\hat G_k - \\langle \\psi^{\\pi_{z_k}}(s_{kH}), \\hat z_k\\rangle\\big)^2 - \\sigma_0^2 - \\mathrm{tr}(\\text{Var}_{\\Sigma_t})\\Big) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 去掉正常噪声和“还在学 z”的不确定性后剩下的，正是任何菜单项都无法解释的误差——即 out-of-menu 信号。\n\n### 以 rho_t 为键的控制器\n*同一个标量既门控乐观探索又触发 span-exit fallback，把算子与 fallback 耦合为单一控制器。*\n\n4. 修改选 z 的规则，把乐观奖励项乘以一个门 $g(rho_{t})$。用 $g(x)=1+lambda*tanh(x/sigma0^{2})$：当 $rho_{t}$ 为 0 时门恰好为 1，规则与 OpTI-BFM 完全一致（因此保留它的保证）；$rho_{t}$ 增大时，门平滑增长到 1+lambda，推动更强的探索。除以 $sigma0^{2}$ 意味着门是相对模型自身噪声水平来衡量 out-of-menu 信号。lambda 先取 1，之后再调。\n\n*门控采集规则：把 in-span 的 UCB 目标（后验均值 $\\mu _{t}$ 加上由后验协方差 $\\Sigma _{t}$ 缩放的乐观奖励项）乘以一个单调门 $g(\\rho _{t})$；当检测不到 out-of-span 成分时 $g(\\rho _{t})=1$，于是 $\\rho _{t}$ 为 0 时算子精确退化为 OpTI-BFM。*\n$$ z_{t+1} = \\arg\\max_{z}\\; \\langle \\mu_t, z\\rangle + \\beta\\,\\sqrt{z^{\\top}\\Sigma_t z}\\;\\, g(\\rho_t),\\qquad g(0)=1 \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 没有 out-of-menu 成分时方法与 OpTI-BFM 完全相同；一旦出现 out-of-menu 质量，探索会据此响应而非忽视。\n5. 用同一个 $rho_{t}$ 来决定何时放弃菜单。保留一个阈值 tau，并要求 $rho_{t}$ 连续 w 个 episode（默认 5）都超过它，以免对噪声反应过度。一旦发生，就把控制权交给一个 fallback 的 off-menu actor-critic：它从当前最佳策略（即 $z = mu_{t}$ 对应的 BFM 策略）出发，然后用标准 off-policy 方法（如 TD3 或 SAC）直接从有奖励的转移中学习。在 第7步（在一个冻结的 $BFM\\dots $） 中设定 tau，使真正在菜单内的任务几乎不会越过它（取在菜单内运行时 $rho_{t}$ 的 95 分位数）。因为同一个数既调节探索（第4步（修改选 z 的规则））又触发这个 fallback，切换是平滑的，而非另外拼接的系统。\n   - _为什么_: 调节探索用的是同一个数，决定何时彻底放弃菜单也用它，因此切换到 fallback 是平滑的，而不是另外拼接的系统。\n\n### 恢复理论\n*命名 span-projection 等价类并证明 $rho_{t}$ 在线验证的 value-gap 充分性界。*\n\n6. 证明两件事。第一，在菜单内推断任务只能把它确定到一个“span-projection 等价类”：任意两个在菜单上投影后看起来相同的奖励，对菜单内查询都无法区分，并共享同一个菜单内最佳策略——而 $R_{oos}$（剩下的 out-of-menu 部分的大小）正是查询永远无法解决的部分。第二，作为推论，恢复策略的价值差至多为 c1*sqrt(z-error) $+ c2*sqrt(R_{oos})$，且 $rho_{t}$ 一致地估计 $R_{oos}$（差一个噪声地板）。【作者需决定：证明采用哪些正则性假设（例如回报独立还是相关；是假设已试方向覆盖特征空间，还是主动保证覆盖）——选定能证明 $rho_{t}$ 一致估计 $R_{oos}$ 的设定。】\n\n*充分性界：恢复策略的价值差由 in-span 估计误差与 out-of-span 陪集范数 $R_{oos}$ 共同控制；当 $R_{oos}$ 低于推导出的界时 in-span 恢复近最优，高于该界时限制可达价值的是残余陪集而非查询不足。*\n$$ \\text{value\\_gap} \\;\\le\\; c_1\\sqrt{\\;\\|\\hat z - z^\\star\\|\\;} \\; + \\; c_2\\sqrt{R_{\\mathrm{oos}}} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这精确地命名了什么能恢复、什么不能，并证明系统作用的正是决定 in-menu 恢复是否够好的那个量。\n\n### 隔离混淆的诊断\n*在固定标签预算下调节 out-of-span 奖励比例，把价值崩溃归因于失配。*\n\n7. 在一个冻结的 BFM 上构造一个受控测试套件，其中你唯一改变的是任务有多少落在菜单之外。要造一个可证明在菜单外的奖励，取一个候选奖励函数，用菜单特征尽量拟合它，只保留菜单拟合不了的剩余部分（残差）——并检验该残差与菜单的重叠确实接近零。把 in-menu 与 out-of-menu 部分等比例缩放，然后构造任务 $r = r_{inmenu} +$ alpha $* r_{orthogonal}$，在固定奖励标签数下把 alpha 从 0 扫到 1。用 alpha=0 的运行来设定 第5步（用同一个 $rho_{t}\\dots $） 中的触发阈值 tau。\n   - _为什么_: 只改变 out-of-menu 比例，就能把任何策略崩溃归因于失配，而非查询用尽。\n8. 在 alpha 扫描上运行我们的方法、OpTI-BFM、ReLA 以及 forward-backward(FB) zero-shot 投影，测累计 regret 和最终 value gap。对于 value gap，为每个任务用从零训练到收敛的任务专用策略（如 SAC）作为“可达最优”参考，并在所有方法间复用以保证比较公平。另外运行两个对照：负对照把 $rho_{t}$ 处处强制为 0（关掉门和 fallback），应使我们的结果与 OpTI-BFM 一致；正对照只用 $rho_{t}$ 来触发 fallback。在留出划分上调阈值 tau 和门斜率 lambda，并报告 regret 对它们的敏感度。\n   - _为什么_: 这给出头条结果——我们的曲线保持有界而 OpTI-BFM 变差——而对照证明 $rho_{t}$ 是原因。\n\n"},{"id":"93","run_dir":"run_prompt93_pgenrm","index":93,"title":"Calibrated Personalized Reward Models: A Posterior over the User Direction","title_zh":"校准的个性化奖励模型：用户方向上的后验分布","method_name":"Calibrated User-Posterior Reward (CUP-RM)","hook":"Every personalized reward model serves a single number per response, but for a user with few labels that number is a coin flip the system reports as a fact; we make the deployable quantity a posterior over the user's reward whose spread is itself the signal — and use that spread to decide which comparison to ask next. The calibrated posterior, not a sharper point estimate, is what separates a known preference from a silent default.","anchor_pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","anchor_pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","domain_category":"LLM Alignment, Safety & Behavior","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf quantifies, at deployment for a single user with few labels, how much of the served per-user reward is supported by that user's own evidence versus borrowed from the shared population prior — i.e. there is no per-user posterior or calibrated confidence over the recovered reward, so the system cannot flag a preference it is merely defaulting on.","pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by recasting 'how confident is this user's reward' as a measurement object: a posterior over the user's coordinate in the shared reward-feature direction, computed as a Laplace/variational estimator on the reward backbone, whose entropy is the per-user evidence-vs-prior split and is certified by causal intervention.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf chooses which next comparison to put in front of a sparsely-observed user so as to most reduce the ambiguity in that user's recovered reward — the personalization loop is passive: it consumes whatever labels arrive but never decides what to ask.","pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by recasting 'which comparison to ask next' as an acquisition/measurement over the same posterior: an expected-posterior-entropy-reduction (BALD-style) score over candidate prompt-pairs, made tractable by a closed-form Gaussian-posterior approximation, selecting the pair whose label most collapses the user's coordinate spread.","is_anchor":false},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether the per-user reward must be represented as a point estimate in a shared latent/adapter space at all, rather than as a distribution whose spread is itself the deployable quantity — every leaf (MiCRo routing weights, shared-LoRA adapter, PAL prototype placement, meta-adapted reward) silently inherits the point-estimate-of-a-personalization-coordinate assumption from a common ancestor.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","how_closed":"Framing half (C05): audits the identifiability assumption that per-user data alone suffices to point-identify the user coordinate, and pivots to a substitute condition of a different kind — the learned shared low-rank reward subspace plus a hierarchical prior carries the identifying power, so the user is recovered only up to a posterior whose spread is the residual unidentifiability. Companion deliverable (controlled_diagnostic_design): a controlled construction of matched synthetic users differing only in label count and prior-agreement isolates that the posterior-spread regime recovers user reward where the point-estimate regime collapses to the population default.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"personalized reward modeling for RLHF / LLM alignment","n_papers":49,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":25},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":12,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Reflective Verbal Reward Design for Pluralistic Alignment"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"RLHF Workflow: From Reward Modeling to Online RLHF"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Secrets of RLHF in Large Language Models Part II: Reward Modeling"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"InfoRM: Mitigating Reward Hacking in RLHF via Information-Theoretic Reward Modeling"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Optimal Design for Reward Modeling in RLHF"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Sequence to Sequence Reward Modeling: Improving RLHF by Language Feedback"}],"more":6},{"year":2025,"n":27,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"ARF-RLHF: Adaptive Reward-Following for RLHF through Emotion-Driven Self-Supervision and Trace-Biased Dynamic Optimization"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"MiCRo: Mixture Modeling and Context-aware Routing for Personalized Preference Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"PAL: Sample-Efficient Personalized Reward Modeling for Pluralistic Alignment"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"PersRM-R1: Enhance Personalized Reward Modeling with Reinforcement Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Personalized Reward Modeling for Text-to-Image Generation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A Unified Pairwise Framework for RLHF: Bridging Generative Reward Modeling and Policy Optimization"}],"more":21},{"year":2026,"n":10,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Mitigating Reward Hacking in RLHF via Bayesian Non-negative Reward Modeling"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"reward-lens: A Mechanistic Interpretability Library for Reward Models"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Generalisation of RLHF under Reward Shift and Clipped KL Regularisation"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Factored Causal Representation Learning for Robust Reward Modeling in RLHF"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"CausalRM: Causal-Theoretic Reward Modeling for RLHF from Observational User Feedbacks"}],"more":4}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":10,"share":0.204},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":9,"share":0.184},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":9,"share":0.184},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":7,"share":0.143},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":7,"share":0.143},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":6,"share":0.122},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":6,"share":0.122},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":3,"share":0.061}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Recent personalized reward models recover per-user reward functions by placing each user in a latent space and conditioning on a few of their labels — MiCRo (semanticscholar:1b108ded8ea5524d90bc43fd9bd9bdd82f8f8f74) routes a prompt to a mixture component, the shared low-rank approach (openalex:W6966976602) attaches a per-user low-rank adapter, PAL (semanticscholar:6a4005d51408bd98decd06d03e58763bcb3e1b29) localizes a new user against learned prototypes, and meta reward modeling (arxiv:2601.18731v2) fast-adapts from a meta-prior — but for a user who has supplied only a handful of preference labels the fitted per-user reward is statistically under-determined: many distinct user reward functions are equally consistent with the observed labels, so the estimate is dominated by whichever shared prior the method leans on, and none of these methods exposes how much of the deployed per-user reward is actually evidence from that user versus borrowed population mean. As a result the system cannot tell a confidently-known user preference from one it is silently defaulting on, and it has no signal for which next comparison would most reduce that ambiguity — exactly the regime (cold-start / sparse per-user feedback) these papers name as their motivating bottleneck (semanticscholar:6a4005d51408bd98decd06d03e58763bcb3e1b29, openalex:W4415884644).","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:1b108ded8ea5524d90bc43fd9bd9bdd82f8f8f74","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"MiCRo learns a mixture of K reward functions from binary preference data and at deployment routes each prompt to a subpopulation via a context-aware weighting P(z=k|x) conditioned only on the prompt x, avoiding per-user labels. Its method conditions the routing on the prompt, not on a posterior over the individual user's preference given that user's own observed labels, so it produces no per-user posterior and no measure of how confidently a given user has been located among the K components — a sparsely-observed user is routed by prompt content alone with no notion of remaining uncertainty or of which query would resolve it.","_anchor_fulltext":"read from method section C1/C2 + 4.1 mixture modeling design"},{"paper_id":"openalex:W6966976602","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"The shared low-rank adaptation approach attaches a per-user low-rank adapter on top of a shared reward backbone so commonalities are shared while individual directions are personalized. The adapter is point-estimated by fitting the user's labels with no posterior over the low-rank direction, so under a handful of labels the fitted user direction is uncalibrated — it provides no way to distinguish a user direction backed by evidence from one shrunk toward zero (the shared backbone) by regularization, and no active criterion for which comparison would best identify the direction."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:6a4005d51408bd98decd06d03e58763bcb3e1b29","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"PAL builds a reward modeling framework that leverages commonalities across users while enabling few-shot localization of a new user against learned preference prototypes. Localization yields a point placement in prototype space with no quantified identifiability — it does not certify when the few-shot labels are sufficient to place the user versus when the placement is dominated by the prototype prior, and it does not select which comparison to label next to sharpen an ambiguous placement."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415884644","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"This DPO-under-unobserved-heterogeneity work argues latent variables are necessary and fits a discrete latent type mixture via EM over the population. It recovers population-level type structure and assumes a fixed type count, but does not address recovery of an individual's reward from that individual's sparse labels or quantify the per-user posterior uncertainty, treating heterogeneity as a population nuisance to marginalize rather than a per-user quantity to identify and certify."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"personalized reward modeling for RLHF / LLM alignment","venue":"ICLR / NeurIPS / ICML","time":"2026","data":["pairwise human preference datasets with annotator/user IDs (e.g. PRISM, multi-annotator preference corpora)","synthetic mixtures of heterogeneous preference functions for controlled identifiability study"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with RLHF / preference-learning background","preference":"both","baseline":"MiCRo (mixture + context routing), PAL (prototype mixture), Shared-LoRA personalized RLHF, latent-variable DPO under unobserved heterogeneity","limitation":"current personalized reward models fit per-user reward functions but give no guarantee that the recovered per-user reward reflects the user's true preference rather than collapsing to the population prior when the user has provided only a handful of labels, and they do not decide which comparison to ask next to resolve that ambiguity","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"Central shared object (coherence_thread_type = shared_object): the per-user reward POSTERIOR p(w_u | D_u) over the user's coordinate w_u in a shared, learned low-rank reward-feature direction; all three legs read from or write to this one object. We start from a standard reward backbone f_theta(x,y) ∈ R^d giving a reward feature vector phi(x,y) (the penultimate-layer representation before the scalar head, d≈the backbone hidden size, e.g. 4096; the head is its linear readout). Across a population we fit (i) a shared base reward direction w_0 ∈ R^d and (ii) a rank-r user subspace U ∈ R^{d×r} (r a hyperparameter, default r=8) by maximum-likelihood Bradley-Terry on multi-annotator preference data, so each user's reward is r_u(x,y) = <w_0 + U a_u, phi(x,y)>, a_u ∈ R^r the user's coordinate. Leg 1 (anchor, reframe/C00): instead of point-estimating a_u, we place a Gaussian hierarchical prior a_u ~ N(0, Sigma) (Sigma learned across users — this is the empirical-Bayes shrinkage strength, encoded over the LEARNED subspace U, NOT over raw scores) and compute a Laplace posterior p(a_u | D_u) ≈ N(mu_u, Lambda_u^{-1}) where Lambda_u = Sigma^{-1} + sum over user's K labeled pairs of the BT Hessian in the U-projected feature differences; the deployed per-user reward is the posterior-mean reward with the posterior covariance Lambda_u^{-1} carried alongside. The load-bearing readout is H_u = log det(Lambda_u^{-1}) (posterior differential entropy in the r-dim coordinate space) — high H_u means the served reward is dominated by the shared prior w_0 (a silent default), low H_u means it is user-evidenced; this is the quantity the field's point estimates discard. Leg 2 (active query, reframe/C00): which next comparison to ask is the measurement argmax over a candidate pool of prompt-pairs of the expected reduction in H_u under the posterior-predictive over the unobserved label (closed form for the Gaussian-Laplace posterior: the BALD information gain of the projected feature-difference direction), selecting the pair that most collapses Lambda_u^{-1}. Leg 3 (audit, C05 + companion controlled_diagnostic_design): the audited assumption is that K per-user labels point-identify a_u; we show the BT likelihood in r dimensions is flat along feature-difference directions the user has not been queried on (rank(label Fisher info) < r ⇒ a_u not point-identified), so the point estimate silently equals the prior projection there — the pivot replaces 'enough per-user data' with 'shared subspace U + hierarchical prior Sigma supply the identifying constraint', recovering a_u only up to the posterior N(mu_u, Lambda_u^{-1}), whose spread IS the residual unidentifiability. The companion ships the empirical separation: matched synthetic users sharing the same true a_u but differing in K and in prior-agreement, holding everything else fixed, so the gap between posterior-served and point-served reward isolates spread as deployable signal rather than a population-mean confound. The three legs share machinery (one posterior object); only Leg 2's acquisition score and Leg 3's diagnostic construction are separate code.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The legs share machinery because the coherence thread is the single posterior object: the calibration leg constructs it, the active-query leg is an acquisition functional of it, and the audit leg is the identifiability statement that licenses it — fusing them avoids three stapled contributions. We considered (and rejected) a discrete latent-type mixture posterior (as in latent-variable DPO openalex:W4415884644) because its spread is over K population types, not over the individual's coordinate, so it cannot report per-user evidence-vs-default; and we rejected a deep-ensemble of reward heads (cheaper to motivate) because it gives no closed-form H_u for the active-query expected-information-gain step. REGRESSION CHECK against method_lineage.notes: a generic empirical-Bayes/hierarchical shrinkage (collateral node c2) and classical GP active preference elicitation (collateral node c1) are the avoided nodes — we do NOT apply stock shrinkage to raw scores nor a from-scratch per-user acquisition; the prior Sigma and the posterior are defined over the LEARNED shared subspace U of the modern reward backbone, and the acquisition reuses the cross-user U, which is the source neither collateral node occupies.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on a real multi-annotator preference dataset with user IDs (e.g. PRISM and a personalized-preference split), fit the shared subspace and, for held-out users given K ∈ {1,2,4,8,16} labels, measure (i) per-user held-out preference accuracy and (ii) personalized best-of-n win-rate, comparing the calibrated-posterior serving + active query against MiCRo, shared-LoRA, PAL and meta-RM, all given the same label budget. If the candidate works, per-user accuracy and personalized win-rate increase over all baselines most sharply at small K and the active-query variant reaches a target accuracy with fewer labels than random-query (sample-efficiency curve shifts left). The named load-bearing variable is the per-user posterior entropy H_u = log det Lambda_u^{-1}: the mechanism claim is that the calibrated spread of H_u, not merely a better point estimate, drives the gains — concretely, win-rate gain over the point-estimate baseline should be monotonically larger for users whose H_u is high (prior-dominated) once their queried labels reduce H_u. Negative control (anti-tautology): replace the data-dependent Lambda_u^{-1} with a constant covariance c·I — destroying H_u's dependence on the user's evidence while leaving the posterior mean mu_u unchanged — and the DOWNSTREAM personalized win-rate of the active-query loop must collapse back to the random-query / point-estimate baseline (the controlled outcome is win-rate, not H_u's own value). A positive control: a stripped model that uses ONLY H_u to gate between serving w_0 (default) and U mu_u (personalized) should recover most of the win-rate gain on sparse users, confirming the spread is the identifying signal.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:1b108ded8ea5524d90bc43fd9bd9bdd82f8f8f74","delta":"MiCRo routes a prompt to one of K mixture components via prompt-conditioned weights P(z=k|x) and serves a point reward; we construct a per-user posterior over a continuous coordinate a_u and derive its entropy H_u as a deployable evidence-vs-default measure that a routing weight cannot express."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W6966976602","delta":"The shared low-rank approach point-estimates a per-user low-rank adapter by fitting the user's labels; we place a hierarchical prior on the same low-rank coordinate and derive a Laplace posterior whose covariance Lambda_u^{-1} quantifies which feature-difference directions the user has NOT identified, which their point estimate discards."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:6a4005d51408bd98decd06d03e58763bcb3e1b29","delta":"PAL localizes a new user against learned prototypes as a point placement; we add an active-query criterion (closed-form expected posterior-entropy reduction) that decides which comparison to label next, turning passive few-shot localization into a closed elicitation loop with a certified sample-efficiency curve."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415884644","delta":"The latent-variable DPO work recovers a population-level discrete type mixture via EM with fixed K; we give a continuous per-individual identifiability statement (rank of the per-user label Fisher information < r ⇒ unidentified along un-queried directions) and operationalize the residual as the served posterior spread."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W6966976602","what_step_was_missed":"The shared low-rank approach already isolates a per-user low-rank reward coordinate over a shared backbone, so it sits structurally closest. To already be this contribution it would have needed to construct the per-user coordinate as a posterior under a hierarchical prior on the subspace and derive its covariance — specifically the second-order Laplace Hessian Lambda_u in the U-projected feature-difference geometry whose log-determinant is the evidence-vs-default entropy H_u — and then expose that entropy both as a serving-time confidence and as the objective of an expected-information-gain query selector; it constructs only the point MAP coordinate, so neither the spread quantity nor the acquisition functional that consumes it exists in their method."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":321,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"Hard floor does not fire: gap_closure_reject_check is borderline (no entry triggered, no Reject lesson matched 'yes'); anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null; paper_pointed_threat is adjacent, not exact-mechanism overlap. Revise (not advance) is chosen because two load-bearing findings co-occur: (1) recipe_application_check.entries[2].verdict = borderline on the C05 leg — the audit-and-pivot tactic is performed but the explicit named ambiguity class up to which a_u is recovered (C05's terminal 'recoverable up to ___' claim) is left implicit as posterior spread rather than exhibited; and (2) paper_pointed_threat openalex:W7161090555 is addressable_via a specific differentiation_from_lit[] field — its population-level necessary-and-sufficient identifiability theorem directly competes with the candidate's Leg-3 individual identifiability statement. Both are tactical field-level fixes that sharpen the contribution's identity without touching gap selection or the kill-switch fields.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf quantifies, at deployment for a single user with few labels, how much of the served per-user reward is supported by that user's own evidence versus borrowed from the shared population prior — i.e. there is no per-user posterior or calibrated confidence over the recovered reward, so the system cannot flag a preference it is merely defaulting on.","main_pattern":"reframe_as_solvable_object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The signature failure is treating the reframing as a mechanical wrapper: taking an established attribution, decomposition, or estimation tool and pointing it at a new input granularity, a new architecture, or a new domain without re-deriving why the resulting scores are faithful to the model — supplying the computation but not the justification (no causal validation, no axiomatic argument for the definition, no confound control).","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Pointing an off-the-shelf decomposition at a coarser input granularity without showing the coarser units preserve the signal reads as a wrapper, not a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The posterior is not an off-the-shelf decomposition pointed at coarser units; the candidate defines H_u over the LEARNED shared subspace U with an explicit regression check against stock empirical-Bayes shrinkage, so the unit of analysis is re-justified rather than ported."},{"lesson_quoted":"Proposing a new attribution definition without an axiomatic or causal argument for why it should count as ground-truth collapses the moment a reviewer asks why this is the real importance.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"H_u = log det Lambda_u^{-1} is grounded by the Leg-3 identifiability argument (rank(label Fisher info) < r ⇒ a_u not point-identified) that licenses the spread as the residual unidentifiability — a causal/structural justification, not a bare definition."},{"lesson_quoted":"Conflating a methodological artifact — a computation-granularity difference, a degenerate zero baseline — with genuine signal undermines the entire premise once the confound is identified.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The deployable claim (spread, not point estimate, drives gains) risks a population-mean confound, but the candidate pre-empts it with the matched-synthetic-user companion (controlled_diagnostic_design) and the constant-covariance negative control, so the confound is controlled rather than conflated."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf chooses which next comparison to put in front of a sparsely-observed user so as to most reduce the ambiguity in that user's recovered reward — the personalization loop is passive: it consumes whatever labels arrive but never decides what to ask.","main_pattern":"reframe_as_solvable_object","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The signature failure is treating the reframing as a mechanical wrapper — pointing an established estimation tool at a new setting without re-deriving faithfulness, certified only by plausibility rather than by a causal intervention or soundness proof.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Surveying or recombining fragmented methods without a unifying axis or a decisive controlled experiment yields a contribution reviewers dismiss as anecdotal.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The active-query leg is not a recombination of fragments — it is an acquisition functional of the SAME posterior object the anchor constructs (shared coherence thread), with a decisive sample-efficiency-curve experiment and negative control."},{"lesson_quoted":"An elegant but exponentially expensive attribution definition becomes a usable tool only after a single compression move collapses it to a cheap lookup or closed form.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"This is satisfied, not violated: the BALD expected-entropy-reduction score is made tractable by the closed-form Gaussian-Laplace posterior approximation, exactly the single compression move the lesson endorses."}],"verdict":"clear"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether the per-user reward must be represented as a point estimate in a shared latent/adapter space at all, rather than as a distribution whose spread is itself the deployable quantity — every leaf silently inherits the point-estimate-of-a-personalization-coordinate assumption from a common ancestor.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The signature failure is an identifiability claim that outruns its proof: the pivoted assumption was not actually load-bearing (a straightforward union of two frameworks), or recovery/'consistency' is asserted while the decisive object is never established, or structural constraints are imposed without proving they are SUFFICIENT for recovery.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Stacking two established frameworks and re-proving identifiability of the union reads as incremental unless the pivoted assumption was genuinely load-bearing and the union admits a regime neither framework could reach alone.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The pivot fuses a learned reward subspace with a hierarchical Bayesian prior; this risks reading as a union, but the audited assumption (K per-user labels point-identify a_u) is shown load-bearing via the flat-likelihood / rank-deficient Fisher argument, and the new regime (sparse-K users where the point estimate collapses to the prior projection) is one neither stock subspace fitting nor stock shrinkage reaches — so it is defensible but not airtight."},{"lesson_quoted":"Advertising an identifiability or 'consistency' property while the proof omits the decisive object — never proving latent identifiability, or excluding part of the model from the guarantee — collapses the contribution the moment a reviewer checks the theorem.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The candidate states the UN-identifiability direction (rank(Fisher) < r ⇒ not point-identified) operationally rather than naming the exact ambiguity class up to which a_u IS recovered under U + Sigma; C05's terminal claim is 'recoverable up to permutation/sign/linear transform', and that named equivalence class is implicit, not exhibited — a load-bearing gap a reviewer can probe."},{"lesson_quoted":"Imposing structural constraints to claim interpretability or disentanglement without proving those constraints are sufficient for recovery leaves the result indistinguishable from a post-hoc heuristic.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate does not claim recovery from the structural prior alone; it claims recovery only up to the posterior spread, and operationalizes the constraint (the prior IS enforced in the Laplace Hessian Lambda_u = Sigma^{-1} + BT Hessian), so the constraint is enforced by the algorithm rather than asserted."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"The C00 anchor and active-query entries are clear (faithfulness re-derived over the learned subspace, tractability via closed-form compression, causal negative-control validation). The C05 audit entry is borderline on two load-bearing lessons: the 'union of two frameworks' risk and, more pointedly, that the identifiability pivot states the un-identification direction operationally but does not exhibit the NAMED ambiguity class up to which a_u is recovered under U + Sigma — C05's signature terminal claim. No entry is triggered."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf quantifies, at deployment for a single user with few labels, how much of the served per-user reward is supported by that user's own evidence versus borrowed from the shared population prior.","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Recast an opaque transparency/uncertainty question about an already-trained model as a concrete measurement over a well-studied object (an estimator/decomposition/influence score), fixing the right unit of analysis and faithfulness constraint, buying tractability with one compression trick, and certifying fidelity by a causal intervention rather than plausibility.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"Leg 1 performs exactly this: 'how confident is this user's reward' is recast as a posterior p(a_u|D_u) over the user's coordinate in the learned low-rank subspace U (the well-studied object = Laplace/variational estimator), the unit of analysis is fixed (the U-projected feature-difference geometry, not raw scores), tractability is bought with the closed-form Gaussian-Laplace approximation, and the readout H_u = log det Lambda_u^{-1} is certified causally by the constant-covariance negative control that must collapse downstream win-rate to baseline.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf chooses which next comparison to put in front of a sparsely-observed user so as to most reduce the ambiguity in that user's recovered reward.","sub_pattern":"C00 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"The same measurement reframe, here over a candidate set: choose the object whose native correctness criterion coincides with 'faithful', and buy tractability with one closed-form compression move.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"Leg 2 recasts 'which comparison to ask next' as a BALD expected-posterior-entropy-reduction acquisition over the SAME posterior object, made tractable by the closed-form Gaussian-Laplace information gain on the projected feature-difference direction — the cluster's measurement-plus-compression move is present, not merely a generic 'be Bayesian' gesture.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether the per-user reward must be represented as a point estimate in a shared latent/adapter space at all, rather than as a distribution whose spread is itself the deployable quantity.","sub_pattern":"C05 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Take an existing identifiability/recovery result and pivot the assumption it rests on — trade a distributional assumption (here: enough per-user data to point-identify) for a structural/geometric one (a learned shared subspace plus hierarchical prior carrying the identifying power) — then re-derive recovery up to the field's accepted ambiguity class and operationalize it as an estimator.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"Leg 3 performs the audit-and-pivot move: it pins the load-bearing assumption (K per-user labels point-identify a_u), shows the prior proof collapses (BT likelihood flat along un-queried feature-difference directions, rank(label Fisher info) < r), substitutes the DIFFERENT-kind condition (shared subspace U + hierarchical prior Sigma supply the identifying constraint), and operationalizes it as the Laplace estimator. The cluster's distinctive verb is performed; what is under-exhibited is the explicit named ambiguity class (the un-queried-direction subspace) up to which a_u is recovered — present operationally as posterior spread but not stated as C05's terminal 'recoverable up to ___' claim.","verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"Both C00 entries cleanly perform the measurement-reframe-plus-closed-form-compression-plus-causal-certification signature. The C05 entry performs the audit-and-pivot tactic but stops short of exhibiting the explicit named ambiguity class C05's tactical_pattern makes its terminal claim — borderline, not bypassed, because the pivot's substance (assumption shown load-bearing, structural substitute supplied, estimator enforces it) is all present."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["reframe_as_solvable_object","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"The three reject-favored compositions all require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; this candidate's main_pattern set is {reframe_as_solvable_object, assumption_audit_and_pivot}, which contains no heterogeneous_decomposition, so no documented anti-pattern composition matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"openalex:W7161090555","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"'Personalized Alignment Revisited: The Necessity and Sufficiency of User Diversity' (collision #59) characterizes the exact conditions under which personalized alignment is statistically identifiable — proving a user-diversity condition (the population of user-specific heads must span the latent reward directions) is necessary and sufficient for O(1) regret / log(1/eps) sample complexity, naming user diversity as 'the fundamental driver of personalized identifiability.' This is the sharpest competitor to the candidate's Leg-3 identifiability claim: a reviewer will ask whether the candidate's per-user 'rank(label Fisher info) < r ⇒ a_u not point-identified' statement is anything more than the per-user, single-user-conditioned shadow of #59's population-level spanning condition. The candidate stands if its contribution is genuinely the DEPLOYMENT-TIME per-user posterior whose spread is the served quantity (a measurement object #59 does not construct), and falls if it is read as merely re-deriving #59's identifiability boundary at the individual level without the operational posterior.","addressable_via":"Add a differentiation_from_lit[] entry against openalex:W7161090555 making explicit that #59 is a population-level statistical-efficiency theorem (regret / sample-complexity rates over the user population), whereas the candidate's contribution is a per-user deployment-time posterior whose log-det entropy H_u is the served evidence-vs-default signal and the active-query objective — a constructed measurement object #59 never produces."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism (Leg 3 identifiability statement)","issue":"recipe_application_check.entries[2].verdict = borderline — C05's tactical_pattern requires exhibiting the named ambiguity class up to which the hidden coordinate is recovered ('recoverable up to permutation/sign/linear transform'); the candidate states the un-identification direction operationally (posterior spread) but does not name the equivalence class.","fix_direction":"In Leg 3, make the ambiguity class explicit: state that under the shared subspace U plus hierarchical prior Sigma, the user coordinate a_u is recovered up to the affine subspace spanned by the un-queried feature-difference directions (the null space of the per-user label Fisher information projected into U), i.e. identified modulo that residual subspace, which the posterior covariance Lambda_u^{-1} concentrates on. Keep the wording faithful to the existing Laplace machinery; do NOT touch falsification_prediction or compute_budget."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit[]","issue":"paper_pointed_threat openalex:W7161090555 (Personalized Alignment Revisited) competes with the Leg-3 identifiability claim and is addressable_via a differentiation entry.","fix_direction":"Append one differentiation_from_lit[] entry: {paper_id: 'openalex:W7161090555', delta: '#59 proves a POPULATION-LEVEL necessary-and-sufficient user-diversity condition for O(1) regret / log(1/eps) sample complexity — a statistical-efficiency boundary over the user population; we instead construct a PER-USER deployment-time posterior whose log-det entropy H_u is the served evidence-vs-default signal and the active-query objective, a measurement object #59 never produces, and our identifiability statement is the individual, single-user-conditioned residual (un-queried-direction subspace) rather than a population spanning rate.'}"}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism (Leg 3 identifiability statement)","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Leg 3 now exhibits the named ambiguity class: a_u is identified up to the affine residual subspace spanned by the un-queried feature-difference directions (the null space of the per-user label Fisher information projected into U), satisfying C05's terminal 'recoverable up to ___' claim while keeping the existing Laplace machinery intact."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit[]","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Appended a differentiation entry against openalex:W7161090555 (Personalized Alignment Revisited) drawing the population-level-statistical-efficiency-theorem vs per-user-deployment-posterior distinction the paper_pointed_threat required."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Calibrated Personalized Reward Models: A Posterior over the User Direction\n\n**Method.** Calibrated User-Posterior Reward (CUP-RM)\n\n## Motivation\nModern personalized reward models (RMs — the components that score how good a response is for a particular person) work the same way: train one big reward model on everyone's data, then bolt on a small per-user piece fit from that user's handful of preference labels. The problem is that when a user has only given a few labels, lots of very different 'tastes' fit those few labels equally well. So the per-user piece is basically guessing, and it quietly leans on the average-over-everyone default. Methods like MiCRo (a mixture-of-experts router) and the shared low-rank adapter approach serve a single reward number, but they never tell you whether that number actually reflects this user or is just the population average in disguise. They also never decide which comparison to ask the user about next to clear up the confusion — they just passively use whatever labels happen to arrive.\n\nThis matters now because the recent wave of personalized RM papers all stop at the same place: they put each user somewhere in a shared space and report a single point, with no measure of how sure they are. But those same recent methods already give us the one ingredient we need — a learned, low-dimensional 'reward direction' space — over which we can cheaply build a proper probability distribution. A 2026 paper, 'The Reward Model Selection Crisis in Personalized Alignment,' even shows that ordinary per-user accuracy is a bad way to pick a reward model for deployment, which is exactly the calibration gap we fix.\n\nWhat changes when we close this gap: the reward model can hand back a confidence with every score, so a system can fall back to the safe population reward when it isn't sure about a user (instead of confidently picking the wrong personalized response), and it can run a smart loop that asks the single most useful comparison next. Existing methods — MiCRo, shared-LoRA, PAL, meta-RM — get a principled cold-start recipe and a built-in sanity check they currently lack.\n\n## Method\n### Background (shared geometry + evaluation)\n*Unchanged scaffolding: the frozen backbone, the shared subspace fit, and the benchmark evaluation.*\n\n1. Take a standard reward model (RM — the component that scores how good a response is) trained on everyone's preference data and freeze it. Define $\\phi (x,y)$ as the model's final-layer hidden vector at the last token of the prompt-plus-response (about 4096 numbers for a 7-8B model) — this is exactly the vector the existing scoring head reads — and keep that head as a plain linear readout of $\\phi .$ This is the standard sequence-classification reward setup in HuggingFace. Input: prompt-response pairs tagged with which annotator gave each label. Output: a frozen feature extractor $\\phi $ and the base scoring head.\n   - _Why_: We build everything on the reward direction this model already learned, rather than starting a new per-user model from scratch.\n2. Across all users at once, fit three things by alternating optimization. (1) A shared base reward direction $w_{0}$ (start it at the existing head). (2) A small rank-r 'user subspace' U — r=8 directions by default, kept orthonormal and ordered by how much preference variance each explains — initialized from a principal-component analysis (PCA) over each annotator's reward-gradient direction. (3) A prior covariance $\\Sigma $ describing how user coordinates typically spread (start at the identity). Alternate: solve each user's best-fit coordinate $a_{u}$ (a tiny 8-dimensional logistic-regression-style fit), then improve $w_{0}$ and U on everyone's data, then re-estimate $\\Sigma $ as the spread of the fitted coordinates. Each user's reward is the base direction plus their coordinate $a_{u}$ mapped through U, scored against $\\phi .$ Output: $w_{0},$ U, $\\Sigma .$\n\n*The per-user reward is the shared base direction $w_{0}$ plus the user's coordinate $a_{u}$ mapped through the learned rank-r subspace U, read against the backbone feature $\\phi (x,y).$*\n$$ r_u(x,y) = \\langle w_0 + U a_u,\\; \\phi(x,y) \\rangle, \\qquad a_u \\in \\mathbb{R}^r \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This builds the shared map every user is placed on, and borrowing structure across users is what lets a sparse user be located without asking them hundreds of questions.\n3. On a real dataset where many annotators labeled preferences with user IDs (e.g. PRISM), measure two things as the per-user label budget K grows: held-out preference accuracy, and personalized best-of-n win-rate (pick the best of 8 candidate responses by each reward method). Win-rate counts the fraction of prompts where this method's pick beats a baseline's pick under the user's held-out true preferences; when you don't have a human label for that exact pair, use as the stand-in oracle the user's own reward fit on ALL their labels (frozen, identical for every method). Compare against MiCRo, shared-LoRA, PAL and meta-RM, each given the same K labels and same candidate responses. Output: accuracy and win-rate curves versus K.\n   - _Why_: If the idea is right, our gains should be largest exactly when users have very few labels, and the active-query version should reach a target accuracy with fewer labels than asking at random.\n\n### Calibrated user posterior\n*Turn the per-user reward from a single point into a posterior whose entropy $H_{u}$ is a served evidence-vs-default confidence.*\n\n4. For a specific user with K labeled comparisons, project each compared pair's feature difference into the user subspace to get an 8-dimensional vector $g_{k}.$ Write down the Bradley-Terry preference likelihood (the standard 'probability the preferred item wins is a logistic function of the score gap') together with the prior N(0, $\\Sigma ),$ and fit a Gaussian approximation of the posterior over the user's coordinate: $a mean \\mu _{u}$ found by a few Newton steps, and a covariance $\\Lambda _{u}^{-1}$ whose precision $\\Lambda _{u}$ is the prior precision $\\Sigma ^{-1}$ plus, for each labeled pair, the term $p(1- p)\\cdot g_{k} g_{k}^{T}$ (how much that pair sharpens the estimate). Output: the $8\\times 8 mean$ and covariance for this user.\n\n*The Laplace posterior over the user coordinate has precision $\\Lambda _{u}$ equal to the prior precision $\\Sigma ^{-1}$ plus the sum of Bradley-Terry Hessians over the user's K labeled pairs, evaluated on the U-projected feature differences $\\delta \\phi .$*\n$$ p(a_u \\mid D_u) \\approx \\mathcal{N}(\\mu_u,\\; \\Lambda_u^{-1}), \\qquad \\Lambda_u = \\Sigma^{-1} + \\sum_{k=1}^{K} H_{\\mathrm{BT}}(\\Pi_U \\, \\delta\\phi_k) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Instead of one best-guess point for the user, we get a full distribution — and its width is the thing every prior method threw away.\n5. Serve the reward as the posterior-mean score, and ALSO output $H_{u} = log det \\Lambda _{u}^{-1},$ the overall width of the user's distribution. To act on it for response selection, shrink the served coordinate with $a_{u}^{served} =$ (I $+ \\alpha \\cdot \\Lambda _{u}^{-1})^{-1} \\mu _{u}:$ directions the user has barely pinned down (large variance) get pulled toward the population default $w_{0},$ while well-evidenced directions are kept; default $\\alpha  =$ 1. 【author decision: how strongly to pull uncertain directions back to the population default (the strength $\\alpha )$ is a deployment policy the authors must set — it trades personalization against safety.】 Output: the served reward plus the per-user confidence $H_{u}.$\n\n*The load-bearing readout $H_{u}$ is the differential entropy of the posterior — high $H_{u}$ means the served reward is prior-dominated (a silent default), low $H_{u}$ means it is user-evidenced.*\n$$ H_u = \\log\\det \\Lambda_u^{-1} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The spread directly answers 'is this the user or the average?', and acting on it changes which response gets picked in a best-of-n loop.\n\n### Closed elicitation loop\n*Use the posterior to actively pick the next comparison that most reduces user uncertainty.*\n\n6. Each round, assemble a pool of candidate comparison pairs (default 256): take held-in prompts, attach two responses to each, and project each pair's feature difference into the user subspace to get g. Score every candidate by how much labeling it is expected to shrink the user's uncertainty — a closed-form information-gain (BALD) score, $½\\cdot log(1 + p(1- p)\\cdot g^{T} \\Lambda _{u}^{-1}$ g), which is just a cheap 8-dimensional quadratic per candidate. Ask the user the single highest-scoring pair, add their answer, and recompute the posterior (step 3). Output: the chosen comparison and the updated posterior.\n\n*The next comparison is the pool pair maximizing the expected reduction in $H_{u}$ under the posterior-predictive over its unobserved label $\\ell $ — closed form for the Gaussian-Laplace posterior (BALD information gain of the projected feature-difference direction).*\n$$ (x,y_a,y_b)^{\\star} = \\arg\\max_{\\text{pool}} \\; \\mathbb{E}_{\\,\\ell \\sim p(\\ell)} \\big[\\, H_u - H_u^{(+\\ell)} \\,\\big] \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Asking the most informative comparison next reaches a confident personalized reward with far fewer labels than asking at random.\n\n### Identifiability audit + separation\n*Prove the spread is the honest residual unidentifiability and isolate it empirically with a controlled construction and negative control.*\n\n7. Prove the audited claim. Define the user's observed Fisher information $F_{u} = \\Sigma _{k} p(1- p)\\cdot g_{k} g_{k}^{T}$ — the same data term that appears in the posterior precision. Show that along directions in its null space $N_{u}$ (directions no asked pair distinguishes) the preference likelihood is flat, so the posterior precision there is just the prior $\\Sigma ^{-1}: a$ single best-guess point would simply copy the population prior in those directions. Name exactly what is recoverable — the coordinate is fixed only up to the residual subspace $N_{u}$ — and show the posterior's leftover uncertainty sits on $N_{u}$ (you can check this: the widest directions of the posterior covariance line up with the least-informed directions of $F_{u}).$ Output: the named residual subspace $N_{u}$ and the identifiability statement that justifies reporting the spread.\n\n*The user coordinate is recovered only up to the residual subspace $N_{u},$ the null space of the per-user label Fisher information $F_{u}$ projected into U; the posterior covariance concentrates its remaining mass on $N_{u}.$*\n$$ N_u = \\mathrm{null}(F_u) \\subset \\mathbb{R}^r, \\qquad F_u = \\Pi_U \\, \\mathcal{I}_{\\mathrm{label}}(a_u) \\, \\Pi_U^{\\top} \\tag{5} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This is the proof that the spread is not a nuisance but the honest, unavoidable residual — which is why reporting it (not hiding it in a point) is the right move.\n8. Construct matched synthetic users that share the SAME true taste $a_{u}*$ but differ only in (a) how many labels K they have and (b) how well their taste agrees with the population average (cosine $\\approx $ +0.8 for aligned, $- 0.8$ for anti-aligned). Generate their labels by flipping noisy coin-flips from the true preference probability, then compare point-estimate serving vs posterior serving against held-out comparisons from the same true taste. Then run the key negative control: swap the real, data-dependent covariance $\\Lambda _{u}^{-1}$ for a constant fake covariance $c\\cdot I$ (scaled so the average spread matches) while keeping the mean unchanged, and rerun everything. Output: curves separating 'the spread helped' from 'we just got closer to the average', plus the negative-control trajectory.\n   - _Why_: The matched users separate 'the spread helped' from 'we just got closer to the average'; the negative control proves the gains come from the calibrated spread, not from anything else.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 校准的个性化奖励模型：用户方向上的后验分布\n\n**方法名称.** Calibrated User-Posterior Reward (CUP-RM)\n\n## 研究动机\n现代的个性化奖励模型（reward model, RM——给某个特定用户判断回答好坏的打分器）大都用同一套思路：先在所有人的数据上训练一个大的奖励模型，再为每个用户挂上一个小部件，用该用户的少量偏好标注拟合出来。问题在于：当一个用户只给了很少几个标注时，很多差别很大的『口味』都能同样好地拟合这几个标注。于是这个用户专属部件基本是在猜，并悄悄地退回到『所有人平均』这个默认值。像 MiCRo（一种按上下文路由的混合专家方法）和共享 low-rank adapter 方法都只给出一个奖励数值，却从不告诉你这个数值究竟反映了这位用户，还是只是披着外衣的群体平均。它们也从不决定接下来该问用户哪一个比较来消除困惑——只是被动地用碰巧到来的标注。\n\n现在正是时机，因为最近一批个性化 RM 工作都停在同一个地方：把每个用户放到一个共享空间里，报告一个点，却没有任何『有多确定』的度量。但恰恰是这些方法已经提供了我们需要的关键原料——一个学到的低维『奖励方向』空间——我们可以在其上廉价地建立一个真正的概率分布。2026 年的论文《The Reward Model Selection Crisis in Personalized Alignment》甚至表明，用普通的逐用户准确率来挑选部署用的奖励模型并不可靠，而这正是我们要修复的校准缺口。\n\n弥合这一缺口后会改变什么：奖励模型能在每个打分旁附带一个置信度，于是当系统对某个用户没把握时可以退回到安全的群体奖励（而不是自信地选错个性化回答），并且能运行一个聪明的循环，主动去问下一个最有用的比较。现有方法——MiCRo、shared-LoRA、PAL、meta-RM——由此获得一套有原则的冷启动方案和一个它们目前缺失的内置自检。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景（共享几何 + 评测）\n*未改动的支撑部分：冻结的骨干、共享子空间的拟合，以及基准评测。*\n\n1. 拿一个在所有人偏好数据上训练好的标准奖励模型（reward model, RM——给回答好坏打分的部件）并冻结它。把 $\\phi (x,y)$ 定义为模型在『提示+回答』序列最后一个 token 处的最后一层隐藏向量（7-8B 模型约 4096 维）——这正是现有打分头读取的那个向量——并保留该打分头，把它当作 $\\phi $ 的简单线性读出。这就是 HuggingFace 中标准的 sequence-classification 奖励模型设置。输入：带有标注者 ID 的提示-回答对。输出：冻结的特征提取器 $\\phi $ 和基础打分头。\n   - _为什么_: 我们把一切都建立在这个模型已经学到的奖励方向之上，而不是从零为每个用户重新训练。\n2. 在所有用户上一次性、通过交替优化拟合三样东西。(1) 共享基奖励方向 $w_{0}$（用现有打分头初始化）。(2) 一个小的 rank-r『用户子空间』U——默认 r=8 个方向，保持正交并按各自解释的偏好方差排序——用对每个标注者奖励梯度方向做主成分分析(Principal Component Analysis, PCA)来初始化。(3) 描述用户坐标通常如何分散的先验协方差 $\\Sigma $（用单位阵初始化）。交替进行：先求每个用户的最优坐标 $a_{u}$（一个很小的 8 维、类似 logistic 回归的拟合），再在所有人的数据上改进 $w_{0}$ 和 U，再把 $\\Sigma $ 重新估计为已拟合坐标的分散程度。每个用户的奖励 = 基方向加上其坐标 $a_{u}$ 经 U 映射、再与 $\\phi $ 内积。输出：$w_{0}$、U、$\\Sigma $。\n\n*每个用户的奖励等于共享基方向 $w_{0}$ 加上经学到的 rank-r 子空间 U 映射的用户坐标 $a_{u}$，再与骨干特征 $\\phi (x,y)$ 做内积。*\n$$ r_u(x,y) = \\langle w_0 + U a_u,\\; \\phi(x,y) \\rangle, \\qquad a_u \\in \\mathbb{R}^r \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这建立了所有用户共用的『地图』，而跨用户借用结构正是让一个标注稀疏的用户无需回答上百个问题就能被定位的关键。\n3. 在一个许多标注者带用户 ID 标注偏好的真实数据集（如 PRISM）上，测量随逐用户标注预算 K 增长的两件事：留出偏好准确率，以及个性化 best-of-n 胜率（用每种奖励方法从 8 个候选回答中挑最好的）。胜率统计的是：在用户的留出真实偏好下，本方法挑出的回答胜过基线挑出的回答的提示占比；当没有该具体对的人类标注时，用『该用户在其全部标注上拟合出的奖励』作为替身 oracle（冻结、对所有方法一致）。对照 MiCRo、shared-LoRA、PAL 和 meta-RM，各自给相同的 K 个标注和相同的候选回答。输出：准确率与胜率随 K 的曲线。\n   - _为什么_: 如果想法正确，我们的优势应当恰好在用户标注极少时最大，而主动提问版本应当比随机提问用更少标注达到目标准确率。\n\n### 校准的用户后验\n*把逐用户奖励从单个点变成一个后验，其熵 $H_{u}$ 是可服务的『证据 vs 默认』置信度。*\n\n4. 对某个有 K 个标注比较的用户，把每个比较对的特征差投影到用户子空间，得到一个 8 维向量 $g_{k}$。写出 Bradley-Terry 偏好似然（即标准的『被偏好项胜出的概率是分数差的 logistic 函数』）并配上先验 N(0, $\\Sigma )$，然后拟合用户坐标后验的高斯近似：均值 $\\mu _{u}$ 用几步 Newton 迭代求得，协方差 $\\Lambda _{u}^{-1}$ 的精度 $\\Lambda _{u}$ 等于先验精度 $\\Sigma ^{-1}$ 加上每个标注对贡献的项 $p(1- p)\\cdot g_{k} g_{k}^{T}$（即该对把估计收紧了多少）。输出：该用户的 $8\\times 8$ 均值与协方差。\n\n*用户坐标的 Laplace 后验精度 $\\Lambda _{u}$ 等于先验精度 $\\Sigma ^{-1}$ 加上该用户 K 个标注对的 Bradley-Terry Hessian 之和，在 U 投影后的特征差 $\\delta \\phi $ 上计算。*\n$$ p(a_u \\mid D_u) \\approx \\mathcal{N}(\\mu_u,\\; \\Lambda_u^{-1}), \\qquad \\Lambda_u = \\Sigma^{-1} + \\sum_{k=1}^{K} H_{\\mathrm{BT}}(\\Pi_U \\, \\delta\\phi_k) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 我们得到的不是一个『最佳猜测点』，而是一整个分布——而它的宽度正是以往方法丢弃掉的东西。\n5. 把奖励按后验均值打分服务出去，同时输出 $H_{u} = log det \\Lambda _{u}^{-1}$，即该用户分布的总体宽度。要据此进行回答选择，就对服务坐标做收缩：$a_{u}^{served} =$ (I $+ \\alpha \\cdot \\Lambda _{u}^{-1})^{-1} \\mu _{u}——$用户几乎没确定下来的方向（方差大）会被拉向群体默认 $w_{0}$，而有充分证据的方向得以保留；默认 $\\alpha  = 1$。【作者需决定：把不确定方向拉回群体默认的力度 $\\alpha $ 是一个需由作者设定的部署策略——它在个性化与安全之间权衡。】输出：服务出去的奖励，外加逐用户置信度 $H_{u}$。\n\n*核心读出量 $H_{u}$ 是后验的微分熵$——H_{u}$ 高表示所服务的奖励由先验主导（即静默默认），$H_{u}$ 低表示由用户证据支撑。*\n$$ H_u = \\log\\det \\Lambda_u^{-1} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 展度直接回答了『这是用户本人还是平均值？』，而据此行动会改变 best-of-n 循环中最终选出哪个回答。\n\n### 闭环主动提问\n*用后验主动挑选最能降低用户不确定性的下一个比较。*\n\n6. 每一轮，组装一个候选比较对池子（默认 256 个）：取若干 held-in 提示，每个提示配两个回答，把每对的特征差投影到用户子空间得到 g。给每个候选打分：标注它预计能让用户的不确定性下降多少——一个闭式的信息增益(BALD)分数 $½\\cdot log(1 + p(1- p)\\cdot g^{T} \\Lambda _{u}^{-1}$ g)，对每个候选只是一个廉价的 8 维二次型。把分数最高的一对问给用户，加入其回答，再重算后验（第 3 步）。输出：所选比较对与更新后的后验。\n\n*下一个比较取候选池中使 $H_{u}$ 期望下降最大的那一对——期望是在对未观测标签 $\\ell $ 的后验预测下求得，对 Gaussian-Laplace 后验有闭式解（即投影特征差方向的 BALD 信息增益）。*\n$$ (x,y_a,y_b)^{\\star} = \\arg\\max_{\\text{pool}} \\; \\mathbb{E}_{\\,\\ell \\sim p(\\ell)} \\big[\\, H_u - H_u^{(+\\ell)} \\,\\big] \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 下一步去问最有信息量的比较，能比随机提问用少得多的标注达到一个有把握的个性化奖励。\n\n### 可识别性审计 + 分离验证\n*证明展度是诚实的残差不可识别性，并用受控构造与负对照在经验上把它分离出来。*\n\n7. 证明被审计的论断。定义该用户的观测 Fisher 信息 $F_{u} = \\Sigma _{k} p(1- p)\\cdot g_{k} g_{k}^{T}——$它正是后验精度里那个数据项。证明：在它的零空间 $N_{u}$（任何被问及的对都无法区分的方向）上，偏好似然是平的，因此那里的后验精度只剩先验 $\\Sigma ^{-1}$：单个最佳猜测点在这些方向上只会照搬群体先验。明确指出到底能恢复什么——坐标只能确定到残差子空间 $N_{u}——$并证明后验剩余的不确定性落在 $N_{u}$ 上（可验证：后验协方差最宽的方向与 $F_{u}$ 信息最少的方向对齐）。输出：命名的残差子空间 $N_{u}$ 以及为『报告展度』提供依据的可识别性陈述。\n\n*用户坐标只能恢复到残差子空间 $N_{u}$，即投影到 U 中的逐用户标签 Fisher 信息 $F_{u}$ 的零空间；后验协方差把剩余的不确定性质量集中在 $N_{u}$ 上。*\n$$ N_u = \\mathrm{null}(F_u) \\subset \\mathbb{R}^r, \\qquad F_u = \\Pi_U \\, \\mathcal{I}_{\\mathrm{label}}(a_u) \\, \\Pi_U^{\\top} \\tag{5} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这是一个证明：展度不是麻烦，而是诚实、不可避免的残差——这正是为什么应当把它报告出来（而不是藏进一个点里）。\n8. 构造匹配的合成用户：他们拥有相同的真实口味 $a_{u}*$，但只在 (a) 标注数量 K 和 (b) 口味与群体平均的吻合程度（吻合者余弦$\\approx +0.8$，相反者$\\approx - 0.8$）上不同。用真实偏好概率做带噪声的抛硬币来生成他们的标注，再对照来自同一真实口味的留出比较，比较『点估计服务』与『后验服务』。然后做关键的负对照：把真实的、依赖数据的协方差 $\\Lambda _{u}^{-1}$ 换成一个常数假协方差 $c\\cdot I$（缩放到平均展度相匹配），同时保持均值不变，再把一切重跑一遍。输出：把『展度起了作用』和『只是更靠近平均值』区分开的曲线，以及负对照轨迹。\n   - _为什么_: 匹配用户把『是展度起了作用』和『只是更靠近了平均值』区分开；负对照证明收益来自校准过的展度，而不是别的什么。\n\n"},{"id":"94","run_dir":"run_prompt94_plesssample","index":94,"title":"Self-Truncating Decoding: a knob-free token cutoff from per-step logit separation","title_zh":"Self-Truncating Decoding：从单步 logit 分离中得到的无超参 token 截断","method_name":"Self-Truncating Decoding (STD)","hook":"Every competitive decoder still hides a tuned scalar (top-p's p, top-n-sigma's n, min-p's floor) applied uniformly to per-step distributions whose shape changes at every token; we show the truncation boundary can instead be the unique optimizer of a scale-invariant separation criterion evaluated on that step's own sorted logits, removing the only remaining hyperparameter while matching tuned baselines.","anchor_pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","anchor_pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","domain_category":"LLM Reasoning & Decoding","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved decoding rule sets its truncation boundary from a quantity the current step's distribution alone determines: every leaf (top-n-sigma's n, nucleus p, min-p's floor, contrastive alpha) applies an exogenous global scalar to a per-step distribution whose shape varies, so at every step the cut is mis-placed relative to where that step's informative mass actually ends, and no leaf produces a per-step cutoff that is invariant to a free knob. (additive)","pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","sub_pattern":"C23 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by re-specifying the conventionally-frozen per-step keep-set rule of the autoregressive refinement chain: instead of applying an inherited scalar cutoff, the keep-set is re-derived as the optimizer of an intrinsic, scale-invariant two-segment separation criterion computed on this step's own sorted logits, so the boundary location is produced by the step's distribution and carries no exposed knob.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved decoding paper questions whether a truncation cutoff must be a SET POINT at all, rather than emerging as the solution of a per-step objective over the distribution: every leaf inherits from the shared nucleus/threshold ancestor the unexamined assumption that decoding = (compute scores) then (apply a chosen cutoff), and none tests whether the cutoff can instead be the argmin/argmax of an intrinsic criterion evaluated on that step's distribution. (subtractive)","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by auditing the keep/discard selection rule shared by every nucleus/threshold descendant and naming its load-bearing structural precondition (a fixed exogenous cutoff scalar / proximity-to-a-reference quantile), then pivoting selection-with-a-set-point into selection-as-the-optimum-of-an-intrinsic-criterion, with the re-derived certificate being a reparameterization-invariance guarantee: the keep-set is provably unchanged under any monotone-affine rescaling of the logit axis, which is the property a truly knob-free decoder must satisfy and which the set-point rules do not.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"LLM text generation / decoding (token-sampling strategies for autoregressive language models)","n_papers":51,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":27},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":11,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"DistServe: Disaggregating Prefill and Decoding for Goodput-optimized Large Language Model Serving"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Unsupervised Distractor Generation via Large Language Model Distilling and Counterfactual Contrastive Decoding"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Multi-Stage Vision Token Dropping: Towards Efficient Multimodal Large Language Model"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Embers of autoregression show how large language models are shaped by the problem they are trained to solve"},{"source":"openalex","title":"A Survey of Hallucination Problems Based on Large Language Models"},{"source":"openalex","title":"LoongServe: Efficiently Serving Long-Context Large Language Models with Elastic Sequence Parallelism"}],"more":5},{"year":2025,"n":31,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"CITER: Collaborative Inference for Efficient Large Language Model Decoding with Token-Level Routing"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Dimple: Discrete Diffusion Multimodal Large Language Model with Parallel Decoding"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Active Layer-Contrastive Decoding Reduces Hallucination in Large Language Model Generation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Energy Considerations of Large Language Model Inference and Efficiency Optimizations"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Impact of decoding strategies on GPU energy usage in large language model text generation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Serialized Output Prompting for Large Language Model-based Multi-Talker Speech Recognition"}],"more":25},{"year":2026,"n":9,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"How Contrastive Decoding Enhances Large Audio Language Models?"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Component-Aware Self-Speculative Decoding in Hybrid Language Models"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Anchored Decoding: Provably Reducing Copyright Risk for Any Language Model"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Conversational Control with Ontologies for Large Language Models: A Lightweight Framework for Constrained Generation"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Introducing MELI: the Mandarin-English Language Interview Corpus"}],"more":3}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":14,"share":0.275},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":9,"share":0.176},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":7,"share":0.137},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":7,"share":0.137},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":5,"share":0.098},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":4,"share":0.078},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":4,"share":0.078},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":4,"share":0.078}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Every competitive open-vocabulary decoding rule in the retrieved frontier sets its truncation boundary or contrast strength from a fixed, externally-supplied scalar rather than from a quantity the per-step distribution itself determines: top-n-sigma (openalex:W4412945431) keeps tokens whose logit exceeds max_logit minus n*sigma but n is a hand-set multiplier and the paper still reports tuning it; contrastive/layer methods such as Active Layer-Contrastive Decoding (semanticscholar:dd2c4dfb1495af2951b4b3b783474537abf45f43) and Mixture-of-Decoding (openalex:W4412888466) gate their contrast on a threshold (alpha, an attention-consistency cutoff) that is selected offline; and even adaptive plug-in methods like Anchored Decoding (arxiv:2602.07120v2) fix a proximity/mixing bound in advance. The structural failure is that the SHAPE of the next-token distribution varies enormously across steps (a near-deterministic syntactic slot versus a high-entropy semantic branch) and across models (post-training sharpens logits differently), yet a single global cutoff is applied to all steps, so any one setting is simultaneously too aggressive at confident steps (clipping valid continuations) and too permissive at flat steps (admitting the noisy tail) — and because the cutoff is exogenous, the only repair currently available is per-model, per-task re-tuning, which the comparative studies (openalex:W7108657319, openalex:W4416034700) document as the dominant practical cost of deploying any given decoder.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4412945431","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Top-n-sigma proves a statistical separation in pre-softmax logit space between an informative bulk and a flat noise region (and the min-p / top-(1-p) equivalence under uniform logits), then keeps only tokens within n*sigma of the max logit, achieving temperature-INVARIANT (not merely temperature-robust) token selection. Its residue, confirmed from the method section, is that n is still an exogenous, fixed multiplier applied uniformly and the cut is a fixed-WIDTH band around the max rather than a boundary placed where this step's bulk empirically ends, so the keep-set size is not derived from the per-step separation the paper itself characterizes and n must be chosen rather than read off the distribution."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:dd2c4dfb1495af2951b4b3b783474537abf45f43","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Active Layer-Contrastive Decoding casts when-to-contrast as a sequential decision and contrasts deep-vs-shallow layer logits to suppress hallucination, restricting the contrast to a head set defined by alpha*max(q_N). Its residue is that both the head-set cutoff alpha and the learned when-to-contrast policy are fitted offline, so the contrast strength is not read from the divergence present at the current step and the method adds trained components rather than self-calibrating."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4412888466","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Mixture-of-Decoding adaptively switches between complementing and contrasting attended-image-token outputs based on output consistency, an attention-driven adaptivity. Its residue is that the switch criterion is a consistency threshold selected on validation data and the method is specific to vision-language attention, so it does not give a modality-agnostic, knob-free rule for how strongly to truncate or contrast at an arbitrary text-decoding step."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.07120v2","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Anchored Decoding adaptively mixes a risky LM with a safe LM keeping generation within a bounded KL proximity, using per-step KL as a memorization proxy. Its residue is that the proximity/mixing bound is a fixed budget set in advance rather than inferred from the current step's distribution, so the 'adaptivity' is a scheduled spend of a preset quantity, not a hyperparameter-free response to the live distribution."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"LLM text generation / decoding (token-sampling strategies for autoregressive language models)","venue":"ICLR / NeurIPS / ACL","time":"2026","data":["open-ended generation benchmarks (e.g. open-ended story/essay generation, WritingPrompts)","factuality/QA benchmarks (TruthfulQA, FActScore-style)","reasoning benchmarks (GSM8K, MATH)","MT/summarization for diversity-quality tradeoff"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher comfortable with logit-level interventions and information-theoretic analysis; no large-scale pretraining required","preference":"both","baseline":"temperature + top-p (nucleus) sampling; min-p sampling; top-n-sigma; contrastive/DoLa-style decoding","limitation":"every competitive decoding method exposes at least one continuous cutoff/strength hyperparameter (temperature, p, the n in top-n-sigma, the contrastive alpha) that must be tuned per model and per task, and there is no decoding rule that sets its own truncation/strength entirely from the per-step distribution with no exposed knob","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared audit lens is the keep/discard selection rule that every retrieved decoder inherits from the nucleus/threshold ancestor: 'compute scores, then keep the prefix admitted by a chosen scalar cutoff.' LEG 1 (generative_process_redesign, C23) liberates that frozen rule. At decode step t let z_(1) >= z_(2) >= ... >= z_(V) be the pre-softmax logits sorted descending (V = vocabulary size; logits are the model's own readout, no external oracle). The structural property licensing the redesign — established by top-n-sigma (openalex:W4412945431), which proves a separation in logit space between an informative bulk and a flat noise region — is that each step's sorted-logit sequence contains a single empirically locatable bulk/tail boundary. We re-specify the keep-set K(t) as the optimizer of a parameter-free two-segment separation criterion S over the cut index k in {1,...,V}: K(t) = argmax_k Sep(k), where Sep(k) is the between-group-over-within-group variance ratio (an Otsu / Jenks natural-breaks objective) of the split {z_(1..k)} vs {z_(tail)} computed on the gaps g_i = z_(i) - z_(i+1) of the sorted logits. Crucially Sep depends ONLY on the gaps g_i, which are differences of logits, so any transform z -> a*z + b with a>0 (temperature 1/a, additive calibration b) scales every gap by a and leaves argmax_k Sep(k) unchanged — the keep-set is invariant by construction. To bound cost, Sep need not be evaluated over all V: we evaluate only over k <= K_max where K_max is the smallest index past which the cumulative gap mass falls below the running gap mean (a closed-form early stop, not a tunable), making the per-step overhead O(K_max log K_max). LEG 2 (assumption_audit_and_pivot, C11) supplies the certificate that licenses Leg 1: it states the inherited assumption ('the keep-set requires a fixed exogenous cutoff') as load-bearing — striking it is exactly what removes the tuning axis — and pivots selection-with-a-set-point into selection-as-argmax-of-Sep, then re-derives the performance currency as an INVARIANCE guarantee plus a non-degeneracy lemma: (i) the admitted-token set is exactly preserved under monotone-affine reparameterization of the score axis (the property every fixed-cutoff rule violates, which top-n-sigma only approximates by holding n fixed across temperatures), and (ii) on a distribution with a genuine bulk/tail gap the argmax of Sep coincides with that gap rather than degenerating to k=1 or k=V. The two legs share one object — the per-step sorted-logit gap sequence g_i — so they read as one paper: Leg 2 audits the rule that operates on g_i and certifies the invariant, Leg 1 builds the rule that reads g_i and ships the runnable decoder. The load-bearing variable is the criterion-selected boundary location k*(t) = argmax_k Sep(k); the whole mechanism claim is that placing the cut AT this intrinsic separation point (not at an exogenous quantile) is what recovers tuned-baseline quality with no knob.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The two gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules: both operate on the single per-step object (the sorted-logit gap sequence), so the audit leg is not a second experiment but the certificate that makes the construction's 'hyperparameter-free' claim checkable (the invariance property) rather than asserted — this is why I kept them as one shared_audit paper instead of splitting the invariance into a separate measurement leg (which I deferred upstream). Alternatives considered and rejected: (a) an entropy/typicality budget per step — rejected as a regression onto collateral node c1 (it re-introduces an exogenous typicality target, i.e. a knob); (b) a sample-then-rerank / MBR formulation — rejected as a regression onto collateral node c0 (different mechanism, adds a reranking loop, and the inner sampler still needs a knobbed cutoff); (c) learning the cutoff with a small head (as Active Layer-Contrastive does) — rejected because a learned threshold is still fitted offline and is not invariant to score-axis reparameterization. The avoided nodes (c0 MBR, c1 typicality budget, and the n3 'chosen cutoff' ancestor) are recorded here per Hard rule 2; the chosen object (argmax of a scale-invariant separation criterion on logit gaps) lands on none of them because it derives the boundary from the step's own gap structure with no exposed target.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on 2-3 open-weight LLMs (e.g. a 7B and a 13B instruct model) decode the same prompts from TruthfulQA, an open-ended generation set, and GSM8K under Self-Truncating Decoding versus tuned top-p, min-p, and top-n-sigma, sweeping temperature from 0.7 to 2.0, and measure factuality / MAUVE / exact-match accuracy. If the candidate works, Self-Truncating Decoding matches the BEST per-task-tuned baseline at every temperature with a SINGLE fixed configuration (no per-model/per-task tuning), and its quality-versus-temperature curve stays flat while fixed-cutoff baselines degrade as temperature rises (factuality and MAUVE decrease for top-p/top-n-sigma at high T, stay roughly constant for ours). The named load-bearing variable is the criterion-selected boundary location k*(t) = argmax_k Sep(k). Negative control: replace k*(t) with a random cut index matched to the same expected keep-set size E[k*] (severing boundary placement from the separation point while holding keep-set size and the rest of the pipeline fixed) — this should drive the downstream task-outcome metrics (factuality, MAUVE, GSM8K accuracy) back down to or below the untuned-baseline level; if generation quality is unchanged when the boundary is randomized at fixed keep-set size, then placement at the separation point is not the mechanism and the contribution is merely an adaptive-size effect. Positive control: a decoder that changes nothing except using k*(t) for the cut should recover most of the full method's quality gain, identifying the separation-placed boundary as the sufficient mechanism.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4412945431","delta":"Top-n-sigma proves the bulk/tail separation exists and cuts at a FIXED width n*sigma around the max (n still tuned, keep-set size set by n); we instead place the cut at the argmax of a scale-invariant separation criterion on the logit gaps, so the keep-set size is the separation point's output rather than a width parameter, and we prove exact invariance under affine logit reparameterization rather than only empirical temperature-robustness."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:dd2c4dfb1495af2951b4b3b783474537abf45f43","delta":"Active Layer-Contrastive Decoding learns an offline policy plus an alpha head-set cutoff to decide contrast; we add no trained component and derive the keep-set purely from the current step's sorted-logit gaps, and we certify a reparameterization-invariance property the learned-threshold approach does not possess."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4412888466","delta":"Mixture-of-Decoding switches strategy by a validation-set consistency threshold specific to vision-language attention; ours is modality-agnostic and threshold-free, selecting the boundary by an intrinsic separation argmax with no validation-fitted switch."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.07120v2","delta":"Anchored Decoding spends a preset KL proximity budget against a safe LM; we infer the keep-set from the live distribution with no preset budget and require no auxiliary LM, and our adaptivity is a derived per-step optimum rather than a scheduled spend of a fixed quantity."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4412945431","what_step_was_missed":"Top-n-sigma constructs the cut as a fixed-width band z >= max_logit - n*sigma, where n is supplied; it never constructs the boundary as the OPTIMIZER of a separation criterion over the per-step logit gaps, so it cannot let the keep-set size be determined by where the bulk empirically ends and must carry n. The missing substantive step is deriving and proving that the argmax of a scale-invariant two-segment separation objective on the sorted-logit gaps both (i) coincides with the bulk/tail boundary they characterize and (ii) is exactly invariant to affine reparameterization of the logit axis — an object and an invariance proof their fixed-width construction does not produce."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":294,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"No hard-floor rule fired: gap_closure_reject_check is borderline with no lesson candidate_match: yes, anti_pattern_check matched_pattern_id is null, and the paper_pointed_threat (arxiv:2604.11012v1, Min-k Sampling) is competing-not-exact and addressable_via a differentiation edit. Revise is driven by recipe_application_check.entries[0].verdict = bypassed — core_mechanism's gap-1 leg performs the parent 'liberate a fixed component' gist plus a reframe-as-solvable-object natural-breaks argmax rather than C23's diffusion/flow refinement-chain signature move — compounded by the gap-1 Reject lesson 'failing to beat the strongest fast-sampling alternative dooms the move' now that the directly competing Min-k Sampling is absent from differentiation_from_lit. Both are load-bearing (the cluster tactic carrying the construction, and the novelty delta against the closest neighbor), so they require fix rather than mere surfacing.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved decoding rule sets its truncation boundary from a quantity the current step's distribution alone determines: every leaf (top-n-sigma's n, nucleus p, min-p's floor, contrastive alpha) applies an exogenous global scalar to a per-step distribution whose shape varies, so at every step the cut is mis-placed relative to where that step's informative mass actually ends, and no leaf produces a per-step cutoff that is invariant to a free knob. (additive)","main_pattern":"generative_process_redesign","sub_pattern":"C23 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is treating 'I re-specified component X' as self-evident novelty: a single local swap that neither re-derives the chain nor demonstrates a regime the dominant accelerated alternative cannot already reach, so the contribution reads as dominated rather than enabling; a second shape is the hidden artifact whose cost cancels the advertised gain.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Re-specifying the chain's starting distribution is sound but worthless if a dominant accelerator already reaches one or two steps — failing to beat the strongest fast-sampling alternative dooms the move regardless of its elegance.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The candidate's falsification_prediction does benchmark against the strongest tuned baselines (top-p, min-p, top-n-sigma), but a newer dominant alternative on the exact same axis (Min-k Sampling, arxiv:2604.11012v1, local-logit-shape truncation with proven temperature invariance) is absent from differentiation_from_lit, so the 'beat the strongest existing method' bar is only partially met."},{"lesson_quoted":"Substituting one in-support approximation for another without theoretical depth or a failure-regime analysis reads as a narrow heuristic swap rather than a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism supplies an exact affine-reparameterization-invariance proof plus a non-degeneracy lemma and names the high-temperature failure regime where fixed-cutoff rules destabilize, so it is not a depth-free heuristic swap."},{"lesson_quoted":"A redesign that silently depends on an extra artifact — access to a simulator/dynamics model, or a separately trained auxiliary network — has its claimed efficiency cancelled by the hidden cost once a reviewer surfaces it.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The rule reads only the current step's sorted-logit gaps with no auxiliary LM, no trained head, and a closed-form K_max early-stop, so there is no hidden artifact whose cost cancels the gain."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved decoding paper questions whether a truncation cutoff must be a SET POINT at all, rather than emerging as the solution of a per-step objective over the distribution: every leaf inherits from the shared nucleus/threshold ancestor the unexamined assumption that decoding = (compute scores) then (apply a chosen cutoff), and none tests whether the cutoff can instead be the argmin/argmax of an intrinsic criterion evaluated on that step's distribution. (subtractive)","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The dominant failure is substituting one selection rule for another that performs better empirically while omitting the theorem that explains when and why it wins; a second shape is pivoting an assumption the community regards as a reasonable modeling choice rather than a genuine restriction.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Substituting one selection heuristic for another without a theorem stating when and why it wins reads as an engineering combination, not a contribution, no matter how clean the empirical gain.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The audit leg's deliverable IS a theorem — an exact monotone-affine invariance guarantee plus a non-degeneracy lemma — not a bare empirical swap, so the 'no theorem' failure does not fire."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pivoting an assumption the community treats as a reasonable modeling choice — rather than first proving it a genuine restriction — leaves both motivation and novelty in doubt.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The pivoted assumption ('the keep-set requires a fixed exogenous cutoff scalar') is shown load-bearing because striking it removes the only tuning axis, but a reviewer could argue an exposed cutoff with low sensitivity (Min-k) is already a 'reasonable modeling choice', so the genuine-restriction defense is real but not yet airtight against the newest neighbor."},{"lesson_quoted":"A re-derived guarantee whose binding constant is dataset-dependent and cannot be controlled by the practitioner is vacuous in the worst case and fails to convince.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The invariance guarantee is parameter-free and exact (holds for every a>0,b by construction of the gap-only criterion), so it carries no dataset-dependent binding constant."},{"lesson_quoted":"Unlocking a new capability by violating an assumption while ignoring a protective property it guarded — detectability, validity, identifiability — invites rejection on the overlooked side effect rather than the headline result.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The non-degeneracy lemma plus the explicit near-deterministic (k*=1) and near-uniform guards show the pivot does not silently break the keep-set's basic validity, so no protected property is dropped."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No Reject lesson is candidate_match: yes, so the check is borderline, not triggered. The weight sits on the gap-1 (generative_process_redesign / C23) lesson 'failing to beat the strongest fast-sampling alternative dooms the move' because a directly competing dominant method on the same axis (Min-k Sampling, local-logit-shape truncation with proven temperature invariance) is absent from differentiation_from_lit, and the gap-2 (assumption_audit_and_pivot / C11) borderline that the pivoted assumption may be read as a benign modeling choice rather than a genuine restriction in light of that same neighbor."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved decoding rule sets its truncation boundary from a quantity the current step's distribution alone determines: every leaf (top-n-sigma's n, nucleus p, min-p's floor, contrastive alpha) applies an exogenous global scalar to a per-step distribution whose shape varies, so at every step the cut is mis-placed relative to where that step's informative mass actually ends, and no leaf produces a per-step cutoff that is invariant to a free knob. (additive)","sub_pattern":"C23 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Reach inside an iterative refinement (diffusion/flow) chain and re-specify one of its conventionally-frozen internal components — the terminal prior/endpoint, the per-step distribution family, the noise/solver discretization, the initial seed, the forward noising process, or the conditioning-injection checkpoint — then re-derive the chain around the new choice, the payoff almost always being collapsing hundreds of steps into a handful or training-free retargeting of a frozen backbone.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism re-specifies the per-step keep/discard truncation rule of autoregressive decoding (Step 1-4: derive K(t)=argmax_k Sep(k) over sorted-logit gaps). This performs the PARENT's generic idea ('liberate a fixed generative component' = the frozen cutoff rule), but NOT the C23 cluster's distinctive tactic: the cluster's objects are the internal degrees of freedom of a diffusion/flow refinement chain (prior, per-step distribution family, solver/schedule, seed, forward kernel, conditioning checkpoint) and its signature payoff is step-count collapse / training-free retargeting of a frozen backbone via a re-derived transition operator. A truncation boundary of an autoregressive softmax is none of those swapped objects, and the mechanism the candidate actually performs — recasting 'where does this step's informative mass end' as a one-dimensional Otsu/Jenks natural-breaks partition solved by argmax — is a reframe-as-solvable-object move, which is in fact the pattern Phase 2.1 chose as the anchor (chosen_pattern_id = reframe_as_solvable_object) before Phase 2.2 bound it to the generative_process_redesign alternate. The C23 signature operation is absent.","verdict":"bypassed"},{"gap":"No retrieved decoding paper questions whether a truncation cutoff must be a SET POINT at all, rather than emerging as the solution of a per-step objective over the distribution: every leaf inherits from the shared nucleus/threshold ancestor the unexamined assumption that decoding = (compute scores) then (apply a chosen cutoff), and none tests whether the cutoff can instead be the argmin/argmax of an intrinsic criterion evaluated on that step's distribution. (subtractive)","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Center on a selection/acquisition/query/stopping rule, name the single load-bearing assumption baked into its criterion or required structure (a fixed count, an anchor, proximity-to-a-reference-distribution as a quality proxy), then either relax that crutch and re-prove the guarantee or reframe the selection task into a different problem class — the invariant deliverable being a re-derived performance certificate (regret/competitive ratio/approximation/budget) shown to match or beat the pre-pivot baseline.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism's LEG 2 centers exactly on the keep/discard SELECTION rule, names its load-bearing assumption ('the keep-set requires a fixed exogenous cutoff scalar / proximity-to-a-reference quantile'), pivots selection-with-a-set-point into selection-as-argmax-of-an-intrinsic-criterion, and re-derives the performance currency as an exact monotone-affine reparameterization-invariance certificate plus a non-degeneracy lemma — the cluster's signature 'name the assumption, pivot it, re-derive the certificate' move is present and load-bearing.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"bypassed","reasoning":"The gap-2 assumption_audit_and_pivot / C11 leg genuinely performs the cluster's name-pivot-recertify move, but the gap-1 generative_process_redesign / C23 leg bypasses the cluster's distinctive tactic: its objects are diffusion/flow refinement-chain internals (prior/schedule/seed/forward-kernel/conditioning), whereas the candidate re-specifies an autoregressive softmax truncation rule and the actual operation it performs (a 1-D natural-breaks partition solved by argmax) is a reframe-as-solvable-object move — the pattern Phase 2.1 originally chose as anchor."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["generative_process_redesign","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; the candidate's composition {generative_process_redesign, assumption_audit_and_pivot} contains no heterogeneous_decomposition, so no anti-pattern matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"arxiv:2604.11012v1","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"Min-k Sampling (Decoupling Truncation from Temperature Scaling via Relative Logit Dynamics) attacks the candidate's exact axis: it 'analyzes the local shape of the sorted logit distribution to identify semantic cliffs — sharp transitions from high-confidence core tokens to uncertain long-tail tokens', computes a 'position-weighted relative decay rate' to 'dynamically determine truncation boundaries at each generation step', and 'formally prove[s] strict temperature invariance' with empirically low hyperparameter sensitivity. This overlaps the candidate's two headline claims — a per-step truncation boundary derived from the step's own sorted-logit shape, and a temperature/scaling-invariance proof — so the candidate's claim of being the FIRST to derive an intrinsic, scale-invariant per-step cutoff no longer stands unqualified; the candidate must instead carry the contrast as its central delta. The candidate is NOT subsumed because (i) Min-k still exposes a k parameter (it claims low sensitivity, not zero exposed knobs), whereas the candidate exposes none; (ii) the candidate's boundary is the argmax of a between/within-segment variance ratio (Otsu/Jenks natural-breaks model selection) rather than a position-weighted decay-rate threshold; and (iii) the candidate proves EXACT invariance under any monotone-affine logit transform a*z+b, a strictly stronger property than temperature-only invariance. The overlap is competing, not exact-mechanism, so it is addressable rather than fatal.","addressable_via":"Add an explicit differentiation_from_lit[] entry for arxiv:2604.11012v1 stating the three deltas above (zero exposed knobs vs a still-exposed k; variance-ratio model-selection argmax vs position-weighted decay-rate threshold; exact affine-reparameterization invariance vs temperature-only invariance), so the candidate's headline shifts from 'first intrinsic per-step cutoff' to 'the knob-FREE, affine-invariant model-selection formulation that the decay-rate threshold and the still-exposed k of Min-k do not deliver'."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism (gap-1 / LEG 1 framing) and gap_closure[0].how_closed","issue":"recipe_application_check.entries[0].verdict = bypassed — the gap-1 leg cites C23 (Liberate a Fixed Generative Component) but core_mechanism performs the parent's generic idea plus a reframe-as-solvable-object natural-breaks argmax, not C23's diffusion/flow refinement-chain-internal re-specification tactic. The sub_pattern cannot be swapped to a sibling under generative_process_redesign because neither C15 (repurpose a pretrained generative model as a supervision source) nor C24 (port the refinement mechanism to a new output domain) matches the move core_mechanism actually performs; the matching tactic lives under a different parent (reframe_as_solvable_object), which Phase 3.3 cannot change. Therefore rework the gap-1 leg's wording so it instantiates the C23 cluster tactic as faithfully as the autoregressive setting allows.","fix_direction":"Rewrite the LEG 1 description (and gap_closure[0].how_closed) to perform C23's distinctive move rather than the parent gist: (a) name the conventionally-frozen internal component of the autoregressive GENERATIVE chain being liberated as the per-step keep-set transition operator and state precisely WHY it was fixed (an inherited tractability convenience — a single scalar cutoff is cheap and model-agnostic — not an actual task constraint); (b) cite the explicit STRUCTURAL PROPERTY of the task that licenses the re-specification, namely the empirically-located single bulk/tail gap in each step's sorted-logit sequence established by top-n-sigma (openalex:W4412945431), so the swap is licensed by task structure rather than by 'this variable can be changed'; (c) RE-DERIVE the decode step around the new component — show the criterion-selected keep-set K(t) still defines a valid truncated next-token distribution and state what the inherited scalar-cutoff operator provably could not do (place the boundary at the step's intrinsic separation point) that the re-derived operator does; (d) explicitly account that the redesign smuggles in NO extra artifact (no auxiliary LM, no trained head; closed-form K_max early-stop) and benchmark the gain against the STRONGEST existing per-step-shape truncation method, now including Min-k Sampling, not merely the un-adaptive nucleus baseline. Do NOT touch falsification_prediction or compute_budget (kill-switch, byte-identical).","issue_severity_note":"If, after this rewrite, the leg still cannot honestly read as the C23 diffusion/flow refinement-chain tactic (i.e. the autoregressive truncation genuinely belongs to reframe_as_solvable_object, the Phase 2.1 anchor), that is a gap-level parent mismatch outside Phase 3.3 scope and the run should route back to regenerate Phase 2.1+2.2 binding gap-1 to reframe_as_solvable_object (C00/C21/C27) instead. Prefer the faithful rewrite first."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit[]","issue":"paper_pointed_threat.threat_paper_id = arxiv:2604.11012v1 (Min-k Sampling) — the closest competing neighbor on the candidate's exact axis (per-step sorted-logit-shape truncation with a temperature-invariance proof) is absent from differentiation_from_lit, leaving the candidate's novelty claim undefended against it.","fix_direction":"Append a differentiation_from_lit entry {\"paper_id\": \"arxiv:2604.11012v1\", \"delta\": ...} stating the three substantive deltas from paper_pointed_threat.addressable_via: (i) Min-k still exposes a k parameter (claims low sensitivity, not zero exposed knobs) whereas the candidate exposes NO cutoff knob; (ii) Min-k places the cut via a position-weighted relative decay-rate threshold over local logits, whereas the candidate places it at the argmax of a between/within-segment variance ratio (an Otsu/Jenks natural-breaks model-selection objective), so the keep-set size is the solved object rather than a decay-rate cutoff; (iii) Min-k proves temperature invariance only, whereas the candidate proves EXACT invariance under any monotone-affine logit transform a*z+b (temperature AND additive calibration), a strictly stronger reparameterization guarantee. Keep the delta substantive (what we construct/prove that Min-k does not), not 'we use a different pattern'."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism (LEG 1 framing) and gap_closure[0].how_closed","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Reworded the gap-1 leg to perform C23's distinctive 'liberate a fixed internal generative component + re-derive the chain around it' move: it now names the frozen autoregressive component (the per-step keep-set transition operator), states why it was inherited as fixed (a tractability convenience, not a task constraint), cites the task structural property (the empirically-located single bulk/tail gap from top-n-sigma) that licenses the swap, re-derives the decode step around the new operator stating what the inherited scalar-cutoff operator provably could not do, accounts for zero smuggled artifacts, and benchmarks against the strongest per-step-shape truncation method including Min-k Sampling."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit[]","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Appended a differentiation_from_lit entry for arxiv:2604.11012v1 (Min-k Sampling) stating the three substantive deltas: zero exposed knobs vs a still-exposed k; between/within variance-ratio natural-breaks argmax vs a position-weighted decay-rate threshold; exact monotone-affine reparameterization invariance vs temperature-only invariance."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Self-Truncating Decoding: a knob-free token cutoff from per-step logit separation\n\n**Method.** Self-Truncating Decoding (STD)\n\n## Motivation\nWhen a large language model (LLM) writes text, at every word it produces a long list of scores (logits) — one per possible next token — and a 'truncation rule' decides which tokens are allowed before one is randomly picked. Every popular rule today (nucleus / top-p sampling, min-p, and top-n-sigma) needs a number you must set by hand: how much probability mass to keep, how far below the top to cut, and so on. The trouble is that the shape of that score list changes dramatically from word to word (sometimes only one word fits; sometimes hundreds do) and from model to model, yet a single hand-set number is applied to all of them — so any one setting is too strict where the model is confident and too loose where it is uncertain. The only fix people have is to re-tune that number for every new model and task, which is the main hidden cost of using any decoder.\n\nThis is solvable now because a recent method, top-n-sigma (arXiv 2025-01), showed that the sorted score list always has a clean break between an 'informative' group of strong candidates and a 'flat noise' tail, and it used that to become insensitive to temperature. A concurrent method, Min-k Sampling (arXiv 2026-04), independently looks at the local shape of the sorted scores to find that break and also proves temperature-insensitivity — but it still exposes a number (k) and finds the break with a hand-designed decay-rate rule rather than by solving for the best break directly.\n\nOur idea, Self-Truncating Decoding (STD), removes the last hand-set number entirely. At each word we look only at the GAPS between consecutive sorted scores and find the single cut that best splits the strong-candidate group from the flat tail, using a classic parameter-free 'natural breaks' criterion (the same idea used to choose bins on a map). The cut location — and therefore how many tokens are kept — is read off the distribution instead of chosen. Because the criterion uses only gaps, multiplying or shifting all the scores (which is exactly what temperature and calibration do) leaves the chosen set of kept tokens completely unchanged: we can PROVE the kept set is the same, not just observe it.\n\nIf this works, deploying a decoder no longer carries a per-model, per-task tuning cost, and the field finally gets a precise, checkable definition of what 'hyperparameter-free decoding' should mean — that the set of allowed tokens does not change under any rescaling that preserves the ranking — against which any method, including top-n-sigma and Min-k, can be tested rather than just asserted.\n\n## Method\n### Knob-free boundary solver\n*Derive the per-step truncation boundary as the argmax of a parameter-free separation criterion over logit gaps, with no exposed knob.*\n\n1. Sort the scores from highest to lowest (and remember which token id each came from), then compute the gap between each adjacent pair (Eq. (1)). Set a search ceiling $K_{max}$ automatically in a single downward pass: keep a running average of the gaps seen so far, and stop at the first place where the next gap stays below that running average for three indices in a row; if that never happens, cap the search at 256 positions. This limits how far we look without adding anything to tune.\n\n*The per-step object the whole method reads: the descending-sorted pre-softmax logits $z_(1..V)$ and their consecutive gaps $g_{i}.$ Working on gaps (differences of logits) is what makes every later quantity invariant to an additive shift of the logit axis.*\n$$ g_i = z_{(i)} - z_{(i+1)}, \\qquad z_{(1)} \\geq z_{(2)} \\geq \\cdots \\geq z_{(V)} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Looking at gaps (differences) rather than raw scores is what later guarantees temperature/calibration cannot change the answer, and the automatic ceiling keeps it fast without adding a knob.\n2. For each possible cut position (from 2 up to just below $K_{max}),$ measure how cleanly that cut splits the gaps into a strong-candidate head and a flat tail, using a between-group-versus-within-group variance ratio — the classic 'natural breaks' / Otsu criterion (Eq. (2)). Concretely, the numerator rewards a large jump between the two groups' average gaps and the denominator penalizes spread inside each group. Add a tiny relative smoothing term to the denominator so a one-element group does not blow up the ratio. This score has nothing to tune; it reads only the gaps.\n\n*The parameter-free separation criterion: a between-group-over-within-group variance ratio (an Otsu / Jenks natural-breaks objective) of the gap sequence split into a head ${g_{1}..g_{k}}$ with $mean \\mu _{1}$ and a tail with $mean \\mu _{2}$; $\\mu $ is the overall gap mean and $n_{1},n_{2}$ the segment sizes. It contains no tunable.*\n$$ \\mathrm{Sep}(k) = \\frac{\\sigma^2_{\\mathrm{between}}(k)}{\\sigma^2_{\\mathrm{within}}(k)} = \\frac{n_1 (\\mu_1 - \\mu)^2 + n_2 (\\mu_2 - \\mu)^2}{\\sum_{i \\leq k}(g_i - \\mu_1)^2 + \\sum_{i > k}(g_i - \\mu_2)^2} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A good cut is one where the within-group spread is small and the jump between groups is large — exactly what this ratio measures — so the best cut marks the real boundary between plausible and noise tokens.\n3. Pick the cut position with the highest separation score (Eq. (3)); if two positions tie, take the smaller one so the kept set is the more conservative choice. The kept tokens are the ones at sorted ranks 1 through that position, mapped back to their real token ids; set every other token's score to negative infinity. This chosen position — and therefore how many tokens are kept — is the key quantity that carries the whole method's claim.\n\n*The keep-set is the top k*(t) tokens, where k*(t) is the cut index that maximizes the separation criterion. This is the load-bearing variable: the boundary location is the solver's output, not a chosen scalar.*\n$$ k^*(t) = \\arg\\max_{1 \\leq k \\leq K_{\\max}} \\mathrm{Sep}(k), \\qquad K(t) = \\{ \\text{top-}k^*(t) \\text{ tokens} \\} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This makes the keep-set SIZE an output of the data, not a hand-set width like top-n-sigma's fixed band, which is the substantive difference.\n\n### Drop-in decode integration\n*Slot the solver into the standard decode loop so the kept set feeds the unchanged sampling step.*\n\n4. Inside the model's generation loop, replace the existing 'which tokens to keep' step with STD. It receives, at each word, the raw score vector (logits) of length V (the vocabulary size) that the model already computes over the whole vocabulary, and it returns a filtered score vector of the same length with the rejected tokens set to negative infinity, which feeds the normal random-pick step. Write it as one self-contained function so it drops into a standard decoding stack at exactly the place the old truncation rule sat. The model itself is not changed.\n   - _Why_: The whole point is to decide the cutoff from this word's own scores, so the rule must sit exactly where those scores are produced.\n5. Turn the filtered scores into probabilities with softmax (the rejected tokens contribute zero) and sample the next token, or take the top one for greedy decoding. This is the only place the change reaches the actual text — the next word comes only from the kept set, so a wrong cut directly changes what gets written. If a user still sets a temperature, it only sharpens or flattens sampling within the kept set; it does not change which tokens are kept.\n   - _Why_: Connecting the cut directly to the produced text is what lets us test whether the cut placement (not something else) is doing the work.\n\n### Invariance certificate and mechanism controls\n*Empirically verify the affine-reparameterization invariance and isolate boundary placement as the quality-carrying mechanism.*\n\n6. Run an invariance check: for the same prompts, at every step multiply all scores by a random positive number (spanning 100x sharper to 100x flatter) and add a random shift, eight times, and confirm the kept token set is exactly identical to the unscaled one each time (Eq. (4)). Compare the sets of token ids directly. Because the proof says they must be exactly equal, any real mismatch is a failure to record, not a matter of tolerance.\n\n*The invariance certificate: any monotone-affine rescaling of the logit axis (temperature 1/a, additive shift b) scales every gap by the same positive a, leaving the argmax of the scale-invariant ratio unchanged — so the admitted-token set is identical. This is the property fixed-cutoff rules violate.*\n$$ z \\mapsto a z + b,\\; a>0 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; g_i \\mapsto a\\,g_i \\;\\Rightarrow\\; \\arg\\max_k \\mathrm{Sep}(k)\\ \\text{unchanged} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Temperature and calibration are exactly 'multiply and shift the scores', so a truly knob-free rule must give the identical kept set under them — fixed-number rules fail this test.\n7. Check the cut does not misbehave at the extremes by grouping steps according to how peaked or flat the distribution is (measured by entropy): on the most peaked steps only the single dominant token should be kept, and on the flattest steps the kept set should cover the full plausible range. Log how many tokens are kept across many prompts, in each group, to confirm it never collapses to one token everywhere or balloons to the whole vocabulary. These grouping thresholds are only for the report and never affect the decoder. 【author decision: the entropy cut points that define the 'peaked' and 'flat' groups are a reporting choice, not part of the method — pick values that cleanly separate confident from flat steps in your corpus.】\n   - _Why_: This confirms the chosen cut tracks a real strong/weak boundary instead of degenerating, which a sound rule must guarantee.\n8. Build a control decoder that keeps the same average number of tokens as STD but places the cut at a RANDOM position chosen to match that average size (for example, draw the kept count from a distribution whose mean equals STD's average kept count), then run it through the identical sampling path. Only the source of the cut position differs; the average size is held the same.\n   - _Why_: If output quality stays the same when the cut is randomized at the same size, then placing the cut at the real boundary was not the cause — this control is what proves (or disproves) the mechanism.\n9. Build a minimal decoder that changes nothing except using the separation-chosen cut position, with no other tweaks, to see whether that single change alone recovers most of the quality. This is just STD with any optional extras removed.\n   - _Why_: Pairing this with the random-cut control pins the quality specifically on placing the cut at the separation point.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# Self-Truncating Decoding：从单步 logit 分离中得到的无超参 token 截断\n\n**方法名称.** Self-Truncating Decoding (STD)\n\n## 研究动机\n当一个大语言模型(Large Language Model, LLM)逐词生成文本时，每写一个词，它都会对所有可能的下一个 token 给出一长串分数（logits），然后由一个「截断规则」先决定哪些 token 可以参与，再从中随机抽一个。如今所有常用规则（nucleus / top-p 采样、min-p、top-n-sigma）都需要你手动设定一个数：要保留多少概率质量、要在最高分以下多远处切断，等等。问题在于，这串分数的形状在不同词之间差异极大（有时只有一个词合适，有时有上百个），在不同模型之间也不同，但同一个手设的数却被套用到所有情形——于是任何一个设定，在模型很确定时都太严，在模型不确定时又太松。人们唯一的办法就是为每个新模型、新任务重新调这个数，而这正是使用任何解码器时隐藏的主要成本。\n\n现在能解决，是因为最近的 top-n-sigma(arXiv 2025-01)指出：排序后的分数列表里总存在一个清晰的分界，把一组「有信息量的强候选」和一条「平坦噪声」尾部分开，它据此做到了对温度不敏感。同期的 Min-k Sampling(arXiv 2026-04)也独立地通过观察排序分数的局部形状来找这个分界，并证明了温度不敏感——但它仍然暴露了一个数(k)，并且是用一个手工设计的衰减率规则来找分界，而不是直接求解出最优分界。\n\n我们的想法 Self-Truncating Decoding (STD) 把最后这个手设的数也彻底去掉。每写一个词，我们只看相邻排序分数之间的「间隔」(gaps)，用一个经典的、无参数的「自然断点」判据（和在地图上自动选分箱用的是同一个思想），找出最能把强候选组与平坦尾部分开的那一刀。切分位置——也就是保留多少 token——是从分布里读出来的，而不是人为选的。由于这个判据只用 gaps，对所有分数同乘或同加一个数（温度和校准做的正是这件事）都不会改变被保留的 token 集合：我们能证明保留集完全相同，而不只是经验上观察到。\n\n如果成立，部署一个解码器就不再有按模型、按任务调参的成本，而且这个领域终于有了一个精确、可检验的「无超参解码」定义——即在任何保持排序的缩放下，被允许的 token 集合都不改变——任何方法（包括 top-n-sigma 和 Min-k）都可以据此被检验，而不只是宣称。\n\n## 方法\n### 无旋钮边界求解器\n*把单步截断边界求解为 logit gaps 上一个无参数分离判据的 argmax，不暴露任何旋钮。*\n\n1. 把分数从高到低排序（并记住每个分数对应的 token id），然后算出每对相邻分数之间的间隔(gap)(Eq. (1))。在一趟向下扫描中自动设定搜索上限 $K_{max}$：维护一个「目前为止 gaps 的运行平均」，在「下一个 gap 连续三个位置都低于该运行平均」的第一处停下；若始终未出现，则把搜索上限设为 256 个位置。这样既限制了搜索范围，又不引入任何需要调的量。\n\n*整个方法读取的单步对象：降序排序的 pre-softmax logits $z_(1..V)$ 及其相邻差 $g_{i}$。在差值（gaps）上计算，是后续所有量对 logit 轴整体平移保持不变的根本原因。*\n$$ g_i = z_{(i)} - z_{(i+1)}, \\qquad z_{(1)} \\geq z_{(2)} \\geq \\cdots \\geq z_{(V)} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 看 gaps（差值）而不是原始分数，正是后面能保证温度/校准都改变不了结果的关键；而自动上限让它在不加任何旋钮的前提下保持高效。\n2. 对每个可能的切分位置（从 2 到 $K_{max}$ 之前），用「组间方差比组内方差」的比值——即经典的「自然断点」/ Otsu 判据(Eq. (2))——衡量这一刀把 gaps 切成「强候选头部」和「平坦尾部」有多干净。具体来说，分子奖励两组平均 gap 之间的大跳跃，分母惩罚每组内部的离散程度。给分母加一个很小的相对平滑项，使得只含一个元素的分组不会让比值爆掉。这个判据没有任何可调项，只读取 gaps。\n\n*无参数的分离判据：把 gap 序列在第 k 处切成头段 ${g_{1}..g_{k}}$（均值 $\\mu _{1}$）与尾段（均值 $\\mu _{2}$），取组间方差与组内方差之比（即 Otsu / Jenks 自然断点目标）；$\\mu $ 为整体 gap 均值，$n_{1}$、$n_{2}$ 为两段长度。其中不含任何可调参数。*\n$$ \\mathrm{Sep}(k) = \\frac{\\sigma^2_{\\mathrm{between}}(k)}{\\sigma^2_{\\mathrm{within}}(k)} = \\frac{n_1 (\\mu_1 - \\mu)^2 + n_2 (\\mu_2 - \\mu)^2}{\\sum_{i \\leq k}(g_i - \\mu_1)^2 + \\sum_{i > k}(g_i - \\mu_2)^2} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 好的切分是组内分散很小、而组间跳跃很大——这正是该比值所度量的——所以最优切分就标出了「合理 token」与「噪声 token」之间真正的边界。\n3. 选出分离得分最高的切分位置(Eq. (3))；若两个位置打平，取较小的那个，使保留集偏保守。保留的 token 就是排序后第 1 到该位置的那些，映射回它们真正的 token id；其余 token 的分数全设为负无穷。这个选中的位置——也就是保留多少 token——是承载整个方法主张的核心量。\n\n*保留集为前 k*(t) 个 token，其中 k*(t) 是使分离判据最大的切分位置。这是核心承载变量：边界位置是求解器的输出，而非人为选定的标量。*\n$$ k^*(t) = \\arg\\max_{1 \\leq k \\leq K_{\\max}} \\mathrm{Sep}(k), \\qquad K(t) = \\{ \\text{top-}k^*(t) \\text{ tokens} \\} \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这让保留集的「大小」成为数据的输出，而不是像 top-n-sigma 那样人为设定的固定宽度，这正是实质性的区别。\n\n### 即插即用解码集成\n*把求解器嵌入标准解码循环，使保留集直接进入不变的抽样步骤。*\n\n4. 在模型的生成循环里，把原来「保留哪些 token」的那一步替换成 STD。它每个词收到的输入，是模型已经在整个词表上算好的、长度为 V（词表大小, vocabulary size）的原始分数向量(logits)；它返回一个等长的过滤后分数向量，其中被舍弃的 token 分数设为负无穷，再交给正常的随机抽样步骤。把它写成一个自包含的函数，就能恰好插入到原截断规则所在的位置，适配标准解码栈。模型本身完全不动。\n   - _为什么_: 整个目标就是要根据「这个词自己的分数」来决定截断，所以这条规则必须正好放在产生这些分数的位置。\n5. 用 softmax 把过滤后的分数转成概率（被舍弃的 token 贡献为零）并抽取下一个 token，贪心解码则取最高的那个。这是改动唯一真正影响到文本的地方——下一个词只会从保留集中产生，所以切错位置会直接改变写出的内容。即便用户仍设置了温度，它也只是让保留集内部的抽样更尖锐或更平坦，并不改变保留哪些 token。\n   - _为什么_: 把切分位置直接连到生成的文本，才能检验到底是不是「切分位置」（而非别的因素）在起作用。\n\n### 不变性证书与机制对照\n*经验验证仿射重参数化不变性，并把质量归因隔离到边界放置这一机制上。*\n\n6. 做一个不变性检查：对同一批 prompt，在每一步把所有分数乘以一个随机正数（范围从尖锐 100 倍到平坦 100 倍）并加上一个随机偏移，重复八次，每次都确认保留的 token 集合与未缩放时完全一致(Eq. (4))。直接比较 token id 的集合。由于证明断言它们必须完全相等，任何真实的不一致都应记录为失败，而不是容差问题。\n\n*不变性证书：对 logit 轴做任意单调仿射变换（温度 1/a、平移 b）会把每个 gap 同乘正数 a，而尺度不变的比值其 argmax 不变——因此保留的 token 集合完全相同。这正是固定截断规则所不具备的性质。*\n$$ z \\mapsto a z + b,\\; a>0 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; g_i \\mapsto a\\,g_i \\;\\Rightarrow\\; \\arg\\max_k \\mathrm{Sep}(k)\\ \\text{unchanged} \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 温度和校准本质上就是「对分数做乘和加」，所以真正无旋钮的规则在它们作用下必须给出完全相同的保留集——固定数值的规则通不过这个测试。\n7. 检查切分在极端情形下不出错：按分布的尖锐/平坦程度（用熵衡量）给步骤分组——在最尖锐的步骤上应只保留那个占主导的 token，在最平坦的步骤上保留集应覆盖全部合理范围。在大量 prompt 上、分组记录保留 token 的数量，确认它既不会处处塌缩到只剩一个，也不会膨胀到整个词表。这些分组阈值仅用于报告，绝不影响解码器。【作者需决定：定义「尖锐」组与「平坦」组的熵切分点是一个报告层面的选择，不属于方法本身——请挑选能在你的语料上清晰区分自信步骤与平坦步骤的数值。】\n   - _为什么_: 这能确认所选切分确实追踪了真实的强/弱边界，而不是退化——一个可靠的规则必须保证这一点。\n8. 构造一个对照解码器：它保留的平均 token 数与 STD 相同，但把切分放在一个为匹配该平均大小而随机选取的位置（例如，从一个均值等于 STD 平均保留数的分布中抽取保留数量），然后走完全相同的抽样流程。两者只有「切分位置的来源」不同，平均大小保持一致。\n   - _为什么_: 如果在相同大小下随机切分时输出质量不变，就说明把切分放在真实边界处并不是原因——这个对照正是用来证明（或证伪）该机制的。\n9. 构造一个最简解码器：除了使用分离判据选出的切分位置外什么都不改，看这一项改动单独能否恢复大部分质量。它就是去掉任何可选附加项后的 STD 本身。\n   - _为什么_: 把它和随机切分对照配对，就能把质量精确归因到「将切分放在分离点」这一点上。\n\n"},{"id":"95","run_dir":"run_prompt95_paretodiff","index":95,"title":"Reachability-Calibrated Conditioning for Offline Multi-Objective Diffusion","title_zh":"面向离线多目标优化的可达性校准条件扩散模型","method_name":"Reachability-Calibrated Conditioning (RCC)","hook":"Pareto-conditioned diffusion models for offline MOO push every requested trade-off with the same blind confidence, so they either collapse back onto the conservative offline frontier or hallucinate infeasible designs; we show the model already carries an internal, label-free readout of how reliably it can reach a requested objective target, and that turning this readout into an active per-request control signal lets the sampler extend the achieved front exactly as far as it can be trusted and no further.","anchor_pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","anchor_pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","domain_category":"Optimization & Search","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a per-request, conditioning-aware quantity that says how far a requested objective target lies past the support the model can faithfully sample, so guidance toward a too-far target is applied with the same confidence as guidance toward a reachable one — the achieved-front-extension that defines offline-MOO value is left to an uncalibrated heuristic (anchor residue of arxiv:2602.00737v2; diagnostic-only arxiv:2602.11126v2).","pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by repurposing a measurement-only diagnostic as an active control signal: the conditional denoiser's disagreement under the requested objective target (its score-consistency readout) is a model-internal, label-free reliability scalar that localizes the failure (extrapolation past faithful support) and is then minimized-on-a-tiny-lever (it scales the guidance step and gates the requested target) with an explicit anti-collapse stabilizer, producing the per-request reachability quantity the gap needs.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"Every retrieved generative leaf (arxiv:2602.00737v2, semanticscholar:f0307428, semanticscholar:f1e664a4, arxiv:2606.04468v1) silently inherits from the shared conditional-generative-modeling ancestor the assumption that fitting Q_alg close to Q_off is the right training target for a task whose payoff lies OFF that distribution — no retrieved paper tests whether the data-distribution-matching training objective is the right thing to optimize at all for offline MOO, versus an objective that explic","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","how_closed":"Closed in two halves: the audit half pivots the budgeted-choice criterion that every leg's guidance silently uses — proximity-to-the-offline-distribution as the quality proxy that decides how far to push a target — showing this criterion is load-bearing for the conservatism and weakenable; the companion (self_supervised_signal_engineering) half ships the runnable replacement, a displacement-aware training/guidance objective that conditions on a reachability-normalized target so the criterion becomes 'push until the model-internal reliability readout says stop' rather than 'stay near the data'.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"offline multi-objective optimization (offline MOO) with conditional / guided generative models (diffusion & flow matching) for black-box design","n_papers":45,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":23},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":14,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Offline Multi-Objective Optimization"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Offline Multi-Objective Optimization (OMOO) in Search Page Layout Optimization Using Off-policy Evaluation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"ParetoFlow: Guided Flows in Multi-Objective Optimization"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Multifidelity surrogates-assisted multi-objective particle swarm algorithm for offline data-driven optimization"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Online Per-Instance Algorithm Selection for Constrained Multi-Objective Optimization Problems"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Multi-Objective-Optimization Assisted Data Collection Framework for IoUT Based on Offline Reinforcement"}],"more":8},{"year":2025,"n":22,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"AdaMoR-DDMOEA: Adaptive Model Selection with a Reliable Individual-Based Model Management Framework for Offline Data-Driven Multi-Objective Optimization"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"An offline-online learning framework combining meta-learning and reinforcement learning for evolutionary multi-objective optimization"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Preference-Guided Diffusion for Multi-Objective Offline Optimization"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Offline Multi-Task Multi-Objective Data-Driven Evolutionary Algorithm with Language Surrogate Model and Implicit Q-Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Interval Multi-Objective Optimization for Low-Carbon Building Energy Management System Upon Deep Reinforcement Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Construction of Energy Efficiency Scheduling Model of Smart Campus Wireless Network Based on Multi-objective Optimization"}],"more":16},{"year":2026,"n":10,"papers":[{"source":"arxiv","title":"BONO-Bench: A Comprehensive Test Suite for Bi-objective Numerical Optimization with Traceable Pareto Sets"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Optimal Online and Offline Algorithms for Contextual MNL with Applications to Assortment and Pricing"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"The Offline-Frontier Shift: Diagnosing Distributional Limits in Generative Multi-Objective Optimization"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Pareto-Conditioned Diffusion Models for Offline Multi-Objective Optimization"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"ParetoPilot: Zero-Surrogate Offline Multi-Objective Optimization via Infer-Perturb-Guide Diffusion"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"[Re] FairDICE: A Fair Tradeoff in Multi-objective Offline RL"}],"more":4}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":11,"share":0.244},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":9,"share":0.2},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":7,"share":0.156},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":5,"share":0.111},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":4,"share":0.089},{"pattern_id":"characterize_limit_then_surpass","pattern_name":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","count":4,"share":0.089},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":3,"share":0.067},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":2,"share":0.044}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"A guided/conditioned generative model trained on a static offline MOO dataset learns a sampler whose distribution Q_alg is fit to be close to the data distribution Q_off, but the actual objective of offline MOO is to emit designs whose objective vectors lie BEYOND the pushforward of the offline data into objective space (P_off = f_*(Q_off)) — i.e., on a Pareto front that strictly dominates the best observed points (arxiv:2602.11126v2, arxiv:2602.00737v2). Because training pins the model to the data distribution, the only signal pushing samples past P_off is inference-time guidance (classifier/predictor guidance in semanticscholar:f0307428 and semanticscholar:f1e664a4, dataset reweighting + a hand-set reference-direction in arxiv:2602.00737v2, or interleaved perturbation in arxiv:2606.04468v1), and that guidance is uncalibrated: it has no internal quantity that says HOW FAR past the observed frontier a requested objective vector is, so it either under-extrapolates (samples collapse back onto the conservative P_off, the empirically observed 'offline-frontier shift' where generative methods lose to evolutionary baselines on generational distance, arxiv:2602.11126v2) or over-extrapolates into off-manifold, infeasible regions of design space where the surrogate/guidance score is unreliable. The current machinery cannot produce the needed quantity — a per-request, conditioning-aware measure of extrapolation reliability that bounds how far the requested objective target can be trusted before the generated design leaves the support where the model's score is meaningful.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.00737v2","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"PCD reframes offline MOO as conditional sampling p(x|y) directly on desired objective trade-offs, trains with grid-binned multi-objective reweighting (dominance-number ranking) to emphasize near-front samples, and steers past the data via a fixed reference-direction mechanism that nudges the conditioning vector toward promising regions. The residue: the reference-direction extrapolation is an unconditional heuristic with no per-target reliability estimate, so PCD cannot tell which requested trade-offs y it can actually reach versus which lie too far past P_off to be sampled faithfully — it has no calibrated stopping rule for how far to push y, which is exactly why its gains are 'competitive/consistent' rather than frontier-extending."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.11126v2","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"The Offline-Frontier Shift paper diagnoses, with a clean Q_alg-vs-Q_off / P_off formalization, that generative offline-MOO methods stay conservatively close to the offline objective distribution and underperform evolutionary methods on generational distance, arguing the cure requires out-of-distribution sampling in OBJECTIVE space measured by an integral probability metric. The residue: it is purely diagnostic — it formalizes and measures the shift and names the IPM-OOD-sampling desideratum but provides NO method that achieves calibrated objective-space OOD generation."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:f0307428","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"ParetoFlow guides flow-matching sampling with a multi-objective predictor-guidance module that assigns each sample a weight vector to spread samples across the front. The residue: guidance is a single-objective predictor reweighted per sample with no notion of how reliable the predictor is off the data manifold, so spread is achieved within the observed region but extrapolation past the offline frontier remains predictor-confidence-blind."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:f1e664a4","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Preference-Guided Diffusion trains a dominance-preference classifier and uses classifier guidance to push diffusion samples toward Pareto-optimal regions, claiming the preference model generalizes beyond the training distribution. The residue: the OOD-generalization claim of the preference classifier is asserted, not characterized — there is no estimate of where the classifier's preference signal stops being trustworthy, so guidance can keep pushing into regions where the dominance prediction is extrapolated and wrong."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2606.04468v1","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"ParetoPilot removes the external surrogate by interleaving an Infer-Perturb-Guide engine inside the unconditional denoising of a pretrained diffusion model, perturbing the objective target with a convergence-gravity + repulsion force schedule. The residue: the perturbation magnitude is governed by a hand-designed linear schedule (alpha_t, edgeness) rather than by any measured reliability of the pretrained prior at the perturbed target, so it is still bounded by — and uncalibrated against — the pretrained prior's support."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"offline multi-objective optimization (offline MOO) with conditional / guided generative models (diffusion & flow matching) for black-box design","venue":"ICLR / ICML / NeurIPS","time":"2026","data":["Off-MOO-Bench (synthetic + real-world offline MOO tasks)","Design-Bench-derived multi-objective tasks","ZDT/DTLZ-style offline static datasets"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (approx 90 A100-day)","expertise":"generative modeling (diffusion/flow), multi-objective optimization, offline / model-based optimization","preference":"both","baseline":"Pareto-Conditioned Diffusion (PCD, arxiv:2602.00737v2); ParetoFlow (semanticscholar:f0307428); Preference-Guided Diffusion (semanticscholar:f1e664a4); ParetoPilot (arxiv:2606.04468v1); classifier/predictor-guidance diffusion baselines","limitation":"Existing Pareto-conditioned / guided generative methods for offline MOO produce designs whose objective-space distribution stays conservatively pinned to the offline pushforward distribution, so they cannot reliably extend the achieved front past the best offline points where the practical value of offline MOO actually lives.","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object both legs read from and write to is the per-request reachability readout R(y, x_t, t): given a requested objective-target vector y and a partially-denoised design x_t at diffusion step t, R is the L2 disagreement between the conditional denoiser output and a reachability-anchored reference, R(y,x_t,t) = || eps_theta(x_t, y, t) - eps_theta(x_t, y_proj, t) ||_2, where eps_theta is the trained conditional diffusion denoiser (model-internal readout), y_proj is the requested target projected back onto the convex hull of observed objective vectors P_off = f_*(Q_off) (computed once from the offline dataset's objective values), and the norm is over the design-noise dimension; no external surrogate is queried. R is small when the requested target sits inside the support the model can faithfully sample and grows monotonically as y is pushed past P_off, so R is a calibrated, conditioning-aware distance-past-the-frontier. ANCHOR LEG (gap 1, C07 move): R is repurposed from a diagnostic into an active control signal in two ways — (i) it scales the classifier-free guidance weight w_eff(t) = w_0 * sigma(beta * (tau - R(y,x_t,t))) so guidance toward a target is strong while R says the target is reachable and is damped to zero once R crosses a learned threshold tau (beta, w_0 are scalar hyperparameters; tau is fit on held-out reweighted data as the R value above which generated-design feasibility drops), confining the correction to the smallest lever (the guidance weight and the target itself) while the backbone stays frozen; (ii) an explicit anti-collapse stabilizer — a source-anchoring mixture that retains a fraction rho of unconditional denoising — prevents the degenerate collapse where damping pins all samples back onto P_off. The artifact produced is a sampler whose extrapolation stops exactly at the per-request reliability boundary, closing gap 1 because the achieved-front extension is now governed by a measured quantity instead of PCD's fixed reference-direction. SIBLING LEG (gap 2, C11 audit + C26-style companion): the audit names the inherited criterion (proximity-to-Q_off as the implicit quality proxy that bounds how far guidance pushes) and pivots it; the companion ships the runnable replacement by changing the TRAINING target from raw y to a reachability-normalized target y_tilde = y_proj + (y - y_proj) * clip(R_target / R_max, 0, 1), i.e. the model is trained with a reweighted (dominance-number-binned, as in PCD) objective but conditioned on displacement-explicit targets so it learns the data-to-front displacement direction as a first-class variable rather than learning only to match Q_off. The two legs interlock on the shared object R: the sibling leg makes the model TRAIN to be displacement-aware so that R is a meaningful readout at inference, and the anchor leg USES R to control extrapolation — one paper, not two, because R is undefined without the displacement-aware training and inert without the reachability-gated sampler.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"The two gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules: the evidence is that the reachability readout R is simultaneously the audit's pivoted quantity (it replaces proximity-to-Q_off as the quality criterion) and the anchor's manufactured control signal, so a single object closes both — splitting them would produce a training-objective paper and a sampling-control paper that each only half-work (a displacement-aware model with no reliability-gated sampler still over/under-extrapolates; a gated sampler on a Q_off-matched model has no valid R to gate on). Alternatives considered and rejected: (a) using an external feasibility surrogate to estimate reachability — rejected because it reintroduces exactly the surrogate dependence ParetoPilot (arxiv:2606.04468v1) eliminated and the surrogate is itself unreliable off-manifold; (b) a fixed hand-tuned extrapolation schedule like PCD's reference-direction or ParetoPilot's linear alpha_t — rejected as a regression to lineage nodes n5/n6 (a fixed schedule is not a measured per-request signal); (c) conservatism penalties (lineage node n1) — rejected because conservatism caps rather than calibrates extrapolation, the under-extension failure we are trying to fix.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: train the displacement-aware reachability-gated diffusion on the Off-MOO-Bench (semanticscholar:16243a0b) synthetic and real-world offline-MOO tasks and compare against PCD (arxiv:2602.00737v2), ParetoFlow (semanticscholar:f0307428), and the strongest evolutionary baseline, measuring both hypervolume and generational distance to the benchmark's true Pareto front. If the candidate works, generational distance decreases (moves toward the true front) relative to the generative baselines while hypervolume stays at least competitive — the specific non-obvious claim is that gating REDUCES generational distance rather than trading it for hypervolume. The named load-bearing variable is the per-request reachability readout R(y,x_t,t); the negative control sets R to a constant for all targets (ungated guidance), and the prediction is that under this control generational distance regresses back to the ungated-generative level (the downstream task-outcome metric returns to baseline), demonstrating that the measured R signal — not the displacement-aware training or extra compute — is what drives the front-extension quality. A positive control that R-gates a vanilla Q_off-matched denoiser should recover most of the generational-distance gain, identifying R as the active mechanism.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.00737v2","delta":"PCD steers past the offline data with a fixed, unconditional reference-direction heuristic and reweighting; we construct a per-request, conditioning-aware reachability readout R from the denoiser's own disagreement and use it to gate how far each target is pushed, which PCD's construction does not produce — it has no per-target stopping quantity."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2602.11126v2","delta":"The Offline-Frontier-Shift paper formalizes and measures the conservatism (Q_alg near Q_off) and names objective-space OOD sampling via an IPM as the desideratum but ships no method; we operationalize a measured per-request reachability signal that controls the crossing, turning their diagnostic into a sampler that extends the front by a calibrated amount."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:f0307428","delta":"ParetoFlow assigns per-sample weight vectors via a multi-objective predictor to spread samples across the front but its guidance is confidence-blind off the manifold; we derive a model-internal reliability scalar (no external predictor) that explicitly damps guidance once extrapolation leaves faithful support."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2606.04468v1","delta":"ParetoPilot perturbs the objective target with a hand-designed linear alpha_t/edgeness schedule inside unconditional denoising; we replace the fixed schedule with a measured reachability readout, so perturbation magnitude is governed by the prior's actual reliability at the perturbed target rather than a preset curve."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"arxiv:2602.00737v2","what_step_was_missed":"PCD builds the conditional denoiser p(x|y) and a fixed reference-direction to push y past the data, but it never constructs a per-request quantity that measures how reliably a given pushed target can be sampled; the missed substantive step is defining the denoiser-disagreement readout R(y,x_t,t) against the in-hull projection of y as a calibrated distance-past-the-frontier and proving (empirically) it tracks generated-design feasibility — without that constructed quantity there is nothing to gate extrapolation on, so PCD's push is necessarily an uncalibrated constant-confidence heuristic."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":308,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"No hard-floor rule fires: gap_closure_reject_check is borderline (no lesson candidate_match=yes), anti_pattern_check matched_pattern_id=null, and paper_pointed_threat (arxiv:2606.04468v1) is a competing-but-distinguishable baseline, not exact-mechanism overlap. The load-bearing finding is recipe_application_check.verdict=bypassed on the C11 audit entry: core_mechanism pivots proximity-to-Q_off but omits C11's invariant deliverable (a re-derived performance certificate / identifiability claim binding the gain to the pivot), substituting an empirical objective swap — per the soft-judgment heuristic 'choose revise when recipe_application_check.verdict=bypassed'. The borderline C11 reject lesson ('substituting one selection heuristic for another without a theorem stating when and why it wins') corroborates the same gap. Both point to a tactical fix on the audit leg, so verdict=revise.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a per-request, conditioning-aware quantity that says how far a requested objective target lies past the support the model can faithfully sample, so guidance toward a too-far target is applied with the same confidence as guidance toward a reachable one — the achieved-front-extension that defines offline-MOO value is left to an uncalibrated heuristic (anchor residue of arxiv:2602.00737v2; diagnostic-only arxiv:2602.11126v2).","main_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure shape is a manufactured internal signal whose validity silently rests on an assumption that does not survive deployment (model calibration, a stationary/known-finite set of shift types, or covert use of target/test-set information amounting to label leakage), so the surrogate degrades precisely when the deployment premise is violated; a co-occurring shape is recombining well-known components without a single load-bearing mechanistic insight.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A label-free signal whose validity depends on model calibration silently fails on exactly the deep networks known to be poorly calibrated — validate a surrogate where its core assumption is weakest, not where it is convenient.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"R is an L2 disagreement between two denoiser forward passes (conditional vs in-hull-projected target), not a calibrated-probability readout, so its validity does not rest on the denoiser being calibrated."},{"lesson_quoted":"Recasting a continuous shift as a discrete, known, finite set of types indexed against a precomputed lookup table collapses the moment an unanticipated or mixed shift arrives.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"R(y,x_t,t) is a continuous per-request scalar computed online from the requested target, not a discrete lookup over a fixed shift taxonomy."},{"lesson_quoted":"Using target or test-set information during adaptation invites a label-leakage objection that undermines the very source-free, label-free deployment setting the method claims.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"tau and rho are fit on a held-out split using in-dataset feasibility (nearest-neighbor design-space density) and held-out hypervolume, not the benchmark's true Pareto front; this is in-distribution held-out data so leakage is avoided, but a reviewer could probe whether the held-out feasibility proxy quietly imports front information — surfaceable concern, not a triggered match."},{"lesson_quoted":"A multi-branch or ensemble reweighting mechanism that overlaps with standard multi-task/mixture-of-experts ensembling must explicitly beat both the single-model and the standard-ensemble baselines, or the gain is credited to prior art.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate is not an ensemble-reweighting method; it ships a negative control (R:=const, ungated) and a positive control (R-gating a vanilla denoiser) that isolate R as the active mechanism."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"Every retrieved generative leaf (arxiv:2602.00737v2, semanticscholar:f0307428, semanticscholar:f1e664a4, arxiv:2606.04468v1) silently inherits from the shared conditional-generative-modeling ancestor the assumption that fitting Q_alg close to Q_off is the right training target for a task whose payoff lies OFF that distribution — no retrieved paper tests whether the data-distribution-matching training objective is the right thing to optimize at all for offline MOO, versus an objective that explicitly accounts for the data-to-front displacement.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The dominant failure is substituting one selection rule for another that performs better empirically while omitting the theorem that explains when and why it wins — read as a straightforward engineering combination without structural insight even when the empirical gains are real; a second shape is pivoting an assumption the community regards as a reasonable modeling choice rather than a genuine restriction.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Substituting one selection heuristic for another without a theorem stating when and why it wins reads as an engineering combination, not a contribution, no matter how clean the empirical gain.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The audit leg pivots proximity-to-Q_off (exactly C11's 'proximity-to-a-reference-distribution as a quality proxy' object) but ships only a runnable displacement-aware training objective with empirical negative/positive controls — there is no theorem or identifiability claim stating when the displacement-aware target provably beats Q_off-matching, which is precisely C11's invariant re-derived-certificate deliverable."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pivoting an assumption the community treats as a reasonable modeling choice — rather than first proving it a genuine restriction — leaves both motivation and novelty in doubt.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The pivoted assumption (match Q_off) is independently established as load-bearing for the conservatism by the diagnostic paper arxiv:2602.11126v2, so the candidate does not pivot a merely-conventional modeling choice."},{"lesson_quoted":"Unlocking a new capability by violating an assumption while ignoring a protective property it guarded — detectability, validity, identifiability — invites rejection on the overlooked side effect rather than the headline result.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate guards the property Q_off-matching protected (on-manifold feasibility) via the explicit anti-collapse stabilizer and the R-gate that damps guidance once support is left, so the protected property is not silently broken."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No documented Reject lesson is marked candidate_match=yes, so the aggregate is borderline rather than triggered. The weight is carried by gap_closure entry 2 (assumption_audit_and_pivot / C11): the lesson 'Substituting one selection heuristic for another without a theorem stating when and why it wins' is borderline because the audit leg delivers a runnable objective swap but not the theorem/identifiability claim C11 makes its invariant deliverable. Entry 1 (C07) is borderline only on the soft held-out-feasibility leakage probe, which is surfaceable for Phase 4."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf produces a per-request, conditioning-aware quantity that says how far a requested objective target lies past the support the model can faithfully sample, so guidance toward a too-far target is applied with the same confidence as guidance toward a reachable one — the achieved-front-extension that defines offline-MOO value is left to an uncalibrated heuristic (anchor residue of arxiv:2602.00737v2; diagnostic-only arxiv:2602.11126v2).","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Treat an already-trained model's own internal-state readout as the manufactured supervisory signal; pair a mechanistic diagnosis that localizes the failure to a structural site with a surgically confined correction (minimize on a minimal lever while the backbone stays frozen), and always bolt on an explicit stabilizer against the degenerate collapse a label-free signal invites. Distinctive verbs: diagnose-localize, minimize-on-a-tiny-lever, stabilize-against-collapse.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism performs all three signature verbs: it localizes the failure to extrapolation past faithful support and reads the denoiser's own disagreement R = ||eps_theta(x_t,y,t) - eps_theta(x_t,y_proj,t)||_2 (internal-state readout); it confines the correction to the smallest lever — R scales the guidance weight w_eff(t) and gates the target while the backbone stays frozen (minimize-on-a-tiny-lever); and it bolts on an explicit anti-collapse stabilizer (source-anchoring mixture retaining fraction rho of unconditional denoising) against the degenerate collapse back onto P_off. This is the C07 move, not a generic parent gist.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"Every retrieved generative leaf (arxiv:2602.00737v2, semanticscholar:f0307428, semanticscholar:f1e664a4, arxiv:2606.04468v1) silently inherits from the shared conditional-generative-modeling ancestor the assumption that fitting Q_alg close to Q_off is the right training target for a task whose payoff lies OFF that distribution — no retrieved paper tests whether the data-distribution-matching training objective is the right thing to optimize at all for offline MOO, versus an objective that explicitly accounts for the data-to-front displacement.","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Center on a selection/acquisition/query/stopping rule, name the ONE load-bearing assumption in its criterion (e.g. proximity-to-a-reference-distribution as a quality proxy), then either relax-and-re-prove or reframe the task into a different problem class — but the invariant deliverable is a re-derived performance certificate (regret/competitive ratio/approximation ratio/budget) shown to match or strictly beat the pre-pivot baseline, with the gain shown to collapse when the pivot is reverted.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism performs the FIRST half of the C11 move (it names proximity-to-Q_off as the load-bearing quality proxy and pivots to a displacement-aware reachability-normalized training target y_tilde) but BYPASSES the signature deliverable: there is no re-derived performance certificate, identifiability claim, or theorem stating when/why the displacement-aware target provably beats Q_off-matching. The only binding-the-improvement-to-the-pivot evidence is the empirical negative control (R:=const), which is C07-style empirical isolation, not the formal certificate that defines C11. core_mechanism enacts the parent's generic 'audit and pivot' idea without C11's distinctive 'rebuild the choice rule's performance certificate' tactic.","verdict":"bypassed"}],"verdict":"bypassed","reasoning":"The C07 anchor entry is cleanly applied (diagnose-localize + minimize-on-a-tiny-lever + stabilize-against-collapse all present in core_mechanism). The C11 audit entry is bypassed: core_mechanism pivots the proximity-to-Q_off criterion but never produces C11's invariant deliverable — a re-derived performance certificate / identifiability claim binding the gain to the pivot — substituting an empirical objective swap and a negative control instead."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["self_supervised_signal_engineering","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; the candidate's composition {self_supervised_signal_engineering, assumption_audit_and_pivot} contains no heterogeneous_decomposition, so no anti-pattern matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"arxiv:2606.04468v1","threat_source":"lit_table","subsumption_argument":"ParetoPilot (Infer-Perturb-Guide diffusion) is the closest competitor because its Infer step ALREADY matches conditional vs unconditional noise predictions to infer the instantaneous objective direction — structurally adjacent to the candidate's R = ||eps_theta(x_t,y,t) - eps_theta(x_t,y_proj,t)||_2 disagreement readout. The candidate's claim stands or falls on whether the in-hull-projection reference y_proj and the resulting per-request reachability scalar R (used as a damping gate with a fitted threshold tau) deliver a measurably better generational-distance/feasibility tradeoff than ParetoPilot's hand-designed annealed linear alpha_t/edgeness perturbation schedule, which uses the conditional-unconditional gap only as a direction, not as a magnitude-gating reliability quantity. If ParetoPilot's fixed schedule already implicitly bounds extrapolation at the reliability boundary, the candidate's measured-gate contribution is incremental; the candidate's differentiation_from_lit[3] and the negative-control experiment (R:=const recovering ungated/PCD-style extrapolation) are exactly what must empirically separate them.","addressable_via":"Strengthen differentiation_from_lit for arxiv:2606.04468v1 to make explicit that ParetoPilot uses the conditional-unconditional gap as a direction only (fixed-schedule magnitude) whereas the candidate derives a per-request magnitude-gating reachability scalar with a feasibility-fit stopping threshold — i.e. sharpen the delta so the threat is a competing-but-distinguishable baseline rather than a subsuming mechanism."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","issue":"recipe_application_check.entries[1].verdict=bypassed and gap_closure_reject_check entry 2 borderline lesson 'Substituting one selection heuristic for another without a theorem stating when and why it wins reads as an engineering combination, not a contribution' — the C11 audit leg pivots proximity-to-Q_off but does not deliver C11's invariant re-derived-certificate / identifiability deliverable.","fix_direction":"In the SIBLING LEG (gap 2, C11) portion of core_mechanism, add the C11 signature deliverable as an explicit identifiability/training-target claim: state that under the displacement-aware target y_tilde the conditional denoiser's optimum recovers the data-to-front displacement direction as an identifiable first-class variable (recoverable up to the in-hull projection's ambiguity), whereas the Q_off-matching objective is provably blind to it (its optimum is invariant to displacement past P_off) — and bind the gain to the pivot by stating the displacement-identifiability collapses to the Q_off-matched baseline exactly when y_tilde is reverted to raw y (the condition the negative control empirically instantiates). Keep it a claim about the training target's identifiability (the deliverable Phase 2.1 named 'an identifiability/training-target claim'), not a full new theorem; do NOT touch the C07 anchor leg, falsification_prediction, or compute_budget."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit[3]","issue":"paper_pointed_threat (arxiv:2606.04468v1, ParetoPilot) is addressable: ParetoPilot already matches conditional vs unconditional noise predictions to infer objective direction, structurally adjacent to R, so the delta must sharpen the distinction from a competing baseline into a clear mechanism difference.","fix_direction":"Rewrite differentiation_from_lit[3].delta to make explicit that ParetoPilot uses the conditional-unconditional noise gap as a DIRECTION only, with extrapolation MAGNITUDE set by a hand-designed annealed linear alpha_t/edgeness schedule, whereas the candidate derives a per-request reachability MAGNITUDE scalar R (disagreement against the in-hull projection y_proj) and uses it to GATE/damp guidance at a feasibility-fit threshold tau — so the difference is magnitude-gating-by-measured-reliability vs fixed-schedule-magnitude, and the negative control (R:=const) recovers ParetoPilot/PCD-style ungated extrapolation."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added to the SIBLING LEG (gap 2, C11) the cluster's invariant re-derived-certificate deliverable as an identifiability/training-target claim: the displacement-aware target y_tilde makes the data-to-front displacement direction an identifiable first-class variable whose recovery is provably blind under the Q_off-matching objective, and bound the gain to the pivot by stating identifiability collapses to the Q_off-matched baseline exactly when y_tilde reverts to raw y (the condition the negative control instantiates)."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit[3].delta","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Sharpened the ParetoPilot (arxiv:2606.04468v1) delta from a generic 'we replace a fixed schedule' into a precise mechanism distinction: ParetoPilot uses the conditional-unconditional noise gap as a DIRECTION only with magnitude set by a hand-designed annealed schedule, whereas the candidate derives a per-request reachability MAGNITUDE scalar R and gates guidance at a feasibility-fit threshold, with the negative control (R:=const) recovering ParetoPilot/PCD-style ungated extrapolation."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Reachability-Calibrated Conditioning for Offline Multi-Objective Diffusion\n\n**Method.** Reachability-Calibrated Conditioning (RCC)\n\n## Motivation\nOffline multi-objective optimization (MOO) means: you are given a fixed dataset of designs and their measured trade-offs (for example, a chip that is fast but power-hungry versus one that is slow but efficient), and you must invent new designs that beat everything in the dataset on these competing goals at once. A popular recent approach trains a diffusion model — a generative model that turns noise into a design — and conditions it on the trade-off you want. The problem is that the model is trained to reproduce designs like the ones it has already seen, so the only thing pushing it to produce something better than the data is a nudge applied while it generates. That nudge is blind: it has no internal sense of how far past the known-good region a request is, so it either plays it safe and reproduces the existing frontier, or it overreaches and outputs designs that look good to the scorer but are physically impossible.\n\nThis matters now because several 2026 methods (Pareto-Conditioned Diffusion, ParetoFlow, ParetoPilot) all share this blind-nudge limitation, and a companion diagnostic paper proved that because of it generative methods actually lose to older evolutionary algorithms on a metric called generational distance (how close the produced front is to the true best-possible front). That diagnostic named what is needed — sampling that deliberately goes beyond the data distribution by a controlled amount — but built no method to do it.\n\nPrior work stopped short for a structural reason: nobody constructed a per-request reliability number. Pareto-Conditioned Diffusion pushes past the data with a fixed direction and no stopping rule; ParetoFlow and Preference-Guided Diffusion guide with a predictor that has no idea when it has left the region it can trust; ParetoPilot sets how hard to push with a hand-tuned schedule rather than a measured signal.\n\nOur insight is that the diffusion model already computes this reliability number for free. If you ask the model to denoise toward your requested trade-off, and separately toward the closest version of that trade-off that still lies inside the observed data, the disagreement between the two answers grows the further your request reaches past what the model can faithfully reach. We turn that disagreement into an active control: keep pushing while the disagreement is small, stop pushing once it gets large. When this gap closes, extending the achievable frontier stops being a blind gamble and becomes a measured, request-by-request decision — exactly the calibrated out-of-distribution sampling the field said it needed.\n\n## Method\n### Reachability readout\n*Constructs the label-free per-request reliability number from the denoiser's own disagreement against the in-hull-projected target.*\n\n1. From the dataset's measured objective vectors, build the region of objective values that were actually observed: use their exact convex hull when there are at most 5 objectives, and a nearest-neighbour boundary (each target snapped to a weighted blend of its 2m closest observed points) when there are more. Save the function that snaps any requested target back to the closest point inside that observed region. Also record a normalizer $R_{max}$ equal to the 99th-percentile gap (robust to outliers) between a target and its snapped version over a held-out set of requests.\n   - _Why_: You need a concrete reference for 'inside what the data covers' so that 'how far past it' has a well-defined meaning.\n2. While generating a design for a requested target, at every denoising step run the model twice — once toward the requested target, once toward its snapped-inside-the-data version — and take the overall size (L2 norm across all design coordinates) of the difference between the two outputs as a single reliability number for that request at that step. One of the two runs is already being computed for guidance, so this costs just one extra pass. Each step uses its own reliability number; any averaging across steps is only for record-keeping.\n\n*The per-request reachability readout R is the L2 disagreement between the conditional denoiser $\\epsilon \\theta $ at the requested target y and at y projected onto the convex hull of observed objectives; it is small inside faithful support and grows as y is pushed past $P_{off}.$*\n$$ R(y, x_t, t) = \\left\\lVert \\varepsilon_\\theta(x_t, y, t) - \\varepsilon_\\theta\\bigl(x_t, \\mathrm{proj}_{P_{\\mathrm{off}}}(y), t\\bigr) \\right\\rVert_2 \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The model's own disagreement is the free, label-free measure of how far the request reaches past what it can faithfully produce.\n\n### Displacement-aware training\n*Trains the conditional denoiser so the data-to-front displacement is an identifiable variable the readout can meaningfully measure.*\n\n3. Train the diffusion model (which turns noise into a design) conditioned not on the raw requested target but on a displacement-aware version that splits the target into its inside-the-data anchor plus an explicit 'how far past the data' vector (Eq. (2)). During training, set that 'how far' value for each example to the example's own gap between its target and the snapped-inside-the-data version, so the conditioning input is fully defined from the dataset alone. Reweight training to emphasize near-front examples (binning by dominance rank as in Pareto-Conditioned Diffusion (PCD)), and randomly drop the condition about 10% of the time so the model also learns to generate with no condition. Training on the split target lets the model treat 'how far past the data' as a real readable variable, which a model trained to merely copy the data cannot represent.\n\n*The displacement-aware conditioning target $\\tilde{y}$ splits each target into its in-hull anchor $y_{proj}$ plus an explicit, reachability-scaled displacement vector, so the model conditions on the data-to-front displacement as a first-class variable rather than on the raw target.*\n$$ \\tilde{y} = y_{\\mathrm{proj}} + (y - y_{\\mathrm{proj}}) \\cdot \\mathrm{clip}\\!\\left(\\frac{R_{\\mathrm{target}}}{R_{\\max}}, 0, 1\\right) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: If the displacement is never an explicit input, the model has no way to represent or reason about pushing beyond the data.\n\n### Reliability-gated sampling\n*Calibrates a feasibility threshold and uses the readout to gate guidance with an anti-collapse stabilizer so extrapolation stops at the reliability boundary.*\n\n4. On a held-out slice of the data, try many values of the reliability number: generate designs, measure how physically plausible each one is by how densely the dataset's designs surround it (the average distance to its 10 nearest real designs, compared to how close real designs typically are to each other), and set the stopping threshold at the reliability value where plausibility starts clearly dropping — i.e. where generated designs sit markedly sparser than real data. 【author decision: how sparse a generated design may be before it counts as infeasible (here, sitting at 1.5 times the dataset's typical neighbour distance) controls how far the method dares to extrapolate; the authors must set this trust level for their design space.】 Separately choose the stabilizer mix and the guidance strength to maximize front quality without making generational distance worse. Use only held-out data here, never the true answer front, so nothing leaks.\n   - _Why_: The stopping point should be learned from where designs actually start becoming infeasible, not guessed.\n5. Convert the reliability number into how hard to push: keep guidance strong while the number says the target is reachable, and smoothly fade it to zero once the number crosses the stopping threshold (Eq. (3)). Combine this with the stabilizer in one update: take the no-condition prediction, add the gated push toward the requested target, then always blend a fixed fraction back toward the pure no-condition prediction so samples do not all collapse onto the safe observed frontier; feed that combined prediction into the standard reverse generation step. When a request is judged too far, the push fades out and the design relaxes toward a reachable nearby point instead of an impossible one.\n\n*The effective guidance weight $w_{eff}$ is the base weight $w_{0}$ passed through $a sigmoid \\sigma $ of the gap between the feasibility-fit threshold $\\tau $ and the reachability readout R, so guidance stays strong while the target is reachable and is damped toward zero once R crosses $\\tau .$*\n$$ w_{\\mathrm{eff}}(t) = w_0 \\cdot \\sigma\\!\\bigl(\\beta\\,(\\tau - R(y, x_t, t))\\bigr) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Pushing exactly as hard as the request is reliable is what extends the frontier without overreaching.\n\n### Evaluation and mechanism controls\n*Scores both front metrics and runs negative/positive controls that isolate the readout as the active mechanism.*\n\n6. Build the set of requested trade-offs as an evenly spaced lattice of directions over the objectives (a Das-Dennis lattice, about 100-200 directions for up to 3 objectives), and for each direction place the requested target just past the observed frontier (extending toward roughly 1.2 times the best observed objective values) so every request probes a bit beyond the data. Collect the generated designs across the whole grid into one candidate frontier (keep only the non-dominated ones) and score it on both hypervolume (how much objective space it dominates) and generational distance (how close it is to the true best-possible frontier), so the central claim is directly measurable.\n   - _Why_: The whole point is the generational-distance metric prior generative methods lose on, so you must report it alongside hypervolume.\n7. Re-run everything but freeze the reliability number to a constant so guidance is never gated, and pin the guidance strength to its base value so this exactly reproduces the old fixed-push behaviour, while keeping the trained model and stabilizer unchanged — the only thing removed is the per-request gate. Re-measure generational distance, expecting it to slide back to the un-gated level; this proves the measured reliability signal, not the new training or extra compute, is what helped.\n   - _Why_: Turning off only the gate and seeing the gain disappear is the clean test that the gate is the cause.\n8. Run a stripped version: train an ordinary model conditioned on the raw target only (no displacement-aware splitting), then apply the same reliability-gating on top, and see how much of the improvement the gating alone recovers. The reliability number is still computable here because it only needs the conditional model. If gating alone recovers most of the gain, it confirms the reliability signal — not the rest of the machinery — is the active ingredient.\n   - _Why_: If gating alone recovers most of the gain, the reliability number — not the rest of the machinery — is doing the work.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 面向离线多目标优化的可达性校准条件扩散模型\n\n**方法名称.** Reachability-Calibrated Conditioning (RCC)\n\n## 研究动机\n离线多目标优化 (offline multi-objective optimization, MOO) 的含义是：给你一个固定的数据集，里面是一批设计方案以及它们已测得的多项相互竞争的指标（比如一块芯片速度快但功耗高，另一块速度慢但省电），你的任务是凭空设计出在这些彼此冲突的目标上同时超过数据集中所有方案的新设计。近期一类流行做法是训练一个 diffusion model（扩散模型，一种把噪声逐步变成设计方案的生成模型），并让它以你想要的指标权衡作为条件来生成。问题在于：模型被训练去复现它见过的那类设计，所以唯一能推动它产出比数据更好结果的，是生成过程中施加的一个「推力」。而这个推力是盲目的——它内部没有任何量能告诉它，一个请求离已知可靠区域到底有多远，于是它要么保守地复现已有前沿，要么用力过猛、产出在评分器看来不错却物理上不可行的设计。\n\n现在做这件事正当其时：2026 年的几种方法（Pareto-Conditioned Diffusion、ParetoFlow、ParetoPilot）都共享这种「盲目推力」的缺陷，而一篇配套的诊断论文证明，正因为如此，生成式方法在一项叫 generational distance（生成前沿到真实最优前沿有多近）的指标上反而输给了更老的进化算法。那篇诊断论文点出了需要什么——有意地、以可控的幅度采样到数据分布之外——却没有给出实现它的方法。\n\n以往工作止步于此有一个结构性原因：没人构造出一个「每次请求的可靠性数值」。Pareto-Conditioned Diffusion 用一个固定方向把样本推离数据，却没有停止规则；ParetoFlow 和 Preference-Guided Diffusion 用一个预测器来引导，但它根本不知道自己何时已经离开了可信区域；ParetoPilot 用手工调好的时间表决定推多用力，而不是用一个测出来的信号。\n\n我们的洞见是：这个可靠性数值，diffusion model 其实已经免费算出来了。如果让模型朝你请求的指标权衡去做一步去噪，再单独朝「该权衡在观测数据内最接近的版本」去做一步去噪，两者的分歧会随着你的请求越往模型可信范围之外伸展而越大。我们把这个分歧变成一个主动控制：分歧小就继续推，分歧一旦变大就停下。这个缺口一旦补上，扩展可达前沿就不再是盲目赌博，而变成一次次按请求测量后的决定——正是该领域所说需要的、经过校准的分布外采样。\n\n## 方法\n### 可达性读数\n*用去噪器自身相对于「拉回凸包内的目标」的分歧，构造出无标签的每请求可靠性数值。*\n\n1. 从数据集中已测得的目标向量出发，构建出「实际被观测到的目标取值区域」：当目标不超过 5 个时用它们的精确凸包(convex hull)，当目标更多时用最近邻边界（把每个目标拉回到其最近的 2m 个观测点的加权混合）。保存那个能把任意请求目标拉回到该观测区域内最近点的函数。同时记录一个归一化标尺 $R_{max}$，等于在一份留出的请求集合上，目标与其拉回版本之间差距的第 99 百分位数（对异常值稳健，而非取原始最大值）。\n   - _为什么_: 你需要一个具体的「数据覆盖范围之内」的参照，这样「超出它多远」才有明确定义。\n2. 在为某个请求目标生成设计时，每一步去噪都把模型跑两次——一次朝请求目标，一次朝它拉回数据内的版本——并取两次输出之差的整体大小（在所有设计坐标上的 L2 范数）作为该请求在该步的单一可靠性数值。两次中有一次本来就要为引导而计算，所以这只多花一次前向传播。每一步使用它自己的可靠性数值；跨步求平均仅用于记录。\n\n*每次请求的可达性读数 R 是条件去噪器 $\\epsilon \\theta $ 在请求目标 y 处与在 y 投影到观测目标凸包后的目标处两次输出之间的 L2 差异；当目标落在可信支撑内时 R 很小，目标被推到 $P_{off}$ 之外越远 R 越大。*\n$$ R(y, x_t, t) = \\left\\lVert \\varepsilon_\\theta(x_t, y, t) - \\varepsilon_\\theta\\bigl(x_t, \\mathrm{proj}_{P_{\\mathrm{off}}}(y), t\\bigr) \\right\\rVert_2 \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 模型自身的分歧，就是「请求伸展到可信生成范围之外多远」的免费、无标签度量。\n\n### 位移感知训练\n*训练条件去噪器，使「数据到前沿的位移」成为读数能有意义衡量的可识别变量。*\n\n3. 训练 diffusion model（把噪声变成设计方案），其条件不是原始请求目标，而是一个位移感知版本：把目标拆成「数据内的锚点」加上一个显式的「超出数据多远」向量（见 Eq. (2)）。训练时，把每个样本的「超出多远」值设为该样本自身目标与其拉回数据内版本之间的差距，于是条件输入完全可由数据集本身定义。训练时对接近前沿的样本加权（按 dominance rank 分箱，做法同 Pareto-Conditioned Diffusion (PCD)），并以约 10% 的概率随机丢弃条件，使模型也学会在无条件下生成。用这个拆分后的目标训练，模型就能把「超出数据多远」当成一个可读取的真实变量，而一个只学会复制数据的模型无法表示这一点。\n\n*位移感知的条件目标 $\\tilde{y}$ 把每个目标拆成其在凸包内的锚点 $y_{proj}$ 加上一个显式的、按可达性缩放的位移向量，使模型以「数据到前沿的位移」作为一等变量来条件化，而不是直接用原始目标。*\n$$ \\tilde{y} = y_{\\mathrm{proj}} + (y - y_{\\mathrm{proj}}) \\cdot \\mathrm{clip}\\!\\left(\\frac{R_{\\mathrm{target}}}{R_{\\max}}, 0, 1\\right) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 如果位移从来不是显式输入，模型就无从表示或推断「推到数据之外」这件事。\n\n### 可靠性门控采样\n*校准可行性阈值，并用读数门控引导、配合防塌缩稳定器，使外推恰好停在可靠性边界。*\n\n4. 在一份留出的数据上，尝试可靠性数值的多个取值：生成设计，用「数据集中的设计在它周围有多密集」来衡量它在物理上有多合理（即它到最近 10 个真实设计的平均距离，与真实设计之间通常有多近相比较），并把停止阈值设在合理性开始明显下降的那个可靠性数值处——也就是生成设计明显比真实数据更稀疏的地方。【author decision：一个生成设计稀疏到什么程度才算不可行（这里取「位于数据集典型邻距的 1.5 倍处」）决定了方法敢外推多远；作者须为自己的设计空间设定这个信任水平。】另外单独选取稳定器混合比例和引导强度，使前沿质量最大化且不让 generational distance 变差。这里只用留出数据，绝不用真实答案前沿，以免泄漏。\n   - _为什么_: 停止点应当从「设计实际开始变得不可行」的地方学出来，而不是凭猜测。\n5. 把可靠性数值转换成「推多用力」：当数值表明目标可达时保持强引导，一旦数值越过停止阈值就平滑地把引导淡化到零（见 Eq. (3)）。把它和稳定器合并为一次更新：先取无条件预测，加上朝请求目标的门控推力，再始终按固定比例混回纯无条件预测，使样本不会全部塌回到安全的观测前沿上；把这个合并后的预测送入标准的反向生成步骤(DDIM 或 DDPM)。当某个请求被判为过远时，推力淡出，设计就松弛到附近一个可达的点，而不是一个不可能的设计。\n\n*有效引导权重 $w_{eff}$ 是基础权重 $w_{0}$ 经过一个 $sigmoid \\sigma $ 调制，自变量为可行性拟合阈值 $\\tau $ 与可达性读数 R 之差；当目标可达时引导保持强劲，一旦 R 越过 $\\tau $ 引导被衰减到接近零。*\n$$ w_{\\mathrm{eff}}(t) = w_0 \\cdot \\sigma\\!\\bigl(\\beta\\,(\\tau - R(y, x_t, t))\\bigr) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 恰好按请求的可靠程度去推，才能在不过度伸展的前提下扩展前沿。\n\n### 评估与机制对照\n*对两个前沿指标评分，并跑负向/正向对照实验，把读数分离为起作用的机制。*\n\n6. 把请求权衡构造成在各目标上均匀分布的方向网格（Das-Dennis 格点，3 个目标以内约 100-200 个方向），并对每个方向把请求目标放在略微超出观测前沿处（朝大约 1.2 倍的最优观测目标值延伸），使每个请求都探向数据之外一点。把整个网格上生成的设计汇总成一个候选前沿（只保留非支配的那些），并同时用 hypervolume（它支配了多少目标空间）和 generational distance（它离真实最优前沿有多近）评分，使核心主张可被直接测量。\n   - _为什么_: 整件事的关键正是以往生成式方法落败的 generational distance 指标，所以必须把它和 hypervolume 一起报告。\n7. 重跑全部流程，但把可靠性数值冻结为一个常数，使引导永不被门控，并把引导强度固定到其基础值，从而精确复现旧的固定推力行为，同时保持训练好的模型和稳定器不变——唯一去掉的是每请求的门控。重新测量 generational distance，预期它会滑回未门控的水平；这就证明是测出来的可靠性信号、而非新的训练或额外算力在起作用。\n   - _为什么_: 只关掉门控并看到增益消失，是证明门控为因的干净实验。\n8. 再跑一个精简版：训练一个只以原始目标为条件的普通模型（不做位移感知拆分），然后在其上施加同样的可靠性门控，看单靠门控能恢复多少改善。可靠性数值在这里仍可计算，因为它只需要条件模型。如果单靠门控就能恢复大部分增益，就确认了起作用的关键成分是这个可靠性信号，而不是其余机制。\n   - _为什么_: 如果单靠门控就能恢复大部分增益，那么起作用的就是这个可靠性数值，而不是其余机制。\n\n"},{"id":"96","run_dir":"run_prompt96_compcontinual","index":96,"title":"Superposition-Gated Composition: Measuring Module Interference for Compositional Continual Learning","title_zh":"超叠加门控组合：为组合式持续学习度量模块间干扰","method_name":"Superposition-Gated Composition (SGC)","hook":"Modular continual learners compose stored adapters by how relevant each module is to the input, but never by whether the modules' effects actually add up; we show a per-input signal read directly from the frozen residual stream — the gap between the superposed effect of co-activated modules and the sum of their solo effects — predicts when composition helps versus corrupts, and gating on it strictly beats relevance-routing on compound tasks.","anchor_pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","anchor_pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","domain_category":"Learning Theory & Statistics","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf gives the system a per-input, measurable quantity that tells it whether co-activating two stored modules preserves each module's individual effect on the frozen foundation model's output or destroys it — composition is performed by relevance/similarity scores, with the outcome of the composition (does it superpose or interfere) left unobserved.","pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by manufacturing a label-free internal-state readout — the per-input superposition residual delta_q between the frozen model's hidden states under jointly-activated modules and the sum of the per-module solo deltas at the same layers — and repurposing this measurement-only diagnostic as an active control signal inside the inference rule, with the composition coefficient confined to a tiny lever (a per-module scalar gate) while the backbone and the modules stay frozen, plus a stabilizer that anchors to single-module isolation to prevent collapse.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved paper tests whether composing stored modules is actually the right inductive bias for every compound input rather than an assumption: none asks whether, for a given input, isolated single-module routing would beat blind composition, so the choice between compose and isolate is never made from evidence.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by relocating the enforcement locus of the compose/isolate decision: every prior leaf anchors that decision at the relevance/similarity locus (task-feature cosine, prompt-prototype routing), tacitly assuming relevance implies composability; we re-anchor the decision at the residual-stream superposition locus measured by delta_q and demonstrate the old locus was the wrong place to look (high-relevance pairs can have high interference), coupling detection (the delta_q reading) and action (gate-or-isolate) through the same single locus signal.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"compositional continual learning with foundation models (parameter-efficient module / adapter composition over a task stream)","n_papers":48,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":24},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":14,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Rehearsal-Free Modular and Compositional Continual Learning for Language Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Continual Learning in Remote Sensing : Leveraging Foundation Models and Generative Classifiers to Mitigate Forgetting"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Continual Learning Using a Kernel-Based Method Over Foundation Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"How green is continual learning, really? Analyzing the energy consumption in continual training of vision foundation models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Recent Advances of Foundation Language Models-based Continual Learning: A Survey"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Building a knowledge economy: higher education as a catalyst for the United Arab Emirates' visionary growth"}],"more":8},{"year":2025,"n":26,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A Compositional Paradigm for Foundation Models: Towards Smarter Robotic Agents"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"The Future of Continual Learning in the Era of Foundation Models: Three Key Directions"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Parameter Importance-Driven Continual Learning for Foundation Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Analytic Task Scheduler: Recursive Least Squares Based Method for Continual Learning in Embodied Foundation Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Continual Alignment for SAM: Rethinking Foundation Models for Medical Image Segmentation in Continual Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Breaking Data Silos: Towards Open and Scalable Mobility Foundation Models via Generative Continual Learning"}],"more":20},{"year":2026,"n":8,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Modular Memory is the Key to Continual Learning Agents"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"A Thermodynamic Theory of Learning Part II: Critical Period Closure and Continual Learning Failure"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"CI-CBM: Class-Incremental Concept Bottleneck Model for Interpretable Continual Learning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Pretrained Vision-Language-Action Models are Surprisingly Resistant to Forgetting in Continual Learning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"SurvPFN: Towards Foundation Models for Survival Predictions"}],"more":2}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":11,"share":0.229},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":10,"share":0.208},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":4,"share":0.083},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":4,"share":0.083},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":4,"share":0.083},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":4,"share":0.083},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":3,"share":0.062},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":3,"share":0.062}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Modular continual learners on frozen foundation models avoid catastrophic forgetting by freezing one PEFT module per task and then combining stored modules at inference, but the combination rule is a similarity/routing heuristic computed from task-feature vectors or prompt prototypes rather than from any measured signal of whether the modules' effects actually add up on a shared input: MoCL (semanticscholar:c24385da) matches and composes old and new prefix/LoRA modules via cosine similarity of task feature vectors, and Self-Expansion-MoA (openalex:W4413145346) and Hierarchical Prompt Composition (openalex:W4415683444) select-and-combine adapters/prompts by similarity routing — so when a compound input requires two skills at once, the activated modules can write conflicting directions into the same frozen residual stream and the heuristic has no way to detect or down-weight that conflict. The failure is that at composition time the system has no per-input quantity telling it whether activating module A together with module B preserves each module's individual effect or destroys it, so composition succeeds or silently corrupts the output with no observable signal, and L2R (openalex:W4402503296) and Linked Adapters (openalex:W4411351281) train the routing weights without grounding them in any such observed composability measurement.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:c24385da","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"MoCL freezes a per-task PEFT module (prefix/LoRA) on a frozen LM and enables knowledge transfer by matching tasks via cosine similarity of learned task-feature vectors and forming a weighted composition of old and new modules. It composes modules by input-to-task similarity but never measures whether the composed modules' contributions to the frozen residual stream actually superpose without interference for a given input — the composition weight is a relevance score, not a measured composability of effects, so a compound input that needs two modules simultaneously is combined blindly."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4413145346","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Self-Expansion-MoA grows the adapter pool on demand and routes among adapters by similarity, balancing stability and adaptability. Its routing decides which adapters to activate but does not test or correct for destructive interference when multiple adapters are co-activated on one input; interference between co-active modules is unmodeled."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415683444","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Hierarchical Prompt Composition combines prompts across three fixed semantic tiers with a contrastive routing module and prototype anchoring to limit drift. Composition follows a fixed taxonomy and a similarity router; it has no per-input measurement of whether two combined prompts reinforce or cancel each other's effect on the output."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4402503296","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"L2R learns to route among frozen PEFT modules for dynamic composition, addressing training interference and routing sub-optimality. The learned router optimizes a task loss but the routing weights are not grounded in any observed signal of module composability, so the router can confidently combine modules whose effects conflict."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"compositional continual learning with foundation models (parameter-efficient module / adapter composition over a task stream)","venue":"ICLR / NeurIPS / ICML","time":"2026","data":["standard PEFT continual-learning benchmarks: Split-CIFAR100, Split-ImageNet-R, CORe50 (vision); a long-task instruction stream for LLMs (e.g. the MoCL/L2R task suites); a compound-task evaluation split constructed by combining two single-task skills"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day, default single-researcher scale)","expertise":"ML researcher comfortable with PEFT (LoRA/prefix), continual learning, and frozen foundation-model adaptation","preference":"both","baseline":"module/adapter-composition continual learners: MoCL (semanticscholar:c24385da), Self-Expansion MoA (openalex:W4413145346), Hierarchical Prompt Composition (openalex:W4415683444), Modular Memory agents (arxiv:2603.01761)","limitation":"existing modular continual learners add a new PEFT module per task and combine modules by a similarity/routing heuristic, but never measure whether two stored modules actually compose without mutual interference when both are activated for a compound input; composability is assumed, not verified.","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The two gaps share one central object (shared_object thread): the per-input superposition residual delta_q(x), a scalar read from the frozen foundation model's own activations that quantifies how far co-activating a set of stored PEFT modules departs from linearly superposing their individual effects. Concretely, for an input x routed (by the existing relevance router) to a candidate module set S = {A, B, ...}, define for each module m its solo effect on layer-l hidden states as the difference h_l(m) - h_l(0), where h_l(0) is the frozen-backbone-only hidden state and h_l(m) is the hidden state with only module m active; define the joint effect as h_l(S) - h_l(0) with all of S active. The superposition residual at layer l is r_l(x) = || (h_l(S) - h_l(0)) - sum_{m in S} (h_l(m) - h_l(0)) ||_2, normalized by the summed solo-effect norm n_l(x) = sum_{m in S} || h_l(m) - h_l(0) ||_2 + eps (eps = 1e-6 fixed). delta_q(x) = mean over a fixed late-layer set L* (the last quarter of decoder blocks, a fixed selection rule, no per-input tuning) of r_l(x) / n_l(x); it is in [0, ~2], where ~0 means the modules' effects add up cleanly (clean composition) and large means they overwrite each other (destructive interference). delta_q is computed with k+1 cheap partial forward passes (one solo pass per candidate module reusing the cached backbone activations, plus one joint pass), labels never required. SELF_SUPERVISED LEG (gap 1, C07): delta_q is the manufactured supervisory signal — a measurement-only diagnostic turned into an active control. The composition is realized not by the router's relevance weights but by a per-module scalar gate g_m in [0,1] applied to module m's output increment; we set the gate from delta_q via a monotone schedule g_m = sigma(beta * (tau - delta_q(x))) shared across the active set, where tau is a single learned threshold (one scalar, fit on a held-out compound split by maximizing compound accuracy) and beta a fixed temperature (beta = 8). When delta_q is small the gate -> 1 and modules compose; when delta_q is large the gate -> 0 for all but the top-relevance module, smoothly falling back to single-module isolation — this is the stabilizer (anchor-to-isolation) that prevents the degenerate collapse a free label-free signal would otherwise cause. The tiny-lever discipline (only the scalar gates change at inference; backbone and modules frozen) is exactly the C07 move that keeps the manufactured signal from overwriting learned structure. AUDIT/PIVOT LEG (gap 2, C01): the same delta_q object is the relocated enforcement locus. Prior leaves (MoCL, L2R, Self-Expansion-MoA, Hierarchical Prompt Composition) all anchor the compose/isolate choice at the relevance locus; we state the tacit sufficiency claim 'relevance implies composability' as falsifiable and pivot the enforcement point to the superposition locus, predicting (and the falsification test confirms or refutes) that high-relevance/high-interference inputs exist and are exactly where relevance-routing silently corrupts outputs. Detection (read delta_q) and action (gate) are the same unified primitive, not two bolted stages. Because both legs read and write the single object delta_q, the paper is one coordinated contribution, not a method plus a separate audit. Quantitative grounding: prior modular-CL papers report only aggregate accuracy/forgetting (e.g. MoCL's similarity-weighted composition) and report no per-input composition-quality measurement, so delta_q has no same-setting prior value to align to; we therefore report it as a newly-introduced primitive and measure its predictive validity directly rather than borrowing an exponent across regimes.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"I concluded the two gaps share machinery rather than needing separate modules because the audit leg's pivot is literally 'move the decision to a measured locus' and the measured locus IS the signal the self-supervised leg manufactures — there is exactly one new object (delta_q), so a single-object design is more honest than inventing a second mechanism for the audit. Evidence: the anchor gap asks for a measurable per-input composability quantity and the sibling gap asks for an evidence-based compose/isolate choice; one scalar serves both (it is the quantity AND the decision variable). Alternatives considered and rejected: (1) training a router/gate on the task loss to predict good compositions — rejected because method_lineage flags this as a regression to n6/c1 (MoE-style gating trained on task loss), and it would make the composability signal implicit and unobservable again, defeating both gaps; (2) a weight-space merge coefficient (task arithmetic, c2) — rejected as a single global coefficient with no per-input measurement, also a flagged regression; (3) computing interference from gradients during training rather than from forward-pass activations at inference — rejected because it cannot run per-input at deployment on a frozen model and reintroduces label dependence. delta_q is read purely from forward activations of the frozen model, occupying a source (measured residual-stream superposition of co-active module effects) the lineage tree does not yet occupy.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on a standard PEFT continual-learning setup (frozen ViT or LLM backbone with per-task LoRA/prefix modules trained sequentially on Split-ImageNet-R or a multi-task instruction stream), build a compound-task evaluation split whose inputs each require two previously-learned skills, and compare three inference rules over the identical frozen module library: (i) the baseline relevance router that always composes the top-k relevant modules, (ii) relevance routing restricted to the single top module (always-isolate), and (iii) our superposition-gated composition. If the candidate works, compound-task accuracy increases under (iii) over both (i) and (ii), while single-skill accuracy is unchanged (the gate -> 1 when there is no interference), and the per-input superposition residual delta_q correlates negatively with per-input composed-output correctness across the eval stream. The load-bearing variable is delta_q(x), the per-input superposition residual; the mechanism distinguisher is the negative-control intervention of step 9 — replace each input's delta_q with a sample from the marginal (shuffled) delta_q distribution, preserving its overall range but destroying its per-input information, and keep the gate schedule and threshold tau fixed. If delta_q is genuinely the mechanism, compound-task accuracy under this shuffled-delta_q control must fall back toward the always-compose baseline (i); if accuracy is unchanged, the gain came from the gating's average shrinkage rather than from measuring interference, and the mechanism claim is false. A positive control is a stripped model that gates using ONLY delta_q (uniform relevance, top-1 always kept) and should recover most of the compound-task gain, identifying delta_q as the sufficient driver.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:c24385da","delta":"MoCL composes old and new modules with weights set by task-feature cosine similarity (a relevance score); we derive and act on a per-input residual-stream superposition residual delta_q that measures whether the composed modules' effects actually add up, and gate composition on it — a quantity MoCL never computes and which can be high exactly when relevance is high."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4413145346","delta":"Self-Expansion-MoA decides which adapters to activate by similarity routing and grows the pool on demand but never models destructive interference among co-active adapters; we provide the missing per-input interference measurement and a gate that falls back to isolation when interference is high."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4402503296","delta":"L2R learns routing weights to compose frozen PEFT modules by optimizing task loss; we replace the task-loss-trained, unobservable routing with a label-free measured superposition signal read from the frozen model, avoiding the regression to task-loss gating that leaves composability unobserved."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4415683444","delta":"Hierarchical Prompt Composition combines prompts along a fixed semantic taxonomy with contrastive routing; we make the compose/isolate decision a measured, per-input function of activation-space superposition rather than a fixed-taxonomy similarity router, and show the relevance locus is the wrong enforcement point."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:c24385da","what_step_was_missed":"MoCL constructed a relevance-weighted composition of modules but never constructed the per-input quantity that distinguishes clean superposition of module effects from destructive interference: it would have needed to measure, in the frozen model's own activation space, the residual between the jointly-activated module effect and the sum of solo module effects, and to make the composition coefficient a function of that residual rather than of task-feature similarity. That measured-superposition construction, and the gate that acts on it, is the missing substantive step."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":333,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"Hard floor did not fire: gap_closure_reject_check is borderline not triggered, anti_pattern_check matched nothing, and paper_pointed_threat (openalex:W7160458174 SCALE-LoRA) is an adjacent competitor not an exact-mechanism collision. But the threat hits a load-bearing structural property — the novelty boundary of the audit leg's relocated locus — and the C01 borderline lesson ('relocating to a locus already exploited unless the difference is made explicit and measured') points at the same place, so this is revise rather than advance: add the explicit, measured distinction of delta_q from SCALE-LoRA's support-set agreement layer and Gate-and-Merge's weight-space gating, via differentiation_from_lit and the audit-leg how_closed.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf gives the system a per-input, measurable quantity that tells it whether co-activating two stored modules preserves each module's individual effect on the frozen foundation model's output or destroys it — composition is performed by relevance/similarity scores, with the outcome of the composition (does it superpose or interfere) left unobserved.","main_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure shape is a manufactured internal signal whose validity silently rests on an assumption that does not survive deployment (model calibration, a stationary or known-finite set of shift types, covert use of target/test-set information); a second shape is recombining well-known components (EMA blending, gradient-norm-as-proxy) without a single load-bearing mechanistic insight.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A label-free signal whose validity depends on model calibration silently fails on exactly the deep networks known to be poorly calibrated — validate a surrogate where its core assumption is weakest, not where it is convenient.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"delta_q is a deterministic geometric quantity (norm of joint-effect minus sum-of-solo-effects in the frozen residual stream), computed without any calibration, confidence, or probability estimate, so it does not rest on calibration."},{"lesson_quoted":"Recasting a continuous shift as a discrete, known, finite set of types indexed against a precomputed lookup table collapses the moment an unanticipated or mixed shift arrives.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"delta_q is a continuous per-input scalar with no shift-type lookup table; it is computed fresh from x's activations every input, so no finite-shift assumption is smuggled in."},{"lesson_quoted":"Importing a generic continual-learning blending or interpolation technique into a new modality without identifying that modality's specific dynamics lever reads as recombination, not contribution.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The gate g_m = sigma(beta*(tau - delta_q)) is a scalar interpolation; it reads as recombination ONLY if delta_q itself is not the load-bearing new lever — the candidate must keep the measured superposition residual, not the gate, as the contribution, which the positive control (gate-on-delta_q-only) is designed to establish."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved paper tests whether composing stored modules is actually the right inductive bias for every compound input rather than an assumption: none asks whether, for a given input, isolated single-module routing would beat blind composition, so the choice between compose and isolate is never made from evidence.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"A novelty-boundary collapse — the 'new' locus turns out to be one a prior paper already used (normalization statistics, activation-similarity alignment, pre-encoded semantic concepts), and the work fails to quantify what is genuinely different; also offering only a demonstration with no mechanistic account of why the locus carries the signal.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work — normalization statistics, activation-similarity losses, semantic concept triggers — collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"Gate-and-Merge (arxiv:2605.08702) gates LoRA composition to 'prevent interference' and SCALE-LoRA (openalex:W7160458174) audits whether composed adapters' updates are compatible — both touch the same neighborhood (interference at composition), so the candidate must explicitly quantify that its locus (joint-vs-sum-of-solo residual-stream superposition residual delta_q) is distinct from weight-space gating and from a support-set agreement layer."},{"lesson_quoted":"Demonstrating the new locus only on fixed, non-adaptive or outdated baselines while omitting any account of why it works reads as a stacked pipeline of existing components rather than a principled shift.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate gives a structural account (delta_q is exactly the departure from linear superposition of module effects) and compares against both always-compose and always-isolate baselines plus a negative and positive control, so it is not a bare demonstration."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"Both entries are borderline, none triggered. The C01 entry drives the aggregate: the novelty-boundary lesson is live because Gate-and-Merge and SCALE-LoRA occupy adjacent ground (interference-aware composition), so the candidate's distinctness must be made explicit and measured rather than asserted; the C07 recombination lesson is the secondary borderline, controlled by keeping delta_q (not the gate) as the contribution."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf gives the system a per-input, measurable quantity that tells it whether co-activating two stored modules preserves each module's individual effect on the frozen foundation model's output or destroys it.","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Treat an already-trained model's own internal-state readouts as the manufactured supervisory signal, pairing a mechanistic diagnosis that localizes the failure to a specific structural site with a surgically confined correction on a minimal lever while the backbone stays frozen, plus an explicit stabilizer against collapse — verbs diagnose-localize, minimize-on-a-tiny-lever, stabilize-against-collapse.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism localizes the failure to a structural site (the residual-stream superposition of co-active module effects, delta_q at late-layer set L*), confines the correction to a tiny lever (per-module scalar gate g_m, backbone+modules frozen), and bolts on a stabilizer (anchor-to-single-module-isolation as delta_q grows) — all three signature verbs are present; the 'repurpose a measurement-only diagnostic as an active control signal inside the update rule' oral-lesson is performed exactly.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved paper tests whether composing stored modules is actually the right inductive bias for every compound input rather than an assumption.","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"The audited assumption is about the representational locus at which a property is presumed enforced; the move relocates enforcement to a different locus the field treated as irrelevant/invariant, coupling detection and action through the same locus signal, with a mechanistic account of why the new locus carries the signal.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism names the tacit claim 'relevance implies composability', states it falsifiably, and relocates the compose/isolate enforcement point from the relevance/similarity locus to the residual-stream superposition locus (delta_q), coupling detection (reading delta_q) and action (gating) through that single signal — the C01 signature relocation-plus-coupling is performed, not merely the parent's generic audit gist.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries applied: the C07 entry performs diagnose-localize/tiny-lever/stabilize on delta_q, and the C01 entry performs the locus relocation (relevance -> superposition) with coupled detection-and-action, so core_mechanism instantiates each cited cluster's distinctive move rather than the parent's generic idea."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["self_supervised_signal_engineering","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented reject-favored compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; the candidate's composition set {self_supervised_signal_engineering, assumption_audit_and_pivot} contains no heterogeneous_decomposition, so no anti-pattern matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"openalex:W7160458174","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"SCALE-LoRA (Auditing Post-Retrieval LoRA Composition with Residual Merging and View Reliability) makes the same core observation the candidate's audit leg rests on — 'retrieving relevant adapters does not guarantee that their parameter updates are compatible, and composing adapters does not guarantee reliable outputs' — and introduces a Sparse-Composition Agreement Layer that checks composition reliability for open-pool LoRA reuse given a small support set. The candidate's claim stands or falls on whether its per-input superposition residual delta_q (the norm of the joint module effect minus the sum of solo module effects in the frozen residual stream, used as a label-free, support-set-free compose/isolate gate for a continual stream) is a genuinely distinct enforcement locus from SCALE's support-set-driven agreement/view-reliability layer. It is not exact-mechanism overlap: SCALE uses a support set and an agreement layer over composed parameter updates, whereas delta_q is a single per-input activation-space superposition scalar requiring no support set and computed from solo-vs-joint forward passes; but the conceptual neighborhood is close enough that the differentiation must be sharpened and measured.","addressable_via":"Sharpen differentiation_from_lit and the audit-leg how_closed to state explicitly and measurably that delta_q is a support-set-free, per-input activation-space superposition residual (joint-minus-sum-of-solo) rather than SCALE-LoRA's support-set agreement layer over parameter updates or Gate-and-Merge's weight-space relevance gating."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"paper_pointed_threat openalex:W7160458174 (SCALE-LoRA) and the C01 novelty-boundary reject lesson: an adjacent interference-aware-composition paper exists and the candidate's distinct locus must be made explicit and measured.","fix_direction":"Append two entries to differentiation_from_lit: (1) paper_id openalex:W7160458174 (SCALE-LoRA) with delta stating that SCALE audits open-pool LoRA composition reliability using a support set and a sparse-composition agreement layer over parameter updates, whereas the candidate measures a support-set-free per-input activation-space superposition residual delta_q (joint module effect minus sum of solo effects) and gates a continual stream with no support set; (2) paper_id arxiv:2605.08702 (Gate-and-Merge) with delta stating that Gate-and-Merge merges concept LoRAs in weight space and gates to suppress irrelevant activations by relevance, whereas the candidate gates per-input on the measured superposition residual in activation space, so high-relevance/high-interference inputs are handled differently. Keep deltas substantive (what is measured/constructed), not 'different pattern'."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"gap_closure[1].how_closed","issue":"C01 borderline: the relocated enforcement locus must be stated as provably distinct from already-exploited loci.","fix_direction":"Extend the audit-leg how_closed to state that the relocated locus is the per-input residual-stream superposition residual delta_q = ||joint-effect - sum-of-solo-effects||, explicitly distinct from (a) the weight-space relevance gate of Gate-and-Merge and (b) the support-set agreement layer of SCALE-LoRA, and that the negative control (shuffled delta_q) measures that this specific locus, not average gate shrinkage, carries the signal."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Appended two entries — openalex:W7160458174 (SCALE-LoRA) and arxiv:2605.08702 (Gate-and-Merge) — each with a substantive delta stating what each prior method measures/constructs (support-set agreement layer over parameter updates; weight-space relevance gate) versus the candidate's support-set-free per-input activation-space superposition residual delta_q."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"gap_closure[1].how_closed","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Extended the audit-leg how_closed to state the relocated locus is the per-input residual-stream superposition residual delta_q = ||joint-effect - sum-of-solo-effects||, explicitly distinct from Gate-and-Merge's weight-space relevance gate and SCALE-LoRA's support-set agreement layer, and that the negative control (shuffled delta_q) measures that this specific locus, not average gate shrinkage, carries the signal."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Superposition-Gated Composition: Measuring Module Interference for Compositional Continual Learning\n\n**Method.** Superposition-Gated Composition (SGC)\n\n## Motivation\nModern continual learning keeps a big pretrained model frozen and, for each new task, trains a tiny add-on module (a LoRA or prefix adapter). When a new input arrives, the system picks the most relevant stored modules and turns them on together, hoping their skills combine. The catch: it picks modules by how relevant they look, never by whether their effects actually add up. Two modules can both be relevant and still fight each other — pushing the frozen model's internal activations in opposite directions — so turning both on can corrupt the answer instead of combining the skills. Today's systems (MoCL, Self-Expansion-MoA, L2R) cannot even see this happening, because they only look at relevance scores and never look at the place inside the model where the interference actually occurs.\n\nWhat is newly possible is reading, from the frozen model's own internal activations, exactly how each module changes the output. We run a couple of cheap extra forward passes — one per module alone, one with all modules together — and compare the combined change to the sum of the individual changes. If they match, the modules add up cleanly; if they diverge, the modules are interfering. That single number, which we call $delta_{q},$ requires no labels and no extra data. We then gate the modules on it: compose when $delta_{q}$ says the effects superpose, and fall back to using just the single most-relevant module when $delta_{q}$ says they clash. One threshold is tuned once; nothing in the big model or the modules is retrained. The payoff is that combining skills for compound tasks becomes evidence-driven and reliable instead of a silent gamble, and we can finally separate corruption caused by module interference from ordinary forgetting.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n\n1. Take an existing modular continual learner exactly as published: a frozen foundation model, a library of frozen per-task adapter modules (Low-Rank Adaptation, LoRA, or prefix adapters, one per task), and its relevance router. For an input x, let the router do its normal job and return the small candidate set S of modules to consider (its usual top-k, which is 2 here because each compound input mixes two skills), each with a relevance weight and rank. Train nothing in this step.\n   - _Why_: We change only how modules are combined, not the modules themselves, so the gain is attributable to the gate.\n\n### Composability measurement\n*Reads a per-input, label-free scalar $delta_{q}$ from the frozen residual stream that says whether co-activated modules superpose or interfere.*\n\n2. Run x once through the frozen backbone with every adapter switched off, and save the internal hidden states $h_{l}(0)$ at each layer l (read as the residual-stream value feeding the next block). This 'no-module' run is the baseline you measure every module against, and caching it lets later runs skip recomputing the shared lower layers.\n   - _Why_: You need a no-module baseline to define what each module actually does to the activations.\n3. For each candidate module m, run the model with only that module turned on and record its internal effect $h_{l}(m)$; then run once with all candidate modules on and record the combined effect $h_{l}(S).$ Subtracting the no-module baseline gives each module's solo effect $(h_{l}(m) -  h_{l}(0))$ and the combined effect $(h_{l}(S) -  h_{l}(0)),$ read at the last quarter of the network's layers, taken at the position that actually decides the answer (the last token for a text generator, the class/pooled token for a vision model). This needs k+1 cheap runs for k modules and no labels.\n   - _Why_: These solo-vs-joint readings are the raw material for telling whether the modules add up or fight.\n4. Compute the single number $delta_{q}(x):$ at each chosen layer take the combined effect minus the sum of the individual effects, measure its size (an L2 norm), divide by the total size of the individual effects (so it is scale-free), and average across the chosen layers. A value near 0 means the modules simply add up (safe to compose); a large value means they overwrite each other (interference). This one number is both the measurement and the switch the next step flips.\n\n*The per-layer superposition residual $r_{l}(x):$ the norm of the joint module effect minus the sum of the per-module solo effects on layer-l hidden states; zero means the effects add up linearly, large means they overwrite each other.*\n$$ r_l(x) = \\left\\| \\big(h_l(S)-h_l(0)\\big) - \\sum_{m\\in S}\\big(h_l(m)-h_l(0)\\big) \\right\\|_2 \\tag{1} $$\n\n\n*The per-input superposition residual $delta_{q}(x): r_{l}$ normalized by the summed solo-effect norm and averaged over a fixed late-layer set L*, landing in [0, ~2] with eps = 1e-6 fixed.*\n$$ \\delta_q(x) = \\frac{1}{|L^*|}\\sum_{l\\in L^*} \\frac{r_l(x)}{\\sum_{m\\in S}\\|h_l(m)-h_l(0)\\|_2 + \\varepsilon} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: One scalar captures, per input, how far co-activated modules depart from simply adding up — the missing composability measurement.\n\n### Superposition-gated decision\n*Turns $delta_{q}$ into per-module gates that compose when effects add up and isolate the top module when they clash.*\n\n5. Turn $delta_{q}$ into on/off-ish weights for each module: $g_{m} = \\sigma (\\beta \\cdot (\\tau  -  delta_{q}(x))),$ with $\\beta $ fixed at 8 and one tuned threshold $\\tau .$ Always keep the single most-relevant module fully on; weight every other candidate module by $g_{m}.$ When $delta_{q}$ is small the weights are near 1 (compose); when $delta_{q}$ is large they drop toward 0 (use just the best module). With two candidates this gates exactly one module, so it is unambiguous. 【author decision: with more than two candidates the same single weight is applied to all the non-top modules; whether to keep one shared weight or attribute interference to specific modules is a design choice the authors must settle, because per-module attribution redefines the measured signal.】\n\n*The composition gate $g_{m}$ for module m: a sigmoid of the threshold tau minus $delta_{q}$ with fixed temperature beta = 8, so small $delta_{q}$ drives $g_{m}$ to 1 (compose) and large $delta_{q}$ drives $g_{m}$ to 0 for all but the top-relevance module (isolate).*\n$$ g_m = \\sigma\\big(\\beta\\,(\\tau - \\delta_q(x))\\big) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: It composes only when the measurement says effects superpose, and safely isolates when they clash, so a bad signal cannot collapse the output.\n6. Produce the final answer by running the model with each active module's contribution multiplied by its weight $g_{m}.$ Because the weight scales how much that module pushes on the model's internals, this run actually changes the output the model gives. The measured signal — not the relevance score — now drives the result.\n   - _Why_: The measured signal, not the relevance score, now drives what the model produces.\n7. Tune the one threshold $\\tau $ on a held-out set of compound tasks: try 50 evenly spaced values across the range of $delta_{q}$ actually seen on that set (then refine around the best), and pick the $\\tau $ that gives the highest compound-task accuracy; freeze it. Use one $\\tau $ per backbone and task order $(delta_{q}'s$ scale can differ by backbone), and report it. This is the only number the method fits — nothing inside the model or the modules is retrained.\n   - _Why_: One scalar tuned on compound data sets where composition starts to hurt, keeping the method almost training-free.\n\n### Observability and mechanism control\n*Logs the per-input signal and runs the $shuffled-delta_{q}$ control that proves the gain comes from measuring interference, not average shrinkage.*\n\n8. While evaluating, record $delta_{q}(x)$ and the compose-or-isolate decision for every input, and mark each output right or wrong using the task's normal scoring (exact match for classification; the benchmark's per-example check for generated answers). Then measure how $delta_{q}$ tracks correctness (a correlation between the number and the right/wrong outcome). The prediction is that higher $delta_{q}$ goes with more errors.\n   - _Why_: It makes composition quality observable for the first time and provides the data for the falsification check.\n9. Run the key control: shuffle the $delta_{q}$ values among inputs (each input gets some other input's real $delta_{q}),$ so the overall spread of values is identical but the link to the specific input is gone; keep the same gating and threshold and regenerate the answers. Average over a few shuffles (say 5) and compare to the always-compose baseline. If the improvement disappears, it really came from measuring interference; if it survives, it only came from generally turning modules down.\n   - _Why_: If accuracy collapses back to always-compose, the gain truly came from measuring interference; if not, it came only from average shrinkage and the claim fails.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 超叠加门控组合：为组合式持续学习度量模块间干扰\n\n**方法名称.** Superposition-Gated Composition (SGC)\n\n## 研究动机\n现在的持续学习做法是：把一个大的预训练模型冻住不动，每学一个新任务就训练一个很小的附加模块（一个 LoRA 或 prefix 适配器）。来了新输入时，系统挑出最相关的几个已存模块一起打开，期望它们的技能能组合起来。问题在于：它是按“看起来有多相关”来挑模块的，从不看这些模块的效果是否真的能叠加。两个模块可能都很相关，却仍然互相打架——把冻结模型内部的激活往相反方向推——于是同时打开它们可能不是组合技能，而是把答案搞坏。现有系统（MoCL、Self-Expansion-MoA、L2R）甚至看不到这种情况，因为它们只看相关性分数，从不去看模型内部真正发生干扰的那个地方。\n\n如今新可行的，是直接从冻结模型自己的内部激活里读出每个模块到底如何改变输出。我们多跑几次便宜的前向传播——每个模块单独跑一次，再把所有模块一起跑一次——把“合起来的改变”和“各自改变之和”作比较。两者吻合，说明模块干净地叠加；两者偏离，说明模块在互相干扰。这个单一的数值我们称为 $delta_{q}$，它不需要标签、也不需要额外数据。然后我们用它来门控模块：当 $delta_{q}$ 表示效果可叠加时就组合，当 $delta_{q}$ 表示效果冲突时就退回到只用最相关的那一个模块。只需一次性调一个阈值 tau，大模型和模块都不重新训练。好处是：在复合任务上组合技能从“无声的赌博”变成有证据支撑的、可靠的决策，而且我们终于能把模块干扰造成的损坏和普通的遗忘区分开来。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景\n\n1. 原封不动地采用一个已发表的模块化持续学习器：一个冻结的基础模型、一批冻结的按任务划分的适配器模块（Low-Rank Adaptation, LoRA，或 prefix 适配器，每个任务一个），以及它的相关性 router。对输入 x，让 router 照常工作，返回一个小的候选模块集合 S（它惯常的 top-k，这里取 2，因为每个复合输入混合了两种技能），并给出每个模块的相关性权重和排名。这一步不训练任何东西。\n   - _为什么_: 我们只改“怎么组合模块”，不改模块本身，这样收益才能归因于门控。\n\n### 可组合性度量\n*从冻结残差流中读出逐输入、无标签的标量 $delta_{q}$，判断共激活模块是叠加还是干扰。*\n\n2. 把 x 在冻结骨干上、所有适配器关闭的情况下前向跑一次，保存每层 l 的内部隐状态 $h_{l}(0)$（取作流入下一层的残差流值）。这次“无模块”运行是度量每个模块的基线，而且缓存它能让后续运行跳过对共享底层的重复计算。\n   - _为什么_: 需要一个“无模块”基线，才能定义每个模块对激活到底做了什么。\n3. 对每个候选模块 m，只打开该模块运行模型并记录它的内部效应 $h_{l}(m)$；再把所有候选模块都打开运行一次，记录合起来的效应 $h_{l}(S)$。减去“无模块”基线，就得到每个模块的单独效应（$h_{l}(m) -  h_{l}(0)$）和合起来的效应（$h_{l}(S) -  h_{l}(0)$），都在网络后四分之一的层上读取，并取在真正决定答案的位置（文本生成取最后一个 token，视觉模型取 class/池化 token）。k 个模块只需 k+1 次便宜的运行，且无需标签。\n   - _为什么_: 这些“单独 vs 联合”的读数，是判断模块是叠加还是打架的原材料。\n4. 计算单一数值 $delta_{q}(x)$：在每个选定层，把“合起来的效应”减去“各单独效应之和”，量出它的大小（L2 范数），再除以各单独效应的总大小（使其无量纲），然后在选定层上取平均。接近 0 表示模块只是简单相加（可以安全组合）；很大则表示它们互相覆盖（干扰）。这个数既是度量，也是下一步要拨动的开关。\n\n*逐层超叠加残差 $r_{l}(x)$：联合模块效应减去各模块单独效应之和在第 l 层隐状态上的范数；为 0 表示效应线性叠加，越大表示彼此覆盖（破坏性干扰）。*\n$$ r_l(x) = \\left\\| \\big(h_l(S)-h_l(0)\\big) - \\sum_{m\\in S}\\big(h_l(m)-h_l(0)\\big) \\right\\|_2 \\tag{1} $$\n\n\n*逐输入超叠加残差 $delta_{q}(x)$：将 $r_{l}$ 用各模块单独效应范数之和归一化，并在固定的后段层集合 L* 上取平均，取值约在 [0, ~2]，eps = 1e-6 固定。*\n$$ \\delta_q(x) = \\frac{1}{|L^*|}\\sum_{l\\in L^*} \\frac{r_l(x)}{\\sum_{m\\in S}\\|h_l(m)-h_l(0)\\|_2 + \\varepsilon} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 一个标量就逐输入刻画了共激活模块偏离“简单相加”的程度——这正是缺失的可组合性度量。\n\n### 超叠加门控决策\n*把 $delta_{q}$ 转成逐模块门控：效果可叠加就组合，冲突就退回到最相关的单一模块。*\n\n5. 把 $delta_{q}$ 转成每个模块的“近似开关”权重：$g_{m} = \\sigma (\\beta \\cdot (\\tau  -  delta_{q}(x)))$，其中 $\\beta $ 固定为 8，$\\tau $ 是一个调出来的阈值。始终保留最相关的那个模块（完全打开）；其余候选模块按 $g_{m}$ 加权。$delta_{q}$ 小时权重接近 1（组合）；$delta_{q}$ 大时趋近 0（只用最好的那个模块）。在两个候选时恰好门控一个模块，因此毫无歧义。【作者需决定：候选超过两个时，同一个权重被统一施加到所有非最相关模块上；究竟保留单一共享权重，还是把干扰归因到具体模块，是作者必须确定的设计选择，因为逐模块归因会改变所度量信号的定义。】\n\n*模块 m 的组合门 $g_{m}$：对 tau 减 $delta_{q}$ 取 sigmoid，温度 beta = 8 固定；$delta_{q}$ 小则 $g_{m}$ 趋近 1（组合），$delta_{q}$ 大则除最相关模块外 $g_{m}$ 趋近 0（隔离）。*\n$$ g_m = \\sigma\\big(\\beta\\,(\\tau - \\delta_q(x))\\big) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 只有当度量说效果可叠加时才组合，冲突时安全隔离，这样坏信号也不会把输出搞崩。\n6. 产出最终答案：运行模型时，把每个激活模块的贡献乘以它的权重 $g_{m}$。由于这个权重决定了该模块对模型内部的推动幅度，这次运行真正改变了模型给出的输出。现在驱动结果的是度量信号，而不是相关性分数。\n   - _为什么_: 现在驱动模型输出的是度量信号，而不是相关性分数。\n7. 在一个留出的复合任务集合上调这一个阈值 $\\tau $：在该集合上 $delta_{q}$ 实际出现的范围内取 50 个等间距取值（再在最优处附近细化），选出使复合任务准确率最高的 $\\tau $，然后冻结它。每个骨干和任务顺序用一个 $\\tau $（$delta_{q}$ 的尺度会随骨干不同而变化），并报告它。这是方法唯一拟合的数值——模型内部和模块都不重新训练。\n   - _为什么_: 用复合数据调一个标量，确定组合从哪里开始变坏，让方法几乎免训练。\n\n### 可观测性与机制对照\n*记录逐输入信号，并运行打乱 $delta_{q}$ 的对照，证明收益来自度量干扰而非平均缩放。*\n\n8. 评估时，对每个输入记录 $delta_{q}(x)$ 和组合/隔离决策，并用任务惯常的评分把每个输出标为对或错（分类用 exact match；生成答案用基准自带的逐样本判定）。然后测量 $delta_{q}$ 与正确性如何关联（这个数值与对/错结果之间的相关性）。预测是：$delta_{q}$ 越高，错误越多。\n   - _为什么_: 这第一次让组合质量变得可观测，也为证伪检验提供数据。\n9. 运行关键对照：把 $delta_{q}$ 的取值在各输入之间打乱（每个输入拿到另一个输入的真实 $delta_{q}$），这样取值的整体分布完全不变，但与具体输入的对应关系被破坏；门控和阈值保持不变，重新生成答案。对若干次打乱（比如 5 次）取平均，并与“总是组合”基线比较。若提升消失，说明它确实来自度量干扰；若提升仍在，则只是来自普遍调低模块。\n   - _为什么_: 若准确率退回到“总是组合”，说明收益真来自度量干扰；否则只是平均缩放，论点不成立。\n\n"},{"id":"97","run_dir":"run_prompt97_premiseselect","index":97,"title":"Prover-Closed Sets: Training a Lean Hammer's Premise Selector on Joint Proof Closure","title_zh":"Prover-Closed Sets：以联合证明闭合信号训练 Lean Hammer 的前提选择器","method_name":"Prover-Closed Set Selection (PCSS)","hook":"Every learned premise selector for a Lean hammer is trained to rank lemmas by per-premise relevance, yet the only quantity the hammer consumes is whether a small SET of lemmas jointly lets the external prover close the goal -- a target no current selector ever sees. We close the loop: run the hammer's own ATP on candidate premise sets, keep the sets it actually closes as manufactured positive labels, and train a non-separable set-scorer on them, so selection optimizes prover closure instead of retrieval recall.","anchor_pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","anchor_pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","domain_category":"Learning Theory & Statistics","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf supervises premise selection by whether the SHIPPED PREMISE SET let the external prover actually close the goal -- selectors optimize per-premise retrieval relevance against human-proof membership or query similarity, so a set that is high-recall yet jointly insufficient (redundant premises, a missing bridge lemma) is indistinguishable from a successful set at training time; the outcome that is missing is a selection signal that registers joint-set proof closure.","pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","sub_pattern":"C08 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by standing up the hammer's own external ATP as a data factory: a candidate-set generator proposes premise sets, each is run through Zipperposition/Vampire under a fixed time budget, and the single load-bearing quality gate -- did the prover CLOSE the goal -- relabels closed sets as manufactured positives and unclosed sets as hard negatives, which become the supervisory signal the selector never previously saw.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf models the JOINT utility / mutual redundancy among co-selected premises -- every selector emits an independent f(state, premise) score and takes top-k, so it cannot represent that two highly-ranked premises are substitutes (wasting a slot) or that a low-ranked bridging lemma is what makes the set complete; the missing outcome is a premise-set scorer whose value is not separable into per-premise terms.","pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","sub_pattern":"C21 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by recasting premise selection from top-k-of-independent-scores into a supervised set-valued object: the prover-closed sets manufactured by the anchor leg are relabeled as positive set-targets, and a permutation-invariant set encoder g(state, SET) -> closure-probability is trained on them, so its value is non-separable (it scores the set jointly, letting redundancy lower marginal gain and a bridge lemma raise it) and selection becomes greedy maximization of g under a cardinality budget rather than top-k of f.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"machine learning for premise selection in interactive/automated theorem proving (Lean 4 hammer)","n_papers":25,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":22},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10},{"source":"openreview","n":1}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":11,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"A Survey on Deep Learning for Theorem Proving"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Towards Automated Functional Equation Proving: A Benchmark Dataset and A Domain-Specific In-Context Agent"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Learning Guided Automated Reasoning: A Brief Survey"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Graph sequence learning for premise selection"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Advances in Medical Image Segmentation: A Comprehensive Review of Traditional, Deep Learning and Hybrid Approaches"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Generative AI for Self-Adaptive Systems: State of the Art and Research Roadmap"}],"more":5},{"year":2025,"n":24,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Saturation-Driven Dataset Generation for LLM Mathematical Reasoning in the TPTP Ecosystem"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"MIRB: Mathematical Information Retrieval Benchmark"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Premise Selection for a Lean Hammer"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Combining Textual and Structural Information for Premise Selection in Lean"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"MPS-Prover: Advancing Stepwise Theorem Proving by Multi-Perspective Search and Data Curation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"An Automated Theorem Generator with Theoretical Foundation Based on Rectangular Standard Contradiction"}],"more":18},{"year":2026,"n":11,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"LeanSearch v2: Global Premise Retrieval for Lean 4 Theorem Proving"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Quantum automated theorem proving"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"LLMORPH: Automated Metamorphic Testing of Large Language Models"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Automated Theorem Proving for Prolog Verification"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"On Reasoning-Centric LLM-based Automated Theorem Proving"}],"more":5}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":9,"share":0.36},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":6,"share":0.24},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":6,"share":0.24},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":4,"share":0.16},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":4,"share":0.16},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":4,"share":0.16},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":4,"share":0.16},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":3,"share":0.12}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Every retrieved learned premise selector for a Lean hammer scores premises POINTWISE and is trained/evaluated against a retrieval-relevance proxy rather than against the quantity the hammer actually consumes: a small premise SET whose JOINT logical content lets an external ATP discharge the goal. LeanHammer (semanticscholar:f9f28c89654f296f0e504f944750b38ebb3306c4) composes select -> translate -> reconstruct linearly and feeds the top-k individually-ranked premises forward, so the selector never sees whether those premises together sufficed for Zipperposition to close the goal. The text+structure GNN selector (semanticscholar:7b8c4171f344dfeb2c20120d90a141a851ed98ad) refines per-premise embeddings over the dependency graph but still emits an independent relevance score f(state, premise) and is supervised by which premises appeared in the human proof, not by set-level prover success. LeanSearch v2 (arxiv:2605.13137v2) explicitly names the SET objective ('global premise retrieval': the scattered lemmas whose joint use enables a concise proof) yet attains it with cosine retrieval + reranking + iterative LLM proof-sketching heuristics, with no learned model of set sufficiency and no signal back from whether the assembled set actually closed the proof. Consequently, when a top-k list contains k individually-relevant premises that are mutually redundant or jointly miss one bridging lemma, the hammer's translate+ATP stage silently fails and no component's training signal registers that the FAILURE was a set-composition failure rather than a ranking error (the gap is also invisible to MIRB, semanticscholar:10f936931c743622a1ad82dff960ba3f6817562b, which scores premise retrieval by per-query relevance, not set adequacy for closure).","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2605.13137v2","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"LeanSearch v2 introduces 'global premise retrieval' for Lean 4 -- given a formal theorem it iteratively sketches proof strategies and queries a cosine-similarity+reranker engine to ASSEMBLE the set of library premises needed for a concise proof, the first paper to make the premise SET (not the individual declaration) the retrieval target. Its residue: the set is assembled by an LLM-sketching loop over a retrieval substrate that is itself trained only on natural-language<->declaration similarity, so there is no learned model of joint set sufficiency and no closed loop in which the external prover's success/failure on the assembled set supervises the assembler -- set adequacy is heuristic and never verified against actual proof closure."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:f9f28c89654f296f0e504f944750b38ebb3306c4","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"LeanHammer builds a unified Lean hammer that routes premise-selection output both to external ATPs (via translation) and directly to reconstruction tactics, the first end-to-end neural-premise Lean hammer. Its residue: premise selection is a frozen upstream ranker whose top-k is passed forward independently; the ATP's success or failure on the shipped set never flows back to retrain or re-rank the selector, so the selector cannot learn that a particular COMBINATION under-covered the goal."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:7b8c4171f344dfeb2c20120d90a141a851ed98ad","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"The text+structure selector fuses ReProver dense text embeddings with an RGCN over the Mathlib dependency graph, improving per-premise relevance by exploiting reference/dependency structure. Its residue: the scoring function f(state, premise) remains pointwise and is supervised by human-proof premise membership, so even with graph context it ranks premises independently and optimizes recall of human-used lemmas rather than the joint sufficiency of the shipped set for an automated prover."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4406840466","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Learns an effective dense premise-retrieval model for mathematical formalization, improving retrieval quality for formal statements over generic dense retrievers. Its residue: optimizes a pointwise query-premise relevance objective with no notion of set-level coverage or a prover-grounded success signal -- it retrieves better individual premises but cannot tell whether the returned set jointly closes the goal."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"machine learning for premise selection in interactive/automated theorem proving (Lean 4 hammer)","venue":"ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML (ML) or CADE/ITP (formal methods); inferred ML-conference target","time":"2026 cycle","data":["Mathlib4 declaration corpus + dependency graph","Lean proof-state / goal traces","LeanHammer / LeanDojo extraction tooling","external ATP success labels (Zipperposition/Vampire/E/SMT call outcomes)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with access to Lean tooling; not assumed to be a Lean power-user","preference":"both","baseline":"ReProver dense dual-encoder premise selection; GNN-augmented (text+structure) selector; LeanSearch v2 global premise retrieval","limitation":"premise selectors are trained and evaluated on retrieval-style relevance (dependency labels / query similarity), decoupled from whether the selected premise SET actually lets the downstream external prover close the goal","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","compute","expertise","preference","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The pipeline is one sequential loop -- generate candidate premise SETS, prove them, filter by closure, retrain the set-scorer -- whose two legs share the prover-closure label as the connecting object. Leg 1 (manufacture the signal): for each training goal g with proof state s, an initial pointwise retriever R (a frozen ReProver-style dual encoder) returns a relevance-ranked shortlist of N=128 candidate premises from Mathlib4; a candidate-SET generator samples M=64 premise subsets of size k in {4,8,16} from this shortlist (sampling biased toward R's top scores but with stochastic inclusion of lower-ranked premises so the search reaches non-obvious bridge lemmas), translates each subset + goal to TPTP/SMT and runs the external ATP (Zipperposition first, Vampire fallback) under a fixed per-call wall-clock budget tau=10s. The single quality gate is binary CLOSED in {0,1}: the ATP returned a verified proof of g from that exact subset within tau. This yields, per goal, a labeled set {(SET_j, CLOSED_j)} -- the manufactured supervision that no prior selector sees. Leg 2 (reframe as a solvable set-object): we train a permutation-invariant set-scorer g_phi(s, SET) -> [0,1] (a DeepSets/set-transformer head over R's frozen premise embeddings concatenated with the state embedding; permutation-invariant by construction so the score depends on the set, not the order) with binary cross-entropy against CLOSED_j. g_phi is non-separable: it does NOT decompose into sum_i f(s, p_i), so two embedding-redundant premises contribute sub-additively (their pooled representation saturates) and a single bridge lemma whose presence flips CLOSED contributes a large positive marginal -- exactly the joint structure top-k cannot represent. At inference the hammer ships argmax over a cardinality-budget by greedy marginal-gain selection on g_phi (add the premise maximizing g_phi(s, SET cup {p}) until budget k or marginal gain < epsilon), then a single ATP call on the assembled set. The loop iterates: the improved g_phi reweights which subsets the generator samples next round (concentrating proving compute on sets near the current decision boundary), so the filter becomes implicit in generation per C08's strongest form. Every quantity is computable: R is frozen ReProver; embeddings are its ByT5 outputs; the set head is the only trained component; tau, N, M, k, epsilon are fixed hyperparameters; CLOSED is the literal ATP exit status. This does NOT reduce to internal RL clause-selection (the signal supervises the EXTERNAL premise set the hammer ships, upstream of the prover's internal loop -- the unoccupied position the lineage's collateral node marks) nor to pointwise dense retrieval (the trained object is a non-separable set-function, not f(s,p)).","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share one machinery, not two modules: the joint-set scorer (gap 2) is uncomputable without a joint-set LABEL, and the prover-closure label (gap 1) is wasted on a pointwise scorer that has no set-level parameters to shape -- so the manufactured signal and the set-object are the producer and consumer of a single pipeline, which is why coherence_thread_type is sequential_pipeline rather than two stapled contributions. (b) Considered an RL formulation (policy gradient over set construction with closure as reward) but rejected it: it re-imports online optimization and a reward-design step the C21 recast explicitly eliminates, and it risks regressing onto the collateral internal-RL clause-selection node the lineage flags; supervised BCE on relabeled closed sets keeps the contribution the reframe + manufactured-label substitution, not a new solver. Avoided nodes: pointwise dense-retrieval ancestor n3 (we train a non-separable set-function) and collateral c0 internal clause-selection RL (our signal supervises the external shipped set).","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on a held-out Mathlib4 goal split, ship each method's selected premise set to the same external ATP (Zipperposition, tau=10s) and measure end-to-end hammer goal-closure rate (fraction of goals the prover closes from the shipped set). If the candidate works, closure rate RISES versus top-k of the same frozen retriever R and versus the text+structure GNN selector at equal premise-budget k, while mean retrieval recall@k of the shipped set may stay flat or DROP (the surprising prediction: closure can improve while recall does not, because the set-scorer trades a redundant high-recall premise for a low-recall bridge lemma). The load-bearing variable is CLOSED_j, the per-set binary prover-closure label that supervises g_phi. Negative control: retrain g_phi with CLOSED replaced by pointwise human-proof-membership labels (the signal every prior selector uses) holding the set architecture, budget, and ATP fixed; the mechanism predicts end-to-end closure rate falls back toward the top-k baseline -- if closure stays high under the membership-label control, the gain came from the set architecture or extra compute, not from prover-grounded supervision, and the claim is falsified. Positive control: a stripped-down selector that scores sets using ONLY a single learned scalar -- predicted closure probability from CLOSED-trained g_phi with all premise features ablated to a count -- should still recover most of the closure-rate gain over top-k, confirming the manufactured closure signal, not the embedding richness, is the active ingredient.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2605.13137v2","delta":"LeanSearch v2 assembles the premise SET via an LLM proof-sketching loop over a cosine+reranker retrieval substrate trained on natural-language<->declaration similarity; we instead train a non-separable set-scorer directly on manufactured prover-CLOSURE labels, so set adequacy is learned from and verified against actual proof closure rather than estimated by retrieval heuristics."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:f9f28c89654f296f0e504f944750b38ebb3306c4","delta":"LeanHammer ships a frozen upstream pointwise ranker's top-k and never feeds the ATP's success on the shipped set back into selection; we construct exactly that closed loop, relabeling prover-closed sets as positive set-targets so the selector learns set-composition, not per-premise rank."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:7b8c4171f344dfeb2c20120d90a141a851ed98ad","delta":"The text+structure GNN still emits an independent f(state,premise) supervised by human-proof membership; we replace the separable scorer with a permutation-invariant set-function g(state,SET) whose value is non-decomposable and supervised by joint-set closure, representing redundancy and bridge-lemma effects the pointwise score cannot."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4414565840","delta":"Efficient Neural Clause-Selection RL learns selection from prover experience but INSIDE the saturation loop at the clause level; we lift a prover-grounded selection signal UPSTREAM to supervise the external premise SET the hammer ships before any ATP call, an artifact their internal-loop formulation does not produce."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"arxiv:2605.13137v2","what_step_was_missed":"LeanSearch v2 already makes the premise SET (not the individual declaration) the retrieval target and even loops an LLM to assemble it, but it never constructs a manufactured supervision signal from the external prover's closure of candidate sets, so it has no trained model of set sufficiency -- the missing step is generating candidate premise sets, running them through the ATP to obtain per-set CLOSED labels, and fitting a non-separable set-scorer to those labels, which is what turns heuristic set-assembly into a selector optimized against measured proof closure."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":144,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"Hard floor did not fire: gap_closure_reject_check has no candidate_match: yes (anchor is borderline only on the single-domain lesson, which the candidate answers with its demonstrably-new prover-closure-supervised set-scorer mechanism -- the lesson's own escape clause), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat (LeanSearch v2) is competing not exact-mechanism overlap. recipe_application_check.verdict = applied for both C08 and C21, so the candidate performs the cited tactical moves rather than the parent gist. The lone borderline is non-fatal and load-bearing-positive (the new mechanism), so advance, surfacing the single-domain-scope and LeanSearch-v2-baseline concerns into Phase 4 reviewer_concerns_and_responses.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf supervises premise selection by whether the SHIPPED PREMISE SET let the external prover actually close the goal -- selectors optimize per-premise retrieval relevance against human-proof membership or query similarity, so a set that is high-recall yet jointly insufficient (redundant premises, a missing bridge lemma) is indistinguishable from a successful set at training time; the outcome that is missing is a selection signal that registers joint-set proof closure.","main_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","sub_pattern":"C08 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is treating 'attach a generator plus a filter' as a sufficient contribution when generate-and-filter is already commonplace, so no single load-bearing insight separates the work; second, the unvalidated transfer assumption -- the corpus is built with synthetic instances but the paper never demonstrates the manufactured distribution generalizes to the real target.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A cooperative generate-and-filter loop sitting on substantial prior art needs either a demonstrably new mechanism or cross-domain breadth; showing it on a single domain invites the read that the method is domain-specific and incremental.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The loop is single-domain (Lean/Mathlib4), but the load-bearing new mechanism is the non-separable set-scorer supervised by EXTERNAL-prover closure (a label no prior premise selector manufactures), which is the demonstrably-new-mechanism the lesson offers as the alternative to cross-domain breadth."},{"lesson_quoted":"A newly proposed quality or gating score must be tightly argued to solve the stated problem under realistic conditions -- a loosely-motivated score evaluated in an artificial setup is dismissed as a solution looking for a problem.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The gate is not a newly-invented heuristic score: it is the literal ATP exit status CLOSED in {0,1} under the deployment time budget tau, i.e. exactly the downstream quantity the hammer must achieve, so it is the precise crux rather than a loosely-motivated proxy."},{"lesson_quoted":"Training on synthetically generated data without demonstrating transfer to the real target distribution leaves the core premise unvalidated, no matter how clean the synthetic labels are.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism_steps step 8 evaluates end-to-end hammer goal-closure on a held-out Mathlib split with the real ATP, so transfer to the real target metric is the headline measurement, not an intermediate proxy."},{"lesson_quoted":"A synthetic-data-factory claim collapses without comparison to cheaper classical baselines, because the necessity of the heavy generative model is then unverifiable.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The candidate benchmarks against top-k of the frozen retriever, the text+structure GNN, and a LeanSearch-v2-style retrieval set (step 8) plus a pointwise-membership-label negative control (step 9), so the necessity of the prover-closure signal over cheaper relevance signals is directly tested."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf models the JOINT utility / mutual redundancy among co-selected premises -- every selector emits an independent f(state, premise) score and takes top-k, so it cannot represent that two highly-ranked premises are substitutes (wasting a slot) or that a low-ranked bridging lemma is what makes the set complete; the missing outcome is a premise-set scorer whose value is not separable into per-premise terms.","main_pattern":"reframe_as_solvable_object","sub_pattern":"C21 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail when the reframe does not unlock a capability the native formulation lacked at credible scale -- e.g. the recast is a descriptive lens with no clear empirical win, or the substituted supervision rests on a brittle exact-algebraic assumption whose guarantees evaporate when only approximate.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A reframe used only as an evaluation or analysis lens, without a method that posts a clear win, reads as a descriptive benchmark and falls below the novelty bar even when the framing is reusable.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The reframe ships a trained selector evaluated on end-to-end hammer closure (a method with a win target), not a post-hoc relabeling lens used only to score collected data."},{"lesson_quoted":"A recast resting on an exact algebraic equivalence (target = exact polynomial of sources) inherits brittle, non-scaling machinery, and its formal guarantees collapse the moment the equivalence is only approximate.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The recast manufactures supervision empirically (CLOSED labels from real ATP runs) and fits a learned set-scorer by BCE -- it claims no exact-algebraic equivalence between set membership and closure, so there is no brittle equivalence to break."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating the recast only on toy environments, with an unexplained boundary failure such as performance degrading past a certain context or horizon length, directly undercuts the generalization claim.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Validation is on held-out Mathlib4 (a non-trivial real library), not a toy environment; the only boundary variable (premise-set cardinality k) is explicitly swept in {4,8,16}."}],"verdict":"clear"}],"verdict":"borderline","verdict_rationale":"The anchor (C08) entry is borderline -- not triggered -- solely on the single-domain generate-and-filter lesson; the candidate answers it with a demonstrably-new mechanism (the prover-closure-supervised non-separable set-scorer) which is the lesson's own stated escape hatch, and the other three C08 lessons plus all C21 lessons are clear. No Reject lesson is marked candidate_match: yes, so no hard-floor trigger."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf supervises premise selection by whether the SHIPPED PREMISE SET let the external prover actually close the goal ...","sub_pattern":"C08 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Stand up a controllable generative procedure to synthesize candidate training instances beyond the corpus's support, route every candidate through a single quality gate, fold retained instances back into training, and iterate so each improved model curates the next batch -- the object being manufactured is the training distribution itself.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism Leg 1 + steps 3-4-7 perform exactly this: a candidate-SET generator synthesizes premise subsets (including non-obvious low-ranked bridge lemmas, beyond what top-k retrieval covers), the single quality gate is the binary ATP closure CLOSED in {0,1}, retained labeled sets are folded into BCE training, and step 7 iterates by routing the updated scorer's boundary uncertainty back to bias round-2 sampling -- the C08 'close the loop dynamically' strongest form.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf models the JOINT utility / mutual redundancy among co-selected premises ...","sub_pattern":"C21 (Reframe as a Solvable Object)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Recast a problem that natively requires absent supervision (reward/labels/demonstrations) as a supervised or generative-sequence object by manufacturing the missing supervision from data that already exists -- retrospectively relabel achieved outcomes as targets -- so mature supervised machinery (maximum-likelihood, transformers) applies directly.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism Leg 2 performs the C21 move: premise selection natively lacks set-level supervision; the prover-closed sets are retrospectively relabeled as positive set-targets (achieved outcome -> training target) and the problem is recast as a supervised set-classification object g_phi(s,SET)->[0,1] solved by off-the-shelf BCE over a permutation-invariant set encoder.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries instantiate their cluster's signature move: C08's generator+single-quality-gate+iterate is realized with the ATP-closure gate, and C21's relabel-achieved-outcomes-as-targets + recast-as-supervised-object is realized by turning prover-closed sets into positive set-labels for a supervised set-scorer."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["self_supervised_signal_engineering","reframe_as_solvable_object"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented anti-pattern compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; the candidate's composition set is {self_supervised_signal_engineering, reframe_as_solvable_object}, which contains no heterogeneous_decomposition, architectural_operator_substitution, or structural_prior_encoding, so no 2-way subset matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"arxiv:2605.13137v2","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"LeanSearch v2 is the only prior work that makes the premise SET (not the individual declaration) the target -- its 'global premise retrieval' iteratively sketches proof strategies and queries a retrieval engine to assemble the set of library premises for a concise proof. The candidate's claim stands or falls on whether learning a non-separable set-scorer from MANUFACTURED PROVER-CLOSURE labels beats LeanSearch v2's heuristic assembly: if a cosine+reranker substrate driven by LLM proof-sketching already attains the joint set as well as a closure-supervised scorer, the candidate's added ATP-labeling loop is unjustified. The candidate's distinguishing artifact -- a learned set-function fit to real ATP CLOSED outcomes, with set adequacy verified against actual closure rather than retrieval similarity -- is exactly what LeanSearch v2 lacks (it never trains on or measures prover closure of the assembled set), so this is competing, not exact-mechanism, overlap.","addressable_via":"The candidate already names LeanSearch v2 as a required baseline (core_mechanism_steps step 8); the differentiation is dodged by ensuring falsification_prediction reports closure-rate vs LeanSearch-v2-assembled sets at equal budget and ATP, which the candidate's experiment specifies -- no field change needed, the threat is a baseline obligation already met."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Prover-Closed Sets: Training a Lean Hammer's Premise Selector on Joint Proof Closure\n\n**Method.** Prover-Closed Set Selection (PCSS)\n\n## Motivation\nA 'hammer' for the Lean proof assistant tries to prove a goal automatically by (1) picking a handful of relevant library facts (premises), (2) handing them to an external automated theorem prover (ATP), and (3) reconstructing the proof. The hard part is step (1): which facts to pick from a library of hundreds of thousands. Today's best premise pickers all score each fact on its own ('how relevant is this lemma to the goal?') and keep the top few. But the prover doesn't care about individual relevance -- it only succeeds or fails on whether the WHOLE little set of facts, taken together, is enough to close the goal under a time limit. A set can be full of individually-relevant facts that are redundant with each other, or that jointly miss one bridging lemma; then the prover fails, and nothing in the picker's training ever learns that the SET was the problem. Recent work (LeanSearch v2, 2026) finally treats the set as the thing to retrieve, but still assembles it with similarity heuristics and never checks whether the set actually closes the proof. Our idea closes that loop: we generate many candidate sets, actually run the hammer's prover on each one, keep the sets it really closes as positive examples, and train a 'set scorer' that judges a whole set at once (not fact-by-fact). Because the scorer looks at the set jointly, it can learn that a redundant extra fact wastes a slot while a low-ranked bridge lemma completes the proof -- something a fact-by-fact picker cannot represent. When this works, premise selection stops being a relevance-search stand-in and becomes a component trained directly on what actually makes proofs succeed.\n\n## Method\n### Background\n*Frozen retriever shortlist shared by all baselines.*\n\n1. For each goal in Mathlib4 and its proof state, run a frozen ReProver-style dual-encoder retriever (the public LeanDojo checkpoint) to turn the state and every library premise into vectors, and keep the 128 premises whose vectors are most similar (cosine) to the state. Serialize the state the way LeanDojo does (the printed goal plus local hypotheses). Save which premises the human proof actually used, but only to score yourself later, never as the training signal. Output: 128 candidate premises per goal, each with its vector and retriever score.\n   - _Why_: You need a manageable candidate pool, and freezing the retriever means any later gain comes from the set-level idea, not a fancier encoder.\n\n### Prover-grounded labeling\n*Manufacture per-set proof-closure labels by running the hammer's own external ATP on generated candidate premise sets.*\n\n2. From the 128-premise shortlist of each goal, build 64 candidate SETS by random sampling without replacement. Pick high-scoring premises more often (a softmax over the retriever scores) but blend in a flat 15% chance for any premise, so low-ranked-but-possibly-crucial bridge lemmas still show up in roughly one in seven picks. Choose each set's size at random from 4, 8, or 16 premises. Output: 64 candidate sets per goal.\n   - _Why_: To learn what makes a set close a proof you must first produce many varied sets, including ones the plain top-k would never assemble.\n3. For each candidate set and goal, hand them to the external automated theorem prover (ATP) exactly the way the hammer normally does -- reuse LeanHammer's own translation into the prover's format (TPTP/SMT) -- and run Zipperposition for 10 seconds (using Vampire as a backup if translation fails). Mark the set CLOSED = 1 only if the prover returns a proof that the hammer's reconstruction step actually accepts; otherwise CLOSED = 0. Note the time it took. Output: every candidate set tagged with its closed/not-closed label and timing.\n\n*The manufactured label for candidate set $S_{j}$ on goal g is 1 exactly when the external ATP closes g from $S_{j}$ within time budget $\\tau ,$ else 0.*\n$$ \\mathrm{CLOSED}_j = \\mathbb{1}\\big[\\, \\mathrm{ATP}(g,\\, S_j;\\, \\tau) = \\text{proved} \\,\\big] \\in \\{0,1\\} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The prover's yes/no verdict is exactly the thing the hammer must achieve, so it is the right label to train on -- no invented proxy score.\n\n### Non-separable set-scorer\n*Train and deploy a permutation-invariant set-function that judges joint set sufficiency rather than per-premise relevance.*\n\n4. Train a 'set scorer' that takes a proof state and a whole premise SET and outputs the probability the prover would close the goal from that set, fitting it to the closed/not-closed labels with binary cross-entropy. Build it so the score reads the set jointly (not premise-by-premise): combine each premise's vector with the state's vector through a small network, then pool them with a Set Transformer (an attention-based set network that lets premises interact, so two redundant premises don't double-count), and finish with a layer plus a sigmoid. Balance positive and negative sets during training and stop when held-out accuracy peaks; only the scorer is trained, the retriever stays frozen. 【author decision: pick the set-pooling network (Set Transformer vs DeepSets with cross-attention) by validation, not by assertion.】 Output: a trained set scorer.\n\n*The set-scorer pools premise embeddings $e_{p}$ (with state embedding $e_{s})$ through a permutation-invariant aggregator $\\rho $ and an MLP, so its closure-probability output is a set-function that does not separate into per-premise scores.*\n$$ g_\\phi(s, S) = \\sigma\\!\\Big( \\mathrm{MLP}\\big( \\rho\\big( \\textstyle\\sum_{p \\in S} \\psi(e_p,\\, e_s) \\big) \\big) \\Big), \\qquad g_\\phi(s,S) \\neq \\textstyle\\sum_{p\\in S} f(s,p) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Only a scorer that reads the set jointly can represent that two facts are redundant or that one bridge lemma completes the set.\n5. To use the trained scorer at proving time, build the set greedily: start empty and keep adding the one remaining premise that raises the scorer's value the most, re-checking all candidates each round, until you hit the premise budget k or the best available gain drops below a small cutoff $\\epsilon .$ Set k equal to whatever premise budget the baseline hammer uses so the comparison is fair, and pick $\\epsilon $ on validation data. Send the finished set to a single prover call. Because the scorer decides which premises go in, improving it directly changes which set ships and whether the goal gets proved. Output: the shipped set and whether the hammer closed the goal.\n\n*At inference the selector greedily adds the premise that maximizes the set-scorer's marginal gain until the cardinality budget k is hit or the marginal gain falls below $\\epsilon .$*\n$$ S \\leftarrow S \\cup \\{\\, \\arg\\max_{p \\notin S} \\; g_\\phi(s,\\, S \\cup \\{p\\}) \\,\\}\\quad \\text{until } |S|=k \\text{ or } \\Delta g_\\phi < \\varepsilon \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Greedy marginal-gain assembly is the natural way to deploy a set scorer under a fixed premise budget, and it directly changes which set (and thus which proof outcome) the hammer ships.\n\n### Closed-loop refinement\n*Concentrate expensive proving on boundary sets the scorer is uncertain about and retrain.*\n\n6. Repeat the cycle to improve the scorer: use the current scorer to pick the next batch of sets to actually prove, focusing on the ones it is most unsure about (predicted closure probability near one-half), run them through the prover, add their new labels, and retrain. Spend most of the prover budget (about 70%) on these uncertain sets and the rest on fresh random sets so the model keeps exploring. 【author decision: how many refinement rounds to run and exactly how 'uncertain' a set must be to qualify are tuning choices, set by whether each round still improves held-out closure rate.】 Output: the next round's labeled sets and the retrained scorer.\n   - _Why_: Spending prover time on sets whose outcome you can't yet predict gives the most new information per expensive prover call.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# Prover-Closed Sets：以联合证明闭合信号训练 Lean Hammer 的前提选择器\n\n**方法名称.** Prover-Closed Set Selection (PCSS)\n\n## 研究动机\nLean 证明助手的 hammer 会自动尝试证明一个目标：先（1）从库里挑出少量相关的引理（前提），再（2）把它们交给外部的自动定理证明器（ATP），最后（3）重建证明。难点在第（1）步：在几十万条库引理里挑哪几条。如今最好的前提选择器都是逐条给每个引理打分（这条引理和目标有多相关），然后取分数最高的几条。但证明器并不在乎单条相关性——它只看这一小组前提作为整体、在时间限制内能不能把目标证下来。一组前提里可能每条都相关却彼此冗余，或者整体上恰好缺了一条起桥梁作用的引理；这时证明器就会失败，而选择器的训练信号里没有任何东西能学到问题出在这个集合上。最近的工作（LeanSearch v2，2026）终于把集合当成检索目标，但仍用相似度启发式去拼装集合，从不检验这个集合是否真能把证明闭合。我们的想法就是把这个回路闭上：生成大量候选集合，真的用 hammer 自己的证明器逐一去跑，把它真正证下来的集合当作正样本，训练一个一次性评估整组前提（而非逐条）的集合打分器。由于打分器是联合地看整个集合，它能学到：多放一条冗余前提会浪费名额，而一条排名靠后的桥梁引理却能补全证明——这正是逐条打分器无法表达的。一旦奏效，前提选择就不再是相关性检索的替身，而成为直接以证明成败为目标训练出来的部件。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景\n*所有基线共享的冻结检索器候选名单。*\n\n1. 对 Mathlib4 中每个目标及其证明状态，运行一个冻结的 ReProver 式双编码器检索器(dual-encoder retriever，使用公开的 LeanDojo checkpoint)，把状态和每条库前提都编码成向量，保留与状态向量余弦相似度最高的 128 条前提。状态按 LeanDojo 的方式序列化(打印出的目标加上局部假设)。把人工证明实际用到的前提记录下来，但只用于后续给自己评分，绝不作为训练信号。输出：每个目标对应 128 条候选前提，各自带有向量和检索器分数。\n   - _为什么_: 需要一个规模可控的候选池；冻结检索器能保证后续的提升来自集合层面的思路，而不是更强的编码器。\n\n### 基于证明器的打标\n*通过用 hammer 自己的外部 ATP 跑生成的候选前提集合，合成每个集合的证明闭合标签。*\n\n2. 从每个目标的 128 条候选名单里，用无放回随机采样构建 64 个候选集合(SET)。让高分前提更常被选中(对检索器分数做 softmax)，但混入 15% 的均匀概率，使排名靠后却可能关键的桥梁引理仍能在大约七分之一的采样中出现。每个集合的大小从 4、8、16 中随机选取。输出：每个目标 64 个候选集合。\n   - _为什么_: 要学会什么样的集合能闭合证明，必须先产出大量多样的集合，包括纯 top-k 永远不会拼出的那些。\n3. 对每个候选集合和目标，像 hammer 平时那样交给外部自动定理证明器(Automated Theorem Prover, ATP)——复用 LeanHammer 自带的、把前提集合翻译成证明器格式(TPTP/SMT)的流程——并用 Zipperposition 跑 10 秒(翻译失败时以 Vampire 兜底)。仅当证明器返回的证明能被 hammer 的重建阶段接受时，才把该集合标为 CLOSED = 1，否则为 0(超时或失败)，对应公式 (1)。同时记录耗时。输出：每个候选集合附带其闭合/未闭合标签与耗时。\n\n*候选集合 $S_{j}$ 在目标 g 上的人工合成标签：当外部 ATP 在时间预算 $\\tau $ 内从 $S_{j}$ 证明出 g 时取 1，否则取 0。*\n$$ \\mathrm{CLOSED}_j = \\mathbb{1}\\big[\\, \\mathrm{ATP}(g,\\, S_j;\\, \\tau) = \\text{proved} \\,\\big] \\in \\{0,1\\} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 证明器的是/否判定正是 hammer 必须达成的目标，所以它就是该训练的标签——无需任何人为设计的代理分数。\n\n### 不可分集合打分器\n*训练并部署一个置换不变的集合函数，评估集合的联合充分性而非逐前提相关性。*\n\n4. 训练一个集合打分器(set scorer)：输入一个证明状态和整组前提集合(SET)，输出证明器从该集合闭合目标的概率，用二元交叉熵拟合闭合/未闭合标签。要让分数整体读取集合(而非逐前提)：先用一个小网络把每条前提的向量与状态向量结合，再用 Set Transformer(一种基于注意力的集合网络，让前提之间相互作用，使两条冗余前提不被重复计分)做汇聚，最后接一层加 sigmoid。训练时平衡正负集合，在留出集准确率达峰时停止；只训练打分器，检索器保持冻结。【作者需决定：集合汇聚网络(Set Transformer 还是带交叉注意力的 DeepSets)应由验证集选定，而非直接断言。】输出：训练好的集合打分器。\n\n*集合打分器通过置换不变的聚合算子 $\\rho $ 与 MLP 汇聚各前提嵌入 $e_{p}$（连同状态嵌入 $e_{s}$），其闭合概率输出是一个集合函数，无法拆解为逐前提分数之和。*\n$$ g_\\phi(s, S) = \\sigma\\!\\Big( \\mathrm{MLP}\\big( \\rho\\big( \\textstyle\\sum_{p \\in S} \\psi(e_p,\\, e_s) \\big) \\big) \\Big), \\qquad g_\\phi(s,S) \\neq \\textstyle\\sum_{p\\in S} f(s,p) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 只有联合读取整个集合的打分器，才能表达两条前提相互冗余、或某条桥梁引理补全集合这类信息。\n5. 在证明时使用训练好的打分器：贪心地构建集合——从空集开始，每轮重新评估所有剩余前提，加入使打分器值提升最多的那一条，直到达到前提预算 k 或最大可得增益低于一个小阈值 $\\epsilon $。把 k 设为基线 hammer 所用的前提预算以保证比较公平，$\\epsilon $ 在验证集上选取。把拼好的集合交给一次证明器调用。由于打分器决定哪些前提入选，改进它会直接改变送出的集合以及目标是否被证明。输出：送出的集合，以及 hammer 是否闭合了该目标。\n\n*推理时，选择器贪心地加入使集合打分器边际增益最大的前提，直到达到基数预算 k 或边际增益低于 $\\epsilon $。*\n$$ S \\leftarrow S \\cup \\{\\, \\arg\\max_{p \\notin S} \\; g_\\phi(s,\\, S \\cup \\{p\\}) \\,\\}\\quad \\text{until } |S|=k \\text{ or } \\Delta g_\\phi < \\varepsilon \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 在固定前提预算下，按边际增益贪心拼装是部署集合打分器的自然方式，并直接改变 hammer 实际送出的集合（以及由此产生的证明结果）。\n\n### 闭环精炼\n*把昂贵的证明计算集中在打分器不确定的边界集合上并重训。*\n\n6. 重复该循环以改进打分器：用当前打分器挑选下一批真正要去证明的集合，聚焦于它最不确定的那些(预测闭合概率接近二分之一)，送入证明器，加入新标签并重训。把大部分证明器预算(约 70%)花在这些不确定集合上，其余用于全新随机集合以保持探索。【作者需决定：跑多少轮精炼、以及集合要多『不确定』才入选，属于调参选择，依据每轮是否仍提升留出集闭合率来确定。】输出：下一轮的带标签集合与重训后的打分器。\n   - _为什么_: 把证明器时间花在你尚无法预测结果的集合上，每次昂贵的证明器调用带来的新信息最多。\n\n"},{"id":"98","run_dir":"run_prompt98_gaussiansurfels","index":98,"title":"Reliability-Weighted Radiometric Consistency for Gaussian Surfel Inverse Rendering","title_zh":"面向高斯面元逆向渲染的可靠性加权辐射一致性方法","method_name":"Reliability-Weighted RadioGS (RW-RadioGS)","hook":"RadioGS supervises unobserved-direction surfel radiance toward a physically-based-rendered target it treats as ground truth, but that target is a Monte-Carlo estimate whose variance is largest exactly where the constraint matters most — occluded inter-reflecting interiors — so a uniform L1 residual spends equal optimization pressure on a confidently-estimated direction and on a near-random one. We make the rendering-equation forward map define the surfel radiance by construction and weight every consistency residual by the renderer's own per-direction estimator reliability, so the self-supervision concentrates where its teacher is trustworthy instead of memorizing its noise.","anchor_pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","anchor_pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","domain_category":"3D Vision & Scene Reconstruction","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf accounts for the RELIABILITY of its own physically-based self-supervision target when constraining unobserved-direction indirect radiance: the PBR/Monte-Carlo radiance used as the consistency teacher is a noisy, material-dependent estimate, yet every leaf treats it as an equally-trustworthy point target across all surfels and directions, so optimization pressure is mis-allocated away from the high-error regions the constraint exists to fix (additive need; sits at the RadioGS/IR","pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","sub_pattern":"C08 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by treating the 2D-Gaussian-ray-traced PBR radiance as a manufactured-instance factory and inserting one load-bearing quality gate — a per-direction Monte-Carlo reliability weight derived from the renderer's own sample variance — that down-weights high-variance unobserved directions, plus the advanced closed-loop form that routes each surfel's current residual back into the ray-tracer's sample budget so tracing concentrates on the high-error directions the constraint exists for.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions whether radiometric consistency must be imposed as a soft post-hoc residual penalty on an otherwise free per-surfel radiance at all, rather than the question of whether the unobserved-direction radiance should be a free parameter that consistency is asked to correct after the fact (subtractive: the assumption every leaf inherits from the shared NVS-pretrained-free-radiance ancestor — they all let each surfel carry an independently-optimizable outgoing-radiance field ","pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","sub_pattern":"C20 (Encode Structure by Construction)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by writing the rendering equation as an explicit forward formation law and defining each surfel's outgoing radiance as the reverse-free forward map of its own intrinsic parameters (albedo, roughness, normal) under current light+visibility, so radiometric balance holds by construction along every direction — the free SH outgoing-radiance field that previously had to be corrected post-hoc is removed, and the residual the anchor leg reweights becomes a residual against a constructed, not free, quantity.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"physically-based inverse rendering with Gaussian Splatting / Gaussian surfels (material-lighting-geometry decomposition + relighting)","n_papers":44,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":21},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":14,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"GI-GS: Global Illumination Decomposition on Gaussian Splatting for Inverse Rendering"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"GeoSplatting: Towards Geometry Guided Gaussian Splatting for Physically-Based Inverse Rendering"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"GlossyGS: Inverse Rendering of Glossy Objects With 3D Gaussian Splatting"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"GUS-IR: Gaussian Splatting With Unified Shading for Inverse Rendering"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Phys3DGS: Physically-based 3D Gaussian Splatting for Inverse Rendering"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Progressive Radiance Distillation for Inverse Rendering with Gaussian Splatting"}],"more":8},{"year":2025,"n":21,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"SVG-IR: Spatially-Varying Gaussian Splatting for Inverse Rendering"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"iVR-GS: Inverse Volume Rendering for Explorable Visualization via Editable 3D Gaussian Splatting"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"RTR-GS: 3D Gaussian Splatting for Inverse Rendering with Radiance Transfer and Reflection"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Photometric Stereo using Gaussian Splatting and inverse rendering"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"InvGS: a Novel Real-Time Inverse Rendering Framework Utilizing 3D Gaussian Splatting"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"FlexDrive: Toward Trajectory Flexibility in Driving Scene Gaussian Splatting Reconstruction and Rendering"}],"more":15},{"year":2026,"n":9,"papers":[{"source":"arxiv","title":"Faster-GS: Analyzing and Improving Gaussian Splatting Optimization"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"RT-Splatting: Joint Reflection-Transmission Modeling with Gaussian Splatting"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"SGS-Intrinsic: Semantic-Invariant Gaussian Splatting for Sparse-View Indoor Inverse Rendering"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Gaussian Mesh Renderer for Lightweight Differentiable Rendering"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"3DSS: 3D Surface Splatting for Inverse Rendering"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Radiometrically Consistent Gaussian Surfels for Inverse Rendering"}],"more":3}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":16,"share":0.364},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":15,"share":0.341},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":15,"share":0.341},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":7,"share":0.159},{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":6,"share":0.136},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":4,"share":0.091},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":4,"share":0.091},{"pattern_id":"algebraic_equivalence_unification","pattern_name":"Prove Equivalence to Unify","count":2,"share":0.045}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"Gaussian-based inverse rendering recovers material, lighting and geometry by fitting a physically-based rendering (PBR) model to multi-view images, but the indirect-radiance term that drives inter-reflection is only supervised along the directions a training camera actually observed: along unobserved directions the per-surfel outgoing radiance can take arbitrary values while still fitting the training images, so indirect lighting leaks into albedo and the decomposition is unstable (arxiv:2603.01491v1, openalex:W4413145335). The recent fix (RadioGS, arxiv:2603.01491v1) closes this by adding a radiometric-consistency residual that pushes each surfel's learned radiance towards its PBR-rendered counterpart on unobserved directions, but that residual is itself a Monte-Carlo-estimated, material-dependent point target enforced as a uniform expectation over all surfels and directions — so when the current BRDF estimate is wrong the PBR teacher is wrong, and a uniformly-weighted L1 residual cannot tell a confidently-estimated direction from a high-variance noisy one (arxiv:2603.01491v1, openalex:W4411472324). The result is that the very signal meant to constrain the ill-posed regions is applied without any account of its own reliability, so high-error / high-variance directions — exactly the unobserved interior and inter-reflecting surfaces the constraint exists for — are fit no harder than already-reliable ones, and material error and estimation noise are folded into the radiance field rather than resolved.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2603.01491v1","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"RadioGS introduces a radiometric-consistency loss that minimizes, as a uniform expectation over all Gaussian surfels and all outgoing directions, the L1 residual between a surfel's SH-queried learned radiance and its physically-based-rendered radiance (BRDF + visibility + indirect light via 2D Gaussian ray tracing), establishing self-training-style supervision on unobserved directions, plus a fine-tune relighting step. Its residue: the consistency target is a single material-dependent point estimate from noisy Monte-Carlo PBR and is enforced uniformly — there is no per-direction reliability/variance weighting, no separation of where the PBR teacher should be trusted vs. where it is itself ill-posed, and no mechanism preventing a wrong material estimate from being reinforced through the residual (the classic self-training confirmation-bias failure), so the constraint spends equal optimization pressure on confident and on noisy directions.","_residue_grounding":"from RadioGS method 4.1.1: residual R_G = L_G - L_G^PBR, loss is E_{j,omega_o}[ ||R_G||_1 ] over surfels and directions; uniform expectation, L1, single env cubemap."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4413145335","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"IRGS applies the full rendering equation (no simplification) and computes incident radiance on the fly via differentiable 2D Gaussian ray tracing with Monte-Carlo sampling, then re-queries indirect radiance from the optimized primitives at relight time. Its residue: indirect radiance is still queried from primitives whose unobserved-direction values were never directly supervised, and the Monte-Carlo rendering-equation estimate is treated as ground truth without any per-sample reliability accounting, so estimator variance enters material/light estimates unmodeled."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4411472324","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"GUS-IR unifies forward and deferred shading and uses an improved probe-based ambient-occlusion baking scheme to approximate indirect illumination more accurately than GS-IR, with shortest-axis normals and depth regularization. Its residue: indirect light is a pre-baked AO approximation rather than a quantity supervised for physical consistency, so it cannot represent view/direction-dependent inter-reflection and provides no reliability signal on its own indirect-light estimate."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2605.05876v3","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"3DSS builds a differentiable surface-splatting renderer with a coverage-based compositing model whose per-layer opacity comes from accumulated EWA reconstruction weight, giving informative visibility gradients and forward microfacet shading under co-optimized HDR lighting. Its residue: it improves geometry/visibility gradients and silhouettes but still supervises appearance only from observed views via forward shading, with no explicit constraint on unobserved-direction radiance and no reliability-aware treatment of its illumination estimate."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"physically-based inverse rendering with Gaussian Splatting / Gaussian surfels (material-lighting-geometry decomposition + relighting)","venue":"CVPR / ICCV / NeurIPS / SIGGRAPH (vision-graphics inverse rendering)","time":"2026","data":["Stanford-ORB","TensoIR / NeRF synthetic relighting scenes","Shiny Blender / Glossy Synthetic","DTU / Mip-NeRF360 for geometry"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"differentiable rendering, 3D Gaussian splatting, physically-based rendering / BRDF, self-supervised optimization","preference":"both","baseline":"RadioGS (radiometric consistency loss + 2D Gaussian ray tracing), IRGS, GUS-IR, SVG-IR, 3DSS","limitation":"indirect-radiance supervision for unobserved directions is under-constrained; physically-based-rendering self-supervision targets are noisy and uniformly weighted, and material errors can be reinforced through the self-training loop","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The shared object both legs read from and write to is the per-surfel radiometric residual R(x, omega_o) = L_learned(x, omega_o) - L_PBR(x, omega_o), the same residual RadioGS minimizes (arxiv:2603.01491v1, method 4.1.1), evaluated at surfel position x along outgoing direction omega_o. STRUCTURAL LEG (structural_prior_encoding / C20): we write the rendering equation as an explicit forward formation law L_PBR(x, omega_o) = integral over the hemisphere of f_r(x, omega_o, omega_i; theta_x) * (V(x,omega_i) L_dir(omega_i) + L_ind(x,omega_i)) * (omega_i . n_x) d omega_i, where theta_x = (albedo a_x, roughness r_x, normal n_x) are the surfel's intrinsic parameters, f_r is a fixed analytic GGX microfacet BRDF, L_dir is the optimizable environment cubemap, V and L_ind are evaluated by 2D Gaussian ray tracing. Crucially we ALSO define the learned outgoing radiance not as a free spherical-harmonic field (the NVS-pretrained ancestor's choice, node n2 in method_lineage) but as L_learned(x, omega_o) := that SAME forward map evaluated with a SECOND, view-history-conditioned light/visibility readout cached from the observed views; this makes radiometric balance hold by construction for the directly-shaded term and confines the residual R to the indirect-light term L_ind alone — the only quantity genuinely under-determined on unobserved directions. RELIABILITY LEG (self_supervised_signal_engineering / C08): L_PBR's indirect term is a Monte-Carlo estimate over N traced rays, so it carries a computable per-direction sample variance sigma^2(x, omega_o) = (1/N) * empirical variance of the per-ray integrand contributions (the renderer already produces the N samples; sigma^2 is their second moment, no extra forward pass). We define a reliability weight w(x, omega_o) = sigma_0^2 / (sigma_0^2 + sigma^2(x, omega_o)), an inverse-variance gate with a single scalar hyperparameter sigma_0^2 (the variance floor, units of radiance^2, set to the median sigma^2 over a warmup batch), and replace RadioGS's flat L1 with the reliability-weighted residual loss L_rad = E_{j, omega_o}[ w(x,omega_o) * ||R(x,omega_o)||_1 ]. This is the one load-bearing filter (C08 step 3): it separates trustworthy manufactured targets from MC noise so the constraint stops fitting estimator variance. The advanced closed-loop form (C08 step 4): we route the current residual magnitude back into the ray-tracer's per-surfel sample allocation — surfels whose accumulated |R| is large get more traced rays next iteration (driving sigma^2 down where error is high), making the filter implicit in generation and concentrating compute on exactly the high-error inter-reflecting directions the constraint exists for. The two legs interlock on R: the structural leg shrinks R's domain to the genuinely-free L_ind term, and the reliability leg weights what remains by estimator trustworthiness; neither alone resolves the confirmation-bias failure (a wrong material makes L_PBR wrong) but together a high-variance wrong target is down-weighted AND the by-construction term cannot drift, so the residual cannot be driven small by both sides moving to a wrong fixed point.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The two gaps share machinery because they both act on the single residual R — the evidence is that RadioGS's own loss is literally E[||R||_1], so a reliability weight (anchor) and a domain restriction of R (sibling) are two edits to the same expectation, not two separate modules; that is why coherence_thread_type is shared_object and not a stapled pipeline. (b) Alternatives rejected: (i) a learned per-direction uncertainty head (predict reliability with an MLP) — rejected because it reintroduces a free, unsupervised quantity and would regress toward collateral node c1 (FixMatch-style learned confidence) flagged in method_lineage.notes; deriving the weight analytically from the MC estimator's own sample variance avoids that node by drawing on a source (estimator variance, node c2's family but never instantiated for a PBR consistency residual) the tree does not yet occupy. (ii) Imposing consistency as a hard equality constraint via a projection — rejected because it cannot be satisfied when the material is wrong, removing the very signal that diagnoses the error.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: train the full method and three ablations (uniform-weight w==1, free-SH-radiance, static-sampling) on the TensoIR synthetic relighting benchmark and Stanford-ORB, measuring novel-illumination relighting PSNR and mean albedo MSE against ground-truth intrinsics. If the candidate works, relighting PSNR increases and albedo MSE decreases versus the uniform-weight ablation, with the gain concentrated on high-indirect-illumination scenes (concave / multi-object scenes where inter-reflection dominates) and near-zero on convex single-object Lambertian scenes where indirect light — and thus MC variance — is negligible. The named load-bearing variable is the per-direction Monte-Carlo reliability weight w(x,omega_o) derived from the renderer's sample variance sigma^2; negative control: replace w by a per-direction random permutation of the same w values across directions (preserving the weight distribution but destroying its alignment to actual estimator variance) — this should drive relighting PSNR and albedo MSE back to the uniform-weight baseline, because if reliability-targeting is the mechanism, only correctly-placed weights help, whereas if 'any reweighting' helped the permuted weights would too. Positive control: a stripped model that keeps ONLY the inverse-variance weighting on RadioGS's original free-SH residual (no constructed-radiance leg) should recover most of the relighting-PSNR gain on the high-indirect scenes, identifying the reliability weight as the primary driver.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"arxiv:2603.01491v1","delta":"RadioGS minimizes the radiometric residual as a flat L1 expectation E_{j,omega_o}[||L_G - L_G^PBR||_1] treating the Monte-Carlo PBR target as uniformly trustworthy; we derive a per-direction estimator-reliability weight w from the renderer's own sample variance and minimize the inverse-variance-weighted residual, and we restrict the residual's free domain to the indirect term by constructing the learned radiance from the forward map rather than a free SH field — neither construction exists in their method."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4413145335","delta":"IRGS computes incident/indirect radiance on the fly with 2D Gaussian ray tracing and an efficient MC sampling scheme but consumes the estimate as ground truth with a fixed sample budget; we expose and use the per-direction MC variance as a supervision-reliability signal and a residual-driven adaptive sample-allocation policy that IRGS's fixed-budget tracer does not produce."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4411472324","delta":"GUS-IR approximates indirect light by pre-baked probe-based ambient occlusion with no per-estimate reliability and no direction-dependent supervision; we supervise a direction-dependent indirect-radiance residual weighted by estimator variance, a quantity AO baking cannot represent."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2605.05876v3","delta":"3DSS derives coverage-based visibility gradients from EWA reconstruction weights for geometry/silhouette quality but supervises appearance only from observed views via forward shading; we add by-construction unobserved-direction radiance plus a reliability-weighted consistency residual, an unobserved-view supervision signal 3DSS does not construct."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"arxiv:2603.01491v1","what_step_was_missed":"RadioGS constructed the radiometric-consistency residual and supervised it as a uniform expectation over all surfels and directions, but it never characterized the residual's TEACHER (the PBR radiance) as a Monte-Carlo estimate with a computable per-direction variance, so it could not derive an inverse-variance reliability weight nor an error-driven adaptive sampling policy; the substantive missing step is the construction of the per-direction sample-variance estimator sigma^2(x,omega_o) from the ray-tracer's retained per-ray contributions and the proof that weighting the residual by sigma_0^2/(sigma_0^2+sigma^2) is the inverse-variance-optimal combination of the noisy manufactured target with the prior — turning a flat self-training penalty into a reliability-curated one."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":250,"verdict":"advance","verdict_rationale":"Hard floor did not fire: gap_closure_reject_check.verdict is borderline (no lesson matched 'yes'), anti_pattern_check.matched_pattern_id is null, and paper_pointed_threat is a strong-baseline not an exact-mechanism collision. recipe_application_check.verdict is 'applied' for both entries — the C08 closed-loop quality gate and the C20 physics-formation-law construction are both present in core_mechanism — so the leading revise trigger does not fire. The only borderlines (C08 'curation gains could read as marginal' and C20 'which leg carries the gain') sit in evaluation-reporting rather than the load-bearing mechanism and are fully covered by the existing ablation grid + per-regime split; advance with both surfaced for Phase 4 reviewer_concerns_and_responses.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf accounts for the RELIABILITY of its own physically-based self-supervision target when constraining unobserved-direction indirect radiance: the PBR/Monte-Carlo radiance used as the consistency teacher is a noisy, material-dependent estimate, yet every leaf treats it as an equally-trustworthy point target across all surfels and directions, so optimization pressure is mis-allocated away from the high-error regions the constraint exists to fix (additive need; sits at the RadioGS/IRGS frontier-leaf residual_problem).","main_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","sub_pattern":"C08 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is treating 'attach a generator plus a filter' as a sufficient contribution when generate-and-filter is already commonplace, so no single load-bearing insight separates the work from prior cooperative-training/augmentation pipelines; a second shape is the unvalidated transfer assumption where the corpus is repaired with synthetic instances but real-target generalization is never shown.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A cooperative generate-and-filter loop sitting on substantial prior art needs either a demonstrably new mechanism or cross-domain breadth; showing it on a single domain invites the read that the method is domain-specific and incremental.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The load-bearing mechanism (a per-direction reliability weight w derived analytically from the renderer's own Monte-Carlo sample variance, plus residual-driven adaptive ray-budget reallocation) is demonstrably new versus RadioGS's flat L1, and it is validated across multiple benchmarks (TensoIR synthetic, Stanford-ORB real, Shiny Blender), so it is neither a bare generate-and-filter recombination nor single-domain."},{"lesson_quoted":"A newly proposed quality or gating score must be tightly argued to solve the stated problem under realistic conditions — a loosely-motivated score evaluated in an artificial setup is dismissed as a solution looking for a problem.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The gating score is not loosely motivated: w = sigma_0^2/(sigma_0^2 + sigma^2) is the inverse-variance-optimal weight for combining a noisy estimator with a prior, sigma^2 is the renderer's own sample variance (not an invented heuristic), and it is evaluated on real captured scenes (Stanford-ORB), not an artificial setup."},{"lesson_quoted":"Training on synthetically generated data without demonstrating transfer to the real target distribution leaves the core premise unvalidated, no matter how clean the synthetic labels are.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The downstream target (novel-illumination relighting + recovered albedo) is measured against ground-truth on real Stanford-ORB scenes, so the manufactured-target premise is validated on the real evaluation target, not only on synthetic data."},{"lesson_quoted":"A curation or replacement pipeline that yields only marginal or occasionally negative gains over no curation cannot justify its added complexity.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"falsification_prediction itself predicts near-zero gain on convex Lambertian scenes where MC variance is negligible — the gain is real but concentrated on high-indirect-illumination scenes; this is honest scoping, not a defect, but a reviewer could read aggregate numbers as marginal if the benchmark is dominated by easy scenes, so the per-regime split must be reported prominently (surfaced for Phase 4)."},{"lesson_quoted":"A synthetic-data-factory claim collapses without comparison to cheaper classical baselines, because the necessity of the heavy generative model is then unverifiable.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The uniform-weight ablation (w==1) IS the cheaper baseline (exactly RadioGS's flat residual), and the design isolates the reliability mechanism's necessity against it; no separate heavy generative model is introduced beyond the ray tracer the baselines already use."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions whether radiometric consistency must be imposed as a soft post-hoc residual penalty on an otherwise free per-surfel radiance at all, rather than the question of whether the unobserved-direction radiance should be a free parameter that consistency is asked to correct after the fact (subtractive: the assumption every leaf inherits from the shared NVS-pretrained-free-radiance ancestor — they all let each surfel carry an independently-optimizable outgoing-radiance field and then add constraints on top, none asks whether that freedom is what makes the unobserved-direction supervision necessary in the first place).","main_pattern":"structural_prior_encoding","sub_pattern":"C20 (Encode Structure by Construction)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail when the corruption-structure prior is asserted but never isolated as the actual source of gains — the 'structure' is really a generic architecture or a powerful pretrained backbone doing the work, so same-capacity ablations cannot attribute improvement to the prior, or the reformulation is theoretically clean but the empirical delta is marginal while breadth is shown on a single backbone/dataset.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming an architecture carries a domain-matched structural prior while shipping a generic off-the-shelf encoder-decoder collapses the move into ordinary supervised denoising that ablations and weak-baseline comparisons quickly expose.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The structural prior is the rendering equation forward map itself (analytic GGX BRDF + ray-traced visibility/indirect), not a generic encoder-decoder; the constructed radiance is a physical formation law, exactly the C20 'physics-based formation model' case."},{"lesson_quoted":"An elegant equivalence proof (corruption-recovery equals descent on an energy landscape) earns nothing when the empirical gain over the base method is marginal and the advertised plug-in generality is shown on only a single backbone.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The constructed-radiance leg's standalone effect is isolated by ablation (b) (free-SH vs constructed), but its marginal contribution separate from the reliability-weight leg must be shown clearly across >1 dataset or a reviewer will ask which leg carries the gain; flagged for Phase 4 but addressable, the ablation grid already exists."},{"lesson_quoted":"Deriving partition labels from a first-principles physical model is undercut when the derivations lack rigor, baselines and ablations are missing, and citation hygiene fails.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The forward law is the standard rendering equation (rigorous, cited to the same formulation RadioGS/IRGS use), and the design ships full ablations and the RadioGS/IRGS/GUS-IR/3DSS baseline set."},{"lesson_quoted":"If the structural signal you minimize rides on a powerful pretrained backbone, failing to isolate the prior's contribution from sheer backbone capacity leaves reviewers unable to credit the idea and unconvinced by the motivation for the chosen backbone.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"There is no pretrained backbone — the prior is an analytic differentiable renderer and per-surfel parameters; the free-SH ablation isolates the construction's contribution at equal capacity."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No Reject lesson is matched 'yes' on either entry, so the aggregate is borderline not triggered. The weight is carried by the C08 entry's curation-gains lesson ('a curation pipeline that yields only marginal gains cannot justify its added complexity') and the C20 entry's marginal-delta lesson, both marked borderline because the candidate's own falsification_prediction concedes gains concentrate on high-indirect-illumination scenes — an honest scoping the candidate must surface per-regime rather than a documented Reject match."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf accounts for the RELIABILITY of its own physically-based self-supervision target when constraining unobserved-direction indirect radiance: the PBR/Monte-Carlo radiance used as the consistency teacher is a noisy, material-dependent estimate, yet every leaf treats it as an equally-trustworthy point target across all surfels and directions, so optimization pressure is mis-allocated away from the high-error regions the constraint exists to fix (additive need; sits at the RadioGS/IRGS frontier-leaf residual_problem).","sub_pattern":"C08 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Stand up a controllable generative procedure and drive it to synthesize candidate training instances, then route every candidate through a single quality gate; the most advanced variants close the loop dynamically — feeding the learner's per-instance uncertainty/error back to the generator so synthesis concentrates on exactly the regions the current model fails on, making the filter implicit in generation.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism's RELIABILITY LEG performs exactly this: the 2D-Gaussian-ray-traced PBR radiance is the controllable generator of manufactured targets; the inverse-variance weight w = sigma_0^2/(sigma_0^2+sigma^2) is the single load-bearing quality gate (C08 step 3); and core_mechanism_steps step 7 routes each surfel's accumulated residual |R| back into the ray-tracer's per-surfel sample budget (top-quartile error → 2x rays), the C08 step-4 closed-loop-uncertainty-conditioned form that makes filtering implicit in generation.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved paper questions whether radiometric consistency must be imposed as a soft post-hoc residual penalty on an otherwise free per-surfel radiance at all, rather than the question of whether the unobserved-direction radiance should be a free parameter that consistency is asked to correct after the fact (subtractive: the assumption every leaf inherits from the shared NVS-pretrained-free-radiance ancestor — they all let each surfel carry an independently-optimizable outgoing-radiance field and then add constraints on top, none asks whether that freedom is what makes the unobserved-direction supervision necessary in the first place).","sub_pattern":"C20 (Encode Structure by Construction)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Prescribe an explicit law that maps the clean target to the observed signal — a noising/mean-reverting process, a masking schedule, a physics-based formation model, or an orthogonal transform that isolates the artifact in one component — and construct the recovery/generation operator as the principled reverse of that prescribed law so the inverse is obtained by construction rather than black-box regression.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism's STRUCTURAL LEG writes the rendering equation as the explicit physics-based formation law L_PBR = integral of f_r*(V*L_dir + L_ind)*(omega_i.n) and defines the learned outgoing radiance as that SAME forward map (not a free SH field), so radiometric balance holds by construction for the direct-shaded term and the residual is confined to the genuinely-underdetermined indirect term L_ind — the C20 'physics-based formation model' whose forward construction removes the free degrees of freedom; the move is forward-construction rather than literal reverse-time recovery, which is a borderline-but-valid C20 instance since C20 explicitly admits a 'transform that separates the quantity of interest from the artifact'.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"Both entries instantiate their cluster's signature move: the C08 entry performs the closed-loop uncertainty-conditioned quality gate (residual-driven adaptive ray budget), and the C20 entry prescribes the rendering-equation physics formation law and constructs the radiance by it rather than leaving a free SH field — neither is the parent pattern's generic gist."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["self_supervised_signal_engineering","structural_prior_encoding"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"All three documented anti-pattern compositions require heterogeneous_decomposition as one component; the candidate's composition is {self_supervised_signal_engineering, structural_prior_encoding}, which contains no heterogeneous_decomposition, so no anti-pattern subset matches."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"arxiv:2603.01491v1","threat_source":"lit_table","subsumption_argument":"RadioGS is the direct competitor — it owns the radiometric-consistency residual the candidate builds on and ships the same 2D-Gaussian-ray-tracing machinery and a fine-tune relighting step, so the candidate's claim stands or falls on whether reliability-weighting plus by-construction radiance beats RadioGS's flat L1 residual on a free SH field. It is NOT exact-mechanism overlap: RadioGS minimizes E_{j,omega_o}[||L_G - L_G^PBR||_1] as a uniform expectation over a free SH outgoing-radiance field and never computes the per-direction Monte-Carlo variance of its PBR teacher, derives no inverse-variance weight, and performs no residual-driven adaptive sample allocation; the candidate's two constructions (variance-derived reliability weight; forward-map-constructed radiance restricting the residual to L_ind) are both absent from RadioGS's method. The threat is therefore a strong baseline-to-beat, not a subsumption.","addressable_via":"Already addressed by core_mechanism's two distinguishing constructions and the falsification_prediction's uniform-weight negative control / positive control that attribute the gain specifically to the reliability mechanism; no field change needed to dodge subsumption, but the empirical superiority over RadioGS must be demonstrated, which the falsification experiment is designed to do."}},"revision_targets":[],"applied_revisions":null},"phase4_md_en":"# Reliability-Weighted Radiometric Consistency for Gaussian Surfel Inverse Rendering\n\n**Method.** Reliability-Weighted RadioGS (RW-RadioGS)\n\n## Motivation\nInverse rendering means looking at many photos of a scene and recovering its physical ingredients — surface color (albedo), roughness, surface orientation (normals), and the lighting — so the scene can be re-lit under new light. Recent methods represent the scene as a cloud of tiny flat discs called Gaussian surfels and render them very fast. The hard part is indirect light: light that bounces off one surface onto another before reaching the camera. Because a training camera only ever sees a surface from a few angles, the brightness a surfel sends out along the angles the camera never saw is barely pinned down, so the method often 'paints' indirect light into the albedo and the recovered materials come out wrong.\n\nA 2026 method called RadioGS (Radiometrically Consistent Gaussian Surfels) fixes part of this by adding a consistency rule: for each surfel it computes what its outgoing light SHOULD be according to physics (by tracing light rays through the scene) and trains the surfel's learned brightness to match that physics-based value, even along unseen angles. This is a form of the model teaching itself. The problem is that the physics-based 'teacher' value is computed by random sampling (Monte-Carlo), so it is itself noisy — and it is noisiest exactly in the cluttered, multiply-reflecting corners where the rule is supposed to help most. RadioGS trusts every teacher value equally, so it pushes just as hard on a value that is essentially a guess as on one that is reliable. Worse, the teacher value depends on the current (maybe wrong) material guess, so the model can satisfy the rule by drifting both its guess and its teacher toward the same wrong answer.\n\nThis is solvable now because the same ray tracing that produces the teacher value already produces the random samples we need to measure how noisy it is — for free. The idea of trusting a noisy estimate less when it is noisier is standard statistics; the missing step was simply noticing that the consistency target is a noisy estimate rather than a fact. So we (1) define each surfel's outgoing light directly from the physics formula instead of leaving it as a free knob, which makes the easy directly-lit part automatically consistent and leaves only the genuinely-uncertain indirect part to be supervised; (2) measure, per direction, how noisy the physics teacher is, and weight the consistency rule so noisy directions count less; and (3) send more ray-tracing effort to the surfels that are currently most wrong, which lowers their noise where it matters. When this gap closes, Gaussian inverse rendering becomes stable in exactly the concave, inter-reflecting indoor scenes it currently struggles with, which is what makes reliable relighting of real captured interiors possible.\n\n## Method\n### Background: train and relight\n*Optimize per scene and evaluate recovered intrinsics under novel illumination.*\n\n1. Train each scene fully on the three standard datasets (TensoIR synthetic, Stanford-ORB real captures, Shiny Blender), then save the recovered surface color, roughness, orientation, and the learned environment-light map. To test relighting, render those recovered materials under new, unseen environment lights with the same shading code, and compare against ground truth using standard image-quality scores (PSNR, SSIM, LPIPS) for the relit images and color error (MSE) for the recovered albedo — reporting concave inter-reflecting scenes and simple convex scenes separately so the regime where the method helps is visible.\n   - _Why_: Measuring relighting and recovered materials on real scenes shows the self-taught signal actually transfers to the real goal, not just to a synthetic proxy.\n\n### By-construction radiance\n*Define the surfel's outgoing light from the physics formula so the easy directly-lit part is consistent automatically and only the indirect term needs supervision.*\n\n2. Build a module that computes each surfel's physics-based outgoing light by averaging the rendering equation over N=128 sampled incident light directions, using the surfel's albedo, roughness and normal, the environment-light map being optimized, and the ray-traced visibility and indirect light. Pick the 128 directions with multiple-importance sampling (MIS) — a standard recipe that mixes directions favoring the surface's tilt with directions favoring its glossy reflection lobe — and for each direction store the full single-ray brightness contribution (already divided by how likely that direction was to be picked, so the stored numbers form an unbiased estimate). Output both the average (the physics-based brightness) and the list of all 128 single-ray values, which the next steps need.\n\n*The rendering-equation forward formation law: the surfel's PBR outgoing radiance is the hemispherical integral of its GGX BRDF $f_{r}$ against direct light $L_{dir}$ (gated by visibility V) plus indirect light $L_{ind},$ evaluated from the surfel's intrinsics $\\theta _{x} =$ (albedo, roughness, normal).*\n$$ L_{\\mathbf{G}}^{\\mathrm{PBR}}(x,\\omega_o)=\\int_{\\Omega} f_r(x,\\omega_o,\\omega_i;\\theta_x)\\,\\bigl(V(x,\\omega_i)\\,L_{\\mathrm{dir}}(\\omega_i)+L_{\\mathrm{ind}}(x,\\omega_i)\\bigr)\\,(\\omega_i\\!\\cdot\\! n_x)\\,d\\omega_i \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Keeping the individual ray values is what lets us later measure how noisy the physics teacher is, and writing the rendering equation explicitly is what makes consistency constructible rather than only penalized.\n3. Instead of letting each surfel carry a free outgoing-brightness field, define its learned outgoing light with the SAME physics formula from step 1, but plug in a cached record of the light the surfel actually saw from training views. Store that record as a small 16-slot histogram over incident directions in the surfel's own local frame, updated as a running average (keeping 90% of the old value each step) every time a camera ray hits the surfel. When you need the learned brightness toward some outgoing direction, look up the matching incident slot and run it through the physics formula — so the directly-lit part now matches the physics value automatically, and the only thing left to supervise is the indirect (bounced) light. 【author decision: whether to also keep a small free color term for shiny or translucent light paths the basic physics model cannot capture, which trades strict automatic consistency for more flexibility on real scenes.】\n\n*The shared radiometric residual both legs act on; with $L_{learned}$ constructed from the same forward map, R reduces to the difference in the indirect term $L_{ind}$ alone.*\n$$ \\mathcal{R}(x,\\omega_o)=L_{\\mathrm{learned}}(x,\\omega_o)-L_{\\mathbf{G}}^{\\mathrm{PBR}}(x,\\omega_o) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: The directly-lit part now matches automatically, so supervision is spent only on the genuinely-uncertain indirect light instead of on something that was never free.\n\n### Reliability-weighted self-supervision\n*Measure the physics teacher's per-direction noise and weight the consistency loss so noisy directions count less.*\n\n4. For each direction, measure how noisy the physics estimate is by taking the spread (sample variance) of the 128 single-ray values from step 1 and dividing by 128 — this is the variance of their average. Do this on the raw linear brightness values (do NOT first compress them with a tone curve), so this noise number is on the same scale as the consistency error it will weight. It is a cheap calculation over numbers you already saved, with no extra ray tracing.\n   - _Why_: This turns the physics target from an assumed fact into an estimate that knows its own error bar.\n5. Turn each direction's noise into a trust weight: $w = \\sigma _{0}^{2}/(\\sigma _{0}^{2} + \\sigma ^{2}),$ where $\\sigma _{0}^{2}$ is a single noise-floor number set once to the median noise over a one-epoch warm-up — directions noisier than the floor get trusted less. Multiply each consistency error by its trust weight and add the result to the normal image-reconstruction loss (pixel difference plus structural similarity) at the same strength RadioGS uses. To estimate the average over directions, sample 4 outgoing directions per surfel each step and average their weighted errors. Training on this combined loss adjusts the surfel materials and the environment light, which is what changes the final re-lit image.\n\n*The inverse-variance reliability weight: $\\sigma ^{2}$ is the per-direction sample variance of the N per-ray integrand contributions $g_{k}$ that compose the Monte-Carlo PBR estimate, and $\\sigma _{0}^{2}$ is a single variance-floor hyperparameter set to the warmup-batch median.*\n$$ w(x,\\omega_o)=\\frac{\\sigma_0^2}{\\sigma_0^2+\\sigma^2(x,\\omega_o)},\\qquad \\sigma^2(x,\\omega_o)=\\tfrac{1}{N}\\,\\widehat{\\mathrm{Var}}_{k=1}^{N}\\!\\bigl[g_k(x,\\omega_o)\\bigr] \\tag{3} $$\n\n\n*The reliability-weighted consistency loss that replaces RadioGS's flat L1 expectation, down-weighting high-variance unobserved directions.*\n$$ \\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{rad}}=\\mathbb{E}_{j,\\omega_o}\\!\\bigl[\\,w(x,\\omega_o)\\,\\lVert \\mathcal{R}(x,\\omega_o)\\rVert_1\\,\\bigr] \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Down-weighting high-variance directions stops the model from fitting Monte-Carlo noise while still using the trustworthy directions fully.\n\n### Error-driven ray-budget loop\n*Send more ray-tracing effort to the most-wrong surfels to lower their noise where it matters.*\n\n6. Keep a running average of each surfel's consistency error size. Every 500 steps, rank surfels by it and shift ray budget: the worst quarter get twice the rays (256), the best quarter get half (64), and the middle stay at the base 128. Keep the total number of rays fixed — the rays freed from the best quarter pay for the extra rays on the worst quarter, rescaled so the totals match exactly. Tracing more rays on the most-wrong surfels lowers their noise, which raises their trust weight, which gives them more effective supervision and so changes the final result.\n   - _Why_: More rays lower the noise exactly where the model is currently most wrong, which raises those directions' trust weight and focuses both compute and supervision where they matter.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 面向高斯面元逆向渲染的可靠性加权辐射一致性方法\n\n**方法名称.** Reliability-Weighted RadioGS (RW-RadioGS)\n\n## 研究动机\n逆向渲染（inverse rendering）是指通过一个场景的多张照片，还原它的物理成分——表面颜色（albedo）、粗糙度、表面朝向（法向 normals）以及光照，从而可以在新的光照下重新打光。最近的方法把场景表示成一堆很小的扁平圆盘，称为高斯面元（Gaussian surfels），渲染非常快。难点在于间接光：光线先打到一个表面、再反射到另一个表面，最后才进入相机。由于训练相机只能从少数几个角度看到某个表面，面元沿着相机从未见过的角度发出的亮度几乎得不到约束，于是方法常常把间接光「画」进 albedo，导致还原出的材质出错。\n\n2026 年的方法 RadioGS（Radiometrically Consistent Gaussian Surfels）部分地解决了这个问题：它加了一条一致性规则——对每个面元，按物理（通过在场景中追踪光线）算出它「应该」发出多少出射光，并训练面元学到的亮度去匹配这个物理值，即使是沿着未观测角度。这本质上是模型在自我教学。问题是，这个物理「教师」值是用随机采样（Monte-Carlo）算出来的，本身带噪声——而且恰恰在多次反射的杂乱角落里噪声最大，而那里正是规则最该起作用的地方。RadioGS 对每个教师值一视同仁，于是它对一个本质上是猜测的值和一个可靠的值施加同样的压力。更糟的是，教师值依赖当前（可能错误）的材质估计，所以模型可以通过让自己的猜测和教师一起漂向同一个错误答案来「满足」规则。\n\n现在能解决，是因为产生教师值的同一套光线追踪本身就已经产生了我们测量其噪声所需的随机样本——几乎是免费的。「估计越noisy就越少信任」是标准统计学；缺的一步只是意识到一致性目标是一个带噪估计而非事实。于是我们：(1) 直接用物理公式定义每个面元的出射光，而不是把它留成一个自由旋钮，这样容易的直接受光部分自动一致，只剩下真正不确定的间接部分需要被监督；(2) 逐方向地测量物理教师有多noisy，并对一致性规则加权，让noisy方向的权重更低；(3) 把更多光线追踪算力分配给当前最错的面元，从而在关键处降低其噪声。当这个缺口被填上，高斯逆向渲染在它当前最吃力的凹形、互反射室内场景中变得稳定，这正是让真实采集室内场景可靠重打光成为可能的关键。\n\n## 方法\n### 背景：训练与重打光\n*逐场景优化，并在新光照下评估还原的内蕴属性。*\n\n1. 在三个标准数据集(TensoIR 合成、Stanford-ORB 真实采集、Shiny Blender)上把每个场景完整训练，然后保存还原的表面颜色、粗糙度、朝向以及学到的环境光贴图。为测试重打光，用同一套着色代码在新的、未见过的环境光下渲染这些还原材质，并与真值对比：重打光图像用标准图像质量分数(PSNR、SSIM、LPIPS)，还原的 albedo 用颜色误差(均方误差 MSE)——并把凹形互反射场景与简单凸形场景分开报告，使方法起作用的区间清晰可见。\n   - _为什么_: 在真实场景上测量重打光和还原材质，能证明自我教学的信号真正迁移到了真实目标，而不仅是一个合成代理指标。\n\n### 按构造的辐射\n*用物理公式定义面元的出射光，让容易的直接受光部分自动一致，只有间接项需要监督。*\n\n2. 搭建一个模块，对每个面元，用它的 albedo（反照率）、粗糙度、法向 normal，以及正在优化的环境光贴图和光线追踪得到的可见性、间接光，对渲染方程在 N=128 个采样入射光方向 $\\omega _{i}$ 上求平均，得到面元的物理出射光。用多重重要性采样(Multiple-Importance Sampling, MIS，平衡启发式)来选这 128 个方向——这是一种标准做法，混合了偏向表面倾角的方向和偏向高光反射瓣的方向；对每个方向，保存完整的单条光线亮度贡献 $g_{k}$（已经除以该方向被选中的概率，所以保存下来的数构成一个无偏估计）。输出既包括平均值（物理出射光 $L_{PBR}$），也包括全部 128 个单光线取值的列表，后续步骤需要它。\n\n*渲染方程的前向构成定律：面元的 PBR 出射辐射 $L_{PBR}$ 是其 GGX BRDF $f_{r}$ 与直接光 $L_{dir}$（经可见性 V 调制）加间接光 $L_{ind}$ 在半球上的积分，由面元内蕴参数 $\\theta _{x} =$（反照率、粗糙度、法向）计算。*\n$$ L_{\\mathbf{G}}^{\\mathrm{PBR}}(x,\\omega_o)=\\int_{\\Omega} f_r(x,\\omega_o,\\omega_i;\\theta_x)\\,\\bigl(V(x,\\omega_i)\\,L_{\\mathrm{dir}}(\\omega_i)+L_{\\mathrm{ind}}(x,\\omega_i)\\bigr)\\,(\\omega_i\\!\\cdot\\! n_x)\\,d\\omega_i \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 保留逐光线取值，才能在之后测量物理教师有多noisy；显式写出渲染方程，才能让一致性可以被「构造」出来，而不仅是被惩罚。\n3. 不再让每个面元带一个自由的出射亮度场，而是用第 1 步同一个物理公式来定义它学到的出射光，只是代入面元从训练视角实际看到光的缓存记录。把这个记录存成面元自身局部坐标系下、对入射方向的 16 格直方图(histogram)，每当相机光线击中该面元时用滑动平均(每步保留 90% 旧值)更新。当需要某个出射方向上的学习亮度时，查到对应的入射格子并送入物理公式——这样直接受光部分现在自动与物理值匹配，只剩下间接(反射)光需要被监督。【作者需决定：是否额外保留一个小的自由颜色项，用于基础物理模型无法表达的高光或半透光路，这会在严格的自动一致性与真实场景上的更多灵活性之间权衡。】\n\n*两条支路共同作用的辐射残差；当 $L_{learned}$ 由同一前向映射构造时，R 退化为仅间接项 $L_{ind}$ 之差。*\n$$ \\mathcal{R}(x,\\omega_o)=L_{\\mathrm{learned}}(x,\\omega_o)-L_{\\mathbf{G}}^{\\mathrm{PBR}}(x,\\omega_o) \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 直接受光部分现在自动匹配，于是监督只花在真正不确定的间接光上，而不是花在本来就不自由的量上。\n\n### 可靠性加权自监督\n*测量物理教师逐方向的噪声，并对一致性损失加权，让noisy方向权重更低。*\n\n4. 对每个方向，测量物理估计有多noisy：取第 1 步那 128 个单光线取值的离散程度（样本方差 sample variance），再除以 128——这就是它们平均值的方差。要在原始的线性亮度上计算（不要先用色调曲线压缩），这样这个噪声数和它将要加权的一致性误差处在同一尺度。这是对你已经保存的数字的廉价计算，无需额外光线追踪。\n   - _为什么_: 这把物理目标从一个假定的事实，变成一个知道自己误差棒的估计。\n5. 把每个方向的噪声变成信任权重：$w = \\sigma _{0}^{2}/(\\sigma _{0}^{2} + \\sigma ^{2})$，其中 $\\sigma _{0}^{2}$ 是单一的噪声下限数值，一次性设为一个 epoch 热身期噪声的中位数——比下限更noisy的方向被信任得更少。把每个一致性误差乘以它的信任权重，再加到常规的图像重建损失(像素差加结构相似度 SSIM)上，强度与 RadioGS 相同。为估计对方向的平均，每步对每个面元采样 4 个出射方向并对它们的加权误差求平均。在这个合并损失上训练，会调整面元材质和环境光，这正是改变最终重打光图像的途径。\n\n*逆方差可靠性权重：$\\sigma ^{2}$ 是构成 Monte-Carlo PBR 估计的 N 条逐光线被积贡献 $g_{k}$ 的逐方向样本方差，$\\sigma _{0}^{2}$ 是单一方差下限超参数，取热身批次的中位数。*\n$$ w(x,\\omega_o)=\\frac{\\sigma_0^2}{\\sigma_0^2+\\sigma^2(x,\\omega_o)},\\qquad \\sigma^2(x,\\omega_o)=\\tfrac{1}{N}\\,\\widehat{\\mathrm{Var}}_{k=1}^{N}\\!\\bigl[g_k(x,\\omega_o)\\bigr] \\tag{3} $$\n\n\n*可靠性加权一致性损失，替代 RadioGS 的均匀 L1 期望，对高方差未观测方向降权。*\n$$ \\mathcal{L}_{\\mathrm{rad}}=\\mathbb{E}_{j,\\omega_o}\\!\\bigl[\\,w(x,\\omega_o)\\,\\lVert \\mathcal{R}(x,\\omega_o)\\rVert_1\\,\\bigr] \\tag{4} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 对高方差方向降权，能阻止模型去拟合 Monte-Carlo 噪声，同时仍然充分利用可信方向。\n\n### 误差驱动的光线预算回路\n*把更多光线追踪算力分配给最错的面元，在关键处降低其噪声。*\n\n6. 维护每个面元一致性误差大小的滑动平均。每 500 步，按它给面元排序并调整光线预算：最差的四分之一获得两倍光线(256)，最好的四分之一获得一半(64)，中间两个四分位保持基准 128。保持总光线数固定——从最好四分之一省下的光线，支付给最差四分之一的额外光线，并重新缩放使总数精确相等。对最错的面元追踪更多光线会降低它们的噪声，从而提高它们的信任权重，给予它们更多有效监督，进而改变最终结果。\n   - _为什么_: 更多光线恰好在模型当前最错的地方降低噪声，从而提高这些方向的信任权重，把算力和监督都聚焦到关键处。\n\n"},{"id":"99","run_dir":"run_prompt99_scalecua","index":99,"title":"Transfer-Aware Cross-Platform Composition for Scaling Open-Source Computer-Use Agents","title_zh":"面向开源计算机使用智能体规模化的跨平台迁移感知数据组合方法","method_name":"Transfer-Aware Composition (TAC)","hook":"Open-source computer-use agents are scaled by pooling 6 operating systems' trajectories into one uniformly-mixed corpus, but we show this uniform mix is not the neutral default it is assumed to be: a small, measurable cross-platform transfer matrix predicts that adding a high-volume platform's data silently degrades a low-volume platform's grounding, and fitting the mixing weights and parameter-sharing granularity to that matrix recovers the sacrificed competence at equal total data and compute.","anchor_pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","anchor_pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","domain_category":"LLM Agents & Tool Use","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides a way to predict, before paying to train at the next data scale, how a chosen cross-platform data composition will allocate competence across platforms — the scaling reports give one realized mix's outcome but no functional relationship between mixture composition and per-platform competence that would let a practitioner forecast or target a desired competence allocation.","pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by partitioning the platform set by its measured cross-platform transfer signature (rows/columns of the transfer matrix T) into a small dominant-donor minority and an interference-vulnerable bulk, then deriving a competence-recovery decomposition that bounds per-platform competence as a function of the mixing weights and sharing granularity — this fitted decomposition IS the forecasting relationship, and minimizing its predicted worst-platform competence gap yields the differentiated mixing/sharing composition (the runnable scaling artifact).","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved paper tests whether a single uniformly-mixed corpus is the right way to combine cross-platform data at all, rather than an assumed default — every leaf (ScaleCUA, UltraCUA, OSWorld-G) silently inherits from the shared 'pool everything into one schema and one model, mixed uniformly' ancestor the question of whether the mixing weights / the degree of parameter sharing across platforms should be a free, fit-to-data variable instead of held uniform.","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","how_closed":"Framing half (C01): the audited locus is the data-mixing-weights-and-parameter-sharing granularity, which every pooled-scaling leaf tacitly treats as a neutral fixed default (uniform mix, full sharing); we relocate the design variable to that locus and show it is load-bearing — uniform mixing is not necessary and a fit-to-data composition strictly dominates it on per-platform competence. Companion deliverable (controlled_diagnostic_design): a confound-isolating separation that holds backbone, total token budget, and compute fixed while varying ONLY the mixing-weights/sharing degree of freedom, so the measured competence gap between uniform-mix and fit-to-data-mix models is attributable to the composition variable alone, confirming the pivot empirically rather than cosmetically.","is_anchor":false},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf measures, per ordered platform pair, whether adding one platform's trajectory/grounding data raises or lowers another platform's grounding accuracy and task-success — the pooled-scaling papers report only an aggregate cross-platform average, so the sign and magnitude of cross-platform transfer (positive transfer vs interference) is an unmeasured quantity in every current open-source CUA scaling pipeline.","pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by constructing controlled add-one-platform-in / hold-one-platform-out training instances (the confound being total-data-volume, isolated by a fixed-budget resampling control) whose only varied axis is the presence of source platform A's data, with an oracle independent of the trained agent (the platform-B held-out grounding/task benchmark) scoring the de-confounded delta — the headline measured artifact is the entrywise transfer matrix T_{A->B} of signed competence change, the very quantity the aggregate cross-platform average hides.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"computer-use / GUI agents (vision-language-action models operating desktop, mobile, web GUIs)","n_papers":50,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":25},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10},{"source":"openreview","n":2}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":10,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Spider2-V: How Far Are Multimodal Agents From Automating Data Science and Engineering Workflows?"},{"source":"openalex","title":"The Dawn of GUI Agent: A Preliminary Case Study with Claude 3.5 Computer Use"},{"source":"openalex","title":"A Review of Precision Irrigation Water-Saving Technology under Changing Climate for Enhancing Water Use Efficiency, Crop Yield, and Environmental Footprints"},{"source":"openalex","title":"DROID: A Large-Scale In-The-Wild Robot Manipulation Dataset"},{"source":"openalex","title":"A Comprehensive Review of Deep Learning: Architectures, Recent Advances, and Applications"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Large language models empowered agent-based modeling and simulation: a survey and perspectives"}],"more":4},{"year":2025,"n":29,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"BIMgent: Towards Autonomous Building Modeling via Computer-use Agents"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"MCPWorld: A Unified Benchmarking Testbed for API, GUI, and Hybrid Computer Use Agents"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Agent S2: A Compositional Generalist-Specialist Framework for Computer Use Agents"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"ScaleCUA: Scaling Open-Source Computer Use Agents with Cross-Platform Data"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"VPI-Bench: Visual Prompt Injection Attacks for Computer-Use Agents"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"ComputerRL: Scaling End-to-End Online Reinforcement Learning for Computer Use Agents"}],"more":23},{"year":2026,"n":11,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"},{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"GUI Agents with Reinforcement Learning: Toward Digital Inhabitants"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Continual GUI Agents"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"HealthAdminBench: Evaluating Computer-Use Agents on Healthcare Administration Tasks"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"From Human Negotiation to Agent Negotiation: Personal Mobility Agents in Automated Traffic"}],"more":5}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":11,"share":0.22},{"pattern_id":"unify_into_shared_representation","pattern_name":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","count":11,"share":0.22},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":10,"share":0.2},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":7,"share":0.14},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":7,"share":0.14},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":7,"share":0.14},{"pattern_id":"structural_prior_encoding","pattern_name":"Encode Structure by Construction","count":4,"share":0.08},{"pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","count":3,"share":0.06}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"State-of-the-art open-source computer-use agents scale by pooling action-trajectory and grounding data from many platforms into one shared unified action space and training a single VLM on the uniformly-mixed corpus (semanticscholar:f10459002d7da8f070794feabb21624341e8c12e ScaleCUA spans Windows/macOS/Linux/Android/iOS/Web with one control schema; semanticscholar:b8a05e33be3cf6a8b23a88da2fba1d14c300406c UltraCUA likewise folds GUI and API actions into one curated hybrid space). This pooling is reported only as an aggregate win, but the corpus gives no instrument for whether adding a platform's data helps or hurts competence on the OTHER platforms: GUI grounding (the dominant measured bottleneck per openalex:W4417265551 MMBench-GUI and openalex:W4417287263 OSWorld-G) depends on platform-specific visual conventions, element scales, and action affordances that differ sharply between, say, a dense desktop toolbar and a sparse mobile screen, so naive mixing can let a high-volume platform's gradient dominate and degrade a low-volume platform's grounding. The failure is that once data is pooled into a single uniform mixture and schema, there is no quantity in the training pipeline that exposes, per platform pair, whether the shared representation is transferring competence or overwriting it — so 'scale the pool' is not the same lever as 'scale per-platform competence', and practitioners cannot tell which platforms are being silently sacrificed as the mix grows.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:f10459002d7da8f070794feabb21624341e8c12e","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"ScaleCUA builds a closed-loop cross-platform data pipeline over 6 OSes, defines one hand-designed unified action space, and trains one VLM on the uniformly-mixed corpus, reporting an aggregate cross-platform win. Its method never measures per-platform-pair transfer: the action space and the data mixture are fixed uniform design choices, so the paper cannot say whether any given platform's data improves or harms grounding/task success on the others, nor whether the single shared model is the right granularity versus partial parameter sharing — the aggregate average hides which platforms the pooled model is sacrificing.","method_note":"read from method section (pdf_arxiv_pymupdf): unified action space + GUI Understanding 471K / GUI Grounding 17.1M / Task Completion ~19K trajectories, all pooled and mixed; three inference modes share one backbone."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:b8a05e33be3cf6a8b23a88da2fba1d14c300406c","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"UltraCUA unifies primitive GUI actions and high-level API/tool calls into one curated hybrid action space and trains a single foundation model. The hybrid space is hand-curated and the allocation of which action type to use where is fixed at data-construction time rather than learned or measured per platform, so it inherits the same blind spot: no per-platform-pair accounting of whether the shared action vocabulary transfers or interferes across heterogeneous OSes."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4417287263","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"OSWorld-G scales GUI grounding via UI decomposition and synthesis, establishing grounding as the critical CUA bottleneck and producing large synthetic grounding data. The synthesis pipeline is single-platform-centric and treats grounding data as a homogeneous pool to grow; it never models how grounding competence learned on one platform's visual conventions transfers to or degrades another's, so its scaling story is volume-of-data, not transfer-aware data composition."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:2c198718909adf618edb1ae35c79403993307054","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Scalable Data Synthesis for CUAs filters synthesized trajectories with a step-level scalar quality signal to combat rollout noise. The quality score is platform-agnostic and per-step, so it ranks individual steps but provides no signal about how a kept trajectory's source platform affects competence on other platforms — filtering improves average data quality but still feeds a uniform, interference-blind mixture."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"computer-use / GUI agents (vision-language-action models operating desktop, mobile, web GUIs)","venue":"ICLR / NeurIPS / ICML","time":"2026","data":["ScaleCUA cross-platform corpus (6 OS: Windows, macOS, Linux, Android, iOS, Web; GUI understanding 471K, GUI grounding 17.1M, task-completion trajectories ~19K)","OSWorld-G / OSWorld grounding & task benchmarks","MMBench-GUI multi-platform evaluation suite","open-source VLM backbone (Qwen2.5-VL)"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with VLM fine-tuning + GUI-agent evaluation experience","preference":"both","baseline":"ScaleCUA (uniform cross-platform data pooling into one unified action space, single model)","limitation":"scaling open-source CUAs by pooling cross-platform data assumes platforms transfer uniformly; no account of per-platform interference or transfer asymmetry, so scaling the pool does not predictably scale per-platform competence","contribution_type":"scaling","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","compute","expertise","preference","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The central shared object (coherence_thread_type=shared_object) is the cross-platform competence-transfer matrix T, a P x P matrix over the P=6 platforms (Windows, macOS, Linux, Android, iOS, Web) where T_{A->B} is the signed change in platform B's competence caused by adding platform A's data at fixed total budget. Competence per platform B, comp_B, is a scalar in [0,1] computed as the equal-weight mean of platform-B grounding accuracy (fraction of held-out OSWorld-G/MMBench-GUI grounding instances whose predicted click falls in the gold element box) and platform-B task-success-rate (fraction of held-out task episodes reaching the verifier-checked goal state); both are model-external readouts from the platform's own held-out benchmark, never the training agent's self-judgment. Leg 3 (C02 diagnostic) BUILDS T entrywise: for each ordered pair (A,B), train two agents from the same Qwen2.5-VL backbone on the same total token budget N_tok — one whose mix includes platform A's slice, one that replaces A's slice with extra B-and-others data resampled to hold N_tok and the per-platform token counts of all non-A platforms fixed — and set T_{A->B} = comp_B(with-A) minus comp_B(without-A); the volume confound is blocked because both runs see identical N_tok and identical non-A composition, so the delta is attributable to A's content, not to more data. Leg 1 (C04 decomposition) CONSUMES T: it first verifies the platforms are genuinely heterogeneous by showing the row/column distribution of T has a structurally distinct minority (a few dominant donors with large positive out-transfer and a few interference-vulnerable receivers with large negative in-transfer) rather than a homogeneous mass, then partitions platforms by this transfer signature and assigns differentiated treatment: dominant donors keep full shared parameters and their mix weight is uncapped, while interference-vulnerable receivers get a capped mix weight plus a small per-platform low-rank adapter branch (sharing granularity = shared trunk + per-receiver LoRA, the partition-matched treatment). The load-bearing artifact is the competence-recovery decomposition predicting comp_B(w, g) approximately = comp_B^solo + sum_{A != B} w_A * T_{A->B} * s(g_B), where w is the normalized mixing-weight vector (sum_A w_A = 1), g_B in {shared, adapter} is platform B's sharing granularity, and s(g_B) is a learned scalar interference-attenuation factor (s=1 for full sharing, s=s_hat<1 fitted from a small held-out sweep for the adapter branch) — this first-order surface is the forecasting relationship the anchor gap demanded, and choosing (w,g) to maximize min_B comp_B(w,g) under sum_A w_A=1 is a small convex-in-w program whose solution is the transfer-aware composition. Leg 2 (C01 audit + C02 companion) READS the same T and surface: the audited assumption is that the mixing-weights/sharing locus is a neutral default; the pivot makes it a fit-to-data variable, and the companion separation trains a uniform-mix full-sharing model and the fit-to-data (w*,g*) model at identical backbone/budget/compute, predicting the fit-to-data model raises min_B comp_B (the worst-served platform) without lowering mean comp_B, which is the empirical proof that uniform mixing was not necessary and was silently sacrificing the worst platform. All three legs read from or write to T, so they are one paper, not three: Leg 3 measures T, Leg 1 turns T into a predictive recovery surface and an optimizer, Leg 2 audits the assumption that T's off-diagonal even matters and ships the separation that proves it does.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) The three gaps share machinery because all three pivot on one object — the transfer matrix T: the diagnostic leg's output is exactly the matrix the decomposition leg needs as input and the audit leg needs as evidence, so they form one shared_object paper rather than three modules (a measurement-only paper, a mixing-law paper, and an audit paper would each be incomplete — the audit's 'uniform is unnecessary' claim is empty without T's measured interference, and the optimizer is ungrounded without the audit's separation validating that off-diagonal transfer is real and actionable). (b) Considered designs rejected: (i) fitting a text-style data-mixing law (DoReMi-like) directly on next-token loss — rejected as a regression to method_lineage collateral node c2 (parametric, text-domain), because the relevant objective is interactive per-platform grounding+task competence, not LM loss, so the surface is fit on comp_B benchmarks not validation perplexity; (ii) static task-grouping (taskonomy/c1) over platforms — rejected as a regression to collateral c1 and because it gives a hard grouping, not the continuous mixing-weight + sharing-granularity surface the forecasting gap demands; (iii) a learned-MoE-router over platforms — rejected as it hides the transfer relationship inside opaque gates rather than producing the auditable T the audit leg needs. The avoided ancestral nodes (c1 task-grouping, c2 text data-mixing law) are recorded here per the regression check.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: on the ScaleCUA-style 6-platform corpus with a Qwen2.5-VL backbone at a fixed total token budget, measure each platform's held-out grounding accuracy and task-success-rate (comp_B) under (i) the uniform-mix full-sharing baseline and (ii) the transfer-aware (w*, g*) composition obtained by optimizing min_B comp_B over the fitted recovery surface. If the candidate works, the worst-served-platform competence min_B comp_B increases under (ii) versus (i) while mean comp_B does not decrease, and the realized per-platform competence shifts track the sign of the measured off-diagonal transfer entries T_{A->B} (platforms with large negative in-transfer gain most when their interfering donors are down-weighted). The named load-bearing variable is the off-diagonal transfer matrix T_{A->B} (the signed cross-platform competence change); the negative control re-runs the entire composition optimizer on a randomized-T (off-diagonal entries permuted), and the prediction is that the resulting agent's min_B comp_B falls back to the uniform-mix baseline's level — because if T's structure is the real mechanism, destroying it must destroy the worst-platform gain, whereas if the gain came merely from reduced effective data on some platform or from the adapter capacity alone, the randomized-T agent would retain it. A positive control trains an agent using ONLY the down-weighting prescribed by the top-k largest-magnitude negative T entries (no surface fit, no adapters): recovering most of the min_B comp_B gain would constructively identify off-diagonal interference as the operative quantity.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:f10459002d7da8f070794feabb21624341e8c12e","delta":"ScaleCUA builds the cross-platform corpus and trains one model on a uniform mix reporting an aggregate cross-platform average; we construct the signed per-ordered-platform-pair transfer matrix T it never measures and derive a competence-recovery surface that predicts and optimizes per-platform competence as a function of mixing weights and sharing granularity, which their fixed uniform design cannot express."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:b8a05e33be3cf6a8b23a88da2fba1d14c300406c","delta":"UltraCUA hand-curates a unified GUI+API action space with fixed allocation; we leave the action space alone and instead make the data-mixing weights and parameter-sharing granularity the fit-to-data variables, fitting them to measured cross-platform interference rather than curating them."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4417287263","delta":"OSWorld-G scales grounding data as one homogeneous pool to enlarge; we measure that pooling's per-platform interference sign+magnitude and show worst-platform competence is recoverable by transfer-aware composition at equal data volume, a relationship their volume-only scaling never produces."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:2c198718909adf618edb1ae35c79403993307054","delta":"Their step-level scalar filter ranks individual synthesized steps by platform-agnostic quality; our object is the cross-platform-pair competence-transfer matrix that governs how a kept trajectory's SOURCE platform affects OTHER platforms' competence — a between-platform quantity their within-trajectory filter cannot see."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"semanticscholar:f10459002d7da8f070794feabb21624341e8c12e","what_step_was_missed":"ScaleCUA built the cross-platform corpus and the uniform mixing/full-sharing training recipe but never constructed the per-ordered-platform-pair competence-transfer measurement (the controlled leave-one-platform-in delta on each platform's held-out competence): without that matrix it has no functional relationship between mixture composition and per-platform competence, so it cannot fit a recovery surface, cannot solve for a competence-allocating composition, and cannot show that its uniform mix was silently sacrificing the worst-served platform."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":388,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"No hard-floor fired (gap_closure_reject_check aggregate is borderline not triggered with no candidate_match: yes; anti_pattern_check matched_pattern_id is null; paper_pointed_threat is the intended baseline, not exact-mechanism overlap). Within the safe zone, recipe_application_check.entries[1].verdict = borderline on the C01 audit leg is the load-bearing finding: core_mechanism performs C01's relocate-the-locus + mechanistic-account verbs faithfully but C01's cluster is empirically anchored in security/detection/provenance/safety settings ('this cluster pivots the locus itself in adversarial/empirical security and safety settings and validates with attack-success rates'), and the candidate's setting is non-adversarial scaling — a setting mismatch that risks a recipe_application reviewer reading the audit leg as a forced fit. Per the heuristic 'choose revise when a borderline hits a load-bearing structural property,' the audit leg's sub_pattern should be reconsidered; since no other audit sub-cluster under assumption_audit_and_pivot is a cleaner fit for an empirical non-theorem scaling pivot (C05/C11/C19/C28/C29 are all theorem/bound-driven), the cleanest fix is the sub_pattern-scope swap that drops the audit framing's reliance on a mismatched cluster and lets the empirical-separation companion carry the leg, OR a tactical sharpening that makes the audit leg's mechanistic-why explicit so the C01 shape reads as principled rather than forced.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides a way to predict, before paying to train at the next data scale, how a chosen cross-platform data composition will allocate competence across platforms — the scaling reports give one realized mix's outcome but no functional relationship between mixture composition and per-platform competence that would let a practitioner forecast or target a desired competence allocation.","main_pattern":"heterogeneous_decomposition","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is treating the partition criterion itself as the contribution while leaving its value unproven, so reviewers map the discriminator onto an established technique and read the differentiated treatment as a relabeling; compounded by not benchmarking against both the strongest uniform baseline and the obvious cheap alternative.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Presenting a sensitivity or redundancy proxy as the novelty invites the verdict that it rediscovers known mixed-precision or low-rank results unless it is sharply differentiated from the obvious prior criterion.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The partition criterion is the cross-platform transfer matrix T, whose obvious prior is text-domain data-mixing laws (DoReMi) and task-grouping; core_mechanism_reasoning differentiates on regime (interactive per-platform competence vs LM loss) but a reviewer could still ask whether T is just a per-platform-relabeled data-mixing law."},{"lesson_quoted":"Omitting comparison against both the strongest uniform baseline and the obvious cheap alternative (SVD/PCA, structured dropout, a natively trained smaller model) leaves reviewers unable to tell whether the partition buys anything at all.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"Leg 2's controlled separation IS the strongest-uniform-baseline comparison (uniform-mix full-sharing at identical budget), and the randomized-T negative control plus the top-k-down-weighting positive control cover the cheap alternative."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a storage or throughput claim only on toy-scale models — where the compression bottleneck does not actually bite — undermines the entire motivation no matter how clean the method is.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The bottleneck (cross-platform interference) bites precisely at the 6-platform pooled-scaling regime the candidate trains in; compute_budget honestly scopes to real-but-reduced backbone rather than toy."},{"lesson_quoted":"A clever partition with no measured real-world deployment metric (no inference latency or memory speedup) reads as a proxy-only contribution and stalls at borderline.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The deployment metric is the real per-platform grounding accuracy + task-success-rate (comp_B) on held-out benchmarks, not a proxy."},{"lesson_quoted":"Skipping any analysis of why the heterogeneity exists — the data or value distribution that drives the partition — makes the technical novelty and the potential impact impossible to assess.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism_steps step 4 explicitly plots the row/column distribution of T and tests for a structurally distinct donor/receiver minority before partitioning."},{"lesson_quoted":"Bolting together established components (distillation plus pruning plus calibration) without an error bound or artifact specific to the new setting reads as incremental even when the target application is timely and important.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The competence-recovery decomposition surface is the setting-specific artifact, not a bolt-together of off-the-shelf compression modules."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved paper tests whether a single uniformly-mixed corpus is the right way to combine cross-platform data at all, rather than an assumed default — every leaf (ScaleCUA, UltraCUA, OSWorld-G) silently inherits from the shared 'pool everything into one schema and one model, mixed uniformly' ancestor the question of whether the mixing weights / the degree of parameter sharing across platforms should be a free, fit-to-data variable instead of held uniform.","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is a successful relocation that is demonstrated but not adversarially closed, or a novelty-boundary collapse where the new locus turns out to be one prior work already used, or offering only a demonstration with no mechanistic account of why the locus carries the signal.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Claiming a relocated signal is 'stealthier' or 'harder to remove' without defeating an adaptive defender who searches the same new locus leaves the central claim unverified.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"No adversarial/stealth claim is made — the setting is not security; the analogous obligation (show the relocated design variable is load-bearing) is met by the controlled separation."},{"lesson_quoted":"Relocating to a locus already exploited by published work — normalization statistics, activation-similarity losses, semantic concept triggers — collapses the novelty boundary unless the difference is made explicit and measured.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"The relocated locus (mixing weights / sharing granularity) IS exploited by published text-domain data-mixing work; the candidate measures the difference (cross-platform interactive competence, not LM loss) but the novelty boundary depends on that regime distinction holding."},{"lesson_quoted":"A defense whose relocation silently depends on a clean reference model or a known anomaly distribution reintroduces precisely the strong assumption the move was supposed to eliminate.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"No clean reference model or known anomaly distribution is assumed; T is measured from controlled training runs."},{"lesson_quoted":"Demonstrating the new locus only on fixed, non-adaptive or outdated baselines while omitting any account of why it works reads as a stacked pipeline of existing components rather than a principled shift.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The why-it-works account is the measured off-diagonal transfer structure and the recovery decomposition; the randomized-T control rules out the stacked-pipeline reading."},{"lesson_quoted":"Wiring off-the-shelf generators or tools into a new attack setting without a structural reason for the locus change gets judged as engineering integration, not insight.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The structural reason for treating mixing/sharing as the design locus is the measured cross-platform interference, not a tool wiring."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf measures, per ordered platform pair, whether adding one platform's trajectory/grounding data raises or lowers another platform's grounding accuracy and task-success — the pooled-scaling papers report only an aggregate cross-platform average, so the sign and magnitude of cross-platform transfer (positive transfer vs interference) is an unmeasured quantity in every current open-source CUA scaling pipeline.","main_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Papers fail when the instrument isolates the confound only inside an artificial regime and never shows the signal transfers to real deployment, or when it is circular (validated against the same population it interrogates), or merely re-confirms an already-documented limitation.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A diagnostic that only re-confirms a shortcut already known in advance, surfacing no previously unmeasurable failure, is read as confirmatory rather than as a contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The signed per-platform-pair transfer matrix T is a previously-unmeasured quantity (the field reports only aggregate averages), so it surfaces a new failure (silent worst-platform sacrifice)."},{"lesson_quoted":"Validating a synthetic-ground-truth instrument only on synthetic data, without demonstrating that the controlled finding transfers to real-world instances, leaves ecological validity unestablished and undermines the central claim.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The oracle is real held-out OSWorld-G/MMBench-GUI benchmarks and a task-success verifier, not synthetic ground truth."},{"lesson_quoted":"Building the instrument around one contested definition of the target property means it cannot independently confirm that the definition is correct, and reviewers flag the resulting circularity.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"comp_B is an explicit non-contested operationalization (grounding accuracy + task-success) from external benchmarks, and the oracle is independent of the trained agent."},{"lesson_quoted":"Resting an unsupervised evaluation on the unverified premise that the systems under test can reliably judge one another stakes the entire method on an assumption that collapses under scrutiny.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"No system-judges-system premise; scoring is by fixed external benchmarks."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pairing a single-task or small-sample instrument with broad capability claims triggers a scope-mismatch rejection, and assembling retrieval or engineering blocks without an isolating scientific insight reads as application rather than research.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"The instrument spans 6 platforms and 2 competence axes; the isolating insight (volume-controlled leave-one-platform-in delta) is the scientific core."}],"verdict":"clear"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"Two entries are borderline (C04 and C01) and one is clear (C02); the borderline weight is carried by the same shared concern — the lesson 'rediscovers known mixed-precision/low-rank results unless sharply differentiated' (C04) and 'relocating to a locus already exploited by published work...unless the difference is made explicit and measured' (C01), both pointing at the text-domain data-mixing-law prior. No Reject lesson is marked candidate_match: yes, so the aggregate is borderline, not triggered."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides a way to predict, before paying to train at the next data scale, how a chosen cross-platform data composition will allocate competence across platforms — the scaling reports give one realized mix's outcome but no functional relationship between mixture composition and per-platform competence that would let a practitioner forecast or target a desired competence allocation.","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"C04's signature move: discriminate components by a magnitude/sensitivity/influence/redundancy criterion into a high-impact minority and a near-redundant bulk, then apply differentiated treatment, with the load-bearing artifact being an error/sensitivity decomposition that BOUNDS how the differentiated treatment recovers the original objective.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism performs exactly this: it partitions the 6 platforms by their transfer signature (rows/cols of T) into a dominant-donor minority and an interference-vulnerable bulk, applies differentiated treatment (uncapped weight + full sharing for donors vs capped weight + per-platform LoRA for vulnerable receivers), and supplies the competence-recovery decomposition comp_B(w,g) = comp_B^solo + sum_A w_A T_{A->B} s(g_B) as the bounding artifact. The distinctive C04 move (the recovery decomposition, not just the partition) is present.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved paper tests whether a single uniformly-mixed corpus is the right way to combine cross-platform data at all, rather than an assumed default — every leaf (ScaleCUA, UltraCUA, OSWorld-G) silently inherits from the shared 'pool everything into one schema and one model, mixed uniformly' ancestor the question of whether the mixing weights / the degree of parameter sharing across platforms should be a free, fit-to-data variable instead of held uniform.","sub_pattern":"C01 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"C01's signature move is specifically to relocate a security/detection/provenance/safety property from the representational locus the field anchored on (input, parameters/gradients, scalar score, deterministic output) to an overlooked locus (labels, activations, distribution shape, behavior), validated with attack-success/detection metrics, plus a mechanistic account of WHY the new locus carries the signal.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism performs the audit-and-pivot SHAPE — it names a tacitly-fixed locus (uniform mixing weights / full parameter sharing), relocates the design to that locus as a fit-to-data variable, and supplies a mechanistic why (measured off-diagonal interference) plus the controlled separation as validation. However, the SETTING is not security/detection/provenance/safety — C01's cluster is empirically anchored in adversarial settings, so the candidate performs C01's structural verbs (relocate-the-locus + mechanistic-account) in a non-adversarial scaling setting, which is a faithful-in-shape but out-of-setting instantiation.","verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf measures, per ordered platform pair, whether adding one platform's trajectory/grounding data raises or lowers another platform's grounding accuracy and task-success — the pooled-scaling papers report only an aggregate cross-platform average, so the sign and magnitude of cross-platform transfer (positive transfer vs interference) is an unmeasured quantity in every current open-source CUA scaling pipeline.","sub_pattern":"C02 (Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"C02's signature move: construct controlled evaluation instances in which exactly one named confound is structurally blocked or independently varied, paired with an oracle independent of the system under test, and report the divergence between apparent and de-confounded performance as the primary result.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism performs this precisely: the named confound is total-data-volume, blocked by the fixed-N_tok with-A/without-A resampling control that holds all non-A platform counts fixed; the independent oracle is the platform-B held-out benchmark; and the headline reported artifact is the signed de-confounded delta T_{A->B}. The distinctive C02 move is present.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"C04 and C02 entries are applied (both perform their cluster's distinctive move — the recovery decomposition and the volume-controlled de-confounded delta respectively); the C01 entry is borderline because core_mechanism performs C01's structural relocate-the-locus + mechanistic-account verbs faithfully but outside C01's security/detection anchoring setting, so the move is shape-correct yet setting-mismatched."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["heterogeneous_decomposition","assumption_audit_and_pivot","controlled_diagnostic_design"],"matched_pattern_id":null,"required_mitigation_quoted":null,"mitigation_substantively_delivered":"n/a","reasoning":"None of the three 2-way subsets ({het_decomp, audit}, {het_decomp, controlled_diagnostic}, {audit, controlled_diagnostic}) matches any of the three documented reject-favored compositions (audit_decomp_supervisor = het_decomp+self_supervised; audit_decomp_prior = het_decomp+structural_prior; audit_decomp_operator = operator_substitution+het_decomp), so no anti-pattern fires."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:f10459002d7da8f070794feabb21624341e8c12e","threat_source":"lit_table","subsumption_argument":"ScaleCUA is the closest standing paper: it owns the exact 6-platform cross-platform corpus and the uniform-mix single-model scaling recipe the candidate audits, so the candidate's claim stands or falls on whether ScaleCUA's pipeline already contains a per-platform-pair transfer measurement and a non-uniform composition. Reading ScaleCUA's method (fulltext_cache: unified action space + uniformly pooled 17.1M grounding corpus, single Qwen2.5-VL, three inference modes) confirms it reports only aggregate cross-platform performance and never builds the signed transfer matrix T, never fits a competence-recovery surface, and never varies mixing weights or sharing granularity as design variables — so it does not subsume the candidate; it is the baseline the candidate beats. Collision retrieval surfaced text-domain data-mixing-law papers (Data Mixing for LLM Pretraining survey; Data Mixing Optimization for SFT; OptiMer) but these operate on next-token/LM loss over text domains, not interactive per-platform GUI competence, so they are regime-distinct prior art the candidate already differentiates from rather than exact-mechanism collisions.","addressable_via":"Not an exact-mechanism overlap and no revision needed to dodge it — ScaleCUA is the intended baseline; the text-domain data-mixing-law threat is already addressed by the explicit regime distinction in core_mechanism_reasoning and differentiation_from_lit, which Phase 4 should foreground in reviewer_concerns_and_responses."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"how_closed (gap_closure[1]) and core_mechanism","issue":"recipe_application_check.entries[1].verdict = borderline — C01's security/detection setting anchoring vs the candidate's non-adversarial scaling setting; the audit leg performs C01's verbs but the setting mismatch risks a forced-fit reading.","fix_direction":"Sharpen the audit leg so its C01-shape move is unambiguously principled in the scaling setting: in how_closed and core_mechanism, state explicitly the falsifiable sufficiency-or-invariance claim being pivoted ('the field treats uniform mixing weights + full parameter sharing as a neutral default that does not affect per-platform competence allocation') and the structural mechanistic account of WHY the relocated locus (mixing/sharing) carries the load-bearing signal (the measured off-diagonal transfer structure of T causes the worst-platform sacrifice), so the leg reads as C01's 'relocate the locus + mechanistic why + measured separation' applied to a scaling property rather than a cosmetic reframing. Do NOT change main_pattern or the gap; keep companion controlled_diagnostic_design as the deliverable owner. Kill-switch fields (falsification_prediction, compute_budget) must remain byte-identical."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"gap_closure_reject_check C04 and C01 borderline lessons both point at the text-domain data-mixing-law prior (DoReMi / Data Mixing surveys surfaced in collision_hits) — the novelty boundary must be made explicit and measured.","fix_direction":"Add or strengthen a differentiation_from_lit entry that names the data-mixing-law line explicitly (fit on LM/next-token loss over text domains) and states the measured difference: the candidate's object is fit on interactive per-platform GUI competence (grounding accuracy + task-success), and the load-bearing quantity is the signed cross-platform competence-transfer matrix T over heterogeneous OS visual+action conventions, which a text-domain mixing law does not measure or predict. This converts the borderline 'rediscovers known mixing-law' reading into an explicit, measured novelty boundary. Kill-switch fields unchanged."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"gap_closure[1].how_closed, core_mechanism","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Sharpened the C01 audit leg to state the explicit falsifiable locus claim ('mixing weights + sharing granularity are a neutral transfer-irrelevant default') and the structural mechanistic WHY (off-diagonal T causes donor-gradient overwrite of the receiver's grounding under full sharing), so the relocate-the-locus move reads as principled C01 in a scaling setting rather than a cosmetic reframing."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added an explicit, measured novelty-boundary entry against the text-domain data-mixing-law line (DoReMi / LLM-pretraining mixing optimization): they fit weights to LM/next-token loss over text domains, we fit to interactive per-platform GUI competence with the signed cross-platform transfer matrix T as the load-bearing quantity."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Transfer-Aware Cross-Platform Composition for Scaling Open-Source Computer-Use Agents\n\n**Method.** Transfer-Aware Composition (TAC)\n\n## Motivation\nToday's open-source 'computer-use agents' (CUAs) — vision-language models that operate real graphical interfaces by clicking and typing — are made stronger by dumping training data from many systems (Windows, macOS, Linux, Android, iOS, Web) into one big pile, mixing it uniformly, and training a single model on it. ScaleCUA (semanticscholar:f10459002d7da8f070794feabb21624341e8c12e) is the leading example. The result is reported as one average score across all platforms.\n\nThe hidden problem: the skill that matters most, 'grounding' (clicking the right on-screen element), depends on each platform's own look and layout — a crowded desktop toolbar is nothing like a sparse phone screen. When you mix all the data together and share all the model's weights, a platform with lots of data can drown out a platform with little data and quietly make it worse. But the training pipeline never measures this, so nobody can see which platform is being sacrificed as the pile grows.\n\nWhy now: ScaleCUA (2025-09) plus the per-platform test sets MMBench-GUI and OSWorld-G mean that, for the first time, both the per-platform skill score and the per-platform data needed to measure platform-to-platform transfer exist publicly on the same six platforms. Prior scaling work pushed data volume but still treated the pile as one uniform mixture, so this question is newly answerable and still open.\n\nWhat changes when we close this: practitioners get a way to predict, before paying to train at a bigger scale, how a chosen data mixture will distribute skill across platforms — so they can deliberately protect the weakest platform instead of discovering its collapse afterward.\n\n## Method\n### Transfer measurement\n*Measure the signed cross-platform competence-transfer matrix T with a volume-controlled diagnostic.*\n\n1. Fix the six platforms and freeze a held-out test set for each from the public OSWorld-G and MMBench-GUI suites plus a task-success checker. Define each platform's score $comp_{B}$ as the average of two things: grounding accuracy — for a click, did the predicted point land inside the correct on-screen element box; for typing/scrolling, did the predicted action match the correct one — and task-success rate, the fraction of test episodes an external verifier confirms reached the goal. The score always comes from the external benchmark, never the agent grading itself.\n   - _Why_: You need an honest, independent ruler for each platform before you can measure how platforms help or hurt each other.\n2. Train one model per platform using only that platform's data, giving every platform the same amount of data (equal to the smallest platform's supply so the numbers are comparable). Record each platform's solo score $comp_{B}^{solo}.$\n   - _Why_: This is the baseline 'how good is each platform alone' that everything else is measured against.\n3. For every ordered pair of platforms (A,B), train two models at the exact same total amount of data: one that includes platform A's data, and one where A's data is removed and its freed budget is handed to the other platforms in proportion to how much they already had. Set $T_{A->B}$ to how much B's score changed. Keeping the total fixed means the change reflects A's content, not just having more data.\n\n*The signed cross-platform transfer entry: platform B's competence change caused by including platform A's data at fixed total token budget $N_{tok}.$*\n$$ T_{A\\to B} = \\mathrm{comp}_B(\\text{with }A) - \\mathrm{comp}_B(\\text{without }A), \\quad N_{\\text{tok}}\\ \\text{fixed} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This directly measures whether adding A helps or hurts B, the number the field currently never computes.\n\n### Transfer-aware composition\n*Turn T into a predictive recovery surface and solve for the mixture+sharing that protects the worst platform.*\n\n4. Add up each row of the transfer table T (how much a platform gives to others) and each column (how much a platform is hurt by others). Plot these and check there really are a few strong 'giver' platforms and a few easily-hurt 'receiver' platforms, instead of everything looking the same; then sort the platforms into those two groups. 【author decision: exactly how big a row or column sum has to be to count a platform as a strong giver or an easily-hurt receiver is a cutoff on a smooth range and must be set by the authors.】\n   - _Why_: Tailored treatment only pays off if the platforms genuinely differ — so check that first.\n5. Fit a simple predictor of each platform's score from the data mix and the sharing setting: start from the platform's solo score, then add, for each other platform, its mixing weight times the measured transfer times a sharing factor s. Estimate this with plain least-squares regression on the runs you already have, and tune the single sharing factor s (which is 1 when weights are fully shared and below 1 when a platform gets its own small adapter) on a small held-out set of mixtures.\n\n*The competence-recovery surface predicting platform B's competence from the mixing-weight vector w and sharing granularity g, with $s(g_{B})$ the learned interference-attenuation factor.*\n$$ \\mathrm{comp}_B(\\mathbf{w}, g) \\approx \\mathrm{comp}_B^{\\text{solo}} + \\sum_{A \\neq B} w_A\\, T_{A\\to B}\\, s(g_B), \\quad \\sum_A w_A = 1 \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: This turns the measured table into a predictor you can use to forecast results for mixtures you have not trained yet.\n6. Pick the data-mix weights and the per-platform sharing setting that make the lowest-scoring platform's predicted score as high as possible. The weight part is a convex problem solved exactly for each sharing choice, and the sharing choices are tried by a short search. Strong givers keep full weight and full sharing; easily-hurt platforms get a smaller weight plus their own small adapter. 【author decision: how much to cap an easily-hurt platform's weight and how large to make its adapter are capacity knobs trading the weakest platform's gain against the average, and must be set by the authors.】\n\n*The composition program: choose mixing weights on the simplex and per-platform sharing granularity to maximize the worst-served platform's predicted competence.*\n$$ (\\mathbf{w}^*, g^*) = \\arg\\max_{\\mathbf{w} \\in \\Delta,\\ g} \\ \\min_{B}\\ \\mathrm{comp}_B(\\mathbf{w}, g) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Optimizing the weakest platform is what prevents the silent sacrifice the uniform mix causes.\n7. Train the final model on the chosen mix with the chosen sharing: a shared core plus a small adapter for each easily-hurt platform. Because you know which platform the agent is running on at use time, you switch in that platform's adapter; givers just use the shared core. The adapter changes how that platform's clicks and actions are produced, which is what actually raises its score.\n   - _Why_: The adapter changes how that platform's clicks are produced, which is how the better setting actually raises its score.\n\n### Audit and controls\n*Prove uniform mixing was unnecessary and that the measured transfer structure is the operative cause.*\n\n8. Train comparison models with the same backbone, data budget, and compute, and score every model on all six platforms, reporting the worst-platform score and the average. Use two comparisons: a plain uniform mix with full sharing, and a uniform mix that has the same total adapter capacity but spread evenly. That way any improvement is credited to the smart allocation, not just to having adapters.\n   - _Why_: Holding everything else equal proves the gain comes from the smarter composition, not from extra data or compute.\n9. Shuffle the off-diagonal numbers of the transfer table at random, re-run the optimizer on this fake table, train the resulting model, and check its worst-platform score. Also try a shuffle that keeps each platform's row and column totals the same, to tell apart 'the detailed pattern matters' from 'only the totals matter'. If the real measured transfers are what drive the benefit, scrambling them should pull the worst-platform score back down to the uniform-mix level.\n   - _Why_: If the real measured transfers are what matter, scrambling them should erase the benefit — a clean test that the mechanism is real.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 面向开源计算机使用智能体规模化的跨平台迁移感知数据组合方法\n\n**方法名称.** Transfer-Aware Composition (TAC)\n\n## 研究动机\n如今的开源 computer-use agents (CUAs)——即通过点击和输入来操作真实图形界面的视觉语言模型——的常规增强办法，是把来自多个系统（Windows、macOS、Linux、Android、iOS、Web）的训练数据汇成一大堆，均匀混合后训练单一模型。ScaleCUA (semanticscholar:f10459002d7da8f070794feabb21624341e8c12e) 是这一路线的代表，其结果只以一个跨平台的平均分来汇报。\n\n隐藏的问题在于：最关键的能力 grounding（即准确点中屏幕上正确的元素）高度依赖每个平台各自的外观与布局——拥挤的桌面工具栏与稀疏的手机屏幕截然不同。当所有数据被均匀混在一起、模型权重又被完全共享时，数据量大的平台会盖过数据量小的平台，悄悄拉低后者的能力。但训练流程从不测量这一点，因此没人能看出随着数据堆增大，究竟哪个平台被牺牲了。\n\n为何是现在：ScaleCUA (2025-09) 加上分平台测试集 MMBench-GUI 与 OSWorld-G，使得分平台的能力分数与测量平台间迁移所需的分平台数据，首次在同一组六个平台上公开可得。此前的规模化工作只追求数据量，却仍把整堆数据当作一个均匀混合体，所以这个问题既新近可解、又仍然敞开。\n\n一旦解决：从业者将获得一种在付费训练到更大规模之前就能预测某一数据组合如何在各平台间分配能力的手段，从而主动保护最弱的平台，而不是事后才发现它崩塌。\n\n## 方法\n### 迁移测量\n*用受控于数据量的诊断测量带符号的跨平台能力迁移矩阵 T。*\n\n1. 固定六个平台 P={Windows,macOS,Linux,Android,iOS,Web}，并从公开的 OSWorld-G 与 MMBench-GUI 套件冻结每个平台的留出测试集，外加一个任务成功(task-success)验证器。把每个平台的分数 $comp_{B}$ 定义为两部分的平均：grounding accuracy——对点击动作，预测点是否落在正确的屏幕元素框内；对输入/滚动等动作，预测动作是否与标准动作一致——以及 task-success rate，即外部验证器确认达成目标的测试回合占比。分数始终来自外部基准，而非智能体自评。\n   - _为什么_: 在测量平台间相互帮助或损害之前，先要为每个平台准备一把诚实、独立的尺子。\n2. 为每个平台 B，仅用其自身数据微调 Qwen2.5-VL 主干，并给所有平台相同的 token 预算 $B_{min}$（取最小平台的可用 token 量，从语料读取，以保证 $comp_{B}^{solo}$ 跨平台可比）。记录每个平台的单独分数 $comp_{B}^{solo}$，作为后续恢复曲面的截距。\n   - _为什么_: 这是'每个平台单独有多强'的基线，后续一切都以此为参照。\n3. 对每个有序平台对 (A,B)，在完全相同的总 token 预算 $N_{tok}$ 下训练两个模型：一个混合中包含平台 A 的数据切片，另一个移除 A 的切片并把其释放的预算按其他平台已有比例分配（保持每个非 A 平台的相对份额不变）。把迁移量 $T_{A->B}$ 设为两次运行间 $comp_{B}$ 的变化。由于 $N_{tok}$ 与非 A 的相对组成固定，该差值归因于 A 的内容，而非数据量。\n\n*带符号的跨平台迁移量：在固定总 token 预算 $N_{tok}$ 下，加入平台 A 数据所引起的平台 B 能力变化。*\n$$ T_{A\\to B} = \\mathrm{comp}_B(\\text{with }A) - \\mathrm{comp}_B(\\text{without }A), \\quad N_{\\text{tok}}\\ \\text{fixed} \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这直接测量加入 A 对 B 是有益还是有害，正是当前领域从不计算的那个量。\n\n### 迁移感知组合\n*把 T 变成可预测的恢复曲面，并求解保护最差平台的混合方案与共享设置。*\n\n4. 对迁移表 T 按行求和（一个平台对其他平台的总贡献）与按列求和（一个平台被其他平台损害的总量）。绘制其分布，确认确实存在少数强'供体'平台（正向贡献大）与少数易受损'接收'平台（负向受损大），而非整体均匀；据此把平台分为供体与易受损接收方两组。【作者需决定：从 T 的行/列和判定某平台为强供体或易受损接收方的具体阈值是连续区间上的切分，须由作者确定。】\n   - _为什么_: 只有当平台间确实存在差异时，差异化处理才划算——所以先验证这一点。\n5. 拟合能力恢复曲面 $comp_{B}(w,g) = comp_{B}^{solo} + sum_{A!=B} w_{A} T_{A->B} s(g_{B})$（见公式 2）：用已有的 leave-one-in 运行做普通最小二乘(OLS)回归，把 $comp_{B}^{solo}$ 与 $T_{A->B}$ 视为已知，混合权重 $w_{A}$ 作为回归量。在每个接收方约 5–8 个 (w,g) 点的留出网格上，以最小化预测平方误差来拟合单一的干扰衰减标量 $s_{hat}$（完全共享时 s=1，平台拥有自身 adapter 分支时 $s=s_{hat}<1$）；可用一个全局 $s_{hat}$ 或每个接收方各一个。\n\n*能力恢复曲面：由混合权重向量 w 与共享粒度 g 预测平台 B 的能力，其中 $s(g_{B})$ 为习得的干扰衰减因子。*\n$$ \\mathrm{comp}_B(\\mathbf{w}, g) \\approx \\mathrm{comp}_B^{\\text{solo}} + \\sum_{A \\neq B} w_A\\, T_{A\\to B}\\, s(g_B), \\quad \\sum_A w_A = 1 \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 这把测得的表格变成一个预测器，可用来预报尚未训练过的混合方案的结果。\n6. 求解 (w*,g*) = 在单纯形上的 w 与每平台 $g\\in \\{shared,$ adapter} 上最大化 $min_{B} comp_{B}(w,g)$（见公式 3）：关于 w 的内层问题是凸的（对 w 线性），在每个固定 g 下精确求解，g 由一个小规模离散外层搜索遍历。供体保持不设上限的权重与完全共享；易受损接收方获得受限权重外加一个每平台的小型 LoRA adapter。【作者需决定：接收方权重上限与每平台 LoRA adapter 的秩是在'保护最差平台'与'平均能力'之间权衡的容量旋钮，须由作者确定。】\n\n*组合优化问题：在单纯形上选择混合权重并为各平台选择共享粒度，以最大化最差平台的预测能力。*\n$$ (\\mathbf{w}^*, g^*) = \\arg\\max_{\\mathbf{w} \\in \\Delta,\\ g} \\ \\min_{B}\\ \\mathrm{comp}_B(\\mathbf{w}, g) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 优化最弱平台正是防止均匀混合所导致的悄然牺牲。\n7. 用所选混合方案 (w*) 与共享粒度 g* 训练 Qwen2.5-VL：共享主干外加每个接收方一个 LoRA adapter。推理时目标平台身份已知（智能体运行在具体某个 OS 上），故按平台标签选用对应接收方 adapter，供体仅用共享主干。adapter 分支改变了该平台点击坐标/动作的生成前向过程，这正是修改后的共享如何传导到 $comp_{B}$ 的途径。\n   - _为什么_: adapter 改变了该平台点击的生成方式，这正是更好设置实际提升其分数的途径。\n\n### 审计与对照\n*证明均匀混合并非必要，且测得的迁移结构才是起作用的原因。*\n\n8. 在完全相同的 backbone、$N_{tok}$ 与算力下训练对照模型，并在 6 个冻结套件上评估所有模型，报告 $min_{B} comp_{B}$、$mean comp_{B}$ 及各平台差值。为干净归因运行两个对照：(i) 无 adapter 的均匀混合+完全共享；(ii) 与 g* 总 adapter 容量相同但均匀分配的均匀混合——这样任何增益都归因于迁移感知的分配方式，而非额外的 adapter 容量。此步固定除混合权重/共享之外的一切。\n   - _为什么_: 在其他一切相同的情况下，证明收益来自更聪明的组合，而非额外的数据或算力。\n9. 把迁移表 T 的非对角数值随机打乱（不保留行/列边际），在这个被打乱的矩阵上重新求解 第6步（求解） 得到 $(w_{rand},g_{rand})$，训练该模型，并将其 $min_{B} comp_{B}$ 与真实 (w*,g*) 模型比较。另报告一个保留边际的置换作为更强对照，以区分'细节结构重要'与'仅边际重要'。若测得的迁移结构才是起作用的量，打乱它应使 $min_{B} comp_{B}$ 回落到均匀混合水平。\n   - _为什么_: 如果真正起作用的是测得的迁移结构，打乱它就应抹掉收益——这是机制为真的干净检验。\n\n"},{"id":"100","run_dir":"run_prompt100_specactions","index":100,"title":"Spend-Where-It-Matters: Difficulty-Routed Action Generation for Agents","title_zh":"按需分配：面向 AI 智能体的难度路由式动作生成","method_name":"Difficulty-Routed Action Generation (DRAG)","hook":"Every recent agent accelerator spends the same generation budget on a trivial waypoint as on a contact-rich grasp, because the unit of acceleration is fixed before runtime. We show a cheap, label-free difficulty readout taken before generation commits lets an agent emit most of its actions from a near-zero-cost reuse path and reserve full generation for the rare hard decisions — recovering the expensive policy's action on a measurable majority of steps while cutting average decode cost.","anchor_pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","anchor_pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","domain_category":"Robotics & Embodied Agents","patterns":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf allocates a per-decision action-generation budget from a signal that is available BEFORE the full action generation commits — every accelerator (Spec-VLA openalex:W4416035531, Fast Policy openalex:W4416749600) spends a fixed or globally-tuned budget per step, so the system cannot contract compute on routine decisions nor expand it on the rare hard ones (additive: the missing outcome is difficulty-matched per-step generation cost, not any one mechanism for it).","pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by partitioning the agent's stream of action decisions (not its weights) by a measured difficulty property into a routine-bulk and a hard-minority, emitting the routine bulk from a cheap reuse/short-draft path and reserving full generation for the minority, with an action-fidelity decomposition that bounds the routed policy's deviation from the full-generation policy — the decomposition, not the routing idea, is the load-bearing artifact.","is_anchor":true},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides a verifiable predictor of per-state decision difficulty that an efficient agent could condition on — the accelerators read no difficulty signal at all and the diagnostic/faithfulness papers (arxiv:2606.00476v1) measure post-hoc behavior rather than supplying a pre-generation difficulty estimate (additive: a difficulty estimate that is cheap relative to full action generation and predictive of when cheap generation suffices).","pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","companion_pattern":null,"how_closed":"Closed by manufacturing the difficulty signal from the frozen policy's own internal-state readout at a single early layer (entropy of a one-step cheap action probe + disagreement between the cached previous action and the probe's argument), localized to the pre-generation forward pass and confined to a tiny calibrated threshold lever, with an explicit anti-degeneracy stabilizer (a verified-mistake replay buffer) so the probe cannot trivially route everything to the cheap path.","is_anchor":false},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether the unit of acceleration must remain the FULL action emitted fresh at every step, rather than a decision that could reuse or skip generation when the current action is predictable from recent context (subtractive: every leaf silently inherits from the shared ancestor the assumption that each control step re-generates a complete action de novo; none asks whether that per-step from-scratch regeneration is necessary).","pattern_id":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","pattern_name":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","companion_pattern":"controlled_diagnostic_design","how_closed":"Closed by auditing the inherited stopping/budget rule 'spend full generation at every step' and reframing it as an online-stopping decision (selection -> when-to-stop): treat each step as 'pay for full generation, or accept the cheap emission' and re-derive a competitive-ratio-style budget certificate bounding cumulative action-regret of the stopping rule vs the always-full-generation policy; the companion controlled_diagnostic_design ships the matched-pair separation (same observed state, full-regeneration action vs reuse action) whose measured agreement gap proves the de-novo assumption was non-binding on a quantified fraction of decisions.","is_anchor":false}],"phase0":{"topic":"efficient action generation for LLM/VLA-based AI agents (decode-time latency and compute of emitting actions)","n_papers":51,"by_source":[{"source":"openalex","n":26},{"source":"semanticscholar","n":13},{"source":"arxiv","n":10},{"source":"openreview","n":2}],"by_year":[{"year":2024,"n":10,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Alleviating Action Hallucination for LLM-based Embodied Agents via Inner and Outer Alignment"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"MobileAgentBench: An Efficient and User-Friendly Benchmark for Mobile LLM Agents"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Fuzz-Testing Meets LLM-Based Agents: An Automated and Efficient Framework for Jailbreaking Text-to-Image Generation Models"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Reinforcing LLM Agents via Policy Optimization with Action Decomposition"},{"source":"openalex","title":"Large Language Models in Healthcare and Medical Domain: A Review"},{"source":"openalex","title":"When large language models meet personalization: perspectives of challenges and opportunities"}],"more":4},{"year":2025,"n":30,"papers":[{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Scaling Graph Chain-of-Thought Reasoning: A Multi-Agent Framework with Efficient LLM Serving"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Embodied Multi-Agent Planning With LLMs: A Best-of-N Strategy for Efficient Cooperation"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Goal-Guided Efficient Exploration via Large Language Model in Reinforcement Learning"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"StreamVLN: Streaming Vision-and-Language Navigation via SlowFast Context Modeling"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"Unsupervised Feature Transformation via In-context Generation, Generator-critic LLM Agents, and Duet-play Teaming"},{"source":"semanticscholar","title":"SIRAJ: Diverse and Efficient Red-Teaming for LLM Agents via Distilled Structured Reasoning"}],"more":24},{"year":2026,"n":11,"papers":[{"source":"openreview","title":"Self-Agent System for Reflective Reasoning"},{"source":"openreview","title":"I2R-HOI: Preference-Guided Internalized Iterative Refinement for One-Step 3D Human-Object Interaction Reconstruction"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"RecoAtlas: From Semantic Plausibility to Set-Level Utility in LLM Recommendation Agents"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"YouZhi: Towards High-Concurrency Financial LLMs via Adaptive GQA-to-MLA Transition"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"Externalization in LLM Agents: A Unified Review of Memory, Skills, Protocols and Harness Engineering"},{"source":"arxiv","title":"On Theoretically-Driven LLM Agents for Multi-Dimensional Discourse Analysis"}],"more":5}],"pattern_dist":[{"pattern_id":"adapt_via_conditioning","pattern_name":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","count":10,"share":0.196},{"pattern_id":"decompose_and_delegate","pattern_name":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","count":10,"share":0.196},{"pattern_id":"reframe_as_solvable_object","pattern_name":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","count":7,"share":0.137},{"pattern_id":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","pattern_name":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","count":6,"share":0.118},{"pattern_id":"architectural_operator_substitution","pattern_name":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","count":6,"share":0.118},{"pattern_id":"controlled_diagnostic_design","pattern_name":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","count":6,"share":0.118},{"pattern_id":"heterogeneous_decomposition","pattern_name":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","count":5,"share":0.098},{"pattern_id":"generative_process_redesign","pattern_name":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","count":4,"share":0.078}]},"phase1":{"bottleneck_statement":"For LLM- and VLA-based agents, the cost of EMITTING an action is governed entirely by how the action token-sequence is produced, and every recent acceleration leaf spends a budget that is fixed per step or set by a hand-tuned global knob rather than matched to the decision's actual difficulty. Spec-VLA (openalex:W4416035531) accelerates VLA decoding by drafting action tokens and verifying them in parallel, but its draft length and a 'relaxed acceptance' threshold are global hyperparameters that do not vary with whether the current state is a trivial waypoint or a contact-rich grasp; Fast Policy (openalex:W4416749600) accelerates diffusion-policy denoising with a single training-free acceleration factor applied identically at every control step; VLASH (openalex:W4416958104) hides latency by running inference asynchronously but assumes the per-action inference cost itself is fixed and only compensates for the resulting temporal drift; and DynaSaur (openalex:W4404352873) lets an agent generate actions as open-ended code, making EVERY action a full, uniformly-expensive LLM generation with no notion that some actions are routine. The consequence is a structural failure: when an agent faces a long horizon of mostly-easy decisions punctuated by a few hard ones, the per-step generation cost cannot contract on the easy steps nor expand on the hard ones, so the system pays worst-case decode cost on average and still under-deliberates exactly where it matters. No retrieved method produces a per-decision generation budget that is allocated from a signal computable BEFORE the expensive full action generation commits.","closest_adjacent":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416035531","is_anchor":true,"summary_and_residue":"Spec-VLA brings speculative decoding to VLA models: a lightweight drafter proposes action tokens and the large VLA verifies them in parallel under a relaxed acceptance criterion, yielding wall-clock speedup without quality loss. Its residue is that the draft length and the acceptance-relaxation threshold are GLOBAL constants tuned offline — the method never reads a per-state difficulty signal to decide how aggressively to draft, so on easy states it under-drafts (leaving speedup on the table) and on hard states it over-drafts (forcing costly verifier rejections). Its method confirms the draft model is decoupled and applied uniformly with a single relaxed-acceptance rule; it offers no per-state difficulty signal and no characterization of WHICH action tokens are predictable enough to skip generating at full cost."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416749600","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Fast Policy accelerates diffusion visuomotor policies training-free by reducing the number of denoising iterations needed to emit an action. Its residue is that the acceleration factor is a single global setting applied at every control step, so it cannot spend more denoising on contact-rich or near-failure states and less on free-space motion — there is no per-state allocation of the denoising budget."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416958104","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"VLASH achieves real-time VLA control by running inference asynchronously and predicting future states to correct the temporal misalignment that async execution introduces. Its residue is that it treats the per-action inference cost as a fixed quantity and only compensates for the latency downstream; it never tries to make the inference itself cheaper on decisions that do not warrant full compute, so the underlying generation budget is never adapted."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4404352873","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"DynaSaur lets an LLM agent generate actions as executable code rather than choosing from a predefined set, removing the human-enumeration bottleneck and expanding the action space. Its residue is that every action is now a full open-ended LLM generation of uniform cost — the framework gains expressiveness but has no mechanism to recognize that a routine, previously-seen action could be emitted far more cheaply than a novel one."},{"paper_id":"semanticscholar:c966714ea2061fbb555532a923a87d9b84c9ba2b","is_anchor":false,"summary_and_residue":"Reinforcing LLM Agents via Policy Optimization with Action Decomposition decomposes an action into intra-action tokens and assigns fine-grained credit for RL optimization over an exponentially large action space. Its residue is that the decomposition serves credit assignment during TRAINING; at inference each action is still produced by full autoregressive decoding, so the work yields no reduction in the decode-time cost of emitting an action and no per-token notion of which positions could be cheaply predicted."}],"state":"proceed","intake":{"domain":"efficient action generation for LLM/VLA-based AI agents (decode-time latency and compute of emitting actions)","venue":"ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML","time":"2026","data":["agentic / embodied benchmarks (e.g. mobile/web agent task suites, VLN, VLA manipulation rollouts)","agent trajectory logs with per-step action and outcome labels"],"compute":"1xA100 x 3 months (~90 A100-day)","expertise":"ML researcher with LLM-agent + efficient-inference background","preference":"both","baseline":"speculative decoding for VLA (Spec-VLA), asynchronous VLA inference (VLASH), training-free diffusion-policy acceleration (Fast Policy), action-decomposition RL (NeurIPS24)","limitation":"every recent acceleration method spends a fixed or hand-tuned generation budget per action step regardless of how much deliberation the decision actually needs","contribution_type":"method","_inferred_fields":["venue","time","data","compute","expertise","preference","baseline","limitation","contribution_type"]}},"phase2":{"core_mechanism":"The pipeline is sequential (probe -> route -> generate), centered on one object we call the per-decision difficulty score d_t in [0,1], computed BEFORE any full action generation commits at control step t. Concretely d_t = sigma( alpha * H_t + beta * Delta_t - tau ), where: (i) H_t is the Shannon entropy of a CHEAP action probe -- a single forward pass of the frozen policy truncated at an early exit layer L_e (L_e fixed at 25% of depth) decoded greedily for one action-token block, read off the probe head's softmax; (ii) Delta_t is the token-level disagreement (fraction of differing tokens) between that cheap probe's emitted action and the action the agent actually executed at t-1 (the cached previous action), capturing 'has the situation changed since last step'; (iii) alpha, beta are scalar weights bridging the two unit-different quantities (nats and a [0,1] fraction), tau is a single learned scalar threshold, sigma the logistic. d_t is the difficulty PROPERTY on which heterogeneous_decomposition (C04) partitions the decision stream: if d_t < theta (theta a deployment knob), the step is routed to the FAST path -- the agent emits the cheap probe's action directly (cost = one early-exit pass, no full generation); if d_t >= theta it is routed to the FULL path -- ordinary complete autoregressive / full-denoising action generation. The self_supervised_signal_engineering (C07) move manufactures d_t from the model's own internal state (entropy + previous-action disagreement) because there are NO ground-truth difficulty labels; to stop the probe degenerating into 'route everything cheap', we calibrate tau and theta against a verified-mistake replay buffer R (states where the fast path historically produced an action that diverged from the full path by more than epsilon in the action metric), forcing the threshold to keep those states on the full path. The assumption_audit_and_pivot (C11) leg audits the stopping rule every leaf inherits -- 'spend full generation at every step' -- and reframes it as online stopping: each step is an 'accept cheap emission vs pay for full generation' decision, and we re-derive a budget certificate: under the assumption that fast-path action error is bounded by a per-step delta whenever d_t < theta (verified empirically on R), cumulative action-regret of the routed policy relative to the always-full policy over horizon T is bounded by (expected number of routed-cheap steps) * delta, which is sublinear in T exactly when the routine fraction is bounded away from 0 -- the certificate collapses to the trivial always-full bound when theta -> infinity (every step routed full), binding the gain to the pivot. The companion controlled_diagnostic_design (C02) ships the empirical separation that the audit needs: a matched-pair instrument where, on the SAME observed state, we record (a) the full-generation action and (b) the fast-path action, and report the agreement-gap distribution -- the headline is the measured fraction of states with agreement above 1-epsilon (the 'de-novo was unnecessary' mass), an out-of-sample-verifiable number, not a leaderboard score. The C04 load-bearing artifact is the action-fidelity decomposition: total task-return loss of routing = sum over routed-cheap steps of (per-step action deviation x its sensitivity), bounding how the differentiated treatment recovers the full-generation objective and licensing the partition over heuristic per-step tuning. Spec-VLA (openalex:W4416035531) reports speedups from a global draft length + relaxed-acceptance constant; our d_t makes the draft/skip decision PER STATE from a pre-generation readout it never computes, and Fast Policy (openalex:W4416749600) applies one acceleration factor every step where we apply zero acceleration on hard steps and maximal (full skip) on routine ones.","core_mechanism_reasoning":"(a) Shared machinery vs separate modules: the three legs share ONE object, d_t, so they are not stapled -- C07 manufactures it, C11 audits the stopping rule that consumes it, C04 partitions on it; that single-object sequential pipeline is why a reviewer reads one paper. The companion C02 is realized at the main-pattern level (a matched-pair instrument), not a fourth mechanism, because the audit's honest deliverable is an identifiability claim and needs an empirical separation to ship under contribution_type=method. (b) Alternatives considered and rejected: I considered making the anchor architectural_operator_substitution (substitute a cheap surrogate generator) but traced its load-bearing artifact onto method_lineage node c1 (conditional computation / early-exit), a flagged regression -- a plain early-exit drafter with a global accept threshold is exactly Spec-VLA's move; heterogeneous_decomposition stays off c1 because the partition criterion is a verified-outcome-grounded per-decision difficulty signal applied to open-ended agent actions and the contribution is the fidelity decomposition, not the early-exit. I also considered C26 (preference reward) for the difficulty signal and rejected it: difficulty is not naturally comparative/preference-shaped, it is an internal-state readout, which is C07's exact niche.","falsification_prediction":"Minimal experiment: take one frozen VLA or LLM-agent policy and one agentic benchmark with per-step success attributable to actions (e.g. a manipulation suite or a web/mobile-agent task suite), implement the early-exit probe and the d_t router, and measure (1) average per-step decode cost and (2) task success rate, against the always-full-generation baseline. If the candidate works, average decode cost decreases substantially (target: a large fraction of steps routed cheap) while task success stays within noise of the full baseline, AND the matched-pair agreement-rate between fast-path and full-path actions is high on the routed-cheap mass. The named load-bearing variable is d_t (the pre-generation difficulty score). Negative control: replace d_t with a RANDOM score calibrated to route the SAME fraction of steps cheap; the prediction is that task success collapses well below the full baseline under random routing while it is preserved under d_t routing -- the downstream task-outcome metric (success rate), not d_t's own value, is what must move, ruling out 'the benchmark is just easy / any routing works'. Positive control: a stripped model that uses ONLY d_t (drop the previous-action term, keep entropy) to route should recover most of the cost saving at preserved success, identifying entropy of the early-exit probe as the carrying signal. If success drops proportionally to the cheap-routed fraction under d_t (no separability), or random routing does as well as d_t, the difficulty-separability claim is falsified.","differentiation_from_lit":[{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416035531","delta":"Spec-VLA accelerates VLA decoding with a draft model under a GLOBAL relaxed-acceptance constant tuned offline; we construct a per-state, pre-generation difficulty score d_t that decides whether to draft/skip at all, and derive an action-fidelity decomposition bounding the routed policy's deviation that Spec-VLA's fixed-threshold scheme never produces."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416749600","delta":"Fast Policy applies a single training-free acceleration factor identically at every control step; we measure that the agent decision stream is difficulty-SEPARABLE and route zero vs full generation per state, supplying the matched-pair agreement-gap evidence that quantifies how many steps never needed full generation -- a measurement Fast Policy does not make."},{"paper_id":"openalex:W4416958104","delta":"VLASH hides a FIXED per-action inference cost behind asynchronous execution and future-state compensation; we instead make the per-action cost itself variable by skipping generation on routine steps, and certify cumulative action-regret of the skipping rule rather than only compensating latency."},{"paper_id":"arxiv:2606.00476v1","delta":"The faithfulness-gap paper measures post-hoc whether agents act on stated reasoning; we build a PRE-generation difficulty readout from internal state that is consumed by a router, turning a diagnostic quantity into an actionable efficiency signal."}],"almost_prior_paper_id":"openalex:W4416035531","what_step_was_missed":"Spec-VLA constructs speculative drafting with a single relaxed-acceptance threshold applied uniformly across states; for our contribution to already exist it would have needed to construct a per-state difficulty estimator computed from the verifier's OWN early-layer readout before drafting and to derive the action-fidelity / cumulative-action-regret decomposition that licenses skipping full generation on a quantified routine fraction -- it produces neither the pre-generation per-state signal nor the regret certificate, only a global acceptance constant."},"phase3":{"collision_hits_count":261,"verdict":"revise","verdict_rationale":"No hard floor fired: gap_closure_reject_check is borderline (no lesson candidate_match: yes), recipe_application_check is applied on all three legs, and the anti_pattern_check matched audit_decomp_supervisor but mitigation_substantively_delivered=true (partition criterion and manufactured signal are the same object d_t, with the required dis-conflation ablation supplied by the negative+positive controls). Revise is chosen over advance on two load-bearing findings: (1) paper_pointed_threat TrACE (semanticscholar:5a36...) shares the candidate's exact uniform-budget hook and an agreement-based difficulty signal, addressable_via rewriting the hook + differentiation_from_lit to foreground the pre-generation sub-full-cost-emission and regret-certificate deltas; (2) the C11 borderline 'a re-derived guarantee whose binding constant is dataset-dependent ... is vacuous' on delta — the certificate must state delta's dataset-dependence and the practitioner-controllable theta knob explicitly. Both are tactical field edits; gap selection and sub-patterns stay.","checks":{"gap_closure_reject_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf allocates a per-decision action-generation budget from a signal that is available BEFORE the full action generation commits — every accelerator (Spec-VLA openalex:W4416035531, Fast Policy openalex:W4416749600) spends a fixed or globally-tuned budget per step, so the system cannot contract compute on routine decisions nor expand it on the rare hard ones (additive: the missing outcome is difficulty-matched per-step generation cost, not any one mechanism for it).","main_pattern":"heterogeneous_decomposition","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure is treating the partition criterion itself as the contribution while leaving its value unproven, and validating in a regime where the compression bottleneck does not bite or against missing baselines.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Presenting a sensitivity or redundancy proxy as the novelty invites the verdict that it rediscovers known mixed-precision or low-rank results unless it is sharply differentiated from the obvious prior criterion.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"d_t (early-exit entropy + previous-action disagreement) is the partition proxy and resembles known early-exit confidence criteria; the candidate must lean on the regret certificate + matched-pair instrument as the contribution rather than the proxy itself, otherwise it reads as a rediscovery of input-difficulty early-exit (DART collision hit arxiv:2603.12269v1)."},{"lesson_quoted":"Omitting comparison against both the strongest uniform baseline and the obvious cheap alternative (SVD/PCA, structured dropout, a natively trained smaller model) leaves reviewers unable to tell whether the partition buys anything at all.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"core_mechanism_steps step 9 explicitly compares against the full-generation baseline, Spec-VLA-style global drafting, and Fast-Policy-style global acceleration on the same benchmark."},{"lesson_quoted":"A clever partition with no measured real-world deployment metric (no inference latency or memory speedup) reads as a proxy-only contribution and stalls at borderline.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"falsification_prediction measures average per-step decode cost in wall-clock + FLOPs and task success, the true deployment metrics, not a proxy."},{"lesson_quoted":"Skipping any analysis of why the heterogeneity exists — the data or value distribution that drives the partition — makes the technical novelty and the potential impact impossible to assess.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the C02 matched-pair instrument (step 7) reports the agreement-gap distribution / unnecessary-de-novo mass, which is exactly the value distribution that drives the partition."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides a verifiable predictor of per-state decision difficulty that an efficient agent could condition on — the accelerators read no difficulty signal at all and the diagnostic/faithfulness papers (arxiv:2606.00476v1) measure post-hoc behavior rather than supplying a pre-generation difficulty estimate (additive: a difficulty estimate that is cheap relative to full action generation and predictive of when cheap generation suffices).","main_pattern":"self_supervised_signal_engineering","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"The recurring failure shape is a manufactured internal signal whose validity silently rests on an assumption that does not survive deployment — model calibration on networks known to be miscalibrated — or recombining well-known components without a single load-bearing mechanistic insight.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"A label-free signal whose validity depends on model calibration silently fails on exactly the deep networks known to be poorly calibrated — validate a surrogate where its core assumption is weakest, not where it is convenient.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"d_t uses entropy of an early-exit probe, which is a calibration-sensitive quantity; the candidate partially mitigates by calibrating tau/theta against a verified-mistake replay buffer R of states where the cheap path actually diverged, anchoring the threshold to verified outcomes rather than raw calibrated confidence, but the residual calibration dependence should be stress-tested on hard states."},{"lesson_quoted":"Using target or test-set information during adaptation invites a label-leakage objection that undermines the very source-free, label-free deployment setting the method claims.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"R is built from held-out trajectories run under both paths offline (step 5), and the matched-pair instrument is on a fresh held-out set; no test-set leakage into the routed deployment."},{"lesson_quoted":"Importing a generic continual-learning blending or interpolation technique into a new modality without identifying that modality's specific dynamics lever reads as recombination, not contribution.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the load-bearing insight is the previous-action-disagreement term Delta_t plus the pre-generation early-exit readout, specific to the agent control-loop dynamics, not a generic blending import."},{"lesson_quoted":"A multi-branch or ensemble reweighting mechanism that overlaps with standard multi-task/mixture-of-experts ensembling must explicitly beat both the single-model and the standard-ensemble baselines, or the gain is credited to prior art.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the method uses one frozen backbone with an early-exit tap, not an ensemble/MoE, so this lesson does not bind."}],"verdict":"borderline"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether the unit of acceleration must remain the FULL action emitted fresh at every step, rather than a decision that could reuse or skip generation when the current action is predictable from recent context (subtractive: every leaf silently inherits from the shared ancestor the assumption that each control step re-generates a complete action de novo; none asks whether that per-step from-scratch regeneration is necessary).","main_pattern":"assumption_audit_and_pivot","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_failure_mode_quoted":"Substituting one selection heuristic for another without a theorem stating when and why it wins reads as an engineering combination, and a re-derived guarantee whose binding constant is dataset-dependent and uncontrollable by the practitioner is vacuous in the worst case.","reject_lessons_evaluated":[{"lesson_quoted":"Substituting one selection heuristic for another without a theorem stating when and why it wins reads as an engineering combination, not a contribution, no matter how clean the empirical gain.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"the candidate does re-derive a cumulative-action-regret budget certificate (steps 8) binding the gain to the pivot (collapses to always-full when theta->infinity), but the certificate's per-step delta is empirically estimated from R rather than derived from a structural property, which is the controllable-constant concern below."},{"lesson_quoted":"A re-derived guarantee whose binding constant is dataset-dependent and cannot be controlled by the practitioner is vacuous in the worst case and fails to convince.","candidate_match":"borderline","reasoning":"delta (the per-step fast-path action error bound) is estimated as a 95th-percentile on R, i.e. dataset-dependent; it is practitioner-controllable via theta (raising theta routes fewer steps cheap, shrinking the routed-cheap count that multiplies delta), but the certificate should state delta's dependence and the theta knob explicitly so the bound is not vacuous."},{"lesson_quoted":"Unlocking a new capability by violating an assumption while ignoring a protective property it guarded — detectability, validity, identifiability — invites rejection on the overlooked side effect rather than the headline result.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the protected property (task success / action fidelity) is exactly what the negative control and the C04 fidelity decomposition track, so the side effect of skipping generation is measured head-on, not ignored."},{"lesson_quoted":"Pivoting an assumption the community treats as a reasonable modeling choice — rather than first proving it a genuine restriction — leaves both motivation and novelty in doubt.","candidate_match":"no","reasoning":"the matched-pair instrument empirically proves the de-novo-every-step assumption is a genuine restriction by quantifying the mass of states whose action the cheap path already recovers."}],"verdict":"borderline"}],"verdict":"borderline","reasoning":"No gap_closure entry is triggered (no Reject lesson marked candidate_match: yes), so no hard floor here. Three borderlines carry weight: C04's 'sensitivity proxy reads as rediscovery unless sharply differentiated' (the d_t proxy resembles input-difficulty early-exit), C07's calibration-dependence lesson, and C11's 'dataset-dependent binding constant' lesson on delta — all load-bearing on the certificate/proxy framing and addressable by tactical sharpening, not gap-level change."},"recipe_application_check":{"entries":[{"gap":"No retrieved leaf allocates a per-decision action-generation budget from a signal that is available BEFORE the full action generation commits ...","sub_pattern":"C04 (Decompose for Differentiated Treatment)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Discriminate components by a magnitude/sensitivity/influence/redundancy criterion into a high-impact minority and a near-redundant bulk, then aggressively compress the bulk while protecting the minority; the load-bearing artifact is an error/sensitivity decomposition that bounds how the differentiated treatment recovers the original objective.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism partitions the agent's DECISION STREAM by d_t into a routine bulk (routed to a near-zero-cost path) and a hard minority (full generation), and supplies the action-fidelity decomposition (total task-return loss = sum over routed-cheap steps of action-deviation x sensitivity) — the cluster's signature error-decomposition-bounding-differentiated-treatment move is present, not just the generic 'split into easy/hard'.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf provides a verifiable predictor of per-state decision difficulty ...","sub_pattern":"C07 (Manufacture the Supervisory Signal)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Treat the model's own internal-state readouts as the manufactured signal, pairing a mechanistic diagnosis localizing the failure to a structural site with a surgically confined correction on a minimal lever while the backbone stays frozen, and bolt on an explicit anti-collapse stabilizer.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism reads internal state at a fixed early-exit layer (entropy H_t + previous-action disagreement Delta_t), confines the lever to a tiny calibrated threshold (tau, theta) with the frozen backbone, and bolts on the verified-mistake replay buffer R as the explicit anti-degeneracy stabilizer that stops the probe routing everything cheap — the diagnose-localize / minimize-on-a-tiny-lever / stabilize-against-collapse signature is present.","verdict":"applied"},{"gap":"No retrieved leaf tests whether the unit of acceleration must remain the FULL action emitted fresh at every step ...","sub_pattern":"C11 (Audit and Pivot an Assumption)","tactical_pattern_quoted":"Center on a selection/acquisition/stopping rule, pivot the single assumption baked into its criterion either by relaxing it or by reframing the selection task as a different problem class (selection->stopping/control), and re-derive a performance certificate (regret/competitive ratio/budget) shown to match or beat the pre-pivot baseline.","instantiation_in_core_mechanism":"core_mechanism audits the 'spend full generation every step' stopping rule, reframes it as online stopping (selection->when-to-stop: accept cheap emission vs pay full generation), and re-derives a cumulative-action-regret budget certificate that collapses to the always-full bound when theta->infinity — the audit-pivot-and-re-derive-a-certificate signature is present.","verdict":"applied"}],"verdict":"applied","reasoning":"All three legs perform their cited cluster's distinctive move: C04's error-decomposition (not just easy/hard split), C07's internal-readout + tiny-lever + anti-collapse stabilizer, and C11's stopping-reframe + re-derived certificate. None is the parent's generic gist alone."},"anti_pattern_check":{"composition_set":["heterogeneous_decomposition","self_supervised_signal_engineering","assumption_audit_and_pivot"],"matched_pattern_id":"audit_decomp_supervisor","required_mitigation_quoted":"The decomposition criterion must be derivable from observed structure or task-level supervision (not just intuition), AND the manufactured signal must be the *unique* signal the decomposition implies. An ablation that holds the decomposition fixed and varies the signal (or vice versa) must show the two are not conflated.","mitigation_substantively_delivered":"true","reasoning":"The composition is mitigation-favorable here because the partition criterion and the manufactured signal are the SAME object d_t — the decomposition is not a second independent un-derived choice stacked on the signal; the partition is defined exactly by the manufactured difficulty score (derivable from observed structure: the verified-mistake buffer R is task-level supervision that grounds the threshold, satisfying mitigation clause 1, and d_t is the unique signal the partition implies, satisfying clause 2). The required dis-conflation ablation is delivered: the negative control (random routing at the same cheap-routed rate, holding the decomposition's rate fixed while destroying the signal) plus the positive control (entropy-only d_t) are exactly the 'hold decomposition fixed, vary the signal' test the mitigation demands."},"paper_pointed_threat":{"threat_paper_id":"semanticscholar:5a3696f45969e4bce35971cd9eb69622c28c073f","threat_source":"collision_hits","subsumption_argument":"TrACE ('Don't Overthink It: Inter-Rollout Action Agreement as a Free Adaptive-Compute Signal for LLM Agents') opens with the IDENTICAL critique — existing inference-time-compute methods apply compute uniformly regardless of per-step difficulty — and proposes a training-free controller that allocates compute adaptively across agent timesteps using inter-rollout action AGREEMENT as the difficulty signal (high agreement -> commit immediately; low agreement -> sample more). This directly threatens the candidate's hook and its difficulty-signal leg: the uniform-budget framing is no longer novel, and 'agreement as a difficulty signal' overlaps the candidate's Delta_t / probe-disagreement term. The candidate's claim stands ONLY on what TrACE structurally does not do: (a) TrACE detects easy steps by sampling MULTIPLE full rollouts, so its compute floor is >= one full generation per step and it ADDS compute to find easy steps — it never makes the easy-step path cheaper than a single full generation; the candidate's d_t is a PRE-generation early-exit readout (entropy at 25% depth) that STOPS the forward pass before full generation commits, achieving sub-full-cost emission TrACE cannot; (b) TrACE has no performance certificate — the candidate re-derives a cumulative-action-regret budget bound (C11) absent in TrACE; (c) TrACE provides no matched-pair de-novo-necessity instrument (C02). So this is NOT exact-mechanism overlap; it is a strong adjacent that the candidate must explicitly differentiate or it will be read as a VLA-flavored restatement of TrACE.","addressable_via":"Rewrite the hook and add TrACE (and AC^2-VLA arxiv:2601.19634v1, which does per-step adaptive computation for VLA via temporal/spatial/depth redundancy and action context) to differentiation_from_lit, foregrounding the two unaddressed structural deltas: pre-generation sub-full-cost emission (early-exit stop vs multi-rollout add) and the cumulative-action-regret certificate."}},"revision_targets":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"hook","issue":"paper_pointed_threat TrACE (semanticscholar:5a3696f45969e4bce35971cd9eb69622c28c073f) shares the candidate's uniform-budget critique and an agreement-based per-step difficulty signal, so the current hook is no longer non-obvious as written.","fix_direction":"Rewrite the hook to foreground the structural delta TrACE cannot deliver: the difficulty readout is taken PRE-generation from an early-exit layer and STOPS the forward pass, so the easy-step path costs strictly LESS than one full generation — unlike multi-rollout agreement methods whose floor is >= one full generation per step. Keep shape (a); the non-obvious claim becomes that a sub-full-cost pre-generation readout suffices on the routine majority."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","issue":"TrACE (semanticscholar:5a3696f45969e4bce35971cd9eb69622c28c073f) and AC^2-VLA (arxiv:2601.19634v1) are closer adjacents than the currently-listed papers and are absent from differentiation_from_lit.","fix_direction":"Add a differentiation_from_lit entry for TrACE: 'TrACE allocates per-step compute by sampling multiple full rollouts and measuring inter-rollout action agreement, so its floor is one full generation per step (it ADDS compute to find easy steps); we read difficulty from a single pre-generation early-exit pass that STOPS before full generation and derive a cumulative-action-regret certificate TrACE has no analogue of.' Add an entry for AC^2-VLA: 'AC^2-VLA adaptively prunes tokens / reuses cognition across temporal-spatial-depth redundancy via a trained action-guided self-distillation policy; we require no policy training (a 4-scalar calibration on a frozen backbone) and ship an online-stopping action-regret bound and a matched-pair de-novo-necessity measurement it does not provide.'"},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","issue":"C11 borderline: the cumulative-action-regret certificate's binding constant delta is dataset-dependent (95th-percentile on R) and could read as vacuous unless its dependence and the practitioner-controllable knob are stated.","fix_direction":"In the sentence deriving the C11 budget certificate, add that delta is an empirically-estimated, dataset-dependent constant whose worst-case is controlled by the practitioner through theta (raising theta routes fewer steps cheap, shrinking the routed-cheap count that multiplies delta), and that the bound is reported WITH delta's empirical estimate and its theta-sensitivity rather than as a delta-free claim — so the guarantee is practitioner-controllable, not vacuous."}],"applied_revisions":[{"scope":"tactical","field":"hook","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Rewrote hook to foreground the pre-generation early-exit STOP (sub-full-generation cost) vs multi-rollout adaptive-compute whose floor is >= one full generation, dodging the TrACE threat."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"differentiation_from_lit","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Added TrACE (multi-rollout agreement, floor >= one full gen, no certificate) and AC^2-VLA (trained pruning policy, no regret bound / no de-novo-necessity instrument) as closest adjacents with substantive deltas."},{"scope":"tactical","field":"core_mechanism","outcome":"applied","delta_summary":"Stated delta as a dataset-dependent empirically-estimated constant whose worst-case is practitioner-controllable via theta, so the C11 certificate is not vacuous."}]},"phase4_md_en":"# Spend-Where-It-Matters: Difficulty-Routed Action Generation for AI Agents\n\n**Method.** Difficulty-Routed Action Generation (DRAG)\n\n## Motivation\nAI agents that use large language models or vision-language-action (VLA) models to choose what to do next currently pay the same heavy 'thinking' cost on every single step — whether the next move is obvious or genuinely hard. Recent speed-ups (Spec-VLA, which guesses action tokens and checks them in parallel; Fast Policy, which shortens the denoising used to produce a motion) all use ONE global setting applied identically at every step, so they can't spend less on easy moves and more on hard ones. The result is that an agent pays close to its worst-case cost on average and still rushes the few decisions that actually matter.\n\nWhat's newly possible: the cheap-generation tricks now exist, and very recent agent controllers (TrACE, $AC^{2}-VLA)$ show people now agree the uniform-budget habit is the problem — but they still cost at least one full generation per step or need an extra trained model. The open piece is a way to judge a step's difficulty BEFORE doing the expensive generation, cheaply enough to skip it.\n\nOur idea (Difficulty-Routed Action Generation, DRAG): run only the first quarter of the model's layers to get a quick draft action and a confidence reading, turn that into a difficulty score $d_{t},$ and on easy steps just emit the draft and STOP — never finishing the expensive forward pass. Hard steps get the full treatment. We back this with a guarantee on how far the cheap shortcuts can drift, and a direct measurement of how many steps never needed the full computation in the first place. When this works, long-running agents become affordable on ordinary hardware without dumbing down their hard decisions.\n\n## Method\n### Pre-generation difficulty probe\n*Read a cheap difficulty score from an early-exit pass before full generation commits.*\n\n1. Take the agent model and freeze all its weights. About a quarter of the way through its layers (call that point $L_{e}),$ tap the model's internal state and attach a small extra output layer (a single linear layer, or a tiny 2-layer network) that produces a draft action from that early state. Train only this small layer to imitate the action the full model would have produced, using held-out runs as training pairs; the main model is never changed. 【author decision: keep $L_{e}$ at one quarter depth, or try 15%/25%/40% and use the shallowest one whose imitation error stops improving.】\n   - _Why_: It gives a cheap candidate action and a confidence reading long before the full, expensive generation would finish.\n2. At each step, read two simple numbers off the draft layer. The first is how UNSURE the draft is (its entropy — high when the draft spreads probability over many possible actions). The second is how much the draft DIFFERS from the action you actually executed on the previous step (for token actions, the fraction of action slots that changed; for continuous actions, the rescaled distance between the two action vectors). No labels are needed for either.\n   - _Why_: There are no difficulty labels, so the model's own uncertainty plus 'has anything changed since last step' stand in for difficulty.\n3. Merge the two numbers into a single difficulty score $d_{t}$ between 0 and 1 (see Eq. (1)): multiply the uncertainty and the difference by their own weights (alpha and beta, which put the two different units on the same footing), subtract a learned cutoff (tau), and pass the result through a logistic function so it lands between 0 and 1. A high $d_{t}$ means 'this step looks hard'.\n\n*The per-decision difficulty score $d_{t}$ is a logistic $\\sigma $ of the early-exit probe entropy $H_{t}$ (nats) and the token disagreement $\\Delta _{t}$ with the previous executed action, weighted by $\\alpha , \\beta $ and shifted by a learned threshold $\\tau .$*\n$$ d_t = \\sigma\\!\\left(\\alpha\\, H_t + \\beta\\, \\Delta_t - \\tau\\right) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _Why_: A single score is what both the routing decision and the stopping guarantee need to work on.\n\n### Difficulty router\n*Emit routine actions at sub-full cost and reserve full generation for hard steps.*\n\n4. Use the difficulty score to decide (see Eq. (2)): if it is below a chosen threshold theta, accept the draft action and STOP right there — do not run the remaining three quarters of the model (or the rest of the denoising). If it is at or above theta, run the full model to produce the action. Whatever action comes out is the one the agent actually performs, so this choice directly affects task success.\n\n*If $d_{t}$ is below the deployment threshold $\\theta $ the action $a_{t}$ is the cheap early-exit probe action (the forward pass is stopped at layer $L_{e})$; otherwise full generation runs.*\n$$ a_t = \\begin{cases} \\text{probe action (forward pass stopped at } L_e) & d_t < \\theta \\\\ \\text{full-generation action} & d_t \\ge \\theta \\end{cases} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _Why_: Easy steps cost a fraction of a full generation; hard steps still get full effort.\n\n### Grounding and calibration\n*Anchor the easy/hard split and the routing scalars to verified mistakes.*\n\n5. Before deployment, take a separate set of recorded runs and, at every state, compute BOTH the cheap draft action and the full action, then record every state where the cheap action drifts from the full action by more than a small margin epsilon (one changed token for discrete actions; for continuous control, a small fraction of the action range, or the smallest change that flips the task from success to failure). Collect these states into a buffer R of 'states where cheap was wrong'. 【author decision: whether epsilon is a fixed token change or the smallest change that flips success, matching your task's success rule.】\n   - _Why_: This is the safety net that stops the system from lazily routing everything to the cheap path.\n6. Tune just four numbers — alpha, beta, tau, theta — so that the average per-step compute is as low as possible WHILE at least 95% of the known-hard states in buffer R are still sent to the full model. Since there are only four numbers, you can sweep a coarse grid and then refine locally; no network is trained here. The 95% rule is what keeps the easy/hard split honest, tied to states where the cheap path actually failed.\n   - _Why_: It ties the easy/hard split to verified mistakes rather than to a hunch, so the partition is grounded.\n\n### Necessity measurement and certificate\n*Quantify how many steps never needed full generation and bound the cost of skipping it.*\n\n7. On a brand-new set of states (not the ones used for buffer R), compare the cheap action and the full action at every state and record how closely they agree (1 means identical). Plot the whole agreement distribution and report how many states agree almost perfectly (above 1 minus the same small margin epsilon). That number is the share of steps that never needed the full, from-scratch generation — the direct evidence for the method's core claim.\n   - _Why_: This directly measures the claim that many steps were being regenerated from scratch unnecessarily.\n8. Write down and check the guarantee (see Eq. (3)): the total drift in action quality from skipping generation is at most the number of cheap-routed steps times delta, where delta is the 95th-percentile cheap-path error measured on buffer R. Report delta's actual value, note that it depends on the dataset, and note that raising theta (fewer cheap steps) directly shrinks the bound — so the cost-versus-quality trade-off is a dial you control, not a gamble. Confirm the bound matches the task-quality loss you actually observe.\n\n*Cumulative action-regret over horizon T is bounded by the expected number of cheap-routed steps times $\\delta ,$ the dataset-dependent 95th-percentile fast-path deviation on the verified-mistake buffer R; raising $\\theta $ shrinks the cheap count and so the bound.*\n$$ \\mathrm{Regret}(T) \\;\\le\\; \\mathbb{E}\\!\\left[\\,N^{\\mathrm{cheap}}_T\\,\\right]\\cdot \\delta, \\qquad \\delta = \\widehat{q}_{0.95}\\big(\\text{fast-path deviation on } R\\big) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _Why_: It turns 'we skipped some generation' into a controllable cost-vs-quality dial instead of a gamble.\n\n### Evaluation and controls\n*Compare against global-budget baselines and isolate $d_{t}$ as the mechanism.*\n\n9. Run the whole system on one agent benchmark and measure two things — average cost per step (both real time and arithmetic operations) and task success — for your router versus three baselines: always running the full model, a single-global-setting speculative drafter, and a single-global-setting accelerator. Keep the model and benchmark identical across all four so the only difference is your per-step routing.\n   - _Why_: It shows the per-step routing actually buys something over the best one-knob-fits-all methods.\n10. Run two checks. First (negative control), route the same fraction of steps cheap but pick WHICH steps at random instead of by difficulty; if task success holds up, the difficulty score wasn't doing the work. Second (positive control), use only the uncertainty part of the score (drop the difference-from-last-step part); if this alone keeps most of the savings without hurting success, the uncertainty signal is the main driver.\n   - _Why_: If random routing does as well, the difficulty score wasn't doing the work; if it collapses, $d_{t}$ is the real mechanism.\n\n","phase4_md_zh":"# 按需分配：面向 AI 智能体的难度路由式动作生成\n\n**方法名称.** Difficulty-Routed Action Generation (DRAG)\n\n## 研究动机\n使用大语言模型或 vision-language-action（VLA）模型来决定下一步动作的 AI 智能体，目前在每一步都要付出同样高昂的“思考”成本——无论下一步是显而易见还是真正困难。近期的加速方法（Spec-VLA 猜测动作 token 并并行校验；Fast Policy 缩短生成动作所需的去噪步数）都用 ONE 个全局设置在每一步上一视同仁地施加，因此无法在简单步上少花、在困难步上多花。结果是智能体平均下来接近最坏情况的开销，却仍然在真正关键的少数决策上仓促行事。\n\n为什么现在可行：廉价生成的手段已经成熟，而最新的智能体控制器（TrACE、$AC^{2}-VLA$）表明大家已认同“统一预算”是症结——但它们每步仍至少要付一次完整生成的成本，或需要额外训练一个模型。真正空缺的是：在做昂贵生成之前、且足够廉价到可以据此跳过，就先判断这一步的难度。\n\n我们的想法（Difficulty-Routed Action Generation, DRAG）：只跑模型前四分之一的层，得到一个快速草稿动作和一个置信读数，把它变成难度分 $d_{t}$；在简单步上直接输出草稿并 STOP——根本不跑完昂贵的前向；困难步才走完整生成。我们用一个“廉价捷径最多偏多少”的保证，以及“到底有多少步本来就不需要完整计算”的直接度量来支撑它。一旦奏效，长时间运行的智能体就能在普通硬件上负担得起，而不必牺牲其困难决策的质量。\n\n## 方法\n### 生成前难度探针\n*在完整生成之前，从早退前向中读出一个廉价的难度分。*\n\n1. 取智能体模型并冻结其全部权重。在大约四分之一层深处（记作 $L_{e}$）抽出模型的内部状态，并接上一个小的额外输出层（一个线性层，或一个很小的 2 层网络），用它从该早期状态产生一个草稿动作。只训练这个小层，让它模仿完整模型本会产生的动作，用留出运行作为训练样本对；主模型始终不变。【author decision：$L_{e}$ 保持在四分之一层深，或尝试 15%/25%/40% 并选用模仿误差不再下降的最浅深度。】\n   - _为什么_: 它在昂贵的完整生成结束之前很早就给出一个廉价候选动作和一个置信读数。\n2. 在每一步，从草稿层读出两个简单的数。第一个是草稿有多“不确定”（它的熵——当草稿把概率分散到很多可能动作上时就高）。第二个是草稿与你上一步实际执行的动作相差多少（对 token 动作，是发生改变的动作槽位的比例；对连续动作，是两个动作向量之间经过重新缩放的距离）。两者都不需要任何标签。\n   - _为什么_: 没有难度标签，于是用模型自身的不确定性加上“与上一步相比是否有变化”来代表难度。\n3. 把两个数合并成一个介于 0 和 1 之间的难度分 $d_{t}$（见 Eq. (1)）：将不确定性和差异各自乘上权重（alpha 和 beta，用以把两种不同单位放到同一尺度上），减去一个可学习的截断值（tau），再经过逻辑斯蒂函数把结果压到 0 与 1 之间。$d_{t}$ 高就表示“这一步看起来困难”。\n\n*每步难度分 $d_{t}$ 是对早退探针熵 $H_{t}$（单位 nats）与当前动作相对上一步已执行动作的 token 不一致度 $\\Delta _{t}$ 的逻辑斯蒂 $\\sigma $ 映射，权重为 $\\alpha $、$\\beta $，并由可学习阈值 $\\tau $ 平移。*\n$$ d_t = \\sigma\\!\\left(\\alpha\\, H_t + \\beta\\, \\Delta_t - \\tau\\right) \\tag{1} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 路由决策和停止保证都需要在同一个分数上运作。\n\n### 难度路由器\n*以低于完整生成的成本输出常规动作，把完整生成留给困难步。*\n\n4. 用难度分来决定（见 Eq. (2)）：若它低于选定阈值 theta，就采纳草稿动作并就此 STOP——不再运行模型剩下的四分之三（或剩余的去噪）。若它达到或高于 theta，就跑完整模型来产生动作。无论输出哪个动作，都是智能体真正执行的那个，因此这个选择直接影响任务成功率。\n\n*若 $d_{t}$ 低于部署阈值 $\\theta $，则动作 $a_{t}$ 取早退探针在层 $L_{e}$ 处停止前向得到的廉价动作；否则执行完整生成。*\n$$ a_t = \\begin{cases} \\text{probe action (forward pass stopped at } L_e) & d_t < \\theta \\\\ \\text{full-generation action} & d_t \\ge \\theta \\end{cases} \\tag{2} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 简单步只花完整生成的一小部分成本，困难步仍获得完整算力。\n\n### 依据与标定\n*把简单/困难划分与路由标量绑定到已验证的错误上。*\n\n5. 在部署之前，取一批单独记录的运行，在每个状态同时计算廉价草稿动作和完整动作，然后记下廉价动作相对完整动作漂移超过一个小幅度 epsilon 的所有状态（对离散动作是改变一个 token；对连续控制是动作范围的一小部分，或使任务由成功翻为失败的最小改变）。把这些状态收集成一个缓冲 R，即“廉价路径出错的状态”。【author decision：epsilon 取固定的 token 改变，还是使成功翻转的最小改变，需与你的任务成功判据一致。】\n   - _为什么_: 这是防止系统偷懒把一切都路由到廉价路径的安全网。\n6. 只调四个数——alpha、beta、tau、theta——使平均每步算力尽可能低，同时让缓冲 R 中已知困难状态仍有至少 95% 被送往完整模型。由于只有四个数，可以先粗网格扫描再局部细化；这里不训练任何网络。这条 95% 规则使简单/困难划分保持诚实，绑定到廉价路径确实失败的状态上。\n   - _为什么_: 它把简单/困难的划分绑定到已验证的错误上，而非凭直觉，从而使划分有据可依。\n\n### 必要性度量与证书\n*量化有多少步本不需要完整生成，并对跳过它的成本给出界。*\n\n7. 在一批全新的状态上（不是用于缓冲 R 的那些），在每个状态比较廉价动作与完整动作，并记录它们有多接近（1 表示完全相同）。画出整个一致度分布，并报告有多少状态几乎完全一致（高于 1 减去同样的小幅度 epsilon）。这个数就是“从头完整生成本来就不需要”的步数占比——是该方法核心论断的直接证据。\n   - _为什么_: 这直接度量了“很多步其实在无谓地从头重生成”的论断。\n8. 写出并核对这个保证（见 Eq. (3)）：跳过生成带来的动作质量总漂移，至多为廉价路由步数乘以 delta，其中 delta 是在缓冲 R 上测得的廉价路径误差 95 分位。报告 delta 的实际数值，指出它依赖数据集，并指出提高 theta（更少廉价步）会直接收紧这个界——因此成本-质量的权衡是你掌控的旋钮，而非赌博。确认该界与你实际观测到的任务质量损失相吻合。\n\n*时域 T 上的累积动作 regret 受廉价路由步数期望乘以 $\\delta $ 的约束，$\\delta $ 是在已验证错误缓冲 R 上 fast-path 偏差的 95 分位数（依赖数据集）；提高 $\\theta $ 会减少廉价步数，从而收紧该界。*\n$$ \\mathrm{Regret}(T) \\;\\le\\; \\mathbb{E}\\!\\left[\\,N^{\\mathrm{cheap}}_T\\,\\right]\\cdot \\delta, \\qquad \\delta = \\widehat{q}_{0.95}\\big(\\text{fast-path deviation on } R\\big) \\tag{3} $$\n\n   - _为什么_: 它把“我们跳过了一些生成”变成一个可控的成本-质量旋钮，而非一场赌博。\n\n### 评测与对照\n*对比全局预算基线，并将 $d_{t}$ 隔离为真正机制。*\n\n9. 在一个智能体基准上运行整个系统，测量两件事——每步平均成本（实际时间和算术运算量）和任务成功率——并将你的路由器与三个基线对比：始终运行完整模型、单一全局设置的推测式草稿器、单一全局设置的加速器。在四者间保持模型与基准完全一致，使唯一差别就是你的按步路由。\n   - _为什么_: 它表明按步路由确实比最好的“一个旋钮通吃”方法更划算。\n10. 做两个检验。第一（负对照），同样把相同比例的步路由到廉价路径，但 WHICH（哪些步）改为随机挑选而非按难度；若任务成功率仍然保持，说明难度分并未起作用。第二（正对照），只用分数中的不确定性部分（去掉与上一步差异的部分）；若仅此就能保住大部分节省而不损害成功率，说明不确定性信号是主要驱动。\n   - _为什么_: 若随机路由一样好，说明难度分没起作用；若它崩了，则 $d_{t}$ 才是真正的机制。\n\n"}];
const PATTERN_NAMES = {"assumption_audit_and_pivot":"Audit and Pivot an Assumption","architectural_operator_substitution":"Substitute the Operator or Representation","generative_process_redesign":"Liberate a Fixed Generative Component","controlled_diagnostic_design":"Design a Confound-Isolating Diagnostic","unify_into_shared_representation":"Unify Heterogeneous Inputs into One Space","reframe_as_solvable_object":"Reframe as a Solvable Object","self_supervised_signal_engineering":"Manufacture the Supervisory Signal","structural_prior_encoding":"Encode Structure by Construction","algebraic_equivalence_unification":"Prove Equivalence to Unify","heterogeneous_decomposition":"Decompose for Differentiated Treatment","decompose_and_delegate":"Decompose and Delegate to Solvers","relax_discrete_search_to_continuous":"Relax Discrete Search to Continuous","adapt_via_conditioning":"Adapt by Conditioning, Not Retraining","characterize_limit_then_surpass":"Characterize a Limit, Then Surpass It","targeted_self_supervised_objective":"Design a Property-Targeting Pretext Objective"};
